Description: """"I just grabbed the latest Xcode 12 beta (beta 3) and now I'm unable to build the SDK or an app. It seems to be complaining about APSHTTPClient and arm64.""""",title+description
TIMOB-28040,12,"""iOS: Make use of shared underlying byte array in Ti.Buffer""","""""""Our current API for Ti.Buffer makes use of an {{NSData}}. While https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11810 helps us to copy those bytes out to an {{ArrayBuffer}} on the JS side (though Ti.Blob), we should consider retooling {{Ti.Buffer}} to use direct allocation pointing to the same exact memory shared by the JS engine's {{ArrayBuffer}}.    This blog post makes reference to how the J2V8 project did exactly this: https://eclipsesource.com/blogs/2016/07/25/typedarrays-sharing-memory-between-v8-and-java/ for Java/JNI/V8    We could then read/write to the bytes from the native or JS side **without** crossing the native bridge. It would likely require us making Ti.Buffer some extension of ArrayBuffer.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Make use of shared underlying byte array in Ti.Buffer
Description: """"Our current API for Ti.Buffer makes use of an {{NSData}}. While https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11810 helps us to copy those bytes out to an {{ArrayBuffer}} on the JS side (though Ti.Blob), we should consider retooling {{Ti.Buffer}} to use direct allocation pointing to the same exact memory shared by the JS engine's {{ArrayBuffer}}. This blog post makes reference to how the J2V8 project did exactly this: https://eclipsesource.com/blogs/2016/07/25/typedarrays-sharing-memory-between-v8-and-java/ for Java/JNI/V8 We could then read/write to the bytes from the native or JS side **without** crossing the native bridge. It would likely require us making Ti.Buffer some extension of ArrayBuffer.""""",title+description
TIMOB-28039,12,"""Android: Make use of shared underlying byte array in Ti.Buffer""","""""""Our current API for Ti.Buffer makes use of a {{byte[]}}. While https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11810 helps us to copy those bytes out to an {{ArrayBuffer}} on the JS side (though Ti.Blob), we should consider retooling {{Ti.Buffer}} to use a {{ByteBuffer}} with direct allocation pointing to the same exact memory shared by the JS engine's {{ArrayBuffer}}.    This blog post makes reference to how the J2V8 project did exactly this: https://eclipsesource.com/blogs/2016/07/25/typedarrays-sharing-memory-between-v8-and-java/    Essentially this would involve Ti.Buffer wrapping a {{ByteBuffer}} rather than a {{byte[]}}. We could then read/write to the bytes from the native or JS side **without** crossing the JNI/V8 native bridge.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Make use of shared underlying byte array in Ti.Buffer
Description: """"Our current API for Ti.Buffer makes use of a {{byte[]}}. While https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11810 helps us to copy those bytes out to an {{ArrayBuffer}} on the JS side (though Ti.Blob), we should consider retooling {{Ti.Buffer}} to use a {{ByteBuffer}} with direct allocation pointing to the same exact memory shared by the JS engine's {{ArrayBuffer}}. This blog post makes reference to how the J2V8 project did exactly this: https://eclipsesource.com/blogs/2016/07/25/typedarrays-sharing-memory-between-v8-and-java/ Essentially this would involve Ti.Buffer wrapping a {{ByteBuffer}} rather than a {{byte[]}}. We could then read/write to the bytes from the native or JS side **without** crossing the JNI/V8 native bridge.""""",title+description
TIMOB-28037,12,"""iOS: Relative path require not working with node_modules""","""""""On iOS, when doing a relative path require from within a file that exists in node_modules, a runtime error occurs:  [ERROR]     message = """"""""Couldn't find module: ./subdir/test3 for architecture: x86_64"""""""";    I've created a standalone test project for this issue here:  https://github.com/<USER>TIMOB-28037  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Relative path require not working with node_modules
Description: """"On iOS, when doing a relative path require from within a file that exists in node_modules, a runtime error occurs: [ERROR] message = """"""""Couldn't find module: ./subdir/test3 for architecture: x86_64""""""""; I've created a standalone test project for this issue here: https://github.com/<USER>TIMOB-28037 """"",title+description
