TIMOB-27911,12,"""Android: ActiveTab not highlighted""","""""""The active tab is not highlighted. It does have the focus however an underline to highlight the active tab is missing.  This is is regression since 9.0.0.GA. It works fine in 8.3.1.GA    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a default classic app  2. Run it on an android device/emulator    Actual Result:  The active/selected tab is not highlighted. Check the attached images for difference between 8.3.1.GA and 9.0.X results.    Expected Result:  The active tab should be highlighted.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ActiveTab not highlighted
Description: """"The active tab is not highlighted. It does have the focus however an underline to highlight the active tab is missing. This is is regression since 9.0.0.GA. It works fine in 8.3.1.GA Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a default classic app 2. Run it on an android device/emulator Actual Result: The active/selected tab is not highlighted. Check the attached images for difference between 8.3.1.GA and 9.0.X results. Expected Result: The active tab should be highlighted.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27908,12,"""CLI: Add dist-inhouse deploy target""","""""""The """"""""dist-inhouse"""""""" is a new target for iOS builds. It sets the deploy type to """"""""production"""""""".    An """"""""In-house"""""""" provisioning profile is what we have been calling an """"""""enterprise ad hoc"""""""" profile. This is defined by the provisioning profile NOT containing a """"""""ProvisionedDevices"""""""" key and containing a """"""""ProvisionsAllDevices"""""""" key with a value of """"""""true"""""""".    ioslib shall continue to identify in-house provisioning profiles as """"""""enterprise"""""""" profiles.    """"""""dist-adhoc"""""""" currently lists both ad hoc and in-house profiles, but it should ONLY list ad hoc profiles. Furthermore, """"""""dist-adhoc"""""""" will be updated to allow a deploy type of """"""""test"""""""" as apart of TIMOB-13396.    All instances in the docs, help, and output should refer to """"""""enterprise"""""""" or """"""""enterprise ad hoc"""""""" as """"""""in-house"""""""".    """"""",Improvement,"Title: CLI: Add dist-inhouse deploy target
Description: """"The """"""""dist-inhouse"""""""" is a new target for iOS builds. It sets the deploy type to """"""""production"""""""". An """"""""In-house"""""""" provisioning profile is what we have been calling an """"""""enterprise ad hoc"""""""" profile. This is defined by the provisioning profile NOT containing a """"""""ProvisionedDevices"""""""" key and containing a """"""""ProvisionsAllDevices"""""""" key with a value of """"""""true"""""""". ioslib shall continue to identify in-house provisioning profiles as """"""""enterprise"""""""" profiles. """"""""dist-adhoc"""""""" currently lists both ad hoc and in-house profiles, but it should ONLY list ad hoc profiles. Furthermore, """"""""dist-adhoc"""""""" will be updated to allow a deploy type of """"""""test"""""""" as apart of TIMOB-13396. All instances in the docs, help, and output should refer to """"""""enterprise"""""""" or """"""""enterprise ad hoc"""""""" as """"""""in-house"""""""". """"",title+description
