TIMOB-27818,12,"""Decomission Docs & Guides on wiki""","""""""Decomission the wiki altogether and use the latest markdown export as the new """"""""source of truth"""""""" going forward for guide contents in Open Docs.""""""",Story,"Title: Decomission Docs & Guides on wiki
Description: """"Decomission the wiki altogether and use the latest markdown export as the new """"""""source of truth"""""""" going forward for guide contents in Open Docs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27817,12,"""Decommission docs.appcelerator.com""","""""""Once we have integrated with Open Docs and are comfortable with he published results/workflow/etc, we should decommission docs.appecelerator.com (by effectively having it redirect to the new pages at Open Docs or docs.axway.com)    Additionally we can then remove the solar server used to power searching on docs.<USER>com""""""",Story,"Title: Decommission docs.appcelerator.com
Description: """"Once we have integrated with Open Docs and are comfortable with he published results/workflow/etc, we should decommission docs.appecelerator.com (by effectively having it redirect to the new pages at Open Docs or docs.axway.com) Additionally we can then remove the solar server used to power searching on docs.<USER>com""""",title+description
TIMOB-27816,12,"""Remove outdated doc wiki guide contents""","""""""We have a significant number of outdated docs that we publish out. It would be useful to comb through and eliminate as many as we can before doing an initial push to the Open Docs repo.    This would lessen the size of the initial PR/commits and help avoid overwhelming the size of that repo.""""""",Story,"Title: Remove outdated doc wiki guide contents
Description: """"We have a significant number of outdated docs that we publish out. It would be useful to comb through and eliminate as many as we can before doing an initial push to the Open Docs repo. This would lessen the size of the initial PR/commits and help avoid overwhelming the size of that repo.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27815,12,"""Modify doctools Jenkins build to export Open Docs contents and push to repo/PR""","""""""Once we have scripts to generate the guides and/or APIDocs in a docsy-compatible markdown format - we should include ether conversion <USER>into our doctors build <USER>so that when contents change we automatically push the updated export to Open Docs.    We'll have to figure out what the <USER>is that would work best with that team:  - Open a new PR with the updated contents?  - Get commit rights to automatically check in updated contents and push?  - Work with their team to automate syncing updates to docs.axway.com  - Need to handle when we publish here and it goes to docs.axway.com vs the current axway push via crawling our wiki!""""""",Story,"Title: Modify doctools Jenkins build to export Open Docs contents and push to repo/PR
Description: """"Once we have scripts to generate the guides and/or APIDocs in a docsy-compatible markdown format - we should include ether conversion <USER>into our doctors build <USER>so that when contents change we automatically push the updated export to Open Docs. We'll have to figure out what the <USER>is that would work best with that team: - Open a new PR with the updated contents? - Get commit rights to automatically check in updated contents and push? - Work with their team to automate syncing updates to docs.axway.com - Need to handle when we publish here and it goes to docs.axway.com vs the current axway push via crawling our wiki!""""",title+description
TIMOB-27811,12,"""Refactor project creation to use template-kit and new project templates""","""""""We have a reusable template library called template-kit (https://github.com/<USER>template-kit). We also have a bunch of Titanium templates that template-kit can install (https://github.com/<USER>titanium-templates).    template-kit will be integrated into titaniumlib and used by the Titanium CLI v6 and Titanium appcd plugin.    However, it would be beneficial if the Titanium SDK was refactored to use template-kit directly or use titaniumlib's template-kit wrapper. This way template-kit (and possibly titaniumlib) would have more testing and users would have access to the new templates.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Refactor project creation to use template-kit and new project templates
Description: """"We have a reusable template library called template-kit (https://github.com/<USER>template-kit). We also have a bunch of Titanium templates that template-kit can install (https://github.com/<USER>titanium-templates). template-kit will be integrated into titaniumlib and used by the Titanium CLI v6 and Titanium appcd plugin. However, it would be beneficial if the Titanium SDK was refactored to use template-kit directly or use titaniumlib's template-kit wrapper. This way template-kit (and possibly titaniumlib) would have more testing and users would have access to the new templates.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27804,12,"""Front camera and cancel button option missing while open camera using ti.barcode module""","""""""The front camera and cancel button missing on open barcode camera.         Please suggest how to fix this issue     Attached screenshot  """"""",Bug,"Title: Front camera and cancel button option missing while open camera using ti.barcode module
Description: """"The front camera and cancel button missing on open barcode camera. Please suggest how to fix this issue Attached screenshot """"",title+description
TIMOB-27802,12,"""Add parity to Android TabGroup by allowing navigation window stack within each tab""","""""""NOTE:  This is the original intent of this related ticket. NavigationWindow in TabWindow.  That ticket has changed into having a TabWindow in a NavigationWindow, which is something different.       https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-27316    ———————    Currently, if you are using BottomTab on Android, and you open a new window using {{activeTab.open()}}, it will open a new window on top of everything and cover up all the whole BottomTab UI.    This feature is to add parity with iOS where it can use the NavigationWindow within a Tab so that the BottomTab group is still functional and you have a history of tabs like you do on iOS.    This would be a *+HUGE+* plus as currently you still have to use a custom BottomTab type implementation or some other workaround if you want to be able to use Tab navigation.     If you are looking for an example of a platform native Android app that uses features like this, I believe the Tesco Android app does this.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Add parity to Android TabGroup by allowing navigation window stack within each tab
Description: """"NOTE: This is the original intent of this related ticket. NavigationWindow in TabWindow. That ticket has changed into having a TabWindow in a NavigationWindow, which is something different. https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-27316 ——————— Currently, if you are using BottomTab on Android, and you open a new window using {{activeTab.open()}}, it will open a new window on top of everything and cover up all the whole BottomTab UI. This feature is to add parity with iOS where it can use the NavigationWindow within a Tab so that the BottomTab group is still functional and you have a history of tabs like you do on iOS. This would be a *+HUGE+* plus as currently you still have to use a custom BottomTab type implementation or some other workaround if you want to be able to use Tab navigation. If you are looking for an example of a platform native Android app that uses features like this, I believe the Tesco Android app does this.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27800,12,"""Webpack: Angular plugin""","""""""Adopt the existing [webpack configuration|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/templates/app/angular-default/template/app/webpack.config.js] for Titanium Angular apps to work in [appcd-plugin-webpack|https://github.com/<USER>appcd-plugin-webpack].""""""",New Feature,"Title: Webpack: Angular plugin
Description: """"Adopt the existing [webpack configuration|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/templates/app/angular-default/template/app/webpack.config.js] for Titanium Angular apps to work in [appcd-plugin-webpack|https://github.com/<USER>appcd-plugin-webpack].""""",title+description
TIMOB-27799,12,"""ios: App crashes when setting video player url to null""","""""""When we try to set the URL of an existing video player to null the app crashes on iOS.  No crash seen on Android.    The issue occurs since Ti SDK 8.2.0.GA.    Steps To Reproduce:  1. Create a classic app. Use the app.js attached   2. Install on iOS. When the app launches the video player starts playing  3. Click on the """"""""Close Video"""""""" button on the bottom right    Actual Result:  The app crashes with following error   """"""",Bug,"Title: ios: App crashes when setting video player url to null
Description: """"When we try to set the URL of an existing video player to null the app crashes on iOS. No crash seen on Android. The issue occurs since Ti SDK 8.2.0.GA. Steps To Reproduce: 1. Create a classic app. Use the app.js attached 2. Install on iOS. When the app launches the video player starts playing 3. Click on the """"""""Close Video"""""""" button on the bottom right Actual Result: The app crashes with following error """"",title+description
TIMOB-27795,12,"""Android: WebView crashes when given local HTML URL with parameters as of 8.1.0""","""""""Since SDK version 8.1.0 I have been unable to specify a URL for a webview that uses a local HTML file with variables in the URL. I pass things like the UDID and other variables to a local HTML file in an Android app. This worked fine up till SDK 8.0.2. It says the file is not found when I add any variable to the local file. Using a remote file has no issue.         The above example fails to run with the following error, I have tired with every SDK after 8.0.2.       """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView crashes when given local HTML URL with parameters as of 8.1.0
Description: """"Since SDK version 8.1.0 I have been unable to specify a URL for a webview that uses a local HTML file with variables in the URL. I pass things like the UDID and other variables to a local HTML file in an Android app. This worked fine up till SDK 8.0.2. It says the file is not found when I add any variable to the local file. Using a remote file has no issue. The above example fails to run with the following error, I have tired with every SDK after 8.0.2. """"",title+description
