TIMOB-27555,12,"""Allow PRs to be tagged with label to enable more exhaustive testing""","""""""We should enable a way to flag specific PRs so that more exhaustive testing is performed.    We have been playing with changing deploy types used by the test suite, as well as adding iPad Simulator recently. But we haven't formalized what exact matrix of testing should occur regularly on PRs or master.    We run tests on 3 android devices on master builds. We have no iOS devices running on any build nodes.    Specifically, we should be able to add a tag to our Github PRs that should allow them to be tested on devices in addition to our typical simulator/emulator testing. That way we can flag only very specific PRs that we think may touch something like encryption, or may be a high impact change to do more extensive testing without necessarily having every single PR go through it.  """"""",Story,"Title: Allow PRs to be tagged with label to enable more exhaustive testing
Description: """"We should enable a way to flag specific PRs so that more exhaustive testing is performed. We have been playing with changing deploy types used by the test suite, as well as adding iPad Simulator recently. But we haven't formalized what exact matrix of testing should occur regularly on PRs or master. We run tests on 3 android devices on master builds. We have no iOS devices running on any build nodes. Specifically, we should be able to add a tag to our Github PRs that should allow them to be tested on devices in addition to our typical simulator/emulator testing. That way we can flag only very specific PRs that we think may touch something like encryption, or may be a high impact change to do more extensive testing without necessarily having every single PR go through it. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27535,12,"""Unexpected text and title in Appium Studio after setting accessibilityLabel to Label and PickerRow""","""""""We have added accessibilityLabel to UI Label or UI PickerView to locate these elements in Automation Testing. After adding accessibilityLabel can't read label text or picker row title. Instead of text and title accessibilityLabel is showing in Appium studio. Please refer attached screenshot. Is it expected behaviour? Do we have any alternate to overcome this issue.    Note: Setting accessibilityLabel to text input is working fine.""""""",Story,"Title: Unexpected text and title in Appium Studio after setting accessibilityLabel to Label and PickerRow
Description: """"We have added accessibilityLabel to UI Label or UI PickerView to locate these elements in Automation Testing. After adding accessibilityLabel can't read label text or picker row title. Instead of text and title accessibilityLabel is showing in Appium studio. Please refer attached screenshot. Is it expected behaviour? Do we have any alternate to overcome this issue. Note: Setting accessibilityLabel to text input is working fine.""""",title+description
