TIMOB-27499,12,"""Android: TableView doesn't trigger the click event views scrolled off/in as of 8.1.0""","""""""I have a tableview with several rows containing views and labels.  If the rows are all visible in the window, I can trigger the click event in the tableview.   If instead I have more elements, as soon as I scroll, I can no longer trigger the click event on the first rows, but only on the final ones.    It works with SDK 8.0.1 and 8.0.2        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView doesn't trigger the click event views scrolled off/in as of 8.1.0
Description: """"I have a tableview with several rows containing views and labels. If the rows are all visible in the window, I can trigger the click event in the tableview. If instead I have more elements, as soon as I scroll, I can no longer trigger the click event on the first rows, but only on the final ones. It works with SDK 8.0.1 and 8.0.2 """"",title+description
