TIMOB-27494,12,"""Add support for iOS Dynamic System Colors""","""""""https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/ios/visual-design/color/#dynamic-system-colors    Apple has added Dynamic System Colors that adapt to both light and dark UI modes.      iOS defines two sets of background colors—system and grouped—each of which contains primary, secondary, and tertiary variants that help you convey a hierarchy of information. In general, use the grouped set of background colors when you have a grouped table view; otherwise, use the system set of background colors. """"""",New Feature,"Title: Add support for iOS Dynamic System Colors
Description: """"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/ios/visual-design/color/#dynamic-system-colors Apple has added Dynamic System Colors that adapt to both light and dark UI modes. iOS defines two sets of background colors—system and grouped—each of which contains primary, secondary, and tertiary variants that help you convey a hierarchy of information. In general, use the grouped set of background colors when you have a grouped table view; otherwise, use the system set of background colors. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27492,12,"""Searchbar issue on tableView with latest iOS SDK""","""""""The customer is facing an issue with searchbar on tableView with latest iOS SDK.  When search bar is clicked rest of the tableview is greyed out and user has to tap twice to remove keyboard and then the gray area.  This is causing major issue with their users are they need to mark items quickly to move on to next inspection item.  Kindly look into this and let they know how to proceed.    Sample Code: Check attachments section    *Steps to Reproduce:*    1. Download the sample project  2. Import the project via studio and run  3. When the search bar is clicked rest of the tableview is greyed out. And need to tap twice to remove the keyboard and then the gray area.    *Note: We also tested this on our end with SDK 8.2.0.GA (iphone SE 13.1.3) and able to reproduce the issue. Please check the attachment section for sample test project and screenshots.*""""""",Story,"Title: Searchbar issue on tableView with latest iOS SDK
Description: """"The customer is facing an issue with searchbar on tableView with latest iOS SDK. When search bar is clicked rest of the tableview is greyed out and user has to tap twice to remove keyboard and then the gray area. This is causing major issue with their users are they need to mark items quickly to move on to next inspection item. Kindly look into this and let they know how to proceed. Sample Code: Check attachments section *Steps to Reproduce:* 1. Download the sample project 2. Import the project via studio and run 3. When the search bar is clicked rest of the tableview is greyed out. And need to tap twice to remove the keyboard and then the gray area. *Note: We also tested this on our end with SDK 8.2.0.GA (iphone SE 13.1.3) and able to reproduce the issue. Please check the attachment section for sample test project and screenshots.*""""",title+description
TIMOB-27490,12,"""iOS: Cannot build to iOS with latest 8.2.1 build""","""""""When trying to build a default classic or alloy project to iOS simulator or device it errors out during with the latest 8.2.1 SDK build.    Steps to Reproduce  1. Create a default classic/alloy project  2. Build to iOS    Actual Result:  An error is shown      Expected Result:  The build to iOS simulator and device should be successful.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot build to iOS with latest 8.2.1 build
