TIMOB-27301,12,"""CLI: Block scoped variables in for loops are attempted to be added to the global scope""","""""""h5.Description    When using a for loop in the top level scope (i.e. not in a function) of an app.js or alloy.js file if the variable declaration used is a block scoped variable (const/let) the below error will be thrown. This is because we try to use add the level to the global scope, but as it is block scope we can't reference it outside of the for loop.    *workaround*: Use {{var}} to declare the variable, or move the code into a function and call that.    *Note*: I believe by default this will only be seen on Android as babel will convert const/let to var on iOS        h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Add the below code to your app.js    2. Build to android    h5.Actual    App will crash with above error    h5.Expected    App should not crash""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Block scoped variables in for loops are attempted to be added to the global scope
Description: """"h5.Description When using a for loop in the top level scope (i.e. not in a function) of an app.js or alloy.js file if the variable declaration used is a block scoped variable (const/let) the below error will be thrown. This is because we try to use add the level to the global scope, but as it is block scope we can't reference it outside of the for loop. *workaround*: Use {{var}} to declare the variable, or move the code into a function and call that. *Note*: I believe by default this will only be seen on Android as babel will convert const/let to var on iOS h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Add the below code to your app.js 2. Build to android h5.Actual App will crash with above error h5.Expected App should not crash""""",title+description
TIMOB-27299,12,"""Camera access from WebView, causing permission error. ""","""""""Hello, I am trying to run a video-chat page inside of a webview. Below is the code I have   index.xml    index.js    index.tss    alloy.js      Also in my tiapp.xml I have the permission set for camera and microphone         Now, After the app opens, when I click on the 'click to start video chat' button inside of the webview, In Android, I get the attached error in my console:        In both iOS and Android, the attached image error in the screen shows up. I can load the URL in Safari and it works. After I click, a dialog opens for accessing camera and microphone, this dialog is not showing up in the <USER>app. What's the issue here?     Tested this issue with the above environment. The issue was reproducible. Thanks.""""""",Bug,"Title: Camera access from WebView, causing permission error.
Description: """"Hello, I am trying to run a video-chat page inside of a webview. Below is the code I have index.xml index.js index.tss alloy.js Also in my tiapp.xml I have the permission set for camera and microphone Now, After the app opens, when I click on the 'click to start video chat' button inside of the webview, In Android, I get the attached error in my console: In both iOS and Android, the attached image error in the screen shows up. I can load the URL in Safari and it works. After I click, a dialog opens for accessing camera and microphone, this dialog is not showing up in the <USER>app. What's the issue here? Tested this issue with the above environment. The issue was reproducible. Thanks.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27295,12,"""When distributing iOS app via testflight certain core js files are missing""","""""""When running on the device over cable, the build is fine  When building for distribution and then installing to iOS over test flight we get app hangs and the following in the console:        If we to an appc ti clean, it works fine on testflight builds. It seems like something is being left behind/ not being rebuilt when doing a build for distribution.  """"""",Bug,"Title: When distributing iOS app via testflight certain core js files are missing
Description: """"When running on the device over cable, the build is fine When building for distribution and then installing to iOS over test flight we get app hangs and the following in the console: If we to an appc ti clean, it works fine on testflight builds. It seems like something is being left behind/ not being rebuilt when doing a build for distribution. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27294,12,"""iOS: When multiple Xcode versions are installed unclear errors are shown when using a Sim linked to a different xcode""","""""""With Xcode 11 beta 3 installed and having Xcode 10.2.1 selected whenever I try build to iOS 13 I get the following error: (I get the same error if I have Xcode 11 beta 3 selected and try to run a iOS 12.2 emulator (all other emulators work fine)).        *Example Test steps (Xcode 11 Beta 3 and Xcode 10.3 ):*  # Have two versions of Xcode installed (preferably xcode 11 beta 3 and 10.3 as they are the latest)  # Make sure xcode 11 beta 3 is selected from the system e.g. {{sudo xcode-select -switch <path/to/>Xcode.app}}  # Try to run a simulator linked to Xcode 10.3 (in this instance 12.4 Sims)    The following message is then shown in the console:       """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: When multiple Xcode versions are installed unclear errors are shown when using a Sim linked to a different xcode
Description: """"With Xcode 11 beta 3 installed and having Xcode 10.2.1 selected whenever I try build to iOS 13 I get the following error: (I get the same error if I have Xcode 11 beta 3 selected and try to run a iOS 12.2 emulator (all other emulators work fine)). *Example Test steps (Xcode 11 Beta 3 and Xcode 10.3 ):* # Have two versions of Xcode installed (preferably xcode 11 beta 3 and 10.3 as they are the latest) # Make sure xcode 11 beta 3 is selected from the system e.g. {{sudo xcode-select -switch <path/to/>Xcode.app}} # Try to run a simulator linked to Xcode 10.3 (in this instance 12.4 Sims) The following message is then shown in the console: """"",title+description
TIMOB-27292,12,"""iOS: App crashes on startup on iOS 9""","""""""h5.Description    When building to an iOS 9 simulator/device the app crashes on startup with the below, I believe this is due to the ios version change in [this commit|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/8cac1f88cb226c36a4b9be6e4dee0beffda9b4ce#diff-09cce02f0aa7063f10a4c555dc65a141R23], as this is used to pass in the min iOS version to babel [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/a48d707984e88e92f05287dcd3c2588025c9c9f2/build/lib/packager.js#L88] which means we're probably dropping some polyfills that are required. I'm not too sure why we have {{minIosVersion}} and a supported ios version range.        h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Create a basic app, classic or alloy  2. Build the app to an iOS 9 simulator or device    h5.Actual    App crashes on startup    h5.Expected    App should not crash""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App crashes on startup on iOS 9
Description: """"h5.Description When building to an iOS 9 simulator/device the app crashes on startup with the below, I believe this is due to the ios version change in [this commit|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/8cac1f88cb226c36a4b9be6e4dee0beffda9b4ce#diff-09cce02f0aa7063f10a4c555dc65a141R23], as this is used to pass in the min iOS version to babel [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/a48d707984e88e92f05287dcd3c2588025c9c9f2/build/lib/packager.js#L88] which means we're probably dropping some polyfills that are required. I'm not too sure why we have {{minIosVersion}} and a supported ios version range. h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Create a basic app, classic or alloy 2. Build the app to an iOS 9 simulator or device h5.Actual App crashes on startup h5.Expected App should not crash""""",title+description
TIMOB-27291,12,"""TiAPI: Create Node-compatible zlib module API""","""""""It'd be useful to create equivalents of some of the core Node modules in Titanium so that users could port/re-use node codebases on mobile devices. Some of the more common modules could map relatively easily to devices, and would be worth investigating.    https://nodejs.org/api/zlib.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Create Node-compatible zlib module API
Description: """"It'd be useful to create equivalents of some of the core Node modules in Titanium so that users could port/re-use node codebases on mobile devices. Some of the more common modules could map relatively easily to devices, and would be worth investigating. https://nodejs.org/api/zlib.html""""",title+description
TIMOB-27290,12,"""TiAPI: Create Node-compatible https module API""","""""""It'd be useful to create equivalents of some of the core Node modules in Titanium so that users could port/re-use node codebases on mobile devices. Some of the more common modules could map relatively easily to devices, and would be worth investigating.    https://nodejs.org/api/https.html    Some of the http module - specifically the http client - could map to similar APIs as our existing docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Create Node-compatible https module API
Description: """"It'd be useful to create equivalents of some of the core Node modules in Titanium so that users could port/re-use node codebases on mobile devices. Some of the more common modules could map relatively easily to devices, and would be worth investigating. https://nodejs.org/api/https.html Some of the http module - specifically the http client - could map to similar APIs as our existing docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient""""",title+description
