TIMOB-27258,12,"""Android: Background Gradient does not work on Ti.UI.Android.CardView""","""""""Our CI highly relies on card-views to create well-shaped rounded views with a background gradient. Unfortunately, this does not work on Android:  {code:js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();    var cardView = Ti.UI.Android.createCardView({      width: 200,      height: 200,      backgroundGradient: {          type: 'linear',          colors: ['#6AECD5', '#50DBB8'],          startPoint: { x: '50%', y: 0 },          endPoint: { x: '50%', y: '100%' },          backFillStart: false      }  });    win.add(cardView);  win.open();  {code}    It works fine on iOS and other views like Ti.UI.View or Ti.UI.Button, but those cannot be used because of the rounded / shadowed combination.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Background Gradient does not work on Ti.UI.Android.CardView
Description: """"Our CI highly relies on card-views to create well-shaped rounded views with a background gradient. Unfortunately, this does not work on Android: {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var cardView = Ti.UI.Android.createCardView({ width: 200, height: 200, backgroundGradient: { type: 'linear', colors: ['#6AECD5', '#50DBB8'], startPoint: { x: '50%', y: 0 }, endPoint: { x: '50%', y: '100%' }, backFillStart: false } }); win.add(cardView); win.open(); {code} It works fine on iOS and other views like Ti.UI.View or Ti.UI.Button, but those cannot be used because of the rounded / shadowed combination.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27255,12,"""Titanium CLI plugin deprecation notices""","""""""There are 2 major Titanium CLI <=5.x plugin related deprecations coming up with the release of the next Titanium CLI, namely version 6.0.    1. Titanium CLI 6 will drop support for all Titanium CLI plugins that are executed for any command other than {{""""""""ti build""""""""}} (or {{""""""""appc run""""""""}}). That means that any plugin that was loaded for a non-build command, such as """"""""create""""""""/""""""""new"""""""", will no longer be loaded in Titanium CLI 6.    * Hooks that will only fire when performing a build  ** {{cli:command-loaded}}  ** {{cli:go}}  ** {{cli:post-execute}}  ** {{cli:post-validate}}  ** {{cli:pre-execute}}  ** {{cli:pre-validate}}  ** {{help:header}}  * Hooks that will no longer be called  ** {{clean.config}}  ** {{clean.post}}  ** {{clean.pre}}  ** {{create.config}}  ** {{create.finalize}}  ** {{create.post}}  ** {{create.pre}}    All other {{build.*}} hooks will continue to fire including Alloy, Hyperloop, Liveview, Ti.shadow, etc.    2. Titanium CLI 7 will drop support for all Titanium CLI plugins including """"""""build"""""""" related commands.    h2. New Titanium CLI 6 Plugin System    The new Titanium CLI 6 will support plugins in the form of Appc Daemon (appcd) plugins. While the daemon's plugin system exists as well as the underlying hook mechanism, the hook registration system (DAEMON-90) does not exist yet.    Once the hook system is implemented in the appcd plugin system, then Titanium CLI <=5.x plugins with {{clean.*}} and {{create.*}} hooks will need to be ported to the new format. Porting is not trivial, but it's hours, not days, of work.    Appcd plugins also have limitations compared to Titanium CLI <=5.x plugins. While pre and post hooks are possible, modifying function hook arguments, the actual hooked function, and the result are not. Furthermore, appcd plugins must be async aware and maintain their own state.    Currently, there are no known plugins that use the {{clean.*}} hooks, however we have several new project templates that use the {{create.*}} hooks. Those project templates will need to be updated.    h2. Titanium CLI 7 Plugin Support    With Ti CLI 7, all Titanium CLI <=5.x plugins will no longer work and thus must be ported. Plugins such as Alloy, Hyperloop, and Liveview will need to be ported to appcd plugins. This is a big effort, however Titanium CLI 7 likely won't ship until the 2nd half of 2020. We have time.    h2. References    https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/Titanium+CLI+Plugins  """"""",Story,"Title: Titanium CLI plugin deprecation notices
Description: """"There are 2 major Titanium CLI <=5.x plugin related deprecations coming up with the release of the next Titanium CLI, namely version 6.0. 1. Titanium CLI 6 will drop support for all Titanium CLI plugins that are executed for any command other than {{""""""""ti build""""""""}} (or {{""""""""appc run""""""""}}). That means that any plugin that was loaded for a non-build command, such as """"""""create""""""""/""""""""new"""""""", will no longer be loaded in Titanium CLI 6. * Hooks that will only fire when performing a build ** {{cli:command-loaded}} ** {{cli:go}} ** {{cli:post-execute}} ** {{cli:post-validate}} ** {{cli:pre-execute}} ** {{cli:pre-validate}} ** {{help:header}} * Hooks that will no longer be called ** {{clean.config}} ** {{clean.post}} ** {{clean.pre}} ** {{create.config}} ** {{create.finalize}} ** {{create.post}} ** {{create.pre}} All other {{build.*}} hooks will continue to fire including Alloy, Hyperloop, Liveview, Ti.shadow, etc. 2. Titanium CLI 7 will drop support for all Titanium CLI plugins including """"""""build"""""""" related commands. h2. New Titanium CLI 6 Plugin System The new Titanium CLI 6 will support plugins in the form of Appc Daemon (appcd) plugins. While the daemon's plugin system exists as well as the underlying hook mechanism, the hook registration system (DAEMON-90) does not exist yet. Once the hook system is implemented in the appcd plugin system, then Titanium CLI <=5.x plugins with {{clean.*}} and {{create.*}} hooks will need to be ported to the new format. Porting is not trivial, but it's hours, not days, of work. Appcd plugins also have limitations compared to Titanium CLI <=5.x plugins. While pre and post hooks are possible, modifying function hook arguments, the actual hooked function, and the result are not. Furthermore, appcd plugins must be async aware and maintain their own state. Currently, there are no known plugins that use the {{clean.*}} hooks, however we have several new project templates that use the {{create.*}} hooks. Those project templates will need to be updated. h2. Titanium CLI 7 Plugin Support With Ti CLI 7, all Titanium CLI <=5.x plugins will no longer work and thus must be ported. Plugins such as Alloy, Hyperloop, and Liveview will need to be ported to appcd plugins. This is a big effort, however Titanium CLI 7 likely won't ship until the 2nd half of 2020. We have time. h2. References https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/Titanium+CLI+Plugins """"",title+description
TIMOB-27254,12,"""[iOS] WebView click event is not being fired""","""""""Webview click event is not being fired when the parent window also has a click event. (Works fine on Android).    *app.js*      *Test steps*  # Create a titanium application with the above test case  # Run the program   # Tap on """"""""click me"""""""" label.    *Expected result*  Three alerts appear on screen with messages """"""""123456"""""""",""""""""WebView Clicked"""""""" and """"""""Window clicked"""""""".     *Actual result*  Only one alert can be seen, """"""""WebView Clicked"""""""". """"""",Bug,"Title: [iOS] WebView click event is not being fired
Description: """"Webview click event is not being fired when the parent window also has a click event. (Works fine on Android). *app.js* *Test steps* # Create a titanium application with the above test case # Run the program # Tap on """"""""click me"""""""" label. *Expected result* Three alerts appear on screen with messages """"""""123456"""""""",""""""""WebView Clicked"""""""" and """"""""Window clicked"""""""". *Actual result* Only one alert can be seen, """"""""WebView Clicked"""""""". """"",title+description
TIMOB-27252,12,"""Hyperloop: Implement instabug sdk in appcelerator app for android and IOS""","""""""The customer is trying to implement instabug sdk in <USER>app for android and IOS both. They are using real device and Xcode version 10.2.1.    *iOS:*     They followed all the steps from [here|https://instabug.com/platforms/ios] . Inclusion of pod file didn't work correctly. They have manually downloaded the framework and placed it under the platform/ios directory and that trick worked.       This statement also works as statement provided below also works.      Only thing they are not able to do is they are suppose to pass IBGInvocationEventShake.     [Instabug startWithToken:@""""""""YOUR-TOKEN-HERE"""""""" invocationEvents: IBGInvocationEventShake | IBGInvocationEventScreenshot];    Note:       *Android:*    While adding instabug on android, getting details about android sdk integration based in below [url|https://docs.instabug.com/docs/android-integration#section-maven]. They are using SDK - 8.0.2 hyperloop - 4.0.2  android API 26. They are facing below issues:  1. *build.gradle* is not working as mentioned in https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/Android+Hyperloop+Programming+Guide.   2.  Downloaded all the jars mentioned in gradle manually. Then  getting below error.  Attaching all the jars that they have included just for references.   3. When they researched this is related to android snackbar but since they are not able to use gradle they can't add gradle script for snackbar as well.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: Implement instabug sdk in appcelerator app for android and IOS
Description: """"The customer is trying to implement instabug sdk in <USER>app for android and IOS both. They are using real device and Xcode version 10.2.1. *iOS:* They followed all the steps from [here|https://instabug.com/platforms/ios] . Inclusion of pod file didn't work correctly. They have manually downloaded the framework and placed it under the platform/ios directory and that trick worked. This statement also works as statement provided below also works. Only thing they are not able to do is they are suppose to pass IBGInvocationEventShake. [Instabug startWithToken:@""""""""YOUR-TOKEN-HERE"""""""" invocationEvents: IBGInvocationEventShake | IBGInvocationEventScreenshot]; Note: *Android:* While adding instabug on android, getting details about android sdk integration based in below [url|https://docs.instabug.com/docs/android-integration#section-maven]. They are using SDK - 8.0.2 hyperloop - 4.0.2 android API 26. They are facing below issues: 1. *build.gradle* is not working as mentioned in https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/Android+Hyperloop+Programming+Guide. 2. Downloaded all the jars mentioned in gradle manually. Then getting below error. Attaching all the jars that they have included just for references. 3. When they researched this is related to android snackbar but since they are not able to use gradle they can't add gradle script for snackbar as well. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27251,12,"""iOS: require in native module assets fails""","""""""*Steps to reproduce the behavior*    # Add the [<USER>syncserver.client|https://github.com/<USER>modules/<USER>syncserver.client] module to a project  # Require the module in the app: {{const client = require('<USER>syncserver.client');}}  # Build and run app    *Actual behavior*  The following error is thrown:      *Expected behavior*  The module loads without issues.    *Notes*  This is most likely related to incorrect handling in [tryNativeModule|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/c465e92795ddaf8eb4ae44319df00e98bd4b3a10/iphone/TitaniumKit/TitaniumKit/Sources/API/KrollBridge.m#L1163]. The module requires {{<USER>syncserver.client/jsdeferred.js}}, which will be split into module id and asset path. Only the asset path will be passed to {{ResolvedModule}} though, which causes  [loadCoreModuleAsset|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/c465e92795ddaf8eb4ae44319df00e98bd4b3a10/iphone/TitaniumKit/TitaniumKit/Sources/API/KrollBridge.m#L802] to throw.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: require in native module assets fails
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce the behavior* # Add the [<USER>syncserver.client|https://github.com/<USER>modules/<USER>syncserver.client] module to a project # Require the module in the app: {{const client = require('<USER>syncserver.client');}} # Build and run app *Actual behavior* The following error is thrown: *Expected behavior* The module loads without issues. *Notes* This is most likely related to incorrect handling in [tryNativeModule|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/c465e92795ddaf8eb4ae44319df00e98bd4b3a10/iphone/TitaniumKit/TitaniumKit/Sources/API/KrollBridge.m#L1163]. The module requires {{<USER>syncserver.client/jsdeferred.js}}, which will be split into module id and asset path. Only the asset path will be passed to {{ResolvedModule}} though, which causes [loadCoreModuleAsset|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/c465e92795ddaf8eb4ae44319df00e98bd4b3a10/iphone/TitaniumKit/TitaniumKit/Sources/API/KrollBridge.m#L802] to throw.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27245,12,"""Android: App crashes on Huawei devices""","""""""We are currently noticing some crashes on Huawei devices (see device logs) related to play-services.    We are using a fork of [Ti.GoogleSignIn|https://github.com/hansemannn/Ti.GoogleSignIn-Android/tree/parity] that seems to trigger the crash, but I think the root issue is the activity handling of Titanium. A rough confirmation would be great!    *EDIT*: We might just need to add some config from [here|https://stackoverflow.com/a/34007675/5537752] to make it work. Sorry for being a bit fast on this one, it can probably be closed.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: App crashes on Huawei devices
Description: """"We are currently noticing some crashes on Huawei devices (see device logs) related to play-services. We are using a fork of [Ti.GoogleSignIn|https://github.com/hansemannn/Ti.GoogleSignIn-Android/tree/parity] that seems to trigger the crash, but I think the root issue is the activity handling of Titanium. A rough confirmation would be great! *EDIT*: We might just need to add some config from [here|https://stackoverflow.com/a/34007675/5537752] to make it work. Sorry for being a bit fast on this one, it can probably be closed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27244,12,"""Opening window in Ti.UI.Tab randomly results in black screen""","""""""*Summary;*  One of our apps suffers from windows appearing black randomly. Navbar & Tabbar stay functional.  No exception, error or even warning is thrown and navigating back & forth renders the window normally again.    Attached are a video and a screenshot demonstrating the issue. We tried but could not create a sample app that repproduces our issue.    The view is opened in the tab by calling;      *Full Description;*  In one of our production apps we're having a problem where sometimes a window transitions into the view completely black. Only the navigation bar and tab bar are visible to the user. The UX is as follows; When the user is on the """"""""Product Categories"""""""" list view and taps a row, the """"""""Product Category"""""""" view is opened, displaying products from that category. Usually this works as expected, however occasionally the """"""""Product Category"""""""" window is completely black.    The odd thing is that whenever the """"""""Product Category"""""""" window is blacked out there are **no** strange logs, the navbar & tabbar are functional, and returning to the """"""""Product Categories"""""""" view, and reopening the """"""""Product Category"""""""" will work as expected.    Because we can't consistently replicate the issue it's been difficult to fix. Initial thoughts were a memory leak, but after some refactoring the app stays well below 100Mb memory usage.    Even after compiling and running the app through Xcode, there are no strange logs indicating that the window can't render properly. We've tried compiling with `KMETHOD_DEBUG` & `KOBJECT_MEMORY_DEBUG` enabled, unfortionately this resulted in to many logs so we weren't able to get to the black screen with those enabeld.    This issue ([AC-5979|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/AC-5979]) seems pretty much identical to the issue that we're having. As stated by @<USER>in [this comment|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/AC-5979?focusedCommentId=442687&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-442687], the issue is very hard to replicate.    Without any warning, error or exception message finding other related issues or possible cause has been difficult.""""""",Bug,"Title: Opening window in Ti.UI.Tab randomly results in black screen
Description: """"*Summary;* One of our apps suffers from windows appearing black randomly. Navbar & Tabbar stay functional. No exception, error or even warning is thrown and navigating back & forth renders the window normally again. Attached are a video and a screenshot demonstrating the issue. We tried but could not create a sample app that repproduces our issue. The view is opened in the tab by calling; *Full Description;* In one of our production apps we're having a problem where sometimes a window transitions into the view completely black. Only the navigation bar and tab bar are visible to the user. The UX is as follows; When the user is on the """"""""Product Categories"""""""" list view and taps a row, the """"""""Product Category"""""""" view is opened, displaying products from that category. Usually this works as expected, however occasionally the """"""""Product Category"""""""" window is completely black. The odd thing is that whenever the """"""""Product Category"""""""" window is blacked out there are **no** strange logs, the navbar & tabbar are functional, and returning to the """"""""Product Categories"""""""" view, and reopening the """"""""Product Category"""""""" will work as expected. Because we can't consistently replicate the issue it's been difficult to fix. Initial thoughts were a memory leak, but after some refactoring the app stays well below 100Mb memory usage. Even after compiling and running the app through Xcode, there are no strange logs indicating that the window can't render properly. We've tried compiling with `KMETHOD_DEBUG` & `KOBJECT_MEMORY_DEBUG` enabled, unfortionately this resulted in to many logs so we weren't able to get to the black screen with those enabeld. This issue ([AC-5979|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/AC-5979]) seems pretty much identical to the issue that we're having. As stated by @<USER>in [this comment|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/AC-5979?focusedCommentId=442687&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-442687], the issue is very hard to replicate. Without any warning, error or exception message finding other related issues or possible cause has been difficult.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27241,12,"""iOS: WebView html fails to reload local JavaScript after unload""","""""""*Describe the bug*  I've a WebView in a ScrollableView. The WebView loads a local html file and a js file. When you scroll to the 3rd or 4th view the WebView will unload its content and it will be reloaded when you go back to the 1st view. This was working fine before 8.0.0.GA. But starting 8.0.0.GA the local JavaScript functions aren't available in the html file after the reload.    *To Reproduce*  # Press 'Tab 5'  # Press 'Tab 1'  # Read the console output    +assets/html/test.html+      assets/html/test.jslocal      +views/index.xml+      +controllers/index.js+      *Expected behavior*  The console output reads 'talk to me! function'    *Actual behavior*  The console output reads 'talk to me! undefined'    *Environment*  iOS; 8.0.0.GA; 8.0.1.GA; 8.0.2.GA""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: WebView html fails to reload local JavaScript after unload
Description: """"*Describe the bug* I've a WebView in a ScrollableView. The WebView loads a local html file and a js file. When you scroll to the 3rd or 4th view the WebView will unload its content and it will be reloaded when you go back to the 1st view. This was working fine before 8.0.0.GA. But starting 8.0.0.GA the local JavaScript functions aren't available in the html file after the reload. *To Reproduce* # Press 'Tab 5' # Press 'Tab 1' # Read the console output +assets/html/test.html+ assets/html/test.jslocal +views/index.xml+ +controllers/index.js+ *Expected behavior* The console output reads 'talk to me! function' *Actual behavior* The console output reads 'talk to me! undefined' *Environment* iOS; 8.0.0.GA; 8.0.1.GA; 8.0.2.GA""""",title+description
TIMOB-27239,12,"""TextField padding property uses different units between Android and iOS""","""""""*Problem*  Adding the same padding to a TextField on Android and iOS leads to different results.  It seems that Android uses pixels beacuse on phones with different densities you have different sizes of padding using the same digit. Instead iOS uses dp (correctly beacuse default unit in tiapp.xml is dp).    *Test case*  # Execute below code  # Padding (focus only on left and right beacuse top and bottom aren't working on iOS) is different between Android (smaller) and iOS (bigger).    {code:title=index.js}  $.win.open();      {code:title=index.tss}  """"""""#win"""""""": {   backgroundColor: 'black'  }    """"""""#field"""""""": {   height: Ti.UI.SIZE,   width: Ti.UI.SIZE,   top: 32,   backgroundColor: 'red',   padding: {    top: 32,    bottom: 32,    right: 32,    left: 32,   },   value: 'Test Test Test Test'  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: TextField padding property uses different units between Android and iOS
Description: """"*Problem* Adding the same padding to a TextField on Android and iOS leads to different results. It seems that Android uses pixels beacuse on phones with different densities you have different sizes of padding using the same digit. Instead iOS uses dp (correctly beacuse default unit in tiapp.xml is dp). *Test case* # Execute below code # Padding (focus only on left and right beacuse top and bottom aren't working on iOS) is different between Android (smaller) and iOS (bigger). {code:title=index.js} $.win.open(); {code:title=index.tss} """"""""#win"""""""": { backgroundColor: 'black' } """"""""#field"""""""": { height: Ti.UI.SIZE, width: Ti.UI.SIZE, top: 32, backgroundColor: 'red', padding: { top: 32, bottom: 32, right: 32, left: 32, }, value: 'Test Test Test Test' } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-27238,12,"""Android: Allow """"onlink"""" property to be set for first time after creating WebView""","""""""*Summary:*  On Android, the {{WebView}} """"""""onlink"""""""" callback property currently must be assigned upon creation in order for it to work. It cannot be set after creation. (However, the """"""""onlink"""""""" property can be changed after assigned upon creation.)    Note that iOS supports setting """"""""onlink"""""""" for the 1st time after creation and our API docs do not document it as a creation-only property. We should do this for convenience and parity.  https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.WebView-property-onlink    *Test case:*  # Build and run the below code on Android.  # Tap on the WebView's """"""""Show Alert"""""""" link.  # Notice that a """"""""Webpage not available"""""""" appears onscreen.  # Build and run on iOS.  # Tap on the WebView's """"""""Show Alert"""""""" link.  # Notice that an alert dialog is displayed. (The """"""""onlink"""""""" callback was invoked.)      """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Allow """"onlink"""" property to be set for first time after creating WebView
Description: """"*Summary:* On Android, the {{WebView}} """"""""onlink"""""""" callback property currently must be assigned upon creation in order for it to work. It cannot be set after creation. (However, the """"""""onlink"""""""" property can be changed after assigned upon creation.) Note that iOS supports setting """"""""onlink"""""""" for the 1st time after creation and our API docs do not document it as a creation-only property. We should do this for convenience and parity. https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.WebView-property-onlink *Test case:* # Build and run the below code on Android. # Tap on the WebView's """"""""Show Alert"""""""" link. # Notice that a """"""""Webpage not available"""""""" appears onscreen. # Build and run on iOS. # Tap on the WebView's """"""""Show Alert"""""""" link. # Notice that an alert dialog is displayed. (The """"""""onlink"""""""" callback was invoked.) """"",title+description
TIMOB-27237,12,"""Android: Animating a Label or Button with borderRadius bugs the backgroundColor animation.""","""""""Adding the property borderRadius to a label or a button and animating the backgroundColor makes it always go from white to the animated color instead of animating from the view background color to the new color.    Test case:    {code: JavaScript}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({          layout : 'vertical',          width : Ti.UI.FILL,          height : Ti.UI.FILL      });        var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({          width :Ti.UI.SIZE,          font : {              fontSize : 14          },          text : 'Should go from blue to black',          textAlign : 'center',          color : 'white',          backgroundColor : 'blue',          borderRadius : 20      });            label.addEventListener('click',function() {          label.animate({              backgroundColor : '#000',              duration : 10000          });      });            win.add(label);      win.open();  {code}    The expected behavior is for the background to go from {color:blue}blue{color} to {color:black}black{color} but instead it goes from white to black. If you remove the borderRadius then it works as expected.  A workaround is to wrap the label/button in a view.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Animating a Label or Button with borderRadius bugs the backgroundColor animation.
Description: """"Adding the property borderRadius to a label or a button and animating the backgroundColor makes it always go from white to the animated color instead of animating from the view background color to the new color. Test case: {code: JavaScript} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ layout : 'vertical', width : Ti.UI.FILL, height : Ti.UI.FILL }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ width :Ti.UI.SIZE, font : { fontSize : 14 }, text : 'Should go from blue to black', textAlign : 'center', color : 'white', backgroundColor : 'blue', borderRadius : 20 }); label.addEventListener('click',function() { label.animate({ backgroundColor : '#000', duration : 10000 }); }); win.add(label); win.open(); {code} The expected behavior is for the background to go from {color:blue}blue{color} to {color:black}black{color} but instead it goes from white to black. If you remove the borderRadius then it works as expected. A workaround is to wrap the label/button in a view.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27236,12,"""Animating View height/width from 0 doesn't work on iOS""","""""""*Problem*  Animating View height/width from 0 doesn't work on iOS.    *Test case*  # Execute below code  # View height remains 0 and no animation is present.    {code:title=index.js}  $.win.open();    function onClick() {   $.v1.animate({ duration: 500, height: 200 });  }      {code:title=index.tss}  """"""""#win"""""""": {   backgroundColor: 'white'  }    """"""""#v1"""""""": {   height: 0,   width: 200,   backgroundColor: 'red'  }    """"""""#btn"""""""": {   height: 40,   width: 260,   bottom: 48,   backgroundColor: 'green',   title: 'Animate'  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Animating View height/width from 0 doesn't work on iOS
Description: """"*Problem* Animating View height/width from 0 doesn't work on iOS. *Test case* # Execute below code # View height remains 0 and no animation is present. {code:title=index.js} $.win.open(); function onClick() { $.v1.animate({ duration: 500, height: 200 }); } {code:title=index.tss} """"""""#win"""""""": { backgroundColor: 'white' } """"""""#v1"""""""": { height: 0, width: 200, backgroundColor: 'red' } """"""""#btn"""""""": { height: 40, width: 260, bottom: 48, backgroundColor: 'green', title: 'Animate' } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-27235,12,"""IOS: Having """"DEBUG=*"""" flag causes the appc run node process to fail due to """"Javascript heap out of memory""""""","""""""h5.Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a default classic app with the CLI using {{appc new}}.  2. Make sure the {{tiapp.xml}} has 8.2.0 SDK. I used 8.2.0.v2019071001261 & 8.1.0.v20190709083308.  3. From the terminal run {{DEBUG=* appc run -p ios -T simulator -l trace}}. I have used simulator here but I guess it does not matter.    h5.Actual results:  1. With {{DEBUG=*}} flag we see a lot of {{babel}} logging as transpiling is always on and eventually the build fails due to node running out of heap memory causing {{Javascript heap out of memory}}.  2. This does not affect runs without {{DEBUG=*}} flag which, directly does not affect out tooling. But, this flag is useful for looking at additional logging which is frequently used by us while testing & development.  3. Building to an Android device/emulator is fine.    h5.Expected results:  1. Build does not fail with {{Javascript heap out of memory}} when flag {{DEBUG=*}} is used.""""""",Bug,"Title: IOS: Having """"DEBUG=*"""" flag causes the appc run node process to fail due to """"Javascript heap out of memory""""
Description: """"h5.Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a default classic app with the CLI using {{appc new}}. 2. Make sure the {{tiapp.xml}} has 8.2.0 SDK. I used 8.2.0.v2019071001261 & 8.1.0.v20190709083308. 3. From the terminal run {{DEBUG=* appc run -p ios -T simulator -l trace}}. I have used simulator here but I guess it does not matter. h5.Actual results: 1. With {{DEBUG=*}} flag we see a lot of {{babel}} logging as transpiling is always on and eventually the build fails due to node running out of heap memory causing {{Javascript heap out of memory}}. 2. This does not affect runs without {{DEBUG=*}} flag which, directly does not affect out tooling. But, this flag is useful for looking at additional logging which is frequently used by us while testing & development. 3. Building to an Android device/emulator is fine. h5.Expected results: 1. Build does not fail with {{Javascript heap out of memory}} when flag {{DEBUG=*}} is used.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27208,12,"""CLI: Build fails to find modules due to different naming in manifest and folder""","""""""h5.Description     When detecting modules prior to 8.1.0 the folder name was used as the source of truth for the module id, with the changes in TIMOB-20379 we started to use the id field in the manifest as the source of truth.     I guess it could be argued that this is down to to.imagcache having an error and our behaviour now is more correct, it *_is_* a change of behaviour from previous SDKs.      h5.Steps to reproduce  1. <USER>https://github.com/ewanharris/test-module-detection  2. Build the project with {{appc run -p ios --build-only}}  3. Change the SDK to and 8.2.0 or 8.1.0 SDK   4. Repeat step 2     h5.Actual    When using 8.2.0/8.1.0 the build fails as it cant find the to.imagecache module    h5.Expected    Unsure, it could argued we're being more correct now but this has introduced a regression through a change in behaviour Build should find the to.imagecache module""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Build fails to find modules due to different naming in manifest and folder
Description: """"h5.Description When detecting modules prior to 8.1.0 the folder name was used as the source of truth for the module id, with the changes in TIMOB-20379 we started to use the id field in the manifest as the source of truth. I guess it could be argued that this is down to to.imagcache having an error and our behaviour now is more correct, it *_is_* a change of behaviour from previous SDKs. h5.Steps to reproduce 1. <USER>https://github.com/ewanharris/test-module-detection 2. Build the project with {{appc run -p ios --build-only}} 3. Change the SDK to and 8.2.0 or 8.1.0 SDK 4. Repeat step 2 h5.Actual When using 8.2.0/8.1.0 the build fails as it cant find the to.imagecache module h5.Expected Unsure, it could argued we're being more correct now but this has introduced a regression through a change in behaviour Build should find the to.imagecache module""""",title+description
TIMOB-27206,12,"""LiveView: unable to require files under node_modules""","""""""SDK:  8.0.2.GA  Titanium: 5.2.1  Alloy:  1.14.0-1  --------------------------------    UPDATE:  Upon further investigation, I've found that it is more than just Alloy.Globals that is being affected by this.  Every time alloy is required using `require()` it is getting a fresh version so any changes that were made to the same module in a different class are lost.      require('/alloy') on index.js gets a clean version and thus all changes made in alloy.js are gone.   Even if I move all the logic of assigning things to Alloy.Globals to index.js, everything added is gone when the next controller is loaded.    I have a stand-alone project that I can share to duplicate this issue.    --------------------------------  When defining an event handler function in alloy.js:          and then using it in index.xml:      {code:xml}  <Label id=""""""""label1"""""""" onClick=""""""""Alloy.Globals.eventHandler"""""""" text=""""""""Hello, World"""""""" />  {code}      When this auto-generated controller code is executed:      {code:java}  $.addListener($.__views.label1, 'click', Alloy.Globals.eventHandler);  {code}      It gets to this code in the BaseController:      {code:java}  proxy.addEventListener(type, callback);  {code}      and then throws an error because callback is undefined.        {code}  [INFO]  [LiveView] Error Evaluating app.js @ Line: 430  [ERROR] Error: Invalid type passed to function  [ERROR] File: app.js  [ERROR] Line: 430  [ERROR] SourceId: <null>  [ERROR] Backtrace:  [ERROR]  undefined    {code}    The file is actually BaseController.js Line: 430 but it just reports app.js when using LiveView.    NOTE:  This does not happen in every app.  I am not sure how LiveView is handling alloy.js code so I might need to get more familiar with that before I can say what or why Alloy.Globals.eventHandler would be undefined even though it is defined in alloy.js.""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: unable to require files under node_modules
Description: """"SDK: 8.0.2.GA Titanium: 5.2.1 Alloy: 1.14.0-1 -------------------------------- UPDATE: Upon further investigation, I've found that it is more than just Alloy.Globals that is being affected by this. Every time alloy is required using `require()` it is getting a fresh version so any changes that were made to the same module in a different class are lost. require('/alloy') on index.js gets a clean version and thus all changes made in alloy.js are gone. Even if I move all the logic of assigning things to Alloy.Globals to index.js, everything added is gone when the next controller is loaded. I have a stand-alone project that I can share to duplicate this issue. -------------------------------- When defining an event handler function in alloy.js: and then using it in index.xml: {code:xml} <Label id=""""""""label1"""""""" onClick=""""""""Alloy.Globals.eventHandler"""""""" text=""""""""Hello, World"""""""" /> {code} When this auto-generated controller code is executed: {code:java} $.addListener($.__views.label1, 'click', Alloy.Globals.eventHandler); {code} It gets to this code in the BaseController: {code:java} proxy.addEventListener(type, callback); {code} and then throws an error because callback is undefined. {code} [INFO] [LiveView] Error Evaluating app.js @ Line: 430 [ERROR] Error: Invalid type passed to function [ERROR] File: app.js [ERROR] Line: 430 [ERROR] SourceId: <null> [ERROR] Backtrace: [ERROR] undefined {code} The file is actually BaseController.js Line: 430 but it just reports app.js when using LiveView. NOTE: This does not happen in every app. I am not sure how LiveView is handling alloy.js code so I might need to get more familiar with that before I can say what or why Alloy.Globals.eventHandler would be undefined even though it is defined in alloy.js.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27190,12,"""Android NavigationWindow back-button UI issue on close""","""""""Recently we added the support to show the Android back-button or home-button as a part of the NavigationWindow. It automatically closes its window.    However, when we press the back-button, sometimes it first hides itself and then closes the window. This is leaving an improper visual effect where the back-button is hidden first and after few milli-seconds, the window is closed.            However, when we add the back-button using *ActionBar* as below, it works fine and closes the entire window altogether and hence doesn't create any lacks.        Watch the attached video and notice the lag when the back-button hides itself and the window is closed later. In this duration, the title of the window is also shift to left once the back-button is closed first.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android NavigationWindow back-button UI issue on close
Description: """"Recently we added the support to show the Android back-button or home-button as a part of the NavigationWindow. It automatically closes its window. However, when we press the back-button, sometimes it first hides itself and then closes the window. This is leaving an improper visual effect where the back-button is hidden first and after few milli-seconds, the window is closed. However, when we add the back-button using *ActionBar* as below, it works fine and closes the entire window altogether and hence doesn't create any lacks. Watch the attached video and notice the lag when the back-button hides itself and the window is closed later. In this duration, the title of the window is also shift to left once the back-button is closed first. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27189,12,"""Webview:Onlink property is not working properly""","""""""The customer is facing this issue on using *onlink* property of webview. On SDK 8.0.2.GA  when webview is created though xml file using onlink property of webview, it provides run time error(android) and the app is crashing on iOS device.    *Note:*    The customer noticed that *onlink* is working properly only if the webview is created inside the controller. We also tested this. On iOS,it worked properly but on android,it provides run time error.         *Test Steps:*    1. Open Studio  2. Copy the sample code and paste via studio  3. Run on android and ios both. The app is crashing on iOS. On android, we got run time error in console.    *Test code:*    *index.js*        index.xml      *Test Output:*    *iOS Crashlog:*      *Android:*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Webview:Onlink property is not working properly
Description: """"The customer is facing this issue on using *onlink* property of webview. On SDK 8.0.2.GA when webview is created though xml file using onlink property of webview, it provides run time error(android) and the app is crashing on iOS device. *Note:* The customer noticed that *onlink* is working properly only if the webview is created inside the controller. We also tested this. On iOS,it worked properly but on android,it provides run time error. *Test Steps:* 1. Open Studio 2. Copy the sample code and paste via studio 3. Run on android and ios both. The app is crashing on iOS. On android, we got run time error in console. *Test code:* *index.js* index.xml *Test Output:* *iOS Crashlog:* *Android:* """"",title+description
TIMOB-27186,12,"""Android: Getting  error when calling the getDeviceList() using hyperloop ""","""""""Hello,    One of our customer is using android.hardware.usb.UsbManager.getDeviceList() to get a list of connected us devices.  The code calls this OK, but the log shows the following error.        *The test code is:*      init() being called from the Window onOpen event.    *The output is:*      *Test Environment:*  SDK: 8.0.2.GA  Hyperloop: 4.0.2 (Android)   Testing on Tablet Android 7    Please let us know if you need any more information. Thanks    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Getting error when calling the getDeviceList() using hyperloop
Description: """"Hello, One of our customer is using android.hardware.usb.UsbManager.getDeviceList() to get a list of connected us devices. The code calls this OK, but the log shows the following error. *The test code is:* init() being called from the Window onOpen event. *The output is:* *Test Environment:* SDK: 8.0.2.GA Hyperloop: 4.0.2 (Android) Testing on Tablet Android 7 Please let us know if you need any more information. Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-27184,12,"""Android: Add VideoPlayer """"scalingMode"""" constants VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_*""","""""""*Summary:*  As of Titanium 7.0.0, we've added the following iOS-only {{Ti.Media.ViewPlayer}} constants. We need to add them to Android as well for parity.  * [Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media-property-VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE]  * [Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media-property-VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT]  * [Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT_FILL|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media-property-VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT_FILL]     *Note:*  The above constants were added to iOS via [TIMOB-19040].  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add VideoPlayer """"scalingMode"""" constants VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_*
Description: """"*Summary:* As of Titanium 7.0.0, we've added the following iOS-only {{Ti.Media.ViewPlayer}} constants. We need to add them to Android as well for parity. * [Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media-property-VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE] * [Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media-property-VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT] * [Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT_FILL|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media-property-VIDEO_SCALING_RESIZE_ASPECT_FILL] *Note:* The above constants were added to iOS via [TIMOB-19040]. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27181,12,"""CLI: add ability to install native modules via npm""","""""""Related to TIMOB-26352 because both would take advantage of npm and node_modules in the root directory of the project.       Specifically for native modules, the directories would not get copied to Resources directory like normal commonjs Titanium packages but would instead get """"""""installed"""""""" by copying to the modules directory and modifying the {{tiapp.xml file}} to add those modules to the app.    One way of doing this would be to add a """"""""titanium"""""""" property to the {{package.json}} of the npm package that contains the native modules.      Possibly something like this:                """"""",Improvement,"Title: CLI: add ability to install native modules via npm
Description: """"Related to TIMOB-26352 because both would take advantage of npm and node_modules in the root directory of the project. Specifically for native modules, the directories would not get copied to Resources directory like normal commonjs Titanium packages but would instead get """"""""installed"""""""" by copying to the modules directory and modifying the {{tiapp.xml file}} to add those modules to the app. One way of doing this would be to add a """"""""titanium"""""""" property to the {{package.json}} of the npm package that contains the native modules. Possibly something like this: """"",title+description
TIMOB-27173,12,"""Android: After liveview reload click event on TableView no longer fires""","""""""The click event on a TableView is not fired after reloading the app using liveview on Android.    Sample code:      {code:js|title:index.js}  $.getView().open();    function clickHandler() {      console.log('clicked');  }  {code}    After compiling and loading it in the emulator the click event works fine, however after reloading liveview (saving any file without altering it does this) the click event never fires again.    *Expected result*  Click event should keep working.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: After liveview reload click event on TableView no longer fires
Description: """"The click event on a TableView is not fired after reloading the app using liveview on Android. Sample code: {code:js|title:index.js} $.getView().open(); function clickHandler() { console.log('clicked'); } {code} After compiling and loading it in the emulator the click event works fine, however after reloading liveview (saving any file without altering it does this) the click event never fires again. *Expected result* Click event should keep working.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27170,12,"""iOS: Tableview Click and Longpress event fire at the same time. ""","""""""Hello, Attached is a sample code that demonstrates the behavior. The tableview has both click and longpress event. The click event is supposed to take to another page. And longpress event should open the alert. The issue when tried the longpress in there both the new window and the alert opens. On the first run, it is reproducible in 3-4 attempts and after a while, it's reproducible more often on longpress on the row title. Attached also a video that demonstrates the issue. The issue is on iOS only. Tested with iOS 12.3.1 device iPhone5S with SDK 8.0.1.GA.      Video longPress.mov is supposed to be the right behavior.   Video longPressTest.mov demonstrate the issue.     The sample code is in https://github.com/jorgehip/longPress    Thanks.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tableview Click and Longpress event fire at the same time.
Description: """"Hello, Attached is a sample code that demonstrates the behavior. The tableview has both click and longpress event. The click event is supposed to take to another page. And longpress event should open the alert. The issue when tried the longpress in there both the new window and the alert opens. On the first run, it is reproducible in 3-4 attempts and after a while, it's reproducible more often on longpress on the row title. Attached also a video that demonstrates the issue. The issue is on iOS only. Tested with iOS 12.3.1 device iPhone5S with SDK 8.0.1.GA. Video longPress.mov is supposed to be the right behavior. Video longPressTest.mov demonstrate the issue. The sample code is in https://github.com/jorgehip/longPress Thanks.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27168,12,"""Android: HTTP requests broken on Android 10+""","""""""On Android 10, the following request never triggers a callback (neither {{success}} nor {{error}}):  {code:js}  function sendRequest() {   var url = """"""""http://www.<USER>com"""""""";   var client = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient({    // function called when the response data is available    onload : function(e) {     Ti.API.info(""""""""Received text: """""""" + this.responseText);     alert('success');    },    // function called when an error occurs, including a timeout    onerror : function(e) {     Ti.API.debug(e.error);     alert('error');    },    timeout : 5000  // in milliseconds   });   // Prepare the connection.   client.open(""""""""GET"""""""", url);   // Send the request.   client.send();  }    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: '#fff'  });    var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({      title: 'Send request!'  });    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {      sendRequest();  });    win.add(btn);  win.open();  {code}  The same request works fine on Android < 10. We hope it just requires some kind of whitelisting like ATS on iOS.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTP requests broken on Android 10+
Description: """"On Android 10, the following request never triggers a callback (neither {{success}} nor {{error}}): {code:js} function sendRequest() { var url = """"""""http://www.<USER>com""""""""; var client = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient({ // function called when the response data is available onload : function(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Received text: """""""" + this.responseText); alert('success'); }, // function called when an error occurs, including a timeout onerror : function(e) { Ti.API.debug(e.error); alert('error'); }, timeout : 5000 // in milliseconds }); // Prepare the connection. client.open(""""""""GET"""""""", url); // Send the request. client.send(); } var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Send request!' }); btn.addEventListener('click', function () { sendRequest(); }); win.add(btn); win.open(); {code} The same request works fine on Android < 10. We hope it just requires some kind of whitelisting like ATS on iOS.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27166,12,"""CLI: re-enable removal of dead code on minification""","""""""When we minify projects we explicitly turned off two options in the minified: """"""""mangling"""""""" and """"""""dead code elimination"""""""".    The first renames variables to shorter names.    The second removes chunks of code that should not be reached.    We turned both of these off to """"""""fix"""""""" TIMOB-25573, but I believe that we should revisit and see if this is still an issue. Ideally we'd try to turn these options back on, especially since we'd like to move more aggressive optimizations from Alloy into the SDK core build for inlining true/false for platform/deploy type/distribution variables/guards.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: re-enable removal of dead code on minification
Description: """"When we minify projects we explicitly turned off two options in the minified: """"""""mangling"""""""" and """"""""dead code elimination"""""""". The first renames variables to shorter names. The second removes chunks of code that should not be reached. We turned both of these off to """"""""fix"""""""" TIMOB-25573, but I believe that we should revisit and see if this is still an issue. Ideally we'd try to turn these options back on, especially since we'd like to move more aggressive optimizations from Alloy into the SDK core build for inlining true/false for platform/deploy type/distribution variables/guards.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27165,12,"""iOS: The localnotificationaction event always contains the notification identifier instead of the action identifier""","""""""*Describe the bug*  When adding category with an action to an iOS local notification the localnotificationaction always contains the notification identifier instead of the action identifier.    *To Reproduce*  # Create a notification action with an identifier  # Create a category with the action  # Schedule notification with the category  # Print the localnotificationaction object  # Check the identifier        *Expected behavior*  The identifier has the value of the action    *Actual behavior*  The identifier has the value of the notification    *Environment*  Titanium SDK version: 7.5.2.GA; 8.0.1.GA    I did create a pull request for this, but I want to be sure that it will be picked up: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/10940""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: The localnotificationaction event always contains the notification identifier instead of the action identifier
Description: """"*Describe the bug* When adding category with an action to an iOS local notification the localnotificationaction always contains the notification identifier instead of the action identifier. *To Reproduce* # Create a notification action with an identifier # Create a category with the action # Schedule notification with the category # Print the localnotificationaction object # Check the identifier *Expected behavior* The identifier has the value of the action *Actual behavior* The identifier has the value of the notification *Environment* Titanium SDK version: 7.5.2.GA; 8.0.1.GA I did create a pull request for this, but I want to be sure that it will be picked up: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/10940""""",title+description
TIMOB-27157,12,"""Android: SearchBar is overlapped by listview content (regression)""","""""""Since a few builds, the search bar is overlapped by the list-view it relates to. We currently don't have time to put together a test-case, but any search-bar related sample code should reproduce it.    Workaround: Use the search-bar within the action-bar.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: SearchBar is overlapped by listview content (regression)
Description: """"Since a few builds, the search bar is overlapped by the list-view it relates to. We currently don't have time to put together a test-case, but any search-bar related sample code should reproduce it. Workaround: Use the search-bar within the action-bar.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27156,12,"""Firebase In-App Messaging Android integration crashes the app on the startup""","""""""Hi Titans,    I was trying to integrate the firebase in-app messaging feature with Titanium and I believe I have strictly followed the instructions from the official website: https://firebase.google.com/docs/in-app-messaging/get-started?platform=android   but here is the issue I've been pulling my hair these days trying to figure out:    I have written my own firebase in-app messaging by including all of the dependencies/libraries pulling from Gradle. The module does not have any exposed method in it as it just provide all those libraries to the firebase.core module to enable the in-app messaging feature. However if I included the platform/android/res/values/strings.xml file with the google_app_id value in the test project the app will crash instantly upon the startup. I think it crashed somewhere in the auto-init <USER>provided by firebase but there is no specific log on the crash.            If I don't include the strings.xml file then the firebase won't initialize properly and when I call the configure() function in firebase.core module [https://github.com/hansemannn/titanium-firebase-core] it gives me the following error message:            I have checked the said """"""""com.google.firebase.analytics.connector.AnalyticsConnector"""""""" interface is included in the lib/firebase-measurement-connector-17.0.1.aar file of my firebase.inappmessaging module. I've been stumped by this problem for several days now and have tried all sorts of different versions and combinations of the libraries/configuration and could not fix it. Could you guys please have a look to see what's causing the issue?    I've tried Ti SDK 7.5.0 + and all have this issue.    Here is the test project which should demonstrate the issue with all the modules I packaged for this firebase integration.  https://www.dropbox.com/s/rnc81u3gy19liow/test.zip?dl=0    Please let me know if there is anything I can help with for quickly resolving this issue as we are desperately waiting on this module to work to ship our app.    Thanks,  Kai""""""",Bug,"Title: Firebase In-App Messaging Android integration crashes the app on the startup
Description: """"Hi Titans, I was trying to integrate the firebase in-app messaging feature with Titanium and I believe I have strictly followed the instructions from the official website: https://firebase.google.com/docs/in-app-messaging/get-started?platform=android but here is the issue I've been pulling my hair these days trying to figure out: I have written my own firebase in-app messaging by including all of the dependencies/libraries pulling from Gradle. The module does not have any exposed method in it as it just provide all those libraries to the firebase.core module to enable the in-app messaging feature. However if I included the platform/android/res/values/strings.xml file with the google_app_id value in the test project the app will crash instantly upon the startup. I think it crashed somewhere in the auto-init <USER>provided by firebase but there is no specific log on the crash. If I don't include the strings.xml file then the firebase won't initialize properly and when I call the configure() function in firebase.core module [https://github.com/hansemannn/titanium-firebase-core] it gives me the following error message: I have checked the said """"""""com.google.firebase.analytics.connector.AnalyticsConnector"""""""" interface is included in the lib/firebase-measurement-connector-17.0.1.aar file of my firebase.inappmessaging module. I've been stumped by this problem for several days now and have tried all sorts of different versions and combinations of the libraries/configuration and could not fix it. Could you guys please have a look to see what's causing the issue? I've tried Ti SDK 7.5.0 + and all have this issue. Here is the test project which should demonstrate the issue with all the modules I packaged for this firebase integration. https://www.dropbox.com/s/rnc81u3gy19liow/test.zip?dl=0 Please let me know if there is anything I can help with for quickly resolving this issue as we are desperately waiting on this module to work to ship our app. Thanks, Kai""""",title+description
TIMOB-27151,12,"""Alloy applications - Security Penetration test""","""""""Hello <USER>team,    One of our client's security team has done penetration test on our <USER>application and they have shared few concerns with us to patch.    Our mobile team have gone through those points and found that those issues are related to native Xcode build generated from <USER>studio.    Please go through below points with description and severity:  1. Binary make use of banned API(s)_CWE-676     Severity: Medium  Description:The binary may contain the following banned API(s) _sprintf, _gets, _alloca, _strlen, _stat, _memcpy, _strncpy, _printf, _fopen, _vsnprintf, _sscanf, _strcpy.    2. Binary make use of the following Weak HASH API(s)_CWE-327    Severity: Medium  Description:The binary may use the following weak hash API(s) CC_SHA1, CC_MD5    3. Binary make use of malloc Function_CWE-789    Severity: Medium  Description:The binary may use malloc function instead of calloc    4. Weak Jaibroken Device Detection  Description: A developer can incorporate different checks in his application to examine whether the device on which the application is running is jailbroken or not. Most of these checks are naive and could be easily bypassed.  for point 4, is there any feature or functionality available to bind extra layer of security to detect whether device is jail broken or rooted through <USER>coding environment?  """"""",Bug,"Title: Alloy applications - Security Penetration test
Description: """"Hello <USER>team, One of our client's security team has done penetration test on our <USER>application and they have shared few concerns with us to patch. Our mobile team have gone through those points and found that those issues are related to native Xcode build generated from <USER>studio. Please go through below points with description and severity: 1. Binary make use of banned API(s)_CWE-676 Severity: Medium Description:The binary may contain the following banned API(s) _sprintf, _gets, _alloca, _strlen, _stat, _memcpy, _strncpy, _printf, _fopen, _vsnprintf, _sscanf, _strcpy. 2. Binary make use of the following Weak HASH API(s)_CWE-327 Severity: Medium Description:The binary may use the following weak hash API(s) CC_SHA1, CC_MD5 3. Binary make use of malloc Function_CWE-789 Severity: Medium Description:The binary may use malloc function instead of calloc 4. Weak Jaibroken Device Detection Description: A developer can incorporate different checks in his application to examine whether the device on which the application is running is jailbroken or not. Most of these checks are naive and could be easily bypassed. for point 4, is there any feature or functionality available to bind extra layer of security to detect whether device is jail broken or rooted through <USER>coding environment? """"",title+description
TIMOB-27148,12,"""[iOS] When selecting 'Text Field' on Kitchensink-v2 the application crashes when using iOS 9 and 10""","""""""When selecting the 'Text field' option from 'Controls' within KitchenSink-v2 the application crashes when building to iOS 9 and 10 (Sim in this instance).    *Test Steps*  # Download KitchenSink-v2 (https://github.com/<USER>kitchensink-v2)  # Run the app   # Go to """"""""Text Field"""""""" when the app launches    *Expected result*  Application should not crash and and Text field options should be shown.    *Actual result*  Application crashes.  """"""",Bug,"Title: [iOS] When selecting 'Text Field' on Kitchensink-v2 the application crashes when using iOS 9 and 10
Description: """"When selecting the 'Text field' option from 'Controls' within KitchenSink-v2 the application crashes when building to iOS 9 and 10 (Sim in this instance). *Test Steps* # Download KitchenSink-v2 (https://github.com/<USER>kitchensink-v2) # Run the app # Go to """"""""Text Field"""""""" when the app launches *Expected result* Application should not crash and and Text field options should be shown. *Actual result* Application crashes. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27147,12,"""iOS 13 : Expose new APIs to customization TabBar and Navigation Bar""","""""""In iOS 13, Apple has added many new APIs to allow customise of Navigation bar appearance via [class| https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/uinavigationbarappearance?language=objc] and TabBar appearance via [class| https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/uitabbarappearance?language=objc]. Expose  APIs in SDK to customize navigation bar and tab bar.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS 13 : Expose new APIs to customization TabBar and Navigation Bar
Description: """"In iOS 13, Apple has added many new APIs to allow customise of Navigation bar appearance via [class| https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/uinavigationbarappearance?language=objc] and TabBar appearance via [class| https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/uitabbarappearance?language=objc]. Expose APIs in SDK to customize navigation bar and tab bar.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27141,12,"""Android 9: App not honoring the Orientation set for Windows.""","""""""Hi Team,     We are observing some abnormal behavior with “orientationModes” property of Ti.UI.Window. When we set orientationModes : [Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT] during window construction, the app is rotating to landscape, when “Auto-Rotate” is turned on in real time device. This is only happening with Android 9.0 and behaving properly on OS versions less than 9.0. The issue is reproducible using SDK 8.0.1.GA and lower release.     Please find the attached sample to reproduce the issue.     Steps to reproduce :     1. Turn on “Auto-Rotate” in Android device with OS 9   2. Run the app on the device.   3. Now hold device in landscape mode and navigate to next screen by tapping on the label.   4. *A new screen will initially load in landscape mode* then turns to Portrait mode.     *Expected result :*  New screen opens is Portrait mode.    Then Run on Android device with OS < 9(Works as expected).     Thanks in advance. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android 9: App not honoring the Orientation set for Windows.
Description: """"Hi Team, We are observing some abnormal behavior with “orientationModes” property of Ti.UI.Window. When we set orientationModes : [Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT] during window construction, the app is rotating to landscape, when “Auto-Rotate” is turned on in real time device. This is only happening with Android 9.0 and behaving properly on OS versions less than 9.0. The issue is reproducible using SDK 8.0.1.GA and lower release. Please find the attached sample to reproduce the issue. Steps to reproduce : 1. Turn on “Auto-Rotate” in Android device with OS 9 2. Run the app on the device. 3. Now hold device in landscape mode and navigate to next screen by tapping on the label. 4. *A new screen will initially load in landscape mode* then turns to Portrait mode. *Expected result :* New screen opens is Portrait mode. Then Run on Android device with OS < 9(Works as expected). Thanks in advance. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27139,12,"""Apple Sign-In as new ArrowDB Social Integration""","""""""iOS 13 just announced “Sign in with Apple”, this is Mandatory when having Social Logins. ArrowDB has Social Integrations already for Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, etc; would it also work for Sign in with Apple? It would be mandatory for Apps being approved on the App Stores as of next year.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Apple Sign-In as new ArrowDB Social Integration
Description: """"iOS 13 just announced “Sign in with Apple”, this is Mandatory when having Social Logins. ArrowDB has Social Integrations already for Twitter, LinkedIn, Facebook, etc; would it also work for Sign in with Apple? It would be mandatory for Apps being approved on the App Stores as of next year.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27138,12,"""Android: Add photo/video capture support to WebView""","""""""*Summary:*  Android's {{Ti.UI.WebView}} does not currently support """"""""capturing"""""""" a photo or video when using one of the below input HTML elements. It will display a photo gallery selection activity window instead.  * {{<input type=""""""""file"""""""" accept=""""""""image/*"""""""" capture=""""""""environment""""""""/>}}  * {{<input type=""""""""file"""""""" accept=""""""""video/*"""""""" capture=""""""""environment""""""""/>}}    *To-Do:*  When configuring our {{Intent}} in [TiWebChromeClient.java|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/webview/TiWebChromeClient.java], we need to set it to [MediaStore.ACTION_IMAGE_CAPTURE|https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/MediaStore#ACTION_IMAGE_CAPTURE] for photo capture support and [MediaStore.ACTION_VIDEO_CAPTURE|https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/MediaStore#ACTION_VIDEO_CAPTURE] for video capture support. We also need to show a CAMERA permission request dialog as well.    *Note:*  We can only add support for Android 5.0 and higher.  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add photo/video capture support to WebView
Description: """"*Summary:* Android's {{Ti.UI.WebView}} does not currently support """"""""capturing"""""""" a photo or video when using one of the below input HTML elements. It will display a photo gallery selection activity window instead. * {{<input type=""""""""file"""""""" accept=""""""""image/*"""""""" capture=""""""""environment""""""""/>}} * {{<input type=""""""""file"""""""" accept=""""""""video/*"""""""" capture=""""""""environment""""""""/>}} *To-Do:* When configuring our {{Intent}} in [TiWebChromeClient.java|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/webview/TiWebChromeClient.java], we need to set it to [MediaStore.ACTION_IMAGE_CAPTURE|https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/MediaStore#ACTION_IMAGE_CAPTURE] for photo capture support and [MediaStore.ACTION_VIDEO_CAPTURE|https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/MediaStore#ACTION_VIDEO_CAPTURE] for video capture support. We also need to show a CAMERA permission request dialog as well. *Note:* We can only add support for Android 5.0 and higher. """"",title+description
TIMOB-27136,12,"""iOS 13 : Implement multiple window support for iPad""","""""""In iOS 13+ Apple has given new APIs https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/app_and_scenes?language=objc to support multiple instance of same app's UI . See WWDC video https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/212/""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS 13 : Implement multiple window support for iPad
Description: """"In iOS 13+ Apple has given new APIs https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/app_and_scenes?language=objc to support multiple instance of same app's UI . See WWDC video https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/212/""""",title+description
TIMOB-27134,12,"""Android: Opening a windows a effect of fade black is showing  with 8.0.1.GA""","""""""Hello!  I compiled my app with new Ti SDK 8.0.1 and it is showing a special behaviour when I open a window on android.  Please, would you review the video to explain more clearly? when I am opening a window an effect of fade black is showing all the time.    {color:red}Note{color}: We can't reproduce this issue with 7.5.0.GA    Steps to reproduce:  1. Download attached test project.  2. Build that project with 8.0.1.GA on Android devices.  3. Open then apps and click on Ground   4. Opening a window an effect of fade black is showing all the time.  5. Now build that project with 7.5.0.GA on Android devices.  6. No effect of fade black    Test devices: Android 8 (Samsung J7)    Test Environment:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Opening a windows a effect of fade black is showing with 8.0.1.GA
Description: """"Hello! I compiled my app with new Ti SDK 8.0.1 and it is showing a special behaviour when I open a window on android. Please, would you review the video to explain more clearly? when I am opening a window an effect of fade black is showing all the time. {color:red}Note{color}: We can't reproduce this issue with 7.5.0.GA Steps to reproduce: 1. Download attached test project. 2. Build that project with 8.0.1.GA on Android devices. 3. Open then apps and click on Ground 4. Opening a window an effect of fade black is showing all the time. 5. Now build that project with 7.5.0.GA on Android devices. 6. No effect of fade black Test devices: Android 8 (Samsung J7) Test Environment: """"",title+description
TIMOB-27132,12,"""iOS 13: Add MacOS as a target for deployment""","""""""iOS 13 introduces the option to deploy iOS apps to MacOS. We should investigate the effort needed to allow Titanium apps to be deployed to MacOS.    Furthermore, this investigation should also contain permission system and possible other changes needed to make all (or as much as possible) of our existing iOS functionality work on MacOS.    *Expected result*  After implementation users should be able to deploy apps to MacOS and run them. If certain functionalities are hard to port we can omit them in initial release so we can at least say we've got support. If usage and interest is high enough we can build out other features from there.""""""",Epic,"Title: iOS 13: Add MacOS as a target for deployment
Description: """"iOS 13 introduces the option to deploy iOS apps to MacOS. We should investigate the effort needed to allow Titanium apps to be deployed to MacOS. Furthermore, this investigation should also contain permission system and possible other changes needed to make all (or as much as possible) of our existing iOS functionality work on MacOS. *Expected result* After implementation users should be able to deploy apps to MacOS and run them. If certain functionalities are hard to port we can omit them in initial release so we can at least say we've got support. If usage and interest is high enough we can build out other features from there.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27131,12,"""TiAPI: Create Node-compatible ws module API""","""""""Although the [ws|https://www.npmjs.com/package/ws] module is no core module, it is widely used and would make it way easier to implement a couple of upcoming cross-platform features like hot reloading for Angular and Vue or out of the box support for real time libraries like pusher or socket.io.    The ws module itself depends on a lot of core modules like http, net and ssl which are one of the most complex ones, so it is probably easier to make use of our already existing socket API for the implementation.    https://github.com/websockets/ws    Some of the ws module - specifically the ws client - could be implemented using our existing https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Network.Socket.TCP""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Create Node-compatible ws module API
Description: """"Although the [ws|https://www.npmjs.com/package/ws] module is no core module, it is widely used and would make it way easier to implement a couple of upcoming cross-platform features like hot reloading for Angular and Vue or out of the box support for real time libraries like pusher or socket.io. The ws module itself depends on a lot of core modules like http, net and ssl which are one of the most complex ones, so it is probably easier to make use of our already existing socket API for the implementation. https://github.com/websockets/ws Some of the ws module - specifically the ws client - could be implemented using our existing https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Network.Socket.TCP""""",title+description
