TIMOB-27086,12,"""iOS: HTTPClient validatesSecureCertificate property not defaulting to false""","""""""I noticed this behavior in one of my own apps and tested it in another separate simple app where it also showed up.     In the docs, the validatesSecureCertificate property of the HTTPClient is stated to default to false in development (simulator) and test (device) deployment types. Android's behavior with this property is as described, however on iOS the property is undefined in both development and test deployment types.    Either the docs are inaccurately describing the correct behavior or this is indeed a bug.  [HTTPClient Documentation|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient-property-validatesSecureCertificate]""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: HTTPClient validatesSecureCertificate property not defaulting to false
Description: """"I noticed this behavior in one of my own apps and tested it in another separate simple app where it also showed up. In the docs, the validatesSecureCertificate property of the HTTPClient is stated to default to false in development (simulator) and test (device) deployment types. Android's behavior with this property is as described, however on iOS the property is undefined in both development and test deployment types. Either the docs are inaccurately describing the correct behavior or this is indeed a bug. [HTTPClient Documentation|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient-property-validatesSecureCertificate]""""",title+description
TIMOB-27085,12,"""Android: Close event not fired when close() called immediately after open()""","""""""When calling {{close()}} immediately after {{open()}} Android and iOS fire different events. I noticed this while working with our unit test suite where this happens frequently.    *Steps to reproduce the behavior*    # Run the following code in a classic app      *Actual behavior*  On iOS both events are fired. On Android the behavior varies depending on the SDK version.    * 8.0.0.GA and before: Only the {{open}} event will be fired  * 8.0.1.GA+: No event will be fired at all    *Expected behavior*  Not sure what should be the right behavior here in terms of what events to fire, but iOS and Android should fire the same events.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Close event not fired when close() called immediately after open()
Description: """"When calling {{close()}} immediately after {{open()}} Android and iOS fire different events. I noticed this while working with our unit test suite where this happens frequently. *Steps to reproduce the behavior* # Run the following code in a classic app *Actual behavior* On iOS both events are fired. On Android the behavior varies depending on the SDK version. * 8.0.0.GA and before: Only the {{open}} event will be fired * 8.0.1.GA+: No event will be fired at all *Expected behavior* Not sure what should be the right behavior here in terms of what events to fire, but iOS and Android should fire the same events.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27079,12,"""iOS: File API broken for projects with space in their name""","""""""*Steps to reproduce the behavior*  # Create a new app with a space in it's name: {{ti create -t app -n space name}}  # Add the following code snipped to {{app.js}}    # Build and run the app with {{ti build -p ios}}    *Actual behavior*  The app throws the following error:      *Expected behavior*  The app does not throw an error and the full native path of the {{app.js}} file inside the app bundle gets logged.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: File API broken for projects with space in their name
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce the behavior* # Create a new app with a space in it's name: {{ti create -t app -n space name}} # Add the following code snipped to {{app.js}} # Build and run the app with {{ti build -p ios}} *Actual behavior* The app throws the following error: *Expected behavior* The app does not throw an error and the full native path of the {{app.js}} file inside the app bundle gets logged.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27078,12,"""IOS: App crash with """"Couldn't find module: ./app for architecture: arm64""""""","""""""h5. Description:  Reporter from https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-26967 & Keerthi saw this crash.   Not exactly sure of the steps followed by the reporter to reproduce this but his app got rejected from IOS appstore.  Keerthi used the sample app in the above ticket & she tried to run it from Xcode which us when she saw the error.    h5. Logs:  *Reporter*:      *Keerthi*:      h5. Actual result:  1. App crash is seen.    h5. Expected result:  1. No app crash should be seen.""""""",Bug,"Title: IOS: App crash with """"Couldn't find module: ./app for architecture: arm64""""
Description: """"h5. Description: Reporter from https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-26967 & Keerthi saw this crash. Not exactly sure of the steps followed by the reporter to reproduce this but his app got rejected from IOS appstore. Keerthi used the sample app in the above ticket & she tried to run it from Xcode which us when she saw the error. h5. Logs: *Reporter*: *Keerthi*: h5. Actual result: 1. App crash is seen. h5. Expected result: 1. No app crash should be seen.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27076,12,"""iOS: App freezes after calling Ti.Network.BonjourService.publish method""","""""""When I built our app on SDK 8.0.0 or old versions with the run-on-main-thread property set to true, our app freezes after calling Ti.Network.BonjourService.publish method.    The sample codes are in the attached file of BoujourSample.zip.    If I build our app on SDK 7.5.x or older version and the run-on-main-thread property set to false, this code works fine.      I read about the issue [TIMOB-25856|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-25856], and I tested another sample code of Ti.Network.BonjourService with ti.worker module. But it didn't change. I still have the same problem.    The sample codes with ti.worker are in the attached file of BoujourSampleWithTiWorker.zip.    I suppose that the cause of freezing might come from the implementation with NSCondition class in TiNetworkBonjourServiceProxy.m and TiNetworkBonjourBrowserProxy.m.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App freezes after calling Ti.Network.BonjourService.publish method
Description: """"When I built our app on SDK 8.0.0 or old versions with the run-on-main-thread property set to true, our app freezes after calling Ti.Network.BonjourService.publish method. The sample codes are in the attached file of BoujourSample.zip. If I build our app on SDK 7.5.x or older version and the run-on-main-thread property set to false, this code works fine. I read about the issue [TIMOB-25856|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-25856], and I tested another sample code of Ti.Network.BonjourService with ti.worker module. But it didn't change. I still have the same problem. The sample codes with ti.worker are in the attached file of BoujourSampleWithTiWorker.zip. I suppose that the cause of freezing might come from the implementation with NSCondition class in TiNetworkBonjourServiceProxy.m and TiNetworkBonjourBrowserProxy.m.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27073,12,"""Push notification badge count is not incrementing by one (Android only)""","""""""After upgrading to <USER>version 7.5.0 this issue has been observed.    When a user receives a push notification, rather than the number going up by 1 on their app icon badge, it is going up by 9-11.    This is occurring only in Android 8 and above devices.    Steps:  1. Trigger push notification  2. Monitor badge count x push    Just FYI- Looks like in <USER>documentation |https://docs.<USER>com/cloud/latest/?mobile=/api/PushNotifications  It says that badge count will not appear on app icon, but it's not the case for Android 8 and above because user can go to settings and enable the app icon badge count. (screenshot attached).    Here is the json payload we are putting in arrow db for push notification.  {code:js}  {    """"""""alert"""""""": """"""""This is for badge testing count24"""""""",    """"""""title"""""""": """"""""Hello world1"""""""",    """"""""vibrate"""""""": true,    """"""""icon"""""""": """"""""notification"""""""",    """"""""badge"""""""": """"""""+1"""""""",    """"""""sound"""""""": """"""""default""""""""  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Push notification badge count is not incrementing by one (Android only)
Description: """"After upgrading to <USER>version 7.5.0 this issue has been observed. When a user receives a push notification, rather than the number going up by 1 on their app icon badge, it is going up by 9-11. This is occurring only in Android 8 and above devices. Steps: 1. Trigger push notification 2. Monitor badge count x push Just FYI- Looks like in <USER>documentation |https://docs.<USER>com/cloud/latest/?mobile=/api/PushNotifications It says that badge count will not appear on app icon, but it's not the case for Android 8 and above because user can go to settings and enable the app icon badge count. (screenshot attached). Here is the json payload we are putting in arrow db for push notification. {code:js} { """"""""alert"""""""": """"""""This is for badge testing count24"""""""", """"""""title"""""""": """"""""Hello world1"""""""", """"""""vibrate"""""""": true, """"""""icon"""""""": """"""""notification"""""""", """"""""badge"""""""": """"""""+1"""""""", """"""""sound"""""""": """"""""default"""""""" } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-27072,12,"""When using Alloy Data Binding, allow the dataCollection to be set in the controller""","""""""In our application we have a composite view that shares models/collections across many sub views.  We also like to utilize data binding wherever possible, however this presents a bit of a challenge.  We can only bind to Collections and Models defined in the XML markup, and we cannot replace those Collections/Models with shared references across each sub controller.  It appears today our only option is to use a singleton Collection/Model which is not ideal if you need multiple instances of Collections/Models to be accessed across multiple view bindings.  If setting the Collection/Model inside the sub controller is not an option perhaps we could introduce a method of passing a reference to the Collection/Model in the createController statement.""""""",New Feature,"Title: When using Alloy Data Binding, allow the dataCollection to be set in the controller
Description: """"In our application we have a composite view that shares models/collections across many sub views. We also like to utilize data binding wherever possible, however this presents a bit of a challenge. We can only bind to Collections and Models defined in the XML markup, and we cannot replace those Collections/Models with shared references across each sub controller. It appears today our only option is to use a singleton Collection/Model which is not ideal if you need multiple instances of Collections/Models to be accessed across multiple view bindings. If setting the Collection/Model inside the sub controller is not an option perhaps we could introduce a method of passing a reference to the Collection/Model in the createController statement.""""",title+description
TIMOB-27071,12,"""Ti SDK 8: Android TabBar and Tab, no way to preserve icon color""","""""""The following settings don't work on Android, using TabBar style bottom, new in Ti 8.0    This is problematic when the background is white, then you can't see the tabs, because the color of the png isn't being preserved.  Also, for some reason it doesn't load the """"""""activeIcon"""""""" when it's selected.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti SDK 8: Android TabBar and Tab, no way to preserve icon color
Description: """"The following settings don't work on Android, using TabBar style bottom, new in Ti 8.0 This is problematic when the background is white, then you can't see the tabs, because the color of the png isn't being preserved. Also, for some reason it doesn't load the """"""""activeIcon"""""""" when it's selected. """"",title+description
