TIMOB-26799,12,"""Android: Recurrence rule is not properly fetched for events received by Id""","""""""On Android, whenever an event is retrieved by calling {{getEventById}} its recurrence rule (if there is one) is not retrieved properly.    Edit: I have attached a sample app.js file for reproducing the problem. It will require adding the calendar permissions in tiapp.xml ({{<uses-permission android:name=""""""""android.permission.READ_CALENDAR""""""""/>}} and {{<uses-permission android:name=""""""""android.permission.WRITE_CALENDAR""""""""/>}}). Also it depends on having already an event with a recurrence rule in a calendar.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Recurrence rule is not properly fetched for events received by Id
Description: """"On Android, whenever an event is retrieved by calling {{getEventById}} its recurrence rule (if there is one) is not retrieved properly. Edit: I have attached a sample app.js file for reproducing the problem. It will require adding the calendar permissions in tiapp.xml ({{<uses-permission android:name=""""""""android.permission.READ_CALENDAR""""""""/>}} and {{<uses-permission android:name=""""""""android.permission.WRITE_CALENDAR""""""""/>}}). Also it depends on having already an event with a recurrence rule in a calendar.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26794,12,"""Android: Cannot show / hide a view created via Common JS""","""""""This is a weird one. When creating a view programmatically, e.g. via a CommonJS file, it later cannot be shown / hidden anymore. We need to elaborate more on it, but it's similar to the following (using Alloy):  **xp.ui.js**  {code:js}  exports.createMyView = (args = {}) => {    };  {code}  **index.xml**  {code:xml}  <Alloy>      <Window onOpen=""""""""hideView"""""""">          <MyView id=""""""""theView"""""""" width=""""""""100"""""""" height=""""""""100"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""red"""""""" />      </Window>  </Alloy>  {code}  **index.js**  {code:js}  function hideView() {      $.theView.hide();  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot show / hide a view created via Common JS
Description: """"This is a weird one. When creating a view programmatically, e.g. via a CommonJS file, it later cannot be shown / hidden anymore. We need to elaborate more on it, but it's similar to the following (using Alloy): **xp.ui.js** {code:js} exports.createMyView = (args = {}) => { }; {code} **index.xml** {code:xml} <Alloy> <Window onOpen=""""""""hideView""""""""> <MyView id=""""""""theView"""""""" width=""""""""100"""""""" height=""""""""100"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""red"""""""" /> </Window> </Alloy> {code} **index.js** {code:js} function hideView() { $.theView.hide(); } {code}""""",title+description
