TIMOB-26783,12,"""iOS: Memory leak in require""","""""""*Steps to reproduce the behavior*    # Create a new classic project and replace {{Resources/app.js}} content with the following code:   {code:js}  const win = Ti.UI.createWindow();  const label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'test require' });  label.addEventListener('click', () => require('test'));  win.add(label);  win.open();    # Build the app and open Instruments. Choose the Leaks template and start recording the running test app, then switch into the """"""""Leak Checks"""""""" view.  # Repeatedly click on the label.    *Actual behavior*  Memory leaks will show up for {{tryFile}} and {{NSString stringByAppendingString:}}    *Expected behavior*  No memory leaks are shown.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Memory leak in require
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce the behavior* # Create a new classic project and replace {{Resources/app.js}} content with the following code: {code:js} const win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); const label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'test require' }); label.addEventListener('click', () => require('test')); win.add(label); win.open(); # Build the app and open Instruments. Choose the Leaks template and start recording the running test app, then switch into the """"""""Leak Checks"""""""" view. # Repeatedly click on the label. *Actual behavior* Memory leaks will show up for {{tryFile}} and {{NSString stringByAppendingString:}} *Expected behavior* No memory leaks are shown.""""",title+description
