Description: """"When stack traces where added to the display of unhandled exceptions in May 2018, the functionality was removed. I can provide a PR to fix that. Files that need to be modified: AppModule.m , line 368 TiExceptionHandler.m , line 58 """"",title+description
TIMOB-26368,12,"""iOS: ScrollView on TableView, Event Listener of ScrollView does not work.""","""""""Please check the following example.  At the first tab the Event listener does not work properly whereas on the second does.    When it has ScrollView on TableView the Event Listener of ScrollView does not work and at the same time it does not work on any view that is connected on the ScrollView and also on createTableViewRow that ScrollView is connected.      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollView on TableView, Event Listener of ScrollView does not work.
Description: """"Please check the following example. At the first tab the Event listener does not work properly whereas on the second does. When it has ScrollView on TableView the Event Listener of ScrollView does not work and at the same time it does not work on any view that is connected on the ScrollView and also on createTableViewRow that ScrollView is connected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26367,12,"""iOS: Xcode 10 cannot build for device with Performance enabled""","""""""When trying to build to device with Xcode 10 and Performance enabled (APM) I receive the error at the bottom of the ticket.    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Create a new project  2. Build that project for an iOS device    *Expected Results*  The build succeeds    *Actual Results*  The build fails with the below error    *Notes*  1. I have tried with an iOS 12 and iOS 11.4.1 device  2. Simulators build without error  3. Removing APM allows the build to succeed  4. Building with Xcode 9.4.1 allows the build to succeed   5. Full build log attached    *Error*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Xcode 10 cannot build for device with Performance enabled
Description: """"When trying to build to device with Xcode 10 and Performance enabled (APM) I receive the error at the bottom of the ticket. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Create a new project 2. Build that project for an iOS device *Expected Results* The build succeeds *Actual Results* The build fails with the below error *Notes* 1. I have tried with an iOS 12 and iOS 11.4.1 device 2. Simulators build without error 3. Removing APM allows the build to succeed 4. Building with Xcode 9.4.1 allows the build to succeed 5. Full build log attached *Error* """"",title+description
TIMOB-26353,12,"""CLI: ES6+ dependencies in app/lib/node_modules not handled properly""","""""""Dependencies that use ES6+ are currently not handled properly in Titanium.    To reproduce:  1. Create a new Ti app  2. Run {{npm init}} in app/lib  3. Run {{npm i redux --save}} (in app/lib as well)  4. Add {{import \{ createStore \} from 'redux'}} to your app.js / index.js (ES6 enabled)  5. Run your app""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: ES6+ dependencies in app/lib/node_modules not handled properly
Description: """"Dependencies that use ES6+ are currently not handled properly in Titanium. To reproduce: 1. Create a new Ti app 2. Run {{npm init}} in app/lib 3. Run {{npm i redux --save}} (in app/lib as well) 4. Add {{import \{ createStore \} from 'redux'}} to your app.js / index.js (ES6 enabled) 5. Run your app""""",title+description
TIMOB-26351,12,"""iOS CLI (Babel): Cannot read property 'isIfStatement' of null""","""""""When using SDK 7.4.0, the following error occurs when building kitchensink-v2 to a device    It looks like a [known Babel issue|https://github.com/babel/minify/issues/850], but is there a way around it?      h5.Steps to reproduce    # Get the latest kitchensink-v2 https://github.com/<USER>kitchensink-v2  # Build for iOS device""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS CLI (Babel): Cannot read property 'isIfStatement' of null
