TIMOB-26338,12,"""iOS: Label not shown when opened in window from tab-group in 7.3.0 (kroll-thread only)""","""""""Createlabel bug    The algorithm below works properly on 7.2.1GA however on 7.3.0GA does not. The label is not created as it should be.    Check the algorithm below with the setting “run on main thread” turned off.        """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Label not shown when opened in window from tab-group in 7.3.0 (kroll-thread only)
Description: """"Createlabel bug The algorithm below works properly on 7.2.1GA however on 7.3.0GA does not. The label is not created as it should be. Check the algorithm below with the setting “run on main thread” turned off. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26334,12,"""iOS: New AVPlayer-based Ti.Media.audioPlayer crashes on second setUrl() call""","""""""Having tested SDK mobilesdk-7.5.0.v20180821233900-osx to try the new (long-awaited) AVPlayer-based Ti.Media.audioPlayer I have discovered a crucial bug.     After setting up a player and then using `player.setUrl(URL)` it works fine.     If you then try to setUrl again, the app will crash.     This is due to the notification observer for """"""""timedmetadata"""""""" not being removed.     To test:     {code:js}      var test_player = Ti.Media.createAudioPlayer({           allowBackground: true      });        var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({          title:'set url'      });      btn.addEventListener('click', function(e){          test_player.setUrl('URL TO MP3');         // Will crash on second call.      });  {code}    To fix the issue, please add one line to TiMediaAudioPlayerProxy.m at line 422:     {{[[[self player] currentItem] removeObserver:self forKeyPath:@""""""""timedMetadata""""""""];}}        """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: New AVPlayer-based Ti.Media.audioPlayer crashes on second setUrl() call
Description: """"Having tested SDK mobilesdk-7.5.0.v20180821233900-osx to try the new (long-awaited) AVPlayer-based Ti.Media.audioPlayer I have discovered a crucial bug. After setting up a player and then using `player.setUrl(URL)` it works fine. If you then try to setUrl again, the app will crash. This is due to the notification observer for """"""""timedmetadata"""""""" not being removed. To test: {code:js} var test_player = Ti.Media.createAudioPlayer({ allowBackground: true }); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'set url' }); btn.addEventListener('click', function(e){ test_player.setUrl('URL TO MP3'); // Will crash on second call. }); {code} To fix the issue, please add one line to TiMediaAudioPlayerProxy.m at line 422: {{[[[self player] currentItem] removeObserver:self forKeyPath:@""""""""timedMetadata""""""""];}} """"",title+description
TIMOB-26332,12,"""iOS/Android: Create executable native test project for native modules""","""""""Right now, native module development is kind of stressful. We generate native projects that can be ran in Xcode (iOS) and Android Studio, but module developers still need to create a test project themself, build it once, go to the build directory and open the native project, link the module target to it, copy the app.js from the test project to it, swap the module from before with the dynamically generated one and finally hope that everything goes well. This developer experience is *horrible*; and it could be resolved quite easily. We only need to change our module project template to also include a test-target, which could be as simple as referencing the example/app.js by default.    For iOS, we could create a workspace that has a test project and the main module target.  For Android, I don't know how Android Studio links targets, but we could eventually create another target there as well, which can be ran from directly from Android Studio, similar to the """"""""TitaniumTest"""""""" project to test the core-SDK.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS/Android: Create executable native test project for native modules
Description: """"Right now, native module development is kind of stressful. We generate native projects that can be ran in Xcode (iOS) and Android Studio, but module developers still need to create a test project themself, build it once, go to the build directory and open the native project, link the module target to it, copy the app.js from the test project to it, swap the module from before with the dynamically generated one and finally hope that everything goes well. This developer experience is *horrible*; and it could be resolved quite easily. We only need to change our module project template to also include a test-target, which could be as simple as referencing the example/app.js by default. For iOS, we could create a workspace that has a test project and the main module target. For Android, I don't know how Android Studio links targets, but we could eventually create another target there as well, which can be ran from directly from Android Studio, similar to the """"""""TitaniumTest"""""""" project to test the core-SDK.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26328,12,"""Hyperloop: Android - Application freezes when trying to reopen window in 7.3.0""","""""""When opening a sample in our [hyperloop-examples|https://github.com/<USER>hyperloop-examples] app (available on GitHub), closing the window and trying to open it again, the app freezes, the console is spammed with GC messages and the """"""""Hyperloop_Sample is not responding"""""""" error is thrown.    An extract of the console:  """"""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: Android - Application freezes when trying to reopen window in 7.3.0
Description: """"When opening a sample in our [hyperloop-examples|https://github.com/<USER>hyperloop-examples] app (available on GitHub), closing the window and trying to open it again, the app freezes, the console is spammed with GC messages and the """"""""Hyperloop_Sample is not responding"""""""" error is thrown. An extract of the console: """"",title+description
TIMOB-26327,12,"""iOS: Be able to use frameworks from outside the platform/ directory""","""""""From recent talks with one of our customers, having to copy frameworks in native modules to platform/ seems to be an unnecessary step these days, because the Xcode-project should be smart enough to locate the frameworks by looking at the {{FRAMEWORK_SEARCH_PATHS}} value of their main executable target. This is explicitly important to support CocoaPods (puts the frameworks into {{Pods/}} or Carthage (puts the frameworks to {{Carthage/Build/}}).     Once this works, we can ideally support CocoaPods and Carthage already. This change needs to be done in the iOS _build.js. The _buildModule.js (responsible to package the module itself) already knows which framework search paths to use.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Be able to use frameworks from outside the platform/ directory
Description: """"From recent talks with one of our customers, having to copy frameworks in native modules to platform/ seems to be an unnecessary step these days, because the Xcode-project should be smart enough to locate the frameworks by looking at the {{FRAMEWORK_SEARCH_PATHS}} value of their main executable target. This is explicitly important to support CocoaPods (puts the frameworks into {{Pods/}} or Carthage (puts the frameworks to {{Carthage/Build/}}). Once this works, we can ideally support CocoaPods and Carthage already. This change needs to be done in the iOS _build.js. The _buildModule.js (responsible to package the module itself) already knows which framework search paths to use.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26319,12,"""iOS: """"usernotificationsettings"""" does not include """"types"""" array on iOS 10 and SDK 7.3.0""","""""""When using iOS 10+ on SDK 7.3.0, the """"""""usernotificationsettings"""""""" event does not include the """"""""types"""""""" array of granted types anymore. An easy workaround is to use the following code, but ideally it should be 100 % backwards compatible.    Workaround:  {code:js}  Ti.App.iOS.NotificationCenter.requestUserNotificationSettings(event => {      const alertSetting = event.alertSetting;      const badgeSetting = event.badgeSetting;      const soundSetting = event.soundSetting;            if (alertSetting === Ti.App.iOS.USER_NOTIFICATION_SETTING_ENABLED) {          // Alert allowed      }  });  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: """"usernotificationsettings"""" does not include """"types"""" array on iOS 10 and SDK 7.3.0
Description: """"When using iOS 10+ on SDK 7.3.0, the """"""""usernotificationsettings"""""""" event does not include the """"""""types"""""""" array of granted types anymore. An easy workaround is to use the following code, but ideally it should be 100 % backwards compatible. Workaround: {code:js} Ti.App.iOS.NotificationCenter.requestUserNotificationSettings(event => { const alertSetting = event.alertSetting; const badgeSetting = event.badgeSetting; const soundSetting = event.soundSetting; if (alertSetting === Ti.App.iOS.USER_NOTIFICATION_SETTING_ENABLED) { // Alert allowed } }); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-26317,12,"""Android: exception handler throws a NullPointerException""","""""""Hi, I had these issue while I was debugging a native module.    When a java exception occurs, a NullPointerException is thrown when {{jsstack}} is null, trying to call {{.contains}} on a null string.     https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/dc00603cdc187b56531b615ce8e864c6597157f4/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/TiExceptionHandler.java#L100-L105    {quote}  Caused by: java.lang.NullPointerException: Attempt to invoke virtual method 'boolean java.lang.String.contains(java.lang.CharSequence)' on a null object reference   at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.getError(TiExceptionHandler.java:100)   at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.handleOpenErrorDialog(TiExceptionHandler.java:141)   at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.openErrorDialog(TiExceptionHandler.java:121)   at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.handleException(TiExceptionHandler.java:246)   at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime.dispatchException(KrollRuntime.java:540)   at org.<USER>titanium.TiApplication$1.uncaughtException(TiApplication.java:365)   at org.<USER>titanium.TiBaseActivity.onCreate(TiBaseActivity.java:677)   at org.<USER>titanium.TiActivity.onCreate(TiActivity.java:22)   at android.app.Activity.performCreate(Activity.java:6975)   at android.app.Instrumentation.callActivityOnCreate(Instrumentation.java:1213)   at android.app.ActivityThread.performLaunchActivity(ActivityThread.java:2770)   ... 9 more  {quote}    Also, the new exception handler doesn't include the java exception title and message.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: exception handler throws a NullPointerException
Description: """"Hi, I had these issue while I was debugging a native module. When a java exception occurs, a NullPointerException is thrown when {{jsstack}} is null, trying to call {{.contains}} on a null string. https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/dc00603cdc187b56531b615ce8e864c6597157f4/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/TiExceptionHandler.java#L100-L105 {quote} Caused by: java.lang.NullPointerException: Attempt to invoke virtual method 'boolean java.lang.String.contains(java.lang.CharSequence)' on a null object reference at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.getError(TiExceptionHandler.java:100) at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.handleOpenErrorDialog(TiExceptionHandler.java:141) at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.openErrorDialog(TiExceptionHandler.java:121) at org.<USER>titanium.TiExceptionHandler.handleException(TiExceptionHandler.java:246) at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime.dispatchException(KrollRuntime.java:540) at org.<USER>titanium.TiApplication$1.uncaughtException(TiApplication.java:365) at org.<USER>titanium.TiBaseActivity.onCreate(TiBaseActivity.java:677) at org.<USER>titanium.TiActivity.onCreate(TiActivity.java:22) at android.app.Activity.performCreate(Activity.java:6975) at android.app.Instrumentation.callActivityOnCreate(Instrumentation.java:1213) at android.app.ActivityThread.performLaunchActivity(ActivityThread.java:2770) ... 9 more {quote} Also, the new exception handler doesn't include the java exception title and message.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26312,12,"""iOS 12 : Expose new NSUserActivity APIs for Siri Intents""","""""""In iOS 12, Apple has given some new APIs in {{NSUserActivity}}. These APIs can be used for Siri shortcut supports as well. It will be good to expose these APIs to developers.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS 12 : Expose new NSUserActivity APIs for Siri Intents
Description: """"In iOS 12, Apple has given some new APIs in {{NSUserActivity}}. These APIs can be used for Siri shortcut supports as well. It will be good to expose these APIs to developers. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26304,12,"""TiAPI: Ti.UI.TableViewRow.selectedBackgroundColor partially deprecated""","""""""As discussed in AC-5803, the """"""""selectedBackgroundColor"""""""" property is deprecated in code on Android, but not on iOS. On Android, the dev should use """"""""backgroundSelectedColor"""""""" instead, on iOS, this property does not even exist. We should likely just un-deprecate Android to have one parity API.""""""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: Ti.UI.TableViewRow.selectedBackgroundColor partially deprecated
Description: """"As discussed in AC-5803, the """"""""selectedBackgroundColor"""""""" property is deprecated in code on Android, but not on iOS. On Android, the dev should use """"""""backgroundSelectedColor"""""""" instead, on iOS, this property does not even exist. We should likely just un-deprecate Android to have one parity API.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26303,12,"""Android: add an option on webview to accept third party cookies""","""""""After the new Api of CookieManager on android, when you use a webview using a local html file on url config, you can't access cookies that were created on the app, even if you use the Titanium.Network.addSystemCookie.  For that, you need to allow third party cookies on webview. The problem is Titanium doesn't support that.  It's important to have a config to allow that.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: add an option on webview to accept third party cookies
Description: """"After the new Api of CookieManager on android, when you use a webview using a local html file on url config, you can't access cookies that were created on the app, even if you use the Titanium.Network.addSystemCookie. For that, you need to allow third party cookies on webview. The problem is Titanium doesn't support that. It's important to have a config to allow that.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26300,12,"""iOS: Initializing Ti.UI.TextArea crashes app when running on kroll-thread""","""""""At version 7.3.0 it seems that the error below appears whereas in version 7.2.0.GA does not.  Check the above algorithm with the setting “run on main thread”  turned off.        """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Initializing Ti.UI.TextArea crashes app when running on kroll-thread
Description: """"At version 7.3.0 it seems that the error below appears whereas in version 7.2.0.GA does not. Check the above algorithm with the setting “run on main thread” turned off. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26297,12,"""Android: Resolve ImageView """"images"""" property so that it'll work when targeting Android P""","""""""Greetings,    Our existing app, found at  https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.imoogi.gevacampus ,  does not seem to work on the new Android Pie. We have not made any changes to the app in the past year or so.  I've asked the app's developer, who no longer works for us (just to explain why I'm here), for help. He used an emulator to come up with the attached log.    Can you tell what the problem is from that? Is there a quick fix?    Edit: I'm not sure what version of the studio the app was compiled with, given that it was uploaded more than a year ago. I'm still trying to figure out if the issue is still occuring on a recent alpha release that was compiled on a newer SDK.    Appreciate your help.  Omri sapir""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Resolve ImageView """"images"""" property so that it'll work when targeting Android P
Description: """"Greetings, Our existing app, found at https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.imoogi.gevacampus , does not seem to work on the new Android Pie. We have not made any changes to the app in the past year or so. I've asked the app's developer, who no longer works for us (just to explain why I'm here), for help. He used an emulator to come up with the attached log. Can you tell what the problem is from that? Is there a quick fix? Edit: I'm not sure what version of the studio the app was compiled with, given that it was uploaded more than a year ago. I'm still trying to figure out if the issue is still occuring on a recent alpha release that was compiled on a newer SDK. Appreciate your help. Omri sapir""""",title+description
TIMOB-26294,12,"""iOS: Added Ti.App event """"userinteraction"""" and property """"trackUserInteraction""""""","""""""In order to create a solution for https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13884, we're trying to capture all user interaction events. For Android, there is support to capture all onUserInteraction events. (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-26278)    We want to achieve the same functionality for iOS by extending the UIApplication and trigger an event for each UIEvent. In order to avoid negative performance impact, an event will be triggered only when a touch event began.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Added Ti.App event """"userinteraction"""" and property """"trackUserInteraction""""
Description: """"In order to create a solution for https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13884, we're trying to capture all user interaction events. For Android, there is support to capture all onUserInteraction events. (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-26278) We want to achieve the same functionality for iOS by extending the UIApplication and trigger an event for each UIEvent. In order to avoid negative performance impact, an event will be triggered only when a touch event began.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26291,12,"""Android: setting view.borderRadius and opacity < 1 causes top of view to be cut off""","""""""Hi,    Firstly this is happening on Android < 5.    I believe this relates to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24898    I left a comment there but saw there was already another comment from November 2017 so I asked and was advised to open a new ticket.    As the title states - when creating a view and setting borderRadius > 0 and opacity < 1 this causes top of child content to be cut off. ie not displayed.    I have attached screenshots of it both working and not working.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Build a new clean alloy app  2. Add the following code to index.js  3. Notice the top of the child view gets cut off.  4. To fix - remove borderRadius / opacity value and build again and the child view will no longer be cut off    {code:js}  // create alertView container  var alertView = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'white',    opacity: 0.90,    borderRadius: 5,    width: """"""""85%"""""""",    height: '200dp',    layout: 'vertical',  });     // create alertTitleView  var alertTitleView = Ti.UI.createView({    width: Ti.UI.FILL,    height: Ti.UI.SIZE,  });     // create alertTitleLabel  var alertTitleLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({    text: """"""""This is a long test title This is a long test title This is a long test title This is a long test title"""""""",    color: 'black',    textAlign: 'center',    touchEnabled: false,     top: """"""""15dp"""""""",    left: 5,    right: 5,    font: {     fontSize: '20dp',    }  });     alertTitleView.add(alertTitleLabel);  alertView.add(alertTitleView);     $.main.backgroundColor = """"""""black"""""""";     $.main.add(alertView);       $.main.open();  {code}  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: setting view.borderRadius and opacity < 1 causes top of view to be cut off
Description: """"Hi, Firstly this is happening on Android < 5. I believe this relates to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24898 I left a comment there but saw there was already another comment from November 2017 so I asked and was advised to open a new ticket. As the title states - when creating a view and setting borderRadius > 0 and opacity < 1 this causes top of child content to be cut off. ie not displayed. I have attached screenshots of it both working and not working. Steps to reproduce: 1. Build a new clean alloy app 2. Add the following code to index.js 3. Notice the top of the child view gets cut off. 4. To fix - remove borderRadius / opacity value and build again and the child view will no longer be cut off {code:js} // create alertView container var alertView = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'white', opacity: 0.90, borderRadius: 5, width: """"""""85%"""""""", height: '200dp', layout: 'vertical', }); // create alertTitleView var alertTitleView = Ti.UI.createView({ width: Ti.UI.FILL, height: Ti.UI.SIZE, }); // create alertTitleLabel var alertTitleLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: """"""""This is a long test title This is a long test title This is a long test title This is a long test title"""""""", color: 'black', textAlign: 'center', touchEnabled: false, top: """"""""15dp"""""""", left: 5, right: 5, font: { fontSize: '20dp', } }); alertTitleView.add(alertTitleLabel); alertView.add(alertTitleView); $.main.backgroundColor = """"""""black""""""""; $.main.add(alertView); $.main.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-26289,12,"""Android: Expose """"listSeparatorInsets"""" for parity""","""""""On iOS, there is the [{{listSeparatorInsets}}|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-property-listSeparatorInsets] property of the {{Ti.UI.ListView}} to define the padding of the separator insets of each cell. On Android, the same [is possible|https://stackoverflow.com/a/16768738/5537752] but currently not exposed.     For parity sake, this should be exposed. I tried to expose the API [on my own|https://github.com/hansemannn/titanium_mobile/commit/520dccdfef2ff82de635158977de442b17b9958c], but it did not seem to work.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Expose """"listSeparatorInsets"""" for parity
Description: """"On iOS, there is the [{{listSeparatorInsets}}|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-property-listSeparatorInsets] property of the {{Ti.UI.ListView}} to define the padding of the separator insets of each cell. On Android, the same [is possible|https://stackoverflow.com/a/16768738/5537752] but currently not exposed. For parity sake, this should be exposed. I tried to expose the API [on my own|https://github.com/hansemannn/titanium_mobile/commit/520dccdfef2ff82de635158977de442b17b9958c], but it did not seem to work.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26288,12,"""Android: Add ability to hide/show back button on Window""","""""""We implemented the ability to hide the back-button on iOS (enabled by default) via TIMOB-25871. For Android, the back-button (home indicator) is not shown, but for parity sake, we should make this toggleable (on creation only).    Right now, the following needs to done for {{every}} sub-window:  {code:js}  function onOpen() {   const actionBar = $.window.getActivity().getActionBar();     if (actionBar !== null) {    actionBar.displayHomeAsUp = true;    actionBar.onHomeIconItemSelected = close;   }  }  {code}  Having a property and doing this internally would be a huge cross-platform shared parity-code improvement, especially for larger scaled apps. On long-term, this should part of the {{Ti.UI.NavigationWindow}} effort, but I think this did not gain much love so far.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add ability to hide/show back button on Window
Description: """"We implemented the ability to hide the back-button on iOS (enabled by default) via TIMOB-25871. For Android, the back-button (home indicator) is not shown, but for parity sake, we should make this toggleable (on creation only). Right now, the following needs to done for {{every}} sub-window: {code:js} function onOpen() { const actionBar = $.window.getActivity().getActionBar(); if (actionBar !== null) { actionBar.displayHomeAsUp = true; actionBar.onHomeIconItemSelected = close; } } {code} Having a property and doing this internally would be a huge cross-platform shared parity-code improvement, especially for larger scaled apps. On long-term, this should part of the {{Ti.UI.NavigationWindow}} effort, but I think this did not gain much love so far.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26287,12,"""Android: String.value error log during startup""","""""""When running a Titanium app on Sim / device, the following error log is shown on startup and should be handled:      In general: There are many noisy zygote / APSAnalytics logs (testing on SDK 7.2.0), do we have this fixed for later versions already?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: String.value error log during startup
Description: """"When running a Titanium app on Sim / device, the following error log is shown on startup and should be handled: In general: There are many noisy zygote / APSAnalytics logs (testing on SDK 7.2.0), do we have this fixed for later versions already?""""",title+description
TIMOB-26284,12,"""Android: Cannot add child-views to views extending UIFragment""","""""""When using Ti.Map to create a map-view, sub-views of the map are not being displayed. This is not the case for iOS. A reproducible test-case can be done by taking the module's example app.js and trying to add a child view to it:    {code:js}  var Map = require('ti.map');  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow();    var mapview = Map.createView({    });    mapview.add(Ti.UI.createView({    width: 50,    height: 50,    backgroundColor: 'red'  }))    win.add(mapview);  win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot add child-views to views extending UIFragment
Description: """"When using Ti.Map to create a map-view, sub-views of the map are not being displayed. This is not the case for iOS. A reproducible test-case can be done by taking the module's example app.js and trying to add a child view to it: {code:js} var Map = require('ti.map'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); var mapview = Map.createView({ }); mapview.add(Ti.UI.createView({ width: 50, height: 50, backgroundColor: 'red' })) win.add(mapview); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-26282,12,"""Android: Opening a regular window from a modal window causes the window to open on top of the previous window which differs from iOS""","""""""When opening a regular window from a modal window Android causes the window to open on top of the previous window while on iOS the window is opened behind the modal window.     *Test Case:*       *Test Steps:*  # Create a Titanium application with the test case above  # Run the app  # Press {{Open Modal}}  # Press {{Open Regular}}    *Actual Result*  Android causes the regular window to open on top of the modal window while on iOS the regular window is opened behind the modal window.    According to the regression test case https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-22829 the regular window should be opened behind the modal window.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Opening a regular window from a modal window causes the window to open on top of the previous window which differs from iOS
Description: """"When opening a regular window from a modal window Android causes the window to open on top of the previous window while on iOS the window is opened behind the modal window. *Test Case:* *Test Steps:* # Create a Titanium application with the test case above # Run the app # Press {{Open Modal}} # Press {{Open Regular}} *Actual Result* Android causes the regular window to open on top of the modal window while on iOS the regular window is opened behind the modal window. According to the regression test case https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-22829 the regular window should be opened behind the modal window. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26281,12,"""Android: Investigate privacy-changes in Android P""","""""""Android P introduces some [behavior changes|https://developer.android.com/about/versions/pie/android-9.0-changes-all#privacy-changes-all] of which some also effect apps not targeting Android P but running on them. In detail, there are privacy changes that for example disallow the microphone or camera to be used from the background. We should investigate if this affects our apps as well.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Investigate privacy-changes in Android P
Description: """"Android P introduces some [behavior changes|https://developer.android.com/about/versions/pie/android-9.0-changes-all#privacy-changes-all] of which some also effect apps not targeting Android P but running on them. In detail, there are privacy changes that for example disallow the microphone or camera to be used from the background. We should investigate if this affects our apps as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26280,12,"""Android: Build for genymotion emulator fails with """"Cannot set property 'child' of undefined"""" in node-titanium-sdk ""","""""""h5. Steps to reproduce:  1. Try to build for genymotion emulator with the specified SDK.    h5. Actual results:  1. The build fails with error:      h5. Expected result:  1. The build should not fail & build the app successfully.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Build for genymotion emulator fails with """"Cannot set property 'child' of undefined"""" in node-titanium-sdk
Description: """"h5. Steps to reproduce: 1. Try to build for genymotion emulator with the specified SDK. h5. Actual results: 1. The build fails with error: h5. Expected result: 1. The build should not fail & build the app successfully.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26277,12,"""Android: Maximizing the video in a webView goes blank""","""""""When a video in a webView is maximized the screen goes blank until the device is rotated.    *Steps to reproduce*   # Create an android application with the testcase below  # Build to android device  # Click on Play and then on the Fullscreen button of the video.    *Testcase*  *app.js*    *webpage.html*        *Error*  The screen goes blank until rotated    *Expected*  The video is shown even if the device is not rotated.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Maximizing the video in a webView goes blank
Description: """"When a video in a webView is maximized the screen goes blank until the device is rotated. *Steps to reproduce* # Create an android application with the testcase below # Build to android device # Click on Play and then on the Fullscreen button of the video. *Testcase* *app.js* *webpage.html* *Error* The screen goes blank until rotated *Expected* The video is shown even if the device is not rotated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26273,12,"""Android: saveToPhotoGallery throws an error if there is no external storage.""","""""""*Steps to reproduce*   # Create an android application with the testcase below  # Build to android device  # Click open camera    *Testcase*          *Error*            *Expected*  No error is thrown and the camera is opened""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: saveToPhotoGallery throws an error if there is no external storage.
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce* # Create an android application with the testcase below # Build to android device # Click open camera *Testcase* *Error* *Expected* No error is thrown and the camera is opened""""",title+description
TIMOB-26272,12,"""Android: Building 7_3_X from source fails due to Android NDK error""","""""""Not sure why, but building 7_3_X locally with {{node scons.js cleanbuild}} currently failed. Initially reported by [~<USER> [via Slack|https://ti-slack.slack.com/archives/C1BT2PKU3/p1533645190000091], I was just able to reproduce it.    *EDIT*: It may be because of a recent Android Studio update, because it tries to build with API 14?! I have 26 and 27 installed.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Building 7_3_X from source fails due to Android NDK error
Description: """"Not sure why, but building 7_3_X locally with {{node scons.js cleanbuild}} currently failed. Initially reported by [~<USER> [via Slack|https://ti-slack.slack.com/archives/C1BT2PKU3/p1533645190000091], I was just able to reproduce it. *EDIT*: It may be because of a recent Android Studio update, because it tries to build with API 14?! I have 26 and 27 installed. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26266,12,"""LiveView: Socket error shown when session is terminated / restarted""","""""""I do not have a 100 % reproducible case so far, but it seems like if I kill a LiveView session, e.g. to recompile the asset catalog manually (TIMOB-26265), an error screen is presented, indicating that the socket connection broke up. This is bad UX and should be validated.    *EDIT*: This can be reproduced when switching from iOS to Android in Atom with LiveView enabled. It may be an Atom-plugin error where we need to kill the server on-stop.""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Socket error shown when session is terminated / restarted
Description: """"I do not have a 100 % reproducible case so far, but it seems like if I kill a LiveView session, e.g. to recompile the asset catalog manually (TIMOB-26265), an error screen is presented, indicating that the socket connection broke up. This is bad UX and should be validated. *EDIT*: This can be reproduced when switching from iOS to Android in Atom with LiveView enabled. It may be an Atom-plugin error where we need to kill the server on-stop.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26265,12,"""LiveView: AssetCatalog not updated if resources change""","""""""When using the asset-catalog on iOS ({{<use-app-thinning>true</use-app-thinning>}}), assets such as images (jp[e]g, png and gif) are compiled into a """""""".xcassets"""""""" file during build. But if we change a file with LiveView enabled, this is not detected and a manual rebuild has to be done.    The {{CompileAssetCatalog}} command could be used to do this.""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: AssetCatalog not updated if resources change
Description: """"When using the asset-catalog on iOS ({{<use-app-thinning>true</use-app-thinning>}}), assets such as images (jp[e]g, png and gif) are compiled into a """""""".xcassets"""""""" file during build. But if we change a file with LiveView enabled, this is not detected and a manual rebuild has to be done. The {{CompileAssetCatalog}} command could be used to do this.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26264,12,"""Android: Add """"BottomAppBar"""" support""","""""""Revision 28 of Google's support libraries supports a new {{BottomAppBar}} Java class which is used to display a toolbar at the bottom of the window with a floating action button. This is a new material design feature that is being introduced with Android P.  https://material.io/design/components/app-bars-bottom.html#  https://developer.android.com/reference/com/google/android/material/bottomappbar/BottomAppBar    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add """"BottomAppBar"""" support
Description: """"Revision 28 of Google's support libraries supports a new {{BottomAppBar}} Java class which is used to display a toolbar at the bottom of the window with a floating action button. This is a new material design feature that is being introduced with Android P. https://material.io/design/components/app-bars-bottom.html# https://developer.android.com/reference/com/google/android/material/bottomappbar/BottomAppBar """"",title+description
TIMOB-26263,12,"""Android: Add """"MaterialButton"""" support to """"Ti.UI.Button""""""","""""""Revision 28 of the Google Support libraries will include a new {{MaterialButton}} Java class to help implement the different button styles dictated by material design here...  https://material.io/design/components/buttons.html  https://developer.android.com/reference/com/google/android/material/button/MaterialButton    We would like to support the following new button styles:  * Text Button  * Outlined Button  _(""""""""Contained Button"""""""" is the default button style we already support.)_  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add """"MaterialButton"""" support to """"Ti.UI.Button""""
Description: """"Revision 28 of the Google Support libraries will include a new {{MaterialButton}} Java class to help implement the different button styles dictated by material design here... https://material.io/design/components/buttons.html https://developer.android.com/reference/com/google/android/material/button/MaterialButton We would like to support the following new button styles: * Text Button * Outlined Button _(""""""""Contained Button"""""""" is the default button style we already support.)_ """"",title+description
TIMOB-26262,12,"""Android: Update used Google Support libraries to revision 28""","""""""Titanium currently uses revision 27 of the Google Support libraries.  We should update to revision 28.0.0 once it has been released by Google. (Currently in beta.)    Revision 28 contains new features such as:  * {{BottomAppBar}}  * {{Chip}} and {{ChipGroup}} (To be used by {{Ti.UI.ButtonBar}}.)  * {{MaterialButton}}  * {{MaterialCardView}}  * New theme called: {{Theme.MaterialComponents}}    The release of this library will coincide with Google's release of Android P.  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Update used Google Support libraries to revision 28
Description: """"Titanium currently uses revision 27 of the Google Support libraries. We should update to revision 28.0.0 once it has been released by Google. (Currently in beta.) Revision 28 contains new features such as: * {{BottomAppBar}} * {{Chip}} and {{ChipGroup}} (To be used by {{Ti.UI.ButtonBar}}.) * {{MaterialButton}} * {{MaterialCardView}} * New theme called: {{Theme.MaterialComponents}} The release of this library will coincide with Google's release of Android P. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26261,12,"""Android: Compile with SDK version 28 (Android P)""","""""""Update """"""""titanium_mobile/android"""""""" to compile for Android P (ie: """"""""compileSdkVersion"""""""" 28).    This is needed in order to use the newest API Level 28 features so that we can work on the """"""""Android P"""""""" epic.    Starting off, Titanium should not target API Level 28 by default until all Android P breaking changes have been resolved. But we should allow the developer to opt-in to targeting API Level 28 to test the newest features/changes.  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Compile with SDK version 28 (Android P)
Description: """"Update """"""""titanium_mobile/android"""""""" to compile for Android P (ie: """"""""compileSdkVersion"""""""" 28). This is needed in order to use the newest API Level 28 features so that we can work on the """"""""Android P"""""""" epic. Starting off, Titanium should not target API Level 28 by default until all Android P breaking changes have been resolved. But we should allow the developer to opt-in to targeting API Level 28 to test the newest features/changes. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26260,12,"""Android: Update """"Ti.Android.Service"""" to handle """"FOREGROUND_SERVICE"""" permission""","""""""Apps targeting Android P must add a new {{FOREGROUND_SERVICE}} permission to the """"""""AndroidManifest.xml"""""""" or else calling {{Ti.Android.Service.foregroundNotify()}} will throw a Java {{SecurityException}} internally and fail to start.  https://developer.android.com/preview/behavior-changes#fg-svc    We need to do the following:  * Log an error if the permission is missing when calling {{Service.foregroundNotify()}}.  * Document that that this permission is required.  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Update """"Ti.Android.Service"""" to handle """"FOREGROUND_SERVICE"""" permission
Description: """"Apps targeting Android P must add a new {{FOREGROUND_SERVICE}} permission to the """"""""AndroidManifest.xml"""""""" or else calling {{Ti.Android.Service.foregroundNotify()}} will throw a Java {{SecurityException}} internally and fail to start. https://developer.android.com/preview/behavior-changes#fg-svc We need to do the following: * Log an error if the permission is missing when calling {{Service.foregroundNotify()}}. * Document that that this permission is required. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26259,12,"""Android: Investigate handling of missing FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK on Android P""","""""""Android P has a breaking change where it now requires flag """"""""FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK"""""""" to be set if an intent will be starting an activity from a non-activity. If the flag is missing, then it will fail to start the activity.  https://developer.android.com/preview/behavior-changes#fant-required    Investigate if this will be an issue for the following:  * Local notification pending intents via {{Ti.Android.NotificationManager}}.  * Push notification pending intents via APS and cloud push module.  * App shortcuts via """"""""com.android.launcher.action.INSTALL_SHORTCUT"""""""" intents.  * Anything else?  """"""",Story,"Title: Android: Investigate handling of missing FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK on Android P
Description: """"Android P has a breaking change where it now requires flag """"""""FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK"""""""" to be set if an intent will be starting an activity from a non-activity. If the flag is missing, then it will fail to start the activity. https://developer.android.com/preview/behavior-changes#fant-required Investigate if this will be an issue for the following: * Local notification pending intents via {{Ti.Android.NotificationManager}}. * Push notification pending intents via APS and cloud push module. * App shortcuts via """"""""com.android.launcher.action.INSTALL_SHORTCUT"""""""" intents. * Anything else? """"",title+description
TIMOB-26258,12,"""Android P: Implement Support""","""""""Lists changes and features that should be implemented for Android P support.""""""",Epic,"Title: Android P: Implement Support
Description: """"Lists changes and features that should be implemented for Android P support.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26257,12,"""Android: Removing and re-adding spinner resets last selection""","""""""*Summary:*  An Android {{Ti.UI.Picker}} whose property """"""""useSpinner"""""""" is set to {{true}} will reset its last selection back to the 1st row for all columns when it's removed and re-added to the window.    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Create a project using the attached [^MultiPickerAddRemoveTest.js] code.  # Build and run on Android.  # Select the last row in all columns in the spinner.  # Tap the """"""""Remove"""""""" button.  # Tap the """"""""Add"""""""" button.  # Observe the spinner's current selections.    *Result:*  Spinner resets its selection to the 1st row in all columns when re-added to the window.    *Expected Result:*  Last selections in each column should be retained.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Removing and re-adding spinner resets last selection
Description: """"*Summary:* An Android {{Ti.UI.Picker}} whose property """"""""useSpinner"""""""" is set to {{true}} will reset its last selection back to the 1st row for all columns when it's removed and re-added to the window. *Steps to reproduce:* # Create a project using the attached [^MultiPickerAddRemoveTest.js] code. # Build and run on Android. # Select the last row in all columns in the spinner. # Tap the """"""""Remove"""""""" button. # Tap the """"""""Add"""""""" button. # Observe the spinner's current selections. *Result:* Spinner resets its selection to the 1st row in all columns when re-added to the window. *Expected Result:* Last selections in each column should be retained. """"",title+description
TIMOB-26256,12,"""iOS: Removing and re-adding a date/time picker resets selection to current time""","""""""*Summary:*  Picker resets its date/time selection back to current time when it's removed and re-added to the window. This happens with {{Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_DATE}} and {{Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_TIME}}.    This is not an issue on Android.    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Create a project using the attached [^DatePickerAddRemoveTest.js] code.  # Build and run on iOS.  # Select a different date/time in the picker.  # Tap the """"""""Remove"""""""" button.  # Tap the """"""""Add"""""""" button.  # Observe the picker's current date/time.    *Result:*  Picker resets its selection to current time. Previous selection was forgotten.    *Expected Result:*  Last date/time selection should be retained.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Removing and re-adding a date/time picker resets selection to current time
Description: """"*Summary:* Picker resets its date/time selection back to current time when it's removed and re-added to the window. This happens with {{Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_DATE}} and {{Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_TIME}}. This is not an issue on Android. *Steps to reproduce:* # Create a project using the attached [^DatePickerAddRemoveTest.js] code. # Build and run on iOS. # Select a different date/time in the picker. # Tap the """"""""Remove"""""""" button. # Tap the """"""""Add"""""""" button. # Observe the picker's current date/time. *Result:* Picker resets its selection to current time. Previous selection was forgotten. *Expected Result:* Last date/time selection should be retained.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26255,12,"""iOS: Removing and re-adding """"plain"""" picker resets last selection""","""""""*Summary:*  Picker resets its selection back to the 1st row when it's removed and re-added to the window. This happens with single-column and multicolumn pickers.    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Create a project using the attached [^SinglePickerAddRemoveTest.js] code.  # Build and run on iOS.  # Select the last row in the picker.  # Tap the """"""""Remove"""""""" button.  # Tap the """"""""Add"""""""" button.  # Observe the picker's current selection.    *Result:*  Picker resets its selection to the 1st row when re-added to the window.    *Expected Result:*  Last selection should be retained.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Removing and re-adding """"plain"""" picker resets last selection
Description: """"*Summary:* Picker resets its selection back to the 1st row when it's removed and re-added to the window. This happens with single-column and multicolumn pickers. *Steps to reproduce:* # Create a project using the attached [^SinglePickerAddRemoveTest.js] code. # Build and run on iOS. # Select the last row in the picker. # Tap the """"""""Remove"""""""" button. # Tap the """"""""Add"""""""" button. # Observe the picker's current selection. *Result:* Picker resets its selection to the 1st row when re-added to the window. *Expected Result:* Last selection should be retained. """"",title+description
