TIMOB-26246,12,"""Android: Handle Android P insetting/display-cutout""","""""""*Summary:*  Android 9.0 (aka: Android P) will support devices with """"""""iPhone X"""""""" style frame insetting where the top frame cuts into the top status bar.   !AndroidP_Inset.png|thumbnail!     We'll need to provide APIs to better support this device feature. Preferably re-use the existing APIs used by iPhone X such as our {{Window.extendSafeArea}} property.    *Note 1:*  Android 9.0 (API Level 28) provides new APIs to help with us. They're listed here...  https://developer.android.com/preview/features#cutout    Quick reference...  https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/DisplayCutout  https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/WindowManager.LayoutParams#LAYOUT_IN_DISPLAY_CUTOUT_MODE_SHORT_EDGES    Also, the window won't render into the cutout unless we set additional window flags such as the following...      *Note 2:*  Huawei has their own custom notch support on Android 8 which they document in the link below. Note that these are not official Google Android APIs.  https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/devservice/doc/30210""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Handle Android P insetting/display-cutout
Description: """"*Summary:* Android 9.0 (aka: Android P) will support devices with """"""""iPhone X"""""""" style frame insetting where the top frame cuts into the top status bar. !AndroidP_Inset.png|thumbnail! We'll need to provide APIs to better support this device feature. Preferably re-use the existing APIs used by iPhone X such as our {{Window.extendSafeArea}} property. *Note 1:* Android 9.0 (API Level 28) provides new APIs to help with us. They're listed here... https://developer.android.com/preview/features#cutout Quick reference... https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/DisplayCutout https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/WindowManager.LayoutParams#LAYOUT_IN_DISPLAY_CUTOUT_MODE_SHORT_EDGES Also, the window won't render into the cutout unless we set additional window flags such as the following... *Note 2:* Huawei has their own custom notch support on Android 8 which they document in the link below. Note that these are not official Google Android APIs. https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/devservice/doc/30210""""",title+description
TIMOB-26245,12,"""iOS: Exclude 32-Bit architectures for iOS 11+ targets""","""""""If the Titanium developer targets iOS 11+, we can remove the 32-bit architectures for all builds, because iOS 11+ does not run on these devices anymore. There is a related discussion over at [CocoaPods|https://github.com/CocoaPods/CocoaPods/issues/7148] about it.""""""",Story,"Title: iOS: Exclude 32-Bit architectures for iOS 11+ targets
Description: """"If the Titanium developer targets iOS 11+, we can remove the 32-bit architectures for all builds, because iOS 11+ does not run on these devices anymore. There is a related discussion over at [CocoaPods|https://github.com/CocoaPods/CocoaPods/issues/7148] about it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-26244,12,"""Hyperloop: iOS - Remove TiCore library, removed copy-resources hook""","""""""As we are removing TiCore from the SDK in 8.0.0, we can remove the native library from the Hyperloop module as well, also updating the build script to use {{ti build}} API's instead of manual compilation.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Hyperloop: iOS - Remove TiCore library, removed copy-resources hook
Description: """"As we are removing TiCore from the SDK in 8.0.0, we can remove the native library from the Hyperloop module as well, also updating the build script to use {{ti build}} API's instead of manual compilation.""""",title+description
