TIMOB-25823,12,"""Liveview: Server not stopped when using a custom ip or port""","""""""h5.Description    On Windows it is generally necessary to use define a custom IP for liveview to use due to the number of network interfaces that can be defined on a developers machine (docker vethernet, windows mobile emulator vethernet etc.), however when the liveview hook attempts to stop running servers it uses a hardcoded value of {{http://localhost:8324/kill}}, this should be dynamic using the defined port/ip    h5.Steps to reproduce    You need to define a custom port for liveview usage using {{--liveview-fport 1234}} (you can define this in the liveview config section of Studio too if not using the cli)  # Build with liveview enabled and a custom port  # Build with liveview enabled and a custom port again    h5.Actual    On the second build the log {{Address in use, retrying...}} will repeatedly be shown in the console as the liveview server couldn't be killed    h5.Expected    Liveview server should be killed between runs""""""",Bug,"Title: Liveview: Server not stopped when using a custom ip or port
Description: """"h5.Description On Windows it is generally necessary to use define a custom IP for liveview to use due to the number of network interfaces that can be defined on a developers machine (docker vethernet, windows mobile emulator vethernet etc.), however when the liveview hook attempts to stop running servers it uses a hardcoded value of {{http://localhost:8324/kill}}, this should be dynamic using the defined port/ip h5.Steps to reproduce You need to define a custom port for liveview usage using {{--liveview-fport 1234}} (you can define this in the liveview config section of Studio too if not using the cli) # Build with liveview enabled and a custom port # Build with liveview enabled and a custom port again h5.Actual On the second build the log {{Address in use, retrying...}} will repeatedly be shown in the console as the liveview server couldn't be killed h5.Expected Liveview server should be killed between runs""""",title+description
TIMOB-25822,12,"""Android: Apps with spaces in names fail to build on Windows""","""""""h5.Description    Building an app with a space in the name on Windows throws an error on the dexer step with the below error, this is a regression from 7.0.1.GA        h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Create an app with spaces in the name  2. Build the app for Android    h5.Actual    App fails to build on dexer step    h5.Expected    App should not fail""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Apps with spaces in names fail to build on Windows
Description: """"h5.Description Building an app with a space in the name on Windows throws an error on the dexer step with the below error, this is a regression from 7.0.1.GA h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Create an app with spaces in the name 2. Build the app for Android h5.Actual App fails to build on dexer step h5.Expected App should not fail""""",title+description
TIMOB-25821,12,"""Liveview: Server does not stop when the build is killed""","""""""h5.Description    When building with liveview enabled the liveview server does not stop when the build has finished. This usually does not lead to multiple servers being started as the liveview hook calls the /kill endpoint before starting a new server (this is hard coded to 127.0.0.1:8324 so it is actually possible for users who specify a custom port or ip).    h5.Steps to reproduce    # Build a project with liveview enabled  # Kill the build <USER>(red square from studio/ctrl+c from cli)  # curl 127.0.0.1:8324    h5.Actual    A response like {{\{""""""""pid"""""""":47754,""""""""path"""""""":""""""""/Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>Studio_Workspace/testbabelstuff/"""""""",""""""""uptime"""""""":12.403,""""""""alloy"""""""":false\}}} comes back from the curl    h5.Expected    No response as the server should not be running""""""",Bug,"Title: Liveview: Server does not stop when the build is killed
Description: """"h5.Description When building with liveview enabled the liveview server does not stop when the build has finished. This usually does not lead to multiple servers being started as the liveview hook calls the /kill endpoint before starting a new server (this is hard coded to 127.0.0.1:8324 so it is actually possible for users who specify a custom port or ip). h5.Steps to reproduce # Build a project with liveview enabled # Kill the build <USER>(red square from studio/ctrl+c from cli) # curl 127.0.0.1:8324 h5.Actual A response like {{\{""""""""pid"""""""":47754,""""""""path"""""""":""""""""/Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>Studio_Workspace/testbabelstuff/"""""""",""""""""uptime"""""""":12.403,""""""""alloy"""""""":false\}}} comes back from the curl h5.Expected No response as the server should not be running""""",title+description
TIMOB-25817,12,"""CLI: gitignore file not copied across on creation of a default project""","""""""h5.Description    When creating a new titanium project the default .gitignore file is not copied across to the application folder, this is because the create <USER>filters out files in config.cli.ignoreFiles, which contains .gitignore    I'm unsure on the best way to fix this, as we have to remove it from the regex in cli.ignoreFiles in the ti config, it might be best to just change the if to    {{} else if (filename === '.gitignore' || !ignoreFiles.test(filename)) {}}    h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Run {{appc new -t titanium --name testgitignore --force --id com.foo  --no-prompt --classic}}  2. Check the testgitignore folder    h5.Actual     No .gitignore file    h5.Expected    .gitignore file should exist""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: gitignore file not copied across on creation of a default project
Description: """"h5.Description When creating a new titanium project the default .gitignore file is not copied across to the application folder, this is because the create <USER>filters out files in config.cli.ignoreFiles, which contains .gitignore I'm unsure on the best way to fix this, as we have to remove it from the regex in cli.ignoreFiles in the ti config, it might be best to just change the if to {{} else if (filename === '.gitignore' || !ignoreFiles.test(filename)) {}} h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Run {{appc new -t titanium --name testgitignore --force --id com.foo --no-prompt --classic}} 2. Check the testgitignore folder h5.Actual No .gitignore file h5.Expected .gitignore file should exist""""",title+description
TIMOB-25816,12,"""Decide on best practices for polyfilling for ES6+ usage""","""""""h5.Description    *I'm making this a story because to me it's something that we need to investigate, discuss and act on*    With the addition of babel in 7.1.0 users can now use new syntax in their applications without worrying about what their targets support. While that is the theory it's not the reality.     If you review Babels [Learning ES2015|https://babeljs.io/learn-es2015/] guide, some features denote {{Support via polyfill}}, this is because babel can only handle syntactical changes (arrow function to function expressions, let/const to var etc.), and for features such as maps and promises it is impossible to transpile these down so babel makes use of polyfills, which instead add these into the JS environment.    To me, there are a two avenues to us handling this    * We distribute [babel-polyfill|https://www.npmjs.com/package/babel-polyfill] in the SDK  * We pass this on down to the user, either through usage of a module or just requiring them to add the module themselves.  * We evaluate including babel-runtime/transform-runtime in the transpile step https://babeljs.io/docs/plugins/transform-runtime    This has been attempted already (kind of) in two ways    * I attempted to add babel-polyfill to an app [~<USER> was writing (TIMOB-25740), it didn't go well for me, I believe we could fix this  * [~<USER> [node-titanium-sdk|https://github.com/<USER>node-titanium-sdk/pull/24] PR, which includes regenerator-runtime to allow apps to use async/await    Here's my first thoughts on drawbacks I see with both ways    * User owned  ** Doesn't adhere with our current way of handling this kind of thing where we deal with it    * SDK owned  ** Unless we're detect what's needed every app will include it, whether they need it or not.  ** We'll need to continually maintain this each release I believe    I looked at how others handle this, and discovered the following    * react-native [rolls its own preset|https://github.com/facebook/react-native], which appears to be dynamic dependent on an apps usage. Polyfills look to be baked into react-native with them being defined when the [app start|https://github.com/facebook/react-native/blob/master/Libraries/Core/InitializeCore.js]""""""",Story,"Title: Decide on best practices for polyfilling for ES6+ usage
Description: """"h5.Description *I'm making this a story because to me it's something that we need to investigate, discuss and act on* With the addition of babel in 7.1.0 users can now use new syntax in their applications without worrying about what their targets support. While that is the theory it's not the reality. If you review Babels [Learning ES2015|https://babeljs.io/learn-es2015/] guide, some features denote {{Support via polyfill}}, this is because babel can only handle syntactical changes (arrow function to function expressions, let/const to var etc.), and for features such as maps and promises it is impossible to transpile these down so babel makes use of polyfills, which instead add these into the JS environment. To me, there are a two avenues to us handling this * We distribute [babel-polyfill|https://www.npmjs.com/package/babel-polyfill] in the SDK * We pass this on down to the user, either through usage of a module or just requiring them to add the module themselves. * We evaluate including babel-runtime/transform-runtime in the transpile step https://babeljs.io/docs/plugins/transform-runtime This has been attempted already (kind of) in two ways * I attempted to add babel-polyfill to an app [~<USER> was writing (TIMOB-25740), it didn't go well for me, I believe we could fix this * [~<USER> [node-titanium-sdk|https://github.com/<USER>node-titanium-sdk/pull/24] PR, which includes regenerator-runtime to allow apps to use async/await Here's my first thoughts on drawbacks I see with both ways * User owned ** Doesn't adhere with our current way of handling this kind of thing where we deal with it * SDK owned ** Unless we're detect what's needed every app will include it, whether they need it or not. ** We'll need to continually maintain this each release I believe I looked at how others handle this, and discovered the following * react-native [rolls its own preset|https://github.com/facebook/react-native], which appears to be dynamic dependent on an apps usage. Polyfills look to be baked into react-native with them being defined when the [app start|https://github.com/facebook/react-native/blob/master/Libraries/Core/InitializeCore.js]""""",title+description
TIMOB-25815,12,"""Android: HTML style  """"position: absolute"""" hiding the div or HTML element in Webview""","""""""Hello,    HTML style  """"""""position: absolute"""""""" hiding the div or HTML element in Webview on Android.     *Test Environment:*  SDK: 7.0.2.GA  <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 7.0.2  Android Device: Samsung Gallaxy Grand prime (5.1.1)  *Test Code:*  app.js      test.html      When we remove the style """"""""position: absolute"""""""" its working fine for Android.    Note: Same code is working fine for iOS.    Thanks""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTML style """"position: absolute"""" hiding the div or HTML element in Webview
Description: """"Hello, HTML style """"""""position: absolute"""""""" hiding the div or HTML element in Webview on Android. *Test Environment:* SDK: 7.0.2.GA <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 7.0.2 Android Device: Samsung Gallaxy Grand prime (5.1.1) *Test Code:* app.js test.html When we remove the style """"""""position: absolute"""""""" its working fine for Android. Note: Same code is working fine for iOS. Thanks""""",title+description
TIMOB-25813,12,"""Android: Ti.Media.AudioRecorder parity on """"format"""" and """"compression""""""","""""""We've added AudioRecorder parity across all platforms in 6.2.0. But {{format}} and {{compression}} are still iOS / Windows only, so we should try to gain some parity across the platforms, at least for the basic file formats (mp3, mp4, wav, caf \[default\]) and compressions (aac, ima4, linear pcm \[default\]).""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Ti.Media.AudioRecorder parity on """"format"""" and """"compression""""
Description: """"We've added AudioRecorder parity across all platforms in 6.2.0. But {{format}} and {{compression}} are still iOS / Windows only, so we should try to gain some parity across the platforms, at least for the basic file formats (mp3, mp4, wav, caf \[default\]) and compressions (aac, ima4, linear pcm \[default\]).""""",title+description
TIMOB-25808,12,"""Android: Improve log quality""","""""""Following up on TIMOB-24311, it would be good to continue to remove all non Ti Log from the Android console.    Testproject    {code:java}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: '#fff'  });    var txt = """""""""""""""";  var counter = 0;  setInterval(function() {   txt += """"""""test """""""" + counter + """"""""\n"""""""";   counter++;   console.log(txt);  }, 500);    win.open();  {code}    Currently there is still some output like        In the new PR I removed the non Ti checks that where used for multiline Ti-Logs. Since I'm not sure where exactly they appear and tested it with two live apps the output was better than before and only showing logs the developer wants to see.    If there are other parts that will need the previous non-ti-regex it would be good to invest if they can be changed (e.g. adding a prefix to filter them out)""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Improve log quality
Description: """"Following up on TIMOB-24311, it would be good to continue to remove all non Ti Log from the Android console. Testproject {code:java} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var txt = """"""""""""""""; var counter = 0; setInterval(function() { txt += """"""""test """""""" + counter + """"""""\n""""""""; counter++; console.log(txt); }, 500); win.open(); {code} Currently there is still some output like In the new PR I removed the non Ti checks that where used for multiline Ti-Logs. Since I'm not sure where exactly they appear and tested it with two live apps the output was better than before and only showing logs the developer wants to see. If there are other parts that will need the previous non-ti-regex it would be good to invest if they can be changed (e.g. adding a prefix to filter them out)""""",title+description
TIMOB-25806,12,"""Hyperloop - iOS: Using ES6 arrow functions in Hyperloop-related code cannot be handled""","""""""When using ES6 in Hyperloop methods, e.g.   {code:js}      var ButtonDelegate = Hyperloop.defineClass('ButtonDelegate', 'NSObject');        ButtonDelegate.addMethod({          selector: 'buttonPressed:',          instance: true,          arguments: ['UIButton'],          callback: (sender) => {   //                         ^-- Here is the issue          }      });    [ERROR] An error occurred during build after 33s 538ms  [ERROR] not sure what to do with this node (/Users/<USER>Documents/Apps/hyperloop-examples/Resources/iphone/alloy/controllers/button.js:58:13)  {code}  The error is happening [here|https://github.com/<USER>hyperloop.next/blob/master/packages/hyperloop-ios-metabase/lib/generate/custom.js#L773] and looks like the arrow function cannot be mapped to the {{FunctionExpression}} and falls through.""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop - iOS: Using ES6 arrow functions in Hyperloop-related code cannot be handled
Description: """"When using ES6 in Hyperloop methods, e.g. {code:js} var ButtonDelegate = Hyperloop.defineClass('ButtonDelegate', 'NSObject'); ButtonDelegate.addMethod({ selector: 'buttonPressed:', instance: true, arguments: ['UIButton'], callback: (sender) => { // ^-- Here is the issue } }); [ERROR] An error occurred during build after 33s 538ms [ERROR] not sure what to do with this node (/Users/<USER>Documents/Apps/hyperloop-examples/Resources/iphone/alloy/controllers/button.js:58:13) {code} The error is happening [here|https://github.com/<USER>hyperloop.next/blob/master/packages/hyperloop-ios-metabase/lib/generate/custom.js#L773] and looks like the arrow function cannot be mapped to the {{FunctionExpression}} and falls through.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25803,12,"""Android: Improve Imageview cache on devices with lesser ram""","""""""h5.Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the code below in your app.js:    2. Build for android device with lesser ram like Nexus 5.  3. After the app launch tap start & select photos from the device.  4. They will appear in a tableview.  5. Tap each tableviewrow to open the image.  6. Image should open in an imageview & close after a timeout of 1000ms i.e 1 sec.  7. Continue doing this for few trys.    h5.Actual results:  1. We see an app crash & error :    2. According to [~<USER>, this can be improved by improving the imageview cache.    h5.Expected result:  1. The app should not crash & the images should keep opening in the imageview.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Improve Imageview cache on devices with lesser ram
Description: """"h5.Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the code below in your app.js: 2. Build for android device with lesser ram like Nexus 5. 3. After the app launch tap start & select photos from the device. 4. They will appear in a tableview. 5. Tap each tableviewrow to open the image. 6. Image should open in an imageview & close after a timeout of 1000ms i.e 1 sec. 7. Continue doing this for few trys. h5.Actual results: 1. We see an app crash & error : 2. According to [~<USER>, this can be improved by improving the imageview cache. h5.Expected result: 1. The app should not crash & the images should keep opening in the imageview.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25802,12,"""SDK: Move to the renamed babel-minify package""","""""""h5.Description    We currently use https://www.npmjs.com/package/babel-preset-babili for minification in node-titanium-sdk, babel seems to have gone away with the babili naming and moved to babel-minify, so we should begin using https://www.npmjs.com/package/babel-preset-minify as it's actually being updated and published""""""",Improvement,"Title: SDK: Move to the renamed babel-minify package
Description: """"h5.Description We currently use https://www.npmjs.com/package/babel-preset-babili for minification in node-titanium-sdk, babel seems to have gone away with the babili naming and moved to babel-minify, so we should begin using https://www.npmjs.com/package/babel-preset-minify as it's actually being updated and published""""",title+description
TIMOB-25800,12,"""iOS11: Support new property """" contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior"""" of scrollview""","""""""Apple has deprecated property """"""""automaticallyAdjustsScrollViewInsets"""""""" of UIViewController which we support as window property  [autoAdjustScrollViewInsets|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-property-autoAdjustScrollViewInsets] and introduced new property for scrollView """"""""contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior"""""""" in iOS 11.    Let's expose this new property to developer.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS11: Support new property """" contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior"""" of scrollview
Description: """"Apple has deprecated property """"""""automaticallyAdjustsScrollViewInsets"""""""" of UIViewController which we support as window property [autoAdjustScrollViewInsets|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-property-autoAdjustScrollViewInsets] and introduced new property for scrollView """"""""contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior"""""""" in iOS 11. Let's expose this new property to developer.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25790,12,"""iOS: Liveview broken when transpiling code""","""""""h5.Description    Using liveview with the {{<transpile>}} flag in the tiapp set to true (or not in the tiapp as it defaults to true) currently throws the below error [link to source|https://github.com/<USER>liveview/blob/713d920a19f9a6b9a444f3de53d92118ad1439f3/build/liveview.js#L427]    - This occurs because the liveview code is attempting to overwrite the global.L variable, globals are defined as readOnly [see here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/5ce893c20d97b8d62b100d331fa40c88744df2f2/iphone/Classes/KrollContext.m#L1101] and as all code in now run in strict mode this is now an error (credit to TIMOB-18465 for helping me figure this one out)    There's two ways we can fix this    1. Remove kTiPropertyAttributeReadOnly on global properties  2. Stop making all JS core run in strict mode by default by adding {{modules: false}} to the object passed to preset-env, which will have a knock on effect to ES6 module support    My vote goes for 1, but again this highlights the fact the transpilation step *_is going to cause breaking changes for people_*        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Enable transpilation by adding the {{<transpile>true</transpile>}} flag to your tiapp.xml  # Build an app using liveview to iOS      h5.Actual    Error above is thrown    h5.Expected    No error thrown, liveview should work as normal""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Liveview broken when transpiling code
Description: """"h5.Description Using liveview with the {{<transpile>}} flag in the tiapp set to true (or not in the tiapp as it defaults to true) currently throws the below error [link to source|https://github.com/<USER>liveview/blob/713d920a19f9a6b9a444f3de53d92118ad1439f3/build/liveview.js#L427] - This occurs because the liveview code is attempting to overwrite the global.L variable, globals are defined as readOnly [see here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/5ce893c20d97b8d62b100d331fa40c88744df2f2/iphone/Classes/KrollContext.m#L1101] and as all code in now run in strict mode this is now an error (credit to TIMOB-18465 for helping me figure this one out) There's two ways we can fix this 1. Remove kTiPropertyAttributeReadOnly on global properties 2. Stop making all JS core run in strict mode by default by adding {{modules: false}} to the object passed to preset-env, which will have a knock on effect to ES6 module support My vote goes for 1, but again this highlights the fact the transpilation step *_is going to cause breaking changes for people_* h5.Steps to reproduce # Enable transpilation by adding the {{<transpile>true</transpile>}} flag to your tiapp.xml # Build an app using liveview to iOS h5.Actual Error above is thrown h5.Expected No error thrown, liveview should work as normal""""",title+description
TIMOB-25786,12,"""Android: WebView eval JS timeout error ""","""""""h5. Issue  When setting run-on-main-thread to true webview.evalJS errors with the following message:     When setting run-on-main-thread to false webview.evalJS calls are executed as expected  This is important since the customer has to have run-on-main-thread in order to use Hyperloop    h5. Steps to replicate  1. download project:  [^evalJs-bug-demo.zip]   2. Run project to Android simulator and view console log  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView eval JS timeout error
Description: """"h5. Issue When setting run-on-main-thread to true webview.evalJS errors with the following message: When setting run-on-main-thread to false webview.evalJS calls are executed as expected This is important since the customer has to have run-on-main-thread in order to use Hyperloop h5. Steps to replicate 1. download project: [^evalJs-bug-demo.zip] 2. Run project to Android simulator and view console log """"",title+description
