TIMOB-25734,12,"""Android : TextField Click event is not firing with 7.0.X SDK""","""""""Click event is not firing on click of text field using with 7.0.X SDK    *Sample code:*          *Test Environment:*  <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 7.0.1  Operating System Mac OS X,Version 10.13.2,Architecture 64bit,   CPUs  4,Memory 8.0GB     Node.js Version             = 8.9.1     npm Version                 = 5.5.1    <USER>CLI 4.2.11    Core Package  7.0.1    Titanium CLI 5.0.14    node-appc Version 0.2.41   Titanium SDK 7.0.1.GA  Android Device: Samsung Galaxy J7  *Steps to reproduce: *  1. Create a sample classic app.   2. Replace app.js with the attached app.js file   3.Run the app in android device.   4.Click on textfield     *Output:* Click event is not firing    *Console logs:*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android : TextField Click event is not firing with 7.0.X SDK
Description: """"Click event is not firing on click of text field using with 7.0.X SDK *Sample code:* *Test Environment:* <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 7.0.1 Operating System Mac OS X,Version 10.13.2,Architecture 64bit, CPUs 4,Memory 8.0GB Node.js Version = 8.9.1 npm Version = 5.5.1 <USER>CLI 4.2.11 Core Package 7.0.1 Titanium CLI 5.0.14 node-appc Version 0.2.41 Titanium SDK 7.0.1.GA Android Device: Samsung Galaxy J7 *Steps to reproduce: * 1. Create a sample classic app. 2. Replace app.js with the attached app.js file 3.Run the app in android device. 4.Click on textfield *Output:* Click event is not firing *Console logs:* """"",title+description
TIMOB-25727,12,"""iOS:  base64decode issue observed with SDK 7.0.0 and above""","""""""Hi,  We have an oAuth login module to login to our app. During the login <USER> we will have to decode a token. For this we have used Titanium.Utils.base64decode(token).   The same code works for TiSDK 6.3.0 and below.   Once we upgraded the sdk to 7.0.0 the same returns undefined   Below is the toke thats received while logging in using oAuth.   token     We have checked this in a simple code with only the below line   Titanium.Utils.base64decode(token)   Works fine in 6.3.0 and returns undefined in 7.0.0 and above     Thanks     *EDIT by Hans*: This ticket also fixes an issues where Android would not accept Ti.Filesystem.File parameters in {{base64decode}}.   """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: base64decode issue observed with SDK 7.0.0 and above
Description: """"Hi, We have an oAuth login module to login to our app. During the login <USER> we will have to decode a token. For this we have used Titanium.Utils.base64decode(token). The same code works for TiSDK 6.3.0 and below. Once we upgraded the sdk to 7.0.0 the same returns undefined Below is the toke thats received while logging in using oAuth. token We have checked this in a simple code with only the below line Titanium.Utils.base64decode(token) Works fine in 6.3.0 and returns undefined in 7.0.0 and above Thanks *EDIT by Hans*: This ticket also fixes an issues where Android would not accept Ti.Filesystem.File parameters in {{base64decode}}. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25706,12,"""Different SDK versione for iOS and Android""","""""""It would be useful to define in the tiapp.xml file different versions of the SDK to be used according to the platform.    Currently I am in the problem of needing to use the latest version of SDK (7+) for iOS, while for Android I am forced to stay in version 6.3 as some third-party modules are not compatible with SDK 7+ (not they are 64bit).    Similar problem I had with the change to the requirements for the android modules with the SDK 6 (many modules have been updated after months).""""""",Improvement,"Title: Different SDK versione for iOS and Android
Description: """"It would be useful to define in the tiapp.xml file different versions of the SDK to be used according to the platform. Currently I am in the problem of needing to use the latest version of SDK (7+) for iOS, while for Android I am forced to stay in version 6.3 as some third-party modules are not compatible with SDK 7+ (not they are 64bit). Similar problem I had with the change to the requirements for the android modules with the SDK 6 (many modules have been updated after months).""""",title+description
TIMOB-25705,12,"""Prevent pasting in textfields""","""""""Right now it is always possible to paste in textfields, even though it is not always something you'd want. Adding a way to prevent this would increase the dynamicness of the textfield greatly.    How to do it in objective-c: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6701019/how-to-disable-copy-paste-option-from-uitextfield-programmatically    Android solution: https://www.myandroidsolutions.com/2013/10/05/android-prevent-cut-copy-paste-popup-to-be-displayed/""""""",Improvement,"Title: Prevent pasting in textfields
Description: """"Right now it is always possible to paste in textfields, even though it is not always something you'd want. Adding a way to prevent this would increase the dynamicness of the textfield greatly. How to do it in objective-c: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6701019/how-to-disable-copy-paste-option-from-uitextfield-programmatically Android solution: https://www.myandroidsolutions.com/2013/10/05/android-prevent-cut-copy-paste-popup-to-be-displayed/""""",title+description
