TIMOB-25618,12,"""App is unable to access Localytics method properly""","""""""h5. Description:   Customer is having issues accessing Localytics method properly    h5.  Code:   We are using the Localytics SDK for Analytics and we are having issues accessing a specific method. Attached is the pod file that we are using.     We are using the setOptions method to set the """"""""max_monitoring_regions"""""""" option in our titanium app but it does not work. Below is the code snippet.     Can you check if we are using the method in the right way with the right arguments?     Code:       h5. Podfile:   {quote}install! 'cocoapods',           :integrate_targets => false    platform :ios, '7.0'    target 'myWorkplace' do  pod 'LocalyticsStaticFramework', '~> 4.2'  end  {quote}    h5. Request:  Can you see any issues in their implementation or have any changes been made in hyperloop that they need to address in the implementation? """"""",Bug,"Title: App is unable to access Localytics method properly
Description: """"h5. Description: Customer is having issues accessing Localytics method properly h5. Code: We are using the Localytics SDK for Analytics and we are having issues accessing a specific method. Attached is the pod file that we are using. We are using the setOptions method to set the """"""""max_monitoring_regions"""""""" option in our titanium app but it does not work. Below is the code snippet. Can you check if we are using the method in the right way with the right arguments? Code: h5. Podfile: {quote}install! 'cocoapods', :integrate_targets => false platform :ios, '7.0' target 'myWorkplace' do pod 'LocalyticsStaticFramework', '~> 4.2' end {quote} h5. Request: Can you see any issues in their implementation or have any changes been made in hyperloop that they need to address in the implementation? """"",title+description
TIMOB-25615,12,"""ListItem height property doesn't work at all & no where it has been mentioned how to set a fixed height""","""""""*ListItem's height* property doesn't set the *height* of ListItem as it's mentioned in the docs at here: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListItem-property-height    Moreover, *height* property is listed as a direct property for *ListItem* since *Ti SDK 3.1.0* instead as an accessor or inherited property, so it is simply supposed to work irrespective of any *Ti SDK*.    Also, it is not mentioned anywhere that how users can set a *fixed height* to a *list-item*, so it's clueless for anyone who wants to set a fixed height.     I have tried this stuff on *Ti SDK 7.0.0.GA* for both iOS & Android & it doesn't just work on any platform. I couldn't try it on older SDK as I only have 7.0.0.GA.    Here's the very sample code picked from doc itself:          I have also attached a sample of how it look like on iOS 11.    One of the user in Ti-Slack told me that it only works if we use a class property on ItemTemplate & set height, backgroundColor on class. Here's what he meant:            Then only it works but again here's a glitch that if you try to set any property directly in XML, it doesn't work. It works only through a class defined in *.tss* file & it also creates below log warnings:            So, it's pretty clear that things are not working at all as they should be. Either way, there's an issue.   Thanks    """"""",Bug,"Title: ListItem height property doesn't work at all & no where it has been mentioned how to set a fixed height
Description: """"*ListItem's height* property doesn't set the *height* of ListItem as it's mentioned in the docs at here: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListItem-property-height Moreover, *height* property is listed as a direct property for *ListItem* since *Ti SDK 3.1.0* instead as an accessor or inherited property, so it is simply supposed to work irrespective of any *Ti SDK*. Also, it is not mentioned anywhere that how users can set a *fixed height* to a *list-item*, so it's clueless for anyone who wants to set a fixed height. I have tried this stuff on *Ti SDK 7.0.0.GA* for both iOS & Android & it doesn't just work on any platform. I couldn't try it on older SDK as I only have 7.0.0.GA. Here's the very sample code picked from doc itself: I have also attached a sample of how it look like on iOS 11. One of the user in Ti-Slack told me that it only works if we use a class property on ItemTemplate & set height, backgroundColor on class. Here's what he meant: Then only it works but again here's a glitch that if you try to set any property directly in XML, it doesn't work. It works only through a class defined in *.tss* file & it also creates below log warnings: So, it's pretty clear that things are not working at all as they should be. Either way, there's an issue. Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-25614,12,"""Windows: Hyperloop module latest version (3.0.1) does not bundle with latest SDK 7.0.0.GA ""","""""""Hello,    The *hyperloop latest version 3.0.1* does not bundle with the latest *SDK 7.0.0.GA* but when we manually download the module then it's working.    *keynotes of this issue:*  1. Customer is only using CLI and update everything from CLI  2. When they updated the latest SDK by using CLI then the Hyperloop does not update    *Hyperloop module shows below error:*       *Current Results:*  Hyperloop does not update with the latest SDK    *Expected Results:*  The latest Hyperloop 3.0.1 should be bundled with SDK 7.0.0.GA     Note: Reference which said """"""""[Highlights for this release include integration of Hyperloop in the SDK core|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Titanium_SDK_Release_Notes]""""""""    Thanks  """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Hyperloop module latest version (3.0.1) does not bundle with latest SDK 7.0.0.GA
Description: """"Hello, The *hyperloop latest version 3.0.1* does not bundle with the latest *SDK 7.0.0.GA* but when we manually download the module then it's working. *keynotes of this issue:* 1. Customer is only using CLI and update everything from CLI 2. When they updated the latest SDK by using CLI then the Hyperloop does not update *Hyperloop module shows below error:* *Current Results:* Hyperloop does not update with the latest SDK *Expected Results:* The latest Hyperloop 3.0.1 should be bundled with SDK 7.0.0.GA Note: Reference which said """"""""[Highlights for this release include integration of Hyperloop in the SDK core|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Titanium_SDK_Release_Notes]"""""""" Thanks """"",title+description
