TIMOB-25514,12,"""Android: Vertical ScrollView.scrollTo() goes to wrong position when animated as of 6.2.2""","""""""*Summary:*  The ScrollView.scrollTo() method, when """"""""animated"""""""" is set to true, will not always scroll to the given position for """"""""vertical"""""""" scroll views as of Titanium 6.2.2.    *Steps to reproduce:*    # Build and run the below code on Android via Titanium 6.2.2 or higher.  # Scroll down to the bottom of the ScrollView.  # Tap the """"""""Scroll to Top"""""""" button.        *Result:*  The ScrollView does not scroll to the top.    *Expected Result:*  The scrollTo() method should go to the given position.    *Notes:*  * The scrollTo() function will work if not set up to be animated.  * The scrollTo() function will work when starting from the top of the ScrollView to scroll down, but is unreliable when called from any other scroll position.  * This is not an issue with horizontal ScrollViews.  * This appears to be a bug in Google's """"""""NestedScrollView"""""""" Java class. It's smoothScrollTo() and fullScroll() methods are now unreliable, but its non-smooth scrolling methods work fine.    *Work-Around:*  The scrollTo() method will work when not set up to be animated, like this...      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Vertical ScrollView.scrollTo() goes to wrong position when animated as of 6.2.2
Description: """"*Summary:* The ScrollView.scrollTo() method, when """"""""animated"""""""" is set to true, will not always scroll to the given position for """"""""vertical"""""""" scroll views as of Titanium 6.2.2. *Steps to reproduce:* # Build and run the below code on Android via Titanium 6.2.2 or higher. # Scroll down to the bottom of the ScrollView. # Tap the """"""""Scroll to Top"""""""" button. *Result:* The ScrollView does not scroll to the top. *Expected Result:* The scrollTo() method should go to the given position. *Notes:* * The scrollTo() function will work if not set up to be animated. * The scrollTo() function will work when starting from the top of the ScrollView to scroll down, but is unreliable when called from any other scroll position. * This is not an issue with horizontal ScrollViews. * This appears to be a bug in Google's """"""""NestedScrollView"""""""" Java class. It's smoothScrollTo() and fullScroll() methods are now unreliable, but its non-smooth scrolling methods work fine. *Work-Around:* The scrollTo() method will work when not set up to be animated, like this... """"",title+description
TIMOB-25509,12,"""Module build should automatically update manifest `apiversion` and `minSDK`""","""""""When building a module if the apiversion in the manifest does not match the platforms apiversion in the SDK then the module build will fail.    Ideally, the {{apiversion}} and {{minSDK}} should be the product of a build, and dictated by the module build for the selected SDK version.  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Module build should automatically update manifest `apiversion` and `minSDK`
Description: """"When building a module if the apiversion in the manifest does not match the platforms apiversion in the SDK then the module build will fail. Ideally, the {{apiversion}} and {{minSDK}} should be the product of a build, and dictated by the module build for the selected SDK version. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25504,12,"""-2436h@3x Images on iPhone X are not used when -736h@3x exists""","""""""When using <EMAIL> images are not picked up when running on iPhone X if  an <EMAIL> exists.  It works fine with splash screens but not on other images.    The code below should be checking if running on iPhone X or iPhone 6/7 Plus and choose file accordingly.    {code:title=TiUtils.m}   if ([TiUtils isRetinaHDDisplay]) {    // first try -736h@3x iPhone 6 Plus specific    NSString *testpath = [NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""%@-736h@3x.%@"""""""",partial,ext];    if ([fm fileExistsAtPath:testpath]) {     return [NSURL fileURLWithPath:testpath];    }              // second try -2436h@3x iPhone X specific        testpath = [NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""%@-2436h@3x.%@"""""""", partial, ext];        if ([fm fileExistsAtPath:testpath]) {         return [NSURL fileURLWithPath:testpath];       }          // third try plain @3x    testpath = [NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""%@@3x.%@"""""""",partial,ext];    if ([fm fileExistsAtPath:testpath]) {     return [NSURL fileURLWithPath:testpath];    }   }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: -2436h@3x Images on iPhone X are not used when -736h@3x exists
Description: """"When using <EMAIL> images are not picked up when running on iPhone X if an <EMAIL> exists. It works fine with splash screens but not on other images. The code below should be checking if running on iPhone X or iPhone 6/7 Plus and choose file accordingly. {code:title=TiUtils.m} if ([TiUtils isRetinaHDDisplay]) { // first try -736h@3x iPhone 6 Plus specific NSString *testpath = [NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""%@-736h@3x.%@"""""""",partial,ext]; if ([fm fileExistsAtPath:testpath]) { return [NSURL fileURLWithPath:testpath]; } // second try -2436h@3x iPhone X specific testpath = [NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""%@-2436h@3x.%@"""""""", partial, ext]; if ([fm fileExistsAtPath:testpath]) { return [NSURL fileURLWithPath:testpath]; } // third try plain @3x testpath = [NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""%@@3x.%@"""""""",partial,ext]; if ([fm fileExistsAtPath:testpath]) { return [NSURL fileURLWithPath:testpath]; } } {code}""""",title+description
