TIMOB-25464,12,"""Windows: bubbleParent=false not working as expected""","""""""h5. Issue Description     Adding bubbleParent: false (either in the tss or controller file) to a UI element does not remove the bubbling.     h5. STEPS TO REPRODUCE:     1.- Open and run the sample project (https://drive.google.com/open?id=0BwTWo-c2a0b9VGQ2V3kxR2Uxd1U)  2.- A blue view (outerWrapper) with a red view in within (innerWrapper1) will be displayed.   3.- Go to index.tss and observe how innerWrapper1 has its bubbleParent property set to false.   4.- Go back to the app and click in the red view (innerWrapper1).   5.- Observe how in the console logs two logging lines are printed, when it should be only one.     NOTE: Exact same thing happens if the bubbleParent property is set in the controller (index.js)     Is this a platform bug?     Console log:       """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: bubbleParent=false not working as expected
Description: """"h5. Issue Description Adding bubbleParent: false (either in the tss or controller file) to a UI element does not remove the bubbling. h5. STEPS TO REPRODUCE: 1.- Open and run the sample project (https://drive.google.com/open?id=0BwTWo-c2a0b9VGQ2V3kxR2Uxd1U) 2.- A blue view (outerWrapper) with a red view in within (innerWrapper1) will be displayed. 3.- Go to index.tss and observe how innerWrapper1 has its bubbleParent property set to false. 4.- Go back to the app and click in the red view (innerWrapper1). 5.- Observe how in the console logs two logging lines are printed, when it should be only one. NOTE: Exact same thing happens if the bubbleParent property is set in the controller (index.js) Is this a platform bug? Console log: """"",title+description
