TIMOB-25452,12,"""iOS: Build fails after Alloy compiling""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce Try to Run on simulator your project, even an 'Hello world' project    Name                        = Mac OS X   Version                     = 10.12.6   Architecture                = 64bit   # CPUs                      = 4   Memory                      = 8589934592 Node.js   Node.js Version             = 4.2.2   npm Version                 = 2.14.7 Titanium CLI   CLI Version                 = 5.0.14 Titanium SDK   SDK Version                 = 6.2.2.GA   SDK Path                    = /Users/braindoo/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/6.2.2.GA   Target Platform             = iphone  h3. Actual Result The build terminates without errors in an abnormal way after starting third party framwork detection: [DEBUG] :  iOS WWDR certificate: installed [INFO] :   Minimum iOS version: 8.0 [INFO] :   Logging enabled on port 40208 [INFO] :   Debugging disabled [INFO] :   Profiler disabled [INFO] :   Set to copy files instead of symlinking [INFO] :   Forcing clean build: /Users/braindoo/Documents/Titanium_Workspace_BDRevolution/testtwo/build/iphone/build-manifest.json does not exist [INFO] :   Initializing the build directory [DEBUG] :  Creating /Users/braindoo/Documents/Titanium_Workspace_BDRevolution/testtwo/build/iphone [TRACE] :  Starting third-party framework detection  h3. Expected Result the build phase continues and appc launches xcode building and ios simulator""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Build fails after Alloy compiling
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce Try to Run on simulator your project, even an 'Hello world' project Name = Mac OS X Version = 10.12.6 Architecture = 64bit # CPUs = 4 Memory = 8589934592 Node.js Node.js Version = 4.2.2 npm Version = 2.14.7 Titanium CLI CLI Version = 5.0.14 Titanium SDK SDK Version = 6.2.2.GA SDK Path = /Users/braindoo/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/6.2.2.GA Target Platform = iphone h3. Actual Result The build terminates without errors in an abnormal way after starting third party framwork detection: [DEBUG] : iOS WWDR certificate: installed [INFO] : Minimum iOS version: 8.0 [INFO] : Logging enabled on port 40208 [INFO] : Debugging disabled [INFO] : Profiler disabled [INFO] : Set to copy files instead of symlinking [INFO] : Forcing clean build: /Users/braindoo/Documents/Titanium_Workspace_BDRevolution/testtwo/build/iphone/build-manifest.json does not exist [INFO] : Initializing the build directory [DEBUG] : Creating /Users/braindoo/Documents/Titanium_Workspace_BDRevolution/testtwo/build/iphone [TRACE] : Starting third-party framework detection h3. Expected Result the build phase continues and appc launches xcode building and ios simulator""""",title+description
TIMOB-25450,12,"""Hyperloop: iOS - Cannot run likely due to outdated dependency""","""""""I'm attempting to enable Hyperloop in an existing Titanium iOS project. I couldn't find documentation on how to do this via the CLI, so I did enabled it using <USER>Studio. Enabling it there, it added the Hyperloop module and the plugin to the project's {{tiapp.xml}}.    On building the project, now with Hyperloop, this error appears:        I suspect the cause of this error is this file and line in Hyperloop plugin: {{hyperloop/2.2.1/hooks/ios/node_modules/acorn/dist/acorn.js:3339}}:        My initial suspicion is that the {{acorn}} module is no longer compatible with more modern versions of Node.js. The {{acorn}} module installed is version {{2.7.0}} (released [January 2016|https://github.com/ternjs/acorn/releases/tag/2.7.0]) whereas [the most recent release is {{5.1.2}}|https://www.npmjs.com/package/acorn].    I could not find instructions on updating Hyperloop manually. I believe Hyperloop 2.2.1 to be the most recent version publicly available.""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: iOS - Cannot run likely due to outdated dependency
Description: """"I'm attempting to enable Hyperloop in an existing Titanium iOS project. I couldn't find documentation on how to do this via the CLI, so I did enabled it using <USER>Studio. Enabling it there, it added the Hyperloop module and the plugin to the project's {{tiapp.xml}}. On building the project, now with Hyperloop, this error appears: I suspect the cause of this error is this file and line in Hyperloop plugin: {{hyperloop/2.2.1/hooks/ios/node_modules/acorn/dist/acorn.js:3339}}: My initial suspicion is that the {{acorn}} module is no longer compatible with more modern versions of Node.js. The {{acorn}} module installed is version {{2.7.0}} (released [January 2016|https://github.com/ternjs/acorn/releases/tag/2.7.0]) whereas [the most recent release is {{5.1.2}}|https://www.npmjs.com/package/acorn]. I could not find instructions on updating Hyperloop manually. I believe Hyperloop 2.2.1 to be the most recent version publicly available.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25449,12,"""iOS: WebView content offset of 20 pixels when positioned at the top""","""""""A """"""""fullscreen"""""""" Titanium.UI.WebView in 6.2.2.GA (older versions too, at least 6.1.2.GA) will contain a dead zone at the top which is 20dip tall (top bar sized). The bar disappears upon scrolling a page that scrolls, but if a full-screen mapping application which manages its own touches and navigation is used, the bar is constant. This does not appear on Android.    Code to reproduce:      See screenshot for example. The green area (#00cc00) is the backgroundColor of the webview. If that color is unset, it defaults to white.    I'm working around this by hiding the webview inside another view container and setting the top property to -20, but this shouldn't be necessary in my mind.    The issue _does not_ seem to happen if you set the top property to something farther down the page by at least 20 dips:  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: WebView content offset of 20 pixels when positioned at the top
Description: """"A """"""""fullscreen"""""""" Titanium.UI.WebView in 6.2.2.GA (older versions too, at least 6.1.2.GA) will contain a dead zone at the top which is 20dip tall (top bar sized). The bar disappears upon scrolling a page that scrolls, but if a full-screen mapping application which manages its own touches and navigation is used, the bar is constant. This does not appear on Android. Code to reproduce: See screenshot for example. The green area (#00cc00) is the backgroundColor of the webview. If that color is unset, it defaults to white. I'm working around this by hiding the webview inside another view container and setting the top property to -20, but this shouldn't be necessary in my mind. The issue _does not_ seem to happen if you set the top property to something farther down the page by at least 20 dips: """"",title+description
TIMOB-25447,12,"""Cannot use setTabs() multiple times on a tabGroup + splitWindow""","""""""My app has a mode that uses the splitWindow on iPad.     The user can change functions which needs to change the tabs / windows available in the splitWindow masterView.    I do this by using TabGroup.setTabs([tabsArray1]); or tabsArray2. This will always work fine the first 2 times, but then the first window in one of the tabs will become FULLSCREEN and the app is effectively dead.    I have created as small an example as possible to illustrate the bug. Click the setTabs1 or 2 buttons a couple of times to see the issue.    I recently upgraded my SDK from 5.2.X > Latest GA it's moving to 6.X.X so this is a regression I believe.    Thanks!""""""",Bug,"Title: Cannot use setTabs() multiple times on a tabGroup + splitWindow
Description: """"My app has a mode that uses the splitWindow on iPad. The user can change functions which needs to change the tabs / windows available in the splitWindow masterView. I do this by using TabGroup.setTabs([tabsArray1]); or tabsArray2. This will always work fine the first 2 times, but then the first window in one of the tabs will become FULLSCREEN and the app is effectively dead. I have created as small an example as possible to illustrate the bug. Click the setTabs1 or 2 buttons a couple of times to see the issue. I recently upgraded my SDK from 5.2.X > Latest GA it's moving to 6.X.X so this is a regression I believe. Thanks!""""",title+description
TIMOB-25445,12,"""Error loading images from res-ldpi, res-hdpi, ect. folders on Android 7.1.1""","""""""When using image folders 'res-ldpi/mdpi/hdpi/xhdpi/xxhdpi/xxxhdpi' for app running on Android Emulator (7.1.1), studio generates following errors and none of the images from these folders are NOT loaded...    [WARN] :   TiDrawableReference: (pool-3-thread-2) [0,671] Could not open stream to get bitmap  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference: (pool-3-thread-1) [89,760] Problem opening stream with url /images/ic_key.png: Resources/images/ic_key.png  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference: java.io.FileNotFoundException: Resources/images/ic_key.png  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at android.content.res.AssetManager.openAsset(Native Method)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:347)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:321)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiFileHelper.openInputStream(TiFileHelper.java:222)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at org.<USER>titanium.view.TiDrawableReference.getInputStream(TiDrawableReference.java:863)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at org.<USER>titanium.view.TiDrawableReference.getBitmap(TiDrawableReference.java:346)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at org.<USER>titanium.view.TiDrawableReference.getBitmap(TiDrawableReference.java:303)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiLoadImageManager$LoadImageJob.run(TiLoadImageManager.java:128)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1133)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:607)  [ERROR] :  TiDrawableReference:  at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:761)  [WARN] :   TiDrawableReference: (pool-3-thread-1) [2,762] Could not open stream to get bitmap      To create the error, change the DPI specific folders in assets/android/images/ to res-hdpi, res-mdpi, etc and access an image from these folders from your app.    Use the following code to replicate the issue:    <Alloy>   <Window  id=""""""""loginWindow""""""""  >    <View  class=""""""""container"""""""">     <View class=""""""""partTop"""""""">      <ImageView image=""""""""logoLogin.png"""""""" />     </View>     <View  layout=""""""""vertical"""""""" top=""""""""0"""""""" class=""""""""partBottom"""""""" >      <View  class=""""""""paneTF"""""""" >       <ImageView image=""""""""/images/ic_person.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconTF"""""""" left=""""""""6""""""""   />       <TextField id=""""""""username"""""""" hintText=""""""""Username"""""""" left=""""""""10"""""""" />      </View>      <View  class=""""""""paneTF"""""""" >       <ImageView image=""""""""/images/ic_key.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconTF"""""""" left=""""""""6"""""""" />       <TextField id=""""""""password"""""""" hintText=""""""""Password"""""""" left=""""""""10"""""""" />      </View>      <Button title=""""""""Sign In"""""""" class=""""""""H3 btn"""""""" onClick=""""""""login"""""""" />       </View>    </View>   </Window>  </Alloy>      """"""",Bug,"Title: Error loading images from res-ldpi, res-hdpi, ect. folders on Android 7.1.1
Description: """"When using image folders 'res-ldpi/mdpi/hdpi/xhdpi/xxhdpi/xxxhdpi' for app running on Android Emulator (7.1.1), studio generates following errors and none of the images from these folders are NOT loaded... [WARN] : TiDrawableReference: (pool-3-thread-2) [0,671] Could not open stream to get bitmap [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: (pool-3-thread-1) [89,760] Problem opening stream with url /images/ic_key.png: Resources/images/ic_key.png [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: java.io.FileNotFoundException: Resources/images/ic_key.png [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at android.content.res.AssetManager.openAsset(Native Method) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:347) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:321) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiFileHelper.openInputStream(TiFileHelper.java:222) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at org.<USER>titanium.view.TiDrawableReference.getInputStream(TiDrawableReference.java:863) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at org.<USER>titanium.view.TiDrawableReference.getBitmap(TiDrawableReference.java:346) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at org.<USER>titanium.view.TiDrawableReference.getBitmap(TiDrawableReference.java:303) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiLoadImageManager$LoadImageJob.run(TiLoadImageManager.java:128) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1133) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:607) [ERROR] : TiDrawableReference: at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:761) [WARN] : TiDrawableReference: (pool-3-thread-1) [2,762] Could not open stream to get bitmap To create the error, change the DPI specific folders in assets/android/images/ to res-hdpi, res-mdpi, etc and access an image from these folders from your app. Use the following code to replicate the issue: <Alloy> <Window id=""""""""loginWindow"""""""" > <View class=""""""""container""""""""> <View class=""""""""partTop""""""""> <ImageView image=""""""""logoLogin.png"""""""" /> </View> <View layout=""""""""vertical"""""""" top=""""""""0"""""""" class=""""""""partBottom"""""""" > <View class=""""""""paneTF"""""""" > <ImageView image=""""""""/images/ic_person.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconTF"""""""" left=""""""""6"""""""" /> <TextField id=""""""""username"""""""" hintText=""""""""Username"""""""" left=""""""""10"""""""" /> </View> <View class=""""""""paneTF"""""""" > <ImageView image=""""""""/images/ic_key.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconTF"""""""" left=""""""""6"""""""" /> <TextField id=""""""""password"""""""" hintText=""""""""Password"""""""" left=""""""""10"""""""" /> </View> <Button title=""""""""Sign In"""""""" class=""""""""H3 btn"""""""" onClick=""""""""login"""""""" /> </View> </View> </Window> </Alloy> """"",title+description
TIMOB-25444,12,"""Titanium.UI.SIZE doesn't work for TableView on Android""","""""""Create a basic alloy app and add the below code to index.xml.    Issues seems to be OK when using Titanium SDK 6.1.2    <Alloy>   <Window class=""""""""container"""""""">    <View layout=""""""""vertical"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""orange"""""""" height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""" >     <TableView width=""""""""90%""""""""  height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""" top=""""""""0"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""olive"""""""" >      <TableViewRow  height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""" >       <ImageView image=""""""""/images/apiHealth.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconRowTitle"""""""" />       <Label text=""""""""API Health"""""""" class=""""""""textRowTitle"""""""" />      </TableViewRow>      <TableViewRow height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""">       <ImageView image=""""""""/images/consEng.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconRowTitle"""""""" />       <Label text=""""""""Consumer Engagement"""""""" class=""""""""textRowTitle"""""""" />      </TableViewRow>      <TableViewRow height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""">       <ImageView image=""""""""/images/apiUsage.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconRowTitle"""""""" />       <Label text=""""""""API Usage"""""""" class=""""""""textRowTitle"""""""" />      </TableViewRow>      <TableViewRow height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""">       <ImageView image=""""""""/images/apiInfra.png"""""""" class=""""""""iconRowTitle"""""""" />       <Label text=""""""""Infrastructure Health"""""""" class=""""""""textRowTitle"""""""" />      </TableViewRow>     </TableView>     <View width=""""""""90%"""""""" height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""" top=""""""""20"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""pink"""""""">      <TableView width=""""""""100%"""""""" height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""" class=""""""""noStyleTable""""""""   backgroundColor=""""""""#f1f8f9"""""""" >       <TableViewSection headerTitle=""""""""Current Activity Performance"""""""" class=""""""""H3""""""""  >        <TableViewRow class=""""""""horizontal"""""""" >         <Label id=""""""""transComp"""""""" text=""""""""0""""""""  class=""""""""data"""""""" />         <Label text=""""""""Transactions Completed""""""""  />        </TableViewRow>        <TableViewRow class=""""""""horizontal"""""""" >         <Label id=""""""""avgResp"""""""" text=""""""""0""""""""  class=""""""""data"""""""" />         <Label text=""""""""Average Response Time""""""""  />        </TableViewRow>        <TableViewRow class=""""""""horizontal"""""""" >         <Label id=""""""""tps"""""""" text=""""""""0""""""""  class=""""""""data"""""""" />         <Label text=""""""""TPS"""""""" />        </TableViewRow>       </TableViewSection>      </TableView>     </View>    </View>   </Window>  </Alloy>""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.UI.SIZE doesn't work for TableView on Android
