TIMOB-25427,12,"""[Android] Add support for Android dynamic animation introduced in Android compat library 25.3""","""""""Add support for dynamic animation in Android, maybe it would be possible to have parity with dynamic animations in ios.    example: [Dynamic animation gist|https://gist.github.com/nickbutcher/7fdce476aaa589680cdd626d78e3149d]     [Android docs|https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/graphics/physics-based-animation.html]""""""",Bug,"Title: [Android] Add support for Android dynamic animation introduced in Android compat library 25.3
Description: """"Add support for dynamic animation in Android, maybe it would be possible to have parity with dynamic animations in ios. example: [Dynamic animation gist|https://gist.github.com/nickbutcher/7fdce476aaa589680cdd626d78e3149d] [Android docs|https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/graphics/physics-based-animation.html]""""",title+description
TIMOB-25426,12,"""Hyperloop: iOS - Metabase binary has wrong file-permissions, causing build to fail""","""""""There are some reports indicating the the Hyperloop metabase binary in {{plugins/hyperloop/2.2.0/hooks/ios/node_modules/hyperloop-metabase/bin/metabase}} seems to have incorrect file permissions ({{\-rw\-rw\-rw\-}}) that prevents it from being executed. The curious thing is that the Github release has correct ones ({{-rwxr-xr-x}}).    So it seems either to be an issue with the dashboard if it's unpacking and repacking it for registry-purposes or with the appc-cli when unpacking it locally after downloading. I remember we had a similar issue a while ago and didn't expect it to come back.    Initially fixed in CLI-1101.    *EDIT*: The real issue is that [this PR|https://github.com/<USER>hyperloop.next/pull/210] messed up quite a few node-related build-steps, which we mainly resolved before 2.2.0 already. But it also moved the path of the node_modules from {{plugins/hyperloop/2.2.0/node_modules/}} to {{plugins/hyperloop/2.2.0/ios/node_modules}} which cannot be detected by the initial [CLI-hook|https://github.com/<USER>appc-cli-titanium/blob/master/plugins/util.js#L554] which still searches for the binary in the old directory. We should rather fix the Hyperloop packaging instead of requiring a new appc-cli update. """"""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: iOS - Metabase binary has wrong file-permissions, causing build to fail
Description: """"There are some reports indicating the the Hyperloop metabase binary in {{plugins/hyperloop/2.2.0/hooks/ios/node_modules/hyperloop-metabase/bin/metabase}} seems to have incorrect file permissions ({{\-rw\-rw\-rw\-}}) that prevents it from being executed. The curious thing is that the Github release has correct ones ({{-rwxr-xr-x}}). So it seems either to be an issue with the dashboard if it's unpacking and repacking it for registry-purposes or with the appc-cli when unpacking it locally after downloading. I remember we had a similar issue a while ago and didn't expect it to come back. Initially fixed in CLI-1101. *EDIT*: The real issue is that [this PR|https://github.com/<USER>hyperloop.next/pull/210] messed up quite a few node-related build-steps, which we mainly resolved before 2.2.0 already. But it also moved the path of the node_modules from {{plugins/hyperloop/2.2.0/node_modules/}} to {{plugins/hyperloop/2.2.0/ios/node_modules}} which cannot be detected by the initial [CLI-hook|https://github.com/<USER>appc-cli-titanium/blob/master/plugins/util.js#L554] which still searches for the binary in the old directory. We should rather fix the Hyperloop packaging instead of requiring a new appc-cli update. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25424,12,"""iOS: Unnecessary symbols compiled to the app""","""""""When using 6.3.x, there were some reports of rejected apps because of the missing NSAppleMusicUsageDescription which we fixed a while ago but popped up with some other changes the last month. This ticket should solve those issues as well as wrapping other API's that were currently compiled although not used (e.g. Ti.WatchSession). """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Unnecessary symbols compiled to the app
Description: """"When using 6.3.x, there were some reports of rejected apps because of the missing NSAppleMusicUsageDescription which we fixed a while ago but popped up with some other changes the last month. This ticket should solve those issues as well as wrapping other API's that were currently compiled although not used (e.g. Ti.WatchSession). """"",title+description
