TIMOB-25410,12,"""Android: ContentHeight set to auto positions a view with bottom zero at the top of a scrollview""","""""""*This is a regression. Not seen with 6.2.2.GA*    h5.Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the below code in your app.js:    2. Build for android device/emulator.    h5.Actual results:  The green label is at the top of ScrollView.    h5.Expected results:  The green label should be at the bottom of the ScrollView.    h5. Work-Around:  Set the ScrollView.contentHeight to Ti.UI.FILL""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ContentHeight set to auto positions a view with bottom zero at the top of a scrollview
Description: """"*This is a regression. Not seen with 6.2.2.GA* h5.Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the below code in your app.js: 2. Build for android device/emulator. h5.Actual results: The green label is at the top of ScrollView. h5.Expected results: The green label should be at the bottom of the ScrollView. h5. Work-Around: Set the ScrollView.contentHeight to Ti.UI.FILL""""",title+description
TIMOB-25406,12,"""Android: First run for emulator doesn't see emulator started""","""""""I have created a nexus device from Android Studio 2. The first time I run for this emulator it wants to start the emulator, and then will install/launch the app when emulator is booted.    However, it never detects the boot completed. I always have to compile a second time for it to see the emulator properly.    The logs are here: https://gist.github.com/Topener/31d24cdb3235d1b4c5f96621ab4ed08a    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: First run for emulator doesn't see emulator started
Description: """"I have created a nexus device from Android Studio 2. The first time I run for this emulator it wants to start the emulator, and then will install/launch the app when emulator is booted. However, it never detects the boot completed. I always have to compile a second time for it to see the emulator properly. The logs are here: https://gist.github.com/Topener/31d24cdb3235d1b4c5f96621ab4ed08a """"",title+description
TIMOB-25404,12,"""Upgrade titanium module for android push notifications to use google firebase sdk""","""""""Based on this https://developers.google.com/cloud-messaging/faq, gcm sdk will no longer receive any new features. It is recommended to upgrade to firebase sdk.    The differences between GCM and FCM setup is outlined here .  https://developers.google.com/cloud-messaging/android/android-migrate-fcm    Since there is are differences in how devices subscribe/register/unregister for Push Notifications, the Titanium Module for Push Notifications should be enhanced to support developers using FCM to send push notifications to Titanium Apps in Android.     Relevant ticket. https://techweb.axway.com/jira/browse/MBAAS-4896""""""",New Feature,"Title: Upgrade titanium module for android push notifications to use google firebase sdk
Description: """"Based on this https://developers.google.com/cloud-messaging/faq, gcm sdk will no longer receive any new features. It is recommended to upgrade to firebase sdk. The differences between GCM and FCM setup is outlined here . https://developers.google.com/cloud-messaging/android/android-migrate-fcm Since there is are differences in how devices subscribe/register/unregister for Push Notifications, the Titanium Module for Push Notifications should be enhanced to support developers using FCM to send push notifications to Titanium Apps in Android. Relevant ticket. https://techweb.axway.com/jira/browse/MBAAS-4896""""",title+description
TIMOB-25393,12,"""Adding Third-Party iOS Framework causes build error with 6.2.x""","""""""We're experimenting with integration of third-party libraries and frameworks with Hyperloop.    We added the ContentfulAPI ObjC Framework to the app/platform/ios directory of the hyperloop_examples app.  When we built the app with either SDK 6.2.1 or 6.2.2, we get this error late in the build <USER>..    2017-10-14T20:24:55.215Z | ERROR  | An uncaught exception was thrown!  (buildSettings.LD_RUNPATH_SEARCH_PATHS || """""""""""""""").replace is not a function  2017-10-14T20:24:55.216Z | ERROR  | (buildSettings.LD_RUNPATH_SEARCH_PATHS || """""""""""""""").replace is not a function    When we remove the Framework, the build completes successfully.      I've attached the log.  This appears to be either a regression based on comments in other reports that this mechanism worked.    Also, parenthetically, and the source of another JIRA report not yet filed - we did attempt to use the Contentful Pod and that also resulted in build errors.  So at this point we're shall we say """"""""stymied"""""""" with respect to integrating the Contentful SDK.  We've also tried to do the same with the Flurry SDK and have also encountered problems.""""""",Bug,"Title: Adding Third-Party iOS Framework causes build error with 6.2.x
Description: """"We're experimenting with integration of third-party libraries and frameworks with Hyperloop. We added the ContentfulAPI ObjC Framework to the app/platform/ios directory of the hyperloop_examples app. When we built the app with either SDK 6.2.1 or 6.2.2, we get this error late in the build <USER>.. 2017-10-14T20:24:55.215Z | ERROR | An uncaught exception was thrown! (buildSettings.LD_RUNPATH_SEARCH_PATHS || """""""""""""""").replace is not a function 2017-10-14T20:24:55.216Z | ERROR | (buildSettings.LD_RUNPATH_SEARCH_PATHS || """""""""""""""").replace is not a function When we remove the Framework, the build completes successfully. I've attached the log. This appears to be either a regression based on comments in other reports that this mechanism worked. Also, parenthetically, and the source of another JIRA report not yet filed - we did attempt to use the Contentful Pod and that also resulted in build errors. So at this point we're shall we say """"""""stymied"""""""" with respect to integrating the Contentful SDK. We've also tried to do the same with the Flurry SDK and have also encountered problems.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25388,12,"""Android: TextField borderColor is not showing on latest SDK (6.2.2.GA)""","""""""Hello,    We have tested an issue on the following environment and find that TextField borderColor is not showing on latest SDK (6.2.2.GA) but it is working on previous SDK.    *Testing Environment:*  Ti SDK: 6.2.2.GA, 6.1.1.GA  <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 6.2.4  Android Device: Samsung Galaxy Grand Prime (5.1.1)    *Test Code:*      *Test Results:*  TextField borderColor is not showing on latest SDK (6.2.2.GA). Attached the output screenShots.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField borderColor is not showing on latest SDK (6.2.2.GA)
