TIMOB-25371,12,"""iOS : Ad Hoc distribution, generate the Appname.plist file for over-the-air installation""","""""""It's possibile to distribute an iOS App from Safari with a simple link, this only if the ipa generated is an adhoc distribution.    I use this option instead of using TestFlight, so the app will expire after 10 months (when the adhoc distribution certificate expire) and not after 3 months as the Testflight builds.    To do this i did this:  # Titanium > Package > iOS Adhoc/Enterprise . Titanium generates these files : Appname.ipa, DistributionSummary.plist, ExportOptions.plist and Packaging.log  # In a webserver with https/ssl enabled i have created an html file with a link with this url:     In the same folder (testfolder) i put: Appname.ipa, Appname.plist, the 2 images and the html file.  # Titanium doesn't generate the Appname.plist file for over-the-air installation. This is the file that is needed (with the same name of the ipa -> Appname.plist)      So the question is if this file can also be generated automatically when we do an adhoc distribution.     On stackoverflow i found this image of xCode 9 (see attachment)    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS : Ad Hoc distribution, generate the Appname.plist file for over-the-air installation
Description: """"It's possibile to distribute an iOS App from Safari with a simple link, this only if the ipa generated is an adhoc distribution. I use this option instead of using TestFlight, so the app will expire after 10 months (when the adhoc distribution certificate expire) and not after 3 months as the Testflight builds. To do this i did this: # Titanium > Package > iOS Adhoc/Enterprise . Titanium generates these files : Appname.ipa, DistributionSummary.plist, ExportOptions.plist and Packaging.log # In a webserver with https/ssl enabled i have created an html file with a link with this url: In the same folder (testfolder) i put: Appname.ipa, Appname.plist, the 2 images and the html file. # Titanium doesn't generate the Appname.plist file for over-the-air installation. This is the file that is needed (with the same name of the ipa -> Appname.plist) So the question is if this file can also be generated automatically when we do an adhoc distribution. On stackoverflow i found this image of xCode 9 (see attachment) """"",title+description
TIMOB-25370,12,"""Android: Scrolling up with Swipe Refresh Control doesn't work""","""""""After upgrading to Titanium SDK 6 we faced a cretical issue with all ListView/TableViews and ScrollView, that uses this module (https://github.com/raymondkam/Ti.SwipeRefreshLayout) for pull to refresh,    The issue is as follows:  * Scrol down in a scrollview for example.  * Remove your finger.  * Try to scroll up, you cannot, since the module will capture the event first and refreshes the list.    Before we were using Titanium SDK 6.1.2.GA and it was working as expected.    Thanks,""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Scrolling up with Swipe Refresh Control doesn't work
Description: """"After upgrading to Titanium SDK 6 we faced a cretical issue with all ListView/TableViews and ScrollView, that uses this module (https://github.com/raymondkam/Ti.SwipeRefreshLayout) for pull to refresh, The issue is as follows: * Scrol down in a scrollview for example. * Remove your finger. * Try to scroll up, you cannot, since the module will capture the event first and refreshes the list. Before we were using Titanium SDK 6.1.2.GA and it was working as expected. Thanks,""""",title+description
TIMOB-25369,12,"""Andriod Theming against Widgets Stopped working in SDK 6.1""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce Create a simple app that contains a button with a mixed case title, and include the attached themes.xml under /platform/android/res/values/.  Build in SDK 6.0.4 and notice that the text on the button supports mixed case.  Build the same app with SDK 6.1.2 and notice that the button tiltle is now in all caps.  If the method of theming has changed, please update latest documentation.  h3. Actual Result The custom theme is not applied to the app when built with SDK 6.1.2 - resulting in button text in all caps.  Note: SDK 6.2 has the same behavior as 6.1.  h3. Expected Result Button title should be displayed in mixed case when built in 6.1.2.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Andriod Theming against Widgets Stopped working in SDK 6.1
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce Create a simple app that contains a button with a mixed case title, and include the attached themes.xml under /platform/android/res/values/. Build in SDK 6.0.4 and notice that the text on the button supports mixed case. Build the same app with SDK 6.1.2 and notice that the button tiltle is now in all caps. If the method of theming has changed, please update latest documentation. h3. Actual Result The custom theme is not applied to the app when built with SDK 6.1.2 - resulting in button text in all caps. Note: SDK 6.2 has the same behavior as 6.1. h3. Expected Result Button title should be displayed in mixed case when built in 6.1.2. """"",title+description
