TIMOB-25301,12,"""iPhone X: Need to be able to control the Insets / Layout Margins""","""""""I am not sure what property will allow control over the indents that seem to automatically happen when the device is rotated into Landscape, but we really need to be able to control these.    The """"""""Designing for iPhone X"""""""" video from Apple mentioned that """"""""Even if you are not using Auto Layout, UIView provides the Safe Area Insets and Layout Margin values as properties.""""""""    There are many instances in my app where a rotation to Landscape causes messy UI issues. If I can programmatically control the Insets and Layout Margin, particularly when it affects ListViews and TableViews, that would be great.    For example see the attached screenshot. I would like to programmatically disable the margin on the ListView if the orientation is LANDSCAPE_RIGHT, as the margin is unnecessary and ugly. But obviously if rotated the other way, then the indent / margin is needed.""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone X: Need to be able to control the Insets / Layout Margins
Description: """"I am not sure what property will allow control over the indents that seem to automatically happen when the device is rotated into Landscape, but we really need to be able to control these. The """"""""Designing for iPhone X"""""""" video from Apple mentioned that """"""""Even if you are not using Auto Layout, UIView provides the Safe Area Insets and Layout Margin values as properties."""""""" There are many instances in my app where a rotation to Landscape causes messy UI issues. If I can programmatically control the Insets and Layout Margin, particularly when it affects ListViews and TableViews, that would be great. For example see the attached screenshot. I would like to programmatically disable the margin on the ListView if the orientation is LANDSCAPE_RIGHT, as the margin is unnecessary and ugly. But obviously if rotated the other way, then the indent / margin is needed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25300,12,"""iOS 11: Window titleControls are not centered in Landscape Orientation""","""""""On the iPhone X, building with 6.2.0 and Xcode 9 GM, there is an interesting issue with Window titleControls when rotated to Landscape orientation.    Standard Window Titles are OK.  When a titleControl is used, it does not center when rotated to Landscape.    See the attached screenshot.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 11: Window titleControls are not centered in Landscape Orientation
Description: """"On the iPhone X, building with 6.2.0 and Xcode 9 GM, there is an interesting issue with Window titleControls when rotated to Landscape orientation. Standard Window Titles are OK. When a titleControl is used, it does not center when rotated to Landscape. See the attached screenshot.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25297,12,"""Windows: Ti.UI.Picker properties not working""","""""""h5. Issue description     For Ti.UI.Picker, touchEnabled property and setSelectedRow method are not working in Windows.    PFA the sample project created to test these. In window open event of the index page, these are applied to the Picker in that page.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  Run the attached windows application - TestPicker.  The picker will stay enabled and the row selected via controller will not be selected in UI.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Ti.UI.Picker properties not working
Description: """"h5. Issue description For Ti.UI.Picker, touchEnabled property and setSelectedRow method are not working in Windows. PFA the sample project created to test these. In window open event of the index page, these are applied to the Picker in that page. h5. Steps to reproduce: Run the attached windows application - TestPicker. The picker will stay enabled and the row selected via controller will not be selected in UI.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25296,12,"""Help on using an 3rd-p SDK with Android that requires Surface V""","""""""h5. Issue Description     So we have this 3rd party SDK that allows our app to do Live Streaming videos. We've successfully integrated it on iOS, and we're looking forward to integrate it with Android as well. One of the requirements that the SDK has for working is that it needs an instance of Surface View - to display a camera preview from where to broadcast the stream signal. On iOS it only needed an instance of UIView, which was accomplished by passing on a TiUIProxyView object to an iOS Titanium Module, that could be casted to UIView. However we couldn't find a way to do so on Android - seems like TiUIProxyView cannot be casted to Surface View object. So the question is: can titanium handle / create Surface Views for Android and pass them to an Android Titanium Module somehow ? """"""",Improvement,"Title: Help on using an 3rd-p SDK with Android that requires Surface V
Description: """"h5. Issue Description So we have this 3rd party SDK that allows our app to do Live Streaming videos. We've successfully integrated it on iOS, and we're looking forward to integrate it with Android as well. One of the requirements that the SDK has for working is that it needs an instance of Surface View - to display a camera preview from where to broadcast the stream signal. On iOS it only needed an instance of UIView, which was accomplished by passing on a TiUIProxyView object to an iOS Titanium Module, that could be casted to UIView. However we couldn't find a way to do so on Android - seems like TiUIProxyView cannot be casted to Surface View object. So the question is: can titanium handle / create Surface Views for Android and pass them to an Android Titanium Module somehow ? """"",title+description
TIMOB-25290,12,"""Error on running application in Android O""","""""""* I have installed application through Xender.   * After successful installation, I have open app and used it.  *  After a while, I have closed application through back button.  * I have received error in module.js when I have opened app again.    This issue appears when application is closed using back button in Android 8.0.""""""",Bug,"Title: Error on running application in Android O
Description: """"* I have installed application through Xender. * After successful installation, I have open app and used it. * After a while, I have closed application through back button. * I have received error in module.js when I have opened app again. This issue appears when application is closed using back button in Android 8.0.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25288,12,"""Android: addAnnotations in Ti.Map crashes app""","""""""When trying to use the 'addAnnotations' function to add map annotations it causes the android application to fail. iOS seems to work fine. Below I have made an extremely simple project using the addAnnotation(s) functions to demonstrate. The only time I have had an annotation successfully added to a view on android is if the annotation is set when the map view is created. This is happening with version 3.3.0 of ti.map and <USER>versions 6.2.0 and 6.1.2. The android phone is running marshmallow.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: addAnnotations in Ti.Map crashes app
Description: """"When trying to use the 'addAnnotations' function to add map annotations it causes the android application to fail. iOS seems to work fine. Below I have made an extremely simple project using the addAnnotation(s) functions to demonstrate. The only time I have had an annotation successfully added to a view on android is if the annotation is set when the map view is created. This is happening with version 3.3.0 of ti.map and <USER>versions 6.2.0 and 6.1.2. The android phone is running marshmallow.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25287,12,"""iPhone X: Ti.UI.SearchBar in list-view get wrongly positioned""","""""""While looking in TIMOB-25271, I found that when search started in list view in iPhone X, search bar get placed at wrong position.       Test Case-      """"""",Bug,"Title: iPhone X: Ti.UI.SearchBar in list-view get wrongly positioned
Description: """"While looking in TIMOB-25271, I found that when search started in list view in iPhone X, search bar get placed at wrong position. Test Case- """"",title+description
TIMOB-25283,12,"""Hyperloop: iOS - Deprecate appc.js third-party configuration""","""""""With the introduction of dynamic frameworks in modules (TIMOB-20557) and the updated framework handling for Hyperloop (TIMOB-23570 and TIMOB-23853) the need to manually configure frameworks is no longer required. The use case to directly use Objective-C and Swift source files should also be discouraged in favor of using frameworks.    For this to happen we should deprecate the {{thirdparty}} setting in the {{appc.js}} and remove it in Hyperloop 3.0.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Hyperloop: iOS - Deprecate appc.js third-party configuration
Description: """"With the introduction of dynamic frameworks in modules (TIMOB-20557) and the updated framework handling for Hyperloop (TIMOB-23570 and TIMOB-23853) the need to manually configure frameworks is no longer required. The use case to directly use Objective-C and Swift source files should also be discouraged in favor of using frameworks. For this to happen we should deprecate the {{thirdparty}} setting in the {{appc.js}} and remove it in Hyperloop 3.0.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25281,12,"""Windows: Ti.Media.saveToPhotoGallery does not accept a blob""","""""""h5.Description    Calling Ti.Media.saveToPhotoGallery with a blob crashes an application, when running normally the app crashes with no error. Running in debug from VS shows that the error is occurring [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/91c53831aa37f46cda9ec9d0140d444fced41a3e/Source/Media/src/Media.cpp#L378] as media is empty        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Add to an existing app.js and build for Windows      h5.Actual    App crashes    h5.Expected    App shouldn't crash, red circle should be written to gallery""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Ti.Media.saveToPhotoGallery does not accept a blob
Description: """"h5.Description Calling Ti.Media.saveToPhotoGallery with a blob crashes an application, when running normally the app crashes with no error. Running in debug from VS shows that the error is occurring [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/91c53831aa37f46cda9ec9d0140d444fced41a3e/Source/Media/src/Media.cpp#L378] as media is empty h5.Steps to reproduce # Add to an existing app.js and build for Windows h5.Actual App crashes h5.Expected App shouldn't crash, red circle should be written to gallery""""",title+description
TIMOB-25280,12,"""Windows: Allow view.toImage to work on elements not in the XAML visual tree""","""""""h5.Description    Currently the .toImage method for views will only work if the view is in the XAML visual tree, that is to say added to another view/window. I believe this is a limitation of the API used [rendertargetbitmap|https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/uwp/api/windows.ui.xaml.media.imaging.rendertargetbitmap], I think it might be possible to use [XamlRenderingBackgroundTask|https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/uwp/api/Windows.UI.Xaml.Media.Imaging.XamlRenderingBackgroundTask] see https://stackoverflow.com/questions/29262195/rendertargetbitmap-without-putting-it-on-ui    """"""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Allow view.toImage to work on elements not in the XAML visual tree
Description: """"h5.Description Currently the .toImage method for views will only work if the view is in the XAML visual tree, that is to say added to another view/window. I believe this is a limitation of the API used [rendertargetbitmap|https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/uwp/api/windows.ui.xaml.media.imaging.rendertargetbitmap], I think it might be possible to use [XamlRenderingBackgroundTask|https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/uwp/api/Windows.UI.Xaml.Media.Imaging.XamlRenderingBackgroundTask] see https://stackoverflow.com/questions/29262195/rendertargetbitmap-without-putting-it-on-ui """"",title+description
TIMOB-25279,12,"""iOS: Clean-up Titanium core, resolve all compiler warnings""","""""""This ticket should resolve all Xcode 9 warnings, including:  * Static analyser warnings    * Fix some """"""""missing localization"""""""" warnings by using {{NSLocalizedString}}    * Fix unreachable code""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Clean-up Titanium core, resolve all compiler warnings
Description: """"This ticket should resolve all Xcode 9 warnings, including: * Static analyser warnings * Fix some """"""""missing localization"""""""" warnings by using {{NSLocalizedString}} * Fix unreachable code""""",title+description
TIMOB-25270,12,"""iPhone X: Support for FaceID""","""""""As discussed on Teams, we may want to create a new module like """"""""Ti.Identity"""""""" to manage all security-related functionalities in one module, including touch-id, face-id and keychain-access. This will also deprecate Ti.TouchID and move Android over as well.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iPhone X: Support for FaceID
Description: """"As discussed on Teams, we may want to create a new module like """"""""Ti.Identity"""""""" to manage all security-related functionalities in one module, including touch-id, face-id and keychain-access. This will also deprecate Ti.TouchID and move Android over as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25269,12,"""iPhone X: Support new launch-images (when not using storyboards)""","""""""*(Currently blocked by a bug inside Xcode, see the comments below)*    Add small change to iOS-build to add the new launch-screen to the asset-catalog. Please note that this only applies for custom splash-screens. Everyone using storyboards (the recommended way be Apple these days that we also support) will not have to change anything.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iPhone X: Support new launch-images (when not using storyboards)
Description: """"*(Currently blocked by a bug inside Xcode, see the comments below)* Add small change to iOS-build to add the new launch-screen to the asset-catalog. Please note that this only applies for custom splash-screens. Everyone using storyboards (the recommended way be Apple these days that we also support) will not have to change anything. """"",title+description
