TIMOB-25232,12,"""Windows: CLI fails when running any appc commands""","""""""When building for Android on Windows ({{appc run}}), the build crashes with the attached error. Same occurs for all other appc commands, e.g. {{appc ti info}}, so we are unable to get the environment. Logging out and in also didn't resolve the issue.    EDIT: The Ti CLI was outdated, after updating it to 5.0.14, the Appc-CLI to 6.2.3 and the SDK to 6.1.2, the new error is:  """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: CLI fails when running any appc commands
Description: """"When building for Android on Windows ({{appc run}}), the build crashes with the attached error. Same occurs for all other appc commands, e.g. {{appc ti info}}, so we are unable to get the environment. Logging out and in also didn't resolve the issue. EDIT: The Ti CLI was outdated, after updating it to 5.0.14, the Appc-CLI to 6.2.3 and the SDK to 6.1.2, the new error is: """"",title+description
TIMOB-25230,12,"""iOS: Intermittent Simulator Crashes during TableView stress test in unit test suite""","""""""We have intermittent unit test suite crashes in the iOS simulator. For master branch, the most recent build failed due to a crash during the TableView stress test here: https://github.com/<USER>titanium-mobile-mocha-suite/blob/master/Resources/ti.ui.tableview.test.js#L1025    I'm attaching the crash report file generated.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Intermittent Simulator Crashes during TableView stress test in unit test suite
Description: """"We have intermittent unit test suite crashes in the iOS simulator. For master branch, the most recent build failed due to a crash during the TableView stress test here: https://github.com/<USER>titanium-mobile-mocha-suite/blob/master/Resources/ti.ui.tableview.test.js#L1025 I'm attaching the crash report file generated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25228,12,"""iOS: Trying to open a second Ti.UI.iPad.Popover will crash the app""","""""""It used to be in previous versions of the SDK, certainly pre-Hyperloop that if you tried to show a second Popover it would automatically close the original one. Now it crashes the whole app everytime!    I've already re-written my app with a PopoverManager that keeps a pointer to the Popover and if it exists, hides it, nulls it then 200ms later will spawn a new one, otherwise it will just spawn a new one.    So the work around is easy enough, but I had to do quite a bit of re-writing for this.    Attached is a small example that re-creates the issue.     Click 1 then 2 = Crash  Click 3 then 4 as many times as you want = No Crash    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Trying to open a second Ti.UI.iPad.Popover will crash the app
Description: """"It used to be in previous versions of the SDK, certainly pre-Hyperloop that if you tried to show a second Popover it would automatically close the original one. Now it crashes the whole app everytime! I've already re-written my app with a PopoverManager that keeps a pointer to the Popover and if it exists, hides it, nulls it then 200ms later will spawn a new one, otherwise it will just spawn a new one. So the work around is easy enough, but I had to do quite a bit of re-writing for this. Attached is a small example that re-creates the issue. Click 1 then 2 = Crash Click 3 then 4 as many times as you want = No Crash """"",title+description
TIMOB-25227,12,"""iOS: Building app with module that contains a framework fails on 6.2.0""","""""""When building an app project (or CI build like in my case), the build fails on 6.2.0/master because of an error in the new framework-hook (TIMOB-20557). See the full build log in the [travis-build|https://travis-ci.org/hansemannn/titanium-google-maps] of my Ti.GoogleMaps module:      It looks like the framework-hook does not pick up the """"""""GooglePlacePicker"""""""" framework correctly. It was just added a day ago and might have a different structure than before. Google also warned developers who are manually integrating frameworks:  {quote}  Note: - The layout of the static frameworks has changed. There is no longer a Versions directory. The contents of Versions/A has been moved to the root directory of the framework. Developers who manually integrate frameworks with their project should take additional care during the upgrade.  {quote}    We should get this under control in 6.2.0.GA so people do not experience module-related crashes. Please note that this module still using the manual framework linking in the module.xcconfig (for backwards-compatibility with older SDK's).    Investgating it more further, it turns out that the error is thrown by the following lines, not being able to detect the framework type:  {code:js}  if (stdout.indexOf('current ar archive') !== -1) {      type = FRAMEWORK_TYPE_STATIC;  } else if (stdout.indexOf('dynamically linked shared library') !== -1) {      type = FRAMEWORK_TYPE_DYNAMIC;  } else {      return reject(new Error('Unknown framework type:\n' + stdout));  }  {code}  Which makes sense when you look into the type (Mach-O) that needs to be handled.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Building app with module that contains a framework fails on 6.2.0
Description: """"When building an app project (or CI build like in my case), the build fails on 6.2.0/master because of an error in the new framework-hook (TIMOB-20557). See the full build log in the [travis-build|https://travis-ci.org/hansemannn/titanium-google-maps] of my Ti.GoogleMaps module: It looks like the framework-hook does not pick up the """"""""GooglePlacePicker"""""""" framework correctly. It was just added a day ago and might have a different structure than before. Google also warned developers who are manually integrating frameworks: {quote} Note: - The layout of the static frameworks has changed. There is no longer a Versions directory. The contents of Versions/A has been moved to the root directory of the framework. Developers who manually integrate frameworks with their project should take additional care during the upgrade. {quote} We should get this under control in 6.2.0.GA so people do not experience module-related crashes. Please note that this module still using the manual framework linking in the module.xcconfig (for backwards-compatibility with older SDK's). Investgating it more further, it turns out that the error is thrown by the following lines, not being able to detect the framework type: {code:js} if (stdout.indexOf('current ar archive') !== -1) { type = FRAMEWORK_TYPE_STATIC; } else if (stdout.indexOf('dynamically linked shared library') !== -1) { type = FRAMEWORK_TYPE_DYNAMIC; } else { return reject(new Error('Unknown framework type:\n' + stdout)); } {code} Which makes sense when you look into the type (Mach-O) that needs to be handled.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25222,12,"""Android: Nested views with Ti.UI.FILL in width/height is not visible""","""""""*Summary:*    Adding two views with width/height `Ti.UI.FILL` inside a view with fixed width/height only shows one view in 6.2.0.RC    *Expected*    Both images should be visible    *Workaround*    Set the inner views width/height to the outer view width/height.    *Code*  *correct* in 6.1.2.GA  *broken* in 6.2.0.RC        *Code (Work-Around)*  *correct* in 6.2.0.RC  *correct* in 6.1.2.GA  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Nested views with Ti.UI.FILL in width/height is not visible
Description: """"*Summary:* Adding two views with width/height `Ti.UI.FILL` inside a view with fixed width/height only shows one view in 6.2.0.RC *Expected* Both images should be visible *Workaround* Set the inner views width/height to the outer view width/height. *Code* *correct* in 6.1.2.GA *broken* in 6.2.0.RC *Code (Work-Around)* *correct* in 6.2.0.RC *correct* in 6.1.2.GA """"",title+description
TIMOB-25221,12,"""Android: Vertical Layout with top+bottom broken""","""""""*Summary:*  When setting both top AND bottom on an element inside a vertical layout view it won't add spacing between the elements but fill up the whole space.     *Versions:*  6.1.2.GA: works fine    !612_ga.png|thumbnail!     6.2.0.RC: broken layout when both properties are set   !620_rc.png|thumbnail!     *Work-around:*  remove top OR bottom   !620_rc_one.png|thumbnail!     *Code:*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Vertical Layout with top+bottom broken
Description: """"*Summary:* When setting both top AND bottom on an element inside a vertical layout view it won't add spacing between the elements but fill up the whole space. *Versions:* 6.1.2.GA: works fine !612_ga.png|thumbnail! 6.2.0.RC: broken layout when both properties are set !620_rc.png|thumbnail! *Work-around:* remove top OR bottom !620_rc_one.png|thumbnail! *Code:* """"",title+description
TIMOB-25218,12,"""Docs: Android Toolbar example broken""","""""""The (new) docs for the Ti.UI.Toolbar on Android are broken: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Toolbar (scroll down to examples). In addition, the example is titled incorrectly and one Ti.UI.iOS.Toolbar reference is still in the docs. We should fix them before GA hits the place.""""""",Bug,"Title: Docs: Android Toolbar example broken
Description: """"The (new) docs for the Ti.UI.Toolbar on Android are broken: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Toolbar (scroll down to examples). In addition, the example is titled incorrectly and one Ti.UI.iOS.Toolbar reference is still in the docs. We should fix them before GA hits the place.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25217,12,"""iOS: WebView """"fireEvent"""" causes app crash on 6.2.0.RC""","""""""regression error:    click href link in webview that uses fireevent causes crash    crash occurs when using   <sdk-version>6.2.0.v20170831112315</sdk-version>    Same code works fine when using  <sdk-version>6.1.2.GA</sdk-version>  <sdk-version>6.1.0.GA</sdk-version>    note in test env  run-on-main-thread is not set  jscore framework is not used    simulator log code and safari debug inspector of the webview attached.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: WebView """"fireEvent"""" causes app crash on 6.2.0.RC
Description: """"regression error: click href link in webview that uses fireevent causes crash crash occurs when using <sdk-version>6.2.0.v20170831112315</sdk-version> Same code works fine when using <sdk-version>6.1.2.GA</sdk-version> <sdk-version>6.1.0.GA</sdk-version> note in test env run-on-main-thread is not set jscore framework is not used simulator log code and safari debug inspector of the webview attached. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25216,12,"""Windows: Docs do not show ti.cloud as supported""","""""""http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Modules.Cloud shows as unsupported on Windows, but it is. We need to     * strip the yaml under here down to just properties methods etc then add platform ['windowsphone'] to everything  * Copy all that over into titanium_mobile_windows  * Edit the Jenkinsfile to archive apidoc\Modules appropriately  * Edit the build scripts to pull in windows\doc\Modules""""""",Story,"Title: Windows: Docs do not show ti.cloud as supported
Description: """"http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Modules.Cloud shows as unsupported on Windows, but it is. We need to * strip the yaml under here down to just properties methods etc then add platform ['windowsphone'] to everything * Copy all that over into titanium_mobile_windows * Edit the Jenkinsfile to archive apidoc\Modules appropriately * Edit the build scripts to pull in windows\doc\Modules""""",title+description
TIMOB-25211,12,"""Android: App crash on using touchID methods ""","""""""H5. Issue Description  The customer is implementing touch ID based authentication for android devices using 6.1.2 GA Ti SDK.     HTH is requiring TouchID module and checking whether the device is supporting touchID by using touchID.isSupported() method. In supported devices, it is working fine whereas in unsupported devices app is getting crashed.  With TouchID module (2.0.1 version) it is working fine in all the devices but touchID.invalidate() method is not available so we cannot go with this version.    H5. Steps to reproduce  1.create a sample project  2.Require the touchID module (2.1.0 version)  3.Use any of the methods available with TouchID module(e.g., isSupported())    In the existing JIRA ticket (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24413), it was told that the issue has been fixed but we are still facing the same issue.    Note: Customer is not getting this issue in Samsung S4(4.4.2 OS) but able to reproduce in Nexus 7 (6.0.1 OS). Please find the attached crash log file and index.js file.    This is a CRITICAL functionality which needs to be delivered to the client in a week. Let us know your free time to quickly connect and discuss on this issue in more detail. We work in IST time zone. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: App crash on using touchID methods
Description: """"H5. Issue Description The customer is implementing touch ID based authentication for android devices using 6.1.2 GA Ti SDK. HTH is requiring TouchID module and checking whether the device is supporting touchID by using touchID.isSupported() method. In supported devices, it is working fine whereas in unsupported devices app is getting crashed. With TouchID module (2.0.1 version) it is working fine in all the devices but touchID.invalidate() method is not available so we cannot go with this version. H5. Steps to reproduce 1.create a sample project 2.Require the touchID module (2.1.0 version) 3.Use any of the methods available with TouchID module(e.g., isSupported()) In the existing JIRA ticket (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24413), it was told that the issue has been fixed but we are still facing the same issue. Note: Customer is not getting this issue in Samsung S4(4.4.2 OS) but able to reproduce in Nexus 7 (6.0.1 OS). Please find the attached crash log file and index.js file. This is a CRITICAL functionality which needs to be delivered to the client in a week. Let us know your free time to quickly connect and discuss on this issue in more detail. We work in IST time zone. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25210,12,"""iOS: Cannot submit builds with iOS 11 / Xcode 9 due to missing """"Marketing Image""""""","""""""I just received feedback from Slack that you currently cannot submit any iOS 11 app due to the error """"""""Missing Marketing Icon - iOS Apps must include a 1024x1024px Marketing Icon in PNG format. Apps that do not include the Marketing Icon cannot be submitted for App Review or Beta App Review."""""""".    The issue simply occurs because Apple introduced a new Icon-type in the asset-catalog called """"""""iOS Marketing"""""""", which represents a 1024x1024 PNG image. As we already have our DefaultIcon.png, the SDK change would simply grab it and reference the new key in the asset-catalog. Also, we should now enforce the users to specify a """"""""DefaultIcon.png"""""""" for iOS 11 distributions and deprecate the manual appicon.png formats.     Also see [this Stackoverflow thread|https://stackoverflow.com/questions/44565883/missing-marketing-icon] for more context.    *EDIT*: Required asset-catalog object to add:  {code:json}   {        """"""""size"""""""" : """"""""1024x1024"""""""",        """"""""idiom"""""""" : """"""""ios-marketing"""""""",        """"""""filename"""""""" : """"""""DefaultIcon.png"""""""",        """"""""scale"""""""" : """"""""1x""""""""  }    The same would probably need to be done for the DefaultIcon.png, so we won't need to deprecate anything, yet, just make sure it's supported for both DefaultIcon, non-DefaultIcon, asset-catalog and non-asset-catalog.    *EDIT 3*: The above change seems to work (although some others are still missing, might be interesting to investigate later):   !Bildschirmfoto 2017-08-30 um 12.19.41.png|thumbnail!     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot submit builds with iOS 11 / Xcode 9 due to missing """"Marketing Image""""
Description: """"I just received feedback from Slack that you currently cannot submit any iOS 11 app due to the error """"""""Missing Marketing Icon - iOS Apps must include a 1024x1024px Marketing Icon in PNG format. Apps that do not include the Marketing Icon cannot be submitted for App Review or Beta App Review."""""""". The issue simply occurs because Apple introduced a new Icon-type in the asset-catalog called """"""""iOS Marketing"""""""", which represents a 1024x1024 PNG image. As we already have our DefaultIcon.png, the SDK change would simply grab it and reference the new key in the asset-catalog. Also, we should now enforce the users to specify a """"""""DefaultIcon.png"""""""" for iOS 11 distributions and deprecate the manual appicon.png formats. Also see [this Stackoverflow thread|https://stackoverflow.com/questions/44565883/missing-marketing-icon] for more context. *EDIT*: Required asset-catalog object to add: {code:json} { """"""""size"""""""" : """"""""1024x1024"""""""", """"""""idiom"""""""" : """"""""ios-marketing"""""""", """"""""filename"""""""" : """"""""DefaultIcon.png"""""""", """"""""scale"""""""" : """"""""1x"""""""" } The same would probably need to be done for the DefaultIcon.png, so we won't need to deprecate anything, yet, just make sure it's supported for both DefaultIcon, non-DefaultIcon, asset-catalog and non-asset-catalog. *EDIT 3*: The above change seems to work (although some others are still missing, might be interesting to investigate later): !Bildschirmfoto 2017-08-30 um 12.19.41.png|thumbnail! """"",title+description
TIMOB-25209,12,"""Android: Support ARCore (parity with ARKit on iOS)""","""""""Apple released the Augmented Reality framework """"""""ARKit"""""""" along with iOS 11 and we support it's basic implementation (load scenes into the camera) with [Ti.ARKit|https://github.com/hansemannn/titanium-arkit] already. I'd be amazing to also support ARCore in the module, so we could eventually even more it to the core (e.g. Ti.AR.xxxx).    References:  - https://developers.google.com/ar/""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support ARCore (parity with ARKit on iOS)
Description: """"Apple released the Augmented Reality framework """"""""ARKit"""""""" along with iOS 11 and we support it's basic implementation (load scenes into the camera) with [Ti.ARKit|https://github.com/hansemannn/titanium-arkit] already. I'd be amazing to also support ARCore in the module, so we could eventually even more it to the core (e.g. Ti.AR.xxxx). References: - https://developers.google.com/ar/""""",title+description
TIMOB-25205,12,"""Remove platform specific code""","""""""h5.Description    This sub-task is to track removal of platform specific code and macros. It's probably best to split this into individual tasks for each grouping of modules Filesystem, Global etc. (everything under [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/tree/f335f2ba034ba707d349cb2e91f6e7738b98888b/Source] to avoid a unreviewable PR""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Remove platform specific code
Description: """"h5.Description This sub-task is to track removal of platform specific code and macros. It's probably best to split this into individual tasks for each grouping of modules Filesystem, Global etc. (everything under [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/tree/f335f2ba034ba707d349cb2e91f6e7738b98888b/Source] to avoid a unreviewable PR""""",title+description
TIMOB-25203,12,"""Remove 8.1 from CI/CD build process""","""""""h5.Description    This sub-task is to remove 8.1 from the Jenkins build <USER> it's pretty much just nuke [these configs|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/f335f2ba034ba707d349cb2e91f6e7738b98888b/Jenkinsfile#L94-L130], and then basking in the glory of the reducing the build times.    Extra points for simplifying any of the necessary build logic""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Remove 8.1 from CI/CD build process
Description: """"h5.Description This sub-task is to remove 8.1 from the Jenkins build <USER> it's pretty much just nuke [these configs|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/f335f2ba034ba707d349cb2e91f6e7738b98888b/Jenkinsfile#L94-L130], and then basking in the glory of the reducing the build times. Extra points for simplifying any of the necessary build logic""""",title+description
TIMOB-25202,12,"""Windows: Drop support for targeting Windows Phone 8.1 and Windows 8.1""","""""""h5.Description    This epic is to track the different aspects of removing Windows Phone 8.1 and Windows 8.1 from Titanium SDK and any related tooling libraries.    At a pretty high level, not in a specific order:    * Stop producing and testing in CI the relevant build artifacts  * Remove platform specific code from within the Titanium Windows source files  * Update documentation  * Remove support from various scripts around building the SDK and stuff  * Spit out a warning? (Probably needs to be slid in before 7, maybe in 6.3.0 or 6.4.0)  * After this is done, close any outstanding tickets as wont fix  * Before doing this, identify if there are any high profile tickets we wish to fix before dropping  * Have Studio remove the  different 8.1 related views (packaging dialog with the SDK choice, not sure on others). Will file the ticket once this is all approved    This *has to be done* for the 7.0.0 timeframe, keeping 8.1 around for another year (we plan 1 major rev a year as I understand) would be a bad choice that would severely limit our ability to move things forward and keep progressing the Windows Platform at the same rate as iOS and Android. I don't believe our current deprecation policy reserves our right to remove a platform at any time like the currently proposed update.    Extra supporting bits  My prior writing on why we should do this https://wiki.<USER>org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=50168498  Article regarding Microsoft dropping Windows Phone 8.1 [Goodbye Windows Phone: What comes next for Microsoft in mobile?|http://www.zdnet.com/article/goodbye-windows-phone-what-comes-next-for-microsoft-in-mobile]  Or if you prefer a nice clickbaity headline [Windows Phone dies today|https://www.theverge.com/2017/7/11/15952654/microsoft-windows-phone-end-of-support]""""""",Epic,"Title: Windows: Drop support for targeting Windows Phone 8.1 and Windows 8.1
Description: """"h5.Description This epic is to track the different aspects of removing Windows Phone 8.1 and Windows 8.1 from Titanium SDK and any related tooling libraries. At a pretty high level, not in a specific order: * Stop producing and testing in CI the relevant build artifacts * Remove platform specific code from within the Titanium Windows source files * Update documentation * Remove support from various scripts around building the SDK and stuff * Spit out a warning? (Probably needs to be slid in before 7, maybe in 6.3.0 or 6.4.0) * After this is done, close any outstanding tickets as wont fix * Before doing this, identify if there are any high profile tickets we wish to fix before dropping * Have Studio remove the different 8.1 related views (packaging dialog with the SDK choice, not sure on others). Will file the ticket once this is all approved This *has to be done* for the 7.0.0 timeframe, keeping 8.1 around for another year (we plan 1 major rev a year as I understand) would be a bad choice that would severely limit our ability to move things forward and keep progressing the Windows Platform at the same rate as iOS and Android. I don't believe our current deprecation policy reserves our right to remove a platform at any time like the currently proposed update. Extra supporting bits My prior writing on why we should do this https://wiki.<USER>org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=50168498 Article regarding Microsoft dropping Windows Phone 8.1 [Goodbye Windows Phone: What comes next for Microsoft in mobile?|http://www.zdnet.com/article/goodbye-windows-phone-what-comes-next-for-microsoft-in-mobile] Or if you prefer a nice clickbaity headline [Windows Phone dies today|https://www.theverge.com/2017/7/11/15952654/microsoft-windows-phone-end-of-support]""""",title+description
TIMOB-25201,12,"""iOS: tintColor doesn't work on imageView if dimensions (height, width) are provided""","""""""if height and width are provided, tintColor doesn't work on iOS for imageView.    *Alloy*      *Classic*      However, you can change the tintColor afterwards from js.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: tintColor doesn't work on imageView if dimensions (height, width) are provided
Description: """"if height and width are provided, tintColor doesn't work on iOS for imageView. *Alloy* *Classic* However, you can change the tintColor afterwards from js.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25200,12,"""Android: Expose BottomNavigationView as new Android Ti.UI.TabGroup""","""""""Right now, we use a tabbed toolbar for the Android Ti.UI.TabGroup. Having the [BottomNavigationView|https://developer.android.com/reference/android/support/design/widget/BottomNavigationView.html] these days, it would provide be a much better parity between the both platforms, especially in terms of the UI (it is actually placed at the bottom, like the iOS Ti.UI.TabGroup).""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Expose BottomNavigationView as new Android Ti.UI.TabGroup
Description: """"Right now, we use a tabbed toolbar for the Android Ti.UI.TabGroup. Having the [BottomNavigationView|https://developer.android.com/reference/android/support/design/widget/BottomNavigationView.html] these days, it would provide be a much better parity between the both platforms, especially in terms of the UI (it is actually placed at the bottom, like the iOS Ti.UI.TabGroup).""""",title+description
TIMOB-25196,12,"""iOS: CLI throws ATS-warning although *.appcelerator.com is properly whitelisted""","""""""_Following up on an email-thread with [~<EMAIL>]._    When manually whitelisting ATS domains, he added {{<USER>com}} to the ATS-configuration, but there was still a warning thrown:    Looking into the [related code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L4001-L4002], it falls through the if-case and lands in the else-case, because he manages the ATS-setting manually instead of setting the {{ios.whitelist.<USER>com}} property to true.     So what should the code do? It should detect ATS references properly in [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L2323-L2324], so it either checks if the property is enabled, but also checks if it is manually set.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: CLI throws ATS-warning although *.appcelerator.com is properly whitelisted
Description: """"_Following up on an email-thread with [~<EMAIL>]._ When manually whitelisting ATS domains, he added {{<USER>com}} to the ATS-configuration, but there was still a warning thrown: Looking into the [related code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L4001-L4002], it falls through the if-case and lands in the else-case, because he manages the ATS-setting manually instead of setting the {{ios.whitelist.<USER>com}} property to true. So what should the code do? It should detect ATS references properly in [here|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L2323-L2324], so it either checks if the property is enabled, but also checks if it is manually set.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25195,12,"""iOS: Improve native module template""","""""""In 6.2.0, we already improved the module template by cleaning up the default-code, general code-style and enabled ARC. As the next step, I would like to do some more adjustments:  * Include our .clang-format for unified formatting  * Rework default .gitignore to do more than just ignoring the .DS_STORE (e.g. build-directory, zip-files, xcode-metadata)  * Rework default README to a) have an actual """""""".md"""""""" file extension and b) be more descriptive for things like CI-integration, license-fields and general structure (features, docs, example, authors, ...)    This should be possible in the 7.0.0 timeframe.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Improve native module template
Description: """"In 6.2.0, we already improved the module template by cleaning up the default-code, general code-style and enabled ARC. As the next step, I would like to do some more adjustments: * Include our .clang-format for unified formatting * Rework default .gitignore to do more than just ignoring the .DS_STORE (e.g. build-directory, zip-files, xcode-metadata) * Rework default README to a) have an actual """""""".md"""""""" file extension and b) be more descriptive for things like CI-integration, license-fields and general structure (features, docs, example, authors, ...) This should be possible in the 7.0.0 timeframe.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25193,12,"""Android: Touches are not shown/intercepted if center of the tableViewRow are clicked""","""""""*This is a regression. Not seen with 6.1.2.GA*    h5.Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the code below in your app.js:    2. Build the app for android device/emulator.  3. After the app launches click on any row.    h5.Actual results:  1. Clicking on the center of the row does nothing. You will have to click near the top or the bottom of the row to see the click/touch.    h5.Expected results:  1. Clicking on the center of the row shows click/touch.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Touches are not shown/intercepted if center of the tableViewRow are clicked
Description: """"*This is a regression. Not seen with 6.1.2.GA* h5.Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the code below in your app.js: 2. Build the app for android device/emulator. 3. After the app launches click on any row. h5.Actual results: 1. Clicking on the center of the row does nothing. You will have to click near the top or the bottom of the row to see the click/touch. h5.Expected results: 1. Clicking on the center of the row shows click/touch.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25190,12,"""Android: touchEnabled is not true by default if we have a property specified for the tableViewRow""","""""""*This is a regression. Worked fine with 6.1.2.GA*    Docs : http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TableViewRow-property-touchEnabled    h5.Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the below code in your app.js.      2. Build for android device/emulator.  3. After the app launches tap on the tableviewrow.    h5.Actual results:  1. No click event is fired.  2. If no properties are used for the table view row then click works fine, but if we have a single property the touch/click stops working & needs {{touchEnabled}} to be set to {{true}} to get the touch/click.    h5.Expected result:  1. Click event is fired.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: touchEnabled is not true by default if we have a property specified for the tableViewRow
Description: """"*This is a regression. Worked fine with 6.1.2.GA* Docs : http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TableViewRow-property-touchEnabled h5.Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the below code in your app.js. 2. Build for android device/emulator. 3. After the app launches tap on the tableviewrow. h5.Actual results: 1. No click event is fired. 2. If no properties are used for the table view row then click works fine, but if we have a single property the touch/click stops working & needs {{touchEnabled}} to be set to {{true}} to get the touch/click. h5.Expected result: 1. Click event is fired.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25189,12,"""Windows: Throw better error when calling style.apply with an incorrect TargetType""","""""""h5.Description    When calling apply with a style, where the TargetType in the XAML style doesn't match the correct underlying control used by Titanium the error message is currently the below, it would be nice if we could catch the error correctly and then report this back to the user                h5.Steps to reproduce    # Copy the above app.js and styles.xaml into your project  # Build for a Windows target    h5.Actual    {{Unknown exception}} error is thrown    h5.Expected    A nicer error that maybe just spits back the error returned from nativeland? {{WinRT information: Cannot apply a Style with TargetType 'Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls.TextBox' to an object of type 'Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls.TextBlock'.}}""""""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Throw better error when calling style.apply with an incorrect TargetType
Description: """"h5.Description When calling apply with a style, where the TargetType in the XAML style doesn't match the correct underlying control used by Titanium the error message is currently the below, it would be nice if we could catch the error correctly and then report this back to the user h5.Steps to reproduce # Copy the above app.js and styles.xaml into your project # Build for a Windows target h5.Actual {{Unknown exception}} error is thrown h5.Expected A nicer error that maybe just spits back the error returned from nativeland? {{WinRT information: Cannot apply a Style with TargetType 'Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls.TextBox' to an object of type 'Windows.UI.Xaml.Controls.TextBlock'.}}""""",title+description
TIMOB-25176,12,"""CLI: SDK 7 broken on node 4""","""""""h5.Description    We're using const in files that don't have {{'use strict'}}, node 4 doesn't like this, if we want node 4 support then we need to add it. If we wont fix we need to update all the Windows <USER>slaves to >=6 as this is currently breaking all Windows builds https://<USER><USER>org/blue/organizations/<USER>titanium-sdk%2Ftitanium_mobile_windows/detail/PR-1073/2/pipeline/38/""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: SDK 7 broken on node 4
Description: """"h5.Description We're using const in files that don't have {{'use strict'}}, node 4 doesn't like this, if we want node 4 support then we need to add it. If we wont fix we need to update all the Windows <USER>slaves to >=6 as this is currently breaking all Windows builds https://<USER><USER>org/blue/organizations/<USER>titanium-sdk%2Ftitanium_mobile_windows/detail/PR-1073/2/pipeline/38/""""",title+description
TIMOB-25173,12,"""Android: Size/Fill layout conflicts are not handled the same as iOS and Windows""","""""""*Summary:*  Android does not resolve a parent Ti.UI.SIZE and child Ti.UI.FILL conflict in the same manner as iOS and Windows Phone. The issue is that the parent wants to auto-size itself based on the child and the child wants to auto-size itself based on the parent. iOS and Windows resolves this by increasing the size of the child to fit the parent's parent. Android resolves this by shrinking the parent to just-fit the child's minimum size. Android should be changed to match iOS and Windows' behavior for portability.    *Cause:*  Titanium uses the Android MATCH_PARENT setting for Ti.UI.FILL. Unfortunately, the native Android behavior does not match iOS and Windows's behavior. Because of this, we cannot use this setting.    *Work-Around:*  Instead of using Ti.UI.FILL, you can use """"""""100%"""""""" instead for vertical and composite layouts. However, this work-around will not work well in a horizontal layout if their are multiple views on the same row.    *Tests to reproduce:*  Please see the attached JavaScript files for testing:  -  [^ListViewFillTest.js]   -  [^SizeFillConflictTest.js]   -  [^VerticalFillTest.js]   -  [^HorizontalFillTest.js]   -  [^HorizontalPinningTest.js]     There are also attached screenshots for each test script above. The """"""""Bad"""""""" screenshots show the buggy behavior on Android. The """"""""Good"""""""" screenshots are the expected results.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Size/Fill layout conflicts are not handled the same as iOS and Windows
Description: """"*Summary:* Android does not resolve a parent Ti.UI.SIZE and child Ti.UI.FILL conflict in the same manner as iOS and Windows Phone. The issue is that the parent wants to auto-size itself based on the child and the child wants to auto-size itself based on the parent. iOS and Windows resolves this by increasing the size of the child to fit the parent's parent. Android resolves this by shrinking the parent to just-fit the child's minimum size. Android should be changed to match iOS and Windows' behavior for portability. *Cause:* Titanium uses the Android MATCH_PARENT setting for Ti.UI.FILL. Unfortunately, the native Android behavior does not match iOS and Windows's behavior. Because of this, we cannot use this setting. *Work-Around:* Instead of using Ti.UI.FILL, you can use """"""""100%"""""""" instead for vertical and composite layouts. However, this work-around will not work well in a horizontal layout if their are multiple views on the same row. *Tests to reproduce:* Please see the attached JavaScript files for testing: - [^ListViewFillTest.js] - [^SizeFillConflictTest.js] - [^VerticalFillTest.js] - [^HorizontalFillTest.js] - [^HorizontalPinningTest.js] There are also attached screenshots for each test script above. The """"""""Bad"""""""" screenshots show the buggy behavior on Android. The """"""""Good"""""""" screenshots are the expected results. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25171,12,"""Ask to try again after installing app to device fails""","""""""Triggered by a [blog post|http://<USER>com/2015/10/arggh-failed-android-install/] by [~<USER> I was thinking maybe we should ask the user to try again when for some reason the CLI failed to install an app on a device.    Currently, you'd need to do the full build again or manually figure out how to use the involved to tooling directly to install the existing build - which would not get you the logs via the CLI.    We could do something like:        By displaying and refreshing the (otherwise cached) list of connected devices the user would be able to try another device, the same or give up.    *UPDATE:* As [~<USER> suggested, it might be even better to have a map of errors-codes to human-readable reasons why the install failed as well as a flag if a retry would make sense. Like in the above example, it would not and the users will simply have to remove the app or bump the version and rebuild.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Ask to try again after installing app to device fails
Description: """"Triggered by a [blog post|http://<USER>com/2015/10/arggh-failed-android-install/] by [~<USER> I was thinking maybe we should ask the user to try again when for some reason the CLI failed to install an app on a device. Currently, you'd need to do the full build again or manually figure out how to use the involved to tooling directly to install the existing build - which would not get you the logs via the CLI. We could do something like: By displaying and refreshing the (otherwise cached) list of connected devices the user would be able to try another device, the same or give up. *UPDATE:* As [~<USER> suggested, it might be even better to have a map of errors-codes to human-readable reasons why the install failed as well as a flag if a retry would make sense. Like in the above example, it would not and the users will simply have to remove the app or bump the version and rebuild.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25169,12,"""Windows: Building TI Windows Module with WinSDK 10.15063 installed fails""","""""""h5. Description:    Trying to build a module while having Windows SDK 10.0.15063.0 installed, fails to build with:      h5. Steps to replicate:  1. Create any windows module project and try to build it with WinSDK 10.15063 installed.    h5. More details:  This also happens when building an Application but, in that scenario using the --wp-sdk 10.0.14393.0 solves the problem. On a module, it does not.    Also tried  TIMOB-24402 and specifying the aforementioned SDK version in the manifest to no avail.    h5. Workaround:   The work around for this is opening the generated project files and manually selecting the Target Platform however, it would be preferred to be able to build in such a scenario directly from the CLI without having to open Visual Studio.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Building TI Windows Module with WinSDK 10.15063 installed fails
Description: """"h5. Description: Trying to build a module while having Windows SDK 10.0.15063.0 installed, fails to build with: h5. Steps to replicate: 1. Create any windows module project and try to build it with WinSDK 10.15063 installed. h5. More details: This also happens when building an Application but, in that scenario using the --wp-sdk 10.0.14393.0 solves the problem. On a module, it does not. Also tried TIMOB-24402 and specifying the aforementioned SDK version in the manifest to no avail. h5. Workaround: The work around for this is opening the generated project files and manually selecting the Target Platform however, it would be preferred to be able to build in such a scenario directly from the CLI without having to open Visual Studio. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25167,12,"""Hyperloop: iOS - Debugging not working reliably with Studio""","""""""*Steps to reproduce the behavior*  # Create a default Alloy app  # Replace the content in {{app/controllers/index.js}} with the following:    # Place the breakpoints and launch the app in debug mode    *Actual behavior*  The second breakpoints gets hit every now and then, but not reliably. The first breakpoint in the button on click handler never gets hit.    *Expected behavior*  The debugger stops at the breakpoints    *Additional notes*  This is probably caused by file modifications Hyperloop does throughout the build. As a workaround it is possible to debug using the Safari Web Inspector as described [here|https://<USER>com/blog/debugging-titanium-applications-using-safari-web-inspector/].""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: iOS - Debugging not working reliably with Studio
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce the behavior* # Create a default Alloy app # Replace the content in {{app/controllers/index.js}} with the following: # Place the breakpoints and launch the app in debug mode *Actual behavior* The second breakpoints gets hit every now and then, but not reliably. The first breakpoint in the button on click handler never gets hit. *Expected behavior* The debugger stops at the breakpoints *Additional notes* This is probably caused by file modifications Hyperloop does throughout the build. As a workaround it is possible to debug using the Safari Web Inspector as described [here|https://<USER>com/blog/debugging-titanium-applications-using-safari-web-inspector/].""""",title+description
TIMOB-25165,12,"""Windows: Clean up the Windows help output""","""""""h5.Description     The Windows build help output could do with some love, it has some dupe options that could be hidden I think, it is missing some helpful items like {{--skipInstallDependencies}} and the text for two options looks messed up (product guid opts)""""""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Clean up the Windows help output
Description: """"h5.Description The Windows build help output could do with some love, it has some dupe options that could be hidden I think, it is missing some helpful items like {{--skipInstallDependencies}} and the text for two options looks messed up (product guid opts)""""",title+description
TIMOB-25164,12,"""Ti.iCloud: Inject iCloud SystemCapabilities via module-hook""","""""""One of my apps uses the Ti.ICloud module, which works great, if you have the SystemCapabilities properly configured. The Xcode project generated by Titanium doesn't have the proper capabilities turned on. So I have to `--build-only`, run some regular expressions to fix the SystemCapabilities, and then `fastlane gym` my project to build and upload it as a part of my CI <USER> Outside of CI, I'd have to build from Xcode directly, if I want iCloud to work right.    If I run my regular expressions, and then do another `appc ti build`, my changes to project.pbxproj are wiped out, so that doesn't work either.    Is there any way to customize the capabilities in the generated project?    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti.iCloud: Inject iCloud SystemCapabilities via module-hook
Description: """"One of my apps uses the Ti.ICloud module, which works great, if you have the SystemCapabilities properly configured. The Xcode project generated by Titanium doesn't have the proper capabilities turned on. So I have to `--build-only`, run some regular expressions to fix the SystemCapabilities, and then `fastlane gym` my project to build and upload it as a part of my CI <USER> Outside of CI, I'd have to build from Xcode directly, if I want iCloud to work right. If I run my regular expressions, and then do another `appc ti build`, my changes to project.pbxproj are wiped out, so that doesn't work either. Is there any way to customize the capabilities in the generated project? """"",title+description
TIMOB-25162,12,"""dynamic setColor() or color are not working for Switch object on Android when elements are inside tableView""","""""""add below to your default Alloy project.     Index.xml  ------------  <tableView>  <tableSection>  <TableViewRow>    <View class=""""""""horizontal w50 """"""""  >  <Switch color=""""""""blue"""""""" id=""""""""projector"""""""" title=""""""""Projector"""""""" style=""""""""Titanium.UI.Android.SWITCH_STYLE_CHECKBOX"""""""" />  </View>    </TableViewRow>  </tableSection>  </tableView>      index.js  -----------  setTimeout(function()  {       $.projector.setColor('#9C1F4D');       $.projector.color = 'orange';       console.log('blabla');  }, 2000);    """"""",Bug,"Title: dynamic setColor() or color are not working for Switch object on Android when elements are inside tableView
Description: """"add below to your default Alloy project. Index.xml ------------ <tableView> <tableSection> <TableViewRow> <View class=""""""""horizontal w50 """""""" > <Switch color=""""""""blue"""""""" id=""""""""projector"""""""" title=""""""""Projector"""""""" style=""""""""Titanium.UI.Android.SWITCH_STYLE_CHECKBOX"""""""" /> </View> </TableViewRow> </tableSection> </tableView> index.js ----------- setTimeout(function() { $.projector.setColor('#9C1F4D'); $.projector.color = 'orange'; console.log('blabla'); }, 2000); """"",title+description
TIMOB-25161,12,"""iOS: Expose """"thin"""", """"light"""", """"ultra-light"""" and """"semi-bold"""" font-weights in Titanium font-system""","""""""h5. Description:  In native iOS development, there is a way to apply a *thin font style* to a label, see attached image from Xcode. How can this be achieved in <USER>alloy project?    As per the docs: https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Font    The only style available is """"""""italic"""""""" or """"""""normal"""""""", though in native it seems there are many other styles are available like """"""""thin"""""""", """"""""ultra thin"""""""" or """"""""light"""""""" which are not there in Titanium.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Expose """"thin"""", """"light"""", """"ultra-light"""" and """"semi-bold"""" font-weights in Titanium font-system
Description: """"h5. Description: In native iOS development, there is a way to apply a *thin font style* to a label, see attached image from Xcode. How can this be achieved in <USER>alloy project? As per the docs: https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Font The only style available is """"""""italic"""""""" or """"""""normal"""""""", though in native it seems there are many other styles are available like """"""""thin"""""""", """"""""ultra thin"""""""" or """"""""light"""""""" which are not there in Titanium.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25160,12,"""Android O : CLI does not detect android O device's model & shows """"android device"""" when """"appc ti info"""" is run ""","""""""This was found when checking the fix for : https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24900. The PR for TIMOB-24900 was already merged in to master while writing this ticket, we will have a backport for it, so this ticket is for both master & 6.2.0.    So probably the cause for this issue is in our {{""""""""node-titanium-sdk/lib/adb.js""""""""}} {{""""""""parseDevices""""""""}} function. Here we do a {{""""""""adb shell cat /system/build.prop""""""""}} to get the device property list & then grab the model, manufacturer etc from it.   But from some reason, on Android O device this {{""""""""cat""""""""}} command returns {{""""""""/system/build.prop: Permission denied""""""""}} which is then the {{""""""""data""""""""}} callback & thus does not have any device properties returned.    h5.Steps to reproduce:  1. Connect device with Android O preview.  2. Make sure {{adb debugging}} is enabled on device.  3. Run {{appc ti info -t android}}    h5.Actual Results:  1. The {{Connected Device}} shows the device as {{Android device}} & not the model.  2. This makes the studio show the device as {{Android device}}.    h5.Expected Results:  1. The device's model name should show up.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android O : CLI does not detect android O device's model & shows """"android device"""" when """"appc ti info"""" is run
Description: """"This was found when checking the fix for : https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24900. The PR for TIMOB-24900 was already merged in to master while writing this ticket, we will have a backport for it, so this ticket is for both master & 6.2.0. So probably the cause for this issue is in our {{""""""""node-titanium-sdk/lib/adb.js""""""""}} {{""""""""parseDevices""""""""}} function. Here we do a {{""""""""adb shell cat /system/build.prop""""""""}} to get the device property list & then grab the model, manufacturer etc from it. But from some reason, on Android O device this {{""""""""cat""""""""}} command returns {{""""""""/system/build.prop: Permission denied""""""""}} which is then the {{""""""""data""""""""}} callback & thus does not have any device properties returned. h5.Steps to reproduce: 1. Connect device with Android O preview. 2. Make sure {{adb debugging}} is enabled on device. 3. Run {{appc ti info -t android}} h5.Actual Results: 1. The {{Connected Device}} shows the device as {{Android device}} & not the model. 2. This makes the studio show the device as {{Android device}}. h5.Expected Results: 1. The device's model name should show up. """"",title+description
TIMOB-25158,12,"""Android: TableView.rightImage incorrect size""","""""""h5. Description   When using tableview in each tableViewRow, customer has added a leftImage, a View and a rightImage. For displaying the left and right images, they used leftImage and rightImage properties of tableViewRow. Left image is getting displayed properly whereas rightImage is getting smaller even the same image is being used for both leftImage and rightImage property.    h5. Additional information from customer  It worked fine with 6.1.2.v20170710160853 version. But getting this issue with 6.1.2RC and 6.1.2 GA sdk.     h5. App  [TableViewAPP|https://axwaysoftware-my.sharepoint.com/personal/<USER>axway_com/_layouts/15/guestaccess.aspx?guestaccesstoken=%2bQlgQWbeaMGVf%2fnDAyIjkw4rHZ0kp36vp6wanD9f3L8%3d&docid=2_1bd6fdd1b0fe2490cbfd1675bdfcd2dd6&rev=1]""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView.rightImage incorrect size
Description: """"h5. Description When using tableview in each tableViewRow, customer has added a leftImage, a View and a rightImage. For displaying the left and right images, they used leftImage and rightImage properties of tableViewRow. Left image is getting displayed properly whereas rightImage is getting smaller even the same image is being used for both leftImage and rightImage property. h5. Additional information from customer It worked fine with 6.1.2.v20170710160853 version. But getting this issue with 6.1.2RC and 6.1.2 GA sdk. h5. App [TableViewAPP|https://axwaysoftware-my.sharepoint.com/personal/<USER>axway_com/_layouts/15/guestaccess.aspx?guestaccesstoken=%2bQlgQWbeaMGVf%2fnDAyIjkw4rHZ0kp36vp6wanD9f3L8%3d&docid=2_1bd6fdd1b0fe2490cbfd1675bdfcd2dd6&rev=1]""""",title+description
