TIMOB-25085,12,"""Unable to set listitem height""","""""""Unable to set listItem height. Tried this from TSS, JS and XML directly, but still no success.    To reproduce:    add below to your XML file    <Alloy>   <Window id=""""""""findRoomWindow"""""""" >  <View id=""""""""listContainer""""""""  width=""""""""100%"""""""" height=""""""""100%"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""blue"""""""" >     <ListView id=""""""""roomList""""""""     bubbleParent=""""""""false"""""""" >      <ListSection id=""""""""roomListSection"""""""" headerTitle=""""""""Select A Room""""""""   >       <ListItem  title=""""""""Checking"""""""" color=""""""""blue"""""""" height=""""""""180dp"""""""" />       <ListItem  title=""""""""Savings"""""""" color=""""""""red"""""""" />      </ListSection>     </ListView>    </View>   </Window>  </Alloy>""""""",Bug,"Title: Unable to set listitem height
Description: """"Unable to set listItem height. Tried this from TSS, JS and XML directly, but still no success. To reproduce: add below to your XML file <Alloy> <Window id=""""""""findRoomWindow"""""""" > <View id=""""""""listContainer"""""""" width=""""""""100%"""""""" height=""""""""100%"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""blue"""""""" > <ListView id=""""""""roomList"""""""" bubbleParent=""""""""false"""""""" > <ListSection id=""""""""roomListSection"""""""" headerTitle=""""""""Select A Room"""""""" > <ListItem title=""""""""Checking"""""""" color=""""""""blue"""""""" height=""""""""180dp"""""""" /> <ListItem title=""""""""Savings"""""""" color=""""""""red"""""""" /> </ListSection> </ListView> </View> </Window> </Alloy>""""",title+description
TIMOB-25084,12,"""Support localized string and model attribute together in binding""","""""""Be able to concatenate a localized string with a model attribute.  According to the documentation, something the following is possible (and works as expected):    <Label text=""""""""{title} by {artist}"""""""" />    However, the hardcoded text, in the example """"""""by"""""""", cannot be replaced with a localized string.  As in:    <Label text=""""""""{title} L('by') {artist}"""""""" />    In this case, the function text (L('by')) is output verbatim rather than being resolved.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Support localized string and model attribute together in binding
Description: """"Be able to concatenate a localized string with a model attribute. According to the documentation, something the following is possible (and works as expected): <Label text=""""""""{title} by {artist}"""""""" /> However, the hardcoded text, in the example """"""""by"""""""", cannot be replaced with a localized string. As in: <Label text=""""""""{title} L('by') {artist}"""""""" /> In this case, the function text (L('by')) is output verbatim rather than being resolved.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25082,12,"""Appbeta.appcelerator.com certificate expired.""","""""""Issue Description:  When I try to download app from appbeta I get the following error:  cannot connect to applbeta.<USER>com    """"""",Bug,"Title: Appbeta.appcelerator.com certificate expired.
Description: """"Issue Description: When I try to download app from appbeta I get the following error: cannot connect to applbeta.<USER>com """"",title+description
TIMOB-25080,12,"""Android: Add Android Studio default SDK location to the scan locations""","""""""h5.Description    I believe that most developers will be installing the Android SDK via Android Studio now, we should probably add the default install locations in our lookups [here|https://github.com/<USER>node-titanium-sdk/blob/e80bba152d54a8049ad6cf3164d6a499b7190d25/lib/android.js#L117-L119]    For Windows it defaults to {{%localappdata%\Android\Sdk}}   Need to check OSX but I think it's something like {{/Users/USERNAME/Library/Android/sdk}}    We could probably expand this to NDK also, but there's probably some caveats there in that the NDK lives under Sdk\ndk-bundle (I was expecting an Ndk folder) and also there is only one install available, not multiple""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add Android Studio default SDK location to the scan locations
Description: """"h5.Description I believe that most developers will be installing the Android SDK via Android Studio now, we should probably add the default install locations in our lookups [here|https://github.com/<USER>node-titanium-sdk/blob/e80bba152d54a8049ad6cf3164d6a499b7190d25/lib/android.js#L117-L119] For Windows it defaults to {{%localappdata%\Android\Sdk}} Need to check OSX but I think it's something like {{/Users/USERNAME/Library/Android/sdk}} We could probably expand this to NDK also, but there's probably some caveats there in that the NDK lives under Sdk\ndk-bundle (I was expecting an Ndk folder) and also there is only one install available, not multiple""""",title+description
TIMOB-25079,12,"""Hyperloop: iOS - Compile error: ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture arm64""","""""""*Description*  When building an app with hyperloop enabled and using SDK 7.0.0, the build fails during compile time with the following error:     ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture arm64    Full logs are attached    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Download/get Hyperloop 2.1.3. You can use this version, or you can <USER>it and build it with SDK 7.0.0. Either case, I get the same failing result.  2. Create a new default classic app with hyperloop enabled.  3. Build the app to device (failure also seen if built to Simulator)    *Expected Results*  App should build successfully with no errors.    *Actual Results*  App fails to build with this error:      *Expected Results*  Build shoud pass with no errors.    *Additional Information*  The error can be avoided if this is added to tiapp.xml  <use-jscore-framework>true</use-jscore-framework>  However with SDK 6.1.2, no error is seen whether ticore or jscore is used. The same behavior is expected with SDK 7.0.0.""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: iOS - Compile error: ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture arm64
Description: """"*Description* When building an app with hyperloop enabled and using SDK 7.0.0, the build fails during compile time with the following error: ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture arm64 Full logs are attached *Steps to reproduce* 1. Download/get Hyperloop 2.1.3. You can use this version, or you can <USER>it and build it with SDK 7.0.0. Either case, I get the same failing result. 2. Create a new default classic app with hyperloop enabled. 3. Build the app to device (failure also seen if built to Simulator) *Expected Results* App should build successfully with no errors. *Actual Results* App fails to build with this error: *Expected Results* Build shoud pass with no errors. *Additional Information* The error can be avoided if this is added to tiapp.xml <use-jscore-framework>true</use-jscore-framework> However with SDK 6.1.2, no error is seen whether ticore or jscore is used. The same behavior is expected with SDK 7.0.0.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25070,12,"""""""ti sdk select"""" shows SDK out of order""","""""""{{ti sdk select}} shows the SDK options out of order, but {{ti sdk}} shows them correctly in order.    *Steps to reproduce issue*  1. Run {{appc ti sdk select}}    *Actual results*  The SDKs listed are out of order    *Expected results*  The SDKs listed are in order    *Notes*  May not be an issue for people not installing non-GA SDKs.    """"""",Improvement,"Title: """"ti sdk select"""" shows SDK out of order
Description: """"{{ti sdk select}} shows the SDK options out of order, but {{ti sdk}} shows them correctly in order. *Steps to reproduce issue* 1. Run {{appc ti sdk select}} *Actual results* The SDKs listed are out of order *Expected results* The SDKs listed are in order *Notes* May not be an issue for people not installing non-GA SDKs. """"",title+description
