TIMOB-25019,12,"""Add titanium-mobile-mocha-suite into the titanium_mobile_windows build process""","""""""After the script has been updated to allow Windows targets we should try and work it into titanium_mobile_windows build <USER> I imagine the <USER>will look something like this    # Add a stage to check out the mocha-suite  # Copy across any new tests from a folder we designate as the temp dir  # Edit the current test script to execute from the mocha-suite dir    There's going to be a ton of roadblocks in this I imagine      H5.References    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/Jenkinsfile  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/66ccc0a080360d147dd2b59c748a075b87107233/Tools/Scripts/build/test.js""""""",Technical task,"Title: Add titanium-mobile-mocha-suite into the titanium_mobile_windows build process
Description: """"After the script has been updated to allow Windows targets we should try and work it into titanium_mobile_windows build <USER> I imagine the <USER>will look something like this # Add a stage to check out the mocha-suite # Copy across any new tests from a folder we designate as the temp dir # Edit the current test script to execute from the mocha-suite dir There's going to be a ton of roadblocks in this I imagine H5.References https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/Jenkinsfile https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/66ccc0a080360d147dd2b59c748a075b87107233/Tools/Scripts/build/test.js""""",title+description
TIMOB-25016,12,"""Allow node-ios-device to be installed on Windows and Linux""","""""""Due to the {{node_modules}} no longer being committed to the git repo, we need to allow {{node-ios-device}} (via {{ioslib}}) to be installable on Windows and Linux.    {{node-ios-device}} must detect the platform and only build if being run on macOS. It also should remove the """"""""os"""""""" restriction in the {{package.json}}.""""""",Bug,"Title: Allow node-ios-device to be installed on Windows and Linux
Description: """"Due to the {{node_modules}} no longer being committed to the git repo, we need to allow {{node-ios-device}} (via {{ioslib}}) to be installable on Windows and Linux. {{node-ios-device}} must detect the platform and only build if being run on macOS. It also should remove the """"""""os"""""""" restriction in the {{package.json}}.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25008,12,"""iOS: Remove deprecated Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_* constants in favor of TI.UI.KEYBOARD_TYPE_*""","""""""We deprecated the Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_* constants in 5.4.0, in favor of the more clear Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_TYPE_* constants that also share parity with Android. In the release 8.0.0, we should get rid of those, so the core is more solid and clean.     I actually thought about doing it in 7.0.0 already (which would be legit), but let's keep it for one more major, since the actual legacy-code is not messing up the core and there might still be some apps using the old one when migrating from last year.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Remove deprecated Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_* constants in favor of TI.UI.KEYBOARD_TYPE_*
Description: """"We deprecated the Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_* constants in 5.4.0, in favor of the more clear Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_TYPE_* constants that also share parity with Android. In the release 8.0.0, we should get rid of those, so the core is more solid and clean. I actually thought about doing it in 7.0.0 already (which would be legit), but let's keep it for one more major, since the actual legacy-code is not messing up the core and there might still be some apps using the old one when migrating from last year.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25007,12,"""Android: repeatMode for VideoPlayer (parity)""","""""""Androids VideoPlayer is missing the repeatMode. This is a parity ticket to add the two repeatStates (loop/no-loop)    Example:    {code:js}  var vidWin = Titanium.UI.createWindow({   title: 'Video View Demo',   backgroundColor: '#fff'  });    var videoPlayer = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({   top: 2,   autoplay: true,   backgroundColor: 'blue',   height: 300,   width: 300,   mediaControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_DEFAULT,   scalingMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT,   repeatMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_ONE  });    videoPlayer.url = 'movie.mp4';  vidWin.add(videoPlayer);  vidWin.open();  {code}    Modes:   * Titanium.Media.VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_NONE  * Titanium.Media.VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_ONE""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: repeatMode for VideoPlayer (parity)
Description: """"Androids VideoPlayer is missing the repeatMode. This is a parity ticket to add the two repeatStates (loop/no-loop) Example: {code:js} var vidWin = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Video View Demo', backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var videoPlayer = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({ top: 2, autoplay: true, backgroundColor: 'blue', height: 300, width: 300, mediaControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_DEFAULT, scalingMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT, repeatMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_ONE }); videoPlayer.url = 'movie.mp4'; vidWin.add(videoPlayer); vidWin.open(); {code} Modes: * Titanium.Media.VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_NONE * Titanium.Media.VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_ONE""""",title+description
TIMOB-25006,12,"""iOS : Disable copy, select all,define,share popup contex menu inside webview without disabling text selection""","""""""This is the feature works fine on Android but not on iOS platform ,   our application is book reader. the notes and highlight feature is more important to us and to make notes and highlight we must have to select the text inside webview. On iOS Platform The properties disableContextMenu : true also disable the text selection as well.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS : Disable copy, select all,define,share popup contex menu inside webview without disabling text selection
Description: """"This is the feature works fine on Android but not on iOS platform , our application is book reader. the notes and highlight feature is more important to us and to make notes and highlight we must have to select the text inside webview. On iOS Platform The properties disableContextMenu : true also disable the text selection as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25005,12,"""iOS: Remove Ti.UI.iPhone namespace""","""""""The {{Ti.UI.iPhone}} namespace components were deprecated between 3.5.0 and 5.2.0. It is time to remove it in 7.0.0 to speed-up the compile time and use all iOS-only API's on the {{Ti.UI.iOS}} namespace instead. Basically, since all API's have been moved already (including Alloy), there is no migration issue as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Remove Ti.UI.iPhone namespace
Description: """"The {{Ti.UI.iPhone}} namespace components were deprecated between 3.5.0 and 5.2.0. It is time to remove it in 7.0.0 to speed-up the compile time and use all iOS-only API's on the {{Ti.UI.iOS}} namespace instead. Basically, since all API's have been moved already (including Alloy), there is no migration issue as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-25004,12,"""Build: ioslib is getting removed in the 6_1_X build process""","""""""ioslib is getting removed in the build <USER>when pruning the dependencies to remove dev only deps, this is because the checked in package version is at 1.4.7, but the package.json of the repo states ^1.4.8, which 1.4.7 does not meet the range for.       ioslib 1.4.8 shipped in 6.1.1.GA, but it was reverted to 1.4.7 in this commit https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/47ded30e2d93f3ed58d85c413e55bdc71d83ecfd     We need to either update again or correct the version in the package.json    This is the reason for the 'Cannot find ioslib' failures on Jenkins, it does not affect an SDK that is published as the build will fail to test that SDK      h5.To verify  No proper steps here really    # Is Jenkins running happy (more than once)  # Does running {{npm i --only=dev}} then {{npm prune --production}} keep ioslib in the node_modules dir?""""""",Bug,"Title: Build: ioslib is getting removed in the 6_1_X build process
Description: """"ioslib is getting removed in the build <USER>when pruning the dependencies to remove dev only deps, this is because the checked in package version is at 1.4.7, but the package.json of the repo states ^1.4.8, which 1.4.7 does not meet the range for. ioslib 1.4.8 shipped in 6.1.1.GA, but it was reverted to 1.4.7 in this commit https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/47ded30e2d93f3ed58d85c413e55bdc71d83ecfd We need to either update again or correct the version in the package.json This is the reason for the 'Cannot find ioslib' failures on Jenkins, it does not affect an SDK that is published as the build will fail to test that SDK h5.To verify No proper steps here really # Is Jenkins running happy (more than once) # Does running {{npm i --only=dev}} then {{npm prune --production}} keep ioslib in the node_modules dir?""""",title+description
TIMOB-24994,12,"""iOS: Remove Ti.UI.iOS.AdView""","""""""We deprecated the Ti.UI.iOS.AdView as part of Titanium SDK 5.5.0 to follow-up with Apple deprecating the iAd framework in iOS 10. We should remove it in Titanium 7.0.0 and leave a message in the docs and core to notify the developer.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Remove Ti.UI.iOS.AdView
Description: """"We deprecated the Ti.UI.iOS.AdView as part of Titanium SDK 5.5.0 to follow-up with Apple deprecating the iAd framework in iOS 10. We should remove it in Titanium 7.0.0 and leave a message in the docs and core to notify the developer.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24992,12,"""TiAPI: Expose asynchronous file-system""","""""""As part of the engineering week decisions, we are planning to have an asynchronous, non blocking file-system module that will eventually deprecate the old one as we are moving forward with it. In an ideal case, it will share the API with the NodeJS system-module {{fs}} for improved interoperability.""""""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: Expose asynchronous file-system
Description: """"As part of the engineering week decisions, we are planning to have an asynchronous, non blocking file-system module that will eventually deprecate the old one as we are moving forward with it. In an ideal case, it will share the API with the NodeJS system-module {{fs}} for improved interoperability.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24991,12,"""iOS: Remove Ti.UI.DashboardView from the core, distribute as module""","""""""As part of the engineering week decisions, we will deprecate {{Ti.UI.DashboardView}} in 7.0.0 and remove it in 8.0.0. Instead, it will be moved to the {{Ti.Dashboard}} module be used the same way as before.    Example (before):  {code:js}  var myDashboardView = Ti.UI.createDashboardView();  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Remove Ti.UI.DashboardView from the core, distribute as module
Description: """"As part of the engineering week decisions, we will deprecate {{Ti.UI.DashboardView}} in 7.0.0 and remove it in 8.0.0. Instead, it will be moved to the {{Ti.Dashboard}} module be used the same way as before. Example (before): {code:js} var myDashboardView = Ti.UI.createDashboardView(); """"",title+description
