TIMOB-24936,12,"""Windows: Build errors out when selecting wp-emulator or wp-device after being prompted for a target""","""""""h5.Description    When building for Windows and providing an invalid value for target, when selecting a target value that requires detecting devices (wp-emulator or wp-device) the CLI will error out with         h5.Steps to reproduce    # Build a Windows app with {{ti build -p windows -T notvalid}}  # Select either {{wp-device}} or {{wp-emulator}}    h5.Actual    CLI will error out with the above    h5.Expected    CLI should not error out, should build as normal""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Build errors out when selecting wp-emulator or wp-device after being prompted for a target
Description: """"h5.Description When building for Windows and providing an invalid value for target, when selecting a target value that requires detecting devices (wp-emulator or wp-device) the CLI will error out with h5.Steps to reproduce # Build a Windows app with {{ti build -p windows -T notvalid}} # Select either {{wp-device}} or {{wp-emulator}} h5.Actual CLI will error out with the above h5.Expected CLI should not error out, should build as normal""""",title+description
TIMOB-24935,12,"""Android Themes throwing an error with 6.1.1.GA""",""""""" Hi,   Android Themes throwing an error with 6.1.1.GA but working as expected 5.1.1.GA.     Steps to reproduce:   1. Create a sample test project.   2. Create a theme XML file in ./platform/android/res/values        3. Build projcet with 5.1.1.GA (No Error)   4. Now bulid project with 6.1.1.GA and getting following error        Test Environmnet:        Thanks """"""",Bug,"Title: Android Themes throwing an error with 6.1.1.GA
Description: """" Hi, Android Themes throwing an error with 6.1.1.GA but working as expected 5.1.1.GA. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a sample test project. 2. Create a theme XML file in ./platform/android/res/values 3. Build projcet with 5.1.1.GA (No Error) 4. Now bulid project with 6.1.1.GA and getting following error Test Environmnet: Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-24932,12,"""Android Hybrid modules: cannot instantiate a proxy in a js file that is packaged in the same module""","""""""Suppose that I have a module is called {{it.andreavitale.commonjs.test}}:  it has a {{it.andreavitale.commonjs.test.js}} file inside {{my-module/android/assets}} folder and a proxy file under {{my-module/android/src/it/andreavitale/commonjs/test/ExampleProxy.java}}    If inside {{it.andreavitale.commonjs.test.js}} file I call {{require('it.andreavitale.commonjs.test').createExample()}} I always get this error:        If I call {{require('it.andreavitale.commonjs.test').createExample()}} inside my app alloy.js the proxy is correctly created.    I attach a sample module project to reproduce the error.  If you comment the line {{9}} inside {{android/assets/it.andreavitale.commonjs.test.js}} and you run the example app everything will work fine.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Hybrid modules: cannot instantiate a proxy in a js file that is packaged in the same module
Description: """"Suppose that I have a module is called {{it.andreavitale.commonjs.test}}: it has a {{it.andreavitale.commonjs.test.js}} file inside {{my-module/android/assets}} folder and a proxy file under {{my-module/android/src/it/andreavitale/commonjs/test/ExampleProxy.java}} If inside {{it.andreavitale.commonjs.test.js}} file I call {{require('it.andreavitale.commonjs.test').createExample()}} I always get this error: If I call {{require('it.andreavitale.commonjs.test').createExample()}} inside my app alloy.js the proxy is correctly created. I attach a sample module project to reproduce the error. If you comment the line {{9}} inside {{android/assets/it.andreavitale.commonjs.test.js}} and you run the example app everything will work fine.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24931,12,"""Android: Validate NDK versions on module build""","""""""h5.Description    When building an Android module there is currently no verification of the NDK versions. So when building with an unsupported version there is no feedback to the user.    We should follow the standards and error on versions that are lower, warn on higher version.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Validate NDK versions on module build
Description: """"h5.Description When building an Android module there is currently no verification of the NDK versions. So when building with an unsupported version there is no feedback to the user. We should follow the standards and error on versions that are lower, warn on higher version.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24930,12,"""Android: Module build process errors out if no NDK path is set""","""""""h5.Description    When building without an Android NDK path set the build <USER>will error out with the below        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Remove the ndk path from your config {{appc ti config --remove android.ndkPath}}  # Build an Android module using {{appc run -p android --build-only    h5.Actual    Errors out with above error    h5.Expected    Should error out with unable to find an Android SDK""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Module build process errors out if no NDK path is set
Description: """"h5.Description When building without an Android NDK path set the build <USER>will error out with the below h5.Steps to reproduce # Remove the ndk path from your config {{appc ti config --remove android.ndkPath}} # Build an Android module using {{appc run -p android --build-only h5.Actual Errors out with above error h5.Expected Should error out with unable to find an Android SDK""""",title+description
