TIMOB-24924,12,"""Android Themes: Hide the action bar of all windows not working as expected with 6.1.1.GA""","""""""Hi,  In the sample app, the custom theme has a property to hide the action bar of all windows through out the application.If you run the app, your window will show up, but without the effect of a custom theme.    Steps to reproduce:    1. Import  [^sampleApp.zip] project.  2. Build project with 6.1.1.GA   3. Action bar of all window will show up.     Test Environmnet:      Thanks """"""",Bug,"Title: Android Themes: Hide the action bar of all windows not working as expected with 6.1.1.GA
Description: """"Hi, In the sample app, the custom theme has a property to hide the action bar of all windows through out the application.If you run the app, your window will show up, but without the effect of a custom theme. Steps to reproduce: 1. Import [^sampleApp.zip] project. 2. Build project with 6.1.1.GA 3. Action bar of all window will show up. Test Environmnet: Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-24923,12,"""Windows: Unable to create a module with VS2017""","""""""h5.Description    When creating a module with VS 2017 installed, it will throw the warning below and never create the cmake projects     Note: ti cli does not throw an error, but appc cli does        h5.Steps to reproduce    # appc new -t timodule --name myawesomemodule --id com.foo    h5.Actual    CLI will error with the above cmake projects not made    h5.Expected    CLI should not error, cmake project should be made""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Unable to create a module with VS2017
Description: """"h5.Description When creating a module with VS 2017 installed, it will throw the warning below and never create the cmake projects Note: ti cli does not throw an error, but appc cli does h5.Steps to reproduce # appc new -t timodule --name myawesomemodule --id com.foo h5.Actual CLI will error with the above cmake projects not made h5.Expected CLI should not error, cmake project should be made""""",title+description
TIMOB-24922,12,"""Windows: Unable to package with VS 2017""","""""""h5.Description    Packaging a Windows application with VS2017 errors out with the below on cert creation (added logging to show the error message), based off other changes in the VS2017 addition I swapped this (and other occurrences of vcvarsalll) to vsdevcmd and it worked        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Create an app {{appc new -t titanium -n myawesomeapp --id com.foo --no-services}}  # Build the app using {{appc run -p windows -T dist-phonestore}}  # Follow the prompts    h5.Actual    When creating a cert the <USER>will error out    h5.Expected    Process should not error out, cert should be created after prompting""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Unable to package with VS 2017
Description: """"h5.Description Packaging a Windows application with VS2017 errors out with the below on cert creation (added logging to show the error message), based off other changes in the VS2017 addition I swapped this (and other occurrences of vcvarsalll) to vsdevcmd and it worked h5.Steps to reproduce # Create an app {{appc new -t titanium -n myawesomeapp --id com.foo --no-services}} # Build the app using {{appc run -p windows -T dist-phonestore}} # Follow the prompts h5.Actual When creating a cert the <USER>will error out h5.Expected Process should not error out, cert should be created after prompting""""",title+description
TIMOB-24920,12,"""Android: Allow selecting stream type in Ti.Media.Sound (instead of always using STREAM_MUSIC)""","""""""This will allow us to (properly) select, e.g. using the earpiece to playing the sound through the speaker.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Allow selecting stream type in Ti.Media.Sound (instead of always using STREAM_MUSIC)
Description: """"This will allow us to (properly) select, e.g. using the earpiece to playing the sound through the speaker.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24916,12,"""[iOS] Application crashes when """"Ti.Geolocation.getLastGeolocation"""" is called before a geoLocation is set ""","""""""When {{Ti.Geolocation.getLastGeolocation}} is called before a geoLocaiton has been set the application crashes and the log displays the following error.     This is different to Android and 6.1.1.GA where the log instead showed:       *Test Steps*  1. Create a new titanium project using SDK version: 6.2.0.v20170630062735  2. Add the following code to the {{app.js}}    3. Run the application on an iOS device   4. Once the application has launched press the {{Get Geo}} button     *Expected result*  Application should not crash and the log should display the following message       *Actual result*  Application crashes and the above error message is displayed    NOTE:* This could also be why some of the newer Jenkins builds have been failing as the test case for this failed in a few builds.    """"""",Bug,"Title: [iOS] Application crashes when """"Ti.Geolocation.getLastGeolocation"""" is called before a geoLocation is set
Description: """"When {{Ti.Geolocation.getLastGeolocation}} is called before a geoLocaiton has been set the application crashes and the log displays the following error. This is different to Android and 6.1.1.GA where the log instead showed: *Test Steps* 1. Create a new titanium project using SDK version: 6.2.0.v20170630062735 2. Add the following code to the {{app.js}} 3. Run the application on an iOS device 4. Once the application has launched press the {{Get Geo}} button *Expected result* Application should not crash and the log should display the following message *Actual result* Application crashes and the above error message is displayed NOTE:* This could also be why some of the newer Jenkins builds have been failing as the test case for this failed in a few builds. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24915,12,"""Windows: run cmake flag does not work from titanium CLI""","""""""h5.Description    When using the {{--run-cmake}} cli flag from ti cli it will not work and silently fail, this is because it errors out when the cli tries to read in the hook with the below, nodeappc is passed in to the hook and has async on it so we can use that rather than requiring it, it works fine from the appc cli because either the module lookup path is altered or the module has been cached already (I think the former)          h5.Steps to reproduce    # Download ti.paint from github https://github.com/<USER>archive/ti.paint  # Run the module build with {{ti build -p windows --build-only --run-cmake}}    h5.Actual    The build skips every architecture as CMake is not run    h5.Expected    CMake should be run""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: run cmake flag does not work from titanium CLI
Description: """"h5.Description When using the {{--run-cmake}} cli flag from ti cli it will not work and silently fail, this is because it errors out when the cli tries to read in the hook with the below, nodeappc is passed in to the hook and has async on it so we can use that rather than requiring it, it works fine from the appc cli because either the module lookup path is altered or the module has been cached already (I think the former) h5.Steps to reproduce # Download ti.paint from github https://github.com/<USER>archive/ti.paint # Run the module build with {{ti build -p windows --build-only --run-cmake}} h5.Actual The build skips every architecture as CMake is not run h5.Expected CMake should be run""""",title+description
TIMOB-24913,12,"""Windows: Officially deprecate support for Visual Studio 2013""","""""""h5.Description    We're adding support for VS 2017, as we do this we should evaluate whether VS 2013 still has a place in our support matrix (imo it doesn't) and if we decide it doesn't. We should    * Output a warning stating that VS 2013 support was deprecated of X and will be removed in <NEXT_MAJOR> (could possibly do this around here https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/master/cli/commands/_build/initialize.js#L58-L62) after we determine the version?  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Officially deprecate support for Visual Studio 2013
Description: """"h5.Description We're adding support for VS 2017, as we do this we should evaluate whether VS 2013 still has a place in our support matrix (imo it doesn't) and if we decide it doesn't. We should * Output a warning stating that VS 2013 support was deprecated of X and will be removed in <NEXT_MAJOR> (could possibly do this around here https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/master/cli/commands/_build/initialize.js#L58-L62) after we determine the version? """"",title+description
TIMOB-24912,12,"""Android: Running a module after it was built fails on Windows.""","""""""Running a module after building it from sources fails on Windows.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Download module sources  e.g. https://github.com/<USER>NappDrawer  2. Build it with 'appc run -p android -l trace'  3. The <USER>fails after the archive and .jar files are created.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Running a module after it was built fails on Windows.
Description: """"Running a module after building it from sources fails on Windows. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Download module sources e.g. https://github.com/<USER>NappDrawer 2. Build it with 'appc run -p android -l trace' 3. The <USER>fails after the archive and .jar files are created.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24911,12,"""Android: Filtering R. files when building Android modules does not work on Windows.""","""""""Filtering R. files while building Android modules does not happen when done on Windows platform.     *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Download module sources:  e.g. https://github.com/<USER>NappDrawer  2. Select one of the above mentioned SDK versions  3. Build with 'appc run -p android --build-only'  _Note: For building with master 'apiversion' and 'minsdk' in the module's manifest should be bumped_  4. Add the module to the SDK and run an application using it.     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Filtering R. files when building Android modules does not work on Windows.
Description: """"Filtering R. files while building Android modules does not happen when done on Windows platform. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Download module sources: e.g. https://github.com/<USER>NappDrawer 2. Select one of the above mentioned SDK versions 3. Build with 'appc run -p android --build-only' _Note: For building with master 'apiversion' and 'minsdk' in the module's manifest should be bumped_ 4. Add the module to the SDK and run an application using it. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24907,12,"""Windows: Investigate Ti.Blob mimetype failures on jenkins""","""""""A high number of <USER>runs have recently failed due to the same test, across both 8.1 and 10    - Investigate the failures (try and find out when it started if possible)  - Isolate the cause  - Fix if an SDK problem, revisit the test if a test problem (as this seems to be new probably the former)    *Do not skip the test*        https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/9009ed6467bbba7098d8efceb57ff45ad2e14a03/Examples/NMocha/src/Assets/ti.blob.test.js#L68    https://<USER><USER>org/blue/organizations/<USER>titanium-sdk%2Ftitanium_mobile_windows/detail/PR-1008/15/tests""""""",Story,"Title: Windows: Investigate Ti.Blob mimetype failures on jenkins
Description: """"A high number of <USER>runs have recently failed due to the same test, across both 8.1 and 10 - Investigate the failures (try and find out when it started if possible) - Isolate the cause - Fix if an SDK problem, revisit the test if a test problem (as this seems to be new probably the former) *Do not skip the test* https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/blob/9009ed6467bbba7098d8efceb57ff45ad2e14a03/Examples/NMocha/src/Assets/ti.blob.test.js#L68 https://<USER><USER>org/blue/organizations/<USER>titanium-sdk%2Ftitanium_mobile_windows/detail/PR-1008/15/tests""""",title+description
TIMOB-24905,12,"""Windows: ListView scrolling event should only fire when user is touching the screen""","""""""h5.Description    Our docs confuse me on what is correct here http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-event-scrolling (hence filing the ticket and not blocking the PR)        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Add the above code to an existing app.js and build for a Windows device  # Scroll the view and ensure the view still scrolls    h5.Actual    Scrolling event stays firing    h5.Expected    Based off Android and iOS the scrolling event should only fire when the user is touching the screen and actively scrolling.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: ListView scrolling event should only fire when user is touching the screen
Description: """"h5.Description Our docs confuse me on what is correct here http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-event-scrolling (hence filing the ticket and not blocking the PR) h5.Steps to reproduce # Add the above code to an existing app.js and build for a Windows device # Scroll the view and ensure the view still scrolls h5.Actual Scrolling event stays firing h5.Expected Based off Android and iOS the scrolling event should only fire when the user is touching the screen and actively scrolling.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24902,12,"""Windows: Update ti_win_yaml to allow specifying deprecated and added in versions""","""""""h5.Description    Currently (to my knowledge) ti_win_yaml doesn't allow for us to specify when something was deprecated or implemented. So it appears that everything is being marked as 4.1.0 on docs.<USER>    For deprecated items I guess the simplest/easiest way would be to add a new C++ macro like TITANIUM_FUNCTION_DEPRECATED(foo, 6.1.0), this would fit in with the existing pattern.    Specifying when something was implemented might be a little more difficult, for the namespace (Ti.FileSystem) could we use an {{\@since 6.1.0}}, but for individual properties and functions I'm unsure""""""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Update ti_win_yaml to allow specifying deprecated and added in versions
Description: """"h5.Description Currently (to my knowledge) ti_win_yaml doesn't allow for us to specify when something was deprecated or implemented. So it appears that everything is being marked as 4.1.0 on docs.<USER> For deprecated items I guess the simplest/easiest way would be to add a new C++ macro like TITANIUM_FUNCTION_DEPRECATED(foo, 6.1.0), this would fit in with the existing pattern. Specifying when something was implemented might be a little more difficult, for the namespace (Ti.FileSystem) could we use an {{\@since 6.1.0}}, but for individual properties and functions I'm unsure""""",title+description
TIMOB-24901,12,"""Android: List disclosure indicators increases size from SDK 5.5.1.GA to SDK 6.1.1.v20170615113917""","""""""List disclosure indicators an Android display far too large when using Titanium SDK 6.1.1.v20170615113917. The indicators are probably around twice the size they used to display when using SDK 5.5.1.GA.    The attached image shows a screenshot of the bug in a test app using Titanium SDK 6.1.1.v20170615113917    I've taken some example code from the <USER>docs and simplified it slightly to show how to reproduce the issue. The Titanium SDK used to test this was 6.1.1.v20170615113917. It is also a bug in Titanium SDK 6.1.0.GA. It is not a bug in Titanium SDK 5.5.1.GA.        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: List disclosure indicators increases size from SDK 5.5.1.GA to SDK 6.1.1.v20170615113917
Description: """"List disclosure indicators an Android display far too large when using Titanium SDK 6.1.1.v20170615113917. The indicators are probably around twice the size they used to display when using SDK 5.5.1.GA. The attached image shows a screenshot of the bug in a test app using Titanium SDK 6.1.1.v20170615113917 I've taken some example code from the <USER>docs and simplified it slightly to show how to reproduce the issue. The Titanium SDK used to test this was 6.1.1.v20170615113917. It is also a bug in Titanium SDK 6.1.0.GA. It is not a bug in Titanium SDK 5.5.1.GA. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24897,12,"""Android : Building android module from CLI fails with error 'spawn ti ENOENT'""","""""""*NOTE: This might be an user error, gonna ask other team members to try on their side as well, to confirm. Seeing this with SDK 6.1.0.GA & 6.0.4.GA as well.*    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a module using studio or CLI.  2. CD into the android folder.  3. Run {{appc run -l trace}} or {{appc run -p android -l trace}}.    h5. Actual results:  1. The module build fails with error below:      h5. Expected Results:  1. The module should complete successfully.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : Building android module from CLI fails with error 'spawn ti ENOENT'
