TIMOB-24896,12,"""Android: HTTPClient does not support literal IPv6 URLs""","""""""*Summary:*  Titanium's """"""""HTTPClient"""""""" API does not support square bracketed literal IPv6 URLs such as """"""""http://[::1]"""""""".    This is a bug in Google's """"""""Uri"""""""" class which fails to parse the hostname and port number in this case.     https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/37069493    *Steps to Reproduce:*  # Run the below code on an Android device.  # Tap the """"""""Send"""""""" button.  # Observe the Android log.        *Result:*  The HTTP request does not get sent and the following caught exception can be seen in the log.          *Recommended Solution:*  The Java """"""""URL"""""""" class (all caps) doesn't have this IPv6 parsing bug. In our """"""""TiHTTPClient.java"""""""" code, we should use the URL class to fetch the hostname and port number instead. Note that our TiHTTPClient class is already doing this in the open() method if a """"""""username:password"""""""" component has been found in the URL.    *Work-Around:*  Use a literal IPv4 address instead.  And for IPv6 """"""""http://[::1]"""""""", use """"""""http://localhost"""""""" instead.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient does not support literal IPv6 URLs
Description: """"*Summary:* Titanium's """"""""HTTPClient"""""""" API does not support square bracketed literal IPv6 URLs such as """"""""http://[::1]"""""""". This is a bug in Google's """"""""Uri"""""""" class which fails to parse the hostname and port number in this case. https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/37069493 *Steps to Reproduce:* # Run the below code on an Android device. # Tap the """"""""Send"""""""" button. # Observe the Android log. *Result:* The HTTP request does not get sent and the following caught exception can be seen in the log. *Recommended Solution:* The Java """"""""URL"""""""" class (all caps) doesn't have this IPv6 parsing bug. In our """"""""TiHTTPClient.java"""""""" code, we should use the URL class to fetch the hostname and port number instead. Note that our TiHTTPClient class is already doing this in the open() method if a """"""""username:password"""""""" component has been found in the URL. *Work-Around:* Use a literal IPv4 address instead. And for IPv6 """"""""http://[::1]"""""""", use """"""""http://localhost"""""""" instead. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24895,12,"""AssetCryptImpl.java symbol not found while build for Android on Linux""","""""""When building a freshly created Titanium Alloy project the build fails when building the Java source files with the following error:        This is because the asset encryption does not finish and the AssetCryptImpl.java does not contain the generated variables. Manually executing the command included in the build output gives a Segmentation Fault. So there seems to be some error with the ELF {{.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/6.1.0.GA/android/titanium_prep.linux64}}        Not quite sure who's responsible because with kernel {{linux-image-4.4.0-79-generic 4.4.0-79.100~14.04.1}} it works like expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: AssetCryptImpl.java symbol not found while build for Android on Linux
Description: """"When building a freshly created Titanium Alloy project the build fails when building the Java source files with the following error: This is because the asset encryption does not finish and the AssetCryptImpl.java does not contain the generated variables. Manually executing the command included in the build output gives a Segmentation Fault. So there seems to be some error with the ELF {{.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/6.1.0.GA/android/titanium_prep.linux64}} Not quite sure who's responsible because with kernel {{linux-image-4.4.0-79-generic 4.4.0-79.100~14.04.1}} it works like expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24891,12,"""CLI: Error should not be output when android executable cannot be found""","""""""h5.Description    When running {{ti setup check}} under Android Environment the following is output, to my knowledge the android executable is now deprecated by Google, we should not spit out an error message like this for a deprecated tool (as long as their versions indicate it is deprecated I guess)          h5.Steps to reproduce    # Run {{\[appc\] ti setup check}}    h5.Actual    {{×  android            """"""""android"""""""" executable not found; please reinstall Android SDK}}    h5.Expected    A warning that is less worrisome, or no output at all if it is no longer relevant to the tools""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Error should not be output when android executable cannot be found
Description: """"h5.Description When running {{ti setup check}} under Android Environment the following is output, to my knowledge the android executable is now deprecated by Google, we should not spit out an error message like this for a deprecated tool (as long as their versions indicate it is deprecated I guess) h5.Steps to reproduce # Run {{\[appc\] ti setup check}} h5.Actual {{× android """"""""android"""""""" executable not found; please reinstall Android SDK}} h5.Expected A warning that is less worrisome, or no output at all if it is no longer relevant to the tools""""",title+description
