TIMOB-24791,12,"""Android: SDK 6_X_X issue with local JS require""","""""""Hello,    I am facing an issue since the SDK 6_X_X on android , where i have the issue bellow    *[ERROR] :  TiExceptionHandler: (main) [125,125] ----- Titanium Javascript Runtime Error -----  [ERROR] :  TiExceptionHandler: (main) [0,125] - In ti:/module.js:303,2  [ERROR] :  TiExceptionHandler: (main) [0,125] - Message: Uncaught Error: Requested module not found: crypto-js/hmac  [ERROR] :  TiExceptionHandler: (main) [0,125] - Source:  throw new Error(""""""""Requested module not found: """""""" + request); // TODO Set 'code' property to 'MODULE_NOT_FOUND' to match Node?  [ERROR] :  V8Exception: Exception occurred at ti:/module.js:303: Uncaught Error: Requested module not found: crypto-js/hmac  *  The same lib working fine on 5_5_X, could you please help me with this.    Best regards.                """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: SDK 6_X_X issue with local JS require
Description: """"Hello, I am facing an issue since the SDK 6_X_X on android , where i have the issue bellow *[ERROR] : TiExceptionHandler: (main) [125,125] ----- Titanium Javascript Runtime Error ----- [ERROR] : TiExceptionHandler: (main) [0,125] - In ti:/module.js:303,2 [ERROR] : TiExceptionHandler: (main) [0,125] - Message: Uncaught Error: Requested module not found: crypto-js/hmac [ERROR] : TiExceptionHandler: (main) [0,125] - Source: throw new Error(""""""""Requested module not found: """""""" + request); // TODO Set 'code' property to 'MODULE_NOT_FOUND' to match Node? [ERROR] : V8Exception: Exception occurred at ti:/module.js:303: Uncaught Error: Requested module not found: crypto-js/hmac * The same lib working fine on 5_5_X, could you please help me with this. Best regards. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24787,12,"""CLI: """"Invalid Version: .DS_Store.0"""" Is Shown when using old build tools to build an Android project""","""""""When building a project with Andorid build tools 22.0.1, I am getting the following error message. (trace enabled) [^log.txt]    *Test steps*  # Uninstall all Android {{build-tools}} apart from {{22.0.1}}  # Create a new project   # {{cd}} in to the project  # Use the following command {{Build a project with appc run -p android -T device --build-only}}    *Expected Result*  Following error message should be displayed: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24779      *Actual result:*  Following error is show (trace enabled)  [^log.txt]    *NOTE: If you use the terminal to {{cd}} in to {{Library/android-sdk-macosx/build-tools}} and use {{rm .DS_Store}} and then build the project (step 4 above) the correct error message is shown.*  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"Invalid Version: .DS_Store.0"""" Is Shown when using old build tools to build an Android project
Description: """"When building a project with Andorid build tools 22.0.1, I am getting the following error message. (trace enabled) [^log.txt] *Test steps* # Uninstall all Android {{build-tools}} apart from {{22.0.1}} # Create a new project # {{cd}} in to the project # Use the following command {{Build a project with appc run -p android -T device --build-only}} *Expected Result* Following error message should be displayed: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24779 *Actual result:* Following error is show (trace enabled) [^log.txt] *NOTE: If you use the terminal to {{cd}} in to {{Library/android-sdk-macosx/build-tools}} and use {{rm .DS_Store}} and then build the project (step 4 above) the correct error message is shown.* """"",title+description
TIMOB-24785,12,"""Android: HTTPClient - Digest authentication not supported""","""""""*Description*  When using HTTPClient Basic Digest, a 401 unauthorized is thrown.    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Create a Titanium Classic App.  2. Replace the app.js code with the attached HttpClientAuthTest.js  3. Build to Android device  4. Press on """"""""BASIC DIGEST - GET HTTPS"""""""" button    *Result*  401 errors are thrown:      *Expected Result*  Should get 200 success response, as it does with iOS devices.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient - Digest authentication not supported
Description: """"*Description* When using HTTPClient Basic Digest, a 401 unauthorized is thrown. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Create a Titanium Classic App. 2. Replace the app.js code with the attached HttpClientAuthTest.js 3. Build to Android device 4. Press on """"""""BASIC DIGEST - GET HTTPS"""""""" button *Result* 401 errors are thrown: *Expected Result* Should get 200 success response, as it does with iOS devices. """"",title+description
