TIMOB-24779,12,"""CLI: Error message for too old build-tools is confusing""","""""""h5.Description    When building with a Android SDK Build-tools version that is too old, the error message is confusing (at least to me). I would expect a warning that my version is too old, not that I have tools missing.        h5.Steps to reproduce    I ran into this while fixing TIMOB-24778, if you test this before that fix is available edit the package.json file under {{<SDK>/android/}} to match {{""""""""android build tools"""""""": """""""">=23 <=25.x"""""""",}}    # Install Android SDK Build-tools@22.0.1  # Build a project with appc run -p android -T device --build-only      h5.Actual    Error message shown is confusing as it says tools are not installed, when they are but are just unsupported    h5.Expect     Error message should match the reality""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Error message for too old build-tools is confusing
Description: """"h5.Description When building with a Android SDK Build-tools version that is too old, the error message is confusing (at least to me). I would expect a warning that my version is too old, not that I have tools missing. h5.Steps to reproduce I ran into this while fixing TIMOB-24778, if you test this before that fix is available edit the package.json file under {{<SDK>/android/}} to match {{""""""""android build tools"""""""": """""""">=23 <=25.x"""""""",}} # Install Android SDK Build-tools@22.0.1 # Build a project with appc run -p android -T device --build-only h5.Actual Error message shown is confusing as it says tools are not installed, when they are but are just unsupported h5.Expect Error message should match the reality""""",title+description
TIMOB-24778,12,"""CLI: Minimum android build tools is incorrect""","""""""h5.Description    TIMOB-24733 appears to have created a dependency on the Android build tools being 23.0.1 or above (see error below). When building with lower than this, due to the hard dependency I would expect that there would be a warning/error telling me that my build tools are unsupported/wont work, but I do not see this.        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Install {{Android SDK Build-tools@22.0.1}}  # Build a project with {{appc run -p android -T device --build-only}}    h5.Actual    Build errors out with the above error    h5.Expected    Build should error out with an error stating the build tools are unsupported""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Minimum android build tools is incorrect
Description: """"h5.Description TIMOB-24733 appears to have created a dependency on the Android build tools being 23.0.1 or above (see error below). When building with lower than this, due to the hard dependency I would expect that there would be a warning/error telling me that my build tools are unsupported/wont work, but I do not see this. h5.Steps to reproduce # Install {{Android SDK Build-tools@22.0.1}} # Build a project with {{appc run -p android -T device --build-only}} h5.Actual Build errors out with the above error h5.Expected Build should error out with an error stating the build tools are unsupported""""",title+description
