TIMOB-24722,12,"""Android: Ti Modules causing conflict with google play services ""","""""""h5. Issue Description     At creating an <USER>android module which uses Google Play services.  I'm using the libraries 'play-services-base-9.4.0.jar' and 'play-services-basement-9.4.0.jar' in my appc module which is attached - testplayservicesmodule.zip    If i use this project in the appc app, everything is working fine.  But, if I add ti.map module as well to my appc app, it is giving error as 'Failed to run dexer' since the ti.map is also using similar jars in it.    h5. Steps to reproduce     1. Import project TestPlayServicesApp.zip into Appc Studio.  2. Import timap module  3. Run the application.    You will see the following error log:  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti Modules causing conflict with google play services
Description: """"h5. Issue Description At creating an <USER>android module which uses Google Play services. I'm using the libraries 'play-services-base-9.4.0.jar' and 'play-services-basement-9.4.0.jar' in my appc module which is attached - testplayservicesmodule.zip If i use this project in the appc app, everything is working fine. But, if I add ti.map module as well to my appc app, it is giving error as 'Failed to run dexer' since the ti.map is also using similar jars in it. h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Import project TestPlayServicesApp.zip into Appc Studio. 2. Import timap module 3. Run the application. You will see the following error log: """"",title+description
