Description: """"We currently use a outdated version of acorn to parse JavaScript files in Hyperloop. As the node-titnaium-sdk recently moved to Babylon for better support of upcoming ES version, we should also make that change in Hyperloop.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24720,12,"""iOS: Error when using ES6 keywords with Hyperloop enabled""","""""""I am getting this error when I try const test = 5   (same thing happens with let)    [ERROR] The keyword 'const' is reserved      NOTE:  In trying to recreate this with new project, I am noticing that it only happens when Hyperloop is enabled.    See steps to recreate below.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Error when using ES6 keywords with Hyperloop enabled
Description: """"I am getting this error when I try const test = 5 (same thing happens with let) [ERROR] The keyword 'const' is reserved NOTE: In trying to recreate this with new project, I am noticing that it only happens when Hyperloop is enabled. See steps to recreate below.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24716,12,"""iOS: Scrollview click event not generated by child.""","""""""Click and double click events having unexpected behaviour in different controls within Scrollview.    *Click Event*  Scrollview click event not generated by nested children, When you click within child area in Scrollview its working fine.    *Double Click Event*  Double click is working fine nested children but ScrollVeiw child having problem in double click.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Scrollview click event not generated by child.
Description: """"Click and double click events having unexpected behaviour in different controls within Scrollview. *Click Event* Scrollview click event not generated by nested children, When you click within child area in Scrollview its working fine. *Double Click Event* Double click is working fine nested children but ScrollVeiw child having problem in double click. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24713,12,"""Windows: VS2017 reported as not installed when no vcvarsall detected""","""""""h5.Description    When a basic install of VS2017 is done (I installed just the editor), {{ti info -t windows}} will report that Visual Studio is not installed. This is because vcvarsall does not exist, and if it does not exist then we do not return any data on the install, [see here|https://github.com/<USER>windowslib/blob/2d2c0c51a1599795fa1cbd0d2aa20e1d30b10c36/lib/visualstudio.js#L123], to help diagnose issues it would be nice to return the base install even when this does not exist.    h5.Steps to reproduce    # Install VS2017 selecting just the editor  # Run {{ti info -t windows}}    h5.Actual    No VS install reported    h5.Expected    VS install should be reporter""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: VS2017 reported as not installed when no vcvarsall detected
Description: """"h5.Description When a basic install of VS2017 is done (I installed just the editor), {{ti info -t windows}} will report that Visual Studio is not installed. This is because vcvarsall does not exist, and if it does not exist then we do not return any data on the install, [see here|https://github.com/<USER>windowslib/blob/2d2c0c51a1599795fa1cbd0d2aa20e1d30b10c36/lib/visualstudio.js#L123], to help diagnose issues it would be nice to return the base install even when this does not exist. h5.Steps to reproduce # Install VS2017 selecting just the editor # Run {{ti info -t windows}} h5.Actual No VS install reported h5.Expected VS install should be reporter""""",title+description
TIMOB-24712,12,"""Android: SDK 6.1.0.RC doesnt honor custom_theme.xml colorPrimary setting""",""""""" I have the following custom scheme.      On compiling under 6.1.0.RC I find that the colorPrimary (#0054a6) is no longer a nice blue, but an ugly gray. Go back to the previous version and it all works as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: SDK 6.1.0.RC doesnt honor custom_theme.xml colorPrimary setting
Description: """" I have the following custom scheme. On compiling under 6.1.0.RC I find that the colorPrimary (#0054a6) is no longer a nice blue, but an ugly gray. Go back to the previous version and it all works as expected.""""",title+description
