TIMOB-24706,12,"""Ti.Geolocation.Android returns """"fused"""" even when device in Airplane mode.""","""""""If I set  Ti.Geolocation.Android.manualMode to true and define only one Ti.Geolocation.Android.createLocationProvider and one Ti.Geolocation.Android.createLocationRule, the Android geolocation module returns """"""""fused"""""""" even when device is in Airplane mode and only occasionally returns GPS results from my defined LocationProvider.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Geolocation.Android returns """"fused"""" even when device in Airplane mode.
Description: """"If I set Ti.Geolocation.Android.manualMode to true and define only one Ti.Geolocation.Android.createLocationProvider and one Ti.Geolocation.Android.createLocationRule, the Android geolocation module returns """"""""fused"""""""" even when device is in Airplane mode and only occasionally returns GPS results from my defined LocationProvider. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24701,12,"""Hyperloop: Android - Generated metabase is copied to /Resources/android in classic projects""","""""""When using Hyperloop Android a classic Titanium project (non-Alloy), the metabase is not only generated to build/hyperloop but also to Resources/android. This should *never* happen, because developers store their application logic there and all generated files should stay in build/.""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: Android - Generated metabase is copied to /Resources/android in classic projects
Description: """"When using Hyperloop Android a classic Titanium project (non-Alloy), the metabase is not only generated to build/hyperloop but also to Resources/android. This should *never* happen, because developers store their application logic there and all generated files should stay in build/.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24700,12,"""Android: button has too much top padding, chops off bottom of title (regression)""","""""""When a button is 44dp tall, a 16dp title appears centered in the button, as it should.  When a button is 33dp tall, 4 pixels of the same title are cropped at the bottom.  The entire title seems shifted down in the button, as if it is not vertically centered.  It appears that the internal label has been given a top, or the button has some top padding that it shouldn't have.    This button appeared correctly in SDK 5.1.x.    Sample code:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: button has too much top padding, chops off bottom of title (regression)
Description: """"When a button is 44dp tall, a 16dp title appears centered in the button, as it should. When a button is 33dp tall, 4 pixels of the same title are cropped at the bottom. The entire title seems shifted down in the button, as if it is not vertically centered. It appears that the internal label has been given a top, or the button has some top padding that it shouldn't have. This button appeared correctly in SDK 5.1.x. Sample code: """"",title+description
TIMOB-24699,12,"""LiveView: Alloy app errors out when built for Windows""","""""""h5.Description    When building an alloy app with liveview for windows platform the app will start, connect to the file server and then error out with         h5.Steps to reproduce    # Create an alloy app with {{appc new}}  # Build the alloy app with {{appc run -p windows -T wp-emulator --liveview --liveview-ip <IP>}} where IP is the ip of {{Ethernet adapter vEthernet (Internal Ethernet Port Windows Phone Emulator Internal}} in {{ipconfig}}    h5.Actual    App errors out with the above error    h5.Expected    App should no error out, liveview should work as normal""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Alloy app errors out when built for Windows
Description: """"h5.Description When building an alloy app with liveview for windows platform the app will start, connect to the file server and then error out with h5.Steps to reproduce # Create an alloy app with {{appc new}} # Build the alloy app with {{appc run -p windows -T wp-emulator --liveview --liveview-ip <IP>}} where IP is the ip of {{Ethernet adapter vEthernet (Internal Ethernet Port Windows Phone Emulator Internal}} in {{ipconfig}} h5.Actual App errors out with the above error h5.Expected App should no error out, liveview should work as normal""""",title+description
TIMOB-24698,12,"""Android: Unable to find default AVD emulator from CLI""","""""""*Description*  When building an Android app with """"""""appc run"""""""" without specifying a particular emulator, a default emulator should automatically launch. Instead an error is occurring. This is a regression. This bug is not present in SDK 6.0.3.GA.    *Steps to reproduce*  From the CLI:  1. appc new  2. cd to the project.  3. appc run  4. Choose android.  5. Wait for app to launch on an emulator.    *Result*  AVD emulator does not launch. A Genymotion emulator is attempted to be launched but fails. Attached logs contain the failures.     *Expected Result*  The default AVD emulator should launch.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Unable to find default AVD emulator from CLI
Description: """"*Description* When building an Android app with """"""""appc run"""""""" without specifying a particular emulator, a default emulator should automatically launch. Instead an error is occurring. This is a regression. This bug is not present in SDK 6.0.3.GA. *Steps to reproduce* From the CLI: 1. appc new 2. cd to the project. 3. appc run 4. Choose android. 5. Wait for app to launch on an emulator. *Result* AVD emulator does not launch. A Genymotion emulator is attempted to be launched but fails. Attached logs contain the failures. *Expected Result* The default AVD emulator should launch. """"",title+description
TIMOB-24696,12,"""Uncaught exception thrown when running appc ti info or ti info""","""""""When running either {{appc ti info}} or {{ti info}}  I am getting the following error:        """"""",Bug,"Title: Uncaught exception thrown when running appc ti info or ti info
Description: """"When running either {{appc ti info}} or {{ti info}} I am getting the following error: """"",title+description
TIMOB-24694,12,"""LiveView: No errors reported to user if the LiveView server process errors""","""""""h5.Description    When passing in a custom IP that does not resolve, LiveView will try to start up and then silently fail with no feedback to the user.    It should not silently fail and let the build continue as the app will go on and launch as normal, giving the user the impression that the server launched fine. At the very least it should log a big nasty error    h5.Steps to reproduce    # Build a app with {{--liveview --liveview-ip 123.4.5.6}}  # Wait for the app to launch    h5.Actual    App starts up and errors out, console gives no impression of any issues with the server other than the absence of the LiveView    h5.Expected    Some sort of representation to the user that the LiveView server failed to start""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: No errors reported to user if the LiveView server process errors
Description: """"h5.Description When passing in a custom IP that does not resolve, LiveView will try to start up and then silently fail with no feedback to the user. It should not silently fail and let the build continue as the app will go on and launch as normal, giving the user the impression that the server launched fine. At the very least it should log a big nasty error h5.Steps to reproduce # Build a app with {{--liveview --liveview-ip 123.4.5.6}} # Wait for the app to launch h5.Actual App starts up and errors out, console gives no impression of any issues with the server other than the absence of the LiveView h5.Expected Some sort of representation to the user that the LiveView server failed to start""""",title+description
TIMOB-24693,12,"""LiveView: Incorrect argument checked for custom IP""","""""""h5.Description    When passing in a custom IP for liveview to use the command line arg is --liveview-ip, liveview checks for liveview-host https://github.com/<USER>liveview/blob/4de3f39330fcd6de5ca90b406f4b94c4feaf32d1/hook/lvhook.js#L129    h5.Steps to reproduce    # Build an app with {{--liveview --liveview-ip 123.4.5.6}}  # Check the logs    h5.Actual    App starts and errors out that it cant access an ip that is not 123.4.5.6    h5.Expected    App should start and error out that it cant access 123.4.5.6  """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Incorrect argument checked for custom IP
Description: """"h5.Description When passing in a custom IP for liveview to use the command line arg is --liveview-ip, liveview checks for liveview-host https://github.com/<USER>liveview/blob/4de3f39330fcd6de5ca90b406f4b94c4feaf32d1/hook/lvhook.js#L129 h5.Steps to reproduce # Build an app with {{--liveview --liveview-ip 123.4.5.6}} # Check the logs h5.Actual App starts and errors out that it cant access an ip that is not 123.4.5.6 h5.Expected App should start and error out that it cant access 123.4.5.6 """"",title+description
TIMOB-24692,12,"""A letter '%' is doubled on Android""","""""""------------------  var myname = """"""""%"""""""";  Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname);    This simple code shows wrong output on Android    Android  [INFO]  test:%%    iOS  [INFO]  test:%    ---------------------  Reproduction procedure:    1.Create new project,  2.Paste this code below  in app.js     var myname = """"""""1%1"""""""";  Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname);    var myname = """"""""1\%1"""""""";  Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname);    var myname = '1%1';  Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname);    3:Build and run on android.    --------------------  Result    [INFO]  test:1%%1""""""",Bug,"Title: A letter '%' is doubled on Android
Description: """"------------------ var myname = """"""""%""""""""; Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname); This simple code shows wrong output on Android Android [INFO] test:%% iOS [INFO] test:% --------------------- Reproduction procedure: 1.Create new project, 2.Paste this code below in app.js var myname = """"""""1%1""""""""; Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname); var myname = """"""""1\%1""""""""; Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname); var myname = '1%1'; Ti.API.info(""""""""test:"""""""" + myname); 3:Build and run on android. -------------------- Result [INFO] test:1%%1""""",title+description
TIMOB-24691,12,"""Forked correct SDK command args doesn't resolve platform when using short flag""","""""""When you run a build where the selected SDK differs from the one in the tiapp.xml, it forks the correct sdk build command. However, if you specify the platform as {{\-p}} instead of {{\-\-platform}}, it doesn't define {{platform}} and thus the platform is never injected into the forked command arguments.    Since Studio always passes in {{\-\-platform}}, this really only affects CLI users. When {{\-\-platform}} is not set in the forked command args, it will simply prompt for the platform (or error and exit if prompting is disabled).""""""",Bug,"Title: Forked correct SDK command args doesn't resolve platform when using short flag
Description: """"When you run a build where the selected SDK differs from the one in the tiapp.xml, it forks the correct sdk build command. However, if you specify the platform as {{\-p}} instead of {{\-\-platform}}, it doesn't define {{platform}} and thus the platform is never injected into the forked command arguments. Since Studio always passes in {{\-\-platform}}, this really only affects CLI users. When {{\-\-platform}} is not set in the forked command args, it will simply prompt for the platform (or error and exit if prompting is disabled).""""",title+description
TIMOB-24688,12,"""Android: Add support for adaptive-icons""","""""""Android 8 or O allows applications to have a adaptive icon with a background and foreground image in the launcher.  It would be nice if Titanium could support the adaptive-icon attribute in AndroidManifest.xml along with roundIcon as mentioned here: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24659.  Follow this link https://developer.android.com/preview/features/adaptive-icons.html to know more about this implementation.    Thanks!""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add support for adaptive-icons
Description: """"Android 8 or O allows applications to have a adaptive icon with a background and foreground image in the launcher. It would be nice if Titanium could support the adaptive-icon attribute in AndroidManifest.xml along with roundIcon as mentioned here: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-24659. Follow this link https://developer.android.com/preview/features/adaptive-icons.html to know more about this implementation. Thanks!""""",title+description
