TIMOB-24681,12,"""Android: AVD detection fails if matching SDK is not installed""","""""""*Steps to reproduce the behavior*  1. Create an AVD in Android Studio via _Tools > Android > AVD Manager_ without the matching SDK being installed, e.g. AVD with Android 5.1 but no SDK 22 installed. This will download the required Google APIs System Image but not the SDK.  2. Try to run an app on that emulator with {{appc run -p android -C <emulator-id> -l trace}}    *Actual behavior*  The build crashes with the following error:      *Expected behavior*  The build succeeds and the app launches on the specified AVD.    *Additional notes*  This also breaks {{appc info}} with the unhelpful error:  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: AVD detection fails if matching SDK is not installed
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce the behavior* 1. Create an AVD in Android Studio via _Tools > Android > AVD Manager_ without the matching SDK being installed, e.g. AVD with Android 5.1 but no SDK 22 installed. This will download the required Google APIs System Image but not the SDK. 2. Try to run an app on that emulator with {{appc run -p android -C <emulator-id> -l trace}} *Actual behavior* The build crashes with the following error: *Expected behavior* The build succeeds and the app launches on the specified AVD. *Additional notes* This also breaks {{appc info}} with the unhelpful error: """"",title+description
TIMOB-24680,12,"""iOS: Enterprise ad hoc provisioning profiles not validating properly for [watch] extensions""","""""""When we introduced proper support for enterprise ad hoc provisioning profiles, it appears we missed the validation for extension provisioning profiles.    The iOS build needs to validate the extension's provisioning profile against the correct data set for the build target (appstore vs ad hoc).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Enterprise ad hoc provisioning profiles not validating properly for [watch] extensions
Description: """"When we introduced proper support for enterprise ad hoc provisioning profiles, it appears we missed the validation for extension provisioning profiles. The iOS build needs to validate the extension's provisioning profile against the correct data set for the build target (appstore vs ad hoc).""""",title+description
TIMOB-24675,12,"""iOS: Ti.Geolocation.hasLocationPermissions returns false for WHEN_IN_USE when ALWAYS is approved""","""""""When you ask if permission has been given for """"""""WHEN_IN_USE"""""""" with Ti.Geolocation.hasLocationPermissions when in fact """"""""ALWAYS"""""""" has been approved you get false. But, technically, when the user approves """"""""ALWAYS"""""""" both ALWAYS and WHEN_IN_USE are approved, not only ALWAYS, as we're still allowed to get geolocation when the app is in use.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Geolocation.hasLocationPermissions returns false for WHEN_IN_USE when ALWAYS is approved
Description: """"When you ask if permission has been given for """"""""WHEN_IN_USE"""""""" with Ti.Geolocation.hasLocationPermissions when in fact """"""""ALWAYS"""""""" has been approved you get false. But, technically, when the user approves """"""""ALWAYS"""""""" both ALWAYS and WHEN_IN_USE are approved, not only ALWAYS, as we're still allowed to get geolocation when the app is in use.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24674,12,"""Windows: require call in node_modules directory fails to find module""","""""""h5.Description    Carrying over from, TIMOB-24642. The demo app at https://www.dropbox.com/s/m4wy91x92gxw63m/demo.zip?dl=1 when built for windows will throw the error below, it seems to be unable to traverse back through to the top level node_modules to find bar        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Download the above app  # Build it for Windows    h5.Actual    Error is thrown    h5.Expected    No error thrown, console should log the below    [INFO] boz index.js loaded  [INFO] boo boo.js loaded  [INFO] baz index.js loaded  [INFO] bar bar.js loaded  [INFO] foo lib/foo.js loaded  [INFO] foo index.js loaded""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: require call in node_modules directory fails to find module
Description: """"h5.Description Carrying over from, TIMOB-24642. The demo app at https://www.dropbox.com/s/m4wy91x92gxw63m/demo.zip?dl=1 when built for windows will throw the error below, it seems to be unable to traverse back through to the top level node_modules to find bar h5.Steps to reproduce # Download the above app # Build it for Windows h5.Actual Error is thrown h5.Expected No error thrown, console should log the below [INFO] boz index.js loaded [INFO] boo boo.js loaded [INFO] baz index.js loaded [INFO] bar bar.js loaded [INFO] foo lib/foo.js loaded [INFO] foo index.js loaded""""",title+description
