TIMOB-24538,12,"""iOS: Setting Ti.UI.ListItem """"bindId"""" property to reserved identifier should fail gracefully""","""""""There are properties like """"""""badge"""""""" and """"""""constants"""""""" that are private API of the {{UITableViewCell}}, which we subclass with our {{TiUIListItem}}. Setting the bindId to those values and trying to update the underlaying key-paths afterwards will cause a crash like """"""""this class is not key value coding-compliant for the key color."""""""" which doesn't say anything to the Titanium developer. Instead, we should show a modal error saying """"""""The bindId """"""""<bind-id>"""""""" is reserved by the system, please choose a different name and try again."""""""". Easy one.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Setting Ti.UI.ListItem """"bindId"""" property to reserved identifier should fail gracefully
Description: """"There are properties like """"""""badge"""""""" and """"""""constants"""""""" that are private API of the {{UITableViewCell}}, which we subclass with our {{TiUIListItem}}. Setting the bindId to those values and trying to update the underlaying key-paths afterwards will cause a crash like """"""""this class is not key value coding-compliant for the key color."""""""" which doesn't say anything to the Titanium developer. Instead, we should show a modal error saying """"""""The bindId """"""""<bind-id>"""""""" is reserved by the system, please choose a different name and try again."""""""". Easy one.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24537,12,"""Android: Ti.Gesture should provide device orientation like iOS""","""""""h6. Description   TI Gesture does not fire orientationchange event on Android. It works fine on iOS    h6. Steps to Replicate  1. Lauch app and tilt the device.    h6. Expected results  Fire event as it does on iOS  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.Gesture should provide device orientation like iOS
Description: """"h6. Description TI Gesture does not fire orientationchange event on Android. It works fine on iOS h6. Steps to Replicate 1. Lauch app and tilt the device. h6. Expected results Fire event as it does on iOS """"",title+description
TIMOB-24536,12,"""Android: Implement getExternalFilesDir in Ti.Filesystem""","""""""Currently, Titanium SDK apps can get paths save data in applicationDataDirectory or externalDataStorage (which seems to go to the SD card if one is installed). Android provides primary external storage for apps. They can retrieve that path using the getExternalFilesDir function. See    https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Context.html#getExternalFilesDir(java.lang.String)    It would be helpful for apps to have access to this directory so they can save documents that are visible to the user (to transfer documents to another device) or to sync using apps like FolderSync. Documents saved in the private app data directory are not visible outside of the app itself.    Please add a field to Ti.Filesystem to provide this directory.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Implement getExternalFilesDir in Ti.Filesystem
Description: """"Currently, Titanium SDK apps can get paths save data in applicationDataDirectory or externalDataStorage (which seems to go to the SD card if one is installed). Android provides primary external storage for apps. They can retrieve that path using the getExternalFilesDir function. See https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Context.html#getExternalFilesDir(java.lang.String) It would be helpful for apps to have access to this directory so they can save documents that are visible to the user (to transfer documents to another device) or to sync using apps like FolderSync. Documents saved in the private app data directory are not visible outside of the app itself. Please add a field to Ti.Filesystem to provide this directory.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24535,12,"""iOS: Ti.Geolocation Speed returning incorrect number or -1 for speed, requires docs-clarification""","""""""When listening for the location event for iOS, the speed returned is very often -1 and sometimes an incorrect value. It's very inconsistent. This was working before with our previous app release with SDK 5.5.0.GA but it no longer does with the newest SDK 6.0.2. I also tried rolling back to 5.5.0.GA but this doesn't seem to fix the issue either.         index.js:  {code:js}  var numOfCalls = 0;  var locationCallback = function(e) {   $.numOfLocationCalls.text = """"""""Num of calls: """""""" + numOfCalls;   numOfCalls++;   if (!e.success || e.error) {    $.labelSpeed.text = """"""""Error:"""""""" + JSON.stringify(e);      } else {       var mph = e.coords.speed * 2.23694;       $.label.text = """"""""Speed: """""""" + mph;       var overSpeed = (e.coords.speed > 5) ? true : false;       $.labelSpeed.text = """"""""Over speed: """""""" + overSpeed;      }  };    Ti.Geolocation.addEventListener('location', locationCallback);  Ti.Geolocation.preferredProvider = Ti.Geolocation.PROVIDER_GPS;  Ti.Geolocation.accuracy = Ti.Geolocation.ACCURACY_BEST;  Ti.Geolocation.distanceFilter = 5;    $.index.open();  {code}    index.xml:  {code:xml}  <Alloy>   <Window class=""""""""container"""""""">    <View layout=""""""""vertical"""""""" height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE"""""""">     <Label id=""""""""label"""""""">Hello, World</Label>     <Label id=""""""""labelSpeed"""""""">Hello, World</Label>     <Label id=""""""""numOfLocationCalls"""""""">Hello, World</Label>    </View>   </Window>  </Alloy>  {code}    in tiapp.xml, I have these permissions:  {code:xml}  <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>  <string>Your location will only be used when the app is running.</string>  {code}    NOTE: I tried adding this to the axway support portal as I am a enterprise developer, but I can't seem to login at the moment. Will likely be adding this there once I get that sorted out.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Geolocation Speed returning incorrect number or -1 for speed, requires docs-clarification
Description: """"When listening for the location event for iOS, the speed returned is very often -1 and sometimes an incorrect value. It's very inconsistent. This was working before with our previous app release with SDK 5.5.0.GA but it no longer does with the newest SDK 6.0.2. I also tried rolling back to 5.5.0.GA but this doesn't seem to fix the issue either. index.js: {code:js} var numOfCalls = 0; var locationCallback = function(e) { $.numOfLocationCalls.text = """"""""Num of calls: """""""" + numOfCalls; numOfCalls++; if (!e.success || e.error) { $.labelSpeed.text = """"""""Error:"""""""" + JSON.stringify(e); } else { var mph = e.coords.speed * 2.23694; $.label.text = """"""""Speed: """""""" + mph; var overSpeed = (e.coords.speed > 5) ? true : false; $.labelSpeed.text = """"""""Over speed: """""""" + overSpeed; } }; Ti.Geolocation.addEventListener('location', locationCallback); Ti.Geolocation.preferredProvider = Ti.Geolocation.PROVIDER_GPS; Ti.Geolocation.accuracy = Ti.Geolocation.ACCURACY_BEST; Ti.Geolocation.distanceFilter = 5; $.index.open(); {code} index.xml: {code:xml} <Alloy> <Window class=""""""""container""""""""> <View layout=""""""""vertical"""""""" height=""""""""Titanium.UI.SIZE""""""""> <Label id=""""""""label"""""""">Hello, World</Label> <Label id=""""""""labelSpeed"""""""">Hello, World</Label> <Label id=""""""""numOfLocationCalls"""""""">Hello, World</Label> </View> </Window> </Alloy> {code} in tiapp.xml, I have these permissions: {code:xml} <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key> <string>Your location will only be used when the app is running.</string> {code} NOTE: I tried adding this to the axway support portal as I am a enterprise developer, but I can't seem to login at the moment. Will likely be adding this there once I get that sorted out.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24534,12,"""iOS: Failed to export Adhoc/Enterprise archive to ipa (No applicable devices found)""","""""""If I try to export the project as an iOS Adhoc / Enterprise ipa, it gives the following error:          If I do the same over Xcode (by using the .xcodeproj file and archiving it), it works flawlessly. One thing to clarify is that I already added the device / certificates to the account/team and the computer, so that's not the issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Failed to export Adhoc/Enterprise archive to ipa (No applicable devices found)
Description: """"If I try to export the project as an iOS Adhoc / Enterprise ipa, it gives the following error: If I do the same over Xcode (by using the .xcodeproj file and archiving it), it works flawlessly. One thing to clarify is that I already added the device / certificates to the account/team and the computer, so that's not the issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24533,12,"""Windows: WebView does not set html property""","""""""On the Windows platform the WebView ui component does not set the html property when loading web pages.  This makes interacting with web pages impossible.    Sample index.js (tested with SDK 6.0.2.GA):    $.index.open();  $.webview.setUrl(""""""""http://www.perfecthomecomputers.co.uk"""""""");  $.webview.addEventListener('load',function(e) {   setTimeout( function(){    Ti.API.info(""""""""> HTML: """"""""+$.webview.getHtml());    $.label.text = """"""""HTML: """""""" + $.webview.getHtml();   }, 10000);  });    The timeout was only put there just in case the html attribute became populated after the load event fired.    Sample project can be downloaded from:  [https://github.com/DesHuth/titanium-test]  """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: WebView does not set html property
Description: """"On the Windows platform the WebView ui component does not set the html property when loading web pages. This makes interacting with web pages impossible. Sample index.js (tested with SDK 6.0.2.GA): $.index.open(); $.webview.setUrl(""""""""http://www.perfecthomecomputers.co.uk""""""""); $.webview.addEventListener('load',function(e) { setTimeout( function(){ Ti.API.info(""""""""> HTML: """"""""+$.webview.getHtml()); $.label.text = """"""""HTML: """""""" + $.webview.getHtml(); }, 10000); }); The timeout was only put there just in case the html attribute became populated after the load event fired. Sample project can be downloaded from: [https://github.com/DesHuth/titanium-test] """"",title+description
TIMOB-24530,12,"""Hyperloop Android: Twilio Video SDK addAudioTrack is not a function""","""""""We are trying to implement Twilio Video SDK in <USER> Our goal is implement Twilio video features in <USER>apps.    Here we face few problems     1. For Room, CameraCapturer, LocalMedia, LocalAudioTrack, LocalVideoTrack class when I try to initialization   Android   {quote}private LocalMedia localMedia;{quote}  <USER> {quote}var localMedia = new LocalMedia () {quote}  its showing error.   [ERROR] :  HyperloopProxy: (main) [1168,1168] Unable to find matching constructor for class: com.twilio.video.LocalMedia, args: []    2. When I call addAudioTrack function from LocalMedia class, its showing me error Message: Uncaught TypeError: localMedia.addAudioTrack is not a function.   Android  {quote}  localMedia = LocalMedia.create(this);  // Share your microphone  localAudioTrack = localMedia.addAudioTrack(true);  {quote}    <USER>  {quote}   localMedia = new LocalMedia.create(activity);          // Share your microphone          localAudioTrack = localMedia.addAudioTrack(true);  {quote}  Test Code:  {code}  // https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-23955  // https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-23953  (function constructor(args) {      var Context = require(""""""""android.content.Context"""""""");      var Button = require(""""""""android.widget.Button"""""""");      var AudioManager = require('android.media.AudioManager');      var Intent = require('android.content.Intent');      var RoomState = require('com.twilio.video.RoomState');      var VideoRenderer = require('com.twilio.video.VideoRenderer');      var TwilioException = require('com.twilio.video.TwilioException');      var AudioTrack = require('com.twilio.video.AudioTrack');      var CameraCapturer = require('com.twilio.video.CameraCapturer');      var CameraSource = require('com.twilio.video.CameraCapturer.CameraSource');      var ConnectOptions = require('com.twilio.video.ConnectOptions');      var LocalAudioTrack = requir