TIMOB-24471,12,"""iOS: Building an iOS module will fail if the module doesn't contain a Classes directory""","""""""If you attempt to build an iOS module with `appc ti build`, it will fail unless there's a Classes directory that already exists. We should simply create the directory before trying to write a file to it if we need to.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Building an iOS module will fail if the module doesn't contain a Classes directory
