TIMOB-24435,12,"""Windows Module: Receive C++ callback from JS ""","""""""h5. Issue Description    Customer need a way to receive a function (callback) from Javascript in the C++ code by looking at the code in TitaniumKit.    Formerly, in Kroll, this would be done by doing something like:    (Assuming this is an android module)  HashMap args = args;  KrollFunction someFunction = (KrollFunction) args.get(""""""""someFunction"""""""");  [...]  someFunction.call(KrollObject, KrollDict);    So Would it be possible you provide an example on this if is possible?     """"""",Improvement,"Title: Windows Module: Receive C++ callback from JS
