TIMOB-24430,12,"""Views are not clickable""","""""""The Green View has click event and a child (Blue View).  The Blue View does not bubble click event to the Green View.  If it has the 'postlayout' event, it becomes clickable again    {code:title=widget.js|borderStyle=solid}  init();  function init() {      var viewBlue = Ti.UI.createView({ width: 200, height: 300, backgroundColor: 'blue' });        // // without this, viewBlue is not click-able      // viewBlue.addEventListener('postlayout', viewBlueReady);        $.containerGreen.add(viewBlue);  }  {code}    Environment:  - OSX 10.12.3  - Xcode 8.2.1  - Titanium SDK 6.0.1.GA  - iOS simulator 10.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Views are not clickable
Description: """"The Green View has click event and a child (Blue View). The Blue View does not bubble click event to the Green View. If it has the 'postlayout' event, it becomes clickable again {code:title=widget.js|borderStyle=solid} init(); function init() { var viewBlue = Ti.UI.createView({ width: 200, height: 300, backgroundColor: 'blue' }); // // without this, viewBlue is not click-able // viewBlue.addEventListener('postlayout', viewBlueReady); $.containerGreen.add(viewBlue); } {code} Environment: - OSX 10.12.3 - Xcode 8.2.1 - Titanium SDK 6.0.1.GA - iOS simulator 10.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-24425,12,"""Ti.Map: Add touchEnabled to PolylineProxy to improve click-performance""","""""""When adding a Polyline with 1370 points to the map my app freezes and will show the """"""""not responding - wait or kill"""""""" message when you click on an empty map field (not on annotation).    Responsible is this part:  https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map/blob/master/android/src/ti/map/TiUIMapView.java#L834    That will check all lines/points which takes a long time. Since I don't want the line to be clickable at all it would be good to have a """"""""touchEnabled()"""""""" parameter for a Polyline to skip the check. Removing the polyline will result in an instant click response!    Device: Samsung Galaxy S 4mini  Ti.Map: Version 3.1.0      Demo:      """"""",Improvement,"Title: Ti.Map: Add touchEnabled to PolylineProxy to improve click-performance
Description: """"When adding a Polyline with 1370 points to the map my app freezes and will show the """"""""not responding - wait or kill"""""""" message when you click on an empty map field (not on annotation). Responsible is this part: https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map/blob/master/android/src/ti/map/TiUIMapView.java#L834 That will check all lines/points which takes a long time. Since I don't want the line to be clickable at all it would be good to have a """"""""touchEnabled()"""""""" parameter for a Polyline to skip the check. Removing the polyline will result in an instant click response! Device: Samsung Galaxy S 4mini Ti.Map: Version 3.1.0 Demo: """"",title+description
