TIMOB-24255,12,"""Android: Different behaviours on device back button when open EmailDialog by Gmail app""","""""""h6.Reproduce.  1. Run a simple app like following on different Android Device    2. Click the button, Then choose Gmail to open EmailDialog  3. Touch the device back button on the bottom.    h6.Problem  1. On Samsung S4 with Android 5.0.1, the device back button will close Gmail app, and go back to our original app. This is what customer expected.  2. But On Samsung S5 snd S6 with Android Lollipop and Marshmallow, the device back button will close all app include our original app.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Different behaviours on device back button when open EmailDialog by Gmail app
Description: """"h6.Reproduce. 1. Run a simple app like following on different Android Device 2. Click the button, Then choose Gmail to open EmailDialog 3. Touch the device back button on the bottom. h6.Problem 1. On Samsung S4 with Android 5.0.1, the device back button will close Gmail app, and go back to our original app. This is what customer expected. 2. But On Samsung S5 snd S6 with Android Lollipop and Marshmallow, the device back button will close all app include our original app.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24251,12,"""Android: Local html video content is not displaying in titanium webview""","""""""*Issue description:*  I tried to use a local html video content in Titanium webview but it doesn't display the video content.     *Test code*:      *movie.html*      Attached is the movie.mp4 video file.  *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a project with the above code and run it on device  2. It doesn't play the video    *Expected:* The video content should play  *Actual:* Video doesn't play """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Local html video content is not displaying in titanium webview
Description: """"*Issue description:* I tried to use a local html video content in Titanium webview but it doesn't display the video content. *Test code*: *movie.html* Attached is the movie.mp4 video file. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a project with the above code and run it on device 2. It doesn't play the video *Expected:* The video content should play *Actual:* Video doesn't play """"",title+description
TIMOB-24248,12,"""Android: Ti.Calendar Recurring Events are not clearly exposed""","""""""The only current way to determine if an event is part of a larger recurrence/set of recurring events is to compare its ID to the ID of other events. The CalendarContract for Android has this data available for consumption in their SDK: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/CalendarContract.Instances.html.    I am under the impression that it is simply not implemented fully in the Titanium SDK, and it would be very helpful if it were.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Ti.Calendar Recurring Events are not clearly exposed
Description: """"The only current way to determine if an event is part of a larger recurrence/set of recurring events is to compare its ID to the ID of other events. The CalendarContract for Android has this data available for consumption in their SDK: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/CalendarContract.Instances.html. I am under the impression that it is simply not implemented fully in the Titanium SDK, and it would be very helpful if it were.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24247,12,"""Layout behave different than native""","""""""Titanium has a horizontal and vertical layout before iOS stack view, by calculating the position of each child view, it was very good at that time.    Since iOS has native support now, thanks UIStackView and very soon iOS 9 will be the minimum iOS supported by Xcode, it's the time to refactor that old code in favor of UIStackView and force autolayout in all apps.    At least it's the time now to refactor Android code with LinearLayout.    This part very important for RTL applications, with UIStackView and LinearLayout, apps flipping automatically with max 5% effort to optimize switching between both RTL and LTR.    Unfortunately till now we need more effort with Titanium.""""""",Bug,"Title: Layout behave different than native
Description: """"Titanium has a horizontal and vertical layout before iOS stack view, by calculating the position of each child view, it was very good at that time. Since iOS has native support now, thanks UIStackView and very soon iOS 9 will be the minimum iOS supported by Xcode, it's the time to refactor that old code in favor of UIStackView and force autolayout in all apps. At least it's the time now to refactor Android code with LinearLayout. This part very important for RTL applications, with UIStackView and LinearLayout, apps flipping automatically with max 5% effort to optimize switching between both RTL and LTR. Unfortunately till now we need more effort with Titanium.""""",title+description
