TIMOB-24184,12,"""Once HttpClient.validatesSecureCertificate is set to false it can't be set to true ""","""""""I tested this and apparently if you dynamically change the validatesSecureCertificate value, once it's set to false it can't be set to true again. Very weird behavior. It's at application level, not even on the same javascript object.    Sample code:        the response is the following:    {code:borderStyle=solid}  [INFO] :   #1 onerror {  [ERROR] :  = """"""""Il certificato di questo server non \U00e8 valido. \U00c8 possibile che tu stia effettuando la connessione a un server che dichiara di essere \U201c192.168.2.138\U201d, ma che potrebbe mettere a rischio le tue informazioni riservate."""""""";  [INFO] :   code = """"""""-1202"""""""";  [ERROR] :  source = """"""""[object TiNetworkHTTPClient]"""""""";  [ERROR] :  success = 0;  [ERROR] :  type = error;  [ERROR] :  }  [INFO] :   #2 onerror {  [INFO] :   code = 401;  [ERROR] :  = """"""""HTTP error"""""""";  [ERROR] :  source = """"""""[object TiNetworkHTTPClient]"""""""";  [ERROR] :  success = 0;  [ERROR] :  type = error;  [ERROR] :  }  [INFO] :   #3 onerror {  [ERROR] :  = """"""""HTTP error"""""""";  [INFO] :   code = 401;  [ERROR] :  source = """"""""[object TiNetworkHTTPClient]"""""""";  [ERROR] :  success = 0;  [ERROR] :  type = error;  [ERROR] :  }  {code}    as you can see the second http call fails with the wrong error (no ssl check)""""""",Bug,"Title: Once HttpClient.validatesSecureCertificate is set to false it can't be set to true
Description: """"I tested this and apparently if you dynamically change the validatesSecureCertificate value, once it's set to false it can't be set to true again. Very weird behavior. It's at application level, not even on the same javascript object. Sample code: the response is the following: {code:borderStyle=solid} [INFO] : #1 onerror { [ERROR] : = """"""""Il certificato di questo server non \U00e8 valido. \U00c8 possibile che tu stia effettuando la connessione a un server che dichiara di essere \U201c192.168.2.138\U201d, ma che potrebbe mettere a rischio le tue informazioni riservate.""""""""; [INFO] : code = """"""""-1202""""""""; [ERROR] : source = """"""""[object TiNetworkHTTPClient]""""""""; [ERROR] : success = 0; [ERROR] : type = error; [ERROR] : } [INFO] : #2 onerror { [INFO] : code = 401; [ERROR] : = """"""""HTTP error""""""""; [ERROR] : source = """"""""[object TiNetworkHTTPClient]""""""""; [ERROR] : success = 0; [ERROR] : type = error; [ERROR] : } [INFO] : #3 onerror { [ERROR] : = """"""""HTTP error""""""""; [INFO] : code = 401; [ERROR] : source = """"""""[object TiNetworkHTTPClient]""""""""; [ERROR] : success = 0; [ERROR] : type = error; [ERROR] : } {code} as you can see the second http call fails with the wrong error (no ssl check)""""",title+description
TIMOB-24180,12,"""Hyperloop: iOS - Swift files referencing each other break metabase generation""","""""""*Steps to reproduce the behavior*  1. Create a new Hyperloop enabled project  2. Add the following sample code under {{src}}:  {{MySwift.swift}}  {code:swift}  import Foundation    public class MySwift {   init() {    let test = Test()   }  }      import Foundation    public class Test {      public func sayHello() {          print(""""""""Hello"""""""")      }  }    module.exports = {   type: 'app',   group: 'titanium',   hyperloop: {    ios: {     thirdparty: {      'MyFramework': {       source: ['src'],       header: 'src',       resource: 'src'      }     }    }   }  };    [INFO]  Generating metabase for swift MyFramework /Users/<USER>Development/appc/hyperloop-examples/src/MySwift.swift  [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Development/appc/hyperloop-examples/src/MySwift.swift:5:14: error: use of unresolved identifier 'Test'  {code}    *Expected behavior*  Metabase generation succeeds and one can reference types from other Swift source files.""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: iOS - Swift files referencing each other break metabase generation
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce the behavior* 1. Create a new Hyperloop enabled project 2. Add the following sample code under {{src}}: {{MySwift.swift}} {code:swift} import Foundation public class MySwift { init() { let test = Test() } } import Foundation public class Test { public func sayHello() { print(""""""""Hello"""""""") } } module.exports = { type: 'app', group: 'titanium', hyperloop: { ios: { thirdparty: { 'MyFramework': { source: ['src'], header: 'src', resource: 'src' } } } } }; [INFO] Generating metabase for swift MyFramework /Users/<USER>Development/appc/hyperloop-examples/src/MySwift.swift [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Development/appc/hyperloop-examples/src/MySwift.swift:5:14: error: use of unresolved identifier 'Test' {code} *Expected behavior* Metabase generation succeeds and one can reference types from other Swift source files.""""",title+description
