TIMOB-24137,12,"""iOS 10 Camera Overlay is not fullscreen ""","""""""h5. Issue description  Prior to iOS 10 when Ti.Media.showCamera was called with showControls set to false the camera would show as full screen. As of iOS 10 there is a large black bar at the bottom     If you run the app in iOS 8 or 9 you will see the camera goes full screen when the controls are hidden. On iOS 10 there will be a black bar at the bottom of the screen.    h5. Steps to Reproduce  # Download the app testcase  # Run   # Click on the custom overlay camera button  # The camera is not fullscreen""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 10 Camera Overlay is not fullscreen
Description: """"h5. Issue description Prior to iOS 10 when Ti.Media.showCamera was called with showControls set to false the camera would show as full screen. As of iOS 10 there is a large black bar at the bottom If you run the app in iOS 8 or 9 you will see the camera goes full screen when the controls are hidden. On iOS 10 there will be a black bar at the bottom of the screen. h5. Steps to Reproduce # Download the app testcase # Run # Click on the custom overlay camera button # The camera is not fullscreen""""",title+description
TIMOB-24133,12,"""Windows phone bug - access denied to device camera""","""""""Hello,    I am facing an issue with the windows phone camera: I am not able to open it using the Titanium.Media.showCamera method. It returns a zero error code (access denied).    I've put all the necessary permissions in the app.xml (correct me if I am wrong):        <windows>          <manifest>              <Package                  xmlns=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/manifest/foundation/windows10""""""""                  xmlns:mp=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/2014/phone/manifest""""""""                  xmlns:rescap=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/manifest/foundation/windows10/restrictedcapabilities"""""""" xmlns:uap=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/manifest/uap/windows10"""""""">                  <Capabilities>                      <DeviceCapability Name=""""""""webcam""""""""/>                      <uap:Capability Name=""""""""picturesLibrary""""""""/>                  </Capabilities>              </Package>          </manifest>      </windows>    I've been stuck on this issue for several days, any help would be greatly appreciated.    Thanks    """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows phone bug - access denied to device camera
Description: """"Hello, I am facing an issue with the windows phone camera: I am not able to open it using the Titanium.Media.showCamera method. It returns a zero error code (access denied). I've put all the necessary permissions in the app.xml (correct me if I am wrong): <windows> <manifest> <Package xmlns=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/manifest/foundation/windows10"""""""" xmlns:mp=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/2014/phone/manifest"""""""" xmlns:rescap=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/manifest/foundation/windows10/restrictedcapabilities"""""""" xmlns:uap=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/appx/manifest/uap/windows10""""""""> <Capabilities> <DeviceCapability Name=""""""""webcam""""""""/> <uap:Capability Name=""""""""picturesLibrary""""""""/> </Capabilities> </Package> </manifest> </windows> I've been stuck on this issue for several days, any help would be greatly appreciated. Thanks """"",title+description
