TIMOB-24066,12,"""iOS: Uploading video from the gallery is not working for iPhone 7 simulator.""","""""""h6. description  Upload a video from the gallery in iPhone7 Simulator is not working but it works as expected with iPhone 7 device .    h6. Testing Environment  Ti SDK version 5.5.1.GA  CLI 5.5.1  Simulator Version iPhone7 v10    h6. Steps to reproduce    1. Just run this following code and try to select any video from the gallery, it get stuck on compressing page.    2. Test Code  {code: title=app.js}    var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor : 'white',   layout : """"""""vertical""""""""  });    // Create a Button.  var gallery = Ti.UI.createButton({   title : 'gallery',   height : Ti.UI.SIZE,   width : Ti.UI.SIZE,   top : 20    });    // Add to the parent view.  win.add(gallery);    function openGallery() {     Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({    success : function(event) {     alert(event.media);    },    cancel : function() {     // called when user cancels taking a picture    },    error : function(error) {     // called when there's an error     var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({      title : 'Camera'     });     if (error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_CAMERA) {      a.setMessage('Please run this test on device');     } else {      a.setMessage('Unexpected error: ' + error.code);     }     a.show();    },    //saveToPhotoGallery : true,    // allowEditing and mediaTypes are iOS-only settings    //allowEditing : true,    mediaTypes : [Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO, Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO]   });  }    gallery.addEventListener('click', function() {   openGallery();  });    win.open();      {code}    Thanks  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Uploading video from the gallery is not working for iPhone 7 simulator.
Description: """"h6. description Upload a video from the gallery in iPhone7 Simulator is not working but it works as expected with iPhone 7 device . h6. Testing Environment Ti SDK version 5.5.1.GA CLI 5.5.1 Simulator Version iPhone7 v10 h6. Steps to reproduce 1. Just run this following code and try to select any video from the gallery, it get stuck on compressing page. 2. Test Code {code: title=app.js} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : 'white', layout : """"""""vertical"""""""" }); // Create a Button. var gallery = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'gallery', height : Ti.UI.SIZE, width : Ti.UI.SIZE, top : 20 }); // Add to the parent view. win.add(gallery); function openGallery() { Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({ success : function(event) { alert(event.media); }, cancel : function() { // called when user cancels taking a picture }, error : function(error) { // called when there's an error var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({ title : 'Camera' }); if (error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_CAMERA) { a.setMessage('Please run this test on device'); } else { a.setMessage('Unexpected error: ' + error.code); } a.show(); }, //saveToPhotoGallery : true, // allowEditing and mediaTypes are iOS-only settings //allowEditing : true, mediaTypes : [Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO, Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO] }); } gallery.addEventListener('click', function() { openGallery(); }); win.open(); {code} Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-24054,12,"""Alloy: Can't name custom common js module folder as """"modules""""""","""""""h5.Issue Description   The folder modules inside app/lib/ can not be named modules, that is causing errors at running.     h5.Steps to Replicate   # Download the attached project   # Run   # Error will appear  # Change the folder name inside app/lib from modules to modulez  # Run  # Project Works     This started on SDK 5.5.0 and 5.5.1""""""",Bug,"Title: Alloy: Can't name custom common js module folder as """"modules""""
Description: """"h5.Issue Description The folder modules inside app/lib/ can not be named modules, that is causing errors at running. h5.Steps to Replicate # Download the attached project # Run # Error will appear # Change the folder name inside app/lib from modules to modulez # Run # Project Works This started on SDK 5.5.0 and 5.5.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-24049,12,"""latest hyperloop module not being downloaded with GA environment""","""""""*Description*  From the CLI, the latest hyperloop modules (1.2.8) are not downloaded in 5.5.1 GA environment, and with hyperloop 1.2.7 currently existing in the folder.    *Steps to reproduce*  From the CLI:  1. Check the hyperloop folders to make sure hyperloop version 1.2.7 is there.  2. Sign into preprod environment.  3. Create a new project choosing: Native App, Titanium SDK, “no” to Test Service, “Yes” to Enable Hyperloop.  4. After project creation, check the respective Hyperloop folders to see if 1.2.8 was downloaded.    *Result*  The latest hyperloop modules/plugins 1.2.8 was not downloaded.    *Expected Result*  The latest hyperloop modules/plugins 1.2.8 should have been downloaded.""""""",Bug,"Title: latest hyperloop module not being downloaded with GA environment
Description: """"*Description* From the CLI, the latest hyperloop modules (1.2.8) are not downloaded in 5.5.1 GA environment, and with hyperloop 1.2.7 currently existing in the folder. *Steps to reproduce* From the CLI: 1. Check the hyperloop folders to make sure hyperloop version 1.2.7 is there. 2. Sign into preprod environment. 3. Create a new project choosing: Native App, Titanium SDK, “no” to Test Service, “Yes” to Enable Hyperloop. 4. After project creation, check the respective Hyperloop folders to see if 1.2.8 was downloaded. *Result* The latest hyperloop modules/plugins 1.2.8 was not downloaded. *Expected Result* The latest hyperloop modules/plugins 1.2.8 should have been downloaded.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24046,12,"""Windows: border properties do not work on Ti.UI.Slider""","""""""h5.Description    When setting border properties on Ti.UI.Slider the properties do not appear to change anything        h5.Steps to reproduce    # Add the code above to an existing app.js  # Build for Windows Platform {{appc run -p windows}}    h5.Actual result    Setting border properties does not add a border    h5.Expected result    Setting border properties should add a border""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: border properties do not work on Ti.UI.Slider
