TIMOB-24044,12,"""Hyperloop iOS: Missing block for SCLAlertView""","""""""When using {{SCLAlertView}} the following error is thrown during the Hyperloop metabase creation: {{Couldn't find block with signature: BOOL (^)(void) for framework: SCLAlertView-Objective-C}}    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a simple app with hyperloop enabled  2. Create a {{Podfile}} at the project root and add {{pod 'SCLAlertView-Objective-C'}}.  3. appc run -p ios    h4. Expected Result  App will build and run successfully    h4. Actual Result  Build errors out with the above message.""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop iOS: Missing block for SCLAlertView
Description: """"When using {{SCLAlertView}} the following error is thrown during the Hyperloop metabase creation: {{Couldn't find block with signature: BOOL (^)(void) for framework: SCLAlertView-Objective-C}} h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a simple app with hyperloop enabled 2. Create a {{Podfile}} at the project root and add {{pod 'SCLAlertView-Objective-C'}}. 3. appc run -p ios h4. Expected Result App will build and run successfully h4. Actual Result Build errors out with the above message.""""",title+description
TIMOB-24038,12,"""Ti.UI elements: Usage of on() in favour of addEventListener()""","""""""I'd like to suggest the implementation of jQuery like event setters for Ti.UI.* elements, like:    `on()`  `once()`  `off()`    Versus the current functions:  `addEventListener()`  `removeEventListener()`    These functions would then apply on every *Ti.UI.xxx* element. This setup has currently already been implemented on controllers and it is imho cleaner and provides some better functionality (especially `off()` and `once()`).  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Ti.UI elements: Usage of on() in favour of addEventListener()
Description: """"I'd like to suggest the implementation of jQuery like event setters for Ti.UI.* elements, like: `on()` `once()` `off()` Versus the current functions: `addEventListener()` `removeEventListener()` These functions would then apply on every *Ti.UI.xxx* element. This setup has currently already been implemented on controllers and it is imho cleaner and provides some better functionality (especially `off()` and `once()`). """"",title+description
