TIMOB-23917,12,"""iOS: popToRootWindow( ) method returns undefined is not a function error""","""""""When I call popToRootWindow method on my NavigationWindow instance, I get an error telling me it's undefined function.    *Test Case:*      *Steps to reproduce the issue:*  - Run the sample code on simulator.  - Click on Open Window 2 button  - Next, click on Open window 3 button    Now click on Close all windows button and it'll return following error:      *Helpful link:*  http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iOS.NavigationWindow-method-popToRootWindow    Thanks.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: popToRootWindow( ) method returns undefined is not a function error
Description: """"When I call popToRootWindow method on my NavigationWindow instance, I get an error telling me it's undefined function. *Test Case:* *Steps to reproduce the issue:* - Run the sample code on simulator. - Click on Open Window 2 button - Next, click on Open window 3 button Now click on Close all windows button and it'll return following error: *Helpful link:* http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iOS.NavigationWindow-method-popToRootWindow Thanks.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23915,12,"""Hyperloop - iOS: Touch event properties and methods are undefined""","""""""Trying to get lastPoint touched in screen return       code to reproduce:     it assumes there is a win defined in xml.     """"""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop - iOS: Touch event properties and methods are undefined
Description: """"Trying to get lastPoint touched in screen return code to reproduce: it assumes there is a win defined in xml. """"",title+description
TIMOB-23910,12,"""iOS 10: 2D transforms not applied in Ti.Media.showCamera""","""""""When adding a transform to on Ti.Media.showCamera, the transform is not applied.      Also applying the trasform directly on the sdk is ignored.      It's probably related to this: [http://stackoverflow.duapp.com/questions/39124794/uiimagepickercontrollers-cameraviewtransform-is-ignoring-scaling-and-transla/39342257#39342257]""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 10: 2D transforms not applied in Ti.Media.showCamera
Description: """"When adding a transform to on Ti.Media.showCamera, the transform is not applied. Also applying the trasform directly on the sdk is ignored. It's probably related to this: [http://stackoverflow.duapp.com/questions/39124794/uiimagepickercontrollers-cameraviewtransform-is-ignoring-scaling-and-transla/39342257#39342257]""""",title+description
TIMOB-23905,12,"""iOS: Build fails when selecting iOS 9.0 and watchOS 2.0 using iOS SDK 9.3 or 9.2""","""""""I receive the below error when trying to build for iOS 9.0 and WatchOS 2.0 sims using the iOS SDK 9.3 or 9.2. One example command is: {{appc run --platform ios --log-level trace --ios-version 9.3 --sim-version 9.0 --watch-device-id E5CE2E3B-84AB-453B-B3FE-0BDD4BBBCBE4 --launch-watch-app --device-id 5C5D053D-D4AE-451F-8573-2E4174315471}}  The error received is:      *Steps to reproduce issue*  1. Create a new project  2. Add a WatchOS app to your project  3. Build the project for simulators {{iOS 9.0/WatchOS 2.0}} using the {{iOS SDK 9.3}} (you can set this in the run configurations, if in Studio)    *Expected Results*  The app builds and runs without issue    *Actual Results*  The build fails with the above error    *Notes*  I have encountered this and received the below error in Studio, but the above error is shown in the CLI with the same command:      These are the sims/xcode version selected:  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Build fails when selecting iOS 9.0 and watchOS 2.0 using iOS SDK 9.3 or 9.2
Description: """"I receive the below error when trying to build for iOS 9.0 and WatchOS 2.0 sims using the iOS SDK 9.3 or 9.2. One example command is: {{appc run --platform ios --log-level trace --ios-version 9.3 --sim-version 9.0 --watch-device-id E5CE2E3B-84AB-453B-B3FE-0BDD4BBBCBE4 --launch-watch-app --device-id 5C5D053D-D4AE-451F-8573-2E4174315471}} The error received is: *Steps to reproduce issue* 1. Create a new project 2. Add a WatchOS app to your project 3. Build the project for simulators {{iOS 9.0/WatchOS 2.0}} using the {{iOS SDK 9.3}} (you can set this in the run configurations, if in Studio) *Expected Results* The app builds and runs without issue *Actual Results* The build fails with the above error *Notes* I have encountered this and received the below error in Studio, but the above error is shown in the CLI with the same command: These are the sims/xcode version selected: """"",title+description
