TIMOB-23829,12,"""Fails to detect Android NDK on Windows""","""""""A regression was introduced in Titanium SDK 5.4.0 with detecting the Android NDK on Windows. When Android NDK 11 came out, it no longer included {{RELEASE.txt}} which we relied on to determine if the folder contained a valid NDK. Thus Titanium could not find the NDK 11 install.    TIMOB-20613 """"""""improved"""""""" Android NDK detection by searching for specific files and directories within the NDK directory to validate it was indeed an NDK. However, there's a typo by which it searches for {{ndk-gdb.cmd}} instead of {{ndk-gdb-py.cmd}} on Windows.""""""",Bug,"Title: Fails to detect Android NDK on Windows
Description: """"A regression was introduced in Titanium SDK 5.4.0 with detecting the Android NDK on Windows. When Android NDK 11 came out, it no longer included {{RELEASE.txt}} which we relied on to determine if the folder contained a valid NDK. Thus Titanium could not find the NDK 11 install. TIMOB-20613 """"""""improved"""""""" Android NDK detection by searching for specific files and directories within the NDK directory to validate it was indeed an NDK. However, there's a typo by which it searches for {{ndk-gdb.cmd}} instead of {{ndk-gdb-py.cmd}} on Windows.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23827,12,"""Module ID with underscores not allowed despite Android only platform""","""""""When trying to create a new module for Android only, the validation says you cannot have an underscore in the module id, despite this being valid for Android. It's iOS that doesn't permit it. The validation logic is bad.""""""",Bug,"Title: Module ID with underscores not allowed despite Android only platform
Description: """"When trying to create a new module for Android only, the validation says you cannot have an underscore in the module id, despite this being valid for Android. It's iOS that doesn't permit it. The validation logic is bad.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23825,12,"""Facebook logout is not working for iOS""","""""""Hello,  Facebook logout is not working for iOS on following Environment:  SDK: 5.4.0 GA  <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 5.4.0  facebook module Version: 5.2    *Test Case:*    *Step to reproduce:*  1)Starts the app, click facebook login   2)it redirects to safari, asks for your fb username and password   3)after logging in, logs in the app with fb data   4)Tried to log out, it will trigger Facebook.logout();   5)Repeat step 1 and 2. but this time it wont ask for your username and password, as you already logged into safari. In this case i can't switch to another fb account""""""",Bug,"Title: Facebook logout is not working for iOS
Description: """"Hello, Facebook logout is not working for iOS on following Environment: SDK: 5.4.0 GA <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 5.4.0 facebook module Version: 5.2 *Test Case:* *Step to reproduce:* 1)Starts the app, click facebook login 2)it redirects to safari, asks for your fb username and password 3)after logging in, logs in the app with fb data 4)Tried to log out, it will trigger Facebook.logout(); 5)Repeat step 1 and 2. but this time it wont ask for your username and password, as you already logged into safari. In this case i can't switch to another fb account""""",title+description
