TIMOB-23695,12,"""LiveView does not work with i18 folder on iOS.""","""""""LiveView does not work with i18 folder on iOS.  If I change anything to i18 folder and save, it does not update to the iOS simulator and Device. But it works on Android Emulator and Device.    *Steps To Reproduce:*  1. Create a single window default Classic project.  2. Change something to *i118/en/string.xml* file.  3. Then Save and check the iOS device or simulator.      *Testing Environment:*  Command-Line Interface, version 4.1.2,  Ti SDK: 4.1.0.GA,  iOS Simulator: 5,6(v8.4)                                                     iOS Device: iPod(v8.4),                         Studio Version: 4.1.1    Thanks.""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView does not work with i18 folder on iOS.
Description: """"LiveView does not work with i18 folder on iOS. If I change anything to i18 folder and save, it does not update to the iOS simulator and Device. But it works on Android Emulator and Device. *Steps To Reproduce:* 1. Create a single window default Classic project. 2. Change something to *i118/en/string.xml* file. 3. Then Save and check the iOS device or simulator. *Testing Environment:* Command-Line Interface, version 4.1.2, Ti SDK: 4.1.0.GA, iOS Simulator: 5,6(v8.4) iOS Device: iPod(v8.4), Studio Version: 4.1.1 Thanks.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23690,12,"""Windows: Htmlbased applications genarates type error in mobile web browser""","""""""just created a simple html project, which is automatically created by <USER> Then tried to run by browser but got an error like “*Application WindowPlatform is not a function at /index.html line 860> Function line(90)*"""""""". In phone it is coming properly.    Test steps:  1. Open studio  2. Create an HTML-based application  3. Run with Mobile Web Preview in Browser  """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Htmlbased applications genarates type error in mobile web browser
Description: """"just created a simple html project, which is automatically created by <USER> Then tried to run by browser but got an error like “*Application WindowPlatform is not a function at /index.html line 860> Function line(90)*"""""""". In phone it is coming properly. Test steps: 1. Open studio 2. Create an HTML-based application 3. Run with Mobile Web Preview in Browser """"",title+description
TIMOB-23688,12,"""iOS: Remove Comments Referencing Password""","""""""When running Fortify code analysis against the SDK the usage of """"""""password"""""""" in comments where detected in the following files.    Reachability.m  TiUIAlertDialogProxy.m    It is recommended these comments be removed as some tools would identity them as providing information disclosure.""""""",Story,"Title: iOS: Remove Comments Referencing Password
Description: """"When running Fortify code analysis against the SDK the usage of """"""""password"""""""" in comments where detected in the following files. Reachability.m TiUIAlertDialogProxy.m It is recommended these comments be removed as some tools would identity them as providing information disclosure.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23681,12,"""Hyperloop: NSInteger or NSUInteger are not working well""","""""""h6.Reproduce  1. If you have following method in custom SDK.  {code:title=TestLib.h}  #import <Foundation/Foundation.h>    @interface TestLib : NSObject     // Takes pointer to NSInteger as third argument to store result  +(void)addNumber: (NSInteger)num1 with:(NSInteger)num2 result:(NSInteger*)result;    @end    var result = 0;         TestLib.addNumberWithResult(1, 2, result); // throws [NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument error                   // TestLib expects a pointer to NSInteger as third argument      alert('Result: ' + result);    -[NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument   [ERROR] : Script Error {   [ERROR] : column = 26;   [ERROR] : description = """"""""-[NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument"""""""";   [ERROR] : line = 98;   [ERROR] : message = """"""""-[NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument"""""""";   [ERROR] : name = NSInvalidArgumentException;   {code}    h6.Note  Note sure is this expected. If yes, please change this to a feature request ticket since customer try to use a RSA SDK, but can't do it because of the above issue.""""""",Story,"Title: Hyperloop: NSInteger or NSUInteger are not working well
Description: """"h6.Reproduce 1. If you have following method in custom SDK. {code:title=TestLib.h} #import <Foundation/Foundation.h> @interface TestLib : NSObject // Takes pointer to NSInteger as third argument to store result +(void)addNumber: (NSInteger)num1 with:(NSInteger)num2 result:(NSInteger*)result; @end var result = 0; TestLib.addNumberWithResult(1, 2, result); // throws [NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument error // TestLib expects a pointer to NSInteger as third argument alert('Result: ' + result); -[NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument [ERROR] : Script Error { [ERROR] : column = 26; [ERROR] : description = """"""""-[NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument""""""""; [ERROR] : line = 98; [ERROR] : message = """"""""-[NSInvocation setArgument:atIndex:]: NULL address argument""""""""; [ERROR] : name = NSInvalidArgumentException; {code} h6.Note Note sure is this expected. If yes, please change this to a feature request ticket since customer try to use a RSA SDK, but can't do it because of the above issue.""""",title+description
