TIMOB-23676,12,"""Security alert : Google Play Warning: WebViewClient.onReceivedSslError handler""","""""""I have received this alert after publishing my app on google pay    Security alert  Your application has an unsafe implementation of the WebViewClient.onReceivedSslError handler. Specifically, the implementation ignores all SSL certificate validation errors, making your app vulnerable to man-in-the-middle attacks. An attacker could change the affected WebView's content, read transmitted data (such as login credentials), and execute code inside the app using JavaScript.  To properly handle SSL certificate validation, change your code to invoke SslErrorHandler.proceed() whenever the certificate presented by the server meets your expectations, and invoke SslErrorHandler.cancel() otherwise. An email alert containing the affected app(s) and class(es) has been sent to your developer account address.  Please address this vulnerability as soon as possible and increment the version number of the upgraded APK. For more information about the SSL error handler, please see our documentation in the Developer Help Center. For other technical questions, you can post to https://www.stackoverflow.com/questions and use the tags “android-security” and “SslErrorHandler.” If you are using a 3rd party library that’s responsible for this, please notify the 3rd party and work with them to address the issue.  To confirm that you've upgraded correctly, upload the updated version to the Developer Console and check back after five hours. If the app hasn't been correctly upgraded, we will display a warning.  Please note, while these specific issues may not affect every app that uses WebView SSL, it's best to stay up to date on all security patches. Apps with vulnerabilities that expose users to risk of compromise may be considered dangerous products in violation of the Content Policy and section 4.4 of the Developer Distribution Agreement.  Please ensure all apps published are compliant with the Developer Distribution Agreement and Content Policy. If you have questions or concerns, please contact our support team through the Google Play Developer Help Center.      im using SDK 5.2.2          in my controller      in my html file      """"""",Bug,"Title: Security alert : Google Play Warning: WebViewClient.onReceivedSslError handler
Description: """"I have received this alert after publishing my app on google pay Security alert Your application has an unsafe implementation of the WebViewClient.onReceivedSslError handler. Specifically, the implementation ignores all SSL certificate validation errors, making your app vulnerable to man-in-the-middle attacks. An attacker could change the affected WebView's content, read transmitted data (such as login credentials), and execute code inside the app using JavaScript. To properly handle SSL certificate validation, change your code to invoke SslErrorHandler.proceed() whenever the certificate presented by the server meets your expectations, and invoke SslErrorHandler.cancel() otherwise. An email alert containing the affected app(s) and class(es) has been sent to your developer account address. Please address this vulnerability as soon as possible and increment the version number of the upgraded APK. For more information about the SSL error handler, please see our documentation in the Developer Help Center. For other technical questions, you can post to https://www.stackoverflow.com/questions and use the tags “android-security” and “SslErrorHandler.” If you are using a 3rd party library that’s responsible for this, please notify the 3rd party and work with them to address the issue. To confirm that you've upgraded correctly, upload the updated version to the Developer Console and check back after five hours. If the app hasn't been correctly upgraded, we will display a warning. Please note, while these specific issues may not affect every app that uses WebView SSL, it's best to stay up to date on all security patches. Apps with vulnerabilities that expose users to risk of compromise may be considered dangerous products in violation of the Content Policy and section 4.4 of the Developer Distribution Agreement. Please ensure all apps published are compliant with the Developer Distribution Agreement and Content Policy. If you have questions or concerns, please contact our support team through the Google Play Developer Help Center. im using SDK 5.2.2 in my controller in my html file """"",title+description
TIMOB-23673,12,"""iOS: Unable to set LaunchScreen.storyboard on classic applications""","""""""h4. Description  I am unable to set LaunchScreen.storyboard on classic applications, Alloy applications work as expected.  h4. Steps to reproduce:  # {{appc new --classic}}  # Create a simple LaunchScreen.Storyboard in xcode  # Add the LaunchScreen.Storyboard to {{Resources/ios/LaunchScreen.storyboard}} [Docs|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/iOS_Launch_Files-section-46245490_iOSLaunchFiles-OptionB:UseacustomStoryboard]    h4. Actual  The LaunchScreen.storyboard is not added to the build folder    h4. Expected  The LaunchScreen.storyboard should be displayed as it does in alloy""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Unable to set LaunchScreen.storyboard on classic applications
Description: """"h4. Description I am unable to set LaunchScreen.storyboard on classic applications, Alloy applications work as expected. h4. Steps to reproduce: # {{appc new --classic}} # Create a simple LaunchScreen.Storyboard in xcode # Add the LaunchScreen.Storyboard to {{Resources/ios/LaunchScreen.storyboard}} [Docs|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/iOS_Launch_Files-section-46245490_iOSLaunchFiles-OptionB:UseacustomStoryboard] h4. Actual The LaunchScreen.storyboard is not added to the build folder h4. Expected The LaunchScreen.storyboard should be displayed as it does in alloy""""",title+description
TIMOB-23659,12,"""NavigationWindow: App stop working after swipe to right on first window of navigation window.""","""""""h6.Reproduce Step:  1. Add the following example Navigation Window code into app.js.  http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iOS.NavigationWindow  2. Run the app.  3. Once app open, DO NOT click the button.  4. First of all, swipe to the right from the edge of the left screen (sometimes maybe do it twice).  5. Then click the button.    h6.Problem.  You will notice the screen is frozen, and app stop working.    h6.Note:  1. if you put the app in background, and re-open it, it will back to work.  2. I tested app on different SDK versions, It happens on SDK 5.3.1 and 5.2.2. And no such problem on SDK 5.1.1""""""",Bug,"Title: NavigationWindow: App stop working after swipe to right on first window of navigation window.
Description: """"h6.Reproduce Step: 1. Add the following example Navigation Window code into app.js. http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iOS.NavigationWindow 2. Run the app. 3. Once app open, DO NOT click the button. 4. First of all, swipe to the right from the edge of the left screen (sometimes maybe do it twice). 5. Then click the button. h6.Problem. You will notice the screen is frozen, and app stop working. h6.Note: 1. if you put the app in background, and re-open it, it will back to work. 2. I tested app on different SDK versions, It happens on SDK 5.3.1 and 5.2.2. And no such problem on SDK 5.1.1""""",title+description
