TIMOB-23647,12,"""Advice on compile time about i18n errors""","""""""Sometimes we find people asking for problems using i18n strings identifiers.    It is easy for anyone to use names as *home.4* or *my-home* that are not allowed or generate errors (sometimes even no errors are generated, simply the translation don't work).    Would be very good that compiler can check for the most usual cases:    # Start a string identifier by a number: *100money*  # Use not allowed chars: *my.money* (this generates a WARN       # Use hyphen instead underscore: *my-money*    Cannot remember now if there are more cases.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Advice on compile time about i18n errors
Description: """"Sometimes we find people asking for problems using i18n strings identifiers. It is easy for anyone to use names as *home.4* or *my-home* that are not allowed or generate errors (sometimes even no errors are generated, simply the translation don't work). Would be very good that compiler can check for the most usual cases: # Start a string identifier by a number: *100money* # Use not allowed chars: *my.money* (this generates a WARN # Use hyphen instead underscore: *my-money* Cannot remember now if there are more cases.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23645,12,"""Android notification: allow to set color of background""","""""""Currently we can't set the color of the circle notification on Android. T  here is no method setColor on ti.cloudpush or style variable that we can override.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android notification: allow to set color of background
Description: """"Currently we can't set the color of the circle notification on Android. T here is no method setColor on ti.cloudpush or style variable that we can override.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23644,12,"""Ability to use Ti.AccountKit (iOS & Android) with ArrowDB""","""""""Ti.AccountKit for iOS: https://github.com/hansemannn/ti.accountkit  Ti.AccountKit for Android: https://github.com/AppWerft/Ti.AccountKit    Previously we used to use SocialIntegrations with ArrowDB, however, if we would like to use the no-password solution for our users, is there a way to associate a confirmed account via Ti.AccountKit (either email or phone number) with an account on ArrowDB?    Anything special to integrate with ArrowDB with the returned result from Ti.AccountKit        """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ability to use Ti.AccountKit (iOS & Android) with ArrowDB
Description: """"Ti.AccountKit for iOS: https://github.com/hansemannn/ti.accountkit Ti.AccountKit for Android: https://github.com/AppWerft/Ti.AccountKit Previously we used to use SocialIntegrations with ArrowDB, however, if we would like to use the no-password solution for our users, is there a way to associate a confirmed account via Ti.AccountKit (either email or phone number) with an account on ArrowDB? Anything special to integrate with ArrowDB with the returned result from Ti.AccountKit """"",title+description
TIMOB-23642,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.View never fires postlayout event""","""""""Ti.UI.View should fire a postlayout event just like most of it's subclasses do. It never does, so any UI tests we have relying on post layout listeners time out on Android.    http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-event-postlayout""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.View never fires postlayout event
Description: """"Ti.UI.View should fire a postlayout event just like most of it's subclasses do. It never does, so any UI tests we have relying on post layout listeners time out on Android. http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-event-postlayout""""",title+description
TIMOB-23640,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.Window never fires postlayout event""","""""""Ti.UI.Window is a subclass of Ti.UI.View and should therefore fire a postlayout event just like all the other subclasses do. It never does, so any UI tests we have relying on post layout listeners time out on Android.    http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-event-postlayout""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.Window never fires postlayout event
Description: """"Ti.UI.Window is a subclass of Ti.UI.View and should therefore fire a postlayout event just like all the other subclasses do. It never does, so any UI tests we have relying on post layout listeners time out on Android. http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-event-postlayout""""",title+description
