TIMOB-23618,12,"""Windows: Alloy.createController() takes much time to execute in windows environment. ""","""""""Alloy.createController() takes 200 ms to execute on windows and 11 ms on Android platform.  Similarly the line """"""""windows.open"""""""" takes 11ms on Android and 78ms on windows platform.  This reduces the response time of the application on windows platform.     We've used following code to measure the time taken by particular line to execute:      *Steps to test:*  1. Run the sample app in windows platform and observe the output of ti.API.info  2. Again run the app on android platform and compare both the output.  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Alloy.createController() takes much time to execute in windows environment.
Description: """"Alloy.createController() takes 200 ms to execute on windows and 11 ms on Android platform. Similarly the line """"""""windows.open"""""""" takes 11ms on Android and 78ms on windows platform. This reduces the response time of the application on windows platform. We've used following code to measure the time taken by particular line to execute: *Steps to test:* 1. Run the sample app in windows platform and observe the output of ti.API.info 2. Again run the app on android platform and compare both the output. """"",title+description
TIMOB-23617,12,"""One specific device get incompatible problem""","""""""Customer get the following problem, One specific device (belong to a their client) get incompatible problem when try to download app from google store. (attached screen)    But I can't find any reason why, they did no use any <user-feature> tage.     Please help to address this, or and idea will be help. (attached tiapp.xml file and Androidmanifest.XML file in case)    Device Info  Model: Vodacom Smart Kicka  Location:  South Africa  Android version: Android 4.4 Kitkat""""""",Story,"Title: One specific device get incompatible problem
