TIMOB-23413,12,"""Picker Width Sizing Bug on iOS""","""""""iOS Picker accepts width styling in units, but not in percentages. When using a percentage for the Picker width, it defaults to smallest possible size. Both units and percentages work in Android. To recreate:    *WORKS:*    {{<Picker selectionIndication=""""""""true"""""""" width=""""""""200"""""""">   <PickerColumn width=""""""""200"""""""">    <PickerRow title=""""""""Unit of Measurement"""""""" />    <PickerRow title=""""""""Imperial"""""""" />    <PickerRow title=""""""""Metric"""""""" />   </PickerColumn>  </Picker>}}    *DOESN'T WORK:*    {{<Picker selectionIndication=""""""""true"""""""" width=""""""""100%"""""""">   <PickerColumn width=""""""""100%"""""""">    <PickerRow title=""""""""Activity Level"""""""" />    <PickerRow title=""""""""Sedentary"""""""" />    <PickerRow title=""""""""Active"""""""" />   </PickerColumn>  </Picker>}}    Issue makes it a nightmare to code standardized forms for multiple devices. """"""",Bug,"Title: Picker Width Sizing Bug on iOS
Description: """"iOS Picker accepts width styling in units, but not in percentages. When using a percentage for the Picker width, it defaults to smallest possible size. Both units and percentages work in Android. To recreate: *WORKS:* {{<Picker selectionIndication=""""""""true"""""""" width=""""""""200""""""""> <PickerColumn width=""""""""200""""""""> <PickerRow title=""""""""Unit of Measurement"""""""" /> <PickerRow title=""""""""Imperial"""""""" /> <PickerRow title=""""""""Metric"""""""" /> </PickerColumn> </Picker>}} *DOESN'T WORK:* {{<Picker selectionIndication=""""""""true"""""""" width=""""""""100%""""""""> <PickerColumn width=""""""""100%""""""""> <PickerRow title=""""""""Activity Level"""""""" /> <PickerRow title=""""""""Sedentary"""""""" /> <PickerRow title=""""""""Active"""""""" /> </PickerColumn> </Picker>}} Issue makes it a nightmare to code standardized forms for multiple devices. """"",title+description
