Description: """"Good morning, I have a bug with customView on annotation map. When i zoom the map or swipe to left or at right of map, some of the annotation disappear. Is there a solution to fix this bug ? Reagards A.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23287,12,"""Windows: drag end event doesn't work for ScrollableView""","""""""Per TIMOB-19958    {quote}  {{dragend}} does not appear to be working.   {{dragstart}},{{scroll}} and {{scrollend}} do work as expected.    Tried following native event handlers (for Windows::UI::Xaml::Controls::ScrollViewer but non of them are working.        ManipulationCompleted      PointerReleased      PointerCanceled      PointerCaptureLost      PointerExited    So I would say we can't make this work because of plataform component spec.  {quote}    *app.js*      """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: drag end event doesn't work for ScrollableView
Description: """"Per TIMOB-19958 {quote} {{dragend}} does not appear to be working. {{dragstart}},{{scroll}} and {{scrollend}} do work as expected. Tried following native event handlers (for Windows::UI::Xaml::Controls::ScrollViewer but non of them are working. ManipulationCompleted PointerReleased PointerCanceled PointerCaptureLost PointerExited So I would say we can't make this work because of plataform component spec. {quote} *app.js* """"",title+description
TIMOB-23286,12,"""Windows: wptools crash?""","""""""I am not sure but with my latest 20160426 nightly build I get this error all the time :    [ERROR] :  The remote procedure call failed.  [ERROR] :  Error: The remote procedure call failed.      at ChildProcess.<anonymous> (C:\Users\jorgenbuder\Library\Application Support\Titanium\mobilesdk\win32\5.4.0.v20160426000033\node_modules\windowslib\lib\wptool.js:703:10)      at ChildProcess.emit (events.js:110:17)      at maybeClose (child_process.js:1015:16)      at Process.ChildProcess._handle.onexit (child_process.js:1087:5)    And I am thinking does this have anything to do with not getting logs at all on device ?    this is what I can recall not happening on Emulator, I will check..""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: wptools crash?
Description: """"I am not sure but with my latest 20160426 nightly build I get this error all the time : [ERROR] : The remote procedure call failed. [ERROR] : Error: The remote procedure call failed. at ChildProcess.<anonymous> (C:\Users\jorgenbuder\Library\Application Support\Titanium\mobilesdk\win32\5.4.0.v20160426000033\node_modules\windowslib\lib\wptool.js:703:10) at ChildProcess.emit (events.js:110:17) at maybeClose (child_process.js:1015:16) at Process.ChildProcess._handle.onexit (child_process.js:1087:5) And I am thinking does this have anything to do with not getting logs at all on device ? this is what I can recall not happening on Emulator, I will check..""""",title+description
TIMOB-23282,12,"""HttpClient file upload, Android, int as key in payload causes java.lang.Integer cannot be cast to java.lang.String""","""""""Having some issues with Android file upload where the key in my payload is an integer.    Sample code to reproduce, taken from Ti API HttpClient file upload docs:        1. Create a Requestbi.n url and replace it in the .open()  2. run this on an Android device.  You should receive the following error, specifying that the int  key cannot be cast to a string, and you will not be able to upload the file to requestbin.    [WARN] :   W/System.err: java.lang.ClassCastException: java.lang.Integer cannot be cast to java.lang.String  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.send(TiHTTPClient.java:1012)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at ti.modules.titanium.network.HTTPClientProxy.send(HTTPClientProxy.java:154)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function.nativeInvoke(Native Method)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function.callSync(V8Function.java:57)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function.call(V8Function.java:43)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function$1.run(V8Function.java:70)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at android.os.Handler.handleCallback(Handler.java:739)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:145)  [WARN] :   W/System.err:  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime$KrollRuntimeThread.run(KrollRuntime.java:118)    3.  as suggested by AppC support, change the .send() to        this will fire and upload to requestbin, however if you look at the response in requestbin, the event.media is a json string and not a binary object.    4.  change the .send() to        this will post the photo and be received as a binary object in requestbin.    I have witnessed this for Android only.  IOS seems to handle things ok, and I can post the object without having to do any additional processing.    I am posting to an API that has been used by our native Android developers, and they are sending the key as an integer.  I believe that the Titanium SDK is somehow tripping over the integer to string conversion    Please let me know if you need any more info.    Thanks  <USER>""""",Bug,"Title: HttpClient file upload, Android, int as key in payload causes java.lang.Integer cannot be cast to java.lang.String
Description: """"Having some issues with Android file upload where the key in my payload is an integer. Sample code to reproduce, taken from Ti API HttpClient file upload docs: 1. Create a Requestbi.n url and replace it in the .open() 2. run this on an Android device. You should receive the following error, specifying that the int key cannot be cast to a string, and you will not be able to upload the file to requestbin. [WARN] : W/System.err: java.lang.ClassCastException: java.lang.Integer cannot be cast to java.lang.String [WARN] : W/System.err: at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.send(TiHTTPClient.java:1012) [WARN] : W/System.err: at ti.modules.titanium.network.HTTPClientProxy.send(HTTPClientProxy.java:154) [WARN] : W/System.err: at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function.nativeInvoke(Native Method) [WARN] : W/System.err: at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function.callSync(V8Function.java:57) [WARN] : W/System.err: at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function.call(V8Function.java:43) [WARN] : W/System.err: at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Function$1.run(V8Function.java:70) [WARN] : W/System.err: at android.os.Handler.handleCallback(Handler.java:739) [WARN] : W/System.err: at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95) [WARN] : W/System.err: at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:145) [WARN] : W/System.err: at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime$KrollRuntimeThread.run(KrollRuntime.java:118) 3. as suggested by AppC support, change the .send() to this will fire and upload to requestbin, however if you look at the response in requestbin, the event.media is a json string and not a binary object. 4. change the .send() to this will post the photo and be received as a binary object in requestbin. I have witnessed this for Android only. IOS seems to handle things ok, and I can post the object without having to do any additional processing. I am posting to an API that has been used by our native Android developers, and they are sending the key as an integer. I believe that the Titanium SDK is somehow tripping over the integer to string conversion Please let me know if you need any more info. Thanks <USER>""",title+description
TIMOB-23270,12,"""Add returnKeyType : Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_NEXT support for webView textfield""","""""""In the webview there are textfields like and username and password. When keyboard is focused on username field I want to make """"""""returnKeyType : Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_NEXT"""""""".   But I am not able to do it in webview's textfield. Application is for Android and iOS. Right now """"""""GO"""""""" return key is getting displayed. Is it possible to add returnKeyType : Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_NEXT for webview textfield?    Link of intercom client for details:  https://app.intercom.io/a/apps/k9rdlb68/inbox/<EMAIL>/conversations/4606270602      """"""",New Feature,"Title: Add returnKeyType : Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_NEXT support for webView textfield
Description: """"In the webview there are textfields like and username and password. When keyboard is focused on username field I want to make """"""""returnKeyType : Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_NEXT"""""""". But I am not able to do it in webview's textfield. Application is for Android and iOS. Right now """"""""GO"""""""" return key is getting displayed. Is it possible to add returnKeyType : Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_NEXT for webview textfield? Link of intercom client for details: https://app.intercom.io/a/apps/k9rdlb68/inbox/<EMAIL>/conversations/4606270602 """"",title+description
