TIMOB-23258,12,"""Android: Ti.Media.AudioPlayer: Support """"audioSessionId""""""","""""""Hi,    for using of 'Ti.AudioVisualizerView' we need the audioSessionId from Mediaplayer instance.    It is a read only property and we need only this method 'getAudioSessionId()'.    Code strong!     """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Ti.Media.AudioPlayer: Support """"audioSessionId""""
Description: """"Hi, for using of 'Ti.AudioVisualizerView' we need the audioSessionId from Mediaplayer instance. It is a read only property and we need only this method 'getAudioSessionId()'. Code strong! """"",title+description
TIMOB-23257,12,"""Windows: Retreiving a string created natively is too """"large""""?""","""""""The example code in the background task at the docs section at the website suggest to use a simple code to count++ a counter witch is a string but code is suppose to count ++ and return to string. Problem is that when I try to get the string at the TI context side the getString gives this error:    Application Error: """"""""Runtime Error: Ti.App.Properties: Unable to restore large strings""""""""    It is a strange error considering this should probably be just a counter.. ??    Tryting to verify the background service by printing the string and see if it did indeed count up over time... but not able to do that now, is this a bug?""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Retreiving a string created natively is too """"large""""?
Description: """"The example code in the background task at the docs section at the website suggest to use a simple code to count++ a counter witch is a string but code is suppose to count ++ and return to string. Problem is that when I try to get the string at the TI context side the getString gives this error: Application Error: """"""""Runtime Error: Ti.App.Properties: Unable to restore large strings"""""""" It is a strange error considering this should probably be just a counter.. ?? Tryting to verify the background service by printing the string and see if it did indeed count up over time... but not able to do that now, is this a bug?""""",title+description
TIMOB-23255,12,"""Windows: Map annotations click do not work""","""""""Since Map is part of the support in Windows release as of today the Map annotations should work better, there are a number of problems where this is one:    *The annotation click view doe snot work and we cannot use the annotation for anything useful*    Additionally:    When we add, remove and add annotations to the map it crashes  The title of the annotation is always displayed (?) this can´t be right  The annotation image is always red..    For the Map to work at all we have to have basic support, these things are very basic support to be able to """"""""use"""""""" the map for anything else than map display...     Let us know where we stand here.. thanks    /Jörgen""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Map annotations click do not work
Description: """"Since Map is part of the support in Windows release as of today the Map annotations should work better, there are a number of problems where this is one: *The annotation click view doe snot work and we cannot use the annotation for anything useful* Additionally: When we add, remove and add annotations to the map it crashes The title of the annotation is always displayed (?) this can´t be right The annotation image is always red.. For the Map to work at all we have to have basic support, these things are very basic support to be able to """"""""use"""""""" the map for anything else than map display... Let us know where we stand here.. thanks /Jörgen""""",title+description
TIMOB-23250,12,"""Creating a mobile project will throw a """"Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, stat""""""","""""""*Details:* Creating a mobile project will throw {{Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, stat '/Users/<USER>.<USER>install/5.3.0-22/package/node_modules/alloy/platforms/windows/project'}}.    *This is a regression from 5.2.2.GA.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Create a mobile project with {{appc new}} and go through the prompts    *Actual:* You will not be able to create a mobile project:      *Expected:* Should be able to create a mobile project.""""""",Bug,"Title: Creating a mobile project will throw a """"Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, stat""""
Description: """"*Details:* Creating a mobile project will throw {{Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, stat '/Users/<USER>.<USER>install/5.3.0-22/package/node_modules/alloy/platforms/windows/project'}}. *This is a regression from 5.2.2.GA.* *Steps to reproduce:* # Create a mobile project with {{appc new}} and go through the prompts *Actual:* You will not be able to create a mobile project: *Expected:* Should be able to create a mobile project.""""",title+description
