TIMOB-23223,12,"""Windows: No splash screen when deploying alloy app to windows 10 mobile""","""""""h2. Description    It was found that when deploying an alloy mobile project to a windows 10 mobile device, the splash screen is not present, and instead presents a black screen with a white crossed box in the center. This does not occur for classic projects, or alloy/classic projects on 8.1 devices.    h2. Steps to Reproduce  1. Create an alloy mobile project.  2. In the Command Prompt, cd into project directory.  3. {{appc run -p windows -T wp-device --wp-sdk 10.0}}  4. Launch app once built.     h2. Actual Result    No splash screen on launch, white box instead      h2. Expected Result    Splash screen should be present on launch of app.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: No splash screen when deploying alloy app to windows 10 mobile
Description: """"h2. Description It was found that when deploying an alloy mobile project to a windows 10 mobile device, the splash screen is not present, and instead presents a black screen with a white crossed box in the center. This does not occur for classic projects, or alloy/classic projects on 8.1 devices. h2. Steps to Reproduce 1. Create an alloy mobile project. 2. In the Command Prompt, cd into project directory. 3. {{appc run -p windows -T wp-device --wp-sdk 10.0}} 4. Launch app once built. h2. Actual Result No splash screen on launch, white box instead h2. Expected Result Splash screen should be present on launch of app.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23212,12,"""Adding or removing font assets should force a full rebuild""","""""""We automatically add OTF and TTF files to the {{Info.plist}}:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/6fa557a07dc723c135704bc86810468900bd381b/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L3565-L3588    However, adding or removing a OTF or TTF file does not trigger a full rebuild. So you need to manually clean the build before you can use the font in the app.    The CLI should automatically do a full rebuild when an OTF or TTF file has been added/removed.""""""",Bug,"Title: Adding or removing font assets should force a full rebuild
Description: """"We automatically add OTF and TTF files to the {{Info.plist}}: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/6fa557a07dc723c135704bc86810468900bd381b/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L3565-L3588 However, adding or removing a OTF or TTF file does not trigger a full rebuild. So you need to manually clean the build before you can use the font in the app. The CLI should automatically do a full rebuild when an OTF or TTF file has been added/removed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23211,12,"""Hyperloop: NodeJS dependencies should not be packaged with plugin""","""""""All node_modules are packaged. We should spawn some {{npm install}} in the hook to load them on the first usage.""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: NodeJS dependencies should not be packaged with plugin
Description: """"All node_modules are packaged. We should spawn some {{npm install}} in the hook to load them on the first usage.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23208,12,"""CLI: Error when building for Windows Phone""","""""""Project appears to successfully build but doesn't launch in the emulator, I get the same error when trying to build for device. This issue was here in 5.1.2 and now still in 5.2.0. However I used to be able to build fine and now getting this error.    [INFO]  Copying results back to project build directory  [INFO]  Finished building the application in 1m 30s 928ms  [INFO]  Finished building the application in 1m 30s 938ms  [INFO]  Installing and launching the application  [INFO]  Project built successfully in 1m 31s 20ms    [WARN]  error while updating tiapp data with appc platform:  [WARN]  error while updating tiapp data with appc platform:  2016-02-24T11:33:32.675Z | ERROR  | An uncaught exception was thrown!  Callback was already called.  2016-02-24T11:33:32.679Z | ERROR  | Callback was already called.  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Error when building for Windows Phone
Description: """"Project appears to successfully build but doesn't launch in the emulator, I get the same error when trying to build for device. This issue was here in 5.1.2 and now still in 5.2.0. However I used to be able to build fine and now getting this error. [INFO] Copying results back to project build directory [INFO] Finished building the application in 1m 30s 928ms [INFO] Finished building the application in 1m 30s 938ms [INFO] Installing and launching the application [INFO] Project built successfully in 1m 31s 20ms [WARN] error while updating tiapp data with appc platform: [WARN] error while updating tiapp data with appc platform: 2016-02-24T11:33:32.675Z | ERROR | An uncaught exception was thrown! Callback was already called. 2016-02-24T11:33:32.679Z | ERROR | Callback was already called. """"",title+description
TIMOB-23207,12,"""Android: Can't get localized app_name from L""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    Create {{app/i18n/ru/app.xml}}        Build app and look at the {{build/android/res/values-ru/strings.xml}}  You can find localized value {{app_neme}} there.    In {{app.js}} add {{Ti.API.warn(L(""""""""app_name"""""""", """"""""I'm default value""""""""));}}    You can see: *I'm default value*  But must be: *Мое приложение*    But {{Ti.Locale.getString(""""""""app_name"""""""");}} works as expected.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Can't get localized app_name from L
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: Create {{app/i18n/ru/app.xml}} Build app and look at the {{build/android/res/values-ru/strings.xml}} You can find localized value {{app_neme}} there. In {{app.js}} add {{Ti.API.warn(L(""""""""app_name"""""""", """"""""I'm default value""""""""));}} You can see: *I'm default value* But must be: *Мое приложение* But {{Ti.Locale.getString(""""""""app_name"""""""");}} works as expected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-23197,12,"""iOS: Ability to create file inside  App's Documents or Downloads folder that can be sync/share""","""""""Hello Guys,    As per Apple documentation: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/FileSystemProgrammingGuide/FileSystemOverview/FileSystemOverview.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40010672-CH2-SW28 app's documents folder data can be shared/sync.    As per <USER>documentation: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Filesystem_Access_and_Storage Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory can only accessible by app itself. If a file is added in app's Documents folder using  {color:#205081}var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(timelogsData,'errors.log');f.write(data); {color}  It can't sync/share it is only accessible by app itself.    We need an ability to create file inside Downloads folder and/or ability to create file inside App's Documents folder that can be share/sync.    Thanks      """"""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Ability to create file inside App's Documents or Downloads folder that can be sync/share
Description: """"Hello Guys, As per Apple documentation: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/FileSystemProgrammingGuide/FileSystemOverview/FileSystemOverview.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40010672-CH2-SW28 app's documents folder data can be shared/sync. As per <USER>documentation: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Filesystem_Access_and_Storage Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory can only accessible by app itself. If a file is added in app's Documents folder using {color:#205081}var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(timelogsData,'errors.log');f.write(data); {color} It can't sync/share it is only accessible by app itself. We need an ability to create file inside Downloads folder and/or ability to create file inside App's Documents folder that can be share/sync. Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-23196,12,"""iOS: App crashes when using Expressions tab during debugging""","""""""h2. Problem    Debugging and setting expressions in the Expressions tab can cause the app to crash.  Without the expressions it does not crash, but if you hit a breakpoint and have something in the expressions tab the app will crash in the simulator.    h2. Test case    # Create a new Mobile App Project in Studio using the Default Alloy Project template (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.11.24.png and Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.12.44.png)  # Set a breakpoint in the index.js file for the click event (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.15.46.png)  # Notice the breakpoint works and suspends the app (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.16.23.png)  # Enter in the Expressions tab the $.label.text that would be shown in the alert (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.16.39.png)  # App will crash in simulator (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.16.39.png)    h2. Logs    {code:lang=none|title=console}  Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM SpringBoard[55508]: HW kbd: Failed to set (null) as keyboard focus  Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM com.apple.CoreSimulator.SimDevice.CBB496B7-CB63-48B1-B533-12BA264C1C52.launchd_sim[55491] (UIKitApplication:com.demandware.crashExampleProject[0xe7a3][61712]): Service exited due to signal: Abort trap: 6  Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM SpringBoard[55508]: Application 'UIKitApplication:com.demandware.crashExampleProject[0xe7a3]' crashed.  Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM assertiond[55512]: assertion failed: 14F1605 13C75: assertiond + 13207 [792516D1-991E-36EE-8454-16F8220758D6]: 0x1  Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM assertiond[55512]: notify_suspend_pid() failed with error 7  Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM assertiond[55512]: assertion failed: 14F1605 13C75: assertiond + 13207 [792516D1-991E-36EE-8454-16F8220758D6]: 0x1      h2. Discussions""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App crashes when using Expressions tab during debugging
Description: """"h2. Problem Debugging and setting expressions in the Expressions tab can cause the app to crash. Without the expressions it does not crash, but if you hit a breakpoint and have something in the expressions tab the app will crash in the simulator. h2. Test case # Create a new Mobile App Project in Studio using the Default Alloy Project template (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.11.24.png and Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.12.44.png) # Set a breakpoint in the index.js file for the click event (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.15.46.png) # Notice the breakpoint works and suspends the app (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.16.23.png) # Enter in the Expressions tab the $.label.text that would be shown in the alert (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.16.39.png) # App will crash in simulator (Screenshot 2016-04-12 08.16.39.png) h2. Logs {code:lang=none|title=console} Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM SpringBoard[55508]: HW kbd: Failed to set (null) as keyboard focus Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM com.apple.CoreSimulator.SimDevice.CBB496B7-CB63-48B1-B533-12BA264C1C52.launchd_sim[55491] (UIKitApplication:com.demandware.crashExampleProject[0xe7a3][61712]): Service exited due to signal: Abort trap: 6 Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM SpringBoard[55508]: Application 'UIKitApplication:com.demandware.crashExampleProject[0xe7a3]' crashed. Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM assertiond[55512]: assertion failed: 14F1605 13C75: assertiond + 13207 [792516D1-991E-36EE-8454-16F8220758D6]: 0x1 Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM assertiond[55512]: notify_suspend_pid() failed with error 7 Apr 12 08:16:29 DW1415USBUM assertiond[55512]: assertion failed: 14F1605 13C75: assertiond + 13207 [792516D1-991E-36EE-8454-16F8220758D6]: 0x1 h2. Discussions""""",title+description
TIMOB-23194,12,"""Android: Backup Service / BackupAgent similar to iOS iCloud parity""","""""""I would like to request research into Android parity with iOS's iCloud automatic backups.    Android 6 now has an automatic backup service, but my app is not being included by default. It would seem Ti apps on this version of Android could be configured via manifest.xml modifications, but would need some documentation to understand how this would work in the Ti SDK context, e.g. supplying file paths etc.    On earlier versions of Android that are compatible with Ti SDK my understanding is that a BackupAgent would need to be added to interface with Android's Backup API. However, it's not clear if this would work as a Ti module.    See this SO thread with <USER>for links to appropriate Android SDK docs: [http://stackoverflow.com/questions/36408739/anyone-implemented-android-backup-service-with-androidbackupagent]""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Backup Service / BackupAgent similar to iOS iCloud parity
Description: """"I would like to request research into Android parity with iOS's iCloud automatic backups. Android 6 now has an automatic backup service, but my app is not being included by default. It would seem Ti apps on this version of Android could be configured via manifest.xml modifications, but would need some documentation to understand how this would work in the Ti SDK context, e.g. supplying file paths etc. On earlier versions of Android that are compatible with Ti SDK my understanding is that a BackupAgent would need to be added to interface with Android's Backup API. However, it's not clear if this would work as a Ti module. See this SO thread with <USER>for links to appropriate Android SDK docs: [http://stackoverflow.com/questions/36408739/anyone-implemented-android-backup-service-with-androidbackupagent]""""",title+description
TIMOB-23189,12,"""iOS: Cannot change the width and height of Titanium.UI.Switch""","""""""*Details:* On iOS, you cannot change the height or width (dp, percents, or absolute values) of Titanium.UI.Switch.    *This is not reproducible on Android i.e. you can change the height and width.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Create a default Alloy app  # In {{index.xml}}, add the following code:    # In {{index.tss}}, add the following code:    # Install app to device    *Actual:* The switch control is not resized; see attachments.  *Expected:* The switch control should be resized.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot change the width and height of Titanium.UI.Switch
Description: """"*Details:* On iOS, you cannot change the height or width (dp, percents, or absolute values) of Titanium.UI.Switch. *This is not reproducible on Android i.e. you can change the height and width.* *Steps to reproduce:* # Create a default Alloy app # In {{index.xml}}, add the following code: # In {{index.tss}}, add the following code: # Install app to device *Actual:* The switch control is not resized; see attachments. *Expected:* The switch control should be resized.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23188,12,"""Package script for automated tests as stand-alone library""","""""""Both the Titanium Mobile and Alloy repositories have scripts to do automated run-time tests, but both in different ways and intertwined with their *.travis.yml*, jake and other scripts.    We need this for other repositories as well. One example is sample apps that we'd like to automatically test against the latest SDK versions so we need which ones need fixing.    We should create an NPM package that we can use in any repo, both locally and in CI. This package should also come with a CLI or bash script to set up the environment on Travis so that in the end we can do something like:    *package.json*    {code:js}    """"""""scripts"""""""": {      """"""""test"""""""": """"""""ti-test run --project ./test""""""""    }      and then run:        or via *.travis.yml*    {code:yml}  language: objective-c  osx_image: xcode7.3  jdk:    - oraclejdk7  install:    - sudo npm install -g ti-test    - sudo ti-test setup --sdk latest    # which would install Titanium CLI & (given) SDK, Android SDK etc.  script:    - npm test  {code}    Ideas [~<USER>, [~<USER>, [~<USER>?""""""",Story,"Title: Package script for automated tests as stand-alone library
Description: """"Both the Titanium Mobile and Alloy repositories have scripts to do automated run-time tests, but both in different ways and intertwined with their *.travis.yml*, jake and other scripts. We need this for other repositories as well. One example is sample apps that we'd like to automatically test against the latest SDK versions so we need which ones need fixing. We should create an NPM package that we can use in any repo, both locally and in CI. This package should also come with a CLI or bash script to set up the environment on Travis so that in the end we can do something like: *package.json* {code:js} """"""""scripts"""""""": { """"""""test"""""""": """"""""ti-test run --project ./test"""""""" } and then run: or via *.travis.yml* {code:yml} language: objective-c osx_image: xcode7.3 jdk: - oraclejdk7 install: - sudo npm install -g ti-test - sudo ti-test setup --sdk latest # which would install Titanium CLI & (given) SDK, Android SDK etc. script: - npm test {code} Ideas [~<USER>, [~<USER>, [~<USER>?""""",title+description
TIMOB-23182,12,"""Facebook login is not working on iOS ""","""""""Facebook login is not working on latest SDK.  *Testing Environment:*  Titanium SDK: 5.2.2.GA  <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 5.2.2  Facebook module version: 5.0.1  Testing device: iPod 5G(9.2)    *Testing Code:*      *Testing Result:*  Facebook login not working and login dialog not appear for IOS.""""""",Bug,"Title: Facebook login is not working on iOS
Description: """"Facebook login is not working on latest SDK. *Testing Environment:* Titanium SDK: 5.2.2.GA <USER>Command-Line Interface, version 5.2.2 Facebook module version: 5.0.1 Testing device: iPod 5G(9.2) *Testing Code:* *Testing Result:* Facebook login not working and login dialog not appear for IOS.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23180,12,"""iOS: Replace deprecated controller inside TI.Media.VideoPlayer""","""""""[MPMoviePlayerController|https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/MediaPlayer/Reference/MPMoviePlayerController_Class/] has been deprecated since iOS 9.0 we should replace it with [AVPlayerViewController|https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/AVFoundation/Reference/AVPlayerViewController_Class/] if running an iOS 9.0 device or higher. """"""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Replace deprecated controller inside TI.Media.VideoPlayer
Description: """"[MPMoviePlayerController|https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/MediaPlayer/Reference/MPMoviePlayerController_Class/] has been deprecated since iOS 9.0 we should replace it with [AVPlayerViewController|https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/AVFoundation/Reference/AVPlayerViewController_Class/] if running an iOS 9.0 device or higher. """"",title+description
TIMOB-23178,12,"""Inconsistent path handling Android / iOS - Live View On / Off""","""""""Paths to *images* and *dbs* are always absolute on iOS, on Android behaviour depends on Liveview, when distributing the app paths are relative to script file.    Attached screenshot and a test app.    app.js      folder/script    """"""",Story,"Title: Inconsistent path handling Android / iOS - Live View On / Off
Description: """"Paths to *images* and *dbs* are always absolute on iOS, on Android behaviour depends on Liveview, when distributing the app paths are relative to script file. Attached screenshot and a test app. app.js folder/script """"",title+description
TIMOB-23173,12,"""Support defining supported SDK version range in tiapp.xml""","""""""I'd like to be able to set a supported Titanium SDK version range for an app in {{tiapp.xml}}:        When Titanium compiles it should check if the Titanium version used to compile is supported by the app and if not fail with a clear message:        The primary use case for this are our [release sample apps|https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/?query=appc-sample-ti] which require the (at the moment of release) latest SDK version to be used and might not always be updated for later SDK versions (DE-359).    Now I know that these sample apps have a {{<sdk-version>5.2.0.GA</sdk-version>}} set to the SDK they were made for, but if you don't have this SDK and you import the sample it will simply use the last SDK version you have and then the build will probably fail with all kinds of errors.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Support defining supported SDK version range in tiapp.xml
Description: """"I'd like to be able to set a supported Titanium SDK version range for an app in {{tiapp.xml}}: When Titanium compiles it should check if the Titanium version used to compile is supported by the app and if not fail with a clear message: The primary use case for this are our [release sample apps|https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/?query=appc-sample-ti] which require the (at the moment of release) latest SDK version to be used and might not always be updated for later SDK versions (DE-359). Now I know that these sample apps have a {{<sdk-version>5.2.0.GA</sdk-version>}} set to the SDK they were made for, but if you don't have this SDK and you import the sample it will simply use the last SDK version you have and then the build will probably fail with all kinds of errors.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23168,12,"""Android: Allow selecting multiple photos with Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery""","""""""It would be nice to have an option to allow the user selecting multiple photos out of his gallery with Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery.    Ther should be an {{allowMultiple}} option in here:  http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/PhotoGalleryOptionsType    The current behavior is the selection window closes as soon as the first photo was selected.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Allow selecting multiple photos with Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery
Description: """"It would be nice to have an option to allow the user selecting multiple photos out of his gallery with Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery. Ther should be an {{allowMultiple}} option in here: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/PhotoGalleryOptionsType The current behavior is the selection window closes as soon as the first photo was selected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23163,12,"""Android 6: webView is unable to open google map url and any pdf url""","""""""*Problem Description:*  When I use google maps url(https://maps.google.com) or any other pdf url(https://www.onguardonline.gov/articles/pdf-0004-mobile-apps.pdf) inside webView, the webView is unable to open those urls. It shows only a blank screen and there is no error in console. This is happening on Android 6.0.1(device: Nexus 7).  Other url inside webView works fine.     *Environment Info:*  <USER>CLI:  5.2.2  Node.js Version             = 0.12.7  Titanium SDKs              = 5.2.2.GA  <USER>Studio, build = 4.5.0.201602170821  Java Development Kit      = 1.7.0_80  android version: 6.0.1  Physical device: Nexus 7    *Steps to reproduced:*  1. Create a classic project with the test case provided.  2. Run the app    *Expected:* webView should load google map webpage  *Actual:* webView is unable to load google map webpage. The app shows only a blank screen with no error log.    *Test Case:*      *Intercom link:*  https://app.intercom.io/a/apps/k9rdlb68/inbox/<EMAIL>/conversations/4493448913  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android 6: webView is unable to open google map url and any pdf url
Description: """"*Problem Description:* When I use google maps url(https://maps.google.com) or any other pdf url(https://www.onguardonline.gov/articles/pdf-0004-mobile-apps.pdf) inside webView, the webView is unable to open those urls. It shows only a blank screen and there is no error in console. This is happening on Android 6.0.1(device: Nexus 7). Other url inside webView works fine. *Environment Info:* <USER>CLI: 5.2.2 Node.js Version = 0.12.7 Titanium SDKs = 5.2.2.GA <USER>Studio, build = 4.5.0.201602170821 Java Development Kit = 1.7.0_80 android version: 6.0.1 Physical device: Nexus 7 *Steps to reproduced:* 1. Create a classic project with the test case provided. 2. Run the app *Expected:* webView should load google map webpage *Actual:* webView is unable to load google map webpage. The app shows only a blank screen with no error log. *Test Case:* *Intercom link:* https://app.intercom.io/a/apps/k9rdlb68/inbox/<EMAIL>/conversations/4493448913 """"",title+description
TIMOB-23162,12,"""Windows: Cannot add data to Picker on SDK 5.4.0""","""""""When I try to add data to Picker, my application crash with Unknown exception.    I tried with SDK 5.2.0.GA and it's work. But on SDK 5.4.0.v20160402025807 it crash.     I tried this       ==> CRASH  and I tried to create the picker and after add columns or data like this and it crash too.     ==> CRASH  OR     ==> CRASH  OR      ==> CRASH    Please help.    The source code :    //index.xml    //index.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Cannot add data to Picker on SDK 5.4.0
