TIMOB-23147,12,"""Tests run on Travis should include apidoc validation script""","""""""We've had a couple of situations lately with broken docs because of errors in the YAML files.    We have an apidoc validation script:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/apidoc/validate.js    This should be added to the tests run by Travis:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/support/ti_mocha_script/test.js    This would make Travis fail on PRs with buggy YAML files and save us headaches.    /cc [~<USER>""""""",Story,"Title: Tests run on Travis should include apidoc validation script
Description: """"We've had a couple of situations lately with broken docs because of errors in the YAML files. We have an apidoc validation script: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/apidoc/validate.js This should be added to the tests run by Travis: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/support/ti_mocha_script/test.js This would make Travis fail on PRs with buggy YAML files and save us headaches. /cc [~<USER>""""",title+description
TIMOB-23142,12,"""Hyperloop: Allow Hyperloop usage without Titanium Mobile""","""""""This ticket should summarize, what's necessary to make Hyperloop available without the usage of Titanium Mobile. Currently, we are hooking Hyperloop into the Ti build-<USER> allowing it to act independently therefore needs:  - Own CLI  - Creation of the AppDelegate  - Handling of assets    Just like ALOY-1488, it's a huge task, but it's here for discussion.""""""",Story,"Title: Hyperloop: Allow Hyperloop usage without Titanium Mobile
Description: """"This ticket should summarize, what's necessary to make Hyperloop available without the usage of Titanium Mobile. Currently, we are hooking Hyperloop into the Ti build-<USER> allowing it to act independently therefore needs: - Own CLI - Creation of the AppDelegate - Handling of assets Just like ALOY-1488, it's a huge task, but it's here for discussion.""""",title+description
