TIMOB-23120,12,"""Windows: picker 'change' event not working from .xml""","""""""Affects 5.2.0    Okay, I provide sample code:    *index.js:*    {code:java}  $.picker.add(_.map(['1', '2', '3'], function(value){   return Ti.UI.createPickerRow({title: value});  }));    function onChangePicker() {   alert('picker changed');  }    $.win.open();  {code}    *index.xml:*      It's not working!""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: picker 'change' event not working from .xml
Description: """"Affects 5.2.0 Okay, I provide sample code: *index.js:* {code:java} $.picker.add(_.map(['1', '2', '3'], function(value){ return Ti.UI.createPickerRow({title: value}); })); function onChangePicker() { alert('picker changed'); } $.win.open(); {code} *index.xml:* It's not working!""""",title+description
TIMOB-23119,12,"""Change auto width behaviour to FILL for text entry components""","""""""Following up with TIMOB-20406, there are some other UI components that would benefit from changing their auto width behaviour to FILL to prevent them from being invisible otherwise.    While a developer will probably always set the text of a label, he would not for text entry components. If these auto width to SIZE this will make them invisible, which is confusing. And if he does it is unlikely that he would want the width to fit the content in these cases.    Text entry components:    * TextArea  * TextField  * SearchBar    Full list of behaviour for components:    http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Layouts,_Positioning,_and_the_View_Hierarchy-section-29004895_Layouts,Positioning,andtheViewHierarchy-AutoSizeBehaviors""""""",Improvement,"Title: Change auto width behaviour to FILL for text entry components
Description: """"Following up with TIMOB-20406, there are some other UI components that would benefit from changing their auto width behaviour to FILL to prevent them from being invisible otherwise. While a developer will probably always set the text of a label, he would not for text entry components. If these auto width to SIZE this will make them invisible, which is confusing. And if he does it is unlikely that he would want the width to fit the content in these cases. Text entry components: * TextArea * TextField * SearchBar Full list of behaviour for components: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Layouts,_Positioning,_and_the_View_Hierarchy-section-29004895_Layouts,Positioning,andtheViewHierarchy-AutoSizeBehaviors""""",title+description
TIMOB-23118,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.iOS.DynamicItemBehavior can possibly crash during iteration""","""""""A community member created a PR to fix a crash that can occur with the above mentioned API. The fix removes the fast-enumeration with a simple {{for}}-iteration.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.iOS.DynamicItemBehavior can possibly crash during iteration
Description: """"A community member created a PR to fix a crash that can occur with the above mentioned API. The fix removes the fast-enumeration with a simple {{for}}-iteration.""""",title+description
TIMOB-23116,12,"""iOS: Add sessionIdentifier to URLSession events""","""""""There is a community PR to add the {{sessionIdentifier}} to the URLSession: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6941    We need to do the following:  * Nil-validations for the case that the sessionIdentifier is nil  * The docs for the new property, as well as the docs for the uploadprogress event  * The missing dictionary in URLSessionDidFinishEventsForBackgroundURLSession.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Add sessionIdentifier to URLSession events
Description: """"There is a community PR to add the {{sessionIdentifier}} to the URLSession: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6941 We need to do the following: * Nil-validations for the case that the sessionIdentifier is nil * The docs for the new property, as well as the docs for the uploadprogress event * The missing dictionary in URLSessionDidFinishEventsForBackgroundURLSession.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20626,12,"""SplashScreen's are packaged even if LaunchScreen storyboard is used""","""""""Originally reported on Ti.Slack. The user reports, that the (legacy) splash screen are packaged, even if the storyboard is used.     Maybe it's just visible on the Simulator because the CLI fallbacks to the SplashScreens and it doesn't package it for production, but we should ensure it's not packaged at all.""""""",Bug,"Title: SplashScreen's are packaged even if LaunchScreen storyboard is used
Description: """"Originally reported on Ti.Slack. The user reports, that the (legacy) splash screen are packaged, even if the storyboard is used. Maybe it's just visible on the Simulator because the CLI fallbacks to the SplashScreens and it doesn't package it for production, but we should ensure it's not packaged at all.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20625,12,"""SplashScreen is used for """"Ti.App.forceSplashAsSnapshot"""" instead of LaunchScreen""","""""""We introduces Storyboards to be default in new projects. That causes an issue when using the property [{{Ti.App.forceSplashAsSnapshot = true}}|docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App-property-forceSplashAsSnapshot] which makes sure to show the launch screen as soon as the user puts the app in background to ensure sensible information like bank accounts and password are not visible during multitasking.    The issue is, that the (legacy) splashscreen-image is shown, not the storyboard. In addition, we should not even package splash screens anymore, if we use storyboards. That issue is tracked [here|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-20626].""""""",Bug,"Title: SplashScreen is used for """"Ti.App.forceSplashAsSnapshot"""" instead of LaunchScreen
Description: """"We introduces Storyboards to be default in new projects. That causes an issue when using the property [{{Ti.App.forceSplashAsSnapshot = true}}|docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App-property-forceSplashAsSnapshot] which makes sure to show the launch screen as soon as the user puts the app in background to ensure sensible information like bank accounts and password are not visible during multitasking. The issue is, that the (legacy) splashscreen-image is shown, not the storyboard. In addition, we should not even package splash screens anymore, if we use storyboards. That issue is tracked [here|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-20626].""""",title+description
TIMOB-20618,12,"""iOS: Splash screen image naming conventions is not available for iOS(4/4s, iPhone 5/5C/5S and iPhone 6) in landscape mode.""","""""""h6. Description  No specific dimensions and naming convention is given by <USER>for splash screen landscape mode support for iphone 4/4s, iPhone 5/5C/5S and iPhone 6.   Dimensions and filenames are provided for iPhone 6+ devices to for splash screen support in landscape mode and its working.     Please find the below link,     http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Icons_and_Splash_Screens-section-29004897_IconsandSplashScreens-iOSgraphicassetrequirementsandoptions    I have created the new project in <USER>which provides default set of images used for App icons and splash images. While running this project the splash screen opens in portrait mode only in iPhone 4/4s, 5/ 5s/ 5c and 6.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Splash screen image naming conventions is not available for iOS(4/4s, iPhone 5/5C/5S and iPhone 6) in landscape mode.
Description: """"h6. Description No specific dimensions and naming convention is given by <USER>for splash screen landscape mode support for iphone 4/4s, iPhone 5/5C/5S and iPhone 6. Dimensions and filenames are provided for iPhone 6+ devices to for splash screen support in landscape mode and its working. Please find the below link, http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Icons_and_Splash_Screens-section-29004897_IconsandSplashScreens-iOSgraphicassetrequirementsandoptions I have created the new project in <USER>which provides default set of images used for App icons and splash images. While running this project the splash screen opens in portrait mode only in iPhone 4/4s, 5/ 5s/ 5c and 6.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20616,12,"""If Map Module Annotation has no title, than selectAnnotation() won't work""","""""""h3. Steps to reproduce:      h3. Actual results  If title is set than selectAnnotation function will work and pull Annotation to front. If title is not set than Annotation won't be pulled to front.    h3. Expected results  Annotation after selectAnnotation() should be pulled to front no matter if it has title or not.""""""",Bug,"Title: If Map Module Annotation has no title, than selectAnnotation() won't work
Description: """"h3. Steps to reproduce: h3. Actual results If title is set than selectAnnotation function will work and pull Annotation to front. If title is not set than Annotation won't be pulled to front. h3. Expected results Annotation after selectAnnotation() should be pulled to front no matter if it has title or not.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20614,12,""" iOS:Ti proxies are not always released from memory""","""""""TiViewProxy (and general proxy) objects do not appear to be always removed from memory, and garbage collection (when it occurs) regularly misses proxy objects, even when they are explicitly removed from parent views and nulled.     *Test Code:* Reporter’s sample  [code|https://www.dropbox.com/s/3zjhjnk1fe27yc2/sampleApp%20%281%29.zip?dl=0].    *Test Environment:*    <USER>Command-Line Interface; 5.2.0  Mac OS X,10.11.1Xcode-7.2.1,iOS SDK: 9.1,iPad  Node.js: 0.12.7  npm: 2.11.3  <USER>CLI    Installer                   = 4.2.3    Core Package                = 5.2.0  Titanium CLI:5.0.6  TI SDK:5.4.0.v20160307212310,5.20GA      *Test Steps:*  #  Import the app  # Run it in a IPad device/simulator.  #  Simply open Instruments 7.2.1 via an iOS 9.2. device   #  Go>Room with List View>Back to home. Same as Go>Room with View>Back to home.Watch the proxy object numbers go up and down inconsistently as we move back and forth within the same screens repeatedly.     *Test Results:*    Check the [link|http://postimg.org/image/q7sz4rtcd/].  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS:Ti proxies are not always released from memory
Description: """"TiViewProxy (and general proxy) objects do not appear to be always removed from memory, and garbage collection (when it occurs) regularly misses proxy objects, even when they are explicitly removed from parent views and nulled. *Test Code:* Reporter’s sample [code|https://www.dropbox.com/s/3zjhjnk1fe27yc2/sampleApp%20%281%29.zip?dl=0]. *Test Environment:* <USER>Command-Line Interface; 5.2.0 Mac OS X,10.11.1Xcode-7.2.1,iOS SDK: 9.1,iPad Node.js: 0.12.7 npm: 2.11.3 <USER>CLI Installer = 4.2.3 Core Package = 5.2.0 Titanium CLI:5.0.6 TI SDK:5.4.0.v20160307212310,5.20GA *Test Steps:* # Import the app # Run it in a IPad device/simulator. # Simply open Instruments 7.2.1 via an iOS 9.2. device # Go>Room with List View>Back to home. Same as Go>Room with View>Back to home.Watch the proxy object numbers go up and down inconsistently as we move back and forth within the same screens repeatedly. *Test Results:* Check the [link|http://postimg.org/image/q7sz4rtcd/]. """"",title+description
TIMOB-20613,12,"""Android native modules build is getting failed with Android NDK r11""","""""""Android native modules build is checking for a release.txt file to validate the Android NDK directory, but with the android NDK r11, {{release.txt}} file is removed.    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/android.js#L927    Here is the log:          *Workaround*: Manually create a {{release.txt}} file in the NDK home directory and run the build.    Studio checks for ndk-build , ndk-gdb , build , prebuilt , platforms files/folders to validate the NDK. How about using the same here ?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android native modules build is getting failed with Android NDK r11
Description: """"Android native modules build is checking for a release.txt file to validate the Android NDK directory, but with the android NDK r11, {{release.txt}} file is removed. https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/android.js#L927 Here is the log: *Workaround*: Manually create a {{release.txt}} file in the NDK home directory and run the build. Studio checks for ndk-build , ndk-gdb , build , prebuilt , platforms files/folders to validate the NDK. How about using the same here ?""""",title+description
