TIMOB-20422,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.iOS.SystemButton is undefined. ""","""""""h6. Reproduce   According to the docs page (http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton)  Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton should be DEPRECATED, and we should use Ti.UI.iOS.SystemButton instead.But when doing test for this, Ti.UI.iOS.SystemButton is undefined, however, Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton works well.    h6.Test Code  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.iOS.SystemButton is undefined.
Description: """"h6. Reproduce According to the docs page (http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton) Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton should be DEPRECATED, and we should use Ti.UI.iOS.SystemButton instead.But when doing test for this, Ti.UI.iOS.SystemButton is undefined, however, Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton works well. h6.Test Code """"",title+description
TIMOB-20421,12,"""ti.cloud module methods are not responding on MobileWeb when building from Windows""","""""""h6.Issue Description  Can't get response from ti.cloud module methods running as mobile web preview in browser on windows environment, the same code running from a Mac OS system is working as expected.     h6. Steps to reproduce    # Create a new classic default project application on studio with cloud services enabled  # Replace the code inside app.js with the next simple test case:     # The alert or Ti info's from the ACS variable are not executed on windows.  """"""",Bug,"Title: ti.cloud module methods are not responding on MobileWeb when building from Windows
Description: """"h6.Issue Description Can't get response from ti.cloud module methods running as mobile web preview in browser on windows environment, the same code running from a Mac OS system is working as expected. h6. Steps to reproduce # Create a new classic default project application on studio with cloud services enabled # Replace the code inside app.js with the next simple test case: # The alert or Ti info's from the ACS variable are not executed on windows. """"",title+description
TIMOB-20420,12,"""Hyperloop: Encrypt module source for licensed deployment""","""""""In order to make Hyperloop modules distributable (TIMOB-20379) on the marketplace / registry, we need to a) encrypt the source code and b) hook the module licensing into the build <USER>    I have no idea how that is done currently, but it looks like it's part of the upload <USER>at the marketplace. Please feel free to discuss here!""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: Encrypt module source for licensed deployment
Description: """"In order to make Hyperloop modules distributable (TIMOB-20379) on the marketplace / registry, we need to a) encrypt the source code and b) hook the module licensing into the build <USER> I have no idea how that is done currently, but it looks like it's part of the upload <USER>at the marketplace. Please feel free to discuss here!""""",title+description
TIMOB-20419,12,"""Hyperloop: Generate new Hyperloop-based module in CLI and Studio""","""""""This ticket described the required <USER>to create a new Hyperloop module from the CLI and Studio. We need to take care of:  - Creating a new template (appc.js configuration file, directory structure, sample view with commonJS conventions)  - Creating a new option """"""""4) Hyperloop module"""""""" when using """"""""ti create""""""""  - Hooking the module configuration file (appc.js) into the Titanium Mobile build <USER>   There is a CSPEC for the template and configuration file available [here|https://github.com/hansemannn/cspec-titanium-hyperloop-modules]""""""",Bug,"Title: Hyperloop: Generate new Hyperloop-based module in CLI and Studio
Description: """"This ticket described the required <USER>to create a new Hyperloop module from the CLI and Studio. We need to take care of: - Creating a new template (appc.js configuration file, directory structure, sample view with commonJS conventions) - Creating a new option """"""""4) Hyperloop module"""""""" when using """"""""ti create"""""""" - Hooking the module configuration file (appc.js) into the Titanium Mobile build <USER> There is a CSPEC for the template and configuration file available [here|https://github.com/hansemannn/cspec-titanium-hyperloop-modules]""""",title+description
