TIMOB-20265,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.View """"borderRadius"""" property not working on android 4.4.2 & 4.2.2""","""""""This is a regression. Works fine with SDK 5.1.2.GA.    h5.Steps To Reproduce:  1. Use the code below in your app.js:    2.Build for android 4.4.2 & 4.4.2 & also with android 6.0 or 5.1.0.  3.After the app launches look at the edges of the view.    h5.Actual Results:  1. The edges of the view are not rounded even though the """"""""borderRadius"""""""" property is specified on android 4.4.2 & 4.2.2.  2. We see the rounded edges on android 6.0 ,5.1.0 & 4.4.4.  Attaching screenshots for reference.    h5.Expected Results:  1. Rounded edges should be visible when """"""""borderRadius' is specified on android 4.4.2 & 4.2.2.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.View """"borderRadius"""" property not working on android 4.4.2 & 4.2.2
Description: """"This is a regression. Works fine with SDK 5.1.2.GA. h5.Steps To Reproduce: 1. Use the code below in your app.js: 2.Build for android 4.4.2 & 4.4.2 & also with android 6.0 or 5.1.0. 3.After the app launches look at the edges of the view. h5.Actual Results: 1. The edges of the view are not rounded even though the """"""""borderRadius"""""""" property is specified on android 4.4.2 & 4.2.2. 2. We see the rounded edges on android 6.0 ,5.1.0 & 4.4.4. Attaching screenshots for reference. h5.Expected Results: 1. Rounded edges should be visible when """"""""borderRadius' is specified on android 4.4.2 & 4.2.2.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20262,12,"""Android: exception when borderColor is modified without setting first in the constructor""","""""""I want to mark a row of a table as selected using a border. Given that the border does not work at all if it is set in the tableViewRow, I tried it using an inner view.    If I try to modify the color of the view border without setting first in the constructor, an exception is thrown.        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: exception when borderColor is modified without setting first in the constructor
Description: """"I want to mark a row of a table as selected using a border. Given that the border does not work at all if it is set in the tableViewRow, I tried it using an inner view. If I try to modify the color of the view border without setting first in the constructor, an exception is thrown. """"",title+description
TIMOB-20261,12,"""iOS: SOASTA duplicate symbols on com.soasta.touchtest module""","""""""h6.Issue Description  While building to iOS added the -l trace and found that got a bunch of these duplicate symbol messages during the link from touchtest:         So, after removing the touchtest module from the project, did a Project->Clean and HellowWorld project succeeded in building and ran on device.     h6.Steps to reproduce   1) Create a HelloWorld app  2) Enable Test service through the Tiapp  3) Attempt building to iOS device (iOS 8.2 on iPhone5 may be a good option)  4) Monitor and watch stack trace from console output. Dupe symbols may be noticeable or just suppressed by the system.     h6.More logs...   I kept getting a ton of similar messages however aren't dupe symbols at my end they are just warnings. i.e:  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: SOASTA duplicate symbols on com.soasta.touchtest module
Description: """"h6.Issue Description While building to iOS added the -l trace and found that got a bunch of these duplicate symbol messages during the link from touchtest: So, after removing the touchtest module from the project, did a Project->Clean and HellowWorld project succeeded in building and ran on device. h6.Steps to reproduce 1) Create a HelloWorld app 2) Enable Test service through the Tiapp 3) Attempt building to iOS device (iOS 8.2 on iPhone5 may be a good option) 4) Monitor and watch stack trace from console output. Dupe symbols may be noticeable or just suppressed by the system. h6.More logs... I kept getting a ton of similar messages however aren't dupe symbols at my end they are just warnings. i.e: """"",title+description
TIMOB-20260,12,"""Android 6: CameraView with overlay crash with message """"AppName is not responding""""""","""""""h6. Issue Description  Android 6.0 camera view with overlay sometimes hangs after taking a picture. The hang resumes for about 45 seconds to a minute after which the app crashes with message """"""""AppName is not responding"""""""". After closing the app camera issue persist. Even native camera app is not working as the result of this crash. The only way to restore both apps to working state is to restart users device.    This was tested on on Nexus 9 tablet and Nexus 5X devices running Marshmallow 6.0.1    h6.Steps to replicate:   # Create a new Alloy Default Project  # Open the app folder and replace the existing folders with the attached files  # Run  # Press """"""""Open Camera"""""""" button; you should be presented with camera screen with an   overlay.   # Press """"""""Take"""""""" button   # If the app does not crash a preview screen will appear with captured picture. If that   happens either press """"""""Keep"""""""" button to return to main page or press """"""""Retake"""""""" button   to come back to camera screen.   # Keep taking pictured until crash is reproduced (it sometimes takes a few tries to   reproduce).   """"""",Bug,"Title: Android 6: CameraView with overlay crash with message """"AppName is not responding""""
Description: """"h6. Issue Description Android 6.0 camera view with overlay sometimes hangs after taking a picture. The hang resumes for about 45 seconds to a minute after which the app crashes with message """"""""AppName is not responding"""""""". After closing the app camera issue persist. Even native camera app is not working as the result of this crash. The only way to restore both apps to working state is to restart users device. This was tested on on Nexus 9 tablet and Nexus 5X devices running Marshmallow 6.0.1 h6.Steps to replicate: # Create a new Alloy Default Project # Open the app folder and replace the existing folders with the attached files # Run # Press """"""""Open Camera"""""""" button; you should be presented with camera screen with an overlay. # Press """"""""Take"""""""" button # If the app does not crash a preview screen will appear with captured picture. If that happens either press """"""""Keep"""""""" button to return to main page or press """"""""Retake"""""""" button to come back to camera screen. # Keep taking pictured until crash is reproduced (it sometimes takes a few tries to reproduce). """"",title+description
TIMOB-20255,12,"""Label will not animate if text property is empty string or not defined""","""""""*Example code*:    *Expected behaviour:*  Animation should work (for example text may be set dynamically and user is not sure if there will be any text) and opacity value should be changed. 'complete' event should be fired.    *Actual behaviour*:  If text property is not set or set to '' (empty string), than animation won't work and complete listener won't be fired.    *Actual workaround*:   Before calling animation user have to check if string is empty/not set and then take appropriate behavior.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Label will not animate if text property is empty string or not defined
Description: """"*Example code*: *Expected behaviour:* Animation should work (for example text may be set dynamically and user is not sure if there will be any text) and opacity value should be changed. 'complete' event should be fired. *Actual behaviour*: If text property is not set or set to '' (empty string), than animation won't work and complete listener won't be fired. *Actual workaround*: Before calling animation user have to check if string is empty/not set and then take appropriate behavior. """"",title+description
TIMOB-20254,12,"""How to detect click in Highcharts and trigger event in application?""","""""""I am using Highcharts version 3.0.5. I am trying to detect click event when user click on bar in graph. The goal is to identify which bar is clicked. Problem is how detect click from graph(webview) and fire event in application.""""""",Bug,"Title: How to detect click in Highcharts and trigger event in application?
Description: """"I am using Highcharts version 3.0.5. I am trying to detect click event when user click on bar in graph. The goal is to identify which bar is clicked. Problem is how detect click from graph(webview) and fire event in application.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20253,12,"""app.js not found""","""""""When deploying from xcode to the device, I get the red screen with 'no app.js' found. This is a basic project created from the Studio wizards.  Downgrading the SDK to v4 works fine.    Please fix this, it has been months and reported multiple time.    app.js code  ~~~  // create tab group  var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup();    var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Home',      backgroundColor:'#fff',      layout:'vertical',      url:'main.js' ,     });  var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({        window:win1,  });          tabGroup.addTab(tab1);        // open tab group          tabGroup.open();  ~~~""""""",Bug,"Title: app.js not found
Description: """"When deploying from xcode to the device, I get the red screen with 'no app.js' found. This is a basic project created from the Studio wizards. Downgrading the SDK to v4 works fine. Please fix this, it has been months and reported multiple time. app.js code ~~~ // create tab group var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup(); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Home', backgroundColor:'#fff', layout:'vertical', url:'main.js' , }); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({ window:win1, }); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); // open tab group tabGroup.open(); ~~~""""",title+description
