Description: """"h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create titanium classic app 2. Use this sample code 3. Show Contacts 4. Select a person h4. Expected Result alert dialog with person's name shown h4. Actual Result alert dialog with '<USER> shown""""",title+description
TIMOB-20144,12,"""Android 6.0: allow native modules to get notified about runtime permission granting results""","""""""With the new Android 6 permissions mechanism, native modules should be able to request runtime permissions outside of the ones exposed by the Ti API (camera, calendar, location and contacts). For example, a native module for sending SMS messages would need to request the SEND_SMS permission at runtime, however it would have no means to get notified about the result of the operation.  I would propose to extend the TiBaseActivity class with a mechanism allowing native modules to register a listener, in order to be notified when the onRequestPermissionsResult method of the current activity is called (see https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/TiBaseActivity.java#L447)""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android 6.0: allow native modules to get notified about runtime permission granting results
Description: """"With the new Android 6 permissions mechanism, native modules should be able to request runtime permissions outside of the ones exposed by the Ti API (camera, calendar, location and contacts). For example, a native module for sending SMS messages would need to request the SEND_SMS permission at runtime, however it would have no means to get notified about the result of the operation. I would propose to extend the TiBaseActivity class with a mechanism allowing native modules to register a listener, in order to be notified when the onRequestPermissionsResult method of the current activity is called (see https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/TiBaseActivity.java#L447)""""",title+description
TIMOB-20141,12,"""Global scope variables can be shared with CommonJS modules""","""""""module.js  ```  console.log(controllerVariable);  moduleVariable = """"""""moduleVariable"""""""";  module.exports = {};  ```    controller.js  ```  controllerVariable = """"""""controllerVariable"""""""";  var module = require(""""""""module"""""""");  console.log(moduleVariable);  ```    Output when running the application is:  moduleVariable  controllerVariable    Expected that the global scope of the controller would not be shared with the global scope of the module.""""""",Bug,"Title: Global scope variables can be shared with CommonJS modules
Description: """"module.js ``` console.log(controllerVariable); moduleVariable = """"""""moduleVariable""""""""; module.exports = {}; ``` controller.js ``` controllerVariable = """"""""controllerVariable""""""""; var module = require(""""""""module""""""""); console.log(moduleVariable); ``` Output when running the application is: moduleVariable controllerVariable Expected that the global scope of the controller would not be shared with the global scope of the module.""""",title+description
