TIMOB-20119,12,"""iOS: If you debug an app with CoreMotion module, then the app will crash on launch""","""""""*Details:* If you debug an app with CoreMotion module, then the app will crash on launch and two types of crashes are generated:   # If you debug an app without the debugger fix for TIMOB-19724, then you will run into the wtf crash which was originally reported in TIMOB-19724 and bugs like it; see wtf.crash  # If you debug the app with the debugger fix for TIMOB-19724 (see [this comment|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-19724?focusedCommentId=372409&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-372409]), then you will encounter a module crash; see module.crash and below snippet:      *Steps to reproduce:*  # Create a default Alloy project  # Make sure to include {{ti.coremotion}} in the tiapp.xml  # In the {{controllers/index.js}} file, require {{ti.coremotion}} module:    # Debug app to an iOS simulator    *Actual:* App will crash on launch as per above mentioned scenarios.  *Expected:* App should not crash when you debug an app with CoreMotion module.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: If you debug an app with CoreMotion module, then the app will crash on launch
Description: """"*Details:* If you debug an app with CoreMotion module, then the app will crash on launch and two types of crashes are generated: # If you debug an app without the debugger fix for TIMOB-19724, then you will run into the wtf crash which was originally reported in TIMOB-19724 and bugs like it; see wtf.crash # If you debug the app with the debugger fix for TIMOB-19724 (see [this comment|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-19724?focusedCommentId=372409&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-372409]), then you will encounter a module crash; see module.crash and below snippet: *Steps to reproduce:* # Create a default Alloy project # Make sure to include {{ti.coremotion}} in the tiapp.xml # In the {{controllers/index.js}} file, require {{ti.coremotion}} module: # Debug app to an iOS simulator *Actual:* App will crash on launch as per above mentioned scenarios. *Expected:* App should not crash when you debug an app with CoreMotion module.""""",title+description
