TIMOB-20071,12,"""Android: Rebuild supported closed and open source modules for Android 6.0""","""""""With the new Titanium SDK 5.0 and above, when you use Android modules on Android 6.0, the app will crash citing `text relocation` errors. Modules need to be updated and rebuild. Some of the modules have already been updated.    List from TIMOB-17928:-    h5. Commonly Used  ti.compression (MOD-2163) (Updated. No Issue.)  ti.imagefactory (MOD-2166) (Updated. No Issue.)  ti.paint (MOD-2167) (Updated. No Issue.)  ti.flurry (MOD-2181)  h5. Packaged with the SDK  ti.facebook: https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.facebook (Recently Updated)  ti.map: https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map (Recently Updated)    h5. Important Enterprise Modules  <USER>encrypteddatabase (TIMOB-19206) (Updated. No Issue)  com.<USER>apm (TIMOB-19293) (Updated. No Issue.)  <USER>https (TIMOB-19729) (Updated. No Issue.)  ti.geofence: (No Issue.)  ti.ldap: (No Issue.)  ti.crypto: (No Issue.)  ti.inappbilling (MOD-2154) (Updated. No Issue.)""""""",Epic,"Title: Android: Rebuild supported closed and open source modules for Android 6.0
Description: """"With the new Titanium SDK 5.0 and above, when you use Android modules on Android 6.0, the app will crash citing `text relocation` errors. Modules need to be updated and rebuild. Some of the modules have already been updated. List from TIMOB-17928:- h5. Commonly Used ti.compression (MOD-2163) (Updated. No Issue.) ti.imagefactory (MOD-2166) (Updated. No Issue.) ti.paint (MOD-2167) (Updated. No Issue.) ti.flurry (MOD-2181) h5. Packaged with the SDK ti.facebook: https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.facebook (Recently Updated) ti.map: https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map (Recently Updated) h5. Important Enterprise Modules <USER>encrypteddatabase (TIMOB-19206) (Updated. No Issue) com.<USER>apm (TIMOB-19293) (Updated. No Issue.) <USER>https (TIMOB-19729) (Updated. No Issue.) ti.geofence: (No Issue.) ti.ldap: (No Issue.) ti.crypto: (No Issue.) ti.inappbilling (MOD-2154) (Updated. No Issue.)""""",title+description
TIMOB-20069,12,"""NSLog calls in Watch extension not shown in console""","""""""When I add {{NSLog(\@""""""""Hello"""""""");}} to the {{showLog}} function [here|https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-watchos2/blob/master/extensions/WatchOS2/WatchOS2%20WatchApp%20Extension/InterfaceController.m#L54] and run the iOS + Apple Watch app in iOS Simulator or on device I don't see """"""""Hello"""""""" anywhere.    The trace logs mention tailing the Apple Watch simulator logs but in the end all that is displayed is the _application log file_ it finds just before the {{-- Start simulator log --}} line.    """"""",Bug,"Title: NSLog calls in Watch extension not shown in console
Description: """"When I add {{NSLog(\@""""""""Hello"""""""");}} to the {{showLog}} function [here|https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-watchos2/blob/master/extensions/WatchOS2/WatchOS2%20WatchApp%20Extension/InterfaceController.m#L54] and run the iOS + Apple Watch app in iOS Simulator or on device I don't see """"""""Hello"""""""" anywhere. The trace logs mention tailing the Apple Watch simulator logs but in the end all that is displayed is the _application log file_ it finds just before the {{-- Start simulator log --}} line. """"",title+description
TIMOB-20065,12,"""iOS Alloy Missing RightNavButton with TabGroup inside NavigationWindow""","""""""h6.Issue Description  When using a TabGroup within a NavigationWindow, the RightNavButton of any Window within the TabGroup do not appear in the navigation bar.    h6.Steps to Replicate  -Create a new titanium alloy project  -Open the app folder  -Replace the index.xml file inside views folder and the index.js file inside controllers  -Add the tabs.xml in in the views folder with the test-case code  -Add the tabs.js in in the controllers folder with the test-case code  -Build and run  -Click open window  -The RightNavButton is not showed    h6. Test Case   //index.xml    //index.js    //tabs.xml    //tabs.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS Alloy Missing RightNavButton with TabGroup inside NavigationWindow
Description: """"h6.Issue Description When using a TabGroup within a NavigationWindow, the RightNavButton of any Window within the TabGroup do not appear in the navigation bar. h6.Steps to Replicate -Create a new titanium alloy project -Open the app folder -Replace the index.xml file inside views folder and the index.js file inside controllers -Add the tabs.xml in in the views folder with the test-case code -Add the tabs.js in in the controllers folder with the test-case code -Build and run -Click open window -The RightNavButton is not showed h6. Test Case //index.xml //index.js //tabs.xml //tabs.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-20061,12,"""TLS Version set in Android ignored on Publish""","""""""Using the latest SDK and studio, using Set TLS version on android functions as expected when built directly to the device, however once published to the store, the setting is ignored and android default behaviour kicks in.    On android versions 5 and above TLS 1.2 is used correctly both locally and published.  On android versions below 5 (4.4.4 and 4.1.0 confirmed) TLS 1.1 or TLS 1.2 is used correctly locally but connections are refused once published (SSL handshake fails)    We have TLS 1.0 disabled on our production environment for security reasons and as a consequence of the setting not taking affect, all android devices cannot connect to the server.      *Repro Steps  Create a service endpoint with TLS 1.1 and TLS 1.2 only enabled.  Create HTTP client initialising TLS version      Set target and min SDKS    Add connection to server endpoint.  Compile using Latest SDK and deploy to android 4.1 or 4.4.4 device (simulator also behaves correctly)  Run application and hit endpoint.-> works    Publish application to play store as beta or live  Run application and hit endpoint -> call fails""""""",Bug,"Title: TLS Version set in Android ignored on Publish
Description: """"Using the latest SDK and studio, using Set TLS version on android functions as expected when built directly to the device, however once published to the store, the setting is ignored and android default behaviour kicks in. On android versions 5 and above TLS 1.2 is used correctly both locally and published. On android versions below 5 (4.4.4 and 4.1.0 confirmed) TLS 1.1 or TLS 1.2 is used correctly locally but connections are refused once published (SSL handshake fails) We have TLS 1.0 disabled on our production environment for security reasons and as a consequence of the setting not taking affect, all android devices cannot connect to the server. *Repro Steps Create a service endpoint with TLS 1.1 and TLS 1.2 only enabled. Create HTTP client initialising TLS version Set target and min SDKS Add connection to server endpoint. Compile using Latest SDK and deploy to android 4.1 or 4.4.4 device (simulator also behaves correctly) Run application and hit endpoint.-> works Publish application to play store as beta or live Run application and hit endpoint -> call fails""""",title+description
TIMOB-20058,12,"""Fail gracefully if an individual platform check fails""","""""""Based on TIMOB-20057, if the Windows platform check fails, ALL building is broken.    Instead, we should try/catch around the individual platform checks so that if one fails, at least the rest would continue to work.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Fail gracefully if an individual platform check fails
Description: """"Based on TIMOB-20057, if the Windows platform check fails, ALL building is broken. Instead, we should try/catch around the individual platform checks so that if one fails, at least the rest would continue to work.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20057,12,"""Windows: Unable to build for any platform if there is no Visual Studio installed""","""""""# Ensure there are no versions of Visual Studio installed.  # Attempt to build. There is an error of:        See this link https://community.<USER>com/topic/4128/issues-with-update-from-4-x-to-5-1""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Unable to build for any platform if there is no Visual Studio installed
Description: """"# Ensure there are no versions of Visual Studio installed. # Attempt to build. There is an error of: See this link https://community.<USER>com/topic/4128/issues-with-update-from-4-x-to-5-1""""",title+description
TIMOB-20053,12,"""JSON.parse not implemented on Windows Phone?""","""""""Hi guys,  I'm trying to parse simple JSON object loaded from web. On iOS it's working fine. On Android, I have to use eval('('+this.responseText+')'). But on Windows phone, JSON.parse does nothing(when I can choose JSON methods, parse method is only for mobile weband windows logo is grayed ) and eval() crash the app(without any error log).   Can somebody please help me?   Thank you.""""""",Bug,"Title: JSON.parse not implemented on Windows Phone?
Description: """"Hi guys, I'm trying to parse simple JSON object loaded from web. On iOS it's working fine. On Android, I have to use eval('('+this.responseText+')'). But on Windows phone, JSON.parse does nothing(when I can choose JSON methods, parse method is only for mobile weband windows logo is grayed ) and eval() crash the app(without any error log). Can somebody please help me? Thank you.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20052,12,"""Back button on Windows Phone 8.1""","""""""Hi guys,  it would be awesome to implement Windows Phone Back button event like on Android. On my app, I navigate through windows and back button is used to get to previous window(as it is supposed to), but if you accidentally press Back button too many times, the app closes without notification. With Vack button event, I can implement question dialog to prevent this(like on android where it is fully working).  Thank you""""""",New Feature,"Title: Back button on Windows Phone 8.1
Description: """"Hi guys, it would be awesome to implement Windows Phone Back button event like on Android. On my app, I navigate through windows and back button is used to get to previous window(as it is supposed to), but if you accidentally press Back button too many times, the app closes without notification. With Vack button event, I can implement question dialog to prevent this(like on android where it is fully working). Thank you""""",title+description
TIMOB-20047,12,"""Parity: iOS support for hintTextColor""","""""""I know TIMOB-5186 was resolved by adding {{attributedHintText}} but I still think it would be good to have parity with {{hintTextColor}} on Android so this common use case is simpler to implement.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Parity: iOS support for hintTextColor
Description: """"I know TIMOB-5186 was resolved by adding {{attributedHintText}} but I still think it would be good to have parity with {{hintTextColor}} on Android so this common use case is simpler to implement.""""",title+description
TIMOB-20046,12,"""Ti.Geolocation.getCurrentPosition returns success:true with no coords""","""""""For a new training app I did:        And of course in {tiapp.xml}}:        But the response in Simulator was:        I expected to get {{coords}} of course, but in case of an error at least {{success:false}} instead of {{true}}.    *NOTE:* The [documentartion|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/LocationResults] only lists {{coords}} and {{provider}} (Android) and not {{success}} and {{error}}.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Geolocation.getCurrentPosition returns success:true with no coords
