TIMOB-19996,12,"""iOS: deadlock occurs on sound.play""","""""""h5. Description:  *This is a regression from 5.0.2.GA*  Sound fails to play when an app is built with Ti SDK {{5.1.0}}. The following error occurs attempting to play a sound from a device:        The bug was originally found when running the sound test cases in KitchenSink, but the same issue occurs when isolated into a separate app.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a Classic project.  2. Include attached .wav file to project directory > Resources > etc   3. Add following demo code to app.js:     3. Run app to device.  4. Press play.    h5. Result:  Receive {{deadlock}} error and sound fails to play.    h5. Expected Result:  app should not deadlock and should succeed in playing the sample file.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: deadlock occurs on sound.play
Description: """"h5. Description: *This is a regression from 5.0.2.GA* Sound fails to play when an app is built with Ti SDK {{5.1.0}}. The following error occurs attempting to play a sound from a device: The bug was originally found when running the sound test cases in KitchenSink, but the same issue occurs when isolated into a separate app. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a Classic project. 2. Include attached .wav file to project directory > Resources > etc 3. Add following demo code to app.js: 3. Run app to device. 4. Press play. h5. Result: Receive {{deadlock}} error and sound fails to play. h5. Expected Result: app should not deadlock and should succeed in playing the sample file.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19995,12,"""CLI: Android build intermittently fails to recognize emulator is ready""","""""""When doing test of the hyperloop example app with Android hyperloop examples, I will run into the CLI intermittently not recognizing that the emulator was already open and ready. The build will stall at """"""""waiting for emulator to be ready"""""""" and will eventually time out.    You simply need to kill the build and start a new one to workaround it (and maybe kill the emulator too for good karma), but it's a pain.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android build intermittently fails to recognize emulator is ready
Description: """"When doing test of the hyperloop example app with Android hyperloop examples, I will run into the CLI intermittently not recognizing that the emulator was already open and ready. The build will stall at """"""""waiting for emulator to be ready"""""""" and will eventually time out. You simply need to kill the build and start a new one to workaround it (and maybe kill the emulator too for good karma), but it's a pain.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19993,12,"""SafariDialog: Title parameter ignored - does it even exist in iOS?""","""""""When I run the [example included in the module|https://github.com/<USER>modules/Ti.SafariDialog/blob/master/example/app.js] on iPhone and iPad I can't see the title parameter of the [open method|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Modules.SafariDialog-method-open] being used anywhere. I also can't find it in [Apple's reference|https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/SafariServices/Reference/SFSafariViewController_Ref/index.html], so does it even exist?""""""",Bug,"Title: SafariDialog: Title parameter ignored - does it even exist in iOS?
