TIMOB-19941,12,"""Black bar at bottom of all ScrollableViews with SDK 5.1.x in IOS""","""""""Wherever a ScrollableView is used it has a black bar at the bottom. I created a new application and it has the same problem.      {code:xml}  <Alloy>   <Window>    <ScrollableView>     <View title=""""""""Tab 1"""""""">      <Label>I am page 1</Label>     </View>     <View title=""""""""Tab 2"""""""">      <Label>I am page 2</Label>     </View>    </ScrollableView>   </Window>  </Alloy>  {code}      {code:java}  """"""""Window"""""""": {   backgroundColor: """"""""#fff""""""""  }    """"""""Label"""""""": {   width: Ti.UI.SIZE,   height: Ti.UI.SIZE,   color: """"""""#000"""""""",   font: {    fontSize: 20,    fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue'   },   textAlign: 'center'  }   {code}    !Simulator Screen Shot Nov 10, 2015, 10.31.39 AM.png|thumbnail!""""""",Bug,"Title: Black bar at bottom of all ScrollableViews with SDK 5.1.x in IOS
Description: """"Wherever a ScrollableView is used it has a black bar at the bottom. I created a new application and it has the same problem. {code:xml} <Alloy> <Window> <ScrollableView> <View title=""""""""Tab 1""""""""> <Label>I am page 1</Label> </View> <View title=""""""""Tab 2""""""""> <Label>I am page 2</Label> </View> </ScrollableView> </Window> </Alloy> {code} {code:java} """"""""Window"""""""": { backgroundColor: """"""""#fff"""""""" } """"""""Label"""""""": { width: Ti.UI.SIZE, height: Ti.UI.SIZE, color: """"""""#000"""""""", font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' }, textAlign: 'center' } {code} !Simulator Screen Shot Nov 10, 2015, 10.31.39 AM.png|thumbnail!""""",title+description
TIMOB-19940,12,"""Add *appearance-properties to AlertDialog""","""""""We've added {{*keyboardType}} and {{*keyboardReturnKeyType}} properties to {{Ti.UI.AlertDialog}} in 5.1.0 but not {{*appearance}}, to switch between the default or alert (black) appearance of the soft keyboard on iOS, like we have for TextField and TextArea.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Add *appearance-properties to AlertDialog
Description: """"We've added {{*keyboardType}} and {{*keyboardReturnKeyType}} properties to {{Ti.UI.AlertDialog}} in 5.1.0 but not {{*appearance}}, to switch between the default or alert (black) appearance of the soft keyboard on iOS, like we have for TextField and TextArea.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19939,12,"""keyboardType should not list KEYBOARD_APPEARANCE_* constants""","""""""The different places where we have the {{keyboardType}} property all list the two {{KEYBOARD_APPEARANCE_*}} constants as valid values, although these are only valid for the {{appearance}} property.    * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextField-property-keyboardType  * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextArea-property-keyboardType  * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-keyboardType  * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-loginKeyboardType  * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-passwordKeyboardType    This is because in the YML's we use {{KEYBOARD_*}} wildcards:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/search?q=KEYBOARD_*    Unless we can make exceptions we should either:    # List each of them manually  # Rename the constants for {{keyboardType}} to {{KEYBOARD_TYPE_*}}    I'm for the second option; deprecate in next 5.x and remove the old in 6.0.  That's why I've created this ticket in TIMOB instead of TIDOC.""""""",Bug,"Title: keyboardType should not list KEYBOARD_APPEARANCE_* constants
Description: """"The different places where we have the {{keyboardType}} property all list the two {{KEYBOARD_APPEARANCE_*}} constants as valid values, although these are only valid for the {{appearance}} property. * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextField-property-keyboardType * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextArea-property-keyboardType * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-keyboardType * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-loginKeyboardType * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-passwordKeyboardType This is because in the YML's we use {{KEYBOARD_*}} wildcards: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/search?q=KEYBOARD_* Unless we can make exceptions we should either: # List each of them manually # Rename the constants for {{keyboardType}} to {{KEYBOARD_TYPE_*}} I'm for the second option; deprecate in next 5.x and remove the old in 6.0. That's why I've created this ticket in TIMOB instead of TIDOC.""""",title+description
