TIMOB-19881,12,"""iOS: Check for 64-bit modules at compile instead of runtime""","""""""When we added support for 64-bit modules TIMOB-18196 was implemented to make clear what architecture a module wasn't found for.    Unfortunately this has two drawbacks:    # It is confusing (ALOY-1249) when the developer intended to require a CommonJS module which has nothing to do with architectures.  # The developer won't find out until runtime.    We should check if modules have the required architectures at compile time so that we can revert TIMOB-18196 and fix both of the above.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Check for 64-bit modules at compile instead of runtime
Description: """"When we added support for 64-bit modules TIMOB-18196 was implemented to make clear what architecture a module wasn't found for. Unfortunately this has two drawbacks: # It is confusing (ALOY-1249) when the developer intended to require a CommonJS module which has nothing to do with architectures. # The developer won't find out until runtime. We should check if modules have the required architectures at compile time so that we can revert TIMOB-18196 and fix both of the above.""""",title+description
