Description: """"h4.What happens: On first rotation no event is triggered. On every orientation change thereafter, the wrong orientation is returned. I have observed similar behavior on a physical device but I can not reproduce it consistently. In genymotion it happens every time. h4.Note: The project must be an alloy project. The problem does not occur in a non alloy project. Orientation works correctly in TI SDK 4.0.0.GA h4.How to reproduce: 1. Create new Empty alloy project 2. Set index.js to: 3. Start app in genymotion 4. Output from console: First rotation results in no output. Next rotation back into Portrait results in the following: Then rotating into Lanscape results in the following: """"",title+description
TIMOB-19877,12,"""Android: Cannot tap to select text in TextArea with """"editable"""" set to false like iOS""","""""""*Summary:*  While a {{TextArea}} object's property """"""""editable"""""""" is set to {{false}}, end-users cannot tap to select text like how it works on iOS. This is a parity issue.    Note that the {{TextArea}} is not disabled. The end-user can scroll the content. The issue is that no cursor is shown and it's impossible for the end-user to make cursor selections. (However, the {{setSelection()}} method works and text selections can be made programmatically.)    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Build and run the below code on Android.  # Tap and hold on a word in the {{TextArea}}.  # Notice that no selection was made. _(This is the issue.)_        *Note:*  On iOS, if {{TextField}} property """"""""editable"""""""" is set {{false}}, then the end-user is unable to tap to select text either. So, in this case, both Android and iOS are in parity. I think this is the """"""""native"""""""" iOS behavior, although it is inconsistent with iOS' own {{TextArea}} behavior.    *Cause:*  Titanium is calling {{setCursorVisible(false)}} in the Java {{TiUIText.handleKeyboard()}} method below.  [TiUIText.java#L650|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/3b75bf2b9f9733bca93ad22d738fea0525da9431/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIText.java#L650]    But since iOS' {{TextField}} does not allow text selection while """"""""editable"""""""" is {{false}}, Android should continue to call {{setCursorVisible(false)}} only for the single-line {{TextField}} case.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot tap to select text in TextArea with """"editable"""" set to false like iOS
Description: """"*Summary:* While a {{TextArea}} object's property """"""""editable"""""""" is set to {{false}}, end-users cannot tap to select text like how it works on iOS. This is a parity issue. Note that the {{TextArea}} is not disabled. The end-user can scroll the content. The issue is that no cursor is shown and it's impossible for the end-user to make cursor selections. (However, the {{setSelection()}} method works and text selections can be made programmatically.) *Steps to reproduce:* # Build and run the below code on Android. # Tap and hold on a word in the {{TextArea}}. # Notice that no selection was made. _(This is the issue.)_ *Note:* On iOS, if {{TextField}} property """"""""editable"""""""" is set {{false}}, then the end-user is unable to tap to select text either. So, in this case, both Android and iOS are in parity. I think this is the """"""""native"""""""" iOS behavior, although it is inconsistent with iOS' own {{TextArea}} behavior. *Cause:* Titanium is calling {{setCursorVisible(false)}} in the Java {{TiUIText.handleKeyboard()}} method below. [TiUIText.java#L650|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/3b75bf2b9f9733bca93ad22d738fea0525da9431/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIText.java#L650] But since iOS' {{TextField}} does not allow text selection while """"""""editable"""""""" is {{false}}, Android should continue to call {{setCursorVisible(false)}} only for the single-line {{TextField}} case. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19875,12,"""Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder gives twisted value of latitude,longitude.""","""""""Recently I tried to solve issue in Q&A forum but I got same result as he got.    So the problem is Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder gives latitude & longitude in reverse order.    Example :   Ti.Geolocation.accuracy = Ti.Geolocation.ACCURACY_HIGH;    Ti.Geolocation.getCurrentPosition(showAddress);    function showAddress(e) {      Ti.API.info(""""""""Latitude == """""""" + e.coords.latitude);      Ti.API.info(""""""""Longitude == """""""" + e.coords.longitude);            Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder(e.coords.latitude , e.coords.longitude, function (data){          Ti.API.info(""""""""\nReverse Geocode address == """""""" + JSON.stringify(data.places[0]));          Ti.API.info(""""""""\nReverse Geocode Lat == """""""" + data.places[0].latitude);          Ti.API.info(""""""""Reverse Geocode Long == """""""" + data.places[0].longitude);      });   }    OUTPUT :   Latitude == 11.12345  Longitude == 55.12345    Reverse Geocode address == {""""""""street"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""city"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""address"""""""":""""""""xxxxxxxx"""""""",""""""""state"""""""":""""""""xxxxxx"""""""",""""""""country_code"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""country"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""longitude"""""""":11.12345,""""""""latitude"""""""":55.12345,""""""""zipcode"""""""":""""""""xxxx""""""""}    Reverse Geocode Lat == 55.12345  Reverse Geocode Long == 11.12345    Reference Link :    https://community.<USER>com/topic/3858/could-anyone-try-the-below-code-get-back-to-me-whether-it-is-really-a-bug-or-i-am-doing-something-wrong""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder gives twisted value of latitude,longitude.
Description: """"Recently I tried to solve issue in Q&A forum but I got same result as he got. So the problem is Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder gives latitude & longitude in reverse order. Example : Ti.Geolocation.accuracy = Ti.Geolocation.ACCURACY_HIGH; Ti.Geolocation.getCurrentPosition(showAddress); function showAddress(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Latitude == """""""" + e.coords.latitude); Ti.API.info(""""""""Longitude == """""""" + e.coords.longitude); Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder(e.coords.latitude , e.coords.longitude, function (data){ Ti.API.info(""""""""\nReverse Geocode address == """""""" + JSON.stringify(data.places[0])); Ti.API.info(""""""""\nReverse Geocode Lat == """""""" + data.places[0].latitude); Ti.API.info(""""""""Reverse Geocode Long == """""""" + data.places[0].longitude); }); } OUTPUT : Latitude == 11.12345 Longitude == 55.12345 Reverse Geocode address == {""""""""street"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""city"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""address"""""""":""""""""xxxxxxxx"""""""",""""""""state"""""""":""""""""xxxxxx"""""""",""""""""country_code"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""country"""""""":""""""""xxxx"""""""",""""""""longitude"""""""":11.12345,""""""""latitude"""""""":55.12345,""""""""zipcode"""""""":""""""""xxxx""""""""} Reverse Geocode Lat == 55.12345 Reverse Geocode Long == 11.12345 Reference Link : https://community.<USER>com/topic/3858/could-anyone-try-the-below-code-get-back-to-me-whether-it-is-really-a-bug-or-i-am-doing-something-wrong""""",title+description
TIMOB-19874,12,"""ListView - Handling Events on Template Views causing Memory Leak!""","""""""Reference: https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Alloy_ListView_Guide-section-40928632_AlloyListViewGuide-HandlingEventsonTemplateViews    Create a default Alloy project with the following:    index.xml      index.js      sample.xml      sample.js      Use XCode Instrument to monitor Allocations. Open and Close the sample window. You'll see the sample window view proxies remain in memory. However, if you remove """"""""doLabelClick,"""""""" this issue is gone. This is a serious problem. Please investigate.""""""",Bug,"Title: ListView - Handling Events on Template Views causing Memory Leak!
Description: """"Reference: https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Alloy_ListView_Guide-section-40928632_AlloyListViewGuide-HandlingEventsonTemplateViews Create a default Alloy project with the following: index.xml index.js sample.xml sample.js Use XCode Instrument to monitor Allocations. Open and Close the sample window. You'll see the sample window view proxies remain in memory. However, if you remove """"""""doLabelClick,"""""""" this issue is gone. This is a serious problem. Please investigate.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19868,12,"""iOS rebuild 'forced' all the time""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce I seem to get a full rebuild each and every time I click the Run button, even without making any change to any source for config file.  My app is using Ti SDK 4.1.1 and I'm building (from within <USER>Studio) using CLI 5.0.3 tools.   I think this problem has existed since the 5.0.0 at least.  h3. Actual Result ``` [INFO] :   Forcing rebuild: /Users/conny/Documents/MyTitaniumApp/build/iphone/build-manifest.json does not exist ```   h3. Expected Result I don't know what it looks like but I would expect a line saying 'found valid existing build, will re-package and launch again...' or something similar? """"""",Improvement,"Title: iOS rebuild 'forced' all the time
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce I seem to get a full rebuild each and every time I click the Run button, even without making any change to any source for config file. My app is using Ti SDK 4.1.1 and I'm building (from within <USER>Studio) using CLI 5.0.3 tools. I think this problem has existed since the 5.0.0 at least. h3. Actual Result ``` [INFO] : Forcing rebuild: /Users/conny/Documents/MyTitaniumApp/build/iphone/build-manifest.json does not exist ``` h3. Expected Result I don't know what it looks like but I would expect a line saying 'found valid existing build, will re-package and launch again...' or something similar? """"",title+description
TIMOB-19866,12,"""iOS: PreviewContext with no previews crashes or freezes app""","""""""When you have no {{preview}} property set for the preview context then the app will crash or - what I saw in the 3D touch app - it will freeze showing the blur effect.    Of course the developer should know it needs a preview, but now we have peek/pop events its easy to make the assumption you could set the preview from the peek-event. So it would be a better dev experience if we provide better feedback then this crash.        *log*    """"""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: PreviewContext with no previews crashes or freezes app
Description: """"When you have no {{preview}} property set for the preview context then the app will crash or - what I saw in the 3D touch app - it will freeze showing the blur effect. Of course the developer should know it needs a preview, but now we have peek/pop events its easy to make the assumption you could set the preview from the peek-event. So it would be a better dev experience if we provide better feedback then this crash. *log* """"",title+description
TIMOB-19863,12,"""iOS9: ListView not filling screen width""","""""""ListView not filling screen width. Occured after updating to the new XCode version    iPad - Landscape  !Screenshot1.png|thumbnail!  Looks like there is some sort of inset being applied?    Test  index.xml      index.tss    {code:tss}  """"""""#listView"""""""":{   style: Ti.UI.iPhone.ListViewStyle.GROUPED  }    """"""""#icon"""""""" : {      width: '50dp', height: '50dp', left: 0  },  """"""""#title"""""""" : {      color: 'black',      font: { fontFamily:'Arial', fontSize: '20dp', fontWeight:'bold' },      left: '60dp', top: 0  },  """"""""#subtitle"""""""" : {      color: 'gray',      font: { fontFamily:'Arial', fontSize: '14dp' },      left: '60dp', top: '25dp'  }  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS9: ListView not filling screen width
Description: """"ListView not filling screen width. Occured after updating to the new XCode version iPad - Landscape !Screenshot1.png|thumbnail! Looks like there is some sort of inset being applied? Test index.xml index.tss {code:tss} """"""""#listView"""""""":{ style: Ti.UI.iPhone.ListViewStyle.GROUPED } """"""""#icon"""""""" : { width: '50dp', height: '50dp', left: 0 }, """"""""#title"""""""" : { color: 'black', font: { fontFamily:'Arial', fontSize: '20dp', fontWeight:'bold' }, left: '60dp', top: 0 }, """"""""#subtitle"""""""" : { color: 'gray', font: { fontFamily:'Arial', fontSize: '14dp' }, left: '60dp', top: '25dp' } {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-19862,12,"""Semicolon in setUsername causes no username to be logged""","""""""Calling {{apm.setUsername(""""""""something;something"""""""")}} causes no username to be set in the performance monitoring. The crash logs have no username set and the username is unable to be found via search.    I expected something other than it just not working to happen - an error when calling setUsername, the semicolon to be stripped out, or it to just work. For it to appear to work and then just absolutely do nothing is definitely frustrating. It took me a while to figure out what was wrong. Also, it is not documented that semicolons are not allowed in the username (probably because it was unintentional, I'm guessing).""""""",Bug,"Title: Semicolon in setUsername causes no username to be logged
Description: """"Calling {{apm.setUsername(""""""""something;something"""""""")}} causes no username to be set in the performance monitoring. The crash logs have no username set and the username is unable to be found via search. I expected something other than it just not working to happen - an error when calling setUsername, the semicolon to be stripped out, or it to just work. For it to appear to work and then just absolutely do nothing is definitely frustrating. It took me a while to figure out what was wrong. Also, it is not documented that semicolons are not allowed in the username (probably because it was unintentional, I'm guessing).""""",title+description
TIMOB-19861,12,"""Alloy Collection - Dealing two or more collections at the same time causes memory leak""","""""""Create a default Alloy project with the following:    index.js      index.xml      models/samplea.js      models/sampleb.js      Using xCode instrument """"""""Leaks"""""""" to monitor the app. Soon after launching the app, there appear several leaked objects.""""""",Bug,"Title: Alloy Collection - Dealing two or more collections at the same time causes memory leak
Description: """"Create a default Alloy project with the following: index.js index.xml models/samplea.js models/sampleb.js Using xCode instrument """"""""Leaks"""""""" to monitor the app. Soon after launching the app, there appear several leaked objects.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19860,12,"""Titanium local differ between simulator to device""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce  iPad ios 9.0.2 Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de-DE Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE  ios 8.4 simulator Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE  h3. Actual Result  iPad ios 9.0.2 Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de-DE Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE  ios 8.4 simulator Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE  h3. Expected Result  iPad ios 9.0.2 Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de-DE Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE  ios 8.4 simulator Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de << With 2 letters as documented Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium local differ between simulator to device
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce iPad ios 9.0.2 Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de-DE Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE ios 8.4 simulator Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE h3. Actual Result iPad ios 9.0.2 Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de-DE Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE ios 8.4 simulator Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE h3. Expected Result iPad ios 9.0.2 Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de-DE Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE ios 8.4 simulator Ti.Locale.currentLanguage: de << With 2 letters as documented Ti.Locale.currentLocale: de-DE""""",title+description
TIMOB-19855,12,"""Android 6.0 : Row height in a TableView on android 6.0 is abnormally big""","""""""h5.Steps To Reproduce:  1. Use the code below in the app.js:    2. Build for android 6.0 device / emulator.  3. After the app launches check out the row height.    h5.Actual Results:  1. The row height is big, equal to the visible area of the app.   2. Works fine with android 5.1.1    h5.Expected Results:  1. The row height should not be abnormally big.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android 6.0 : Row height in a TableView on android 6.0 is abnormally big
Description: """"h5.Steps To Reproduce: 1. Use the code below in the app.js: 2. Build for android 6.0 device / emulator. 3. After the app launches check out the row height. h5.Actual Results: 1. The row height is big, equal to the visible area of the app. 2. Works fine with android 5.1.1 h5.Expected Results: 1. The row height should not be abnormally big. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19854,12,"""Android: Prompt user to update installed app when installed with different cert""","""""""I'm not sure how often people will run into this, but I see it a lot switching back and forth between my hyperloop module/Android SDK app, and a different version of the app from Titanium SDK/Studio.    The ADT tooling is smart enough to know when the app is already installed with a different cert and allows me to force delete/overwrite it. Studio and our CLI just fail with:  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Prompt user to update installed app when installed with different cert
Description: """"I'm not sure how often people will run into this, but I see it a lot switching back and forth between my hyperloop module/Android SDK app, and a different version of the app from Titanium SDK/Studio. The ADT tooling is smart enough to know when the app is already installed with a different cert and allows me to force delete/overwrite it. Studio and our CLI just fail with: """"",title+description
TIMOB-19852,12,"""Android: Media - automatically add necessary permissions to tiapp.xml""","""""""h2. Request    Note, Marshall asked me to raise this.    Currently, media permissions must be explicitly configured in tiapp.xml in order to access the calendar.    Just as is done for other APIs, add permissions automatically during the build <USER>    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Media - automatically add necessary permissions to tiapp.xml
Description: """"h2. Request Note, Marshall asked me to raise this. Currently, media permissions must be explicitly configured in tiapp.xml in order to access the calendar. Just as is done for other APIs, add permissions automatically during the build <USER> """"",title+description
TIMOB-19851,12,"""Android: Permissions (Camera) crash and other bugs""","""""""The following sample will always call back with {{success:false}} without showing the dialog:        To make it work you need to declare the permission in {{tiapp.xml}}, which is not documented in either the [Ti.Media Reference|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media] nor [Camera and Photo Gallery APIs Guide|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Camera_and_Photo_Gallery_APIs] or [tiapp.xml Common Requirements|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference-section-29004921_tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-CommonRequirements].        If you do so Android 6+ will prompt for two permissions:    !android_20151103-113339.png|thumbnail!    The first time after each new install I deny either one of two the callback will receive {{success:true}} but the next call to {{Ti.Media.hasCameraPermissions()}} will still return {{false}} and {{Ti.Media.requestCameraPermissions()}} will again prompt for both permissions, including the one I already granted.    After the first time I deny only one of two permissions, every next time I do the exact same thing the app crashes with the attached log as soon as I deny the first or second permission.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Permissions (Camera) crash and other bugs
Description: """"The following sample will always call back with {{success:false}} without showing the dialog: To make it work you need to declare the permission in {{tiapp.xml}}, which is not documented in either the [Ti.Media Reference|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media] nor [Camera and Photo Gallery APIs Guide|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Camera_and_Photo_Gallery_APIs] or [tiapp.xml Common Requirements|https://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference-section-29004921_tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-CommonRequirements]. If you do so Android 6+ will prompt for two permissions: !android_20151103-113339.png|thumbnail! The first time after each new install I deny either one of two the callback will receive {{success:true}} but the next call to {{Ti.Media.hasCameraPermissions()}} will still return {{false}} and {{Ti.Media.requestCameraPermissions()}} will again prompt for both permissions, including the one I already granted. After the first time I deny only one of two permissions, every next time I do the exact same thing the app crashes with the attached log as soon as I deny the first or second permission.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19849,12,"""Android: Contacts - automatically add necessary permissions to tiapp.xml""","""""""h2. Request    Note, Marshall asked me to raise this.    Currently, contacts permissions must be explicitly configured in tiapp.xml in order to access the contacts.    Just as is done for other APIs, add permissions automatically during the build <USER>    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Contacts - automatically add necessary permissions to tiapp.xml
Description: """"h2. Request Note, Marshall asked me to raise this. Currently, contacts permissions must be explicitly configured in tiapp.xml in order to access the contacts. Just as is done for other APIs, add permissions automatically during the build <USER> """"",title+description
TIMOB-19847,12,"""Image won't upload from Android to ArrowDB using API 5.0+""","""""""If you create a photo object in ArrowDB using an android device, the following error occurs when you try to upload with version 5.0+ of the Titanium API. The SAME CODE running 4.0 - < 5.0 works when uploading an image to Arrow DB. When using 5.0+, I get the following JSON error response after uploading an image:    {""""""""success"""""""" : false, """"""""error"""""""" : true, """"""""code"""""""" : 400, """"""""message"""""""" : """"""""Failed to upload photo: Cannot serialize an object of class ActionDispatch::Http::UploadedFile in BSON.""""""""}      """"""",Bug,"Title: Image won't upload from Android to ArrowDB using API 5.0+
Description: """"If you create a photo object in ArrowDB using an android device, the following error occurs when you try to upload with version 5.0+ of the Titanium API. The SAME CODE running 4.0 - < 5.0 works when uploading an image to Arrow DB. When using 5.0+, I get the following JSON error response after uploading an image: {""""""""success"""""""" : false, """"""""error"""""""" : true, """"""""code"""""""" : 400, """"""""message"""""""" : """"""""Failed to upload photo: Cannot serialize an object of class ActionDispatch::Http::UploadedFile in BSON.""""""""} """"",title+description
TIMOB-19846,12,"""Android fix documentation errors in activity transition.""","""""""Fix documentation errors for activity transition and its methods.     [ERROR] ./Titanium/UI/Window.yml  Titanium.UI.Window: found 1 error(s)!      methods          addSharedElement              parameters                  view                      type                          View    [ERROR] ./Titanium/UI/Window.yml  openWindowParams: found 8 error(s)!      properties          activityExitTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*          activityEnterTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*          activityReturnTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*          activityReenterTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*          activitySharedElementExitTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*          activitySharedElementEnterTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*          activitySharedElementReturnTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*          activitySharedElementReenterTransition              constants                  Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*""""""",Bug,"Title: Android fix documentation errors in activity transition.
Description: """"Fix documentation errors for activity transition and its methods. [ERROR] ./Titanium/UI/Window.yml Titanium.UI.Window: found 1 error(s)! methods addSharedElement parameters view type View [ERROR] ./Titanium/UI/Window.yml openWindowParams: found 8 error(s)! properties activityExitTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_* activityEnterTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_* activityReturnTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_* activityReenterTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_* activitySharedElementExitTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_* activitySharedElementEnterTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_* activitySharedElementReturnTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_* activitySharedElementReenterTransition constants Invalid constant: Titanium.UI.Android.TRANSITION_*""""",title+description
TIMOB-19845,12,"""Android: Generate separate ARM and ARMv7a versions of V8 static library""","""""""We currently generate a single ARM static library. There are GYP flags we can set to turn on usage of ARMv7 floating point operations. We should generate a version of the lib with this on and off.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Generate separate ARM and ARMv7a versions of V8 static library
Description: """"We currently generate a single ARM static library. There are GYP flags we can set to turn on usage of ARMv7 floating point operations. We should generate a version of the lib with this on and off.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19844,12,"""Android: If either uses-permission is missing hasCalendarPermissions will always be false but requestCalendarPermissions returns success""","""""""Until TIMOB-7949 is resolved you have to manually add this to your tiapp.xml:        But if either is missing (e.g. because you don't need WRITE) weird stuff happens:    1. {{Ti.Calendar.hasCalendarPermissions()}} will always be {{false}}  2. {{Ti.Calendar.requestCalendarPermissions}} will always show the dialog and if you grant permissions call back with {{success:true}}.    I'd assume {{Ti.Calendar.requestCalendarPermissions}} to always call back with {{success:false}} - as it does when you don't have either {{user-permission}} in place.    I think the best approach is to resolve TIMOB-7949 and with that this one as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: If either uses-permission is missing hasCalendarPermissions will always be false but requestCalendarPermissions returns success
Description: """"Until TIMOB-7949 is resolved you have to manually add this to your tiapp.xml: But if either is missing (e.g. because you don't need WRITE) weird stuff happens: 1. {{Ti.Calendar.hasCalendarPermissions()}} will always be {{false}} 2. {{Ti.Calendar.requestCalendarPermissions}} will always show the dialog and if you grant permissions call back with {{success:true}}. I'd assume {{Ti.Calendar.requestCalendarPermissions}} to always call back with {{success:false}} - as it does when you don't have either {{user-permission}} in place. I think the best approach is to resolve TIMOB-7949 and with that this one as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19839,12,"""iOS: Support multiple cell selection in Ti.UI.ListView""","""""""Currently, we cover all {{UITableView}} properties except the following for the multiple selection of {{UITableViewCells}}.     *New properties*:  - {{allowsMultipleSelection}}  - {{allowsSelectionDuringEditing}}  - {{allowsMultipleSelectionDuringEditing}}    *Docs*:  https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UITableView_Class/#//apple_ref/occ/instp/UITableView/allowsMultipleSelection    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Support multiple cell selection in Ti.UI.ListView
Description: """"Currently, we cover all {{UITableView}} properties except the following for the multiple selection of {{UITableViewCells}}. *New properties*: - {{allowsMultipleSelection}} - {{allowsSelectionDuringEditing}} - {{allowsMultipleSelectionDuringEditing}} *Docs*: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UITableView_Class/#//apple_ref/occ/instp/UITableView/allowsMultipleSelection """"",title+description
TIMOB-19835,12,"""iPad: Separator Insets Ignored on Left Side""","""""""h1. Problem  The separator insets for a list view, which work on iPhone, aren't working on iPads. They seem to have a minimum value for the left, and any value I set less than about 50 is ignored. Also, the insets for the empty rows after the defined rows show the opposite problem -- the inset is messed up on the right side.    See the attached screenshots.    h2. Expected Behavior  If I set the insets to 0, they should reach from edge to edge.    h2. Reproduction    """"""",Bug,"Title: iPad: Separator Insets Ignored on Left Side
Description: """"h1. Problem The separator insets for a list view, which work on iPhone, aren't working on iPads. They seem to have a minimum value for the left, and any value I set less than about 50 is ignored. Also, the insets for the empty rows after the defined rows show the opposite problem -- the inset is messed up on the right side. See the attached screenshots. h2. Expected Behavior If I set the insets to 0, they should reach from edge to edge. h2. Reproduction """"",title+description
TIMOB-19834,12,"""Support ES6 for Titanium Application Development""","""""""ES6 is the new standard for JavaScript that introduces a ton of feature improvements to the language structure. These include Classes, Generators, Modules,  syntax improvements and much much more!    Areas of Focus will be:  * Titanium  * Alloy  * Arrow (should work now with Node 4.x+ support but need to verify)    """"""",Epic,"Title: Support ES6 for Titanium Application Development
Description: """"ES6 is the new standard for JavaScript that introduces a ton of feature improvements to the language structure. These include Classes, Generators, Modules, syntax improvements and much much more! Areas of Focus will be: * Titanium * Alloy * Arrow (should work now with Node 4.x+ support but need to verify) """"",title+description
TIMOB-19832,12,"""Incremental build after removing image leaves empty .imageasset folder""","""""""Probably not harmful (though I haven't tested what happens if you would reference the file somewhere) but something I noticed while doing tests:    *Steps*    # Build https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-3dtouch  # Verify {{build/iphone/Assets/xcassets/6ce9fb071294c440a20ff73b7c09fef2082c2206.imageset}} is there and not empty  # Remove the three {{shortcutItemIcon.png}} images in {{app/assets/iphone/images/}}  # Build again  # Verify {{build/iphone/Assets/xcassets/6ce9fb071294c440a20ff73b7c09fef2082c2206.imageset}} is still there but now empty""""""",Bug,"Title: Incremental build after removing image leaves empty .imageasset folder
Description: """"Probably not harmful (though I haven't tested what happens if you would reference the file somewhere) but something I noticed while doing tests: *Steps* # Build https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-3dtouch # Verify {{build/iphone/Assets/xcassets/6ce9fb071294c440a20ff73b7c09fef2082c2206.imageset}} is there and not empty # Remove the three {{shortcutItemIcon.png}} images in {{app/assets/iphone/images/}} # Build again # Verify {{build/iphone/Assets/xcassets/6ce9fb071294c440a20ff73b7c09fef2082c2206.imageset}} is still there but now empty""""",title+description
TIMOB-19829,12,"""iOS: Add trackTintColor to Ti.UI.ProgressBar""","""""""Currently, the {{Ti.UI.ProgressBar}} on iOS support coloring options for the active progress. This improvement allows to also set the {{trackTintColor}} to cover color of the tracked progress.    *Demo*:  """"""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Add trackTintColor to Ti.UI.ProgressBar
Description: """"Currently, the {{Ti.UI.ProgressBar}} on iOS support coloring options for the active progress. This improvement allows to also set the {{trackTintColor}} to cover color of the tracked progress. *Demo*: """"",title+description
TIMOB-19827,12,"""Allow object type in Ti.UI.OptionDialog.options""","""""""It is currently not possible to use image options inside the {{Ti.UI.OptionDialog}}. The proposal is to introduce support those by making the {{options}} property ready to hold either string- or object-values. That needs changes on both iOS and Android to achieve parity.    *Proposal*:   """"""",Improvement,"Title: Allow object type in Ti.UI.OptionDialog.options
Description: """"It is currently not possible to use image options inside the {{Ti.UI.OptionDialog}}. The proposal is to introduce support those by making the {{options}} property ready to hold either string- or object-values. That needs changes on both iOS and Android to achieve parity. *Proposal*: """"",title+description
TIMOB-19824,12,"""Automatically call needsSave when user activity is updated""","""""""In TIMOB-19567 we concluded we can't support the official route for updating an user activity:    1. Listen to {{useractivitywillsave}}.  2. Set {{needsSave:true}} each time you have a change.  3. Update the user activity with the actual change when {{useractivitywillsave}} is fired.    Instead you now have to:    1. Update the user activity each time you have a change.  2. Set {{needsSave:true}} each time you have a change.    I'd request that we take care of step 2 for the users and set the property automatically when the users updates the user activity.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Automatically call needsSave when user activity is updated
Description: """"In TIMOB-19567 we concluded we can't support the official route for updating an user activity: 1. Listen to {{useractivitywillsave}}. 2. Set {{needsSave:true}} each time you have a change. 3. Update the user activity with the actual change when {{useractivitywillsave}} is fired. Instead you now have to: 1. Update the user activity each time you have a change. 2. Set {{needsSave:true}} each time you have a change. I'd request that we take care of step 2 for the users and set the property automatically when the users updates the user activity.""""",title+description
