TIMOB-19772,12,"""Prompt user to accept Xcode license agreement in response to """"Error 69"""" in debug log""","""""""If Xcode needs a license to be accepted, you will get the following error:        You will see this in the build log:  [TRACE]  Agreeing to the Xcode/iOS license requires admin privileges, please re-run as root via sudo.    However, error """"""""69"""""""" seems to be indicative of this specific problem. We should catch that error value and correctly prompt the user to accept the license agreement.    If we want to be truly elegant, we can do """"""""sudo xcrun cc"""""""" and prompt the user ourselves.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Prompt user to accept Xcode license agreement in response to """"Error 69"""" in debug log
Description: """"If Xcode needs a license to be accepted, you will get the following error: You will see this in the build log: [TRACE] Agreeing to the Xcode/iOS license requires admin privileges, please re-run as root via sudo. However, error """"""""69"""""""" seems to be indicative of this specific problem. We should catch that error value and correctly prompt the user to accept the license agreement. If we want to be truly elegant, we can do """"""""sudo xcrun cc"""""""" and prompt the user ourselves.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19764,12,"""previewContext does not work when set while modal window is open or closing""","""""""In the 3D Touch sample app we have to use a {{setTimeout()}} of ~500ms to delay the rendering of the list (and as part of that setting the previewContext on each thumbnail) after finishing selecting a picture from the device's Photo Gallery. If we don't than Peek and Pop will not work.    This happens only with Camera, Photo Gallery or another modal window. If non-modal window is open while we set previewContext it does work.    Sample code: https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-3dtouch/blob/master/app/controllers/list.js#L81""""""",Bug,"Title: previewContext does not work when set while modal window is open or closing
Description: """"In the 3D Touch sample app we have to use a {{setTimeout()}} of ~500ms to delay the rendering of the list (and as part of that setting the previewContext on each thumbnail) after finishing selecting a picture from the device's Photo Gallery. If we don't than Peek and Pop will not work. This happens only with Camera, Photo Gallery or another modal window. If non-modal window is open while we set previewContext it does work. Sample code: https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-3dtouch/blob/master/app/controllers/list.js#L81""""",title+description
TIMOB-19763,12,"""iOS: Support item-specific peek for previewContext on ListView""","""""""Our current implementation of [Ti.UI.iOS.PreviewContext.preview|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iOS.PreviewContext-property-preview] does not allow you to render a specific preview for a list item / row when used with [ListView.previewContext|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-property-previewContext] or the same property for TableView. This is because the view must be created when you create the previewContext object.    The wrapped [UIPreviewAction|https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIPreviewAction_Class/index.html#//apple_ref/occ/instp/UIPreviewAction/handler] has a handler handler to construct the view when it is actually required. It seems like we should make our {{preview}} property a callback as well that receives the section and item index/id and either returns a view directly or via another callback passed to it.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Support item-specific peek for previewContext on ListView
Description: """"Our current implementation of [Ti.UI.iOS.PreviewContext.preview|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iOS.PreviewContext-property-preview] does not allow you to render a specific preview for a list item / row when used with [ListView.previewContext|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-property-previewContext] or the same property for TableView. This is because the view must be created when you create the previewContext object. The wrapped [UIPreviewAction|https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIPreviewAction_Class/index.html#//apple_ref/occ/instp/UIPreviewAction/handler] has a handler handler to construct the view when it is actually required. It seems like we should make our {{preview}} property a callback as well that receives the section and item index/id and either returns a view directly or via another callback passed to it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19756,12,"""iOS9 LiveView error: Failed to copy app to device (0xe8000005) ""","""""""When building a new Classic project to an iOS9 device with LiveView enabled, the following error is received:        This error does not occur on android device / emulators, or iOS simulators (8.4 & 9.0). a different error is thrown when building a project to an 8.4 device with liveView enabled:  [https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-19749]    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a *Classic* project.  2. Build to 9.0 device.      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS9 LiveView error: Failed to copy app to device (0xe8000005)
Description: """"When building a new Classic project to an iOS9 device with LiveView enabled, the following error is received: This error does not occur on android device / emulators, or iOS simulators (8.4 & 9.0). a different error is thrown when building a project to an 8.4 device with liveView enabled: [https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-19749] *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a *Classic* project. 2. Build to 9.0 device. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19752,12,"""Add support for mutual ssl authentication ""","""""""It would be nice if users of the Titanium SDK could take advantage of the added security that is available by using Mutual (2way) authentication.     Right now it doesn't not appear possible to provide the server with a PFX certificate to prove the clients identity.     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mutual_authentication""""""",Improvement,"Title: Add support for mutual ssl authentication
Description: """"It would be nice if users of the Titanium SDK could take advantage of the added security that is available by using Mutual (2way) authentication. Right now it doesn't not appear possible to provide the server with a PFX certificate to prove the clients identity. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mutual_authentication""""",title+description
TIMOB-19750,12,"""TiSDK 4.1 Example App doesn't run with Visual Studio 2015 Community on Windows 10...""","""""""I'm trying to get the Ti SDK 4.1 Example App and eventually my app built under Windows 10  I have <USER>Studio, build: 4.1.1.201507141126 installed on Windows 10 Pro (released)  No <USER>updates were found  OS Name Microsoft Windows 10 Pro  Version 10.0.10240 Build 10240  The Windows, Android and Mobile Web SDKs are installed  I have Visual Studio 2015 Community version 14.0.23107.0 D14REL installed  When I run the Windows Phone Developer Power Tools 8.1 I can connect to an emulator  I have """"""""Debug"""""""" selected in the """"""""Run/Debug/Profile/Test/Package"""""""" dropdown  I have tried selecting several of the windows mobile emulators including """"""""Emulator 8.1 1080P 5.5 inch"""""""" and """"""""Emulator 10.0.10240.0 720p 5 inch 1 GB"""""""" from the target drop down list.  When I click on the green """"""""Debug"""""""" button absolutely nothing happens in the console window even if the emulator is already launched from the Power Tools  I noticed that node 0.12.2 was installed already so I installed nvmw and node v0.10.13 which is working properly on my Mac. However the problem still persists. I click on the """"""""Debug"""""""" button and nothing happens.    When I run app run -p windows -C """"""""Emulator 8.1 1080P 6 inch"""""""" I do get some output. I get an error that says    CMake error at CMakeLists.txt:15 (project):  A windows Phone component with CMake requires both the Windows Desktop SDK  as well as the Windows Phone """"""""8.1"""""""" SDK. Please make sure that you have  both installed.    Since I have Visual Studio Community 2015 Version 14.0.23107.0 D14REL (release version) installed I believe that the SDKs must be there and <USER>Studio just doesn't know where to find them.    I have the Windows SDK Home: preference set to """"""""C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft SDKs"""""""" which is what I assume it should be so I'm not sure what to try next.  """"""",Bug,"Title: TiSDK 4.1 Example App doesn't run with Visual Studio 2015 Community on Windows 10...
Description: """"I'm trying to get the Ti SDK 4.1 Example App and eventually my app built under Windows 10 I have <USER>Studio, build: 4.1.1.201507141126 installed on Windows 10 Pro (released) No <USER>updates were found OS Name Microsoft Windows 10 Pro Version 10.0.10240 Build 10240 The Windows, Android and Mobile Web SDKs are installed I have Visual Studio 2015 Community version 14.0.23107.0 D14REL installed When I run the Windows Phone Developer Power Tools 8.1 I can connect to an emulator I have """"""""Debug"""""""" selected in the """"""""Run/Debug/Profile/Test/Package"""""""" dropdown I have tried selecting several of the windows mobile emulators including """"""""Emulator 8.1 1080P 5.5 inch"""""""" and """"""""Emulator 10.0.10240.0 720p 5 inch 1 GB"""""""" from the target drop down list. When I click on the green """"""""Debug"""""""" button absolutely nothing happens in the console window even if the emulator is already launched from the Power Tools I noticed that node 0.12.2 was installed already so I installed nvmw and node v0.10.13 which is working properly on my Mac. However the problem still persists. I click on the """"""""Debug"""""""" button and nothing happens. When I run app run -p windows -C """"""""Emulator 8.1 1080P 6 inch"""""""" I do get some output. I get an error that says CMake error at CMakeLists.txt:15 (project): A windows Phone component with CMake requires both the Windows Desktop SDK as well as the Windows Phone """"""""8.1"""""""" SDK. Please make sure that you have both installed. Since I have Visual Studio Community 2015 Version 14.0.23107.0 D14REL (release version) installed I believe that the SDKs must be there and <USER>Studio just doesn't know where to find them. I have the Windows SDK Home: preference set to """"""""C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft SDKs"""""""" which is what I assume it should be so I'm not sure what to try next. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19749,12,"""LiveView enabled fails to build to iOS 8.4 device: """"Could not find the file app.js""""""","""""""When building a *Classic* project to an iOS 8.4 device with LiveView enabled, the app successfully installs to the device, however upon launch, the following error is thrown:        The error does not occur when building an alloy project to an 8.4 device.  The error does not occur when building to a 9.0 device, or an 8.4 simulator.   The error does not occur when building the same *Classic* project to the same device, with LiveView disabled.    *Update:* In some cases, the app will fail on first build, but it has been reported that in other cases the app will launch successfully on first build, but will fail on an incremental build.      *Steps to reproduce:*  1.Create a *Classic* project.  2. Run to an 8.4 device.  3. Launch app.    *Actual Result:*  app fails to launch successfully either upon first build, or incremental builds.    *Expected Result:*  app should launch successfully, and changes made should correctly update the app with LiveView enabled.""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView enabled fails to build to iOS 8.4 device: """"Could not find the file app.js""""
Description: """"When building a *Classic* project to an iOS 8.4 device with LiveView enabled, the app successfully installs to the device, however upon launch, the following error is thrown: The error does not occur when building an alloy project to an 8.4 device. The error does not occur when building to a 9.0 device, or an 8.4 simulator. The error does not occur when building the same *Classic* project to the same device, with LiveView disabled. *Update:* In some cases, the app will fail on first build, but it has been reported that in other cases the app will launch successfully on first build, but will fail on an incremental build. *Steps to reproduce:* 1.Create a *Classic* project. 2. Run to an 8.4 device. 3. Launch app. *Actual Result:* app fails to launch successfully either upon first build, or incremental builds. *Expected Result:* app should launch successfully, and changes made should correctly update the app with LiveView enabled.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19748,12,"""Unable to prohibit TabGroup scrolling""","""""""After upgrading Titanium SDK 5.0.2.GA TapGroup become scrollable and only 3 tap is visible. User should scroll to view other Taps,     There is no way to stop or disable Tap scroll and keep it like before.       """"""",Bug,"Title: Unable to prohibit TabGroup scrolling
