TIMOB-19728,12,"""iOS Simulator is launched and closed ok debug mode<terminated, exit value: 1>iOS build and deploy""","""""""h6. Issue Description    When trying to run a project in debug mode on iOS, <USER>Studio terminates the debug thread.    Here is the error:    <USER>iOS Simulator - iPhone 6s - DebugTest [<USER>iOS Simulator]   <terminated>iOS JS Debugger   Thread [main] (Terminated)   iOS build and deploy   <terminated, exit value: -1>DebugTest    h6.Steps to reproduce   1- create a sample app project  2. run as debug mode  3. The app is terminated the messages on the debug tab:     <USER>iOS Simulator - iPhone 6s - DebugTest [<USER>iOS Simulator]   <terminated>iOS JS Debugger   Thread [main] (Terminated)   iOS build and deploy   <terminated, exit value: -1>DebugTest    In other debug builds the error is the next:     [ERROR] :  Error connecting to debugger: Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=57 """"""""Socket is not connected""""""""      **Log file is attached  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS Simulator is launched and closed ok debug mode<terminated, exit value: 1>iOS build and deploy
Description: """"h6. Issue Description When trying to run a project in debug mode on iOS, <USER>Studio terminates the debug thread. Here is the error: <USER>iOS Simulator - iPhone 6s - DebugTest [<USER>iOS Simulator] <terminated>iOS JS Debugger Thread [main] (Terminated) iOS build and deploy <terminated, exit value: -1>DebugTest h6.Steps to reproduce 1- create a sample app project 2. run as debug mode 3. The app is terminated the messages on the debug tab: <USER>iOS Simulator - iPhone 6s - DebugTest [<USER>iOS Simulator] <terminated>iOS JS Debugger Thread [main] (Terminated) iOS build and deploy <terminated, exit value: -1>DebugTest In other debug builds the error is the next: [ERROR] : Error connecting to debugger: Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=57 """"""""Socket is not connected"""""""" **Log file is attached """"",title+description
TIMOB-19726,12,"""Android: Refactor map module to remove deprecated method getMap()""","""""""getMap() method is deprecated, we need to use getMapAsync() instead.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Refactor map module to remove deprecated method getMap()
Description: """"getMap() method is deprecated, we need to use getMapAsync() instead.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19718,12,"""Building app to iOS8 installs successfully but fails on launch""","""""""When building a classic / alloy project to either an iOS8 device or simulator, the app successfully installs, however fails to launch and returns to the main screen. The following error occurs on each attempt to launch the app from the device:       *Steps to Reproduce:*  1. Create a Classic / Alloy project.  2. Build to either iOS8 device or sim.  3. Launch app, receive error.    *Expected Result:* App should launch successfully with no errors.    *Actual Result:* App fails to launch and throws an error.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Building app to iOS8 installs successfully but fails on launch
Description: """"When building a classic / alloy project to either an iOS8 device or simulator, the app successfully installs, however fails to launch and returns to the main screen. The following error occurs on each attempt to launch the app from the device: *Steps to Reproduce:* 1. Create a Classic / Alloy project. 2. Build to either iOS8 device or sim. 3. Launch app, receive error. *Expected Result:* App should launch successfully with no errors. *Actual Result:* App fails to launch and throws an error. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19715,12,"""SDK 5.1.0.CI crashed when run on iOS 8.4""","""""""An iOS 8.4 Simulator crashes when using 5.1.0 CI, likely due to {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts}} implementation.    *Code*        *Console* (see attached crash log)        The crash log points to:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/c2f83a627787ea90e936545ecd77f784f1109199/iphone/Classes/TiApp.m#L415-L421    So probably we need a device OS version check as well there. After this has been fixed it needs another test round to see if we haven't got similar code elsewhere.""""""",Bug,"Title: SDK 5.1.0.CI crashed when run on iOS 8.4
Description: """"An iOS 8.4 Simulator crashes when using 5.1.0 CI, likely due to {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts}} implementation. *Code* *Console* (see attached crash log) The crash log points to: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/c2f83a627787ea90e936545ecd77f784f1109199/iphone/Classes/TiApp.m#L415-L421 So probably we need a device OS version check as well there. After this has been fixed it needs another test round to see if we haven't got similar code elsewhere.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19714,12,"""Add Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.getDynamicShortcut()""","""""""I'd find it useful to have {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.getDynamicShortcut(type)}} so that I can check if the userInfo of that shortcut is what I want it to be or if I need to remove and add one with another.    It would be even more useful if I could update the userInfo property on the object returned, but then it would need to be a full proxy instead of a JS object so that would be more work.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Add Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.getDynamicShortcut()
Description: """"I'd find it useful to have {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.getDynamicShortcut(type)}} so that I can check if the userInfo of that shortcut is what I want it to be or if I need to remove and add one with another. It would be even more useful if I could update the userInfo property on the object returned, but then it would need to be a full proxy instead of a JS object so that would be more work.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19713,12,"""Accept type instead of object with type for dynamicShortcutExists() and removeShortcutItem()""","""""""Would it make sense for {{dynamicShortcutExists()}} and {{removeShortcutItem()}} to accept a string type as arguments instead of an object with the type as the only property?""""""",Improvement,"Title: Accept type instead of object with type for dynamicShortcutExists() and removeShortcutItem()
Description: """"Would it make sense for {{dynamicShortcutExists()}} and {{removeShortcutItem()}} to accept a string type as arguments instead of an object with the type as the only property?""""",title+description
TIMOB-19712,12,"""Improve consistency of Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts method names""","""""""I think these names (changes in *bold*) would be more consistent:    * *addDynamicShortcut()* (was: addShortcutItem)  * dynamicShortcutExists()  * listDynamicShortcuts()  * listStaticShortcuts()  * removeAllDynamicShortcuts()  * *removeDynamicShortcut()* (was: removeShortcutItem)""""""",Improvement,"Title: Improve consistency of Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts method names
Description: """"I think these names (changes in *bold*) would be more consistent: * *addDynamicShortcut()* (was: addShortcutItem) * dynamicShortcutExists() * listDynamicShortcuts() * listStaticShortcuts() * removeAllDynamicShortcuts() * *removeDynamicShortcut()* (was: removeShortcutItem)""""",title+description
TIMOB-19711,12,"""Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listDynamicShortcuts() lacks icon""","""""""The dictionary that {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listDynamicShortcuts()}} returns lacks the icon. Perhaps this is related to the [duplicate code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/361f942eaa9372f1fa25bad0f395c2822eab68be/iphone/Classes/TiUIiOSApplicationShortcutsProxy.m#L19] and one of the duplicates should have been for the icon.    *JavaScript*        *Console*    """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listDynamicShortcuts() lacks icon
Description: """"The dictionary that {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listDynamicShortcuts()}} returns lacks the icon. Perhaps this is related to the [duplicate code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/361f942eaa9372f1fa25bad0f395c2822eab68be/iphone/Classes/TiUIiOSApplicationShortcutsProxy.m#L19] and one of the duplicates should have been for the icon. *JavaScript* *Console* """"",title+description
TIMOB-19710,12,"""Use same keys in Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listStaticShortcuts() as in listDynamicShortcuts()""","""""""Would it make sense to use the same keys in {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listStaticShortcuts()}} as in {{listDynamicShortcuts()}}?    """"""",Improvement,"Title: Use same keys in Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listStaticShortcuts() as in listDynamicShortcuts()
Description: """"Would it make sense to use the same keys in {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.listStaticShortcuts()}} as in {{listDynamicShortcuts()}}? """"",title+description
TIMOB-19709,12,"""Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.addDynamicShortcut icon does not work with custom images""","""""""When you use a custom image for {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.addDynamicShortcut()}} it won't work because the [source code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIiOSApplicationShortcutsProxy.m#L182] doesn't [hash the passed image path|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/7248/files] so it work with now we're generate asset catalogs for images with TIMOB-19296.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.addDynamicShortcut icon does not work with custom images
Description: """"When you use a custom image for {{Ti.UI.iOS.ApplicationShortcuts.addDynamicShortcut()}} it won't work because the [source code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIiOSApplicationShortcutsProxy.m#L182] doesn't [hash the passed image path|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/7248/files] so it work with now we're generate asset catalogs for images with TIMOB-19296. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19708,12,"""Ti.App.iOS:shortcutitemclick lacks shortcutitem type""","""""""If you define a shortcut in {{tiapp.xml}}:        The {{shortcutitemclick}} event will not have the shortcut's type, probably because it is overwritten by the event type:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.App.iOS:shortcutitemclick lacks shortcutitem type
Description: """"If you define a shortcut in {{tiapp.xml}}: The {{shortcutitemclick}} event will not have the shortcut's type, probably because it is overwritten by the event type: """"",title+description
TIMOB-19706,12,"""Prevent older previous major-version CLIs from using next major SDK version""","""""""⚡ ti create  Titanium Command-Line Interface, CLI version 4.0.1, Titanium SDK version 5.1.0  Copyright (c) 2012-2015, <USER> Inc.  All Rights Reserved.    Please report bugs to http://jira.<USER>org/    What type of project would you like to create?   1)  Titanium App   2)  Titanium Module   3)  Apple Watch™ App  Select a type by number or name [app]:    [INFO]  Creating app project  /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/titanium.js:671   platforms.toLowerCase().split(',').forEach(function (platform) {            ^  TypeError: Cannot read property 'toLowerCase' of undefined      at Object.exports.scrubPlatforms (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/titanium.js:671:11)      at AppCreator.run (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/cli/lib/creators/app.js:94:18)      at CreateCommand.<anonymous> (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/cli/commands/create.js:166:12)      at /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:689:13      at iterate (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:265:13)      at <USER>_tickCallback (node.js:355:11)    We should allow CLI 4.X to work with SDK <= 4.X. If attempting to use a newer 5.X version, let the user know they need to upgrade their CLI version.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Prevent older previous major-version CLIs from using next major SDK version
Description: """"⚡ ti create Titanium Command-Line Interface, CLI version 4.0.1, Titanium SDK version 5.1.0 Copyright (c) 2012-2015, <USER> Inc. All Rights Reserved. Please report bugs to http://jira.<USER>org/ What type of project would you like to create? 1) Titanium App 2) Titanium Module 3) Apple Watch™ App Select a type by number or name [app]: [INFO] Creating app project /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/titanium.js:671 platforms.toLowerCase().split(',').forEach(function (platform) { ^ TypeError: Cannot read property 'toLowerCase' of undefined at Object.exports.scrubPlatforms (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/titanium.js:671:11) at AppCreator.run (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/cli/lib/creators/app.js:94:18) at CreateCommand.<anonymous> (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/cli/commands/create.js:166:12) at /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:689:13 at iterate (/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/5.1.0/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:265:13) at <USER>_tickCallback (node.js:355:11) We should allow CLI 4.X to work with SDK <= 4.X. If attempting to use a newer 5.X version, let the user know they need to upgrade their CLI version.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19696,12,"""Use one term instead ActionBar, TitleBar and NavBar""","""""""We're using 3 different terms for the same thing:    * Action Bar: [guide|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Android_Action_Bar], [api|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Android.ActionBar]  * TitleBar: [guide|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Android_Action_Bar-section-36735509_AndroidActionBar-HidingtheActionBar], [titanium themes|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/search?utf8=✓&q=notitlebar], [android themes|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/R.style.html#Theme_NoTitleBar]  * NavBar: [tiapp.xml|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference-section-29004921_tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-navbar-hidden]    It is Android that already makes it confusing by using both ActionBar and TitleBar of course, so I'm not sure how/if we can improve this. Just leaving it here if we think of a good way.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Use one term instead ActionBar, TitleBar and NavBar
Description: """"We're using 3 different terms for the same thing: * Action Bar: [guide|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Android_Action_Bar], [api|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Android.ActionBar] * TitleBar: [guide|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Android_Action_Bar-section-36735509_AndroidActionBar-HidingtheActionBar], [titanium themes|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/search?utf8=✓&q=notitlebar], [android themes|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/R.style.html#Theme_NoTitleBar] * NavBar: [tiapp.xml|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference-section-29004921_tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-navbar-hidden] It is Android that already makes it confusing by using both ActionBar and TitleBar of course, so I'm not sure how/if we can improve this. Just leaving it here if we think of a good way.""""",title+description
