TIMOB-19668,12,"""iOS simulator is not started on build and run""","""""""h6.Issue Description    iOS simulator is not started on build and run    h6.Issue Description    1. Open <USER>Studio   2. Choose """"""""Run"""""""" configuration on """"""""iPad 2 (v8.4)"""""""" simulator   3. Press play button (normally this builds and then launches the simulator)   4. Wait for application to finish building and launch the simulator   5. Note that the build completes but the simulator does not launch     **appc info and logs are attached    h6.* Additional notes  - The simulator also will not start if appc studio is closed and reopened, even if the stop button not pressed.   -If the stop button is not pressed on the console this issue does not occur  -A way to run on the simulator is to open up the run configurations dialogue and run from there.  -Restart the system and run works too. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS simulator is not started on build and run
Description: """"h6.Issue Description iOS simulator is not started on build and run h6.Issue Description 1. Open <USER>Studio 2. Choose """"""""Run"""""""" configuration on """"""""iPad 2 (v8.4)"""""""" simulator 3. Press play button (normally this builds and then launches the simulator) 4. Wait for application to finish building and launch the simulator 5. Note that the build completes but the simulator does not launch **appc info and logs are attached h6.* Additional notes - The simulator also will not start if appc studio is closed and reopened, even if the stop button not pressed. -If the stop button is not pressed on the console this issue does not occur -A way to run on the simulator is to open up the run configurations dialogue and run from there. -Restart the system and run works too. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19658,12,"""Remove JDK 1.6 check from Android build and add new titanium_prep""","""""""Now that we've got a version of titanium_prep that no longer depends on JDK 1.6, we can remove the check from the Android build.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Remove JDK 1.6 check from Android build and add new titanium_prep
Description: """"Now that we've got a version of titanium_prep that no longer depends on JDK 1.6, we can remove the check from the Android build.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19649,12,"""Android: use `children` property in createView""","""""""Would be very useful, allow to use `children` property in createView arguments like *I can do it in iOS*.  But according to the docs in http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-property-children, the `children` property is readonly.     Related issues:  TIMOB-19551  ALOY-1221""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: use `children` property in createView
Description: """"Would be very useful, allow to use `children` property in createView arguments like *I can do it in iOS*. But according to the docs in http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-property-children, the `children` property is readonly. Related issues: TIMOB-19551 ALOY-1221""""",title+description
TIMOB-19645,12,"""CLI: Builder.generateAppIcons ignores existing assets""","""""""Let say we want to create app icons with several sizes and create them during build <USER>like below.    {code:title=cli/commands/_build/copy.js}   function createAppIconSet(next) {    var appIconSetDir = path.join(this.buildDir, 'Assets'),     missingIcons = [     // Square44x44Logo     {      description: 'Square44x44Logo.png - Used for logo',      file: path.join(appIconSetDir, 'Square44x44Logo.png'),      width: 44,      height: 44,      required: true     },       // Square71x71Logo     {      description: 'Square71x71Logo.png - Used for logo',      file: path.join(appIconSetDir, 'Square71x71Logo.png'),      width: 71,      height: 71,      required: true     },       // Square150x150Logo     {      description: 'Square150x150Logo.png - Used for logo',      file: path.join(appIconSetDir, 'Square150x150Logo.png'),      width: 150,      height: 150,      required: true     }    ];    this.generateAppIcons(missingIcons, next);   }  {code}     Even when you want to use custom images and place those images in your project (e.g. place custom images under platform/windows/ or project root directory), they are always ignored by the builder during the build.    !vs.png|thumbnail!""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Builder.generateAppIcons ignores existing assets
Description: """"Let say we want to create app icons with several sizes and create them during build <USER>like below. {code:title=cli/commands/_build/copy.js} function createAppIconSet(next) { var appIconSetDir = path.join(this.buildDir, 'Assets'), missingIcons = [ // Square44x44Logo { description: 'Square44x44Logo.png - Used for logo', file: path.join(appIconSetDir, 'Square44x44Logo.png'), width: 44, height: 44, required: true }, // Square71x71Logo { description: 'Square71x71Logo.png - Used for logo', file: path.join(appIconSetDir, 'Square71x71Logo.png'), width: 71, height: 71, required: true }, // Square150x150Logo { description: 'Square150x150Logo.png - Used for logo', file: path.join(appIconSetDir, 'Square150x150Logo.png'), width: 150, height: 150, required: true } ]; this.generateAppIcons(missingIcons, next); } {code} Even when you want to use custom images and place those images in your project (e.g. place custom images under platform/windows/ or project root directory), they are always ignored by the builder during the build. !vs.png|thumbnail!""""",title+description
TIMOB-19643,12,"""CLI: Runtime error when no DefaultIcon.png exists""","""""""There's a  typo at builder.generateAppIcons, which causes runtime error when there's no DefaultIcon.png.    PR: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/7249    {code:diff}    if (!fs.existsSync(defaultIcon)) {      if (requiredMissing === 0) {  -      this.logger.warn(__n('There is a missing app icon', 'There are missing app icons', icons.length));  +     this.logger.warn(__('There is a missing app icon', 'There are missing app icons', icons.length));         this.logger.warn(__('You can either create the missing icons below or create an image named """"""""DefaultIcon.png"""""""" in the root of your project'));  ...  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Runtime error when no DefaultIcon.png exists
Description: """"There's a typo at builder.generateAppIcons, which causes runtime error when there's no DefaultIcon.png. PR: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/7249 {code:diff} if (!fs.existsSync(defaultIcon)) { if (requiredMissing === 0) { - this.logger.warn(__n('There is a missing app icon', 'There are missing app icons', icons.length)); + this.logger.warn(__('There is a missing app icon', 'There are missing app icons', icons.length)); this.logger.warn(__('You can either create the missing icons below or create an image named """"""""DefaultIcon.png"""""""" in the root of your project')); ... {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-19642,12,"""Enable access to ListItem child views""","""""""For an example, see this Q&A issue: http://developer.<USER>com/question/159217/is-it-possible-to-animate-a-view-inside-a-listitem  I also tried using the postlayout event on a ListItem child view to grab the event source to then animate it. No success.  Thus the feature request would be to provide an event that signals when the view is """"""""live"""""""" (i.e. something like postlayout), so we can then do something with it. Additionally, it may be useful to get a """"""""view recycled"""""""" event when the ListView code recycles the cells  - so for example we can stop animating.    To highlight this issue: for example, it's impossible to use the images property on an ImageView in a ListItem, since we can't call the ImageView.animate() method.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Enable access to ListItem child views
Description: """"For an example, see this Q&A issue: http://developer.<USER>com/question/159217/is-it-possible-to-animate-a-view-inside-a-listitem I also tried using the postlayout event on a ListItem child view to grab the event source to then animate it. No success. Thus the feature request would be to provide an event that signals when the view is """"""""live"""""""" (i.e. something like postlayout), so we can then do something with it. Additionally, it may be useful to get a """"""""view recycled"""""""" event when the ListView code recycles the cells - so for example we can stop animating. To highlight this issue: for example, it's impossible to use the images property on an ImageView in a ListItem, since we can't call the ImageView.animate() method.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19641,12,"""Create a function to check for an existing listener""","""""""Sometimes would be really useful to know if there is an event attached to an object.    For example, let's say we want to attach  *Ti.App.addEventListener('app:whatever', myfunction)* but, to avoid double attach, we want to check previously if it is not attached yet.    Something like  *Ti.App.hasListener('app:whatever')* would be really useful to do a check before attach.    P.d.- I know *Ti.App.add...* is not recommended, but sometimes is better than other possibilities.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Create a function to check for an existing listener
Description: """"Sometimes would be really useful to know if there is an event attached to an object. For example, let's say we want to attach *Ti.App.addEventListener('app:whatever', myfunction)* but, to avoid double attach, we want to check previously if it is not attached yet. Something like *Ti.App.hasListener('app:whatever')* would be really useful to do a check before attach. P.d.- I know *Ti.App.add...* is not recommended, but sometimes is better than other possibilities.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19638,12,"""Memory Leak in Alloy android Menu?""","""""""I test my code for memory leaks. When I use Menu in my View I can't to make sure that memory fully released. Not all proxy removed from memory after closing test window. Some time but rarely all proxies and his native views removed fully.     Why it happens and how to deal with this behavior?  The situation is complicated by using a more complex controller with a many of child Views.    {code:xml|title=testWindow.xml}  <Alloy>      <Window>                 <Menu id=""""""""menu"""""""" platform=""""""""android"""""""">                         <MenuItem id=""""""""submitButton"""""""" title=""""""""123"""""""">              </MenuItem>          </Menu>              <Label>Close this window and then create second HPROF dump. Then compare difference against two dumps.</Label>          </Window>  </Alloy>  {code}    {code:javascript|title=testWindow.js}  // empty  {code}      {code:javascript|title=index.js}  function doClick(e) {      Alloy.createController('testWindow').getView().open();  }    $.index.open();  {code}    {code:xml|title=index.xml}  <Alloy>   <Window class=""""""""container"""""""" layout=""""""""vertical"""""""">       <Label>Create first HPROF dump now</Label>    <Button id=""""""""label"""""""" onClick=""""""""doClick"""""""">Click to open test window</Button>   </Window>  </Alloy>  {code}    !dumps.png|thumbnail!  """"""",Bug,"Title: Memory Leak in Alloy android Menu?
Description: """"I test my code for memory leaks. When I use Menu in my View I can't to make sure that memory fully released. Not all proxy removed from memory after closing test window. Some time but rarely all proxies and his native views removed fully. Why it happens and how to deal with this behavior? The situation is complicated by using a more complex controller with a many of child Views. {code:xml|title=testWindow.xml} <Alloy> <Window> <Menu id=""""""""menu"""""""" platform=""""""""android""""""""> <MenuItem id=""""""""submitButton"""""""" title=""""""""123""""""""> </MenuItem> </Menu> <Label>Close this window and then create second HPROF dump. Then compare difference against two dumps.</Label> </Window> </Alloy> {code} {code:javascript|title=testWindow.js} // empty {code} {code:javascript|title=index.js} function doClick(e) { Alloy.createController('testWindow').getView().open(); } $.index.open(); {code} {code:xml|title=index.xml} <Alloy> <Window class=""""""""container"""""""" layout=""""""""vertical""""""""> <Label>Create first HPROF dump now</Label> <Button id=""""""""label"""""""" onClick=""""""""doClick"""""""">Click to open test window</Button> </Window> </Alloy> {code} !dumps.png|thumbnail! """"",title+description
