TIMOB-19636,12,"""iOS - Custom Keyboard overlaps TextField in ScrollView""","""""""When using a custom keyboard (example SwiftKey) with TextField that is child of a ScrollView, the view is not automatically scrolled to accommodate  the keyboard and keep the TextField in view while typing. This doesn't occur when using the default iOS keyboard.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Custom Keyboard overlaps TextField in ScrollView
Description: """"When using a custom keyboard (example SwiftKey) with TextField that is child of a ScrollView, the view is not automatically scrolled to accommodate the keyboard and keep the TextField in view while typing. This doesn't occur when using the default iOS keyboard.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19634,12,"""ListView not appearing sometimes if <Templates> is present""","""""""I have a very strange problem related to ListView. I have created custom tab navigation system and dynamically add page view when tab is selected inside main container. The problem is that when that page contains a ListView it sometimes doesn't appear if I restart my app and open that tab again. This happens on average once in every 5-6 try.    I'm attaching the source I'm having the problem with. There are many unnecessary code which you can simply ignore. Try selecting the second tab below. Than quit the app (don't simply close) and re-open it and try to select the tab again. Repeat this <USER>several time and you'll the that sometimes the ListView doesn't appear at all.    The listview is inside places_list.xml which is included from search.xml.    If you remove the <Templates> node completely than it should work fine.""""""",Bug,"Title: ListView not appearing sometimes if <Templates> is present
Description: """"I have a very strange problem related to ListView. I have created custom tab navigation system and dynamically add page view when tab is selected inside main container. The problem is that when that page contains a ListView it sometimes doesn't appear if I restart my app and open that tab again. This happens on average once in every 5-6 try. I'm attaching the source I'm having the problem with. There are many unnecessary code which you can simply ignore. Try selecting the second tab below. Than quit the app (don't simply close) and re-open it and try to select the tab again. Repeat this <USER>several time and you'll the that sometimes the ListView doesn't appear at all. The listview is inside places_list.xml which is included from search.xml. If you remove the <Templates> node completely than it should work fine.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19632,12,"""Alloy widget always converts argument type to string""","""""""Pass the argument as follows will result in all arguments - i.e ratable, rate being converted to String type in widget.js      However, if I attach arguments to a view as below          I think we need make widget behave the same as view in terms of arguments type.              """"""",Bug,"Title: Alloy widget always converts argument type to string
Description: """"Pass the argument as follows will result in all arguments - i.e ratable, rate being converted to String type in widget.js However, if I attach arguments to a view as below I think we need make widget behave the same as view in terms of arguments type. """"",title+description
