TIMOB-19619,12,"""Use a different data directory (tishadow)""","""""""This issue relate to pull request: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6698    You need to add the ability to specify a data directory in tiapp.xml. Like this:    '<property name = """"""""dataDirectory"""""""" type = """"""""string""""""""> data / data / com.app.name / .... </ property>'    Without it will not work services, webview and some other functions with tishadow.    P.S. I wanted to do it myself, but now there's no time at all.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Use a different data directory (tishadow)
Description: """"This issue relate to pull request: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6698 You need to add the ability to specify a data directory in tiapp.xml. Like this: '<property name = """"""""dataDirectory"""""""" type = """"""""string""""""""> data / data / com.app.name / .... </ property>' Without it will not work services, webview and some other functions with tishadow. P.S. I wanted to do it myself, but now there's no time at all.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19616,12,"""Changes to app content are not updated on rebuild to device ""","""""""Similar to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/CLI-820 , However the issue is seen occurring when building application to device.     A range of CLI & SDK versions were tested in an attempt to recreate the issue, but could not find a consistent result:    SDK versions: 4.1.0.GA, 5.0.0.GA, 5.0.1.v20150922104152, 5.0.1.v20150924103934 (latest)  CLI versions: 5.0.1, 5.0.2-19  Devices: iOS 8.4, 9.0.1    However, the issue could be consistently created after creating projects both with & without platform services.     with platform services ENABLED, Xcode should do a clean on the initial build, however will not for the second build, and will not update file changes.    With platform services DISABLED, Xcode should do a clean on the initial build, however will not for the second build, but will update file changes.    This was tested on different devices and CLI versions, using Ti SDK: 5.0.1.v20150924103934, on two different machines, and the results were consistent. Also refer to the spreadsheet, which details the different combinations of tests that were preformed, and the result.     Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create a new mobile app project with platform services ENABLED.  2. Save & build to device.  3. Edit content in app.js / index.xml.  4. Save & rebuild to device.    Actual Result: Changes to file made in step 3 will not be visible after step 4.  Expected Result: Changes to files made should be visible after rebuilding to device.""""""",Bug,"Title: Changes to app content are not updated on rebuild to device
Description: """"Similar to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/CLI-820 , However the issue is seen occurring when building application to device. A range of CLI & SDK versions were tested in an attempt to recreate the issue, but could not find a consistent result: SDK versions: 4.1.0.GA, 5.0.0.GA, 5.0.1.v20150922104152, 5.0.1.v20150924103934 (latest) CLI versions: 5.0.1, 5.0.2-19 Devices: iOS 8.4, 9.0.1 However, the issue could be consistently created after creating projects both with & without platform services. with platform services ENABLED, Xcode should do a clean on the initial build, however will not for the second build, and will not update file changes. With platform services DISABLED, Xcode should do a clean on the initial build, however will not for the second build, but will update file changes. This was tested on different devices and CLI versions, using Ti SDK: 5.0.1.v20150924103934, on two different machines, and the results were consistent. Also refer to the spreadsheet, which details the different combinations of tests that were preformed, and the result. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new mobile app project with platform services ENABLED. 2. Save & build to device. 3. Edit content in app.js / index.xml. 4. Save & rebuild to device. Actual Result: Changes to file made in step 3 will not be visible after step 4. Expected Result: Changes to files made should be visible after rebuilding to device.""""",title+description
