TIMOB-19524,12,"""Is there an alternative for android fragment master/detail for tablets?""","""""""as iOS has splitview to handle tablet versions , andorid uses fragment to manage tablet version     titanium doesn't handle such thing   please check this   https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/advanced/master_detail    it handle android tablets as handheld phones , and window doesn't accept another window inside as workaround !    please handle this . """"""",Improvement,"Title: Is there an alternative for android fragment master/detail for tablets?
Description: """"as iOS has splitview to handle tablet versions , andorid uses fragment to manage tablet version titanium doesn't handle such thing please check this https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/advanced/master_detail it handle android tablets as handheld phones , and window doesn't accept another window inside as workaround ! please handle this . """"",title+description
TIMOB-19523,12,"""IOS: ImageView within ListView with defaultImage set is not resized accordingly to remote image""","""""""I have a listview, which displays remote images of different dimensions. While images are loaded, I show defaultImage with spinner.  Here's a template I have for this  {code:title=template|borderStyle=solid}  {      bindId: 'main',      properties: {height: Ti.UI.SIZE},      childTemplates: [          {              type: 'Ti.UI.ImageView',              bindId: 'image',              properties: {                  width: Ti.UI.SIZE,                  height: Ti.UI.SIZE,                  defaultImage: 'icon_spinner_wide.png'              }          }      ]  }    but unfortunately as soon as 'load' event handler is declared, I get following error on listview.setSections:  *** setObjectForKey: object cannot be nil (key: section)  If I add handler for click event, it works. Probably these 2 issues are connected.  Also it works on Android (both resize after remote image is loaded and load event).  """"""",Bug,"Title: IOS: ImageView within ListView with defaultImage set is not resized accordingly to remote image
Description: """"I have a listview, which displays remote images of different dimensions. While images are loaded, I show defaultImage with spinner. Here's a template I have for this {code:title=template|borderStyle=solid} { bindId: 'main', properties: {height: Ti.UI.SIZE}, childTemplates: [ { type: 'Ti.UI.ImageView', bindId: 'image', properties: { width: Ti.UI.SIZE, height: Ti.UI.SIZE, defaultImage: 'icon_spinner_wide.png' } } ] } but unfortunately as soon as 'load' event handler is declared, I get following error on listview.setSections: *** setObjectForKey: object cannot be nil (key: section) If I add handler for click event, it works. Probably these 2 issues are connected. Also it works on Android (both resize after remote image is loaded and load event). """"",title+description
TIMOB-19521,12,"""Ti.Map MapView setLocation zooms out to the maximum on Android unless latitudeDelta longitudeDelta are present""","""""""function setLocation (e) {      Ti.API.info(""""""""Annotation """""""" + e.title + """""""" clicked, id: """""""" + e.annotation.myid);      $.mapview.setLocation({          latitude: 32.8245525,          longitude: -117.0951632,          animate: true,      });  }    Calling that function will center the map on the specified location but zoom the map out to the maximum. The documentation makes it seem like latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta are optional.    I just want to center the map, not change the zoom level. I'm not aware of any workarounds on Android.    GitHub repo illustrating problem: https://github.com/<USER>setLocationBug    The above application can be built for iOS and Android. Clicking the annotation will center and zoom the map out on Android. It only centers the map on iOS.    Titanium: 3.3.0.GA  Platform: 4.4.2  API: 19  Google APIs x86""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Map MapView setLocation zooms out to the maximum on Android unless latitudeDelta longitudeDelta are present
Description: """"function setLocation (e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Annotation """""""" + e.title + """""""" clicked, id: """""""" + e.annotation.myid); $.mapview.setLocation({ latitude: 32.8245525, longitude: -117.0951632, animate: true, }); } Calling that function will center the map on the specified location but zoom the map out to the maximum. The documentation makes it seem like latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta are optional. I just want to center the map, not change the zoom level. I'm not aware of any workarounds on Android. GitHub repo illustrating problem: https://github.com/<USER>setLocationBug The above application can be built for iOS and Android. Clicking the annotation will center and zoom the map out on Android. It only centers the map on iOS. Titanium: 3.3.0.GA Platform: 4.4.2 API: 19 Google APIs x86""""",title+description
TIMOB-19514,12,"""iOS 9 - Facebook Support""","""""""Facebook is now complaining about iOS 9 support and asking for updating the FB SDK along with some changes on the iOS Info.plist file.      I'm worried on how this can affect our iOS apps once iOS 9 final is released.      On Facebook Developer Console, a warning says:    Apple's iOS 9 introduces many changes that will affect the Facebook integration of your app “PiniOn”. You will need to make changes to preserve app functionality and ensure the best possible experience for people who use your iOS 9 app. Read this blog post for more information.    Action items you will need to take:    Download the new SDK for iOS 4.6 or v3.24.  The iOS 9 rollout introduces a new feature called App Transport Security which will require you to whitelist Facebook domains in your app's plist.  Update your app's plist to handle the changes to canOpenURL described here, so that your app can open dialogs in the Facebook app (for Login, share, invite friends, or native Likes).  Submit the new version of your app to Apple's app store.  Please refer to this guide and changelog for more information.      Facebook iOS 9 Guide:  https://developers.facebook.com/docs/ios/ios9    Facebook Dev Post about iOS 9 Support:  https://developers.facebook.com/blog/post/2015/09/10/new-SDK-for-iOS9/    Should Titanium developers worry about this? Is a Facebook SDK update planned for iOS 9? Should we change our tiapp.xml manually in order to reflect those changes like Facebook servers/network requests whitelisting?""""""",Story,"Title: iOS 9 - Facebook Support
Description: """"Facebook is now complaining about iOS 9 support and asking for updating the FB SDK along with some changes on the iOS Info.plist file. I'm worried on how this can affect our iOS apps once iOS 9 final is released. On Facebook Developer Console, a warning says: Apple's iOS 9 introduces many changes that will affect the Facebook integration of your app “PiniOn”. You will need to make changes to preserve app functionality and ensure the best possible experience for people who use your iOS 9 app. Read this blog post for more information. Action items you will need to take: Download the new SDK for iOS 4.6 or v3.24. The iOS 9 rollout introduces a new feature called App Transport Security which will require you to whitelist Facebook domains in your app's plist. Update your app's plist to handle the changes to canOpenURL described here, so that your app can open dialogs in the Facebook app (for Login, share, invite friends, or native Likes). Submit the new version of your app to Apple's app store. Please refer to this guide and changelog for more information. Facebook iOS 9 Guide: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/ios/ios9 Facebook Dev Post about iOS 9 Support: https://developers.facebook.com/blog/post/2015/09/10/new-SDK-for-iOS9/ Should Titanium developers worry about this? Is a Facebook SDK update planned for iOS 9? Should we change our tiapp.xml manually in order to reflect those changes like Facebook servers/network requests whitelisting?""""",title+description
TIMOB-19511,12,"""Add support for platform specific DefaultIcon.png files""","""""""Titanium SDK 5.0.0 added support for DefaultIcon.png in the project root directory. This image is intended to be applied to all platforms. Since iOS does not support app icons with an alpha channel, we must allow platform specific images.    DefaultIcon.png will continue to live in the project root, but this ticket is meant to add a platform specific override from the {{<project-dir>/platform/<platform>/DefaultIcon.png}} file.    This logic should be added to to {{titanium_mobile/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/builder.js}} in the {{generateAppIcons()}} function (https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/builder.js#L412).    It should check for the platform specific DefaultIcon.png, then if that doesn't exist, fall back to the one in the project root before failing out.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Add support for platform specific DefaultIcon.png files
Description: """"Titanium SDK 5.0.0 added support for DefaultIcon.png in the project root directory. This image is intended to be applied to all platforms. Since iOS does not support app icons with an alpha channel, we must allow platform specific images. DefaultIcon.png will continue to live in the project root, but this ticket is meant to add a platform specific override from the {{<project-dir>/platform/<platform>/DefaultIcon.png}} file. This logic should be added to to {{titanium_mobile/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/builder.js}} in the {{generateAppIcons()}} function (https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/builder.js#L412). It should check for the platform specific DefaultIcon.png, then if that doesn't exist, fall back to the one in the project root before failing out.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19510,12,"""Add Ti.App.iOS.UserActivity.isSupported()""","""""""{{Ti.App.iOS.UserActivity}} has an (undocumented: TIDOC-2306) {{supported}} property but no {{isSupported()}} method.    I'd expect such a method since the tightly related [Ti.App.iOS.SearchableIndex.isSupported|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableIndex-method-isSupported] also exists, just like [Ti.WatchSession.isSupported|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.WatchSession-property-isSupported] by the way.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Add Ti.App.iOS.UserActivity.isSupported()
Description: """"{{Ti.App.iOS.UserActivity}} has an (undocumented: TIDOC-2306) {{supported}} property but no {{isSupported()}} method. I'd expect such a method since the tightly related [Ti.App.iOS.SearchableIndex.isSupported|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableIndex-method-isSupported] also exists, just like [Ti.WatchSession.isSupported|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.WatchSession-property-isSupported] by the way.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19509,12,"""DefaultIcon.png needs to support platform specific versions""","""""""TIMOB-19477 has introduced a new {{/DefaultIcon.png}} to generate all iOS icons from.  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/5_0_X/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/builder.js#L385    There are tickets to do the same for other platforms.  TIMOB-19485, TIMOB-19486, TIMOB-19487    There are differences in icon guidelines and requirements between platforms:    - iOS requires 24-bit (no alpha)  - Other platforms support 32-bit (with alpha) and some ([Android|https://www.google.com/design/spec/style/icons.html]) actively promoot using transparency to produce unique icon shapes    Take our 4.1.0 sample app:    * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti410/blob/master/app/assets/iphone/appicon.png  * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti410/blob/master/platform/android/res/drawable-hdpi/appicon.png    To support this we need optional platform-specific versions of {{DefaultIcon.png}}. Since the icon itself should not be packaged with the app, the platform specific icons should reside under:    * {{/platforms/<platform>/DefaultIcon.png}}    If this icon does not exist for the target platform it should look for {{/DefaultIcon.png}}    Additionally, validation of specific platform requirements could be added like TIMOB-19512 requests for 24-bit on iOS.""""""",Improvement,"Title: DefaultIcon.png needs to support platform specific versions
Description: """"TIMOB-19477 has introduced a new {{/DefaultIcon.png}} to generate all iOS icons from. https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/5_0_X/node_modules/titanium-sdk/lib/builder.js#L385 There are tickets to do the same for other platforms. TIMOB-19485, TIMOB-19486, TIMOB-19487 There are differences in icon guidelines and requirements between platforms: - iOS requires 24-bit (no alpha) - Other platforms support 32-bit (with alpha) and some ([Android|https://www.google.com/design/spec/style/icons.html]) actively promoot using transparency to produce unique icon shapes Take our 4.1.0 sample app: * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti410/blob/master/app/assets/iphone/appicon.png * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti410/blob/master/platform/android/res/drawable-hdpi/appicon.png To support this we need optional platform-specific versions of {{DefaultIcon.png}}. Since the icon itself should not be packaged with the app, the platform specific icons should reside under: * {{/platforms/<platform>/DefaultIcon.png}} If this icon does not exist for the target platform it should look for {{/DefaultIcon.png}} Additionally, validation of specific platform requirements could be added like TIMOB-19512 requests for 24-bit on iOS.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19507,12,"""[TRACE] should be [INFO] for """"Agreeing to the Xcode/iOS license requires admin privileges..""""""","""""""After installing/upgrading Xcode and without having run Xcode before using the CLI will get you:        The message is clear, but since it's at trace-level little users will actually see it. It should be info-level.""""""",Bug,"Title: [TRACE] should be [INFO] for """"Agreeing to the Xcode/iOS license requires admin privileges..""""
Description: """"After installing/upgrading Xcode and without having run Xcode before using the CLI will get you: The message is clear, but since it's at trace-level little users will actually see it. It should be info-level.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19505,12,"""Ti.Network.HTTPClient Default addition of Appcelerator User-Agent header can impact success of network calls""","""""""On Android and iOS the addition of the default User-Agent string for each http network request is impacting the expected response of the network request.    The code that is causing the issue:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/4_1_X/android/modules/network/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/network/TiHTTPClient.java#L943    The issue seems to be that the protected endpoint is validating against known UserAgents and returning an error response if it is not an approved UserAgent string. Trying to set the user agent with Ti.Network.HTTPClient.setRequestHeader appends the header, but does not remove the default header.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Network.HTTPClient Default addition of Appcelerator User-Agent header can impact success of network calls
Description: """"On Android and iOS the addition of the default User-Agent string for each http network request is impacting the expected response of the network request. The code that is causing the issue: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/4_1_X/android/modules/network/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/network/TiHTTPClient.java#L943 The issue seems to be that the protected endpoint is validating against known UserAgents and returning an error response if it is not an approved UserAgent string. Trying to set the user agent with Ti.Network.HTTPClient.setRequestHeader appends the header, but does not remove the default header. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19489,12,"""iOS9: 3D-Touch: Support UIApplicationShortcutItem (""""Quick Actions"""")""","""""""Apple just presented the new 3D-Touch feature of the iPhone6S. User can press a view and will review an instant feedback providing a context-like menu to select different actions, called {{UIApplicationShortcutItem}}. After clicking on one of the actions, the user will guided to the app where several actions can be performed depending on the action. There are the properties {{type}}, {{localizedTitle}}, {{localizedSubtitle}}, {{icon}} and {{userInfo}}. There is also a {{UIApplicationShortcutIcon}} to configure the icon or associate it with existing (contact) images to personalize the experience.    We differentiate *static* vs. *dynamic* shortcut items:  - *Static*: Are set in the Info.plist before launching the app.  - *Dynamic*: Are set in the app to offer a dynamic behavior at runtime.    As is currently see it, we can support static action very easy by letting the user write them in the <ios> section of our tiapp.xml. Dynamic shortcut items will need an own proxy to receive existing actions and configure own actions.    *Related documents*:  - https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIApplicationShortcutItem_class/  - https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIApplicationShortcutIcon_Class/index.html#//apple_ref/occ/cl/UIApplicationShortcutIcon  - https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/General/Reference/InfoPlistKeyReference/Articles/iPhoneOSKeys.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40009252-SW36""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS9: 3D-Touch: Support UIApplicationShortcutItem (""""Quick Actions"""")
Description: """"Apple just presented the new 3D-Touch feature of the iPhone6S. User can press a view and will review an instant feedback providing a context-like menu to select different actions, called {{UIApplicationShortcutItem}}. After clicking on one of the actions, the user will guided to the app where several actions can be performed depending on the action. There are the properties {{type}}, {{localizedTitle}}, {{localizedSubtitle}}, {{icon}} and {{userInfo}}. There is also a {{UIApplicationShortcutIcon}} to configure the icon or associate it with existing (contact) images to personalize the experience. We differentiate *static* vs. *dynamic* shortcut items: - *Static*: Are set in the Info.plist before launching the app. - *Dynamic*: Are set in the app to offer a dynamic behavior at runtime. As is currently see it, we can support static action very easy by letting the user write them in the <ios> section of our tiapp.xml. Dynamic shortcut items will need an own proxy to receive existing actions and configure own actions. *Related documents*: - https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIApplicationShortcutItem_class/ - https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIApplicationShortcutIcon_Class/index.html#//apple_ref/occ/cl/UIApplicationShortcutIcon - https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/General/Reference/InfoPlistKeyReference/Articles/iPhoneOSKeys.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40009252-SW36""""",title+description
TIMOB-19485,12,"""MobileWeb: Generate missing app icons based on DefaultIcon.png""","""""""If any of the app icons are missing, then search for {{<project-dir>/platforms/mobileweb/DefaultIcon.png}} and {{<project-dir>/DefaultIcon.png}} and us it to generate missing app icons.    You simply need to the base Builder object's {{generateAppIcons()}} method:    """"""",Improvement,"Title: MobileWeb: Generate missing app icons based on DefaultIcon.png
Description: """"If any of the app icons are missing, then search for {{<project-dir>/platforms/mobileweb/DefaultIcon.png}} and {{<project-dir>/DefaultIcon.png}} and us it to generate missing app icons. You simply need to the base Builder object's {{generateAppIcons()}} method: """"",title+description
TIMOB-19480,12,"""iOS9: Ti info does not work with latest TiSDK & Xcode7 beta leading to studio unable to find xcode""","""""""h6.Reproduce  1. Install TiSDK 3.5.0.GA       1.1. run ti sdk install 3.5.0.GA       1.2. run ti sdk select 3.5.0.GA       1.3. run ti info      1.4. notice it finds xcode as expected   2. Intall latest SDK      2.1. ti sdk install --branch 5_0_X 5.0.0.v20150908113920       2.2. ti sdk select 5.0.0.v20150908113920       2.3. ti info, notice how it fails.   3. This then once the computer reboots fails to find xcode 7 leading to builds in studio not working but working from the cmd line.    h6.Note  Not sure this is a CLI problem or SDK problem, since 3.5.0 SDK, ti info works well.  seems this is only introduced by latest SDK.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS9: Ti info does not work with latest TiSDK & Xcode7 beta leading to studio unable to find xcode
Description: """"h6.Reproduce 1. Install TiSDK 3.5.0.GA 1.1. run ti sdk install 3.5.0.GA 1.2. run ti sdk select 3.5.0.GA 1.3. run ti info 1.4. notice it finds xcode as expected 2. Intall latest SDK 2.1. ti sdk install --branch 5_0_X 5.0.0.v20150908113920 2.2. ti sdk select 5.0.0.v20150908113920 2.3. ti info, notice how it fails. 3. This then once the computer reboots fails to find xcode 7 leading to builds in studio not working but working from the cmd line. h6.Note Not sure this is a CLI problem or SDK problem, since 3.5.0 SDK, ti info works well. seems this is only introduced by latest SDK.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19475,12,"""Android: Build fails if target SDK is lower than API 23""","""""""h5.Description    When building an app for Android and API 23 (Android 6.0) is not installed or is not set as the target SDK then the build will fail with the below errors        This error is related to app compat which has been updated in [this commit|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/7128]    h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Either uninstall API 23 or set the target SDK in the tiapp.xml using {{<uses-sdk android:targetSdkVersion=""""""""21""""""""/>}}  2. Build for Android using {{appc run -p android -T device --build-only}}      h5.Actual result    The build will fail    h5.Expected result    The build should exit and tell the user that API 23 is required to build using 5.0.0""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Build fails if target SDK is lower than API 23
Description: """"h5.Description When building an app for Android and API 23 (Android 6.0) is not installed or is not set as the target SDK then the build will fail with the below errors This error is related to app compat which has been updated in [this commit|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/7128] h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Either uninstall API 23 or set the target SDK in the tiapp.xml using {{<uses-sdk android:targetSdkVersion=""""""""21""""""""/>}} 2. Build for Android using {{appc run -p android -T device --build-only}} h5.Actual result The build will fail h5.Expected result The build should exit and tell the user that API 23 is required to build using 5.0.0""""",title+description
TIMOB-19472,12,"""watchOS 2: Template should not include (empty) glance and other scenes""","""""""The current watchOS 2 template's storyboard includes scenes for glances and notifications. The glance storyboard is empty resulting in an empty glance. We shouldn't include these scenes if we don't include sample code for it. Users can easily add these scenes (plus for complications) themselves if they require.""""""",Improvement,"Title: watchOS 2: Template should not include (empty) glance and other scenes
Description: """"The current watchOS 2 template's storyboard includes scenes for glances and notifications. The glance storyboard is empty resulting in an empty glance. We shouldn't include these scenes if we don't include sample code for it. Users can easily add these scenes (plus for complications) themselves if they require.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19466,12,"""Ti.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet is missing phoneNumbers, latitude and longitude""","""""""While [supportsNavigation|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet-property-supportsNavigation] and [supportsPhoneCall|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet-property-supportsPhoneCall] are there and talk about the related phoneNumbers, latitude and longitude properties these are in fact [missing|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiAppiOSSearchableItemAttributeSetProxy.m], making the first 2 unusable.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet is missing phoneNumbers, latitude and longitude
Description: """"While [supportsNavigation|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet-property-supportsNavigation] and [supportsPhoneCall|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet-property-supportsPhoneCall] are there and talk about the related phoneNumbers, latitude and longitude properties these are in fact [missing|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiAppiOSSearchableItemAttributeSetProxy.m], making the first 2 unusable.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19461,12,"""iOS9: Window Background Image is Black""","""""""h6.Issue Description  When you build and run the attached project on iOS8 the Splash screen image is shown. When you build and run the attached project on iOS 9 then the splash screen is shown as black and the image is not shown.     h6.Steps to Reproduce:   # Get sample app   # Build against iOS 8   # Notice the titanium splash screen is shown   # Rebuild with iOS 9   # Notice the titanium splash screen is not shown but its a black window, the splash screen should be shown.   # add backgroundColor: 'blue', to the window   # Rebuild with iOS 9   # Notice the window is blue but the image is still not shown. The image should still be shown.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS9: Window Background Image is Black
Description: """"h6.Issue Description When you build and run the attached project on iOS8 the Splash screen image is shown. When you build and run the attached project on iOS 9 then the splash screen is shown as black and the image is not shown. h6.Steps to Reproduce: # Get sample app # Build against iOS 8 # Notice the titanium splash screen is shown # Rebuild with iOS 9 # Notice the titanium splash screen is not shown but its a black window, the splash screen should be shown. # add backgroundColor: 'blue', to the window # Rebuild with iOS 9 # Notice the window is blue but the image is still not shown. The image should still be shown. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19460,12,"""Silent Push notification payload may be wrong..""","""""""The documentation states that the following payload will trigger the silent push notificaiton:    {""""""""alert"""""""":"""""""""""""""",""""""""content-available"""""""":1}    how ever I have positively verified that this string does NOT trigger the notification, the string below does however trigger the silent notification according to the rest of the docs here.     {""""""""aps"""""""":{""""""""content-available"""""""":1}}    Please change, lots of people might be confused...    did not do any deep analyses, just concluded by testing on device iOS 8.4 with SDK 4.1.0    Let me know if you need help (possibly the string might work in Arrow but then again this is not always the case...""""""",Story,"Title: Silent Push notification payload may be wrong..
Description: """"The documentation states that the following payload will trigger the silent push notificaiton: {""""""""alert"""""""":"""""""""""""""",""""""""content-available"""""""":1} how ever I have positively verified that this string does NOT trigger the notification, the string below does however trigger the silent notification according to the rest of the docs here. {""""""""aps"""""""":{""""""""content-available"""""""":1}} Please change, lots of people might be confused... did not do any deep analyses, just concluded by testing on device iOS 8.4 with SDK 4.1.0 Let me know if you need help (possibly the string might work in Arrow but then again this is not always the case...""""",title+description
TIMOB-19458,12,"""iOS: Timeout property of Ti.Network.HttpClient is being ignored""","""""""h6.Issue Description  Running the sample code below, we're trying to set a very high timeout for our HttpClient request. (It's a necessary change for our test environment.) Unfortunately, our increase seems to be ignored, and the connection always times out after 120 seconds.     h6.Runnable Test Case   The variable ‘someurl’ can be replaced with the url of a slow responding API (an API which takes longer to respond).   """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Timeout property of Ti.Network.HttpClient is being ignored
Description: """"h6.Issue Description Running the sample code below, we're trying to set a very high timeout for our HttpClient request. (It's a necessary change for our test environment.) Unfortunately, our increase seems to be ignored, and the connection always times out after 120 seconds. h6.Runnable Test Case The variable ‘someurl’ can be replaced with the url of a slow responding API (an API which takes longer to respond). """"",title+description
TIMOB-19454,12,"""iOS: info/warn level """"unhandled action FBSSceneSnapshotAction"""" when locking iOS 9 device""","""""""When you (auto) lock your device a Titanium app will log (sometimes at WARN-level):        This seems to be not our bug but Apple's:    * https://github.com/mapbox/mapbox-gl-native/issues/2172  * http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32344082/handlenonlaunchspecificactions-error-in-ios9""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: info/warn level """"unhandled action FBSSceneSnapshotAction"""" when locking iOS 9 device
Description: """"When you (auto) lock your device a Titanium app will log (sometimes at WARN-level): This seems to be not our bug but Apple's: * https://github.com/mapbox/mapbox-gl-native/issues/2172 * http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32344082/handlenonlaunchspecificactions-error-in-ios9""""",title+description
TIMOB-19453,12,"""iOS: Apply recommended settings when building with extensions""","""""""After building an iOS app with extensions the Xcode projects warns to update to recommended settings for both the Titanium app and the extensions. See the attached screenshot.    We should update the Xcode projects we build with these recommendations.    * Target .. - Adopt 'Product Bundle Identifier' build setting  * Project .. - Turn on 'Enable Testability' When Debugging""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Apply recommended settings when building with extensions
Description: """"After building an iOS app with extensions the Xcode projects warns to update to recommended settings for both the Titanium app and the extensions. See the attached screenshot. We should update the Xcode projects we build with these recommendations. * Target .. - Adopt 'Product Bundle Identifier' build setting * Project .. - Turn on 'Enable Testability' When Debugging""""",title+description
TIMOB-19451,12,"""IntentProxy should have removeExtra method""","""""""The intent Proxy don't have removeExtra() method, as a workaround I just empty my extra like intent.putExtra('extra', ''); but it feel more like a hack, is there a special reason why there is no such method??""""""",New Feature,"Title: IntentProxy should have removeExtra method
Description: """"The intent Proxy don't have removeExtra() method, as a workaround I just empty my extra like intent.putExtra('extra', ''); but it feel more like a hack, is there a special reason why there is no such method??""""",title+description
TIMOB-19450,12,"""Event handlers are assigned to the wrong event when removing and re-adding""","""""""The project consists of a single Alloy controller which creates a WebView which in turn loads index.html.  The project was too big to include so please download from...    https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/5641333/EventingError.7z    There are 2 distinct sides to the app namely the local js file which is loaded by index.html and the Alloy controller, index.js.  For ease I will refer to these as web-side and app-side.    On the web-side I've created a <USER>which creates 10 eventListeners and then fires an event which is picked up on the app-side.  The app-side responds by firing the previously added events. On the web-side the eventListeners respond to the events by sequentially logging one to ten to the console.  Finally when the last event (ten) is fired the eventListeners are removed.  So in simple terms we create the listeners, fire the associated events and then remove the listeners.    When first running the sequence one to ten is printed to the console as expected however, subsequent runs call the events out of order suggesting the event handler is somehow assigned to the wrong event when it has previously removed.    To reproduce please run the attached project, click run and see one to ten printed to the console.  When the events have been removed (logged in the console) click run again, you'll see events one to ten fire in the correct order on the app-side but on the web-side they do not, worse still all the event handlers do not fire.""""""",Bug,"Title: Event handlers are assigned to the wrong event when removing and re-adding
Description: """"The project consists of a single Alloy controller which creates a WebView which in turn loads index.html. The project was too big to include so please download from... https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/5641333/EventingError.7z There are 2 distinct sides to the app namely the local js file which is loaded by index.html and the Alloy controller, index.js. For ease I will refer to these as web-side and app-side. On the web-side I've created a <USER>which creates 10 eventListeners and then fires an event which is picked up on the app-side. The app-side responds by firing the previously added events. On the web-side the eventListeners respond to the events by sequentially logging one to ten to the console. Finally when the last event (ten) is fired the eventListeners are removed. So in simple terms we create the listeners, fire the associated events and then remove the listeners. When first running the sequence one to ten is printed to the console as expected however, subsequent runs call the events out of order suggesting the event handler is somehow assigned to the wrong event when it has previously removed. To reproduce please run the attached project, click run and see one to ten printed to the console. When the events have been removed (logged in the console) click run again, you'll see events one to ten fire in the correct order on the app-side but on the web-side they do not, worse still all the event handlers do not fire.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19449,12,"""iOS schedule local notification doesn't make the default sound or phone vibration""","""""""h6.Issue Description    When the type Ti.App.iOS.USER_NOTIFICATION_TYPE_SOUND is defined and the sound property is not defined in the scheduleLocalNotification function, the device is not making the default sound and the device vibration on the alert.     h6.Expected behavior  The device should make the sound alert and vibrate.     h6.Steps to Replicate:   1. Create a new titanium classic project   2. Grab the app.js file  3. Replace the code with the testcase code   4. Run the application on iOS device    h6.Test Case      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS schedule local notification doesn't make the default sound or phone vibration
Description: """"h6.Issue Description When the type Ti.App.iOS.USER_NOTIFICATION_TYPE_SOUND is defined and the sound property is not defined in the scheduleLocalNotification function, the device is not making the default sound and the device vibration on the alert. h6.Expected behavior The device should make the sound alert and vibrate. h6.Steps to Replicate: 1. Create a new titanium classic project 2. Grab the app.js file 3. Replace the code with the testcase code 4. Run the application on iOS device h6.Test Case """"",title+description
