TIMOB-19441,12,"""useractivitywillsave does not fire before continuing on other device""","""""""The [Ti 5.0 sample app|https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti500] will show that the {{useractivitywillsave}} event only fires when you call {{becomeCurrent()}}. It does not fire before/when you continue the activity on another device, like the [docs|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.UserActivity-property-needsSave] say it will when you set {{needSave}} to {{true}}. This leaves you with no way to update the activity before the other devices takes over.""""""",Bug,"Title: useractivitywillsave does not fire before continuing on other device
Description: """"The [Ti 5.0 sample app|https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti500] will show that the {{useractivitywillsave}} event only fires when you call {{becomeCurrent()}}. It does not fire before/when you continue the activity on another device, like the [docs|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.UserActivity-property-needsSave] say it will when you set {{needSave}} to {{true}}. This leaves you with no way to update the activity before the other devices takes over.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19439,12,"""Date properties of Ti.App.iOS.Searchable* and UserActivity should accept JS Date object""","""""""The new [Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItem|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItem], [Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet] and [Titanium.App.iOS.UserActivity|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.UserActivity] API's all have one or more date-properties, all of which require:    {quote}  The date will be a string in the following format: """"""""yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss.SSS'+0000'"""""""" For example, 2015-12-25T23:30:55.978+0000  {quote}    Since Titanium developers work with the JS Date object all the time, we should support that (as well) just like we do in many other API's like [Titanium.App.iOS.LocalNotification|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/NotificationParams-property-date] and [Titanium.UI.Picker|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Picker-property-maxDate]""""""",Improvement,"Title: Date properties of Ti.App.iOS.Searchable* and UserActivity should accept JS Date object
Description: """"The new [Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItem|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItem], [Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.SearchableItemAttributeSet] and [Titanium.App.iOS.UserActivity|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.App.iOS.UserActivity] API's all have one or more date-properties, all of which require: {quote} The date will be a string in the following format: """"""""yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss.SSS'+0000'"""""""" For example, 2015-12-25T23:30:55.978+0000 {quote} Since Titanium developers work with the JS Date object all the time, we should support that (as well) just like we do in many other API's like [Titanium.App.iOS.LocalNotification|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/NotificationParams-property-date] and [Titanium.UI.Picker|https://<USER>github.io/appc-docs/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Picker-property-maxDate]""""",title+description
TIMOB-19436,12,"""Android: Ti.XML.parseString() did not recognise tag name without namespace ""","""""""h6.Reproduce Step:  1. Simply run the following code in a default project.      h6.Expect Result:  The XML tag should be recongise.    h6.Actual Result:  On android, the tag can't be recongised. But on iOS, it works well.    h6.Note:  If using full tag name with namespace (ns1:EmiratenameEn), it will work well.   But this XML is a response from httpClient, the namespace is changing every time.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.XML.parseString() did not recognise tag name without namespace
Description: """"h6.Reproduce Step: 1. Simply run the following code in a default project. h6.Expect Result: The XML tag should be recongise. h6.Actual Result: On android, the tag can't be recongised. But on iOS, it works well. h6.Note: If using full tag name with namespace (ns1:EmiratenameEn), it will work well. But this XML is a response from httpClient, the namespace is changing every time.""""",title+description
