TIMOB-19360,12,"""Android: Video player is not playing mp4 files on 4.X android & genymotion emulators""","""""""*This issue is seen with SDK 4.1.0.GA as well.*    h5.Steps To Reproduce:  1. Run the code below on 4.X android & genymotion emulator's.      h5. Actual Result:  1. The video player fails to play the video with error:    2. Ran the code on the following android 4.X devices & the video plays successfully with *no* errors:  * Samsung Galaxy S4 - Android 4.4.2  * Samsung Galaxy S3 - Android 4.0.4  * Galaxy Nexus - Android 4.2.2  * Samsung Note - Android 4.3    h5.Expected Results:  1.Video player should play Mp4 videos with no errors on 4.X android & genymotion emulator's   """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Video player is not playing mp4 files on 4.X android & genymotion emulators
Description: """"*This issue is seen with SDK 4.1.0.GA as well.* h5.Steps To Reproduce: 1. Run the code below on 4.X android & genymotion emulator's. h5. Actual Result: 1. The video player fails to play the video with error: 2. Ran the code on the following android 4.X devices & the video plays successfully with *no* errors: * Samsung Galaxy S4 - Android 4.4.2 * Samsung Galaxy S3 - Android 4.0.4 * Galaxy Nexus - Android 4.2.2 * Samsung Note - Android 4.3 h5.Expected Results: 1.Video player should play Mp4 videos with no errors on 4.X android & genymotion emulator's """"",title+description
TIMOB-19359,12,"""Cannot create a Titanium project with CLI 4.1.X and SDK 4.2.0 or 5.0.0""","""""""*Details:* Cannot create a Titanium project with Appc CLI NPM: 4.1.0-2 and Appc CLI Core: 4.1.3-2 with SDK 4.2.0 or 5.0.0.    *Note:* In this configuration, you can still create an Alloy project with just {{appc new}}. However, this is still a blocker because a Titanium project cannot be created.    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Make sure you are using Appc CLI NPM 4.1.0-2, Appc CLI Core 4.1.3-2, and SDK 4.2.0  # Run the following command to create a Titanium project: {{appc new --type titanium --platforms android --id com.<USER>testing --name android --project-dir ~/android --log-level trace --url http:// --subtype new --no-services --force}}    *Actual:* {{Failed to run command """"""""create""""""""}} error will appear:      *Expected:* Should be able to create a Titanium project without any issues.""""""",Bug,"Title: Cannot create a Titanium project with CLI 4.1.X and SDK 4.2.0 or 5.0.0
Description: """"*Details:* Cannot create a Titanium project with Appc CLI NPM: 4.1.0-2 and Appc CLI Core: 4.1.3-2 with SDK 4.2.0 or 5.0.0. *Note:* In this configuration, you can still create an Alloy project with just {{appc new}}. However, this is still a blocker because a Titanium project cannot be created. *Steps to reproduce:* # Make sure you are using Appc CLI NPM 4.1.0-2, Appc CLI Core 4.1.3-2, and SDK 4.2.0 # Run the following command to create a Titanium project: {{appc new --type titanium --platforms android --id com.<USER>testing --name android --project-dir ~/android --log-level trace --url http:// --subtype new --no-services --force}} *Actual:* {{Failed to run command """"""""create""""""""}} error will appear: *Expected:* Should be able to create a Titanium project without any issues.""""",title+description
