TIMOB-19338,12,"""iOS: cacheSize property does not work on XML""","""""""The ScrollableView does not load onto the screen when I assign the cacheSize property in the XML, like:    {code:xml}  <Alloy>      <ScrollableView id=""""""""slider"""""""" cacheSize=5 />  </Alloy>  {code}    It also does not work when I assign a string `cacheSize=""""""""5""""""""`.    Feature seems to work when i add it using .tss:    {code:javascript}  """"""""#slider"""""""": {    cacheSize: 5  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: cacheSize property does not work on XML
Description: """"The ScrollableView does not load onto the screen when I assign the cacheSize property in the XML, like: {code:xml} <Alloy> <ScrollableView id=""""""""slider"""""""" cacheSize=5 /> </Alloy> {code} It also does not work when I assign a string `cacheSize=""""""""5""""""""`. Feature seems to work when i add it using .tss: {code:javascript} """"""""#slider"""""""": { cacheSize: 5 } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-19336,12,"""iOS9: WatchOS2 build settings have wrong values""","""""""Was trying to integrate my work on watch connectivity with the latest timobile SDK. There is an error when communicating between watch and phone simulators, stating that the watch app is not installed, but it is.    Did some investigations and realised that the build settings on my native Xcode project vs the ti build generated Xcode project is different for targets watchapp and watch extension. See attached screenshots to see the difference. basically, the base SDK on watch app and watch extension should be WatchOS2, and not iOS9. I believe we need to change it to WatchOS2 with the correct architecture in order to get the watch app running on WatchOS2.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. *ti create* titanium app  2. enter project folder  3. *ti create* apple watch  4. enter extensions folder and open apple watch Xcode project  5. enter storyboard and add a new label with some text  6. *ti build -p ios -I 9.0 --launch-watch-app*    h4. Actual result  you will see the label with the new text on the watch app, indicating it's correctly working.  However, if you enter the build folder, and open the Xcode project, click on the watch app target and watch app extension target, they are NOT using watchOS2 as base SDK.    h4. Expected result  It is supposed to be watchOS2. We can either automatically force all watch apps to watchOS2 for builds on Xcode 7, or we include a flag to indicate in ti build (or ti create) telling the CLI we want to build for watch kit 1.0 or watch OS2.    *Note*: For watch app and watch extension targets, the base SDK in the build folder generated by *ti build*, *as well as* the base SDK of the Xcode project in the extensions folder created by *ti create*, are not WatchOS2.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS9: WatchOS2 build settings have wrong values
Description: """"Was trying to integrate my work on watch connectivity with the latest timobile SDK. There is an error when communicating between watch and phone simulators, stating that the watch app is not installed, but it is. Did some investigations and realised that the build settings on my native Xcode project vs the ti build generated Xcode project is different for targets watchapp and watch extension. See attached screenshots to see the difference. basically, the base SDK on watch app and watch extension should be WatchOS2, and not iOS9. I believe we need to change it to WatchOS2 with the correct architecture in order to get the watch app running on WatchOS2. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. *ti create* titanium app 2. enter project folder 3. *ti create* apple watch 4. enter extensions folder and open apple watch Xcode project 5. enter storyboard and add a new label with some text 6. *ti build -p ios -I 9.0 --launch-watch-app* h4. Actual result you will see the label with the new text on the watch app, indicating it's correctly working. However, if you enter the build folder, and open the Xcode project, click on the watch app target and watch app extension target, they are NOT using watchOS2 as base SDK. h4. Expected result It is supposed to be watchOS2. We can either automatically force all watch apps to watchOS2 for builds on Xcode 7, or we include a flag to indicate in ti build (or ti create) telling the CLI we want to build for watch kit 1.0 or watch OS2. *Note*: For watch app and watch extension targets, the base SDK in the build folder generated by *ti build*, *as well as* the base SDK of the Xcode project in the extensions folder created by *ti create*, are not WatchOS2.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19334,12,"""iOS: URLSession - large file download in the background - some events are not fired and other issues.""","""""""1. Events not fired. To re-produce, download a large file > 1GB, press """"""""Home"""""""" to make the app go to the background. Once the download finishes, only """"""""backgroundtransfer"""""""" is fired. The other events are not: sessioneventscompleted, downloadcompleted, etc.    Without downloadcompleted, the file can't be saved. Without sessioneventscompleted, the app won't call endBackgroundHandler, and it will run over 30 seconds, eventually being terminated by the system.    I think the problem is that after the download finishes, the file is """"""""copied"""""""" instead of """"""""moved"""""""" to the temp folder (see TIMOB-17502). Copying a large file can take longer than 30 seconds, so the system kills the app before it finishes copying. We should just """"""""move"""""""" it to the temp location. This is also suggested in Apple's docs.    2. If the download fails, the partial file is still copied to the temp folder. I think it should copy only when a download is successful. First, the file is useless. Second, """"""""downloadcompleted is not even called in this situation. The app can't get the handle of the partial file anyway. To re-produce, download a file. During the download, kill the app manually.    Also, in the above test, sometimes """"""""sessioncompleted"""""""" isn't fired right after force closing the app (sometimes it is). The app won't be able to mark the download as failed if this issue happens. Again, I think this happens because the partial file is being copied to the temp folder, and if the file is large enough, """"""""sessioncompleted"""""""" won't get fired before the app exits.    3. When downloading a file (> 1GB) in the background, sometimes I got crash reports like the attached. I don't understand why the app was woken and running in the background over 3 minutes. Please investigate.    4. With a medium size download (2-300MB) in the background, calling endBackgroundHandler when sessioneventscompleted fired throws the following error, and the callback is failed to complete. The size of the file doesn't matter. Use files around 2-300MB so that you can re-produce the issue. I think the issue is endBackgroundHandler itself alone.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: URLSession - large file download in the background - some events are not fired and other issues.
Description: """"1. Events not fired. To re-produce, download a large file > 1GB, press """"""""Home"""""""" to make the app go to the background. Once the download finishes, only """"""""backgroundtransfer"""""""" is fired. The other events are not: sessioneventscompleted, downloadcompleted, etc. Without downloadcompleted, the file can't be saved. Without sessioneventscompleted, the app won't call endBackgroundHandler, and it will run over 30 seconds, eventually being terminated by the system. I think the problem is that after the download finishes, the file is """"""""copied"""""""" instead of """"""""moved"""""""" to the temp folder (see TIMOB-17502). Copying a large file can take longer than 30 seconds, so the system kills the app before it finishes copying. We should just """"""""move"""""""" it to the temp location. This is also suggested in Apple's docs. 2. If the download fails, the partial file is still copied to the temp folder. I think it should copy only when a download is successful. First, the file is useless. Second, """"""""downloadcompleted is not even called in this situation. The app can't get the handle of the partial file anyway. To re-produce, download a file. During the download, kill the app manually. Also, in the above test, sometimes """"""""sessioncompleted"""""""" isn't fired right after force closing the app (sometimes it is). The app won't be able to mark the download as failed if this issue happens. Again, I think this happens because the partial file is being copied to the temp folder, and if the file is large enough, """"""""sessioncompleted"""""""" won't get fired before the app exits. 3. When downloading a file (> 1GB) in the background, sometimes I got crash reports like the attached. I don't understand why the app was woken and running in the background over 3 minutes. Please investigate. 4. With a medium size download (2-300MB) in the background, calling endBackgroundHandler when sessioneventscompleted fired throws the following error, and the callback is failed to complete. The size of the file doesn't matter. Use files around 2-300MB so that you can re-produce the issue. I think the issue is endBackgroundHandler itself alone. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19333,12,"""iOS: URLSession Module not working properly if system terminates the app during download""","""""""If the system terminates the app during a download, after the download finishes (the app remains not running), there are some problems:    1. backgroundtransfer is the last event fired (should be the first)    2. downloadcompleted event handler doesn't get the file blob (evt.data.size==0)    If the system terminates the app during a download, before the download finishes, you launch the app and cancel the download, there is one problem:    1. The partially downloaded file is remained in the storage, not cleaned up. UPDATE: With SDK 4.1.0, it seems the partially downloaded file is cleaned up in this scenario.    These issues didn't exist in previous SDKs, as I've tested it before.    To simulate system terminating the app:    1. download a large enough file    2. during the download, using the Studio to build the app to the device    3. App installed successfully on the device, causing the running instance terminated by the system    4. test the above two scenarios.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: URLSession Module not working properly if system terminates the app during download
Description: """"If the system terminates the app during a download, after the download finishes (the app remains not running), there are some problems: 1. backgroundtransfer is the last event fired (should be the first) 2. downloadcompleted event handler doesn't get the file blob (evt.data.size==0) If the system terminates the app during a download, before the download finishes, you launch the app and cancel the download, there is one problem: 1. The partially downloaded file is remained in the storage, not cleaned up. UPDATE: With SDK 4.1.0, it seems the partially downloaded file is cleaned up in this scenario. These issues didn't exist in previous SDKs, as I've tested it before. To simulate system terminating the app: 1. download a large enough file 2. during the download, using the Studio to build the app to the device 3. App installed successfully on the device, causing the running instance terminated by the system 4. test the above two scenarios.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19332,12,"""Intermittently, if you try to install to an iOS device, then the Appc CLI will install your app to iTunes""","""""""*Details:* Intermittently, if you try to install to an iOS device, then the Appc CLI will install your app to iTunes.    *Possible steps to reproduce:*  # Create a Titanium project from Appc CLI: {{appc new}}  # Install your project to an iOS device: {{appc run -p ios -T device -l trace}}  # Then, clean your project: {{appc ti clean}}  # Install your project again to an iOS device: {{appc run -p ios -T device -l trace}}    *Actual:* Occasionally, the CLI will install your app to iTunes; see below for a short version of the trace logs and see attachment for the verbose trace logs:      *Expected:* The CLI should not install your app to iTunes when you specify to install to device.""""""",Bug,"Title: Intermittently, if you try to install to an iOS device, then the Appc CLI will install your app to iTunes
Description: """"*Details:* Intermittently, if you try to install to an iOS device, then the Appc CLI will install your app to iTunes. *Possible steps to reproduce:* # Create a Titanium project from Appc CLI: {{appc new}} # Install your project to an iOS device: {{appc run -p ios -T device -l trace}} # Then, clean your project: {{appc ti clean}} # Install your project again to an iOS device: {{appc run -p ios -T device -l trace}} *Actual:* Occasionally, the CLI will install your app to iTunes; see below for a short version of the trace logs and see attachment for the verbose trace logs: *Expected:* The CLI should not install your app to iTunes when you specify to install to device.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19327,12,"""ListView - template event handler not working if using """"var"""" declaratoin""","""""""Create a default Alloy project with the following:    index.xml      index.js      On iOS, the function """"""""handler"""""""" is simply not working. On Android, it'll throw exception saying event handler undefined. However, itemclick event works fine.    If we declare function """"""""handler"""""""" like the following, then it works fine on both iOS and Android.      So event handler for template element can't be declared using """"""""var."""""""" This inconsistency could cause confusion to developer.""""""",Bug,"Title: ListView - template event handler not working if using """"var"""" declaratoin
Description: """"Create a default Alloy project with the following: index.xml index.js On iOS, the function """"""""handler"""""""" is simply not working. On Android, it'll throw exception saying event handler undefined. However, itemclick event works fine. If we declare function """"""""handler"""""""" like the following, then it works fine on both iOS and Android. So event handler for template element can't be declared using """"""""var."""""""" This inconsistency could cause confusion to developer.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19323,12,"""CLI: """"Apple Watch™"""" should be changed to """"Apple Watch""""""","""""""h5. Description:  Since we are providing a disclaimer in the help, it is not necessary to include the """"""""™"""""""" in the text of the Titanium CLI """"""""ti create"""""""" command or in """"""""help"""""""" or elsewhere.        h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Install SDK 4.2.0+ (master as of today's date)  2) Install Titanium NPM package with """"""""sudo npm install -g titanium""""""""  3) Create a new project with """"""""ti create"""""""" - note the output  OR  3) Get help with """"""""ti create -h"""""""" - note the output    h5. Result:  """"""""Apple Watch™"""""""" appears in multiple places    h5. Expected Result:  No """"""""™"""""""" needed.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"Apple Watch™"""" should be changed to """"Apple Watch""""
Description: """"h5. Description: Since we are providing a disclaimer in the help, it is not necessary to include the """"""""™"""""""" in the text of the Titanium CLI """"""""ti create"""""""" command or in """"""""help"""""""" or elsewhere. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install SDK 4.2.0+ (master as of today's date) 2) Install Titanium NPM package with """"""""sudo npm install -g titanium"""""""" 3) Create a new project with """"""""ti create"""""""" - note the output OR 3) Get help with """"""""ti create -h"""""""" - note the output h5. Result: """"""""Apple Watch™"""""""" appears in multiple places h5. Expected Result: No """"""""™"""""""" needed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19321,12,"""Glitch/Bug in Universal Unit Support in Ti SDK 4.0.1 and 4.1.0""","""""""I noticed a strange difference in behavior between Titanium SDK after version 3.5.1 when it comes to images that are created from a view and then saved to the device's file system.    In the code example below, Ti SDK 3.5.1 produces an image file that is 240 dp x 320 dp, which is my desired outcome; in Ti SDK 4.0.0/4.1.0 however, the image that is created is 240 px x 320 px (i.e., 720 x 960 when created on iPhone 6 Plus):    *Setting in tiapp.xml:*  {quote}...      <property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""" type=""""""""string"""""""">dp</property>  ...{quote}    *View in /app/views/index.xml:*    {quote}    <View id=""""""""lgImageContainer"""""""" width=""""""""240"""""""" height=""""""""320"""""""">          <ImageView id=""""""""lgImageMaker"""""""" width=""""""""240"""""""" height=""""""""620""""""""/>      </View>  {quote}    *In /app/controllers/index.js:*    {quote}var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory, 'INPUT.jpg').read();  $.lgImageMaker.image = f;  var b = $.lgImageContainer.toImage();  var m = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory, 'OUTPUT.png');  m.write(b);{quote}    I can replicate the behavior described above 100% of the time simply by switching between SDK 3.5.1 and either 4.0.1 or 4.1.0.    Let me know if there is any other information I can provide that will help troubleshoot this.    Thanks.""""""",Bug,"Title: Glitch/Bug in Universal Unit Support in Ti SDK 4.0.1 and 4.1.0
Description: """"I noticed a strange difference in behavior between Titanium SDK after version 3.5.1 when it comes to images that are created from a view and then saved to the device's file system. In the code example below, Ti SDK 3.5.1 produces an image file that is 240 dp x 320 dp, which is my desired outcome; in Ti SDK 4.0.0/4.1.0 however, the image that is created is 240 px x 320 px (i.e., 720 x 960 when created on iPhone 6 Plus): *Setting in tiapp.xml:* {quote}... <property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""" type=""""""""string"""""""">dp</property> ...{quote} *View in /app/views/index.xml:* {quote} <View id=""""""""lgImageContainer"""""""" width=""""""""240"""""""" height=""""""""320""""""""> <ImageView id=""""""""lgImageMaker"""""""" width=""""""""240"""""""" height=""""""""620""""""""/> </View> {quote} *In /app/controllers/index.js:* {quote}var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory, 'INPUT.jpg').read(); $.lgImageMaker.image = f; var b = $.lgImageContainer.toImage(); var m = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory, 'OUTPUT.png'); m.write(b);{quote} I can replicate the behavior described above 100% of the time simply by switching between SDK 3.5.1 and either 4.0.1 or 4.1.0. Let me know if there is any other information I can provide that will help troubleshoot this. Thanks.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19317,12,"""iOS: Navigation Buttons have different margins when using title or backgroundImage""","""""""In xml create a NavigationWindow with a Left and Right Nav Button.  Set the title for one and the backgroundImage for the other.    The margins do not match and are very difficult to align.    The margin when using title appears to be the appropriate size.    See sample xml and tss to recreate.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Navigation Buttons have different margins when using title or backgroundImage
Description: """"In xml create a NavigationWindow with a Left and Right Nav Button. Set the title for one and the backgroundImage for the other. The margins do not match and are very difficult to align. The margin when using title appears to be the appropriate size. See sample xml and tss to recreate.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19316,12,"""iOS: App with WatchKit 1.0 fails to build if watch extension app project is edited""","""""""When i tried to add a label to the interface.storyboard on watchkit app, *ti build -p ios --launch-watch-app* will fail to build with the following message:  {quote}  [TRACE] [ioslib] Running: /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/simctl install C06EE826-1875-4966-9C6E-605797352883 /Users/kiat/titaniumTestWatch/SGTestWatch2/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator/SGTestWatch2.app  [TRACE] [ioslib] Watch App installation failure: <SPCompanionAppServer.m __51-[SPCompanionAppServer sendToRemoteInterface:call:]_block_invoke_3:903> ERROR: App extension not active: SPExtensionTerminatedCommand: com.<USER>sg.SGTestWatch2.watchkitapp 0x7fbdf4314d00  [ERROR] Watch App installation failure: <SPCompanionAppServer.m __51-[SPCompanionAppServer sendToRemoteInterface:call:]_block_invoke_3:903> ERROR: App extension not active: SPExtensionTerminatedCommand: com.<USER>sg.SGTestWatch2.watchkitapp 0x7fbdf4314d00  {quote}    h4. steps to reproduce  1. *ti create* titanium app  2. enter app folder  3. *ti create* apple watch  4. go to the created extensions folder and open the Xcode project  5. in the storyboard file, under watch kit app, add in a label with any text  6. *ti build -p ios --launch-watch-app*    h4. expected result  iphone simulator and watch external display will appear, with the edited text    h4. actual result  build fails with above message    *Note* If we don't edit the Xcode project, *ti build -p ios --launch-watch-app* will work and show the simulator and external display.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App with WatchKit 1.0 fails to build if watch extension app project is edited
Description: """"When i tried to add a label to the interface.storyboard on watchkit app, *ti build -p ios --launch-watch-app* will fail to build with the following message: {quote} [TRACE] [ioslib] Running: /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/simctl install C06EE826-1875-4966-9C6E-605797352883 /Users/kiat/titaniumTestWatch/SGTestWatch2/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator/SGTestWatch2.app [TRACE] [ioslib] Watch App installation failure: <SPCompanionAppServer.m __51-[SPCompanionAppServer sendToRemoteInterface:call:]_block_invoke_3:903> ERROR: App extension not active: SPExtensionTerminatedCommand: com.<USER>sg.SGTestWatch2.watchkitapp 0x7fbdf4314d00 [ERROR] Watch App installation failure: <SPCompanionAppServer.m __51-[SPCompanionAppServer sendToRemoteInterface:call:]_block_invoke_3:903> ERROR: App extension not active: SPExtensionTerminatedCommand: com.<USER>sg.SGTestWatch2.watchkitapp 0x7fbdf4314d00 {quote} h4. steps to reproduce 1. *ti create* titanium app 2. enter app folder 3. *ti create* apple watch 4. go to the created extensions folder and open the Xcode project 5. in the storyboard file, under watch kit app, add in a label with any text 6. *ti build -p ios --launch-watch-app* h4. expected result iphone simulator and watch external display will appear, with the edited text h4. actual result build fails with above message *Note* If we don't edit the Xcode project, *ti build -p ios --launch-watch-app* will work and show the simulator and external display.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19314,12,"""Android Map doesn't compile with 4.1.0.GA""","""""""Building map module with 4.1.0.GA result in with this error:     [javac]    KrollDict d = ((TiViewProxy) obj).toImage();      [javac]                                             ^      [javac]   required: KrollDict      [javac]   found:    TiBlob      [javac] Note: Some input files use unchecked or unsafe operations.      [javac] Note: Recompile with -Xlint:unchecked for details.      [javac] 1 error      [javac] 10 warnings    This is the result of a method signature change in: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6907    Reproducible steps:  1. Build the module with 4.1.0.GA and observe the logs.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Map doesn't compile with 4.1.0.GA
Description: """"Building map module with 4.1.0.GA result in with this error: [javac] KrollDict d = ((TiViewProxy) obj).toImage(); [javac] ^ [javac] required: KrollDict [javac] found: TiBlob [javac] Note: Some input files use unchecked or unsafe operations. [javac] Note: Recompile with -Xlint:unchecked for details. [javac] 1 error [javac] 10 warnings This is the result of a method signature change in: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6907 Reproducible steps: 1. Build the module with 4.1.0.GA and observe the logs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19313,12,"""iOS: appc info -t ios command lists device not physically connected""","""""""h5. Description:  While doing some testing, I had my personal device """"""""<USER>s 6"""""""" sitting on my desk. After a few test installs to a device called """"""""newton"""""""" I got this error:      Since I didn't have my device connected I was surprised to see it in the list of available devices. Doing some investigation I noted that """"""""newton"""""""" seemed to be available unreliably when this issue occurs. Meaning if """"""""<USER>s 6"""""""" is listed, """"""""newton"""""""" may not be in the list. It was sometimes however, as shown here:      *Please note:*  iTunes wireless sync was not enabled, and iTunes running did not have an effect on this issue.  My device is on the same wifi network. When wifi is turned off on the phone it isn't visible to """"""""appc info""""""""  """"""""newton"""""""" device is mostly not available when my phone is awake and listed in the appc info output    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Connect a device via cable to test machine running Mac OS 10.10.x or better  2) run command  - verify device is visible  3) Using additional device connected to same wifi as Mac system, wake it up  4) run     h5. Result:  Physically connected device is no longer shown in output. Wireless device is listed in output but can't be installed to.    h5. Expected Result:  Only physically connected devices are shown in """"""""appc ti info"""""""" output     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: appc info -t ios command lists device not physically connected
Description: """"h5. Description: While doing some testing, I had my personal device """"""""<USER>s 6"""""""" sitting on my desk. After a few test installs to a device called """"""""newton"""""""" I got this error: Since I didn't have my device connected I was surprised to see it in the list of available devices. Doing some investigation I noted that """"""""newton"""""""" seemed to be available unreliably when this issue occurs. Meaning if """"""""<USER>s 6"""""""" is listed, """"""""newton"""""""" may not be in the list. It was sometimes however, as shown here: *Please note:* iTunes wireless sync was not enabled, and iTunes running did not have an effect on this issue. My device is on the same wifi network. When wifi is turned off on the phone it isn't visible to """"""""appc info"""""""" """"""""newton"""""""" device is mostly not available when my phone is awake and listed in the appc info output h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Connect a device via cable to test machine running Mac OS 10.10.x or better 2) run command - verify device is visible 3) Using additional device connected to same wifi as Mac system, wake it up 4) run h5. Result: Physically connected device is no longer shown in output. Wireless device is listed in output but can't be installed to. h5. Expected Result: Only physically connected devices are shown in """"""""appc ti info"""""""" output """"",title+description
TIMOB-19310,12,"""Indie Plan: Cannot package to iOS Adhoc/Enterprise ""","""""""h6.Issue Description  When you want to package an """"""""<USER>iOS Ad Hoc_Enterprise Distribution"""""""" Studio Dashboard asked to change plan whereas I am already on Indie plan.    h6.Steps to Reproduce  1. Login to <USER>Studio/CLI/Dashboard using Indie plan credentials.  2. Attempt packaging app """"""""iOS Adhoc/Enterprise"""""""" option   3. Studio takes Plan Details over and over again. """"""",Bug,"Title: Indie Plan: Cannot package to iOS Adhoc/Enterprise
Description: """"h6.Issue Description When you want to package an """"""""<USER>iOS Ad Hoc_Enterprise Distribution"""""""" Studio Dashboard asked to change plan whereas I am already on Indie plan. h6.Steps to Reproduce 1. Login to <USER>Studio/CLI/Dashboard using Indie plan credentials. 2. Attempt packaging app """"""""iOS Adhoc/Enterprise"""""""" option 3. Studio takes Plan Details over and over again. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19309,12,"""Cannot install to iOS device with latest SDK""","""""""*Details:* With the latest SDK, you cannot install to an iOS device from Titanium CLI; you will get {{Specified .app path is not a valid app}} error message. And, if you do a {{ti clean}} and build to device again, CLI will install to iTunes.    *This is a regression from SDK 4.2.0.v20150729122818 i.e. was working on July 29.*    *Note:* *This will affect Appc CLI.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a Titanium project  2. Install project to iOS device: {{ti build -p ios -T device -l trace}}    *Actual:* You are not able to install to device and the following error will appear:      3. Run {{ti clean}}  4. Install project to device again: {{ti build -p ios -T device -l trace}}    *Actual:* CLI will install to iTunes:      *Expected:* Should be able to install app to device.""""""",Bug,"Title: Cannot install to iOS device with latest SDK
Description: """"*Details:* With the latest SDK, you cannot install to an iOS device from Titanium CLI; you will get {{Specified .app path is not a valid app}} error message. And, if you do a {{ti clean}} and build to device again, CLI will install to iTunes. *This is a regression from SDK 4.2.0.v20150729122818 i.e. was working on July 29.* *Note:* *This will affect Appc CLI.* *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a Titanium project 2. Install project to iOS device: {{ti build -p ios -T device -l trace}} *Actual:* You are not able to install to device and the following error will appear: 3. Run {{ti clean}} 4. Install project to device again: {{ti build -p ios -T device -l trace}} *Actual:* CLI will install to iTunes: *Expected:* Should be able to install app to device.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19307,12,"""iOS: ListView with custom template shows nothing""","""""""When navigating to and from a ListView that has a custom template, sometimes the view stays completely empty. This is a 100% reoccuring issue in our project when following these steps:  1. Open List View (content visible)  2. Navigate back (iOS Navigation bar back button)  3. Open List View (content not visible)  All further trys except for the second one result in the content being visible.    *This issue is only related to the newest version of the studio. Version 4.0 works fine.*""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ListView with custom template shows nothing
Description: """"When navigating to and from a ListView that has a custom template, sometimes the view stays completely empty. This is a 100% reoccuring issue in our project when following these steps: 1. Open List View (content visible) 2. Navigate back (iOS Navigation bar back button) 3. Open List View (content not visible) All further trys except for the second one result in the content being visible. *This issue is only related to the newest version of the studio. Version 4.0 works fine.*""""",title+description
TIMOB-19306,12,"""MobileWeb: Option Dialog UI does not fire when click on the option button in Mobile Web""","""""""when create an option dialog box, it show normally but when click on any button will not fire anything, and the option dialog keep showing no matter what you click     try the following code on mobile web and you will see    Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('white');  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    title: 'Click window to test',    backgroundColor: 'white',    exitOnClose: true,    fullscreen: false  });    var opts = {    cancel: 2,    options: ['Confirm', 'Help', 'Cancel'],    selectedIndex: 2,    destructive: 0,    title: 'Delete File?'  };    win.addEventListener('click', function(e){    var dialog = Ti.UI.createOptionDialog(opts).show();  });  win.open();      """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Option Dialog UI does not fire when click on the option button in Mobile Web
Description: """"when create an option dialog box, it show normally but when click on any button will not fire anything, and the option dialog keep showing no matter what you click try the following code on mobile web and you will see Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('white'); var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Click window to test', backgroundColor: 'white', exitOnClose: true, fullscreen: false }); var opts = { cancel: 2, options: ['Confirm', 'Help', 'Cancel'], selectedIndex: 2, destructive: 0, title: 'Delete File?' }; win.addEventListener('click', function(e){ var dialog = Ti.UI.createOptionDialog(opts).show(); }); win.open(); """"",title+description
TIMOB-19298,12,"""Develop a Titanium Asset Management System""","""""""Titanium needs a cross-platform asset management system for managing system controlled resources (launch screens) and application specific assets (image sets, etc). During build time, files are copied to specific destinations and an index is compiled.    For iOS, assets would be tranformed into an Asset Catalog and automatically resolve naming conflicts.    For Android, certain assets would be copied into the {{res}} directory.    Not sure about Windows.    When a platform goes to resolve an asset, it needs to check the compiled asset index before checking the filesystem.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Develop a Titanium Asset Management System
Description: """"Titanium needs a cross-platform asset management system for managing system controlled resources (launch screens) and application specific assets (image sets, etc). During build time, files are copied to specific destinations and an index is compiled. For iOS, assets would be tranformed into an Asset Catalog and automatically resolve naming conflicts. For Android, certain assets would be copied into the {{res}} directory. Not sure about Windows. When a platform goes to resolve an asset, it needs to check the compiled asset index before checking the filesystem.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19296,12,"""iOS9: Update image related methods to support the use of assets catalogs""","""""""Currently, titanium image related methods expect a local or remote url. Assets catalog work by finding the image based on just the name of the image.  So we have to modify the methods such that, it will first check if the assets catalog exist and contains the image, if it doesn't, then it will proceed as usual to treat it as a local or remote url.""""""",Technical task,"Title: iOS9: Update image related methods to support the use of assets catalogs
Description: """"Currently, titanium image related methods expect a local or remote url. Assets catalog work by finding the image based on just the name of the image. So we have to modify the methods such that, it will first check if the assets catalog exist and contains the image, if it doesn't, then it will proceed as usual to treat it as a local or remote url.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19295,12,"""iOS9: Titanium CLI automatically converts existing images to assets catalog""","""""""*Need titanium CLI to be able to *  1. generate a default Media.xcassets folder in xcode project  2. transfer existing image files in titanium project into this folder  3. generate corresponding Contents.json file    *Note*  - Details in the Contents.json and folder naming and structure will be based on existing titanium naming convention i.e. <EMAIL>, <EMAIL> etc.  - Ignore Android specific images. only consider iOS specific, and common platform images.""""""",Technical task,"Title: iOS9: Titanium CLI automatically converts existing images to assets catalog
Description: """"*Need titanium CLI to be able to * 1. generate a default Media.xcassets folder in xcode project 2. transfer existing image files in titanium project into this folder 3. generate corresponding Contents.json file *Note* - Details in the Contents.json and folder naming and structure will be based on existing titanium naming convention i.e. <EMAIL>, <EMAIL> etc. - Ignore Android specific images. only consider iOS specific, and common platform images.""""",title+description
