TIMOB-19285,12,"""iOS: App throws error when building to device with commonjs modules""","""""""h5.Description    When building to a device and including commonjs modules the app will crash with {{\[ERROR] Script Error Couldn't find module: ti.cloud for architecture: arm64}}. Requiring modules such as ti.map work fine.    *When building to simulator the app works fine*    h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Create a project using {{appc new}} and ensure services are enabled  2.Build to device    h5.Actual result    The app will crash with {{\[ERROR] Script Error Couldn't find module: ti.cloud for architecture: arm64}}    h5.Expected result    The app should not crash""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App throws error when building to device with commonjs modules
Description: """"h5.Description When building to a device and including commonjs modules the app will crash with {{\[ERROR] Script Error Couldn't find module: ti.cloud for architecture: arm64}}. Requiring modules such as ti.map work fine. *When building to simulator the app works fine* h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Create a project using {{appc new}} and ensure services are enabled 2.Build to device h5.Actual result The app will crash with {{\[ERROR] Script Error Couldn't find module: ti.cloud for architecture: arm64}} h5.Expected result The app should not crash""""",title+description
TIMOB-19284,12,"""xcode-select is not being respected by """"appc run -p ios""""""","""""""*Details:* If you have two Xcode versions in a single folder (e.g. /Applications) and have {{xcode-select -s}} pointing to the *older* version, then {{appc run -p ios}} will launch the latest iOS simulator from the *newer* Xcode.    *Note:* To workaround this, you can specify the I flag to launch the simulator from Xcode 6.4: {{appc run -I 8.4 -p ios}}    *Steps to reproduce:*  # Have both Xcode 6.4 and Xcode 7 (beta 4) in one folder e.g. {{/Applications}}  # Make xcode-select point to Xcode 6.4: {{sudo xcode-select -s <PATH_TO_XCODE_6.4>}}  # Create a project with {{appc new}}  # Then, run with {{appc run -p ios}}  # Wait for simulator to launch    *Actual:* iOS simulator 9.0 from Xcode 7 (beta 4) is launched instead; see attachment.  *Expected:* iOS simulator 8.4 from Xcode 6.4 should be launched.""""""",Bug,"Title: xcode-select is not being respected by """"appc run -p ios""""
Description: """"*Details:* If you have two Xcode versions in a single folder (e.g. /Applications) and have {{xcode-select -s}} pointing to the *older* version, then {{appc run -p ios}} will launch the latest iOS simulator from the *newer* Xcode. *Note:* To workaround this, you can specify the I flag to launch the simulator from Xcode 6.4: {{appc run -I 8.4 -p ios}} *Steps to reproduce:* # Have both Xcode 6.4 and Xcode 7 (beta 4) in one folder e.g. {{/Applications}} # Make xcode-select point to Xcode 6.4: {{sudo xcode-select -s <PATH_TO_XCODE_6.4>}} # Create a project with {{appc new}} # Then, run with {{appc run -p ios}} # Wait for simulator to launch *Actual:* iOS simulator 9.0 from Xcode 7 (beta 4) is launched instead; see attachment. *Expected:* iOS simulator 8.4 from Xcode 6.4 should be launched.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19283,12,"""Cannot build to iOS 9 device using appc run""","""""""An error is shown while trying to build to a iOS 9 device    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a new titanium project using """"""""appc new""""""""  2. Go to the project folder and try to build the project to iOS 9 device using """"""""appc run"""""""" or """"""""appc ti build""""""""    Actual Result:  An error is shown  """"""",Bug,"Title: Cannot build to iOS 9 device using appc run
Description: """"An error is shown while trying to build to a iOS 9 device Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a new titanium project using """"""""appc new"""""""" 2. Go to the project folder and try to build the project to iOS 9 device using """"""""appc run"""""""" or """"""""appc ti build"""""""" Actual Result: An error is shown """"",title+description
TIMOB-19280,12,"""iOS: MAP Click event not returning clicksource properly""","""""""Using the same code on 3.5.1 and 4.0,4.1    In 3.5.1 the annotation clicksource reports properly (leftpane, rightpane, pin, etc) the same code on 4.0 or 4.1 does not report any of the annotation clicksource options, only 'pin'. Once the annotation is highlighted, clicking on any part of the annotation callout does NOT fire the click event.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: MAP Click event not returning clicksource properly
Description: """"Using the same code on 3.5.1 and 4.0,4.1 In 3.5.1 the annotation clicksource reports properly (leftpane, rightpane, pin, etc) the same code on 4.0 or 4.1 does not report any of the annotation clicksource options, only 'pin'. Once the annotation is highlighted, clicking on any part of the annotation callout does NOT fire the click event.""""",title+description
