TIMOB-19197,12,"""Out of memory problems with backgroundImage property on Android""","""""""My app earlier used a number of rather large jpg images, but it worked well with Android devices even on the markets, after upgrading to SDK 5.02 on Android along with Ti SDK 4 the build now looks very different. It uses art: messages and tries to alloc the same amount of memory unsuccessfully. I have to decrease the amount of images loaded, unfortunately affecting our app much.     This is the error log:    It repeats it self many times and then crashes. I have to decrease or remove the images and then it builds, but I am surprised that before it worked well and after upgrade there now seem to be a lower limit to image sizes supported somewhere in the stack.    :(    art: Clamp target GC heap from 207MB to 192MB  [INFO] :   art: Alloc concurrent mark sweep GC freed 3(96B) AllocSpace objects, 0(0B) LOS objects, 0% free, 191MB/192MB, paused 955us total 19.905ms  [ERROR] :  art: Throwing OutOfMemoryError """"""""Failed to allocate a 4194316 byte allocation with 499367 free bytes and 487KB until OOM""""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: Out of memory problems with backgroundImage property on Android
Description: """"My app earlier used a number of rather large jpg images, but it worked well with Android devices even on the markets, after upgrading to SDK 5.02 on Android along with Ti SDK 4 the build now looks very different. It uses art: messages and tries to alloc the same amount of memory unsuccessfully. I have to decrease the amount of images loaded, unfortunately affecting our app much. This is the error log: It repeats it self many times and then crashes. I have to decrease or remove the images and then it builds, but I am surprised that before it worked well and after upgrade there now seem to be a lower limit to image sizes supported somewhere in the stack. :( art: Clamp target GC heap from 207MB to 192MB [INFO] : art: Alloc concurrent mark sweep GC freed 3(96B) AllocSpace objects, 0(0B) LOS objects, 0% free, 191MB/192MB, paused 955us total 19.905ms [ERROR] : art: Throwing OutOfMemoryError """"""""Failed to allocate a 4194316 byte allocation with 499367 free bytes and 487KB until OOM""""""""""""",title+description
TIMOB-19191,12,"""alloy.js file is not recreated by build procedure""","""""""# Use an alloy project  # Delete file alloy.js in ..\plugins\ti.alloy\hooks folder  # Delete everything in the Resources folder  # Run build    *Result:* Build is broken as alloy pre-processor do not start    *Expected:* The alloy.js is re-created by build procedure and build procedure proceeds with the alloy pre-processor    At the same time build recovers alloy.js the if something is changed manually inside of the file.  Btw, is that right to attach the alloy.js file to the project structure? Imho, the file belongs to the build procedures. No? """"""",Bug,"Title: alloy.js file is not recreated by build procedure
Description: """"# Use an alloy project # Delete file alloy.js in ..\plugins\ti.alloy\hooks folder # Delete everything in the Resources folder # Run build *Result:* Build is broken as alloy pre-processor do not start *Expected:* The alloy.js is re-created by build procedure and build procedure proceeds with the alloy pre-processor At the same time build recovers alloy.js the if something is changed manually inside of the file. Btw, is that right to attach the alloy.js file to the project structure? Imho, the file belongs to the build procedures. No? """"",title+description
