TIMOB-19141,12,"""Parity: Support Ti.UI.ListView.seperatorStyle on Android""","""""""Basically map to setting dividerHeight to 0 when TIMOB-19140 is resolved.    Move constants from the iPhone NS:    * {{Titanium.UI.iPhone.ListViewSeparatorStyle.NONE}} > {{Titanium.UI.ListViewSeparatorStyle.NONE}}  * {{Titanium.UI.iPhone.ListViewSeparatorStyle.SINGLE_LINE}} > {{Titanium.UI.ListViewSeparatorStyle.SINGLE_LINE}}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Parity: Support Ti.UI.ListView.seperatorStyle on Android
Description: """"Basically map to setting dividerHeight to 0 when TIMOB-19140 is resolved. Move constants from the iPhone NS: * {{Titanium.UI.iPhone.ListViewSeparatorStyle.NONE}} > {{Titanium.UI.ListViewSeparatorStyle.NONE}} * {{Titanium.UI.iPhone.ListViewSeparatorStyle.SINGLE_LINE}} > {{Titanium.UI.ListViewSeparatorStyle.SINGLE_LINE}}""""",title+description
TIMOB-19134,12,"""CLI: The reported architecture in the information banner is for the node process rather than the OS architecture""","""""""h5.Description  The architecture reported in the information banner on build is for the architecture of Node rather than the OS architecture.  For example if I run 32-bit Node on 64-bit Windows then the following is reported        [This is a Node issue|https://github.com/joyent/node/issues/2862]    h5.Steps To Reproduce     1. On a 64-bit Windows machine install 32-bit Node   2. Run an build comand to show the banner {{appc run -p android -T device --build-only}}     h5.Actual Result     32-bit is shown as the architecture     h5.Expected Result     64-bit should be shown""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: The reported architecture in the information banner is for the node process rather than the OS architecture
Description: """"h5.Description The architecture reported in the information banner on build is for the architecture of Node rather than the OS architecture. For example if I run 32-bit Node on 64-bit Windows then the following is reported [This is a Node issue|https://github.com/joyent/node/issues/2862] h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. On a 64-bit Windows machine install 32-bit Node 2. Run an build comand to show the banner {{appc run -p android -T device --build-only}} h5.Actual Result 32-bit is shown as the architecture h5.Expected Result 64-bit should be shown""""",title+description
