TIMOB-19113,12,"""Platform-specific resources copied into builds for platforms not available in SDK/on OS""","""""""This probably includes TIMOB-19112.    Compile the following Alloy app for the Windows SDK:  https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti410    As the first screenshot shows the {{Resources}} folder only has a {{windows}} folder.    Still, as the second screenshots shows the {{build/windows/Assets}} folder has a {{iphone}} folder which can only have been copied straight from {{app/assets/iphone}}. Furthermore, while the compiled Alloy app from {{Resources/windows}} is there in the root, the icons and splash screens which where there as well are missing.""""""",Bug,"Title: Platform-specific resources copied into builds for platforms not available in SDK/on OS
Description: """"This probably includes TIMOB-19112. Compile the following Alloy app for the Windows SDK: https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/appc-sample-ti410 As the first screenshot shows the {{Resources}} folder only has a {{windows}} folder. Still, as the second screenshots shows the {{build/windows/Assets}} folder has a {{iphone}} folder which can only have been copied straight from {{app/assets/iphone}}. Furthermore, while the compiled Alloy app from {{Resources/windows}} is there in the root, the icons and splash screens which where there as well are missing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19110,12,"""iOS: Animation to height '0dp' and back to a greater height fails""","""""""https://developer.<USER>com/question/173546/animation-not-working-on-iphone    This post describes the bug perfectly. What happens is that as soon as you animate an object to height 0, it wont allow you to animate back again to a greater height.        second animation wont play. Ive tried running it in the callback of the 1st, but it has the same result. I tested it on a Ti.UI.View element, but i guess it applies to all""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Animation to height '0dp' and back to a greater height fails
Description: """"https://developer.<USER>com/question/173546/animation-not-working-on-iphone This post describes the bug perfectly. What happens is that as soon as you animate an object to height 0, it wont allow you to animate back again to a greater height. second animation wont play. Ive tried running it in the callback of the 1st, but it has the same result. I tested it on a Ti.UI.View element, but i guess it applies to all""""",title+description
