Description: """"h5. Steps To Reproduce: 1. Use the code below in your app.js: 2. Build for windows device/emulator. 3. After the app launches click on any row. h5.Actual Result: 1. The alert shows [object object] rather than row data. h5.Expected Result: 1. The alert should the row value. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19064,12,"""Adding TableView to a default Alloy project results in invisible items""","""""""Reported via Q&A:  https://community.<USER>com/topic/794/very-basic-start-with-tableview/12    The default Alloy app sets the backgroundColor of the Window to white. When you add a simple TableView and populate it with a data array instead of TableViewRows, the titles will by default be white as well on Android, which makes them invisible on the white background.    We should either force the same default colours for Windows, Labels, TableViewRow etc for all platforms (probably in the SDK, not in Alloy TSS), or set none at all, which would in this case have resulted in a dark background and visible white titles on Android.""""""",Bug,"Title: Adding TableView to a default Alloy project results in invisible items
Description: """"Reported via Q&A: https://community.<USER>com/topic/794/very-basic-start-with-tableview/12 The default Alloy app sets the backgroundColor of the Window to white. When you add a simple TableView and populate it with a data array instead of TableViewRows, the titles will by default be white as well on Android, which makes them invisible on the white background. We should either force the same default colours for Windows, Labels, TableViewRow etc for all platforms (probably in the SDK, not in Alloy TSS), or set none at all, which would in this case have resulted in a dark background and visible white titles on Android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19060,12,"""Cannot run Appc Studio in """"Debug"""" mode when on VPN""","""""""h6.Issue Description  For <USER>Studio:     (1) Run and Debug work fine for our iOS app in the simulator on our corporate network.     (2) Run and Debug work fine for our iOS app in the simulator when I'm home on my wireless network.     (3) When connected to our Enterprise network from home (using our Cisco AnyConnect VPN client over my wireless network):   (a) Run works fine.   (b) Debug does not work.     For this last case, the simulator starts up, the desktop shows, the splash screen shows, and then I eventually see the attached dialog in Studio and this in the Studio console:     """"""",Bug,"Title: Cannot run Appc Studio in """"Debug"""" mode when on VPN
Description: """"h6.Issue Description For <USER>Studio: (1) Run and Debug work fine for our iOS app in the simulator on our corporate network. (2) Run and Debug work fine for our iOS app in the simulator when I'm home on my wireless network. (3) When connected to our Enterprise network from home (using our Cisco AnyConnect VPN client over my wireless network): (a) Run works fine. (b) Debug does not work. For this last case, the simulator starts up, the desktop shows, the splash screen shows, and then I eventually see the attached dialog in Studio and this in the Studio console: """"",title+description
TIMOB-19053,12,"""Expose date of build (UTC) via `Ti.App.buildDate`""","""""""Just like we have {{Ti.buildDate}} it would be nice to have {{Ti.App.buildDate}} for the date (UTC) when the app was build.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Expose date of build (UTC) via `Ti.App.buildDate`
Description: """"Just like we have {{Ti.buildDate}} it would be nice to have {{Ti.App.buildDate}} for the date (UTC) when the app was build.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19050,12,"""Android: onNewIntent event not being thrown""","""""""h3. Issue    When calling an intent the onNewIntent event is not being thrown.    h3.Test case        h3. Steps to reproduce    1. Run the test case  2. Introduce a message in the textfield   3. Press the send button    Expected Result  After receiving the local notification the message textfield will throw the newIntent event and show the sent message or a """"""""No data received"""""""" message    Actual Result  The newIntent event is not thrown   """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: onNewIntent event not being thrown
Description: """"h3. Issue When calling an intent the onNewIntent event is not being thrown. h3.Test case h3. Steps to reproduce 1. Run the test case 2. Introduce a message in the textfield 3. Press the send button Expected Result After receiving the local notification the message textfield will throw the newIntent event and show the sent message or a """"""""No data received"""""""" message Actual Result The newIntent event is not thrown """"",title+description
TIMOB-19049,12,"""iOS9: investigate how best to support App Thinning""","""""""With iOS 9, Apple is introducing App Thinning, a means of repackaging the application for specific devices requirements so only the right assets are downloaded, reducing the overall download size required.    One way that this will be accomplished is by utilizing the image asset library storage mechanism for iOS Apps. The asset library allows users to specify different assets etc for different devices/screen resolutions.    Additionally dynamic content downloads are also used (think game levels) as well.    """"""",Story,"Title: iOS9: investigate how best to support App Thinning
Description: """"With iOS 9, Apple is introducing App Thinning, a means of repackaging the application for specific devices requirements so only the right assets are downloaded, reducing the overall download size required. One way that this will be accomplished is by utilizing the image asset library storage mechanism for iOS Apps. The asset library allows users to specify different assets etc for different devices/screen resolutions. Additionally dynamic content downloads are also used (think game levels) as well. """"",title+description
TIMOB-19047,12,"""Windows: Cmake should support PRIResource element""","""""""In order to make Windows resource management classes work with {{cmake}}, we need a way to handle Windows string resource files {{*.resw}} with cmake. (See [How to load string resources (XAML)|https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/xaml/hh965323.aspx] for details). The problem is tha it looks like latest {{cmake}} doesn't support {{PRIResource}} element for Visual Studio project, which is used to create link to the resource files.     Currently it is not a problem for Titanium CLI build <USER>because CLI is able to add those lines from template by updating {{.vcxproj}} files manually. This ticket is mainly for calling for attention on build <USER>using cmake.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Cmake should support PRIResource element
Description: """"In order to make Windows resource management classes work with {{cmake}}, we need a way to handle Windows string resource files {{*.resw}} with cmake. (See [How to load string resources (XAML)|https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/xaml/hh965323.aspx] for details). The problem is tha it looks like latest {{cmake}} doesn't support {{PRIResource}} element for Visual Studio project, which is used to create link to the resource files. Currently it is not a problem for Titanium CLI build <USER>because CLI is able to add those lines from template by updating {{.vcxproj}} files manually. This ticket is mainly for calling for attention on build <USER>using cmake.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19046,12,"""Android: error with requestWithGraphPath and facebook sdk 4.0.3""","""""""I have just started working with <USER>Studio. But when I try to use the new facebook sdk 4.0.3 I no longer use the follow request:      I have made the following changes, found in the documentation of the module Facebook in <USER>documentation:  http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Modules.Facebook    1) Add         in tiapp.xml file    2) Add      in platform/android/res/values/strings.xml file  3) Add      in index.js file  4) Add      But the result are these errors:      for android platform      for iOS platform    The same request was working with the facebook module ver 3.x.x""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: error with requestWithGraphPath and facebook sdk 4.0.3
Description: """"I have just started working with <USER>Studio. But when I try to use the new facebook sdk 4.0.3 I no longer use the follow request: I have made the following changes, found in the documentation of the module Facebook in <USER>documentation: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Modules.Facebook 1) Add in tiapp.xml file 2) Add in platform/android/res/values/strings.xml file 3) Add in index.js file 4) Add But the result are these errors: for android platform for iOS platform The same request was working with the facebook module ver 3.x.x""""",title+description
TIMOB-19036,12,"""iOS: Remote ImageViews not loading while scrolling ListView ""","""""""As of this version (4.0.1) on iOS, when scrolling through a ListView that contains ImageViews that use remote images, the images are not loaded until the scrolling of the ListView comes to a complete stop.    Running the same project with 3.5.1 yields the expected result where the ImageViews get loaded as you scroll through the list.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Remote ImageViews not loading while scrolling ListView
Description: """"As of this version (4.0.1) on iOS, when scrolling through a ListView that contains ImageViews that use remote images, the images are not loaded until the scrolling of the ListView comes to a complete stop. Running the same project with 3.5.1 yields the expected result where the ImageViews get loaded as you scroll through the list.""""",title+description
TIMOB-19027,12,"""Windows: ti.windows.publishername property should be populated on project creation""","""""""h5.Description    When creating a Windows platform project the ti.windows.publishername property is not present in the tiapp.xml, this causes the build to fail as described in TIMOB-19025. This property should be auto-populated upon project creation    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Create a new project  2. Open the tiapp.xml    h5.Actual Result    The ti.windows.publishername property is not defined    h5.Expected Result    The ti.windows.publishername should be defined on project creation""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: ti.windows.publishername property should be populated on project creation
Description: """"h5.Description When creating a Windows platform project the ti.windows.publishername property is not present in the tiapp.xml, this causes the build to fail as described in TIMOB-19025. This property should be auto-populated upon project creation h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Create a new project 2. Open the tiapp.xml h5.Actual Result The ti.windows.publishername property is not defined h5.Expected Result The ti.windows.publishername should be defined on project creation""""",title+description
TIMOB-19014,12,"""Windows: Inconsistencies between implemented APIs and parity report""","""""""h5.Description    *I will use this ticket to track any APIs that we come across during testing that the parity report shows as implemented but can not be found in the source code*    There appears to be inconsistencies between the parity report and what apis are actually implemented. For example the parity report show Ti.UI.textArea as implemented. However when trying to use the code below it errors with undefined is not a function for Ti.UI.createTextArea        After a discussion with [~<USER> we figured out that the stub has been generated for textArea in TitaniumKit, causing the parity report to believe it is implemented but it is not actually implemented yet. This will also lead to issues after release as the documentation will show this as being implemented when it is not.    *Below is a list of apis we believe are reported incorrectly*    ||API||  | TextArea|    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Using the above code build to a windows phone device or emulator    h5.Actual Result    The app will throw an error saying undefined is not a function for Ti.UI.createTextArea    h5.Expected Result    The parity report should reflect what is implemented""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Inconsistencies between implemented APIs and parity report
Description: """"h5.Description *I will use this ticket to track any APIs that we come across during testing that the parity report shows as implemented but can not be found in the source code* There appears to be inconsistencies between the parity report and what apis are actually implemented. For example the parity report show Ti.UI.textArea as implemented. However when trying to use the code below it errors with undefined is not a function for Ti.UI.createTextArea After a discussion with [~<USER> we figured out that the stub has been generated for textArea in TitaniumKit, causing the parity report to believe it is implemented but it is not actually implemented yet. This will also lead to issues after release as the documentation will show this as being implemented when it is not. *Below is a list of apis we believe are reported incorrectly* ||API|| | TextArea| h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Using the above code build to a windows phone device or emulator h5.Actual Result The app will throw an error saying undefined is not a function for Ti.UI.createTextArea h5.Expected Result The parity report should reflect what is implemented""""",title+description
