TIMOB-18925,12,"""Ti.Media.Sound duration property inconsistent value types""","""""""http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media.Sound-property-duration    On iOS, this is seconds; on Android it's milliseconds.    Note that the time property is milliseconds (but also used to be seconds for iOS prior to 3.0: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media.Sound-property-time)""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Media.Sound duration property inconsistent value types
Description: """"http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media.Sound-property-duration On iOS, this is seconds; on Android it's milliseconds. Note that the time property is milliseconds (but also used to be seconds for iOS prior to 3.0: http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media.Sound-property-time)""""",title+description
TIMOB-18924,12,"""Ti.Media.AudioPlayer properties: progress and time appear to be same data, but used on different platforms""","""""""From https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/pull/244#discussion_r30416236    http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer-property-progress    There's a progress property and a time property on Ti.media.AudioPlayer. progress is used on iOS, time is used on Android. They are both durations reported in milliseconds. I'm not sure what he difference is between them.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Media.AudioPlayer properties: progress and time appear to be same data, but used on different platforms
Description: """"From https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_windows/pull/244#discussion_r30416236 http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer-property-progress There's a progress property and a time property on Ti.media.AudioPlayer. progress is used on iOS, time is used on Android. They are both durations reported in milliseconds. I'm not sure what he difference is between them.""""",title+description
