TIMOB-18914,12,"""Android: Mark splitActionBar as removed""","""""""Mark the following apis as removed    * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-property-splitActionBar  * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-method-setSplitActionBar  * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-method-getSplitActionBar    Better remove unused code for splitActionBar  * https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/ae0079017c200b285049c951dc468555e53c4421/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/TiC.java  * https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/8b832e29bb93ffc8909578f3b66f9a60d271e4e2/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/WindowProxy.java""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Mark splitActionBar as removed
Description: """"Mark the following apis as removed * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-property-splitActionBar * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-method-setSplitActionBar * http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Window-method-getSplitActionBar Better remove unused code for splitActionBar * https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/ae0079017c200b285049c951dc468555e53c4421/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/TiC.java * https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/8b832e29bb93ffc8909578f3b66f9a60d271e4e2/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/WindowProxy.java""""",title+description
TIMOB-18912,12,"""iOS: Implement new iOS 8 Navigation Bar Options""","""""""There are several new properties made available in iOS 8:    * hidesBarsOnTap  * hidesBarsOnSwipe  * hidesBarsWhenVerticallyCompact  * hidesBarsWhenKeyboardAppears  * navigationBarHidden  * barHideOnTapGestureRecognizer  * barHideOnSwipeGestureRecognizer    ... and more.    These are covered here:  https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UINavigationController_Class/    I came across these when trying to implement the same behaviour as Safari iOS 8 where you scroll down and the top navigation bar disappears to maximise the screen space.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Implement new iOS 8 Navigation Bar Options
Description: """"There are several new properties made available in iOS 8: * hidesBarsOnTap * hidesBarsOnSwipe * hidesBarsWhenVerticallyCompact * hidesBarsWhenKeyboardAppears * navigationBarHidden * barHideOnTapGestureRecognizer * barHideOnSwipeGestureRecognizer ... and more. These are covered here: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UINavigationController_Class/ I came across these when trying to implement the same behaviour as Safari iOS 8 where you scroll down and the top navigation bar disappears to maximise the screen space.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18909,12,"""Expose build and named version via Ti.App""","""""""Currently, we set Ti.App.version to the version-tag of the {{tiapp.xml}} file:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/35c0034605a800f5a6241d602a58d744222b2e1a/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L2816    For Android you can already set the {{versionName}} and {{versionCode}} directly and once TIMOB-17993 is resolved so can you for iOS's {{CFBundleShortVersionString}} and {{CFBundleVersion}}. If you set these, then {{Ti.App.version}} may not be the actual release version, affecting our own analytics - which uses this value - as well.    Suggestions:    * Let {{android:versionName}} and {{CFBundleShortVersionString}} override {{<version>}} {{Ti.App.version}}  * Let {{android:versionCode}} and {{CFBundleVersion}} override {{<build>}} for  {{Ti.App.build}} once TIMOB-19173 is resolved""""""",Improvement,"Title: Expose build and named version via Ti.App
Description: """"Currently, we set Ti.App.version to the version-tag of the {{tiapp.xml}} file: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/35c0034605a800f5a6241d602a58d744222b2e1a/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L2816 For Android you can already set the {{versionName}} and {{versionCode}} directly and once TIMOB-17993 is resolved so can you for iOS's {{CFBundleShortVersionString}} and {{CFBundleVersion}}. If you set these, then {{Ti.App.version}} may not be the actual release version, affecting our own analytics - which uses this value - as well. Suggestions: * Let {{android:versionName}} and {{CFBundleShortVersionString}} override {{<version>}} {{Ti.App.version}} * Let {{android:versionCode}} and {{CFBundleVersion}} override {{<build>}} for {{Ti.App.build}} once TIMOB-19173 is resolved""""",title+description
TIMOB-18908,12,"""Android: 5 9-patch splash screen images don't show up correctly""","""""""9-patch splash screen images aren't showing up correctly in Android 5, they show black squares on the left side of the screen.    !housters-splash-bug.png|thumbnail!    On Android 4 they show up correctly and if I change to non-9-patch they work on Android 5. I've attached a sample 9-patch for reproducing.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: 5 9-patch splash screen images don't show up correctly
Description: """"9-patch splash screen images aren't showing up correctly in Android 5, they show black squares on the left side of the screen. !housters-splash-bug.png|thumbnail! On Android 4 they show up correctly and if I change to non-9-patch they work on Android 5. I've attached a sample 9-patch for reproducing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18907,12,"""MobileWeb: NavigationGroup barColor set via Window does not work for child Windows""","""""""To set the bar-color for Windows in a {{Ti.UI.MobileWeb.NavigationGroup}} it seems that you have to use {{barColor}} on the Windows in the navigation group. This works for the initial window, but not for child windows you open in it later.    h1. To reproduce    Run the new Alloy version of the Sample.RSS on MobileWeb:  https://github.com/<USER>Sample.RSS/tree/alloy    As you see in the [app.tss|https://github.com/FokkeZB/Sample.RSS/blob/alloy/app/styles/app.tss#L14] I have set the barColor to red on all windows (thus including child windows). But as you see when you run it only the initial window has a red bar.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: NavigationGroup barColor set via Window does not work for child Windows
Description: """"To set the bar-color for Windows in a {{Ti.UI.MobileWeb.NavigationGroup}} it seems that you have to use {{barColor}} on the Windows in the navigation group. This works for the initial window, but not for child windows you open in it later. h1. To reproduce Run the new Alloy version of the Sample.RSS on MobileWeb: https://github.com/<USER>Sample.RSS/tree/alloy As you see in the [app.tss|https://github.com/FokkeZB/Sample.RSS/blob/alloy/app/styles/app.tss#L14] I have set the barColor to red on all windows (thus including child windows). But as you see when you run it only the initial window has a red bar.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18903,12,"""Android: Text entry for TextField within ListView not working correctly with Android 5.0""","""""""h2. Problem    Text entry for TextField within ListView not working correctly with Android 5.0.    h2. Test case    1) Launch KitchenSink app  2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > List View > Update Items  3) Focus the first text field and enter text on the *on-screen keyboard* of the device.  4) You will be able to to enter 1 or a few characters. After that, no more text entry is possible.  (Focusing the textfield again and deleting all characters will make the app responsive again)    h2. Logs    After executing step 4 above, the log will be filled repeatedly with these messges  {code:lang=none|title=console}  [WARN] :   View: requestLayout() improperly called by android.widget.ListView{e376f24 VFED.VC. ......ID 0,0-1440,2136} during layout: running second layout pass  [WARN] :   View: requestLayout() improperly called by ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIText$TiEditText{1e3c5442 VFED..CL .F....ID 720,18-1440,156 #81} during layout: running second layout pass  [WARN] :   IInputConnectionWrapper: getTextBeforeCursor on inactive InputConnection  [WARN] :   IInputConnectionWrapper: getTextBeforeCursor on inactive InputConnection    ((EditText)focusedView).setSelection(cursorPosition);  {code}    in TiListView.java in ListViewWrapper onLayout (Lini 161) seems to trigger a layout within a layout in Android 5.0.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Text entry for TextField within ListView not working correctly with Android 5.0
Description: """"h2. Problem Text entry for TextField within ListView not working correctly with Android 5.0. h2. Test case 1) Launch KitchenSink app 2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > List View > Update Items 3) Focus the first text field and enter text on the *on-screen keyboard* of the device. 4) You will be able to to enter 1 or a few characters. After that, no more text entry is possible. (Focusing the textfield again and deleting all characters will make the app responsive again) h2. Logs After executing step 4 above, the log will be filled repeatedly with these messges {code:lang=none|title=console} [WARN] : View: requestLayout() improperly called by android.widget.ListView{e376f24 VFED.VC. ......ID 0,0-1440,2136} during layout: running second layout pass [WARN] : View: requestLayout() improperly called by ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIText$TiEditText{1e3c5442 VFED..CL .F....ID 720,18-1440,156 #81} during layout: running second layout pass [WARN] : IInputConnectionWrapper: getTextBeforeCursor on inactive InputConnection [WARN] : IInputConnectionWrapper: getTextBeforeCursor on inactive InputConnection ((EditText)focusedView).setSelection(cursorPosition); {code} in TiListView.java in ListViewWrapper onLayout (Lini 161) seems to trigger a layout within a layout in Android 5.0.""""",title+description
