e(HttpURLConnectionImpl.java:373) 11-26 10:32:40.491: E/REQUEST(6264): at com.android.okhttp.internal.http.HttpURLConnectionImpl.connect(HttpURLConnectionImpl.java:106) 11-26 10:32:40.491: E/REQUEST(6264): at com.android.okhttp.internal.http.HttpURLConnectionImpl.getOutputStream(HttpURLConnectionImpl.java:208) 11-26 10:32:40.491: E/REQUEST(6264): at com.android.okhttp.internal.http.DelegatingHttpsURLConnection.getOutputStream(DelegatingHttpsURLConnection.java:218) 11-26 10:32:40.491: E/REQUEST(6264): at com.android.okhttp.internal.http.HttpsURLConnectionImpl.getOutputStream(HttpsURLConnectionImpl.java:25) 11-26 10:32:40.491: E/REQUEST(6264): at com.google.maps.api.android.lib6.b.l.run(Unknown Source) 11-26 10:32:40.491: E/REQUEST(6264): at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:818) 11-26 10:32:43.330: E/NuCachedSource2(188): source returned error -1, 5 retries left 11-26 10:32:45.049: E/WifiStateMachine(596): WifiStateMachine CMD_START_SCAN source -2 txSuccessRate=116,23 rxSuccessRate=206,11 targetRoamBSSID=any RSSI=-53 11-26 10:32:46.344: E/NuCachedSource2(188): source returned error -1, 4 retries left 11-26 10:32:49.357: E/NuCachedSource2(188): source returned error -1, 3 retries left 11-26 10:32:52.389: E/NuCachedSource2(188): source returned error -1, 2 retries left 11-26 10:32:55.412: E/NuCachedSource2(188): source returned error -1, 1 retries left 11-26 10:32:56.634: E/audio_a2dp_hw(188): adev_set_parameters: ERROR: set param called even when stream out is null 11-26 10:32:56.639: E/native(596): do suspend true 11-26 10:32:57.414: E/ANDR-PERF-LOCK(195): Failed to apply optimization for resource: 4 level: 0 11-26 10:32:58.427: E/NuCachedSource2(188): source returned error -1, 0 retries left 11-26 10:32:58.523: E/GenericSource(188): Failed to init from data source! 11-26 10:32:58.541: E/MediaPlayer(24537): error (1, -2147483648) 11-26 10:32:58.549: E/MediaPlayer(24537): Error (1,-2147483648) """"",title+description
TIMOB-18886,12,"""Android App Icon/Logo not showing on ActionBar on 4.0.0.RC2""","""""""The appicon is no longer showing on Android ActionBar on Ti SDK 4.0.0.RCX    When I compile with 3.5.1.GA or lower it shows normally, on 4.0.0.RC1 and RC2 it shows no logo, only the app title.    Also setLogo and setIcon are also not working to force a new logo on the ActionBar""""""",Bug,"Title: Android App Icon/Logo not showing on ActionBar on 4.0.0.RC2
Description: """"The appicon is no longer showing on Android ActionBar on Ti SDK 4.0.0.RCX When I compile with 3.5.1.GA or lower it shows normally, on 4.0.0.RC1 and RC2 it shows no logo, only the app title. Also setLogo and setIcon are also not working to force a new logo on the ActionBar""""",title+description
TIMOB-18885,12,"""Code Analyzer: Analysis fails with: 'Cannot read property 'value' of undefined'""","""""""h5.Description    When attempting to run Code Analyzer on an Alloy project in Studio the analysis fails with the following {{Cannot read property 'value' of undefined}}.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. In Studio create a new Alloy project  2. Right click on the project and choose Code Analysis->iPhone    h5.Actual Result    The code analysis will fail with the error {{Cannot read property 'value' of undefined}}      h5.Expected Result    The code analysis should not fail""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Analyzer: Analysis fails with: 'Cannot read property 'value' of undefined'
Description: """"h5.Description When attempting to run Code Analyzer on an Alloy project in Studio the analysis fails with the following {{Cannot read property 'value' of undefined}}. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. In Studio create a new Alloy project 2. Right click on the project and choose Code Analysis->iPhone h5.Actual Result The code analysis will fail with the error {{Cannot read property 'value' of undefined}} h5.Expected Result The code analysis should not fail""""",title+description
TIMOB-18884,12,"""Android: hintText does not display""","""""""Per https://community.<USER>com/topic/331/hinttext-color-for-textfield-is-always-white/2    On android, using the 4.0RC2 SDK, text boxes with hintText don't display the hintText.  The hintText is properly displayed on iOS and android using older 3.x SDKs.  This is a regression.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: hintText does not display
Description: """"Per https://community.<USER>com/topic/331/hinttext-color-for-textfield-is-always-white/2 On android, using the 4.0RC2 SDK, text boxes with hintText don't display the hintText. The hintText is properly displayed on iOS and android using older 3.x SDKs. This is a regression.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18872,12,"""Actionbar 'icon' property is broken with latest 4.0.0 SDK""","""""""h6.This is a regression. Works fine with 3.5.1.GA SDK.    h5.Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create an app for android for actionbar.    2. Build for android device/emulator with latest 4.0.0 SDK.    h5.Actual Result:  1. The actionbar icon is not shown.  2. When built with SDK 3.5.1.GA the actionbar icon is shown as expected.    h5. Expected Result:  1. The actionbar icon should be seen with latest 4.0.0 SDK.""""""",Bug,"Title: Actionbar 'icon' property is broken with latest 4.0.0 SDK
Description: """"h6.This is a regression. Works fine with 3.5.1.GA SDK. h5.Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an app for android for actionbar. 2. Build for android device/emulator with latest 4.0.0 SDK. h5.Actual Result: 1. The actionbar icon is not shown. 2. When built with SDK 3.5.1.GA the actionbar icon is shown as expected. h5. Expected Result: 1. The actionbar icon should be seen with latest 4.0.0 SDK.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18869,12,"""iOS: """"Invalid JSON in where parameter""""""","""""""When using 4.0.0.RC2 and making an ACS objects query, I get an error where there previously was not one:      *Steps to reproduce issue*  1. Create a project and include a query for an ACS Object  2. Run the project    *Actual Results*:  The above error is thrown    *Expected Results*:  No error is thrown    *Notes*:  This is the query I am using:      The community is also encountering this: https://community.<USER>com/topic/329/4-0-0-rc2-query-invalid-json-in-where-parameter/2    If I switch to use SDK 4.0.0.RC then I do not get the error.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: """"Invalid JSON in where parameter""""
Description: """"When using 4.0.0.RC2 and making an ACS objects query, I get an error where there previously was not one: *Steps to reproduce issue* 1. Create a project and include a query for an ACS Object 2. Run the project *Actual Results*: The above error is thrown *Expected Results*: No error is thrown *Notes*: This is the query I am using: The community is also encountering this: https://community.<USER>com/topic/329/4-0-0-rc2-query-invalid-json-in-where-parameter/2 If I switch to use SDK 4.0.0.RC then I do not get the error.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18868,12,"""Do not overwrite Info.plist keys set by user""","""""""This ticket describes the changes in the original PR ([#6408|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6408]) for TIMOB-17993. That issue requested a way to set CFBundleVersion and CFBundleShortVersionString separately without asking for a specific solution. The PR resolved this by no longer overwriting these two, *but also other keys* set in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} or a custom {{Info.plist}}.    So the request of this new ticket is for the build <USER>to not overwrite keys set in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} or a custom {{Info.plist}}.    h2. Current situation    1. Set some defaults ({{UIStatusBarStyle}}, {{CFBundleIdentifier}}..)  2. Merge keys in custom {{Info.plist}} in project root  3. Merge keys in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}}  4. Set {{CFBundleVersion}}, {{CFBundleShortVersionString}}  5. Set {{CFBundleIconFiles}}, {{UILaunchImages}}, {{UIAppFonts}}    h2. New situation    1. Set some defaults ({{UIStatusBarStyle}}, {{CFBundleIdentifier}}..)  2. Merge keys in custom {{Info.plist}} in project root  3. Merge keys in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}}  4. Set {{CFBundleVersion}}, {{CFBundleShortVersionString}} *only if not set by 2 or 3* (fixed by [#6818|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6818] for TIMOB-17993)  5. Set {{CFBundleIconFiles}}, {{UILaunchImages}}, {{UIAppFonts}} *only if not set by 2 or 3* (fixed by [#6408|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6408] for this issue)    h2. PR  The PR on master for this issue, but also including that of TIMOB-17993:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6408    h2. Note  For {{UILaunchImages}} [417f378430ba85908135c41a2806a5d49f271ae4|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/417f378430ba85908135c41a2806a5d49f271ae4#diff-f430483233aa01af5b10df8390f9635dR2083] already tried to not overwrite values set via {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} or {{Info.plist}} but because it was checking the merged {{plist}} variable, it also skipped when the build directory already was generated, requiring the project to be cleaned every time you add a launch image. My PR fixes this.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Do not overwrite Info.plist keys set by user
Description: """"This ticket describes the changes in the original PR ([#6408|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6408]) for TIMOB-17993. That issue requested a way to set CFBundleVersion and CFBundleShortVersionString separately without asking for a specific solution. The PR resolved this by no longer overwriting these two, *but also other keys* set in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} or a custom {{Info.plist}}. So the request of this new ticket is for the build <USER>to not overwrite keys set in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} or a custom {{Info.plist}}. h2. Current situation 1. Set some defaults ({{UIStatusBarStyle}}, {{CFBundleIdentifier}}..) 2. Merge keys in custom {{Info.plist}} in project root 3. Merge keys in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} 4. Set {{CFBundleVersion}}, {{CFBundleShortVersionString}} 5. Set {{CFBundleIconFiles}}, {{UILaunchImages}}, {{UIAppFonts}} h2. New situation 1. Set some defaults ({{UIStatusBarStyle}}, {{CFBundleIdentifier}}..) 2. Merge keys in custom {{Info.plist}} in project root 3. Merge keys in {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} 4. Set {{CFBundleVersion}}, {{CFBundleShortVersionString}} *only if not set by 2 or 3* (fixed by [#6818|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6818] for TIMOB-17993) 5. Set {{CFBundleIconFiles}}, {{UILaunchImages}}, {{UIAppFonts}} *only if not set by 2 or 3* (fixed by [#6408|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6408] for this issue) h2. PR The PR on master for this issue, but also including that of TIMOB-17993: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6408 h2. Note For {{UILaunchImages}} [417f378430ba85908135c41a2806a5d49f271ae4|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/417f378430ba85908135c41a2806a5d49f271ae4#diff-f430483233aa01af5b10df8390f9635dR2083] already tried to not overwrite values set via {{tiapp.xml/ios/plist}} or {{Info.plist}} but because it was checking the merged {{plist}} variable, it also skipped when the build directory already was generated, requiring the project to be cleaned every time you add a launch image. My PR fixes this.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18858,12,"""Android: Videoplayer events do not work well on Android lollipop""","""""""The 'complete' event does not seem to fire from the VideoPlayer closes, nor does the click handler for the """"""""Exit Video"""""""" button I added fire when I hit """"""""Exit Video"""""""", but the VideoPlayer does close. Using the """"""""back"""""""" button on the device itself to close the video player does not cause 'complete' to fire either.    I have some code similar to the following:    {code:js}  function openPlayer(e) {    var videoPlayer = Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer({      url: """"""""/demo.mp4"""""""",      mediaControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_FULLSCREEN,      scalingMode: Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT,      fullscreen: true,      autoplay: true    });       var closeButton = Ti.UI.createButton({      title: """"""""Exit Video"""""""",      top: """"""""0dp"""""""",      height: """"""""40dp"""""""",      left: """"""""10dp"""""""",      right: """"""""10dp""""""""    });       closeButton.addEventListener('click', function() {      videoPlayer.hide();      videoPlayer.release();      videoPlayer = null;    });       videoPlayer.add(closeButton);       videoPlayer.addEventListener('load', function(player) {      console.log(""""""""loaded"""""""");    });       videoPlayer.addEventListener('keypressed', function(e) {      console.log(""""""""keypressed"""""""");    });    videoPlayer.addEventListener('complete', function(player) {      console.log(""""""""DONE"""""""");    });    videoPlayer.addEventListener('playing', function(player) {      console.log(""""""""playing"""""""");    });    videoPlayer.addEventListener('error', function(player) {      console.log(""""""""error"""""""");    });  }     function onClick(e) {    openPlayer(null);  }  $.btn_open.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", onClick);  $.index.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Videoplayer events do not work well on Android lollipop
Description: """"The 'complete' event does not seem to fire from the VideoPlayer closes, nor does the click handler for the """"""""Exit Video"""""""" button I added fire when I hit """"""""Exit Video"""""""", but the VideoPlayer does close. Using the """"""""back"""""""" button on the device itself to close the video player does not cause 'complete' to fire either. I have some code similar to the following: {code:js} function openPlayer(e) { var videoPlayer = Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer({ url: """"""""/demo.mp4"""""""", mediaControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_FULLSCREEN, scalingMode: Ti.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT, fullscreen: true, autoplay: true }); var closeButton = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: """"""""Exit Video"""""""", top: """"""""0dp"""""""", height: """"""""40dp"""""""", left: """"""""10dp"""""""", right: """"""""10dp"""""""" }); closeButton.addEventListener('click', function() { videoPlayer.hide(); videoPlayer.release(); videoPlayer = null; }); videoPlayer.add(closeButton); videoPlayer.addEventListener('load', function(player) { console.log(""""""""loaded""""""""); }); videoPlayer.addEventListener('keypressed', function(e) { console.log(""""""""keypressed""""""""); }); videoPlayer.addEventListener('complete', function(player) { console.log(""""""""DONE""""""""); }); videoPlayer.addEventListener('playing', function(player) { console.log(""""""""playing""""""""); }); videoPlayer.addEventListener('error', function(player) { console.log(""""""""error""""""""); }); } function onClick(e) { openPlayer(null); } $.btn_open.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", onClick); $.index.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-18857,12,"""Developers should be able to set the Environment for builds through the studio / CLI / Dashboard""","""""""As a developer / product owner / business analyst - I may be building or managing mobile applications a specific way for my organization. This management <USER>may mean that when packaging my mobile app for Ad Hoc/Enterprise or even App Store / Google Store / Windows Store this build would be considered a """"""""Test Build"""""""" vs actually production.    As such I need the ability to tag builds and build versions in a manner that would let me better filter them in the dashboard.     Expectation:  When building / packaging the application there should be a way to tag that build as either development or production (or even a custom environment tag such as """"""""Staging"""""""" or """"""""QA"""""""") that could then be picked up by the dashboard and allow Dashboard Users to better filter their views at the aggregate and application level.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Developers should be able to set the Environment for builds through the studio / CLI / Dashboard
Description: """"As a developer / product owner / business analyst - I may be building or managing mobile applications a specific way for my organization. This management <USER>may mean that when packaging my mobile app for Ad Hoc/Enterprise or even App Store / Google Store / Windows Store this build would be considered a """"""""Test Build"""""""" vs actually production. As such I need the ability to tag builds and build versions in a manner that would let me better filter them in the dashboard. Expectation: When building / packaging the application there should be a way to tag that build as either development or production (or even a custom environment tag such as """"""""Staging"""""""" or """"""""QA"""""""") that could then be picked up by the dashboard and allow Dashboard Users to better filter their views at the aggregate and application level.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18852,12,"""Ti.App.iOS.UserDefaults needs ability to set the suiteName in order for it to work with Apple Watch""","""""""I was looking at the new UserDefaults API we have for sharing data between iOS extensions and it's missing the ability to specify a suiteName.  Without this, this API cannot share data across extensions.    Example in a watch extension:      Currently you can only do something like:      Which points to the standard user defaults...which the apple watch can't access.  Maybe a 3rd param needs to be introduced in these methods where you can specify the suiteName.    Ref. http://stackoverflow.com/questions/27007288/watchkit-sdk-not-retrieving-data-from-nsuserdefaults""""""",Improvement,"Title: Ti.App.iOS.UserDefaults needs ability to set the suiteName in order for it to work with Apple Watch
Description: """"I was looking at the new UserDefaults API we have for sharing data between iOS extensions and it's missing the ability to specify a suiteName. Without this, this API cannot share data across extensions. Example in a watch extension: Currently you can only do something like: Which points to the standard user defaults...which the apple watch can't access. Maybe a 3rd param needs to be introduced in these methods where you can specify the suiteName. Ref. http://stackoverflow.com/questions/27007288/watchkit-sdk-not-retrieving-data-from-nsuserdefaults""""",title+description
TIMOB-18850,12,"""Titanium CLI plugin doesn't properly handle getting correct platform modules""","""""""The appc-cli-titanium module has some issues on my machine when downloading Test and Perf.  There is a logic problem when you have more than one version of the module locally.  Always finds the oldest release, not the newest downloaded version.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Titanium CLI plugin doesn't properly handle getting correct platform modules
Description: """"The appc-cli-titanium module has some issues on my machine when downloading Test and Perf. There is a logic problem when you have more than one version of the module locally. Always finds the oldest release, not the newest downloaded version. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18848,12,"""Create a cross-platform API for ActionBar/Toolbar/CommandBar/AppBar""","""""""We have no concept of a cross-platform APi for a fairly common UI pattern of an App/Tool/ActionBar.    We have Ti.UI.iOS.Toolbar, Ti.Android.ActionBar - and we're looking at exposing Windows' CommandBar and/or AppBar.    They are fairly similar and typically involve a bar across the top or bottom of the app with some buttons/navigation.    iOS Toolbar: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UserExperience/Conceptual/MobileHIG/Bars.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40006556-CH12-SW4  Android ActionBar: http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/actionbar.html  Windows CommandBar: https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/windows.ui.xaml.controls.commandbar.Aspx  Windows AppBar: https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/windows.ui.xaml.controls.appbar.Aspx""""""",New Feature,"Title: Create a cross-platform API for ActionBar/Toolbar/CommandBar/AppBar
Description: """"We have no concept of a cross-platform APi for a fairly common UI pattern of an App/Tool/ActionBar. We have Ti.UI.iOS.Toolbar, Ti.Android.ActionBar - and we're looking at exposing Windows' CommandBar and/or AppBar. They are fairly similar and typically involve a bar across the top or bottom of the app with some buttons/navigation. iOS Toolbar: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UserExperience/Conceptual/MobileHIG/Bars.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40006556-CH12-SW4 Android ActionBar: http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/actionbar.html Windows CommandBar: https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/windows.ui.xaml.controls.commandbar.Aspx Windows AppBar: https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/windows.ui.xaml.controls.appbar.Aspx""""",title+description
TIMOB-18846,12,"""Parity: HTTPClient sends array of objects differently on iOS then it does on Android""","""""""A [Q&A user|https://community.<USER>com/topic/178/http-request-problem-with-array-data/3] discovered that when following the [docs|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient-method-send] to send arrays, but if those arrays include objects, the result on iOS is different then it is on Android. The expected result is seen on Android, while the result on iOS is unusable because of added {{+}} characters, newlines and {{;}}.    h1. To reproduce    Run the following code on both iOS and Android with an updated requestb.in URL.        h1. Android    The {{console.log}} will show:        The body shown on requestb.in will be:        which decoded is the expected:        h1. iOS    The {{console.log}} will show similar:        But the body shown on requestb.in will be:        which decoded is:        h1. Solution    The Android output is better, although {{\{b=y\}}} is no valid JSON or form data either. It might better be {{\{""""""""b"""""""":""""""""y""""""""\}}}?""""""",Bug,"Title: Parity: HTTPClient sends array of objects differently on iOS then it does on Android
Description: """"A [Q&A user|https://community.<USER>com/topic/178/http-request-problem-with-array-data/3] discovered that when following the [docs|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient-method-send] to send arrays, but if those arrays include objects, the result on iOS is different then it is on Android. The expected result is seen on Android, while the result on iOS is unusable because of added {{+}} characters, newlines and {{;}}. h1. To reproduce Run the following code on both iOS and Android with an updated requestb.in URL. h1. Android The {{console.log}} will show: The body shown on requestb.in will be: which decoded is the expected: h1. iOS The {{console.log}} will show similar: But the body shown on requestb.in will be: which decoded is: h1. Solution The Android output is better, although {{\{b=y\}}} is no valid JSON or form data either. It might better be {{\{""""""""b"""""""":""""""""y""""""""\}}}?""""",title+description
TIMOB-18844,12,"""iOS: Swift is not supported for Extensions""","""""""I have built a WatchKit extension in Swift. All works beautifully in the simulator when running directly from xcode.    I have linked to the extension from my Titanium project, and everything builds without error, yet when running the """"""""xcrun simctl launch booted"""""""" command to launch the watch, I get an infinite loading animation.    Upon digging through the logs I got many errors such as “Unable to start plugin” and """"""""activePlugInForIdentifier: returned nil for application"""""""". I also stumbled upon a crash log which seems to point the finger more accurately:    Process:               JAS Watch WatchKit Extension [27101]    Dyld Error Message:      Library not loaded: @rpath/libswiftCore.dylib      Referenced from: /Users/USER/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Devices/4CEFE848-E6EB-41D2-8968-754C449E19A8/data/Containers/Bundle/Application/5B42A276-DD25-4288-82A4-C1C2CFBE527E/Just a Score.app/PlugIns/JAS Watch WatchKit Extension.appex/JAS Watch WatchKit Extension      Reason: image not found    It seems that “libswiftCore.dylib” is not getting included, a quick Google search will lead you to discover that there is a flag in a projects build settings called “Embedded Content Contains Swift Code”. This flag needs to be checked in order to run an objective-c project with embedded Swift content.    I’m sure this would be the case with any Swift extension and Titanium for reproduction. Hopefully this flag solves the issue.   Urgency in finding a solution to this would be greatly appreciated.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Swift is not supported for Extensions
Description: """"I have built a WatchKit extension in Swift. All works beautifully in the simulator when running directly from xcode. I have linked to the extension from my Titanium project, and everything builds without error, yet when running the """"""""xcrun simctl launch booted"""""""" command to launch the watch, I get an infinite loading animation. Upon digging through the logs I got many errors such as “Unable to start plugin” and """"""""activePlugInForIdentifier: returned nil for application"""""""". I also stumbled upon a crash log which seems to point the finger more accurately: Process: JAS Watch WatchKit Extension [27101] Dyld Error Message: Library not loaded: @rpath/libswiftCore.dylib Referenced from: /Users/USER/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Devices/4CEFE848-E6EB-41D2-8968-754C449E19A8/data/Containers/Bundle/Application/5B42A276-DD25-4288-82A4-C1C2CFBE527E/Just a Score.app/PlugIns/JAS Watch WatchKit Extension.appex/JAS Watch WatchKit Extension Reason: image not found It seems that “libswiftCore.dylib” is not getting included, a quick Google search will lead you to discover that there is a flag in a projects build settings called “Embedded Content Contains Swift Code”. This flag needs to be checked in order to run an objective-c project with embedded Swift content. I’m sure this would be the case with any Swift extension and Titanium for reproduction. Hopefully this flag solves the issue. Urgency in finding a solution to this would be greatly appreciated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18841,12,"""LiveView: """"Titanium Project Path does not exist at...""""""","""""""There is another old ticket (TISTUD-6948) about this issue but is closed, so I repost here:    Liveview enabled Alloy apps doesn't reload the changes on device for Windows 8.1.   It seems studio is looking in wrong app location to reload the project.    I have this issue with the following configuration:  <USER>Studio 4.0.0.201504131149  titanium.liveview.core (1.1.0.1426229149)  CLI version 3.4.1  Windows 8.1  Target platform: Android  Both Appecelerator Studio and Titanium Studio are installed on the machine.    STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Create the default Alloy App  2. Run the app on Android Device with LiveView enabled;  3. Make a change in the TSS file and Save.        but when saving files I get the following error:  """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: """"Titanium Project Path does not exist at...""""
Description: """"There is another old ticket (TISTUD-6948) about this issue but is closed, so I repost here: Liveview enabled Alloy apps doesn't reload the changes on device for Windows 8.1. It seems studio is looking in wrong app location to reload the project. I have this issue with the following configuration: <USER>Studio 4.0.0.201504131149 titanium.liveview.core (1.1.0.1426229149) CLI version 3.4.1 Windows 8.1 Target platform: Android Both Appecelerator Studio and Titanium Studio are installed on the machine. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Create the default Alloy App 2. Run the app on Android Device with LiveView enabled; 3. Make a change in the TSS file and Save. but when saving files I get the following error: """"",title+description
TIMOB-18837,12,"""Android: Hiding ActionBar Broken with SDK 4.0.0.Beta2""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce  Create an Android Application and use method 2 of this guide http://www.<USER>com/blog/2014/08/hiding-the-android-actionbar/.    If you compile with SDK 3.5.1.GA all works fine, if you compile with SDK 4.0.0.Beta2 ActionBar is still present    I'm attaching two screenshots of the same app compiled with both version. In the screenshots you can see Android Action Bar in BLACK  and the RED one is a widget.    This is the Custome Theme used:      This is the Android Manifest (used by TiApp.xml)    h3. Actual Result  ActionBar is still present    h3. Expected Result  Hide ActionBar""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Hiding ActionBar Broken with SDK 4.0.0.Beta2
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce Create an Android Application and use method 2 of this guide http://www.<USER>com/blog/2014/08/hiding-the-android-actionbar/. If you compile with SDK 3.5.1.GA all works fine, if you compile with SDK 4.0.0.Beta2 ActionBar is still present I'm attaching two screenshots of the same app compiled with both version. In the screenshots you can see Android Action Bar in BLACK and the RED one is a widget. This is the Custome Theme used: This is the Android Manifest (used by TiApp.xml) h3. Actual Result ActionBar is still present h3. Expected Result Hide ActionBar""""",title+description
