TIMOB-18792,12,"""Liveview: Recompiling an Alloy app fails when Alloy is not installed globally""","""""""h5.Description    When building an alloy project with Liveview enabled, when making changes to an app the re-compile of the app fails with the below        This is because at [line 451 in fserver.js|https://github.com/<USER>liveview/blob/master/lib/fserver.js#L451] to recompile the app the alloy command line is used, this should be changed to appc alloy so that we are using the alloy installed in the CLI.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Make sure you have no global install of Alloy  2. From Studio build an Alloy app with Liveview enabled  3. When the app has opened make changes and save the file    h5.Actual Result    The recompile will fail with the above error    h5.Expected Result    The recompile should work with no issues""""""",Bug,"Title: Liveview: Recompiling an Alloy app fails when Alloy is not installed globally
Description: """"h5.Description When building an alloy project with Liveview enabled, when making changes to an app the re-compile of the app fails with the below This is because at [line 451 in fserver.js|https://github.com/<USER>liveview/blob/master/lib/fserver.js#L451] to recompile the app the alloy command line is used, this should be changed to appc alloy so that we are using the alloy installed in the CLI. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Make sure you have no global install of Alloy 2. From Studio build an Alloy app with Liveview enabled 3. When the app has opened make changes and save the file h5.Actual Result The recompile will fail with the above error h5.Expected Result The recompile should work with no issues""""",title+description
