TIMOB-18725,12,"""iOS: Unable to build a project using 4.0.0 that was created using 3.5.1.GA""","""""""h5.Description    When building a project using SDK from branch 4_0_X, I regularly see errors such as below, I am unsure as to the actual root cause of these errors but I believe I have narrowed it down to the SDK as during my investigation it appeared the CLI had no effect.              h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Create a project using SDK 3.5.1.GA  2. Build the project using ti build -p ios  3. Change the SDK in the tiapp.xml and run ti sdk select and choose the latest 4_0_X SDK  4. Run ti build -p ios again    h5.Actual result    2. The build will pass  4. The build will fail with errors such as the one listed above    h5.Expected result    The build should pass both times""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Unable to build a project using 4.0.0 that was created using 3.5.1.GA
Description: """"h5.Description When building a project using SDK from branch 4_0_X, I regularly see errors such as below, I am unsure as to the actual root cause of these errors but I believe I have narrowed it down to the SDK as during my investigation it appeared the CLI had no effect. h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Create a project using SDK 3.5.1.GA 2. Build the project using ti build -p ios 3. Change the SDK in the tiapp.xml and run ti sdk select and choose the latest 4_0_X SDK 4. Run ti build -p ios again h5.Actual result 2. The build will pass 4. The build will fail with errors such as the one listed above h5.Expected result The build should pass both times""""",title+description
TIMOB-18717,12,"""KitchenSink: iOS - Facebook module add photo publish example""","""""""KitchenSink example for iOS does not include the photo publish function. This should be implemented as it is available for the Android.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: iOS - Facebook module add photo publish example
Description: """"KitchenSink example for iOS does not include the photo publish function. This should be implemented as it is available for the Android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18709,12,"""iOS: Incorrect fallback in Authentication Challenge""","""""""It seems like the implementation of the authentication challenge on https://github.com/<USER>APSHTTPClient/blob/master/APSHTTPClient/APSHTTPRequest.m is not done properly.    Specifically in this part:      Whenever an error occurs by the validation (for example when the server gives back a wrong certificate), Titanium fallbacks to the standard certificate checks bypassing the desired and given certificate pinning.    This bug has successfully reproduced by installing our own CA-certificate in a test device and thus bypassing the check with the certificate of the server and being able to perform a man in the middle attack.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Incorrect fallback in Authentication Challenge
Description: """"It seems like the implementation of the authentication challenge on https://github.com/<USER>APSHTTPClient/blob/master/APSHTTPClient/APSHTTPRequest.m is not done properly. Specifically in this part: Whenever an error occurs by the validation (for example when the server gives back a wrong certificate), Titanium fallbacks to the standard certificate checks bypassing the desired and given certificate pinning. This bug has successfully reproduced by installing our own CA-certificate in a test device and thus bypassing the check with the certificate of the server and being able to perform a man in the middle attack.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18706,12,"""Windows: Build- Cannot build Titanium project on a Windows machine""","""""""*Details:* Cannot build Titanium project on a Windows machine; longjohn error is returned.    *Note:* This is a *regression* from SDK build 3.5.1.GA i.e. I can build a Titanium project with SDK 3.5.1.GA.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a Titanium project from CLI  2. Run: {{ti build}}    *Actual:* Longjohn error is returned:      *Expected:* Should be able to build and run the Titanium project on a Windows machine.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Build- Cannot build Titanium project on a Windows machine
Description: """"*Details:* Cannot build Titanium project on a Windows machine; longjohn error is returned. *Note:* This is a *regression* from SDK build 3.5.1.GA i.e. I can build a Titanium project with SDK 3.5.1.GA. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a Titanium project from CLI 2. Run: {{ti build}} *Actual:* Longjohn error is returned: *Expected:* Should be able to build and run the Titanium project on a Windows machine.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18705,12,"""Tooling: Move module dependencies into package.json""","""""""Rather than having a separate location to store this data, we move the modules from:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_releases/blob/master/titanium.json    into a """"""""titaniumDependencies"""""""" area of:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/package.json""""""",Story,"Title: Tooling: Move module dependencies into package.json
Description: """"Rather than having a separate location to store this data, we move the modules from: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_releases/blob/master/titanium.json into a """"""""titaniumDependencies"""""""" area of: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/package.json""""",title+description
TIMOB-18701,12,"""KitchenSink: Android: When building, the build fails when packaging the application""","""""""h5.Description    When attempting to build KitchenSink from github or Studio the build fails with errors such as         This is because in the tiapp.xml the target Android SDK is set to 14, due to TIMOB-17357 the target Android SDK should be set to 21 which will fix this problem.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. In Studio import KitchenSink from the samples  2. Build to device  3. In the tiapp.xml change <uses-sdk android:targetSdkVersion=""""""""14""""""""/> to <uses-sdk android:targetSdkVersion=""""""""21""""""""/>  4. Build to device again    h5.Actual Result    2. The build will fail  4. The build will pass    h5.Expected Result    The build should pass""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Android: When building, the build fails when packaging the application
Description: """"h5.Description When attempting to build KitchenSink from github or Studio the build fails with errors such as This is because in the tiapp.xml the target Android SDK is set to 14, due to TIMOB-17357 the target Android SDK should be set to 21 which will fix this problem. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. In Studio import KitchenSink from the samples 2. Build to device 3. In the tiapp.xml change <uses-sdk android:targetSdkVersion=""""""""14""""""""/> to <uses-sdk android:targetSdkVersion=""""""""21""""""""/> 4. Build to device again h5.Actual Result 2. The build will fail 4. The build will pass h5.Expected Result The build should pass""""",title+description
TIMOB-18680,12,"""iOS - Incorrect Caching of ListItems containing Textfields""","""""""One of our Titanium apps uses ListViews extensively, including for building forms, where each ListItem contains a form control (TextField, Picker, etc...) If the form has more ListItems than the size of the screen, as you scroll down it causes issues where the values from certain TextFields are copied into other ListItems' TextFields.    This is clearly connected to the ListView's row caching, it's expected that it would cache the list rows so that you only have as many as are on the screen in memory, however it's clearly not setting the values correctly for each row as scrolling occurs.    I've boiled it down to a simple reproduction case below, simply input values into the first few rows (e.g. """"""""test 1"""""""", """"""""test 2"""""""", """"""""test 3"""""""") then scroll down and you'll see those 3 values populated into other rows.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Incorrect Caching of ListItems containing Textfields
Description: """"One of our Titanium apps uses ListViews extensively, including for building forms, where each ListItem contains a form control (TextField, Picker, etc...) If the form has more ListItems than the size of the screen, as you scroll down it causes issues where the values from certain TextFields are copied into other ListItems' TextFields. This is clearly connected to the ListView's row caching, it's expected that it would cache the list rows so that you only have as many as are on the screen in memory, however it's clearly not setting the values correctly for each row as scrolling occurs. I've boiled it down to a simple reproduction case below, simply input values into the first few rows (e.g. """"""""test 1"""""""", """"""""test 2"""""""", """"""""test 3"""""""") then scroll down and you'll see those 3 values populated into other rows. """"",title+description
