TIMOB-18631,12,"""Android: AlertDialog.show() causes crash""","""""""AlertDIalog show() causes crash on Android but OK on iOS    I have a demo app that i am creating and want to show() and AlertDialog on a button click to confirm the user's action.    I am following the code example in the online docs and it works fine on iOS. On Android it will work once or twice and then on the 3rd or fourth time, it causes a fatal crash (logs attached).    Ricardo has the project and can help anyone in Mountain View.    TEST ACCOUNT LOGIN:  username: a  password: 1234    When I use the same code in a simpler Hello World app it works fine on iOS and Android.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: AlertDialog.show() causes crash
Description: """"AlertDIalog show() causes crash on Android but OK on iOS I have a demo app that i am creating and want to show() and AlertDialog on a button click to confirm the user's action. I am following the code example in the online docs and it works fine on iOS. On Android it will work once or twice and then on the 3rd or fourth time, it causes a fatal crash (logs attached). Ricardo has the project and can help anyone in Mountain View. TEST ACCOUNT LOGIN: username: a password: 1234 When I use the same code in a simpler Hello World app it works fine on iOS and Android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18628,12,"""Update the node version in vendorDependencies in the package.json""","""""""h5.Description    In the package.json for each platform within the SDK the node version needs to be updated from         to          This needs to be done for every platform supported.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Open finder and navigate to your SDK folder (~/Library/Application\ Support/Titanium/)    2. Open an SDK and check the package.json in each platform folder.    h5.Actual Result    The node versions under vendorDependencies will be *"""""""": """""""">0.8.0 <=0.10.x"""""""",*    h5.Expected Result    The node versions under vendorDependencies should be *""""""""node"""""""": """""""">=0.10.0 <=0.12.x"""""""",*""""""",Bug,"Title: Update the node version in vendorDependencies in the package.json
Description: """"h5.Description In the package.json for each platform within the SDK the node version needs to be updated from to This needs to be done for every platform supported. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Open finder and navigate to your SDK folder (~/Library/Application\ Support/Titanium/) 2. Open an SDK and check the package.json in each platform folder. h5.Actual Result The node versions under vendorDependencies will be *"""""""": """""""">0.8.0 <=0.10.x"""""""",* h5.Expected Result The node versions under vendorDependencies should be *""""""""node"""""""": """""""">=0.10.0 <=0.12.x"""""""",*""""",title+description
TIMOB-18624,12,"""iOS Map Kit pinchangedragstate Event not firing after enabling Test services""","""""""h6.Issue Description  Using pins on a map (Ti.Map) an event wired up to the PinChangeDragState event. When we enable either the test service or the performance services built in to <USER>Studio, the event no longer fires. If the client disables those services, the event fires again as expected.     h6.Expected Behaviour  pinchangedragstate - event fires when the pin's drag state changes     h6.Actual Behaviour  pinchangedragstate - event no longer fires    h6.Module Combos   From our tests these are the different outcomes when Services were enabled:  - With APM/SOASTA event not fired  - With SOASTA events not fired  - With APM event is fired    h6.Sample Code  As example, get following map code to interact with it and notice outputs information to the console when each event fires:  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/iOS_Map_Kit-section-37540542_iOSMapKit-EventHandling        h6.App running with no services      h6.This is soasta/apm    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS Map Kit pinchangedragstate Event not firing after enabling Test services
Description: """"h6.Issue Description Using pins on a map (Ti.Map) an event wired up to the PinChangeDragState event. When we enable either the test service or the performance services built in to <USER>Studio, the event no longer fires. If the client disables those services, the event fires again as expected. h6.Expected Behaviour pinchangedragstate - event fires when the pin's drag state changes h6.Actual Behaviour pinchangedragstate - event no longer fires h6.Module Combos From our tests these are the different outcomes when Services were enabled: - With APM/SOASTA event not fired - With SOASTA events not fired - With APM event is fired h6.Sample Code As example, get following map code to interact with it and notice outputs information to the console when each event fires: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/iOS_Map_Kit-section-37540542_iOSMapKit-EventHandling h6.App running with no services h6.This is soasta/apm """"",title+description
TIMOB-18623,12,"""Tooling: Add Grunt/JSCS/JSHint to Titanium Mobile repository""","""""""To enforce our coding style and prevent errors, we should add JSHint and JSCS rules to titanium_mobile.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Tooling: Add Grunt/JSCS/JSHint to Titanium Mobile repository
Description: """"To enforce our coding style and prevent errors, we should add JSHint and JSCS rules to titanium_mobile.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18621,12,"""Consolidate Java coding standards""","""""""We have several different coding standards in use that may or may not differ from our official standards, and are somewhat different from our other languages:    https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/Java+Coding+Standards    Some highlights of cross-language similarity I'd like to achieve:    * Tabs  * Opening brace on new line, except blocks and flow control  * Closing brace on new line (except blocks and flow control, i.e. } else {)  * Max line length of 120 (to fit within a normal GitHub review window)    A proposed formatting file for Eclipse can be found here:    https://github.com/<USER>appc-standards/blob/master/languages/java/eclipse-format.xml    And below are two examples of what this would change in our code:    * Studio: https://github.com/aptana/studio3/pull/297  * Titanium: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6668    """"""",Improvement,"Title: Consolidate Java coding standards
Description: """"We have several different coding standards in use that may or may not differ from our official standards, and are somewhat different from our other languages: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/Java+Coding+Standards Some highlights of cross-language similarity I'd like to achieve: * Tabs * Opening brace on new line, except blocks and flow control * Closing brace on new line (except blocks and flow control, i.e. } else {) * Max line length of 120 (to fit within a normal GitHub review window) A proposed formatting file for Eclipse can be found here: https://github.com/<USER>appc-standards/blob/master/languages/java/eclipse-format.xml And below are two examples of what this would change in our code: * Studio: https://github.com/aptana/studio3/pull/297 * Titanium: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6668 """"",title+description
TIMOB-18616,12,"""iOS Debugger: Breakpoints not recognized on files that are required()""","""""""*Steps to reproduce issue*:  1. Create a new application   2. Replace the content of app.js with the following:    3. Create a lib.js file in the """"""""Resources"""""""" folder of the project with the following code:    4. Add a breakpoint to line 2 of lib.js   5. Debug the application.   6. Scroll the text box.    *Expected Result*:  The breakpoint is hit on scroll.    *Actual Result*:  Breakpoint is not hit    *Notes*:  This is not a regression as the same is seen with 3.5.0.GA.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Debugger: Breakpoints not recognized on files that are required()
