TIMOB-18615,12,"""iOS Debugger: Breakpoints not recognized on files that are added to app.js using URL""","""""""Files added in a project with 'url' are not allowing break points to be hit. This is not a regression as I also see it with 3.5.0.GA.    *Steps To Reproduce*:  1. create app with code below.  2. Put a breakpoint on any line in newWin.js file.  3. Run the app.  4. Click Test button.    *Actual*: Breakpoint is not recognized in newWin File.    *Expected*: Breakpoint must get hit.    app.js      newWin.js      *Notes*:  See related ticket. Looks like this was fixed for Android in the past and iOS was verified. Possibly broke since then.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Debugger: Breakpoints not recognized on files that are added to app.js using URL
Description: """"Files added in a project with 'url' are not allowing break points to be hit. This is not a regression as I also see it with 3.5.0.GA. *Steps To Reproduce*: 1. create app with code below. 2. Put a breakpoint on any line in newWin.js file. 3. Run the app. 4. Click Test button. *Actual*: Breakpoint is not recognized in newWin File. *Expected*: Breakpoint must get hit. app.js newWin.js *Notes*: See related ticket. Looks like this was fixed for Android in the past and iOS was verified. Possibly broke since then.""""",title+description
