TIMOB-18610,12,"""Debugger: Breakpoint not hit in loop of click event""","""""""Using the attached file in a project, I do not see a breakpoint being hit when inside the loop of the click event (line 31).    *Steps to reproduce issue*:  1. Use the attached app.js to create a new project  2. Add a breakpoint to line 31 (Ti.API.debug(""""""""Hello: """""""" + i);)  3. Debug the project and click on the label: """"""""I am Window 1""""""""  4. Notice that the breakpoint is not hit    *Expected result*:  The breakpoint is hit on each iteration of the for-loop    """"""",Bug,"Title: Debugger: Breakpoint not hit in loop of click event
Description: """"Using the attached file in a project, I do not see a breakpoint being hit when inside the loop of the click event (line 31). *Steps to reproduce issue*: 1. Use the attached app.js to create a new project 2. Add a breakpoint to line 31 (Ti.API.debug(""""""""Hello: """""""" + i);) 3. Debug the project and click on the label: """"""""I am Window 1"""""""" 4. Notice that the breakpoint is not hit *Expected result*: The breakpoint is hit on each iteration of the for-loop """"",title+description
TIMOB-18604,12,"""LiveView: Running liveview-server status shows that LiveView servers are running when they are not""","""""""h5.Description    When navigating to the LiveView folder within the Studio plugins and running the command ./liveview-server status all the LiveView servers that have been started since LiveView was installed are listed.     However if you run *ps aux | grep node* it will show only one or none LiveView processes running.    If you try to kill the servers using ./liveview-server stop then it will attempt to kill the servers and will print out the following for each server.        h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. From Studio build a few projects with LiveView enabled, making sure to terminate them once the app has launched and LiveView has connected  2. Navigate to the LiveView folder at /Applications/<USER>Studio/plugins/com.<USER>titanium.liveview.core_1.1.0.1424300841/node_modules/liveview/bin     3. Run ./liveview-server status  4. Run .ps aux | grep node  5. Run ./liveview-server stop    h5.Actual Result    3. Multiple liveview servers will be listed  4. Only one liveview server will be shown as running, as expected  5. LiveView will attempt to kill the servers but it will fail    h5.Expected Result    LiveView should not list inactive servers as active""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Running liveview-server status shows that LiveView servers are running when they are not
Description: """"h5.Description When navigating to the LiveView folder within the Studio plugins and running the command ./liveview-server status all the LiveView servers that have been started since LiveView was installed are listed. However if you run *ps aux | grep node* it will show only one or none LiveView processes running. If you try to kill the servers using ./liveview-server stop then it will attempt to kill the servers and will print out the following for each server. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. From Studio build a few projects with LiveView enabled, making sure to terminate them once the app has launched and LiveView has connected 2. Navigate to the LiveView folder at /Applications/<USER>Studio/plugins/com.<USER>titanium.liveview.core_1.1.0.1424300841/node_modules/liveview/bin 3. Run ./liveview-server status 4. Run .ps aux | grep node 5. Run ./liveview-server stop h5.Actual Result 3. Multiple liveview servers will be listed 4. Only one liveview server will be shown as running, as expected 5. LiveView will attempt to kill the servers but it will fail h5.Expected Result LiveView should not list inactive servers as active""""",title+description
TIMOB-18603,12,"""Windows: Implement EmailDialog.addAttachment""","""""""I skipped doing the actual email attachment implementation since it wasn't necessary for corporate directory and was more involved than the rest of the impl. We need to cast the JSObject to Blob or File in TitaniumKit and call to overloaded addAttachment methods for either, and then do the actual hooking up to the email message in open().""""""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Implement EmailDialog.addAttachment
Description: """"I skipped doing the actual email attachment implementation since it wasn't necessary for corporate directory and was more involved than the rest of the impl. We need to cast the JSObject to Blob or File in TitaniumKit and call to overloaded addAttachment methods for either, and then do the actual hooking up to the email message in open().""""",title+description
TIMOB-18602,12,"""iOS8: Support for Lock Screen Widgets""","""""""h4. Problem description  Please add support for the new iOS 8 calls, """"""""Today Screen Widgets"""""""". These are widgets that you can actually interact with on the """"""""Today"""""""" screen (not the Notifications screen). """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS8: Support for Lock Screen Widgets
Description: """"h4. Problem description Please add support for the new iOS 8 calls, """"""""Today Screen Widgets"""""""". These are widgets that you can actually interact with on the """"""""Today"""""""" screen (not the Notifications screen). """"",title+description
TIMOB-18598,12,"""LiveView: App does not launch when building from the CLI with LiveView enabled""","""""""h5.Description    *This does not occur in Studio*    When attempting to build using LiveView from the CLI, opening the app fails on both iOS and Android. On iOS the build fails with a runtime error as shown below        and on Android it fails with a runtime error shown below        If LiveView is run through Studio then there are no errors. *This only occurs in the CLI*    This is because the *LiveView server is not started* when building from the CLI.    This *is a regression* as in previous versions of LiveView I was able to launch from the CLI with no errors.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Build an existing project in the CLI using the ti build command with --liveview   2. Open the app on device    h5.Actual Result    2. Depending on the platform the app will throw one of the errors shown above    h5.Expected Result    2. The app should not throw an error, or LiveView should not be allowed to be used in the CLI""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: App does not launch when building from the CLI with LiveView enabled
Description: """"h5.Description *This does not occur in Studio* When attempting to build using LiveView from the CLI, opening the app fails on both iOS and Android. On iOS the build fails with a runtime error as shown below and on Android it fails with a runtime error shown below If LiveView is run through Studio then there are no errors. *This only occurs in the CLI* This is because the *LiveView server is not started* when building from the CLI. This *is a regression* as in previous versions of LiveView I was able to launch from the CLI with no errors. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Build an existing project in the CLI using the ti build command with --liveview 2. Open the app on device h5.Actual Result 2. Depending on the platform the app will throw one of the errors shown above h5.Expected Result 2. The app should not throw an error, or LiveView should not be allowed to be used in the CLI""""",title+description
TIMOB-18597,12,"""LiveView: Support selective compilation for Alloy""","""""""With ALOY-1216 resolved, Alloy 1.7 will support selective compilation. LiveView should use this feature to drastically reduce the time between detecting a change and having the app updated.""""""",New Feature,"Title: LiveView: Support selective compilation for Alloy
Description: """"With ALOY-1216 resolved, Alloy 1.7 will support selective compilation. LiveView should use this feature to drastically reduce the time between detecting a change and having the app updated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18596,12,"""Code Analyzer: Analyzing for iPhone always has grade of N/A""","""""""When analyzing a project for iPhone, the results always return a grade of N/A.    *Steps to reproduce issue*:  1. Create a default Alloy project.  2. Run Code Analysis for iPhone on the project.  3. Notice that the results have N/A for grades under the Project Score tab.    *Expected Results*:  A grade is provided for iPhone, like the other platforms    *Notes*:  This is not a regression as it also occurs in 3.5.0.GA""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Analyzer: Analyzing for iPhone always has grade of N/A
Description: """"When analyzing a project for iPhone, the results always return a grade of N/A. *Steps to reproduce issue*: 1. Create a default Alloy project. 2. Run Code Analysis for iPhone on the project. 3. Notice that the results have N/A for grades under the Project Score tab. *Expected Results*: A grade is provided for iPhone, like the other platforms *Notes*: This is not a regression as it also occurs in 3.5.0.GA""""",title+description
TIMOB-18595,12,"""Code Analyzer: Process Unvisited Code throws error: Object.run undefined is not a function""","""""""When attempting to analyze project with 'Process Unvisited Code' checked, in preferences. The analysis fails with the below error:      *Steps to reproduce issue*:  1. Create Alloy Project with all common deployment targets.     2. Project Context Menu > Code Analysis > Preferences > Code Analyzer settings.   3. Under the Settings select the check box for all three available option for analyzing :   - Invoke Methods   - Evaluate Loops   - Process Unvisited Code   4. Choose Platform: iPhone from Project Context Menu > Code Analysis > Run Selected Platforms.    *Expected Results*:  Code processor should run normally and the analyzed result should be generated.    *Notes*:  This is not a regression as it also occurs with 3.5.0.GA""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Analyzer: Process Unvisited Code throws error: Object.run undefined is not a function
Description: """"When attempting to analyze project with 'Process Unvisited Code' checked, in preferences. The analysis fails with the below error: *Steps to reproduce issue*: 1. Create Alloy Project with all common deployment targets. 2. Project Context Menu > Code Analysis > Preferences > Code Analyzer settings. 3. Under the Settings select the check box for all three available option for analyzing : - Invoke Methods - Evaluate Loops - Process Unvisited Code 4. Choose Platform: iPhone from Project Context Menu > Code Analysis > Run Selected Platforms. *Expected Results*: Code processor should run normally and the analyzed result should be generated. *Notes*: This is not a regression as it also occurs with 3.5.0.GA""""",title+description
