Description: """"The items under https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/tree/master/demos now reside in: * https://github.com/<USER>KitchenSink * https://github.com/<USER>KitchenSinkNook * https://github.com/<USER>KitchenSinkiPad * SmokeTest (deleted) * ApiCheck (deleted)""""",title+description
TIMOB-18491,12,"""Android: PullView For Listviews (parity)""","""""""Right now, pullView is working for only iOS. It would be nice if this was cross-platform right out of Titanium.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: PullView For Listviews (parity)
Description: """"Right now, pullView is working for only iOS. It would be nice if this was cross-platform right out of Titanium.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18490,12,"""Collision with Ti.Map when including Google Play Services within module""","""""""We need to include Google Play Services in our module. We do so by including the google-play-services.jar in the lib folder, all the appropriate resources, and specifying the Play Service version metadata tag in the manifest. However, if an app needs to use our module and the Ti.Map module,  it will fail to compile do to the Jar mismatch. (Our module is including the latest lib, but Ti.Map is currently including revision 21).    To get around this issue, we will not include Play Services in our module but instead direct users to include the Ti.Map module even though they may not be using maps, as this will add the appropriate Play Services library to their app.    Is it possible to include Google Play Services at the app level and not the module level? """"""",New Feature,"Title: Collision with Ti.Map when including Google Play Services within module
Description: """"We need to include Google Play Services in our module. We do so by including the google-play-services.jar in the lib folder, all the appropriate resources, and specifying the Play Service version metadata tag in the manifest. However, if an app needs to use our module and the Ti.Map module, it will fail to compile do to the Jar mismatch. (Our module is including the latest lib, but Ti.Map is currently including revision 21). To get around this issue, we will not include Play Services in our module but instead direct users to include the Ti.Map module even though they may not be using maps, as this will add the appropriate Play Services library to their app. Is it possible to include Google Play Services at the app level and not the module level? """"",title+description
TIMOB-18489,12,"""OptionDialogs have no way to specify the context window""","""""""Related to TC-5260. In that issue you can see how an OptionDialog, not attached to a view (and therefore not in _popover-mode_) will open as a modal view inside a window.    In TC-5260 that window was (incorrectly) the Popover’s main window.    However, once TC-5260 is resolved we will not be able to do that on purpose, that is creating a modal OptionDialog inside a specific window.    I propose the addition of a {{targetWindow}} property to the {{showParams}} for the {{dialog.show({})}} method, so we can explicitly tell where we want the dialog to attach.""""""",New Feature,"Title: OptionDialogs have no way to specify the context window
Description: """"Related to TC-5260. In that issue you can see how an OptionDialog, not attached to a view (and therefore not in _popover-mode_) will open as a modal view inside a window. In TC-5260 that window was (incorrectly) the Popover’s main window. However, once TC-5260 is resolved we will not be able to do that on purpose, that is creating a modal OptionDialog inside a specific window. I propose the addition of a {{targetWindow}} property to the {{showParams}} for the {{dialog.show({})}} method, so we can explicitly tell where we want the dialog to attach.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18488,12,"""Android build fails, probably due to length of encrypted JS string""","""""""TUI have reported that they cannot build for Android devices because the encryption <USER>fails to generate any code (support case #00003559). Their project is very large which suggests the encryption <USER>fails because the output is too long. The generated AssetCryptImpl.java file suggests the encrypted string should be 7586232 chars in length, but the actual string is not present. In testing they can resolve the issue by removing some JS source code from the project.    Please find attached the error log and generated AssetCryptImpl.java file.    This is related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-16077, although the build does not show the same error.    It would be very helpful to understand:    - is there a hard limit on the length of the encrypted source string which is embedded in the generated AssetCryptImpl.java file? If so what is this?    - is there also a hard limit on the length of the encrypted source string when building for iOS? And other platforms?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android build fails, probably due to length of encrypted JS string
Description: """"TUI have reported that they cannot build for Android devices because the encryption <USER>fails to generate any code (support case #00003559). Their project is very large which suggests the encryption <USER>fails because the output is too long. The generated AssetCryptImpl.java file suggests the encrypted string should be 7586232 chars in length, but the actual string is not present. In testing they can resolve the issue by removing some JS source code from the project. Please find attached the error log and generated AssetCryptImpl.java file. This is related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-16077, although the build does not show the same error. It would be very helpful to understand: - is there a hard limit on the length of the encrypted source string which is embedded in the generated AssetCryptImpl.java file? If so what is this? - is there also a hard limit on the length of the encrypted source string when building for iOS? And other platforms?""""",title+description
