TIMOB-18323,12,"""Windows: UI-related module should be notified when app window is ready""","""""""Some UI-related modules like `Ti.Gesture`,  `Ti.Accelerometer` and `Ti.Platform.DisplayCaps` needs reference to """"""""current display information"""""""" (`Windows::Graphics::Display::DisplayInformation`) to initialize internal state, but currently initializing it at module constructor is causing crash.    Let say we have `Gesture` module and want to get current view after module is initialized, to initialize event listener. We could do it at constructor like below...        Unfortunately, this ends up crash with following error. Note that WinRT complains about thread usage, but it is not quite right. Seems like problem here is that CoreWindow is not initialized at the moment.        So, what we actually need is """"""""callback"""""""" which is called when window is ready. UI-related module should get notified after window is ready, so that it can setup UI-related stuff safely. It could be something like this:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: UI-related module should be notified when app window is ready
Description: """"Some UI-related modules like `Ti.Gesture`, `Ti.Accelerometer` and `Ti.Platform.DisplayCaps` needs reference to """"""""current display information"""""""" (`Windows::Graphics::Display::DisplayInformation`) to initialize internal state, but currently initializing it at module constructor is causing crash. Let say we have `Gesture` module and want to get current view after module is initialized, to initialize event listener. We could do it at constructor like below... Unfortunately, this ends up crash with following error. Note that WinRT complains about thread usage, but it is not quite right. Seems like problem here is that CoreWindow is not initialized at the moment. So, what we actually need is """"""""callback"""""""" which is called when window is ready. UI-related module should get notified after window is ready, so that it can setup UI-related stuff safely. It could be something like this: """"",title+description
TIMOB-18321,12,"""Windows: Updating UI property from timer causes crash""","""""""Updating UI property (like Ti.UI.Button.title) from timer function causes crash inside HAL. Likely related to #30 and #47. Note that `Ti.API.info` works in this case.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Updating UI property from timer causes crash
Description: """"Updating UI property (like Ti.UI.Button.title) from timer function causes crash inside HAL. Likely related to #30 and #47. Note that `Ti.API.info` works in this case. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18316,12,"""Windows: Cannot launch app into emulator with """"Failed to install app"""" error""","""""""Win8 Preview, cannot launch app into emulator or device    I am following the instructions from the Blog Post (http://www.<USER>com/blog/2014/12/windows-platform-preview/)    When i launch to the emulator, using:     ti build -p windows -T wp-emulator -C 8-1-1 --wp-publisher-guid 00000000-0000-1000-8000-000000000000    it builds and installs the app on the emulator but exists immediately    Error message is:    [ERROR] Failed to install app (code -2146233088)    Terminal log with """"""""ti info"""""""" and screen shot attached""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows: Cannot launch app into emulator with """"Failed to install app"""" error
