TIMOB-18296,12,"""iOS: Click on accessory not recognised in list view when clicked on disclosure or checkmark accessory type""","""""""This is not a regression as the issue also occurs in 3.4.1 and 3.4.0.GA    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create a project with code below and install the app on device  2. Launch the app. A list view with three rows is shown. Each having a different accessory type (Detail, Disclosure, Checkmark)  3. Click on the accessory in each row and check logs    Actual Result:  For row 2 and row 3 having accessory of types disclosure and checkmark, the logs show """"""""accessoryClicked:false"""""""" even though it was clicked. For accessory type detail it shows true.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Click on accessory not recognised in list view when clicked on disclosure or checkmark accessory type
Description: """"This is not a regression as the issue also occurs in 3.4.1 and 3.4.0.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a project with code below and install the app on device 2. Launch the app. A list view with three rows is shown. Each having a different accessory type (Detail, Disclosure, Checkmark) 3. Click on the accessory in each row and check logs Actual Result: For row 2 and row 3 having accessory of types disclosure and checkmark, the logs show """"""""accessoryClicked:false"""""""" even though it was clicked. For accessory type detail it shows true. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18294,12,"""iOS: initialPlaybackTime property for video player does not work consistently for local video""","""""""This is not a regression as the issue happens with older SDK as well (tested as far back as 3.3.0.GA)    The initialPlaybackTime property of video player does not work consistently. The issue seems intermittent but for me the scenario created through the code below reproduced the issue almost every time.  The issue seems to occur only for local video but does work for remote video. The issue does not occur on Android.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create a project with code below and install it on iOS device  2. In the app click on any row in the tableview  3. The video should play in the new window. Check the video time.  Note: When the app did not had a tableview and the video was on the starting window then the issue was intermittent.    Actual Result:  The video plays from the very start despite of initialPlaybackTime defined as 20 seconds.    Expected Result:  The video should start to play from 20 seconds.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: initialPlaybackTime property for video player does not work consistently for local video
Description: """"This is not a regression as the issue happens with older SDK as well (tested as far back as 3.3.0.GA) The initialPlaybackTime property of video player does not work consistently. The issue seems intermittent but for me the scenario created through the code below reproduced the issue almost every time. The issue seems to occur only for local video but does work for remote video. The issue does not occur on Android. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a project with code below and install it on iOS device 2. In the app click on any row in the tableview 3. The video should play in the new window. Check the video time. Note: When the app did not had a tableview and the video was on the starting window then the issue was intermittent. Actual Result: The video plays from the very start despite of initialPlaybackTime defined as 20 seconds. Expected Result: The video should start to play from 20 seconds. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18292,12,"""iOS8: HTTPClient onload callback doesn't get called in iOS 8.1""","""""""HTTPClient onload callback doen't get called in iOS 8.1 devices.  It's working as expected in iOS 7.1 devices    h5. Steps To Reproduce  1. Create a classic app using following code in app.js    2. Run on iOS 8.1 device    h5. Expected Result  Appc logo should be saved in gallery and there should be an alert dialog with the message of *Check your photo gallery for a titanium logo*.    h5.  Actual Result  Alert with *error*.  Following log message was observed in console but this log was not consistent.      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: HTTPClient onload callback doesn't get called in iOS 8.1
Description: """"HTTPClient onload callback doen't get called in iOS 8.1 devices. It's working as expected in iOS 7.1 devices h5. Steps To Reproduce 1. Create a classic app using following code in app.js 2. Run on iOS 8.1 device h5. Expected Result Appc logo should be saved in gallery and there should be an alert dialog with the message of *Check your photo gallery for a titanium logo*. h5. Actual Result Alert with *error*. Following log message was observed in console but this log was not consistent. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18291,12,"""Android: Feature Request to Expose Typeface.createFromFile to dynamically include the fonts""","""""""h6.Feature Request  Create a font form from file which is really required to load the dynamic font downloaded from our server or at least if the mCustomTypeFaces variable is declared as public.    h6.Android API  Create a new typeface from the specified font file.  http://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/Typeface.html#createFromFile(java.lang.String)    h6.Use Case  Our requirement is to download the fonts (TTF) files form server and put them inside app directory, then use it. So if we like to change the fonts tomorrow after app release, we don't have to make a new release. """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Feature Request to Expose Typeface.createFromFile to dynamically include the fonts
Description: """"h6.Feature Request Create a font form from file which is really required to load the dynamic font downloaded from our server or at least if the mCustomTypeFaces variable is declared as public. h6.Android API Create a new typeface from the specified font file. http://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/Typeface.html#createFromFile(java.lang.String) h6.Use Case Our requirement is to download the fonts (TTF) files form server and put them inside app directory, then use it. So if we like to change the fonts tomorrow after app release, we don't have to make a new release. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18290,12,"""iOS: Ti.Media audioSessionMode components generate invalid warning messages""","""""""AudioSessionMode related components are generating invalid warnings.  For example:      Here, We don't have a version called 3.4.2.    h5. Steps To Reproduce  1. Install and launch KitchenSink app  2. Go to Phone -> Record  3. Check the studio console log    h5. Actual Result  Deprecated version should not be 3.4.2 which is a  invalid version number      h5. Expected Result  Deprecated version could be 3.5.0""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Media audioSessionMode components generate invalid warning messages
Description: """"AudioSessionMode related components are generating invalid warnings. For example: Here, We don't have a version called 3.4.2. h5. Steps To Reproduce 1. Install and launch KitchenSink app 2. Go to Phone -> Record 3. Check the studio console log h5. Actual Result Deprecated version should not be 3.4.2 which is a invalid version number h5. Expected Result Deprecated version could be 3.5.0""""",title+description
TIMOB-18289,12,"""KitchenSink: App Fails to login Facebook""","""""""KitchenSink app fails to login Facebook. Please see the attachments for more details about error messages.    h5. Steps To Reproduce  1. Install and Launch KitchenSink App  2. Go to Mashups -> Facebook -> Login/Logout  3. Click on the Facebook Login button    h5. Expected Result  Facebook should be logged in.    h5. Actual Result  It shows some Graph API versioning errors. Please see the attachment *Screen Shot 2014-12-26 at 12.29.08 PM.png*  If we click OK button on above screen, we'll get some error alert. Please see the attachment *Screen Shot 2014-12-26 at 12.29.18 PM.png*""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: App Fails to login Facebook
Description: """"KitchenSink app fails to login Facebook. Please see the attachments for more details about error messages. h5. Steps To Reproduce 1. Install and Launch KitchenSink App 2. Go to Mashups -> Facebook -> Login/Logout 3. Click on the Facebook Login button h5. Expected Result Facebook should be logged in. h5. Actual Result It shows some Graph API versioning errors. Please see the attachment *Screen Shot 2014-12-26 at 12.29.08 PM.png* If we click OK button on above screen, we'll get some error alert. Please see the attachment *Screen Shot 2014-12-26 at 12.29.18 PM.png*""""",title+description
TIMOB-18288,12,"""iOS: Empty tableview with footer causes app to crash""","""""""h4. Problem Description   When a tableview has a textfield added to the footer and the tableview is not populated clicking on the textfield causes the app to crash with the error in attached log.    h4. Test Case  {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  var title_view = Ti.UI.createView({   height : 100  });  title_view.add(Ti.UI.createTextField({   width : """"""""90%"""""""",   height : 40,   borderStyle : Ti.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL  }));    var items_view = Ti.UI.createTableView({   top : 30,   data : [],   footerView : title_view  });  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor : """"""""#fff""""""""  });  win.add(items_view);  win.open();  {code}    h4. Expected result  Text field should be focused    h4. Actual result  App crashes after text field is focused  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Empty tableview with footer causes app to crash
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When a tableview has a textfield added to the footer and the tableview is not populated clicking on the textfield causes the app to crash with the error in attached log. h4. Test Case {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var title_view = Ti.UI.createView({ height : 100 }); title_view.add(Ti.UI.createTextField({ width : """"""""90%"""""""", height : 40, borderStyle : Ti.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL })); var items_view = Ti.UI.createTableView({ top : 30, data : [], footerView : title_view }); var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : """"""""#fff"""""""" }); win.add(items_view); win.open(); {code} h4. Expected result Text field should be focused h4. Actual result App crashes after text field is focused """"",title+description
