TIMOB-18277,12,"""Https module: include support for two-way authentication""","""""""h3. Request    Customer is looking to do a two-way ssl authentication using the <USER>https module, but currently there is no mention  on the documentation about a feature like this.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Https module: include support for two-way authentication
Description: """"h3. Request Customer is looking to do a two-way ssl authentication using the <USER>https module, but currently there is no mention on the documentation about a feature like this. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18276,12,"""UI.Notification.setMessage function is not found even though it is documented""","""""""h4. Problem Description  I am unable to dynamically set a Notification (toast) """"""""message"""""""" attribute using the setting method """"""""setMessage"""""""" from my controller.  When called I get:    """"""""Object #<Notification> has no method 'setMessage'""""""""    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project (Classic Titanium)  2. Add this code into app.js:    3. Run it into device.     h4. Expected results  The toast showing.     h4. Actual Results    When called I get:    """"""""Object #<Notification> has no method 'setMessage'""""""""        h4. Extra info (Workaround)  Putting """"""""toast.setMessage = """"""""Please Stand By"""""""";"""""""" or """"""""toast.message = """"""""Please Stand By"""""""";"""""""" dynamically, shows notification with blank message. The workaround is to set the message when it is created.    """"""",Bug,"Title: UI.Notification.setMessage function is not found even though it is documented
Description: """"h4. Problem Description I am unable to dynamically set a Notification (toast) """"""""message"""""""" attribute using the setting method """"""""setMessage"""""""" from my controller. When called I get: """"""""Object #<Notification> has no method 'setMessage'"""""""" h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project (Classic Titanium) 2. Add this code into app.js: 3. Run it into device. h4. Expected results The toast showing. h4. Actual Results When called I get: """"""""Object #<Notification> has no method 'setMessage'"""""""" h4. Extra info (Workaround) Putting """"""""toast.setMessage = """"""""Please Stand By"""""""";"""""""" or """"""""toast.message = """"""""Please Stand By"""""""";"""""""" dynamically, shows notification with blank message. The workaround is to set the message when it is created. """"",title+description
