TIMOB-18263,12,"""iOS: Debugger suspends the thread though all breakpoints are suspended""","""""""- Debug a iOS app onto device/simulator.  - After the app is suspended at the breakpoints, resume (F8) the execution.  - Now skip all breakpoints : Run > Skip All Breakpoints.  - Try to run through the same scenario - the thread should not be suspended at the breakpoints now.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Debugger suspends the thread though all breakpoints are suspended
Description: """"- Debug a iOS app onto device/simulator. - After the app is suspended at the breakpoints, resume (F8) the execution. - Now skip all breakpoints : Run > Skip All Breakpoints. - Try to run through the same scenario - the thread should not be suspended at the breakpoints now. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18261,12,"""iOS: Correct missing newlines at ends of header files""","""""""It appears that some of our header files are missing newlines and triggering Apple warnings. While this should no longer be an issue when using C++ 11, it appears to still cause warnings with default Apple settings:    http://stackoverflow.com/questions/72271/no-newline-at-end-of-file-compiler-warning    To find:    {code:title=find_newlines.sh}  #!/usr/bin/env bash  for i in $(find . -type f -name """"""""*.h"""""""") ; do \   if diff /dev/null """"""""$i"""""""" | tail -1 | \    grep '^\\ No newline' > /dev/null; then  echo $i; \  fi; done  """"""",Story,"Title: iOS: Correct missing newlines at ends of header files
Description: """"It appears that some of our header files are missing newlines and triggering Apple warnings. While this should no longer be an issue when using C++ 11, it appears to still cause warnings with default Apple settings: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/72271/no-newline-at-end-of-file-compiler-warning To find: {code:title=find_newlines.sh} #!/usr/bin/env bash for i in $(find . -type f -name """"""""*.h"""""""") ; do \ if diff /dev/null """"""""$i"""""""" | tail -1 | \ grep '^\\ No newline' > /dev/null; then echo $i; \ fi; done """"",title+description
TIMOB-18259,12,"""ListView: Get the items currently filtered by searchText or searchView""","""""""h1. Current situation  Given I have a ListView with X items and I do a search using either {{searchText}} or {{searchView}} currently there is no way to now which items are filtered (shown).    h1. Desired situation  I'd like to have a {{getFilteredItems()}} method or (less preferable) a flag on the items themselves so I can tell which are currently filtered (shown).    h1. Use case  I have a list the user can filter and then either select one (or more) or use a *Select All* button to select all items currently filtered.""""""",New Feature,"Title: ListView: Get the items currently filtered by searchText or searchView
Description: """"h1. Current situation Given I have a ListView with X items and I do a search using either {{searchText}} or {{searchView}} currently there is no way to now which items are filtered (shown). h1. Desired situation I'd like to have a {{getFilteredItems()}} method or (less preferable) a flag on the items themselves so I can tell which are currently filtered (shown). h1. Use case I have a list the user can filter and then either select one (or more) or use a *Select All* button to select all items currently filtered.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18258,12,"""iOS: Breakpoints in files that are included in app.js causes the app to crash""","""""""This is a regression as the app can be successfully debugged using titanium sdk 3.4.1 GA.    When a file is included in app.js and breakpoints are placed in the included file, the app crashes and hence unable to debug successfully.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Close any running emulators or simulators.   2. Import and open the attached project into studio  3. From Titanium Studio go to Debug perspective (Window > Open perspective > Debug)   4. In the Breakpoints view, Remove All existing breakpoints   5. Go to file -> import -> select breakpoints under Run/Debug and click next   6. Browse to breakpoint-basic.bkpt in Test File Location   7. Debug the test project.      Actual Results:  App is installed on to device, and when the app is launched when the studio prompts it tries to connect to debugger however it crashes immediately when it has connected.    Expected Results:  App should be installed, and when the app connects to debugger, the app should be suspended at the breakpoint in import.js line 6.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Breakpoints in files that are included in app.js causes the app to crash
Description: """"This is a regression as the app can be successfully debugged using titanium sdk 3.4.1 GA. When a file is included in app.js and breakpoints are placed in the included file, the app crashes and hence unable to debug successfully. Steps to reproduce: 1. Close any running emulators or simulators. 2. Import and open the attached project into studio 3. From Titanium Studio go to Debug perspective (Window > Open perspective > Debug) 4. In the Breakpoints view, Remove All existing breakpoints 5. Go to file -> import -> select breakpoints under Run/Debug and click next 6. Browse to breakpoint-basic.bkpt in Test File Location 7. Debug the test project. Actual Results: App is installed on to device, and when the app is launched when the studio prompts it tries to connect to debugger however it crashes immediately when it has connected. Expected Results: App should be installed, and when the app connects to debugger, the app should be suspended at the breakpoint in import.js line 6.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18255,12,"""iOS: Step Back (F7) does not return the execution to parent method""","""""""- Put a breakpoint at lines 3, 9 in the below code       - Debug the app onto iOS device/simulator.  - Click on the label to suspend the app at the expected breakpoints.  - When the thread is suspended at line 9, try to step back to the parent method using F7 (Step Back) in debug perspective.    The debugger suspends indicating that stepping in, instead of going back to parent method. The behavior is working good in _master_ branch, but not for 3_5_X branch.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Step Back (F7) does not return the execution to parent method
Description: """"- Put a breakpoint at lines 3, 9 in the below code - Debug the app onto iOS device/simulator. - Click on the label to suspend the app at the expected breakpoints. - When the thread is suspended at line 9, try to step back to the parent method using F7 (Step Back) in debug perspective. The debugger suspends indicating that stepping in, instead of going back to parent method. The behavior is working good in _master_ branch, but not for 3_5_X branch.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18254,12,"""Using wrong value type should give informative error instead of crash (on Android)""","""""""The following code crashes on Android with an IllegalArgumentException because the value needs to be a Boolean. But on iOS it works fine. I would expect a informative error in both cases and no crash on Android.        Crash log:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Using wrong value type should give informative error instead of crash (on Android)
Description: """"The following code crashes on Android with an IllegalArgumentException because the value needs to be a Boolean. But on iOS it works fine. I would expect a informative error in both cases and no crash on Android. Crash log: """"",title+description
TIMOB-18253,12,"""iOS: Debugger crashed when the variable value is changed to random object""","""""""- Put a breakpoint  at line 3 in the below code.    - Debug the app onto iOS device or simulator.  - Click on the label, so that the thread suspends its execution at line 3.  - Now, change the value of 'txt' to """"""""changed"""""""". Press F8 (Resume). The dialog shows the message """"""""changed"""""""". It works !    Click on the label again to suspend the thread at the same line. Now, change the value of 'txt' to _changed_. Press F8 (Resume). The debugger/app will crash.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Debugger crashed when the variable value is changed to random object
Description: """"- Put a breakpoint at line 3 in the below code. - Debug the app onto iOS device or simulator. - Click on the label, so that the thread suspends its execution at line 3. - Now, change the value of 'txt' to """"""""changed"""""""". Press F8 (Resume). The dialog shows the message """"""""changed"""""""". It works ! Click on the label again to suspend the thread at the same line. Now, change the value of 'txt' to _changed_. Press F8 (Resume). The debugger/app will crash.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18252,12,"""KitchenSink: Base UI->Tab Groups Animate Tab Group uses the incorrect orientation when in landscape""","""""""h5.Description    When animating the tab group in Base UI->Animate Tab Group if the button is pressed when the device is landscape the tab group is portrait during the animation and then turns to landscape afterwards.  *This only occurs on a iPhone, I am unable to make it happen on an iPad*    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Install KitchenSink to device  2. Hold the device in landscape and navigate to Base UI->Tab Groups  3. Tap Animate Tab Group    h5.Actual Result    The tab group goes portrait for the animation then changes to landscape    h5.Expected Result    The tab group should be landscape during the animation""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Base UI->Tab Groups Animate Tab Group uses the incorrect orientation when in landscape
Description: """"h5.Description When animating the tab group in Base UI->Animate Tab Group if the button is pressed when the device is landscape the tab group is portrait during the animation and then turns to landscape afterwards. *This only occurs on a iPhone, I am unable to make it happen on an iPad* h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Install KitchenSink to device 2. Hold the device in landscape and navigate to Base UI->Tab Groups 3. Tap Animate Tab Group h5.Actual Result The tab group goes portrait for the animation then changes to landscape h5.Expected Result The tab group should be landscape during the animation""""",title+description
TIMOB-18251,12,"""KitchenSink: Base UI->Views->Hi-Res Image remote does not display on iPhone 6+""","""""""h5.Description    In Base UI->Views->Hi-Res Image remote the image does not display and instead there is a label saying *Test only valid on retina devices*, this is because the image is only shown if Ti.Platform.displayCaps.density is equal to *high* and the 6 Plus returns *xhigh*.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Install KitchenSink onto a iPhone 6 plus  2. Navigate to Base UI->Views->Hi-Res Image remote    h5.Actual Result    The image will not display due to 'it not being a retina display'    h5.Expected Result    The image should display""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Base UI->Views->Hi-Res Image remote does not display on iPhone 6+
Description: """"h5.Description In Base UI->Views->Hi-Res Image remote the image does not display and instead there is a label saying *Test only valid on retina devices*, this is because the image is only shown if Ti.Platform.displayCaps.density is equal to *high* and the 6 Plus returns *xhigh*. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Install KitchenSink onto a iPhone 6 plus 2. Navigate to Base UI->Views->Hi-Res Image remote h5.Actual Result The image will not display due to 'it not being a retina display' h5.Expected Result The image should display""""",title+description
TIMOB-18250,12,"""iOS: When adding a tab the active tab icon does not stay highlighted""","""""""h5.Description    This is *is not a regression*    When a tab is added to a tabgroup, the icon for the current tab is no longer highlighted as the active tab in the bar at the bottom of the screen.     h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Add the attached app.js to an existing project and build to a device  2. Tap 'Click me'    h5.Actual Result    The current tab will no longer be shown as the active tab in the bottom of the screen    h5.Expected Result    The current tab should be shown as the active tab in the bottom of the screen""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: When adding a tab the active tab icon does not stay highlighted
Description: """"h5.Description This is *is not a regression* When a tab is added to a tabgroup, the icon for the current tab is no longer highlighted as the active tab in the bar at the bottom of the screen. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Add the attached app.js to an existing project and build to a device 2. Tap 'Click me' h5.Actual Result The current tab will no longer be shown as the active tab in the bottom of the screen h5.Expected Result The current tab should be shown as the active tab in the bottom of the screen""""",title+description
