TIMOB-18154,12,"""Android 5.0: Edges of buttons using 9-patch images appear white when depressed ""","""""""h6.Issue Description  The corners of Ti.UI.Button objects appear white when depressed. This occurs when using the 3.4.x and 3.5.0.Alpha Ti SDKs and happens when setting the backgroundImage and backgroundSelectedImage properties using 9-patch images. The issue does not occur on previous Android OS versions.    h6.Testing Device Details:   Connected Android Devices   Nexus 5   ID = 08256ce40c79c27b   State = device   SDK Version = 5.0 (android-21)   ABIs = armeabi-v7a, armeabi, armeabi-v7a,armeabi, armeabi-v7a,armeabi,     h6.Expected   No white corners appear when button is clicked (Xperia Play Android OS 4.0)    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Import Titanium Mobile project (attached)   2. Run it in device   3. Click in the button to see the issue.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android 5.0: Edges of buttons using 9-patch images appear white when depressed
Description: """"h6.Issue Description The corners of Ti.UI.Button objects appear white when depressed. This occurs when using the 3.4.x and 3.5.0.Alpha Ti SDKs and happens when setting the backgroundImage and backgroundSelectedImage properties using 9-patch images. The issue does not occur on previous Android OS versions. h6.Testing Device Details: Connected Android Devices Nexus 5 ID = 08256ce40c79c27b State = device SDK Version = 5.0 (android-21) ABIs = armeabi-v7a, armeabi, armeabi-v7a,armeabi, armeabi-v7a,armeabi, h6.Expected No white corners appear when button is clicked (Xperia Play Android OS 4.0) h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Import Titanium Mobile project (attached) 2. Run it in device 3. Click in the button to see the issue. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18153,12,"""iOS: iPhone 6+ shares more orientation features with iPad than with iPhone, but Titanium controls as """"iPhone""""""","""""""h5. Description:  The iPhone 6+ shares many similarities with iPad in regards to orientation. Currently orientation is controlled with the iPhone tiapp.xml tag, so is not reaching it's full screen real estate potential.    The suggested improvement is to treat the 6+ orientation either separately or with more finite control for orientation to distinguish it from iPhone <=6.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Compare native applications run on iPhone 6, iPhone 6+ and iPad    h5. Result:  Most applications that do not rotate on iPhone 6 will rotate on iPhone 6+. In some cases, a master/detail view similar to iPad is shown on iPhone 6+ while the iPhone 6 retains a simpler view.    Also, the main UI rotates on iPad and iPhone 6+ but does not on iPhone 6    See the screen shots for comparison""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: iPhone 6+ shares more orientation features with iPad than with iPhone, but Titanium controls as """"iPhone""""
Description: """"h5. Description: The iPhone 6+ shares many similarities with iPad in regards to orientation. Currently orientation is controlled with the iPhone tiapp.xml tag, so is not reaching it's full screen real estate potential. The suggested improvement is to treat the 6+ orientation either separately or with more finite control for orientation to distinguish it from iPhone <=6. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Compare native applications run on iPhone 6, iPhone 6+ and iPad h5. Result: Most applications that do not rotate on iPhone 6 will rotate on iPhone 6+. In some cases, a master/detail view similar to iPad is shown on iPhone 6+ while the iPhone 6 retains a simpler view. Also, the main UI rotates on iPad and iPhone 6+ but does not on iPhone 6 See the screen shots for comparison""""",title+description
TIMOB-18151,12,"""Packaging the app onto Windows platform fails with invalid deploy type""","""""""Running the below command to package a mobile app onto Windows platform fails with invalid deploy type error, though we pass in """"""""production"""""""" when the target is set to dist-phonestore.        Looks CLI is looking for only test and development deploy types even for distribution builds.""""""",Bug,"Title: Packaging the app onto Windows platform fails with invalid deploy type
Description: """"Running the below command to package a mobile app onto Windows platform fails with invalid deploy type error, though we pass in """"""""production"""""""" when the target is set to dist-phonestore. Looks CLI is looking for only test and development deploy types even for distribution builds.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18148,12,"""Android: showAsAction can't take multiple parameters for MenuItem of Action Bar""","""""""Per Android action bar docs http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/actionbar.html    If your menu item supplies both a title and an icon—with the title and icon attributes—then the action item shows only the icon by default. If you want to display the text title, add """"""""withText"""""""" to the showAsAction attribute. For example:    <item yourapp:showAsAction=""""""""ifRoom|withText"""""""" ... />    it appears that you can't """"""""or"""""""" them together in titanium. It always just does the """"""""ifRoom"""""""" argument    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: showAsAction can't take multiple parameters for MenuItem of Action Bar
Description: """"Per Android action bar docs http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/actionbar.html If your menu item supplies both a title and an icon—with the title and icon attributes—then the action item shows only the icon by default. If you want to display the text title, add """"""""withText"""""""" to the showAsAction attribute. For example: <item yourapp:showAsAction=""""""""ifRoom|withText"""""""" ... /> it appears that you can't """"""""or"""""""" them together in titanium. It always just does the """"""""ifRoom"""""""" argument """"",title+description
TIMOB-18147,12,"""Android: Cannot get current activity from JavaScript broadcast receiver""","""""""REPRODUCTION:  Run the code below in the Genymotion emulator and click the """"""""Send Broadcast"""""""" button.    RESULTS:  Logcat reports that the current activity is a BroadcastReceiver object.        OTHER INFO:  Can get current activity using `this.Ti.Android.currentActivity`    */Resources/app.js*      */Resources/testintent.js*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot get current activity from JavaScript broadcast receiver
Description: """"REPRODUCTION: Run the code below in the Genymotion emulator and click the """"""""Send Broadcast"""""""" button. RESULTS: Logcat reports that the current activity is a BroadcastReceiver object. OTHER INFO: Can get current activity using `this.Ti.Android.currentActivity` */Resources/app.js* */Resources/testintent.js* """"",title+description
TIMOB-18141,12,"""LiveView reporting constant handled exceptions to APM""","""""""When LiveView disconnects from the server it starts throwing exception after exception.  We are currently capturing all of these exceptions which pollutes the Performance Management results for that application.  We either need to recognize that it is a LiveView error and not capture it OR we need LiveView to not fire off a bunch of errors when it gets disconnected.    Not to mention this is increasing API usage and server load.  For one sample app (single user), these errors account for over 1000 handled exceptions in a 24 hour period.        AND         AND     """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView reporting constant handled exceptions to APM
Description: """"When LiveView disconnects from the server it starts throwing exception after exception. We are currently capturing all of these exceptions which pollutes the Performance Management results for that application. We either need to recognize that it is a LiveView error and not capture it OR we need LiveView to not fire off a bunch of errors when it gets disconnected. Not to mention this is increasing API usage and server load. For one sample app (single user), these errors account for over 1000 handled exceptions in a 24 hour period. AND AND """"",title+description
TIMOB-18139,12,"""iOS: Alert gets moved if on screen when application error thrown""","""""""h5.Description    If an alert is on screen when the 'red screen' is thrown on device, when the screen is dismissed the alert appears in the upper left hand corner of the screen, as shown in the screenshot 3.5.0.     *This is a regression* as when using 3.4.1 and running the same code the behaviour is different. The alert is displayed on top of the 'red screen' and always stays centred, as shown in the screenshot 3.4.1    *Notes*    I am investigating to see if there are any other actions which cause this behaviour.  The alert can still be dismissed from it's position as the bottom can still be tapped        h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Add the code above to an existing project build and run on an iOS device using 3.5.0 SDK    h5.Actual Result    The alert will not be displayed on top of the 'red screen', when the 'red screen' is dismissed the alert is positioned at the top left of the screen.    h5.Expected Result    The alert should  be the top item in the window and should always be centred""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Alert gets moved if on screen when application error thrown
Description: """"h5.Description If an alert is on screen when the 'red screen' is thrown on device, when the screen is dismissed the alert appears in the upper left hand corner of the screen, as shown in the screenshot 3.5.0. *This is a regression* as when using 3.4.1 and running the same code the behaviour is different. The alert is displayed on top of the 'red screen' and always stays centred, as shown in the screenshot 3.4.1 *Notes* I am investigating to see if there are any other actions which cause this behaviour. The alert can still be dismissed from it's position as the bottom can still be tapped h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Add the code above to an existing project build and run on an iOS device using 3.5.0 SDK h5.Actual Result The alert will not be displayed on top of the 'red screen', when the 'red screen' is dismissed the alert is positioned at the top left of the screen. h5.Expected Result The alert should be the top item in the window and should always be centred""""",title+description
