TIMOB-18100,12,"""Android: Adding both swipe and scroll feature on a table view makes scroll choppy""","""""""Android: Adding both swipe and scroll feature on a table view makes scroll choppy.    h6.Reproduce Step:  1. Run the test case in Android (Simply attached the .xml, .tss and .js files for a Alloy project).  2. Scrolling the tableview Rows.    h6.Expect Result:  When you scroll down on the table view, there's some inertia and the table view keeps scrolling for a little bit, like the behave in iOS.    h6.Actual Result:  The scrolling stops as soon as the finger is lifted, making it hard to scroll through a long list    h6.N.B.   There is a same case for this issue [TIMOB-17539|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17539], but it has been few months, it keep in review but PR was close, So I am not sure what is the solution, or even is there is workaround for this.   """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Adding both swipe and scroll feature on a table view makes scroll choppy
Description: """"Android: Adding both swipe and scroll feature on a table view makes scroll choppy. h6.Reproduce Step: 1. Run the test case in Android (Simply attached the .xml, .tss and .js files for a Alloy project). 2. Scrolling the tableview Rows. h6.Expect Result: When you scroll down on the table view, there's some inertia and the table view keeps scrolling for a little bit, like the behave in iOS. h6.Actual Result: The scrolling stops as soon as the finger is lifted, making it hard to scroll through a long list h6.N.B. There is a same case for this issue [TIMOB-17539|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17539], but it has been few months, it keep in review but PR was close, So I am not sure what is the solution, or even is there is workaround for this. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18097,12,"""Android: App with module containing a native '.so' library fail to build""","""""""h5.Description:  1. Create a default app with services enabled.  2. Build it to an android device/emulator with sdk 3.6.0.v20141125101716.    h5.Actual Result:  1. The build fails with the following errors:    2. Talking to <USER>barber figured out that javascript context is not passed into forEach() loop in file _build.js at 1569 as there is no  which causes the failure.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: App with module containing a native '.so' library fail to build
Description: """"h5.Description: 1. Create a default app with services enabled. 2. Build it to an android device/emulator with sdk 3.6.0.v20141125101716. h5.Actual Result: 1. The build fails with the following errors: 2. Talking to <USER>barber figured out that javascript context is not passed into forEach() loop in file _build.js at 1569 as there is no which causes the failure.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18096,12,"""iOS: Proxies not being released""","""""""Titanium proxies are not being released.    Proxies are released correctly using 3.4.1.GA    h6. Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the code below  2. Run instruments on the xcode project generated  3. Look at allocations  4. Filter by """"""""proxy""""""""  5. Click the buttons in the example app.  6. Notice that the proxies are never released    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Proxies not being released
Description: """"Titanium proxies are not being released. Proxies are released correctly using 3.4.1.GA h6. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the code below 2. Run instruments on the xcode project generated 3. Look at allocations 4. Filter by """"""""proxy"""""""" 5. Click the buttons in the example app. 6. Notice that the proxies are never released """"",title+description
TIMOB-18088,12,"""iOS developer certs are not being recognized and 'Get new' button fails to authenticate""","""""""My developer certifications are not being recognized by Studio, nor is the WWDR certificate. All certs are verified and present in my keychains, but whether the default, System, or login keychains are selected, the refresh button only loads my Distribution certs. Attempting to obtain new copies through Studio's 'Get New' button errors out on the daw.apple.com side as can be seen in the following screen-cap: http://cl.ly/image/0F2c3a1Q0c1y   Here is another screen cap of an attempted deployment to device: http://cl.ly/image/2f2s263m471p (at the end, it goes to the same """"""""Oops!"""""""" page as the other).  I have already attempted to uninstall and re-install <USER>Studio to no avail.   """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS developer certs are not being recognized and 'Get new' button fails to authenticate
Description: """"My developer certifications are not being recognized by Studio, nor is the WWDR certificate. All certs are verified and present in my keychains, but whether the default, System, or login keychains are selected, the refresh button only loads my Distribution certs. Attempting to obtain new copies through Studio's 'Get New' button errors out on the daw.apple.com side as can be seen in the following screen-cap: http://cl.ly/image/0F2c3a1Q0c1y Here is another screen cap of an attempted deployment to device: http://cl.ly/image/2f2s263m471p (at the end, it goes to the same """"""""Oops!"""""""" page as the other). I have already attempted to uninstall and re-install <USER>Studio to no avail. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18086,12,"""iOS: file.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_READ) crashes while opening the file object.""","""""""Description:    In the below test case, getFile() method of Filesystem is used for returning the file present at apps Resources folder.   The application crashes when tried to open the return file object by using its open() method.     This is not a regression as able to reproduce it with 3.4.0 GA and 3.3.0.GA.    TestCase:  var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory, 'acceptance.js');  var stream = f.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_READ); // crash    STEPS TO REPRODUCE:  1. Create the classic iOS titanium application.  2. Replace the code in app.js with the code mentioned above.  3. Add any file named as acceptance.js in its Resources folder.  4. Build the application and launch it on device.    EXPECTED RESULTs:  4. The application should launch successfully on device.    ACTUAL RESULTS:  4. The application crashes while launching with the below error.      Please refer attachment as well.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: file.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_READ) crashes while opening the file object.
Description: """"Description: In the below test case, getFile() method of Filesystem is used for returning the file present at apps Resources folder. The application crashes when tried to open the return file object by using its open() method. This is not a regression as able to reproduce it with 3.4.0 GA and 3.3.0.GA. TestCase: var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory, 'acceptance.js'); var stream = f.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_READ); // crash STEPS TO REPRODUCE: 1. Create the classic iOS titanium application. 2. Replace the code in app.js with the code mentioned above. 3. Add any file named as acceptance.js in its Resources folder. 4. Build the application and launch it on device. EXPECTED RESULTs: 4. The application should launch successfully on device. ACTUAL RESULTS: 4. The application crashes while launching with the below error. Please refer attachment as well. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18084,12,"""Make a built-in cache clearing for WebView""","""""""Having a built-in feature to clear a WebView's cache just seems right. If modern web browsers give users the ability to clear the cache or cookies or sessions, a cross-platform like Titanium's WebView should give that feature as well. """"""",New Feature,"Title: Make a built-in cache clearing for WebView
Description: """"Having a built-in feature to clear a WebView's cache just seems right. If modern web browsers give users the ability to clear the cache or cookies or sessions, a cross-platform like Titanium's WebView should give that feature as well. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18083,12,"""Android: DisplayCaps density for nexus 6 is shown as medium""","""""""h5.Description:  1. Replace the app.js with the code below:    2. Build & run the app on Nexus 6 device.    h5.Actual Results:  1. The alert shows the displayCaps.density property to be """"""""medium"""""""", but Nexus 6 has a resolution of 1440 x 2560 pixels & 493ppi density.  2. A Nexus 5 which is 1080 x 1920 pixels & 445ppi density shows as """"""""xxhigh"""""""" for the same code.    h5.Expected Results:  1. We should see xxhigh or more for displayCaps.density for Nexus 6.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: DisplayCaps density for nexus 6 is shown as medium
Description: """"h5.Description: 1. Replace the app.js with the code below: 2. Build & run the app on Nexus 6 device. h5.Actual Results: 1. The alert shows the displayCaps.density property to be """"""""medium"""""""", but Nexus 6 has a resolution of 1440 x 2560 pixels & 493ppi density. 2. A Nexus 5 which is 1080 x 1920 pixels & 445ppi density shows as """"""""xxhigh"""""""" for the same code. h5.Expected Results: 1. We should see xxhigh or more for displayCaps.density for Nexus 6.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18078,12,"""iOS: Ti.Stream.read() doesn't work with Ti.Filesystem.FileStream""","""""""h2. problem    Using {{Ti.Stream.read()}} with an open {{Ti.Filesystem.FileStream}} does nothing. The read call never invokes the result callback. Android works fine, but iOS always fails as described above, despite the documentation indicating that both support {{Ti.Stream.read()}} on FileStream. Without this support there is no asynchronous way to read files with Titanium on iOS, all reads must be blocking.    h2. test case        h2. expected    The results callback should return an event object ({{e}}) containing all relevant information regarding the read operation. Both {{Ti.API.error}} calls should execute and print the results.    h2. actual    The results callback is never executed. Nothing is printed.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Stream.read() doesn't work with Ti.Filesystem.FileStream
Description: """"h2. problem Using {{Ti.Stream.read()}} with an open {{Ti.Filesystem.FileStream}} does nothing. The read call never invokes the result callback. Android works fine, but iOS always fails as described above, despite the documentation indicating that both support {{Ti.Stream.read()}} on FileStream. Without this support there is no asynchronous way to read files with Titanium on iOS, all reads must be blocking. h2. test case h2. expected The results callback should return an event object ({{e}}) containing all relevant information regarding the read operation. Both {{Ti.API.error}} calls should execute and print the results. h2. actual The results callback is never executed. Nothing is printed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18077,12,"""iOS:Double tap on the textfield to show an alert message does not work when the keyboard is displayed""","""""""When double tap event is used for eventListener, the alert message doesn't show up once the keyboard appears. When the event is changed to other events like swipe the alert message appears even when the keyboard is visible.     This is not a regression as it also reproducible with Titanium SDK 3.4.1    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the attached app.js   2. double tap on the textfield  3. single tap on the textfield   4. double tap on the textfield    Actual Results:  2. The alert message showing """"""""textfield value:"""""""" should appear  3. The keyboard appears  4. Sometimes the alert message appears but repeating steps 3 and 4 several times results in the alert message not appearing after that.    Expected Results:  4. The alert message should appear and it should not be intermittent. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS:Double tap on the textfield to show an alert message does not work when the keyboard is displayed
Description: """"When double tap event is used for eventListener, the alert message doesn't show up once the keyboard appears. When the event is changed to other events like swipe the alert message appears even when the keyboard is visible. This is not a regression as it also reproducible with Titanium SDK 3.4.1 Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the attached app.js 2. double tap on the textfield 3. single tap on the textfield 4. double tap on the textfield Actual Results: 2. The alert message showing """"""""textfield value:"""""""" should appear 3. The keyboard appears 4. Sometimes the alert message appears but repeating steps 3 and 4 several times results in the alert message not appearing after that. Expected Results: 4. The alert message should appear and it should not be intermittent. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18076,12,"""iOS: Keyboard disappears when alert message is fired due to an eventListener on the textfield""","""""""When an eventListener is added to a textfield to show an alert box when the textfield is in focus the keyboard immediately disappears as soon as the alert message appears. This happens regardless of the type of event used in the eventListener. However, using titanium SDK 3.4.1 the alert message appears with the keyboard backgrounded and clicking on the OK button of the alert message allows the user to continue typing which is not possible with the current version.     -->This is a regression.    Steps to reproduce:  1.Run the attached app.js  2. Click on textfield to bring up the softkeyboard     Actual Results:  The keyboard appears and immediately disappears when the alert message appears and hence unable to type anything on to the textfield.    Expected results:  The softkeyboard should show up and alert with no textfield value should also appear. Clicking on the ok button of the alert message should bring the keyboard to focus allowing the user to type.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Keyboard disappears when alert message is fired due to an eventListener on the textfield
Description: """"When an eventListener is added to a textfield to show an alert box when the textfield is in focus the keyboard immediately disappears as soon as the alert message appears. This happens regardless of the type of event used in the eventListener. However, using titanium SDK 3.4.1 the alert message appears with the keyboard backgrounded and clicking on the OK button of the alert message allows the user to continue typing which is not possible with the current version. -->This is a regression. Steps to reproduce: 1.Run the attached app.js 2. Click on textfield to bring up the softkeyboard Actual Results: The keyboard appears and immediately disappears when the alert message appears and hence unable to type anything on to the textfield. Expected results: The softkeyboard should show up and alert with no textfield value should also appear. Clicking on the ok button of the alert message should bring the keyboard to focus allowing the user to type. """"",title+description
TIMOB-18075,12,"""iOS: Window focus event is not triggered when switch back from another tab""","""""""Window *Focus* Event is not triggered when we switch between tabs in iOS device.   For Android, It works fine.    This is a *regression* since it doesn't occur in SDK 3.4.1 GA    h5. Steps To Reproduce  1. Create a default titanium classic project  2. Insert following code in your app.js file    3. Run the app in iOS device   4. Switch between *tab 1* and *tab 2*    h5. Expected Result  An alert should appear with text """"""""focused!""""""""    h5. Actual Result  Alert does not appear with SDK version 3.5.0    h5. Tested app.js file  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window focus event is not triggered when switch back from another tab
Description: """"Window *Focus* Event is not triggered when we switch between tabs in iOS device. For Android, It works fine. This is a *regression* since it doesn't occur in SDK 3.4.1 GA h5. Steps To Reproduce 1. Create a default titanium classic project 2. Insert following code in your app.js file 3. Run the app in iOS device 4. Switch between *tab 1* and *tab 2* h5. Expected Result An alert should appear with text """"""""focused!"""""""" h5. Actual Result Alert does not appear with SDK version 3.5.0 h5. Tested app.js file """"",title+description
TIMOB-18071,12,"""CLI: Fail build if compiled architectures do not match module manifest""","""""""With the addition of 64-bit support, it becomes helpful to know the architectures available in a compiled module. We can then use this ins tooling to make sure modules are compiled correctly for use.    See TIMOB-18065 for more information.    Once the module build is complete, we need to check the architectures specified and fail the build if they do not match.    * If the line exists, but is wrong, suggest the updated version. If they are missing 64-bit for iOS, warn them  * If the line does not exist, suggest what it should be.""""""",Improvement,"Title: CLI: Fail build if compiled architectures do not match module manifest
Description: """"With the addition of 64-bit support, it becomes helpful to know the architectures available in a compiled module. We can then use this ins tooling to make sure modules are compiled correctly for use. See TIMOB-18065 for more information. Once the module build is complete, we need to check the architectures specified and fail the build if they do not match. * If the line exists, but is wrong, suggest the updated version. If they are missing 64-bit for iOS, warn them * If the line does not exist, suggest what it should be.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18069,12,"""Android: make ListSection.getItemCount() and/or getContentCount() public""","""""""For now it is not possible to get count if items inside list (or section) filtered by search view on android. ListSection.itemCount is avaliable for iOS (however not documented) but not for android.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: make ListSection.getItemCount() and/or getContentCount() public
Description: """"For now it is not possible to get count if items inside list (or section) filtered by search view on android. ListSection.itemCount is avaliable for iOS (however not documented) but not for android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18068,12,"""Text field in table won't retain focus on some Android devices""","""""""Please see attached Alloy project. On a Samsung Galaxy Nexus running Android 4.3, it's very difficult to edit the text field because it seems to lose focus as soon as you click on it.    I tried this on 3 other Android devices running various Android versions and could not find any other device exhibiting this problem.""""""",Bug,"Title: Text field in table won't retain focus on some Android devices
Description: """"Please see attached Alloy project. On a Samsung Galaxy Nexus running Android 4.3, it's very difficult to edit the text field because it seems to lose focus as soon as you click on it. I tried this on 3 other Android devices running various Android versions and could not find any other device exhibiting this problem.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18067,12,"""CLI: Running """"ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal -P --no-colors"""" command throws longjohn error. ""","""""""Description:  CLI throws longjohn error while building an iOS application with colors flag set to false and when input value is given for provisioning profile prompt.    This is not a regression. Reproducible with earlier releases.    STEPS TO REPRODUCE:-  1. Create titanium iOS project and cd to the project.  2. Run """"""""ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal -P --no-colors"""""""" command.   OR  2. Run the below commands   """"""""ti config cli.colors false""""""""  """"""""ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal -P""""""""    EXPECTED RESULT  2. The CLI should accept all the valid input values from the user and build the project successfully.    ACTUAL RESULT  2. The CLI throws the below long john error when input value '1' is given for the distribution certificate prompt.        Note: """"""""ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal --pp-uuid --no-colors"""""""" works fine.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Running """"ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal -P --no-colors"""" command throws longjohn error.
Description: """"Description: CLI throws longjohn error while building an iOS application with colors flag set to false and when input value is given for provisioning profile prompt. This is not a regression. Reproducible with earlier releases. STEPS TO REPRODUCE:- 1. Create titanium iOS project and cd to the project. 2. Run """"""""ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal -P --no-colors"""""""" command. OR 2. Run the below commands """"""""ti config cli.colors false"""""""" """"""""ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal -P"""""""" EXPECTED RESULT 2. The CLI should accept all the valid input values from the user and build the project successfully. ACTUAL RESULT 2. The CLI throws the below long john error when input value '1' is given for the distribution certificate prompt. Note: """"""""ti build -p ios -T dist-adhoc -F universal --pp-uuid --no-colors"""""""" works fine.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18064,12,"""iOS: New Profiler does not generate function names""","""""""After the update of TiJSCore(TIMOB-11093) and titanium_profiler(TIMOB-17925) for 64 bit support the profiler is no longer emitting explicit function names. Most function calls show up as either (anonymous functions) or (program). This is a change in behavior from the old profiler behavior where the function names would show up.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: New Profiler does not generate function names
Description: """"After the update of TiJSCore(TIMOB-11093) and titanium_profiler(TIMOB-17925) for 64 bit support the profiler is no longer emitting explicit function names. Most function calls show up as either (anonymous functions) or (program). This is a change in behavior from the old profiler behavior where the function names would show up.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18061,12,"""Kitchen Sink: Platform > XHR > Error Callback attempts to open nonexistent URL""","""""""The KitchenSink test:  Platform > XHR > Error Callback, makes a call to http://www.fre100.com which currently does not exist. This causes no response to be given for the UTF-8 GET.    Recommend we change the URL to: http://www.<USER>com/    *Steps to reproduce issue:*  1. Launch KitchenSink  2. Go to the Platform > XHR > Error Callback test  3. Notice that the response says """"""""A server with the specified hostname could not be found.""""""""    *Expected Result*:  A proper response should be shown, without error.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Kitchen Sink: Platform > XHR > Error Callback attempts to open nonexistent URL
Description: """"The KitchenSink test: Platform > XHR > Error Callback, makes a call to http://www.fre100.com which currently does not exist. This causes no response to be given for the UTF-8 GET. Recommend we change the URL to: http://www.<USER>com/ *Steps to reproduce issue:* 1. Launch KitchenSink 2. Go to the Platform > XHR > Error Callback test 3. Notice that the response says """"""""A server with the specified hostname could not be found."""""""" *Expected Result*: A proper response should be shown, without error.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18060,12,"""CLI: When building to simulator the log output contains two [DEBUG] tags""","""""""h5.Description    When building to an iOS Simulator after the simulator has finished launching the following is logged to the terminal, on lines 4 to 11 the logging contains two \[DEBUG] tags and both \[ioslib] and \[ios-sim]      however on 3.4.1.GA the output is the following      h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Using 3.4.2 or 3.5.0 SDK build a project to an iOS Simulator with the log level set to trace     2. After the simulator has launched check the output in the terminal    h5.Actual Result      The output matches what is shown above and contains two \[DEBUG] tags    h5.Expected Result    The output should not contain two tags""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: When building to simulator the log output contains two [DEBUG] tags
Description: """"h5.Description When building to an iOS Simulator after the simulator has finished launching the following is logged to the terminal, on lines 4 to 11 the logging contains two \[DEBUG] tags and both \[ioslib] and \[ios-sim] however on 3.4.1.GA the output is the following h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Using 3.4.2 or 3.5.0 SDK build a project to an iOS Simulator with the log level set to trace 2. After the simulator has launched check the output in the terminal h5.Actual Result The output matches what is shown above and contains two \[DEBUG] tags h5.Expected Result The output should not contain two tags""""",title+description
TIMOB-18059,12,"""Tooling: Create """"Tested"""" status page for SDK dependencies""","""""""Between Google and Apple alone, there have been 30+ releases this year of various pieces of our software stack.    While we blog when something is truly broken (i.e. http://www.<USER>com/blog/2014/10/updating-to-android-platform-tools-version-21/), and we link people to tickets to track status, it's not feasible to let everyone know in this way if Android SDK 23.0.2 is safe to use (though we may have tested it internally to confirm)    A easy proposal would be to create a status page, similar to http://status.<USER>com. I have investigated reusing an existing status page sites, but they are not quite right for the purpose, so I believe we may need to create our own.    Requirements:  * Groups for each of the main families (Apple, Google, BlackBerry, Microsoft, etc)  * Sub-sections for each of the individual areas (iOS, OS X). Debatable if we should instead just have them in a date-ordered cross-product list.  * Columns for name, version, test environment, related JIRA tickets  ** green = tested  ** yellow = test in progress  ** red = test failed  ** grey = untested    My expectation this would be a Node.ACS application with some way of adding items to the matrix, and another item for updating status. Perhaps we can query status based on JIRA tickets...even if QE has an internal ticket to verify it working, the status page changes color based on that.    See attached page for a sample (though could be made prettier)""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Create """"Tested"""" status page for SDK dependencies
Description: """"Between Google and Apple alone, there have been 30+ releases this year of various pieces of our software stack. While we blog when something is truly broken (i.e. http://www.<USER>com/blog/2014/10/updating-to-android-platform-tools-version-21/), and we link people to tickets to track status, it's not feasible to let everyone know in this way if Android SDK 23.0.2 is safe to use (though we may have tested it internally to confirm) A easy proposal would be to create a status page, similar to http://status.<USER>com. I have investigated reusing an existing status page sites, but they are not quite right for the purpose, so I believe we may need to create our own. Requirements: * Groups for each of the main families (Apple, Google, BlackBerry, Microsoft, etc) * Sub-sections for each of the individual areas (iOS, OS X). Debatable if we should instead just have them in a date-ordered cross-product list. * Columns for name, version, test environment, related JIRA tickets ** green = tested ** yellow = test in progress ** red = test failed ** grey = untested My expectation this would be a Node.ACS application with some way of adding items to the matrix, and another item for updating status. Perhaps we can query status based on JIRA tickets...even if QE has an internal ticket to verify it working, the status page changes color based on that. See attached page for a sample (though could be made prettier)""""",title+description
TIMOB-18058,12,"""Kitchen Sink: Not able to change url of sound; Remove button""","""""""In the Kitchen Sink test: Phone > Sound > Local with File URL, there is a button to """"""""Change file"""""""". It is intended to change the file that the sound is playing by changing the URL of that sound. This does not work and the sound is not changed.    Please see TIMOB-3348 and TIMOB-1488 where this issue was flagged and marked as 'won't fix'. Requesting that the """"""""Change file"""""""" button be removed from the test.    *Steps to reproduce issue:*  1. Launch Kitchen Sink  2. Go to the Phone > Sound > Local with File URL test  3. Click Play. Notice that the crickets noise plays  4. Click Change file. Notice that the crickets noise continues to play    *Expected Result:*  Either the noise will change or the button should not be present if the functionality doesn't exist (looks like the case)    *Actual Result:*  The sound doesn't change    The """"""""Change file"""""""" button should be removed.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Kitchen Sink: Not able to change url of sound; Remove button
Description: """"In the Kitchen Sink test: Phone > Sound > Local with File URL, there is a button to """"""""Change file"""""""". It is intended to change the file that the sound is playing by changing the URL of that sound. This does not work and the sound is not changed. Please see TIMOB-3348 and TIMOB-1488 where this issue was flagged and marked as 'won't fix'. Requesting that the """"""""Change file"""""""" button be removed from the test. *Steps to reproduce issue:* 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Go to the Phone > Sound > Local with File URL test 3. Click Play. Notice that the crickets noise plays 4. Click Change file. Notice that the crickets noise continues to play *Expected Result:* Either the noise will change or the button should not be present if the functionality doesn't exist (looks like the case) *Actual Result:* The sound doesn't change The """"""""Change file"""""""" button should be removed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18057,12,"""Android: Setting """"backgroundColor"""" on a Window or View hides the TextFields grey underline denoting that it is editable""","""""""h4. Problem Description  In the Android OS TextFields should have a grey/black line underneath them when they are unfocused so users can see that it is an editable field.  This line is not visible when the """"""""backgroundColor"""""""" style is applied to any Windows/Views containing TextFields.  This is a significant issue as it makes all TextFields look like Labels.    The blue """"""""focused"""""""" line appears ok.        h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a simple project.  2.Update app.js with test code    3. Run on android device      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Setting """"backgroundColor"""" on a Window or View hides the TextFields grey underline denoting that it is editable
Description: """"h4. Problem Description In the Android OS TextFields should have a grey/black line underneath them when they are unfocused so users can see that it is an editable field. This line is not visible when the """"""""backgroundColor"""""""" style is applied to any Windows/Views containing TextFields. This is a significant issue as it makes all TextFields look like Labels. The blue """"""""focused"""""""" line appears ok. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a simple project. 2.Update app.js with test code 3. Run on android device """"",title+description
TIMOB-18056,12,"""iOS: StatusBar disappears on forced orientation change ""","""""""    Opening win2 by clicking the button, after opening the window change the orientation of the simulator to either landscape then press the navigation windows back button, now the all the sudden the StatusBar is gone from the application, rotating the simulator back to portrait will bring it back but shouldn't it appear as soon as the forced orientation change is made?""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: StatusBar disappears on forced orientation change
Description: """" Opening win2 by clicking the button, after opening the window change the orientation of the simulator to either landscape then press the navigation windows back button, now the all the sudden the StatusBar is gone from the application, rotating the simulator back to portrait will bring it back but shouldn't it appear as soon as the forced orientation change is made?""""",title+description
TIMOB-18055,12,"""Titanium VideoPlayer initialPlaybackTime setting does not work for second video in VideoPlayer""","""""""Hello,    I am using a playlist to simulate some kind of Live-TV.  When the user initially opens the window and plays the video, the initialplaybacktime is set correctly of the video.     Then if the user stops the video by clicking on it (Looks like it's being paused but actually it's stopped ($.video.stop()) to reload the playlist and get the live elapsed time) and then clicks it again.    When the user clicks it after it's stopped, the playlist is reloaded and the current video is set as url and it's elapsed time is set with setInitialPlaybackTime().    But this doesn't work, and it results into a 'NaN' if I try to retrieve it the playback has started the second time, so not the initial time the user opens the window.    h4. Testcase      This code exactly shows in the logs that it does not work.    Regards,  <USER>""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium VideoPlayer initialPlaybackTime setting does not work for second video in VideoPlayer
Description: """"Hello, I am using a playlist to simulate some kind of Live-TV. When the user initially opens the window and plays the video, the initialplaybacktime is set correctly of the video. Then if the user stops the video by clicking on it (Looks like it's being paused but actually it's stopped ($.video.stop()) to reload the playlist and get the live elapsed time) and then clicks it again. When the user clicks it after it's stopped, the playlist is reloaded and the current video is set as url and it's elapsed time is set with setInitialPlaybackTime(). But this doesn't work, and it results into a 'NaN' if I try to retrieve it the playback has started the second time, so not the initial time the user opens the window. h4. Testcase This code exactly shows in the logs that it does not work. Regards, <USER>""",title+description
