TIMOB-18040,12,"""Android: Expose """"gravity"""" constants in Ti.UI.Notification""","""""""I'd like to position an Android Toast ({{Ti.UI.Notification}} on the top half of the screen. I thought this wasn't possible, but then found that the first [gravity|http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/notifiers/toasts.html#Positioning] argument for {{setGravity}} that I needed is actually [exposed|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/58198c641d77e17d156431666e80bae732b5c130/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUINotification.java#L65-L69], just not documented.    Using the integer value of the Android documentation for [Gravity.TOP|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/Gravity.html#TOP] I was able to position the Toast on the top half of the screen:        My request is:    * Document the `gravity` property  * Expose the gravity constants ({{Ti.UI.Android.GRAVITY_TOP}} etc..)""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose """"gravity"""" constants in Ti.UI.Notification
Description: """"I'd like to position an Android Toast ({{Ti.UI.Notification}} on the top half of the screen. I thought this wasn't possible, but then found that the first [gravity|http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/notifiers/toasts.html#Positioning] argument for {{setGravity}} that I needed is actually [exposed|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/58198c641d77e17d156431666e80bae732b5c130/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUINotification.java#L65-L69], just not documented. Using the integer value of the Android documentation for [Gravity.TOP|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/Gravity.html#TOP] I was able to position the Toast on the top half of the screen: My request is: * Document the `gravity` property * Expose the gravity constants ({{Ti.UI.Android.GRAVITY_TOP}} etc..)""""",title+description
TIMOB-18039,12,"""Add `once`, `on` and `off` to Titanium proxies""","""""""When digging through some source code I discovered Android has a hidden {{once()}} method to add an event listener that only fires once and {{removeAllListeners()}} to remove all listeners to a certain event:    - http://www.tidev.io/2014/11/10/hidden-event-methods-on-android/    Why aren't these methods documented and why not bring these to all platforms?    Both have very good use cases to me in almost every app.    I'd even suggest the following:        The last one would make cleaning up and preventing memory leaks a lot easier as well.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Add `once`, `on` and `off` to Titanium proxies
Description: """"When digging through some source code I discovered Android has a hidden {{once()}} method to add an event listener that only fires once and {{removeAllListeners()}} to remove all listeners to a certain event: - http://www.tidev.io/2014/11/10/hidden-event-methods-on-android/ Why aren't these methods documented and why not bring these to all platforms? Both have very good use cases to me in almost every app. I'd even suggest the following: The last one would make cleaning up and preventing memory leaks a lot easier as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18037,12,"""Parity: Handing of links in Attributed Strings for Label, TextField and TextArea""","""""""Only for TextArea we have a property [handleLinks|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextArea-property-handleLinks] which if set to `true` fires the `link` event for a single-tap on a link in an Attributed String.    - For Label only a long-press can trigger this event, making a poor UX.  - For TextField there's no such event at all, making the attribute type useless.  - For TextArea the link has a different color, no underline and a tap will always open the URL in Safari before firing the {{link}} event, allowing no custom actions. Also, the documentation does not inform you about the need for {{editable}} to be set to {{false}} to capture link events.    h1. Test case        h1. Suggested changes:    * Bring {{handleLinks}} to TextField and Label  * Let {{handleLinks}} automatically set {{editable}} to {{false}}.  * Use the same color and underlining of links in TextAreas as in TextFields and Labels.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Parity: Handing of links in Attributed Strings for Label, TextField and TextArea
Description: """"Only for TextArea we have a property [handleLinks|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextArea-property-handleLinks] which if set to `true` fires the `link` event for a single-tap on a link in an Attributed String. - For Label only a long-press can trigger this event, making a poor UX. - For TextField there's no such event at all, making the attribute type useless. - For TextArea the link has a different color, no underline and a tap will always open the URL in Safari before firing the {{link}} event, allowing no custom actions. Also, the documentation does not inform you about the need for {{editable}} to be set to {{false}} to capture link events. h1. Test case h1. Suggested changes: * Bring {{handleLinks}} to TextField and Label * Let {{handleLinks}} automatically set {{editable}} to {{false}}. * Use the same color and underlining of links in TextAreas as in TextFields and Labels.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18036,12,"""Ti.Calendar.Event - Maintain the same properties on both iOS and Android""","""""""Description of a calendar event is exposed by Ti.Calendar.Event.description property on android and Ti.Calendar.Event.notes property in iOS. Since the purpose is same, it is nice to have common property name to support cross platform code.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Ti.Calendar.Event - Maintain the same properties on both iOS and Android
Description: """"Description of a calendar event is exposed by Ti.Calendar.Event.description property on android and Ti.Calendar.Event.notes property in iOS. Since the purpose is same, it is nice to have common property name to support cross platform code.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18032,12,"""CLI: Add support for the create command for Windows platform""","""""""By default the """"""""ti create"""""""" command will copy all Windows platform specific template files. If the Windows platform has specific logic above and beyond simply copying files, then this ticket is for that work. If creating a Windows app only copies template files, then this ticket may be resolved as invalid.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Add support for the create command for Windows platform
Description: """"By default the """"""""ti create"""""""" command will copy all Windows platform specific template files. If the Windows platform has specific logic above and beyond simply copying files, then this ticket is for that work. If creating a Windows app only copies template files, then this ticket may be resolved as invalid.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18030,12,"""Android: The version number in the analytics payload is incorrect when using getLastEvent or lastEvent to show payload on device""","""""""h5.Description    *Please note* This only is incorrect when checking the last event on the device, the payload sent by the device has the correct version number as verified by checking what staging server is receiving. On iOS the correct version number is returned.    When using the getLastEvent method or checking the lastEvent property the payload returned refers to the version as 4, when it is actually version 3. This only occurs since the change in the payload version, prior to 3.3.0 the version number is correctly referred to as 2.    *On device*      *On staging*    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Add the attached app.js to an existing project and build to device.  2. Run the app and send an event by tapping one of the buttons in the top half of the screen  3. Tap the getLastEvent button and the bottom of the screen will be updated with the event sent.     h5.Actual Result    The payload is like the above, the version number is 4.    h5.Expected Result    The payload should match what we see on staging, with the version number being 3.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: The version number in the analytics payload is incorrect when using getLastEvent or lastEvent to show payload on device
Description: """"h5.Description *Please note* This only is incorrect when checking the last event on the device, the payload sent by the device has the correct version number as verified by checking what staging server is receiving. On iOS the correct version number is returned. When using the getLastEvent method or checking the lastEvent property the payload returned refers to the version as 4, when it is actually version 3. This only occurs since the change in the payload version, prior to 3.3.0 the version number is correctly referred to as 2. *On device* *On staging* h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Add the attached app.js to an existing project and build to device. 2. Run the app and send an event by tapping one of the buttons in the top half of the screen 3. Tap the getLastEvent button and the bottom of the screen will be updated with the event sent. h5.Actual Result The payload is like the above, the version number is 4. h5.Expected Result The payload should match what we see on staging, with the version number being 3.""""",title+description
TIMOB-18024,12,"""iOS: Referencing Titanium object from Xcode Instruments Native objects""","""""""I'd like to understand if its possible to identify a reference from a TiUIView or a TiUIViewProxy from Xcode instruments to Alloy.  Is this currently possible?  If not, what would it take to do this?""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Referencing Titanium object from Xcode Instruments Native objects
Description: """"I'd like to understand if its possible to identify a reference from a TiUIView or a TiUIViewProxy from Xcode instruments to Alloy. Is this currently possible? If not, what would it take to do this?""""",title+description
TIMOB-18023,12,"""Android: Feature Request: To be able to configure the android location update settings to use GPS, NETWORK, or PASSIVE so that we can just configure the updateDistance and time for the location updates""","""""""h6.Request Description  While using the Titanium.Geolocation.Android manual mode, only one provider is registered at the time. If the application is facing these scenarios:     * If the application isn't getting updates frequently enough, it can adjust its provider settings to provide more updates, or relax its location rules to allow less accurate updates through.   * If the application isn't receiving accurate enough updates from one provider, it can add another provider to try to improve results.   * If the application is getting sufficiently accurate results from the network provider, it can disable the GPS provider to save power.    h6.Customer's remarks  That would require a lot of additional logic for android only to have it switch between them during the scenarios outlined previously.     Would it be possible that we be able to configure the android location update settings to use GPS, NETWORK, or PASSIVE so that we can just configure the updateDistance and time for the location updates.    That would bring this into close parity with the iOS implementation.     h6.Titanium Docs  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Geolocation.Android""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Feature Request: To be able to configure the android location update settings to use GPS, NETWORK, or PASSIVE so that we can just configure the updateDistance and time for the location updates
Description: """"h6.Request Description While using the Titanium.Geolocation.Android manual mode, only one provider is registered at the time. If the application is facing these scenarios: * If the application isn't getting updates frequently enough, it can adjust its provider settings to provide more updates, or relax its location rules to allow less accurate updates through. * If the application isn't receiving accurate enough updates from one provider, it can add another provider to try to improve results. * If the application is getting sufficiently accurate results from the network provider, it can disable the GPS provider to save power. h6.Customer's remarks That would require a lot of additional logic for android only to have it switch between them during the scenarios outlined previously. Would it be possible that we be able to configure the android location update settings to use GPS, NETWORK, or PASSIVE so that we can just configure the updateDistance and time for the location updates. That would bring this into close parity with the iOS implementation. h6.Titanium Docs http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.Geolocation.Android""""",title+description
