TIMOB-17936,12,"""Implement onLoadResource event for Android WebViews""","""""""The TiWebviewClient.java overrides the """"""""onPageStarted"""""""" method to trigger the """"""""beforeload"""""""" event.  As the Android API states:   bq. This method is called once for each main frame load so a page with iframes or framesets will call onPageStarted one time for the main frame.    This means, that the method won't get triggered, when a URL inside an iFrame/Frame changes.     Implementing an """"""""onLoadResource"""""""" function and triggering a new """"""""beforeresourceload"""""""" event would solve this issue.    The problem does not exist on iOS devices, as the event gets triggered with iFrames as well.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Implement onLoadResource event for Android WebViews
Description: """"The TiWebviewClient.java overrides the """"""""onPageStarted"""""""" method to trigger the """"""""beforeload"""""""" event. As the Android API states: bq. This method is called once for each main frame load so a page with iframes or framesets will call onPageStarted one time for the main frame. This means, that the method won't get triggered, when a URL inside an iFrame/Frame changes. Implementing an """"""""onLoadResource"""""""" function and triggering a new """"""""beforeresourceload"""""""" event would solve this issue. The problem does not exist on iOS devices, as the event gets triggered with iFrames as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17935,12,"""Android: Implement listview indexes""","""""""For both tableviews and listviews the quick access index is only available on iOS. The feature is available in the Android UI and so please can the parity be fixed?    Ref for example: http://www.brightec.co.uk/blog/android-listview-alphabet-scroller  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Implement listview indexes
Description: """"For both tableviews and listviews the quick access index is only available on iOS. The feature is available in the Android UI and so please can the parity be fixed? Ref for example: http://www.brightec.co.uk/blog/android-listview-alphabet-scroller """"",title+description
TIMOB-17934,12,"""Tooling needs project validation similar to iTunes Connect validation in xcode""","""""""h4.iOS    With now 3 densities to support, we have an increase in graphics required by a  project.  It would be great if when building for dist-appstore or dist-adhoc missing splash screen and icon assets were flagged and a warning displayed for the user.    h4. Android    Android is a bit more difficult as assets are not required, but density specific resources are recommended.    """"""",Improvement,"Title: Tooling needs project validation similar to iTunes Connect validation in xcode
Description: """"h4.iOS With now 3 densities to support, we have an increase in graphics required by a project. It would be great if when building for dist-appstore or dist-adhoc missing splash screen and icon assets were flagged and a warning displayed for the user. h4. Android Android is a bit more difficult as assets are not required, but density specific resources are recommended. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17932,12,"""Investigate android material design support via updated appcompat library for older android devices""","""""""h4. Reference  http://android-developers.blogspot.com/2014/10/appcompat-v21-material-design-for-pre.html    https://developer.android.com/tools/support-library/features.html#v7-appcompat""""""",New Feature,"Title: Investigate android material design support via updated appcompat library for older android devices
