TIMOB-17871,12,"""Android: Genymotion - Cannot install Titanium app to Genymotion with latest Android Platform-tools and build-tools 20""","""""""*Details:* Cannot install Titanium app to Genymotion with latest Android Platform-tools (21) and old Android SDK build-tools (20).    *Notes:*  * With this current environment setup, you can still install a Titanium app to the stock Android emulator.  * If you use Android Platform-tools 21 and Android SDK build-tools 21 (latest), then you will get the *Failed to package application* error for both Genymotion *and* stock emulator; see ticket https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17872    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Make sure you have Android SDK Tools 23.0.5 *and* Android SDK Build-tools 20  2. Create a titanium app from CLI  3. Install app to Genymotion emulator e.g. {{ti build --no-banner --no-colors -p android -T emulator -C """"""""API19_Genymotion_4.4.4""""""""}}    *Actual:* CLI will eventually exit (stop processing) and not install the app to Genymotion emulator even though Genymotion emulator is launched; see attachment terminal_logs.txt.    *Expected:* Should be able to install Titanium app to Genymotion emulator with this setup.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Genymotion - Cannot install Titanium app to Genymotion with latest Android Platform-tools and build-tools 20
Description: """"*Details:* Cannot install Titanium app to Genymotion with latest Android Platform-tools (21) and old Android SDK build-tools (20). *Notes:* * With this current environment setup, you can still install a Titanium app to the stock Android emulator. * If you use Android Platform-tools 21 and Android SDK build-tools 21 (latest), then you will get the *Failed to package application* error for both Genymotion *and* stock emulator; see ticket https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17872 *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Make sure you have Android SDK Tools 23.0.5 *and* Android SDK Build-tools 20 2. Create a titanium app from CLI 3. Install app to Genymotion emulator e.g. {{ti build --no-banner --no-colors -p android -T emulator -C """"""""API19_Genymotion_4.4.4""""""""}} *Actual:* CLI will eventually exit (stop processing) and not install the app to Genymotion emulator even though Genymotion emulator is launched; see attachment terminal_logs.txt. *Expected:* Should be able to install Titanium app to Genymotion emulator with this setup.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17870,12,"""Android: HAXM not working with MAC Yosemite GM Candidate 2""","""""""h6.NOTE: This is not an <USER>sdk issue. This is due to some other potential compatibility issue with HAXM & Yosemite.  h6. I have opened this ticket so that we have it in jira.    h5.Description:  1. We are seeing an issue where HAXM is not working on Yosemite GM candidate 2.  2. Even though HAXM is installed & the processor supports virtualization technologies the x86 emulators for android fails to launch.  3. We get the following error in the android avd manager when we try to launch an x86 emulator:    4. This issue is not seen on Maverics 10.9.5 which is dual booted along with Yosemite GM candidate 2 on the same machine.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HAXM not working with MAC Yosemite GM Candidate 2
Description: """"h6.NOTE: This is not an <USER>sdk issue. This is due to some other potential compatibility issue with HAXM & Yosemite. h6. I have opened this ticket so that we have it in jira. h5.Description: 1. We are seeing an issue where HAXM is not working on Yosemite GM candidate 2. 2. Even though HAXM is installed & the processor supports virtualization technologies the x86 emulators for android fails to launch. 3. We get the following error in the android avd manager when we try to launch an x86 emulator: 4. This issue is not seen on Maverics 10.9.5 which is dual booted along with Yosemite GM candidate 2 on the same machine.""""",title+description
