TIMOB-17857,12,"""Maps v2 module - getRegion() fails on Android - working on iOS""","""""""On Android (tested multiple versions, currently on 4.4.2) using maps module v2 the getRegion() method does not exist and pulling the region variable returns undefined.   http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Modules.Map.View-property-region    This works as expected on iOS.     Q/A Regarding this issue here.  https://developer.<USER>com/question/176937/android-maps-v2-getregion-function-undefined    """"""",Bug,"Title: Maps v2 module - getRegion() fails on Android - working on iOS
Description: """"On Android (tested multiple versions, currently on 4.4.2) using maps module v2 the getRegion() method does not exist and pulling the region variable returns undefined. http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Modules.Map.View-property-region This works as expected on iOS. Q/A Regarding this issue here. https://developer.<USER>com/question/176937/android-maps-v2-getregion-function-undefined """"",title+description
TIMOB-17844,12,"""Dashboard: Windows Hybrid average session length is not shown for device""","""""""h5. Description    The average session length is not shown for Windows Hybrid devices in both pre-prod and production, in pre-prod it is shown that there are six active sessions despite the session being closed as shown in the attached screenshot.     This is only seen if the app is built to a device, if built to emulator then the average session can be seen.    h5.Steps to reproduce    1. Build an app to a Windows Phone device  2. Open and close the app a few times    h5. Actual Results  Average session length is not shown and it is shown as having a number of sessions open    h5. Expected Results  The average sessions length should be shown and there should be no active sessions.    *Notes*  The ti.end is being sent by the device as verified by checking the payload using staging.    It is only the average session length that is not being shown, the installs and sessions are correct.""""""",Bug,"Title: Dashboard: Windows Hybrid average session length is not shown for device
Description: """"h5. Description The average session length is not shown for Windows Hybrid devices in both pre-prod and production, in pre-prod it is shown that there are six active sessions despite the session being closed as shown in the attached screenshot. This is only seen if the app is built to a device, if built to emulator then the average session can be seen. h5.Steps to reproduce 1. Build an app to a Windows Phone device 2. Open and close the app a few times h5. Actual Results Average session length is not shown and it is shown as having a number of sessions open h5. Expected Results The average sessions length should be shown and there should be no active sessions. *Notes* The ti.end is being sent by the device as verified by checking the payload using staging. It is only the average session length that is not being shown, the installs and sessions are correct.""""",title+description
