TIMOB-17826,12,"""iOS: Disabling analytics in tiapp.xml leads to iads crash on device""","""""""If you disable the analytics in tiapp.xml and then try to use iAds it will crash with the following log:      The only place where I see an object with a key """"""""sid"""""""" is the Geolocation module    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/ad9eea392dd7b0820c1b5f65c9147cf1ce4c8662/iphone/Classes/GeolocationModule.m#L525    that asks for a Ti.App.sessionId that seems to be set by the analytics.    Putting back analytics to true in tiapp.xml fixes the issue, however it is not ok.     How to reproduce:  1. Disable analytics in tiapp.xml      2. Add this is alloy.js (or anywhere)      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Disabling analytics in tiapp.xml leads to iads crash on device
Description: """"If you disable the analytics in tiapp.xml and then try to use iAds it will crash with the following log: The only place where I see an object with a key """"""""sid"""""""" is the Geolocation module https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/ad9eea392dd7b0820c1b5f65c9147cf1ce4c8662/iphone/Classes/GeolocationModule.m#L525 that asks for a Ti.App.sessionId that seems to be set by the analytics. Putting back analytics to true in tiapp.xml fixes the issue, however it is not ok. How to reproduce: 1. Disable analytics in tiapp.xml 2. Add this is alloy.js (or anywhere) """"",title+description
TIMOB-17825,12,"""Android: Picker: minDate and maxDate are not respected when setting the value in constructor""","""""""h5.Description    When a value of a picker is set in .createPicker() minDate and maxDate are not respected and it is possible for the value to be passed these two values      *Notes*  On iOS the minDate and maxDate values are respected and if the value is set above or below these then it is defaulted to the either the maxDate or minDate.    If the value is set using setValue() then it defaults to the highest or lowest it can go.    This also occurs in 3.4.0.GA and 3.3.0.GA.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Using the attached app.js build to an Android device or emulator  2. Observe the dates that are set  3. Tap the button and the dates will be set via setValue()    h5.Actual Result    2. The dates will be past the min and max values  3. The dates are changed to the min and max    h5.Expected Result    2. The dates should be the same as the min and max  3. The dates are changed to the min and max""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Picker: minDate and maxDate are not respected when setting the value in constructor
Description: """"h5.Description When a value of a picker is set in .createPicker() minDate and maxDate are not respected and it is possible for the value to be passed these two values *Notes* On iOS the minDate and maxDate values are respected and if the value is set above or below these then it is defaulted to the either the maxDate or minDate. If the value is set using setValue() then it defaults to the highest or lowest it can go. This also occurs in 3.4.0.GA and 3.3.0.GA. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Using the attached app.js build to an Android device or emulator 2. Observe the dates that are set 3. Tap the button and the dates will be set via setValue() h5.Actual Result 2. The dates will be past the min and max values 3. The dates are changed to the min and max h5.Expected Result 2. The dates should be the same as the min and max 3. The dates are changed to the min and max""""",title+description
TIMOB-17823,12,"""Android : App crashes on android 2.3.X with java.lang.NoSuchMethodError when splitActionBar is true""","""""""h5.Description:  1. Replace the app.js with the following code:    2. Build for android 2.3.X device/emulator.    h5.Actual Result:  1. The app crashes with following errors:    2. If the application is built with """"""""splitActionBar: false"""""""" the app builds & runs fine.  3. My targetSdkVersion in tiapp.xml is set to 19 and for actionbar the min targetSdkVersion should be 14 or higher    h5. Expected Result:  1. The app should not crash & we should be able to see the splitActionBar.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : App crashes on android 2.3.X with java.lang.NoSuchMethodError when splitActionBar is true
Description: """"h5.Description: 1. Replace the app.js with the following code: 2. Build for android 2.3.X device/emulator. h5.Actual Result: 1. The app crashes with following errors: 2. If the application is built with """"""""splitActionBar: false"""""""" the app builds & runs fine. 3. My targetSdkVersion in tiapp.xml is set to 19 and for actionbar the min targetSdkVersion should be 14 or higher h5. Expected Result: 1. The app should not crash & we should be able to see the splitActionBar.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17821,12,"""Android: Add Support for Custom View to ActionBar""","""""""Add support for Custom View to ActionBar:    http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/ActionBar.html#setCustomView(int""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add Support for Custom View to ActionBar
Description: """"Add support for Custom View to ActionBar: http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/ActionBar.html#setCustomView(int""""",title+description
TIMOB-17819,12,"""ti.cloud module -> ACS function to delete objects should align with Cloud REST API""","""""""Currently using Cloud REST API, you need to call the """"""""delete"""""""" function on the cloud object.    Ex      However on the `ti.cloud` module for Titanium, the function on the ACS object is titled `remove`.    Ex.       It would cause less confusion, if the `ti.cloud` module function on ACS Objects to delete the object was entitled `delete` to create better parity with the Cloud documentation and REST API.""""""",Improvement,"Title: ti.cloud module -> ACS function to delete objects should align with Cloud REST API
Description: """"Currently using Cloud REST API, you need to call the """"""""delete"""""""" function on the cloud object. Ex However on the `ti.cloud` module for Titanium, the function on the ACS object is titled `remove`. Ex. It would cause less confusion, if the `ti.cloud` module function on ACS Objects to delete the object was entitled `delete` to create better parity with the Cloud documentation and REST API.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17817,12,"""Android: Google libraries should always be up to date in Titanium and modules""","""""""The version of the Google Play Services becomes an issue when there are two modules using them. For example - I'm developing a Chromecast module which must use a recent version of this library, in a project that also uses the ti.map module. The project will not build if there are two different versions of Google Play Services, thus in any case I overwrite the version in ti.map with the newest copy.  This is also true of other libraries, such as the Android support libraries. A project will not build if there are two different versions of the library in modules, Titanium, etc.  Thus, Titanium and its modules should always have the latest version of the relevant libraries - good practice in any case due to bug fixes, etc.  Relevant cases:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6022  https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map/issues/59  In most cases all that is needed is just replacing the file with the new version.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Google libraries should always be up to date in Titanium and modules
Description: """"The version of the Google Play Services becomes an issue when there are two modules using them. For example - I'm developing a Chromecast module which must use a recent version of this library, in a project that also uses the ti.map module. The project will not build if there are two different versions of Google Play Services, thus in any case I overwrite the version in ti.map with the newest copy. This is also true of other libraries, such as the Android support libraries. A project will not build if there are two different versions of the library in modules, Titanium, etc. Thus, Titanium and its modules should always have the latest version of the relevant libraries - good practice in any case due to bug fixes, etc. Relevant cases: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6022 https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map/issues/59 In most cases all that is needed is just replacing the file with the new version.""""",title+description
