Description: """"I came accross this GitHub repo for testing remote notifications on the iOS simulator and thought it might be great to put into Appc https://github.com/acoomans/SimulatorRemoteNotifications Just an idea""""",title+description
TIMOB-17810,12,"""iOS Kitchen Sink:Phone - Contacts - Groups - added contacts are hidden behind the picker""","""""""h5. To reproduce  1. Install and launch KS on iOS device  2. Navigate to Phone> Contacts> Groups  3. Add person (in case no people are in the group)  h5. Actual result  Contacts are partially hidden behind the picker  h5. Expected result  All contacts should be visible """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS Kitchen Sink:Phone - Contacts - Groups - added contacts are hidden behind the picker
Description: """"h5. To reproduce 1. Install and launch KS on iOS device 2. Navigate to Phone> Contacts> Groups 3. Add person (in case no people are in the group) h5. Actual result Contacts are partially hidden behind the picker h5. Expected result All contacts should be visible """"",title+description
TIMOB-17809,12,"""Android Theme is not used by widget when widget opens a new window""","""""""App is using a custom theme that defines the following:    {code:xml}  <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""utf-8""""""""?>  <resources xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"""""""">    <style name=""""""""MyTheme""""""""  parent=""""""""@style/Theme.AppCompat.Light"""""""">        <!-- Hides the title and action bar at the top -->      <item name=""""""""android:windowNoTitle"""""""">true</item>      <item name=""""""""windowActionBar"""""""">false</item>    </style>  </resources>  {code}      Subsequently, we have an in-house alloy widget that acts as a menu bar. It opens a separate window which should also have the title and action bar hidden based on the above theme.    However, this is not the case.    When the window opens, the action bar is present. We tried using:    {code:javascript}  function hideActionbar() {    $.win.activity.actionBar.hide();  }  {code}    after the window opens, however this is not a great user experience. For a split second, the action bar is visible and the UI elements shift after it has hidden.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android Theme is not used by widget when widget opens a new window
Description: """"App is using a custom theme that defines the following: {code:xml} <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""utf-8""""""""?> <resources xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""> <style name=""""""""MyTheme"""""""" parent=""""""""@style/Theme.AppCompat.Light""""""""> <!-- Hides the title and action bar at the top --> <item name=""""""""android:windowNoTitle"""""""">true</item> <item name=""""""""windowActionBar"""""""">false</item> </style> </resources> {code} Subsequently, we have an in-house alloy widget that acts as a menu bar. It opens a separate window which should also have the title and action bar hidden based on the above theme. However, this is not the case. When the window opens, the action bar is present. We tried using: {code:javascript} function hideActionbar() { $.win.activity.actionBar.hide(); } {code} after the window opens, however this is not a great user experience. For a split second, the action bar is visible and the UI elements shift after it has hidden. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17802,12,"""Windows: Get Coverity Scan running on sample repository""","""""""Coverity Scan is a free service allow us to test our C++ code for flaws.    It has a very nice Travis CI integration, however it only works on public projects.    For now, we've created a sample repo:    https://github.com/<USER>coverity_test    To test running it.    """"""",Improvement,"Title: Windows: Get Coverity Scan running on sample repository
