TIMOB-17792,12,"""Android: showTimePickerDialog does appear if you didn't added the picker before.""","""""""h4. Problem Description  showTimePickerDialog doesn't work if you don't add the picker before to the window.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project  2. Add this testcase to app.js:   {code:js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      exitOnClose: true  });     var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({      type: Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_TIME  });    var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({      title : 'Show time picker dialog'  });    win.add( btn );  win.open( );    btn.addEventListener( 'singletap', function( ) {      picker.showTimePickerDialog({          callback: function( e ) {              if ( e.cancel ) {                  Ti.API.info( 'User canceled dialog' );              } else {                  Ti.API.info( 'User selected time: ' + e.value );              }          }      });  });    [WARN]  HardwareRenderer: Attempting to initialize hardware acceleration outside of the main thread, aborting    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      exitOnClose : true,      layout : 'vertical'  });      var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({      type : Titanium.UI.PICKER_TYPE_TIME,      top : 10,      left:-1000,  });      win.add(picker);     var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({      title : 'Show time picker dialog',      top : 10  });      win.add(btn);  //win.add(picker);  win.open();      btn.addEventListener('singletap', function() {      picker.showTimePickerDialog({          callback : function(e) {              if (e.cancel) {                  Ti.API.info('User canceled dialog');              } else {                  Ti.API.info('User selected time: ' + e.value);              }          }      });      });  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: showTimePickerDialog does appear if you didn't added the picker before.
Description: """"h4. Problem Description showTimePickerDialog doesn't work if you don't add the picker before to the window. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project 2. Add this testcase to app.js: {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ exitOnClose: true }); var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({ type: Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_TIME }); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Show time picker dialog' }); win.add( btn ); win.open( ); btn.addEventListener( 'singletap', function( ) { picker.showTimePickerDialog({ callback: function( e ) { if ( e.cancel ) { Ti.API.info( 'User canceled dialog' ); } else { Ti.API.info( 'User selected time: ' + e.value ); } } }); }); [WARN] HardwareRenderer: Attempting to initialize hardware acceleration outside of the main thread, aborting var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ exitOnClose : true, layout : 'vertical' }); var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({ type : Titanium.UI.PICKER_TYPE_TIME, top : 10, left:-1000, }); win.add(picker); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Show time picker dialog', top : 10 }); win.add(btn); //win.add(picker); win.open(); btn.addEventListener('singletap', function() { picker.showTimePickerDialog({ callback : function(e) { if (e.cancel) { Ti.API.info('User canceled dialog'); } else { Ti.API.info('User selected time: ' + e.value); } } }); }); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-17791,12,"""Android: Add support for offscreenPageLimit to Ti.UI.ScrollableView""","""""""There is no option to set offscreenPageLimit size in the underlying ViewPager object.  This can cause slow navigation when there are more than 3 views in a scrollable view.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add support for offscreenPageLimit to Ti.UI.ScrollableView
Description: """"There is no option to set offscreenPageLimit size in the underlying ViewPager object. This can cause slow navigation when there are more than 3 views in a scrollable view.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17789,12,"""CLI: iOS: Add config option to specify default iOS simulator""","""""""The CLI gives us the option to turn off device auto-selection, after which you're prompted with a list of simulators on which to run your app. I'd like to be able to specify a default sim to be used when autoSelectDevice is set to true. (Currently, the first detected simulator type is used.) This would help when repeatedly testing an app on a specific target sim type.    Something like:    {{ti config ios.defaultSimulator <UUID>}}""""""",Improvement,"Title: CLI: iOS: Add config option to specify default iOS simulator
Description: """"The CLI gives us the option to turn off device auto-selection, after which you're prompted with a list of simulators on which to run your app. I'd like to be able to specify a default sim to be used when autoSelectDevice is set to true. (Currently, the first detected simulator type is used.) This would help when repeatedly testing an app on a specific target sim type. Something like: {{ti config ios.defaultSimulator <UUID>}}""""",title+description
TIMOB-17785,12,"""Having ONLY i18n launch images doesn't work""","""""""If you *only* have launch images in i18n folder, including those of the default ({{CFBundleDevelopmentRegion}} or {{en}}) language ones, then your app won't show any launch image at all when the phone/simulator is running that default or an unsupported language.    h1. Test case    1. Create a default app  2. Move launch images from {{Resources/iphone}} to {{i18n/en}}  3. Build the app  4. Run the app to see there is no launch image showing    h1. Cause    This bug was introduced by automatically generating {{UILaunchImages}} keys in {{Info.plist}} for TIMOB-17663. It only checks {{Resources}}, {{Resources/iphone}} and {{Resources/ios}} and not the {{i18n}} folder for the default language.    h1. Solution    The script should be updated to also search in all or at least the default ({{CFBundleDevelopmentRegion}}) locale.    - PR on master: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6162  - PR on 3_4_x: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6163""""""",Bug,"Title: Having ONLY i18n launch images doesn't work
Description: """"If you *only* have launch images in i18n folder, including those of the default ({{CFBundleDevelopmentRegion}} or {{en}}) language ones, then your app won't show any launch image at all when the phone/simulator is running that default or an unsupported language. h1. Test case 1. Create a default app 2. Move launch images from {{Resources/iphone}} to {{i18n/en}} 3. Build the app 4. Run the app to see there is no launch image showing h1. Cause This bug was introduced by automatically generating {{UILaunchImages}} keys in {{Info.plist}} for TIMOB-17663. It only checks {{Resources}}, {{Resources/iphone}} and {{Resources/ios}} and not the {{i18n}} folder for the default language. h1. Solution The script should be updated to also search in all or at least the default ({{CFBundleDevelopmentRegion}}) locale. - PR on master: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6162 - PR on 3_4_x: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/6163""""",title+description
