TIMOB-17759,12,"""iOS8: KitchenSink control TextField does not show the soft keyboard when the focus is set. ""","""""""Description:    While testing KS controls, I found that the soft keyboard didn't appear with the TextField when the focus is set with the Portrait orientation. Rotating the device to Landscape orientation will show just a small part of the soft keyboard.The keys are not working when pressed.    STEPS TO REPRODUCE:-  1. Install the KitchenSink on iPhone 6/6+ simulator.  2. Navigate to: Controls => text field => Events    3.  Click on a text field or/and """"""""Focus"""""""" button     EXPECTED RESULT:  3. Text field should be active and Soft keyboard should appear in portrait orientation.    ACTUAL RESULT:  3. Text Field become active but the soft keyboard didn't appear in Portrait orientation.     Then Rotate the Simulator. The small part of hidden soft keyboard can be seen and the keys are disabled.  Please find the attached screen shots for details.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: KitchenSink control TextField does not show the soft keyboard when the focus is set.
Description: """"Description: While testing KS controls, I found that the soft keyboard didn't appear with the TextField when the focus is set with the Portrait orientation. Rotating the device to Landscape orientation will show just a small part of the soft keyboard.The keys are not working when pressed. STEPS TO REPRODUCE:- 1. Install the KitchenSink on iPhone 6/6+ simulator. 2. Navigate to: Controls => text field => Events 3. Click on a text field or/and """"""""Focus"""""""" button EXPECTED RESULT: 3. Text field should be active and Soft keyboard should appear in portrait orientation. ACTUAL RESULT: 3. Text Field become active but the soft keyboard didn't appear in Portrait orientation. Then Rotate the Simulator. The small part of hidden soft keyboard can be seen and the keys are disabled. Please find the attached screen shots for details. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17757,12,"""KitchenSink: Platform - Intermittent XHR large file download fails with timed out error""","""""""h5. To reproduce  1. Install KS 3.3.1 on iOS device  2. Navigate to KS> Platform> XHR> File download  3. Press """"""""Large File Download""""""""  h5. Actual result  The progress bar is showing the <USER> it can be aborted, however continuing  downloading the file  results in the Error: The request timed out.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Platform - Intermittent XHR large file download fails with timed out error
Description: """"h5. To reproduce 1. Install KS 3.3.1 on iOS device 2. Navigate to KS> Platform> XHR> File download 3. Press """"""""Large File Download"""""""" h5. Actual result The progress bar is showing the <USER> it can be aborted, however continuing downloading the file results in the Error: The request timed out.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17756,12,"""iOS8: Tapping """"open in"""" function in Safari leads to uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException'""","""""""h6.Issue description   The """"""""Open In"""""""" function does not work when building an app with <USER>and running on iOS8.     h6.Steps to reproduce  # Install sample app to iOS simulator  # Go to Safari and put this URL: http://www.act.org/compass/sample/pdf/reading.pdf  # The app Opens, Splash Screen appears and quickly crashes.  # Built app on 3.3.0.GA/iOS7 and same sequence launches the app as we expect.     h6.Crash logs      h6.Details  This appears to be regression since works on 3.3.0.GA/iOS7 but crashes only on 3.4.0.v20140903121714 though there is no crash on 3.4.0.v20140918202513.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: Tapping """"open in"""" function in Safari leads to uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException'
Description: """"h6.Issue description The """"""""Open In"""""""" function does not work when building an app with <USER>and running on iOS8. h6.Steps to reproduce # Install sample app to iOS simulator # Go to Safari and put this URL: http://www.act.org/compass/sample/pdf/reading.pdf # The app Opens, Splash Screen appears and quickly crashes. # Built app on 3.3.0.GA/iOS7 and same sequence launches the app as we expect. h6.Crash logs h6.Details This appears to be regression since works on 3.3.0.GA/iOS7 but crashes only on 3.4.0.v20140903121714 though there is no crash on 3.4.0.v20140918202513. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17755,12,"""KitchenSink: Intermittent failure Uploading Photo from Gallery with Graph API""","""""""h5. To reproduce  1. Install KS  2. Navigate to Mashups> Photos> Upload Photo Gallery with Graph API  3. Choose the photo  h5. Actual result  It takes forever to complete the <USER> ending with the failure Alert.  h5. Expected result  Alert Success, the photo should be uploaded and visible in Facebook""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Intermittent failure Uploading Photo from Gallery with Graph API
Description: """"h5. To reproduce 1. Install KS 2. Navigate to Mashups> Photos> Upload Photo Gallery with Graph API 3. Choose the photo h5. Actual result It takes forever to complete the <USER> ending with the failure Alert. h5. Expected result Alert Success, the photo should be uploaded and visible in Facebook""""",title+description
TIMOB-17752,12,"""iOS8: PDF inside WebView has black border""","""""""h4. Problem Description  PDF inside webview has a black border.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project (classic titanium)   2. Copy the PDF file attached here to Resources.  3. Paste this code into app.ks:    4. Run it in a device.    h4. Expected Results  The PDF showing just fine.     h4. Actual Results  I get a black border around the webview. Not visible under iOS7 with the same code    h4. Extra info  http://stackoverflow.com/questions/25813551/rendering-pdf-in-uiwebview-ios-8-causes-a-black-border-around-pdf  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: PDF inside WebView has black border
Description: """"h4. Problem Description PDF inside webview has a black border. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project (classic titanium) 2. Copy the PDF file attached here to Resources. 3. Paste this code into app.ks: 4. Run it in a device. h4. Expected Results The PDF showing just fine. h4. Actual Results I get a black border around the webview. Not visible under iOS7 with the same code h4. Extra info http://stackoverflow.com/questions/25813551/rendering-pdf-in-uiwebview-ios-8-causes-a-black-border-around-pdf """"",title+description
TIMOB-17751,12,"""iOS8: unable to set object property inside object""","""""""h4. Problem Description  If I have an object (status:{}) inside an object (Ti.UI.View), and I want to edit/add a new property to 'status', in android works perfectly, but on iOS it doesn't change the property, defined on 'Ti.UI.View' creation.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project (Classic Titanium)  2. Paste this sample into app.js:    3. Run it in device.   4. Click on the White box. It should turn red. Click in the red box. It should turn white. Repeat.     h4. Expected Results  When you click in the box, it should go from white to red and viceversa.     h4. Actual Results  It's working fine in Android, failing in iOS. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: unable to set object property inside object
Description: """"h4. Problem Description If I have an object (status:{}) inside an object (Ti.UI.View), and I want to edit/add a new property to 'status', in android works perfectly, but on iOS it doesn't change the property, defined on 'Ti.UI.View' creation. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project (Classic Titanium) 2. Paste this sample into app.js: 3. Run it in device. 4. Click on the White box. It should turn red. Click in the red box. It should turn white. Repeat. h4. Expected Results When you click in the box, it should go from white to red and viceversa. h4. Actual Results It's working fine in Android, failing in iOS. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17750,12,"""Expose contentOffset property on TableView on iOS""","""""""TableView does not expose the contentOffset property.    On iOS UITableView is a subclass of UIScrollView which contains the contentOffset property. In Titanium we expose contentOffset for ScrollView but not for TableView. While we provide a scrollToIndex() method, there is no way to manually scroll the TableView, for example to show or hide the header.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Expose contentOffset property on TableView on iOS
Description: """"TableView does not expose the contentOffset property. On iOS UITableView is a subclass of UIScrollView which contains the contentOffset property. In Titanium we expose contentOffset for ScrollView but not for TableView. While we provide a scrollToIndex() method, there is no way to manually scroll the TableView, for example to show or hide the header.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17748,12,"""iOS8: Camera overlay rotates on app locked in portrait orientation mode""","""""""h4. Problem Description  Camera overlay on iPad rotates in an app that is locked in portrait mode.   Expected: Camera overlay should stay in portrait mode      h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project (classic titanium)  2. Paste this to app.js  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor : '#fff',   layout : 'vertical'  });    var frmcamera = Ti.UI.createButton({   backgroundColor : '#ff0000',   title : 'Open Camera',   color : '#fff',   width : Ti.UI.SIZE,   height : Ti.UI.SIZE,   top : 30    });    frmcamera.addEventListener('click', function() {   fireUpTheCamera();  });    win.add(frmcamera);      var overlay = Ti.UI.createView({   width : 50,   height : 50,  });  // Create an ImageView.  var overlayImg = Ti.UI.createImageView({   image : '/KS_nav_ui.png',   width : Ti.UI.SIZE,   height : Ti.UI.SIZE,   autorotate : true,  });    overlayImg.addEventListener('click', function() {   Ti.Media.takePicture();  });  overlay.add(overlayImg);       function fireUpTheCamera() {   Titanium.Media.showCamera({      success : function(event) {      },    cancel : function() {    },    error : function(error) {      },    saveToPhotoGallery : true,    allowEditing : false,    overlay : overlay,    mediaTypes : [Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO]   });  }    win.open();      4. Test in a device""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: Camera overlay rotates on app locked in portrait orientation mode
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Camera overlay on iPad rotates in an app that is locked in portrait mode. Expected: Camera overlay should stay in portrait mode h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project (classic titanium) 2. Paste this to app.js {code:title=app.js} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : '#fff', layout : 'vertical' }); var frmcamera = Ti.UI.createButton({ backgroundColor : '#ff0000', title : 'Open Camera', color : '#fff', width : Ti.UI.SIZE, height : Ti.UI.SIZE, top : 30 }); frmcamera.addEventListener('click', function() { fireUpTheCamera(); }); win.add(frmcamera); var overlay = Ti.UI.createView({ width : 50, height : 50, }); // Create an ImageView. var overlayImg = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image : '/KS_nav_ui.png', width : Ti.UI.SIZE, height : Ti.UI.SIZE, autorotate : true, }); overlayImg.addEventListener('click', function() { Ti.Media.takePicture(); }); overlay.add(overlayImg); function fireUpTheCamera() { Titanium.Media.showCamera({ success : function(event) { }, cancel : function() { }, error : function(error) { }, saveToPhotoGallery : true, allowEditing : false, overlay : overlay, mediaTypes : [Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO] }); } win.open(); 4. Test in a device""""",title+description
