TIMOB-17745,12,"""iOS8: Unable to scroll on an alert""","""""""h5.Description    When the text within an alert is too long to display on an iOS7 device the user is able to scroll to see the whole text. However on an iOS8 device the user is unable to scroll and the text is cutoff.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Add the code from the attached app.js and build to an iOS8 device.    h5.Actual Result    The alert can't be scrolled    h5.Expected Result    The alert should be able to be scrolled.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: Unable to scroll on an alert
Description: """"h5.Description When the text within an alert is too long to display on an iOS7 device the user is able to scroll to see the whole text. However on an iOS8 device the user is unable to scroll and the text is cutoff. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Add the code from the attached app.js and build to an iOS8 device. h5.Actual Result The alert can't be scrolled h5.Expected Result The alert should be able to be scrolled.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17742,12,"""iOS: Create a better way to request Geo Permissions""","""""""Geo Permissions support has been added in TIMOB-17638 . But other modules that interact with geo such as map or ibeacons need to be able to request geo permissions as well. Instead of copy/pasting code for each of these, it would be better to have a central place to request/permissions based on the keys added to the info.plist. Also need a delegate that gets called when the permissions requested are approved or rejected like       We need to create an implementation that can be used by modules. We may also want to consider exposing something to javascript to allow developers to request this permissions, but I am not sure if this is necessary.    The conversation that resulted in this ticket and more info can be found here: TIMOB-17638""""""",Story,"Title: iOS: Create a better way to request Geo Permissions
Description: """"Geo Permissions support has been added in TIMOB-17638 . But other modules that interact with geo such as map or ibeacons need to be able to request geo permissions as well. Instead of copy/pasting code for each of these, it would be better to have a central place to request/permissions based on the keys added to the info.plist. Also need a delegate that gets called when the permissions requested are approved or rejected like We need to create an implementation that can be used by modules. We may also want to consider exposing something to javascript to allow developers to request this permissions, but I am not sure if this is necessary. The conversation that resulted in this ticket and more info can be found here: TIMOB-17638""""",title+description
TIMOB-17741,12,"""Android: overlay property in showCamera causes error when LiveView is enabled""","""""""When overlay property of show camera is used, it creates a run time error when live view is enabled. Without liveview, the app works as expected.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Import the attached app.js into a new classic project  2. Run the app on an android device  3. Press on 'Camera' on the centre of the app  3. Enable the liveview feature in the studio and run the app again on device  4. Press on 'Camera' on the centre of the app    Actual Results:  2. App runs successfully and you should see 'Camera' on the centre of the app  3. Camera opens up  4. Runtime error is shown on the device with the following message:  """"""""Uncaught Error: unable to find explicit activity class {ti.modules.titanium.media.TiCameraActivity}; have you declared this activity in your AndroidManifest.xml?""""""""    Expected Results:  4. Camera should open up without any errors    However, this works fine with iOS.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: overlay property in showCamera causes error when LiveView is enabled
Description: """"When overlay property of show camera is used, it creates a run time error when live view is enabled. Without liveview, the app works as expected. Steps to reproduce: 1. Import the attached app.js into a new classic project 2. Run the app on an android device 3. Press on 'Camera' on the centre of the app 3. Enable the liveview feature in the studio and run the app again on device 4. Press on 'Camera' on the centre of the app Actual Results: 2. App runs successfully and you should see 'Camera' on the centre of the app 3. Camera opens up 4. Runtime error is shown on the device with the following message: """"""""Uncaught Error: unable to find explicit activity class {ti.modules.titanium.media.TiCameraActivity}; have you declared this activity in your AndroidManifest.xml?"""""""" Expected Results: 4. Camera should open up without any errors However, this works fine with iOS.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17739,12,"""BlackBerry: Unable to build app in BlackBerry 10""","""""""Unable to build app in BlackBerry 10  h6.Reproduce: 1.Download BlackBerry SDK from Ti Studio. 2.Create a simple app, like a tabWindow Template. 3.Run it in BlackBerry simulator.  Error happen, Here is the console log:    N.B. There are two similar files in BlackBerry NDK: libQtXml.4.8.5.dylib and libQtXml.4.dylib. and libQtXml.4.dylib is 0 size. Also same as other libQt file.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Unable to build app in BlackBerry 10
Description: """"Unable to build app in BlackBerry 10 h6.Reproduce: 1.Download BlackBerry SDK from Ti Studio. 2.Create a simple app, like a tabWindow Template. 3.Run it in BlackBerry simulator. Error happen, Here is the console log: N.B. There are two similar files in BlackBerry NDK: libQtXml.4.8.5.dylib and libQtXml.4.dylib. and libQtXml.4.dylib is 0 size. Also same as other libQt file.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17737,12,"""iOS: Xcode - Packaged application's version has 3 digits vs 2 in the app, registered in iTunes connect""","""""""h5. Description  When we package the app for iTunes Store, the version of the archived app has 3 digits (1.0.0). However, the version of the app and the bundle version have 2.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Xcode - Packaged application's version has 3 digits vs 2 in the app, registered in iTunes connect
Description: """"h5. Description When we package the app for iTunes Store, the version of the archived app has 3 digits (1.0.0). However, the version of the app and the bundle version have 2.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17735,12,"""iOS8: Launching Image Capture when device is flat on the desk and in Landscape mode results in the UI being rotated and black bars present""","""""""h6.Issue description  If you leave the iPad flat on the desk and click launch camera, it shows rotated sideways with the black bars present.     h6.Issue description  I have already consumed the change from https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17662 by setting autorotate to false in CameraDevice.js and this issue is still present.     h6.Steps to Reproduce   # Build sample app  # Pick up the device and rotate it to landscape orientation (Home button on Right) <- This is key, it seems in portrait this issue does not occur   # Lay the device flat on the desk   # Launch the app, then launch image capture by clicking the image capture button.   # Notice that the image shown is sideways and there are black bars present. If this does not occur close the image capture and repeat steps 3-4 leaving the device flat on the desk.   # Close the camera viewfinder   # Pick the ipad up off your desk   # Click the image capture button.   # Notice that the viewfinder appears correctly. It should appear like this when its flat on the desk.   """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: Launching Image Capture when device is flat on the desk and in Landscape mode results in the UI being rotated and black bars present
Description: """"h6.Issue description If you leave the iPad flat on the desk and click launch camera, it shows rotated sideways with the black bars present. h6.Issue description I have already consumed the change from https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17662 by setting autorotate to false in CameraDevice.js and this issue is still present. h6.Steps to Reproduce # Build sample app # Pick up the device and rotate it to landscape orientation (Home button on Right) <- This is key, it seems in portrait this issue does not occur # Lay the device flat on the desk # Launch the app, then launch image capture by clicking the image capture button. # Notice that the image shown is sideways and there are black bars present. If this does not occur close the image capture and repeat steps 3-4 leaving the device flat on the desk. # Close the camera viewfinder # Pick the ipad up off your desk # Click the image capture button. # Notice that the viewfinder appears correctly. It should appear like this when its flat on the desk. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17732,12,"""iOS: Push - If you send an iOS push with a badge > 0, then another push with badge = 0, the alert dialog will appear momentarily ""","""""""*Details:* If you send an iOS push with a badge > 0, then another push with badge = 0, the alert dialog will appear momentarily.    *Note:*  - This behavior appears on iOS 7 devices.  - This behavior appears on 3.3.0.GA SDK.  - Potentially, an Apple bug.    *Steps to reproduce:*  0. Make sure you are setup for iOS push on dashboard  1. Create a Titanium app with the ti.cloud sample app  2. Install app to device  3. Create a user  4. Go to Push Notifications > Settings for This Device; enable for push  5. Next, go to Push Notifications > Subscribe Token; subscribe to a channel  6. Background your app and make sure the Alerts notification is selected in the phone's setting for the app  7. On dashboard, find your app and go to Cloud > Push Notifications > Send Push Notification  8. Specify an alert and a badge greater than 0; click on Save Changes  9. Alert dialog should appear on device; dismiss the alert dialog  10. Specify an alert and a badge equal to 0; click on Save Changes    *Actual:* Alert dialog will appear momentarily.  *Expected:* Alert dialog should not disappear.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Push - If you send an iOS push with a badge > 0, then another push with badge = 0, the alert dialog will appear momentarily
Description: """"*Details:* If you send an iOS push with a badge > 0, then another push with badge = 0, the alert dialog will appear momentarily. *Note:* - This behavior appears on iOS 7 devices. - This behavior appears on 3.3.0.GA SDK. - Potentially, an Apple bug. *Steps to reproduce:* 0. Make sure you are setup for iOS push on dashboard 1. Create a Titanium app with the ti.cloud sample app 2. Install app to device 3. Create a user 4. Go to Push Notifications > Settings for This Device; enable for push 5. Next, go to Push Notifications > Subscribe Token; subscribe to a channel 6. Background your app and make sure the Alerts notification is selected in the phone's setting for the app 7. On dashboard, find your app and go to Cloud > Push Notifications > Send Push Notification 8. Specify an alert and a badge greater than 0; click on Save Changes 9. Alert dialog should appear on device; dismiss the alert dialog 10. Specify an alert and a badge equal to 0; click on Save Changes *Actual:* Alert dialog will appear momentarily. *Expected:* Alert dialog should not disappear.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17730,12,"""Android: Changed hint text on textfield not shown in landscape mode""","""""""The changed hint text on a textfield does not show when the device is in landscape orientation. This happens when soft keyboard is shown and on android devices that show only the text field for edit in landscape mode.     This is not a regression as the issue also occurs in 3.3.0.GA    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create a project and replace its app.js with the code below  2. Run the app on a device  3. When the app launches the textfield shows a hint text as """"""""123"""""""".  4. Click on """"""""click me!"""""""" button. The hint text of the textfield changes to """"""""456""""""""  5. Click on the textfield to invoke the soft keyboard  6. Now rotate the device to landscape mode    Actual Result:  The textfield shows the hint text as """"""""123"""""""" instead of """"""""456""""""""    Expected Result:  The changed hint text should show even after orientation change    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Changed hint text on textfield not shown in landscape mode
Description: """"The changed hint text on a textfield does not show when the device is in landscape orientation. This happens when soft keyboard is shown and on android devices that show only the text field for edit in landscape mode. This is not a regression as the issue also occurs in 3.3.0.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a project and replace its app.js with the code below 2. Run the app on a device 3. When the app launches the textfield shows a hint text as """"""""123"""""""". 4. Click on """"""""click me!"""""""" button. The hint text of the textfield changes to """"""""456"""""""" 5. Click on the textfield to invoke the soft keyboard 6. Now rotate the device to landscape mode Actual Result: The textfield shows the hint text as """"""""123"""""""" instead of """"""""456"""""""" Expected Result: The changed hint text should show even after orientation change """"",title+description
TIMOB-17728,12,"""Implement the optional ACRA library""","""""""As far as I know, there's currently no method to catch and handle application crashes on Android.  For the app I'm currently developing I would like to implement the open source library ACRA ( http://acra.ch/ ) which enables exactly this feature.  The library catches crashes and is able to send the catched data via email, post it to web forms, show a toast message to the user, etc.    I thought about creating a native module, but sadly this isn't possible, because ACRA needs to be added in the Application.java file, which gets generated by Titanium.    It would be great, if this feature could be enabled and configured inside the tiapp.xml.  The implementation is very easy.    If there is any other way of implementing it without editing core files, please let me know!  I don't want to break the possibility of updating, by manually changing the generation <USER>""""""",New Feature,"Title: Implement the optional ACRA library
Description: """"As far as I know, there's currently no method to catch and handle application crashes on Android. For the app I'm currently developing I would like to implement the open source library ACRA ( http://acra.ch/ ) which enables exactly this feature. The library catches crashes and is able to send the catched data via email, post it to web forms, show a toast message to the user, etc. I thought about creating a native module, but sadly this isn't possible, because ACRA needs to be added in the Application.java file, which gets generated by Titanium. It would be great, if this feature could be enabled and configured inside the tiapp.xml. The implementation is very easy. If there is any other way of implementing it without editing core files, please let me know! I don't want to break the possibility of updating, by manually changing the generation <USER>""""",title+description
TIMOB-17725,12,"""iOS: add TouchID module to titanium sdk""",,New Feature,Title: iOS: add TouchID module to titanium sdk,title-only
TIMOB-17724,12,"""Android: Only last row with same classname is shown when tableview has height set to TI.UI.SIZE""","""""""When a tableview has few rows with same classname then only the last row amongst them is shown. Also this happens when the height of the tableview is set to TI.UI.SIZE.    This is a Regression as the issue does not occur in SDK 3.3.0.GA    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run the app with code below on an Android device    Actual Result:  Only two rows out of four are shown. Both the rows are the last row within the the set of rows that have same classname. (refer to attached screenshots for difference in 3.3.0 and 3.4.0 SDK)  If the height of tableview is not TI.UI.SIZE, then the issue will not occur.    Expected Result:  All the rows in the tableview should be shown    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Only last row with same classname is shown when tableview has height set to TI.UI.SIZE
Description: """"When a tableview has few rows with same classname then only the last row amongst them is shown. Also this happens when the height of the tableview is set to TI.UI.SIZE. This is a Regression as the issue does not occur in SDK 3.3.0.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the app with code below on an Android device Actual Result: Only two rows out of four are shown. Both the rows are the last row within the the set of rows that have same classname. (refer to attached screenshots for difference in 3.3.0 and 3.4.0 SDK) If the height of tableview is not TI.UI.SIZE, then the issue will not occur. Expected Result: All the rows in the tableview should be shown """"",title+description
TIMOB-17722,12,"""Android : The change event for textfield fires on orientation change""","""""""The textfield change event gets fired when the soft keyboard is up and the device orientation is changed.    This is not a regression as the issue also occurs in SDK 3.3.0.GA  The issue occurs only on Android and not on iOS    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run an application with code below on Android device  2. Click on the textfield to invoke the soft keyboard  3. Rotate the device to another orientation    Actual Result:  The change event for the textfield is fired and the console shows """"""""[info] Change Event Fired: TestChantgeEvent""""""""     Expected Result:  The change event should fire only when there is change in text value in textfield and not on orientation change.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android : The change event for textfield fires on orientation change
Description: """"The textfield change event gets fired when the soft keyboard is up and the device orientation is changed. This is not a regression as the issue also occurs in SDK 3.3.0.GA The issue occurs only on Android and not on iOS Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run an application with code below on Android device 2. Click on the textfield to invoke the soft keyboard 3. Rotate the device to another orientation Actual Result: The change event for the textfield is fired and the console shows """"""""[info] Change Event Fired: TestChantgeEvent"""""""" Expected Result: The change event should fire only when there is change in text value in textfield and not on orientation change. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17721,12,"""Tizen: Tizen app freezes on splashscreen""","""""""Tizen app hangs on splash screen, both on device and Emulator.  Everything compiles, but then does not continue on to app.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen: Tizen app freezes on splashscreen
Description: """"Tizen app hangs on splash screen, both on device and Emulator. Everything compiles, but then does not continue on to app.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17720,12,"""iOS8: Popover does not position correctly when the orientation is changed""","""""""h5.Description    When a popover is displayed on screen and then the screen orientation is changed, the popover is positioned on the screen incorrectly.     The issue does not appear on an iOS7 iPad, the popover is aligned correctly when orientation is changed.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    1. Using the attached app.js build to an iOS8 iPad.   2. Tap show gallery and when the popover appears rotate the device.    h5.Actual Result    The popover is not centered when rotated.    h5.Expected Result    The popover should be centered when rotated.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: Popover does not position correctly when the orientation is changed
Description: """"h5.Description When a popover is displayed on screen and then the screen orientation is changed, the popover is positioned on the screen incorrectly. The issue does not appear on an iOS7 iPad, the popover is aligned correctly when orientation is changed. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Using the attached app.js build to an iOS8 iPad. 2. Tap show gallery and when the popover appears rotate the device. h5.Actual Result The popover is not centered when rotated. h5.Expected Result The popover should be centered when rotated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17714,12,"""iOS8: registerForPushNotifications events do not fire, no token returned""","""""""Running latest RC of 3.4 + 3.4.0.v20140916181713 SDK and XCode6    Building with iOS8SDK with the following code:-        works and onSuccess is fired, a token is received - but the error :-    """"""""Passing `types` to registerForPushNotifications is not supported on iOS 8 and greater. Use registerUserNotificationSettings to register notification types.""""""""    is reported in the logs    If I use the recommended approach in the docs:-        onSuccess is not called, no token received, push is not registered.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: registerForPushNotifications events do not fire, no token returned
Description: """"Running latest RC of 3.4 + 3.4.0.v20140916181713 SDK and XCode6 Building with iOS8SDK with the following code:- works and onSuccess is fired, a token is received - but the error :- """"""""Passing `types` to registerForPushNotifications is not supported on iOS 8 and greater. Use registerUserNotificationSettings to register notification types."""""""" is reported in the logs If I use the recommended approach in the docs:- onSuccess is not called, no token received, push is not registered. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17709,12,"""iOS: TableViewSection headerTitle font size difference between iOS 7.1 and 8""","""""""The following app.js shows a different font size for a tableview sections headerTitle:    {code:js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   title: 'Tableview header test'  });    var tableview = Ti.UI.createTableView({   top: 43  });  var headerRow = Ti.UI.createTableViewSection({   headerTitle: 'HEADERTEXT HEADERTEXT HEADERTEXT'  });  tableview.data = [headerRow];  win.add(tableview);  win.open();  {code}    Of course both should show the same given the same device (in the example screenshots iPhone 5S Simulator)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableViewSection headerTitle font size difference between iOS 7.1 and 8
Description: """"The following app.js shows a different font size for a tableview sections headerTitle: {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Tableview header test' }); var tableview = Ti.UI.createTableView({ top: 43 }); var headerRow = Ti.UI.createTableViewSection({ headerTitle: 'HEADERTEXT HEADERTEXT HEADERTEXT' }); tableview.data = [headerRow]; win.add(tableview); win.open(); {code} Of course both should show the same given the same device (in the example screenshots iPhone 5S Simulator)""""",title+description
TIMOB-17704,12,"""iOS: XHR onreadystatechange called multiple times""","""""""When using a XHR createHTTPClient the onreadystatechange is called multiple times. This mostly seems to happen on readystate 4. If your app uses a lot of XHR threads this will cause the app to hang and crash.     Log from test app:    {quote}  [DEBUG] Application booted in 62.319040 ms  [INFO] readystate: 1  [INFO] readystate: 4  [INFO] size 104874307  [INFO] readystate: 4  [INFO] size 104874307  {quote}    Test app:    {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({title: 'Demo', tabBarHidden: true, backgroundColor: '#fff'});    var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({     title: 'Start',     top: 10,     width: 100,     height: 50  });    win.add(button);    function getSize() {          var self = this,       xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient({       timeout: this.timeout,          onreadystatechange: function (e) {         Titanium.API.info(""""""""readystate: """""""" + this.readyState);            if (this.readyState === this.DONE) {                Titanium.API.info('size ' + parseInt(this.getResponseHeader('Content-Length')));              }        },          onerror: function (e) {                    }    });    xhr.open('HEAD', 'http://speedtest.dal05.softlayer.com/downloads/test100.zip');    xhr.send();  }    button.addEventListener('click',function(e)  {     getSize();  });    win.open();  {code}  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: XHR onreadystatechange called multiple times
Description: """"When using a XHR createHTTPClient the onreadystatechange is called multiple times. This mostly seems to happen on readystate 4. If your app uses a lot of XHR threads this will cause the app to hang and crash. Log from test app: {quote} [DEBUG] Application booted in 62.319040 ms [INFO] readystate: 1 [INFO] readystate: 4 [INFO] size 104874307 [INFO] readystate: 4 [INFO] size 104874307 {quote} Test app: {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({title: 'Demo', tabBarHidden: true, backgroundColor: '#fff'}); var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({ title: 'Start', top: 10, width: 100, height: 50 }); win.add(button); function getSize() { var self = this, xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient({ timeout: this.timeout, onreadystatechange: function (e) { Titanium.API.info(""""""""readystate: """""""" + this.readyState); if (this.readyState === this.DONE) { Titanium.API.info('size ' + parseInt(this.getResponseHeader('Content-Length'))); } }, onerror: function (e) { } }); xhr.open('HEAD', 'http://speedtest.dal05.softlayer.com/downloads/test100.zip'); xhr.send(); } button.addEventListener('click',function(e) { getSize(); }); win.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-17701,12,"""Code Analyzer: Shows """"Object #<UnknownType> has no method get"""" error when run for iPhone.""","""""""Description:  Running Code Analyzer for iPhone on small Alloy Application with 'Process Unvisited code' set shows """"""""Object #<UndefinedType> has no method 'get' """""""" an error message.   Code processor is showing error with 'Process Unvisited code' set and only with the iPhone as a target. With 'iPad' as a target, its works successfully.    This is not an regression.  The error is reproducible with <USER>Studio 3.3.0.201407111535 and titanium SDK 3.3.0.GA.     Settings:  Enabled the code Analyzer preferences setting for """"""""Process Unvisited Code""""""""  Platform: iPhone    Steps to Reproduce:-  1. Create an alloy project.  2. Project context menu>code Analysis>Run on iPhone platform.  3. Observe that it is showing error message.     Expected Result:   1. Code processor should run normally and the analyzed result should be generated for the iPhone target.    Actual Result:  2. Code processor shows """"""""Object #<UndefinedType> has no method 'get' """""""" an error message instead of generating the report.  Refer to the attached screenshot for your reference.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Code Analyzer: Shows """"Object #<UnknownType> has no method get"""" error when run for iPhone.
Description: """"Description: Running Code Analyzer for iPhone on small Alloy Application with 'Process Unvisited code' set shows """"""""Object #<UndefinedType> has no method 'get' """""""" an error message. Code processor is showing error with 'Process Unvisited code' set and only with the iPhone as a target. With 'iPad' as a target, its works successfully. This is not an regression. The error is reproducible with <USER>Studio 3.3.0.201407111535 and titanium SDK 3.3.0.GA. Settings: Enabled the code Analyzer preferences setting for """"""""Process Unvisited Code"""""""" Platform: iPhone Steps to Reproduce:- 1. Create an alloy project. 2. Project context menu>code Analysis>Run on iPhone platform. 3. Observe that it is showing error message. Expected Result: 1. Code processor should run normally and the analyzed result should be generated for the iPhone target. Actual Result: 2. Code processor shows """"""""Object #<UndefinedType> has no method 'get' """""""" an error message instead of generating the report. Refer to the attached screenshot for your reference. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17698,12,"""iOS8: iPad Image Capture Black Bars if rotated immediately when clicking launch Image capture""","""""""h6.Isue description  If the user rotates the device immediately when launching image capture then there are black bars present and the video is rotated.     h6.Steps to reproduce  # Launch sample and put the app in landscape orientation.   # Click launch image capture, and immediately rotate it to portrait mode.   # Notice that there are black bars present and that the image capture is rotated. This is despite setting the autorotate property to false when calling showCamera.     h6.Expected  The image capture view is full screen, just how it launches if the user does not rotate the device immediately upon launching image capture. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: iPad Image Capture Black Bars if rotated immediately when clicking launch Image capture
Description: """"h6.Isue description If the user rotates the device immediately when launching image capture then there are black bars present and the video is rotated. h6.Steps to reproduce # Launch sample and put the app in landscape orientation. # Click launch image capture, and immediately rotate it to portrait mode. # Notice that there are black bars present and that the image capture is rotated. This is despite setting the autorotate property to false when calling showCamera. h6.Expected The image capture view is full screen, just how it launches if the user does not rotate the device immediately upon launching image capture. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17697,12,"""iOS8: Ti.Platform  - Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight returning incorrect values for iPhone6 and 6+""","""""""h4. Problem The method """"""""Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight"""""""" is used in our application to identify the iPhone device the application is being run on to dynamically adjust UI components.  With iPhone6 and 6+ this method still return 568 which is the same value returned for iPhone5/5S making it impossible to distinguish the devices.  Is this an issue currently being looked at or will new API methods be made available to identify the iPhone device in Titanium SDK 3.4.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile app  2. Paste into app.js this:    3. Run it in simulator iphone 6 / iphone 6 plus.     h4. Extra info  It's failing both iphone6/6plus.  If you run the same code it will work fine in an ipad air.   """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: Ti.Platform - Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight returning incorrect values for iPhone6 and 6+
Description: """"h4. Problem The method """"""""Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight"""""""" is used in our application to identify the iPhone device the application is being run on to dynamically adjust UI components. With iPhone6 and 6+ this method still return 568 which is the same value returned for iPhone5/5S making it impossible to distinguish the devices. Is this an issue currently being looked at or will new API methods be made available to identify the iPhone device in Titanium SDK 3.4. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile app 2. Paste into app.js this: 3. Run it in simulator iphone 6 / iphone 6 plus. h4. Extra info It's failing both iphone6/6plus. If you run the same code it will work fine in an ipad air. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17683,12,"""iOS8: call registerUserNotificationSettings when Ti.Network.registerForPushNotifications() is called""","""""""In a comment in TIMOB-17238, Timan said that is was confusing to have to call     before       We could take the `types` passed into `registerForPushNotifications` and call `registerUserNotificationSettings` for the user behind the scenes to make it work like it did in iOS8. I am not sure if this would be a good abstraction, but it is possible.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS8: call registerUserNotificationSettings when Ti.Network.registerForPushNotifications() is called
Description: """"In a comment in TIMOB-17238, Timan said that is was confusing to have to call before We could take the `types` passed into `registerForPushNotifications` and call `registerUserNotificationSettings` for the user behind the scenes to make it work like it did in iOS8. I am not sure if this would be a good abstraction, but it is possible.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17680,12,"""Android: Add support for NDK 64bit""","""""""Getting error on installing the app if app contains module packaged using option output Location as “Mobile App Project”       *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create Android module.  2. Create Classic Project.   3. Package android module using option “Mobile App Project” (Select the same project from drop down created in Step 2)  4. Install App on device.      {color:green}*Expected Result:*{color}  App must get installed successfully.    {color:red}*Actual Result:*{color}  App is not getting installed on device.  Getting the logs attached.    Note: Working fine with 3.3.0GA environment with ndk:android-ndk-r9d            Also working fine with 3.4.0 studio using ndk:android-ndk-r9d""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Add support for NDK 64bit
Description: """"Getting error on installing the app if app contains module packaged using option output Location as “Mobile App Project” *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create Android module. 2. Create Classic Project. 3. Package android module using option “Mobile App Project” (Select the same project from drop down created in Step 2) 4. Install App on device. {color:green}*Expected Result:*{color} App must get installed successfully. {color:red}*Actual Result:*{color} App is not getting installed on device. Getting the logs attached. Note: Working fine with 3.3.0GA environment with ndk:android-ndk-r9d Also working fine with 3.4.0 studio using ndk:android-ndk-r9d""""",title+description
TIMOB-17679,12,"""iOS: NavWindow needs a back button clicked event""","""""""iOS natively supports calling a selector for back button clicked events for things that need to happen immediately once a back button is clicked, most often a rapid UI change. For these types of things the close event takes too long and results in a glitchy UI.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: NavWindow needs a back button clicked event
Description: """"iOS natively supports calling a selector for back button clicked events for things that need to happen immediately once a back button is clicked, most often a rapid UI change. For these types of things the close event takes too long and results in a glitchy UI.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17674,12,"""Android: On Android Ti.UI.ImageView can show the wrong image (cache bug, explained)""","""""""If an application has two different images with urls/paths that map to the same hash code at java.lang.String level then Ti.UI.ImageView can show the wrong one.    TiUIImageView internally uses a memory cache for the Bitmaps with TiDrawableReference.hashCode() as keys. In case of an url-based drawable reference TiDrawableReference.hashCode() turns into a simple java.lang.String.hashCode(url) wrapper.    See line 115 of  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/view/TiDrawableReference.java  and line 694 of  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIImageView.java     java.lang.String.hashCode() is very likely to generate collisions.  The following code prints the same number for both urls.      The cache should use a stronger hashing algorithm (such as SHA1) and possibly add more data to be hashed (the file size?).  """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: On Android Ti.UI.ImageView can show the wrong image (cache bug, explained)
Description: """"If an application has two different images with urls/paths that map to the same hash code at java.lang.String level then Ti.UI.ImageView can show the wrong one. TiUIImageView internally uses a memory cache for the Bitmaps with TiDrawableReference.hashCode() as keys. In case of an url-based drawable reference TiDrawableReference.hashCode() turns into a simple java.lang.String.hashCode(url) wrapper. See line 115 of https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/view/TiDrawableReference.java and line 694 of https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIImageView.java java.lang.String.hashCode() is very likely to generate collisions. The following code prints the same number for both urls. The cache should use a stronger hashing algorithm (such as SHA1) and possibly add more data to be hashed (the file size?). """"",title+description
TIMOB-17673,12,"""Animation duration is ignored if property is same as currently applied""","""""""If an animation is trying to change a property to what is already applied (e.g. view has width of 1px, animation is setting to 1px), then the completion event is immediately fired, ignoring the animation duration.    To see this in action, run the code below. You'll see that for the first animation you get the console output one time; 2 seconds later, a flurry of console items appear.    This is problematic, as if you assume the complete event will not fire until after the duration has elapsed, this could lead to circumstances which cripple a running application.    {code:title=index.xml}  <Alloy>   <Window id=""""""""win"""""""">    <View id=""""""""container""""""""></View>   </Window>  </Alloy>      {code:title=index.js}  function animateView() {   Ti.API.error(""""""""Running animateView"""""""");      var anim = Ti.UI.createAnimation({    width: 1,    duration: 2000   });      anim.addEventListener(""""""""complete"""""""", function() {    gradient();   });      $.container.animate(anim);  }    $.win.addEventListener(""""""""open"""""""", animateView);    $.win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Animation duration is ignored if property is same as currently applied
Description: """"If an animation is trying to change a property to what is already applied (e.g. view has width of 1px, animation is setting to 1px), then the completion event is immediately fired, ignoring the animation duration. To see this in action, run the code below. You'll see that for the first animation you get the console output one time; 2 seconds later, a flurry of console items appear. This is problematic, as if you assume the complete event will not fire until after the duration has elapsed, this could lead to circumstances which cripple a running application. {code:title=index.xml} <Alloy> <Window id=""""""""win""""""""> <View id=""""""""container""""""""></View> </Window> </Alloy> {code:title=index.js} function animateView() { Ti.API.error(""""""""Running animateView""""""""); var anim = Ti.UI.createAnimation({ width: 1, duration: 2000 }); anim.addEventListener(""""""""complete"""""""", function() { gradient(); }); $.container.animate(anim); } $.win.addEventListener(""""""""open"""""""", animateView); $.win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-17672,12,"""iOS: Black bar added over navBar when rotating back from full screen""","""""""h5. To reproduce  app.js    1. Click Win2  2. Return to Tab1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Black bar added over navBar when rotating back from full screen
Description: """"h5. To reproduce app.js 1. Click Win2 2. Return to Tab1""""",title+description
