TIMOB-17617,12,"""iOS: Adding titleAttributes to Ti.UI.TableViewRow""","""""""This is more of a nice to have :)    Instead of adding a Label within a TableViewRow, _(while crossing over the JSbridge into Native to create a Label & Row)_ is to have the possibility to have titleAttributes to the Row's title     (see this for more on TableViewRow performance: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/video/97758718 ??@10:37?? ).    Ideally is to have the possibility to modify the *titleAttributes* of Rows as objects to be placed in an Array and then passed to the TableView's data:    example:    The above would be much more performant than creating a Label within a TableViewRow for each row.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Adding titleAttributes to Ti.UI.TableViewRow
Description: """"This is more of a nice to have :) Instead of adding a Label within a TableViewRow, _(while crossing over the JSbridge into Native to create a Label & Row)_ is to have the possibility to have titleAttributes to the Row's title (see this for more on TableViewRow performance: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/video/97758718 ??@10:37?? ). Ideally is to have the possibility to modify the *titleAttributes* of Rows as objects to be placed in an Array and then passed to the TableView's data: example: The above would be much more performant than creating a Label within a TableViewRow for each row.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17616,12,"""iOS: Child views showing as visible when outside parent bounds""","""""""h4. Problem Description  There is a change of how we make objects visible with 3.3.0.GA     *VIEW A* [width 30 - height 30]  *VIEW B* [width 30 - height 30 - left 30]    - With SDK <= *3.2.3.GA* if i add the *VIEW B* to *VIEW A* , the *VIEW B* is not visible  [CORRECT]  - With SDK *3.3.0.GA* if i add the *VIEW B* to *VIEW A* , the *VIEW B* is visible             [NOT CORRECT]      h4. Steps to Reproduce    - Create a new mobile project (Classic Titanium)  - Replace app.js content with this:     - Run the test code with 3.2.3GA SDK  - Run the test code with 3.3.0GA SDK    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Child views showing as visible when outside parent bounds
Description: """"h4. Problem Description There is a change of how we make objects visible with 3.3.0.GA *VIEW A* [width 30 - height 30] *VIEW B* [width 30 - height 30 - left 30] - With SDK <= *3.2.3.GA* if i add the *VIEW B* to *VIEW A* , the *VIEW B* is not visible [CORRECT] - With SDK *3.3.0.GA* if i add the *VIEW B* to *VIEW A* , the *VIEW B* is visible [NOT CORRECT] h4. Steps to Reproduce - Create a new mobile project (Classic Titanium) - Replace app.js content with this: - Run the test code with 3.2.3GA SDK - Run the test code with 3.3.0GA SDK """"",title+description
TIMOB-17615,12,"""Selected defaultunit should be available under Ti.UI""","""""""If you set the defaultunit via {{tiapp.xml}} using {{<property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""">dp</property>}} you can request this in run-time using {{Ti.App.Properties.getString('ti.ui.defaultunit');}}.    However, I'd like to also have {{Ti.App.defaultUnit}} return one of the {{Ti.UI.UNIT_*}} constants, so that in a widget or module (where I'm not in control of the {{tiapp.xml}}) I can more easily detect the current setting and use this e.g. in {{Ti.UI.convertUnits}} when doing complex layout calculations.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Selected defaultunit should be available under Ti.UI
Description: """"If you set the defaultunit via {{tiapp.xml}} using {{<property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""">dp</property>}} you can request this in run-time using {{Ti.App.Properties.getString('ti.ui.defaultunit');}}. However, I'd like to also have {{Ti.App.defaultUnit}} return one of the {{Ti.UI.UNIT_*}} constants, so that in a widget or module (where I'm not in control of the {{tiapp.xml}}) I can more easily detect the current setting and use this e.g. in {{Ti.UI.convertUnits}} when doing complex layout calculations.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17614,12,"""Android: Facebook-Login-Callback needs JSON.parse (parity)""","""""""h4. Problem Description  I recently discovered an issue on Android when logging into Facebook to use the user-data like name & id. Therefor the login callback returns a """"""""data"""""""" object, which needs to be parsed manually on Android, but in iOS you don't need to do anything extra.      h4. Steps to reproduce    - Create a simple project.  - Update app.js with:      - Add facebook module in tiapp.xml  - Run on android device      h4. Extra info  The difference in the callbacks are here.   iOS: https://gist.github.com/hansknoechel/9e63d4b683bd72cc29bd  Android: https://gist.github.com/hansknoechel/f0f3280fda26f98d52c0    The bug was also discussed 2 years ago in the Q&A: https://developer.<USER>com/question/135341/titaniumfacebook-login-callback---cant-access-user-data-on-android-device    h4. Workaround  The bug can be """"""""fixed"""""""" by using a conditional statement like:    But a consistent behaviour is clearly the better way.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook-Login-Callback needs JSON.parse (parity)
Description: """"h4. Problem Description I recently discovered an issue on Android when logging into Facebook to use the user-data like name & id. Therefor the login callback returns a """"""""data"""""""" object, which needs to be parsed manually on Android, but in iOS you don't need to do anything extra. h4. Steps to reproduce - Create a simple project. - Update app.js with: - Add facebook module in tiapp.xml - Run on android device h4. Extra info The difference in the callbacks are here. iOS: https://gist.github.com/hansknoechel/9e63d4b683bd72cc29bd Android: https://gist.github.com/hansknoechel/f0f3280fda26f98d52c0 The bug was also discussed 2 years ago in the Q&A: https://developer.<USER>com/question/135341/titaniumfacebook-login-callback---cant-access-user-data-on-android-device h4. Workaround The bug can be """"""""fixed"""""""" by using a conditional statement like: But a consistent behaviour is clearly the better way.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17608,12,"""iOS: Picker is not being visible if Picker Column added with height and width as “Ti.UI.SIZE”""","""""""Picker is not being visible if Picker Column added with height and width as “Ti.UI.SIZE”  But works fine on Android.  Not a regression since not working on 3.3.0.GA also    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Copy paste the code given below and run the app.  2. Comment line no 17,18 and run the app again     {color:green}*Expected Result:*{color}  1.Picker must be visible.   2.Picker must be visible.    {color:red}*Actual Result:*{color}  1. Picker is not visible.  2. Picker is visible.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Picker is not being visible if Picker Column added with height and width as “Ti.UI.SIZE”
