TIMOB-17580,12,"""Android : Memory was Increased Reading file from SDCard""","""""""h4. Problem Description   In my app we used icons and images. All the file size less than 20Kb. All this files are Download from server and store to SDCard. When we getting file from SDCard HEAP memory was increased and some time app will be EXIT. we put the same file inside the RESOURCE folder after we tried Heap Memory was not increased and app was stabled. Please refer the screenshot.       Hello, We have tested the issue with the following code below and we have observed the same problem.    h5. TESTING ENVIRONMENT    CLI version 3.3.0,   Titanium SDK version 3.3.0.GA  Android Device      h4. STEP TO TEST    - Create a new Project  - Copy the Code above to the project """"""""app.js"""""""" file    - Substitute the file name """"""""Untitled.rtf"""""""" with the file's name that you want to read from SDCard, in your """"""""app.js"""""""" file. (Untitled.rtf is here attached)  - Run the app  - Click """"""""Read From File"""""""" to read your file, which will show in alert.    h4. Actual results  The console shows  which indicates that the heap memory has raised.      h4. Extra information  tiapp.xml        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android : Memory was Increased Reading file from SDCard
Description: """"h4. Problem Description In my app we used icons and images. All the file size less than 20Kb. All this files are Download from server and store to SDCard. When we getting file from SDCard HEAP memory was increased and some time app will be EXIT. we put the same file inside the RESOURCE folder after we tried Heap Memory was not increased and app was stabled. Please refer the screenshot. Hello, We have tested the issue with the following code below and we have observed the same problem. h5. TESTING ENVIRONMENT CLI version 3.3.0, Titanium SDK version 3.3.0.GA Android Device h4. STEP TO TEST - Create a new Project - Copy the Code above to the project """"""""app.js"""""""" file - Substitute the file name """"""""Untitled.rtf"""""""" with the file's name that you want to read from SDCard, in your """"""""app.js"""""""" file. (Untitled.rtf is here attached) - Run the app - Click """"""""Read From File"""""""" to read your file, which will show in alert. h4. Actual results The console shows which indicates that the heap memory has raised. h4. Extra information tiapp.xml """"",title+description
TIMOB-17579,12,"""Child view using Ti.UI.SIZE will NOT grow beyond a parent with clipMode disabled""","""""""h4. Problem Description  As the example and the second screenshot shows, the image view (which is {{Ti.UI.SIZE}} by default) will stay contained in the smaller parent view, even though it has clipMode disabled.    If you would add the image view directly to the window you'd get the expected behaviour, also shown in the first screenshot.    Hello,  We have tested this issue with our sample code. Child view using Ti.UI.SIZE will NOT grow beyond a parent with clipMode disabled. It’s a bug.     *TESTING ENVIRONMENT:*      Titanium SDK: 3.3.0.GA and 3.2.3.GA      Titanium CLI: 3.3.0      OS X Version: 10.9.3     Android API Level: 17 and 19     h4. Steps  to reproduce      a) Create a simple project.      b) Copy the Code Sample into app.js        c) Run this with testing environment    h4. Code Sample  """"""",Bug,"Title: Child view using Ti.UI.SIZE will NOT grow beyond a parent with clipMode disabled
