TIMOB-17577,12,"""CLI: ti create generates wrong directory structure""","""""""The iOS module development guide (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/iOS_Module_Development_Guide) did not work seamlessly. In order to run the example app correctly, I needed to move the example directory from ~/tmp/test/example to ~/tmp/test/iphone/example.    I'm not sure if this is a problem with the documentation or the CLI, but it did cause my some confusion when I tried to follow the guide.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: ti create generates wrong directory structure
Description: """"The iOS module development guide (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/iOS_Module_Development_Guide) did not work seamlessly. In order to run the example app correctly, I needed to move the example directory from ~/tmp/test/example to ~/tmp/test/iphone/example. I'm not sure if this is a problem with the documentation or the CLI, but it did cause my some confusion when I tried to follow the guide.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17575,12,"""Studio: Run Menu shows device name directly when only one device is connected instead off under iOS/Android Devices option""","""""""Launch Studio. Connect only one iOS or Android Device  Create classic/alloy app.  Click on Run.  Choose Refresh Devices options from Run menu    {color:green}*Expected Result:*{color}  1. Must get respective device name under iOS/Android Devices option.    {color:red}*Actual Result:*{color}  1.Will observe the respective device name is shown directly in the popup instead of under  iOS/Android Devices option where device name was shown previously.     Note: Observed this issue after upgrading the studio build to (3.4.0.201408282203) and after installing latest sdk build(3.4.0.v20140829010914)    Please Refer to the screenshot attached.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Studio: Run Menu shows device name directly when only one device is connected instead off under iOS/Android Devices option
Description: """"Launch Studio. Connect only one iOS or Android Device Create classic/alloy app. Click on Run. Choose Refresh Devices options from Run menu {color:green}*Expected Result:*{color} 1. Must get respective device name under iOS/Android Devices option. {color:red}*Actual Result:*{color} 1.Will observe the respective device name is shown directly in the popup instead of under iOS/Android Devices option where device name was shown previously. Note: Observed this issue after upgrading the studio build to (3.4.0.201408282203) and after installing latest sdk build(3.4.0.v20140829010914) Please Refer to the screenshot attached. """"",title+description
