TIMOB-17546,12,"""Android: make ScrollableView paging controls same as in iOS""","""""""The ScrollableView paging controls on iOS are attractive, and the same model is now used on numerous native Android apps as well. Unfortunately, the Titanium paging controls for Android are large ugly arrows. Since neither is native to Android, there is no justification for having a custom view different from what exists in iOS. It would be great if this were improved.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: make ScrollableView paging controls same as in iOS
Description: """"The ScrollableView paging controls on iOS are attractive, and the same model is now used on numerous native Android apps as well. Unfortunately, the Titanium paging controls for Android are large ugly arrows. Since neither is native to Android, there is no justification for having a custom view different from what exists in iOS. It would be great if this were improved.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17543,12,"""Set default emulator/simulator via CLI ""","""""""I almost always build/launch Android apps in a Genymotion emulator.     {{ti build -p android -C <device-id>}}    Since I can never remember the device ID string, which may contain multiple words (Custom Phone 7 - 4.3 - API 18 - 1024x600) my workaround is to pass a bogus value for the device ID, which makes the CLI prompt me with a list of available devices:        I would like to be able to set the default emulator to one of the Genymotion emulators, maybe via one of the {{ti setup android}} prompts?    """"""",Improvement,"Title: Set default emulator/simulator via CLI
Description: """"I almost always build/launch Android apps in a Genymotion emulator. {{ti build -p android -C <device-id>}} Since I can never remember the device ID string, which may contain multiple words (Custom Phone 7 - 4.3 - API 18 - 1024x600) my workaround is to pass a bogus value for the device ID, which makes the CLI prompt me with a list of available devices: I would like to be able to set the default emulator to one of the Genymotion emulators, maybe via one of the {{ti setup android}} prompts? """"",title+description
TIMOB-17542,12,"""iOS: Window title blinks""","""""""Window title in a sub window blinks after is window opened instead of making animation. See attached videos...    app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window title blinks
Description: """"Window title in a sub window blinks after is window opened instead of making animation. See attached videos... app.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-17541,12,"""Android: AlertDialog has no method 'setAndroidView'""","""""""h4. Problem Description    Can't set the {{androidView}} property of Ti.UI.AlertDialog after creation.    setAndroidView is a documented method.  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-method-setAndroidView      h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a simple project.  2.. Paste the testcase into app.js:    3.Run on Android    h4. Expected Result  The app should work.     h4. Actual Result  throws Titanium Javascript Runtime Error:  {color:red}      Message: Uncaught TypeError: Object #<AlertDialog> has no method 'setAndroidView'  {color}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: AlertDialog has no method 'setAndroidView'
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Can't set the {{androidView}} property of Ti.UI.AlertDialog after creation. setAndroidView is a documented method. http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-method-setAndroidView h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a simple project. 2.. Paste the testcase into app.js: 3.Run on Android h4. Expected Result The app should work. h4. Actual Result throws Titanium Javascript Runtime Error: {color:red} Message: Uncaught TypeError: Object #<AlertDialog> has no method 'setAndroidView' {color}""""",title+description
TIMOB-17540,12,"""Cannot add TTID to Map annotations because they are not a part of Ti.UI.View""","""""""From SOASTA engineering:  """"""""I see in my index.js code that the following is being set:        And we are not currently getting the touchTestIds during recordings.  The reason is when this is being created, it’s not a part of the TiUIView, so we cannot capture this information.    I would like to see what the code gets translated to in Java, but I don’t know where to look for it.  Can you point me to documentation, or let me know who to contact, so I know which method on your side I need to look at (I.e. In the titanium.jar) that will allow me to capture the touchTestIds being set here?""""""""      This is a similar issue to TIMOB-16978, as we will need some cooperation between SOASTA and AppC engineers to identify the correct methods to change so that recordings can detect the TouchTestIds on map annotations.""""""",Bug,"Title: Cannot add TTID to Map annotations because they are not a part of Ti.UI.View
Description: """"From SOASTA engineering: """"""""I see in my index.js code that the following is being set: And we are not currently getting the touchTestIds during recordings. The reason is when this is being created, it’s not a part of the TiUIView, so we cannot capture this information. I would like to see what the code gets translated to in Java, but I don’t know where to look for it. Can you point me to documentation, or let me know who to contact, so I know which method on your side I need to look at (I.e. In the titanium.jar) that will allow me to capture the touchTestIds being set here?"""""""" This is a similar issue to TIMOB-16978, as we will need some cooperation between SOASTA and AppC engineers to identify the correct methods to change so that recordings can detect the TouchTestIds on map annotations.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17537,12,"""Android Expanded notifications""","""""""Now that iOS Interactive Notifications (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17238?filter=15595) is being considered, perhaps it's a good idea to also consider """"""""Android's Expanded Layout"""""""" Notifications: http://developer.android.com/design/patterns/notifications.html , which are available since Jelly Bean.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android Expanded notifications
Description: """"Now that iOS Interactive Notifications (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-17238?filter=15595) is being considered, perhaps it's a good idea to also consider """"""""Android's Expanded Layout"""""""" Notifications: http://developer.android.com/design/patterns/notifications.html , which are available since Jelly Bean.""""",title+description
