TIMOB-17512,12,"""Android: ListView ListItems disappear on scrolling when height set as TI.UI.SIZE""","""""""Steps -   1. Run the below code sample  2. Observe that ListView items are appearing in correct order (small medium and big)  3. Now scroll the list items up and down.  4. Observe the ListView items.    Actual result - ListView item “big” is not appearing in the ListView. See the attached screen shot.    Expected Result - ListView items should not disappear on scrolling the list items    Additional Info - In the below code, if I set the height (ex - height : ’20dp’) instead of height : TI.UI.SIZE then scrolling is working fine  Note - Working fine on iOS device.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ListView ListItems disappear on scrolling when height set as TI.UI.SIZE
Description: """"Steps - 1. Run the below code sample 2. Observe that ListView items are appearing in correct order (small medium and big) 3. Now scroll the list items up and down. 4. Observe the ListView items. Actual result - ListView item “big” is not appearing in the ListView. See the attached screen shot. Expected Result - ListView items should not disappear on scrolling the list items Additional Info - In the below code, if I set the height (ex - height : ’20dp’) instead of height : TI.UI.SIZE then scrolling is working fine Note - Working fine on iOS device. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17511,12,"""Android: Tableview row not showing the  hasChild button correctly""","""""""h3. Issue    When setting the hasChild property as true in the Tableview row and installing the app to a device with 1080x1920 screen size the hasChild button is not correctly rendered being to small to be seen, on smaller sizes the button is correctly shown (screens attached).    h3. Test code    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tableview row not showing the hasChild button correctly
Description: """"h3. Issue When setting the hasChild property as true in the Tableview row and installing the app to a device with 1080x1920 screen size the hasChild button is not correctly rendered being to small to be seen, on smaller sizes the button is correctly shown (screens attached). h3. Test code """"",title+description
TIMOB-17510,12,"""iOS 8 - Add new notification permissions""","""""""In iOS 8, there has been a change in the way the local notifications work. Now we need to ask the user for permission before registering.    Reference: https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIUserNotificationSettings_class/index.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS 8 - Add new notification permissions
