TIMOB-17496,12,"""Electric Company - ScrollView with child scrollableView not responding to touches""","""""""When the Electric Company app is first opened, there is a scrollable view nested within a ScrollView, and the parent ScrollView is unresponsive to touches until the ScrollableView has been swiped. Only then can you actually scroll to the rest of the ScrollView.     Steps to Reproduce:  -Open Electric Company app  -Attempt to scroll vertically     Actual Result:  -View fails to respond    Expected Result:  -View scrolls properly    Additional Notes: Works as expected with Ti SDK 3.2.2  Electric Company app is available here: https://www.dropbox.com/s/g0g3ffigsr9nhbp/Electric%20Company.zip""""""",Bug,"Title: Electric Company - ScrollView with child scrollableView not responding to touches
Description: """"When the Electric Company app is first opened, there is a scrollable view nested within a ScrollView, and the parent ScrollView is unresponsive to touches until the ScrollableView has been swiped. Only then can you actually scroll to the rest of the ScrollView. Steps to Reproduce: -Open Electric Company app -Attempt to scroll vertically Actual Result: -View fails to respond Expected Result: -View scrolls properly Additional Notes: Works as expected with Ti SDK 3.2.2 Electric Company app is available here: https://www.dropbox.com/s/g0g3ffigsr9nhbp/Electric%20Company.zip""""",title+description
TIMOB-17495,12,"""Ti.Network.online and change events do not work reliably""","""""""We are using the Ti.Network.online to check of data connection exist (does not matter if it is data, Wifi or other) usually this has been reliable, but now it returns true most of the time or actually presently all the time... We have seen this both in Sim and Device (iPhone5, iOS 7)     We also tried the change event and just print the object returned, it says online even without any data contact    We are critically depending on this and it is a blocker for app deploy, can you please help?     I used this code in alloy.js        and got this result:    NETWORK STAT: {""""""""online"""""""":true,""""""""networkType"""""""":1,""""""""networkTypeName"""""""":""""""""WIFI"""""""",""""""""bubbles"""""""":true,""""""""type"""""""":""""""""change"""""""",""""""""source"""""""":{},""""""""cancelBubble"""""""":false}  [INFO] :   NETWORK : true type: 1  [INFO] :   NETWORK STAT: {""""""""online"""""""":true,""""""""networkType"""""""":1,""""""""networkTypeName"""""""":""""""""WIFI"""""""",""""""""bubbles"""""""":true,""""""""type"""""""":""""""""change"""""""",""""""""source"""""""":{},""""""""cancelBubble"""""""":false}  [INFO] :   NETWORK : true type: 1    this is a off and on switching of the network... and as you can see it remains true!!    Please help""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Network.online and change events do not work reliably
Description: """"We are using the Ti.Network.online to check of data connection exist (does not matter if it is data, Wifi or other) usually this has been reliable, but now it returns true most of the time or actually presently all the time... We have seen this both in Sim and Device (iPhone5, iOS 7) We also tried the change event and just print the object returned, it says online even without any data contact We are critically depending on this and it is a blocker for app deploy, can you please help? I used this code in alloy.js and got this result: NETWORK STAT: {""""""""online"""""""":true,""""""""networkType"""""""":1,""""""""networkTypeName"""""""":""""""""WIFI"""""""",""""""""bubbles"""""""":true,""""""""type"""""""":""""""""change"""""""",""""""""source"""""""":{},""""""""cancelBubble"""""""":false} [INFO] : NETWORK : true type: 1 [INFO] : NETWORK STAT: {""""""""online"""""""":true,""""""""networkType"""""""":1,""""""""networkTypeName"""""""":""""""""WIFI"""""""",""""""""bubbles"""""""":true,""""""""type"""""""":""""""""change"""""""",""""""""source"""""""":{},""""""""cancelBubble"""""""":false} [INFO] : NETWORK : true type: 1 this is a off and on switching of the network... and as you can see it remains true!! Please help""""",title+description
