Description: """"On iOS, the height of the HeaderView of a ListView cannot be higher than the screen size. As a result, long views cannot be displayed entirely. The HeaderView is not entirely displayed. On Android, the entire HeaderView is displayed. See attached screenshots.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17479,12,"""iOS: Memory leak when ListView template contains an event listener that update the listview""","""""""h5. Problem Description   The TiUIListViewProxy is never released and the memory usage keeps increasing with Titanium SDK 3.3.0 and 3.2.X.GA. It’s a valid bug.      h5. Testing Environment:     Mac OS X 10.9  Ti CLI 3.3.0  Titanium SDK: 3.3.0.RC and 3.2.X.GA  iOS 7.1     h5. Test Code         h5. Steps To Test     - Create a new project  - Update app.js file with sample code  - Run on iPad simulator 7.1  - Test allocation summary for running 10 times  - Memory usage keeps increasing.    Screenshot: https://www.dropbox.com/s/jn0xsh5rltbrbao/Screen%20Shot.jpg       h5. Expected Result     It’s not working as expected.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Memory leak when ListView template contains an event listener that update the listview
Description: """"h5. Problem Description The TiUIListViewProxy is never released and the memory usage keeps increasing with Titanium SDK 3.3.0 and 3.2.X.GA. It’s a valid bug. h5. Testing Environment: Mac OS X 10.9 Ti CLI 3.3.0 Titanium SDK: 3.3.0.RC and 3.2.X.GA iOS 7.1 h5. Test Code h5. Steps To Test - Create a new project - Update app.js file with sample code - Run on iPad simulator 7.1 - Test allocation summary for running 10 times - Memory usage keeps increasing. Screenshot: https://www.dropbox.com/s/jn0xsh5rltbrbao/Screen%20Shot.jpg h5. Expected Result It’s not working as expected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17474,12,"""Splash screen resizes on app launch""","""""""h4. Problem Description  With Ipad, the Splash screen resizes on app launch.  In addition to this, the default spash images have the wrong size in the default project.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new project in Titanium.  2. Run/build the project in titanium.  3. Go to the projects """"""""build/iphone/..."""""""" folder.  4. Open the (""""""""projectname"""""""".xcodeproj) file in xcode.  5. Copy the content of """"""""iphone"""""""" folder in """"""""Resource"""""""" Directory of the project to the """"""""iphone"""""""" folder in the """"""""build"""""""" directory of the project.  6. Deleate the project from the iphone/simulator.  7. Run the project by xcode.   8. The splash screen shows on full screen on the device/simulator.    h4. Expected results  The splash Screen should resizes on the first launch of the app.    h4. Actual Results  On iPad the splash Screen resizes and app launches on a small screen.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Splash screen resizes on app launch
Description: """"h4. Problem Description With Ipad, the Splash screen resizes on app launch. In addition to this, the default spash images have the wrong size in the default project. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new project in Titanium. 2. Run/build the project in titanium. 3. Go to the projects """"""""build/iphone/..."""""""" folder. 4. Open the (""""""""projectname"""""""".xcodeproj) file in xcode. 5. Copy the content of """"""""iphone"""""""" folder in """"""""Resource"""""""" Directory of the project to the """"""""iphone"""""""" folder in the """"""""build"""""""" directory of the project. 6. Deleate the project from the iphone/simulator. 7. Run the project by xcode. 8. The splash screen shows on full screen on the device/simulator. h4. Expected results The splash Screen should resizes on the first launch of the app. h4. Actual Results On iPad the splash Screen resizes and app launches on a small screen. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17473,12,"""iOS: Bluetooth LE state restoration callbacks are blocked in Titanium""","""""""The following 2 callbacks never get called in Titanium when adding handling for the callback in a module.    - (void)centralManager:(CBCentralManager *)central willRestoreState:(NSDictionary *)dict  - (void)peripheralManager:(CBPeripheralManager *)peripheral willRestoreState:(NSDictionary *)dict    The code for handling the callbacks works as expected in a native app.   The same code can be inserted into Titanium module and tested in a Titanium app and you will notice that the the app does restore itself to the background however the callback handlers never fire.     The callbacks are supposed to be called only when the app was previously in the background, then was killed off by iOS,   and then some bluetooth activity for the app comes in.    Similarly, the situation occurs for the following iBeacon related callbacks when the app has been killed off.    - (void)locationManager:(CLLocationManager *)manager didDetermineState:(CLRegionState)state forRegion:(CLRegion *)region  - (void)locationManager:(CLLocationManager *)manager didEnterRegion:(CLRegion *)region  - (void)locationManager:(CLLocationManager *)manager didExitRegion:(CLRegion *)region    The above iBeacon related functions are being called under normal circumstances, just not when the app was killed off as they are in a native app.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Bluetooth LE state restoration callbacks are blocked in Titanium
Description: """"The following 2 callbacks never get called in Titanium when adding handling for the callback in a module. - (void)centralManager:(CBCentralManager *)central willRestoreState:(NSDictionary *)dict - (void)peripheralManager:(CBPeripheralManager *)peripheral willRestoreState:(NSDictionary *)dict The code for handling the callbacks works as expected in a native app. The same code can be inserted into Titanium module and tested in a Titanium app and you will notice that the the app does restore itself to the background however the callback handlers never fire. The callbacks are supposed to be called only when the app was previously in the background, then was killed off by iOS, and then some bluetooth activity for the app comes in. Similarly, the situation occurs for the following iBeacon related callbacks when the app has been killed off. - (void)locationManager:(CLLocationManager *)manager didDetermineState:(CLRegionState)state forRegion:(CLRegion *)region - (void)locationManager:(CLLocationManager *)manager didEnterRegion:(CLRegion *)region - (void)locationManager:(CLLocationManager *)manager didExitRegion:(CLRegion *)region The above iBeacon related functions are being called under normal circumstances, just not when the app was killed off as they are in a native app. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17470,12,"""IOS: setCameraFlashMode();  getCameraFlashMode(); do not work""","""""""h4. Problem Description  The getFlashMode never work, even after set it.     h4. Test Case      h4. Steps To Reproduce     - Create a new project  - Update app.js file with sample code  - And run on iOS device 7.1  - Camera Flash Mode always set to Auto and returns 0.     h4. Expected Result   It’s not working as expected.  """"""",Bug,"Title: IOS: setCameraFlashMode(); getCameraFlashMode(); do not work
Description: """"h4. Problem Description The getFlashMode never work, even after set it. h4. Test Case h4. Steps To Reproduce - Create a new project - Update app.js file with sample code - And run on iOS device 7.1 - Camera Flash Mode always set to Auto and returns 0. h4. Expected Result It’s not working as expected. """"",title+description
