TIMOB-17445,12,"""TiAPI: HttpClient abort not consistent across platforms""","""""""Calling abort on the httpClient behaves different on android vs ios    * iOS: the client simply stops, there is no event triggered (it should trigger a **onreadystatechange** as [~<USER> said)  * Android: the client stops after a while, the ondatastream event still triggers a few more times and then the **onsuccess** event is triggered.""""""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: HttpClient abort not consistent across platforms
Description: """"Calling abort on the httpClient behaves different on android vs ios * iOS: the client simply stops, there is no event triggered (it should trigger a **onreadystatechange** as [~<USER> said) * Android: the client stops after a while, the ondatastream event still triggers a few more times and then the **onsuccess** event is triggered.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17444,12,"""Include into Ti.Utils crypto-js""","""""""Please if possible include https://code.google.com/p/crypto-js/ library into Ti.Utils, would help a lot working with encrypted data from all sources.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Include into Ti.Utils crypto-js
Description: """"Please if possible include https://code.google.com/p/crypto-js/ library into Ti.Utils, would help a lot working with encrypted data from all sources.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17443,12,"""Android: Include native Switch UI element""","""""""h3. Request    Currently when we create a Switch with the Titanium SDK in Android we are able to create a Toggle button, since Android 4.0 a new component has been include in the Android SDK called Switch which allow the user to create a toggle button in the form of a slider.    Customer would like to have the Switch available in order to be used in the UI.    h3. Info    https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/controls/togglebutton.html  https://developer.android.com/reference/android/widget/Switch.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Include native Switch UI element
Description: """"h3. Request Currently when we create a Switch with the Titanium SDK in Android we are able to create a Toggle button, since Android 4.0 a new component has been include in the Android SDK called Switch which allow the user to create a toggle button in the form of a slider. Customer would like to have the Switch available in order to be used in the UI. h3. Info https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/controls/togglebutton.html https://developer.android.com/reference/android/widget/Switch.html""""",title+description
TIMOB-17441,12,"""MobileWeb: Fix HTML5 sample app to avoid application errors when preview in browser ""","""""""h5. Description  Error, when the default HTML5 app is being previewed in browser.  It happens with packaged for mobile web app as well.  h5. To reproduce  1. Create a default HTML5-based app  2. Run Mobile Web Preview in Browser  h5. Actual result    h5. Expected result  """"""""TARZAN OF THE APES"""""""" HTML file should be loaded  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Fix HTML5 sample app to avoid application errors when preview in browser
Description: """"h5. Description Error, when the default HTML5 app is being previewed in browser. It happens with packaged for mobile web app as well. h5. To reproduce 1. Create a default HTML5-based app 2. Run Mobile Web Preview in Browser h5. Actual result h5. Expected result """"""""TARZAN OF THE APES"""""""" HTML file should be loaded """"",title+description
TIMOB-17440,12,"""Android: support setting properties to the tabgroup activity before tabgroup opens""","""""""As described in [this comment|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-16889?focusedCommentId=305488&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-305488], the lifecycle callbacks, onCreate etc., need to be set in different mechanisms for window and tabgroup right now.     Need to refactor tabgroup so the lifecycle callbacks can be set before tabgroup opens.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: support setting properties to the tabgroup activity before tabgroup opens
Description: """"As described in [this comment|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-16889?focusedCommentId=305488&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-305488], the lifecycle callbacks, onCreate etc., need to be set in different mechanisms for window and tabgroup right now. Need to refactor tabgroup so the lifecycle callbacks can be set before tabgroup opens.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17439,12,"""Ti.UI.Animation with backgroundColor is not wokring""","""""""h4. Problem Description  Ti.UI.animation with backgroundColor doesn't work with 3.3.0.  We tested this issue with our sample code. Its working well as we expected in Titanium SDK version 3.2.3 GA  but its not working in Titanium SDK version 3.3.0 RC.It’s a bug.     h5. Testing Environment  Titanium SDK: 3.2.3.GA and 3.3.0.RC  Titanium CLI: 3.2.3  OS X Version: 10.9.3  IOS Simulator: 7.1  Android API Level: 17 and 19     h5. TEST CODE     XML Markup     TSS     index.js(Controller)    h5. STEPS TO REPRODUCE:  a) Create a simple project.  b) Update this code in app.js  c) Run this with testing environment     h5. TESTING RESULT(Titanium SDK: 3.3.0.RC):  In iOS : Nothing happens.Only show the Button.     In Android : The backgroundColor of the curved area (in TSS I have given a border Radius)  only changing and rest remains same.   """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.UI.Animation with backgroundColor is not wokring
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Ti.UI.animation with backgroundColor doesn't work with 3.3.0. We tested this issue with our sample code. Its working well as we expected in Titanium SDK version 3.2.3 GA but its not working in Titanium SDK version 3.3.0 RC.It’s a bug. h5. Testing Environment Titanium SDK: 3.2.3.GA and 3.3.0.RC Titanium CLI: 3.2.3 OS X Version: 10.9.3 IOS Simulator: 7.1 Android API Level: 17 and 19 h5. TEST CODE XML Markup TSS index.js(Controller) h5. STEPS TO REPRODUCE: a) Create a simple project. b) Update this code in app.js c) Run this with testing environment h5. TESTING RESULT(Titanium SDK: 3.3.0.RC): In iOS : Nothing happens.Only show the Button. In Android : The backgroundColor of the curved area (in TSS I have given a border Radius) only changing and rest remains same. """"",title+description
