TIMOB-17409,12,"""Both Ti.UI.View.rect and event coordinates should use the (same) documented unit""","""""""While making the [nl.<USER>color|https://github.com/<USER>nl.<USER>color] widget I noticed {{Ti.UI.View.rect}} and the {{x}} and {{y}} coordinate given in click (and other) events use different units.    The documentation of [rect|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-property-rect] clearly states it always uses the system unit (px on Android, dp on iOS) while the click docs (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-event-click) don't specify the unit.    When you execute the following {{app.js}} without and with {{ti.ui.defaultunit}} set to both {{dp}} and {{px}} on both platforms and click in the bottom right corner of the screen you'll see {{rect}} does *not* use the system unit but rather the defaultunit. The event coordinates *do* always use the system unit. The results can be found under the code snippet.    The documentation should be fixed, but I'd also request for both to use the same units, be it system or default unit.        h2. iOS    ||ti.ui.defaultunit||rect||click||  |(none)|dp|dp|  |px|px|dp|  |dp|dp|dp|    h2. Android    ||ti.ui.defaultunit||rect||click||  |(none)|px|px|  |px|px|px|  |dp|dp|px|""""""",Bug,"Title: Both Ti.UI.View.rect and event coordinates should use the (same) documented unit
Description: """"While making the [nl.<USER>color|https://github.com/<USER>nl.<USER>color] widget I noticed {{Ti.UI.View.rect}} and the {{x}} and {{y}} coordinate given in click (and other) events use different units. The documentation of [rect|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-property-rect] clearly states it always uses the system unit (px on Android, dp on iOS) while the click docs (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.View-event-click) don't specify the unit. When you execute the following {{app.js}} without and with {{ti.ui.defaultunit}} set to both {{dp}} and {{px}} on both platforms and click in the bottom right corner of the screen you'll see {{rect}} does *not* use the system unit but rather the defaultunit. The event coordinates *do* always use the system unit. The results can be found under the code snippet. The documentation should be fixed, but I'd also request for both to use the same units, be it system or default unit. h2. iOS ||ti.ui.defaultunit||rect||click|| |(none)|dp|dp| |px|px|dp| |dp|dp|dp| h2. Android ||ti.ui.defaultunit||rect||click|| |(none)|px|px| |px|px|px| |dp|dp|px|""""",title+description
