TIMOB-17405,12,"""iOS8: Keyboard with toolbar becomes hidden when clicking its toolbar icon ""","""""""*Steps to reproduce:*  1. Install KS on iOS 8 device.  2. Navigate to Controls>TextField>ToolBar  3.Click on a textfield that says """"""""Focus to see keyboard w/toolbar""""""""  Keyboard with toolbar appear.  4.Press any toolbar's icon (Camera) on a Toolbar      {color:red}*Actual Result:*{color}  Get an alert message """"""""Toolbar. You clicked camera!""""""""  But Keyboard moves down leaving its toolbar behind on the bottom of the screen   Refer to screenShot attached.    {color:green}*Expected Result:*{color}  Should get a message """"""""Toolbar. You clicked camera!""""""""  Keyboard must not get hidden.    Note: Keyboard remains appear on screen on iOS7""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS8: Keyboard with toolbar becomes hidden when clicking its toolbar icon
Description: """"*Steps to reproduce:* 1. Install KS on iOS 8 device. 2. Navigate to Controls>TextField>ToolBar 3.Click on a textfield that says """"""""Focus to see keyboard w/toolbar"""""""" Keyboard with toolbar appear. 4.Press any toolbar's icon (Camera) on a Toolbar {color:red}*Actual Result:*{color} Get an alert message """"""""Toolbar. You clicked camera!"""""""" But Keyboard moves down leaving its toolbar behind on the bottom of the screen Refer to screenShot attached. {color:green}*Expected Result:*{color} Should get a message """"""""Toolbar. You clicked camera!"""""""" Keyboard must not get hidden. Note: Keyboard remains appear on screen on iOS7""""",title+description
TIMOB-17403,12,"""iOS: final ondatastream event should be fired before final onreadystatechange event""","""""""The final {{ondatastream}} event containing progress=1 is fired after the DONE {{onreadystatechange}} event. This means you fall into a wonky state where the request is finished but you haven't been notified that all of the data has been received.        Apparently, this is how the events are dispatched in native land.    To resolve this issue, when the DONE {{onreadystatechange}} event is fired, disconnect the {{ondatastream}} event handler, manually fire the {{ondatastream}} event with progress=1, then continue to fire the DONE {{onreadystatechange}} event.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: final ondatastream event should be fired before final onreadystatechange event
Description: """"The final {{ondatastream}} event containing progress=1 is fired after the DONE {{onreadystatechange}} event. This means you fall into a wonky state where the request is finished but you haven't been notified that all of the data has been received. Apparently, this is how the events are dispatched in native land. To resolve this issue, when the DONE {{onreadystatechange}} event is fired, disconnect the {{ondatastream}} event handler, manually fire the {{ondatastream}} event with progress=1, then continue to fire the DONE {{onreadystatechange}} event.""""",title+description
