TIMOB-17295,12,"""CLI: Android build install and retry timeouts are too short""","""""""Currently the Android build waits 2 minutes for ADB install to complete. It also waits 1 second before retrying when an install fails.    To account for large apks and slow emulators, these values should be increased to 4 minutes for the install timeout and 2 seconds for the retry.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android build install and retry timeouts are too short
Description: """"Currently the Android build waits 2 minutes for ADB install to complete. It also waits 1 second before retrying when an install fails. To account for large apks and slow emulators, these values should be increased to 4 minutes for the install timeout and 2 seconds for the retry.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17294,12,"""CLI: Android build has incorrect verbiage when installing apk""","""""""When running an Android build, it displays:        which has bad grammar. Should be:        Then if ADB install fails, it will display:        This is confusing since ADB install will not start until the system_server <USER>is running which assumes the package manager has started. It needs to display:    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android build has incorrect verbiage when installing apk
Description: """"When running an Android build, it displays: which has bad grammar. Should be: Then if ADB install fails, it will display: This is confusing since ADB install will not start until the system_server <USER>is running which assumes the package manager has started. It needs to display: """"",title+description
TIMOB-17292,12,"""CLI: Naming of the custom splash screen should not be restricted to background.9.png""","""""""h5.Description:  1. Currently if a custom splash screen is named anything other than """"""""background.9.png"""""""" the CLI does not pick the custom splash screen & rather uses the default splash screen from the titanium SDK    2. Create an app & follow the docs for how to have custom splash screen : http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Icons_and_Splash_Screens-section-29004897_IconsandSplashScreens-Splashscreens    3. See that in the docs we use the name """"""""splash.9.png"""""""" as the filename for the custom splash screen.    4. Build the app for android device.    5. Rename the """"""""splash.9.png"""""""" to """"""""background.9.png"""""""" & build for android device again.    h5. Actual Result:  1. When name """"""""splash.9.png"""""""" is used the default splash screen is picked up from the titanium sdk & displayed.    2. When name """"""""background.9.png"""""""" is used the custom splash screen is picked up & displayed.    h5. Expected Result:  1. The naming of the custom splash screen file should not be restricted to """"""""background.9.png"""""""".  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Naming of the custom splash screen should not be restricted to background.9.png
Description: """"h5.Description: 1. Currently if a custom splash screen is named anything other than """"""""background.9.png"""""""" the CLI does not pick the custom splash screen & rather uses the default splash screen from the titanium SDK 2. Create an app & follow the docs for how to have custom splash screen : http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Icons_and_Splash_Screens-section-29004897_IconsandSplashScreens-Splashscreens 3. See that in the docs we use the name """"""""splash.9.png"""""""" as the filename for the custom splash screen. 4. Build the app for android device. 5. Rename the """"""""splash.9.png"""""""" to """"""""background.9.png"""""""" & build for android device again. h5. Actual Result: 1. When name """"""""splash.9.png"""""""" is used the default splash screen is picked up from the titanium sdk & displayed. 2. When name """"""""background.9.png"""""""" is used the custom splash screen is picked up & displayed. h5. Expected Result: 1. The naming of the custom splash screen file should not be restricted to """"""""background.9.png"""""""". """"",title+description
TIMOB-17290,12,"""UNIT_PT is missing in Ti.UI""","""""""Not that I use it, but the *Points* (pt) unit [mentioned in the docs|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Transitioning_to_the_New_UI_Layout_System-section-30088148_TransitioningtotheNewUILayoutSystem-UniversalUnitSupport] is not in the list of {{UNIT_*}} constants, both in the documentation (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI-property-UNIT_CM) and [actual code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/e91102a8f8152a68dcb63115e09260be5f002f2c/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/UIModule.java#L130-L134]""""""",Bug,"Title: UNIT_PT is missing in Ti.UI
Description: """"Not that I use it, but the *Points* (pt) unit [mentioned in the docs|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Transitioning_to_the_New_UI_Layout_System-section-30088148_TransitioningtotheNewUILayoutSystem-UniversalUnitSupport] is not in the list of {{UNIT_*}} constants, both in the documentation (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI-property-UNIT_CM) and [actual code|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/e91102a8f8152a68dcb63115e09260be5f002f2c/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/UIModule.java#L130-L134]""""",title+description
TIMOB-17289,12,"""iOS Safari Smart App Banner: non-empty """"app-argument"""" crashes an app""","""""""h4. Problem Description    Smart Banner successfully launches an app. But as soon as we try to use """"""""app-argument"""""""" parameter to pass anything (even with a custom scheme url that app supports) app will crash right after the launch/resume due to uncaught exception:      <Error>: *** Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException', reason: '*** setObjectForKey: object cannot be nil (key: source)'    Smart Banners doc: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/AppleApplications/Reference/SafariWebContent/PromotingAppswithAppBanners/PromotingAppswithAppBanners.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40002051-CH6-SW2      h4. Extra information    ERROR] The application has crashed with an uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException'.  Reason:    setObjectForKey: object cannot be nil (key: source)  Stack trace:  I think the issue is related to launchOptions dictionary.  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/launchOptions    It seems that Titanium code doesn't check and set nil value where it cannot be nil.    h4. Steps to reproduce  Get the app from here:     TapHunter - The Craft Beer Finder   https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/taphunter-craft-beer-finder/id512023104?mt=8    (anyone compiled with the latest 3.2.3 SDK).     How to reproduce:   1) Download an app (one of the mentioned above or any other you know that was built using latest SDK and are in app store)   2) Create a html page with the following meta tag:    <meta name=""""""""apple-itunes-app"""""""" content=""""""""app-id=512023104, app-argument= http://test.com """""""">    Where 512023104 is the """"""""TapHunter - The Craft Beer Finder"""""""" app id but can be your app id or 421224709 if you want to try with """"""""Farm Progress"""""""".    3) Open this page using safari on your device with the installed app   4) Click on Smart Banner """"""""OPEN"""""""" link and app will crash right after the launch""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Safari Smart App Banner: non-empty """"app-argument"""" crashes an app
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Smart Banner successfully launches an app. But as soon as we try to use """"""""app-argument"""""""" parameter to pass anything (even with a custom scheme url that app supports) app will crash right after the launch/resume due to uncaught exception: <Error>: *** Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException', reason: '*** setObjectForKey: object cannot be nil (key: source)' Smart Banners doc: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/AppleApplications/Reference/SafariWebContent/PromotingAppswithAppBanners/PromotingAppswithAppBanners.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40002051-CH6-SW2 h4. Extra information ERROR] The application has crashed with an uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException'. Reason: setObjectForKey: object cannot be nil (key: source) Stack trace: I think the issue is related to launchOptions dictionary. http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/launchOptions It seems that Titanium code doesn't check and set nil value where it cannot be nil. h4. Steps to reproduce Get the app from here: TapHunter - The Craft Beer Finder https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/taphunter-craft-beer-finder/id512023104?mt=8 (anyone compiled with the latest 3.2.3 SDK). How to reproduce: 1) Download an app (one of the mentioned above or any other you know that was built using latest SDK and are in app store) 2) Create a html page with the following meta tag: <meta name=""""""""apple-itunes-app"""""""" content=""""""""app-id=512023104, app-argument= http://test.com """"""""> Where 512023104 is the """"""""TapHunter - The Craft Beer Finder"""""""" app id but can be your app id or 421224709 if you want to try with """"""""Farm Progress"""""""". 3) Open this page using safari on your device with the installed app 4) Click on Smart Banner """"""""OPEN"""""""" link and app will crash right after the launch""""",title+description
TIMOB-17287,12,"""Advance Sample - inheritance: Animated dialog does not appears on clicking animatedDialog button""","""""""This is a regression since it works fine on 3.2.3 GA.    On clicking """"""""animatedDialog"""""""" button, Dialog with animation does not appears and app crashes.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Copy 'apps/advanced/inheritance' content into an existing project 'app' folder.  2. Build the app on android device.  3. Click on animatedDialog button.    Actual Result: No dialog box appears with animation and app crashes.    Expected Result: Dialog with animation should appears, displaying the 'Opened animatedDialog' text.    Note: It is working fine on iOS.""""""",Bug,"Title: Advance Sample - inheritance: Animated dialog does not appears on clicking animatedDialog button
Description: """"This is a regression since it works fine on 3.2.3 GA. On clicking """"""""animatedDialog"""""""" button, Dialog with animation does not appears and app crashes. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Copy 'apps/advanced/inheritance' content into an existing project 'app' folder. 2. Build the app on android device. 3. Click on animatedDialog button. Actual Result: No dialog box appears with animation and app crashes. Expected Result: Dialog with animation should appears, displaying the 'Opened animatedDialog' text. Note: It is working fine on iOS.""""",title+description
