TIMOB-17236,12,"""Android: actionBar.setNavigationMode(2) throws IlegalStateException and crashes app""","""""""h5.This is a regression. It works fine with 3.2.3.GA.    h5.Description:  1. Use the code from https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13135.  2. Make sure you use the legacy window property as the test code uses light weight window.    2. Build the app for android device 4.4 & android 2.3.7.  3. After the app launches, tap on """"""""Open childWin(same activity).  4. Tap on """"""""Show the tabs"""""""".    h5.Actual Result:  1. We get errors below and the app crashes.  Nexus 5 - android 4.4:      Sony Xperia - android 2.3.7:      h5.Expected Result:  1. We should see the tabs after tapping button """"""""Show the tabs"""""""".    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: actionBar.setNavigationMode(2) throws IlegalStateException and crashes app
Description: """"h5.This is a regression. It works fine with 3.2.3.GA. h5.Description: 1. Use the code from https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13135. 2. Make sure you use the legacy window property as the test code uses light weight window. 2. Build the app for android device 4.4 & android 2.3.7. 3. After the app launches, tap on """"""""Open childWin(same activity). 4. Tap on """"""""Show the tabs"""""""". h5.Actual Result: 1. We get errors below and the app crashes. Nexus 5 - android 4.4: Sony Xperia - android 2.3.7: h5.Expected Result: 1. We should see the tabs after tapping button """"""""Show the tabs"""""""". """"",title+description
TIMOB-17234,12,"""Android: Support Android Wear""","""""""h5. Description:  1. After the update to the android SDK tools to ver23 you will be getting new titanium SDK for Android 4.4W (Wear) API20.  2. Create an emulator for android 4.4W in the android avd manager.  3. In studio create a default classic/alloy app.  4. Build it for android 4.4W emulator.    h5.Actual Result:  1. The emulator for android 4.4W gets launched but the app fails to start giving errors:      h5.Expected Result:  1. As this is a new sdk & not tested for titanium apps, not sure what should be the expected result.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support Android Wear
Description: """"h5. Description: 1. After the update to the android SDK tools to ver23 you will be getting new titanium SDK for Android 4.4W (Wear) API20. 2. Create an emulator for android 4.4W in the android avd manager. 3. In studio create a default classic/alloy app. 4. Build it for android 4.4W emulator. h5.Actual Result: 1. The emulator for android 4.4W gets launched but the app fails to start giving errors: h5.Expected Result: 1. As this is a new sdk & not tested for titanium apps, not sure what should be the expected result.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17233,12,"""Android: Analytics - Analytics are still being sent if you change the base URL to a non-supported endpoint""","""""""*Details:* Analytics are still being sent if you change the base URL to a non-supported endpoint e.g. https://www.google.com/    *Note:* Was *not* able to reproduce the issue on iOS i.e. if I change the base URL to a non-supported endpoint, then analytics payload are not sent.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Import bob.zip into Eclipse; this project already has {{<meta-data android:name=""""""""APSAnalyticsBaseURL"""""""" android:value=""""""""https://www.google.com/""""""""/>}} in the manifest file and is the default Android project  2. Install app onto device that is pointing to staging  3. Go to staging and verify payloads with the guid 40060543-0d1b-4738-bcf7-20002a932a50    *Actual:* Analytic events are still being sent (see payload.txt attachment).  *Expected:* Analytic events should not be sent.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Analytics - Analytics are still being sent if you change the base URL to a non-supported endpoint
Description: """"*Details:* Analytics are still being sent if you change the base URL to a non-supported endpoint e.g. https://www.google.com/ *Note:* Was *not* able to reproduce the issue on iOS i.e. if I change the base URL to a non-supported endpoint, then analytics payload are not sent. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Import bob.zip into Eclipse; this project already has {{<meta-data android:name=""""""""APSAnalyticsBaseURL"""""""" android:value=""""""""https://www.google.com/""""""""/>}} in the manifest file and is the default Android project 2. Install app onto device that is pointing to staging 3. Go to staging and verify payloads with the guid 40060543-0d1b-4738-bcf7-20002a932a50 *Actual:* Analytic events are still being sent (see payload.txt attachment). *Expected:* Analytic events should not be sent.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17232,12,"""iOS: Analytics - Killing an app before the session timeout is generating a new session""","""""""*Details:* Killing an app before the session timeout is generating a new session i.e. ti.background and a new ti.foreground (new sid) is sent.    *Note:* This does *not* occur on native Android i.e. killing the app (backing out) and relaunching before a session timeout does not generate a new session.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a default app in Xcode with APS analytics enabled OR import check.zip into Xcode  2. Install app onto device and wait for app to launch; point device to staging  3. Next, background the app, wait a couple of seconds, then kill the app (double-press home button and swipe up on app)  4. Bring the app back to the foreground before 30 seconds    *Actual:* ti.background and a new ti.foreground is sent (see payloads.txt attachment).    *Expected:* ti.background and ti.foreground should not be generated.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Analytics - Killing an app before the session timeout is generating a new session
Description: """"*Details:* Killing an app before the session timeout is generating a new session i.e. ti.background and a new ti.foreground (new sid) is sent. *Note:* This does *not* occur on native Android i.e. killing the app (backing out) and relaunching before a session timeout does not generate a new session. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a default app in Xcode with APS analytics enabled OR import check.zip into Xcode 2. Install app onto device and wait for app to launch; point device to staging 3. Next, background the app, wait a couple of seconds, then kill the app (double-press home button and swipe up on app) 4. Bring the app back to the foreground before 30 seconds *Actual:* ti.background and a new ti.foreground is sent (see payloads.txt attachment). *Expected:* ti.background and ti.foreground should not be generated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17231,12,"""iOS: Analytics - ti.background is not sent if you background an app after you send the custom app events""","""""""*Details:* ti.background is not sent if you background an app after you send the custom app events (NavEvent, FeatureEvent, or GeoEvent).    *Note:* I was *not* able to reproduce this issue on Android.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Send custom events such as feature or nav events  2. Immediately background the application  3. Wait a minute or two for the analytic data to send  4. Check the analytic payloads    *Actual:* ti.background, app.nav, app.feature, and ti.geo are not sent.  *Expected:* ti.background, app.nav, app.feature, and ti.geo should be sent. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Analytics - ti.background is not sent if you background an app after you send the custom app events
Description: """"*Details:* ti.background is not sent if you background an app after you send the custom app events (NavEvent, FeatureEvent, or GeoEvent). *Note:* I was *not* able to reproduce this issue on Android. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Send custom events such as feature or nav events 2. Immediately background the application 3. Wait a minute or two for the analytic data to send 4. Check the analytic payloads *Actual:* ti.background, app.nav, app.feature, and ti.geo are not sent. *Expected:* ti.background, app.nav, app.feature, and ti.geo should be sent. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17229,12,"""Android TextArea in DataBinding Calls Blur after Focus when Focusing""","""""""Create a textarea from a dataCollection, as demonstrated. When the textarea is focused, the focused and blurred events are both called. The textarea isn't actually blurred, although this bug can lead to needing to use hacks to fix it.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android TextArea in DataBinding Calls Blur after Focus when Focusing
Description: """"Create a textarea from a dataCollection, as demonstrated. When the textarea is focused, the focused and blurred events are both called. The textarea isn't actually blurred, although this bug can lead to needing to use hacks to fix it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17228,12,"""Android: Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_MAP_ADDRESSES not working on android >= 4.4""","""""""Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_MAP_ADDRESSES not working on android >= 4.4    *Steps to Reproduce*  1. Install KS.Navigate to Controls>Label>Autolink  2. Tap on Map Addresses.    {color:green}Expected Result:{color}  2. Map address should be highlighted on the Contact info.    {color:red}Actual Result:{color}  2. Map address does not get highlighted.    Working fine on Android Nexus7(v4.3),LG-P970(v4.0.4)  Not working on Nexus7(v4.4.4),Nexus5(v4.4.4)""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_MAP_ADDRESSES not working on android >= 4.4
Description: """"Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_MAP_ADDRESSES not working on android >= 4.4 *Steps to Reproduce* 1. Install KS.Navigate to Controls>Label>Autolink 2. Tap on Map Addresses. {color:green}Expected Result:{color} 2. Map address should be highlighted on the Contact info. {color:red}Actual Result:{color} 2. Map address does not get highlighted. Working fine on Android Nexus7(v4.3),LG-P970(v4.0.4) Not working on Nexus7(v4.4.4),Nexus5(v4.4.4)""""",title+description
