TIMOB-17217,12,"""Android: KitchenSink: BackgroundColor for view inside scrollview not visible ""","""""""BackgroundColor for view inside scrollview not visible.  Working fine on iOS.  Working fine on LG-P970(v4.0.4),HTC Desire(v4.0.3)  On Nexus5(v4.4.4),Nexus4(v4.1.1),Nexus7(v4.3) view with blue background color is not visible.    But if height of blue colored view is changed then it works fine.      *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Install KS.  Navigate to BaseUI>Views>Scroll Views>Basic    {color:green}Expected Result:{color}  1.A blue view with two buttons must appear    {color:red}Actual Result:{color}   1.A blue view black background color appears with only one button""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink: BackgroundColor for view inside scrollview not visible
Description: """"BackgroundColor for view inside scrollview not visible. Working fine on iOS. Working fine on LG-P970(v4.0.4),HTC Desire(v4.0.3) On Nexus5(v4.4.4),Nexus4(v4.1.1),Nexus7(v4.3) view with blue background color is not visible. But if height of blue colored view is changed then it works fine. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Install KS. Navigate to BaseUI>Views>Scroll Views>Basic {color:green}Expected Result:{color} 1.A blue view with two buttons must appear {color:red}Actual Result:{color} 1.A blue view black background color appears with only one button""""",title+description
TIMOB-17216,12,"""Android: KitchenSink: navBarHidden property for window not working""","""""""navBarHidden property for window not working for Android.  Working fine on iOS.    It is regression.Working fine on 3.2.3.GA    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Install KS.  Navigate to BaseUI>Window (standalone)>Open(Nav bar covered)    {color:green}Expected Result:{color}  1.A blue view with close button which covers the nav bar should appear.  Refer to screenshot.[expected.png]    {color:red}Actual Result:{color}   1.A blue view with close button appears but nav bar is not covered.  Refer to screenshot.[actual.png]""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink: navBarHidden property for window not working
Description: """"navBarHidden property for window not working for Android. Working fine on iOS. It is regression.Working fine on 3.2.3.GA *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Install KS. Navigate to BaseUI>Window (standalone)>Open(Nav bar covered) {color:green}Expected Result:{color} 1.A blue view with close button which covers the nav bar should appear. Refer to screenshot.[expected.png] {color:red}Actual Result:{color} 1.A blue view with close button appears but nav bar is not covered. Refer to screenshot.[actual.png]""""",title+description
TIMOB-17215,12,"""Android Module Resources cannot be overridden""","""""""Its not possible to override resources such as xml or images that is used by a  android module. e.g. changing the theme of a module's activity.    So the app folder APPFOLDER/platform/android/res/ will not override the MODULEFOLDER/platform/android/res/    This makes modules very unflexible to style/setup. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android Module Resources cannot be overridden
Description: """"Its not possible to override resources such as xml or images that is used by a android module. e.g. changing the theme of a module's activity. So the app folder APPFOLDER/platform/android/res/ will not override the MODULEFOLDER/platform/android/res/ This makes modules very unflexible to style/setup. """"",title+description
