TIMOB-17209,12,"""CLI: Unable to create iOS module with module id beginning with a number""","""""""Cannot create an iOS module that has a module id such as """"""""ti.123"""""""" i.e. part of id begins with a number  This is a regression. The issue does not occur on 3.2.3.GA    Steps to Reproduce:  1. In the terminal run the command """"""""ti create --type module -d ~/Documents/ --name test --id ti.5815 --platforms ios""""""""  or   From Studio, try to create a new Mobile Module project. Mention the Module id as """"""""ti.5815""""""""    Actual Result:  An error is shown.  On terminal the following error is shown      Attached is the screenshot for error shown in Studio""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Unable to create iOS module with module id beginning with a number
Description: """"Cannot create an iOS module that has a module id such as """"""""ti.123"""""""" i.e. part of id begins with a number This is a regression. The issue does not occur on 3.2.3.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. In the terminal run the command """"""""ti create --type module -d ~/Documents/ --name test --id ti.5815 --platforms ios"""""""" or From Studio, try to create a new Mobile Module project. Mention the Module id as """"""""ti.5815"""""""" Actual Result: An error is shown. On terminal the following error is shown Attached is the screenshot for error shown in Studio""""",title+description
TIMOB-17207,12,"""CLI: """"--platform"""" option does not work for """"ti create"""" command""","""""""The """"""""--platform"""""""" option in the """"""""ti create"""""""" command does not work and the user is prompted to select the platform for the module/app. The """"""""-p"""""""" works fine.  The """"""""--platform"""""""" options works fine for other commands like """"""""ti build"""""""" and """"""""ti clean""""""""    Steps to Reproduce:  1. In the terminal run the CLI command """"""""ti create --type app --platform android""""""""    Actual Result:  The CLI prompts for selecting the target platform, even though a valid platform was mentioned in the command      Expected Result:  The --platform option should work for """"""""ti create"""""""" command""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"--platform"""" option does not work for """"ti create"""" command
Description: """"The """"""""--platform"""""""" option in the """"""""ti create"""""""" command does not work and the user is prompted to select the platform for the module/app. The """"""""-p"""""""" works fine. The """"""""--platform"""""""" options works fine for other commands like """"""""ti build"""""""" and """"""""ti clean"""""""" Steps to Reproduce: 1. In the terminal run the CLI command """"""""ti create --type app --platform android"""""""" Actual Result: The CLI prompts for selecting the target platform, even though a valid platform was mentioned in the command Expected Result: The --platform option should work for """"""""ti create"""""""" command""""",title+description
