TIMOB-17201,12,"""Android: """"Genymotion.enabled"""" should be set to true by default ""","""""""h5. Description:  Currently, we have to set genymotion.enabled to true manually in """"""""ti.config"""""""" command in CLI to enable genymotion. If you don't , you don't see the genymotion emulator's.     Since we are officially supporting genymotion from 3.3.0 this flag should be set to true by default. """"""",Improvement,"Title: Android: """"Genymotion.enabled"""" should be set to true by default
Description: """"h5. Description: Currently, we have to set genymotion.enabled to true manually in """"""""ti.config"""""""" command in CLI to enable genymotion. If you don't , you don't see the genymotion emulator's. Since we are officially supporting genymotion from 3.3.0 this flag should be set to true by default. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17200,12,"""MobileWeb: DatePicker 'change' event does not fire when clicking on the calendar""","""""""h2. Description  When changing the date in the DatePicker in MobileWeb, the 'change' event is not fired when clicking on the calendar.    h2. Code      h2. Test case  1. Click on the date picker (event will fire)  2. Click on the arrow to show the calendar, and pick a date (no event fired)  3. Click on the arrow again and event will fire now""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: DatePicker 'change' event does not fire when clicking on the calendar
Description: """"h2. Description When changing the date in the DatePicker in MobileWeb, the 'change' event is not fired when clicking on the calendar. h2. Code h2. Test case 1. Click on the date picker (event will fire) 2. Click on the arrow to show the calendar, and pick a date (no event fired) 3. Click on the arrow again and event will fire now""""",title+description
TIMOB-17198,12,"""Android: Closing Titanium app on Android 4.4.3 will show previous app""","""""""h4. Problem Description  Closing a titanium app on Android 4.4.3 will lead to the previous app from the task switcher showing up for a short time.     h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create new app (classic titanium)  2. Using Mobile SDK 3.3.0.RC  3. Use the default project (two tabs)  4. Install it on a device with 4.4.3  5. Do this:  *  home screen  *    opening camera app  *    closing camera app  *    home screen  *    opening titanium app  *    closing titanium app  *    camera app shows up shortly  *    home screen    h4. Extra information  QA Link: http://developer.<USER>com/question/175386/android-443-closing-ti-app-will-show-previous-app""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Closing Titanium app on Android 4.4.3 will show previous app
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Closing a titanium app on Android 4.4.3 will lead to the previous app from the task switcher showing up for a short time. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create new app (classic titanium) 2. Using Mobile SDK 3.3.0.RC 3. Use the default project (two tabs) 4. Install it on a device with 4.4.3 5. Do this: * home screen * opening camera app * closing camera app * home screen * opening titanium app * closing titanium app * camera app shows up shortly * home screen h4. Extra information QA Link: http://developer.<USER>com/question/175386/android-443-closing-ti-app-will-show-previous-app""""",title+description
