TIMOB-17191,12,"""CLI: """"ti build"""" command doesn't ask for project directory in Windows""","""""""*ti build* command should prompt for project directory if the current directory doesn't contain the tiapp.xml file.  In windows, Cursor blinks and waits indefinitely without any output message when we run """"""""ti build -p android* command. (Please refer attachment win.png)    h5. Steps To Reproduce:   1. Open the command prompt and navigate it to desktop as current directory. (make sure there is no tiapp.xml file in desktop)   2. run *ti build -p android*    h5. Actual Result:  Cursor  will blinks and waits indefinitely.     h5. Expected Result:  CLI should prompt with following message      Note:   *cli.prompt = true* is correctly set in titanium configuration.   This is *not a regression* since it is reproducible in SDK 3.2.3 GA as well.  Issue does *not occur* in Mac OSX (see attachment Mac.png)""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"ti build"""" command doesn't ask for project directory in Windows
Description: """"*ti build* command should prompt for project directory if the current directory doesn't contain the tiapp.xml file. In windows, Cursor blinks and waits indefinitely without any output message when we run """"""""ti build -p android* command. (Please refer attachment win.png) h5. Steps To Reproduce: 1. Open the command prompt and navigate it to desktop as current directory. (make sure there is no tiapp.xml file in desktop) 2. run *ti build -p android* h5. Actual Result: Cursor will blinks and waits indefinitely. h5. Expected Result: CLI should prompt with following message Note: *cli.prompt = true* is correctly set in titanium configuration. This is *not a regression* since it is reproducible in SDK 3.2.3 GA as well. Issue does *not occur* in Mac OSX (see attachment Mac.png)""""",title+description
