TIMOB-17144,12,"""Native module zip not automatically extracting in project folder""","""""""h2. problem    I'm seeing this same issue as in TIMOB-15714, but when putting the module zip in the local project root folder. The zip file is being ignored and I'm getting an error like this:        If I move the zipped module to the global modules folder, {{~/Library/Application Support/Titanium}} in my case, the module extracts automatically on build and works just fine.     h2. expected    A zipped native module in my project folder should automatically extract when I execute {{ti build}}    h2. actual    The native module is not extracted and I encounter a build error    h2. test    This case is the same as the case in TIMOB-15714, with only the location of the native module changed.    # create an app in either Studio or CLI  # add any module to tiapp.xml  # place module zip file in the newly created project's folder  # build app for any platform/target  # encounter the error listed in the {{problem}} section""""""",Bug,"Title: Native module zip not automatically extracting in project folder
Description: """"h2. problem I'm seeing this same issue as in TIMOB-15714, but when putting the module zip in the local project root folder. The zip file is being ignored and I'm getting an error like this: If I move the zipped module to the global modules folder, {{~/Library/Application Support/Titanium}} in my case, the module extracts automatically on build and works just fine. h2. expected A zipped native module in my project folder should automatically extract when I execute {{ti build}} h2. actual The native module is not extracted and I encounter a build error h2. test This case is the same as the case in TIMOB-15714, with only the location of the native module changed. # create an app in either Studio or CLI # add any module to tiapp.xml # place module zip file in the newly created project's folder # build app for any platform/target # encounter the error listed in the {{problem}} section""""",title+description
TIMOB-17142,12,"""Android: ListView crashes after using .replaceSectionAt() several times""","""""""h6.Issue description  I'm building an amortisation calculator as part of a financial calculator app.      Since amortization tables are fairly lengthy, I'm using a ListView with two different versions of the ListView data to simulate a list expansion effect.  On itemclick, .replaceSectionAt() is called to replace a section of the summarized list with data from another object.  Any open section is replaced again with the summarized version.      This is working flawlessly on iOS, but crashes after several clicks on Android 4.4.2.  Testing on older Android versions causes an immediate crash.  The console returns the error:        The error can be replicated by clicking on """"""""Show more"""""""" in the app several times on an Android device.    Alloy Sample: https://www.dropbox.com/s/hdsudc0mkiw1fzr/list-view-crash-app.zip""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ListView crashes after using .replaceSectionAt() several times
Description: """"h6.Issue description I'm building an amortisation calculator as part of a financial calculator app. Since amortization tables are fairly lengthy, I'm using a ListView with two different versions of the ListView data to simulate a list expansion effect. On itemclick, .replaceSectionAt() is called to replace a section of the summarized list with data from another object. Any open section is replaced again with the summarized version. This is working flawlessly on iOS, but crashes after several clicks on Android 4.4.2. Testing on older Android versions causes an immediate crash. The console returns the error: The error can be replicated by clicking on """"""""Show more"""""""" in the app several times on an Android device. Alloy Sample: https://www.dropbox.com/s/hdsudc0mkiw1fzr/list-view-crash-app.zip""""",title+description
TIMOB-17140,12,"""TiAPI : MediaPlayer don't speak chinese/korean/japanese""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce First  Use this url : http://translate.google.com/translate_tts?tl=ja&q=%E3%81%93%E3%82%93%E3%81%AB%E3%81%A1%E3%81%AF (Hello in japanese) In your Chrome browser. it's ok.  But if you use it with the media player with  ti.media.player { url : http://translate.google.com/translate_tts?tl=ja&q=%E3%81%93%E3%82%93%E3%81%AB%E3%81%A1%E3%81%AF }  You will heard something, but it's no japan but some noise :)  It doesn't work with chinese,arabic,japanese but work with latina langage and russia.   h3. Actual Result Some noise  h3. Expected Result The same voice as in your browser.""""""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI : MediaPlayer don't speak chinese/korean/japanese
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce First Use this url : http://translate.google.com/translate_tts?tl=ja&q=%E3%81%93%E3%82%93%E3%81%AB%E3%81%A1%E3%81%AF (Hello in japanese) In your Chrome browser. it's ok. But if you use it with the media player with ti.media.player { url : http://translate.google.com/translate_tts?tl=ja&q=%E3%81%93%E3%82%93%E3%81%AB%E3%81%A1%E3%81%AF } You will heard something, but it's no japan but some noise :) It doesn't work with chinese,arabic,japanese but work with latina langage and russia. h3. Actual Result Some noise h3. Expected Result The same voice as in your browser.""""",title+description
