TIMOB-17113,12,"""iOS: APSHTTPClient should provide documentation""","""""""APSHTTPClient should provide documentation in the form of a short user guide with examples. See, for example, http://cocoadocs.org/docsets/AFNetworking/""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: APSHTTPClient should provide documentation
Description: """"APSHTTPClient should provide documentation in the form of a short user guide with examples. See, for example, http://cocoadocs.org/docsets/AFNetworking/""""",title+description
TIMOB-17112,12,"""iOS: APSHTTPClient model objects should be immutable.""","""""""APSHTTPClient model objects should be immutable (they are currently mutable). This standard engineering practice provides these benefits:    1. Automatic thread safety.  2. Easier to reason about.  3. Easier to maintain since there are no class/object invariants when mutating from one state to another.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: APSHTTPClient model objects should be immutable.
Description: """"APSHTTPClient model objects should be immutable (they are currently mutable). This standard engineering practice provides these benefits: 1. Automatic thread safety. 2. Easier to reason about. 3. Easier to maintain since there are no class/object invariants when mutating from one state to another.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17111,12,"""iOS: APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLResponse""","""""""APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLResponse. Apple's docs, videos and examples consistently demonstrate and recommend that a url response should be immutable, and that readonly properties should be added to NSURLRequest via subclassing. Additionally, the url response should only include the metadata of the server's response and not the actual data - these two concepts are independent and should be modeled independently (they are currently clubbed together).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLResponse
Description: """"APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLResponse. Apple's docs, videos and examples consistently demonstrate and recommend that a url response should be immutable, and that readonly properties should be added to NSURLRequest via subclassing. Additionally, the url response should only include the metadata of the server's response and not the actual data - these two concepts are independent and should be modeled independently (they are currently clubbed together).""""",title+description
TIMOB-17110,12,"""iOS: APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLRequest""","""""""APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLRequest. Apple's docs, videos and examples consistently demonstrate and recommend that a url request should be immutable, and that readonly properties should be added to NSURLRequest via custom categories.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLRequest
Description: """"APSHTTPClient should not wrap NSURLRequest. Apple's docs, videos and examples consistently demonstrate and recommend that a url request should be immutable, and that readonly properties should be added to NSURLRequest via custom categories.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17109,12,"""iOS: APSHTTPClient should use liberal and consistent logging that follows standard iOS logging practices""","""""""APSHTTPClient should use liberal and consistent logging that follows standard iOS logging practices. It currently uses multiple logging macros in an inconsistent manner. Also the logging is sparse and generally unhelpful.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: APSHTTPClient should use liberal and consistent logging that follows standard iOS logging practices
Description: """"APSHTTPClient should use liberal and consistent logging that follows standard iOS logging practices. It currently uses multiple logging macros in an inconsistent manner. Also the logging is sparse and generally unhelpful.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17108,12,"""iOS: APSHTTPClient should have its design and implementation peer reviewed""","""""""APSHTTPClient should have its design and implementation peer reviewed. Publishing a new library that is a dependency for <USER>projects should undergo critical peer review. Characteristics that such a library should be held to account for are:    1. If it is going to do things different than Apple, then it needs to make the case that convinces a jury of its peers for why it is better.  2. It needs to compare and contrast itself with other respected open source libraries that provide similar functionality that convinces a jury of its peers for why it is better.     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: APSHTTPClient should have its design and implementation peer reviewed
Description: """"APSHTTPClient should have its design and implementation peer reviewed. Publishing a new library that is a dependency for <USER>projects should undergo critical peer review. Characteristics that such a library should be held to account for are: 1. If it is going to do things different than Apple, then it needs to make the case that convinces a jury of its peers for why it is better. 2. It needs to compare and contrast itself with other respected open source libraries that provide similar functionality that convinces a jury of its peers for why it is better. """"",title+description
