Description: """"h5. To reproduce 1. Create the default app and build for BB device or Simulator h5. Actual result h5. Expected result The app should be built and run successfully""""",title+description
TIMOB-17057,12,"""iOS: HTTPClient - responseText is not cleared between two requests""","""""""I use the HTTPClient to retrieve new tweets.    Since 3.3.0, it seems that the responseText prepends the previous value to the new one, so my JSON parser crashes the app.    At the first launch, here's what I get:  bq. {""""""""tweets"""""""":[{""""""""tweet"""""""":{""""""""text"""""""":""""""""Our friends @felttip_band have a new single and it's a great one again ! Hooked by the whistling https://t.co/6Wt1vkVhEs"""""""",""""""""created_time"""""""":""""""""20140507112956"""""""",""""""""guid"""""""":""""""""463973998452170752""""""""}}]}    But if I try to refresh, here's what I get:  bq. {""""""""tweets"""""""":[{""""""""tweet"""""""":{""""""""text"""""""":""""""""Our friends @felttip_band have a new single and it's a great one again ! Hooked by the whistling https://t.co/6Wt1vkVhEs"""""""",""""""""created_time"""""""":""""""""20140507112956"""""""",""""""""guid"""""""":""""""""463973998452170752""""""""}}]}{""""""""tweets"""""""":[]}    As you can see, the correct response (empty array) is at the end, but the previous value is still there...    This does not happen with SDK 3.2.3.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: HTTPClient - responseText is not cleared between two requests
Description: """"I use the HTTPClient to retrieve new tweets. Since 3.3.0, it seems that the responseText prepends the previous value to the new one, so my JSON parser crashes the app. At the first launch, here's what I get: bq. {""""""""tweets"""""""":[{""""""""tweet"""""""":{""""""""text"""""""":""""""""Our friends @felttip_band have a new single and it's a great one again ! Hooked by the whistling https://t.co/6Wt1vkVhEs"""""""",""""""""created_time"""""""":""""""""20140507112956"""""""",""""""""guid"""""""":""""""""463973998452170752""""""""}}]} But if I try to refresh, here's what I get: bq. {""""""""tweets"""""""":[{""""""""tweet"""""""":{""""""""text"""""""":""""""""Our friends @felttip_band have a new single and it's a great one again ! Hooked by the whistling https://t.co/6Wt1vkVhEs"""""""",""""""""created_time"""""""":""""""""20140507112956"""""""",""""""""guid"""""""":""""""""463973998452170752""""""""}}]}{""""""""tweets"""""""":[]} As you can see, the correct response (empty array) is at the end, but the previous value is still there... This does not happen with SDK 3.2.3.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17056,12,"""CLI: --sdk argument doesn't override SDK version set in tiapp.xml""","""""""Re-opening this as a feature request. I need to be able to specify the SDK version via the command line so that I can test various configurations and SDKs.    As I read [the CLI docs|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Titanium_Command-Line_Interface_Reference-section-35619828_TitaniumCommand-LineInterfaceReference-GenericBuildOptionsandFlags], I should be able to override the SDK version set in tiapp.xml by adding the {{--sdk}} argument to the {{ti build}} command. However, doing so has no effect.        Tested with CLI 3.2.3 (release) and 3.3.0-beta    I've tried {{ti build -p ios --sdk 3.4.0}} and it likewise has no effect. So, it doesn't seem to be that you can override only one way (ie. to force using a newer SDK). It doesn't override either way.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: --sdk argument doesn't override SDK version set in tiapp.xml
Description: """"Re-opening this as a feature request. I need to be able to specify the SDK version via the command line so that I can test various configurations and SDKs. As I read [the CLI docs|http://docs.<USER>com/platform/latest/#!/guide/Titanium_Command-Line_Interface_Reference-section-35619828_TitaniumCommand-LineInterfaceReference-GenericBuildOptionsandFlags], I should be able to override the SDK version set in tiapp.xml by adding the {{--sdk}} argument to the {{ti build}} command. However, doing so has no effect. Tested with CLI 3.2.3 (release) and 3.3.0-beta I've tried {{ti build -p ios --sdk 3.4.0}} and it likewise has no effect. So, it doesn't seem to be that you can override only one way (ie. to force using a newer SDK). It doesn't override either way.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17055,12,"""Android: if there are several consecutive alert windows, the latest alert window replaces previous alert windows""","""""""Alert window replaces the previous alert windows if there are multiple consecutive alert windows.  For example: following code prints only last alert window.     *Actual Result:* Only alert('3.Hi') is visible in the device  *Expected Result:* It should show all 3 alerts as stacks.   It's not the regression since issue occurs in 3.2.3 GA as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: if there are several consecutive alert windows, the latest alert window replaces previous alert windows
Description: """"Alert window replaces the previous alert windows if there are multiple consecutive alert windows. For example: following code prints only last alert window. *Actual Result:* Only alert('3.Hi') is visible in the device *Expected Result:* It should show all 3 alerts as stacks. It's not the regression since issue occurs in 3.2.3 GA as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17054,12,"""Android: Changing device timezone realtime does not alter time""","""""""h5. Problem description    When I display the date/time localized for my timezone it does not update if I change the timezone on the device while the app is running. It maintains the old timezone. This causes the time portion (and possibly the day) to not change as expected.    h5. Test Code          h5. Step to reproduces:    1) Set timezone of device to Pacific  2) Run the app  3) Tap """"""""Now"""""""" button  4) Note that the top date string is localized to Pacific timezone  5) Do not kill the app  6) Open device settings  7) Change timezone to Eastern  8) Go back to app  9) Tap """"""""Now"""""""" button  10) Force close the app and relaunch  11) Tap """"""""Now""""""""    h5. Expected Result   The top localized date string displays in Easter time (3 hours ahead)    h5. Result:   The date time still reflect a Pacific timezone *HOWEVER* the displayed timezone is Eastern. The displayed timezone code is just information. It had no bearing on the date time localization.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Changing device timezone realtime does not alter time
Description: """"h5. Problem description When I display the date/time localized for my timezone it does not update if I change the timezone on the device while the app is running. It maintains the old timezone. This causes the time portion (and possibly the day) to not change as expected. h5. Test Code h5. Step to reproduces: 1) Set timezone of device to Pacific 2) Run the app 3) Tap """"""""Now"""""""" button 4) Note that the top date string is localized to Pacific timezone 5) Do not kill the app 6) Open device settings 7) Change timezone to Eastern 8) Go back to app 9) Tap """"""""Now"""""""" button 10) Force close the app and relaunch 11) Tap """"""""Now"""""""" h5. Expected Result The top localized date string displays in Easter time (3 hours ahead) h5. Result: The date time still reflect a Pacific timezone *HOWEVER* the displayed timezone is Eastern. The displayed timezone code is just information. It had no bearing on the date time localization. """"",title+description
