TIMOB-17049,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Building app does not remove older versions""","""""""h5.Description  When you run 'ti build' for Windows Hybrid, it will install your application without first uninstalling your old version.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Create a Windows Hybrid application  2. Run 'ti build -p mobileweb -C xd -T wp8'  3. When the app closes, press the hardware back button  4. Run 'ti build -p mobileweb -C xd -T wp8' again    h5.Expected Result  Build script should uninstall the old application and install the new application    h5.Actual Result  Keeps all versions of the application as well as adding the new application. """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Building app does not remove older versions
Description: """"h5.Description When you run 'ti build' for Windows Hybrid, it will install your application without first uninstalling your old version. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Create a Windows Hybrid application 2. Run 'ti build -p mobileweb -C xd -T wp8' 3. When the app closes, press the hardware back button 4. Run 'ti build -p mobileweb -C xd -T wp8' again h5.Expected Result Build script should uninstall the old application and install the new application h5.Actual Result Keeps all versions of the application as well as adding the new application. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17047,12,"""iOS: HTTPClient callbacks are not triggered for synchronous  request""","""""""HTTPClient callbacks are not triggered when HTTPClient synchronous requests. Following callbacks are tested and not triggered in SDK 3.3.0.v20140528144113.   Callbacks  1. onload  2. onerror  3. onreadystatechange  4. onsendstream    It's a *regression* since it doesn't happen in 3.2.3 GA.     *Steps to reproduce:*   1. Run the application with the code below.   2. Check the alert dialogs from the callbacks.    *Actual Result:* Alert box are not showing for any callbacks for the synchronous requests. It works for asynchronous requests.    *Expected Result:* callbacks should work for both synchronous and asynchronous requests.      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: HTTPClient callbacks are not triggered for synchronous request
Description: """"HTTPClient callbacks are not triggered when HTTPClient synchronous requests. Following callbacks are tested and not triggered in SDK 3.3.0.v20140528144113. Callbacks 1. onload 2. onerror 3. onreadystatechange 4. onsendstream It's a *regression* since it doesn't happen in 3.2.3 GA. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Run the application with the code below. 2. Check the alert dialogs from the callbacks. *Actual Result:* Alert box are not showing for any callbacks for the synchronous requests. It works for asynchronous requests. *Expected Result:* callbacks should work for both synchronous and asynchronous requests. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17046,12,"""CLI: Analytics fails to send if event data greater than 8KB""","""""""With the introduction of TIMOB-16617, we can now collect Titanium API usage, however the data generated is greater than 8KB which is causing issues when forking the analytics send <USER>    The Titanium CLI needs to move the sending of analytics from the {{<USER>on('exit')}} event to a callback that is fired after the command finishes.    We also need to rework node-appc's analytics library so that the parent <USER>writes the analytics events to disk, then forks the analytics send <USER>with the minimal amount of data.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Analytics fails to send if event data greater than 8KB
Description: """"With the introduction of TIMOB-16617, we can now collect Titanium API usage, however the data generated is greater than 8KB which is causing issues when forking the analytics send <USER> The Titanium CLI needs to move the sending of analytics from the {{<USER>on('exit')}} event to a callback that is fired after the command finishes. We also need to rework node-appc's analytics library so that the parent <USER>writes the analytics events to disk, then forks the analytics send <USER>with the minimal amount of data.""""",title+description
