Description: """"When OTHER_CFLAGS are defined in module.xcconfig they are only applied to Release builds. This issue makes it very hard to test my module in an app, and users of my module are confused as to why they only works in Release builds.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17029,12,"""iOS: Webview: Loading spinner shows after orientation change even when webview has incorrect URL""","""""""When a webview URL is an incorrect one and webview fires an error event. Then a loading spinner starts to show if the orientation of the device is changed afterwards.    This is not a regression. The issue exists atleast as back as 3.1.3.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run the application  2. Click on """"""""Open Invalid URL"""""""" button  3. The webView error event fires and shows an alert. Dismiss the alert. No loading icon is shown.  4. Change the orientation of the device    Actual Result:  On orientation change, a loading spinner starts to show up    Expected Result:  The loading spinner should not show up after change of orientation    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Webview: Loading spinner shows after orientation change even when webview has incorrect URL
Description: """"When a webview URL is an incorrect one and webview fires an error event. Then a loading spinner starts to show if the orientation of the device is changed afterwards. This is not a regression. The issue exists atleast as back as 3.1.3. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the application 2. Click on """"""""Open Invalid URL"""""""" button 3. The webView error event fires and shows an alert. Dismiss the alert. No loading icon is shown. 4. Change the orientation of the device Actual Result: On orientation change, a loading spinner starts to show up Expected Result: The loading spinner should not show up after change of orientation """"",title+description
TIMOB-17028,12,"""iOS: ListView delete event returning incorrect data""","""""""h3. Issue    In iOS when using the property """"""""canEdit:true"""""""" in a template and deleting a row to catch the """"""""delete event"""""""" the data received is from the listView state after the user action,  even when the documentation mention that this information will return the data from before the user action.    """"""""Note that the sectionIndex and itemIndex properties of this event correspond to the List View state before the user action.""""""""    h3. Steps to repro    1. Open the test case  2. Swipe on any of the rows  3. Click the delete button    Expected Result:    The alert will show the information of the row that has been deleted.    Actual Result:    The alert shows the information form the row that takes the position of the deleted row.    h3. Sample Code        h3. Documentation  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-event-delete""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ListView delete event returning incorrect data
Description: """"h3. Issue In iOS when using the property """"""""canEdit:true"""""""" in a template and deleting a row to catch the """"""""delete event"""""""" the data received is from the listView state after the user action, even when the documentation mention that this information will return the data from before the user action. """"""""Note that the sectionIndex and itemIndex properties of this event correspond to the List View state before the user action."""""""" h3. Steps to repro 1. Open the test case 2. Swipe on any of the rows 3. Click the delete button Expected Result: The alert will show the information of the row that has been deleted. Actual Result: The alert shows the information form the row that takes the position of the deleted row. h3. Sample Code h3. Documentation http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListView-event-delete""""",title+description
TIMOB-17027,12,"""iOS: The webview reloads on being removed and re-add to a window""","""""""The webview reloads when re-added to a window after being removed.    This is a regression as the issue does not occur on 3.2.3. Also the issue does not occur on Android.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run the application   2. Click on the """"""""remove and add webview"""""""" button   3. Click on the """"""""remove and release and add webview"""""""" button    Actual Result:  The webview gets loaded at all the three steps. The alert """"""""The webview is loaded"""""""" is shown on all the three steps    Expected Result:  The load event of webview should not be called when it is simply removed and re-added.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: The webview reloads on being removed and re-add to a window
Description: """"The webview reloads when re-added to a window after being removed. This is a regression as the issue does not occur on 3.2.3. Also the issue does not occur on Android. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the application 2. Click on the """"""""remove and add webview"""""""" button 3. Click on the """"""""remove and release and add webview"""""""" button Actual Result: The webview gets loaded at all the three steps. The alert """"""""The webview is loaded"""""""" is shown on all the three steps Expected Result: The load event of webview should not be called when it is simply removed and re-added. """"",title+description
TIMOB-17024,12,"""iOS Profiling on device fails consistently with iOS7.1 & Instruments 5.1""","""""""1. I created a default Alloy application from within <USER>Studio (by default using the 3.2.2.GA SDK)  2. The app is then built to a device connected to the computer using the 7.1 iOS SDK  3. Launch Instruments  4. Select Device and Attach the app you have just built as the target    Your app launches on the device and begins to start profiling in Instruments. Depending on the version of the SDK you have used to build the app, it will either stay stuck on the splash page OR the first page of your app loads.    In the case that the first page shows, you can not interact with any of the elements on the screen, which is not the correct behaviour.    Another side effect here is that there is no """"""""Leak"""""""" information only Allocation information returned.    The desired behaviour is that after attaching the app to instruments is that you can interact with your app as it records and displays performance/memory information.    There is another ticket that raises a similar issue https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15215     This is a current blocker for us.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Profiling on device fails consistently with iOS7.1 & Instruments 5.1
Description: """"1. I created a default Alloy application from within <USER>Studio (by default using the 3.2.2.GA SDK) 2. The app is then built to a device connected to the computer using the 7.1 iOS SDK 3. Launch Instruments 4. Select Device and Attach the app you have just built as the target Your app launches on the device and begins to start profiling in Instruments. Depending on the version of the SDK you have used to build the app, it will either stay stuck on the splash page OR the first page of your app loads. In the case that the first page shows, you can not interact with any of the elements on the screen, which is not the correct behaviour. Another side effect here is that there is no """"""""Leak"""""""" information only Allocation information returned. The desired behaviour is that after attaching the app to instruments is that you can interact with your app as it records and displays performance/memory information. There is another ticket that raises a similar issue https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15215 This is a current blocker for us.""""",title+description
TIMOB-17022,12,"""KitchenSink: Controls > Text Area > Basic > Blur event doesn't fire""","""""""KitchenSink: Controls -> Text Area -> Basic ->Blur event does not fire    Steps to reproduce:  1 .Reach out to KitchenSink: Controls -> Text Area -> Basic  2. Click Blur    Expected:  Blur event should fire and Message on left corner will be """"""""Blur fired, value=I am a text area"""""""" """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Controls > Text Area > Basic > Blur event doesn't fire
Description: """"KitchenSink: Controls -> Text Area -> Basic ->Blur event does not fire Steps to reproduce: 1 .Reach out to KitchenSink: Controls -> Text Area -> Basic 2. Click Blur Expected: Blur event should fire and Message on left corner will be """"""""Blur fired, value=I am a text area"""""""" """"",title+description
