TIMOB-16960,12,"""CLI: Rearchitect to analytics to allow atomic events and only one process to send payload""","""""""Whenever an analytics event is generated, it is persisted to disk until the event has successfully been sent to the server. The problem is that all events are written to the same json file. This will cause issues when more than one analytics <USER>is being run at the same time.    So we solve this by writing events to separate files as well as creating a pid file that only allows one <USER>to send analytics at a time.    FYI, these changes take place in node-appc.""""""",Improvement,"Title: CLI: Rearchitect to analytics to allow atomic events and only one process to send payload
Description: """"Whenever an analytics event is generated, it is persisted to disk until the event has successfully been sent to the server. The problem is that all events are written to the same json file. This will cause issues when more than one analytics <USER>is being run at the same time. So we solve this by writing events to separate files as well as creating a pid file that only allows one <USER>to send analytics at a time. FYI, these changes take place in node-appc.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16958,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Detect PowerShell permissions""","""""""Windows Hybrid winstore builds requires PowerShell scripts and if the execution policy hasn't been set to allow PowerShell scripts, then we need to alert the error in """"""""ti info"""""""" and during """"""""ti build"""""""".""""""",Improvement,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Detect PowerShell permissions
Description: """"Windows Hybrid winstore builds requires PowerShell scripts and if the execution policy hasn't been set to allow PowerShell scripts, then we need to alert the error in """"""""ti info"""""""" and during """"""""ti build"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-16957,12,"""iOS : Opening popover on iPad breaks focus/blur events of the current window""","""""""example:  {code:title=popover.javascript|borderStyle=solid}    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();  win.addEventListener('focus', function(){      Ti.API.log('focus');  });  win.addEventListener('blur', function(){      Ti.API.log('blur');  });    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: 'Open Popover!'});  button.addEventListener('click', function(e){      popover.show({ view: button });  });  win.add(button);    var view = Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor: 'green'});  view.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({text: """"""""It's not easy being green.""""""""}));    var rightButton = Ti.UI.createButton({title: 'Robin'});  rightButton.addEventListener('click', function(e){      alert(""""""""But green's the color of spring."""""""");  });    var popover = Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover({      width: 250,      height: 100,      contentView : Ti.UI.createWindow({}),  });  popover.add(view);    win.open();  {code}  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Opening popover on iPad breaks focus/blur events of the current window
Description: """"example: {code:title=popover.javascript|borderStyle=solid} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); win.addEventListener('focus', function(){ Ti.API.log('focus'); }); win.addEventListener('blur', function(){ Ti.API.log('blur'); }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: 'Open Popover!'}); button.addEventListener('click', function(e){ popover.show({ view: button }); }); win.add(button); var view = Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor: 'green'}); view.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({text: """"""""It's not easy being green.""""""""})); var rightButton = Ti.UI.createButton({title: 'Robin'}); rightButton.addEventListener('click', function(e){ alert(""""""""But green's the color of spring.""""""""); }); var popover = Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover({ width: 250, height: 100, contentView : Ti.UI.createWindow({}), }); popover.add(view); win.open(); {code} """"",title+description
