TIMOB-16902,12,"""Android: App crashes intermittently at launch when debugging""","""""""h4.NOTE: This is an intermittent issue. I could reproduce it 4-5 times with sdk 3.2.3.v20140422101718 & once with sdk 3.2.2.GA. So I guess this is not regression.    h5. Description:  1. Create an app alloy or classic.  2. Set a breakpoint in the app for debug.  3. Debug it on device.    h5. Actual Result:  1. The app crashes and we get """"""""the app has stopped working"""""""" message.    2. Alan saw some timing issue while opening the window:      3. My console logs:      h5. Expected Result:  1. The app should not crash & successfully launch.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: App crashes intermittently at launch when debugging
Description: """"h4.NOTE: This is an intermittent issue. I could reproduce it 4-5 times with sdk 3.2.3.v20140422101718 & once with sdk 3.2.2.GA. So I guess this is not regression. h5. Description: 1. Create an app alloy or classic. 2. Set a breakpoint in the app for debug. 3. Debug it on device. h5. Actual Result: 1. The app crashes and we get """"""""the app has stopped working"""""""" message. 2. Alan saw some timing issue while opening the window: 3. My console logs: h5. Expected Result: 1. The app should not crash & successfully launch.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16901,12,"""iOS: Custom Archive location not working""","""""""h3. Issue    When setting a custom location for the archive files in Xcode and building from Studio the file is saved in the default location /Users/username/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives  instead of the new directory making the archive file unavailable for the organizer.    h3. Steps to repro    Open Xcode Preferences  Modify Archive directory in Locations to /Users/username/documents/archive  In Studio package an app for iTunes Store    Expected Results:  The .xcarchive file will be created in the custom directory /Users/username/documents/archive and will be available in the Xcode Organizer for Validation and Upload    Actual Results:  The .xcarchive file is created in the default directory /Users/username/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives  and is not available for the Xcode Organizer to be validated.    """"""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Custom Archive location not working
Description: """"h3. Issue When setting a custom location for the archive files in Xcode and building from Studio the file is saved in the default location /Users/username/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives instead of the new directory making the archive file unavailable for the organizer. h3. Steps to repro Open Xcode Preferences Modify Archive directory in Locations to /Users/username/documents/archive In Studio package an app for iTunes Store Expected Results: The .xcarchive file will be created in the custom directory /Users/username/documents/archive and will be available in the Xcode Organizer for Validation and Upload Actual Results: The .xcarchive file is created in the default directory /Users/username/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives and is not available for the Xcode Organizer to be validated. """"",title+description
