TIMOB-16898,12,"""iOS: ListView: cancelBubble = true on swipe does not prevent itemclick event from firing""","""""""On a ListView with a 'swipe' event, when cancelBubble is enabled on the  'swipe' event, it does not prevent the sequential 'itemclick' event from firing.    This issue is also documented on the following Q/A (second answer): http://developer.<USER>com/question/152014    Test:  Load the sample code and swipe left or right on a row item. Both swipe and itemclick  events are logged on the console.    Expected result:   Since the swipe event sets cancelBubble = true, the itemclick event should not be fired, and the row item should not be selected.    Use case:   A swipe event that does not trigger an itemclick can be required on some cases, like swiping a slide menu (listview) to hide it from the screen without having one of its items register a click.     app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ListView: cancelBubble = true on swipe does not prevent itemclick event from firing
Description: """"On a ListView with a 'swipe' event, when cancelBubble is enabled on the 'swipe' event, it does not prevent the sequential 'itemclick' event from firing. This issue is also documented on the following Q/A (second answer): http://developer.<USER>com/question/152014 Test: Load the sample code and swipe left or right on a row item. Both swipe and itemclick events are logged on the console. Expected result: Since the swipe event sets cancelBubble = true, the itemclick event should not be fired, and the row item should not be selected. Use case: A swipe event that does not trigger an itemclick can be required on some cases, like swiping a slide menu (listview) to hide it from the screen without having one of its items register a click. app.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-16897,12,"""Android: Ti.Platform.openURL throws Unknown Java Exception intermittently""","""""""On Android, using Ti.Platform.openURL(""""""""http://www.google.com"""""""") causes app to crash with an exception: """"""""Uncaught Error: Java Exception ocurred"""""""".  I believe it's the same issue of issue [TC-3319] .    Issue is intermittent (sometimes had to click the button 4-5 times to happen) and only happens when Window is created with """"""""exitOnClose"""""""" = true.    Managed to reproduce the issue, sample code attached.    Video (7.8mb) showing how it happened on sample: http://www.techme.com.br/download/Titanium_openURL_bug_Android_480p.mov""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.Platform.openURL throws Unknown Java Exception intermittently
Description: """"On Android, using Ti.Platform.openURL(""""""""http://www.google.com"""""""") causes app to crash with an exception: """"""""Uncaught Error: Java Exception ocurred"""""""". I believe it's the same issue of issue [TC-3319] . Issue is intermittent (sometimes had to click the button 4-5 times to happen) and only happens when Window is created with """"""""exitOnClose"""""""" = true. Managed to reproduce the issue, sample code attached. Video (7.8mb) showing how it happened on sample: http://www.techme.com.br/download/Titanium_openURL_bug_Android_480p.mov""""",title+description
TIMOB-16896,12,"""Android: Label is missing setCenter method""","""""""When trying to set the center property of a Ti.UI.Label after creation it will throw an error:  *Uncaught TypeError: Object #<Label> has no method 'setCenter'*    Here is a very simple test case to reproduce:      Docs: [Ti.UI.Label.setCenter|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Label-method-setCenter]    Q&A: [http://developer.<USER>com/question/173192/uncaught-typeerror-object-label-has-no-method-setcenter]""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Label is missing setCenter method
Description: """"When trying to set the center property of a Ti.UI.Label after creation it will throw an error: *Uncaught TypeError: Object #<Label> has no method 'setCenter'* Here is a very simple test case to reproduce: Docs: [Ti.UI.Label.setCenter|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Label-method-setCenter] Q&A: [http://developer.<USER>com/question/173192/uncaught-typeerror-object-label-has-no-method-setcenter]""""",title+description
TIMOB-16895,12,"""Add argument to accept analytics deploy type""","""""""With the introduction of VPC environments, Studio might pass in the VPC cluster environment name as the deploy-type, to channel the analytics events for a specific server.    One of the use case is that the user might want to package the app with their STAGING server environment, so that while testing their package app, they would like to receive the analytics even on their staging server, instead of production server.    So, CLI might need to add an additional argument (similar to '--build-type') to take any VPC environment name and set the analytics handler in the SDK. If this argument is not set during the build command, then CLI should fall back to using --deploy-type to assign the analytics environment type.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Add argument to accept analytics deploy type
Description: """"With the introduction of VPC environments, Studio might pass in the VPC cluster environment name as the deploy-type, to channel the analytics events for a specific server. One of the use case is that the user might want to package the app with their STAGING server environment, so that while testing their package app, they would like to receive the analytics even on their staging server, instead of production server. So, CLI might need to add an additional argument (similar to '--build-type') to take any VPC environment name and set the analytics handler in the SDK. If this argument is not set during the build command, then CLI should fall back to using --deploy-type to assign the analytics environment type.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16894,12,"""CLI should accept production value for '--deploy-type' argument while packaging iOS app""","""""""CLI accepts '--deploy-type' value as production for MobileWeb for packaging the app. However, it doesn't accept 'production' for --deploy-type argument while packaging Android and iOS apps.""""""",Improvement,"Title: CLI should accept production value for '--deploy-type' argument while packaging iOS app
Description: """"CLI accepts '--deploy-type' value as production for MobileWeb for packaging the app. However, it doesn't accept 'production' for --deploy-type argument while packaging Android and iOS apps.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16893,12,"""Android: textField and textArea enableReturnKey property not working""","""""""h3. Issue     Currently when user enables as true the property enableReturnKey in a textField or textArea in iOS the button is disabled until the value is different from null while in the case of Android is not working even when the documentation specify that the property is enabled for Android in textfield ( http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextField-property-enableReturnKey ) and textarea ( http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextArea-property-enableReturnKey ).    h3. Test Case        h3. Steps to repro    Run the app  Select the textfield  Click on the Return Key    Expected Result  The Return key will be disabled preventing the action from being executed until the textfield value is different form null.    Actual Result  The result key is enabled from start allowing user to call the action even there no value on textfield  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: textField and textArea enableReturnKey property not working
Description: """"h3. Issue Currently when user enables as true the property enableReturnKey in a textField or textArea in iOS the button is disabled until the value is different from null while in the case of Android is not working even when the documentation specify that the property is enabled for Android in textfield ( http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextField-property-enableReturnKey ) and textarea ( http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.TextArea-property-enableReturnKey ). h3. Test Case h3. Steps to repro Run the app Select the textfield Click on the Return Key Expected Result The Return key will be disabled preventing the action from being executed until the textfield value is different form null. Actual Result The result key is enabled from start allowing user to call the action even there no value on textfield """"",title+description
TIMOB-16892,12,"""Android: """"Error posting events: Connect to /54.214.252.38:443 timed out"""" when app sends analytic events, was seen once & is not reproducible""","""""""h4.NOTE: This issue was seen once & was not reproducible again. Opening this ticket case just in case we see this issue later.    h5. Description:  1. Create a normal 2 tabbed app.  2. Build & run it on an android device.  3. Look at the studio logs. After 30 seconds the app will send you the analytics events.    h5. Actual Result:  1. We get error regarding analytics in the studio logs:      h5. Expected Result:  1. We should not see any timeout errors & the analytics events should be sent successfully.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: """"Error posting events: Connect to /54.214.252.38:443 timed out"""" when app sends analytic events, was seen once & is not reproducible
Description: """"h4.NOTE: This issue was seen once & was not reproducible again. Opening this ticket case just in case we see this issue later. h5. Description: 1. Create a normal 2 tabbed app. 2. Build & run it on an android device. 3. Look at the studio logs. After 30 seconds the app will send you the analytics events. h5. Actual Result: 1. We get error regarding analytics in the studio logs: h5. Expected Result: 1. We should not see any timeout errors & the analytics events should be sent successfully.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16889,12,"""Android: Adding 'resume' event to Ti.Android.currentActivity does not work with SDK >= 3.2.0""","""""""h2. Problem description  When adding the resume event to Ti.Android.currentActivity, the resume is not called when the app is resumed. This works well in SDK 3.1.3    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Use the code below  2. Run the app on Android  3. Hit the home button on the device  4. Restore the app: no alert is shown    h2. Code to reproduce      h2. Note  The same code and steps work fine on SDK 3.1.3""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Adding 'resume' event to Ti.Android.currentActivity does not work with SDK >= 3.2.0
