TIMOB-16851,12,"""CLI: force module project creation even if path already exists is not respected inside an app project""","""""""It is not a regression.    This issue occurs only if a module project is being created inside an app project.    h5. To reproduce  1. Create a project, using     Enter all prompted options  2. Inside the project's directory run    Enter all prompted options  3. Run     use same id and name    h5. Actual result      Note:  If a module project created outside an app project, force to create option works as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: force module project creation even if path already exists is not respected inside an app project
Description: """"It is not a regression. This issue occurs only if a module project is being created inside an app project. h5. To reproduce 1. Create a project, using Enter all prompted options 2. Inside the project's directory run Enter all prompted options 3. Run use same id and name h5. Actual result Note: If a module project created outside an app project, force to create option works as expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16850,12,"""Android: Are force stopped applications supposed to receive push notifications?""","""""""The customer is claiming that their app used to still receive applications after it was """"""""Force Stopped"""""""" in Android's App Info. Right now the app no longer receives applications if it has been force stopped.    h3. Expected by Customer  1. Subscribe to push notifications  2. Force Stop in Android's App Info view  3. App continues to receive push notifications    h3. What actually happens  1. Subscribe to push notificatios  2. Force Stop in Android's App Info view  3. App no longer receives push notifications    Is the customer wrong or did we used to support this?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Are force stopped applications supposed to receive push notifications?
Description: """"The customer is claiming that their app used to still receive applications after it was """"""""Force Stopped"""""""" in Android's App Info. Right now the app no longer receives applications if it has been force stopped. h3. Expected by Customer 1. Subscribe to push notifications 2. Force Stop in Android's App Info view 3. App continues to receive push notifications h3. What actually happens 1. Subscribe to push notificatios 2. Force Stop in Android's App Info view 3. App no longer receives push notifications Is the customer wrong or did we used to support this?""""",title+description
