TIMOB-16847,12,"""Mobile web(Win 8): Black area renders when a text field gains focus""","""""""Sample App: https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/54185251/TextFieldTest.zip     1.- Run the sample application on a windows device (internet explorer)   2.- Focus the 1st text field, then focus the 2nd one, then 3rd one, and then the 4th one.   3.- Observe how the black area's height seems to increase as you focus the four text fields on the screen; at this point, when the 4th text field has the focus on it, the screen is practically all black.     Expected Result: The window scrolls up on each focus and reveals the following objects on the view.    Actual Result: The window scrolls up but fails to render data previously blocked by the keyboard, creating a large black box. """"""",Bug,"Title: Mobile web(Win 8): Black area renders when a text field gains focus
Description: """"Sample App: https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/54185251/TextFieldTest.zip 1.- Run the sample application on a windows device (internet explorer) 2.- Focus the 1st text field, then focus the 2nd one, then 3rd one, and then the 4th one. 3.- Observe how the black area's height seems to increase as you focus the four text fields on the screen; at this point, when the 4th text field has the focus on it, the screen is practically all black. Expected Result: The window scrolls up on each focus and reveals the following objects on the view. Actual Result: The window scrolls up but fails to render data previously blocked by the keyboard, creating a large black box. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16846,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Windows Phone 8.1 not detected by CLI""","""""""h5.Description  Windows 8.1 Developer Preview is available for developers. The Titanium CLI does not detect this new phone OS, therefore blocking the user from building Windows Hybrid applications to device    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Install the latest 8.1 phone update  2. Run 'ti info'  3. Create and build a Windows Hybrid Application to the device    h5.Expected Result  Phone should be detected, application should also be built to device.    h5.Actual Result  Phone is not detected, cannot build to device.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Windows Phone 8.1 not detected by CLI
Description: """"h5.Description Windows 8.1 Developer Preview is available for developers. The Titanium CLI does not detect this new phone OS, therefore blocking the user from building Windows Hybrid applications to device h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Install the latest 8.1 phone update 2. Run 'ti info' 3. Create and build a Windows Hybrid Application to the device h5.Expected Result Phone should be detected, application should also be built to device. h5.Actual Result Phone is not detected, cannot build to device.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16845,12,"""iOS: WebView: Add contentInsets property""","""""""Request:    To take advantage of the translucent properties of the window's nav bar, as well as the Toolbar control, it would be great to have contentInsets added to the WebView control.     This should allow web content to scroll below translucent nav bars and Tolbars, yet fully show the content below the nav bar (or above a bottom toolbar) when the top scroll (or bottom) is reached.     The Safari app features this effect in iOS 7.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: WebView: Add contentInsets property
Description: """"Request: To take advantage of the translucent properties of the window's nav bar, as well as the Toolbar control, it would be great to have contentInsets added to the WebView control. This should allow web content to scroll below translucent nav bars and Tolbars, yet fully show the content below the nav bar (or above a bottom toolbar) when the top scroll (or bottom) is reached. The Safari app features this effect in iOS 7.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16844,12,"""iOS: SearchBar focused in ScrollView, scrolling does not work""","""""""Symptom:  You have a ScrollView with a SearchBar inside. When a SearchBar is the first text input that is focused, the keyboard will cover up the ScrollView, and not scroll any differently than if the keyboard was not displayed.    Expected:  The ScrollView should resize itself to the available space on the screen, allowing for scrolling if necessary.    Workaround:  None that are acceptable. You can put whitespace at the end of your ScrollView content, but that's a poor user experience.    {code:xml|title=index.xml}  <Alloy>   <Window backgroundColor=""""""""#fff"""""""">    <ScrollView top=""""""""0"""""""" bottom=""""""""0"""""""" left=""""""""0"""""""" right=""""""""0"""""""" layout=""""""""vertical"""""""">     <Label id=""""""""justAddingSpace"""""""" text=""""""""Click here to hide keyboard"""""""" height=""""""""400"""""""" width=""""""""200"""""""" bottom=""""""""10"""""""" color=""""""""#fff"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""#C00"""""""" onClick=""""""""doBlur""""""""/>     <TextField id=""""""""myTextField"""""""" width=""""""""250"""""""" border=""""""""1"""""""" borderColor=""""""""#000""""""""></TextField>     <SearchBar id=""""""""mySearchBar"""""""" top=""""""""10"""""""" bottom=""""""""10"""""""" height=""""""""50""""""""></SearchBar>     <Button id=""""""""btn"""""""" title=""""""""Button At The End"""""""" bottom=""""""""20"""""""" onClick=""""""""doBlur""""""""/>    </ScrollView>   </Window>  </Alloy>  {code}    {code:javascript|title=index.js}  var doBlur = function() {   $.myTextField.blur();   $.mySearchBar.blur();  };    $.index.open();  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: SearchBar focused in ScrollView, scrolling does not work
Description: """"Symptom: You have a ScrollView with a SearchBar inside. When a SearchBar is the first text input that is focused, the keyboard will cover up the ScrollView, and not scroll any differently than if the keyboard was not displayed. Expected: The ScrollView should resize itself to the available space on the screen, allowing for scrolling if necessary. Workaround: None that are acceptable. You can put whitespace at the end of your ScrollView content, but that's a poor user experience. {code:xml|title=index.xml} <Alloy> <Window backgroundColor=""""""""#fff""""""""> <ScrollView top=""""""""0"""""""" bottom=""""""""0"""""""" left=""""""""0"""""""" right=""""""""0"""""""" layout=""""""""vertical""""""""> <Label id=""""""""justAddingSpace"""""""" text=""""""""Click here to hide keyboard"""""""" height=""""""""400"""""""" width=""""""""200"""""""" bottom=""""""""10"""""""" color=""""""""#fff"""""""" backgroundColor=""""""""#C00"""""""" onClick=""""""""doBlur""""""""/> <TextField id=""""""""myTextField"""""""" width=""""""""250"""""""" border=""""""""1"""""""" borderColor=""""""""#000""""""""></TextField> <SearchBar id=""""""""mySearchBar"""""""" top=""""""""10"""""""" bottom=""""""""10"""""""" height=""""""""50""""""""></SearchBar> <Button id=""""""""btn"""""""" title=""""""""Button At The End"""""""" bottom=""""""""20"""""""" onClick=""""""""doBlur""""""""/> </ScrollView> </Window> </Alloy> {code} {code:javascript|title=index.js} var doBlur = function() { $.myTextField.blur(); $.mySearchBar.blur(); }; $.index.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-16843,12,"""CLI: create command should allow names to begin with a number""","""""""You should be able to create an app that has a name beginning with a number.    """"""",Story,"Title: CLI: create command should allow names to begin with a number
Description: """"You should be able to create an app that has a name beginning with a number. """"",title+description
