TIMOB-16840,12,"""Android: Webview with '_.template' rendered HTML not displayed""","""""""h5. Problem description  In the Dynamic Styling Alloy sample https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/advanced/dynamic_styling , in the 'rawStyle' window, there is a webView whose html content is rendered using the Underscore.js '_.template' utility:        Alloy.Globals.htmlTemplate (in app/alloy.js):      If no targetSdkVersion is specified or if a targetSdkVersion specified is greater than 13, running the sample on Android using the latest SDK (3.2.3.v20140403105720), the Webview is not visible.  Is correctly visible using 3.2.2.GA on both iOS and Android.    h5. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new Alloy project and import the Alloy sample code https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/advanced/dynamic_styling (or get the attached project)  2. Run on Android and click on 'Raw Style Modules'  Result: second webView (<WebView id=""""""""styleArray"""""""" height=""""""""800dp""""""""/>) is not visible.     3. Edit tiapp.xml, add the following and run on Android:      Result: the webView is now correctly displayed    4. Edit tiapp.xml, add the following and run on Android:      Result: Webview is no longer displayed.      5. Edit tiapp.xml, switch to SDK 3.2.2.GA, use any targetSdkVersion (from 11 to 19) and run on device:  Result: webview is always correctly displayed. It seems to be a regression on the SDK (also no changes made on Alloy).      Attached screenshots for comparison between a displayed and not-displayed webview.      h5. Note  If using Jake to import the Alloy sample project, it works fine as in this case an Harness template with targetSdkVersion='11' is being used.  If using the default new app tiapp.xml file (with no targetSdkVersion being specified in the manifest), the sample webview is not visible.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Webview with '_.template' rendered HTML not displayed
Description: """"h5. Problem description In the Dynamic Styling Alloy sample https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/advanced/dynamic_styling , in the 'rawStyle' window, there is a webView whose html content is rendered using the Underscore.js '_.template' utility: Alloy.Globals.htmlTemplate (in app/alloy.js): If no targetSdkVersion is specified or if a targetSdkVersion specified is greater than 13, running the sample on Android using the latest SDK (3.2.3.v20140403105720), the Webview is not visible. Is correctly visible using 3.2.2.GA on both iOS and Android. h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new Alloy project and import the Alloy sample code https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/advanced/dynamic_styling (or get the attached project) 2. Run on Android and click on 'Raw Style Modules' Result: second webView (<WebView id=""""""""styleArray"""""""" height=""""""""800dp""""""""/>) is not visible. 3. Edit tiapp.xml, add the following and run on Android: Result: the webView is now correctly displayed 4. Edit tiapp.xml, add the following and run on Android: Result: Webview is no longer displayed. 5. Edit tiapp.xml, switch to SDK 3.2.2.GA, use any targetSdkVersion (from 11 to 19) and run on device: Result: webview is always correctly displayed. It seems to be a regression on the SDK (also no changes made on Alloy). Attached screenshots for comparison between a displayed and not-displayed webview. h5. Note If using Jake to import the Alloy sample project, it works fine as in this case an Harness template with targetSdkVersion='11' is being used. If using the default new app tiapp.xml file (with no targetSdkVersion being specified in the manifest), the sample webview is not visible.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16839,12,"""Android: When the textField has the autocorrect set in false certain keyboard types are not shown""","""""""h3. Issue    On Android versions 4.2 and 4.4 when the textfield has the autocorrect parameter as false some of the keyboard typed will not be displayed, Customer has reported that everything works ok on 4.0.X and during testing we confirmed that in older versions (Android 2.3.5) works correctly.    h3. Steps to repro    - Run the test case  - Focus on each of the 4 textfields to show the keyboard    Expected Results:  Autocorrect Decimal will show the Decimal Pad keyboard.  Autocorrect Email will show the Email keyboard.  Autocorrect False Url will show the Url keyboard.  Autocorrect True Url will show Url Pad keyboard.    Actual Results:  Autocorrect Decimal shows the Decimal Pad keyboard.  Autocorrect Email does not show the Email keyboard.  Autocorrect False Url does not show the Url keyboard.  Autocorrect True Url shows the Url Pad keyboard.    h3. Test Case    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: When the textField has the autocorrect set in false certain keyboard types are not shown
Description: """"h3. Issue On Android versions 4.2 and 4.4 when the textfield has the autocorrect parameter as false some of the keyboard typed will not be displayed, Customer has reported that everything works ok on 4.0.X and during testing we confirmed that in older versions (Android 2.3.5) works correctly. h3. Steps to repro - Run the test case - Focus on each of the 4 textfields to show the keyboard Expected Results: Autocorrect Decimal will show the Decimal Pad keyboard. Autocorrect Email will show the Email keyboard. Autocorrect False Url will show the Url keyboard. Autocorrect True Url will show Url Pad keyboard. Actual Results: Autocorrect Decimal shows the Decimal Pad keyboard. Autocorrect Email does not show the Email keyboard. Autocorrect False Url does not show the Url keyboard. Autocorrect True Url shows the Url Pad keyboard. h3. Test Case """"",title+description
TIMOB-16837,12,"""TiAPI: Add property to support Inverted ListView (similar to Skype)""","""""""I would like to make my list growing from bottom to top (like Skype messages view). It could be done manually, but not completely, because list is built to grow from up to down.  Loading more items (view chat history) would work crappy this way because of following things:  1) setMarker  (according to documentation) Fired when the list view displays the reference item or an item BEYOND the reference item. So it's not possible to track when should loadmore be fired (if I set marker on top item). Having 'scroll' event for ListView solves this problem (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-14317)  2) appending items to list: items are appended, but the scroll position remains constant, relatively to TOP of list. Thus, the list content """"""""jumps"""""""" up.    I would be great to have an 'invert' property for ListView control or at least to be able to configure those things I listed above (BEYOND or BEFORE, TOP or BOTTOM).""""""",Improvement,"Title: TiAPI: Add property to support Inverted ListView (similar to Skype)
Description: """"I would like to make my list growing from bottom to top (like Skype messages view). It could be done manually, but not completely, because list is built to grow from up to down. Loading more items (view chat history) would work crappy this way because of following things: 1) setMarker (according to documentation) Fired when the list view displays the reference item or an item BEYOND the reference item. So it's not possible to track when should loadmore be fired (if I set marker on top item). Having 'scroll' event for ListView solves this problem (https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-14317) 2) appending items to list: items are appended, but the scroll position remains constant, relatively to TOP of list. Thus, the list content """"""""jumps"""""""" up. I would be great to have an 'invert' property for ListView control or at least to be able to configure those things I listed above (BEYOND or BEFORE, TOP or BOTTOM).""""",title+description
TIMOB-16836,12,"""Parity: Android -  Log messages lost when logging commands are placed in a loop""","""""""Using the default titanium project and the attachment, there is no correct output in the console.  It does work on iOS.    h5. To reproduce:  1. Create the Titanium project.  2. Add the attached app.js  3. Run on Android device and check the log.    h5. Expected results:  All console output should be shown filtered based on settings.      h5. Actual results:  Console output missing lines from the looped log calls.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Parity: Android - Log messages lost when logging commands are placed in a loop
Description: """"Using the default titanium project and the attachment, there is no correct output in the console. It does work on iOS. h5. To reproduce: 1. Create the Titanium project. 2. Add the attached app.js 3. Run on Android device and check the log. h5. Expected results: All console output should be shown filtered based on settings. h5. Actual results: Console output missing lines from the looped log calls. """"",title+description
