TIMOB-16829,12,"""BlackBerry: Setting analytics to false in the tiapp.xml causes the application to crash and force close""","""""""h5.Description  Having analytics set to true in the tiapp.xml causes no error, and analytical data is sent and received properly.  However, setting it to false crashes the application whenever an event is sent (e.g, featureEvent)    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Download the attached project  2. Set analytics to false in the tiapp.xml  3. Run the project on blackberry device  4. Select featureEvent    h5.Expected Result  Nothing should happen, no analytics should be sent and the app should continue running.    h5.Actual Result  Application crashes and closes""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Setting analytics to false in the tiapp.xml causes the application to crash and force close
Description: """"h5.Description Having analytics set to true in the tiapp.xml causes no error, and analytical data is sent and received properly. However, setting it to false crashes the application whenever an event is sent (e.g, featureEvent) h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Download the attached project 2. Set analytics to false in the tiapp.xml 3. Run the project on blackberry device 4. Select featureEvent h5.Expected Result Nothing should happen, no analytics should be sent and the app should continue running. h5.Actual Result Application crashes and closes""""",title+description
TIMOB-16828,12,"""BlackBerry: Implement all analytic payload events""","""""""h5.Description  All of the analytical event payloads from the documentation do not work for BlackBerry. The only one that does work is 'featureEvent'.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Add the attached code to a default project  2. Run the application on a BlackBerry device  3. Click all of the buttons.  4. Check the analytical payloads    h5.Expected Result  All event payloads should send correctly    h5.Actual Result  Only featureEvent sends data.""""""",Improvement,"Title: BlackBerry: Implement all analytic payload events
