TIMOB-16747,12,"""CLI: ti setup check fails to parse online status on Windows""","""""""h5.Description  Running ti setup check on a Windows machine outputs that the machine is not connected to the internet, even if it is.  This causes the rest of the check to fail due to it thinking it is offline.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Run `ti setup check`  2. Check the online status    h5.Expected Result  Should say online (if you are online)    h5.Actual Result  Says you are offline, even if you are actually online""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: ti setup check fails to parse online status on Windows
Description: """"h5.Description Running ti setup check on a Windows machine outputs that the machine is not connected to the internet, even if it is. This causes the rest of the check to fail due to it thinking it is offline. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Run `ti setup check` 2. Check the online status h5.Expected Result Should say online (if you are online) h5.Actual Result Says you are offline, even if you are actually online""""",title+description
TIMOB-16745,12,"""iOS: Failed to install app on device""","""""""App fails to run on device using SDK: 3.2.3.v20140326144913  Note: However we can install app using iTunes. Working fine using iOS simulator    Steps to Reproduce:  1) Create a new project using above sdk  2) Try and run it on ios device    Actual Result:        Expected:  App must run without error.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Failed to install app on device
Description: """"App fails to run on device using SDK: 3.2.3.v20140326144913 Note: However we can install app using iTunes. Working fine using iOS simulator Steps to Reproduce: 1) Create a new project using above sdk 2) Try and run it on ios device Actual Result: Expected: App must run without error.""""",title+description
