TIMOB-16712,12,"""Mobile Web: App fails to load on Windows Phone 8 (IE10) due to Ti.Filesystem calling unsupported xhr.overrideMimeType()""","""""""h5.Description  Posting a local file from an application using the following code sample results in an error.    h5.Steps To Reproduce    Add a text file called 'textfile.txt' in your resources folder.    h5.Expected Result  Should alert the user saying """"""""SUCCESS""""""""    h5.Actual Result  Throws error saying """"""""Object doesn't support property or method 'overrideMimeType' at x-wmapp0:index.html (line 4030)"""""""" """"""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web: App fails to load on Windows Phone 8 (IE10) due to Ti.Filesystem calling unsupported xhr.overrideMimeType()
Description: """"h5.Description Posting a local file from an application using the following code sample results in an error. h5.Steps To Reproduce Add a text file called 'textfile.txt' in your resources folder. h5.Expected Result Should alert the user saying """"""""SUCCESS"""""""" h5.Actual Result Throws error saying """"""""Object doesn't support property or method 'overrideMimeType' at x-wmapp0:index.html (line 4030)"""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-16710,12,"""Android: Emulators created with Android SDK-Tools 22.6.2 will not work with 3.2.2.GA SDK or lower""","""""""h5.Description  The latest Android SDK-Tools (22.6.2) causes any project with the SDK set to 3.2.2.GA or lower to fail if building to emulator.  Android devices work fine with any version of the SDK.  This means that users must either use the 3.2.3 branch, or not update their Android SDK-Tools version.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Update to Android SDK-Tools to version 22.6.2  2. Create a default emulator or let Studio create one for you  3. Set the SDK version to 3.2.2 or below  4. Build to the emulator    h5.Expected Result  Project should be installed to emulator    h5.Actual Result  Project fails to build""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Emulators created with Android SDK-Tools 22.6.2 will not work with 3.2.2.GA SDK or lower
Description: """"h5.Description The latest Android SDK-Tools (22.6.2) causes any project with the SDK set to 3.2.2.GA or lower to fail if building to emulator. Android devices work fine with any version of the SDK. This means that users must either use the 3.2.3 branch, or not update their Android SDK-Tools version. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Update to Android SDK-Tools to version 22.6.2 2. Create a default emulator or let Studio create one for you 3. Set the SDK version to 3.2.2 or below 4. Build to the emulator h5.Expected Result Project should be installed to emulator h5.Actual Result Project fails to build""""",title+description
