TIMOB-16707,12,"""Android:TableView Row height doesn't resize when multiple views are added""","""""""h2. Description  TableView Row height doesn't resize when adding multiple views. But once tableview scrolls, rows height will adjust as expected.    h2. Test Case      h2. Steps to Reproduce  1. Create a project with above sample code and run on android device  Note : Notice that top row's height is not adjusted properly at first.  2. Scroll the table view down and then again on top.  Note : Now you will notice that height is adjusted as expected.    Expected Result  Height of tableViewRow should be adjusted automatically on application launch    Actual Result  Height is not adjusted properly at first but after scrolling it gets adjusted""""""",Bug,"Title: Android:TableView Row height doesn't resize when multiple views are added
Description: """"h2. Description TableView Row height doesn't resize when adding multiple views. But once tableview scrolls, rows height will adjust as expected. h2. Test Case h2. Steps to Reproduce 1. Create a project with above sample code and run on android device Note : Notice that top row's height is not adjusted properly at first. 2. Scroll the table view down and then again on top. Note : Now you will notice that height is adjusted as expected. Expected Result Height of tableViewRow should be adjusted automatically on application launch Actual Result Height is not adjusted properly at first but after scrolling it gets adjusted""""",title+description
TIMOB-16706,12,"""Android: MapView annotation images invisible ""","""""""Some PNG images used as map annotations are not shown. There are 3 images: a solid color circle w/ a black border, 24-bit color w/ transparency. Having the images in different dimensions increases the number of """"""""dots"""""""" shown.    (The test app uses same sized images. Similar to TIMOB-16502.)""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: MapView annotation images invisible
Description: """"Some PNG images used as map annotations are not shown. There are 3 images: a solid color circle w/ a black border, 24-bit color w/ transparency. Having the images in different dimensions increases the number of """"""""dots"""""""" shown. (The test app uses same sized images. Similar to TIMOB-16502.)""""",title+description
TIMOB-16705,12,"""iOS: Orientation problem when slightly tilting forward/backward""","""""""There is a problem with """"""""orientationchange"""""""", in some cases event is fired when orientation is not changed. To see that run this example code:        You must test it on device. Hold device in hand (in vertical position) and then try to put it on the table :) (so, it goes from 90 degrees in hand to 0 degrees on table). You should be able to see white sidebar on right side - which means event is fired and orientation is wrongly set in event listener argument.      My tests have found that """"""""Ti.UI.orientation"""""""" works correctly but it's deprecated since 1.7.2 SDK.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Orientation problem when slightly tilting forward/backward
Description: """"There is a problem with """"""""orientationchange"""""""", in some cases event is fired when orientation is not changed. To see that run this example code: You must test it on device. Hold device in hand (in vertical position) and then try to put it on the table :) (so, it goes from 90 degrees in hand to 0 degrees on table). You should be able to see white sidebar on right side - which means event is fired and orientation is wrongly set in event listener argument. My tests have found that """"""""Ti.UI.orientation"""""""" works correctly but it's deprecated since 1.7.2 SDK.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16704,12,"""Android: when showing a listview with a custom template, child elements are displayed incorrectly""","""""""In an Alloy Project, when rendering a ListView with ListItems using an external Custom template, sometimes the Views contained in the vertical layout will be rendered not in proper order.     For example, if my template contains a view with a vertical layout and inside it there are two child views, view A and view B, sometimes the order of the two will change, displaying sometimes A first and then B, while other times B will be first and A will be second.    The expected behaviour should be for view A to be displayed always first and then view B should be underneath view A.    I'm supplying two images showing the expected behaviour and the unexpected behaviour, plus a test project, if the items aren't rendered as in the unexpected behaviour image close the app and try again, sometimes it happens the first time and others after 5 or 6 tries.    If the vertical layout is removed then the views overlaps on each other but which view is shown on top changes. For example, sometimes view A will be on top view B, while other times view B will be on top of view A. The expected behaviour here should be first view declared on the xml should be the one on the bottom while the last view declared on the xml should be the one on the top.    The unexpected behaviour happens at an inconsistent rate so it's hard to predict when will it happen or at least I haven't being able to pinpoint what triggers the bug. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: when showing a listview with a custom template, child elements are displayed incorrectly
Description: """"In an Alloy Project, when rendering a ListView with ListItems using an external Custom template, sometimes the Views contained in the vertical layout will be rendered not in proper order. For example, if my template contains a view with a vertical layout and inside it there are two child views, view A and view B, sometimes the order of the two will change, displaying sometimes A first and then B, while other times B will be first and A will be second. The expected behaviour should be for view A to be displayed always first and then view B should be underneath view A. I'm supplying two images showing the expected behaviour and the unexpected behaviour, plus a test project, if the items aren't rendered as in the unexpected behaviour image close the app and try again, sometimes it happens the first time and others after 5 or 6 tries. If the vertical layout is removed then the views overlaps on each other but which view is shown on top changes. For example, sometimes view A will be on top view B, while other times view B will be on top of view A. The expected behaviour here should be first view declared on the xml should be the one on the bottom while the last view declared on the xml should be the one on the top. The unexpected behaviour happens at an inconsistent rate so it's hard to predict when will it happen or at least I haven't being able to pinpoint what triggers the bug. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16703,12,"""iOS: Remove instance NavigationGroup from KitchenSink""","""""""Since class Titanium.UI.iPhone.NavigationGroup was removed, please use the Titanium.UI.iOS.NavigationWindow class instead.    /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/3298.js  /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/handheld/ios/baseui/navgroup.js  /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/main_tests.js  /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/nav_controller.js  /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/split_view_nav.js    h5.To reproduce  1. Run KS>iPhone>iPad Feature> Main Tests    h5.Actual result      Note:  Documentation http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iPhone.NavigationGroup""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Remove instance NavigationGroup from KitchenSink
Description: """"Since class Titanium.UI.iPhone.NavigationGroup was removed, please use the Titanium.UI.iOS.NavigationWindow class instead. /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/3298.js /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/handheld/ios/baseui/navgroup.js /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/main_tests.js /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/nav_controller.js /Kitchen Sink/Resources/ui/tablet/ios/baseui/split_view_nav.js h5.To reproduce 1. Run KS>iPhone>iPad Feature> Main Tests h5.Actual result Note: Documentation http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.iPhone.NavigationGroup""""",title+description
