TIMOB-16674,12,"""Android build/package: versionName loses zeros after the decimal""","""""""When publishing an app to Google Play, if the versionName has trailing zeros (e.g. 3.0, 3.10), those zeros are lost by the build <USER> so that in AndroidManifest.xml, versionName comes out as, for example, 3 instead of 3.0.    Example tiapp.xml snippet:  {panel}      <android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"""""""">          <manifest android:installLocation=""""""""auto""""""""              android:versionCode=""""""""15"""""""" android:versionName=""""""""*3.0*"""""""">  {panel}    You can see that versionName is set to """"""""3.0"""""""", a string.  In AndroidManifest.xml, you get this:  {panel}  <manifest xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"""""""" package=""""""""com.MyCompany.MyAppName"""""""" android:versionCode=""""""""15"""""""" android:versionName=""""""""*3*"""""""" android:installLocation=""""""""auto"""""""">  {panel}    I noticed that in _build.js, versionName is sometimes being treated as a  number, and sometimes as a string.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android build/package: versionName loses zeros after the decimal
Description: """"When publishing an app to Google Play, if the versionName has trailing zeros (e.g. 3.0, 3.10), those zeros are lost by the build <USER> so that in AndroidManifest.xml, versionName comes out as, for example, 3 instead of 3.0. Example tiapp.xml snippet: {panel} <android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""> <manifest android:installLocation=""""""""auto"""""""" android:versionCode=""""""""15"""""""" android:versionName=""""""""*3.0*""""""""> {panel} You can see that versionName is set to """"""""3.0"""""""", a string. In AndroidManifest.xml, you get this: {panel} <manifest xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"""""""" package=""""""""com.MyCompany.MyAppName"""""""" android:versionCode=""""""""15"""""""" android:versionName=""""""""*3*"""""""" android:installLocation=""""""""auto""""""""> {panel} I noticed that in _build.js, versionName is sometimes being treated as a number, and sometimes as a string. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16673,12,"""IOS: emoji keyboard and utf8mb4 encoding is not work with ACS""","""""""     h5. Problem Description      Emoji keyboard and utf8mb4 encoding is not working in ACS. When user tries to post smiles from IOS and store into ACS server and get back to display in Apps its not showing.       h5. Testing Environment:    Titanium SDK: 3.2.1.GA, 3.2.2.GA    Titanium CLI: 3.2.1  IOS Simulator 7.0.3  Dashboard  <USER>Studio, build: 3.2.1.201402061120  Cloud module 3.2.1     h5. Test Code          h5. Step to Reproduce     # Create a sample Ti Classic project from AppC Studio   # Add cloud   module in tiapp.xml file   # Activated <USER>service in tiapp.xml  # Add one user in dashboard.<USER>com (username: username and password: password)  # Update app.js file with test code   # Run on IOS device/simulator     # Add data text field and click create post button   # Check TableView list (smiles is not working )      h5. Expected Result   Smiles should be display in TableView properly     h5. Actual Result     Smiles will not display     Ref: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-755425/homepage    Thanks       """"""",Bug,"Title: IOS: emoji keyboard and utf8mb4 encoding is not work with ACS
Description: """" h5. Problem Description Emoji keyboard and utf8mb4 encoding is not working in ACS. When user tries to post smiles from IOS and store into ACS server and get back to display in Apps its not showing. h5. Testing Environment: Titanium SDK: 3.2.1.GA, 3.2.2.GA Titanium CLI: 3.2.1 IOS Simulator 7.0.3 Dashboard <USER>Studio, build: 3.2.1.201402061120 Cloud module 3.2.1 h5. Test Code h5. Step to Reproduce # Create a sample Ti Classic project from AppC Studio # Add cloud module in tiapp.xml file # Activated <USER>service in tiapp.xml # Add one user in dashboard.<USER>com (username: username and password: password) # Update app.js file with test code # Run on IOS device/simulator # Add data text field and click create post button # Check TableView list (smiles is not working ) h5. Expected Result Smiles should be display in TableView properly h5. Actual Result Smiles will not display Ref: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-755425/homepage Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-16672,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Downloading a file while offline crashes the app""","""""""When testing downloading a file using tiwp8.downloadFile() and your device is offline, the app crashes. We need to capture the error and properly throw an exception.    On a side note, the XHR proxy seems to report 400 bad request for all requests when offline. That may be ok, but check what other environments do when offline and perhaps throw a better error.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Downloading a file while offline crashes the app
Description: """"When testing downloading a file using tiwp8.downloadFile() and your device is offline, the app crashes. We need to capture the error and properly throw an exception. On a side note, the XHR proxy seems to report 400 bad request for all requests when offline. That may be ok, but check what other environments do when offline and perhaps throw a better error.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16671,12,"""CLI: Add tmp dir check to 'setup check'""","""""""In the 'ti setup check' command, check if the tmp dir exists and is writeable. By default, it looks for the TMPDIR, TMP, and TEMP environment vars, but if those don't exist, it will use ~/tmp. When the CLI is run as sudo and ~/tmp does not exist, then the directory is created as root and will break any command that needs to write a temp file.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Add tmp dir check to 'setup check'
Description: """"In the 'ti setup check' command, check if the tmp dir exists and is writeable. By default, it looks for the TMPDIR, TMP, and TEMP environment vars, but if those don't exist, it will use ~/tmp. When the CLI is run as sudo and ~/tmp does not exist, then the directory is created as root and will break any command that needs to write a temp file.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16670,12,"""iOS: Unable to post a status with attached photo to ACS""","""""""h5. Description:  While trying to upload a status using the sample ti.cloud app, the upload fails. See screenshot.     h5. Note:  This is a regression. It does not occur with 3.2.2.GA  This may be the same root cause as the linked ticket, so may be a duplicate    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a default Titanium classic app  2. Drop in example project from ti.cloud example folder  3. Install and launch app to an iOS device  4. Go to Users and create a user and log in  5. Press Back button to get to main menu and select """"""""Status""""""""  6. Press """"""""Create Status""""""""  7. Enter a message in the """"""""Message"""""""" field  8. Choose either Photo option and add a photo  9. Press """"""""Create""""""""    h5. Result:  The status posting will fail. See screenshot    h5. Expected Result:  The status posting succeeds and the photo plus status can be viewed on the dashboard""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Unable to post a status with attached photo to ACS
Description: """"h5. Description: While trying to upload a status using the sample ti.cloud app, the upload fails. See screenshot. h5. Note: This is a regression. It does not occur with 3.2.2.GA This may be the same root cause as the linked ticket, so may be a duplicate h5. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a default Titanium classic app 2. Drop in example project from ti.cloud example folder 3. Install and launch app to an iOS device 4. Go to Users and create a user and log in 5. Press Back button to get to main menu and select """"""""Status"""""""" 6. Press """"""""Create Status"""""""" 7. Enter a message in the """"""""Message"""""""" field 8. Choose either Photo option and add a photo 9. Press """"""""Create"""""""" h5. Result: The status posting will fail. See screenshot h5. Expected Result: The status posting succeeds and the photo plus status can be viewed on the dashboard""""",title+description
TIMOB-16659,12,"""Manifest.json should contain list of all SHAs of included projects""","""""""The current manifest.json includes the SHA of just the last github commit    However, that's not really true. It's also the sum of the github commits for:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_tizen  https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map  https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.facebook  https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.cloud  https://github.com/<USER>modules/cloudpush  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_modules/tree/master/urlSession    That should somehow be reflected here:        So the display on builds.<USER>com can be more accurate.""""""",Improvement,"Title: Manifest.json should contain list of all SHAs of included projects
Description: """"The current manifest.json includes the SHA of just the last github commit However, that's not really true. It's also the sum of the github commits for: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_tizen https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.map https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.facebook https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.cloud https://github.com/<USER>modules/cloudpush https://github.com/<USER>titanium_modules/tree/master/urlSession That should somehow be reflected here: So the display on builds.<USER>com can be more accurate.""""",title+description
