TIMOB-16626,12,"""Android: Changing the opacity into a view have a flashing loading indicator""","""""""h6.Issue description  Since Titanium Project upgraded from the 3.1.3.GA TiSDK to the 3.2.0.GA and 3.2.1.GA SDK the splash screen and/or loading indicators flicker when the app is starting up.     Sometimes the indicator is barely visible and other times the screen flickers. That sample code does reproduce the issue. It was verified (the loading indicator was made a bit larger to clarify the issue and uploaded a video here: https://www.dropbox.com/s/vp5mrhuay0h1nsu/IMG_0874.MOV    h6.Devices affected  Seems to only happen on subset of devices with Gingerbread. i.e Samsung Galaxy Note running Android 2.3.6 and Droid Razr 2.3.6.    Not reproducible on Android 4.0.X though.     h6.Steps to replicate  # Get and run sample: https://www.dropbox.com/s/vfi2gmvf7c5zknt/APP-212883_TestCase.zip  # Launch app at device  # Monitor activity indicator. From time to time the issue occurs. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Changing the opacity into a view have a flashing loading indicator
Description: """"h6.Issue description Since Titanium Project upgraded from the 3.1.3.GA TiSDK to the 3.2.0.GA and 3.2.1.GA SDK the splash screen and/or loading indicators flicker when the app is starting up. Sometimes the indicator is barely visible and other times the screen flickers. That sample code does reproduce the issue. It was verified (the loading indicator was made a bit larger to clarify the issue and uploaded a video here: https://www.dropbox.com/s/vp5mrhuay0h1nsu/IMG_0874.MOV h6.Devices affected Seems to only happen on subset of devices with Gingerbread. i.e Samsung Galaxy Note running Android 2.3.6 and Droid Razr 2.3.6. Not reproducible on Android 4.0.X though. h6.Steps to replicate # Get and run sample: https://www.dropbox.com/s/vfi2gmvf7c5zknt/APP-212883_TestCase.zip # Launch app at device # Monitor activity indicator. From time to time the issue occurs. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16624,12,"""CLI: install only feature""","""""""Would be nice to have an """"""""install-only"""""""" feature in the CLI, for the cases when we connect a new device or start a new emulator, etc, and we just want to reinstall the app on that device without rebuilding everything.  This could also help for the cases when Ti fails to install on device (I get this from time to time on iOs)    I did something like this in SugarTi :)""""""",Improvement,"Title: CLI: install only feature
Description: """"Would be nice to have an """"""""install-only"""""""" feature in the CLI, for the cases when we connect a new device or start a new emulator, etc, and we just want to reinstall the app on that device without rebuilding everything. This could also help for the cases when Ti fails to install on device (I get this from time to time on iOs) I did something like this in SugarTi :)""""",title+description
TIMOB-16623,12,"""iOS: Some annotations won't show when removing and re-adding if the annotations has a customView""","""""""I store all my annotations in an array.     When removing the array (mapview.removeAnnotations(annotationsArr)) they all disappear, but when re-adding them (mapview.addAnnotations(annotationsArr)), only a few re-appear.    They still seem to be there, since they are still """"""""clickable"""""""", but they won't show.     This only happens when using the customView property in annotations. When not using the customView, and only using the standard pins, there seems to be no problem.    app.js and a simple """"""""H"""""""" image attached.    Add the """"""""busStop.png"""""""" image to Resources\images    Testcase:  Using customView:  1. Run the app.  2. Press the Hide/Show annotations button. (The annotations disappear)  3. Press the Hide/Show annotations button again. (Only some annotations reappear)    Using standard pins:  1. Run the app.  2. Press the Hide/Show annotations button. (The annotations disappear)  3. Press the Hide/Show annotations button. (The annotations reappear)    The problem only seem to exist on iOS, using the same code works on android (Titanium SDK 3.1.3.GA).    Thanks.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Some annotations won't show when removing and re-adding if the annotations has a customView
Description: """"I store all my annotations in an array. When removing the array (mapview.removeAnnotations(annotationsArr)) they all disappear, but when re-adding them (mapview.addAnnotations(annotationsArr)), only a few re-appear. They still seem to be there, since they are still """"""""clickable"""""""", but they won't show. This only happens when using the customView property in annotations. When not using the customView, and only using the standard pins, there seems to be no problem. app.js and a simple """"""""H"""""""" image attached. Add the """"""""busStop.png"""""""" image to Resources\images Testcase: Using customView: 1. Run the app. 2. Press the Hide/Show annotations button. (The annotations disappear) 3. Press the Hide/Show annotations button again. (Only some annotations reappear) Using standard pins: 1. Run the app. 2. Press the Hide/Show annotations button. (The annotations disappear) 3. Press the Hide/Show annotations button. (The annotations reappear) The problem only seem to exist on iOS, using the same code works on android (Titanium SDK 3.1.3.GA). Thanks.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16621,12,"""iOS: Limit on number of times Ti.App.iOS.scheduleLocalNotification can be used""","""""""Scheduling 3 or more notifications with Ti.App.iOS.scheduleLocalNotification renders either no notifications or just the last one. Is there a limit on the number of notifications that can be scheduled or the frequency in which they are scheduled?  Currently using millisecond time to ensure unique id.     Sample app attached        h3. Steps to reproduce:   1. Click on schedule label three times to schedule three notifications (each has a time 15 sec from now).   2. Exit App  3. Either one, or no local notifications will appear in the notification center. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Limit on number of times Ti.App.iOS.scheduleLocalNotification can be used
Description: """"Scheduling 3 or more notifications with Ti.App.iOS.scheduleLocalNotification renders either no notifications or just the last one. Is there a limit on the number of notifications that can be scheduled or the frequency in which they are scheduled? Currently using millisecond time to ensure unique id. Sample app attached h3. Steps to reproduce: 1. Click on schedule label three times to schedule three notifications (each has a time 15 sec from now). 2. Exit App 3. Either one, or no local notifications will appear in the notification center. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16620,12,"""CLI: Add configurable source for new project templates""","""""""Currently custom templates can be built and placed in the templates folder in the root of each installed SDK.    Would like to have an entry called *paths.templates* added to the *config.json* that could be searched for custom templates (and possibly overwrite/overrule those located in the {sdk}/templates folder) when creating a new project.    This would allow large enterprise orgs to:    # share common project templates across development environments  # reduce the time to adopt a new sdk (currently requires moving custom templates to the new sdk on all systems)  # reduce required storage space caused by duplication  """"""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Add configurable source for new project templates
Description: """"Currently custom templates can be built and placed in the templates folder in the root of each installed SDK. Would like to have an entry called *paths.templates* added to the *config.json* that could be searched for custom templates (and possibly overwrite/overrule those located in the {sdk}/templates folder) when creating a new project. This would allow large enterprise orgs to: # share common project templates across development environments # reduce the time to adopt a new sdk (currently requires moving custom templates to the new sdk on all systems) # reduce required storage space caused by duplication """"",title+description
TIMOB-16618,12,"""Android: Unable to build app after update to SDK 3.2.2""","""""""h3. Issue    After upgrading to SDK 3.2.2 customer is not able to build the app receiving compiler errors related to AssetCryptImpl.java (cannot find symbol and uses unchecked or unsafe operations). During the call we try with different versions from the JDK (1.7 and 1.6) that throw the same error logs.    Other apps are being correctly builded with 3.2.1 and failing with 3.2.2, but one app created after the SDK update is not building neither in 3.2.2 or 3.2.1.       h3. Log        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Unable to build app after update to SDK 3.2.2
Description: """"h3. Issue After upgrading to SDK 3.2.2 customer is not able to build the app receiving compiler errors related to AssetCryptImpl.java (cannot find symbol and uses unchecked or unsafe operations). During the call we try with different versions from the JDK (1.7 and 1.6) that throw the same error logs. Other apps are being correctly builded with 3.2.1 and failing with 3.2.2, but one app created after the SDK update is not building neither in 3.2.2 or 3.2.1. h3. Log """"",title+description
