TIMOB-16552,12,"""Android: Table View Row alignment getting disturbed when using Class Name""","""""""h3. Issue    When using the classname in the rows the alignment starts to get disturbed and some rows get cut off, if the classname is removed the alignment works ok but customer reports a slow performance during the scroll.    h3. Test case    app.js      h3. Steps to Repro    1. Run the testcase  2. Scrolldown the tableview    Expected Results: The rows should look correctly aligned and completely visible.    Actual Results: Some of the rows are cut off and extra space is added in others.    h3. Testing    When removing the class name the rows work as expected. Also this issue is not present on SDK 3.1.3 and prior      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Table View Row alignment getting disturbed when using Class Name
Description: """"h3. Issue When using the classname in the rows the alignment starts to get disturbed and some rows get cut off, if the classname is removed the alignment works ok but customer reports a slow performance during the scroll. h3. Test case app.js h3. Steps to Repro 1. Run the testcase 2. Scrolldown the tableview Expected Results: The rows should look correctly aligned and completely visible. Actual Results: Some of the rows are cut off and extra space is added in others. h3. Testing When removing the class name the rows work as expected. Also this issue is not present on SDK 3.1.3 and prior """"",title+description
TIMOB-16551,12,"""Android: Third party Java library in a module fails to compile in App""","""""""h3. Issue    While working into the integration of a module that includes a third party java library into an app customer receives some error logs related to the mfacoreframework.jar library and the absence of an associated EnclosingMethod attribute while compiling Android classes.dex    After testing with the sample module provided we notice the error is not present anymore in SDK 3.2.X.GA, customer has confirmed this and that the module works correctly but the project they are working is developed and built in 3.1.3.GA     h3. Console Log        h3. Steps to repro    1. Download the moduleTestApp  2. Run the App with SDK 3.1.3  3. Check the log for the compile Error from the library  4. Run the App with SDK 3.2  5. There will be no compile error from the library  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Third party Java library in a module fails to compile in App
Description: """"h3. Issue While working into the integration of a module that includes a third party java library into an app customer receives some error logs related to the mfacoreframework.jar library and the absence of an associated EnclosingMethod attribute while compiling Android classes.dex After testing with the sample module provided we notice the error is not present anymore in SDK 3.2.X.GA, customer has confirmed this and that the module works correctly but the project they are working is developed and built in 3.1.3.GA h3. Console Log h3. Steps to repro 1. Download the moduleTestApp 2. Run the App with SDK 3.1.3 3. Check the log for the compile Error from the library 4. Run the App with SDK 3.2 5. There will be no compile error from the library """"",title+description
TIMOB-16550,12,"""Android: Button title shifts to the left when Texfield is focus""","""""""h3. Issue    Customer is using textfields and a button to create a simple form in their project and after they focus on any of the textfield elements the button shifts the title align from center to left.    Tested and reproduce by customer in HTC Ruby with Android 4.0.3 and     h3. Testing    After testing we have found this behavior appears to be be present on Android versions under 4.3    Test and reproduced by support at:    Sony LT 22i  Android 4.1.2    While testing this issue is not reproducible with devices:    Samsung Galaxy S4  Android 4.3    Nexus 7  Android 4.4    h3. Sample Code        h3. Steps to repro    1. Run the test case  2. Focus on a textfield  3. Close the keyboard    After this the button title will be aligned to the left.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Button title shifts to the left when Texfield is focus
Description: """"h3. Issue Customer is using textfields and a button to create a simple form in their project and after they focus on any of the textfield elements the button shifts the title align from center to left. Tested and reproduce by customer in HTC Ruby with Android 4.0.3 and h3. Testing After testing we have found this behavior appears to be be present on Android versions under 4.3 Test and reproduced by support at: Sony LT 22i Android 4.1.2 While testing this issue is not reproducible with devices: Samsung Galaxy S4 Android 4.3 Nexus 7 Android 4.4 h3. Sample Code h3. Steps to repro 1. Run the test case 2. Focus on a textfield 3. Close the keyboard After this the button title will be aligned to the left. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16549,12,"""Android: Crash when hintText value is numeric ""","""""""h5. Problem Description    Apps will crash when we set hint text to a numeric value in textbox after opening window.      Looks like error is from:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIText.java#L233    h5. Test Environment    Ti SDK 3.2.1.GA  Ti CLI 3.2.1  Android 4.4.2     h5. Test Code  index.xml      index.js            h5. Steps to reproduce:      # Create new allow project 3.2.1.GA  # Update test code to index.js and index.xml file    # Launch in android; press label 'throw error'        h3. Error Logs        h3. Explanation of Error:  http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8973381/why-cannot-cast-integer-to-string-in-java    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Crash when hintText value is numeric
Description: """"h5. Problem Description Apps will crash when we set hint text to a numeric value in textbox after opening window. Looks like error is from: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIText.java#L233 h5. Test Environment Ti SDK 3.2.1.GA Ti CLI 3.2.1 Android 4.4.2 h5. Test Code index.xml index.js h5. Steps to reproduce: # Create new allow project 3.2.1.GA # Update test code to index.js and index.xml file # Launch in android; press label 'throw error' h3. Error Logs h3. Explanation of Error: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8973381/why-cannot-cast-integer-to-string-in-java """"",title+description
TIMOB-16548,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Error while building the application for winstore""","""""""Error is shown during the build <USER>of an application for winstore target. The build stage of the <USER>happens successfully and .appxupload file is also created. However, an error is reported during the <USER>of installing and launching of application.    The issue occurs on the latest CI build. The issue did not occur on previous CI build of SDk (3.2.1.v20140206172952 (Windows Hybrid))    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create a default classic/alloy application  2. Build the application for winstore    Actual result:  An error is shown during the build <USER> Please find the attached logs    Expected Result:  There should not be any error shown when building an application for winstore.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Error while building the application for winstore
Description: """"Error is shown during the build <USER>of an application for winstore target. The build stage of the <USER>happens successfully and .appxupload file is also created. However, an error is reported during the <USER>of installing and launching of application. The issue occurs on the latest CI build. The issue did not occur on previous CI build of SDk (3.2.1.v20140206172952 (Windows Hybrid)) Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a default classic/alloy application 2. Build the application for winstore Actual result: An error is shown during the build <USER> Please find the attached logs Expected Result: There should not be any error shown when building an application for winstore.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16547,12,"""iOS: Add ability to set color and backgroundColor for Picker control""","""""""The backgroundColor of the Picker control on iOS is hardcoded to white:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIPicker.m#L64    This becomes a problem when designing dark themed apps, that would need to reverse the colors of the picker (light colored text over dark background).    Ideally, color and backgroundColor should be exposed through properties of the Ti Picker control.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Add ability to set color and backgroundColor for Picker control
Description: """"The backgroundColor of the Picker control on iOS is hardcoded to white: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIPicker.m#L64 This becomes a problem when designing dark themed apps, that would need to reverse the colors of the picker (light colored text over dark background). Ideally, color and backgroundColor should be exposed through properties of the Ti Picker control.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16546,12,"""MobileWeb: ActivityIndicator does not animate properly on Firefox browser""","""""""Animation does not work for activity indicator when using MobileWeb on Firefox. This is due to the setTimeout delay being too short.    This is fixed in this pull request:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/4968""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: ActivityIndicator does not animate properly on Firefox browser
Description: """"Animation does not work for activity indicator when using MobileWeb on Firefox. This is due to the setTimeout delay being too short. This is fixed in this pull request: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/4968""""",title+description
TIMOB-16545,12,"""MobileWeb: AlertDialog message property, accepted value varies by platform""","""""""ENVIRONMENT:  Studio and SDK 3.2.1.GA  Android API Level 10, Genymotion Emulator  Android API Level 16, Genymotion Emulator  iOS 7.0.3 / Xcode 5.0.2  Chrome Version 32.0.1700.107    REPRODUCTION:  Run the test code below on the Android emulator, iOS simulator and in a browser, then click on each button.    EXPECTED RESULTS:  Each message should be similar.    ACTUAL RESULTS:  Android cannot stringify the array values, Mobile Web cannot stringify the object value, but iOS can stringify both.    MORE INFO:  Note that the current documentation says that only a string value is accepted:  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-message    Perhaps the type should be enforced rather than allow other types to be passed in.    TEST CODE:  """"""",Improvement,"Title: MobileWeb: AlertDialog message property, accepted value varies by platform
Description: """"ENVIRONMENT: Studio and SDK 3.2.1.GA Android API Level 10, Genymotion Emulator Android API Level 16, Genymotion Emulator iOS 7.0.3 / Xcode 5.0.2 Chrome Version 32.0.1700.107 REPRODUCTION: Run the test code below on the Android emulator, iOS simulator and in a browser, then click on each button. EXPECTED RESULTS: Each message should be similar. ACTUAL RESULTS: Android cannot stringify the array values, Mobile Web cannot stringify the object value, but iOS can stringify both. MORE INFO: Note that the current documentation says that only a string value is accepted: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-property-message Perhaps the type should be enforced rather than allow other types to be passed in. TEST CODE: """"",title+description
