TIMOB-16541,12,"""iOS: System is issuing two alerts in a rapid fire style when location services are off on device ""","""""""h2. Description  When user has location services off the system is issuing alerts in a rapid fire style and fade off.     First alert saying:  Location Services disabled  You currently have all location services for this device disabled.If you proceed, you will be asked to confirm whether location services should be reenabled.    Second alert saying:  Turn on location services to determine your location.  with 'settings' and 'cancel' button    h2. Test code  Please find the attached app.js""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: System is issuing two alerts in a rapid fire style when location services are off on device
Description: """"h2. Description When user has location services off the system is issuing alerts in a rapid fire style and fade off. First alert saying: Location Services disabled You currently have all location services for this device disabled.If you proceed, you will be asked to confirm whether location services should be reenabled. Second alert saying: Turn on location services to determine your location. with 'settings' and 'cancel' button h2. Test code Please find the attached app.js""""",title+description
TIMOB-16540,12,"""iOS7: TableViewRow: leftImage property renders improper image alignment""","""""""iOS7: TableViewRow: leftImage property renders improper image allignment.  It works fine on iOS 6 device(iPOD touch iOS:6.1.3). Issue also occurs on 3.2.1.GA,3.2.0.GA sdk    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the below app.      Expected:  left image in tableviewrow should be properly alligned.    Actual:  left image overlaps with the label. Screenshots are attached for iOS7 and iOS:6 devices.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: TableViewRow: leftImage property renders improper image alignment
Description: """"iOS7: TableViewRow: leftImage property renders improper image allignment. It works fine on iOS 6 device(iPOD touch iOS:6.1.3). Issue also occurs on 3.2.1.GA,3.2.0.GA sdk Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the below app. Expected: left image in tableviewrow should be properly alligned. Actual: left image overlaps with the label. Screenshots are attached for iOS7 and iOS:6 devices. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16538,12,"""Android: Analytics crashes App intermittently onResume""","""""""From time to time, when the application is resumed, it does not start. The logcat reveals a stacktrace leading to the Analytics module. Seems like this has been already reported  http://developer.<USER>com/question/156480/application-crashes-after-a-period-in-the-background-including-services    I will try to workaround it by catching the exception, hoping that there are no other dependencies""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Analytics crashes App intermittently onResume
Description: """"From time to time, when the application is resumed, it does not start. The logcat reveals a stacktrace leading to the Analytics module. Seems like this has been already reported http://developer.<USER>com/question/156480/application-crashes-after-a-period-in-the-background-including-services I will try to workaround it by catching the exception, hoping that there are no other dependencies""""",title+description
TIMOB-16537,12,"""iOS: Titanium performs full rebuild after 3.2.0.GA""","""""""The scenario is as follows:  1. I build a project without any modules, everything ok.  2. I add a custom module and build again. This module requires to import external libs on the XCode project. The build fails as the libs are not there.  3. I open the XCode proj, add the libs.  4. Build from titanium again: now I get that it has to perform a full rebuild and XCode looses the references of the libs! Build fails.    Before 3.2 (and on ios 7 instead of iOS 7.03) step 4 was not doing a full rebuild of the project""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium performs full rebuild after 3.2.0.GA
Description: """"The scenario is as follows: 1. I build a project without any modules, everything ok. 2. I add a custom module and build again. This module requires to import external libs on the XCode project. The build fails as the libs are not there. 3. I open the XCode proj, add the libs. 4. Build from titanium again: now I get that it has to perform a full rebuild and XCode looses the references of the libs! Build fails. Before 3.2 (and on ios 7 instead of iOS 7.03) step 4 was not doing a full rebuild of the project""""",title+description
TIMOB-16536,12,"""MobileWeb: Image """"load"""" event does not fire due to incorrect context""","""""""Mobile web Image.js does not fire """"""""load"""""""" event due to incorrect """"""""this"""""""" context on the callback""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Image """"load"""" event does not fire due to incorrect context
Description: """"Mobile web Image.js does not fire """"""""load"""""""" event due to incorrect """"""""this"""""""" context on the callback""""",title+description
TIMOB-16535,12,"""MobileWeb: Button.js issue with missing font property and inconsisent treatment of whitespace characters in title""","""""""On Mobile Web Buttons have two deficiencies.    1. Buttons are missing a font property, so you can't change the font size or face.  2. Buttons do not treat leading spaces in the """"""""title"""""""" the same as other platforms. HTML ignores the spaces, so button.title = """"""""   Some Text"""""""" would be treated as if it were button.title = """"""""Some Text"""""""". This is not true on Android or iOS    I'm combining these as I have a fix I'll submit as a pull request.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Button.js issue with missing font property and inconsisent treatment of whitespace characters in title
Description: """"On Mobile Web Buttons have two deficiencies. 1. Buttons are missing a font property, so you can't change the font size or face. 2. Buttons do not treat leading spaces in the """"""""title"""""""" the same as other platforms. HTML ignores the spaces, so button.title = """""""" Some Text"""""""" would be treated as if it were button.title = """"""""Some Text"""""""". This is not true on Android or iOS I'm combining these as I have a fix I'll submit as a pull request.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16534,12,"""MobileWeb: MouseWheel does not work on MobileWeb, Firefox and IE""","""""""Mousewheel code is developed to only support chrome and safari. Does not contain the correct code for Firefox or IE.    Fixed in this pull request:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/4968""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: MouseWheel does not work on MobileWeb, Firefox and IE
Description: """"Mousewheel code is developed to only support chrome and safari. Does not contain the correct code for Firefox or IE. Fixed in this pull request: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/4968""""",title+description
TIMOB-16533,12,"""Android: Button does not resize image to fit within boundaries""","""""""If you create a button view with an image:      if the image is taller than 40, it will be cropped, rather than scale to fit in the available space. This isn't really an issue on iOS, as there are only two image size choices, but on Android, a 2x (XHDPI) image may be chosen, even if the interface is scaled by some other method. Thus the image may be cropped.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Button does not resize image to fit within boundaries
Description: """"If you create a button view with an image: if the image is taller than 40, it will be cropped, rather than scale to fit in the available space. This isn't really an issue on iOS, as there are only two image size choices, but on Android, a 2x (XHDPI) image may be chosen, even if the interface is scaled by some other method. Thus the image may be cropped. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16532,12,"""TiAPI: Provide a consolidated Social API""","""""""Right now Facebook is its own module.  There is also ACS.  However, the configuration for ACS and things like twitter vs. facbook vs. Pintrest is disjointed and or incomplete.  At the same time, you have third party modules in the marketplace that attempt to consolidate these services and simplify them.  However, they are at an additional cost, not supported, usually not able to be tested, and come with varying degrees of documentation.  An all-in-one social module that consolidates all of those services and simply asks for your relevant credentials while hiding much of the complexity would add a lot of power to the community.  There are some examples of this in the marketplace - many of which could be improved.  I think it would be a huge addition to the Studio functionality in today's connected world.""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Provide a consolidated Social API
Description: """"Right now Facebook is its own module. There is also ACS. However, the configuration for ACS and things like twitter vs. facbook vs. Pintrest is disjointed and or incomplete. At the same time, you have third party modules in the marketplace that attempt to consolidate these services and simplify them. However, they are at an additional cost, not supported, usually not able to be tested, and come with varying degrees of documentation. An all-in-one social module that consolidates all of those services and simply asks for your relevant credentials while hiding much of the complexity would add a lot of power to the community. There are some examples of this in the marketplace - many of which could be improved. I think it would be a huge addition to the Studio functionality in today's connected world.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16531,12,"""Android: Animation transform does not work with SDK 3.2.0 and later versions""","""""""Hello there,    While doing development I have found some bugs related to Android 4.3 and earlier Support. Please see the screencast to get more details:  http://www.screencast.com/t/otYiOr6j.    There are three devices used when producing the screencast (from left to right):     1. Android 4.4.2 and TiSDK 3.2.1.  2. Android 4.1.1 and TiSDK 3.2.1  3. Android 4.3 and TiSDK 3.1.3  The screen resolution of all enumerated devices is 1280x800 160dpi.    As it was mentioned above, the screencast shows the problems connected to Android 4.3 and earlier versions support. In the video you will see the so called “wheel” component. This component gets frozen after some time of being used on  Android 4.1.1 and TiSDK 3.2.1.     Also, the video demonstrates the general problem for Android 4.4.2 and Android 4.1.1, such as non-working rotate method of 2DMatrix class in the """"""""touchmove"""""""" event (you will see switching done between the images for TiSDK3.2.1 without animation, while moving finger (mouse-pointer) on screen) and  wheel rotating to a random angle, after that the lost focus of the window with wheel is shown). Actually, TiSDK 3.1.3 is free from these bugs.    Moreover, please note that  Android 4.4.2 and TiSDK 3.2.1 are working slower than Android 4.1.1 and TiSDK 3.2.1. This bug is more evident for TiSDK  3.1.3 and earlier.    Please see the demo app as an attachment. Feel free to ask additional questions.      Best regards,      <USER><USER> VELVETECH, LLC  www.velvetech.com  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Animation transform does not work with SDK 3.2.0 and later versions
Description: """"Hello there, While doing development I have found some bugs related to Android 4.3 and earlier Support. Please see the screencast to get more details: http://www.screencast.com/t/otYiOr6j. There are three devices used when producing the screencast (from left to right): 1. Android 4.4.2 and TiSDK 3.2.1. 2. Android 4.1.1 and TiSDK 3.2.1 3. Android 4.3 and TiSDK 3.1.3 The screen resolution of all enumerated devices is 1280x800 160dpi. As it was mentioned above, the screencast shows the problems connected to Android 4.3 and earlier versions support. In the video you will see the so called “wheel” component. This component gets frozen after some time of being used on Android 4.1.1 and TiSDK 3.2.1. Also, the video demonstrates the general problem for Android 4.4.2 and Android 4.1.1, such as non-working rotate method of 2DMatrix class in the """"""""touchmove"""""""" event (you will see switching done between the images for TiSDK3.2.1 without animation, while moving finger (mouse-pointer) on screen) and wheel rotating to a random angle, after that the lost focus of the window with wheel is shown). Actually, TiSDK 3.1.3 is free from these bugs. Moreover, please note that Android 4.4.2 and TiSDK 3.2.1 are working slower than Android 4.1.1 and TiSDK 3.2.1. This bug is more evident for TiSDK 3.1.3 and earlier. Please see the demo app as an attachment. Feel free to ask additional questions. Best regards, <USER><USER> VELVETECH, LLC www.velvetech.com """"",title+description
TIMOB-16530,12,"""Android: setActive tab is not working""","""""""h5. Problem Description     setActive method is not working in tabgroup. It displays an error “Invalid tab index”.    h5. Test Environment    Mac OX X 10.9.2  Ti SDK 3.1.3.GA, 3.2.0.GA, 3.2.1.GA  Ti CLI 3.2.1  Android 2.3.3    h5. Test Code         h5. Step to reproduce     # Create ti sample project in titanium classic  # Update app.js file with sample code   # Run on android device/emulator   # Check console log for error     h5. Expected Result    Tab 2 will select when app is run.    h5. Actual result     Tab 1 selected.    h5. Logs          h5. Workaround Code           Thanks  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: setActive tab is not working
Description: """"h5. Problem Description setActive method is not working in tabgroup. It displays an error “Invalid tab index”. h5. Test Environment Mac OX X 10.9.2 Ti SDK 3.1.3.GA, 3.2.0.GA, 3.2.1.GA Ti CLI 3.2.1 Android 2.3.3 h5. Test Code h5. Step to reproduce # Create ti sample project in titanium classic # Update app.js file with sample code # Run on android device/emulator # Check console log for error h5. Expected Result Tab 2 will select when app is run. h5. Actual result Tab 1 selected. h5. Logs h5. Workaround Code Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-16529,12,"""Need to remove all warnings when project is opened in Xcode""","""""""Steps to reproduce are:  - create a new project in <USER>Studio with iOS as the target.  - build the project for simulator  = browse to build folder and open the xcode project in xcode.    - run the project.  You will see around 40 warnings there.  Most can be corrected with modification to the output files, while others refer to deprecation.     URGENCY:  - we need a clean version of the SDK that eliminates as many warnings as possible.  No warnings is preferred, but the rule for customer is under 10.  If some cannot be removed, we need explanation.       Let me know if you have any questions""""""",Bug,"Title: Need to remove all warnings when project is opened in Xcode
Description: """"Steps to reproduce are: - create a new project in <USER>Studio with iOS as the target. - build the project for simulator = browse to build folder and open the xcode project in xcode. - run the project. You will see around 40 warnings there. Most can be corrected with modification to the output files, while others refer to deprecation. URGENCY: - we need a clean version of the SDK that eliminates as many warnings as possible. No warnings is preferred, but the rule for customer is under 10. If some cannot be removed, we need explanation. Let me know if you have any questions""""",title+description
