TIMOB-16495,12,"""TiAPI: Remove <fullscreen> from default tiapp.xml and deprecate in docs""","""""""I had a discussion lately on FlowDock with Tim Poulson about the {{<fullscreen>}} element in {{tiapp.xml}} and we both came to the conclusion that this element is iOS-only and does exactly the same as setting {{UIStatusBarHidden}} in the {{<ios>}} section.    If this is indeed true then:    - The element should be removed from the [default tiapp.xml|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/support/all/tiapp.xml].  - The [docs|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference-section-29004921_tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-fullscreen] should list {{<fullscreen>}} under *Deprecated elements*.""""""",Improvement,"Title: TiAPI: Remove <fullscreen> from default tiapp.xml and deprecate in docs
Description: """"I had a discussion lately on FlowDock with Tim Poulson about the {{<fullscreen>}} element in {{tiapp.xml}} and we both came to the conclusion that this element is iOS-only and does exactly the same as setting {{UIStatusBarHidden}} in the {{<ios>}} section. If this is indeed true then: - The element should be removed from the [default tiapp.xml|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/support/all/tiapp.xml]. - The [docs|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference-section-29004921_tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-fullscreen] should list {{<fullscreen>}} under *Deprecated elements*.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16492,12,"""Android: Not able to capture intent data from a Notification created from Background service""","""""""h6.Issue description  I am using a simple background service to create a notification. The notification intent has extra data to it, and is then fired. The notification is displayed in the status bar. I pull down the bar and my app is opened/resumed. I try to read the intent data, but it appears as if the app is not resuming and even if I try to get both resume(d) and or the open on the activity I am not able to read any intent data added from the background service.    Please note that even if the service is registered again at next start the notification should still be possible to catch. I have read all things I can get, but I have not found any instruction on how to capture the notification intent data. All guides stop where it has appeared in the status bar, even den android dev ones.     h6.Test outcomes  - Data intent is only retrieved when you get it through android service resource: """"""""app/lib/background_locationservice_android.js""""""""        However you can't get intent data either in app/alloy.js or controllers/index.js    h6.Steps to reproduce  # Get and run stripped down version on Android device.  # Wait until a notification get trigger.  # Quit app then click at notification at the statusBar.   # Monitor Logs. Depending where was getStringExtra set will be the outcome.    Sample: https://www.dropbox.com/s/wow58vtprsiktu3/Arkiv_TestCase.zip""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Not able to capture intent data from a Notification created from Background service
Description: """"h6.Issue description I am using a simple background service to create a notification. The notification intent has extra data to it, and is then fired. The notification is displayed in the status bar. I pull down the bar and my app is opened/resumed. I try to read the intent data, but it appears as if the app is not resuming and even if I try to get both resume(d) and or the open on the activity I am not able to read any intent data added from the background service. Please note that even if the service is registered again at next start the notification should still be possible to catch. I have read all things I can get, but I have not found any instruction on how to capture the notification intent data. All guides stop where it has appeared in the status bar, even den android dev ones. h6.Test outcomes - Data intent is only retrieved when you get it through android service resource: """"""""app/lib/background_locationservice_android.js"""""""" However you can't get intent data either in app/alloy.js or controllers/index.js h6.Steps to reproduce # Get and run stripped down version on Android device. # Wait until a notification get trigger. # Quit app then click at notification at the statusBar. # Monitor Logs. Depending where was getStringExtra set will be the outcome. Sample: https://www.dropbox.com/s/wow58vtprsiktu3/Arkiv_TestCase.zip""""",title+description
TIMOB-16491,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Icons not copied to correct location when project is built""","""""""h5.Description  Icons are not being copied to the correct location when a project is built.  Icons are being copied to """"""""Apps/"""""""" when the should be in """"""""images/""""""""  I have attached a project with a few crude images and their expected file names and sizes.    Windows will ignore any images you have saved in the """"""""Apps/"""""""" folder and displays the windows default app-icon, and the only way to correct the icons is to manually copy the icons into the correct location and then build and deploy the project using the generated visual studio solution file.    +Extra Information+  The following link is the official windows documentation for file names and icon sizes: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/hh846296.aspx""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Icons not copied to correct location when project is built
Description: """"h5.Description Icons are not being copied to the correct location when a project is built. Icons are being copied to """"""""Apps/"""""""" when the should be in """"""""images/"""""""" I have attached a project with a few crude images and their expected file names and sizes. Windows will ignore any images you have saved in the """"""""Apps/"""""""" folder and displays the windows default app-icon, and the only way to correct the icons is to manually copy the icons into the correct location and then build and deploy the project using the generated visual studio solution file. +Extra Information+ The following link is the official windows documentation for file names and icon sizes: http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/apps/hh846296.aspx""""",title+description
TIMOB-16490,12,"""statusBar Problems when used together with barImage on Ti SDK 3.2.1.GA + iOS 7""","""""""When using Ti 3.2.1.GA the statusbar remains black on the top of the window, the exact same code with Ti 3.2.0.GA produces a transparent statusBar over the top of the NavBar image (barImage).    Tried with UIViewControllerBasedStatusBarAppearance set to true and to false... no effect whatsoever.    statusBarStyle also seems to have no effect.    It seems 3.2.1.GA broken something with barImage and statusbar. Smells like regression.    Screenshots attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: statusBar Problems when used together with barImage on Ti SDK 3.2.1.GA + iOS 7
Description: """"When using Ti 3.2.1.GA the statusbar remains black on the top of the window, the exact same code with Ti 3.2.0.GA produces a transparent statusBar over the top of the NavBar image (barImage). Tried with UIViewControllerBasedStatusBarAppearance set to true and to false... no effect whatsoever. statusBarStyle also seems to have no effect. It seems 3.2.1.GA broken something with barImage and statusbar. Smells like regression. Screenshots attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16489,12,"""Android: TableView longclick event also fires click when row has view inside""","""""""h2. Problem description  Adding a 'longclick' event listener to a TableView will also fire the 'click' event if the row inside the TableView has a child view.    h2. Steps to reproduce    1. Use the code below  2. Click on the row: 'click' is fired  3. Long-click on the row: 'longclick' is fired, but also 'click'    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView longclick event also fires click when row has view inside
Description: """"h2. Problem description Adding a 'longclick' event listener to a TableView will also fire the 'click' event if the row inside the TableView has a child view. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Use the code below 2. Click on the row: 'click' is fired 3. Long-click on the row: 'longclick' is fired, but also 'click' """"",title+description
TIMOB-16487,12,"""Android: Remove support for navbar-hidden""","""""""With AppCompat implementation, navBarHidden is not needed anymore. We wil only support 'fullscreen' and 'modal'.    Testing steps:  1. Run KS and Anvil to make sure no new regressions  2. When KS is built, go to build/android/gen/com/<USER>kitchensink/KitchensinkAppInfo.java and make sure the method isNavBarHidden() isn't generated.""""""",Technical task,"Title: Android: Remove support for navbar-hidden
Description: """"With AppCompat implementation, navBarHidden is not needed anymore. We wil only support 'fullscreen' and 'modal'. Testing steps: 1. Run KS and Anvil to make sure no new regressions 2. When KS is built, go to build/android/gen/com/<USER>kitchensink/KitchensinkAppInfo.java and make sure the method isNavBarHidden() isn't generated.""""",title+description
