Description: """"When using tableview.updateSection, row layout:'horizontal' and layout:'vertical' does not work. Layout: 'composite' gives a blank table. The code below lays out sections one and two (figure A) then updates section two (figure B). """"",title+description
TIMOB-16481,12,"""CLI: """"Xcode 5.1 is too new"""" message will appear with CLI GA (3.2.1) plus latest 3.2.2 SDK plus Xcode 5.1 beta 5""","""""""*Details:* If you have CLI GA (3.2.1) with latest 3.2.2 SDK build, *ti info \-t ios* will return """"""""Xcode 5.1 is too new"""""""" message if you have xcode-select pointing to Xcode 5.1 beta 5.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Make sure your xcode-select is pointing to Xcode 5.1 beta 5: *sudo xcode-select -s <PATH_TO>/Xcode51-Beta5.app*  2. Get latest 3.2.2 SDK build  3. In terminal, run the info command: *ti info \-t ios*  4. Scroll to the bottom to iOS Issues    *Actual:* This message will appear:  {quote}  iOS Issues    !  Xcode 5.1 is too new and may or may not work with Titanium SDK 3.2.2. The maximum supported       Xcode version by Titanium SDK 3.2.2 is Xcode 5.0..   {quote}    *Expected:* The CLI should not report this config as an issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"Xcode 5.1 is too new"""" message will appear with CLI GA (3.2.1) plus latest 3.2.2 SDK plus Xcode 5.1 beta 5
Description: """"*Details:* If you have CLI GA (3.2.1) with latest 3.2.2 SDK build, *ti info \-t ios* will return """"""""Xcode 5.1 is too new"""""""" message if you have xcode-select pointing to Xcode 5.1 beta 5. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Make sure your xcode-select is pointing to Xcode 5.1 beta 5: *sudo xcode-select -s <PATH_TO>/Xcode51-Beta5.app* 2. Get latest 3.2.2 SDK build 3. In terminal, run the info command: *ti info \-t ios* 4. Scroll to the bottom to iOS Issues *Actual:* This message will appear: {quote} iOS Issues ! Xcode 5.1 is too new and may or may not work with Titanium SDK 3.2.2. The maximum supported Xcode version by Titanium SDK 3.2.2 is Xcode 5.0.. {quote} *Expected:* The CLI should not report this config as an issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16479,12,"""Android: local HTML-based Google Maps in webview fails to open""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When you open a local html file in a webview, it fails (in Android 4.4, using Mobile SDK 3.2.1).     h4. Test Case  App.js:      index.html:      h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create new mobile project (titanium classic) using Mobile SDK 3.2.1  2. Paste the code sample to app.js  3. Paste the index.html contents into a new file index.html in Resources directory  4. Run the app into Nexus 4 or any device with KITKAT  5. See the error messages attached to this bug    h4. Error messages      h4. Extra info   - If you run the webview with google.com it will work just fine, it's not a general issue.  - If you want the original html file, you can locate it here: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/examples/map-simple    h4. Q&A Question  http://developer.<USER>com/question/162782/google-maps-v3-on-android-44--just-blank    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: local HTML-based Google Maps in webview fails to open
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When you open a local html file in a webview, it fails (in Android 4.4, using Mobile SDK 3.2.1). h4. Test Case App.js: index.html: h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create new mobile project (titanium classic) using Mobile SDK 3.2.1 2. Paste the code sample to app.js 3. Paste the index.html contents into a new file index.html in Resources directory 4. Run the app into Nexus 4 or any device with KITKAT 5. See the error messages attached to this bug h4. Error messages h4. Extra info - If you run the webview with google.com it will work just fine, it's not a general issue. - If you want the original html file, you can locate it here: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/examples/map-simple h4. Q&A Question http://developer.<USER>com/question/162782/google-maps-v3-on-android-44--just-blank """"",title+description
TIMOB-16478,12,"""Ability to fire event from a web view when the contents are loaded from a hosted site (e.g. non local resource)""","""""""Ability to fire event from a web view when the contents are loaded from a hosted site (e.g. non local resource)    If your web contents are stored locally in the assets folder, then the Ti.App.fireEvent works and the titanium app can respond.    e.g.:    Ti.App.fireEvent('app:fromWebView', { message: 'event fired from WebView, handled in Titanium' });    If the web contents are stored on a web site, then the event doesn't fire.    This has come up twice today, once with <USER>s and once with Louisville, Gas & Electric.    Both prospects have existing HTML5 web apps that they would want to use with an <USER>container. Event firing is useful for normal native/web view interaction as well as for leveraging Analytics and Breadcrumbs for the web view by firing an event to the native app and having the native app fire an analytics feature event and breadcrumb events.    I have provided a sample app where you can switch between local and remote html resources (settable in index.xml). Screen shots are also attached.    After entering a stock symbol (AAPL) in the web view and clicking submit, the web view fires an event. The container has an event listener for the even and displays an alert.    If the web resources are local this works. If the web resources are remote, it does not.    We hope to get a workaround or a solution for this.    Is there some javascript library that can be added to the remote web app so that Ti.App.fireEvent will work""""""",New Feature,"Title: Ability to fire event from a web view when the contents are loaded from a hosted site (e.g. non local resource)
Description: """"Ability to fire event from a web view when the contents are loaded from a hosted site (e.g. non local resource) If your web contents are stored locally in the assets folder, then the Ti.App.fireEvent works and the titanium app can respond. e.g.: Ti.App.fireEvent('app:fromWebView', { message: 'event fired from WebView, handled in Titanium' }); If the web contents are stored on a web site, then the event doesn't fire. This has come up twice today, once with <USER>s and once with Louisville, Gas & Electric. Both prospects have existing HTML5 web apps that they would want to use with an <USER>container. Event firing is useful for normal native/web view interaction as well as for leveraging Analytics and Breadcrumbs for the web view by firing an event to the native app and having the native app fire an analytics feature event and breadcrumb events. I have provided a sample app where you can switch between local and remote html resources (settable in index.xml). Screen shots are also attached. After entering a stock symbol (AAPL) in the web view and clicking submit, the web view fires an event. The container has an event listener for the even and displays an alert. If the web resources are local this works. If the web resources are remote, it does not. We hope to get a workaround or a solution for this. Is there some javascript library that can be added to the remote web app so that Ti.App.fireEvent will work""""",title+description
TIMOB-16477,12,"""iOS: Section index overlap with the search bar""","""""""h6.Issue description  iOS native issue causing the section index overlap with the search bar on TiUIListView.    h6.Steps to reproduce  (1) Run Sample code: https://gist.github.com/egomez99/1288d6ff7d97c5b76230  (2) When App launches Cancel button of searchBar is displayed but overlapped by Section Index. Image on the left of screen shoot.   (3) Click search box and type anything.   (4) Click either cancel or search. Section index overlap searchBar (Image on the right of screen shoot).  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Section index overlap with the search bar
Description: """"h6.Issue description iOS native issue causing the section index overlap with the search bar on TiUIListView. h6.Steps to reproduce (1) Run Sample code: https://gist.github.com/egomez99/1288d6ff7d97c5b76230 (2) When App launches Cancel button of searchBar is displayed but overlapped by Section Index. Image on the left of screen shoot. (3) Click search box and type anything. (4) Click either cancel or search. Section index overlap searchBar (Image on the right of screen shoot). """"",title+description
TIMOB-16476,12,"""iOS: Cannot hide Tab title when SplitWindow is inside a Tab""","""""""h2. Problem description  Adding a SplitWindow in a TabGroup does not allow to hide the title of the Tab.    h2. Use case  The use case is to be able to have the following structure:    TabGroup  --| SplitWindow  ----| NavigationWindow  ----| NavigationWindow    Previously it was possible to use the NavigationGroup directly in the TabGroup, but the recent change to NavigationWindow does not allow to do so.    The use of SplitWindow inside TabGroup seems to be unsupported (from the doc), but it works fine, and recently an Alloy bug has been fixed to allow it (see ALOY-831).    h2. Test code  index.js      index.xml  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot hide Tab title when SplitWindow is inside a Tab
Description: """"h2. Problem description Adding a SplitWindow in a TabGroup does not allow to hide the title of the Tab. h2. Use case The use case is to be able to have the following structure: TabGroup --| SplitWindow ----| NavigationWindow ----| NavigationWindow Previously it was possible to use the NavigationGroup directly in the TabGroup, but the recent change to NavigationWindow does not allow to do so. The use of SplitWindow inside TabGroup seems to be unsupported (from the doc), but it works fine, and recently an Alloy bug has been fixed to allow it (see ALOY-831). h2. Test code index.js index.xml """"",title+description
TIMOB-16475,12,"""Android: Regression: Saving an image **after** transformation, will produce the original image""","""""""h4. Problem Description  In 3.1.3.GA, you were able to """"""""save"""""""" the images after transformations. Starting with 3.2.0, the saved image will reflect the original image, not the one after the transformation.     h4. Test Case      h4. Steps to reproduce the issue  1. Create a new mobile project (classic titanium)  2. Paste the code sample into app.js  3. Run it  4. You will see a transformed image in the screen.  5. Press the label that will produce a copy of the image  6. You will see the image being added to the window, with the original size and setup.     h4. Q&A Related question  http://developer.<USER>com/question/162746/toimage-does-not-respect-transform-on-320-android""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Regression: Saving an image **after** transformation, will produce the original image
Description: """"h4. Problem Description In 3.1.3.GA, you were able to """"""""save"""""""" the images after transformations. Starting with 3.2.0, the saved image will reflect the original image, not the one after the transformation. h4. Test Case h4. Steps to reproduce the issue 1. Create a new mobile project (classic titanium) 2. Paste the code sample into app.js 3. Run it 4. You will see a transformed image in the screen. 5. Press the label that will produce a copy of the image 6. You will see the image being added to the window, with the original size and setup. h4. Q&A Related question http://developer.<USER>com/question/162746/toimage-does-not-respect-transform-on-320-android""""",title+description
TIMOB-16474,12,"""KitchenSink:Mashups - Publish Stream - login process is cancelled after being logged in ""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. KS>Mashups>Publish Stream>Login    Actual result:  Leaving KS > Safari>Facebook> login>enter the user name and the password> white screen.  Background FB and foreground KS app and go to Facebook login/logout.  The result is Logged In = false    Log out of Facebook(Safari) and go to KS>Mashups>Login/Logout> force dialog and then  KS>Mashups> Facebook>Publish Stream - works as expected        """"""",Improvement,"Title: KitchenSink:Mashups - Publish Stream - login process is cancelled after being logged in
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. KS>Mashups>Publish Stream>Login Actual result: Leaving KS > Safari>Facebook> login>enter the user name and the password> white screen. Background FB and foreground KS app and go to Facebook login/logout. The result is Logged In = false Log out of Facebook(Safari) and go to KS>Mashups>Login/Logout> force dialog and then KS>Mashups> Facebook>Publish Stream - works as expected """"",title+description
TIMOB-16472,12,"""Android: View width changes after animation""","""""""A view slides to the right. On a galaxy s3 phone, the view goes off the edge of the screen. On an iphone and early version of android, the view has a new size and is redrawn. ie the top right button is still visible.  clicking on size shows the new size.  The size should remain the same.   Change the example (search for UNCOMMENT) for the workaround.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: View width changes after animation
Description: """"A view slides to the right. On a galaxy s3 phone, the view goes off the edge of the screen. On an iphone and early version of android, the view has a new size and is redrawn. ie the top right button is still visible. clicking on size shows the new size. The size should remain the same. Change the example (search for UNCOMMENT) for the workaround.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16469,12,"""MobileWeb: TableViewRow creates unused Views causing poor performance""","""""""TableView rows create, by default:  Left Image,   Center Content   Center Content > TitleLabel  Right Image    Even if no leftImage, title, or rightImage are declared.    This results in:    1. Poor performance  2. Additional views, especially when adding custom views  3. Inconsistent behavior when compared with ios / android    Views should only be created as declared or needed.    I have modified this functionality in the attached file.        """"""",Improvement,"Title: MobileWeb: TableViewRow creates unused Views causing poor performance
Description: """"TableView rows create, by default: Left Image, Center Content Center Content > TitleLabel Right Image Even if no leftImage, title, or rightImage are declared. This results in: 1. Poor performance 2. Additional views, especially when adding custom views 3. Inconsistent behavior when compared with ios / android Views should only be created as declared or needed. I have modified this functionality in the attached file. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16468,12,"""Android: SSLException with certificate validation with HTTPClient with multiple virtual hosts""","""""""The HTTPClient fails to verify the SSL Certificate and I think I know the reason why.    Log:        What is happening here is that I have 2 virtual hosts running on the same server, so when the HTTPClient is going to check the certificate, he is resolving host1.com to get the ip address and then connects and ask for the certificate without specifing the host. So by default the server return the certificate for host2.com. I have checked this and the HTTPClient correctly validates the SSL Certificate for host2.com because it is the default. This bug is on Android only.    Enviorment:  Titanium Studio 3.2.0.201312191547  Titanium SDK 3.2.0  Windows 7  Android device Samsung Galaxy S2 Android v4.2.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: SSLException with certificate validation with HTTPClient with multiple virtual hosts
Description: """"The HTTPClient fails to verify the SSL Certificate and I think I know the reason why. Log: What is happening here is that I have 2 virtual hosts running on the same server, so when the HTTPClient is going to check the certificate, he is resolving host1.com to get the ip address and then connects and ask for the certificate without specifing the host. So by default the server return the certificate for host2.com. I have checked this and the HTTPClient correctly validates the SSL Certificate for host2.com because it is the default. This bug is on Android only. Enviorment: Titanium Studio 3.2.0.201312191547 Titanium SDK 3.2.0 Windows 7 Android device Samsung Galaxy S2 Android v4.2.2""""",title+description
