TIMOB-16465,12,"""iOS: Add iTunes artwork to default classic project sample""","""""""h5.Description  Creating a classic project will create default icons in the resources folder for the appicon and splashscreens. However no iTunes artwork is provided. If a default classic application is packaged for the iTunes store then no icon will be displayed.    Alloy projects have this in the template so this problem only occurs with classic projects.""""""",Improvement,"Title: iOS: Add iTunes artwork to default classic project sample
Description: """"h5.Description Creating a classic project will create default icons in the resources folder for the appicon and splashscreens. However no iTunes artwork is provided. If a default classic application is packaged for the iTunes store then no icon will be displayed. Alloy projects have this in the template so this problem only occurs with classic projects.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16464,12,"""Android:ListView:appendSection method not working properly""","""""""appendSection method not working properly on Android.  It overwrites the previous listView data.  Not a regression as it occurs on 3.2.0.GA also.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Copy paste the code in app.js and run the app.    Expected Result:  1.Should get Header as """"""""Fruits and Fish"""""""" and Apple and Banana under Fruits header.  Getting this in iOS.    Actual Result:  1.Getting only Fish Header.        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android:ListView:appendSection method not working properly
Description: """"appendSection method not working properly on Android. It overwrites the previous listView data. Not a regression as it occurs on 3.2.0.GA also. Steps to reproduce: 1. Copy paste the code in app.js and run the app. Expected Result: 1.Should get Header as """"""""Fruits and Fish"""""""" and Apple and Banana under Fruits header. Getting this in iOS. Actual Result: 1.Getting only Fish Header. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16463,12,"""iOS: Search bar disappears in some cases""","""""""Certain actions make the searchbar disappear. The easiest to reproduce is changing the device orientation when the searchbar is off screen (so when you have scrolled down a bit).  Another way, for which I cannot easily create a piece of reproducing code, is if you update the data of a listview by simply assigning the sections again.    The attached video shows the searchbar disappearing after rotating the device.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Search bar disappears in some cases
Description: """"Certain actions make the searchbar disappear. The easiest to reproduce is changing the device orientation when the searchbar is off screen (so when you have scrolled down a bit). Another way, for which I cannot easily create a piece of reproducing code, is if you update the data of a listview by simply assigning the sections again. The attached video shows the searchbar disappearing after rotating the device. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16462,12,"""iOS: Poor animation when opening a window from a tab on a slow simulator / device""","""""""When you open a new window from within a tab the open animation sort of animates in a jagged/shocking way. As if the animation is rendered using large blocks with a height of ~100pixels at a time. Even the root window's background color often shows in the bottom half of the screen.    I managed to capture the effect in a screenshot using the iPad Retina simulator.    You can reproduce the issue by creating the default Classic/Tabbed application template and opening the window. The effect is most obvious on a retina iPad in landscape.    This is the call that triggers the open with the default animation.      The issue has been in Ti SDK for as long as I know. I always thought I was doing something wrong, but I am not... So time to report the issue cause apparently no one else is seeing it...""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Poor animation when opening a window from a tab on a slow simulator / device
Description: """"When you open a new window from within a tab the open animation sort of animates in a jagged/shocking way. As if the animation is rendered using large blocks with a height of ~100pixels at a time. Even the root window's background color often shows in the bottom half of the screen. I managed to capture the effect in a screenshot using the iPad Retina simulator. You can reproduce the issue by creating the default Classic/Tabbed application template and opening the window. The effect is most obvious on a retina iPad in landscape. This is the call that triggers the open with the default animation. The issue has been in Ti SDK for as long as I know. I always thought I was doing something wrong, but I am not... So time to report the issue cause apparently no one else is seeing it...""""",title+description
TIMOB-16461,12,"""iOS: Customise badge and close icon of TiUIDashboard items""","""""""h6.Feature Request  Customer have used the custom view (with image & label) and added to dashboardItem.     The issue is that they have implemented the dashboardView by adding a view which contains an imageView and a label to dashboardItems. When they do longpress on a dashboardItem the delete icon that is supposed to show up on the top left side of the item appears in the centre.     Having the text as part of the image is not an option for them because they need to be able to translate the strings to many different languages.    h6.Expected behavior  Badge number screen shoot: expected_1.png  Close button screen shoot: expected_2.png    h6.Actual behavior  Following are the issues they faced:  1. """"""""Close"""""""" (x) icon is not aligned in top-left corner of the image.   2. Badge icon was not displayed at the top-right of the image.    Screen shoot: DashBoard_iOS.jpg    h6.Steps to reproduce  I have attached the sample code (Dashboard_11Feb14.zip) where Dashboard view is created.   """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Customise badge and close icon of TiUIDashboard items
Description: """"h6.Feature Request Customer have used the custom view (with image & label) and added to dashboardItem. The issue is that they have implemented the dashboardView by adding a view which contains an imageView and a label to dashboardItems. When they do longpress on a dashboardItem the delete icon that is supposed to show up on the top left side of the item appears in the centre. Having the text as part of the image is not an option for them because they need to be able to translate the strings to many different languages. h6.Expected behavior Badge number screen shoot: expected_1.png Close button screen shoot: expected_2.png h6.Actual behavior Following are the issues they faced: 1. """"""""Close"""""""" (x) icon is not aligned in top-left corner of the image. 2. Badge icon was not displayed at the top-right of the image. Screen shoot: DashBoard_iOS.jpg h6.Steps to reproduce I have attached the sample code (Dashboard_11Feb14.zip) where Dashboard view is created. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16460,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Winstore App Certification Kit shows errors in default Windows Hybrid WINSTORE application""","""""""h5.Description  Creating a default application for Windows Hybrid works successfully through CLI. Building to device and emulator works fine too. Packaging the application for distribution also works fine. However after running the Windows App Certification Kit, errors start to show.    I have attached the results of the test to this ticket.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  0. Make sure you have Windows App Certification Kit installed.  1. Create a default windows hybrid application  2. Build the application for *winstore*  3. Open the generated solution file in the build directory  4. Once open in Visual Studio, click Project -> Studio -> Create App Packages.  5. Run the Windows App Certification Kit on the packaged build.    h5.Expected Result  Should successfully pass the tests.    h5.Actual Result  Errors are detected in the code.    +Extra Information+  Windows App Certification Kit runs a series of tests against the users application to make sure it is suitable for the windows store, putting it through multiple stress tests.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Winstore App Certification Kit shows errors in default Windows Hybrid WINSTORE application
Description: """"h5.Description Creating a default application for Windows Hybrid works successfully through CLI. Building to device and emulator works fine too. Packaging the application for distribution also works fine. However after running the Windows App Certification Kit, errors start to show. I have attached the results of the test to this ticket. h5.Steps To Reproduce 0. Make sure you have Windows App Certification Kit installed. 1. Create a default windows hybrid application 2. Build the application for *winstore* 3. Open the generated solution file in the build directory 4. Once open in Visual Studio, click Project -> Studio -> Create App Packages. 5. Run the Windows App Certification Kit on the packaged build. h5.Expected Result Should successfully pass the tests. h5.Actual Result Errors are detected in the code. +Extra Information+ Windows App Certification Kit runs a series of tests against the users application to make sure it is suitable for the windows store, putting it through multiple stress tests.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16459,12,"""Android: Add support for android.os.Debug.startMethodTracing() and android.os.Debug.stopMethodTracing()""","""""""h4. New Feature description  The user wants to be able to start and stop the trace method in android.os.Debug, so they can profile their application in android.    h4. Related Docs    Debug class - http://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Debug.html  debugging profiling - http://developer.android.com/tools/debugging/debugging-tracing.html    h4. Q&A Question  http://developer.<USER>com/question/162584/setting-up-profiling-in-titanium    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add support for android.os.Debug.startMethodTracing() and android.os.Debug.stopMethodTracing()
Description: """"h4. New Feature description The user wants to be able to start and stop the trace method in android.os.Debug, so they can profile their application in android. h4. Related Docs Debug class - http://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Debug.html debugging profiling - http://developer.android.com/tools/debugging/debugging-tracing.html h4. Q&A Question http://developer.<USER>com/question/162584/setting-up-profiling-in-titanium """"",title+description
