Description: """"On Mobile Web: Button in the navigation bar not displaying the alert when clicked. Works fine on Ti 3.1.3, broken on Ti 3.2.0 and 3.2.1 """"",title+description
TIMOB-16456,12,"""Android: WebView scrolling up when typing if top property has negative value""","""""""h3. Issue    When a webview is assigned a negative value in the top property will start scrolling up when user starts typing into a textfield, this will occur while the focus textfield is visible in the screen, once this textfield is our of screen the scrolling will stop.    h3. Testing    Tested on SDK 3.2.0, SDK 3.2.1 and SDK 3.1.3     While testing this issue comes to our attention that this issue will not be reproducible across all android devices and versions.    Showing the issue:    Samsung Galaxy III mini - Android 4.1.3  Samsung Galaxy S2 - Android 4.2.2  Sony Ericsson Xperia Play - Android 4.0.4    Not Showing the issue:    Nexus 7 - Android 4.4  Samsung Galaxy Player - Android 2.3.5    h3. Steps to Repro    1. Run the test case  2. Click on a webview textfield  3. Start Typing  4. The webview will start scrolling up    h3. Test case    index.xml      index.tss      index.js      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView scrolling up when typing if top property has negative value
Description: """"h3. Issue When a webview is assigned a negative value in the top property will start scrolling up when user starts typing into a textfield, this will occur while the focus textfield is visible in the screen, once this textfield is our of screen the scrolling will stop. h3. Testing Tested on SDK 3.2.0, SDK 3.2.1 and SDK 3.1.3 While testing this issue comes to our attention that this issue will not be reproducible across all android devices and versions. Showing the issue: Samsung Galaxy III mini - Android 4.1.3 Samsung Galaxy S2 - Android 4.2.2 Sony Ericsson Xperia Play - Android 4.0.4 Not Showing the issue: Nexus 7 - Android 4.4 Samsung Galaxy Player - Android 2.3.5 h3. Steps to Repro 1. Run the test case 2. Click on a webview textfield 3. Start Typing 4. The webview will start scrolling up h3. Test case index.xml index.tss index.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-16455,12,"""Android: Event object on ListItem child's change doesn't match iOS""","""""""Source: http://developer.<USER>com/question/162482/alloy-listview-with-switch-in-template     The event object, in particular e.source does not include the same properties as on iOS making it impossible to create a cross-platform solution to the developer's question.    In addition to the code I provided in that Q&A thread, I tried other solutions including this:            In all cases, e.source doesn't include the custom myID property.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Event object on ListItem child's change doesn't match iOS
Description: """"Source: http://developer.<USER>com/question/162482/alloy-listview-with-switch-in-template The event object, in particular e.source does not include the same properties as on iOS making it impossible to create a cross-platform solution to the developer's question. In addition to the code I provided in that Q&A thread, I tried other solutions including this: In all cases, e.source doesn't include the custom myID property.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16454,12,"""TiAPI: Customize button title similar to TableView deleteButtonTitle""","""""""Unable to find it in the documentation but I use 'deleteButtonTitle' when swiping on an editable TableView so I can customize the label 'Delete' to something else, eg: 'Add', 'Remove', 'Hide' etc..    TableView example:   {code:tableView.js}  var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({      data:data,      deleteButtonTitle: """"""""Hide"""""""", //L(""""""""hide"""""""")      editable:true  });   {code}      It would be great to have this feature on a ListView...   Well, would be even better to have it on a 'ListItem' so that it can be customizable on an item/row rather than the same label across a single list.    As all the features of a TableView haven't been implemented on a ListView yet, I'm having to slowly migrate, however would be useful (if this feature is possible to implemented) that it works with ListView's main/child templates also.    Many thanks  @Hardbyte   """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Customize button title similar to TableView deleteButtonTitle
Description: """"Unable to find it in the documentation but I use 'deleteButtonTitle' when swiping on an editable TableView so I can customize the label 'Delete' to something else, eg: 'Add', 'Remove', 'Hide' etc.. TableView example: {code:tableView.js} var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({ data:data, deleteButtonTitle: """"""""Hide"""""""", //L(""""""""hide"""""""") editable:true }); {code} It would be great to have this feature on a ListView... Well, would be even better to have it on a 'ListItem' so that it can be customizable on an item/row rather than the same label across a single list. As all the features of a TableView haven't been implemented on a ListView yet, I'm having to slowly migrate, however would be useful (if this feature is possible to implemented) that it works with ListView's main/child templates also. Many thanks @Hardbyte """"",title+description
TIMOB-16453,12,"""iOS: Build failed while parsing html""","""""""h5. Problem     WebView throw an error in Ti apps for local html file.        h5. Testing Environments   Mac OS X 10.8.5   Titanium SDK: 3.2.1.GA  Titanium CLI: 3.2.1  IOS Simulator 7.0.3   <USER>Studio, build: 3.2.1.201402061120      h5. Test Code        h5. Steps to reproduce   # Create New Ti Sample project  # Save attached html file to resource folder   # Update app.js file with test code   # Run test code in IOS Simulator   # Check console log for error message           h5. Error Logs        Thanks """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Build failed while parsing html
Description: """"h5. Problem WebView throw an error in Ti apps for local html file. h5. Testing Environments Mac OS X 10.8.5 Titanium SDK: 3.2.1.GA Titanium CLI: 3.2.1 IOS Simulator 7.0.3 <USER>Studio, build: 3.2.1.201402061120 h5. Test Code h5. Steps to reproduce # Create New Ti Sample project # Save attached html file to resource folder # Update app.js file with test code # Run test code in IOS Simulator # Check console log for error message h5. Error Logs Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-16449,12,"""Android: When touchEnabled and enabled properties are set to false the event listener added to the view stops working""","""""""h6. Issue description  To enable and disable the buttons developer use the touchEnabled and enabled properties of the Titanium View's.    Many of the buttons created this way start off in a disabled state so touchEnabled and enabled are both set to false. Clicking on the button in this state does nothing which is expected. When ready we set touchEnabled and enabled to true to enable touch events on the view and to fire the attached event listeners such as a touchstart event.     In the 3.1.3.GA SDK this works perfectly however on the 3.2.0.GA SDK it appears that once those 2 properties are set to false the event listener added to the view stops working.     h6. Test Case Steps:  # Launch Bug_Testing_TC sample with the 3.1.3.GA on an android device.  # Tap the Pink Rectangle -> Nothing happens, that is expected since the view is disabled.  # Tap on the Blue Square -> Notice an alert pops up indicating that touchEnabled and enabled are set to true now for the pink square.  # Click OK  # Now Tap on the Pink Rectangle Again -> Notice that there is an alert that says PINK VIEW CLICKED!! that is expected since the view is now in an enabled and touchenabled state. Also notice that both of those states are now set to false so the view is again disabled.  # Click OK  # Tap on the Pink Rectangle Again -> Notice nothing happens since it is disabled. That is how we expect it to work.  # Change the TiSDk to 3.2.0.GA  # Launch Bug_Testing on an android device.  # Tap the Pink Rectangle -> Nothing happens, that is expected since the view is disabled.  # Tap on the Blue Square -> Notice an alert pops up indicating that touchEnabled and enabled are set to true now for the pink square.  # Click OK  # Now Tap on the Pink Rectangle Again -> Notice that Nothing happens  # Repeat 10-12, notice that the pink rectangles touchstart event is not firing, it should be firing since touchEnabled and enabled are both set to true.    h6. Tested on  This was reproduced on the Samsung Note 10.1 2014 MN: SM-P600 running Android 4.3 and Galaxy Nexus 4.1.1.    It could not be reproduced this on a Saumsung Note Phone MN: SGH-I717 running Android 2.3.6.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: When touchEnabled and enabled properties are set to false the event listener added to the view stops working
Description: """"h6. Issue description To enable and disable the buttons developer use the touchEnabled and enabled properties of the Titanium View's. Many of the buttons created this way start off in a disabled state so touchEnabled and enabled are both set to false. Clicking on the button in this state does nothing which is expected. When ready we set touchEnabled and enabled to true to enable touch events on the view and to fire the attached event listeners such as a touchstart event. In the 3.1.3.GA SDK this works perfectly however on the 3.2.0.GA SDK it appears that once those 2 properties are set to false the event listener added to the view stops working. h6. Test Case Steps: # Launch Bug_Testing_TC sample with the 3.1.3.GA on an android device. # Tap the Pink Rectangle -> Nothing happens, that is expected since the view is disabled. # Tap on the Blue Square -> Notice an alert pops up indicating that touchEnabled and enabled are set to true now for the pink square. # Click OK # Now Tap on the Pink Rectangle Again -> Notice that there is an alert that says PINK VIEW CLICKED!! that is expected since the view is now in an enabled and touchenabled state. Also notice that both of those states are now set to false so the view is again disabled. # Click OK # Tap on the Pink Rectangle Again -> Notice nothing happens since it is disabled. That is how we expect it to work. # Change the TiSDk to 3.2.0.GA # Launch Bug_Testing on an android device. # Tap the Pink Rectangle -> Nothing happens, that is expected since the view is disabled. # Tap on the Blue Square -> Notice an alert pops up indicating that touchEnabled and enabled are set to true now for the pink square. # Click OK # Now Tap on the Pink Rectangle Again -> Notice that Nothing happens # Repeat 10-12, notice that the pink rectangles touchstart event is not firing, it should be firing since touchEnabled and enabled are both set to true. h6. Tested on This was reproduced on the Samsung Note 10.1 2014 MN: SM-P600 running Android 4.3 and Galaxy Nexus 4.1.1. It could not be reproduced this on a Saumsung Note Phone MN: SGH-I717 running Android 2.3.6. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16448,12,"""When installing code processor from command line, git shows error of get remote.orgin.url returned wrong result""","""""""During installation, we had to install code processor from command line, and when we did, it installed successfully, but the installation did show one warning error message attached""""""",Story,"Title: When installing code processor from command line, git shows error of get remote.orgin.url returned wrong result
Description: """"During installation, we had to install code processor from command line, and when we did, it installed successfully, but the installation did show one warning error message attached""""",title+description
TIMOB-16446,12,"""Set default color of Switch object's title to black""","""""""Steps:    1. Create app (Alloy or classic) that displays a Switch control with {{SWITCH_STYLE_CHECKBOX}} style, e.g:        2. Build for Android.    Result: Checkbox label is white by default, so doesn't appear on white background.  Expected: Checkbox label is black by default, like most Titanium label/text objects.    Found the solution from a StackOverflow poster who encountered same problem:   http://stackoverflow.com/questions/14171078/title-is-not-displayed-in-a-checkbox-in-titanium""""""",Improvement,"Title: Set default color of Switch object's title to black
Description: """"Steps: 1. Create app (Alloy or classic) that displays a Switch control with {{SWITCH_STYLE_CHECKBOX}} style, e.g: 2. Build for Android. Result: Checkbox label is white by default, so doesn't appear on white background. Expected: Checkbox label is black by default, like most Titanium label/text objects. Found the solution from a StackOverflow poster who encountered same problem: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/14171078/title-is-not-displayed-in-a-checkbox-in-titanium""""",title+description
TIMOB-16445,12,"""Anvil: issues using Ti.Filesystem.getFile""","""""""h5. Problem description    Using Anvil for SyncServer testing, an issue is surfacing when using Ti.Filesystem.getFile for checking folder.     Attached sample code run manually on device works as expected.    See lines 153 to 170 of the attached sample code 'app.js':      When run on device, it works as expected (destFile.exists() returns true).    However, running the same code on Anvil and adding a valueOf check:      is returning false, thus an error.      'externalfilesync.js' file attached is the Anvil test sample - see 'function copyfiles()' line 214.""""""",Bug,"Title: Anvil: issues using Ti.Filesystem.getFile
Description: """"h5. Problem description Using Anvil for SyncServer testing, an issue is surfacing when using Ti.Filesystem.getFile for checking folder. Attached sample code run manually on device works as expected. See lines 153 to 170 of the attached sample code 'app.js': When run on device, it works as expected (destFile.exists() returns true). However, running the same code on Anvil and adding a valueOf check: is returning false, thus an error. 'externalfilesync.js' file attached is the Anvil test sample - see 'function copyfiles()' line 214.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16443,12,"""MobileWeb: ScrollView does not fire """"scrollend"""", fires """"scrollEnd""""""","""""""The documentation says """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" has been deprecated for all platforms. However mobile web only fires """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" and does not fire the """"""""scrollend"""""""" event.    You can see this in line 63 of """"""""ScrollView.js""""""""    self.fireEvent('scrollEnd');    should be, per the current documentation    self.fireEvent('scrollend');""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: ScrollView does not fire """"scrollend"""", fires """"scrollEnd""""
Description: """"The documentation says """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" has been deprecated for all platforms. However mobile web only fires """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" and does not fire the """"""""scrollend"""""""" event. You can see this in line 63 of """"""""ScrollView.js"""""""" self.fireEvent('scrollEnd'); should be, per the current documentation self.fireEvent('scrollend');""""",title+description
TIMOB-16440,12,"""Alloy app runtime error: could not find the file app.js""","""""""Studio 3.2.1.201402041146 (OS X)  CLI - 3.2.1  SDK - 3.2.1  Alloy - 1.3.1    Steps:    1. Create an Alloy project (using CLI or Studio) and build for device/sim.    Results: Runtime error (see attached).    I've also attached my ti info output.""""""",Bug,"Title: Alloy app runtime error: could not find the file app.js
Description: """"Studio 3.2.1.201402041146 (OS X) CLI - 3.2.1 SDK - 3.2.1 Alloy - 1.3.1 Steps: 1. Create an Alloy project (using CLI or Studio) and build for device/sim. Results: Runtime error (see attached). I've also attached my ti info output.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16439,12,"""CLI: Android: Add support for debugging Android apps in a Genymotion emulator""","""""""As of Titanium SDK 3.2.0, the Android build supports Genymotion emulators, however debugging apps in the Genymotion emulator is not working.    This may be solvable by simply changing line 1344 of android/cli/commands/_build.js from:        to        Here's the originating Q&A question: http://developer.<USER>com/question/162337/genymotion-and-debug-mode.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Android: Add support for debugging Android apps in a Genymotion emulator
Description: """"As of Titanium SDK 3.2.0, the Android build supports Genymotion emulators, however debugging apps in the Genymotion emulator is not working. This may be solvable by simply changing line 1344 of android/cli/commands/_build.js from: to Here's the originating Q&A question: http://developer.<USER>com/question/162337/genymotion-and-debug-mode.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16436,12,"""Android: Integrate AppCompat custom theme + ActionBarActivity""","""""""Now that we have integrated appcompat libraries, the next step is to extend ActionBarActivity to TiBaseActivity, set up custom themes and add support for ActionBarActivity (ActionBar support for older devices)    Android theme source for reference: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/master/core/res/res/values/themes.xml    Testing steps:   1. Run scons and make sure basic titanium apps run successfully.  2. Run Anvil to make sure no new failures  3. Run this code on both HoneyComb+ and 2.x devices    You should see the action bar with 2.x device.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Android: Integrate AppCompat custom theme + ActionBarActivity
Description: """"Now that we have integrated appcompat libraries, the next step is to extend ActionBarActivity to TiBaseActivity, set up custom themes and add support for ActionBarActivity (ActionBar support for older devices) Android theme source for reference: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/refs/heads/master/core/res/res/values/themes.xml Testing steps: 1. Run scons and make sure basic titanium apps run successfully. 2. Run Anvil to make sure no new failures 3. Run this code on both HoneyComb+ and 2.x devices You should see the action bar with 2.x device.""""",title+description
