TIMOB-16422,12,"""CLI: Android build fails if user is not logged in to CLI""","""""""h5.Description  If you are logged out of the CLI, building to an Android emulator or device will fail. The CLI will ask the user to log in before it starts the build, but after logging in the fail occurs.        h5.Steps To Reproduce  1) Run 'ti logout'  2) Create and cd into an Android project  3) Run 'ti build -p android -T emulator'    h5.Expected Result  CLI should request the user to log in, then build to the emulator if the log in details are correct.    h5.Actual Result  CLI stops the build after asking for your keystore password.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android build fails if user is not logged in to CLI
Description: """"h5.Description If you are logged out of the CLI, building to an Android emulator or device will fail. The CLI will ask the user to log in before it starts the build, but after logging in the fail occurs. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1) Run 'ti logout' 2) Create and cd into an Android project 3) Run 'ti build -p android -T emulator' h5.Expected Result CLI should request the user to log in, then build to the emulator if the log in details are correct. h5.Actual Result CLI stops the build after asking for your keystore password.""""",title+description
