TIMOB-16418,12,"""iOS: Scrollableview forces a reload of webview every single time that a view is added""","""""""h4. Problem Description  If you have webviews in your scrollableview, they will reload every time any other view is added to the scrollableview.     Can we try not to reload the webviews already there?    h4. Code Sample      h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile (classic) project.  2. Paste the testcase to app.js  3. Run in simulator iOS  4. Click on the button to add a second view.   5. You will get an alert that the webview reloaded.     h4. Extra info  Q&A Link: http://developer.<USER>com/question/162289/is-it-possible-to-prevent-webviews-on-scrollableview-from-reloading-when-adding-new-views-to-the-scrollableview""""""",Story,"Title: iOS: Scrollableview forces a reload of webview every single time that a view is added
Description: """"h4. Problem Description If you have webviews in your scrollableview, they will reload every time any other view is added to the scrollableview. Can we try not to reload the webviews already there? h4. Code Sample h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile (classic) project. 2. Paste the testcase to app.js 3. Run in simulator iOS 4. Click on the button to add a second view. 5. You will get an alert that the webview reloaded. h4. Extra info Q&A Link: http://developer.<USER>com/question/162289/is-it-possible-to-prevent-webviews-on-scrollableview-from-reloading-when-adding-new-views-to-the-scrollableview""""",title+description
TIMOB-16417,12,"""CLI: Build - If you have 3.2.0 CLI with 3.2.1 SDK selected in CLI and in tiapp.xml, then """"Invalid platform """"undefined"""""""" message is returned ""","""""""*Details:* If you have 3.2.0 CLI with 3.2.1 SDK selected in CLI *and* in the project's tiapp.xml, then """"""""Invalid platform """"""""undefined"""""""""""""""" message is returned.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Download Titanium CLI 3.2.0.GA  2. Get the latest 3.2.1 SDK build and make CLI select it: ti sdk install -b 3_2_X -d  3. Create a project in studio or via CLI; make sure the tiapp.xml has SDK 3.2.1 selected  4. In terminal, go to the project directory, do a build: ti build -p android or ti build -p ios    *Actual:* You will see this message returned:      *Expected:* Should not see undefined message and should guide the user how to get back to a proper state.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Build - If you have 3.2.0 CLI with 3.2.1 SDK selected in CLI and in tiapp.xml, then """"Invalid platform """"undefined"""""""" message is returned
Description: """"*Details:* If you have 3.2.0 CLI with 3.2.1 SDK selected in CLI *and* in the project's tiapp.xml, then """"""""Invalid platform """"""""undefined"""""""""""""""" message is returned. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Download Titanium CLI 3.2.0.GA 2. Get the latest 3.2.1 SDK build and make CLI select it: ti sdk install -b 3_2_X -d 3. Create a project in studio or via CLI; make sure the tiapp.xml has SDK 3.2.1 selected 4. In terminal, go to the project directory, do a build: ti build -p android or ti build -p ios *Actual:* You will see this message returned: *Expected:* Should not see undefined message and should guide the user how to get back to a proper state.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16416,12,"""Update the SDK commands for build, clean, create and project to have correct min CLI version for 3.2.1""","""""""h5. Description:  When using CLI 3.2.0 and trying to build with SDK 3.2.1, an error is produced since the min SDK in the CLI commands has not been updated to 3.2.1.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Install CLI 3.2.0  2) Install SDK 3.2.1  3) Using an existing project, try running a build, such as """"""""ti build -p android""""""""    h5. Result:  Obscure and unrelated error produced since the min SDK versions in the CLI commands are not accurate and are still """"""""3.2""""""""    h5. Expected Result:  An error describing the incompatibility between the CLI and the SDK versions""""""",Bug,"Title: Update the SDK commands for build, clean, create and project to have correct min CLI version for 3.2.1
Description: """"h5. Description: When using CLI 3.2.0 and trying to build with SDK 3.2.1, an error is produced since the min SDK in the CLI commands has not been updated to 3.2.1. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install CLI 3.2.0 2) Install SDK 3.2.1 3) Using an existing project, try running a build, such as """"""""ti build -p android"""""""" h5. Result: Obscure and unrelated error produced since the min SDK versions in the CLI commands are not accurate and are still """"""""3.2"""""""" h5. Expected Result: An error describing the incompatibility between the CLI and the SDK versions""""",title+description
