TIMOB-16378,12,"""TiAPI: Add Get default format methods to Global.String class""","""""""It would be very helpfull if String.Global could have methods to return the current date and timeformats. Somthing like:  getDateFormat('medium') -> 'MM/DD/YYYY'  getTimeFormat('medium') -> 'hh:mm'  getCurrencySymbol() -> $    This would be helpfull when you have a backend that provides titles and labels to your mobile app.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Add Get default format methods to Global.String class
Description: """"It would be very helpfull if String.Global could have methods to return the current date and timeformats. Somthing like: getDateFormat('medium') -> 'MM/DD/YYYY' getTimeFormat('medium') -> 'hh:mm' getCurrencySymbol() -> $ This would be helpfull when you have a backend that provides titles and labels to your mobile app. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16377,12,"""CLI: Android: Restart adb if it stops seeing Android devices""","""""""There are times when adb stops seeing an Android device despite being connected. This can be fixed by restarting adb, however it can be confusing when the Android build says there are no Android devices connected.    To fix this, we need to scan all connected USB devices and identify all Android devices, then query """"""""adb devices"""""""". If """"""""adb devices"""""""" does not return all of the connected devices, then restart adb and try again.    To detect connected USB devices on Mac OS X run {{system_profiler SPUSBDataType}} and on Linux run {{lsusb -v}}.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Android: Restart adb if it stops seeing Android devices
Description: """"There are times when adb stops seeing an Android device despite being connected. This can be fixed by restarting adb, however it can be confusing when the Android build says there are no Android devices connected. To fix this, we need to scan all connected USB devices and identify all Android devices, then query """"""""adb devices"""""""". If """"""""adb devices"""""""" does not return all of the connected devices, then restart adb and try again. To detect connected USB devices on Mac OS X run {{system_profiler SPUSBDataType}} and on Linux run {{lsusb -v}}.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16376,12,"""Android: Expose Webview's configuration flags in Android for fine tuning""","""""""h4. Problem Description    Currently, the Android implementation of Titanium Mobile API, will hardcode the flags for the webview behavior like:        The user wants to be able to control those from within the JS level, in order to accomplish things like:    """"""""I need to prevent the webview to open another window""""""""    h4. Q&A reference  http://developer.<USER>com/question/162213/webview-prevent-target-blank-from-opening-in-new-window--android-settings    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose Webview's configuration flags in Android for fine tuning
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Currently, the Android implementation of Titanium Mobile API, will hardcode the flags for the webview behavior like: The user wants to be able to control those from within the JS level, in order to accomplish things like: """"""""I need to prevent the webview to open another window"""""""" h4. Q&A reference http://developer.<USER>com/question/162213/webview-prevent-target-blank-from-opening-in-new-window--android-settings """"",title+description
TIMOB-16374,12,"""Windows Hybrid: setBackgroundImage does not render on Windows 8 Builds""","""""""When coding an application for Window 8 Hybrid with  Mobile web, if you call the setBackgroundImage() for a View, Window, or ImageView, it will not work.      It works fine if you view the build from MobileWeb, however once you build for simulator on Windows 8, the images never show up.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: setBackgroundImage does not render on Windows 8 Builds
Description: """"When coding an application for Window 8 Hybrid with Mobile web, if you call the setBackgroundImage() for a View, Window, or ImageView, it will not work. It works fine if you view the build from MobileWeb, however once you build for simulator on Windows 8, the images never show up. """"",title+description
