TIMOB-16353,12,"""Android: Transparent windows are opaque on Android""","""""""Here is the XML used to generate a transparent window. I don't think that the content matters as long as the content is smaller than the window so that you can see through to the window underneath. Basically I'm creating a transparent window with a list view in it to simulate a popup menu control.    Instead of seeing the window behind the list view, there is a black background on Android (iOS works fine).        I think that this is a bug in Titanium. The generated code seems to look right.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Transparent windows are opaque on Android
Description: """"Here is the XML used to generate a transparent window. I don't think that the content matters as long as the content is smaller than the window so that you can see through to the window underneath. Basically I'm creating a transparent window with a list view in it to simulate a popup menu control. Instead of seeing the window behind the list view, there is a black background on Android (iOS works fine). I think that this is a bug in Titanium. The generated code seems to look right. """"",title+description
