TIMOB-16342,12,"""Genymotion emulator not generating any Analytics""","""""""Genymotion emulator not generating any Analytics    I run an app on a Genymotion 2.0.3 Nexus One 4.3 emulator and no analytics are generated (Sessions, installs, events).    If I run the same app on an Android emulator (in exactly the same fashion and app), I do get analytics.""""""",Bug,"Title: Genymotion emulator not generating any Analytics
Description: """"Genymotion emulator not generating any Analytics I run an app on a Genymotion 2.0.3 Nexus One 4.3 emulator and no analytics are generated (Sessions, installs, events). If I run the same app on an Android emulator (in exactly the same fashion and app), I do get analytics.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16341,12,"""CLI: Support defining Ti dependencies in modules""","""""""During build time, the CLI excludes Ti Classes that are not found in the app's js code. This is problematic when a module uses a class that is not used in any js code.     For example, the Brightcove module uses TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy class and it is necessary to have a line of code referencing `Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer` so that class will be included in the build (see MOD-1628).    It would be very helpful if we could define the classes that are used in a module and have the build <USER>include those classes without having to reference them in the js.""""""",Story,"Title: CLI: Support defining Ti dependencies in modules
Description: """"During build time, the CLI excludes Ti Classes that are not found in the app's js code. This is problematic when a module uses a class that is not used in any js code. For example, the Brightcove module uses TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy class and it is necessary to have a line of code referencing `Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer` so that class will be included in the build (see MOD-1628). It would be very helpful if we could define the classes that are used in a module and have the build <USER>include those classes without having to reference them in the js.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16340,12,"""Allow launching an Android emulator by device id without forcing app to build for Android""","""""""Inside Studio we have an option to preview a MobileWeb app on an Android emulator. Unfortunately with the new CLI we have no command to tell it to launch the selected nAndroid emulator without also building the app for Android. In the meantime I can hack in basic support for launching on my own, but it'd be nice if there were a command to launch a given emulator for us.  """"""",Story,"Title: Allow launching an Android emulator by device id without forcing app to build for Android
Description: """"Inside Studio we have an option to preview a MobileWeb app on an Android emulator. Unfortunately with the new CLI we have no command to tell it to launch the selected nAndroid emulator without also building the app for Android. In the meantime I can hack in basic support for launching on my own, but it'd be nice if there were a command to launch a given emulator for us. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16338,12,"""Kitchen Sink: Window barImage not working properly on iOS6""","""""""Window's barImage property not working properly on iOS 6 device with latest sdk build and on 3.2.0.GA.    It work fine on 3.1.3.GA on iOS6 Device.    For iOS7 its working fine on both latest build and 3.2.0.GA, 3.1.3.GA builds.    Steps to reproduce:  1.Install KS and run on iOS6 device.  2.Goto BaseUI>Window NavBar>Set Bar Image    Expected Result:  Please refer screenshot attached as expected.png    Actual Result:  Please refer screenshot attached as actual.png  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen Sink: Window barImage not working properly on iOS6
Description: """"Window's barImage property not working properly on iOS 6 device with latest sdk build and on 3.2.0.GA. It work fine on 3.1.3.GA on iOS6 Device. For iOS7 its working fine on both latest build and 3.2.0.GA, 3.1.3.GA builds. Steps to reproduce: 1.Install KS and run on iOS6 device. 2.Goto BaseUI>Window NavBar>Set Bar Image Expected Result: Please refer screenshot attached as expected.png Actual Result: Please refer screenshot attached as actual.png """"",title+description
TIMOB-16337,12,"""iOS7: ListView: BackgroundColor not working properly""","""""""There is different behavior for setting of BackgroundColor for listView on iOS6 and iOS7 Versions.    This is not a regression. Since issue occurs on 3.2.0.GA also.    Steps to reproduce:    1.Install KS and run.  2.Go to BaseUI>View>ListView>Basic Functions> Background Colors & Scroll Indicator  3. Click on the 'next' button       Expected Result:    2. A new window should get displayed with 'ScrollIndicator=true'. The first listitem in the listview 'My background is yellow' should have a yellow background.The listview should have 100 listitems and no background.     3. The background of listview turns red(its plain and not grouped).Listitem with yellow background remains yellow.'ScrollIndicator=false'       Actual Result:    3.The background of listview does not turns red.  Please refer to screenshots attached for both iOS6 and iOS7 version(theres is difference in behavior).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: ListView: BackgroundColor not working properly
Description: """"There is different behavior for setting of BackgroundColor for listView on iOS6 and iOS7 Versions. This is not a regression. Since issue occurs on 3.2.0.GA also. Steps to reproduce: 1.Install KS and run. 2.Go to BaseUI>View>ListView>Basic Functions> Background Colors & Scroll Indicator 3. Click on the 'next' button Expected Result: 2. A new window should get displayed with 'ScrollIndicator=true'. The first listitem in the listview 'My background is yellow' should have a yellow background.The listview should have 100 listitems and no background. 3. The background of listview turns red(its plain and not grouped).Listitem with yellow background remains yellow.'ScrollIndicator=false' Actual Result: 3.The background of listview does not turns red. Please refer to screenshots attached for both iOS6 and iOS7 version(theres is difference in behavior).""""",title+description
