Description: """"The android app icon is using the default Android robot icon and not the one we have specified in the Resource/android/appicon.png file. h5. Test Environment Mac OS X 10.8.5 Ti SDK 3.1.3.GA, 3.2.0.GA Ti CLI 3.2.1-beta3 Android 2.3.4(API 10) h5. Step for Reproduces # Create default Ti classic project in 3.2.0 Studio # Remove appicon.png from Resources/android # Put appicon.png in Resources that is different from the default Ti logo appicon.png file # Build for android device # appicon not changed Thanks """"",title+description
TIMOB-16313,12,"""iOS 7: TextArea: TextArea with property Ti.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL will highlight all valid links when you press on a link""","""""""*Details:*  When you create a TextArea with property autoLink set to Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL, then all links will be highlighted when you press on a link.     *This is not a regression as this occurs in 3.2.0.GA and only occurs on an iOS 7 device.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Install the following app.js to a iOS 7 device:      2. Press on any of the links before the address e.g. the first link    *Actual:* All links will be highlighted (see highlight.png).  *Expected:* Only the pressed link should be highlighted.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 7: TextArea: TextArea with property Ti.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL will highlight all valid links when you press on a link
Description: """"*Details:* When you create a TextArea with property autoLink set to Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL, then all links will be highlighted when you press on a link. *This is not a regression as this occurs in 3.2.0.GA and only occurs on an iOS 7 device.* *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Install the following app.js to a iOS 7 device: 2. Press on any of the links before the address e.g. the first link *Actual:* All links will be highlighted (see highlight.png). *Expected:* Only the pressed link should be highlighted.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16312,12,"""iOS 7: TextArea: Maps app is not launched if you select an address in a TextArea with property Ti.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL""","""""""*Details:* When you create a TextArea with property autoLink set to Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL, then the iOS maps will not launch if you select an address in the text area.    *This is not a regression as this occurs in 3.2.0.GA and only occurs on an iOS 7 device.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Install the following app.js to a iOS 7 device:      2. Press on the address    *Actual:* Maps does not get launched.  *Expected:* Maps should be launched after pressing on the address.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 7: TextArea: Maps app is not launched if you select an address in a TextArea with property Ti.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL
Description: """"*Details:* When you create a TextArea with property autoLink set to Titanium.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL, then the iOS maps will not launch if you select an address in the text area. *This is not a regression as this occurs in 3.2.0.GA and only occurs on an iOS 7 device.* *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Install the following app.js to a iOS 7 device: 2. Press on the address *Actual:* Maps does not get launched. *Expected:* Maps should be launched after pressing on the address.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16311,12,"""Android: HTML JavaScript files not loading with absolute paths""","""""""h2. Problem description    When loading a HTML page in a WebView that includes a JS file, the JS file is not loaded if the URL is absolute or uses the app:// protocol.        Both """"""""app://lib/html/js/test.js"""""""" and """"""""/lib/html/js/test.js"""""""" fail.    h2. Code to reproduce    /app.js      /lib/html/test.html      /lib/html/js/test.js      h2. Steps to reproduce  Using the code above, build the app for emulator, device or distribution.    h2. Note  This is NOT a CLI related bug. The CLI puts the JS file in the correct location.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTML JavaScript files not loading with absolute paths
Description: """"h2. Problem description When loading a HTML page in a WebView that includes a JS file, the JS file is not loaded if the URL is absolute or uses the app:// protocol. Both """"""""app://lib/html/js/test.js"""""""" and """"""""/lib/html/js/test.js"""""""" fail. h2. Code to reproduce /app.js /lib/html/test.html /lib/html/js/test.js h2. Steps to reproduce Using the code above, build the app for emulator, device or distribution. h2. Note This is NOT a CLI related bug. The CLI puts the JS file in the correct location.""""",title+description
