TIMOB-16306,12,"""Code Processor: Fails when only minimum Android SDK is installed""","""""""h5.Description  Code analysis will fail to display result if only Android SDK 2.3.3 (API 10) is installed.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Remove or rename any previous Android SDK folder you have  2. Make sure Studio is not detecting any Android SDK at all  3. Run the configuration wizard and install Android 2.3.3  4. Create a classic project  5. Run the code analysis on the project    h5.Expected Result  Code analysis should show the results of the project    h5.Actual Result  User is prompted with an alert saying that Android SDK must have 2.3.3 or higher installed""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Processor: Fails when only minimum Android SDK is installed
Description: """"h5.Description Code analysis will fail to display result if only Android SDK 2.3.3 (API 10) is installed. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Remove or rename any previous Android SDK folder you have 2. Make sure Studio is not detecting any Android SDK at all 3. Run the configuration wizard and install Android 2.3.3 4. Create a classic project 5. Run the code analysis on the project h5.Expected Result Code analysis should show the results of the project h5.Actual Result User is prompted with an alert saying that Android SDK must have 2.3.3 or higher installed""""",title+description
TIMOB-16305,12,"""Android: Alloy Projects Stuck at Splash screen (Samsung Note 10.1)""","""""""On a Samsung Galaxy Note 10.1 (2012 Edition), any project that is built with Alloy gets stuck at the splash screen. Projects built in """"""""Classic"""""""" have no such issue.     When the project is built in """"""""Debug"""""""" mode (connected to the debugger) it works as expected. However, if this app is restarted on the device, without the debugger, is gets stuck at the splash screen.     Application log    -- Start application log -----------------------------------------------------  [INFO] :   TiApplication: (main) [0,0] checkpoint, app created.  [INFO] :   TiApplication: (main) [103,103] Titanium 3.3.0 (2014/01/14 17:57 5d19c60)  [INFO] :   I/dalvikvm-heap: Grow heap (frag case) to 7.942MB for 272514-byte allocation  [INFO] :   I/dalvikvm-heap: Grow heap (frag case) to 8.385MB for 136265-byte allocation  [INFO] :   TiApplication: (main) [410,513] Titanium Javascript runtime: v8  [WARN] :   V8Object: Runtime disposed, cannot set property 'userAgent'  [INFO] :   TiRootActivity: (main) [0,0] checkpoint, on root activity create, savedInstanceState: null  [INFO] :   TiApplication: (main) [0,0] Analytics have been disabled  [INFO] :   I/dalvikvm-heap: Grow heap (frag case) to 8.833MB for 614416-byte allocation  [INFO] :   TiRootActivity: (main) [0,0] checkpoint, on root activity resume. activity = com.mycompany.myappname@41d0c9c8    Anything in alloy.js never runs.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Alloy Projects Stuck at Splash screen (Samsung Note 10.1)
Description: """"On a Samsung Galaxy Note 10.1 (2012 Edition), any project that is built with Alloy gets stuck at the splash screen. Projects built in """"""""Classic"""""""" have no such issue. When the project is built in """"""""Debug"""""""" mode (connected to the debugger) it works as expected. However, if this app is restarted on the device, without the debugger, is gets stuck at the splash screen. Application log -- Start application log ----------------------------------------------------- [INFO] : TiApplication: (main) [0,0] checkpoint, app created. [INFO] : TiApplication: (main) [103,103] Titanium 3.3.0 (2014/01/14 17:57 5d19c60) [INFO] : I/dalvikvm-heap: Grow heap (frag case) to 7.942MB for 272514-byte allocation [INFO] : I/dalvikvm-heap: Grow heap (frag case) to 8.385MB for 136265-byte allocation [INFO] : TiApplication: (main) [410,513] Titanium Javascript runtime: v8 [WARN] : V8Object: Runtime disposed, cannot set property 'userAgent' [INFO] : TiRootActivity: (main) [0,0] checkpoint, on root activity create, savedInstanceState: null [INFO] : TiApplication: (main) [0,0] Analytics have been disabled [INFO] : I/dalvikvm-heap: Grow heap (frag case) to 8.833MB for 614416-byte allocation [INFO] : TiRootActivity: (main) [0,0] checkpoint, on root activity resume. activity = com.mycompany.myappname@41d0c9c8 Anything in alloy.js never runs. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16303,12,"""BlackBerry: Enabling services after project creation will prevent building BlackBerry project""","""""""h5.Description  Enabling services through tiapp.xml breaks the BlackBerry project    The three scenarios tested are;  Disable analytics in project creation wizard: Project builds successfully.  Enabled analytics in project creation wizard: Project builds successfully.  Enable the previous disabled project: Project fails to build.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Create a project with services disabled  2. Run the project on device  3. Enable the services  4. Run the project on device  5. Clean the project  6. Run the project on device    h5.Expected Result  Steps 2, 4 & 6: project should install successfully    h5.Actual Result  2. Project builds successfully  4 & 6. Project fails to build""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Enabling services after project creation will prevent building BlackBerry project
Description: """"h5.Description Enabling services through tiapp.xml breaks the BlackBerry project The three scenarios tested are; Disable analytics in project creation wizard: Project builds successfully. Enabled analytics in project creation wizard: Project builds successfully. Enable the previous disabled project: Project fails to build. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Create a project with services disabled 2. Run the project on device 3. Enable the services 4. Run the project on device 5. Clean the project 6. Run the project on device h5.Expected Result Steps 2, 4 & 6: project should install successfully h5.Actual Result 2. Project builds successfully 4 & 6. Project fails to build""""",title+description
TIMOB-16302,12,"""Android:Can't build for publishing with an old key""","""""""h4. Problem Description    When you are using a pre-made key (let's say, if you created that one in a previous version of Ti Studio and now you are using it in the new one), you will get an error in the Ti Studio's console saying:        even if the password is the right one to the key (if you try it with the wrong password, it will properly complain about it).     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android:Can't build for publishing with an old key
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When you are using a pre-made key (let's say, if you created that one in a previous version of Ti Studio and now you are using it in the new one), you will get an error in the Ti Studio's console saying: even if the password is the right one to the key (if you try it with the wrong password, it will properly complain about it). """"",title+description
TIMOB-16301,12,"""Android: Module packaging fails on Windows""","""""""h5.Description  Packaging an Android module to any of the three options from within Studio will fail with the following console output        I have attached a file containing the output of the studio log.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Create an Android module  2. Package the module to the Titanium SDK    h5.Expected Result  The module should package successfully    h5.Actual Result  The package fails""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Module packaging fails on Windows
Description: """"h5.Description Packaging an Android module to any of the three options from within Studio will fail with the following console output I have attached a file containing the output of the studio log. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Create an Android module 2. Package the module to the Titanium SDK h5.Expected Result The module should package successfully h5.Actual Result The package fails""""",title+description
TIMOB-16299,12,"""iOS: Expose Navigation Bar Management on all WindowProxy objects""","""""""Titanium developers have expressed an interest in nesting top level window managers (Tab hosting a NavigationWindow, NavigationWindow hosting TabGroup etc). While it is possible to do that there is no support for NavigationBar management in the WindowProxy object. The NavigationBar management is only exposed in the TiUIWindowProxy object.     This ticket is a request to expose that functionality on the base WindowProxy object.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Expose Navigation Bar Management on all WindowProxy objects
Description: """"Titanium developers have expressed an interest in nesting top level window managers (Tab hosting a NavigationWindow, NavigationWindow hosting TabGroup etc). While it is possible to do that there is no support for NavigationBar management in the WindowProxy object. The NavigationBar management is only exposed in the TiUIWindowProxy object. This ticket is a request to expose that functionality on the base WindowProxy object.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16298,12,"""CLI: Running """"ti create -p"""" throws errors, instead should ask what platform you wish to use""","""""""h5.Description  Running """"""""ti create"""""""" prompts the user to pick a platform for the project.  Running """"""""ti create -p"""""""" skips that step and prompts for the App ID.  No matter what is entered the user will get      h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Open a terminal window  2. Run 'ti create -p'  3. Type in a valid App ID    h5.Expected Result  The CLI should notice the missing parameters for the platform and ask for a valid input.    h5.Actual Result  The CLI moves on to the App ID, then fails to create.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Running """"ti create -p"""" throws errors, instead should ask what platform you wish to use
Description: """"h5.Description Running """"""""ti create"""""""" prompts the user to pick a platform for the project. Running """"""""ti create -p"""""""" skips that step and prompts for the App ID. No matter what is entered the user will get h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Open a terminal window 2. Run 'ti create -p' 3. Type in a valid App ID h5.Expected Result The CLI should notice the missing parameters for the platform and ask for a valid input. h5.Actual Result The CLI moves on to the App ID, then fails to create.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16297,12,"""Android: builds throw errors when only minimum Android SDK is installed""","""""""h5.Description  If you only have Android SDK 2.3.3 installed then projects will throw an error while building to device or simulator.    With only 2.3.3 installed, the user is alerted with """"""""Please download SDK targets (API level 10 or newer)""""""""  If the user install API 11 (3.0) then everything works fine.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Install Android SDK 2.3.3 and remove any others you have installed.  2. Run the project on device.    h5.Expected Result  Project should to install to device without any errors    h5.Actual Result  Project installs to device but throws errors""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: builds throw errors when only minimum Android SDK is installed
Description: """"h5.Description If you only have Android SDK 2.3.3 installed then projects will throw an error while building to device or simulator. With only 2.3.3 installed, the user is alerted with """"""""Please download SDK targets (API level 10 or newer)"""""""" If the user install API 11 (3.0) then everything works fine. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Install Android SDK 2.3.3 and remove any others you have installed. 2. Run the project on device. h5.Expected Result Project should to install to device without any errors h5.Actual Result Project installs to device but throws errors""""",title+description
TIMOB-16296,12,"""Android: Uncaught errors on TiWebChromeClient""","""""""h6.Use case  Need Bing maps to display in an app and had it doing so in Android OS 4.3 on most Android devices.  However, it doesn't seem to work anymore on Android OS 4.4 KitKat. Attached stripped down version works on iPhone and on 4.3, however not on 4.4 and few Android versions like 4.0.x.     h6.Steps to reproduce  1) Get and run sample attached  2) Watch monitor console    h6.Test results  iOS 7.0 - Maps fully loaded and event logged.  {quote}  Jan 22 13:00:16 lAlO BingMapsKitKat[284] <Warning>: [WARN] In Maps WebView  Jan 22 13:00:16 lAlO BingMapsKitKat[284] <Warning>: [DEBUG] Firing app event: app:updateWebView  Jan 22 13:00:16 lAlO BingMapsKitKat[284] <Warning>: [WARN] [       latitude = """"""""76.2361273"""""""";       longitude = """"""""36.8527915"""""""";   }  {quote}    Android 4.0.4 (Xperia) & 4.4 (nexus 7) SDK 3.2.0.GA & 3.3.0.v20140121162449 does not render Map and eventually throw """"""""Uncaught ReferenceErrors"""""""":  {quote}  01-22 14:59:31.826: W/TiAPI(18562): In Maps WebView  01-22 14:59:32.256: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.android.defcontainer (pid 18452) has died.  01-22 14:59:32.276: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.android.keychain (pid 18526) has died.  01-22 14:59:32.366: W/TiAPI(18562): undefined  01-22 14:59:32.426: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.google.android.partnersetup (pid 18587) has died.  01-22 14:59:32.456: I/TiWebChromeClient.console(18562): (main) [6082,6082] Uncaught TypeError: Cannot call method 'appendChild' of null (1:http://ecn.dev.virtualearth.net/mapcontrol/v7.0/7.0.20131202145924.46/js/en-us/veapicore.js)  01-22 14:59:32.476: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.android.voicedialer (pid 18473) has died.  01-22 14:59:32.566: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.noshufou.android.su (pid 18507) has died.  01-22 14:59:32.676: W/V8Object(18695): Runtime disposed, cannot set property 'userAgent'  {quote}    {quote}  01-22 14:43:44.196: W/TiAPI(12171): In Maps WebView  01-22 14:43:45.286: I/TiWebChromeClient.console(12171): (main) [41984,82089] Uncaught ReferenceError: Microsoft is not defined (63:file:///android_asset/Resources/web/index.html)  {quote}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Uncaught errors on TiWebChromeClient
Description: """"h6.Use case Need Bing maps to display in an app and had it doing so in Android OS 4.3 on most Android devices. However, it doesn't seem to work anymore on Android OS 4.4 KitKat. Attached stripped down version works on iPhone and on 4.3, however not on 4.4 and few Android versions like 4.0.x. h6.Steps to reproduce 1) Get and run sample attached 2) Watch monitor console h6.Test results iOS 7.0 - Maps fully loaded and event logged. {quote} Jan 22 13:00:16 lAlO BingMapsKitKat[284] <Warning>: [WARN] In Maps WebView Jan 22 13:00:16 lAlO BingMapsKitKat[284] <Warning>: [DEBUG] Firing app event: app:updateWebView Jan 22 13:00:16 lAlO BingMapsKitKat[284] <Warning>: [WARN] [ latitude = """"""""76.2361273""""""""; longitude = """"""""36.8527915""""""""; } {quote} Android 4.0.4 (Xperia) & 4.4 (nexus 7) SDK 3.2.0.GA & 3.3.0.v20140121162449 does not render Map and eventually throw """"""""Uncaught ReferenceErrors"""""""": {quote} 01-22 14:59:31.826: W/TiAPI(18562): In Maps WebView 01-22 14:59:32.256: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.android.defcontainer (pid 18452) has died. 01-22 14:59:32.276: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.android.keychain (pid 18526) has died. 01-22 14:59:32.366: W/TiAPI(18562): undefined 01-22 14:59:32.426: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.google.android.partnersetup (pid 18587) has died. 01-22 14:59:32.456: I/TiWebChromeClient.console(18562): (main) [6082,6082] Uncaught TypeError: Cannot call method 'appendChild' of null (1:http://ecn.dev.virtualearth.net/mapcontrol/v7.0/7.0.20131202145924.46/js/en-us/veapicore.js) 01-22 14:59:32.476: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.android.voicedialer (pid 18473) has died. 01-22 14:59:32.566: I/ActivityManager(224): Process com.noshufou.android.su (pid 18507) has died. 01-22 14:59:32.676: W/V8Object(18695): Runtime disposed, cannot set property 'userAgent' {quote} {quote} 01-22 14:43:44.196: W/TiAPI(12171): In Maps WebView 01-22 14:43:45.286: I/TiWebChromeClient.console(12171): (main) [41984,82089] Uncaught ReferenceError: Microsoft is not defined (63:file:///android_asset/Resources/web/index.html) {quote}""""",title+description
TIMOB-16295,12,"""Ti.Filesystem.isExternalStoragePresent() always returns true on Android devices""","""""""Any app released on Android which queries isExternalStoragePresent using the Ti.Filesystem method will return true whether external storage is present or not. This includes devices that have no facility for external storage (such as Nexus 7). """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Filesystem.isExternalStoragePresent() always returns true on Android devices
Description: """"Any app released on Android which queries isExternalStoragePresent using the Ti.Filesystem method will return true whether external storage is present or not. This includes devices that have no facility for external storage (such as Nexus 7). """"",title+description
TIMOB-16294,12,"""iOS: ToImage() functionality on TabbedBar/ButtonBar removes text of the selected tab in image""","""""""h2. Description  When we implement ToImage functionality over a view which contains a tabbedbar/buttonbar, then the resulting image that is generated doesn't show the text on the selected index of the tab.    h2. Steps to Reproduce    1. Run the app in simulator  2. tap on the button """"""""Click me""""""""  3. Go to the application documents directory in iphone simulator folder on the path """"""""/Users/<username name>/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/7.0/Applications/<app guid>/Documents""""""""  4. check out the image """"""""test.png""""""""    h2. Test Code  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ToImage() functionality on TabbedBar/ButtonBar removes text of the selected tab in image
Description: """"h2. Description When we implement ToImage functionality over a view which contains a tabbedbar/buttonbar, then the resulting image that is generated doesn't show the text on the selected index of the tab. h2. Steps to Reproduce 1. Run the app in simulator 2. tap on the button """"""""Click me"""""""" 3. Go to the application documents directory in iphone simulator folder on the path """"""""/Users/<username name>/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/7.0/Applications/<app guid>/Documents"""""""" 4. check out the image """"""""test.png"""""""" h2. Test Code """"",title+description
TIMOB-16293,12,"""CLI: When showing a prompt, display what the direct CLI option would be""","""""""The prompts in the new Titanium CLI are great! But of course using CLI options and flags is much faster once you know them. To help users learn about the options, prompts should not inform what the related option or flag is.    For example:    h1. Before      h1. After  """"""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: When showing a prompt, display what the direct CLI option would be
Description: """"The prompts in the new Titanium CLI are great! But of course using CLI options and flags is much faster once you know them. To help users learn about the options, prompts should not inform what the related option or flag is. For example: h1. Before h1. After """"",title+description
TIMOB-16292,12,"""iOS: Behavior for titanium build --build-only is now different with 3.2.0 release""","""""""titanium build --build-only --platform ios --device-family universal --target dist-appstore --project-dir /code/ --distribution-name 'cert' --pp-uuid id    Originally when you ran the command it just created the app and then you could run xcode to create the ipa.  now it fires off xcode and shows the Organizer - Archives.  It seems to build correctly but is very annoying.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Behavior for titanium build --build-only is now different with 3.2.0 release
Description: """"titanium build --build-only --platform ios --device-family universal --target dist-appstore --project-dir /code/ --distribution-name 'cert' --pp-uuid id Originally when you ran the command it just created the app and then you could run xcode to create the ipa. now it fires off xcode and shows the Organizer - Archives. It seems to build correctly but is very annoying.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16291,12,"""Android: Maps V2 displays black with anyDensity=false""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce    Create a project that use Android Maps V2 and set tag anyDensity=false.    SDK: 3.2.0    Android: Samsung GS 4 mini with Andorid 4.2.2    I am using all the steps of this link: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/guide/Google_Maps_v2_for_Android    h3. Actual Result  When opening the app shows a black window instead the map.    h3. Expected Result  The map should open like when I use anyDensity=true""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Maps V2 displays black with anyDensity=false
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce Create a project that use Android Maps V2 and set tag anyDensity=false. SDK: 3.2.0 Android: Samsung GS 4 mini with Andorid 4.2.2 I am using all the steps of this link: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/guide/Google_Maps_v2_for_Android h3. Actual Result When opening the app shows a black window instead the map. h3. Expected Result The map should open like when I use anyDensity=true""""",title+description
TIMOB-16288,12,"""Anvil: Integrate test results with CI build page""","""""""Once a build has been completed in the CI build, we need to run it though Anvil.    We wish to add a line below the CI builds to indicate the results of Anvil testing. As a suggestion, below each of the SDK builds, we should show the results at a very high-level    Since the testing is all done on OS X machines, we should probably indicate that in the results as perhaps in the future we could have more machines for more platforms;    For each test configuration, show a check or an X indicating if the test succeeded 100% or failed.    Hovering over the test shows the number of succeeded vs failed tests    Clicking on the test shows the test results.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Anvil: Integrate test results with CI build page
Description: """"Once a build has been completed in the CI build, we need to run it though Anvil. We wish to add a line below the CI builds to indicate the results of Anvil testing. As a suggestion, below each of the SDK builds, we should show the results at a very high-level Since the testing is all done on OS X machines, we should probably indicate that in the results as perhaps in the future we could have more machines for more platforms; For each test configuration, show a check or an X indicating if the test succeeded 100% or failed. Hovering over the test shows the number of succeeded vs failed tests Clicking on the test shows the test results. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16287,12,"""iOS: image taken in landscape orients itself to portrait""","""""""Image taken in landscape orients itself to portrait. This occurs in SDK:3.2.0.GA & 3.1.3.GA as well, Hence not a regression  Steps To Reproduce:  1. Create app using below code.  2. Run app  3. In landscape orientation, click picture    Actual: Picture orients itself in portrait mode.    Expected: Picture must remain in landscape mode until orientation is changed    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: image taken in landscape orients itself to portrait
Description: """"Image taken in landscape orients itself to portrait. This occurs in SDK:3.2.0.GA & 3.1.3.GA as well, Hence not a regression Steps To Reproduce: 1. Create app using below code. 2. Run app 3. In landscape orientation, click picture Actual: Picture orients itself in portrait mode. Expected: Picture must remain in landscape mode until orientation is changed """"",title+description
