TIMOB-16222,12,"""Kitchen Sink: Pressing Return Key on keyboard does not move the cursor on to the new/next line in TextArea ""","""""""Pressing Return Key on keyboard does not move the cursor on to the new/next line in TextArea.      Not a regression.  Issue occurs in 3.2.0.GA AND 3.1.3.GA also    Steps to reproduce:    1. Install KitchenSink BaseUI>views>scroll Views>Scroll Views TextArea   2. Enter some text, tap return     Expected Result:  2. On pressing return it must go to a new line.    Actual Result:  2. Keyboard disappears.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen Sink: Pressing Return Key on keyboard does not move the cursor on to the new/next line in TextArea
Description: """"Pressing Return Key on keyboard does not move the cursor on to the new/next line in TextArea. Not a regression. Issue occurs in 3.2.0.GA AND 3.1.3.GA also Steps to reproduce: 1. Install KitchenSink BaseUI>views>scroll Views>Scroll Views TextArea 2. Enter some text, tap return Expected Result: 2. On pressing return it must go to a new line. Actual Result: 2. Keyboard disappears. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16221,12,"""iOS: TextField: Change event is not being fired when changing the textField value using Button click""","""""""Change event is not being fired when changing the textField value using Button click.      Not a Regression.  Since issue occurs in 3.2.0.GA, 3.1.3.GA also.      Steps to reproduce:  1. Deploy the test case to device.  2. Tap on textField. Console logs prints logs(change event being fired)  3. Tap on Button.  4. The change event is not fired.(where as in android it gets fired)  5. After that again tap on textfield. Console logs prints logs(change event being fired)     Expected Result:  The change event of textField should also get fired when value gets changed on button click.    Actual Result:  Change event not fired.    Working fine on Android.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TextField: Change event is not being fired when changing the textField value using Button click
Description: """"Change event is not being fired when changing the textField value using Button click. Not a Regression. Since issue occurs in 3.2.0.GA, 3.1.3.GA also. Steps to reproduce: 1. Deploy the test case to device. 2. Tap on textField. Console logs prints logs(change event being fired) 3. Tap on Button. 4. The change event is not fired.(where as in android it gets fired) 5. After that again tap on textfield. Console logs prints logs(change event being fired) Expected Result: The change event of textField should also get fired when value gets changed on button click. Actual Result: Change event not fired. Working fine on Android. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16220,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.WebView doesn't trigger 'load' event when having 'touchEnabled' set to false""","""""""When you add a Titanium.UI.WebView with the property _touchEnabled_ set to _false_, the _load_ event will not get triggered anymore.    As the documentation for WebViews ^*^ describes for using the _evalJS()_ method, I'm calling the _evalJS_ method from the _load_ event.    ^*^ http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Communication_Between_WebViews_and_Titanium    Tested on iOS only.    Sample: someWebView1 load event does not get triggered while someWebView2 load event does get triggered.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.WebView doesn't trigger 'load' event when having 'touchEnabled' set to false
Description: """"When you add a Titanium.UI.WebView with the property _touchEnabled_ set to _false_, the _load_ event will not get triggered anymore. As the documentation for WebViews ^*^ describes for using the _evalJS()_ method, I'm calling the _evalJS_ method from the _load_ event. ^*^ http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Communication_Between_WebViews_and_Titanium Tested on iOS only. Sample: someWebView1 load event does not get triggered while someWebView2 load event does get triggered. """"",title+description
