TIMOB-16215,12,"""CLI: Android: Show error and abort build if app name contains an ampersand""","""""""If you try to build an app that has an ampersand in the app name, then the build completes, but adb is unable to install the app to the emulator/device.        The solution is to simply disallow ampersands in the app name. When creating a new app, only allow ampersands in the name if Android is NOT selected, however do show an warning.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android: Show error and abort build if app name contains an ampersand
Description: """"If you try to build an app that has an ampersand in the app name, then the build completes, but adb is unable to install the app to the emulator/device. The solution is to simply disallow ampersands in the app name. When creating a new app, only allow ampersands in the name if Android is NOT selected, however do show an warning.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16214,12,"""""""Unsupported zip format"""" thrown by CLI""","""""""When building both alloy and traditional projects to Android the error """"""""Invalid or unsupported zip format. No END header found"""""""" is thrown.  This is actually caused because the crittercism.jar file was 0 bytes and is corrupt (this ticket [APPTS-2530|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/appts-2530].)    But [~<USER> wants this to be encapsulated in a Try/Catch block to not fail the build.  The method is getNativeModuleBindings(something.jar).    Error caused in the first place by """"""",Bug,"Title: """"Unsupported zip format"""" thrown by CLI
Description: """"When building both alloy and traditional projects to Android the error """"""""Invalid or unsupported zip format. No END header found"""""""" is thrown. This is actually caused because the crittercism.jar file was 0 bytes and is corrupt (this ticket [APPTS-2530|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/appts-2530].) But [~<USER> wants this to be encapsulated in a Try/Catch block to not fail the build. The method is getNativeModuleBindings(something.jar). Error caused in the first place by """"",title+description
TIMOB-16213,12,"""CLI: Packaging - CLI should throw a warning if you are using a SHA256withRSA signature keystore when packaging to a non-KitKat device""","""""""If you try to package an app (from CLI) to a non-KitKat device, then the CLI should throw a warning if you signed the packaged app with a SHA256withRSA signature algorithm keystore. And, indicate to the user to use a SHA1withRSA signature keystore for a non-KitKat device.    Java 1.6.X only ships with SHA1withRSA.  Java 1.7.X ships with both SHA1withRSA and SHA256withRSA.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Packaging - CLI should throw a warning if you are using a SHA256withRSA signature keystore when packaging to a non-KitKat device
Description: """"If you try to package an app (from CLI) to a non-KitKat device, then the CLI should throw a warning if you signed the packaged app with a SHA256withRSA signature algorithm keystore. And, indicate to the user to use a SHA1withRSA signature keystore for a non-KitKat device. Java 1.6.X only ships with SHA1withRSA. Java 1.7.X ships with both SHA1withRSA and SHA256withRSA.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16212,12,"""Android: ActionBar expose setDisplayShowHomeEnabled and setDisplayShowTitleEnabled""","""""""h3. Request     Expose the setDisplayShowHomeEnabled and setDisplayShowTitleEnabled methods from the Android actionBar in order to allow the user to disable the action bar icon and title in order to let the navigation tabs to collapse into the main actionBar when user is using a split actionBar and TabGroup(as shown on the right in actionbar.png).    h3. Current Behavior    Even whene user is able to split the actionBar the TitleBar will remain always on top of the tabs when using the tabgroup even when there no title or icon(splitActionBar.png).    h3. Reference    http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/actionbar.html  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: ActionBar expose setDisplayShowHomeEnabled and setDisplayShowTitleEnabled
Description: """"h3. Request Expose the setDisplayShowHomeEnabled and setDisplayShowTitleEnabled methods from the Android actionBar in order to allow the user to disable the action bar icon and title in order to let the navigation tabs to collapse into the main actionBar when user is using a split actionBar and TabGroup(as shown on the right in actionbar.png). h3. Current Behavior Even whene user is able to split the actionBar the TitleBar will remain always on top of the tabs when using the tabgroup even when there no title or icon(splitActionBar.png). h3. Reference http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/actionbar.html """"",title+description
TIMOB-16209,12,"""iOS: Kitchen Sink : Cannot stop audio recording""","""""""  Steps to reproduce:   1) Install Kitchen Sink on iPhone or iPhone Simulator  2) Launch Kitchen Sink  3) Choose Phone Tab > Sound > Record  4) Hit Start Recording.  5) Hit Stop Recording.      Result:  Recording never stops when Stop Recording button pressed.    Expected Result:  Recording should stop when Stop Recording button pressed.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchen Sink : Cannot stop audio recording
Description: """" Steps to reproduce: 1) Install Kitchen Sink on iPhone or iPhone Simulator 2) Launch Kitchen Sink 3) Choose Phone Tab > Sound > Record 4) Hit Start Recording. 5) Hit Stop Recording. Result: Recording never stops when Stop Recording button pressed. Expected Result: Recording should stop when Stop Recording button pressed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16208,12,"""iOS: Window focus and blur events no longer fire after hiding a window""","""""""Create a window which has focus and blur events. These events fire correctly when you open and close a new window over top. However, if you open a new window over top and then hide that new window, the window below no longer fires focus and blur events, nor do any other windows that are opened and closed.    Consider the following code below that reproduces the issue. As you open and close win1, the focus and blur events of baseWindow fire correctly. However after you open window 2 and then hide it, no more focus and blur events are fired for baseWindow. You could also add focus and blur events to win1, and these wouldn't fire after hiding win2 either.        This worked fine with Titanium SDK 3.1.x and iOS 6 but no longer does. I also tried setting the opacity and height of win2 to 0 but it had no affect. As long as win2 is open (but hidden), the focus and blur events of other windows will not fire.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window focus and blur events no longer fire after hiding a window
Description: """"Create a window which has focus and blur events. These events fire correctly when you open and close a new window over top. However, if you open a new window over top and then hide that new window, the window below no longer fires focus and blur events, nor do any other windows that are opened and closed. Consider the following code below that reproduces the issue. As you open and close win1, the focus and blur events of baseWindow fire correctly. However after you open window 2 and then hide it, no more focus and blur events are fired for baseWindow. You could also add focus and blur events to win1, and these wouldn't fire after hiding win2 either. This worked fine with Titanium SDK 3.1.x and iOS 6 but no longer does. I also tried setting the opacity and height of win2 to 0 but it had no affect. As long as win2 is open (but hidden), the focus and blur events of other windows will not fire.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16207,12,"""Android: Setting a property that expect a boolean to a string throws ClassCastException""","""""""Originally reported as an Alloy issue, this is a platform issue. Setting a property to a string that expects a boolean will work on iOS but throw an exception on Android.    Test case: returnKeyEnabled expects boolean, drop the following into a new classic project, build for Android, tap the text field then with or without entering text in the field, tap the Done (return) button to cause the crash.    App works as-is on iOS (7.0 simulator)          """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Setting a property that expect a boolean to a string throws ClassCastException
Description: """"Originally reported as an Alloy issue, this is a platform issue. Setting a property to a string that expects a boolean will work on iOS but throw an exception on Android. Test case: returnKeyEnabled expects boolean, drop the following into a new classic project, build for Android, tap the text field then with or without entering text in the field, tap the Done (return) button to cause the crash. App works as-is on iOS (7.0 simulator) """"",title+description
TIMOB-16206,12,"""Android: ImageView containing large image 3264x2448 fail to upload""","""""""Image having large size of approx 3264x2448 fail to upload.  Works fine in SDK: 3.1.3.GA. hence it is a regression    Steps To Reproduce:  1. Create app using code below  2. Use Image of size 3264x2448    Actual: Warning appears  [WARN] :   OpenGLRenderer: Bitmap too large to be uploaded into a texture (3264x2448, max=2048x2048)  [WARN] :   OpenGLRenderer: Bitmap too large to be uploaded into a texture (3264x2448, max=2048x2048)    Expected:  Image should be uploaded.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView containing large image 3264x2448 fail to upload
Description: """"Image having large size of approx 3264x2448 fail to upload. Works fine in SDK: 3.1.3.GA. hence it is a regression Steps To Reproduce: 1. Create app using code below 2. Use Image of size 3264x2448 Actual: Warning appears [WARN] : OpenGLRenderer: Bitmap too large to be uploaded into a texture (3264x2448, max=2048x2048) [WARN] : OpenGLRenderer: Bitmap too large to be uploaded into a texture (3264x2448, max=2048x2048) Expected: Image should be uploaded. """"",title+description
