TIMOB-16194,12,"""Alloy: Memory leaking if animation call callback""","""""""Application is leaking if animation call callback function. If is animation without callback everything is alright...     I have putted to the archive whole project including video from the app & instruments.    (If is possible please reupload it on some better place / pick up only important informations. Archive can be deleted in the future)    http://www.filedropper.com/memleak""""""",Bug,"Title: Alloy: Memory leaking if animation call callback
Description: """"Application is leaking if animation call callback function. If is animation without callback everything is alright... I have putted to the archive whole project including video from the app & instruments. (If is possible please reupload it on some better place / pick up only important informations. Archive can be deleted in the future) http://www.filedropper.com/memleak""""",title+description
TIMOB-16193,12,"""Android: Animation - not possible to rotate and resize an object simultaneously""",""""""" h2. Problem    On Android rotating and resizing an object with one animation is not possible, only one effect at a single time seems to be allowed (rotating OR resizing, not both of them). Up until version 3.2.0 I used a module (https://github.com/<USER>ti-android-animation) that is now integrated right into the Titanium SDK and therefore can't be included any more (see: http://developer.<USER>com/question/160709/studio-320-with-<USER>animation-module). Nevertheless, the desired animation is not possible. It works on iOS though.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var view = Ti.UI.createView({   backgroundColor: 'red',   width: 100,   height: 100  });  view.addEventListener('click', doAnimation);  win.add(view);  win.open();    function doAnimation() {   var _2DMatrix = Ti.UI.create2DMatrix();     var animation = Ti.UI.createAnimation({    transform: _2DMatrix.rotate(100),    duration: 2000,    width: 300,    height: 300   });     view.animate(animation);  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Animation - not possible to rotate and resize an object simultaneously
Description: """" h2. Problem On Android rotating and resizing an object with one animation is not possible, only one effect at a single time seems to be allowed (rotating OR resizing, not both of them). Up until version 3.2.0 I used a module (https://github.com/<USER>ti-android-animation) that is now integrated right into the Titanium SDK and therefore can't be included any more (see: http://developer.<USER>com/question/160709/studio-320-with-<USER>animation-module). Nevertheless, the desired animation is not possible. It works on iOS though. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'red', width: 100, height: 100 }); view.addEventListener('click', doAnimation); win.add(view); win.open(); function doAnimation() { var _2DMatrix = Ti.UI.create2DMatrix(); var animation = Ti.UI.createAnimation({ transform: _2DMatrix.rotate(100), duration: 2000, width: 300, height: 300 }); view.animate(animation); } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-16191,12,"""CLI: Add Java login test to CLI connection diagnosis tool""","""""""On the heels of APPTS-1213 and other SSLPeerUnverifiedExceptions, I would like to update our configuration test to also test logging in via Java as opposed to Node.js    I have to believe there is something weird about the <USER>login library or certificate.    Using the existing network proxy settings for the connection test:    * Make a simple app to use the straight Java lib to log in to 360  * Make a simple app using the 360 lib to log in to 360    https://github.com/<USER>titanium-connection-test  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Add Java login test to CLI connection diagnosis tool
Description: """"On the heels of APPTS-1213 and other SSLPeerUnverifiedExceptions, I would like to update our configuration test to also test logging in via Java as opposed to Node.js I have to believe there is something weird about the <USER>login library or certificate. Using the existing network proxy settings for the connection test: * Make a simple app to use the straight Java lib to log in to 360 * Make a simple app using the 360 lib to log in to 360 https://github.com/<USER>titanium-connection-test """"",title+description
TIMOB-16190,12,"""Getting """"Failed to compile java source files"""" error when build for device/emulator.""","""""""h5.Description;  Note: I am not exactly sure how I started getting this error but I remember I enabled <USER>services for my app which downloaded the apm & touchtest modules & during updating apm module the <USER>just froze & I had to restart the studio.After restarting I saw that the modules are present in the modules folder,but not sure if these modules got corrupt, ticket for the same : https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TISTUD-6026.    1. Create an alloy/ classic app.  2. Enable <USER>services for the app.  2. Build for device/simulator.    Actual Results:  1. We get the following erros logs:      2. I tried removing the modules from the tiapp.xml & re build the app & I get the error logs below:      h5. Expected Results:  1. We should not see any errors & the app should launch successfully.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Getting """"Failed to compile java source files"""" error when build for device/emulator.
Description: """"h5.Description; Note: I am not exactly sure how I started getting this error but I remember I enabled <USER>services for my app which downloaded the apm & touchtest modules & during updating apm module the <USER>just froze & I had to restart the studio.After restarting I saw that the modules are present in the modules folder,but not sure if these modules got corrupt, ticket for the same : https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TISTUD-6026. 1. Create an alloy/ classic app. 2. Enable <USER>services for the app. 2. Build for device/simulator. Actual Results: 1. We get the following erros logs: 2. I tried removing the modules from the tiapp.xml & re build the app & I get the error logs below: h5. Expected Results: 1. We should not see any errors & the app should launch successfully. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16189,12,"""Android: Package - Installing a packaged app fails with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES on a non-KitKat device ""","""""""*Details:* After packaging an app from Studio *or* CLI (see CLI command below) and installing to a non-KitKat Android device (4.4), install will fail with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES. However, installing a packaged app to a KitKat Android device (e.g. Nexus 5 (4.4)) works fine.    This seems to occur after a clean install of Windows (so far) i.e. no Java, no node.js.    Here is the CLI command used by Studio:      To work around this for a non-kitkat device, you will need to manually sign the packaged app ([source|http://developer.<USER>com/question/153717/installing-apk-file-on-device---installparsefailednocertificates]): jarsigner -verbose -sigalg SHA1withRSA -digestalg SHA1 -keystore KEYSTORE_FILE_LOCATION APK_FILE_LOCATION KEYSTORE_ALIAS    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a default Titanium Classic *or* Alloy app  2. Package the app to the Android App Store from Studio *or* using the above CLI command  3. After the app is packaged, go to the packaged app directory and install app to a non-KitKat device: adb install <APP>.apk    *Actual:* App will fail with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES in the cmd.    *Expected:* App should not fail with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES after packaging from Studio.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Package - Installing a packaged app fails with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES on a non-KitKat device
Description: """"*Details:* After packaging an app from Studio *or* CLI (see CLI command below) and installing to a non-KitKat Android device (4.4), install will fail with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES. However, installing a packaged app to a KitKat Android device (e.g. Nexus 5 (4.4)) works fine. This seems to occur after a clean install of Windows (so far) i.e. no Java, no node.js. Here is the CLI command used by Studio: To work around this for a non-kitkat device, you will need to manually sign the packaged app ([source|http://developer.<USER>com/question/153717/installing-apk-file-on-device---installparsefailednocertificates]): jarsigner -verbose -sigalg SHA1withRSA -digestalg SHA1 -keystore KEYSTORE_FILE_LOCATION APK_FILE_LOCATION KEYSTORE_ALIAS *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a default Titanium Classic *or* Alloy app 2. Package the app to the Android App Store from Studio *or* using the above CLI command 3. After the app is packaged, go to the packaged app directory and install app to a non-KitKat device: adb install <APP>.apk *Actual:* App will fail with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES in the cmd. *Expected:* App should not fail with INSTALL_PARSE_FAILED_NO_CERTIFICATES after packaging from Studio.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16188,12,"""Studio: Cannot locate Android SDK with 3.2.0 release even when it is configured properly""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce  Clean install on Windows 8.1 Single Language (Turkish)   Enter android sdk path to Window>Preferences>Platforms>Android    h3. Actual Result  No Android SDKs were found under the specified SDK location    h3. Expected Result  Locate SDKs successfully""""""",Bug,"Title: Studio: Cannot locate Android SDK with 3.2.0 release even when it is configured properly
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce Clean install on Windows 8.1 Single Language (Turkish) Enter android sdk path to Window>Preferences>Platforms>Android h3. Actual Result No Android SDKs were found under the specified SDK location h3. Expected Result Locate SDKs successfully""""",title+description
TIMOB-16187,12,"""Android: node attributes inside timodule.xml overwrite the attribute inside AndroidManifest.xml""","""""""Inside studio:    1. Create a mobile project  2. Add the module  3. Replace Resources/app.js with modules/android/com.testmodule/0.1/example/app.js  4. Build the app    Expected result:  The app should build fine    Actual result:  The build <USER>fails with the error: """"""""[ERROR] :  Unable to find generated R.java file""""""""  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: node attributes inside timodule.xml overwrite the attribute inside AndroidManifest.xml
Description: """"Inside studio: 1. Create a mobile project 2. Add the module 3. Replace Resources/app.js with modules/android/com.testmodule/0.1/example/app.js 4. Build the app Expected result: The app should build fine Actual result: The build <USER>fails with the error: """"""""[ERROR] :  Unable to find generated R.java file"""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-16186,12,"""CLI: ti install sdk fails if download response does not contain a content length""","""""""When downloading a Titanium SDK that does not have a content length returned from the server, the command crashes because it doesn't know the length needed for the progress bar.    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: ti install sdk fails if download response does not contain a content length
Description: """"When downloading a Titanium SDK that does not have a content length returned from the server, the command crashes because it doesn't know the length needed for the progress bar. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16184,12,"""Android: TabGroup setActiveTab not working if tabs are added with addTab method""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a tabgroup and add 2 or more tabs via tabGroup.addTab method.  2. set tab 1 as active tab via tabGroup.setActiveTab method  3. open tabgroup.    Expected result: tabgroup is open and active tab is #1.    Actual Result: tabgroup is open and active tab is #0.    Here is a code snippet:       When tabGroup is open you'll see the following log message:    [ERROR] :  TabGroupProxy: (KrollRuntimeThread) [353,353] Invalid tab index.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TabGroup setActiveTab not working if tabs are added with addTab method
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a tabgroup and add 2 or more tabs via tabGroup.addTab method. 2. set tab 1 as active tab via tabGroup.setActiveTab method 3. open tabgroup. Expected result: tabgroup is open and active tab is #1. Actual Result: tabgroup is open and active tab is #0. Here is a code snippet: When tabGroup is open you'll see the following log message: [ERROR] : TabGroupProxy: (KrollRuntimeThread) [353,353] Invalid tab index.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16182,12,"""Android: Camera """"cancel"""" function not called from Android """"back"""" button when camera has overlay""","""""""On Android using         Pressing the Android back button will not fire the """"""""cancel"""""""" callback;    However, when no overlay is specified, the cancel callback fires as expected.         """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Camera """"cancel"""" function not called from Android """"back"""" button when camera has overlay
Description: """"On Android using Pressing the Android back button will not fire the """"""""cancel"""""""" callback; However, when no overlay is specified, the cancel callback fires as expected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16181,12,"""Appcelerator Studio was not able to locate the correct Simulator Version""","""""""h3. Issue  When trying to build a project for iOS from within <USER>Studio, you consistently get an error stating that you require SDK 7.0.3 for iOS.    h3. Problem  Proper version of Xcode is not getting detected    h3. Validate  Make sure you have the latest version of Xcode (v 5.0.2)  - from the project root directory (E.G. ~/Users/yourusername/<USER>Studio_Workspace/HelloWorld) run the following command line:         titanium build --platform ios --ios-version 7.0.3       - you should see an error about locating a configuration file    h3. Fix  force a redirection of Xcode by Titanium using the following command from terminal         sudo xcode-select -s /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer""""""",Bug,"Title: Appcelerator Studio was not able to locate the correct Simulator Version
Description: """"h3. Issue When trying to build a project for iOS from within <USER>Studio, you consistently get an error stating that you require SDK 7.0.3 for iOS. h3. Problem Proper version of Xcode is not getting detected h3. Validate Make sure you have the latest version of Xcode (v 5.0.2) - from the project root directory (E.G. ~/Users/yourusername/<USER>Studio_Workspace/HelloWorld) run the following command line: titanium build --platform ios --ios-version 7.0.3 - you should see an error about locating a configuration file h3. Fix force a redirection of Xcode by Titanium using the following command from terminal sudo xcode-select -s /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer""""",title+description
TIMOB-16180,12,"""Android: Map v2 new features""","""""""Expose new functionalities to the existing map v2 module:  1. New properties:  -compassEnabled: Enable/disable the compass on the map  -zoom: allows zoom dynamically  -bearing: Direction that the camera is pointing in, in degrees clockwise from north.  -tilt: Angle of camera  -maxZoomLevel: returns max zoom level of the map  -minZoomLevel: returns min zoom level of the map  -onsnapshotready: Fired when the snapshot is ready.    2. New methods:  -snapshot: takes a snapshot of the map    3. Update google play services library""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Map v2 new features
Description: """"Expose new functionalities to the existing map v2 module: 1. New properties: -compassEnabled: Enable/disable the compass on the map -zoom: allows zoom dynamically -bearing: Direction that the camera is pointing in, in degrees clockwise from north. -tilt: Angle of camera -maxZoomLevel: returns max zoom level of the map -minZoomLevel: returns min zoom level of the map -onsnapshotready: Fired when the snapshot is ready. 2. New methods: -snapshot: takes a snapshot of the map 3. Update google play services library""""",title+description
TIMOB-16178,12,"""iOS: Push notification callback not fired if app is in background and resumed without clicking the notification""","""""""h2. Problem description  When receiving a push notification, if the app is in background and it is resumed without clicking the notification in the bar, the callback is not fired.    h2. Code  Tested with this sample code: https://gist.github.com/davidecassenti/3ca943961098c0534e97    h2. Steps  1. Run the app  2. Click subscribe  3. Put the app in background  4. Send a notification  5. Open the app using the icon, not the notification""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Push notification callback not fired if app is in background and resumed without clicking the notification
Description: """"h2. Problem description When receiving a push notification, if the app is in background and it is resumed without clicking the notification in the bar, the callback is not fired. h2. Code Tested with this sample code: https://gist.github.com/davidecassenti/3ca943961098c0534e97 h2. Steps 1. Run the app 2. Click subscribe 3. Put the app in background 4. Send a notification 5. Open the app using the icon, not the notification""""",title+description
TIMOB-16177,12,"""iOS LANDSCAPE Orientation Upside Down""","""""""*Problem Description*    Opening a modal window with a Scrollable view, with orientationModes set to LANDSCAPE_LEFT & LANDSCAPE_RIGHT display incorrectly.  Image displays upside down, however can be reset by turning the phone one way then back again.     *Reproduction Steps*  1.  Run the code below in a new Alloy Project.  2.  Tilt the device to the left and notice the image is upside down instead of showing in.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT.  3.  Press Close  4.  Tilt device to the right and notice the image is showing LANDSCAPE_LEFT which is correct    *index.js*    *index.tss*    *index.xml*        *LandscapePhotoViewer.js*    *LandscapePhotoViewer.tss*    *LandscapePhotoViewer.xml*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS LANDSCAPE Orientation Upside Down
Description: """"*Problem Description* Opening a modal window with a Scrollable view, with orientationModes set to LANDSCAPE_LEFT & LANDSCAPE_RIGHT display incorrectly. Image displays upside down, however can be reset by turning the phone one way then back again. *Reproduction Steps* 1. Run the code below in a new Alloy Project. 2. Tilt the device to the left and notice the image is upside down instead of showing in.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT. 3. Press Close 4. Tilt device to the right and notice the image is showing LANDSCAPE_LEFT which is correct *index.js* *index.tss* *index.xml* *LandscapePhotoViewer.js* *LandscapePhotoViewer.tss* *LandscapePhotoViewer.xml* """"",title+description
TIMOB-16176,12,"""Android: Cannot change TextField value in change event handler""","""""""changing the value of the text field in change handler is not possible.   textField.addEventListener(""""""""change"""""""", function(){   textField.value = textField.value.replace(/some regex/,"""""""""""""""");  }     this code is crushing whole device. I have to restart the device. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot change TextField value in change event handler
Description: """"changing the value of the text field in change handler is not possible. textField.addEventListener(""""""""change"""""""", function(){ textField.value = textField.value.replace(/some regex/,""""""""""""""""); } this code is crushing whole device. I have to restart the device. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16174,12,"""TiAPI: Add file information to returned Blob when camera is set to saveToPhotoGallery = true""","""""""It would great, if when setting saveToPhotoGallery = true for an image taken with the camera, that file information is returned to the Blob.     Currently, the file is saved, but we have no way of know the name or path of this file.    This would require a quick update to TiCameraActivity.java turning    private static void saveToPhotoGallery(byte[] data)    into    private static File saveToPhotoGallery(byte[] data)    And updating the Blob in     public void onPictureTaken(byte[] data, Camera camera)    With a TiFile reference.    I'm not sure if iOS has this same issue.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Add file information to returned Blob when camera is set to saveToPhotoGallery = true
Description: """"It would great, if when setting saveToPhotoGallery = true for an image taken with the camera, that file information is returned to the Blob. Currently, the file is saved, but we have no way of know the name or path of this file. This would require a quick update to TiCameraActivity.java turning private static void saveToPhotoGallery(byte[] data) into private static File saveToPhotoGallery(byte[] data) And updating the Blob in public void onPictureTaken(byte[] data, Camera camera) With a TiFile reference. I'm not sure if iOS has this same issue. """"",title+description
