Description: """"The picker completely ignores the minDate and maxDate when shown as dialog. Code to reproduce: """"",title+description
TIMOB-16171,12,"""Android: Build error for applications with a module if SDK is installed in non default location""","""""""Titanium SDK is installed not in default location, it is in D:\SDKs\Titanium  This path is set in Studio: Window -> Preferences -> Studio -> Platforms  Trying to build Kitchen Sink sample containing facebook module I get error in Studio:    [ERROR] Application Installer abnormal <USER>termination. Process exit value was 1    It says nothing, but building app in command line I get error:    [ERROR] Could not find all required Titanium Modules:  [ERROR]  id: facebook  version: latest platform: android  deploy-type: development    When I copied Titanium SDK to (default) path:      C:\Users\Janusz\AppData\Roaming\Titanium  build was successful. I doesn't change the path in Studio, I leave it      D:\SDKs\Titanium    During building app Titanium uses module and other things from D:\SDKs\Titanium, but in default location SDK must exist to start building - I thing during checking if Titanium has all needed components to build.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Build error for applications with a module if SDK is installed in non default location
Description: """"Titanium SDK is installed not in default location, it is in D:\SDKs\Titanium This path is set in Studio: Window -> Preferences -> Studio -> Platforms Trying to build Kitchen Sink sample containing facebook module I get error in Studio: [ERROR] Application Installer abnormal <USER>termination. Process exit value was 1 It says nothing, but building app in command line I get error: [ERROR] Could not find all required Titanium Modules: [ERROR] id: facebook version: latest platform: android deploy-type: development When I copied Titanium SDK to (default) path: C:\Users\Janusz\AppData\Roaming\Titanium build was successful. I doesn't change the path in Studio, I leave it D:\SDKs\Titanium During building app Titanium uses module and other things from D:\SDKs\Titanium, but in default location SDK must exist to start building - I thing during checking if Titanium has all needed components to build. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16170,12,"""iOS: Titanium.Calendar.Alert.setRelativeOffset method does not work because of misspelling""","""""""The setter method for the relativeOffset property in Ti.Calendar.Alert is misspelled:    {code:obj-c}  -(void)setRelavtiveOffset:(id)arg  {      alert.relativeOffset = [TiUtils doubleValue:arg] / 1000;  }  {code}    This causes the following code to not set an alert properly:    {code:javascript}  // get or create an Event object named """"""""event""""""""  var a = event.createAlert({ relativeOffset: 0 });  a.setRelativeOffset(-60 * 60 * 1000);  event.setAlerts([a]);  event.save();  {code}    The resulting event will have an alert at the time of the event, not one hour before.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.Calendar.Alert.setRelativeOffset method does not work because of misspelling
Description: """"The setter method for the relativeOffset property in Ti.Calendar.Alert is misspelled: {code:obj-c} -(void)setRelavtiveOffset:(id)arg { alert.relativeOffset = [TiUtils doubleValue:arg] / 1000; } {code} This causes the following code to not set an alert properly: {code:javascript} // get or create an Event object named """"""""event"""""""" var a = event.createAlert({ relativeOffset: 0 }); a.setRelativeOffset(-60 * 60 * 1000); event.setAlerts([a]); event.save(); {code} The resulting event will have an alert at the time of the event, not one hour before.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16169,12,"""Android: Build error with _build.js file with 3.2.0 release""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce I tried to compile an existing project with new SDK 3.2.0 in Android and got a critical error  [ERROR] Application Installer abnormal <USER>termination. Process exit value was 8 (see log attachment for more details)  h3. Actual Result error  h3. Expected Result I solved changhing in the file /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/3.2.0.GA/android/cli/commands/_build.js:2195 m[3].toLowerCase() in m[1].toLowerCase().  please, fix it with the next release! :) """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Build error with _build.js file with 3.2.0 release
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce I tried to compile an existing project with new SDK 3.2.0 in Android and got a critical error [ERROR] Application Installer abnormal <USER>termination. Process exit value was 8 (see log attachment for more details) h3. Actual Result error h3. Expected Result I solved changhing in the file /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/3.2.0.GA/android/cli/commands/_build.js:2195 m[3].toLowerCase() in m[1].toLowerCase(). please, fix it with the next release! :) """"",title+description
TIMOB-16168,12,"""Android: CLI does not detect Android device after upgrading to 3.2.0 release""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce fresh installation of titanium 3.2, beta or even nightly,  plugin android phone, click refresh device list, go to run configuration, the device is not shown up, I can't develop android app with it at all. however, it works fine with old titanium 2.0  h3. Actual Result android device not show up  h3. Expected Result android device shows up in the list""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: CLI does not detect Android device after upgrading to 3.2.0 release
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce fresh installation of titanium 3.2, beta or even nightly, plugin android phone, click refresh device list, go to run configuration, the device is not shown up, I can't develop android app with it at all. however, it works fine with old titanium 2.0 h3. Actual Result android device not show up h3. Expected Result android device shows up in the list""""",title+description
TIMOB-16167,12,"""Android: Escape character '\n' does not work for textArea if 'editable' property is set""","""""""h5. Problem description    Escape character '\n' does not work for textArea on Android if also the 'editable' property is set    h5. Steps to reproduce      '\n' characters are ignored and FOO BAR is displayed in the same line    Commenting the 'editable:false' line works and FOO BAR is displayed as expected.    Not reproducible with 3.1.3.GA""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Escape character '\n' does not work for textArea if 'editable' property is set
Description: """"h5. Problem description Escape character '\n' does not work for textArea on Android if also the 'editable' property is set h5. Steps to reproduce '\n' characters are ignored and FOO BAR is displayed in the same line Commenting the 'editable:false' line works and FOO BAR is displayed as expected. Not reproducible with 3.1.3.GA""""",title+description
