TIMOB-16147,12,"""Android: Support immediate transition for Ti.UI.ScrollableView.setCurrentPage""","""""""It would be nice if you could add an option to have immediate transition when invoking 'setCurrentPage' on Ti.UI.ScrollableView. It is useful if the views are dynamically preloaded, and helps to allow rotating the views w/o the user noticing it. e.g. scroll a large amount of data, and have only a couple of views initialized  On IOS it already works this way.  For Android, i tried to hardcode it in TiUIScrollableView.java, method move(int), line 383, to  mPager.setCurrentItem(index, false);  //false = immediate transition  and it works as expected (but is not configurable)""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support immediate transition for Ti.UI.ScrollableView.setCurrentPage
Description: """"It would be nice if you could add an option to have immediate transition when invoking 'setCurrentPage' on Ti.UI.ScrollableView. It is useful if the views are dynamically preloaded, and helps to allow rotating the views w/o the user noticing it. e.g. scroll a large amount of data, and have only a couple of views initialized On IOS it already works this way. For Android, i tried to hardcode it in TiUIScrollableView.java, method move(int), line 383, to mPager.setCurrentItem(index, false); //false = immediate transition and it works as expected (but is not configurable)""""",title+description
TIMOB-16146,12,"""Android: orientation lock in Android manifest buggy when screen locked""","""""""I am using the android:screenOrientation=""""""""portrait"""""""" property to lock app activities into portrait mode. However, I noticed that the app was behaving very strangely  when coming out of screen lock in landscape mode. Upon investigating, I realized that the window was being closed and re-opened when the screen lock went into landscape mode. Run the app below, and here is how to reproduce.  1. Open the app - it will run in portrait mode as expected. Rotating the tablet has no effect - good.  2. With the app active, lock the screen.  3. Rotate the tablet to landscape mode, and wait for the screen lock to adjust accordingly.  4. Unlock the screen in landscape mode: you will see that the window was opened multiple times, which will totally screw up application logic in most cases. Note that the window is instantiated only once, but the close and open events fire multiple times.     app.js:      Android section in tiapp.xml:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: orientation lock in Android manifest buggy when screen locked
Description: """"I am using the android:screenOrientation=""""""""portrait"""""""" property to lock app activities into portrait mode. However, I noticed that the app was behaving very strangely when coming out of screen lock in landscape mode. Upon investigating, I realized that the window was being closed and re-opened when the screen lock went into landscape mode. Run the app below, and here is how to reproduce. 1. Open the app - it will run in portrait mode as expected. Rotating the tablet has no effect - good. 2. With the app active, lock the screen. 3. Rotate the tablet to landscape mode, and wait for the screen lock to adjust accordingly. 4. Unlock the screen in landscape mode: you will see that the window was opened multiple times, which will totally screw up application logic in most cases. Note that the window is instantiated only once, but the close and open events fire multiple times. app.js: Android section in tiapp.xml: """"",title+description
TIMOB-16145,12,"""Android: Animation issue when setting borderColor & borderWidth on a Ti.UI.View""","""""""h6.Issue description  When animating a view with a border on android, the animations are clipped to the bounds of the border. It appears that the border becomes the new 'parent' of the view, rather than the window that owns it.    h6.Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch application using Titanium SDK 3.2 on an Android device  2. Swipe down on each of the rectangles and observe behaviour.  3. Run once again on iOS simulator to notice parity    h6.Sample code  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Animation issue when setting borderColor & borderWidth on a Ti.UI.View
Description: """"h6.Issue description When animating a view with a border on android, the animations are clipped to the bounds of the border. It appears that the border becomes the new 'parent' of the view, rather than the window that owns it. h6.Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch application using Titanium SDK 3.2 on an Android device 2. Swipe down on each of the rectangles and observe behaviour. 3. Run once again on iOS simulator to notice parity h6.Sample code """"",title+description
TIMOB-16144,12,"""iOS: SQLite doesn't support LIKE for non ASCII chars""","""""""h4. Problem Description  The user needs to search in SQLite for a string like ängs, his SQLite contains the word Ängs, which should be a match, since he used LIKE. In the iOS simulator, he gets 0 rows as result.       h4. Workaround   Right now we requested him to search for ängs and Ängs in order to find the matches.     h4. Extra info  From this item:    http://stackoverflow.com/questions/10356062/how-to-deal-with-accented-characters-in-ios-sqlite    appears that the LIKE function can be overwritten in order to support upper/lower case queries in non ASCII chars.     h4. Community issue  http://developer.<USER>com/question/161275/sqlite-query-with-    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: SQLite doesn't support LIKE for non ASCII chars
Description: """"h4. Problem Description The user needs to search in SQLite for a string like ängs, his SQLite contains the word Ängs, which should be a match, since he used LIKE. In the iOS simulator, he gets 0 rows as result. h4. Workaround Right now we requested him to search for ängs and Ängs in order to find the matches. h4. Extra info From this item: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/10356062/how-to-deal-with-accented-characters-in-ios-sqlite appears that the LIKE function can be overwritten in order to support upper/lower case queries in non ASCII chars. h4. Community issue http://developer.<USER>com/question/161275/sqlite-query-with- """"",title+description
TIMOB-16143,12,"""iOS 7: Items liked with Ti.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL do not open when clicked upon""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When the user uses Ti.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL in the TextArea in iOS, the automated autolink will show the url and the phone in an URL fashion, and it's clickeable, but never will happen when you click on it.     h4. Test Case      h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project (Classic Titanium) with Mobile SDK 3.2.0  2. Paste the test case into app.js  3. Compile into the simulator.  4. Click on the url, won't open Safari.     h4. Extra info  If you test this with 3.1.3.GA, it will work as expected. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS 7: Items liked with Ti.UI.AUTOLINK_ALL do not open when clicked upon
