TIMOB-16053,12,"""Windows Hybrid: Cannot publish to Windows appstore using VS2013""","""""""h5.Description  Packaging the application works fine. I can run the application on devices and simulators without any errors.    However when I try to upload the packaged application to the windows store I get errors shown in the attached picture.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Create a hybrid application  2. Package the application for Windows Store  3. Sign into a Windows Developer account  4. Submit the application to be published    h5.Expected Result  Packaged application should be okay to publish to the Windows store.    h5.Actual Result  I get errors about the apps packages being incorrect.""""""",Bug,"Title: Windows Hybrid: Cannot publish to Windows appstore using VS2013
Description: """"h5.Description Packaging the application works fine. I can run the application on devices and simulators without any errors. However when I try to upload the packaged application to the windows store I get errors shown in the attached picture. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Create a hybrid application 2. Package the application for Windows Store 3. Sign into a Windows Developer account 4. Submit the application to be published h5.Expected Result Packaged application should be okay to publish to the Windows store. h5.Actual Result I get errors about the apps packages being incorrect.""""",title+description
TIMOB-16052,12,"""CLI: """"Invalid Version: 3.2.0 copy""""""","""""""h2. problem    If I attempt to run a {{ti sdk}} command that requires iterating through the list of installed Titanium SDKs, I get the following error and crash if I have a TiSDK folder with a space in the name (in this case """"""""3.2.0 copy""""""""):        h2. expected    I think that instead of causing the command to crash, it should instead print a warning to the screen that says it is an invalid version and that it will be skipping it         then continue on with the {{ti sdk}} command as expected""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"Invalid Version: 3.2.0 copy""""
Description: """"h2. problem If I attempt to run a {{ti sdk}} command that requires iterating through the list of installed Titanium SDKs, I get the following error and crash if I have a TiSDK folder with a space in the name (in this case """"""""3.2.0 copy""""""""): h2. expected I think that instead of causing the command to crash, it should instead print a warning to the screen that says it is an invalid version and that it will be skipping it then continue on with the {{ti sdk}} command as expected""""",title+description
TIMOB-16051,12,"""Titanium.UI.ListItem.accessoryView""","""""""Potential use case    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: 'white'});  var basicSwitch = Ti.UI.createSwitch({    value:true  });  basicSwitch.addEventListener('change',function(e){    Ti.API.info('Switch value: ' + basicSwitch.value);  });  var data = [      {          properties: {              title: 'Title',              image: 'KS_nav_views.png', // not used by this template              accessoryView: basicSwitch          },          template: Ti.UI.LIST_ITEM_TEMPLATE_DEFAULT      }  ];    var listSection = Ti.UI.createListSection({items: data});  var listView = Ti.UI.createListView({sections: [listSection]});  win.add(listView);  win.open();    <Alloy>      <Window backgroundColor=""""""""white"""""""">          <ListView id=""""""""listView"""""""">              <ListSection>                  <ListItem title=""""""""Airplane Mode"""""""">                      <AccessoryView>                          <Switch id=""""""""basicSwitch"""""""" value=""""""""true"""""""" onChange=""""""""outputState""""""""/>                      </AccessoryView>                  </ListItem>                  <ListItem title=""""""""Wi-Fi""""""""/>                  <ListItem title=""""""""Bluetooth""""""""/>              </ListSection>          </ListView>      </Window>  </Alloy>  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Titanium.UI.ListItem.accessoryView
Description: """"Potential use case {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: 'white'}); var basicSwitch = Ti.UI.createSwitch({ value:true }); basicSwitch.addEventListener('change',function(e){ Ti.API.info('Switch value: ' + basicSwitch.value); }); var data = [ { properties: { title: 'Title', image: 'KS_nav_views.png', // not used by this template accessoryView: basicSwitch }, template: Ti.UI.LIST_ITEM_TEMPLATE_DEFAULT } ]; var listSection = Ti.UI.createListSection({items: data}); var listView = Ti.UI.createListView({sections: [listSection]}); win.add(listView); win.open(); <Alloy> <Window backgroundColor=""""""""white""""""""> <ListView id=""""""""listView""""""""> <ListSection> <ListItem title=""""""""Airplane Mode""""""""> <AccessoryView> <Switch id=""""""""basicSwitch"""""""" value=""""""""true"""""""" onChange=""""""""outputState""""""""/> </AccessoryView> </ListItem> <ListItem title=""""""""Wi-Fi""""""""/> <ListItem title=""""""""Bluetooth""""""""/> </ListSection> </ListView> </Window> </Alloy> {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-16048,12,"""Only first Image is showing on a tableview when taking a picture from camera""","""""""Taking picture from the camera and adding new row with the picture to a tableview shows only the first one.     h2.Steps to reproduce:     h4.Expected result:     once a picture is taken, a new row should be added with that image.    h4.Actual result:     A row is added but only the first row shows an image.    h3.Important:   I tried this also on a listview and a scrollview also I changed from o.media to o.media.nativePath but nevermind the combination all had the same unfortunate result of showing only the first image.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Only first Image is showing on a tableview when taking a picture from camera
Description: """"Taking picture from the camera and adding new row with the picture to a tableview shows only the first one. h2.Steps to reproduce: h4.Expected result: once a picture is taken, a new row should be added with that image. h4.Actual result: A row is added but only the first row shows an image. h3.Important: I tried this also on a listview and a scrollview also I changed from o.media to o.media.nativePath but nevermind the combination all had the same unfortunate result of showing only the first image. """"",title+description
TIMOB-16047,12,"""iOS: Textfield adding a leading white space when text is autocorrected ""","""""""  1. Create app with the above code.  2. Enter a word and allow the phone to auto-complete for you  3. Press space and enter another word  NOTE: (Good idea to keep on going til the you have scrolled off screen)    h3.Actual:   A whitespace will be appended to the beginning of the text field.    h4.Expected:  No leading whitespace""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Textfield adding a leading white space when text is autocorrected
Description: """" 1. Create app with the above code. 2. Enter a word and allow the phone to auto-complete for you 3. Press space and enter another word NOTE: (Good idea to keep on going til the you have scrolled off screen) h3.Actual: A whitespace will be appended to the beginning of the text field. h4.Expected: No leading whitespace""""",title+description
TIMOB-16046,12,"""iOS7: keyboardToolbar disappears after focussing textField 2-3 times""","""""""h6.Issue description   This happens in both iOS 6 and 7 devices with Ti SDK 3.1.3.GA    h6.Steps to replicate  To replicate focus the text field and then dispose the keyboard clicking the done button multiple times (it may require 2-3 times).    Important: Reproducible only at device (iPhone 4 with iOS 7.0.3)    h6.Runnable sample  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: keyboardToolbar disappears after focussing textField 2-3 times
