TIMOB-15893,12,"""CLI: Unable to specify a alternate sdks directory using ti config paths.sdks""","""""""I am trying to add a alternate SDK's folder.   Tried adding the paths to the config using    ti config paths.sdks path/to/sdk    verified that the paths is added properly.    But if i try running ti sdk, the SDK's in the new path do not show up and if i try building a app with the sdk from the alternate location, the build fails showing the selected sdk does not exist.    h3.Steps to Reproduce.    1. Create a folder with some SDK's say : /Users/sabilrahim/SDK/  2. Include the path in ti config : `ti config paths.sdks /Users/sabilrahim/SDK/`  3. Confirm the path has been added properly. Run ` ti config` and check the paths.sdks  4. Run `ti sdk`    h3.Actual Result  SDK's from the new folder are not listed    h3.Expected Result  SDK's from the new folder are listed and can build apps using SDK's placed in directories other than the default one.     """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Unable to specify a alternate sdks directory using ti config paths.sdks
Description: """"I am trying to add a alternate SDK's folder. Tried adding the paths to the config using ti config paths.sdks path/to/sdk verified that the paths is added properly. But if i try running ti sdk, the SDK's in the new path do not show up and if i try building a app with the sdk from the alternate location, the build fails showing the selected sdk does not exist. h3.Steps to Reproduce. 1. Create a folder with some SDK's say : /Users/sabilrahim/SDK/ 2. Include the path in ti config : `ti config paths.sdks /Users/sabilrahim/SDK/` 3. Confirm the path has been added properly. Run ` ti config` and check the paths.sdks 4. Run `ti sdk` h3.Actual Result SDK's from the new folder are not listed h3.Expected Result SDK's from the new folder are listed and can build apps using SDK's placed in directories other than the default one. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15892,12,"""CLI: BlackBerry - add prompt to build command""","""""""When running command    and choose BlackBerry platform, CLI does not prompt necessary build options.    The command can be executed only passing all  Build blackberry Usage: titanium build --platform blackberry [--debug-token <path>] [--ip-address                          <address>] [--keystore-password <value>] [--ndk <path>] [--output-dir                          <path>] [--password <value>] [--target <value>]    """"""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: BlackBerry - add prompt to build command
