Description: """"*Details:* Double platform options appear when creating an app from the CLI. *This is a regression as this does not occur with CLI 3.1.2 GA.* *Steps to reproduce:* 1. In terminal, type: ti create *Actual:* Double platform options appear: *Expected:* Only a single row of platform options should appear: """"",title+description
TIMOB-15868,12,"""Android: Few analytics events are not seen till a ti.end or ti.start event is fired""","""""""h5.Description:  1. Build the attached analytics app on an android device.  2. After install launch the app & you should get a ti.enroll & ti.start event at 30 seconds after the app is launched.  3. Now tap on any of the event buttons on the app like 'feature','nav','settings','timed','user' etc.    h5.Actual Results:  1. We do not see any of the tapped events.  2. Close the app.  3. After 30 seconds you will see an ti.end event along with the previous events which did not show up.    h5.Expected Results:  1. We should see all types of events at 30 seconds after they have been sent from the device.    So,ti summarize we see the ti.end & ti.start events exactly at 30 seconds after sending the events from the device, but we do not see any events mentioned above till a ti.end or ti.start is fired.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Few analytics events are not seen till a ti.end or ti.start event is fired
Description: """"h5.Description: 1. Build the attached analytics app on an android device. 2. After install launch the app & you should get a ti.enroll & ti.start event at 30 seconds after the app is launched. 3. Now tap on any of the event buttons on the app like 'feature','nav','settings','timed','user' etc. h5.Actual Results: 1. We do not see any of the tapped events. 2. Close the app. 3. After 30 seconds you will see an ti.end event along with the previous events which did not show up. h5.Expected Results: 1. We should see all types of events at 30 seconds after they have been sent from the device. So,ti summarize we see the ti.end & ti.start events exactly at 30 seconds after sending the events from the device, but we do not see any events mentioned above till a ti.end or ti.start is fired. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15867,12,"""CLI: """"ti login"""" - ignoring an invalid authentication""","""""""*regression* against 3.1.3.GA    h5. To reproduce  run command """"""""ti logout""""""""  run command """"""""ti status""""""""  run command """"""""ti login""""""""  run command """"""""ti status""""""""    h5.actual result      h5. Expected result    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"ti login"""" - ignoring an invalid authentication
Description: """"*regression* against 3.1.3.GA h5. To reproduce run command """"""""ti logout"""""""" run command """"""""ti status"""""""" run command """"""""ti login"""""""" run command """"""""ti status"""""""" h5.actual result h5. Expected result """"",title+description
TIMOB-15866,12,"""MobileWeb: Analytics Events are not generated""","""""""*Regression*, does not occur in 3.1.3.GA    Analytics Events are not generated with the above environment.  h5. To reproduce  1. Download the test application from <GitHub>/titanium_mobile_tests_internal/FeatureTest/Analytics   2. Create your own Studio project (to get a new GUID) and then move the app.js from the downloaded project into your new project   3. Make sure your device and desktop are on staging server.  4. Package App for Mobile Web  5. Start Apache server and copy content of packaged app  6. Try to generate analytics events    h5.Actual result  No Analytics events, no console output    h5. Expected result  Should see logged analytics events   """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Analytics Events are not generated
Description: """"*Regression*, does not occur in 3.1.3.GA Analytics Events are not generated with the above environment. h5. To reproduce 1. Download the test application from <GitHub>/titanium_mobile_tests_internal/FeatureTest/Analytics 2. Create your own Studio project (to get a new GUID) and then move the app.js from the downloaded project into your new project 3. Make sure your device and desktop are on staging server. 4. Package App for Mobile Web 5. Start Apache server and copy content of packaged app 6. Try to generate analytics events h5.Actual result No Analytics events, no console output h5. Expected result Should see logged analytics events """"",title+description
TIMOB-15865,12,"""TiAPI: Ability to turn off Geolocation analytics while gathering the rest of analytics""","""""""mFoundry wants the ability to turn off the ability of gathering Geolocation analytics while still gathering the other analytics data that we gather.  Today it is an all or nothing.  An app can either have analytics turned on or turned off.  They cannot configure which parts of analytics to collect or not.    The application that mFoundry is talking about using mapping to find ATMs and bank locations.  So the app itself is already using geo events.  That means that if they turn on analytics, we will receive the geo analytic events.      They want the ability, based on the project to have all analytics on/off or all analytics turned on except for geo events.""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Ability to turn off Geolocation analytics while gathering the rest of analytics
Description: """"mFoundry wants the ability to turn off the ability of gathering Geolocation analytics while still gathering the other analytics data that we gather. Today it is an all or nothing. An app can either have analytics turned on or turned off. They cannot configure which parts of analytics to collect or not. The application that mFoundry is talking about using mapping to find ATMs and bank locations. So the app itself is already using geo events. That means that if they turn on analytics, we will receive the geo analytic events. They want the ability, based on the project to have all analytics on/off or all analytics turned on except for geo events.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15864,12,"""Check for spaces for Android NDK paths in CLI setup""","""""""When trying to build a module with 'ant', it fails when the Android NDK path contains spaces.    The module build scripts aren't directly related to the CLI, but the CLI should validate the NDK path during the setup command to help avoid this scenario.    This should be fixed in both """"""""ti setup"""""""" and the Android detection code in the SDK.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Check for spaces for Android NDK paths in CLI setup
Description: """"When trying to build a module with 'ant', it fails when the Android NDK path contains spaces. The module build scripts aren't directly related to the CLI, but the CLI should validate the NDK path during the setup command to help avoid this scenario. This should be fixed in both """"""""ti setup"""""""" and the Android detection code in the SDK.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15863,12,"""Android: ScrollableView scroll indicators blurry/distorted on device""","""""""On an Android device, ScrollableView arrows/indicators are blurry/distorted compared to the same app running in an emulator. See images below. Test project also attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ScrollableView scroll indicators blurry/distorted on device
