TIMOB-15839,12,"""CLI: Android - On Windows, cannot install an app to an Android device""","""""""*Details*: On Windows 7 and 8, you cannot install an app to an Android device.    *Note:*  *1. This does not occur on Mavericks 10.9*  *2. This is a regression as this issue does not occur on Windows 7 with Titanium GA stack*  3. This issue still occurs with SDK  FRI NOV 15, 2013 1:16:45 PM (3.2.0.v20131115115645); the oldest SDK I could get for Windows 7    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. On Windows 7, create a new Classic or Alloy project  2. Install to an Android device; here is the cli command:        *Actual:* A """"""""Failed to compile Java source files"""""""" (see attachment)  *Expected:* Should be able to install an app to an Android device regardless of Java 1.6 or Java 1.7""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android - On Windows, cannot install an app to an Android device
Description: """"*Details*: On Windows 7 and 8, you cannot install an app to an Android device. *Note:* *1. This does not occur on Mavericks 10.9* *2. This is a regression as this issue does not occur on Windows 7 with Titanium GA stack* 3. This issue still occurs with SDK FRI NOV 15, 2013 1:16:45 PM (3.2.0.v20131115115645); the oldest SDK I could get for Windows 7 *Steps to reproduce:* 1. On Windows 7, create a new Classic or Alloy project 2. Install to an Android device; here is the cli command: *Actual:* A """"""""Failed to compile Java source files"""""""" (see attachment) *Expected:* Should be able to install an app to an Android device regardless of Java 1.6 or Java 1.7""""",title+description
TIMOB-15838,12,"""node-appc: version - node-appc version in CLI and SDK do not match""","""""""*Details:* node-appc modules in SDK and CLI do not match.     Specifically, <SDK>/node_modules/node-appc is not a beta version where as /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc is a beta version    *Step to reproduce:*  1. Get the beta CLI: sudo npm install -g titanium@3.2.0-beta  2. Get the latest 3_2_X SDK: ti sdk install -b 3_2_X -d  3. Go to <SDK>/node_modules/node-appc/package.json and /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/package.json    *Actual:* Both versions do not match (see attachments)  *Expected:* The SDK node-appc should be beta version and from the same source.""""""",Bug,"Title: node-appc: version - node-appc version in CLI and SDK do not match
Description: """"*Details:* node-appc modules in SDK and CLI do not match. Specifically, <SDK>/node_modules/node-appc is not a beta version where as /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc is a beta version *Step to reproduce:* 1. Get the beta CLI: sudo npm install -g titanium@3.2.0-beta 2. Get the latest 3_2_X SDK: ti sdk install -b 3_2_X -d 3. Go to <SDK>/node_modules/node-appc/package.json and /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/package.json *Actual:* Both versions do not match (see attachments) *Expected:* The SDK node-appc should be beta version and from the same source.""""",title+description
