TIMOB-15835,12,"""AndroidModule:onResult is not called back for launchActivityForResult when heavyweight window is used""","""""""h2. Description  I developed a custom Android module. In this module I am opening gallery window using launchActivityForResult, it works fine only in light weight windows. But in heavy weight windows(fullscreen:true, navBarHidden:true,.. ) launchActivityForResult not working. There is no result back in heavy weight windows. onResult method is not called in case of heavyweight window is used.    h2. Test Case  Please find the attached sample project that reproduces the issue.  """"""",Bug,"Title: AndroidModule:onResult is not called back for launchActivityForResult when heavyweight window is used
Description: """"h2. Description I developed a custom Android module. In this module I am opening gallery window using launchActivityForResult, it works fine only in light weight windows. But in heavy weight windows(fullscreen:true, navBarHidden:true,.. ) launchActivityForResult not working. There is no result back in heavy weight windows. onResult method is not called in case of heavyweight window is used. h2. Test Case Please find the attached sample project that reproduces the issue. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15834,12,"""MobileWeb: Android - reloading browser with the new packaged app, displays previously previewed app""","""""""When packaging a new app for mobile web and previewing it in browsers on a different Android version devices, I noticed, that most of the time it will load a previously packaged app. I used Kitchen Sink and a default projects.    h5.To reproduce  1. Package KS for MobileWeb and place in usr/Library/WebServer/Documents  2. Devices and your machine have to be on the same network  3. On the device open the browser and type IP address  4. Package any other app and try to preview in browser on your device    h5. Actual result  3. The app is loading  4. The first app is displayed    h5.Expected result  The new app should load    h5.Work around  Clear cache depends on device:    Settings>Privacy and security>Clear cache  Settings>Privacy>Clear browsing data  Settings>Privacy>Delete personal data>Browsing history""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Android - reloading browser with the new packaged app, displays previously previewed app
Description: """"When packaging a new app for mobile web and previewing it in browsers on a different Android version devices, I noticed, that most of the time it will load a previously packaged app. I used Kitchen Sink and a default projects. h5.To reproduce 1. Package KS for MobileWeb and place in usr/Library/WebServer/Documents 2. Devices and your machine have to be on the same network 3. On the device open the browser and type IP address 4. Package any other app and try to preview in browser on your device h5. Actual result 3. The app is loading 4. The first app is displayed h5.Expected result The new app should load h5.Work around Clear cache depends on device: Settings>Privacy and security>Clear cache Settings>Privacy>Clear browsing data Settings>Privacy>Delete personal data>Browsing history""""",title+description
TIMOB-15833,12,"""iOS: Weak link MapKit""","""""""When the Map module was removed from the SDK, the linking to the Map framework was also removed MOD-1514. This has caused issues with other modules that are using the MapKit, but are assuming that it will already be linked because it was in the SDK.    To resolve this issue we need to weak link to MapKit in the SDK.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Weak link MapKit
Description: """"When the Map module was removed from the SDK, the linking to the Map framework was also removed MOD-1514. This has caused issues with other modules that are using the MapKit, but are assuming that it will already be linked because it was in the SDK. To resolve this issue we need to weak link to MapKit in the SDK.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15832,12,"""iOS: View centered in window quickly shifts about 10dp down""","""""""If you have a view centered in a window about 1 out of 2 or 3 times the window is opened, you notice the view quickly shifting down about 10dp.    h1. Steps to reproduce    # Create a new app: {{titanium create -p ios -n testShift --id test.shift -d .}}  # As {{app.js}} use:        # Run the app on a device: {{titanium build -p ios -T device}}  # Repeatedly click the blue view to keep opening the same window again  # Pay close attention to the blue view and notice it quickly shifting about {{10dp}} down every now and then after opening a new window.     h1. Notes    * Explicitly center {{v}} using {{center:\{x:'50%',y:'50%'\}}} won't help.  * Setting an absolute {{top}} on {{v}} fixes it, but that's not what we want.  * This **only** happens in device testing""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: View centered in window quickly shifts about 10dp down
Description: """"If you have a view centered in a window about 1 out of 2 or 3 times the window is opened, you notice the view quickly shifting down about 10dp. h1. Steps to reproduce # Create a new app: {{titanium create -p ios -n testShift --id test.shift -d .}} # As {{app.js}} use: # Run the app on a device: {{titanium build -p ios -T device}} # Repeatedly click the blue view to keep opening the same window again # Pay close attention to the blue view and notice it quickly shifting about {{10dp}} down every now and then after opening a new window. h1. Notes * Explicitly center {{v}} using {{center:\{x:'50%',y:'50%'\}}} won't help. * Setting an absolute {{top}} on {{v}} fixes it, but that's not what we want. * This **only** happens in device testing""""",title+description
TIMOB-15831,12,"""Android: Ti.Media.createSound """"looping"""" set on creation fails ""","""""""On iOS this works fine:        On Android you need to set {{looping}} after creation and in the tests I ran even right before calling `play()`, or the music will stop after one or some loops.        h1. Logs  When the playback on Android stops, the logs show:        h1. Steps to reproduce    # Create a new app: {{titanium create -p ios,android -n testLoop -d . --id test.loop}}  # As {{app.js}} use:        # Drop the attached {{music.acc}} (CCL) in the {{Resources}} folder.  # Run the app on both iOS and Android and see the music stop on Android after one or some loops.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.Media.createSound """"looping"""" set on creation fails
Description: """"On iOS this works fine: On Android you need to set {{looping}} after creation and in the tests I ran even right before calling `play()`, or the music will stop after one or some loops. h1. Logs When the playback on Android stops, the logs show: h1. Steps to reproduce # Create a new app: {{titanium create -p ios,android -n testLoop -d . --id test.loop}} # As {{app.js}} use: # Drop the attached {{music.acc}} (CCL) in the {{Resources}} folder. # Run the app on both iOS and Android and see the music stop on Android after one or some loops.""""",title+description
