TIMOB-15789,12,"""Android: ListView UI changed in respect to width of row and border line missing in 3.2 SDK""","""""""In SDK: 3.2.0.v20131121163252 the height of a row in listView has increased to a large extent as compared to SDK:3.1.3.GA    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the code using SDK:3.1.3.GA and SDK: 3.2.0.v20131121163252    Actual: UI has changed in respect to width of row  Expected : UI must remain same and width must be as expected    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ListView UI changed in respect to width of row and border line missing in 3.2 SDK
Description: """"In SDK: 3.2.0.v20131121163252 the height of a row in listView has increased to a large extent as compared to SDK:3.1.3.GA Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the code using SDK:3.1.3.GA and SDK: 3.2.0.v20131121163252 Actual: UI has changed in respect to width of row Expected : UI must remain same and width must be as expected """"",title+description
TIMOB-15787,12,"""Android: Provide access to Async Task API""","""""""h3. Issue  Simple async tasks currently must be done the UI thread when there is AsyncTasks available specifically for background async tasks on Android.    h3. Solution  Provide access to the AsyncTask API via the Titanium SDK or a module.    h3. Reference  http://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/AsyncTask.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Provide access to Async Task API
Description: """"h3. Issue Simple async tasks currently must be done the UI thread when there is AsyncTasks available specifically for background async tasks on Android. h3. Solution Provide access to the AsyncTask API via the Titanium SDK or a module. h3. Reference http://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/AsyncTask.html""""",title+description
TIMOB-15786,12,""" iOS: Provide access to Grand Central Dispatch API""","""""""h3. Issue  It is not currently possible to access a separate thread for data processing as a async task that will not affect the UI thread.    h3. Solution  Provide access to the Grand Central Dispatch API via the Titanium SDK or a module.    h3. Reference  https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/Performance/Reference/GCD_libdispatch_Ref/Reference/reference.html """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Provide access to Grand Central Dispatch API
Description: """"h3. Issue It is not currently possible to access a separate thread for data processing as a async task that will not affect the UI thread. h3. Solution Provide access to the Grand Central Dispatch API via the Titanium SDK or a module. h3. Reference https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/Performance/Reference/GCD_libdispatch_Ref/Reference/reference.html """"",title+description
TIMOB-15785,12,"""iOS: Push Notifications callback not being fired""","""""""Apps using Ti SDK 3.2.0 master are not receiving the callback event in registerForPushNotifications  when the app is open.      This means the app cannot present any information from a push notification while the app is open.     note: I do NOT use ti.cloud - I have my own APN server which works fine.     I am not using Alloy.     Notifications are correctly received when the app is closed/paused.     Should be easy enough to confirm without a specific test case.    #urgent    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Push Notifications callback not being fired
Description: """"Apps using Ti SDK 3.2.0 master are not receiving the callback event in registerForPushNotifications when the app is open. This means the app cannot present any information from a push notification while the app is open. note: I do NOT use ti.cloud - I have my own APN server which works fine. I am not using Alloy. Notifications are correctly received when the app is closed/paused. Should be easy enough to confirm without a specific test case. #urgent """"",title+description
TIMOB-15784,12,"""ScrollView contentOffset not taking effect if set in tss but OK as setContentOffset method""","""""""ScrollView contentOffset not taking effect if set in tss but OK as setContentOffset method    ScrollView  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ScrollView    contentOffset  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ScrollView-property-contentOffset    setContentOffset  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ScrollView-method-setContentOffset    Sample Project and screen shots attached    * Run on iPhone Simulator (Xcode 4.6.3/iOS 6.1)  * See that image is not offset on startup and see that property contentOffset does not take effect (in tss)  * Click on Label """"""""Center"""""""" and see that method setContentOffset works fine""""""",Bug,"Title: ScrollView contentOffset not taking effect if set in tss but OK as setContentOffset method
Description: """"ScrollView contentOffset not taking effect if set in tss but OK as setContentOffset method ScrollView http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ScrollView contentOffset http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ScrollView-property-contentOffset setContentOffset http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ScrollView-method-setContentOffset Sample Project and screen shots attached * Run on iPhone Simulator (Xcode 4.6.3/iOS 6.1) * See that image is not offset on startup and see that property contentOffset does not take effect (in tss) * Click on Label """"""""Center"""""""" and see that method setContentOffset works fine""""",title+description
TIMOB-15783,12,"""CLI: Add CLI config option to bypass SSL certificate validation (3_1_X backport)""","""""""The Titanium CLI uses HTTP requests for authentication, analytics, and downloading Titanium SDKs. If any of these use an invalid SSL cert, especially in the case of a proxy server, then the requests fail. This may be remedied by adding a CLI option that disabled the """"""""rejectUnauthorized"""""""" request parameter.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Add CLI config option to bypass SSL certificate validation (3_1_X backport)
Description: """"The Titanium CLI uses HTTP requests for authentication, analytics, and downloading Titanium SDKs. If any of these use an invalid SSL cert, especially in the case of a proxy server, then the requests fail. This may be remedied by adding a CLI option that disabled the """"""""rejectUnauthorized"""""""" request parameter.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15782,12,"""CLI: --no-prompt not being honored""","""""""--no-prompt does not work anymore in the Titanium CLI.        This is a regression that was introduced by https://github.com/<USER>titanium/commit/4fd10d1b37ef19c32eee2b8c19ce45c3ecbb6668, which was fixing another bug where passing in --quiet, --no-prompt, or --no-progress-bars to a 'ti config <key> <value>' or 'ti setup' command would persist those flags in the config.    Expected results:  Command should display the error and then exit.    Actual results:  Command displays the error, but then continues to prompt.    Fix:  The fix is relatively simple: replace all references to {{this.config.cli.prompt}} with {{this.argv.prompt}} in {{cli.js}}.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: --no-prompt not being honored
Description: """"--no-prompt does not work anymore in the Titanium CLI. This is a regression that was introduced by https://github.com/<USER>titanium/commit/4fd10d1b37ef19c32eee2b8c19ce45c3ecbb6668, which was fixing another bug where passing in --quiet, --no-prompt, or --no-progress-bars to a 'ti config <key> <value>' or 'ti setup' command would persist those flags in the config. Expected results: Command should display the error and then exit. Actual results: Command displays the error, but then continues to prompt. Fix: The fix is relatively simple: replace all references to {{this.config.cli.prompt}} with {{this.argv.prompt}} in {{cli.js}}.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15781,12,"""Android: KitKat crash when calling WebView method on wrong thread""","""""""The following code crashes on Android 4.4, does not crash on Android 4.1.2.  The crash log is:  11-20 22:32:31.861: E/TiExceptionHandler(9656): (main) [0,995] - Message: Uncaught Error: java.lang.Throwable: A WebView method was called on thread 'KrollRuntimeThread'. All WebView methods must be called on the same thread. (Expected Looper Looper{41e338c0} called on Looper{41e52348}, FYI main Looper is Looper{41e338c0})  11-20 22:32:31.861: E/TiExceptionHandler(9656): (main) [0,995] - Source:         Ti.API.debug(""""""""user agent: """""""" + $.webview.userAgent);    index.xml:      index.js:      lib/test.html      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitKat crash when calling WebView method on wrong thread
Description: """"The following code crashes on Android 4.4, does not crash on Android 4.1.2. The crash log is: 11-20 22:32:31.861: E/TiExceptionHandler(9656): (main) [0,995] - Message: Uncaught Error: java.lang.Throwable: A WebView method was called on thread 'KrollRuntimeThread'. All WebView methods must be called on the same thread. (Expected Looper Looper{41e338c0} called on Looper{41e52348}, FYI main Looper is Looper{41e338c0}) 11-20 22:32:31.861: E/TiExceptionHandler(9656): (main) [0,995] - Source: Ti.API.debug(""""""""user agent: """""""" + $.webview.userAgent); index.xml: index.js: lib/test.html """"",title+description
