TIMOB-15764,12,"""IOS Webview using setHTML shows an ERROR 'Couldn't determine the proper encoding.' at closing""","""""""h4. Problem Description    When a webview is closed which was filled by using setHTML, it shows errors in the console    h4. Test case      h4. Extra info (error message)   [ERROR] Couldn't determine the proper encoding. Make sure this file: LucepediAPP.app is UTF-8 encoded.  [ERROR] Error loading file: /Users/ncdegroot/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications/F751D4EE-E3B7-4823-B3F3-F8A76ED38238/LucepediAPP.app. Message was: Error Domain=NSCocoaErrorDomain Code=257 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. (Cocoa error 257.)"""""""" UserInfo=0xae690e0 {NSFilePath=/Users/ncdegroot/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications/F751D4EE-E3B7-4823-B3F3-F8A76ED38238/LucepediAPP.app, NSUnderlyingError=0xae69140 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. Permission deni  """"""",Bug,"Title: IOS Webview using setHTML shows an ERROR 'Couldn't determine the proper encoding.' at closing
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When a webview is closed which was filled by using setHTML, it shows errors in the console h4. Test case h4. Extra info (error message) [ERROR] Couldn't determine the proper encoding. Make sure this file: LucepediAPP.app is UTF-8 encoded. [ERROR] Error loading file: /Users/ncdegroot/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications/F751D4EE-E3B7-4823-B3F3-F8A76ED38238/LucepediAPP.app. Message was: Error Domain=NSCocoaErrorDomain Code=257 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. (Cocoa error 257.)"""""""" UserInfo=0xae690e0 {NSFilePath=/Users/ncdegroot/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications/F751D4EE-E3B7-4823-B3F3-F8A76ED38238/LucepediAPP.app, NSUnderlyingError=0xae69140 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. Permission deni """"",title+description
TIMOB-15763,12,"""Android: Ti.App.fireEvent will not work on file missing .html extension""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce when putting <script type='text/javascript'>Ti.App.fireEvent('someEvent');</script> in a file without .html extension, the command not work.  for example, Ti.App.fireEvent() not work in .xhtml file but work in .html file  h3. Actual Result Ti.App.fireEvent() not work in .xhtml file  h3. Expected Result Ti.App.fireEvent() should work in .xhtml file""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.App.fireEvent will not work on file missing .html extension
