TIMOB-15731,12,"""Samples: RSS Reader sample has warnings - missing semicolons and deprecated objects""","""""""h5. Description:  The RSS Sample has missing semicolons which is indicated as an exclamation mark on each file with the problem.    The sample also uses the newly-deprecated """"""""navgroup"""""""" object which also produces a warning.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) import the RSS reader sample  2) Open the file resources/services/rss.js  3) Open the file resources/ui/handheld/ios/ApplicationWindow.js    h5. Result:  rss.ja has missing semicolons.  ApplicationWindow.js has deprecated objects    h5. Expected Result:  No warnings""""""",Bug,"Title: Samples: RSS Reader sample has warnings - missing semicolons and deprecated objects
Description: """"h5. Description: The RSS Sample has missing semicolons which is indicated as an exclamation mark on each file with the problem. The sample also uses the newly-deprecated """"""""navgroup"""""""" object which also produces a warning. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) import the RSS reader sample 2) Open the file resources/services/rss.js 3) Open the file resources/ui/handheld/ios/ApplicationWindow.js h5. Result: rss.ja has missing semicolons. ApplicationWindow.js has deprecated objects h5. Expected Result: No warnings""""",title+description
TIMOB-15730,12,"""iOS: Cannot install to iOS devices or simulators""","""""""*Details:* Currently, cannot install to iOS devices or simulators. It is related to TIMOB-15711.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a default app using latest SDK build  2. Install to either iOS device or simulator    *Actual:* Build <USER>will stall here:    [DEBUG] : Removing empty directories  [INFO] : Image optimization complete    *Expected:* Should be able to install to iOS devices and simulators.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot install to iOS devices or simulators
Description: """"*Details:* Currently, cannot install to iOS devices or simulators. It is related to TIMOB-15711. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a default app using latest SDK build 2. Install to either iOS device or simulator *Actual:* Build <USER>will stall here: [DEBUG] : Removing empty directories [INFO] : Image optimization complete *Expected:* Should be able to install to iOS devices and simulators.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15729,12,"""iOS: Large apps fail to install on device""","""""""Larger iOS apps fail to install to device.    Here are the steps I used to reproduce this issue:  1. Create a new titanium project  2. Add the /Library/Desktop Pictures directory into the Resources/iphone directory  (copy the directory twice if it's doesn't repro the issue)  3. Install to the app to device: ti build -p ios -T device    Expected Result:  Device fails to install on xcode  Actual Result:  The app fails to install     Notes:   The threshold seems to be around 200MB.  I get this error in xcode: _select_socket: receive secure message timeout!    Installing the large apps seems to hang on iTunes deployment as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Large apps fail to install on device
Description: """"Larger iOS apps fail to install to device. Here are the steps I used to reproduce this issue: 1. Create a new titanium project 2. Add the /Library/Desktop Pictures directory into the Resources/iphone directory (copy the directory twice if it's doesn't repro the issue) 3. Install to the app to device: ti build -p ios -T device Expected Result: Device fails to install on xcode Actual Result: The app fails to install Notes: The threshold seems to be around 200MB. I get this error in xcode: _select_socket: receive secure message timeout! Installing the large apps seems to hang on iTunes deployment as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15728,12,"""CLI: Add some diagnostic capabilities for setup/info""","""""""we are having a number of challenges in certain complex IT environment that use SOCKS, HTTP Proxies, blocked outbound websites, etc.      we need to add something either to setup or info (or maybe a specific command?) that will perform a series of tests to attempt to reach our systems.  it would be good as well to have this also dump out any whitelisted IP / hostnames we depend on so that an administrator could easily give that to their NetOps people.  (this would suggested by a customer recently).  This would include not only the CLI but Titanium SDK and Studio, etc.    we should hit NPM, api.<USER>net, Tistudio update service, etc with a test request and validate that we can use those services correctly in the environment the CLI is running.   """"""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Add some diagnostic capabilities for setup/info
Description: """"we are having a number of challenges in certain complex IT environment that use SOCKS, HTTP Proxies, blocked outbound websites, etc. we need to add something either to setup or info (or maybe a specific command?) that will perform a series of tests to attempt to reach our systems. it would be good as well to have this also dump out any whitelisted IP / hostnames we depend on so that an administrator could easily give that to their NetOps people. (this would suggested by a customer recently). This would include not only the CLI but Titanium SDK and Studio, etc. we should hit NPM, api.<USER>net, Tistudio update service, etc with a test request and validate that we can use those services correctly in the environment the CLI is running. """"",title+description
