TIMOB-15698,12,"""Anvil: iOS tests in anvil fail to run""","""""""Due to the changes in secure storage, specifically https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/0056de40007059a256db0da56438f5ff2b1cb049, the old python scripts no longer work for Ti.App.Properties.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run anvil for iOS   a. In titanium_mobile/anvil/driver, run 'node driver.js --mode=local --platform=ios""""""""   b. In the CLI prompt, type 'start'    Expected Results:  All the tests should run    Actual Results:  Anvil fails with the error: data parameter is nil at init.js  (The line actually points to an problem with Ti.App.Properties)""""""",Bug,"Title: Anvil: iOS tests in anvil fail to run
Description: """"Due to the changes in secure storage, specifically https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/0056de40007059a256db0da56438f5ff2b1cb049, the old python scripts no longer work for Ti.App.Properties. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run anvil for iOS a. In titanium_mobile/anvil/driver, run 'node driver.js --mode=local --platform=ios"""""""" b. In the CLI prompt, type 'start' Expected Results: All the tests should run Actual Results: Anvil fails with the error: data parameter is nil at init.js (The line actually points to an problem with Ti.App.Properties)""""",title+description
