TIMOB-15694,12,"""NPM: CLI - NPM creates titanium aliases in different bin directories""","""""""*Details:* NPM have some how created titanium aliases in two different location: /usr/local/bin and /usr/bin (see attachments). Both aliases are pointing to the correct titanium executable which is: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/bin/titanium    Also, TiStudio seems to be using the titanium alias from the /usr/bin directory:    Verified with other QE members that their TiStudio is using the titanium alias from /usr/local/bin; *this is only affecting my machine.*      *Possible reproducible steps:*  1. Switch between different versions of TiStudio i.e. GA, RC, or Nightly  2. Allow TiStudio to install Titanium CLI    *Actual:* Titanium aliases are created in different directories (see attachments).    *Expected:* Titanium aliases should only be created in /usr/local/bin since my *npm get prefix* is set to /usr/local.""""""",Bug,"Title: NPM: CLI - NPM creates titanium aliases in different bin directories
Description: """"*Details:* NPM have some how created titanium aliases in two different location: /usr/local/bin and /usr/bin (see attachments). Both aliases are pointing to the correct titanium executable which is: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/bin/titanium Also, TiStudio seems to be using the titanium alias from the /usr/bin directory: Verified with other QE members that their TiStudio is using the titanium alias from /usr/local/bin; *this is only affecting my machine.* *Possible reproducible steps:* 1. Switch between different versions of TiStudio i.e. GA, RC, or Nightly 2. Allow TiStudio to install Titanium CLI *Actual:* Titanium aliases are created in different directories (see attachments). *Expected:* Titanium aliases should only be created in /usr/local/bin since my *npm get prefix* is set to /usr/local.""""",title+description
