Description: """"h4. Description Ability to set the position of the media playback to start the media from the middle instead of from start.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15674,12,"""ListView: Set data including sections and items with one call ""","""""""h1. Request    A way to set data both sections and items with just one call into a listview.    Example:         h1. Current Behavior    Customer currently have a listview and they create 20 to 30 sections dynamically but counting the items in each section they made near 200 """"""""cross the bridge"""""""" actions and they are worried about impact in the performance.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: ListView: Set data including sections and items with one call
Description: """"h1. Request A way to set data both sections and items with just one call into a listview. Example: h1. Current Behavior Customer currently have a listview and they create 20 to 30 sections dynamically but counting the items in each section they made near 200 """"""""cross the bridge"""""""" actions and they are worried about impact in the performance. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15673,12,"""MobileWeb: Windows Store: Support Visual Studio 2013""","""""""The current windows store packaging for Mobile Web only supports Visual Studio 2012. 2013 has a different project structure unfortunately. To support both, the CLI will need to detect which version the developer is using and offer up separate project templates depending on the version. Currently, only 2012 is supported. Note that Windows Phone development is not (yet?) supported in Visual Studio 2013, so this only affects Windows Store projects.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Windows Store: Support Visual Studio 2013
Description: """"The current windows store packaging for Mobile Web only supports Visual Studio 2012. 2013 has a different project structure unfortunately. To support both, the CLI will need to detect which version the developer is using and offer up separate project templates depending on the version. Currently, only 2012 is supported. Note that Windows Phone development is not (yet?) supported in Visual Studio 2013, so this only affects Windows Store projects.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15672,12,"""iOS: ScrollIndicatoryStyle - ScrollIndicatoryStyle property is returning 'undefined' error when launching on device""","""""""*Details:* Ti.UI.iPhone.ScrollIdnicatoryStyle property is returning 'undefined' error when launching on device.    *This is a regression because it worked on 3.1.3.GA stack.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Install SampleTab.zip attachment to an ipad device; app was built specifically for ipad  2. Launch app    *Actual:* 'undefined' error is returned when app is launched (see undefined_error.png).    If you comment out line 10 (scrollIndicatorStyle:Ti.UI.iPhone.ScrollIndicatorStyle.DEFAULT), then the error will not be thrown.    *Expected:* An 'undefined' error should not thrown.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollIndicatoryStyle - ScrollIndicatoryStyle property is returning 'undefined' error when launching on device
Description: """"*Details:* Ti.UI.iPhone.ScrollIdnicatoryStyle property is returning 'undefined' error when launching on device. *This is a regression because it worked on 3.1.3.GA stack.* *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Install SampleTab.zip attachment to an ipad device; app was built specifically for ipad 2. Launch app *Actual:* 'undefined' error is returned when app is launched (see undefined_error.png). If you comment out line 10 (scrollIndicatorStyle:Ti.UI.iPhone.ScrollIndicatorStyle.DEFAULT), then the error will not be thrown. *Expected:* An 'undefined' error should not thrown.""""",title+description
