TIMOB-15645,12,"""Andorid: CLI: Legacy flag does not work on CLI""","""""""Test steps:    Running something like """"""""ti build -p android --avd-id 14 --avd-skin HVGA --legacy"""""""" will return an error:        This could be related to the fact that the templates were moved.  After resolving this issue, we will most likely need to modify AppInfo.java to include the new getDeployType() method as well.    Another thing to note is that the '-T device' flag does not seem to work for legacy either.  It just assumes that it is an emulator and prompts the user for an avd-id.""""""",Bug,"Title: Andorid: CLI: Legacy flag does not work on CLI
Description: """"Test steps: Running something like """"""""ti build -p android --avd-id 14 --avd-skin HVGA --legacy"""""""" will return an error: This could be related to the fact that the templates were moved. After resolving this issue, we will most likely need to modify AppInfo.java to include the new getDeployType() method as well. Another thing to note is that the '-T device' flag does not seem to work for legacy either. It just assumes that it is an emulator and prompts the user for an avd-id.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15644,12,"""ListItem """"searchableText"""" should default to """"title""""""","""""""h2. problem    In TiSDK 3.2.0 the {{searchableText}} property was introduced for Ti.UI.ListItem. This is to work along with the {{searchView}}.     If I attempt to use the default template using simply the {{title}} property on ListItems, the {{title}} is not used by the {{searchView}}. I instead need to explicitly add {{searchableText}} with the same value as the {{title}}. My expectation is that in the absence of {{searchableText}} it would use the given {{title}} as the {{searchableText}}.    h2. example        If I search for """"""""row"""""""" in an attached {{searchView}}, only the second list item will be listed. I think the expected behavior would be that both would show, using the {{title}} as the default {{searchableText}}. It also seems quite redundant to have to list both.""""""",Bug,"Title: ListItem """"searchableText"""" should default to """"title""""
Description: """"h2. problem In TiSDK 3.2.0 the {{searchableText}} property was introduced for Ti.UI.ListItem. This is to work along with the {{searchView}}. If I attempt to use the default template using simply the {{title}} property on ListItems, the {{title}} is not used by the {{searchView}}. I instead need to explicitly add {{searchableText}} with the same value as the {{title}}. My expectation is that in the absence of {{searchableText}} it would use the given {{title}} as the {{searchableText}}. h2. example If I search for """"""""row"""""""" in an attached {{searchView}}, only the second list item will be listed. I think the expected behavior would be that both would show, using the {{title}} as the default {{searchableText}}. It also seems quite redundant to have to list both.""""",title+description
