TIMOB-15627,12,"""iOS: Ti.Media.Item.artwork returns TiBlob even if it has no Artwork.""","""""""""""""""Image for the item's artwork as a Blob object, or null if no artwork is available."""""""" - TiDoc    Even if there is no artwork for the Item, this property will return a TiBlob, causing many problems if you are trying to filter for null or not.        Note that this code must be tested on an iOS Device with an iPod library full of songs, with both artwork and not. The simulator does not have the iPod installed on it.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Media.Item.artwork returns TiBlob even if it has no Artwork.
Description: """"""""""""Image for the item's artwork as a Blob object, or null if no artwork is available."""""""" - TiDoc Even if there is no artwork for the Item, this property will return a TiBlob, causing many problems if you are trying to filter for null or not. Note that this code must be tested on an iOS Device with an iPod library full of songs, with both artwork and not. The simulator does not have the iPod installed on it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15626,12,"""Android: Modified sample 2-tab Alloy project does not run on Android devices with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce  1) Create a new 2-tab Alloy project, and follow the guide as per http://www.webdevd.com/titanium-apps-with-android-action-bar-tabgroups-and-menu-items/ until just before Adding Menu Items  2) Export project as Android APK and install on device with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side (e.g. Samsung Galaxy S3/S4, Xperia V, etc.)    h3. Actual Result  Shows the application splash screen on Android devices with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side    h3. Expected Result  Should show the application windows and tabs on Android devices with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Modified sample 2-tab Alloy project does not run on Android devices with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce 1) Create a new 2-tab Alloy project, and follow the guide as per http://www.webdevd.com/titanium-apps-with-android-action-bar-tabgroups-and-menu-items/ until just before Adding Menu Items 2) Export project as Android APK and install on device with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side (e.g. Samsung Galaxy S3/S4, Xperia V, etc.) h3. Actual Result Shows the application splash screen on Android devices with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side h3. Expected Result Should show the application windows and tabs on Android devices with screen size larger than 800 px on any one side""""",title+description
TIMOB-15624,12,"""iOS: AttributedString - Shadow attribute does not appear with the underline attribute for a label text""","""""""*Details:* Shadow attribute does not appear with the underline attribute for a label text.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Install the following app.js code to device:      *Actual:* A green shadow does not appear behind """"""""<USER>"""""" (see no_shadow.png).    *Expected:* A green shadow should appear behind """"""""<USER>"""""" (see shadow.png).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: AttributedString - Shadow attribute does not appear with the underline attribute for a label text
Description: """"*Details:* Shadow attribute does not appear with the underline attribute for a label text. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Install the following app.js code to device: *Actual:* A green shadow does not appear behind """"""""<USER>"""""" (see no_shadow.png). *Expected:* A green shadow should appear behind """"""""<USER>"""""" (see shadow.png).""""",title+description
TIMOB-15622,12,"""iOS7: On Swipe back event (on TabGroup windows) UI not functioning properly""","""""""h6.Issue description  When using the TabGroup in an application  developer is getting strange behaviour in the app, some times app crashes and/or not functioning properly. iOS7 introduces the new swipe back to the before window in the TabGroup.     h6.Test scenario  A Tab contains several windows, I.E. win1, win2, win3. Every window contains a tableView. If you navigate back to first window from second window using swipe back, you can observe how tableViews become unusable (attached video """"""""IMG_1312.MOV"""""""").    h6.Steps to reproduce  1) Please get sample attached running (it has a tabGroup, that requires couple of windows adding the TableViews).  2) Click any row.   3) You can either go back (Back button) or resume navigation to next window. At this point everything runs smoothly.  4) Try out to go with the cursor to the left side (few pixels from left side), click to slide (Important: Do not drag completely).  5) TableViews are unusable now.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: On Swipe back event (on TabGroup windows) UI not functioning properly
Description: """"h6.Issue description When using the TabGroup in an application developer is getting strange behaviour in the app, some times app crashes and/or not functioning properly. iOS7 introduces the new swipe back to the before window in the TabGroup. h6.Test scenario A Tab contains several windows, I.E. win1, win2, win3. Every window contains a tableView. If you navigate back to first window from second window using swipe back, you can observe how tableViews become unusable (attached video """"""""IMG_1312.MOV""""""""). h6.Steps to reproduce 1) Please get sample attached running (it has a tabGroup, that requires couple of windows adding the TableViews). 2) Click any row. 3) You can either go back (Back button) or resume navigation to next window. At this point everything runs smoothly. 4) Try out to go with the cursor to the left side (few pixels from left side), click to slide (Important: Do not drag completely). 5) TableViews are unusable now.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15621,12,"""Android: convertPointToView gives different results with SDK 3.1.3 compared to 3.0.2""","""""""h3. Problem description  User relies on convertPointToView to show a tooltip in a particular position, based on the user's click. However, using SDK 3.1.3, the coordinates given back by the function are negative, and the code is not working anymore.    h3. Sample code  I reduced their code as much as possible. This sample shows the different values of 'y' when clicking the button using SDK 3.0.2 and SDK 3.1.3    index.xml      pickerRow.xml      index.tss      index.js      h3. Steps  1. Build with SDK 3.0.2  2. Open the app on Android  3. Click the red button and see logs  4. Repeat the steps using SDK 3.1.3    h3. **Result**  The values for 'y' are very different; in particular, with 3.0.2 and my device I get around 600, while 3.1.3 gives a -500 (negative) for the same value.    h3. Work-around:  The workaround is setting the height of the tableview to some specific number e.g. """"""""500dp"""""""" or """"""""90%"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: convertPointToView gives different results with SDK 3.1.3 compared to 3.0.2
Description: """"h3. Problem description User relies on convertPointToView to show a tooltip in a particular position, based on the user's click. However, using SDK 3.1.3, the coordinates given back by the function are negative, and the code is not working anymore. h3. Sample code I reduced their code as much as possible. This sample shows the different values of 'y' when clicking the button using SDK 3.0.2 and SDK 3.1.3 index.xml pickerRow.xml index.tss index.js h3. Steps 1. Build with SDK 3.0.2 2. Open the app on Android 3. Click the red button and see logs 4. Repeat the steps using SDK 3.1.3 h3. **Result** The values for 'y' are very different; in particular, with 3.0.2 and my device I get around 600, while 3.1.3 gives a -500 (negative) for the same value. h3. Work-around: The workaround is setting the height of the tableview to some specific number e.g. """"""""500dp"""""""" or """"""""90%"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-15619,12,"""toImage does not honor 'width' when rasterizing a Label. Rasterizing to a window works properly.""","""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: toImage does not honor 'width' when rasterizing a Label. Rasterizing to a window works properly.
Description: """"""""",title+description
TIMOB-15618,12,"""Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer fires COMPLETE event when url changes""","""""""After changing the Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer.url value the videoPlayer fires a onComplete event that should not be fired, or at least fired including the real reason for it, but currently the event.reason is 0 (Ti.Media.VIDEO_FINISH_REASON_PLAYBACK_ENDED).    This is causing a lot of trouble to create a playlist app.  We could have a VIDEO_FINISH_REASON_SOURCE_CHANGED as a new reason, would be way better    This is a very old topic: [http://developer.<USER>com/question/121674/complete-event-firing-when-changing-url-on-video-player]      """"""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer fires COMPLETE event when url changes
Description: """"After changing the Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer.url value the videoPlayer fires a onComplete event that should not be fired, or at least fired including the real reason for it, but currently the event.reason is 0 (Ti.Media.VIDEO_FINISH_REASON_PLAYBACK_ENDED). This is causing a lot of trouble to create a playlist app. We could have a VIDEO_FINISH_REASON_SOURCE_CHANGED as a new reason, would be way better This is a very old topic: [http://developer.<USER>com/question/121674/complete-event-firing-when-changing-url-on-video-player] """"",title+description
TIMOB-15617,12,"""Android: Update google_service_library in ti_cloudpush module""","""""""It seems that ti.cloudpush google_services_library is outdated. We need to update it to the latest version.  Testing steps:   - Build the module, run the sample cloudpush code: example/app.js. Make sure everything is still working.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Update google_service_library in ti_cloudpush module
Description: """"It seems that ti.cloudpush google_services_library is outdated. We need to update it to the latest version. Testing steps: - Build the module, run the sample cloudpush code: example/app.js. Make sure everything is still working.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15616,12,"""iOS: Hash value empty for local file system URL in WebView""","""""""h3. Description:  User tried to load an html file located in the filesystem with an appended hash value (#value) but when trying to retrieve the value via window.location.hash this is null.    h3. Test case:    Index.js      index.html      h3. Output:  [INFO] :   url: file:///Users/<USER>Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2FA2A5DA-7AA4-4FFA-86F3-D634BD77BB39/WebViewHash.app/html/index.html  [INFO] :   hash:    h3. Additional Comments:  This only happens when the url is from the local filesystem, when the url is an http:// address returns the hash value correctly.    h3. Work-around:  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Hash value empty for local file system URL in WebView
Description: """"h3. Description: User tried to load an html file located in the filesystem with an appended hash value (#value) but when trying to retrieve the value via window.location.hash this is null. h3. Test case: Index.js index.html h3. Output: [INFO] : url: file:///Users/<USER>Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2FA2A5DA-7AA4-4FFA-86F3-D634BD77BB39/WebViewHash.app/html/index.html [INFO] : hash: h3. Additional Comments: This only happens when the url is from the local filesystem, when the url is an http:// address returns the hash value correctly. h3. Work-around: """"",title+description
