TIMOB-15614,12,"""Tizen: Project fails to install onto phone or simulator""","""""""h5.Description  Creating a Tizen project works as expected, and building the project also works.  However, installing the application fails and gives no reason why it does.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Build a Tizen project in studio  2. Run the project on Tizen simulator or device    h5.Expected Result  The project should be installed on the device and should run as expected.    h5.Actual Result  The project builds successfully, then stops running and gives no output.    +Extra Information+  Log file has been added to show studios attempt at installing.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen: Project fails to install onto phone or simulator
Description: """"h5.Description Creating a Tizen project works as expected, and building the project also works. However, installing the application fails and gives no reason why it does. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Build a Tizen project in studio 2. Run the project on Tizen simulator or device h5.Expected Result The project should be installed on the device and should run as expected. h5.Actual Result The project builds successfully, then stops running and gives no output. +Extra Information+ Log file has been added to show studios attempt at installing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15613,12,"""iOS7: Ti.Map.View always asks for permission to use current location""","""""""The following code will show a alert asking the user for permission to use his current location, regardless if {{userLocation}} is set to {{false}} or unset:        h1. Cause  When the map is initialized in [TiMapView.m|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiMapView.m#L63], {{showsUsersLocation}} is always set to {{YES}}. Instead, this should depend on whether {{userLocation}} was set.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Ti.Map.View always asks for permission to use current location
Description: """"The following code will show a alert asking the user for permission to use his current location, regardless if {{userLocation}} is set to {{false}} or unset: h1. Cause When the map is initialized in [TiMapView.m|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiMapView.m#L63], {{showsUsersLocation}} is always set to {{YES}}. Instead, this should depend on whether {{userLocation}} was set.""""",title+description
