TIMOB-15585,12,"""Tizen: Cannot find module adm-zip.js""","""""""h5.Description:  1.Install CLI 3.2.0  2.Download the mentioned ti sdk.  3.Build for android,IOS,Blackberry,Mobile web.    h5.Actual Result:  1.We can't build for any platform & get following errors:    2.It is caused because of some issues with the tizen sdk inside of ti sdk.  3.Removing tizen folder from the sdk & updating the manifest.json fixes the issue.    h5.Expected Result:  1.We should be able to build for all platforms normally.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen: Cannot find module adm-zip.js
Description: """"h5.Description: 1.Install CLI 3.2.0 2.Download the mentioned ti sdk. 3.Build for android,IOS,Blackberry,Mobile web. h5.Actual Result: 1.We can't build for any platform & get following errors: 2.It is caused because of some issues with the tizen sdk inside of ti sdk. 3.Removing tizen folder from the sdk & updating the manifest.json fixes the issue. h5.Expected Result: 1.We should be able to build for all platforms normally.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15584,12,"""Android: Spinner picker does not layout correctly""","""""""This is a regression in master (3.2.0). 3.1.3.GA works fine.  To reproduce:  1. KS->Controls->Picker->Android """"""""useSpinner""""""""-text.   i) Expected behavior: show 3 spinners. Actual behavior: only show 1 spinner. See the attached screenshot for the latest master and 3.1.3.GA.  ii) Click the button """"""""Add 'Manny'"""""""" and then scroll the spinner. The app crashes. The log is     2. KS->Controls->Picker->Android """"""""useSpinner""""""""-text2. Some spinners do not show. See the attached screenshot for the latest master and 3.1.3.GA.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Spinner picker does not layout correctly
Description: """"This is a regression in master (3.2.0). 3.1.3.GA works fine. To reproduce: 1. KS->Controls->Picker->Android """"""""useSpinner""""""""-text. i) Expected behavior: show 3 spinners. Actual behavior: only show 1 spinner. See the attached screenshot for the latest master and 3.1.3.GA. ii) Click the button """"""""Add 'Manny'"""""""" and then scroll the spinner. The app crashes. The log is 2. KS->Controls->Picker->Android """"""""useSpinner""""""""-text2. Some spinners do not show. See the attached screenshot for the latest master and 3.1.3.GA.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15583,12,"""CLI : cli.progressBars should be true by default in ti config""","""""""h5.Description:  1.Install the 3.2.0 CLI.  2.Run command """"""""ti sdk install -b master -d"""""""".    h5.Actual result:  1. We do not see any progress bar as """"""""cli.progressBars"""""""" is set to false in ti config by default.    h5.Expected Result:  1. """"""""cli.progressBars"""""""" should be true by default in ti config.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI : cli.progressBars should be true by default in ti config
Description: """"h5.Description: 1.Install the 3.2.0 CLI. 2.Run command """"""""ti sdk install -b master -d"""""""". h5.Actual result: 1. We do not see any progress bar as """"""""cli.progressBars"""""""" is set to false in ti config by default. h5.Expected Result: 1. """"""""cli.progressBars"""""""" should be true by default in ti config.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15582,12,"""Nexus 7 navigation bar causes changes in device height, width on orientation change""","""""""Nexus 7 has 7"""""""" screen with 1280x800 , 216 ppi resolution.  See """"""""Technical specifications"""""""" section at following official Google Nexus 7 website   https://play.google.com/store/devices/details?id=nexus_7_16gb&feature=device-featured#?t=W251bGwsMSwxLDIwMiwibnVsbC13ZWJfaG9tZV81MDAwMDA1X25leHVzSU5fZGV2aWNlc19JTl9fNTAwMDAwNV9uZXh1c0lOXzFfcHJvbW9fMTM2NzYyNDkxOTkzMSJd    While using Tatanium SDK, when I change orientation, navigation bar and status bar height varies. Which causes change in following properties    In portrait orientation  Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth = 800  Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight = 1205    In landscape orientation  Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth = 1280  Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight = 736    Actually it should only interchange height and width when orientation changes.    I am using these properties to decide the diagonal screen size of every device on which my app runs. Most of all Android and iOS devices works fine but only Nexus 7 has above mentioned problem.    Method to reproduce the bug :    Source code :  Create new app in Titanium SDK 3.1.3 and put following lines in app.js.    Ti.API.info('Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth : '+Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth);  Ti.API.info('Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight : '+Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight);    Now, run this app on Nexus 7 portrait mode and note the log.     After that change orientation, run this app again on Nexus 7 and note the log.""""""",Bug,"Title: Nexus 7 navigation bar causes changes in device height, width on orientation change
Description: """"Nexus 7 has 7"""""""" screen with 1280x800 , 216 ppi resolution. See """"""""Technical specifications"""""""" section at following official Google Nexus 7 website https://play.google.com/store/devices/details?id=nexus_7_16gb&feature=device-featured#?t=W251bGwsMSwxLDIwMiwibnVsbC13ZWJfaG9tZV81MDAwMDA1X25leHVzSU5fZGV2aWNlc19JTl9fNTAwMDAwNV9uZXh1c0lOXzFfcHJvbW9fMTM2NzYyNDkxOTkzMSJd While using Tatanium SDK, when I change orientation, navigation bar and status bar height varies. Which causes change in following properties In portrait orientation Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth = 800 Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight = 1205 In landscape orientation Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth = 1280 Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight = 736 Actually it should only interchange height and width when orientation changes. I am using these properties to decide the diagonal screen size of every device on which my app runs. Most of all Android and iOS devices works fine but only Nexus 7 has above mentioned problem. Method to reproduce the bug : Source code : Create new app in Titanium SDK 3.1.3 and put following lines in app.js. Ti.API.info('Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth : '+Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth); Ti.API.info('Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight : '+Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight); Now, run this app on Nexus 7 portrait mode and note the log. After that change orientation, run this app again on Nexus 7 and note the log.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15581,12,"""iOS: Tab title does not show if there is no icon""","""""""h2. problem    Before TiSDK 3.2.0, tabs that had a title but no icon showed the title just fine. Using the current TiSDK 3.2.0 though, the title does not show if there is no icon.    h2. test case    # Create a default traditional titanium app (2 tabbed)  # Comment out the {{icon}} property in both {{createTab}} calls in the app.js file  # Set the TiSDK version in the tiapp.xml to be the current 3.2.0 CI (install if necessary)  # Run the app for iOS 6.0, 6.1, and 7.0 sims. None will show the tab titles.  # Change the TiSDK version in tiapp.xml to anything in the 3.1.X branch.  # Run the app for iOS 6.0, 6.1, and 7.0 sims. The titles will show in all cases.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tab title does not show if there is no icon
Description: """"h2. problem Before TiSDK 3.2.0, tabs that had a title but no icon showed the title just fine. Using the current TiSDK 3.2.0 though, the title does not show if there is no icon. h2. test case # Create a default traditional titanium app (2 tabbed) # Comment out the {{icon}} property in both {{createTab}} calls in the app.js file # Set the TiSDK version in the tiapp.xml to be the current 3.2.0 CI (install if necessary) # Run the app for iOS 6.0, 6.1, and 7.0 sims. None will show the tab titles. # Change the TiSDK version in tiapp.xml to anything in the 3.1.X branch. # Run the app for iOS 6.0, 6.1, and 7.0 sims. The titles will show in all cases.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15580,12,"""Android: Add sub title property to the ActionBar""","""""""In native Android it is possible to add a subtitle to the ActionBar as follows:        This is not possible in Titanium, please implement the subtitle feature for Android action bars.    Related Android Doc: http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/ActionBar.html#setSubtitle(java.lang.CharSequence)""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add sub title property to the ActionBar
Description: """"In native Android it is possible to add a subtitle to the ActionBar as follows: This is not possible in Titanium, please implement the subtitle feature for Android action bars. Related Android Doc: http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/ActionBar.html#setSubtitle(java.lang.CharSequence)""""",title+description
TIMOB-15579,12,"""Android: START_REDELIVER_INTENT can cause black screen""","""""""h1. Problem  Assume we have a heavyweight window, and a service with START_REDELIVER_INTENT. If the app is closed (for low memory, or any other reason), and the service is restarted by the OS, launching the app shows only a black screen.    h2. What's Worse  Because heavyweight/lightweight is being antiquated, and every window will now be heavyweight, the latest master builds exhibit this problem on every window. Using older versions of the SDK (3.1.3.GA), making the window lightweight would avoid this issue, somewhat, but properties like exitOnClose don't work properly.    h2. Example  Follow the 4 steps in the app to reproduce this.  {panel:title=app.js}{panel}    {panel:title=service.js}{panel}    {panel:title=tiapp.xml}{panel}    h2. Console  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: START_REDELIVER_INTENT can cause black screen
Description: """"h1. Problem Assume we have a heavyweight window, and a service with START_REDELIVER_INTENT. If the app is closed (for low memory, or any other reason), and the service is restarted by the OS, launching the app shows only a black screen. h2. What's Worse Because heavyweight/lightweight is being antiquated, and every window will now be heavyweight, the latest master builds exhibit this problem on every window. Using older versions of the SDK (3.1.3.GA), making the window lightweight would avoid this issue, somewhat, but properties like exitOnClose don't work properly. h2. Example Follow the 4 steps in the app to reproduce this. {panel:title=app.js}{panel} {panel:title=service.js}{panel} {panel:title=tiapp.xml}{panel} h2. Console """"",title+description
TIMOB-15578,12,"""Android: Map module crashes when trying to exit the app""","""""""Build map v2 against latest master, run this code on latest master:    1. hit the back button, observe crash""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Map module crashes when trying to exit the app
Description: """"Build map v2 against latest master, run this code on latest master: 1. hit the back button, observe crash""""",title+description
TIMOB-15577,12,"""iOS: Disallow snapshot of app appearing on app resume""","""""""h3. Description  When the app goes to the background a screenshot of the current app state is taken. When the app resumes that screenshot is shown for a split of a second. This is to make a visual hint to the user that the app is still running where it was before going to the background. On iOS 7 that screenshot image is used also to display the app in the multitasking experience.    h3. The problem:  For some customers this is a security concern, since that screenshot can reveal confidential app data, such as user back account numbers, usernames, private messages, etc...    h3. New feature.  A property will be exposed in the Ti.App module to avoid this from happening. The splash screen image of the app will be shown instead of a snapshot.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Disallow snapshot of app appearing on app resume
Description: """"h3. Description When the app goes to the background a screenshot of the current app state is taken. When the app resumes that screenshot is shown for a split of a second. This is to make a visual hint to the user that the app is still running where it was before going to the background. On iOS 7 that screenshot image is used also to display the app in the multitasking experience. h3. The problem: For some customers this is a security concern, since that screenshot can reveal confidential app data, such as user back account numbers, usernames, private messages, etc... h3. New feature. A property will be exposed in the Ti.App module to avoid this from happening. The splash screen image of the app will be shown instead of a snapshot. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15576,12,"""iOS: Simulator - Add support for iPad Retina (64-bit)""","""""""*Details:* If you have Xcode 5.0.1, which has iOS 7.0.3, Studio GA (3.1.3.201309132423) and Studio RC (3.1.4.201310152018) cannot launch simulator iPad Retina (64-bit).    Simulator iPad Retina (64-bit) will simulate the iPad Air and iPad Mini with retina display hardware.    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Make sure to install Xcode 5.0.1 on your machine  2. In either Studio GA or Studio RC, create a default Titanium or Alloy app  3. Right-click on the newly created project  4. Go to Run As > Run Configurations ...  5. Find *Titanium iOS Simulator* and create a new configuration  6. Specify Device as iPad, Simulator Version as 7.0, and Display Type as Retina & Tall (64-bit); see config.png  7. Press Apply and press Run    *Actual:* Simulator iPad Retina 7.0.3 is launched; see ipad_simu.png and ipad_simu2.png    *Expected:* Simulator iPad Retina (64-bit) 7.0.3 should be launched instead; see ipad_simu3.png    *Note:* We also noticed Studio not picking up the iOS 7.0.3 SDK: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15575""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Simulator - Add support for iPad Retina (64-bit)
Description: """"*Details:* If you have Xcode 5.0.1, which has iOS 7.0.3, Studio GA (3.1.3.201309132423) and Studio RC (3.1.4.201310152018) cannot launch simulator iPad Retina (64-bit). Simulator iPad Retina (64-bit) will simulate the iPad Air and iPad Mini with retina display hardware. *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Make sure to install Xcode 5.0.1 on your machine 2. In either Studio GA or Studio RC, create a default Titanium or Alloy app 3. Right-click on the newly created project 4. Go to Run As > Run Configurations ... 5. Find *Titanium iOS Simulator* and create a new configuration 6. Specify Device as iPad, Simulator Version as 7.0, and Display Type as Retina & Tall (64-bit); see config.png 7. Press Apply and press Run *Actual:* Simulator iPad Retina 7.0.3 is launched; see ipad_simu.png and ipad_simu2.png *Expected:* Simulator iPad Retina (64-bit) 7.0.3 should be launched instead; see ipad_simu3.png *Note:* We also noticed Studio not picking up the iOS 7.0.3 SDK: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15575""""",title+description
TIMOB-15575,12,"""CLI: iOS7.0.3 is not recognized by CLI""","""""""h5.To reproduce  Run command """"""""ti info"""""""" in the terminal    h5.Actual result      h5.Expected result  Should see 7.0.3 iOS Simulator    Note: We believe this is blocking users from launching simulator iPad Retina (64-bit) through Studio: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TISTUD-5597  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS7.0.3 is not recognized by CLI
Description: """"h5.To reproduce Run command """"""""ti info"""""""" in the terminal h5.Actual result h5.Expected result Should see 7.0.3 iOS Simulator Note: We believe this is blocking users from launching simulator iPad Retina (64-bit) through Studio: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TISTUD-5597 """"",title+description
TIMOB-15574,12,"""iOS7: It is not possible close window inside a navgroup, after a small sliding ""","""""""h4. Problem Description    When you have a NavigationWindow, you can open a window and then obtain either:    # a left arrow to close the window  # you can slide the window to close or  # you can actually have a button that closes the window    If you do a small slide of the window and don't actually close it, the close button won't work anymore.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project with Mobile SDK 3.1.3 for iOS 7  2. Paste the provided testcase and run it.  3. Click the label """"""""open window"""""""".   4. Do a little bit of scrolling and then get it back.   5. Click on the close window button, the window won't close.     h4. Testcase    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: It is not possible close window inside a navgroup, after a small sliding
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When you have a NavigationWindow, you can open a window and then obtain either: # a left arrow to close the window # you can slide the window to close or # you can actually have a button that closes the window If you do a small slide of the window and don't actually close it, the close button won't work anymore. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project with Mobile SDK 3.1.3 for iOS 7 2. Paste the provided testcase and run it. 3. Click the label """"""""open window"""""""". 4. Do a little bit of scrolling and then get it back. 5. Click on the close window button, the window won't close. h4. Testcase """"",title+description
TIMOB-15573,12,"""Allow support for control center next/previous/pause buttons""","""""""Currentrly I'm working with one app that will have a playlist, and so I would like to keep it playing on background and I though I would be able to use these controls.    I think would be really nice to have this feature native from <USER> so we would not need to use a module for this feature, wich I think is part of basic iOS features.      Module that does this: https://marketplace.<USER>com/apps/5573?651090353""""""",New Feature,"Title: Allow support for control center next/previous/pause buttons
Description: """"Currentrly I'm working with one app that will have a playlist, and so I would like to keep it playing on background and I though I would be able to use these controls. I think would be really nice to have this feature native from <USER> so we would not need to use a module for this feature, wich I think is part of basic iOS features. Module that does this: https://marketplace.<USER>com/apps/5573?651090353""""",title+description
