Description: """"The default value of a view added to a window is """"""""undefined"""""""". This is not a regression. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create an application with code below and launch the application 2. Click on Show/Hide button Actual: An alert with value """"""""undefined"""""""" is shown which is the value of visible property of view. Expected: The value should be returned as """"""""true"""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-15542,12,"""iOS: BarImage - Setting a barImage property on windows crashes on SDK 3.2.0 with iOS 5.1.X""","""""""*Details:* Setting a barImage property on windows crashes on SDK 3.2.0 with iOS 5.1.X.    This is a *regression* as this does not occur on SDK 3.1.3.GA. However, severity is set to Minor because [minimum iOS support for SDK 3.2.0 is 6.0.X|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/guide/Installing_the_iOS_SDK-section-29004875_InstallingtheiOSSDK-iOSSDK%2FTargetiOSPlatform]    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create a new Titanium app using the app.js, barImage.png, and <EMAIL> attachments; put barImage.png and <EMAIL> in /Resources/iphone  2. Install app to an iOS 5.1.X device    *Actual:* On launch, app will crash (see xcode_console.log).     But, if you comment out the barImage property, then the app will not crash.    *Expected:* App should not crash *or* a warning message should appear indicating the minimum iOS support for SDK 3.2.0.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: BarImage - Setting a barImage property on windows crashes on SDK 3.2.0 with iOS 5.1.X
Description: """"*Details:* Setting a barImage property on windows crashes on SDK 3.2.0 with iOS 5.1.X. This is a *regression* as this does not occur on SDK 3.1.3.GA. However, severity is set to Minor because [minimum iOS support for SDK 3.2.0 is 6.0.X|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/guide/Installing_the_iOS_SDK-section-29004875_InstallingtheiOSSDK-iOSSDK%2FTargetiOSPlatform] *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create a new Titanium app using the app.js, barImage.png, and <EMAIL> attachments; put barImage.png and <EMAIL> in /Resources/iphone 2. Install app to an iOS 5.1.X device *Actual:* On launch, app will crash (see xcode_console.log). But, if you comment out the barImage property, then the app will not crash. *Expected:* App should not crash *or* a warning message should appear indicating the minimum iOS support for SDK 3.2.0.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15541,12,"""iOS: ListView - appendSection() will not display items in the ListView when opening a new window for the first time""","""""""*Details:* If you use listView.appendSection(), then items will not appear in the ListView when opening a new window for the first time.    *This is a regression as this does not occur on SDK 3.1.3.GA.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Launch the following app.js code on a iOS device      2. Press on """"""""dataset1""""""""    *Actual:* Items do not appear (see no_items.png). But, if you go back and press """"""""dataset1"""""""" again, then items will appear.    *Expected:* If you uncomment line 53 and comment line 56, then items should appear after pressing on """"""""dataset1"""""""" for the first time (see items.png)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ListView - appendSection() will not display items in the ListView when opening a new window for the first time
Description: """"*Details:* If you use listView.appendSection(), then items will not appear in the ListView when opening a new window for the first time. *This is a regression as this does not occur on SDK 3.1.3.GA.* *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Launch the following app.js code on a iOS device 2. Press on """"""""dataset1"""""""" *Actual:* Items do not appear (see no_items.png). But, if you go back and press """"""""dataset1"""""""" again, then items will appear. *Expected:* If you uncomment line 53 and comment line 56, then items should appear after pressing on """"""""dataset1"""""""" for the first time (see items.png)""""",title+description
TIMOB-15540,12,"""iOS7: TableView singletap and doubletap events do not provide row information""","""""""h4. Problem Description  The source of events like click, singletap, are not being reported. Instead, you get random internal information.     h4. Steps to Reproduce  1. Create new mobile project with 3.1.3 in iOS  2. Paste the testcase to app.js  3. Run the app, click on the row.  4. You will see the source.     h4. Testcase      h4. Extra info  With singletap and doubletap events, the event contains no row information:    [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':222,'y':31,'bubbles':true,'type':'singletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false}  [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':91,'y':61,'bubbles':true,'type':'singletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false}  [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':145,'y':101,'bubbles':true,'type':'singletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false}  [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':137,'y':22,'bubbles':true,'type':'doubletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false}  [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':130,'y':73,'bubbles':true,'type':'doubletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false}  [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':129,'y':100,'bubbles':true,'type':'doubletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false}    With click events, the event object correctly contains row information:    [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':122,'section':{'horizontalWrap':true},'row':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_0'},'index':0,'y':36,'rowData':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_0'},'searchMode':false,'detail':false,'bubbles':true,'type':'click','source':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_0'},'cancelBubble':false}  [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':135,'section':{'horizontalWrap':true},'row':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_1'},'index':1,'y':9,'rowData':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_1'},'searchMode':false,'detail':false,'bubbles':true,'type':'click','source':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_1'},'cancelBubble':false}  [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':166,'section':{'horizontalWrap':true},'row':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_2'},'index':2,'y':23,'rowData':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_2'},'searchMode':false,'detail':false,'bubbles':true,'type':'click','source':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_2'},'cancelBubble':false}      h4. Expected Result  Row information from singletap, doubletap, and click events (as per current API documentation).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: TableView singletap and doubletap events do not provide row information
Description: """"h4. Problem Description The source of events like click, singletap, are not being reported. Instead, you get random internal information. h4. Steps to Reproduce 1. Create new mobile project with 3.1.3 in iOS 2. Paste the testcase to app.js 3. Run the app, click on the row. 4. You will see the source. h4. Testcase h4. Extra info With singletap and doubletap events, the event contains no row information: [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':222,'y':31,'bubbles':true,'type':'singletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false} [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':91,'y':61,'bubbles':true,'type':'singletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false} [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':145,'y':101,'bubbles':true,'type':'singletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false} [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':137,'y':22,'bubbles':true,'type':'doubletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false} [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':130,'y':73,'bubbles':true,'type':'doubletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false} [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':129,'y':100,'bubbles':true,'type':'doubletap','source':{'hideSearchOnSelection':true,'horizontalWrap':true,'searchHidden':false},'cancelBubble':false} With click events, the event object correctly contains row information: [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':122,'section':{'horizontalWrap':true},'row':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_0'},'index':0,'y':36,'rowData':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_0'},'searchMode':false,'detail':false,'bubbles':true,'type':'click','source':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_0'},'cancelBubble':false} [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':135,'section':{'horizontalWrap':true},'row':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_1'},'index':1,'y':9,'rowData':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_1'},'searchMode':false,'detail':false,'bubbles':true,'type':'click','source':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_1'},'cancelBubble':false} [TRACE] : Event from table: {'x':166,'section':{'horizontalWrap':true},'row':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_2'},'index':2,'y':23,'rowData':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_2'},'searchMode':false,'detail':false,'bubbles':true,'type':'click','source':{'horizontalWrap':true,'title':'row_2'},'cancelBubble':false} h4. Expected Result Row information from singletap, doubletap, and click events (as per current API documentation).""""",title+description
TIMOB-15539,12,"""MobileWeb - Animation throws uncaught exceptions""","""""""Hi,    I'm experiencing uncaught exceptions for already a few months when trying to scroll a ScrollView/Tableviews in MobileWeb with the continuous builds of 3.2.0SDK. The last version I tried is 3.2.0.v20131004155410.    h4. Example 1 TableView:    {code:title=index.js}  $.index.open();      h4. Example 2 ScrollView:    {code:title=index.js}   $.index.open();      h4. Steps to reproduce:     - Open the examples for instance in Chromium / Chrome (I am using version 30 at the moment) and try to scroll.    - A red application error will appear saying """"""""Uncaught TypeError: Cannot call method 'push' of undefined at / (line 9012)"""""""".     - Within Ti/UI/Animation the function go fails to call  {{ animations[wid].push(.... }}    I also tried to use {{<allow-touch>}} in tiapp.xml but it did not help. I am using the 3.2.0 builds because it contains the """"""""[TIMOB-13697] Added jet rockets to Mobile Web"""""""" fix which makes the mobile app much faster.    Link to Q&A [http://developer.<USER>com/question/158326]""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb - Animation throws uncaught exceptions
Description: """"Hi, I'm experiencing uncaught exceptions for already a few months when trying to scroll a ScrollView/Tableviews in MobileWeb with the continuous builds of 3.2.0SDK. The last version I tried is 3.2.0.v20131004155410. h4. Example 1 TableView: {code:title=index.js} $.index.open(); h4. Example 2 ScrollView: {code:title=index.js} $.index.open(); h4. Steps to reproduce: - Open the examples for instance in Chromium / Chrome (I am using version 30 at the moment) and try to scroll. - A red application error will appear saying """"""""Uncaught TypeError: Cannot call method 'push' of undefined at / (line 9012)"""""""". - Within Ti/UI/Animation the function go fails to call {{ animations[wid].push(.... }} I also tried to use {{<allow-touch>}} in tiapp.xml but it did not help. I am using the 3.2.0 builds because it contains the """"""""[TIMOB-13697] Added jet rockets to Mobile Web"""""""" fix which makes the mobile app much faster. Link to Q&A [http://developer.<USER>com/question/158326]""""",title+description
TIMOB-15538,12,"""iOS7: Clicking a label in first row of table view is not working on 3.1.3GA version""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When I press a label in first row of table view, it is returning [object TiUITableViewRow] instead of [object TiUILabel].   All other rows, it is returning correct label [object TiUILabel].   What could be a reason for this issue happening for only first row?   This issue happens only with 3.1.3GA version when I compiled for iPhone/iPad.    h4. Test case       h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project for iOS7, with 3.1.3  2. Paste the testcase into app.js  3. Run in the simulator  4. Click on the first row.  5. Click on the second row.   6. Check console, you will see the difference, even if you created the two rows in the same way.     h4. Extra info  Log when 1YY label is clicked in TableView:  First row output:  [INFO] e.row =[object TiUITableViewRow], e.source = [object TiUILabel]  Second or any other row is clicked:   [INFO] e.row =[object TiUITableViewRow], e.source = [object TiUITableViewRow]""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Clicking a label in first row of table view is not working on 3.1.3GA version
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When I press a label in first row of table view, it is returning [object TiUITableViewRow] instead of [object TiUILabel]. All other rows, it is returning correct label [object TiUILabel]. What could be a reason for this issue happening for only first row? This issue happens only with 3.1.3GA version when I compiled for iPhone/iPad. h4. Test case h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project for iOS7, with 3.1.3 2. Paste the testcase into app.js 3. Run in the simulator 4. Click on the first row. 5. Click on the second row. 6. Check console, you will see the difference, even if you created the two rows in the same way. h4. Extra info Log when 1YY label is clicked in TableView: First row output: [INFO] e.row =[object TiUITableViewRow], e.source = [object TiUILabel] Second or any other row is clicked: [INFO] e.row =[object TiUITableViewRow], e.source = [object TiUITableViewRow]""""",title+description
TIMOB-15537,12,"""Get rid of Clean Project option""","""""""The programmer should *never* have to run """"""""Clean"""""""". I see this solution being proposed for numerous issues with builds not updating properly. Running """"""""Clean"""""""" is not an acceptable solution. The build <USER>should be smart enough to rebuild everything that needs rebuilding.     I assert that when there is a <USER>in which a """"""""Clean"""""""" is required to correctly build, that is a bug in titanium.    Thoughts?""""""",New Feature,"Title: Get rid of Clean Project option
Description: """"The programmer should *never* have to run """"""""Clean"""""""". I see this solution being proposed for numerous issues with builds not updating properly. Running """"""""Clean"""""""" is not an acceptable solution. The build <USER>should be smart enough to rebuild everything that needs rebuilding. I assert that when there is a <USER>in which a """"""""Clean"""""""" is required to correctly build, that is a bug in titanium. Thoughts?""""",title+description
