TIMOB-15507,12,"""CLI: Selecting an old version of SDK leaves the CLI in an invalid state.""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Select an old sdk... """"""""ti sdk select 2.1.3.GA""""""""  (You should see an error like """"""""[ERROR] Specified Titanium SDK """"""""2.1.3.GA"""""""" is too old"""""""")  2. Try to switch back to a newer/valid sdk """"""""ti sdk select 3.0.0.GA""""""""    Expected result:  The sdk should switch back properly    Actual Result:  You always get the error message """"""""[ERROR] Specified Titanium SDK """"""""2.1.3.GA"""""""" is too old""""""""    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Selecting an old version of SDK leaves the CLI in an invalid state.
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Select an old sdk... """"""""ti sdk select 2.1.3.GA"""""""" (You should see an error like """"""""[ERROR] Specified Titanium SDK """"""""2.1.3.GA"""""""" is too old"""""""") 2. Try to switch back to a newer/valid sdk """"""""ti sdk select 3.0.0.GA"""""""" Expected result: The sdk should switch back properly Actual Result: You always get the error message """"""""[ERROR] Specified Titanium SDK """"""""2.1.3.GA"""""""" is too old"""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-15506,12,"""Android: ListView textfield inside headerView types backwards""","""""""Test code:     1. Run code, focus the textfield and type 'apple'. Notice how the cursor is stuck at one position.   2. Hit back space to delete all letters, retype 'apple'. Then move cursor manually to position 2, between 'p' and 'l'. Type 'hello'. Notice how 'hello' is being written backwards""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ListView textfield inside headerView types backwards
Description: """"Test code: 1. Run code, focus the textfield and type 'apple'. Notice how the cursor is stuck at one position. 2. Hit back space to delete all letters, retype 'apple'. Then move cursor manually to position 2, between 'p' and 'l'. Type 'hello'. Notice how 'hello' is being written backwards""""",title+description
TIMOB-15505,12,"""iOS: HttpClient onload event returns responseCode of 0""","""""""h3. PROBLEM    When using an httpClient connection and this is succesful the event return a response code of 0, when user tries to do a validation of the response code they get a false as they expect a 200 response.       h3. EVENT OUTPUT          h3. TEST CASE        h3. CONSOLE LOG        h3. SDK CODE    As doing a review we found that a 0 response is hard coded in the Titanium SDK on TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: HttpClient onload event returns responseCode of 0
Description: """"h3. PROBLEM When using an httpClient connection and this is succesful the event return a response code of 0, when user tries to do a validation of the response code they get a false as they expect a 200 response. h3. EVENT OUTPUT h3. TEST CASE h3. CONSOLE LOG h3. SDK CODE As doing a review we found that a 0 response is hard coded in the Titanium SDK on TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m """"",title+description
TIMOB-15504,12,"""Android: No Android SDKs were found under the specified SDK location""","""""""Since an recent update my Android dev environment has stopped working.     Even though I have all the pre-requisite SDK versions installed (and have had for a while) and the locations set in the Studio prefs, I'm getting the message :     """"""""[Android SDK Home] No Android SDKs were found under the specified SDK location""""""""    I've tried re-installing android and the SDKs again to no avail.      Others are having the issue too, but I can't seem to resolve this. Any ideas what's happened?      https://developer.<USER>com/question/158387/since-studio-320---its-not-finding-my-android-sdk    http://developer.<USER>com/question/158401/android-sdk""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: No Android SDKs were found under the specified SDK location
