TIMOB-15500,12,"""Android: Analyze the behavior of ti.android.bug2373.finishfalseroot""","""""""On Android, when """"""""ti.android.bug2737.finishfalseroot"""""""" is set to true, we don't restart the app when launching in eclipse like we usually do when it's false. We need to analyze the difference in behavior when the above property is set to true or false.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Analyze the behavior of ti.android.bug2373.finishfalseroot
Description: """"On Android, when """"""""ti.android.bug2737.finishfalseroot"""""""" is set to true, we don't restart the app when launching in eclipse like we usually do when it's false. We need to analyze the difference in behavior when the above property is set to true or false.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15499,12,"""Blackberry - Blackberry project does not package successfully""","""""""h5.Description    Packaging a BlackBerry project will build successfully    However when it looks for the keystore it fails.    +This bug will not occur straight away, the first few packages will work well.+  +It just randomly stops working+    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Open Studio  2. Create a BlackBerry project in Studio  3. Package the project to a BlackBerry device    h5.Actual Result  Throws an error in the console within studio. The app will build but the keystore has failed so it won't install to the device    h5.Expected Result  The project to be packaged and added to the device""""""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry - Blackberry project does not package successfully
Description: """"h5.Description Packaging a BlackBerry project will build successfully However when it looks for the keystore it fails. +This bug will not occur straight away, the first few packages will work well.+ +It just randomly stops working+ h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Open Studio 2. Create a BlackBerry project in Studio 3. Package the project to a BlackBerry device h5.Actual Result Throws an error in the console within studio. The app will build but the keystore has failed so it won't install to the device h5.Expected Result The project to be packaged and added to the device""""",title+description
TIMOB-15497,12,"""iOS: i18n: Error message """"Unable to configure network read stream""""""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When you are trying to stream an audio file using *createAudioPlayer*, if you don't have an active connetcion, or you lose your connection while streaming, the message *""""""""Unable to configure network read stream""""""""* will show up.    The problem is that it's an English only message, and it's not clear for users about what is happening.    Possible solution is to allow us changing the message text, or disabling it and checking manually the connection.    h4. Test Case  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: i18n: Error message """"Unable to configure network read stream""""
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When you are trying to stream an audio file using *createAudioPlayer*, if you don't have an active connetcion, or you lose your connection while streaming, the message *""""""""Unable to configure network read stream""""""""* will show up. The problem is that it's an English only message, and it's not clear for users about what is happening. Possible solution is to allow us changing the message text, or disabling it and checking manually the connection. h4. Test Case """"",title+description
TIMOB-15496,12,"""Android TabGroup's actionBar actionViews don't expand""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When adding a menuItem to the actionBar with an actionView and {code}showAsAction : Ti.Android.SHOW_AS_ACTION_COLLAPSE_ACTION_VIEW | Ti.Android.SHOW_AS_ACTION_ALWAYS{code} to a TabGroup, the item never expands to show the actionView. This is with a TabGroup, and nothing happens when i click the 'search' icon.    h4. Test Case    {code:javascript}var win = Ti.UI.createTabGroup({      backgroundColor: 'blue',      fullscreen: false  });  var tab = Ti.UI.createTab({title: """"""""test""""""""});  var tabWin = Ti.UI.createWindow({title: """"""""testWin""""""""});  tab.window = tabWin;  win.add(tab);    var search;  var searchAsChild = false;    if (Ti.Platform.name == 'android' && Ti.Platform.Android.API_LEVEL > 11) {      // Use action bar search view      search = Ti.UI.Android.createSearchView({          hintText: """"""""Table Search""""""""      });     win.addEventListener(""""""""open"""""""", function(e) {      win.getActivity().onCreateOptionsMenu = function(e) {          var menu = e.menu;          var menuItem = menu.add({              title: 'Table Search',              actionView : search,              icon: (Ti.Android.R.drawable.ic_menu_search ? Ti.Android.R.drawable.ic_menu_search : """"""""my_search.png""""""""),              showAsAction: Ti.Android.SHOW_AS_ACTION_IF_ROOM | Ti.Android.SHOW_AS_ACTION_COLLAPSE_ACTION_VIEW          });      };   });  }  else {      // Use search bar      search = Ti.UI.createSearchBar({          hintText: """"""""Table Search""""""""      });      searchAsChild = true;  }    var data = [];  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Apple'}));  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Banana'}));  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Orange'}));  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Raspberry'}));    var tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({      data:data,      search:search,      searchAsChild:searchAsChild  });    win.add(tableview);  win.open();{code}    h4. Extra info   However, when i try it with a Window instead of a TabGroup, it does work: (note: this is identical to previous case except for changing the tabgroup to a window)  {code:javascript}var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: 'blue',      fullscreen: false  });  //var tab = Ti.UI.createTab({title: """"""""test""""""""});  //var tabWin = Ti.UI.createWindow({title: """"""""testWin""""""""});  //tab.window = tabWin;  //win.add(tab);    var search;  var searchAsChild = false;    if (Ti.Platform.name == 'android' && Ti.Platform.Android.API_LEVEL > 11) {      // Use action bar search view      search = Ti.UI.Android.createSearchView({          hintText: """"""""Table Search""""""""      });     win.addEventListener(""""""""open"""""""", function(e) {      win.getActivity().onCreateOptionsMenu = function(e) {          var menu = e.menu;          var menuItem = menu.add({              title: 'Table Search',              actionView : search,              icon: (Ti.Android.R.drawable.ic_menu_search ? Ti.Android.R.drawable.ic_menu_search : """"""""my_search.png""""""""),              showAsAction: Ti.Android.SHOW_AS_ACTION_IF_ROOM | Ti.Android.SHOW_AS_ACTION_COLLAPSE_ACTION_VIEW          });      };   });  }  else {      // Use search bar      search = Ti.UI.createSearchBar({          hintText: """"""""Table Search""""""""      });      searchAsChild = true;  }    var data = [];  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Apple'}));  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Banana'}));  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Orange'}));  data.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Raspberry'}));    var tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({      data:data,      search:search,      searchAsChild:searchAsChild  });    win.add(tableview);  win.open();{code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android TabGroup's actionBar actionViews don't expand
