TIMOB-15467,12,"""CLI: Android - incomplete .project file causes project to not show as part of an Org in the tiapp.xml""","""""""Customer developed a project from the CLI and the .project file was missing these values:     <nature>com.<USER>titanium.mobile.nature</nature>  <nature>com.aptana.projects.webnature</nature>    Once we added them back we could enable services for the app in the proper org.  Without the values, the app shows it isn't part of any org and won't properly link to Crittercism and SOASTA.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android - incomplete .project file causes project to not show as part of an Org in the tiapp.xml
Description: """"Customer developed a project from the CLI and the .project file was missing these values: <nature>com.<USER>titanium.mobile.nature</nature> <nature>com.aptana.projects.webnature</nature> Once we added them back we could enable services for the app in the proper org. Without the values, the app shows it isn't part of any org and won't properly link to Crittercism and SOASTA.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15466,12,"""Apps crash after enabling LiveView""","""""""After on-boarding two separate enterprise customers (SMC Treviso and HD Supply GSC) to AppceleratorStudio and Platform, LiveView does not work.  On both occasions, we confirmed the build and ran on emulator.  After enabling LiveView, the build fails and will not run.  You can instantly fix the issue by disabling LiveView.  Here is the log file of the error:    [ERROR] :  TypeError: 'undefined' is not an object (evaluating 'Alloy.CFG')  [ERROR] :  File: app.js  [ERROR] :  Line: 16  [ERROR] :  SourceId: 292427296  [ERROR] :  Backtrace:  [ERROR] :   #0 () at :130  [ERROR] :  #1 initializeList() at :8  [ERROR] :  #2 Controller() at :89  [ERROR] :  #3 () at :214  [ERROR] :  #4 Controller() at :51  [ERROR] :  #5 () at :214  [ERROR] :  #6 anonymous() at :22  [ERROR] :  #7 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:628  [ERROR] :  #8 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:493  [ERROR] :  #9 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:460  [ERROR] :  #10 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:392  [ERROR] :  #11 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:663  [ERROR] :  [LiveView] The operation couldn’t be completed. Socket is not connected""""""",Bug,"Title: Apps crash after enabling LiveView
Description: """"After on-boarding two separate enterprise customers (SMC Treviso and HD Supply GSC) to AppceleratorStudio and Platform, LiveView does not work. On both occasions, we confirmed the build and ran on emulator. After enabling LiveView, the build fails and will not run. You can instantly fix the issue by disabling LiveView. Here is the log file of the error: [ERROR] : TypeError: 'undefined' is not an object (evaluating 'Alloy.CFG') [ERROR] : File: app.js [ERROR] : Line: 16 [ERROR] : SourceId: 292427296 [ERROR] : Backtrace: [ERROR] : #0 () at :130 [ERROR] : #1 initializeList() at :8 [ERROR] : #2 Controller() at :89 [ERROR] : #3 () at :214 [ERROR] : #4 Controller() at :51 [ERROR] : #5 () at :214 [ERROR] : #6 anonymous() at :22 [ERROR] : #7 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:628 [ERROR] : #8 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:493 [ERROR] : #9 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:460 [ERROR] : #10 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:392 [ERROR] : #11 () at file:///Users/vamsi.vidala/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/7.0/Applications/2BCED025-11A5-4C86-8731-1BDE0AE424BB/FRProto.app/app.js:663 [ERROR] : [LiveView] The operation couldn’t be completed. Socket is not connected""""",title+description
TIMOB-15465,12,"""Mobile Web: Ti/_/include.js is included in the build twice""","""""""The contents of Ti/_/include.js are bundled inside of index.html twice. This doesn't cause any runtime problems with the app, but it does bloat the code size. This may be the only one included twice, but it should be confirmed first.""""""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web: Ti/_/include.js is included in the build twice
Description: """"The contents of Ti/_/include.js are bundled inside of index.html twice. This doesn't cause any runtime problems with the app, but it does bloat the code size. This may be the only one included twice, but it should be confirmed first.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15461,12,"""CLI - CLI would install 3.2.0 instead of 3.1.2""","""""""h5.Description  I tried to downgrade CLI from version 3.2.0 to 3.1.2 and came across a problem. It would install 3.2.0 over and over again no matter what method I tried. I tried uninstalling 3.2.0 and getting fresh install of 3.1.2 using    I tried uninstalling 3.2.0 and cleaning the cache and getting a fresh install of 3.1.2 using      h5.Steps  1. Open Terminal  2. Uninstall CLI and reinstall the latest available version (3.1.2)    h5.Result  It would reinstall version 3.2.0    h5.Expected Result  It should install version 3.1.2    +*Additional Information*+  I eventually got it to work by uninstalling 3.2.0, opening Studio and installing CLI through Studio.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI - CLI would install 3.2.0 instead of 3.1.2
Description: """"h5.Description I tried to downgrade CLI from version 3.2.0 to 3.1.2 and came across a problem. It would install 3.2.0 over and over again no matter what method I tried. I tried uninstalling 3.2.0 and getting fresh install of 3.1.2 using I tried uninstalling 3.2.0 and cleaning the cache and getting a fresh install of 3.1.2 using h5.Steps 1. Open Terminal 2. Uninstall CLI and reinstall the latest available version (3.1.2) h5.Result It would reinstall version 3.2.0 h5.Expected Result It should install version 3.1.2 +*Additional Information*+ I eventually got it to work by uninstalling 3.2.0, opening Studio and installing CLI through Studio.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15460,12,"""Android:Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard not working in window close event callback""","""""""h2. Problem    Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard does not work when called in a window close event callback.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: """"""""#FFF"""""""", layout: 'vertical'});  var textField = Ti.UI.createTextField({width: Ti.UI.FILL});  var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: """"""""Close"""""""", width: Ti.UI.FILL});    button.addEventListener('click', function(e) {    // Works as expected    //Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard();    window.close();  });    window.addEventListener('close', function() {    // Doesn't work    Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard();  });    window.add(textField);  window.add(button);  window.open();  {code}    h2. Workaround  Call Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard before closing the window.    h2. Related  https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15336  The issue may be related to the same race issue described here.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android:Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard not working in window close event callback
Description: """"h2. Problem Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard does not work when called in a window close event callback. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: """"""""#FFF"""""""", layout: 'vertical'}); var textField = Ti.UI.createTextField({width: Ti.UI.FILL}); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: """"""""Close"""""""", width: Ti.UI.FILL}); button.addEventListener('click', function(e) { // Works as expected //Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard(); window.close(); }); window.addEventListener('close', function() { // Doesn't work Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard(); }); window.add(textField); window.add(button); window.open(); {code} h2. Workaround Call Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard before closing the window. h2. Related https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15336 The issue may be related to the same race issue described here.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15459,12,"""iOS: Impossible to add elements to ListView if scrollToItem has been called when there were no elements in it""","""""""h2. Problem description  If scrollToItem has been called when there are no elements in the ListView, it is then impossible to add elements to the view.    h2. Steps to reproduce  The following code shows the issue; after 2s an element is added, but it does not work. Removing the scrollToItem line fixes the issue.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Impossible to add elements to ListView if scrollToItem has been called when there were no elements in it
Description: """"h2. Problem description If scrollToItem has been called when there are no elements in the ListView, it is then impossible to add elements to the view. h2. Steps to reproduce The following code shows the issue; after 2s an element is added, but it does not work. Removing the scrollToItem line fixes the issue. """"",title+description
