TIMOB-15456,12,"""VMWare Fusion 5 and 6 errors on Mac 10.9 Mavericks""","""""""h5.Description  Installing VMWare Fusion 5 or 6 and using blackberry simulator works partially.  User can click on the screen and hit buttons but cannot use slide features such as sliding across home screen to see apps or scrolling down a page on browser.    Also to note is that the Simulator never fetches an IP address so cannot be linked to run applications on through Studio.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  1. Install VMWare Fusion 5 or 6  2. Download and install latest BlackBerry simulator  3. Install the simulator through VMWare Fusion  4. Run the simulation through VMWare Fusion  5. Try scrolling around and note that the IP address in the bottom left corner is never obtained.    h5.Actual Result  Simulators swipe function does not work.  Simulator IP address is never obtained    h5.Expected Result  Simulator functions like a phone, swipe enabled.  IP address to be obtained so it can be linked to Studio""""""",Bug,"Title: VMWare Fusion 5 and 6 errors on Mac 10.9 Mavericks
Description: """"h5.Description Installing VMWare Fusion 5 or 6 and using blackberry simulator works partially. User can click on the screen and hit buttons but cannot use slide features such as sliding across home screen to see apps or scrolling down a page on browser. Also to note is that the Simulator never fetches an IP address so cannot be linked to run applications on through Studio. h5.Steps To Reproduce 1. Install VMWare Fusion 5 or 6 2. Download and install latest BlackBerry simulator 3. Install the simulator through VMWare Fusion 4. Run the simulation through VMWare Fusion 5. Try scrolling around and note that the IP address in the bottom left corner is never obtained. h5.Actual Result Simulators swipe function does not work. Simulator IP address is never obtained h5.Expected Result Simulator functions like a phone, swipe enabled. IP address to be obtained so it can be linked to Studio""""",title+description
TIMOB-15455,12,"""Tizen: Hard hang on launch of emulator on Mavericks when HAXM is turned on""","""""""h4.New Bug  h5.Description  Mavericks is currently not supported by HAXM so running the Tizen emulator will result in a crash.  To get around this the user can disable HAXM on the Tizen emulator manager by deselecting CPU-VT and GPU.    +Note+  This will make the emulator very slow but it will still run. Until HAXM solves the incompatibility with Mavericks this is the only way of running Tizen emulators.    h4.Old Bug  h5.Description  Launching Tizen emulator results in a hang that requires hard restart on OSX 10.9 (Mavericks) with HAXM. This occurred with Tizen SDK 2.1 and SDK 2.2. With console app up, HAXM errors shown in the console (see attachment)    h5.To reproduce  1. Install Tizen  2. Configure as required for ability to launch emulator - see notes below  3. Open console app and monitor during next step  3. Launch Tizen emulator    h5.Actual result  OSX 10.9 Mavericks freezes with haxm errors in console    h5.Expected result  Tizen emulator launches and displays project    h5.Notes:  To run the emulator you must enter the following commands via terminal or script. You will need to renter the commands prior to running the emulator if you restart your mac:  sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmmax=1610612736  sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmall=393216  sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmmin=1  sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmmni=32  sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmseg=8  sudo sysctl -w kern.maxprocperuid=512  sudo sysctl -w kern.maxproc=2048""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen: Hard hang on launch of emulator on Mavericks when HAXM is turned on
Description: """"h4.New Bug h5.Description Mavericks is currently not supported by HAXM so running the Tizen emulator will result in a crash. To get around this the user can disable HAXM on the Tizen emulator manager by deselecting CPU-VT and GPU. +Note+ This will make the emulator very slow but it will still run. Until HAXM solves the incompatibility with Mavericks this is the only way of running Tizen emulators. h4.Old Bug h5.Description Launching Tizen emulator results in a hang that requires hard restart on OSX 10.9 (Mavericks) with HAXM. This occurred with Tizen SDK 2.1 and SDK 2.2. With console app up, HAXM errors shown in the console (see attachment) h5.To reproduce 1. Install Tizen 2. Configure as required for ability to launch emulator - see notes below 3. Open console app and monitor during next step 3. Launch Tizen emulator h5.Actual result OSX 10.9 Mavericks freezes with haxm errors in console h5.Expected result Tizen emulator launches and displays project h5.Notes: To run the emulator you must enter the following commands via terminal or script. You will need to renter the commands prior to running the emulator if you restart your mac: sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmmax=1610612736 sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmall=393216 sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmmin=1 sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmmni=32 sudo sysctl -w kern.sysv.shmseg=8 sudo sysctl -w kern.maxprocperuid=512 sudo sysctl -w kern.maxproc=2048""""",title+description
TIMOB-15451,12,"""iOS: ListView with custom Template in navigationWindow : listItems not displayed first time when calling appendSection()""","""""""After setting a ListView with custom template in a navigation window, the listItems are not correctly displayed first time when you use appendSection().     Titanium SDK version 3.2.0.v20131009134844 : KO    works with 3.1.4    See below for test case.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ListView with custom Template in navigationWindow : listItems not displayed first time when calling appendSection()
Description: """"After setting a ListView with custom template in a navigation window, the listItems are not correctly displayed first time when you use appendSection(). Titanium SDK version 3.2.0.v20131009134844 : KO works with 3.1.4 See below for test case.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15450,12,"""iOS7: Can't style more-tab same as other tabs""","""""""I try to style a tab group's navigation bar background- and tint colors in such a way that both the 4 showing tabs as well as the the automatic *More* tab holding any other tabs look exactly the same. This seems impossible.    Run the following code:        h1. More-Tab extendEdges  When you're on one of the first 4 tabs you'll see the green of {{Ti.UI.backgroundColor}} shine through the tab bar, like shown in screenshot A. But on the *More* tab, the tab bar is grey-ish like shown in screenshot B. It looks like this window has extendEdges for bottom enabled by default and setting {{extendEdges}} to {{NONE}} on the {{TabGroup}} doesn't change this.    h1. More-Tab barColor  The above is also true for the nav bar, which is clear red instead of translucent like on the other tabs (screenshots A and B).    h1. More-Tab edit-dialog barColor  When you press the *Edit* button on the *More* tab, you will see that the nav bar for the modal window that pops up is grey-ish (screenshot C), instead of the red I've set on the tab group. Again, I could not find a way to change this.    h1. More-Tab navTintColor  If you go to one of the tabs you find under the *More* tab, you'll see the back arrow is white (screenshot D) because I've set the {{navTintColor}} of all windows to green. Now when you return to the *More* tab by pressing that arrow, you'll notice the *Edit* button of the *More* tab now also changed to white (screenshot E and compare B)! You would think you can set {{navTintColor}} on the {{TabGroup}} as well, but this has no effect. On the other hand, when you set {{tintColor}} it does change the *Edit* button's color, but also the color of the active tab's icon, all icons in the *Edit* window that are currently not in the tab bar, as well as the *Done* button on that window (screenshot F). And since we cannot change the {{barColor}} of that *Edit* window, this leaves you with a lot of white-on-white.    h1. More-Tab title  The color of the nav bar titles nicely changes to white when you set {{UIStatusBarStyle}} to {{UIStatusBarStyleLightContent}}. However, only on the *More* tab the title will still be black and I cannot see how to change this (screenshot G).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Can't style more-tab same as other tabs
Description: """"I try to style a tab group's navigation bar background- and tint colors in such a way that both the 4 showing tabs as well as the the automatic *More* tab holding any other tabs look exactly the same. This seems impossible. Run the following code: h1. More-Tab extendEdges When you're on one of the first 4 tabs you'll see the green of {{Ti.UI.backgroundColor}} shine through the tab bar, like shown in screenshot A. But on the *More* tab, the tab bar is grey-ish like shown in screenshot B. It looks like this window has extendEdges for bottom enabled by default and setting {{extendEdges}} to {{NONE}} on the {{TabGroup}} doesn't change this. h1. More-Tab barColor The above is also true for the nav bar, which is clear red instead of translucent like on the other tabs (screenshots A and B). h1. More-Tab edit-dialog barColor When you press the *Edit* button on the *More* tab, you will see that the nav bar for the modal window that pops up is grey-ish (screenshot C), instead of the red I've set on the tab group. Again, I could not find a way to change this. h1. More-Tab navTintColor If you go to one of the tabs you find under the *More* tab, you'll see the back arrow is white (screenshot D) because I've set the {{navTintColor}} of all windows to green. Now when you return to the *More* tab by pressing that arrow, you'll notice the *Edit* button of the *More* tab now also changed to white (screenshot E and compare B)! You would think you can set {{navTintColor}} on the {{TabGroup}} as well, but this has no effect. On the other hand, when you set {{tintColor}} it does change the *Edit* button's color, but also the color of the active tab's icon, all icons in the *Edit* window that are currently not in the tab bar, as well as the *Done* button on that window (screenshot F). And since we cannot change the {{barColor}} of that *Edit* window, this leaves you with a lot of white-on-white. h1. More-Tab title The color of the nav bar titles nicely changes to white when you set {{UIStatusBarStyle}} to {{UIStatusBarStyleLightContent}}. However, only on the *More* tab the title will still be black and I cannot see how to change this (screenshot G).""""",title+description
TIMOB-15449,12,"""iOS: ScrollViews lag while scrolling""","""""""Since the updated to 3.1.3, xcode 5 and ios 7, the project attached is scrolling very very laggy, it was very smoth on 3.1.0 with xcode 5 and ios 6.    I'm not sure if this is because the components inside the scrollView, or some memory leak.    May be related to [https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15095]    Not tested on android.    Test steps:  1 - Just import to titanium and build to ipad simulator, or ipad device(both show the same problem).    If any extra info needed, just let me know.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollViews lag while scrolling
Description: """"Since the updated to 3.1.3, xcode 5 and ios 7, the project attached is scrolling very very laggy, it was very smoth on 3.1.0 with xcode 5 and ios 6. I'm not sure if this is because the components inside the scrollView, or some memory leak. May be related to [https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-15095] Not tested on android. Test steps: 1 - Just import to titanium and build to ipad simulator, or ipad device(both show the same problem). If any extra info needed, just let me know.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15445,12,"""iOS7: Scrollview contentHeight not adjusting after Keyboard is dismissed""","""""""h2. Description  I have a scrollview which doesn't take the full height of the screen, so it doesn't move at all when I try to scroll it. It has a text field inside, though, and when I put focus in that text field, then blur it after, I find that the scrollview is now scrolling even though it shouldn't be anymore now that the keyboard is gone.    Steps:  (1) Observe you can't scroll the screen  (2) Click into the text field  (3) Click out of the text field (or lose focus some other way)  (4) Observe that the screen is now still scrollable even though it shouldn't be.    Note : If keyboardToolbar property is removed then its not reproducible.    h2. Test Code  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Scrollview contentHeight not adjusting after Keyboard is dismissed
Description: """"h2. Description I have a scrollview which doesn't take the full height of the screen, so it doesn't move at all when I try to scroll it. It has a text field inside, though, and when I put focus in that text field, then blur it after, I find that the scrollview is now scrolling even though it shouldn't be anymore now that the keyboard is gone. Steps: (1) Observe you can't scroll the screen (2) Click into the text field (3) Click out of the text field (or lose focus some other way) (4) Observe that the screen is now still scrollable even though it shouldn't be. Note : If keyboardToolbar property is removed then its not reproducible. h2. Test Code """"",title+description
TIMOB-15444,12,"""MobileWeb: Can't Type in TextFields inside ScrollableView""","""""""h4. Problem Description  If you have a TextField inside a scrollable view, when you try type in it on mobile web it just doesn't get focus, instead the scrollable view tries to scroll.    h4. Steps to reproduce   1. Create a new mobile web project  2. Paste the code sample to app.js  3. Run in browser     h4. Test case       h4. Extra comments   The bug is in the kitchen sink demo also if you add a TextField inside the ScrollableView demo, the above code should let you replicate the issue.    """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Can't Type in TextFields inside ScrollableView
Description: """"h4. Problem Description If you have a TextField inside a scrollable view, when you try type in it on mobile web it just doesn't get focus, instead the scrollable view tries to scroll. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile web project 2. Paste the code sample to app.js 3. Run in browser h4. Test case h4. Extra comments The bug is in the kitchen sink demo also if you add a TextField inside the ScrollableView demo, the above code should let you replicate the issue. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15441,12,"""iOS: Fix Label sizing issues""","""""""The Label proxy has some sizing issues and needs to be revisited.  1. ClipsToBounds is false so label text might overflow if content rect is larger than supplied bounds  2. Attributed Strings are displaying weird behavior on iOS7. Need to investigate and fix.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Fix Label sizing issues
Description: """"The Label proxy has some sizing issues and needs to be revisited. 1. ClipsToBounds is false so label text might overflow if content rect is larger than supplied bounds 2. Attributed Strings are displaying weird behavior on iOS7. Need to investigate and fix.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15440,12,"""Android: Android SDK not detected""","""""""h5.Description  Upon updating my set up to 3.2.0 I noticed that the android SDK is not picked up.  In more detail, it does pick up the SDK, files and folders, but it doesn't pick up the platforms.    h5.Steps To Reproduce  +Studio:+  Nightly streams – version 3.2.0  http://preview.<USER>com/<USER>studio/standalone/update/nightly/  +SDK:+  Master branch - 3.2.0.v20131008134043 or later  Use the terminal command via CLI:  """"""""ti sdk install -b master –d""""""""  There is a bug. If you encounter it, try setting cli.prompt in config to true and then try to install  ti config cli.prompt """"""""true""""""""  +CLI:+  Install from git  """"""""sudo npm install -g git://github.com/<USER>titanium.git""""""""    Make sure you have android SDK and NDK installed with atleast 1 platform installed.  Open terminal and run """"""""ti info -t android""""""""    h5.Result  Throws and error:  TypeError: Object #<Object> has no method 'detectDevices'    h5.Expected Result  Should find the correct android locations and platforms    +Extra Information+  Error thrown is in the function in info.js on line 232    /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/lib/commands/info.js""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Android SDK not detected
Description: """"h5.Description Upon updating my set up to 3.2.0 I noticed that the android SDK is not picked up. In more detail, it does pick up the SDK, files and folders, but it doesn't pick up the platforms. h5.Steps To Reproduce +Studio:+ Nightly streams – version 3.2.0 http://preview.<USER>com/<USER>studio/standalone/update/nightly/ +SDK:+ Master branch - 3.2.0.v20131008134043 or later Use the terminal command via CLI: """"""""ti sdk install -b master –d"""""""" There is a bug. If you encounter it, try setting cli.prompt in config to true and then try to install ti config cli.prompt """"""""true"""""""" +CLI:+ Install from git """"""""sudo npm install -g git://github.com/<USER>titanium.git"""""""" Make sure you have android SDK and NDK installed with atleast 1 platform installed. Open terminal and run """"""""ti info -t android"""""""" h5.Result Throws and error: TypeError: Object #<Object> has no method 'detectDevices' h5.Expected Result Should find the correct android locations and platforms +Extra Information+ Error thrown is in the function in info.js on line 232 /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/lib/commands/info.js""""",title+description
TIMOB-15439,12,"""Android: App crashes with just a few ImageViews""","""""""h2. Description of the problem  When there are few ImageViews in the app, if the image is big, the Emulator crashes with an 'out-of-memory' error. Images in the test is 280KB and is added 5 times to the app.    h2. Steps to reproduce  Use the attached image, and the following code:        h2. Note  Running this on Nexus 4 with Android 4.3.3 works fine; same using SDK 3.1.2. Before the crash, the heap size increases up to ~48MB and then the app exits.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: App crashes with just a few ImageViews
