TIMOB-15421,12,"""iOS7: Installing ad-hoc app with mismatched bundle identifier on iOS7 device leads to a residual """"installing"""" icon""","""""""h2. Description of the problem  When an app is distributed as ad-hoc, and insalled through a web server (e.g. not iTunes), the installing icon never disappear after the app is correctly installed. See the screenshot.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Create any app and build ad-hoc  2. Need to publish the app and download it on the device (see notes below)  3. The installation runs, but in the end the """"""""Installing..."""""""" icon is not removed    h2. Notes  The screenshot shows also that it is impossible to remove the """"""""installing"""""""" icon once it is there. Long press on the app will allow to delete the """"""""normal"""""""" icon, but not the residual one.    To publish the app, I used the following template files, replacing the required fields; the ipa is cammed myapp.ipa and published online. Opening the html file on the device allows you to install the app.    myapp.html      myapp.plist  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Installing ad-hoc app with mismatched bundle identifier on iOS7 device leads to a residual """"installing"""" icon
Description: """"h2. Description of the problem When an app is distributed as ad-hoc, and insalled through a web server (e.g. not iTunes), the installing icon never disappear after the app is correctly installed. See the screenshot. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Create any app and build ad-hoc 2. Need to publish the app and download it on the device (see notes below) 3. The installation runs, but in the end the """"""""Installing..."""""""" icon is not removed h2. Notes The screenshot shows also that it is impossible to remove the """"""""installing"""""""" icon once it is there. Long press on the app will allow to delete the """"""""normal"""""""" icon, but not the residual one. To publish the app, I used the following template files, replacing the required fields; the ipa is cammed myapp.ipa and published online. Opening the html file on the device allows you to install the app. myapp.html myapp.plist """"",title+description
TIMOB-15420,12,"""iOS: TableView delete buttons rendered behind tableview index""","""""""h5. Delete button positioning problem for iOS tableview in edit mode.      The delete button (either by swiping, or after pressing the delete button when the tableview.editing = true) is rendered behind the tableview index.    Possibly related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-666    *My testing environment follows:*      OS: MAC OX X 10.8.5  iOS SDK: 7.0,Xcode 5  iOS   Simulator: 6.0  Ti SDK: 3.1.2 GA, 3.1.3 GA and 3.1.4   Ti CLI: 3.2.0        h5. Step to reproduce    Please follow my steps for reproducing this issue.    1. Create new apps for Titanium Classic  2. Replace test code to app.js file  3. Now run in iOS simulator for testing  4. Click on Toggle Edit mode button  5. Then click on left button for appeared delete  6. Please check delete button in right side. Its not right positions and its look line behind on index    Thanks     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView delete buttons rendered behind tableview index
Description: """"h5. Delete button positioning problem for iOS tableview in edit mode. The delete button (either by swiping, or after pressing the delete button when the tableview.editing = true) is rendered behind the tableview index. Possibly related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-666 *My testing environment follows:* OS: MAC OX X 10.8.5 iOS SDK: 7.0,Xcode 5 iOS Simulator: 6.0 Ti SDK: 3.1.2 GA, 3.1.3 GA and 3.1.4 Ti CLI: 3.2.0 h5. Step to reproduce Please follow my steps for reproducing this issue. 1. Create new apps for Titanium Classic 2. Replace test code to app.js file 3. Now run in iOS simulator for testing 4. Click on Toggle Edit mode button 5. Then click on left button for appeared delete 6. Please check delete button in right side. Its not right positions and its look line behind on index Thanks """"",title+description
