TIMOB-15418,12,"""iOS7: AccessibilityLabel on button does not show when set as a leftNavButton / rightNavButton""","""""""h2. Description  I am using accessibilityLabel with a button that I then put as a {{leftNavButton}} or {{rightNavButton}} on a window. The problem is that I cannot get the {{accessibilityLabel}} to show (using VoiceOver on the device or the accessibility inspector in the simulator). If I do not set the button as the {{leftNavButton}} or {{rightNavButton}} it works.    h2. Test Code  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: AccessibilityLabel on button does not show when set as a leftNavButton / rightNavButton
Description: """"h2. Description I am using accessibilityLabel with a button that I then put as a {{leftNavButton}} or {{rightNavButton}} on a window. The problem is that I cannot get the {{accessibilityLabel}} to show (using VoiceOver on the device or the accessibility inspector in the simulator). If I do not set the button as the {{leftNavButton}} or {{rightNavButton}} it works. h2. Test Code """"",title+description
TIMOB-15417,12,"""Feature request to add x, y coordinates to item clickevent in list view...""","""""""I would like to be passed the x, y coordinates into the itemclick event (in the same way that the click event passes in x,y coordinates) for a ListView. I want to be able to simulate a custom control by clicking on an item in the ListView and bringing up a transparent window with my control on top of the item that I clicked on. However, I don't know where to place the control if I don't have the x, y coordinates. This is especially difficult if the window scrolls.    When I first wrote the bug, I had tested this on iOS and by looking at the document I thought that 'accessoryClicked' was the only field that was not common to both Android and iOS. In the debugger I found out that bindId is not passed in the itemclick event parameters on Android but x and y coordinates are passed in the event. Can I get both bindId and x,y coordinates passed into the event on both platforms? Also, can you update the documentation so that it at least correctly states the parameters being passed in?""""""",New Feature,"Title: Feature request to add x, y coordinates to item clickevent in list view...
Description: """"I would like to be passed the x, y coordinates into the itemclick event (in the same way that the click event passes in x,y coordinates) for a ListView. I want to be able to simulate a custom control by clicking on an item in the ListView and bringing up a transparent window with my control on top of the item that I clicked on. However, I don't know where to place the control if I don't have the x, y coordinates. This is especially difficult if the window scrolls. When I first wrote the bug, I had tested this on iOS and by looking at the document I thought that 'accessoryClicked' was the only field that was not common to both Android and iOS. In the debugger I found out that bindId is not passed in the itemclick event parameters on Android but x and y coordinates are passed in the event. Can I get both bindId and x,y coordinates passed into the event on both platforms? Also, can you update the documentation so that it at least correctly states the parameters being passed in?""""",title+description
TIMOB-15416,12,"""Unable to create menu item """"com.appcelerator.titanium.mobile.command.install.blackberry""""""","""""""I'm using some older code to recreate an iphone app. During the building <USER>Studio complains and quits.    it tells me:  [ERROR] :  ** BUILD FAILED **  [ERROR] :  The following build commands failed:  [ERROR] :   CodeSign build/Release-iphoneos/MenukaartInDeBuurt.app  [ERROR] :  (1 failure)    The log tells me:  ENTRY org.eclipse.ui 4 4 2013-08-29 14:59:49.844  !MESSAGE Unable to create menu item """"""""com.<USER>titanium.mobile.command.install.blackberry"""""""", command """"""""com.<USER>titanium.mobile.command.install.blackberry"""""""" not defined      What is this blackberry stuff, I didn't put it there, as far as I know.    thanks!""""""",Bug,"Title: Unable to create menu item """"com.appcelerator.titanium.mobile.command.install.blackberry""""
Description: """"I'm using some older code to recreate an iphone app. During the building <USER>Studio complains and quits. it tells me: [ERROR] : ** BUILD FAILED ** [ERROR] : The following build commands failed: [ERROR] : CodeSign build/Release-iphoneos/MenukaartInDeBuurt.app [ERROR] : (1 failure) The log tells me: ENTRY org.eclipse.ui 4 4 2013-08-29 14:59:49.844 !MESSAGE Unable to create menu item """"""""com.<USER>titanium.mobile.command.install.blackberry"""""""", command """"""""com.<USER>titanium.mobile.command.install.blackberry"""""""" not defined What is this blackberry stuff, I didn't put it there, as far as I know. thanks!""""",title+description
TIMOB-15414,12,"""iOS7: Allow users to set the Title Color of the Windows""","""""""We should allow users to set the Window titleColor without having to create a custom Label and setting it as the titleControl since you can do this natively (at least on Interface Builder).    Ideally, beside the navTintColor and the tintColor window parameters we should have a parameter called titleColor where the user can define the color for the title text on the NavBar.    Also we should map titleShadowColor, titleShadowOffset and titleFont for setting a title shadow color, offset and font as those are all available natively on IB.    Those are all supported natively on the Interface Builder and should be mapped to Ti.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS7: Allow users to set the Title Color of the Windows
Description: """"We should allow users to set the Window titleColor without having to create a custom Label and setting it as the titleControl since you can do this natively (at least on Interface Builder). Ideally, beside the navTintColor and the tintColor window parameters we should have a parameter called titleColor where the user can define the color for the title text on the NavBar. Also we should map titleShadowColor, titleShadowOffset and titleFont for setting a title shadow color, offset and font as those are all available natively on IB. Those are all supported natively on the Interface Builder and should be mapped to Ti. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15413,12,"""iOS: Logging date to console shifts time by several hours""","""""""    *OUTPUT:*  2013-10-01 01:00:00 +0000 // WRONG  3 // RIGHT    The right date is: 2013-10-01 03:00:00 +0000, you can test it in browser's console or http://www.ruddwire.com/handy-code/date-to-millisecond-calculators    // I have no idea how it is possible ,but now it shows two hours instead three.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Logging date to console shifts time by several hours
Description: """" *OUTPUT:* 2013-10-01 01:00:00 +0000 // WRONG 3 // RIGHT The right date is: 2013-10-01 03:00:00 +0000, you can test it in browser's console or http://www.ruddwire.com/handy-code/date-to-millisecond-calculators // I have no idea how it is possible ,but now it shows two hours instead three.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15412,12,"""Focus events stops working when you create and open a new window before opening of tabgroup""","""""""h4. Problem Description  I have test this issue with provided test code. I got this bug. When I clicked on tab its not firing focus event. But when I removed playerWindow.open() its working well. It’s working well for 3.1.2 GA and 3.1.1 GA.     h4. Test case      h4. Steps to reproduce*  1. Create default tabbed application in Titanium Classic  2. Open ApplicationTabGroup.js file and replace with my test code  3. Run this apps  4. Click on settings tab, focus event not firing   5. Now change Ti SDK 3.1.3 GA to 3.1.2 GA   6. Continue step 3 to 4  7. Remove playerWindow.open(); script form test code and follow step 6  """"""",Bug,"Title: Focus events stops working when you create and open a new window before opening of tabgroup
Description: """"h4. Problem Description I have test this issue with provided test code. I got this bug. When I clicked on tab its not firing focus event. But when I removed playerWindow.open() its working well. It’s working well for 3.1.2 GA and 3.1.1 GA. h4. Test case h4. Steps to reproduce* 1. Create default tabbed application in Titanium Classic 2. Open ApplicationTabGroup.js file and replace with my test code 3. Run this apps 4. Click on settings tab, focus event not firing 5. Now change Ti SDK 3.1.3 GA to 3.1.2 GA 6. Continue step 3 to 4 7. Remove playerWindow.open(); script form test code and follow step 6 """"",title+description
TIMOB-15411,12,"""CLI: 3.2.0 version doesn't take the arguments in account if the sdk in config is different from the one in tiapp.xml""","""""""If I have in config (titanium config) the app.sdk set to other version than the one present in tiapp.xml of the current project, the forked command doesn't take in account the arguments -  like target, or sdk, simulator version, etc    How to reproduce ([~<USER> *don't close* the damn ticket!)    1. Set the sdk in tiapp.xml to 3.2.0.v20130927153242  2. Set the config to 3.1.2.GA    3. Run       The result:      and the emulator starts instead of deploying to device.    Same stuff happens for iOS too.  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: 3.2.0 version doesn't take the arguments in account if the sdk in config is different from the one in tiapp.xml
Description: """"If I have in config (titanium config) the app.sdk set to other version than the one present in tiapp.xml of the current project, the forked command doesn't take in account the arguments - like target, or sdk, simulator version, etc How to reproduce ([~<USER> *don't close* the damn ticket!) 1. Set the sdk in tiapp.xml to 3.2.0.v20130927153242 2. Set the config to 3.1.2.GA 3. Run The result: and the emulator starts instead of deploying to device. Same stuff happens for iOS too. """"",title+description
