TIMOB-15409,12,"""New Relic: IOError: [Errno 13] Permission denied""","""""""Created an empty project with New Relic Module 1.0  I followed this tutorial: http://developer.<USER>com/blog/2013/08/you-can-now-easily-add-new-relic-to-your-titanium-studio-apps.html    When compiling project got the following error:   """"""",Bug,"Title: New Relic: IOError: [Errno 13] Permission denied
Description: """"Created an empty project with New Relic Module 1.0 I followed this tutorial: http://developer.<USER>com/blog/2013/08/you-can-now-easily-add-new-relic-to-your-titanium-studio-apps.html When compiling project got the following error: """"",title+description
TIMOB-15408,12,"""Android: TableView/ListView behaves incorrectly when ScrollableView inside TableView/ListView""","""""""After fixing TIMOB-13610, there are a few issues exposed on the Android platform.  1. Run the test case for tableview without . Scroll the first row to the green view. Scroll the tableview down to the bottom and then up to the top. Scroll the first row to other color again. The app crashes with the error """"""""E/AndroidRuntime( 4744): java.lang.IllegalStateException: The specified child already has a parent. You must call removeView() on the child's parent first.""""""""  2. Run the test case for tableview with/without . Scroll the first row to the green view and then scroll the tableview up and down several times. The first row does not stay at the green view. Probably because the item views in the TableView get recycled when they are off screen.  -3.- Run the test case for listview. Scroll the first row to page 2. Expected behavior: page 2 is a yellow view. Actual behavior: page 2 is a white view. (TIMOB-13868)  4. Run the test case for listview. Scroll the first row to the green view and then scroll the listview up and down several times. The first row does not stay at the green view and the other rows do not stay at the blue views. Probably because the item views in the ListView get recycled when they are off screen.     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView/ListView behaves incorrectly when ScrollableView inside TableView/ListView
Description: """"After fixing TIMOB-13610, there are a few issues exposed on the Android platform. 1. Run the test case for tableview without . Scroll the first row to the green view. Scroll the tableview down to the bottom and then up to the top. Scroll the first row to other color again. The app crashes with the error """"""""E/AndroidRuntime( 4744): java.lang.IllegalStateException: The specified child already has a parent. You must call removeView() on the child's parent first."""""""" 2. Run the test case for tableview with/without . Scroll the first row to the green view and then scroll the tableview up and down several times. The first row does not stay at the green view. Probably because the item views in the TableView get recycled when they are off screen. -3.- Run the test case for listview. Scroll the first row to page 2. Expected behavior: page 2 is a yellow view. Actual behavior: page 2 is a white view. (TIMOB-13868) 4. Run the test case for listview. Scroll the first row to the green view and then scroll the listview up and down several times. The first row does not stay at the green view and the other rows do not stay at the blue views. Probably because the item views in the ListView get recycled when they are off screen. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15407,12,"""Android: Performance: String manipulation experiment""","""""""In production builds, we're still calling """"""""Log.d(TAG, a + b) """""""" in many places (300+), generating unnecessary strings. We need to conduct an experiment to see how much memory and performance boost we'll get by removing these strings.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Performance: String manipulation experiment
Description: """"In production builds, we're still calling """"""""Log.d(TAG, a + b) """""""" in many places (300+), generating unnecessary strings. We need to conduct an experiment to see how much memory and performance boost we'll get by removing these strings.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15406,12,"""package the version which includes TIMODOPEN-270 of the ti.cloud module.""","""""""Package the version which includes TIMODOPEN-270 of the ti.cloud module.  Probably 2.3.9 version.""""""",New Feature,"Title: package the version which includes TIMODOPEN-270 of the ti.cloud module.
Description: """"Package the version which includes TIMODOPEN-270 of the ti.cloud module. Probably 2.3.9 version.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15405,12,"""3.2.0 CLI doesn't add all symbols when compiling ad-hoc""","""""""There is a an error in the *iphone/cli/commands/_build.js* file that prevent all the symbols to set to *define.h* in production.    The function *addSymbol* resets the symbols matrix to an empty array each time it is called.        Changing this to         fixes the issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: 3.2.0 CLI doesn't add all symbols when compiling ad-hoc
Description: """"There is a an error in the *iphone/cli/commands/_build.js* file that prevent all the symbols to set to *define.h* in production. The function *addSymbol* resets the symbols matrix to an empty array each time it is called. Changing this to fixes the issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15403,12,"""iOS: Not possible to build adhoc IPA with CLI 3.2.0""","""""""I cannot build an adhoc file with the new CLI. Although there occur no errors no IPA file is created. If I don't add the --build-only flag the simulator opens.      In Studio the ad hoc provisioning profile cannot be selected it says that it is a development instead of adhoc profile. I cannot select the profile when I'm in the Distribute adhoc screen.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Not possible to build adhoc IPA with CLI 3.2.0
Description: """"I cannot build an adhoc file with the new CLI. Although there occur no errors no IPA file is created. If I don't add the --build-only flag the simulator opens. In Studio the ad hoc provisioning profile cannot be selected it says that it is a development instead of adhoc profile. I cannot select the profile when I'm in the Distribute adhoc screen.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15402,12,"""iOS: Unable to add NavigationWindow to Popover""","""""""With the next release NavigationGroup is removed and NavigationWindow will take over.    But the new NavigationWindow can not be added to a Popover on the iPad, this will break hundreds of applications now running with NavigationGroup's in popovers.    Steps to Reproduce  1 Create a new Alloy project   2 Paste the attached files in the newly created project  3 Run the project    Actual Result  The log states:  [INFO] Can not add a window as a child of a view. Returning    Expected Result  The NavigationWindow should be apearing inside the Popover""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Unable to add NavigationWindow to Popover
Description: """"With the next release NavigationGroup is removed and NavigationWindow will take over. But the new NavigationWindow can not be added to a Popover on the iPad, this will break hundreds of applications now running with NavigationGroup's in popovers. Steps to Reproduce 1 Create a new Alloy project 2 Paste the attached files in the newly created project 3 Run the project Actual Result The log states: [INFO] Can not add a window as a child of a view. Returning Expected Result The NavigationWindow should be apearing inside the Popover""""",title+description
TIMOB-15401,12,"""iOS7: Text typed beyond the end of a textArea are not visible""","""""""h2. Description  In textarea when we type character after the end of the textarea its not visible and hides under the keyboard. Please see the attached screenshot.    h4. Steps to reproduce :    a)Type some characters - Press return.  b)Repeat the above step till the end of the text area and beyond.  c)When a new line is entered, the text area does not scroll enough to be visible.    Note : The issue is in iOS7 only and it work fine on iOS6.    h2. Test Case  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Text typed beyond the end of a textArea are not visible
Description: """"h2. Description In textarea when we type character after the end of the textarea its not visible and hides under the keyboard. Please see the attached screenshot. h4. Steps to reproduce : a)Type some characters - Press return. b)Repeat the above step till the end of the text area and beyond. c)When a new line is entered, the text area does not scroll enough to be visible. Note : The issue is in iOS7 only and it work fine on iOS6. h2. Test Case """"",title+description
