TIMOB-15393,12,"""iOS: Feature Request to Support Asset Catalogs""","""""""h6.Feature Request  Customers would like to use static images which are displayed in app. They are mainly looking for displaying different images for <=iOS6 and iOS7.     - TO SUPPORT BOTH IOS 6 AND IOS 7:  {quote}  Two asset catalogs will be needed for apps that need to support both versions. The layout in iOS 6 and iOS 7 will be different since there are changes in metrics and in styles of UIKit controls and views. Bars, bar controls, content views and temporary views have a different appearance in different iOS versions so two asset catalogs are needed. Custom assets, such as custom buttons, background images or other controls, will be stored in these catalogs and loaded conditionally in runtime.  {quote}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Feature Request to Support Asset Catalogs
Description: """"h6.Feature Request Customers would like to use static images which are displayed in app. They are mainly looking for displaying different images for <=iOS6 and iOS7. - TO SUPPORT BOTH IOS 6 AND IOS 7: {quote} Two asset catalogs will be needed for apps that need to support both versions. The layout in iOS 6 and iOS 7 will be different since there are changes in metrics and in styles of UIKit controls and views. Bars, bar controls, content views and temporary views have a different appearance in different iOS versions so two asset catalogs are needed. Custom assets, such as custom buttons, background images or other controls, will be stored in these catalogs and loaded conditionally in runtime. {quote}""""",title+description
TIMOB-15392,12,"""Android: Docking and Undocking device causes app to restart""","""""""This may be a device specific issue with the device: GETAC z710. We have not been able to test the issue as we do not have the device.    The device comes with a dock and the customer has found that undocking the device causes the application to restart/crash. Docking the device causes the app to background and return to an undesired screen. This also occurs with the Kitchen Sink app.    Attached are the resulting log files when the restart/crash occurs when docking and undocking the device.    Please also see their attached tiapp.xml file.    Any suggestions on things they could try? Is this something that is very device specific that we have no control over?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Docking and Undocking device causes app to restart
Description: """"This may be a device specific issue with the device: GETAC z710. We have not been able to test the issue as we do not have the device. The device comes with a dock and the customer has found that undocking the device causes the application to restart/crash. Docking the device causes the app to background and return to an undesired screen. This also occurs with the Kitchen Sink app. Attached are the resulting log files when the restart/crash occurs when docking and undocking the device. Please also see their attached tiapp.xml file. Any suggestions on things they could try? Is this something that is very device specific that we have no control over?""""",title+description
TIMOB-15391,12,"""iOS: Ti.Contacts.requestAuthorization always returns e.success=true in the callback, even if the users doesn't allow""","""""""h2. Description of the problem  Running the sample code in the documentation, when the user tries to add a contact and does not allow the app to access the Contacts, the app crashes. This is because the callback of Ti.Contacts.requestAuthorization always has e.success set to true.    h2. Steps to reproduce  Using the code below, just click on the label and click on """"""""Don't Allow"""""""". The app crashes.        h2. Note  You might add a check for Ti.Contacts.contactsAuthorization == Ti.Contacts.AUTHORIZATION_AUTHORIZED in the callback to avoid the issue. From the docs, is not fully clear if the callback should return e.success=true only if the user allows. The sample is the same as above.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Contacts.requestAuthorization always returns e.success=true in the callback, even if the users doesn't allow
Description: """"h2. Description of the problem Running the sample code in the documentation, when the user tries to add a contact and does not allow the app to access the Contacts, the app crashes. This is because the callback of Ti.Contacts.requestAuthorization always has e.success set to true. h2. Steps to reproduce Using the code below, just click on the label and click on """"""""Don't Allow"""""""". The app crashes. h2. Note You might add a check for Ti.Contacts.contactsAuthorization == Ti.Contacts.AUTHORIZATION_AUTHORIZED in the callback to avoid the issue. From the docs, is not fully clear if the callback should return e.success=true only if the user allows. The sample is the same as above.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15390,12,"""CLI: Validate provided app icons are correct for intended deployment target""","""""""The CLI needs to validate app icons by making sure that the correct icons are provided for the selected deployment targets. For example if the iPad icon(s) are missing then the build should warn if iPad is specified as a deployment target.  For iOS, the icon-to-deployment mapping rules are specified here:   https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/iPhone/Conceptual/iPhoneOSProgrammingGuide/Introduction/Introduction.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40007072""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Validate provided app icons are correct for intended deployment target
Description: """"The CLI needs to validate app icons by making sure that the correct icons are provided for the selected deployment targets. For example if the iPad icon(s) are missing then the build should warn if iPad is specified as a deployment target. For iOS, the icon-to-deployment mapping rules are specified here: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/iPhone/Conceptual/iPhoneOSProgrammingGuide/Introduction/Introduction.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40007072""""",title+description
TIMOB-15388,12,"""Add functionality to analyze Ti.Analytics featureEvent() and navEvent()""","""""""The dashboard need here is to be able to display a list of all available analytics events that an app can send.    This list will be displayed to users to select which events they want to see in an event funnel (APPTS-784).    During the API analysis, the two methods indicated (featureEvent() and navEvent()) should have the event name or from/to combination associated with the api call.    The list of event names and the from/to combinations should be compiled""""""",Story,"Title: Add functionality to analyze Ti.Analytics featureEvent() and navEvent()
Description: """"The dashboard need here is to be able to display a list of all available analytics events that an app can send. This list will be displayed to users to select which events they want to see in an event funnel (APPTS-784). During the API analysis, the two methods indicated (featureEvent() and navEvent()) should have the event name or from/to combination associated with the api call. The list of event names and the from/to combinations should be compiled""""",title+description
TIMOB-15386,12,"""Investigate side effects of setting navbar-hidden=true in tiapp.xml""","""""""There is a suggestion we set navbar-hidden=true by default in tiapp.xml. We need to see what side effects this has on the various platforms.""""""",Story,"Title: Investigate side effects of setting navbar-hidden=true in tiapp.xml
Description: """"There is a suggestion we set navbar-hidden=true by default in tiapp.xml. We need to see what side effects this has on the various platforms.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15385,12,"""HTTPClient Not Validating SSL Certificate on Android""","""""""Setting the validatesSecureCertificate property to true in the HTTPClient module does not work on the Android platform. Requests to invalid SSL sites are allowed to go through without exception. This feature does work as designed for iOS.    Example:    """"""",Bug,"Title: HTTPClient Not Validating SSL Certificate on Android
Description: """"Setting the validatesSecureCertificate property to true in the HTTPClient module does not work on the Android platform. Requests to invalid SSL sites are allowed to go through without exception. This feature does work as designed for iOS. Example: """"",title+description
TIMOB-15384,12,"""LiveView: Alloy RSS Reader sample: error saying 'null' is not an object at app.js""","""""""1. From Samples view in <USER>Studio, import Alloy > RSS Reader;  2. Enable LiveView and run the project on iPhone simulator;  3. Open app/views/master.xml;  4. Make a modification and save.    Expected result: the app reloads correctly in iPhone simulator.    Actual result: an error screen appears.    Clicking to dismiss the error does return the app to its working state.  """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Alloy RSS Reader sample: error saying 'null' is not an object at app.js
Description: """"1. From Samples view in <USER>Studio, import Alloy > RSS Reader; 2. Enable LiveView and run the project on iPhone simulator; 3. Open app/views/master.xml; 4. Make a modification and save. Expected result: the app reloads correctly in iPhone simulator. Actual result: an error screen appears. Clicking to dismiss the error does return the app to its working state. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15383,12,"""MobileWeb: Animations need to be made more asynchronous via setTimeout to avoid hideously huge stacks""","""""""If a startup delay is not specified, the go() method is called immediately, which causes the animation to become more synchronous. This causes call-stacks to grow over time and makes memory leaks more common. Wrapping it in a setTimeout(0) will fix it.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Animations need to be made more asynchronous via setTimeout to avoid hideously huge stacks
Description: """"If a startup delay is not specified, the go() method is called immediately, which causes the animation to become more synchronous. This causes call-stacks to grow over time and makes memory leaks more common. Wrapping it in a setTimeout(0) will fix it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15382,12,"""iOS7: slider rendering issue if custom thumbImage set before left/rightTrackImage""","""""""the problem is simple, with this configuration :   (Apple iOS 7 SDK, SDK 3.1.3.v20130908095038, GM xCode 5.0, iOS 7 simulator), the thumbImage appears in an incorrect manner (second attached image)    with this configuration :  (Apple iOS 7 SDK, SDK 3.1.3.v20130908095038, GM xCode 5.0, iOS 6.1 simulator), the problem there isn't (first attached image)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: slider rendering issue if custom thumbImage set before left/rightTrackImage
Description: """"the problem is simple, with this configuration : (Apple iOS 7 SDK, SDK 3.1.3.v20130908095038, GM xCode 5.0, iOS 7 simulator), the thumbImage appears in an incorrect manner (second attached image) with this configuration : (Apple iOS 7 SDK, SDK 3.1.3.v20130908095038, GM xCode 5.0, iOS 6.1 simulator), the problem there isn't (first attached image)""""",title+description
TIMOB-15381,12,"""iOS7: Button title not shown with image in navBar""","""""""If you want to emulate the back button in navigation bar and specify both an image and a title for the button, only the image will be displayed.  If the button is placed in the window, both the image and title appear.    See attached and try in a new alloy project.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Button title not shown with image in navBar
Description: """"If you want to emulate the back button in navigation bar and specify both an image and a title for the button, only the image will be displayed. If the button is placed in the window, both the image and title appear. See attached and try in a new alloy project. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15378,12,"""Android: Different Behaviour of Window within TabGroup in iOS and Android when set with borderRadius and BorderColor""","""""""Different Behaviour of Window when within TabGroup in iOS and Android when window is set with borderRadius and borderColor and backgroundColor.          Expected Result:  Window with red background color must get open with label in middle.    Actual Result:  Gets black colored screen with no label.    Result with 3.1.3.GA and 3.1.2.GA  On Android: black colored screen appears.  On iOS: red background colored window gets open along with label in the center.    Result with 3.1.1.GA  On Android: black colored screen appears along with red background colored window on the top left corner along with the label in the corner.  On iOS: red background colored window gets open along with label in the center.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Different Behaviour of Window within TabGroup in iOS and Android when set with borderRadius and BorderColor
Description: """"Different Behaviour of Window when within TabGroup in iOS and Android when window is set with borderRadius and borderColor and backgroundColor. Expected Result: Window with red background color must get open with label in middle. Actual Result: Gets black colored screen with no label. Result with 3.1.3.GA and 3.1.2.GA On Android: black colored screen appears. On iOS: red background colored window gets open along with label in the center. Result with 3.1.1.GA On Android: black colored screen appears along with red background colored window on the top left corner along with the label in the corner. On iOS: red background colored window gets open along with label in the center. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15377,12,"""iOS: using Label with tableViewRow prevents selection until scrolled out of visible portion""","""""""Using Label with table view row object, prevents row selection until i scroll the selected row out of visible portion and then take it back to visible portion.    Steps to reproduce:  !: Use the below attached app.js and use it in new project.  2: Build the project for iOS6 or iOS7 simulator.  3: Test with table view 3, selection won't happen after first time until scrolling is performed.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: using Label with tableViewRow prevents selection until scrolled out of visible portion
Description: """"Using Label with table view row object, prevents row selection until i scroll the selected row out of visible portion and then take it back to visible portion. Steps to reproduce: !: Use the below attached app.js and use it in new project. 2: Build the project for iOS6 or iOS7 simulator. 3: Test with table view 3, selection won't happen after first time until scrolling is performed. """"",title+description
