TIMOB-15365,12,"""EXC_ARM_DA_ALIGN in KrollContext StringFormatCallback()""","""""""I started running into a memory alignment issue on iOS 7 that wasn't present in 6.1: the code for formatting a string has been throwing EXC_ARM_DA_ALIGN errors.  I found [this web page|http://www.splinter.com.au/what-do-do-with-excarmdaalign-on-an-iphone-ap/] which briefly explains the cause and gives a workaround.    I wasn't able to reproduce the bug with a simple test of different String.format() calls, but I was able to fix the problem in the app that was crashing by replacing lines 384-386 in KrollContext.m with the following:    {code:objective-c}  double tmp = TiValueToNumber(jsContext, valueRef, NULL);  memcpy(argList, &tmp, sizeof(tmp));  argList += sizeof(double);  {code}    I made a similar change in the boolean arg value at lines 390-392.""""""",Bug,"Title: EXC_ARM_DA_ALIGN in KrollContext StringFormatCallback()
Description: """"I started running into a memory alignment issue on iOS 7 that wasn't present in 6.1: the code for formatting a string has been throwing EXC_ARM_DA_ALIGN errors. I found [this web page|http://www.splinter.com.au/what-do-do-with-excarmdaalign-on-an-iphone-ap/] which briefly explains the cause and gives a workaround. I wasn't able to reproduce the bug with a simple test of different String.format() calls, but I was able to fix the problem in the app that was crashing by replacing lines 384-386 in KrollContext.m with the following: {code:objective-c} double tmp = TiValueToNumber(jsContext, valueRef, NULL); memcpy(argList, &tmp, sizeof(tmp)); argList += sizeof(double); {code} I made a similar change in the boolean arg value at lines 390-392.""""",title+description
