TIMOB-15336,12,"""Android TiViewProxy crashes with NullPointerException with blur()""","""""""Included is a sample app which demonstrates this bug; it seems like running blur on a text view right before it get removed from its parent view causes this crash reliably (the buggy section noted with a XXX comment).    Digging into it more, it seems like a general race issue; underlying this is blur uses TiMessenger#postOnMain, which uses Message#sendToTarget underneath, whereas TiUIView#remove uses TiMessenger#sendBlockingMessage, which if another sendBlockingMessage was already running, will be ran before that sendBlockingMessage finishes, and more notably before the blur message is processed.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android TiViewProxy crashes with NullPointerException with blur()
Description: """"Included is a sample app which demonstrates this bug; it seems like running blur on a text view right before it get removed from its parent view causes this crash reliably (the buggy section noted with a XXX comment). Digging into it more, it seems like a general race issue; underlying this is blur uses TiMessenger#postOnMain, which uses Message#sendToTarget underneath, whereas TiUIView#remove uses TiMessenger#sendBlockingMessage, which if another sendBlockingMessage was already running, will be ran before that sendBlockingMessage finishes, and more notably before the blur message is processed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15335,12,"""iOS7: No console logging from Titanium CLI""","""""""After upgrading to 3.1.3.GA the CLI no longer outputs to the console when using an iOS7 device.  The customer states that if they switch to iOS 6.1 then the console outputs return.  The customer builds using Titanium CLI only, not studio.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: No console logging from Titanium CLI
Description: """"After upgrading to 3.1.3.GA the CLI no longer outputs to the console when using an iOS7 device. The customer states that if they switch to iOS 6.1 then the console outputs return. The customer builds using Titanium CLI only, not studio.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15334,12,"""Facebook: make sure Titanium's Facebook module is in accordance with best practices""","""""""https://developers.facebook.com/docs/facebook-login/checklist/  The iOS and Android Facebook modules fail on several requirements:  - Standardized Facebook login button not used  - Custom web views used when Facebook is prohibiting them (it will break October 2nd)  - Reauthorization available only in the iOS module, and it's required for Android too    The only real solution is to upgrade to the latest Facebook SDKs and use them as recommended.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Facebook: make sure Titanium's Facebook module is in accordance with best practices
Description: """"https://developers.facebook.com/docs/facebook-login/checklist/ The iOS and Android Facebook modules fail on several requirements: - Standardized Facebook login button not used - Custom web views used when Facebook is prohibiting them (it will break October 2nd) - Reauthorization available only in the iOS module, and it's required for Android too The only real solution is to upgrade to the latest Facebook SDKs and use them as recommended.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15333,12,"""Android: Support for Gzip on ImageViews""","""""""When a server has Content-Encoding:gzip for images, android will not download the remote image. This works on iOS, but Android will not accept the gzipped image data.    DDMS log:  SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null          I know this issue exists: TIMOB-2698 but that for the XHR object.    Is this a bug, or did Android SDK never support this?""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support for Gzip on ImageViews
Description: """"When a server has Content-Encoding:gzip for images, android will not download the remote image. This works on iOS, but Android will not accept the gzipped image data. DDMS log: SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null I know this issue exists: TIMOB-2698 but that for the XHR object. Is this a bug, or did Android SDK never support this?""""",title+description
