TIMOB-15296,12,"""Android: Support for window flags""","""""""h2. Description  Currently Titanium doesn't support setting the flags on window. This is possible in native Android SDK when we add flags in the onCreate method of the window object.    h4. Android Native Example      This is basically required to show the message screen over the lock-screen. When a message is send to the app the message window should be shown even if the phone's screen is locked.     For reference:  http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/WindowManager.LayoutParams.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support for window flags
Description: """"h2. Description Currently Titanium doesn't support setting the flags on window. This is possible in native Android SDK when we add flags in the onCreate method of the window object. h4. Android Native Example This is basically required to show the message screen over the lock-screen. When a message is send to the app the message window should be shown even if the phone's screen is locked. For reference: http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/WindowManager.LayoutParams.html""""",title+description
