TIMOB-15254,12,"""Titanium does not handle 64bit integer correctly in Sqlite on iOS""","""""""If you store a 64bit integer in Sqlite it returns a truncated version when you try to read it back using resultset.field or resultset.fieldByName    This is due to two things:  1) A problem in the underlying pldatabase that the use:  http://code.google.com/p/pldatabase/issues/detail?id=25&thanks=25&ts=1377514140    2) Even if the above problem was fixed Titanium still truncates in TiDatabaseResultSetProxy.m aprox. line #90 in the function transformObject :  result = NUMINT([TiUtils intValue:obj def:NSNotFound valid:&valid]);    There is a work around that requires no modification of the pldatabase library, since if Titanium were to use PLSqliteResultSet->bigIntForColumnIndex it correctly returns a 64bit Objective long long.""""""",Story,"Title: Titanium does not handle 64bit integer correctly in Sqlite on iOS
Description: """"If you store a 64bit integer in Sqlite it returns a truncated version when you try to read it back using resultset.field or resultset.fieldByName This is due to two things: 1) A problem in the underlying pldatabase that the use: http://code.google.com/p/pldatabase/issues/detail?id=25&thanks=25&ts=1377514140 2) Even if the above problem was fixed Titanium still truncates in TiDatabaseResultSetProxy.m aprox. line #90 in the function transformObject : result = NUMINT([TiUtils intValue:obj def:NSNotFound valid:&valid]); There is a work around that requires no modification of the pldatabase library, since if Titanium were to use PLSqliteResultSet->bigIntForColumnIndex it correctly returns a 64bit Objective long long.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15252,12,"""Android: Cannot reference proxy methods""","""""""On iOS you can do:        But on Android you'll get:        This is unfortunate, because this means you cannot link an Alloy widget's exported methods through to one of it's view elements.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Cannot reference proxy methods
