TIMOB-15205,12,"""iOS7: Value not changed at touchEnd event of Switch""","""""""The """"""""change"""""""" event of the switch on iOS 7 with SDK 3.1.3 (and Apple iOS 7 SDK) behaves differently than the previous SDK (for example with the 3.0.2 SDK and Apple iOS 6 SDK)    basically if you run the movement shown in the video attached, the """"""""change"""""""" event is invoked, although actually at the """"""""touchEnd"""""""" of the finger on the switch the switch has not really changed the value.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Value not changed at touchEnd event of Switch
Description: """"The """"""""change"""""""" event of the switch on iOS 7 with SDK 3.1.3 (and Apple iOS 7 SDK) behaves differently than the previous SDK (for example with the 3.0.2 SDK and Apple iOS 6 SDK) basically if you run the movement shown in the video attached, the """"""""change"""""""" event is invoked, although actually at the """"""""touchEnd"""""""" of the finger on the switch the switch has not really changed the value.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15204,12,"""iOS7: Contents flash during refresh of TableViewRow""","""""""When there is a refresh of the contents of a row of TableViewRow, the contents of the row """"""""flashes"""""""", practically it is understood that the contents of the row was updated (I have a function that updates every few seconds the content of tableviewrow)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Contents flash during refresh of TableViewRow
