TIMOB-15191,12,"""iOS7: Color and Translucency of Window default Navigation and TabGroups are wrong""","""""""By default the level of translucency of the tabGroup and top window navigation do not match the default Apps from Apple, or what Xcode 5 natively builds in iOS 7, or what the Apple docs show as the default UI here:  https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UserExperience/Conceptual/TransitionGuide/index.html    The tabGroup and top navigation are too grey in Titanium, and the level of translucency seems less than what the default should be. Perhaps it is simple the default color (being too grey) that is the problem, and the translucency will come right if the color does.    Please see attached screenshot with the Apple default on the left, and what Titanium builds on the right.        Can this please be fixed as part of 3.1.3?""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Color and Translucency of Window default Navigation and TabGroups are wrong
Description: """"By default the level of translucency of the tabGroup and top window navigation do not match the default Apps from Apple, or what Xcode 5 natively builds in iOS 7, or what the Apple docs show as the default UI here: https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UserExperience/Conceptual/TransitionGuide/index.html The tabGroup and top navigation are too grey in Titanium, and the level of translucency seems less than what the default should be. Perhaps it is simple the default color (being too grey) that is the problem, and the translucency will come right if the color does. Please see attached screenshot with the Apple default on the left, and what Titanium builds on the right. Can this please be fixed as part of 3.1.3?""""",title+description
TIMOB-15190,12,"""iOS7: Ti.media.showCamera does not show flash or camera toggle buttons""","""""""Using the standard methods for taking a photo or video, the camera does not provide means to toggle the front or back camera or the flash.     It's possible this could be native to the picker now. I don't know.       To reproduce, use the KitchenSink camera examples.       It would be good to have the ability in the Titanium SDK to use the AVFoundation / AVCaptureConnection methods. That way, developers could have absolute total control over all available camera features and never have to worry about the differences when using an overlay or not.     """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS7: Ti.media.showCamera does not show flash or camera toggle buttons
Description: """"Using the standard methods for taking a photo or video, the camera does not provide means to toggle the front or back camera or the flash. It's possible this could be native to the picker now. I don't know. To reproduce, use the KitchenSink camera examples. It would be good to have the ability in the Titanium SDK to use the AVFoundation / AVCaptureConnection methods. That way, developers could have absolute total control over all available camera features and never have to worry about the differences when using an overlay or not. """"",title+description
TIMOB-15189,12,"""iOS7: Opening a Modal Window removes BarImage of the Parent-Window for a moment""","""""""When opening a modal window from a child window having a the property """"""""barImage"""""""", this property is ignored and the underlayed """"""""barColor"""""""" is used, if set. The given app.js and barImage.png shows this problem.    Expected behaviour: The barImage stays where it is and the modal window opens.  Given behaviour: The barImage is beeing removed for a moment and comes back after closing the modal window""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Opening a Modal Window removes BarImage of the Parent-Window for a moment
Description: """"When opening a modal window from a child window having a the property """"""""barImage"""""""", this property is ignored and the underlayed """"""""barColor"""""""" is used, if set. The given app.js and barImage.png shows this problem. Expected behaviour: The barImage stays where it is and the modal window opens. Given behaviour: The barImage is beeing removed for a moment and comes back after closing the modal window""""",title+description
TIMOB-15188,12,"""iOS7: Tapping Tab Orphans Windows on Tab's Stack""","""""""h2. Problem  In version 3.1.3 and above tapping the tab's button to return to the root window of the tab orphans any windows between the current window and the root window. This works as expected in 3.1.2 GA but 3.1.3 has serious regression bug    h2. Why This Is A Problem  Orphaned windows equate to leaked memory. Windows in the middle of the root and last window are orphaned and all resources are trapped. Causes crash on device after lots of use.    h2. Expected Behavior  Tapping the tab's button should close every window that is open on that tab's stack, not just the current window. On version 3.1.2 it does the following which is correct:    {code:lang=none|title=3.1.2 Console Log}  [ERROR] :  Opened: A  [ERROR] :  Opened: B  [ERROR] :  Opened: C  [ERROR] :  Closed: C  [ERROR] :  Closed: B  [ERROR] :  Closed: A      h2. Logs  {code:lang=none|title=3.1.3 Console Log}  [ERROR] :  Opened: A  [ERROR] :  Opened: B  [ERROR] :  Opened: C  [ERROR] :  Closed: C  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Tapping Tab Orphans Windows on Tab's Stack
Description: """"h2. Problem In version 3.1.3 and above tapping the tab's button to return to the root window of the tab orphans any windows between the current window and the root window. This works as expected in 3.1.2 GA but 3.1.3 has serious regression bug h2. Why This Is A Problem Orphaned windows equate to leaked memory. Windows in the middle of the root and last window are orphaned and all resources are trapped. Causes crash on device after lots of use. h2. Expected Behavior Tapping the tab's button should close every window that is open on that tab's stack, not just the current window. On version 3.1.2 it does the following which is correct: {code:lang=none|title=3.1.2 Console Log} [ERROR] : Opened: A [ERROR] : Opened: B [ERROR] : Opened: C [ERROR] : Closed: C [ERROR] : Closed: B [ERROR] : Closed: A h2. Logs {code:lang=none|title=3.1.3 Console Log} [ERROR] : Opened: A [ERROR] : Opened: B [ERROR] : Opened: C [ERROR] : Closed: C {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-15187,12,"""iOS7: focus event not triggered in window opened in a tab if another non-fullscreen window is overlaid on the tabgroup""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    # run the attached app.js   # click on the """"""""open new window"""""""" button    Expected:    * The """"""""focus"""""""" event should be triggered on the newly opened window (new_window)    Actual:    * The """"""""focus"""""""" event is not fired      Additional notes:  * The focus event is fired on win1 the first time the tabgroup is presented, but not when closing new_window  * the same example works as expected when built with Ti SDK 3.1.2.GA""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: focus event not triggered in window opened in a tab if another non-fullscreen window is overlaid on the tabgroup
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: # run the attached app.js # click on the """"""""open new window"""""""" button Expected: * The """"""""focus"""""""" event should be triggered on the newly opened window (new_window) Actual: * The """"""""focus"""""""" event is not fired Additional notes: * The focus event is fired on win1 the first time the tabgroup is presented, but not when closing new_window * the same example works as expected when built with Ti SDK 3.1.2.GA""""",title+description
TIMOB-15186,12,"""iOS 7 - Translucent setting forces the search bar for a tableview to go behind the nav bar.""","""""""Compare the following:  http://www.screencast.com/t/lT6RZSM2AKlr    vs.    http://www.screencast.com/t/68GpUv3f10e    When setting the translucent property, it forces the search to go under the nav bar.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 7 - Translucent setting forces the search bar for a tableview to go behind the nav bar.
Description: """"Compare the following: http://www.screencast.com/t/lT6RZSM2AKlr vs. http://www.screencast.com/t/68GpUv3f10e When setting the translucent property, it forces the search to go under the nav bar.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15185,12,"""KitchenSink: Application-specific console logs does not appear for iphone 64bit simulator""","""""""Application specific Console logs does not appear for iOS Simulator 7.0: Retina & Tall (4-inch 64-bit). Console logs appear for iOS simulator 7.0 Retina.  This is not regression issue. This issue is specific to 64bit simulator.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Install kitchensink on iOS 7.0 device or Simulator v7.0  2. Go to Kitchensink. Right click >Run as >Run Config > 64 bit iphone simulator. Change simulator config to """"""""Retina & Tall (4-inch 64-bit)"""""""". OR iOS Simulator>Hardware>Device>iPhone Retina(4-inch 64-bit)  3. Go to KS>Controls>Progress Bar  4. Click """"""""Start Progress"""""""" button    Actual: Console does not show following info:  [INFO] INTERVAL FIRED value 0  [INFO] INTERVAL FIRED value 1  [INFO] INTERVAL FIRED value 2      Logs do not appear in 64bit for:  Ti.API.info('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val);  Ti.API.debug('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val);  Ti.API.warn('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val);  Ti.API.error('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val);  Ti.API.trace('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val);    Expected: The above info must appear in console. Changing iphone simulator to """"""""Retina"""""""" will display above info  """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Application-specific console logs does not appear for iphone 64bit simulator
Description: """"Application specific Console logs does not appear for iOS Simulator 7.0: Retina & Tall (4-inch 64-bit). Console logs appear for iOS simulator 7.0 Retina. This is not regression issue. This issue is specific to 64bit simulator. Steps to reproduce: 1. Install kitchensink on iOS 7.0 device or Simulator v7.0 2. Go to Kitchensink. Right click >Run as >Run Config > 64 bit iphone simulator. Change simulator config to """"""""Retina & Tall (4-inch 64-bit)"""""""". OR iOS Simulator>Hardware>Device>iPhone Retina(4-inch 64-bit) 3. Go to KS>Controls>Progress Bar 4. Click """"""""Start Progress"""""""" button Actual: Console does not show following info: [INFO] INTERVAL FIRED value 0 [INFO] INTERVAL FIRED value 1 [INFO] INTERVAL FIRED value 2 Logs do not appear in 64bit for: Ti.API.info('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val); Ti.API.debug('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val); Ti.API.warn('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val); Ti.API.error('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val); Ti.API.trace('INTERVAL FIRED value ' + val); Expected: The above info must appear in console. Changing iphone simulator to """"""""Retina"""""""" will display above info """"",title+description
TIMOB-15184,12,"""iOS7: KitchenSink: Could not  hide/show status bar, also could not toggle status bar style""","""""""Show/hide and toggle style does not work for iOS 7. Verified on iOS simulator 7.0 64bit and iPhone5(v7.0)  Although this functionality works fine for iPOD touch4(v6.1)  This is not a regression issue.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Install kitchensink on iOS 7.0 device or Simulator v7.0. (Download from https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/KitchenSink/tree/3_1_X)  2. Go to Kitchensink > Phone > Status Bar  3. Click Hide/show button (Nothing happens)  4. Click """"""""toggle Style"""""""" button (Nothing happens)    Actual: Show/hide and toggle style does not work for iOS 7  Expected: Status bar should be hidden or shown on click of """"""""Hide/show"""""""" button and Style of status bar must be changed on clicking """"""""Toggle style"""""""" button.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: KitchenSink: Could not hide/show status bar, also could not toggle status bar style
Description: """"Show/hide and toggle style does not work for iOS 7. Verified on iOS simulator 7.0 64bit and iPhone5(v7.0) Although this functionality works fine for iPOD touch4(v6.1) This is not a regression issue. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Install kitchensink on iOS 7.0 device or Simulator v7.0. (Download from https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/KitchenSink/tree/3_1_X) 2. Go to Kitchensink > Phone > Status Bar 3. Click Hide/show button (Nothing happens) 4. Click """"""""toggle Style"""""""" button (Nothing happens) Actual: Show/hide and toggle style does not work for iOS 7 Expected: Status bar should be hidden or shown on click of """"""""Hide/show"""""""" button and Style of status bar must be changed on clicking """"""""Toggle style"""""""" button.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15180,12,"""Android: Implement an event """"taskremoved"""" when Service.onTaskRemoved() is called""","""""""Swiping app away from the recent apps list will kill any background or empty processes of the application but it won't stop the running services or remove the notifications from the status bar. See the discussion here:  http://www.howtogeek.com/169549/what-exactly-happens-when-you-swipe-an-android-app-from-the-recent-apps-list/  http://lifehacker.com/what-happens-when-you-remove-an-app-from-androids-mult-1179868228  In order to get notified when the app is swiped away, we need to implement a new event which is fired from [Service.onTaskRemoved()|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Service.html#onTaskRemoved(android.content.Intent)].""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Implement an event """"taskremoved"""" when Service.onTaskRemoved() is called
Description: """"Swiping app away from the recent apps list will kill any background or empty processes of the application but it won't stop the running services or remove the notifications from the status bar. See the discussion here: http://www.howtogeek.com/169549/what-exactly-happens-when-you-swipe-an-android-app-from-the-recent-apps-list/ http://lifehacker.com/what-happens-when-you-remove-an-app-from-androids-mult-1179868228 In order to get notified when the app is swiped away, we need to implement a new event which is fired from [Service.onTaskRemoved()|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Service.html#onTaskRemoved(android.content.Intent)].""""",title+description
