TIMOB-15106,12,"""Android: Closing an heavyweight window soon after opening it doesn't work""","""""""If you close an heavyweight window soon after having opened it, the window won't be closed.    h1. Steps to reproduce    # Use the following code as {{app.js}}  # Run the app  # You ought to see the red screen (like on iOS), but you will see the green screen still open  # Remove line 7 ({{modal:false}}) to make the window lightweight and you *wil* see the red screen        This issue is probably related to TIMOB-7705 resolved as {{Cannot Reproduce}}.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Closing an heavyweight window soon after opening it doesn't work
Description: """"If you close an heavyweight window soon after having opened it, the window won't be closed. h1. Steps to reproduce # Use the following code as {{app.js}} # Run the app # You ought to see the red screen (like on iOS), but you will see the green screen still open # Remove line 7 ({{modal:false}}) to make the window lightweight and you *wil* see the red screen This issue is probably related to TIMOB-7705 resolved as {{Cannot Reproduce}}.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15105,12,"""Android: Opening heavyweight window delayed by following heavy operations""","""""""If opening a heavyweight window is followed by heavy operations, the window won't show until those computations are done.      h1. Steps to reproduce  # Execute the following code:        # The console will say red opened a few seconds before green:        # But on the device you won't see the red window at all.      h1. Quick analysis    Looking at the Titanium Android [WindowProxy|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/WindowProxy.java#L294], line 294 I see that the open event is fired when the activity is created. So I guess this means it's not an Titanium bug but an Android one that actual showing the window is delayed by the heavy computation that follows.      h1. Notes    - When you change the red window to be lightweight it works fine.  - When you wrap everything after line 6 in {{setTimeout}} statement it works fine.  - When you replace adding the blue views by a non-UI/non-Proxy heavy computation, the problem stays the same.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Opening heavyweight window delayed by following heavy operations
Description: """"If opening a heavyweight window is followed by heavy operations, the window won't show until those computations are done. h1. Steps to reproduce # Execute the following code: # The console will say red opened a few seconds before green: # But on the device you won't see the red window at all. h1. Quick analysis Looking at the Titanium Android [WindowProxy|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/WindowProxy.java#L294], line 294 I see that the open event is fired when the activity is created. So I guess this means it's not an Titanium bug but an Android one that actual showing the window is delayed by the heavy computation that follows. h1. Notes - When you change the red window to be lightweight it works fine. - When you wrap everything after line 6 in {{setTimeout}} statement it works fine. - When you replace adding the blue views by a non-UI/non-Proxy heavy computation, the problem stays the same.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15103,12,"""Possibility to change name of More tab in TabGroup""","""""""Hello,  please add an option to change name of More tab in TabGroup to createTabGroup method.  Thank you""""""",New Feature,"Title: Possibility to change name of More tab in TabGroup
Description: """"Hello, please add an option to change name of More tab in TabGroup to createTabGroup method. Thank you""""",title+description
TIMOB-15102,12,"""Bubbling of events in listview items in newer android versions""","""""""For some reason, and after upgrading Android to 4.x from 2.x, the itemclick event on ListView doesn't fire anymore.  It works if you click on the very edge of the item, i.e. if you manage to click on the ListItem itself directly and not on any child items.    Our Alloy template is set up like this:        And then in our controller we have the following:  {code:js}  $.objectList.addEventListener('itemclick', function(e){   handleAction(e);  });  {code}    This works perfectly fine in iOS and in older versions of Android, but in 4.x, nothing...""""""",Bug,"Title: Bubbling of events in listview items in newer android versions
Description: """"For some reason, and after upgrading Android to 4.x from 2.x, the itemclick event on ListView doesn't fire anymore. It works if you click on the very edge of the item, i.e. if you manage to click on the ListItem itself directly and not on any child items. Our Alloy template is set up like this: And then in our controller we have the following: {code:js} $.objectList.addEventListener('itemclick', function(e){ handleAction(e); }); {code} This works perfectly fine in iOS and in older versions of Android, but in 4.x, nothing...""""",title+description
TIMOB-15101,12,"""ScrollableView in ListView's items, causes a bug after the scroll of any ScrollableView""","""""""*Problem description*  If you use a ScrollableView in a ListView, it has a bug.  By default, in every item I show the first image of ScrollableView (currentPage = 0). After the scroll in any one of ScrollableViews, if then I scroll the ListView, many other ScrollableViews will have changed the image. Even if I try to reload the ListView, it will not show the first image of ScrollableView in all items.    *Test case*  This is a generic code that reproduces the problem:   """"""",Bug,"Title: ScrollableView in ListView's items, causes a bug after the scroll of any ScrollableView
Description: """"*Problem description* If you use a ScrollableView in a ListView, it has a bug. By default, in every item I show the first image of ScrollableView (currentPage = 0). After the scroll in any one of ScrollableViews, if then I scroll the ListView, many other ScrollableViews will have changed the image. Even if I try to reload the ListView, it will not show the first image of ScrollableView in all items. *Test case* This is a generic code that reproduces the problem: """"",title+description
TIMOB-15099,12,"""Android: borderRadius does not adhere to defaultunit""","""""""The {{borderRadius}} property does not adhere to the default unit set in {{tiapp.xml}}. Both {{borderWidth}} and {{borderRadius}} only accept {{Number}}, so it's not possible to workaround by explicitly setting the unit. Like most other dimension-related properties (except {{fontSize}} as far as I know) {{borderWidth}} *does* use the default unit.    h1. To reproduce    # Create a new app  # Replace the code in {{app.js}} by:        # Run the app on both iOS and Android and the result will be like screenshots 1 and 2.  # Now set the default unit to {{dp}} by adding this to the {{tiapp.xml}}:        # Run the app on both platforms again and the result will be like screenshots 1 and 3. As you can see because of the DPI of the tested device the border radius is about half of what we expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: borderRadius does not adhere to defaultunit
Description: """"The {{borderRadius}} property does not adhere to the default unit set in {{tiapp.xml}}. Both {{borderWidth}} and {{borderRadius}} only accept {{Number}}, so it's not possible to workaround by explicitly setting the unit. Like most other dimension-related properties (except {{fontSize}} as far as I know) {{borderWidth}} *does* use the default unit. h1. To reproduce # Create a new app # Replace the code in {{app.js}} by: # Run the app on both iOS and Android and the result will be like screenshots 1 and 2. # Now set the default unit to {{dp}} by adding this to the {{tiapp.xml}}: # Run the app on both platforms again and the result will be like screenshots 1 and 3. As you can see because of the DPI of the tested device the border radius is about half of what we expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15098,12,"""Android: (Parity) Add support for shadowColor & shadowOffset to labels""","""""""Adding a shadow to text is a very common request I get. For simple texts I can get away with stacking 2 labels, but as it gets more complex (alignment, wordWrap..) this gets more tricky.    I'm reading that Android {{TextView}} has a {{shadowLayer}} which seems to be able to do the job.    IMHO parity should be high priority.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: (Parity) Add support for shadowColor & shadowOffset to labels
Description: """"Adding a shadow to text is a very common request I get. For simple texts I can get away with stacking 2 labels, but as it gets more complex (alignment, wordWrap..) this gets more tricky. I'm reading that Android {{TextView}} has a {{shadowLayer}} which seems to be able to do the job. IMHO parity should be high priority.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15096,12,"""Android: (Parity) Ti.Media.Sound.allowBackground:false should not mute when opening new (heavyweight) window""","""""""Leaving {{Ti.Media.Sound.allowBackground}} to the default {{false}} will not only mute the sound when the app moves to the background, but also when you open a new heavyweight window (and thus activity) within the app. I can understand why this is because of the activity that created the sound is then paused, but I think this should not be happening for the sake of parity with iOS.    h1. Proposed improvement  Only mute when the app itself is paused.    h1. Workaround  Create the sound in {{app.js}}. But then, even if you explicitly set {{Ti.Media.Sound.allowBackground}} to {{false}}, the music will continue to play when the app moves to the background.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: (Parity) Ti.Media.Sound.allowBackground:false should not mute when opening new (heavyweight) window
Description: """"Leaving {{Ti.Media.Sound.allowBackground}} to the default {{false}} will not only mute the sound when the app moves to the background, but also when you open a new heavyweight window (and thus activity) within the app. I can understand why this is because of the activity that created the sound is then paused, but I think this should not be happening for the sake of parity with iOS. h1. Proposed improvement Only mute when the app itself is paused. h1. Workaround Create the sound in {{app.js}}. But then, even if you explicitly set {{Ti.Media.Sound.allowBackground}} to {{false}}, the music will continue to play when the app moves to the background.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15095,12,"""iOS: ScrollableView's manageCache causing lag halfway through page""","""""""When scrolling through the pages of a ScrollableView composed out of several 'heavy' views, a noticeable lag occurs halfway scrolling to the next page.    h1. Code to reproduce        h1. Problem    Me and [~<USER> tracked down the problem and {{manageCache}} seems to be the problem. When the nextPage changes half-way, manageCache renders *all* views within range, instead of just the new view getting into the range. It must be possible to make this more efficient. But even if it's just 1 or 2 views that need to be rendered, if they are heavy, the lag still occurs.    h1. Solution  We investigated if the rendering could possibly be delayed until after fully having slide to the next page, but then the lag occurs 1 or 2 pixels before reaching the next page *and* if you scroll through the pages fast, the rendering won't be triggerd at all. We didn't manage to find a satisfying solution, but I'm sure the <USER>iOS experts can ;)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollableView's manageCache causing lag halfway through page
Description: """"When scrolling through the pages of a ScrollableView composed out of several 'heavy' views, a noticeable lag occurs halfway scrolling to the next page. h1. Code to reproduce h1. Problem Me and [~<USER> tracked down the problem and {{manageCache}} seems to be the problem. When the nextPage changes half-way, manageCache renders *all* views within range, instead of just the new view getting into the range. It must be possible to make this more efficient. But even if it's just 1 or 2 views that need to be rendered, if they are heavy, the lag still occurs. h1. Solution We investigated if the rendering could possibly be delayed until after fully having slide to the next page, but then the lag occurs 1 or 2 pixels before reaching the next page *and* if you scroll through the pages fast, the rendering won't be triggerd at all. We didn't manage to find a satisfying solution, but I'm sure the <USER>iOS experts can ;)""""",title+description
TIMOB-15094,12,"""Android: Support Titanium.App pause/resume events""","""""""Like discussed in TIMOB-7360 (SDK 1.8.x) Android natively doesn't really support {{pause}}/{{resume}} events for the app as a whole, but only for separate activities within the app.    However, since both closing the current heavyweight window and closing the app fire the exact same {{pause}} event on that window, there is no way to workaround, making this a critical issue!    Having talked about this with several developers and trying multiple workarounds without much success, [~<USER> remembered [~<USER> actually did got this working in a [fork of the 2.1.x Titanium SDK|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commits/2_1_X_iamyellow].    I have cloned the current branch and it seems the 2 commits involved should still work. I can't get the SDK to build on my system (never been there) to verify, but since this is such an frustrating parity problem I kindly ask to have a look at the 2 commits and consider pulling them into the SDK.    I know [~<USER> would be happy to be of help.    * Main commit: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/42ccc574cd2a285b68aebfa4a4bb88fd9b8becce  * Commit to fix triggering the events for {{TiLaunchActivity}}'s: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/73ed97415bf9a12ca1d1849eba4c889f6b51f4ba""""""",Improvement,"Title: Android: Support Titanium.App pause/resume events
Description: """"Like discussed in TIMOB-7360 (SDK 1.8.x) Android natively doesn't really support {{pause}}/{{resume}} events for the app as a whole, but only for separate activities within the app. However, since both closing the current heavyweight window and closing the app fire the exact same {{pause}} event on that window, there is no way to workaround, making this a critical issue! Having talked about this with several developers and trying multiple workarounds without much success, [~<USER> remembered [~<USER> actually did got this working in a [fork of the 2.1.x Titanium SDK|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commits/2_1_X_iamyellow]. I have cloned the current branch and it seems the 2 commits involved should still work. I can't get the SDK to build on my system (never been there) to verify, but since this is such an frustrating parity problem I kindly ask to have a look at the 2 commits and consider pulling them into the SDK. I know [~<USER> would be happy to be of help. * Main commit: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/42ccc574cd2a285b68aebfa4a4bb88fd9b8becce * Commit to fix triggering the events for {{TiLaunchActivity}}'s: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/73ed97415bf9a12ca1d1849eba4c889f6b51f4ba""""",title+description
TIMOB-15093,12,"""Use data parameter for GET request in httpclient too""","""""""Hello,    At this time, it's possible to pass a data argument to httpClient.send method for POST request. (an object will be serialized)    I don't know if people would need the following but I found it useful.  I didn't want to concatenate params to url by hand anymore, for GET requests.    A more elegant solution was to create a simple function that would do the same for GET request as you do for POSTs.    For example at this time I do the following:        This results in the following request:    http://api.whatever.com/users/search.json?age=25&sex=male    It would be nice to have this supported natively by titanium.    So doing this:        would have the same result as my function.    I think this adds some nice abstraction and a clearer code.    What do you think?    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Use data parameter for GET request in httpclient too
Description: """"Hello, At this time, it's possible to pass a data argument to httpClient.send method for POST request. (an object will be serialized) I don't know if people would need the following but I found it useful. I didn't want to concatenate params to url by hand anymore, for GET requests. A more elegant solution was to create a simple function that would do the same for GET request as you do for POSTs. For example at this time I do the following: This results in the following request: http://api.whatever.com/users/search.json?age=25&sex=male It would be nice to have this supported natively by titanium. So doing this: would have the same result as my function. I think this adds some nice abstraction and a clearer code. What do you think? """"",title+description
TIMOB-15092,12,"""Android: Multiple PickerViews inside a TableView shuffling options / disappearing""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When you add multiple Pickers inside a TableView (one picker per row), they get very buggy after scrolling the screen.    What I have noticed is that some previously selected pickerView options just disappear, or the options are changed randomly.    In the testcase I'm submitting I'm using the same options for different pickerviews, but if the options are different the problem get even worse.    I have also found out that If I set a className to each different pickerView ROW the problem vanishes. Problem is that it seems that there is a limit of 32 classNames, past that and the app crashes (which is a big problem as I'm building dynamic forms and some forms reach 50+ questions).  Also, by setting a different className to each row, you lose the tableView optimization.    h4. Testcase      h4. Instructions to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile Project (Classic Titanium)  2. Paste the code into app.js  3. Run it in a device  4. In question 0, put answer 0, in question 1, answer 1 and so on.   5. Scroll down and up.  6. You will see your answers changed.     h4. Extra info  In the logs I can see this:      when scrolling the tableview.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Multiple PickerViews inside a TableView shuffling options / disappearing
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When you add multiple Pickers inside a TableView (one picker per row), they get very buggy after scrolling the screen. What I have noticed is that some previously selected pickerView options just disappear, or the options are changed randomly. In the testcase I'm submitting I'm using the same options for different pickerviews, but if the options are different the problem get even worse. I have also found out that If I set a className to each different pickerView ROW the problem vanishes. Problem is that it seems that there is a limit of 32 classNames, past that and the app crashes (which is a big problem as I'm building dynamic forms and some forms reach 50+ questions). Also, by setting a different className to each row, you lose the tableView optimization. h4. Testcase h4. Instructions to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile Project (Classic Titanium) 2. Paste the code into app.js 3. Run it in a device 4. In question 0, put answer 0, in question 1, answer 1 and so on. 5. Scroll down and up. 6. You will see your answers changed. h4. Extra info In the logs I can see this: when scrolling the tableview. """"",title+description
