TIMOB-15077,12,"""iOS7: Support new UIStatusBarStyleLightContent style""","""""""If you don't want your (lightweight) view to be positioned under the status bar, you can set {{top}} to {{20}}. This will cause the main view's background color (set via {{Ti.UI.backgroundColor}} or image to be visible under the status bar.    This works fine as long as the background color/image is light, because the status bar text is always black. On a dark (black) background, the only thing you will see is the green battery icon.    To fix this, all we need is the new {{UIStatusBarStyleLightContent}} style to be exposed as an option for {{Ti.UI.iPhone.statusBarStyle}}. For example as {{Ti.UI.iPhone.StatusBar.LIGHT_CONTENT}}.    Information can be found at: https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UserExperience/Conceptual/TransitionGuide/Bars.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40013174-CH8-SW2    h1. To reproduce/test    # Create app: {{titanium create -p ios --id test.statusbar -n TestStatusBar}}  # Use as {{app.js}}:        # Run the app to see you can only see the green battery icon (as attached).  # Change the first line to:        # Run the app to see the text was actually there but not visible black on black.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Support new UIStatusBarStyleLightContent style
Description: """"If you don't want your (lightweight) view to be positioned under the status bar, you can set {{top}} to {{20}}. This will cause the main view's background color (set via {{Ti.UI.backgroundColor}} or image to be visible under the status bar. This works fine as long as the background color/image is light, because the status bar text is always black. On a dark (black) background, the only thing you will see is the green battery icon. To fix this, all we need is the new {{UIStatusBarStyleLightContent}} style to be exposed as an option for {{Ti.UI.iPhone.statusBarStyle}}. For example as {{Ti.UI.iPhone.StatusBar.LIGHT_CONTENT}}. Information can be found at: https://developer.apple.com/library/prerelease/ios/documentation/UserExperience/Conceptual/TransitionGuide/Bars.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40013174-CH8-SW2 h1. To reproduce/test # Create app: {{titanium create -p ios --id test.statusbar -n TestStatusBar}} # Use as {{app.js}}: # Run the app to see you can only see the green battery icon (as attached). # Change the first line to: # Run the app to see the text was actually there but not visible black on black.""""",title+description
TIMOB-15070,12,"""iOS7: Camera - Video record - video exit when  using reverse and forward controls""","""""""*not a regression* occurs in 3.1.2.GA as well.  *NOT in iOS6*    While testing KS> >Phone> Camera> Video Record,  I encountered an issue after taking a video and playing it back, when using forward and reverse controls forse video to exit. Black screen is the result.    Steps to reproduce:  1. KS>Phone>Camera>Video Record  2. After stop recording press forward or reverse controls    Actual result:  Black screen.  If this log can help:    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Camera - Video record - video exit when using reverse and forward controls
