TIMOB-14989,12,"""Code Processor: Investigate efficacy of multi-pass analysis""","""""""To aid in increasing the accuracy of the code processor, a multi-pass mechanism could be implemented that will attempt to determine all of the functions in the project and where they are called from. This information will be fed into the final pass, which is the current implementation of the code processor. This information should help greatly in solving the following:    which currently reports less than 100% coverage because either a or b will be unvisited. The information from the previous passes can be fed into the code processor so we can determine that b was called from the skipped block, and thus we can mark it as skipped.""""""",Story,"Title: Code Processor: Investigate efficacy of multi-pass analysis
Description: """"To aid in increasing the accuracy of the code processor, a multi-pass mechanism could be implemented that will attempt to determine all of the functions in the project and where they are called from. This information will be fed into the final pass, which is the current implementation of the code processor. This information should help greatly in solving the following: which currently reports less than 100% coverage because either a or b will be unvisited. The information from the previous passes can be fed into the code processor so we can determine that b was called from the skipped block, and thus we can mark it as skipped.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14988,12,"""iOS: Error when opening a modal window : """"NSCFString charValue: unrecognized selector""""""","""""""h5. Update  The issue is related to the fact the opened window is modal.  Attached a small sample code showing the issue.      h5. Problem description    'Journal' Alloy sample app (https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/models/journal) is throwing an exception on iOS when using TiSDK 3.1.3 (tested using latest 3.1.3.v20130828104626).    On Android it works as expected.    The issue seems to be reproducible only using 3.1.3SDK - Alloy version is the latest GA.  Using TiSDK 3.1.2.GA and Alloy 1.2.1.GA it works as expected on iOS.      h5. Steps to reproduce  1. Grab the Alloy model sample 'Journal' (attached the whole project).  2. Run on device or emulator (tested on a Iphone 5 with iOS 6.1.4 and on iPhone simulator version 6.0/Xcode4.6 and 7.0/Xcode5)  3. Run the app and click on the 'add entry' button    Result: Application Error red-screen is shown (see screenshot).    Error log:      Full log attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Error when opening a modal window : """"NSCFString charValue: unrecognized selector""""
Description: """"h5. Update The issue is related to the fact the opened window is modal. Attached a small sample code showing the issue. h5. Problem description 'Journal' Alloy sample app (https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/master/test/apps/models/journal) is throwing an exception on iOS when using TiSDK 3.1.3 (tested using latest 3.1.3.v20130828104626). On Android it works as expected. The issue seems to be reproducible only using 3.1.3SDK - Alloy version is the latest GA. Using TiSDK 3.1.2.GA and Alloy 1.2.1.GA it works as expected on iOS. h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Grab the Alloy model sample 'Journal' (attached the whole project). 2. Run on device or emulator (tested on a Iphone 5 with iOS 6.1.4 and on iPhone simulator version 6.0/Xcode4.6 and 7.0/Xcode5) 3. Run the app and click on the 'add entry' button Result: Application Error red-screen is shown (see screenshot). Error log: Full log attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14987,12,"""TiAPI: Add getRow* related functions to TableViewRow""","""""""It would be very nice to have the folowing functions on TableViewRow  getRowCount() return the totoal number of rows - for iteration  getRow(index) return row for index - for iteration  getRows() return array of all rows - for iteration  getRowIndex(row) get the index of a row - deleteRow()/updateRow() ect. takes index  """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Add getRow* related functions to TableViewRow
Description: """"It would be very nice to have the folowing functions on TableViewRow getRowCount() return the totoal number of rows - for iteration getRow(index) return row for index - for iteration getRows() return array of all rows - for iteration getRowIndex(row) get the index of a row - deleteRow()/updateRow() ect. takes index """"",title+description
TIMOB-14986,12,"""iOS7: Support separatorInsets property""","""""""h3. Expected results    TableView in Window in Tab with left:0 (or no left value set) would be left-aligned to its parent as is the case with iOS6.    h3. Actual results    As shown in the attached screenshot, the tableview is inset from the left edge of the screen.     Project is https://github.com/<USER>training/tcd_training/tree/master/labcode/Finished/05_alloy""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS7: Support separatorInsets property
