TIMOB-14955,12,"""BlackBerry: Build fails after updating to 10.2 as it can't find bbndk-env.sh file""","""""""Description:  1. Download the new BB 10.2 momentics on your machine  2. From the momentics preferences download the desired BB NDK    h4. On MAC OSX:  1. The new BB NDK will get downloaded in the packaged contents of the momentics app.  2. Point both appcel studio & titanium studio to the path '/Applications/Momentics.app/'  3. Build/Run an app for BB simulator/device    Actual results:  1. We get the following errors in the console:      Expected Result:  1. The build/run should happen successfully     h4. On Win 7 & 8:  1. The new BB NDK will get downloaded in 'C:/bbndk'  2. Point both appcel studio & titanium studio to the path 'C:/bbndk'  3. Build/Run an app for BB simulator/device    Actual results:  1. We get the following errors in the console:      Expected Result:  1. The build/run should happen successfully       """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Build fails after updating to 10.2 as it can't find bbndk-env.sh file
Description: """"Description: 1. Download the new BB 10.2 momentics on your machine 2. From the momentics preferences download the desired BB NDK h4. On MAC OSX: 1. The new BB NDK will get downloaded in the packaged contents of the momentics app. 2. Point both appcel studio & titanium studio to the path '/Applications/Momentics.app/' 3. Build/Run an app for BB simulator/device Actual results: 1. We get the following errors in the console: Expected Result: 1. The build/run should happen successfully h4. On Win 7 & 8: 1. The new BB NDK will get downloaded in 'C:/bbndk' 2. Point both appcel studio & titanium studio to the path 'C:/bbndk' 3. Build/Run an app for BB simulator/device Actual results: 1. We get the following errors in the console: Expected Result: 1. The build/run should happen successfully """"",title+description
TIMOB-14954,12,"""iOS: ASI HTTP Library converts DELETE requests to POST requests""","""""""The ASIHTTP lib converts DELETE requests to POST.  Reference the file here:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/ASI/ASIHTTPRequest.m#L561    Per a typical RESTful service, DELETE is a normal verb used for...deleting a resource.  This needs to be supported.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ASI HTTP Library converts DELETE requests to POST requests
Description: """"The ASIHTTP lib converts DELETE requests to POST. Reference the file here: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/ASI/ASIHTTPRequest.m#L561 Per a typical RESTful service, DELETE is a normal verb used for...deleting a resource. This needs to be supported.""""",title+description
