TIMOB-14939,12,"""Android: POST method does not work""","""""""*Test case*        test.php      test.php print_r the $_POST and the $_GET arrays. On the screenshot I attached you can see the android code does not send POST Data correctly.    BUT    the strengest thing is, if you send a request to this file:    http://<USER>com/test.php?testget=1    its only printing the $_POST (but it doesn't metter)    you get a correct response.    First I was thinking it might be a server problem, but the iOS App send data correctly to both servers.    <sdk-version>3.2.0.v20130522185622</sdk-version>  <sdk-version>3.1.0.GA</sdk-version>""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: POST method does not work
