TIMOB-14938,12,"""iOS: VideoPlayer Timeline and Navigation Bar mispositioned after using Fullscreen mode (Tabgroup)""","""""""h6.Problem  VideoPlayer time bar and navigation bar are mispositioned. Using TiUITabgroup follow reproduction steps:    h6.Steps to reproduce  First, click the video so the control bar shows.  Second, change orientation.   Third, you'll see the time bar mispositioned.   Forth, close the video player, the tab group navigation bar is mispositioned too. e.g. Screen shoot attached. On iPad, if you change orientation during splash screen, you'll see the same issue.    h6.Simple sample      h6.tiapp.xml  Support orientations so app can rotate along with device  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: VideoPlayer Timeline and Navigation Bar mispositioned after using Fullscreen mode (Tabgroup)
Description: """"h6.Problem VideoPlayer time bar and navigation bar are mispositioned. Using TiUITabgroup follow reproduction steps: h6.Steps to reproduce First, click the video so the control bar shows. Second, change orientation. Third, you'll see the time bar mispositioned. Forth, close the video player, the tab group navigation bar is mispositioned too. e.g. Screen shoot attached. On iPad, if you change orientation during splash screen, you'll see the same issue. h6.Simple sample h6.tiapp.xml Support orientations so app can rotate along with device """"",title+description
TIMOB-14937,12,"""iOS 7: NavigationGroup on Tab displays windows with wrong height""","""""""*Steps to Reproduce*  1. Create new mobile project (Alloy)  2. Paste attached index.xml into project  3. Run project    *Actual Result*  When running in iOS 7, the blue window in the NavigationGroup is displayed with wrong height. It works on iOS 6.    *Expected Result*  The blue window int the NavigationGroup should fill the tab.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 7: NavigationGroup on Tab displays windows with wrong height
Description: """"*Steps to Reproduce* 1. Create new mobile project (Alloy) 2. Paste attached index.xml into project 3. Run project *Actual Result* When running in iOS 7, the blue window in the NavigationGroup is displayed with wrong height. It works on iOS 6. *Expected Result* The blue window int the NavigationGroup should fill the tab.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14936,12,"""iOS7: Titanium.UI.Tab icon and activeIcon issue and proposed selectedIcon""","""""""According to ios7 UIKit User Interface Catalog under Tab Bars:  Each item in a tab bar can have a custom selected image and unselected image. You can specify these images when you initialize a tab bar item using the initWithTitle:image:selectedImage: method.    When you look at the bundled ios7 apps from Apple, you'll notice that they use outline icons for the unselected tabs, and then the icon subtly changes to a new image for the selected tab. This is an important feature of ios7 tabs.    sdk 3.1.2 has properties for icon and activeIcon, though the activeIcon doesn't work. If you specify the activeIcon, then you get a non-tinted icon that acts as both the icon and activeIcon. In effect, you never see the activeIcon image, just the icon without tinting.    Ideally there would be icon and selectedIcon properties and let ios7 do the coloring/tinting.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Titanium.UI.Tab icon and activeIcon issue and proposed selectedIcon
Description: """"According to ios7 UIKit User Interface Catalog under Tab Bars: Each item in a tab bar can have a custom selected image and unselected image. You can specify these images when you initialize a tab bar item using the initWithTitle:image:selectedImage: method. When you look at the bundled ios7 apps from Apple, you'll notice that they use outline icons for the unselected tabs, and then the icon subtly changes to a new image for the selected tab. This is an important feature of ios7 tabs. sdk 3.1.2 has properties for icon and activeIcon, though the activeIcon doesn't work. If you specify the activeIcon, then you get a non-tinted icon that acts as both the icon and activeIcon. In effect, you never see the activeIcon image, just the icon without tinting. Ideally there would be icon and selectedIcon properties and let ios7 do the coloring/tinting. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14935,12,"""Android: Application restarts on 'orientationChange' when applied holo theme on Modal windows""","""""""Application restarts/crashes when we change orientation(either `portrait` to `landscape` or `landscape` to `portrait`) when applied holo theme to the modal windows.  Here is the test case:    1. copy the code in `app.js`:      2. Modify the tiapp.xml for <android></android>      3. Tested with placing `themes.xml` under `platform/android/res/values` and found the same issue.  themes.xml      Note : In `app.js`, two different windows showing two different behaviors in 'orientationChange'. Normal window works fine with holo theme.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Application restarts on 'orientationChange' when applied holo theme on Modal windows
Description: """"Application restarts/crashes when we change orientation(either `portrait` to `landscape` or `landscape` to `portrait`) when applied holo theme to the modal windows. Here is the test case: 1. copy the code in `app.js`: 2. Modify the tiapp.xml for <android></android> 3. Tested with placing `themes.xml` under `platform/android/res/values` and found the same issue. themes.xml Note : In `app.js`, two different windows showing two different behaviors in 'orientationChange'. Normal window works fine with holo theme. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14934,12,"""Android: WebView: the pause button does not work when playing a youtube video on 4.0 devices""","""""""*Note:* This issue only happens on 4.0 devices. It does not happen on 2.3, 3.2, 4.1, 4.2, 4.3 devices.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the test case.  2. Click the play button. Should see the video starts playing.  3. Click the pause button.  Expected behavior: The video should be paused.  Actual behavior: The video is still playing.  Test case:    Please enable Settings->Developer options->Force GPU rendering, and add    to the tiapp.xml.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView: the pause button does not work when playing a youtube video on 4.0 devices
Description: """"*Note:* This issue only happens on 4.0 devices. It does not happen on 2.3, 3.2, 4.1, 4.2, 4.3 devices. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the test case. 2. Click the play button. Should see the video starts playing. 3. Click the pause button. Expected behavior: The video should be paused. Actual behavior: The video is still playing. Test case: Please enable Settings->Developer options->Force GPU rendering, and add to the tiapp.xml.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14932,12,"""Code analyzer should recommend platform specific enhancements""","""""""Code analyzer should recommend platform specific enhancements    Would be nice enhancement for Code Analyzer to help folks know of key features that the developer did not leverage in their app. For example, when you run Code Analyzer and select Android it would be nice to flag that the Menu and Heavyweight window is not being utilized.    Today, on a prospect call, a developer asked if we """"""""handle"""""""" Android menu automatically because this developer is an iOS developer and wouldn't necessarily know that Android and BB have a menu feature so how would they know that they need to deal with it.    My thought is that some of our best practice and device knowledge can be exposed to the developer when they run a code analysis.    I hope this makes sense.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Code analyzer should recommend platform specific enhancements
Description: """"Code analyzer should recommend platform specific enhancements Would be nice enhancement for Code Analyzer to help folks know of key features that the developer did not leverage in their app. For example, when you run Code Analyzer and select Android it would be nice to flag that the Menu and Heavyweight window is not being utilized. Today, on a prospect call, a developer asked if we """"""""handle"""""""" Android menu automatically because this developer is an iOS developer and wouldn't necessarily know that Android and BB have a menu feature so how would they know that they need to deal with it. My thought is that some of our best practice and device knowledge can be exposed to the developer when they run a code analysis. I hope this makes sense.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14929,12,"""iOS7: Ti.Platform.openURL does not work properly on iOS7 and iTunes links""","""""""h2. Problem description  In some cases, iOS7 does not properly open the iTunes links using Ti.Platform.openURL. It looks like the device fails to open the link if the country code is not correct. Tested using MobileWeb.    h2. Steps to reproduce  Create a MobileWeb app with this code:        When clicking the button on Safari on iOS7, the store is not opened. Seems to work fine on my device if I remove the country code.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Ti.Platform.openURL does not work properly on iOS7 and iTunes links
