TIMOB-14877,12,"""Liveview: Unable to launch liveview enable session for device or emulator on windows""","""""""h5. Description:  When trying to launch a liveview instance on Windows 7 in the emulator, the command was unrecognized and the launch failed. Here is the console output:      Subsequent attempts on device also failed with the same error. Attempts on our windows 8 machines also failed with the same error on device and emulator.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Ensure the plugin version of liveview is uninstalled  2) Update to the latest RC studio version for windows  3) Launch an emulator or device build with liveview enabled    h5. Result:  Failure to install/launch and errors in the console    h5. Expected Result:  Emulator or device build launches, liveview event/file servers working, liveview functions as expected on device or emulator.""""""",Bug,"Title: Liveview: Unable to launch liveview enable session for device or emulator on windows
Description: """"h5. Description: When trying to launch a liveview instance on Windows 7 in the emulator, the command was unrecognized and the launch failed. Here is the console output: Subsequent attempts on device also failed with the same error. Attempts on our windows 8 machines also failed with the same error on device and emulator. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Ensure the plugin version of liveview is uninstalled 2) Update to the latest RC studio version for windows 3) Launch an emulator or device build with liveview enabled h5. Result: Failure to install/launch and errors in the console h5. Expected Result: Emulator or device build launches, liveview event/file servers working, liveview functions as expected on device or emulator.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14875,12,"""Android: HTTP requests generate SkImageDecoder message for non-image responses""","""""""HTTP requests that return non-image data (e.g. content-type of 'application/json') are processing the content as potential images and thus are generating extraneous messages in the console saying """"""""SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null"""""""". This is also adding overhead to every non-image HTTP request (albeit minor).    I tracked it down to the 'loadBitmapInfo' method that is called in 'blobFromData' (line 182 in TiBlob.java), which is called from 'handleEntityData' (line 358 in TiHTTPClient.java). It looks like the logic on line 216 in TiBlob.java is incorrect:        Should be        What is happening is that 'guessContentTypeFromStream' is returning null for 'application/json' type data (which is correct, but it means that 'mt' is null) and it ends up thinking that the data should be processed as an image, when in fact the mimetype value is 'application/json' and thus should not be processed as a potential image.    Looks like the wrong variable is being checked on line 216 of TiBlob.java. I did a quick test and changed the logic to the latter and the warning messages went away.    To reproduce:    1) Issue an Ti.Network.HTTPClient request that returns JSON text    Note in the log the """"""""SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null"""""""" message  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTP requests generate SkImageDecoder message for non-image responses
Description: """"HTTP requests that return non-image data (e.g. content-type of 'application/json') are processing the content as potential images and thus are generating extraneous messages in the console saying """"""""SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null"""""""". This is also adding overhead to every non-image HTTP request (albeit minor). I tracked it down to the 'loadBitmapInfo' method that is called in 'blobFromData' (line 182 in TiBlob.java), which is called from 'handleEntityData' (line 358 in TiHTTPClient.java). It looks like the logic on line 216 in TiBlob.java is incorrect: Should be What is happening is that 'guessContentTypeFromStream' is returning null for 'application/json' type data (which is correct, but it means that 'mt' is null) and it ends up thinking that the data should be processed as an image, when in fact the mimetype value is 'application/json' and thus should not be processed as a potential image. Looks like the wrong variable is being checked on line 216 of TiBlob.java. I did a quick test and changed the logic to the latter and the warning messages went away. To reproduce: 1) Issue an Ti.Network.HTTPClient request that returns JSON text Note in the log the """"""""SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null"""""""" message """"",title+description
TIMOB-14874,12,"""Socket: Server and client example - Runtime Error listening socket output - fix test case""","""""""Not a regression.  Test steps:  1. Install and run KS> Platform> Sockets> Server and client example    Actual result:  Runtime error (see attached files)  Expected result:  No Error""""""",Bug,"Title: Socket: Server and client example - Runtime Error listening socket output - fix test case
Description: """"Not a regression. Test steps: 1. Install and run KS> Platform> Sockets> Server and client example Actual result: Runtime error (see attached files) Expected result: No Error""""",title+description
TIMOB-14873,12,"""Android: Ti.Geolocation's HeadingData is based on deprecated feature""","""""""HeadingData uses Orientation sensor that was deprecated in Android 2.2.  http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/sensors/sensors_position.html  Isn't it time to implement new approach?  It would also be good if we could get rotation matrix from HeadingData as that would resolve many problems related to augmented reality apps at once.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Ti.Geolocation's HeadingData is based on deprecated feature
Description: """"HeadingData uses Orientation sensor that was deprecated in Android 2.2. http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/sensors/sensors_position.html Isn't it time to implement new approach? It would also be good if we could get rotation matrix from HeadingData as that would resolve many problems related to augmented reality apps at once.""""",title+description
