TIMOB-14651,12,"""Android: Add support for HttpClient Cookie Path Validation""","""""""h6.Feature Request  To add the ability to custom Cookie management for HttpClient Path Validation. To achieve this Titanium could allow to custom cookie policy and registering their own cookie support.    h6.Rationale  When the server is setting a cookie with an invalid path and HttpClient is properly rejecting the cookie. According to the RFC spec, a server must set the cookie path using the URL path, or an ancestor path.     h6.Use case  On Titanium abort a XHR tears down underlying TCP connection which forces client to accept cookies.    h6.Stack Trace      To avoid this Browsers can ignore the spec and just accept the cookie.    h6.Additional details  For example, when accessing http://foo.com/a/b/, the server may set a cookie with path /a/b/, /a, or /, but not /a/c.  But since most all browsers (I only checked Firefox) ignore the spec and accept the cookie, I need HttpClient to do the same.    Similar discussion: http://highaltitudedev.blogspot.mx/2011/03/httpclient-cookie-path-validation.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add support for HttpClient Cookie Path Validation
Description: """"h6.Feature Request To add the ability to custom Cookie management for HttpClient Path Validation. To achieve this Titanium could allow to custom cookie policy and registering their own cookie support. h6.Rationale When the server is setting a cookie with an invalid path and HttpClient is properly rejecting the cookie. According to the RFC spec, a server must set the cookie path using the URL path, or an ancestor path. h6.Use case On Titanium abort a XHR tears down underlying TCP connection which forces client to accept cookies. h6.Stack Trace To avoid this Browsers can ignore the spec and just accept the cookie. h6.Additional details For example, when accessing http://foo.com/a/b/, the server may set a cookie with path /a/b/, /a, or /, but not /a/c. But since most all browsers (I only checked Firefox) ignore the spec and accept the cookie, I need HttpClient to do the same. Similar discussion: http://highaltitudedev.blogspot.mx/2011/03/httpclient-cookie-path-validation.html""""",title+description
TIMOB-14648,12,"""iOS: Consider using a library other than asi-http-request""","""""""I think this comment is rather worrying:    https://github.com/pokeb/asi-http-request/issues/368#issuecomment-21515820    """"""",Story,"Title: iOS: Consider using a library other than asi-http-request
