TIMOB-14640,12,"""Android: Kitchensink - TabGroups has 2 tabs but the label on the page states that TabGroup has 5 tabs""","""""""TabGroups has 2 tabs but the label on the page states that TabGroup has 5 tabs.  This is not regression since the issue occurs on 3.1.1 GA as well    Steps to reproduce:  1. Go to KS> BASE UI>TabGroups  2. Observe the screen    Actual:  There are two tabs on the screen but the label below states,"""""""" Tab Group has 5 tabs""""""""    Expected:  If there are two tabs, label should state that Tab Group has 2 tabs  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Kitchensink - TabGroups has 2 tabs but the label on the page states that TabGroup has 5 tabs
Description: """"TabGroups has 2 tabs but the label on the page states that TabGroup has 5 tabs. This is not regression since the issue occurs on 3.1.1 GA as well Steps to reproduce: 1. Go to KS> BASE UI>TabGroups 2. Observe the screen Actual: There are two tabs on the screen but the label below states,"""""""" Tab Group has 5 tabs"""""""" Expected: If there are two tabs, label should state that Tab Group has 2 tabs """"",title+description
TIMOB-14639,12,"""LiveView: running an app on iPad simulator with LiveView the second time causes error""","""""""Stephen saw an issue with one of his demo apps where the first time the app is run on iPad simulator with LiveView, it works fine, but the second time it is run, the following error occurs in the console:        Running """"""""killall node"""""""" from the command line will get iOS simulator back to a working state, but running the app twice will re-create the issue.  """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: running an app on iPad simulator with LiveView the second time causes error
Description: """"Stephen saw an issue with one of his demo apps where the first time the app is run on iPad simulator with LiveView, it works fine, but the second time it is run, the following error occurs in the console: Running """"""""killall node"""""""" from the command line will get iOS simulator back to a working state, but running the app twice will re-create the issue. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14636,12,"""LiveView: 'alloy compile' command is used to recompile the Alloy code without specifying the platform""","""""""h5. Problem description  When modifying an Alloy project, LiveView is triggering the 'alloy compile' command in order to recompile the Alloy code and then update the running app.  However, the correct compile command should be always passed specifying the platform, for ex. alloy compile --config platform=ios    For this reason, with Alloy 1.2.0, the 'alloy compile' command is returning an error and in this case LiveView is not working at all.       h5. Steps to reproduce  1. Modify an Alloy project running LiveView  Result: App is not updated.  Error log:  """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: 'alloy compile' command is used to recompile the Alloy code without specifying the platform
Description: """"h5. Problem description When modifying an Alloy project, LiveView is triggering the 'alloy compile' command in order to recompile the Alloy code and then update the running app. However, the correct compile command should be always passed specifying the platform, for ex. alloy compile --config platform=ios For this reason, with Alloy 1.2.0, the 'alloy compile' command is returning an error and in this case LiveView is not working at all. h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Modify an Alloy project running LiveView Result: App is not updated. Error log: """"",title+description
TIMOB-14635,12,"""Android: Default Titanium Tab App won't run on phone""","""""""h6.Steps to reproduce  Just create a Titanium Default Tab Application and install to Device.    h6.Expected results  App is able to launch and run    h6.Actual results   It shows the splash screen, displays the main screen for about a second and then shuts down.    h6.Reproducible  - Android Motorola Phone (logPhoneShutdown.txt attached)  Model #: MOTOROLA RAZRi  Android Version: 4.1.2  Kernel Version: 3.0.34-g261995f  Build Number: 9.8.2I-50_SMI-29.1359956748    h6.Not reproducible   Droid Razr 2.3.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Default Titanium Tab App won't run on phone
Description: """"h6.Steps to reproduce Just create a Titanium Default Tab Application and install to Device. h6.Expected results App is able to launch and run h6.Actual results It shows the splash screen, displays the main screen for about a second and then shuts down. h6.Reproducible - Android Motorola Phone (logPhoneShutdown.txt attached) Model #: MOTOROLA RAZRi Android Version: 4.1.2 Kernel Version: 3.0.34-g261995f Build Number: 9.8.2I-50_SMI-29.1359956748 h6.Not reproducible Droid Razr 2.3.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-14634,12,"""Android: Postlayout event does not fire on ImageViews that are in a ScrollableView""","""""""h6.Problem  I have x amount of ImageViews that are all different sizes. For each ImageView I have captions (labels) that overlay the image and the coords are set by a left/top percentage. The problem is the only way to currently retrieve these views is to get a reference to the currentview and call the toImage method to get the size. I would think by adding a post layout to each view or to the ScrollableView you should be able to get that views size when it is scrolled to.    h6.Snippet  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Postlayout event does not fire on ImageViews that are in a ScrollableView
Description: """"h6.Problem I have x amount of ImageViews that are all different sizes. For each ImageView I have captions (labels) that overlay the image and the coords are set by a left/top percentage. The problem is the only way to currently retrieve these views is to get a reference to the currentview and call the toImage method to get the size. I would think by adding a post layout to each view or to the ScrollableView you should be able to get that views size when it is scrolled to. h6.Snippet """"",title+description
TIMOB-14633,12,"""Liveview: Runtime error when loading KS""","""""""When running KS with liveview, I get a runtime error saying the backtrace field is undefined.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run liveview with KS on <USER>studio  2. As soon as you launch the app, you will see a runtime error saying:        Even if there is an uncaught exception, it shouldn't fail when logging it.  I'm guessing 'backtrace' isn't a valid field.""""""",Bug,"Title: Liveview: Runtime error when loading KS
Description: """"When running KS with liveview, I get a runtime error saying the backtrace field is undefined. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run liveview with KS on <USER>studio 2. As soon as you launch the app, you will see a runtime error saying: Even if there is an uncaught exception, it shouldn't fail when logging it. I'm guessing 'backtrace' isn't a valid field.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14631,12,"""BlackBerry: Not able to get e.source on click event for UI controls such as window, view, button etc""","""""""Not getting e.source on click event for UI controls.  Checked with view,button and window.      This is not a regression.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Make a test Project and replace app.js with the code given below.  2) Launch the app.  3) After the app gets launched. Click the button.      Actual Result: Do not get anything it just returns empty JSON as""""""""{}""""""""     Expected Result:It must return button properties as in ios and android.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Not able to get e.source on click event for UI controls such as window, view, button etc
