TIMOB-14630,12,"""Android: Modules: Can't package Android module in OSX 10.8""","""""""h6.Problem  When trying to package an android module to an app project I get an error about xcode commandline tools.    Yet it works just fine when doing it using ant  !http://i.imgur.com/cZFldlD.png!    h6.Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create an Android Module.  2. Package Android Module using ant, either from Studio or command line.    h6.Actual Result:  Error.    h6.Expected Result:  Android Module Packages.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Modules: Can't package Android module in OSX 10.8
Description: """"h6.Problem When trying to package an android module to an app project I get an error about xcode commandline tools. Yet it works just fine when doing it using ant !http://i.imgur.com/cZFldlD.png! h6.Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an Android Module. 2. Package Android Module using ant, either from Studio or command line. h6.Actual Result: Error. h6.Expected Result: Android Module Packages.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14629,12,"""CLI: iOS Symbols wrongly imported from metadata.json""","""""""h6.Issue  When you want a module to export symbols for the app build you create a metadata.json and put something like this in it  {""""""""exports"""""""": [""""""""Ti.Media""""""""]}    Now in CLI at [that|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L2760] line, symbols are wrongly imported because the """"""""Ti."""""""" should be first removed.    Consequently we get the wrong #define and we get link errors. The """"""""addSymbol"""""""" method should handle this with something like this:  - symbol = symbol.replace(/^(Ti|Titanium)./, """""""""""""""");    h6.PR  Actually the find symbols <USER>was very dirty for iOS.  Decided to clean it: https://github.com/Akylas/titanium_mobile/commit/79efdba3d89cd536c7e84d037a1126030d92dff9    I will create a PR if asked to do so""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS Symbols wrongly imported from metadata.json
Description: """"h6.Issue When you want a module to export symbols for the app build you create a metadata.json and put something like this in it {""""""""exports"""""""": [""""""""Ti.Media""""""""]} Now in CLI at [that|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/cli/commands/_build.js#L2760] line, symbols are wrongly imported because the """"""""Ti."""""""" should be first removed. Consequently we get the wrong #define and we get link errors. The """"""""addSymbol"""""""" method should handle this with something like this: - symbol = symbol.replace(/^(Ti|Titanium)./, """"""""""""""""); h6.PR Actually the find symbols <USER>was very dirty for iOS. Decided to clean it: https://github.com/Akylas/titanium_mobile/commit/79efdba3d89cd536c7e84d037a1126030d92dff9 I will create a PR if asked to do so""""",title+description
TIMOB-14628,12,"""MobileWeb: Data with JSON mime type seen as binary ""","""""""When reading in a file that has a mime type of """"""""application/json"""""""", the contents are seen as binary and then cannot be parsed correctly.    I created pull request 4465 to fix this issue:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/4465  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Data with JSON mime type seen as binary
Description: """"When reading in a file that has a mime type of """"""""application/json"""""""", the contents are seen as binary and then cannot be parsed correctly. I created pull request 4465 to fix this issue: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/4465 """"",title+description
TIMOB-14627,12,"""Android: Expose the constant """"android.intent.action.PHONE_STATE""""""","""""""Sometimes the developers want to know the call state of the phone, eg. incoming call ringing, like the situation described in TIMOB-1608.  Need to expose [ACTION_PHONE_STATE_CHANGED|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#ACTION_PHONE_STATE_CHANGED], [EXTRA_STATE|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE], [EXTRA_STATE_IDLE|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE_IDLE], [EXTRA_STATE_OFFHOOK|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE_OFFHOOK] and [EXTRA_STATE_RINGING|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE_RINGING].  Here is the [test case|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-1608#comment-262736].""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose the constant """"android.intent.action.PHONE_STATE""""
Description: """"Sometimes the developers want to know the call state of the phone, eg. incoming call ringing, like the situation described in TIMOB-1608. Need to expose [ACTION_PHONE_STATE_CHANGED|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#ACTION_PHONE_STATE_CHANGED], [EXTRA_STATE|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE], [EXTRA_STATE_IDLE|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE_IDLE], [EXTRA_STATE_OFFHOOK|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE_OFFHOOK] and [EXTRA_STATE_RINGING|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#EXTRA_STATE_RINGING]. Here is the [test case|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-1608#comment-262736].""""",title+description
