TIMOB-14616,12,"""iOS: Ti.Calendar.getEventsInMonth uses 1-based months instead of 0-based""","""""""h6.Issue  Ti.Calendar.getEventsInMonth (and presumably its other variants) expect a 1-based month number instead of 0-based on iOS (Android version uses 0-based).    h6.Sample   See a CalendarTestcase.zip attached.    This is the date I use to create the event:      And this is what it finds:      I.e. it finds the newly-created event looking for month 8. It should be the problem in one of the two functions. Best would be if the behaviour were the same across platforms, of course.    h6.Additional details  Moreover, the docs don't mention one should call event.save() after calendar.createEvent() in order to have the event be actually saved on iOS (Android doesn't need this).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Calendar.getEventsInMonth uses 1-based months instead of 0-based
Description: """"h6.Issue Ti.Calendar.getEventsInMonth (and presumably its other variants) expect a 1-based month number instead of 0-based on iOS (Android version uses 0-based). h6.Sample See a CalendarTestcase.zip attached. This is the date I use to create the event: And this is what it finds: I.e. it finds the newly-created event looking for month 8. It should be the problem in one of the two functions. Best would be if the behaviour were the same across platforms, of course. h6.Additional details Moreover, the docs don't mention one should call event.save() after calendar.createEvent() in order to have the event be actually saved on iOS (Android doesn't need this).""""",title+description
