TIMOB-14481,12,"""Android: Lack of keypass support when distributing to Android Market""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce Please check the problem and my solution in this URL: http://developer.<USER>com/question/152821/titanium-cli-command-line-option-to-pass-key-password-missing#answer-265287  You must add this support since deploying is useful daily sometimes. Thanks  h3. Actual Result If your keystore has keypass, Titanium doesn't support it and it's waiting at the last line ('… might take some time') forever. If you stop the build, you can see the 'error' message asking for missing keypass password.  h3. Expected Result All built-in without user manual terminal executing.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Lack of keypass support when distributing to Android Market
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce Please check the problem and my solution in this URL: http://developer.<USER>com/question/152821/titanium-cli-command-line-option-to-pass-key-password-missing#answer-265287 You must add this support since deploying is useful daily sometimes. Thanks h3. Actual Result If your keystore has keypass, Titanium doesn't support it and it's waiting at the last line ('… might take some time') forever. If you stop the build, you can see the 'error' message asking for missing keypass password. h3. Expected Result All built-in without user manual terminal executing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14480,12,"""TiAPI: Fire 'remove' event when a view is removed from it's parent""","""""""I would like to have a {{remove}} event fired when a view is removed from a parent, with the parent in {{e.parent}} or {{e.source}}.    This is particular useful if the removed view is provided by another controller and that controllers needs to cleanup.    Of course you could work around this by manually notifying the other controller that its view has been removed, but if it's a list of views you will need to keep references to all their providing controllers as well.    Just for the sake of feature symmetry... we could add {{add}} as well, allowing the providing controller to keep track of who's using it's view, possibly resetting state when removed and then added again. Or even taking a property of the parent (e.g. Window title) and use it on the view (re-display title there).""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Fire 'remove' event when a view is removed from it's parent
Description: """"I would like to have a {{remove}} event fired when a view is removed from a parent, with the parent in {{e.parent}} or {{e.source}}. This is particular useful if the removed view is provided by another controller and that controllers needs to cleanup. Of course you could work around this by manually notifying the other controller that its view has been removed, but if it's a list of views you will need to keep references to all their providing controllers as well. Just for the sake of feature symmetry... we could add {{add}} as well, allowing the providing controller to keep track of who's using it's view, possibly resetting state when removed and then added again. Or even taking a property of the parent (e.g. Window title) and use it on the view (re-display title there).""""",title+description
