TIMOB-14407,12,"""Android: Enable Android AVD Keyboard Support when Studio created an AVD""","""""""Enable Android AVD Keyboard Support when Studio created an AVD    When you create an AVD, by default Keyboard Support is not enabled and this makes it very difficult to enter characters because you cannot use the computer keyboard. Instead you must use the Android on screen keyboard.    You can edit the AVD and add this parameter set to """"""""yes"""""""" (see attached screen shot).    It would be nice if we could add this parameter when we create an AVD.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Enable Android AVD Keyboard Support when Studio created an AVD
Description: """"Enable Android AVD Keyboard Support when Studio created an AVD When you create an AVD, by default Keyboard Support is not enabled and this makes it very difficult to enter characters because you cannot use the computer keyboard. Instead you must use the Android on screen keyboard. You can edit the AVD and add this parameter set to """"""""yes"""""""" (see attached screen shot). It would be nice if we could add this parameter when we create an AVD.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14406,12,"""Node.ACS Bindings generated module causes script errors when response header is undefined""","""""""h3. Steps to Reproduce  1) Create a new project 2) Create a new Node.ACS service 3) Create a new Node.ACS method - it should be based on HTTP GET and return no value as part of the response 4) Import Node.ACS Bindings 5) make a call to the method via the Node.ACS binding created  Note: See workaround in the image attached   h3. Actual Result Invoke function errors out since the call xhr.getResponseHeader returns undefined, preventing the callback function from being called.  h3. Expected Result InvokeService function should make the call to the node.ACS service and fire off the callback""""""",Bug,"Title: Node.ACS Bindings generated module causes script errors when response header is undefined
Description: """"h3. Steps to Reproduce 1) Create a new project 2) Create a new Node.ACS service 3) Create a new Node.ACS method - it should be based on HTTP GET and return no value as part of the response 4) Import Node.ACS Bindings 5) make a call to the method via the Node.ACS binding created Note: See workaround in the image attached h3. Actual Result Invoke function errors out since the call xhr.getResponseHeader returns undefined, preventing the callback function from being called. h3. Expected Result InvokeService function should make the call to the node.ACS service and fire off the callback""""",title+description
