TIMOB-14404,12,"""iOS: PLAIN style button has no border margin when height/width = SIZE""","""""""*Problem*  When a button with {{height: Ti.UI.SIZE, width: Ti.UI.SIZE}} uses the default {{style}}, the auto-sized button has a margin around the text. When it use a style of {{PLAIN}}, there is no margin around the text. Both scenarios should have the same auto-size behavior. At least I hope this isn't by design, because otherwise there is effectively no useful auto-size feature with PLAIN buttons.    *app.js*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: PLAIN style button has no border margin when height/width = SIZE
Description: """"*Problem* When a button with {{height: Ti.UI.SIZE, width: Ti.UI.SIZE}} uses the default {{style}}, the auto-sized button has a margin around the text. When it use a style of {{PLAIN}}, there is no margin around the text. Both scenarios should have the same auto-size behavior. At least I hope this isn't by design, because otherwise there is effectively no useful auto-size feature with PLAIN buttons. *app.js* """"",title+description
TIMOB-14403,12,"""iOS7: Slider - slider, added to title, navbar or toolbar, does not respond to touch ""","""""""Sliders, added to Navbar, Toolbar and Title do not respond to touch, as expected.    Test steps:  1. Install and run KS> Cotrols> Slider> Basic  2. Toggle Slider in Navbar,Toggle Slider in Toolbar, Toggle Slider in Title  3. Try to move sliders' thumbs    Actual result:  Sliders do not respond to touch    Expected:  A value of sliders should be changed """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS7: Slider - slider, added to title, navbar or toolbar, does not respond to touch
