TIMOB-14351,12,"""Android: TTC files not supported for custom fonts""","""""""h2. Problem description  When using a TTC (TrueType Collection) file on Android, only the regular font seems to be taken in account. Applying a 'bold' effect on the font does not use the 'bold' variant inside the file. The same works fine on iOS.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Need a TTC font that contains both regular and bold  2. create an Alloy app and configure it to support the custom font added  3. Create the following index.xml      4. Use the following index.tss:    5. Run the app on both platforms  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TTC files not supported for custom fonts
Description: """"h2. Problem description When using a TTC (TrueType Collection) file on Android, only the regular font seems to be taken in account. Applying a 'bold' effect on the font does not use the 'bold' variant inside the file. The same works fine on iOS. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Need a TTC font that contains both regular and bold 2. create an Alloy app and configure it to support the custom font added 3. Create the following index.xml 4. Use the following index.tss: 5. Run the app on both platforms """"",title+description
