TIMOB-14310,12,"""Allow either the Code Analyzer or Static Code Analysis Engine to be extensible to 3rd Parties""","""""""Partners and customers should be able to add to our code analysis engines.  Either the Dynamic Code Analyzer or our static code analysis.  One or both of these engines should be extensible.  We will never be able to provide all the functionality that customers want:  Ex. Security checks, performance analysis, code formatting, depth level of call stacks, etc...    So we should allow 3rd parties or customers to add to the rules engine.  This will provide added value to the platform, plus add our open and extensible claims""""""",Story,"Title: Allow either the Code Analyzer or Static Code Analysis Engine to be extensible to 3rd Parties
Description: """"Partners and customers should be able to add to our code analysis engines. Either the Dynamic Code Analyzer or our static code analysis. One or both of these engines should be extensible. We will never be able to provide all the functionality that customers want: Ex. Security checks, performance analysis, code formatting, depth level of call stacks, etc... So we should allow 3rd parties or customers to add to the rules engine. This will provide added value to the platform, plus add our open and extensible claims""""",title+description
