TIMOB-14299,12,"""Android does not respect opacity: 0 / opacity: 1 property""","""""""On Android device, views with Opacity: 0 are shown and views that had an animation turn their opacity to 1, do not become visible again when setting their opacity to 1. They do become visible again if another animation changes their opacity to the desired value.    To sum it up:  Animation works both ways.    Setting view's opacity to 0 on creation, doesn't work. Setting later a view's opacity to 1 (myView.opacity = 1) doesn't work either.    *Test case*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android does not respect opacity: 0 / opacity: 1 property
Description: """"On Android device, views with Opacity: 0 are shown and views that had an animation turn their opacity to 1, do not become visible again when setting their opacity to 1. They do become visible again if another animation changes their opacity to the desired value. To sum it up: Animation works both ways. Setting view's opacity to 0 on creation, doesn't work. Setting later a view's opacity to 1 (myView.opacity = 1) doesn't work either. *Test case* """"",title+description
