TIMOB-14295,12,"""Mobileweb: properties set to """"null"""" are assigned as  """"undefined"""" on proxy objects""","""""""h2. problem    On Mobileweb, if I assign {{null}} to a proxy property and then attempt to access that property, it will return {{undefined}}. This is a parity issue as under the same circumstances iOS and Android will return {{null}}. This was uncovered during Alloy unit testing of adding/removing style classes on proxy objects.    h2. expected    When a Titanium proxy object is assigned a property with the value of {{null}}, accessing that property should also return {{null}}, not {{undefined}}.    h2. test case      h2. output  h4. iOS 6.1 iPhone sim      h4. Android 2.3.3 HVGA emulator      h4. Mobileweb + chrome  """"""",Bug,"Title: Mobileweb: properties set to """"null"""" are assigned as """"undefined"""" on proxy objects
Description: """"h2. problem On Mobileweb, if I assign {{null}} to a proxy property and then attempt to access that property, it will return {{undefined}}. This is a parity issue as under the same circumstances iOS and Android will return {{null}}. This was uncovered during Alloy unit testing of adding/removing style classes on proxy objects. h2. expected When a Titanium proxy object is assigned a property with the value of {{null}}, accessing that property should also return {{null}}, not {{undefined}}. h2. test case h2. output h4. iOS 6.1 iPhone sim h4. Android 2.3.3 HVGA emulator h4. Mobileweb + chrome """"",title+description
