TIMOB-14286,12,"""iOS: Calendar future occurrences are not deleted""","""""""h6.Issue  Developer is getting the first occurrence of the event and calling remove() on it. Although he has previously saved the event as event.save(Ti.Calendar.SPAN_FUTUREEVENTS); the future occurrences are not deleted; only the first one is. Attempt to remove the events likewise: event.remove(Ti.Calendar.SPAN_FUTUREEVENTS);    h6.Steps  (1) Run app and allow access to Calendar  (2) Click the first button then a new ical event is added.  (3) Now press the second button in order to delete this event and all the future events related to it. However only its first occurrence is successfully deleted.    h6.Simple sample      - Additional info  Object ID appears to be removed but future events are not. Device logs since simulator lacks the ability to browse the ical.      - Developer remarks  """"""""Paradoxically, trying to delete more than once (I refer to same event id) it successfully retrieves the event for some reason, although this event has been deleted from ical...""""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Calendar future occurrences are not deleted
Description: """"h6.Issue Developer is getting the first occurrence of the event and calling remove() on it. Although he has previously saved the event as event.save(Ti.Calendar.SPAN_FUTUREEVENTS); the future occurrences are not deleted; only the first one is. Attempt to remove the events likewise: event.remove(Ti.Calendar.SPAN_FUTUREEVENTS); h6.Steps (1) Run app and allow access to Calendar (2) Click the first button then a new ical event is added. (3) Now press the second button in order to delete this event and all the future events related to it. However only its first occurrence is successfully deleted. h6.Simple sample - Additional info Object ID appears to be removed but future events are not. Device logs since simulator lacks the ability to browse the ical. - Developer remarks """"""""Paradoxically, trying to delete more than once (I refer to same event id) it successfully retrieves the event for some reason, although this event has been deleted from ical...""""""""""""",title+description
