TIMOB-14270,12,"""Android: Add support for New Relic module""","""""""This change modifies the Android builder script to look for the New Relic module, and if present passes an additional argument to the dx command when it is called. This allows New Relic to do bytecode rewriting for instrumentation.    The Java agent argument to dx is passed via a temporary file to avoid issues the dx command has with spaces in file paths. This temporary file is cleaned up after dx runs.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Add support for New Relic module
Description: """"This change modifies the Android builder script to look for the New Relic module, and if present passes an additional argument to the dx command when it is called. This allows New Relic to do bytecode rewriting for instrumentation. The Java agent argument to dx is passed via a temporary file to avoid issues the dx command has with spaces in file paths. This temporary file is cleaned up after dx runs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14269,12,"""iOS 7: Several UI Feature Requests""","""""""Feature Request for the following:    - Tint Color property for all applicable UIKit Elements. If natively present in Ti, it reduces the dependancy on external modules, given that the tint color has become the most widely used property in iOS7 for UI Elements.    - Simple MACRO so developers can detect if the OS>=7. If lesser, they can adapt the UI accordingly to be suitable for previous OS UI Guidelines.    - UICollectionView: This has been long due. Over a year now. A separate module or natively available under Ti.UI.iPhone or similar.    - UIKit Dynamics (Low Priority)    - TextKit (Medium Priority)""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS 7: Several UI Feature Requests
Description: """"Feature Request for the following: - Tint Color property for all applicable UIKit Elements. If natively present in Ti, it reduces the dependancy on external modules, given that the tint color has become the most widely used property in iOS7 for UI Elements. - Simple MACRO so developers can detect if the OS>=7. If lesser, they can adapt the UI accordingly to be suitable for previous OS UI Guidelines. - UICollectionView: This has been long due. Over a year now. A separate module or natively available under Ti.UI.iPhone or similar. - UIKit Dynamics (Low Priority) - TextKit (Medium Priority)""""",title+description
TIMOB-14268,12,"""Android: Facebook Module in 3.1.1 has same version as in 3.1.0""","""""""The Facebook Android module was updated for 3.1.1, e.g. https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13738  but the module version number released with 3.1.1 is the same as earlier - 3.0.0  The """"""""new"""""""" module behaves differently (e.g. for login cancellation), but since the version number is the same it's breaking existing code. Please bring back the previous module (released with 3.1.0.GA) as 3.0.0, and re-release the new module under a higher version.  Thanks.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook Module in 3.1.1 has same version as in 3.1.0
Description: """"The Facebook Android module was updated for 3.1.1, e.g. https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13738 but the module version number released with 3.1.1 is the same as earlier - 3.0.0 The """"""""new"""""""" module behaves differently (e.g. for login cancellation), but since the version number is the same it's breaking existing code. Please bring back the previous module (released with 3.1.0.GA) as 3.0.0, and re-release the new module under a higher version. Thanks.""""",title+description
