TIMOB-14257,12,"""LiveView: Alloy Themes not respected when LiveView is enabled and a modification is made""","""""""h5. Problem description  Themes are no longer applied and respected when modifying an Alloy project with LiveView enabled.    h5. Steps to reproduce  1. Run an Alloy project using themes. Tested has been made with https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/1_1_X/test/apps/advanced/themes  2. Run on the Android emulator enabling LiveView  3. Modify some code, for example the     in the 'views/index.xml' file, modify it in:      Result: App is reloaded and the modification is applied, however Themes are no longer applied.     See screenshots - before and after modification.    """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Alloy Themes not respected when LiveView is enabled and a modification is made
Description: """"h5. Problem description Themes are no longer applied and respected when modifying an Alloy project with LiveView enabled. h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Run an Alloy project using themes. Tested has been made with https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/1_1_X/test/apps/advanced/themes 2. Run on the Android emulator enabling LiveView 3. Modify some code, for example the in the 'views/index.xml' file, modify it in: Result: App is reloaded and the modification is applied, however Themes are no longer applied. See screenshots - before and after modification. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14255,12,"""iOS: TextField keyboard doesn't maintain number/symbol view when in TableView if TextField doesn't have height set""","""""""*Problem*  On iOS, when you create a Textfield that doesn't have a height set and then add it to a TableView, the keyboard doesn't perform the standard way. When you press the """""""".?123"""""""" key, it shows the number/symbol keyboard view.    *Actual result*  After pressing one key it goes back automatically to the """"""""ABC"""""""" keyboard, which provides for a poor UX when you want to type in multiple numbers.    *Expected result*  The default behavior is for it to stay in this keyboard view until you press """"""""ABC"""""""" to go back to the letters keyboard.    *Test case*      *Note*  Notice that the top textfield, which is not within the tableview, performs correctly. The textfield below that, which is within the tableview, doesn't maintain the """""""".?123"""""""" keyboard as you type.     *Workaround*  Add a height to the textfield within the tableview and then it will maintain the proper keyboard view.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TextField keyboard doesn't maintain number/symbol view when in TableView if TextField doesn't have height set
Description: """"*Problem* On iOS, when you create a Textfield that doesn't have a height set and then add it to a TableView, the keyboard doesn't perform the standard way. When you press the """""""".?123"""""""" key, it shows the number/symbol keyboard view. *Actual result* After pressing one key it goes back automatically to the """"""""ABC"""""""" keyboard, which provides for a poor UX when you want to type in multiple numbers. *Expected result* The default behavior is for it to stay in this keyboard view until you press """"""""ABC"""""""" to go back to the letters keyboard. *Test case* *Note* Notice that the top textfield, which is not within the tableview, performs correctly. The textfield below that, which is within the tableview, doesn't maintain the """""""".?123"""""""" keyboard as you type. *Workaround* Add a height to the textfield within the tableview and then it will maintain the proper keyboard view.""""",title+description
