TIMOB-14204,12,"""iOS: TextArea text invisible on iPad under certain circumstances""","""""""h2. Problem description  The text written in the TextArea becomes invisible under certain circumstances. See the sample code below:        The code as it is written, replicates the issue. However, it becomes fixed with the following changes:    1) uncomment the setTimeout - this will simulate a scrolling and the text becomes visible afterwards. Note that, if the ScrollView is long enough to scroll, the same happens by scrolling it manually.    2) removing the contentWidth in the ScrollView    3) removing the layout vertical from the Window    4) removing left and right from the TextArea  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TextArea text invisible on iPad under certain circumstances
Description: """"h2. Problem description The text written in the TextArea becomes invisible under certain circumstances. See the sample code below: The code as it is written, replicates the issue. However, it becomes fixed with the following changes: 1) uncomment the setTimeout - this will simulate a scrolling and the text becomes visible afterwards. Note that, if the ScrollView is long enough to scroll, the same happens by scrolling it manually. 2) removing the contentWidth in the ScrollView 3) removing the layout vertical from the Window 4) removing left and right from the TextArea """"",title+description
TIMOB-14202,12,"""LiveView: Field service app doesn't work with LiveView""","""""""Field service app doesn't work with enabled liveview.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Import the field service app to the project explorer.  2. Enable liveview and run the app on iOS simulator.  3. Click 'login' button.  4. An alert is dispalyed with the message,""""""""Would you like to generate a demo user?""""""""  5. Make changes in the code and change the alert message. Save the app.    Expected:  The changes should reflect in the simulator.    Actual:  An script Error is observed in console and the app hangs at login button. Error logs are as below:    ERROR] :  Script Error {  [ERROR] :      backtrace = """"""""#0 loginClick() at :22"""""""";  [ERROR] :      line = 10;  [ERROR] :      message = """"""""'undefined' is not an object (evaluating 'Ti.UI.ActivityIndicatorStyle.DARK')"""""""";  [ERROR] :      name = TypeError;  [ERROR] :      sourceId = 200756288;  [ERROR] :  }    """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Field service app doesn't work with LiveView
Description: """"Field service app doesn't work with enabled liveview. Steps to reproduce: 1. Import the field service app to the project explorer. 2. Enable liveview and run the app on iOS simulator. 3. Click 'login' button. 4. An alert is dispalyed with the message,""""""""Would you like to generate a demo user?"""""""" 5. Make changes in the code and change the alert message. Save the app. Expected: The changes should reflect in the simulator. Actual: An script Error is observed in console and the app hangs at login button. Error logs are as below: ERROR] : Script Error { [ERROR] : backtrace = """"""""#0 loginClick() at :22""""""""; [ERROR] : line = 10; [ERROR] : message = """"""""'undefined' is not an object (evaluating 'Ti.UI.ActivityIndicatorStyle.DARK')""""""""; [ERROR] : name = TypeError; [ERROR] : sourceId = 200756288; [ERROR] : } """"",title+description
TIMOB-14200,12,"""Android: Date Picker and Time Picker change event not firing when value changed by pressing """"done"""" through keyboard""","""""""While using the keyboard to enter values in picker, and entering some value in last field then tapping done to dismiss the keyboard; the value though visible in the field (year column) but the picker's """"""""value"""""""" property does not reflects the same, and therefore selected value (on UI) is not reflected in the field above.  If the user taps on any other field, so that year field loose focus, changed value get registered and is set by the picker in the above text field.  This seems to be a defect at the SDK level. The same problem exists for TimePicker as well for the minute field.    Following is code snippet containing date picker code, same happens with time picker also:    ----------------------------------------  var moment = require('alloy/moment');      var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   exitOnClose : true,   layout : 'vertical',   width : Ti.UI.FILL,   height : Ti.UI.FILL,   backgroundColor:'white'  });    var text = Ti.UI.createTextField({   hintText : 'ENTER YOUR DATE OF BIRTH',   top : 10,   width : Ti.UI.SIZE,   height : 120,   left : 0  });    var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({   type : Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_DATE,   top : 50,   visible : false  });    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({   title : 'Select',   top : 100,   width:Ti.UI.SIZE,   height:Ti.UI.SIZE  })    text.addEventListener('click', function(e) {   picker.visible = true;  })    picker.addEventListener('change', function(e) {   Ti.API.info(""""""""User selected date: """""""" + e.value.toLocaleString());  });    button.addEventListener('click', function(e) {   var labelText = moment(picker.value.toString(), 'ddd MMM DD YYYY HH:mm:ss Z').format('MMMM DD, YYYY');   text.value = labelText;  });    win.add(text);  win.add(picker);  win.add(button);  win.open();  ----------------------------------------    Screenshots attached display the wrong value selected within the textField""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Date Picker and Time Picker change event not firing when value changed by pressing """"done"""" through keyboard
Description: """"While using the keyboard to enter values in picker, and entering some value in last field then tapping done to dismiss the keyboard; the value though visible in the field (year column) but the picker's """"""""value"""""""" property does not reflects the same, and therefore selected value (on UI) is not reflected in the field above. If the user taps on any other field, so that year field loose focus, changed value get registered and is set by the picker in the above text field. This seems to be a defect at the SDK level. The same problem exists for TimePicker as well for the minute field. Following is code snippet containing date picker code, same happens with time picker also: ---------------------------------------- var moment = require('alloy/moment'); var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ exitOnClose : true, layout : 'vertical', width : Ti.UI.FILL, height : Ti.UI.FILL, backgroundColor:'white' }); var text = Ti.UI.createTextField({ hintText : 'ENTER YOUR DATE OF BIRTH', top : 10, width : Ti.UI.SIZE, height : 120, left : 0 }); var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({ type : Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_DATE, top : 50, visible : false }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Select', top : 100, width:Ti.UI.SIZE, height:Ti.UI.SIZE }) text.addEventListener('click', function(e) { picker.visible = true; }) picker.addEventListener('change', function(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""User selected date: """""""" + e.value.toLocaleString()); }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e) { var labelText = moment(picker.value.toString(), 'ddd MMM DD YYYY HH:mm:ss Z').format('MMMM DD, YYYY'); text.value = labelText; }); win.add(text); win.add(picker); win.add(button); win.open(); ---------------------------------------- Screenshots attached display the wrong value selected within the textField""""",title+description
TIMOB-14199,12,"""Android: ImageView scaling not working""","""""""h2. Problem description  ImageViews does not scale the image properly on Android, when width is specified and the surrounding view has height=Ti.UI.SIZE, or when put into a TableViewRow  This works fine on IOS.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1) Create an empty Alloy project  2) Add the attached image to the assets directory  3) Use the following index.xml and run the app        In iOS the image is scaled properly.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView scaling not working
Description: """"h2. Problem description ImageViews does not scale the image properly on Android, when width is specified and the surrounding view has height=Ti.UI.SIZE, or when put into a TableViewRow This works fine on IOS. h2. Steps to reproduce 1) Create an empty Alloy project 2) Add the attached image to the assets directory 3) Use the following index.xml and run the app In iOS the image is scaled properly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14198,12,"""Android: Application is crashing on Android 4.2.x""","""""""Client App which is running fine on devices running Android version except 4.2.x.  Trying to install the app on android version 4.2.x device, crashes the app after some time.    **Steps to reproduce**  On the Android 4.2.x phone we launch the app and then do something like the following:    1) Scroll all the way down the list  2) Tap on Tab 2  3) Scroll down  4) Repeat steps 2-3 tapping the other tabs    After a few tab changes (~6), the app starts to slow down, clic clicking from tab to tab is not responsive and eventually app would crash.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Application is crashing on Android 4.2.x
Description: """"Client App which is running fine on devices running Android version except 4.2.x. Trying to install the app on android version 4.2.x device, crashes the app after some time. **Steps to reproduce** On the Android 4.2.x phone we launch the app and then do something like the following: 1) Scroll all the way down the list 2) Tap on Tab 2 3) Scroll down 4) Repeat steps 2-3 tapping the other tabs After a few tab changes (~6), the app starts to slow down, clic clicking from tab to tab is not responsive and eventually app would crash. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14196,12,"""Tizen: Apps don't progress beyond splash screen on device""","""""""Description:  1. Create an app for tizen in titanium or <USER>studio  2. Build & run the app on the tizen device  3. The app will launch automatically  4. Observe app behaviour    Actual Result:  1. The app gets stuck at appcel splash screen & does not go beyond it    Expected Result:  1. The app should go beyond the splash screen & not hang on it    Note : I have successfully flashed the tizen device to OS 2.1 so it rules out old OS 2.0 issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen: Apps don't progress beyond splash screen on device
Description: """"Description: 1. Create an app for tizen in titanium or <USER>studio 2. Build & run the app on the tizen device 3. The app will launch automatically 4. Observe app behaviour Actual Result: 1. The app gets stuck at appcel splash screen & does not go beyond it Expected Result: 1. The app should go beyond the splash screen & not hang on it Note : I have successfully flashed the tizen device to OS 2.1 so it rules out old OS 2.0 issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14195,12,"""Maps V2: Version and changelog should be incremented to show additions for new API""","""""""h5. Description:  We added an API for """"""""isGooglePlayServicesAvailable"""""""", but the changelog and module version remain unchanged. To avoid confusion and a possible overwrite of an existing 1.2.0 module folder in the SDK install location, we should rev the version.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Install SDK 3.1.1.v20130611153550  2) Navigate to your module install location (generally ~/Library/application support/titanium/modules/android/ti.map/  3) Examine the sample code line #4    h5. Result:  The version is 1.2.0 prior to the change, and 1.2.0 after. If line 4 contains the new API, then you have the latest version.  The change log does not reflect the changes to 1.2.0 (to include the new api)    h5. Expected Result:  Version is installed side-by-side with 1.2.0, has a unique version, and the changelog describes new API addition.""""""",Bug,"Title: Maps V2: Version and changelog should be incremented to show additions for new API
Description: """"h5. Description: We added an API for """"""""isGooglePlayServicesAvailable"""""""", but the changelog and module version remain unchanged. To avoid confusion and a possible overwrite of an existing 1.2.0 module folder in the SDK install location, we should rev the version. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install SDK 3.1.1.v20130611153550 2) Navigate to your module install location (generally ~/Library/application support/titanium/modules/android/ti.map/ 3) Examine the sample code line #4 h5. Result: The version is 1.2.0 prior to the change, and 1.2.0 after. If line 4 contains the new API, then you have the latest version. The change log does not reflect the changes to 1.2.0 (to include the new api) h5. Expected Result: Version is installed side-by-side with 1.2.0, has a unique version, and the changelog describes new API addition.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14192,12,"""Code Processor: FieldService App: """"ACS CREDENTIALS NOT SPECIFIED!"""" error is being reported""","""""""h5. Problem description  Running the Code Analyzer on the Field Service App, an """"""""ACS CREDENTIALS NOT SPECIFIED! (2 occurances)"""""""" error is reported in the Code Analyzer report.    h5. Steps to reproduce  1. Import the Field Service App  2. Be sure to have a Resources/app.js file present in the project folder (build/run once or create it manually - app.js could be also empty)  3. Run the Code Analyzer and check results.    Result: """"""""ACS CREDENTIALS NOT SPECIFIED! (2 occurances)"""""""" error is reported in the Code Analyzer report.  The File being pointed is the ti.cloud.js module itself.    See screenshot.""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Processor: FieldService App: """"ACS CREDENTIALS NOT SPECIFIED!"""" error is being reported
Description: """"h5. Problem description Running the Code Analyzer on the Field Service App, an """"""""ACS CREDENTIALS NOT SPECIFIED! (2 occurances)"""""""" error is reported in the Code Analyzer report. h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Import the Field Service App 2. Be sure to have a Resources/app.js file present in the project folder (build/run once or create it manually - app.js could be also empty) 3. Run the Code Analyzer and check results. Result: """"""""ACS CREDENTIALS NOT SPECIFIED! (2 occurances)"""""""" error is reported in the Code Analyzer report. The File being pointed is the ti.cloud.js module itself. See screenshot.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14191,12,"""Code Processor: Error messages from alloy recompile are not being displayed in studio""","""""""h5. Problem description  There might be some scenarios when Alloy is not able to compile for some user error - see sample.     These error messages are not being transmitted to studio    h5. Steps to reproduce  1. Run the sample code reported here (notice the <All> tag instead of <Alloy> at the beginning)    h6. index.xml    2. Run the code processor  Result: 'Code processor has encountered a problem. No output received.' error popup message is displayed.  3. Click on the 'details'.  Result: 'No output received' error message is displayed again and duplicated.     The alloy error messages should be displayed in studio""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Processor: Error messages from alloy recompile are not being displayed in studio
Description: """"h5. Problem description There might be some scenarios when Alloy is not able to compile for some user error - see sample. These error messages are not being transmitted to studio h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Run the sample code reported here (notice the <All> tag instead of <Alloy> at the beginning) h6. index.xml 2. Run the code processor Result: 'Code processor has encountered a problem. No output received.' error popup message is displayed. 3. Click on the 'details'. Result: 'No output received' error message is displayed again and duplicated. The alloy error messages should be displayed in studio""""",title+description
TIMOB-14190,12,"""BlackBerry: Window does not resize itself on orientation change from portrait to landscape""","""""""This is a regression.    Description:  1. Create an app for BB & replace the app.js with the code below:    2. Build & run the app on BB device  3. Launch the app & change the orientation from portrait to landscape    Actual result:  1. Thought the orientation changes to landscape the window does not resize accordingly & does not fill the width""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Window does not resize itself on orientation change from portrait to landscape
