TIMOB-14163,12,"""LiveView: iOS: App prevented from launching on iPhone simulator""","""""""Live View prevents app from launching on iPhone simulator    On a Mountain Lion VM, I followed Neeraj's email for installation so there are no legacy components on my system.    I created a new Alloy app (Hello World) and it ran fine on iPhone and Android simulators.    When I enable Live View on iPhone Simulator and launch the app, it freezes at the splash screen and the app will not run. I have to turn off Live View and then run the app again to get it to run on the iPhone simulator.    Studio diag (with all version info is attached).""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: iOS: App prevented from launching on iPhone simulator
Description: """"Live View prevents app from launching on iPhone simulator On a Mountain Lion VM, I followed Neeraj's email for installation so there are no legacy components on my system. I created a new Alloy app (Hello World) and it ran fine on iPhone and Android simulators. When I enable Live View on iPhone Simulator and launch the app, it freezes at the splash screen and the app will not run. I have to turn off Live View and then run the app again to get it to run on the iPhone simulator. Studio diag (with all version info is attached).""""",title+description
TIMOB-14161,12,"""Android: maps V2 are not displayed if packaging an app on a device without Google Play""","""""""h5. Problem description  Maps V2 are not visible if installed on an Android device with no Google Play store installed.    h5. Steps to reproduce  - Factory reset the Android device  - See the attached sample app. Package it for distribution.  - Install and run the project    Result: Maps are not visible (a gray area is visible instead).    As a user, I'm expecting in this case to receive a meaningful error message.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: maps V2 are not displayed if packaging an app on a device without Google Play
Description: """"h5. Problem description Maps V2 are not visible if installed on an Android device with no Google Play store installed. h5. Steps to reproduce - Factory reset the Android device - See the attached sample app. Package it for distribution. - Install and run the project Result: Maps are not visible (a gray area is visible instead). As a user, I'm expecting in this case to receive a meaningful error message.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14160,12,"""iOS: Transport.py images missing on the iPhone 5""","""""""h6.Issue  The graphic assets that are in the build directory under Resources/iPhone/Images folder need to be moved to resources/images, and then they show up fine.    h6.How to re-create:  (1) Get Titanium project attached targeting a 3.0.2 build  (2) Run transport.py   (3) Open in xcode and try to run in iPhone 5    h6.Actual results  You'll see the images missing on the iPhone 5, as well as the appicon.    They are getting put in build/iphone/Resources/iphone/images directory. They have to copy them to the build/iphone/Resources/images directory manually.    They also have to copy the build/iphone/Resources/iphone/<EMAIL> to the build/iphone/Resources directory manually.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Transport.py images missing on the iPhone 5
Description: """"h6.Issue The graphic assets that are in the build directory under Resources/iPhone/Images folder need to be moved to resources/images, and then they show up fine. h6.How to re-create: (1) Get Titanium project attached targeting a 3.0.2 build (2) Run transport.py (3) Open in xcode and try to run in iPhone 5 h6.Actual results You'll see the images missing on the iPhone 5, as well as the appicon. They are getting put in build/iphone/Resources/iphone/images directory. They have to copy them to the build/iphone/Resources/images directory manually. They also have to copy the build/iphone/Resources/iphone/<EMAIL> to the build/iphone/Resources directory manually. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14159,12,"""iOS: Crash when closing modal window after inputting text into a TextField inside a ScrollView (iPad only)""","""""""*Problem description*  There is a crash when closing a modal window after inputting text into a TextField inside a ScrollView on iPad only. There is no crash on iPhone.    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Run the test case on iPad simulator  2. Click Login  3. Input any amount of characters into the TextField  4. Click close on the modal view  5. Wait and observe resulting crash    *Workaround*  Change the ScrollView to a regular view (see comments).    *Test case*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Crash when closing modal window after inputting text into a TextField inside a ScrollView (iPad only)
Description: """"*Problem description* There is a crash when closing a modal window after inputting text into a TextField inside a ScrollView on iPad only. There is no crash on iPhone. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Run the test case on iPad simulator 2. Click Login 3. Input any amount of characters into the TextField 4. Click close on the modal view 5. Wait and observe resulting crash *Workaround* Change the ScrollView to a regular view (see comments). *Test case* """"",title+description
TIMOB-14158,12,"""Blackberry: Change TableView's class name from ListView to TableView""","""""""Currently, Titanium's TableView implementation is created through the _NativeListViewObject_ class. The TableViewRows are also created through the _NativeListItemObject_ class.    The TableView should be called _NativeTableViewObject_ and the TableViewRow should be called _NativeTableViewRowObject_ so that Titanium's ListView can be implemented.     Internally, both TableView and ListView are the same native component but in Titanium we have the two separate APIs.""""""",Story,"Title: Blackberry: Change TableView's class name from ListView to TableView
Description: """"Currently, Titanium's TableView implementation is created through the _NativeListViewObject_ class. The TableViewRows are also created through the _NativeListItemObject_ class. The TableView should be called _NativeTableViewObject_ and the TableViewRow should be called _NativeTableViewRowObject_ so that Titanium's ListView can be implemented. Internally, both TableView and ListView are the same native component but in Titanium we have the two separate APIs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14157,12,"""Android: TextField: Nexus 10: soft keyboard covers the textfield when using Ti.UI.TEXT_ALIGNMENT_CENTER/RIGHT in HW window""","""""""Test case:      Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the above code.  2. Click on the textfield. The soft keyboard shows and does not cover the textfield.  3. Dismiss the keyboard.  4. Click on the textfield.    Expect behavior: the soft keyboard shows and does not cover the textfield.  Actual behavior: the soft keyboard covers the textfield.    Only reproduce on Nexus 10 (4.2).  Cannot reproduce on Nexus 7 (4.1), Galaxy Tab 10.1(3.2).""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField: Nexus 10: soft keyboard covers the textfield when using Ti.UI.TEXT_ALIGNMENT_CENTER/RIGHT in HW window
Description: """"Test case: Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the above code. 2. Click on the textfield. The soft keyboard shows and does not cover the textfield. 3. Dismiss the keyboard. 4. Click on the textfield. Expect behavior: the soft keyboard shows and does not cover the textfield. Actual behavior: the soft keyboard covers the textfield. Only reproduce on Nexus 10 (4.2). Cannot reproduce on Nexus 7 (4.1), Galaxy Tab 10.1(3.2).""""",title+description
TIMOB-14156,12,"""Profiler: profile on iOS device hangs on  """"launch app on your device"""" ""","""""""Test steps:  1. Create project  2. Profile on iOS device    Actual result:  Profiler hangs  Might be related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TISTUD-3434    Expected result  Profiling session should begin after launching app on device  """"""",Bug,"Title: Profiler: profile on iOS device hangs on """"launch app on your device""""
Description: """"Test steps: 1. Create project 2. Profile on iOS device Actual result: Profiler hangs Might be related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TISTUD-3434 Expected result Profiling session should begin after launching app on device """"",title+description
TIMOB-14155,12,""" iOS: 'Invalid Region <center:nan, nan span:nan, nan>' with MapView on SDK 3.1.1""","""""""*Problem*  When trying to show a MapView with region and annotations in SDK 3.1.1 I get this error:    *Log*      *Note*  This works fine on 3.0.2 GA and previous versions. It seems that the problem occurs with 3.1 GA and above.    *Workaround*  Add left and right properties to Ti.Map creation. The error will no longer occur.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: 'Invalid Region <center:nan, nan span:nan, nan>' with MapView on SDK 3.1.1
Description: """"*Problem* When trying to show a MapView with region and annotations in SDK 3.1.1 I get this error: *Log* *Note* This works fine on 3.0.2 GA and previous versions. It seems that the problem occurs with 3.1 GA and above. *Workaround* Add left and right properties to Ti.Map creation. The error will no longer occur.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14154,12,"""iOS: SplitWindow inside TabGroup layout problems on rotation""","""""""*Problem description*  In my application I have a tabgroup. Each tab contains a SplitView that, inside, contains two navigation group (one for the detailwin and one for the masterwin). The problem is that the size of the window changes after the rotation of the device, or when you step from one tab to another.    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Run project in iPad simulator (portrait)  2. Rotate right (to landscape)  3. Switch to tab 2  4. Switch back to tab 1  5. Rotate right again (to portrait)  6. Observe that the portrait window is now smaller    1. Run project in iPad simulator (portrait)  2. Switch to tab 2  3. Switch back to tab 1  4. Rotate right (to landscape)  5. Observe that the landscape window is now larger    *Test case*  This is a generic code that reproduces the problem:     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: SplitWindow inside TabGroup layout problems on rotation
Description: """"*Problem description* In my application I have a tabgroup. Each tab contains a SplitView that, inside, contains two navigation group (one for the detailwin and one for the masterwin). The problem is that the size of the window changes after the rotation of the device, or when you step from one tab to another. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Run project in iPad simulator (portrait) 2. Rotate right (to landscape) 3. Switch to tab 2 4. Switch back to tab 1 5. Rotate right again (to portrait) 6. Observe that the portrait window is now smaller 1. Run project in iPad simulator (portrait) 2. Switch to tab 2 3. Switch back to tab 1 4. Rotate right (to landscape) 5. Observe that the landscape window is now larger *Test case* This is a generic code that reproduces the problem: """"",title+description
TIMOB-14153,12,"""Android: Parity with iOS zoom-in via pinch""","""""""h6.Issue  Scaling (pinch & zoom) from ScrollableView -   https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4738  was removed due a design decision for 1) parity with Android and 2) performance.    In iOS the pinch and zoom can be done using a scrollview inside a scrollable view. With parity in mind the developer is asking for bring this up in Android.    h6.Actual Sample  - app.js      - scroll_views_scaling.js      h6.Work around  It works but zooming the image to a larger size could make view to disappear. (not reproducible on 3.x though) e.g. https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9785  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Parity with iOS zoom-in via pinch
Description: """"h6.Issue Scaling (pinch & zoom) from ScrollableView - https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4738 was removed due a design decision for 1) parity with Android and 2) performance. In iOS the pinch and zoom can be done using a scrollview inside a scrollable view. With parity in mind the developer is asking for bring this up in Android. h6.Actual Sample - app.js - scroll_views_scaling.js h6.Work around It works but zooming the image to a larger size could make view to disappear. (not reproducible on 3.x though) e.g. https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9785 """"",title+description
TIMOB-14152,12,"""Android: Sound resumes during the phone lock screen in Gingerbread devices""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Run the following code:    2. Hit the power button to lock the phone  3. Hit the power button to go to the unlock screen    Expected Result:  The sound should not resume until you actually unlock the screen    Actual Result:  Sound resumes as soon as you reach the unlock screen""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Sound resumes during the phone lock screen in Gingerbread devices
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the following code: 2. Hit the power button to lock the phone 3. Hit the power button to go to the unlock screen Expected Result: The sound should not resume until you actually unlock the screen Actual Result: Sound resumes as soon as you reach the unlock screen""""",title+description
TIMOB-14151,12,"""Code Processor cannot recognize modules for iPad""","""""""When project is analyzed using iPad as selected platform, code processor cannot recognize modules """"""""com.<USER>apm"""""""" and """"""""com.soasta.touchtest"""""""".  There is no issue using iPhone as selected platform, although the modules are the same for both iPhone and iPad.    Test steps:  1. Create Titanium Project with all common deployment targets.   2. Project Context Menu > Code Analysis > Run Selected Platforms.  Actual result:  The module """"""""com.<USER>apm"""""""" could not be found  The module """"""""com.soasta.touchtest"""""""" could not be found  although these moduls are visible in tiapp.xml overview  """"""",Bug,"Title: Code Processor cannot recognize modules for iPad
Description: """"When project is analyzed using iPad as selected platform, code processor cannot recognize modules """"""""com.<USER>apm"""""""" and """"""""com.soasta.touchtest"""""""". There is no issue using iPhone as selected platform, although the modules are the same for both iPhone and iPad. Test steps: 1. Create Titanium Project with all common deployment targets. 2. Project Context Menu > Code Analysis > Run Selected Platforms. Actual result: The module """"""""com.<USER>apm"""""""" could not be found The module """"""""com.soasta.touchtest"""""""" could not be found although these moduls are visible in tiapp.xml overview """"",title+description
TIMOB-14150,12,"""iOS: ti.cloud not found when running the app in Xcode with iOS < 6.1""","""""""h2. Problem description  When trying to build a project using Xcode, if the target is iPhone v6.0 and below, the build fails as ti.cloud is not found.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1) Include ti.cloud in tiapp.xml  2) Just require it in app.js  3) Build for iPhone Simulator  4) Open the project in Xcode and build choosing iPhone 6.0 or below    The expected result would be a running app, but instead the following error is raised:    [ERROR] Script Error Couldn't find module: ti.cloud    Same code works fine using iPhone 6.1 in Xcode""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ti.cloud not found when running the app in Xcode with iOS < 6.1
Description: """"h2. Problem description When trying to build a project using Xcode, if the target is iPhone v6.0 and below, the build fails as ti.cloud is not found. h2. Steps to reproduce 1) Include ti.cloud in tiapp.xml 2) Just require it in app.js 3) Build for iPhone Simulator 4) Open the project in Xcode and build choosing iPhone 6.0 or below The expected result would be a running app, but instead the following error is raised: [ERROR] Script Error Couldn't find module: ti.cloud Same code works fine using iPhone 6.1 in Xcode""""",title+description
