TIMOB-14145,12,"""iOS: Analytics - If you background an iOS app, the background event does not get sent until next launch""","""""""*Details:* If you background an iOS app, the background event does not get sent within the 15 second threshold and does not get sent after the threshold. You will not get that background event until next launch.    *On Android now (SDK 3.1.1.X), if you press the back button or home button, the end event does get sent within the 30 second threshold.*    *Steps to reproduce:*  0. Make sure you have RightScale opened in a terminal to view analytics  1. Install default app to an iOS device  2. Make sure the device is pointing to the staging wifi  3. Launch the app  4. Then, press the home button to background the app    *Actual:* ti.background event is not sent within the 15 seconds threshold and still not sent after the threshold.    *Expected:* ti.background event should be sent within the 15 seconds threshold if you background the app.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Analytics - If you background an iOS app, the background event does not get sent until next launch
Description: """"*Details:* If you background an iOS app, the background event does not get sent within the 15 second threshold and does not get sent after the threshold. You will not get that background event until next launch. *On Android now (SDK 3.1.1.X), if you press the back button or home button, the end event does get sent within the 30 second threshold.* *Steps to reproduce:* 0. Make sure you have RightScale opened in a terminal to view analytics 1. Install default app to an iOS device 2. Make sure the device is pointing to the staging wifi 3. Launch the app 4. Then, press the home button to background the app *Actual:* ti.background event is not sent within the 15 seconds threshold and still not sent after the threshold. *Expected:* ti.background event should be sent within the 15 seconds threshold if you background the app.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14144,12,"""Blackberry: Ti.UI.Views defaults height to FILL if content is SIZE""","""""""h4. Problem  When creating Views, if no height is passed in or if height is set to Ti.UI.SIZE, the height behaves as if it were Ti.UI.FILL when the content's height is set to SIZE.    h4. Code      h4. What works  If the content has a hardcoded height, then the outer view will resize accordingly.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry: Ti.UI.Views defaults height to FILL if content is SIZE
Description: """"h4. Problem When creating Views, if no height is passed in or if height is set to Ti.UI.SIZE, the height behaves as if it were Ti.UI.FILL when the content's height is set to SIZE. h4. Code h4. What works If the content has a hardcoded height, then the outer view will resize accordingly. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14143,12,"""TiAPI: Ability to set cookies in a WebView before the response is committed""","""""""*Problem*  WebView should have a method to allow you to set a cookie before a response occurs.    *Invalid workarounds*  - 'beforeload' event - According to the [documentation|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.WebView-event-beforeload] this does not work for remote requests  - 'load' event - At this point the request has already been received""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Ability to set cookies in a WebView before the response is committed
Description: """"*Problem* WebView should have a method to allow you to set a cookie before a response occurs. *Invalid workarounds* - 'beforeload' event - According to the [documentation|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.WebView-event-beforeload] this does not work for remote requests - 'load' event - At this point the request has already been received""""",title+description
TIMOB-14142,12,"""BlackBerry : Wrong date format on BlackBerry analytics events""","""""""Description:  1. Create an app & replace the app.js with the app.js for analytics test in feature test repo  2. Follow the instructions for rightscale from this wiki page: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan  3. Build & run the app on BB device  4. The app will launch automatically  5. On right scale you will get an enroll & a start event  6. check the time & date stamp in the events     Actual Result:  1. We see a wrong format like this """"""""2013-6-46T10:46:29.814"""""""" which is wrong we do not have 46 days in june. Also, I think we are seeing the minutes stamp duplicated in place of the date     Expected Results:  1. We should see a time & date format in proper format     For proper time stamp format refer : https://wiki.<USER>org/display/cls/Example+Analytics+JSON+payloads  """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Wrong date format on BlackBerry analytics events
Description: """"Description: 1. Create an app & replace the app.js with the app.js for analytics test in feature test repo 2. Follow the instructions for rightscale from this wiki page: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan 3. Build & run the app on BB device 4. The app will launch automatically 5. On right scale you will get an enroll & a start event 6. check the time & date stamp in the events Actual Result: 1. We see a wrong format like this """"""""2013-6-46T10:46:29.814"""""""" which is wrong we do not have 46 days in june. Also, I think we are seeing the minutes stamp duplicated in place of the date Expected Results: 1. We should see a time & date format in proper format For proper time stamp format refer : https://wiki.<USER>org/display/cls/Example+Analytics+JSON+payloads """"",title+description
TIMOB-14140,12,"""MobileWeb: Add support for """"test"""" deploy type""","""""""Mobile Web currently support development and production builds. The problem is there's no support for a """"""""test"""""""" build that is like production (minified code, etc), but not production.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Add support for """"test"""" deploy type
Description: """"Mobile Web currently support development and production builds. The problem is there's no support for a """"""""test"""""""" build that is like production (minified code, etc), but not production.""""",title+description
