TIMOB-14138,12,"""CLI: iOS: Immediately call the pre-compile phase after the prepare phase""","""""""After the prepare phase is executed, xcodebuild is called. The first thing Xcode does is call the CLI again and initiates the pre-compile phase. While this works, it adds several seconds to the build time.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: iOS: Immediately call the pre-compile phase after the prepare phase
Description: """"After the prepare phase is executed, xcodebuild is called. The first thing Xcode does is call the CLI again and initiates the pre-compile phase. While this works, it adds several seconds to the build time.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14137,12,"""Android: camera returns low resolution image using overlay""","""""""The image returns by the camera is a low res image instead of the full size image on some devices when using an overlay.    The galaxy nexus (4.1) returns an image of 320x240  The ZTE N860 (2.3.5) returns an image of 640x480    Samsung Galaxy S1 (2.3.3) is returning a full size image (2592x1944)    Here is the code sample from bug TIMOB-8151 adapted to display image size.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: camera returns low resolution image using overlay
Description: """"The image returns by the camera is a low res image instead of the full size image on some devices when using an overlay. The galaxy nexus (4.1) returns an image of 320x240 The ZTE N860 (2.3.5) returns an image of 640x480 Samsung Galaxy S1 (2.3.3) is returning a full size image (2592x1944) Here is the code sample from bug TIMOB-8151 adapted to display image size. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14136,12,"""Android: anyDensity flag needs to be set as true ""","""""""h6.Issue  Client had to set <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" /> explicitly in order to load the density-specific resources correctly.    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. use demo https://github.com/<USER>KitchenSink/  2. Remove from tiapp.xml <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/> tag  3. Install & run    h6.Expected behavior  The default is true already.    h6.Actual behavior  The screen looks scaled (like if anyDensity true wasn't honored).    h6.Additional details  They used <tool-api-level>17</tool-api-level> and <uses-sdk  targetSdkVersion=""""""""17""""""""/>.    They have to include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" /> in order to get correct resources on devices of different resolutions.    h6.Tested on  tested on a xhdpi device, android 4.1.2 a S3 as well as new htc one.    If they don't include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" />, the app is displayed with mdpi assets. If they include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" />, the app is displayed correctly with xhdpi assets.    They use unit """"""""dp"""""""" in all places of their code.    Right now this isn't an issue for their app because they can simply include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" /> for everything to work.    h6.Documentation  The Titanium project was clean up as our docs say:  """"""""You may or may not need to clean your project (force Titanium to freshly re-generate the native project files) to ensure your new configuration settings are picked up""""""""    - http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Using_density-specific_resources_on_Android-section-29004808_Usingdensity-specificresourcesonAndroid-DisablingMultipleDensityHandling""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: anyDensity flag needs to be set as true
Description: """"h6.Issue Client had to set <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" /> explicitly in order to load the density-specific resources correctly. h6.Steps to reproduce 1. use demo https://github.com/<USER>KitchenSink/ 2. Remove from tiapp.xml <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/> tag 3. Install & run h6.Expected behavior The default is true already. h6.Actual behavior The screen looks scaled (like if anyDensity true wasn't honored). h6.Additional details They used <tool-api-level>17</tool-api-level> and <uses-sdk targetSdkVersion=""""""""17""""""""/>. They have to include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" /> in order to get correct resources on devices of different resolutions. h6.Tested on tested on a xhdpi device, android 4.1.2 a S3 as well as new htc one. If they don't include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" />, the app is displayed with mdpi assets. If they include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" />, the app is displayed correctly with xhdpi assets. They use unit """"""""dp"""""""" in all places of their code. Right now this isn't an issue for their app because they can simply include <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" /> for everything to work. h6.Documentation The Titanium project was clean up as our docs say: """"""""You may or may not need to clean your project (force Titanium to freshly re-generate the native project files) to ensure your new configuration settings are picked up"""""""" - http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/Using_density-specific_resources_on_Android-section-29004808_Usingdensity-specificresourcesonAndroid-DisablingMultipleDensityHandling""""",title+description
TIMOB-14135,12,"""Android: Allow customization for JS error popups""","""""""Lanica needs the ability to disable and customize runtime JS error popup for production Android builds for their """"""""Gardens of Time"""""""" app. On Android, [error dialogs always show up|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/runtime/v8/src/native/V8Util.cpp#L127], even in production, which is incorrect.    From <USER>    {quote}  For going to release with aGOT (and presumably any other games!) we need to disable the Runtime Error (JS error) popups and ideally replace them with some more friendly error.    Engineering says this would need to be changed in the SDK, and references this bug:  https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9735    Can you shed some light on this? We're trying to go to Canada release within the week.  {quote}    This is the peer issue in Playdom's JIRA server: AHOG-1093""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Allow customization for JS error popups
Description: """"Lanica needs the ability to disable and customize runtime JS error popup for production Android builds for their """"""""Gardens of Time"""""""" app. On Android, [error dialogs always show up|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/runtime/v8/src/native/V8Util.cpp#L127], even in production, which is incorrect. From <USER> {quote} For going to release with aGOT (and presumably any other games!) we need to disable the Runtime Error (JS error) popups and ideally replace them with some more friendly error. Engineering says this would need to be changed in the SDK, and references this bug: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9735 Can you shed some light on this? We're trying to go to Canada release within the week. {quote} This is the peer issue in Playdom's JIRA server: AHOG-1093""""",title+description
TIMOB-14134,12,"""Android: ANR during Imageview animation ""","""""""h6.Issue  App is not responding if you press the Android power button 2-3 times, then you can reproduce the ANR. Sometimes even at first time pressing power button you can reproduce this issue.    h6.Tested on  Samsung S3 - 4.1.2 , Sony Xperia U - 2.3.7 , HTC amaze - 2.3.4 , Droid Razr 2.3.5    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Run app   2. Click """"""""sync"""""""" button (there will be a HTTP call after got the response from the server)  3. Huge data will be inserted into local database.    He is trying to stop the animation and start it again while locking and unlocking the mobile screen. Like:        It would also save the extra overhead of the app when the phone screen is locked since they have a requirement they have to use a custom indicator.    h6.Reproduction sample      sqlite and loadingSmall assets were attached or can be downloaded here: https://github.com/karthi-anubavam/indicator-test    h6.Stack trace  Eventually App is not responding, device logs have been attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ANR during Imageview animation
Description: """"h6.Issue App is not responding if you press the Android power button 2-3 times, then you can reproduce the ANR. Sometimes even at first time pressing power button you can reproduce this issue. h6.Tested on Samsung S3 - 4.1.2 , Sony Xperia U - 2.3.7 , HTC amaze - 2.3.4 , Droid Razr 2.3.5 h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Run app 2. Click """"""""sync"""""""" button (there will be a HTTP call after got the response from the server) 3. Huge data will be inserted into local database. He is trying to stop the animation and start it again while locking and unlocking the mobile screen. Like: It would also save the extra overhead of the app when the phone screen is locked since they have a requirement they have to use a custom indicator. h6.Reproduction sample sqlite and loadingSmall assets were attached or can be downloaded here: https://github.com/karthi-anubavam/indicator-test h6.Stack trace Eventually App is not responding, device logs have been attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14133,12,"""Code Processor: Category names in the 'Project Score - Category Scores' table need format improvement""","""""""h5. Problem description    Category names in the 'Project Score - Category Scores' table should have first upper case letter and have a space in between if composed by multiple words.    For example:  """"""""platformInconsistencies"""""""" should be """"""""Platform Inconsistencies""""""""  """"""""deprecatedAPIUsage"""""""" should be """"""""Deprecated API Usage""""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Processor: Category names in the 'Project Score - Category Scores' table need format improvement
Description: """"h5. Problem description Category names in the 'Project Score - Category Scores' table should have first upper case letter and have a space in between if composed by multiple words. For example: """"""""platformInconsistencies"""""""" should be """"""""Platform Inconsistencies"""""""" """"""""deprecatedAPIUsage"""""""" should be """"""""Deprecated API Usage""""""""""""",title+description
TIMOB-14132,12,"""Code Processor: typo in the .html 'ProjectScore -> CategoryScore -> platformInconsistencies' results""","""""""h5. Problem description  In the Results .html files, the description relative to 'ProjectScore -> CategoryScore -> platformInconsistencies' has a typo.    'deprecated APIs' wording is present instead of 'platform-specific APIs'.    See screenshot.""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Processor: typo in the .html 'ProjectScore -> CategoryScore -> platformInconsistencies' results
