TIMOB-14131,12,"""Blackberry: Labels only show one line of text""","""""""h3. Problem  Ti.UI.Labels only show one line of text. They're supposed to be multi-line labels, like they are on iOS, Android, and MobileWeb  h3. Code    h3. Workaround  Setting the wordWrap to false. This should be true by default.""""""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry: Labels only show one line of text
Description: """"h3. Problem Ti.UI.Labels only show one line of text. They're supposed to be multi-line labels, like they are on iOS, Android, and MobileWeb h3. Code h3. Workaround Setting the wordWrap to false. This should be true by default.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14130,12,"""Android: Window events, windows in the Tab and test""","""""""Make sure the """"""""open"""""""", """"""""close"""""""", """"""""focus"""""""", """"""""blur"""""""", """"""""androidback"""""""" events work fine.  Make sure the new window works fine in Tabgroup.  Need test case.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Android: Window events, windows in the Tab and test
Description: """"Make sure the """"""""open"""""""", """"""""close"""""""", """"""""focus"""""""", """"""""blur"""""""", """"""""androidback"""""""" events work fine. Make sure the new window works fine in Tabgroup. Need test case.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14129,12,"""BlackBerry: Ti.UI.SIZE for width on components break position""","""""""h3. Problem  When creating a UI component and giving it a width of Ti.UI.SIZE, the component will be placed at the 0,0 position of the parent view, no matter if top, left, right, and bottom are defined.  h3. Code    h3. More  If margins are given, the component must respect them - not ignore them. If margin are not given, the component must be centered in the parent view, not be placed at 0,0""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Ti.UI.SIZE for width on components break position
Description: """"h3. Problem When creating a UI component and giving it a width of Ti.UI.SIZE, the component will be placed at the 0,0 position of the parent view, no matter if top, left, right, and bottom are defined. h3. Code h3. More If margins are given, the component must respect them - not ignore them. If margin are not given, the component must be centered in the parent view, not be placed at 0,0""""",title+description
TIMOB-14128,12,"""Android: Implement the """"url"""" property for windows and Ti.UI.currentWindow""","""""""Need to handle this property specially because the window with a url will create a new JavaScript sub-context that will run in its own thread and global variable space.   Need to handle Ti.UI.currentWindow. Ti.UI.currentWindow should and should only works in the sub-context of the url window. In the other cases, Ti.UI.currentWindow returns null on Android and returns undefined on iOS.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Android: Implement the """"url"""" property for windows and Ti.UI.currentWindow
Description: """"Need to handle this property specially because the window with a url will create a new JavaScript sub-context that will run in its own thread and global variable space. Need to handle Ti.UI.currentWindow. Ti.UI.currentWindow should and should only works in the sub-context of the url window. In the other cases, Ti.UI.currentWindow returns null on Android and returns undefined on iOS.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14127,12,"""Android: Implement all the properties except """"url"""" for both LW and HW windows""","""""""Go through the doc and implement all the window properties (except """"""""url"""""""") for both LW/HW windows.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Android: Implement all the properties except """"url"""" for both LW and HW windows
Description: """"Go through the doc and implement all the window properties (except """"""""url"""""""") for both LW/HW windows.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14126,12,"""Android: Create a new window proxy to handle both LW and HW windows""","""""""Don't need any wrapper proxy for windows. Create a new window proxy can be used by both LW/HW windows.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Android: Create a new window proxy to handle both LW and HW windows
Description: """"Don't need any wrapper proxy for windows. Create a new window proxy can be used by both LW/HW windows.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14125,12,"""BlackBerry: Analytics should send navigation events as is done in iOS""","""""""Currently on BB10 client there are no navigation event sending latitude and longitude as is done on iOS. Since the server will do a lookup based on IP it's not urgent to fix this because the server will """"""""geo loc"""""""" the ip address but client side nav events will be more accurate.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Analytics should send navigation events as is done in iOS
Description: """"Currently on BB10 client there are no navigation event sending latitude and longitude as is done on iOS. Since the server will do a lookup based on IP it's not urgent to fix this because the server will """"""""geo loc"""""""" the ip address but client side nav events will be more accurate.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14124,12,"""Android: V8Exception when getting Tab's title on KitchenSink""","""""""h6.Issue  Looks like e.tab.title can be only read once.    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Get Kitchen Sink app :)  2. Install & Run  3. Monitor output - a runtime exception is noticeable.    h6.Offending code  - https://github.com/<USER>KitchenSink/blob/master/Resources/ui/common/ApplicationTabGroup.js#L140    If you add a such line of code the Tab's title shows up:  - Ti.API.info(' JSON.stringify(e.tab.title): '+ JSON.stringify(e.tab.title));  Output:  - 06-05 11:54:19.297: I/TiAPI(11303):   JSON.stringify(e.tab.title): """"""""Base UI""""""""      Then you will eventually get (Device stack trace):      h6.Associated Q&A thread  http://developer.<USER>com/question/150744/downloaded-kitchensink-210-now-working-on-my-android-device""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: V8Exception when getting Tab's title on KitchenSink
Description: """"h6.Issue Looks like e.tab.title can be only read once. h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Get Kitchen Sink app :) 2. Install & Run 3. Monitor output - a runtime exception is noticeable. h6.Offending code - https://github.com/<USER>KitchenSink/blob/master/Resources/ui/common/ApplicationTabGroup.js#L140 If you add a such line of code the Tab's title shows up: - Ti.API.info(' JSON.stringify(e.tab.title): '+ JSON.stringify(e.tab.title)); Output: - 06-05 11:54:19.297: I/TiAPI(11303): JSON.stringify(e.tab.title): """"""""Base UI"""""""" Then you will eventually get (Device stack trace): h6.Associated Q&A thread http://developer.<USER>com/question/150744/downloaded-kitchensink-210-now-working-on-my-android-device""""",title+description
