TIMOB-14114,12,"""BlackBerry: We get two background events when the app is automatically put in background by another app &  again brought to foreground""","""""""Description:  1. Create an app & replace the app.js with the app.js for analytics test in feature test repo  2. Follow the instructions for rightscale from this wiki page: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan  3. Build & run the app on BB device  4. The app will launch automatically  5. Now with the app launched install another app from the studio  6. The above step will automatically background the app & launch the new app  7. Now close the newly launched app & bring the original app in for ground    Actual Result:  1. We see 2 background events & one foreground events    Expected Results:  1. We should see one background & one foreground event""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: We get two background events when the app is automatically put in background by another app & again brought to foreground
Description: """"Description: 1. Create an app & replace the app.js with the app.js for analytics test in feature test repo 2. Follow the instructions for rightscale from this wiki page: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan 3. Build & run the app on BB device 4. The app will launch automatically 5. Now with the app launched install another app from the studio 6. The above step will automatically background the app & launch the new app 7. Now close the newly launched app & bring the original app in for ground Actual Result: 1. We see 2 background events & one foreground events Expected Results: 1. We should see one background & one foreground event""""",title+description
TIMOB-14113,12,"""BlackBerry : We see multiple enroll events (extra 2 in my case) on the first app launch""","""""""Description:  1. Create an app & replace the app.js with the app.js for analytics test in feature test repo  2. Follow the instructions for rightscale from this wiki page: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan  3. Build & run the app on BB device  4. Check rightscale for enroll event    Actual result:  1. We see 2 extra ti.enroll events along with the original ti.enroll & a ti.start    Expected Result:  1. We should see only one ti.enroll event   """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : We see multiple enroll events (extra 2 in my case) on the first app launch
