TIMOB-14097,12,"""BlackBerry: Proxies are never collected by GC""","""""""The proxy objects are never being collected by the V8 engine.  We appear to be using Persistent handles, but never make them weak  or setup callbacks to properly dispose of them once the JS object is unreachable.    h3. Test Case      If you run the above test case and monitor the memory usage, you  will see it continue to go up with out any collections.  """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Proxies are never collected by GC
Description: """"The proxy objects are never being collected by the V8 engine. We appear to be using Persistent handles, but never make them weak or setup callbacks to properly dispose of them once the JS object is unreachable. h3. Test Case If you run the above test case and monitor the memory usage, you will see it continue to go up with out any collections. """"",title+description
TIMOB-14095,12,"""iOS: Enabling Appcelerator services, causes the Build to fail when compiled using Xcode 4.4 and target iOS SDK 5.1""","""""""Environment:  Mac osx 10.8.3 Mountain Lion  <USER>Studio, build: 3.1.1.201306012403  Titanium Studio, build: 3.1.1.201305312303  SDK, build: 3.1.1.v20130531163723  XCode 4.4.1  Device:  iPhone 5 iOS 6.0  CLI: 3.1.1-alpha    It is a *regression*, not occurs in 3.1.0.GA    Description:  Enabling <USER>services and compiling the project, using XCode 4.4.1 and iOS SDK 5.1, results in compiler failure.      Test steps:  1. Create the default project, using <USER>Titanium Studio (Do Not Enable Services)  2. Build for device or simulator  3. Add ti.cloud module or enable services and build again    Using CLI, run the command: ti build -p ios -T device -I 5.1 ------------ failed    Actual result:  2. Build succeeded  3. Build failed      Expected result:  Build should succeed""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Enabling Appcelerator services, causes the Build to fail when compiled using Xcode 4.4 and target iOS SDK 5.1
Description: """"Environment: Mac osx 10.8.3 Mountain Lion <USER>Studio, build: 3.1.1.201306012403 Titanium Studio, build: 3.1.1.201305312303 SDK, build: 3.1.1.v20130531163723 XCode 4.4.1 Device: iPhone 5 iOS 6.0 CLI: 3.1.1-alpha It is a *regression*, not occurs in 3.1.0.GA Description: Enabling <USER>services and compiling the project, using XCode 4.4.1 and iOS SDK 5.1, results in compiler failure. Test steps: 1. Create the default project, using <USER>Titanium Studio (Do Not Enable Services) 2. Build for device or simulator 3. Add ti.cloud module or enable services and build again Using CLI, run the command: ti build -p ios -T device -I 5.1 ------------ failed Actual result: 2. Build succeeded 3. Build failed Expected result: Build should succeed""""",title+description
