Description: """"We have a continuous integration server (Jenkins) that builds an application via the CLI (ti build). We recently just duplicated the target in Jenkins so we can build both a debug and release variant. After we did this, we *sometimes* (not always) see a build failure. In the logs, the failure point seems to be this message: [ERROR] OperationalError: database is locked There shouldn't be any shared dependencies between our two targets (each gets its own copies of data and its own workspace directories) My best guess is there is there is some shared resource invoked by 'ti build'. Is this true? Is there something that can be done to improve this? This is not a showstopper at the moment. I can tell Jenkins to only build one project at a time and I think the problem goes away (hard to verify since the problem is intermittent). But it would be nice to not have this limitation. Full build log is pasted below: Started by an SCM change Building in workspace /Users/lanica/Jenkins/Home/jobs/GardensOfTimeAndroid_Debug/workspace Checkout:workspace / /Users/lanica/Jenkins/Home/jobs/GardensOfTimeAndroid_Debug/workspace - hudson.remoting.LocalChannel@2f56a6be Using strategy: Default Last Built Revision: Revision 64b7da5d1dfc4c4d83f78e47a54944bfe52615d8 (origin/master) Fetching changes from 1 remote Git repository Fetching upstream changes from origin Commencing build of Revision 70971df323ec76200a45e467e339b8ef29b6ddd1 (origin/master) Checking out Revision 70971df323ec76200a45e467e339b8ef29b6ddd1 (origin/master) Cleaning workspace Resetting working tree [workspace] $ /bin/sh -xe /var/folders/cb/116ms69s1sd31zlvttqgxl8c0000gn/T/hudson1399061169376581932.sh + export PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/local/bin + PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/local/bin + [[ ! -z '' ]] [workspace] $ /bin/sh -xe /var/folders/cb/116ms69s1sd31zlvttqgxl8c0000gn/T/hudson1572198374200878275.sh + export NUM_CPUS=2 + NUM_CPUS=2 + export ANDROID_SDK=/Library/Frameworks/Android/a