TIMOB-14056,12,"""Code Analyzer: Alloy: Model/Collection name is marked as 'not defined' in the Errors list in the report""","""""""h5. Problem description  Analyzing an Alloy project using Model/Collections, there is an unexpected error in the Code Analyzer report regarding the Collection name, which is reported as not defined.    h5. Steps to reproduce  1. Use Alloy sample app: https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/1_1_X/test/apps/models/journal (also attached here in the Jira)  2. Run the Code Analyzer    Result:   Error [""""""""journal' is not defined] is reported.    Description: """"""""journal"""""""" is not defined  File: Alloy.Collections.instance(""""""""journal"""""""");  Line: 37    'journal' is the value of the 'collection_name'.    It seems the line number is also not correct.    line is present in Resources/alloy/controllers/index.js but at line 44 (Resources files are included in the Project attached too).    """"""",Bug,"Title: Code Analyzer: Alloy: Model/Collection name is marked as 'not defined' in the Errors list in the report
Description: """"h5. Problem description Analyzing an Alloy project using Model/Collections, there is an unexpected error in the Code Analyzer report regarding the Collection name, which is reported as not defined. h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Use Alloy sample app: https://github.com/<USER>alloy/tree/1_1_X/test/apps/models/journal (also attached here in the Jira) 2. Run the Code Analyzer Result: Error [""""""""journal' is not defined] is reported. Description: """"""""journal"""""""" is not defined File: Alloy.Collections.instance(""""""""journal""""""""); Line: 37 'journal' is the value of the 'collection_name'. It seems the line number is also not correct. line is present in Resources/alloy/controllers/index.js but at line 44 (Resources files are included in the Project attached too). """"",title+description
TIMOB-14055,12,"""Allow user location to be shown in Google Maps V2 module without the built-in """"My Location"""" button""","""""""We have several """"""""map modes"""""""" (where following the current location is just one) in our app, so we would like our own """"""""buttons"""""""" for these, while still showing the current location on the map. Suggestion: new property enableMyLocationControl: Boolean (default: true) in Modules.Map.View that decides visibility of the """"""""My location"""""""" button rather than userLocation property. If you want backwards compability, it should only have effect when userLocation is true. In my case, I would then set userLocation = true and enableMyLocationControl = false.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Allow user location to be shown in Google Maps V2 module without the built-in """"My Location"""" button
Description: """"We have several """"""""map modes"""""""" (where following the current location is just one) in our app, so we would like our own """"""""buttons"""""""" for these, while still showing the current location on the map. Suggestion: new property enableMyLocationControl: Boolean (default: true) in Modules.Map.View that decides visibility of the """"""""My location"""""""" button rather than userLocation property. If you want backwards compability, it should only have effect when userLocation is true. In my case, I would then set userLocation = true and enableMyLocationControl = false.""""",title+description
TIMOB-14054,12,"""iOS: Buttons on camera overlay not working when showCamera allowEditing property is true""","""""""*Problem*  When showCamera's allowEditing property is set to true, buttons added to the camera overlay are not working.    *Test case*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Buttons on camera overlay not working when showCamera allowEditing property is true
