TIMOB-14012,12,"""Android: Parity - XHR user agent is null on Android, populated on iOS""","""""""h5. Description:  While verifying results from an XHR feature change, I noted that the user agent for iOS and Android were different. On Android, the user agent is null.    Here are examples of the user agent info for iOS and android:  h6. Android  { 'x-titanium-id': 'd67defe8-12dd-45ba-b8fd-1e915158ee1b',  'x-requested-with': 'XMLHttpRequest',  'user-agent': '',  host: '172.16.83.53:8000',  connection: 'Keep-Alive' }    h6. iOS  { host: '127.0.0.1:8000', 'x-titanium-id': '589be76d-ff3d-42ff-baca-07f1363aced0', 'accept-encoding': 'gzip', 'user-agent': '<USER>Titanium/3.1.1.v20130522190722 (iPhone Simulator/6.0; iPhone OS; en_US;)', connection: 'close', 'x-requested-with': 'XMLHttpRequest' }      h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Download and run the attached """""""".js"""""""" file with """"""""node testserver.js""""""""  2) Install the following test code and run in simulator  3) Press the send request button    h6. Test code      h5. Result:  Android user agent is null    h5. Expected Result:  iOS and Android have parity with regards to user agent""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Parity - XHR user agent is null on Android, populated on iOS
Description: """"h5. Description: While verifying results from an XHR feature change, I noted that the user agent for iOS and Android were different. On Android, the user agent is null. Here are examples of the user agent info for iOS and android: h6. Android { 'x-titanium-id': 'd67defe8-12dd-45ba-b8fd-1e915158ee1b', 'x-requested-with': 'XMLHttpRequest', 'user-agent': '', host: '172.16.83.53:8000', connection: 'Keep-Alive' } h6. iOS { host: '127.0.0.1:8000', 'x-titanium-id': '589be76d-ff3d-42ff-baca-07f1363aced0', 'accept-encoding': 'gzip', 'user-agent': '<USER>Titanium/3.1.1.v20130522190722 (iPhone Simulator/6.0; iPhone OS; en_US;)', connection: 'close', 'x-requested-with': 'XMLHttpRequest' } h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Download and run the attached """""""".js"""""""" file with """"""""node testserver.js"""""""" 2) Install the following test code and run in simulator 3) Press the send request button h6. Test code h5. Result: Android user agent is null h5. Expected Result: iOS and Android have parity with regards to user agent""""",title+description
