TIMOB-14001,12,"""Android: Allow sending extra data to the intent when opening a notification""","""""""h2. Description of the problem  When clicking on a notification, if we want to restore the app which is in background, is currently not possible to understand if the click comes from the notification or not, as we cannot send extra data    h2. Use case  When clicking on a notification, you want to switch to a particular tab/page of the app. Opening a NEW intent would work (e.g. we can create the intent with extra data), but if we use the currently open one (Ti.Android.currentActivity.intent) there is not way to provide such information.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Allow sending extra data to the intent when opening a notification
Description: """"h2. Description of the problem When clicking on a notification, if we want to restore the app which is in background, is currently not possible to understand if the click comes from the notification or not, as we cannot send extra data h2. Use case When clicking on a notification, you want to switch to a particular tab/page of the app. Opening a NEW intent would work (e.g. we can create the intent with extra data), but if we use the currently open one (Ti.Android.currentActivity.intent) there is not way to provide such information.""""",title+description
