TIMOB-13963,12,"""BlackBerry : Currently the analytics events are set to been sent every 10 min which is not in parity with other platforms""","""""""Currently the analytics events are set to send events every 10 min which according to blain's comment """""""" if the queue was empty, analytics waits 5 seconds for other events to come in before sending to the server. On a server issue, the wait for trying again is 15 seconds."""""""" should be much less to be in parity with other platforms.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Currently the analytics events are set to been sent every 10 min which is not in parity with other platforms
Description: """"Currently the analytics events are set to send events every 10 min which according to blain's comment """""""" if the queue was empty, analytics waits 5 seconds for other events to come in before sending to the server. On a server issue, the wait for trying again is 15 seconds."""""""" should be much less to be in parity with other platforms.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13958,12,"""Code Processor: Reuse project validation mechanisms from the CLI""","""""""Now that the code processor is a part of the CLI, we should reuse as much CLI code as possible when parsing projects. Doing things like SDK version matching, module version matching, project validation, platform validation, is currently done using custom code in the code processor (a by product of it originally being a separate product). Now that it's part of the CLI, the code processor should let the CLI do these operations.    In addition to increasing code reuse, it will put project validation at parity with the CLI, which it currently is not.""""""",Story,"Title: Code Processor: Reuse project validation mechanisms from the CLI
Description: """"Now that the code processor is a part of the CLI, we should reuse as much CLI code as possible when parsing projects. Doing things like SDK version matching, module version matching, project validation, platform validation, is currently done using custom code in the code processor (a by product of it originally being a separate product). Now that it's part of the CLI, the code processor should let the CLI do these operations. In addition to increasing code reuse, it will put project validation at parity with the CLI, which it currently is not.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13957,12,"""Titanium Runtime: Identify Use Cases""","""""""The Titanium Runtime requirements will initially be specified as a collection of either Use Case briefs or fully dressed Use Cases that describe how the various pieces of the Titanium Runtime interact with one another as well as external dependencies such as <USER>Debugger, <USER>Profilers, Live View, etc.    This ticket tracks the effort for identifying the use cases.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Titanium Runtime: Identify Use Cases
Description: """"The Titanium Runtime requirements will initially be specified as a collection of either Use Case briefs or fully dressed Use Cases that describe how the various pieces of the Titanium Runtime interact with one another as well as external dependencies such as <USER>Debugger, <USER>Profilers, Live View, etc. This ticket tracks the effort for identifying the use cases.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13956,12,"""Create architecture specification for new Titanium Runtime""","""""""This is an umbrella ticket for creating the architecture specification for a new Titanium Runtime, which is the mobile platform upon which a Titanium Application executes.    The Titanium Runtime is the collection of software that runs on a mobile device which provides the common services required by a Titanium Application. This specification will be created by a tiger team assembled by Neeraj which is charged with completing the initial version of the spec by the end of June 2013 that will be of suitable detail and quality as to allow an engineering team to implement a prototype of the Titanium Runtime on a Windows 8 Mobile device.    The specification is being collaboratively documented on the [Titanium Runtime wiki|https://wiki.<USER>org/display/coreruntime/Titanium+Runtime].    This is a high-level diagram showing where the Titanium Runtime fits into the overall component architecture:    !Core Runtime.png!""""""",Epic,"Title: Create architecture specification for new Titanium Runtime
Description: """"This is an umbrella ticket for creating the architecture specification for a new Titanium Runtime, which is the mobile platform upon which a Titanium Application executes. The Titanium Runtime is the collection of software that runs on a mobile device which provides the common services required by a Titanium Application. This specification will be created by a tiger team assembled by Neeraj which is charged with completing the initial version of the spec by the end of June 2013 that will be of suitable detail and quality as to allow an engineering team to implement a prototype of the Titanium Runtime on a Windows 8 Mobile device. The specification is being collaboratively documented on the [Titanium Runtime wiki|https://wiki.<USER>org/display/coreruntime/Titanium+Runtime]. This is a high-level diagram showing where the Titanium Runtime fits into the overall component architecture: !Core Runtime.png!""""",title+description
TIMOB-13955,12,"""iOS: ImageView returns empty blob when """"no-cache"""" is present in HTTP response headers""","""""""*Problem*  ImageView returns empty blob when """"""""no-cache"""""""" is present in HTTP response headers.    *Actual Result*  {code}[INFO] :   Image loaded!, blob length: 0{code}    *Expected Result*  ImageView should return non empty blob.    *Test case*  {code:javascript}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor : 'white'  });    var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({   image : 'http://www.voltimum.es/imageDisplay.php?w=265&h=265&f=./files/es/flipbooks/others/G/20130522271201301181170.jpg'  });    imageView.addEventListener('load', function(e) {   Ti.API.info('Image loaded! blob length: ' + e.source.toBlob().length);  });    win.add(imageView);    win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ImageView returns empty blob when """"no-cache"""" is present in HTTP response headers
