TIMOB-13950,12,"""BlackBerry : Analytics events for BB do not show up until we restart the app & sometimes even after restarting""","""""""Description:  1. Create an app & replace the app.js with the app.js for analytics test in feature test repo  2. Follow the instructions for rightscale from this wiki page: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan  3. Build & run the app on BB device  4. Now generate the events using the app    Actual Result:  1. We do not see any new analytics events after they are sent but restarting the app shows us the events  2. Sometimes even after restarting the app we do not see the events    Expected Result:  1. We should see the events every time the are sent    """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Analytics events for BB do not show up until we restart the app & sometimes even after restarting
Description: """"Description: 1. Create an app & replace the app.js with the app.js for analytics test in feature test repo 2. Follow the instructions for rightscale from this wiki page: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan 3. Build & run the app on BB device 4. Now generate the events using the app Actual Result: 1. We do not see any new analytics events after they are sent but restarting the app shows us the events 2. Sometimes even after restarting the app we do not see the events Expected Result: 1. We should see the events every time the are sent """"",title+description
TIMOB-13949,12,"""Streamline iOS KrollContext to reduce lock dependancy""","""""""Currently, KrollContext, for every event fired, uses a mutable array that has to be protected by a recursive lock. Given that these actions are a pure producer/consumer model, with one consumer and multiple producers, we can optimize out the locks and make a cleaner implementation that may be reusable, as well.""""""",Story,"Title: Streamline iOS KrollContext to reduce lock dependancy
Description: """"Currently, KrollContext, for every event fired, uses a mutable array that has to be protected by a recursive lock. Given that these actions are a pure producer/consumer model, with one consumer and multiple producers, we can optimize out the locks and make a cleaner implementation that may be reusable, as well.""""",title+description
