TIMOB-13911,12,"""KitchenSink: Set Active Tab index does not show CONTROLS tab""","""""""We see wrong tab with Controls view after setting an active tab index.  Could be considered as regression for phone devices. Tablet has same behavior.  1. Install KS  2. Run Base UI> Tab Groups (in landscape mode for a phone and portrait for a tablet)   3. Tap on Set Active Tab(index)  Actual result:  The view now has control's content, but Tab is """"""""Base UI"""""""".   Expected results:  2:The view should now be 'Controls' (tap on the back button on the phone to see)   Should see Tab changed to 1 old index 0   Active Title Controls old Title BaseUI""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Set Active Tab index does not show CONTROLS tab
Description: """"We see wrong tab with Controls view after setting an active tab index. Could be considered as regression for phone devices. Tablet has same behavior. 1. Install KS 2. Run Base UI> Tab Groups (in landscape mode for a phone and portrait for a tablet) 3. Tap on Set Active Tab(index) Actual result: The view now has control's content, but Tab is """"""""Base UI"""""""". Expected results: 2:The view should now be 'Controls' (tap on the back button on the phone to see) Should see Tab changed to 1 old index 0 Active Title Controls old Title BaseUI""""",title+description
TIMOB-13910,12,"""CLI: node-appc needs to follow the major.minor.point numbering scheme like other projects""","""""""The current versioning scheme for node-appc doesn't allow for multi-branch development like the other products do (e.g. there's no way to work on 3.2.0 and 3.1.1 at the same time). We need to bump to version 1.0.0 and increment the minor version to coincide with the SDK minor version increases.    Note: all other projects that depend on node-appc will need to update their package.json dependencies to match.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: node-appc needs to follow the major.minor.point numbering scheme like other projects
Description: """"The current versioning scheme for node-appc doesn't allow for multi-branch development like the other products do (e.g. there's no way to work on 3.2.0 and 3.1.1 at the same time). We need to bump to version 1.0.0 and increment the minor version to coincide with the SDK minor version increases. Note: all other projects that depend on node-appc will need to update their package.json dependencies to match.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13909,12,"""Android: MenuItem has no id in click event""","""""""*Problem*  MenuItem has only title as a identifier on the click event. This is a very bad idea, when you are building multi language apps. With any other Ti Proxy object, I get the id and all the custom properties in the e.source object.     *Steps to reproduce*  1. Run test case on Android  2. Open the menu - on the emulator this can be done with the circular """"""""Menu"""""""" button  3. Click the item, observe that e.source.customProp returns """"""""undefined""""""""    *Test case*      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: MenuItem has no id in click event
Description: """"*Problem* MenuItem has only title as a identifier on the click event. This is a very bad idea, when you are building multi language apps. With any other Ti Proxy object, I get the id and all the custom properties in the e.source object. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Run test case on Android 2. Open the menu - on the emulator this can be done with the circular """"""""Menu"""""""" button 3. Click the item, observe that e.source.customProp returns """"""""undefined"""""""" *Test case* """"",title+description
TIMOB-13908,12,"""CLI: If the analytics config files in .titanium are not writable, the CLI crashes""","""""""if ~/.titanium/analytics.json or ~/.titanium/analytics_session.json are not writable by the user that the node <USER>is running under, the CLI crashes. In practice, these files are mode 644 by default (writable only by the owner), so running node as anything other than the user that installed the CLI will cause a crash. An easy way to replicate:    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: If the analytics config files in .titanium are not writable, the CLI crashes
Description: """"if ~/.titanium/analytics.json or ~/.titanium/analytics_session.json are not writable by the user that the node <USER>is running under, the CLI crashes. In practice, these files are mode 644 by default (writable only by the owner), so running node as anything other than the user that installed the CLI will cause a crash. An easy way to replicate: """"",title+description
