TIMOB-13869,12,"""CLI: Version in tiapp.xml is stripped to a maximum of 3 dot separated groups""","""""""If specifying a version including a build number as well, ie in tiapp.xml:  {code:xml}<version>1.2.3.1000</version>{code}    When building the project with 'titanium build', the Info.plist that gets generated will only contain a maximum of 3 groups, ie:  {code:xml}<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>  <string>1.2.3</string>  <key>CFBundleVersion</key>  <string>1.2.3</string>{code}    In fact the resulting plist should contain something like:  {code:xml}<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>  <string>1.2.3</string>  <key>CFBundleVersion</key>  <string>1.2.3.1000</string>{code}    This is useful to identify the build number in the final installed app.    This can be fixed in: iphone/cli/commands/_build.js  {code:javascript}plist.CFBundleVersion = appc.version.format(this.tiapp.version, 3, 3);{code}    should in fact be:  {code:javascript}plist.CFBundleVersion = appc.version.format(this.tiapp.version, 3, 4);{code}""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Version in tiapp.xml is stripped to a maximum of 3 dot separated groups
Description: """"If specifying a version including a build number as well, ie in tiapp.xml: {code:xml}<version>1.2.3.1000</version>{code} When building the project with 'titanium build', the Info.plist that gets generated will only contain a maximum of 3 groups, ie: {code:xml}<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key> <string>1.2.3</string> <key>CFBundleVersion</key> <string>1.2.3</string>{code} In fact the resulting plist should contain something like: {code:xml}<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key> <string>1.2.3</string> <key>CFBundleVersion</key> <string>1.2.3.1000</string>{code} This is useful to identify the build number in the final installed app. This can be fixed in: iphone/cli/commands/_build.js {code:javascript}plist.CFBundleVersion = appc.version.format(this.tiapp.version, 3, 3);{code} should in fact be: {code:javascript}plist.CFBundleVersion = appc.version.format(this.tiapp.version, 3, 4);{code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-13868,12,"""Android: ScrollableView pages within ListView not displayed correctly""","""""""*Problem*  The pages of a ScrollableView are not drawn correctly when placed within a ListView.    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Launch the app with the code below.  2. Scroll to the third page on the ScrollableView.  3. Problem: The third page is not displayed (no green background is shown). (The first two pages are displayed correctly).  4. Scroll back to the first page. Problem: This page is now also not displayed anymore.  5. Scroll down the list, so that the ScrollableView leaves the screen.  6. Scroll up again. The first page of the ScrollableView is now displayed correctly again.    Note: Scrolling the ScrollableView within the ListView works much better when the fix of issue TIMOB-13610 is used.    *Test Case*  """"""",Sub-task,"Title: Android: ScrollableView pages within ListView not displayed correctly
Description: """"*Problem* The pages of a ScrollableView are not drawn correctly when placed within a ListView. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Launch the app with the code below. 2. Scroll to the third page on the ScrollableView. 3. Problem: The third page is not displayed (no green background is shown). (The first two pages are displayed correctly). 4. Scroll back to the first page. Problem: This page is now also not displayed anymore. 5. Scroll down the list, so that the ScrollableView leaves the screen. 6. Scroll up again. The first page of the ScrollableView is now displayed correctly again. Note: Scrolling the ScrollableView within the ListView works much better when the fix of issue TIMOB-13610 is used. *Test Case* """"",title+description
TIMOB-13867,12,"""BlackBerry : Studio sample apps with spaces in project name fails to build & gives errors""","""""""Description:  1. Import the todo sample app from studio into the workspace  2. make sure it has 'blackberry' as deployment targets selected in the tiapp.xml  3. Now build & run on BB simulator or device.    Actual Result:  1. The build fails & throws the following errors for Todo app:      Error Logs for RSS Reader app :      Expected Result:  1. The todo app should build & run successfully on the device & the simulator""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Studio sample apps with spaces in project name fails to build & gives errors
Description: """"Description: 1. Import the todo sample app from studio into the workspace 2. make sure it has 'blackberry' as deployment targets selected in the tiapp.xml 3. Now build & run on BB simulator or device. Actual Result: 1. The build fails & throws the following errors for Todo app: Error Logs for RSS Reader app : Expected Result: 1. The todo app should build & run successfully on the device & the simulator""""",title+description
TIMOB-13866,12,"""LiveView doesn't work with FSA 1.0 on iOS simulator when an Alloy .tss file is edited""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. From Studio launch FSA 1.0 on iPad Simulator with Live View enabled.    2. Using Studio edit line 75 of /Field-Service-App/app/styles/my-service-outlets/placard.tss by changing """"""""left: 0"""""""" to """"""""left: 30"""""""".    3. iOS Simulator shows black screen and Studio Console displays this error:    [LiveView] Alloy recompile initiated  [LiveView] Error loading watching file { [Error: ENOENT, readdir '/Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/Resources/iphone/service-outlet-detail']    errno: 34,    code: 'ENOENT',    path: '/Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/Resources/iphone/service-outlet-detail' }  [LiveView] Reload Triggered   -REASON: File Changed   -FILE: /Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/app/styles/my-service-outlets/placard.tss  [INFO] :   [LiveView] Reloading App  [INFO] :   Ti.FieldService/1.0 (3.1.1.d356cff)  [ERROR] :  Error loading path: file://localhost/Users/<USER>Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/6.1/Applications/EBB05FC5-16C3-4506-ACC8-AEBD6E958816/Ti.FieldService.app/app.js, Error Domain=NSCocoaErrorDomain Code=260 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. (Cocoa error 260.)"""""""" UserInfo=0x16344790 {NSFilePath=/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications/EBB05FC5-16C3-4506-ACC8-AEBD6E958816/Ti.FieldService.app/app.js, NSUnderlyingError=0x16347940 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. No such file or directory""""""""}  [ERROR] :  Script Error Could not find the file app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView doesn't work with FSA 1.0 on iOS simulator when an Alloy .tss file is edited
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. From Studio launch FSA 1.0 on iPad Simulator with Live View enabled. 2. Using Studio edit line 75 of /Field-Service-App/app/styles/my-service-outlets/placard.tss by changing """"""""left: 0"""""""" to """"""""left: 30"""""""". 3. iOS Simulator shows black screen and Studio Console displays this error: [LiveView] Alloy recompile initiated [LiveView] Error loading watching file { [Error: ENOENT, readdir '/Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/Resources/iphone/service-outlet-detail'] errno: 34, code: 'ENOENT', path: '/Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/Resources/iphone/service-outlet-detail' } [LiveView] Reload Triggered -REASON: File Changed -FILE: /Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/app/styles/my-service-outlets/placard.tss [INFO] : [LiveView] Reloading App [INFO] : Ti.FieldService/1.0 (3.1.1.d356cff) [ERROR] : Error loading path: file://localhost/Users/<USER>Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/6.1/Applications/EBB05FC5-16C3-4506-ACC8-AEBD6E958816/Ti.FieldService.app/app.js, Error Domain=NSCocoaErrorDomain Code=260 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. (Cocoa error 260.)"""""""" UserInfo=0x16344790 {NSFilePath=/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications/EBB05FC5-16C3-4506-ACC8-AEBD6E958816/Ti.FieldService.app/app.js, NSUnderlyingError=0x16347940 """"""""The operation couldn’t be completed. No such file or directory""""""""} [ERROR] : Script Error Could not find the file app.js """"",title+description
