TIMOB-13855,12,"""iOS: TableView SearchBox width isn't adjusted with presence of index on load""","""""""*Actual behavior*  TableView SearchBox width isn't adjusted with presence of index on load. See attached screenshot.    *Expected behavior*  The search box should be adjusted to the width on load, not just when tapping or scrolling the table view.    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Run the test case  2. See that the width of the search box overlaps the index  3. Tap or scroll table view and see that the search box is now adjusted to the correct width    *index.xml*      *index.js*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView SearchBox width isn't adjusted with presence of index on load
Description: """"*Actual behavior* TableView SearchBox width isn't adjusted with presence of index on load. See attached screenshot. *Expected behavior* The search box should be adjusted to the width on load, not just when tapping or scrolling the table view. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Run the test case 2. See that the width of the search box overlaps the index 3. Tap or scroll table view and see that the search box is now adjusted to the correct width *index.xml* *index.js* """"",title+description
TIMOB-13854,12,"""BlackBerry: Create Navigation Group""","""""""The Navigation Control is used in tabs. It should also be available as standalone like in iOS. It should live like the other platforms in it's one namespace  """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Create Navigation Group
Description: """"The Navigation Control is used in tabs. It should also be available as standalone like in iOS. It should live like the other platforms in it's one namespace """"",title+description
TIMOB-13853,12,"""i18n: textid should use text as hint""","""""""Often I use {{hint}} - the second parameter for {{L}} ({{Ti.Locale.getString}}) - to specify the default (English) text. In this way, I only have to provide a {{strings.xml}} for alternative languages.    I think it would be a small but nice improvement to use the {{text}} property as the {{hint}} when a {{textid}} property is set. Right now, the {{text}} ({{title}}, {{message}} etc.) property is completely ignored if you have a {{textid}} ({{titleid}}, {{messageid}} etc.) property.""""""",New Feature,"Title: i18n: textid should use text as hint
Description: """"Often I use {{hint}} - the second parameter for {{L}} ({{Ti.Locale.getString}}) - to specify the default (English) text. In this way, I only have to provide a {{strings.xml}} for alternative languages. I think it would be a small but nice improvement to use the {{text}} property as the {{hint}} when a {{textid}} property is set. Right now, the {{text}} ({{title}}, {{message}} etc.) property is completely ignored if you have a {{textid}} ({{titleid}}, {{messageid}} etc.) property.""""",title+description
