Description: """"h2. Description In a quite big tableview with around 500 rows when Scrolling the table slowly, there is no problem at all. But on scrolling the table quickly, the app runs out of memory and it crashes h2. Test Code """"",title+description
TIMOB-13851,12,"""LiveView: does not work when editing FSA 1.0 Alloy generated .js files within Studio""","""""""LiveView does not work when editing FSA 1.0 Alloy generated .js files. I tried this both with and without the """"""""app restart"""""""" logic from Allen with the same non-working Live View result. Steps to reproduce:    1. Enable Live View for FSA 1.0.    2. Open this Alloy generated file in Studio:  /Field-Service-App/Resources/alloy/controllers/my-service-outlets/myServiceOutlets.js    3. Insert this line under line 328:  Ti.API.info(""""""""MDL: LiveView detected my change."""""""");    4. Save the file (File > Save) to trigger Live View.     5. Live View will claim to detect the change with this output from Studio's console:  [32m [LiveView][39m  Reload Triggered  [90m  -REASON:[39m  File Changed  [90m  -FILE:[39m  /Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/Resources/alloy/controllers/my-service-outlets/myServiceOutlets.js    5. From within the FSA 1.0 app click the map icon next to """"""""464 Hanover Street"""""""", which should trigger the output from step 3.    6. The output from step 3 is not in the logcat output, which can be verified by running this command from Terminal and not seeing the output from step #3:    adb logcat -d -v threadtime | grep """"""""MDL: LiveView detected my change.""""""""  """"""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: does not work when editing FSA 1.0 Alloy generated .js files within Studio
Description: """"LiveView does not work when editing FSA 1.0 Alloy generated .js files. I tried this both with and without the """"""""app restart"""""""" logic from Allen with the same non-working Live View result. Steps to reproduce: 1. Enable Live View for FSA 1.0. 2. Open this Alloy generated file in Studio: /Field-Service-App/Resources/alloy/controllers/my-service-outlets/myServiceOutlets.js 3. Insert this line under line 328: Ti.API.info(""""""""MDL: LiveView detected my change.""""""""); 4. Save the file (File > Save) to trigger Live View. 5. Live View will claim to detect the change with this output from Studio's console: [32m [LiveView][39m Reload Triggered [90m -REASON:[39m File Changed [90m -FILE:[39m /Users/<USER>Documents/<USER>src/titanium_mobile_repos/forks/field_service_app/Resources/alloy/controllers/my-service-outlets/myServiceOutlets.js 5. From within the FSA 1.0 app click the map icon next to """"""""464 Hanover Street"""""""", which should trigger the output from step 3. 6. The output from step 3 is not in the logcat output, which can be verified by running this command from Terminal and not seeing the output from step #3: adb logcat -d -v threadtime | grep """"""""MDL: LiveView detected my change."""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-13850,12,"""LiveView: Clicking login on field service app (from Studio Sample) throws error.""","""""""h5. Description:  WHile testing using the field service app installed via the Studio Samples pane, clicking the login button with no user or password info (which should work) results in an error being thrown in the console:        h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Import the field sample app via Studio sample pane  2) Enable liveview in run configurations  3) Launch a liveview session in iPad simulator  4) Click login button    h5. Result:  Error thrown as seen above    h5. Expected Result:  No error, prompting for creating sample user and data""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Clicking login on field service app (from Studio Sample) throws error.
Description: """"h5. Description: WHile testing using the field service app installed via the Studio Samples pane, clicking the login button with no user or password info (which should work) results in an error being thrown in the console: h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Import the field sample app via Studio sample pane 2) Enable liveview in run configurations 3) Launch a liveview session in iPad simulator 4) Click login button h5. Result: Error thrown as seen above h5. Expected Result: No error, prompting for creating sample user and data""""",title+description
TIMOB-13849,12,"""LiveView: Alloy project files emptied of contents in error condition where multiple node processes are spawned""","""""""h5. Description:  While attempting to recreate the issue where the combination of Alloy and Liveview produces hundreds of node processes, I noticed after a few attempts that my files where still there but the content was gone.     I thought this might be related to me running """"""""killall node"""""""" when the processes started to multiply, but <USER>had experienced this as well and did not use this technique.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  Steps to reproduce are difficult since this might be related to the repro steps of the other bug, and if not carefully monitored it requires a hard restart.  0) Ensure you have no space in the path to <USER>Studio plugin folder  1) Import field services app from Studio sample pane  2) Set run configuration to use liveview  3) Open terminal and type """"""""killall node"""""""" but do not hit enter (this will allow you to recover form error condition without restart)  4) Launch <USER>s handy script to monitor processes (see related bug for script)  5) make an edit to the field service app (use App/my-service-outlets/myServiceOutlets.js)  6) When <USER>s script shows more than 20 or so processes, move to the """"""""killall node"""""""" terminal created earlier and hit enter.  7) Close and reopen the Studio editor for the myServiceOutlets.js file. If still populated, repeat.      h5. Result:  The file is present but the contents are gone.    h5. Expected Result:  Files remain unedited by the <USER>""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Alloy project files emptied of contents in error condition where multiple node processes are spawned
Description: """"h5. Description: While attempting to recreate the issue where the combination of Alloy and Liveview produces hundreds of node processes, I noticed after a few attempts that my files where still there but the content was gone. I thought this might be related to me running """"""""killall node"""""""" when the processes started to multiply, but <USER>had experienced this as well and did not use this technique. h5. Steps to reproduce: Steps to reproduce are difficult since this might be related to the repro steps of the other bug, and if not carefully monitored it requires a hard restart. 0) Ensure you have no space in the path to <USER>Studio plugin folder 1) Import field services app from Studio sample pane 2) Set run configuration to use liveview 3) Open terminal and type """"""""killall node"""""""" but do not hit enter (this will allow you to recover form error condition without restart) 4) Launch <USER>s handy script to monitor processes (see related bug for script) 5) make an edit to the field service app (use App/my-service-outlets/myServiceOutlets.js) 6) When <USER>s script shows more than 20 or so processes, move to the """"""""killall node"""""""" terminal created earlier and hit enter. 7) Close and reopen the Studio editor for the myServiceOutlets.js file. If still populated, repeat. h5. Result: The file is present but the contents are gone. h5. Expected Result: Files remain unedited by the <USER>""",title+description
TIMOB-13848,12,"""Android: TextArea loses focus when the string wraps and changes the height of the view""","""""""*Problem*  When the user types anything that makes the text area wrap down to the next line, thus extending the height of the TextArea, it loses focus. The keyboard stays up but nothing shows up when keys are pressed.    *Steps to reproduce*  1. Create a new blank Alloy project  2. Add the controller, style and view.xml from the .rar file and add the code below to index.js  3. Run on Android  4. Enter text into the TextField until it wraps to the next line  5. Observe that the TextField loses focus    *index.js*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextArea loses focus when the string wraps and changes the height of the view
