TIMOB-13829,12,"""BlackBerry: Fix Ti.UI.SIZE - Buttons and Labels are going to 0 size""","""""""Code to reproduce issue:    {code: javascript}  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       backgroundColor:'#000'  });    var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({     color:'#999',     text:'Label Test',     font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue',fontStyle:'italic'},     width: Ti.UI.SIZE,     height: Ti.UI.SIZE  });    win1.add(label1);  win1.open();    {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Fix Ti.UI.SIZE - Buttons and Labels are going to 0 size
Description: """"Code to reproduce issue: {code: javascript} var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#000' }); var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({ color:'#999', text:'Label Test', font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue',fontStyle:'italic'}, width: Ti.UI.SIZE, height: Ti.UI.SIZE }); win1.add(label1); win1.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-13828,12,"""MobileWeb: Apps do not work when hosted in a subdirectory""","""""""Mobile Web apps do not run if the contents are put in a subdirectory. We need to wire up the baseUrl config option and make sure all requests take into account this baseUrl such as images.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Apps do not work when hosted in a subdirectory
Description: """"Mobile Web apps do not run if the contents are put in a subdirectory. We need to wire up the baseUrl config option and make sure all requests take into account this baseUrl such as images.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13827,12,"""Code Processor: Get alloy to recompile before an analysis""","""""""The code processor analysis the generated code from Alloy projects, not the original source. To prevent developer heartache, the code processor should have alloy generate new code each time. This can be accomplished via a hook since the code processor is now a CLI command""""""",New Feature,"Title: Code Processor: Get alloy to recompile before an analysis
Description: """"The code processor analysis the generated code from Alloy projects, not the original source. To prevent developer heartache, the code processor should have alloy generate new code each time. This can be accomplished via a hook since the code processor is now a CLI command""""",title+description
TIMOB-13826,12,"""iOS: ti.cloud not found in iOS 6 and iOS 5""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When you try to use/add ti.cloud in a program running in iOS 5 or iOS6, you will get an """"""""ti.cloud not found"""""""".     h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new mobile project.  2. Add this to app.js:    3. Run the app.     h4. Actual results   if you run this in iOS 6.1, will work just fine. IF you try this in iOS 6 or iOS 5, you will get:         h4. Extra info  http://developer.<USER>com/question/151843/problem-with-ticloud-sdk-310-and-ios-51    h4. Workaround  Solved the issue by:  Installing the ti.cloud module into the project from https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.cloud/blob/master/commonjs/ti.cloud-commonjs-2.3.3.zip?raw=true  symbolically linking ti.cloud.js into Resources/ui/module/ (cd Resources/ui/module ; ln -sf ../../../modules/commonjs/ti.cloud/2.3.3/ti.cloud.js)  initializing it as var Cloud = require('ui/module/ti.cloud');""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ti.cloud not found in iOS 6 and iOS 5
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When you try to use/add ti.cloud in a program running in iOS 5 or iOS6, you will get an """"""""ti.cloud not found"""""""". h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new mobile project. 2. Add this to app.js: 3. Run the app. h4. Actual results if you run this in iOS 6.1, will work just fine. IF you try this in iOS 6 or iOS 5, you will get: h4. Extra info http://developer.<USER>com/question/151843/problem-with-ticloud-sdk-310-and-ios-51 h4. Workaround Solved the issue by: Installing the ti.cloud module into the project from https://github.com/<USER>modules/ti.cloud/blob/master/commonjs/ti.cloud-commonjs-2.3.3.zip?raw=true symbolically linking ti.cloud.js into Resources/ui/module/ (cd Resources/ui/module ; ln -sf ../../../modules/commonjs/ti.cloud/2.3.3/ti.cloud.js) initializing it as var Cloud = require('ui/module/ti.cloud');""""",title+description
