TIMOB-13779,12,"""Android: remove access to V8's gc from JavaScript""","""""""Access to V8's gc from JavaScript was inadvertently introduced into the public API as a part of integrating the V8 profiler. This should be corrected and access to V8's gc from JavaScript should be removed.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: remove access to V8's gc from JavaScript
Description: """"Access to V8's gc from JavaScript was inadvertently introduced into the public API as a part of integrating the V8 profiler. This should be corrected and access to V8's gc from JavaScript should be removed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13778,12,"""Android: Maps V2 module - selecting a map pin pops up an annotation that runs off the edge of the screen""","""""""h6.Issue  When an annotation is selected using the selectAnnotation function or when a pin is clicked on the map the map view used to automatically move so that the annotation title and subtitle would be visible.     This is how the native google maps application and current TiMap View object performs. Sample attached reproduces on TiMapView object. Tap on """"""""Open TiMapView"""""""" row.    Using the V2 Maps module when an annotation is selected using the function or when a pin is clicked the map stay stationary and the annotation is shown with half or more of it potentially cut off. Tap on """"""""Open MapModule"""""""" row.    h6.Actual behavior  selecting a map pin pops up an annotation that runs off the edge of the screen,     h6.Expected behavior  the map should move so that the annotation title and subtitle are fully visible.    h6.snippet      Testing Steps:    1. Click on """"""""Open MapModule""""""""  2. Click on an annotation, it should be centered.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Maps V2 module - selecting a map pin pops up an annotation that runs off the edge of the screen
Description: """"h6.Issue When an annotation is selected using the selectAnnotation function or when a pin is clicked on the map the map view used to automatically move so that the annotation title and subtitle would be visible. This is how the native google maps application and current TiMap View object performs. Sample attached reproduces on TiMapView object. Tap on """"""""Open TiMapView"""""""" row. Using the V2 Maps module when an annotation is selected using the function or when a pin is clicked the map stay stationary and the annotation is shown with half or more of it potentially cut off. Tap on """"""""Open MapModule"""""""" row. h6.Actual behavior selecting a map pin pops up an annotation that runs off the edge of the screen, h6.Expected behavior the map should move so that the annotation title and subtitle are fully visible. h6.snippet Testing Steps: 1. Click on """"""""Open MapModule"""""""" 2. Click on an annotation, it should be centered. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13777,12,"""BlackBerry - Setting left and right does not calculate the width. The same thing with top and bottom.""","""""""Take the following example. You should see a white margin around this red view. Instead you'll see that margin only on the top and left side of the view.  """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry - Setting left and right does not calculate the width. The same thing with top and bottom.
Description: """"Take the following example. You should see a white margin around this red view. Instead you'll see that margin only on the top and left side of the view. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13776,12,"""ti.background events are not sent until the next app session start""","""""""Vasil and I observed while tailing logs of events sent by both the ipad/iphone simulator and from actual devices that end events are buffered in the device until a subsequent session starts again.    In other words we're seeing:    ti.enroll  ti.start  (flush batch to server)  ti.background  … time passes between sessions.. simulator is restarted…   ti.start  (flush batch to server)  ti.background  etc...    Is the policy that a flush happens after a start event (ti.start ti.foreground) or is it based on a timeout or number of event threshold?    This messes up active session calculation by realtime analytics since the session will only be ended when the next session starts (if ever). It seems that if the app is backgrounded or killed gracefully, the final ti.background event could be sent to api.<USER>net in a background task when the app enters the inactive state (on iOS at least).""""""",Bug,"Title: ti.background events are not sent until the next app session start
Description: """"Vasil and I observed while tailing logs of events sent by both the ipad/iphone simulator and from actual devices that end events are buffered in the device until a subsequent session starts again. In other words we're seeing: ti.enroll ti.start (flush batch to server) ti.background … time passes between sessions.. simulator is restarted… ti.start (flush batch to server) ti.background etc... Is the policy that a flush happens after a start event (ti.start ti.foreground) or is it based on a timeout or number of event threshold? This messes up active session calculation by realtime analytics since the session will only be ended when the next session starts (if ever). It seems that if the app is backgrounded or killed gracefully, the final ti.background event could be sent to api.<USER>net in a background task when the app enters the inactive state (on iOS at least).""""",title+description
TIMOB-13775,12,"""CLI: Android: Build fails if default AVD id is not found""","""""""When building for Android and the AVD id is not passed in or invalid, the Android build should attempt to find Android SDK 8 or newer.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android: Build fails if default AVD id is not found
Description: """"When building for Android and the AVD id is not passed in or invalid, the Android build should attempt to find Android SDK 8 or newer.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13773,12,"""MobileWeb: MapView creates duplicate markers""","""""""When running the Sample.Mapping app on Mobile Web, it creates map markers twice. There's allow the possibility this is also causing multiple events to be dispatched at the same time and cause an error.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: MapView creates duplicate markers
Description: """"When running the Sample.Mapping app on Mobile Web, it creates map markers twice. There's allow the possibility this is also causing multiple events to be dispatched at the same time and cause an error.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13769,12,"""Android: Nine-patch image does not work on emulator when fastdev is enabled""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Set """"""""<property name=""""""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" type=""""""""bool"""""""">true</property>"""""""" in tiapp.xml.  2. Run KS->Controls->Slider->Min/Max Range on emulator and see the slider image is not displayed correctly.    Note: if we set """"""""<property name=""""""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" type=""""""""bool"""""""">false</property>"""""""", the slider shows fine.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Nine-patch image does not work on emulator when fastdev is enabled
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Set """"""""<property name=""""""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" type=""""""""bool"""""""">true</property>"""""""" in tiapp.xml. 2. Run KS->Controls->Slider->Min/Max Range on emulator and see the slider image is not displayed correctly. Note: if we set """"""""<property name=""""""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" type=""""""""bool"""""""">false</property>"""""""", the slider shows fine.""""",title+description
