TIMOB-13737,12,"""ListSection.setItems() does not respect {animated:false}""","""""""h2. problem    [Ti.UI.ListSection.setItems|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.ListSection-method-setItems] takes a second parameter on iOS that allows you to specify a [ListViewAnimationProperties|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/ListViewAnimationProperties] object. In this object one of the properties is *animated*. Setting *animated* to *false* for this parameter should prevent the items from animating down when they are added to the ListView. Despite setting animated to false, the items still animate.    h2. expected    ListItems will be added but not animated when the 2nd parameter to setItems() is set like this         h2. test case     You'll notice when running this on iOS that no matter what the value of the object for the second parameter in setItems() the items will still animate down from the top when added.    """"""",Bug,"Title: ListSection.setItems() does not respect {animated:false}
