TIMOB-13726,12,"""Android: Ensure the minimum version is updated""","""""""As Android 2.3.2 and earlier has dropped into single digits long ago, TiMob 3.1.1 will drop it for testing, performance, and other reasons. The code should reflect this, if nothing else, in making sure the manifest's api version moves to 10, and that the CLI does not override this and pull it down to 8.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Ensure the minimum version is updated
Description: """"As Android 2.3.2 and earlier has dropped into single digits long ago, TiMob 3.1.1 will drop it for testing, performance, and other reasons. The code should reflect this, if nothing else, in making sure the manifest's api version moves to 10, and that the CLI does not override this and pull it down to 8.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13725,12,"""iOS: Ensure the minimum version is updated""","""""""As iOS 4.x has dropped into single digits long ago, TiMob 3.1.1 will drop it for testing, performance, and other reasons. The code should reflect this, if nothing else, in making sure the info.plist's Target SDK moves to 5.0, and that the CLI does not override this and pull it down to 4.x.""""""",Story,"Title: iOS: Ensure the minimum version is updated
Description: """"As iOS 4.x has dropped into single digits long ago, TiMob 3.1.1 will drop it for testing, performance, and other reasons. The code should reflect this, if nothing else, in making sure the info.plist's Target SDK moves to 5.0, and that the CLI does not override this and pull it down to 4.x.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13724,12,"""Android: Maps V2: One mapView added over another mapView will be displayed only once until user performs some other device activity""","""""""Adding one map view over another map view does not display map until we do some other activity and then launch the app.    Steps to reproduce:  1: Use the below mentioned code as sample to test.  2: build the app using MapModule.  3: deploy the app in android device and launch the app.  4: press add one more map button.  5: Second map is not displayed till now.  6: press the recent app button if using nexus or some other activity.  7: open app again and it will display map 2.    **Sample code**  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Maps V2: One mapView added over another mapView will be displayed only once until user performs some other device activity
Description: """"Adding one map view over another map view does not display map until we do some other activity and then launch the app. Steps to reproduce: 1: Use the below mentioned code as sample to test. 2: build the app using MapModule. 3: deploy the app in android device and launch the app. 4: press add one more map button. 5: Second map is not displayed till now. 6: press the recent app button if using nexus or some other activity. 7: open app again and it will display map 2. **Sample code** """"",title+description
