TIMOB-13618,12,"""iOS: leftPadding on textfield causes clicking issues""","""""""*Problem description*  When using leftPadding on a textfield it causes the textfield to become quite user un-friendly.    There are two main issues:    1) Even though you only add say 20px of leftPadding, almost 100px of the field becomes un-clickable.    2) The same space does not react to a longpress for magnifying glass i.e. 100px from the left is un-clickable what's so ever. So for example if you managed to type text into the box, you cannot edit text that appears in the first 100px of the field, unless you first long-press to the right hand side and drag to the left.    *Expected behavior*  Can click within the padded area to activate the text field and longpress to reveal the magnifying glass.    *Actual behavior*  Cannot click within the padded area to activate the text field or longpress to reveal the magnifying glass.    *Test case*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: leftPadding on textfield causes clicking issues
Description: """"*Problem description* When using leftPadding on a textfield it causes the textfield to become quite user un-friendly. There are two main issues: 1) Even though you only add say 20px of leftPadding, almost 100px of the field becomes un-clickable. 2) The same space does not react to a longpress for magnifying glass i.e. 100px from the left is un-clickable what's so ever. So for example if you managed to type text into the box, you cannot edit text that appears in the first 100px of the field, unless you first long-press to the right hand side and drag to the left. *Expected behavior* Can click within the padded area to activate the text field and longpress to reveal the magnifying glass. *Actual behavior* Cannot click within the padded area to activate the text field or longpress to reveal the magnifying glass. *Test case* """"",title+description
TIMOB-13617,12,"""BlackBerry : Using the CLI, locale resources are not copied in the build folder after building the project""","""""""This is a regression. When python scripts are used to build the project the 'i18n' folder is copied to the assets folder but not with the CLI    Description:  1. Create an app for BlackBerry which has locale functionality e.g the single window app from the default templates in studio  2. Build & run the app on BlackBerry simulator/device  3. Now go to the app project in studio & expand the build folder  4. Under assets folder check if folder named 'i18n' is present    Actual Result:  1. The 'i18n' folder for localization does not get copied in assets in build folder    Expected Result:  1. The 'i18n' folder gets copied in to the assets folder  """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Using the CLI, locale resources are not copied in the build folder after building the project
Description: """"This is a regression. When python scripts are used to build the project the 'i18n' folder is copied to the assets folder but not with the CLI Description: 1. Create an app for BlackBerry which has locale functionality e.g the single window app from the default templates in studio 2. Build & run the app on BlackBerry simulator/device 3. Now go to the app project in studio & expand the build folder 4. Under assets folder check if folder named 'i18n' is present Actual Result: 1. The 'i18n' folder for localization does not get copied in assets in build folder Expected Result: 1. The 'i18n' folder gets copied in to the assets folder """"",title+description
