TIMOB-13589,12,"""Debugger: using Alloy, Android has an unexpected behavior if setting a breakpoint next to a function declaration""","""""""h5. Problem description    The issue is probably related to the debugger behavior on Android, as described in https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13586    See Alloy sample code:    h6. index.xml      h6. index.js      1. Set a breakpoint next to the function declaration (index.js, line 1) and debug.   Result: the debugger breaks when the app is started instead of when the function is triggered clicking on the label. In that case, in the Debug window the generated """"""""Resources/alloy/controllers/index.js"""""""" file is shown instead of the """"""""app/controllers/index.js"""""""" file.    See screenshot.    2. Click on the label.  Result: function doClick() is triggered, breakpoint is being ignored.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Debugger: using Alloy, Android has an unexpected behavior if setting a breakpoint next to a function declaration
Description: """"h5. Problem description The issue is probably related to the debugger behavior on Android, as described in https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-13586 See Alloy sample code: h6. index.xml h6. index.js 1. Set a breakpoint next to the function declaration (index.js, line 1) and debug. Result: the debugger breaks when the app is started instead of when the function is triggered clicking on the label. In that case, in the Debug window the generated """"""""Resources/alloy/controllers/index.js"""""""" file is shown instead of the """"""""app/controllers/index.js"""""""" file. See screenshot. 2. Click on the label. Result: function doClick() is triggered, breakpoint is being ignored. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13586,12,"""Debugger: Android and iOS different behavior when setting a breakpoint on a function declaration""","""""""h5. Problem description  Android and iOS behave in a different way when setting breakpoints on function declaration.    See sample code:      If a breakpoint is set on line 5 ( function test(){ ) , on Android it actually breaks at line 6 after triggering the 'click' event on the view.  On iOS it breaks on line 5.     If setting breakpoints for both lines 5 and 6, on Android it only breaks once at line 6, while on iOS it breaks for both.    If setting breakpoints both on line 6, it works correctly as expected for both the platforms.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Debugger: Android and iOS different behavior when setting a breakpoint on a function declaration
Description: """"h5. Problem description Android and iOS behave in a different way when setting breakpoints on function declaration. See sample code: If a breakpoint is set on line 5 ( function test(){ ) , on Android it actually breaks at line 6 after triggering the 'click' event on the view. On iOS it breaks on line 5. If setting breakpoints for both lines 5 and 6, on Android it only breaks once at line 6, while on iOS it breaks for both. If setting breakpoints both on line 6, it works correctly as expected for both the platforms. """"",title+description
