TIMOB-13558,12,"""Android: Button with a touchstart event can look disabled if you call setEnabled(true)""","""""""h6.Problem  if you have a Button with a touchstart event it can look disabled if you call setEnabled(true) after the button is clicked. If they use a touchend, or click event then this issue is not present or if I use the 2.1.3.GA sdk then this issue does not occur with the touchstart event.    h6.To reproduce  1. Install this app to a android device.   2. Launch ADB so you can see when the buttons are pressed.   3. Click Button 1, watch the logs to verify the button was clicked.   4. Click Enable Button 1  5. Notice that Button 1 is now in a depressed state.   6. Click on Button 1, notice it clicked and is now in a enabled state  7. Click Enable BUtton  8. Notice its back to the depressed state.    h6. == app.js ==      h6. == FirstView.js ==  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Button with a touchstart event can look disabled if you call setEnabled(true)
Description: """"h6.Problem if you have a Button with a touchstart event it can look disabled if you call setEnabled(true) after the button is clicked. If they use a touchend, or click event then this issue is not present or if I use the 2.1.3.GA sdk then this issue does not occur with the touchstart event. h6.To reproduce 1. Install this app to a android device. 2. Launch ADB so you can see when the buttons are pressed. 3. Click Button 1, watch the logs to verify the button was clicked. 4. Click Enable Button 1 5. Notice that Button 1 is now in a depressed state. 6. Click on Button 1, notice it clicked and is now in a enabled state 7. Click Enable BUtton 8. Notice its back to the depressed state. h6. == app.js == h6. == FirstView.js == """"",title+description
TIMOB-13557,12,"""iOS: Ti.Map.View.removeAnnotations doesn't work + solution. ""","""""""Q&A link to issue and solution.    http://developer.<USER>com/question/146932/how-to-delete-an-array-of-annotations#answer-260727      In following code ENSURE_TYPE makes array with one element which is array of annotations.      to resolve it we must replace         with more correct      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Map.View.removeAnnotations doesn't work + solution.
Description: """"Q&A link to issue and solution. http://developer.<USER>com/question/146932/how-to-delete-an-array-of-annotations#answer-260727 In following code ENSURE_TYPE makes array with one element which is array of annotations. to resolve it we must replace with more correct """"",title+description
TIMOB-13555,12,"""MobileWeb: Cannot change Content-Type passing an object in the send() method of Ti.Network.HTTPClient""","""""""h2. Problem description  When trying to change the Content-Type of the HTTPClient request (e.g. to set it to application/json), the header sent still contains the default application/json,application/x-www-form-urlencoded value, in addition to what was set.    h2. Steps to reproduce    Use the following code:        When running the code in MobileWeb, the Content-Type header will contain:    Content-Type: application/json, application/x-www-form-urlencoded    h2. Additional notes  According to the XMLHttpRequest specifications, setRequestHeader will add the request header when called, and not replace it. Apparently, """"""""application/x-www-form-urlencoded"""""""" is always set if any data is sent.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Cannot change Content-Type passing an object in the send() method of Ti.Network.HTTPClient
Description: """"h2. Problem description When trying to change the Content-Type of the HTTPClient request (e.g. to set it to application/json), the header sent still contains the default application/json,application/x-www-form-urlencoded value, in addition to what was set. h2. Steps to reproduce Use the following code: When running the code in MobileWeb, the Content-Type header will contain: Content-Type: application/json, application/x-www-form-urlencoded h2. Additional notes According to the XMLHttpRequest specifications, setRequestHeader will add the request header when called, and not replace it. Apparently, """"""""application/x-www-form-urlencoded"""""""" is always set if any data is sent.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13554,12,"""LiveView: Unable to run an Alloy app through LiveView""","""""""h4. Steps to reproduce    # Install LiveView from https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tools/LiveView  # Create a new Alloy project  # Run the project from the command line using a command like (replace the appropriate spots): \\    # Now do the same, but add the --liveview flag to the end.    h4. Result    I've gotten a number of different behaviors.    * A syntax error in app.js  * [DEBUG] Bad plugin hooks that failed to load: [DEBUG] /usr/local/lib/node_modules/liveview/hook/lvhook.js""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: Unable to run an Alloy app through LiveView
Description: """"h4. Steps to reproduce # Install LiveView from https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tools/LiveView # Create a new Alloy project # Run the project from the command line using a command like (replace the appropriate spots): \\ # Now do the same, but add the --liveview flag to the end. h4. Result I've gotten a number of different behaviors. * A syntax error in app.js * [DEBUG] Bad plugin hooks that failed to load: [DEBUG] /usr/local/lib/node_modules/liveview/hook/lvhook.js""""",title+description
TIMOB-13550,12,"""CLI: LiveView process messages result in a Studio freeze or error of some kind""","""""""iOS Device Run Config: unable to create config with unknown char error: closing running liveview <USER>id.    Probably related to a previous liveview run, using either android device or iphone simulator.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create an iOS Device run configuration.    Actual Result:    Failure. Every time.    Expected Result:    Config created successfully, even if liveview was run at some previous time.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: LiveView process messages result in a Studio freeze or error of some kind
Description: """"iOS Device Run Config: unable to create config with unknown char error: closing running liveview <USER>id. Probably related to a previous liveview run, using either android device or iphone simulator. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an iOS Device run configuration. Actual Result: Failure. Every time. Expected Result: Config created successfully, even if liveview was run at some previous time.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13549,12,"""CLI: node-appc: When building for device from studio or CLI, an execvp(): No such file or directory error is printed to the console""","""""""*Note* this did not prevent the app from being installed to the device, nor cause nay bad behavior when launching or running the app    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a default titanium classic app  2. Run it on device    Actaul result:  The app is installed to device but the following error is printed to the console    execvp(): No such file or directory  [ERROR] Install app failed with exit code 127    *CLI output attached*    Expected result:  There isn't an error when installed to device""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: node-appc: When building for device from studio or CLI, an execvp(): No such file or directory error is printed to the console
Description: """"*Note* this did not prevent the app from being installed to the device, nor cause nay bad behavior when launching or running the app Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a default titanium classic app 2. Run it on device Actaul result: The app is installed to device but the following error is printed to the console execvp(): No such file or directory [ERROR] Install app failed with exit code 127 *CLI output attached* Expected result: There isn't an error when installed to device""""",title+description
