TIMOB-13544,12,"""TiAPI: bubbleParent property not being set properly on both iOS and Android""","""""""*Problem description*  the bubbleParent property is not being set correctly, on Android and iOS for creation of a button, and on iOS only when using the setter function.    *Test case*  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor : """"""""#FFF""""""""  });    try {   var button1 = Ti.UI.createButton({    bubbleParent : false,   });   Ti.API.info('button1 bubbleParent:false = ' + button1.getBubbleParent());   button1.setBubbleParent(false);   Ti.API.info('button1 setBubbleParent(false) = ' + button1.getBubbleParent());   win.add(button1);  } catch (e) {   Ti.API.error('button1 getBubbleParent() error:' + e);  }    win.open();      *Logs: iOS*  {code:lang=none|title=console}  button1 bubbleParent:false = 0  button1 setBubbleParent(false) = true  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: bubbleParent property not being set properly on both iOS and Android
Description: """"*Problem description* the bubbleParent property is not being set correctly, on Android and iOS for creation of a button, and on iOS only when using the setter function. *Test case* {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : """"""""#FFF"""""""" }); try { var button1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ bubbleParent : false, }); Ti.API.info('button1 bubbleParent:false = ' + button1.getBubbleParent()); button1.setBubbleParent(false); Ti.API.info('button1 setBubbleParent(false) = ' + button1.getBubbleParent()); win.add(button1); } catch (e) { Ti.API.error('button1 getBubbleParent() error:' + e); } win.open(); *Logs: iOS* {code:lang=none|title=console} button1 bubbleParent:false = 0 button1 setBubbleParent(false) = true {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-13543,12,"""Android: add support for activityEnterAnimation and activityExitAnimation for Window.close method""","""""""*Problem*  The ability to animate enter and exit activities on opening windows is working fine, but this is only useful when you need to progress forward in an apps UI. If one wants to close windows and go backwards (hit the back button) they cannot use the animations which only work on win.open() and not on win.close(). The pull request below allows the ability to use the activityAnimations when closing a window.    test case for the pull request  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: add support for activityEnterAnimation and activityExitAnimation for Window.close method
Description: """"*Problem* The ability to animate enter and exit activities on opening windows is working fine, but this is only useful when you need to progress forward in an apps UI. If one wants to close windows and go backwards (hit the back button) they cannot use the animations which only work on win.open() and not on win.close(). The pull request below allows the ability to use the activityAnimations when closing a window. test case for the pull request """"",title+description
TIMOB-13542,12,"""Android: single click on a textField does not open the soft keyboard""","""""""h5. Problem description When clicking on a non-focused TextField, the soft keyboard is not automatically shown.  Not reproducible with TiSDK 3.0.2 GA - Regression  h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new project with two text fields/ text areas (see sample code) 2. Run the project Result: first text field is focused by default 3. Click on the second field Result: second field get focused, but the soft keyboard does not show 4. Click on the second field again Result: soft keyboard is now shown 5. Click on the back button and then on the first field Result: soft keyboard is hidden, then clicking on the first field only the focus and the i-beam is moved, but no soft keyboard is shown. User has to click again on the field to have the keyboard being displayed.  h6. Sample code """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: single click on a textField does not open the soft keyboard
Description: """"h5. Problem description When clicking on a non-focused TextField, the soft keyboard is not automatically shown. Not reproducible with TiSDK 3.0.2 GA - Regression h5. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new project with two text fields/ text areas (see sample code) 2. Run the project Result: first text field is focused by default 3. Click on the second field Result: second field get focused, but the soft keyboard does not show 4. Click on the second field again Result: soft keyboard is now shown 5. Click on the back button and then on the first field Result: soft keyboard is hidden, then clicking on the first field only the focus and the i-beam is moved, but no soft keyboard is shown. User has to click again on the field to have the keyboard being displayed. h6. Sample code """"",title+description
TIMOB-13541,12,"""Android Emulator: Python scripts async activities can intermittently cause multiple failure messages""","""""""h5. Description:  While investigating some android emulator failures, we encountered a dual error which we believe is related to the async nature of some areas of the python. There are two sections of code that when run independently and there is a failure, could conceivably both produce a build failure error. We encountered this:    Please note the two build failure messages      h5. Steps to reproduce:  Note: This will be difficult to reproduce. Here are the recommended steps:  1) Build an android project for emulator using a new AVD (this will cause a timeout due to TIMOB-9153)  2) Watch for the build failure    h5. Result:  Sometimes the build will fail, and some of those times, you will get two build failure notifications.    h5. Expected Result:  No failure, but if so, a single notification of the failure  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android Emulator: Python scripts async activities can intermittently cause multiple failure messages
Description: """"h5. Description: While investigating some android emulator failures, we encountered a dual error which we believe is related to the async nature of some areas of the python. There are two sections of code that when run independently and there is a failure, could conceivably both produce a build failure error. We encountered this: Please note the two build failure messages h5. Steps to reproduce: Note: This will be difficult to reproduce. Here are the recommended steps: 1) Build an android project for emulator using a new AVD (this will cause a timeout due to TIMOB-9153) 2) Watch for the build failure h5. Result: Sometimes the build will fail, and some of those times, you will get two build failure notifications. h5. Expected Result: No failure, but if so, a single notification of the failure """"",title+description
TIMOB-13539,12,"""Android: intermittent Packaging succeeds, app freezes at splash screen""","""""""Android: Packaging succeeds, app freezes at splash screen.    This is a regression. Works in Titanium Studio 3.0.2 (no Android CLI).    Runtime error:        Titanium Studio 3.0.2 w/o CLI (app loads successfuly):        Titanium Studio 3.1.0 w/CLI (build succeeds, app fails to load):        Test Steps:    1. Open Titanium Studio 3.1.0.  2. Create Titanium Project.  3. Package > Android (Google APIs 2.2).  4. Run on Device (Android 4.1.1).    Test Result:    Packaging operation succeeds, app freezes on splash screen at launch. This works in Titanium Studio 3.0.2 using the old python build script.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: intermittent Packaging succeeds, app freezes at splash screen
Description: """"Android: Packaging succeeds, app freezes at splash screen. This is a regression. Works in Titanium Studio 3.0.2 (no Android CLI). Runtime error: Titanium Studio 3.0.2 w/o CLI (app loads successfuly): Titanium Studio 3.1.0 w/CLI (build succeeds, app fails to load): Test Steps: 1. Open Titanium Studio 3.1.0. 2. Create Titanium Project. 3. Package > Android (Google APIs 2.2). 4. Run on Device (Android 4.1.1). Test Result: Packaging operation succeeds, app freezes on splash screen at launch. This works in Titanium Studio 3.0.2 using the old python build script.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13538,12,"""Android: Table view scrolling freezes after toggle""","""""""*Problem description*  --I have a table with several images that can be clicked and basically represent yes/no.  It is really a 4 value system.  The images should only change if you have tapped the image.  If you change one of the images and then scroll the table, random images in that column change to the value that you changed.  If you scroll the window before clicking an image, the images do not randomly change.  It doesn't seem to happen on iOS (this example may not format properly using iOS.)  It appears that just the display is messed up because I do a count of the image settings after doing a click on one of the images and the image setting count is correct.  Attached is the project in compress format.--    *Appc Update*  The images randomly changing seems to have been fixed in 3.1 CI, but now the table view """"""""freezes"""""""" once one of the images has been toggled.    *Test case*  See attachment.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Table view scrolling freezes after toggle
Description: """"*Problem description* --I have a table with several images that can be clicked and basically represent yes/no. It is really a 4 value system. The images should only change if you have tapped the image. If you change one of the images and then scroll the table, random images in that column change to the value that you changed. If you scroll the window before clicking an image, the images do not randomly change. It doesn't seem to happen on iOS (this example may not format properly using iOS.) It appears that just the display is messed up because I do a count of the image settings after doing a click on one of the images and the image setting count is correct. Attached is the project in compress format.-- *Appc Update* The images randomly changing seems to have been fixed in 3.1 CI, but now the table view """"""""freezes"""""""" once one of the images has been toggled. *Test case* See attachment.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13537,12,"""Android: Emulator launch choking on stdin""","""""""in android's _build.py, the """"""""detached"""""""" emulator <USER>seems to be freezing the android emulator on a regular basis. Redirecting stdin to null is making it work properly. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Emulator launch choking on stdin
Description: """"in android's _build.py, the """"""""detached"""""""" emulator <USER>seems to be freezing the android emulator on a regular basis. Redirecting stdin to null is making it work properly. """"",title+description
