TIMOB-13533,12,"""Android: Emulator fails with IndexError: list index out of range""","""""""h5. Description:  While trying to validate a related bug, we were unable to run the emulator. We saw a variety of strange behavior related to this, but the end result is no emulator run. At best we were able to launch the emulator, but no app was installed or launched. We see some of the following:    h6. Failure one:  Emulator launches, no console output in Studio. No app launch in emulator. Clicking terminate in studio gets you a single error line in the console.    h6. Failure two:  Emulator launch from studio fails with:      If you run the simulator over and over with this failure, the processes just sit there so you must kill all previous run attempts.    Running with an SDK build back (3.1.0.v20130305095817) gets you:      And the emulator launches.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a project in studio (Using SDK 3.1.0.v20130410180128  2) Try to launch in the emulator    h5. Result:  Launch failure either with emulator launch but no app, or with console errors.  Previous launch attempts stay active    h5. Expected Result:  The emulator launches and the app is shown  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Emulator fails with IndexError: list index out of range
Description: """"h5. Description: While trying to validate a related bug, we were unable to run the emulator. We saw a variety of strange behavior related to this, but the end result is no emulator run. At best we were able to launch the emulator, but no app was installed or launched. We see some of the following: h6. Failure one: Emulator launches, no console output in Studio. No app launch in emulator. Clicking terminate in studio gets you a single error line in the console. h6. Failure two: Emulator launch from studio fails with: If you run the simulator over and over with this failure, the processes just sit there so you must kill all previous run attempts. Running with an SDK build back (3.1.0.v20130305095817) gets you: And the emulator launches. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a project in studio (Using SDK 3.1.0.v20130410180128 2) Try to launch in the emulator h5. Result: Launch failure either with emulator launch but no app, or with console errors. Previous launch attempts stay active h5. Expected Result: The emulator launches and the app is shown """"",title+description
TIMOB-13532,12,"""Keep Track of Ti.CloudPush 2.2 Update""","""""""For a new feature raised from ACS side to use a general Haproxy to assign different apps to different environment (production or enterprise), we need to add appKey along with all Coordinator's HTTP request. For getting device token, it already had that. For now getting host adds appKey as well.    This ticket is for a track on TIMOB part, and concerete implementation has been done by CLOUDSRV-2281.""""""",Story,"Title: Keep Track of Ti.CloudPush 2.2 Update
Description: """"For a new feature raised from ACS side to use a general Haproxy to assign different apps to different environment (production or enterprise), we need to add appKey along with all Coordinator's HTTP request. For getting device token, it already had that. For now getting host adds appKey as well. This ticket is for a track on TIMOB part, and concerete implementation has been done by CLOUDSRV-2281.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13531,12,"""BlackBerry: Remove control is not working.""","""""""table.addEventListener('click', function(e) {          scrollView.remove(view);          win2.remove(scrollView);      });""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Remove control is not working.
Description: """"table.addEventListener('click', function(e) { scrollView.remove(view); win2.remove(scrollView); });""""",title+description
TIMOB-13530,12,"""ListView: implement separatorColor in v2""","""""""SeparatorColor property for ListView is currently planned for v2.    ListViews currently show black separators on Android, grey separators on iOS.    However, it is quite unlikely that an existing app, which might have a lot of TableViews with custom separatorColors (e.g. to follow color guidelines for the app brand), can be updated to use ListView with those default colors.    While many other v2 features can be simulated in v1, or manually added with additional coding, the lack of separatorColor forces a VISUAL limitation which cannot be circumvented.    Please consider including separatorColor in 3.1 GA """"""",New Feature,"Title: ListView: implement separatorColor in v2
Description: """"SeparatorColor property for ListView is currently planned for v2. ListViews currently show black separators on Android, grey separators on iOS. However, it is quite unlikely that an existing app, which might have a lot of TableViews with custom separatorColors (e.g. to follow color guidelines for the app brand), can be updated to use ListView with those default colors. While many other v2 features can be simulated in v1, or manually added with additional coding, the lack of separatorColor forces a VISUAL limitation which cannot be circumvented. Please consider including separatorColor in 3.1 GA """"",title+description
TIMOB-13529,12,"""iOS: ListView: ListItem property """"backgroundImage"""" not recognized""","""""""*Problem*  When trying to assign a custom backgroundImage to a ListItem, the property is not recognized.    *Steps to Reproduce*  1. copy and paste code into app.js  2. download the background images, place into resources folder  3. run code  4. notice listViewRow does not have applied background image    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ListView: ListItem property """"backgroundImage"""" not recognized
Description: """"*Problem* When trying to assign a custom backgroundImage to a ListItem, the property is not recognized. *Steps to Reproduce* 1. copy and paste code into app.js 2. download the background images, place into resources folder 3. run code 4. notice listViewRow does not have applied background image """"",title+description
TIMOB-13528,12,"""iOS: Regression in behaviour with custom views on {right,left} NavButton for iOS""","""""""Changing the hierarchy (or doing something that has this as a collateral effect) make the view set as rightNavButton centered in the navBar.    Just launch the provided code both as 3.0 and 3.1. """"""""Clicking"""""""" on the button on 3.0 will work correctly, on 3.1 will expose the issue.    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');    var nav = Ti.UI.createView({   width: Ti.UI.SIZE,   layout: 'horizontal'  });    var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({   width: 40,   left: 2,   right: 2,   image: 'KS_nav_views.png'  });    var toggle = true;    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {   toggle = !toggle;   btn.image = toggle ? 'KS_nav_views.png' : 'KS_nav_ui.png';  });    nav.add(btn);    var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({   title: 'Example',   rightNavButton: nav,   navBarHidden: false,   backgroundColor: 'white',   modal: true  });    window.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Regression in behaviour with custom views on {right,left} NavButton for iOS
Description: """"Changing the hierarchy (or doing something that has this as a collateral effect) make the view set as rightNavButton centered in the navBar. Just launch the provided code both as 3.0 and 3.1. """"""""Clicking"""""""" on the button on 3.0 will work correctly, on 3.1 will expose the issue. {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var nav = Ti.UI.createView({ width: Ti.UI.SIZE, layout: 'horizontal' }); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ width: 40, left: 2, right: 2, image: 'KS_nav_views.png' }); var toggle = true; btn.addEventListener('click', function () { toggle = !toggle; btn.image = toggle ? 'KS_nav_views.png' : 'KS_nav_ui.png'; }); nav.add(btn); var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Example', rightNavButton: nav, navBarHidden: false, backgroundColor: 'white', modal: true }); window.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-13527,12,"""TiAPI: Enable memory profiling of Titanium apps""","""""""Add memory profiling support to the existing profiler. For more information, please see:    https://wiki.<USER>org/display/spe/Memory+Profiling+of+Titanium+Applications    Estimate is 3w for iOS, 2w for Android""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Enable memory profiling of Titanium apps
Description: """"Add memory profiling support to the existing profiler. For more information, please see: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/spe/Memory+Profiling+of+Titanium+Applications Estimate is 3w for iOS, 2w for Android""""",title+description
TIMOB-13525,12,"""iOS: Endless loop in AudioStreamerCUR""","""""""The following method is from AudioStreamerCUR.m in SDK 3.0.2.GA. When you call the stop method while in AS_STOPPING state the app gets into an endless loop at the end of the method. Depending on the audio file the AS_STOPPING state can be several seconds at the end of the song. Also it seems that other methods have problems with that state, e.g. pause seems to do nothing. This means that the player cannot be controlled and might hang the app in this state.      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Endless loop in AudioStreamerCUR
Description: """"The following method is from AudioStreamerCUR.m in SDK 3.0.2.GA. When you call the stop method while in AS_STOPPING state the app gets into an endless loop at the end of the method. Depending on the audio file the AS_STOPPING state can be several seconds at the end of the song. Also it seems that other methods have problems with that state, e.g. pause seems to do nothing. This means that the player cannot be controlled and might hang the app in this state. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13524,12,"""BlackBerry: Can't test media(sound), maps, orientation as the proper fields have not been added to tiapp.xml""","""""""Description:  1. Create an app for media,maps,orientation  2. Build & run for BB device/simulator    Actual Results:  1. We get errors & build fails    Expected results:  1. The build should succeed""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Can't test media(sound), maps, orientation as the proper fields have not been added to tiapp.xml
Description: """"Description: 1. Create an app for media,maps,orientation 2. Build & run for BB device/simulator Actual Results: 1. We get errors & build fails Expected results: 1. The build should succeed""""",title+description
TIMOB-13523,12,"""iOS Apps with a number at the beginning of the name are not able to submit to the store.""","""""""h2. Bug    When the name of an app starts with a number (i.e. 10tips) the app cannot be deployed at the store due to the generated CFBundleURLSchemes on the info.plist files. See attached screenshot.    h2. Test case    Create an app with number and try to submit it to the store.    h2. Solution     Copy and replace the CFBundleURLSchemes tags from the generated info.plist to tiapp.xml and add a letter at the begging.    tiapp.xml  {code:lang=xml|title=tiapp.xml}  <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>  <ti:app xmlns:ti=""""""""http://ti.<USER>org"""""""">  <ios>          <plist>              <dict>                  <key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>                  <array>                      <dict>                          <key>CFBundleURLName</key>                          <string>com.appc.10tips</string>                          <key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>                          <array>                              <string>a10tips</string> <!-- Letter 'a' added -->                          </array>                      </dict>                  </array>                  <key>UIApplicationExitsOnSuspend</key>                  <true/>              </dict>          </plist>      </ios>  </ti:app>  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Apps with a number at the beginning of the name are not able to submit to the store.
Description: """"h2. Bug When the name of an app starts with a number (i.e. 10tips) the app cannot be deployed at the store due to the generated CFBundleURLSchemes on the info.plist files. See attached screenshot. h2. Test case Create an app with number and try to submit it to the store. h2. Solution Copy and replace the CFBundleURLSchemes tags from the generated info.plist to tiapp.xml and add a letter at the begging. tiapp.xml {code:lang=xml|title=tiapp.xml} <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?> <ti:app xmlns:ti=""""""""http://ti.<USER>org""""""""> <ios> <plist> <dict> <key>CFBundleURLTypes</key> <array> <dict> <key>CFBundleURLName</key> <string>com.appc.10tips</string> <key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key> <array> <string>a10tips</string> <!-- Letter 'a' added --> </array> </dict> </array> <key>UIApplicationExitsOnSuspend</key> <true/> </dict> </plist> </ios> </ti:app> {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-13522,12,"""Android:Video camera does not fire the callback on startActivityForResult on save""","""""""h2. Description  Video camera after recording is done does not fire the callback for startActivityForResult on clicking the save button.    h2. Test code  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android:Video camera does not fire the callback on startActivityForResult on save
