TIMOB-13521,12,"""Android:In tableViewRow containing the scrollable view when updateRow method is called it does not display the first row of the scrollable view""","""""""h2. Description  In TableView having 2 rows one with ScrollableView in it and other having a button. ScrollableView contains 3 views with different colors(pink/green/black) is added using appendRow works fine for the first time when application started. But on click event listener of button the updateRow method is called which causes ScrollableView dosen't display the first view! if you scroll through the ScrollableView and back to the first, then it display correctly.    h2. Steps to Reproduce  1. Please use the code below:    2. Install ad run the application. You see the first row having pink color and other views on scrolling.  3. Click on refresh button  4. First view is not displayed.    Note: It worked fine on 2.1.4 GA""""""",Bug,"Title: Android:In tableViewRow containing the scrollable view when updateRow method is called it does not display the first row of the scrollable view
Description: """"h2. Description In TableView having 2 rows one with ScrollableView in it and other having a button. ScrollableView contains 3 views with different colors(pink/green/black) is added using appendRow works fine for the first time when application started. But on click event listener of button the updateRow method is called which causes ScrollableView dosen't display the first view! if you scroll through the ScrollableView and back to the first, then it display correctly. h2. Steps to Reproduce 1. Please use the code below: 2. Install ad run the application. You see the first row having pink color and other views on scrolling. 3. Click on refresh button 4. First view is not displayed. Note: It worked fine on 2.1.4 GA""""",title+description
TIMOB-13518,12,"""BlackBerry : Alloy : Any changes in the code are not reflected in the BB build till we build the same app for IOS or android first""","""""""Description:  1. Create an simple alloy app for blackberry which has a button on a window  2. Run it on BB emulator/device  3. Now change the positioning of the button & add another control to the code  4. Run the app again on BB simulator/device    Actual Result:  1. The changes done in the code do not reflect when the app is re reun on the simulator/device.  2. Now run the code with the new changes for IOS simulator  3. After the app launches in the IOS simulator run it on BB simulator/device again.  4. Note that the changes we made in the positioning & a new control are now being seen    Expected Result:  1. The changes in the code should be reflected in the app immediately    App attached for reference""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Alloy : Any changes in the code are not reflected in the BB build till we build the same app for IOS or android first
Description: """"Description: 1. Create an simple alloy app for blackberry which has a button on a window 2. Run it on BB emulator/device 3. Now change the positioning of the button & add another control to the code 4. Run the app again on BB simulator/device Actual Result: 1. The changes done in the code do not reflect when the app is re reun on the simulator/device. 2. Now run the code with the new changes for IOS simulator 3. After the app launches in the IOS simulator run it on BB simulator/device again. 4. Note that the changes we made in the positioning & a new control are now being seen Expected Result: 1. The changes in the code should be reflected in the app immediately App attached for reference""""",title+description
TIMOB-13517,12,"""MobileWeb: Need to evaluate property/constant store in getter/setter""","""""""Properties and constants are currently stored in an internal object and we cache this destination. By moving the reference to __values__ inside the setters/getters, then we can override the destination store.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Need to evaluate property/constant store in getter/setter
Description: """"Properties and constants are currently stored in an internal object and we cache this destination. By moving the reference to __values__ inside the setters/getters, then we can override the destination store.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13516,12,"""Android: Maps V2 Module - Missing """"longitudeDelta"""" and """"latitudeDelta"""" properties on the """"regionchanged"""" event""","""""""It still seems to be missing """"""""longitudeDelta"""""""" and """"""""latitidueDelta"""""""" properties on the """"""""regionchanged"""""""" event. Without it, it's impossible to calculate the current lat/lon area (box) the user is currenlty viewing.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Maps V2 Module - Missing """"longitudeDelta"""" and """"latitudeDelta"""" properties on the """"regionchanged"""" event
Description: """"It still seems to be missing """"""""longitudeDelta"""""""" and """"""""latitidueDelta"""""""" properties on the """"""""regionchanged"""""""" event. Without it, it's impossible to calculate the current lat/lon area (box) the user is currenlty viewing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13515,12,"""Titanium Studio 3.1 can't use Android x86 emulator""","""""""Even Android [x86] api, Titanium studio launch Android[armebi-xx]  This is a big problem in my case. Please fix this problem.    Follow steps,    1. Create Project (android)  2. Right click on Project, Run as > Run configurations...  3. Click """"""""New launch configuration."""""""" button (look left-top of dialog)  4. *choose Android  4.1.x [x86], (and choose project... etc)*  5. Click """"""""Apply""""""""  6. Click """"""""Run""""""""    Expected Result  1. Launch Android Emulator [x86]  2. Launch App    But  1. Launch Android Emulator [arm...]  2. Launch App      p.s.  If I use Ti Studio 3.0.2 on same workspace and same run configuration, It work properly.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Titanium Studio 3.1 can't use Android x86 emulator
Description: """"Even Android [x86] api, Titanium studio launch Android[armebi-xx] This is a big problem in my case. Please fix this problem. Follow steps, 1. Create Project (android) 2. Right click on Project, Run as > Run configurations... 3. Click """"""""New launch configuration."""""""" button (look left-top of dialog) 4. *choose Android 4.1.x [x86], (and choose project... etc)* 5. Click """"""""Apply"""""""" 6. Click """"""""Run"""""""" Expected Result 1. Launch Android Emulator [x86] 2. Launch App But 1. Launch Android Emulator [arm...] 2. Launch App p.s. If I use Ti Studio 3.0.2 on same workspace and same run configuration, It work properly. """"",title+description
