TIMOB-13502,12,"""Popover sizing is calculated incorrectly when POPOVER_ARROW_DIRECTION_LEFT or RIGHT""","""""""*Problem*  When a Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover uses a LEFT or RIGHT arrow, the popover seems to be the wrong size. Some of my content is being cut off.   UP and DOWN work as expected.     Orientation seems to make no difference. (problem is in landscape or portrait)    Suggestion of where to patch TiSDK would be welcome, as this is a bit of a blocker for me.     *Steps to reproduce*  1. Copy and paste code provided into app.js  2. Run on iPad simulator  3. Click left side button, notice popover functionality as expected  4. Click right side button, notice popover content being cut off  """"""",Bug,"Title: Popover sizing is calculated incorrectly when POPOVER_ARROW_DIRECTION_LEFT or RIGHT
Description: """"*Problem* When a Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover uses a LEFT or RIGHT arrow, the popover seems to be the wrong size. Some of my content is being cut off. UP and DOWN work as expected. Orientation seems to make no difference. (problem is in landscape or portrait) Suggestion of where to patch TiSDK would be welcome, as this is a bit of a blocker for me. *Steps to reproduce* 1. Copy and paste code provided into app.js 2. Run on iPad simulator 3. Click left side button, notice popover functionality as expected 4. Click right side button, notice popover content being cut off """"",title+description
