TIMOB-13496,12,"""iOS: Titanium.Contacts.removeGroup fails""","""""""The following code fails:    Titanium.Contacts.removeGroup(groupObj);  Titanium.Contacts.save();    The error given is:  {code:title=Error|borderStyle=solid}  [ERROR] :  Invalid type passed to function. expected: TiContactsPerson, was: TiContactsGroup  in -[ContactsModule removePerson:] (ContactsModule.m:431)  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.Contacts.removeGroup fails
Description: """"The following code fails: Titanium.Contacts.removeGroup(groupObj); Titanium.Contacts.save(); The error given is: {code:title=Error|borderStyle=solid} [ERROR] :  Invalid type passed to function. expected: TiContactsPerson, was: TiContactsGroup in -[ContactsModule removePerson:] (ContactsModule.m:431) """"",title+description
TIMOB-13495,12,"""Android: HTML5 audio tag does not play in WebView""","""""""h1. Problem description  When using the <audio> tag in a WebView, the audio file does not play. This is not working both for local files (inside Resources, or in the SDCARD), nor for remote ones.    h1. Steps to reproduce  1) Create an app with a WebView:        2) Create an HTML file with an <audio> tag:        3) Put the cricket.wav file in the same directory (or use a remote URL).    4) Run the app and try to play the file: no audio is played, and no log is written.    h1. Notes    Tested with 2.1.4 and 3.1.0.v20130404173046 as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTML5 audio tag does not play in WebView
Description: """"h1. Problem description When using the <audio> tag in a WebView, the audio file does not play. This is not working both for local files (inside Resources, or in the SDCARD), nor for remote ones. h1. Steps to reproduce 1) Create an app with a WebView: 2) Create an HTML file with an <audio> tag: 3) Put the cricket.wav file in the same directory (or use a remote URL). 4) Run the app and try to play the file: no audio is played, and no log is written. h1. Notes Tested with 2.1.4 and 3.1.0.v20130404173046 as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13494,12,"""Android: Image View does not maintain image boundary ""","""""""When we zoom in or out an image in Image View using enableZoomControls property,  then image can be slide out of the image view and there is not way to restrict this behavior.    Steps to reproduce:    1: Launch the sample code present in the JIRA in Android App Project  2: Tap on the image and move your finger in any direction, for example to right. You should be able to see part image and part green.  3: Lift up your finder.  4: Tap on the image again and move the image to the right. Move it unless the image disappears.  5: Lift up for your finger.    Now you will find that the image is no longer visible. Only the green color background is visible.    *sample Code*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image View does not maintain image boundary
Description: """"When we zoom in or out an image in Image View using enableZoomControls property, then image can be slide out of the image view and there is not way to restrict this behavior. Steps to reproduce: 1: Launch the sample code present in the JIRA in Android App Project 2: Tap on the image and move your finger in any direction, for example to right. You should be able to see part image and part green. 3: Lift up your finder. 4: Tap on the image again and move the image to the right. Move it unless the image disappears. 5: Lift up for your finger. Now you will find that the image is no longer visible. Only the green color background is visible. *sample Code* """"",title+description
