TIMOB-13436,12,"""iOS: CoverFlowView displays half image after image modification""","""""""*Steps to Reproduce*  - create a project with Alloy with a single CoverFlowView  - add a couple of images  - when a user clicks one of the images, modify the actual image as follows     a) create a view with the actual image as background     b) add a label text wit some text (i.e. Date())     c) save the view as image back to the original image file     d) do a setImage () reloading the image with correct index    *Actual Result*  When the images are loaded the first time, they show up perfect  When an image is peformed, only the top half of that image shows in the coverflowview  When the app is killed and restarted, the correct images appear.  The click even works perfect as the images are correctly changed    *Expected Result*  When an image is changed, it should display the full changed image. Not the top half. I have isolated this problem in a separate project and the results are the same.    h3. Appc Support Team Notes    The attached project references the data directory. I have modified it to reference the resources folder; now simply drop the images into assets/iphone. I have also modified the index.xml; before the cover flow was being created off-screen.    *index.xml*        *index.js*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: CoverFlowView displays half image after image modification
Description: """"*Steps to Reproduce* - create a project with Alloy with a single CoverFlowView - add a couple of images - when a user clicks one of the images, modify the actual image as follows a) create a view with the actual image as background b) add a label text wit some text (i.e. Date()) c) save the view as image back to the original image file d) do a setImage () reloading the image with correct index *Actual Result* When the images are loaded the first time, they show up perfect When an image is peformed, only the top half of that image shows in the coverflowview When the app is killed and restarted, the correct images appear. The click even works perfect as the images are correctly changed *Expected Result* When an image is changed, it should display the full changed image. Not the top half. I have isolated this problem in a separate project and the results are the same. h3. Appc Support Team Notes The attached project references the data directory. I have modified it to reference the resources folder; now simply drop the images into assets/iphone. I have also modified the index.xml; before the cover flow was being created off-screen. *index.xml* *index.js* """"",title+description
TIMOB-13435,12,"""iOS: TableView with search and rows containing labels""","""""""Run the attached app.js in Ti SDK 3.1.0.    Steps to reproduce bug:  1. Tap table search and enter 0.  2. Tap the first matching row to open the detail window.  3. Tap the back button to return, notice the previously selected row appears blank. (Expected: selected row should display visibly)  4. Scroll row 0 off screen and back and notice the label reappears and row displays correctly.    This is a regression from Ti SDK 2.1.4.GA. If you run the same app.js with the steps above in 2.1.4.GA it works correctly.    Note related bug TIMOB-12750 that I also logged and was recently fixed in 3.1.0.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView with search and rows containing labels
Description: """"Run the attached app.js in Ti SDK 3.1.0. Steps to reproduce bug: 1. Tap table search and enter 0. 2. Tap the first matching row to open the detail window. 3. Tap the back button to return, notice the previously selected row appears blank. (Expected: selected row should display visibly) 4. Scroll row 0 off screen and back and notice the label reappears and row displays correctly. This is a regression from Ti SDK 2.1.4.GA. If you run the same app.js with the steps above in 2.1.4.GA it works correctly. Note related bug TIMOB-12750 that I also logged and was recently fixed in 3.1.0. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13434,12,"""iOS: TableViewRow .hasCheck bug when used in combination with highlightedColor""","""""""If you set the hasCheck property on a tableViewRow on a click event, then the highlightedColor on any labels within that tableViewRow gets stuck.        The label within that row has a highlightedColor of #fff. When clicking on a row, the label turns permanently white. Selecting it again fixes the problem.    A workaround is to call setHasCheck twice, while setting the font color explicitly in between the two calls:        This will still cause the same bug if the row is selected twice in a row now. To work around that, you have to make sure that this row isn't already selected.    This bug was introduced in Titanium 3.0.0. I am building using the iOS 6 sdk with Titanium Studio 3.0. The problem exists in both the simulator and on a physical iPhone 5 device.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableViewRow .hasCheck bug when used in combination with highlightedColor
Description: """"If you set the hasCheck property on a tableViewRow on a click event, then the highlightedColor on any labels within that tableViewRow gets stuck. The label within that row has a highlightedColor of #fff. When clicking on a row, the label turns permanently white. Selecting it again fixes the problem. A workaround is to call setHasCheck twice, while setting the font color explicitly in between the two calls: This will still cause the same bug if the row is selected twice in a row now. To work around that, you have to make sure that this row isn't already selected. This bug was introduced in Titanium 3.0.0. I am building using the iOS 6 sdk with Titanium Studio 3.0. The problem exists in both the simulator and on a physical iPhone 5 device.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13433,12,"""LiveView: generated liveview.js exists in Resources instead of build folder""","""""""When a LiveView enabled-project is run, the liveview.js generated code is placed in the project Resources instead of the build folder.    Test Steps:    1. Open <USER>Studio.  2. Create Titanium Project w/<USER>Services.  3. Enable LiveView in Run Configurations... Android Emulator or iOS Simulator.  4. Run Project.    Actual Result:    liveview.js appears in Resources.    Expected Result:    liveview.js appears in hidden build folder, as it is a generated file.""""""",Bug,"Title: LiveView: generated liveview.js exists in Resources instead of build folder
Description: """"When a LiveView enabled-project is run, the liveview.js generated code is placed in the project Resources instead of the build folder. Test Steps: 1. Open <USER>Studio. 2. Create Titanium Project w/<USER>Services. 3. Enable LiveView in Run Configurations... Android Emulator or iOS Simulator. 4. Run Project. Actual Result: liveview.js appears in Resources. Expected Result: liveview.js appears in hidden build folder, as it is a generated file.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13432,12,"""Code Processor: """"SDK version 3.1.x is not available"""" error message on analyzing project code""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create <USER>Project from <USER>Studio.   2. Go to the terminal.  3. Run command from the top-level directory of the created project - titanium-code-processor analyze -o iphone -a    Actual: Error message appears """"""""SDK version 3.1.x is not available"""""""".  Expected: Project code should analyze properly.""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Processor: """"SDK version 3.1.x is not available"""" error message on analyzing project code
