TIMOB-13412,12,"""iOS: TiProxy fireSyncEvent""","""""""On android there a fireSyncEvent on android.  This is very practical for modules that have a high frequency of event fired and where they need to be treated as soon as possible(i use it for a motion module).  iOs only have a fireEvent.  I looked a little at TiBindingEvent, but was easy enough for me to do it right now ;)  Yet i could really use this in a number of modules.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: TiProxy fireSyncEvent
Description: """"On android there a fireSyncEvent on android. This is very practical for modules that have a high frequency of event fired and where they need to be treated as soon as possible(i use it for a motion module). iOs only have a fireEvent. I looked a little at TiBindingEvent, but was easy enough for me to do it right now ;) Yet i could really use this in a number of modules.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13410,12,"""CLI: ti clean command doesn't work if build dir contains a .DS_Store file""","""""""When you run """"""""ti clean"""""""", it doesn't properly clean all the build directories. If you specify a specific platform to clean (i.e. """"""""ti clean -p iphone""""""""), then it works as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: ti clean command doesn't work if build dir contains a .DS_Store file
Description: """"When you run """"""""ti clean"""""""", it doesn't properly clean all the build directories. If you specify a specific platform to clean (i.e. """"""""ti clean -p iphone""""""""), then it works as expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13409,12,"""Android: Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(); parity issue on Android""","""""""h5. Description:  A report came in from the field regarding a runtime error generated when attempting to open a tab with Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(). The behavior is that calling open in this way does not open a tab, but opens a new heavyweight window. On that window, when trying to open another tab in the same manner, a runtime error is generated because Titanium.UI.currentTab is null since not in a tabgroup.    Please visit github.com/veamon/Tabs for code.    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Install project from github and launch  2) Note you are in tab group. Click """"""""next""""""""  3) Note you are not in tab group. Click """"""""next""""""""    h5. Result:  Runtime error.    h5. Expected Result:  If comparing to iOS, expect to stay in tab group and instead of runtime error, a new tab is opened.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(); parity issue on Android
Description: """"h5. Description: A report came in from the field regarding a runtime error generated when attempting to open a tab with Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(). The behavior is that calling open in this way does not open a tab, but opens a new heavyweight window. On that window, when trying to open another tab in the same manner, a runtime error is generated because Titanium.UI.currentTab is null since not in a tabgroup. Please visit github.com/veamon/Tabs for code. h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install project from github and launch 2) Note you are in tab group. Click """"""""next"""""""" 3) Note you are not in tab group. Click """"""""next"""""""" h5. Result: Runtime error. h5. Expected Result: If comparing to iOS, expect to stay in tab group and instead of runtime error, a new tab is opened.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13408,12,"""Android: ListView Enhancement: Update itemCount automatically""","""""""About the crash which fixed in this [commit|https://github.com/hieupham007/Titanium_Mobile/commit/6a099fe4dd0ca9630967a08b98808d51b5b38628], we should think about one way to automatically update itemCount, eg the getItemCount() method return the size of the data arraylist. So whenever the adapter is trying to notify data change, the data and the itemCount are always sync/consistent. This issue also forces the getSectionCount() method to be called in UI thread.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: ListView Enhancement: Update itemCount automatically
Description: """"About the crash which fixed in this [commit|https://github.com/hieupham007/Titanium_Mobile/commit/6a099fe4dd0ca9630967a08b98808d51b5b38628], we should think about one way to automatically update itemCount, eg the getItemCount() method return the size of the data arraylist. So whenever the adapter is trying to notify data change, the data and the itemCount are always sync/consistent. This issue also forces the getSectionCount() method to be called in UI thread.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13407,12,"""Android: WebView 'swipe' event is not getting triggered""","""""""*Problem*  The 'swipe' event for the WebView has been registered but when the swipe event is done, it is not getting triggered. If it is changed from WebView to Window, then the gesture is getting detected, but the same is not hapenning in WebView.    *Steps to Reproduce*  1. Copy and paste code into app.js  2. try to swipe, notice no event triggered.        Doc Supported: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.WebView-event-swipe""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView 'swipe' event is not getting triggered
Description: """"*Problem* The 'swipe' event for the WebView has been registered but when the swipe event is done, it is not getting triggered. If it is changed from WebView to Window, then the gesture is getting detected, but the same is not hapenning in WebView. *Steps to Reproduce* 1. Copy and paste code into app.js 2. try to swipe, notice no event triggered. Doc Supported: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.WebView-event-swipe""""",title+description
TIMOB-13406,12,"""iOS: ListView: Listview on iOS 5.0+ shows black bars in some items""","""""""h5. Description:  WHile testing Kitchensink on iOS, I noticed that some of the listview items had a black bar nearly obscuring the entire item row. These bar are not visible when the row is highlighted, and may move on scroll to other list view items    See screen shots    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS from master branch of https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/KitchenSink  2) Navigate to base UI > Views > List View > Background color    h5. Result:  Some list view items are almost solid black    h5. Expected Result:  All rows have uniform coloring and attributes""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ListView: Listview on iOS 5.0+ shows black bars in some items
