TIMOB-13404,12,"""Android: TextField update value on Return event""","""""""h2. Description of the problem  Using an app with username and password fields, when a text is entered in the first, then the cursor goes to the second, the value of the first text field is not valid anymore (it takes the password's value).    h2. Steps to reproduce  - Run the following code on Android  - See the logs with adb logcat  - Enter something in the username field (e.g. """"""""foo"""""""") - you will see """"""""foo/"""""""" in the log  - Click the return button, and start writing something in the password field (e.g. """"""""bar"""""""") - you will see """"""""bar/bar"""""""" in the log        h2. Additional info  The code above is what is generated by Alloy - the bug was found using it. Using SDK 2.1.4 the problem is not visible.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField update value on Return event
Description: """"h2. Description of the problem Using an app with username and password fields, when a text is entered in the first, then the cursor goes to the second, the value of the first text field is not valid anymore (it takes the password's value). h2. Steps to reproduce - Run the following code on Android - See the logs with adb logcat - Enter something in the username field (e.g. """"""""foo"""""""") - you will see """"""""foo/"""""""" in the log - Click the return button, and start writing something in the password field (e.g. """"""""bar"""""""") - you will see """"""""bar/bar"""""""" in the log h2. Additional info The code above is what is generated by Alloy - the bug was found using it. Using SDK 2.1.4 the problem is not visible.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13403,12,"""Android: SOAP does not show result and log shows """"Internal Server Error"""" exception""","""""""This is not a regression. The issue also exist on 3.0.2.    SDK - 3.1.0.v20130404173046  Studio - 3.1.0.201304022134  Devices - Nexus7(v4.1), Galaxy Note(2.3.6)  Mac OS - 10.8    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Open KitchenSink  2. Tap on Mashups>SOAP    Actual: Does not show result on device and log shows """"""""Internal Server Error"""""""" exception. See the attached screen shot and log file.  Expected: Should show the result without any Error/Exception.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: SOAP does not show result and log shows """"Internal Server Error"""" exception
Description: """"This is not a regression. The issue also exist on 3.0.2. SDK - 3.1.0.v20130404173046 Studio - 3.1.0.201304022134 Devices - Nexus7(v4.1), Galaxy Note(2.3.6) Mac OS - 10.8 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Open KitchenSink 2. Tap on Mashups>SOAP Actual: Does not show result on device and log shows """"""""Internal Server Error"""""""" exception. See the attached screen shot and log file. Expected: Should show the result without any Error/Exception.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13402,12,"""Android: Kitchen Sink: Webviews -> Image Url - Pinch and Zoom does not work.""","""""""Android: Kitchen Sink: Webviews -> Image Url - Pinch and Zoom does not work.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Navigate to KitchenSink:Views>Web Views>Image URL  2. 2:Tap on the zoom in and zoom out.    Expected:  Should be able to see change in the image size  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Kitchen Sink: Webviews -> Image Url - Pinch and Zoom does not work.
