TIMOB-13387,12,"""Specification: Define/consolidate/deprecate Titanium.Database.ResultSet.fieldCount""","""""""One of two things needs to happen:  # fieldCount (as a property) needs to be defined on iOS and fieldCount (as a method) deprecated on iOS  # getFieldCount (as a method) needs to be defined on both iOS and android and fieldCount needs to be deprecated on both platforms""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Specification: Define/consolidate/deprecate Titanium.Database.ResultSet.fieldCount
Description: """"One of two things needs to happen: # fieldCount (as a property) needs to be defined on iOS and fieldCount (as a method) deprecated on iOS # getFieldCount (as a method) needs to be defined on both iOS and android and fieldCount needs to be deprecated on both platforms""""",title+description
TIMOB-13386,12,"""Specification: Create Ti.UI.View.replaceAt/insertAt/getAt specification""","""""""Need to document three new methods on Ti.UI.View: replaceAt, insertAt, and getAt. The new listview module should be used as a reference on how to define these types of methods, since we recently had a discussion on what insert/replace/get methods should look like.    Also, need to deprecate Ti.UI.View.zindex. The specification shall state that the behavior when combining zindex and these new methods is undefined.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Specification: Create Ti.UI.View.replaceAt/insertAt/getAt specification
Description: """"Need to document three new methods on Ti.UI.View: replaceAt, insertAt, and getAt. The new listview module should be used as a reference on how to define these types of methods, since we recently had a discussion on what insert/replace/get methods should look like. Also, need to deprecate Ti.UI.View.zindex. The specification shall state that the behavior when combining zindex and these new methods is undefined.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13385,12,"""Specification: Create 'click' event specification for pickers""","""""""The spec needs to take into consideration what is possible on the different platforms, if it is possible at all, and what information is available for the event.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Specification: Create 'click' event specification for pickers
Description: """"The spec needs to take into consideration what is possible on the different platforms, if it is possible at all, and what information is available for the event.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13382,12,"""Specification: Create Ti.UI.Label.shadowOffset property specificaltion""","""""""The spec needs to take into consideration what is possible on the different platforms, and how each platform specifies text shadows. Also, the name shadowOffset is not set in stone. If the name doesn't make sense given what is being specified, then change it to be more descriptive.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Specification: Create Ti.UI.Label.shadowOffset property specificaltion
Description: """"The spec needs to take into consideration what is possible on the different platforms, and how each platform specifies text shadows. Also, the name shadowOffset is not set in stone. If the name doesn't make sense given what is being specified, then change it to be more descriptive.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13381,12,"""Android Emulator: process launches in new terminal on Windows""","""""""Android Emulator: <USER>launches in new terminal.    The emulator output should exist in the Studio console.    See screenshots.    Test Steps:    1. Run Android Emulator.    Test Results:    Process launches in new OS terminal, logs appear in external terminal.    Stable Results:    Process launches and log appear in Studio console.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Emulator: process launches in new terminal on Windows
Description: """"Android Emulator: <USER>launches in new terminal. The emulator output should exist in the Studio console. See screenshots. Test Steps: 1. Run Android Emulator. Test Results: Process launches in new OS terminal, logs appear in external terminal. Stable Results: Process launches and log appear in Studio console.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13380,12,"""iOS: TextArea trims white spaces""","""""""When TextArea has automatic width, it trims white spaces. To reproduce the issue, run this code, focus the textarea and touch the spacebar. You would expect to see a white space appended to the text but nothing.  Look also at the """"""""change"""""""" event listener. It fires twice, the first time correctly with the white space appended to the text, while the second time the text is trimmed.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TextArea trims white spaces
Description: """"When TextArea has automatic width, it trims white spaces. To reproduce the issue, run this code, focus the textarea and touch the spacebar. You would expect to see a white space appended to the text but nothing. Look also at the """"""""change"""""""" event listener. It fires twice, the first time correctly with the white space appended to the text, while the second time the text is trimmed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13378,12,"""Ti API: Define a formal module naming convention""","""""""The naming scheme we have for modules is rather inconsistent at the moment. as an example, we have Ti.Mapping and Facebook, but they should follow the same convention. Should we prefix things with Ti or not? Should we use a dot as a separate, or should we use the CommonJS/AMD pattern of slashes? Should we prepend Ti, and if so under what conditions? These questions and more should be formalized in a naming guide document. There are also some technical considerations on some of the platforms, and this could require some changes to them.""""""",Story,"Title: Ti API: Define a formal module naming convention
Description: """"The naming scheme we have for modules is rather inconsistent at the moment. as an example, we have Ti.Mapping and Facebook, but they should follow the same convention. Should we prefix things with Ti or not? Should we use a dot as a separate, or should we use the CommonJS/AMD pattern of slashes? Should we prepend Ti, and if so under what conditions? These questions and more should be formalized in a naming guide document. There are also some technical considerations on some of the platforms, and this could require some changes to them.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13377,12,"""Ti API: Design a new key-frame based animation system""","""""""The current animation system uses matrix transforms to define how the animation behaves. The problem with this system is that affine transforms can only show rotations less than 360 degrees, and 180 degree rotations do not have a defined direction. Mathematically speaking, these problems cannot be worked around. A better solution is to use a key-frame based animation system, similar to how requestAnimationFrame works in the web world.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Design a new key-frame based animation system
Description: """"The current animation system uses matrix transforms to define how the animation behaves. The problem with this system is that affine transforms can only show rotations less than 360 degrees, and 180 degree rotations do not have a defined direction. Mathematically speaking, these problems cannot be worked around. A better solution is to use a key-frame based animation system, similar to how requestAnimationFrame works in the web world.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13376,12,"""iOS: App crashes when tested by iTunes on iPhone 5 and iPad running iOS 6.0.1""","""""""the apps work on the local simulators, and build for distribution with no errors. but crash consistently when tested by iTunes.  here are iTunes crash reports for 3 separate apps built and reviewed using the same codebase, with slightly different resources (graphics, custom variable settings)  - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/b1/5e/32/b15e32fd-c7fa-9b19-ab09-20f9e370636f/temp..fnfzfgyc.crash  - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/f9/95/b1/f995b144-56c4-3bb4-e794-7be7d613d40e/temp..dyqqfxch.crash    - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/f5/84/23/f5842358-7603-e1be-bee3-f1d8ffe3f798/temp..eumvmncy.crash    - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/3e/74/ae/3e74aea9-ba00-aa1e-4689-d98c38186116/temp..orofqsqg.crash  - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/90/dc/70/90dc709e-1b69-af62-5b63-0a02d6a59524/temp..yfapebdo.crash    Since this effectively prevents us from submitting any iOS apps, it is critical to us.  thank you!  David""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App crashes when tested by iTunes on iPhone 5 and iPad running iOS 6.0.1
Description: """"the apps work on the local simulators, and build for distribution with no errors. but crash consistently when tested by iTunes. here are iTunes crash reports for 3 separate apps built and reviewed using the same codebase, with slightly different resources (graphics, custom variable settings) - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/b1/5e/32/b15e32fd-c7fa-9b19-ab09-20f9e370636f/temp..fnfzfgyc.crash - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/f9/95/b1/f995b144-56c4-3bb4-e794-7be7d613d40e/temp..dyqqfxch.crash - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/f5/84/23/f5842358-7603-e1be-bee3-f1d8ffe3f798/temp..eumvmncy.crash - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/3e/74/ae/3e74aea9-ba00-aa1e-4689-d98c38186116/temp..orofqsqg.crash - http://a1.phobos.apple.com/us/r30/Purple/v4/90/dc/70/90dc709e-1b69-af62-5b63-0a02d6a59524/temp..yfapebdo.crash Since this effectively prevents us from submitting any iOS apps, it is critical to us. thank you! David""""",title+description
TIMOB-13374,12,"""CLI: --no-colors flag is disregarded""","""""""h5. Description  We noticed an issue in studio with color codes in the console. After further investigation, this turns out to be a regression from 3.0.24 in the CLI. The --no-colors flag is not honored, so all activity is output in color. This presents a problem more so in Studio where the text includes codes for the colors and therefore looks """"""""non-ideal"""""""".    This is a CLI regression from 3.0.24    h5. Steps to reproduce:  1) Try any CLI command with the --no-color flag (I like to use """"""""ti config --no-colors"""""""")    h5. Result:  Colors still present in the output    h5. Expected result:  No colors in the output""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: --no-colors flag is disregarded
Description: """"h5. Description We noticed an issue in studio with color codes in the console. After further investigation, this turns out to be a regression from 3.0.24 in the CLI. The --no-colors flag is not honored, so all activity is output in color. This presents a problem more so in Studio where the text includes codes for the colors and therefore looks """"""""non-ideal"""""""". This is a CLI regression from 3.0.24 h5. Steps to reproduce: 1) Try any CLI command with the --no-color flag (I like to use """"""""ti config --no-colors"""""""") h5. Result: Colors still present in the output h5. Expected result: No colors in the output""""",title+description
TIMOB-13373,12,"""Android: ImageView canScale property does not maintain boundary""","""""""If the following code is run, once the image is displayed, pan the image without zooming. It can be observed that the image is going outside the viewable region and the view becomes green and the image is not longer displayed.    It should be within the viewable region.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView canScale property does not maintain boundary
Description: """"If the following code is run, once the image is displayed, pan the image without zooming. It can be observed that the image is going outside the viewable region and the view becomes green and the image is not longer displayed. It should be within the viewable region. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13372,12,"""Build error: /bin/sh: bad interpreter: Operation not permitted problem""","""""""Project which used to build just fine refuses to build.  Brand new sample project also refuses to build.  iPhone simulator is the build target.    The error is """"""""/bin/sh: bad interpreter: Operation not permitted"""""""" here are the last few entries from the build log:    [TRACE] :      setenv YACC yacc  [TRACE] :      /bin/sh -c /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh  [TRACE] :  /bin/sh: /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh: /bin/sh: bad interpreter: Operation not permitted  [TRACE] :  Command /bin/sh failed with exit code 126  [ERROR] :  ** BUILD FAILED **  [ERROR] :  The following build commands failed:  [ERROR] :   PhaseScriptExecution Pre-Compile build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh  [ERROR] :  (1 failure)    (Searching the web indicated that this might be a problem with the com.apple.quarantine attribute, but I have checked and there are no cases of that attribute being anywhere - ran xattr to remove them regardless with no change in result)    If I manually run the build sh script from terminal with the following command line it gives the error:    /bin/sh -c /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh    But if instead I run it without the -c it builds just fine.  e.g.    /bin/sh /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh  """"""",Bug,"Title: Build error: /bin/sh: bad interpreter: Operation not permitted problem
Description: """"Project which used to build just fine refuses to build. Brand new sample project also refuses to build. iPhone simulator is the build target. The error is """"""""/bin/sh: bad interpreter: Operation not permitted"""""""" here are the last few entries from the build log: [TRACE] : setenv YACC yacc [TRACE] : /bin/sh -c /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh [TRACE] : /bin/sh: /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh: /bin/sh: bad interpreter: Operation not permitted [TRACE] : Command /bin/sh failed with exit code 126 [ERROR] : ** BUILD FAILED ** [ERROR] : The following build commands failed: [ERROR] : PhaseScriptExecution Pre-Compile build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh [ERROR] : (1 failure) (Searching the web indicated that this might be a problem with the com.apple.quarantine attribute, but I have checked and there are no cases of that attribute being anywhere - ran xattr to remove them regardless with no change in result) If I manually run the build sh script from terminal with the following command line it gives the error: /bin/sh -c /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh But if instead I run it without the -c it builds just fine. e.g. /bin/sh /Volumes/Source/Demo/build/iphone/build/Demo.build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Demo.build/Script-241EAF36118E30260081A5BE.sh """"",title+description
