TIMOB-13368,12,"""Android emulator cannot be launched using titanium.py""","""""""When I run {{$TITANIUM_HOME/titanium.py emulator --platform=android}} or {{ant run.emulator}} from the command line, I get the following error:    {code:none}  Traceback (most recent call last):    File """"""""/Users/paul/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/3.0.0.GA/module/builder.py"""""""", line 256, in <module>      main(sys.argv)    File """"""""/Users/paul/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/3.0.0.GA/module/builder.py"""""""", line 188, in main      manifest = Manifest(os.path.join(project_dir, 'manifest'))    File """"""""/Users/paul/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/3.0.0.GA/manifest.py"""""""", line 11, in __init__      f = open(data, 'r')  IOError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/usr/local/Cellar/android-sdk/r21.0.1/manifest'  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android emulator cannot be launched using titanium.py
