TIMOB-13360,12,"""iOS: Removing camera media from temp""","""""""Once video / picture is shot and returned as a TiBlob, it has to be removed from the """"""""YourApp.app/tmp/capture"""""""" folder. Applications like PhoneView provide access to private application data. Since it isn't documented that Titanium leaves the trail behind, it may hurt privacy-related apps, like ours.    (I'll be working on this myself. Pull request to come soon)""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Removing camera media from temp
Description: """"Once video / picture is shot and returned as a TiBlob, it has to be removed from the """"""""YourApp.app/tmp/capture"""""""" folder. Applications like PhoneView provide access to private application data. Since it isn't documented that Titanium leaves the trail behind, it may hurt privacy-related apps, like ours. (I'll be working on this myself. Pull request to come soon)""""",title+description
TIMOB-13359,12,"""Android: Support error object of an event payload other than string""","""""""Changes introduced in TIMOB-12651 enforced that error objects of an event payload must be of type String, but this broke backward compatibility discovered while optimizing Lanica's """"""""Gardens of Time"""""""" app. We should still allow error object to be other than String for backwards compatibility, but also issue e deprecation warning.    See here for the change introduced in 3.1.0:    https://github.com/BlainHamon/titanium_mobile/commit/d2102b5d9020a11b26cd51a92c23029b68082240  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Support error object of an event payload other than string
Description: """"Changes introduced in TIMOB-12651 enforced that error objects of an event payload must be of type String, but this broke backward compatibility discovered while optimizing Lanica's """"""""Gardens of Time"""""""" app. We should still allow error object to be other than String for backwards compatibility, but also issue e deprecation warning. See here for the change introduced in 3.1.0: https://github.com/BlainHamon/titanium_mobile/commit/d2102b5d9020a11b26cd51a92c23029b68082240 """"",title+description
TIMOB-13358,12,"""Code Analyzer: Native methods that modify their objects don't respect ambiguous blocks""","""""""If a native method is called that modifies the base object and is in an ambiguous block, it needs to convert the object to unknown. For example:    both branches of the if are evaluated, but the first branch is evaluated first and deletes x[2] before the second branch is evaluated, resulting in a """"""""undefined value has no property """"""""length"""""""""""""""" exception. Instead, the array needs to be converted to unknown.""""""",Bug,"Title: Code Analyzer: Native methods that modify their objects don't respect ambiguous blocks
Description: """"If a native method is called that modifies the base object and is in an ambiguous block, it needs to convert the object to unknown. For example: both branches of the if are evaluated, but the first branch is evaluated first and deletes x[2] before the second branch is evaluated, resulting in a """"""""undefined value has no property """"""""length"""""""""""""""" exception. Instead, the array needs to be converted to unknown.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13357,12,"""Android: Titanium does not properly handle arrays in form-encoded POSTs""","""""""When using the HTTPClient in Titanium Mobile, the documentation (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.1/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient-method-send) says that if you pass a serializable JavaScript object, it will automatically turn it into form-encoded POST data. However, this breaks when your data contains an array.    Using the free service httpbin (http://httpbin.org/) to view the POST data that is sent, you can see that the array is not properly encoded. By sending POST data to httpbin.org/post, we can see the POST data that Titanium sends.    Example code:     {code:js}  var xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient();  xhr.onload = function(ev) {    Ti.API.info(this.responseText);  };  xhr.open('POST','http://httpbin.org/post');  xhr.send({    'test_text': 'testing',    'test_array': ['one','two','three']  });    {     """"""""files"""""""": {},     """"""""form"""""""": {        """"""""test_array"""""""": """"""""[Ljava.lang.Object;@41a6e560"""""""",        """"""""test_text"""""""": """"""""testing""""""""     },     """"""""url"""""""": """"""""http://httpbin.org/post"""""""",     """"""""args"""""""": {},     """"""""headers"""""""": {        """"""""Content-Length"""""""": """"""""63"""""""",        """"""""Connection"""""""": """"""""keep-alive"""""""",        """"""""User-Agent"""""""": """""""""""""""",        """"""""Host"""""""": """"""""httpbin.org"""""""",        """"""""X-Requested-With"""""""": """"""""XMLHttpRequest"""""""",        """"""""Content-Type"""""""": """"""""application/x-www-form-urlencoded""""""""     },     """"""""json"""""""": null,     """"""""data"""""""": """"""""""""""""  }      Creates the correct post data:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium does not properly handle arrays in form-encoded POSTs
Description: """"When using the HTTPClient in Titanium Mobile, the documentation (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.1/#!/api/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient-method-send) says that if you pass a serializable JavaScript object, it will automatically turn it into form-encoded POST data. However, this breaks when your data contains an array. Using the free service httpbin (http://httpbin.org/) to view the POST data that is sent, you can see that the array is not properly encoded. By sending POST data to httpbin.org/post, we can see the POST data that Titanium sends. Example code: {code:js} var xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function(ev) { Ti.API.info(this.responseText); }; xhr.open('POST','http://httpbin.org/post'); xhr.send({ 'test_text': 'testing', 'test_array': ['one','two','three'] }); { """"""""files"""""""": {}, """"""""form"""""""": { """"""""test_array"""""""": """"""""[Ljava.lang.Object;@41a6e560"""""""", """"""""test_text"""""""": """"""""testing"""""""" }, """"""""url"""""""": """"""""http://httpbin.org/post"""""""", """"""""args"""""""": {}, """"""""headers"""""""": { """"""""Content-Length"""""""": """"""""63"""""""", """"""""Connection"""""""": """"""""keep-alive"""""""", """"""""User-Agent"""""""": """""""""""""""", """"""""Host"""""""": """"""""httpbin.org"""""""", """"""""X-Requested-With"""""""": """"""""XMLHttpRequest"""""""", """"""""Content-Type"""""""": """"""""application/x-www-form-urlencoded"""""""" }, """"""""json"""""""": null, """"""""data"""""""": """""""""""""""" } Creates the correct post data: """"",title+description
TIMOB-13356,12,"""Android: make TiBaseService an interface""","""""""I was looking at creating a Service inheriting Service but without being android.app.Service. As a consequence of that i couldnt use TiBaseService and ServiceProxy as they just inherit android.app.Service.  So i had to copy everything.  Would be great if it was made an interface so that we could use subclasses of android.app.Service.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: make TiBaseService an interface
Description: """"I was looking at creating a Service inheriting Service but without being android.app.Service. As a consequence of that i couldnt use TiBaseService and ServiceProxy as they just inherit android.app.Service. So i had to copy everything. Would be great if it was made an interface so that we could use subclasses of android.app.Service.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13355,12,"""TiAPI: Require relative path from compile module and directly from within an app""","""""""Following [this|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9524] pull request i started working on a new commonjs structure in my projects. The idea was this   \\  \\  * create a module """"""""com.foo.bar.js""""""""  * either use that module directly in an app (git submodule for example)  * or use that module compiled in a Ti Module for distribution  \\  \\  That way i could easily work in my private project directly with the module (and thus modify it). And when i need to use it for a client i can compile it and simply use it as a native module.  \\  \\  This actually work except for one thing. If you want to """"""""require"""""""" relative modules inside  """"""""com.foo.bar.js"""""""" you are facing a problem  \\  \\  * If directly used in an App project you need to use './'  * If you work from a module assets directory, you need to use '/'  \\  \\  So my request is this: could './' be treated as '/' when used from a module assets directory. Right now the './' looks from the app js file and not the module assets dir.  I dont see any case where you would need that  \\  \\  Obviously if possible, i would love to have that on ios and android ;)  \\  Thanks""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Require relative path from compile module and directly from within an app
Description: """"Following [this|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9524] pull request i started working on a new commonjs structure in my projects. The idea was this \\ \\ * create a module """"""""com.foo.bar.js"""""""" * either use that module directly in an app (git submodule for example) * or use that module compiled in a Ti Module for distribution \\ \\ That way i could easily work in my private project directly with the module (and thus modify it). And when i need to use it for a client i can compile it and simply use it as a native module. \\ \\ This actually work except for one thing. If you want to """"""""require"""""""" relative modules inside """"""""com.foo.bar.js"""""""" you are facing a problem \\ \\ * If directly used in an App project you need to use './' * If you work from a module assets directory, you need to use '/' \\ \\ So my request is this: could './' be treated as '/' when used from a module assets directory. Right now the './' looks from the app js file and not the module assets dir. I dont see any case where you would need that \\ \\ Obviously if possible, i would love to have that on ios and android ;) \\ Thanks""""",title+description
TIMOB-13354,12,"""CLI commands does not work after setup""","""""""1. Download Titanium Studio and install it.(on clean machine, it should be first attempt to install Titanium)  2. Allow Studio install everything it asks (SDK, Alloy, etc.)  3. Open shell and try execute titanium -v. And you will see error.  TypeError: Cannot call method 'match' of undefined    Workaround:  execute in console  titanium setup   and configure your <USER>account    should note that in Titanium Studio I was successfully logged in before. But CLI ignores this login    Full error log:  aod@ubntu:~/tizen-sdk/tools/ide/bin$ node -v  v0.8.18  aod@ubntu:~/tizen-sdk/tools/ide/bin$ titanium -v  3.0.24  aod@ubntu:~/tizen-sdk/tools/ide/bin$   /usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/analytics.js:180      sessionCookie = status.cookie.match(/(PHPSESSID=[A-Za-z0-9]+)/),                                    ^  TypeError: Cannot call method 'match' of undefined      at /usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/analytics.js:180:35      at async.parallel (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:476:17)      at async.forEach (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:94:25)      at async.parallel (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:473:21)      at <USER>on.async.parallel.osinfo (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/analytics.js:56:5)      at module.exports.getOSInfo (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/environ.js:215:4)      at ChildProcess.exithandler (child_process.js:538:7)      at ChildProcess.EventEmitter.emit (events.js:99:17)      at maybeClose (child_process.js:638:16)      at Process._handle.onexit (child_process.js:680:5)    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI commands does not work after setup
Description: """"1. Download Titanium Studio and install it.(on clean machine, it should be first attempt to install Titanium) 2. Allow Studio install everything it asks (SDK, Alloy, etc.) 3. Open shell and try execute titanium -v. And you will see error. TypeError: Cannot call method 'match' of undefined Workaround: execute in console titanium setup and configure your <USER>account should note that in Titanium Studio I was successfully logged in before. But CLI ignores this login Full error log: aod@ubntu:~/tizen-sdk/tools/ide/bin$ node -v v0.8.18 aod@ubntu:~/tizen-sdk/tools/ide/bin$ titanium -v 3.0.24 aod@ubntu:~/tizen-sdk/tools/ide/bin$ /usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/analytics.js:180 sessionCookie = status.cookie.match(/(PHPSESSID=[A-Za-z0-9]+)/), ^ TypeError: Cannot call method 'match' of undefined at /usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/analytics.js:180:35 at async.parallel (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:476:17) at async.forEach (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:94:25) at async.parallel (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:473:21) at <USER>on.async.parallel.osinfo (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/analytics.js:56:5) at module.exports.getOSInfo (/usr/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/node-appc/lib/environ.js:215:4) at ChildProcess.exithandler (child_process.js:538:7) at ChildProcess.EventEmitter.emit (events.js:99:17) at maybeClose (child_process.js:638:16) at Process._handle.onexit (child_process.js:680:5) """"",title+description
TIMOB-13353,12,"""Android: Event name inconsistency""","""""""In the current master branch there is an inconsistency in android specific events names  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/titanium/src/java/org/<USER>titanium/TiC.java#L31    and a recent pull request  https://github.com/hieupham007/Titanium_Mobile/commit/571ec00d1b7174f8b9efa3c237ff828c8a8873ac#commitcomment-2014775    What s the right one?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Event name inconsistency
