Description: """"In the titanium-sdk module's tiappxml.js file, it's missing the XML serialization of the <code-processor> section.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13346,12,"""Android: A couple of app icons gets created, the first one fails and the second launches""","""""""h6.Issue  When an app is installed on certain Android OS versions, that may create couple of instances by instance I mean an app icon. Meanwhile one of them is able to run, the other just fails. We couldn't get customer's source but that can be replicated using the Kitchen Sink demo which is available below.    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Get Kitchen Sink app from http://dl.dropbox.com/u/34061091/KitchenSInk1.zip  2. Use """"""""Install to Android Device"""""""" option from Studio IDE  3. At device goto """"""""All apps"""""""" and launch KitchenSink. From there, couple icons can be seen (at the top left on my device's screen shoot).    h4.Console outputs  h6.Console output: Clicking on 1st app icon  The app is unable to run, fails throwing the following runtime error:      h6.Console output: Clicking on 2nd app icon  The app launches as expected      h6.Additional details  Customer have found an issue in the appname they were providing via tiapp.xml.  If this name starts with a digit [0-9], there is logic in the Ti android.py script to prepend the appname with an underscore '_' character.  This results in multiple intents begin added to the manifest file and potentially the cause of this issue.        <application android:label=""""""""BeB 878"""""""" android:icon=""""""""@drawable/appicon"""""""" android:name=""""""""_878_readinessApplication"""""""" android:debuggable=""""""""false"""""""" android:screenOrientation=""""""""portrait"""""""">""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: A couple of app icons gets created, the first one fails and the second launches
Description: """"h6.Issue When an app is installed on certain Android OS versions, that may create couple of instances by instance I mean an app icon. Meanwhile one of them is able to run, the other just fails. We couldn't get customer's source but that can be replicated using the Kitchen Sink demo which is available below. h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Get Kitchen Sink app from http://dl.dropbox.com/u/34061091/KitchenSInk1.zip 2. Use """"""""Install to Android Device"""""""" option from Studio IDE 3. At device goto """"""""All apps"""""""" and launch KitchenSink. From there, couple icons can be seen (at the top left on my device's screen shoot). h4.Console outputs h6.Console output: Clicking on 1st app icon The app is unable to run, fails throwing the following runtime error: h6.Console output: Clicking on 2nd app icon The app launches as expected h6.Additional details Customer have found an issue in the appname they were providing via tiapp.xml. If this name starts with a digit [0-9], there is logic in the Ti android.py script to prepend the appname with an underscore '_' character. This results in multiple intents begin added to the manifest file and potentially the cause of this issue. <application android:label=""""""""BeB 878"""""""" android:icon=""""""""@drawable/appicon"""""""" android:name=""""""""_878_readinessApplication"""""""" android:debuggable=""""""""false"""""""" android:screenOrientation=""""""""portrait"""""""">""""",title+description
TIMOB-13343,12,"""CodeProcessor: The internal [[Call]] methods have mismatched signatures""","""""""The internal [[Call]] method has been extended in a few places, but unfortunately there are two separate signatures with no way to distinguish between them. This is causing bugs with native methods and ambiguous contexts and potentially with eval contexts. They need to be refactored to call(thisVal, args, options).""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: The internal [[Call]] methods have mismatched signatures
Description: """"The internal [[Call]] method has been extended in a few places, but unfortunately there are two separate signatures with no way to distinguish between them. This is causing bugs with native methods and ambiguous contexts and potentially with eval contexts. They need to be refactored to call(thisVal, args, options).""""",title+description
TIMOB-13342,12,"""Profiler: Android: results are inconsistent and lacking some function calls""","""""""If you run more than one to three snapshots for Android, all results are one node: (program) 100%    The other nodes only appear on the creation of the first few snapshots.    Test Steps:    1. Run code (app.js) in Android Profiler:        2. Create a few snapshots and click on some of the buttons.    Test Results:    After a few snapshots, all data stops appearing.""""""",Bug,"Title: Profiler: Android: results are inconsistent and lacking some function calls
Description: """"If you run more than one to three snapshots for Android, all results are one node: (program) 100% The other nodes only appear on the creation of the first few snapshots. Test Steps: 1. Run code (app.js) in Android Profiler: 2. Create a few snapshots and click on some of the buttons. Test Results: After a few snapshots, all data stops appearing.""""",title+description
