TIMOB-13302,12,"""Android: Create a number stepper widget""","""""""Android has a common UI pattern for number fields: a text field with plus and minus buttons, be it vertically or horizontally. I think that Titanium could create a custom widget for that, instead of offering an iOS picker emulator - that's very awful for UX in Android, since it's not a real, """"""""native"""""""", common pattern on Android apps.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Create a number stepper widget
Description: """"Android has a common UI pattern for number fields: a text field with plus and minus buttons, be it vertically or horizontally. I think that Titanium could create a custom widget for that, instead of offering an iOS picker emulator - that's very awful for UX in Android, since it's not a real, """"""""native"""""""", common pattern on Android apps.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13301,12,"""iOS: Add animation to scrollToView, moveNext, movePrevious on ScrollableView""","""""""* on android setCurrentPage sets the page with animation.  On ios it doesnt.  * movePrevious and moveNext should be implemented on iOS  * it would be nice to be able to choose if scrollToView, moveNext, movePrevious happen with animation""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add animation to scrollToView, moveNext, movePrevious on ScrollableView
Description: """"* on android setCurrentPage sets the page with animation. On ios it doesnt. * movePrevious and moveNext should be implemented on iOS * it would be nice to be able to choose if scrollToView, moveNext, movePrevious happen with animation""""",title+description
TIMOB-13300,12,"""CodeProcessor: Internal methods don't register as ambiguous blocks correctly""","""""""Some native methods do things that query aspects of the current context. Since native methods don't create their own context, they query the calling context, which is bad. A dummy context needs to be created""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Internal methods don't register as ambiguous blocks correctly
Description: """"Some native methods do things that query aspects of the current context. Since native methods don't create their own context, they query the calling context, which is bad. A dummy context needs to be created""""",title+description
TIMOB-13298,12,"""iOS: Paging Control in the ScrollableView is failing to show the current status of the page""","""""""h4. Problem Description   in the ScrollableView, the dots show and lights correctly but NOT if it's selected the last view. In this case the last dot lights but then returns to the previous one.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create new mobile project  2. Add this code to app.js:    3. Scroll to the right, and when yuou reach to the last view in the scrollableview, the pager will show the previous one, even if the view is the right one.     h4. Extra info  http://developer.<USER>com/question/150306/pagingcontrol-dots-behave-uncorrectly  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Paging Control in the ScrollableView is failing to show the current status of the page
