TIMOB-13221,12,"""Android: Maps V2 Module - addAnnotations method not working on a map""","""""""h6.Issue  addAnnotations method forces app to close.    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. load app - app opens and run Maps as expected  2. click on any annotation - offending code under Resources/ui/common/FirstView.js  3. Monitor logs - from there     h6.console logs      h6.Additional details  Patched 2.1.3.GA SDK for use:  http://dl.dropbox.com/u/34061091/mobilesdk-2.1.3.MapsModule-osx.zip    h6.Further info  Map Module does not force the app to close as long as all the annotations have been added during Map creation i.e. """"""""var map = MapModule.createView({ annotations : [anno1, anno2, anno3],""""""""  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Maps V2 Module - addAnnotations method not working on a map
Description: """"h6.Issue addAnnotations method forces app to close. h6.Steps to reproduce 1. load app - app opens and run Maps as expected 2. click on any annotation - offending code under Resources/ui/common/FirstView.js 3. Monitor logs - from there h6.console logs h6.Additional details Patched 2.1.3.GA SDK for use: http://dl.dropbox.com/u/34061091/mobilesdk-2.1.3.MapsModule-osx.zip h6.Further info Map Module does not force the app to close as long as all the annotations have been added during Map creation i.e. """"""""var map = MapModule.createView({ annotations : [anno1, anno2, anno3],"""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-13220,12,"""Android: Can not set width on label and ellipsize no longer works""","""""""h2. Problem    Setting width property of label does nothing, and ellipsize stopped working because of it.    This works with Ti SDk 3.1.0.v20130304xxxx  h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win  = Ti.UI.createWindow();      win.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({   text: 'this is some text that should ellipsize because it is too long',   width: 100,   height: 25,   color: 'white',   ellipsize: true,   wordWrap: false,   backgroundColor: 'pink'  }));      win.open();      {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Can not set width on label and ellipsize no longer works
Description: """"h2. Problem Setting width property of label does nothing, and ellipsize stopped working because of it. This works with Ti SDk 3.1.0.v20130304xxxx h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); win.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'this is some text that should ellipsize because it is too long', width: 100, height: 25, color: 'white', ellipsize: true, wordWrap: false, backgroundColor: 'pink' })); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-13219,12,"""BlackBerry: Exceptions cause app failure with no error output or log""","""""""Basic exceptions in Blackberry Titanium apps are causing the app the crash and fail with no error output whatsoever, making debugging and troubleshooting next to impossible. For example, take this code which represents a common mistake in Titanium development:        Ti.UI.Window() should be Ti.UI.createWindow(). Instead of throwing a red screen of death notifying me that there was a runtime exception at a specific file and line, or notifying me in the TiStudio console, I get nothing in both places leaving me with zero information to act on. If I run the exact same code on iOS, I get the following log in TiStudio and I also get the attached image in the simulator itself, making it very clear where I went wrong.        IMHO this is a *very* important issue that needs to be resolved otherwise developer iterations will be painfully slow and generally ineffective.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Exceptions cause app failure with no error output or log
Description: """"Basic exceptions in Blackberry Titanium apps are causing the app the crash and fail with no error output whatsoever, making debugging and troubleshooting next to impossible. For example, take this code which represents a common mistake in Titanium development: Ti.UI.Window() should be Ti.UI.createWindow(). Instead of throwing a red screen of death notifying me that there was a runtime exception at a specific file and line, or notifying me in the TiStudio console, I get nothing in both places leaving me with zero information to act on. If I run the exact same code on iOS, I get the following log in TiStudio and I also get the attached image in the simulator itself, making it very clear where I went wrong. IMHO this is a *very* important issue that needs to be resolved otherwise developer iterations will be painfully slow and generally ineffective.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13218,12,"""Android: Adding values other then 'v8' or 'rhino' to android runtime in tiapp.xml, error should occur.""","""""""Android: Adding values other then 'v8' or 'rhino' to android runtime in tiapp.xml, error should occur.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a default titanium project.  2. Add values like '%#*@#^*@#(sd' to ti.android.runtime property in tiapp.xml  3. Run the project.    Expected:  Error should occur as  [ERROR] invalid runtime """"""""$$^#@#$o"""""""" requested, must be 'v8' or 'rhino'    Actual :   No error occur.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Adding values other then 'v8' or 'rhino' to android runtime in tiapp.xml, error should occur.
Description: """"Android: Adding values other then 'v8' or 'rhino' to android runtime in tiapp.xml, error should occur. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a default titanium project. 2. Add values like '%#*@#^*@#(sd' to ti.android.runtime property in tiapp.xml 3. Run the project. Expected: Error should occur as [ERROR] invalid runtime """"""""$$^#@#$o"""""""" requested, must be 'v8' or 'rhino' Actual : No error occur.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13217,12,"""Blackberry: dialog_test.js is invalid""","""""""h2. Problem    The dialog_test.js app is found here: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry/blob/master/test/apps/native/tibbtest/Resources/dialog_test.js    It is currently littered with unescaped special characters, the indention is erratic, and it has elements in it that are not Javascript code. It appears that this code was copied from a chat client of some kind and committed into the list of test apps without testing. The content of this sample should be cleaned up so that it can be executed properly.    h2. Pull Request    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry/pull/27""""""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry: dialog_test.js is invalid
Description: """"h2. Problem The dialog_test.js app is found here: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry/blob/master/test/apps/native/tibbtest/Resources/dialog_test.js It is currently littered with unescaped special characters, the indention is erratic, and it has elements in it that are not Javascript code. It appears that this code was copied from a chat client of some kind and committed into the list of test apps without testing. The content of this sample should be cleaned up so that it can be executed properly. h2. Pull Request https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry/pull/27""""",title+description
TIMOB-13216,12,"""Blackberry: Ti.UI.SIZE and doesn't work with Labels""","""""""h2. problem    Ti.UI.SIZE used for the height and width of a Ti.UI.Label causes the label not to appear at all on Blackberry. The use of Ti.UI.SIZE is critical with this component and is commonly used as the default behavior for a Label is typically Ti.UI.FILL.     h2. expected behavior    Using Ti.UI.SIZE for the height and width of a Ti.UI.Label should result in the Label being the exact height and width of the text within it, based on the Label's set or default font properties.    h2. test case    """"""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry: Ti.UI.SIZE and doesn't work with Labels
Description: """"h2. problem Ti.UI.SIZE used for the height and width of a Ti.UI.Label causes the label not to appear at all on Blackberry. The use of Ti.UI.SIZE is critical with this component and is commonly used as the default behavior for a Label is typically Ti.UI.FILL. h2. expected behavior Using Ti.UI.SIZE for the height and width of a Ti.UI.Label should result in the Label being the exact height and width of the text within it, based on the Label's set or default font properties. h2. test case """"",title+description
TIMOB-13215,12,"""Blackberry: Window in Tab does not fill the tab""","""""""Using the default 2 tabbed app: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry/blob/master/test/apps/native/tibbtest/Resources/tabgroup_test.js    The window with the white background in each tab should fill the entire tabgroup, as the initial layout state of Ti.UI.Window should be Ti.UI.FILL. Instead, it appears that the Window's size is only big enough for its content, similar to what you would expect to with Ti.UI.SIZE (see attached). Setting the height value of the Window manually has no effect using either Ti.UI.FILL or a static value like 300. Ti.UI.FILL should be the default behavior.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry: Window in Tab does not fill the tab
Description: """"Using the default 2 tabbed app: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry/blob/master/test/apps/native/tibbtest/Resources/tabgroup_test.js The window with the white background in each tab should fill the entire tabgroup, as the initial layout state of Ti.UI.Window should be Ti.UI.FILL. Instead, it appears that the Window's size is only big enough for its content, similar to what you would expect to with Ti.UI.SIZE (see attached). Setting the height value of the Window manually has no effect using either Ti.UI.FILL or a static value like 300. Ti.UI.FILL should be the default behavior. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13213,12,"""Android: Adding label to TabGroup addTab method, No Exception is thrown""","""""""When a label is passed to a tab group's addTab method, Exception is expected but no exception is displayed.  This is not a regression.It exists on 3.0.2 GA as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Add the following to app.js and run the app.    var tabs = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();  tabs.addTab(Ti.UI.createLabel());  tabs.open();    Expected:  A classCastException should occur.  E/TiApplication(8640): (main) [5973,6039] Sending event: exception on thread: main msg:java.lang.ClassCastException: ti.modules.titanium.ui.LabelProxy; Titanium 1.8.1,2012/01/27 17:31,a24502a  E/TiApplication(8640): java.lang.ClassCastException: ti.modules.titanium.ui.LabelProxy    Actual:  No exception is occurred.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Adding label to TabGroup addTab method, No Exception is thrown
Description: """"When a label is passed to a tab group's addTab method, Exception is expected but no exception is displayed. This is not a regression.It exists on 3.0.2 GA as well. Steps to reproduce: 1) Add the following to app.js and run the app. var tabs = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); tabs.addTab(Ti.UI.createLabel()); tabs.open(); Expected: A classCastException should occur. E/TiApplication(8640): (main) [5973,6039] Sending event: exception on thread: main msg:java.lang.ClassCastException: ti.modules.titanium.ui.LabelProxy; Titanium 1.8.1,2012/01/27 17:31,a24502a E/TiApplication(8640): java.lang.ClassCastException: ti.modules.titanium.ui.LabelProxy Actual: No exception is occurred.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13209,12,"""Tizen : App run on tizen device fails from studio where as from CLI works properly""","""""""NOTE:  1.)This issue is only seen when run through studio. With CLI the app builds & run fine on the device  2.)The tizen environments have been freshly setup today after the invalid environment issue which we had earlier.  3.)From studio run on emulator works fine    Description:  1.Follow the setup instructions on the preview page & do the tizen setup  2.Connect the tizen device to the machine  3.Create an app with tizen as target  4.Run on device    Actual Results:  1.The app does not install on the device & launch fails  2.Studio logs:      3.Console log:      Expected Device:  1.The app should run on device normally & expected  """"""",Bug,"Title: Tizen : App run on tizen device fails from studio where as from CLI works properly
Description: """"NOTE: 1.)This issue is only seen when run through studio. With CLI the app builds & run fine on the device 2.)The tizen environments have been freshly setup today after the invalid environment issue which we had earlier. 3.)From studio run on emulator works fine Description: 1.Follow the setup instructions on the preview page & do the tizen setup 2.Connect the tizen device to the machine 3.Create an app with tizen as target 4.Run on device Actual Results: 1.The app does not install on the device & launch fails 2.Studio logs: 3.Console log: Expected Device: 1.The app should run on device normally & expected """"",title+description
TIMOB-13208,12,"""CodeProcessor: Indirect infinite loops are not detected""","""""""It's possible to create an infinite loop of sorts using circular-calling functions that are not infinitely recursive (or recursive at all). To solve this, a generic cycle detector should be implemented.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Indirect infinite loops are not detected
Description: """"It's possible to create an infinite loop of sorts using circular-calling functions that are not infinitely recursive (or recursive at all). To solve this, a generic cycle detector should be implemented.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13207,12,"""Tizen : App hangs on the appcelerator splashscreen on device""","""""""NOTE: The app runs fine on the emulator which came with the 2.0.0 tizen sdk    Description:  1.Follow the setup instructions on the preview page & do the tizen setup  2.Connect the tizen device to the machine  3.Using CLI or studio create an app with tizen as target  4.Run on device    Actual Result:  1.The app launches & hangs at the <USER>splash screen    Expected Result:  1.The app should not hang at the splash screen""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen : App hangs on the appcelerator splashscreen on device
Description: """"NOTE: The app runs fine on the emulator which came with the 2.0.0 tizen sdk Description: 1.Follow the setup instructions on the preview page & do the tizen setup 2.Connect the tizen device to the machine 3.Using CLI or studio create an app with tizen as target 4.Run on device Actual Result: 1.The app launches & hangs at the <USER>splash screen Expected Result: 1.The app should not hang at the splash screen""""",title+description
TIMOB-13206,12,"""searchHidden set to true breaks setData() on tableView (3.0.2 Regression)""","""""""h3. Description  If you add a searchBar to a tableView and set searchHidden:true on the tableView, you can not properly setData to the table.    h3. iOS Error Message      h3.Simple Sample App  """"""",Bug,"Title: searchHidden set to true breaks setData() on tableView (3.0.2 Regression)
Description: """"h3. Description If you add a searchBar to a tableView and set searchHidden:true on the tableView, you can not properly setData to the table. h3. iOS Error Message h3.Simple Sample App """"",title+description
TIMOB-13196,12,"""CLI: Create hook to process macros""","""""""Implement an AST walker-transformer that will replace the macros defined in the spec with their actual values""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CLI: Create hook to process macros
Description: """"Implement an AST walker-transformer that will replace the macros defined in the spec with their actual values""""",title+description
TIMOB-13195,12,"""TiAPI: Create macro specification""","""""""Need to create the specification for macros. Most likely will be:    __file  __line  __function  """"""",Sub-task,"Title: TiAPI: Create macro specification
Description: """"Need to create the specification for macros. Most likely will be: __file __line __function """"",title+description
TIMOB-13194,12,"""CLI: Change config logger to console and default log level to trace""","""""""There are too many people that are having problems and when they submit logs, the default info log level doesn't have enough info. If we default this to trace, it will output everything and save a lot of time.    To test:    Run """"""""titanium config cli.logLevel"""""""" and it should just say the log level in all lower case with out square brackets and without colors.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Change config logger to console and default log level to trace
Description: """"There are too many people that are having problems and when they submit logs, the default info log level doesn't have enough info. If we default this to trace, it will output everything and save a lot of time. To test: Run """"""""titanium config cli.logLevel"""""""" and it should just say the log level in all lower case with out square brackets and without colors.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13193,12,"""TiAPI: Native JS module: support Ti.include""","""""""Thanks to TIMOB-9317 we now are able to require submodules inside modules    Now it would nice to be able to use Ti.include with module compiled js files.    h2. Test Steps    h3. Module build  # Create a new module project for Android/ios with the id com.foo.bar.  # Download the attached assets.zip  # Unzip assets.zip in the directory of the new module project  # Run ant to build the module.    h3. Project  # Download the attached tic2043.zip and unzip it.  # Import the resulting directory into TiStudio  # Run project    h3. Pass:  # The test is simple, if you see """"""""woo :)"""""""" in the console then it worked!  """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Native JS module: support Ti.include
Description: """"Thanks to TIMOB-9317 we now are able to require submodules inside modules Now it would nice to be able to use Ti.include with module compiled js files. h2. Test Steps h3. Module build # Create a new module project for Android/ios with the id com.foo.bar. # Download the attached assets.zip # Unzip assets.zip in the directory of the new module project # Run ant to build the module. h3. Project # Download the attached tic2043.zip and unzip it. # Import the resulting directory into TiStudio # Run project h3. Pass: # The test is simple, if you see """"""""woo :)"""""""" in the console then it worked! """"",title+description
TIMOB-13192,12,"""CodeProcessor: Ambiguous blocks do not handle throws properly""","""""""Statements that alter the flow of execution outside of am ambiguous block are not handled correctly. There are two ways to do this: returns and throws. Throws are very complex, and I'm not sure how to fix them yet, but something has to be done.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Ambiguous blocks do not handle throws properly
Description: """"Statements that alter the flow of execution outside of am ambiguous block are not handled correctly. There are two ways to do this: returns and throws. Throws are very complex, and I'm not sure how to fix them yet, but something has to be done.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13191,12,"""CodeProcessor: Ambiguous blocks do not handle returns properly""","""""""Statements that alter the flow of execution outside of am ambiguous block are not handled correctly. There are two ways to do this: returns and throws. Throws are very complex, and I don't know how to handle those yet, but returns are fairly easy (and more common)""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Ambiguous blocks do not handle returns properly
Description: """"Statements that alter the flow of execution outside of am ambiguous block are not handled correctly. There are two ways to do this: returns and throws. Throws are very complex, and I don't know how to handle those yet, but returns are fairly easy (and more common)""""",title+description
TIMOB-13189,12,"""MobileWeb:In Alloy, view is visible even when visible='false' is specified in xml file""","""""""h2. Description  In a view (availView in attached xml file) that contains a Mapview and tableview. The view (availView) is coded to visible=""""""""false"""""""". The map will be shown when the user clicks on the Show Map button. But the map is shown when the application first starts even though it is coded not to be shown. This works fine on iOS but not when used in Mobileweb.    h2. Test Case:  1. Create an alloy project.  2. Replace the index.js, index.tss and index.xml file with the attached one.  3. Start app in browser.  4. The map is shown when it should not be visible.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb:In Alloy, view is visible even when visible='false' is specified in xml file
Description: """"h2. Description In a view (availView in attached xml file) that contains a Mapview and tableview. The view (availView) is coded to visible=""""""""false"""""""". The map will be shown when the user clicks on the Show Map button. But the map is shown when the application first starts even though it is coded not to be shown. This works fine on iOS but not when used in Mobileweb. h2. Test Case: 1. Create an alloy project. 2. Replace the index.js, index.tss and index.xml file with the attached one. 3. Start app in browser. 4. The map is shown when it should not be visible.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13188,12,"""CodeProcessor: create* method override needs to be for all create methods, not just UI.create methods""","""""""Currently, only Ti.UI.create* methods are overridden so that properties are handled correctly, but really all Ti.*.create* methods should be overridden to make sure that, for example, Ti.Network.createHTTPClient is also overridden.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: create* method override needs to be for all create methods, not just UI.create methods
Description: """"Currently, only Ti.UI.create* methods are overridden so that properties are handled correctly, but really all Ti.*.create* methods should be overridden to make sure that, for example, Ti.Network.createHTTPClient is also overridden.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13186,12,"""CodeProcessor: Unknown visualization shows known values as unknown""","""""""The unknown ambiguous visualizer reports things that are unknown that are actually known because the current mechanism for detecting isn't very intelligent.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Unknown visualization shows known values as unknown
Description: """"The unknown ambiguous visualizer reports things that are unknown that are actually known because the current mechanism for detecting isn't very intelligent.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13185,12,"""CodeProcessor: Expose Ti.version""","""""""We already have Ti.version since each run is tied to a specific SDK, so we should expose it.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Expose Ti.version
Description: """"We already have Ti.version since each run is tied to a specific SDK, so we should expose it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13184,12,"""CodeProcessor: code coverage includes non-platform specific files that it shouldn't""","""""""Files that are not platform specific that are overridden by platform specific files are not excluded from coverage data but should be.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: code coverage includes non-platform specific files that it shouldn't
Description: """"Files that are not platform specific that are overridden by platform specific files are not excluded from coverage data but should be.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13183,12,"""CodeProcessor: Merge require and common-globals plugins into ti-api-provider""","""""""When we move to adding support for node.acs, there will be a clash with the existing require and common-globals. These plugins are really ti-specific, so they should go inside of the ti-api-provider plugin. This is also necessary to fix a current architectural issue preventing TIMOB-13088 from being implemented. Currently, the plugins directly set their variables/methods on the global object, but when they are integrated with ti-api-provider, they need to be updated to use the JSCA reading mechanisms in ti-api-provider""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Merge require and common-globals plugins into ti-api-provider
Description: """"When we move to adding support for node.acs, there will be a clash with the existing require and common-globals. These plugins are really ti-specific, so they should go inside of the ti-api-provider plugin. This is also necessary to fix a current architectural issue preventing TIMOB-13088 from being implemented. Currently, the plugins directly set their variables/methods on the global object, but when they are integrated with ti-api-provider, they need to be updated to use the JSCA reading mechanisms in ti-api-provider""""",title+description
TIMOB-13182,12,"""CodeProcessor: getters and setters are not generated for Titanium properties""","""""""Getter and setter methods are not generated for properties in the Titanium API.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: getters and setters are not generated for Titanium properties
Description: """"Getter and setter methods are not generated for properties in the Titanium API.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13181,12,"""CodeProcessor: Ti.Filesystem.ResourcesDirectory is unknown, but shouldn't be""","""""""It is somewhat common for apps to use Ti.FileSystem.ResourcesDirectory to get around historical quirks/bugs in our require mechanism, but this value is unknown currently. It seems safe enough to assign it a value of '/' since the code processor's require mechanism works correctly.""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Ti.Filesystem.ResourcesDirectory is unknown, but shouldn't be
Description: """"It is somewhat common for apps to use Ti.FileSystem.ResourcesDirectory to get around historical quirks/bugs in our require mechanism, but this value is unknown currently. It seems safe enough to assign it a value of '/' since the code processor's require mechanism works correctly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13180,12,"""CodeProcessor: Cleanup Runtime module""","""""""The Runtime module has grown to be ungainly in size and is poorly organized and needs to be cleaned up and possibly split into multiple modules.""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Cleanup Runtime module
Description: """"The Runtime module has grown to be ungainly in size and is poorly organized and needs to be cleaned up and possibly split into multiple modules.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13178,12,"""CLI: Alpha package will not install with node v0.8.17 and npm v1.2.0 configuration""","""""""h3. Error  When attempting to install the npm package for the CLI """"""""sudo npm install -g titanium@3.0.25-alpha"""""""", I would get two lines, then the install seemed to hang:      npm cache clean gave slightly better results:      But the CLI was not installed. We found this:  https://github.com/isaacs/npm/issues/3058    h3. Workaround:  Update npm version with: sudo npm install npm -g  Then retry install.    h3. Steps to reproduce:  1) Ensure you have the indicated versions of node and npm  2) try to install alpha version with """"""""sudo npm install -g titanium@3.0.25-alpha""""""""    h3. Result:  The install fails with 2-4 lines then hang    h3. Expected:  Install succeeds""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Alpha package will not install with node v0.8.17 and npm v1.2.0 configuration
Description: """"h3. Error When attempting to install the npm package for the CLI """"""""sudo npm install -g titanium@3.0.25-alpha"""""""", I would get two lines, then the install seemed to hang: npm cache clean gave slightly better results: But the CLI was not installed. We found this: https://github.com/isaacs/npm/issues/3058 h3. Workaround: Update npm version with: sudo npm install npm -g Then retry install. h3. Steps to reproduce: 1) Ensure you have the indicated versions of node and npm 2) try to install alpha version with """"""""sudo npm install -g titanium@3.0.25-alpha"""""""" h3. Result: The install fails with 2-4 lines then hang h3. Expected: Install succeeds""""",title+description
TIMOB-13177,12,"""iOS: Parity - view properties are not applying correctly on iOS""","""""""Tapping the button shows the view flickering not just from top left to bottom right as it should be, but random places.    Description:  1. Run the following code:    2. Tap on """"""""Test!"""""""" button      Actual result:  2. The view is flickering allover the screen    Expected result:  2. The view should flicker from top left to bottom right  on each tap.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Parity - view properties are not applying correctly on iOS
Description: """"Tapping the button shows the view flickering not just from top left to bottom right as it should be, but random places. Description: 1. Run the following code: 2. Tap on """"""""Test!"""""""" button Actual result: 2. The view is flickering allover the screen Expected result: 2. The view should flicker from top left to bottom right on each tap.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13176,12,"""Tizen : Emulator fails to launch on mac osx gives 'not enough shared memory' error""","""""""NOTE: I am filing this issue as a blocker.This is a big issue,as its not our bug feel free to change the severity    Description:  1.Follow the setup instructions on the tizen preview page here :http://ec2-50-16-19-245.compute-1.amazonaws.com/studio/tizen  2.Fire up an instance of the emulator    Actual Result:  1.Starting the emulator gives """"""""Cannot start this emulator, shared memory not enough"""""""" error & the emulator does not start    2.On doing some research I found a workaround where we have to manually add some values to the 'sysctl.conf' file by sudoing in the file (basically increase the shared memory manually)  3.The tizen jira ticket for the same : https://bugs.tizen.org/jira/browse/TSDK-81   4.This workaround worked for me : http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15000628/tizen-emulator-not-running-in-tizen     NOTE: I don't know if its hardware dependent, but my machine has good hardware.This is a big usability issue.    Expected Result:  1.The emulator should launch without any errors""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen : Emulator fails to launch on mac osx gives 'not enough shared memory' error
Description: """"NOTE: I am filing this issue as a blocker.This is a big issue,as its not our bug feel free to change the severity Description: 1.Follow the setup instructions on the tizen preview page here :http://ec2-50-16-19-245.compute-1.amazonaws.com/studio/tizen 2.Fire up an instance of the emulator Actual Result: 1.Starting the emulator gives """"""""Cannot start this emulator, shared memory not enough"""""""" error & the emulator does not start 2.On doing some research I found a workaround where we have to manually add some values to the 'sysctl.conf' file by sudoing in the file (basically increase the shared memory manually) 3.The tizen jira ticket for the same : https://bugs.tizen.org/jira/browse/TSDK-81 4.This workaround worked for me : http://stackoverflow.com/questions/15000628/tizen-emulator-not-running-in-tizen NOTE: I don't know if its hardware dependent, but my machine has good hardware.This is a big usability issue. Expected Result: 1.The emulator should launch without any errors""""",title+description
TIMOB-13175,12,"""iOS: TableView setData() is broken on 3.0.2.GA""","""""""I have always used setData() to dynamically change or empty tableViews (even the ones which are not on foreground at any given time).    Ti 3.0.2.GA has broken this completely.    First I always get the following error when I use setData() with no parameters or a empty list:            Second, when I issue setData() it doesn't redraw the tableView automatically anymore. It seems I have to redraw the whole screen so the new data can get rendered every time. (like reopening the window which the tableView is on again after a setData).    Looking at the source changes since 3.0.0 and the Assertion failure on TiUITableView.m it looks like it is something related to sections (which I don't use in this case).    I have tested this in 2 big projects I'm working on (AirportChatter / PiniOn). All tableViews that uses setData dynamically are breaking with 3.0.2 on both projects.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView setData() is broken on 3.0.2.GA
Description: """"I have always used setData() to dynamically change or empty tableViews (even the ones which are not on foreground at any given time). Ti 3.0.2.GA has broken this completely. First I always get the following error when I use setData() with no parameters or a empty list: Second, when I issue setData() it doesn't redraw the tableView automatically anymore. It seems I have to redraw the whole screen so the new data can get rendered every time. (like reopening the window which the tableView is on again after a setData). Looking at the source changes since 3.0.0 and the Assertion failure on TiUITableView.m it looks like it is something related to sections (which I don't use in this case). I have tested this in 2 big projects I'm working on (AirportChatter / PiniOn). All tableViews that uses setData dynamically are breaking with 3.0.2 on both projects.""""",title+description
TIMOB-13174,12,"""Android: Tableview: Shows Runtime Error on longpressing on any row""","""""""This is regression. The issue does not exist on 3.0.2.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create an application with code below and launch the application  2. Longpress on any row    Actual: Shows Runtime Error with source error """"""""Ti.API.info('customProp: ' + e.rowData.customProp);"""""""". Please find the attached log file and screen shot.  Expected: Should not show the Runtime Error.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tableview: Shows Runtime Error on longpressing on any row
Description: """"This is regression. The issue does not exist on 3.0.2. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an application with code below and launch the application 2. Longpress on any row Actual: Shows Runtime Error with source error """"""""Ti.API.info('customProp: ' + e.rowData.customProp);"""""""". Please find the attached log file and screen shot. Expected: Should not show the Runtime Error. """"",title+description
TIMOB-13173,12,"""Android: TableView: Softkeyboard appears on clicking any tableviewrow but immediately disappear""","""""""This is regression. The issue does not exist on 3.0.2. But the textfield in tableviewrow is never editable on any build.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create an application with code below and launch the application  2. Click on any row in the tableview    Actual: Softkeyboard appears but disappears immediately.  Expected: Softkeyboard should not disappear immediately. It should disappear when click return on the keyboard.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView: Softkeyboard appears on clicking any tableviewrow but immediately disappear
Description: """"This is regression. The issue does not exist on 3.0.2. But the textfield in tableviewrow is never editable on any build. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an application with code below and launch the application 2. Click on any row in the tableview Actual: Softkeyboard appears but disappears immediately. Expected: Softkeyboard should not disappear immediately. It should disappear when click return on the keyboard. """"",title+description
