TIMOB-13122,12,"""CLI: Android application launch on device fail with Error 3""","""""""Changing SDK build in tiapp.xml makes Android inactive as Deployment Target.  It only happens with builds I mentioned, what are consecutive.  Although Building app for the device returns Error, app is being installed though and it is possible to run it on device. See attached screen shots.    It is a *regression*, does not occur in 3.1.0.v20130318141656 SDK build    This issue was reproducible with the following test steps:  1. Create or import the project via Studio  2. Change sdk version inside tiapp.xml to the latest (in my case I used above noted builds)  Result: Android target remains checked but goes grey.  3. Attempt to build for Android device    Actual result:  Error type 3  Error: Activity class {com.<USER>kitchensink/com.<USER>kitchensink.KitchenSinkActivity} does not exist.  [INFO] :   Project built successfully in 38s 689ms    Device build does install and work despite the error.    Expected result:  Android target in Tiapp editor remains active.  Build for device completes with no error.    Note:Please refer to attachments from related issue TIMOB-13126""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Android application launch on device fail with Error 3
Description: """"Changing SDK build in tiapp.xml makes Android inactive as Deployment Target. It only happens with builds I mentioned, what are consecutive. Although Building app for the device returns Error, app is being installed though and it is possible to run it on device. See attached screen shots. It is a *regression*, does not occur in 3.1.0.v20130318141656 SDK build This issue was reproducible with the following test steps: 1. Create or import the project via Studio 2. Change sdk version inside tiapp.xml to the latest (in my case I used above noted builds) Result: Android target remains checked but goes grey. 3. Attempt to build for Android device Actual result: Error type 3 Error: Activity class {com.<USER>kitchensink/com.<USER>kitchensink.KitchenSinkActivity} does not exist. [INFO] :   Project built successfully in 38s 689ms Device build does install and work despite the error. Expected result: Android target in Tiapp editor remains active. Build for device completes with no error. Note:Please refer to attachments from related issue TIMOB-13126""""",title+description
TIMOB-13121,12,"""iOS: View click event fires twice when adding the listener in a callback from another event""","""""""h4. Description    First we have a view inside a table view row. When we add a click event listener to the view in the callback of another click event (from another UI component), clicking the view will cause the event to fire twice.    h4. Code to Reproduce    Please see the attached file.    h4. Steps to Reproduce    1. Run app  2. Click """"""""Approve"""""""" button once  3. Click on blue square once  4. See the console for the output of the click event firing twice    h4. Additional Notes    This issue did not occur in 2.1.4GA.    The event does not fire twice if we add the event listener outside of the callback for clicking the """"""""Approve"""""""" button.    The event does not fire twice if we do not add the extra view (the """"""""view"""""""" variable in the code) to the table row.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: View click event fires twice when adding the listener in a callback from another event
Description: """"h4. Description First we have a view inside a table view row. When we add a click event listener to the view in the callback of another click event (from another UI component), clicking the view will cause the event to fire twice. h4. Code to Reproduce Please see the attached file. h4. Steps to Reproduce 1. Run app 2. Click """"""""Approve"""""""" button once 3. Click on blue square once 4. See the console for the output of the click event firing twice h4. Additional Notes This issue did not occur in 2.1.4GA. The event does not fire twice if we add the event listener outside of the callback for clicking the """"""""Approve"""""""" button. The event does not fire twice if we do not add the extra view (the """"""""view"""""""" variable in the code) to the table row.""""",title+description
