TIMOB-12969,12,"""Crittercism module does not show any crash or handled exception in live stat section""","""""""I Tested the sample code provided with Crittercism module and found that live stats are not working for Crash and Handled Exception with Android 2.2 and above.  Also i get app load only for 1st time app launch with Titanium SDK version change. like when i change TiSDK from 3.0.0 to 3.0.2 or vice versa.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Crittercism module does not show any crash or handled exception in live stat section
Description: """"I Tested the sample code provided with Crittercism module and found that live stats are not working for Crash and Handled Exception with Android 2.2 and above. Also i get app load only for 1st time app launch with Titanium SDK version change. like when i change TiSDK from 3.0.0 to 3.0.2 or vice versa. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12968,12,"""Ti API: Create cross-platform notification manager API""","""""""Currently, Android notifications are created via Ti.Android and iOS notifications are created using Ti.App.iOS. We should investigate whether it's possible to implement a common, cross-platform notification API rather than force users to implement them separately for each platform.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Create cross-platform notification manager API
Description: """"Currently, Android notifications are created via Ti.Android and iOS notifications are created using Ti.App.iOS. We should investigate whether it's possible to implement a common, cross-platform notification API rather than force users to implement them separately for each platform. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12967,12,"""CodeProcessor: The """"results"""" message is sent before the results have been written to file""","""""""Right now, writing to files is asynchronous, and the code processor doesn't wait until they are finished before sending the """"""""results"""""""" message when sub processing""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: The """"results"""" message is sent before the results have been written to file
Description: """"Right now, writing to files is asynchronous, and the code processor doesn't wait until they are finished before sending the """"""""results"""""""" message when sub processing""""",title+description
TIMOB-12966,12,"""TiAPI: Define API for cross-platform maskedimage component""","""""""Currently, we have a MaskedImage control under Ti.UI, which is iOS-only and closely tied to the iOS API (for example, we support all 28 blend modes used by iOS).    Android supports 18 porter-duff transfer modes, plus two others.     If this is valuable, we should create a cross-platform alternative.    I suspect there is a popular set of use cases which is significantly smaller than the set that MaskedImage supports, which would make it easier to support the control across platforms.         """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Define API for cross-platform maskedimage component
Description: """"Currently, we have a MaskedImage control under Ti.UI, which is iOS-only and closely tied to the iOS API (for example, we support all 28 blend modes used by iOS). Android supports 18 porter-duff transfer modes, plus two others. If this is valuable, we should create a cross-platform alternative. I suspect there is a popular set of use cases which is significantly smaller than the set that MaskedImage supports, which would make it easier to support the control across platforms. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12965,12,"""Mobile Web: Animating FontWidget UI elements doesn't work""","""""""The animation engine assumes the DOM node that needs to be updated is always elem.domNode, but for UI elements derived from FontWidget, the animation engine needs to animate the DOM nodes in elem._styleableDomNodes.    Bug description: Ti.UI.Animation.color doesn't work    Reproduction steps:        Create label with green text      Create Animation object      Set Animation color to red and delay to 3 seconds      Call animate on label    Expected behavior: Label text should become red after 3 seconds    Actual behavior: Label text doesn't change color.    Note: test project is in the attachment    Code example:     """"""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web: Animating FontWidget UI elements doesn't work
Description: """"The animation engine assumes the DOM node that needs to be updated is always elem.domNode, but for UI elements derived from FontWidget, the animation engine needs to animate the DOM nodes in elem._styleableDomNodes. Bug description: Ti.UI.Animation.color doesn't work Reproduction steps: Create label with green text Create Animation object Set Animation color to red and delay to 3 seconds Call animate on label Expected behavior: Label text should become red after 3 seconds Actual behavior: Label text doesn't change color. Note: test project is in the attachment Code example: """"",title+description
TIMOB-12964,12,"""BlackBerry : Maps is not working with build 3.1.0.v20130305095817, the app just quits""","""""""Description:  1.Build & run the test app for maps given by russ on BB device/simulator    2.Observe the behaviour after app launches    Actual Result:  1. The app just quits after splash screen    Expected Result:  1. The app should launch & show the maps""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Maps is not working with build 3.1.0.v20130305095817, the app just quits
Description: """"Description: 1.Build & run the test app for maps given by russ on BB device/simulator 2.Observe the behaviour after app launches Actual Result: 1. The app just quits after splash screen Expected Result: 1. The app should launch & show the maps""""",title+description
TIMOB-12963,12,"""Tizen : Tizen developer website does not mention intel (HAXM) support for win 8""","""""""Description:  1.According to tizen developer website, there is no mention of intel(HAXM) support on win 8  2.Intel (HAXM) utility is used by the tizen emulator for virtulization purposes & is a necessary install step in setup  3.Also, there is no mention of this on our tizen preview page  4.We should add this to our preview page to make our users aware of this fact     More info can be found here: https://developer.tizen.org/downloads/sdk/installing-sdk/hardware-accelerated-execution-manager""""""",Bug,"Title: Tizen : Tizen developer website does not mention intel (HAXM) support for win 8
Description: """"Description: 1.According to tizen developer website, there is no mention of intel(HAXM) support on win 8 2.Intel (HAXM) utility is used by the tizen emulator for virtulization purposes & is a necessary install step in setup 3.Also, there is no mention of this on our tizen preview page 4.We should add this to our preview page to make our users aware of this fact More info can be found here: https://developer.tizen.org/downloads/sdk/installing-sdk/hardware-accelerated-execution-manager""""",title+description
