Description: """"rows will be undefined, expected result would be 0 rows""""",title+description
TIMOB-12939,12,"""Android: Developer option """"do not keep activities"""" cause Titanium apps to close""","""""""Expected behavior: App remains open and maintains focus after first activity is loaded regardless of Developer Options settings.    Current behavior: Activating the """"""""Don't keep activities"""""""" option in Developer Options on devices causes Titanium apps to close after the first activity is loaded.    This is a major difference between Titanium apps and native Android apps as this option may be checked unbeknownst to the client and thus seen as a bug in the app.  Seeing as though users are being instructed to turn this setting on to improve the performance of their devices this becomes a very large problem for those of us developing apps whose success hinges on user confidence.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Developer option """"do not keep activities"""" cause Titanium apps to close
Description: """"Expected behavior: App remains open and maintains focus after first activity is loaded regardless of Developer Options settings. Current behavior: Activating the """"""""Don't keep activities"""""""" option in Developer Options on devices causes Titanium apps to close after the first activity is loaded. This is a major difference between Titanium apps and native Android apps as this option may be checked unbeknownst to the client and thus seen as a bug in the app. Seeing as though users are being instructed to turn this setting on to improve the performance of their devices this becomes a very large problem for those of us developing apps whose success hinges on user confidence.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12938,12,"""Android: Google map v2 module, annotation image path inconsistent with standard""","""""""*Problem*  The file path format for annotation image is not consistent with the standard which should be: '/images/image.png'.  Rather in order to get the image the path currently needed to be provided is: 'images/image.png'        the imagePath is not taken if it is under any folder, doesn't matter it is under folder """"""""android"""""""" or not, ( I usually put android specific images under android,), but it works partially when I put the image directly under resource folder, so in a word,  'home.png' works  '/img/home.png' will not work,  if I don't have the leading slash in the path, having images under folder works, so the imagePath needs to be 'img/abc/home.png', then it can work. However, this is not consistent with current standard.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Google map v2 module, annotation image path inconsistent with standard
Description: """"*Problem* The file path format for annotation image is not consistent with the standard which should be: '/images/image.png'. Rather in order to get the image the path currently needed to be provided is: 'images/image.png' the imagePath is not taken if it is under any folder, doesn't matter it is under folder """"""""android"""""""" or not, ( I usually put android specific images under android,), but it works partially when I put the image directly under resource folder, so in a word, 'home.png' works '/img/home.png' will not work, if I don't have the leading slash in the path, having images under folder works, so the imagePath needs to be 'img/abc/home.png', then it can work. However, this is not consistent with current standard. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12937,12,"""CodeProcessor: Update READMEs""","""""""The current docs are horrendously outdated, and if you try to use them to figure out how to use the code processor, bad things happen. Since Studio et al is using these to add support, the need to be updated ASAP""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Update READMEs
Description: """"The current docs are horrendously outdated, and if you try to use them to figure out how to use the code processor, bad things happen. Since Studio et al is using these to add support, the need to be updated ASAP""""",title+description
TIMOB-12936,12,"""TiAPI: Implement multi-threading""","""""""Adding threading to the SDK would be incredibly awesome. It would also be incredibly difficult because the current implementations are VERY non-thread-safe. We should use web workers as a basis for implementation because a) It's the only threading model Mobile Web can support and b) many of the JS engines already have support for it.""""""",Epic,"Title: TiAPI: Implement multi-threading
Description: """"Adding threading to the SDK would be incredibly awesome. It would also be incredibly difficult because the current implementations are VERY non-thread-safe. We should use web workers as a basis for implementation because a) It's the only threading model Mobile Web can support and b) many of the JS engines already have support for it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12935,12,"""Custom Theme creation and overriding common.css in Mobile Web""","""""""I want ability create my own custom CSS theme rather than provided default, overriding common.css.   I don't want to apply to all project, only to specific project.   Customizing splash.css does not work because common.css override it.  For example, I want to have white as background but because common.css has 'black' for body, my application has annoying black background.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Custom Theme creation and overriding common.css in Mobile Web
Description: """"I want ability create my own custom CSS theme rather than provided default, overriding common.css. I don't want to apply to all project, only to specific project. Customizing splash.css does not work because common.css override it. For example, I want to have white as background but because common.css has 'black' for body, my application has annoying black background.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12934,12,"""MobileWeb CLI does not respect tiapp.xml Ti SDK""","""""""h3. Problem  The CLI does not respect the Titanium version on tiapp.xml. It uses the """"""""[active]"""""""" SDK instead.    h3. To reproduce:  Create a project and set a Titanium SDK different from the """"""""active"""""""". Save, clean, and run the following command in the terminal:  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb CLI does not respect tiapp.xml Ti SDK
Description: """"h3. Problem The CLI does not respect the Titanium version on tiapp.xml. It uses the """"""""[active]"""""""" SDK instead. h3. To reproduce: Create a project and set a Titanium SDK different from the """"""""active"""""""". Save, clean, and run the following command in the terminal: """"",title+description
TIMOB-12933,12,"""CLI: iOS debug builds unnecessarily force rebuild""","""""""Every time a debug build is performed, the port changes, thus the debugger.plist changes and forces a rebuild. This is the desired effect for device and packaged builds, but is unnecessary for simulator builds since we don't need to run Xcode and sign the app to run in the simulator.    To test:    1. Create a iOS project  2. Debug for iOS (will open simulator)  3. Change Studio console log level to """"""""trace""""""""  4. Debug again for iOS  5. Inspect console and see that there is no full rebuilds due to debugger.plist changing    Note: this ONLY affects simulator builds.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS debug builds unnecessarily force rebuild
Description: """"Every time a debug build is performed, the port changes, thus the debugger.plist changes and forces a rebuild. This is the desired effect for device and packaged builds, but is unnecessary for simulator builds since we don't need to run Xcode and sign the app to run in the simulator. To test: 1. Create a iOS project 2. Debug for iOS (will open simulator) 3. Change Studio console log level to """"""""trace"""""""" 4. Debug again for iOS 5. Inspect console and see that there is no full rebuilds due to debugger.plist changing Note: this ONLY affects simulator builds.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12932,12,"""BlackBerry: Window.title""","""""""Support setting a title on a window (both for tabs and standalone windows).    h3. Acceptance Test  h4. Standalone Window      1. Verify a window opens (blue background).  2. There should be a title at the top.    h4. Tab window      1. Verify the tab group opens with two tabs.  2. Verify each tab has a title (bottom) for each color.  3. Try selecting both tabs and verify title for window is displayed on top.  """"""",Sub-task,"Title: BlackBerry: Window.title
Description: """"Support setting a title on a window (both for tabs and standalone windows). h3. Acceptance Test h4. Standalone Window 1. Verify a window opens (blue background). 2. There should be a title at the top. h4. Tab window 1. Verify the tab group opens with two tabs. 2. Verify each tab has a title (bottom) for each color. 3. Try selecting both tabs and verify title for window is displayed on top. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12931,12,"""Android: View - App crashes if you click on a switch control at the end of a view that passes the phone's screen""","""""""*Details:* If you extend a view (that is a child of ScrollView) pass the phone's screen and click on a switch control at the end, then the app will crash and return a SIGSEGV in logcat.    *This bug is reproducible on 3.0.0.GA*    *Steps to Reproduce:*  1. Install attached sample app  2. Go to *basic vertical panning* or *basic horizontal panning*  3. Scroll vertically or horizontally (depending on which test) to the end of the view  3a. While scrolling to the end of the view, tap the view a couple of times  4. Press the switch control    *Actual:* App will crash and return SIGSEGV error in logcat (see attachments)  *Expected:* App should not crash if view is extended pass the phone's screen    *Note:*  1. This error seems to occur on initial install of the app. After a couple of hours, the issue does not reappear again.  2. Was not able to reproduce on the Nexus 4 (4.2.1)  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: View - App crashes if you click on a switch control at the end of a view that passes the phone's screen
Description: """"*Details:* If you extend a view (that is a child of ScrollView) pass the phone's screen and click on a switch control at the end, then the app will crash and return a SIGSEGV in logcat. *This bug is reproducible on 3.0.0.GA* *Steps to Reproduce:* 1. Install attached sample app 2. Go to *basic vertical panning* or *basic horizontal panning* 3. Scroll vertically or horizontally (depending on which test) to the end of the view 3a. While scrolling to the end of the view, tap the view a couple of times 4. Press the switch control *Actual:* App will crash and return SIGSEGV error in logcat (see attachments) *Expected:* App should not crash if view is extended pass the phone's screen *Note:* 1. This error seems to occur on initial install of the app. After a couple of hours, the issue does not reappear again. 2. Was not able to reproduce on the Nexus 4 (4.2.1) """"",title+description
TIMOB-12930,12,"""Android: Streamline V8 Kroll bridge""","""""""While related to other tasks, this one is meant to be quicker, and part of a larger change. There's a lot of times where we scan global methods to rediscover what we could already know through the call stack, such as env.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Streamline V8 Kroll bridge
Description: """"While related to other tasks, this one is meant to be quicker, and part of a larger change. There's a lot of times where we scan global methods to rediscover what we could already know through the call stack, such as env.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12928,12,"""CodeProcessor: Merge unknown-ambiguous-visualizer and unknown-callback-detector plugins""","""""""These two plugins perform very similar functions, and considering that unknown-callback-detector is so tiny, they should just be merged""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Merge unknown-ambiguous-visualizer and unknown-callback-detector plugins
Description: """"These two plugins perform very similar functions, and considering that unknown-callback-detector is so tiny, they should just be merged""""",title+description
TIMOB-12927,12,"""CodeProcessor: Rearchitect packet format for errors, warnings, and plugins""","""""""The current format for error, warnings, and some plugin entries is really messy. Some data goes in the root level and some goes in a """"""""data"""""""" sub-object. There used to be a clear delineation between what went where, but that is long gone. Also, subprocess error/warning messages don't have the same structure as errors do internally, but they should""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Rearchitect packet format for errors, warnings, and plugins
Description: """"The current format for error, warnings, and some plugin entries is really messy. Some data goes in the root level and some goes in a """"""""data"""""""" sub-object. There used to be a clear delineation between what went where, but that is long gone. Also, subprocess error/warning messages don't have the same structure as errors do internally, but they should""""",title+description
TIMOB-12926,12,"""Expose Android API - Content Provider""","""""""Expose of an Android specific API to allow other application access the sandbox storage of an app using Content Provider.    Reference docs  http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/providers/content-providers.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: Expose Android API - Content Provider
Description: """"Expose of an Android specific API to allow other application access the sandbox storage of an app using Content Provider. Reference docs http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/providers/content-providers.html""""",title+description
TIMOB-12925,12,"""Android: Support FLAG_SECURE window flag""","""""""Currently Titanium doesn't support the following:    *Native example*      From: http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/WindowManager.LayoutParams.html    {quote}Treat the content of the window as secure, preventing it from appearing in screenshots or from being viewed on non-secure displays.{quote}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support FLAG_SECURE window flag
Description: """"Currently Titanium doesn't support the following: *Native example* From: http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/WindowManager.LayoutParams.html {quote}Treat the content of the window as secure, preventing it from appearing in screenshots or from being viewed on non-secure displays.{quote}""""",title+description
TIMOB-12924,12,"""iOS: App becomes unresponsive in landscape mode""","""""""The attached sample application has login type, username and password fields. Tapping logintype will open another window. When the application is launched in landscape mode, the events are not fired to open the login type window. The password field is uneditable. If the device is tilted to portrait or if the app is launched in portrait all the events work fine.     This happens ONLY on the device and not on the sandbox using titanium studio.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App becomes unresponsive in landscape mode
Description: """"The attached sample application has login type, username and password fields. Tapping logintype will open another window. When the application is launched in landscape mode, the events are not fired to open the login type window. The password field is uneditable. If the device is tilted to portrait or if the app is launched in portrait all the events work fine. This happens ONLY on the device and not on the sandbox using titanium studio.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12923,12,"""iOS: Toolbar buttons have very large hitbox""","""""""*Problem*  When a toolbar has buttons in it separated by a flexible/fixed space, the buttons have very large hitboxes well outside of actual button itself    *Steps to Reproduce*  1. Open Kitchen Sink  2. Navigate to Controls > Toolbar > (Click middle of the two buttons in the bottom bar)  3. Controls > System Buttons > Button Group 2 > (Click between trash and reply in the bottom bar)    Notice in comparison to: Controls > System Buttons > Button Group 5  The bottom bar between the info buttons work as expected.  The add button in the topbar and back button also work as expected.    This bug causes end users some bad ui problems, as clicking anywhere in the toolbar, even when not on a button, will trigger some action in the app.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Toolbar buttons have very large hitbox
Description: """"*Problem* When a toolbar has buttons in it separated by a flexible/fixed space, the buttons have very large hitboxes well outside of actual button itself *Steps to Reproduce* 1. Open Kitchen Sink 2. Navigate to Controls > Toolbar > (Click middle of the two buttons in the bottom bar) 3. Controls > System Buttons > Button Group 2 > (Click between trash and reply in the bottom bar) Notice in comparison to: Controls > System Buttons > Button Group 5 The bottom bar between the info buttons work as expected. The add button in the topbar and back button also work as expected. This bug causes end users some bad ui problems, as clicking anywhere in the toolbar, even when not on a button, will trigger some action in the app.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12922,12,"""Tizen : The tizen 64 bit install manager looks for 64 bit java & fails if only 32 bit java installed on windows""","""""""Description:  1.Follow the setup instructions on : http://preview.<USER>com/studio/tizen/  2.Download the 64 bit version of install manager for windows 7 & 8 -- 64 bit  3.Launch the installer  4.Observe the error    Actual result:  1.You will get error like this:""""""""You must have either JRE or JDK in version 6 installed on your computer.""""""""  2.In reality it actually looks for 64 bit java  3.We do not force people who use our studio to download a 64 bit version of java   4.This might create complexities as users having 64 bit windows will download the 64 bit tizen installer & encounter this error.  5.Also,there is no way user can figure out if he requires a 64-bit version of java from the error message  6.Running a 32-bit installer works fine  """"""",Bug,"Title: Tizen : The tizen 64 bit install manager looks for 64 bit java & fails if only 32 bit java installed on windows
Description: """"Description: 1.Follow the setup instructions on : http://preview.<USER>com/studio/tizen/ 2.Download the 64 bit version of install manager for windows 7 & 8 -- 64 bit 3.Launch the installer 4.Observe the error Actual result: 1.You will get error like this:""""""""You must have either JRE or JDK in version 6 installed on your computer."""""""" 2.In reality it actually looks for 64 bit java 3.We do not force people who use our studio to download a 64 bit version of java 4.This might create complexities as users having 64 bit windows will download the 64 bit tizen installer & encounter this error. 5.Also,there is no way user can figure out if he requires a 64-bit version of java from the error message 6.Running a 32-bit installer works fine """"",title+description
TIMOB-12921,12,"""iOS: Fix debugger memory leak""","""""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_debugger/commit/2f4df8cafa183201dc843233bf3292f5cd2b5191#commitcomment-2720670""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Fix debugger memory leak
Description: """"https://github.com/<USER>titanium_debugger/commit/2f4df8cafa183201dc843233bf3292f5cd2b5191#commitcomment-2720670""""",title+description
TIMOB-12920,12,"""Android: setting textfield's autocapitalization property to boolean force-closes app""","""""""Expected result: app wouldn't crash or would throw a meaningful error    Actual result: app force-closes with Java dump that gives no indication of the nature of the problem. iOS runs without error.    ~~~  """"""""#tfield"""""""":{     top: 100,     borderStyle: Ti.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED,     autocapitalization: false  }  ~~~    To reproduce, unzip the attached file and drop it in place of a default Alloy project's app folder. Build for the Android emulator or device. App crashes on load.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: setting textfield's autocapitalization property to boolean force-closes app
Description: """"Expected result: app wouldn't crash or would throw a meaningful error Actual result: app force-closes with Java dump that gives no indication of the nature of the problem. iOS runs without error. ~~~ """"""""#tfield"""""""":{ top: 100, borderStyle: Ti.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED, autocapitalization: false } ~~~ To reproduce, unzip the attached file and drop it in place of a default Alloy project's app folder. Build for the Android emulator or device. App crashes on load. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12919,12,"""Android: Setting textfield's value to non-string crashes app""","""""""Programmatically setting the value of a text field to a non-string value crashes the app on Android. You get a force-close message and a Java dump that does not indicate the nature of the problem. Explicitly casting the value as a string before setting it eliminates the problem.    Expected results: non-string data types should be converted to strings internally, matching JavaScript's typical auto-casting behavior. This is what happens on iOS.    To reproduce, unzip the attached file. Drop its app folder into a new Alloy project. Build for the Android emulator or device. Click the button.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Setting textfield's value to non-string crashes app
Description: """"Programmatically setting the value of a text field to a non-string value crashes the app on Android. You get a force-close message and a Java dump that does not indicate the nature of the problem. Explicitly casting the value as a string before setting it eliminates the problem. Expected results: non-string data types should be converted to strings internally, matching JavaScript's typical auto-casting behavior. This is what happens on iOS. To reproduce, unzip the attached file. Drop its app folder into a new Alloy project. Build for the Android emulator or device. Click the button.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12918,12,"""Code Processor: Re-architect to be a collection of tools""","""""""There have been requests for a number of features in the code processor that are syntactic in nature, but the Code Processor can really only do semantic analysis. There have also been requests to do analysis on non-js files, such as analyzing images, etc. To accomplish this, we can change the code processor to be a suite of tools, one of which is dynamic analysis consisting of the existing code processor.""""""",Story,"Title: Code Processor: Re-architect to be a collection of tools
Description: """"There have been requests for a number of features in the code processor that are syntactic in nature, but the Code Processor can really only do semantic analysis. There have also been requests to do analysis on non-js files, such as analyzing images, etc. To accomplish this, we can change the code processor to be a suite of tools, one of which is dynamic analysis consisting of the existing code processor.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12917,12,"""Alloy: on iOS, manually deleting the Resources folder might prevent the app from recompiling and building""","""""""h6. Problem description  Manually deleting the Resources folder and performing the build for iOS, does not recompile and returns an error (looking for app.js)    h6. Steps  1. Create a project (either from Studio or from CLI)  2. Build/run (either from Studio or using 'ti build -p ios' from Terminal)  3. Go in the Resources folder and manually delete all his contents  4. Build again like in point 2    Result: the app is not recompiled and build fails returning error:      5. type 'alloy compile -config platform=ios' and build/run  Result: app is build/run as expected    6. Repeat point 3 (delete Resources contents). Build/run for Android.  Result: app is recompiled and then run correctly as expected""""""",Bug,"Title: Alloy: on iOS, manually deleting the Resources folder might prevent the app from recompiling and building
Description: """"h6. Problem description Manually deleting the Resources folder and performing the build for iOS, does not recompile and returns an error (looking for app.js) h6. Steps 1. Create a project (either from Studio or from CLI) 2. Build/run (either from Studio or using 'ti build -p ios' from Terminal) 3. Go in the Resources folder and manually delete all his contents 4. Build again like in point 2 Result: the app is not recompiled and build fails returning error: 5. type 'alloy compile -config platform=ios' and build/run Result: app is build/run as expected 6. Repeat point 3 (delete Resources contents). Build/run for Android. Result: app is recompiled and then run correctly as expected""""",title+description
TIMOB-12901,12,"""Android: Ti.FileSystemProxy interprets resourceDir as a File""","""""""While testing New iOS feature for parity with Android I noticed that resources """"""""Directory"""""""" is interpreted as a """"""""File"""""""" on Android.    Test steps:  1.Run the following code      Actual result:  Android - resourceDir isFile true  iOS - resourceDir isFile false    Expected:  resourceDir isFile false""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.FileSystemProxy interprets resourceDir as a File
Description: """"While testing New iOS feature for parity with Android I noticed that resources """"""""Directory"""""""" is interpreted as a """"""""File"""""""" on Android. Test steps: 1.Run the following code Actual result: Android - resourceDir isFile true iOS - resourceDir isFile false Expected: resourceDir isFile false""""",title+description
TIMOB-12900,12,"""Android: Image views in table views swap in and out when scrolling if className is set""","""""""h4. Description    When scrolling up and down in a table view with rows that contain image views, the images will swap in and out as we scroll if the className property is set on the row. If there is no className set, the images just blink.    h4. Code to Reproduce        h4. Steps to reproduce    1. Open app  2. Scroll up and down    Note that this happens regardless of whether or not the images are remote or local.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image views in table views swap in and out when scrolling if className is set
Description: """"h4. Description When scrolling up and down in a table view with rows that contain image views, the images will swap in and out as we scroll if the className property is set on the row. If there is no className set, the images just blink. h4. Code to Reproduce h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Open app 2. Scroll up and down Note that this happens regardless of whether or not the images are remote or local.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12899,12,"""Blackberry : Not able to run BlackBerry apps on device & simulator on win 8, giving errors""","""""""This might be related to BB sdk version or simulator version or user error, I am working to figure out what is causing the error & will comment accordingly    Description:  1.Launch the studio.  2.Create an app for Blackberry  3.Run on device    Actual Result:  1.We get the following error in the console for device:    3.For simulator:      Expected result:  1.Should be able to run app on both simulator & device""""""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry : Not able to run BlackBerry apps on device & simulator on win 8, giving errors
