TIMOB-12880,12,"""Android: ImageView parity on Android, not rendering the image as expected ""","""""""While testing image rendering from a URL using the following code with imageView properties set to width: Ti.UI.FILL and height: Ti.UI.SIZE, there is a parity on how the image is being rendered on Android.  Please see the attached screenshots for parity on Android vs iOS.  This is not a regression. Also occurs on 3.0.0.GA and 2.1.4.GA.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a Titanium app in the Studio  2. Copy the following code in the app.js  3. Build the app using SDK: 3.0.2.GA on an Android device       Actual result:  The <USER>logo is not being scaled correctly.    Expected result:  The <USER>logo should be scaled correctly.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView parity on Android, not rendering the image as expected
Description: """"While testing image rendering from a URL using the following code with imageView properties set to width: Ti.UI.FILL and height: Ti.UI.SIZE, there is a parity on how the image is being rendered on Android. Please see the attached screenshots for parity on Android vs iOS. This is not a regression. Also occurs on 3.0.0.GA and 2.1.4.GA. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a Titanium app in the Studio 2. Copy the following code in the app.js 3. Build the app using SDK: 3.0.2.GA on an Android device Actual result: The <USER>logo is not being scaled correctly. Expected result: The <USER>logo should be scaled correctly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12879,12,"""BlackBerry: Store Ti.App.Properties using application settings (QSettings).""","""""""Switch the backend storage for application properties to use settings (QSettings).  This simplifies things and maps better to the key/value API we provide.  It should also make life easier to support tiapp.xml properties.    h3. Acceptance Testing  1. Run KitchenSink and go to the properties test.  2. Verify in the logs that everything still passes.""""""",New Feature,"Title: BlackBerry: Store Ti.App.Properties using application settings (QSettings).
Description: """"Switch the backend storage for application properties to use settings (QSettings). This simplifies things and maps better to the key/value API we provide. It should also make life easier to support tiapp.xml properties. h3. Acceptance Testing 1. Run KitchenSink and go to the properties test. 2. Verify in the logs that everything still passes.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12878,12,"""Create AST visitor/transformer for """"view-aggregation""""""","""""""Adding multiple objects to a view hierarchy like this:    w.add(view1);  w.add(view2);  w.add(view3);    will be transformed to this:    w.add(view1,view2,view3);  """"""",Sub-task,"Title: Create AST visitor/transformer for """"view-aggregation""""
