TIMOB-12794,12,"""Android: Cannot run Debug on Android with both the Android emulator open and device connected""","""""""h6. Problem description  Issues running an App in Debug mode (either on device or on emulator) on Android, when the Android emulator is open and a device connected.    h6. Steps to reproduce  - Have an Android device connected and recognized  - Create a project in Studio and run in Debug mode on either the device or in the Android emulator (Studio allows to choose the target)    Result: App is being installed and it runs, but eventually remains stuck at the splashscreen.    Error log:      1. Remove the device and run in Debug mode on emulator  Result: App runs in Debug mode as expected  2. Close the emulator and connect an Android device. Run in Debug mode.  Result: App runs in Debug mode as expected""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Cannot run Debug on Android with both the Android emulator open and device connected
Description: """"h6. Problem description Issues running an App in Debug mode (either on device or on emulator) on Android, when the Android emulator is open and a device connected. h6. Steps to reproduce - Have an Android device connected and recognized - Create a project in Studio and run in Debug mode on either the device or in the Android emulator (Studio allows to choose the target) Result: App is being installed and it runs, but eventually remains stuck at the splashscreen. Error log: 1. Remove the device and run in Debug mode on emulator Result: App runs in Debug mode as expected 2. Close the emulator and connect an Android device. Run in Debug mode. Result: App runs in Debug mode as expected""""",title+description
