TIMOB-12735,12,"""CodeProcessor: Remove redundant errors and warnings""","""""""Normally when an exception is thrown, execution of JavaScript terminates, but because of the code processor's ability to recover from errors, the same error can be reported multiple times    Redundant errors and warnings should be collapsed into a single one, perhaps with a counter of how many times the error has occured""""""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Remove redundant errors and warnings
Description: """"Normally when an exception is thrown, execution of JavaScript terminates, but because of the code processor's ability to recover from errors, the same error can be reported multiple times Redundant errors and warnings should be collapsed into a single one, perhaps with a counter of how many times the error has occured""""",title+description
TIMOB-12734,12,"""Android: View.setLayout() does not change the view's layout property""","""""""I've added an event to a button to change the layout property of a view. Each tap will turn the layout of this view to horizontal -> vertical -> composite then come back at horizontal, etc...    In the iOS simulator everything works like expected, the children views are relocated as the layout of the parent changes. But it does not work in the Android simulator or Android device (HTC Sensation, Android 4.1) They stay at the same place.    (The purpose of this app, was a simple test to understand the layout property.)    Could this be a bug?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: View.setLayout() does not change the view's layout property
Description: """"I've added an event to a button to change the layout property of a view. Each tap will turn the layout of this view to horizontal -> vertical -> composite then come back at horizontal, etc... In the iOS simulator everything works like expected, the children views are relocated as the layout of the parent changes. But it does not work in the Android simulator or Android device (HTC Sensation, Android 4.1) They stay at the same place. (The purpose of this app, was a simple test to understand the layout property.) Could this be a bug?""""",title+description
TIMOB-12733,12,"""MapView always asks permission for users location even if userLocation is set to false""","""""""Create a default Alloy project, add a MapView and set userLocation to false (in the view, style or controller) and the app will still request permission for the users current location. """"""",Bug,"Title: MapView always asks permission for users location even if userLocation is set to false
