TIMOB-12722,12,"""CLI: Cannot build Alloy app from clean state""","""""""h6.Problem  Developer encounter """"""""No app.js found"""""""" when building alloy project from clean state using: *titanium build --platform iphone*    Clean state means, remove the build/ and Resources/ folders    h6.Environment      h6.Console output      The Work around to get past this they have to manually create Resources and the app.js    They've confirmed that the build <USER>works correctly/smoothly from clean condition when building after:  - titanium sdk select 3.0.1.v20130114133207    But demonstrates the problem above when  - titanium sdk select 3.0.2.v20130207164659      """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Cannot build Alloy app from clean state
Description: """"h6.Problem Developer encounter """"""""No app.js found"""""""" when building alloy project from clean state using: *titanium build --platform iphone* Clean state means, remove the build/ and Resources/ folders h6.Environment h6.Console output The Work around to get past this they have to manually create Resources and the app.js They've confirmed that the build <USER>works correctly/smoothly from clean condition when building after: - titanium sdk select 3.0.1.v20130114133207 But demonstrates the problem above when - titanium sdk select 3.0.2.v20130207164659 """"",title+description
TIMOB-12721,12,"""Improve the error message CLI returns when the specified sdk doesn't exist""","""""""Noticed this when debugging a customer issue where Titanium project creation from Studio was failing.    Run """"""""titanium create --sdk 3.0.0.GA"""""""" when 3.0.0.GA doesn't exist (or any string that isn't a valid version) produces the following output:        This is confusing, and it took us a bit to figure out which flag is causing the issue among all the ones we passed in. Instead, it would be more helpful if the error says the SDK version is not recognized.  """"""",Story,"Title: Improve the error message CLI returns when the specified sdk doesn't exist
Description: """"Noticed this when debugging a customer issue where Titanium project creation from Studio was failing. Run """"""""titanium create --sdk 3.0.0.GA"""""""" when 3.0.0.GA doesn't exist (or any string that isn't a valid version) produces the following output: This is confusing, and it took us a bit to figure out which flag is causing the issue among all the ones we passed in. Instead, it would be more helpful if the error says the SDK version is not recognized. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12720,12,"""Code Processor: should support building for multiple platforms at once""","""""""In Studio we would like to invoke code processor at project build time, e.g. when saving a file, but it requires code processor to support passing in multiple platforms and return the combined result since we are not running against a particular platform at that point.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Code Processor: should support building for multiple platforms at once
Description: """"In Studio we would like to invoke code processor at project build time, e.g. when saving a file, but it requires code processor to support passing in multiple platforms and return the combined result since we are not running against a particular platform at that point. """"",title+description
