TIMOB-12670,12,"""Android: Parity of enabled property ""","""""""Run the following code on device:      Results:    On Android, when clicking on the TextArea, the software keyboard appears and I can change the text.  I cannot reproduce this on the emulator.  This only happens on device.    On iOS and MobileWeb, the software keyboard does not appear and the contents are not editable.    Expected Results:  Software keyboard should not appears and the contents should not be editable.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Parity of enabled property
Description: """"Run the following code on device: Results: On Android, when clicking on the TextArea, the software keyboard appears and I can change the text. I cannot reproduce this on the emulator. This only happens on device. On iOS and MobileWeb, the software keyboard does not appear and the contents are not editable. Expected Results: Software keyboard should not appears and the contents should not be editable. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12669,12,"""MobileWeb: Parity of enabled property ""","""""""Test the following code with Chrome:      Results:    On Mobile Web, when enabled is set to false, click events fire for TextArea and TextField.  Switch, Slider and Button do not fire the click event.    On Android, no click events are fired and on iOS, the click events fire for Switch, Slider, TextArea and TextField.    Expected Results:  Click events should not fire if these elements are disabled.    """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Parity of enabled property
Description: """"Test the following code with Chrome: Results: On Mobile Web, when enabled is set to false, click events fire for TextArea and TextField. Switch, Slider and Button do not fire the click event. On Android, no click events are fired and on iOS, the click events fire for Switch, Slider, TextArea and TextField. Expected Results: Click events should not fire if these elements are disabled. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12668,12,"""iOS: Parity of enabled property ""","""""""Run the following code on the iOS simulator:      Results:    On iOS, when enabled is set to false, click events fire for Switch, Slider, TextArea and TextField.  Button does not fire the click event.    On Android, no click events are fired and on MobileWeb, the click events only fire for TextArea and TextField.    Expected Results:  Click events should not fire if these elements are disabled.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Parity of enabled property
Description: """"Run the following code on the iOS simulator: Results: On iOS, when enabled is set to false, click events fire for Switch, Slider, TextArea and TextField. Button does not fire the click event. On Android, no click events are fired and on MobileWeb, the click events only fire for TextArea and TextField. Expected Results: Click events should not fire if these elements are disabled. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12667,12,"""Mobile Web: Event Bubbling Regression""","""""""Event bubbling on 3.0.2/latest 3.1 is broken. In the 3.0GA, when event bubbles, event.source contains actual widget that generates the event. In the 3.0.2, event.source it points to the parent widget which makes it useless.    The attached project demonstrates the problem. A parent view is created which contains a single label. A click event listener is set up on the parent view. When you click the label, event bubbles to the parent view. In the 3.0GA, event.source point to the label which has been used to turn border to red. However, in the 3.0.2RC, it points to parent view. So there is no way to tell which object has actually fired the event.""""""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web: Event Bubbling Regression
Description: """"Event bubbling on 3.0.2/latest 3.1 is broken. In the 3.0GA, when event bubbles, event.source contains actual widget that generates the event. In the 3.0.2, event.source it points to the parent widget which makes it useless. The attached project demonstrates the problem. A parent view is created which contains a single label. A click event listener is set up on the parent view. When you click the label, event bubbles to the parent view. In the 3.0GA, event.source point to the label which has been used to turn border to red. However, in the 3.0.2RC, it points to parent view. So there is no way to tell which object has actually fired the event.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12666,12,"""CodeProcessor: Analysis coverage visits different platform nodes""","""""""When the code processor is run against iphone, then the analysis coverage plugin details that it visited nodes for resources defined under other platform folders as well (for ex: MasterDetail/Resources/ui/handheld/android/ or mobileweb).     Since those resources are specific to other platforms, I guess they should not be visited as part of code analysis. For example, the output of analysis-coverage plugin shows the visited nodes of android even when the code processor is run against iphone platform -  """"""""/Users/<USER>Documents/Titanium_Studio_Workspace_New/MasterDetail/Resources/ui/handheld/android/ApplicationWindow.js"""""""":{""""""""numNodesVisited"""""""":86,""""""""numNodesSkipped"""""""":0,""""""""numTotalNodes"""""""":89},  """"""",Bug,"Title: CodeProcessor: Analysis coverage visits different platform nodes
Description: """"When the code processor is run against iphone, then the analysis coverage plugin details that it visited nodes for resources defined under other platform folders as well (for ex: MasterDetail/Resources/ui/handheld/android/ or mobileweb). Since those resources are specific to other platforms, I guess they should not be visited as part of code analysis. For example, the output of analysis-coverage plugin shows the visited nodes of android even when the code processor is run against iphone platform - """"""""/Users/<USER>Documents/Titanium_Studio_Workspace_New/MasterDetail/Resources/ui/handheld/android/ApplicationWindow.js"""""""":{""""""""numNodesVisited"""""""":86,""""""""numNodesSkipped"""""""":0,""""""""numTotalNodes"""""""":89}, """"",title+description
TIMOB-12665,12,"""BlackBerry: Style property does not work on any controls""","""""""Description:  1.Create an app with any control with the style property (e.g. Titanium.UI.ActivityIndicatorStyle.DARK)  2.Run the app on BB simulator /device    Actual Result:  1.The app crashes    Expected Result:  1.The app should not crash & the control should display the appropriate style""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Style property does not work on any controls
Description: """"Description: 1.Create an app with any control with the style property (e.g. Titanium.UI.ActivityIndicatorStyle.DARK) 2.Run the app on BB simulator /device Actual Result: 1.The app crashes Expected Result: 1.The app should not crash & the control should display the appropriate style""""",title+description
TIMOB-12664,12,"""CLI: Mobile Web: Add support for TTF fonts and spaces in font name""","""""""Right now Mobile Web only support OTF and WOFF fonts. We need to also add support for TTF.    Look at mobileweb/cli/commands/_build.js around line 727.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Mobile Web: Add support for TTF fonts and spaces in font name
Description: """"Right now Mobile Web only support OTF and WOFF fonts. We need to also add support for TTF. Look at mobileweb/cli/commands/_build.js around line 727.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12663,12,"""Android: Facebook module won't work if there is a strings.xml in /platform/android/res/values/""","""""""If there is a strings.xml in the /platform/android/res/values/ folder, it will overwrite the one in the Facebook module, therefore the module can not find the resources and can not work correctly. Need to fix the build script to merge all the xml resources.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook module won't work if there is a strings.xml in /platform/android/res/values/
Description: """"If there is a strings.xml in the /platform/android/res/values/ folder, it will overwrite the one in the Facebook module, therefore the module can not find the resources and can not work correctly. Need to fix the build script to merge all the xml resources.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12662,12,"""Blackberry 10 & 10.1 Beta : The Blackberry 10 & 10.1 beta simulators take a long time to start on windows""","""""""Description:  1.Launch the Blackberry 10 & 10.1 Beta simulators on win 7 & win 8  2.Notice the total startup time    Actual Result:  1.The BB 10 & BB 10.1 beta simulators take a long time to start as compared to mac osx which is very quick    Expected Result:  1.The BB 10 & BB 10.1 simulators should startup quickly as in case of mac osx   """"""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry 10 & 10.1 Beta : The Blackberry 10 & 10.1 beta simulators take a long time to start on windows
Description: """"Description: 1.Launch the Blackberry 10 & 10.1 Beta simulators on win 7 & win 8 2.Notice the total startup time Actual Result: 1.The BB 10 & BB 10.1 beta simulators take a long time to start as compared to mac osx which is very quick Expected Result: 1.The BB 10 & BB 10.1 simulators should startup quickly as in case of mac osx """"",title+description
TIMOB-12660,12,"""Blackberry: Standardize error reporting in callbacks and events""","""""""All events conforming to an error protocol type have the following properties:  # success: boolean: True if the command was successful, otherwise false.  # code: integer: 0 if the command was successful, otherwise an internal value. If the OS does not provide one, this will be -1.  # error: optional string: undefined if the command was successful, otherwise a concatenation of the localized String and userinfo's message if it exists.    Sub, sub task of https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10376    Values derived from analysis at https://wiki.<USER>org/display/pe/Event+property+catalog    Take a look at changes made in https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-12610 for hints on what will need changing for consistency and parity.""""""",Story,"Title: Blackberry: Standardize error reporting in callbacks and events
Description: """"All events conforming to an error protocol type have the following properties: # success: boolean: True if the command was successful, otherwise false. # code: integer: 0 if the command was successful, otherwise an internal value. If the OS does not provide one, this will be -1. # error: optional string: undefined if the command was successful, otherwise a concatenation of the localized String and userinfo's message if it exists. Sub, sub task of https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10376 Values derived from analysis at https://wiki.<USER>org/display/pe/Event+property+catalog Take a look at changes made in https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-12610 for hints on what will need changing for consistency and parity.""""",title+description
