TIMOB-12652,12,"""iOS: Customized Default.png isn't taken into account when installing on physical device""","""""""There is a problem with Ti SDK 3.0.0.GA when we customize Default.png (/Resources/iphone) and install the app on device.  Default.png isnt taken into account during compilation.    First  1. I created an iPhone app   2. I compiled it in the simulator   3. I installed it on my iPhone through iTunes (normal <USER>  Everything seemed ok.    Then    1. I created custom Default.png (in Resources/iphone folder). I also customized (to be sure where the problem apply)  <EMAIL>  <EMAIL>  Default-Landscape.png  Default-Portrait.png  appicon.png    2. I compiled it in the simulator -> ok -> Default.png & so on are taken into account  3. I installed it on my iPhone through iTunes but Default.png is not taken into account. Default.png from Titanium is taken instead.    It is possible to check this in Project folder/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/ProjectName/ where Default.png from Titanium (instead of mine) can be seen.  Other Customized images (<EMAIL> etc) are present and ok.  The problem apply only to Default.png    Also    To be sure, i also:  1. created a new app   2. customized all images in /Resources/iphone before launching it in simulator  3. built app on simulator -> ok  4. built app to install on device and Default.png isnt taken into account""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Customized Default.png isn't taken into account when installing on physical device
Description: """"There is a problem with Ti SDK 3.0.0.GA when we customize Default.png (/Resources/iphone) and install the app on device. Default.png isnt taken into account during compilation. First 1. I created an iPhone app 2. I compiled it in the simulator 3. I installed it on my iPhone through iTunes (normal <USER> Everything seemed ok. Then 1. I created custom Default.png (in Resources/iphone folder). I also customized (to be sure where the problem apply) <EMAIL> <EMAIL> Default-Landscape.png Default-Portrait.png appicon.png 2. I compiled it in the simulator -> ok -> Default.png & so on are taken into account 3. I installed it on my iPhone through iTunes but Default.png is not taken into account. Default.png from Titanium is taken instead. It is possible to check this in Project folder/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/ProjectName/ where Default.png from Titanium (instead of mine) can be seen. Other Customized images (<EMAIL> etc) are present and ok. The problem apply only to Default.png Also To be sure, i also: 1. created a new app 2. customized all images in /Resources/iphone before launching it in simulator 3. built app on simulator -> ok 4. built app to install on device and Default.png isnt taken into account""""",title+description
TIMOB-12651,12,"""Android: Standardize error reporting in callbacks and events""","""""""All events conforming to an error protocol type have the following properties:  # success: boolean: True if the command was successful, otherwise false.  # code: integer: 0 if the command was successful, otherwise an internal value. If the OS does not provide one, this will be -1.  # error: optional string: undefined if the command was successful, otherwise a concatenation of the localized String and userinfo's message if it exists.    Sub, sub task of https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10376    Values derived from analysis at https://wiki.<USER>org/display/pe/Event+property+catalog    Take a look at changes made in https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-12610 for hints on what will need changing for consistency and parity.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Standardize error reporting in callbacks and events
Description: """"All events conforming to an error protocol type have the following properties: # success: boolean: True if the command was successful, otherwise false. # code: integer: 0 if the command was successful, otherwise an internal value. If the OS does not provide one, this will be -1. # error: optional string: undefined if the command was successful, otherwise a concatenation of the localized String and userinfo's message if it exists. Sub, sub task of https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10376 Values derived from analysis at https://wiki.<USER>org/display/pe/Event+property+catalog Take a look at changes made in https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-12610 for hints on what will need changing for consistency and parity.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12650,12,"""iOS: """"iOS Simulator failed to install the application""""""","""""""Works fine with Xcode 4.5.    Steps To Reproduce:  ======================  1. Create a default project.  2. Run project in iOS simulator    Actual:   ========  [ERROR] :  An error occurred running the iOS Simulator  [ERROR] :  [DEBUG] Session could not be started: Error Domain=DTiPhoneSimulatorErrorDomain Code=1 """"""""iOS Simulator failed to install the application."""""""" UserInfo=0x101a0f2a0 {NSLocalizedDescription=iOS Simulator failed to install the application., DTiPhoneSimulatorUnderlyingErrorCodeKey=-1}  [ERROR] :    [ERROR] :  Project failed to build after 21s 304ms    Expected:  ==========  Project must launch successfully in simulator.    Workaround:  ============  Deleting files from /Users/pragya.rastogi/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications resolves the issue temporarily.  'iOS Simulator > Reset Content and Settings...' works as well.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: """"iOS Simulator failed to install the application""""
Description: """"Works fine with Xcode 4.5. Steps To Reproduce: ====================== 1. Create a default project. 2. Run project in iOS simulator Actual: ======== [ERROR] : An error occurred running the iOS Simulator [ERROR] : [DEBUG] Session could not be started: Error Domain=DTiPhoneSimulatorErrorDomain Code=1 """"""""iOS Simulator failed to install the application."""""""" UserInfo=0x101a0f2a0 {NSLocalizedDescription=iOS Simulator failed to install the application., DTiPhoneSimulatorUnderlyingErrorCodeKey=-1} [ERROR] : [ERROR] : Project failed to build after 21s 304ms Expected: ========== Project must launch successfully in simulator. Workaround: ============ Deleting files from /Users/pragya.rastogi/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.1/Applications resolves the issue temporarily. 'iOS Simulator > Reset Content and Settings...' works as well. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12649,12,"""Android: Implement reusable cell/row template with data binding""",,Sub-task,Title: Android: Implement reusable cell/row template with data binding,title-only
TIMOB-12648,12,"""TiAPI: Create a """"global"""" variable""","""""""Sharing variables between modules is complex. The proper way is to use an intermediary to pass the values back and forth, but this is a lot of effort for something simple. Some platforms simply reuse the same context for all modules (this is undocumented), but that is a bad idea for both performance reasons and because it increases the chance of nasty bugs.    The proper way is to have some variable in the """"""""module"""""""" scope that allows access to the true global scope. There is plenty of precedence for this because browsers have the """"""""window"""""""" object and node.js has the """"""""global"""""""" object that references the """"""""true"""""""" global scope.    We should do something similar and provide a """"""""global"""""""" object.""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Create a """"global"""" variable
Description: """"Sharing variables between modules is complex. The proper way is to use an intermediary to pass the values back and forth, but this is a lot of effort for something simple. Some platforms simply reuse the same context for all modules (this is undocumented), but that is a bad idea for both performance reasons and because it increases the chance of nasty bugs. The proper way is to have some variable in the """"""""module"""""""" scope that allows access to the true global scope. There is plenty of precedence for this because browsers have the """"""""window"""""""" object and node.js has the """"""""global"""""""" object that references the """"""""true"""""""" global scope. We should do something similar and provide a """"""""global"""""""" object.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12647,12,"""iOS: iTunes Sync - """"Failed to initiate iTunes sync"""" message is returned even though your app is synced with iTunes""","""""""*Details:* If you run an app in simulator then install to an iOS device, Studio will return """"""""Failed to initiate iTunes sync"""""""" even though app is synced to iTunes.    *This is not a regression. This issue occurs in 3.0.0.GA*    *Steps to reproduce:*  1. Create default Titanium app  2. Run app in simulator  3. Next, install app to an iOS device    *Actual:* Studio will return """"""""Failed to initiate iTunes sync"""""""" message (see attachments)    *Expected:* Should not see error message because app is synced to iTunes.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iTunes Sync - """"Failed to initiate iTunes sync"""" message is returned even though your app is synced with iTunes
Description: """"*Details:* If you run an app in simulator then install to an iOS device, Studio will return """"""""Failed to initiate iTunes sync"""""""" even though app is synced to iTunes. *This is not a regression. This issue occurs in 3.0.0.GA* *Steps to reproduce:* 1. Create default Titanium app 2. Run app in simulator 3. Next, install app to an iOS device *Actual:* Studio will return """"""""Failed to initiate iTunes sync"""""""" message (see attachments) *Expected:* Should not see error message because app is synced to iTunes.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12645,12,"""CodeProcessor: SDK upgrade assistant""","""""""One of the biggest (the biggest?) pain point with Titanium is upgrading to a new SDK. Using other plugins such as the deprecated API detector and some new logic, we can create a tool that will attempt to automatically upgrade applications to a new SDK and warn when something can't be upgraded (similar to how the Visual Studio upgrade assistant works). This tool may be part of the code processor, or an external tool that uses the code processor""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: SDK upgrade assistant
Description: """"One of the biggest (the biggest?) pain point with Titanium is upgrading to a new SDK. Using other plugins such as the deprecated API detector and some new logic, we can create a tool that will attempt to automatically upgrade applications to a new SDK and warn when something can't be upgraded (similar to how the Visual Studio upgrade assistant works). This tool may be part of the code processor, or an external tool that uses the code processor""""",title+description
TIMOB-12644,12,"""CodeProcessor: Implement Memory Leak Detector plugin""","""""""Finding memory leaks is very difficult to do at the application level, but shouldn't be _too_ difficult to do at the JavaScript VM level and would provide immense value.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CodeProcessor: Implement Memory Leak Detector plugin
Description: """"Finding memory leaks is very difficult to do at the application level, but shouldn't be _too_ difficult to do at the JavaScript VM level and would provide immense value.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12643,12,"""iOS: TableView selectRow method is moving TableView to the middle""","""""""*Problem*    Method selectRow of Ti.UI.TableView centers the selected row to the middle of the screen.     *Test Code*      It happens because of selectRow method in iOS Class (TiUITableView.m at line 2051) the parameter *atScrollPosition* is {{UITableViewScrollPositionMiddle}}.    *Requested Change*    IMHO, what need to happens:    1) When TableViewRow isn't visible (100%) at the top, it needs to be scrolled to the top, using {{UITableViewScrollPositionTop}}.  2) When TableViewRow isn't visible (100%) at the bottom, it needs to be scrolled to the bottom, using {{UITableViewScrollPositionBottom}}.  3) When TableViewRow is complete visible, it doesn't needs to be scrolled to anywhere, using {{UITableViewScrollPositionNone}}.    *Or*    Allow developers to """"""""force"""""""" scrollPosition with a second parameter of *selectRow*, using constants like """"""""top"""""""", """"""""bottom"""""""", """"""""middle"""""""" or """"""""none"""""""".    *Note*    Tested selectRow on Android (4.1.1) and seems to be broken. Use the same test code above on Android OS and rows are not selected, rather when a row is clicked, the tableView just scrolls down.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: TableView selectRow method is moving TableView to the middle
Description: """"*Problem* Method selectRow of Ti.UI.TableView centers the selected row to the middle of the screen. *Test Code* It happens because of selectRow method in iOS Class (TiUITableView.m at line 2051) the parameter *atScrollPosition* is {{UITableViewScrollPositionMiddle}}. *Requested Change* IMHO, what need to happens: 1) When TableViewRow isn't visible (100%) at the top, it needs to be scrolled to the top, using {{UITableViewScrollPositionTop}}. 2) When TableViewRow isn't visible (100%) at the bottom, it needs to be scrolled to the bottom, using {{UITableViewScrollPositionBottom}}. 3) When TableViewRow is complete visible, it doesn't needs to be scrolled to anywhere, using {{UITableViewScrollPositionNone}}. *Or* Allow developers to """"""""force"""""""" scrollPosition with a second parameter of *selectRow*, using constants like """"""""top"""""""", """"""""bottom"""""""", """"""""middle"""""""" or """"""""none"""""""". *Note* Tested selectRow on Android (4.1.1) and seems to be broken. Use the same test code above on Android OS and rows are not selected, rather when a row is clicked, the tableView just scrolls down. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12642,12,"""CodeProcessor: Come up with profile of how to expose data""","""""""The code processor generates a lot of data. Some of it should be consumed directly, but some of it can be summarized, and some of it isn't necessary for end-users. We need to determine which is which.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Come up with profile of how to expose data
Description: """"The code processor generates a lot of data. Some of it should be consumed directly, but some of it can be summarized, and some of it isn't necessary for end-users. We need to determine which is which.""""",title+description
