TIMOB-12615,12,"""iOS: Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder is not getting Non US address to lat and long values""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When you pass a non us address to Ti.GeoLocation.forwardGeocoder(), it will fail returning null values.     h4. Test Case  Same location queried through out Maps GoogleAPIs returns coords according the place.         h4. Extra info  The customer just want to show a proper annotation in the map to a particular location. i.e., need latitude and longitude values for """"""""Ameerpet, Hyderabad""""""""         Right now a workaround will be changing from """"""""Ameerpet, Hyderabad"""""""" to """"""""Ameerpet-Hyderabad"""""""", that will return the right coordinates, except in cases where you send a full address, like: """"""""Shantipath, Chanakyapuri New Delhi, India"""""""", which is a valid address and will return empty.     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder is not getting Non US address to lat and long values
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When you pass a non us address to Ti.GeoLocation.forwardGeocoder(), it will fail returning null values. h4. Test Case Same location queried through out Maps GoogleAPIs returns coords according the place. h4. Extra info The customer just want to show a proper annotation in the map to a particular location. i.e., need latitude and longitude values for """"""""Ameerpet, Hyderabad"""""""" Right now a workaround will be changing from """"""""Ameerpet, Hyderabad"""""""" to """"""""Ameerpet-Hyderabad"""""""", that will return the right coordinates, except in cases where you send a full address, like: """"""""Shantipath, Chanakyapuri New Delhi, India"""""""", which is a valid address and will return empty. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12613,12,"""CLI: Second build of App fails to install on iOS device with code signing error""","""""""h6. Problem  Second build of App fails to install on iOS device with code signing error    h6. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new sample project and build for iOS device. Install on device (used Xcode organizer to add the app to the device)  2. Build again and install again on device (still used Xcode organizer)    Result: app fails to install – attached a screenshot of Xcode and LOG file    Works fine using 3.0.0. GA""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Second build of App fails to install on iOS device with code signing error
Description: """"h6. Problem Second build of App fails to install on iOS device with code signing error h6. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new sample project and build for iOS device. Install on device (used Xcode organizer to add the app to the device) 2. Build again and install again on device (still used Xcode organizer) Result: app fails to install – attached a screenshot of Xcode and LOG file Works fine using 3.0.0. GA""""",title+description
TIMOB-12612,12,"""BlackBerry 10 & 10.1 Beta : Difference in default text color & window color for apps in BB10 & BB10.1 Beta""","""""""Description:  1.Build & run KS or the todo app(from Russ) in BB 10 & BB 10.1 simulator  2.After the app launches open up any test case in KS    Actual Result:  1.The default text color is white in BB 10.1 Beta & black in BB 10  2.The default window color is white in BB 10 while its black in BB 10.1 Beta    Attached are the screenshots showing the difference  Also,no change to the code is made when ran on these two simulators.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry 10 & 10.1 Beta : Difference in default text color & window color for apps in BB10 & BB10.1 Beta
Description: """"Description: 1.Build & run KS or the todo app(from Russ) in BB 10 & BB 10.1 simulator 2.After the app launches open up any test case in KS Actual Result: 1.The default text color is white in BB 10.1 Beta & black in BB 10 2.The default window color is white in BB 10 while its black in BB 10.1 Beta Attached are the screenshots showing the difference Also,no change to the code is made when ran on these two simulators.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12611,12,"""BlackBerry 10.1 Beta: The text & tableviewrows in KS appear very faint (you can hardly see it)""","""""""Description:  1.Build & run the kitchensink (given by pedro & or josh) on BB 10.1 Beta  2.Notice the app after it launches    Actual Result:  1.The text & the tableviewrow appear very faint & you can hardly see tham  NOTE: Clicking on the table view rows opens the appropriate test    Expected Results:  1.The text & tableviewrow should be seen clearly    Screenshot attached.Not sure if the faint text would be visible in the screenshot  """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry 10.1 Beta: The text & tableviewrows in KS appear very faint (you can hardly see it)
Description: """"Description: 1.Build & run the kitchensink (given by pedro & or josh) on BB 10.1 Beta 2.Notice the app after it launches Actual Result: 1.The text & the tableviewrow appear very faint & you can hardly see tham NOTE: Clicking on the table view rows opens the appropriate test Expected Results: 1.The text & tableviewrow should be seen clearly Screenshot attached.Not sure if the faint text would be visible in the screenshot """"",title+description
TIMOB-12610,12,"""DOC: Standardize error reporting in callbacks and events""","""""""All events conforming to an error protocol type have the following properties:  # success: boolean: True if the command was successful, otherwise false.  # code: integer: 0 if the command was successful, otherwise an internal value. If the OS does not provide one, this will be -1.  # error: optional string: undefined if the command was successful, otherwise a concatenation of the localized String and userinfo's message if it exists.    Sub, sub task of https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10376    Values derived from analysis at https://wiki.<USER>org/display/pe/Event+property+catalog    First step is to list all the points where iOS changed behavior.""""""",Story,"Title: DOC: Standardize error reporting in callbacks and events
Description: """"All events conforming to an error protocol type have the following properties: # success: boolean: True if the command was successful, otherwise false. # code: integer: 0 if the command was successful, otherwise an internal value. If the OS does not provide one, this will be -1. # error: optional string: undefined if the command was successful, otherwise a concatenation of the localized String and userinfo's message if it exists. Sub, sub task of https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10376 Values derived from analysis at https://wiki.<USER>org/display/pe/Event+property+catalog First step is to list all the points where iOS changed behavior.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12609,12,"""BlackBerry : The BlackBerry simulators do not have any provision for screen orientation change ""","""""""I think it might not relate to our sdk but want to keep this in database for future reference.    The simulators for Blackberry have no provision to change orientation to landscape or portrait & vice versa.  So,as of now we can't test orientation change issues on simulators.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : The BlackBerry simulators do not have any provision for screen orientation change
Description: """"I think it might not relate to our sdk but want to keep this in database for future reference. The simulators for Blackberry have no provision to change orientation to landscape or portrait & vice versa. So,as of now we can't test orientation change issues on simulators.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12607,12,"""Android: Text field not displaying keyboard on focus on HTC device""","""""""h3. Issue    The keyboard does not show up after focusing on a textfield. This is happening on a specific device i.e HTC Explorer (Android 2.3.5) and only with 3.0.0.GA Titanium SDK.    Here is a screencast from the customer showing the issue: http://www.screencast.com/t/TcbZoTsa (This could take some time to load)    h3. Steps to Reproduce    1. Run the sample code: http://pastie.org/private/iuuxonkphngntjalhjt82g    2. Type in the first textbox. Notice on other devices, the other textfield gains focus without dismissing the keyboard but HTC Explorer dismisses the keyboard.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Text field not displaying keyboard on focus on HTC device
Description: """"h3. Issue The keyboard does not show up after focusing on a textfield. This is happening on a specific device i.e HTC Explorer (Android 2.3.5) and only with 3.0.0.GA Titanium SDK. Here is a screencast from the customer showing the issue: http://www.screencast.com/t/TcbZoTsa (This could take some time to load) h3. Steps to Reproduce 1. Run the sample code: http://pastie.org/private/iuuxonkphngntjalhjt82g 2. Type in the first textbox. Notice on other devices, the other textfield gains focus without dismissing the keyboard but HTC Explorer dismisses the keyboard.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12606,12,"""Ti.UI.DashboardView.setData() appends to dataset, it doesn't actually reset it""","""""""h2. problem    When calling Ti.UI.DashboardView.setData(), one would expect, like with Ti.UI.TableView, that the data given to the function call would reset the DashboardView. The problem is that instead of reseting it with the given array of DashboardItems, it instead appends the array to the existing list of data. This essentially leaves developers with no programmatic way to reset or remove items from the DashboardView. The remove() function operates on Views added to the Dashboard's view hierarchy, not its collection of items and will not work on DashboardItems.    This creates an issue with applications that contain a data model that describes the items. This existed originally in this Q&A question (unresolved): http://developer.<USER>com/question/92191/bug-in-dashboardview-when-adding-view-items    Additionally, this is a problem for Alloy when it comes to data binding. Developers in Alloy should be able to define their DashboardItems as a collection and use binding to control the appearance of the DashboardView. As of now this is not possible and will cause unexpected behavior.    h2. test case    # Create a new Titanium mobile project  # Run the following code for iOS (iphone sim is what I tested):    # Click a DashboardItem. It should set the badge to zero. It instead appends all the items again, having unexpected behavior with its re-rendering as well as with the resulting badge numbers.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.UI.DashboardView.setData() appends to dataset, it doesn't actually reset it
Description: """"h2. problem When calling Ti.UI.DashboardView.setData(), one would expect, like with Ti.UI.TableView, that the data given to the function call would reset the DashboardView. The problem is that instead of reseting it with the given array of DashboardItems, it instead appends the array to the existing list of data. This essentially leaves developers with no programmatic way to reset or remove items from the DashboardView. The remove() function operates on Views added to the Dashboard's view hierarchy, not its collection of items and will not work on DashboardItems. This creates an issue with applications that contain a data model that describes the items. This existed originally in this Q&A question (unresolved): http://developer.<USER>com/question/92191/bug-in-dashboardview-when-adding-view-items Additionally, this is a problem for Alloy when it comes to data binding. Developers in Alloy should be able to define their DashboardItems as a collection and use binding to control the appearance of the DashboardView. As of now this is not possible and will cause unexpected behavior. h2. test case # Create a new Titanium mobile project # Run the following code for iOS (iphone sim is what I tested): # Click a DashboardItem. It should set the badge to zero. It instead appends all the items again, having unexpected behavior with its re-rendering as well as with the resulting badge numbers.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12605,12,"""Android: No error comes, when guid is not present in tiapp.xml""","""""""Android: No error comes, when guid is not present in tiapp.xml  Its not a regression.    Tested on google nexus, android version: 4.1    Steps to reproduce:  1. Comment out guid in tiapp.xml in default titanium project.  2. Reach out to the project directory in terminal.  3. Run titanium build -T device    Actual:  No error comes and app installs on device.    Expected:  ERROR] :  tiapp.xml is missing the <guid> element  The guid must be in the format XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX and consist of letters and numbers.     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: No error comes, when guid is not present in tiapp.xml
Description: """"Android: No error comes, when guid is not present in tiapp.xml Its not a regression. Tested on google nexus, android version: 4.1 Steps to reproduce: 1. Comment out guid in tiapp.xml in default titanium project. 2. Reach out to the project directory in terminal. 3. Run titanium build -T device Actual: No error comes and app installs on device. Expected: ERROR] : tiapp.xml is missing the <guid> element The guid must be in the format XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX and consist of letters and numbers. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12603,12,"""IOS: Kitchensink - Picker is unable to focus on disabled option and keeps on flickering""","""""""Picker is unable to focus on disabled option and keeps on flickering.    This is not regression since the issue occurs in 3.0.0 GA as well.  This behaviour is observed in iPhone5 only and not in iPhone3GS.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch Kitchensink app.  2. Go to Controls > picker > Countdown picker.  3. In the picker, select 0hours 1 min.  4. press start.   5. Observe the picker.    Actual:  The picker constantly changes its value from 0 to 1 even if it's there only.    Expected:  No need to show this behavior.    """"""",Bug,"Title: IOS: Kitchensink - Picker is unable to focus on disabled option and keeps on flickering
Description: """"Picker is unable to focus on disabled option and keeps on flickering. This is not regression since the issue occurs in 3.0.0 GA as well. This behaviour is observed in iPhone5 only and not in iPhone3GS. Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchensink app. 2. Go to Controls > picker > Countdown picker. 3. In the picker, select 0hours 1 min. 4. press start. 5. Observe the picker. Actual: The picker constantly changes its value from 0 to 1 even if it's there only. Expected: No need to show this behavior. """"",title+description
