Description: """"-Expose errorName as well as splitting iOS stack traces into an array of strings""""",title+description
TIMOB-12599,12,"""Android: label.toImage().width does not return correct width when Ti.UI.SIZE is assigned""","""""""h2.Problem  Titanium documentation says that width property value of 'auto' has been deprecated and to use Ti.UI.SIZE.  However, setting label.width to Ti.UI.SIZE causes label.toImage().width to always return value of 100. Setting the label.width to 'auto' always returns the correct width.  This problem occurs on Android only and is not a problem on iOS so this is a parity issue.     h2.Testcase      Run enclosed app.js file on Android emulator. This app will display two  labels.  Label one will be created with width:'auto' and label two will be created with width:Ti.UI.SIZE.  The function .toImage() will be called to get the width of each label.  The results will be displayed in the console.          Expected Result     <----- The width of label one using property width:'auto' is 145 ----->    <----- The width of label two using property width:Ti.UI.Size is 145 ----->'      Actual Result       <----- The width of label one using property width:'auto' is 145 ----->    <----- The width of label two using property width:Ti.UI.Size is 100 ----->'    {panel:title=app.js}    {panel}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: label.toImage().width does not return correct width when Ti.UI.SIZE is assigned
Description: """"h2.Problem Titanium documentation says that width property value of 'auto' has been deprecated and to use Ti.UI.SIZE. However, setting label.width to Ti.UI.SIZE causes label.toImage().width to always return value of 100. Setting the label.width to 'auto' always returns the correct width. This problem occurs on Android only and is not a problem on iOS so this is a parity issue. h2.Testcase Run enclosed app.js file on Android emulator. This app will display two labels. Label one will be created with width:'auto' and label two will be created with width:Ti.UI.SIZE. The function .toImage() will be called to get the width of each label. The results will be displayed in the console. Expected Result <----- The width of label one using property width:'auto' is 145 -----> <----- The width of label two using property width:Ti.UI.Size is 145 ----->' Actual Result <----- The width of label one using property width:'auto' is 145 -----> <----- The width of label two using property width:Ti.UI.Size is 100 ----->' {panel:title=app.js} {panel}""""",title+description
TIMOB-12598,12,"""iOS: Reverse Geocoder returning invalid parameters for all latitudes & longitudes""","""""""h6.Issue  Recently several Developers are experiencing problems with it, on *both iOS & Android*.    ReverseGeocoder failed to get too common locations.     - [London|https://www.google.com.mx/search?num=100&hl=en&safe=off&client=firefox-a&hs=wpp&tbo=d&rls=org.mozilla%3Aen-GB%3Aofficial&q=london+lat+lon&oq=london+lat+lon&gs_l=serp.3..0l2j0i7i30j0i30l3j0i7i30l2j0i5i30l2.364190.364971.0.365291.6.6.0.0.0.1.202.659.4j1j1.6.0.les%3B..0.0...1c.1.2.serp.W80lmVkSzU4]       - [New York|https://www.google.com.mx/search?q=new+york+lat+lon&ie=utf-8&oe=utf-8&aq=t&rls=org.mozilla:en-GB:official&client=firefox-a]        h6.Tested on  iOS 6 simulator and iPhone device    h6.Runnable JS      h6.Output      h6.Community thread associated  http://developer.<USER>com/question/147885/reverse-geocoder-returning-invalid-parameters-for-all-latitudes--longitudes#comment-157532""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Reverse Geocoder returning invalid parameters for all latitudes & longitudes
Description: """"h6.Issue Recently several Developers are experiencing problems with it, on *both iOS & Android*. ReverseGeocoder failed to get too common locations. - [London|https://www.google.com.mx/search?num=100&hl=en&safe=off&client=firefox-a&hs=wpp&tbo=d&rls=org.mozilla%3Aen-GB%3Aofficial&q=london+lat+lon&oq=london+lat+lon&gs_l=serp.3..0l2j0i7i30j0i30l3j0i7i30l2j0i5i30l2.364190.364971.0.365291.6.6.0.0.0.1.202.659.4j1j1.6.0.les%3B..0.0...1c.1.2.serp.W80lmVkSzU4] - [New York|https://www.google.com.mx/search?q=new+york+lat+lon&ie=utf-8&oe=utf-8&aq=t&rls=org.mozilla:en-GB:official&client=firefox-a] h6.Tested on iOS 6 simulator and iPhone device h6.Runnable JS h6.Output h6.Community thread associated http://developer.<USER>com/question/147885/reverse-geocoder-returning-invalid-parameters-for-all-latitudes--longitudes#comment-157532""""",title+description
TIMOB-12597,12,"""BlackBerry 10.1 Beta : Appcelerator splash screen does not show up on app launch""","""""""Description:  1.Create the default app for BB in studio  2.Build & run on BB 10.1 beta simulator    Actual Result:  1.We do not see any <USER>splash screen    Expected Result:  1.We should see the <USER>splash screen""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry 10.1 Beta : Appcelerator splash screen does not show up on app launch
Description: """"Description: 1.Create the default app for BB in studio 2.Build & run on BB 10.1 beta simulator Actual Result: 1.We do not see any <USER>splash screen Expected Result: 1.We should see the <USER>splash screen""""",title+description
TIMOB-12596,12,"""Android: Cookie store should be shared between clients""","""""""  """"""""On Android in development mode the cookie store appears to be shared across instances of XHR clients, whereas in production mode it does not. clearCookies in Android works on the cookie store of a client instance.""""""""    A shared cookie store was actually implemented just before the V8 merge, and apparently part of it got clobbered in the merge. See original PR:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/474    In particular, it appears this line went missing:    +      client.setCookieStore(TiCookieStore.getInstance());    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cookie store should be shared between clients
Description: """" """"""""On Android in development mode the cookie store appears to be shared across instances of XHR clients, whereas in production mode it does not. clearCookies in Android works on the cookie store of a client instance."""""""" A shared cookie store was actually implemented just before the V8 merge, and apparently part of it got clobbered in the merge. See original PR: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/474 In particular, it appears this line went missing: + client.setCookieStore(TiCookieStore.getInstance()); """"",title+description
TIMOB-12594,12,"""Ti API: Change all node.js projects to include the changelog in the package.json file""","""""""Right now, getting the changelog for one of our node.js projects (cli, alloy, code processor, etc) is difficult because you have to first download that version of the project. If we put the changelog in the package.json file, this can be fetched via 'npm info <project>' without downloading the entire project.    This should probably be put in a """"""""changelog"""""""" field and, for readabilities sake, should probably go at the end.    The format will be Markdown""""""",Story,"Title: Ti API: Change all node.js projects to include the changelog in the package.json file
Description: """"Right now, getting the changelog for one of our node.js projects (cli, alloy, code processor, etc) is difficult because you have to first download that version of the project. If we put the changelog in the package.json file, this can be fetched via 'npm info <project>' without downloading the entire project. This should probably be put in a """"""""changelog"""""""" field and, for readabilities sake, should probably go at the end. The format will be Markdown""""",title+description
TIMOB-12593,12,"""iOS: Caps not working for View/ImageView""","""""""h3. Issue    Using backgroundLeftCaps and backgroundTopCaps on views/imageviews does not have the same effect as the button. The image in imageview/view interpolates/blends the stretched region unlike a button image.    h3. Steps to Reproduce    1. Run the sample code here:    http://pastie.org/private/h9rbm8ky381wvtob04ghww     Copy the attached image """"""""testimage.png"""""""" to Resources folder.    2. Notice the output in the screenshot attached.     The button version at the top is correct, it only shows the pixels we want and it does not do any interpolation. However the view and imageview with the same """"""""caps"""""""" data, blends/interpolates the stretched region.     h3. Expected Output    The imageview/view should look the same as a button.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Caps not working for View/ImageView
Description: """"h3. Issue Using backgroundLeftCaps and backgroundTopCaps on views/imageviews does not have the same effect as the button. The image in imageview/view interpolates/blends the stretched region unlike a button image. h3. Steps to Reproduce 1. Run the sample code here: http://pastie.org/private/h9rbm8ky381wvtob04ghww Copy the attached image """"""""testimage.png"""""""" to Resources folder. 2. Notice the output in the screenshot attached. The button version at the top is correct, it only shows the pixels we want and it does not do any interpolation. However the view and imageview with the same """"""""caps"""""""" data, blends/interpolates the stretched region. h3. Expected Output The imageview/view should look the same as a button.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12592,12,"""Change Ti.UI.DashboardView to Ti.UI.iOS.DashboardView""","""""""The Titanium APIs Ti.UI.DashboardView and Ti.UI.DashboardItem only work on iOS, so should likely be in a more appropriate namespace. They should probably be moved to Ti.UI.iOS.DashboardView and Ti.UI.iOS.DashboardItem.""""""",Story,"Title: Change Ti.UI.DashboardView to Ti.UI.iOS.DashboardView
Description: """"The Titanium APIs Ti.UI.DashboardView and Ti.UI.DashboardItem only work on iOS, so should likely be in a more appropriate namespace. They should probably be moved to Ti.UI.iOS.DashboardView and Ti.UI.iOS.DashboardItem.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12591,12,"""Titanium Studio does not copy contents of /platform/android/assets folder to /build/android/bin/assets folder""","""""""when any file is added to /platform/android/assets folder that file is not accessed by an SDK consumed by titanium module as it accesses file from the assets folder.    As analyzed any file which is present in /platform/android/assets folder is not copied by builder.py to /build/android/bin/assets folder. As a result this file is not picked by SDK consumed by titanium module.    I tried modifying builder.py to fix the issue and it worked in all cases but not when /build/android/bin/assets is not created for the first time.    I am attaching modified builder.py file for your reference and you can check the code added by searching comments having text """"""""Perminder""""""""    I am using Titanium SDK 2.1.2GA    Please provide a quick resolution to this issue as this can halt a delivery. """"""",Bug,"Title: Titanium Studio does not copy contents of /platform/android/assets folder to /build/android/bin/assets folder
Description: """"when any file is added to /platform/android/assets folder that file is not accessed by an SDK consumed by titanium module as it accesses file from the assets folder. As analyzed any file which is present in /platform/android/assets folder is not copied by builder.py to /build/android/bin/assets folder. As a result this file is not picked by SDK consumed by titanium module. I tried modifying builder.py to fix the issue and it worked in all cases but not when /build/android/bin/assets is not created for the first time. I am attaching modified builder.py file for your reference and you can check the code added by searching comments having text """"""""Perminder"""""""" I am using Titanium SDK 2.1.2GA Please provide a quick resolution to this issue as this can halt a delivery. """"",title+description
