TIMOB-12578,12,"""Add current region property to MapView""","""""""h1. Feature description  The MapView object does not have a property to tell the current region shown; the only way to get the bounds is by listening to the regionchanged event. The region property (or an additional one) should be kept up-to-date so that it is possible to read this information outside the listener.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Add current region property to MapView
Description: """"h1. Feature description The MapView object does not have a property to tell the current region shown; the only way to get the bounds is by listening to the regionchanged event. The region property (or an additional one) should be kept up-to-date so that it is possible to read this information outside the listener.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12577,12,"""[android] horizontal layout doesnt compute correctly""","""""""When using a horizontal layout with a view where the width is Ti.UI.FILL, you expect that view to take as much width as possible without expanding outside its parent.  Running the example below, you can see that it works correctly on ios (click the label for info)  On android, the label will actually have the width of its parent, and not the expected width    i did not test but i assume the problem is the same with vertical layout  """"""",Bug,"Title: [android] horizontal layout doesnt compute correctly
Description: """"When using a horizontal layout with a view where the width is Ti.UI.FILL, you expect that view to take as much width as possible without expanding outside its parent. Running the example below, you can see that it works correctly on ios (click the label for info) On android, the label will actually have the width of its parent, and not the expected width i did not test but i assume the problem is the same with vertical layout """"",title+description
TIMOB-12576,12,"""iOS: Background mode """"audio"""" does not work with SDK 3.0.0.GA""","""""""*Problem description*  iOS Background Mode """"""""audio"""""""" is not correctly converted to the Info.plist file with SDK 3.0.0.GA.    *tiapp.xml*      *Workaround*  1. Set for Ti.SDK 3.0.0  2. Compile the app to go on the device  3. DO NOT TRANSFER it  4. In the folder {appfolder}/build/iphone find the file info.plist  5. Copy this file into {appfolder}/  6. Edit this file; and add the key above (exactly as it is shown)  7. Compile again for the device  8. Put it on the device now  9. Test it - should work.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Background mode """"audio"""" does not work with SDK 3.0.0.GA
Description: """"*Problem description* iOS Background Mode """"""""audio"""""""" is not correctly converted to the Info.plist file with SDK 3.0.0.GA. *tiapp.xml* *Workaround* 1. Set for Ti.SDK 3.0.0 2. Compile the app to go on the device 3. DO NOT TRANSFER it 4. In the folder {appfolder}/build/iphone find the file info.plist 5. Copy this file into {appfolder}/ 6. Edit this file; and add the key above (exactly as it is shown) 7. Compile again for the device 8. Put it on the device now 9. Test it - should work.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12574,12,"""iOS: Failed to download  specific images for iPad 3 and 4 (Retina)""","""""""Although specific suffixes used as default in images' names for iPad and iPhone, it seems to be not always picking up the right file during packaging or deployment on device.    Not a regression, occurs in 3.0.0.GA  Test steps:  1. Create default project.  2. Replace app.js with the following code    3. unzip the attachment and add images in to Resources>iphone folder  4. Build the project on device and run it   5. Run in Simulator(Retina)  6. Package, install .ipa file to device and run it    Actual result:  4. An image of the car(wrong)  5. An image of the Universe(right)  6. An image of the car(wrong)      Expected result:  An image of the Universe should be used (background@2x~ipad.png)  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Failed to download specific images for iPad 3 and 4 (Retina)
Description: """"Although specific suffixes used as default in images' names for iPad and iPhone, it seems to be not always picking up the right file during packaging or deployment on device. Not a regression, occurs in 3.0.0.GA Test steps: 1. Create default project. 2. Replace app.js with the following code 3. unzip the attachment and add images in to Resources>iphone folder 4. Build the project on device and run it 5. Run in Simulator(Retina) 6. Package, install .ipa file to device and run it Actual result: 4. An image of the car(wrong) 5. An image of the Universe(right) 6. An image of the car(wrong) Expected result: An image of the Universe should be used (background@2x~ipad.png) """"",title+description
