Description: """"h3. Problem: Currently all the controls that we see in the screen, tested with KS, look tiny and cut off. Also, dimensions are not working, dp, dip, etc.. h3. Test code: h3. Expected You should see a button, normal size, in the window h3. Current result: The button is tiny and cut off""""",title+description
TIMOB-12554,12,"""BlackBerry : Not able to run apps on BlackBerry device on win 8, gives network is unreachable error. ""","""""""Not sure if its a platform bug or win 8 bug, but keeping it so that we have it in our database    Description:  1.Connect the BB 10 device to the win 8 machine using a usb cable  2.Make sure you install the blackberry device manager  3.Run an app on device using titanium studio    Actual rssult:  1.It fails to run & gives network is unreachable error    Normally if you install the blackberry device manager it installs the necessary drivers which detects the device.Also,we can only put apps on device if we have this manager installed     The same steps on win 7 & mac osx 10.8.2 does not have any issues    Expected Results:  1.We should be able to run the app successfully""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry : Not able to run apps on BlackBerry device on win 8, gives network is unreachable error.
Description: """"Not sure if its a platform bug or win 8 bug, but keeping it so that we have it in our database Description: 1.Connect the BB 10 device to the win 8 machine using a usb cable 2.Make sure you install the blackberry device manager 3.Run an app on device using titanium studio Actual rssult: 1.It fails to run & gives network is unreachable error Normally if you install the blackberry device manager it installs the necessary drivers which detects the device.Also,we can only put apps on device if we have this manager installed The same steps on win 7 & mac osx 10.8.2 does not have any issues Expected Results: 1.We should be able to run the app successfully""""",title+description
TIMOB-12553,12,"""TiAPI: Implement """"apiName"""" property on proxies""","""""""Currently there is no way to inspect an object's type reliably. typeof just returns """"""""object"""""""" and toString() is notoriously unreliable, and parsing toString is considered a big no-no (similar to parsing user agents).    Alloy needs this information to implement dynamic styles.""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Implement """"apiName"""" property on proxies
Description: """"Currently there is no way to inspect an object's type reliably. typeof just returns """"""""object"""""""" and toString() is notoriously unreliable, and parsing toString is considered a big no-no (similar to parsing user agents). Alloy needs this information to implement dynamic styles.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12552,12,"""Android: KrollException enhancements""","""""""Add a couple enhancements to KrollException:  1. Expose error name  2. Format to array of strings.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: KrollException enhancements
