TIMOB-12531,12,"""iOS: Animation - Image changes size during continuous rotation""","""""""Description:  Starting animation and rotating device result in upper image stretching on each rotation. The upper image returns it's original size after animation finished (in about 2-3 seconds)    It is not a regression, occurs in 3.0.0.GA    Test steps:  1. KitchenSink> Base UI> Animation> 2D Transform  2. Click Animate and start rotating the device    Actual:  An upper image changes size and resizes back in 2-3 seconds after animation completed.  Expected:  Images should be the same size""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Animation - Image changes size during continuous rotation
Description: """"Description: Starting animation and rotating device result in upper image stretching on each rotation. The upper image returns it's original size after animation finished (in about 2-3 seconds) It is not a regression, occurs in 3.0.0.GA Test steps: 1. KitchenSink> Base UI> Animation> 2D Transform 2. Click Animate and start rotating the device Actual: An upper image changes size and resizes back in 2-3 seconds after animation completed. Expected: Images should be the same size""""",title+description
