TIMOB-12522,12,"""BlackBerry: Layout Auto Sizing Behavior""","""""""Currently our layout does not support auto sizing of all views.  Views will either """"""""size"""""""" or """"""""fill"""""""" by default if height and/or width  is not specified. Currently if neither of these is provided, no value  is computed causing the view to not be rendered.    See [UI Composite Layout, Auto Size Classification|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/UI_Composite_Layout_Behavior_Spec-section-4196675_UICompositeLayoutBehaviorSpec-Viewautosizeclassification] for details on how views should auto size.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Layout Auto Sizing Behavior
Description: """"Currently our layout does not support auto sizing of all views. Views will either """"""""size"""""""" or """"""""fill"""""""" by default if height and/or width is not specified. Currently if neither of these is provided, no value is computed causing the view to not be rendered. See [UI Composite Layout, Auto Size Classification|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/guide/UI_Composite_Layout_Behavior_Spec-section-4196675_UICompositeLayoutBehaviorSpec-Viewautosizeclassification] for details on how views should auto size.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12520,12,"""IOS: Visual Glitch on TableView after Search with hideOnSearch set to true.""","""""""Minor Visual Glitch that corrects itself as soon as user scrolls the tableView  Steps to reproduce:    1. Go to KS->Base UI->Views->Table Views->Headers with Filter  2. Focus Search Bar and type 'Cam'. Search result will show <USER> 3. Hide the keyboard by clicking Search button in KB  4. Click the search result  5. Observe that the Section Header for the first section (A) is rendered incorrectly""""""",Bug,"Title: IOS: Visual Glitch on TableView after Search with hideOnSearch set to true.
Description: """"Minor Visual Glitch that corrects itself as soon as user scrolls the tableView Steps to reproduce: 1. Go to KS->Base UI->Views->Table Views->Headers with Filter 2. Focus Search Bar and type 'Cam'. Search result will show <USER> 3. Hide the keyboard by clicking Search button in KB 4. Click the search result 5. Observe that the Section Header for the first section (A) is rendered incorrectly""""",title+description
