TIMOB-12459,12,"""Android: optionsMenu items are incorrectly placed""","""""""h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Create a project in Studio using the tabbed application wizard, target SDK 3.0  2. Change tiapp.xml to target Android SDK 11 or higher, tool-api level 15 or higher  3. Titanium will replace old-style tabs with actionbar  4. Add an options menu to the root ApplicationWindow.js:        h6.Result  The options icons is correctly placed in the bar, but selecting it results in the menu option label being offset too far to the right  Tested on a Nexus 4, Jellybean 4.2.1    If I set the target SDK to lower than 11 and run the app again on the device, the old-style tabs return and the options menu is now located in the lower navigation bar, and works as expected.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: optionsMenu items are incorrectly placed
Description: """"h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Create a project in Studio using the tabbed application wizard, target SDK 3.0 2. Change tiapp.xml to target Android SDK 11 or higher, tool-api level 15 or higher 3. Titanium will replace old-style tabs with actionbar 4. Add an options menu to the root ApplicationWindow.js: h6.Result The options icons is correctly placed in the bar, but selecting it results in the menu option label being offset too far to the right Tested on a Nexus 4, Jellybean 4.2.1 If I set the target SDK to lower than 11 and run the app again on the device, the old-style tabs return and the options menu is now located in the lower navigation bar, and works as expected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12458,12,"""Add BlackBerry to CI Server""","""""""Setup the CI machine with the BB10 NDK detailed instructions at https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry#how-to-get-started-with-titanium-blackberry-development    Run nightly after the CI builds has happened:  # Change directory /tmp execute """"""""git <USER>--recursive https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry"""""""".  # To create the the blackberry drop-in, from the bb cloned repo change directory to cli/commands and then execute """"""""./create_sdk"""""""" this will create a build folder with the blackberry sdk folder in it (see 4 below).  # Grab from the repo  build/sdk/ the blackberry folder and copy it to the latest CI sdk build put it at the same level as android, iphone, mobile web. The folder should go in OSX, Linux, Windows""""""",Story,"Title: Add BlackBerry to CI Server
Description: """"Setup the CI machine with the BB10 NDK detailed instructions at https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry#how-to-get-started-with-titanium-blackberry-development Run nightly after the CI builds has happened: # Change directory /tmp execute """"""""git <USER>--recursive https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile_blackberry"""""""". # To create the the blackberry drop-in, from the bb cloned repo change directory to cli/commands and then execute """"""""./create_sdk"""""""" this will create a build folder with the blackberry sdk folder in it (see 4 below). # Grab from the repo build/sdk/ the blackberry folder and copy it to the latest CI sdk build put it at the same level as android, iphone, mobile web. The folder should go in OSX, Linux, Windows""""",title+description
