TIMOB-12447,12,"""Android: Cannot convert BLOB image to string using SQL""","""""""h1. Problem description    Reading blob from an SQL database (tested with mbtiles sqlite file) results in the following error:        The database """"""""mbtiles"""""""" can be any sqlite mbtiles database. Many samples are available on the Internet.    http://mapbox.com/developers/mbtiles/    h1. Steps to reproduce    Use this code to reproduce the bug:        h1. Note    There is a workaround of converting the BLOB images to base64 outside of Titanium before installing the database. Mbtiles sqlite files are used for offline mapping capabilities. The mbtiles specification requires that the images be stored in a BLOB field.    This is a possible regression of an earlier bug.  https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-741""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot convert BLOB image to string using SQL
Description: """"h1. Problem description Reading blob from an SQL database (tested with mbtiles sqlite file) results in the following error: The database """"""""mbtiles"""""""" can be any sqlite mbtiles database. Many samples are available on the Internet. http://mapbox.com/developers/mbtiles/ h1. Steps to reproduce Use this code to reproduce the bug: h1. Note There is a workaround of converting the BLOB images to base64 outside of Titanium before installing the database. Mbtiles sqlite files are used for offline mapping capabilities. The mbtiles specification requires that the images be stored in a BLOB field. This is a possible regression of an earlier bug. https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-741""""",title+description
TIMOB-12446,12,"""Android: Distribution fails with false syntax errors""","""""""h1. Problem Description    When distributing to app store (google play), compilation fails with several false syntax errors.    the project runs without errors on normal emulator/install to device runs    Attached: The console output from the build, and the file 'm.js' that triggers the errors    Here is some sample errors:        It's a straight forward function declaration that looks like this:        There are other types. All of them are marked as syntax errors, none of them really are    This prevents me from publishing, and that's very serious - so I marked this ticket 'critical'    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Distribution fails with false syntax errors
Description: """"h1. Problem Description When distributing to app store (google play), compilation fails with several false syntax errors. the project runs without errors on normal emulator/install to device runs Attached: The console output from the build, and the file 'm.js' that triggers the errors Here is some sample errors: It's a straight forward function declaration that looks like this: There are other types. All of them are marked as syntax errors, none of them really are This prevents me from publishing, and that's very serious - so I marked this ticket 'critical' """"",title+description
TIMOB-12445,12,"""CodeProcessor: Add config file support to the analyze sub-command""","""""""The subprocess subcommand currently accepts a config file as an argument. Compared to the CLI interface, the config file provides more options and is faster as well. We should add support for this from the CLI, but since the CLI can specify options as well, we need to merge the CLI argument with the config file.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CodeProcessor: Add config file support to the analyze sub-command
Description: """"The subprocess subcommand currently accepts a config file as an argument. Compared to the CLI interface, the config file provides more options and is faster as well. We should add support for this from the CLI, but since the CLI can specify options as well, we need to merge the CLI argument with the config file.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12444,12,"""CodeProcessor: Add support for an 'exit' message in subprocess mode""","""""""It would be really useful if studio could send the code processor a message telling it to quit but still return all results collected to date. We can do this via an 'exit' message""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Add support for an 'exit' message in subprocess mode
Description: """"It would be really useful if studio could send the code processor a message telling it to quit but still return all results collected to date. We can do this via an 'exit' message""""",title+description
TIMOB-12443,12,"""Android: focusable does not prevent focusing while using trackball""","""""""h6.Issue  While using the trackball within a tableview each row is selected although the focusable property is (default and explicitly) set to false.    h6.Expected Result  Navigating with the trackball may scroll a tableview but does not select its rows.    h6.Actual Result  Rows are selected (green background in my case, like you've tapped them) while using trackball    h6.Repro sequence  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: focusable does not prevent focusing while using trackball
Description: """"h6.Issue While using the trackball within a tableview each row is selected although the focusable property is (default and explicitly) set to false. h6.Expected Result Navigating with the trackball may scroll a tableview but does not select its rows. h6.Actual Result Rows are selected (green background in my case, like you've tapped them) while using trackball h6.Repro sequence """"",title+description
TIMOB-12442,12,"""CLI: Update the i18n-sync tool to use Uglify2""","""""""The i18n-sync tool still uses UglifyJS v1. It doesn't really hurt it to leave it that way, but we should normalize everything onto v2 so we don't run into potential version conflicts down the road.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Update the i18n-sync tool to use Uglify2
Description: """"The i18n-sync tool still uses UglifyJS v1. It doesn't really hurt it to leave it that way, but we should normalize everything onto v2 so we don't run into potential version conflicts down the road.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12441,12,"""Developer options on Android devices cause Titanium apps to close""","""""""""""""""Don't keep activities"""""""" option in Developer Options on devices cause Titanium apps to close after the first activity is loaded.  This is a major difference between Titanium apps and native Android apps as this option may be checked unbeknownst to the client and thus seen as a bug in the app.""""""",Bug,"Title: Developer options on Android devices cause Titanium apps to close
Description: """"""""""""Don't keep activities"""""""" option in Developer Options on devices cause Titanium apps to close after the first activity is loaded. This is a major difference between Titanium apps and native Android apps as this option may be checked unbeknownst to the client and thus seen as a bug in the app.""""",title+description
