TIMOB-12361,12,"""BlackBerry: Can't create a blackberry project when we have a space or some other characters in the app name.""","""""""Description:  1.Launch  the studio.  2.Go to create titanium project.  3.Select default template.  4.In the app name field type the name of the app with a space e.g 'default app'    Actual Result:  1.You will get the error in studio like """"""""A BlackBerry project cannot have a space, or any of these characters in its name: !$("""""""")&`:;'*?[]#~=%<>{} """"""""  There are no issues with other platforms.    Expected Result:  1.We should be able to create a BB project with spaces in the project name """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Can't create a blackberry project when we have a space or some other characters in the app name.
