TIMOB-12328,12,"""iOS: search bar layout issues when setting 'width' property""","""""""h3. Problem description  When setting 'width' property for the search bar on top of a TableView, the search bar is then being wrongly displayed.    h3. Steps to reproduce  Create a Search Bar and set the width property value.   Result: Search Bar is not longer correctly displayed (see screenshot).  Setting 'width' value should not have effect on Search Bar size.    Note that setting also the right property, in this case the Search Bar is also always displayed below the right Index (see TIMOB-666)    Search Bar resize issues also reported in TIMOB-11676    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: search bar layout issues when setting 'width' property
Description: """"h3. Problem description When setting 'width' property for the search bar on top of a TableView, the search bar is then being wrongly displayed. h3. Steps to reproduce Create a Search Bar and set the width property value. Result: Search Bar is not longer correctly displayed (see screenshot). Setting 'width' value should not have effect on Search Bar size. Note that setting also the right property, in this case the Search Bar is also always displayed below the right Index (see TIMOB-666) Search Bar resize issues also reported in TIMOB-11676 """"",title+description
TIMOB-12327,12,"""iOS: Window close method does not play nice with animation style constants""","""""""h6.Issue  iOS: Window close method does not play nice with [property transition|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/latest/#!/api/Titanium.UI.Animation-property-transition] (using animation style constants).    h6.Tested on  iOS 6 simulator & iPhone 4 w/ 6.0.1    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Run sample  2. Press """"""""Click me to open""""""""  3. Press """"""""Click me to close""""""""  4. First UI item flickers  5. Repeat steps 2 and 3. Both UI items flickers now.    h6.Stripped down version  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window close method does not play nice with animation style constants
