TIMOB-12283,12,"""CLI: Entering the data when CLI prompts in CLI setup wizard, entered data is not correctly placed on the screen.""","""""""CLI: Entering the data when CLI prompts in CLI setup wizard, the entered data on the terminal overlaps the data on the terminal and misplaced, entered data is not correctly placed on the screen.    Steps to Reproduce:   1. run """"""""Titanium setup -a""""""""  2. When CLI prompts for various options, then enter the data, hit backspace, then enter again    Actual result:  After hitting the backspace, the cursor goes to previous line , vertically upward  Please refer to screenshots    Expected :    Entered data is not properly aligned to the terminal window.  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Entering the data when CLI prompts in CLI setup wizard, entered data is not correctly placed on the screen.
Description: """"CLI: Entering the data when CLI prompts in CLI setup wizard, the entered data on the terminal overlaps the data on the terminal and misplaced, entered data is not correctly placed on the screen. Steps to Reproduce: 1. run """"""""Titanium setup -a"""""""" 2. When CLI prompts for various options, then enter the data, hit backspace, then enter again Actual result: After hitting the backspace, the cursor goes to previous line , vertically upward Please refer to screenshots Expected : Entered data is not properly aligned to the terminal window. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12282,12,"""CLI: Setup wizard throws an error while input is provided to iOS distribution certificate prompt. ""","""""""Setup wizard prompts name of the iOS distribution certificate , provided the correct name , error comes stating """"""""TypeError: Object true has no method 'trim'   CLI: Setup wizard throws an error while input is provided to iOS distribution certificate prompt.     Steps to reproduce:   1. run """"""""Titanium setup -a""""""""   2. Process till the prompt for iOS distribution certificate comes  3. Provide the valid distribution certificate name.    Actual result :  An error is shown as follows    /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/longjohn/index.js:111        throw e;              ^  TypeError: Object true has no method 'trim'      at exports.run (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/lib/commands/setup.js:310:42)      at Array.forEach (native)      at exports.run (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/lib/commands/setup.js:309:25)      at prompt.get (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:317:32)      at async.forEachSeries.iterate (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:116:25)      at assembler (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:314:9)      at prompt.get (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:323:32)      at prompt.getInput (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:598:5)      at Interface.onLine (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/node_modules/read/lib/read.js:110:5)    Expected Result :   Setup wizard should successfully configure the iOS distribution certificate  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Setup wizard throws an error while input is provided to iOS distribution certificate prompt.
Description: """"Setup wizard prompts name of the iOS distribution certificate , provided the correct name , error comes stating """"""""TypeError: Object true has no method 'trim' CLI: Setup wizard throws an error while input is provided to iOS distribution certificate prompt. Steps to reproduce: 1. run """"""""Titanium setup -a"""""""" 2. Process till the prompt for iOS distribution certificate comes 3. Provide the valid distribution certificate name. Actual result : An error is shown as follows /usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/longjohn/index.js:111 throw e; ^ TypeError: Object true has no method 'trim' at exports.run (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/lib/commands/setup.js:310:42) at Array.forEach (native) at exports.run (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/lib/commands/setup.js:309:25) at prompt.get (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:317:32) at async.forEachSeries.iterate (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/async/lib/async.js:116:25) at assembler (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:314:9) at prompt.get (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:323:32) at prompt.getInput (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/lib/prompt.js:598:5) at Interface.onLine (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/titanium/node_modules/prompt/node_modules/read/lib/read.js:110:5) Expected Result : Setup wizard should successfully configure the iOS distribution certificate """"",title+description
TIMOB-12281,12,"""Android: Feature: Allow non-visible zoom controls in WebView""","""""""h6.Feature Request  Expose setDisplayZoomControls method so the zoom buttons are disabled in a webview but pinch zoom works    h6.Use Case  Developer want pinch zoom on, zoom buttons off    h6.setDisplayZoomControls method  public void setDisplayZoomControls (boolean enabled)    Added in API level 11  Sets whether the WebView should display on-screen zoom controls when using the built-in zoom mechanisms. See [setBuiltInZoomControls(boolean)|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/webkit/WebSettings.html#setBuiltInZoomControls(boolean)]. The default is true.    Parameters  enabled whether the WebView should display on-screen zoom controls    h6.Android docs  http://developer.android.com/reference/android/webkit/WebSettings.html#setDisplayZoomControls(boolean)""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Feature: Allow non-visible zoom controls in WebView
Description: """"h6.Feature Request Expose setDisplayZoomControls method so the zoom buttons are disabled in a webview but pinch zoom works h6.Use Case Developer want pinch zoom on, zoom buttons off h6.setDisplayZoomControls method public void setDisplayZoomControls (boolean enabled) Added in API level 11 Sets whether the WebView should display on-screen zoom controls when using the built-in zoom mechanisms. See [setBuiltInZoomControls(boolean)|http://developer.android.com/reference/android/webkit/WebSettings.html#setBuiltInZoomControls(boolean)]. The default is true. Parameters enabled whether the WebView should display on-screen zoom controls h6.Android docs http://developer.android.com/reference/android/webkit/WebSettings.html#setDisplayZoomControls(boolean)""""",title+description
TIMOB-12279,12,"""MobileWeb: JS files are not copied over if you put them in the mobileweb directory""","""""""h4. Problem description  Customers are used to use the """"""""platform"""""""" directory for several versions of the same file. I.e.,     android/samefile.js  iphone/samefile.js    they know that the right samefile.js will get copied over when compiling. This is failing when you are doing    mobileweb/samefile.js     since the file samefile.js won't be copied over in the resultant compiled mobileweb.    h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create new project  2. Copy app.js to app.js in Resources  3. Copy result_iphone.js to Resources/iphone/result.js  4. Copy result_mobileweb.js to Resources/mobileweb/result.js  5. Compile for iphone. You will see a """"""""I'm in the ios version""""""""  6. compile for mobileweb. You will get an error.     h4. Files  App.js      result_iphone.js      result_mobileweb.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: JS files are not copied over if you put them in the mobileweb directory
Description: """"h4. Problem description Customers are used to use the """"""""platform"""""""" directory for several versions of the same file. I.e., android/samefile.js iphone/samefile.js they know that the right samefile.js will get copied over when compiling. This is failing when you are doing mobileweb/samefile.js since the file samefile.js won't be copied over in the resultant compiled mobileweb. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create new project 2. Copy app.js to app.js in Resources 3. Copy result_iphone.js to Resources/iphone/result.js 4. Copy result_mobileweb.js to Resources/mobileweb/result.js 5. Compile for iphone. You will see a """"""""I'm in the ios version"""""""" 6. compile for mobileweb. You will get an error. h4. Files App.js result_iphone.js result_mobileweb.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-12275,12,"""iOS: setting ti.facebook.appid property in tiapp.xml creates an invalid Info.plist file""","""""""h1. Problem description  When adding the property ti.facebook.appid in the tiapp.xml, the Info.plist file generated is invalid. Working fine on 2.1.4    h1. Steps to reproduce  1. create a new Titanium app in Studio  2. add the ti.facebook.appid property in tiapp.xml:        3. build the app, then open build/Info.plist    In the file, you can see under URL Types / Url Schemes that there is an item with value fb[Object object]; building the same app with SDK 2.1.4 shows the correct value fb1234567890.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: setting ti.facebook.appid property in tiapp.xml creates an invalid Info.plist file
Description: """"h1. Problem description When adding the property ti.facebook.appid in the tiapp.xml, the Info.plist file generated is invalid. Working fine on 2.1.4 h1. Steps to reproduce 1. create a new Titanium app in Studio 2. add the ti.facebook.appid property in tiapp.xml: 3. build the app, then open build/Info.plist In the file, you can see under URL Types / Url Schemes that there is an item with value fb[Object object]; building the same app with SDK 2.1.4 shows the correct value fb1234567890.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12274,12,"""Runtime errors: Codify and implement a consistent interface for thrown errors across platforms""","""""""Currently, both iOS and Android report errors with line number, file path, stack trace, native reasons, and/or native locations. However, the format and name of the properties is undefined, and vary from OS to OS. With adding new OSes, it would be ideal if we had parity or consistency to better facilitate debugging and tracking from the field.""""""",Story,"Title: Runtime errors: Codify and implement a consistent interface for thrown errors across platforms
Description: """"Currently, both iOS and Android report errors with line number, file path, stack trace, native reasons, and/or native locations. However, the format and name of the properties is undefined, and vary from OS to OS. With adding new OSes, it would be ideal if we had parity or consistency to better facilitate debugging and tracking from the field.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12273,12,"""CodeProcessor: Analysis runs should be timestamped so that multiple analysis runs can be saved""","""""""Analysis runs should store their data inside of a timestamped folder inside the analysis folder so that multiple runs (say, for different platforms) can be saved""""""",New Feature,"Title: CodeProcessor: Analysis runs should be timestamped so that multiple analysis runs can be saved
Description: """"Analysis runs should store their data inside of a timestamped folder inside the analysis folder so that multiple runs (say, for different platforms) can be saved""""",title+description
TIMOB-12272,12,"""CodeProcessor: Proper report sending mechanism""","""""""A mechanism for sending reports to <USER>could be very useful. This would involve integration with studio and something in the cloud (ACS?). The use case is that customers having problems can run the code processor and submit a report to PS for analysis, making it a lot easier for PS to identify and correct customer issues""""""",New Feature,"Title: CodeProcessor: Proper report sending mechanism
Description: """"A mechanism for sending reports to <USER>could be very useful. This would involve integration with studio and something in the cloud (ACS?). The use case is that customers having problems can run the code processor and submit a report to PS for analysis, making it a lot easier for PS to identify and correct customer issues""""",title+description
TIMOB-12270,12,"""Android:KitchenSink - App crashes on launch""","""""""Kitchensink app crashes on launch.   This is not regression since the issue occurs on 3.0.0 GA as well.    Steps to reproduce:  Install Kitchensink on device and launch app.    Expected:  The app should launch successfully.    Actual:  The app shows the runtime error on launch. Find the error logs below:    01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [2039,17246] ----- Titanium Javascript Runtime Error -----  01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [0,17246] - In ui/common/ApplicationTabGroup.js:135,31  01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [0,17246] - Message: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'title' of undefined  01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [0,17246] - Source:     Ti.API.info('tab ' + e.tab.title + ' prevTab = ' + (e.previousTab ? e.prev  01-11 09:08:29.199: E/V8Exception(6769): Exception occurred at ui/common/ApplicationTabGroup.js:135: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'title' of undefined        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android:KitchenSink - App crashes on launch
Description: """"Kitchensink app crashes on launch. This is not regression since the issue occurs on 3.0.0 GA as well. Steps to reproduce: Install Kitchensink on device and launch app. Expected: The app should launch successfully. Actual: The app shows the runtime error on launch. Find the error logs below: 01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [2039,17246] ----- Titanium Javascript Runtime Error ----- 01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [0,17246] - In ui/common/ApplicationTabGroup.js:135,31 01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [0,17246] - Message: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'title' of undefined 01-11 09:08:29.195: E/TiExceptionHandler(6769): (main) [0,17246] - Source: Ti.API.info('tab ' + e.tab.title + ' prevTab = ' + (e.previousTab ? e.prev 01-11 09:08:29.199: E/V8Exception(6769): Exception occurred at ui/common/ApplicationTabGroup.js:135: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'title' of undefined """"",title+description
