TIMOB-12264,12,"""CLI: JSS font-* properties do not work with new CLI""","""""""In an app with the below app.js and app.jss there is an issue with font size. When trying to change the font size after cleaning it does not work. It stays in a same no matter what size is given as font size. It works fine with Ti SDK 3.0.0 and XCode 4.5.1 but does not work with Ti SDK 3.0.0 and XCode 4.5.2.  Again Ti SDK 2.1.4 and XCode 4.5.2 works as well. Only on the prime combination of 3.0.0 and 4.5.2 does not work.      h2.app.js      h2.app.jss      h4.Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the app with Ti SDK 3.0.0 and XCode 4.5.2  2. Change the font size in app.jss  3. Clean the project  4. Run the app on iphone simulator     Expected Result: Font size should change.    Actual Result: Font size does not change.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: JSS font-* properties do not work with new CLI
Description: """"In an app with the below app.js and app.jss there is an issue with font size. When trying to change the font size after cleaning it does not work. It stays in a same no matter what size is given as font size. It works fine with Ti SDK 3.0.0 and XCode 4.5.1 but does not work with Ti SDK 3.0.0 and XCode 4.5.2. Again Ti SDK 2.1.4 and XCode 4.5.2 works as well. Only on the prime combination of 3.0.0 and 4.5.2 does not work. h2.app.js h2.app.jss h4.Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the app with Ti SDK 3.0.0 and XCode 4.5.2 2. Change the font size in app.jss 3. Clean the project 4. Run the app on iphone simulator Expected Result: Font size should change. Actual Result: Font size does not change.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12263,12,"""CodeProcessor: Allow arbitrary Ti API values to be specified""","""""""We currently allow Ti.Platform.osname and a few other values to be specified, but they are handled explicitly. We should allow any value to be specified. This should be done sooner rather than later because it wil change how some existing configuration options work""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Allow arbitrary Ti API values to be specified
Description: """"We currently allow Ti.Platform.osname and a few other values to be specified, but they are handled explicitly. We should allow any value to be specified. This should be done sooner rather than later because it wil change how some existing configuration options work""""",title+description
TIMOB-12262,12,"""iOS: enable native Photos gallery-like zoomable image""","""""""h1. Problem description  ImageView should support a Photos gallery-like pan and zoom; this means, the image should be centered at first, then should bounce back on all sides when is bigger than the screen.    For more information, we are currently using the following code:        This works fairly well, but when zooming in, the """"""""borders"""""""" on top and bottom (or left-right if the image is portrait) will not disappear, but will be zoomed as well. Need something that behaves as the native gallery pan and zoom.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: enable native Photos gallery-like zoomable image
Description: """"h1. Problem description ImageView should support a Photos gallery-like pan and zoom; this means, the image should be centered at first, then should bounce back on all sides when is bigger than the screen. For more information, we are currently using the following code: This works fairly well, but when zooming in, the """"""""borders"""""""" on top and bottom (or left-right if the image is portrait) will not disappear, but will be zoomed as well. Need something that behaves as the native gallery pan and zoom.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12260,12,"""CodeProcessor: Create a plugin for detecting webview CORS issues""","""""""We should create a plugin to detect when a user set's a webview url to something subject to CORS/X-Frame-Options/etc limitations""""""",New Feature,"Title: CodeProcessor: Create a plugin for detecting webview CORS issues
Description: """"We should create a plugin to detect when a user set's a webview url to something subject to CORS/X-Frame-Options/etc limitations""""",title+description
TIMOB-12259,12,"""CodeProcessor: Create studio interface""","""""""An interface should be created to allow studio to quickly call the code processor. It should be request/response based using stdin/stdout and will be used instead of the bin/codeprocessor script""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Create studio interface
Description: """"An interface should be created to allow studio to quickly call the code processor. It should be request/response based using stdin/stdout and will be used instead of the bin/codeprocessor script""""",title+description
TIMOB-12258,12,"""CodeProcessor: Create run profiles""","""""""We need to create easy to use run profile mechanism. Two key profiles need to be created, but the system should be extensible to allow for more profiles  * Optimization-oriented  ** Do not <USER>files/methods/etc unless they are explicitly called  ** Tuned for accuracy (looser limits, evaluate loops, etc)  * Analysis-oriented  ** Do <USER>files/methods/etc even if they are not explicitly called  ** Tuned for speed (tighter limits, don't evaluate loops, etc)""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Create run profiles
Description: """"We need to create easy to use run profile mechanism. Two key profiles need to be created, but the system should be extensible to allow for more profiles * Optimization-oriented ** Do not <USER>files/methods/etc unless they are explicitly called ** Tuned for accuracy (looser limits, evaluate loops, etc) * Analysis-oriented ** Do <USER>files/methods/etc even if they are not explicitly called ** Tuned for speed (tighter limits, don't evaluate loops, etc)""""",title+description
TIMOB-12257,12,"""CodeProcessor: Add plugin search path capabilities""","""""""Right now plugins must reside at a specific location inside of the code processor directory. Allowing multiple search paths to be specified externally is necessary for future plugin integration""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Add plugin search path capabilities
Description: """"Right now plugins must reside at a specific location inside of the code processor directory. Allowing multiple search paths to be specified externally is necessary for future plugin integration""""",title+description
TIMOB-12256,12,"""CodeProcessor: Plugin configuration mechanism""","""""""Plugins currently cannot accept configuration information aside from the (global) code processor config. Being able to pass in plugin-specific configuration information will be really useful for creating more fine-grained plugins""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Plugin configuration mechanism
Description: """"Plugins currently cannot accept configuration information aside from the (global) code processor config. Being able to pass in plugin-specific configuration information will be really useful for creating more fine-grained plugins""""",title+description
TIMOB-12253,12,"""CodeProcessor: Research methods for making well known samples work""","""""""The first step in getting the well-known samples to work is to figure out why they aren't working and file some tickets.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Research methods for making well known samples work
Description: """"The first step in getting the well-known samples to work is to figure out why they aren't working and file some tickets.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12252,12,"""CodeProcessor: Rework unit tests to be more efficient""","""""""Unit tests are structured such that a library is evaluated along with the test code. The library is around 2k lines of code, but the tests cases are usually only a dozen. Re-evaluating the library per-test causes everything to run extremely slowly. It should be possible to run the library only once and then run each test separately. This may require some new functionality in the core engine to support contexts properly.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CodeProcessor: Rework unit tests to be more efficient
Description: """"Unit tests are structured such that a library is evaluated along with the test code. The library is around 2k lines of code, but the tests cases are usually only a dozen. Re-evaluating the library per-test causes everything to run extremely slowly. It should be possible to run the library only once and then run each test separately. This may require some new functionality in the core engine to support contexts properly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12251,12,"""CodeProcessor: Add support for window URLs""","""""""Window URL's are ignored, meaning those files are never processed. We need to catch them and <USER>them properly.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Add support for window URLs
Description: """"Window URL's are ignored, meaning those files are never processed. We need to catch them and <USER>them properly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12249,12,"""Unable to create any titanium project if its project id has any single capital letter""","""""""Test Steps:    1.Create a Titanium Project for android and mobileweb both.  2.Use any capital letter in its app id (anywhere)  (eg. Com.<USER>test;  com.<USER>test;  com.<USER>tesT;  Com.<USER>Test;)    Actual Result:  Error prompt :'Unable to create new project - The app id must consist of letters, numbers, and underscores'.(screenshot attached)""""""",Bug,"Title: Unable to create any titanium project if its project id has any single capital letter
