TIMOB-12243,12,"""iOS: Tab.open doesn't animate the Window if it's specified on the second parameter""","""""""If I specify some transition for opening a Window inside a Tab, it will be ignored and the window is opened with the default transition.    Code Example:    {code:title=Tab.js|borderStyle=solid|language:JavaScript}  var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();  var w1 = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var w2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'red'  });  var t1 = Ti.UI.createTab({   window: w1  });  tabGroup.addTab(t1);  tabGroup.open();    t1.open(w1, {   animated: true,   transition: Titanium.UI.iPhone.AnimationStyle.FLIP_FROM_LEFT  });  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tab.open doesn't animate the Window if it's specified on the second parameter
Description: """"If I specify some transition for opening a Window inside a Tab, it will be ignored and the window is opened with the default transition. Code Example: {code:title=Tab.js|borderStyle=solid|language:JavaScript} var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); var w1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var w2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'red' }); var t1 = Ti.UI.createTab({ window: w1 }); tabGroup.addTab(t1); tabGroup.open(); t1.open(w1, { animated: true, transition: Titanium.UI.iPhone.AnimationStyle.FLIP_FROM_LEFT }); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-12242,12,"""CLI: iOS: Xcode build fails when iphone build folder path is changed""","""""""When building directly from Xcode after renaming the build directory from """"""""iphone"""""""" to anything, the Xcode pre-compile phase fails because it expects the directory to be named """"""""iphone"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS: Xcode build fails when iphone build folder path is changed
