Description: """"In the myapp/build/iphone/Resources directory contains default startup images and plist files. This directory is unneeded as these files can just be copied to or created in the actually app build directory.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12234,12,"""BlackBerry: Implement important Titanium.Geolocation functionality""","""""""h3. Acceptance Tests    h4. Location event      Verify when you click the toggle button your current position is displayed and updated as you move.  Clicking the toggle again should turn off updates. Repeat a few times to verify it switches on/off.    h4. Heading event      Verify clicking the toggle button starts displaying compass heading values.  Try rotating the phone to verify the degrees changes. Click the toggle again  to verify the compass events stop.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: BlackBerry: Implement important Titanium.Geolocation functionality
Description: """"h3. Acceptance Tests h4. Location event Verify when you click the toggle button your current position is displayed and updated as you move. Clicking the toggle again should turn off updates. Repeat a few times to verify it switches on/off. h4. Heading event Verify clicking the toggle button starts displaying compass heading values. Try rotating the phone to verify the degrees changes. Click the toggle again to verify the compass events stop. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12232,12,"""CodeProcessor: Beef up the custom CLI interface""","""""""There are some new features we should add surrounding the bin script:  1) If no plugins are specified we should load no plugins (instead of loading all)  2) Add an --all-plugins flag, or something similar  3) Add a --no-titanium flag that loads all non-Titanium specific plugins  4) Add a get-plugins command to get a list of all plugins  5) Add dependency checking for plugins""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Beef up the custom CLI interface
Description: """"There are some new features we should add surrounding the bin script: 1) If no plugins are specified we should load no plugins (instead of loading all) 2) Add an --all-plugins flag, or something similar 3) Add a --no-titanium flag that loads all non-Titanium specific plugins 4) Add a get-plugins command to get a list of all plugins 5) Add dependency checking for plugins""""",title+description
TIMOB-12231,12,"""KitchenSink: BaseUI: NavGroup: Red background is not seen, rather we see a light grey background""","""""""Description:  1.Build kitchensink with the build mentioned in the environment & install it on ipad 3iOS 6.0.1  2.Go to baseui -> Nav Group.  3.Look at the background color.    Actual result:  1.It is light grey color.    Expected results:  1.It should be red color as in 2.1.3 GA baseline used for automation.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: BaseUI: NavGroup: Red background is not seen, rather we see a light grey background
