TIMOB-12210,12,"""iOS: Audio Ducking Support""","""""""h1. Feature  Add support for """"""""ducking"""""""" and """"""""unducking"""""""" the iOS audio session. The SDK doesn't expose this right now, but it can very easily.    An example of ducking is when the GPS lowers other sounds to say something, then raises them after it is done speaking.    h2. Proposed Solution  Expose """"""""Ti.Media.ducking = true /* or false */;"""""""". Something like the following:    In TiMediaAudioSession.m:      And in MediaModule.m:      h2. Apple Documentation  Apple talks about this feature in the last paragraph on this page: http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/Audio/Conceptual/AudioSessionProgrammingGuide/Configuration/Configuration.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Audio Ducking Support
Description: """"h1. Feature Add support for """"""""ducking"""""""" and """"""""unducking"""""""" the iOS audio session. The SDK doesn't expose this right now, but it can very easily. An example of ducking is when the GPS lowers other sounds to say something, then raises them after it is done speaking. h2. Proposed Solution Expose """"""""Ti.Media.ducking = true /* or false */;"""""""". Something like the following: In TiMediaAudioSession.m: And in MediaModule.m: h2. Apple Documentation Apple talks about this feature in the last paragraph on this page: http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/Audio/Conceptual/AudioSessionProgrammingGuide/Configuration/Configuration.html""""",title+description
