TIMOB-12203,12,"""KitchenSink: Seeing some slight pixel variations in buttons which is failing the automation screenshot verifications.""","""""""This is not a regression.    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchensink with 2.1.3 GA.  2.Go to views -> table view -> empty_table_views & controls -> tabbed bar  3.build another kitchensink with sdk 3.0.1.v20121228113204 on another similar device running the same iOS version.  4.Go to views -> table view -> empty_table_views & controls -> tabbed bar.    Expected results:  1.You should not see any variations in the buttons when you compare the two kitchensinks.    Actual result:  2.We see slight variations which is causing the automation screenshot verifications to fail.   """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Seeing some slight pixel variations in buttons which is failing the automation screenshot verifications.
Description: """"This is not a regression. Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchensink with 2.1.3 GA. 2.Go to views -> table view -> empty_table_views & controls -> tabbed bar 3.build another kitchensink with sdk 3.0.1.v20121228113204 on another similar device running the same iOS version. 4.Go to views -> table view -> empty_table_views & controls -> tabbed bar. Expected results: 1.You should not see any variations in the buttons when you compare the two kitchensinks. Actual result: 2.We see slight variations which is causing the automation screenshot verifications to fail. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12202,12,"""Android: Section header views are redrawn when a TabGroup is used ""","""""""h6.Problem  We are getting this issue only once when the orientation of the Window changes in the tabGroup.    h6.Tested on  Droid Razr 2.3.5    h6.Expected behavior  It looks like if a single window is used, issue does not happens.    h6.Additional details  To try out please uncomment line near the very bottom instead of open the tabGroup:     //contactusWindow.open();    Issues does not seem to occur in iOS    h6.Current behavior  Section header Views swapping issues    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Run sample  2. Press tab 2.  3. Change orientation from portrait to landscape.   4. Change it back.   5. the second tableViewSections disappears.     **Notice how the first 2 tableViewSections are """"""""gone""""""""** (or at least redrawn).    h6.Repro sequence      h6.Customer remarks  we observed this issue in HTC Sensation OS 2.3.4, Samsung Galaxy S2 OS 4.0.3, Sony Xperia OS 4.0.4.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Section header views are redrawn when a TabGroup is used
Description: """"h6.Problem We are getting this issue only once when the orientation of the Window changes in the tabGroup. h6.Tested on Droid Razr 2.3.5 h6.Expected behavior It looks like if a single window is used, issue does not happens. h6.Additional details To try out please uncomment line near the very bottom instead of open the tabGroup: //contactusWindow.open(); Issues does not seem to occur in iOS h6.Current behavior Section header Views swapping issues h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Run sample 2. Press tab 2. 3. Change orientation from portrait to landscape. 4. Change it back. 5. the second tableViewSections disappears. **Notice how the first 2 tableViewSections are """"""""gone""""""""** (or at least redrawn). h6.Repro sequence h6.Customer remarks we observed this issue in HTC Sensation OS 2.3.4, Samsung Galaxy S2 OS 4.0.3, Sony Xperia OS 4.0.4. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12201,12,"""Android: e.PreventDefault(ontouchmove) does not disable the swipe on the ScrollableView""","""""""The customer is listening to the swipe event on certain divs, but on Android the scrollableView is navigation to the next or previous view instead of firing the event in the webView. On Android, e.PreventDefault(ontouchmove) does not disable the swipe on the scrollableView. In the attached project I've included the Zepto.js  h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create an alloy project in the studio.  2. Replace its app folder with the attached app folder  2. Open the application, when try to swipe the upperleft image it'll swipe the scrollableView.  The screencast link is here showing how it works fine on iPad http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AKqzmnNXts8 """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: e.PreventDefault(ontouchmove) does not disable the swipe on the ScrollableView
Description: """"The customer is listening to the swipe event on certain divs, but on Android the scrollableView is navigation to the next or previous view instead of firing the event in the webView. On Android, e.PreventDefault(ontouchmove) does not disable the swipe on the scrollableView. In the attached project I've included the Zepto.js h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create an alloy project in the studio. 2. Replace its app folder with the attached app folder 2. Open the application, when try to swipe the upperleft image it'll swipe the scrollableView. The screencast link is here showing how it works fine on iPad http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AKqzmnNXts8 """"",title+description
