TIMOB-12174,12,"""cannot unzip SDK with WinZip or default windows utility with path too long errors""","""""""When the SDK is unzipped, there is a """"""""path too long"""""""" error when using WinZip or the default windows utility.    Skipping the errors appears to allow the SDK to unzip correctly.    The work-around is to use 7-Zip.    WinZip log excerpt:        Steps to Reproduce:    1. Download SDK zip file (http://builds.<USER>com.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html).  2. Unzip SDK using WinZip or the default windows utility.    Actual Result:    Error.    Expected Result:    SDK unzips without error.  """"""",Bug,"Title: cannot unzip SDK with WinZip or default windows utility with path too long errors
Description: """"When the SDK is unzipped, there is a """"""""path too long"""""""" error when using WinZip or the default windows utility. Skipping the errors appears to allow the SDK to unzip correctly. The work-around is to use 7-Zip. WinZip log excerpt: Steps to Reproduce: 1. Download SDK zip file (http://builds.<USER>com.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html). 2. Unzip SDK using WinZip or the default windows utility. Actual Result: Error. Expected Result: SDK unzips without error. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12173,12,"""iOS: Build fails if a project's id contains capital letters""","""""""Description:  iOS build fails if an app id starts with a capital letter.  It is a *regression*, builds without error on 3.0.0.GA    It fails only for iOS, works for Android    Test steps:  1. Create a new mobile project  2. Use a capital letters in app id(in my case I used ABC)  3. Run as iOS simulator or build it on device    Actual result:    [ERROR] :  tiapp.xml contains an invalid app id """"""""com.<USER>ABC""""""""  The app id must consist of letters, numbers, and underscores.  The first character must be a letter or underscore.    Expected result:  App should build with no error""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Build fails if a project's id contains capital letters
Description: """"Description: iOS build fails if an app id starts with a capital letter. It is a *regression*, builds without error on 3.0.0.GA It fails only for iOS, works for Android Test steps: 1. Create a new mobile project 2. Use a capital letters in app id(in my case I used ABC) 3. Run as iOS simulator or build it on device Actual result: [ERROR] :  tiapp.xml contains an invalid app id """"""""com.<USER>ABC"""""""" The app id must consist of letters, numbers, and underscores. The first character must be a letter or underscore. Expected result: App should build with no error""""",title+description
TIMOB-12172,12,"""CodeProcessor: Upgrade to Uglify 2""","""""""Uglify 1 has some problems (fails unit tests, etc), doesn't generate source maps, and ditches comments. We need to upgrade to Uglify 2 to address these issues, as well as cleaning up a lot of code in the code processor itself written for dealing with some of the idiosyncrasies of Uglify 1""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Upgrade to Uglify 2
Description: """"Uglify 1 has some problems (fails unit tests, etc), doesn't generate source maps, and ditches comments. We need to upgrade to Uglify 2 to address these issues, as well as cleaning up a lot of code in the code processor itself written for dealing with some of the idiosyncrasies of Uglify 1""""",title+description
TIMOB-12170,12,"""Mobile Web: Problem with rows in TableView beyond the first TableViewSection""","""""""*Reproduction steps*  1. Create basic titanium mobile project.  2. Add one TableView with two TableViewSections. Each TableViewSection has several rows (TableViewRow).  3. Run it as mobile web preview in web browser.    *Expected behavior*  TableView with two sections and rows.     *Actual behavior*  Only the first section has rows (property rows is undefined for second section).    NOT reproducible in 2.1.4.GA version.    *Sample program*      *Expected program printout*      *Actual program printout*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web: Problem with rows in TableView beyond the first TableViewSection
Description: """"*Reproduction steps* 1. Create basic titanium mobile project. 2. Add one TableView with two TableViewSections. Each TableViewSection has several rows (TableViewRow). 3. Run it as mobile web preview in web browser. *Expected behavior* TableView with two sections and rows. *Actual behavior* Only the first section has rows (property rows is undefined for second section). NOT reproducible in 2.1.4.GA version. *Sample program* *Expected program printout* *Actual program printout* """"",title+description
TIMOB-12168,12,"""CLI: Fix setup command serialization""","""""""When the setup command finishes prompting for all values, the values are serialized and saved. It's (somehow) possible that the serialization fails when a value is thought to be a string, but instead it's a boolean.        Here's the Q&A question where the bug was found: http://developer.<USER>com/question/146242/problem-occurred-unable-to-create-new-project-with-sdk3.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Fix setup command serialization
Description: """"When the setup command finishes prompting for all values, the values are serialized and saved. It's (somehow) possible that the serialization fails when a value is thought to be a string, but instead it's a boolean. Here's the Q&A question where the bug was found: http://developer.<USER>com/question/146242/problem-occurred-unable-to-create-new-project-with-sdk3.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12167,12,"""CLI: Build fails if custom Info.plist contains empty string value""","""""""The build will fail if it encounters a <string></string> in a i18n file.    This bug was discovered via the Q&A: http://developer.<USER>com/question/146090/typeerror-cannot-read-property-data-of-null-0.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Build fails if custom Info.plist contains empty string value
