TIMOB-12161,12,"""Android: Localization of string names with '.'""","""""""*Issue*    It is known that the strings.xml file is less flexible in Android as it is used to generate the R.java file. (E.g. a build will fail if a string name starts with an integer or includes a '+', etc.)    The above stated, if a string name includes a '.' character, a build will succeed but replace the '.' characters with '_'.     {code:xml}  <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>  <resources>    <string name=""""""""my.value"""""""">Hello World</string>  </resources>    {code}    Since the replacement is silent, the dev is unaware of the change so the following will not work.    {code:javascript}  alert(L(""""""""my.value""""""""});  {code}    *Temporary Work Around*    For large code bases that cannot change the naming convention, the L function can be redefined, e.g.:    {code:javascript}  (function(object) {    if (exports.osname ===""""""""android"""""""") {      object.L = function(lookup, defaults) {       return  Ti.Locale.getString(lookup.replace(/\./g,""""""""_""""""""), defaults);      };    }  })(this);  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Localization of string names with '.'
Description: """"*Issue* It is known that the strings.xml file is less flexible in Android as it is used to generate the R.java file. (E.g. a build will fail if a string name starts with an integer or includes a '+', etc.) The above stated, if a string name includes a '.' character, a build will succeed but replace the '.' characters with '_'. {code:xml} <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?> <resources> <string name=""""""""my.value"""""""">Hello World</string> </resources> {code} Since the replacement is silent, the dev is unaware of the change so the following will not work. {code:javascript} alert(L(""""""""my.value""""""""}); {code} *Temporary Work Around* For large code bases that cannot change the naming convention, the L function can be redefined, e.g.: {code:javascript} (function(object) { if (exports.osname ===""""""""android"""""""") { object.L = function(lookup, defaults) { return Ti.Locale.getString(lookup.replace(/\./g,""""""""_""""""""), defaults); }; } })(this); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-12160,12,"""Android: Memory leak on heavy weight windows""","""""""There was a memory leak caused by the new bubbling implementation, TIMOB-10463 (Timob-11439 was built on top of this bug as well).  It looks like windows are not being cleaned up correctly.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the following code:      2. Add the following code in your tiapp.xml:    3. Launch the app  4. Hit open window  5. Hit back and watch the allocated memory grow in DDMS  6. Do steps 4&5 at least 5-6 times    Expected result:  The memory should get cleaned up, and you shouldn't see it grow and grow.    Actual Result:  The memory continues to grow even when you back out of the window.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Memory leak on heavy weight windows
Description: """"There was a memory leak caused by the new bubbling implementation, TIMOB-10463 (Timob-11439 was built on top of this bug as well). It looks like windows are not being cleaned up correctly. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run the following code: 2. Add the following code in your tiapp.xml: 3. Launch the app 4. Hit open window 5. Hit back and watch the allocated memory grow in DDMS 6. Do steps 4&5 at least 5-6 times Expected result: The memory should get cleaned up, and you shouldn't see it grow and grow. Actual Result: The memory continues to grow even when you back out of the window.""""",title+description
