Description: """"When the name in the tiapp.xml changes between builds, Xcode fails saying there are conflicting Xcode projects. As a simple fix, if a name change is detected, remove the build directory effectively performing a clean operation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12148,12,"""Android: Action Bar backgroundImage isn't set properly in click event handlers.""","""""""When setting the actionBar.backgroundImage property from a window's """"""""open"""""""" event handler, the change takes effect immediately. However, when setting the background from a click event handler, the change does _not_ take effect.    If you subsequently set the action bar's title property, the previous backgroundImage change takes effect. In addition, when setting one of the actionBar properties, the following message is logged:    [ERROR][Proxy   ( 1017)] Unable to lookup Proxy.prototype.setProperty    Test code:        To reproduce: Create a project, set up to build with targetSdkVersion=11 or higher and api-tool-level 14 or higher. Run app.    Click """"""""Set Background"""""""", then """"""""Set Title"""""""". Note that background doesn't get set when you click Set Background, but DOES get set when you click """"""""Set Title.""""""""    Sometimes you need to repeat this cycle once or twice before the background appears.    After the background has been set, clicking """"""""Set Background"""""""" again causes the background to disappear, although no change should be evident.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Action Bar backgroundImage isn't set properly in click event handlers.
Description: """"When setting the actionBar.backgroundImage property from a window's """"""""open"""""""" event handler, the change takes effect immediately. However, when setting the background from a click event handler, the change does _not_ take effect. If you subsequently set the action bar's title property, the previous backgroundImage change takes effect. In addition, when setting one of the actionBar properties, the following message is logged: [ERROR][Proxy ( 1017)] Unable to lookup Proxy.prototype.setProperty Test code: To reproduce: Create a project, set up to build with targetSdkVersion=11 or higher and api-tool-level 14 or higher. Run app. Click """"""""Set Background"""""""", then """"""""Set Title"""""""". Note that background doesn't get set when you click Set Background, but DOES get set when you click """"""""Set Title."""""""" Sometimes you need to repeat this cycle once or twice before the background appears. After the background has been set, clicking """"""""Set Background"""""""" again causes the background to disappear, although no change should be evident. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12147,12,"""iOS: regression: button created in require()d unit won't fire click event""","""""""h2.Problem  There is a regression in SDK 3.0.0.GA that prevents a button's click event from firing when the button is created in a require()d unit.    Works in SDK 2.1.4.GA  Broken in SDK 3.0.0.GA    Note that this works fine on Android under SDK 3.0.0.GA (and SDK 2.1.4.GA)...the problem only exists on iOS.    h2.Testcase  Run the following code and click the button.  A console message should appear when the button is clicked, and the button's title should change to """"""""Clicked!"""""""", but under SDK 3.0.0.GA this does not happen.    Note that this testcase is reduced down to the smallest reproducable code from a very large app.    {panel:title=app.js}    {panel}    {panel:title=win1.js}    {panel}    {panel:title=ButtonMaker.js}    {panel}  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: regression: button created in require()d unit won't fire click event
Description: """"h2.Problem There is a regression in SDK 3.0.0.GA that prevents a button's click event from firing when the button is created in a require()d unit. Works in SDK 2.1.4.GA Broken in SDK 3.0.0.GA Note that this works fine on Android under SDK 3.0.0.GA (and SDK 2.1.4.GA)...the problem only exists on iOS. h2.Testcase Run the following code and click the button. A console message should appear when the button is clicked, and the button's title should change to """"""""Clicked!"""""""", but under SDK 3.0.0.GA this does not happen. Note that this testcase is reduced down to the smallest reproducable code from a very large app. {panel:title=app.js} {panel} {panel:title=win1.js} {panel} {panel:title=ButtonMaker.js} {panel} """"",title+description
TIMOB-12146,12,"""CLI: iOS certs not displaying due to insufficient buffer size""","""""""When the node-appc iOS detection library calls """"""""security dump-keychain"""""""", the buffer to capture the output has a fixed size of 1,048,576 bytes. If that buffer is exceeded, it will return that it didn't find any certs.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS certs not displaying due to insufficient buffer size
Description: """"When the node-appc iOS detection library calls """"""""security dump-keychain"""""""", the buffer to capture the output has a fixed size of 1,048,576 bytes. If that buffer is exceeded, it will return that it didn't find any certs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12145,12,"""Android: JavaScript heap dumps""","""""""Discovering the source of memory leaks caused by references in JavaScript  is currently difficult. To help locate the source of such leaks we  can use a heap dump to inspect the reference graph of the VM current state.    This task is to expose a way to request such a dump and serialize  it to the SDCARD so it can be pulled down through ADB.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: JavaScript heap dumps
Description: """"Discovering the source of memory leaks caused by references in JavaScript is currently difficult. To help locate the source of such leaks we can use a heap dump to inspect the reference graph of the VM current state. This task is to expose a way to request such a dump and serialize it to the SDCARD so it can be pulled down through ADB.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12141,12,"""Android: Unable to animate from the last position/condition""","""""""In the case of animations which change size or coordinates, this is basically a duplicate of TIMOB-1101.  But others like color or opacity animations are special.  If you run an animation on a view (such as an opacity animation) and then later run another one, you of course want the newer animation to start from what is the current visible state of the view on screen.  For example, if you animated to 50% animation and want to now animate to 100% opacity, you want this second animation to obviously start at 50% and move to 100%.  With old Android animation, the actual properties of the view do not change after the animation is complete.  And there are no properties available to tell you what the view currently looks like (post-first-animation).  So in the example, at the time I want to make the second animation (to 100%) there is no property I can check that will tell me that it's currently at 50% opacity, and for the second animation I must tell it the """"""""starting"""""""" opacity.  So Ti Android has ugly code in there to set variables to """"""""remember"""""""" the last-animated-to-opacity (and color, etc.) It's ugly.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Unable to animate from the last position/condition
Description: """"In the case of animations which change size or coordinates, this is basically a duplicate of TIMOB-1101. But others like color or opacity animations are special. If you run an animation on a view (such as an opacity animation) and then later run another one, you of course want the newer animation to start from what is the current visible state of the view on screen. For example, if you animated to 50% animation and want to now animate to 100% opacity, you want this second animation to obviously start at 50% and move to 100%. With old Android animation, the actual properties of the view do not change after the animation is complete. And there are no properties available to tell you what the view currently looks like (post-first-animation). So in the example, at the time I want to make the second animation (to 100%) there is no property I can check that will tell me that it's currently at 50% opacity, and for the second animation I must tell it the """"""""starting"""""""" opacity. So Ti Android has ugly code in there to set variables to """"""""remember"""""""" the last-animated-to-opacity (and color, etc.) It's ugly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12140,12,"""Android: Integrate Android animation compatibility layer""","""""""In order to achieve better parity with animation on iOS, we need to investigate wrapping this compatibility layer for older Android devices:    http://nineoldandroids.com""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Integrate Android animation compatibility layer
Description: """"In order to achieve better parity with animation on iOS, we need to investigate wrapping this compatibility layer for older Android devices: http://nineoldandroids.com""""",title+description
TIMOB-12139,12,"""Android: Textfield change event behaves differently in 2.1.4 and 3.0.0 SDK""","""""""h3. Issue    The textfield change event listener in 2.1.4 is fired differently from 3.0.0.GA SDK.    h3. Steps to Reproduce    Run the sample below:        2. Enter the letter """"""""A"""""""" at the end of the text in the textfield.    3. Notice the characters before A turn to """"""""*"""""""".    4. If you look at the logs the API info statements show 2 change events fired for the above steps in 3.0.0.GA while in 2.1.4.GA, 3 events were fired.      Is this an intentional behavior?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Textfield change event behaves differently in 2.1.4 and 3.0.0 SDK
Description: """"h3. Issue The textfield change event listener in 2.1.4 is fired differently from 3.0.0.GA SDK. h3. Steps to Reproduce Run the sample below: 2. Enter the letter """"""""A"""""""" at the end of the text in the textfield. 3. Notice the characters before A turn to """"""""*"""""""". 4. If you look at the logs the API info statements show 2 change events fired for the above steps in 3.0.0.GA while in 2.1.4.GA, 3 events were fired. Is this an intentional behavior?""""",title+description
TIMOB-12138,12,"""Ti API: Feature to disable alertdialog dismissal when clicked outside its bounds""","""""""h3. Issue    As of now, the alert dialog in Android gets dismissed even when we click outside its bounds.     It has been requested to add a new feature that would allow to disable this.    h3. Reference    I believe there is a native method called *setCancelledOnTouchOutside* that is is not exposed yet in the Titanium API. """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Feature to disable alertdialog dismissal when clicked outside its bounds
Description: """"h3. Issue As of now, the alert dialog in Android gets dismissed even when we click outside its bounds. It has been requested to add a new feature that would allow to disable this. h3. Reference I believe there is a native method called *setCancelledOnTouchOutside* that is is not exposed yet in the Titanium API. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12137,12,"""BlackBerry: Native extensions API""","""""""Design and implement a runtime API for native extension development.  This API will allow developers to expose new JavaScript APIs implemented  in C/C++. Not only will this be used for third party extensions, but the Titanium  APIs will use the same system.""""""",Story,"Title: BlackBerry: Native extensions API
Description: """"Design and implement a runtime API for native extension development. This API will allow developers to expose new JavaScript APIs implemented in C/C++. Not only will this be used for third party extensions, but the Titanium APIs will use the same system.""""",title+description
