TIMOB-12090,12,"""KitchenSink: The image for appcelerator logo appears stretched""","""""""Description:  1.Build kitchensink with the build mentioned in the environment & install it on ipad 3 iOS 6.0.1  2.Go to baseui -> views -> imageview -> basic.  3.Look at the <USER>logo image.  4.Also goto baseui -> views -> imageview ->remote image.  5.Look at the <USER>logo image.  6.Tap on 'assign remote url'  7.Look at the second <USER>logo image which just came up.    Actual result:  1.Its appears to be stretched.    Expected results:  1.It should not appear stretched.    The issue is also seen in the following kitchensink test cases:  *Base_UI -> views -> remote URL  *Base_UI -> Image views -> Image Scaling  *Base_UI -> views --> table views -> table with remote image  """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: The image for appcelerator logo appears stretched
Description: """"Description: 1.Build kitchensink with the build mentioned in the environment & install it on ipad 3 iOS 6.0.1 2.Go to baseui -> views -> imageview -> basic. 3.Look at the <USER>logo image. 4.Also goto baseui -> views -> imageview ->remote image. 5.Look at the <USER>logo image. 6.Tap on 'assign remote url' 7.Look at the second <USER>logo image which just came up. Actual result: 1.Its appears to be stretched. Expected results: 1.It should not appear stretched. The issue is also seen in the following kitchensink test cases: *Base_UI -> views -> remote URL *Base_UI -> Image views -> Image Scaling *Base_UI -> views --> table views -> table with remote image """"",title+description
TIMOB-12089,12,"""iOS: Feature: Support animating two views within a single animation. ""","""""""This feature would free the developer to give animations a extra time to complete, in order to compensate for JS bridge and layout engine delays.    Also, animations nested it would provide more fluid visual transitions to enrich different states of user interface.    Related ticket: [TIMOB-11973]""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Feature: Support animating two views within a single animation.
Description: """"This feature would free the developer to give animations a extra time to complete, in order to compensate for JS bridge and layout engine delays. Also, animations nested it would provide more fluid visual transitions to enrich different states of user interface. Related ticket: [TIMOB-11973]""""",title+description
TIMOB-12088,12,"""iOS: Implement Ti.UI.ActivityIndicatorStyle""","""""""As of Release 3.0, both Android and Mobile Web support Ti.UI.ActivityIndicatorStyle, but iOS still uses Ti.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle, which defines exactly the same constants.    iOS should implement the new module and deprecate Ti.UI.iPhone.AIStyle.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Implement Ti.UI.ActivityIndicatorStyle
