TIMOB-12069,12,"""CLI: Custom Info.plist values not properly overwritten by tiapp.xml values or inheriting from default Info.plist""","""""""This is a regression from 2.1.4 GA.    After discovering some issues with KS and its custom info.plist, we did some additional investigation in this area.    It seems that including a custom info.plist file in the root of your Studio project will result in this file being used as the info.plist for iOS application and therefore replacing values found in tiapp.xml.    According to what I know, the keys/values for the final info.plist file are gathered for some values from the tiapp.xml, for others from the plist, and for some there is a merge of the values from the plist and the tiapp.xml.    The result of this behavior is that settings in the tiapp.xml are not being used in the final project.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Unzip and import into studio the attached project  2) Build the project with the build mentioned.  3) Copy the resulting info.plist form the build folder  4) Build again with 2.1.4 GA and grab the info.plist  5) Compare the info.plists    Result:  The 3.0X info.plist will match exactly the custom info.plist included at the project root  The 2.1.4 GA info.plist will not match exactly with the custom info.plist.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Custom Info.plist values not properly overwritten by tiapp.xml values or inheriting from default Info.plist
Description: """"This is a regression from 2.1.4 GA. After discovering some issues with KS and its custom info.plist, we did some additional investigation in this area. It seems that including a custom info.plist file in the root of your Studio project will result in this file being used as the info.plist for iOS application and therefore replacing values found in tiapp.xml. According to what I know, the keys/values for the final info.plist file are gathered for some values from the tiapp.xml, for others from the plist, and for some there is a merge of the values from the plist and the tiapp.xml. The result of this behavior is that settings in the tiapp.xml are not being used in the final project. Steps to reproduce: 1) Unzip and import into studio the attached project 2) Build the project with the build mentioned. 3) Copy the resulting info.plist form the build folder 4) Build again with 2.1.4 GA and grab the info.plist 5) Compare the info.plists Result: The 3.0X info.plist will match exactly the custom info.plist included at the project root The 2.1.4 GA info.plist will not match exactly with the custom info.plist.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12067,12,"""MobileWeb: Update scrollable view to use a custom simple but fast gesture mechanism""","""""""The gesture part of scrollable view is laughably broken. We need to replace it with a custom written gesture system that avoids the overhead of the generic system we currently use. See the attached prototype""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Update scrollable view to use a custom simple but fast gesture mechanism
Description: """"The gesture part of scrollable view is laughably broken. We need to replace it with a custom written gesture system that avoids the overhead of the generic system we currently use. See the attached prototype""""",title+description
TIMOB-12066,12,"""iOS: - App with custom info.plist with version number in it will not trigger resync of App in iTunes. ""","""""""Test steps:  1. Install KS (in our case it is an App with custom info.plist with version #) from Studio on device, make sure there is no KS previously installed on device.     2. Change SDK build in tiapp.xml, save it and install on device. There will be an iTunes dialog window, asking to replace an existing App. Please, do.    3. Go to iTunes device's Apps.    Actual result:  After step 3 NO automatic """"""""resync"""""""" happened, and there is """"""""Remove"""""""" button next to the App instead """"""""Update"""""""". The only way to replace an App is to delete it from device and install it from iTunes again.    Expected result:  After step 3 the button """"""""Update"""""""" should be next to the App, so the App could be updated.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: - App with custom info.plist with version number in it will not trigger resync of App in iTunes.
Description: """"Test steps: 1. Install KS (in our case it is an App with custom info.plist with version #) from Studio on device, make sure there is no KS previously installed on device. 2. Change SDK build in tiapp.xml, save it and install on device. There will be an iTunes dialog window, asking to replace an existing App. Please, do. 3. Go to iTunes device's Apps. Actual result: After step 3 NO automatic """"""""resync"""""""" happened, and there is """"""""Remove"""""""" button next to the App instead """"""""Update"""""""". The only way to replace an App is to delete it from device and install it from iTunes again. Expected result: After step 3 the button """"""""Update"""""""" should be next to the App, so the App could be updated.""""",title+description
