TIMOB-12022,12,"""Android:  TableView section number wrong on events fired""","""""""Run the attached program.    Click on a section    Actual results:  Section number is always 12    Expected results:  Section number should be 1 to 12      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView section number wrong on events fired
Description: """"Run the attached program. Click on a section Actual results: Section number is always 12 Expected results: Section number should be 1 to 12 """"",title+description
TIMOB-12021,12,"""BlackBerry: Cannot access ACS keys from tiapp.xml""","""""""Expected Behavior:    I should be able to set ACS keys in the tiapp.xml.     Actual Behavior:    I must set them in code.    See https://github.com/joshthecoder/todo_titanium_bb10 for a sample app. Comment out the ACS key in app.js. The app builds, but you cannot log in. You're not able to connect to ACS.     I tried by creating my own app (and thus ACS keys), creating an initial user object via the ACS control panel, and then building. I have to put my keys into the app.js file or the Login button does nothing.  """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: Cannot access ACS keys from tiapp.xml
Description: """"Expected Behavior: I should be able to set ACS keys in the tiapp.xml. Actual Behavior: I must set them in code. See https://github.com/joshthecoder/todo_titanium_bb10 for a sample app. Comment out the ACS key in app.js. The app builds, but you cannot log in. You're not able to connect to ACS. I tried by creating my own app (and thus ACS keys), creating an initial user object via the ACS control panel, and then building. I have to put my keys into the app.js file or the Login button does nothing. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12020,12,"""Android: audio file in application data directory does not play on certain devices""","""""""h1. Problem description  When playing a sound downloaded in the application data directory, on certain devices (e.g. HTC Desire HD) the sound doesn't play. Everything works fine with other devices, or with the same device using the external directory.    h1. Steps to reproduce  Use this code to reproduce the issue:        Running the code on HTC devices does not play the sound.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: audio file in application data directory does not play on certain devices
Description: """"h1. Problem description When playing a sound downloaded in the application data directory, on certain devices (e.g. HTC Desire HD) the sound doesn't play. Everything works fine with other devices, or with the same device using the external directory. h1. Steps to reproduce Use this code to reproduce the issue: Running the code on HTC devices does not play the sound.""""",title+description
