TIMOB-12012,12,"""SQLite fieldCount() Crashes on iOS""","""""""In 3.0 RC2 iOS crashes when trying to use fieldCount().  If changed to just fieldCount (the property) it works.  Previously fieldCount as a property wasn't supported in iOS but I see it's available now (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.Database.ResultSet-property-fieldCount).  Probably was a parity issue that was fixed but in the <USER>causes this crash.    The code that makes it crash (from the Joli ORM lib on github):                if (Titanium.Platform.name !== 'android') {                  fieldCount = rows.fieldCount;              } else {                  fieldCount = rows.fieldCount();              }""""""",Bug,"Title: SQLite fieldCount() Crashes on iOS
Description: """"In 3.0 RC2 iOS crashes when trying to use fieldCount(). If changed to just fieldCount (the property) it works. Previously fieldCount as a property wasn't supported in iOS but I see it's available now (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/3.0/#!/api/Titanium.Database.ResultSet-property-fieldCount). Probably was a parity issue that was fixed but in the <USER>causes this crash. The code that makes it crash (from the Joli ORM lib on github): if (Titanium.Platform.name !== 'android') { fieldCount = rows.fieldCount; } else { fieldCount = rows.fieldCount(); }""""",title+description
TIMOB-12011,12,"""CLI: iOS: UIPrerenderedIcon ignored and icons are always glossy""","""""""According to <USER> """"""""I noticed when deploying the app to the device (adhoc and installing with iTunes) the app icon always gets the gloss, which means its not respecting the UIPrerenderedIcon property in tiapp.xml.""""""""    This will require some investigation.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS: UIPrerenderedIcon ignored and icons are always glossy
Description: """"According to <USER> """"""""I noticed when deploying the app to the device (adhoc and installing with iTunes) the app icon always gets the gloss, which means its not respecting the UIPrerenderedIcon property in tiapp.xml."""""""" This will require some investigation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12010,12,"""iOS: Customize selected tab ImageTintColor""","""""""iOS 5+ supports to customize colors of TabBar.    There is one ticket to supports to change the tabsBackgroundColor (http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9135?page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:all-tabpanel), but this ticket doesn't implement to change the selectedImageTintColor (when selected).    This feature must be implemented too.    In the attachment, the selectedImageTintColor is green. Default is blue. This feature is to allow user change this color.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Customize selected tab ImageTintColor
Description: """"iOS 5+ supports to customize colors of TabBar. There is one ticket to supports to change the tabsBackgroundColor (http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9135?page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:all-tabpanel), but this ticket doesn't implement to change the selectedImageTintColor (when selected). This feature must be implemented too. In the attachment, the selectedImageTintColor is green. Default is blue. This feature is to allow user change this color.""""",title+description
TIMOB-12009,12,"""iOS 6: Add the supressesIncrementalRendering parameter to iOS WebViews""","""""""On iOS6, apple introduced the supressesIncrementalRendering parameter for UIWebViews.    This parameter allows developers to disable the natural incremental rendering, default of html engines and only render the content fully when everything is loaded on memory.    This, when properly used (probably combined with the load event), can make webviews look more like native views as the whole html content is loaded in a single shot.    Titanium should allow a supressesIncrementalRendering BOOLEAN parameter as a parameter of Ti.UI.createWebView in order to enable this functionality.    This is compatible with iOS6 and higher.      Link to official Apple docs on this matter:  https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIWebView_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40006950-CH3-SW37      """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS 6: Add the supressesIncrementalRendering parameter to iOS WebViews
Description: """"On iOS6, apple introduced the supressesIncrementalRendering parameter for UIWebViews. This parameter allows developers to disable the natural incremental rendering, default of html engines and only render the content fully when everything is loaded on memory. This, when properly used (probably combined with the load event), can make webviews look more like native views as the whole html content is loaded in a single shot. Titanium should allow a supressesIncrementalRendering BOOLEAN parameter as a parameter of Ti.UI.createWebView in order to enable this functionality. This is compatible with iOS6 and higher. Link to official Apple docs on this matter: https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIWebView_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40006950-CH3-SW37 """"",title+description
TIMOB-12008,12,"""iOS: Window backgroundImage ignored in grouped TableView""","""""""h3.Repro steps  Example code:      h5. Behaviour on 2.1.3 SDK  TableView is grouped and background image displayed.    [^TableView SDK_213.png]    h5. Behaviour on 2.1.4 SDK (broken)  TableView is grouped and background image ignored. Instead, the standard iOS pinstripe pattern is shown.    [^TableView SDK_214.png]    h3. Expected behaviour  As per 2.1.3 SDK.    h3.Community thread  http://developer.<USER>com/question/144761/sdk-214-backgroundimage-not-working-in-grouped-table-views#251163""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window backgroundImage ignored in grouped TableView
Description: """"h3.Repro steps Example code: h5. Behaviour on 2.1.3 SDK TableView is grouped and background image displayed. [^TableView SDK_213.png] h5. Behaviour on 2.1.4 SDK (broken) TableView is grouped and background image ignored. Instead, the standard iOS pinstripe pattern is shown. [^TableView SDK_214.png] h3. Expected behaviour As per 2.1.3 SDK. h3.Community thread http://developer.<USER>com/question/144761/sdk-214-backgroundimage-not-working-in-grouped-table-views#251163""""",title+description
TIMOB-12007,12,"""iOS: UICompositeLayout - View is displayed at the top left corner of the screen momentarily before being displayed at center.""","""""""View is displayed at the top left corner of the screen momentarily before being displayed at center.  This is not regression since the issue occurs since 2.1.3.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create an app using the code below.  2. Launch app on iPad.    Actual:  The View is displayed at the top left corner of the screen momentarily before being displayed at center.    Expected:  The view should be displayed at the center only.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UICompositeLayout - View is displayed at the top left corner of the screen momentarily before being displayed at center.
Description: """"View is displayed at the top left corner of the screen momentarily before being displayed at center. This is not regression since the issue occurs since 2.1.3. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create an app using the code below. 2. Launch app on iPad. Actual: The View is displayed at the top left corner of the screen momentarily before being displayed at center. Expected: The view should be displayed at the center only. """"",title+description
TIMOB-12006,12,"""Android:  Fast scroll of tableview produces blank images""","""""""This is NOT a 3.0.X bug -- it's very likely to have been introduced  with changes for TIMOB-11282.    See TIMOB-8708 for the test case here.    Steps to reproduce:    (1) Modify the app in TIMOB-8708 so images are 200 x 200.    (2) You'll need a large number of contacts, 100 is good, probably      40 would be enough.      (3) Run the app.  Kick scroll to move the table      quickly.   You need to move the table fast enough that      a few screens scroll by.      (4) Notice that images shown are now blank.    Actual results:  Images are blank    Expected result:  Images show pictures of contacts  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Fast scroll of tableview produces blank images
Description: """"This is NOT a 3.0.X bug -- it's very likely to have been introduced with changes for TIMOB-11282. See TIMOB-8708 for the test case here. Steps to reproduce: (1) Modify the app in TIMOB-8708 so images are 200 x 200. (2) You'll need a large number of contacts, 100 is good, probably 40 would be enough. (3) Run the app. Kick scroll to move the table quickly. You need to move the table fast enough that a few screens scroll by. (4) Notice that images shown are now blank. Actual results: Images are blank Expected result: Images show pictures of contacts """"",title+description
TIMOB-12005,12,"""CLI: use paths.sdks config for default Titanium SDK install directory""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1.Run titanium sdk install --branch 3_0_X -default in CLI.  2.Notice that it will download the sdk & extract it to 'programdata/titanium'.    Actual Result:  1.Extract it to 'C:/programdata/titanium'.    Expected Result:  1.It should extract to 'users/-user-/appdata/roaming/titanium'.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: use paths.sdks config for default Titanium SDK install directory
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1.Run titanium sdk install --branch 3_0_X -default in CLI. 2.Notice that it will download the sdk & extract it to 'programdata/titanium'. Actual Result: 1.Extract it to 'C:/programdata/titanium'. Expected Result: 1.It should extract to 'users/-user-/appdata/roaming/titanium'.""""",title+description
