TIMOB-11973,12,"""iOS: Animating 'top' value of UITableView causes it stop scrolling""","""""""h6.Issue  Not able to longer scroll the tableView all the way to the bottom, when attempt animating the 'top' value of a tableView, causes it the contentView to stop scrolling correctly on iOS.    h6.Reproducible steps   * 1. Start the app! :)   * 2. Scroll the tableView up/down to make sure that all rows are visible   * 3. Click on the blue bar (Where it says 'Click me!')   * 4. Attempt to scroll the tableView all the way to the bottom   * 5. Click on the blue bar    * 6. Attempt to scroll the tableView (after it is now in its original state)    This happens after step 4, and then step 6 will return the table to its original state, where you are still unable to scroll to the bottom.    h6.Expected  Scroll tableView as needed    h6.Actual  You can scroll the entire tableView, only once, when actually the application is first launched.    h6.Tested on  iOS 6 simulator  iPhone 4 - iOS 6    h6.Console output  [WARN] New layout set while view [object TiUITableView] animating: Will relayout after animation.    h6.Runnable sample  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Animating 'top' value of UITableView causes it stop scrolling
Description: """"h6.Issue Not able to longer scroll the tableView all the way to the bottom, when attempt animating the 'top' value of a tableView, causes it the contentView to stop scrolling correctly on iOS. h6.Reproducible steps * 1. Start the app! :) * 2. Scroll the tableView up/down to make sure that all rows are visible * 3. Click on the blue bar (Where it says 'Click me!') * 4. Attempt to scroll the tableView all the way to the bottom * 5. Click on the blue bar * 6. Attempt to scroll the tableView (after it is now in its original state) This happens after step 4, and then step 6 will return the table to its original state, where you are still unable to scroll to the bottom. h6.Expected Scroll tableView as needed h6.Actual You can scroll the entire tableView, only once, when actually the application is first launched. h6.Tested on iOS 6 simulator iPhone 4 - iOS 6 h6.Console output [WARN] New layout set while view [object TiUITableView] animating: Will relayout after animation. h6.Runnable sample """"",title+description
TIMOB-11972,12,"""CLI: Building for iOS device is failing to install the app because of invalid code signing""","""""""*Note* This issue did not occur using SDK 2.1.4.GA  *Note* I am the first QE member to encounter this issue  *Note* I also have multiple certificates in my keychain with the same name    Steps to reproduce  1. Create a new single window application in Studio  2. Build for iOS device  3. Allow codesign to use key    Actual result:  During compilation a modal alert is displayed *See screenshot* that wants codesign to use """"""""<key>"""""""". The build succeeds but then fails to install to device.    log attached    Expected result:  Codesign finds the right key, and I am able to successfully install to device""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Building for iOS device is failing to install the app because of invalid code signing
Description: """"*Note* This issue did not occur using SDK 2.1.4.GA *Note* I am the first QE member to encounter this issue *Note* I also have multiple certificates in my keychain with the same name Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new single window application in Studio 2. Build for iOS device 3. Allow codesign to use key Actual result: During compilation a modal alert is displayed *See screenshot* that wants codesign to use """"""""<key>"""""""". The build succeeds but then fails to install to device. log attached Expected result: Codesign finds the right key, and I am able to successfully install to device""""",title+description
