TIMOB-11967,12,"""CLI : Need to change verbage of the '-s' & '--sdk' flags in build command which parses the tiapp.xml for the sdk,rather than using the sdk mentioned in the command to build the app.""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1.Create an android(or iOS) app using CLI.  2.Build using the 'build' command with '-s <sdk-version>' or '--sdk<sdk version>'.  3.Notice that CLI builds the app using the sdk in the tiapp.xml rather than the sdk specified in the '-s' or '--sdk'.    4.The '-s' command just parses the tiapp.xml & picks up the sdk in the tiapp.xml to build the app & ignores the sdk passed with '-s' flag.    This is confusing with the current description of '-s' & '--sdk' flag in CLI which is: """"""""Titanium SDK version to use""""""""    Expected results:  We need to change it to a proper description which is not confusing.    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI : Need to change verbage of the '-s' & '--sdk' flags in build command which parses the tiapp.xml for the sdk,rather than using the sdk mentioned in the command to build the app.
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1.Create an android(or iOS) app using CLI. 2.Build using the 'build' command with '-s <sdk-version>' or '--sdk<sdk version>'. 3.Notice that CLI builds the app using the sdk in the tiapp.xml rather than the sdk specified in the '-s' or '--sdk'. 4.The '-s' command just parses the tiapp.xml & picks up the sdk in the tiapp.xml to build the app & ignores the sdk passed with '-s' flag. This is confusing with the current description of '-s' & '--sdk' flag in CLI which is: """"""""Titanium SDK version to use"""""""" Expected results: We need to change it to a proper description which is not confusing. """"",title+description
