TIMOB-11913,12,"""CLI: Make distinction between iPhone and iPad at compile time during Universal build""","""""""As far as I know, right now, the CLI does not give a distinction between iPhone and iPad during a universal build. It would be ideal if we could make this distinction at compile time. If we were able to make this distinction for all iOS builds, Alloy would be able to further improve the runtime performance of apps by eliminating unnecessary platform conditionals at runtime. Ideally this distinction would be available as a parameter that could be used in the Alloy hook into the CLI <USER>    This is already done for Android, iOS, and Mobileweb for all {{Ti.Platform.name}} conditional checks. If we were able to make the above distinction, we could do the same for all {{Ti.Platform.osname}} conditionals on iOS, just as we do now for Android and Mobileweb. """"""",Story,"Title: CLI: Make distinction between iPhone and iPad at compile time during Universal build
Description: """"As far as I know, right now, the CLI does not give a distinction between iPhone and iPad during a universal build. It would be ideal if we could make this distinction at compile time. If we were able to make this distinction for all iOS builds, Alloy would be able to further improve the runtime performance of apps by eliminating unnecessary platform conditionals at runtime. Ideally this distinction would be available as a parameter that could be used in the Alloy hook into the CLI <USER> This is already done for Android, iOS, and Mobileweb for all {{Ti.Platform.name}} conditional checks. If we were able to make the above distinction, we could do the same for all {{Ti.Platform.osname}} conditionals on iOS, just as we do now for Android and Mobileweb. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11912,12,"""MobileWeb: Unable to open map correctly second time""","""""""h6.Issue  Using a mapView to display locations on map, when I open the map the first time it comes fine. But, when I try to access the map second time, the map does not come as expected, instead it comes as a cropped image.     h6.Actual result  It covers only few portion of the screen (usually top-left). This image is draggable and can be moved on the screen.     On zooming also, I am not able to get the exact position of my location pins.    h6.Tested on  Browsers - Safari 6.0.2    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Click on Open  2. Go back  3. Repeat steps 1 & 2 - note a cropped map - as seen as image attached     h6.Repro sequence  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Unable to open map correctly second time
Description: """"h6.Issue Using a mapView to display locations on map, when I open the map the first time it comes fine. But, when I try to access the map second time, the map does not come as expected, instead it comes as a cropped image. h6.Actual result It covers only few portion of the screen (usually top-left). This image is draggable and can be moved on the screen. On zooming also, I am not able to get the exact position of my location pins. h6.Tested on Browsers - Safari 6.0.2 h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Click on Open 2. Go back 3. Repeat steps 1 & 2 - note a cropped map - as seen as image attached h6.Repro sequence """"",title+description
TIMOB-11911,12,"""CodeProcessor: Including Ti.cloud causes the code processor to crash""","""""""Ti.cloud is a special module since it's CommonJS but """"""""automagically"""""""" linked in. We have to write custom logic to support it.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Including Ti.cloud causes the code processor to crash
Description: """"Ti.cloud is a special module since it's CommonJS but """"""""automagically"""""""" linked in. We have to write custom logic to support it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11910,12,"""iOS: WebView - rendering issue after remote URL is opened""","""""""Description:  While testing Web view, I noticed rendering problem when page content is changing. There is a partial black screen appearance before the next view displayed. It happens on iPhone5 and iPad mini with iOS 6.0. iPad3,4 do not have this issue. This issue disappears after pinch/zoom of the view.  *not a regression*, occurs in 2.1.4 looks like devices specific.  Test stept:  1. Run the code below:    2. Watch a view behavior.  Actual result:  Black screen appearance before view change.    Expected:  Proper render of views.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: WebView - rendering issue after remote URL is opened
Description: """"Description: While testing Web view, I noticed rendering problem when page content is changing. There is a partial black screen appearance before the next view displayed. It happens on iPhone5 and iPad mini with iOS 6.0. iPad3,4 do not have this issue. This issue disappears after pinch/zoom of the view. *not a regression*, occurs in 2.1.4 looks like devices specific. Test stept: 1. Run the code below: 2. Watch a view behavior. Actual result: Black screen appearance before view change. Expected: Proper render of views.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11908,12,"""CodeProcessor: Beef up the analysis coverage plugin""","""""""We can make the analysis coverage plugin much more useful by doing the following:  * Report nodes skipped (i.e. nodes that we knowingly did not <USER>. This will make it easier to determine which nodes were not analyzed improperly  * Create document maps that show what was and what was not analyzed for easy visualization.  * Determine and report which files were not analyzed that had the possibility of being analyzed (i.e. files not in Resources/<platform not being analyzed>)    This should help considerably in dealing with situations where the code processor is not analyzing code for no apparent reason""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Beef up the analysis coverage plugin
Description: """"We can make the analysis coverage plugin much more useful by doing the following: * Report nodes skipped (i.e. nodes that we knowingly did not <USER>. This will make it easier to determine which nodes were not analyzed improperly * Create document maps that show what was and what was not analyzed for easy visualization. * Determine and report which files were not analyzed that had the possibility of being analyzed (i.e. files not in Resources/<platform not being analyzed>) This should help considerably in dealing with situations where the code processor is not analyzing code for no apparent reason""""",title+description
