TIMOB-11882,12,"""Android r21: emulator deploy with r21 clean install fails with 'WVGA854' is not a valid skin name or size (NNNxMMM)""","""""""When Titanium Project is run on Android Emulator, emulator fails to create with errors:        When I switched the Android SDK to r20 w/update to r21, the issue went away. I deleted the .android/avds and could no longer reproduce the issue with the clean install of r21.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Download Android SDK r21 from scratch.  2. Open Studio, Create Project, Run Project in Emulator.    Actual Result:    skin errors    Expected Result:    Emulator creates and app runs without error.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android r21: emulator deploy with r21 clean install fails with 'WVGA854' is not a valid skin name or size (NNNxMMM)
Description: """"When Titanium Project is run on Android Emulator, emulator fails to create with errors: When I switched the Android SDK to r20 w/update to r21, the issue went away. I deleted the .android/avds and could no longer reproduce the issue with the clean install of r21. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Download Android SDK r21 from scratch. 2. Open Studio, Create Project, Run Project in Emulator. Actual Result: skin errors Expected Result: Emulator creates and app runs without error.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11881,12,"""Android: applicationCacheDirectory still exists after uninstall""","""""""h6.Issue  Uninstalling app did not help, the directory with application cache files is still there. It will happen on devices that     h6.Tested on  - Doesn't appear to happen on Razr 2.3.5 (app was saved at Internal Storage).  - It does appear on Samsung Galaxy Note 2.3 (app got installed on SD Card)    h6.Expected   Cache directory got wiped out after uninstalling the app.    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Install and run Codestrong 2012 app on Android,   2. uninstall.   3. Using File browser, go to */Android/data/com.<USER>codestrong2012* and notice that cache directory including *cache/_tmp/remote-cache* still exists.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: applicationCacheDirectory still exists after uninstall
Description: """"h6.Issue Uninstalling app did not help, the directory with application cache files is still there. It will happen on devices that h6.Tested on - Doesn't appear to happen on Razr 2.3.5 (app was saved at Internal Storage). - It does appear on Samsung Galaxy Note 2.3 (app got installed on SD Card) h6.Expected Cache directory got wiped out after uninstalling the app. h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Install and run Codestrong 2012 app on Android, 2. uninstall. 3. Using File browser, go to */Android/data/com.<USER>codestrong2012* and notice that cache directory including *cache/_tmp/remote-cache* still exists. """"",title+description
