TIMOB-11876,12,"""iOS 6: Drop shadow in navigation bar cannot be disabled through Titanium""","""""""*Feature description*  iOS 6 automatically adds drop shadow to the navigation bar that cannot be disabled through Titanium (2.1.3).    *Proposed solution*  See the objective-c solution here: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/11084331/how-do-i-disable-the-navigation-bar-shadow-in-ios-6-for-navigation-bars-with-cus    controller.navigationBar.shadowImage = [[[UIImage alloc] init] autorelease];  controller is a UINavigationController.    This should driven by a Property that we can enable disable on Window(?) or on NavigationGroup. Whatever makes more sense.   """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS 6: Drop shadow in navigation bar cannot be disabled through Titanium
Description: """"*Feature description* iOS 6 automatically adds drop shadow to the navigation bar that cannot be disabled through Titanium (2.1.3). *Proposed solution* See the objective-c solution here: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/11084331/how-do-i-disable-the-navigation-bar-shadow-in-ios-6-for-navigation-bars-with-cus controller.navigationBar.shadowImage = [[[UIImage alloc] init] autorelease]; controller is a UINavigationController. This should driven by a Property that we can enable disable on Window(?) or on NavigationGroup. Whatever makes more sense. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11875,12,"""CLI: Unable to package for iOS distribution using non-default keychain""","""""""Studio runs the following command to distribute for adhoc using a non-default keychain:    """"""""/usr/local/bin/titanium"""""""" """"""""--no-banner"""""""" """"""""--no-colors"""""""" """"""""--no-prompt"""""""" """"""""build"""""""" """"""""--platform"""""""" """"""""ios"""""""" """"""""--sdk"""""""" """"""""3.0.0.v20121121161553"""""""" """"""""--log-level"""""""" """"""""trace"""""""" """"""""--project-dir"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Documents/Titanium_Studio_Workspace_test/adsfasdfasd"""""""" """"""""--build-type"""""""" """"""""production"""""""" """"""""--distribution-name"""""""" """"""""<USER>"""""" """"""""--ios-version"""""""" """"""""5.1"""""""" """"""""--keychain"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Library/Keychains/login.keychain"""""""" """"""""--output-dir"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Downloads/gggggg"""""""" """"""""--pp-uuid"""""""" """"""""7FAA87EF-238D-4356-AC3F-55DE3614DA7D"""""""" """"""""--target"""""""" """"""""dist-adhoc""""""""    The result is the following error:  [ERROR] :  ** BUILD FAILED **  [ERROR] :  The following build commands failed:  [ERROR] :   Check dependencies  [ERROR] :  (1 failure)  [ERROR] :  Error details: unsupported build action '/Users/<USER>Library/Keychains/login.keychain'  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Unable to package for iOS distribution using non-default keychain
Description: """"Studio runs the following command to distribute for adhoc using a non-default keychain: """"""""/usr/local/bin/titanium"""""""" """"""""--no-banner"""""""" """"""""--no-colors"""""""" """"""""--no-prompt"""""""" """"""""build"""""""" """"""""--platform"""""""" """"""""ios"""""""" """"""""--sdk"""""""" """"""""3.0.0.v20121121161553"""""""" """"""""--log-level"""""""" """"""""trace"""""""" """"""""--project-dir"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Documents/Titanium_Studio_Workspace_test/adsfasdfasd"""""""" """"""""--build-type"""""""" """"""""production"""""""" """"""""--distribution-name"""""""" """"""""<USER>"""""" """"""""--ios-version"""""""" """"""""5.1"""""""" """"""""--keychain"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Library/Keychains/login.keychain"""""""" """"""""--output-dir"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Downloads/gggggg"""""""" """"""""--pp-uuid"""""""" """"""""7FAA87EF-238D-4356-AC3F-55DE3614DA7D"""""""" """"""""--target"""""""" """"""""dist-adhoc"""""""" The result is the following error: [ERROR] :  ** BUILD FAILED ** [ERROR] :  The following build commands failed: [ERROR] :   Check dependencies [ERROR] :  (1 failure) [ERROR] :  Error details: unsupported build action '/Users/<USER>Library/Keychains/login.keychain' """"",title+description
TIMOB-11874,12,"""Android & iOS: PersistentHttpClient""","""""""*Feature description*  In a project of mine I needed a persistent HTTP connection (called comet session). The existing HttpClient doesn't support persistent connection (continuous ondatastream). So I implemented a PersistentHttpClient.    *Pull request*  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/2844""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android & iOS: PersistentHttpClient
Description: """"*Feature description* In a project of mine I needed a persistent HTTP connection (called comet session). The existing HttpClient doesn't support persistent connection (continuous ondatastream). So I implemented a PersistentHttpClient. *Pull request* https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/2844""""",title+description
TIMOB-11873,12,"""iOS: Custom Label in Button stays in highlightedColor state once button is released.""","""""""*Actual result*  Adding a label to a button, with a color and highlightedColor will initially work, and show the highlightedColor on press. But on release it remains in the highlightedColor, and does not revert back to the color. If you press and drag off the button, you can sometimes get the color back.    *Test case*  This is reproducible in the kitchen sink example of custom label button. (Once pressed the label stays green and does not revert back to red).    *Workaround*  It looks like something changed in iOS 6 with the event cycle for the button.  In TiUIButton : - (void)controlAction:(id)sender forEvent:(UIEvent *)event    It sets the highlighted state of child views to button.highlighted.  However, in this controlAction method, button.highlighted appears to always be true, regardless of   the touch.phase. So the label will never be told to to remove its highlighted state.    I fixed this by manually setting the state on child views:      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Custom Label in Button stays in highlightedColor state once button is released.
Description: """"*Actual result* Adding a label to a button, with a color and highlightedColor will initially work, and show the highlightedColor on press. But on release it remains in the highlightedColor, and does not revert back to the color. If you press and drag off the button, you can sometimes get the color back. *Test case* This is reproducible in the kitchen sink example of custom label button. (Once pressed the label stays green and does not revert back to red). *Workaround* It looks like something changed in iOS 6 with the event cycle for the button. In TiUIButton : - (void)controlAction:(id)sender forEvent:(UIEvent *)event It sets the highlighted state of child views to button.highlighted. However, in this controlAction method, button.highlighted appears to always be true, regardless of the touch.phase. So the label will never be told to to remove its highlighted state. I fixed this by manually setting the state on child views: """"",title+description
TIMOB-11872,12,"""iOS: Nimbus framework integration""","""""""Nimbus kit is a great framework for ios development  You can find it [here|http://nimbuskit.info/]    By using it we could get feature very close to android, and would gain much time implementing new features.  For example html property for label  http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusAttributedLabel.html    or photoAlbum like gallery on android  http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusPhotos.html    Improved webview with toolbar  http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusWebController.html    We could also use to better manage network images  http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusNetworkImage.html    NiAttributeLabel already handle textalign and verticalAlign    And we could even think about using their great models to improve tableview management  http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/TableViewModels.html    I was about to start integrating it in my branch to get html property in labels, but i thought it was a better idea to first talk about it here.    What do you think?  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Nimbus framework integration
Description: """"Nimbus kit is a great framework for ios development You can find it [here|http://nimbuskit.info/] By using it we could get feature very close to android, and would gain much time implementing new features. For example html property for label http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusAttributedLabel.html or photoAlbum like gallery on android http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusPhotos.html Improved webview with toolbar http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusWebController.html We could also use to better manage network images http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/NimbusNetworkImage.html NiAttributeLabel already handle textalign and verticalAlign And we could even think about using their great models to improve tableview management http://latest.docs.nimbuskit.info/TableViewModels.html I was about to start integrating it in my branch to get html property in labels, but i thought it was a better idea to first talk about it here. What do you think? """"",title+description
