TIMOB-11801,12,"""iOS: Window height increases by iPad status bar height when camera or full screen window atop rotates""","""""""h3. Issue    Window increases in height by the height of the iPad status bar (20px) when a """"""""fullscreen"""""""" window is opened on top and rotated. It also increases when the camera view is opened and rotated.    h3. Sample Code        h3. Steps to Reproduce    1) Start the app  2) Notice the red footer 20 pixels above the ipad simulator's window bottom that is black  3) Rotate the iPad (device or simulator)  4) The 20 pixel height is maintained  5) Tap the """"""""fullscreen window"""""""" button  6) Rotate  7) Tap [close] button  8) The 20 pixel height area is gone  9) Rotate again and the 20 pixel height area reappears    Same issue also occurs with the camera overlay (code included in the sample)   """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window height increases by iPad status bar height when camera or full screen window atop rotates
Description: """"h3. Issue Window increases in height by the height of the iPad status bar (20px) when a """"""""fullscreen"""""""" window is opened on top and rotated. It also increases when the camera view is opened and rotated. h3. Sample Code h3. Steps to Reproduce 1) Start the app 2) Notice the red footer 20 pixels above the ipad simulator's window bottom that is black 3) Rotate the iPad (device or simulator) 4) The 20 pixel height is maintained 5) Tap the """"""""fullscreen window"""""""" button 6) Rotate 7) Tap [close] button 8) The 20 pixel height area is gone 9) Rotate again and the 20 pixel height area reappears Same issue also occurs with the camera overlay (code included in the sample) """"",title+description
TIMOB-11800,12,"""TIAPI:  Rework borders for views""","""""""Borders for views look different for iOS and Android.  This is due to the difference of how it is implemented.  We need to have a parity discussion and write out a spec on how it should work.  An example of this can be found on the screenshots here: http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-11020    Android has run into a couple of problems with border views that should be addressed when we rework the borders on views.  For example:  http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-11222  """"""",New Feature,"Title: TIAPI: Rework borders for views
Description: """"Borders for views look different for iOS and Android. This is due to the difference of how it is implemented. We need to have a parity discussion and write out a spec on how it should work. An example of this can be found on the screenshots here: http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-11020 Android has run into a couple of problems with border views that should be addressed when we rework the borders on views. For example: http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-11222 """"",title+description
TIMOB-11799,12,"""Android: Galaxy Nexus with Jelly Bean 4.2 changed the /sdcard symlink and mount points, breaking our builder.py""","""""""h3. Fail / Test Case    With the mentioned device and Android version:    # Create a new Titanium app (any template is okay).  # Build the app for testing on the device (don't package it for distribution: just build it to test on device.)  # The build will get hung up on """"""""Waiting for SDCard to become available"""""""".  Eventually it will continue and finish building.    When testing the fix, the build should not get hung up on Waiting for SDCard.  Please also test on a non-Galaxy Nexus to confirm this has caused no regressions.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Galaxy Nexus with Jelly Bean 4.2 changed the /sdcard symlink and mount points, breaking our builder.py
Description: """"h3. Fail / Test Case With the mentioned device and Android version: # Create a new Titanium app (any template is okay). # Build the app for testing on the device (don't package it for distribution: just build it to test on device.) # The build will get hung up on """"""""Waiting for SDCard to become available"""""""". Eventually it will continue and finish building. When testing the fix, the build should not get hung up on Waiting for SDCard. Please also test on a non-Galaxy Nexus to confirm this has caused no regressions.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11798,12,"""Android: Allow setting action bar properties before window is opened""","""""""It would be nice if we could specify action bar properties in advance, the way we specify activity properties (such as onCreateOptionsMenu) on an activity before it's created.    For the activity, we create an empty object (I think) that we can set properties on until the real activity exists, at which point the properties are copied to the new activity. Or something like that.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Allow setting action bar properties before window is opened
Description: """"It would be nice if we could specify action bar properties in advance, the way we specify activity properties (such as onCreateOptionsMenu) on an activity before it's created. For the activity, we create an empty object (I think) that we can set properties on until the real activity exists, at which point the properties are copied to the new activity. Or something like that. """"",title+description
