TIMOB-11783,12,"""CodeProcessor: Refactor Base into true separate files""","""""""Right now, Base is written in separate files that get assembled into one enormous JavaScript file. This approach was taken for historical reasons and is no longer necessary. Splitting into multiple files will make debugging easier, could increase performance a bit, and is just generally a good idea for maintenance.""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Refactor Base into true separate files
Description: """"Right now, Base is written in separate files that get assembled into one enormous JavaScript file. This approach was taken for historical reasons and is no longer necessary. Splitting into multiple files will make debugging easier, could increase performance a bit, and is just generally a good idea for maintenance.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11782,12,"""iOS: Kitchensink - Pinch and zoom is enabled even on clicking 'Remove pinch' button given on the window.""","""""""  Kitchensink > views > View Gestures.  Pinch and zoom is enabled even on clicking 'Remove pinch' button given on the window.    Test steps  1:Pinch and zoom on the image(titanium ribbon)  2:Press on remove pinch    Expected result  1:Should be able to pinch and zoom the image  2:Should not be able to pinch and zoom the images    Actual: Able to pinch and zoom images even after pressing 'remove pinch' button.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchensink - Pinch and zoom is enabled even on clicking 'Remove pinch' button given on the window.
Description: """" Kitchensink > views > View Gestures. Pinch and zoom is enabled even on clicking 'Remove pinch' button given on the window. Test steps 1:Pinch and zoom on the image(titanium ribbon) 2:Press on remove pinch Expected result 1:Should be able to pinch and zoom the image 2:Should not be able to pinch and zoom the images Actual: Able to pinch and zoom images even after pressing 'remove pinch' button. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11781,12,"""CLI: titanium build for android cannot detect the Android SDK targets even when they are available""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create an application  2. Run """"""""titanium build""""""""  3. type """"""""android""""""""    Actual:  [ERROR] Unable to detect Android SDK targets.    Please download SDK targets via Android SDK Manager and try again. (version 2.2 or newer)    Expected:  To build the android application""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: titanium build for android cannot detect the Android SDK targets even when they are available
