TIMOB-11777,12,"""Kitchen Sink: Views - Auto Size unexpected behavior on continuous  device rotation""","""""""Description:  While testing Auto Size I noticed that an image changes size (increases) every time the device is rotated.     *Not a regression, occurs on 2.1.4 and 2.1.3*    Test steps:  1. Run Kitchen Sink > Base UI > Web Views > Auto Size on iOS devices  2. Rotate device continuously    Actual result:  View increases in size     Expected:  The image should autosize to fit the screen and orientation      """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen Sink: Views - Auto Size unexpected behavior on continuous device rotation
Description: """"Description: While testing Auto Size I noticed that an image changes size (increases) every time the device is rotated. *Not a regression, occurs on 2.1.4 and 2.1.3* Test steps: 1. Run Kitchen Sink > Base UI > Web Views > Auto Size on iOS devices 2. Rotate device continuously Actual result: View increases in size Expected: The image should autosize to fit the screen and orientation """"",title+description
TIMOB-11776,12,"""CLI: Could not find all required Titanium Modules: ti.cloud if Titanium SDK not in default location""","""""""Can't build project containing modules if cli is enabled and sdk path is in non-default location.    This is a regression. It works from the old cli.    .titanium/config.json        Note: Setting paths.modules had no effect (either for '.../titanium' or '.../titanium/modules').    Steps to Reproduce:    Note: Steps 1-3 are meant to configure a Titanium SDK in a non-standard location.    1. Move Titanium SDK to the Desktop (e.g., Desktop/Titanium/<modules & mobilesdk>).  2. Set Titanium SDK in Studio Preferences to new location.  3. Add titanium path to .titanium/config.json (see above, or use 'titanium config paths.sdk <Titanium>' command in terminal).    4. Create Titanium Project w/ACS Enabled.  5. Run Project in SDK 3.0.0+.    Actual Result:    Command (in Studio):        Error:        Expected Result:    Same result as old CLI, which is success.    Old Python Command (in Studio):    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Could not find all required Titanium Modules: ti.cloud if Titanium SDK not in default location
Description: """"Can't build project containing modules if cli is enabled and sdk path is in non-default location. This is a regression. It works from the old cli. .titanium/config.json Note: Setting paths.modules had no effect (either for '.../titanium' or '.../titanium/modules'). Steps to Reproduce: Note: Steps 1-3 are meant to configure a Titanium SDK in a non-standard location. 1. Move Titanium SDK to the Desktop (e.g., Desktop/Titanium/<modules & mobilesdk>). 2. Set Titanium SDK in Studio Preferences to new location. 3. Add titanium path to .titanium/config.json (see above, or use 'titanium config paths.sdk <Titanium>' command in terminal). 4. Create Titanium Project w/ACS Enabled. 5. Run Project in SDK 3.0.0+. Actual Result: Command (in Studio): Error: Expected Result: Same result as old CLI, which is success. Old Python Command (in Studio): """"",title+description
TIMOB-11775,12,"""KitchenSink: Play Movie - """"Event PlaybackState Fired"""" returns """"undefined""""""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink Play Movie Local I noticed that """"""""Event PlaybackState Fired"""""""" returns """"""""undefined"""""""" value.    This is a regression, does not occur on 2.1.4.    Steps:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Phone - Play Movie - Local  3. Check the console    Actual:  Ti.API.info: Event PlaybackState Fired: 'undefined'    Expected:  Ti.API.info: Event PlaybackState Fired: '+e.playbackState'""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Play Movie - """"Event PlaybackState Fired"""" returns """"undefined""""
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink Play Movie Local I noticed that """"""""Event PlaybackState Fired"""""""" returns """"""""undefined"""""""" value. This is a regression, does not occur on 2.1.4. Steps: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Phone - Play Movie - Local 3. Check the console Actual: Ti.API.info: Event PlaybackState Fired: 'undefined' Expected: Ti.API.info: Event PlaybackState Fired: '+e.playbackState'""""",title+description
