TIMOB-11712,12,"""Andoid: Background Images Load Four Times Acording to FastDev""","""""""Make a simple window, set its background image to anything, compile it with 2.1.0 or 2.1.1, and watch the fastdev console. You will see that every background image loads four times. When an animation completes, it again loads the images four times. I do not know if this is android specific. http://developer.<USER>com/question/140652/andoid-background-images-load-4-times""""""",Bug,"Title: Andoid: Background Images Load Four Times Acording to FastDev
Description: """"Make a simple window, set its background image to anything, compile it with 2.1.0 or 2.1.1, and watch the fastdev console. You will see that every background image loads four times. When an animation completes, it again loads the images four times. I do not know if this is android specific. http://developer.<USER>com/question/140652/andoid-background-images-load-4-times""""",title+description
TIMOB-11711,12,"""KitchenSink: Phone - Unable to play full screen movie on iPad with iOS 6.0 ""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink, I wasn't able to zoom in view to make it a full screen.   *It happens  on iPad with iOS 6.0 only.Not a regression, occurs on 2.1.3*  It is possible to use zoom in on iOS lower then 6.0.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Build KS   2) Install on iPad iOS 6.0  3) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Local  4) Start movie playback  5) Zoom in    Result:  Unable to zoom in    Expected:  Should be able to zoom in   """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Phone - Unable to play full screen movie on iPad with iOS 6.0
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, I wasn't able to zoom in view to make it a full screen. *It happens on iPad with iOS 6.0 only.Not a regression, occurs on 2.1.3* It is possible to use zoom in on iOS lower then 6.0. Steps to reproduce: 1) Build KS 2) Install on iPad iOS 6.0 3) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Local 4) Start movie playback 5) Zoom in Result: Unable to zoom in Expected: Should be able to zoom in """"",title+description
TIMOB-11710,12,"""CLI build failure reason is only available when tracing is on""","""""""When launching the build command to perform an iOS debug on device, the error log output a generic error """"""""Check dependencies"""""""", but does not output the real error reason.    For example:      The TRACE is actually indicating the error, not the ERROR. So, in case the CLI command is executed with an 'Error' log level, the user never gets the reason.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI build failure reason is only available when tracing is on
Description: """"When launching the build command to perform an iOS debug on device, the error log output a generic error """"""""Check dependencies"""""""", but does not output the real error reason. For example: The TRACE is actually indicating the error, not the ERROR. So, in case the CLI command is executed with an 'Error' log level, the user never gets the reason.""""",title+description
