TIMOB-11682,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, launching test in landscape mode causes  dashboard being open in portrait mode""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, I entered the test in landscape mode and the dashboard view had opened in portrat mode. Entering test in portrait mode and rotating device does not change orientation, it keeps portrait mode. Also Views button can be pressed from landscape, and layout will be changed respectively.  Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Rotate device to Landscape orientation  3) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Dashboard view  4) Launch test  Result:  Portrait mode  Expected:  Icons should appear in landscape mode.  Notes:  *not a regression, occurs in 2.1.3*  *This does not occur on iPad mini, only on iPad2,3,4*""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, launching test in landscape mode causes dashboard being open in portrait mode
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, I entered the test in landscape mode and the dashboard view had opened in portrat mode. Entering test in portrait mode and rotating device does not change orientation, it keeps portrait mode. Also Views button can be pressed from landscape, and layout will be changed respectively. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Rotate device to Landscape orientation 3) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Dashboard view 4) Launch test Result: Portrait mode Expected: Icons should appear in landscape mode. Notes: *not a regression, occurs in 2.1.3* *This does not occur on iPad mini, only on iPad2,3,4*""""",title+description
