Description: """"If keys in strings.xml contain a . (dot) the values are not displayed on android. On iOS it works fine. This is not well documented in http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.1/index.html#!/guide/Internationalization-section-29004892_Internationalization-Resourcefilestructure""""",title+description
TIMOB-11680,12,"""Add command line service (provisioner.py) to load multiple iOS provisioning profiles""","""""""Studio runs the provisioner.py to load provisioning profiles on a user's system. For systems that have a multiple provisioning profiles, Xcode has to start/stop for each profile. The provisioner.py (or CLI command) needs to support a list of provisioning profiles.""""""",Story,"Title: Add command line service (provisioner.py) to load multiple iOS provisioning profiles
Description: """"Studio runs the provisioner.py to load provisioning profiles on a user's system. For systems that have a multiple provisioning profiles, Xcode has to start/stop for each profile. The provisioner.py (or CLI command) needs to support a list of provisioning profiles.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11679,12,"""Android: Text field triggers """"focus"""" event of TiUIWindow""","""""""h2. Problem description    If window has """"""""focus"""""""" event listener attached and it contains text fields, text fields triggers window's focus event.              h2. Sample code        Clicking on the textFields not focused, the windows 'focus' event listener is triggered.              h6. Expected behavior:  Text fields 'focus' event listener should not be triggered in this case""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Text field triggers """"focus"""" event of TiUIWindow
Description: """"h2. Problem description If window has """"""""focus"""""""" event listener attached and it contains text fields, text fields triggers window's focus event. h2. Sample code Clicking on the textFields not focused, the windows 'focus' event listener is triggered. h6. Expected behavior: Text fields 'focus' event listener should not be triggered in this case""""",title+description
TIMOB-11678,12,"""CLI: iOS: iPad Simulator launches as iPhone Simulator""","""""""This is regression issue. With 2.1.2 Studio and latest SDK, iPAD Simulator launches.  Steps To Reproduce:  1. Install Studio 3.0 latest version with latest SDK and plugins.  2. Create a default app.  3. Run same app using iPAD Simulator    Actual: App launches in iPhone Simulator.  Expected: App must launch in iPAD Simulator.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS: iPad Simulator launches as iPhone Simulator
Description: """"This is regression issue. With 2.1.2 Studio and latest SDK, iPAD Simulator launches. Steps To Reproduce: 1. Install Studio 3.0 latest version with latest SDK and plugins. 2. Create a default app. 3. Run same app using iPAD Simulator Actual: App launches in iPhone Simulator. Expected: App must launch in iPAD Simulator.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11677,12,"""iOS: Subversion folders are present in iOS distribution build package""","""""""h3. Issue    Projects downloaded from svn and packaged for distribution have Subversion .svn folders present in the builds. This is the case building through both titanium.py script or from the """"""""publish"""""""" option from Titanium Studio.    h3. Steps to Reproduce    1. Create a new project in Titanium Studio.  2. Commit that project to a Subversion repository.  3. Delete the project from Titanium Studio.  4. Checkout the project from Subversion.  5. Import the project into Titanium Studio.  6. Create a distribution build.    Now, view the contents of the bundle. There are Subversion folders (.svn) present in the distribution application.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Subversion folders are present in iOS distribution build package
Description: """"h3. Issue Projects downloaded from svn and packaged for distribution have Subversion .svn folders present in the builds. This is the case building through both titanium.py script or from the """"""""publish"""""""" option from Titanium Studio. h3. Steps to Reproduce 1. Create a new project in Titanium Studio. 2. Commit that project to a Subversion repository. 3. Delete the project from Titanium Studio. 4. Checkout the project from Subversion. 5. Import the project into Titanium Studio. 6. Create a distribution build. Now, view the contents of the bundle. There are Subversion folders (.svn) present in the distribution application.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11676,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink - the search bar failed  to return the screen's  width after orientation was changed""","""""""Description:  While testing Kitchen sink, the search bar does not resize when rotating the device to landscape then back to portrait. Not a regression, did occur in 2.1.3  Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS   2) Launch KS > Base UI > Views > Table Views > Headers with Filter  3) Rotate the device to landscape  Searchbar autofill  size of the screen.  3) Rotate the device back to portrait  Actual result:  Searchbar is shorter then the width of the screen. See screenshots.  Expected:  Searchbar resizes based on orientation.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink - the search bar failed to return the screen's width after orientation was changed
Description: """"Description: While testing Kitchen sink, the search bar does not resize when rotating the device to landscape then back to portrait. Not a regression, did occur in 2.1.3 Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 2) Launch KS > Base UI > Views > Table Views > Headers with Filter 3) Rotate the device to landscape Searchbar autofill size of the screen. 3) Rotate the device back to portrait Actual result: Searchbar is shorter then the width of the screen. See screenshots. Expected: Searchbar resizes based on orientation.""""",title+description
