Description: """"An application with tabgroup which has more than one tab with a mapview, crashes when the second tab with mapview is opened This is not a regression. The issue occurs as atleast as far as 2.1.1 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an application with code below and launch the application 2. Click on Tab2 Actual Result: After Step1: Application opens up with mapview shown in tab1 After step2: Application crashes. (refer to the attached error logs) Expected Result: After Step 2, the application should not crash and tab2 with mapview should be shown """"",title+description
TIMOB-11662,12,"""Android: Debugger: can't step-into win.open to view win.url javascript file""","""""""Can't step-into win.open() to view win.url javascript file. However any breakpoints in the file are hit.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code in Debug mode:    app.js        module.js        2. Add a breakpoint near the beginning and step-over unti you hit win.open();  3. Step into win.open();    Actual Result:    Skips over win.url javascript file. There seems to be no way to debug into this file without pre-existing breakpoints in the file.    Expected Result:    Stepping into win.open() seems like it should hit the first line of the win.url javascript file ('module.js').""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Debugger: can't step-into win.open to view win.url javascript file
Description: """"Can't step-into win.open() to view win.url javascript file. However any breakpoints in the file are hit. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code in Debug mode: app.js module.js 2. Add a breakpoint near the beginning and step-over unti you hit win.open(); 3. Step into win.open(); Actual Result: Skips over win.url javascript file. There seems to be no way to debug into this file without pre-existing breakpoints in the file. Expected Result: Stepping into win.open() seems like it should hit the first line of the win.url javascript file ('module.js').""""",title+description
