TIMOB-11597,12,"""Android: Action bar displays differently based on launch orientation""","""""""The Action bar doesn't appear to handle orientation changes correctly. For example, if I specify an action item (menu item) with an icon and        The text shows up only if the app is launched in landscape orientation, and doesn't go away if the app is rotated into portrait orientation. On the other hand, if I launch the app in portrait, only the icon is displayed, even when I rotate into landscape.    On a related topic, the app icon is displayed larger when I launch in landscape mode. It appears that we use two different sizes, one for the stacked action bar and one for the ordinary portrait-mode action bar. I'm not sure if this behavior is correct in the first place--I can't see a reference to it in the Android docs. However, both versions seem to be scaled differently based on whether it's launched in portrait or landscape, which is definitely wrong.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Action bar displays differently based on launch orientation
Description: """"The Action bar doesn't appear to handle orientation changes correctly. For example, if I specify an action item (menu item) with an icon and The text shows up only if the app is launched in landscape orientation, and doesn't go away if the app is rotated into portrait orientation. On the other hand, if I launch the app in portrait, only the icon is displayed, even when I rotate into landscape. On a related topic, the app icon is displayed larger when I launch in landscape mode. It appears that we use two different sizes, one for the stacked action bar and one for the ordinary portrait-mode action bar. I'm not sure if this behavior is correct in the first place--I can't see a reference to it in the Android docs. However, both versions seem to be scaled differently based on whether it's launched in portrait or landscape, which is definitely wrong. """"",title+description
