TIMOB-11533,12,"""CLI: creating an application from terminal creates the project with just the resource folder at your current location""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create Test directory on desktop  2. cd to that directory  3. Run titanium create  4. Create the application on ~/Desktop    Actual:  In the Test directory you will have a project folder with just the resource folder    Expected:  To only create the project directory on desktop and not a partial one in your current directory""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: creating an application from terminal creates the project with just the resource folder at your current location
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create Test directory on desktop 2. cd to that directory 3. Run titanium create 4. Create the application on ~/Desktop Actual: In the Test directory you will have a project folder with just the resource folder Expected: To only create the project directory on desktop and not a partial one in your current directory""""",title+description
TIMOB-11532,12,"""CLI: combining options from all the SDK causes problems""","""""""Steps To Reproduce  1. Install various 3.x builds  2. run titanium build -h    Actual:  You get options from old sdks that have been removed from the new one    Expected:  Should not load all the options and commands from previous builds    Note:  It is a problem when you have failures from previous builds. ie: TIMOB-11481, couldn't build until you remove all the old builds""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: combining options from all the SDK causes problems
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce 1. Install various 3.x builds 2. run titanium build -h Actual: You get options from old sdks that have been removed from the new one Expected: Should not load all the options and commands from previous builds Note: It is a problem when you have failures from previous builds. ie: TIMOB-11481, couldn't build until you remove all the old builds""""",title+description
TIMOB-11531,12,"""CLI: iOS: Modules - Cannot install modules onto iOS""","""""""Details: If you install an app to an iOS device with either an iOS module or CommonJS module, then the app will not be able to find the module.  \\ \\  *Note:*  You *can* install an app to an Android device with either an Android module or CommonJS module  This bug does not appear in SDK build 2.1.3  \\ \\  Steps to reproduce:  1. Download monkeyModule.zip attachment  2. Unzip attachment and import project into TiStudio  3. Make sure to add the ti.cloud module in tiapp.xml (TISTUD-2564)  \\ \\  -4. Install app to iOS device-  -Actual: During installation of app, console will print out this error message:-    \\ \\  4. Launch app on iOS device  Actual: iOS cannot find module (see no_module.png)  \\ \\  Expected: Should be able to install apps with modules  \\ \\  *Note:* To test with iOS module, in app.js, comment line 2 and uncomment line 3. Then repeat steps 4-5  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iOS: Modules - Cannot install modules onto iOS
Description: """"Details: If you install an app to an iOS device with either an iOS module or CommonJS module, then the app will not be able to find the module. \\ \\ *Note:* You *can* install an app to an Android device with either an Android module or CommonJS module This bug does not appear in SDK build 2.1.3 \\ \\ Steps to reproduce: 1. Download monkeyModule.zip attachment 2. Unzip attachment and import project into TiStudio 3. Make sure to add the ti.cloud module in tiapp.xml (TISTUD-2564) \\ \\ -4. Install app to iOS device- -Actual: During installation of app, console will print out this error message:- \\ \\ 4. Launch app on iOS device Actual: iOS cannot find module (see no_module.png) \\ \\ Expected: Should be able to install apps with modules \\ \\ *Note:* To test with iOS module, in app.js, comment line 2 and uncomment line 3. Then repeat steps 4-5 """"",title+description
