TIMOB-11527,12,"""iOS: View: Removing a view from ScrollView leaves a black view at first position""","""""""This is not a regression. It occurs since 2.1.1.    Steps to reproduce  1. Copy the code below in app.js and run the app    2. Click on any of the view,(except the first view in the top most row).     Expected result:  2. The touched view should be removed.The rest of the views should not be affected.    Actual result:  2. The touched view gets removed.It leaves a black view in the top row at the left corner, which is not a part of the scrollview.It should not be there.You can see it by scrolling the scrollview up and down. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: View: Removing a view from ScrollView leaves a black view at first position
Description: """"This is not a regression. It occurs since 2.1.1. Steps to reproduce 1. Copy the code below in app.js and run the app 2. Click on any of the view,(except the first view in the top most row). Expected result: 2. The touched view should be removed.The rest of the views should not be affected. Actual result: 2. The touched view gets removed.It leaves a black view in the top row at the left corner, which is not a part of the scrollview.It should not be there.You can see it by scrolling the scrollview up and down. """"",title+description
