TIMOB-11508,12,"""Android: Adding WebView to ScrollView causes ScrollView to be initialized scrolled-down""","""""""h3. Issue    When a WebView is added to a ScrollView containing multiple views stacked vertically, the scrollView get scrolled down to where the WebView has been added (bottom), causing the page to load with the ScrollView initially displaying Accounts near the bottom of the list.    h3. Sample Test case        *In iOS, the top most view is visible first.*""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Adding WebView to ScrollView causes ScrollView to be initialized scrolled-down
Description: """"h3. Issue When a WebView is added to a ScrollView containing multiple views stacked vertically, the scrollView get scrolled down to where the WebView has been added (bottom), causing the page to load with the ScrollView initially displaying Accounts near the bottom of the list. h3. Sample Test case *In iOS, the top most view is visible first.*""""",title+description
TIMOB-11505,12,"""Android: (V8 only) Using require() a second time for the same module returns undefined instead of cached module object.""","""""""Titanium Mobile 3.0.0, V8, any android version, any desktop os, any Studio version.    # Create a project and target 3.0.0.  # Put the attached module zip file in the project folder.  # Add the module to the project (i.e., edit tiapp.xml <modules> section appropriately).  # Make this the project's app.js:  {code:title=app.js}  require(""""""""ti.bertram"""""""").example();  require(""""""""ti.bertram"""""""").example();  {code}  # Run the project and you'll get the runtime error that you can't call """"""""example"""""""" of undefined.    This is a *regression* and is not present in 2.1.3.  The problem does not occur when Rhino is the runtime.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: (V8 only) Using require() a second time for the same module returns undefined instead of cached module object.
Description: """"Titanium Mobile 3.0.0, V8, any android version, any desktop os, any Studio version. # Create a project and target 3.0.0. # Put the attached module zip file in the project folder. # Add the module to the project (i.e., edit tiapp.xml <modules> section appropriately). # Make this the project's app.js: {code:title=app.js} require(""""""""ti.bertram"""""""").example(); require(""""""""ti.bertram"""""""").example(); {code} # Run the project and you'll get the runtime error that you can't call """"""""example"""""""" of undefined. This is a *regression* and is not present in 2.1.3. The problem does not occur when Rhino is the runtime.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11504,12,"""CLI: provide a change log page in git repo""","""""""When there is a CLI update detected in Studio, we would open an update dialog with release notes information (please see the screenshot in TISTUD-2441), but currently the content is hard-coded in Studio and pretty minimal. The suggestion is to have CLI provide a change log page that will get updated each time a new version is pushed. The link could be https://github.com/<USER>cli/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md, and the content could be something like the following:        """"""",Story,"Title: CLI: provide a change log page in git repo
Description: """"When there is a CLI update detected in Studio, we would open an update dialog with release notes information (please see the screenshot in TISTUD-2441), but currently the content is hard-coded in Studio and pretty minimal. The suggestion is to have CLI provide a change log page that will get updated each time a new version is pushed. The link could be https://github.com/<USER>cli/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md, and the content could be something like the following: """"",title+description
