TIMOB-11452,12,"""MobileWeb: Cannot animate element's bottom, right, or center properties""","""""""There's a number of things that are causing this to break. For starters, we simply do not allow bottom, right, and center to be animated. Second, even if we did, we don't query the current bottom, right, or center values properly.    The problem is partly solved by tinkering with the layout engine and part with the animation code. We may need to convert all bottom, right, and center animations to height/top or left/width based animations.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Cannot animate element's bottom, right, or center properties
Description: """"There's a number of things that are causing this to break. For starters, we simply do not allow bottom, right, and center to be animated. Second, even if we did, we don't query the current bottom, right, or center values properly. The problem is partly solved by tinkering with the layout engine and part with the animation code. We may need to convert all bottom, right, and center animations to height/top or left/width based animations.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11451,12,"""CLI: Don't require a debug host or port""","""""""The --debug-host option for iOS builds needs to support empty hosts and ports:    """"""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Don't require a debug host or port
Description: """"The --debug-host option for iOS builds needs to support empty hosts and ports: """"",title+description
TIMOB-11450,12,"""CLI: Scons fails if no write access to npm directory""","""""""When scons runs npm, it will fail if it can't write to the npm directory. This might be caused if installing the Titanium CLI first using sudo which might write lock files to the real user's npm directory as root.        This might be as simple as checking if the files are writeable and if not erroring.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Scons fails if no write access to npm directory
Description: """"When scons runs npm, it will fail if it can't write to the npm directory. This might be caused if installing the Titanium CLI first using sudo which might write lock files to the real user's npm directory as root. This might be as simple as checking if the files are writeable and if not erroring.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11444,12,"""CLI: TItanium build should not have --device-family option""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run """"""""titanium build -h""""""""    Actual:  -F, --device-family <value>                   the device family to build for  [iphone, ipad, universal]    Expected:  tiapp.xml should indicate if the project is iphone, ipad or universal and it is not set during the build level""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: TItanium build should not have --device-family option
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run """"""""titanium build -h"""""""" Actual: -F, --device-family <value> the device family to build for [iphone, ipad, universal] Expected: tiapp.xml should indicate if the project is iphone, ipad or universal and it is not set during the build level""""",title+description
TIMOB-11443,12,"""CLI: iPad needs to be a target platform when creating apps""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Run """"""""titanium create""""""""    Actual:  android,iphone,mobileweb    Expected:  iPad is not a target to create for and when loading the app to studio, iPad will not be supported""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: iPad needs to be a target platform when creating apps
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Run """"""""titanium create"""""""" Actual: android,iphone,mobileweb Expected: iPad is not a target to create for and when loading the app to studio, iPad will not be supported""""",title+description
TIMOB-11442,12,"""CLI: titanium build should not allow --deploy-type to be set""","""""""Steps to Reproduce  1. Run """"""""titanium build -h""""""""    Actual:  Allows for user to set --deploy-type    Expected:  Deploy type is hard coded and   Simulator = test  Device = development  Package = production    If we allow use to modify this it will ruin all the analytics""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: titanium build should not allow --deploy-type to be set
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce 1. Run """"""""titanium build -h"""""""" Actual: Allows for user to set --deploy-type Expected: Deploy type is hard coded and Simulator = test Device = development Package = production If we allow use to modify this it will ruin all the analytics""""",title+description
TIMOB-11441,12,"""iOS: Size of images placed inside Resources/iPhone folder increases by 30-40kb in the generated the ipa/app file""","""""""Create a new Titanium mobile project in Studio.  Note that the size of Default-Landscape.png file inside Resources/iPhone folder. Its 517kB.  Build the project in either simulator or device. Note the size of the generated image size. Its 544kB.    If the image size is around 1MB, the final image size is around 1.4MB which results in increase in size of ipa.    Screenshots of image sizes are attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Size of images placed inside Resources/iPhone folder increases by 30-40kb in the generated the ipa/app file
Description: """"Create a new Titanium mobile project in Studio. Note that the size of Default-Landscape.png file inside Resources/iPhone folder. Its 517kB. Build the project in either simulator or device. Note the size of the generated image size. Its 544kB. If the image size is around 1MB, the final image size is around 1.4MB which results in increase in size of ipa. Screenshots of image sizes are attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11440,12,"""CLI: titanium build mobile web flag is being ignored""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run """"""""titanium --platform mobileweb -B production    Actual:  [INFO] Compiling """"""""development"""""""" build    Expected:  [INFO] Compiling """"""""production"""""""" build    Workaround  1. Run """"""""titanium --platform mobileweb --deploy-type production""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: titanium build mobile web flag is being ignored
