TIMOB-11342,12,"""Android: ActionItems do not display correctly""","""""""Running the test code in TIMOB-9910 for ActionItems on a 4.0 device, the """"""""Expand"""""""" item that appears appears partly off-screen, below the action bar.    (This assumes that all of the manifest voodoo is setup correctly to run using the action bar and associated themes.)    In my other testing, adding a menu item with showAsAction set to ALWAYS, I'm getting nothing in the action bar, a menu button displayed in the bottom row (like the legacy menu button), which brings up the menu item in the same place--below the action bar and halfway off screen.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ActionItems do not display correctly
Description: """"Running the test code in TIMOB-9910 for ActionItems on a 4.0 device, the """"""""Expand"""""""" item that appears appears partly off-screen, below the action bar. (This assumes that all of the manifest voodoo is setup correctly to run using the action bar and associated themes.) In my other testing, adding a menu item with showAsAction set to ALWAYS, I'm getting nothing in the action bar, a menu button displayed in the bottom row (like the legacy menu button), which brings up the menu item in the same place--below the action bar and halfway off screen. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11341,12,"""Android: App build with targetSdkVersion > 11 should use newer themes""","""""""Setting tool-api-version and targetSdkVersion to something about 11 should let us use the device's built-in themes, but apps still show up in the old themes unless we override the themes explicitly. I added the following to the {{tiapp.xml}} file:        However, the app still looks old-style on a Nexus 7. For example, menu items are displayed in the options menu, not the action bar, even if showAsAction is set. And for that matter--no action bar.    Testing with the sample code for Action Items from TIMOB-9910.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: App build with targetSdkVersion > 11 should use newer themes
Description: """"Setting tool-api-version and targetSdkVersion to something about 11 should let us use the device's built-in themes, but apps still show up in the old themes unless we override the themes explicitly. I added the following to the {{tiapp.xml}} file: However, the app still looks old-style on a Nexus 7. For example, menu items are displayed in the options menu, not the action bar, even if showAsAction is set. And for that matter--no action bar. Testing with the sample code for Action Items from TIMOB-9910. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11340,12,"""Android: Can't add menu items to ActionBar-style tab group""","""""""In 3.0, we have support for ActionBar-based tabs and menu items.    However, to add a menu item to the action bar, we need to access the current activity. Attempting to access the window activity for the tab window doesn't work in 3.0, though it works in 2.X. Currently attempting to set the optionsmenu on the window activity in a tab group crashes for *both* 2.X and 4.X devices on 3.0.    Using Ti.Android.currentActivity fails in the same way.    I think there are two issues here:    * We don't seem to expose the activity associated with the tab group in any fashion I can see.  * We have a regression that is causing the following code to throw an exception in 3.0.        Tested with SDK 3.0.0.v20121009034227.  Nexus 7   Galaxy S 2 (2.3.6).    Error message is:      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Can't add menu items to ActionBar-style tab group
Description: """"In 3.0, we have support for ActionBar-based tabs and menu items. However, to add a menu item to the action bar, we need to access the current activity. Attempting to access the window activity for the tab window doesn't work in 3.0, though it works in 2.X. Currently attempting to set the optionsmenu on the window activity in a tab group crashes for *both* 2.X and 4.X devices on 3.0. Using Ti.Android.currentActivity fails in the same way. I think there are two issues here: * We don't seem to expose the activity associated with the tab group in any fashion I can see. * We have a regression that is causing the following code to throw an exception in 3.0. Tested with SDK 3.0.0.v20121009034227. Nexus 7 Galaxy S 2 (2.3.6). Error message is: """"",title+description
