TIMOB-11338,12,"""iOS6 on iPad: Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery doesn't work and blocks app""","""""""h1. Steps to reproduce the issue    # Execute the attached app.js  # Click the 'openPhotoGallery' button  # Close the first alert telling 'I will now call Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery'  # Notice there is no gallery opening  # Try to click the 'click me later' button  # Notice you cannot click it because the app (by some invisible layer?) is blocked""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS6 on iPad: Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery doesn't work and blocks app
Description: """"h1. Steps to reproduce the issue # Execute the attached app.js # Click the 'openPhotoGallery' button # Close the first alert telling 'I will now call Ti.Media.openPhotoGallery' # Notice there is no gallery opening # Try to click the 'click me later' button # Notice you cannot click it because the app (by some invisible layer?) is blocked""""",title+description
TIMOB-11337,12,"""iOS: Slide functionality of the master view over the detail view in a Split Window (like iPad mail App)""","""""""In a split window, there should be an option of sliding in and sliding out the master window when the Detail window is at the background. Just like in iPad mail app.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Slide functionality of the master view over the detail view in a Split Window (like iPad mail App)
Description: """"In a split window, there should be an option of sliding in and sliding out the master window when the Detail window is at the background. Just like in iPad mail app.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11336,12,"""Tooling: Device-specific Info.plist entries in tiapp.xml cause builder to fail""","""""""In 2.1, we introduced a new feature to add custom info.plist values directly into the tiapp.xml file, in place of the old hard-coded titanium-specific flags.    However, the new system lacks the ability to specify device-specific keys.    Specifies which interface orientations this application supports. In particular, we've introduced the UISupportedInterfaceOrientations key as an alternative to the older:        However, it's less functional than the previous version, because there's no way to specify a device type.    In the raw plist format, you can introduce a device specifier as a suffix to the device key:        However, adding code like this to the tiapp.xml file causes the build to fail with the following error:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: Device-specific Info.plist entries in tiapp.xml cause builder to fail
Description: """"In 2.1, we introduced a new feature to add custom info.plist values directly into the tiapp.xml file, in place of the old hard-coded titanium-specific flags. However, the new system lacks the ability to specify device-specific keys. Specifies which interface orientations this application supports. In particular, we've introduced the UISupportedInterfaceOrientations key as an alternative to the older: However, it's less functional than the previous version, because there's no way to specify a device type. In the raw plist format, you can introduce a device specifier as a suffix to the device key: However, adding code like this to the tiapp.xml file causes the build to fail with the following error: """"",title+description
TIMOB-11335,12,"""iOS: Table view row selected background doesn't fade out when backgroundGradient is set""","""""""*Expected behavior*  On touch end the selected background should fade out.    *Actual behavior*  On touch end the selected background disappears instantly and there is a delay period when the title text remains in selected state.    *Note*  Remove the backgroundGradient property and see that the selected background fades out as expected on touch end.    *Code*  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Table view row selected background doesn't fade out when backgroundGradient is set
Description: """"*Expected behavior* On touch end the selected background should fade out. *Actual behavior* On touch end the selected background disappears instantly and there is a delay period when the title text remains in selected state. *Note* Remove the backgroundGradient property and see that the selected background fades out as expected on touch end. *Code* """"",title+description
TIMOB-11334,12,"""iOS: Geolocation - Crash on app launch""","""""""While testing Geolocation Module I noticed crash on launch on *ios 5.1 - 5.1.1* with console [ERROR] The application has crashed with an uncaught exception 'NSRangeException'.    *It is a regression, does not occur on 2.1.3*    Test steps:  1. Run this code below    2. The log returns ERROR] The application has crashed with an uncaught exception 'NSRangeException'.   Reason:   *** -[__NSArrayI objectAtIndex:]: index 0 beyond bounds for empty array""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Geolocation - Crash on app launch
