TIMOB-11316,12,"""Mobile Web: distribution folder size has increased 0.1 MB from 2.1.3 SDKs to 3.0.X SDKs""","""""""This is a regression bug.  Mobile web distribution folder size in 2.1.3 SDK is 4.6MB    Steps To Reproduce:  1.Launch Titanium Studio.  2.Create > Titanium Project and select Deployment target as  > Mobile Web.  3.Select 'Publish' that project as > 'package - Mobile web.'  4.Select option : Copy mobile web app to a local file system. and browse to any desired folder path.  5.Make sure you have selected SDK as 3.0.0.v20121008225713  6.Verify mobile web folder size .    Actual: In 3.0 SDK build, folder size is 4.7MB whereas in 2.1.3 its size is 4.6MB""""""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web: distribution folder size has increased 0.1 MB from 2.1.3 SDKs to 3.0.X SDKs
Description: """"This is a regression bug. Mobile web distribution folder size in 2.1.3 SDK is 4.6MB Steps To Reproduce: 1.Launch Titanium Studio. 2.Create > Titanium Project and select Deployment target as > Mobile Web. 3.Select 'Publish' that project as > 'package - Mobile web.' 4.Select option : Copy mobile web app to a local file system. and browse to any desired folder path. 5.Make sure you have selected SDK as 3.0.0.v20121008225713 6.Verify mobile web folder size . Actual: In 3.0 SDK build, folder size is 4.7MB whereas in 2.1.3 its size is 4.6MB""""",title+description
TIMOB-11314,12,"""CLI: """"ValueError: year is out of range"""" on Alloy for android build""","""""""I am attempting to build a project for android with alloy. The alloy compile finishes, so I don't think the problem is there, but here is the relevant output        Not exactly sure what is going on here, it appears to be choking on resolving file timestamps or something.    Things I've tried:    * clean  * restart tistudio  * adb kill-server && adb start-server    No luck.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: """"ValueError: year is out of range"""" on Alloy for android build
Description: """"I am attempting to build a project for android with alloy. The alloy compile finishes, so I don't think the problem is there, but here is the relevant output Not exactly sure what is going on here, it appears to be choking on resolving file timestamps or something. Things I've tried: * clean * restart tistudio * adb kill-server && adb start-server No luck.""""",title+description
