TIMOB-11285,12,"""iOS: Textfield.blur is having a strange race condition when blurring a textfield and then opening a window""","""""""h4. Problem   If you execute blur and then open a window, looks like the blur never happened. If you run an example with Kitchensink, the blur will work as expected. It's like there is a race condition between the execution of the blur in the textfield and the open of the window, where the window opening will take precedence.       h4. Actual Results  The textfield never gets the blur command, when followed by a window opening.     h4. Expected results  The textfield should blur, then the window should open.     h4. Test case   1. Copy this code to an app.js:    2. Now run the code with 2.1.3.GA on iOS 4.x.   3. If you click on the textfield, the window will open. Close the window, the textfield shouldn't be focused.      h4. Extra info.  This is a regression. This used to work just fine with TiSDK 2.1.3.v20120915120319, now with 2.1.3.GA is broken. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Textfield.blur is having a strange race condition when blurring a textfield and then opening a window
Description: """"h4. Problem If you execute blur and then open a window, looks like the blur never happened. If you run an example with Kitchensink, the blur will work as expected. It's like there is a race condition between the execution of the blur in the textfield and the open of the window, where the window opening will take precedence. h4. Actual Results The textfield never gets the blur command, when followed by a window opening. h4. Expected results The textfield should blur, then the window should open. h4. Test case 1. Copy this code to an app.js: 2. Now run the code with 2.1.3.GA on iOS 4.x. 3. If you click on the textfield, the window will open. Close the window, the textfield shouldn't be focused. h4. Extra info. This is a regression. This used to work just fine with TiSDK 2.1.3.v20120915120319, now with 2.1.3.GA is broken. """"",title+description
