TIMOB-11277,12,"""iOS6: hide() and show () do not get fired if they are tapped for more than four times in second.""","""""""When the show and hide buttons are tapped in rapid succession the events do not get fired. It cannot hide child view immediately after tap on parent view.  h4.Steps to Reproduce:    1. run the code below   2. click btn1 - btn3 will disappear   3. click btn2 - btn3 will reappear   4. in rapid succession, click btn1, click the open window space between btn1 and btn2, then click btn2 - btn3 will disappear, but will not reappear      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS6: hide() and show () do not get fired if they are tapped for more than four times in second.
Description: """"When the show and hide buttons are tapped in rapid succession the events do not get fired. It cannot hide child view immediately after tap on parent view. h4.Steps to Reproduce: 1. run the code below 2. click btn1 - btn3 will disappear 3. click btn2 - btn3 will reappear 4. in rapid succession, click btn1, click the open window space between btn1 and btn2, then click btn2 - btn3 will disappear, but will not reappear """"",title+description
TIMOB-11275,12,"""iOS: Click event is fired even when click is outside the icon of an item in the Titanium.UI.DashboardView""","""""""h1. Problem description  When the icon that represents an item inside a DashboardView is smaller than the """"""""cell"""""""" size, clicking outside the icon fires the 'click' event.    h1. Steps to reproduce  - Use the following code:        - Make sure the icons used are smaller than the cell size  - Run the app and click outside the icon: the click event is fired    h1. Note  The x-y value returned in the click event is fixed for each element, no metter where the user clicks. In particular, first element is always 0-0, second 256-0, third 512-0 etc.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Click event is fired even when click is outside the icon of an item in the Titanium.UI.DashboardView
Description: """"h1. Problem description When the icon that represents an item inside a DashboardView is smaller than the """"""""cell"""""""" size, clicking outside the icon fires the 'click' event. h1. Steps to reproduce - Use the following code: - Make sure the icons used are smaller than the cell size - Run the app and click outside the icon: the click event is fired h1. Note The x-y value returned in the click event is fixed for each element, no metter where the user clicks. In particular, first element is always 0-0, second 256-0, third 512-0 etc.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11274,12,"""iOS :Kitchen Sink: Webviews - Pinch and Zoom does not work on iPad ""","""""""Pinch and Zoom does not work on iPad.    This is not a regression.This even occurs on 2.1.3.GA    Steps to reproduce:    1. Install Kitchen Sink on device  2. Tap on base UI>Views>WebViews>Local Pinch/Zoom.  3. Pinch/Zoom out the image.    Actual Result:    Pinch and Zoom effect does not happens on image.It works fine on iPhone device.    Expected Result:    Pinch and Zoom effect should happen on image.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS :Kitchen Sink: Webviews - Pinch and Zoom does not work on iPad
Description: """"Pinch and Zoom does not work on iPad. This is not a regression.This even occurs on 2.1.3.GA Steps to reproduce: 1. Install Kitchen Sink on device 2. Tap on base UI>Views>WebViews>Local Pinch/Zoom. 3. Pinch/Zoom out the image. Actual Result: Pinch and Zoom effect does not happens on image.It works fine on iPhone device. Expected Result: Pinch and Zoom effect should happen on image. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11273,12,"""Android: KS Web Views > Local URL: Apple logo and html text not appearing.""","""""""This is a regression. It works fine with 2.1.3GA.    The different screen shots are attached with the bug.The apple logo and the html script text 'Click Me to Hide the Toolbar' are not appearing with 3.0.0 sdk. Seems html script is not being read . It appears with 2.1.3 sdk.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it.  2) Go to Base UI -> Views-> Web View -> Local URL    Expected result:  1) The app should run successfully over device.  2) It should display the screen as shown for 2.1.3. And clicking the text 'Click Me to Hide the Toolbar' should hide the toolbar shown at the bottom.    Actual result:  1) The app runs successfully over device.  2) It displays no apple logo and no text. Not able to hide toolbar. """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS Web Views > Local URL: Apple logo and html text not appearing.
Description: """"This is a regression. It works fine with 2.1.3GA. The different screen shots are attached with the bug.The apple logo and the html script text 'Click Me to Hide the Toolbar' are not appearing with 3.0.0 sdk. Seems html script is not being read . It appears with 2.1.3 sdk. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it. 2) Go to Base UI -> Views-> Web View -> Local URL Expected result: 1) The app should run successfully over device. 2) It should display the screen as shown for 2.1.3. And clicking the text 'Click Me to Hide the Toolbar' should hide the toolbar shown at the bottom. Actual result: 1) The app runs successfully over device. 2) It displays no apple logo and no text. Not able to hide toolbar. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11272,12,"""iOS: Kitchensink - Buttons do not lose the effect of last click unless Editable:Enable and Editable:Disable button is clicked.""","""""""Buttons do not lose the effect of last click unless Editable:Enable and Editable:Disable button is clicked.  This is not regression since the issue occurs as far as 2.1.2    Steps to reproduce:  1. Go to Kitchensink> Controls> Text Area> AutoLink. All links are enabled by default.  2. Click 'Detect address' button.  3. Click Editable:Enable and then Editable:Disabled button.    Actual:  2. Nothing happens.  3. Address appears as selected.    Expected:  Buttons should work without Editable:Enable and  Editable:Disabled button click.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchensink - Buttons do not lose the effect of last click unless Editable:Enable and Editable:Disable button is clicked.
Description: """"Buttons do not lose the effect of last click unless Editable:Enable and Editable:Disable button is clicked. This is not regression since the issue occurs as far as 2.1.2 Steps to reproduce: 1. Go to Kitchensink> Controls> Text Area> AutoLink. All links are enabled by default. 2. Click 'Detect address' button. 3. Click Editable:Enable and then Editable:Disabled button. Actual: 2. Nothing happens. 3. Address appears as selected. Expected: Buttons should work without Editable:Enable and Editable:Disabled button click.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11271,12,"""iOS: Kitchensink - Text field shows bounce effect if enabled when it's half visible on the screen.""","""""""Text field shows bounce effect if enabled when it's half visible on the screen.  This is not regression since the issue occurs as far as 2.1.2 GA    Steps to reproduce:  1. Go to Kitchensink> Controls> TextField in scrollview.  2. Scroll up till the middle text field is half visible.  3. Click on it to enable the textfield.    Actual:  Textfield bounces to come down and then go up. It occurs only on device, not on simulator.    Expected:  The textfield should not bounce.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchensink - Text field shows bounce effect if enabled when it's half visible on the screen.
Description: """"Text field shows bounce effect if enabled when it's half visible on the screen. This is not regression since the issue occurs as far as 2.1.2 GA Steps to reproduce: 1. Go to Kitchensink> Controls> TextField in scrollview. 2. Scroll up till the middle text field is half visible. 3. Click on it to enable the textfield. Actual: Textfield bounces to come down and then go up. It occurs only on device, not on simulator. Expected: The textfield should not bounce.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11270,12,"""Kitchen sink:Base UI:Window (Standalone)->Opening 'Traditional Modal' window throws a runtime error.""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.0.1.    Logs for runtime error attached with the bug.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it.  2) Go to Base UI -> Window (Standalone)  3) Now press button 'Traditional Modal'    Expected result:  1) The app should run successfully over device.  2) It should display 4 buttons to open different windows.  3) A modal window should get displayed and no runtime error should be shown.    Actual result:  1) The app runs successfully over device.  2) It displays 4 buttons to open different windows.  3) It gives a runtime error """"""""Message: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'title' of undefined""""""""      """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen sink:Base UI:Window (Standalone)->Opening 'Traditional Modal' window throws a runtime error.
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.0.1. Logs for runtime error attached with the bug. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it. 2) Go to Base UI -> Window (Standalone) 3) Now press button 'Traditional Modal' Expected result: 1) The app should run successfully over device. 2) It should display 4 buttons to open different windows. 3) A modal window should get displayed and no runtime error should be shown. Actual result: 1) The app runs successfully over device. 2) It displays 4 buttons to open different windows. 3) It gives a runtime error """"""""Message: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'title' of undefined"""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-11269,12,"""Kitchen sink:Base UI:Window Properties->Toggling height/width changing opacity of window""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.0.1.    Toggle height/width changes opacity of window from transparent to opaque. Even if it is resetting it, then it should not take 2 clicks to make it transparent again.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it.  2) Go to Base UI -> Window Properties  3) Now press 'Toggle Opacity'.  4) Press button 'Toggle Height/Width' twice.  5) Now press 'Toggle Opacity'.    Expected result:  1) The app should run successfully over device.  2) It should display 5 buttons to perform window actions.  3) It should change the opacity of the window to transparent.  4) It should resize the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background.  5) It should change the opacity of the window to transparent in single click.    Actual result:  1) The app runs successfully over device.  2) It displays 5 buttons to perform window actions.  3) It changes the opacity of the window to transparent.  4) It resizes the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background.  5) It do changes the opacity of the window to transparent on a single click. Even though it is opaque, it takes 2 clicks to turn screen transparent.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen sink:Base UI:Window Properties->Toggling height/width changing opacity of window
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.0.1. Toggle height/width changes opacity of window from transparent to opaque. Even if it is resetting it, then it should not take 2 clicks to make it transparent again. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it. 2) Go to Base UI -> Window Properties 3) Now press 'Toggle Opacity'. 4) Press button 'Toggle Height/Width' twice. 5) Now press 'Toggle Opacity'. Expected result: 1) The app should run successfully over device. 2) It should display 5 buttons to perform window actions. 3) It should change the opacity of the window to transparent. 4) It should resize the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background. 5) It should change the opacity of the window to transparent in single click. Actual result: 1) The app runs successfully over device. 2) It displays 5 buttons to perform window actions. 3) It changes the opacity of the window to transparent. 4) It resizes the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background. 5) It do changes the opacity of the window to transparent on a single click. Even though it is opaque, it takes 2 clicks to turn screen transparent. """"",title+description
