TIMOB-11264,12,"""Android: Event """"closeFromActivity"""" cannot be fired on Android""","""""""Description:  While testing Android I noticed, that clicking on Android """"""""back"""""""" button, which should return user to the red (previous) window, returns to the apps menue.   In the console getting a warning:     This is a regression, does not occur on 2.1.3.    Steps:  1. Run the following code:    2. Click """"""""open red win"""""""" button  3. Click """"""""open yellow"""""""" button  4. Press Android """"""""back"""""""" button    Expected:  You should return to the red (previous) window     Actual:  Returning to the apps menue""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Event """"closeFromActivity"""" cannot be fired on Android
Description: """"Description: While testing Android I noticed, that clicking on Android """"""""back"""""""" button, which should return user to the red (previous) window, returns to the apps menue. In the console getting a warning: This is a regression, does not occur on 2.1.3. Steps: 1. Run the following code: 2. Click """"""""open red win"""""""" button 3. Click """"""""open yellow"""""""" button 4. Press Android """"""""back"""""""" button Expected: You should return to the red (previous) window Actual: Returning to the apps menue""""",title+description
TIMOB-11263,12,"""CLI: Tiapp.xml parsing doesn't respect comments/tag order of the original file""","""""""Whenever the tiapp.xml file is written, comments, tag order, and extraneous tags are ignored. When writing to the tiapp.xml file, we need to compare with the original and mix together to preserve these.""""""",Bug,"Title: CLI: Tiapp.xml parsing doesn't respect comments/tag order of the original file
Description: """"Whenever the tiapp.xml file is written, comments, tag order, and extraneous tags are ignored. When writing to the tiapp.xml file, we need to compare with the original and mix together to preserve these.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11261,12,"""iOS 6: setTimeout doesn't work after touchmove""","""""""Using a WebView loading a local html file (attached, app.js and webview_repaint_source.html) and have a setTimeout call in the touchend event. To reproduce:  1. Run the app in iOS simulator 6.0  2. Click and release, then an alert will pop up (500ms delay).  3. But when click, scroll, and release, no alert pop up.  4. Run the app in iOS simulator 5.0, step 3 does popup an alert dialog.   """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS 6: setTimeout doesn't work after touchmove
Description: """"Using a WebView loading a local html file (attached, app.js and webview_repaint_source.html) and have a setTimeout call in the touchend event. To reproduce: 1. Run the app in iOS simulator 6.0 2. Click and release, then an alert will pop up (500ms delay). 3. But when click, scroll, and release, no alert pop up. 4. Run the app in iOS simulator 5.0, step 3 does popup an alert dialog. """"",title+description
