TIMOB-11255,12,"""iOS6 Custom Slider does not render correctly""","""""""Using the leftTrackImage, rightTrackImage properties for the slider, it does not render correctly on the new iOS6 as can be seen in the attached screen shots.  iOS Simulator Screen shot Sep 24, 2012 8.37.22 PM.png is running iOS6 while iOS Simulator Screen shot Sep 24, 2012 8.37.47 PM.png is iOS 5.1    The default slider renders as it should.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS6 Custom Slider does not render correctly
Description: """"Using the leftTrackImage, rightTrackImage properties for the slider, it does not render correctly on the new iOS6 as can be seen in the attached screen shots. iOS Simulator Screen shot Sep 24, 2012 8.37.22 PM.png is running iOS6 while iOS Simulator Screen shot Sep 24, 2012 8.37.47 PM.png is iOS 5.1 The default slider renders as it should.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11254,12,"""iOS: When resizing a view, a centered child label does not go along with the animation""","""""""When resizing a view with an animation, a centered child label will jump to its new position immediately rather than sliding along with the redraw Animation. This happens when animating to a different height (i.e. when the label should be vertically centered in the view) and when animating to a different width in case the label is set to textAlign: Ti.UI.TEXT_ALIGNMENT_CENTER (i.e. when the label should be horizontally centered in the view). This works perfectly fine on Android.    h4.Steps to reproduce    1. Create a default master / detail application and use the following detail function (ui/common/DetailView).    Expected Behavior: label should slide along with the animation    Actual behavior: label just jumps off to the new position.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: When resizing a view, a centered child label does not go along with the animation
Description: """"When resizing a view with an animation, a centered child label will jump to its new position immediately rather than sliding along with the redraw Animation. This happens when animating to a different height (i.e. when the label should be vertically centered in the view) and when animating to a different width in case the label is set to textAlign: Ti.UI.TEXT_ALIGNMENT_CENTER (i.e. when the label should be horizontally centered in the view). This works perfectly fine on Android. h4.Steps to reproduce 1. Create a default master / detail application and use the following detail function (ui/common/DetailView). Expected Behavior: label should slide along with the animation Actual behavior: label just jumps off to the new position. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11253,12,"""SDK: The demos/ folder should probably be removed altogether""","""""""Kitchen Sink exists elsewhere now.  Smoke Test was an internal tool used by QE but not any longer.  ApiCheck has only been updated 3 times and the last time was 3 years ago -- no idea what it actually is.""""""",Story,"Title: SDK: The demos/ folder should probably be removed altogether
Description: """"Kitchen Sink exists elsewhere now. Smoke Test was an internal tool used by QE but not any longer. ApiCheck has only been updated 3 times and the last time was 3 years ago -- no idea what it actually is.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11252,12,"""Android: Entries in tiapp.xml do not replace stock values in generated AndroidManifest.xml""","""""""Android manifest changes in the tiapp.xml file do not replace the """"""""stock"""""""" manifest entries created by the build <USER> Instead, the stock entries are copied after the custom entries, overriding the customizations.    h2. Steps to reproduce    # Create a default Ti project targeting Android  # Build the app (for emulator or device, doesn't matter)  # Open tiapp.xml, view the XML source  # Change the <android tag to be container tags and add manifest tags, like this:\\    # Open <project>/builds/android/AndroidManifest.xml and copy the <activity> and <service> tags that follow the <!-- TI_APPLICATION --> comment  # Paste the copied text into the tiapp.xml between the <manifest></manifest> tags  # Edit the pasted in code to remove |orientation from each of the <activity configChanges""""""""> attributes  # To each of those tags, add  android:screenOrientation=""""""""portrait""""""""  to force portrait orientation in the app  # Save and build the app  # Open <project>/builds/android/AndroidManifest.xml. It will have both your customized entries followed by the generated stock entries. As a result, the app will display in both portrait and landscape orientation.    h2. Expected results     Changes in tiapp.xml would override the stock/generated AndroidManifest.xml values    h2. Actual results    Stock/generated AndroidManifest values pasted in after custom entries, negating the effect of the custom entries.      This is likely a regression as it used to work properly. The tiapp.xml customization technique is taught in the ATMD training course.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Entries in tiapp.xml do not replace stock values in generated AndroidManifest.xml
Description: """"Android manifest changes in the tiapp.xml file do not replace the """"""""stock"""""""" manifest entries created by the build <USER> Instead, the stock entries are copied after the custom entries, overriding the customizations. h2. Steps to reproduce # Create a default Ti project targeting Android # Build the app (for emulator or device, doesn't matter) # Open tiapp.xml, view the XML source # Change the <android tag to be container tags and add manifest tags, like this:\\ # Open <project>/builds/android/AndroidManifest.xml and copy the <activity> and <service> tags that follow the <!-- TI_APPLICATION --> comment # Paste the copied text into the tiapp.xml between the <manifest></manifest> tags # Edit the pasted in code to remove |orientation from each of the <activity configChanges""""""""> attributes # To each of those tags, add android:screenOrientation=""""""""portrait"""""""" to force portrait orientation in the app # Save and build the app # Open <project>/builds/android/AndroidManifest.xml. It will have both your customized entries followed by the generated stock entries. As a result, the app will display in both portrait and landscape orientation. h2. Expected results Changes in tiapp.xml would override the stock/generated AndroidManifest.xml values h2. Actual results Stock/generated AndroidManifest values pasted in after custom entries, negating the effect of the custom entries. This is likely a regression as it used to work properly. The tiapp.xml customization technique is taught in the ATMD training course.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11251,12,"""OSX Titanium SDK GA contains win32 folder with bat files""","""""""OSX Titanium SDK GA contains win32 folder with bat files.    Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.3.GA/win32/findpython.bat  Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.3.GA/win32/python.bat  Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.3.GA/win32/titanium.bat    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Download SDK GA in OSX.  2. Open SDK folder.  3. Look for win32 bat files.    Actual Result:    bat files exist.    Expected Result:    No bat files, this is OSX.""""""",Bug,"Title: OSX Titanium SDK GA contains win32 folder with bat files
Description: """"OSX Titanium SDK GA contains win32 folder with bat files. Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.3.GA/win32/findpython.bat Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.3.GA/win32/python.bat Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.3.GA/win32/titanium.bat Steps to Reproduce: 1. Download SDK GA in OSX. 2. Open SDK folder. 3. Look for win32 bat files. Actual Result: bat files exist. Expected Result: No bat files, this is OSX.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11250,12,"""iOS: blur() callback fails to blur keyboard on textfields with custom toolbar.""","""""""The problem does not appear on iOS5 with 2.1.2.    It is only reproducable when there are many onscreen elements.    blur() causes the custom toolbar to hide but focus remains on textfield with keyboard still displayed.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: blur() callback fails to blur keyboard on textfields with custom toolbar.
Description: """"The problem does not appear on iOS5 with 2.1.2. It is only reproducable when there are many onscreen elements. blur() causes the custom toolbar to hide but focus remains on textfield with keyboard still displayed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11246,12,"""KitchenSink: Map view demo uses iOS-specific controls so that Android has no buttons for options""","""""""/ui/common/baseui/mapview.js uses an iOS-specific Toolbar so that there are no buttons for map controls on Android. The sample should enable the user to select map type (satellite, hybrid, etc.), change map location, and so forth. These need to be implemented as an Android menu or as standard buttons to be cross-platform.     Sample as written currently will likely also fail on MobileWeb.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Map view demo uses iOS-specific controls so that Android has no buttons for options
Description: """"/ui/common/baseui/mapview.js uses an iOS-specific Toolbar so that there are no buttons for map controls on Android. The sample should enable the user to select map type (satellite, hybrid, etc.), change map location, and so forth. These need to be implemented as an Android menu or as standard buttons to be cross-platform. Sample as written currently will likely also fail on MobileWeb.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11245,12,"""KitchenSink: Need Android sample for Map view with routing""","""""""Routing is now supported in Android. The KitchenSink does not include a demo (current demo is iOS only)    Current sample is ui/handheld/ios/baseui/map_view2""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Need Android sample for Map view with routing
Description: """"Routing is now supported in Android. The KitchenSink does not include a demo (current demo is iOS only) Current sample is ui/handheld/ios/baseui/map_view2""""",title+description
TIMOB-11243,12,"""KitchenSink - geolocation example needs to implement Android-specific techniques""","""""""The KitchenSink geolocation demo (ui/common/phone/geolocation.js) uses iOS-specific properties and methods that are now deprecated on Android. There is no corresponding Android-specific version, which there should be to show off the new Android properties and methods. See https://github.com/<USER>training/tcad-code/tree/master/Starting_code/AndroidGeo for sample code that could be used.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink - geolocation example needs to implement Android-specific techniques
Description: """"The KitchenSink geolocation demo (ui/common/phone/geolocation.js) uses iOS-specific properties and methods that are now deprecated on Android. There is no corresponding Android-specific version, which there should be to show off the new Android properties and methods. See https://github.com/<USER>training/tcad-code/tree/master/Starting_code/AndroidGeo for sample code that could be used.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11241,12,"""iOS 6: View:Pinching in to a large size makes view to disappear (if it contains label in it).""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.1.1.  This is an iOS 6 issue. It works fine on iPad iOS 5.1,iPHONE 3G S(iOS 5.0.1) and iPhone 4S(iOS 5.1) with xcode 4.5.  It also works on simulator iOS 5.1/xcode 4.4.1. But issue occurs on iOS 6 with xcode 4.5 and 4.4.1.    If the view is pinched in to a large size without label, it do not disappears.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the code below in app.js    2. Launch the app and pinch in the view until it disappears    Expected result:  2. It should not disappear    Actual result:  2. It disappears on pinching in to large size.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 6: View:Pinching in to a large size makes view to disappear (if it contains label in it).
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.1.1. This is an iOS 6 issue. It works fine on iPad iOS 5.1,iPHONE 3G S(iOS 5.0.1) and iPhone 4S(iOS 5.1) with xcode 4.5. It also works on simulator iOS 5.1/xcode 4.4.1. But issue occurs on iOS 6 with xcode 4.5 and 4.4.1. If the view is pinched in to a large size without label, it do not disappears. Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the code below in app.js 2. Launch the app and pinch in the view until it disappears Expected result: 2. It should not disappear Actual result: 2. It disappears on pinching in to large size.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11240,12,"""iOS: App crashes on changing orientation while opening photogallery from modal window""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.0.1.  This seems to be an ipad issue. It works fine on iPHONE 3G S(iOS 5.0.1) and iPhone 4S(iOS 5.1)    Steps to reproduce  1. Use the app below in app.js    2. Run the app and press button 'Push me'   3. Rotate the device to different orientation now.    Expected result  2. After step 2, the photo gallery should get displayed.  3. App should rotate to different orientations without crash.    Actual result:  2. After step 2, the photo gallery is not displayed.  3. App crashes on rotating to different orientation.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App crashes on changing orientation while opening photogallery from modal window
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists as far as 2.0.1. This seems to be an ipad issue. It works fine on iPHONE 3G S(iOS 5.0.1) and iPhone 4S(iOS 5.1) Steps to reproduce 1. Use the app below in app.js 2. Run the app and press button 'Push me' 3. Rotate the device to different orientation now. Expected result 2. After step 2, the photo gallery should get displayed. 3. App should rotate to different orientations without crash. Actual result: 2. After step 2, the photo gallery is not displayed. 3. App crashes on rotating to different orientation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11239,12,"""iOS: multiple Ti.Analytics.featureEvent calls in a short time causes the app to crash""","""""""h1. Problem description  Calling two or more Ti.Analytics.featureEvent in a short period of time causes the app to crash.    h1. Steps to reproduce  Use the following code to test the problem:        - Run the app  - Click on the table row: the app crashes    h1. Note  Sometimes, the app does not crash the first time, but clicking 2-3 times on the row will do that. I've tested with SDK 2.1.2.GA and the app crashes without any error in the console. Opening the app with XCode, however, shows this error: EXC_BAD_ACCESS    I also tried testing with SDK 3.0.0.v20121002161335 and I see the following error in the Titanium console:    {color:red}  [ERROR] A SQLite database error occurred on database '/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.0/Applications/C6577659-96DC-4234-9051-2FE866115B98/Library/Application Support/analytics/analytics.db': Error Domain=com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase Code=3 """"""""An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement."""""""" UserInfo=0xb216820 {com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.code=1, NSLocalizedDescription=An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement., com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.query.string=INSERT INTO pending_events VALUES (?), com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.string=table pending_events has 1 columns but 2 values were supplied} (SQLite #1: table pending_events has 1 columns but 2 values were supplied) (query: 'INSERT INTO pending_events VALUES (?)')  {color}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: multiple Ti.Analytics.featureEvent calls in a short time causes the app to crash
Description: """"h1. Problem description Calling two or more Ti.Analytics.featureEvent in a short period of time causes the app to crash. h1. Steps to reproduce Use the following code to test the problem: - Run the app - Click on the table row: the app crashes h1. Note Sometimes, the app does not crash the first time, but clicking 2-3 times on the row will do that. I've tested with SDK 2.1.2.GA and the app crashes without any error in the console. Opening the app with XCode, however, shows this error: EXC_BAD_ACCESS I also tried testing with SDK 3.0.0.v20121002161335 and I see the following error in the Titanium console: {color:red} [ERROR] A SQLite database error occurred on database '/Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/6.0/Applications/C6577659-96DC-4234-9051-2FE866115B98/Library/Application Support/analytics/analytics.db': Error Domain=com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase Code=3 """"""""An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement."""""""" UserInfo=0xb216820 {com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.code=1, NSLocalizedDescription=An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement., com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.query.string=INSERT INTO pending_events VALUES (?), com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.string=table pending_events has 1 columns but 2 values were supplied} (SQLite #1: table pending_events has 1 columns but 2 values were supplied) (query: 'INSERT INTO pending_events VALUES (?)') {color}""""",title+description
TIMOB-11238,12,"""Android: local webviews fail with removed js files when packaged for android""","""""""h3. Issue    When the app is packaged for distribution, .js files are removed. This appears to be causing problems with the javascript files that are referenced by the local html files.    This works fine with an iOS app when packaged. The js files are missing from the package but seem to load and execute with no issues.     h4. Workaround    The javascript files can be renamed with .jsx extension and this will disable them from getting removed from the app package.    h3. Steps to Reproduce    1. Run the attached test project.   2. When launched in android emulator or on device, the test.js file work update the html file correctly. The apk file still has the test.js resource.  3. When packaged for distribution the test.js file is removed and the html file does not get updated.  4. When the test.html is modified to reference test.jsx, the testcase succeeds    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: local webviews fail with removed js files when packaged for android
Description: """"h3. Issue When the app is packaged for distribution, .js files are removed. This appears to be causing problems with the javascript files that are referenced by the local html files. This works fine with an iOS app when packaged. The js files are missing from the package but seem to load and execute with no issues. h4. Workaround The javascript files can be renamed with .jsx extension and this will disable them from getting removed from the app package. h3. Steps to Reproduce 1. Run the attached test project. 2. When launched in android emulator or on device, the test.js file work update the html file correctly. The apk file still has the test.js resource. 3. When packaged for distribution the test.js file is removed and the html file does not get updated. 4. When the test.html is modified to reference test.jsx, the testcase succeeds """"",title+description
