TIMOB-11213,12,"""iOS: orientation - iOS 6 only: Forcing landscape on a window then opening an email dialog in portrait will result in your original window allowed to rotate to portrait""","""""""While investigating an issue posted on the Q&A, I was unable to reproduce the exact problem, but did discover another:    When you allow only portrait in Tiapp.xml:      And then open a window with landscape left allowed and attempt to send a mail, the email dialog can rotate as you wish. If you close the email dialog and return to your window in portrait, the win will be in portrait - which shouldn't be allowed.    Sample code:      Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a new application  2) Set tiapp.xml to portrait orientation as above  3) Use sample code  4) Launch sample app in portrait orientation, not splash is portrait as desired  5) Note window is locked landscape left - Click the """"""""Click me"""""""" button  5) note email dialog comes up in portrait  6) Cancel email    Result:  The red window is now displayed in portrait - any orientation change returns it to its only approved orientation    Expected:  The red window does not change orientation    Note: this does not occur on iOS 5 devices""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: orientation - iOS 6 only: Forcing landscape on a window then opening an email dialog in portrait will result in your original window allowed to rotate to portrait
Description: """"While investigating an issue posted on the Q&A, I was unable to reproduce the exact problem, but did discover another: When you allow only portrait in Tiapp.xml: And then open a window with landscape left allowed and attempt to send a mail, the email dialog can rotate as you wish. If you close the email dialog and return to your window in portrait, the win will be in portrait - which shouldn't be allowed. Sample code: Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a new application 2) Set tiapp.xml to portrait orientation as above 3) Use sample code 4) Launch sample app in portrait orientation, not splash is portrait as desired 5) Note window is locked landscape left - Click the """"""""Click me"""""""" button 5) note email dialog comes up in portrait 6) Cancel email Result: The red window is now displayed in portrait - any orientation change returns it to its only approved orientation Expected: The red window does not change orientation Note: this does not occur on iOS 5 devices""""",title+description
TIMOB-11212,12,"""iOS: VideoPlayer goes into a loading mode at the end of the video when created in a two  window app""","""""""Video player goes into a loading mode at the end of the video when created in a two window application. It works fine in a single window app.     h4. Repo Steps  1. Run the below code in your projects app.js.  2. Open the app. Click in the button """"""""Go to second window"""""""".  3. Now click the button """"""""Play video""""""""  4. Go to the end of the video and you can see the loading window after the video ends.      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: VideoPlayer goes into a loading mode at the end of the video when created in a two window app
Description: """"Video player goes into a loading mode at the end of the video when created in a two window application. It works fine in a single window app. h4. Repo Steps 1. Run the below code in your projects app.js. 2. Open the app. Click in the button """"""""Go to second window"""""""". 3. Now click the button """"""""Play video"""""""" 4. Go to the end of the video and you can see the loading window after the video ends. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11211,12,"""Ti: Samples do not contain ios new default structure for tiapp.xml""","""""""Description:  While creating a new mobile project for ios devices, I noticed an absence of <ios> element in tiapp.xml, which is intended to replace the <iphone> section, which is now deprecated.  See iOS specific section in API documentation:  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.1/index.html#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference     Here are the samples that need updating:    * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.HTML  * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.MasterDetail  * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.SingleWindow  * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.Tabbed  """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti: Samples do not contain ios new default structure for tiapp.xml
Description: """"Description: While creating a new mobile project for ios devices, I noticed an absence of <ios> element in tiapp.xml, which is intended to replace the <iphone> section, which is now deprecated. See iOS specific section in API documentation: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.1/index.html#!/guide/tiapp.xml_and_timodule.xml_Reference Here are the samples that need updating: * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.HTML * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.MasterDetail * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.SingleWindow * https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/Template.Tabbed """"",title+description
TIMOB-11210,12,"""Win8: Changes aren't reverted when user goes back with """"Home"""" button""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. submit  a report  2. switch to manager view  3. reject the report  4. switch to employee view  5. add or delete a charge  6. click """"""""Home""""""""  7. click """"""""OK""""""""  8. open the report again    Actual result: the change is there""""""",Bug,"Title: Win8: Changes aren't reverted when user goes back with """"Home"""" button
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. submit a report 2. switch to manager view 3. reject the report 4. switch to employee view 5. add or delete a charge 6. click """"""""Home"""""""" 7. click """"""""OK"""""""" 8. open the report again Actual result: the change is there""""",title+description
