TIMOB-11208,12,"""Kitchen Sink: On iOS 6, no response to user for unable to add contacts and error in console when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts""","""""""On iOS 6, adding contacts through Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Add Contact does not add a contact and also no response for failure to add contact is shown when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts  Steps to Reproduce:  1. Go to Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Add Contacts  2. Enter details and click on Add Contact button    Actual: No response is shown. Also an error is shown in console. Find the attached logs.    Expected: There should be an information shown that the app does not have access to contacts (as is shown in other cases in KS for contacts)""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen Sink: On iOS 6, no response to user for unable to add contacts and error in console when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts
Description: """"On iOS 6, adding contacts through Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Add Contact does not add a contact and also no response for failure to add contact is shown when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts Steps to Reproduce: 1. Go to Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Add Contacts 2. Enter details and click on Add Contact button Actual: No response is shown. Also an error is shown in console. Find the attached logs. Expected: There should be an information shown that the app does not have access to contacts (as is shown in other cases in KS for contacts)""""",title+description
TIMOB-11207,12,"""Kitchen Sink: On iOS 6, the cases for Contacts->Groups and Contacts->Display People do not work when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts""","""""""On iOS 6, the cases of Groups, Display people in Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Contacts do not show any response when selected and throw an error in log when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Go to Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Contacts  2. Click on Groups / Display People    Actual: No response is shown as no window opens up. Also an error is shown in console. Find the attached logs.    Expected: There should be an information shown that the app does not have access to contacts (as is shown in other cases in KS for  contacts)""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen Sink: On iOS 6, the cases for Contacts->Groups and Contacts->Display People do not work when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts
Description: """"On iOS 6, the cases of Groups, Display people in Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Contacts do not show any response when selected and throw an error in log when Kitchen Sink does not have permission to contacts Steps to Reproduce: 1. Go to Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Contacts 2. Click on Groups / Display People Actual: No response is shown as no window opens up. Also an error is shown in console. Find the attached logs. Expected: There should be an information shown that the app does not have access to contacts (as is shown in other cases in KS for contacts)""""",title+description
