TIMOB-11198,12,"""KitchenSink: WebViews - An image disappears after reloading a page""","""""""Description:  An image of apple disappears after reloading a page.  Also tested on iPhone 4S (5.1.1) and iPhone 4S (4.3.5) - after reloading the page the image stays on its place.    h3. Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink from dev-relations repo on a device with iOS 6.0  2. Go to Base UI-Views-WebViews-Local URL  3. Press """"""""Reload"""""""" button    h3. Actual result:  The image of apple disappears    h3. Expected result:  The image should not disappear""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: WebViews - An image disappears after reloading a page
Description: """"Description: An image of apple disappears after reloading a page. Also tested on iPhone 4S (5.1.1) and iPhone 4S (4.3.5) - after reloading the page the image stays on its place. h3. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink from dev-relations repo on a device with iOS 6.0 2. Go to Base UI-Views-WebViews-Local URL 3. Press """"""""Reload"""""""" button h3. Actual result: The image of apple disappears h3. Expected result: The image should not disappear""""",title+description
TIMOB-11197,12,"""iOS: Request to support iPhone5 specific images (-568h suffix) in the resources other than the splash screen""","""""""As of now, with 2.1.3RC, only default splash screen with -568h suffix are identified as iPhon5 specific by Titanium build <USER>    It would be useful to have Titanium identify other images ( placed in resources ) with -568h suffix as iphone 5 specific , the way @2X images are included for retina devices.    Currently the workaround is to use if/else logic and include iphone5 specific assets like below.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Request to support iPhone5 specific images (-568h suffix) in the resources other than the splash screen
Description: """"As of now, with 2.1.3RC, only default splash screen with -568h suffix are identified as iPhon5 specific by Titanium build <USER> It would be useful to have Titanium identify other images ( placed in resources ) with -568h suffix as iphone 5 specific , the way @2X images are included for retina devices. Currently the workaround is to use if/else logic and include iphone5 specific assets like below. """"",title+description
