TIMOB-11175,12,"""iOS 6: Project using sdk 6.0 has strange target architecture""","""""""Yesterday i add to debug my app on an ipad 3 running 6.0  So i launch the generated xcode project for my app, selected universal target and run.    Xcode told me that i could not run the app on that device.  After looking at the project i found out something strange about the targets. Valid architecture was not the same for all of them.    Screenshots speak for themselves.    After changing valid archs of the universal target to """"""""armv7 armv7s"""""""", the app did run on the device.    If i am correct a project using 6.0 sdk should not have any mention of armv6, right?""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 6: Project using sdk 6.0 has strange target architecture
Description: """"Yesterday i add to debug my app on an ipad 3 running 6.0 So i launch the generated xcode project for my app, selected universal target and run. Xcode told me that i could not run the app on that device. After looking at the project i found out something strange about the targets. Valid architecture was not the same for all of them. Screenshots speak for themselves. After changing valid archs of the universal target to """"""""armv7 armv7s"""""""", the app did run on the device. If i am correct a project using 6.0 sdk should not have any mention of armv6, right?""""",title+description
