TIMOB-11120,12,"""Android: Expose a way for users to exclude js files from being encrypted.""","""""""We need a way to allow users to ship an app without encrypting certain js files in the project.  For now, we are telling users to rename their .js files to .jslocal, but we want to add another mechanism to do so.  Please refer to http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10391 for more information.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose a way for users to exclude js files from being encrypted.
Description: """"We need a way to allow users to ship an app without encrypting certain js files in the project. For now, we are telling users to rename their .js files to .jslocal, but we want to add another mechanism to do so. Please refer to http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10391 for more information.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11119,12,"""Android: Modules: Windows 7: android module packaging fails due to missing docs folder""","""""""Android Modules fail to package on Windows 7.    This is not a regression. This was uncovered during clean install testing.    Error Log:        The work-around is to manually create a <android module project>\build\docs folder.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. On Windows 7, create an Android Module.  2. Package the module (i.e., to Project, to SDK folder).    Actual Result:    Build folder error.    Expected Result:    Module should package.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Modules: Windows 7: android module packaging fails due to missing docs folder
Description: """"Android Modules fail to package on Windows 7. This is not a regression. This was uncovered during clean install testing. Error Log: The work-around is to manually create a <android module project>\build\docs folder. Steps to Reproduce: 1. On Windows 7, create an Android Module. 2. Package the module (i.e., to Project, to SDK folder). Actual Result: Build folder error. Expected Result: Module should package.""""",title+description
