TIMOB-11073,12,"""KitchenSink: Label added into TableViewRow gets invisible on longpress and then swipe.""","""""""This is not a regression. It occurs since 2.0.1.    Steps to reproduce  1. Launch KitchenSink  2. Go to """"""""Base UI""""""""- """"""""Views"""""""" - """"""""Table Views""""""""  3. Tap on """"""""Touch Events""""""""   4. Longpress each row(on the text) then without lifting finger,swipe the label(may need to try 3-4 times,start with last row)    Expected Result:  4. After step 4, the label should only change to blue and back to white when finger is lifted off    Actual Result:  4. After step 4, the label gets disappeared. It appears again on clicking back on the tableviewrow.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Label added into TableViewRow gets invisible on longpress and then swipe.
Description: """"This is not a regression. It occurs since 2.0.1. Steps to reproduce 1. Launch KitchenSink 2. Go to """"""""Base UI""""""""- """"""""Views"""""""" - """"""""Table Views"""""""" 3. Tap on """"""""Touch Events"""""""" 4. Longpress each row(on the text) then without lifting finger,swipe the label(may need to try 3-4 times,start with last row) Expected Result: 4. After step 4, the label should only change to blue and back to white when finger is lifted off Actual Result: 4. After step 4, the label gets disappeared. It appears again on clicking back on the tableviewrow.""""",title+description
