TIMOB-11056,12,"""KitchenSink (iOS): Phone: Play Movie: Embedded Video: video window does not close on video complete""","""""""KitchenSink: Phone: Play Movie: Embedded Video: video window does not close on video complete.    This does not occur in iOS 4.3.5 or 5.X.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink: Phone: Play Movie: Embedded Video, enter fullscreen, and wait for video to finish playing.    Actual Result:    Complete dialog appears, video window never closes when dialog is dismissed.    Expected Result:    Complete dialog appears, video window closes automatically.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink (iOS): Phone: Play Movie: Embedded Video: video window does not close on video complete
Description: """"KitchenSink: Phone: Play Movie: Embedded Video: video window does not close on video complete. This does not occur in iOS 4.3.5 or 5.X. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink: Phone: Play Movie: Embedded Video, enter fullscreen, and wait for video to finish playing. Actual Result: Complete dialog appears, video window never closes when dialog is dismissed. Expected Result: Complete dialog appears, video window closes automatically.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11055,12,"""Android: WebView event JSON object conversion bug causing crash.""","""""""Firing an event from a WebView will cause a crash if the event object  contains a null value. This is due to how we bridge the object between Java <-> WebView  as a JSON string. We do not properly convert JSONObject.NULL values back to Java nulls  which causes our Kroll layer to crash since it can't convert this type.    h4. Test Case  1. Create an application with the attached app.js and index.html.  2. Click the button in the web view (""""""""click me"""""""") to trigger an event.    Pass: alert appears displaying the event object.  Fail: application crashes due to conversion error (""""""""Unable to convert unknown Java object class 'org.json.JSONObject$1' to Js value"""""""")    h4. Credit  Thanks to Tristan Waddington for reporting this bug and the detailed write up on his blog.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView event JSON object conversion bug causing crash.
Description: """"Firing an event from a WebView will cause a crash if the event object contains a null value. This is due to how we bridge the object between Java <-> WebView as a JSON string. We do not properly convert JSONObject.NULL values back to Java nulls which causes our Kroll layer to crash since it can't convert this type. h4. Test Case 1. Create an application with the attached app.js and index.html. 2. Click the button in the web view (""""""""click me"""""""") to trigger an event. Pass: alert appears displaying the event object. Fail: application crashes due to conversion error (""""""""Unable to convert unknown Java object class 'org.json.JSONObject$1' to Js value"""""""") h4. Credit Thanks to Tristan Waddington for reporting this bug and the detailed write up on his blog.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11054,12,"""iPhone 5 only - starting html5 video in landscape plays it in portrait""","""""""1.publish KS (https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/KitchenSink) using the noted config  2.install onto an iphone5 running ios6 (10A405)  3.Base UI > Views > Web Views > HTML5 Video  4.hold the device in landscape and tap the play button    results: window orients itself to portrait  epxected: res[ect the current orientation    notes:   same app works as expected on an 4s running ios6.  If I rotate at this point i can force it into the desired orientation    this is seen in the console when I tap the play button:  Sep 22 13:46:10 Ganymede KitchenSink[840] <Warning>: [MPAVController] Autoplay: Enabling autoplay  Sep 22 13:46:10 Ganymede KitchenSink[840] <Warning>: [MPAVController] Autoplay: Enabling autoplay""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone 5 only - starting html5 video in landscape plays it in portrait
Description: """"1.publish KS (https://github.com/<USER>developer-relations/KitchenSink) using the noted config 2.install onto an iphone5 running ios6 (10A405) 3.Base UI > Views > Web Views > HTML5 Video 4.hold the device in landscape and tap the play button results: window orients itself to portrait epxected: res[ect the current orientation notes: same app works as expected on an 4s running ios6. If I rotate at this point i can force it into the desired orientation this is seen in the console when I tap the play button: Sep 22 13:46:10 Ganymede KitchenSink[840] <Warning>: [MPAVController] Autoplay: Enabling autoplay Sep 22 13:46:10 Ganymede KitchenSink[840] <Warning>: [MPAVController] Autoplay: Enabling autoplay""""",title+description
