TIMOB-11026,12,"""iOS: tooling - Studio console reports """"Minimum iOS version: 4.0"""" when building with iOS 6 using default tiapp.xml""","""""""While testing iOS 6 capabilities, I noted that during a build, the console reports:      This is an issue since the project (if built with iOS 6 SDK) will not run on iOS 4.0-4.2 due to missing armv6 support.     This is not a regression as iOS 6 was not supported for 2.1.2GA release.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a new project in Studio  2) Do not set a min-ios-sdk in tiapp.xml  3) Build for device and target iOS SDK 6.0    Result:  Console reports min iOS SDK as 4.0    Expected:  Console reports min ios sdk as 4.3, and project set to reflect that.    Notes:  It is possible to manually set this minimum and the project will perform as expected.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: tooling - Studio console reports """"Minimum iOS version: 4.0"""" when building with iOS 6 using default tiapp.xml
Description: """"While testing iOS 6 capabilities, I noted that during a build, the console reports: This is an issue since the project (if built with iOS 6 SDK) will not run on iOS 4.0-4.2 due to missing armv6 support. This is not a regression as iOS 6 was not supported for 2.1.2GA release. Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a new project in Studio 2) Do not set a min-ios-sdk in tiapp.xml 3) Build for device and target iOS SDK 6.0 Result: Console reports min iOS SDK as 4.0 Expected: Console reports min ios sdk as 4.3, and project set to reflect that. Notes: It is possible to manually set this minimum and the project will perform as expected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-11025,12,"""iOS 6: Grouped style tabelview background doesn't work (kitchen sink)""","""""""If you set tableview style is grouped,  you can't change background color and background image.    You can see this bug on kitchen sink. (table_view_layout3.js, table_views.js)  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS 6: Grouped style tabelview background doesn't work (kitchen sink)
