TIMOB-11021,12,"""Email developers when an Anvil test suite fails""","""""""Anvil runs each time a code change is made to platform.    We should email the platform team if the test runs and any failures are generated. A sample email from Studio when a similar thing happens, which might provide some inspiration. There is also a corresponding email sent out when the tests start passing again.    {panel}  titanium-core-development-tests - Build # 1300 - Still Unstable:    Check console output at http://hudson-master.hdqt.<USER>com/hudson/job/titanium-core-development-tests/1300/ to view the full results.    1 of 160 tests failed    Failed tests:  1 tests failed.  REGRESSION:  com.<USER>titanium.core.tests.TitaniumProjectBuilderTest.testClean    Error Message:  Failed to delete file under build/iphone    Stack Trace:  junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Failed to delete file under build/iphone   at com.<USER>titanium.core.tests.TitaniumProjectBuilderTest.testClean(TitaniumProjectBuilderTest.java:83)   at org.eclipse.test.EclipseTestRunner.run(EclipseTestRunner.java:376)   at org.eclipse.test.EclipseTestRunner.run(EclipseTestRunner.java:209)   at org.eclipse.test.CoreTestApplication.runTests(CoreTestApplication.java:35)   at org.eclipse.test.CoreTestApplication.run(CoreTestApplication.java:31)   at org.eclipse.equinox.internal.app.EclipseAppContainer.callMethodWithException(EclipseAppContainer.java:587)   at org.eclipse.equinox.internal.app.EclipseAppHandle.run(EclipseAppHandle.java:198)   at org.eclipse.core.runtime.internal.adaptor.EclipseAppLauncher.runApplication(EclipseAppLauncher.java:110)   at org.eclipse.core.runtime.internal.adaptor.EclipseAppLauncher.start(EclipseAppLauncher.java:79)   at org.eclipse.core.runtime.adaptor.EclipseStarter.run(EclipseStarter.java:344)   at org.eclipse.core.runtime.adaptor.EclipseStarter.run(EclipseStarter.java:179)   at org.eclipse.equinox.launcher.Main.invokeFramework(Main.java:622)   at org.eclipse.equinox.launcher.Main.basicRun(Main.java:577)   at org.eclipse.equinox.launcher.Main.run(Main.java:1410)    Changes since last successful build:  Changes for Build #1290  [<USER> Fixed an error about tiapp.xml not found when creating a new ACCS project.    Changes for Build #1291    Changes for Build #1292    Changes for Build #1293  [<USER> Implement TISTUD-2205 On ACCS project creation or enablement, auto-create server  {panel}    As a refinement, we can later improve this mechanism to allow people external to AppC to be added to the notification list.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Email developers when an Anvil test suite fails
Description: """"Anvil runs each time a code change is made to platform. We should email the platform team if the test runs and any failures are generated. A sample email from Studio when a similar thing happens, which might provide some inspiration. There is also a corresponding email sent out when the tests start passing again. {panel} titanium-core-development-tests - Build # 1300 - Still Unstable: Check console output at http://hudson-master.hdqt.<USER>com/hudson/job/titanium-core-development-tests/1300/ to view the full results. 1 of 160 tests failed Failed tests: 1 tests failed. REGRESSION: com.<USER>titanium.core.tests.TitaniumProjectBuilderTest.testClean Error Message: Failed to delete file under build/iphone Stack Trace: junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Failed to delete file under build/iphone at com.<USER>titanium.core.tests.TitaniumProjectBuilderTest.testClean(TitaniumProjectBuilderTest.java:83) at org.eclipse.test.EclipseTestRunner.run(EclipseTestRunner.java:376) at org.eclipse.test.EclipseTestRunner.run(EclipseTestRunner.java:209) at org.eclipse.test.CoreTestApplication.runTests(CoreTestApplication.java:35) at org.eclipse.test.CoreTestApplication.run(CoreTestApplication.java:31) at org.eclipse.equinox.internal.app.EclipseAppContainer.callMethodWithException(EclipseAppContainer.java:587) at org.eclipse.equinox.internal.app.EclipseAppHandle.run(EclipseAppHandle.java:198) at org.eclipse.core.runtime.internal.adaptor.EclipseAppLauncher.runApplication(EclipseAppLauncher.java:110) at org.eclipse.core.runtime.internal.adaptor.EclipseAppLauncher.start(EclipseAppLauncher.java:79) at org.eclipse.core.runtime.adaptor.EclipseStarter.run(EclipseStarter.java:344) at org.eclipse.core.runtime.adaptor.EclipseStarter.run(EclipseStarter.java:179) at org.eclipse.equinox.launcher.Main.invokeFramework(Main.java:622) at org.eclipse.equinox.launcher.Main.basicRun(Main.java:577) at org.eclipse.equinox.launcher.Main.run(Main.java:1410) Changes since last successful build: Changes for Build #1290 [<USER> Fixed an error about tiapp.xml not found when creating a new ACCS project. Changes for Build #1291 Changes for Build #1292 Changes for Build #1293 [<USER> Implement TISTUD-2205 On ACCS project creation or enablement, auto-create server {panel} As a refinement, we can later improve this mechanism to allow people external to AppC to be added to the notification list.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11020,12,"""Android: In 2.1.3 RC if borderWidth is used, show/hide on the border does not work and all views added on top will be hidden behind the border ""","""""""h3. Issue    In 2.1.3.v201209151203192.1.3 RC, on Android:    1. If borderWidth is used the border cannot be hidden using the show()/hide() view functions.   2. Also, any view placed on top of the view that has borderWidth set will be hidden from the view.      h3. Steps to Reproduce    1. Run the code below in 2.1.2GA, notice the red dot in the center of the circle. Tap the hello button to see the View appear and disappear. 2. Using 2.1.3.v20120915120319, notice that there is no red circle, and tapping the button does nothing.        *NOTE: The above code works fine on iOS on 2.1.3 RC build.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: In 2.1.3 RC if borderWidth is used, show/hide on the border does not work and all views added on top will be hidden behind the border
Description: """"h3. Issue In 2.1.3.v201209151203192.1.3 RC, on Android: 1. If borderWidth is used the border cannot be hidden using the show()/hide() view functions. 2. Also, any view placed on top of the view that has borderWidth set will be hidden from the view. h3. Steps to Reproduce 1. Run the code below in 2.1.2GA, notice the red dot in the center of the circle. Tap the hello button to see the View appear and disappear. 2. Using 2.1.3.v20120915120319, notice that there is no red circle, and tapping the button does nothing. *NOTE: The above code works fine on iOS on 2.1.3 RC build.""""",title+description
