TIMOB-11004,12,"""iOS: Popover sizing not working properly on event 'orientationchange'""","""""""When you change Popover size on 'orientationchange',it leaves blue blank parts around the tableview. It is not changing the internal content of the tableview.     h4. Repo Step    1. Run the attached app.js file in your project.  2. Click the button 'Open Popover' to open the popover.  3. Change the orientation of the iPad to landscape and you can see the popover window with blue wide border.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Popover sizing not working properly on event 'orientationchange'
Description: """"When you change Popover size on 'orientationchange',it leaves blue blank parts around the tableview. It is not changing the internal content of the tableview. h4. Repo Step 1. Run the attached app.js file in your project. 2. Click the button 'Open Popover' to open the popover. 3. Change the orientation of the iPad to landscape and you can see the popover window with blue wide border.""""",title+description
TIMOB-11003,12,"""iOS: UITextField autocompletion suggestion is not committed""","""""""h6.Issue  With a TextArea, one can programmatically set it to editable=false to commit the current autocompletion suggestion.    With a TextFiled, setting editable=false does not commit the autocompletion suggestion.    h6.Reproduction steps  1. Run sample code  2. Type """"""""test"""""""" into the TextArea (first field) - iOS will suggest """"""""Test"""""""" (initial caps)  3. Click the """"""""Get TextArea Value"""""""" button, and """"""""Test"""""""" is alerted and the value of the TextArea is updated to reflect the committed autocompletion suggestion.    h6.Actual behavior  If you reproduce the above steps in the TextField (second field), the autocompletion suggestion is not committed.    h6.Expected behavior  To have the TextField work like the TextArea, so that the TextField works like the iOS native Messages app, committing the autocompletion suggestion on a button click.    h6.Tested on   iOS 5.1 simulator    h6.Actual Sample  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UITextField autocompletion suggestion is not committed
Description: """"h6.Issue With a TextArea, one can programmatically set it to editable=false to commit the current autocompletion suggestion. With a TextFiled, setting editable=false does not commit the autocompletion suggestion. h6.Reproduction steps 1. Run sample code 2. Type """"""""test"""""""" into the TextArea (first field) - iOS will suggest """"""""Test"""""""" (initial caps) 3. Click the """"""""Get TextArea Value"""""""" button, and """"""""Test"""""""" is alerted and the value of the TextArea is updated to reflect the committed autocompletion suggestion. h6.Actual behavior If you reproduce the above steps in the TextField (second field), the autocompletion suggestion is not committed. h6.Expected behavior To have the TextField work like the TextArea, so that the TextField works like the iOS native Messages app, committing the autocompletion suggestion on a button click. h6.Tested on iOS 5.1 simulator h6.Actual Sample """"",title+description
