TIMOB-10980,12,"""TableView scrollEnd event contentOffset y returns incorrect value upon release""","""""""TableView scrollEnd event contentOffset.y returns either 0 or table height regardless of the offset upon release preventing an implementation of pull to refresh.  The Kitchen Sink app is a good example of 'Pull To Refresh' example failing because of the contentOffset.y=0 .  Kitchen Sink example can be found here BaseUI->Views->Table Views->Pull to Refresh""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView scrollEnd event contentOffset y returns incorrect value upon release
Description: """"TableView scrollEnd event contentOffset.y returns either 0 or table height regardless of the offset upon release preventing an implementation of pull to refresh. The Kitchen Sink app is a good example of 'Pull To Refresh' example failing because of the contentOffset.y=0 . Kitchen Sink example can be found here BaseUI->Views->Table Views->Pull to Refresh""""",title+description
TIMOB-10979,12,"""Win8: The application is minimized when running with .bat files (A)""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. open command line  2. run files testcreate.bat, testbuild.bat, testrun.bat    Expected result: the application should be launched successfuly  Actual result: the application is launched and automatically minimized immediately. After, I can maximize it swiping from the left edge of the screen (touch control). If I close the app and run by clicking on the tile, it is launched without minimizing.    see the attached video""""""",Bug,"Title: Win8: The application is minimized when running with .bat files (A)
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. open command line 2. run files testcreate.bat, testbuild.bat, testrun.bat Expected result: the application should be launched successfuly Actual result: the application is launched and automatically minimized immediately. After, I can maximize it swiping from the left edge of the screen (touch control). If I close the app and run by clicking on the tile, it is launched without minimizing. see the attached video""""",title+description
