TIMOB-10975,12,"""iOS: Kitchen Sink: Picker: Countdown picker - Date is not displayed properly with iOS 5.x ""","""""""Date is not displayed properly with iOS 5.x whereas it is being displayed well with iOS 6.    This is not a regression.This even occurs on 2.1.2.GA    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the Kitchen Sink application  2. Tap on Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker  3. Choose hours and minutes by scrolling up and down.    Actual Result:  Date is not being displayed properly.The complete Year value is not displaying.    Note: It is displaying properly in iOS 6    Expected Result:  Date should display properly.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchen Sink: Picker: Countdown picker - Date is not displayed properly with iOS 5.x
Description: """"Date is not displayed properly with iOS 5.x whereas it is being displayed well with iOS 6. This is not a regression.This even occurs on 2.1.2.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the Kitchen Sink application 2. Tap on Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker 3. Choose hours and minutes by scrolling up and down. Actual Result: Date is not being displayed properly.The complete Year value is not displaying. Note: It is displaying properly in iOS 6 Expected Result: Date should display properly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10974,12,"""Android: Sound - Play sound and click hardware back button does not kill the sound.""","""""""Play sound and click hardware back button does not kill the sound.  This is not regression since the issue occurs in 2.1.2 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Go to Kitchensink> Phone> Sound> local  2. Click play. Sound starts playing.  3. set looping true.  4. Click hardware back button.   5. Again click local.  6. Again click hardware back button.    Actual:  4. Sound keeps playing.  5. Sound stops playing.  6. Sound starts playing.    Expected:  4. Sound should stop playing.  5. Sound should not play unless started.  6. Sound should not play.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Sound - Play sound and click hardware back button does not kill the sound.
Description: """"Play sound and click hardware back button does not kill the sound. This is not regression since the issue occurs in 2.1.2 as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Go to Kitchensink> Phone> Sound> local 2. Click play. Sound starts playing. 3. set looping true. 4. Click hardware back button. 5. Again click local. 6. Again click hardware back button. Actual: 4. Sound keeps playing. 5. Sound stops playing. 6. Sound starts playing. Expected: 4. Sound should stop playing. 5. Sound should not play unless started. 6. Sound should not play.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10973,12,"""iOS 6 : Child window is not opening if parent window has modal property set to true.""","""""""This is not a regression. It occurs on 2.1.2 also on iOS 6 device/simulator. It works fine on iOS 5.    If parent window has set 'modal:true' , then child window could not be opened from it.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the code below in app.js    2. Run the app  3. Click open button.    Expected result:  2. A black window with 'open' button should be displayed.  3. A red window should be displayed.    Actual result:  2. A black window with 'open' button is displayed.  3. A red window do not gets displayed.Instead a warning is displayed in console. Warning message attached.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS 6 : Child window is not opening if parent window has modal property set to true.
Description: """"This is not a regression. It occurs on 2.1.2 also on iOS 6 device/simulator. It works fine on iOS 5. If parent window has set 'modal:true' , then child window could not be opened from it. Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the code below in app.js 2. Run the app 3. Click open button. Expected result: 2. A black window with 'open' button should be displayed. 3. A red window should be displayed. Actual result: 2. A black window with 'open' button is displayed. 3. A red window do not gets displayed.Instead a warning is displayed in console. Warning message attached. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10972,12,"""iOS 6: Window orientation modes are neglected for second level child window ""","""""""This is not a regression. It occurs on 2.1.2 also on iOS 6 device/simulator. It works fine on iOS 5.    If you have 3 windows - one parent,one child and third one grandchild, each with their set of orientationmodes,then orientationmodes of grandchild window are over ruled by the child window.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the code below-    2. Click 'open' button  3. Click 'open' button again    Expected result:  1. A black window with 'open' button should get displayed in landscape mode.  2. A blue window with 'open' and 'close' button should get displayed in portrait mode.  3. A green window with 'close' button should get displayed in landscape mode.    Actual result:  1. A black window with 'open' button gets displayed in landscape mode.  2. A blue window with 'open' and 'close' button gets displayed in portrait mode.  3. A green window with 'close' button gets displayed in portrait mode.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 6: Window orientation modes are neglected for second level child window
Description: """"This is not a regression. It occurs on 2.1.2 also on iOS 6 device/simulator. It works fine on iOS 5. If you have 3 windows - one parent,one child and third one grandchild, each with their set of orientationmodes,then orientationmodes of grandchild window are over ruled by the child window. Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the code below- 2. Click 'open' button 3. Click 'open' button again Expected result: 1. A black window with 'open' button should get displayed in landscape mode. 2. A blue window with 'open' and 'close' button should get displayed in portrait mode. 3. A green window with 'close' button should get displayed in landscape mode. Actual result: 1. A black window with 'open' button gets displayed in landscape mode. 2. A blue window with 'open' and 'close' button gets displayed in portrait mode. 3. A green window with 'close' button gets displayed in portrait mode.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10971,12,"""Win8: User has to click 2 times to open drop-down pickers using touch control (A)""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. On the simulator select the touch control(hand icon)  2. tap on """"""""Create Report""""""""  3. tap on """"""""Category"""""""" or """"""""Department"""""""" picker field    Expected result: the drop-down list should be opened  Actual result:  it isn't opened. Only when you tap the second time, the list is opened.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Win8: User has to click 2 times to open drop-down pickers using touch control (A)
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. On the simulator select the touch control(hand icon) 2. tap on """"""""Create Report"""""""" 3. tap on """"""""Category"""""""" or """"""""Department"""""""" picker field Expected result: the drop-down list should be opened Actual result: it isn't opened. Only when you tap the second time, the list is opened. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10970,12,"""Win8: User can't delete a charge from a report (A)""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. click """"""""Create Report"""""""" button  2. fill in all fields in """"""""Add charge"""""""" section  3. click """"""""Add to report""""""""  4. click on 'X' icon on the end of the charge row    Expected result: the charge should be removed from the """"""""Charges"""""""" table  Actual result: the charge isn't removed    Workaround: if you click somewhere else on the screen, hold the button clicked, move to the 'X' icon and release the button, the charge is removed. (see the attached video)""""""",Bug,"Title: Win8: User can't delete a charge from a report (A)
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. click """"""""Create Report"""""""" button 2. fill in all fields in """"""""Add charge"""""""" section 3. click """"""""Add to report"""""""" 4. click on 'X' icon on the end of the charge row Expected result: the charge should be removed from the """"""""Charges"""""""" table Actual result: the charge isn't removed Workaround: if you click somewhere else on the screen, hold the button clicked, move to the 'X' icon and release the button, the charge is removed. (see the attached video)""""",title+description
TIMOB-10969,12,"""iOS: Kitchen Sink: TextField: keyboard - ASCII keyboard opens up with transparent background.""",""""""" ASCII keyboard opens up with transparent background.    This is not a regression.This even occurs on 2.1.0.GA    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the Kitchen Sink application  2. Tap on Controls>Text Field>Keyboard  3. Press the """"""""ASCII"""""""" button.  4. Press the """""""" Numbers Pad"""""""" button.    Actual Result:  After Step 3:The keyboard opens up in transparent mode.  After Step 4:The keyboard opens up in transparent mode. ( If we press the """"""""Numbers Pad"""""""" button directly i.e. for the first time,then it doesn't opens in transparent mode.)      Expected Result:  After Step 3: The keyboard should open up in transparent mode.  After Step 4: The keyboard should open up in transparent mode.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchen Sink: TextField: keyboard - ASCII keyboard opens up with transparent background.
Description: """" ASCII keyboard opens up with transparent background. This is not a regression.This even occurs on 2.1.0.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the Kitchen Sink application 2. Tap on Controls>Text Field>Keyboard 3. Press the """"""""ASCII"""""""" button. 4. Press the """""""" Numbers Pad"""""""" button. Actual Result: After Step 3:The keyboard opens up in transparent mode. After Step 4:The keyboard opens up in transparent mode. ( If we press the """"""""Numbers Pad"""""""" button directly i.e. for the first time,then it doesn't opens in transparent mode.) Expected Result: After Step 3: The keyboard should open up in transparent mode. After Step 4: The keyboard should open up in transparent mode. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10968,12,"""Android: Textfield - Clicking on 'Enable' toggle button does not disable the textfield and does not bring keyboard down.""","""""""Clicking on 'Enable' toggle button does not disable the textfield and does not bring keyboard down. This issue occurs on the devices with Android version lesser than 3.0.   This is not regression since the issue occurs on 2.1.2 GA as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Go to Kitchensink> Controls> Textfield> The Rest.  2. Click on the textfield. The textfield should be enabled and keyboard should pop up.  3. Click the button 'Enabled' two times(another bug is logged for it). The textfield seems disabled(opacity changes).    Actual:  The keyboard is up and if you type something, it's being typed into textfield.    Expected:  The textfield is disabled. So, keyboard should be down and user should not be able to type anything into it.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Textfield - Clicking on 'Enable' toggle button does not disable the textfield and does not bring keyboard down.
Description: """"Clicking on 'Enable' toggle button does not disable the textfield and does not bring keyboard down. This issue occurs on the devices with Android version lesser than 3.0. This is not regression since the issue occurs on 2.1.2 GA as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Go to Kitchensink> Controls> Textfield> The Rest. 2. Click on the textfield. The textfield should be enabled and keyboard should pop up. 3. Click the button 'Enabled' two times(another bug is logged for it). The textfield seems disabled(opacity changes). Actual: The keyboard is up and if you type something, it's being typed into textfield. Expected: The textfield is disabled. So, keyboard should be down and user should not be able to type anything into it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10967,12,"""Blackberry: Design Module Framework""","""""""Design the module framework that will be used for implementing both our core modules (ex: UI, Network) and third party modules.    h3. Requirements    - Each module should be contained in its own folder (Ex: modules/ui)    - Use the CommonJS API for loading both JS and native modules.    - Define a native API for exporting modules. When a native module      library is loaded and """"""""init"""""""" method should be invoked providing      an exports object. This is simliar to how JS modules export APIs.    - Provide an ABI stable interface to maintain module compatibility with platform releases.      While providing ABI safety across all platform versions may be impractical,      we should still provide compatibility at least between minor version releases      (ex: compile module against 3.0 remains compatible with 3.1, but not 4.0).    - Build system to compile modules and package for deployment.    - Ability to export asset files (ex: images) for use at runtime.    h3. Architectural Designs    References to any architectural documents and diagrams  that will serve as guidelines during the project.    """"""",Story,"Title: Blackberry: Design Module Framework
Description: """"Design the module framework that will be used for implementing both our core modules (ex: UI, Network) and third party modules. h3. Requirements - Each module should be contained in its own folder (Ex: modules/ui) - Use the CommonJS API for loading both JS and native modules. - Define a native API for exporting modules. When a native module library is loaded and """"""""init"""""""" method should be invoked providing an exports object. This is simliar to how JS modules export APIs. - Provide an ABI stable interface to maintain module compatibility with platform releases. While providing ABI safety across all platform versions may be impractical, we should still provide compatibility at least between minor version releases (ex: compile module against 3.0 remains compatible with 3.1, but not 4.0). - Build system to compile modules and package for deployment. - Ability to export asset files (ex: images) for use at runtime. h3. Architectural Designs References to any architectural documents and diagrams that will serve as guidelines during the project. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10966,12,"""iOS: Some of the pictures  in """"Coverflow Remote Files"""" page are missing.""","""""""Description:   Pictures #15 and #24 in """"""""Coverflow Remote Files"""""""" page are missing.    Steps:  1. Launch KitchenSink.   2. Go to Views> Coverflow View > Coverflow Remote Files.  3. Try to open every picture on the page.    Expected results:  All pictures should be successfully loaded.    Actual results:  Pictures #15 and #24 are missing.    Note: broken links http://grin.hq.nasa.gov/IMAGES/SMALL/GPN-2000-000061.jpg  http://grin.hq.nasa.gov/IMAGES/SMALL/GPN-2000-000052.jpg""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Some of the pictures in """"Coverflow Remote Files"""" page are missing.
Description: """"Description: Pictures #15 and #24 in """"""""Coverflow Remote Files"""""""" page are missing. Steps: 1. Launch KitchenSink. 2. Go to Views> Coverflow View > Coverflow Remote Files. 3. Try to open every picture on the page. Expected results: All pictures should be successfully loaded. Actual results: Pictures #15 and #24 are missing. Note: broken links http://grin.hq.nasa.gov/IMAGES/SMALL/GPN-2000-000061.jpg http://grin.hq.nasa.gov/IMAGES/SMALL/GPN-2000-000052.jpg""""",title+description
TIMOB-10965,12,"""iOS: Feature: Add property to determine if the app is being launched by the OS or by the user""","""""""h6.Feature request  Provide a way (check property) to programmatically determine if the app is being launched in the background by the OS or in the foreground by the user.    h6.Test case  When using the [TrackSignificantLocationChange|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10041] in Ti.Geolocation, the app is launched in the background when the users location changes and the app is not running.    h6.Actual behavior  The issue is in the scenario where the app is not launched. The significant location change event will launch the app, firing all code in the app.js file as if the user launched the app.     h6.Customer needs  _""""""""Some of this code I only want processed if its a user-generated event.""""""""_    h3.Expected result  Something similar to the 'source' property in this examples should be exposed on the resume/resumed events.      h6.Repro sequence  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Feature: Add property to determine if the app is being launched by the OS or by the user
Description: """"h6.Feature request Provide a way (check property) to programmatically determine if the app is being launched in the background by the OS or in the foreground by the user. h6.Test case When using the [TrackSignificantLocationChange|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10041] in Ti.Geolocation, the app is launched in the background when the users location changes and the app is not running. h6.Actual behavior The issue is in the scenario where the app is not launched. The significant location change event will launch the app, firing all code in the app.js file as if the user launched the app. h6.Customer needs _""""""""Some of this code I only want processed if its a user-generated event.""""""""_ h3.Expected result Something similar to the 'source' property in this examples should be exposed on the resume/resumed events. h6.Repro sequence """"",title+description
TIMOB-10964,12,"""Blackberry: V8 prebuilt upload/download support.""","""""""To minimize compile time we should add support for using a prebuilt version of V8.  The follow make targets should be added:      - """"""""package"""""""": package a V8 build into a zip for upload    - """"""""upload"""""""": uploads V8 build to hosting (ex: s3)    - """"""""download"""""""": downloads and extracts V8 prebuilt  """"""",Story,"Title: Blackberry: V8 prebuilt upload/download support.
Description: """"To minimize compile time we should add support for using a prebuilt version of V8. The follow make targets should be added: - """"""""package"""""""": package a V8 build into a zip for upload - """"""""upload"""""""": uploads V8 build to hosting (ex: s3) - """"""""download"""""""": downloads and extracts V8 prebuilt """"",title+description
TIMOB-10963,12,"""Blackberry: KS: Fix cosmetic issues from move to R8""","""""""Fix cosmetic issues from move to R8    Most obvious are:    - Fonts are now way bigger  - default theme is dark, so places that set the background white without setting the font color results in very hard to read light gray on white text""""""",Story,"Title: Blackberry: KS: Fix cosmetic issues from move to R8
Description: """"Fix cosmetic issues from move to R8 Most obvious are: - Fonts are now way bigger - default theme is dark, so places that set the background white without setting the font color results in very hard to read light gray on white text""""",title+description
