TIMOB-10960,12,"""iOS:  Zoom in (+) button do not work when map zoomed out on maximum.(iPad 3 -iOS6).""","""""""Description:  Zoom in (+) button do not work when map zoomed out on maximum.    Steps:  1. Launch KitchenSink.  2. Go to BaseUI> Views> Map View.  3. Press zoom out button (-) until maximum (press 4 times).  4. Press zoom in (+) button.    Expected results:  Should be able to zoom in.    Actual results:  Not able to zoom in map.    Note: this occurs on iPad 3 iOS6.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Zoom in (+) button do not work when map zoomed out on maximum.(iPad 3 -iOS6).
Description: """"Description: Zoom in (+) button do not work when map zoomed out on maximum. Steps: 1. Launch KitchenSink. 2. Go to BaseUI> Views> Map View. 3. Press zoom out button (-) until maximum (press 4 times). 4. Press zoom in (+) button. Expected results: Should be able to zoom in. Actual results: Not able to zoom in map. Note: this occurs on iPad 3 iOS6.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10959,12,"""Blackberry: workaround whitespace in path issue of bbndk for mac""","""""""The bbndk toolchain doesn't support paths containing whitespaces.    On mac the build step happens within the path containing the mobile sdk, namely: """"""""~/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx"""""""".  Building from that folder fails because of the space in """"""""Application Support"""""""" and using a symlink doesn't help.    To workaround that, the idea is to modify the build scripts to build from a temporary folder, likely /tmp or it could be configurable by the user from the Studio preferences.""""""",Story,"Title: Blackberry: workaround whitespace in path issue of bbndk for mac
Description: """"The bbndk toolchain doesn't support paths containing whitespaces. On mac the build step happens within the path containing the mobile sdk, namely: """"""""~/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx"""""""". Building from that folder fails because of the space in """"""""Application Support"""""""" and using a symlink doesn't help. To workaround that, the idea is to modify the build scripts to build from a temporary folder, likely /tmp or it could be configurable by the user from the Studio preferences.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10958,12,"""Ti.API: Default background color for new window is black for iOS and transparent for Android""","""""""Description:  Default background color for new window is black for iOS and transparent for Android    Steps:  1. Run the following code on Android and iOS:  https://jira.<USER>org/secure/attachment/24221/app.js    Expected:  Default background color for new window should be the same on Android and iOS    Actual:  Default background color for new window is black for iOS and transparent for Android    """"""",Bug,"Title: Ti.API: Default background color for new window is black for iOS and transparent for Android
Description: """"Description: Default background color for new window is black for iOS and transparent for Android Steps: 1. Run the following code on Android and iOS: https://jira.<USER>org/secure/attachment/24221/app.js Expected: Default background color for new window should be the same on Android and iOS Actual: Default background color for new window is black for iOS and transparent for Android """"",title+description
