TIMOB-10955,12,"""CLI: Windows and Linux parity""","""""""Testing of the CLI has been done mostly on OS X to date. We need to make sure that Windows and Linux are first class citizens. Current known issues that need to be fixed:  * Unzip is broken on Windows  * Progress bars only work properly on OS X  There are most likely other bugs as well so a full sweep of functionality should be performed. Small bugs should be fixed as part of this ticket, but larger bugs/architecture issues should be spun off into separate tickets.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CLI: Windows and Linux parity
Description: """"Testing of the CLI has been done mostly on OS X to date. We need to make sure that Windows and Linux are first class citizens. Current known issues that need to be fixed: * Unzip is broken on Windows * Progress bars only work properly on OS X There are most likely other bugs as well so a full sweep of functionality should be performed. Small bugs should be fixed as part of this ticket, but larger bugs/architecture issues should be spun off into separate tickets.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10954,12,"""CLI: """"setup"""" builtin""","""""""Need to implement a """"""""setup"""""""" command that will create a config.json file for the user, prompting for the required information. This command will not be used by studio (no need). The help screen should detect if the user has a config.json file and display a warning if it doesn't exist.""""""",Story,"Title: CLI: """"setup"""" builtin
Description: """"Need to implement a """"""""setup"""""""" command that will create a config.json file for the user, prompting for the required information. This command will not be used by studio (no need). The help screen should detect if the user has a config.json file and display a warning if it doesn't exist.""""",title+description
