TIMOB-10950,12,"""Android: Kitchensink - Contacts display google synced contacts also when fetched through id whereas it doesn't while picking contacts through display people or contacts picker""","""""""Contacts display google synched contacts also when fetched through id whereas it doesn't while picking contacts through display people or contacts picker.  This is not regression as this issue occurs as far as 2.1.0.    Steps to reproduce:  Add some contacts to contacts list and sync google account with some contacts.  1. Go to Kitchensink> Phone> Contacts.  2. Click on display people.   3. Click on search by Id. enter ids.    Actual:  2. Contacts are displayed but google account contacts are not displayed.   3. It extracts the google contacts and phone contacts both.    Expected:  Same contacts should be retrieved while fetching through 'display people' and ' Search by Id'.   """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Kitchensink - Contacts display google synced contacts also when fetched through id whereas it doesn't while picking contacts through display people or contacts picker
Description: """"Contacts display google synched contacts also when fetched through id whereas it doesn't while picking contacts through display people or contacts picker. This is not regression as this issue occurs as far as 2.1.0. Steps to reproduce: Add some contacts to contacts list and sync google account with some contacts. 1. Go to Kitchensink> Phone> Contacts. 2. Click on display people. 3. Click on search by Id. enter ids. Actual: 2. Contacts are displayed but google account contacts are not displayed. 3. It extracts the google contacts and phone contacts both. Expected: Same contacts should be retrieved while fetching through 'display people' and ' Search by Id'. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10949,12,"""iOS: Picker: getValue method for date picker, created without value property, return null till change event occurs""","""""""The date picker created without a value property returns null for getValue method till date is changed in the picker. This works fine in Android.    This is not a regression. The issue occurs atleast as far as 2.0.1    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create a test application with code below  2. Launch the application and click on the Get Value button and check console  3. Change the date  4. Again click on the Get Value button and check console    Actual Result: After step 2: The getValue returns null  After step 4: The getValue returns the selected value in the picker    Expected Result: After step 2: The getValue should return the selected value (as the current date is shown selected in the picker by default)     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Picker: getValue method for date picker, created without value property, return null till change event occurs
Description: """"The date picker created without a value property returns null for getValue method till date is changed in the picker. This works fine in Android. This is not a regression. The issue occurs atleast as far as 2.0.1 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a test application with code below 2. Launch the application and click on the Get Value button and check console 3. Change the date 4. Again click on the Get Value button and check console Actual Result: After step 2: The getValue returns null After step 4: The getValue returns the selected value in the picker Expected Result: After step 2: The getValue should return the selected value (as the current date is shown selected in the picker by default) """"",title+description
TIMOB-10948,12,"""iOS : Kitchen Sink - Video is not playing when play button is pressed for the first time.""","""""""Video is not playing when play button is pressed for the first time.It maximizes the screen but the video doesn't start playing.    This is not a regression.It even occurs on 2.1.0.GA    Steps To Reproduce:    1. Run the Kitchen Sink application  2. Tap on Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video  3. Press the """"""""Play"""""""" button.  4. Press the done button and and Press the Play button again    Actual Result:  After Step 3:The screen gets maximised but video is not played  After Step 4: The screen gets maximised and the video also starts playing    Expected Result:  After Step 3: Video should start playing  After Step 4: Video should start playing""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Kitchen Sink - Video is not playing when play button is pressed for the first time.
Description: """"Video is not playing when play button is pressed for the first time.It maximizes the screen but the video doesn't start playing. This is not a regression.It even occurs on 2.1.0.GA Steps To Reproduce: 1. Run the Kitchen Sink application 2. Tap on Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video 3. Press the """"""""Play"""""""" button. 4. Press the done button and and Press the Play button again Actual Result: After Step 3:The screen gets maximised but video is not played After Step 4: The screen gets maximised and the video also starts playing Expected Result: After Step 3: Video should start playing After Step 4: Video should start playing""""",title+description
