TIMOB-10892,12,"""iOS: App gives error for, center and span, being nan (iOS 6)""","""""""This is not a regression. It happens on 2.1.2 also.  App works fine on iOS 5.1  Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the app below    2. Run the app on iOS 6    Expected result  2. App should run successfully.    Actual result  2. It gives a error 'Invalid Region <center:nan,nan span:nan,nan> at app.js (line 91)' Snapshot attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App gives error for, center and span, being nan (iOS 6)
Description: """"This is not a regression. It happens on 2.1.2 also. App works fine on iOS 5.1 Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the app below 2. Run the app on iOS 6 Expected result 2. App should run successfully. Actual result 2. It gives a error 'Invalid Region <center:nan,nan span:nan,nan> at app.js (line 91)' Snapshot attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10891,12,"""iOS: App having 'tabgroup containing map' crashes when opened from a window (iOS 6)""","""""""This is not a regression. It happens on 2.1.2 also.  App do not crashes on iOS 5.1  Steps to reproduce:  1. Use the app below    2. Run app on iOS 6.Click the 'Case 1' button.  3. Click the 'Close' button.  4. Click the 'Case 1' button again(may need to repeat steps 2 to 4 couple of times).    Expected result  2. After step 2, a tabgroup with a map in first tab will get open.  3. Tabgroup will be closed.Initial window will be displayed.  4. Again the tabgroup with a map in first tab should get open.    Actual result:  2. After step 2, a tabgroup with a map in first tab will get open.  3. Tabgroup will be closed.Initial window is displayed.  4. The tabgroup opens up, but after a while the app also crahes.    Device logs are attached with the bug.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App having 'tabgroup containing map' crashes when opened from a window (iOS 6)
Description: """"This is not a regression. It happens on 2.1.2 also. App do not crashes on iOS 5.1 Steps to reproduce: 1. Use the app below 2. Run app on iOS 6.Click the 'Case 1' button. 3. Click the 'Close' button. 4. Click the 'Case 1' button again(may need to repeat steps 2 to 4 couple of times). Expected result 2. After step 2, a tabgroup with a map in first tab will get open. 3. Tabgroup will be closed.Initial window will be displayed. 4. Again the tabgroup with a map in first tab should get open. Actual result: 2. After step 2, a tabgroup with a map in first tab will get open. 3. Tabgroup will be closed.Initial window is displayed. 4. The tabgroup opens up, but after a while the app also crahes. Device logs are attached with the bug.""""",title+description
