TIMOB-10880,12,"""Android: Slider value not being set on creation on OS 4.0+""","""""""h3. Problem description  Slider value is not being set on creation on OS 4.0+    h3. Steps to Reproduce  Create a slider with a value property and build the app.  Result: Slider value is not set - it keeps the default value = 0        Note: The slider shows the correct value if the value property is set after the slider has been created.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Slider value not being set on creation on OS 4.0+
Description: """"h3. Problem description Slider value is not being set on creation on OS 4.0+ h3. Steps to Reproduce Create a slider with a value property and build the app. Result: Slider value is not set - it keeps the default value = 0 Note: The slider shows the correct value if the value property is set after the slider has been created.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10879,12,"""Tooling: Android SDK build (scons etc) fails on Windows when using NDK 8b""","""""""h3. Fail case / test case    You need a Windows machine which is configured to build the SDK.    * Install latest NDK (r8b) http://developer.android.com/tools/sdk/ndk/index.html    * Be sure to set your ANDROID_NDK environment variable to point to it (_before_ opening the command window in which you'll run {{scons}}).    * Open a command window.    * Test to be sure that the right NDK will be used: run {{echo %ANDROID_NDK%}} and make sure the result is the path to r8b.    * Go to the titanium mobile source folder and try to build the sdk with {{scons}}.    * Soon after the build starts it should stop with an error like this:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: Android SDK build (scons etc) fails on Windows when using NDK 8b
Description: """"h3. Fail case / test case You need a Windows machine which is configured to build the SDK. * Install latest NDK (r8b) http://developer.android.com/tools/sdk/ndk/index.html * Be sure to set your ANDROID_NDK environment variable to point to it (_before_ opening the command window in which you'll run {{scons}}). * Open a command window. * Test to be sure that the right NDK will be used: run {{echo %ANDROID_NDK%}} and make sure the result is the path to r8b. * Go to the titanium mobile source folder and try to build the sdk with {{scons}}. * Soon after the build starts it should stop with an error like this: """"",title+description
