TIMOB-10868,12,"""Android: TextField.autocorrect returns a default value of undefined, but behaves as if autocorrect == true""","""""""This is related to a doc bug reported on the Titans list.    All platforms were reporting default values at variance with their behavior.    Probably applies to TextArea as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField.autocorrect returns a default value of undefined, but behaves as if autocorrect == true
Description: """"This is related to a doc bug reported on the Titans list. All platforms were reporting default values at variance with their behavior. Probably applies to TextArea as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10867,12,"""iOS: TextField.autocorrect reports false when not set, but behavior actually defaults to true.""","""""""On iOS, TextField.autocorrect returns `false` if it's never been set, but in practice, it behaves as if autocorrect was `true` by default.    All platforms currently behave as if autocorrect was `true`, so we should just correct the default value returned by the platform.    This probably applies to TextArea as well.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TextField.autocorrect reports false when not set, but behavior actually defaults to true.
Description: """"On iOS, TextField.autocorrect returns `false` if it's never been set, but in practice, it behaves as if autocorrect was `true` by default. All platforms currently behave as if autocorrect was `true`, so we should just correct the default value returned by the platform. This probably applies to TextArea as well. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10866,12,"""MobileWeb: Photos in the Chat disappear from the view when a chat message is sent from mobileweb""","""""""In the mobileweb, photos in the Chat disappear when a chat message is sent. On Android and iOS devices, the photos are visible even when a new Chat message is sent. This is not regression, this occurs in 2.1.2.GA also.    Note: The ti.cloud app is not designed to upload photos from mobile web. This issue is only about existing pictures in the Chat that disappear once a chat is sent using mobile web.   Steps to reproduce:  1. In the Studio, clean the project and compile it using """"""""Mobile Web Preview in Browser""""""""  2. Go to Users > Login User  3. Enter """"""""<EMAIL>"""""""" in """"""""Login"""""""" field  4. Enter """"""""1234"""""""" in the """"""""Password"""""""" field, click """"""""Login User"""""""" button and go back to the root level  5. Now click on """"""""Chats"""""""", click on the chat group(sm app, sm g)  6. Observe the chat view which has photos in the chat  7. Now enter a chat message    Actual result:  When a chat is entered using mobile web, all the pictures in the chat disappear. This only happens on mobile web. On iOS and Android devices, the photos are still visible after sending the chat. Please see the attached screenshots.     Expected result:   When a chat is sent using mobile web, the pictures in the chat should still be visible.    Please use the attached cloud project """"""""C1236"""""""".  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Photos in the Chat disappear from the view when a chat message is sent from mobileweb
Description: """"In the mobileweb, photos in the Chat disappear when a chat message is sent. On Android and iOS devices, the photos are visible even when a new Chat message is sent. This is not regression, this occurs in 2.1.2.GA also. Note: The ti.cloud app is not designed to upload photos from mobile web. This issue is only about existing pictures in the Chat that disappear once a chat is sent using mobile web. Steps to reproduce: 1. In the Studio, clean the project and compile it using """"""""Mobile Web Preview in Browser"""""""" 2. Go to Users > Login User 3. Enter """"""""<EMAIL>"""""""" in """"""""Login"""""""" field 4. Enter """"""""1234"""""""" in the """"""""Password"""""""" field, click """"""""Login User"""""""" button and go back to the root level 5. Now click on """"""""Chats"""""""", click on the chat group(sm app, sm g) 6. Observe the chat view which has photos in the chat 7. Now enter a chat message Actual result: When a chat is entered using mobile web, all the pictures in the chat disappear. This only happens on mobile web. On iOS and Android devices, the photos are still visible after sending the chat. Please see the attached screenshots. Expected result: When a chat is sent using mobile web, the pictures in the chat should still be visible. Please use the attached cloud project """"""""C1236"""""""". """"",title+description
TIMOB-10865,12,"""iOS: builder.py adhoc build is broken""","""""""h3. Issue    If i build my project:  builder.py adhoc ...  then the resources of my project are not copied in the app folder    It works with 2.1.2.GA    h3. Steps to Reproduce    1. Create a templated tabbed application in Studio.  2. Publish using adhoc license.  3. Look in the app generated. The package contents do not have KS_nav_ui and KS_nav_views.png files""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: builder.py adhoc build is broken
Description: """"h3. Issue If i build my project: builder.py adhoc ... then the resources of my project are not copied in the app folder It works with 2.1.2.GA h3. Steps to Reproduce 1. Create a templated tabbed application in Studio. 2. Publish using adhoc license. 3. Look in the app generated. The package contents do not have KS_nav_ui and KS_nav_views.png files""""",title+description
TIMOB-10864,12,"""iOS: While playing Video if scaled back down the mainWindow is resized""","""""""h2. Problem  While playing video (local or url) on fullscreen, mainWindow is rotated back to portrait mode after the video is scaled back down:    - Screenshot, before fullscreen/minimize: [http://perso.iloadev.fr/before.png]  - Screenshot, after: [http://perso.iloadev.fr/after.png]    h3.Steps to reproduce  1. wait for video to load  2. play it & put it on full screen (with pinch or button control)  3. Then, minimise the video - (see the """"""""mainWin"""""""" has been resized)    h2. Test case  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');     var mainWin = Titanium.UI.createWindow({      orientationModes:[Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT],      exitOnClose:true,      navBarHidden:true,      fullscreen:true,      title:'Slide Box',      backgroundColor:'#ffffff',      zIndex:0  });     var VideoPlayer=Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer({      zIndex:3,      top:350,      left:300,      url:"""""""""""""""",      backgroundColor:""""""""#000000"""""""",      mediaControlStyle:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_EMBEDDED,      scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT,      width:308,      height:208,      visible:true,      url:""""""""http://movies.apple.com/media/us/ipad/2010/tours/apple-ipad-video-us-20100127_r848-9cie.mov""""""""  });  mainWin.add(VideoPlayer);     mainWin.open();      h2. Community forum thread  [http://developer.<USER>com/question/142048/nice-videoplayer-ios-bug-with-212]""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: While playing Video if scaled back down the mainWindow is resized
Description: """"h2. Problem While playing video (local or url) on fullscreen, mainWindow is rotated back to portrait mode after the video is scaled back down: - Screenshot, before fullscreen/minimize: [http://perso.iloadev.fr/before.png] - Screenshot, after: [http://perso.iloadev.fr/after.png] h3.Steps to reproduce 1. wait for video to load 2. play it & put it on full screen (with pinch or button control) 3. Then, minimise the video - (see the """"""""mainWin"""""""" has been resized) h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var mainWin = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ orientationModes:[Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT], exitOnClose:true, navBarHidden:true, fullscreen:true, title:'Slide Box', backgroundColor:'#ffffff', zIndex:0 }); var VideoPlayer=Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer({ zIndex:3, top:350, left:300, url:"""""""""""""""", backgroundColor:""""""""#000000"""""""", mediaControlStyle:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_EMBEDDED, scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT, width:308, height:208, visible:true, url:""""""""http://movies.apple.com/media/us/ipad/2010/tours/apple-ipad-video-us-20100127_r848-9cie.mov"""""""" }); mainWin.add(VideoPlayer); mainWin.open(); h2. Community forum thread [http://developer.<USER>com/question/142048/nice-videoplayer-ios-bug-with-212]""""",title+description
TIMOB-10863,12,"""Android: Application restarts when orientation changes and targetSdkVersion is 13 or higher""","""""""If an app targets Android api level 13 (Honeycomb MR2, aka Android 3.2) or higher, the {{screenSize}} config change (which occurs when the orientation changes, for example) is not handled automatically by Android, and thus causes (by default) an activity restart (cf http://developer.android.com/reference/android/R.attr.html#configChanges).  We don't accept activity restarts in Titanium and instead just restart the app (i.e., close all activities and restart the root activity).  Traditionally we overcome the problem with orientation changes using the {{configChanges}} attribute's {{orientation}} value in our Activity entries in AndroidManifest.xml.  But now {{screenSize}} also needs to be handled.    So if an app developer changes their tiapp.xml to add {{android:targetApiLevel=""""""""13""""""""}} (or higher) -- which is something they would do to get an ICS look-and-feel, for example, and will therefore occur more and more -- their app will restart (on 3.2 or higher devices) when the orientation changes because of the unhandled screenSize.  So we need to add  {{screenSize}} to the {{configChanges}} in AndroidManifest.xml Activity entries.  However, it's not that easy: to do that, we need be sure to also build against api 13 or higher, since building against an older version will cause aapt to fail if {{screenSize}} is in there; this fails the application build.  So a somewhat clever solution is required.    h3. Fail Case / Test Case      * Create a Titanium mobile app.    * Change its tiapp.xml so that the <android> section looks like this:        * Replace the app.js with this:    {code:title=""""""""app.js""""""""}  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Root Window',      backgroundColor:'#fff',   exitOnClose: true  }),  btn = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: """"""""Open Heavyweight Window"""""""",   left: """"""""16dp"""""""", right: """"""""16dp"""""""", height: """"""""48dp"""""""",   bottom: """"""""16dp""""""""  });    win.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({   text: """"""""This is the root window"""""""",   color: """"""""#000"""""""",   height: """"""""48dp""""""""  }));    win.add(btn);    btn.on(""""""""click"""""""", function() {   var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor: """"""""#f00"""""""",    title: """"""""New Activity"""""""",    fullscreen: false   });   w.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({    text: """"""""This is a new Activity"""""""",    height: """"""""48dp"""""""",    color: """"""""#fff""""""""   }));   w.open();  });    win.open();  {code}    * Run the app on 3.2 or higher device.    * After the app loads, click the """"""""Open Heavyweight Window"""""""" button.    * After the red window opens, turn the device to a different orientation (i.e., from portrait to landscape or vice-versa).    * In the fail case, the app will actually close completely and re-open back at the first (white, not red) window.  When testing the fix, the app should not close and the red window should still be showing.    * Also build and run the app on a pre-3.2 device (a 2.3 phone, for example) to be sure nothing is broken for older versions of android.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Application restarts when orientation changes and targetSdkVersion is 13 or higher
Description: """"If an app targets Android api level 13 (Honeycomb MR2, aka Android 3.2) or higher, the {{screenSize}} config change (which occurs when the orientation changes, for example) is not handled automatically by Android, and thus causes (by default) an activity restart (cf http://developer.android.com/reference/android/R.attr.html#configChanges). We don't accept activity restarts in Titanium and instead just restart the app (i.e., close all activities and restart the root activity). Traditionally we overcome the problem with orientation changes using the {{configChanges}} attribute's {{orientation}} value in our Activity entries in AndroidManifest.xml. But now {{screenSize}} also needs to be handled. So if an app developer changes their tiapp.xml to add {{android:targetApiLevel=""""""""13""""""""}} (or higher) -- which is something they would do to get an ICS look-and-feel, for example, and will therefore occur more and more -- their app will restart (on 3.2 or higher devices) when the orientation changes because of the unhandled screenSize. So we need to add {{screenSize}} to the {{configChanges}} in AndroidManifest.xml Activity entries. However, it's not that easy: to do that, we need be sure to also build against api 13 or higher, since building against an older version will cause aapt to fail if {{screenSize}} is in there; this fails the application build. So a somewhat clever solution is required. h3. Fail Case / Test Case * Create a Titanium mobile app. * Change its tiapp.xml so that the <android> section looks like this: * Replace the app.js with this: {code:title=""""""""app.js""""""""} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Root Window', backgroundColor:'#fff', exitOnClose: true }), btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: """"""""Open Heavyweight Window"""""""", left: """"""""16dp"""""""", right: """"""""16dp"""""""", height: """"""""48dp"""""""", bottom: """"""""16dp"""""""" }); win.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: """"""""This is the root window"""""""", color: """"""""#000"""""""", height: """"""""48dp"""""""" })); win.add(btn); btn.on(""""""""click"""""""", function() { var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: """"""""#f00"""""""", title: """"""""New Activity"""""""", fullscreen: false }); w.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: """"""""This is a new Activity"""""""", height: """"""""48dp"""""""", color: """"""""#fff"""""""" })); w.open(); }); win.open(); {code} * Run the app on 3.2 or higher device. * After the app loads, click the """"""""Open Heavyweight Window"""""""" button. * After the red window opens, turn the device to a different orientation (i.e., from portrait to landscape or vice-versa). * In the fail case, the app will actually close completely and re-open back at the first (white, not red) window. When testing the fix, the app should not close and the red window should still be showing. * Also build and run the app on a pre-3.2 device (a 2.3 phone, for example) to be sure nothing is broken for older versions of android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10862,12,"""iOS: Tooling: Build fails if Application_Id field contains underscore ( '_' ).""","""""""It is not a regression. Issue exists as far as 2.1.2    Steps to reproduce:  1. Make a project with application id field having an underscore(eg - 'test_case')  2. Try to install this project on device having iOS 6.    Expected result  1. It should get installed successfully on device    Actual result  It gives an error mentioned below and build fails-  [ERROR] (null): error: CFBundleIdentifier 'com.<USER>Build_timob7674' contains illegal character '_'   [ERROR]   [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tooling: Build fails if Application_Id field contains underscore ( '_' ).
Description: """"It is not a regression. Issue exists as far as 2.1.2 Steps to reproduce: 1. Make a project with application id field having an underscore(eg - 'test_case') 2. Try to install this project on device having iOS 6. Expected result 1. It should get installed successfully on device Actual result It gives an error mentioned below and build fails- [ERROR] (null): error: CFBundleIdentifier 'com.<USER>Build_timob7674' contains illegal character '_' [ERROR] [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):""""",title+description
