TIMOB-10776,12,"""CodeProcessor: Implement full support for unknown data types""","""""""Many internal methods take action depending on types. Every time this happens, unknown data types must be explicitly handled but are currently only handled haphazardly. Need to check every call to Base.type() and every reference to <instance>.className.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Implement full support for unknown data types
Description: """"Many internal methods take action depending on types. Every time this happens, unknown data types must be explicitly handled but are currently only handled haphazardly. Need to check every call to Base.type() and every reference to <instance>.className.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10775,12,"""CodeProcessor: Inject browser add-on APIs in a plugin""","""""""We need to implement the following methods that the Titanium API borrows from the browser world:  * console  ** debug  ** error  ** info  ** log  ** warn  * alert  * setTimeout  * setInterval  * clearTimeout  * clearInterval""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Inject browser add-on APIs in a plugin
Description: """"We need to implement the following methods that the Titanium API borrows from the browser world: * console ** debug ** error ** info ** log ** warn * alert * setTimeout * setInterval * clearTimeout * clearInterval""""",title+description
TIMOB-10774,12,"""MobileWeb: Only send ti.geo analytics event once when user sets a ti.geolocation callback""","""""""Currently, when user sets ti.geolocation, ti.geo analytics events are sent for every callback. We only care about one lat/long pair, and it's wasteful to send all ti.geo info.    Testing steps:   1. Launch a simple app with this code in production (Package in iOS/Android App store)    2. Drive around a little bit to trigger location change (home -> work. etc.)  3. Put app's name and GUID in this ticket so we can look up analytics events that was fired.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Only send ti.geo analytics event once when user sets a ti.geolocation callback
Description: """"Currently, when user sets ti.geolocation, ti.geo analytics events are sent for every callback. We only care about one lat/long pair, and it's wasteful to send all ti.geo info. Testing steps: 1. Launch a simple app with this code in production (Package in iOS/Android App store) 2. Drive around a little bit to trigger location change (home -> work. etc.) 3. Put app's name and GUID in this ticket so we can look up analytics events that was fired.""""",title+description
