TIMOB-10691,12,"""Android: Android app crashes when Annotation latitude/longitude is not set in createAnnotation()""","""""""h2. Problem    On Android, you must set the {{latitude}} and {{longitude}} properties of a {{Ti.Map.Annotation}} in the {{createAnnotation()}} function, otherwise your app will crash with the error log below when Android attempts to add the annotation to a {{Ti.Map.View}} at runtime.    iOS and Mobileweb can specify these properties at any time before the annotations are added and work fine.    h2. Proposed Fix    Allow longitude and latitude to be set on an Annotation anytime before the annotations are assigned to a {{Ti.Map.View}} on Android.    h2. Test Case        h2. android error log    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Android app crashes when Annotation latitude/longitude is not set in createAnnotation()
Description: """"h2. Problem On Android, you must set the {{latitude}} and {{longitude}} properties of a {{Ti.Map.Annotation}} in the {{createAnnotation()}} function, otherwise your app will crash with the error log below when Android attempts to add the annotation to a {{Ti.Map.View}} at runtime. iOS and Mobileweb can specify these properties at any time before the annotations are added and work fine. h2. Proposed Fix Allow longitude and latitude to be set on an Annotation anytime before the annotations are assigned to a {{Ti.Map.View}} on Android. h2. Test Case h2. android error log """"",title+description
TIMOB-10689,12,"""Android: customer app is getting minimized unexpectedly after upgrade to 2.1.2 CI""","""""""h3. Problem description    In EMC NGOA project we are facing another unexpected issue which was not present in 2.0 GA  After login and entering the numeric passcode, the app is being minimized in the background.    We are investigating and collected the log (attached), any feedback or help it's much appreciated.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: customer app is getting minimized unexpectedly after upgrade to 2.1.2 CI
Description: """"h3. Problem description In EMC NGOA project we are facing another unexpected issue which was not present in 2.0 GA After login and entering the numeric passcode, the app is being minimized in the background. We are investigating and collected the log (attached), any feedback or help it's much appreciated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10688,12,"""CLI: Expose Docgen.py and YAML as Alternative to Markdown in Modules""","""""""h1. New Feature  Expose docgen.py / YAML so that our modules' documentation can be rewritten. The docgen.py looks hard coded for use with the core Titanium Mobile, and it isn't packaged up with the SDK.     h2. Example Usage  Take a look at the attached Barcode.yml. If this were included in a module's """"""""documentation"""""""" folder, build.py on iOS or ant on Android should generate an index.html etc in the distribution folder.    I'm guessing we'll need platform specific tickets for this... let me know.    * *validate.py* should be able to be run against module docs that have references to Titanium.* Currently, the module docs need to be copied to the apidoc folder in titanium_mobile so that it can validate without throwing errors that Titanium.* could not be found. I believe if validate.py could accept multiple -d directories it would fix this.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Expose Docgen.py and YAML as Alternative to Markdown in Modules
Description: """"h1. New Feature Expose docgen.py / YAML so that our modules' documentation can be rewritten. The docgen.py looks hard coded for use with the core Titanium Mobile, and it isn't packaged up with the SDK. h2. Example Usage Take a look at the attached Barcode.yml. If this were included in a module's """"""""documentation"""""""" folder, build.py on iOS or ant on Android should generate an index.html etc in the distribution folder. I'm guessing we'll need platform specific tickets for this... let me know. * *validate.py* should be able to be run against module docs that have references to Titanium.* Currently, the module docs need to be copied to the apidoc folder in titanium_mobile so that it can validate without throwing errors that Titanium.* could not be found. I believe if validate.py could accept multiple -d directories it would fix this.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10687,12,"""KitchenSink: KitchenSink crashes on launch on Android Emulator 2.2 and Android device 2.2""","""""""Description:   KitchenSink crashes on launch on Android Emulator 2.2 and Android device 2.2.  Getting [ERROR][TiApplication(  419)] (KrollRuntimeThread) [819,819] APP PROXY: ti.modules.titanium.app.AppModule@45063970.    This is regression, does not happen on 2.1.2    Steps to reproduce:  Run Refactored KitchenSink on Android Emulator 2.2/Android device 2.2    Actual result:  The app crashes    Expected result:  The app opens successfully""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: KitchenSink crashes on launch on Android Emulator 2.2 and Android device 2.2
Description: """"Description: KitchenSink crashes on launch on Android Emulator 2.2 and Android device 2.2. Getting [ERROR][TiApplication( 419)] (KrollRuntimeThread) [819,819] APP PROXY: ti.modules.titanium.app.AppModule@45063970. This is regression, does not happen on 2.1.2 Steps to reproduce: Run Refactored KitchenSink on Android Emulator 2.2/Android device 2.2 Actual result: The app crashes Expected result: The app opens successfully""""",title+description
TIMOB-10686,12,"""iOS:Textfield:'Click' event always taking precedence to 'Focus' event,making textfield un-editable.""","""""""This is not a regression.'Click' event did not fired at all till 2.1.2.    Till 2.1.2, no 'click' event is fired on textfield.  In 2.2.0, when 'click' and 'focus' both events are added to a textfield, 'click' event always gets fired on clicking textfield. So the user is unable to edit the textfield.    Note: Sometimes both event fire for the first time. But afterwards,it follows the bug.    Steps to reproduce.  1. Run the code below on simulator      2. Click the top most textfield(tf)  3. Click the middle textfield(tf1)  4. Click the bottom most textfield(tf2)    Expected result  2. Afte step 2, the focus and click event should get fired on textfield and it should become editable.  3. After step 3, the focus event should get fired on textfield and it should become editable.  4. After step 4, the 'click' event should get fired on textfield and it should become editable.    Actual result  2. Afte step 2, the click event is fired on textfield and it do not becomes editable.  3. After step 3, the focus event gets fired on textfield and it becomes editable.  4. After step 4, the 'click' event gets fired on textfield and it do not becomes editable.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS:Textfield:'Click' event always taking precedence to 'Focus' event,making textfield un-editable.
Description: """"This is not a regression.'Click' event did not fired at all till 2.1.2. Till 2.1.2, no 'click' event is fired on textfield. In 2.2.0, when 'click' and 'focus' both events are added to a textfield, 'click' event always gets fired on clicking textfield. So the user is unable to edit the textfield. Note: Sometimes both event fire for the first time. But afterwards,it follows the bug. Steps to reproduce. 1. Run the code below on simulator 2. Click the top most textfield(tf) 3. Click the middle textfield(tf1) 4. Click the bottom most textfield(tf2) Expected result 2. Afte step 2, the focus and click event should get fired on textfield and it should become editable. 3. After step 3, the focus event should get fired on textfield and it should become editable. 4. After step 4, the 'click' event should get fired on textfield and it should become editable. Actual result 2. Afte step 2, the click event is fired on textfield and it do not becomes editable. 3. After step 3, the focus event gets fired on textfield and it becomes editable. 4. After step 4, the 'click' event gets fired on textfield and it do not becomes editable.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10685,12,"""Android: distribute apps to the Play Store fails if the code contains """"const""""""","""""""h2. Problem description    When creating an app containing constansts declared with const, the app works untill you try to distribute to the store. In that case, the following error is shown:     ~~~  ERROR - Parse error. Unsupported syntax: CONST  ~~~    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a simple app with a constant:    ~~~  const test = """"""""Hello World!"""""""";  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: 'black'  });  alert(test);  win.open();  ~~~    2. Test the app on the device or simulator: everything works.  3. Distribute the app: the app fails with the error above""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: distribute apps to the Play Store fails if the code contains """"const""""
Description: """"h2. Problem description When creating an app containing constansts declared with const, the app works untill you try to distribute to the store. In that case, the following error is shown: ~~~ ERROR - Parse error. Unsupported syntax: CONST ~~~ h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a simple app with a constant: ~~~ const test = """"""""Hello World!""""""""; var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'black' }); alert(test); win.open(); ~~~ 2. Test the app on the device or simulator: everything works. 3. Distribute the app: the app fails with the error above""""",title+description
TIMOB-10684,12,"""iOS: Ti.App.getArguments() fails when opening the app from a local notification""","""""""h3. Problem description  Error when opening an app from local notification using Ti.App.getArguments()     h3. Sample code and steps to reproduce    Run the sample code.  Local notification is correctly received. When clicking on the notification, everything works fine if the app is backgrounded. If the app is closed, an error is thrown and the app is not opened (see attached error log)    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.App.getArguments() fails when opening the app from a local notification
Description: """"h3. Problem description Error when opening an app from local notification using Ti.App.getArguments() h3. Sample code and steps to reproduce Run the sample code. Local notification is correctly received. When clicking on the notification, everything works fine if the app is backgrounded. If the app is closed, an error is thrown and the app is not opened (see attached error log) """"",title+description
TIMOB-10683,12,"""iOS: TextField - In iOS simulator, the capitalized word gets appended to existing word when creating an ACS custom object""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch attached zip to an iOS Simulator  2. In the app, go to *Users > Login User*. Login using *a/1234*  3. Next, go to Custom Objects > Create Object  4. Specify a class name and property key. Then, press *Add New Property*  5. In the newly created text field, type a word using your keyboard (not soft keyboard) e.g. *green*  6. Wait for the autocapitalization hint to appear (see green.png)  7. Press enter on your keyboard  8. Go to http://cloud.<USER>com/38ff33d9-dc4d-4fd3-bd71-c7e84efe216c/objects. Login using *luuwilson+<EMAIL>/1234*. Make sure development tab is selected.    Actual: Capitalized word is appended to existing word. See bug.png  Expected: The capitalized word should not be appended to exiting word.    Note:  * This is not a regression  * This bug does not occur on Android devices/emulators or iOS devices  * Source code is in Resources/window/customObjects/create.js  ** Look at doCreateNewProperty() and submitForm()""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TextField - In iOS simulator, the capitalized word gets appended to existing word when creating an ACS custom object
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch attached zip to an iOS Simulator 2. In the app, go to *Users > Login User*. Login using *a/1234* 3. Next, go to Custom Objects > Create Object 4. Specify a class name and property key. Then, press *Add New Property* 5. In the newly created text field, type a word using your keyboard (not soft keyboard) e.g. *green* 6. Wait for the autocapitalization hint to appear (see green.png) 7. Press enter on your keyboard 8. Go to http://cloud.<USER>com/38ff33d9-dc4d-4fd3-bd71-c7e84efe216c/objects. Login using *luuwilson+<EMAIL>/1234*. Make sure development tab is selected. Actual: Capitalized word is appended to existing word. See bug.png Expected: The capitalized word should not be appended to exiting word. Note: * This is not a regression * This bug does not occur on Android devices/emulators or iOS devices * Source code is in Resources/window/customObjects/create.js ** Look at doCreateNewProperty() and submitForm()""""",title+description
TIMOB-10682,12,"""KitchenSink: Application crashes when trying to open """"Point Conversion"""" (iOS 6 Beta 4)""","""""""Description:  Point Conversion crashes when tying to open the application. Crash only occurs on iPhone with beta version 6.   This is not a regression. Behavior also occurs on 2.1.1.     Steps:  1.Open BaseUI >Views >Point Conversion.    Expected results:  Application opens successfully.    Actual results:  Application crashes.     """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Application crashes when trying to open """"Point Conversion"""" (iOS 6 Beta 4)
Description: """"Description: Point Conversion crashes when tying to open the application. Crash only occurs on iPhone with beta version 6. This is not a regression. Behavior also occurs on 2.1.1. Steps: 1.Open BaseUI >Views >Point Conversion. Expected results: Application opens successfully. Actual results: Application crashes. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10680,12,"""TiMapView regionChanged events do not update the region in the map""","""""""// mapView is a TiMapView object  var regionA = mapView.getRegion(), regionB, regionC;  mapView.addEventListener('regionChanged', function(event) {    regionB = {latitude: event.latitude, longitude: event.longitude, latitudeDelta..... };    // regionB is updated properly    regionC = mapView.getRegion();    // regionC is still the same as regionA  });    // I had to work around this by tracking the viewport separately""""""",Bug,"Title: TiMapView regionChanged events do not update the region in the map
Description: """"// mapView is a TiMapView object var regionA = mapView.getRegion(), regionB, regionC; mapView.addEventListener('regionChanged', function(event) { regionB = {latitude: event.latitude, longitude: event.longitude, latitudeDelta..... }; // regionB is updated properly regionC = mapView.getRegion(); // regionC is still the same as regionA }); // I had to work around this by tracking the viewport separately""""",title+description
TIMOB-10679,12,"""Titanium.Map.View.removeAnnotations([]) did not remove annotations""","""""""mapView is object of type TiMapView    var toRemove = []  var ar = mapView.getAnnotations();  // ... push some elements of ar[] into toRemove  mapView.removeAnnotations(toRemove);    // all annotations remain  // mapView.removeAnnotation(ar[i]) removing annotations one at a time worked.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.Map.View.removeAnnotations([]) did not remove annotations
Description: """"mapView is object of type TiMapView var toRemove = [] var ar = mapView.getAnnotations(); // ... push some elements of ar[] into toRemove mapView.removeAnnotations(toRemove); // all annotations remain // mapView.removeAnnotation(ar[i]) removing annotations one at a time worked. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10678,12,"""iOS: App rejected for use of non-public API '_updateTitleView'""","""""""Submitting an app built using the above specs, Apple rejects based on grounds of using a non-public API of theirs.    {quote}  We found that your app uses one or more non-public APIs, which is not in compliance with the App Store Review Guidelines. The use of non-public APIs is not permissible because it can lead to a poor user experience should these APIs change.     We found the following non-public API/s in your app:     _updateTitleView  {quote}    After searching through all project files, the string 'updateTitleView' appears only in Titanium build files, not any code written by myself.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App rejected for use of non-public API '_updateTitleView'
Description: """"Submitting an app built using the above specs, Apple rejects based on grounds of using a non-public API of theirs. {quote} We found that your app uses one or more non-public APIs, which is not in compliance with the App Store Review Guidelines. The use of non-public APIs is not permissible because it can lead to a poor user experience should these APIs change. We found the following non-public API/s in your app: _updateTitleView {quote} After searching through all project files, the string 'updateTitleView' appears only in Titanium build files, not any code written by myself.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10675,12,"""CLI: Allow android apps to automatically launch when deployed to device""","""""""Allow titanium apps to launch automatically when deployed to android device.    Currently the app must be manually launched after it is 'installed'.    Note: apps installed to emulator are automatically launched.    Proposed Usage:    1. Create titanium project.  2. Deploy to Android device.    Expected Result:    App should install and automatically launch.""""""",New Feature,"Title: CLI: Allow android apps to automatically launch when deployed to device
Description: """"Allow titanium apps to launch automatically when deployed to android device. Currently the app must be manually launched after it is 'installed'. Note: apps installed to emulator are automatically launched. Proposed Usage: 1. Create titanium project. 2. Deploy to Android device. Expected Result: App should install and automatically launch.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10674,12,"""Tooling: Add a Finalize Hook into the plugin build script""","""""""Add a """"""""finalize"""""""" hook to the plug-in build script so that a plug-in gets a chance to cleanup in case a plug-in build exits before post-build hook is invoked.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Add a Finalize Hook into the plugin build script
Description: """"Add a """"""""finalize"""""""" hook to the plug-in build script so that a plug-in gets a chance to cleanup in case a plug-in build exits before post-build hook is invoked.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10673,12,"""CodeProcessor: Implement support for incremental building""","""""""We should detect what, if any, files have changed since the last run. This means we need mechanisms to:    * Compare current options to previous options (some of them will force a complete re-run)  * Determine what code a change in a file affects (it could affect other files which need to be re-run)  * Have mechanisms for serializing data necessary to do a re-run with cached information""""""",New Feature,"Title: CodeProcessor: Implement support for incremental building
Description: """"We should detect what, if any, files have changed since the last run. This means we need mechanisms to: * Compare current options to previous options (some of them will force a complete re-run) * Determine what code a change in a file affects (it could affect other files which need to be re-run) * Have mechanisms for serializing data necessary to do a re-run with cached information""""",title+description
TIMOB-10672,12,"""CodeProcessor: Implement support for modules in the Code processor""","""""""Right now, the code processor/require-provider don't support modules and will simply indicate that the module could not be found.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Implement support for modules in the Code processor
Description: """"Right now, the code processor/require-provider don't support modules and will simply indicate that the module could not be found.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10671,12,"""Create C++ macros to ease adding properties to Titanium objects.""",,Story,Title: Create C++ macros to ease adding properties to Titanium objects.,title-only
TIMOB-10643,12,"""CodeProcessor: Add code annotation capabilities""","""""""We should add the ability to add annotations for the code processor in code similar to how JSHint interprets /*global foo*/    There are a few key features we need to support:  * Whether or not the file should be evaluated in ambiguous mode if it's not processed  ** If it should be evaluated as a require or a Ti.include  ** Conditionals (e.g. should only be evaluated if on Android)  * Perhaps add hints for values being passed in to delayed functions (e.g. event handlers)  * Ability to suppress warnings""""""",Story,"Title: CodeProcessor: Add code annotation capabilities
Description: """"We should add the ability to add annotations for the code processor in code similar to how JSHint interprets /*global foo*/ There are a few key features we need to support: * Whether or not the file should be evaluated in ambiguous mode if it's not processed ** If it should be evaluated as a require or a Ti.include ** Conditionals (e.g. should only be evaluated if on Android) * Perhaps add hints for values being passed in to delayed functions (e.g. event handlers) * Ability to suppress warnings""""",title+description
TIMOB-10642,12,"""Support value bags (json) in object constructors.""",,Story,Title: Support value bags (json) in object constructors.,title-only
TIMOB-10641,12,"""KitchenSink: Imageview should be set to display appcelerator logo image with correct aspect ratio on android.""","""""""While testing Kitchen Sink fix (TIMOB-9365)Image Views I noticed an image being stretched vertically.    It is not a regression, as the image did not exist prior.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run Kitchen Sink > Base UI > Views > Image Views > Basic  2. An Image of <USER>s logo appears    Actual result:  See attachments    Expected result:  The image should look well-formed  """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Imageview should be set to display appcelerator logo image with correct aspect ratio on android.
Description: """"While testing Kitchen Sink fix (TIMOB-9365)Image Views I noticed an image being stretched vertically. It is not a regression, as the image did not exist prior. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run Kitchen Sink > Base UI > Views > Image Views > Basic 2. An Image of <USER>s logo appears Actual result: See attachments Expected result: The image should look well-formed """"",title+description
