TIMOB-10605,12,"""Win8: Implement Create expense report functionality""","""""""The attached wireframe is a rough concept. There will be an updated wireframe provided by Susan later in the week.    - when the page is open for the first time, the charges table is empty  - the user uses the left panel to enter charge information; all fields are simple text fields without special logic or formatting  - tap """"""""Add to Report"""""""" button to add the charge as a table entry in the report  - there is no sorting in the report table, all new charges are added at the top of the table  - the report table should be a simple table, taking up the whole right panel width, there is no need in alternating background (I didn't bother redoing style in the wireframe)  - expense report title is specified by typing it in the text field at the top of the right section""""""",Story,"Title: Win8: Implement Create expense report functionality
Description: """"The attached wireframe is a rough concept. There will be an updated wireframe provided by Susan later in the week. - when the page is open for the first time, the charges table is empty - the user uses the left panel to enter charge information; all fields are simple text fields without special logic or formatting - tap """"""""Add to Report"""""""" button to add the charge as a table entry in the report - there is no sorting in the report table, all new charges are added at the top of the table - the report table should be a simple table, taking up the whole right panel width, there is no need in alternating background (I didn't bother redoing style in the wireframe) - expense report title is specified by typing it in the text field at the top of the right section""""",title+description
TIMOB-10604,12,"""Android: Animation - Text font size changes while rotating a view from 0 to 45 degrees""","""""""Text font size changes while rotating a view from 0 to 45 degrees.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Download and import the attached app.  2. Launch the app.  3. Click on blue box with text 'MENU' on it.    Actual:  The size of the text changes while rotation whereas the size of the box remains same.    Expected:  The size of the text should be same.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Animation - Text font size changes while rotating a view from 0 to 45 degrees
Description: """"Text font size changes while rotating a view from 0 to 45 degrees. Steps to reproduce: 1. Download and import the attached app. 2. Launch the app. 3. Click on blue box with text 'MENU' on it. Actual: The size of the text changes while rotation whereas the size of the box remains same. Expected: The size of the text should be same. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10603,12,"""iOS: When rotate webview from portrait to landscape font size is getting large""","""""""I have a sample application which open a webview and the web view is showing one html content. When I rotate web view from portrait to landscape font size of the web view content is getting enlarged and when coming back to the portrait then font size is also reset to the original size. It is happening only in iPhone and in android it is working fine.     +Source Code+    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: When rotate webview from portrait to landscape font size is getting large
Description: """"I have a sample application which open a webview and the web view is showing one html content. When I rotate web view from portrait to landscape font size of the web view content is getting enlarged and when coming back to the portrait then font size is also reset to the original size. It is happening only in iPhone and in android it is working fine. +Source Code+ """"",title+description
TIMOB-10602,12,"""Android: When there are Multiple Search Bars Return key goes to the next SearchBar instead of populating results of the current Search Bar.""","""""""When there are more than one search bars in a window and when we type something in the first search bar and return key is pressed, the next search bar is getting focused instead of populating the results for the first search bar. When the last search bar has some value entered and when return key is pressed it stays on that search bar which is the exact behavior that is expected for the first Search Bar. It works fine on iOS.    h4.Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the application with the below sample app.js.  2. Type something in the first Search bar and then press the return key on the keyboard.  Expected Result: The control should stay in the first search bar.  Actual Result: It goes to the second search bar Automatically on pressing the return key.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: When there are Multiple Search Bars Return key goes to the next SearchBar instead of populating results of the current Search Bar.
Description: """"When there are more than one search bars in a window and when we type something in the first search bar and return key is pressed, the next search bar is getting focused instead of populating the results for the first search bar. When the last search bar has some value entered and when return key is pressed it stays on that search bar which is the exact behavior that is expected for the first Search Bar. It works fine on iOS. h4.Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the application with the below sample app.js. 2. Type something in the first Search bar and then press the return key on the keyboard. Expected Result: The control should stay in the first search bar. Actual Result: It goes to the second search bar Automatically on pressing the return key. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10601,12,"""ButtonBar:  The keyboard's Toolbar does not remain static, it redraws itself on each click event.""","""""""Description:  ButtonBar does not remain static, it redraws itself on each click event.    It is not a regression, it occurs on 2.1.1 as well.    Test steps:  1. Run this code from TIMOB-6463    2. Touch the first row textfield   3. Press """"""""next"""""""" button on the keyboard's Toolbar    Actual result:  The Toolbar is redrawing itself    Expected result:  The Toolbar should remain static      """"""",Bug,"Title: ButtonBar: The keyboard's Toolbar does not remain static, it redraws itself on each click event.
Description: """"Description: ButtonBar does not remain static, it redraws itself on each click event. It is not a regression, it occurs on 2.1.1 as well. Test steps: 1. Run this code from TIMOB-6463 2. Touch the first row textfield 3. Press """"""""next"""""""" button on the keyboard's Toolbar Actual result: The Toolbar is redrawing itself Expected result: The Toolbar should remain static """"",title+description
TIMOB-10600,12,"""CodeProcessor: Implement event processing plugin for Code Processor""","""""""Event listener callbacks (functions supplied to Ti.Proxy.addEventListener) are currently not evaluated. We should implement a plugin that processes this code. The code should be processed with an event value of unknown (at least for now) and called in ambiguous mode.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Implement event processing plugin for Code Processor
Description: """"Event listener callbacks (functions supplied to Ti.Proxy.addEventListener) are currently not evaluated. We should implement a plugin that processes this code. The code should be processed with an event value of unknown (at least for now) and called in ambiguous mode.""""",title+description
