TIMOB-10598,12,"""Android: KS: Platform > XHR > Error Callback -v8: Different response on different devices""","""""""Description:  Receive a different response on different devices.  On Motorola Droid (2.2.3) received: 'www.fre100.com'  On Asus Nexus7 (4.1) received: 'Unable to resolve host """"""""www.fre100.com"""""""": No address associated with hostname'    It is not a regression it occurs in 2.1.1.GA    Steps to reproduce:  Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Platform > XHR > Error Callback""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS: Platform > XHR > Error Callback -v8: Different response on different devices
Description: """"Description: Receive a different response on different devices. On Motorola Droid (2.2.3) received: 'www.fre100.com' On Asus Nexus7 (4.1) received: 'Unable to resolve host """"""""www.fre100.com"""""""": No address associated with hostname' It is not a regression it occurs in 2.1.1.GA Steps to reproduce: Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Platform > XHR > Error Callback""""",title+description
TIMOB-10597,12,"""iOS: Not scaling imageView when images property is assigned an array of images for animation""","""""""When an imageView is created with an """"""""images"""""""" property, iOS no longer respects the width and height specified by the imageView.  In my case the image is drawn much larger and off the screen.  It may be rendering the image to it's actual size, rather than scaling it to the dimensions specified.    When the imageView specified a single image via the """"""""image"""""""" property (non plural) iOS scales the image properly.    On android imageViews will render the correct dimensions when either the """"""""image"""""""" or """"""""images"""""""" property is called. (Android works properly)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Not scaling imageView when images property is assigned an array of images for animation
Description: """"When an imageView is created with an """"""""images"""""""" property, iOS no longer respects the width and height specified by the imageView. In my case the image is drawn much larger and off the screen. It may be rendering the image to it's actual size, rather than scaling it to the dimensions specified. When the imageView specified a single image via the """"""""image"""""""" property (non plural) iOS scales the image properly. On android imageViews will render the correct dimensions when either the """"""""image"""""""" or """"""""images"""""""" property is called. (Android works properly)""""",title+description
TIMOB-10596,12,"""Android: Textfield change event gets triggered when window opens.""","""""""h2. Problem    If you create a window and add textfields to it to which a 'change' event handler is attached, when the window opens the textfield 'change' event gets triggered. It's reproducible only on Android.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({   title: 'Bug'  });    var textField1 = Ti.UI.createTextField();  var textField2 = Ti.UI.createTextField();    win1.add(textField1);  win1.add(textField2);    textField1.addEventListener('change', function() {   alert('field 1 changed');  });  textField2.addEventListener('change', function() {   alert('field 2 changed');  });    win1.open();  {code}    h2. Discussions    http://developer.<USER>com/question/141228/android-textfield-change-event-firing-when-its-parent-window-opens""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Textfield change event gets triggered when window opens.
Description: """"h2. Problem If you create a window and add textfields to it to which a 'change' event handler is attached, when the window opens the textfield 'change' event gets triggered. It's reproducible only on Android. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Bug' }); var textField1 = Ti.UI.createTextField(); var textField2 = Ti.UI.createTextField(); win1.add(textField1); win1.add(textField2); textField1.addEventListener('change', function() { alert('field 1 changed'); }); textField2.addEventListener('change', function() { alert('field 2 changed'); }); win1.open(); {code} h2. Discussions http://developer.<USER>com/question/141228/android-textfield-change-event-firing-when-its-parent-window-opens""""",title+description
TIMOB-10595,12,"""iOS: Expose UIDocumentInteractionController APIs""","""""""The client has requested a feature in my app to open a local PDF in iBooks.  As iBooks only accepts URL-schemes from the iBookstore, the only way I can do this is via the UIDocumentInteractionController API.  Would it be possible to expose this API via a proxy object in Titanium Mobile?""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Expose UIDocumentInteractionController APIs
Description: """"The client has requested a feature in my app to open a local PDF in iBooks. As iBooks only accepts URL-schemes from the iBookstore, the only way I can do this is via the UIDocumentInteractionController API. Would it be possible to expose this API via a proxy object in Titanium Mobile?""""",title+description
TIMOB-10594,12,"""Android: HTML5 <video> tag is not working as expected inside a webview""","""""""h2. Problem description  When opening a page with a <video> tag, the video is not properly shown in a webview. The same url works in the native browser of the device, as well as on iOS.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Create the following app and open it:    ~~~  (function() {      var window = Titanium.UI.createWindow();    var webView = Titanium.UI.createWebView();  webView.url = 'http://camendesign.com/code/video_for_everybody/test.html';  window.add(webView);  window.open();  })();  ~~~    h2. Additional note  The same URL works in Chrome and in the native browser""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTML5 <video> tag is not working as expected inside a webview
Description: """"h2. Problem description When opening a page with a <video> tag, the video is not properly shown in a webview. The same url works in the native browser of the device, as well as on iOS. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Create the following app and open it: ~~~ (function() { var window = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); var webView = Titanium.UI.createWebView(); webView.url = 'http://camendesign.com/code/video_for_everybody/test.html'; window.add(webView); window.open(); })(); ~~~ h2. Additional note The same URL works in Chrome and in the native browser""""",title+description
