TIMOB-10574,12,"""MobileWeb: HintText functionality is broken""","""""""The fix for issue TIMOB-10374 broke hintText functionality.    See attached test case file TC10374.zip.  If I click button, correct value should be 'postValue'.  Instead field value is 'empty.  I tried when view is opened.  Same result.    Broken functionality:  (1) Create TextField object with hintText  (2) Set the value of the textfield with some other value (either after window as opened and before)  (3) This clears the hintText and also set the value to be empty. Now if I get back value, it returns the empty    This used to be working in 2.1.1 GA.    Confirmed on Safari 6""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: HintText functionality is broken
Description: """"The fix for issue TIMOB-10374 broke hintText functionality. See attached test case file TC10374.zip. If I click button, correct value should be 'postValue'. Instead field value is 'empty. I tried when view is opened. Same result. Broken functionality: (1) Create TextField object with hintText (2) Set the value of the textfield with some other value (either after window as opened and before) (3) This clears the hintText and also set the value to be empty. Now if I get back value, it returns the empty This used to be working in 2.1.1 GA. Confirmed on Safari 6""""",title+description
TIMOB-10573,12,"""BlackBerry: KitchenSink is staying frozen in some cases""","""""""KitchenSink is staying frozen when opening and closing many windows/views very quickly.  Android and iPhone don't have such issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: KitchenSink is staying frozen in some cases
Description: """"KitchenSink is staying frozen when opening and closing many windows/views very quickly. Android and iPhone don't have such issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10571,12,"""MobileWeb: animation - is throwing Cannot read property '_layout' of undefined""","""""""Animations are causing an error """"""""Cannot read property '_layout' of undefined"""""""" when they are trying to run on an item that is not yet attached to a the window.    h4. Steps to repro:  1. run the code below  2. click the window  3. notice the error """"""""Cannot read property '_layout' of undefined""""""""    {code:js}  var win  = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'white'  });  win.open();    win.addEventListener('click', function(){   var view = Ti.UI.createView({    height: 50,    width: 50,    backgroundColor: 'blue'   });     view.animate({    top: 0,    duration: 300   });  });  {code}      """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: animation - is throwing Cannot read property '_layout' of undefined
Description: """"Animations are causing an error """"""""Cannot read property '_layout' of undefined"""""""" when they are trying to run on an item that is not yet attached to a the window. h4. Steps to repro: 1. run the code below 2. click the window 3. notice the error """"""""Cannot read property '_layout' of undefined"""""""" {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white' }); win.open(); win.addEventListener('click', function(){ var view = Ti.UI.createView({ height: 50, width: 50, backgroundColor: 'blue' }); view.animate({ top: 0, duration: 300 }); }); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-10570,12,"""iOS: TableViewRow: Setting background image of TableViewRow as null or empty does not empty it always""","""""""On iOS, Setting background image of TableViewRow as null or empty does not empty it always instead would show the image of earlier emptied row.    This is not a regression. The issue occurs as far as 2.0.1    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create application with code below and launch the application  2. Click on Row1. BackgroundImage for Row 1 gets set  3. Click on Row2. BackgroundImage for Row 2 gets set  4. Again click on Row1. BackgroundImage for Row 1 gets empty  5. Again click on Row2.    Actual: After Step 5: The row 2 shows the BackgroundImage that was set for Row 1.    Expected: After Step 5: The row 2 should get empty    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableViewRow: Setting background image of TableViewRow as null or empty does not empty it always
Description: """"On iOS, Setting background image of TableViewRow as null or empty does not empty it always instead would show the image of earlier emptied row. This is not a regression. The issue occurs as far as 2.0.1 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create application with code below and launch the application 2. Click on Row1. BackgroundImage for Row 1 gets set 3. Click on Row2. BackgroundImage for Row 2 gets set 4. Again click on Row1. BackgroundImage for Row 1 gets empty 5. Again click on Row2. Actual: After Step 5: The row 2 shows the BackgroundImage that was set for Row 1. Expected: After Step 5: The row 2 should get empty """"",title+description
TIMOB-10569,12,"""iOS: Label - Vertical alignment on label is not set properly""","""""""Vertical alignment on label is not set properly.    This is not a Regression.It happens as far as 2.0.1.    Steps To reproduce:    1. install and launch the app on to the device.  2. Click on Top or Bottom button    Expected Result:    After Step 2: the text on the label should be vertically aligned as per the button click.    Actual Result:    After Step 2: The text doesn't get vertically aligned    app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Label - Vertical alignment on label is not set properly
