TIMOB-10567,12,"""Ti API: Expose EXIF data of an image through Titanium API""","""""""This ticket stems from the architecture discussion for https://wiki.<USER>org/display/eng/Architecture+Proposal+-+Add+orientation+property+to+image+view+and+add+functionality+to+expose+EXIF+data    The exif data of an image will include information that may be helpful for users to have during app development. This includes things like orientation of the image, geolocation for the image etc.  We want to allow users to get this data given a particular image.    This first step in this task is to decide on how we would like to expose this.  There have been ideas of including it in an image blob, or creating a separate proxy for the exif data.  We need to discuss which properties we want to expose, how we want to expose them (getters/setters vs a single getAttribute() method with attribute constants), and other details regarding how the API will look like.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Expose EXIF data of an image through Titanium API
Description: """"This ticket stems from the architecture discussion for https://wiki.<USER>org/display/eng/Architecture+Proposal+-+Add+orientation+property+to+image+view+and+add+functionality+to+expose+EXIF+data The exif data of an image will include information that may be helpful for users to have during app development. This includes things like orientation of the image, geolocation for the image etc. We want to allow users to get this data given a particular image. This first step in this task is to decide on how we would like to expose this. There have been ideas of including it in an image blob, or creating a separate proxy for the exif data. We need to discuss which properties we want to expose, how we want to expose them (getters/setters vs a single getAttribute() method with attribute constants), and other details regarding how the API will look like. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10566,12,"""iOS: Add 'autorotate' property to imageview""","""""""Android recently added a property called 'autorotate' which will rotate the image inside an image view based on the exif data of the image.  iOS does this by default, but we want to add this property to be able to disable it.      Android has this flag false by default, and iOS will have it true by default.  Since there are performance implications on the Android side, we can't have the same default value.    You can use the following code with the attached image to test out this behavior:    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add 'autorotate' property to imageview
Description: """"Android recently added a property called 'autorotate' which will rotate the image inside an image view based on the exif data of the image. iOS does this by default, but we want to add this property to be able to disable it. Android has this flag false by default, and iOS will have it true by default. Since there are performance implications on the Android side, we can't have the same default value. You can use the following code with the attached image to test out this behavior: """"",title+description
TIMOB-10565,12,"""MobileWeb: TextField - clearing value when focused ""","""""""The text set by the value property in textField is being cleared when you focus the textField. Also, textField.value does not have the correct value if it was set durring creation.    h4. Steps to repro (text disappearing):  1. run the code below  2. notice the text in the text field  3. click on the text field  4. notice that the text in the field disappears    h4. Steps to repro (value empty):  1. run the code below  2. click anywhere  3. notice the alert dialog pop up, but the textField has no value  4. type in the text field  5. click again  6. notice that the textField now has a value    {code:js}  var win  = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'white'  });  win.open();    var textField = Ti.UI.createTextField({   height: 50,   width: 300,   backgroundColor: 'yellow',   value: """"""""some text""""""""  });  win.add(textField);    win.addEventListener('click', function(){   alert('Value: '+textField.value);  });  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: TextField - clearing value when focused
Description: """"The text set by the value property in textField is being cleared when you focus the textField. Also, textField.value does not have the correct value if it was set durring creation. h4. Steps to repro (text disappearing): 1. run the code below 2. notice the text in the text field 3. click on the text field 4. notice that the text in the field disappears h4. Steps to repro (value empty): 1. run the code below 2. click anywhere 3. notice the alert dialog pop up, but the textField has no value 4. type in the text field 5. click again 6. notice that the textField now has a value {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white' }); win.open(); var textField = Ti.UI.createTextField({ height: 50, width: 300, backgroundColor: 'yellow', value: """"""""some text"""""""" }); win.add(textField); win.addEventListener('click', function(){ alert('Value: '+textField.value); }); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-10564,12,"""iOS: Cannot dynamically resize a View inside a TableViewRow""","""""""h2. Problem description  When a View is child of TableViewRow, it becomes impossible to resize it dynamically. Parameters width and height are actually changed, but the view inside the app does not change.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Test out this app:          Clicking on the squares, the result should be a resize of the view; while the square on top works (view is inside the window), the second does not (view inside tableviewrow).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot dynamically resize a View inside a TableViewRow
Description: """"h2. Problem description When a View is child of TableViewRow, it becomes impossible to resize it dynamically. Parameters width and height are actually changed, but the view inside the app does not change. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Test out this app: Clicking on the squares, the result should be a resize of the view; while the square on top works (view is inside the window), the second does not (view inside tableviewrow).""""",title+description
TIMOB-10563,12,"""MobileWeb: Double tapping on any tab makes the back button to disappear for that tab""","""""""This is not a regression,issue is seen on 2.1.1 GA.    Steps to reproduce:  1.Package the kitchensink app for mobileweb.  2.Host it on to your apache server.  3.Fireup the app in device browser.  4.Now tap on any tab e.g phone.  5.Tap on e.g shake table row in phone tab.  6.Now again tap on the phone tab.this takes us back to the table rows in the phone tab.  7.Now tap on any table row e.g contacts in the phone tab.  8.You will see that after the test in the contacts is launched & when you go to tap on the back button the back button disappears.    Note : This only happens in the same tab.The back button will not disappear for a table row in any other tab.    Actual result:  1.Double tapping on any tab makes the back button to disappear for that tab.    Expected result:  2.The back button should not disappear.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Double tapping on any tab makes the back button to disappear for that tab
Description: """"This is not a regression,issue is seen on 2.1.1 GA. Steps to reproduce: 1.Package the kitchensink app for mobileweb. 2.Host it on to your apache server. 3.Fireup the app in device browser. 4.Now tap on any tab e.g phone. 5.Tap on e.g shake table row in phone tab. 6.Now again tap on the phone tab.this takes us back to the table rows in the phone tab. 7.Now tap on any table row e.g contacts in the phone tab. 8.You will see that after the test in the contacts is launched & when you go to tap on the back button the back button disappears. Note : This only happens in the same tab.The back button will not disappear for a table row in any other tab. Actual result: 1.Double tapping on any tab makes the back button to disappear for that tab. Expected result: 2.The back button should not disappear.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10562,12,"""Android: KS: Facebook>Query -v8: Runtime Error occurs intermittently (on 2.2.x devices)""","""""""Description:  Runtime Error intermittently occurs when tap on 'Run Query' button or back button on a device.    It is not a regression it occurs in 2.1.1.GA    Steps to reproduce:  1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Mashups > Facebook > Query  2) Login to Facebook using test id  3) Tap on 'Run Query' button  4) Tap on back button on a device  5) Leave device for some time (approximately 2 min)  6) Tap on 'Run Query' button or back button on a device    Actual result:  Runtime Error occurs    Expected result:  Application works without Runtime Error      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS: Facebook>Query -v8: Runtime Error occurs intermittently (on 2.2.x devices)
Description: """"Description: Runtime Error intermittently occurs when tap on 'Run Query' button or back button on a device. It is not a regression it occurs in 2.1.1.GA Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Mashups > Facebook > Query 2) Login to Facebook using test id 3) Tap on 'Run Query' button 4) Tap on back button on a device 5) Leave device for some time (approximately 2 min) 6) Tap on 'Run Query' button or back button on a device Actual result: Runtime Error occurs Expected result: Application works without Runtime Error """"",title+description
TIMOB-10561,12,"""MobileWeb: Testing kitchensink with safari remote debugging console (IOS 6 beta 4) open in your laptop causes some tests to freeze while executing""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1.From IOS 6 we can view console logs from mobile safari using remote debugging using USB cable on to our desktop safari.  2.Setup the remote debugging for Iphone.  3.Package kitchensink for mobileweb & host it on to your apache server.  4.Host it on your apache server.  5.Launch the kitchensink app on mobile safari.  6.Launch the console window on your desktop machine or laptop through desktop safari.  7.In the kitchensink app execute tests like ,KitchenSink:Views>Web Views>Inline HTML w/Trans Bg ; KitchenSink:Views>Web Views>Inline HTML w/Color Bg etc.  8.You will see that tapping on them freezes the app & we have to refresh the page to load the app again.  9.If we do not launch the console & execute the same tests they work perfectly fine.    Actual result:  1.Testing kitchensink with safari remote debugging console(IOS 6) open in your laptop,causes some tests to freeze while executing.    Expected result:  2.The tests should not freeze.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Testing kitchensink with safari remote debugging console (IOS 6 beta 4) open in your laptop causes some tests to freeze while executing
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1.From IOS 6 we can view console logs from mobile safari using remote debugging using USB cable on to our desktop safari. 2.Setup the remote debugging for Iphone. 3.Package kitchensink for mobileweb & host it on to your apache server. 4.Host it on your apache server. 5.Launch the kitchensink app on mobile safari. 6.Launch the console window on your desktop machine or laptop through desktop safari. 7.In the kitchensink app execute tests like ,KitchenSink:Views>Web Views>Inline HTML w/Trans Bg ; KitchenSink:Views>Web Views>Inline HTML w/Color Bg etc. 8.You will see that tapping on them freezes the app & we have to refresh the page to load the app again. 9.If we do not launch the console & execute the same tests they work perfectly fine. Actual result: 1.Testing kitchensink with safari remote debugging console(IOS 6) open in your laptop,causes some tests to freeze while executing. Expected result: 2.The tests should not freeze.""""",title+description
