TIMOB-10530,12,"""Android: Java exceptions should be converted and thrown as JS exceptions.""","""""""When making a JS call that binds to a Java method and an exception is thrown  we should catch it in  Kroll and convert it into a JS exception.    This can allow developers to handle them more gracefully and also  pinpoints where in the JS code the crash originated. Having both a JS and Java  trace would be valuable in debugging platform bugs reported by our developers.    This also allows us to throw exception due to invalid calls.  For example if the developer calls View.add() passing a non-view we  can throw an exception. This provides a trace to the point of the error  so the developer does not need to hunt for the bad JS call site.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Java exceptions should be converted and thrown as JS exceptions.
Description: """"When making a JS call that binds to a Java method and an exception is thrown we should catch it in Kroll and convert it into a JS exception. This can allow developers to handle them more gracefully and also pinpoints where in the JS code the crash originated. Having both a JS and Java trace would be valuable in debugging platform bugs reported by our developers. This also allows us to throw exception due to invalid calls. For example if the developer calls View.add() passing a non-view we can throw an exception. This provides a trace to the point of the error so the developer does not need to hunt for the bad JS call site. """"",title+description
