TIMOB-10415,12,"""Android: Location property not set for Ti.Android.Calendar.Event by createEvent method""","""""""calendar.createEvent does not create 'location' property - it is ignored.    // Create the event  var eventBegins = new Date(2010, 11, 26, 12, 0, 0);  var eventEnds = new Date(2010, 11, 26, 14, 0, 0);  var details = {      title: 'Do some stuff',      description: """"""""I'm going to do some stuff at this time."""""""",      location : """"""""At this Place"""""""",      begin: eventBegins,      end: eventEnds  };     var event = calendar.createEvent(details);    Ti.API.info (event.getLocation());   -- prints null    See http://developer.<USER>com/question/131770/location-property-ignored-in-tiandroidcalendarcreateevent#comment-127907    Bug is in android / calendar / EventProxy.java """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Location property not set for Ti.Android.Calendar.Event by createEvent method
Description: """"calendar.createEvent does not create 'location' property - it is ignored. // Create the event var eventBegins = new Date(2010, 11, 26, 12, 0, 0); var eventEnds = new Date(2010, 11, 26, 14, 0, 0); var details = { title: 'Do some stuff', description: """"""""I'm going to do some stuff at this time."""""""", location : """"""""At this Place"""""""", begin: eventBegins, end: eventEnds }; var event = calendar.createEvent(details); Ti.API.info (event.getLocation()); -- prints null See http://developer.<USER>com/question/131770/location-property-ignored-in-tiandroidcalendarcreateevent#comment-127907 Bug is in android / calendar / EventProxy.java """"",title+description
TIMOB-10414,12,"""iOS : VideoPlayer - App crashes when the videoplayer is restarted.""","""""""App crashes when the videoPlayer is restarted.  This is not a regression.It occurs since 2.1.0.GA    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Install the app on device and launch it.  2. Click on Start Video label.  3. Then click on done button in the videoplayer.  4. again click on Start video label.   5. Repeat Step 3 and 4 until the simulator exits.(approximately 3 to 4 times)    Actual Result:  after step 4: The video does not show up and generates the logs attached.  After Step 5: The app crashes.    Expected Result:  After Step 4: The video should start playing again.    app.js    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS : VideoPlayer - App crashes when the videoplayer is restarted.
Description: """"App crashes when the videoPlayer is restarted. This is not a regression.It occurs since 2.1.0.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. Install the app on device and launch it. 2. Click on Start Video label. 3. Then click on done button in the videoplayer. 4. again click on Start video label. 5. Repeat Step 3 and 4 until the simulator exits.(approximately 3 to 4 times) Actual Result: after step 4: The video does not show up and generates the logs attached. After Step 5: The app crashes. Expected Result: After Step 4: The video should start playing again. app.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-10413,12,"""iOS: iPad Simulator: Mountain Lion: Xcode 4.4: simulator screen size cuts off top of apps""","""""""When the iPad Simulator is run, apps are cut off at the top and the simulator cannot be resized.    This is not a regression.    This also affects regular Xcode projects. See screenshots.    -Note: This may be related to Retina support.-    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run app in iPad Simulator on Mountain Lion.    Actual Result:    Simulator is improperly sized, the top of the app is cut off, and the simulator cannot be resized to correct the display.    Expected Result:    App is entirely visible in iPad Simulator.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad Simulator: Mountain Lion: Xcode 4.4: simulator screen size cuts off top of apps
Description: """"When the iPad Simulator is run, apps are cut off at the top and the simulator cannot be resized. This is not a regression. This also affects regular Xcode projects. See screenshots. -Note: This may be related to Retina support.- Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run app in iPad Simulator on Mountain Lion. Actual Result: Simulator is improperly sized, the top of the app is cut off, and the simulator cannot be resized to correct the display. Expected Result: App is entirely visible in iPad Simulator.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10412,12,"""MobileWeb: inject RTE for addEventListener call with null or undefined callback argument""","""""""If addEventListener is called on a Titanium object with a null, undefined, or any non-function callback argument, a runtime error should be generated (as in Android and iOS). See runtime errors below.    This not a regression.    See API Docs below.    API Docs 2.1:        iOS Runtime Error:        Android Runtime Error:        MobileWeb Runtime Error:    <silent failure>    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run sample code:        Actual Result:    No runtime error. Program executes without interference.    Expected Result:    Runtime error.    2. If no runtime error is generated, click on green background.    Expected Result:    Click events should fire, runtime errors should generate.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: inject RTE for addEventListener call with null or undefined callback argument
Description: """"If addEventListener is called on a Titanium object with a null, undefined, or any non-function callback argument, a runtime error should be generated (as in Android and iOS). See runtime errors below. This not a regression. See API Docs below. API Docs 2.1: iOS Runtime Error: Android Runtime Error: MobileWeb Runtime Error: <silent failure> Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run sample code: Actual Result: No runtime error. Program executes without interference. Expected Result: Runtime error. 2. If no runtime error is generated, click on green background. Expected Result: Click events should fire, runtime errors should generate.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10410,12,"""APIDoc: All of Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps properties are read only, and should not have setter functions""","""""""All of Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps properties are read only, and should not have setter functions in the documentation.    http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.1/index.html#!/api/Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps-method-setDensity""""""",Bug,"Title: APIDoc: All of Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps properties are read only, and should not have setter functions
Description: """"All of Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps properties are read only, and should not have setter functions in the documentation. http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.1/index.html#!/api/Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps-method-setDensity""""",title+description
TIMOB-10409,12,"""TIAPI: Deprecate updateLayout, startLayout, finishLayout""","""""""With the advent of applyProperties, the value of applyLayout lessens. For several reasons, the promise of delayed/batched UI had never reached fruition. There may be ways to do this more elegantly, to re-approach this situation.    In the mean time, it is suggested that we deprecate for 2.1.2 and remove the dead code afterwards.""""""",Story,"Title: TIAPI: Deprecate updateLayout, startLayout, finishLayout
Description: """"With the advent of applyProperties, the value of applyLayout lessens. For several reasons, the promise of delayed/batched UI had never reached fruition. There may be ways to do this more elegantly, to re-approach this situation. In the mean time, it is suggested that we deprecate for 2.1.2 and remove the dead code afterwards.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10408,12,"""Android: Remove deprecated classes when we bump module_apiversion""","""""""We have a bunch of classes that are deprecated and should be removed.  We have avoided doing this in the past since it will break older modules like https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10404.  If we bump the module_apiversion, we should also remember to remove these deprecated classes as well.      Some examples:    org.<USER>titanium.util.Log  org.<USER>titanium.util.TiConfig""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Remove deprecated classes when we bump module_apiversion
Description: """"We have a bunch of classes that are deprecated and should be removed. We have avoided doing this in the past since it will break older modules like https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-10404. If we bump the module_apiversion, we should also remember to remove these deprecated classes as well. Some examples: org.<USER>titanium.util.Log org.<USER>titanium.util.TiConfig""""",title+description
TIMOB-10407,12,"""Android: Window containing webView crashes the App""","""""""The app is crashing when trying to access a window that contains a webview. Please find attached the crash logs and the sample project provided by the customer.  h4. Repo Steps  1. Run the attached project in studio.  2. Open the app.  3. Tap on tab to the right (Open web view url).  4. Quickly scroll to the bottom of the window.  5. Tap hard back button  6. Wait for a second or two and a dialog window is displayed 'Unfortunately, OpenURL has stopped'""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window containing webView crashes the App
Description: """"The app is crashing when trying to access a window that contains a webview. Please find attached the crash logs and the sample project provided by the customer. h4. Repo Steps 1. Run the attached project in studio. 2. Open the app. 3. Tap on tab to the right (Open web view url). 4. Quickly scroll to the bottom of the window. 5. Tap hard back button 6. Wait for a second or two and a dialog window is displayed 'Unfortunately, OpenURL has stopped'""""",title+description
TIMOB-10406,12,"""Android: KS crashes on Galaxy Tab and HTC Sensation 4G on V8 only""","""""""KS crashes on Galaxy Tab (3.2) and HTC Sensation 4G (2.3.4) on V8 only. It doesn't happen on Galaxy SII (2.3.6) and Galaxy Nexus (4.0.2). The log is attached.  This crash happens on master but not on 2.1.1.GA.  The stack trace is  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS crashes on Galaxy Tab and HTC Sensation 4G on V8 only
Description: """"KS crashes on Galaxy Tab (3.2) and HTC Sensation 4G (2.3.4) on V8 only. It doesn't happen on Galaxy SII (2.3.6) and Galaxy Nexus (4.0.2). The log is attached. This crash happens on master but not on 2.1.1.GA. The stack trace is """"",title+description
TIMOB-10405,12,"""Android: Mapview setLocation Parity Issue""","""""""On android, when the mapview has regionFit set to false using setLocation and changing the zoom (delta) doesn't actually change the delta.  It seems to work on iPhone and on Android if regionFit is true.  The different behavior in Android/iPhone makes me think this is not desired behavior.  Sample code below:      Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');      navWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow();      //  // create base UI tab and root window  //  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var regionSV = {latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993,animate:true,latitudeDelta:0.02, longitudeDelta:0.02,animate:true};    //  // CREATE MAP VIEW  //      var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({   mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,   region:{latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993, latitudeDelta:0.5, longitudeDelta:0.5},       animate:false,       regionFit:false,  //this set to false prevents zooming on Android only       userLocation:false  });    win1.add(mapview);    win1.open();    setTimeout(function(){   mapview.setLocation(regionSV);  },5000);  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Mapview setLocation Parity Issue
Description: """"On android, when the mapview has regionFit set to false using setLocation and changing the zoom (delta) doesn't actually change the delta. It seems to work on iPhone and on Android if regionFit is true. The different behavior in Android/iPhone makes me think this is not desired behavior. Sample code below: Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); navWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow(); // // create base UI tab and root window // var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var regionSV = {latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993,animate:true,latitudeDelta:0.02, longitudeDelta:0.02,animate:true}; // // CREATE MAP VIEW // var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({ mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, region:{latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993, latitudeDelta:0.5, longitudeDelta:0.5}, animate:false, regionFit:false, //this set to false prevents zooming on Android only userLocation:false }); win1.add(mapview); win1.open(); setTimeout(function(){ mapview.setLocation(regionSV); },5000); """"",title+description
TIMOB-10404,12,"""Android: Error when creating new modules/ running old modules""","""""""This was caused by the fix for https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9003. One of the deprecated classes were removed, but it looks like many of our modules depend on the deprecated class.    To test:    1. Create a new module:    2. After you create it, go into the mod1 directory and type 'ant'    Expected Result: The module should build successfully.    Actual Result: The module fails to build.    AND    1. Create a module using an older sdk (same steps as above, but use a titanium.py from an older sdk)  2. After the module is created, take the zip file from the dist directory and put it in the top level directory in your titanium app  3. Use the app.js from the examples directory in your module, and put it in your titanium app  4. Edit your tiapp.xml in your titanium project with the new module entry:    5. Run the app    Expected result:  The app should run with a hello world app    Actual result:  The app does not run and crashes.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Error when creating new modules/ running old modules
Description: """"This was caused by the fix for https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9003. One of the deprecated classes were removed, but it looks like many of our modules depend on the deprecated class. To test: 1. Create a new module: 2. After you create it, go into the mod1 directory and type 'ant' Expected Result: The module should build successfully. Actual Result: The module fails to build. AND 1. Create a module using an older sdk (same steps as above, but use a titanium.py from an older sdk) 2. After the module is created, take the zip file from the dist directory and put it in the top level directory in your titanium app 3. Use the app.js from the examples directory in your module, and put it in your titanium app 4. Edit your tiapp.xml in your titanium project with the new module entry: 5. Run the app Expected result: The app should run with a hello world app Actual result: The app does not run and crashes. """"",title+description
