TIMOB-10402,12,"""Android: Feature: Handle SSLPeerUnverifiedException on HTTPClient Object""","""""""h6.Feature  Add the ability to handle the SSLPeerUnverifiedException on Android (on HTTPClient object when validatesSecureCertificate = true) so that developers can handle what happens when an SSL certificate is rejected. Having this exposed would allow developers further alternatives on how to proceed on such cases.     var loader = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient();  loader.validatesSecureCertificate = true    h6.Customer's remarks  *My problem here is our production server has CA certificate and testing server is has self signed certificate. So for production We should enable certificate validation.*    h6.Output      h6.Released docs  http://developer.android.com/reference/javax/net/ssl/SSLPeerUnverifiedException.html    h6.Associated tickets  Android webView onReceivedSslError method: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4488""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Feature: Handle SSLPeerUnverifiedException on HTTPClient Object
Description: """"h6.Feature Add the ability to handle the SSLPeerUnverifiedException on Android (on HTTPClient object when validatesSecureCertificate = true) so that developers can handle what happens when an SSL certificate is rejected. Having this exposed would allow developers further alternatives on how to proceed on such cases. var loader = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); loader.validatesSecureCertificate = true h6.Customer's remarks *My problem here is our production server has CA certificate and testing server is has self signed certificate. So for production We should enable certificate validation.* h6.Output h6.Released docs http://developer.android.com/reference/javax/net/ssl/SSLPeerUnverifiedException.html h6.Associated tickets Android webView onReceivedSslError method: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4488""""",title+description
TIMOB-10401,12,"""MobileWeb: Tab: window property not respected post-initialization""","""""""Ti.UI.Tab.window and setWindow are not respected.    Uncaught TypeError: Object [object TiUITab] has no method 'setWindow'    This is not a regression. This works on iOS and Android.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code:        Actual Result:    window property is ignored or setWindow method generates runtime error    Expected Result:    A tab group should open with colored tabs and colored windows.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Tab: window property not respected post-initialization
Description: """"Ti.UI.Tab.window and setWindow are not respected. Uncaught TypeError: Object [object TiUITab] has no method 'setWindow' This is not a regression. This works on iOS and Android. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code: Actual Result: window property is ignored or setWindow method generates runtime error Expected Result: A tab group should open with colored tabs and colored windows.""""",title+description
