TIMOB-10360,12,"""iOS: Xcode 4.4: Xcode does not function as expected when installed on partition other than boot volume""","""""""While running some tests for Mountain Lion, the Mac App store app discovered the Xcode installation on my Lion partition. I updated. When trying to build, I encountered various errors that were cleared up when I copied the Xcode.app locally and reset my xcode-select path to the local copy. (It seems that Xcode 4.4 now once again sets Xcode-select when launched)    Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a Mountain Lion partition on system with Lion partition  2) Boot into Mtn. Lion and configure.  3) Attempt to install Xcode (it should update your existing Lion copy)  4) Try to launch and build a project in studio    Result:  Generic errors when trying to build    Expected:  Normal build and install to iTunes""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Xcode 4.4: Xcode does not function as expected when installed on partition other than boot volume
Description: """"While running some tests for Mountain Lion, the Mac App store app discovered the Xcode installation on my Lion partition. I updated. When trying to build, I encountered various errors that were cleared up when I copied the Xcode.app locally and reset my xcode-select path to the local copy. (It seems that Xcode 4.4 now once again sets Xcode-select when launched) Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a Mountain Lion partition on system with Lion partition 2) Boot into Mtn. Lion and configure. 3) Attempt to install Xcode (it should update your existing Lion copy) 4) Try to launch and build a project in studio Result: Generic errors when trying to build Expected: Normal build and install to iTunes""""",title+description
TIMOB-10359,12,"""MobileWeb: Imageview parity for scaling behavior""","""""""As part of TIMOB-3749 scaling behavior of imageViews was changed. If either width or height of image view are set to follow SIZE behavior('auto',Ti.UI.SIZE,undefined) then the image is scaled with aspect ratio intact. Otherwise the image is scaled ignoring aspect ratio. Test code below      """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Imageview parity for scaling behavior
Description: """"As part of TIMOB-3749 scaling behavior of imageViews was changed. If either width or height of image view are set to follow SIZE behavior('auto',Ti.UI.SIZE,undefined) then the image is scaled with aspect ratio intact. Otherwise the image is scaled ignoring aspect ratio. Test code below """"",title+description
TIMOB-10358,12,"""Android: ImageView parity for scaling behavior""","""""""While testing for parity on current scaling behavior of imageViews on Android, noticed all kinds of layout issues. Basically if an image is loaded with auto width and height and then the width and height properties are specifically overwritten, setting the width and height back to auto does not return image to original dimensions. Had similar issues with IOS which were fixed as part of TIMOB-3749    IOS behavior is as follows. If either width or height of image view are set to follow SIZE behavior('auto',Ti.UI.SIZE,undefined) then the image is scaled with aspect ratio intact. Otherwise the image is scaled ignoring aspect ratio.    Test case is below    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView parity for scaling behavior
Description: """"While testing for parity on current scaling behavior of imageViews on Android, noticed all kinds of layout issues. Basically if an image is loaded with auto width and height and then the width and height properties are specifically overwritten, setting the width and height back to auto does not return image to original dimensions. Had similar issues with IOS which were fixed as part of TIMOB-3749 IOS behavior is as follows. If either width or height of image view are set to follow SIZE behavior('auto',Ti.UI.SIZE,undefined) then the image is scaled with aspect ratio intact. Otherwise the image is scaled ignoring aspect ratio. Test case is below """"",title+description
