TIMOB-10313,12,"""Android: A NetworkOnMainThreadException lead app to crash when FastDev is enabled""","""""""h6.Issue  App crashes when opening any page with XHR call: NetworkOnMainThreadException.    Titanium may not be able to split the UI into a separate thread. According to the android developers website, this happens because in later SDKs, gingerbread and above, they no longer allow network calls on the main thread.      I.E. http://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/NetworkOnMainThreadException.html    h6.To replicate  1) Get please sample attached (consist of one Alloy controller) and,  2) run on either device or emulator under listed target environments.    h6.Old Stack trace  This is the first stack trace that the reporter attached when the ticket was originally created:      *NOTE*  It is important to note this happens when fastdev is enabled. Disabling fastdev DOES NOT fixes the issue.     There was a similar ticket related to fastdev that was opened before and fixed:  https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9666    h5.Recent logs    h6.Samsung Galaxy 4.1  Customer running into crash on below logs:      h6.Emulator 4.3  Myself was able to experience the crash by just running attached controller (XHR called from app/assets/include/xhr.js)  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: A NetworkOnMainThreadException lead app to crash when FastDev is enabled
Description: """"h6.Issue App crashes when opening any page with XHR call: NetworkOnMainThreadException. Titanium may not be able to split the UI into a separate thread. According to the android developers website, this happens because in later SDKs, gingerbread and above, they no longer allow network calls on the main thread. I.E. http://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/NetworkOnMainThreadException.html h6.To replicate 1) Get please sample attached (consist of one Alloy controller) and, 2) run on either device or emulator under listed target environments. h6.Old Stack trace This is the first stack trace that the reporter attached when the ticket was originally created: *NOTE* It is important to note this happens when fastdev is enabled. Disabling fastdev DOES NOT fixes the issue. There was a similar ticket related to fastdev that was opened before and fixed: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9666 h5.Recent logs h6.Samsung Galaxy 4.1 Customer running into crash on below logs: h6.Emulator 4.3 Myself was able to experience the crash by just running attached controller (XHR called from app/assets/include/xhr.js) """"",title+description
TIMOB-10309,12,"""Android: Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder() callback is not called for a bad address""","""""""h3. Issue    When an address is passed into Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder() the callback function is not called and it gets stuck in an infinite loop. It should behave just like it does on iOS where the callback is called upon success/failure. The sample code is attached. On iOS we receive both alerts that the callback was successful and the finished alert. On Android we do not see the alert that the callback was successful just that we started the fowardGeocoder().    h3. Sample Code    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder() callback is not called for a bad address
Description: """"h3. Issue When an address is passed into Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder() the callback function is not called and it gets stuck in an infinite loop. It should behave just like it does on iOS where the callback is called upon success/failure. The sample code is attached. On iOS we receive both alerts that the callback was successful and the finished alert. On Android we do not see the alert that the callback was successful just that we started the fowardGeocoder(). h3. Sample Code """"",title+description
