TIMOB-10300,12,"""KitchenSink: Base UI > Views > Web Views > Local URL: on iPhone the telephone number isn't a link""","""""""Description:  The telephone number isn't a link on iPhone.    This is not a regression it occurs on SDK 2.1.0.GA    Steps to reproduce:  1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Base UI > Views > Web Views  2)  Tap on 'Local URL'.    Actual result:  The telephone number isn't a link.    Expected result:  The telephone number should be a link.          """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Base UI > Views > Web Views > Local URL: on iPhone the telephone number isn't a link
Description: """"Description: The telephone number isn't a link on iPhone. This is not a regression it occurs on SDK 2.1.0.GA Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Base UI > Views > Web Views 2) Tap on 'Local URL'. Actual result: The telephone number isn't a link. Expected result: The telephone number should be a link. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10298,12,"""BlackBerry: KitchenSink doesn't open any view the second time on device""","""""""KitchenSink doesn't open any view the second time on device.   It is reproducible in the sdk with the following githash number: githash=33051bf .    Steps to reproduce:    Step1. Launch KitchenSink  Step2. Open e.g. """"""""controls_win_title""""""""  STep3. Click on e.g. """"""""Activity Indicator""""""""  Step4. Go back by clicking """"""""Back"""""""" button in the left below corner  Step5. CLick again and again on """"""""Activity Indicator""""""""  Actual Result: No any reaction    Step6. You can click any other view, e.g. """"""""Slider""""""""  Step7. Go back to the list (or even going back to Tab list and returning to the """"""""controls_win_title"""""""" list which works fine doesn't matter how much time you go back and click it again)  STep8. Click again """"""""Activity Indicator"""""""" or """"""""Slider""""""""  Actual Result: No any reaction    Expected result: in STep5 and Step8 we should see the corresponding tabs opened.  Solution to overcome: You can only open the """"""""Activity Indicator"""""""" or """"""""Slider"""""""" after closing and opening KitchenSink again.     """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry: KitchenSink doesn't open any view the second time on device
Description: """"KitchenSink doesn't open any view the second time on device. It is reproducible in the sdk with the following githash number: githash=33051bf . Steps to reproduce: Step1. Launch KitchenSink Step2. Open e.g. """"""""controls_win_title"""""""" STep3. Click on e.g. """"""""Activity Indicator"""""""" Step4. Go back by clicking """"""""Back"""""""" button in the left below corner Step5. CLick again and again on """"""""Activity Indicator"""""""" Actual Result: No any reaction Step6. You can click any other view, e.g. """"""""Slider"""""""" Step7. Go back to the list (or even going back to Tab list and returning to the """"""""controls_win_title"""""""" list which works fine doesn't matter how much time you go back and click it again) STep8. Click again """"""""Activity Indicator"""""""" or """"""""Slider"""""""" Actual Result: No any reaction Expected result: in STep5 and Step8 we should see the corresponding tabs opened. Solution to overcome: You can only open the """"""""Activity Indicator"""""""" or """"""""Slider"""""""" after closing and opening KitchenSink again. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10297,12,"""Android: Two labels disappear after changing device mode to landscape in """"Horizontal Layout"""".""","""""""Description:    Two labels disappear after changing device mode to landscape in """"""""Horizontal Layout"""""""".    This occurs only on LG VS910 4G (2.3.6) phone.    Steps:    1. Run Refactored KitchenSink in portrait mode.  2. In """"""""Base UI"""""""" module press on """"""""Horizontal Layout"""""""".  3. After three labels are displayed turn device on landscape mode.    Expected results:    Three labels visible on the screen.    Actual results:     Only third label is visible.                """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Two labels disappear after changing device mode to landscape in """"Horizontal Layout"""".
Description: """"Description: Two labels disappear after changing device mode to landscape in """"""""Horizontal Layout"""""""". This occurs only on LG VS910 4G (2.3.6) phone. Steps: 1. Run Refactored KitchenSink in portrait mode. 2. In """"""""Base UI"""""""" module press on """"""""Horizontal Layout"""""""". 3. After three labels are displayed turn device on landscape mode. Expected results: Three labels visible on the screen. Actual results: Only third label is visible. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10296,12,"""Android: Annotations with the same title cannot be uniquley selected. The first is always selected.""","""""""h3. Issue    On Android if we have annotations with the same title, only 1st of the annotations with the title can be selected. In iOS the correct annotation is selected, even if the titles are the same. It would make more sense to have annotations identified by the titleid instead of the title since the title can be the same.    h3. Sample Code    In the attached code there are 4 annotations created with unique titleid's. On iOS, when the Select Annotation button is clicked Citibank #3 is selected (which is correct).  On Android however the first annotation with that title is selected so Citibank #1 is selected.       """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Annotations with the same title cannot be uniquley selected. The first is always selected.
Description: """"h3. Issue On Android if we have annotations with the same title, only 1st of the annotations with the title can be selected. In iOS the correct annotation is selected, even if the titles are the same. It would make more sense to have annotations identified by the titleid instead of the title since the title can be the same. h3. Sample Code In the attached code there are 4 annotations created with unique titleid's. On iOS, when the Select Annotation button is clicked Citibank #3 is selected (which is correct). On Android however the first annotation with that title is selected so Citibank #1 is selected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10295,12,"""iOS: Enabling a TextArea in a ScrollView automatically scrolls to TextArea.""","""""""This is for an app in which controls may dynamically be disabled and enabled. When disabled a TextArea and enabled it, the ScrollView is automatically getting scrolled to the newly enabled TextArea which is not desirable. There is a textField in this app as well, but it does not have this behavior.     h4.Sample Code  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Enabling a TextArea in a ScrollView automatically scrolls to TextArea.
Description: """"This is for an app in which controls may dynamically be disabled and enabled. When disabled a TextArea and enabled it, the ScrollView is automatically getting scrolled to the newly enabled TextArea which is not desirable. There is a textField in this app as well, but it does not have this behavior. h4.Sample Code """"",title+description
TIMOB-10294,12,"""MobileWeb: Transition all event names to lower case designs""","""""""In the aug 1 architectural meeting, it was resolved that events should use only lowercase letters 'a'-'z', for reasons of consistency, aligning with W3C and for making life easy for Alloy. For example:  * android:back should be androidback  * durationAvailable should be durationavailable    To transition, lowercase versions of the events should be made, deprecating but still using the camelCase and namespaced events. Document as such. Then eventually drop the non-lowercase events.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: MobileWeb: Transition all event names to lower case designs
Description: """"In the aug 1 architectural meeting, it was resolved that events should use only lowercase letters 'a'-'z', for reasons of consistency, aligning with W3C and for making life easy for Alloy. For example: * android:back should be androidback * durationAvailable should be durationavailable To transition, lowercase versions of the events should be made, deprecating but still using the camelCase and namespaced events. Document as such. Then eventually drop the non-lowercase events.""""",title+description
