TIMOB-10250,12,"""Blackberry: Global API clearInterval() method crashes when parameter is 'undefined'""","""""""When calling clearInterval(interval) with interval parameter 'undefined' - clearInterval() crashes.    This could be tested on Kitchen Sink application - Controls -> Progress bar (ui\common\controls\progress_bar.js line 138 - clearInterval(interval))""""""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry: Global API clearInterval() method crashes when parameter is 'undefined'
Description: """"When calling clearInterval(interval) with interval parameter 'undefined' - clearInterval() crashes. This could be tested on Kitchen Sink application - Controls -> Progress bar (ui\common\controls\progress_bar.js line 138 - clearInterval(interval))""""",title+description
TIMOB-10248,12,"""iOS: Kitchen Sink : Platform : Error Callback is unable to resolve host""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists atleast as far as 2.0.1.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Launch KitchenSink  2) Open Platform -> XHR -> Error Callback    Expected results:  UTF-8 GET  www.fre100.com    Actual results:   UTF-8 GET  Error Domain=ASIHTPRequestErrorDomain...    Snapshot attached for both android(which is expected for iOS as well) and iOS behavior.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchen Sink : Platform : Error Callback is unable to resolve host
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists atleast as far as 2.0.1. Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch KitchenSink 2) Open Platform -> XHR -> Error Callback Expected results: UTF-8 GET www.fre100.com Actual results: UTF-8 GET Error Domain=ASIHTPRequestErrorDomain... Snapshot attached for both android(which is expected for iOS as well) and iOS behavior. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10246,12,"""iOS: Ti.App.Properties that are not persistent is iOS simulator""","""""""From a community member wrt Mountain Lion,    """"""""Yup, everything works except for the Ti.App.Properties that are not persistent when I relaunch the app in the simulator.""""""""    It's uncertain if this is due to clean builds, or happens every time. Will have to recreate first.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.App.Properties that are not persistent is iOS simulator
Description: """"From a community member wrt Mountain Lion, """"""""Yup, everything works except for the Ti.App.Properties that are not persistent when I relaunch the app in the simulator."""""""" It's uncertain if this is due to clean builds, or happens every time. Will have to recreate first. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10245,12,"""KitchenSink: KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery ""","""""""Description:    KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery. It happens during testing KitchenSink on on LG VS910 4G (2.3.6).    Steps:    1. Run Refactored KitchenSink  2. In """"""""Phone"""""""" module press on """"""""Photo Gallery"""""""".  3. Click on photo album.  4. Click on any single photo.    Expected results:    Should be able to open single photo.    Actual results:    Application crashes.    Note:  Similar behavior observed in Phone > Contacts > Contacts Picker. After clicking on the single picker app crashes.""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery
Description: """"Description: KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery. It happens during testing KitchenSink on on LG VS910 4G (2.3.6). Steps: 1. Run Refactored KitchenSink 2. In """"""""Phone"""""""" module press on """"""""Photo Gallery"""""""". 3. Click on photo album. 4. Click on any single photo. Expected results: Should be able to open single photo. Actual results: Application crashes. Note: Similar behavior observed in Phone > Contacts > Contacts Picker. After clicking on the single picker app crashes.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10244,12,"""Refactored KitchenSink: KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery ""","""""""Description:    KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery. It happens during testing KitchenSink on on LG VS910 4G (2.3.6).    Steps:    1. Run Refactored KitchenSink  2. In """"""""Phone"""""""" module press on """"""""Photo Gallery"""""""".  3. Click on photo album.  4. Click on any single photo.    Expected results:    Should be able to open single photo.    Actual results:    Application crashes.""""""",Bug,"Title: Refactored KitchenSink: KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery
Description: """"Description: KitchenSink crashes while trying to open single photo in Photo gallery. It happens during testing KitchenSink on on LG VS910 4G (2.3.6). Steps: 1. Run Refactored KitchenSink 2. In """"""""Phone"""""""" module press on """"""""Photo Gallery"""""""". 3. Click on photo album. 4. Click on any single photo. Expected results: Should be able to open single photo. Actual results: Application crashes.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10243,12,"""iOS: dyld: DYLD_ environment variables being ignored because main executable (/usr/bin/osascript) is code signed with entitlements (iOS)""","""""""During launching the simulator, the warning:    dyld: DYLD_ environment variables being ignored because main executable (/usr/bin/osascript) is code signed with entitlements    happens. This can be solved by putting os.unsetenv('DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH') outside the if statement on line 1401 of iphone/builder.py as the DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH variable is only needed for launching iphoneSim, and not for the osascript that happens afterwards.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: dyld: DYLD_ environment variables being ignored because main executable (/usr/bin/osascript) is code signed with entitlements (iOS)
Description: """"During launching the simulator, the warning: dyld: DYLD_ environment variables being ignored because main executable (/usr/bin/osascript) is code signed with entitlements happens. This can be solved by putting os.unsetenv('DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH') outside the if statement on line 1401 of iphone/builder.py as the DYLD_FRAMEWORK_PATH variable is only needed for launching iphoneSim, and not for the osascript that happens afterwards. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10242,12,"""KitchenSink:  Phone > Photo Gallery: on iPad """"Photo Albums"""" appear after shaking a device""","""""""Description:  The """"""""Photo Albums"""""""" don't appear after launching the application until shaking the device. Occurs on iPad.    This is not a regression it occurs on SDK 2.0.1.GA2    Steps to reproduce:  1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Phone  2)  Tap on 'Photo Gallery"""""""".    Actual result:  Can't choose a picture, there is no """"""""Photo Albums"""""""".  Shake the device to get """"""""Photo Albums"""""""".    Expected result:  """"""""Photo Albums"""""""" should appear after launching the application.  """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Phone > Photo Gallery: on iPad """"Photo Albums"""" appear after shaking a device
Description: """"Description: The """"""""Photo Albums"""""""" don't appear after launching the application until shaking the device. Occurs on iPad. This is not a regression it occurs on SDK 2.0.1.GA2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Phone 2) Tap on 'Photo Gallery"""""""". Actual result: Can't choose a picture, there is no """"""""Photo Albums"""""""". Shake the device to get """"""""Photo Albums"""""""". Expected result: """"""""Photo Albums"""""""" should appear after launching the application. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10241,12,"""APIDoc: docgen.py should mark creator method as deprecated when the associated object is deprecated""","""""""Added a deprecated version of Ti.UI.3DMatrix, but Ti.UI.create3DMatrix shows up as non-deprecated.    We could add it back in manually and deprecate it, but it seems like it should be deprecated automatically.    There might be some issues here with producing the correct documentation, however. If the deprecation annotation  included an alternate field (or something like that) identifying the Ti type replacing the object, we could generate  the appropriate summary text automatically. Have to think on that, but I'm noting the issue now before I forget it.""""""",Bug,"Title: APIDoc: docgen.py should mark creator method as deprecated when the associated object is deprecated
Description: """"Added a deprecated version of Ti.UI.3DMatrix, but Ti.UI.create3DMatrix shows up as non-deprecated. We could add it back in manually and deprecate it, but it seems like it should be deprecated automatically. There might be some issues here with producing the correct documentation, however. If the deprecation annotation included an alternate field (or something like that) identifying the Ti type replacing the object, we could generate the appropriate summary text automatically. Have to think on that, but I'm noting the issue now before I forget it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10240,12,"""APIDoc: Add """"notes"""" or """"see"""" field to """"deprecated"""" annotation""","""""""It would be nice if the deprecation annotation included a free-text field where we could describe what to use instead. The alternative is to reuse the summary text, possibly removing the only documentation describing the item.    This proposal is to add a field, which for the sake of argument I'll call notes, like this:        For summary tables, the deprecated.notes field could be used in place of the summary, so  users would see something like:    bq. DEPRECATED Use <Titanium.UI.iPhone.Hicky> instead.    For the detail page, the note would show up as part of the deprecation warning, and   the usual summary would appear:    bq. Deprecated since 1.8.0, removed in 1.9.0. Use <Titanium.UI.iPhone.Hicky> instead.  bq.  bq. Summary    bq. A view which automatically renders as an octagon.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: APIDoc: Add """"notes"""" or """"see"""" field to """"deprecated"""" annotation
Description: """"It would be nice if the deprecation annotation included a free-text field where we could describe what to use instead. The alternative is to reuse the summary text, possibly removing the only documentation describing the item. This proposal is to add a field, which for the sake of argument I'll call notes, like this: For summary tables, the deprecated.notes field could be used in place of the summary, so users would see something like: bq. DEPRECATED Use <Titanium.UI.iPhone.Hicky> instead. For the detail page, the note would show up as part of the deprecation warning, and the usual summary would appear: bq. Deprecated since 1.8.0, removed in 1.9.0. Use <Titanium.UI.iPhone.Hicky> instead. bq. bq. Summary bq. A view which automatically renders as an octagon. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10239,12,"""iOS: icons in the tableview if the """"more"""" tab disappear ""","""""""h3. Description  If all the tabs in a tab group don't fit, a """"""""more"""""""" tab appears with a table view containing a list the rest of the windows with it's tab icon in the left hand of the each row.    h3. The problem  If you navigate through a window from the """"""""more"""""""" tab at least two windows deep and come back by pressing the back button, an icon will be missing from that table view.    h3. Sample code    h3. To reproduce:  1. Run that code in app.js  2. Click on the """"""""more"""""""" tab and open one of the windows  3. Click on the button from the window  4. Go back to the beginning with the back button  5. That's it, an icon will be missing.    h3. Note:  If you're two windows deep or more and go back with the back button, you'll see this behavior, but if you press the tab itself, it will go back and everything will be as it should. This bug only happens with the back button.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: icons in the tableview if the """"more"""" tab disappear
Description: """"h3. Description If all the tabs in a tab group don't fit, a """"""""more"""""""" tab appears with a table view containing a list the rest of the windows with it's tab icon in the left hand of the each row. h3. The problem If you navigate through a window from the """"""""more"""""""" tab at least two windows deep and come back by pressing the back button, an icon will be missing from that table view. h3. Sample code h3. To reproduce: 1. Run that code in app.js 2. Click on the """"""""more"""""""" tab and open one of the windows 3. Click on the button from the window 4. Go back to the beginning with the back button 5. That's it, an icon will be missing. h3. Note: If you're two windows deep or more and go back with the back button, you'll see this behavior, but if you press the tab itself, it will go back and everything will be as it should. This bug only happens with the back button.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10238,12,"""Android: Wrong row index when using TableView with Ti.UI.SIZE and specifying row className""","""""""h3. Problem description  row """"""""index"""""""" value it's wrong when using tableViews, with Ti.UI.SIZE height property set, containing complex rows (rows that contain other components) with """"""""className"""""""" property set.      h3. Steps to reproduce  Run the sample code:          Click on any row except the last one. You should get alert dialog saying that index is 9. After first click example usually works fine (only first click generates wrong index), but sometimes it does not work (it seems that issue is random and sometimes index is 9 and sometimes index is the index of the row that was clicked). The only reliable information is that first click never generates right index.    Not specifying 'height' value, setting it to 'auto' or if """"""""className"""""""" property is commented out, everything works fine.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Wrong row index when using TableView with Ti.UI.SIZE and specifying row className
Description: """"h3. Problem description row """"""""index"""""""" value it's wrong when using tableViews, with Ti.UI.SIZE height property set, containing complex rows (rows that contain other components) with """"""""className"""""""" property set. h3. Steps to reproduce Run the sample code: Click on any row except the last one. You should get alert dialog saying that index is 9. After first click example usually works fine (only first click generates wrong index), but sometimes it does not work (it seems that issue is random and sometimes index is 9 and sometimes index is the index of the row that was clicked). The only reliable information is that first click never generates right index. Not specifying 'height' value, setting it to 'auto' or if """"""""className"""""""" property is commented out, everything works fine.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10236,12,"""iOS: refactored Kitchen Sink crashes randomly on start""","""""""Description:  Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) can randomly crash the app.        Steps to reproduce:  Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version)     Actual results:  The application randomly crashes.    Expected results:  The application shouldn't crash.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: refactored Kitchen Sink crashes randomly on start
Description: """"Description: Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) can randomly crash the app. Steps to reproduce: Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) Actual results: The application randomly crashes. Expected results: The application shouldn't crash. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10235,12,"""iOS: Make navigation controller optional in tabs""","""""""h3. Feature request  Make the navigation controller of the tab optional. A native tab controller does not come with the navigation controller built in. We ship with it because it makes sense and it is very useful. There are occasions, tho, that the developer needs to have a window without the navigation part. For example, placing a tab group inside a split window, or vice versa. The developer can remove the tab bar by hiding it, but the navigation controller will still be there creating overhead.    h3. Backwards compatibility  Of course, we don't want to break all the apps out there using the stands tab group component. So this should be an optional boolean in the creation of the tabs it self.    h3. Proposed example  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Make navigation controller optional in tabs
Description: """"h3. Feature request Make the navigation controller of the tab optional. A native tab controller does not come with the navigation controller built in. We ship with it because it makes sense and it is very useful. There are occasions, tho, that the developer needs to have a window without the navigation part. For example, placing a tab group inside a split window, or vice versa. The developer can remove the tab bar by hiding it, but the navigation controller will still be there creating overhead. h3. Backwards compatibility Of course, we don't want to break all the apps out there using the stands tab group component. So this should be an optional boolean in the creation of the tabs it self. h3. Proposed example """"",title+description
TIMOB-10234,12,"""iOS: Platform > XHR > File Download: 'Large File Download' after downloading file leads to crash.""","""""""Description:  After completing the large file download, KitchenSink crashes. Device logs are attached.    This is a regression it doesn't occur on SDK 2.0.1.GA2    Steps to reproduce:  1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Platform > XHR > File Download  2)  Tap on 'Large File Download.    Actual results:  Afte complete downloading the application crashes.    Expected results:  Large File should be successfully downloaded.     Note:  According to recent investigations, this also affects Android""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Platform > XHR > File Download: 'Large File Download' after downloading file leads to crash.
Description: """"Description: After completing the large file download, KitchenSink crashes. Device logs are attached. This is a regression it doesn't occur on SDK 2.0.1.GA2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Platform > XHR > File Download 2) Tap on 'Large File Download. Actual results: Afte complete downloading the application crashes. Expected results: Large File should be successfully downloaded. Note: According to recent investigations, this also affects Android""""",title+description
TIMOB-10232,12,"""Android: Capturing onKeyPress from the hardware keyboard""","""""""h3. Requirement    There is a request of a new feature to support the hardware keyboard on Android apart. The only way to capture keystrokes on the device is via a focus event on a textfield or textarea.     It has been requested to expose the onKeyPress native Android method (primarily on a view) so the hardware keyboard can be accessed from outside the textfield/textarea.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Capturing onKeyPress from the hardware keyboard
Description: """"h3. Requirement There is a request of a new feature to support the hardware keyboard on Android apart. The only way to capture keystrokes on the device is via a focus event on a textfield or textarea. It has been requested to expose the onKeyPress native Android method (primarily on a view) so the hardware keyboard can be accessed from outside the textfield/textarea. """"",title+description
