TIMOB-10127,12,"""kitchenSink: Tableview:Row selection starts appearing after search ""","""""""This is not a regression. This exists as far as 2.0.2    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it.  2) Go to Base UI -> Views -> Table Views -> Headers  3) Click any character on the soft keyboard,then press 'next/enter'  4) Again press any character followed by enter.  5) Press enter again.  6) Press android 'back' button twice, to go back to the 'Table Views'.    Expected result:  3) After step 3, the search results for the pressed character should be displayed and textfield should loose focus.  4) The soft keyboard should be disabled. No changes should be displayed on screen.  5) No changes should be displayed on screen.  6) The 'Table Views' list should get displayed with no row selected.    Actual result:  3) After step 3, the search results for the pressed character is displayed and textfield looses focus.  4) The first search result gets selected.  5) The alert is displayed as if clicked on the highlighted row.  6) The 'Headers' row is shown as selected.    """"""",Bug,"Title: kitchenSink: Tableview:Row selection starts appearing after search
Description: """"This is not a regression. This exists as far as 2.0.2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it. 2) Go to Base UI -> Views -> Table Views -> Headers 3) Click any character on the soft keyboard,then press 'next/enter' 4) Again press any character followed by enter. 5) Press enter again. 6) Press android 'back' button twice, to go back to the 'Table Views'. Expected result: 3) After step 3, the search results for the pressed character should be displayed and textfield should loose focus. 4) The soft keyboard should be disabled. No changes should be displayed on screen. 5) No changes should be displayed on screen. 6) The 'Table Views' list should get displayed with no row selected. Actual result: 3) After step 3, the search results for the pressed character is displayed and textfield looses focus. 4) The first search result gets selected. 5) The alert is displayed as if clicked on the highlighted row. 6) The 'Headers' row is shown as selected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10125,12,"""Android: Window properties:Background image is not setting up after height/width toggling.""","""""""This is a regression. It is working fine in 2.1.0.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it.  2) Go to Base UI -> Window Properties  3) Press button 'Toggle Height/Width' twice.  4) Now press 'Change BG Image'.  5) Again press 'Toggle Height/Width'.  6) Press 'Change BG Image'.    Expected result:  1) The app should run successfully over device.  2) It should display 5 buttons to perform window actions.  3) It should resize the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background.  4) It should change the background image of the window.  5) It will resize the window to a smaller size (300*300) and should change background to black.  6) It should change the background image of the window.    Actual result:  1) The app should run successfully over device.  2) It displays 5 buttons to perform window actions.  3) It resizes the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background.  4) It changes the background image of the window.  5) It resizes the window to a smaller size (300*300) and changes background to black.  6) It DO NOT changes the background image of the window.    The background image should change after window resizing.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window properties:Background image is not setting up after height/width toggling.
Description: """"This is a regression. It is working fine in 2.1.0. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install the refactored kitchen sink on android device and run it. 2) Go to Base UI -> Window Properties 3) Press button 'Toggle Height/Width' twice. 4) Now press 'Change BG Image'. 5) Again press 'Toggle Height/Width'. 6) Press 'Change BG Image'. Expected result: 1) The app should run successfully over device. 2) It should display 5 buttons to perform window actions. 3) It should resize the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background. 4) It should change the background image of the window. 5) It will resize the window to a smaller size (300*300) and should change background to black. 6) It should change the background image of the window. Actual result: 1) The app should run successfully over device. 2) It displays 5 buttons to perform window actions. 3) It resizes the window to a smaller size (300*300) and then again to full screen size with a black background. 4) It changes the background image of the window. 5) It resizes the window to a smaller size (300*300) and changes background to black. 6) It DO NOT changes the background image of the window. The background image should change after window resizing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10124,12,"""Android: KS is forced to restart after login facebook with force_dialog=false on Galaxy Nexus""","""""""This issue only happens on Galaxy Nexus (4.0.2).   It does not happen on Droid One (2.2), HTC Sensation 4G (2.3.4), Galaxy SII (2.3.6), Nexus S(4.0.4) and Xoom (4.0.3)  Steps to reproduce:  1. Make sure Facebook app is installed on the device.  2. Run KS->Mashups->Facebook->Login/Logout  3. Click the button so the label shows """"""""Force dialog: false""""""""  4. Click facebook login button and type the account/password.  5. KS is forced to restart and the log shows  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS is forced to restart after login facebook with force_dialog=false on Galaxy Nexus
Description: """"This issue only happens on Galaxy Nexus (4.0.2). It does not happen on Droid One (2.2), HTC Sensation 4G (2.3.4), Galaxy SII (2.3.6), Nexus S(4.0.4) and Xoom (4.0.3) Steps to reproduce: 1. Make sure Facebook app is installed on the device. 2. Run KS->Mashups->Facebook->Login/Logout 3. Click the button so the label shows """"""""Force dialog: false"""""""" 4. Click facebook login button and type the account/password. 5. KS is forced to restart and the log shows """"",title+description
TIMOB-10123,12,"""Android: Expose Action Bar API's hide method to hide the action bar ""","""""""h3. Problem    The action bar on Android is appearing by default on devices running Android OS version 3.0 or greater. This is device specific. It happens on Samsung Galaxy Nexus and HTC One X but not on Samsung Galaxy S3.     It is requested to expose the hide method that would probably hide the action bar for these devices.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose Action Bar API's hide method to hide the action bar
Description: """"h3. Problem The action bar on Android is appearing by default on devices running Android OS version 3.0 or greater. This is device specific. It happens on Samsung Galaxy Nexus and HTC One X but not on Samsung Galaxy S3. It is requested to expose the hide method that would probably hide the action bar for these devices. """"",title+description
TIMOB-10122,12,"""iOS: Phone > Sound > Background Audio: 'KitchenSink.Media.Sound.audioSessionMode' message in console""","""""""The message: """"""""[WARN] 'KitchenSink.Media.Sound.audioSessionMode' is deprecated; use 'KitchenSink.Media.audioSessionMode'"""""""" is shown by the console.    This is not regression it occurs on SDK 2.1.0.GA    Steps to reproduce:   1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Phone > Sound  2)  Tap on 'Background Audio'>'Start'.      Result:  The message appears in the console:  """"""""[WARN] 'KitchenSink.Media.Sound.audioSessionMode' is deprecated; use 'KitchenSink.Media.audioSessionMode'""""""""    Expected Result:  Deprecation warnings should refer to actual Titanium APIs              """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Phone > Sound > Background Audio: 'KitchenSink.Media.Sound.audioSessionMode' message in console
Description: """"The message: """"""""[WARN] 'KitchenSink.Media.Sound.audioSessionMode' is deprecated; use 'KitchenSink.Media.audioSessionMode'"""""""" is shown by the console. This is not regression it occurs on SDK 2.1.0.GA Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch refactored Kitchen Sink (Kevin Winnerey/Developer relations version) > Phone > Sound 2) Tap on 'Background Audio'>'Start'. Result: The message appears in the console: """"""""[WARN] 'KitchenSink.Media.Sound.audioSessionMode' is deprecated; use 'KitchenSink.Media.audioSessionMode'"""""""" Expected Result: Deprecation warnings should refer to actual Titanium APIs """"",title+description
TIMOB-10120,12,"""Android: 'Uncaught RangeError' when you download & open app from Google Play directly""","""""""*Expected behavior*  When you download a Titanium app from Google Play on the device, it should launch just fine, without any errors.    *Actual behavior*  When you download the app, it throws the following error: https://img.skitch.com/20120724-8jwhabpui82hbr965qj1y44qm1.png    *Steps to reproduce*  -Download a Titanium app from Google Play.  -Open the app from within Google Play, it should force restart the app.  -Here you might get the error, if not, uninstall and try again until you get the same error.    *Notes*  -This only happens sometimes, this isn't consistently reproducible. You will need to give it a few tries (keep installing/opening/uninstalling) until you manage to reproduce it.  -Only tested on a Samsung Galaxy S2 running 2.3.6 with TiSDK 2.1.0GA.  -HD ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-243998""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: 'Uncaught RangeError' when you download & open app from Google Play directly
Description: """"*Expected behavior* When you download a Titanium app from Google Play on the device, it should launch just fine, without any errors. *Actual behavior* When you download the app, it throws the following error: https://img.skitch.com/20120724-8jwhabpui82hbr965qj1y44qm1.png *Steps to reproduce* -Download a Titanium app from Google Play. -Open the app from within Google Play, it should force restart the app. -Here you might get the error, if not, uninstall and try again until you get the same error. *Notes* -This only happens sometimes, this isn't consistently reproducible. You will need to give it a few tries (keep installing/opening/uninstalling) until you manage to reproduce it. -Only tested on a Samsung Galaxy S2 running 2.3.6 with TiSDK 2.1.0GA. -HD ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-243998""""",title+description
TIMOB-10119,12,"""iOS: CameraView: showControls: false leaves a black bar across bottom of screen""","""""""h4. Problem  When user specifies false for showControls on iOS cameraView, a black bar appears across the bottom of the page where the tab group (camera controls) used to be.    h4. Sample Code      h4. Desired Result  The black bar should not be shown when showControls property is set to false. The cameraView should fill up the whole screen.  link:  http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2674375/uiimagepickercontroller-doesnt-fill-screen  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: CameraView: showControls: false leaves a black bar across bottom of screen
