TIMOB-10117,12,"""CodeProcessor: Inject built-in global objects""","""""""There are a lot of global variables defined by the JavaScript runtime itself, such as console, Object, etc. These need to be injected before the Titanium API is injected.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CodeProcessor: Inject built-in global objects
Description: """"There are a lot of global variables defined by the JavaScript runtime itself, such as console, Object, etc. These need to be injected before the Titanium API is injected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10115,12,"""Android: Closing tabGroup on Android closes the entire application even when creating a separate root window. ""","""""""According to the official documentation (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.TabGroup) it is possible to close a TabGroup on Android if you have created a root window (On Android, only one tab group may exist at one time. A tab group may be closed to allow a new one to be opened later, but the root of the application must be a heavyweight window to prevent it exiting.)    However I am getting an issue where closing a TabGroup on Android does close the app despite a heavyweight root window being present. Occasionally this appears to work on 2.0.2 however results are inconsistent and behave differently between screen sizes of the Android emulator.     Code attached to this issue.     The issue appears to be related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-630""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Closing tabGroup on Android closes the entire application even when creating a separate root window.
Description: """"According to the official documentation (http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.TabGroup) it is possible to close a TabGroup on Android if you have created a root window (On Android, only one tab group may exist at one time. A tab group may be closed to allow a new one to be opened later, but the root of the application must be a heavyweight window to prevent it exiting.) However I am getting an issue where closing a TabGroup on Android does close the app despite a heavyweight root window being present. Occasionally this appears to work on 2.0.2 however results are inconsistent and behave differently between screen sizes of the Android emulator. Code attached to this issue. The issue appears to be related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-630""""",title+description
TIMOB-10113,12,"""iOS: Pagination in scrollable view does not look nice with lots of views""","""""""h2. Problem description  ScollableView pagination does not work well if there are lots of views; the """"""""dots"""""""" in the pagination row goes out of the screen.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Open Kitchen Sink  2. Go to Base Ui > View > Scroll Views > Scrollable View  3. Click the 'Add' button multiple times (~25 times)  4. Swipe views: at some point, the white dot that <USER>the current selected view goes out of the screen  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Pagination in scrollable view does not look nice with lots of views
Description: """"h2. Problem description ScollableView pagination does not work well if there are lots of views; the """"""""dots"""""""" in the pagination row goes out of the screen. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Open Kitchen Sink 2. Go to Base Ui > View > Scroll Views > Scrollable View 3. Click the 'Add' button multiple times (~25 times) 4. Swipe views: at some point, the white dot that <USER>the current selected view goes out of the screen """"",title+description
TIMOB-10112,12,"""Android: Views: A view animated to change position shows a trail while reversing""","""""""A view that is animated with a change in position, shows a trail back to the original position during reversal of animation.    This is not a regression. The reversal of animated view did not work in 2.1.0    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create an app with code below  2. Lauch the app  3. Click on the blue view    Actual: The blue view animated to a new position and then reverses back. During reverse it shows a trail of the path followed for reversal (Refer to attached screenshot)    Expected: The animation reversal should be smooth and should not show a reverse trace    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Views: A view animated to change position shows a trail while reversing
