TIMOB-10111,12,"""Android: Titanium.Android - An unexpected small box shown (intermittently) on closing the window inside the intent""","""""""On Android platform,An unexpected small box shown (intermittently) on closing the window inside the intent    This is not a regression.It also occurs on 2.1.0    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Install and Launch Test app  2. A button should appear """"""""Press Me I error Ti SDK 1.8+"""""""", click it  3. Another button will appear """"""""Press 2 Close"""""""" with a green border, click it for long.     Expected result    After step #2: Another button will appear and the first button and background image will visibly blur  After step #3: The second button will be dismissed, and you will return to view with the first button and red background    Actual result  After step #3: A small box is shown before the first window is displayed.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.Android - An unexpected small box shown (intermittently) on closing the window inside the intent
Description: """"On Android platform,An unexpected small box shown (intermittently) on closing the window inside the intent This is not a regression.It also occurs on 2.1.0 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Install and Launch Test app 2. A button should appear """"""""Press Me I error Ti SDK 1.8+"""""""", click it 3. Another button will appear """"""""Press 2 Close"""""""" with a green border, click it for long. Expected result After step #2: Another button will appear and the first button and background image will visibly blur After step #3: The second button will be dismissed, and you will return to view with the first button and red background Actual result After step #3: A small box is shown before the first window is displayed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-10110,12,"""Android: view with borders are not correctly removed in scrollview""","""""""In android when you create a view with borders, two views are actually created to create the border.  The problem with this is that when trying to remove the view from a scrollview, you only remove the """"""""container"""""""" view and not the border view.    The example       and here is a simple example of what should happen  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: view with borders are not correctly removed in scrollview
Description: """"In android when you create a view with borders, two views are actually created to create the border. The problem with this is that when trying to remove the view from a scrollview, you only remove the """"""""container"""""""" view and not the border view. The example and here is a simple example of what should happen """"",title+description
TIMOB-10109,12,"""MobileWeb: Only listen for deviceorientation event if explicitly listening for orientationchange event""","""""""Ti.Gesture listens to deviceorientation which fires events dozens of times a second with the latest accelerometer information. If it detects a change, then it fires the orientationchange event. However, if we never listen to orientationchange, then we are wasting precious resources calculating orientation change that we don't care about.    This can be fixed by overriding addEventListener and removeEventListener and doing the deviceorientation event connect/disconnect on an as needed basis. Be sure to only listen once for the deviceorientation event!""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Only listen for deviceorientation event if explicitly listening for orientationchange event
Description: """"Ti.Gesture listens to deviceorientation which fires events dozens of times a second with the latest accelerometer information. If it detects a change, then it fires the orientationchange event. However, if we never listen to orientationchange, then we are wasting precious resources calculating orientation change that we don't care about. This can be fixed by overriding addEventListener and removeEventListener and doing the deviceorientation event connect/disconnect on an as needed basis. Be sure to only listen once for the deviceorientation event!""""",title+description
TIMOB-10108,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.API.log INFO level messages do not display as correct type""","""""""Ti.API.log messages show as [LOG] level instead of the log type passed in as the first argument. This is either an API or a documentation issue. Screenshots attached.    This is not a regression.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create app with code:        2. Preview in MobileWeb Browser.  3. Open the console view in the browser (command + option + i in chrome os x).    Actual Result:    [LOG] level messages appear.    Expected Result:    [ERROR], [WARN], [TRACE], [DEBUG], and [INFO] messages should appear, based on the first argument of Ti.API.log().""""""",Sub-task,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.API.log INFO level messages do not display as correct type
Description: """"Ti.API.log messages show as [LOG] level instead of the log type passed in as the first argument. This is either an API or a documentation issue. Screenshots attached. This is not a regression. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create app with code: 2. Preview in MobileWeb Browser. 3. Open the console view in the browser (command + option + i in chrome os x). Actual Result: [LOG] level messages appear. Expected Result: [ERROR], [WARN], [TRACE], [DEBUG], and [INFO] messages should appear, based on the first argument of Ti.API.log().""""",title+description
