TIMOB-10038,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.ImageView.opacity doesn't seem to have any effect""","""""""*Code*  Sample project attached, with image files.    *Expected behavior*  When you click on any image view, they should light up, be brighter, have full opacity, just like on iOS.    *Actual behavior*  When the app is ran on the device, the opacity seems to be ignored. It doesn't even start semi-transparent, like it should do.   Plus when you tap on an image, it doesn't seem to do anything.    *Notes*  -Works fine on the iOS simulator.  -Tested only on a Samsung Galaxy S2 with 2.3.6, using TiSDK 1.8.2 and 2.1GA.   -HD ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-938936""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.ImageView.opacity doesn't seem to have any effect
