TIMOB-9997,12,"""Android: Built project cannot open in Eclipse without changes""","""""""h2. Problem description    Built project for Android (%project_dir%/build/android) cannot be imported into Eclipse (that has ADT plugin) and compiled without modification.      h2. Steps to reproduce  - compile small Titanium application:        - inside Eclipse, run the import and select """"""""%project_dir%/build/android""""""""    h2. Expected behavior  Titanium should generate Android project that can be compiled without any modifications.  Titanium project compiled for iOS has no problem with importing and compiling with Xcode    h2. Current behavior  Eclipse shows the following error message:    """"""""Android requires compiler compliance level 5.0 or 6.0. Found '1.4' instead. Please use Android Tools > Fix Project Properties.""""""""    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Built project cannot open in Eclipse without changes
Description: """"h2. Problem description Built project for Android (%project_dir%/build/android) cannot be imported into Eclipse (that has ADT plugin) and compiled without modification. h2. Steps to reproduce - compile small Titanium application: - inside Eclipse, run the import and select """"""""%project_dir%/build/android"""""""" h2. Expected behavior Titanium should generate Android project that can be compiled without any modifications. Titanium project compiled for iOS has no problem with importing and compiling with Xcode h2. Current behavior Eclipse shows the following error message: """"""""Android requires compiler compliance level 5.0 or 6.0. Found '1.4' instead. Please use Android Tools > Fix Project Properties."""""""" """"",title+description
