TIMOB-9960,12,"""Android: Window: V8 -  Background color doesn't change color after each tap on some tablets""","""""""Description  Run the attached code and note that the color does not always change to the color shown in the label, it stays black (or alternates with the color shown before rotation). Rotating the device forces the color update generally.    This is not a regression, this occurs with 2.1.0GA as well.  :          Steps to reproduce:  1) create new studio project with attached code and run on device   2) tap the screen     Actual result:    In each tap, the color of the window is black, and some """"""""color name"""""""" label appears at the top of the screen.       Expected Result:  The window changes color on each tap. In each case, the color of the window should match the color name label shown at the top""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window: V8 - Background color doesn't change color after each tap on some tablets
Description: """"Description Run the attached code and note that the color does not always change to the color shown in the label, it stays black (or alternates with the color shown before rotation). Rotating the device forces the color update generally. This is not a regression, this occurs with 2.1.0GA as well. : Steps to reproduce: 1) create new studio project with attached code and run on device 2) tap the screen Actual result: In each tap, the color of the window is black, and some """"""""color name"""""""" label appears at the top of the screen. Expected Result: The window changes color on each tap. In each case, the color of the window should match the color name label shown at the top""""",title+description
TIMOB-9959,12,"""Android: ScrollableView: v8- The application crashes when scrolling a scrollable view with video playing""","""""""Scrolling a scrollable view while a video is playing resulted in an app crash.    This is not a regression it occurs on SDK 2.1.0.GA        Steps to reproduce:   1) Create new studio project with attached code and run on device   2)  Scroll to any view    Result:  1) A scrollable view is shown with first view as the current view. A video start playing when application opens  2) The application crashes    Expected Result:  1) A scrollable view is shown with first view as the current view. A video start playing when application opens   2) On scrolling to any view the video plays from the start.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ScrollableView: v8- The application crashes when scrolling a scrollable view with video playing
Description: """"Scrolling a scrollable view while a video is playing resulted in an app crash. This is not a regression it occurs on SDK 2.1.0.GA Steps to reproduce: 1) Create new studio project with attached code and run on device 2) Scroll to any view Result: 1) A scrollable view is shown with first view as the current view. A video start playing when application opens 2) The application crashes Expected Result: 1) A scrollable view is shown with first view as the current view. A video start playing when application opens 2) On scrolling to any view the video plays from the start. """"",title+description
