TIMOB-9956,12,"""MobileWeb: Analytics - Button clicks on firefox browser do not show the buttons being clicked.""","""""""This is regression, this works on 2.0.2 GA    Button clicks on firefox browser do not show the buttons being clicked.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Make a default app in the studio.  2. Copy the attached app.js to resources.  3. Publish it for mobile web.  4. Change the DNS to your computers ip.  5. Launch the app through the firefox browser(desktop).  6. Tap on a button like 'feature event','nav event' etc.    Actual Result:  1. When you tap on a button there is no click animation.    Expected Result:  1. Tapping on the button should show click animation.    Note: we do not see the click but the analytics events are getting generated.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Analytics - Button clicks on firefox browser do not show the buttons being clicked.
Description: """"This is regression, this works on 2.0.2 GA Button clicks on firefox browser do not show the buttons being clicked. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Make a default app in the studio. 2. Copy the attached app.js to resources. 3. Publish it for mobile web. 4. Change the DNS to your computers ip. 5. Launch the app through the firefox browser(desktop). 6. Tap on a button like 'feature event','nav event' etc. Actual Result: 1. When you tap on a button there is no click animation. Expected Result: 1. Tapping on the button should show click animation. Note: we do not see the click but the analytics events are getting generated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9955,12,"""Android: ScrollView with a wrap view becomes unscrollable on android Ti 2.1""","""""""ScrollView with a wrap view becomes unscrollable on android Ti SDK 2.1.0.GA. It works on Ti SDK 2.0.1.GA2. It works fine on iOS.  h4. Repo Steps  1. Run the below code in your app.js  2. You can see the scrollView becomes unscrollable.   """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: ScrollView with a wrap view becomes unscrollable on android Ti 2.1
Description: """"ScrollView with a wrap view becomes unscrollable on android Ti SDK 2.1.0.GA. It works on Ti SDK 2.0.1.GA2. It works fine on iOS. h4. Repo Steps 1. Run the below code in your app.js 2. You can see the scrollView becomes unscrollable. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9954,12,"""Android: Animate incorrectly positions when ti.ui.defaultunit is set to a non-platform default (Tiapp.xml)""","""""""To alleviate differences in platform units, the following can be inserted into Tiapp.xml (in this case to force everything to dip):  <property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""">dip</property>    This however breaks the animate function when using positioning on Android. For example if I have a view (bear in mind, units are not given so defaults to dip):  {quote}  var view = Ti.UI.createView(\{   backgroundColor:'#252525',   top:80,   left:0,   width:100,   height:100   \});  {quote}  Which I then choose to animate:  {quote}  var a2 = Titanium.UI.createAnimation();  a2.top = 80;  a2.left = 50;  a2.duration = 800;  view.animate(a2);  {quote}  It seems that while the animation is occuring, it reads the top/left animate values in pixels (rather than dip) which really ruins the animation. At the end of the animation it switches back to dip so ultimately the view does get put in the correct place but obviously in very buggy way.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Animate incorrectly positions when ti.ui.defaultunit is set to a non-platform default (Tiapp.xml)
Description: """"To alleviate differences in platform units, the following can be inserted into Tiapp.xml (in this case to force everything to dip): <property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""">dip</property> This however breaks the animate function when using positioning on Android. For example if I have a view (bear in mind, units are not given so defaults to dip): {quote} var view = Ti.UI.createView(\{ backgroundColor:'#252525', top:80, left:0, width:100, height:100 \}); {quote} Which I then choose to animate: {quote} var a2 = Titanium.UI.createAnimation(); a2.top = 80; a2.left = 50; a2.duration = 800; view.animate(a2); {quote} It seems that while the animation is occuring, it reads the top/left animate values in pixels (rather than dip) which really ruins the animation. At the end of the animation it switches back to dip so ultimately the view does get put in the correct place but obviously in very buggy way. """"",title+description
