TIMOB-9905,12,"""Android: Tableview not updated when a new view is added to a tableviewrow""","""""""Tableview does not get updated when a new view ( label, text area) is added to the tableviewrow. Works fine on iOS.    1. Run the code below in app.js      On iOS, new label gets added to the tableview row.  On Android, label gets added to the tableview row ( info statement seen in ddms) but view not updated.    Workaround: Use setData() to reset the tableview rows. ( works fine on both iOS and Android)""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tableview not updated when a new view is added to a tableviewrow
Description: """"Tableview does not get updated when a new view ( label, text area) is added to the tableviewrow. Works fine on iOS. 1. Run the code below in app.js On iOS, new label gets added to the tableview row. On Android, label gets added to the tableview row ( info statement seen in ddms) but view not updated. Workaround: Use setData() to reset the tableview rows. ( works fine on both iOS and Android)""""",title+description
TIMOB-9904,12,"""iOS: Using Ti.UI.SIZE for a textArea truncates the text included in the text area""","""""""1. Run the below code in app.js to see the text getting truncated in the text area.  App.js      This works fine on Android.  Workaround is to calculate the height of the text area using postLayout event as listed here.  http://pastie.org/4212176""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Using Ti.UI.SIZE for a textArea truncates the text included in the text area
Description: """"1. Run the below code in app.js to see the text getting truncated in the text area. App.js This works fine on Android. Workaround is to calculate the height of the text area using postLayout event as listed here. http://pastie.org/4212176""""",title+description
