TIMOB-9893,12,"""TiAPI: CommonJS 1.1 compliance""","""""""Needs to implement the """"""""minispec"""""""" for require() that was decided on by core:    # Conform to commonjs spec: http://wiki.commonjs.org/wiki/Modules/1.1  -> Testing to be https://github.com/commonjs/commonjs/tree/master/tests/modules  # non-MW platforms throw an exception when confronted with async syntax  -> {{ require([""""""""foo""""""""], callbackFunction); }}    There is also the possibility of:  # Leading '/' not allowed in module names  # Leading '/' always indicates a resource at the root of the project    This should be done for all platforms.""""""",Story,"Title: TiAPI: CommonJS 1.1 compliance
Description: """"Needs to implement the """"""""minispec"""""""" for require() that was decided on by core: # Conform to commonjs spec: http://wiki.commonjs.org/wiki/Modules/1.1 -> Testing to be https://github.com/commonjs/commonjs/tree/master/tests/modules # non-MW platforms throw an exception when confronted with async syntax -> {{ require([""""""""foo""""""""], callbackFunction); }} There is also the possibility of: # Leading '/' not allowed in module names # Leading '/' always indicates a resource at the root of the project This should be done for all platforms.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9892,12,"""Android: Emulator: MacBook Pro Retina Display: Emulator is improperly sized and touch events are inaccurate""","""""""The Android Emulator is improperly displayed and the touch events are inaccurate on the MacBook Pro Retina Display.    This is an android issue: http://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=33383  Attached image courtesy of: http://stackoverflow.com/users/147333/<USER>d    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Buy a MacBook Pro w/Retina Display.  2. Install Titanium Studio and the Android SDK.  3. Open Titanium Studio and create a new Titanium Mobile project.  4. Run project in Android Emulator.    Actual Result:    Emulator is poorly displayed.    Expected Result:    Emulator should display properly and receive events in the correct location.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Emulator: MacBook Pro Retina Display: Emulator is improperly sized and touch events are inaccurate
Description: """"The Android Emulator is improperly displayed and the touch events are inaccurate on the MacBook Pro Retina Display. This is an android issue: http://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=33383 Attached image courtesy of: http://stackoverflow.com/users/147333/<USER>d Steps to Reproduce: 1. Buy a MacBook Pro w/Retina Display. 2. Install Titanium Studio and the Android SDK. 3. Open Titanium Studio and create a new Titanium Mobile project. 4. Run project in Android Emulator. Actual Result: Emulator is poorly displayed. Expected Result: Emulator should display properly and receive events in the correct location.""""",title+description
