TIMOB-9882,12,"""Android: HTTPClient send() and ready states behavior inconsistent with other platforms.""","""""""The Android HTTPClient currently supports calling send() any time even if  a request is currently pending. We should not allow send() to be called if the ready state  is not """"""""OPEN"""""""".    We should also make sure our ready state transitions match up with the other platforms.  Ex: make sure the ready state changes to OPEN once the request is done.    We need to document any of this behavior once it has been determined what is """"""""correct"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient send() and ready states behavior inconsistent with other platforms.
Description: """"The Android HTTPClient currently supports calling send() any time even if a request is currently pending. We should not allow send() to be called if the ready state is not """"""""OPEN"""""""". We should also make sure our ready state transitions match up with the other platforms. Ex: make sure the ready state changes to OPEN once the request is done. We need to document any of this behavior once it has been determined what is """"""""correct"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-9881,12,"""Blackberry: Support JIT loading of non core Ti Modules""","""""""Ti module other than the core ones (API, UI, Analytics and possibly App, Filesystem and Gesture) need to be loaded only when needed by the js code""""""",Story,"Title: Blackberry: Support JIT loading of non core Ti Modules
Description: """"Ti module other than the core ones (API, UI, Analytics and possibly App, Filesystem and Gesture) need to be loaded only when needed by the js code""""",title+description
TIMOB-9880,12,"""Android: custom title bar is not updated on device orientation change""","""""""h2. Problem description  When a custom background image is set for the title bar in Android, the image is not updated when the device is rotated. Opening a window with the right orientation, opens the right image inside the drawable-land or drawable-port directory, but that is not updated when orientation changes after the window has been open.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Create an app with the code below:        2. Be sure to put 2 different images (one large for landscape, one narrow for portrait) for the title bar under:     - platform/android/res/drawable-land/fullnavimage.png     - platform/android/res/drawable-port/fullnavimage.png    3. Set a custom theme by creating a platform/android/res/values/themes.xml file like this:        4. Open the app with the device in portrait and click the 'Open' button    5. Rotate the device in landscape: the customized title bar does not change, but the portrait one appeares stretched.    6. Keeping the device in landscape, go back, click 'Open' again: the custom image now shows correctly, but going back to portrait gives the same problem as in #5      h2. Expected result  Rotating the device shows the correct customized image  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: custom title bar is not updated on device orientation change
Description: """"h2. Problem description When a custom background image is set for the title bar in Android, the image is not updated when the device is rotated. Opening a window with the right orientation, opens the right image inside the drawable-land or drawable-port directory, but that is not updated when orientation changes after the window has been open. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Create an app with the code below: 2. Be sure to put 2 different images (one large for landscape, one narrow for portrait) for the title bar under: - platform/android/res/drawable-land/fullnavimage.png - platform/android/res/drawable-port/fullnavimage.png 3. Set a custom theme by creating a platform/android/res/values/themes.xml file like this: 4. Open the app with the device in portrait and click the 'Open' button 5. Rotate the device in landscape: the customized title bar does not change, but the portrait one appeares stretched. 6. Keeping the device in landscape, go back, click 'Open' again: the custom image now shows correctly, but going back to portrait gives the same problem as in #5 h2. Expected result Rotating the device shows the correct customized image """"",title+description
TIMOB-9879,12,"""Blackberry: Implement UI.View.fireEvent""",,Sub-task,Title: Blackberry: Implement UI.View.fireEvent,title-only
TIMOB-9878,12,"""TiAPI: Facebook authorization has changed and login does not work anymore""","""""""h2. Problem description  When using Ti.Facebook to login, once the user has entered their credentials and clicks login, the screen shows a 'Page not found' error and the login fails. However, trying to login again the second time, works. It also works if the app on Facebook is set as Native/Desktop and not Web.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a Facebook app (be sure it is set to Web, as it is by default)  2. Create an app with the code below (set the app id accordingly to the Facebook app)  3. Click the 'Login with Facebook' button  4. Enter a valid Facbeook account credentials and click Login        h2. Expected result  Facebook authentication happens and we are able to log into Facebook.    h2. Current result  A 'Page not found' screen is shown as soon as the login is performed.    h2. Related links  Looks like the problem is also present on native apps, and it does not occour if the app is set as Native/Desktop.    See this topic for some details: http://developers.facebook.com/blog/post/2012/03/02/enhanced-auth-dialog-and-updates-to-permissions/""""""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: Facebook authorization has changed and login does not work anymore
Description: """"h2. Problem description When using Ti.Facebook to login, once the user has entered their credentials and clicks login, the screen shows a 'Page not found' error and the login fails. However, trying to login again the second time, works. It also works if the app on Facebook is set as Native/Desktop and not Web. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a Facebook app (be sure it is set to Web, as it is by default) 2. Create an app with the code below (set the app id accordingly to the Facebook app) 3. Click the 'Login with Facebook' button 4. Enter a valid Facbeook account credentials and click Login h2. Expected result Facebook authentication happens and we are able to log into Facebook. h2. Current result A 'Page not found' screen is shown as soon as the login is performed. h2. Related links Looks like the problem is also present on native apps, and it does not occour if the app is set as Native/Desktop. See this topic for some details: http://developers.facebook.com/blog/post/2012/03/02/enhanced-auth-dialog-and-updates-to-permissions/""""",title+description
