TIMOB-9824,12,"""API: backgroundGradient """"colors"""" default value""","""""""We need to define the default behavior for when no """"""""colors"""""""" property is specified  in the backgroundGradient object.    Right now on iOS if you specify no value, there will be no visible gradient.  On Android not setting this property to an array causes a Java exception.    We should agree on the """"""""correct"""""""" behavior and document it.""""""",Bug,"Title: API: backgroundGradient """"colors"""" default value
Description: """"We need to define the default behavior for when no """"""""colors"""""""" property is specified in the backgroundGradient object. Right now on iOS if you specify no value, there will be no visible gradient. On Android not setting this property to an array causes a Java exception. We should agree on the """"""""correct"""""""" behavior and document it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9823,12,"""Tooling: Collate platform-since versions before calling generator""","""""""For the JSDuck generator, I'm trying to improve the display of the """"""""since"""""""" dates, but the logic is complicated when dealing with per-platform since dates. For example, given:    since: { android: """"""""2.1.0"""""""" }    The generator just gets the object. To turn it into a reasonable display, it needs to figure out:    - which platforms are supported  - the default """"""""since"""""""" values for each of those platforms, since they're not specified  - whether the enclosing object has a since: date on it, which we should use instead of the default """"""""since"""""""" date, if it's newer    It would be excellent if docgen could collate this information, and replace the partial """"""""since"""""""" object with a complete one. This would make it trivial to display since.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Collate platform-since versions before calling generator
Description: """"For the JSDuck generator, I'm trying to improve the display of the """"""""since"""""""" dates, but the logic is complicated when dealing with per-platform since dates. For example, given: since: { android: """"""""2.1.0"""""""" } The generator just gets the object. To turn it into a reasonable display, it needs to figure out: - which platforms are supported - the default """"""""since"""""""" values for each of those platforms, since they're not specified - whether the enclosing object has a since: date on it, which we should use instead of the default """"""""since"""""""" date, if it's newer It would be excellent if docgen could collate this information, and replace the partial """"""""since"""""""" object with a complete one. This would make it trivial to display since. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9822,12,"""MobileWeb: customer wants use a Slider with two thumbImages setting a custom range""","""""""h2. Request description  Customer wants to use a slider displaying two 'thumbImage' and being able to get a range value between the two.    We can create a slider including only one thumbImage and getting a value ranging from the starting point to the ending point of the slider. Customer wants to be able to dynamically set lower and higher value of the range using two thumbImages.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: customer wants use a Slider with two thumbImages setting a custom range
