Description: """"h2. Request description Customer wants to use a slider displaying two 'thumbImage' and being able to get a range value between the two. We can create a slider including only one thumbImage and getting a value ranging from the starting point to the ending point of the slider. Customer wants to be able to dynamically set lower and higher value of the range using two thumbImages. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9819,12,"""Android: backgroundGradient on heavyweight window force-closes app""","""""""h2. Expected results    Per the changes in TIMOB-1124, I should be able to set a backgroundGradient on a heavyweight Android window (i.e. in a tab group or purposely set)    h2. Actual results    Causes force-close. Works as expected on lightweight window.        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: backgroundGradient on heavyweight window force-closes app
Description: """"h2. Expected results Per the changes in TIMOB-1124, I should be able to set a backgroundGradient on a heavyweight Android window (i.e. in a tab group or purposely set) h2. Actual results Causes force-close. Works as expected on lightweight window. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9817,12,"""Tooling: Create machine-readable file format to describe tiapp.xml platform configuration options""","""""""Reviewing TISTUD-568 and TISTUD-1524, it seems worthwhile to create some sort of description that encapsulates the possible values for per-platform configuration options.    The goal would be to provide a file Titanium Studio could read, interpret, and then display GUI configuration options for common platform settings as part of an extension of TISTUD-1824    While Studio could natively create a GUI for these items, the mix of an increasing number of supported platforms as well as version differences between SDKs makes this an increasingly problematic direction to take.    Some thoughts:  * XSD seems a natural option, but JSON is okay as well. We are alsread planning on creating an XSD for the root tiapp.xml file.  * Some items may require a drop down list of options, perhaps pulled from available SDKs (see iOS Deployment targets). Perhaps these could be encoded in a format Studio knows how to fill in with live values  * Android activities pose a problem, but perhaps there is some simple way that we can describe the common use case.    """"""",Story,"Title: Tooling: Create machine-readable file format to describe tiapp.xml platform configuration options
Description: """"Reviewing TISTUD-568 and TISTUD-1524, it seems worthwhile to create some sort of description that encapsulates the possible values for per-platform configuration options. The goal would be to provide a file Titanium Studio could read, interpret, and then display GUI configuration options for common platform settings as part of an extension of TISTUD-1824 While Studio could natively create a GUI for these items, the mix of an increasing number of supported platforms as well as version differences between SDKs makes this an increasingly problematic direction to take. Some thoughts: * XSD seems a natural option, but JSON is okay as well. We are alsread planning on creating an XSD for the root tiapp.xml file. * Some items may require a drop down list of options, perhaps pulled from available SDKs (see iOS Deployment targets). Perhaps these could be encoded in a format Studio knows how to fill in with live values * Android activities pose a problem, but perhaps there is some simple way that we can describe the common use case. """"",title+description
