TIMOB-9803,12,"""Android: Upgrade Rhino to version 1.7R4""","""""""We recently fixed an issue in Titanium Studio with JS Lint running slowly by upgrading to the latest version of Rhino.    Based on the release notes for 1.7R4, there seem to be performance improvements over the last release. It appears that the 1.7R4 release happened after Titanium Mobile last upgraded.    https://developer.mozilla.org/en/New_in_Rhino_1.7R4""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Upgrade Rhino to version 1.7R4
Description: """"We recently fixed an issue in Titanium Studio with JS Lint running slowly by upgrading to the latest version of Rhino. Based on the release notes for 1.7R4, there seem to be performance improvements over the last release. It appears that the 1.7R4 release happened after Titanium Mobile last upgraded. https://developer.mozilla.org/en/New_in_Rhino_1.7R4""""",title+description
TIMOB-9802,12,"""Android: ScrollView - ScrollView scrolls horizontally when manually set to vertical layout""","""""""This is a regression.Was not occuring in 2.0.2.    Details:  If the scrollView.width and scrollView.height are manually set to a vertical layout i.e. do not use the layout property, vertical scrollView will not scroll.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch code in app.js:    2. Press Flip  3. Try scrolling    Actual: ScrollView will not scroll vertically, but is will scroll horizontally.  Expected: Should be able to scroll vertically and not horizontally.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ScrollView - ScrollView scrolls horizontally when manually set to vertical layout
Description: """"This is a regression.Was not occuring in 2.0.2. Details: If the scrollView.width and scrollView.height are manually set to a vertical layout i.e. do not use the layout property, vertical scrollView will not scroll. Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch code in app.js: 2. Press Flip 3. Try scrolling Actual: ScrollView will not scroll vertically, but is will scroll horizontally. Expected: Should be able to scroll vertically and not horizontally.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9801,12,"""iOS: Window - Black area appears after modal window closes along with change in orientation""","""""""Black area appears after modal window closes along with change in orientation    This is not a Regression.It even occurs on 2.0.2    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Install the app on device and launch it.  2. Press the """"""""Press Me"""""""" button.  3. Rotate the device as top is pointing right.  4. Keep pressing the Close button and rotate the device to portrait mode and then release the button.    Expected Result:  The modal window should be closed    Actual result:  Black area appears on the first window. And, the first window continues to appear in the landscape mode.    app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window - Black area appears after modal window closes along with change in orientation
Description: """"Black area appears after modal window closes along with change in orientation This is not a Regression.It even occurs on 2.0.2 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Install the app on device and launch it. 2. Press the """"""""Press Me"""""""" button. 3. Rotate the device as top is pointing right. 4. Keep pressing the Close button and rotate the device to portrait mode and then release the button. Expected Result: The modal window should be closed Actual result: Black area appears on the first window. And, the first window continues to appear in the landscape mode. app.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-9800,12,"""iOS: Should not exit search mode when click on tableview""","""""""If I search for """"""""aa"""""""" in the below code, I get to see only two rows. If I click on any of the rows, the search exits and the 4 rows gets visible again. In the real application, clicking on a row will load a new screen. The customer wants that, when you hit the back button, you come back on the table with the search still there.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Should not exit search mode when click on tableview
Description: """"If I search for """"""""aa"""""""" in the below code, I get to see only two rows. If I click on any of the rows, the search exits and the 4 rows gets visible again. In the real application, clicking on a row will load a new screen. The customer wants that, when you hit the back button, you come back on the table with the search still there. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9799,12,"""APIDoc: Need way to identify varargs""","""""""Would be good to add a format for this. JSDuck supports varargs so we can translate straight through for that format.  It appears to be supported in JSCA as well, using the """"""""usage"""""""" field, which can be """"""""required,"""""""" """"""""optional,"""""""" """"""""zero-or-more,"""""""" or """"""""one-or-more.""""""""    Perhaps we could just add a field to the parameter description like repeatable: true or vararg: true?  """"""",New Feature,"Title: APIDoc: Need way to identify varargs
Description: """"Would be good to add a format for this. JSDuck supports varargs so we can translate straight through for that format. It appears to be supported in JSCA as well, using the """"""""usage"""""""" field, which can be """"""""required,"""""""" """"""""optional,"""""""" """"""""zero-or-more,"""""""" or """"""""one-or-more."""""""" Perhaps we could just add a field to the parameter description like repeatable: true or vararg: true? """"",title+description
TIMOB-9797,12,"""Android: HTTP Post will save a photo at Internal phone storage""","""""""h6.Issue  HTTP Post a photo that will be saved at Internal phone storage    h6.Tested on  Droid Razr 2.3.5    h6.Repro steps  1) Run code below & pick up an image from the gallery  2) Wait till the image gets uploaded  3) Go through with any File Manager app to monitor Internal phone storage directory. Notice the uploaded image is present at such location having a similar file name: """"""""tixhr***.jpeg""""""""    h6.Repro sequences  - app.js      - upload.php      h6.Work around  Walk through all files that start with the name """"""""tixhr"""""""" to manually purge them.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTP Post will save a photo at Internal phone storage
Description: """"h6.Issue HTTP Post a photo that will be saved at Internal phone storage h6.Tested on Droid Razr 2.3.5 h6.Repro steps 1) Run code below & pick up an image from the gallery 2) Wait till the image gets uploaded 3) Go through with any File Manager app to monitor Internal phone storage directory. Notice the uploaded image is present at such location having a similar file name: """"""""tixhr***.jpeg"""""""" h6.Repro sequences - app.js - upload.php h6.Work around Walk through all files that start with the name """"""""tixhr"""""""" to manually purge them.""""",title+description
