TIMOB-9738,12,"""MobileWeb: 'focus' tabGroup event it's triggered when opening a child window when using an activity indicator""","""""""h3. Problem description  'focus' event on tabGroup it's triggered also when opening a child window when using an activity indicator    h3. Steps to reproduce  Run the sample code.  'focus' event it's correctly triggered when opening the tabGroup.  Then click on the 'Child window'. activity indicator should appear. Then, when also win2 it's opened, the focus event on the tabGroup it's triggered again.  On iOS only the first event it's triggered. Also on MobileWeb it's correctly being triggered only the first one if we just remove the activity indicator.        """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: 'focus' tabGroup event it's triggered when opening a child window when using an activity indicator
Description: """"h3. Problem description 'focus' event on tabGroup it's triggered also when opening a child window when using an activity indicator h3. Steps to reproduce Run the sample code. 'focus' event it's correctly triggered when opening the tabGroup. Then click on the 'Child window'. activity indicator should appear. Then, when also win2 it's opened, the focus event on the tabGroup it's triggered again. On iOS only the first event it's triggered. Also on MobileWeb it's correctly being triggered only the first one if we just remove the activity indicator. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9737,12,"""iOS: using number for facebook appID account causes crash on IPad""","""""""UPDATE UPDATE: Changing this from a crasher to a feature request to compensate for setting facebook module's appID to a number, not a string.    UPDATE: this test fails on all Ipad 1 - 5.1.1, Ipad 2 - 4.3.5 and Ipad 3 - 5.1.1    Clicking on Users->Social->External Link->Login with facebook     Repro steps:  1. Switch to DNS: 184.73.81.90 on IPad     1.5  edit Resources/windows/social/externalLink.js and set Ti.Facebook.appid to 378694535499807   b.  edit Resources/windows/social/externalLogin.js and set Ti.Facebook.appid to 378694535499807    2. launch ti.cloud sample app  3. click on Users->Social->External Link->Login with facebook     Actual:  App quits, crash log is attached.    Expected:  Bring up facebook login window    Note: This works correctly on android ICS galaxy nexus """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: using number for facebook appID account causes crash on IPad
Description: """"UPDATE UPDATE: Changing this from a crasher to a feature request to compensate for setting facebook module's appID to a number, not a string. UPDATE: this test fails on all Ipad 1 - 5.1.1, Ipad 2 - 4.3.5 and Ipad 3 - 5.1.1 Clicking on Users->Social->External Link->Login with facebook Repro steps: 1. Switch to DNS: 184.73.81.90 on IPad 1.5 edit Resources/windows/social/externalLink.js and set Ti.Facebook.appid to 378694535499807 b. edit Resources/windows/social/externalLogin.js and set Ti.Facebook.appid to 378694535499807 2. launch ti.cloud sample app 3. click on Users->Social->External Link->Login with facebook Actual: App quits, crash log is attached. Expected: Bring up facebook login window Note: This works correctly on android ICS galaxy nexus """"",title+description
TIMOB-9736,12,"""iOS: Text Area in Scroll View in Modal Window Goes offscreen on focus""","""""""h3. Description   When text area inside scroll view, inside modal window, is focused, the scroll view jumps up out of view then settles back down to the correct position above the keyboard. If text is entered the text area does not settle back down above the keyboard. It stays up and out of view. This only happens on device and works fine in simulator.     h3. Test Case         h3. To Reproduce    1. Copy and paste this code into your app.js  2. Run the app on the device  3. Click on the button and it will open a modal window  4. Scroll down and tap in the text area  5. Type in the text area""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Text Area in Scroll View in Modal Window Goes offscreen on focus
Description: """"h3. Description When text area inside scroll view, inside modal window, is focused, the scroll view jumps up out of view then settles back down to the correct position above the keyboard. If text is entered the text area does not settle back down above the keyboard. It stays up and out of view. This only happens on device and works fine in simulator. h3. Test Case h3. To Reproduce 1. Copy and paste this code into your app.js 2. Run the app on the device 3. Click on the button and it will open a modal window 4. Scroll down and tap in the text area 5. Type in the text area""""",title+description
TIMOB-9735,12,"""Android: Error Dialog Platform Parity""","""""""h1. Parity Issue  Error dialogs are inconsistent across deploy types and platforms.    h2. Android Behavior  On Android, [error dialogs always show up|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/runtime/v8/src/native/V8Util.cpp#L127], even in production.    h2. iOS Behavior  iOS only shows error dialogs [when the deploy type is not equal to production|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiApp.m#L524].    h2. Mobile Web Behavior  Mobile Web [shows errors|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/mobileweb/titanium/Ti.js#L306] depending on the [config|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/mobileweb/src/config.js#L36].    h2. Reproduction  This will throw an error. The various platforms will handle it as they wish.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: '#fff'  });  win.add(fail);  win.open();  {code}    h2. Desired Behavior  Error dialogs are consistent across deployment types. Config values are also equally exposed on all platforms.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Error Dialog Platform Parity
Description: """"h1. Parity Issue Error dialogs are inconsistent across deploy types and platforms. h2. Android Behavior On Android, [error dialogs always show up|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/runtime/v8/src/native/V8Util.cpp#L127], even in production. h2. iOS Behavior iOS only shows error dialogs [when the deploy type is not equal to production|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiApp.m#L524]. h2. Mobile Web Behavior Mobile Web [shows errors|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/mobileweb/titanium/Ti.js#L306] depending on the [config|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/mobileweb/src/config.js#L36]. h2. Reproduction This will throw an error. The various platforms will handle it as they wish. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); win.add(fail); win.open(); {code} h2. Desired Behavior Error dialogs are consistent across deployment types. Config values are also equally exposed on all platforms.""""",title+description
