TIMOB-9729,12,"""Android: Image Views - Device rotation restarts stopped animation on Droid devices ""","""""""Description:  While testing KS Views I noticed that stopped Animation restarts after device rotation.    Not a regression, occurs on 2.0.2 and on Droid devices only.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch KitchenSink  2. Go to Base UI-Views-Image Views-Animated  3. Press """"""""Stop Animation""""""""  4. Rotate device    Expected result:  Animation should not restart.    Actual result:  Animation restarts""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image Views - Device rotation restarts stopped animation on Droid devices
Description: """"Description: While testing KS Views I noticed that stopped Animation restarts after device rotation. Not a regression, occurs on 2.0.2 and on Droid devices only. Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch KitchenSink 2. Go to Base UI-Views-Image Views-Animated 3. Press """"""""Stop Animation"""""""" 4. Rotate device Expected result: Animation should not restart. Actual result: Animation restarts""""",title+description
TIMOB-9728,12,"""MobileWeb: Add data-widget-properties to all Titanium DOM nodes.""","""""""Being able to add properties to a dom node is extremely useful. It allows developers to learn more about a DOM node in Element inspector in WebKit Inspector to make it easier to interpret.    The key property to add is whether or not a control is hidden. For this to work, the View._publish() method must be rock solid, which doesn't quite seem to be yet. This must be fixed first.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Add data-widget-properties to all Titanium DOM nodes.
Description: """"Being able to add properties to a dom node is extremely useful. It allows developers to learn more about a DOM node in Element inspector in WebKit Inspector to make it easier to interpret. The key property to add is whether or not a control is hidden. For this to work, the View._publish() method must be rock solid, which doesn't quite seem to be yet. This must be fixed first.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9727,12,"""Tooling: Improve continuous integration JSON stream to provide similar format to release stream""","""""""Currently the two streams (continuous integration and release) have different formats:    Release:      Continuous integration:      Converting the continuous integration stream to the same format as release will allow us to provide it as an option to download in the """"""""Install Titanium SDK from URL"""""""" feature/""""""",Story,"Title: Tooling: Improve continuous integration JSON stream to provide similar format to release stream
Description: """"Currently the two streams (continuous integration and release) have different formats: Release: Continuous integration: Converting the continuous integration stream to the same format as release will allow us to provide it as an option to download in the """"""""Install Titanium SDK from URL"""""""" feature/""""",title+description
TIMOB-9726,12,"""Android: Tableview:Softkeyboard waits for 'focus' alert to get dismissed to get hide.""","""""""This is not a regression.It exists as far as 1.8.2    It is not reproducible on Android 3.2 samsung galaxy tab 620,Android 4.0.2 samsung galaxy nexus.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Use the code below:     2) Run the app in portrait mode.  3) Click on any row of the tableview.  4) WITHOUT clicking ok on the focus alert,rotate the device to landscape mode.    Expected result:  2) After step 2, app should be running with tableview shown along with 10 rows.  3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard should be displayed.  4) 'Blur fired' alert should be displayed and soft keyboard should be hidden.    Actual result:  2) After step 2, app gets running with tableview shown along with 10 rows.  3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard gets displayed.  4) 'Blur fired' alert is displayed and soft keyboard do not hide.    Issue - Softkeyboard waits for 'focus fired' alert to get dismissed.After user clicks ok on alert,softkeyboard hides.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tableview:Softkeyboard waits for 'focus' alert to get dismissed to get hide.
Description: """"This is not a regression.It exists as far as 1.8.2 It is not reproducible on Android 3.2 samsung galaxy tab 620,Android 4.0.2 samsung galaxy nexus. Steps to reproduce: 1) Use the code below: 2) Run the app in portrait mode. 3) Click on any row of the tableview. 4) WITHOUT clicking ok on the focus alert,rotate the device to landscape mode. Expected result: 2) After step 2, app should be running with tableview shown along with 10 rows. 3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard should be displayed. 4) 'Blur fired' alert should be displayed and soft keyboard should be hidden. Actual result: 2) After step 2, app gets running with tableview shown along with 10 rows. 3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard gets displayed. 4) 'Blur fired' alert is displayed and soft keyboard do not hide. Issue - Softkeyboard waits for 'focus fired' alert to get dismissed.After user clicks ok on alert,softkeyboard hides.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9725,12,"""Android: Tableview:Softkeyboard hiding on blur event call depends on number of rows in tableview""","""""""This is not a regression.It exists as far as 1.8.2    Steps to reproduce:  1) Use the code below:    2) Run the app in portrait mode.  3) Click on any row of the tableview.  4) Click ok on the focus alert and rotate the device to landscape mode.  5) Click ok on the blur event and click on any row of the tableview.  6) Click ok on the focus alert and rotate the device back to portrait mode.    Expected result:  2) After step 2, app should be running with tableview shown along with 10 rows.  3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard should be displayed.  4) 'Blur fired' alert should be displayed and soft keyboard should be hidden.  5) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard should be displayed.  6) 'Blur fired' alert should be displayed and soft keyboard should be hidden.    Actual result:  2) After step 2, app gets running with tableview shown along with 10 rows.  3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard gets displayed.  4) 'Blur fired' alert is displayed and soft keyboard gets hidden.  5) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard gets displayed.  6) 'Blur fired' alert is displayed and soft keyboard is not hidden.    When the number of rows get out of screen,keyboard stops hiding on blur event call.If number of rows are kept like under 5,softkeyboard gets hide as expected.    Particular issue -  In above code, replace  var win=Titanium.UI.createWindow();  win.backgroundColor='red';    with     var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    softInputMode : (Titanium.UI.Android) ? Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN : '',    windowSoftInputMode : (Titanium.UI.Android) ? Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN : ''    });  Now portrait to landscape orientationchange will always hide the softkeyboard,but landscape to portrait would not hide it for larger(say >20) no. of rows.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tableview:Softkeyboard hiding on blur event call depends on number of rows in tableview
Description: """"This is not a regression.It exists as far as 1.8.2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Use the code below: 2) Run the app in portrait mode. 3) Click on any row of the tableview. 4) Click ok on the focus alert and rotate the device to landscape mode. 5) Click ok on the blur event and click on any row of the tableview. 6) Click ok on the focus alert and rotate the device back to portrait mode. Expected result: 2) After step 2, app should be running with tableview shown along with 10 rows. 3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard should be displayed. 4) 'Blur fired' alert should be displayed and soft keyboard should be hidden. 5) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard should be displayed. 6) 'Blur fired' alert should be displayed and soft keyboard should be hidden. Actual result: 2) After step 2, app gets running with tableview shown along with 10 rows. 3) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard gets displayed. 4) 'Blur fired' alert is displayed and soft keyboard gets hidden. 5) 'Focus fired' alert and soft keyboard gets displayed. 6) 'Blur fired' alert is displayed and soft keyboard is not hidden. When the number of rows get out of screen,keyboard stops hiding on blur event call.If number of rows are kept like under 5,softkeyboard gets hide as expected. Particular issue - In above code, replace var win=Titanium.UI.createWindow(); win.backgroundColor='red'; with var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ softInputMode : (Titanium.UI.Android) ? Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN : '', windowSoftInputMode : (Titanium.UI.Android) ? Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN : '' }); Now portrait to landscape orientationchange will always hide the softkeyboard,but landscape to portrait would not hide it for larger(say >20) no. of rows.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9724,12,"""Android: VideoPlayer: The paused Remote Streaming video starts playing when application brought back to foreground and initially resumes from wrong point""","""""""The remote streaming video when paused and application put to background, starts to play automatically when application brought to foreground. Also when it starts playing it initially plays video for first couple of seconds of the video and then resumes from the point where it was paused.    Not a Regression. This also occurs on 2.0.2    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Open Kitchen Application  2. Go to Phone -> Play Movie -> Remote Streaming  3. Let the video play for few seconds  4. Pause the video and background the Kitchen Sink application  5. Again open the Kitchen Sink application (to bring to foreground)    Actual: The video starts to pay itself. Also it initially plays video and sound of the first few seconds of the video and then resumes playing from the point it was paused.    Expected: The video should remain in paused state when the application again comes to foreground""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: VideoPlayer: The paused Remote Streaming video starts playing when application brought back to foreground and initially resumes from wrong point
Description: """"The remote streaming video when paused and application put to background, starts to play automatically when application brought to foreground. Also when it starts playing it initially plays video for first couple of seconds of the video and then resumes from the point where it was paused. Not a Regression. This also occurs on 2.0.2 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Open Kitchen Application 2. Go to Phone -> Play Movie -> Remote Streaming 3. Let the video play for few seconds 4. Pause the video and background the Kitchen Sink application 5. Again open the Kitchen Sink application (to bring to foreground) Actual: The video starts to pay itself. Also it initially plays video and sound of the first few seconds of the video and then resumes playing from the point it was paused. Expected: The video should remain in paused state when the application again comes to foreground""""",title+description
TIMOB-9723,12,"""Android: Textfield:Focus event is getting fired with blur event call on orientation change.""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists as far as 1.8.2    Steps to reproduce:  1) Use the code below:    2) Run the app  3) Click 'ok' on the focus alert and rotate device to a new orientation.    Expected result:  2) After step 2,app should be running and an alert 'Focus fired' should be displayed.  3) Alert 'Blur fired' should be displayed.    Actual result:  2) After step 2,app is running and an alert 'Focus fired'is displayed.  3) 2 alerts 'Blur fired' and 'Focus fired' are displayed.    Focus event should not get fired.It is not called in orientationchange eventlistener.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Textfield:Focus event is getting fired with blur event call on orientation change.
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists as far as 1.8.2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Use the code below: 2) Run the app 3) Click 'ok' on the focus alert and rotate device to a new orientation. Expected result: 2) After step 2,app should be running and an alert 'Focus fired' should be displayed. 3) Alert 'Blur fired' should be displayed. Actual result: 2) After step 2,app is running and an alert 'Focus fired'is displayed. 3) 2 alerts 'Blur fired' and 'Focus fired' are displayed. Focus event should not get fired.It is not called in orientationchange eventlistener.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9722,12,"""Android: Textfield:Focus event is fired when soft keyboard 'done' button is pressed.""","""""""This is not a regression.It exists as far as 1.8.2.  It occurs only on android 4.0.2 samsung galaxy nexus.  This is working fine on android 2.2 and android 3.2     Steps to reproduce:  1) Use the code below:    2) Run the app.  3) Click 'ok'on the alert displayed and again click the textfield.  4) Press 'done' on the soft keyboard.    Expected result:  2) After step 2,app should be running and an alert should be displayed stating 'Focus fired'.  3) The soft keyboard should be invoked.  4) The soft keyboard should get dismissed without any alerts.    Actual result:  2) After step 2,app should be running and an alert should be displayed stating 'Focus fired'.  3) The soft keyboard should be invoked.  4) The soft keyboard should get dismissed but a focus alert 'Focus fired' is displayed.    Focus event should not get fired.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Textfield:Focus event is fired when soft keyboard 'done' button is pressed.
Description: """"This is not a regression.It exists as far as 1.8.2. It occurs only on android 4.0.2 samsung galaxy nexus. This is working fine on android 2.2 and android 3.2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Use the code below: 2) Run the app. 3) Click 'ok'on the alert displayed and again click the textfield. 4) Press 'done' on the soft keyboard. Expected result: 2) After step 2,app should be running and an alert should be displayed stating 'Focus fired'. 3) The soft keyboard should be invoked. 4) The soft keyboard should get dismissed without any alerts. Actual result: 2) After step 2,app should be running and an alert should be displayed stating 'Focus fired'. 3) The soft keyboard should be invoked. 4) The soft keyboard should get dismissed but a focus alert 'Focus fired' is displayed. Focus event should not get fired.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9721,12,"""Android: WebView: Zooming out of webview with image background shows blank area on Android 2.X and 3.X""","""""""The webview with background image shows a white blank space when zoom out on webview is done.    Not a Regression. The issues exists as far as 1.8.2    The issue occurs on Android 2.X and 3.X. It does not happen on Android 4.X.    Steps To Reproduce:  1. Open Kitchen Sink application  2. Go to Base UI -> Views -> Web Views -> Local URL  3. Swipe on the screen to get the zoom control  4. Click on the Zoom out button one or more times    Actual: A white blank space start to show below the web view    Expected: Zoom Out should not show any white space""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView: Zooming out of webview with image background shows blank area on Android 2.X and 3.X
Description: """"The webview with background image shows a white blank space when zoom out on webview is done. Not a Regression. The issues exists as far as 1.8.2 The issue occurs on Android 2.X and 3.X. It does not happen on Android 4.X. Steps To Reproduce: 1. Open Kitchen Sink application 2. Go to Base UI -> Views -> Web Views -> Local URL 3. Swipe on the screen to get the zoom control 4. Click on the Zoom out button one or more times Actual: A white blank space start to show below the web view Expected: Zoom Out should not show any white space""""",title+description
TIMOB-9720,12,"""Android: Textfield:Soft keyboard is not displayed after focus event fired,one more click is needed for its display.""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists as far as 1.8.2  Steps to reproduce:  1) Use the below code:    It creates a textfield on window with its focusable property to true.  2) Run the app.    Expected result:  The soft keyboard should be displayed with the app running.    Actual result:  No soft keyboard is displayed unless user clicks on textfield.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Textfield:Soft keyboard is not displayed after focus event fired,one more click is needed for its display.
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists as far as 1.8.2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Use the below code: It creates a textfield on window with its focusable property to true. 2) Run the app. Expected result: The soft keyboard should be displayed with the app running. Actual result: No soft keyboard is displayed unless user clicks on textfield.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9719,12,"""Android: Webview: Zoom Out does not work correctly on Android ICS""","""""""The zoom out control on Webview does not function correctly on Android ICS. The zoom out gets disabled before complete zoom out.    Not a regression. This occurs as far as 1.8.2    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create an application with a webview  2. Launch the application  3. Double tap on the screen to show view at min size / rotate the device  4. Now click on the Zoom in button (+) more than once  5. Next start Zoom out (-)    Actual: After 2-3 clicks on zoom out, the zoom out would get disabled. Wait for the zoom control to hide. Swipe on the screen would again show the zoom control but with zoom out enabled again.  The above cycle would continue until the view completely zooms out.    Expected: The zoom out control should be enabled till it completely zooms out    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Webview: Zoom Out does not work correctly on Android ICS
Description: """"The zoom out control on Webview does not function correctly on Android ICS. The zoom out gets disabled before complete zoom out. Not a regression. This occurs as far as 1.8.2 Steps to reproduce: 1. Create an application with a webview 2. Launch the application 3. Double tap on the screen to show view at min size / rotate the device 4. Now click on the Zoom in button (+) more than once 5. Next start Zoom out (-) Actual: After 2-3 clicks on zoom out, the zoom out would get disabled. Wait for the zoom control to hide. Swipe on the screen would again show the zoom control but with zoom out enabled again. The above cycle would continue until the view completely zooms out. Expected: The zoom out control should be enabled till it completely zooms out """"",title+description
TIMOB-9718,12,"""MobileWeb: textField events generate bad behaviors""","""""""h3. Problem description  Setting event listeners (tested using 'blur', 'focus' and 'change') to a textField results in getting bad behaviors, depending on the browser (tested on Firefox and Safari)    h3. Steps to reproduce    Run sample code and click on the textField.  Result:  Firefox: blur and focus events are triggered, then textField it's not focused.  Safari: blur and focus events are triggered continuously (then have to actually kill the browser in this case)          h3. Additional Notes:  Set only one single event to be triggered.    Result:  only the 'focus' event it's not behaving correctly:  Firefox: focus event triggered, textField it's not being focused. Other events work fine.  Safari: focus event triggered continuously. Other events work fine.    However, there are issues when setting 'blur' and 'change' events together:  Firefox: typing a character, also the blur event it's triggered (should be triggered only the change one)  Safari: typing a character, the blur event it's triggered continuously (have to kill the browser in this case too)  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: textField events generate bad behaviors
Description: """"h3. Problem description Setting event listeners (tested using 'blur', 'focus' and 'change') to a textField results in getting bad behaviors, depending on the browser (tested on Firefox and Safari) h3. Steps to reproduce Run sample code and click on the textField. Result: Firefox: blur and focus events are triggered, then textField it's not focused. Safari: blur and focus events are triggered continuously (then have to actually kill the browser in this case) h3. Additional Notes: Set only one single event to be triggered. Result: only the 'focus' event it's not behaving correctly: Firefox: focus event triggered, textField it's not being focused. Other events work fine. Safari: focus event triggered continuously. Other events work fine. However, there are issues when setting 'blur' and 'change' events together: Firefox: typing a character, also the blur event it's triggered (should be triggered only the change one) Safari: typing a character, the blur event it's triggered continuously (have to kill the browser in this case too) """"",title+description
TIMOB-9717,12,"""MobileWeb: textFields are not focusable on Chrome""","""""""h2. Problem description  textFields are not focusable on Google Chrome    h2. Sample code  Steps to reproduce:  Run sample code on Google Chrome and click on the text field.  Result: text field it's not focusable and it's not possible to type in it    """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: textFields are not focusable on Chrome
Description: """"h2. Problem description textFields are not focusable on Google Chrome h2. Sample code Steps to reproduce: Run sample code on Google Chrome and click on the text field. Result: text field it's not focusable and it's not possible to type in it """"",title+description
TIMOB-9716,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.SIZE for TableView in ScrollView doesn't work as expected""","""""""Ti.UI.SIZE for TableView in ScrollView doesn't work. If you give height an explicit value it shows all the rows but using Ti.UI.SIZE produces a table view that is only 1.5 rows high. If you don't put the table view into a scroll view, then these two configurations produce the exact same table view.  h5. Explicit value for the height property: The pastie link of the sample code   http://pastie.org/4112802    h5. Ti.UI.SIZE for the height property: The pastie link of the sample code      http://pastie.org/4112830      h4. Repo Steps  1. Run the above code samples in your app.js  2. The tableview with explicit height value appears as expected but the table view with TI.UI.SIZE appears only 1.5 rows high.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.SIZE for TableView in ScrollView doesn't work as expected
Description: """"Ti.UI.SIZE for TableView in ScrollView doesn't work. If you give height an explicit value it shows all the rows but using Ti.UI.SIZE produces a table view that is only 1.5 rows high. If you don't put the table view into a scroll view, then these two configurations produce the exact same table view. h5. Explicit value for the height property: The pastie link of the sample code http://pastie.org/4112802 h5. Ti.UI.SIZE for the height property: The pastie link of the sample code http://pastie.org/4112830 h4. Repo Steps 1. Run the above code samples in your app.js 2. The tableview with explicit height value appears as expected but the table view with TI.UI.SIZE appears only 1.5 rows high.""""",title+description
