TIMOB-9676,12,"""MobileWeb: BaseUI-->Tab Groups:Tapping on base UI does not open any page.""","""""""Tapping on base UI does not open any page.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for Windows Phone mango).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on Base UI tab.  6.Tap on the tab group table row.  7.You will notice that nothing happens on tapping on tab roups.    Actual result:  1.Tapping on base UI does not open any page.    Expected result:  1.should see 6 buttons .     A. Add/Remove TAB     B. Animate Tab Group     C.Close/Animate Tab Group     D.Set Active Tab(Index)     E.Set Active Tab(Object)     F.Switch customization off""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: BaseUI-->Tab Groups:Tapping on base UI does not open any page.
Description: """"Tapping on base UI does not open any page. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for Windows Phone mango). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on Base UI tab. 6.Tap on the tab group table row. 7.You will notice that nothing happens on tapping on tab roups. Actual result: 1.Tapping on base UI does not open any page. Expected result: 1.should see 6 buttons . A. Add/Remove TAB B. Animate Tab Group C.Close/Animate Tab Group D.Set Active Tab(Index) E.Set Active Tab(Object) F.Switch customization off""""",title+description
TIMOB-9675,12,"""KitchenSink: Swipe event returns Runtime Error on Kindle Fire""","""""""Description:  Swipe event returns Runtime Error on Kindle Fire. Log is attached.    Regression, does not occur in 2.0.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink-Nook  2. Go to Base UI - Window Events  3. Swipe on screen    Actual result:  Runtime Error appears    Expected result:  No Runtime Error""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Swipe event returns Runtime Error on Kindle Fire
Description: """"Description: Swipe event returns Runtime Error on Kindle Fire. Log is attached. Regression, does not occur in 2.0.2. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink-Nook 2. Go to Base UI - Window Events 3. Swipe on screen Actual result: Runtime Error appears Expected result: No Runtime Error""""",title+description
TIMOB-9674,12,"""MobileWeb: view - can not click a view that is over top of an imageView when there is not backgroundColor set on the view in IE9""","""""""You can not click a view that is over top of an imageView when there is not backgroundColor set on the view in IE9    h4. Steps to repro:  Step 1: run the code below in ie9  Step 2: click on the image and notice that the singletap event is not fired unless you click to the side of the image on the view (if you run it in another browser like chrome you will be able to click directly on the image and the singletap event will fire).    {code:js}  var win  = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'white'  });  win.open();    var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({   height: 300,   width: 300,   backgroundColor: '#666',   image: """"""""http://outskirtsbattledome.wikispaces.com/file/view/Bender.jpg/125149777/Bender.jpg"""""""",   zIndex: 5  });    var view = Ti.UI.createView({   // Workaround   // backgroundColor: '#000',   // opacity: 0,   zIndex: 10  });  view.addEventListener('singletap', function(){   Ti.API.info('########### singletap');  });    win.add(iv);  win.add(view);  {code}    h4. Workaround:  Set the backgroundColor and set the view opacity to zero""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: view - can not click a view that is over top of an imageView when there is not backgroundColor set on the view in IE9
Description: """"You can not click a view that is over top of an imageView when there is not backgroundColor set on the view in IE9 h4. Steps to repro: Step 1: run the code below in ie9 Step 2: click on the image and notice that the singletap event is not fired unless you click to the side of the image on the view (if you run it in another browser like chrome you will be able to click directly on the image and the singletap event will fire). {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white' }); win.open(); var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({ height: 300, width: 300, backgroundColor: '#666', image: """"""""http://outskirtsbattledome.wikispaces.com/file/view/Bender.jpg/125149777/Bender.jpg"""""""", zIndex: 5 }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ // Workaround // backgroundColor: '#000', // opacity: 0, zIndex: 10 }); view.addEventListener('singletap', function(){ Ti.API.info('########### singletap'); }); win.add(iv); win.add(view); {code} h4. Workaround: Set the backgroundColor and set the view opacity to zero""""",title+description
TIMOB-9673,12,"""Android - Map View HYBRID_TYPE does not include satellite imagery""","""""""This is a <USER>of Pedro's original bug, which got turned into a doc bug. We are fixing the doc for 2.1, but this is an actual code bug which should be addressed in the future.     According to the doc, Ti.Map.HYBRID_TYPE is defined as a map with satellite imagery with roads and road names, and Ti.Map.SATELLITE_TYPE is defined as a map with satellite imagery with _no_ roads or names.    On Android, specifying SATELLITE_TYPE brings up the map with satellite imagery and road names, i.e., a hybrid map. Google's Android Map APIs don't support a pure satellite map, so this is probably as good as we can do.    However, on Android, HYBRID_TYPE for a map actually brings up a road map with _no_ satellite imagery.    Here's why:    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/map/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/map/TiMapView.java#L750      Expected behavior: HYBRID_TYPE on Android should match HYBRID_TYPE on iOS and Mobile Web. SATELLITE_TYPE should come as close as it can--which in this case is matching HYBRID_TYPE.    If we want to turn on traffic or street view, IMO that should be a separate switch.    Test Code:      Label displays the current map type. Click the label to change map types.    Expected behavior:     Hybrid view should show satellite image with roads and names overlaid.    Actual behavior:    Hybrid view shows road map, not satellite image.    From the original bug:  In Android:  - Titanium.Map.SATELLITE_TYPE -> hybrid map  - Titanium.Map.HYBRID_TYPE -> nothing happens.    To test open KS:  Base UI -> Views -> Map View -> Menu Button -> Hyb and Sat    Tested in Android Emulator APIs 2.2  and Droid Device running 2.2.2    Helpdesk Ticket: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/KTM-16476-116/homepage""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - Map View HYBRID_TYPE does not include satellite imagery
Description: """"This is a <USER>of Pedro's original bug, which got turned into a doc bug. We are fixing the doc for 2.1, but this is an actual code bug which should be addressed in the future. According to the doc, Ti.Map.HYBRID_TYPE is defined as a map with satellite imagery with roads and road names, and Ti.Map.SATELLITE_TYPE is defined as a map with satellite imagery with _no_ roads or names. On Android, specifying SATELLITE_TYPE brings up the map with satellite imagery and road names, i.e., a hybrid map. Google's Android Map APIs don't support a pure satellite map, so this is probably as good as we can do. However, on Android, HYBRID_TYPE for a map actually brings up a road map with _no_ satellite imagery. Here's why: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/map/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/map/TiMapView.java#L750 Expected behavior: HYBRID_TYPE on Android should match HYBRID_TYPE on iOS and Mobile Web. SATELLITE_TYPE should come as close as it can--which in this case is matching HYBRID_TYPE. If we want to turn on traffic or street view, IMO that should be a separate switch. Test Code: Label displays the current map type. Click the label to change map types. Expected behavior: Hybrid view should show satellite image with roads and names overlaid. Actual behavior: Hybrid view shows road map, not satellite image. From the original bug: In Android: - Titanium.Map.SATELLITE_TYPE -> hybrid map - Titanium.Map.HYBRID_TYPE -> nothing happens. To test open KS: Base UI -> Views -> Map View -> Menu Button -> Hyb and Sat Tested in Android Emulator APIs 2.2 and Droid Device running 2.2.2 Helpdesk Ticket: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/KTM-16476-116/homepage""""",title+description
TIMOB-9672,12,"""Android: app crashes when Slider object it's inside a tableViewRow and has the 'value' property""","""""""h2. Problem description  Application crashes when a Slider object is created specifying the 'value' property and it's placed inside a tableViewRow    h2. Steps to reproduce  Run the sample code:          h2. Further notes:  Comment out the 'value' property and then set it manually (for example, clicking a button).  In this case, the value it's correctly stored and displayed.  Adding the slider directly to the Window works. Crash only occurs when slider it's added in a tableViewRow.    Attached the crash log file too.    Escalated as per customer request.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: app crashes when Slider object it's inside a tableViewRow and has the 'value' property
Description: """"h2. Problem description Application crashes when a Slider object is created specifying the 'value' property and it's placed inside a tableViewRow h2. Steps to reproduce Run the sample code: h2. Further notes: Comment out the 'value' property and then set it manually (for example, clicking a button). In this case, the value it's correctly stored and displayed. Adding the slider directly to the Window works. Crash only occurs when slider it's added in a tableViewRow. Attached the crash log file too. Escalated as per customer request.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9671,12,"""MobileWeb: Controls-->Label-->Basic:Testing is blocked as we cant scroll down the page to unhide the 'change label 2' & 'label 1 background' buttons.""","""""""Testing is blocked as we cant scroll down the page to unhide the 'change label 2' & 'label 1 background' buttons.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for Windows Phone mango).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on controls tab.  6.Tap on the label table row.  7.Tap on the basic table row.  8.Notice that we can only see the 'Hide/show' button while the 'change label 2' & 'label 1 background'buttons are not visible because we cant scroll the page down to unhide them.     Actual result:  1.The 'change label 2' & '1 background' buttons are missing on the page.  2.Label 2 should be changed 1    Expected result: label  3.Tapping on """"""""Change Label 2"""""""" should change the label 2.  2.Press """"""""Change Label 2"""""""" .  4.Press """"""""Label 1 background"""""""".  3.Label 1 background should be changed.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Controls-->Label-->Basic:Testing is blocked as we cant scroll down the page to unhide the 'change label 2' & 'label 1 background' buttons.
Description: """"Testing is blocked as we cant scroll down the page to unhide the 'change label 2' & 'label 1 background' buttons. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for Windows Phone mango). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on controls tab. 6.Tap on the label table row. 7.Tap on the basic table row. 8.Notice that we can only see the 'Hide/show' button while the 'change label 2' & 'label 1 background'buttons are not visible because we cant scroll the page down to unhide them. Actual result: 1.The 'change label 2' & '1 background' buttons are missing on the page. 2.Label 2 should be changed 1 Expected result: label 3.Tapping on """"""""Change Label 2"""""""" should change the label 2. 2.Press """"""""Change Label 2"""""""" . 4.Press """"""""Label 1 background"""""""". 3.Label 1 background should be changed.""""",title+description
