TIMOB-9663,12,"""iOS: Parity issue with 'NaN'""","""""""An issue has been identified during the investigation of MOD-682 having to do with how 'NaN' is converted to a string only on iOS. I have narrowed down the issue to the 'NaN' value being converted to lowercase 'nan' in certain situations. This causes an issue when the OAuth signature, for example, has been calculated based on a string value of 'NaN' but the value sent in the HTTP request is converted internally to a string value of 'nan' (ie. signature mismatch occurs). The serialization of the dictionary argument that is passed to the HTTPClient.send method is where the value is getting converted to 'nan' instead of 'NaN'.    This works correctly on Android and MobileWeb, but not on iOS.    I have reproduced this in the following sample application:        The following output is generated on each of the platforms:    || iOS || Android || MobileWeb ||  | A1: NaN | A1: NaN | A1: NaN |  | B1: NaN | B1: NaN | B1: NaN |  | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN |  | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN |  | A2: NaN | A2: NaN | A2: NaN |  | B2: NaN | B2: NaN | B2: NaN |  | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN |  | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN |    Notice that the value of 'nan' is generated when the value is being converted directly to a string and not being concatenated to another string.      Some additional information regarding this issue on iOS. Given the following Objective-C code:        When this is run from XCode, note the following values (in order of being set):    1. value of classname is 'NSDecimalNumber'  2. value of test is 'NaN'  3. value of classname is '__NSCFNumber'  4. value of test is 'nan'  5. value of classname is '__NSCFNumber'  6. value of test is 'nan'    Not sure if that helps pinpoint the issue.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Parity issue with 'NaN'
Description: """"An issue has been identified during the investigation of MOD-682 having to do with how 'NaN' is converted to a string only on iOS. I have narrowed down the issue to the 'NaN' value being converted to lowercase 'nan' in certain situations. This causes an issue when the OAuth signature, for example, has been calculated based on a string value of 'NaN' but the value sent in the HTTP request is converted internally to a string value of 'nan' (ie. signature mismatch occurs). The serialization of the dictionary argument that is passed to the HTTPClient.send method is where the value is getting converted to 'nan' instead of 'NaN'. This works correctly on Android and MobileWeb, but not on iOS. I have reproduced this in the following sample application: The following output is generated on each of the platforms: || iOS || Android || MobileWeb || | A1: NaN | A1: NaN | A1: NaN | | B1: NaN | B1: NaN | B1: NaN | | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN | | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN | | A2: NaN | A2: NaN | A2: NaN | | B2: NaN | B2: NaN | B2: NaN | | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN | | {color:red}nan{color} | NaN | NaN | Notice that the value of 'nan' is generated when the value is being converted directly to a string and not being concatenated to another string. Some additional information regarding this issue on iOS. Given the following Objective-C code: When this is run from XCode, note the following values (in order of being set): 1. value of classname is 'NSDecimalNumber' 2. value of test is 'NaN' 3. value of classname is '__NSCFNumber' 4. value of test is 'nan' 5. value of classname is '__NSCFNumber' 6. value of test is 'nan' Not sure if that helps pinpoint the issue. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9662,12,"""Android: Nested CommonJS Modules Replace Existing CommonJS Modules""","""""""h1. Problem  When nesting CommonJS modules, module definitions can override existing CommonJS module definitions. This is a regression introduced sometime in the last month, though I do not have a specific point.    h2. Reproduction  Attached """"""""NestedConfusionReproduction.zip"""""""". Extract it to the Resources directory of an app, and run it on any Android environment. (Note that in this reduced reproduction, moving some of the requires around can avoid this bug. But in larger projects, or more complicated require scenarios, it cannot be so easily avoided.)    h2. What's Happening Wrong in Reproduction  The app does the following:    - app.js require's a specific view (ti.cloud.ui/buttons/chooseAPhoto).  - The specific view requires a generic view (ti.cloud.ui/buttons/generic).  - Both views require a single utility module (ti.cloud.ui/utils) and store it in a variable U.    When the generic view's createView method is called, it alerts the U variable. It also alerts a fresh require of the utility module. The expected behavior is these two would output the same thing, right? But the alert shows that both are messed up: U contains buttons/generic and the fresh require contains buttons/chooseAPhoto. (Each has unique methods, so it is easy to tell which module has been passed to alert.)""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Nested CommonJS Modules Replace Existing CommonJS Modules
Description: """"h1. Problem When nesting CommonJS modules, module definitions can override existing CommonJS module definitions. This is a regression introduced sometime in the last month, though I do not have a specific point. h2. Reproduction Attached """"""""NestedConfusionReproduction.zip"""""""". Extract it to the Resources directory of an app, and run it on any Android environment. (Note that in this reduced reproduction, moving some of the requires around can avoid this bug. But in larger projects, or more complicated require scenarios, it cannot be so easily avoided.) h2. What's Happening Wrong in Reproduction The app does the following: - app.js require's a specific view (ti.cloud.ui/buttons/chooseAPhoto). - The specific view requires a generic view (ti.cloud.ui/buttons/generic). - Both views require a single utility module (ti.cloud.ui/utils) and store it in a variable U. When the generic view's createView method is called, it alerts the U variable. It also alerts a fresh require of the utility module. The expected behavior is these two would output the same thing, right? But the alert shows that both are messed up: U contains buttons/generic and the fresh require contains buttons/chooseAPhoto. (Each has unique methods, so it is easy to tell which module has been passed to alert.)""""",title+description
TIMOB-9661,12,"""Android: Fullscreen window redraws itself after device rotation""","""""""Description:  Fullscreen window redraws itself after device rotation from landscape to portrait mode, and pressing """"""""Close"""""""" button.    Not a regression, occurs in 2.0.2 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink-Nook in landscape  2. Go to Base UI - Window (Standalone)  3. Press """"""""Open (Fullscreen)"""""""" button  4. Rotate device to portrait mode    Actual result:  Fullscreen window redraws itself    Expected result:  Fullscreen window shouldn't redraw itself""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Fullscreen window redraws itself after device rotation
Description: """"Description: Fullscreen window redraws itself after device rotation from landscape to portrait mode, and pressing """"""""Close"""""""" button. Not a regression, occurs in 2.0.2 as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink-Nook in landscape 2. Go to Base UI - Window (Standalone) 3. Press """"""""Open (Fullscreen)"""""""" button 4. Rotate device to portrait mode Actual result: Fullscreen window redraws itself Expected result: Fullscreen window shouldn't redraw itself""""",title+description
TIMOB-9660,12,"""MobileWeb: KitchenSink:We are not able to scroll any pages(up<-->down;left<-->right) on windows phone (mango) which blocks testing in portrait as well as landscape orientation.""","""""""We are not able to scroll any pages(up<-->down;left<-->right) on windows phone (mango) in portrait as well as landscape orientation    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(IE for Windows Phone mango).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on any tab & try to scroll up,down,left & right.  6.You will see that we cant scroll in either direction in portrait as well as landscape orientation,which blocks test cases from being executed.    Actual result:  1.Unable to scroll any pages(up<-->down;left<-->right) on windows phone (mango) in portrait as well as landscape orientation.    Expected result:  1.We should be able to scroll in all possible directions on windows phone mango in portrait as well as landscape orientation.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: KitchenSink:We are not able to scroll any pages(up<-->down;left<-->right) on windows phone (mango) which blocks testing in portrait as well as landscape orientation.
Description: """"We are not able to scroll any pages(up<-->down;left<-->right) on windows phone (mango) in portrait as well as landscape orientation Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(IE for Windows Phone mango). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on any tab & try to scroll up,down,left & right. 6.You will see that we cant scroll in either direction in portrait as well as landscape orientation,which blocks test cases from being executed. Actual result: 1.Unable to scroll any pages(up<-->down;left<-->right) on windows phone (mango) in portrait as well as landscape orientation. Expected result: 1.We should be able to scroll in all possible directions on windows phone mango in portrait as well as landscape orientation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9659,12,"""MobileWeb:Launching kitchensink always lands us on the 'Controls' tab & not on the 'Base UI' tab even though base UI comes before controls.""","""""""Launching kitchensink always lands us on the 'Controls' tab & not on the 'Base UI' tab even though base UI comes before controls.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:    Iphone:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for Windows Phone mango).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Notice that the current tab highlighted is 'Controls' & not 'Base UI',even though baseUI comes before controls from left to right direction.    Actual result:  1.Launching kitchensink always lands us on the 'Controls' tab & not on the 'Base UI' tab even though base UI comes before controls.    Expected result:  1.Launching Kitchensink should land on 'Base UI' tab instead of 'Controls' tab.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb:Launching kitchensink always lands us on the 'Controls' tab & not on the 'Base UI' tab even though base UI comes before controls.
Description: """"Launching kitchensink always lands us on the 'Controls' tab & not on the 'Base UI' tab even though base UI comes before controls. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: Iphone: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for Windows Phone mango). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Notice that the current tab highlighted is 'Controls' & not 'Base UI',even though baseUI comes before controls from left to right direction. Actual result: 1.Launching kitchensink always lands us on the 'Controls' tab & not on the 'Base UI' tab even though base UI comes before controls. Expected result: 1.Launching Kitchensink should land on 'Base UI' tab instead of 'Controls' tab.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9657,12,"""iOS: TableView: Swipe event not fired when the view is of certain width""","""""""The swipe event on tableview does not fire when the width of the view which contains the tableview is a certain value i.e. 19% or 20%. Checked on few other random width values like 15%,18%, 21%, 25%, 30% on which the event gets fired.  The issue occurs only on iPAD and not on iPhone.    The issue occurs since 2.0.1.    Step to Reproduce:  1. Create an application with the code below and launch the application  2. Swipe on the left view (blue color) which is a tableview    Actual: The swipe event is not fired. After the device is rotated, the swipe event gets fired on the same tableview.    Expected: The swipe event should fire for all width of the tableview.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView: Swipe event not fired when the view is of certain width
Description: """"The swipe event on tableview does not fire when the width of the view which contains the tableview is a certain value i.e. 19% or 20%. Checked on few other random width values like 15%,18%, 21%, 25%, 30% on which the event gets fired. The issue occurs only on iPAD and not on iPhone. The issue occurs since 2.0.1. Step to Reproduce: 1. Create an application with the code below and launch the application 2. Swipe on the left view (blue color) which is a tableview Actual: The swipe event is not fired. After the device is rotated, the swipe event gets fired on the same tableview. Expected: The swipe event should fire for all width of the tableview. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9655,12,"""Android: Twitter: Title and timestamp for a twitter post shown truncated in the tableview""","""""""The title and timestamp for one of the twitter posts, shown in the tableview, are getting truncated in Kitchen Sink.    Not a Regression. This also occurs on 2.0.2    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Open Kitchen Sink Application  2. Go to MashUp -> Twitter  3. Check the twitter posts    Actual: One of the twitter posts have truncated title and timestamp. (Refer to attached screenshot)    Expected: All the rows in the tableview should be of consistent height and show data completely""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Twitter: Title and timestamp for a twitter post shown truncated in the tableview
Description: """"The title and timestamp for one of the twitter posts, shown in the tableview, are getting truncated in Kitchen Sink. Not a Regression. This also occurs on 2.0.2 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Open Kitchen Sink Application 2. Go to MashUp -> Twitter 3. Check the twitter posts Actual: One of the twitter posts have truncated title and timestamp. (Refer to attached screenshot) Expected: All the rows in the tableview should be of consistent height and show data completely""""",title+description
TIMOB-9654,12,"""Android: Slider: Setting slider max value greater than 1 shows slider at zero irrespective of value set - on Android Honeycomb and ICS""","""""""Creating a slider control with max value greater than one, shows the slider at value zero by default, irrespective of the value set for the slider.    Not a regression. The issue also occurs on 2.0.2    The issue occurs on Android version 3.2 and 4.0.2 but does not occur on Android 2.2 and 2.3 (which behave like iOS).    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create an application with code below  2. Launch the application    Actual: The slider is shown at value zero.    Expected: The slider should be shown at position respective to value and min and max defined.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Slider: Setting slider max value greater than 1 shows slider at zero irrespective of value set - on Android Honeycomb and ICS
Description: """"Creating a slider control with max value greater than one, shows the slider at value zero by default, irrespective of the value set for the slider. Not a regression. The issue also occurs on 2.0.2 The issue occurs on Android version 3.2 and 4.0.2 but does not occur on Android 2.2 and 2.3 (which behave like iOS). Steps to reproduce: 1. Create an application with code below 2. Launch the application Actual: The slider is shown at value zero. Expected: The slider should be shown at position respective to value and min and max defined. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9653,12,"""Android: VideoPlayer: The video control not positioned correctly after orientation change""","""""""The video control not properly positioned after changing orientation from Landscape to Portrait.    Not a regression. This issue occurs as far as 1.8.2    The issue does not seem to occur on Android ICS. Tested with Galaxy Nexus (V4.0.2) on which the issue does not occur.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create an application with code below.  2. Launch the application with device in landscape mode  3. While video is playing, tap on the video to see the video control.  4. While the video control is shown, rotate the device to Portrait orientation    Actual: The video control is shown positioned in the middle of the screen and is truncated from the right. (Refer to attached screenshot)    Expected: The video control should be shown at the bottom of the video    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: VideoPlayer: The video control not positioned correctly after orientation change
Description: """"The video control not properly positioned after changing orientation from Landscape to Portrait. Not a regression. This issue occurs as far as 1.8.2 The issue does not seem to occur on Android ICS. Tested with Galaxy Nexus (V4.0.2) on which the issue does not occur. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create an application with code below. 2. Launch the application with device in landscape mode 3. While video is playing, tap on the video to see the video control. 4. While the video control is shown, rotate the device to Portrait orientation Actual: The video control is shown positioned in the middle of the screen and is truncated from the right. (Refer to attached screenshot) Expected: The video control should be shown at the bottom of the video """"",title+description
TIMOB-9652,12,"""MobileWeb: scrollView - does not scroll correctly when contentHeight is changed""","""""""ScrollView does not scroll when contentHeight is changed    h4. Steps to repro:  0. Run the code below  1. Click the button  2. Scroll the view (you can't scroll to the bottom)    {code:title}  var win  = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'white'  });  win.open();      var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({   contentWidth:'auto',   contentHeight:'auto',   top:0,   showVerticalScrollIndicator:true,   showHorizontalScrollIndicator:true  });      var view = Ti.UI.createView({   backgroundColor:'#336699',   borderRadius:10,   width:300,   height:400,   top:10  });    scrollView.add(view);    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: 'Click me'  });  button.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function(){   view.height = (view.height === 2000) ? 400 : 2000;  });  view.add(button);    win.add(scrollView);  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: scrollView - does not scroll correctly when contentHeight is changed
Description: """"ScrollView does not scroll when contentHeight is changed h4. Steps to repro: 0. Run the code below 1. Click the button 2. Scroll the view (you can't scroll to the bottom) {code:title} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white' }); win.open(); var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({ contentWidth:'auto', contentHeight:'auto', top:0, showVerticalScrollIndicator:true, showHorizontalScrollIndicator:true }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'#336699', borderRadius:10, width:300, height:400, top:10 }); scrollView.add(view); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Click me' }); button.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function(){ view.height = (view.height === 2000) ? 400 : 2000; }); view.add(button); win.add(scrollView); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-9651,12,"""MobileWeb: Kitchensink is not working on blackberry 7.X & blackberry Playbook,we just see the appcelerator splash screen.""","""""""Kitchensink is not working on blackberry 7.1.0.163,we just see the <USER>splash screen.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.  3.Hit go or enter.  4.You will see that you just get the <USER>splash & nothing goes ahead.  5.We do not get the kitchensink app.    Actual result:  1.We just get the <USER>splash & nothing goes ahead.    Expected result:  1.We should see the kitchensink fireup with all the tabs & table rows.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Kitchensink is not working on blackberry 7.X & blackberry Playbook,we just see the appcelerator splash screen.
Description: """"Kitchensink is not working on blackberry 7.1.0.163,we just see the <USER>splash screen. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser. 3.Hit go or enter. 4.You will see that you just get the <USER>splash & nothing goes ahead. 5.We do not get the kitchensink app. Actual result: 1.We just get the <USER>splash & nothing goes ahead. Expected result: 1.We should see the kitchensink fireup with all the tabs & table rows.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9650,12,"""iOS: Modal window does not change orientation""","""""""Description:  During KS testing I noticed, that if """"""""Partial Curl"""""""" chosen, Modal Window does not change orientation from landscape to portrait mode. There is also no rotation to the portrait mode after """"""""Close"""""""" button pressed and """"""""Main"""""""" Window appears.    Not a regression, occurs in 2.0.2 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink in landscape mode  2. Go to Base UI - Modal Windows  3. Scroll down to """"""""Partial Curl"""""""" in first column  4. Press """"""""Show modal""""""""  5. Rotate device to portrait  6. Press """"""""Close"""""""" button    Expected result:  Modal and """"""""Main"""""""" windows should change orientation    Actual result:  Modal and """"""""Main"""""""" windows don't change orientation  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Modal window does not change orientation
Description: """"Description: During KS testing I noticed, that if """"""""Partial Curl"""""""" chosen, Modal Window does not change orientation from landscape to portrait mode. There is also no rotation to the portrait mode after """"""""Close"""""""" button pressed and """"""""Main"""""""" Window appears. Not a regression, occurs in 2.0.2 as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink in landscape mode 2. Go to Base UI - Modal Windows 3. Scroll down to """"""""Partial Curl"""""""" in first column 4. Press """"""""Show modal"""""""" 5. Rotate device to portrait 6. Press """"""""Close"""""""" button Expected result: Modal and """"""""Main"""""""" windows should change orientation Actual result: Modal and """"""""Main"""""""" windows don't change orientation """"",title+description
