TIMOB-9621,12,"""MobileWeb:Platform-->JS Includes:Tapping on JS Includes gives an expected alert but is missing the last name:Smith in portrait & middle & last name:Smith in landscape.""","""""""MobileWeb:Platform-->JS Includes:Tapping on JS Includes gives an expected alert but is missing the last name:Smith in portrait & middle & last name:Smith in landscape.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:    Iphone 4.3.5:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the JS Includes table row.  7.You will get an alert 'JS includes first name,middle name but is missing the last name in device portrait mode.  8.Now rotate the device into landscape orientation,you will see that we are not able to see the middle name & the last name.    Windows Mobile mango:  1.Can't scroll the page down to unhide JS Includes.Thus cant proceed forward with the test case.    Actual result:  Tapping on JS Includes gives an expected alert but is missing the last name:Smith in portrait & middle & last name:Smith in landscape.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on JS Includes gives an alert """"""""JS Includes.   First name: Joey   Middle name: Waldo   Last name: Smith""""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb:Platform-->JS Includes:Tapping on JS Includes gives an expected alert but is missing the last name:Smith in portrait & middle & last name:Smith in landscape.
Description: """"MobileWeb:Platform-->JS Includes:Tapping on JS Includes gives an expected alert but is missing the last name:Smith in portrait & middle & last name:Smith in landscape. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: Iphone 4.3.5: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the JS Includes table row. 7.You will get an alert 'JS includes first name,middle name but is missing the last name in device portrait mode. 8.Now rotate the device into landscape orientation,you will see that we are not able to see the middle name & the last name. Windows Mobile mango: 1.Can't scroll the page down to unhide JS Includes.Thus cant proceed forward with the test case. Actual result: Tapping on JS Includes gives an expected alert but is missing the last name:Smith in portrait & middle & last name:Smith in landscape. Expected result: 1.Tapping on JS Includes gives an alert """"""""JS Includes. First name: Joey Middle name: Waldo Last name: Smith""""""""""""",title+description
TIMOB-9620,12,"""iOS: Sound - Recorded sounds are not reproducible""","""""""Description:  During KS testing I noticed, that recorded sounds cannot be reproduced by pressing """"""""Playback Recording"""""""" button.    Regression, does not occur in 2.0.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Phone - Sound - Record  3. Press """"""""Start recording"""""""" button and start recording sounds   4. Press """"""""Stop Recording""""""""  5. Press """"""""Playback Recording""""""""    Expected result:  Should hear recorded sounds    Actual result:  Cannot hear recorded sounds""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Sound - Recorded sounds are not reproducible
Description: """"Description: During KS testing I noticed, that recorded sounds cannot be reproduced by pressing """"""""Playback Recording"""""""" button. Regression, does not occur in 2.0.2. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Phone - Sound - Record 3. Press """"""""Start recording"""""""" button and start recording sounds 4. Press """"""""Stop Recording"""""""" 5. Press """"""""Playback Recording"""""""" Expected result: Should hear recorded sounds Actual result: Cannot hear recorded sounds""""",title+description
TIMOB-9619,12,"""MobileWeb:Platform-->Proporties API:Tapping on 'proporties API' gives a message 'see log output' but we are unable to see any log in the xcode console.""","""""""Tapping on 'proporties API' gives a message 'see log output' but we are unable to see any log in the xcode console.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the application API table row.    Actual result:  1.Tapping on 'proporties API' gives a message 'see log output' but we are unable to see any log in the xcode console.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on 'proporties API' will give a message 'see log output' & in the console should see property data and the following message should appear:   [INFO] String should be null - value = Test Success (null==null)   [INFO] Int should be null - value = Test Success (null==null)   [INFO] AppSetting Name = null   [INFO] AppSetting Enabled = null   [INFO] AppSetting Slider = null""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb:Platform-->Proporties API:Tapping on 'proporties API' gives a message 'see log output' but we are unable to see any log in the xcode console.
Description: """"Tapping on 'proporties API' gives a message 'see log output' but we are unable to see any log in the xcode console. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the application API table row. Actual result: 1.Tapping on 'proporties API' gives a message 'see log output' but we are unable to see any log in the xcode console. Expected result: 1.Tapping on 'proporties API' will give a message 'see log output' & in the console should see property data and the following message should appear: [INFO] String should be null - value = Test Success (null==null) [INFO] Int should be null - value = Test Success (null==null) [INFO] AppSetting Name = null [INFO] AppSetting Enabled = null [INFO] AppSetting Slider = null""""",title+description
TIMOB-9618,12,"""MobileWeb:Platform-->Application Data:Tapping on 'Application Data' does not give us any application data on the page.""","""""""Tapping on 'Application Data' does not give us any application data on the page.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the application data table row.    Actual result:  1.Tapping on 'Application Data' does not give us any application data on the page.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on application data should give us application data including: ID, Name, Version, Publisher, URL, Description, Copyright, GUID, Path and Build.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb:Platform-->Application Data:Tapping on 'Application Data' does not give us any application data on the page.
Description: """"Tapping on 'Application Data' does not give us any application data on the page. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the application data table row. Actual result: 1.Tapping on 'Application Data' does not give us any application data on the page. Expected result: 1.Tapping on application data should give us application data including: ID, Name, Version, Publisher, URL, Description, Copyright, GUID, Path and Build.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9617,12,"""MobileWeb:Platform-->Logging:Not seeing any log in the xcode console after tapping on the 'logging' table row.""","""""""Not seeing any log in the xcode console after tapping on the 'logging' table row.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the logging table row.  7.You will get an alert 'ALERT LOG FROM FUNCTION - name: foo, value: bar'.  8.After tapping on the 'ok' button we get a message 'check log for output.  9.now check the xcode console for the log output.  10.You will see that we do not get any expected log.     Actual result:  1.Tapping on the 'logging' table row gives an alert 'ALERT LOG FROM FUNCTION - name: foo, value: bar'.  2.Tapping on 'ok' gives us a message 'check log for output'.  3.We do not get any expected log in the xcode console.    Expected result:  1.Tap on 'logging' table view.you will get an alert 'ALERT LOG FROM FUNCTION - name: foo, value: bar'.  2.Checking the xcode console you should get log like this:  [ERROR] ERROR MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [DEBUG] DEBUG MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [ERROR] ERROR MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [WARN] WARN MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [INFO] INFO MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [TRACE] TRACE MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [INFO] NOTICE MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [ERROR] CRITICAL MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar   [INFO] 1   [INFO] 2   [INFO] 3   [INFO] 4   [INFO] 5   [INFO] 6   [INFO] 7   [INFO] 8   [INFO] 9   [INFO] 10   [INFO] 11   [INFO] 12   [INFO] 13   [INFO] 14   [INFO] 15""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb:Platform-->Logging:Not seeing any log in the xcode console after tapping on the 'logging' table row.
Description: """"Not seeing any log in the xcode console after tapping on the 'logging' table row. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the logging table row. 7.You will get an alert 'ALERT LOG FROM FUNCTION - name: foo, value: bar'. 8.After tapping on the 'ok' button we get a message 'check log for output. 9.now check the xcode console for the log output. 10.You will see that we do not get any expected log. Actual result: 1.Tapping on the 'logging' table row gives an alert 'ALERT LOG FROM FUNCTION - name: foo, value: bar'. 2.Tapping on 'ok' gives us a message 'check log for output'. 3.We do not get any expected log in the xcode console. Expected result: 1.Tap on 'logging' table view.you will get an alert 'ALERT LOG FROM FUNCTION - name: foo, value: bar'. 2.Checking the xcode console you should get log like this: [ERROR] ERROR MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [DEBUG] DEBUG MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [ERROR] ERROR MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [WARN] WARN MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [INFO] INFO MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [TRACE] TRACE MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [INFO] NOTICE MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [ERROR] CRITICAL MESSAGE FROM FUNCTION - name: foo value: bar [INFO] 1 [INFO] 2 [INFO] 3 [INFO] 4 [INFO] 5 [INFO] 6 [INFO] 7 [INFO] 8 [INFO] 9 [INFO] 10 [INFO] 11 [INFO] 12 [INFO] 13 [INFO] 14 [INFO] 15""""",title+description
TIMOB-9616,12,"""Android: on ICS 4, 'backgroundSelectedImage:image' does not disappear after clicking on a tableViewRow ""","""""""h2. Problem description  Background Selected Image it's being displayed when clicking on a tableViewRow, but then it does not disappear    h2. Steps to reproduce  Run the sample code (choose an image as backgroundSelectedImage).  Click on the tableViewRow.  Result: backgroundImage is shown but does not disappear after releasing the click.    Only reproducible on Android ICS OS 4.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: on ICS 4, 'backgroundSelectedImage:image' does not disappear after clicking on a tableViewRow
Description: """"h2. Problem description Background Selected Image it's being displayed when clicking on a tableViewRow, but then it does not disappear h2. Steps to reproduce Run the sample code (choose an image as backgroundSelectedImage). Click on the tableViewRow. Result: backgroundImage is shown but does not disappear after releasing the click. Only reproducible on Android ICS OS 4. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9615,12,"""MobileWeb:Platform-->XHR-->set timeout:Missing the 'toggle timeout' button & we do not get any progress indicator & messages like 'sending w/data' or 'sending w/o data'.""","""""""Missing the 'toggle timeout' button & we do not get any progress indicator & messages like 'sending w/data' or 'sending w/o data'.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:    IPhone 4.3.5:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the XHR table row.  7.Tap on the set timeout table row.  8.You will get a page with a 'toggle send' button on it & a text 'testing timeout with send data & without'.  9.Tapping on 'toggle send' gives us 'registered error:time passed = xxxx seconds.Where 'xxxx' can be any no.    Windows Phone Mango:  1.We are not seeing the table row 'set timeout' as we are not able to scroll down the XHR page.Thus cant move ahead with the test.    Actual result:  1.You will get a page only with a 'toggle send' button on it & a text 'testing timeout with send data & without' & missing the 'toggle timeout' button.  2.We are not seeing any progress bar & any messages like 'sending w/data' or 'sending w/o data'.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on 'toggle timeout' should give us progress indicator and message """"""""sending with data"""""""". After approximately 30-50 sec should get a message """"""""Registered error: time passed=...""""""""  2.Tapping on 'toggle send' should give us progress indicator and message """"""""sending without data"""""""". After approximately 30-50 sec should get a message """"""""Registered error: time passed=...""""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb:Platform-->XHR-->set timeout:Missing the 'toggle timeout' button & we do not get any progress indicator & messages like 'sending w/data' or 'sending w/o data'.
Description: """"Missing the 'toggle timeout' button & we do not get any progress indicator & messages like 'sending w/data' or 'sending w/o data'. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: IPhone 4.3.5: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the XHR table row. 7.Tap on the set timeout table row. 8.You will get a page with a 'toggle send' button on it & a text 'testing timeout with send data & without'. 9.Tapping on 'toggle send' gives us 'registered error:time passed = xxxx seconds.Where 'xxxx' can be any no. Windows Phone Mango: 1.We are not seeing the table row 'set timeout' as we are not able to scroll down the XHR page.Thus cant move ahead with the test. Actual result: 1.You will get a page only with a 'toggle send' button on it & a text 'testing timeout with send data & without' & missing the 'toggle timeout' button. 2.We are not seeing any progress bar & any messages like 'sending w/data' or 'sending w/o data'. Expected result: 1.Tapping on 'toggle timeout' should give us progress indicator and message """"""""sending with data"""""""". After approximately 30-50 sec should get a message """"""""Registered error: time passed=..."""""""" 2.Tapping on 'toggle send' should give us progress indicator and message """"""""sending without data"""""""". After approximately 30-50 sec should get a message """"""""Registered error: time passed=...""""""""""""",title+description
TIMOB-9614,12,"""iOS: Buttons """"One"""" and """"Two"""" change size after device rotation""","""""""Description:  Buttons """"""""One"""""""" and """"""""Two"""""""" on the Navbar change size after device rotation.    Not a regression, occurs in 2.0.2 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Controls - Tabbed Bar  3. Rotate device from portrait to landscape  4. Rotate device back    Expected result:  Buttons shouldn't change size    Actual result:  Buttons change size (see attachments)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Buttons """"One"""" and """"Two"""" change size after device rotation
Description: """"Description: Buttons """"""""One"""""""" and """"""""Two"""""""" on the Navbar change size after device rotation. Not a regression, occurs in 2.0.2 as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Controls - Tabbed Bar 3. Rotate device from portrait to landscape 4. Rotate device back Expected result: Buttons shouldn't change size Actual result: Buttons change size (see attachments)""""",title+description
TIMOB-9613,12,"""MobileWeb: Platform-->XHR-->Cookies:Tapping on 'Test Login Cookie' after entering valid google credentials gives us application error page & not cookie code on windows phone (mango).""","""""""Tapping on 'Test Login Cookie' after entering valid google credentials gives us application error page & not cookie code on windows phone (mango).    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the XHR table row.  7.Tap on the cookies table row.  8.Enter valid google credentials in the text boxes.  9.Tap on 'test login cookie'.  10.You will notice we get an application error page & not any cookie code.    Actual result:  1.We are getting an application error page & no cookie code.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on the cookies table row should give us a page which should have text boxes to input a valid google username & password.  2.Enter the credentials & tap on test login cookie button.  3.You should get a success message & a cookie code on the screen.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Platform-->XHR-->Cookies:Tapping on 'Test Login Cookie' after entering valid google credentials gives us application error page & not cookie code on windows phone (mango).
Description: """"Tapping on 'Test Login Cookie' after entering valid google credentials gives us application error page & not cookie code on windows phone (mango). Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the XHR table row. 7.Tap on the cookies table row. 8.Enter valid google credentials in the text boxes. 9.Tap on 'test login cookie'. 10.You will notice we get an application error page & not any cookie code. Actual result: 1.We are getting an application error page & no cookie code. Expected result: 1.Tapping on the cookies table row should give us a page which should have text boxes to input a valid google username & password. 2.Enter the credentials & tap on test login cookie button. 3.You should get a success message & a cookie code on the screen.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9612,12,"""MobileWeb: Platform-->XHR-->Cookies:Tapping on cookies table row does not do open up any page on iPhone 4.3.5.""","""""""Tapping on cookies table row does not do open up any page on iPhone 4.3.5.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the XHR table row.  7.Tap on the cookies table row.  8.Notice that we do not get any child page or screen after tapping on cookies.    Actual result:  1.We do not get any screen or child page after on tapping the cookies table row.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on the cookies table row should give us a page which should have text boxes to input a valid google username & password.  2.Enter the credentials & tap on test login cookie button.  3.You should get a success message & a cookie code on the screen.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Platform-->XHR-->Cookies:Tapping on cookies table row does not do open up any page on iPhone 4.3.5.
Description: """"Tapping on cookies table row does not do open up any page on iPhone 4.3.5. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the XHR table row. 7.Tap on the cookies table row. 8.Notice that we do not get any child page or screen after tapping on cookies. Actual result: 1.We do not get any screen or child page after on tapping the cookies table row. Expected result: 1.Tapping on the cookies table row should give us a page which should have text boxes to input a valid google username & password. 2.Enter the credentials & tap on test login cookie button. 3.You should get a success message & a cookie code on the screen.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9611,12,"""MobileWeb: Platform-->XHR-->File download:Tapping on the 'file download' does not open up any child page.""","""""""Tapping on the 'File download' table row does not open up any child page.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on platform tab.  6.Tap on the XHR table row.  7.Tap on the file download table row.  8.Notice that we do not get any child page after tapping on file download ta.    Actual result:  1.We do not get any screen or page after tapping on file download table row.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on the file download table row gives us a page with """"""""Large File Download"""""""",""""""""Set Web View (url)"""""""",""""""""Abort"""""""",""""""""Set Web View (url)"""""""",""""""""Set Web View (data) options on it.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Platform-->XHR-->File download:Tapping on the 'file download' does not open up any child page.
Description: """"Tapping on the 'File download' table row does not open up any child page. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on platform tab. 6.Tap on the XHR table row. 7.Tap on the file download table row. 8.Notice that we do not get any child page after tapping on file download ta. Actual result: 1.We do not get any screen or page after tapping on file download table row. Expected result: 1.Tapping on the file download table row gives us a page with """"""""Large File Download"""""""",""""""""Set Web View (url)"""""""",""""""""Abort"""""""",""""""""Set Web View (url)"""""""",""""""""Set Web View (data) options on it.""""",title+description
