TIMOB-9602,12,"""iOS: Tabbed Bar: Index of title tabbed bar not setting to 0 on reset""","""""""This is not a regression. It exists at least as far as 1.8.2.  Steps to reproduce:  1.Navigate to KitchenSink:Controls:Tabbed bar  1. Press each button   2. Press """"""""Set Tab 0 Active""""""""   3. Click on image in the middle of Toggle Style  Expected results:  1. Should get a visual feedback that the button is clicked. Each button should have appropriate index.   2. All indexes should be nulled   3. Style should be changed  Actual results:  1. Should get a visual feedback that the button is clicked. Each button should have appropriate index.   2. All indexes get nulled,but the title tabbed bar do not sets index to null.   3. Style should be changed    The title tabbed bar should also be set to null.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tabbed Bar: Index of title tabbed bar not setting to 0 on reset
Description: """"This is not a regression. It exists at least as far as 1.8.2. Steps to reproduce: 1.Navigate to KitchenSink:Controls:Tabbed bar 1. Press each button 2. Press """"""""Set Tab 0 Active"""""""" 3. Click on image in the middle of Toggle Style Expected results: 1. Should get a visual feedback that the button is clicked. Each button should have appropriate index. 2. All indexes should be nulled 3. Style should be changed Actual results: 1. Should get a visual feedback that the button is clicked. Each button should have appropriate index. 2. All indexes get nulled,but the title tabbed bar do not sets index to null. 3. Style should be changed The title tabbed bar should also be set to null.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9601,12,"""iOS: System Buttons - Tap on spinner button does not display the alert message.""","""""""Tap on spinner button does not display the alert message.  This is not regression. This issue occurs in 2.0.X as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Go to Kitchensink >Controls >System Buttons.  2. Click on 'Set button Group 5'.  3. Click on the spinner in the toolbar.    Actual:  It does not display the alert message.    Expected:  It should display the alert message with its appropriate name.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: System Buttons - Tap on spinner button does not display the alert message.
Description: """"Tap on spinner button does not display the alert message. This is not regression. This issue occurs in 2.0.X as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Go to Kitchensink >Controls >System Buttons. 2. Click on 'Set button Group 5'. 3. Click on the spinner in the toolbar. Actual: It does not display the alert message. Expected: It should display the alert message with its appropriate name.""""",title+description
