TIMOB-9591,12,"""Android: Webview: Having an event listener for click event of webview or any of its parent view does not allow web interaction with web view components ""","""""""If the application has the addeventlistener method for the click event for the webview or its parent view, then the web components (like links, web buttons etc.) on the web view do not work.    Regression. This does not happen in 2.0.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create an application with code below  2. Launch the application  3. In the google web page that opens, click on any link    Actual: The link does not work. Instead it opens the options for text edit    Expected: The link should work normally    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Webview: Having an event listener for click event of webview or any of its parent view does not allow web interaction with web view components
Description: """"If the application has the addeventlistener method for the click event for the webview or its parent view, then the web components (like links, web buttons etc.) on the web view do not work. Regression. This does not happen in 2.0.2. Steps to reproduce: 1. Create an application with code below 2. Launch the application 3. In the google web page that opens, click on any link Actual: The link does not work. Instead it opens the options for text edit Expected: The link should work normally """"",title+description
TIMOB-9590,12,"""Android: Using HTTPClient to PUT an image on Android uploads 15 bytes of text""","""""""When I run the below code on Android, the image is not uploaded, rather a 15 byte text file with the following text:  [object TiBlob]    The code below runs fine on iOS, the image uploads successfully.  h4. Repo Steps  1. Run the given code sample in your app.js  2. Click upload image button.   3. It will then display the URL to the uploaded image.  4. For Android, you have to load the link in a browser and Save as.  5. Then change the extension to .txt to see its just a text file with the [object TiBlob] text.     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Using HTTPClient to PUT an image on Android uploads 15 bytes of text
Description: """"When I run the below code on Android, the image is not uploaded, rather a 15 byte text file with the following text: [object TiBlob] The code below runs fine on iOS, the image uploads successfully. h4. Repo Steps 1. Run the given code sample in your app.js 2. Click upload image button. 3. It will then display the URL to the uploaded image. 4. For Android, you have to load the link in a browser and Save as. 5. Then change the extension to .txt to see its just a text file with the [object TiBlob] text. """"",title+description
