TIMOB-9582,12,"""Mobile Web:Mashups-->YQL-->local search : List scroll for the sushi restaurants does not work after the first time we use it.""","""""""List scroll for the sushi restaurants does not work after the first time we use it.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on mashups tab.  6.Tap on the YQL table row.  7.Tap on the YQL local search.  8.You will see that you will get a list of sushi restaurants near <USER>  9.Now scroll the list.  10.Notice that you will be able to scroll the results for the first time,if you try to scroll the second time it does not scroll.    Actual result:  1.List scroll for the sushi restaurants does not work after the first time we use it.    Expected result:  1.Should be able to scroll the list of sushi restaurants smoothly even after the first time we scroll it.""""""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web:Mashups-->YQL-->local search : List scroll for the sushi restaurants does not work after the first time we use it.
Description: """"List scroll for the sushi restaurants does not work after the first time we use it. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on mashups tab. 6.Tap on the YQL table row. 7.Tap on the YQL local search. 8.You will see that you will get a list of sushi restaurants near <USER> 9.Now scroll the list. 10.Notice that you will be able to scroll the results for the first time,if you try to scroll the second time it does not scroll. Actual result: 1.List scroll for the sushi restaurants does not work after the first time we use it. Expected result: 1.Should be able to scroll the list of sushi restaurants smoothly even after the first time we scroll it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9581,12,"""Mobile Web : Mashups-->facebook-->photos : Just seeing a facebook login button which tapping on does nothing & missing 'upload photos from gallery with graph API' & 'upload photos from file with REST API' .""","""""""We are just seeing a facebook login button which tapping on does nothing & missing 'upload photos from gallery with graph API' & 'upload photos from file with REST API' .    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on mashups tab.  6.Tap on the facebook table row.  7.Tap on the photos table row.  8.You will just see a facebook login page & tapping on it does not do anything,just an animation.  9.We are missing 'upload photos from gallery with graph API' & 'upload photos from file with REST API'.    Actual result:  1.We are just seeing a facebook login button which tapping on does nothing & are missing upload photos from gallery with graph API & upload photos from file with REST API .    Expected result:  1.Tapping on facebook login button should give us the login page.  2.Tapping on upload photos from gallery with graph API we should be able to upload a photo from gallery window.  3.Tapping on upload photos from file with REST API we should see should see an Alert :Success & On facebook page look for photo posted.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web : Mashups-->facebook-->photos : Just seeing a facebook login button which tapping on does nothing & missing 'upload photos from gallery with graph API' & 'upload photos from file with REST API' .
Description: """"We are just seeing a facebook login button which tapping on does nothing & missing 'upload photos from gallery with graph API' & 'upload photos from file with REST API' . Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on mashups tab. 6.Tap on the facebook table row. 7.Tap on the photos table row. 8.You will just see a facebook login page & tapping on it does not do anything,just an animation. 9.We are missing 'upload photos from gallery with graph API' & 'upload photos from file with REST API'. Actual result: 1.We are just seeing a facebook login button which tapping on does nothing & are missing upload photos from gallery with graph API & upload photos from file with REST API . Expected result: 1.Tapping on facebook login button should give us the login page. 2.Tapping on upload photos from gallery with graph API we should be able to upload a photo from gallery window. 3.Tapping on upload photos from file with REST API we should see should see an Alert :Success & On facebook page look for photo posted. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9580,12,"""Android: Images captured using Ti.Media.showCamera() are written to SD card on Android""","""""""h3. Problem    Captured images are written to the Android device's SD card at /DCIM/Camera/<app name>. (even with saveToPhotoGallery option as false)    h5. From the customer:    This is a potential security issue for us because  we are capturing images of checks, which contain bank account numbers. We need a way to disable this behavior.    For our purposes it is not sufficient to delete the image after writing it to the file system. Forensics tools can still recover the data from the file system even if the file is deleted. The image can never be written to storage at all.    Here is a sample app.js that reproduces the problem:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Images captured using Ti.Media.showCamera() are written to SD card on Android
Description: """"h3. Problem Captured images are written to the Android device's SD card at /DCIM/Camera/<app name>. (even with saveToPhotoGallery option as false) h5. From the customer: This is a potential security issue for us because we are capturing images of checks, which contain bank account numbers. We need a way to disable this behavior. For our purposes it is not sufficient to delete the image after writing it to the file system. Forensics tools can still recover the data from the file system even if the file is deleted. The image can never be written to storage at all. Here is a sample app.js that reproduces the problem: """"",title+description
TIMOB-9579,12,"""Mobile Web: Mashups-->facebook-->proporties :The Facebook login & the display proporties buttons are overlapping each other.""","""""""The Facebook login button & the display proporties buttons are overlapping each other.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on mashups tab.  6.Tap on the facebook table row.  7.Tap on the proporties table row.  8.You will see that the facebook login button & the display proporties button are overlapping each other.    Actual result:  1.facebook login button & the display proporties button are overlapping each other.    Expected result:  1.facebook login button & the display proporties button should not be overlapping each other.""""""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web: Mashups-->facebook-->proporties :The Facebook login & the display proporties buttons are overlapping each other.
Description: """"The Facebook login button & the display proporties buttons are overlapping each other. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on mashups tab. 6.Tap on the facebook table row. 7.Tap on the proporties table row. 8.You will see that the facebook login button & the display proporties button are overlapping each other. Actual result: 1.facebook login button & the display proporties button are overlapping each other. Expected result: 1.facebook login button & the display proporties button should not be overlapping each other.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9578,12,"""MobileWeb: Mashups-->facebook-->publish stream : The buttons like 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api'& 'publish wall post with graph api' are missing from the publish stream page.""","""""""The buttons like 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api'& 'publish wall post with graph api' are missing from the publish stream page.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on mashups tab.  6.Tap on the facebook table row.  7.Tap on the publish stream table row.  8.Notice that you just see a facebook login button where as 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api' are missing.  9.Tapping on the facebook login button does nothing we just get a button press animation.    Actual result:  1.Buttons 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api','publish wall post with a dialog' are missing & tapping on the facebook login button does nothing.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on the login button should show us the facebook login page.  2.Tapping on publish stream with graph api should give us an Alert :success.Log into facebook account & look for <USER>logo posted which says <times> ago via Titanium <USER>  3.Tapping on publish stream with graph api should give us an Alert :Success. Look for wall post use Mozilla online javascript reference.  4.Tapping on publish wall post with a dialog should give us an Alert :Success.Look for the wall post you typed in..on the webpage.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Mashups-->facebook-->publish stream : The buttons like 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api'& 'publish wall post with graph api' are missing from the publish stream page.
Description: """"The buttons like 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api'& 'publish wall post with graph api' are missing from the publish stream page. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on mashups tab. 6.Tap on the facebook table row. 7.Tap on the publish stream table row. 8.Notice that you just see a facebook login button where as 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api' are missing. 9.Tapping on the facebook login button does nothing we just get a button press animation. Actual result: 1.Buttons 'publish status with graph api','publish wall post with graph api','publish wall post with a dialog' are missing & tapping on the facebook login button does nothing. Expected result: 1.Tapping on the login button should show us the facebook login page. 2.Tapping on publish stream with graph api should give us an Alert :success.Log into facebook account & look for <USER>logo posted which says <times> ago via Titanium <USER> 3.Tapping on publish stream with graph api should give us an Alert :Success. Look for wall post use Mozilla online javascript reference. 4.Tapping on publish wall post with a dialog should give us an Alert :Success.Look for the wall post you typed in..on the webpage.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9577,12,"""MobileWeb: Mashups-->facebook-->proporties : Tapping on login button does not give us the facebook login page & does not display any display proporties.""","""""""Tapping on login button does not give us the facebook login page & does not display any display proporties.    Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA    Steps to reproduce:  1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio.  2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone).   3.Hit go or enter.  4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser.  5.Tap on mashups tab.  6.Tap on the facebook table row.  7.Tap on the properties table row.  8.Tap on the facebook login button.  9.Notice that we do not get any login page,we just have a button press animation.Thus rest of the test case cant be executed.    Actual result:  1.Nothing happens on tapping the facebook login button.We just see a button press animation,thus we cant proceed with the test case further.    Expected result:  1.Tapping on the login button should show us the facebook login page.  2.Tapping on display proporties should display a window where various properties and the current values are displayed...   3.On console we should see:  [INFO] Query result from facebook: eg:[{""""""""email"""""""":0,""""""""offline_access"""""""":0,""""""""rsvp_event"""""""":0,""""""""user_photos"""""""":0,""""""""user_about_me"""""""":0,""""""""user_online_presence"""""""":0,""""""""user_work_history"""""""":0,""""""""xmpp_login"""""""":0,""""""""manage_pages"""""""":0,""""""""user_status"""""""":0,""""""""read_requests"""""""":0,""""""""user_groups"""""""":0,""""""""user_activities"""""""":0,""""""""read_insights"""""""":0,""""""""sms"""""""":0,""""""""user_events"""""""":0,""""""""read_friendlists"""""""":0,.....]  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Mashups-->facebook-->proporties : Tapping on login button does not give us the facebook login page & does not display any display proporties.
Description: """"Tapping on login button does not give us the facebook login page & does not display any display proporties. Not a Regression, occurs with 2.0.2GA Steps to reproduce: 1.Build kitchen sink for mobile web in titanium studio. 2.Type the ip address of your laptop into the mobile device's web browser.(safari for iphone & IE for windows phone). 3.Hit go or enter. 4.Kitchen sink will fire up in the browser. 5.Tap on mashups tab. 6.Tap on the facebook table row. 7.Tap on the properties table row. 8.Tap on the facebook login button. 9.Notice that we do not get any login page,we just have a button press animation.Thus rest of the test case cant be executed. Actual result: 1.Nothing happens on tapping the facebook login button.We just see a button press animation,thus we cant proceed with the test case further. Expected result: 1.Tapping on the login button should show us the facebook login page. 2.Tapping on display proporties should display a window where various properties and the current values are displayed... 3.On console we should see: [INFO] Query result from facebook: eg:[{""""""""email"""""""":0,""""""""offline_access"""""""":0,""""""""rsvp_event"""""""":0,""""""""user_photos"""""""":0,""""""""user_about_me"""""""":0,""""""""user_online_presence"""""""":0,""""""""user_work_history"""""""":0,""""""""xmpp_login"""""""":0,""""""""manage_pages"""""""":0,""""""""user_status"""""""":0,""""""""read_requests"""""""":0,""""""""user_groups"""""""":0,""""""""user_activities"""""""":0,""""""""read_insights"""""""":0,""""""""sms"""""""":0,""""""""user_events"""""""":0,""""""""read_friendlists"""""""":0,.....] """"",title+description
