TIMOB-9529,12,"""MobileWeb: Add buttons to scrollableview""","""""""Scrolling scrollable views doesn't work on WP7.5 because it doesn't support the events necessary to do dragging and it doesn't support animation. In this case, we should add buttons to the scrollable view that a user can tap to go forwards and backwards.    We should consider making a new top-level API for managing these buttons.""""""",Story,"Title: MobileWeb: Add buttons to scrollableview
Description: """"Scrolling scrollable views doesn't work on WP7.5 because it doesn't support the events necessary to do dragging and it doesn't support animation. In this case, we should add buttons to the scrollable view that a user can tap to go forwards and backwards. We should consider making a new top-level API for managing these buttons.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9528,12,"""Android: Saved Camera images are not getting stored on sdcard but the internal storage""","""""""h3. Problem    Cannot Save the images taken by camera on the external directory by this method: Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.externalStorageDirectory, 'PlayGroundPhotos');    The sample code is here:          The above code saves the image in internal phone storage even when sdcard is present on the phone.     Tested with HTC Sensation 4G, Motorola Atrix (2.3.3 Android OS)    *NOTE: Running the above code in 1.8.2 SDK saves it in the correct location (external storage)*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Saved Camera images are not getting stored on sdcard but the internal storage
Description: """"h3. Problem Cannot Save the images taken by camera on the external directory by this method: Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.externalStorageDirectory, 'PlayGroundPhotos'); The sample code is here: The above code saves the image in internal phone storage even when sdcard is present on the phone. Tested with HTC Sensation 4G, Motorola Atrix (2.3.3 Android OS) *NOTE: Running the above code in 1.8.2 SDK saves it in the correct location (external storage)* """"",title+description
TIMOB-9527,12,"""iOS: Views - Activity indicator keeps spinning""","""""""Description:  During KS testing I noticed, that after launching """"""""Local URL"""""""" activity indicator keeps spinning. """"""""Hide indicator"""""""" app event not being fired. It does not happen if running test case first time after app was installed.         Regression, does not occur in 2.0.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Base UI - Views - Web Views - Local URL  3. Press """"""""back"""""""" button  4. Launch Local URL one more time    Expected result:  Activity indicator should appear and then disappear.    Actual result:  Activity indicator keeps spinning.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Views - Activity indicator keeps spinning
Description: """"Description: During KS testing I noticed, that after launching """"""""Local URL"""""""" activity indicator keeps spinning. """"""""Hide indicator"""""""" app event not being fired. It does not happen if running test case first time after app was installed. Regression, does not occur in 2.0.2. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Base UI - Views - Web Views - Local URL 3. Press """"""""back"""""""" button 4. Launch Local URL one more time Expected result: Activity indicator should appear and then disappear. Actual result: Activity indicator keeps spinning. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9526,12,"""Android: Views - Default Web View changes Text size  on rotation.""","""""""While testing KS Views I noticed unexpected text's size change on rotation from a landscape mode to portrait. Zooming a Web View before rotation is not affecting text size. It appears when a test case run from a landscape mode only.    This is not a regression. The issue occurs on 2.0.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Run Base UI - Views - Web Views - Inline HTML in a landscape mode.  3. Rotate the device.    Expected result:  No text's size change on rotation    Actual result:  Text size changes""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Views - Default Web View changes Text size on rotation.
Description: """"While testing KS Views I noticed unexpected text's size change on rotation from a landscape mode to portrait. Zooming a Web View before rotation is not affecting text size. It appears when a test case run from a landscape mode only. This is not a regression. The issue occurs on 2.0.2. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Run Base UI - Views - Web Views - Inline HTML in a landscape mode. 3. Rotate the device. Expected result: No text's size change on rotation Actual result: Text size changes""""",title+description
TIMOB-9525,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.iOS.TabbedBar - no 'click' events get triggered on already selected button""","""""""h2. Problem description  Ti.UI.iOS.TabbedBar does not fire a click event if the user taps on a button that's already selected.    h2. Steps to reproduce and sample code  1. Run sample code and click on a tabbedBar button  Result: 'click' eventListener it's correctly triggered. Button it's now selected.  2. Click again on the same button  Result: no 'click' event it's triggered        """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.iOS.TabbedBar - no 'click' events get triggered on already selected button
Description: """"h2. Problem description Ti.UI.iOS.TabbedBar does not fire a click event if the user taps on a button that's already selected. h2. Steps to reproduce and sample code 1. Run sample code and click on a tabbedBar button Result: 'click' eventListener it's correctly triggered. Button it's now selected. 2. Click again on the same button Result: no 'click' event it's triggered """"",title+description
TIMOB-9524,12,"""iOS: Support multiple JS files per module""","""""""See umbrella bug for description. MobileWeb has already implemented this; see the ticket for the full details, but the general structure is:    * require('module.id') requires the main module JS  * require('module.id/sub-lib') requires the JS file 'sub-lib.js' which is loaded in the module    Introducing this may require some significant changes in iOS' module-loading infrastructure.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: iOS: Support multiple JS files per module
Description: """"See umbrella bug for description. MobileWeb has already implemented this; see the ticket for the full details, but the general structure is: * require('module.id') requires the main module JS * require('module.id/sub-lib') requires the JS file 'sub-lib.js' which is loaded in the module Introducing this may require some significant changes in iOS' module-loading infrastructure.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9522,12,"""Android: Views - Flickers on launch""","""""""While testing KS Views I noticed the flicker after Local URL was launched.    Not a regression, affects 2.0.2     Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run the KS  2. Click View - Web Views - Local URL    Actual  See the flicker as it is launching    Expected  Should not flicker""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Views - Flickers on launch
Description: """"While testing KS Views I noticed the flicker after Local URL was launched. Not a regression, affects 2.0.2 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the KS 2. Click View - Web Views - Local URL Actual See the flicker as it is launching Expected Should not flicker""""",title+description
TIMOB-9521,12,"""TiAPI: Analytic Events: Review and define what information should be sent for each event""","""""""Currently some events are sending more data than needed. We need to define what needs to be sent for each of the different events. Below is a list of data that is being sent:  id  mid  rdu  type  aguid  event  seq  ver  deploytype  sid  ts  data    Need to document when we should be sending all this information and when some information can be omitted""""""",Story,"Title: TiAPI: Analytic Events: Review and define what information should be sent for each event
Description: """"Currently some events are sending more data than needed. We need to define what needs to be sent for each of the different events. Below is a list of data that is being sent: id mid rdu type aguid event seq ver deploytype sid ts data Need to document when we should be sending all this information and when some information can be omitted""""",title+description
TIMOB-9520,12,"""Tooling: Implement deprecation warnings Code Processor plugin""","""""""We should support deprecation warnings when an old API is used.""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Tooling: Implement deprecation warnings Code Processor plugin
Description: """"We should support deprecation warnings when an old API is used.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9519,12,"""MobileWeb: Update Kinetic Scroll Views to use new animation""","""""""The kinetic scroll views (ScrollableView, ScrollView, TableView) currently use transitions for their animation. Unfortunately, once an animation starts, it can't be stopped, so when something happens mid-animation (such as touching and grabbing again), undesirable side-effects occur. Using the cancel() method of the new animation mechanism should solve this issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Update Kinetic Scroll Views to use new animation
Description: """"The kinetic scroll views (ScrollableView, ScrollView, TableView) currently use transitions for their animation. Unfortunately, once an animation starts, it can't be stopped, so when something happens mid-animation (such as touching and grabbing again), undesirable side-effects occur. Using the cancel() method of the new animation mechanism should solve this issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9518,12,"""iOS: Views - Ability to bring a search bar not only by pressing a Show button, but also by scrolling down the screen""","""""""While testing KS I noticed that a screen with 4 rows appears after some redrawing, and I can bring a search bar not only by pressing show button, but also by scrolling down the screen.    Not a regression, appears in 2.0.2    Test steps  1. Run KS  2. Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Search  3. Scroll down the screen     Actual result:  An ability to bring a search bar by scrolling down the screen    Expected result:  Ability to bring a search bar by pressing a show button  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Views - Ability to bring a search bar not only by pressing a Show button, but also by scrolling down the screen
Description: """"While testing KS I noticed that a screen with 4 rows appears after some redrawing, and I can bring a search bar not only by pressing show button, but also by scrolling down the screen. Not a regression, appears in 2.0.2 Test steps 1. Run KS 2. Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Search 3. Scroll down the screen Actual result: An ability to bring a search bar by scrolling down the screen Expected result: Ability to bring a search bar by pressing a show button """"",title+description
