TIMOB-9505,12,"""iOS: New feature to add ability to choose keychain at codesign""","""""""Currently, even when we set the default keychain to the separate keychain in OS X, codesign will still look at not only the separate keychain but also the default login keychain.     The codesign man pages say that we are allowed to pass an argument with the keychain that we would like to use and codesign will only look at that keychain.    It has been requested to add a new feature to have the ability to select the desired keychain from command line through builder.py.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: New feature to add ability to choose keychain at codesign
Description: """"Currently, even when we set the default keychain to the separate keychain in OS X, codesign will still look at not only the separate keychain but also the default login keychain. The codesign man pages say that we are allowed to pass an argument with the keychain that we would like to use and codesign will only look at that keychain. It has been requested to add a new feature to have the ability to select the desired keychain from command line through builder.py.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9504,12,"""Android: Android builder.py script fails with Ti 2.1 SDK""","""""""h3. Problem    The Android builder.py script in the 2.1 SDK fails when it calls the zipalign tool in the Android SDK, with the error """"""""Unable to open <apk file> as zip archive.""""""""    h4. From the customer:    The error seems to be caused by a change to builder.py in 2.1. When it calls out to the Android jarsigner tool, the 2.1 script uses two additional parameters, """"""""-sigalg MD5withRSA"""""""" and """"""""-digestalg SHA1"""""""". The 2.0.X builder.py script does not have these two extra arguments. The script calls zipalign right after that, which fails. When the two arguments from the 2.1 builder.py are removed it runs successfully, and if those are added to the 2.0 builder.py, it fails with the same error.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Android builder.py script fails with Ti 2.1 SDK
Description: """"h3. Problem The Android builder.py script in the 2.1 SDK fails when it calls the zipalign tool in the Android SDK, with the error """"""""Unable to open <apk file> as zip archive."""""""" h4. From the customer: The error seems to be caused by a change to builder.py in 2.1. When it calls out to the Android jarsigner tool, the 2.1 script uses two additional parameters, """"""""-sigalg MD5withRSA"""""""" and """"""""-digestalg SHA1"""""""". The 2.0.X builder.py script does not have these two extra arguments. The script calls zipalign right after that, which fails. When the two arguments from the 2.1 builder.py are removed it runs successfully, and if those are added to the 2.0 builder.py, it fails with the same error. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9503,12,"""iOS: iPhone builder.py script fails with Ti 2.1 SDK""","""""""h3. Problem    The iPhone builder.py script fails with this error:    [ERROR]   [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):  File """"""""builder.py"""""""", line 1548, in main  execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False)  File """"""""builder.py"""""""", line 1237, in execute_xcode  output = run.run(args,False,False,o)  File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.0.v20120601150541/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 41, in run  sys.exit(rc)  SystemExit: 65    This occurs using Ti nightly build 2.1.0.v20120601150541 downloaded from the CI builds page.     This occurs on building the Kitchen Sink app too.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPhone builder.py script fails with Ti 2.1 SDK
Description: """"h3. Problem The iPhone builder.py script fails with this error: [ERROR] [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""builder.py"""""""", line 1548, in main execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False) File """"""""builder.py"""""""", line 1237, in execute_xcode output = run.run(args,False,False,o) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/2.1.0.v20120601150541/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 41, in run sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65 This occurs using Ti nightly build 2.1.0.v20120601150541 downloaded from the CI builds page. This occurs on building the Kitchen Sink app too. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9502,12,"""iOS: Focus and open events don't fire on first window when require() is used""","""""""h4.Problem  There is a regression in mobile SDK 2.1.0.v20120608174150 that causes an intermittent failure of open and focus events at the Window level.  Sometimes neither event will fire.  Sometimes the open event fires but the focus event won't.    h4.Testcase  Use the sample project that is attached.  This code is reduced down from a much larger app.  I have reduced it down as far as I can and still demonstrate the problem.  You'll notice that much of the code in the require()d and/or include()d units is not executed, but removing it hides the problem.  During testing, I noticed that volume of code seemed to affect the reproducibility of the problem.    Just run the app, and look at the console log.  You may need to run it several times!  In my testing, it failed more often than it succeeded.    h4.Expected Result  In the console log you should see:  {panel}  == Loading Procs  == Loading Themes  top  bottom  MainWinLoad fired  MainWinFocus fired from [object Object]  {panel}    h4.Actual Result  {panel}  == Loading Procs  == Loading Themes  top  bottom  {panel}    sometimes the """"""""MainWinLoad fired"""""""" line will show up, and sometimes the """"""""MainWinFocus fired from [object Object]"""""""" line also appears.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Focus and open events don't fire on first window when require() is used
Description: """"h4.Problem There is a regression in mobile SDK 2.1.0.v20120608174150 that causes an intermittent failure of open and focus events at the Window level. Sometimes neither event will fire. Sometimes the open event fires but the focus event won't. h4.Testcase Use the sample project that is attached. This code is reduced down from a much larger app. I have reduced it down as far as I can and still demonstrate the problem. You'll notice that much of the code in the require()d and/or include()d units is not executed, but removing it hides the problem. During testing, I noticed that volume of code seemed to affect the reproducibility of the problem. Just run the app, and look at the console log. You may need to run it several times! In my testing, it failed more often than it succeeded. h4.Expected Result In the console log you should see: {panel} == Loading Procs == Loading Themes top bottom MainWinLoad fired MainWinFocus fired from [object Object] {panel} h4.Actual Result {panel} == Loading Procs == Loading Themes top bottom {panel} sometimes the """"""""MainWinLoad fired"""""""" line will show up, and sometimes the """"""""MainWinFocus fired from [object Object]"""""""" line also appears. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9501,12,"""TiAPI: Protected compiled source code""","""""""Titanium is great, but when it comes to give a client the mobile project, we see ourselves handing over 2 years of titanium javascript work.    I need a feature, where I can give my clients the source code, but not all of the source javascript files.   The dream senario would be to let titanium generate all the javascript into objC .h and .m files, and .java files for android. I guess this is never going to happen?    The second solution would be to compile the javascript into one secure file, where its not possible to view the javascript source code.   """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Protected compiled source code
Description: """"Titanium is great, but when it comes to give a client the mobile project, we see ourselves handing over 2 years of titanium javascript work. I need a feature, where I can give my clients the source code, but not all of the source javascript files. The dream senario would be to let titanium generate all the javascript into objC .h and .m files, and .java files for android. I guess this is never going to happen? The second solution would be to compile the javascript into one secure file, where its not possible to view the javascript source code. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9500,12,"""iOS: Table view rows that are not visible on screen should be recycled""","""""""h2. Problem    When adding table rows dynamically to a table view and there is a large data set, eventually the application will run out of memory because table rows and their child UI components are never released as more rows are scrolled through and added.    h2. Feature requested    In native iOS the table view rows are recycled so even for large or infinite data sets, there is always a limited number of rows that are in memory at any given time. In Titanium, this is not the case. It is not possible to have an infinite amount of table view rows without the application crashing or degrade in performance.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Table view rows that are not visible on screen should be recycled
Description: """"h2. Problem When adding table rows dynamically to a table view and there is a large data set, eventually the application will run out of memory because table rows and their child UI components are never released as more rows are scrolled through and added. h2. Feature requested In native iOS the table view rows are recycled so even for large or infinite data sets, there is always a limited number of rows that are in memory at any given time. In Titanium, this is not the case. It is not possible to have an infinite amount of table view rows without the application crashing or degrade in performance.""""",title+description
