TIMOB-9474,12,"""Android: ScrollableView throws exception when using scrollToView()""","""""""Trying to use scrollToView() on a ScrollableView sometimes results in an exception being thrown.  This appears to be triggered by creating the ScrollableView and passing a """"""""currentPage"""""""" parameter.    This regression appears in the KS Base UI > Views > Scroll Views > Scrollable View.  Try scrolling to the next view by using the arrows on the bottom (these call scrollToView()).    h3. Standalone test case        Run the test case and try switching views by using the """"""""next"""""""" or """"""""prev"""""""" buttons.    Expected: Views change without any crash.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ScrollableView throws exception when using scrollToView()
Description: """"Trying to use scrollToView() on a ScrollableView sometimes results in an exception being thrown. This appears to be triggered by creating the ScrollableView and passing a """"""""currentPage"""""""" parameter. This regression appears in the KS Base UI > Views > Scroll Views > Scrollable View. Try scrolling to the next view by using the arrows on the bottom (these call scrollToView()). h3. Standalone test case Run the test case and try switching views by using the """"""""next"""""""" or """"""""prev"""""""" buttons. Expected: Views change without any crash.""""",title+description
