TIMOB-9467,12,"""MobileWeb: Default Project - Android 2.2.3 device browser will load default project, but stay at the splash screen""","""""""Details: On SDK 2.1.0.v20120608070223, while launching default TiMobile project on Droid 1's browser, the app will stay on the splash screen. However, on SDK 2.0.2.GA, the app will be fully launched; app will not stay on the splash screen.    Also, I noticed some logs similar to what Dustin found in TIMOB-8255:    In SDK 2.1.0.v20120608070223:      In SDK 2.0.2.GA:      Note: *This is a regression.* Was able to fully launch default TiMobile app in 2.0.2.GA    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create default TiMobile project in TiStudio  2. Package app for Mobile Web   3. Put packaged app on server.  4. Access app via Droid 1's browser    Actual: Default project will be launched, but stay on the splash screen  Expected: The default project should not stay on the splash screen""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Default Project - Android 2.2.3 device browser will load default project, but stay at the splash screen
Description: """"Details: On SDK 2.1.0.v20120608070223, while launching default TiMobile project on Droid 1's browser, the app will stay on the splash screen. However, on SDK 2.0.2.GA, the app will be fully launched; app will not stay on the splash screen. Also, I noticed some logs similar to what Dustin found in TIMOB-8255: In SDK 2.1.0.v20120608070223: In SDK 2.0.2.GA: Note: *This is a regression.* Was able to fully launch default TiMobile app in 2.0.2.GA Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create default TiMobile project in TiStudio 2. Package app for Mobile Web 3. Put packaged app on server. 4. Access app via Droid 1's browser Actual: Default project will be launched, but stay on the splash screen Expected: The default project should not stay on the splash screen""""",title+description
TIMOB-9466,12,"""Android: Scrollview content can think it is bigger then it actually is""","""""""h6.Problem  The scroll content could change dynamically, but if it is very small, it wants to scroll anyway! The scroll height is fine, but it thinks its content is much larger then it actually is?    In iOS the Scrollview it won't scroll due to contents are very small.    h4.Tested on  h6.Testing on android  2.0.1GA2, 2.0.2.GA > Droid Razr 2.3.5    h6.Testing on iOS  iOS 5 simulator    h5.app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Scrollview content can think it is bigger then it actually is
Description: """"h6.Problem The scroll content could change dynamically, but if it is very small, it wants to scroll anyway! The scroll height is fine, but it thinks its content is much larger then it actually is? In iOS the Scrollview it won't scroll due to contents are very small. h4.Tested on h6.Testing on android 2.0.1GA2, 2.0.2.GA > Droid Razr 2.3.5 h6.Testing on iOS iOS 5 simulator h5.app.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-9465,12,"""TiAPI: Geolocation.hasCompass function vs property""","""""""Android and iOS have an API for accessing the device's compass.  Since not all devices have a hardware compass, you must test for its existence.    Android implements this as a getter property called """"""""hasCompass"""""""".  Android also provides a function called """"""""getHasCompass"""""""".  iOS implements this as a method called """"""""hasCompass"""""""".    This creates an unnecessary parity difference. We should determine if this property  should be changed on one of the platforms to be either a function or getter property.  We could also introduce a new property/function to avoid breaking changes to this API.  """"""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: Geolocation.hasCompass function vs property
Description: """"Android and iOS have an API for accessing the device's compass. Since not all devices have a hardware compass, you must test for its existence. Android implements this as a getter property called """"""""hasCompass"""""""". Android also provides a function called """"""""getHasCompass"""""""". iOS implements this as a method called """"""""hasCompass"""""""". This creates an unnecessary parity difference. We should determine if this property should be changed on one of the platforms to be either a function or getter property. We could also introduce a new property/function to avoid breaking changes to this API. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9464,12,"""Android: Orientation: Screen does not restrict to orientation modes supported in app.js""","""""""On Android platform, the application screen shows up even in those orientation mode that are not supported for the application.    This is not a regression. This issue occurs as far back as 1.8.2    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a mobile application with the code below  2. Launch the application with device in portrait  3. Hold device so top is pointing left   4. Hold device upside down   5. Hold device so top is pointing right    Actual Result:  After step 4, on galaxy tab the screen in shown in upside down orientation mode  After step 5, the screen is shown in Landscape left mode  Both Upside down and Landscape left are not supported modes for this application    Expected Result:  1. After step 2, the screen should be in portrait mode  2. For all further steps, the screen should be in Landscape right mode    App.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Orientation: Screen does not restrict to orientation modes supported in app.js
Description: """"On Android platform, the application screen shows up even in those orientation mode that are not supported for the application. This is not a regression. This issue occurs as far back as 1.8.2 Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a mobile application with the code below 2. Launch the application with device in portrait 3. Hold device so top is pointing left 4. Hold device upside down 5. Hold device so top is pointing right Actual Result: After step 4, on galaxy tab the screen in shown in upside down orientation mode After step 5, the screen is shown in Landscape left mode Both Upside down and Landscape left are not supported modes for this application Expected Result: 1. After step 2, the screen should be in portrait mode 2. For all further steps, the screen should be in Landscape right mode App.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-9462,12,"""Android:Window:modal and exitOnClose properties when used together causes app crash""","""""""It is not a regression.This issue exists as far as 1.8.2.    Refer the code below        Steps to reproduce:  1)Install the app and run it  2)Click 'Show Webview' button  3)Click 'Close' button    Expected results:  1)After step 1,a window should get opened with 'Show Webview' button  2)After step 2,a webview should get opened with 'Close' button.  3)After step 3,the webview should get closed and user should return to initial window of step 1.    Actual result:  1)After step 1,a window gets opened with 'Show Webview' button  2)After step 2,a webview gets opened with 'Close' button.  3)After step 3,the app crashes.    When at least one property,modal or exitOnClose is commented in the above code,it works fine.No crash happens after commenting them out.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android:Window:modal and exitOnClose properties when used together causes app crash
Description: """"It is not a regression.This issue exists as far as 1.8.2. Refer the code below Steps to reproduce: 1)Install the app and run it 2)Click 'Show Webview' button 3)Click 'Close' button Expected results: 1)After step 1,a window should get opened with 'Show Webview' button 2)After step 2,a webview should get opened with 'Close' button. 3)After step 3,the webview should get closed and user should return to initial window of step 1. Actual result: 1)After step 1,a window gets opened with 'Show Webview' button 2)After step 2,a webview gets opened with 'Close' button. 3)After step 3,the app crashes. When at least one property,modal or exitOnClose is commented in the above code,it works fine.No crash happens after commenting them out.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9461,12,"""iOS: Titanium.UI.WebView - Back button doesn't work after first navigation to second page.""","""""""Back button doesn't work after first navigation to second page.  This is not a regression. The issue occurs as far back as 1.8.2    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create an application using the code below.  2. launch the application.  3. Press 'Goto Second Page'link. Should navigate to page 2.  4. Press forward. Nothing should happen.  5. Press back. Should go to page 1.     Actual:  After navigation to second page, the back button does not work to bring back the first page.    Expected:  After navigation to second page, the back button should be able to take the user to the first page.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.UI.WebView - Back button doesn't work after first navigation to second page.
Description: """"Back button doesn't work after first navigation to second page. This is not a regression. The issue occurs as far back as 1.8.2 Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an application using the code below. 2. launch the application. 3. Press 'Goto Second Page'link. Should navigate to page 2. 4. Press forward. Nothing should happen. 5. Press back. Should go to page 1. Actual: After navigation to second page, the back button does not work to bring back the first page. Expected: After navigation to second page, the back button should be able to take the user to the first page. """"",title+description
