TIMOB-9452,12,"""Tooling: -all_load flag not supported for iOS Module development""","""""""h2. Problem description    Customer is building a module for a third-party library and the developers of the library specify that you must use the -ObjC and -all_load flags when integrating into an app.    However, if they use -all_load to build the module, when they build the app they get this linker error:        Leaving out -all_load they get a boatload of unresolved symbol errors.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: -all_load flag not supported for iOS Module development
Description: """"h2. Problem description Customer is building a module for a third-party library and the developers of the library specify that you must use the -ObjC and -all_load flags when integrating into an app. However, if they use -all_load to build the module, when they build the app they get this linker error: Leaving out -all_load they get a boatload of unresolved symbol errors.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9451,12,"""Android: Distribution build for Android breaks events in webview""","""""""I have a webview that fire events inside the webview when user clicks on links and interacts with form elements. This functionality works fine when building for emulator or device but when building for distribution nothing happens when clicking links or any other form elements in the webview.    Use case is attached.  Using SDK 2.0.1.GA2 with the latest Titanium Studio on a Mac it works when selecting """"""""Run on Device"""""""" but event does not work after a signed APK was generated with the """"""""Distribute - Android Marketplace"""""""" option and the signed APK is installed on a device.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Distribution build for Android breaks events in webview
Description: """"I have a webview that fire events inside the webview when user clicks on links and interacts with form elements. This functionality works fine when building for emulator or device but when building for distribution nothing happens when clicking links or any other form elements in the webview. Use case is attached. Using SDK 2.0.1.GA2 with the latest Titanium Studio on a Mac it works when selecting """"""""Run on Device"""""""" but event does not work after a signed APK was generated with the """"""""Distribute - Android Marketplace"""""""" option and the signed APK is installed on a device.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9450,12,"""iOS: Table Views - Pull to Refresh fails to add more rows""","""""""Description:  Pull to Refresh fails to update table with new rows after pull down.     This is a regression bug. It doesn't exist on 2.0.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Base UI- Views- Table Views- Pull to Refresh  3. Press and pull down    Expected Result:  Table should be updated with more rows each time a pull down is done to refresh    Actual Result:  Table is not being updated with new rows after pull down""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Table Views - Pull to Refresh fails to add more rows
Description: """"Description: Pull to Refresh fails to update table with new rows after pull down. This is a regression bug. It doesn't exist on 2.0.2. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Base UI- Views- Table Views- Pull to Refresh 3. Press and pull down Expected Result: Table should be updated with more rows each time a pull down is done to refresh Actual Result: Table is not being updated with new rows after pull down""""",title+description
TIMOB-9449,12,"""Android: TextField - Missing custom background image ""","""""""Description:  Missing custom background image, only label """"""""Custom background image"""""""" is displayed.  The similar issue exists on Controls - Text Field - The Rest. Clicking """"""""Background Image"""""""" button does not displays an image.    This is regression, does not occur on 2.0.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Controls - Text Field - Border Style    Expected result:  The label and custom background image should be displayed    Actual result:  Custom background image is missing""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField - Missing custom background image
