TIMOB-9429,12,"""Android: Views - Image is not clear and fills all screen""","""""""Description:  During a KitchenSink testing I noticed that an image's size doesn't match an expected size. Image is not clear and fills all screen. This issue occurs only if you're running test case first time after installation KS on a device. If you go back and run test case second time the image appears in correct size and it is clear.     Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.2 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Install KitchenSink on a device  2. Go to Base UI - Views - Image Views - Image View Encoding    Actual result:  The image is not clear     Expected result:  The image should be clear  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Views - Image is not clear and fills all screen
Description: """"Description: During a KitchenSink testing I noticed that an image's size doesn't match an expected size. Image is not clear and fills all screen. This issue occurs only if you're running test case first time after installation KS on a device. If you go back and run test case second time the image appears in correct size and it is clear. Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.2 as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Install KitchenSink on a device 2. Go to Base UI - Views - Image Views - Image View Encoding Actual result: The image is not clear Expected result: The image should be clear """"",title+description
