TIMOB-9405,12,"""Android: slider 'touchEnd'  event it's not always fired""","""""""h2. Problem description  On Android, slider """"""""touchend"""""""" events are not triggered if the finger is released from the screen when it's no longer on the picker    h2. Expected results  The alert being shown on touchend event.     h3. Actual Results  In SDK 2.1.1 it's working fine in Android 2.2.2, but failing to provide the alert in Android OS 4.1    h2. Sample code    Run the sample code below.  Start moving the slider and release the finger when the finger is still on top of the slider.  Result: alert it's being displayed    Move the slider again and release the finger when the finger it's no longer on top of the slider  Result: event it's not triggered and alert it's not displayed.    It's only reproducible on Android OS. On iOS platform works as expected.        h2. Simpler Test Case       h2. Additional notes / Discussion   Ticket link: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-933556/conversation/read_all    h2. Extra comments  This is failing in some devices, like:    DeviceS: Motorola MB860 (OS ver 2.3.4) - FAILING.  Devices: Google Nexus Tablet 7 OS Ver 4.1 - FAILING    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: slider 'touchEnd' event it's not always fired
Description: """"h2. Problem description On Android, slider """"""""touchend"""""""" events are not triggered if the finger is released from the screen when it's no longer on the picker h2. Expected results The alert being shown on touchend event. h3. Actual Results In SDK 2.1.1 it's working fine in Android 2.2.2, but failing to provide the alert in Android OS 4.1 h2. Sample code Run the sample code below. Start moving the slider and release the finger when the finger is still on top of the slider. Result: alert it's being displayed Move the slider again and release the finger when the finger it's no longer on top of the slider Result: event it's not triggered and alert it's not displayed. It's only reproducible on Android OS. On iOS platform works as expected. h2. Simpler Test Case h2. Additional notes / Discussion Ticket link: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-933556/conversation/read_all h2. Extra comments This is failing in some devices, like: DeviceS: Motorola MB860 (OS ver 2.3.4) - FAILING. Devices: Google Nexus Tablet 7 OS Ver 4.1 - FAILING """"",title+description
TIMOB-9404,12,"""MobileWeb: Map - Add centerOffset property to Ti.Map.Annotation""","""""""See if Mobile Web can provide the same functionality.    Original ticket:    Add centerOffset property to a custom annotation to be able to set a x & y offset to the image of the annotation.  Right now the center of the annotation is the center of the image size. This makes that some images appear not to be in their proper place at certain zoom levels.    Reference to official documentation: http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/MapKit/Reference/MKAnnotationView_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40008207    I have already coded the feature and I open this ticket in order to get the pull request accepted.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Map - Add centerOffset property to Ti.Map.Annotation
Description: """"See if Mobile Web can provide the same functionality. Original ticket: Add centerOffset property to a custom annotation to be able to set a x & y offset to the image of the annotation. Right now the center of the annotation is the center of the image size. This makes that some images appear not to be in their proper place at certain zoom levels. Reference to official documentation: http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/MapKit/Reference/MKAnnotationView_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40008207 I have already coded the feature and I open this ticket in order to get the pull request accepted.""""",title+description
