TIMOB-9336,12,"""Android:Packaging:V8:Error occurring while packaging with sdk 2.1.0 whereas same project gets packaged with sdk 2.0.2 ""","""""""A regression, the behavior do not exists in 1.8.2 and 2.0.2.  This occurs only on windows.On MAC,packaging with sdk 2.1.0 is not throwing error.    Steps to reproduce :  1) Create the default Titanium project with sdk selected as 2.1.0.  2) Go to Publish > Distribute - Android app store  3) Fill in your Distribution Location, Keystore Location, Keystore Password, and Key Alias   4) Click Publish      Actual result  While packaging a project if sdk is 2.1.0,it gives error.While with 2.0.2(or 1.8.2), the same project packages successfully.  The logs received with different sdks(1.8.2, 2.0.2 and 2.1.0) are  attached with the bug.  Error shown is below :  [ERROR] Error(s) compiling generated Java code  [ERROR] C:\<USER>Tit alternate workspace\test3\build\android\gen\com\appc\test3\AssetCryptImpl.java:24: <identifier> expected  None      ^  1 error    Expected result:  Packaging should be successful with sdk 2.1.0 also.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android:Packaging:V8:Error occurring while packaging with sdk 2.1.0 whereas same project gets packaged with sdk 2.0.2
Description: """"A regression, the behavior do not exists in 1.8.2 and 2.0.2. This occurs only on windows.On MAC,packaging with sdk 2.1.0 is not throwing error. Steps to reproduce : 1) Create the default Titanium project with sdk selected as 2.1.0. 2) Go to Publish > Distribute - Android app store 3) Fill in your Distribution Location, Keystore Location, Keystore Password, and Key Alias 4) Click Publish Actual result While packaging a project if sdk is 2.1.0,it gives error.While with 2.0.2(or 1.8.2), the same project packages successfully. The logs received with different sdks(1.8.2, 2.0.2 and 2.1.0) are attached with the bug. Error shown is below : [ERROR] Error(s) compiling generated Java code [ERROR] C:\<USER>Tit alternate workspace\test3\build\android\gen\com\appc\test3\AssetCryptImpl.java:24: <identifier> expected None ^ 1 error Expected result: Packaging should be successful with sdk 2.1.0 also.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9335,12,"""iOS: New feature to add a """"paused"""" event listener""","""""""This is new feature requested to add a """"""""paused"""""""" event listener that is fired when the application enters background. This will be added to the      method    This is needed since the https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9299 issue was marked as invalid and it is a requirement to detect the double tap of the home button and not fire the pause event (where they are implementing some other functionality) but a """"""""paused"""""""" type event.    This will have a similar effect to what """"""""resume"""""""" and """"""""resumed"""""""" have.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: New feature to add a """"paused"""" event listener
Description: """"This is new feature requested to add a """"""""paused"""""""" event listener that is fired when the application enters background. This will be added to the method This is needed since the https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-9299 issue was marked as invalid and it is a requirement to detect the double tap of the home button and not fire the pause event (where they are implementing some other functionality) but a """"""""paused"""""""" type event. This will have a similar effect to what """"""""resume"""""""" and """"""""resumed"""""""" have. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9334,12,"""Android: TI.UI.TableViewRow  - v8:  ability to change value of the checkbox by tapping  outside this box""","""""""While testing TableViewRow I was able to check and uncheck box by tapping white area outside this box above """"""""Create TableView"""""""" button. Tapping below """"""""Create TableView"""""""" button doesn't change value.    Otherwise the result as expected.    Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well.     Test steps  1. Run app.   2. Navigate to acceptance tab and press timob_4648   3. Press the check box (it should start out checked, so uncheck it)   4. Press the Create TableView button   5. Press the check box   6. Press the Create TableView button  Expected result  After step 4: Evil row should be yellow and With opacity row should be yellow with 0.8 opacity   After step 6: Should be same as step 4 above""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TI.UI.TableViewRow - v8: ability to change value of the checkbox by tapping outside this box
Description: """"While testing TableViewRow I was able to check and uncheck box by tapping white area outside this box above """"""""Create TableView"""""""" button. Tapping below """"""""Create TableView"""""""" button doesn't change value. Otherwise the result as expected. Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well. Test steps 1. Run app. 2. Navigate to acceptance tab and press timob_4648 3. Press the check box (it should start out checked, so uncheck it) 4. Press the Create TableView button 5. Press the check box 6. Press the Create TableView button Expected result After step 4: Evil row should be yellow and With opacity row should be yellow with 0.8 opacity After step 6: Should be same as step 4 above""""",title+description
TIMOB-9333,12,"""Android: UI components do not respect positioning properties in """"horizontal"""" layout""","""""""h2. The problem      When components are added to the parent view that has """"""""layout"""""""" property defined as """"""""horizontal"""""""", positioning properties are not respected.      To see that, run this example:          You should see that second label and picker are not positioned well.      h2. Expected result      Second label and picker should be positioned as the first one (with """"""""left"""""""" and """"""""top"""""""" margins).      This issue is related to this: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-874      On iPhone simulator this doesn't work at all.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: UI components do not respect positioning properties in """"horizontal"""" layout
Description: """"h2. The problem When components are added to the parent view that has """"""""layout"""""""" property defined as """"""""horizontal"""""""", positioning properties are not respected. To see that, run this example: You should see that second label and picker are not positioned well. h2. Expected result Second label and picker should be positioned as the first one (with """"""""left"""""""" and """"""""top"""""""" margins). This issue is related to this: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-874 On iPhone simulator this doesn't work at all.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9332,12,"""iOS: Map - Add centerOffset property to Ti.Map.Annotation""","""""""Add centerOffset property to a custom annotation to be able to set a x & y offset to the image of the annotation.  Right now the center of the annotation is the center of the image size. This makes that some images appear not to be in their proper place at certain zoom levels.    Reference to official documentation: http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/MapKit/Reference/MKAnnotationView_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40008207    I have already coded the feature and I open this ticket in order to get the pull request accepted.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Map - Add centerOffset property to Ti.Map.Annotation
Description: """"Add centerOffset property to a custom annotation to be able to set a x & y offset to the image of the annotation. Right now the center of the annotation is the center of the image size. This makes that some images appear not to be in their proper place at certain zoom levels. Reference to official documentation: http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/MapKit/Reference/MKAnnotationView_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40008207 I have already coded the feature and I open this ticket in order to get the pull request accepted.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9331,12,"""iOS: Videos in a ScrollableView stop working when moving back and forth in the views""","""""""h2. Problem description  Issues displaying the video while moving back and forth the scrollableView.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Create an app with the code below  2. Open the app and scroll to the right 2-3 times: in each page, a view is displayed  3. Go back to a previous video by scrolling to the left: the videos disappear and the screen goes black              h2. Expected result  Videos are displayed correctly  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Videos in a ScrollableView stop working when moving back and forth in the views
Description: """"h2. Problem description Issues displaying the video while moving back and forth the scrollableView. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Create an app with the code below 2. Open the app and scroll to the right 2-3 times: in each page, a view is displayed 3. Go back to a previous video by scrolling to the left: the videos disappear and the screen goes black h2. Expected result Videos are displayed correctly """"",title+description
TIMOB-9330,12,"""iOS: iPad: webView.width = Ti.UI.FILL not being honored""","""""""h6.Issue  WebView with inline HTML in splitWindow does not align horizontally correctly in landscape orientation. Having set URL property exhibits this issue as well.    Putting webView within another view as a wrapper or adding an 'orientationchange' event listener on Ti.Gesture to update the webView width to either 695 (landscape) or 768 (portrait) depending on the orientation but this did not work either.    h6.Tested on  iPad simulator    h6.Reproduction steps  1. Run sample below - The webView display correctly in portrait orientation mode.  2. Tap any row to display contents.   3. Rotate to landscape mode, the webView displays with horizontal scrolling. If you tap another row from the masterView tableView, the detailView inline HTML resizes correctly without horizontal scrolling.     h6.Expected behavior  WebView it should not display with horizontal scrolling therefore FILL property being respected.    h6.Current behavior  WebView initially displayed in landscape mode, it displays with horizontal scrolling.    h4.app.js        h4.master.js      h4.Having set webView.width = Ti.UI.FILL doesn't have effect:    h4.detail.js      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad: webView.width = Ti.UI.FILL not being honored
Description: """"h6.Issue WebView with inline HTML in splitWindow does not align horizontally correctly in landscape orientation. Having set URL property exhibits this issue as well. Putting webView within another view as a wrapper or adding an 'orientationchange' event listener on Ti.Gesture to update the webView width to either 695 (landscape) or 768 (portrait) depending on the orientation but this did not work either. h6.Tested on iPad simulator h6.Reproduction steps 1. Run sample below - The webView display correctly in portrait orientation mode. 2. Tap any row to display contents. 3. Rotate to landscape mode, the webView displays with horizontal scrolling. If you tap another row from the masterView tableView, the detailView inline HTML resizes correctly without horizontal scrolling. h6.Expected behavior WebView it should not display with horizontal scrolling therefore FILL property being respected. h6.Current behavior WebView initially displayed in landscape mode, it displays with horizontal scrolling. h4.app.js h4.master.js h4.Having set webView.width = Ti.UI.FILL doesn't have effect: h4.detail.js """"",title+description
