Description: """"Cleanup the existing TODO's in the scripts?""""",title+description
TIMOB-9308,12,"""iOS: Editable property not respected for a TextField""","""""""1. Compile and run the attached project.  2. Click on the text field.  EXPECTED RESULTS: you should not be able to edit the results of the text field as its editable property is set to false  ACTUAL RESULTS: you can edit the text field    Works fine on Android.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Editable property not respected for a TextField
Description: """"1. Compile and run the attached project. 2. Click on the text field. EXPECTED RESULTS: you should not be able to edit the results of the text field as its editable property is set to false ACTUAL RESULTS: you can edit the text field Works fine on Android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9305,12,"""iOS: Vertical layout View inside ScrollView bug""","""""""h1. Intro    I just started migrating my app from sdk1.8.2 to 2.0.1.GA2 and I am having issues with my views inside tableviews .. I think the one in fault here is the view that doesn't actualize its automatic height once it reaches the screen height.    h1. Test Case        h1. Problem    {quote}  [INFO] Application started  [INFO] test/1.0 (2.0.2.v20120418121806.0684d32)  [INFO] Calling addLabels  [INFO] width=320 & height=480  ...  [INFO] width=320 & height=480  [INFO] Calling addLabels  [INFO] width=320 & height=560  [INFO] width=320 & height=560  [INFO] Opening window  [INFO] width=320 & height=960  [INFO] width=320 & height=960  [INFO] Closing window  [INFO] width=320 & height=960  ...  {quote}    After 2 seconds, there should be 12 labels on top of each other, but only 7 appear. You can only see the rest after a redraw action (in this case, a modal window, but a regular window or even a keyboard would do the trick).    As you can see, there are only two postlayout events after the second call and the size does not correspond to 6 * 80 pixels labels added. As soon as the modal window opens, new postlayout events are called but this time with the right height.    h1. Note    I know a tableview would work just fine in this case, but it is just a basic sample code to show you the but i am having with more complicated code.    And the problem also appears with a horizontal layout.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Vertical layout View inside ScrollView bug
Description: """"h1. Intro I just started migrating my app from sdk1.8.2 to 2.0.1.GA2 and I am having issues with my views inside tableviews .. I think the one in fault here is the view that doesn't actualize its automatic height once it reaches the screen height. h1. Test Case h1. Problem {quote} [INFO] Application started [INFO] test/1.0 (2.0.2.v20120418121806.0684d32) [INFO] Calling addLabels [INFO] width=320 & height=480 ... [INFO] width=320 & height=480 [INFO] Calling addLabels [INFO] width=320 & height=560 [INFO] width=320 & height=560 [INFO] Opening window [INFO] width=320 & height=960 [INFO] width=320 & height=960 [INFO] Closing window [INFO] width=320 & height=960 ... {quote} After 2 seconds, there should be 12 labels on top of each other, but only 7 appear. You can only see the rest after a redraw action (in this case, a modal window, but a regular window or even a keyboard would do the trick). As you can see, there are only two postlayout events after the second call and the size does not correspond to 6 * 80 pixels labels added. As soon as the modal window opens, new postlayout events are called but this time with the right height. h1. Note I know a tableview would work just fine in this case, but it is just a basic sample code to show you the but i am having with more complicated code. And the problem also appears with a horizontal layout.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9304,12,"""Android: TI.UI.Window  - v8: a background window changed after the device's rotation from portrait to landscape mode and back""","""""""While testing Window Acceptance I notised changes in a background window after rotating the device from a portrait mode to a lanscape and back. It changing from a white screen to an <USER>s logo.    Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run Application Titanium.UI.Window Acceptance TIMOB-7931.     Expected result:  You should see a white screen with the text 'Hello World""""""""    Actual Result:  see Attachments""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TI.UI.Window - v8: a background window changed after the device's rotation from portrait to landscape mode and back
Description: """"While testing Window Acceptance I notised changes in a background window after rotating the device from a portrait mode to a lanscape and back. It changing from a white screen to an <USER>s logo. Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run Application Titanium.UI.Window Acceptance TIMOB-7931. Expected result: You should see a white screen with the text 'Hello World"""""""" Actual Result: see Attachments""""",title+description
TIMOB-9303,12,"""Android: TI.UI.Window  - v8:  text of the button flashes on the screen after button pressed and dismissed ""","""""""While testing Window Acceptance I notised that the  text of a """"""""Close Window 2"""""""" button moves and flashes on a bottom of the screen after the button was pressed and disappeared.    Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run Application Titanium.UI.Window Acceptance TIMOB-7694.   2. Press 'Open Window 2' button.   3. Press 'Close Window 2' button.     Expected result:  App should not crash.    Actual Result:  see Attachment        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TI.UI.Window - v8: text of the button flashes on the screen after button pressed and dismissed
