TIMOB-9282,12,"""Android: Utils.md5HexDigest() not reading blob""","""""""h2. Problem    When reading a locally stored file (in both resources directory and a downloaded file in the app data directory), {{Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest()}} should read the blob and return a string, but instead NULL is returned on Android.    Works on iOS.    h2. Test case    Add the following snippet to the end of a new mobile project and iOS will return MD5 hex string, android won't.    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  downloadPath     =     Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory, 'KS_nav_ui.png');    var localFile     =     downloadPath.read();  Ti.API.info(typeof localFile);  localmd5checksum     =     Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest(localFile);  Ti.API.info(localmd5checksum);  alert(localmd5checksum);  {code}    h2. Discussions    http://developer.<USER>com/question/122224/verify-file-checksum (11 months old)              """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Utils.md5HexDigest() not reading blob
Description: """"h2. Problem When reading a locally stored file (in both resources directory and a downloaded file in the app data directory), {{Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest()}} should read the blob and return a string, but instead NULL is returned on Android. Works on iOS. h2. Test case Add the following snippet to the end of a new mobile project and iOS will return MD5 hex string, android won't. {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} downloadPath = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory, 'KS_nav_ui.png'); var localFile = downloadPath.read(); Ti.API.info(typeof localFile); localmd5checksum = Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest(localFile); Ti.API.info(localmd5checksum); alert(localmd5checksum); {code} h2. Discussions http://developer.<USER>com/question/122224/verify-file-checksum (11 months old) """"",title+description
TIMOB-9281,12,"""Android: Sound - RemoteURL failed to reproduce  sound after Stop and Play again""","""""""While testing Remote URL I noticed that sound is not coming back after an interrupting by pressing """"""""Stop"""""""" and  """"""""Play"""""""" button one more time.    Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well.   This issue occurs only on Android devices with 2.2 version    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Phone - Sound - Remote URL  3. Press """"""""Play"""""""" button  4. Press """"""""Stop"""""""" button  5. Press """"""""Play"""""""" button again    Expected Result:  Should hear sound     Actual Result:  Sound is not playing""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Sound - RemoteURL failed to reproduce sound after Stop and Play again
