TIMOB-9263,12,"""Android: UI.Clipboard - setData, hasData and getData have no effect""","""""""h2. Problem    The setData, hasData and getData methods of [Titanium.UI.Clipboard|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.Clipboard] do not have any effect. This is mostly because setData's source code only converts the input to string but does not save it. Also, has data should return a boolean, but does not.    See the test case below, and the source at [ClipboardModule.java|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/clipboard/ClipboardModule.java].    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  Ti.UI.Clipboard.setData('text/plain', 'hello'); // does not store data  Ti.API.log('Does the Clipboard contain any data?...' + Ti.UI.Clipboard.hasData('text/plain')); // does not output boolean  Ti.API.log('Getting hello text from Clipboard...' + Ti.UI.Clipboard.getData('text/plain')); // does not generate any output  Ti.API.log('getText: ' + Ti.UI.Clipboard.getText()); // should this return data stored with setData where a mime type with a text prefix is specified?  {code}    h2. Logs    No errors are generated.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: UI.Clipboard - setData, hasData and getData have no effect
Description: """"h2. Problem The setData, hasData and getData methods of [Titanium.UI.Clipboard|http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.Clipboard] do not have any effect. This is mostly because setData's source code only converts the input to string but does not save it. Also, has data should return a boolean, but does not. See the test case below, and the source at [ClipboardModule.java|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/clipboard/ClipboardModule.java]. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); Ti.UI.Clipboard.setData('text/plain', 'hello'); // does not store data Ti.API.log('Does the Clipboard contain any data?...' + Ti.UI.Clipboard.hasData('text/plain')); // does not output boolean Ti.API.log('Getting hello text from Clipboard...' + Ti.UI.Clipboard.getData('text/plain')); // does not generate any output Ti.API.log('getText: ' + Ti.UI.Clipboard.getText()); // should this return data stored with setData where a mime type with a text prefix is specified? {code} h2. Logs No errors are generated. """"",title+description
