TIMOB-9215,12,"""MobileWeb: ActivityIndicator is invisible on white background""","""""""The MW activity indicator is all-white, and there's no option to change colors.    iOS has three style options for activity indicators: small light-colored, small dark-colored, and large light-colored (there is no large dark-colored option, go figure). We might want to consider doing this for MW.     See:    http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle    """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: ActivityIndicator is invisible on white background
Description: """"The MW activity indicator is all-white, and there's no option to change colors. iOS has three style options for activity indicators: small light-colored, small dark-colored, and large light-colored (there is no large dark-colored option, go figure). We might want to consider doing this for MW. See: http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle """"",title+description
TIMOB-9214,12,"""Android: Trace messages (Ti.API.trace) do not appear in Studio because of how Android builder.py launches the emulator""","""""""h3. Fail case / Test case:    * Create a new app in Ti Studio.    * In the Console area, change the filter to Trace.    * Run this app.js *in an emulator*:    {code:name=""""""""app.js""""""""}  Ti.API.trace(""""""""TRACE TRACE TRACE"""""""");  Ti.API.info(""""""""INFO INFO INFO"""""""");  Ti.API.debug(""""""""DEBUG DEBUG DEBUG"""""""");  {code}    * Display the """"""""Titanium Android Emulator"""""""" console in the console area.    * In the fail case, you'll see only the INFO and DEBUG messages.  While testing the fix, you should see all three.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Trace messages (Ti.API.trace) do not appear in Studio because of how Android builder.py launches the emulator
Description: """"h3. Fail case / Test case: * Create a new app in Ti Studio. * In the Console area, change the filter to Trace. * Run this app.js *in an emulator*: {code:name=""""""""app.js""""""""} Ti.API.trace(""""""""TRACE TRACE TRACE""""""""); Ti.API.info(""""""""INFO INFO INFO""""""""); Ti.API.debug(""""""""DEBUG DEBUG DEBUG""""""""); {code} * Display the """"""""Titanium Android Emulator"""""""" console in the console area. * In the fail case, you'll see only the INFO and DEBUG messages. While testing the fix, you should see all three.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9213,12,"""Android: RSS Reader: intermittent crash on use with Fatal Signal 11 SIGSEGV""","""""""When the RSS Reader Sample is used, there is an intermittent crash on use. Log attached.    The crash occurred on a tab, so the back button was not a factor.    It is unknown if this is a regression due to the intermittent and unpredictable nature of the issue.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Download the RSS Reader sample from studio and deploy on Android device.  2. Navigate casually through the app.    Expected Result:    No crash.    Actual Result:    Intermittent crash.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: RSS Reader: intermittent crash on use with Fatal Signal 11 SIGSEGV
Description: """"When the RSS Reader Sample is used, there is an intermittent crash on use. Log attached. The crash occurred on a tab, so the back button was not a factor. It is unknown if this is a regression due to the intermittent and unpredictable nature of the issue. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Download the RSS Reader sample from studio and deploy on Android device. 2. Navigate casually through the app. Expected Result: No crash. Actual Result: Intermittent crash.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9212,12,"""MobileWeb: Label - wordWrap is not working""","""""""WordWrap was working in 2.0.1.GA2 but is not working in TiSDK 2.1.0.v20120522144410    h4. Steps to reproduce:  Step 1: run the code below  Step 2: notice that the text is not wrapping    {code:js}  var win  = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'green'  });  win.open();    var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({   text: """"""""One Two Three Four Five"""""""",   width: 100,   height: 50,   font: {fontSize: 16},   wordWrap: true,   backgroundColor: 'red'  });  win.add(label);  {code}  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Label - wordWrap is not working
Description: """"WordWrap was working in 2.0.1.GA2 but is not working in TiSDK 2.1.0.v20120522144410 h4. Steps to reproduce: Step 1: run the code below Step 2: notice that the text is not wrapping {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'green' }); win.open(); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: """"""""One Two Three Four Five"""""""", width: 100, height: 50, font: {fontSize: 16}, wordWrap: true, backgroundColor: 'red' }); win.add(label); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-9211,12,"""MobileWeb: Add support to Ti.UI.Slider for thumb, left, and right images""","""""""There are a couple things that are missing from Ti.UI.Slider:    * disabledLeftTrackImage  * disabledRightTrackImage  * disabledThumbImage  * highlightedLeftTrackImage  * highlightedRightTrackImage  * highlightedThumbImage  * leftTrackImage  * rightTrackImage  * selectedLeftTrackImage  * selectedRightTrackImage  * selectedThumbImage  * thumbImage    Also, the change event needs correct values for thumbOffset and thumbSize.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Add support to Ti.UI.Slider for thumb, left, and right images
Description: """"There are a couple things that are missing from Ti.UI.Slider: * disabledLeftTrackImage * disabledRightTrackImage * disabledThumbImage * highlightedLeftTrackImage * highlightedRightTrackImage * highlightedThumbImage * leftTrackImage * rightTrackImage * selectedLeftTrackImage * selectedRightTrackImage * selectedThumbImage * thumbImage Also, the change event needs correct values for thumbOffset and thumbSize.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9210,12,"""Android: OptionDialog - The last option from the dialog box is selected, and the label displays an unexpected value when radio button is not checked.""","""""""Description:  While testing Options Dialog I noticed that a label """"""""You selected 2 option"""""""" appears after I tapped """"""""Show Dialog1"""""""" button and then pressed Return button on the device (non of the radio buttons were checked).  Tap """"""""Show Dialog1"""""""" again displays a Dialog box (I am a title) with a checked radio button for Option 3, which is the last item on the list. Return displays the same label """"""""You selected 2 option""""""""    Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Base UI - Views - Options Dialog  3. Press """"""""Show Dialog1"""""""" button  4. Press Return Button on device    Expected Result:  Should see label """"""""No selection""""""""    Actual Result:  """"""""You selected 2 option"""""""" label is displayed       """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: OptionDialog - The last option from the dialog box is selected, and the label displays an unexpected value when radio button is not checked.
Description: """"Description: While testing Options Dialog I noticed that a label """"""""You selected 2 option"""""""" appears after I tapped """"""""Show Dialog1"""""""" button and then pressed Return button on the device (non of the radio buttons were checked). Tap """"""""Show Dialog1"""""""" again displays a Dialog box (I am a title) with a checked radio button for Option 3, which is the last item on the list. Return displays the same label """"""""You selected 2 option"""""""" Not a regression, the behavior exists on 2.0.1 as well Steps to reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Base UI - Views - Options Dialog 3. Press """"""""Show Dialog1"""""""" button 4. Press Return Button on device Expected Result: Should see label """"""""No selection"""""""" Actual Result: """"""""You selected 2 option"""""""" label is displayed """"",title+description
TIMOB-9209,12,"""Android: backgroundRepeat returns black view when using density images (xhdpi, hdpi etc...)""","""""""So I was trying to repeat a background, which always works. But when using density images (xhdpi, hdpi etc...) it's not working. It returns a black view.  To reproduce:  Put an image in your Resources directory, according to the docs: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/Using+density-specific+resources+on+Android    I have this code:  {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   navBarHidden : true,   exitOnClose : true  });  var logo = Ti.UI.createView({   left : 0,   top : 0,   right : 0,   height : """"""""44dp"""""""",   zIndex : 3,   backgroundImage : """"""""/images/barbg.png"""""""",      backgroundRepeat : true  });  win.add(logo);  win.open();  {code}  The view will be black instead of a repeated image.    Thanks!""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: backgroundRepeat returns black view when using density images (xhdpi, hdpi etc...)
Description: """"So I was trying to repeat a background, which always works. But when using density images (xhdpi, hdpi etc...) it's not working. It returns a black view. To reproduce: Put an image in your Resources directory, according to the docs: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/Using+density-specific+resources+on+Android I have this code: {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ navBarHidden : true, exitOnClose : true }); var logo = Ti.UI.createView({ left : 0, top : 0, right : 0, height : """"""""44dp"""""""", zIndex : 3, backgroundImage : """"""""/images/barbg.png"""""""", backgroundRepeat : true }); win.add(logo); win.open(); {code} The view will be black instead of a repeated image. Thanks!""""",title+description
TIMOB-9208,12,"""Android: Table view rows in Nook-KS have inconsistent alignment (kindle fire/nook) only""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch KS Nook  2. Click on Miscellaneous Tab (there should be no indentation on rows)  3. Click on another tab  4. Click on Miscellaneous Tab again (rows are slightly indented)      The problem is that we are setting the class name to """"""""normal"""""""" inside rowProxyFor() in TableViewProxy.  If we don't set the classname to normal there, we get the bug TIMOB-9189.  We need to figure out a way to fix this behavior without causing TIMOB-9189.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Table view rows in Nook-KS have inconsistent alignment (kindle fire/nook) only
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch KS Nook 2. Click on Miscellaneous Tab (there should be no indentation on rows) 3. Click on another tab 4. Click on Miscellaneous Tab again (rows are slightly indented) The problem is that we are setting the class name to """"""""normal"""""""" inside rowProxyFor() in TableViewProxy. If we don't set the classname to normal there, we get the bug TIMOB-9189. We need to figure out a way to fix this behavior without causing TIMOB-9189. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9207,12,"""Android: Animation Center Parity and Jerkiness""","""""""h1. Problem  When animating a view on Android through the transform property, the top left of the view is used, unlike on iOS where the center is used. Also, chained animations result in a jerky, unsmooth transition.    h2. Reproduction  On iOS, this results in a blue box shrinking to 20% its size, then growing to 180%, then shrinking smoothly down to 20%, and so on, always centered. On Android, it shrinks to 20%, to the top left corner. Then it jumps to 100% size, and grows to 180%. Then it jumps to 100%, leaving the splash screen image visible through the white window, and shrinks to 20% the size.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: '#fff'  });    var box = Ti.UI.createView({      backgroundColor: 'blue',      width: 100, height: 100  });  win.add(box);    var shrink = Ti.UI.createAnimation({      transform: Ti.UI.create2DMatrix().scale(0.2, 0.2),      duration: 1000  });  function doShrink() {      box.animate(shrink);  }  shrink.addEventListener('complete', doGrow);    var grow = Ti.UI.createAnimation({      transform: Ti.UI.create2DMatrix().scale(1.8, 1.8),      duration: 1000  });  function doGrow() {      box.animate(grow);  }  grow.addEventListener('complete', doShrink);    win.addEventListener('open', doShrink);    win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Animation Center Parity and Jerkiness
Description: """"h1. Problem When animating a view on Android through the transform property, the top left of the view is used, unlike on iOS where the center is used. Also, chained animations result in a jerky, unsmooth transition. h2. Reproduction On iOS, this results in a blue box shrinking to 20% its size, then growing to 180%, then shrinking smoothly down to 20%, and so on, always centered. On Android, it shrinks to 20%, to the top left corner. Then it jumps to 100% size, and grows to 180%. Then it jumps to 100%, leaving the splash screen image visible through the white window, and shrinks to 20% the size. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var box = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'blue', width: 100, height: 100 }); win.add(box); var shrink = Ti.UI.createAnimation({ transform: Ti.UI.create2DMatrix().scale(0.2, 0.2), duration: 1000 }); function doShrink() { box.animate(shrink); } shrink.addEventListener('complete', doGrow); var grow = Ti.UI.createAnimation({ transform: Ti.UI.create2DMatrix().scale(1.8, 1.8), duration: 1000 }); function doGrow() { box.animate(grow); } grow.addEventListener('complete', doShrink); win.addEventListener('open', doShrink); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-9206,12,"""Android: Scroll View Touch Listeners Prevent Scrolling""","""""""h1. Problem  Adding a touch listener to a scroll view on Android prevents the scroll view from being scrollable. Although the events do then fire, they fire with the scroll view always as the source. This is inconsistent with iOS.    h2. Expected Behavior  It should behave as iOS does. The events should fire, and the scroll view should scroll. Further, the source should be the most deeply child touchable view, like on iOS.    h2. Reproduction  Drop the following in an app.js. It adds a vertically scrollable list of draggable rectangles. On iOS, you can drag them horizontally. On Android, you can't drag them anywhere, or even scroll the scroll view.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: '#fff'  });  var scroll = Ti.UI.createScrollView({      scrollType: 'vertical',      contentHeight: 3010,      text: 'Scroll View'  });  var width = 150, height = 90;  for (var i = 0; i < 30; i++) {      scroll.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({          draggable: true,          text: 'Drag Me Horizontally ' + (i + 1), textAlign: 'center',          color: '#000',          top: i * 100 + 10,          width: width, height: height,          backgroundColor: '#eee'      }));  }  scroll.addEventListener('touchstart', doDrag);  scroll.addEventListener('touchmove', doDrag);  scroll.addEventListener('touchcancel', doDrag);  scroll.addEventListener('touchend', doDrag);  function doDrag(evt) {      Ti.API.info('Event Fired On: ' + evt.source.text);      if (evt.source.draggable) {          var global = evt.source.convertPointToView({ x: evt.x, y: evt.y }, scroll);          evt.source.updateLayout({              left: global.x - width / 2          });      }  }  win.add(scroll);  win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Scroll View Touch Listeners Prevent Scrolling
Description: """"h1. Problem Adding a touch listener to a scroll view on Android prevents the scroll view from being scrollable. Although the events do then fire, they fire with the scroll view always as the source. This is inconsistent with iOS. h2. Expected Behavior It should behave as iOS does. The events should fire, and the scroll view should scroll. Further, the source should be the most deeply child touchable view, like on iOS. h2. Reproduction Drop the following in an app.js. It adds a vertically scrollable list of draggable rectangles. On iOS, you can drag them horizontally. On Android, you can't drag them anywhere, or even scroll the scroll view. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var scroll = Ti.UI.createScrollView({ scrollType: 'vertical', contentHeight: 3010, text: 'Scroll View' }); var width = 150, height = 90; for (var i = 0; i < 30; i++) { scroll.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ draggable: true, text: 'Drag Me Horizontally ' + (i + 1), textAlign: 'center', color: '#000', top: i * 100 + 10, width: width, height: height, backgroundColor: '#eee' })); } scroll.addEventListener('touchstart', doDrag); scroll.addEventListener('touchmove', doDrag); scroll.addEventListener('touchcancel', doDrag); scroll.addEventListener('touchend', doDrag); function doDrag(evt) { Ti.API.info('Event Fired On: ' + evt.source.text); if (evt.source.draggable) { var global = evt.source.convertPointToView({ x: evt.x, y: evt.y }, scroll); evt.source.updateLayout({ left: global.x - width / 2 }); } } win.add(scroll); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
