TIMOB-9193,12,"""iOS: Windows opened with NavGroup don't fire open or focus events""","""""""h2.Problem description  Windows opened with a NavigationGroup don't fire their open or focus events at all. This is regression: was working well with v2.0.1.GA    h2.Steps to reproduce and sample code  Create an app (see following sample) that opens a window with a NavigationGroup; two events should be fired ('focus' and 'open'), but they aren't.    app.js    win1.js        Expected Result  3 console log lines:      set simple event listeners successfully      open event      focus event    Actual Result  1 console log line:      set simple event listeners successfully  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Windows opened with NavGroup don't fire open or focus events
Description: """"h2.Problem description Windows opened with a NavigationGroup don't fire their open or focus events at all. This is regression: was working well with v2.0.1.GA h2.Steps to reproduce and sample code Create an app (see following sample) that opens a window with a NavigationGroup; two events should be fired ('focus' and 'open'), but they aren't. app.js win1.js Expected Result 3 console log lines: set simple event listeners successfully open event focus event Actual Result 1 console log line: set simple event listeners successfully """"",title+description
TIMOB-9192,12,"""iOS: Repeated background image (@2x version) doesn't display correctly on a retina device.""","""""""When a repeated background image is used and a @2x graphic is supplied for retina devices, the @2x image doesn't display correctly.  h4. Repo Steps  1. Run the below code in your app.js  2. Copy the attached images to the resources folder of your project.  3. In the BG Repeat tab you can see the pixellated image.     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Repeated background image (@2x version) doesn't display correctly on a retina device.
Description: """"When a repeated background image is used and a @2x graphic is supplied for retina devices, the @2x image doesn't display correctly. h4. Repo Steps 1. Run the below code in your app.js 2. Copy the attached images to the resources folder of your project. 3. In the BG Repeat tab you can see the pixellated image. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9191,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.View backgroundLeftCap backgroundTopCap Broken on Retina Displays""","""""""h1. Problem  The backgroundLeftCap is broken on Ti.UI.Views on Retina displays. It works fine on Ti.UI.Buttons.    h2. Reproduction  Drop the following in an app.js, and download the two attached images.    Note that the two search.png and <EMAIL> images are color coded so you can see that it is consistently using the @2x image on the Retina device, it's just messing up (miscalculating?) the stretching somehow.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: '#fff'  });  // WORKS: buttons backgrounds stretch properly on Retina displays!  win.add(Ti.UI.createButton({      top: 10, right: 10, left: 10,      height: 30,      // """"""""search.png"""""""" is:      // - On Non-Retina: 35x30      // - On Retina: 70x60      backgroundImage: 'search.png',      // 35 / 2 = 17.5, so use 17, 34 pixels for the edges, with 1 pixel to repeat in the middle.      backgroundLeftCap: 17  }));  // FAILS: ends up distorted on the left and right caps on Retina displays!  win.add(Ti.UI.createView({      top: 50, right: 10, left: 10,      height: 30,      backgroundImage: 'search.png',      backgroundLeftCap: 17  }));  win.open();  {code}    h2. Workaround  Use buttons with their touch disabled as backgrounds. Weird, a bit heavier, but... whatever.    h2. Screenshot  Attached as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.View backgroundLeftCap backgroundTopCap Broken on Retina Displays
Description: """"h1. Problem The backgroundLeftCap is broken on Ti.UI.Views on Retina displays. It works fine on Ti.UI.Buttons. h2. Reproduction Drop the following in an app.js, and download the two attached images. Note that the two search.png and <EMAIL> images are color coded so you can see that it is consistently using the @2x image on the Retina device, it's just messing up (miscalculating?) the stretching somehow. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); // WORKS: buttons backgrounds stretch properly on Retina displays! win.add(Ti.UI.createButton({ top: 10, right: 10, left: 10, height: 30, // """"""""search.png"""""""" is: // - On Non-Retina: 35x30 // - On Retina: 70x60 backgroundImage: 'search.png', // 35 / 2 = 17.5, so use 17, 34 pixels for the edges, with 1 pixel to repeat in the middle. backgroundLeftCap: 17 })); // FAILS: ends up distorted on the left and right caps on Retina displays! win.add(Ti.UI.createView({ top: 50, right: 10, left: 10, height: 30, backgroundImage: 'search.png', backgroundLeftCap: 17 })); win.open(); {code} h2. Workaround Use buttons with their touch disabled as backgrounds. Weird, a bit heavier, but... whatever. h2. Screenshot Attached as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9190,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.API causes WP7.5 to break""","""""""The contents of Ti.API causes the module to not load on WP7.5, which causes the app itself to never load.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.API causes WP7.5 to break
