TIMOB-9163,12,"""Anvil:  create working harness manager sub component and base harness for Android""","""""""Create working harness manager sub component that allows for multiplatform expansion and built in CLI.  Should be able to generate harness for Android, install, launch and get test results back.  Base harness should be able to run test suites and return results to harness manager subcomponent over tcp server.    Communication with hub, mw integration, iOS integration and test creation is not included in the scope of this task.""""""",Story,"Title: Anvil: create working harness manager sub component and base harness for Android
Description: """"Create working harness manager sub component that allows for multiplatform expansion and built in CLI. Should be able to generate harness for Android, install, launch and get test results back. Base harness should be able to run test suites and return results to harness manager subcomponent over tcp server. Communication with hub, mw integration, iOS integration and test creation is not included in the scope of this task.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9161,12,"""Ti API: Blob.type is exposed as property, but type values are not exposed as constants""","""""""Near as I can tell, both Android and iOS expose the Blob.type property, but not the constants for the type values (TYPE_IMAGE, TYPE_DATA, etc.)    At present, type is not documented in Blob.yml because it's not terribly useful without the constants. I think we should either expose the constants or not expose the 'type' property.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti API: Blob.type is exposed as property, but type values are not exposed as constants
Description: """"Near as I can tell, both Android and iOS expose the Blob.type property, but not the constants for the type values (TYPE_IMAGE, TYPE_DATA, etc.) At present, type is not documented in Blob.yml because it's not terribly useful without the constants. I think we should either expose the constants or not expose the 'type' property.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9160,12,"""Android: Font sizing should obey the ti.ui.defaultunit setting in tiapp.xml""","""""""h1. Expected results:    I can set the ti.ui.defaultunit property in tiapp.xml to 'dip' and have font sizes respect that setting.    h2. Actual results:    I can explicitly set fontSize='14dip' and text will be sized appropriately. But setting the default unit in tiapp.xml and setting fontSize=14 gives px based font sizing.    See the attached screen: <property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""" type=""""""""string"""""""">dip</property> is included in the tiapp.xml file, the field labels (URL, Username, etc.) are set with fontSize=## whereas the contents of the first text field is set with fontSize='14dip'    Tested on my Galaxy Nexus running ICS/4.0.2. I'm using the https://github.com/gshipley/BeerShift application featured in the developer blog.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Font sizing should obey the ti.ui.defaultunit setting in tiapp.xml
Description: """"h1. Expected results: I can set the ti.ui.defaultunit property in tiapp.xml to 'dip' and have font sizes respect that setting. h2. Actual results: I can explicitly set fontSize='14dip' and text will be sized appropriately. But setting the default unit in tiapp.xml and setting fontSize=14 gives px based font sizing. See the attached screen: <property name=""""""""ti.ui.defaultunit"""""""" type=""""""""string"""""""">dip</property> is included in the tiapp.xml file, the field labels (URL, Username, etc.) are set with fontSize=## whereas the contents of the first text field is set with fontSize='14dip' Tested on my Galaxy Nexus running ICS/4.0.2. I'm using the https://github.com/gshipley/BeerShift application featured in the developer blog.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9159,12,"""Ti API: Easier way to convert between Blobs and Buffers""","""""""To go from a Buffer to a Blob we have Buffer.toBlob. However, there's no matching Blob.toBuffer. This would be handy since Buffers are more easily mutable than blobs, and some methods only accept one type or the other.    I think the current workaround for Blob > Buffer is something like:        This is muy ugly. It seems like it would be a lot simpler to add support for creating a buffer from a Blob in Ti.createBuffer:        """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Easier way to convert between Blobs and Buffers
Description: """"To go from a Buffer to a Blob we have Buffer.toBlob. However, there's no matching Blob.toBuffer. This would be handy since Buffers are more easily mutable than blobs, and some methods only accept one type or the other. I think the current workaround for Blob > Buffer is something like: This is muy ugly. It seems like it would be a lot simpler to add support for creating a buffer from a Blob in Ti.createBuffer: """"",title+description
