TIMOB-9138,12,"""Tooling: Unlicensed module error on existing projects""","""""""When a user purchases a module from the marketplace and tries to use it with an existing project, it doesn't work and shows the 'unlicensed module error' screen. It works fine if you create a new project and add the module to it.    A workaround is to create a new project and copy/paste the existing resource files into the new project, however this is not acceptable and shouldn't be happening.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: Unlicensed module error on existing projects
Description: """"When a user purchases a module from the marketplace and tries to use it with an existing project, it doesn't work and shows the 'unlicensed module error' screen. It works fine if you create a new project and add the module to it. A workaround is to create a new project and copy/paste the existing resource files into the new project, however this is not acceptable and shouldn't be happening.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9137,12,"""iOS: TableView scroll event contentOffset returning 0""","""""""h6.Issue  As the title    h6.Tested on  iOS simulator    h6.Expected behavior  Pull down to refresh works in Titanium SDKs 2.0.x    h6.Current behavior  Pull down to refresh doesn't works in Titanium SDKs 2.1.x    h6.Steps to reproduce  1. Run Kitchen Sink demos  2. Go to sample: Base UI tab > Views > TableViews > Pull to refresh     h6.Titanium SDK version: 2.0.2 (05/10/12 22:31 82d3920)      h6.Titanium SDK version: 2.1.0 (05/02/12 17:33 85e7af3)      h6.contentOffset  http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.TableView-event-scrollEnd""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView scroll event contentOffset returning 0
Description: """"h6.Issue As the title h6.Tested on iOS simulator h6.Expected behavior Pull down to refresh works in Titanium SDKs 2.0.x h6.Current behavior Pull down to refresh doesn't works in Titanium SDKs 2.1.x h6.Steps to reproduce 1. Run Kitchen Sink demos 2. Go to sample: Base UI tab > Views > TableViews > Pull to refresh h6.Titanium SDK version: 2.0.2 (05/10/12 22:31 82d3920) h6.Titanium SDK version: 2.1.0 (05/02/12 17:33 85e7af3) h6.contentOffset http://docs.<USER>com/titanium/2.0/index.html#!/api/Titanium.UI.TableView-event-scrollEnd""""",title+description
TIMOB-9136,12,"""iOS: Ti.Media.AudioPlayer audio only in right channel""","""""""h4. Issue  ----    On iOS 5.0+ only, the sound produced by Ti.Media.AudioPlayer (with default settings) only comes out of the right channel of a headset. The behavior (stereo sound) is correct on the 4.3.5 simulator, so this may be an Apple bug or behavior change between major versions.    h4. Testing  ----    You're going to want a pair of headphones for this one.    Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Sound -> Remote Streaming -> """"""""Start Streaming""""""""    *PASS:* Sound comes from both channels  *FAIL:* Sound from right (or left) channel only""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Media.AudioPlayer audio only in right channel
Description: """"h4. Issue ---- On iOS 5.0+ only, the sound produced by Ti.Media.AudioPlayer (with default settings) only comes out of the right channel of a headset. The behavior (stereo sound) is correct on the 4.3.5 simulator, so this may be an Apple bug or behavior change between major versions. h4. Testing ---- You're going to want a pair of headphones for this one. Kitchen Sink -> Phone -> Sound -> Remote Streaming -> """"""""Start Streaming"""""""" *PASS:* Sound comes from both channels *FAIL:* Sound from right (or left) channel only""""",title+description
TIMOB-9135,12,"""iOS: Customize tab group""","""""""Since iOS5+ supports customizing tabgroup like changing the background color by """"""""tintColor"""""""" property, our platform should provide similar functions to let customers do those in Titanium as well.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Customize tab group
Description: """"Since iOS5+ supports customizing tabgroup like changing the background color by """"""""tintColor"""""""" property, our platform should provide similar functions to let customers do those in Titanium as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9134,12,"""BlackBerry: Detect spaces in temp directory when running unit tests when they are hidden by 8.3 format in Windows""","""""""Currently the unit tests create a temp project folder in the temp folder, but the default location on Windows XP (or if the user changed it) contains spaces. For some reason python receives this in 8.3 format (eg C:\DOCUME~1\<username>\LOCALS~1\Temp and there doesn't seem to be a built-in python way to expand the string to detect spaces. The build fails when there are spaces so this should be fixed.  Note: the default temp folder on Windows 7 (and probably Vista) is fine: C:\Users\<username>\AppData\Local\Temp""""""",Story,"Title: BlackBerry: Detect spaces in temp directory when running unit tests when they are hidden by 8.3 format in Windows
Description: """"Currently the unit tests create a temp project folder in the temp folder, but the default location on Windows XP (or if the user changed it) contains spaces. For some reason python receives this in 8.3 format (eg C:\DOCUME~1\<username>\LOCALS~1\Temp and there doesn't seem to be a built-in python way to expand the string to detect spaces. The build fails when there are spaces so this should be fixed. Note: the default temp folder on Windows 7 (and probably Vista) is fine: C:\Users\<username>\AppData\Local\Temp""""",title+description
TIMOB-9132,12,"""Android: Maps V2 Module - Feature to allow modifications to the android mapview zoom buttons""","""""""It has been requested to add a new feature to Android Mapview that would allow the modification of zoom controls such as changing the position, hide/show the zoom control, set the size of the control.    According to the Android Developer doc:     http://developer.android.com/reference/android/widget/ZoomButtonsController.html    The ZoomButtonController class has this functionality.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Maps V2 Module - Feature to allow modifications to the android mapview zoom buttons
Description: """"It has been requested to add a new feature to Android Mapview that would allow the modification of zoom controls such as changing the position, hide/show the zoom control, set the size of the control. According to the Android Developer doc: http://developer.android.com/reference/android/widget/ZoomButtonsController.html The ZoomButtonController class has this functionality. """"",title+description
TIMOB-9131,12,"""MobileWeb: Apps do not load if the Google Maps server are inaccessible.""","""""""When the google maps server cannot be accessed, such as when developing locally w/o internet, the app fails to load.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Apps do not load if the Google Maps server are inaccessible.
Description: """"When the google maps server cannot be accessed, such as when developing locally w/o internet, the app fails to load.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9130,12,"""Android: FastDev: old module versions appear to be included in app apk""","""""""When an android project containing two versions of the same module is redeployed to the emulator using a different module version without cleaning the project, it appears both modules are included in the app.apk.    app.apk size with one module version: 5.5 MB  app.apk size with both module versions and project cleaning between deployments: 5.5 MB  app.apk size with both module versions when packaged for distribution: 5.5 MB    app.apk size with both module versions and no project cleaning between deployments: 6.2 MB    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create a new Titanium Mobile project with Android selected.  2. Create a new Android Module with version set to 1.0.  3. Package the module to the project.  4. In the module """"""""manifest"""""""" file, change the version to 2.0.  5. Package the module to the project (again).    There should now be a 1.0 and 2.0 version of the module in the project modules directory.    6. Copy the example app.js from the module to the project.  7. Clean the project.  8. Deploy project to emulator.  9. Check the app.apk size.  10. Change the module version in the project tiapp.xml to 1.0 (it was 2.0).  11. Without cleaning, deploy project to emulator.  10. Check the app.apk size.    Expected Result:    Both app.apk sizes should be identical.    Actual Result:    app.apk size is larger if the project is not cleaned and the module version is changed for the second emulator deployment.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: FastDev: old module versions appear to be included in app apk
Description: """"When an android project containing two versions of the same module is redeployed to the emulator using a different module version without cleaning the project, it appears both modules are included in the app.apk. app.apk size with one module version: 5.5 MB app.apk size with both module versions and project cleaning between deployments: 5.5 MB app.apk size with both module versions when packaged for distribution: 5.5 MB app.apk size with both module versions and no project cleaning between deployments: 6.2 MB Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new Titanium Mobile project with Android selected. 2. Create a new Android Module with version set to 1.0. 3. Package the module to the project. 4. In the module """"""""manifest"""""""" file, change the version to 2.0. 5. Package the module to the project (again). There should now be a 1.0 and 2.0 version of the module in the project modules directory. 6. Copy the example app.js from the module to the project. 7. Clean the project. 8. Deploy project to emulator. 9. Check the app.apk size. 10. Change the module version in the project tiapp.xml to 1.0 (it was 2.0). 11. Without cleaning, deploy project to emulator. 10. Check the app.apk size. Expected Result: Both app.apk sizes should be identical. Actual Result: app.apk size is larger if the project is not cleaned and the module version is changed for the second emulator deployment.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9129,12,"""iOS: Titanium.NavGroup - Navbar comes in partial size after orientation is changed""","""""""Description:  Navbar comes in partial size after orientation is changed from portrait to landscape mode.  This bug exists on 2.0.1 as well.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run the following code:    2. Press the """"""""poke me to open the next window"""""""" label   3. Rotate device to the lanscape mode    Expected result:  The navbar should fill all width of the screen    Actual result:  Navbar comes in partial size """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.NavGroup - Navbar comes in partial size after orientation is changed
