TIMOB-9090,12,"""iOS: Timing out waiting on main thread causing rejections""","""""""h6.Issue  We got a report about an app rejected due time out issue, most likely the splash screen. Along with many other non less important quantity of developers.    Unfortunately I have little data available at this time to reliable reproduce this. Its needed some more research in order to validate due this generation mechanism.    h6.Apple App Store - Summary Report      h6.Community thread  http://developer.<USER>com/question/136335/timing-out-waiting-on-main-thread-possibly-a-deadlock    h6.Related jira issues  https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-8516""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Timing out waiting on main thread causing rejections
Description: """"h6.Issue We got a report about an app rejected due time out issue, most likely the splash screen. Along with many other non less important quantity of developers. Unfortunately I have little data available at this time to reliable reproduce this. Its needed some more research in order to validate due this generation mechanism. h6.Apple App Store - Summary Report h6.Community thread http://developer.<USER>com/question/136335/timing-out-waiting-on-main-thread-possibly-a-deadlock h6.Related jira issues https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-8516""""",title+description
TIMOB-9088,12,"""iOS: Remove AudioStreamerBC""","""""""Due to incompatibilities between iOS 3.x and 4.x+ with regards to audio streaming capability, iOS currently has two """"""""AudioStreamer"""""""" classes which are interfaced with through a generic frontend. One of these, {{AudioStreamerBC}}, is for 3.x-compatibility purposes only and should be removed since it is dead code.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Remove AudioStreamerBC
Description: """"Due to incompatibilities between iOS 3.x and 4.x+ with regards to audio streaming capability, iOS currently has two """"""""AudioStreamer"""""""" classes which are interfaced with through a generic frontend. One of these, {{AudioStreamerBC}}, is for 3.x-compatibility purposes only and should be removed since it is dead code.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9087,12,"""iOS: Remove """"deprecated"""" properties""","""""""iOS has a disturbingly large number of """"""""deprecated"""""""" properties and functions hanging around in the API, some of which have been deprecated since 1.6 (and declared to have been """"""""removed"""""""" in 1.8). As a first step in codebase evaluation and maintenance, these deprecated properties/methods/classes should be removed.    Any property which is stated to have been removed in 1.9 or earlier should be removed from the codebase, and the documentation updated accordingly.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Remove """"deprecated"""" properties
Description: """"iOS has a disturbingly large number of """"""""deprecated"""""""" properties and functions hanging around in the API, some of which have been deprecated since 1.6 (and declared to have been """"""""removed"""""""" in 1.8). As a first step in codebase evaluation and maintenance, these deprecated properties/methods/classes should be removed. Any property which is stated to have been removed in 1.9 or earlier should be removed from the codebase, and the documentation updated accordingly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9086,12,"""Android: Tooling: project name not respected when creating new module""","""""""When creating a new module from either the command line or studio, the specified name is not respected. It is replaced by """"""""titanium-<lowercase_name>"""""""". However, the project is initially created with a correct project directory name.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create an android module (remove it from the project explorer if created in studio).  2. Import the module into studio (note: the module may have to be removed from the workspace directory first).    Expected Result:    The project name should be the one specified during creation (and the module directory name).    Actual Result:    The project name is """"""""titanium-<lowercase_name>"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tooling: project name not respected when creating new module
Description: """"When creating a new module from either the command line or studio, the specified name is not respected. It is replaced by """"""""titanium-<lowercase_name>"""""""". However, the project is initially created with a correct project directory name. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create an android module (remove it from the project explorer if created in studio). 2. Import the module into studio (note: the module may have to be removed from the workspace directory first). Expected Result: The project name should be the one specified during creation (and the module directory name). Actual Result: The project name is """"""""titanium-<lowercase_name>"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-9085,12,"""iOS: """"this"""" value in event listener is set to child component when child component is clicked""","""""""h2. Problem  """"""""this"""""""" value in event listener is set to child component when child component is clicked.    h2. Steps to reproduce        Result: Click on the button and see the output. """"""""this"""""""" value produces """"""""[object TiUIButton]"""""""".    Expected result: """"""""this"""""""" inside event listener should point to UI object to which that listener is attached (the output should produce """"""""[object TiUIView]"""""""").    This works as expected on Android.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: """"this"""" value in event listener is set to child component when child component is clicked
Description: """"h2. Problem """"""""this"""""""" value in event listener is set to child component when child component is clicked. h2. Steps to reproduce Result: Click on the button and see the output. """"""""this"""""""" value produces """"""""[object TiUIButton]"""""""". Expected result: """"""""this"""""""" inside event listener should point to UI object to which that listener is attached (the output should produce """"""""[object TiUIView]""""""""). This works as expected on Android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9084,12,"""iOS: XML xmlns:xmlns definition""","""""""h1. Problem  When defining namespaces, xmlns:xmlns is explicitly defined. This isn't a valid definition, and if it isn't stripped out, other xml validators or libraries will choke on it.    h2. Workaround  Stringify the XML and rip out the xmlns:xmlns attribute.    h2. Reproduction  {code:title=app.js}  (function (document, Ti) {      document = document || Ti && Ti.XML.parseString('<a/>');        function xmlAddNamespaceAttribute(domNode, name, attributeNamespace) {          var doc = domNode.ownerDocument || document;          var attribute = doc.createAttributeNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/xmlns/', name);          attribute.nodeValue = attributeNamespace;          (domNode.documentElement || domNode).setAttributeNode(attribute);      }        var feed = document.implementation.createDocument('http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom', 'atom:feed', null);      xmlAddNamespaceAttribute(feed, """"""""xmlns:m"""""""", 'http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices/metadata');      xmlAddNamespaceAttribute(feed, """"""""xmlns:d"""""""", 'http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices');        var expected = '<?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>\              <atom:feed xmlns:atom=""""""""http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom""""""""\              xmlns:m=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices/metadata""""""""\              xmlns:d=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices""""""""/>'.replace(/\s{1,}/ig, ' ').replace(/> </ig, '><');        var actual = '<?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>' + ((Ti && Ti.XML) || new XMLSerializer()).serializeToString(feed);        if (Ti) {          Ti.API.info('Expected:\n' + expected);          Ti.API.info('Actual:\n' + actual);      }      else {          console.log('Expected:\n' + expected);          console.log('Actual:\n' + actual);      }        if (expected != actual) {          alert('FAIL! Check logs for more information.');      }      else {          alert('PASS!');      }  })(this['document'], this['Ti']);      Actual XML results:  {code:title=actual.xml}  <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>  <atom:feed xmlns:xmlns=""""""""http://www.w3.org/2000/xmlns/""""""""       xmlns:m=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices/metadata""""""""       xmlns:d=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices""""""""/>  {code}    Discrepancies:  - xmlns:xmlns  - absence of xmlns:atom""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: XML xmlns:xmlns definition
Description: """"h1. Problem When defining namespaces, xmlns:xmlns is explicitly defined. This isn't a valid definition, and if it isn't stripped out, other xml validators or libraries will choke on it. h2. Workaround Stringify the XML and rip out the xmlns:xmlns attribute. h2. Reproduction {code:title=app.js} (function (document, Ti) { document = document || Ti && Ti.XML.parseString('<a/>'); function xmlAddNamespaceAttribute(domNode, name, attributeNamespace) { var doc = domNode.ownerDocument || document; var attribute = doc.createAttributeNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/xmlns/', name); attribute.nodeValue = attributeNamespace; (domNode.documentElement || domNode).setAttributeNode(attribute); } var feed = document.implementation.createDocument('http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom', 'atom:feed', null); xmlAddNamespaceAttribute(feed, """"""""xmlns:m"""""""", 'http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices/metadata'); xmlAddNamespaceAttribute(feed, """"""""xmlns:d"""""""", 'http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices'); var expected = '<?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>\ <atom:feed xmlns:atom=""""""""http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom""""""""\ xmlns:m=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices/metadata""""""""\ xmlns:d=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices""""""""/>'.replace(/\s{1,}/ig, ' ').replace(/> </ig, '><'); var actual = '<?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>' + ((Ti && Ti.XML) || new XMLSerializer()).serializeToString(feed); if (Ti) { Ti.API.info('Expected:\n' + expected); Ti.API.info('Actual:\n' + actual); } else { console.log('Expected:\n' + expected); console.log('Actual:\n' + actual); } if (expected != actual) { alert('FAIL! Check logs for more information.'); } else { alert('PASS!'); } })(this['document'], this['Ti']); Actual XML results: {code:title=actual.xml} <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?> <atom:feed xmlns:xmlns=""""""""http://www.w3.org/2000/xmlns/"""""""" xmlns:m=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices/metadata"""""""" xmlns:d=""""""""http://schemas.microsoft.com/ado/2007/08/dataservices""""""""/> {code} Discrepancies: - xmlns:xmlns - absence of xmlns:atom""""",title+description
TIMOB-9083,12,"""iOS: barImage does not resize as per the orientation ""","""""""h3. Problem and Steps to Reproduce    Start the image in iPad/iPhone simulator. The barImage added to a window looks fine in portrait mode when the app starts, but when changing the orientation to landscape, the barImage that shows is still of the portrait size. However, if the tabs are switched in landscape mode the barImage looks fine. Then, if we go back to portrait the image isn't scaled right again until the tabs are switched again.    Please find attached the sample code.     h3. Expected Behavior    The barImage should scale according to the orientation.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: barImage does not resize as per the orientation
Description: """"h3. Problem and Steps to Reproduce Start the image in iPad/iPhone simulator. The barImage added to a window looks fine in portrait mode when the app starts, but when changing the orientation to landscape, the barImage that shows is still of the portrait size. However, if the tabs are switched in landscape mode the barImage looks fine. Then, if we go back to portrait the image isn't scaled right again until the tabs are switched again. Please find attached the sample code. h3. Expected Behavior The barImage should scale according to the orientation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9082,12,"""MobileWeb: Slider Parity""","""""""IOS and android have default values of 0 and 1 for min and max and both support fractional values. MW should have the same.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Slider Parity
Description: """"IOS and android have default values of 0 and 1 for min and max and both support fractional values. MW should have the same.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9081,12,"""iOS: Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer - Audio Player keeps playing after leaving test case, and you cannot stop or pause streaming  when running test case second time""","""""""Description:   While testing Media module, I noticed, that audio player keeps playing music after leaving test case by pressing """"""""Done"""""""" button. Also, when you run test case one more time, buttons """"""""Pause Streaming"""""""" and """"""""Start/Stop Streaming"""""""" do not work anymore, and music keeps playing.   This bug also exists on 2.0.1.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Run attached code  2. Press """"""""Start Streaming""""""""  3. Press """"""""Done"""""""" button  4. Run test case one more time  5. Press """"""""Pause Streaming""""""""  6. Press """"""""Start/Stop Streaming""""""""    Expected result:  - after step 3 - Player should stop play music  - after step 5 - Should be able to pause streaming  - after step 6 - Should be able to stop streaming    Actual result:  - after step 3 - Player keeps playing music  - after step 5 - Unable to pause streaming  - after step 6 - Unable to stop streaming""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer - Audio Player keeps playing after leaving test case, and you cannot stop or pause streaming when running test case second time
Description: """"Description: While testing Media module, I noticed, that audio player keeps playing music after leaving test case by pressing """"""""Done"""""""" button. Also, when you run test case one more time, buttons """"""""Pause Streaming"""""""" and """"""""Start/Stop Streaming"""""""" do not work anymore, and music keeps playing. This bug also exists on 2.0.1. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run attached code 2. Press """"""""Start Streaming"""""""" 3. Press """"""""Done"""""""" button 4. Run test case one more time 5. Press """"""""Pause Streaming"""""""" 6. Press """"""""Start/Stop Streaming"""""""" Expected result: - after step 3 - Player should stop play music - after step 5 - Should be able to pause streaming - after step 6 - Should be able to stop streaming Actual result: - after step 3 - Player keeps playing music - after step 5 - Unable to pause streaming - after step 6 - Unable to stop streaming""""",title+description
TIMOB-9080,12,"""iOS: send navigationType when beforeload event is fired in iOS webview""","""""""Implement UIWebViewNavigationType such that the beforeload event will include this in its parameters    http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/uikit/reference/UIWebView_Class/Reference/Reference.html    Test case:      """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: send navigationType when beforeload event is fired in iOS webview
Description: """"Implement UIWebViewNavigationType such that the beforeload event will include this in its parameters http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/uikit/reference/UIWebView_Class/Reference/Reference.html Test case: """"",title+description
TIMOB-9079,12,"""Tooling: Organize """"Resources"""" folder with a """"platforms"""" directory""","""""""It would make the {{Resources}} folder in a Titanium project much cleaner if we had a {{platforms}} folder, under which all specific platform folders, like {{iphone}}, {{android}}, {{mobileweb}}, would reside. It just makes for less clutter in the overall project.    While they serve 2 different purposes, we may also want to consider condensing what can be done with the root-level {{platform}} directory, and what can be done in the {{Resources/PLATFORM}} directories. Just throwing ideas out for discussion, but perhaps a layout like this would work...    * Resources  ** app.js  ** platform  *** android  **** native  ***** AndroidManifest.xml  ***** res  ****** values  ******* strings.xml  **** project  ***** app.js  *** iphone  *** mobileweb    This is probably not an ideal layout, but it gives an idea of how we can organize all platform-specific elements in one location without continue to crowd the project structure.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Organize """"Resources"""" folder with a """"platforms"""" directory
Description: """"It would make the {{Resources}} folder in a Titanium project much cleaner if we had a {{platforms}} folder, under which all specific platform folders, like {{iphone}}, {{android}}, {{mobileweb}}, would reside. It just makes for less clutter in the overall project. While they serve 2 different purposes, we may also want to consider condensing what can be done with the root-level {{platform}} directory, and what can be done in the {{Resources/PLATFORM}} directories. Just throwing ideas out for discussion, but perhaps a layout like this would work... * Resources ** app.js ** platform *** android **** native ***** AndroidManifest.xml ***** res ****** values ******* strings.xml **** project ***** app.js *** iphone *** mobileweb This is probably not an ideal layout, but it gives an idea of how we can organize all platform-specific elements in one location without continue to crowd the project structure. """"",title+description
