TIMOB-9073,12,"""MobileWeb: Implement Mobile Web specific annotations""","""""""The annotations are using Google's, but this has 2 disadvantages: 1) We don't support left/right button views and 2) doesn't look like iOS or Android.    We should be able to build the annotations using Ti.UI.Views. For the callout arrow, we could use a CSS solution like this: http://cssarrowplease.com/.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Implement Mobile Web specific annotations
Description: """"The annotations are using Google's, but this has 2 disadvantages: 1) We don't support left/right button views and 2) doesn't look like iOS or Android. We should be able to build the annotations using Ti.UI.Views. For the callout arrow, we could use a CSS solution like this: http://cssarrowplease.com/.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9072,12,"""iOS: Compiled CommonJS modules failing link""","""""""It looks like commonjs module compiles for iOS are currently failing because the `filterData` function is not being properly exported as part of {{libtiverify}}.    Relevant build log error, for device:        Note that the device builds (armv6, armv7) indicate C++ name mangling; builds for i386 do not.    TESTING:  ----  Follow the steps in the [Building Native JS Modules|https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/iOS+Module+Development+Guide#iOSModuleDevelopmentGuide-BuildingJavaScriptNativeModules] guide. Expected behavior is for the module to compile and run correctly.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Compiled CommonJS modules failing link
Description: """"It looks like commonjs module compiles for iOS are currently failing because the `filterData` function is not being properly exported as part of {{libtiverify}}. Relevant build log error, for device: Note that the device builds (armv6, armv7) indicate C++ name mangling; builds for i386 do not. TESTING: ---- Follow the steps in the [Building Native JS Modules|https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides2/iOS+Module+Development+Guide#iOSModuleDevelopmentGuide-BuildingJavaScriptNativeModules] guide. Expected behavior is for the module to compile and run correctly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9071,12,"""iOS: getAttributeNS and createAttributeNS Don't Accept Null First Argument""","""""""h1. Problem  On iOS, getAttributeNS doesn't accept a null first argument. It requires a string. This isn't consistent with browser behavior, which accepts a null value. The same applies to createAttributeNS.    h2. Expected Behavior  Calling getAttributeNS with null as the first argument should behave identically to getAttribute. The same applies to createAttributeNS.    h2. Reproduction  {code:title=app.js}  var xmlDoc = Ti.XML.parseString('<html><head></head><body><a href=""""""""http://<USER>com/"""""""" /></body></html>');  var anchor = xmlDoc.getElementsByTagName('a').item(0);  try {      alert(anchor.getAttributeNS(null, 'href'));  }  catch (err) {      alert('FAIL: getAttributeNS: ' + err);  }  try {      alert(xmlDoc.createAttributeNS(null, 'id'));  }  catch (err) {      alert('FAIL: createAttributeNS: ' + err);  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: getAttributeNS and createAttributeNS Don't Accept Null First Argument
Description: """"h1. Problem On iOS, getAttributeNS doesn't accept a null first argument. It requires a string. This isn't consistent with browser behavior, which accepts a null value. The same applies to createAttributeNS. h2. Expected Behavior Calling getAttributeNS with null as the first argument should behave identically to getAttribute. The same applies to createAttributeNS. h2. Reproduction {code:title=app.js} var xmlDoc = Ti.XML.parseString('<html><head></head><body><a href=""""""""http://<USER>com/"""""""" /></body></html>'); var anchor = xmlDoc.getElementsByTagName('a').item(0); try { alert(anchor.getAttributeNS(null, 'href')); } catch (err) { alert('FAIL: getAttributeNS: ' + err); } try { alert(xmlDoc.createAttributeNS(null, 'id')); } catch (err) { alert('FAIL: createAttributeNS: ' + err); } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-9070,12,"""Tooling: Porting evaluation tool Stories""","""""""Porting tool Stories    As a developer, I would like this tool to evaluate my titanium-developed application and provide a rating (preferably in a graphical manner) as to the suitability of this application for both android and IOS application compilation. I would like it to identify where modifications can be made to increase the suitability for multiplatform, or identify device/operation system specific functions that should be isolated to those folders. Success would be accurate representation of an titanium application's potential porting issues, and identification of where within the app those problems exist.    As a developer    As a development manager, I would like the tool to enable retroactive scanning of titanium developed apps and rate the suitability of those apps for porting to additional operation systems. Example would be a titanium built IOS App that has been deployed, the tool would enable inspection titanium code and identify potential problems for android port, could occur.  Success would be the tool's ability to examine titanium applications (in JavaScript) and provide reports consumable by developers and development managers  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Porting evaluation tool Stories
Description: """"Porting tool Stories As a developer, I would like this tool to evaluate my titanium-developed application and provide a rating (preferably in a graphical manner) as to the suitability of this application for both android and IOS application compilation. I would like it to identify where modifications can be made to increase the suitability for multiplatform, or identify device/operation system specific functions that should be isolated to those folders. Success would be accurate representation of an titanium application's potential porting issues, and identification of where within the app those problems exist. As a developer As a development manager, I would like the tool to enable retroactive scanning of titanium developed apps and rate the suitability of those apps for porting to additional operation systems. Example would be a titanium built IOS App that has been deployed, the tool would enable inspection titanium code and identify potential problems for android port, could occur. Success would be the tool's ability to examine titanium applications (in JavaScript) and provide reports consumable by developers and development managers """"",title+description
TIMOB-9069,12,"""Android: View inside ScrollView doesn't scroll up if its height is defined as percentage""","""""""h2. Problem    To see the issue, run this example:        Text field should automatically receive focus and button should be seen on the screen. The problem is that """"""""toolbar"""""""" view did not scroll up and it is not visible on the screen. If keyboard is lowered, """"""""toolbar"""""""" view is visible on the bottom of the screen. If text field is again focused (by clicking on it), same issue can be seen.    h2. Expected behavior    """"""""toolbar"""""""" should be scrolled up. This issue does not exist if """"""""height"""""""" property is defined as numeric value.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: View inside ScrollView doesn't scroll up if its height is defined as percentage
Description: """"h2. Problem To see the issue, run this example: Text field should automatically receive focus and button should be seen on the screen. The problem is that """"""""toolbar"""""""" view did not scroll up and it is not visible on the screen. If keyboard is lowered, """"""""toolbar"""""""" view is visible on the bottom of the screen. If text field is again focused (by clicking on it), same issue can be seen. h2. Expected behavior """"""""toolbar"""""""" should be scrolled up. This issue does not exist if """"""""height"""""""" property is defined as numeric value.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9068,12,"""MobileWeb: Parity in ScrollableView for """"scroll"""" and """"scrollEnd"""" events""","""""""To achieve parity with recent re-definition of the meaning of """"""""scroll"""""""" and addition of the event """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" via TIMOB-8933 (iOS) and TIMOB-9061 (Android), both of were settled via this PR: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/2101.    See updated ScrollableView.yml file for documentation.  (As I type this, it isn't merged yet, but will be soon.)    Test app.js from the community contributor:    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: """"""""#444""""""""});  var view1 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'#123', width: 250 });  var view2 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'#246', width: 250 });  var view3 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'#48b', width: 250 });     var scrollableView = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({    views: [view1,view2,view3],    showPagingControl: true,    width: 260,    height: 430  });     win.add(scrollableView);  win.open();     scrollableView.addEventListener('scroll', function (e) {     Ti.API.debug('scrollableView got a scroll event: float:' + e.currentPageAsFloat +  ' int: ' + e.currentPage);  });       scrollableView.addEventListener('scrollEnd', function (e) {     Ti.API.debug('scrollableView got a scrollEnd event: ' + e.currentPage);  });  {code}    Run that and watch console, making sure the logged values are logical.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Parity in ScrollableView for """"scroll"""" and """"scrollEnd"""" events
Description: """"To achieve parity with recent re-definition of the meaning of """"""""scroll"""""""" and addition of the event """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" via TIMOB-8933 (iOS) and TIMOB-9061 (Android), both of were settled via this PR: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/2101. See updated ScrollableView.yml file for documentation. (As I type this, it isn't merged yet, but will be soon.) Test app.js from the community contributor: {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: """"""""#444""""""""}); var view1 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'#123', width: 250 }); var view2 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'#246', width: 250 }); var view3 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'#48b', width: 250 }); var scrollableView = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({ views: [view1,view2,view3], showPagingControl: true, width: 260, height: 430 }); win.add(scrollableView); win.open(); scrollableView.addEventListener('scroll', function (e) { Ti.API.debug('scrollableView got a scroll event: float:' + e.currentPageAsFloat + ' int: ' + e.currentPage); }); scrollableView.addEventListener('scrollEnd', function (e) { Ti.API.debug('scrollableView got a scrollEnd event: ' + e.currentPage); }); {code} Run that and watch console, making sure the logged values are logical.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9067,12,"""CLI: Add analytics support""","""""""We need to add in analytics support to the CLI, by request. Whoever takes this ticket is expected to work with Chung and Ingo to make sure that:    * We provide appropriate event support  * Studio and the CLI are tightly coupled when it comes to analytics    Here are the events that need to be tracked:  * creating a project: platforms, type, template, acs (y/n)  * building a project: platform, package, device/simulator, production/ development  * install an app: platform, device, simulator/emulator  * run an app: platform, device, simulator/emulator  * migrate a project""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CLI: Add analytics support
Description: """"We need to add in analytics support to the CLI, by request. Whoever takes this ticket is expected to work with Chung and Ingo to make sure that: * We provide appropriate event support * Studio and the CLI are tightly coupled when it comes to analytics Here are the events that need to be tracked: * creating a project: platforms, type, template, acs (y/n) * building a project: platform, package, device/simulator, production/ development * install an app: platform, device, simulator/emulator * run an app: platform, device, simulator/emulator * migrate a project""""",title+description
TIMOB-9065,12,"""Android: Sound - Remote URL does not play""","""""""Remote URL does not play.  Steps To Reproduce:  1. LG-P970 > Kitchensink > Phone> Sound> RemoteURL  2. Press Play    Actual:  05-09 06:43:26.673: V/MediaPlayerService(1627): [68] notify (0x920d8, 100, 1, -2112880640)  05-09 06:43:26.680: E/MediaPlayer(11860): error (1, -2112880640)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860): (KrollRuntimeThread) [2746,8112398] Issue while initializing :   05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860): java.io.IOException: Prepare failed.: status=0x1  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at android.media.MediaPlayer.prepare(Native Method)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at ti.modules.titanium.media.TiSound.initialize(TiSound.java:119)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at ti.modules.titanium.media.TiSound.play(TiSound.java:178)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at ti.modules.titanium.media.SoundProxy.play(SoundProxy.java:135)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Object.nativeFireEvent(Native Method)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Object.fireEvent(V8Object.java:60)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollProxy.doFireEvent(KrollProxy.java:494)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollProxy.handleMessage(KrollProxy.java:675)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at org.<USER>titanium.proxy.TiViewProxy.handleMessage(TiViewProxy.java:398)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123)  05-09 06:43:26.680: W/TiSound(11860):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime$KrollRuntimeThread.run(KrollRuntime.java:104)  05-09 06:43:26.680: V/MediaPlayerService(1627): disconnect(68) from pid 11860    Expected:  File should play successfully    Note: Also occured in 1.8.2  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Sound - Remote URL does not play
