TIMOB-9049,12,"""Android: Clicking the focus button does not bring the keyboard up.""","""""""Clicking the focus button does not bring the keyboard up.(Kitchensink > Controls > TextArea > Basic)  1. Click on a text field  2. Leave test case  3. Launch test case  4. Press """"""""Focus"""""""" button    Expected result  After step 1: Text field should be activated and keyboard should appear. Message on the left corner will be """"""""Focus fired, value=I am a text area""""""""  After step 4: Focus should appear in the text area and keyboard should pop up. Message on the left corner will be """"""""Focus fired, value=I am a text area""""""""     Actual Result:   Clicking on focus button does not bring the keyboard up but the text area is focused and the message is correct on the left corner.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Clicking the focus button does not bring the keyboard up.
Description: """"Clicking the focus button does not bring the keyboard up.(Kitchensink > Controls > TextArea > Basic) 1. Click on a text field 2. Leave test case 3. Launch test case 4. Press """"""""Focus"""""""" button Expected result After step 1: Text field should be activated and keyboard should appear. Message on the left corner will be """"""""Focus fired, value=I am a text area"""""""" After step 4: Focus should appear in the text area and keyboard should pop up. Message on the left corner will be """"""""Focus fired, value=I am a text area"""""""" Actual Result: Clicking on focus button does not bring the keyboard up but the text area is focused and the message is correct on the left corner.""""",title+description
TIMOB-9048,12,"""Android: KS Controls:Text Field:The Rest: passwordMask and clearOnEdit fields give value as undefined in ddms.""","""""""Repro steps  1. Click on text field   2. Press """"""""Enabled"""""""" button and check ddms   3. Press other functional buttons and check ddms    Expected result  1. Text field should be activated and keyboard should appear   2. Text field should be blocked for typing, and keyboard should disappear. In ddms should see:   [INFO] enabled true   3. All buttons should work properly and in ddms should appear appropriate info:   [INFO] autocorrect true/false   [INFO] passwordMask true/false   [INFO] clearButtonMode   [INFO] backgroundImage ../images/chat.png   [INFO] clearOnEdit true/false   [INFO] autocapitalization    Actual result:  [INFO] passwordMask and [INFO] clearOnEdit shows value as undefined instead of true/false in ddms at first.Afterwards, it starts showing correct values.   """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS Controls:Text Field:The Rest: passwordMask and clearOnEdit fields give value as undefined in ddms.
Description: """"Repro steps 1. Click on text field 2. Press """"""""Enabled"""""""" button and check ddms 3. Press other functional buttons and check ddms Expected result 1. Text field should be activated and keyboard should appear 2. Text field should be blocked for typing, and keyboard should disappear. In ddms should see: [INFO] enabled true 3. All buttons should work properly and in ddms should appear appropriate info: [INFO] autocorrect true/false [INFO] passwordMask true/false [INFO] clearButtonMode [INFO] backgroundImage ../images/chat.png [INFO] clearOnEdit true/false [INFO] autocapitalization Actual result: [INFO] passwordMask and [INFO] clearOnEdit shows value as undefined instead of true/false in ddms at first.Afterwards, it starts showing correct values. """"",title+description
