TIMOB-8910,12,"""Android: Window """"focus"""" event not firing when returning to main window of tabgroup in android""","""""""h2. Problem  Android doesn't fire focus events (or other events) when returning to the main window of a tabgroup. (Works as expected in iOS)    Please note that this is NOT the same issue as [TIMOB-4063|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4063] or [TIMOB-8714|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-8714]. This is not about switching between tabs but rather returning from child windows.    h2. Test Case  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  //app.js    //create win1. button1 opens win2  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow();  var button1 = Ti.UI.createButton({title:'Open win2'});  button1.addEventListener('click', function(){ tab1.open(win2); });   win1.add(button1);    //create win2. button2 closes win2  var win2 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({title:'Window 2'});  var button2 = Titanium.UI.createButton({title:'Close win2'});  button2.addEventListener('click', function(){ win2.close(); });   win2.add(button2);       win1.addEventListener('focus',  function(e){Ti.API.info('win1 focused');});   win1.addEventListener('blur',  function(e){Ti.API.info('win1 blurred');});   win2.addEventListener('focus', function(e){Ti.API.info('win2 focused');});  win2.addEventListener('blur', function(e){Ti.API.info('win2 blurred');});    // open tab group  var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup();  var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({title:'Tab 1',window:win1});  tabGroup.addTab(tab1);  tabGroup.open();  {code}      h2. Community Discussions  http://developer.<USER>com/question/66591/window-in-tab-group-focus-events-still-not-working-on-android  http://developer.<USER>com/question/27971/does-android-not-get-the-window-events-blur-and-focus    h2. Logs  N/A""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window """"focus"""" event not firing when returning to main window of tabgroup in android
Description: """"h2. Problem Android doesn't fire focus events (or other events) when returning to the main window of a tabgroup. (Works as expected in iOS) Please note that this is NOT the same issue as [TIMOB-4063|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4063] or [TIMOB-8714|https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-8714]. This is not about switching between tabs but rather returning from child windows. h2. Test Case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} //app.js //create win1. button1 opens win2 var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); var button1 = Ti.UI.createButton({title:'Open win2'}); button1.addEventListener('click', function(){ tab1.open(win2); }); win1.add(button1); //create win2. button2 closes win2 var win2 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({title:'Window 2'}); var button2 = Titanium.UI.createButton({title:'Close win2'}); button2.addEventListener('click', function(){ win2.close(); }); win2.add(button2); win1.addEventListener('focus', function(e){Ti.API.info('win1 focused');}); win1.addEventListener('blur', function(e){Ti.API.info('win1 blurred');}); win2.addEventListener('focus', function(e){Ti.API.info('win2 focused');}); win2.addEventListener('blur', function(e){Ti.API.info('win2 blurred');}); // open tab group var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup(); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({title:'Tab 1',window:win1}); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.open(); {code} h2. Community Discussions http://developer.<USER>com/question/66591/window-in-tab-group-focus-events-still-not-working-on-android http://developer.<USER>com/question/27971/does-android-not-get-the-window-events-blur-and-focus h2. Logs N/A""""",title+description
TIMOB-8909,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.View.children is not the empty array when no children are present""","""""""Currently, Android (and presumably mobileweb) return the empty array {{\[\]}} for {{Ti.UI.View.children}} when the view has no children. On iOS, we return {{undefined}}. Complicating matters is the fact that internally, we rely on this value for views with no children; this ticket could involve a substantial amount of work to ensure that no subsystems which rely on checking children content are affected.    h4. Testing  ----    Run the following test; it should not contain errors, but will only work after [pull request 2098|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/2098] is processed.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.View.children is not the empty array when no children are present
Description: """"Currently, Android (and presumably mobileweb) return the empty array {{\[\]}} for {{Ti.UI.View.children}} when the view has no children. On iOS, we return {{undefined}}. Complicating matters is the fact that internally, we rely on this value for views with no children; this ticket could involve a substantial amount of work to ensure that no subsystems which rely on checking children content are affected. h4. Testing ---- Run the following test; it should not contain errors, but will only work after [pull request 2098|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/2098] is processed. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8908,12,"""iOS: Click/Swipe events fired differently in iOS and Android""","""""""    In this code, Android will only fire the swipe event whenever we swipe.  In iOS, we fire a click event first, then a swipe event.    We need to determine which is the correct behavior and change the other accordingly.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Click/Swipe events fired differently in iOS and Android
Description: """" In this code, Android will only fire the swipe event whenever we swipe. In iOS, we fire a click event first, then a swipe event. We need to determine which is the correct behavior and change the other accordingly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8907,12,"""Android: click event does not fire correctly when touchStart listener is present on view""","""""""Click event does not fire for view when a touchStart listener is present on view.  Example code:      Commenting out the touchstart listener will allow the click events to get through.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: click event does not fire correctly when touchStart listener is present on view
Description: """"Click event does not fire for view when a touchStart listener is present on view. Example code: Commenting out the touchstart listener will allow the click events to get through.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8906,12,"""Android: createHttpClient cannot determine the charset encoding by html meta tag""","""""""h1. Problem    To determine the character encoding, determining sequence is as follows:    * HTTP Header (Content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8)  * HTML meta tag (meta http-equiv=""""""""Content-Type"""""""" content=""""""""text/html; charset=utf-8"""""""")    iOS handring is correct, but Android ignores HTML meta tag encoding name.    h1. Test Case    I make a sample code which accesses each charset sample webpage and display their results.  {code:js}  var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'white',  });  var text = Ti.UI.createLabel({   text: '',  });  win1.add(text);  win1.open();  charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/utf8.html"""""""");  charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/shiftjis.html"""""""");  charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/eucjp.html"""""""");  charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/iso2022jp.html"""""""");    function charsetTest(url){   var xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient();      xhr.onload = function() {    if(this.status == 200) {     var html = this.responseText;     if(html == null){      text.text = text.text + url + ' is null.\n\n';     }     else if(html.match(/<body>([\s\S]*)<\/body>/)){      var body = RegExp.$1;      text.text = text.text + url + body;     }else{      text.text = text.text + url + ' is 200, but no body element.\n\n';     }    }else{     text.text = text.text + url + ' status code is ' + this.status + '\n\n';    }   };   xhr.onerror = function() {    text.text = text.text + url + ' status code is ' + this.status + '\n\n';     };   xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""", url, false);   xhr.send();     }  {code}   Result and screenshot is below:  ||OS||UTF-8||Shift_JIS||EUC-JP||ISO-2022-JP||  |Android|OK|NG|NG|NG|    h1. Suggested Fix    To fix this bug, set charset in getResponseText()    See https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/590      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: createHttpClient cannot determine the charset encoding by html meta tag
Description: """"h1. Problem To determine the character encoding, determining sequence is as follows: * HTTP Header (Content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8) * HTML meta tag (meta http-equiv=""""""""Content-Type"""""""" content=""""""""text/html; charset=utf-8"""""""") iOS handring is correct, but Android ignores HTML meta tag encoding name. h1. Test Case I make a sample code which accesses each charset sample webpage and display their results. {code:js} var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white', }); var text = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: '', }); win1.add(text); win1.open(); charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/utf8.html""""""""); charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/shiftjis.html""""""""); charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/eucjp.html""""""""); charsetTest(""""""""http://kangaechu.com/iso2022jp.html""""""""); function charsetTest(url){ var xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function() { if(this.status == 200) { var html = this.responseText; if(html == null){ text.text = text.text + url + ' is null.\n\n'; } else if(html.match(/<body>([\s\S]*)<\/body>/)){ var body = RegExp.$1; text.text = text.text + url + body; }else{ text.text = text.text + url + ' is 200, but no body element.\n\n'; } }else{ text.text = text.text + url + ' status code is ' + this.status + '\n\n'; } }; xhr.onerror = function() { text.text = text.text + url + ' status code is ' + this.status + '\n\n'; }; xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""", url, false); xhr.send(); } {code} Result and screenshot is below: ||OS||UTF-8||Shift_JIS||EUC-JP||ISO-2022-JP|| |Android|OK|NG|NG|NG| h1. Suggested Fix To fix this bug, set charset in getResponseText() See https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/590 """"",title+description
