TIMOB-8903,12,"""Android: scrollView - does not resize width of content with device is rotated""","""""""The view in a scrollView does not resize correctly when the window it is in is rotated to landscape and then back to portrait.  Broken on 2.1.0  Working on 1.8.2    h4. Steps to repro:  Step 1: run the code   Step 2: hold the device in portrait and launch the app  Step 3: notice the red views on the left and right of the screen  Step 4: rotate the device to landscape  Step 5: notice the red views move out and stay at the sides of the screen  Step 6: rotate the device back to portrait  Step 7: notice that the views on the right side are missing (they should have moved back in to be at the side of the screen)  Step 8: repeat the steps above with TiSDK 1.8.2 to see the correct behavior    {code:js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: 'blue'});  win.open();    var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({   left:0,   top:0,   right:0,   bottom:0,   contentHeight:'auto',   backgroundColor: 'green'  });  win.add(scrollView);    var innerView = Ti.UI.createView({   height:Ti.UI.SIZE,   layout:'vertical',   left:0,   top:0,   right:0  });  scrollView.add(innerView);    for(var i = 0; i < 10;  i++){   var params = {    backgroundColor: 'red',    top: 5,    height: 20,    width: 100,   }      if(i%2 === 0){    params.left = 5;   }else{    params.right = 5;   }      innerView.add(Ti.UI.createView(params));  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: scrollView - does not resize width of content with device is rotated
Description: """"The view in a scrollView does not resize correctly when the window it is in is rotated to landscape and then back to portrait. Broken on 2.1.0 Working on 1.8.2 h4. Steps to repro: Step 1: run the code Step 2: hold the device in portrait and launch the app Step 3: notice the red views on the left and right of the screen Step 4: rotate the device to landscape Step 5: notice the red views move out and stay at the sides of the screen Step 6: rotate the device back to portrait Step 7: notice that the views on the right side are missing (they should have moved back in to be at the side of the screen) Step 8: repeat the steps above with TiSDK 1.8.2 to see the correct behavior {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor: 'blue'}); win.open(); var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({ left:0, top:0, right:0, bottom:0, contentHeight:'auto', backgroundColor: 'green' }); win.add(scrollView); var innerView = Ti.UI.createView({ height:Ti.UI.SIZE, layout:'vertical', left:0, top:0, right:0 }); scrollView.add(innerView); for(var i = 0; i < 10; i++){ var params = { backgroundColor: 'red', top: 5, height: 20, width: 100, } if(i%2 === 0){ params.left = 5; }else{ params.right = 5; } innerView.add(Ti.UI.createView(params)); } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-8901,12,"""Refactoring - Renaming a file should detect everything else with that name and change it too, so you don't have to re-name everything one at a time.""","""""""Renaming a file should detect everything else with that name and change it too, so you don't have to re-name everything one at a time.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Refactoring - Renaming a file should detect everything else with that name and change it too, so you don't have to re-name everything one at a time.
Description: """"Renaming a file should detect everything else with that name and change it too, so you don't have to re-name everything one at a time.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8900,12,"""Android: HTTP request causes intermittent """"Connection reset by peer"""" error""","""""""This is for a customer delivery that is due 4/27.      In the app, we are seeing intermittent """"""""Connection reset by peer"""""""".  There is no error on the server logs.  We suspect that there is a bug in the platform that is throwing this error message.   A similar bug is here but for iOS:  https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-2801?page=com.atlassian.streams.streams-jira-plugin:activity-stream-issue-tab    APP FLOW  Every web service call goes through the """"""""send"""""""" function and from inside there, it calls createHTTPClient -  so... each new call should be a new instance of createHTTPClient.  Intermittently, we get the error  """"""""Connection reset by peer""""""""    CODE:  https://github.com/<USER>services/IRTHNet-Utilisphere/blob/master/Resources/api/api_app.js  the only two functions that are relevant are:   send  createHTTPClient""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTP request causes intermittent """"Connection reset by peer"""" error
Description: """"This is for a customer delivery that is due 4/27. In the app, we are seeing intermittent """"""""Connection reset by peer"""""""". There is no error on the server logs. We suspect that there is a bug in the platform that is throwing this error message. A similar bug is here but for iOS: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-2801?page=com.atlassian.streams.streams-jira-plugin:activity-stream-issue-tab APP FLOW Every web service call goes through the """"""""send"""""""" function and from inside there, it calls createHTTPClient - so... each new call should be a new instance of createHTTPClient. Intermittently, we get the error """"""""Connection reset by peer"""""""" CODE: https://github.com/<USER>services/IRTHNet-Utilisphere/blob/master/Resources/api/api_app.js the only two functions that are relevant are: send createHTTPClient""""",title+description
