TIMOB-8893,12,"""iOS: Implement Ti.Media.createItem""","""""""h2. Request description  Customer is trying to save a user's playlist by storing the properties from a media item and calling Ti.Media.createItem.    Ti.Media.createItem is not implemented but documented http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.createItem-method.html        Right now, using it, the error message returned is: 'invalid method (createItem) passed to MediaModule'    h2. Additional notes and links  Documentation bug: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIDOC-556  TiMOB bug: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3425  Ticket link: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-239728""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Implement Ti.Media.createItem
Description: """"h2. Request description Customer is trying to save a user's playlist by storing the properties from a media item and calling Ti.Media.createItem. Ti.Media.createItem is not implemented but documented http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.createItem-method.html Right now, using it, the error message returned is: 'invalid method (createItem) passed to MediaModule' h2. Additional notes and links Documentation bug: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIDOC-556 TiMOB bug: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3425 Ticket link: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-239728""""",title+description
TIMOB-8891,12,"""Android: scrollView not scrolling if contentHeight = 'auto'""","""""""scrollView not scrolling if contentHeight = 'auto' and height of the childView of scrollView is set to SIZE.  It works fine if you set the height of the childView to something static instead of SIZE    h4. Steps to repro  Step 1: run code  Step 2: try to scroll (if it doesn't scroll then it is still broken)    {code:js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();  win.open();    var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({   contentHeight:'auto',   backgroundColor: 'green'  });  win.add(scrollView);    var innerView = Ti.UI.createView({   height:Ti.UI.SIZE, // works if set to 1000   layout:'vertical',   left:0,   top:0,   right:0  });  scrollView.add(innerView);    var colors = ['red', 'blue', 'pink', 'white', 'black'];    var max = 10;  for(var i = 0; i < max; i++){   innerView.add(Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor: colors[i%colors.length],    height: 100,    top: 20   }));  }  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: scrollView not scrolling if contentHeight = 'auto'
Description: """"scrollView not scrolling if contentHeight = 'auto' and height of the childView of scrollView is set to SIZE. It works fine if you set the height of the childView to something static instead of SIZE h4. Steps to repro Step 1: run code Step 2: try to scroll (if it doesn't scroll then it is still broken) {code:js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); win.open(); var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({ contentHeight:'auto', backgroundColor: 'green' }); win.add(scrollView); var innerView = Ti.UI.createView({ height:Ti.UI.SIZE, // works if set to 1000 layout:'vertical', left:0, top:0, right:0 }); scrollView.add(innerView); var colors = ['red', 'blue', 'pink', 'white', 'black']; var max = 10; for(var i = 0; i < max; i++){ innerView.add(Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: colors[i%colors.length], height: 100, top: 20 })); } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-8890,12,"""Android: Unable to catch any errors while creating a crash reporter""","""""""The customer wants to create a crash reporter. He needs to have a global listener that just catches errors and makes an api call before it raises. At the moment he's just trying to log beforehand then raise. The below code doesn't catch any errors. Is it because it's a KrollRuntime Thread not a Thread?     Is it possible to accomplish this with titanium?""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Unable to catch any errors while creating a crash reporter
Description: """"The customer wants to create a crash reporter. He needs to have a global listener that just catches errors and makes an api call before it raises. At the moment he's just trying to log beforehand then raise. The below code doesn't catch any errors. Is it because it's a KrollRuntime Thread not a Thread? Is it possible to accomplish this with titanium?""""",title+description
TIMOB-8889,12,"""Android: android:back event does not get fired from activity indicator""","""""""Repro steps:    1. Run the code below  2. hit back while the activity indicator is running    Expected result:  You should see 'back!!!!!!!' in the logs    Actual result:  The event is never fired.      Note, I tried adding the listener to the win1, win2, and activityIndicator with the same results.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: android:back event does not get fired from activity indicator
Description: """"Repro steps: 1. Run the code below 2. hit back while the activity indicator is running Expected result: You should see 'back!!!!!!!' in the logs Actual result: The event is never fired. Note, I tried adding the listener to the win1, win2, and activityIndicator with the same results. """"",title+description
