TIMOB-8793,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink - Options Dialog does not change orientation on iPhone and iPod""","""""""Description:  While testing """"""""Options Dialog"""""""" on iPhone and iPod, I noticed, that options dialog does not change orientation after device is rotated from portrait to landscape.  This bug exists on 1.8.2 and 2.0.1. Does not reproduce with iPad devices.    Steps:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Base UI-Views-Options Dialog  3. Press """"""""Show Dialog 1""""""""  4. Rotate device to landscape mode    Expected result:  Options dialog should change orientation fron portrait to landscape     Actual result:  Options dialog does not change orientation""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink - Options Dialog does not change orientation on iPhone and iPod
Description: """"Description: While testing """"""""Options Dialog"""""""" on iPhone and iPod, I noticed, that options dialog does not change orientation after device is rotated from portrait to landscape. This bug exists on 1.8.2 and 2.0.1. Does not reproduce with iPad devices. Steps: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Base UI-Views-Options Dialog 3. Press """"""""Show Dialog 1"""""""" 4. Rotate device to landscape mode Expected result: Options dialog should change orientation fron portrait to landscape Actual result: Options dialog does not change orientation""""",title+description
TIMOB-8792,12,"""MobileWeb: Clean up UI Inheritence and create """"core"""" controls""","""""""We should create two """"""""core"""""""" or """"""""simple"""""""" controls for text and images. ImageView and Label are really heavy weight and are reused elsewhere...creating a simplified version that is used by those two controls, and any controls that use them, should give us a performance improvement (especially in memory usage).    These controls should inherit from Element to keep them lightweight.    We should go ahead and do the inheritence switch as Element->Widget->View, and move things like _add(), borders, etc into Widget to try and lighten up Element.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Clean up UI Inheritence and create """"core"""" controls
Description: """"We should create two """"""""core"""""""" or """"""""simple"""""""" controls for text and images. ImageView and Label are really heavy weight and are reused elsewhere...creating a simplified version that is used by those two controls, and any controls that use them, should give us a performance improvement (especially in memory usage). These controls should inherit from Element to keep them lightweight. We should go ahead and do the inheritence switch as Element->Widget->View, and move things like _add(), borders, etc into Widget to try and lighten up Element.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8791,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming , Movie does not get streamed and played from the given URL.""","""""""While testing KitchenSink: Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming , iPhone 3GS does not stream movie from the given URL.    Test to reproduce:  1.Launch Kitchensink; phone> Play movie> Remote Streaming.  2. Move the thumb at the end of the track or wait when movie will finish playing    Expected results:  1. Should see a movie playing (may take a few seconds to load) and streaming should begin and continue until movie is complete. All controls should work appropriately.  2. Should get an alert """"""""Movie Completed!""""""""    Actual Result:   1. Movie does not get streamed and played. After a few seconds,alert,""""""""Movie Cpmpleted"""""""" is shown twice.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming , Movie does not get streamed and played from the given URL.
Description: """"While testing KitchenSink: Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming , iPhone 3GS does not stream movie from the given URL. Test to reproduce: 1.Launch Kitchensink; phone> Play movie> Remote Streaming. 2. Move the thumb at the end of the track or wait when movie will finish playing Expected results: 1. Should see a movie playing (may take a few seconds to load) and streaming should begin and continue until movie is complete. All controls should work appropriately. 2. Should get an alert """"""""Movie Completed!"""""""" Actual Result: 1. Movie does not get streamed and played. After a few seconds,alert,""""""""Movie Cpmpleted"""""""" is shown twice.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8790,12,"""Android:KS- Setting up the SeparatorColor property as null displays separator color as yellow""","""""""Setting up the SeparatorColor property as null displays separator color as yellow.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Open up the kitchen Sink application.  2. Tap on base UI  3. Tap on Views  4. Tap on table Views.  5. Tap on Set Row data  6. Tap on Set2    Actual result:  After step 6: Could see 'Set TableView 1','Set TableView 2'Set TableView 3' and three rows of Row<number> row separator was single line and yellow color for the separator color    Expected Result:  After Step 6: Should see 'Set TableView 1','Set TableView 2'Set TableView 3' and three rows of Row<number> row separator should be single line and no color for the separator color    Note: This behavior is observed 1.8.2 , 2.0.1 and 2.1.0.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android:KS- Setting up the SeparatorColor property as null displays separator color as yellow
Description: """"Setting up the SeparatorColor property as null displays separator color as yellow. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Open up the kitchen Sink application. 2. Tap on base UI 3. Tap on Views 4. Tap on table Views. 5. Tap on Set Row data 6. Tap on Set2 Actual result: After step 6: Could see 'Set TableView 1','Set TableView 2'Set TableView 3' and three rows of Row<number> row separator was single line and yellow color for the separator color Expected Result: After Step 6: Should see 'Set TableView 1','Set TableView 2'Set TableView 3' and three rows of Row<number> row separator should be single line and no color for the separator color Note: This behavior is observed 1.8.2 , 2.0.1 and 2.1.0. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8789,12,"""Android: headerView label displaying issues after scrolling the tableView""","""""""h2. Scenario description    Define a label inside a view and add the view to a tableView as headerView property.  After scrolling the tableView, the label might move outside of the view, resulting being invisible or truncated.      h2. Sample code and step to reproduce    - Run the code below.  - Scroll up and down the tableView.  Result: the label in the headerView might move outside of the view, resulting in being invisible or truncated.  This behavior does not seems to be always reproducible, it might take two or three scrolling attempts.  Also, I've not been able to reproduce the issue if commenting out all properties from the label (except 'text' of course).    Not reproducible on 1.7.6 TiSDK    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: headerView label displaying issues after scrolling the tableView
Description: """"h2. Scenario description Define a label inside a view and add the view to a tableView as headerView property. After scrolling the tableView, the label might move outside of the view, resulting being invisible or truncated. h2. Sample code and step to reproduce - Run the code below. - Scroll up and down the tableView. Result: the label in the headerView might move outside of the view, resulting in being invisible or truncated. This behavior does not seems to be always reproducible, it might take two or three scrolling attempts. Also, I've not been able to reproduce the issue if commenting out all properties from the label (except 'text' of course). Not reproducible on 1.7.6 TiSDK """"",title+description
