TIMOB-8779,12,"""MobileWeb: Late bind gestures in elements""","""""""When an element is created, all gestures are instantiated and wired up. It would be far more efficient to bind the gesture at the time addEventListener() is called.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Late bind gestures in elements
Description: """"When an element is created, all gestures are instantiated and wired up. It would be far more efficient to bind the gesture at the time addEventListener() is called.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8778,12,"""MobileWeb: Queue up touch/mouse events and process and a slower frequency than realtime""","""""""Right now events are processed immediately, but since events (i.e. touchmove events) can fire faster than the eye can perseve, it makes no sense to <USER>the events right away. Instead, the gesture system should queue up touch events, then <USER>them all at once. This interval should perhaps be 30 times per second. This can be done with a setInterval(), but might be better to use requestAnimationFrame() if there is enough browser support.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Queue up touch/mouse events and process and a slower frequency than realtime
Description: """"Right now events are processed immediately, but since events (i.e. touchmove events) can fire faster than the eye can perseve, it makes no sense to <USER>the events right away. Instead, the gesture system should queue up touch events, then <USER>them all at once. This interval should perhaps be 30 times per second. This can be done with a setInterval(), but might be better to use requestAnimationFrame() if there is enough browser support.""""",title+description
