TIMOB-8776,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink 2.1.0 - Expected label is not displayed on the video from Kitchensink-PlayMovie-local""","""""""Expected label is not displayed when video is played from Kitchensink-PlayMovie-local.    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch test case  2. Press the movie label  3. Wait until movie will finish playing two times and check xCode console    Expected results:  1. Should see a movie playing and movie label should say """"""""Do not try this at home""""""""  2. The movie label should be changed on """"""""mediaControlStyle= movieControlStyle= """"""""  3. Should get an alert """"""""Movie Completed!""""""""  In console should see info:  [INFO] Event PlaybackState Fired:  [INFO] activeMovie.endPlaybackTime:  [INFO] activeMovie.playableDuration: """"""""    Actual Result:  Movie plays successfully and console gets correct messages but labels are not displayed.     Note: The scenario works fine with 1_8_x and 2_0_X.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink 2.1.0 - Expected label is not displayed on the video from Kitchensink-PlayMovie-local
Description: """"Expected label is not displayed when video is played from Kitchensink-PlayMovie-local. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch test case 2. Press the movie label 3. Wait until movie will finish playing two times and check xCode console Expected results: 1. Should see a movie playing and movie label should say """"""""Do not try this at home"""""""" 2. The movie label should be changed on """"""""mediaControlStyle= movieControlStyle= """""""" 3. Should get an alert """"""""Movie Completed!"""""""" In console should see info: [INFO] Event PlaybackState Fired: [INFO] activeMovie.endPlaybackTime: [INFO] activeMovie.playableDuration: """""""" Actual Result: Movie plays successfully and console gets correct messages but labels are not displayed. Note: The scenario works fine with 1_8_x and 2_0_X. """"",title+description
