TIMOB-8770,12,"""Conflicts between ASI Http symbols and modules""","""""""We are increasingly running into conflicts with the ASI Http component of TiSDK when integrating 3rd party libraries into a module. The situation is that developers are trying to build a module using a pre-built static library provided by a 3rd party. That library includes their own copy of the ASI Http code. In the cases where the 3rd party library developer has not renamed the ASI Http code (ie. class name, variables, etc) they encounter duplicate symbol errors when attempting to build a Titanium application that uses that module. This is because TiSDK exposes the ASI Http symbols as well. This has typically been handled by requesting the module developer to request the provider of the 3rd party library to rebuild their SDK with all of the ASI Http code renamed in order to avoid the naming conflict.    However, we can eliminate this issue in TiSDK by renaming the ASI Http classes, interfaces, etc. to include a 'Ti' prefix or something. It will present a much better module development experience for our module developers.    Note that this issue is related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-5973""""""",Story,"Title: Conflicts between ASI Http symbols and modules
Description: """"We are increasingly running into conflicts with the ASI Http component of TiSDK when integrating 3rd party libraries into a module. The situation is that developers are trying to build a module using a pre-built static library provided by a 3rd party. That library includes their own copy of the ASI Http code. In the cases where the 3rd party library developer has not renamed the ASI Http code (ie. class name, variables, etc) they encounter duplicate symbol errors when attempting to build a Titanium application that uses that module. This is because TiSDK exposes the ASI Http symbols as well. This has typically been handled by requesting the module developer to request the provider of the 3rd party library to rebuild their SDK with all of the ASI Http code renamed in order to avoid the naming conflict. However, we can eliminate this issue in TiSDK by renaming the ASI Http classes, interfaces, etc. to include a 'Ti' prefix or something. It will present a much better module development experience for our module developers. Note that this issue is related to https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-5973""""",title+description
TIMOB-8769,12,"""iOS: App build fails on Snow Leopard/iOS 4.3 configured machine""","""""""For Snow Leopard and iOS 4.3 configuration, the app is not building for iOS on a 2.0.x release. I have tested this on the latest CI 2.0 (4/10/2012) available on the CI server. This can be tested with a simple 1 window application.    Here is the log shown on the console:        The customer added the following to ASIHTTPRequest.h by looking into the error code above:    #ifndef __IPHONE_5_0  #define __IPHONE_5_0 50000  #endif    To match the other #ifdefs in that file. This does removes the above error, but then compilation fails as follows:    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App build fails on Snow Leopard/iOS 4.3 configured machine
Description: """"For Snow Leopard and iOS 4.3 configuration, the app is not building for iOS on a 2.0.x release. I have tested this on the latest CI 2.0 (4/10/2012) available on the CI server. This can be tested with a simple 1 window application. Here is the log shown on the console: The customer added the following to ASIHTTPRequest.h by looking into the error code above: #ifndef __IPHONE_5_0 #define __IPHONE_5_0 50000 #endif To match the other #ifdefs in that file. This does removes the above error, but then compilation fails as follows: """"",title+description
TIMOB-8768,12,"""Android: App restart required on first launch when installed from sdcard""","""""""When an app is installed to device using adb push, the app must restart on first launch.    This is not a regression (tested in 1.8.1+).    This may be an Android bug according to the log (attached):    Android issue 2373 detected (missing intent CATEGORY_LAUNCHER or FLAG_ACTIVITY_RESET_TASK_IF_NEEDED), restarting app.    This issue also intermittently affects the 3.X and 4.X emulators on regular launch (see linked issue).    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create a new project.  2. Package app or build to emulator to obtain the app.apk.  3. In the terminal, push apk to device using command (apk name may vary):        4. Navigate to app apk in device file system (i.e., Astro).  5. Click on the apk, press install, press open/run app.    Expected Result:    App should run without error.    Actual Result:    App force restarts on first run, but runs correctly on future launches.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: App restart required on first launch when installed from sdcard
Description: """"When an app is installed to device using adb push, the app must restart on first launch. This is not a regression (tested in 1.8.1+). This may be an Android bug according to the log (attached): Android issue 2373 detected (missing intent CATEGORY_LAUNCHER or FLAG_ACTIVITY_RESET_TASK_IF_NEEDED), restarting app. This issue also intermittently affects the 3.X and 4.X emulators on regular launch (see linked issue). Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new project. 2. Package app or build to emulator to obtain the app.apk. 3. In the terminal, push apk to device using command (apk name may vary): 4. Navigate to app apk in device file system (i.e., Astro). 5. Click on the apk, press install, press open/run app. Expected Result: App should run without error. Actual Result: App force restarts on first run, but runs correctly on future launches.""""",title+description
