TIMOB-8750,12,"""Android: Production builds are breaking app events""","""""""h4. Problem Description  When creating a distribution build for the Google market, it will break the app.     h4. Actual Results  The app is broken when built for distribution.    h4. Expected results  The app working just fine (as the build to test/ build to device does).    h4. Test Case  1. Grab the code ( Included app source code in the internal comments)  2. Import it as project.  3. Build it to a device/emulator (open the app, Go to kalendar, then medecine, press +) - It will work fine.  4. Remove it from device/emulator.  5. Build the project for distribution. (open the app, go to kalendar, then medicine, press +) - it will crash.     h4. HD discussion  http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-412855    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Production builds are breaking app events
Description: """"h4. Problem Description When creating a distribution build for the Google market, it will break the app. h4. Actual Results The app is broken when built for distribution. h4. Expected results The app working just fine (as the build to test/ build to device does). h4. Test Case 1. Grab the code ( Included app source code in the internal comments) 2. Import it as project. 3. Build it to a device/emulator (open the app, Go to kalendar, then medecine, press +) - It will work fine. 4. Remove it from device/emulator. 5. Build the project for distribution. (open the app, go to kalendar, then medicine, press +) - it will crash. h4. HD discussion http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-412855 """"",title+description
TIMOB-8749,12,"""Android: app crashes when logging out""","""""""h2. Problem description  App crashes after logging out from the application.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Login and, from the home screen, press the logout button  Result: user is logged out but after a few seconds the app crashes with the classic 'Force close' error message.    2. The issue seems to be related to the usage of the activityIndicator.show() and activityIndicator.hide() methods as commenting them the logout works just fine. It is not reproducible on 1.7.6 also including activityIndicator.show/hide    Attaching log""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: app crashes when logging out
Description: """"h2. Problem description App crashes after logging out from the application. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Login and, from the home screen, press the logout button Result: user is logged out but after a few seconds the app crashes with the classic 'Force close' error message. 2. The issue seems to be related to the usage of the activityIndicator.show() and activityIndicator.hide() methods as commenting them the logout works just fine. It is not reproducible on 1.7.6 also including activityIndicator.show/hide Attaching log""""",title+description
TIMOB-8747,12,"""iOS: tabGroup not correctly reopened after being closed""","""""""h2. Problem description  ING reported issue for their app - tabGroup is not reopened after being closed    h2. Steps to reproduce:  1. Click on the login button and click on the plan name in the home window.  Result: tabgroup correctly displayed,   2. Click on the home tab and the home window opens (closing the tabGroup). Repeat step 1, clicking on the plan name.  Result: tabGroup is not opened anymore.     /Resource/common/tabhandler.js is where tabGroup behaviors are defined.    sample tabGroup is correctly displayed in 1.7.6""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: tabGroup not correctly reopened after being closed
Description: """"h2. Problem description ING reported issue for their app - tabGroup is not reopened after being closed h2. Steps to reproduce: 1. Click on the login button and click on the plan name in the home window. Result: tabgroup correctly displayed, 2. Click on the home tab and the home window opens (closing the tabGroup). Repeat step 1, clicking on the plan name. Result: tabGroup is not opened anymore. /Resource/common/tabhandler.js is where tabGroup behaviors are defined. sample tabGroup is correctly displayed in 1.7.6""""",title+description
