TIMOB-8740,12,"""MobileWeb: require() isn't properly loading async resources""","""""""require() fails to load async resources because if a module is loaded twice (which internally happens often), then only the first execute call is going to fire the callback. This means once a module is loaded, only the first time it's asked to be loaded does it notify the loader the resource is loaded. Other modules will never be marked as loaded.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: require() isn't properly loading async resources
Description: """"require() fails to load async resources because if a module is loaded twice (which internally happens often), then only the first execute call is going to fire the callback. This means once a module is loaded, only the first time it's asked to be loaded does it notify the loader the resource is loaded. Other modules will never be marked as loaded.""""",title+description
