TIMOB-8694,12,"""Android: Feature to add a property to detect if keyboard is being displayed or not""","""""""It has been requested to add a new feature to check if soft keyboard on the device is displayed or not. iOS currently has this feature implemented as the {{Ti.APP.keyboardVisible}} property.    Some initial investigation from Alan indicated that this may require some fancy work to detect window sizing changes, and therefore may be impractical. Feel free to invalidate this ticket if that is the case.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Feature to add a property to detect if keyboard is being displayed or not
Description: """"It has been requested to add a new feature to check if soft keyboard on the device is displayed or not. iOS currently has this feature implemented as the {{Ti.APP.keyboardVisible}} property. Some initial investigation from Alan indicated that this may require some fancy work to detect window sizing changes, and therefore may be impractical. Feel free to invalidate this ticket if that is the case.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8693,12,"""MobileWeb: Borders/width/height settings in absolute containers behave differently on Firefox.""","""""""It appears that firefox handles borders differently from the other browsers when width/height are specified in an absolute container. Need to work around this limitation. Buttons are most obviously affected by this bug, but all controls are affected.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Borders/width/height settings in absolute containers behave differently on Firefox.
Description: """"It appears that firefox handles borders differently from the other browsers when width/height are specified in an absolute container. Need to work around this limitation. Buttons are most obviously affected by this bug, but all controls are affected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8692,12,"""MobileWeb: Remove redundant containers in UI elements""","""""""There are a handful of UI elements that create containers inside the element when the element itself is a container, thus there is a duplicate container. ScrollView and ActivityIndicator are examples of this.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Remove redundant containers in UI elements
Description: """"There are a handful of UI elements that create containers inside the element when the element itself is a container, thus there is a duplicate container. ScrollView and ActivityIndicator are examples of this.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8690,12,"""iOS: Add a shouldLoad event / callback to WebView""","""""""h4. Feature Description     Just fire a new event in the UIWebView component when the delegate shouldStartLoadWithRequest was fired.    The event will return the URL that the application is trying to open.    It's useful to URLs that have redirects.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add a shouldLoad event / callback to WebView
Description: """"h4. Feature Description Just fire a new event in the UIWebView component when the delegate shouldStartLoadWithRequest was fired. The event will return the URL that the application is trying to open. It's useful to URLs that have redirects.""""",title+description
