TIMOB-8668,12,"""iPhone: OptionDialog has wrong rotation if displayed within a Modal Window and landscape orientation""","""""""h2. Problem    I think I found a bug in the OptionDialog. If one rotates an app to landscape, then opens a ModalWindow and there an OptionDialog. The OptionDialog is displayed centered and in portrait mode instead of landscape.    h2. Test case    {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({orientationModes:[Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT,     Titanium.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT,     Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,     Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT,]});  win1.open();     setTimeout(function() {         var win    = Ti.UI.createWindow({title: 'MyApp'});      var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: 'open'});         win.open({modal: true});      win.add(button);         button.addEventListener('click', function () {             var dialog = Ti.UI.createOptionDialog({title: 'test', options: ['1', '2', '3']});          dialog.show();      });     }, 5000);  {code}    I just set a timeout cause you need a few seconds to rotate the device. All orientations are allowed in {{tiapp.xml}}    h3. Steps to reproduce:    * Open app and rotate the iPhone or Simulator to landscape (cmd + left/right) while the window is black.  * After 5 seconds it'll open a Modal Window with white background and a button.  * Open the OptionDialog by pressing the 'open' Button.    h3. Result:    The option dialog is centered and not correct displayed. See attached image.    h2. Community Discussion    Q&A [iPhone: OptionDialog has wrong rotation if displayed within a Modal Window and landscape orientation|http://developer.<USER>com/question/134792/iphone-optiondialog-has-wrong-rotation-if-displayed-within-a-modal-window-and-landscape-orientation]""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: OptionDialog has wrong rotation if displayed within a Modal Window and landscape orientation
Description: """"h2. Problem I think I found a bug in the OptionDialog. If one rotates an app to landscape, then opens a ModalWindow and there an OptionDialog. The OptionDialog is displayed centered and in portrait mode instead of landscape. h2. Test case {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({orientationModes:[Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT, Titanium.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT,]}); win1.open(); setTimeout(function() { var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({title: 'MyApp'}); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: 'open'}); win.open({modal: true}); win.add(button); button.addEventListener('click', function () { var dialog = Ti.UI.createOptionDialog({title: 'test', options: ['1', '2', '3']}); dialog.show(); }); }, 5000); {code} I just set a timeout cause you need a few seconds to rotate the device. All orientations are allowed in {{tiapp.xml}} h3. Steps to reproduce: * Open app and rotate the iPhone or Simulator to landscape (cmd + left/right) while the window is black. * After 5 seconds it'll open a Modal Window with white background and a button. * Open the OptionDialog by pressing the 'open' Button. h3. Result: The option dialog is centered and not correct displayed. See attached image. h2. Community Discussion Q&A [iPhone: OptionDialog has wrong rotation if displayed within a Modal Window and landscape orientation|http://developer.<USER>com/question/134792/iphone-optiondialog-has-wrong-rotation-if-displayed-within-a-modal-window-and-landscape-orientation]""""",title+description
TIMOB-8667,12,"""Android: KS Platform > Sockets > Connecting Socket: Read Error on Disconnect""","""""""When using Kitchen Sink (or KitchenSink-Nook on Kindle Fire/Nook Color) Platform > Sockets > Connecting Socket the socket is connected, then disconnected, a read error is generated in 2.3+ devices. A correct 'Disconnected' error is generated on 2.2 devices and Nook Color.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run Kitchen Sink => Platform > Sockets > Connecting Sockets.  2. Follow https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Sockets+Test+Plan Platform->Sockets->Connecting socket up to Step 5.  3. Press Disconnect (Step 6).    Expected Result:    'Disconnected' message should appear. Python server should remain active, and the app should no longer be able to write data to the server.    Actual Result:    'READ ERROR: Unable to read from socket, IO error' appears. The python server exits.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS Platform > Sockets > Connecting Socket: Read Error on Disconnect
Description: """"When using Kitchen Sink (or KitchenSink-Nook on Kindle Fire/Nook Color) Platform > Sockets > Connecting Socket the socket is connected, then disconnected, a read error is generated in 2.3+ devices. A correct 'Disconnected' error is generated on 2.2 devices and Nook Color. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run Kitchen Sink => Platform > Sockets > Connecting Sockets. 2. Follow https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Sockets+Test+Plan Platform->Sockets->Connecting socket up to Step 5. 3. Press Disconnect (Step 6). Expected Result: 'Disconnected' message should appear. Python server should remain active, and the app should no longer be able to write data to the server. Actual Result: 'READ ERROR: Unable to read from socket, IO error' appears. The python server exits.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8666,12,"""Android: KS Facebook>Run Query does not display status messages of friends""","""""""on KS >MashUps >Facebook>run Query does not display status message    steps to reproduce:  1:log in to Facebook  2:post a status message  3:on the device tap on Query  4:Tap on run Query      Actual Result: Friends are displayed,but no status messages are shown  Expected Result: Friends should be displayed with their status messages      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS Facebook>Run Query does not display status messages of friends
Description: """"on KS >MashUps >Facebook>run Query does not display status message steps to reproduce: 1:log in to Facebook 2:post a status message 3:on the device tap on Query 4:Tap on run Query Actual Result: Friends are displayed,but no status messages are shown Expected Result: Friends should be displayed with their status messages """"",title+description
TIMOB-8664,12,"""MobileWeb: IE specific endTransition event should be MSTransitionEnd""","""""""There is a typo in Ti/_/Element where the IE specific endTransition event should be called """"""""MSTransitionEnd"""""""", not """"""""msTransitionEnd"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: IE specific endTransition event should be MSTransitionEnd
Description: """"There is a typo in Ti/_/Element where the IE specific endTransition event should be called """"""""MSTransitionEnd"""""""", not """"""""msTransitionEnd"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-8663,12,"""R&D: Evaluate various obfuscation / minification engines for common use across platforms""","""""""We need to investigate the various JS obfuscation and minification options in the wild and decide on a common approach across platforms. Some obvious contenders:  * Google Closure Compiler  * YUI compressor    When evaluating the various options, we should keep in mind the ability to feed in more data (i.e. an AST or other API heuristics) to further optimize the minification <USER>""""",Sub-task,"Title: R&D: Evaluate various obfuscation / minification engines for common use across platforms
Description: """"We need to investigate the various JS obfuscation and minification options in the wild and decide on a common approach across platforms. Some obvious contenders: * Google Closure Compiler * YUI compressor When evaluating the various options, we should keep in mind the ability to feed in more data (i.e. an AST or other API heuristics) to further optimize the minification <USER>""",title+description
TIMOB-8661,12,"""MobileWeb: Add vendor prefixed vibrate function for Ti.Media.vibrate()""","""""""Mobile web uses navigator.vibrate() when it should check for navigator.vibrate and navigator.mozVibrate. Probably also should check for webkitVibrate too.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Add vendor prefixed vibrate function for Ti.Media.vibrate()
Description: """"Mobile web uses navigator.vibrate() when it should check for navigator.vibrate and navigator.mozVibrate. Probably also should check for webkitVibrate too.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8660,12,"""Android: KS Table Views > Insert row does not create headers where needed""","""""""on KitchenSink BaseUI>Views>Table Views>insert row does not create headers where needed    Steps to reproduce  1:tap on InsertRow Above-Header-1  2:tap on InsertRow Above-Header-2  3:tap on InsertRow below-Header    Actual Result: Rows are created without any headers  Expected result: Rows should be created above or below the current row with header      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS Table Views > Insert row does not create headers where needed
Description: """"on KitchenSink BaseUI>Views>Table Views>insert row does not create headers where needed Steps to reproduce 1:tap on InsertRow Above-Header-1 2:tap on InsertRow Above-Header-2 3:tap on InsertRow below-Header Actual Result: Rows are created without any headers Expected result: Rows should be created above or below the current row with header """"",title+description
TIMOB-8659,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Filesystem base64 encodes application/x-javascript files""","""""""When using Ti.Filesystem to read in a javascript file, it will base64 encode the file into the blob because the mime type starts with """"""""application"""""""". The """"""""application/x-javascript"""""""" mime type will need to be whitelisted to be treated as plain text.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Filesystem base64 encodes application/x-javascript files
Description: """"When using Ti.Filesystem to read in a javascript file, it will base64 encode the file into the blob because the mime type starts with """"""""application"""""""". The """"""""application/x-javascript"""""""" mime type will need to be whitelisted to be treated as plain text.""""",title+description
