TIMOB-8641,12,"""Android: KitchenSink-Nook: SIGSEGV crash on app restart after using database""","""""""When using KitchenSink-Nook (sequentially from """"""""Base UI > Views > Table Views > Delete Row"""""""" to """"""""Platform > Database""""""""), in the Database test, after pressing """"""""DB in 2nd Context"""""""", then backing out of the app and redeploying, the app crashed on restart. Unable to reproduce.    Steps to Reproduce.    1. Run KitchenSink-Nook tests sequentially from """"""""Base UI > Views > Table Views > Delete Row"""""""" to """"""""Platform > Database"""""""".  2. In Database, click """"""""DB in 2nd Context"""""""".  3. Press back repeatedly (at a normal pace) until app is closed.  4. Click on the app in the phone app browser to start it.    Expected Result:    App should load.    Actual Result:    Crash.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink-Nook: SIGSEGV crash on app restart after using database
Description: """"When using KitchenSink-Nook (sequentially from """"""""Base UI > Views > Table Views > Delete Row"""""""" to """"""""Platform > Database""""""""), in the Database test, after pressing """"""""DB in 2nd Context"""""""", then backing out of the app and redeploying, the app crashed on restart. Unable to reproduce. Steps to Reproduce. 1. Run KitchenSink-Nook tests sequentially from """"""""Base UI > Views > Table Views > Delete Row"""""""" to """"""""Platform > Database"""""""". 2. In Database, click """"""""DB in 2nd Context"""""""". 3. Press back repeatedly (at a normal pace) until app is closed. 4. Click on the app in the phone app browser to start it. Expected Result: App should load. Actual Result: Crash.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8640,12,"""CLI: Evaluate using node.js in build scripts""","""""""We need to investigate what it would take to migrate build infrastructure from python to node.js (or another alternative, ideally a solution that allows us to use JS end-to-end.) We need to figure out issues like:    * Distribution (footprint, installation/distribution, etc.)  * API assessment  * Supporting infrastructure  * IPC (for studio and drillbit/simulator integration)""""""",Sub-task,"Title: CLI: Evaluate using node.js in build scripts
Description: """"We need to investigate what it would take to migrate build infrastructure from python to node.js (or another alternative, ideally a solution that allows us to use JS end-to-end.) We need to figure out issues like: * Distribution (footprint, installation/distribution, etc.) * API assessment * Supporting infrastructure * IPC (for studio and drillbit/simulator integration)""""",title+description
TIMOB-8639,12,"""Android: WebView: KS crashes when Zoom in button pressed to max""","""""""in KS>BaseUI>Views>Web Views>Image URL ,KS crashes when Zoom in is done to the maximum and return button is pressed the second time.    Steps to Reproduce:  1:tap on KS>BaseUI>Views>web Views>Image URL  2:swipe on the screen to make visible the zoom-in zoom-out button  3:keep tapping on zoom-in button until max  4:press on the back button  5:repeat 1 thru 4      Actual Result: KS Crashes and log shows    Activity org.<USER>titanium.TiActivity has leaked IntentReceiver android.widget.ZoomButtonsController$1@4129c650    Expected Result: no Crashes should occur    note: Also fails when Zoom-in is activated for Inline HTML, Inline HTML w/ Trans Bg,Inline HTML w/Color Bg          """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView: KS crashes when Zoom in button pressed to max
Description: """"in KS>BaseUI>Views>Web Views>Image URL ,KS crashes when Zoom in is done to the maximum and return button is pressed the second time. Steps to Reproduce: 1:tap on KS>BaseUI>Views>web Views>Image URL 2:swipe on the screen to make visible the zoom-in zoom-out button 3:keep tapping on zoom-in button until max 4:press on the back button 5:repeat 1 thru 4 Actual Result: KS Crashes and log shows Activity org.<USER>titanium.TiActivity has leaked IntentReceiver android.widget.ZoomButtonsController$1@4129c650 Expected Result: no Crashes should occur note: Also fails when Zoom-in is activated for Inline HTML, Inline HTML w/ Trans Bg,Inline HTML w/Color Bg """"",title+description
TIMOB-8638,12,"""Android: MapView loses user location when it loses focus or on resume""","""""""When you create a map view with userLocation = true, the user location is shown until the focus changes, the app is placed in the background or the device goes to sleep. Then the user's location disappears. Several workarounds have been tried unsuccessfully and this has been reported multiple times in Q&A.    Test case:    {code:filename=""""""""app.js""""""""}  var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup();  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Tab 1',      backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({        icon:'KS_nav_views.png',      title:'Tab 1',      window:win1  });  var regionSV = {latitude:37.337681,longitude:-122.038193,latitudeDelta:0.04, longitudeDelta:0.04};      var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({      mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,      animate:true,      region: regionSV,      regionFit:true,      userLocation:true,      visible: true,  });  win1.add(mapview);      var win2 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Tab 2',      backgroundColor:'#fff'  });  var tab2 = Titanium.UI.createTab({        icon:'KS_nav_ui.png',      title:'Tab 2',      window:win2  });    var label2 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({   color:'#999',   text:'I am Window 2',   font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'},   textAlign:'center',   width:'auto'  });    win2.add(label2);    tabGroup.addTab(tab1);    tabGroup.addTab(tab2);        // open tab group  tabGroup.open();  {code}    To reproduce:     1) Run app, verify that your blue userlocation marker shows up.    2) click on Tab 2 then back on Tab 1. Where are you?       If you're not on this map, you may need to change the region so      your marker shows.    Other reports:    http://developer.<USER>com/question/121360/userlocation-marker-disapppers-after-the-mapview-lost-focus  http://developer.<USER>com/question/127963/userlocation-marker-blue-dot-disappears-bug-still-exist--android  http://developer.<USER>com/question/120280/android-map-user-location-disappears  http://developer.<USER>com/question/125490/android---userlocation-marker-disappears  https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-105 (reported in relation to another issue, which was resolved)  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: MapView loses user location when it loses focus or on resume
Description: """"When you create a map view with userLocation = true, the user location is shown until the focus changes, the app is placed in the background or the device goes to sleep. Then the user's location disappears. Several workarounds have been tried unsuccessfully and this has been reported multiple times in Q&A. Test case: {code:filename=""""""""app.js""""""""} var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup(); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({ icon:'KS_nav_views.png', title:'Tab 1', window:win1 }); var regionSV = {latitude:37.337681,longitude:-122.038193,latitudeDelta:0.04, longitudeDelta:0.04}; var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({ mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, animate:true, region: regionSV, regionFit:true, userLocation:true, visible: true, }); win1.add(mapview); var win2 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Tab 2', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var tab2 = Titanium.UI.createTab({ icon:'KS_nav_ui.png', title:'Tab 2', window:win2 }); var label2 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({ color:'#999', text:'I am Window 2', font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'}, textAlign:'center', width:'auto' }); win2.add(label2); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.addTab(tab2); // open tab group tabGroup.open(); {code} To reproduce: 1) Run app, verify that your blue userlocation marker shows up. 2) click on Tab 2 then back on Tab 1. Where are you? If you're not on this map, you may need to change the region so your marker shows. Other reports: http://developer.<USER>com/question/121360/userlocation-marker-disapppers-after-the-mapview-lost-focus http://developer.<USER>com/question/127963/userlocation-marker-blue-dot-disappears-bug-still-exist--android http://developer.<USER>com/question/120280/android-map-user-location-disappears http://developer.<USER>com/question/125490/android---userlocation-marker-disappears https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-105 (reported in relation to another issue, which was resolved) """"",title+description
TIMOB-8637,12,"""Android: auto-focuses and shows keyboard for first textfield on Samsung Galaxy Tab on window open or textfield create after window open""","""""""On a Samsung Galaxy Tab running Android 3.2, if you have a textfield in your window, it will auto set focus to it when either the window is opened or when you create the textfield after the window is opened. This is OK for some situations, such as when you have a form and want it to set focus to the first element by default. However, in other cases, such as when you have a TextField hiding off of the screen and then slide it into view when the user presses a button, it becomes an issue as the keyboard slides up for no reason. Note that it does not set focus to the textfield within the Android emulator.    Here is code to reproduce, which creates the textfield after opening the window.        And more code, which shows the same behavior when creating the textfield and then opening the window.        Even setting the textfield to enabled: false, it still auto focuses it. At the very least, there should be a property that you can set that will prevent it from auto focusing the textfield. Ideally it should not auto focus the textfield, that way you have the option of focusing it with the textfield.focus(); method yourself.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: auto-focuses and shows keyboard for first textfield on Samsung Galaxy Tab on window open or textfield create after window open
Description: """"On a Samsung Galaxy Tab running Android 3.2, if you have a textfield in your window, it will auto set focus to it when either the window is opened or when you create the textfield after the window is opened. This is OK for some situations, such as when you have a form and want it to set focus to the first element by default. However, in other cases, such as when you have a TextField hiding off of the screen and then slide it into view when the user presses a button, it becomes an issue as the keyboard slides up for no reason. Note that it does not set focus to the textfield within the Android emulator. Here is code to reproduce, which creates the textfield after opening the window. And more code, which shows the same behavior when creating the textfield and then opening the window. Even setting the textfield to enabled: false, it still auto focuses it. At the very least, there should be a property that you can set that will prevent it from auto focusing the textfield. Ideally it should not auto focus the textfield, that way you have the option of focusing it with the textfield.focus(); method yourself.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8636,12,"""Android: KitchenSink-Nook: App freezes with 'no window to dispatch pointer action' logs on touch""","""""""When using KitchenSink-Nook from the beginning to Table Views > Append Row, then clicking on the Base UI tab, then clicking on Base UI > Views, the app screen turned black and touch events logged as 'No window to dispatch pointer action'. No force close dialog appeared. The app permanently had a black screen. App is force-closed when the back button is pressed. Unable to reproduce.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink-Nook from Base UI > Tab Groups to Base UI > Views > Table Views > Append Row.  2. Go back to the main menu and press Base UI > Views.    Expected Result:    Views menu should load.    Actual Result:    Screen turns black and 'No window to dispatch pointer action' logs to console. App never actually hard crashes or force-closes.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink-Nook: App freezes with 'no window to dispatch pointer action' logs on touch
Description: """"When using KitchenSink-Nook from the beginning to Table Views > Append Row, then clicking on the Base UI tab, then clicking on Base UI > Views, the app screen turned black and touch events logged as 'No window to dispatch pointer action'. No force close dialog appeared. The app permanently had a black screen. App is force-closed when the back button is pressed. Unable to reproduce. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink-Nook from Base UI > Tab Groups to Base UI > Views > Table Views > Append Row. 2. Go back to the main menu and press Base UI > Views. Expected Result: Views menu should load. Actual Result: Screen turns black and 'No window to dispatch pointer action' logs to console. App never actually hard crashes or force-closes.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8635,12,"""Android: KitchenSink-Nook: ANR when Table Views > Append Row test is first clicked""","""""""When running KitchenSink-Nook from the beginning, a crash occurred when loading Base UI > Views > Table Views > Append Row. The screen turned black, and a force close dialog appeared. keyDispatchingTimedOut was logged to the console and a stack trace was generated (attached). The crash occurred as soon as 'Append Row' was clicked. Unable to reproduce.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink-Nook.  2. Use all tests from Base UI > Tab Groups to Base UI > Views > Table Views > Table Empty Dataset (Create).  3. Click Table Views > Append Row.    Expected Result:    Test should load.    Actual Result:    Black screen, force close dialog, ANR console logs, stack trace.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink-Nook: ANR when Table Views > Append Row test is first clicked
Description: """"When running KitchenSink-Nook from the beginning, a crash occurred when loading Base UI > Views > Table Views > Append Row. The screen turned black, and a force close dialog appeared. keyDispatchingTimedOut was logged to the console and a stack trace was generated (attached). The crash occurred as soon as 'Append Row' was clicked. Unable to reproduce. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink-Nook. 2. Use all tests from Base UI > Tab Groups to Base UI > Views > Table Views > Table Empty Dataset (Create). 3. Click Table Views > Append Row. Expected Result: Test should load. Actual Result: Black screen, force close dialog, ANR console logs, stack trace.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8634,12,"""iOS: Unexpected warning from UITabBarController""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Create a default titanium mobile application   2. Run on device while viewing the logs    Actual:  <Warning>: -[UITabBarController setSelectedViewController:] only a view controller in the tab bar controller's list of view controllers can be selected.    Expected:  Not to throw a warning    Note:   Happens back to 1.8.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Unexpected warning from UITabBarController
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Create a default titanium mobile application 2. Run on device while viewing the logs Actual: <Warning>: -[UITabBarController setSelectedViewController:] only a view controller in the tab bar controller's list of view controllers can be selected. Expected: Not to throw a warning Note: Happens back to 1.8.2""""",title+description
