TIMOB-8620,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.View is a live reference, not copy""","""""""h1. BUG  ----    Currently, when {{Ti.UI.View.children}} is queried, the live copy of children is returned, meaning that if it is modified in-place during a loop (which might be a common operation) there are some issues. Even worse, it follows copy semantics before a view is put into the full hierarchy, and reference semantics after.    h1. INITIAL DESCRIPTION  ----  h4. Feature description  Provide an easy way to clean the contents of a view/window, like a magic """"""""remove all children"""""""" that will remove them in the right order.     h4. Current behavior    Customer is trying to do this:        which causes a crash in the app because they are removing stuff without any order. Maybe we should provide a tree with all the dependencies in the view, so they can be properly removed.     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.View is a live reference, not copy
Description: """"h1. BUG ---- Currently, when {{Ti.UI.View.children}} is queried, the live copy of children is returned, meaning that if it is modified in-place during a loop (which might be a common operation) there are some issues. Even worse, it follows copy semantics before a view is put into the full hierarchy, and reference semantics after. h1. INITIAL DESCRIPTION ---- h4. Feature description Provide an easy way to clean the contents of a view/window, like a magic """"""""remove all children"""""""" that will remove them in the right order. h4. Current behavior Customer is trying to do this: which causes a crash in the app because they are removing stuff without any order. Maybe we should provide a tree with all the dependencies in the view, so they can be properly removed. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8619,12,"""iOS: Overlay views on camera are always displayed in portrait mode""","""""""h2. Problem description  Overlays on Camera are always displayed in portrait mode, no matter which orientation is set in tiapp.xml or using .orientationModes = [Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT/RIGHT]    h2. Steps to reproduce  - Add <orientation>Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT</orientation> to TiApp.xml for iphone orientations  - Run sample code attached on real device    Camera window custom overlays should be shown in landscape mode.  Actual result: custom overlay is only shown in portrait mode    h2. Additional note  Customer ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-624949  Jira bug https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-8555 should be a related consequence of this bug""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Overlay views on camera are always displayed in portrait mode
Description: """"h2. Problem description Overlays on Camera are always displayed in portrait mode, no matter which orientation is set in tiapp.xml or using .orientationModes = [Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT/RIGHT] h2. Steps to reproduce - Add <orientation>Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT</orientation> to TiApp.xml for iphone orientations - Run sample code attached on real device Camera window custom overlays should be shown in landscape mode. Actual result: custom overlay is only shown in portrait mode h2. Additional note Customer ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-624949 Jira bug https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-8555 should be a related consequence of this bug""""",title+description
