TIMOB-8615,12,"""iOS : Options Dialog - In KS > Base UI > Views > Options Dialog - Pressing the Show w/hide, animated and Show w/hide, nonanimated buttons caused the app to crash""","""""""*Note* This exists in 2.0.0 also    Steps to reproduce    1. Launch 2_0_X KS on iOS device  2. Navigate to KS > Base UI > Views > Options Dialog  3. Press Show w/hide, animated  4. Press Option 1  5. Press Show w/hide, nonanimated  6. Press Option 1  7. Press Show w/hide, animated  8. Press Option 1    Actual result:  The app crashed    Expected result:  The option dialog is dismissed without crashing""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Options Dialog - In KS > Base UI > Views > Options Dialog - Pressing the Show w/hide, animated and Show w/hide, nonanimated buttons caused the app to crash
Description: """"*Note* This exists in 2.0.0 also Steps to reproduce 1. Launch 2_0_X KS on iOS device 2. Navigate to KS > Base UI > Views > Options Dialog 3. Press Show w/hide, animated 4. Press Option 1 5. Press Show w/hide, nonanimated 6. Press Option 1 7. Press Show w/hide, animated 8. Press Option 1 Actual result: The app crashed Expected result: The option dialog is dismissed without crashing""""",title+description
TIMOB-8614,12,"""iOS: ImageView's load event fires before image's size is known""","""""""h3. Problem    The imageView's load event seems to fire prematurely on the first load of the app. Subsequent loads work as intended however it's most likely because the image is cached. Deleting the app and re-running will make the problem appear again.    h3. Steps to Reproduce    1. Run the code sample below        2. On initial load, the size and width are returned as 0, On later runs the approproiate size and width are returned.    3. To recreate the issue, delete the app from the simulator and clean the project and rerun the app.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ImageView's load event fires before image's size is known
Description: """"h3. Problem The imageView's load event seems to fire prematurely on the first load of the app. Subsequent loads work as intended however it's most likely because the image is cached. Deleting the app and re-running will make the problem appear again. h3. Steps to Reproduce 1. Run the code sample below 2. On initial load, the size and width are returned as 0, On later runs the approproiate size and width are returned. 3. To recreate the issue, delete the app from the simulator and clean the project and rerun the app.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8613,12,"""iOS: window title bar doesn't show""","""""""The window title bar doesn't show.  h4. Repro Steps  1. Run the below code in the app.js  2. You can see window without the title.    [code]  var tabGrp = Ti.UI.createTabGroup({});  var tab = Ti.UI.createTab({});    var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' });    var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({  title:'Click Me'   })    btn.addEventListener('click',function(e){  var titleView = Ti.UI.createView({  })  var Lable = Ti.UI.createLabel({  text:'TEST',  top:10  })  //This will not work  //titleView.add(Lable);  //win1.titleControl = titleView;    //This will work  win1.titleControl = Lable;  })    win1.add(btn);    tab.window = win1;    tabGrp.addTab(tab);  tabGrp.open();  [code]""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: window title bar doesn't show
Description: """"The window title bar doesn't show. h4. Repro Steps 1. Run the below code in the app.js 2. You can see window without the title. [code] var tabGrp = Ti.UI.createTabGroup({}); var tab = Ti.UI.createTab({}); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Click Me' }) btn.addEventListener('click',function(e){ var titleView = Ti.UI.createView({ }) var Lable = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text:'TEST', top:10 }) //This will not work //titleView.add(Lable); //win1.titleControl = titleView; //This will work win1.titleControl = Lable; }) win1.add(btn); tab.window = win1; tabGrp.addTab(tab); tabGrp.open(); [code]""""",title+description
