TIMOB-8555,12,"""iOS: Camera needs to support overlay for Landscape and Portrait (right now, you can only provide one overlay).""","""""""h4. Problem Description  As there is no way to limit the iPad2/3 camera from automatically changing the orientation of the live camera if there is an orientation change, I need to find a way to dynamically change the overlay that we are showing over the live camera view.    I have added an orientationchange event handler to allow me to try to reset the overlay view width/height but any changes that I make to the overlay view width/height (changing from landscape to portrait and vica versa) do not appear to be picked up and applied to the overlay - the overlay remains showing with the original width and height in the live camera view.    h4. Actual Results  The overlay won't change    h4. Expected results  being able to provide the right overlay for landscape or portrait    h4. Extra info  One way to accomplish this would be to provide a secondary overview for the landscape or portrait orientation""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Camera needs to support overlay for Landscape and Portrait (right now, you can only provide one overlay).
Description: """"h4. Problem Description As there is no way to limit the iPad2/3 camera from automatically changing the orientation of the live camera if there is an orientation change, I need to find a way to dynamically change the overlay that we are showing over the live camera view. I have added an orientationchange event handler to allow me to try to reset the overlay view width/height but any changes that I make to the overlay view width/height (changing from landscape to portrait and vica versa) do not appear to be picked up and applied to the overlay - the overlay remains showing with the original width and height in the live camera view. h4. Actual Results The overlay won't change h4. Expected results being able to provide the right overlay for landscape or portrait h4. Extra info One way to accomplish this would be to provide a secondary overview for the landscape or portrait orientation""""",title+description
