TIMOB-8546,12,"""Android:  handle invalid values on width and height gracefully""","""""""when invalid values are set for width and height an exception occurs when trying to convert the values into TiDimension:        * this would be when win.width is undefined.  This test case can be found in the KS camera test.        Resulting error:      We should gracefully handle invalid values when they are set or processed either by throwing exceptions to let the developer know of the problem or defaulting to valid values.  Requires parity discussion.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: handle invalid values on width and height gracefully
Description: """"when invalid values are set for width and height an exception occurs when trying to convert the values into TiDimension: * this would be when win.width is undefined. This test case can be found in the KS camera test. Resulting error: We should gracefully handle invalid values when they are set or processed either by throwing exceptions to let the developer know of the problem or defaulting to valid values. Requires parity discussion. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8545,12,"""Android: when imageview width or height are set to 0 or invalid, no bitmap scaling occurs""","""""""When the imageview has no valid width or height we dont scale the underlying bitmap.  This is extremely problematic since the resulting bitmap loaded into memory can be very large.  We should have a default level of scaling based on screen size reported by the window manager in order to avoid run away memory usage.  This can be tested with the KS camera test and setting the imageview width and height (in the success callback) to Ti.UI.FILL.    Example log output resulting:  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: when imageview width or height are set to 0 or invalid, no bitmap scaling occurs
Description: """"When the imageview has no valid width or height we dont scale the underlying bitmap. This is extremely problematic since the resulting bitmap loaded into memory can be very large. We should have a default level of scaling based on screen size reported by the window manager in order to avoid run away memory usage. This can be tested with the KS camera test and setting the imageview width and height (in the success callback) to Ti.UI.FILL. Example log output resulting: """"",title+description
TIMOB-8518,12,"""Android: ImageView does not handle width or height set to Ti.UI.FILL correctly""","""""""This behavior can be seen when running the KS (1.8.2 version) camera test.  Setting the width for the image view in the success callback to Ti.UI.FILL will result in the bounds of the bitmap created not being able to be determined.  A work around of setting width to win.size.width addresses the symptom but there appears to be a timing issue where the bounds of the bitmap are determined before the Ti.UI.SIZE value is computed resulting in massive bitmaps with no scaling.  This can result in memory issues.    It is suspected that this is a order of operations issue that needs to be addressed.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView does not handle width or height set to Ti.UI.FILL correctly
Description: """"This behavior can be seen when running the KS (1.8.2 version) camera test. Setting the width for the image view in the success callback to Ti.UI.FILL will result in the bounds of the bitmap created not being able to be determined. A work around of setting width to win.size.width addresses the symptom but there appears to be a timing issue where the bounds of the bitmap are determined before the Ti.UI.SIZE value is computed resulting in massive bitmaps with no scaling. This can result in memory issues. It is suspected that this is a order of operations issue that needs to be addressed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8516,12,"""iOS: UI.View: intermittent deadlock warning""","""""""When running the code below, a deadlock warning intermittently appears:    Apr  4 14:59:27 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>timob8193[0x13cc][3489] <Notice>: [WARN] Timing out waiting on main thread. Possibly a deadlock?  in TiThreadPerformOnMainThread (TiBase.m:238)    Attempted to reproduce in 2.0.0.GA, but could not.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code.        Expected Result:    Views should appear without deadlock warnings.    Actual Result:    Views appear with deadlock warning, intermittent.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI.View: intermittent deadlock warning
Description: """"When running the code below, a deadlock warning intermittently appears: Apr 4 14:59:27 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>timob8193[0x13cc][3489] <Notice>: [WARN] Timing out waiting on main thread. Possibly a deadlock? in TiThreadPerformOnMainThread (TiBase.m:238) Attempted to reproduce in 2.0.0.GA, but could not. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code. Expected Result: Views should appear without deadlock warnings. Actual Result: Views appear with deadlock warning, intermittent.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8512,12,"""iOS: you can' ask new Facebook permission without user logout""","""""""h1. Description  If you ask some Facebook permissions to a user and (s)he accepts, you won't be enabled to ask her/him for a new permission until (s)he disconnect from Facebook.      h1. Steps to reproduce  I have attached an 'app.js' file to reproduce the bug:   - check that the permissions asked are: ['email', 'user_birthday'] (see the label at the bottom of the windonw)   - click on the """"""""Facebook.authorize()"""""""" button to call: Ti.Facebook.authorize()   - accept the permissions requested   - now, click on """"""""Change permissions""""""""   - check that the permissions asked are: ['email', 'user_birthday', 'user_likes'] (see the label at the bottom of the windonw)   - click on the """"""""Facebook.authorize()"""""""" button to call: Ti.Facebook.authorize()  ==> the app doesn't ask for the new permission   - click on """"""""Logout Facebook""""""""   - click on the """"""""Facebook.authorize()"""""""" button to call: Ti.Facebook.authorize()  ==> the app ask for the new permission      This issue is due to your class [FacebookModule.m|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/FacebookModule.m] at this line:  {code:title=FacebookModule.m|borderStyle=solid}  -(void)authorize:(id)args  {   ENSURE_UI_THREAD(authorize, args);     VerboseLog(@""""""""[DEBUG] facebook authorize"""""""");     if ([self isLoggedIn]) // <============== [HERE] ===============   {    // if already authorized, this should do nothing    return;   }     if (appid==nil)   {    [self throwException:@""""""""missing appid"""""""" subreason:nil location:CODELOCATION];   }     // forget in case it fails   [self _unsave];     NSArray *permissions_ = permissions == nil ? [NSArray array] : permissions;   [facebook setForceDialog:forceDialogAuth];   [facebook authorize:permissions_];  }  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: you can' ask new Facebook permission without user logout
Description: """"h1. Description If you ask some Facebook permissions to a user and (s)he accepts, you won't be enabled to ask her/him for a new permission until (s)he disconnect from Facebook. h1. Steps to reproduce I have attached an 'app.js' file to reproduce the bug: - check that the permissions asked are: ['email', 'user_birthday'] (see the label at the bottom of the windonw) - click on the """"""""Facebook.authorize()"""""""" button to call: Ti.Facebook.authorize() - accept the permissions requested - now, click on """"""""Change permissions"""""""" - check that the permissions asked are: ['email', 'user_birthday', 'user_likes'] (see the label at the bottom of the windonw) - click on the """"""""Facebook.authorize()"""""""" button to call: Ti.Facebook.authorize() ==> the app doesn't ask for the new permission - click on """"""""Logout Facebook"""""""" - click on the """"""""Facebook.authorize()"""""""" button to call: Ti.Facebook.authorize() ==> the app ask for the new permission This issue is due to your class [FacebookModule.m|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/FacebookModule.m] at this line: {code:title=FacebookModule.m|borderStyle=solid} -(void)authorize:(id)args { ENSURE_UI_THREAD(authorize, args); VerboseLog(@""""""""[DEBUG] facebook authorize""""""""); if ([self isLoggedIn]) // <============== [HERE] =============== { // if already authorized, this should do nothing return; } if (appid==nil) { [self throwException:@""""""""missing appid"""""""" subreason:nil location:CODELOCATION]; } // forget in case it fails [self _unsave]; NSArray *permissions_ = permissions == nil ? [NSArray array] : permissions; [facebook setForceDialog:forceDialogAuth]; [facebook authorize:permissions_]; } {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-8511,12,"""MobileWeb: Add support for FirefoxOS""","""""""This encompasses:    * Generation of manifest.webapp file  * Enable cross-domain XHR  * New tiapp.xml settings  * Varied icon size generation  * Expose an API for installing apps to home screen  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Add support for FirefoxOS
Description: """"This encompasses: * Generation of manifest.webapp file * Enable cross-domain XHR * New tiapp.xml settings * Varied icon size generation * Expose an API for installing apps to home screen """"",title+description
TIMOB-8510,12,"""Ti API: Provide a Way To Override the Accept-Encoding header in the HTTPClient""","""""""The Accept-Encoding header is currently ignored when set on the HTTPClient.   The following code has no affect on the header sent out - it always defaults to gzip     xhr.open(""""""""POST"""""""", """"""""http://url.tld/api_jsonrpc.php"""""""");   xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""Accept-Encoding"""""""", """""""""""""""");     Looking at the generated code, gzip is always set to be the Accept-Encoding header.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Provide a Way To Override the Accept-Encoding header in the HTTPClient
Description: """"The Accept-Encoding header is currently ignored when set on the HTTPClient. The following code has no affect on the header sent out - it always defaults to gzip xhr.open(""""""""POST"""""""", """"""""http://url.tld/api_jsonrpc.php""""""""); xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""Accept-Encoding"""""""", """"""""""""""""); Looking at the generated code, gzip is always set to be the Accept-Encoding header. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8509,12,"""Error when upgrading Xcode 3.x to 4.2 (unusable install)""","""""""h4. Problem Description  we used xCode 3.X for some time with Ti Studio (latest), today we upgraded to xCode 4.2 on top of OSX snow leopard.    Now, we can't build anyome, any project, new or old, including Kitchen Sink results in.     h4. Actual Results  [INFO] Detected third-party module: ti.barcode/1.7  [INFO] Detected third-party module: ti.barcode/1.7  [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.1 (01/27/12 17:31 a24502a)  [INFO] iPhone Device family: iphone  [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0  [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone  [ERROR]   [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):    File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1286, in main      execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % link_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=__LOG__ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s %s %s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version,debugstr,kroll_coverage)],False)    File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1192, in execute_xcode      output = run.run(args,False,False,o)    File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run      sys.exit(rc)  SystemExit: 65  when trying to run directly from xCode we get this error:    env: python: No such file or directory        h4. Expected Results  The machine working fine after upgrading Xcode.    h4. Extra info    """"""",Bug,"Title: Error when upgrading Xcode 3.x to 4.2 (unusable install)
Description: """"h4. Problem Description we used xCode 3.X for some time with Ti Studio (latest), today we upgraded to xCode 4.2 on top of OSX snow leopard. Now, we can't build anyome, any project, new or old, including Kitchen Sink results in. h4. Actual Results [INFO] Detected third-party module: ti.barcode/1.7 [INFO] Detected third-party module: ti.barcode/1.7 [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.1 (01/27/12 17:31 a24502a) [INFO] iPhone Device family: iphone [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0 [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone [ERROR] [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1286, in main execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % link_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=__LOG__ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s %s %s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version,debugstr,kroll_coverage)],False) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1192, in execute_xcode output = run.run(args,False,False,o) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65 when trying to run directly from xCode we get this error: env: python: No such file or directory h4. Expected Results The machine working fine after upgrading Xcode. h4. Extra info """"",title+description
