TIMOB-8452,12,"""iOS: 4.3 Device: KitchenSink: Controls > Picker Time Picker: am pm column missing""","""""""Time Picker in KitchenSink is missing am/pm column on 4.3 device. Does not occur in simulator. Works in 4.3 simulator and iOS 5.X. Also missing in 1.8.2, not an immediate regression.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink > Controls > Picker Time Picker.    Expected Result:    Should see hour, minutes, and am/pm columns.    Actual Result:    Only see hour and minute columns. am/pm missing. Screenshot attached. Log attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: 4.3 Device: KitchenSink: Controls > Picker Time Picker: am pm column missing
Description: """"Time Picker in KitchenSink is missing am/pm column on 4.3 device. Does not occur in simulator. Works in 4.3 simulator and iOS 5.X. Also missing in 1.8.2, not an immediate regression. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink > Controls > Picker Time Picker. Expected Result: Should see hour, minutes, and am/pm columns. Actual Result: Only see hour and minute columns. am/pm missing. Screenshot attached. Log attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8451,12,"""Android: You can't modify the view border multiple times""","""""""h4. Problem Description  The customer is trying to modify the view's border width as the user's interact with it, and it never changes.    h4. Actual results  the view's border width doesn't change    h4. EXpected results   being able to modify the view's border width as needed.    h4. Test case.  1. Create a new mobile project for android  2. Paste this code in app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: You can't modify the view border multiple times
Description: """"h4. Problem Description The customer is trying to modify the view's border width as the user's interact with it, and it never changes. h4. Actual results the view's border width doesn't change h4. EXpected results being able to modify the view's border width as needed. h4. Test case. 1. Create a new mobile project for android 2. Paste this code in app.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-8450,12,"""iOS: 4.3: KitchenSink-iPad: Split View w/Nav Group: window blur event does not fire""","""""""On iOS 4.3, blur events not fired on window. Tested from KitchenSink-iPad. Otherwise, events fire on iOS 5.1.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink-iPad > Split View w/Nav Group.  2. Click 'Open Window'.  3. Click 'Show Modal'.    Expected Result:    Alert indicating blur event fired.    Actual Result:    No alert, no blur event fired.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: 4.3: KitchenSink-iPad: Split View w/Nav Group: window blur event does not fire
Description: """"On iOS 4.3, blur events not fired on window. Tested from KitchenSink-iPad. Otherwise, events fire on iOS 5.1. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink-iPad > Split View w/Nav Group. 2. Click 'Open Window'. 3. Click 'Show Modal'. Expected Result: Alert indicating blur event fired. Actual Result: No alert, no blur event fired.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8449,12,"""Mobile Web: Add support for repeating backgrounds on a view that is similar to background-repeat property in CSS""","""""""PROBLEM  A customer wants to create titled backgrounds, so they look the same in any platform, and they don't have to generate different background images for each different platform.    There is a screenshot showing the expected behavior. Additionally, you can see an example of code that will do the same effect, using insane amount of memory:    {code:title=titledapp.js|borderStyle=solid}  win = Ti.UI.createWindow();    var background = Ti.UI.createView();    var image1 = Ti.UI.createImageView({   // use whatever image you have here    image: 'appicon.png',    height: 'auto',    width: 'auto'  });     var width=image1.size.width;  var height=image1.size.height;    var deviceW= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth;  var deviceH= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight;    var repeatX = (deviceW % width) + 1;   var repeatY = (deviceH % height) + 1;       for(i=0;i<repeatX; i++)   for(j=0;j<repeatY; j++){    background.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({     image: 'appicon.png',     height: 'auto',     width: 'auto',     top:j*height,      left:i*width,    }));   }     win.add(background);  win.open();    {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Mobile Web: Add support for repeating backgrounds on a view that is similar to background-repeat property in CSS
Description: """"PROBLEM A customer wants to create titled backgrounds, so they look the same in any platform, and they don't have to generate different background images for each different platform. There is a screenshot showing the expected behavior. Additionally, you can see an example of code that will do the same effect, using insane amount of memory: {code:title=titledapp.js|borderStyle=solid} win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var background = Ti.UI.createView(); var image1 = Ti.UI.createImageView({ // use whatever image you have here image: 'appicon.png', height: 'auto', width: 'auto' }); var width=image1.size.width; var height=image1.size.height; var deviceW= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth; var deviceH= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight; var repeatX = (deviceW % width) + 1; var repeatY = (deviceH % height) + 1; for(i=0;i<repeatX; i++) for(j=0;j<repeatY; j++){ background.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'appicon.png', height: 'auto', width: 'auto', top:j*height, left:i*width, })); } win.add(background); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-8448,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Controls > Slider > Basic: custom thumbImage disappears if user's thumb is too far from thumb handle""","""""""When the user's thumb is pressed on the button slider handle, and then the thumb is moved away, the custom thumb handle image disappears and is replaced by the default image. When the thumb is moved closer, the custom image reappears. This is an old issue.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run Kitchen Sink > Controls > Slider > Basic.  2. On the top slider (there are two), press and hold the handle.  3. Move """"""""thumb"""""""" (while keeping handle pressed) away from the handle.    Expected Result:    Custom image should remain.    Actual Result:    Custom image disappears.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Controls > Slider > Basic: custom thumbImage disappears if user's thumb is too far from thumb handle
Description: """"When the user's thumb is pressed on the button slider handle, and then the thumb is moved away, the custom thumb handle image disappears and is replaced by the default image. When the thumb is moved closer, the custom image reappears. This is an old issue. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run Kitchen Sink > Controls > Slider > Basic. 2. On the top slider (there are two), press and hold the handle. 3. Move """"""""thumb"""""""" (while keeping handle pressed) away from the handle. Expected Result: Custom image should remain. Actual Result: Custom image disappears.""""",title+description
