TIMOB-8443,12,"""Android: setting orientationModes on a Ti.UI.TabGroup does not work""","""""""Setting orientationModes on a tab group proxy seems to have no effect.  This can be observed in the tab layout in KS by trying to force orientationModes.    A work around is to set the orientation in the tiapp.xml via:    """"""""<activity             android:configChanges=""""""""keyboardHidden|orientation""""""""             android:name=""""""""ti.modules.titanium.ui.TiTabActivity""""""""            android:screenOrientation=""""""""landscape""""""""            />""""""""    A fix should be investigated though to allow for setting the orientation modes in a programmatic way.  In addition, it appears that setting the orientation modes for a window on a tab have no effect either.    h3. TabGroup orientationMode example    1. Run the code bellow in an application.  2. Initially the orientations of the group should be locked in both left and right landscape.  3. Click the 'Toggle orientationModes' button.  4. You should now be able to orientate the group in all modes (ex: landscape, portrait).  5. Click the toggle button again. Should lock the group back into landscape only mode.  6. Repeat until you are satisfied.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: setting orientationModes on a Ti.UI.TabGroup does not work
Description: """"Setting orientationModes on a tab group proxy seems to have no effect. This can be observed in the tab layout in KS by trying to force orientationModes. A work around is to set the orientation in the tiapp.xml via: """"""""<activity android:configChanges=""""""""keyboardHidden|orientation"""""""" android:name=""""""""ti.modules.titanium.ui.TiTabActivity"""""""" android:screenOrientation=""""""""landscape"""""""" />"""""""" A fix should be investigated though to allow for setting the orientation modes in a programmatic way. In addition, it appears that setting the orientation modes for a window on a tab have no effect either. h3. TabGroup orientationMode example 1. Run the code bellow in an application. 2. Initially the orientations of the group should be locked in both left and right landscape. 3. Click the 'Toggle orientationModes' button. 4. You should now be able to orientate the group in all modes (ex: landscape, portrait). 5. Click the toggle button again. Should lock the group back into landscape only mode. 6. Repeat until you are satisfied. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8442,12,"""Android: Facebook - If Titanium.Facebook.forceDialogAuth is false, cannot login to Facebook account""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Get and install KS from 1_8_X or 2_0_X branch  2. Go to Mashups > Facebook > login/logout  3. Make """"""""Force dialog: false""""""""  4. Press """"""""Connect with Facebook""""""""    Actual: Cannot connect to Facebook. See attachment for logcat log.  Expected: Should be able to login to Facebook when """"""""Force dialog"""""""" is false    Note: Only tested on v8. Did not test on rhino.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook - If Titanium.Facebook.forceDialogAuth is false, cannot login to Facebook account
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Get and install KS from 1_8_X or 2_0_X branch 2. Go to Mashups > Facebook > login/logout 3. Make """"""""Force dialog: false"""""""" 4. Press """"""""Connect with Facebook"""""""" Actual: Cannot connect to Facebook. See attachment for logcat log. Expected: Should be able to login to Facebook when """"""""Force dialog"""""""" is false Note: Only tested on v8. Did not test on rhino.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8441,12,"""Android: Kindle Fire using global reference workaround""","""""""Our current check for emulator in determining if we should use the global reference workaround  is returning true for the Kindle Fire. We need to change this conditional to correctly detect  the Kindle as a device and to use JNI global references.    While this bug shouldn't create any stability problems, it may impact performance.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Kindle Fire using global reference workaround
Description: """"Our current check for emulator in determining if we should use the global reference workaround is returning true for the Kindle Fire. We need to change this conditional to correctly detect the Kindle as a device and to use JNI global references. While this bug shouldn't create any stability problems, it may impact performance.""""",title+description
