TIMOB-8434,12,"""MobileWeb: 2DMatrix scale() y-factor should use x-factor if not specified""","""""""A 2D matrix object has a scale() function that accepts a x and y scaling factor, but if y is omitted, then it should x's factor.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: 2DMatrix scale() y-factor should use x-factor if not specified
Description: """"A 2D matrix object has a scale() function that accepts a x and y scaling factor, but if y is omitted, then it should x's factor.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8433,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.ImageView does not follow explicit sizing""","""""""  Currently, iOS image views do not obey explicit sizing instructions for percentage measurements (and possibly others). For example, when we have an image of 300 x 419 at """"""""50%"""""""" embedded in a parent view of 200, we do not see the behavior of the image view which would be expected (it measures 100 x 100, with image stretching).        h4. Pass  ----    The blue view should not be visible, since it has the same dimensions as the image view, which should overlay it.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.ImageView does not follow explicit sizing
Description: """" Currently, iOS image views do not obey explicit sizing instructions for percentage measurements (and possibly others). For example, when we have an image of 300 x 419 at """"""""50%"""""""" embedded in a parent view of 200, we do not see the behavior of the image view which would be expected (it measures 100 x 100, with image stretching). h4. Pass ---- The blue view should not be visible, since it has the same dimensions as the image view, which should overlay it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8432,12,"""Android: Camera - On V8, taking a picture at least twice causes an OutOfMemoryError exception""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Get and install KS from 2_0_X branch  2. Go to Phone > Camera > Camera Basic  3. Take picture and press OK     May need to repeat step 3 a couple of times.    Actual: The taken picture does not appear on screen and get OutOfMemoryError exception in logcat. See attachment.  Expected: Should not get OutOfMemoryError exception and should see taken picture.    Note:  * This does not occur in 1.8.2  * Tested only on v8. Did not test on rhino.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Camera - On V8, taking a picture at least twice causes an OutOfMemoryError exception
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Get and install KS from 2_0_X branch 2. Go to Phone > Camera > Camera Basic 3. Take picture and press OK May need to repeat step 3 a couple of times. Actual: The taken picture does not appear on screen and get OutOfMemoryError exception in logcat. See attachment. Expected: Should not get OutOfMemoryError exception and should see taken picture. Note: * This does not occur in 1.8.2 * Tested only on v8. Did not test on rhino.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8430,12,"""Android: TimePicker - Switching between am and pm time does not makes changes in time format on the top of the page""","""""""Description:  Switching between am and pm time does not makes changes in time format on the top of the page.   Also occurs on  Motorola Xoom 4.0.3, and on both devices on 1.8.2    Steps:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Controls-Picker-Time picker  3. Choose a time  4. Switch time format    Expected result:  Time in correct time format should be shown on the top of the page    Actual result:  Time format on the top of the page is incorrect  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TimePicker - Switching between am and pm time does not makes changes in time format on the top of the page
Description: """"Description: Switching between am and pm time does not makes changes in time format on the top of the page. Also occurs on Motorola Xoom 4.0.3, and on both devices on 1.8.2 Steps: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Controls-Picker-Time picker 3. Choose a time 4. Switch time format Expected result: Time in correct time format should be shown on the top of the page Actual result: Time format on the top of the page is incorrect """"",title+description
TIMOB-8429,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: crash after one hour with endpointIOTimerExpired logs""","""""""After using Kitchen Sink for an hour, app crashed with console logs (no crash report).    Occurred using UI > Views > Table Views > Events, unable to reproduce.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run Kitchen Sink for an hour.    Expected Result:    No crash.    Actual Result:    Crash.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: crash after one hour with endpointIOTimerExpired logs
