TIMOB-8381,12,"""iOS: ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX macro does not handle NSNull instance""","""""""In my native module, I check for optional arguments to a method using the ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX macro as follows:    {code:none}  - (id)myMethod:(id)args {      NSString * requiredArg;      NSString * optionalArg1;      NSNumber * optionalArg2;            ENSURE_ARG_AT_INDEX(requiredArg, args, 0, NSString);      ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX(optionalArg1, args, 1, NSString);      ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX(optionalArg2, args, 2, NSNumber);            /* remainder of method */  }      Fix is to add a check for NSNull in the macro as shown on line 13 below:    {code:none}  #define ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX(out,args,index,type) \  if (args==nil || args==[NSNull null]) \  { \  out = nil; \  } \  else if ([args isKindOfClass:[NSArray class]]) { \  if ([args count]>index) {\  out = [args objectAtIndex:index]; \  }\  else { \  out = nil; \  } \  if (out && ![out isKindOfClass:[NSNull class]] && ![out isKindOfClass:[type class]]) { \  [self throwException:TiExceptionInvalidType subreason:[NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""expected: %@, was: %@"""""""",[type class],[out class]] location:CODELOCATION]; \  } \  } \  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX macro does not handle NSNull instance
Description: """"In my native module, I check for optional arguments to a method using the ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX macro as follows: {code:none} - (id)myMethod:(id)args { NSString * requiredArg; NSString * optionalArg1; NSNumber * optionalArg2; ENSURE_ARG_AT_INDEX(requiredArg, args, 0, NSString); ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX(optionalArg1, args, 1, NSString); ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX(optionalArg2, args, 2, NSNumber); /* remainder of method */ } Fix is to add a check for NSNull in the macro as shown on line 13 below: {code:none} #define ENSURE_ARG_OR_NIL_AT_INDEX(out,args,index,type) \ if (args==nil || args==[NSNull null]) \ { \ out = nil; \ } \ else if ([args isKindOfClass:[NSArray class]]) { \ if ([args count]>index) {\ out = [args objectAtIndex:index]; \ }\ else { \ out = nil; \ } \ if (out && ![out isKindOfClass:[NSNull class]] && ![out isKindOfClass:[type class]]) { \ [self throwException:TiExceptionInvalidType subreason:[NSString stringWithFormat:@""""""""expected: %@, was: %@"""""""",[type class],[out class]] location:CODELOCATION]; \ } \ } \ {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-8380,12,"""Android: KitchenSink-platform>XML RSS -text property warning in log""","""""""in KitchenSink-platform>XML RSS a warning:     -(KrollRunTimeThread)-the text property of Element is deprecated,use textContent instead is seen in the log.    After this  KitchenSink-platform>Utils gives a runtime Error and warning.  However this runtime error occurs only randomly, on the first run, after clearing the cache or switching the device on    steps to reproduce:    1: run XML RSS  2: view the logs file    Actual result: Gives a warning message and all the RSS can be seen in the view    Expected result: no warning messages should occur.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink-platform>XML RSS -text property warning in log
Description: """"in KitchenSink-platform>XML RSS a warning: -(KrollRunTimeThread)-the text property of Element is deprecated,use textContent instead is seen in the log. After this KitchenSink-platform>Utils gives a runtime Error and warning. However this runtime error occurs only randomly, on the first run, after clearing the cache or switching the device on steps to reproduce: 1: run XML RSS 2: view the logs file Actual result: Gives a warning message and all the RSS can be seen in the view Expected result: no warning messages should occur. """"",title+description
