TIMOB-8357,12,"""MobileWeb: Tabbed Template - Icon images does not appear on the tabs""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a TiMob project using Tabbed template  2. Package for Mobile Web  3. Place packaged project on a local server  4. Access website through any browser e.g. Chrome, Android's browser, iPhone's browser    Actual: Icon images are missing in the tab. See attachment.  Expected: Icon images should appear.    Note: When you Run As > Mobile Web Preview in Browser or Emulator, the icon images appear.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Tabbed Template - Icon images does not appear on the tabs
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a TiMob project using Tabbed template 2. Package for Mobile Web 3. Place packaged project on a local server 4. Access website through any browser e.g. Chrome, Android's browser, iPhone's browser Actual: Icon images are missing in the tab. See attachment. Expected: Icon images should appear. Note: When you Run As > Mobile Web Preview in Browser or Emulator, the icon images appear.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8356,12,"""MobileWeb: Master/Detail Templates: When viewing in iOS browser, the Back button will eventually disappear""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a TiMob project using Master/Detail Template  2. Package for Mobile Web  3. Place packaged project on a local server  4. Access website via iPhone browser  5. Click on an item then Back several times    Actual: Back button will eventually disappear.  Expected: Back button should not disappear.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Master/Detail Templates: When viewing in iOS browser, the Back button will eventually disappear
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a TiMob project using Master/Detail Template 2. Package for Mobile Web 3. Place packaged project on a local server 4. Access website via iPhone browser 5. Click on an item then Back several times Actual: Back button will eventually disappear. Expected: Back button should not disappear.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8355,12,"""MobileWeb: Improve performance of Mobile Web""","""""""Need to make mobile web as fast as possible. Ideas include:    * AST parser to optimize code  ** Eliminate dead code  ** Reduce size of code  ** Detect event behavior, disable unused events and speed up responsiveness  ** Use """"""""Ti"""""""" instead of """"""""Titanium""""""""  ** Remove named functions that are assigned to local variables  ** Inline """"""""small"""""""" constants (i.e. Ti.UI.FILL and Ti.UI.SIZE)  ** Remove exceptions  ** Convert all named colors to hex  * Custom AMD aware code minifier  ** This would be an extension of the AST parser and would replace the closure compiler  ** Remove comments  ** Minify CSS, HTML, JSON  ** Remove log calls based on log level  ** Inline images  * General code reduction best practices  * Gestures/touch events  ** Bind gestures on first use  ** Queue and <USER>touches every X milliseconds (where X could be 15ms)  * DNS prefetching  ** Use <link rel=""""""""dns-prefetch"""""""" href=""""""""//somedomain.com"""""""">  * Lazy loading  ** Split dependencies to soften the initial load time  * Deferred execution  ** Only cache top priority JavaScript in require.cache()  ** All other JavaScript is cached in commented <script> tags  * Local storage caching  ** Cache modules in local storage with hash in cookie (requires server-side logic)  * Removing non-visible DOM nodes from view  * Moving static CSS styles out of code and into style sheets  ** We set position, display, height, width, etc a lot and could be done using CSS  * Possibly use right and bottom styles to control width and height of elements instead of explicitly calculating width and height  ** Browsers optimize for this  * Build a custom CSS manager to reduce number of CSS rules  * Make sure we're using hardware acceleration for all transforms and animations  ** We may need to do a 3D transform to enable hardware acceleration  * Investigate the use of web workers to do background computations  ** Layout computations  * Make layout UI elements lazy load (i.e. huge tableviews)  * Add support for appcache  ** Device specific appcache optimizations""""""",Story,"Title: MobileWeb: Improve performance of Mobile Web
Description: """"Need to make mobile web as fast as possible. Ideas include: * AST parser to optimize code ** Eliminate dead code ** Reduce size of code ** Detect event behavior, disable unused events and speed up responsiveness ** Use """"""""Ti"""""""" instead of """"""""Titanium"""""""" ** Remove named functions that are assigned to local variables ** Inline """"""""small"""""""" constants (i.e. Ti.UI.FILL and Ti.UI.SIZE) ** Remove exceptions ** Convert all named colors to hex * Custom AMD aware code minifier ** This would be an extension of the AST parser and would replace the closure compiler ** Remove comments ** Minify CSS, HTML, JSON ** Remove log calls based on log level ** Inline images * General code reduction best practices * Gestures/touch events ** Bind gestures on first use ** Queue and <USER>touches every X milliseconds (where X could be 15ms) * DNS prefetching ** Use <link rel=""""""""dns-prefetch"""""""" href=""""""""//somedomain.com""""""""> * Lazy loading ** Split dependencies to soften the initial load time * Deferred execution ** Only cache top priority JavaScript in require.cache() ** All other JavaScript is cached in commented <script> tags * Local storage caching ** Cache modules in local storage with hash in cookie (requires server-side logic) * Removing non-visible DOM nodes from view * Moving static CSS styles out of code and into style sheets ** We set position, display, height, width, etc a lot and could be done using CSS * Possibly use right and bottom styles to control width and height of elements instead of explicitly calculating width and height ** Browsers optimize for this * Build a custom CSS manager to reduce number of CSS rules * Make sure we're using hardware acceleration for all transforms and animations ** We may need to do a 3D transform to enable hardware acceleration * Investigate the use of web workers to do background computations ** Layout computations * Make layout UI elements lazy load (i.e. huge tableviews) * Add support for appcache ** Device specific appcache optimizations""""",title+description
