TIMOB-8331,12,"""iOS: HW window fires open and focus events in wrong order""","""""""h2.Problem  This is the same problem as https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7023.  When a heavyweight window is open()ed, the focus event fires first, then the open event fires.    h2.Expected Results  In parity with Android, the open event should fire first, then the focus event should fire.    h2.Testcase  # Run sample code below.  # In the log, we can find it fires focus first and then open.    app.js        win1.js    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: HW window fires open and focus events in wrong order
Description: """"h2.Problem This is the same problem as https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7023. When a heavyweight window is open()ed, the focus event fires first, then the open event fires. h2.Expected Results In parity with Android, the open event should fire first, then the focus event should fire. h2.Testcase # Run sample code below. # In the log, we can find it fires focus first and then open. app.js win1.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-8330,12,"""Android: Global variables causing memory leak on windows""","""""""Assigning window to a global variable causes that window to leak when closing via back button.  Steps to reproduce:  1. Run this code:     2. Click on 'create Window' button.  3. Click back  4. Repeat and observe memory in DDMS    NOTE: if you don't assign global variable, then it won't leak. Try moving the open() call into createWin() function and don't return anything.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Global variables causing memory leak on windows
Description: """"Assigning window to a global variable causes that window to leak when closing via back button. Steps to reproduce: 1. Run this code: 2. Click on 'create Window' button. 3. Click back 4. Repeat and observe memory in DDMS NOTE: if you don't assign global variable, then it won't leak. Try moving the open() call into createWin() function and don't return anything. """"",title+description
