Description: """"h2. Problem If you use the {{returnKeyType}} property with a {{Ti.UI.TextArea}} in mobileweb, you get the following error: h2. Test case """"",title+description
TIMOB-8222,12,"""Android: Open event for window on first tab of tab group fires when it shouldn't""","""""""In Kitchen Sink, the open event for the window attached to the first tab will fire when the tab group is opened even if the active tab when opened is the second tab.  This can be seen by using the test case in timob-8192 (assumes 8192 is merged into master).    The open event in the situation described above should not fire.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Open event for window on first tab of tab group fires when it shouldn't
Description: """"In Kitchen Sink, the open event for the window attached to the first tab will fire when the tab group is opened even if the active tab when opened is the second tab. This can be seen by using the test case in timob-8192 (assumes 8192 is merged into master). The open event in the situation described above should not fire.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8221,12,"""MobileWeb: Create an """"inner"""" or """"hidden"""" control concept""","""""""Many of our controls are created by assembling other controls. While this is great from a reuse standpoint, it makes the element graph look different than the user expects. This also affects the """"""""source"""""""" object in UI events that can be unexpected from the user's perspective. We need to create a property of some sort that tells a control it is one of these hidden controls and needs to hide itself from the user.    This affects the """"""""children"""""""" property. Hidden children should NOT be returned in the array of children.    We need to add some general helpers to the View subclass.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Create an """"inner"""" or """"hidden"""" control concept
Description: """"Many of our controls are created by assembling other controls. While this is great from a reuse standpoint, it makes the element graph look different than the user expects. This also affects the """"""""source"""""""" object in UI events that can be unexpected from the user's perspective. We need to create a property of some sort that tells a control it is one of these hidden controls and needs to hide itself from the user. This affects the """"""""children"""""""" property. Hidden children should NOT be returned in the array of children. We need to add some general helpers to the View subclass.""""",title+description
