TIMOB-8199,12,"""Tooling: scons: TI_DEBUG environment variable is ignored on Windows 7""","""""""TI_DEBUG is ignored on Windows 7.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Get latest titanium_mobile from git.  2. Set TI_DEBUG environment variable by adding it to global variables (next to JAVA_HOME). TI_DEBUG=1  3. Build sdk by using scons command in titanium_mobile folder.  4. Run a default project using built sdk.  5. Deploy to device.  6. Check DDMS.  7. Click on UI elements in app.    Expected Result:    V - click events should log to console.    Actual Result:    No events, SDK was built in regular mode.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: scons: TI_DEBUG environment variable is ignored on Windows 7
Description: """"TI_DEBUG is ignored on Windows 7. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Get latest titanium_mobile from git. 2. Set TI_DEBUG environment variable by adding it to global variables (next to JAVA_HOME). TI_DEBUG=1 3. Build sdk by using scons command in titanium_mobile folder. 4. Run a default project using built sdk. 5. Deploy to device. 6. Check DDMS. 7. Click on UI elements in app. Expected Result: V - click events should log to console. Actual Result: No events, SDK was built in regular mode.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8198,12,"""MobileWeb: Slider: Last pixel is getting clipped on the max end of the slider""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Slider > Change Min/Max  2. Slide the slider to max    Actual:  The slider is clipped     Expected:  Slider should not be clipped  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Slider: Last pixel is getting clipped on the max end of the slider
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Slider > Change Min/Max 2. Slide the slider to max Actual: The slider is clipped Expected: Slider should not be clipped """"",title+description
TIMOB-8197,12,"""MobileWeb: Move tab icon above text""","""""""Tab icons are located to the left of text, but the other platforms put it above the text. In many cases this causes our text to get clipped because the window is too narrow, but the other platforms look fine.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Move tab icon above text
Description: """"Tab icons are located to the left of text, but the other platforms put it above the text. In many cases this causes our text to get clipped because the window is too narrow, but the other platforms look fine.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8196,12,"""MobileWeb: Improve Mobile Web visual experience (colors, animations, interaction)""","""""""There is a desire to make the default theme look a little more flashy and less grayscale. We need flashier transitions between windows. We need nice visuals such as velocity scrolling.""""""",Story,"Title: MobileWeb: Improve Mobile Web visual experience (colors, animations, interaction)
Description: """"There is a desire to make the default theme look a little more flashy and less grayscale. We need flashier transitions between windows. We need nice visuals such as velocity scrolling.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8195,12,"""MobileWeb: Click events sometimes report e.source as undefined""","""""""Controls with custom created children don't have a widget id, and the event handler gets confused by this, causes source to be undefined. Custom children need to have a pointer events.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Click events sometimes report e.source as undefined
Description: """"Controls with custom created children don't have a widget id, and the event handler gets confused by this, causes source to be undefined. Custom children need to have a pointer events.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8194,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.TableViewRow doesn't continuously update Ti.UI.ImageView objects inside of it""","""""""*Code*  .zip file attached with this ticket, which includes some images to reproduce this issue.    *Expected behavior*  When you tap on the row, it should update the image view with the correct image, continuously.    *Actual behavior*  On Android, it only seems to switch images once, and then never again.    *Notes*  -Only tested on an Android device and iOS simulator.  -On the iOS simulator, it seems to work perfectly fine.  -Only tested on 1.8.2.  -HD ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-786776""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.TableViewRow doesn't continuously update Ti.UI.ImageView objects inside of it
Description: """"*Code* .zip file attached with this ticket, which includes some images to reproduce this issue. *Expected behavior* When you tap on the row, it should update the image view with the correct image, continuously. *Actual behavior* On Android, it only seems to switch images once, and then never again. *Notes* -Only tested on an Android device and iOS simulator. -On the iOS simulator, it seems to work perfectly fine. -Only tested on 1.8.2. -HD ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-786776""""",title+description
TIMOB-8193,12,"""iOS: Composite layout - horizontal layout Views don't position children correctly""","""""""Horizontal layout Views don't position children correctly.  h4. Expected behavior   A red view at the top of the window (full width).  An orange view occupying the left half of the red view.  A blue square view immediately to the right of the orange view.    h4. Repo Steps  1.Run the below code in app.js  2.You will see the orange view actually appears centered on the red view and the blue view actually appears at position 0,0    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Composite layout - horizontal layout Views don't position children correctly
Description: """"Horizontal layout Views don't position children correctly. h4. Expected behavior A red view at the top of the window (full width). An orange view occupying the left half of the red view. A blue square view immediately to the right of the orange view. h4. Repo Steps 1.Run the below code in app.js 2.You will see the orange view actually appears centered on the red view and the blue view actually appears at position 0,0 """"",title+description
TIMOB-8192,12,"""Android: Open events do not fire for windows on tabs""","""""""Open event for windows on tabs do not fire when opened.  This can be seen by adding open event listeners to the main tabs in KS.  Currently, only the window associated with the active tab when the tab group is opened will fire a open event.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Open events do not fire for windows on tabs
Description: """"Open event for windows on tabs do not fire when opened. This can be seen by adding open event listeners to the main tabs in KS. Currently, only the window associated with the active tab when the tab group is opened will fire a open event. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8191,12,"""Android: TextField loses focus if resized""","""""""h2. Problem  TextField in a TableViewRow loses focus if it has been resized after being focused    h2. Code and steps to reproduce  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   title:'pippo',   backgroundColor:'white'  });    function addRow(addTextArea)  {   var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({height:200});        var $tTF = Ti.UI.createTextField({    height: 30,    top : 30,    width: 100,    borderStyle:Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED   });      $tTF.addEventListener('focus',function(_e){       Ti.API.error(""""""""focus """"""""+_e.source.height);       Ti.API.error(_e);       _e.source.animate({height:  _e.source.height*2});   });            row.add($tTF);   row.selectionStyle = Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewCellSelectionStyle.NONE;   row.className = 'control';   return row;  }    // create table view data object  var data = [];    for (var x=0;x<1;x++)  {   if (x==1){    data[x] = addRow(true);   } else {    data[x] = addRow();   }    }    var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({   data:data,   style: Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED  });  win.addEventListener('focus', function()  {   Ti.API.info('window focus fired');  });  win.add(tableView);    win.open();    {code}    To reproduce:  - Run the app and click the textField: textField is animated increasing in height.  Result: focus on textField is lost.    h2. Additional notes  Ticket associated for iOS: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-995689/conversation/read_all""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField loses focus if resized
Description: """"h2. Problem TextField in a TableViewRow loses focus if it has been resized after being focused h2. Code and steps to reproduce {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title:'pippo', backgroundColor:'white' }); function addRow(addTextArea) { var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({height:200}); var $tTF = Ti.UI.createTextField({ height: 30, top : 30, width: 100, borderStyle:Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED }); $tTF.addEventListener('focus',function(_e){ Ti.API.error(""""""""focus """"""""+_e.source.height); Ti.API.error(_e); _e.source.animate({height: _e.source.height*2}); }); row.add($tTF); row.selectionStyle = Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewCellSelectionStyle.NONE; row.className = 'control'; return row; } // create table view data object var data = []; for (var x=0;x<1;x++) { if (x==1){ data[x] = addRow(true); } else { data[x] = addRow(); } } var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({ data:data, style: Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED }); win.addEventListener('focus', function() { Ti.API.info('window focus fired'); }); win.add(tableView); win.open(); {code} To reproduce: - Run the app and click the textField: textField is animated increasing in height. Result: focus on textField is lost. h2. Additional notes Ticket associated for iOS: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-995689/conversation/read_all""""",title+description
TIMOB-8190,12,"""Samples: Todo List and Kitchen Sink: no mobileweb build sub-folder""","""""""Samples should contain empty build folders for each platform.    Todo List and Kitchen Sink do not contain mobileweb build folders.      Should be:    Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build  Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build\android  Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build\iphone  Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build\mobileweb    with platform sub-folders empty""""""",Bug,"Title: Samples: Todo List and Kitchen Sink: no mobileweb build sub-folder
Description: """"Samples should contain empty build folders for each platform. Todo List and Kitchen Sink do not contain mobileweb build folders. Should be: Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build\android Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build\iphone Titanium Studio Workspace\RSS Reader\build\mobileweb with platform sub-folders empty""""",title+description
