TIMOB-8183,12,"""MobileWeb: Implement event overloading mechanism in Evented""","""""""Currently, controls can override touch event behavior by overriding a special _handleTouchEvent method. This is kinda hacky and not very scalable. Instead we should provide a formal generic mechanism in Evented that allows object to """"""""hook"""""""" or """"""""override"""""""" events to modify event data/behavior.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Implement event overloading mechanism in Evented
Description: """"Currently, controls can override touch event behavior by overriding a special _handleTouchEvent method. This is kinda hacky and not very scalable. Instead we should provide a formal generic mechanism in Evented that allows object to """"""""hook"""""""" or """"""""override"""""""" events to modify event data/behavior.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8182,12,"""MobileWeb: Implement support for Window.*NavImage, or some sort of equivalent.""",,New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Implement support for Window.*NavImage, or some sort of equivalent.",title-only
TIMOB-8181,12,"""Android: View.toImage() is not proper size when View.width is Ti.UI.SIZE""","""""""h4. Problem Description   There is a bug in the new Composite Layout engine. When a view of a certain size is placed inside a second view, and the second view's width is set to Ti.UI.SIZE, the second view's toimage() size is exactly 100 instead of being the same size as the first view.    h4. Actual Results  Run the testcase below. The console will show    --> TheOrange width:160dp  --> GreenView.swidth:0  --> GreenView.iwidth:100  --> GreenView.swidth2:0  But the GreenView.iwidth should be 160 (on a medium-resolution emulator). Also, you can see that GreenView.size.width (GreenView.swidth2) returns 0, but it should be 160.    h4. Expected results  The SIZE component working as the docs says.      h4. Test case  1. Create a new mobile project  2. Add this code to app.js  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: View.toImage() is not proper size when View.width is Ti.UI.SIZE
Description: """"h4. Problem Description There is a bug in the new Composite Layout engine. When a view of a certain size is placed inside a second view, and the second view's width is set to Ti.UI.SIZE, the second view's toimage() size is exactly 100 instead of being the same size as the first view. h4. Actual Results Run the testcase below. The console will show --> TheOrange width:160dp --> GreenView.swidth:0 --> GreenView.iwidth:100 --> GreenView.swidth2:0 But the GreenView.iwidth should be 160 (on a medium-resolution emulator). Also, you can see that GreenView.size.width (GreenView.swidth2) returns 0, but it should be 160. h4. Expected results The SIZE component working as the docs says. h4. Test case 1. Create a new mobile project 2. Add this code to app.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-8180,12,"""MobileWeb: Use web workers for layout""","""""""Since the layout algorithm is hefty but not really DOM dependent, we should throw it in a web worker.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Use web workers for layout
Description: """"Since the layout algorithm is hefty but not really DOM dependent, we should throw it in a web worker.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8179,12,"""iOS: View """"auto"""" should behave as the old auto instead of FILL (this is breaking apps in 2.0)""","""""""h4. Problem Description  The new behaviour of 'auto' in a view, it's to FILL the space to match the parent size. This change will break apps. If a new feature like 'FILL' behavior is added to the platform, should be a new feature, so no apps will break.     This is causing some customer pain, because they will need to implement a bunch of changes in their apps to be 2.0 compatible. """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: View """"auto"""" should behave as the old auto instead of FILL (this is breaking apps in 2.0)
Description: """"h4. Problem Description The new behaviour of 'auto' in a view, it's to FILL the space to match the parent size. This change will break apps. If a new feature like 'FILL' behavior is added to the platform, should be a new feature, so no apps will break. This is causing some customer pain, because they will need to implement a bunch of changes in their apps to be 2.0 compatible. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8178,12,"""MobileWeb: Module build.py Inconsistencies""","""""""h1. Inconsistencies  Two problems:    1. By convention on iOS, sdk_path should come from titanium.xcconfig.  2. Markdown or markdown2 is included in sdk/module/support. But the path was not being changed before importing them, forcing users to manually install the modules.    I have demonstrated how to fix these two problems in a commit on GitHub. I did not send a pull request, because I have been informed that pull requests are detrimental.    https://github.com/dawsontoth/titanium_mobile/commit/a5d9bf95ba7bcb1f98b9f51964410a7b3376cb89  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Module build.py Inconsistencies
Description: """"h1. Inconsistencies Two problems: 1. By convention on iOS, sdk_path should come from titanium.xcconfig. 2. Markdown or markdown2 is included in sdk/module/support. But the path was not being changed before importing them, forcing users to manually install the modules. I have demonstrated how to fix these two problems in a commit on GitHub. I did not send a pull request, because I have been informed that pull requests are detrimental. https://github.com/dawsontoth/titanium_mobile/commit/a5d9bf95ba7bcb1f98b9f51964410a7b3376cb89 """"",title+description
