TIMOB-8165,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder() not working""","""""""Affects 2.0.0.v20120321134756    h2. Problem    As the title states, I can get {{Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder()}} to work under no circumstances on any platforms. All errors indicate """"""""Not Found"""""""". This does not mean that the specified location cannot be found, as I've tried many. I believe that it is occurring because the underlying URL seems to be looking for        when it should be looking for        h2. Test Case    This will give """"""""not Found"""""""" errors on all platforms        h2. Proposed Solution    make the service use the domain {{api.<USER>net}}, not {{api.<USER>com}}  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder() not working
Description: """"Affects 2.0.0.v20120321134756 h2. Problem As the title states, I can get {{Ti.Geolocation.forwardGeocoder()}} to work under no circumstances on any platforms. All errors indicate """"""""Not Found"""""""". This does not mean that the specified location cannot be found, as I've tried many. I believe that it is occurring because the underlying URL seems to be looking for when it should be looking for h2. Test Case This will give """"""""not Found"""""""" errors on all platforms h2. Proposed Solution make the service use the domain {{api.<USER>net}}, not {{api.<USER>com}} """"",title+description
TIMOB-8164,12,"""Mobileweb: FF 10.0.2 throws exception when attempting to access local file with HTTPClient""","""""""Affects latest CI as of this writing: 2.0.0.v20120321134756    h2. Problem    Firefox 10.0.2 will throw an exception whenever you attempt to access a local file with {{Ti.Network.HTTPClient}}. This was not the case a week ago in the CI. Also, Chrome and Safari work fine with local files. The error is the one below:        h2. Test Case    This test case will run as expected in Chrome and Safari, but will throw the above error in Firefix    """"""",Bug,"Title: Mobileweb: FF 10.0.2 throws exception when attempting to access local file with HTTPClient
Description: """"Affects latest CI as of this writing: 2.0.0.v20120321134756 h2. Problem Firefox 10.0.2 will throw an exception whenever you attempt to access a local file with {{Ti.Network.HTTPClient}}. This was not the case a week ago in the CI. Also, Chrome and Safari work fine with local files. The error is the one below: h2. Test Case This test case will run as expected in Chrome and Safari, but will throw the above error in Firefix """"",title+description
TIMOB-8163,12,"""MobileWeb: Add support for commonjs modules in compiler""","""""""We need to be able to support resolving modules that are in the commonjs modules directory.    Order of precedence:  - modules/mobileweb  - modules/commonjs  - global/mobileweb  - global/commonjs""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Add support for commonjs modules in compiler
Description: """"We need to be able to support resolving modules that are in the commonjs modules directory. Order of precedence: - modules/mobileweb - modules/commonjs - global/mobileweb - global/commonjs""""",title+description
