TIMOB-8148,12,"""No.26 - Fastdev Acceptance 1025 Android Only""","""""""h3. Description  Verify that turning off Fastdev in tiapp.xml turns off Fastdev  h3. Steps to reproduce issue  1. Put flag to turn off Fastdev in the top level of the tiapp.xml:  <property name=""""""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" type=""""""""bool"""""""">false</property>  2. Launch project in emulator  3. From a new terminal, navigate to the project  4. Then type """"""""titanium fastdev status""""""""  h3. Expected result  Should display: """"""""No Fastdev servers running in <project>""""""""  h3. Actual result  Failed: fastdev is still able to run  Test run: http://<USER>testlodge.com/projects/1317/test_runs/8375#executed_case_161993""""""",Bug,"Title: No.26 - Fastdev Acceptance 1025 Android Only
Description: """"h3. Description Verify that turning off Fastdev in tiapp.xml turns off Fastdev h3. Steps to reproduce issue 1. Put flag to turn off Fastdev in the top level of the tiapp.xml: <property name=""""""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" type=""""""""bool"""""""">false</property> 2. Launch project in emulator 3. From a new terminal, navigate to the project 4. Then type """"""""titanium fastdev status"""""""" h3. Expected result Should display: """"""""No Fastdev servers running in <project>"""""""" h3. Actual result Failed: fastdev is still able to run Test run: http://<USER>testlodge.com/projects/1317/test_runs/8375#executed_case_161993""""",title+description
TIMOB-8147,12,"""iOS: Regression: View with 'auto' height is much taller than it should be""","""""""h4. Problem  In the 2.0.0.v20120319003254 continuous-build SDK, a View with a height of """"""""auto"""""""" is displayed much taller than it should be.  In SDK 1.8.2, the height was correct (only as tall as it needs to be to surround those things it contains).  Therefore, this is a regression.    h4. Actual result  With the 2.0.0.v20120319003254 continuous-build SDK, the view (yellow in the testcase below) appears almost the full height of the screen.    h4. Expected result  The view (yellow in the testcase below) should be only tall enough to surround the """"""""X"""""""" that is placed into it.  This is how it appeared with the 1.8.2 and earlier SDKs.    h4. Testcase  {code:title=app.js}  var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({        backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({    backgroundColor:'green',   color:'white',   text:'Spinner should be on top of the X',   font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'},   textAlign:'center',   top:40,   height:40,   width:'auto'  });  win1.add(label1);    var view1 = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'yellow',    height:'auto',     top:100,    width:100  });  win1.add(view1);    var spin1=Ti.UI.createActivityIndicator({                      //right:25,                      left:25,                      style:Ti.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle.DARK                    });  view1.add(spin1);  var marker1=Ti.UI.createLabel({                      height:'auto',                      width:'auto',                      text:'X',                      //right:25,                      left:25,                    });  view1.add(marker1);    win1.open();  spin1.show();  {code}    h4. Extra info  This test is working fine in 1.8.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Regression: View with 'auto' height is much taller than it should be
Description: """"h4. Problem In the 2.0.0.v20120319003254 continuous-build SDK, a View with a height of """"""""auto"""""""" is displayed much taller than it should be. In SDK 1.8.2, the height was correct (only as tall as it needs to be to surround those things it contains). Therefore, this is a regression. h4. Actual result With the 2.0.0.v20120319003254 continuous-build SDK, the view (yellow in the testcase below) appears almost the full height of the screen. h4. Expected result The view (yellow in the testcase below) should be only tall enough to surround the """"""""X"""""""" that is placed into it. This is how it appeared with the 1.8.2 and earlier SDKs. h4. Testcase {code:title=app.js} var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({ backgroundColor:'green', color:'white', text:'Spinner should be on top of the X', font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'}, textAlign:'center', top:40, height:40, width:'auto' }); win1.add(label1); var view1 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'yellow', height:'auto', top:100, width:100 }); win1.add(view1); var spin1=Ti.UI.createActivityIndicator({ //right:25, left:25, style:Ti.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle.DARK }); view1.add(spin1); var marker1=Ti.UI.createLabel({ height:'auto', width:'auto', text:'X', //right:25, left:25, }); view1.add(marker1); win1.open(); spin1.show(); {code} h4. Extra info This test is working fine in 1.8.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-8146,12,"""MobileWeb: Horiontal and vertical layouts with a FILL item don't respect other controls margins.""","""""""When two elements are added to a horizontal or vertical view, one with a width/height of FILL and the other with some sort of margin defined, the layout algorithm ignores those margins when calculating the width/height of the FILL.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Horiontal and vertical layouts with a FILL item don't respect other controls margins.
Description: """"When two elements are added to a horizontal or vertical view, one with a width/height of FILL and the other with some sort of margin defined, the layout algorithm ignores those margins when calculating the width/height of the FILL.""""",title+description
