TIMOB-8133,12,"""iOS: Ti.Analytics.featureEvent not sending data""","""""""*Code*      *Expected behavior*  When you click on either of the buttons, it should sent analytics data to our server.    *Actual behavior*  When you click on either of the buttons, it indeed does print out the following:       However the data is not being captured by our end. I worked with <USER>to figure out what the issue is, and we have concluded that this seems to be issue with the platform not sending Ti.Analytics.featureEvent events. He told me to open a TIMOB JIRA ticket about this.    *Notes*  -This only seems to be affected by iOS, Android seems to work fine.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.Analytics.featureEvent not sending data
Description: """"*Code* *Expected behavior* When you click on either of the buttons, it should sent analytics data to our server. *Actual behavior* When you click on either of the buttons, it indeed does print out the following: However the data is not being captured by our end. I worked with <USER>to figure out what the issue is, and we have concluded that this seems to be issue with the platform not sending Ti.Analytics.featureEvent events. He told me to open a TIMOB JIRA ticket about this. *Notes* -This only seems to be affected by iOS, Android seems to work fine.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8132,12,"""No.97 - Titanium Studio Template Smoke 1018 Mobile Web""","""""""h3. Description  PackageApplicationMobileWeb   Package the application for distribution on Mobile Web  h3. Steps to reproduce issue  1. Select the application in Project Explorer or App Explorer.  2. Choose Deploy > Package - Mobile Web  3. Select """"""""Create a new Project"""""""" and give the project a unique name  4. Complete the wizard  5. Find the new project in the workspace  6. Double-click on the index.html file to open up the main page  7. Click on the preview button in the header  h3. Expected result  Opening up the index.html file in that project and clicking the """"""""Preview"""""""" button should give a page preview that resembles the intended app.  Test run: http://<USER>testlodge.com/projects/1317/test_runs/8365#executed_case_161643""""""",Bug,"Title: No.97 - Titanium Studio Template Smoke 1018 Mobile Web
Description: """"h3. Description PackageApplicationMobileWeb Package the application for distribution on Mobile Web h3. Steps to reproduce issue 1. Select the application in Project Explorer or App Explorer. 2. Choose Deploy > Package - Mobile Web 3. Select """"""""Create a new Project"""""""" and give the project a unique name 4. Complete the wizard 5. Find the new project in the workspace 6. Double-click on the index.html file to open up the main page 7. Click on the preview button in the header h3. Expected result Opening up the index.html file in that project and clicking the """"""""Preview"""""""" button should give a page preview that resembles the intended app. Test run: http://<USER>testlodge.com/projects/1317/test_runs/8365#executed_case_161643""""",title+description
TIMOB-8130,12,"""Android: Tab icons look very small when anyDensity=""""false"""" is not set in tiapp.xml""","""""""h4. Problem Description  Customer doesn't set  <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/> is NOT added to tiapp.xml. The app scales the icon size correctly when anyDensity=""""""""false"""""""" but I'm trying to see how this works without that property. My confusion is because the icon size guidelines from the Android documentation (http://developer.android.com/guide/practices/ui_guidelines/icon_design_tab.html) don't match my testing. The docs says that an hdpi screen should have a tab icon of 42x42, but testing on the WVGA800 emulator (dpi 240) it looks like an icon of size ~96x96 is the correct size. I'm not sure if this is necessarily a bug but I was wondering if it was already known/documented what size icons should be used, and why it's different from the official documentation.    Attached is a screen from the WVGA800 emulator. The icon on the tab """"""""Test"""""""" is 42x42, the icon on the tab """"""""Settings"""""""" is 96x96    h4. Actual results  Even if you follow the guideline, the icon will be small in the tab.    h4. Expected results  The icon should be bigger in the tab.    h4. Test case  check the screenshot.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tab icons look very small when anyDensity=""""false"""" is not set in tiapp.xml
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Customer doesn't set <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/> is NOT added to tiapp.xml. The app scales the icon size correctly when anyDensity=""""""""false"""""""" but I'm trying to see how this works without that property. My confusion is because the icon size guidelines from the Android documentation (http://developer.android.com/guide/practices/ui_guidelines/icon_design_tab.html) don't match my testing. The docs says that an hdpi screen should have a tab icon of 42x42, but testing on the WVGA800 emulator (dpi 240) it looks like an icon of size ~96x96 is the correct size. I'm not sure if this is necessarily a bug but I was wondering if it was already known/documented what size icons should be used, and why it's different from the official documentation. Attached is a screen from the WVGA800 emulator. The icon on the tab """"""""Test"""""""" is 42x42, the icon on the tab """"""""Settings"""""""" is 96x96 h4. Actual results Even if you follow the guideline, the icon will be small in the tab. h4. Expected results The icon should be bigger in the tab. h4. Test case check the screenshot.""""",title+description
