TIMOB-8125,12,"""MobileWeb: Update controls to take advantage of the new INHERIT constant""","""""""Now that we have Ti.UI.INHERIT support, we can remove the instances where we manually set the width/height of controls based on it's parent's control.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Update controls to take advantage of the new INHERIT constant
Description: """"Now that we have Ti.UI.INHERIT support, we can remove the instances where we manually set the width/height of controls based on it's parent's control.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8124,12,"""MobileWeb: Update tableview's to not create heavyweight borders""","""""""Mobile Web creates separators in table views by creating actual Ti.UI.Views. These are heavyweight and have other issues. We should rearchitect tableviews to set border-bottom instead. This is a technical debt issue and does not affect functionality.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Update tableview's to not create heavyweight borders
Description: """"Mobile Web creates separators in table views by creating actual Ti.UI.Views. These are heavyweight and have other issues. We should rearchitect tableviews to set border-bottom instead. This is a technical debt issue and does not affect functionality.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8123,12,"""iOS: Geolocation - Doesn't show """"Reverse Geo"""", """"Current location"""", and """"Updated location"""" info""","""""""Description:  When running Geolocation second time after reinstallation or killing app, it doesn't show """"""""Revers Geo"""""""", """"""""Current location"""""""", and """"""""Updated location"""""""" info.  Also occurs in 1.8.2    Steps:  1. Reinstall or kill KitchenSink, if it's already installed.  2. Run KitchenSink  3. Go to """"""""Phone-Geolocation""""""""  4. Go back  5. Launch """"""""Geolocation"""""""" second time    Expected result:  Every time when running Geolocation, all information should be presented.    Actual result:  After second time launching Geolocation it doesn't show """"""""Revers Geo"""""""", """"""""Current location"""""""", and """"""""Updated location"""""""" info.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Geolocation - Doesn't show """"Reverse Geo"""", """"Current location"""", and """"Updated location"""" info
Description: """"Description: When running Geolocation second time after reinstallation or killing app, it doesn't show """"""""Revers Geo"""""""", """"""""Current location"""""""", and """"""""Updated location"""""""" info. Also occurs in 1.8.2 Steps: 1. Reinstall or kill KitchenSink, if it's already installed. 2. Run KitchenSink 3. Go to """"""""Phone-Geolocation"""""""" 4. Go back 5. Launch """"""""Geolocation"""""""" second time Expected result: Every time when running Geolocation, all information should be presented. Actual result: After second time launching Geolocation it doesn't show """"""""Revers Geo"""""""", """"""""Current location"""""""", and """"""""Updated location"""""""" info. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8122,12,"""iOS: Implement support for Ti.UI.INHERIT""","""""""Ti.UI.INHERIT tells a control that it's width/height should be based on the parent's width/height, respectively. If the parent's width (for example) is SIZE, then the inherited width is SIZE, otherwise it is FILL. As a result, if a control inherits, the result will be either SIZE or FILL but nothing else. Another way to think about this is that inherit is a different type of """"""""auto""""""""...instead of looking to the controls default of FILL/SIZE, it looks to the parent to infer FILL/SIZE.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Implement support for Ti.UI.INHERIT
Description: """"Ti.UI.INHERIT tells a control that it's width/height should be based on the parent's width/height, respectively. If the parent's width (for example) is SIZE, then the inherited width is SIZE, otherwise it is FILL. As a result, if a control inherits, the result will be either SIZE or FILL but nothing else. Another way to think about this is that inherit is a different type of """"""""auto""""""""...instead of looking to the controls default of FILL/SIZE, it looks to the parent to infer FILL/SIZE.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8121,12,"""Android: Implement support for Ti.UI.INHERIT""","""""""Ti.UI.INHERIT tells a control that it's width/height should be based on the parent's width/height, respectively. If the parent's width (for example) is SIZE, then the inherited width is SIZE, otherwise it is FILL. As a result, if a control inherits, the result will be either SIZE or FILL but nothing else. Another way to think about this is that inherit is a different type of """"""""auto""""""""...instead of looking to the controls default of FILL/SIZE, it looks to the parent to infer FILL/SIZE.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Implement support for Ti.UI.INHERIT
Description: """"Ti.UI.INHERIT tells a control that it's width/height should be based on the parent's width/height, respectively. If the parent's width (for example) is SIZE, then the inherited width is SIZE, otherwise it is FILL. As a result, if a control inherits, the result will be either SIZE or FILL but nothing else. Another way to think about this is that inherit is a different type of """"""""auto""""""""...instead of looking to the controls default of FILL/SIZE, it looks to the parent to infer FILL/SIZE.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8120,12,"""iOS: Contacts - Text fields to enter contact information don't exist""","""""""Description:  There are no text fields to enter contact information.     Steps:  1. Run KitchenSink  2. Go to Phone-Contacts-Add Contact    Expected result:  Should see the text fields and should have an ability to enter contact information, and add a new contact.    Actual result:  Text fields don't exist.    Note: Doesn't occur in 1.8.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Contacts - Text fields to enter contact information don't exist
Description: """"Description: There are no text fields to enter contact information. Steps: 1. Run KitchenSink 2. Go to Phone-Contacts-Add Contact Expected result: Should see the text fields and should have an ability to enter contact information, and add a new contact. Actual result: Text fields don't exist. Note: Doesn't occur in 1.8.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-8119,12,"""MobileWeb: Splash screen shows artifacts when changing orientation or resizing""","""""""The splash screen needs to be position:fixed, top:0, left:0, right:0, and bottom:0 during launch. After launch, if the browser is resized or orientation is changed, you can see the splash screen while the layout system waits to render the screen again.    We either need to break parity with ios and android and hide the splash screen once a window is opened and then show it again when all windows are closed -or- we need to reset the splash screen's right and bottom and override the width and height with the browser size during the layout function so that they are synced.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Splash screen shows artifacts when changing orientation or resizing
Description: """"The splash screen needs to be position:fixed, top:0, left:0, right:0, and bottom:0 during launch. After launch, if the browser is resized or orientation is changed, you can see the splash screen while the layout system waits to render the screen again. We either need to break parity with ios and android and hide the splash screen once a window is opened and then show it again when all windows are closed -or- we need to reset the splash screen's right and bottom and override the width and height with the browser size during the layout function so that they are synced.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8116,12,"""MobileWeb: maxRowHeight and minRowHeight in TableView are not layout aware""","""""""maxRowHeight and minRowHeight naively set minHeight and maxHeight on the dom node, but this means the layout algorithm won't know when the row is being clamped, and thus not layout correctly.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: maxRowHeight and minRowHeight in TableView are not layout aware
Description: """"maxRowHeight and minRowHeight naively set minHeight and maxHeight on the dom node, but this means the layout algorithm won't know when the row is being clamped, and thus not layout correctly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8115,12,"""iOS: Feature to detect different versions of iPhone and iPad""","""""""It has been requested to add a new feature to detect different versions of iPad and iPhone i.e. iPad 1, 2 and 3 and iPhone 3GS, 4, 4S to Titanium platform.   """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Feature to detect different versions of iPhone and iPad
Description: """"It has been requested to add a new feature to detect different versions of iPad and iPhone i.e. iPad 1, 2 and 3 and iPhone 3GS, 4, 4S to Titanium platform. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8114,12,"""iOS: Mapview regionChanged event does not fire""","""""""Ran the attached app.js file to reproduce the issue.    The regionChanged event listener is giving the same latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta values even when the mapview is zoomed in or out.        The API info statements print out the same values on the console.    *EXPECTED BEHAVIOR*    The delta values should be updated on every zoom activity.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Mapview regionChanged event does not fire
