TIMOB-8112,12,"""Coverage: Update namespace parsing / mangling for both Android and iOS""","""""""To test this, you will need to first have iOS Coverage results from Magnesium:  https://github.com/<USER>Magnesium    Once you've succesfully built / run the Magnesium collector, run the coverage report generator, and open the result html:      There are many classes that are incorrectly parsed / mangled, resulting in things like:  * `Titanium.D`  * `Titanium.Appi`  * `Titanium.D.OMDocFrag` (many more like this)  * `Titanium.Stream.Titanium.Stream.BlobStream` (many more like this)  * `Titanium.XML.XML.Attr` (many more like this)""""""",Bug,"Title: Coverage: Update namespace parsing / mangling for both Android and iOS
Description: """"To test this, you will need to first have iOS Coverage results from Magnesium: https://github.com/<USER>Magnesium Once you've succesfully built / run the Magnesium collector, run the coverage report generator, and open the result html: There are many classes that are incorrectly parsed / mangled, resulting in things like: * `Titanium.D` * `Titanium.Appi` * `Titanium.D.OMDocFrag` (many more like this) * `Titanium.Stream.Titanium.Stream.BlobStream` (many more like this) * `Titanium.XML.XML.Attr` (many more like this)""""",title+description
TIMOB-8111,12,"""Coverage: Filter Cloud APIs from coverage report""","""""""The Ti.Cloud module and other Ti.Cloud* proxies are showing the current coverage report, but they should not count against total platform coverage. To test this, run the coverage report, and view the output html to see that Ti.Cloud APIs are documented, but """"""""not implemented"""""""" in platform.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Coverage: Filter Cloud APIs from coverage report
Description: """"The Ti.Cloud module and other Ti.Cloud* proxies are showing the current coverage report, but they should not count against total platform coverage. To test this, run the coverage report, and view the output html to see that Ti.Cloud APIs are documented, but """"""""not implemented"""""""" in platform. """"",title+description
TIMOB-8110,12,"""MobileWeb: Create a new height/width constant of Ti.UI.INHERIT""","""""""There are a number of times where controls need to do either UI.SIZE or UI.FILL based on the parent's width/height. Right now this is accomplished manually, resulting in a lot of repeated code. We should implement a new constant of UI.INHERIT to avoid this code repetition.    Ti.UI.INHERIT tells a control that it's width/height should be set to the parent's width/height, respectively. This operation is considered a raw copy of the user assigned value, not the calculated value. If the parent width/height is undefined, then the child inherits the parent's default width/height, which is always defined. If a parent's width/height or default width/height is also INHERIT, then the child goes up the element chain until it finds a width/height that is not INHERIT.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Create a new height/width constant of Ti.UI.INHERIT
Description: """"There are a number of times where controls need to do either UI.SIZE or UI.FILL based on the parent's width/height. Right now this is accomplished manually, resulting in a lot of repeated code. We should implement a new constant of UI.INHERIT to avoid this code repetition. Ti.UI.INHERIT tells a control that it's width/height should be set to the parent's width/height, respectively. This operation is considered a raw copy of the user assigned value, not the calculated value. If the parent width/height is undefined, then the child inherits the parent's default width/height, which is always defined. If a parent's width/height or default width/height is also INHERIT, then the child goes up the element chain until it finds a width/height that is not INHERIT.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8109,12,"""iOS: Samples - Todo List sample crashes at launch""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. In TiStudio, import Todo List sample from the Samples pane  2. Install to an iOS device  3. Launch app    Actual: App crashes at launch. See attachments for console output and crash report.  Expected: App should not crash.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Samples - Todo List sample crashes at launch
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. In TiStudio, import Todo List sample from the Samples pane 2. Install to an iOS device 3. Launch app Actual: App crashes at launch. See attachments for console output and crash report. Expected: App should not crash.""""",title+description
