TIMOB-8097,12,"""Splash Screen Orientation 2004 Test upside down orientation on iphone is crashing on launch""","""""""1) Install the upPortrait app on device    2) Hold device upside down and launch app    3) Hold the device in portrait mode    4) Hold the device so that the top is pointing right    5) Hold the device so that the top is pointing left    6) Close app    Orientation- upsideDownOnly App crashes on launching it to iphone""""""",Bug,"Title: Splash Screen Orientation 2004 Test upside down orientation on iphone is crashing on launch
Description: """"1) Install the upPortrait app on device 2) Hold device upside down and launch app 3) Hold the device in portrait mode 4) Hold the device so that the top is pointing right 5) Hold the device so that the top is pointing left 6) Close app Orientation- upsideDownOnly App crashes on launching it to iphone""""",title+description
TIMOB-8095,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Platform.openURL() causes errors if it can't load a URL""","""""""If you do Ti.Platform.openURL(""""""""tel:1231231233""""""""), the browser will attempt to redirect to the telephone number. If the browser doesn't know how to deal with phone numbers, then it results in an error page and you need to hit the back button which reloads the page.    Instead of doing a window.location.href, try opening the URL in an iframe.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Platform.openURL() causes errors if it can't load a URL
Description: """"If you do Ti.Platform.openURL(""""""""tel:1231231233""""""""), the browser will attempt to redirect to the telephone number. If the browser doesn't know how to deal with phone numbers, then it results in an error page and you need to hit the back button which reloads the page. Instead of doing a window.location.href, try opening the URL in an iframe.""""",title+description
TIMOB-8092,12,"""iOS: Mapview zooms to Titanium default even after modifying the mapview region property""","""""""1. Run the attached app.js sample.    2. Click on the Select Annotation button (This event listener has mapview region modified)    3. The map zooms to what seems to be a default zoom level instead of what is specified in the event listener above.    4. Now move the map around and then from this point, on clicking the Select Annotation button the zoom level is always taken as the one that has been modified.       *Note:* Just modifying the latitude and longitude properties and not the delta ones for the map too has this behavior.          *EXPECTED BEHAVIOR*    The mapview should center around the window with the assigned coordinates.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Mapview zooms to Titanium default even after modifying the mapview region property
Description: """"1. Run the attached app.js sample. 2. Click on the Select Annotation button (This event listener has mapview region modified) 3. The map zooms to what seems to be a default zoom level instead of what is specified in the event listener above. 4. Now move the map around and then from this point, on clicking the Select Annotation button the zoom level is always taken as the one that has been modified. *Note:* Just modifying the latitude and longitude properties and not the delta ones for the map too has this behavior. *EXPECTED BEHAVIOR* The mapview should center around the window with the assigned coordinates.""""",title+description
