TIMOB-7898,12,"""iOS: Expose applicationDidReceiveMemoryWarning to JavaScript side""","""""""The requirement is to expose applicationDidReceiveMemoryWarning to the JS side of the application, possibly as an event, so that custom memory management could be put in place (like manually removing any UI elements etc.).""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Expose applicationDidReceiveMemoryWarning to JavaScript side
Description: """"The requirement is to expose applicationDidReceiveMemoryWarning to the JS side of the application, possibly as an event, so that custom memory management could be put in place (like manually removing any UI elements etc.).""""",title+description
TIMOB-7896,12,"""iOS: Modal window disappears""","""""""While testing TIMOB-6391 for another bug, I noticed that by opening the KS iPad -> plain split view in portrait, then clicking """"""""Show modal"""""""", then dismissing the modal, and then clicking """"""""Show modal"""""""" again displayed a black window.    Testing instructions are on TIMOB-6391 and described above.    Only reproducible 1x, making this bug a lower priority.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Modal window disappears
Description: """"While testing TIMOB-6391 for another bug, I noticed that by opening the KS iPad -> plain split view in portrait, then clicking """"""""Show modal"""""""", then dismissing the modal, and then clicking """"""""Show modal"""""""" again displayed a black window. Testing instructions are on TIMOB-6391 and described above. Only reproducible 1x, making this bug a lower priority.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7895,12,"""iOS: Clearing backgroundImage turns off clipsToBounds""","""""""In -[TiUIView setBackgroundImage_:], the second-to-last line `self.clipsToBounds = bgImage!=nil;` indicates that clearing bgImage will turn off clipsToBounds, despite the possibility of subviews needing clipping or rounded corners needing clipping. This is NOT a regression, as this code has existed previously.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Clearing backgroundImage turns off clipsToBounds
Description: """"In -[TiUIView setBackgroundImage_:], the second-to-last line `self.clipsToBounds = bgImage!=nil;` indicates that clearing bgImage will turn off clipsToBounds, despite the possibility of subviews needing clipping or rounded corners needing clipping. This is NOT a regression, as this code has existed previously.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7894,12,"""iOS: Splash screen is being displayed also when bringing back the app from background""","""""""h2. Problem description  Splash screen is displayed also after bringing back the app from the background.  Splash image should be displayed only after the app is launched.    h2. Steps to reproduce  1. Install and open the default titanium studio app  2. Click on the home button  3. Launch again the app (both from app menu and from running app menu)      Expected result: app is openend with no splash screen displayed.  Result: app is opened with splash screen displayed.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Splash screen is being displayed also when bringing back the app from background
Description: """"h2. Problem description Splash screen is displayed also after bringing back the app from the background. Splash image should be displayed only after the app is launched. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Install and open the default titanium studio app 2. Click on the home button 3. Launch again the app (both from app menu and from running app menu) Expected result: app is openend with no splash screen displayed. Result: app is opened with splash screen displayed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7893,12,"""iOS: UI.ScrollView - canCancelEvents property does not work""","""""""h2. Problem    According to stramer in [this comment|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1515/files#r492538], the [Titanium.UI.ScrollView|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.ScrollView-object] [canCancelEvents|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.ScrollView.canCancelEvents-property.html] property does not work due to an invalid setter.      Once fixed, add the following back to the documentation:    {code:lang=none|title=ScrollView.yml}    - name: canCancelEvents      summary: |          Determines whether this scroll view can cancel subview touches in order to scroll instead.      description: Set to `false` to ensure that subview touches always take effect.      type: Boolean      default: true      platforms: [iphone, ipad]  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI.ScrollView - canCancelEvents property does not work
Description: """"h2. Problem According to stramer in [this comment|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1515/files#r492538], the [Titanium.UI.ScrollView|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.ScrollView-object] [canCancelEvents|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.ScrollView.canCancelEvents-property.html] property does not work due to an invalid setter. Once fixed, add the following back to the documentation: {code:lang=none|title=ScrollView.yml} - name: canCancelEvents summary: | Determines whether this scroll view can cancel subview touches in order to scroll instead. description: Set to `false` to ensure that subview touches always take effect. type: Boolean default: true platforms: [iphone, ipad] {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-7892,12,"""Android: Ti.Gesture.orientationchange event only fires once""","""""""Not sure if this is Emulator-specific or not. When running the code below in the emulator, the first time I rotate the device (Ctrl+F11), I see the label change to show the current orientation. However, subsequent rotations produce no update to the label. Also, the whole app seems to get stuck in the first orientation it switches into, such as landscape left.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.Gesture.orientationchange event only fires once
Description: """"Not sure if this is Emulator-specific or not. When running the code below in the emulator, the first time I rotate the device (Ctrl+F11), I see the label change to show the current orientation. However, subsequent rotations produce no update to the label. Also, the whole app seems to get stuck in the first orientation it switches into, such as landscape left. """"",title+description
