TIMOB-7878,12,"""iOS: Xcode 4.3 - Xcode-select must be run on clean install of Xcode 4.3 in order to use Titanium""","""""""Description:  While testing Xcode 4.3 integration with our tools I used a clean system to install Xcode 4.3 then Studio and 1.8.2 SDK. I was unable to use the Xcode install until I used Xcode-select and set the path to /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer.    Steps to reproduce:  1) On a clean Mac OS X image, install Xcode 4.3 from the Mac App store  2) Install Studio 1.0.9  3) Allow Studio to install 1.8.2 GA SDK  4) Check Dashboard configuration or try to build a project    Result:  You will be unable to make use of Xcode    Expected:  Xcode available and projects can be created and run  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Xcode 4.3 - Xcode-select must be run on clean install of Xcode 4.3 in order to use Titanium
Description: """"Description: While testing Xcode 4.3 integration with our tools I used a clean system to install Xcode 4.3 then Studio and 1.8.2 SDK. I was unable to use the Xcode install until I used Xcode-select and set the path to /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer. Steps to reproduce: 1) On a clean Mac OS X image, install Xcode 4.3 from the Mac App store 2) Install Studio 1.0.9 3) Allow Studio to install 1.8.2 GA SDK 4) Check Dashboard configuration or try to build a project Result: You will be unable to make use of Xcode Expected: Xcode available and projects can be created and run """"",title+description
TIMOB-7877,12,"""Android: TableView scroll event contentOffset returning null""","""""""TableView scroll event contentOffset returning null on android. It works fine on iOS but not on android.  h4. Repro Steps  1. Run the below code.  2. In the alert the scroll event contentOffset will return null.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView scroll event contentOffset returning null
Description: """"TableView scroll event contentOffset returning null on android. It works fine on iOS but not on android. h4. Repro Steps 1. Run the below code. 2. In the alert the scroll event contentOffset will return null. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7876,12,"""Android: Ti.App.addEventListener() from a commonJS unit causes later Ti.App.removeEventListener() to crash""","""""""h2.Problem  When Ti.App.addEventListener() is called from a commonJS unit, other attempts to add an event listener to Ti.App on the same event in normal app units, and then remove that event listener, causes a crash:      *This is a regression*, as it did not occur in SDK 1.8.1.    h2.Testcase  Ti.App.addEventListener(a,b) is called from a commonJS unit.  Another Ti.App.addEventListener(a,c) is called from app.js (notice that the first parameter, the event name, is the same in both calls).  Also in app.js, Ti.App.removeEventListener(a,c) is called, which causes the crash.    Put the following code into a new Ti mobile project and run it to the emulator.  The crash occurs without any interaction, as soon as the main window appears.    {code:title=app.js}  var Procs=require('CommonProcs');  Procs.FirstStep();    var win1=Ti.UI.createWindow({                      exitOnClose:true,                      navBarHidden:true                     })    var TheLabel=Ti.UI.createLabel({          color:'white',          text:'Hello World',          width:'auto'       });  win1.add(TheLabel);  win1.open();      function MainWinOrientationChange()  {    Ti.API.info('MainWinOrientationChange');  }  Ti.App.addEventListener('CustomOrientationChange',MainWinOrientationChange);  Ti.App.removeEventListener('CustomOrientationChange',MainWinOrientationChange);    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.App.addEventListener() from a commonJS unit causes later Ti.App.removeEventListener() to crash
Description: """"h2.Problem When Ti.App.addEventListener() is called from a commonJS unit, other attempts to add an event listener to Ti.App on the same event in normal app units, and then remove that event listener, causes a crash: *This is a regression*, as it did not occur in SDK 1.8.1. h2.Testcase Ti.App.addEventListener(a,b) is called from a commonJS unit. Another Ti.App.addEventListener(a,c) is called from app.js (notice that the first parameter, the event name, is the same in both calls). Also in app.js, Ti.App.removeEventListener(a,c) is called, which causes the crash. Put the following code into a new Ti mobile project and run it to the emulator. The crash occurs without any interaction, as soon as the main window appears. {code:title=app.js} var Procs=require('CommonProcs'); Procs.FirstStep(); var win1=Ti.UI.createWindow({ exitOnClose:true, navBarHidden:true }) var TheLabel=Ti.UI.createLabel({ color:'white', text:'Hello World', width:'auto' }); win1.add(TheLabel); win1.open(); function MainWinOrientationChange() { Ti.API.info('MainWinOrientationChange'); } Ti.App.addEventListener('CustomOrientationChange',MainWinOrientationChange); Ti.App.removeEventListener('CustomOrientationChange',MainWinOrientationChange); """"",title+description
TIMOB-7875,12,"""iOS: Focus event not firing on window under iOS 4.3, but works under iOS 5.0""","""""""BUG:   Focus event on window doesn't fire under iOS version 4.3 when modal window closes.    Expected Behaviour (iOS 5):  Open modal window, close modal window, focus event fires putting alert on screen    Bug (iOS 4.3):  Open modal window, close modal window, focus event doesn't fire.    See attached example""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Focus event not firing on window under iOS 4.3, but works under iOS 5.0
Description: """"BUG: Focus event on window doesn't fire under iOS version 4.3 when modal window closes. Expected Behaviour (iOS 5): Open modal window, close modal window, focus event fires putting alert on screen Bug (iOS 4.3): Open modal window, close modal window, focus event doesn't fire. See attached example""""",title+description
TIMOB-7874,12,"""iOS: Include app name in the user agent""","""""""Right now the user agent received on the cocoafish server is something like:    """"""""<USER>Titanium/1.8.2.v20120217114657 (iPhone Simulator/5.0; iPhone OS; en_US;)    It would be nice to include the app name for better debugging and tracking:    For example:  User agent """"""""FestSelects 1.0 (iPod touch; iPhone OS 5.0.1; en_US)""""""""  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Include app name in the user agent
Description: """"Right now the user agent received on the cocoafish server is something like: """"""""<USER>Titanium/1.8.2.v20120217114657 (iPhone Simulator/5.0; iPhone OS; en_US;) It would be nice to include the app name for better debugging and tracking: For example: User agent """"""""FestSelects 1.0 (iPod touch; iPhone OS 5.0.1; en_US)"""""""" """"",title+description
TIMOB-7873,12,"""iOS: Anchor point affects pinning""","""""""In iOS, setting the {{anchorPoint}} property of a view's layer influences how it is laid out with respect to the geometry of the containing view. It does not affect """"""""just transforms"""""""" on the object (in actuality, it's affecting the identity transform), but also the ability to pin l/r/t/b on views.    From Blain in IRC as an example:  bq. Position should be clarified. On iOS, position is defined by the anchorpoint, which defaults to 0.5, 0.5. That is, for an object whose top is 50, left is 50, bottom is 100, and right is 100, x=75, y=75. If the anchorpoint was changed to 0,0, the same object with given top/left/bottom/right bounds's x and y would be 50. If the anchorpoint is 1,1, the same object's x and y would be 100.     See: https://developer.apple.com/library/mac/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/CoreAnimation_guide/Articles/Layers.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40006082-SW9""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Anchor point affects pinning
Description: """"In iOS, setting the {{anchorPoint}} property of a view's layer influences how it is laid out with respect to the geometry of the containing view. It does not affect """"""""just transforms"""""""" on the object (in actuality, it's affecting the identity transform), but also the ability to pin l/r/t/b on views. From Blain in IRC as an example: bq. Position should be clarified. On iOS, position is defined by the anchorpoint, which defaults to 0.5, 0.5. That is, for an object whose top is 50, left is 50, bottom is 100, and right is 100, x=75, y=75. If the anchorpoint was changed to 0,0, the same object with given top/left/bottom/right bounds's x and y would be 50. If the anchorpoint is 1,1, the same object's x and y would be 100. See: https://developer.apple.com/library/mac/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/CoreAnimation_guide/Articles/Layers.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40006082-SW9""""",title+description
TIMOB-7872,12,"""Android: Finalize module API specification""","""""""Based on the initial module API docs, we need to pare down the set of public functions and create a reasonable specification. This will include evaluating the included APIs, excluded but relevant APIs, and determining APIs which should be immediately deprecated for replacement.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Finalize module API specification
Description: """"Based on the initial module API docs, we need to pare down the set of public functions and create a reasonable specification. This will include evaluating the included APIs, excluded but relevant APIs, and determining APIs which should be immediately deprecated for replacement.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7871,12,"""iOS: Finalize module API specification""","""""""Based on the initial module API docs, we need to pare down the set of public functions and create a reasonable specification. This will include evaluating the included APIs, excluded but relevant APIs, and determining APIs which should be immediately deprecated for replacement.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Finalize module API specification
