Description: """"If possible, expose a method similar to iOS that allows a user to get the path of where the database file is being stored. For example on iOS if I use the following code I will get the path to where the db file has been stored on the filesystem.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7850,12,"""Android: Can't upload files via HTTPClient (parity issue)""","""""""h4. Problem description  Customer wants to upload a file thru a webservice. When we test this code in iOS, works like a charm. When trying to upload with Android, it fails. (same webservice, user, etc).    h4. Actual Results  The file can't be uploaded when running the program from Android    h4. Expected results  The app being able to upload files to the webservice    h4. Test case    1. Create a new mobile project  2. Paste the code  3. Run it  4. Press """"""""Click"""""""" button  5. See the logs    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Can't upload files via HTTPClient (parity issue)
Description: """"h4. Problem description Customer wants to upload a file thru a webservice. When we test this code in iOS, works like a charm. When trying to upload with Android, it fails. (same webservice, user, etc). h4. Actual Results The file can't be uploaded when running the program from Android h4. Expected results The app being able to upload files to the webservice h4. Test case 1. Create a new mobile project 2. Paste the code 3. Run it 4. Press """"""""Click"""""""" button 5. See the logs """"",title+description
TIMOB-7849,12,"""iOS: TiUIWebView beforeload event doesn't have the URL ""","""""""When beforeload event called in TiUIWebView.m the URL is unknown. The beforeload event should be moved to shouldStartLoadWithRequest, to let beforeload know what url will be opened.    A suggested fix can be found here:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/538""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TiUIWebView beforeload event doesn't have the URL
Description: """"When beforeload event called in TiUIWebView.m the URL is unknown. The beforeload event should be moved to shouldStartLoadWithRequest, to let beforeload know what url will be opened. A suggested fix can be found here: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/538""""",title+description
