TIMOB-7832,12,"""Android: Honeycomb 3.X: TabGroup: Default App and Tabbed Template: First tab not properly displayed on launch""","""""""When the default app is run on Honeycomb, the first tab is not displayed properly. Screenshots attached.  The tab displays correctly when re-selected.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the default app using Honeycomb (Android 3.X).  2. Observe first tab.    Expected Result:    Tab should be gray.    Actual Result:    Tab is not gray (as it is in all the other Android versions, and on re-selection of the tab).""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Honeycomb 3.X: TabGroup: Default App and Tabbed Template: First tab not properly displayed on launch
Description: """"When the default app is run on Honeycomb, the first tab is not displayed properly. Screenshots attached. The tab displays correctly when re-selected. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the default app using Honeycomb (Android 3.X). 2. Observe first tab. Expected Result: Tab should be gray. Actual Result: Tab is not gray (as it is in all the other Android versions, and on re-selection of the tab).""""",title+description
TIMOB-7831,12,"""Android: Master/Detail Application Template: console logs JNI: DeleteGlobalRef(0xdebcce57) failed to find entry warnings""","""""""When the Master/Detail Application template app is used, JNI: DeleteGlobalRef(0xdebcce57) failed to find entry warnings are repeatedly logged to the console.  This only occurs in 1.8.2.X across all Android versions, with the exception of Android 4.0.2.  This does not occur in 1.8.1. This is a regression.    Note: The functionality of the app does not appear to be affected.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the Master/Detail Application template using 1.8.2.X.  2. Click on a row.  3. Press 'back' button if applicable.  4. Cycle as needed. Check the console.    Expected Result:    No warnings.    Actual Result:    A flood of 02-27 17:52:48.179: W/dalvikvm(3195): JNI: DeleteGlobalRef(0xdebcce57) failed to find entry (valid=0) warnings. Log attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Master/Detail Application Template: console logs JNI: DeleteGlobalRef(0xdebcce57) failed to find entry warnings
Description: """"When the Master/Detail Application template app is used, JNI: DeleteGlobalRef(0xdebcce57) failed to find entry warnings are repeatedly logged to the console. This only occurs in 1.8.2.X across all Android versions, with the exception of Android 4.0.2. This does not occur in 1.8.1. This is a regression. Note: The functionality of the app does not appear to be affected. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the Master/Detail Application template using 1.8.2.X. 2. Click on a row. 3. Press 'back' button if applicable. 4. Cycle as needed. Check the console. Expected Result: No warnings. Actual Result: A flood of 02-27 17:52:48.179: W/dalvikvm(3195): JNI: DeleteGlobalRef(0xdebcce57) failed to find entry (valid=0) warnings. Log attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7830,12,"""iOS: keyboardToolbar behavior issues with multiple text fields""","""""""h3. Issue  -keyboardToolbar hides then shows when moving from one textField to another while the keyboard remains up  -after selecting a different textField, when you come back to the first, the buttons are gone from the keyboardToolbar.    h3. Repor Steps  -Build code below  -Click on the top textField, then the second, then the third, then back to the first.  -You will see the toolbar hide and show, then lose all of its buttons on the fourth focus.    h3. Code  {code:title=app.js}  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'#fff'});    var send = Titanium.UI.createButton({  title : 'Send',  style : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.DONE,  });    var camera = Titanium.UI.createButton({  systemButton : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.CAMERA,  });    var cancel = Titanium.UI.createButton({  systemButton : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.CANCEL  });    var flexSpace = Titanium.UI.createButton({  systemButton : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.FLEXIBLE_SPACE  });      var textfield1 = Titanium.UI.createTextField({  hintText : 'Focus to see keyboard with toolbar',  height : 35,  width : 300,  top : 50,  borderStyle : Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL,  keyboardToolbar : [cancel, flexSpace, camera, flexSpace, send],  keyboardToolbarColor : '#999',  keyboardToolbarHeight : 40,  });    var textfield2 = Titanium.UI.createTextField({  hintText : 'Focus to see keyboard with toolbar',  height : 35,  width : 300,  top : 100,  borderStyle : Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL,  keyboardToolbar : [cancel, flexSpace, camera, flexSpace, send],  keyboardToolbarColor : '#999',  keyboardToolbarHeight : 40,  });    var textfield3 = Titanium.UI.createTextField({  hintText : 'Focus to see keyboard with toolbar',  height : 35,  width : 300,  top : 150,  borderStyle : Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL,  keyboardToolbar : [cancel, flexSpace, camera, flexSpace, send],  keyboardToolbarColor : '#999',  keyboardToolbarHeight : 40,  });    win1.add(textfield1);  win1.add(textfield2);  win1.add(textfield3);    win1.open();  {code}  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: keyboardToolbar behavior issues with multiple text fields
Description: """"h3. Issue -keyboardToolbar hides then shows when moving from one textField to another while the keyboard remains up -after selecting a different textField, when you come back to the first, the buttons are gone from the keyboardToolbar. h3. Repor Steps -Build code below -Click on the top textField, then the second, then the third, then back to the first. -You will see the toolbar hide and show, then lose all of its buttons on the fourth focus. h3. Code {code:title=app.js} var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var send = Titanium.UI.createButton({ title : 'Send', style : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.DONE, }); var camera = Titanium.UI.createButton({ systemButton : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.CAMERA, }); var cancel = Titanium.UI.createButton({ systemButton : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.CANCEL }); var flexSpace = Titanium.UI.createButton({ systemButton : Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.FLEXIBLE_SPACE }); var textfield1 = Titanium.UI.createTextField({ hintText : 'Focus to see keyboard with toolbar', height : 35, width : 300, top : 50, borderStyle : Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL, keyboardToolbar : [cancel, flexSpace, camera, flexSpace, send], keyboardToolbarColor : '#999', keyboardToolbarHeight : 40, }); var textfield2 = Titanium.UI.createTextField({ hintText : 'Focus to see keyboard with toolbar', height : 35, width : 300, top : 100, borderStyle : Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL, keyboardToolbar : [cancel, flexSpace, camera, flexSpace, send], keyboardToolbarColor : '#999', keyboardToolbarHeight : 40, }); var textfield3 = Titanium.UI.createTextField({ hintText : 'Focus to see keyboard with toolbar', height : 35, width : 300, top : 150, borderStyle : Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_BEZEL, keyboardToolbar : [cancel, flexSpace, camera, flexSpace, send], keyboardToolbarColor : '#999', keyboardToolbarHeight : 40, }); win1.add(textfield1); win1.add(textfield2); win1.add(textfield3); win1.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-7829,12,"""Android: IllegalFormatConversionException in String.format for integers with positional arguments""","""""""h4. Problem Description  Integer format strings that contain positional arguments result in an IllegalFormatConversionException when passed to String.format().  If the positional part of the format is removed, the call works fine.    h4. Expected Results  Strings with positional should work fine.    h4. Actual results  The strings with positional information are throwing an exception.     h4. Test case           h4. Crashlog    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: IllegalFormatConversionException in String.format for integers with positional arguments
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Integer format strings that contain positional arguments result in an IllegalFormatConversionException when passed to String.format(). If the positional part of the format is removed, the call works fine. h4. Expected Results Strings with positional should work fine. h4. Actual results The strings with positional information are throwing an exception. h4. Test case h4. Crashlog """"",title+description
TIMOB-7828,12,"""Ti API: Problem with remove method to clear all children in a scrollview""","""""""Hi,    Lots of problem with remove method. Didn't find any function to clear all children.  Create a simple scrollView (i guess it's the same for views), add some ImageViews inside and try :      or      then ...        Getting sometimes :     at this line :      I tried other ways to do removeChildren method but none works well on titanium mobile 1.8.1.0 ( http://developer.<USER>com/question/131151/emptying-a-view#228486 )    ********************    Another method is the following :       but there's a warning on each remove invocation (in my case it's a scrollView instead of a view but i guess it's the same pb) :        and sometimes i get    for line      ********************    - In general it's hard to loop through children of a view an to remove some children. This kind of way to do return sometimes an error :        at line  it launch sometimes this exception          Best Regards  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Problem with remove method to clear all children in a scrollview
Description: """"Hi, Lots of problem with remove method. Didn't find any function to clear all children. Create a simple scrollView (i guess it's the same for views), add some ImageViews inside and try : or then ... Getting sometimes : at this line : I tried other ways to do removeChildren method but none works well on titanium mobile 1.8.1.0 ( http://developer.<USER>com/question/131151/emptying-a-view#228486 ) ******************** Another method is the following : but there's a warning on each remove invocation (in my case it's a scrollView instead of a view but i guess it's the same pb) : and sometimes i get for line ******************** - In general it's hard to loop through children of a view an to remove some children. This kind of way to do return sometimes an error : at line it launch sometimes this exception Best Regards """"",title+description
TIMOB-7827,12,"""Android: Add support for extrahigh density (320 dpi) devices""","""""""h2.Request  Android devices with dpi of 320 are now appearing on the market.  Titanium Studio supports low (120 dpi), medium (160 dpi), and high (240 dpi) images via the \Resources\android\images\ directory's low, medium, and high subdirectories.    This request is for a new *extrahigh* subdirectory to be supported during the build <USER> which would map to the appropriate res\drawable-*xhdpi*\ directory.    We would also need support for extrahigh density splash screens, presumably in directories like \Resources\android\images\res-notlong-port-*xhdpi*, etc.    h2.Relevant Q&A  [http://developer.<USER>com/question/128278/xdpi-android-res-supported]""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add support for extrahigh density (320 dpi) devices
Description: """"h2.Request Android devices with dpi of 320 are now appearing on the market. Titanium Studio supports low (120 dpi), medium (160 dpi), and high (240 dpi) images via the \Resources\android\images\ directory's low, medium, and high subdirectories. This request is for a new *extrahigh* subdirectory to be supported during the build <USER> which would map to the appropriate res\drawable-*xhdpi*\ directory. We would also need support for extrahigh density splash screens, presumably in directories like \Resources\android\images\res-notlong-port-*xhdpi*, etc. h2.Relevant Q&A [http://developer.<USER>com/question/128278/xdpi-android-res-supported]""""",title+description
TIMOB-7826,12,"""iOS: Change the mail's dialogue language  dynamically""","""""""h4. Problem description  Currently, the i18n support allows the customer to change the language of the app when running, except for the mail dialogs, that stick to the default settings of CFBundleDevelopmentRegion in Info.plist.     h4. Actual results  Even if you changed the phone's language to a new one, you will be seeing the default language from CFBundleDevelopmentRegion.    h4. Expected Results.  When you change the language in the phone's settings, it should reflect in the mail dialog.     h4. Steps to reproduce  1. Create a mobile App  2. Add the code  3. Change the phone's language in the main settings  4. Start the app and start the dialogue  4. You won't see the i18n change in the mail dialogue language.      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Change the mail's dialogue language dynamically
Description: """"h4. Problem description Currently, the i18n support allows the customer to change the language of the app when running, except for the mail dialogs, that stick to the default settings of CFBundleDevelopmentRegion in Info.plist. h4. Actual results Even if you changed the phone's language to a new one, you will be seeing the default language from CFBundleDevelopmentRegion. h4. Expected Results. When you change the language in the phone's settings, it should reflect in the mail dialog. h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a mobile App 2. Add the code 3. Change the phone's language in the main settings 4. Start the app and start the dialogue 4. You won't see the i18n change in the mail dialogue language. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7825,12,"""MobileWeb: Expose withCredentials and userAgent on HTTPClient""","""""""h1. Feature  Two properties are needed for a particular instance of cross domain requesting:  - Expose the withCredentials property of XMLHttpRequest via HTTPClient.  - Allow overriding or excluding the UserAgent request header via a userAgent property passed in the constructor.    h2. Why  For some cross domain requests, these properties need to be set, or the request won't be valid. (Cookies and authorization need to be included, and the server doesn't accept the UserAgent header.)""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Expose withCredentials and userAgent on HTTPClient
Description: """"h1. Feature Two properties are needed for a particular instance of cross domain requesting: - Expose the withCredentials property of XMLHttpRequest via HTTPClient. - Allow overriding or excluding the UserAgent request header via a userAgent property passed in the constructor. h2. Why For some cross domain requests, these properties need to be set, or the request won't be valid. (Cookies and authorization need to be included, and the server doesn't accept the UserAgent header.)""""",title+description
TIMOB-7823,12,"""iOS: Place fonts in Resources/fonts for Android parity""","""""""Currently, iOS only checks for custom fonts in {{Resources}} and Android checks in {{Resources/fonts}}. We need to make sure that both platforms are checking both places. For iOS this will have to happen during build.    *NOTE:* This issue may only affect simulator but will have an influence on how TIMOB-7824 is resolved.    h4. Testing  ----    You will need to build an app with custom fonts in {{Resources/fonts}}, and follow the https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/Custom+Fonts instructions (if necessary; custom font building may be fixed before this ticket)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Place fonts in Resources/fonts for Android parity
Description: """"Currently, iOS only checks for custom fonts in {{Resources}} and Android checks in {{Resources/fonts}}. We need to make sure that both platforms are checking both places. For iOS this will have to happen during build. *NOTE:* This issue may only affect simulator but will have an influence on how TIMOB-7824 is resolved. h4. Testing ---- You will need to build an app with custom fonts in {{Resources/fonts}}, and follow the https://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/Custom+Fonts instructions (if necessary; custom font building may be fixed before this ticket)""""",title+description
TIMOB-7822,12,"""iOS: Application crashes deleting inbox messages""","""""""h2. Problem  Application is crashing after deleting a number of threads and messages in the inbox.    h2. Steps to reproduce  - Run the app and login  - Populate the inbox with at least ten threads with multiple messages each  - Delete and reinstall the app  - Delete some message, scroll down to load more messages and click on a thread    App crashes.    Attaching the crash log  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Application crashes deleting inbox messages
Description: """"h2. Problem Application is crashing after deleting a number of threads and messages in the inbox. h2. Steps to reproduce - Run the app and login - Populate the inbox with at least ten threads with multiple messages each - Delete and reinstall the app - Delete some message, scroll down to load more messages and click on a thread App crashes. Attaching the crash log """"",title+description
TIMOB-7820,12,"""iOS: Events - Focus event is fired multiple times during initial launch of app ""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Run following code:  {code:title=app.js}  var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();    var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({   name: """"""""win 1""""""""  });  var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({   name: """"""""Tab 1"""""""",   title:'Tab 1',   window:win1  });    var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({   name: """"""""win 2"""""""",   title:'Tab 2',   backgroundColor:'#fff'  });  var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({   name: """"""""Tab 2"""""""",   title:'Tab 2',   window:win2  });    tabGroup.addTab(tab1);  tabGroup.addTab(tab2);    tabGroup.addEventListener('focus', function(e){   Ti.API.info('-------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });  tab1.addEventListener('focus', function(e){   Ti.API.info('-------------> tab1 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });  tab2.addEventListener('focus', function(e){   Ti.API.info('-------------> tab2 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });  win1.addEventListener('focus', function(e){   Ti.API.info('-------------> win1 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });  win2.addEventListener('focus', function(e){   Ti.API.info('-------------> win2 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });    tab1.addEventListener('blur', function(e){   Ti.API.info('**************> tab1 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });  tab2.addEventListener('blur', function(e){   Ti.API.info('**************> tab2 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });  win1.addEventListener('blur', function(e){   Ti.API.info('**************> win1 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });  win2.addEventListener('blur', function(e){   Ti.API.info('**************> win2 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name);  });    tabGroup.open();  {code}    Actual: After initial launch of code, focus event is fired 3 times for tabGroup and 2 times for tab:  {code:xml}  Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - undefined  Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - undefined  Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tab1 focus event fired! - Tab 1  Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - undefined  Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tab1 focus event fired! - Tab 1  Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> win1 focus event fired! - win 1  {code}    Expected: Focus event should be fired once similarly when running code on Android:  {code:xml}  I/TiAPI   ( 1770): -------------> tab1 focus event fired! - Tab 1  I/TiAPI   ( 1770): -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - Tab 1  I/TiAPI   ( 1770): -------------> win1 focus event fired! - win 1  {code}    Note: Bug still occurs in 1.8.1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Events - Focus event is fired multiple times during initial launch of app
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Run following code: {code:title=app.js} var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ name: """"""""win 1"""""""" }); var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({ name: """"""""Tab 1"""""""", title:'Tab 1', window:win1 }); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ name: """"""""win 2"""""""", title:'Tab 2', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({ name: """"""""Tab 2"""""""", title:'Tab 2', window:win2 }); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.addTab(tab2); tabGroup.addEventListener('focus', function(e){ Ti.API.info('-------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); tab1.addEventListener('focus', function(e){ Ti.API.info('-------------> tab1 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); tab2.addEventListener('focus', function(e){ Ti.API.info('-------------> tab2 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); win1.addEventListener('focus', function(e){ Ti.API.info('-------------> win1 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); win2.addEventListener('focus', function(e){ Ti.API.info('-------------> win2 focus event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); tab1.addEventListener('blur', function(e){ Ti.API.info('**************> tab1 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); tab2.addEventListener('blur', function(e){ Ti.API.info('**************> tab2 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); win1.addEventListener('blur', function(e){ Ti.API.info('**************> win1 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); win2.addEventListener('blur', function(e){ Ti.API.info('**************> win2 blur event fired! - ' + e.source.name); }); tabGroup.open(); {code} Actual: After initial launch of code, focus event is fired 3 times for tabGroup and 2 times for tab: {code:xml} Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - undefined Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - undefined Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tab1 focus event fired! - Tab 1 Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - undefined Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> tab1 focus event fired! - Tab 1 Feb 27 10:26:42 unknown UIKitApplication:com.monkey.test[0x2b31][16642] <Notice>: [INFO] -------------> win1 focus event fired! - win 1 {code} Expected: Focus event should be fired once similarly when running code on Android: {code:xml} I/TiAPI ( 1770): -------------> tab1 focus event fired! - Tab 1 I/TiAPI ( 1770): -------------> tabGroup focus event fired! - Tab 1 I/TiAPI ( 1770): -------------> win1 focus event fired! - win 1 {code} Note: Bug still occurs in 1.8.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7819,12,"""Android: View - height:'auto' causing view to expand rather than contract to the size of its children""","""""""View does not resize correctly when height set to 'auto'. It should contract to the size of its children.  iPhone works correctly. See attached screenshot.    h4. Steps to reproduce:  Step 1: run the code below.  Step 2: notice that the second red block fills the bottom of the screen. It should only be ass tall as its child label as it is on the iphone in the attached screenshot.    {code:title=app.sj}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'white'  });  win.open();    var view1 = Ti.UI.createView({   top: 10,   height: 100,   backgroundColor: 'red',  });  var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({   text: 'Static',   height: 'auto',   width: 'auto',   backgroundColor: 'yellow',  });    var view3 = Ti.UI.createView({   top: 120,   height: 'auto',   backgroundColor: 'red',  });  var label2 = Ti.UI.createLabel({   text: 'Auto',   height: 'auto',   width: 'auto',   backgroundColor: 'yellow',  });    win.add(view1);  view1.add(label1);    win.add(view3);  view3.add(label2);  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: View - height:'auto' causing view to expand rather than contract to the size of its children
Description: """"View does not resize correctly when height set to 'auto'. It should contract to the size of its children. iPhone works correctly. See attached screenshot. h4. Steps to reproduce: Step 1: run the code below. Step 2: notice that the second red block fills the bottom of the screen. It should only be ass tall as its child label as it is on the iphone in the attached screenshot. {code:title=app.sj} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white' }); win.open(); var view1 = Ti.UI.createView({ top: 10, height: 100, backgroundColor: 'red', }); var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'Static', height: 'auto', width: 'auto', backgroundColor: 'yellow', }); var view3 = Ti.UI.createView({ top: 120, height: 'auto', backgroundColor: 'red', }); var label2 = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'Auto', height: 'auto', width: 'auto', backgroundColor: 'yellow', }); win.add(view1); view1.add(label1); win.add(view3); view3.add(label2); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-7818,12,"""MobileWeb: Switch Ti.Filesystem to use array buffers""","""""""NOTE: This feature cannot be implemented until browsers start to support array buffers. Current supported browsers include: iOS 4+, Android 4+, IE 10+, FF4+.    Right now, all binary files are treated as strings.  We should switch to array buffers, which better aligns with Titanium's buffers, blobs, and steams.    More info here: https://developer.mozilla.org/En/XMLHttpRequest/Using_XMLHttpRequest""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Switch Ti.Filesystem to use array buffers
Description: """"NOTE: This feature cannot be implemented until browsers start to support array buffers. Current supported browsers include: iOS 4+, Android 4+, IE 10+, FF4+. Right now, all binary files are treated as strings. We should switch to array buffers, which better aligns with Titanium's buffers, blobs, and steams. More info here: https://developer.mozilla.org/En/XMLHttpRequest/Using_XMLHttpRequest""""",title+description
