TIMOB-7784,12,"""Android: TableView shows only partial rows""","""""""If you create a view with 100% width, height, and have this view add top view and table, it will only show partial rows. I've created 50 rows in the code but when I scroll down t shows only 48 rows.  h4. Repro Steps   1. Run the below code.  2. Scroll down to the bottom only 48 rows are visible. There should be 50 rows.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView shows only partial rows
Description: """"If you create a view with 100% width, height, and have this view add top view and table, it will only show partial rows. I've created 50 rows in the code but when I scroll down t shows only 48 rows. h4. Repro Steps 1. Run the below code. 2. Scroll down to the bottom only 48 rows are visible. There should be 50 rows. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7783,12,"""Android: File.createTimestamp error message on resource files is unhelpful""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.5.0.91838a G2 (2.2)</p>  <p>1.Platform &gt; Filesystem<br>  2.check adb output</p>  <p>W/TiBaseFile( 9246): (kroll$15) [2,387126] Method is not  supported org.<USER>titanium.io.TiResourceFile :  createTimestamp</p></div>{html}    This issue (which has been logged twice before) created yet another panic in testing.    The error message here is utterly unhelpful. If someone tries out this method on a resource file, they get a """"""""method not supported"""""""" error. From an internal point of view, this makes complete sense--TiResourceFile is a separate class from TiFile. However, from a user point of view, they are both instances of Ti.Filesystem.File.     If we're going to log a message, it should provide some information which might be useful to the end user. If we cut and pasted Don's comment from the linked bug into the log message, """"""""Resource files don't have timestamps,"""""""" it would be a vast improvement on the current situation.       """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: File.createTimestamp error message on resource files is unhelpful
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.5.0.91838a G2 (2.2)</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; Filesystem<br> 2.check adb output</p> <p>W/TiBaseFile( 9246): (kroll$15) [2,387126] Method is not supported org.<USER>titanium.io.TiResourceFile : createTimestamp</p></div>{html} This issue (which has been logged twice before) created yet another panic in testing. The error message here is utterly unhelpful. If someone tries out this method on a resource file, they get a """"""""method not supported"""""""" error. From an internal point of view, this makes complete sense--TiResourceFile is a separate class from TiFile. However, from a user point of view, they are both instances of Ti.Filesystem.File. If we're going to log a message, it should provide some information which might be useful to the end user. If we cut and pasted Don's comment from the linked bug into the log message, """"""""Resource files don't have timestamps,"""""""" it would be a vast improvement on the current situation. """"",title+description
