TIMOB-7704,12,"""iOS: UI - SearchBar in Ti.UI.iPad.Popover shows incorrect barColor""","""""""h2. Problem    When I add a search bar to an iPad popover's title bar, the search bar does not match the popover's style. If I set the search bar's barColor to """"""""transparent"""""""", the barColor becomes black instead of transparent.    h2. Test case  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor(""""""""#FFF"""""""");  var window = Ti.UI.createWindow();    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({   height: 40,   title: """"""""Show popover"""""""",   width: 200  });    button.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function() {   var popover = Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover({    height: 500,    width: 200   });     var searchBar = Ti.UI.createSearchBar({    // barColor: """"""""transparent"""""""",    height: 30,    width: 130   });   popover.setLeftNavButton(searchBar);     popover.show({    view: button   });  });    window.add(button);  window.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI - SearchBar in Ti.UI.iPad.Popover shows incorrect barColor
Description: """"h2. Problem When I add a search bar to an iPad popover's title bar, the search bar does not match the popover's style. If I set the search bar's barColor to """"""""transparent"""""""", the barColor becomes black instead of transparent. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor(""""""""#FFF""""""""); var window = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ height: 40, title: """"""""Show popover"""""""", width: 200 }); button.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function() { var popover = Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover({ height: 500, width: 200 }); var searchBar = Ti.UI.createSearchBar({ // barColor: """"""""transparent"""""""", height: 30, width: 130 }); popover.setLeftNavButton(searchBar); popover.show({ view: button }); }); window.add(button); window.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-7703,12,"""Android: Tables: Rows created with anonymous objects randomly styled""","""""""User is creating a table with anonymous rows and applying style settings (font & color) to just one of the rows.    h3. Expected results    Only the explicitly styled row should be formatted.    h3: Actual results    Random rows are formatted. Additionally rows get randomly formatted as the table is scrolled or orientation changes. The problem doesn't exist when creating rows with explicit TableViewRow objects        This might be related to TIMOB-1193.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tables: Rows created with anonymous objects randomly styled
Description: """"User is creating a table with anonymous rows and applying style settings (font & color) to just one of the rows. h3. Expected results Only the explicitly styled row should be formatted. h3: Actual results Random rows are formatted. Additionally rows get randomly formatted as the table is scrolled or orientation changes. The problem doesn't exist when creating rows with explicit TableViewRow objects This might be related to TIMOB-1193.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7702,12,"""iOS: Snow Leopard: local module resources not generated in app package""","""""""Projects built in Snow Leopard that contain local modules do not contain module zip resources in the app package.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create a default app in Snow Leopard.  2. Add ti.bump-iphone-1.0.zip module to top level of project.  3. Deploy to device.  4. Open path: Titanium Studio Workspace/App/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/App.app.  5. Context click on app and Show Package Contents.      Expected Result:    Resource should exist: Titanium Studio Workspace/App/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/App.app/ti.bump-iphone-1.0.zip      Actual Result:    No zip resource exists. Only in Lion.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Snow Leopard: local module resources not generated in app package
Description: """"Projects built in Snow Leopard that contain local modules do not contain module zip resources in the app package. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a default app in Snow Leopard. 2. Add ti.bump-iphone-1.0.zip module to top level of project. 3. Deploy to device. 4. Open path: Titanium Studio Workspace/App/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/App.app. 5. Context click on app and Show Package Contents. Expected Result: Resource should exist: Titanium Studio Workspace/App/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/App.app/ti.bump-iphone-1.0.zip Actual Result: No zip resource exists. Only in Lion.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7701,12,"""IOS : camera- does not switch between front and back cameras correctly""","""""""after CAMERA_BACK is added to the switchCamera method, then CAMERA_FRONT is added to the swithCamera method,when you launch the app the back camera is activated instead of front camera    steps to reproduce:  1. Launch code in app.js:  {code:title=app.js}  var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'#000'  });    // create button, register the modified click callback, add button to window  function addButton(title, clickCallback)  {   var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title:title, width:'300', height:'50'});      button.addEventListener('click', function() {    Ti.Media.showCamera({mediaType:Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO});    clickCallback();    Ti.Media.vibrate();    });       window.add(button);  }    // camera with front specified after switching to back  // checks if switch function actually works, opposed to it being the default  addButton('Front Camera Test 2', function(){   Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_BACK);   Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_FRONT);  });    window.open();  {code}    2. tap on front camera test2  expected result   :  front camera should be active  Actual   result   :  Back camera is active    Note: it works as expected in 1.8.1""""""",Bug,"Title: IOS : camera- does not switch between front and back cameras correctly
Description: """"after CAMERA_BACK is added to the switchCamera method, then CAMERA_FRONT is added to the swithCamera method,when you launch the app the back camera is activated instead of front camera steps to reproduce: 1. Launch code in app.js: {code:title=app.js} var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#000' }); // create button, register the modified click callback, add button to window function addButton(title, clickCallback) { var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title:title, width:'300', height:'50'}); button.addEventListener('click', function() { Ti.Media.showCamera({mediaType:Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO}); clickCallback(); Ti.Media.vibrate(); }); window.add(button); } // camera with front specified after switching to back // checks if switch function actually works, opposed to it being the default addButton('Front Camera Test 2', function(){ Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_BACK); Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_FRONT); }); window.open(); {code} 2. tap on front camera test2 expected result : front camera should be active Actual result : Back camera is active Note: it works as expected in 1.8.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7699,12,"""Simple mobile app doesn't run with Mobile Web browser (Windows only)""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. create a starter mobile project from TiStudio (don't use any template).  2. Build and run it with mobile web browser.  3. Difference in source code (which is the cause of error):  http://pastie.org/private/vbgdbebqkr2f4ba92wqzoq""""""",Bug,"Title: Simple mobile app doesn't run with Mobile Web browser (Windows only)
