TIMOB-7685,12,"""Android: HW window: view does not show on 3.x devices""","""""""Sample code:      Steps to reproduce:  1. run the above sample code on 3.x devices.    Expected result:  There should be two views in the window: one is white and one is green.    Actual result:  There is only one green view showing in the window. The white view will show up after an orientation change.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HW window: view does not show on 3.x devices
Description: """"Sample code: Steps to reproduce: 1. run the above sample code on 3.x devices. Expected result: There should be two views in the window: one is white and one is green. Actual result: There is only one green view showing in the window. The white view will show up after an orientation change.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7684,12,"""iOS: Timing changes affect drawing""","""""""As a result of the fix for #1542, we had to change a lot of the timing of when events occur on the main thread. This causes some visual problems such as views animating in at odd times, windows """"""""popping"""""""" in/out of visibility while transitions in tab groups are occuring, animations not syncing, etc. It's difficult to describe the full behavior and reproduction steps. The easiest behavior to see is with Base UI->Standalone Window seeming to """"""""pop in"""""""".    Trying to regress against 1.8.1, 1.8.0.1 to see if the issue is present.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Timing changes affect drawing
Description: """"As a result of the fix for #1542, we had to change a lot of the timing of when events occur on the main thread. This causes some visual problems such as views animating in at odd times, windows """"""""popping"""""""" in/out of visibility while transitions in tab groups are occuring, animations not syncing, etc. It's difficult to describe the full behavior and reproduction steps. The easiest behavior to see is with Base UI->Standalone Window seeming to """"""""pop in"""""""". Trying to regress against 1.8.1, 1.8.0.1 to see if the issue is present.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7682,12,"""Android: """"timeout"""" property on HTTPClient should only set a connect timeout""","""""""Currently in iOS, the """"""""timeout"""""""" property only affects the socket connect, but in Android it affects both the socket connect and socket read. Removing the latter would improve our parity. We may also want to further investigate a """"""""soTimeout"""""""" property to keep the read timeout behavior.    Test Case:        Test Server:      * Run the attached test server  * Change """"""""some_existing_host"""""""" to your server's IP address, and run the app  * The app will connect to the server program, and no error will occurs during the connection (though an error will be rise after 10 seconds before the modification)""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: """"timeout"""" property on HTTPClient should only set a connect timeout
Description: """"Currently in iOS, the """"""""timeout"""""""" property only affects the socket connect, but in Android it affects both the socket connect and socket read. Removing the latter would improve our parity. We may also want to further investigate a """"""""soTimeout"""""""" property to keep the read timeout behavior. Test Case: Test Server: * Run the attached test server * Change """"""""some_existing_host"""""""" to your server's IP address, and run the app * The app will connect to the server program, and no error will occurs during the connection (though an error will be rise after 10 seconds before the modification)""""",title+description
TIMOB-7681,12,"""iOS: hires property not respected for remote imageviews""","""""""h2. Problem  remote imageviews with property hires set to true are displayed blurry, showing visible square pixels    h2. Steps to reproduce  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}    var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'win',      backgroundColor:'black'  });     var image = Ti.UI.createImageView({          """"""""width"""""""": 45,          """"""""height"""""""": 45,          """"""""hires"""""""": true,          """"""""image"""""""": """"""""http://cloud.rabble.se/images/offers/100_80_20110524154748.jpg""""""""      });    win1.add(image);    win1.open();  {code}    h2. Results  Attaching 2 screenshots displaying the image with 1.8.1 and 1.8.0.1      h2. Ticket  Customer ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-337519""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: hires property not respected for remote imageviews
Description: """"h2. Problem remote imageviews with property hires set to true are displayed blurry, showing visible square pixels h2. Steps to reproduce {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'win', backgroundColor:'black' }); var image = Ti.UI.createImageView({ """"""""width"""""""": 45, """"""""height"""""""": 45, """"""""hires"""""""": true, """"""""image"""""""": """"""""http://cloud.rabble.se/images/offers/100_80_20110524154748.jpg"""""""" }); win1.add(image); win1.open(); {code} h2. Results Attaching 2 screenshots displaying the image with 1.8.1 and 1.8.0.1 h2. Ticket Customer ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-337519""""",title+description
TIMOB-7680,12,"""iOS: iTunes_sync.scpt - Error reported when iTunes sync script launched during build with iPod connected to iTunes""","""""""Description:  While building some test projects, Studio reported the following:  [INFO] Performing clean build  [INFO] Installing application in iTunes ... one moment  [DEBUG] executing command: /Developer/Platforms/iPhoneOS.platform/Developer/usr/bin/PackageApplication /Users/<USER>Documents/fromGit/titanium_mobile_tests_internal/FeatureTest/OrientationModes/all/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/all.app  /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.2.v20120214163156/iphone/itunes_sync.scpt: execution error: Can't make name of 3 into type Unicode text. (-1700)  [INFO] iTunes sync initiated    The build seemed to complete, and the application was placed in iTunes as expected.    A quick check of the iTunes_sync.scpt shows a suspect line:  log """"""""The device """""""" & name of n & """""""" was unable to sync ("""""""" & errorStr & """""""":"""""""" & errorNumber & """""""")""""""""    When changing the line to include """"""""name of source n"""""""", the error went away. (Kudos to Blain for the suggestion)    Also, without the iPod hooked up, the error was not presented.      Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a sample project using Studio 1.0.9  2) Attach an iPod for use in testing  3) Build the project for device using SDK 1.8.2    Result:  Error reported in Studio    Expected:  No errors reported    Note:  This appears on the Q&A page as occurring as early as 1.7.1, so not marking as regression. Link:  http://developer.<USER>com/question/122993/error-while-moving-app-to-ios-device""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iTunes_sync.scpt - Error reported when iTunes sync script launched during build with iPod connected to iTunes
Description: """"Description: While building some test projects, Studio reported the following: [INFO] Performing clean build [INFO] Installing application in iTunes ... one moment [DEBUG] executing command: /Developer/Platforms/iPhoneOS.platform/Developer/usr/bin/PackageApplication /Users/<USER>Documents/fromGit/titanium_mobile_tests_internal/FeatureTest/OrientationModes/all/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphoneos/all.app /Users/<USER>Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.2.v20120214163156/iphone/itunes_sync.scpt: execution error: Can't make name of 3 into type Unicode text. (-1700) [INFO] iTunes sync initiated The build seemed to complete, and the application was placed in iTunes as expected. A quick check of the iTunes_sync.scpt shows a suspect line: log """"""""The device """""""" & name of n & """""""" was unable to sync ("""""""" & errorStr & """""""":"""""""" & errorNumber & """""""")"""""""" When changing the line to include """"""""name of source n"""""""", the error went away. (Kudos to Blain for the suggestion) Also, without the iPod hooked up, the error was not presented. Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a sample project using Studio 1.0.9 2) Attach an iPod for use in testing 3) Build the project for device using SDK 1.8.2 Result: Error reported in Studio Expected: No errors reported Note: This appears on the Q&A page as occurring as early as 1.7.1, so not marking as regression. Link: http://developer.<USER>com/question/122993/error-while-moving-app-to-ios-device""""",title+description
TIMOB-7679,12,"""iOS: popover - Rotating device 270 degrees with popover displayed causes rendering and location problems""","""""""Description:  When testing KitchenSink iPad, I clicked """"""""Show popover"""""""" to enable a popover, and while it was displayed, rotated the device 270 degrees. The popover became disjointed from the button. I repeated the test with the remaining two buttons and found the same problem. In the case of """"""""popover 1"""""""" the popover display also had some rendering problems resulting in its being unusable. See attached screenshots    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install Kitchensink iPad on device built with SDK 1.8.2  2) Click """"""""Open Main Tests"""""""" button  3) Click """"""""Popovers""""""""  4) Click """"""""Show popover 1""""""""  5) With the popover displayed, rotate the device 270 degrees    Result:  The popover may disappear. Continue to rotate the device in 90 degree increments and the popover should appear with rendering problems    Expected:  The popover remains usable and attached to the button that spawned it.    Note:  This also occurs in SDK 1.8.1  Repeat with other popovers for better illustration of the disjointed problem""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: popover - Rotating device 270 degrees with popover displayed causes rendering and location problems
Description: """"Description: When testing KitchenSink iPad, I clicked """"""""Show popover"""""""" to enable a popover, and while it was displayed, rotated the device 270 degrees. The popover became disjointed from the button. I repeated the test with the remaining two buttons and found the same problem. In the case of """"""""popover 1"""""""" the popover display also had some rendering problems resulting in its being unusable. See attached screenshots Steps to reproduce: 1) Install Kitchensink iPad on device built with SDK 1.8.2 2) Click """"""""Open Main Tests"""""""" button 3) Click """"""""Popovers"""""""" 4) Click """"""""Show popover 1"""""""" 5) With the popover displayed, rotate the device 270 degrees Result: The popover may disappear. Continue to rotate the device in 90 degree increments and the popover should appear with rendering problems Expected: The popover remains usable and attached to the button that spawned it. Note: This also occurs in SDK 1.8.1 Repeat with other popovers for better illustration of the disjointed problem""""",title+description
TIMOB-7678,12,"""Android: OptionDialog does not always not always open""","""""""h3. Problem Description  On Android (2.3, but reports of 2.2 also), using SDK 1.8+, OptionDialog behaviour seems to be erratic.    There seems to be two separate issues:    # Dialogs on our main screen open fine one first load, repeated opening and closing, however once you navigate away from that window, when you return, the dialogs no longer display  # App wide events which display dialogs open fine once, but sometimes not subsequently    Some code to replicate issue 1 is below. This bug occurs on both device and emulator. This does not occur with SDK < 1.8    h3. Actual results  option dialog not showing, and you get this in the log:  W/TiUIDialog(  386): (main) [2,8442] dialog activity is destroyed, unable to show dialog with message: null    h3. Expected Results  The option dialog showing always    h3. Test case  # Open app  # Click """"""""Open dialog"""""""", dialog opens  # Close dialog  # Click """"""""Open window"""""""", window 2 opens  # Go back to window 1  # Click """"""""Open dialog"""""""", dialog does not open  # If dialog opens, repeat steps 3-6 multiple times, dialog will fail within 2-3 repeats    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: OptionDialog does not always not always open
Description: """"h3. Problem Description On Android (2.3, but reports of 2.2 also), using SDK 1.8+, OptionDialog behaviour seems to be erratic. There seems to be two separate issues: # Dialogs on our main screen open fine one first load, repeated opening and closing, however once you navigate away from that window, when you return, the dialogs no longer display # App wide events which display dialogs open fine once, but sometimes not subsequently Some code to replicate issue 1 is below. This bug occurs on both device and emulator. This does not occur with SDK < 1.8 h3. Actual results option dialog not showing, and you get this in the log: W/TiUIDialog( 386): (main) [2,8442] dialog activity is destroyed, unable to show dialog with message: null h3. Expected Results The option dialog showing always h3. Test case # Open app # Click """"""""Open dialog"""""""", dialog opens # Close dialog # Click """"""""Open window"""""""", window 2 opens # Go back to window 1 # Click """"""""Open dialog"""""""", dialog does not open # If dialog opens, repeat steps 3-6 multiple times, dialog will fail within 2-3 repeats """"",title+description
TIMOB-7677,12,"""Android : Distribute - v8, rhino - After selecting to distribute a template in Ti Studio it fails with errors on Windows""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. In Ti Studio create a new project using a template (e.g. Single Window Application)  2. Select to distribute to the Android Marketplace    *Actual result:*  The following error is generated:  [ERROR] Error(s) compiling generated Java code  [ERROR] C:\Documents and Settings\Administrator\My Documents\Titanium Studio Workspace\singleAnd\build\android\gen\com\<USER>singleAnd\AssetCryptImpl.java:17: illegal escape character        assets.put(""""""""ui\ApplicationWindow.js"""""""", """"""""ZnVuY3Rpb24gQXBwbGljYXRpb25XaW5kb3coKXt2YXIgYT1yZXF1aXJlKCJ1aS9GaXJzdFZpZXciKSxiPVRpLlVJLmNyZWF0ZVdpbmRvdyh7YmFja2dyb3VuZENvbG9yOiIjZmZmZmZmIixuYXZCYXJIaWRkZW46ITAsZXhpdE9uQ2xvc2U6ITB9KSxhPW5ldyBhO2IuYWRkKGEpO3JldHVybiBifW1vZHVsZS5leHBvcnRzPUFwcGxpY2F0aW9uV2luZG93Owo="""""""");                       ^    C:\Documents and Settings\Administrator\My Documents\Titanium Studio Workspace\singleAnd\build\android\gen\com\<USER>singleAnd\AssetCryptImpl.java:18: illegal escape character    assets.put(""""""""ui\FirstView.js"""""""", """""""""""""""");                   ^    2 errors    *Expected result:*  Application is built without error    *Note this doesn't occur with a hello world app*  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android : Distribute - v8, rhino - After selecting to distribute a template in Ti Studio it fails with errors on Windows
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. In Ti Studio create a new project using a template (e.g. Single Window Application) 2. Select to distribute to the Android Marketplace *Actual result:* The following error is generated: [ERROR] Error(s) compiling generated Java code [ERROR] C:\Documents and Settings\Administrator\My Documents\Titanium Studio Workspace\singleAnd\build\android\gen\com\<USER>singleAnd\AssetCryptImpl.java:17: illegal escape character assets.put(""""""""ui\ApplicationWindow.js"""""""", """"""""ZnVuY3Rpb24gQXBwbGljYXRpb25XaW5kb3coKXt2YXIgYT1yZXF1aXJlKCJ1aS9GaXJzdFZpZXciKSxiPVRpLlVJLmNyZWF0ZVdpbmRvdyh7YmFja2dyb3VuZENvbG9yOiIjZmZmZmZmIixuYXZCYXJIaWRkZW46ITAsZXhpdE9uQ2xvc2U6ITB9KSxhPW5ldyBhO2IuYWRkKGEpO3JldHVybiBifW1vZHVsZS5leHBvcnRzPUFwcGxpY2F0aW9uV2luZG93Owo=""""""""); ^ C:\Documents and Settings\Administrator\My Documents\Titanium Studio Workspace\singleAnd\build\android\gen\com\<USER>singleAnd\AssetCryptImpl.java:18: illegal escape character assets.put(""""""""ui\FirstView.js"""""""", """"""""""""""""); ^ 2 errors *Expected result:* Application is built without error *Note this doesn't occur with a hello world app* """"",title+description
TIMOB-7676,12,"""Android: ImageViews cause app to unexpectedly crash""","""""""*The code*  Attached with this project (includes sample images).    *The issue*  The issue is if you toggle the buttons back and forth, it restarts the app. On my device, you have to tap 2 red buttons before it crashes.    *Expected behavior*  The app should be toggling the two buttons without crashing. There should only be one white and one red imageView at any one time.    *Notes*  The white image means the 'button' (which is an imageView) is currently pressed down. The red image means it is currently not selected.    *Android*  TiSDK 1.9.0.v20120209110134 (custom SDK build from Hieu https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7615)""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageViews cause app to unexpectedly crash
Description: """"*The code* Attached with this project (includes sample images). *The issue* The issue is if you toggle the buttons back and forth, it restarts the app. On my device, you have to tap 2 red buttons before it crashes. *Expected behavior* The app should be toggling the two buttons without crashing. There should only be one white and one red imageView at any one time. *Notes* The white image means the 'button' (which is an imageView) is currently pressed down. The red image means it is currently not selected. *Android* TiSDK 1.9.0.v20120209110134 (custom SDK build from Hieu https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7615)""""",title+description
TIMOB-7675,12,"""Parent window size incorrect during open event in iOS""","""""""1. Launch the sample app in the iOS simulator  2. Rotate the window 90 degrees right  3. Rotate the window 90 degrees left  4. Examine the console output:  [INFO] CONSTRUCTION Parent Window Size (w:320 h: 460)  [INFO] OPEN EVENT Parent Window Size (w:320 h: 416)  [INFO] ORIENTATION CHANGE Parent Window Size (w:480 h: 300)  [INFO] ORIENTATION CHANGE Parent Window Size (w:320 h: 460)    EXPECTED: All window sizes should be the same (accounting for orientation)  ACTUAL: During the open event the window height is smaller by 44 pixels (navbar?)""""""",Bug,"Title: Parent window size incorrect during open event in iOS
Description: """"1. Launch the sample app in the iOS simulator 2. Rotate the window 90 degrees right 3. Rotate the window 90 degrees left 4. Examine the console output: [INFO] CONSTRUCTION Parent Window Size (w:320 h: 460) [INFO] OPEN EVENT Parent Window Size (w:320 h: 416) [INFO] ORIENTATION CHANGE Parent Window Size (w:480 h: 300) [INFO] ORIENTATION CHANGE Parent Window Size (w:320 h: 460) EXPECTED: All window sizes should be the same (accounting for orientation) ACTUAL: During the open event the window height is smaller by 44 pixels (navbar?)""""",title+description
TIMOB-7674,12,"""iOS: CFBundleShortVersionString not set correctly""","""""""actual: putting <version>2</version> in tiapp.xml generates the following xcode project properties:        <key>CFBundleVersion</key>      <string>2</string>      <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>      <string>1.0</string>    expected: allow additional setting for short version in tiapp.xml""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: CFBundleShortVersionString not set correctly
Description: """"actual: putting <version>2</version> in tiapp.xml generates the following xcode project properties: <key>CFBundleVersion</key> <string>2</string> <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key> <string>1.0</string> expected: allow additional setting for short version in tiapp.xml""""",title+description
TIMOB-7673,12,"""Ti API: """"replaceAt"""", """"insertAt"""", and """"getAt"""" functionality for view-like UI components""","""""""h2. Problem    In dynamic scenarios, we often need to add view components at specific positions in parent view container. For example, if parent view container has 3 child view components, we may want to add view at first position (""""""""add"""""""" always adds at the end).      Currently, this is not possible to do natively in Titanium, but it's very useful feature which Titanium should have supported natively.    h2. Workaround    As a workaround, this approach can be used: https://gist.github.com/1485751      It works fine for small number of child elements, but for large number of child elements there could be performance drop.    h2. Solution    Implement those functionality for all view-like components (for those components that can contain other components). I suggest following syntax:    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: """"replaceAt"""", """"insertAt"""", and """"getAt"""" functionality for view-like UI components
Description: """"h2. Problem In dynamic scenarios, we often need to add view components at specific positions in parent view container. For example, if parent view container has 3 child view components, we may want to add view at first position (""""""""add"""""""" always adds at the end). Currently, this is not possible to do natively in Titanium, but it's very useful feature which Titanium should have supported natively. h2. Workaround As a workaround, this approach can be used: https://gist.github.com/1485751 It works fine for small number of child elements, but for large number of child elements there could be performance drop. h2. Solution Implement those functionality for all view-like components (for those components that can contain other components). I suggest following syntax: """"",title+description
TIMOB-7672,12,"""MobileWeb: Check for resources in Resources/mobileweb directory first""","""""""When resources (images or code) are being loaded, we need to check for the resource in the Resources/mobileweb directory first, then the Resources folder.  This will either require serializing the complete directory structure at compile time (not a great option) or polling the server prior to pull the file (also not a great option).  The better solution would be to have the AST parser do the heavy lifting, but the AST parser is a ways out.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Check for resources in Resources/mobileweb directory first
Description: """"When resources (images or code) are being loaded, we need to check for the resource in the Resources/mobileweb directory first, then the Resources folder. This will either require serializing the complete directory structure at compile time (not a great option) or polling the server prior to pull the file (also not a great option). The better solution would be to have the AST parser do the heavy lifting, but the AST parser is a ways out.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7671,12,"""Refactor all view-like UI components so they share common API""","""""""h2. Problem    There is common problem with Titanium API method names. For example, TableView component has """"""""add"""""""" method which does ... nothing. That leads to confusion because it is intuitive to use """"""""add"""""""" method to add table view rows (especially after View and ScrollView usage).    h2. Solution    To make things simple, I suggest that all view-like UI components use same method names. Therefore:    * TableView  ** """"""""add"""""""" method should accept row or section components.        (mixture of what """"""""add"""""""" accepts as argument is made because I find it more flexible)      To make user confusion even bigger, """"""""TableViewSection"""""""" supports """"""""add"""""""" method:        (TableViewRow also, since it's a view)    So, why to have """"""""TableView"""""""" different (even this can be implemented: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-640 )?        * TabGroup  ** """"""""add"""""""" should support adding """"""""Tab"""""""" (what """"""""addTab"""""""" now does)    * PickerColumn  ** """"""""add"""""""" should do what """"""""addRow"""""""" does    * ScrollableView  ** """"""""add"""""""" should do what """"""""addView"""""""" does        I hope I didn't miss something. :)          http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KISS_principle""""""",New Feature,"Title: Refactor all view-like UI components so they share common API
Description: """"h2. Problem There is common problem with Titanium API method names. For example, TableView component has """"""""add"""""""" method which does ... nothing. That leads to confusion because it is intuitive to use """"""""add"""""""" method to add table view rows (especially after View and ScrollView usage). h2. Solution To make things simple, I suggest that all view-like UI components use same method names. Therefore: * TableView ** """"""""add"""""""" method should accept row or section components. (mixture of what """"""""add"""""""" accepts as argument is made because I find it more flexible) To make user confusion even bigger, """"""""TableViewSection"""""""" supports """"""""add"""""""" method: (TableViewRow also, since it's a view) So, why to have """"""""TableView"""""""" different (even this can be implemented: https://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-640 )? * TabGroup ** """"""""add"""""""" should support adding """"""""Tab"""""""" (what """"""""addTab"""""""" now does) * PickerColumn ** """"""""add"""""""" should do what """"""""addRow"""""""" does * ScrollableView ** """"""""add"""""""" should do what """"""""addView"""""""" does I hope I didn't miss something. :) http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KISS_principle""""",title+description
TIMOB-7670,12,"""VLC module wrapper for Titanium Mobile""","""""""Is it possible to add VLC to the contributed modules so it's accessible through Titanium Mobile? This would probably expand the codec's you could use when playing videos & make it so you could embed a video in an app on android not just iOS.    IOS: http://git.videolan.org/?p=MobileVLC.git;a=summary    Android: http://git.videolan.org/?p=vlc-ports/android.git;a=summary    Not so much a question as a feature request I suppose. Please remove or answer with the proper place to ask feature requests.""""""",New Feature,"Title: VLC module wrapper for Titanium Mobile
Description: """"Is it possible to add VLC to the contributed modules so it's accessible through Titanium Mobile? This would probably expand the codec's you could use when playing videos & make it so you could embed a video in an app on android not just iOS. IOS: http://git.videolan.org/?p=MobileVLC.git;a=summary Android: http://git.videolan.org/?p=vlc-ports/android.git;a=summary Not so much a question as a feature request I suppose. Please remove or answer with the proper place to ask feature requests.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7669,12,"""Provide Error Message if JSON.parse() fails""","""""""h4. Feature proposal    Would it be possible to attach a callback to JSON.parse for error handling? Currently only a try{}catch(){} is working.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Provide Error Message if JSON.parse() fails
Description: """"h4. Feature proposal Would it be possible to attach a callback to JSON.parse for error handling? Currently only a try{}catch(){} is working. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7668,12,"""iOS: Facebook - login in with dialog produces (NSURLErrorDomain error -999.) error""","""""""Logging into facebook using the facebook dialog causes this error """"""""The operation couldn't be completed. (NSURLErrorDomain error -999.)"""""""".    h4. Steps to reproduce:  Step 1: run the code below  Step 2: click on the window  Step 3: enter your facebook creds and hit Login  Step 4: notice that the dialog closes  Step 5: check the console and see the error below  {code:title=console}  {""""""""type"""""""":""""""""result"""""""",""""""""source"""""""":{},""""""""error"""""""":""""""""The operation couldn't be completed. (NSURLErrorDomain error -999.)"""""""",""""""""success"""""""":false,""""""""cancelled"""""""":false}  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Facebook - login in with dialog produces (NSURLErrorDomain error -999.) error
Description: """"Logging into facebook using the facebook dialog causes this error """"""""The operation couldn't be completed. (NSURLErrorDomain error -999.)"""""""". h4. Steps to reproduce: Step 1: run the code below Step 2: click on the window Step 3: enter your facebook creds and hit Login Step 4: notice that the dialog closes Step 5: check the console and see the error below {code:title=console} {""""""""type"""""""":""""""""result"""""""",""""""""source"""""""":{},""""""""error"""""""":""""""""The operation couldn't be completed. (NSURLErrorDomain error -999.)"""""""",""""""""success"""""""":false,""""""""cancelled"""""""":false} """"",title+description
TIMOB-7667,12,"""On mapview, blinking rounded indicator disappeared when change tab""","""""""h4. Problem description   I have a map view and a function for geolocalization.  The function works great: my map is centered in the user location and a blinking rounded indicator appears on the position.  The problem occurs when I change tab and I then go back in the tab with the map: the geolocalization works again but the blinking rounded indicator is disappeared!    h4. Actual Results  The current user's location disappears.    h4. Expected results  The current user's location is shown.     h4. Test case  1. Add this code to a project    Wait until the map shows the user's location.  Change tab  Go back to map's tab  The current user's location disappear.       """"""",Bug,"Title: On mapview, blinking rounded indicator disappeared when change tab
Description: """"h4. Problem description I have a map view and a function for geolocalization. The function works great: my map is centered in the user location and a blinking rounded indicator appears on the position. The problem occurs when I change tab and I then go back in the tab with the map: the geolocalization works again but the blinking rounded indicator is disappeared! h4. Actual Results The current user's location disappears. h4. Expected results The current user's location is shown. h4. Test case 1. Add this code to a project Wait until the map shows the user's location. Change tab Go back to map's tab The current user's location disappear. """"",title+description
