TIMOB-7547,12,"""iOS: Webview should be able to handle events even if the parent view defines some events as well (Parity issue)""","""""""h4. Problem Description  Customer wants to have a webview as part of the UI in a tablet. That webview will be showing interactive stuff, so you can actually interact with it. That webview is being added on top of a view with attached events.     h4. Expected Results  Being able to interact with the webview, even if the parent view has related events. This is, If I'm clicking on the webview, the webview should work as usual, and if I click outside the webview, the parent view should do the     h4. Actual Results  In Android, this works just fine. In iOS, the webview is blocked to any activity.     h4. Test Case        h4. Extra info   For the customer would be handy if we can set a way to tell the webview to not pass events to the parent, and continue handling it's own events. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Webview should be able to handle events even if the parent view defines some events as well (Parity issue)
Description: """"h4. Problem Description Customer wants to have a webview as part of the UI in a tablet. That webview will be showing interactive stuff, so you can actually interact with it. That webview is being added on top of a view with attached events. h4. Expected Results Being able to interact with the webview, even if the parent view has related events. This is, If I'm clicking on the webview, the webview should work as usual, and if I click outside the webview, the parent view should do the h4. Actual Results In Android, this works just fine. In iOS, the webview is blocked to any activity. h4. Test Case h4. Extra info For the customer would be handy if we can set a way to tell the webview to not pass events to the parent, and continue handling it's own events. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7546,12,"""MobileWeb: Properly set HttpClient responseData property""","""""""HttpClient's responseData property should be set to the """"""""responseText"""""""" value, not the responseHeader.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Properly set HttpClient responseData property
Description: """"HttpClient's responseData property should be set to the """"""""responseText"""""""" value, not the responseHeader.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7545,12,"""Android: ant clean does not work in windows when building titanium mobile sdk""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Inside the titanium_mobile\android directory, run 'ant clean'    ant clean does not currently work when building titanium mobile sdk in windows.  There is currently a work around for this issue by running 'git clean -fxd' instead.  More investigation needs to be done, but it seems related to the android ndk r7 (which has experimental components in windows).""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ant clean does not work in windows when building titanium mobile sdk
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Inside the titanium_mobile\android directory, run 'ant clean' ant clean does not currently work when building titanium mobile sdk in windows. There is currently a work around for this issue by running 'git clean -fxd' instead. More investigation needs to be done, but it seems related to the android ndk r7 (which has experimental components in windows).""""",title+description
TIMOB-7544,12,"""Tooling: validate.py should generate errors for unsupported YAML keys""","""""""If we insert an invalid keyword in the YAML markup, it's silently ignored. This includes errors such as:    - misspelling """"""""description"""""""" as """"""""desciption""""""""  - including fields that aren't defined in the TDoc spec, such as """"""""note""""""""  - leaving the s off the end of """"""""platforms:""""""""    All of these fail silently in both validate and docgen, so the information is omitted from the docs without warning.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: validate.py should generate errors for unsupported YAML keys
Description: """"If we insert an invalid keyword in the YAML markup, it's silently ignored. This includes errors such as: - misspelling """"""""description"""""""" as """"""""desciption"""""""" - including fields that aren't defined in the TDoc spec, such as """"""""note"""""""" - leaving the s off the end of """"""""platforms:"""""""" All of these fail silently in both validate and docgen, so the information is omitted from the docs without warning.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7543,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Media.VideoPlayer positioning overriding default UI element positioning""","""""""The VideoPlayer is explicitly set to position:relative which overrides the position:absolute set by TiUIElement.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Media.VideoPlayer positioning overriding default UI element positioning
Description: """"The VideoPlayer is explicitly set to position:relative which overrides the position:absolute set by TiUIElement.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7542,12,"""MobileWeb: View children not properly being destroyed""","""""""When a view is destroyed, it loops through its children, destroys them, then sets the child to null. The problem is it needs to splice() out the child instead of setting it to null otherwise you'll have conflicts where a nested destroy() will try to <USER>the array of children where children are null.  Simply removing the children from the array fixes it.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: View children not properly being destroyed
Description: """"When a view is destroyed, it loops through its children, destroys them, then sets the child to null. The problem is it needs to splice() out the child instead of setting it to null otherwise you'll have conflicts where a nested destroy() will try to <USER>the array of children where children are null. Simply removing the children from the array fixes it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7541,12,"""MobileWeb: Remove dependency on PIL and replace with a Java utility""","""""""Mobile web's compile <USER>currently depends on PIL. This means we need to distribute PIL, but PIL relies on a C compiler. This over complicates the compile <USER>and distribution.    The image resizing that PIL is used for needs to be replaced with a command line Java app with the following signature:    {code:title=Signature}  resize <source> <dest> <width> <height>      The app needs to be able to read in jpg, gif, and png files, and generate png files and perhaps jpg.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Remove dependency on PIL and replace with a Java utility
Description: """"Mobile web's compile <USER>currently depends on PIL. This means we need to distribute PIL, but PIL relies on a C compiler. This over complicates the compile <USER>and distribution. The image resizing that PIL is used for needs to be replaced with a command line Java app with the following signature: {code:title=Signature} resize <source> <dest> <width> <height> The app needs to be able to read in jpg, gif, and png files, and generate png files and perhaps jpg.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7540,12,"""iOS: Titanium.UI.Label: click event fails to fire""","""""""iOS: Titanium.UI.Label: click event fails to fire. Regression. Works in 1.7.5. Works on Android.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code.    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'white',   layout:'vertical'   });     var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({   text:'Click Label',   color:'black',   height:'auto',   width:'auto'   });    win.add(label);  win.open();    label.addEventListener('click',function(){   Ti.API.info('Label Clicked');   label.text = 'Label Clicked';  });  {code}    2. Click label.    Expected Result:    Label text should change to 'Label Clicked', and  'Label Clicked' should print to the console.    Actual Result:    Nothing happens.    Note: Will investigate more hardware in future.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.UI.Label: click event fails to fire
Description: """"iOS: Titanium.UI.Label: click event fails to fire. Regression. Works in 1.7.5. Works on Android. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'white', layout:'vertical' }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text:'Click Label', color:'black', height:'auto', width:'auto' }); win.add(label); win.open(); label.addEventListener('click',function(){ Ti.API.info('Label Clicked'); label.text = 'Label Clicked'; }); {code} 2. Click label. Expected Result: Label text should change to 'Label Clicked', and 'Label Clicked' should print to the console. Actual Result: Nothing happens. Note: Will investigate more hardware in future.""""",title+description
