TIMOB-7474,12,"""Android: Support selecting what ABI to target when using V8 runtime.""","""""""Allow developer to specify in tiapp.xml which ABI to support when using V8 runtime.  Currently we always bundle both ABI versions of the native library. If the developer only wishes  to support one ABI version to cut down size of the APK they may choose to do so.    http://developer.<USER>com/question/131313/why-are-both-rhino-and-v8-bundled-in-the-apk""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support selecting what ABI to target when using V8 runtime.
Description: """"Allow developer to specify in tiapp.xml which ABI to support when using V8 runtime. Currently we always bundle both ABI versions of the native library. If the developer only wishes to support one ABI version to cut down size of the APK they may choose to do so. http://developer.<USER>com/question/131313/why-are-both-rhino-and-v8-bundled-in-the-apk""""",title+description
TIMOB-7473,12,"""Android: Add Shadow (based on png image pattern) to a View ""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer wants to get views with a smooth drop shadow. Customer wants to add a png image with a pattern, so that one will appear under the view.    h4. EXTRA INFO   Right now, they are using a workaround similar to this one:         Instead of adding the container and the shadow, customer wants to have a special view with where you can set the png for the shadow, and a size for it.     The goal is having something like the attachment, but with any png. """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add Shadow (based on png image pattern) to a View
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer wants to get views with a smooth drop shadow. Customer wants to add a png image with a pattern, so that one will appear under the view. h4. EXTRA INFO Right now, they are using a workaround similar to this one: Instead of adding the container and the shadow, customer wants to have a special view with where you can set the png for the shadow, and a size for it. The goal is having something like the attachment, but with any png. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7472,12,"""Android: APK includes both Javascript runtimes libraries regardless of the chose runtime""","""""""It looks like we're including both the Rhino js.jar (via classes.dex) and the 2 V8 ABI-specific shared libraries (libkroll-v8.so, libstlport_shared.so) regardless of which runtime was chosen for the application in the tiapp.xml. We should only bundle the runtime that is given by the `ti.android.runtime` property in the tiapp.xml, or only bundle V8 by default.    For V8 we should still be bundling both ABI-specific variations of the libraries in `armeabi` and `armeabi-v7a` folders.    Q&A issue:  http://developer.<USER>com/question/131313/why-are-both-rhino-and-v8-bundled-in-the-apk""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: APK includes both Javascript runtimes libraries regardless of the chose runtime
Description: """"It looks like we're including both the Rhino js.jar (via classes.dex) and the 2 V8 ABI-specific shared libraries (libkroll-v8.so, libstlport_shared.so) regardless of which runtime was chosen for the application in the tiapp.xml. We should only bundle the runtime that is given by the `ti.android.runtime` property in the tiapp.xml, or only bundle V8 by default. For V8 we should still be bundling both ABI-specific variations of the libraries in `armeabi` and `armeabi-v7a` folders. Q&A issue: http://developer.<USER>com/question/131313/why-are-both-rhino-and-v8-bundled-in-the-apk""""",title+description
TIMOB-7471,12,"""Enable Vacuum - SQL command""","""""""Feature request to include Vacuum , a SQL command to rebuild database. Used to free memory space and resize the database size. Used to clear out deleted records.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Enable Vacuum - SQL command
Description: """"Feature request to include Vacuum , a SQL command to rebuild database. Used to free memory space and resize the database size. Used to clear out deleted records. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7470,12,"""iOS: Set TLS version for imageview""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer addressed an XHR issue we had using SSL on iOS5 against our test server. iOS5 uses TLS v1.2 by default and our server fails to negotiate v1.2. They used this:    http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.tlsVersion-property.html    and worked fine. The only issue is that they are getting images from the secure server with iOS5, will fail.     h4. EXPECTED BEHAVIOR  The TLS configuration impacting the imageview url     h4. ACTUAL BEHAVIOR  The image is failing to download in iOS5    h4. TEST CASE      h4. TEAMWORK DISCUSSION  https://<USER>teamworkpm.net/tasks/524931    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Set TLS version for imageview
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer addressed an XHR issue we had using SSL on iOS5 against our test server. iOS5 uses TLS v1.2 by default and our server fails to negotiate v1.2. They used this: http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.tlsVersion-property.html and worked fine. The only issue is that they are getting images from the secure server with iOS5, will fail. h4. EXPECTED BEHAVIOR The TLS configuration impacting the imageview url h4. ACTUAL BEHAVIOR The image is failing to download in iOS5 h4. TEST CASE h4. TEAMWORK DISCUSSION https://<USER>teamworkpm.net/tasks/524931 """"",title+description
TIMOB-7468,12,"""Android: tooling - Rhino/V8 - On windows systems during emulator build, console reports error attempting to kill emulator process""","""""""Description:  When buiding for Andorid emulator on Windows systems, the console will report the following:  [DEBUG] calling emulator kill on 2924  ERROR: The <USER>""""""""2924"""""""" not found.    The <USER>ID will vary, and there seems to be no visible effect on the emulator launch.     Steps to reproduce:  1) Launch Studio 1.0.8  2) Using a new or existing project in Studio, build for emulator  3) Watch the console output during the build    Result:  Console reports error    Expected:  No error reported    Notes:  This also occurs in 1.8.0.1""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: tooling - Rhino/V8 - On windows systems during emulator build, console reports error attempting to kill emulator process
Description: """"Description: When buiding for Andorid emulator on Windows systems, the console will report the following: [DEBUG] calling emulator kill on 2924 ERROR: The <USER>""""""""2924"""""""" not found. The <USER>ID will vary, and there seems to be no visible effect on the emulator launch. Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch Studio 1.0.8 2) Using a new or existing project in Studio, build for emulator 3) Watch the console output during the build Result: Console reports error Expected: No error reported Notes: This also occurs in 1.8.0.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7466,12,"""Android: Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer: video doesn't show paused image when player paused and brought from foreground in 2.2 and 2.3""","""""""In Android 2.2 and 2.3, when a video player is paused and brought from the foreground, the paused image of the video does not show (only black). The paused image does show in 3.1 and 4.0.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run timob6210.rar project attached.  2. Wait for video to load.  3. Press play.  4. Press pause.  5. Press 'home' to background the app.  6. Relaunch the app.    Expected Result:    Video still should be visible.    Actual Result:    Black screen (but app is still properly paused at the correct video time).    Note: Test exists in titanium_mobile_tests_internal\FeatureTest\Media\timob6210""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer: video doesn't show paused image when player paused and brought from foreground in 2.2 and 2.3
Description: """"In Android 2.2 and 2.3, when a video player is paused and brought from the foreground, the paused image of the video does not show (only black). The paused image does show in 3.1 and 4.0. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run timob6210.rar project attached. 2. Wait for video to load. 3. Press play. 4. Press pause. 5. Press 'home' to background the app. 6. Relaunch the app. Expected Result: Video still should be visible. Actual Result: Black screen (but app is still properly paused at the correct video time). Note: Test exists in titanium_mobile_tests_internal\FeatureTest\Media\timob6210""""",title+description
TIMOB-7464,12,"""Android: UI.PickerColumn - make rows property read-only""","""""""h2. Problem    The [Titanium.UI.PickerColumn.rows|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.PickerColumn.rows-property.html] property on Android is supposed to be read-only, as with iOS, but currently the developer is able to change it. Hence, this is a parity request.    See [PickerColumnProxy.java|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/PickerColumnProxy.java#L179].    h2. Discussion    See Allen's comment in [this pull request|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1269/files#r394074].""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: UI.PickerColumn - make rows property read-only
Description: """"h2. Problem The [Titanium.UI.PickerColumn.rows|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.PickerColumn.rows-property.html] property on Android is supposed to be read-only, as with iOS, but currently the developer is able to change it. Hence, this is a parity request. See [PickerColumnProxy.java|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/ui/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/ui/PickerColumnProxy.java#L179]. h2. Discussion See Allen's comment in [this pull request|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1269/files#r394074].""""",title+description
TIMOB-7463,12,"""MobileWeb: Split CalculateSize into two methods for layout and animations.""","""""""Right now, animations and call CalculateSize to convert the coordinates into ones that are layout-compatible. This call actually causes some controls to be re-layed out. While it doesn't cause any visual artifacting, it is inefficient. The method should be split into two versions that are each optimized for layout and animation.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Split CalculateSize into two methods for layout and animations.
Description: """"Right now, animations and call CalculateSize to convert the coordinates into ones that are layout-compatible. This call actually causes some controls to be re-layed out. While it doesn't cause any visual artifacting, it is inefficient. The method should be split into two versions that are each optimized for layout and animation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7462,12,"""MobileWeb: Default app fails to load with facebook loading message in Linux Firefox""","""""""Default app fails to run after first deployment, page reload fixes issue. Page stalls with: 'Read connect.facebook.net' message.  Occurs in Linux Firefox. Did not occur in 1.8.0.1.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create new project in Linux.  2. Deploy to mobileweb.  3. Deploy a second time.    Expected Result:    App should load.    Actual Result:    App fails to load with message.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Default app fails to load with facebook loading message in Linux Firefox
Description: """"Default app fails to run after first deployment, page reload fixes issue. Page stalls with: 'Read connect.facebook.net' message. Occurs in Linux Firefox. Did not occur in 1.8.0.1. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create new project in Linux. 2. Deploy to mobileweb. 3. Deploy a second time. Expected Result: App should load. Actual Result: App fails to load with message.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7461,12,"""Mobile Web : Tab Group - When launching a default two tab application to preview in emulator, one cannot switch back and forth between the two tabs""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a new default two tab mobile application  2. From Studio select the run option 'Mobile Web Preview in Emulator'  3. Attempt to switch between tab 1 and tab 2    Actual Result:  One is not able to switch between the tabs    Expected result:  One is able to switch between tabs""""""",Bug,"Title: Mobile Web : Tab Group - When launching a default two tab application to preview in emulator, one cannot switch back and forth between the two tabs
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a new default two tab mobile application 2. From Studio select the run option 'Mobile Web Preview in Emulator' 3. Attempt to switch between tab 1 and tab 2 Actual Result: One is not able to switch between the tabs Expected result: One is able to switch between tabs""""",title+description
TIMOB-7459,12,"""iOS: Add Shadow (based on png image pattern) to a View ""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer wants to get views with a smooth drop shadow. Customer wants to add a png image with a pattern, so that one will appear under the view.    h4. EXTRA INFO   Right now, they are using a workaround similar to this one:         Instead of adding the container and the shadow, customer wants to have a special view with where you can set the png for the shadow, and a size for it.     The goal is having something like the attachment, but with any png. """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add Shadow (based on png image pattern) to a View
