TIMOB-7394,12,"""Android: Drillbit:  JSS drillbit test fails under Rhino""","""""""Drillbit test for JSS fails under Rhino with the following error:    should be: """"""""red"""""""", was: """"""""undefined""""""""  at the line: valueOf(test.backgroundColor).shouldBe(""""""""red"""""""");""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Drillbit: JSS drillbit test fails under Rhino
Description: """"Drillbit test for JSS fails under Rhino with the following error: should be: """"""""red"""""""", was: """"""""undefined"""""""" at the line: valueOf(test.backgroundColor).shouldBe(""""""""red"""""""");""""",title+description
TIMOB-7390,12,"""iOS: AudioPlayer.bitRate returns very large number""","""""""While streaming an MP3 from the internet, audioPlayer.bitRate returns 4292870144.    Yes, 4.29 billion bits per second. No wonder the network is slow. I think this is a bad cast.    In AudioStreamer, we have:        UInt32 bitRate;             // Bits per second in the file    And in TiMediaAudioPlayerProxy.m, we have:    PLAYER_PROP_DOUBLE(bitRate,bitRate);      """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: AudioPlayer.bitRate returns very large number
Description: """"While streaming an MP3 from the internet, audioPlayer.bitRate returns 4292870144. Yes, 4.29 billion bits per second. No wonder the network is slow. I think this is a bad cast. In AudioStreamer, we have: UInt32 bitRate; // Bits per second in the file And in TiMediaAudioPlayerProxy.m, we have: PLAYER_PROP_DOUBLE(bitRate,bitRate); """"",title+description
TIMOB-7389,12,"""iOS: Content Assist - Content Assist does not work""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Create default Titanium project  2. In app.js, type Ti.    Actual: Nothing appears.  Expected: Pop over dialog should appear that has access to different API classes.    Note: Content Assist works in 1.8.0.1 and 1.9.0.v20120115231633 (1/16/12 Weekly Regression Pass)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Content Assist - Content Assist does not work
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Create default Titanium project 2. In app.js, type Ti. Actual: Nothing appears. Expected: Pop over dialog should appear that has access to different API classes. Note: Content Assist works in 1.8.0.1 and 1.9.0.v20120115231633 (1/16/12 Weekly Regression Pass)""""",title+description
TIMOB-7388,12,"""iOS: splitView - Rotating iPad with modal window displayed causes UI rendering problems""","""""""Description:  In KitchenSink iPad, while exercising the """"""""Split View"""""""" test, I opened the modal window with """"""""Show Modal"""""""" and then rotated the device from Portrait to upside-portrait. When I dismissed the modal, the UI was compressed and the status bar was on the side as if in landscape mode. See screenshot.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS iPad on iPad device  2) Launch KS iPad and choose """"""""Split View - Plain""""""""  3) hold iPad in portrait mode and press """"""""Show Modal""""""""  4) With the modal up, rotate the device 180 to upside-portrait  5) Dismiss the modal with """"""""Dismiss modal""""""""    Result:  UI does not fill screen, and status bar on side of screen as if in landscape mode.    Note:   This also occurs with 1.8.0.1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: splitView - Rotating iPad with modal window displayed causes UI rendering problems
Description: """"Description: In KitchenSink iPad, while exercising the """"""""Split View"""""""" test, I opened the modal window with """"""""Show Modal"""""""" and then rotated the device from Portrait to upside-portrait. When I dismissed the modal, the UI was compressed and the status bar was on the side as if in landscape mode. See screenshot. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS iPad on iPad device 2) Launch KS iPad and choose """"""""Split View - Plain"""""""" 3) hold iPad in portrait mode and press """"""""Show Modal"""""""" 4) With the modal up, rotate the device 180 to upside-portrait 5) Dismiss the modal with """"""""Dismiss modal"""""""" Result: UI does not fill screen, and status bar on side of screen as if in landscape mode. Note: This also occurs with 1.8.0.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7367,12,"""iOS: optionsDialog - Rotating iPad with options dialog up causes rendering problems""","""""""Description:  In KitchenSink iPad, while testing the """"""""Main Tests -> Option Dialogs"""""""" I selected Dialog 1 and rotated the device with the option dialog displayed. While rotating, I noted two behaviors. The more common was a detaching of the Option dialog from the button that spawned it. Less common was a black non-functional options dialog. See screen shots.    It was easiest to reproduce by rotating the device 270 degrees or more.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS iPad on iPad device  2) Launch KS iPad and choose """"""""main tests""""""""  3) Select options dialog  4) With the dialog up, rotate the device.    Result:  Frequent rendering of the options dialog in random screen locations, occasional black options dialog.    Note:   This also occurs with 1.8.0.1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: optionsDialog - Rotating iPad with options dialog up causes rendering problems
Description: """"Description: In KitchenSink iPad, while testing the """"""""Main Tests -> Option Dialogs"""""""" I selected Dialog 1 and rotated the device with the option dialog displayed. While rotating, I noted two behaviors. The more common was a detaching of the Option dialog from the button that spawned it. Less common was a black non-functional options dialog. See screen shots. It was easiest to reproduce by rotating the device 270 degrees or more. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS iPad on iPad device 2) Launch KS iPad and choose """"""""main tests"""""""" 3) Select options dialog 4) With the dialog up, rotate the device. Result: Frequent rendering of the options dialog in random screen locations, occasional black options dialog. Note: This also occurs with 1.8.0.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7366,12,"""iOS: iPad 5.0: Titanium.UI.EmailDialog attachment icon does not display""","""""""Titanium.UI.EmailDialog attachment icon does not display in iPad 5.0. Screenshots Attached.  Icons display correctly in all other iOS configurations.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code.    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'#FFFFFF',   orientationModes:[Ti.UI.PORTRAIT,Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT]  });    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: 'ScreenShot!!'  });    button.addEventListener('click',function(){   Titanium.Media.takeScreenshot(function(event){    var screenShot = event.media;    var img = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ image: screenShot });    Ti.API.info('saving the image into photogallery');    Titanium.Media.saveToPhotoGallery(img.image);    Ti.API.info('saving the blob into photogallery');    Titanium.Media.saveToPhotoGallery(img.toImage());    Ti.API.info('launch the email client!!');    var emailDialog = Titanium.UI.createEmailDialog()    emailDialog.subject = """"""""Colors of..."""""""";    emailDialog.messageBody = 'Lorem ipsum...';    emailDialog.addAttachment(img.toImage());    emailDialog.open();    win.add(img);   });  });    win.add(button);  win.open();  {code}    2. Press button to take screenshot.    . . . App takes screenshot, saves it, and adds it to an email attachment.    Expected Result:    Email attachement icon should be visible.    Actual Result:    Email attachment icon does not show.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad 5.0: Titanium.UI.EmailDialog attachment icon does not display
Description: """"Titanium.UI.EmailDialog attachment icon does not display in iPad 5.0. Screenshots Attached. Icons display correctly in all other iOS configurations. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#FFFFFF', orientationModes:[Ti.UI.PORTRAIT,Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT] }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'ScreenShot!!' }); button.addEventListener('click',function(){ Titanium.Media.takeScreenshot(function(event){ var screenShot = event.media; var img = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ image: screenShot }); Ti.API.info('saving the image into photogallery'); Titanium.Media.saveToPhotoGallery(img.image); Ti.API.info('saving the blob into photogallery'); Titanium.Media.saveToPhotoGallery(img.toImage()); Ti.API.info('launch the email client!!'); var emailDialog = Titanium.UI.createEmailDialog() emailDialog.subject = """"""""Colors of...""""""""; emailDialog.messageBody = 'Lorem ipsum...'; emailDialog.addAttachment(img.toImage()); emailDialog.open(); win.add(img); }); }); win.add(button); win.open(); {code} 2. Press button to take screenshot. . . . App takes screenshot, saves it, and adds it to an email attachment. Expected Result: Email attachement icon should be visible. Actual Result: Email attachment icon does not show.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7364,12,"""Android: Debugger on windows 7 throw an error""","""""""h3. Actual behavior  When the Debugger is invoked, the builds start, the app goes on and the Titanium studio report an error (image attached)    h3. Expected behavior  Run the debugger without problems    h3. Notes  I use the 2.2 google API android SDK I don't be able to reproduce with 2.2    h3. Steps to reproduce the bug  1. Create a new android project  2. Invoque the debugger  3. App goes up  4. Debugger throws an error""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Debugger on windows 7 throw an error
Description: """"h3. Actual behavior When the Debugger is invoked, the builds start, the app goes on and the Titanium studio report an error (image attached) h3. Expected behavior Run the debugger without problems h3. Notes I use the 2.2 google API android SDK I don't be able to reproduce with 2.2 h3. Steps to reproduce the bug 1. Create a new android project 2. Invoque the debugger 3. App goes up 4. Debugger throws an error""""",title+description
TIMOB-7363,12,"""iOS: flash on transition between splash and tab group when barImage is set""","""""""h3. Actual behavior  The app launch, the splash screen comes up, when the splash goes and the tab group enter, there's a flash on the up bar, and then takes all the attributes (image and color).    h3. Expected behavior  Smooth transition and no flashing when the splash screen goes off, and the tab group goes up.    h3. Notes  It's almost an imperceptible thing, on big apps it's a little bit more notorious, I'm using a background for the bar, I'm attaching the png file, I'm notice that with the barImage propert,  happens, without, it's totally imperceptible     h4. Code    {code:title=Bar.java|borderStyle=solid}    var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();    var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'1',     backgroundColor:'#000',    barImage:'navbar.png',    barColor: '#AAA'  });     var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({       icon:'KS_nav_views.png',      title:'1',     window:win1  });      tabGroup.addTab(tab1);  tabGroup.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: flash on transition between splash and tab group when barImage is set
Description: """"h3. Actual behavior The app launch, the splash screen comes up, when the splash goes and the tab group enter, there's a flash on the up bar, and then takes all the attributes (image and color). h3. Expected behavior Smooth transition and no flashing when the splash screen goes off, and the tab group goes up. h3. Notes It's almost an imperceptible thing, on big apps it's a little bit more notorious, I'm using a background for the bar, I'm attaching the png file, I'm notice that with the barImage propert, happens, without, it's totally imperceptible h4. Code {code:title=Bar.java|borderStyle=solid} var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'1', backgroundColor:'#000', barImage:'navbar.png', barColor: '#AAA' }); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({ icon:'KS_nav_views.png', title:'1', window:win1 }); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-7362,12,"""iOS: Nav Bar - In KS, Mashups Nav Bar becomes red after clicking on RSS test""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch KS from 1_8_X branch  2. Go to Mashups > RSS  3. Click on the left nav bar button to get back to Mashups    Actual: The Mashups nav bar becomes red. See attachment.  Expected: The nav bar should not change color.    Note: This does not occur in KS 1.8.0.1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Nav Bar - In KS, Mashups Nav Bar becomes red after clicking on RSS test
