Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Compile the attached project 2. Run and click on the lable """"""""This is a test"""""""" Actual: Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: [WARN] Exception in event callback. { Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: expressionBeginOffset = 117; Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: expressionCaretOffset = 135; Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: expressionEndOffset = 140; Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: line = 7; Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: message = """"""""Result of expression 'tabGroup.activeTab' [undefined] is not an object.""""""""; Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: name = TypeError; Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: sourceId = 64277384; Jan 23 17:53:51 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>manualdestruction[0x8410][462] <Notice>: sourceURL = """"""""file://localhost/var/mobile/Applications/31A5A696-95C7-4317-8866-DA97028B0D6F/ManualWindowDestruction.app/helper.js""""""""; Expected: To load a new window with table views with 4 rows Note: Works in 1.8.0.1 """"",title+description
TIMOB-7345,12,"""iOS: Tab Groups - In KS, cannot add/remove tabs dynamically any more""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch KS from 1_8_X branch  2. Go to Base UI > Tab groups    3. Press """"""""Add/Remove Tab""""""""  Actual: """"""""Mashups"""""""" tab does not dynamically change to """"""""More""""""""  Expected: """"""""Mashups"""""""" tab should dynamically change to """"""""More""""""""     4. Press """"""""Close/Animate Tab Group""""""""  Actual: """"""""Mashups"""""""" tab will change to """"""""More"""""""" after tab group closes  Expected: Should not see any changes to tab after pressing this button    Note: This new behavior does not occur in 1.8.0.1 KS""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tab Groups - In KS, cannot add/remove tabs dynamically any more
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch KS from 1_8_X branch 2. Go to Base UI > Tab groups 3. Press """"""""Add/Remove Tab"""""""" Actual: """"""""Mashups"""""""" tab does not dynamically change to """"""""More"""""""" Expected: """"""""Mashups"""""""" tab should dynamically change to """"""""More"""""""" 4. Press """"""""Close/Animate Tab Group"""""""" Actual: """"""""Mashups"""""""" tab will change to """"""""More"""""""" after tab group closes Expected: Should not see any changes to tab after pressing this button Note: This new behavior does not occur in 1.8.0.1 KS""""",title+description
TIMOB-7344,12,"""iOS: Views - Nested view cannot be displayed when dimension property is defined using percentage""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Copy code below to app.js:  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    layout: 'vertical',     fullscreen: true  });    var view = Ti.UI.createView({    layout: 'horizontal',    height: 50,    backgroundColor: '#ccf',    width: '50%'  });  var nested_view = Ti.UI.createView({    height: 50,    backgroundColor: '#cfc',    width: '50%'  });    var control = Ti.UI.createView({   layout:'horizontal',   height:50,   backgroundColor: 'red',   width: 160 // 50% of portrait screen width  });  var nested_control = Ti.UI.createView({   height:50,   backgroundColor:'green',   width: 80 // 25% of portrait screen width  });    view.add(nested_view);  win.add(view);    control.add(nested_control);  win.add(control);    win.open();  {code}  2. Launch app to an iOS device    Actual: Nested view is not displayed i.e. only one color is displayed on the view. See attachment.  Expected: Should see two colors on the view like Android's behavior. See attachment.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Views - Nested view cannot be displayed when dimension property is defined using percentage
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Copy code below to app.js: {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ layout: 'vertical', fullscreen: true }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ layout: 'horizontal', height: 50, backgroundColor: '#ccf', width: '50%' }); var nested_view = Ti.UI.createView({ height: 50, backgroundColor: '#cfc', width: '50%' }); var control = Ti.UI.createView({ layout:'horizontal', height:50, backgroundColor: 'red', width: 160 // 50% of portrait screen width }); var nested_control = Ti.UI.createView({ height:50, backgroundColor:'green', width: 80 // 25% of portrait screen width }); view.add(nested_view); win.add(view); control.add(nested_control); win.add(control); win.open(); {code} 2. Launch app to an iOS device Actual: Nested view is not displayed i.e. only one color is displayed on the view. See attachment. Expected: Should see two colors on the view like Android's behavior. See attachment.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7343,12,"""MobileWeb: Create graphics assets for emulated controls""","""""""MobileWeb needs to create several controls to mimic native controls. Mobile web team needs art assets for the following controls:    TableViewRow: hasChild, hasDetail, and hasCheck row decorations  Slider: Handle and rail    See attached screenshot and sample app for more info.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Create graphics assets for emulated controls
Description: """"MobileWeb needs to create several controls to mimic native controls. Mobile web team needs art assets for the following controls: TableViewRow: hasChild, hasDetail, and hasCheck row decorations Slider: Handle and rail See attached screenshot and sample app for more info.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7342,12,"""MobileWeb: Improve performance of Ti.UI.TableView with thousands of rows""","""""""Performance on mobile web devices is sluggish with TableViews containing thousands of rows.    Consider using a paging/tiling solution that groups rows into """"""""super rows"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Improve performance of Ti.UI.TableView with thousands of rows
Description: """"Performance on mobile web devices is sluggish with TableViews containing thousands of rows. Consider using a paging/tiling solution that groups rows into """"""""super rows"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-7341,12,"""iOS : Video/Navigation - When navigating between embedded video detail view and the Play Movie view, after a few times the app will crash  ""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Launch master KS on iOS device  2. Navigate to phone > Play Movie  3. Press Embedded Video then press the Play Movie back nav button  4. Repeat step 3 a few times    Actual result:  App will crash    Expected result:  App navigates correctly while playing a movie""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Video/Navigation - When navigating between embedded video detail view and the Play Movie view, after a few times the app will crash
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch master KS on iOS device 2. Navigate to phone > Play Movie 3. Press Embedded Video then press the Play Movie back nav button 4. Repeat step 3 a few times Actual result: App will crash Expected result: App navigates correctly while playing a movie""""",title+description
