TIMOB-7338,12,"""MobileWeb: Dragging TableView or ScrollView scrollbars interferes with touch/click event system""","""""""When clicking on the scroll bar and dragging in a desktop browser, the Scroll/TableView receives the mousedown event, but not the mouseup event causing the scrolling to be tied to the mouse position despite no buttons are being held down.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Dragging TableView or ScrollView scrollbars interferes with touch/click event system
Description: """"When clicking on the scroll bar and dragging in a desktop browser, the Scroll/TableView receives the mousedown event, but not the mouseup event causing the scrolling to be tied to the mouse position despite no buttons are being held down.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7337,12,"""Android: Size.height and size.width are 0 for Views with height: """"auto"""" and layout: """"vertical""""""","""""""Using Ti 1.8.0.1 with Android and V8, Views with height: """"""""auto"""""""" and layout: """"""""vertical"""""""" have their size.height and size.width properties set to 0, even after the window is opened.    Here is code to reproduce:      Results:  android 2.2 emulator (V8): view width: 0, view height: 0 <--incorrect  droid x2 w/android 2.3.4 (V8): view width: 0, view height: 0 <--incorrect  iphone simulator: view width: 320, view height: 44 <--correct""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Size.height and size.width are 0 for Views with height: """"auto"""" and layout: """"vertical""""
Description: """"Using Ti 1.8.0.1 with Android and V8, Views with height: """"""""auto"""""""" and layout: """"""""vertical"""""""" have their size.height and size.width properties set to 0, even after the window is opened. Here is code to reproduce: Results: android 2.2 emulator (V8): view width: 0, view height: 0 <--incorrect droid x2 w/android 2.3.4 (V8): view width: 0, view height: 0 <--incorrect iphone simulator: view width: 320, view height: 44 <--correct""""",title+description
TIMOB-7336,12,"""Android: Size.height and size.width are always 0 for Labels created after window is opened""","""""""Using Ti 1.8.0.1 with Android and V8, Labels always have their size.height and size.width properties set to 0. They obviously can't be calculated before the window is open, but after it is and the labels are drawn these properties should be set correctly.    Here is code to reproduce:      Results:  android 2.2 emulator (V8): label 1 height: 0, label 2 height: 0, label 3 height: 0 <--incorrect  droid x2 w/android 2.3.4 (V8): label 1 height: 0, label 2 height: 0, label 3 height: 0 0 <--incorrect  iphone simulator: label 1 height: 22, label 2 height: 42, label 3 height: 30 <--correct""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Size.height and size.width are always 0 for Labels created after window is opened
Description: """"Using Ti 1.8.0.1 with Android and V8, Labels always have their size.height and size.width properties set to 0. They obviously can't be calculated before the window is open, but after it is and the labels are drawn these properties should be set correctly. Here is code to reproduce: Results: android 2.2 emulator (V8): label 1 height: 0, label 2 height: 0, label 3 height: 0 <--incorrect droid x2 w/android 2.3.4 (V8): label 1 height: 0, label 2 height: 0, label 3 height: 0 0 <--incorrect iphone simulator: label 1 height: 22, label 2 height: 42, label 3 height: 30 <--correct""""",title+description
TIMOB-7335,12,"""Android: V8: handle JS failure when invoking V8Function ""","""""""When invoking a V8Function that results in a JS error, the app would crash hard instead of handling and reporting the error    Test app:  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: V8: handle JS failure when invoking V8Function
Description: """"When invoking a V8Function that results in a JS error, the app would crash hard instead of handling and reporting the error Test app: """"",title+description
TIMOB-7331,12,"""Android: Picker nested in TableView Row not working""","""""""h3.Problem  Under Ti SDK 1.8.0.1 a Ti.UI picker control hosted in a table view row does not render above the active window, but rather below it.    h6.Use to work on 1.7.5 (as seen in screen_1.7.5.jpg).      h6.Steps to reproduce  1) Run code below  2) Click one of the row's buttons to open a new window.   3) Click one of the row's pickers - it does not open the picker row options, when it should do - it works fine in Ti SDK 1.7.5.  4) Now navigate back using the back button - you see the picker options from the previous window briefly before being destroyed as the previous window closes (as seen in screen_1.8.0.1.jpg).    h6.Expected behavior  See fully operational Pickers whose options render above, rather than below the current window    h6.Repro sequence  {code:title=app.js}  var browserWin = require('browser').browserWin;  var browser = new browserWin();  browser.open();    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Picker nested in TableView Row not working
Description: """"h3.Problem Under Ti SDK 1.8.0.1 a Ti.UI picker control hosted in a table view row does not render above the active window, but rather below it. h6.Use to work on 1.7.5 (as seen in screen_1.7.5.jpg). h6.Steps to reproduce 1) Run code below 2) Click one of the row's buttons to open a new window. 3) Click one of the row's pickers - it does not open the picker row options, when it should do - it works fine in Ti SDK 1.7.5. 4) Now navigate back using the back button - you see the picker options from the previous window briefly before being destroyed as the previous window closes (as seen in screen_1.8.0.1.jpg). h6.Expected behavior See fully operational Pickers whose options render above, rather than below the current window h6.Repro sequence {code:title=app.js} var browserWin = require('browser').browserWin; var browser = new browserWin(); browser.open(); """"",title+description
