TIMOB-7317,12,"""IOS: ImageView fires the load event with state 'url' instead of 'image'""","""""""Android has """"""""image"""""""" and """"""""images"""""""" for load states.  IOS has """"""""url"""""""" and """"""""images"""""""".  Since """"""""url"""""""" property has been deprecated and replaced by """"""""image"""""""", load event should fire with state """"""""image""""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: IOS: ImageView fires the load event with state 'url' instead of 'image'
Description: """"Android has """"""""image"""""""" and """"""""images"""""""" for load states. IOS has """"""""url"""""""" and """"""""images"""""""". Since """"""""url"""""""" property has been deprecated and replaced by """"""""image"""""""", load event should fire with state """"""""image""""""""""""",title+description
TIMOB-7315,12,"""Android: Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer: cannot unpause or start player depending on scope of source code""","""""""Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer cannot unpause or start player depending on the structure of the enclosing app script.      There are two attached test projects:    Stand-Alone App: Test.zip // audioplayer code in a stand-alone app  Modularized App: module_media.zip (test-case Acceptance > TIMOB-2135) // audioplayer code in a larger code structure (using the anonymous closure namespace-object titanium-module pattern)      Using the attached projects:    The audioplayer cannot be unpaused in the modularized app (http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3124 (linked)). No Log Messages.  The audioplayer cannot be started in the stand-alone app. Log Attached: stand-alone start error.txt.  Both work correctly and identically in iOS.      Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run stand-alone test: Test on Android.  2. Press Start.    Expected Result:    Player should start.    Actual Result:    Player fails to start, error printed.      /* Re-iteration of http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3124 (linked)*/    3. Run modularized test: module_media on Android.  4. Navigate to Acceptance > timob_2135.  5. Press Start. Allow player to start.  6. Press Pause.  7. Press Unpause.    Expected Result:    Player should resume playing.    Actual Result:    Player does not resume.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer: cannot unpause or start player depending on scope of source code
Description: """"Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer cannot unpause or start player depending on the structure of the enclosing app script. There are two attached test projects: Stand-Alone App: Test.zip // audioplayer code in a stand-alone app Modularized App: module_media.zip (test-case Acceptance > TIMOB-2135) // audioplayer code in a larger code structure (using the anonymous closure namespace-object titanium-module pattern) Using the attached projects: The audioplayer cannot be unpaused in the modularized app (http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3124 (linked)). No Log Messages. The audioplayer cannot be started in the stand-alone app. Log Attached: stand-alone start error.txt. Both work correctly and identically in iOS. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run stand-alone test: Test on Android. 2. Press Start. Expected Result: Player should start. Actual Result: Player fails to start, error printed. /* Re-iteration of http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3124 (linked)*/ 3. Run modularized test: module_media on Android. 4. Navigate to Acceptance > timob_2135. 5. Press Start. Allow player to start. 6. Press Pause. 7. Press Unpause. Expected Result: Player should resume playing. Actual Result: Player does not resume.""""",title+description
