TIMOB-7284,12,"""Android: Build gives incomplete error message when emulator/device out of space""","""""""When building & installing an Android app to an emulator that is out of space, you get this error:    [ERROR] Failed installing com.<USER>requiretest:  pkg: /data/local/tmp/app.apk    In prior versions, the error was something like [FAILED_INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE] which is helpfully-specific.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Build gives incomplete error message when emulator/device out of space
Description: """"When building & installing an Android app to an emulator that is out of space, you get this error: [ERROR] Failed installing com.<USER>requiretest: pkg: /data/local/tmp/app.apk In prior versions, the error was something like [FAILED_INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE] which is helpfully-specific.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7283,12,"""Android: Support Synchronous HTTPClient calls""","""""""h3.Feature Request  The purpose of this feature request is to support Synchronous HTTP Calls on android as currently is in iOS.    h6.HTTPClient method  http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.open-method.html    h6.Repro sequence to test  Pass a third argument (true/false) to open()  {code:title=app.js}  var bool, xhr;    xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient();    bool = false;    xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""", """"""""http://api.twitter.com/1/help/test.json"""""""", false);    xhr.onreadystatechange = function() {      Ti.API.debug(""""""""Ready State change to """""""" + xhr.status);      if (xhr.status === 200) {        Ti.API.debug(""""""""Setting bool to true"""""""");        bool = true;      }    };    xhr.send();    Ti.API.debug(""""""""Bool is: """""""" + bool);  {code}    h6.Output  D/TiAPI  (  304): Bool is: false""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support Synchronous HTTPClient calls
Description: """"h3.Feature Request The purpose of this feature request is to support Synchronous HTTP Calls on android as currently is in iOS. h6.HTTPClient method http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.open-method.html h6.Repro sequence to test Pass a third argument (true/false) to open() {code:title=app.js} var bool, xhr; xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); bool = false; xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""", """"""""http://api.twitter.com/1/help/test.json"""""""", false); xhr.onreadystatechange = function() { Ti.API.debug(""""""""Ready State change to """""""" + xhr.status); if (xhr.status === 200) { Ti.API.debug(""""""""Setting bool to true""""""""); bool = true; } }; xhr.send(); Ti.API.debug(""""""""Bool is: """""""" + bool); {code} h6.Output D/TiAPI ( 304): Bool is: false""""",title+description
TIMOB-7281,12,"""APIDoc: Document coding pattern for providing pinch/zoom while in a ScrollableView""","""""""h4. PROBLEM  Zoom used to work inside a ScrollableView, with 1.7.5. The same code doesn't work (doesn't zoom) in 1.8.     h4. TESTCASE   Test this code in 1.7.5, do a zoom. Works fine. Do the same with 1.8, won't work.         h4. Community Discusion   http://developer.<USER>com/question/130153/image-zoom-not-working-after-update-to-sdk-18""""""",Bug,"Title: APIDoc: Document coding pattern for providing pinch/zoom while in a ScrollableView
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM Zoom used to work inside a ScrollableView, with 1.7.5. The same code doesn't work (doesn't zoom) in 1.8. h4. TESTCASE Test this code in 1.7.5, do a zoom. Works fine. Do the same with 1.8, won't work. h4. Community Discusion http://developer.<USER>com/question/130153/image-zoom-not-working-after-update-to-sdk-18""""",title+description
TIMOB-7279,12,"""iOS: Add API to load WebView content from string with baseURL""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Install KitchenSink  2. Navigate to Base UI > Views >Web Views > XHR to Filesystem   3. Click on any link    Actual: Debug and error messages about files not loading are printed out to the console:      Expected: Should able to load clicked links.    Note: Bug existed in 1.8.0.1""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add API to load WebView content from string with baseURL
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Install KitchenSink 2. Navigate to Base UI > Views >Web Views > XHR to Filesystem 3. Click on any link Actual: Debug and error messages about files not loading are printed out to the console: Expected: Should able to load clicked links. Note: Bug existed in 1.8.0.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7278,12,"""iOS : Modules - When including a local module and running on iOS Simulator, the modules contents are copied to into the application""","""""""<<Note this issue relates to TIMOB-5026 except that issue has been fixed for building for device, this issue strictly relates to iOS simulators>>    Steps to reproduce:  1. Install an iOS module into the application's folder by placing the module's zip file in the application folder (e.g. ti.bump-iphone-1.0.zip)  2. Build the application for iOS Simulator (e.g. iPhone simulator)  3. Navigate to the 'build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator' (or other target) folder for the application  4. Right-click on the application package and select """"""""Show Package Contents""""""""    Actual result:  If this issue hasn't been fixed there will be a module directory for the module you tested (i.e. ti.bump)    Expected result:  The module directory will not be included at the location specified above""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Modules - When including a local module and running on iOS Simulator, the modules contents are copied to into the application
Description: """"<<Note this issue relates to TIMOB-5026 except that issue has been fixed for building for device, this issue strictly relates to iOS simulators>> Steps to reproduce: 1. Install an iOS module into the application's folder by placing the module's zip file in the application folder (e.g. ti.bump-iphone-1.0.zip) 2. Build the application for iOS Simulator (e.g. iPhone simulator) 3. Navigate to the 'build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator' (or other target) folder for the application 4. Right-click on the application package and select """"""""Show Package Contents"""""""" Actual result: If this issue hasn't been fixed there will be a module directory for the module you tested (i.e. ti.bump) Expected result: The module directory will not be included at the location specified above""""",title+description
TIMOB-7276,12,"""iOS: Icons - After installing Titanium Apps to iPod, icons will intermittently disappear""","""""""Details:  After installing Titanium Apps specifically to iPod 3rd Gen (4.02), default and custom icons will intermittently disappear on the device. See attachment.    To get the icons back, you will need to reinstall the app again onto the device. Restarting the device will not bring the icons back. This might be related to an Apple bug: https://discussions.apple.com/thread/2753249?start=0&tstart=0    Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a Titanium project using default or custom icons  2. Install project to iOS devices. Preferably an iPod    Actual: Icons will disappear intermittently.  Expected: Icons should not disappear.    Note: Filing this bug in case other Titanium users come across this issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Icons - After installing Titanium Apps to iPod, icons will intermittently disappear
Description: """"Details: After installing Titanium Apps specifically to iPod 3rd Gen (4.02), default and custom icons will intermittently disappear on the device. See attachment. To get the icons back, you will need to reinstall the app again onto the device. Restarting the device will not bring the icons back. This might be related to an Apple bug: https://discussions.apple.com/thread/2753249?start=0&tstart=0 Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a Titanium project using default or custom icons 2. Install project to iOS devices. Preferably an iPod Actual: Icons will disappear intermittently. Expected: Icons should not disappear. Note: Filing this bug in case other Titanium users come across this issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7275,12,"""MobileWeb: Kitchen Sink html5 not able to click any table row""","""""""h3.Issue  When I run kitchen sink html5 in 1.9, I'm not able to click any table row. It was able to click in 1.8.    h6.Tested on  1.8.0.1 > It does work  1.9.0 (Build release the 01.17) > It doesn't work    h6.Steps to reproduce  1) Create Mobile Web project with Studio  2) Embed Kitchen Sink Html 5 demos  3) Run as Mobile Web Preview in Browser    h6.Expected behavior  Navigate through the pages    h6.Unexpected behavior  Not able to click any row""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Kitchen Sink html5 not able to click any table row
Description: """"h3.Issue When I run kitchen sink html5 in 1.9, I'm not able to click any table row. It was able to click in 1.8. h6.Tested on 1.8.0.1 > It does work 1.9.0 (Build release the 01.17) > It doesn't work h6.Steps to reproduce 1) Create Mobile Web project with Studio 2) Embed Kitchen Sink Html 5 demos 3) Run as Mobile Web Preview in Browser h6.Expected behavior Navigate through the pages h6.Unexpected behavior Not able to click any row""""",title+description
TIMOB-7273,12,"""iOS: tableView - Header disappears when clicking section row until table is scrolled""","""""""Description:  While testing kitchensink, Base UI>Views>Table Views>Headers, I noticed the header disappears when the section row is partially behind it when clicked. It reappears after scrolling the tableView. This does not occur with 1.8.0.1.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS built with SDK 1.9.0.v20120115231633  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Headers  3) Scroll the table so a row is partially behind the topmost header  4) Click the row    Result:  The header disappears    Expected:  The header is updated to include """"""""section has been clicked""""""""    Note:  Please review the attached screens for details and comparison to 1.8.0.1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: tableView - Header disappears when clicking section row until table is scrolled
Description: """"Description: While testing kitchensink, Base UI>Views>Table Views>Headers, I noticed the header disappears when the section row is partially behind it when clicked. It reappears after scrolling the tableView. This does not occur with 1.8.0.1. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS built with SDK 1.9.0.v20120115231633 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Headers 3) Scroll the table so a row is partially behind the topmost header 4) Click the row Result: The header disappears Expected: The header is updated to include """"""""section has been clicked"""""""" Note: Please review the attached screens for details and comparison to 1.8.0.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7272,12,"""Android: change map annotation to fire event when the annotation pin is clicked""","""""""In Android, when click on a annotation pin within the map view the description box is presented but not click event is fired.  A user must click the description box that is displayed in order to fire a event back to javascript.  A click event should be fired in both cases.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: change map annotation to fire event when the annotation pin is clicked
Description: """"In Android, when click on a annotation pin within the map view the description box is presented but not click event is fired. A user must click the description box that is displayed in order to fire a event back to javascript. A click event should be fired in both cases.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7271,12,"""iOS: eventListener - Click event listener not firing""","""""""Description:  During testing using Kitchen Sink, the rapid image update test did not respond to click events. The test will log """"""""I WAS CLICKED"""""""" in the console and the animation will change. This did not occur.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Build KS with SDK 1.9.0.v20120115231633  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Image Views>Image Rapid Update  3) Ensure console is running  4) Click stick figure    Result:  Nothing changes, no console output    Expected:  """"""""I WAS CLICKED"""""""" in the console, and the animation changes    Note:  This does not occur with KS and SDK 1.8.0.1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: eventListener - Click event listener not firing
Description: """"Description: During testing using Kitchen Sink, the rapid image update test did not respond to click events. The test will log """"""""I WAS CLICKED"""""""" in the console and the animation will change. This did not occur. Steps to reproduce: 1) Build KS with SDK 1.9.0.v20120115231633 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Image Views>Image Rapid Update 3) Ensure console is running 4) Click stick figure Result: Nothing changes, no console output Expected: """"""""I WAS CLICKED"""""""" in the console, and the animation changes Note: This does not occur with KS and SDK 1.8.0.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-7268,12,"""iOS: Application suddenly crash after navigate around views and tableviews""","""""""h3. Expected behavior  Navigate around the application without random crashes    h3. Actual behavior  Start to navigate around the app, and after some time (random) the app crash (random crash)    h3. Steps to reproduce  Open the app on the device, go to product, search for """"""""jacket"""""""" , browse the information, go back, enter again, and again, eventually the app it's gonna crash    h3. Resources  I can't attach the project, because it's bigger than 10MB, please send me an email to attach the project    h3. Log Crashes  I'm attaching some log crashes""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Application suddenly crash after navigate around views and tableviews
Description: """"h3. Expected behavior Navigate around the application without random crashes h3. Actual behavior Start to navigate around the app, and after some time (random) the app crash (random crash) h3. Steps to reproduce Open the app on the device, go to product, search for """"""""jacket"""""""" , browse the information, go back, enter again, and again, eventually the app it's gonna crash h3. Resources I can't attach the project, because it's bigger than 10MB, please send me an email to attach the project h3. Log Crashes I'm attaching some log crashes""""",title+description
TIMOB-7266,12,"""iOS: UI view size property values incorrect if queried too soon after orientation change""","""""""h2. Problem    The view's size property values are incorrect (they remain the previous values) when they are used/queried immediately after they have been modified.    h2. Test case    In the example below, the width property is changed within a {{orientationchange}} event listener. When the device is reorientated, the logged value is the previous rather than new value.    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({  // fullscreen: false, // once fixed, please check with this line uncommented  backgroundColor:'red'  });    var view = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'blue',    width:'50',    height:50  });    win.add(view);    Ti.API.info(""""""""*** Before window open - view.size.width = 50 ***"""""""");  Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); // correct    view.width = 100;    win.addEventListener('open', function(){    Ti.API.info(""""""""*** Window open - view.size.width = 100 ***"""""""");    Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); // correct  });      Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange', function(){    Ti.API.info(""""""""*** orientationchange - view.size.width = 200 ***"""""""");    view.width = 200;    Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); // incorrect on first orientation change  });  win.open();      h2. Workaround    Using setTimeout allows the size values to be updated to reflect the re-rendered view.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI view size property values incorrect if queried too soon after orientation change
Description: """"h2. Problem The view's size property values are incorrect (they remain the previous values) when they are used/queried immediately after they have been modified. h2. Test case In the example below, the width property is changed within a {{orientationchange}} event listener. When the device is reorientated, the logged value is the previous rather than new value. {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ // fullscreen: false, // once fixed, please check with this line uncommented backgroundColor:'red' }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'blue', width:'50', height:50 }); win.add(view); Ti.API.info(""""""""*** Before window open - view.size.width = 50 ***""""""""); Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); // correct view.width = 100; win.addEventListener('open', function(){ Ti.API.info(""""""""*** Window open - view.size.width = 100 ***""""""""); Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); // correct }); Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange', function(){ Ti.API.info(""""""""*** orientationchange - view.size.width = 200 ***""""""""); view.width = 200; Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); // incorrect on first orientation change }); win.open(); h2. Workaround Using setTimeout allows the size values to be updated to reflect the re-rendered view. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7265,12,"""MobileWeb: Window: After opening a window in a tabbed application user cannot close it""","""""""Steps To Reproduce  1. Create a new mobile application with the Tabbed Application Template  2. Compile mobile web to browser  3. Click on open window  4. Click back button from browser    Actual:  Nothing happens the window cannot be closed, note the window is also not full screen    Expected:  Should close the window that was opened  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Window: After opening a window in a tabbed application user cannot close it
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce 1. Create a new mobile application with the Tabbed Application Template 2. Compile mobile web to browser 3. Click on open window 4. Click back button from browser Actual: Nothing happens the window cannot be closed, note the window is also not full screen Expected: Should close the window that was opened """"",title+description
TIMOB-7264,12,"""Android: HTTPClient not working for upload files (Parity)""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer can't upload files thru HTTPClient from Android. Code is working perfect in iOS.     h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Create mobile project  2. Paste this code to app.js      3. Run this on Android    h4. ACTUAL RESULTS  The upload is not working    h4. EXPECTED RESULTS  The upload working fine, as in iOS.     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient not working for upload files (Parity)
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer can't upload files thru HTTPClient from Android. Code is working perfect in iOS. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Create mobile project 2. Paste this code to app.js 3. Run this on Android h4. ACTUAL RESULTS The upload is not working h4. EXPECTED RESULTS The upload working fine, as in iOS. """"",title+description
