TIMOB-7230,12,"""MobileWeb: Override the html and body tag height with the browser's height when DOM ready""","""""""Once the DOM ready event fires, we need change the height of the <html> and <body> tag from 100% to the height in pixels of the browser window.    This becomes a problem on Android tablets when the URL bar is focused and the keyboard pops up which shrinks the size of the page.    Also investigate the location bar and JavaScript console bars on iOS.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Override the html and body tag height with the browser's height when DOM ready
Description: """"Once the DOM ready event fires, we need change the height of the <html> and <body> tag from 100% to the height in pixels of the browser window. This becomes a problem on Android tablets when the URL bar is focused and the keyboard pops up which shrinks the size of the page. Also investigate the location bar and JavaScript console bars on iOS.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7229,12,"""iOS: UI.Window - open and focus events not fired when open method before eventlisteners""","""""""h2. Problem    Neither window open or focus events are fired.    Note that both work on Android, albeit with bugs (that can be worked around). See linked ticket, and its linked tickets.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor:'red'  });  win.open();    win.addEventListener('open', function() {  Ti.API.info('------- Window open event fired ------');  });    win.addEventListener('focus', function() {  Ti.API.info('------- Window focus event fired ------');  });  {code}    h2. Logs    Nothing output to the logs.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI.Window - open and focus events not fired when open method before eventlisteners
Description: """"h2. Problem Neither window open or focus events are fired. Note that both work on Android, albeit with bugs (that can be worked around). See linked ticket, and its linked tickets. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'red' }); win.open(); win.addEventListener('open', function() { Ti.API.info('------- Window open event fired ------'); }); win.addEventListener('focus', function() { Ti.API.info('------- Window focus event fired ------'); }); {code} h2. Logs Nothing output to the logs. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7228,12,"""iOS: Simulator: KitchenSink: intermittent EXC_BAD_ACCESS (SIGBUS) crash""","""""""When navigating back to a main tableviewrow menu in KitchenSink, simulator intermittently crashes with EXC_BAD_ACCESS (SIGBUS).    Able to reproduce via stress test in Lion and Snow Leopard on iPhone Simulator 5.0 and 4.3.    Log Attached.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink in the iPhone Simulator.  2. Cycle in and out (back) of a any test window/windows (stress test).    Expected Result:    App should remain stable.    Actual Result:    App occasionally crashes.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Simulator: KitchenSink: intermittent EXC_BAD_ACCESS (SIGBUS) crash
Description: """"When navigating back to a main tableviewrow menu in KitchenSink, simulator intermittently crashes with EXC_BAD_ACCESS (SIGBUS). Able to reproduce via stress test in Lion and Snow Leopard on iPhone Simulator 5.0 and 4.3. Log Attached. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink in the iPhone Simulator. 2. Cycle in and out (back) of a any test window/windows (stress test). Expected Result: App should remain stable. Actual Result: App occasionally crashes.""""",title+description
