TIMOB-7205,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.UI.Picker implementation""","""""""This UI element is most similar to a select dropdown, though there is no rendered DOM element, only the options.  This could be achieved using a <select> element that is positioned offscreen or with opacity=0 that gets focused during show(). The only problem with this approach is it only supports 1 column.  It's probably better to create a custom UI widget.    Extends Evented.    Methods:  * add()  * getSelectedRow()  * reloadColumn()  * setSelectedRow()    Properties:  * columns - Array  * countDownDuration  * format24  * locale  * minDate  * minuteInterval  * selectionIndicator  * type - Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_* constants  * useSpinner  * value  * visibleItems    Events:  * change    Update API docs with support for methods and properties:  Methods:  * reloadColumn()  Properties:  * format24  * useSpinner  * visibleItems  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.UI.Picker implementation
Description: """"This UI element is most similar to a select dropdown, though there is no rendered DOM element, only the options. This could be achieved using a <select> element that is positioned offscreen or with opacity=0 that gets focused during show(). The only problem with this approach is it only supports 1 column. It's probably better to create a custom UI widget. Extends Evented. Methods: * add() * getSelectedRow() * reloadColumn() * setSelectedRow() Properties: * columns - Array * countDownDuration * format24 * locale * minDate * minuteInterval * selectionIndicator * type - Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_* constants * useSpinner * value * visibleItems Events: * change Update API docs with support for methods and properties: Methods: * reloadColumn() Properties: * format24 * useSpinner * visibleItems """"",title+description
TIMOB-7204,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.API.log() does not properly print objects, arrays""","""""""Given the following code:        It outputs """"""""[LOG] [object Object]"""""""" instead of """"""""[LOG]"""""""" followed by the object's value.  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.API.log() does not properly print objects, arrays
Description: """"Given the following code: It outputs """"""""[LOG] [object Object]"""""""" instead of """"""""[LOG]"""""""" followed by the object's value. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7203,12,"""iOS: UI.View - make size property read-only""","""""""h2. Problem    According to Arthur's comment [here|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6785?focusedCommentId=176740&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-176740], the [Ti.UI.View.size|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.View.size-property.html] property on iOS is writable.    The property is intended to be read-only. Users should only modify the {{view.width}} and {{view.height}} properties.    On Android, the property is read-only as expected. Hence, this is a parity ticket.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    fullscreen:false,    backgroundColor:'red'  });    var view = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'blue',    width:50,    height:50  });    win.add(view);  win.open();    Ti.API.info(""""""""*** Before width changes 50 ***"""""""");  Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height);  Ti.API.info(""""""""view w x h: """""""" + view.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.height);    Ti.API.info(""""""""*** view.size.width change 100 ***"""""""");  view.size.width = 100; // this should NOT work  Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height);  Ti.API.info(""""""""view w x h: """""""" + view.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.height);    Ti.API.info(""""""""*** view.width change 200 ***"""""""");  view.width = 200; // this should work  Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height);  Ti.API.info(""""""""view w x h: """""""" + view.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.height);    [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.0.1 (12/22/11 13:09 fbdc96f)  [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal  [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0  [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone  [INFO] testing11/1.0 (1.8.0.1.fbdc96f)  [INFO] *** Before width changes 50 ***  [INFO] view.size w x h: 50 x 50  [INFO] view w x h: 50 x 50  [INFO] *** view.size.width change 100 ***  [INFO] view.size w x h: 50 x 50  [INFO] view w x h: 50 x 50  [INFO] *** view.width change 200 ***  [INFO] view.size w x h: 50 x 50  [INFO] view w x h: 200 x 50  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI.View - make size property read-only
Description: """"h2. Problem According to Arthur's comment [here|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6785?focusedCommentId=176740&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-176740], the [Ti.UI.View.size|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.View.size-property.html] property on iOS is writable. The property is intended to be read-only. Users should only modify the {{view.width}} and {{view.height}} properties. On Android, the property is read-only as expected. Hence, this is a parity ticket. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ fullscreen:false, backgroundColor:'red' }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'blue', width:50, height:50 }); win.add(view); win.open(); Ti.API.info(""""""""*** Before width changes 50 ***""""""""); Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); Ti.API.info(""""""""view w x h: """""""" + view.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.height); Ti.API.info(""""""""*** view.size.width change 100 ***""""""""); view.size.width = 100; // this should NOT work Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); Ti.API.info(""""""""view w x h: """""""" + view.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.height); Ti.API.info(""""""""*** view.width change 200 ***""""""""); view.width = 200; // this should work Ti.API.info(""""""""view.size w x h: """""""" + view.size.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.size.height); Ti.API.info(""""""""view w x h: """""""" + view.width + """""""" x """""""" + view.height); [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.0.1 (12/22/11 13:09 fbdc96f) [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0 [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone [INFO] testing11/1.0 (1.8.0.1.fbdc96f) [INFO] *** Before width changes 50 *** [INFO] view.size w x h: 50 x 50 [INFO] view w x h: 50 x 50 [INFO] *** view.size.width change 100 *** [INFO] view.size w x h: 50 x 50 [INFO] view w x h: 50 x 50 [INFO] *** view.width change 200 *** [INFO] view.size w x h: 50 x 50 [INFO] view w x h: 200 x 50 {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-7201,12,"""Android: UI.window - open and focus events fire more than once""","""""""h2. Problem    Window open and focus events fire more than once (twice, in my tests).    Note that open and focus is not currently fired at all for lightweight windows. See linked ticket for more info.    Works as expected in 1.7.5, hence this is a regression.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    fullscreen:false,    backgroundColor:'red'  });    win.open();    win.addEventListener('open', function() {    Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: open --------"""""""");  });    win.addEventListener('focus', function() {    Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: focus --------"""""""");  });      h2. Workaround    Use a boolean variable to determine whether the event has already been fired.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: UI.window - open and focus events fire more than once
Description: """"h2. Problem Window open and focus events fire more than once (twice, in my tests). Note that open and focus is not currently fired at all for lightweight windows. See linked ticket for more info. Works as expected in 1.7.5, hence this is a regression. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ fullscreen:false, backgroundColor:'red' }); win.open(); win.addEventListener('open', function() { Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: open --------""""""""); }); win.addEventListener('focus', function() { Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: focus --------""""""""); }); h2. Workaround Use a boolean variable to determine whether the event has already been fired.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7200,12,"""Android: UI.window - open event does not fire for lightweight windows when window open method is after addEventListener""","""""""h2. Problem    Window open event does not fire for lightweight windows when window open() method positioned before {{addEventListener}}    The open event works as expected in 1.7.5. Hence this is a regression.    Note that the focus event also suffers the same issue.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    // fullscreen:false, // enable this to workaround the issue    backgroundColor:'red'  });    win.open(); // move this after eventListeners to workaround isssue    win.addEventListener('open', function() {    Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: open --------"""""""");  });    win.addEventListener('focus', function() {    Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: focus --------"""""""");  });  {code}    h2. Logs    No output produced    h2. Workaround    Use heavyweight window or ensure that window open() method is positioned after eventListeners  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: UI.window - open event does not fire for lightweight windows when window open method is after addEventListener
Description: """"h2. Problem Window open event does not fire for lightweight windows when window open() method positioned before {{addEventListener}} The open event works as expected in 1.7.5. Hence this is a regression. Note that the focus event also suffers the same issue. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ // fullscreen:false, // enable this to workaround the issue backgroundColor:'red' }); win.open(); // move this after eventListeners to workaround isssue win.addEventListener('open', function() { Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: open --------""""""""); }); win.addEventListener('focus', function() { Ti.API.info(""""""""------- Window event fired: focus --------""""""""); }); {code} h2. Logs No output produced h2. Workaround Use heavyweight window or ensure that window open() method is positioned after eventListeners """"",title+description
