TIMOB-7192,12,"""view.animate() does not update the properties of the view that have been updated""","""""""h3. Problem    After a {{Ti.UI.Animation}} is run on a view with the {{animate()}} function, the properties that were animated should be updated on the view. For example, the following code animates a view to a new {{top}} position, but the {{top}} property of the view does not reflect this afterwards.        After the view animates and you click on it, it still indicates that the {{top}} property is a value of 0 (zero).     h3. Expected Behavior    The view's {{top}} property in the above example should be 200 after the animation.    h3. Workaround    For now, if you want the properties to be updated, you need to do it manually in the animation's {{complete}} event. This is troublesome because of the fact that you don't get a reference to the animated view in the {{complete}} event, it needs to be either manually assigned to the Ti.UI.Animation, or into ta closure, as referenced in ticket [TIMOB-7190|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7190]    Here is the above code modified with the workaround    """"""",Bug,"Title: view.animate() does not update the properties of the view that have been updated
Description: """"h3. Problem After a {{Ti.UI.Animation}} is run on a view with the {{animate()}} function, the properties that were animated should be updated on the view. For example, the following code animates a view to a new {{top}} position, but the {{top}} property of the view does not reflect this afterwards. After the view animates and you click on it, it still indicates that the {{top}} property is a value of 0 (zero). h3. Expected Behavior The view's {{top}} property in the above example should be 200 after the animation. h3. Workaround For now, if you want the properties to be updated, you need to do it manually in the animation's {{complete}} event. This is troublesome because of the fact that you don't get a reference to the animated view in the {{complete}} event, it needs to be either manually assigned to the Ti.UI.Animation, or into ta closure, as referenced in ticket [TIMOB-7190|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7190] Here is the above code modified with the workaround """"",title+description
TIMOB-7191,12,"""view.animate() does not update the properties of the view that have been updated""","""""""h3. Problem    After a {{Ti.UI.Animation}} is run on a view with the {{animate()}} function, the properties that were animated should be updated on the view. For example, the following code animates a view to a new {{top}} position, but the {{top}} property of the view does not reflect this afterwards.        After the view animates and you click on it, it still indicates that the {{top}} property is a value of 0 (zero).     h3. Expected Behavior    The view's {{top}} property in the above example should be 200 after the animation.    h3. Workaround    For now, if you want the properties to be updated, you need to do it manually in the animation's {{complete}} event. This is troublesome because of the fact that you don't get a reference to the animated view in the {{complete}} event, it needs to be either manually assigned to the Ti.UI.Animation, or into ta closure, as referenced in ticket [TIMOB-7190|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7190]    Here is the above code modified with the workaround    """"""",Bug,"Title: view.animate() does not update the properties of the view that have been updated
Description: """"h3. Problem After a {{Ti.UI.Animation}} is run on a view with the {{animate()}} function, the properties that were animated should be updated on the view. For example, the following code animates a view to a new {{top}} position, but the {{top}} property of the view does not reflect this afterwards. After the view animates and you click on it, it still indicates that the {{top}} property is a value of 0 (zero). h3. Expected Behavior The view's {{top}} property in the above example should be 200 after the animation. h3. Workaround For now, if you want the properties to be updated, you need to do it manually in the animation's {{complete}} event. This is troublesome because of the fact that you don't get a reference to the animated view in the {{complete}} event, it needs to be either manually assigned to the Ti.UI.Animation, or into ta closure, as referenced in ticket [TIMOB-7190|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-7190] Here is the above code modified with the workaround """"",title+description
TIMOB-7190,12,"""Add 'view' property to Ti.UI.Animation""","""""""Currently there is no way to know what view a {{Ti.UI.Animation}} is operating on. So for example, if I want to perform another operation on the target view after the {{Animation}} completes, I need to add that reference directly to the {{Animation}} manually.        It would be much easier if when {{view.animate()}} was called, the {{Animate}} object automatically had the appropriate view added to it as a property.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Add 'view' property to Ti.UI.Animation
Description: """"Currently there is no way to know what view a {{Ti.UI.Animation}} is operating on. So for example, if I want to perform another operation on the target view after the {{Animation}} completes, I need to add that reference directly to the {{Animation}} manually. It would be much easier if when {{view.animate()}} was called, the {{Animate}} object automatically had the appropriate view added to it as a property.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7189,12,"""MobileWeb: Complete Ti.UI.Button implementation""","""""""Finished the Button implementation.    Extends FontWidget (which extends Widget/View and Evented).    Properties:  * backgroundColor - currently sets the button's color, not backgroundColor  * selectedColor  * style  * titleid    Remove unsupported properties:  * backgroundLeftCap  * backgroundTopCap    Update API docs with supported """"""""transform"""""""" property.  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Complete Ti.UI.Button implementation
Description: """"Finished the Button implementation. Extends FontWidget (which extends Widget/View and Evented). Properties: * backgroundColor - currently sets the button's color, not backgroundColor * selectedColor * style * titleid Remove unsupported properties: * backgroundLeftCap * backgroundTopCap Update API docs with supported """"""""transform"""""""" property. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7188,12,"""Android: Media module methods takeScreenshot and previewImage not implemented in 1.8.0.1""","""""""Ti.Media.takeScreenshot and Ti.Media.previewImage are commented out inside MediaModule.java since 1.8.0.1.  We need investigate why (if any reason) and re-enable these.  Documentation should be updated with the addition of these methods.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Media module methods takeScreenshot and previewImage not implemented in 1.8.0.1
Description: """"Ti.Media.takeScreenshot and Ti.Media.previewImage are commented out inside MediaModule.java since 1.8.0.1. We need investigate why (if any reason) and re-enable these. Documentation should be updated with the addition of these methods.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7187,12,"""TI API: validRow property exists in iOS, but not Android""","""""""iOS has both the isValidRow method and validRow property    Android has the isValidRow method, but it doesn't currently have a validRow property.""""""",Bug,"Title: TI API: validRow property exists in iOS, but not Android
Description: """"iOS has both the isValidRow method and validRow property Android has the isValidRow method, but it doesn't currently have a validRow property.""""",title+description
