TIMOB-7170,12,"""MobileWeb: Complete Ti.UI.AlertDialog implementation""","""""""Missing entire correct implementation. AlertDialog widgets allow an arbitrary number of buttons with their own labels. This means you could have a dialog with a """"""""accept"""""""" and """"""""reject"""""""" buttons. This is not possible in mobileweb using an alert() or confirm() dialog. Instead, we'll need a custom UI widget that mimics a modal dialog. By default, there's only an OK button.    Extends Evented.    Methods:  * hide()  * show()    Properties:  * buttonNames [stage]  * cancel  * message  * messageid  * ok  * okid  * title  * titleid    Events:  * click    Update API docs with the supported methods, properties, and constants.  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Complete Ti.UI.AlertDialog implementation
Description: """"Missing entire correct implementation. AlertDialog widgets allow an arbitrary number of buttons with their own labels. This means you could have a dialog with a """"""""accept"""""""" and """"""""reject"""""""" buttons. This is not possible in mobileweb using an alert() or confirm() dialog. Instead, we'll need a custom UI widget that mimics a modal dialog. By default, there's only an OK button. Extends Evented. Methods: * hide() * show() Properties: * buttonNames [stage] * cancel * message * messageid * ok * okid * title * titleid Events: * click Update API docs with the supported methods, properties, and constants. """"",title+description
