TIMOB-7106,12,"""Android: API Debug - Internal Titanium code is exposed through Ti.API.debug() method""","""""""Details: While closing bug [TIMOB-6372|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6372], Ivan found a bug that exposes Titanium internal code through Ti.API.debug() method.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch following code to Android device/emulator in V8 or Rhino:  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   modal: true,   backgroundColor: '#0f0'  });     var button = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: 'Close me!'  });    button.addEventListener('click', function() {   win.close();  });    win.addEventListener('close', function() {   Ti.API.info('Close event');   Ti.API.debug(this.close);  });    win.add(button);    win.open();  {code}  2. Press close button  3. Check logcat    Actual: Internal Titanium code is exposed in the logcat.  Expected: Internal Titanium code should not be exposed.    Note:  * Bug also occurs on 1.7.5  * Bug does not appear on iOS""""""",Sub-task,"Title: Android: API Debug - Internal Titanium code is exposed through Ti.API.debug() method
Description: """"Details: While closing bug [TIMOB-6372|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6372], Ivan found a bug that exposes Titanium internal code through Ti.API.debug() method. Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch following code to Android device/emulator in V8 or Rhino: {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ modal: true, backgroundColor: '#0f0' }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Close me!' }); button.addEventListener('click', function() { win.close(); }); win.addEventListener('close', function() { Ti.API.info('Close event'); Ti.API.debug(this.close); }); win.add(button); win.open(); {code} 2. Press close button 3. Check logcat Actual: Internal Titanium code is exposed in the logcat. Expected: Internal Titanium code should not be exposed. Note: * Bug also occurs on 1.7.5 * Bug does not appear on iOS""""",title+description
TIMOB-7104,12,"""MobileWeb: Complete Ti.Database.DB implementation""","""""""Finish the Ti.Database.DB implementation.    Extends Evented.    Methods:  * getLastInsertRowId()  * getName()  * getRowsAffected()  * setLastInsertRowId()  * setName()  * setRowsAffected()    There are properties for these already, so should use lang.mixProps() to automatically create the setters/getters.  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Complete Ti.Database.DB implementation
Description: """"Finish the Ti.Database.DB implementation. Extends Evented. Methods: * getLastInsertRowId() * getName() * getRowsAffected() * setLastInsertRowId() * setName() * setRowsAffected() There are properties for these already, so should use lang.mixProps() to automatically create the setters/getters. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7103,12,"""MobileWeb: Add support for installing SQLite databases in Ti.Database.install()""","""""""Implement the Ti.Database.install() method. It needs to check if database exists, if not, synchronously download and populate the data.    During compile type, compiler.py will need to find all SQLite databases in the Resource directory and convert them to a JavaScript file to be downloaded via require(). The contents of the file is a JSON object wrapped in a define() call.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Add support for installing SQLite databases in Ti.Database.install()
Description: """"Implement the Ti.Database.install() method. It needs to check if database exists, if not, synchronously download and populate the data. During compile type, compiler.py will need to find all SQLite databases in the Resource directory and convert them to a JavaScript file to be downloaded via require(). The contents of the file is a JSON object wrapped in a define() call.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7102,12,"""MobileWeb: Complete Ti.Database implementation""","""""""Implement Ti.Database.    Methods  * install() - Depends on TIMOB-7103    Constants  * FIELD_TYPE_DOUBLE  * FIELD_TYPE_FLOAT  * FIELD_TYPE_INT  * FIELD_TYPE_STRING  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Complete Ti.Database implementation
Description: """"Implement Ti.Database. Methods * install() - Depends on TIMOB-7103 Constants * FIELD_TYPE_DOUBLE * FIELD_TYPE_FLOAT * FIELD_TYPE_INT * FIELD_TYPE_STRING """"",title+description
TIMOB-7101,12,"""MobileWeb: CSS rule manager""","""""""Setting styles on many DOM nodes can be a huge performance issue and cause multiple reflows. The browser is capable of optimizing the number of style changes per reflow by applying a CSS rule that contains several style settings.    A CSS rule manager would create multiple rules and apply them based on common style changes.    For example, if ever DOM node is set to a specific font and color, it is more efficient for a CSS rule manager to create a rule, then add the rule to each node.    We may need to break up rules into categories (background, font, size, pointer events, transitions, etc). Since the style properties will vary, perhaps a hash of the properties and their values can be used to speed up creation and applying of rules.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: CSS rule manager
Description: """"Setting styles on many DOM nodes can be a huge performance issue and cause multiple reflows. The browser is capable of optimizing the number of style changes per reflow by applying a CSS rule that contains several style settings. A CSS rule manager would create multiple rules and apply them based on common style changes. For example, if ever DOM node is set to a specific font and color, it is more efficient for a CSS rule manager to create a rule, then add the rule to each node. We may need to break up rules into categories (background, font, size, pointer events, transitions, etc). Since the style properties will vary, perhaps a hash of the properties and their values can be used to speed up creation and applying of rules.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7100,12,"""Android: tiapp.xml anyDensity tag causes crash on device in Android 4.0""","""""""KitchenSink: Android 4.0 - tiapp.xml tag <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/> causes KS to crash on device.    Changing the value to """"""""true"""""""" fixes the behavior, but text fields and button text are no longer readable.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink on Android 4.0 device.    Expected Result:    App should run.    Actual result:    Crash with graphics artifacts.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: tiapp.xml anyDensity tag causes crash on device in Android 4.0
Description: """"KitchenSink: Android 4.0 - tiapp.xml tag <supports-screens android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/> causes KS to crash on device. Changing the value to """"""""true"""""""" fixes the behavior, but text fields and button text are no longer readable. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink on Android 4.0 device. Expected Result: App should run. Actual result: Crash with graphics artifacts.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7099,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Codec implementation""","""""""Implement Ti.Codec which converts Numbers and Strings to and from a Titanium.Buffer.    Extends Evented.    Methods:  * decodeNumber()  * decodeString()  * encodeNumber()  * encodeString()  * getNativeByteOrder()    Constants:  * BIG_ENDIAN  * CHARSET_ASCII  * CHARSET_ISO_LATIN_1  * CHARSET_UTF16  * CHARSET_UTF16BE  * CHARSET_UTF16LE  * CHARSET_UTF8  * LITTLE_ENDIAN  * TYPE_BYTE  * TYPE_DOUBLE  * TYPE_FLOAT  * TYPE_INT  * TYPE_LONG  * TYPE_SHORT  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Codec implementation
Description: """"Implement Ti.Codec which converts Numbers and Strings to and from a Titanium.Buffer. Extends Evented. Methods: * decodeNumber() * decodeString() * encodeNumber() * encodeString() * getNativeByteOrder() Constants: * BIG_ENDIAN * CHARSET_ASCII * CHARSET_ISO_LATIN_1 * CHARSET_UTF16 * CHARSET_UTF16BE * CHARSET_UTF16LE * CHARSET_UTF8 * LITTLE_ENDIAN * TYPE_BYTE * TYPE_DOUBLE * TYPE_FLOAT * TYPE_INT * TYPE_LONG * TYPE_SHORT """"",title+description
TIMOB-7098,12,"""MobileWeb: Move build hash/date embedding in scons to compiler.py""","""""""The build hash and build date are directly replaced in the mobile web source at the time scons builds the titanium mobile project. It would be better if the build info was written to a file that the compiler.py can read and embed directly in the require.config.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Move build hash/date embedding in scons to compiler.py
Description: """"The build hash and build date are directly replaced in the mobile web source at the time scons builds the titanium mobile project. It would be better if the build info was written to a file that the compiler.py can read and embed directly in the require.config.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7097,12,"""MobileWeb: Complete Ti.App implementation""","""""""Missing the following:    * getCopyright()  * getDescription()  * getGuid()  * getId()  * getName()  * getPublisher()  * getUrl()  * getVersion()    Since we already have properties for these, we can probably use lang.mixProps() to automatically create the setter/getters.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Complete Ti.App implementation
Description: """"Missing the following: * getCopyright() * getDescription() * getGuid() * getId() * getName() * getPublisher() * getUrl() * getVersion() Since we already have properties for these, we can probably use lang.mixProps() to automatically create the setter/getters.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7096,12,"""MobileWeb: Add line and filename to log functions at compile time""","""""""Once the AST parser is integrated into the compiler, it would be nice to rewrite log statements to include line numbers and filenames. To optimize file size, Ti.API.log(""""""""hi"""""""") would be rewritten to Ti.API.log(0, """"""""hi"""""""") where """"""""0"""""""" is a unique integer that is used to lookup the line number and filename from a compiled map appended to the end of titanium.js.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Add line and filename to log functions at compile time
Description: """"Once the AST parser is integrated into the compiler, it would be nice to rewrite log statements to include line numbers and filenames. To optimize file size, Ti.API.log(""""""""hi"""""""") would be rewritten to Ti.API.log(0, """"""""hi"""""""") where """"""""0"""""""" is a unique integer that is used to lookup the line number and filename from a compiled map appended to the end of titanium.js.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7095,12,"""MobileWeb: Complete Ti implementation""","""""""The Ti namespace is missing the following:    * getBuildDate()  * getBuildHash()  * getUserAgent()  * getVersion()  * setUserAgent()    Since we already have these defined as properties, consider using lang.mixProps() to automatically create the setters/getters.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Complete Ti implementation
Description: """"The Ti namespace is missing the following: * getBuildDate() * getBuildHash() * getUserAgent() * getVersion() * setUserAgent() Since we already have these defined as properties, consider using lang.mixProps() to automatically create the setters/getters.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7094,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.IOStream implementation""","""""""Implement Ti.IOStream interface. Should NOT extend Evented (or anything else). Methods are just stubbed out.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.IOStream implementation
