TIMOB-7090,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.BufferStream implementation""","""""""Implement Ti.BufferStream. Extends Evented and Ti.IOStream. Wraps reads/writes around Ti.Buffer.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.BufferStream implementation
Description: """"Implement Ti.BufferStream. Extends Evented and Ti.IOStream. Wraps reads/writes around Ti.Buffer.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7089,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Buffer implementation""","""""""Implement Ti.Buffer. Extends Evented. Created from Ti.createBuffer().""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Buffer implementation
Description: """"Implement Ti.Buffer. Extends Evented. Created from Ti.createBuffer().""""",title+description
TIMOB-7088,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.BlobStream implementation""","""""""Implement Ti.BlobStream. Extends Evented and Ti.IOStream. Used to read/write data to a Ti.Blob.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.BlobStream implementation
Description: """"Implement Ti.BlobStream. Extends Evented and Ti.IOStream. Used to read/write data to a Ti.Blob.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7086,12,"""Implement Ti.Event""","""""""Need to implement Ti.Event, specifically an instantiable (declare) object that wraps a mixin of source, type, and custom event properties as well as the get/set source/type methods. fireEvent() in Evented needs to create an instance of this object prior to firing event notifications.""""""",Bug,"Title: Implement Ti.Event
Description: """"Need to implement Ti.Event, specifically an instantiable (declare) object that wraps a mixin of source, type, and custom event properties as well as the get/set source/type methods. fireEvent() in Evented needs to create an instance of this object prior to firing event notifications.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7085,12,"""MobileWeb: Code coverage tool""","""""""Build a tool to determine API code coverage and parity with other platforms. This tool will likely be written in Python or JavaScript running on node.js.  It may or may not benefit from the AST parser.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Code coverage tool
Description: """"Build a tool to determine API code coverage and parity with other platforms. This tool will likely be written in Python or JavaScript running on node.js. It may or may not benefit from the AST parser.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7084,12,"""Ti API: Ti.Filesystem.File.getParent returns incompatible types in iOS, Android""","""""""On Android, Ti.Filesystem.File.parent is a property of type File, so getParent returns a File object.    On iOS, there's no parent property, but there is a getParent method, which returns the parent's path, as a String.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti API: Ti.Filesystem.File.getParent returns incompatible types in iOS, Android
Description: """"On Android, Ti.Filesystem.File.parent is a property of type File, so getParent returns a File object. On iOS, there's no parent property, but there is a getParent method, which returns the parent's path, as a String.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7083,12,"""MobileWeb: Add has() control around shim code""","""""""Use has() control blocks around shim code to allow compiler to more easily strip it out if need be.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Add has() control around shim code
Description: """"Use has() control blocks around shim code to allow compiler to more easily strip it out if need be.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7082,12,"""MobileWeb: Display warning message when running in old unsupported browsers""","""""""Detect if the browser is capable of running Titanium and if not, display a message warning the user. This screen should be easily customizable by the developer. The browser detection should happen after the loader but before the project's app.js is downloaded.    Create a default warning template with no dependencies (i.e. inline images, styles, etc) in the mobileweb/src directory.    At compile time, if the Resources folder does NOT contain an overriding template, then use the default warning.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Display warning message when running in old unsupported browsers
Description: """"Detect if the browser is capable of running Titanium and if not, display a message warning the user. This screen should be easily customizable by the developer. The browser detection should happen after the loader but before the project's app.js is downloaded. Create a default warning template with no dependencies (i.e. inline images, styles, etc) in the mobileweb/src directory. At compile time, if the Resources folder does NOT contain an overriding template, then use the default warning.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7081,12,"""Android: toBlob on imageView causes runtime error with an invalid resource""","""""""Run the following code:        NOTE: make sure the resource 'images/schat.png' does not exist    Expected:  No runtime error. It should be a white screen without an image    Actual:  JS runtime error occurs""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: toBlob on imageView causes runtime error with an invalid resource
Description: """"Run the following code: NOTE: make sure the resource 'images/schat.png' does not exist Expected: No runtime error. It should be a white screen without an image Actual: JS runtime error occurs""""",title+description
TIMOB-7080,12,"""MobileWeb: Move inlined """"cached"""" modules from loader.js into individual files""","""""""The loader.js has a require.cache() after the loader definition that is supposed to be dynamically generated at compile time. These inlined modules are meant to be moved into external files for better maintainability.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Move inlined """"cached"""" modules from loader.js into individual files
Description: """"The loader.js has a require.cache() after the loader definition that is supposed to be dynamically generated at compile time. These inlined modules are meant to be moved into external files for better maintainability.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7079,12,"""MobileWeb: Support new UI layout API spec""","""""""Titanium has a new UI layout spec that mobile web needs to conform to: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/spe/UI+Layout+API+Spec""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Support new UI layout API spec
Description: """"Titanium has a new UI layout spec that mobile web needs to conform to: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/spe/UI+Layout+API+Spec""""",title+description
TIMOB-7078,12,"""MobileWeb: Cache modules using local storage""","""""""When modules are require()'d, the can be cached in local storage. We may want to implement this as either an AMD plugin or directly into the loader itself. Either way, there needs to be a way to enable/disable it, as well as bypass if needed.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Cache modules using local storage
Description: """"When modules are require()'d, the can be cached in local storage. We may want to implement this as either an AMD plugin or directly into the loader itself. Either way, there needs to be a way to enable/disable it, as well as bypass if needed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7077,12,"""MobileWeb: Create a Mobile Web Inspector""","""""""Build a """"""""mobile web inspector"""""""" that would popup in a window on load and allow developers to show the Ti element tree, inspect individual Ti elements, events, view console output, loaded modules, cache status, Ti.Database browser, Ti.Filesystem browser, Ti.Network traffic, resize window, and search.    This inspector would only be visible when in """"""""development"""""""" mode.    For desktop browsers, the inspector would be a separate browser window. For devices, we may choose to not support device debugging, create a bridge to a desktop browser, or use a dialog (which would obscure the view).""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Create a Mobile Web Inspector
Description: """"Build a """"""""mobile web inspector"""""""" that would popup in a window on load and allow developers to show the Ti element tree, inspect individual Ti elements, events, view console output, loaded modules, cache status, Ti.Database browser, Ti.Filesystem browser, Ti.Network traffic, resize window, and search. This inspector would only be visible when in """"""""development"""""""" mode. For desktop browsers, the inspector would be a separate browser window. For devices, we may choose to not support device debugging, create a bridge to a desktop browser, or use a dialog (which would obscure the view).""""",title+description
TIMOB-7076,12,"""MobileWeb: Label text gets clipped by label region""","""""""Need to properly determine the font height for labels with height=auto so that certain letters (gjpqy) don't get clipped.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Label text gets clipped by label region
Description: """"Need to properly determine the font height for labels with height=auto so that certain letters (gjpqy) don't get clipped.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7075,12,"""MobileWeb: Cancel animations when a UI element is destroyed""","""""""When a UI element is animating and then is destroyed, make sure the callback is not fired. Need to experiment with removing the transition end event and with removing the transition settings from the element node.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Cancel animations when a UI element is destroyed
Description: """"When a UI element is animating and then is destroyed, make sure the callback is not fired. Need to experiment with removing the transition end event and with removing the transition settings from the element node.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7074,12,"""Parity: Default images are different in iOS and Android""","""""""Right now the default behavior for images in annotations is different in iOS and android.  Android defaults to the pin image property, and iOS shows a red pin.  For reproduction steps, I would refer to [this| http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6895?focusedCommentId=177491&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-177491]  You will need to tweak the image property to be an invalid resource.""""""",Bug,"Title: Parity: Default images are different in iOS and Android
Description: """"Right now the default behavior for images in annotations is different in iOS and android. Android defaults to the pin image property, and iOS shows a red pin. For reproduction steps, I would refer to [this| http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6895?focusedCommentId=177491&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-177491] You will need to tweak the image property to be an invalid resource.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7073,12,"""API: Default behavior for map pins""","""""""As per ticket TIMOB-6967 and [PR 1149|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1149] we need to discuss default behavior for map pins, and how they behave when {{image}} or {{color}} (or both) is invalid.""""""",Bug,"Title: API: Default behavior for map pins
Description: """"As per ticket TIMOB-6967 and [PR 1149|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1149] we need to discuss default behavior for map pins, and how they behave when {{image}} or {{color}} (or both) is invalid.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7072,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Yahoo has incorrect module name""","""""""Ti.Yahoo's module name should be """"""""Ti/Yahoo"""""""", not """"""""Ti/Utils"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Yahoo has incorrect module name
Description: """"Ti.Yahoo's module name should be """"""""Ti/Yahoo"""""""", not """"""""Ti/Utils"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-7071,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.XML has incorrect module name""","""""""Ti.XML's module name should be """"""""Ti/XML"""""""", not """"""""Ti/Utils"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.XML has incorrect module name
Description: """"Ti.XML's module name should be """"""""Ti/XML"""""""", not """"""""Ti/Utils"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-7070,12,"""Tooling: Android builder.py - rename simulator argument to make more intuitive""","""""""h2. Problem    The {{simulator}} argument that the Android {{build.py}} script accepts may cause confusion for users who presume that it relates to the ios Simulator:    {code:lang=none}  appcel@shatner-ubuntu:~/.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/1.8.0.1/android$ ./builder.py   builder.py <command> <project_name> <sdk_dir> <project_dir> <app_id> [key] [password] [alias] [dir] [avdid] [avdsdk]    available commands:       emulator      build and run the emulator    simulator     build and run the app on the simulator    install       build and install the app on the device    distribute    build final distribution package for upload to marketplace    run           build and run the project using values from tiapp.xml    run-emulator  run the emulator with a default AVD ID and skin  {code}    As agreed by Opie and Marshall, it would be good to rename this to something more intuitive.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: Android builder.py - rename simulator argument to make more intuitive
Description: """"h2. Problem The {{simulator}} argument that the Android {{build.py}} script accepts may cause confusion for users who presume that it relates to the ios Simulator: {code:lang=none} appcel@shatner-ubuntu:~/.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/1.8.0.1/android$ ./builder.py builder.py <command> <project_name> <sdk_dir> <project_dir> <app_id> [key] [password] [alias] [dir] [avdid] [avdsdk] available commands: emulator build and run the emulator simulator build and run the app on the simulator install build and install the app on the device distribute build final distribution package for upload to marketplace run build and run the project using values from tiapp.xml run-emulator run the emulator with a default AVD ID and skin {code} As agreed by Opie and Marshall, it would be good to rename this to something more intuitive. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7069,12,"""MobileWeb: Support for compiling Ti+ modules into projects""","""""""While mobileweb has support for Ti+ modules, the only way to load them is to drop them into the project's Resources folder.  The support/mobileweb/compiler.py needs to detect required modules in the tiapp.xml, then locate them in the Titanium """"""""modules"""""""" directory, then add them to the build.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Support for compiling Ti+ modules into projects
Description: """"While mobileweb has support for Ti+ modules, the only way to load them is to drop them into the project's Resources folder. The support/mobileweb/compiler.py needs to detect required modules in the tiapp.xml, then locate them in the Titanium """"""""modules"""""""" directory, then add them to the build.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7068,12,"""MobileWeb: Define Ti module by merging titanium.js and Ti/ti.js into Ti.js""","""""""The Ti namespace is defined by Ti/ti.js, but this is the incorrect filename and file location.  It should be moved from mobileweb/src/Ti/ti.js to mobileweb/src/Ti.js.  Since this overlaps with titanium.js, merge the two together.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Define Ti module by merging titanium.js and Ti/ti.js into Ti.js
Description: """"The Ti namespace is defined by Ti/ti.js, but this is the incorrect filename and file location. It should be moved from mobileweb/src/Ti/ti.js to mobileweb/src/Ti.js. Since this overlaps with titanium.js, merge the two together.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7067,12,"""MobileWeb: Build time dependency bundling""","""""""During build time, scan the project's code for all Ti APIs used and build a dependency map. Using this dependency map, assemble the files into a single file. This should be done in support/mobileweb/compiler.py. Also remove the unneeded map.prop file.    This should be accomplished using the AST parser.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Build time dependency bundling
Description: """"During build time, scan the project's code for all Ti APIs used and build a dependency map. Using this dependency map, assemble the files into a single file. This should be done in support/mobileweb/compiler.py. Also remove the unneeded map.prop file. This should be accomplished using the AST parser.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7066,12,"""MobileWeb: Convert APIs from old syntax to new declare()/setObject() syntax""","""""""There are a number of APIs that still need to be rewritten to use the new declare() or setObject() functions:    * Ti/Accelerometer.js  * -Ti/Analytics.js- DONE!  * -Ti/API.js- DONE!  * -Ti/App.js- DONE!  * -Ti/App/Properties.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Blob.js- DONE!  * Ti/Database.js  * Ti/Database/DB.js  * Ti/Database/ResultSet.js  * -Ti/Facebook.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Facebook/LoginButton.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Filesystem.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Filesystem/File.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Geolocation.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Locale.js- DONE!  * Ti/Map.js  * Ti/Map/Annotation.js  * Ti/Map/MapView.js  * Ti/Media/AudioPlayer.js  * Ti/Media/Sound.js  * -Ti/Network.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Network/HTTPClient.js- DONE!  * -Ti/Utils.js- Done!  * -Ti/XML.js- DONE!  * Ti/Yahoo.js""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Convert APIs from old syntax to new declare()/setObject() syntax
Description: """"There are a number of APIs that still need to be rewritten to use the new declare() or setObject() functions: * Ti/Accelerometer.js * -Ti/Analytics.js- DONE! * -Ti/API.js- DONE! * -Ti/App.js- DONE! * -Ti/App/Properties.js- DONE! * -Ti/Blob.js- DONE! * Ti/Database.js * Ti/Database/DB.js * Ti/Database/ResultSet.js * -Ti/Facebook.js- DONE! * -Ti/Facebook/LoginButton.js- DONE! * -Ti/Filesystem.js- DONE! * -Ti/Filesystem/File.js- DONE! * -Ti/Geolocation.js- DONE! * -Ti/Locale.js- DONE! * Ti/Map.js * Ti/Map/Annotation.js * Ti/Map/MapView.js * Ti/Media/AudioPlayer.js * Ti/Media/Sound.js * -Ti/Network.js- DONE! * -Ti/Network/HTTPClient.js- DONE! * -Ti/Utils.js- Done! * -Ti/XML.js- DONE! * Ti/Yahoo.js""""",title+description
