TIMOB-7058,12,"""MobileWeb: loadstate event in Ti.Media.VideoPlayer not correctly lowercase""","""""""Ti.Media.VideoPlayer has the load state event as """"""""loadState"""""""" instead of """"""""loadstate"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: loadstate event in Ti.Media.VideoPlayer not correctly lowercase
Description: """"Ti.Media.VideoPlayer has the load state event as """"""""loadState"""""""" instead of """"""""loadstate"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-7057,12,"""Ti.API: UI - prohibit child views being added to views other than UI.Window and UI.View""","""""""h2. Problem    Currently, Android silently ignores a label added to an imageView, whereas iOS accepts and shows the label. Test this using the code below.    From what I understand, only Ti.UI.View and Ti.UI.Window should accept child views.  Hence, this ticket requests parity between the two platforms.    My feeling is that an exception should be thrown on both platforms, to make the intended behavior clear to the user.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var imageview = Ti.UI.createImageView({    image:'KS_nav_views.png'  });  var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({    color:'#000',    text:'I am a label',    font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'},    textAlign:'center',    width:'auto'  });  imageview.add(label);  win.add(imageview);    win.open();  {code}    h2. References    See ticket TC-550, where this situation caused confusion.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Ti.API: UI - prohibit child views being added to views other than UI.Window and UI.View
Description: """"h2. Problem Currently, Android silently ignores a label added to an imageView, whereas iOS accepts and shows the label. Test this using the code below. From what I understand, only Ti.UI.View and Ti.UI.Window should accept child views. Hence, this ticket requests parity between the two platforms. My feeling is that an exception should be thrown on both platforms, to make the intended behavior clear to the user. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var imageview = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image:'KS_nav_views.png' }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color:'#000', text:'I am a label', font:{fontSize:20,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'}, textAlign:'center', width:'auto' }); imageview.add(label); win.add(imageview); win.open(); {code} h2. References See ticket TC-550, where this situation caused confusion.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7056,12,"""TiMob: imageView - support a base64 string as a valid image in the image property""","""""""Doing this will allow devs to share/re-use commonJS modules that need graphics (like for custom UI elements) without worrying about image file paths or if all the images were copied over to the new project.    Based on my research, this should be able to be done in under 5 lines of code.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiMob: imageView - support a base64 string as a valid image in the image property
Description: """"Doing this will allow devs to share/re-use commonJS modules that need graphics (like for custom UI elements) without worrying about image file paths or if all the images were copied over to the new project. Based on my research, this should be able to be done in under 5 lines of code. """"",title+description
TIMOB-7054,12,"""Change the default project to lose the KS images and simplify app.js""","""""""We're working on new templates to roll out in Studio - to help support this effort, the current artifacts that are generated for new projects needs to be pared down a bit.  app.js should be very minimal, and we should drop the kitchen sink tab group images, so that less """"""""junk"""""""" is left when project templates are used.""""""",Story,"Title: Change the default project to lose the KS images and simplify app.js
Description: """"We're working on new templates to roll out in Studio - to help support this effort, the current artifacts that are generated for new projects needs to be pared down a bit. app.js should be very minimal, and we should drop the kitchen sink tab group images, so that less """"""""junk"""""""" is left when project templates are used.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7053,12,"""Tooling: Android - when using Run on Device provide support for multiple devices""","""""""h2. Problem    Launching app on device using """"""""Run on device"""""""" results in error when multiple devices are connected at once.    I have a testbed of Android devices, and it would be nice to just have them all connected all the time (ie for charging purposes). Since adb allows you to get a list of attached devices, it seems that it would be simple enough for Titanium and/or Studio to prompt for a connected device, instead of erroring with the """"""""multiple devices"""""""" error, shown below.    h2. Steps to reproduce    * create default app  * connect 3 android devices to computer  * run on device  * see resulting error below    h2. Logs    The following is an excerpt from the attached {{build.log}}    {code:lang=none|title=build.log}  [DEBUG] Waiting for device to be ready ...  [TRACE] adb devices returned 3 devices/emulators  [DEBUG] Device connected... (waited 0 seconds)  [DEBUG] waited 0.021664 seconds on emulator to get ready  [INFO] Installing application on emulator  [DEBUG] /android-sdk-macosx/platform-tools/adb -d install -r /Users/shan/Dropbox/dev/NEIRA-mobile/build/android/bin/app.apk  [ERROR] error: more than one device  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Android - when using Run on Device provide support for multiple devices
Description: """"h2. Problem Launching app on device using """"""""Run on device"""""""" results in error when multiple devices are connected at once. I have a testbed of Android devices, and it would be nice to just have them all connected all the time (ie for charging purposes). Since adb allows you to get a list of attached devices, it seems that it would be simple enough for Titanium and/or Studio to prompt for a connected device, instead of erroring with the """"""""multiple devices"""""""" error, shown below. h2. Steps to reproduce * create default app * connect 3 android devices to computer * run on device * see resulting error below h2. Logs The following is an excerpt from the attached {{build.log}} {code:lang=none|title=build.log} [DEBUG] Waiting for device to be ready ... [TRACE] adb devices returned 3 devices/emulators [DEBUG] Device connected... (waited 0 seconds) [DEBUG] waited 0.021664 seconds on emulator to get ready [INFO] Installing application on emulator [DEBUG] /android-sdk-macosx/platform-tools/adb -d install -r /Users/shan/Dropbox/dev/NEIRA-mobile/build/android/bin/app.apk [ERROR] error: more than one device {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-7051,12,"""iOS: UI.imageView - changing image property results in memory leak""","""""""h2. Problem    I have an ImageView, clicking on the right, i want to change its image to the next image, clicking to the left, to the previous image, for browsing 50 images.    Changing the {{image}} property of the imageView causes a memory leak which never recovers when using 1.8.0.1.    Note that there is no memory leak when using 1.7.5.      h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  (function(){    var screenWidth = Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth;    Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');       var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor:'#000000',     fullscreen: true    });       win.open();       var currentImage=1;    var max = 20;       var myImageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({     image: 'img/'+currentImage+'.jpg',     touchEnabled:false    });    win.add(myImageView);       function setImage(view, image){     view.image = 'img/'+image+'.jpg';    }       win.addEventListener('click', function(e){     if(e.x > (screenWidth/2)){     currentImage++;     if (currentImage>max) {     currentImage=1;     }     } else {     currentImage--;     if(currentImage<1){     currentImage=max;     }     }         setImage(win.children[0], currentImage);         Ti.API.info(""""""""memory = """"""""+Ti.Platform.availableMemory);    });       setInterval(function() {    win.fireEvent('click');   }, 100);  })();       {code:lang=none|title=console using 1.7.5}  [INFO] One moment, building ...  [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.7.5  [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal  [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0  [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone  [INFO] Performing full rebuild. This will take a little bit. Hold tight...  [INFO] Skipping JS compile, running from simulator  [INFO] Performing clean build  [INFO] Launching application in Simulator  [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (12.99 seconds)  [INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed  [INFO] Application started  [INFO] ImageViewTest/1.0 (1.7.5.ab20af7)  [INFO] memory = 3165.79296875  [INFO] memory = 3153.82421875  [INFO] memory = 3154.390625  [INFO] memory = 3154.45703125  [INFO] memory = 3154.53515625  [INFO] memory = 3154.6015625  [INFO] memory = 3154.66015625  [INFO] memory = 3152.76953125  [INFO] memory = 3152.890625  [INFO] memory = 3152.98046875  [INFO] memory = 3153.0703125  [INFO] memory = 3157.1953125  {code}    h2. Workaround    Although it's depreciated, using the {{url}} instead of {{image}} property resolves the issue.    h2. Discussions    Q&A: [changing image of an imageview does not free memory|http://developer.<USER>com/question/130317/changing-image-of-an-imageview-does-not-free-memory]""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI.imageView - changing image property results in memory leak
Description: """"h2. Problem I have an ImageView, clicking on the right, i want to change its image to the next image, clicking to the left, to the previous image, for browsing 50 images. Changing the {{image}} property of the imageView causes a memory leak which never recovers when using 1.8.0.1. Note that there is no memory leak when using 1.7.5. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} (function(){ var screenWidth = Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth; Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#000000', fullscreen: true }); win.open(); var currentImage=1; var max = 20; var myImageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'img/'+currentImage+'.jpg', touchEnabled:false }); win.add(myImageView); function setImage(view, image){ view.image = 'img/'+image+'.jpg'; } win.addEventListener('click', function(e){ if(e.x > (screenWidth/2)){ currentImage++; if (currentImage>max) { currentImage=1; } } else { currentImage--; if(currentImage<1){ currentImage=max; } } setImage(win.children[0], currentImage); Ti.API.info(""""""""memory = """"""""+Ti.Platform.availableMemory); }); setInterval(function() { win.fireEvent('click'); }, 100); })(); {code:lang=none|title=console using 1.7.5} [INFO] One moment, building ... [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.7.5 [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0 [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone [INFO] Performing full rebuild. This will take a little bit. Hold tight... [INFO] Skipping JS compile, running from simulator [INFO] Performing clean build [INFO] Launching application in Simulator [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (12.99 seconds) [INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed [INFO] Application started [INFO] ImageViewTest/1.0 (1.7.5.ab20af7) [INFO] memory = 3165.79296875 [INFO] memory = 3153.82421875 [INFO] memory = 3154.390625 [INFO] memory = 3154.45703125 [INFO] memory = 3154.53515625 [INFO] memory = 3154.6015625 [INFO] memory = 3154.66015625 [INFO] memory = 3152.76953125 [INFO] memory = 3152.890625 [INFO] memory = 3152.98046875 [INFO] memory = 3153.0703125 [INFO] memory = 3157.1953125 {code} h2. Workaround Although it's depreciated, using the {{url}} instead of {{image}} property resolves the issue. h2. Discussions Q&A: [changing image of an imageview does not free memory|http://developer.<USER>com/question/130317/changing-image-of-an-imageview-does-not-free-memory]""""",title+description
TIMOB-7049,12,"""MobileWeb: Controls are overzealous about triggering a doFullLayout() call""","""""""Some controls, such as label, trigger a full layout under certain circumstances, such as changing the text for a label. These controls need to be more efficient and only trigger a layout change if the dimensions of the control will actually change.    Similarly, controls can trigger a layout even if they are in an inactive window or are not attached to a window. Need to track if a control is in an active window or not.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Controls are overzealous about triggering a doFullLayout() call
Description: """"Some controls, such as label, trigger a full layout under certain circumstances, such as changing the text for a label. These controls need to be more efficient and only trigger a layout change if the dimensions of the control will actually change. Similarly, controls can trigger a layout even if they are in an inactive window or are not attached to a window. Need to track if a control is in an active window or not.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7048,12,"""MobileWeb: Scope full layout calculations to the active window""","""""""The internal _doFullLayout() computes layouts for ALL UI elements, regardless of which window is active and opened.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Scope full layout calculations to the active window
Description: """"The internal _doFullLayout() computes layouts for ALL UI elements, regardless of which window is active and opened.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7047,12,"""MobileWeb: Use correct integer values for Ti.Media constants""","""""""The Ti.Media constants are not the same as iOS and Android and must be set to the same values for places where apps are doing comparisons based on the real integer values instead of the constants.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Use correct integer values for Ti.Media constants
Description: """"The Ti.Media constants are not the same as iOS and Android and must be set to the same values for places where apps are doing comparisons based on the real integer values instead of the constants.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7046,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Media.VideoPlayer video times must be in milliseconds, not seconds""","""""""HTML5 video times are all in seconds, but Titanium's video player is in milliseconds.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Media.VideoPlayer video times must be in milliseconds, not seconds
Description: """"HTML5 video times are all in seconds, but Titanium's video player is in milliseconds.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7045,12,"""MobileWeb: Text fields sometimes cannot regain focus""","""""""In certain scenarios, once a text field looses it's (default) focus, it cannot be regained.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Text fields sometimes cannot regain focus
Description: """"In certain scenarios, once a text field looses it's (default) focus, it cannot be regained.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7044,12,"""MobileWeb: Implement touch events and guestures""","""""""Need to implement support for mouse/touch events other than click and double click. Also, some controls report more information than the parent control, so need to ensure parity.    This will likely go in a base class Ti._.PointerEvents.    Must implement the following Ti events:  * click  * dblclick  * doubletap  * longclick  * longpress  * pinch  * singletap  * swipe  * touchcancel  * touchend  * touchmove  * touchstart  * twofingertap  """"""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Implement touch events and guestures
Description: """"Need to implement support for mouse/touch events other than click and double click. Also, some controls report more information than the parent control, so need to ensure parity. This will likely go in a base class Ti._.PointerEvents. Must implement the following Ti events: * click * dblclick * doubletap * longclick * longpress * pinch * singletap * swipe * touchcancel * touchend * touchmove * touchstart * twofingertap """"",title+description
TIMOB-7043,12,"""MobileWeb: Allow directories named """"iphone"""" and """"android""""""","""""""If an app has a directory called """"""""iphone"""""""" or """"""""android"""""""", it's copied to the build directory even if it is valid.  Just need copy iphone and android folders.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Allow directories named """"iphone"""" and """"android""""
Description: """"If an app has a directory called """"""""iphone"""""""" or """"""""android"""""""", it's copied to the build directory even if it is valid. Just need copy iphone and android folders.""""",title+description
TIMOB-7041,12,"""iOS: getAttribute value from XML does not work in 1.8.0.1""","""""""h3. Problem    GetAttribute value from XML does not work in 1.8.0.1    h3. Reproducible steps:     1. Run the code below with 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK.  Please see the 1.8.0.1 attached image.    2. Run the the code below with 1.7.5 Titanium SDK.  Please see the 1.7.5 attached image.    Notice that in 1.7.5 Titanium SDK the the value is displayed on the window.    h3. Expected behavior:  Customer wants to have the same behavior in 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK.    h3. Tested with the next specs:    Simulator    iPhone 4  Version of the device: 5.0.1    Titanium Studio, build: 1.0.8.201112291658  Titanium SDK: 1.8.0.1 & 1.7.5    h3. Console Logs:    {code: title=1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK  & 2.3.3-Bad Behavior}  1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK.[INFO] One moment, building ...[INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.0.1 (12/22/11 13:09 fbdc96f)[INFO] iPhone Device family: universal  [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0[INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone  [INFO] Launching application in Simulator  [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (1.71 seconds)[INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed  [INFO] Application started  [INFO] v1.8 Demo/1.0 (1.8.0.1.fbdc96f)[INFO] Loaded  [INFO] [object TiDOMNodeList][INFO] 0[INFO] 26      h3. Code:  {Code}  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({   title: 'Tab 1',   backgroundColor: '#fff'});  var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({   color: '#999',   text: '',   font: {     fontSize: 20,     fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue'      },   textAlign: 'center',   width: 'auto'});win1.add(label1);    var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient();  xhr.onerror = function(e)   { Ti.API.error('Error received while requesting library data: ' + JSON.stringify(e));  };    xhr.onload = function()   { if (this.readyState == 4)    {    var xmldoc = this.responseXML.documentElement;    Ti.API.info('Loaded');    Ti.API.info(xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('archive')); //This line of code says that the archive tag is detected    Ti.API.info(xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('archive').length); // this line says that it recieves an archive tag with no nodes    Ti.API.info(xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('media').length); // this line says it recieves 26 nodes for """"""""media"""""""" tag which is a child of """"""""archive"""""""" tag    label1.text = 'XML Version : ' + xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('archive').item(0).getAttribute('version');   }};  xhr.open('GET', 'http://apps.<USER>com/Kingfisher-IR/Library.xml');  xhr.send();  win1.open();  {Code}    h3. Helpdesk  APP-697182                           """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: getAttribute value from XML does not work in 1.8.0.1
Description: """"h3. Problem GetAttribute value from XML does not work in 1.8.0.1 h3. Reproducible steps: 1. Run the code below with 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK. Please see the 1.8.0.1 attached image. 2. Run the the code below with 1.7.5 Titanium SDK. Please see the 1.7.5 attached image. Notice that in 1.7.5 Titanium SDK the the value is displayed on the window. h3. Expected behavior: Customer wants to have the same behavior in 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK. h3. Tested with the next specs: Simulator iPhone 4 Version of the device: 5.0.1 Titanium Studio, build: 1.0.8.201112291658 Titanium SDK: 1.8.0.1 & 1.7.5 h3. Console Logs: {code: title=1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK & 2.3.3-Bad Behavior} 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK.[INFO] One moment, building ...[INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.0.1 (12/22/11 13:09 fbdc96f)[INFO] iPhone Device family: universal [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0[INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone [INFO] Launching application in Simulator [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (1.71 seconds)[INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed [INFO] Application started [INFO] v1.8 Demo/1.0 (1.8.0.1.fbdc96f)[INFO] Loaded [INFO] [object TiDOMNodeList][INFO] 0[INFO] 26 h3. Code: {Code} var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Tab 1', backgroundColor: '#fff'}); var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({ color: '#999', text: '', font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' }, textAlign: 'center', width: 'auto'});win1.add(label1); var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onerror = function(e) { Ti.API.error('Error received while requesting library data: ' + JSON.stringify(e)); }; xhr.onload = function() { if (this.readyState == 4) { var xmldoc = this.responseXML.documentElement; Ti.API.info('Loaded'); Ti.API.info(xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('archive')); //This line of code says that the archive tag is detected Ti.API.info(xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('archive').length); // this line says that it recieves an archive tag with no nodes Ti.API.info(xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('media').length); // this line says it recieves 26 nodes for """"""""media"""""""" tag which is a child of """"""""archive"""""""" tag label1.text = 'XML Version : ' + xmldoc.getElementsByTagName('archive').item(0).getAttribute('version'); }}; xhr.open('GET', 'http://apps.<USER>com/Kingfisher-IR/Library.xml'); xhr.send(); win1.open(); {Code} h3. Helpdesk APP-697182 """"",title+description
TIMOB-7040,12,"""iOS: Coverflow - navigating away then back to a coverflow results in redraw and sorting issues""","""""""h4.Issue  Images shown in Coverflow has redraw issues if navigating till its end then back from another app tab (As seen in the Kitchen Sink)    h6.Tested on  iPhone 5.0.1  Titanium SDK 1.8.0.1     h6.Steps to reproduce  1.base ui > views> coverflow view> either coverflow local or replace images  2.tap the right arrow until you reach the end of the images  3.tap another tab, wait a second or two  4.tap the base UI tab and check out the screen    h6.results: (screen shot) images are not shown as expected, seems the order is off as well.      h6.Additional data  The picture shows an iPhone 4.3, and an iPhone 5.0.1 on the right""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Coverflow - navigating away then back to a coverflow results in redraw and sorting issues
Description: """"h4.Issue Images shown in Coverflow has redraw issues if navigating till its end then back from another app tab (As seen in the Kitchen Sink) h6.Tested on iPhone 5.0.1 Titanium SDK 1.8.0.1 h6.Steps to reproduce 1.base ui > views> coverflow view> either coverflow local or replace images 2.tap the right arrow until you reach the end of the images 3.tap another tab, wait a second or two 4.tap the base UI tab and check out the screen h6.results: (screen shot) images are not shown as expected, seems the order is off as well. h6.Additional data The picture shows an iPhone 4.3, and an iPhone 5.0.1 on the right""""",title+description
