Description: """"h3. Problem The image path lost his reference after doing a require and export. h3. Reproducible steps: 1. Run the attached code with 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK. Please see the 1.8.0.1 attached image. 2. Run the attached code with 1.7.5 Titanium SDK. Please see the 1.7.5 attached image. Notice that in 1.7.5 Titanium SDK the all images are displayed well on the first window. h3. Expected behavior: Customer wants to have the same behavior in 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK like the 1.7.5 attached image. h3. More info: The images are displayed well in 1.7.5 Titanium SDK. h3. Tested with the next specs: Simulator Android version : 2.3.3 iPhone 4 Version of the device: 5.0.1 Titanium Studio, build: 1.0.8.201112291658 Titanium SDK: 1.8.0.1 & 1.7.5 Samsung Fit Android version of the device: 2.2.1 {code: title=1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK & Android 2.3.3-Bad Behavior} 1.8.0.1 Titanium SDK 01-05 12:56:10.154: I/DEBUG(31): debuggerd: Feb 3 2011 14:45:34 01-05 12:56:10.194: D/qemud(38): entering main loop 01-05 12:56:10.234: I/Vold(29): Vold 2.1 (the revenge) firing up 01-05 12:56:10.234: D/Vold(29): USB mass storage support is not enabled in the kernel 01-05 12:56:10.234: D/Vold(29): usb_configuration switch is not enabled in the kernel 01-05 12:56:10.234: D/Vold(29): Volume sdcard state changing -1 (Initializing) -> 0 (No-Media) 01-05 12:56:10.264: I/Netd(30): Netd 1.0 starting 01-05 12:56:10.583: D/Vold(29): Volume sdcard state changing 0 (No-Media) -> 1 (Idle-Unmounted) 01-05 12:56:10.734: D/qemud(38): fdhandler_accept_event: accepting on fd 9 01-05 12:56:10.734: D/qemud(38): created client 0xe078 listening on fd 10 01-05 12:56:10.754: D/qemud(38): client_fd_receive: attempting registration for service 'boot-properties' 01-05 12:56:10.754: D/qemud(38): client_fd_receive: -> received channel id 1 01-05 12:56:10.764: D/qemud(38): client_registration: registration succeeded for client 1 01-05 12:56:10.764: I/qemu-props(53): connected to 'boot-properties' qemud service. 01-05 12:56:10