TIMOB-6969,12,"""iOS: Database.DB - implement remove() method""","""""""The [DB|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Database.DB-object] remove() method exists in Android (see [source|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/database/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/database/TiDatabaseProxy.java#L182]) but not in iOS.    This ticket requests parity.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Database.DB - implement remove() method
Description: """"The [DB|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Database.DB-object] remove() method exists in Android (see [source|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/android/modules/database/src/java/ti/modules/titanium/database/TiDatabaseProxy.java#L182]) but not in iOS. This ticket requests parity. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6967,12,"""Android - add blob support for Ti.map.annotation.image""","""""""for Ti.Map.Annotation you should be able to set the image property to a blob in order to support dynamic annotation creation. Right now it only accepts a URL to an image file.    Comment from customer:    We're facing a technical challenge that can actually make or break us at this point. We have a deadline at the end of january to build a mobile app in titanium that can closely mimic our current app for iOS.    Our problem: We need the ability to add labels with dynamic text to annotations. We would actually love to be able to add views to the  annotation view but labels would be enough for our current needs.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android - add blob support for Ti.map.annotation.image
Description: """"for Ti.Map.Annotation you should be able to set the image property to a blob in order to support dynamic annotation creation. Right now it only accepts a URL to an image file. Comment from customer: We're facing a technical challenge that can actually make or break us at this point. We have a deadline at the end of january to build a mobile app in titanium that can closely mimic our current app for iOS. Our problem: We need the ability to add labels with dynamic text to annotations. We would actually love to be able to add views to the annotation view but labels would be enough for our current needs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6966,12,"""iOS: titanium_prep file is 64 bits only""","""""""h4. PROBLEM  The titanium_prep distributed with the mobile sdk is 64 bits only.     h4. TEST CASE  1. Open Terminal  2. Type:  $ cd  /Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.0.1/iphone  $ ./titanium_prep   you will get: -bash: ./titanium_prep: Bad CPU type in executable  (if you are running on an intel core duo)    h4. Community discusion  http://developer.<USER>com/question/130172/iphone-app-hang-after-distribution-build""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: titanium_prep file is 64 bits only
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM The titanium_prep distributed with the mobile sdk is 64 bits only. h4. TEST CASE 1. Open Terminal 2. Type: $ cd /Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.0.1/iphone $ ./titanium_prep you will get: -bash: ./titanium_prep: Bad CPU type in executable (if you are running on an intel core duo) h4. Community discusion http://developer.<USER>com/question/130172/iphone-app-hang-after-distribution-build""""",title+description
TIMOB-6965,12,"""Console keeps showing old outputs""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer's console is stucked with the output of a previous run. From the Customer: """"""""for some days now Studio's console shows output from a project I worked on some days ago. When I work on any other project its output will show correctly but often the old output from that other project instantly returns and I can't see the output I need at this moment.""""""""    h4. EXTRA INFO  I asked the customer to try different workarounds (none of them solved the issue):    1. Press the button marked with the red arrow in the attachment. The one that says """"""""Remove all terminated launches"""""""".  2. Run ./studio3 -clean  3. Rename the offending project  4. Remove the offending project  5. Update to the latest version  6. Delete all configurations related to the project    No succes at all. """"""",Bug,"Title: Console keeps showing old outputs
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer's console is stucked with the output of a previous run. From the Customer: """"""""for some days now Studio's console shows output from a project I worked on some days ago. When I work on any other project its output will show correctly but often the old output from that other project instantly returns and I can't see the output I need at this moment."""""""" h4. EXTRA INFO I asked the customer to try different workarounds (none of them solved the issue): 1. Press the button marked with the red arrow in the attachment. The one that says """"""""Remove all terminated launches"""""""". 2. Run ./studio3 -clean 3. Rename the offending project 4. Remove the offending project 5. Update to the latest version 6. Delete all configurations related to the project No succes at all. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6964,12,"""iOS: Establish code guidelines and source beautifier""","""""""iOS needs to establish code guidelines and a source beautifying tool so that we can begin code cleanup and encourage new people working on the source to follow convention rather than paradigms from other languages or currently incorrect methodologies in the iOS codebase.    We will also eventually want a clang AST plugin to perform tasks such as variable name analysis to ensure that everybody is following the right naming rules (camelcase, trailing underscore in args only, etc.) which could probably be integrated with the API metrics to provide some better information.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Establish code guidelines and source beautifier
Description: """"iOS needs to establish code guidelines and a source beautifying tool so that we can begin code cleanup and encourage new people working on the source to follow convention rather than paradigms from other languages or currently incorrect methodologies in the iOS codebase. We will also eventually want a clang AST plugin to perform tasks such as variable name analysis to ensure that everybody is following the right naming rules (camelcase, trailing underscore in args only, etc.) which could probably be integrated with the API metrics to provide some better information.""""",title+description
