TIMOB-6941,12,"""Android: Media - AudioPlayer progress event units of measure not consistent between 1.7.X and 1.8.0.X""","""""""h2. Problem    AudioPlayer progress event units of measure not consistent between 1.7.X and 1.8.0.X.    On 1.7.5 units are seconds  On 1.8.0.1 units are milliseconds    Is this a regression, or intended?    The APIDocs at [Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer.progress|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer.progress-property.html] do not explain which units are intended.    Note: this needs to be tested on iOS to ensure parity.    h2. Logs    The following logs are output when the test case below is run    {code:lang=none|title=1.8.0.1 / v8}  I/TiAPI   ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 1121  I/TiAPI   ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 2113  I/TiAPI   ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 3104  I/TiAPI   ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 4122  I/TiAPI   ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 5113      {code:lang=none|title=1.7.5 / Rhino}  I/TiAPI   ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [1005,12541] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 2.087  I/TiAPI   ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [998,13539] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 3.078  I/TiAPI   ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [1009,14548] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 4.07  I/TiAPI   ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [996,15544] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 5.061  I/TiAPI   ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [1000,16544] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 6.079  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Media - AudioPlayer progress event units of measure not consistent between 1.7.X and 1.8.0.X
Description: """"h2. Problem AudioPlayer progress event units of measure not consistent between 1.7.X and 1.8.0.X. On 1.7.5 units are seconds On 1.8.0.1 units are milliseconds Is this a regression, or intended? The APIDocs at [Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer.progress|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.AudioPlayer.progress-property.html] do not explain which units are intended. Note: this needs to be tested on iOS to ensure parity. h2. Logs The following logs are output when the test case below is run {code:lang=none|title=1.8.0.1 / v8} I/TiAPI ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 1121 I/TiAPI ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 2113 I/TiAPI ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 3104 I/TiAPI ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 4122 I/TiAPI ( 5265): EAC LOGGING: Progress: 5113 {code:lang=none|title=1.7.5 / Rhino} I/TiAPI ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [1005,12541] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 2.087 I/TiAPI ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [998,13539] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 3.078 I/TiAPI ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [1009,14548] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 4.07 I/TiAPI ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [996,15544] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 5.061 I/TiAPI ( 5614): (kroll$1: app://app.js) [1000,16544] EAC LOGGING: Progress: 6.079 """"",title+description
TIMOB-6940,12,"""Android: Remote image cache does not recognize missing files after activity.finish() and restart""","""""""h2. Problem    I write this code to clean built-in remote images cache on sd-card, it works, but if I exit app with back button or with activity.finish(), at the next restart all images in my tableview are broken (empty), like the app don't recognize that cache file is missing.    I need to kill app with task killer to have all works fine again.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  // delete cache files  var dir = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.externalStorageDirectory);   var cache_folder = dir.nativePath.toString()+'/remote-image-cache';  var deldir = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(cache_folder);   deldir.deleteDirectory(true);    // exit app  var activity = Titanium.Android.currentActivity;  activity.finish();     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Remote image cache does not recognize missing files after activity.finish() and restart
Description: """"h2. Problem I write this code to clean built-in remote images cache on sd-card, it works, but if I exit app with back button or with activity.finish(), at the next restart all images in my tableview are broken (empty), like the app don't recognize that cache file is missing. I need to kill app with task killer to have all works fine again. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} // delete cache files var dir = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.externalStorageDirectory); var cache_folder = dir.nativePath.toString()+'/remote-image-cache'; var deldir = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(cache_folder); deldir.deleteDirectory(true); // exit app var activity = Titanium.Android.currentActivity; activity.finish(); """"",title+description
TIMOB-6939,12,"""iOS: ScrollView - the ability to turn of animation when calling setContentOffset""","""""""Requesting the ability to turn off animation of the scrollView when calling setContentOffset.    This is the link for where it needs to be added. It is currently always true.  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIScrollView.m#L180""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: ScrollView - the ability to turn of animation when calling setContentOffset
Description: """"Requesting the ability to turn off animation of the scrollView when calling setContentOffset. This is the link for where it needs to be added. It is currently always true. https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIScrollView.m#L180""""",title+description
TIMOB-6938,12,"""iOS: Media - VideoPlayer fullscreen landscape video will not close window on complete event""","""""""h2. Expected Behavior  The application is restricted to starting in Portrait mode. When the user clicks a button, the video player will play an external video ( amazon s3 bucket file )  in landscape window mode.  The video file is a .m4v and is formatted for landscape dimension already. The """"""""complete"""""""" eventListener is attached to the video Player in the new window.  When adding and """"""""complete"""""""" event listener on the VideoPlayer, I should be able to run a window.close() and the root window will now be visible.     h2. Actual Behavior  The window will not close when the Done button is hit by user or the video play back ends.  Both conditions that are captured by the complete eventListener on the video player.    When playing the video in portrait mode, the window will close.  So I have narrowed it down to being in landscape mode only.    h2. Test Case    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  // create Window  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({});      var button = Ti.UI.createButton({    title: 'View Landscape Fullscreen Video',    width: 250,    height: 60   });   button.addEventListener('click', function(e){        var _win = Ti.UI.createWindow({     url: 'video-player.js'    });        _win.open({animated:true});       });     win.add(button);  win.open();        """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Media - VideoPlayer fullscreen landscape video will not close window on complete event
Description: """"h2. Expected Behavior The application is restricted to starting in Portrait mode. When the user clicks a button, the video player will play an external video ( amazon s3 bucket file ) in landscape window mode. The video file is a .m4v and is formatted for landscape dimension already. The """"""""complete"""""""" eventListener is attached to the video Player in the new window. When adding and """"""""complete"""""""" event listener on the VideoPlayer, I should be able to run a window.close() and the root window will now be visible. h2. Actual Behavior The window will not close when the Done button is hit by user or the video play back ends. Both conditions that are captured by the complete eventListener on the video player. When playing the video in portrait mode, the window will close. So I have narrowed it down to being in landscape mode only. h2. Test Case {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); // create Window var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({}); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'View Landscape Fullscreen Video', width: 250, height: 60 }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e){ var _win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ url: 'video-player.js' }); _win.open({animated:true}); }); win.add(button); win.open(); """"",title+description
TIMOB-6937,12,"""iOS: Pre-compile library for development to speed up application launch times from full compile""","""""""one of the things i would like to see to speed up development and the first run experience is a pre-compile of the dev library so that the first simulator launch is fast.  right now, each new project requires a full compile (with debug settings and all symbols included).     it would be nice for simulator only (can't use this for test on device or distribute since it will cause all symbols to be used) to be ship a pre-compiled .a/.jar that could be used for dev and fast launch.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Pre-compile library for development to speed up application launch times from full compile
Description: """"one of the things i would like to see to speed up development and the first run experience is a pre-compile of the dev library so that the first simulator launch is fast. right now, each new project requires a full compile (with debug settings and all symbols included). it would be nice for simulator only (can't use this for test on device or distribute since it will cause all symbols to be used) to be ship a pre-compiled .a/.jar that could be used for dev and fast launch.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6935,12,"""API: UI - determine platforms that will support buttonBar""","""""""Currently the buttonBar is an iOS-only feature. Are there plans to provide support in any other platforms (Android & Mobile Web)?    If it will remain iOS-only, then it needs to be moved to the UI.iOS namespace.    This ticket is to track the final decision, to allow us to begin work on the linked APIDoc ticket.""""""",Bug,"Title: API: UI - determine platforms that will support buttonBar
Description: """"Currently the buttonBar is an iOS-only feature. Are there plans to provide support in any other platforms (Android & Mobile Web)? If it will remain iOS-only, then it needs to be moved to the UI.iOS namespace. This ticket is to track the final decision, to allow us to begin work on the linked APIDoc ticket.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6932,12,"""iOS: Incorrect deprecation of Ti.Filesystem.File.writable""","""""""According to the Filesystem parity spec:    https://wiki.<USER>org/display/spe/Filesystem+Behavior+Parity    The """"""""writeable"""""""" property is supposed to be deprecated in favor of writable.    However, in the iOS code, the writable property returns a deprecation warning and points users to """"""""writeable""""""""--just the opposite of the spec.    Android only supports writable. Propose we change the iOS code--or else update the spec and Android code to match.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Incorrect deprecation of Ti.Filesystem.File.writable
Description: """"According to the Filesystem parity spec: https://wiki.<USER>org/display/spe/Filesystem+Behavior+Parity The """"""""writeable"""""""" property is supposed to be deprecated in favor of writable. However, in the iOS code, the writable property returns a deprecation warning and points users to """"""""writeable""""""""--just the opposite of the spec. Android only supports writable. Propose we change the iOS code--or else update the spec and Android code to match. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6931,12,"""Android: JSS not working in new opened window""","""""""h2. Expected Behavior     The label should be displayed with a black color and positioned in the top left corner.    h2. Actual Behavior    The definitions from {{bootstrap.jss}} are not applied - the label is gray and centered.     I get the expected behavior with the Titanium 1.7.6 release on Android. It works as expected on iOS with 1.7.6 and 1.8.0.1    h2. Test case     {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#ffffff');  var options = {url: 'bootstrap.js',                 className: 'mainwindow'};  var win     = Ti.UI.createWindow(options);  win.open();         {code:lang=javascript|title=bootstrap.js}  var message = Ti.UI.createLabel({text: 'Hello World', className:'messageLabel'});  Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(message);       h2. Community Discussion   [Android: JSS not working with 1.8.0.1 release (v8 and rhino) - Regression|http://developer.<USER>com/question/129819/android-jss-not-working-with-1801-release-v8-and-rhino---regression]""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: JSS not working in new opened window
Description: """"h2. Expected Behavior The label should be displayed with a black color and positioned in the top left corner. h2. Actual Behavior The definitions from {{bootstrap.jss}} are not applied - the label is gray and centered. I get the expected behavior with the Titanium 1.7.6 release on Android. It works as expected on iOS with 1.7.6 and 1.8.0.1 h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#ffffff'); var options = {url: 'bootstrap.js', className: 'mainwindow'}; var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(options); win.open(); {code:lang=javascript|title=bootstrap.js} var message = Ti.UI.createLabel({text: 'Hello World', className:'messageLabel'}); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(message); h2. Community Discussion [Android: JSS not working with 1.8.0.1 release (v8 and rhino) - Regression|http://developer.<USER>com/question/129819/android-jss-not-working-with-1801-release-v8-and-rhino---regression]""""",title+description
TIMOB-6928,12,"""Android: Intents - missing createPendingIntent() and createNotification() methods""","""""""h2.Problem    A call to {{Ti.Android.createPendingIntent()}} or {{Ti.Android.createNotification()}} fails with the following errors:         The code runs fine in SDK 1.8.0.v20110913141920 (also using V8).    This problem completely kills any app that uses notifications.    h2.Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor:'#fff',    windowSoftInputMode:Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_STATE_ALWAYS_HIDDEN,    exitOnClose:true,    navBarHidden:true  });     var btn1 = Ti.UI.createButton({    title:'Make Notification',    width:'auto',    top:100  });  function DoBtn1Click()  {    NewNotification(2,Ti.App.name,'I am workin here',null,null,true);  }  btn1.addEventListener('click',DoBtn1Click);  win1.add(btn1);     win1.open();     function NewNotification(ID, AppTitle, Content, Icon, Ticker, OnGoing)  {    var AppIntent=Ti.Android.createIntent({                    flags: Ti.Android.FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TOP | Ti.Android.FLAG_ACTIVITY_SINGLE_TOP,                    className:'org.<USER>titanium.TiActivity',                    packageName:Ti.App.id                  });    AppIntent.addCategory(Ti.Android.CATEGORY_LAUNCHER);    var NotificationClickAction=Ti.Android.createPendingIntent({                                  activity:Ti.Android.currentActivity,                                  intent:AppIntent,                                  flags:Ti.Android.FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT,                                  type:Ti.Android.PENDING_INTENT_FOR_ACTIVITY                                });    var NotificationMembers = {contentTitle: AppTitle,                               contentText: Content,                               when: 0, // This will keep the time from showing on the notification                               contentIntent: NotificationClickAction                              };    if (Icon != null)      NotificationMembers.icon='images/'+Icon;    else // default to barber pole      NotificationMembers.icon=Ti.Android.R.drawable.progress_indeterminate_horizontal;       if (Ticker != null)      NotificationMembers.tickerText = Ticker;       if ((OnGoing != null) && (OnGoing))      NotificationMembers.flags = (Ti.Android.FLAG_ONGOING_EVENT | Ti.Android.FLAG_NO_CLEAR);       Ti.Android.NotificationManager.notify(ID, Ti.Android.createNotification(NotificationMembers));  }  {code}     h2. Relevant Q&A:  [1.8.0.1 - createPendingIntent missing from Ti.Android|http://developer.<USER>com/question/129961/]    Another commenter reports the same problem (slightly different error msg) with Rhino.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Intents - missing createPendingIntent() and createNotification() methods
Description: """"h2.Problem A call to {{Ti.Android.createPendingIntent()}} or {{Ti.Android.createNotification()}} fails with the following errors: The code runs fine in SDK 1.8.0.v20110913141920 (also using V8). This problem completely kills any app that uses notifications. h2.Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff', windowSoftInputMode:Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_STATE_ALWAYS_HIDDEN, exitOnClose:true, navBarHidden:true }); var btn1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Make Notification', width:'auto', top:100 }); function DoBtn1Click() { NewNotification(2,Ti.App.name,'I am workin here',null,null,true); } btn1.addEventListener('click',DoBtn1Click); win1.add(btn1); win1.open(); function NewNotification(ID, AppTitle, Content, Icon, Ticker, OnGoing) { var AppIntent=Ti.Android.createIntent({ flags: Ti.Android.FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TOP | Ti.Android.FLAG_ACTIVITY_SINGLE_TOP, className:'org.<USER>titanium.TiActivity', packageName:Ti.App.id }); AppIntent.addCategory(Ti.Android.CATEGORY_LAUNCHER); var NotificationClickAction=Ti.Android.createPendingIntent({ activity:Ti.Android.currentActivity, intent:AppIntent, flags:Ti.Android.FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT, type:Ti.Android.PENDING_INTENT_FOR_ACTIVITY }); var NotificationMembers = {contentTitle: AppTitle, contentText: Content, when: 0, // This will keep the time from showing on the notification contentIntent: NotificationClickAction }; if (Icon != null) NotificationMembers.icon='images/'+Icon; else // default to barber pole NotificationMembers.icon=Ti.Android.R.drawable.progress_indeterminate_horizontal; if (Ticker != null) NotificationMembers.tickerText = Ticker; if ((OnGoing != null) && (OnGoing)) NotificationMembers.flags = (Ti.Android.FLAG_ONGOING_EVENT | Ti.Android.FLAG_NO_CLEAR); Ti.Android.NotificationManager.notify(ID, Ti.Android.createNotification(NotificationMembers)); } {code} h2. Relevant Q&A: [1.8.0.1 - createPendingIntent missing from Ti.Android|http://developer.<USER>com/question/129961/] Another commenter reports the same problem (slightly different error msg) with Rhino. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6927,12,"""iOS: Add label styling to map annotations""","""""""A feature request has come in for the ability to style text on annotations. This would need to be a completely new annotation type which displays an object styled as a label. Will probably have to accept {{Ti.UI.Label}} objects for {{title}} and {{subtitle}} properties to ensure that they're styled correctly, and that we support every styling feature that a label does.    Android will need a parity ticket if this feature is implemented.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add label styling to map annotations
Description: """"A feature request has come in for the ability to style text on annotations. This would need to be a completely new annotation type which displays an object styled as a label. Will probably have to accept {{Ti.UI.Label}} objects for {{title}} and {{subtitle}} properties to ensure that they're styled correctly, and that we support every styling feature that a label does. Android will need a parity ticket if this feature is implemented.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6925,12,"""Android: Adding CookieManager functionality into Ti Mobile""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customers sometimes want to share cookies between webviews and Titanium views, this works perfectly fine in iOS, but it's not working as nice in Android.     h4. DOCUMENTATION  http://developer.android.com/reference/android/webkit/CookieManager.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Adding CookieManager functionality into Ti Mobile
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customers sometimes want to share cookies between webviews and Titanium views, this works perfectly fine in iOS, but it's not working as nice in Android. h4. DOCUMENTATION http://developer.android.com/reference/android/webkit/CookieManager.html""""",title+description
TIMOB-6923,12,"""iOS: App.iOS - LocalNotification scheduled from a background process dismiss after 40 seconds""","""""""h2. Problem    * [Titanium.App.iOS.LocalNotification|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.App.iOS.LocalNotification-object] notifications scheduled from a background <USER>last for exactly 40 seconds  * Firing an event from a background <USER>causing app.js to schedule a local notification does not solve the problem. In this case the notification lasts for exactly 30 seconds    Note that Local notifications scheduled directly from {{app.js}} work as expected (last forever)    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Ti.Geolocation.purpose = 'Geolocation';  Ti.App.service = Ti.App.iOS.registerBackgroundService({url: 'service.js'});         h2. Discussions    Helpdesk: [APP-564871|http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-564871]""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App.iOS - LocalNotification scheduled from a background process dismiss after 40 seconds
Description: """"h2. Problem * [Titanium.App.iOS.LocalNotification|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.App.iOS.LocalNotification-object] notifications scheduled from a background <USER>last for exactly 40 seconds * Firing an event from a background <USER>causing app.js to schedule a local notification does not solve the problem. In this case the notification lasts for exactly 30 seconds Note that Local notifications scheduled directly from {{app.js}} work as expected (last forever) h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Ti.Geolocation.purpose = 'Geolocation'; Ti.App.service = Ti.App.iOS.registerBackgroundService({url: 'service.js'}); h2. Discussions Helpdesk: [APP-564871|http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-564871]""""",title+description
TIMOB-6920,12,"""iOS: UI - imageView incorrect image height when hires property set to true""","""""""h2. Problem    When setting the height of an imageView to {{height: 'auto'}} and {{hires: true}}, the imageView height expands the height of the window, instead of the height of the image.    It works correctly if {{hires: true}} is removed.    See attached screenshots, with hires and without.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javaScript|title=app.js}  Ti.UI.backgroundColor = '#fff';    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();    var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({   image: 'noop',   top: 0,   width: 280,   hires: true,   height: 'auto',   backgroundColor: 'green'  });    win.add( imageView );    win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: UI - imageView incorrect image height when hires property set to true
Description: """"h2. Problem When setting the height of an imageView to {{height: 'auto'}} and {{hires: true}}, the imageView height expands the height of the window, instead of the height of the image. It works correctly if {{hires: true}} is removed. See attached screenshots, with hires and without. h2. Test case {code:lang=javaScript|title=app.js} Ti.UI.backgroundColor = '#fff'; var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'noop', top: 0, width: 280, hires: true, height: 'auto', backgroundColor: 'green' }); win.add( imageView ); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6915,12,"""iOS: Mimetype information is inadequate / misleading""","""""""Currently, iOS' {{Mimetype.m}} mimetype processor does not recognize all of the available mimetypes for the device - in particular, it does not identify """"""""mp4"""""""" correctly as of mimetype class """"""""video"""""""" (or as anything, for that matter).    We need to either upgrade this file to accurately map mimetypes or use internal support from the OS for mimetype ID.    Part of this ticket should be creating a drillbit test to check for valid mimetypes of a subset of common files which the user may be performing operations on.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Mimetype information is inadequate / misleading
Description: """"Currently, iOS' {{Mimetype.m}} mimetype processor does not recognize all of the available mimetypes for the device - in particular, it does not identify """"""""mp4"""""""" correctly as of mimetype class """"""""video"""""""" (or as anything, for that matter). We need to either upgrade this file to accurately map mimetypes or use internal support from the OS for mimetype ID. Part of this ticket should be creating a drillbit test to check for valid mimetypes of a subset of common files which the user may be performing operations on.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6913,12,"""iOS: Picker labels disappear when user scrolls quickly the picker""","""""""h4. Expected Behavior  The user can scroll down and up through the picker and the labels or views, always need to be there    h4. Actual Behavior  When the user scrolls quickly some views or labels of the column picker just disappear    h4. Test Case  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Picker labels disappear when user scrolls quickly the picker
Description: """"h4. Expected Behavior The user can scroll down and up through the picker and the labels or views, always need to be there h4. Actual Behavior When the user scrolls quickly some views or labels of the column picker just disappear h4. Test Case """"",title+description
TIMOB-6911,12,"""Android: Parent View's size.height (and width) will return '0' when set to auto.  (Parity issue)""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  You have a parent view with height and width set to 'auto'. When you add views to this parent view, you eventually can ask for the current width and height, via the """"""""size"""""""" dictionary. In iOS, it's working just fine, you add a child view, and the parent view will get you the right height. That is not working on Android.    h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Create a mobile project  2. Paste the code below to the app.js  3. Run in Android.    h4. CODE      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Parent View's size.height (and width) will return '0' when set to auto. (Parity issue)
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION You have a parent view with height and width set to 'auto'. When you add views to this parent view, you eventually can ask for the current width and height, via the """"""""size"""""""" dictionary. In iOS, it's working just fine, you add a child view, and the parent view will get you the right height. That is not working on Android. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Create a mobile project 2. Paste the code below to the app.js 3. Run in Android. h4. CODE """"",title+description
TIMOB-6910,12,"""Android: Emulator - V8/Rhino, StrictMode policy violation is thrown in the console when launching to Ice Cream Sandwich emulator""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Launch empty Titanium project to Android Emulator 4.0    Results: StrictMode policy violation is thrown in the TiStud console:        Expected: Should not see this error.    Note: This error still persists when I launch an empty 1.7.5 Titanium project against Android Emulator 4.0""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Emulator - V8/Rhino, StrictMode policy violation is thrown in the console when launching to Ice Cream Sandwich emulator
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch empty Titanium project to Android Emulator 4.0 Results: StrictMode policy violation is thrown in the TiStud console: Expected: Should not see this error. Note: This error still persists when I launch an empty 1.7.5 Titanium project against Android Emulator 4.0""""",title+description
TIMOB-6908,12,"""Android: png image file transparency problem""","""""""h2. Problem    On Android, PNGs containing transparency/semi-transparency (such as shadows and glow) look very bad compared to both the iPhone version and the Photoshop reference mockup (see attached screenshots).    The PNGs are normal 32bit (RGBA) straight from Photoshop and looks fine in iPhone simulator. On Android both the emulator and device (HTC Legend) are affected.     h2. Test case    The test is made up of a Window with a background PNG, and two child views with unscaled background PNG's with both solid and semi-transparent content.    Assets are attached    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundImage:'bg.png',  });     var shadow = Ti.UI.createView({      backgroundImage:'shadow.png',      width:'179dp',      height:'179dp',      top:'25dp',  });     var glow = Ti.UI.createView({      backgroundImage:'glow.png',      width:'189dp',      height:'189dp',      bottom:'15dp',  });     win.add(shadow);  win.add(glow);  win.open();  {code}    h2. Discussions    Q&A: [severe android png rendering bug|http://developer.<USER>com/question/127038/severe-android-png-rendering-bug]    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: png image file transparency problem
Description: """"h2. Problem On Android, PNGs containing transparency/semi-transparency (such as shadows and glow) look very bad compared to both the iPhone version and the Photoshop reference mockup (see attached screenshots). The PNGs are normal 32bit (RGBA) straight from Photoshop and looks fine in iPhone simulator. On Android both the emulator and device (HTC Legend) are affected. h2. Test case The test is made up of a Window with a background PNG, and two child views with unscaled background PNG's with both solid and semi-transparent content. Assets are attached {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundImage:'bg.png', }); var shadow = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundImage:'shadow.png', width:'179dp', height:'179dp', top:'25dp', }); var glow = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundImage:'glow.png', width:'189dp', height:'189dp', bottom:'15dp', }); win.add(shadow); win.add(glow); win.open(); {code} h2. Discussions Q&A: [severe android png rendering bug|http://developer.<USER>com/question/127038/severe-android-png-rendering-bug] """"",title+description
TIMOB-6907,12,"""Android: minSdkVersion incorrect in template AndroidManifest.xml""","""""""{{minSdkVersion}} still set to 7, should be 8.      h3. Testing steps:    1. create a new project.  2. build and run project.  3. open build/android/AndroidManifest.xml.  4. in the fail case, you will see {{<uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion=""""""""7"""""""" />}}, when testing the fix you should see {{<uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion=""""""""8"""""""" />}}.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: minSdkVersion incorrect in template AndroidManifest.xml
Description: """"{{minSdkVersion}} still set to 7, should be 8. h3. Testing steps: 1. create a new project. 2. build and run project. 3. open build/android/AndroidManifest.xml. 4. in the fail case, you will see {{<uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion=""""""""7"""""""" />}}, when testing the fix you should see {{<uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion=""""""""8"""""""" />}}. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6906,12,"""Tooling: tiapp.xml - line breaks in description field break compilation""","""""""h2. Problem  If a character return/line feed is anywhere in the description field of the TIAPP.xml, compilation fails.    h2. Steps to Reproduce  1. Create a new blank project.  2. Edit the project settings in TIAPP.xml (or use attached file)  3. Add a multi-line description using char returns/line breaks.  4. Build for simulators/emulators  5. Observe errors below    h2. Logs    {code:lang=none|title=iOS Error}  [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/iphone/main.m:16:47: error: unexpected '@' in program [1]  [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/iphone/main.m:18:44: error: expected ';' after top level declarator [1]  [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/iphone/main.m:18:45: error: unexpected '@' in program [1]  [ERROR]   [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):      {code:lang=none|title=Android Error}  [ERROR] Error(s) compiling generated Java code  [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/android/gen/com/evangelapps/church/EvangelappsChurchAppInfo.java:55: unclosed string literal      """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: tiapp.xml - line breaks in description field break compilation
Description: """"h2. Problem If a character return/line feed is anywhere in the description field of the TIAPP.xml, compilation fails. h2. Steps to Reproduce 1. Create a new blank project. 2. Edit the project settings in TIAPP.xml (or use attached file) 3. Add a multi-line description using char returns/line breaks. 4. Build for simulators/emulators 5. Observe errors below h2. Logs {code:lang=none|title=iOS Error} [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/iphone/main.m:16:47: error: unexpected '@' in program [1] [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/iphone/main.m:18:44: error: expected ';' after top level declarator [1] [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/iphone/main.m:18:45: error: unexpected '@' in program [1] [ERROR] [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): {code:lang=none|title=Android Error} [ERROR] Error(s) compiling generated Java code [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/Developer/Titanium Studio Workspace/evangelapps-church/build/android/gen/com/evangelapps/church/EvangelappsChurchAppInfo.java:55: unclosed string literal """"",title+description
TIMOB-6905,12,"""Tooling: iOS - variables in custom Info.plist not populated during build""","""""""h2. Problem    Under 1.8.0.1, in a custom Info.plist (required for proper background modes), variable placeholders are not populated on build    Screenshots show generated Info.plist from App package.    Note: 1.7.5 works as expected.    h2. Steps to reproduce    1. Create a new default mobile project.  2. Build for iOS simulator.  3. Copy the Info.plist from the build/iphone directory to \{project\}/platform/iphone   Note Placeholders for Product Name and Executable Name:    4. Clean project.  5. Edit \{project\}/platform/iphone to customize (add a background requirement or something)  6. Rebuild for iOS.  7. Name of app in Springboard will be $(Prog...)  8. If you browse the app Package under the simulator directory, you will find that in the packaged Info.plist, those variable/placeholders have not been populated.""""""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: iOS - variables in custom Info.plist not populated during build
Description: """"h2. Problem Under 1.8.0.1, in a custom Info.plist (required for proper background modes), variable placeholders are not populated on build Screenshots show generated Info.plist from App package. Note: 1.7.5 works as expected. h2. Steps to reproduce 1. Create a new default mobile project. 2. Build for iOS simulator. 3. Copy the Info.plist from the build/iphone directory to \{project\}/platform/iphone Note Placeholders for Product Name and Executable Name: 4. Clean project. 5. Edit \{project\}/platform/iphone to customize (add a background requirement or something) 6. Rebuild for iOS. 7. Name of app in Springboard will be $(Prog...) 8. If you browse the app Package under the simulator directory, you will find that in the packaged Info.plist, those variable/placeholders have not been populated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6904,12,"""Tooling: Android - run app on device outputs erroneous INFO message to console""","""""""h2. Problem    When building for device, the second-to-last INFO message in the console says:    """"""""[INFO] Installing application on emulator""""""""    It should say """"""""on device""""""""    h2. Steps to reproduce    Attach an Android device and from Titanium Studio launch the default app to it    h2. Logs    {code:title=console}  [INFO] logfile = /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9/build.log  [DEBUG] /home/appcel/.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/1.8.0.1/android/builder.py install testing9 /opt/android-sdk-linux_86 /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9 com.testing.testing9 4  [TRACE] app property, ti.android.runtime : v8  [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.0.1 (12/22/11 13:09 fbdc96f)  [DEBUG] Waiting for device to be ready ...  [TRACE] adb devices returned 1 devices/emulators  [DEBUG] Device connected... (waited 0 seconds)  [DEBUG] waited 0.003751 seconds on emulator to get ready  [DEBUG] /opt/android-sdk-linux_86/platform-tools/adb -d shell ls /data/app/com.testing.testing9*.apk  [DEBUG] com.testing.testing9 installed? False  [TRACE] app property, ti.android.runtime : v8  [INFO] Copying project resources..  [INFO] Detected tiapp.xml change (or assets deleted), forcing full re-build...  [TRACE] COPYING CREATED FILE: /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9/Resources/scoreModule.js => /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/scoreModule.js  [TRACE] COPYING CREATED FILE: /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9/Resources/app.js => /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/app.js  [TRACE] COPYING CREATED FILE: /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9/Resources/test1.js => /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/test1.js  [TRACE] COPYING CREATED FILE: /home/appcel/Titanium Studio Workspace/testing9