TIMOB-6855,12,"""Android: Function to get the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta from a MapView""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer wants to be able to regenerate a map centered in a given location, but drawing the region with the same level of zoom that the user is using right now.    h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Create a mapview centered in the whitehouse  2. Zoom the map  3. The user provided another point to center in the map.   4. Before the redraw, they need to know the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta after the zoom. """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Function to get the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta from a MapView
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer wants to be able to regenerate a map centered in a given location, but drawing the region with the same level of zoom that the user is using right now. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Create a mapview centered in the whitehouse 2. Zoom the map 3. The user provided another point to center in the map. 4. Before the redraw, they need to know the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta after the zoom. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6854,12,"""iOS """"load"""" event when the engine ends parsing the JavaScript code""","""""""h3.Feature Request  Feature request for the """"""""load"""""""" event which will tell us when the JavaScript parser has finished. This is available in other JavaScript engines, example: http://www.w3schools.com/js/js_events.asp . It should be the equivalent to the """"""""load"""""""" event on webpage.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS """"load"""" event when the engine ends parsing the JavaScript code
Description: """"h3.Feature Request Feature request for the """"""""load"""""""" event which will tell us when the JavaScript parser has finished. This is available in other JavaScript engines, example: http://www.w3schools.com/js/js_events.asp . It should be the equivalent to the """"""""load"""""""" event on webpage.""""",title+description
