Description: """"The Android FastDev is very useful. There should be a FastDev for iOS too. [Someone on GitHub has created an unofficial version|https://github.com/<USER>TiiOSFastDev]""""",title+description
TIMOB-6840,12,"""Android : Build - v8, Rhino When launching to emulator 3.0 on Windows 7 a panic occurs and fails to launch to emulator""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Create a new mobile project in Studio  2. Launch in the 3.0 emulator    Actual results:  PANIC: Could not open: C:\Users\labuser\.android/avd/titanium_18_WXGA.ini    Expected results:  App is launched in the 3.0 simulator""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : Build - v8, Rhino When launching to emulator 3.0 on Windows 7 a panic occurs and fails to launch to emulator
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a new mobile project in Studio 2. Launch in the 3.0 emulator Actual results: PANIC: Could not open: C:\Users\labuser\.android/avd/titanium_18_WXGA.ini Expected results: App is launched in the 3.0 simulator""""",title+description
TIMOB-6839,12,"""Android: Missing jars in the .classpath of the Mobile Modules project""","""""""When creating a new Mobile Module project from the Studio we see compilation errors. These errors are resolved after manually adding *kroll-apt* and *kroll-common* Jars from the SDK.    Seems like they are missing for the initial generated .classpath file.    To fix:    # Right-click on a project  # Choose *Properties*  # Select *Java Build Path > Libraries* and click on *External JARs*  # Navigate to your Titanium SDK installation directory (Default locations are at the bottom of here https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tis/Downloading+Titanium+SDKs+in+Titanium+Studio, or look in *Preferences > Titanium Studio > Titanium*)  # Navigate further to /mobilesdk/_yourOS_/_SDKversion_/andorid  # Select the kroll-* JAR files  # Save and exit out of the dialogs.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Missing jars in the .classpath of the Mobile Modules project
Description: """"When creating a new Mobile Module project from the Studio we see compilation errors. These errors are resolved after manually adding *kroll-apt* and *kroll-common* Jars from the SDK. Seems like they are missing for the initial generated .classpath file. To fix: # Right-click on a project # Choose *Properties* # Select *Java Build Path > Libraries* and click on *External JARs* # Navigate to your Titanium SDK installation directory (Default locations are at the bottom of here https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tis/Downloading+Titanium+SDKs+in+Titanium+Studio, or look in *Preferences > Titanium Studio > Titanium*) # Navigate further to /mobilesdk/_yourOS_/_SDKversion_/andorid # Select the kroll-* JAR files # Save and exit out of the dialogs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6838,12,"""iOS : XHR - When running the XHR > File Download test, pressing abort - Large File Download in succession multiple times causes Kitchen Sink to crash""","""""""This issue probably doesn't exhibit normal user behavior    Steps to reproduce:  1. Install 1_8_X Kitchen Sink on iOS device  2. Navigate to Platform > XHR > File Download  3. Press Abort and Large file download multiple times (briskly), sometimes pressing abort twice in a row (note if an alert appears, dismiss it)    Expected result:  XHR request aborts    Actual result:  Kitchen Sink crashes    *Note see attached crash log (my machine won't symbolicate)    *Also, console outputs segmentation fault: 11""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : XHR - When running the XHR > File Download test, pressing abort - Large File Download in succession multiple times causes Kitchen Sink to crash
Description: """"This issue probably doesn't exhibit normal user behavior Steps to reproduce: 1. Install 1_8_X Kitchen Sink on iOS device 2. Navigate to Platform > XHR > File Download 3. Press Abort and Large file download multiple times (briskly), sometimes pressing abort twice in a row (note if an alert appears, dismiss it) Expected result: XHR request aborts Actual result: Kitchen Sink crashes *Note see attached crash log (my machine won't symbolicate) *Also, console outputs segmentation fault: 11""""",title+description
TIMOB-6837,12,"""Tooling: iOS package size is too large""","""""""h2. Problem  For iOS, when you create a new mobile project in Titanium Studio and run it on device, the ipa file it generates is well over 4MB.     That's a blank project!    The application size should not be that big.    h2. Steps to Reproduce    * create a new project in titanium studio  * hit run on device  * see the size of the ipa file it generates is over 4MB. If you unzip the ipa file and look at the actual executable inside the .app package, the executable is over 5MB.     {panel}  Please see the comment below regarding the distribution package size.  {panel}    """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: iOS package size is too large
Description: """"h2. Problem For iOS, when you create a new mobile project in Titanium Studio and run it on device, the ipa file it generates is well over 4MB. That's a blank project! The application size should not be that big. h2. Steps to Reproduce * create a new project in titanium studio * hit run on device * see the size of the ipa file it generates is over 4MB. If you unzip the ipa file and look at the actual executable inside the .app package, the executable is over 5MB. {panel} Please see the comment below regarding the distribution package size. {panel} """"",title+description
TIMOB-6836,12,"""MobileWeb: ScrollableView does not support direct setting of the 'views' property. Views set directly will not get added to the DOM parent.""","""""""If you try to directly set the views property of a ScrollableView, the views are not added to the ScrollableView DOM node.  ie:          None of the views will be added to the DOM parent as they need to be passed into ScrollableView.addView in order to be set correctly.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: ScrollableView does not support direct setting of the 'views' property. Views set directly will not get added to the DOM parent.
Description: """"If you try to directly set the views property of a ScrollableView, the views are not added to the ScrollableView DOM node. ie: None of the views will be added to the DOM parent as they need to be passed into ScrollableView.addView in order to be set correctly.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6835,12,"""iOS: Network - createHttpClient cannot handle Japanese Shift_JIS and EUC-JP encoding""","""""""h2. Problem    Most of Japanese webpages use utf-8 encoding, but some pages use old encodings (Shift-JIS or EUC-JP).    charset list (as reference)  http://www.iana.org/assignments/character-sets    But a return value will be set to null if Japanese webpage is acquired using Titanium.Network.createHttpClient.      h2. Test case    I make a sample code which accesses each charset sample webpage and display their results.        result is below:  ||OS || UTF-8 || Shift_JIS || EUC-JP ||  |iOS | OK | null | null|    h2. Suggested Fix    To fix this bug, add charset list to TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m    See https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/590""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Network - createHttpClient cannot handle Japanese Shift_JIS and EUC-JP encoding
Description: """"h2. Problem Most of Japanese webpages use utf-8 encoding, but some pages use old encodings (Shift-JIS or EUC-JP). charset list (as reference) http://www.iana.org/assignments/character-sets But a return value will be set to null if Japanese webpage is acquired using Titanium.Network.createHttpClient. h2. Test case I make a sample code which accesses each charset sample webpage and display their results. result is below: ||OS || UTF-8 || Shift_JIS || EUC-JP || |iOS | OK | null | null| h2. Suggested Fix To fix this bug, add charset list to TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m See https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/590""""",title+description
TIMOB-6834,12,"""Coverage: Create test app to check event availability/responses""","""""""Going forward, as part of the parity reports, we need to determine a way to have a test app that processes events for objects (especially views) and reports some parity information. We would have to drive it based on doc information for now (maybe not the greatest...) and it would have to be delayed until we could hook in automation of some kind (so that we're not adding event listeners which are fired by manually triggering them in the code itself).    This could allow us to detect many problems where the documentation is wrong, we lack parity on which events are supported, what is reported by the event, etc.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Coverage: Create test app to check event availability/responses
Description: """"Going forward, as part of the parity reports, we need to determine a way to have a test app that processes events for objects (especially views) and reports some parity information. We would have to drive it based on doc information for now (maybe not the greatest...) and it would have to be delayed until we could hook in automation of some kind (so that we're not adding event listeners which are fired by manually triggering them in the code itself). This could allow us to detect many problems where the documentation is wrong, we lack parity on which events are supported, what is reported by the event, etc.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6833,12,"""Android:  Cached notification data on android""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  The data I get from notifications I create remains cached on Android.    h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  0. Create new mobile project with Android support.  1. Paste the above code into app.js  2. Compile.  3. Put a value in the field on the window  4. Click the button, we create a pending notification with the data you typed  5. Find the notification in the Android notification bar and click it  6. The app instance alread open is found and the """"""""newintent"""""""" event correctly fires  7. The data we get back from the event is correct if this is the first try  8. Do steps 1 - 4 again with a different value in the textfield    h4. ACTUAL RESULTS  You will get a cached value    h4. EXPECTED RESULTS  The latest value.    h4. CODE    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cached notification data on android
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION The data I get from notifications I create remains cached on Android. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 0. Create new mobile project with Android support. 1. Paste the above code into app.js 2. Compile. 3. Put a value in the field on the window 4. Click the button, we create a pending notification with the data you typed 5. Find the notification in the Android notification bar and click it 6. The app instance alread open is found and the """"""""newintent"""""""" event correctly fires 7. The data we get back from the event is correct if this is the first try 8. Do steps 1 - 4 again with a different value in the textfield h4. ACTUAL RESULTS You will get a cached value h4. EXPECTED RESULTS The latest value. h4. CODE """"",title+description
TIMOB-6832,12,"""iOS: Search for response headers is case sensitive""","""""""h4. Expected Behavior  Create a custom header with a name, and find it by this name case insensitive    h4. Actual Behavior  While upgrading from iOS4 to iOS5 we ran into some issues where iOS4 appeared to be changing the case of response header names--so """"""""MY-Custom-Header"""""""" would become """"""""My-Custom-Header"""""""". As a result when we tried searching for """"""""MY-Custom-Header"""""""" it would not be found. To solve this problem we performed a case-insensitive search for response headers.  In the Titanium Mobile's caseCorrect method (iPhone/Classes/TiUtils.m) it looks like the code is attempting to fix this case-changing problem on pre-iOS5 versions. There's a problem here though: if the a response header is called """"""""my-custom-header"""""""" it will not be found in pre-iOS5 versions because caseCorrect converts it to """"""""My-Custom-Header"""""""".    h4.Test Case         h4. Response    The debug output on the iPhone 4.3 Simulator was:  [DEBUG] Custom response header: my-custom-header = undefined  The debug output on the iPhone 5 Simulator was:  [DEBUG] Custom response header: my-custom-header = header value    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Search for response headers is case sensitive
Description: """"h4. Expected Behavior Create a custom header with a name, and find it by this name case insensitive h4. Actual Behavior While upgrading from iOS4 to iOS5 we ran into some issues where iOS4 appeared to be changing the case of response header names--so """"""""MY-Custom-Header"""""""" would become """"""""My-Custom-Header"""""""". As a result when we tried searching for """"""""MY-Custom-Header"""""""" it would not be found. To solve this problem we performed a case-insensitive search for response headers. In the Titanium Mobile's caseCorrect method (iPhone/Classes/TiUtils.m) it looks like the code is attempting to fix this case-changing problem on pre-iOS5 versions. There's a problem here though: if the a response header is called """"""""my-custom-header"""""""" it will not be found in pre-iOS5 versions because caseCorrect converts it to """"""""My-Custom-Header"""""""". h4.Test Case h4. Response The debug output on the iPhone 4.3 Simulator was: [DEBUG] Custom response header: my-custom-header = undefined The debug output on the iPhone 5 Simulator was: [DEBUG] Custom response header: my-custom-header = header value """"",title+description
TIMOB-6831,12,"""iOS: Function to get the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta from a MapView""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer wants to be able to regenerate a map centered in a given location, but drawing the region with the same level of zoom that the user is using right now.    h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Create a mapview centered in the whitehouse  2. Zoom the map  3. The user provided another point to center in the map.   4. Before the redraw, they need to know the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta after the zoom. """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Function to get the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta from a MapView
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer wants to be able to regenerate a map centered in a given location, but drawing the region with the same level of zoom that the user is using right now. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Create a mapview centered in the whitehouse 2. Zoom the map 3. The user provided another point to center in the map. 4. Before the redraw, they need to know the current latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta after the zoom. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6830,12,"""iOS: Create a function to keep the date-time of the last activity on the events""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer wants to have a function that keeps the track of the last touch event related to UI, so they can run a custom function when that happens. This is needed in order to run a logout function in the app, in case of the app not being used by certain period of time.    h4. EXTRA INFO   This function is something that can be used by many of our enterprise customers having similar issues.    h4. WORKAROUND  The suggested workaround to the customer was to keep a var in the Ti.App.Properties with the date/time of the last event related to UI. They understand the workaround, but they want this kind of general tracking handed by ourselves. """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Create a function to keep the date-time of the last activity on the events
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer wants to have a function that keeps the track of the last touch event related to UI, so they can run a custom function when that happens. This is needed in order to run a logout function in the app, in case of the app not being used by certain period of time. h4. EXTRA INFO This function is something that can be used by many of our enterprise customers having similar issues. h4. WORKAROUND The suggested workaround to the customer was to keep a var in the Ti.App.Properties with the date/time of the last event related to UI. They understand the workaround, but they want this kind of general tracking handed by ourselves. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6829,12,"""iOS: Tooling - Can't build iOS project if a file name matches the name of its parent directory""","""""""In Titanium Studio v1.0.7 -> v1.1 (mobile SDK v1.7.5 -> v1.8.0), a project will not build if it contains a file in a directory of the same name. For example:    app.js  Resources  --mymod  ----mymod.js    Depending on the version of Titanium Studio, the build error message ranges from marginally helpful to not helpful at all. In the best case, the build message indicates that the iOS Simulator can't find a file it is looking for within the app bundle, but gives no indication as to why. To the developer, it looks like the file exists and is in the correct place (in the project).    Note, the build fails even if mymod.js is not referenced in any way (no includes, requires, etc.). Changing the name of the parent folder (e.g. to """"""""mymodFramework"""""""") allows the project to build successfully again.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tooling - Can't build iOS project if a file name matches the name of its parent directory
Description: """"In Titanium Studio v1.0.7 -> v1.1 (mobile SDK v1.7.5 -> v1.8.0), a project will not build if it contains a file in a directory of the same name. For example: app.js Resources --mymod ----mymod.js Depending on the version of Titanium Studio, the build error message ranges from marginally helpful to not helpful at all. In the best case, the build message indicates that the iOS Simulator can't find a file it is looking for within the app bundle, but gives no indication as to why. To the developer, it looks like the file exists and is in the correct place (in the project). Note, the build fails even if mymod.js is not referenced in any way (no includes, requires, etc.). Changing the name of the parent folder (e.g. to """"""""mymodFramework"""""""") allows the project to build successfully again.""""",title+description
