TIMOB-6769,12,"""iOS: Set tableViewRow height using percentages""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  Customer wants to Set tableViewRow height using percentages.     h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Create a window  2. Create a tableViewRow with height '100%'  3. Create a tableView  4. Add the row to the tableView  5. Add tv to window  6. Open window      h4. ACTUAL RESULTS   A bunch of rows     h4. EXPECTED RESULTS  the row height should be the height of the tableView    h4. CODE    {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}    var win=Ti.UI.createWindow();  var tableview=Ti.UI.createTableView();  var tableviewrow=Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({   height:'100%',  });  tableview.add(tableviewrow);  win.add(tableview);  win.open();    {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Set tableViewRow height using percentages
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION Customer wants to Set tableViewRow height using percentages. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Create a window 2. Create a tableViewRow with height '100%' 3. Create a tableView 4. Add the row to the tableView 5. Add tv to window 6. Open window h4. ACTUAL RESULTS A bunch of rows h4. EXPECTED RESULTS the row height should be the height of the tableView h4. CODE {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var win=Ti.UI.createWindow(); var tableview=Ti.UI.createTableView(); var tableviewrow=Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ height:'100%', }); tableview.add(tableviewrow); win.add(tableview); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6767,12,"""iOS: Disappearing events in tabbedbar nested in Views""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  If you have a tabbedbar inside a view, the view won't get the events, like singletap.    h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Create a new mobile project  2. Paste the code below into app.js  3. Singletap on the buttons of the tabbedbar.    h4. ACTUAL RESULTS  The singletap event is not fired.    h4. EXPECTED RESULTS  Singletap event should be fired.     h4. CODE    {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var view = Ti.UI.createView({   touchEnabled:   true,  });   var bb1 = Titanium.UI.createTabbedBar({    labels:['One', 'Two', 'Three'],    backgroundColor:'#336699',    top:50,    style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.BAR,    height:25,    width:200 });      view.add(bb1);  view.addEventListener('singletap',function(){   Ti.API.info('Event singletap was fired!');  });  win.add(view);  win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Disappearing events in tabbedbar nested in Views
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION If you have a tabbedbar inside a view, the view won't get the events, like singletap. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Create a new mobile project 2. Paste the code below into app.js 3. Singletap on the buttons of the tabbedbar. h4. ACTUAL RESULTS The singletap event is not fired. h4. EXPECTED RESULTS Singletap event should be fired. h4. CODE {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ touchEnabled: true, }); var bb1 = Titanium.UI.createTabbedBar({ labels:['One', 'Two', 'Three'], backgroundColor:'#336699', top:50, style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.BAR, height:25, width:200 }); view.add(bb1); view.addEventListener('singletap',function(){ Ti.API.info('Event singletap was fired!'); }); win.add(view); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6764,12,"""Android: UrbanAirship: Rhino/V8: Certain devices are failing on registration for urban airship""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Run UrbanAirship Application github: titanium_mobile_tests_internal  2. Click on the Enable Push  3. View the logs    Actual:  D/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Starting C2DM  I/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Initializing C2DM Push ...  D/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Generating APID: 73fc6a91-d8cb-42dd-b6d1-0fe793f99e52  W/TiVerify( 2578): (Timer-0) [5005,5005] Verifying module licenses...  I/TiVerify( 2578): (Timer-0) [299,5304] Succesfully verified module licenses  E/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Error posting to /firstrun  E/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): BoxOffice failure.  E/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): BoxOffice firstRun failed. Unable to continue C2DM registration.    Expected:  To complete registration and display the APID    Note:  Works on   Nexus One 2.2  Xoom 3.2.1  Droid 2.3.4""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: UrbanAirship: Rhino/V8: Certain devices are failing on registration for urban airship
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Run UrbanAirship Application github: titanium_mobile_tests_internal 2. Click on the Enable Push 3. View the logs Actual: D/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Starting C2DM I/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Initializing C2DM Push ... D/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Generating APID: 73fc6a91-d8cb-42dd-b6d1-0fe793f99e52 W/TiVerify( 2578): (Timer-0) [5005,5005] Verifying module licenses... I/TiVerify( 2578): (Timer-0) [299,5304] Succesfully verified module licenses E/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): Error posting to /firstrun E/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): BoxOffice failure. E/UrbanAirship - UALib( 2578): BoxOffice firstRun failed. Unable to continue C2DM registration. Expected: To complete registration and display the APID Note: Works on Nexus One 2.2 Xoom 3.2.1 Droid 2.3.4""""",title+description
TIMOB-6763,12,"""iOS: App Crashes trying to play sound while app resumes from background.""","""""""h4. Problem description  Customer compiled his app with the new Mobile SDK 1.8RC3 and it's getting continuous crashing (at startup, when sending audio, etc.).     h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Install app into device  2. Start another instance of the app in the simulator  3. Follow the setup instructions in the section """"""""EXTRA INFO""""""""  4. Send audio and photos from the device to the simulator app.   4. Close the app in the device.  5. Send several messages from the app in the simulator, to the app/number in the device.  6. Resume the app in the device    h4. EXPECTED RESULTS  The app able to receive the data.     h4. ACTUAL RESULTS  The app is crashing.     h4. EXTRA INFO  You can get the source code from the dropbox:    CE Team Share (shared with Steven Tramer and Marshall). Others can be added to access this source as necessary.  <USER>gt2appcelerator-d69a09e50fff07296c384da08ff1b8cf3f51dd5a.zip    h5. Here is more setup info.    Testing: You will need to setup your iphone and the simulator. Once installed the app into the two devices, you will need to go to the agenda and add a number, doesn't matter which number you put, let's say you assign:    Device = +1-650-11  Simulator  = +1-650-12  Then you wil need to add the simulator number to the Device's address book, and viceversa. When you start the app, you will need to """"""""register"""""""" the device, add the device number to the device login, and the simulator number to the simulator.     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App Crashes trying to play sound while app resumes from background.
Description: """"h4. Problem description Customer compiled his app with the new Mobile SDK 1.8RC3 and it's getting continuous crashing (at startup, when sending audio, etc.). h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Install app into device 2. Start another instance of the app in the simulator 3. Follow the setup instructions in the section """"""""EXTRA INFO"""""""" 4. Send audio and photos from the device to the simulator app. 4. Close the app in the device. 5. Send several messages from the app in the simulator, to the app/number in the device. 6. Resume the app in the device h4. EXPECTED RESULTS The app able to receive the data. h4. ACTUAL RESULTS The app is crashing. h4. EXTRA INFO You can get the source code from the dropbox: CE Team Share (shared with Steven Tramer and Marshall). Others can be added to access this source as necessary. <USER>gt2appcelerator-d69a09e50fff07296c384da08ff1b8cf3f51dd5a.zip h5. Here is more setup info. Testing: You will need to setup your iphone and the simulator. Once installed the app into the two devices, you will need to go to the agenda and add a number, doesn't matter which number you put, let's say you assign: Device = +1-650-11 Simulator = +1-650-12 Then you wil need to add the simulator number to the Device's address book, and viceversa. When you start the app, you will need to """"""""register"""""""" the device, add the device number to the device login, and the simulator number to the simulator. """"",title+description
