TIMOB-6740,12,"""Android: Modules: Unable to build modules with RC2""","""""""Using the RC2 build of Titanium Studio, module builds are now failing with the error shown below.    NOTE: Module builds are successful when using the zip downloaded from the CI build (branch 1_8_X)        version=1.8.0.1      module_apiversion=2      timestamp=12/16/11 14:31      githash=c903964    but not with the RC2 build        version=1.8.0.1      module_apiversion=2      timestamp=12/16/11 15:23      githash=c903964    Even though the githash is the same, the RC2 zip file does not contain the """"""""libstlport_shared.so"""""""" file whereas the zip file in the CI build does include the """"""""libstlport_shared.so"""""""" file. We did confirm that if the libstlport_shared.so file is copied into the folders for the RC2 then the modules do build successfully.      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Modules: Unable to build modules with RC2
Description: """"Using the RC2 build of Titanium Studio, module builds are now failing with the error shown below. NOTE: Module builds are successful when using the zip downloaded from the CI build (branch 1_8_X) version=1.8.0.1 module_apiversion=2 timestamp=12/16/11 14:31 githash=c903964 but not with the RC2 build version=1.8.0.1 module_apiversion=2 timestamp=12/16/11 15:23 githash=c903964 Even though the githash is the same, the RC2 zip file does not contain the """"""""libstlport_shared.so"""""""" file whereas the zip file in the CI build does include the """"""""libstlport_shared.so"""""""" file. We did confirm that if the libstlport_shared.so file is copied into the folders for the RC2 then the modules do build successfully. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6739,12,"""MobileWeb: Unable to package project in Titanium Studio""","""""""I seem to be unable to package a project for MobileWeb in Titanium Studio.    Steps to replicate:    # Install 1.8.0.1.RC2  # Create a new mobile project, selecting at least Mobile Web as a platform  # Make sure the selected SDK in tiapp.xml is 1.8.0.1.RC2  # Choose Deploy > Package Mobile Web  # Select """"""""Copy Mobile Web app to a directory"""""""" and select a location on your file system  # Click """"""""Finish""""""""    A dialog comes up with """"""""Failed to package project""""""""    To diagnose, turn on Preferences > Studio > Troubleshooting, turn the slider to """"""""ALL"""""""" and checkmark """"""""Debug specific components"""""""", clicking on """"""""com.aptana.core/debug/shell"""""""". Exit the preference dialog. Re-run the build and once the error happens, view the log file.    At the bottom is the command used to run the builder. For me, it is:    """"""""/usr/bin/python"""""""" """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.0.1.RC2/mobileweb/builder.py"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Documents/Aptana Studio 3 Workspace/rc2test"""""""" """"""""production""""""""    Running that on the command line results in:        Note...switching from """"""""production"""""""" to """"""""development"""""""" makes the above command line work.  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Unable to package project in Titanium Studio
Description: """"I seem to be unable to package a project for MobileWeb in Titanium Studio. Steps to replicate: # Install 1.8.0.1.RC2 # Create a new mobile project, selecting at least Mobile Web as a platform # Make sure the selected SDK in tiapp.xml is 1.8.0.1.RC2 # Choose Deploy > Package Mobile Web # Select """"""""Copy Mobile Web app to a directory"""""""" and select a location on your file system # Click """"""""Finish"""""""" A dialog comes up with """"""""Failed to package project"""""""" To diagnose, turn on Preferences > Studio > Troubleshooting, turn the slider to """"""""ALL"""""""" and checkmark """"""""Debug specific components"""""""", clicking on """"""""com.aptana.core/debug/shell"""""""". Exit the preference dialog. Re-run the build and once the error happens, view the log file. At the bottom is the command used to run the builder. For me, it is: """"""""/usr/bin/python"""""""" """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.0.1.RC2/mobileweb/builder.py"""""""" """"""""/Users/<USER>Documents/Aptana Studio 3 Workspace/rc2test"""""""" """"""""production"""""""" Running that on the command line results in: Note...switching from """"""""production"""""""" to """"""""development"""""""" makes the above command line work. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6738,12,"""Tooling: titanium.py - titanium command line program needs version number in help/main display menu""","""""""titanium command line program needs version number in help/main display menu to enhance validity of working environment. Screenshot attached, just for clarity, not necessarily accurate.    The command line program is located in (depending on the os and sdk version):  e.g., OS X: <dir>/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.0.1.v20111216124633/titanium.py    help menu function: titanium.py line ~361    Note:    This is from the compiled SDK and may not necessarily be the original location of the code.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: titanium.py - titanium command line program needs version number in help/main display menu
Description: """"titanium command line program needs version number in help/main display menu to enhance validity of working environment. Screenshot attached, just for clarity, not necessarily accurate. The command line program is located in (depending on the os and sdk version): e.g., OS X: <dir>/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.8.0.1.v20111216124633/titanium.py help menu function: titanium.py line ~361 Note: This is from the compiled SDK and may not necessarily be the original location of the code.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6737,12,"""Android: sockets - rhino/v8 - Connecting socket does not disconnect on the mac when disconnected from Nook""","""""""Description:  During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I Noted that the disconnect button in the test did not disconnect the socket    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with SDK 1.8.0.1 with rhino/v8  2) Navigate to Platform>Sockets>Connecting socket  3) Run the echoserver.py attached  4) Connect to the IP address and port 50007  5) Click the disconnect button    Result:  The socket doesn't disconnect    Expected:  the socket disconnects""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: sockets - rhino/v8 - Connecting socket does not disconnect on the mac when disconnected from Nook
Description: """"Description: During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I Noted that the disconnect button in the test did not disconnect the socket Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with SDK 1.8.0.1 with rhino/v8 2) Navigate to Platform>Sockets>Connecting socket 3) Run the echoserver.py attached 4) Connect to the IP address and port 50007 5) Click the disconnect button Result: The socket doesn't disconnect Expected: the socket disconnects""""",title+description
TIMOB-6736,12,"""Android: sockets - rhino/v8 - Listening socket on Nook displays sent text plus a square character which may indicate garbage character""","""""""Description:  During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I Noted that the text displayed from the Mac during the listening socket test would always end with a square character.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with SDK 1.8.0.1 with rhino/v8  2) Navigate to Platform>Sockets>Listening socket  3) connect to the device from mac with """"""""telnet (ip address) 40404""""""""  4) Send some text    Result:  Square character displayed (See attached image)    Expected:  No square sent""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: sockets - rhino/v8 - Listening socket on Nook displays sent text plus a square character which may indicate garbage character
Description: """"Description: During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I Noted that the text displayed from the Mac during the listening socket test would always end with a square character. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with SDK 1.8.0.1 with rhino/v8 2) Navigate to Platform>Sockets>Listening socket 3) connect to the device from mac with """"""""telnet (ip address) 40404"""""""" 4) Send some text Result: Square character displayed (See attached image) Expected: No square sent""""",title+description
TIMOB-6734,12,"""Android: selectedBackgroundColor - V8/Rhino, Selected row stays highlighted until you rotate the device""","""""""Steps to reproduce:   1. Copy and run the following code:    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Test',      backgroundColor:'#000',   exitOnClose: true  });    var cb, btn;  var tv = null;  win.add(cb = Ti.UI.createSwitch({   value: true,   style: Ti.UI.Android.SWITCH_STYLE_CHECKBOX,   title: """"""""Give one row backgroundSelectedColor"""""""",   top: """"""""5dp"""""""", left: """"""""5dp"""""""", right: """"""""5dp"""""""", height: """"""""60dp""""""""  }));  win.add(btn = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: """"""""Create TableView"""""""",   top: """"""""65dp"""""""", left: """"""""5dp"""""""", width: """"""""200dp"""""""", height: """"""""40dp""""""""  }));  btn.addEventListener('click', function(e) {   if (tv !== null) {    win.remove(tv);   }   win.add(tv = Ti.UI.createTableView({    top: """"""""110dp"""""""", left: """"""""0dp"""""""", right: """"""""0dp"""""""", bottom: """"""""0dp""""""""   }));       var rows = [];   for (var i = 0; i < 10; i++) {    var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow();    row.title = """"""""Row """""""" + (i + 1);    if (i === 5 && cb.value) {     row.title = """"""""The Evil Row"""""""";     row.backgroundSelectedColor = """"""""blue"""""""";    }    if (i === 8) {     // Just testing standard background     row.backgroundColor = """"""""yellow"""""""";     row.title = """"""""I am yellow"""""""";    }    rows.push(row);   }   tv.setData(rows);  });      win.open();  {code}    2. Click on """"""""Create TableView""""""""  3. Click on """"""""The Evil Row""""""""    Result: Row stays highlighted in blue until you rotate the device.  Expected: Selected row should not stay highlighted regardless of row color.    Note:  * Bug appears on both V8 and Rhino  * Tested on Droid 1 (2.2.2) running V8/Rhino and bug does not appear on Droid 1""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: selectedBackgroundColor - V8/Rhino, Selected row stays highlighted until you rotate the device
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Copy and run the following code: {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#000', exitOnClose: true }); var cb, btn; var tv = null; win.add(cb = Ti.UI.createSwitch({ value: true, style: Ti.UI.Android.SWITCH_STYLE_CHECKBOX, title: """"""""Give one row backgroundSelectedColor"""""""", top: """"""""5dp"""""""", left: """"""""5dp"""""""", right: """"""""5dp"""""""", height: """"""""60dp"""""""" })); win.add(btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: """"""""Create TableView"""""""", top: """"""""65dp"""""""", left: """"""""5dp"""""""", width: """"""""200dp"""""""", height: """"""""40dp"""""""" })); btn.addEventListener('click', function(e) { if (tv !== null) { win.remove(tv); } win.add(tv = Ti.UI.createTableView({ top: """"""""110dp"""""""", left: """"""""0dp"""""""", right: """"""""0dp"""""""", bottom: """"""""0dp"""""""" })); var rows = []; for (var i = 0; i < 10; i++) { var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow(); row.title = """"""""Row """""""" + (i + 1); if (i === 5 && cb.value) { row.title = """"""""The Evil Row""""""""; row.backgroundSelectedColor = """"""""blue""""""""; } if (i === 8) { // Just testing standard background row.backgroundColor = """"""""yellow""""""""; row.title = """"""""I am yellow""""""""; } rows.push(row); } tv.setData(rows); }); win.open(); {code} 2. Click on """"""""Create TableView"""""""" 3. Click on """"""""The Evil Row"""""""" Result: Row stays highlighted in blue until you rotate the device. Expected: Selected row should not stay highlighted regardless of row color. Note: * Bug appears on both V8 and Rhino * Tested on Droid 1 (2.2.2) running V8/Rhino and bug does not appear on Droid 1""""",title+description
TIMOB-6733,12,"""Android: date/time - rhino/v8 - Date and time are displayed differently based on compiler used""","""""""Description:  During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I Noted that the time displayed in the Date Picker was different for the rhino versus the v8 compile. Rhino shows """"""""February 1, 2009 12:00:00 AM PST"""""""" and the v8 showed """"""""Sun Feb 01 2009 00:00:00 GMT-0800 (PST)""""""""      Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with SDK 1.8.0.1 with rhino/v8  2) Navigate to controls>Picker>Date Picker  3) Change the date    Result:  The two compiles show different dates    Expected:  The dates match""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: date/time - rhino/v8 - Date and time are displayed differently based on compiler used
Description: """"Description: During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I Noted that the time displayed in the Date Picker was different for the rhino versus the v8 compile. Rhino shows """"""""February 1, 2009 12:00:00 AM PST"""""""" and the v8 showed """"""""Sun Feb 01 2009 00:00:00 GMT-0800 (PST)"""""""" Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with SDK 1.8.0.1 with rhino/v8 2) Navigate to controls>Picker>Date Picker 3) Change the date Result: The two compiles show different dates Expected: The dates match""""",title+description
TIMOB-6732,12,"""Android: html - rhino - Nook on rhino loads desktop google site while v8 loads mobile""","""""""Description:  During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I noticed that the rhino compile loaded the desktop google site, while the v8 compile loaded the mobile google site.      Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS nook with SDK 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>External URL    Result:  Desktop site loaded    Expected:  Mobile site loaded    Notes:  The Base UI>Views>Web Views>XHR to Filesystem test loads the mobile site""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: html - rhino - Nook on rhino loads desktop google site while v8 loads mobile
Description: """"Description: During a KS nook pass on v8 and Rhino on the Nook, I noticed that the rhino compile loaded the desktop google site, while the v8 compile loaded the mobile google site. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS nook with SDK 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>External URL Result: Desktop site loaded Expected: Mobile site loaded Notes: The Base UI>Views>Web Views>XHR to Filesystem test loads the mobile site""""",title+description
TIMOB-6731,12,"""MobileWeb: minHeight on window is getting set to the sum of the height of all child views""","""""""When adding child views to a window, the setMinHeight() method in window.js is setting the windows minHeight to the sum of all the child views, which results in content being pushed beyond the height of the screen.    setMinHeight() can be found on line 143 of window.js""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: minHeight on window is getting set to the sum of the height of all child views
Description: """"When adding child views to a window, the setMinHeight() method in window.js is setting the windows minHeight to the sum of all the child views, which results in content being pushed beyond the height of the screen. setMinHeight() can be found on line 143 of window.js""""",title+description
