TIMOB-6726,12,"""Android : Debugger - V8 when running basic breakpoint test, breakpoint shows import instead of import(x)""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Follow the test steps located here https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Debugger+Test+Plan to set up debug test project  2. Run test 1013 until step 20    Expected result:  On iOS and rhino imported call shows """"""""imported( x )""""""""    Actual result:  On V8 imported call shows imported()""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : Debugger - V8 when running basic breakpoint test, breakpoint shows import instead of import(x)
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Follow the test steps located here https://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Debugger+Test+Plan to set up debug test project 2. Run test 1013 until step 20 Expected result: On iOS and rhino imported call shows """"""""imported( x )"""""""" Actual result: On V8 imported call shows imported()""""",title+description
TIMOB-6725,12,"""Ti API: TableViewRow.selectedBackgroundColor reported as deprecated in Android""","""""""On Android, the View class has backgroundSelectedColor, backgroundSelectedImage properties.    In TableViewRow, we expose selectedBackgroundColor, selectedBackgroundImage properties.    On iOS, I believe this is the only way to set the selected background color.     On Android, we issue a deprecation warning and tell people they should be using backgroundSelectedColor, backgroundSelectedImage properties instead.    Something here is a tad fishy.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti API: TableViewRow.selectedBackgroundColor reported as deprecated in Android
Description: """"On Android, the View class has backgroundSelectedColor, backgroundSelectedImage properties. In TableViewRow, we expose selectedBackgroundColor, selectedBackgroundImage properties. On iOS, I believe this is the only way to set the selected background color. On Android, we issue a deprecation warning and tell people they should be using backgroundSelectedColor, backgroundSelectedImage properties instead. Something here is a tad fishy.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6724,12,"""Android: QTS - In Rhino, running test case 1387 throws a runtime error""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Install and launch QTS in Rhino  2. Click on 1387    Result: A runtime error is thrown. See attachment.  Expected: A success should be displayed.    Note:   * Did not get a runtime error in V8 on LG Slate (3.1)   * Bug does not appear in 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: QTS - In Rhino, running test case 1387 throws a runtime error
