TIMOB-6714,12,"""Android: Fastdev - resources fail to update on app re-deployment""","""""""Resources fail to update on app re-deployment. For instance, an existing image that is edited will not be updated by Fastdev after re-deploying the app.    This affects V8/Rhino. Regression.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Create Default Project, Run Code in Android Emulator 2.3.3 using V8:    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.createWindow({backgroundImage:'KS_nav_ui.png'}).open();  {code}    2. Navigate to 'KS_nav_ui.png' in the OS file system.  3. Open 'KS_nav_ui.png' in an image editor, and change it in a noticeable way (save over original).  4. Re-deploy the app in Studio without cleaning.    Expected Result:    The app should have the newest version of the image.    Actual Result:    The app still has the old version of the image. If the image did not exist before, nothing will be shown in it's place because the old version of the image in the resources was null.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Fastdev - resources fail to update on app re-deployment
Description: """"Resources fail to update on app re-deployment. For instance, an existing image that is edited will not be updated by Fastdev after re-deploying the app. This affects V8/Rhino. Regression. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create Default Project, Run Code in Android Emulator 2.3.3 using V8: {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.createWindow({backgroundImage:'KS_nav_ui.png'}).open(); {code} 2. Navigate to 'KS_nav_ui.png' in the OS file system. 3. Open 'KS_nav_ui.png' in an image editor, and change it in a noticeable way (save over original). 4. Re-deploy the app in Studio without cleaning. Expected Result: The app should have the newest version of the image. Actual Result: The app still has the old version of the image. If the image did not exist before, nothing will be shown in it's place because the old version of the image in the resources was null.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6713,12,"""Android: Timers are not being cancelled when onDestroy() is called.""","""""""Expected:    After hitting """"""""back"""""""" button to leave the application and trigger a destroy,    the timer should stop running and no more messages should be logged.    Actual:    Timer continues to run logging out messages.    {code:title=app.js}  setInterval(function () {    Ti.API.info(""""""""Beep."""""""");  }, 1000);  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Timers are not being cancelled when onDestroy() is called.
Description: """"Expected: After hitting """"""""back"""""""" button to leave the application and trigger a destroy, the timer should stop running and no more messages should be logged. Actual: Timer continues to run logging out messages. {code:title=app.js} setInterval(function () { Ti.API.info(""""""""Beep.""""""""); }, 1000); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6708,12,"""TiAPI: Update Rows in TableView""","""""""h5. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  The customer has a TableView with several rows. He wants to update each row with small text with the distance to a certain point after a refresh of GPS; doing it efficiently.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Update Rows in TableView
