TIMOB-6605,12,"""MobileWeb: Implement String.format() function""","""""""Need to implement the String.format() function. This function offers similar semantics as printf() as described in the IEEE printf specification: http://www.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/009695399/functions/printf.html.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Implement String.format() function
Description: """"Need to implement the String.format() function. This function offers similar semantics as printf() as described in the IEEE printf specification: http://www.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/009695399/functions/printf.html.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6604,12,"""MobileWeb: Build a robust internationalization and locale system""","""""""Mobile web needs a newly designed internationalization (i18n) and localization (l10n system. The system needs to be designed so that there's a default implementation in en-US, but then have several subdirectories for each language/locale with specific overrides.    For i18n, these are string tables.  This is tied into the Ti.Locale.getString() or L() function.    For l10n, we need modules that describe things such as currency, decimal, and date/time formatting.    When the app launches, it will detect the language and locale, then load the appropriate strings.  Language/locale bundles can be lazy loaded.    The build system will need to have support for i18n and l10n bundles.  That means that when you do a build, you can specify the supported languages that you want bundled into the build.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Build a robust internationalization and locale system
Description: """"Mobile web needs a newly designed internationalization (i18n) and localization (l10n system. The system needs to be designed so that there's a default implementation in en-US, but then have several subdirectories for each language/locale with specific overrides. For i18n, these are string tables. This is tied into the Ti.Locale.getString() or L() function. For l10n, we need modules that describe things such as currency, decimal, and date/time formatting. When the app launches, it will detect the language and locale, then load the appropriate strings. Language/locale bundles can be lazy loaded. The build system will need to have support for i18n and l10n bundles. That means that when you do a build, you can specify the supported languages that you want bundled into the build.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6603,12,"""iOS: iPad Popovers - Rotating the device while in the middle of a scrollable view causes it be stuck on screen and cannot be dismissed""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch KS-iPad  2. Open Main Tests   3. Click Show List  4. Click Popovers  5. Click Show Popover 3  6. Scroll to View 2 and pass it so you can see half the screen blue and the other half green (while holding the scrollview in this view), rotate device to landscape  7. Repeat step 6 and rotate to portrait  8. Click outside the popover to dismiss    Actual Result:  Cannot dismiss the popover    Expected Result:  Should be able to dismiss the popover    Note:  Existed in 1.7.5 """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad Popovers - Rotating the device while in the middle of a scrollable view causes it be stuck on screen and cannot be dismissed
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch KS-iPad 2. Open Main Tests 3. Click Show List 4. Click Popovers 5. Click Show Popover 3 6. Scroll to View 2 and pass it so you can see half the screen blue and the other half green (while holding the scrollview in this view), rotate device to landscape 7. Repeat step 6 and rotate to portrait 8. Click outside the popover to dismiss Actual Result: Cannot dismiss the popover Expected Result: Should be able to dismiss the popover Note: Existed in 1.7.5 """"",title+description
TIMOB-6602,12,"""Android: CommonJS Relative path in require() statement prevents file from loading""","""""""Expected: require('ui').createMainWindow().open() should load module and call methods  Actual: throws file not found error; need to use require('/ui').createMainWindow().open()    Attached file demonstrates problem.     The relative path worked in 1.7.6 and the CI build of 1.8 noted in the code comments""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: CommonJS Relative path in require() statement prevents file from loading
Description: """"Expected: require('ui').createMainWindow().open() should load module and call methods Actual: throws file not found error; need to use require('/ui').createMainWindow().open() Attached file demonstrates problem. The relative path worked in 1.7.6 and the CI build of 1.8 noted in the code comments""""",title+description
TIMOB-6601,12,"""iOS: Touchstart event is not being listening on the right view.""","""""""h3. Problem    Touchstart event is being listening for two views.    The customer is listening the touchstart event of the parent view, but when he press the child view he got the touch event of the parent view, and child view.    h3. Reproducible steps:     1. Run the code below  2. Click on the child view ( red square )    After pressing the child view ( red square ) you get the following outputs:    [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child  [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: parent    h3. Expected behavior:    The client wants to get the following output when he press the red button.    [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child    h3. Tested with the next specs:    iPhone 3G Version: 4.3.5  iPAD 2 Version: 5  Simulator    Titanium Studio, build: 1.0.7.201112080131  Titanium SDK: 1.8.0.1.RC1, 1.8.0.1.v20111205164258 & 1.7.5    h3.More info:    With 1.7.5 Titanium SDK you get the correct expected behavior.    h3. Sample code:         h3.Log Console:    {code: title=1.8.0.1.v20111205164258 Titanium CI Build  & iOS 5 SDK}    [INFO] One moment, building ...  [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.0.1 (12/05/11 16:42 d54627f...)  [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal  [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0  [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone  [INFO] Launching application in Simulator  [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (4.73 seconds)  [INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed  [INFO] Application started  [INFO] i13392/1.0 (1.8.0.1.v20111205164258.d54627f...)  [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child  [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: parent      {code: title=1.7.5 Titanium SDK  & iOS 5 SDK}      [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.7.5  [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal  [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0  [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone  [INFO] Performing full rebuild. This will take a little bit. Hold tight...  [INFO] Skipping JS compile, running from simulator  [INFO] Performing clean build  [INFO] Launching application in Simulator  [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (70.61 seconds)  [INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed  [INFO] Application started  [INFO] i13392/1.0 (1.7.5.ab20af7)  [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child  {code}    h3. Helpdesk  APP-796571                        """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Touchstart event is not being listening on the right view.
Description: """"h3. Problem Touchstart event is being listening for two views. The customer is listening the touchstart event of the parent view, but when he press the child view he got the touch event of the parent view, and child view. h3. Reproducible steps: 1. Run the code below 2. Click on the child view ( red square ) After pressing the child view ( red square ) you get the following outputs: [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: parent h3. Expected behavior: The client wants to get the following output when he press the red button. [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child h3. Tested with the next specs: iPhone 3G Version: 4.3.5 iPAD 2 Version: 5 Simulator Titanium Studio, build: 1.0.7.201112080131 Titanium SDK: 1.8.0.1.RC1, 1.8.0.1.v20111205164258 & 1.7.5 h3.More info: With 1.7.5 Titanium SDK you get the correct expected behavior. h3. Sample code: h3.Log Console: {code: title=1.8.0.1.v20111205164258 Titanium CI Build & iOS 5 SDK} [INFO] One moment, building ... [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.8.0.1 (12/05/11 16:42 d54627f...) [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0 [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone [INFO] Launching application in Simulator [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (4.73 seconds) [INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed [INFO] Application started [INFO] i13392/1.0 (1.8.0.1.v20111205164258.d54627f...) [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: parent {code: title=1.7.5 Titanium SDK & iOS 5 SDK} [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.7.5 [INFO] iPhone Device family: universal [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 5.0 [INFO] iPhone simulated device: iphone [INFO] Performing full rebuild. This will take a little bit. Hold tight... [INFO] Skipping JS compile, running from simulator [INFO] Performing clean build [INFO] Launching application in Simulator [INFO] Launched application in Simulator (70.61 seconds) [INFO] Found 5.0 patch installed [INFO] Application started [INFO] i13392/1.0 (1.7.5.ab20af7) [INFO] parent received TOUCHSTART event. Source: child {code} h3. Helpdesk APP-796571 """"",title+description
TIMOB-6600,12,"""Android: V8: Debugger: Unable to bind listening port if in use by another app.""","""""""Since we use a static port number for the V8 debugger agent's listening port, it may sometimes create conflicts  if multiple applications in debug mode are running on the device.    To test this launch an application in debug mode. Then switch to another application in your  workspace and launch that as well in debug mode. Watch logcat and you should see an error from V8  that it failed to bind the port and will try again.    Solution is probably to use the port number in deploy data for the device side (V8) like we do with the adb forwarding port (on host).""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: V8: Debugger: Unable to bind listening port if in use by another app.
Description: """"Since we use a static port number for the V8 debugger agent's listening port, it may sometimes create conflicts if multiple applications in debug mode are running on the device. To test this launch an application in debug mode. Then switch to another application in your workspace and launch that as well in debug mode. Watch logcat and you should see an error from V8 that it failed to bind the port and will try again. Solution is probably to use the port number in deploy data for the device side (V8) like we do with the adb forwarding port (on host).""""",title+description
TIMOB-6596,12,"""iOS: transition - Window open curl_up style plus device rotation results in UI only occupying a portion of the display. ""","""""""Description:  In KS, on the Base UI>Animation>transitions test, Rotating the device while the page_curl animation is rendering causes the UI to not use the full extent of the display when the animated window is closed. The timing of the device rotation is critical in reproducing this bug.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS built with SDK 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to Base Base UI>Animation>transitions  3) Click the """"""""full window"""""""" button and immediately rotate the device  4) Click the close button    Result:  The UI now only uses about two thirds of the display area.    Expected:  No changes in UI.    Notes: Also occurs with KS and SDK version 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: transition - Window open curl_up style plus device rotation results in UI only occupying a portion of the display.
Description: """"Description: In KS, on the Base UI>Animation>transitions test, Rotating the device while the page_curl animation is rendering causes the UI to not use the full extent of the display when the animated window is closed. The timing of the device rotation is critical in reproducing this bug. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS built with SDK 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Base Base UI>Animation>transitions 3) Click the """"""""full window"""""""" button and immediately rotate the device 4) Click the close button Result: The UI now only uses about two thirds of the display area. Expected: No changes in UI. Notes: Also occurs with KS and SDK version 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6595,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.Slider.thumbImage - custom image disappears when slider is being moved and physical pressure object (i.e., your thumb) is too close to the slider button""","""""""When a custom image is loaded into the Slider.thumbImage property, and the user moves the slider button, if their finger is too close to the slider button, the custom image temporarily disappears and is replaced by the default thumb image.    This affects 1.8.0.1/1.7.5 iOS.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the attached project SliderTest (images included).  2. Use the slider button, drag it back and forth.    Expected Result:    The custom slider button image should be visible when the button is being moved.    Actual Result:    When the slider button is being moved, the custom image disappears and the default image takes it's place during the course of the movement.  If the user moves their finger vertically away from the main slider while the slider button is being moved, the custom image reappears.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.Slider.thumbImage - custom image disappears when slider is being moved and physical pressure object (i.e., your thumb) is too close to the slider button
Description: """"When a custom image is loaded into the Slider.thumbImage property, and the user moves the slider button, if their finger is too close to the slider button, the custom image temporarily disappears and is replaced by the default thumb image. This affects 1.8.0.1/1.7.5 iOS. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the attached project SliderTest (images included). 2. Use the slider button, drag it back and forth. Expected Result: The custom slider button image should be visible when the button is being moved. Actual Result: When the slider button is being moved, the custom image disappears and the default image takes it's place during the course of the movement. If the user moves their finger vertically away from the main slider while the slider button is being moved, the custom image reappears.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6593,12,"""Android: Window.close() on windows with """"navBarHidden"""" attribute causes freezing events""","""""""h4. Issue  If I use the attribute """"""""navBarHidden"""""""" for any window in a tabgroup, upon closing them, the main window freezes and no event are generated.    h4. Reproduce Steps  - Click on the """"""""click to open another window"""""""" label  - Click on the """"""""Open final window"""""""" label  - Click on the """"""""Close All windows until tab main window"""""""" label  - Try to click again the """"""""Click to open another window"""""""" label , not works      h4. Code        h4. Working on 1.8.0.1  It's working good on 1.8.0.1 but i didn't find a jira bug related with this issue""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window.close() on windows with """"navBarHidden"""" attribute causes freezing events
Description: """"h4. Issue If I use the attribute """"""""navBarHidden"""""""" for any window in a tabgroup, upon closing them, the main window freezes and no event are generated. h4. Reproduce Steps - Click on the """"""""click to open another window"""""""" label - Click on the """"""""Open final window"""""""" label - Click on the """"""""Close All windows until tab main window"""""""" label - Try to click again the """"""""Click to open another window"""""""" label , not works h4. Code h4. Working on 1.8.0.1 It's working good on 1.8.0.1 but i didn't find a jira bug related with this issue""""",title+description
TIMOB-6592,12,"""Android: Gesture change event not fired when switching tab""","""""""h4. Issue  When user change the tab and then rotate the device, the orientation change event listener is not getting fired. I have attached a sample code and steps to recreate this issue is as below    h4. Steps  to reproduce  1. Switch to tab2  2. tilt the device to landscape  3. click on tab1 and rotate the phone to portrait.   Now the gesture change event will not be fired.        h4. Expected behavior  If TiSDK 1.8.01 is used the event is fired when we follow the steps above. We could not locate any existing JIRA log that has fixed the issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Gesture change event not fired when switching tab
Description: """"h4. Issue When user change the tab and then rotate the device, the orientation change event listener is not getting fired. I have attached a sample code and steps to recreate this issue is as below h4. Steps to reproduce 1. Switch to tab2 2. tilt the device to landscape 3. click on tab1 and rotate the phone to portrait. Now the gesture change event will not be fired. h4. Expected behavior If TiSDK 1.8.01 is used the event is fired when we follow the steps above. We could not locate any existing JIRA log that has fixed the issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6591,12,"""iOS: CoverFlowView - Coverflow view rendering and functional issues when leaving and returning to tab""","""""""Description:  In KS, on the Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files test, scrolling to the far right side of the stack of images then switching tabs and returning results in rendering problems. In addition to the imediately visible rendering issue, there may be a an image partially rendered behind the center image that is visible as you scroll through the images. This image goes away as you scroll by the same image in the stack.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS built with SDK 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files  3) Scroll to the far right of the stack  4) Switch tab  5) Switch back to the base UI tab    Result:  Image stack not as you left it with additional rendering problems as you manipulate the stack    Expected:  Images as you left them, no additional rendering issues    Note:  This also occurs on KS and SDK 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: CoverFlowView - Coverflow view rendering and functional issues when leaving and returning to tab
Description: """"Description: In KS, on the Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files test, scrolling to the far right side of the stack of images then switching tabs and returning results in rendering problems. In addition to the imediately visible rendering issue, there may be a an image partially rendered behind the center image that is visible as you scroll through the images. This image goes away as you scroll by the same image in the stack. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS built with SDK 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files 3) Scroll to the far right of the stack 4) Switch tab 5) Switch back to the base UI tab Result: Image stack not as you left it with additional rendering problems as you manipulate the stack Expected: Images as you left them, no additional rendering issues Note: This also occurs on KS and SDK 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6590,12,"""iOS: Contacts Picker - Received a deny file-write notice when selecting a contact from KS's Contacts Picker test""","""""""Details: A deny file-write notice is printed out to the console when selecting a contact with """"""""Address only"""""""" set to ON.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Install and launch KitchenSink  2. Navigate to: Phone>Contacts>Contacts picker  3. Switch """"""""Animated"""""""" to OFF and """"""""Address only"""""""" to ON  4. Press """"""""Show picker""""""""  5. Select a contact    Actual: A deny file-write notice is printed out to the console:        But, you can still see the address of the contact.    Expected: This notice should not appear.    Note: This bug persist in 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Contacts Picker - Received a deny file-write notice when selecting a contact from KS's Contacts Picker test
Description: """"Details: A deny file-write notice is printed out to the console when selecting a contact with """"""""Address only"""""""" set to ON. Steps to reproduce: 1. Install and launch KitchenSink 2. Navigate to: Phone>Contacts>Contacts picker 3. Switch """"""""Animated"""""""" to OFF and """"""""Address only"""""""" to ON 4. Press """"""""Show picker"""""""" 5. Select a contact Actual: A deny file-write notice is printed out to the console: But, you can still see the address of the contact. Expected: This notice should not appear. Note: This bug persist in 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6589,12,"""Android: Modules: runOnUiThread needs to be supported""","""""""Specifying """"""""@Kroll.setProperty(runOnUiThread = true)"""""""" has no effect on the thread that the method is executed. This is exhibited in the StyledLabel and Gigya modules. The StyledLabel module sets a property during an event notification from a button click. When the property is updated it makes a call to refresh the display of the label. Since the execution thread is different than the thread that created the view a CalledFromWrongThreadExeption is thrown. The label, in this case, was created on the main thread but the property update and subsequent attempt to update the view is running on the Kroll runtime thread.        To duplicate this issue,   1. Build the StyedLabel module from the apilevel2 branch of my module fork.   2. Run the example application from the module. The styled label will display correctly.  3. Click on the """"""""Only allow links"""""""" button -- this will force an update of the property that attempts to update the styled label view  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Modules: runOnUiThread needs to be supported
Description: """"Specifying """"""""@Kroll.setProperty(runOnUiThread = true)"""""""" has no effect on the thread that the method is executed. This is exhibited in the StyledLabel and Gigya modules. The StyledLabel module sets a property during an event notification from a button click. When the property is updated it makes a call to refresh the display of the label. Since the execution thread is different than the thread that created the view a CalledFromWrongThreadExeption is thrown. The label, in this case, was created on the main thread but the property update and subsequent attempt to update the view is running on the Kroll runtime thread. To duplicate this issue, 1. Build the StyedLabel module from the apilevel2 branch of my module fork. 2. Run the example application from the module. The styled label will display correctly. 3. Click on the """"""""Only allow links"""""""" button -- this will force an update of the property that attempts to update the styled label view """"",title+description
