TIMOB-6586,12,"""Android - Add support for repeating backgrounds on a view that is similar to background-repeat property in CSS""","""""""PROBLEM  A customer wants to create titled backgrounds, so they look the same in any platform, and they don't have to generate different background images for each different platform.    There is a screenshot showing the expected behavior. Additionally, you can see an example of code that will do the same effect, using insane amount of memory:    {code:title=titledapp.js|borderStyle=solid}  win = Ti.UI.createWindow();    var background = Ti.UI.createView();    var image1 = Ti.UI.createImageView({   // use whatever image you have here    image: 'appicon.png',    height: 'auto',    width: 'auto'  });     var width=image1.size.width;  var height=image1.size.height;    var deviceW= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth;  var deviceH= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight;    var repeatX = (deviceW % width) + 1;   var repeatY = (deviceH % height) + 1;       for(i=0;i<repeatX; i++)   for(j=0;j<repeatY; j++){    background.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({     image: 'appicon.png',     height: 'auto',     width: 'auto',     top:j*height,      left:i*width,    }));   }     win.add(background);  win.open();    {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android - Add support for repeating backgrounds on a view that is similar to background-repeat property in CSS
Description: """"PROBLEM A customer wants to create titled backgrounds, so they look the same in any platform, and they don't have to generate different background images for each different platform. There is a screenshot showing the expected behavior. Additionally, you can see an example of code that will do the same effect, using insane amount of memory: {code:title=titledapp.js|borderStyle=solid} win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var background = Ti.UI.createView(); var image1 = Ti.UI.createImageView({ // use whatever image you have here image: 'appicon.png', height: 'auto', width: 'auto' }); var width=image1.size.width; var height=image1.size.height; var deviceW= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth; var deviceH= Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.platformHeight; var repeatX = (deviceW % width) + 1; var repeatY = (deviceH % height) + 1; for(i=0;i<repeatX; i++) for(j=0;j<repeatY; j++){ background.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'appicon.png', height: 'auto', width: 'auto', top:j*height, left:i*width, })); } win.add(background); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6585,12,"""Android: Modules: V8 Cannot find symbol for mixed case module bootstrap class""","""""""Unable to build an application that uses the Urban Airship module. Receive the following build error when attempting to build an application that uses the UA module:        The problem is that the generated application java file references the bootstrap class with uppercase first letter and lowercase on everything else    Generated application.java file snippet      It is referencing the bootstrap class as """"""""ti.urbanairship.UrbanairshipBootstrap.class"""""""". Notice in the generated module bootstrap.java file that the class is """"""""ti.urbanairship.UrbanAirshipBootstrap"""""""" (with mixed case).        While we could workaround this for the UA module I am sure that other modules out in the marketplace are going to experience the same issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Modules: V8 Cannot find symbol for mixed case module bootstrap class
Description: """"Unable to build an application that uses the Urban Airship module. Receive the following build error when attempting to build an application that uses the UA module: The problem is that the generated application java file references the bootstrap class with uppercase first letter and lowercase on everything else Generated application.java file snippet It is referencing the bootstrap class as """"""""ti.urbanairship.UrbanairshipBootstrap.class"""""""". Notice in the generated module bootstrap.java file that the class is """"""""ti.urbanairship.UrbanAirshipBootstrap"""""""" (with mixed case). While we could workaround this for the UA module I am sure that other modules out in the marketplace are going to experience the same issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6584,12,"""iOS: Youtube Video: Rotating device while video is loading results in status bar out of sync and navbar rendering issues""","""""""Description:  In KS, on the Base UI>Views>Web Views>Youtube Video test, rotating the device while the video is loading first results in the status bar rotating without the UI (see attached image) then after the video is complete, the navbar is either drawn behind the status bar or is drawn with a gap between them. (See additional attached images).     Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS built with SDK 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Youtube Video  3) Rotate the device while the video is loading    Result:  Status bar rotates without the UI, then rendering of the navbar is incorrect    Note, This also occurs with KS and SDK 1.7.5    Expected:  Either status bar doesn't rotate, or entire UI rotates preventing navbar rendering issues.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Youtube Video: Rotating device while video is loading results in status bar out of sync and navbar rendering issues
Description: """"Description: In KS, on the Base UI>Views>Web Views>Youtube Video test, rotating the device while the video is loading first results in the status bar rotating without the UI (see attached image) then after the video is complete, the navbar is either drawn behind the status bar or is drawn with a gap between them. (See additional attached images). Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS built with SDK 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Youtube Video 3) Rotate the device while the video is loading Result: Status bar rotates without the UI, then rendering of the navbar is incorrect Note, This also occurs with KS and SDK 1.7.5 Expected: Either status bar doesn't rotate, or entire UI rotates preventing navbar rendering issues.""""",title+description
