TIMOB-6555,12,"""iOS: A Tab Bar's Child's leftNavButton Can Get Placed on Child""","""""""If navigation click events occur simultaneously, NavButtons get re-parented (every time) until further navigation.    In 1.8.0.1, the parent's leftNavButton displays in the child's tab bar (screenshot attached).  In 1.7.5, the child's tab bar displays in the parent's window (screenshot attached).    This bug is a permutation of http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-5351 <iOS: A Tab Bar's Child's rightNavButton Can Get Placed on Parent>.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code sample.        2. Press 'Open Middle' (nav bar button) to go to the middle window.  3. Press and hold 'I Am Middle, Click to Open...' (nav bar button). Order matters.  4. Press and hold 'I Am Outer' (table view row).  5. Release both at the same time.    Expected Result:    NavButton hierarchies should be maintained (screenshot attached) according to the original code, regardless of event synchronicity.    Actual Result:    In 1.8.0.1, the parent's leftNavButton displays in the child's tab bar.  In 1.7.5, the child's tab bar displays in the parent's window.  Correct parenting resumes on further navigation.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: A Tab Bar's Child's leftNavButton Can Get Placed on Child
Description: """"If navigation click events occur simultaneously, NavButtons get re-parented (every time) until further navigation. In 1.8.0.1, the parent's leftNavButton displays in the child's tab bar (screenshot attached). In 1.7.5, the child's tab bar displays in the parent's window (screenshot attached). This bug is a permutation of http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-5351 <iOS: A Tab Bar's Child's rightNavButton Can Get Placed on Parent>. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code sample. 2. Press 'Open Middle' (nav bar button) to go to the middle window. 3. Press and hold 'I Am Middle, Click to Open...' (nav bar button). Order matters. 4. Press and hold 'I Am Outer' (table view row). 5. Release both at the same time. Expected Result: NavButton hierarchies should be maintained (screenshot attached) according to the original code, regardless of event synchronicity. Actual Result: In 1.8.0.1, the parent's leftNavButton displays in the child's tab bar. In 1.7.5, the child's tab bar displays in the parent's window. Correct parenting resumes on further navigation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6554,12,"""Android: Module: """"'V8Util' has not been declared"""" error when building modules""","""""""When building several of the 2.0 versions of the modules, receiving an error of """"""""error: 'V8Util' has not been declared"""""""" during the ndk.build step.    Occurs on the imagefactory and styledlabel modules (as well as a couple of others).    The build output for the imagefactory module is as follows:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Module: """"'V8Util' has not been declared"""" error when building modules
