TIMOB-6485,12,"""iOS: Window - Opening and closing a modal window with split view while the device is upside down does not automatically reorient itself ""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Install and launch KS-iPad  2. Click Split View - Plain  3. Rotate ipad until it's upside down i.e. the menu button is the top  4. Click Show Modal  5. Click Dismiss modal    Results: The split view does not reorient itself while the ipad is upside down. See attachments.  Expected: The split view should automatically reorient itself.      Note: Bug does not occur in 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Window - Opening and closing a modal window with split view while the device is upside down does not automatically reorient itself
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Install and launch KS-iPad 2. Click Split View - Plain 3. Rotate ipad until it's upside down i.e. the menu button is the top 4. Click Show Modal 5. Click Dismiss modal Results: The split view does not reorient itself while the ipad is upside down. See attachments. Expected: The split view should automatically reorient itself. Note: Bug does not occur in 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6483,12,"""iOS: Debugger: return value should be undefined but is returning null""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run TC1013 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Debugger+Test+Plan  2. Get to Step 9    Actual Result:  foo is null    Expected Result:  foo should be undefined""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Debugger: return value should be undefined but is returning null
