TIMOB-6465,12,"""Android: Titanium.Media.Sound - V8/Rhino - Sound.setPaused method not found at runtime""","""""""In Android, the Titanium.Media.Sound.setPaused method is not found at runtime. This method is in the documentation.  This is not new, as it affects Android V8/Rhino in 1.8.0.1 and 1.7.5. Log and screen capture attached.  iOS is not affected.  Could be a doc bug or functional bug.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code, or check documentation: Titanium.Media.Sound.setPaused.        Expected Result:    App should run without runtime errors, or docs should not reference an unsupported method.    Actual Result:    App generates runtime error indicating """"""""Sound.setPaused"""""""" method not found.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Titanium.Media.Sound - V8/Rhino - Sound.setPaused method not found at runtime
Description: """"In Android, the Titanium.Media.Sound.setPaused method is not found at runtime. This method is in the documentation. This is not new, as it affects Android V8/Rhino in 1.8.0.1 and 1.7.5. Log and screen capture attached. iOS is not affected. Could be a doc bug or functional bug. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code, or check documentation: Titanium.Media.Sound.setPaused. Expected Result: App should run without runtime errors, or docs should not reference an unsupported method. Actual Result: App generates runtime error indicating """"""""Sound.setPaused"""""""" method not found.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6464,12,"""Tooling: Ensure that APIDoc summary field format is correct""","""""""Convention dictates that summary fields should start with a capital letter and end with a period.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Ensure that APIDoc summary field format is correct
Description: """"Convention dictates that summary fields should start with a capital letter and end with a period.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6462,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.Network.HTTPClient support for cross domain resources""","""""""Need to make sure that Ti.Network.HTTPClient support cross domain resources. This can be achieved with both Bryan's Ti.Network.httpURLFormatter as well as CORS server-side configuration. CORS support needs to be documented.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.Network.HTTPClient support for cross domain resources
Description: """"Need to make sure that Ti.Network.HTTPClient support cross domain resources. This can be achieved with both Bryan's Ti.Network.httpURLFormatter as well as CORS server-side configuration. CORS support needs to be documented.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6461,12,"""iOS: XML drillbit test exception failures""","""""""We currently have drillbit failures in XML from the 12/5/11 run of master@8f6f25b. Failures are:        We should make sure that exceptions are thrown at the correct points for error handling parity with Android. In general, we should make an effort to be DOM L2-compliant and throw exceptions where it's indicated that we need to in the spec.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: XML drillbit test exception failures
Description: """"We currently have drillbit failures in XML from the 12/5/11 run of master@8f6f25b. Failures are: We should make sure that exceptions are thrown at the correct points for error handling parity with Android. In general, we should make an effort to be DOM L2-compliant and throw exceptions where it's indicated that we need to in the spec.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6460,12,"""iOS: App always launches to non-retina iOS Simulator""","""""""h3.Problem  App always launches to non-retina iOS Simulator. It doesn't matter whether you build the app, then select retina, then build the app again. It will launch the non-retina screen.    h3.REGRESSION - that used to work with the old version of CI build 1.8.0.1v20111118152656    h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Build the sample code  2. When the simulator appears switch to Retina screen  3. Build the app again    h3.Sample Code  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App always launches to non-retina iOS Simulator
Description: """"h3.Problem App always launches to non-retina iOS Simulator. It doesn't matter whether you build the app, then select retina, then build the app again. It will launch the non-retina screen. h3.REGRESSION - that used to work with the old version of CI build 1.8.0.1v20111118152656 h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Build the sample code 2. When the simulator appears switch to Retina screen 3. Build the app again h3.Sample Code """"",title+description
TIMOB-6459,12,"""Android: MapView Annotations - leftButton/rightButton don't appear when included from a commonjs subdirectory""","""""""h2. Expected bahavior    Given the test case below, the delete.png image should be shown as the leftButton on the MapView Annotation when selected.    h2. Actual Behavior    The leftButton does not appear at all. This occurs only on 1.8.0.1 for both rhino and v8. 1.7.5 and 1.8.0v20111114 perform as expected.    The problem occurs only when the annotation/mapview are created in a commonjs module that is in a subdirectory of the Resources directory. So for example, the below test case will show the failing behavior, but if you moved winInclude.js to the main Resources directory, instead of the 'ui' subdirectory, it will work as it should.    h2. test case  h4. app.js    Creating the window from *Resources/winInclude.js* rather than *Resources/ui/winInclude.js* will make everything work fine.        h4. ui/winInclude.js      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: MapView Annotations - leftButton/rightButton don't appear when included from a commonjs subdirectory
Description: """"h2. Expected bahavior Given the test case below, the delete.png image should be shown as the leftButton on the MapView Annotation when selected. h2. Actual Behavior The leftButton does not appear at all. This occurs only on 1.8.0.1 for both rhino and v8. 1.7.5 and 1.8.0v20111114 perform as expected. The problem occurs only when the annotation/mapview are created in a commonjs module that is in a subdirectory of the Resources directory. So for example, the below test case will show the failing behavior, but if you moved winInclude.js to the main Resources directory, instead of the 'ui' subdirectory, it will work as it should. h2. test case h4. app.js Creating the window from *Resources/winInclude.js* rather than *Resources/ui/winInclude.js* will make everything work fine. h4. ui/winInclude.js """"",title+description
TIMOB-6458,12,"""iOS: CommonJS - native JavaScript modules for iOS encounter errors when referencing classes/objects in the Ti namespace""","""""""It looks like Titanium is having issues resolving symbols in the Ti/Titanium namespace referenced in code that is interpreted at run time. This issue has been observed when creating CommonJS native JavaScript modules for iOS.    To replicate the issue create a native JavaScript module for iOS using the steps described in the developer guide:    http://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/iOS+Module+Development+Guide#iOSModuleDevelopmentGuide-BuildingJavaScriptNativeModules    In the CommonJS code for the module attempt to open a file using the following code:    var file = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory + """"""""foo.txt"""""""");    This code will execute without issue in the iOS simulator, however on the handset it will cause your application to crash. Putting a reference to the Ti.Filesystem namespace in the app.js file before the module is loaded """"""""fixes"""""""" the issue on the handset, e.g.:    Ti.API.info(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory);  var o = require('your.module.name');    It appears that Titanium needs to resolve these symbols in code loaded in the main interpreter context before they can be used in code that is interpreted at run time.    Sample crash log:  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: CommonJS - native JavaScript modules for iOS encounter errors when referencing classes/objects in the Ti namespace
Description: """"It looks like Titanium is having issues resolving symbols in the Ti/Titanium namespace referenced in code that is interpreted at run time. This issue has been observed when creating CommonJS native JavaScript modules for iOS. To replicate the issue create a native JavaScript module for iOS using the steps described in the developer guide: http://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/iOS+Module+Development+Guide#iOSModuleDevelopmentGuide-BuildingJavaScriptNativeModules In the CommonJS code for the module attempt to open a file using the following code: var file = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory + """"""""foo.txt""""""""); This code will execute without issue in the iOS simulator, however on the handset it will cause your application to crash. Putting a reference to the Ti.Filesystem namespace in the app.js file before the module is loaded """"""""fixes"""""""" the issue on the handset, e.g.: Ti.API.info(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory); var o = require('your.module.name'); It appears that Titanium needs to resolve these symbols in code loaded in the main interpreter context before they can be used in code that is interpreted at run time. Sample crash log: """"",title+description
TIMOB-6457,12,"""iOS: CommonJS - Console errors not understandable""","""""""errors in apps using CommonJS in iOS are not allowing errors to show in the console correctly    In a non CommonJS app using this code:    We get this error...      But when using CommonJS:      Generates this error that is rather useless...      h2. Workaround    See [Tony's Comment|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6457?focusedCommentId=176700&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-176700] below.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: CommonJS - Console errors not understandable
Description: """"errors in apps using CommonJS in iOS are not allowing errors to show in the console correctly In a non CommonJS app using this code: We get this error... But when using CommonJS: Generates this error that is rather useless... h2. Workaround See [Tony's Comment|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6457?focusedCommentId=176700&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-176700] below.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6453,12,"""MobileWeb: Ti.include() relative files sometimes causes irrational paths""","""""""After the loader resolves a relative path, it does the following check:        The problem is sometimes a valid path can be """"""""../path/to/somefile.js"""""""" which gets appended to the base URL which throws an irrational path error.    The problem is discovered when testing Ti.Facebook in the KitchenSink.    The solution may be to just remove these lines of code, but there is probably a more fundamental problem with the relative path resolution that needs to be fleshed out with a specific test case.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Ti.include() relative files sometimes causes irrational paths
Description: """"After the loader resolves a relative path, it does the following check: The problem is sometimes a valid path can be """"""""../path/to/somefile.js"""""""" which gets appended to the base URL which throws an irrational path error. The problem is discovered when testing Ti.Facebook in the KitchenSink. The solution may be to just remove these lines of code, but there is probably a more fundamental problem with the relative path resolution that needs to be fleshed out with a specific test case.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6452,12,"""MobileWeb: Implement Ti.Label.ellipsize""","""""""Ti.Label.ellipsize is not supported, but can be with either text-overflow:ellipsis or overflow:hidden.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Implement Ti.Label.ellipsize
Description: """"Ti.Label.ellipsize is not supported, but can be with either text-overflow:ellipsis or overflow:hidden.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6451,12,"""Android: Drillbit: Unable to run any test suites, error in harness (app.js:45).""","""""""Drillbit fails to run any tests. Get the follow error w/ Rhino (also occurs w/ v8):    {quote}  E/ScriptsModule(22261): org.mozilla.javascript.EcmaError: TypeError: Cannot find function addEventListener in object [object Object]. (Resources/app.js#45)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.constructError(ScriptRuntime.java:3784)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.constructError(ScriptRuntime.java:3762)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.typeError(ScriptRuntime.java:3790)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.typeError2(ScriptRuntime.java:3809)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.notFunctionError(ScriptRuntime.java:3880)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.getPropFunctionAndThisHelper(ScriptRuntime.java:2359)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.getPropFunctionAndThis(ScriptRuntime.java:2326)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpretLoop(Interpreter.java:1514)  E/ScriptsModule(22261):  at script(Resources/app.js:45)  ...  {quote}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Drillbit: Unable to run any test suites, error in harness (app.js:45).
Description: """"Drillbit fails to run any tests. Get the follow error w/ Rhino (also occurs w/ v8): {quote} E/ScriptsModule(22261): org.mozilla.javascript.EcmaError: TypeError: Cannot find function addEventListener in object [object Object]. (Resources/app.js#45) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.constructError(ScriptRuntime.java:3784) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.constructError(ScriptRuntime.java:3762) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.typeError(ScriptRuntime.java:3790) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.typeError2(ScriptRuntime.java:3809) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.notFunctionError(ScriptRuntime.java:3880) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.getPropFunctionAndThisHelper(ScriptRuntime.java:2359) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.getPropFunctionAndThis(ScriptRuntime.java:2326) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpretLoop(Interpreter.java:1514) E/ScriptsModule(22261): at script(Resources/app.js:45) ... {quote}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6450,12,"""Android: Menu Button - KS's Basic Menu test crashes on Android Emulator 4.0 (V8 only)""","""""""Details: Running KS's Basic Menu test on Android Emulator 4.0 with V8 only crashes application.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Import KitchenSink  2. Run Base UI>Menu (Android)>Basic Menu    Results: KS crashes. See attachment basicMenuError.png  Expected: KS should not crash on Android Emulator 4.0    Note: Basic Menu test does not crash on 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Menu Button - KS's Basic Menu test crashes on Android Emulator 4.0 (V8 only)
Description: """"Details: Running KS's Basic Menu test on Android Emulator 4.0 with V8 only crashes application. Steps to reproduce: 1. Import KitchenSink 2. Run Base UI>Menu (Android)>Basic Menu Results: KS crashes. See attachment basicMenuError.png Expected: KS should not crash on Android Emulator 4.0 Note: Basic Menu test does not crash on 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6448,12,"""Nook: Orientation - v8/Rhino - Nook UI only displays landscape right when both landscape orientations are allowed by the app""","""""""Description:  If the user sets the window orientation modes allowed to both Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT and Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT then opens the window, the UI will be displayed only in landscape right. This does not occur on other android-based devices.    Sample code:      Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a project in studio and use the sample code for app.js  2) Install on Nook  3) Launch the app    Result:  UI will be landscape right and will not rotate to landscape left    Expected:  UI will rotate to either landscape based on device orientation""""""",Bug,"Title: Nook: Orientation - v8/Rhino - Nook UI only displays landscape right when both landscape orientations are allowed by the app
Description: """"Description: If the user sets the window orientation modes allowed to both Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT and Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT then opens the window, the UI will be displayed only in landscape right. This does not occur on other android-based devices. Sample code: Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a project in studio and use the sample code for app.js 2) Install on Nook 3) Launch the app Result: UI will be landscape right and will not rotate to landscape left Expected: UI will rotate to either landscape based on device orientation""""",title+description
TIMOB-6446,12,"""Android: Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.send - V8/Rhino - Android 2.x - send() loads text instead of image""","""""""Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.send loads text instead of image (log and screenshot attached).  Bug specific to Android 2.x.   Behavior not found in iOS or Android 3.x.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run KitchenSink (or KitchenSink-Nook if using the NookColor to have a valid test configuration).  2. Go to Platform > XHR > File Download.  3. Click """"""""Set Web View (Data)"""""""".    Expected Result:    Image should display.    Actual Result:    Text displays (screenshot attached). Errors log (attached).""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.send - V8/Rhino - Android 2.x - send() loads text instead of image
Description: """"Titanium.Network.HTTPClient.send loads text instead of image (log and screenshot attached). Bug specific to Android 2.x. Behavior not found in iOS or Android 3.x. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run KitchenSink (or KitchenSink-Nook if using the NookColor to have a valid test configuration). 2. Go to Platform > XHR > File Download. 3. Click """"""""Set Web View (Data)"""""""". Expected Result: Image should display. Actual Result: Text displays (screenshot attached). Errors log (attached).""""",title+description
TIMOB-6444,12,"""Android: Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer - V8/Rhino - createVideoPlayer fails to create video player""","""""""Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer fails to create video player.  Affects 1.8.0.1 on all Android devices. Does not affect 1.7.5 or iOS (1.8.0.1). Regression.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run videoTest project (attached).    Expected Result:    A short movie should play showing a failed slam-dunk attempt.    Actual Result:    Blank screen (screenshot attached). One log message (attached).    Log Excerpt:     12-02 15:11:04.040: W/VideoPlayerProxy(1637): (main) [4462,35857] Player action ignored; player has not been created.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer - V8/Rhino - createVideoPlayer fails to create video player
Description: """"Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer fails to create video player. Affects 1.8.0.1 on all Android devices. Does not affect 1.7.5 or iOS (1.8.0.1). Regression. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run videoTest project (attached). Expected Result: A short movie should play showing a failed slam-dunk attempt. Actual Result: Blank screen (screenshot attached). One log message (attached). Log Excerpt: 12-02 15:11:04.040: W/VideoPlayerProxy(1637): (main) [4462,35857] Player action ignored; player has not been created.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6443,12,"""Android: Keyboard: v8/rhino: Nook Only, Pressing on the button to change keyboard type blurs focus on the textfield""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch KS  2. Controls > Text Field > Keyboard  3. Give focus to the text field  4. Press any button    Actual Result:  The focus on the text field is blurred    Expected Result:  To change the keyboard type based on the button pressed """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Keyboard: v8/rhino: Nook Only, Pressing on the button to change keyboard type blurs focus on the textfield
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch KS 2. Controls > Text Field > Keyboard 3. Give focus to the text field 4. Press any button Actual Result: The focus on the text field is blurred Expected Result: To change the keyboard type based on the button pressed """"",title+description
TIMOB-6441,12,"""iOS : TableView - When pressing a table view row with a check, text disappears in other rows""","""""""This issue was discovered through http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3600    and goes back to 1.7.2    Steps to reproduce:  1. Grab the sample app.js provided and drop it into a new mobile app  2. Lauch the app  3. Press the first table view row  4. Press the second table view row    Expected result:  The table view row check mark toggles correctly    Actual Result:  In 1.7.2 the text is displayed in another empty table view row  In 1.8.0.1 the text disappears when another row is pressed""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : TableView - When pressing a table view row with a check, text disappears in other rows
Description: """"This issue was discovered through http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3600 and goes back to 1.7.2 Steps to reproduce: 1. Grab the sample app.js provided and drop it into a new mobile app 2. Lauch the app 3. Press the first table view row 4. Press the second table view row Expected result: The table view row check mark toggles correctly Actual Result: In 1.7.2 the text is displayed in another empty table view row In 1.8.0.1 the text disappears when another row is pressed""""",title+description
TIMOB-6440,12,"""Android: Analytics: When applications are backgrounded, analytics are recording as if the application is still running in the foreground""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Create a new application  2. Launch application   3. Press the home key  4. Wait 10 minute and re-launch application   5. Press the back button    Actual:  You get a start event and end event that is 10 minutes apart from each other    Expected:  Should get a background or something to tell the app owner that their application isn't actually being ran the entire time.  According to analytics this app was running for well over 10 minutes when in fact it was just launched and put in the background    Note:   Has been like this all the way back to 1.7.2""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Analytics: When applications are backgrounded, analytics are recording as if the application is still running in the foreground
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Create a new application 2. Launch application 3. Press the home key 4. Wait 10 minute and re-launch application 5. Press the back button Actual: You get a start event and end event that is 10 minutes apart from each other Expected: Should get a background or something to tell the app owner that their application isn't actually being ran the entire time. According to analytics this app was running for well over 10 minutes when in fact it was just launched and put in the background Note: Has been like this all the way back to 1.7.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-6439,12,"""Android: Menu: Rhino/v8: Adding onCreateOptionsMenu after window creation does not work""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Launch the app.js specified  2. Click on menu    Expected Result:  Menu appears with an """"""""Add Task"""""""" option. (should say 'works' when invoked)    Actual Result:  Menu does not appear    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Menu: Rhino/v8: Adding onCreateOptionsMenu after window creation does not work
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Launch the app.js specified 2. Click on menu Expected Result: Menu appears with an """"""""Add Task"""""""" option. (should say 'works' when invoked) Actual Result: Menu does not appear """"",title+description
TIMOB-6437,12,"""Android: TableViewRow display does not refresh on property change""","""""""TableViewRow display does not refresh on property change. To refresh the row, you must cause the refresh yourself (i.e., scroll up and down a few times). This affects Rhino and V8 in 1.8.0.1. This does not happen in 1.7.5 or iOS.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the following code in a new app.        2. Click on a row.    Expected Result:    Row should refresh with new properties (screenshot attached).    Actual Result:    Row does not refresh, must be manually refreshed to display property changes.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableViewRow display does not refresh on property change
Description: """"TableViewRow display does not refresh on property change. To refresh the row, you must cause the refresh yourself (i.e., scroll up and down a few times). This affects Rhino and V8 in 1.8.0.1. This does not happen in 1.7.5 or iOS. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the following code in a new app. 2. Click on a row. Expected Result: Row should refresh with new properties (screenshot attached). Actual Result: Row does not refresh, must be manually refreshed to display property changes.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6436,12,"""Android: change window.js addEventListener and addWrappedListener to use this.view rather than window""","""""""In window.js, the addEventListener and addWrappedListener method should use this.view rather than this.window as this.window in the case of LW windows will not represent the actual view we are interested in getting events from.  The implementation works but only due to bubbling.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: change window.js addEventListener and addWrappedListener to use this.view rather than window
Description: """"In window.js, the addEventListener and addWrappedListener method should use this.view rather than this.window as this.window in the case of LW windows will not represent the actual view we are interested in getting events from. The implementation works but only due to bubbling.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6435,12,"""MobileWeb: Add a formal proxy mechanism in HTTPClient""","""""""Add a mechanism that allows devs to define how cross domain requests are proxied.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Add a formal proxy mechanism in HTTPClient
Description: """"Add a mechanism that allows devs to define how cross domain requests are proxied.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6434,12,"""Android: insertRowAfter & insertRowBefore do not respect the header property of createTableViewRow""","""""""This is the Android version of: http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-1260.    When Ti.UI.TableView.insertRowBefore or insertRowAfter are used to insert a new row into a Ti.UI.TableView, any header properties in the row are lost.    iOS does not have this behavior.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the following code in a new app.        2. Click the buttons to add rows using the available options: Insert Row Before, Insert Row After, Append Row.     All new rows have a header property defined.    Expected Result:    New rows should display with a header.    Actual Result:    Only rows inserted using appendRow display headers. The headers are not displayed using the other methods.        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: insertRowAfter & insertRowBefore do not respect the header property of createTableViewRow
Description: """"This is the Android version of: http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-1260. When Ti.UI.TableView.insertRowBefore or insertRowAfter are used to insert a new row into a Ti.UI.TableView, any header properties in the row are lost. iOS does not have this behavior. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the following code in a new app. 2. Click the buttons to add rows using the available options: Insert Row Before, Insert Row After, Append Row. All new rows have a header property defined. Expected Result: New rows should display with a header. Actual Result: Only rows inserted using appendRow display headers. The headers are not displayed using the other methods. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6433,12,"""Android: v8 Nook Emulator: cannot run kitchensink-nook on the nook emulator skin with v8 Runtime but runs with WVGA854 on Lion Only""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Compile KitchenSink-Nook with v8 Runtime (Make sure to use the Nook Color Screen)  2. Compile KitchenSink-Nook with v8 Runtime (This time use WVGA854) - Works on Lion not Snow Leopard    Actual:  lvikvm(  294): threadid=8: thread exiting with uncaught exception (group=0x4001d800)  E/TiApplication(  294): (KrollRuntimeThread) [40,1421] Sending event: exception on thread: KrollRuntimeThread msg:java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: Library kroll-v8-device not found; Titanium 1.8.0.1,2011/12/01 13:43,4af3059  E/TiApplication(  294): java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: Library kroll-v8-device not found  E/TiApplication(  294):  at java.lang.Runtime.loadLibrary(Runtime.java:461)  E/TiApplication(  294):  at java.lang.System.loadLibrary(System.java:557)  E/TiApplication(  294):  at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Runtime.initRuntime(V8Runtime.java:43)  E/TiApplication(  294):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime.doInit(KrollRuntime.java:145)  E/TiApplication(  294):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime$KrollRuntimeThread.run(KrollRuntime.java:98)  I/TiRootActivity(  294): (main) [0,0] checkpoint, on root activity create, savedInstanceState: null    Expected:   To run on emulator    Note: Using a WVGA854 sreen works fine with the V8 Runtime only on Lion not on Snow Leopard. Rhino works with the Nook Color Screen""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: v8 Nook Emulator: cannot run kitchensink-nook on the nook emulator skin with v8 Runtime but runs with WVGA854 on Lion Only
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Compile KitchenSink-Nook with v8 Runtime (Make sure to use the Nook Color Screen) 2. Compile KitchenSink-Nook with v8 Runtime (This time use WVGA854) - Works on Lion not Snow Leopard Actual: lvikvm( 294): threadid=8: thread exiting with uncaught exception (group=0x4001d800) E/TiApplication( 294): (KrollRuntimeThread) [40,1421] Sending event: exception on thread: KrollRuntimeThread msg:java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: Library kroll-v8-device not found; Titanium 1.8.0.1,2011/12/01 13:43,4af3059 E/TiApplication( 294): java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: Library kroll-v8-device not found E/TiApplication( 294): at java.lang.Runtime.loadLibrary(Runtime.java:461) E/TiApplication( 294): at java.lang.System.loadLibrary(System.java:557) E/TiApplication( 294): at org.<USER>kroll.runtime.v8.V8Runtime.initRuntime(V8Runtime.java:43) E/TiApplication( 294): at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime.doInit(KrollRuntime.java:145) E/TiApplication( 294): at org.<USER>kroll.KrollRuntime$KrollRuntimeThread.run(KrollRuntime.java:98) I/TiRootActivity( 294): (main) [0,0] checkpoint, on root activity create, savedInstanceState: null Expected: To run on emulator Note: Using a WVGA854 sreen works fine with the V8 Runtime only on Lion not on Snow Leopard. Rhino works with the Nook Color Screen""""",title+description
TIMOB-6432,12,"""MobileWeb: Parity for high-priority APIs""","""""""We need to reach feature parity on certain high-priority APIs quickly. Some of these APIs work, some don't, and most we are unsure. Formal verification is necessary including both simulators and devices.    Ti.App.Properites  * getBool()  * getList()  * getString()  * removeProperty()  * setBool()  * setList()  * setString()    Note: Must persist values across page reloads    Ti.Facebook  * """"""""login"""""""" event  * authorize()  * request()  * logout()    Note: Must persist logged in state across page reloads    Ti.Network  * createHTTPClient()  * """"""""change"""""""" event  * networkType  * online    Ti.Platform  * openURL()  * canOpenURL()    Ti.UI  * 2DMatrix  ** Need to pull from <USER>timob-6017  * ActivityIndicator  * AlertDialog  * Animation  * Button  * ImageView  * Label  * Picker  * PickerColumn  * PickerRow  * ScrollableView  * ScrollView  * Slider  * Switch  * TabbedBar  * TableView  * TableViewRow  * TableViewSection  * TextArea  * TextField  * View  * WebView  ** Known issue that we can't load sites with frame busters (i.e. stackoverflow.com)  * Window    Note: It is advised to tackle Ti.UI APIs last.  """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Parity for high-priority APIs
Description: """"We need to reach feature parity on certain high-priority APIs quickly. Some of these APIs work, some don't, and most we are unsure. Formal verification is necessary including both simulators and devices. Ti.App.Properites * getBool() * getList() * getString() * removeProperty() * setBool() * setList() * setString() Note: Must persist values across page reloads Ti.Facebook * """"""""login"""""""" event * authorize() * request() * logout() Note: Must persist logged in state across page reloads Ti.Network * createHTTPClient() * """"""""change"""""""" event * networkType * online Ti.Platform * openURL() * canOpenURL() Ti.UI * 2DMatrix ** Need to pull from <USER>timob-6017 * ActivityIndicator * AlertDialog * Animation * Button * ImageView * Label * Picker * PickerColumn * PickerRow * ScrollableView * ScrollView * Slider * Switch * TabbedBar * TableView * TableViewRow * TableViewSection * TextArea * TextField * View * WebView ** Known issue that we can't load sites with frame busters (i.e. stackoverflow.com) * Window Note: It is advised to tackle Ti.UI APIs last. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6431,12,"""iOS: Blank Row Regression""","""""""h1. Problem  Blank rows appear in the table view. This regression is present in builds from today, back to around the 29th (the environment contains more specific information on which ones).    h2. How to Reproduce  1. Drop the following in an app.js  2. Run in iPad simulator  3. Drag the table view around; the quickest way to reproduce is to bounce at the top of the table view    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: '#ccc'  });    var data = [];  for (var i = 0; i < 200; i++) {      var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({          hasChild: true      });      row.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({          height: 24, top: 3, left: 34,          text: 'Row ' + i,          font: {              fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue',              fontSize: 18,              fontWeight: 'bold'          }      }));      row.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({          height: 20, top: 24, left: 34,          text: 'Subtitle for ' + i,          font: {              fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue',              fontSize: 14,              fontWeight: 'normal'          }      }));      row.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({          height: 24, width: 60, top: 10, right: 10,          textAlign: 'right',          text: i,          font: {              fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue',              fontSize: 18,              fontWeight: 'bold'          }      }));      data.push(row);  }    win.add(Ti.UI.createTableView({      style: Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED,      data: data  }));    win.open();  {code}      h2. Video of Behavior  http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ALMe0VsBXWQ""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Blank Row Regression
Description: """"h1. Problem Blank rows appear in the table view. This regression is present in builds from today, back to around the 29th (the environment contains more specific information on which ones). h2. How to Reproduce 1. Drop the following in an app.js 2. Run in iPad simulator 3. Drag the table view around; the quickest way to reproduce is to bounce at the top of the table view {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#ccc' }); var data = []; for (var i = 0; i < 200; i++) { var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ hasChild: true }); row.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ height: 24, top: 3, left: 34, text: 'Row ' + i, font: { fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue', fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 'bold' } })); row.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ height: 20, top: 24, left: 34, text: 'Subtitle for ' + i, font: { fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue', fontSize: 14, fontWeight: 'normal' } })); row.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ height: 24, width: 60, top: 10, right: 10, textAlign: 'right', text: i, font: { fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue', fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 'bold' } })); data.push(row); } win.add(Ti.UI.createTableView({ style: Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED, data: data })); win.open(); {code} h2. Video of Behavior http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ALMe0VsBXWQ""""",title+description
TIMOB-6429,12,"""MobileWeb: Remove all pre-1.8 deprecated APIs and platform specific namespaces""","""""""There's a number of deprecated APIs in mobile web that can be removed.  For example, Ti.UI has a ton of constants that are deprecated. Need to check with latest API docs to see what is really deprecated.    Platform specific namespaces to remove:  * Ti.Android  * Ti.App.Android  * Ti.App.iOS  * Ti.Media.MusicPlayer  * Ti.Network.BonjourBrowser  * Ti.Network.BonjourService  * Ti.UI.3DMatrix  * Ti.UI.Android  * Ti.UI.CoverFlowView  * Ti.UI.iOS.AdView  * Ti.UI.iOS  * Ti.UI.iPad  * Ti.UI.iPad.Popover  * Ti.UI.iPad.SplitWindow  * Ti.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone.AnimationStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone  * Ti.UI.iPhone.NavigationGroup  * Ti.UI.iPhone.ProgressBarStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone.RowAnimationStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone.ScrollIndicatorStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone.StatusBar  * Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton  * Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemIcon  * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewCellSelectionStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewScrollPosition  * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle  * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewSeparatorStyle  * Ti.UI.TabbedBar  * Ti.UI.Toolbar""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Remove all pre-1.8 deprecated APIs and platform specific namespaces
Description: """"There's a number of deprecated APIs in mobile web that can be removed. For example, Ti.UI has a ton of constants that are deprecated. Need to check with latest API docs to see what is really deprecated. Platform specific namespaces to remove: * Ti.Android * Ti.App.Android * Ti.App.iOS * Ti.Media.MusicPlayer * Ti.Network.BonjourBrowser * Ti.Network.BonjourService * Ti.UI.3DMatrix * Ti.UI.Android * Ti.UI.CoverFlowView * Ti.UI.iOS.AdView * Ti.UI.iOS * Ti.UI.iPad * Ti.UI.iPad.Popover * Ti.UI.iPad.SplitWindow * Ti.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone.AnimationStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone * Ti.UI.iPhone.NavigationGroup * Ti.UI.iPhone.ProgressBarStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone.RowAnimationStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone.ScrollIndicatorStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone.StatusBar * Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton * Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemIcon * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewCellSelectionStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewScrollPosition * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle * Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewSeparatorStyle * Ti.UI.TabbedBar * Ti.UI.Toolbar""""",title+description
TIMOB-6428,12,"""Android: Rhino only: Titanium.Android.R.drawable does not work""","""""""Description:    The menu icon does not appear on Rhino if it is retrieved from a resource using Ti.Android.R    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Base UI >Menu (android)> Menu Handlers(window options)  3) Click on """"""""Open Window""""""""  3) On next window, Click on menu    Result:  No icon is displayed on the menu    Expected:  A little x icon above the close option""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Rhino only: Titanium.Android.R.drawable does not work
Description: """"Description: The menu icon does not appear on Rhino if it is retrieved from a resource using Ti.Android.R Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Base UI >Menu (android)> Menu Handlers(window options) 3) Click on """"""""Open Window"""""""" 3) On next window, Click on menu Result: No icon is displayed on the menu Expected: A little x icon above the close option""""",title+description
TIMOB-6427,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.TableView incorrectly orders row elements and fails to display post-initialization header properties""","""""""Ti.UI.TableView incorrectly orders row elements and fails to display header property (when assigned after initialization) in all Android SDKs using TiMobile 1.8.0.1. In contrast, iOS (1.8.0.1) and all Android SDKs running 1.7.5 do not exhibit this behavior. Logs and screenshots attached.    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run code in new app. Use Android 1.8.0.1.        Expected Result:    Rows should display in order. All rows with an explicit header should display the header.    Actual Result:    Rows are out of order. Rows with headers assigned after initialization do not display header.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.TableView incorrectly orders row elements and fails to display post-initialization header properties
Description: """"Ti.UI.TableView incorrectly orders row elements and fails to display header property (when assigned after initialization) in all Android SDKs using TiMobile 1.8.0.1. In contrast, iOS (1.8.0.1) and all Android SDKs running 1.7.5 do not exhibit this behavior. Logs and screenshots attached. Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run code in new app. Use Android 1.8.0.1. Expected Result: Rows should display in order. All rows with an explicit header should display the header. Actual Result: Rows are out of order. Rows with headers assigned after initialization do not display header.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6426,12,"""MobileWeb: Add support for non-http protocols to Ti.Platform.openURL() and Ti.Platform.canOpenURL()""","""""""Ti.Platform.canOpenURL() just returns true for any and all urls.  Ti.Platform.openURL() performs an window.open() for all URLs.    For canOpenURL(), say true if url does NOT contain a """""""":"""""""" or it does contain a """""""":"""""""" but is http or https, otherwise false.  It would also be nice to have checks for if running in a simulator, then blacklist known unsupported protocols. For example, iPhone simulator doesn't support mailto, tel, sms, itms, itms-apps.    For openURL(), simply do something like:        canOpenURL(url) ? window.open(url) : window.location = url;    Problem with window.location is we may accidentally redirect the browser to a malformed mailto: or something. Perhaps we need to create a dummy iframe and target it by name with window.open()?    Note: this needs to be tested on all browsers including devices (ios & android) and simulators.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Add support for non-http protocols to Ti.Platform.openURL() and Ti.Platform.canOpenURL()
Description: """"Ti.Platform.canOpenURL() just returns true for any and all urls. Ti.Platform.openURL() performs an window.open() for all URLs. For canOpenURL(), say true if url does NOT contain a """""""":"""""""" or it does contain a """""""":"""""""" but is http or https, otherwise false. It would also be nice to have checks for if running in a simulator, then blacklist known unsupported protocols. For example, iPhone simulator doesn't support mailto, tel, sms, itms, itms-apps. For openURL(), simply do something like: canOpenURL(url) ? window.open(url) : window.location = url; Problem with window.location is we may accidentally redirect the browser to a malformed mailto: or something. Perhaps we need to create a dummy iframe and target it by name with window.open()? Note: this needs to be tested on all browsers including devices (ios & android) and simulators.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6425,12,"""Android: Packaging - Debug information is being printed out to DDMS when packaging KS to production""","""""""Details: After packaging KitchenSink for Android and installing it to device, debug data is being printed out to DDMS    Steps to reproduce:  1. Import KitchenSink to TiStudio  2. Package KitchenSink via TiStudio's """"""""Distribute - Android"""""""" menu option  3. Open DDMS  4. Install KitchenSink.apk to device  5. Press different tabs    Result: Debug data will be printed out to DDMS. See attachment.  Expected: Debug data should not be printed out to DDMS if app is packaged for Android production.    Note: Bug does not appear in 1.7.5  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Packaging - Debug information is being printed out to DDMS when packaging KS to production
Description: """"Details: After packaging KitchenSink for Android and installing it to device, debug data is being printed out to DDMS Steps to reproduce: 1. Import KitchenSink to TiStudio 2. Package KitchenSink via TiStudio's """"""""Distribute - Android"""""""" menu option 3. Open DDMS 4. Install KitchenSink.apk to device 5. Press different tabs Result: Debug data will be printed out to DDMS. See attachment. Expected: Debug data should not be printed out to DDMS if app is packaged for Android production. Note: Bug does not appear in 1.7.5 """"",title+description
TIMOB-6424,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.createImageView fails to either find or decode remote initial image""","""""""Ti.UI.createImageView fails to decode image on creation (log attached) in Android 2.2 (NookColor and Emulator). The Android 2.3.6 Device and Tab 3.1 have a separate error of filenotfound (attached), but the iPhone Simulator 5.0 and iPhone 5.0 correctly load and decode the remote image. Local images work in all cases.    Android 2.2 Error Log Excerpt:    12-01 14:12:07.093: W/TiDrawableReference(374): (main) [6,1703] Bitmap bounds could not be determined.  If bitmap is loaded, it won't be scaled.  12-01 14:12:07.103: D/skia(374): --- SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null  12-01 14:12:07.113: E/TiUIImageView(374): (main) [20,1723] Max retries reached, giving up decoding image source: http://www.zoomout.gr/assets/media/PICTURES/???????/651_thumb1.jpg    Android 2.3.6, 3.1 Error Log Excerpt:    12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): (pool-3-thread-1) [365,13155] Exception downloading http://www.zoomout.gr/assets/media/PICTURES/???????/651_thumb1.jpg  12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): java.io.FileNotFoundException: http://www.zoomout.gr/assets/media/PICTURES/???????/651_thumb1.jpg  12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872):  at org.apache.harmony.luni.internal.net.www.protocol.http.HttpURLConnectionImpl.getInputStream(HttpURLConnectionImpl.java:521)  12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872):  at java.net.URL.openStream(URL.java:645)  12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872):  at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiDownloadManager$DownloadJob.run(TiDownloadManager.java:134)  12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872):  at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1088)  12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872):  at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:581)  12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872):  at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1019)    Steps to Reproduce:    1. Run the following code in a new app.        Expected Result:    Image should download, decode and display.    Actual Result:    No image displays, errors log to the console. Android 2.2 has decode errors, Android 2.3.6 has filenotfound errors, iOS Simulators/Devices work correctly.    Note:    The local image 'KS_nav_ui.png' works as expected across platforms.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.createImageView fails to either find or decode remote initial image
Description: """"Ti.UI.createImageView fails to decode image on creation (log attached) in Android 2.2 (NookColor and Emulator). The Android 2.3.6 Device and Tab 3.1 have a separate error of filenotfound (attached), but the iPhone Simulator 5.0 and iPhone 5.0 correctly load and decode the remote image. Local images work in all cases. Android 2.2 Error Log Excerpt: 12-01 14:12:07.093: W/TiDrawableReference(374): (main) [6,1703] Bitmap bounds could not be determined. If bitmap is loaded, it won't be scaled. 12-01 14:12:07.103: D/skia(374): --- SkImageDecoder::Factory returned null 12-01 14:12:07.113: E/TiUIImageView(374): (main) [20,1723] Max retries reached, giving up decoding image source: http://www.zoomout.gr/assets/media/PICTURES/???????/651_thumb1.jpg Android 2.3.6, 3.1 Error Log Excerpt: 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): (pool-3-thread-1) [365,13155] Exception downloading http://www.zoomout.gr/assets/media/PICTURES/???????/651_thumb1.jpg 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): java.io.FileNotFoundException: http://www.zoomout.gr/assets/media/PICTURES/???????/651_thumb1.jpg 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): at org.apache.harmony.luni.internal.net.www.protocol.http.HttpURLConnectionImpl.getInputStream(HttpURLConnectionImpl.java:521) 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): at java.net.URL.openStream(URL.java:645) 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiDownloadManager$DownloadJob.run(TiDownloadManager.java:134) 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1088) 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): at java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:581) 12-01 15:11:26.505: E/TiDownloadManager(2872): at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1019) Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run the following code in a new app. Expected Result: Image should download, decode and display. Actual Result: No image displays, errors log to the console. Android 2.2 has decode errors, Android 2.3.6 has filenotfound errors, iOS Simulators/Devices work correctly. Note: The local image 'KS_nav_ui.png' works as expected across platforms.""""",title+description
