TIMOB-6375,12,"""Android: showContacts - v8/rhino - Selecting a person then clicking """"back"""" results in crash""","""""""Description:  In KitchenSink, in Phone>Contacts>Display people, I was presented with a list of contacts. I selected one, then hit the Android """"""""back"""""""" button. I was presented with a dialog stating that Kitchensink had stopped unexpectedly. Please see the attached file for console output.      Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to Phone>Contacts>Display people  3) Click on a contact in the list  4) On the resulting screen, click the android """"""""back"""""""" button    Result:  KS Crash    Expected:  User is returned to the Contacts table    Note:  Does not occur with 1.7.5 GA  Not observed on phones, just on the two tabs.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: showContacts - v8/rhino - Selecting a person then clicking """"back"""" results in crash
Description: """"Description: In KitchenSink, in Phone>Contacts>Display people, I was presented with a list of contacts. I selected one, then hit the Android """"""""back"""""""" button. I was presented with a dialog stating that Kitchensink had stopped unexpectedly. Please see the attached file for console output. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Phone>Contacts>Display people 3) Click on a contact in the list 4) On the resulting screen, click the android """"""""back"""""""" button Result: KS Crash Expected: User is returned to the Contacts table Note: Does not occur with 1.7.5 GA Not observed on phones, just on the two tabs.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6374,12,"""iOS: Module Template's Setter Property is Incorrect""","""""""h1. Problem  The setter example property in the default module template is written incorrectly, so it ends up hiding the getter.    h2. Test app.js  Run the following with the module for the conclusions to follow:  {code:title=app.js}  var test = require('ti.test');  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'white'  });  win.add(Titanium.UI.createLabel({   text: test.exampleProp  }));  test.exampleProp = 'Goodbyte, module!';  win.open();      The label will display """"""""[object ti.test]"""""""" (or whatever the ID of your module is), not the expected """"""""Hello, world!"""""""".    h2. How to Fix  The setter should be prefixed with """"""""set"""""""", as in the following:  {code:title=Good.m}  -(void)setExampleProp:(id)value  {   NSLog(@""""""""setExampleProp called!"""""""");  }  {code}    With that in hand, everything works as expected.    h2. Pull Request  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/788""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Module Template's Setter Property is Incorrect
Description: """"h1. Problem The setter example property in the default module template is written incorrectly, so it ends up hiding the getter. h2. Test app.js Run the following with the module for the conclusions to follow: {code:title=app.js} var test = require('ti.test'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'white' }); win.add(Titanium.UI.createLabel({ text: test.exampleProp })); test.exampleProp = 'Goodbyte, module!'; win.open(); The label will display """"""""[object ti.test]"""""""" (or whatever the ID of your module is), not the expected """"""""Hello, world!"""""""". h2. How to Fix The setter should be prefixed with """"""""set"""""""", as in the following: {code:title=Good.m} -(void)setExampleProp:(id)value { NSLog(@""""""""setExampleProp called!""""""""); } {code} With that in hand, everything works as expected. h2. Pull Request https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/788""""",title+description
