TIMOB-6371,12,"""Android: CommonJS apps crashing on android (V8 + Rhino) on Windows 7 / XP""","""""""h3. Expected Result:  A CommonJS project should build and run without build errors or runtime errors.    h3. Actual Result:  Rhino and V8 crash every time with the following error:        h3. Steps to Reproduce:    # Create a new project using 1.8.0.1 (V8 or Rhino), choose next (instead of finish).  # Use the code below to create the app  # Run the project (emulator or device) on a windows OS.    {code:lang=javascript|title=Resources/app.js}  // This is a single context application with mutliple windows in a stack  (function() {     var Window = require('ApplicationWindow').ApplicationWindow;      new Window().open();  })();      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: CommonJS apps crashing on android (V8 + Rhino) on Windows 7 / XP
Description: """"h3. Expected Result: A CommonJS project should build and run without build errors or runtime errors. h3. Actual Result: Rhino and V8 crash every time with the following error: h3. Steps to Reproduce: # Create a new project using 1.8.0.1 (V8 or Rhino), choose next (instead of finish). # Use the code below to create the app # Run the project (emulator or device) on a windows OS. {code:lang=javascript|title=Resources/app.js} // This is a single context application with mutliple windows in a stack (function() { var Window = require('ApplicationWindow').ApplicationWindow; new Window().open(); })(); """"",title+description
TIMOB-6370,12,"""iOS: TextArea scroll discrepancy behavior for modal windows on iPhone with/without retina""","""""""1. Create modal window with a scrollView and a TextArea - see code: http://pastie.org/2942088  2. Run the app and click on the textArea.    On an iOS device with retina (like iPhone 4) the behavior is the expected one.  On devices with no retina (like iPhone 3 emulator) the textArea is not fully scrolling up. The whole area is not shown and is partially covered by the keyboard.    This is only happening with windows with modal property (verifiable commenting/uncommenting lines 15 and 16).""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TextArea scroll discrepancy behavior for modal windows on iPhone with/without retina
Description: """"1. Create modal window with a scrollView and a TextArea - see code: http://pastie.org/2942088 2. Run the app and click on the textArea. On an iOS device with retina (like iPhone 4) the behavior is the expected one. On devices with no retina (like iPhone 3 emulator) the textArea is not fully scrolling up. The whole area is not shown and is partially covered by the keyboard. This is only happening with windows with modal property (verifiable commenting/uncommenting lines 15 and 16).""""",title+description
TIMOB-6368,12,"""iOS: Setting headers outside of table view row creation crashes the app""","""""""If we are trying to add a large number of rows into a tableview and set the header for each row, that will crash the app.     h4. Repro Steps  Step 1. Create an application based on the following code.  Step 2. Run the app and a crash will be happened.  Step 2. If you comment out the line """"""""row.header='A'"""""""", the app won't crash.        h4. Associated Helpdesk Tickdet:   http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-654533""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Setting headers outside of table view row creation crashes the app
Description: """"If we are trying to add a large number of rows into a tableview and set the header for each row, that will crash the app. h4. Repro Steps Step 1. Create an application based on the following code. Step 2. Run the app and a crash will be happened. Step 2. If you comment out the line """"""""row.header='A'"""""""", the app won't crash. h4. Associated Helpdesk Tickdet: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-654533""""",title+description
TIMOB-6367,12,"""Android: searchBar.blur() - v8/rhino - Blurring search bar attempts to hide soft KB but fails""","""""""Description:  In KitchenSink, in Controls>Search bar, blurring the search bar should dismiss the soft kb if it's onscreen but does not. A visible movement of the KB is perceived as it starts to dismiss, but does not actually complete the <USER> It remains on screen.     The workaround is to hide the field and then attempt to blur. THe KB will be removed from the screen.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to Controls>Search bar  3) Click on the search to bring up the soft KB  4) Click the cancel button or click the """"""""blur search bar""""""""    Result:  KB moves slightly as if it will move offscreen, but the KB remains on screen    Expected:  KB is removed from the screen    Note:  Also Occurs With 1.7.5 GA""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: searchBar.blur() - v8/rhino - Blurring search bar attempts to hide soft KB but fails
Description: """"Description: In KitchenSink, in Controls>Search bar, blurring the search bar should dismiss the soft kb if it's onscreen but does not. A visible movement of the KB is perceived as it starts to dismiss, but does not actually complete the <USER> It remains on screen. The workaround is to hide the field and then attempt to blur. THe KB will be removed from the screen. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Controls>Search bar 3) Click on the search to bring up the soft KB 4) Click the cancel button or click the """"""""blur search bar"""""""" Result: KB moves slightly as if it will move offscreen, but the KB remains on screen Expected: KB is removed from the screen Note: Also Occurs With 1.7.5 GA""""",title+description
TIMOB-6366,12,"""iOS: Misspelled color name in Webcolor.m""","""""""Webcolor.m contains a list of color names. Most of them are standard web colors. One of them is an iOS-specific color called """"""""stripped.""""""""      56                        [UIColor groupTableViewBackgroundColor],@""""""""stripped"""""""",    I'm pretty sure this is supposed to be """"""""striped.""""""""     If not, I recommend we rename it to """"""""nude"""""""" to avoid confusion.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Misspelled color name in Webcolor.m
