Description: """"Description: In KitchenSink, in email dialog, the first attempt to email failed after selecting an image. On both devices, """"""""no email available"""""""" was presented. The Galaxy had gmail configured, and the Xoom had both a Gmail and another email account configured. The second attempt was successful. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog 3) Select an image Result: """"""""no email available"""""""" presented Expected: Email sent dialog Note: Does not occur with 1.7.5 Does not occur on the second attempt""""",title+description
TIMOB-6362,12,"""Android: HTML - v8/rhino - Some image and text items not rendering""","""""""Description:  In KitchenSink, in local URL, text """"""""Click me to hide the Toolbar"""""""" and an apple logo should be rendered, but are not.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL      Result:  No """"""""click me..."""""""" text or apple logo image are rendered     Expected:  """"""""Click me..."""""""" text allowing hiding of the toolbar and an apple logo.    Note:  Does not occur with 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTML - v8/rhino - Some image and text items not rendering
Description: """"Description: In KitchenSink, in local URL, text """"""""Click me to hide the Toolbar"""""""" and an apple logo should be rendered, but are not. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL Result: No """"""""click me..."""""""" text or apple logo image are rendered Expected: """"""""Click me..."""""""" text allowing hiding of the toolbar and an apple logo. Note: Does not occur with 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6361,12,"""Android: Runtime -  A """"Titanium Javascript Runtime Error"""" is thrown in the console when clicking on the Back button in KitchenSink's Platform Data""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Import KitchenSink  2. Go to Platform>Platform Data  3. Click on Back button until you see tabs    Result:  A """"""""Titanium Javascript Runtime Error"""""""" is thrown in the console. See attachment.  Expected: Error should not be thrown in the console.    Note: Bug still appears in 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Runtime - A """"Titanium Javascript Runtime Error"""" is thrown in the console when clicking on the Back button in KitchenSink's Platform Data
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Import KitchenSink 2. Go to Platform>Platform Data 3. Click on Back button until you see tabs Result: A """"""""Titanium Javascript Runtime Error"""""""" is thrown in the console. See attachment. Expected: Error should not be thrown in the console. Note: Bug still appears in 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6360,12,"""Android: tableViewRow - v8/rhino - Expecting objects, but proxies are returned for row and section when row is clicked""","""""""Description:  In KitchenSink, a tableview row listener is expected to return a row and section object, but returns proxies.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1  2) Navigate to any of the following:  Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table API Basic  Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Custom Row Header  Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Empty DataSet (Create)  Base UI>Views>Table Views>Append Row  Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Auto Height  Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Search  3) Click on a row    Result:  Alert with:  row [object TableViewRowProxy] index 1 section [object TableViewSectionProxy] row data null    Expected:  Alert with:  row [Ti.UI.TableViewRow] index 1 section [object TiUITableViewSection] title Row 2    Note:  Does not occur with 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: tableViewRow - v8/rhino - Expecting objects, but proxies are returned for row and section when row is clicked
Description: """"Description: In KitchenSink, a tableview row listener is expected to return a row and section object, but returns proxies. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with 1.8.0.1 2) Navigate to any of the following: Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table API Basic Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Custom Row Header Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Empty DataSet (Create) Base UI>Views>Table Views>Append Row Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Auto Height Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Search 3) Click on a row Result: Alert with: row [object TableViewRowProxy] index 1 section [object TableViewSectionProxy] row data null Expected: Alert with: row [Ti.UI.TableViewRow] index 1 section [object TiUITableViewSection] title Row 2 Note: Does not occur with 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6359,12,"""Android: Menu Button - Pressing the menu button does not bring up menu options""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Import KitchenSink  2. Go to one of the following:  Base UI>Menu (Android)>Basic Menu  Base UI>Menu (Android)>Menu Handlers (Window Options)  Base UI>Menu (Android)>Menu Handlers (Activity Property)    3. Press the Menu button on device    Result: Menu option does not appear.  Expected: Android's Menu option should appear    Note: Bug does not appear in sdk 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Menu Button - Pressing the menu button does not bring up menu options
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Import KitchenSink 2. Go to one of the following: Base UI>Menu (Android)>Basic Menu Base UI>Menu (Android)>Menu Handlers (Window Options) Base UI>Menu (Android)>Menu Handlers (Activity Property) 3. Press the Menu button on device Result: Menu option does not appear. Expected: Android's Menu option should appear Note: Bug does not appear in sdk 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6358,12,"""Android: Keyboard - """"Request Hide Keyboard"""" does not hide the keyboard""","""""""Description:  Pressing the """"""""Request Hide Keyboard"""""""" button in KitchenSink does not hide the keyboard.    Steps to reproduce:  1. Import KitchenSink  2. Go to Base UI>Hide Soft Keyboard (Android)  3. Type something in the text field  4. Press """"""""Request Hide Keyboard""""""""    Result: Keyboard does not hide.  Expected: Keyboard should hide after pressing the button.    Note: Bug does not persist in sdk 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Keyboard - """"Request Hide Keyboard"""" does not hide the keyboard
Description: """"Description: Pressing the """"""""Request Hide Keyboard"""""""" button in KitchenSink does not hide the keyboard. Steps to reproduce: 1. Import KitchenSink 2. Go to Base UI>Hide Soft Keyboard (Android) 3. Type something in the text field 4. Press """"""""Request Hide Keyboard"""""""" Result: Keyboard does not hide. Expected: Keyboard should hide after pressing the button. Note: Bug does not persist in sdk 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-6357,12,"""Android: Duplicating file with another name on android after saving a picture""","""""""h3. Problem    After taking a picture in android with the code below the application creates 2 files in the next path:  /sdcard/DCIM/camera/  One of them is named with the initials tiaxxx.jpg    h3. Reproducible steps:     1. Run the code below  2. Take a picture  3. Go to the next path: /sdcard/DCIM/camera/    Notice that in the above path is created a file with the name of tiaxxx.jpg    h3. Expected behavior:    Customer does not want to have another image stored with the name Tiaxxxx.jpg in the next path: /sdcard/DCIM/camera/    h3. More info:  I use saveToPhotoGallery:false too, but it's the same expected behavior.    h3. Sample code:       h3. Helpdesk  APP-344567                            """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Duplicating file with another name on android after saving a picture
Description: """"h3. Problem After taking a picture in android with the code below the application creates 2 files in the next path: /sdcard/DCIM/camera/ One of them is named with the initials tiaxxx.jpg h3. Reproducible steps: 1. Run the code below 2. Take a picture 3. Go to the next path: /sdcard/DCIM/camera/ Notice that in the above path is created a file with the name of tiaxxx.jpg h3. Expected behavior: Customer does not want to have another image stored with the name Tiaxxxx.jpg in the next path: /sdcard/DCIM/camera/ h3. More info: I use saveToPhotoGallery:false too, but it's the same expected behavior. h3. Sample code: h3. Helpdesk APP-344567 """"",title+description
TIMOB-6356,12,"""iOS: DashboardView change of page event""","""""""PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  The customer wants to receive a callback when the user changes the page in a dashboard view. Any suggestions how to make this happen?    STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Copy this code to a new project http://pastie.org/2926791  2. Compile and open the app in the simulator    ACTUAL RESULTS  We can't get any event when changing the page     EXPECTED RESULTS  We would love to get an event when changing the page.    EXTRA COMMENTS  The customer tried  swipe, touchstart, and touchmove events, but they are not being fired;     I tried touchstart, touchend without success.     Original Ticket in HelpDesk: APP-335973    EXAMPLE CODE  {code:title=app.js}  var mainWindow = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var dashboardView;    var createDashboardItem = function(index) {   var item, label;      item = Titanium.UI.createDashboardItem({    canDelete : true   });     label = Titanium.UI.createLabel({    borderColor: 'red',    borderWidth: 1,    text : 'build 6:' + index,    color : 'red',    textAlign : 'center'   });       item.add(label);     return item;  };    var eventListener = function(e) {   Ti.API.info('received ' + e.type + ' event.');  };    var updateDashboard = function() {   var i, dashboardData;      if (dashboardView) {    mainWindow.remove(dashboardView);    for(i = 0; i < 4; i++) {     dashboardView.data[i] = null;    }     dashboardView = null;   }     dashboardData = [];     for(i = 0; i < 10; i++) {    dashboardData.push(createDashboardItem(i));   }   // Here we should ideally just do this:   //   // dashboardView.data = dashboardData;   //   // but that completely messes up the DashboardView.   // Related JIRA ticket:   //    http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-2635      dashboardView = Titanium.UI.createDashboardView({    height : 400,    width : 300,    top : 15,    left : 10   });      dashboardView.addEventListener('click', eventListener);   dashboardView.addEventListener('swipe', eventListener);   dashboardView.addEventListener('touchstart', eventListener);   dashboardView.addEventListener('touchmove', eventListener);      dashboardView.data = dashboardData;   mainWindow.add(dashboardView);  };    // updateDashboard sets dashboardView and adds it to mainWindow  updateDashboard();    var button1 = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: 'Refresh',   width: 100, height: 40, bottom: 0,   left:0  });  button1.addEventListener('click', function(){   updateDashboard();  });    mainWindow.add(button1);    mainWindow.open();  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: DashboardView change of page event
Description: """"PROBLEM DESCRIPTION The customer wants to receive a callback when the user changes the page in a dashboard view. Any suggestions how to make this happen? STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Copy this code to a new project http://pastie.org/2926791 2. Compile and open the app in the simulator ACTUAL RESULTS We can't get any event when changing the page EXPECTED RESULTS We would love to get an event when changing the page. EXTRA COMMENTS The customer tried swipe, touchstart, and touchmove events, but they are not being fired; I tried touchstart, touchend without success. Original Ticket in HelpDesk: APP-335973 EXAMPLE CODE {code:title=app.js} var mainWindow = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var dashboardView; var createDashboardItem = function(index) { var item, label; item = Titanium.UI.createDashboardItem({ canDelete : true }); label = Titanium.UI.createLabel({ borderColor: 'red', borderWidth: 1, text : 'build 6:' + index, color : 'red', textAlign : 'center' }); item.add(label); return item; }; var eventListener = function(e) { Ti.API.info('received ' + e.type + ' event.'); }; var updateDashboard = function() { var i, dashboardData; if (dashboardView) { mainWindow.remove(dashboardView); for(i = 0; i < 4; i++) { dashboardView.data[i] = null; } dashboardView = null; } dashboardData = []; for(i = 0; i < 10; i++) { dashboardData.push(createDashboardItem(i)); } // Here we should ideally just do this: // // dashboardView.data = dashboardData; // // but that completely messes up the DashboardView. // Related JIRA ticket: // http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-2635 dashboardView = Titanium.UI.createDashboardView({ height : 400, width : 300, top : 15, left : 10 }); dashboardView.addEventListener('click', eventListener); dashboardView.addEventListener('swipe', eventListener); dashboardView.addEventListener('touchstart', eventListener); dashboardView.addEventListener('touchmove', eventListener); dashboardView.data = dashboardData; mainWindow.add(dashboardView); }; // updateDashboard sets dashboardView and adds it to mainWindow updateDashboard(); var button1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Refresh', width: 100, height: 40, bottom: 0, left:0 }); button1.addEventListener('click', function(){ updateDashboard(); }); mainWindow.add(button1); mainWindow.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6355,12,"""iOS: Support handleOpenURL""","""""""h3.New Feature Request    Please add the handleOpenURL functionality so that it would allow you to register the specific url path. Please also add the support for properties for URL Scheme / URL from info.plist so that will be able to register the custom URL schemes.     Native iOS tutorial of how it could be accomplished: http://mobile.tutsplus.com/tutorials/iphone/ios-sdk-working-with-url-schemes    The final result should be that while inside some .html file we put <a href=""""""""myapp://test"""""""">test</a> it would open the myapp and we will get the input (""""""""test""""""""). That should also work when we are inside the application and using the webview (should trigger the internal event).    The Titanium code should look like:        h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-228477""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Support handleOpenURL
Description: """"h3.New Feature Request Please add the handleOpenURL functionality so that it would allow you to register the specific url path. Please also add the support for properties for URL Scheme / URL from info.plist so that will be able to register the custom URL schemes. Native iOS tutorial of how it could be accomplished: http://mobile.tutsplus.com/tutorials/iphone/ios-sdk-working-with-url-schemes The final result should be that while inside some .html file we put <a href=""""""""myapp://test"""""""">test</a> it would open the myapp and we will get the input (""""""""test""""""""). That should also work when we are inside the application and using the webview (should trigger the internal event). The Titanium code should look like: h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-228477""""",title+description
