TIMOB-6351,12,""" Android: saveToPhotoGallery:false does not work in android.""","""""""h3. Problem    SaveToPhotoGallery:false does not work in android.    h3. Reproducible steps:     1. Run the code below    h3. Expected behavior:    Customer does not want to save the image to the gallery after taking a picture.    h3. More info:    In iOS works well.  http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.showCamera-method.html  saveToPhotoGalleryboolean if the media should be saved to the photo gallery upon successful capture.    h3. Tested with the next specs:  Samsung Galaxy Fit-Android Version : 2.2.1  iPhone 3G Version: 4.3.5  Simulator  Titanium Studio, build: 1.0.7.201111231202  Titanium SDK: 1.8.0.v20111114103905  Google APIs Android 2.3.3    h3. Sample code:       h3. Helpdesk  APP-344567                          """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: saveToPhotoGallery:false does not work in android.
Description: """"h3. Problem SaveToPhotoGallery:false does not work in android. h3. Reproducible steps: 1. Run the code below h3. Expected behavior: Customer does not want to save the image to the gallery after taking a picture. h3. More info: In iOS works well. http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.showCamera-method.html saveToPhotoGalleryboolean if the media should be saved to the photo gallery upon successful capture. h3. Tested with the next specs: Samsung Galaxy Fit-Android Version : 2.2.1 iPhone 3G Version: 4.3.5 Simulator Titanium Studio, build: 1.0.7.201111231202 Titanium SDK: 1.8.0.v20111114103905 Google APIs Android 2.3.3 h3. Sample code: h3. Helpdesk APP-344567 """"",title+description
TIMOB-6349,12,"""iOS: Read database from the Resources folder""","""""""h3.New feature request    Please add the possibility of running the .db (read only) file from the Resources folder. For now the Ti.Database.install copies the .db file and leaves the old under Resources which makes the app to weight too much. For example having 50MB of read only database makes the app to weight 100MB.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Read database from the Resources folder
Description: """"h3.New feature request Please add the possibility of running the .db (read only) file from the Resources folder. For now the Ti.Database.install copies the .db file and leaves the old under Resources which makes the app to weight too much. For example having 50MB of read only database makes the app to weight 100MB.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6348,12,"""iOS: ProgressBar does not display correctly when 'top' is not set""","""""""For some reason, when the 'top' property is not set up a progress bar, the progress is always displayed as 100%.    This was reported as a doc error, (TIMOB-5809) but I believe this part of the bug is an iOS bug. This behavior does not occur on Android.    To reproduce, use the following code in app.js:        When run on iOS, the progress bar shows up as 100% done. If you uncomment the """"""""top: 10"""""""" line and re-run, the progress bar shows up with the proper value--50% done.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ProgressBar does not display correctly when 'top' is not set
Description: """"For some reason, when the 'top' property is not set up a progress bar, the progress is always displayed as 100%. This was reported as a doc error, (TIMOB-5809) but I believe this part of the bug is an iOS bug. This behavior does not occur on Android. To reproduce, use the following code in app.js: When run on iOS, the progress bar shows up as 100% done. If you uncomment the """"""""top: 10"""""""" line and re-run, the progress bar shows up with the proper value--50% done. """"",title+description
