TIMOB-6229,12,"""iOS: DashboardView is leaking memory""","""""""h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION  If you are updating a DashboardView (by means of removing the data, then the view, then creating new data, then creating the dashboardview). In the test code (attached or included here) we only have a button that will refresh the DashboardView, and a DashboardView. Everytime that the button is pressed, the DashboardView will refresh, but will leak some stuff.     h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE  1. Get the code: http://pastie.org/private/nifrkckutcfyinasidqucg  2. Create a new mobile project in Titanium  3. Get the code into the app.js  4. Compile  5. Press """"""""Refresh"""""""" until crash.    h4. EXPECTED RESULTS  The DashboardView refreshing without issues.    h4. ACTUAL RESULTS  The App is crashing.    h4. EXTRA INFO  This happens in iOS 4.x and 5.0. The leak size is like 300k each refresh.     """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: DashboardView is leaking memory
Description: """"h4. PROBLEM DESCRIPTION If you are updating a DashboardView (by means of removing the data, then the view, then creating new data, then creating the dashboardview). In the test code (attached or included here) we only have a button that will refresh the DashboardView, and a DashboardView. Everytime that the button is pressed, the DashboardView will refresh, but will leak some stuff. h4. STEPS TO REPRODUCE 1. Get the code: http://pastie.org/private/nifrkckutcfyinasidqucg 2. Create a new mobile project in Titanium 3. Get the code into the app.js 4. Compile 5. Press """"""""Refresh"""""""" until crash. h4. EXPECTED RESULTS The DashboardView refreshing without issues. h4. ACTUAL RESULTS The App is crashing. h4. EXTRA INFO This happens in iOS 4.x and 5.0. The leak size is like 300k each refresh. """"",title+description
TIMOB-6228,12,"""iOS: animate callback never gets executed when when using Ti.UI.createAnimation""","""""""Animate callback never gets called if you use Ti.UI.createAnimation. It get called if you use an object instead.    Step 1: Run the code below  Step 2: click the window  Step 3: notice that the info statement never shows   Step 4: in animate() replace 'animation' with 'animationObj'.  Step 5: run code  Step 6: click the window  Step 7: notice the info statement in the callback shows up.        h4. Workaround(s)  1. use an object for your animation  2. animation.addEventListener('complete', function(){});""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: animate callback never gets executed when when using Ti.UI.createAnimation
Description: """"Animate callback never gets called if you use Ti.UI.createAnimation. It get called if you use an object instead. Step 1: Run the code below Step 2: click the window Step 3: notice that the info statement never shows Step 4: in animate() replace 'animation' with 'animationObj'. Step 5: run code Step 6: click the window Step 7: notice the info statement in the callback shows up. h4. Workaround(s) 1. use an object for your animation 2. animation.addEventListener('complete', function(){});""""",title+description
