TIMOB-6204,12,"""Android: V8 - fireEvent does not work for Views""","""""""h3. Problem:  Setting a fireEvent() on any UI element does work with V8.    h3. Example:    h3. To Reproduce:  Simple run the sample code in app.js and click the button.    h3. What has to happen:  The background of the window has to turn green    h3. What happens:  nothing""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: V8 - fireEvent does not work for Views
Description: """"h3. Problem: Setting a fireEvent() on any UI element does work with V8. h3. Example: h3. To Reproduce: Simple run the sample code in app.js and click the button. h3. What has to happen: The background of the window has to turn green h3. What happens: nothing""""",title+description
TIMOB-6203,12,"""Android: Expose a way to hook into logging API.""","""""""To re-enable debugging we need a way to hook into the API logging methods.  The best approach is probably to add a hook into KrollLogging. V8 does not use this  by default, instead it uses a C API exposed by Android. So when debugging is active, we need  V8 to instead call into Java and use KrollLogging. Rhino should already be using KrollLogging.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: Expose a way to hook into logging API.
Description: """"To re-enable debugging we need a way to hook into the API logging methods. The best approach is probably to add a hook into KrollLogging. V8 does not use this by default, instead it uses a C API exposed by Android. So when debugging is active, we need V8 to instead call into Java and use KrollLogging. Rhino should already be using KrollLogging.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6202,12,"""MobileWeb: Creating new classes without a definition throws error when instantiating""","""""""In Ti._5.createClass(), if the class definition (value) is not a function, it defaults the definition to """"""""new Object()"""""""".  This works fine, however if you try to create a new instance of this class, it throws a JavaScript error.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Creating new classes without a definition throws error when instantiating
Description: """"In Ti._5.createClass(), if the class definition (value) is not a function, it defaults the definition to """"""""new Object()"""""""". This works fine, however if you try to create a new instance of this class, it throws a JavaScript error.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6201,12,"""Android: V8 shared libraries need to be packaged in ARM specific lib folders""","""""""Right now we have two shared libraries in V8: libkroll-v8-device.so (for armeabi v7) and libkroll-v8-emulator.so (for armeabi v5). We need to move to using the ARM ABI specific folders in our packaging so apps can be correctly distributed to end users.    Right now, some Froyo and above devices have ARM v5 chips (such as Bill's LG-P509), and the libkroll-v8-device.so library won't work for them.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: V8 shared libraries need to be packaged in ARM specific lib folders
Description: """"Right now we have two shared libraries in V8: libkroll-v8-device.so (for armeabi v7) and libkroll-v8-emulator.so (for armeabi v5). We need to move to using the ARM ABI specific folders in our packaging so apps can be correctly distributed to end users. Right now, some Froyo and above devices have ARM v5 chips (such as Bill's LG-P509), and the libkroll-v8-device.so library won't work for them.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6200,12,"""iOS: Table View setData Now Animates Rows In""","""""""h1. Problem  Calling setData on a table view after the window has opened now causes the rows to animate in to view. By """"""""animate in to view"""""""", I mean that they initially start at 0 height, and then expand to their regular height over the course of approximately half a second.    h2. Expected Behavior  The rows should appear without any animation, unless I were to somehow specify that I wanted an animation. The existing behavior, before some recent commit to 1.8.0.1, should be maintained.    h2. Demonstration Video  http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q8bcT6JqdDE    h2. How to Reproduce  Drop the following in an app.js, and run it in the simulator.    A couple of points to note:    - I was very explicit about the height, although this isn't necessary to see the new animation behavior. I wanted to demonstrate that the issue wasn't caused by automatic height calculations, but is behavior that we introduced only recently.  - If you setData outside of the 'open' event, you won't see the animation.    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' });    var table = Ti.UI.createTableView({      rowHeight: 30  });  win.add(table);    win.addEventListener('open', function (evt) {      table.setData([          { title: 'Row 1', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 2', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 3', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 4', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 5', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 6', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 7', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 8', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 9', height: 30 },          { title: 'Row 10', height: 30 }      ]);  });    win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Table View setData Now Animates Rows In
Description: """"h1. Problem Calling setData on a table view after the window has opened now causes the rows to animate in to view. By """"""""animate in to view"""""""", I mean that they initially start at 0 height, and then expand to their regular height over the course of approximately half a second. h2. Expected Behavior The rows should appear without any animation, unless I were to somehow specify that I wanted an animation. The existing behavior, before some recent commit to 1.8.0.1, should be maintained. h2. Demonstration Video http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q8bcT6JqdDE h2. How to Reproduce Drop the following in an app.js, and run it in the simulator. A couple of points to note: - I was very explicit about the height, although this isn't necessary to see the new animation behavior. I wanted to demonstrate that the issue wasn't caused by automatic height calculations, but is behavior that we introduced only recently. - If you setData outside of the 'open' event, you won't see the animation. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var table = Ti.UI.createTableView({ rowHeight: 30 }); win.add(table); win.addEventListener('open', function (evt) { table.setData([ { title: 'Row 1', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 2', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 3', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 4', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 5', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 6', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 7', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 8', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 9', height: 30 }, { title: 'Row 10', height: 30 } ]); }); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6198,12,"""MobileWeb: Event handlers causes memory leak in IE""","""""""IE generates memory leaks in the event handling system.  Need to implement a DOM0 alternative for IE only.  Should try to remove the use of attachEvent(), but may still be needed for script tag onload events.  This leak affects IE8 and older on Windows Vista and older.  Refer to dojo/on for how to fix this.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Event handlers causes memory leak in IE
Description: """"IE generates memory leaks in the event handling system. Need to implement a DOM0 alternative for IE only. Should try to remove the use of attachEvent(), but may still be needed for script tag onload events. This leak affects IE8 and older on Windows Vista and older. Refer to dojo/on for how to fix this.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6197,12,"""MobileWeb: Handle touch events properly""","""""""The small on() event library does not support touch events.  Needs to properly implement the touch start and end events in a cross browser manner.""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Handle touch events properly
Description: """"The small on() event library does not support touch events. Needs to properly implement the touch start and end events in a cross browser manner.""""",title+description
