Description: """"After building an APK, you can see that many of the resources that we depend on at runtime from the classpath have the wrong path prefix. For example: To reproduce this, just build an Android project in any mode and look at it's APK. We shouldn't have those prefixes..""""",title+description
TIMOB-6157,12,"""MobileWeb: Compile-time optimiziations to minimize resource loading""","""""""The compile <USER>needs to properly identify resources that are require()'d or Ti.include()'d, then bundle those resources into the generated files. This should use the AST mechanism Bryan has been working on. This mechanism can also be used to identify what Ti APIs are used and further optimize which APIs should be bundled.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Compile-time optimiziations to minimize resource loading
Description: """"The compile <USER>needs to properly identify resources that are require()'d or Ti.include()'d, then bundle those resources into the generated files. This should use the AST mechanism Bryan has been working on. This mechanism can also be used to identify what Ti APIs are used and further optimize which APIs should be bundled.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6156,12,"""Android: Parity: setBackgroundColor - v8/Rhino - UI background color lost when device rotates""","""""""Description:  Setting a background of white with Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor works as expected until you rotate the device. At that point, the color is gone, and the splash screen is visible.    Sample code:      Steps to reproduce:  1) create app with sample code above  2) install to android device  3) note white color with label  4) Rotate device    Result:  White background is gone, splash screen visible    Expected:  White background persists through rotations  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Parity: setBackgroundColor - v8/Rhino - UI background color lost when device rotates
Description: """"Description: Setting a background of white with Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor works as expected until you rotate the device. At that point, the color is gone, and the splash screen is visible. Sample code: Steps to reproduce: 1) create app with sample code above 2) install to android device 3) note white color with label 4) Rotate device Result: White background is gone, splash screen visible Expected: White background persists through rotations """"",title+description
TIMOB-6155,12,"""Android: Hiding a view and changing the height of another in a vertical layout scrollview cuts off the contentHeight early""","""""""h3. Problem:  I have a scrollView with a vertical layout and a bunch of views. Depending on the content, some of these views need to hide and the views after that one need to be repositioned.  h3. Example code:    h3. Explanation:  So, here we have a simple window with a scrollView. In the scrollView there are two white views, a red view, a green view, two more white views, and a blue one. After a 4 second timer, I remove the red view and push back the green view. When this happens, you'll see that the last view, the blue one (which is 100px height) will be cut off at the middle.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Hiding a view and changing the height of another in a vertical layout scrollview cuts off the contentHeight early
Description: """"h3. Problem: I have a scrollView with a vertical layout and a bunch of views. Depending on the content, some of these views need to hide and the views after that one need to be repositioned. h3. Example code: h3. Explanation: So, here we have a simple window with a scrollView. In the scrollView there are two white views, a red view, a green view, two more white views, and a blue one. After a 4 second timer, I remove the red view and push back the green view. When this happens, you'll see that the last view, the blue one (which is 100px height) will be cut off at the middle.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6154,12,"""Tooling: Path issue, ascii codec can't decode byte""","""""""As per [this Q&A thread|http://developer.<USER>com/question/121635/<USER>studio-cannot-work-with-non-ascii-paths], the user cannot use Titanium Studio when non-ascii characters exist in the path to Studio's settings data.        The question <USER>in the path {{C:\Users\????\AppData\}} are {{%D0%94%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B0}} (in utf8) or {{%C4%E8%EC%E0}} (in win 1251)    """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: Path issue, ascii codec can't decode byte
Description: """"As per [this Q&A thread|http://developer.<USER>com/question/121635/<USER>studio-cannot-work-with-non-ascii-paths], the user cannot use Titanium Studio when non-ascii characters exist in the path to Studio's settings data. The question <USER>in the path {{C:\Users\????\AppData\}} are {{%D0%94%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B0}} (in utf8) or {{%C4%E8%EC%E0}} (in win 1251) """"",title+description
TIMOB-6153,12,"""Android: Packaging - Rhino/v8 - Pushed apks installed via Astro hang on black screen when launched from Astro""","""""""Description:  As part of our packaging tests for android, we use both adb install and adb push then astro to install. For the astro test, we push to sdcard, then use astro to install. While still in astro we select launch. While normally this will launch the app, then relaunch the app, with both v8 and rhino packaged apps this results in a single launch then a black screen.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Package an app with 1.8.0.1  2) use adb push to place on device scard  3) Launch astro and navigate to the apk  4) Choose install  5) When complete, choose launch    Result:  App launches, then goes to black screen with only status bar. No logcat info is output    Expected:  App launches then launches again""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Packaging - Rhino/v8 - Pushed apks installed via Astro hang on black screen when launched from Astro
Description: """"Description: As part of our packaging tests for android, we use both adb install and adb push then astro to install. For the astro test, we push to sdcard, then use astro to install. While still in astro we select launch. While normally this will launch the app, then relaunch the app, with both v8 and rhino packaged apps this results in a single launch then a black screen. Steps to reproduce: 1) Package an app with 1.8.0.1 2) use adb push to place on device scard 3) Launch astro and navigate to the apk 4) Choose install 5) When complete, choose launch Result: App launches, then goes to black screen with only status bar. No logcat info is output Expected: App launches then launches again""""",title+description
TIMOB-6152,12,"""iPad: Toggle popover""","""""""It would be nice if there was a way to toggle the Ti.UI.iPad.Popover.    The usual usecase is that you have a button that opens the popover. If the button is clicked while the popover is visible, nothing happens, but the expected action is that the visible popover is dismissed.    h4. Testcase  The testcase shows that if you click the button while the popover is open, nothing happens. What I would like to do is to just switch out the """""""".show"""""""" method with """""""".toggle"""""""" and then it would work as intended.      This could be easily solved by having a method on the popover object called """""""".toggle()"""""""", that will show the popover if it's not visible, otherwise hide it.    There is a [simple way of doing this|http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2642405/dismissing-ipad-uipopovercontroller-when-barbuttonitem-is-pushed-while-its-open] on StackOverflow.""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad: Toggle popover
Description: """"It would be nice if there was a way to toggle the Ti.UI.iPad.Popover. The usual usecase is that you have a button that opens the popover. If the button is clicked while the popover is visible, nothing happens, but the expected action is that the visible popover is dismissed. h4. Testcase The testcase shows that if you click the button while the popover is open, nothing happens. What I would like to do is to just switch out the """""""".show"""""""" method with """""""".toggle"""""""" and then it would work as intended. This could be easily solved by having a method on the popover object called """""""".toggle()"""""""", that will show the popover if it's not visible, otherwise hide it. There is a [simple way of doing this|http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2642405/dismissing-ipad-uipopovercontroller-when-barbuttonitem-is-pushed-while-its-open] on StackOverflow.""""",title+description
TIMOB-6151,12,"""Label shadow - blur and opacity properties""","""""""Ti.UI.Label has the properties {{shadowColor}} and {{shadowOffset}}.    It would be nice if it also supported setting the blur and opacity of the shadow.    This is useful when you don't want that hard shadow you get by just setting color and offset.    It could instead be a {{label.shadow}} property, that takes an object as an argument:  {code:JavaScript}  var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({   shadow: {    color: '#000',    offset: {     x: 0,     y: 1    },    opacity: 0.4,    blur: 2   }  });  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Label shadow - blur and opacity properties
Description: """"Ti.UI.Label has the properties {{shadowColor}} and {{shadowOffset}}. It would be nice if it also supported setting the blur and opacity of the shadow. This is useful when you don't want that hard shadow you get by just setting color and offset. It could instead be a {{label.shadow}} property, that takes an object as an argument: {code:JavaScript} var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ shadow: { color: '#000', offset: { x: 0, y: 1 }, opacity: 0.4, blur: 2 } }); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-6150,12,"""Android: Packaging - Rhino/v8 - Studio console logs """"WARNING - Suspicious code"""" and fails to package""","""""""Description:  While packaging some apps for testing, I got a strange error in the console during compile which prevents the build from completing  [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/fromGit/titanium_mobile/demos/KitchenSink/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/examples/table_view_layout_2.js:13: WARNING - Suspicious code. The result of the 'getprop' operator is not being used.   e.value; // search string as user types   ^    0 error(s), 1 warning(s)    A quick check of the code in question shows:  search.addEventListener('change', function(e)  {   e.value; // search string as user types  });    Steps to reproduce:  1) Sync with master  2) Import KS into studio  3) Attempt to package for distribution on Android  4) Watch console log    Result:  No .apk produced, console warning    Expected:  No warning, .apk produced as expected""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Packaging - Rhino/v8 - Studio console logs """"WARNING - Suspicious code"""" and fails to package
Description: """"Description: While packaging some apps for testing, I got a strange error in the console during compile which prevents the build from completing [ERROR] /Users/<USER>Documents/fromGit/titanium_mobile/demos/KitchenSink/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/examples/table_view_layout_2.js:13: WARNING - Suspicious code. The result of the 'getprop' operator is not being used. e.value; // search string as user types ^ 0 error(s), 1 warning(s) A quick check of the code in question shows: search.addEventListener('change', function(e) { e.value; // search string as user types }); Steps to reproduce: 1) Sync with master 2) Import KS into studio 3) Attempt to package for distribution on Android 4) Watch console log Result: No .apk produced, console warning Expected: No warning, .apk produced as expected""""",title+description
TIMOB-6149,12,"""CLONE - Kroll Callback on timer thread fails""","""""""h4.Problem  A module is using the native CADisplayLink timer and have the timer callback invoke a KrollCallback.    The fireCallback it's being used with a property bound to the KrollCallback object.    This causes a program crash with a SIGBUS error on the calling thread    h5.Module  Testing code attached:  try """"""""titanium run"""""""" (badanimation.zip)    h5.Repro sequence  If the module is attached to a Titanium project throw this to an app.js and embed module to Tiapp.xml file  {code:title=app.js}  // open a single window  var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'white'  });  var label = Ti.UI.createLabel();  window.add(label);  window.open();    // TODO: write your module tests here  var badanimation = require('com.badanimation');  Ti.API.info(""""""""module is => """""""" + badanimation);    var animator = badanimation.createAnimator({      callback: function(e){Ti.API.info(""""""""time is """"""""+e.timestamp);}  });    Ti.API.info(""""""""animator is => """""""" + animator);    animator.startAnimation();  {code}    h5.Tiapp.xml      h5.SDK 1.7.2 - Console output      h5.SDK 1.8 - console output      h5.Associated HD ticket  APP-355595  """"""",Bug,"Title: CLONE - Kroll Callback on timer thread fails
Description: """"h4.Problem A module is using the native CADisplayLink timer and have the timer callback invoke a KrollCallback. The fireCallback it's being used with a property bound to the KrollCallback object. This causes a program crash with a SIGBUS error on the calling thread h5.Module Testing code attached: try """"""""titanium run"""""""" (badanimation.zip) h5.Repro sequence If the module is attached to a Titanium project throw this to an app.js and embed module to Tiapp.xml file {code:title=app.js} // open a single window var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'white' }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel(); window.add(label); window.open(); // TODO: write your module tests here var badanimation = require('com.badanimation'); Ti.API.info(""""""""module is => """""""" + badanimation); var animator = badanimation.createAnimator({ callback: function(e){Ti.API.info(""""""""time is """"""""+e.timestamp);} }); Ti.API.info(""""""""animator is => """""""" + animator); animator.startAnimation(); {code} h5.Tiapp.xml h5.SDK 1.7.2 - Console output h5.SDK 1.8 - console output h5.Associated HD ticket APP-355595 """"",title+description
