TIMOB-6130,12,"""Android: WIndow: Rhino/v8, setting background color to 'gray' displays the window in black""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch Application  2. Base UI>Window Soft Input (Android)    Actual Result:  Background is black    Expected Result:  Background should be gray  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: WIndow: Rhino/v8, setting background color to 'gray' displays the window in black
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch Application 2. Base UI>Window Soft Input (Android) Actual Result: Background is black Expected Result: Background should be gray """"",title+description
TIMOB-6129,12,"""Android: Vertical Layout- v8/Rhino - Footer does not remain at the bottom of the screen or in sync relative to other UI elements""","""""""Description:  It seems that the footer (Base UI>Vertical Layout> Basic) is being rendered in the center of the screen. This remains true regardless of device rotation.      Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Base UI>Vertical Layout> Basic  3) Rotate device    Result:  Footer renders in center of screen    Expected:  Footer renders at bottom of screen""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Vertical Layout- v8/Rhino - Footer does not remain at the bottom of the screen or in sync relative to other UI elements
Description: """"Description: It seems that the footer (Base UI>Vertical Layout> Basic) is being rendered in the center of the screen. This remains true regardless of device rotation. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Base UI>Vertical Layout> Basic 3) Rotate device Result: Footer renders in center of screen Expected: Footer renders at bottom of screen""""",title+description
TIMOB-6128,12,"""Android: OrientationModes - Setting OrientationModes does nothing""","""""""1) Create a new project and place the following in the app.js    2) Place the attached grouch.jpg in the Resources folder  3) Launch the application    Expected results: Image is shown in landscape mode only  Actual results: Image is shown in portrait and landscape mode.  Same behavior as not defining the orientationModes.    Notes:  Same behavior occurs if rhino tag is put in the tiapp.xml""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: OrientationModes - Setting OrientationModes does nothing
Description: """"1) Create a new project and place the following in the app.js 2) Place the attached grouch.jpg in the Resources folder 3) Launch the application Expected results: Image is shown in landscape mode only Actual results: Image is shown in portrait and landscape mode. Same behavior as not defining the orientationModes. Notes: Same behavior occurs if rhino tag is put in the tiapp.xml""""",title+description
TIMOB-6127,12,"""Android: Email: v8/Rhino: """"email unavailable"""" on Nexus S phone, works fine on tablets and Droid 3""","""""""Description:  A dialog stating """"""""email not available"""""""" is presented on both phones (Nexus S, Droid 3) tested using KS Base UI > Views > Email Dialog. Gmail accounts were set up on each device using test account, and verified functional. Both tabs worked with this same test. Droid 3 now functions correctly with no change in setup. So this is limited to the Nexus S    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > Email Dialog  3) Select photo from gallery to email    Result:  Dialog """"""""ERROR: Email not available    Expected:  Email composed is presented for sending""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Email: v8/Rhino: """"email unavailable"""" on Nexus S phone, works fine on tablets and Droid 3
Description: """"Description: A dialog stating """"""""email not available"""""""" is presented on both phones (Nexus S, Droid 3) tested using KS Base UI > Views > Email Dialog. Gmail accounts were set up on each device using test account, and verified functional. Both tabs worked with this same test. Droid 3 now functions correctly with no change in setup. So this is limited to the Nexus S Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > Email Dialog 3) Select photo from gallery to email Result: Dialog """"""""ERROR: Email not available Expected: Email composed is presented for sending""""",title+description
TIMOB-6126,12,"""Android: UI - v8 - rhino, Nook only pressing any table view row of vertical layout causes crash on rhino and does nothing on v8""","""""""Navigating to Base UI, Vertical Layout and then pressing any table view row doesn't do anything on v8 and crashes on rhino    Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch KS  2. Navigate to Base UI  3. Press Vertical Layout table view row  4. Press any table view row    Actual Result:  on v8 ddms shows: TypeError: Cannot call method 'open' of undefined  on rhino ddms shows: TypeError: Cannot call method """"""""open"""""""" of undefined (app://common.js#26)    Expected result:  Should be able to open table view row""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: UI - v8 - rhino, Nook only pressing any table view row of vertical layout causes crash on rhino and does nothing on v8
Description: """"Navigating to Base UI, Vertical Layout and then pressing any table view row doesn't do anything on v8 and crashes on rhino Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch KS 2. Navigate to Base UI 3. Press Vertical Layout table view row 4. Press any table view row Actual Result: on v8 ddms shows: TypeError: Cannot call method 'open' of undefined on rhino ddms shows: TypeError: Cannot call method """"""""open"""""""" of undefined (app://common.js#26) Expected result: Should be able to open table view row""""",title+description
TIMOB-6125,12,"""Android: Scrolling tabs: v8/Rhino: Slow UI element rendering or delay in rendering""","""""""Description:  The UI elements in KS Base UI > Views > scroll views > scrolling tabs are drawn so slowly that you can perceive the draw start location and the UI element looks painted in from one side. On the LG Slate, there is a couple second delay before the UI elements are rendered, and they may appear piecemeal, or all together with no perceptible drawing <USER>    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > scroll views > scrolling tabs  3) Watch as the UI elements render    Result:  Delay in some cases, slow draw in all others.    Expected:  Quick rendering of UI elements with no delay in render start""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Scrolling tabs: v8/Rhino: Slow UI element rendering or delay in rendering
Description: """"Description: The UI elements in KS Base UI > Views > scroll views > scrolling tabs are drawn so slowly that you can perceive the draw start location and the UI element looks painted in from one side. On the LG Slate, there is a couple second delay before the UI elements are rendered, and they may appear piecemeal, or all together with no perceptible drawing <USER> Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > scroll views > scrolling tabs 3) Watch as the UI elements render Result: Delay in some cases, slow draw in all others. Expected: Quick rendering of UI elements with no delay in render start""""",title+description
TIMOB-6124,12,"""Android: TextField: Rhino/v8, hint text are not getting displayed""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch Application  Platform>Sockets>Connecting socket    Actual Result:  Hint text are not displayed in the text field    Expected Result:  Should display hint text in the text fields  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField: Rhino/v8, hint text are not getting displayed
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch Application Platform>Sockets>Connecting socket Actual Result: Hint text are not displayed in the text field Expected Result: Should display hint text in the text fields """"",title+description
TIMOB-6123,12,"""Android: Image: v8/Rhino: No animated images are displayed""","""""""Description:  During our KS pass on the image views section, I noted that no images were displayed and no console output showing frame was logged for the """"""""animated"""""""" test. Additionally, the same behavior occurred with """"""""image rapid update""""""""    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > Image Views > Animated OR Base UI > Views > Image Views > Image Rapid Update  3) Click """"""""start animation"""""""" button    Result:  No images displayed, no console output    Expected:  Images of fire animated, console outputting frame counter""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image: v8/Rhino: No animated images are displayed
Description: """"Description: During our KS pass on the image views section, I noted that no images were displayed and no console output showing frame was logged for the """"""""animated"""""""" test. Additionally, the same behavior occurred with """"""""image rapid update"""""""" Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Base UI > Views > Image Views > Animated OR Base UI > Views > Image Views > Image Rapid Update 3) Click """"""""start animation"""""""" button Result: No images displayed, no console output Expected: Images of fire animated, console outputting frame counter""""",title+description
TIMOB-6122,12,"""Android: Sound - Static/noise heard before the start of a sound playing the first time""","""""""The first time a sound file (mp4) is played, there will be noise in the form of static/crackle/pop before the actual sound file is played. This behavior seems to be related to these specific Samsung devices, although it is intermittent without 100% occurrence.    To reproduce:  # Create a new Mobile project.  # Place the attached {{205048_low.mp4}} file in the Resources directory.  # Replace the {{app.js}} with the following code.  # Load the built app onto a device.  # Press the """"""""Play"""""""" button to start the sound; *the sound problem should occur now*.  # Once the sound has been played once, kill the app and restart to test again.    {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({});  var sound = Ti.Media.createSound({url:'205048_low.mp4'});  var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title:'Play', width:100, height:100, top:100});  button.addEventListener('click', function() {sound.play();});  win.add(button);  win.open();  {code}    h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-954677""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Sound - Static/noise heard before the start of a sound playing the first time
Description: """"The first time a sound file (mp4) is played, there will be noise in the form of static/crackle/pop before the actual sound file is played. This behavior seems to be related to these specific Samsung devices, although it is intermittent without 100% occurrence. To reproduce: # Create a new Mobile project. # Place the attached {{205048_low.mp4}} file in the Resources directory. # Replace the {{app.js}} with the following code. # Load the built app onto a device. # Press the """"""""Play"""""""" button to start the sound; *the sound problem should occur now*. # Once the sound has been played once, kill the app and restart to test again. {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({}); var sound = Ti.Media.createSound({url:'205048_low.mp4'}); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title:'Play', width:100, height:100, top:100}); button.addEventListener('click', function() {sound.play();}); win.add(button); win.open(); {code} h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-954677""""",title+description
