TIMOB-6033,12,"""Android: Heavyweight root window causes incorrect  CommonJS global variable behavior""","""""""{panel}  Please see <USER>s contribution [here|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6033?focusedCommentId=173145&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-173145] regarding what is deemed correct behavior.  {panel}    h3. Expected Behavior    After modifying a global variable created in app.js inside of a CommonJS module, the variable should be modified globally (also outside of the module). The test case demonstrates this behavior.    The following results show the correct behavior, obtained when the root window is lightweight (without fullscreen property configured):        h3. Actual Behavior    The correct behavior is exhibited on Android *ONLY* when the root window is lightweight.    The following results show the incorrect behavior, obtained when the root window is heavyweight (with fullscreen property configured):        Note that the behavior on iOS is correct regardless of the root window properties    h3. Test case  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var globalVar = """"""""From global scope"""""""";    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor:'green',    // fullscreen:false,  // uncomment this to see different behavior    exitOnClose:true  });    win.open();    win.addEventListener('click', function() {    var test = require('test');    Ti.API.info('globalVar from CommonJS module: ' + test.testGlobalVar());    Ti.API.info('globalVar from global scope: ' + globalVar);    test.testGlobalVar();  });    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Heavyweight root window causes incorrect CommonJS global variable behavior
Description: """"{panel} Please see <USER>s contribution [here|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-6033?focusedCommentId=173145&page=com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:comment-tabpanel#comment-173145] regarding what is deemed correct behavior. {panel} h3. Expected Behavior After modifying a global variable created in app.js inside of a CommonJS module, the variable should be modified globally (also outside of the module). The test case demonstrates this behavior. The following results show the correct behavior, obtained when the root window is lightweight (without fullscreen property configured): h3. Actual Behavior The correct behavior is exhibited on Android *ONLY* when the root window is lightweight. The following results show the incorrect behavior, obtained when the root window is heavyweight (with fullscreen property configured): Note that the behavior on iOS is correct regardless of the root window properties h3. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var globalVar = """"""""From global scope""""""""; var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'green', // fullscreen:false, // uncomment this to see different behavior exitOnClose:true }); win.open(); win.addEventListener('click', function() { var test = require('test'); Ti.API.info('globalVar from CommonJS module: ' + test.testGlobalVar()); Ti.API.info('globalVar from global scope: ' + globalVar); test.testGlobalVar(); }); """"",title+description
TIMOB-6030,12,"""iOS: Table views cannot be created inside an event listener""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Compile the attached app.js  2. Launch the application  3. Click the """"""""Create a big table"""""""" button    Actual:  Table View not generated    Expected:  To generate a table view with a red box in the first row    Note: works when not in the event listener  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Table views cannot be created inside an event listener
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Compile the attached app.js 2. Launch the application 3. Click the """"""""Create a big table"""""""" button Actual: Table View not generated Expected: To generate a table view with a red box in the first row Note: works when not in the event listener """"",title+description
