TIMOB-5976,12,"""iOS: Kitchensink - Base UI>Views>Events Propagation does not report label clicks""","""""""Description:  Base UI>Views>Events Propagation normally reports clicks on the window, the views, and the labels within the views. With my latest run on KS using 1.8.0, clicks on the labels are not reported.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on iPad 2  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Events Propagation  3) Click on any of the labels (""""""""A"""""""", """"""""B"""""""", """"""""C"""""""", or """"""""D"""""""")    Result:  The label clicks are not reported at the bottom of the screen    Note:  DOES NOT occur with 1.7.5""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchensink - Base UI>Views>Events Propagation does not report label clicks
Description: """"Description: Base UI>Views>Events Propagation normally reports clicks on the window, the views, and the labels within the views. With my latest run on KS using 1.8.0, clicks on the labels are not reported. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on iPad 2 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Events Propagation 3) Click on any of the labels (""""""""A"""""""", """"""""B"""""""", """"""""C"""""""", or """"""""D"""""""") Result: The label clicks are not reported at the bottom of the screen Note: DOES NOT occur with 1.7.5""""",title+description
TIMOB-5975,12,"""iOS: Default Module Template with Xcode 4.2 Doesn't Target Latest iOS, Excludes armv6""","""""""h1. Problem  When building with Xcode 4.2, modules don't target the latest iOS, and since the default architecture changed, they also don't target armv6. This results in the module not being usable in a Titanium Mobile project that is targeting armv6.    h2. Solution  The project template for modules should be updated to:    1. Also target armv6, where appropriate  2. Target the latest iOS    h2. How To Test    - Create a module from the terminal:    - Open the module's project in Xcode 4.2:    - In Xcode, verify that it does NOT say """"""""missing base SDK"""""""" beneath the project name in the Project navigator.  - Click on the project name in the Project navigator to open up the settings.  - Under the Build Settings tab for BOTH the project and the target, verify that all references to armv7 are accompanied by armv6. It shouldn't say just """"""""armv7"""""""" anywhere.    h2. Pull Request  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/625""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Default Module Template with Xcode 4.2 Doesn't Target Latest iOS, Excludes armv6
Description: """"h1. Problem When building with Xcode 4.2, modules don't target the latest iOS, and since the default architecture changed, they also don't target armv6. This results in the module not being usable in a Titanium Mobile project that is targeting armv6. h2. Solution The project template for modules should be updated to: 1. Also target armv6, where appropriate 2. Target the latest iOS h2. How To Test - Create a module from the terminal: - Open the module's project in Xcode 4.2: - In Xcode, verify that it does NOT say """"""""missing base SDK"""""""" beneath the project name in the Project navigator. - Click on the project name in the Project navigator to open up the settings. - Under the Build Settings tab for BOTH the project and the target, verify that all references to armv7 are accompanied by armv6. It shouldn't say just """"""""armv7"""""""" anywhere. h2. Pull Request https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/625""""",title+description
TIMOB-5974,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink iPad - UI rotates unexpectedly and then modal window animates from a different direction""","""""""Description:  While testing KS iPad on an iPad 2 (iOS 4.3.5) I noted that if the device is rotated on the """"""""Split View-Plain"""""""" test and then a modal window is displayed, the main UI is rotated from landscape to portrait and then the next modal window is animated from the left side instead of from the bottom of the display. In addition, the main UI rotates back from portrait to landscape poorly (status bar disconnected and slow to animate, master window redraws over itself). 1.7.2 SDK behaves differently, please see note below.    See attachments for details.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS iPad (1.8.0 branch) on iPad 2  2) While device is in portrait select """"""""split view plain"""""""", note UI rotates to landscape  3) Select """"""""show modal"""""""", note window opens animating from the bottom of the screen  4) Dismiss modal, noting that the main UI was rotated to portrait behind the modal then rotates poorly back to landscape  5) Rotate device to landscape and select """"""""show modal"""""""" again, noting that the modal animates in from the left  6) Dismiss the modal and select """"""""show modal"""""""" again. Note the modal animates in from the bottom    Results:  Main UI window rotates behind modal, rotates back with poor animation, and the first modal window after this <USER>animates in from the left.    Expected:  Main UI stays in landscape, rotates if needed with components in unison, and modal always animates from the bottom.    Note: Also occurs with KS iPad 1.7.2, although not initially. KS iPad 1.7.2 on this test rotates the initial UI clockwise, where 1.8.0 rotates counter-clockwise. 1.7.2 has solid animation in that state but does display the modal animating in from the side (opposite in this case). When 1.7.2 is forced to the same landscape as the 1.8.0 default, the animation is poor. 1.8.0 shows poor animation in either landscape orientation.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink iPad - UI rotates unexpectedly and then modal window animates from a different direction
Description: """"Description: While testing KS iPad on an iPad 2 (iOS 4.3.5) I noted that if the device is rotated on the """"""""Split View-Plain"""""""" test and then a modal window is displayed, the main UI is rotated from landscape to portrait and then the next modal window is animated from the left side instead of from the bottom of the display. In addition, the main UI rotates back from portrait to landscape poorly (status bar disconnected and slow to animate, master window redraws over itself). 1.7.2 SDK behaves differently, please see note below. See attachments for details. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS iPad (1.8.0 branch) on iPad 2 2) While device is in portrait select """"""""split view plain"""""""", note UI rotates to landscape 3) Select """"""""show modal"""""""", note window opens animating from the bottom of the screen 4) Dismiss modal, noting that the main UI was rotated to portrait behind the modal then rotates poorly back to landscape 5) Rotate device to landscape and select """"""""show modal"""""""" again, noting that the modal animates in from the left 6) Dismiss the modal and select """"""""show modal"""""""" again. Note the modal animates in from the bottom Results: Main UI window rotates behind modal, rotates back with poor animation, and the first modal window after this <USER>animates in from the left. Expected: Main UI stays in landscape, rotates if needed with components in unison, and modal always animates from the bottom. Note: Also occurs with KS iPad 1.7.2, although not initially. KS iPad 1.7.2 on this test rotates the initial UI clockwise, where 1.8.0 rotates counter-clockwise. 1.7.2 has solid animation in that state but does display the modal animating in from the side (opposite in this case). When 1.7.2 is forced to the same landscape as the 1.8.0 default, the animation is poor. 1.8.0 shows poor animation in either landscape orientation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5973,12,"""ASIHTTP no longer under active development; need to investigate replacement""","""""""ASIHTTPRequest is no longer under active development:    http://allseeing-i.com/%5Brequest_release%5D;  http://groups.google.com/group/asihttprequest/browse_thread/thread/7731197dbe71c260    Normally, for 3rd party components, we can continue to support them long after development has stopped. ASI is a special case since it's extremely complex code, and is integral to a lot of mobile app support. We need to investigate alternatives, and then replace it.""""""",New Feature,"Title: ASIHTTP no longer under active development; need to investigate replacement
Description: """"ASIHTTPRequest is no longer under active development: http://allseeing-i.com/%5Brequest_release%5D; http://groups.google.com/group/asihttprequest/browse_thread/thread/7731197dbe71c260 Normally, for 3rd party components, we can continue to support them long after development has stopped. ASI is a special case since it's extremely complex code, and is integral to a lot of mobile app support. We need to investigate alternatives, and then replace it.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5972,12,""" When the width of the ScrollableView is changed the current page of a ScrollableView is changed""","""""""h3. Problem  When the width of the ScrollableView changes, the current page on the screen inexplicably jumps to 0, while the currentPage property itself remains whatever you set it to.   This is visible if you press """"""""scroll"""""""" and then the """"""""resize"""""""" button.    h3. Reproducible steps:     1. Run the code below  2. Scroll to page 1 on the green square  3. Press the scroll button  4. Press the resize button    notice that the current page is changed    h3. Expected behavior:  Customer wants to keep the number of the current page after press the resize button.    h3. More details:  Tested in a mobile device with Android, and worked well.    h3. Sample code:    h3. Helpdesk  APP-256873                            """"""",Bug,"Title: When the width of the ScrollableView is changed the current page of a ScrollableView is changed
Description: """"h3. Problem When the width of the ScrollableView changes, the current page on the screen inexplicably jumps to 0, while the currentPage property itself remains whatever you set it to. This is visible if you press """"""""scroll"""""""" and then the """"""""resize"""""""" button. h3. Reproducible steps: 1. Run the code below 2. Scroll to page 1 on the green square 3. Press the scroll button 4. Press the resize button notice that the current page is changed h3. Expected behavior: Customer wants to keep the number of the current page after press the resize button. h3. More details: Tested in a mobile device with Android, and worked well. h3. Sample code: h3. Helpdesk APP-256873 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5970,12,"""iPad: Once Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery is called, it can not be cancelled.""","""""""Once """"""""Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery"""""""" is called, you can not cancel it. There is no such """"""""cancel"""""""" button as shown on iPhone. If you click twice outside the photo gallery, an error will be generated.      h4. Repro Steps  Step 1: create a project to run the example code below.  Step 2: click on the space outside the photo gallery.  Step 3: click again on the space outside the photo gallery, the """"""""error"""""""" alert will be popped up.    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#000' });    win.addEventListener('click', function(){     Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({           success:function(event)         {             alert('success');         },         cancel:function(cancel)         {             alert('cancel');         },         error:function(error)         {             alert('error');         }     });  })    win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad: Once Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery is called, it can not be cancelled.
Description: """"Once """"""""Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery"""""""" is called, you can not cancel it. There is no such """"""""cancel"""""""" button as shown on iPhone. If you click twice outside the photo gallery, an error will be generated. h4. Repro Steps Step 1: create a project to run the example code below. Step 2: click on the space outside the photo gallery. Step 3: click again on the space outside the photo gallery, the """"""""error"""""""" alert will be popped up. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#000' }); win.addEventListener('click', function(){ Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({ success:function(event) { alert('success'); }, cancel:function(cancel) { alert('cancel'); }, error:function(error) { alert('error'); } }); }) win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-5968,12,"""iOS: Text is not aligning correctly in the text area""","""""""1) Launch QTS  2) Navigate to test 4748  3) Click start    Results: Text is not aligning properly in text field.  See attached screenshots    Notes:  This is a regression.  It works fine in 1.7.5.  If all the other tests in QTS are commented out in aTestList.js, then it works as expected.  Assigning to myself for now, pending further investigation.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Text is not aligning correctly in the text area
Description: """"1) Launch QTS 2) Navigate to test 4748 3) Click start Results: Text is not aligning properly in text field. See attached screenshots Notes: This is a regression. It works fine in 1.7.5. If all the other tests in QTS are commented out in aTestList.js, then it works as expected. Assigning to myself for now, pending further investigation.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5967,12,"""Packaged apps failing verification, reporting """"...icon not found under the top level app wrapper: iTunesArtwork""""""","""""""Description:  I recently added an additional test case to my packaging testing. After packaging, I now """"""""validate"""""""" the app with apple. Prior to 1.8.0 SDK, this test would pass using the same test project. As of 1.8.0, the test app fails validation with the error """"""""Icon specified in the Info.plist not found under the top level app wrapper: iTunesArtwork"""""""".     Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a Studio project with all 7 possible apple icons present  2) Be sure to remove the png extension from iTunesArtwork  3) Package for distribution from Studio  4) From the Xcode archive, select """"""""validate""""""""    Result:  Validation fails with error shown in attachment    Expected result:  Validation succeeds""""""",Bug,"Title: Packaged apps failing verification, reporting """"...icon not found under the top level app wrapper: iTunesArtwork""""
Description: """"Description: I recently added an additional test case to my packaging testing. After packaging, I now """"""""validate"""""""" the app with apple. Prior to 1.8.0 SDK, this test would pass using the same test project. As of 1.8.0, the test app fails validation with the error """"""""Icon specified in the Info.plist not found under the top level app wrapper: iTunesArtwork"""""""". Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a Studio project with all 7 possible apple icons present 2) Be sure to remove the png extension from iTunesArtwork 3) Package for distribution from Studio 4) From the Xcode archive, select """"""""validate"""""""" Result: Validation fails with error shown in attachment Expected result: Validation succeeds""""",title+description
TIMOB-5966,12,"""iOS: Arti: Intermittent crash when moving around and backing out to update list of places""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch the ARti app and log in  2. Click the """"""""whats near me"""""""" button  3. Click the icon in the top right to invoke the camera on overlay  4. Move around until an object is presented to tap, and tap it.  5. Click back and repeat step 2-5    Actual:   Eventually will crash  Nov  2 15:23:42 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] <Warning>: (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>arti[0xd267]) Job appears to have crashed: Segmentation fault: 11  Nov  2 15:23:42 unknown SpringBoard[15] <Warning>: Application 'arti' exited abnormally with signal 11: Segmentation fault: 11  Nov  2 15:23:43 unknown ReportCrash[3611] <Error>: Saved crashreport to /var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter/arti_2011-11-02-152341_openDoc.plist using uid: 0 gid: 0, synthetic_euid: 501 egid: 0    Expected:  Should not crash    Note:  Cannot test pre 1.8.0 because of TIMOB-4664    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Arti: Intermittent crash when moving around and backing out to update list of places
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch the ARti app and log in 2. Click the """"""""whats near me"""""""" button 3. Click the icon in the top right to invoke the camera on overlay 4. Move around until an object is presented to tap, and tap it. 5. Click back and repeat step 2-5 Actual: Eventually will crash Nov 2 15:23:42 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] <Warning>: (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>arti[0xd267]) Job appears to have crashed: Segmentation fault: 11 Nov 2 15:23:42 unknown SpringBoard[15] <Warning>: Application 'arti' exited abnormally with signal 11: Segmentation fault: 11 Nov 2 15:23:43 unknown ReportCrash[3611] <Error>: Saved crashreport to /var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter/arti_2011-11-02-152341_openDoc.plist using uid: 0 gid: 0, synthetic_euid: 501 egid: 0 Expected: Should not crash Note: Cannot test pre 1.8.0 because of TIMOB-4664 """"",title+description
