TIMOB-5959,12,"""iOS: Application error message says expression is undefined instead of null""","""""""1) Create a new project and put the following the app.js    2) Launch app    Actual results:  Application Error.  Result of expression 'doc.getElementsByTagName(""""""""<USER>"""""")' [undefined]  is not an object    Expected Results: Application Error.  Result of expression 'doc.getElementsByTagName(""""""""<USER>"""""")' [null]  is not an object    Notes:  Issue seems to be a regression.  The error message is as expected in 1.7.4 and 1.7.5.v20111101114654.    Issue is related to TIMOB-3464""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Application error message says expression is undefined instead of null
Description: """"1) Create a new project and put the following the app.js 2) Launch app Actual results: Application Error. Result of expression 'doc.getElementsByTagName(""""""""<USER>"""""")' [undefined] is not an object Expected Results: Application Error. Result of expression 'doc.getElementsByTagName(""""""""<USER>"""""")' [null] is not an object Notes: Issue seems to be a regression. The error message is as expected in 1.7.4 and 1.7.5.v20111101114654. Issue is related to TIMOB-3464""""",title+description
TIMOB-5958,12,"""Regression: require() for non-CommonJS, when called from a require()d CommonJS, assumes """".js"""", crashes app""","""""""Using SDK 1.8.0.v20111010113820 and later, when a native module is require()d from within a CommonJS module, the following runtime error is generated (immediately upon running the app in the Android emulator):    {panel:title=Error| borderStyle=dashed| titleBGColor=red| bgColor=white}  ReferenceError: """"""""NOT_FOUND"""""""" is not defined. (app://com.thirdpartycompany.specialmodule.js#1)  {panel}     In SDK 1.8.0.v20110913...., there is no problem.    Simply using require() to pull in the native module works fine, as long as it is called from a js file that hasn't been require()d into the app (e.g. app.js).    From the error message (ReferenceError: """"""""NOT_FOUND"""""""" is not defined. (app://com.thirdpartycompany.specialmodule.js#1)), it's obvious that Titanium is appending """""""".js"""""""" to the module name, assuming it is a CommonJS module.  But it is a *native* module, so Titanium shouldn't being trying to append """""""".js"""""""" to it.    My """"""""require()"""""""" call is like this;    {code:borderStyle=solid}  var SpecialModule=require('com.thirdpartycompany.specialmodule');      According to <USER>  _...using the require for a native module inside a commonjs module. I can imagine what's happening there -- while executing the commonjs require, rhino likely hijacks """"""""require"""""""", meaning our """"""""require"""""""" gets ignored so it mises that step that checks first for a native module. I'll find a solution._    Simple sample code:  {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  var Procs=require('CommonProcs'); // my commonJS unit    var TheWindow=Ti.UI.createWindow({                    layout:'vertical',                    exitOnClose:true,                    navBarHidden:true                   });  var TheLabel=Ti.UI.createLabel({          color:'white',          text:'Hello World',          font:{fontSize:'18dp',fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'},          width:'auto'       });  TheWindow.add(TheLabel);                    TheWindow.open();      I have also attached an actual project example that can be run.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Regression: require() for non-CommonJS, when called from a require()d CommonJS, assumes """".js"""", crashes app
Description: """"Using SDK 1.8.0.v20111010113820 and later, when a native module is require()d from within a CommonJS module, the following runtime error is generated (immediately upon running the app in the Android emulator): {panel:title=Error| borderStyle=dashed| titleBGColor=red| bgColor=white} ReferenceError: """"""""NOT_FOUND"""""""" is not defined. (app://com.thirdpartycompany.specialmodule.js#1) {panel} In SDK 1.8.0.v20110913...., there is no problem. Simply using require() to pull in the native module works fine, as long as it is called from a js file that hasn't been require()d into the app (e.g. app.js). From the error message (ReferenceError: """"""""NOT_FOUND"""""""" is not defined. (app://com.thirdpartycompany.specialmodule.js#1)), it's obvious that Titanium is appending """""""".js"""""""" to the module name, assuming it is a CommonJS module. But it is a *native* module, so Titanium shouldn't being trying to append """""""".js"""""""" to it. My """"""""require()"""""""" call is like this; {code:borderStyle=solid} var SpecialModule=require('com.thirdpartycompany.specialmodule'); According to <USER> _...using the require for a native module inside a commonjs module. I can imagine what's happening there -- while executing the commonjs require, rhino likely hijacks """"""""require"""""""", meaning our """"""""require"""""""" gets ignored so it mises that step that checks first for a native module. I'll find a solution._ Simple sample code: {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var Procs=require('CommonProcs'); // my commonJS unit var TheWindow=Ti.UI.createWindow({ layout:'vertical', exitOnClose:true, navBarHidden:true }); var TheLabel=Ti.UI.createLabel({ color:'white', text:'Hello World', font:{fontSize:'18dp',fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'}, width:'auto' }); TheWindow.add(TheLabel); TheWindow.open(); I have also attached an actual project example that can be run. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5957,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink - crash on iOS device running iOS version 5.0 due to connecting to a nonexistent socket""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1. Install 1_7_x branch of Kitchen Sink on iOS device running iOS version 5.0  2. Navigate to platform>sockets>connecting sockets  3. press the connect button  4. Navigate back to sockets and let app sit ~2-3 seconds    Actual Result:  App crashes    Expected result:  App should not crash and should display table view of socket options.    *Note  Crashes on 1.7.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink - crash on iOS device running iOS version 5.0 due to connecting to a nonexistent socket
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Install 1_7_x branch of Kitchen Sink on iOS device running iOS version 5.0 2. Navigate to platform>sockets>connecting sockets 3. press the connect button 4. Navigate back to sockets and let app sit ~2-3 seconds Actual Result: App crashes Expected result: App should not crash and should display table view of socket options. *Note Crashes on 1.7.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-5956,12,"""iOS: clicking login with facebook multiple times display the dialog each time without killing the previous""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Mashups > Facebook > Login/Logout  2. Click on login with Facebook multiple times    Actual Result:  A new web dialog is displayed for each click    Expected Result:  To close the previous before opening a new one""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: clicking login with facebook multiple times display the dialog each time without killing the previous
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Mashups > Facebook > Login/Logout 2. Click on login with Facebook multiple times Actual Result: A new web dialog is displayed for each click Expected Result: To close the previous before opening a new one""""",title+description
TIMOB-5955,12,"""iOS: Intermittent: Logging into facebook sometime displays the facebook in the dialog""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. KS > Mashups > Facebook > Login/Logout  2. Log in with your credentials    Actual Result:  The dialog that comes up becomes the facebook webview and navigating elsewhere does not close the log in dialog (see image)    Expected Result:  Should exit the dialog after logging in  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Intermittent: Logging into facebook sometime displays the facebook in the dialog
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. KS > Mashups > Facebook > Login/Logout 2. Log in with your credentials Actual Result: The dialog that comes up becomes the facebook webview and navigating elsewhere does not close the log in dialog (see image) Expected Result: Should exit the dialog after logging in """"",title+description
TIMOB-5954,12,"""iOS: click event fired more than once""","""""""h3.Problem  The click event is raised for every object on a view. For example if I have a view with a label (custom button). The click event will be raised twice when the user taps the view.    h4.Regession issue - works fine with mobile SDKs 1.7.4.v20111025165811 & 1.7.3 & 1.7.2      h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Run the sample code  2. Click the """"""""Click me"""""""" label  3. Check the Titanium logs    h3.Sample Code      h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-287373""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: click event fired more than once
Description: """"h3.Problem The click event is raised for every object on a view. For example if I have a view with a label (custom button). The click event will be raised twice when the user taps the view. h4.Regession issue - works fine with mobile SDKs 1.7.4.v20111025165811 & 1.7.3 & 1.7.2 h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Run the sample code 2. Click the """"""""Click me"""""""" label 3. Check the Titanium logs h3.Sample Code h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-287373""""",title+description
