Description: """"We need a pair programming effort to eliminate the remaining warnings.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5937,12,"""Update CreateHTTPClient to better align with the XMLHttpRequest spec""","""""""When working on TIMOB-5249, Sabil and I decided to look up the actual spec for handling responseText and responseXML, and found them to not match what we had implemented (In past as well as in android). Due to the timing, TIMOB-5249 will continue unchanged, but this bug is created so that both iOS and Android maintain parity while transitioning to to the spec.    See http://www.w3.org/TR/XMLHttpRequest for the spec.""""""",Story,"Title: Update CreateHTTPClient to better align with the XMLHttpRequest spec
Description: """"When working on TIMOB-5249, Sabil and I decided to look up the actual spec for handling responseText and responseXML, and found them to not match what we had implemented (In past as well as in android). Due to the timing, TIMOB-5249 will continue unchanged, but this bug is created so that both iOS and Android maintain parity while transitioning to to the spec. See http://www.w3.org/TR/XMLHttpRequest for the spec.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5936,12,"""iOS: Application crash on launch on iOS device pre iOS version 4.0 due to module case-sensitvity""","""""""Step to reproduce:  1. Create an iphone sub-directory in your Titanium>modules directory (i.e. ~/Library/Application Support/Titanium/modules/iphone)  2. create an app with ti.urbanairship module by adding urbanAirship module which can be found here http://support.<USER>com/kb/66/tickets , into the iphone sub-directory you just created.  3. Paste the code below into tiapp.xml *note, you may need to change the version number*   <modules>          <module platform=""""""""iphone"""""""" version=""""""""1.0"""""""">ti.urbanAirship</module>  </modules>  2. Test once with module name as ti.urbanairship (fail case)  3. Test once with module named as ti.urbanAirship (pass case)  4. Run on iOS device with OS version less than 4.0    Actual Result:  App crashes on launch    Expected Result:  App should launch and tab group should be displayed.    **Note that this iOS version will not be supported in 1.8.0""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Application crash on launch on iOS device pre iOS version 4.0 due to module case-sensitvity
Description: """"Step to reproduce: 1. Create an iphone sub-directory in your Titanium>modules directory (i.e. ~/Library/Application Support/Titanium/modules/iphone) 2. create an app with ti.urbanairship module by adding urbanAirship module which can be found here http://support.<USER>com/kb/66/tickets , into the iphone sub-directory you just created. 3. Paste the code below into tiapp.xml *note, you may need to change the version number* <modules> <module platform=""""""""iphone"""""""" version=""""""""1.0"""""""">ti.urbanAirship</module> </modules> 2. Test once with module name as ti.urbanairship (fail case) 3. Test once with module named as ti.urbanAirship (pass case) 4. Run on iOS device with OS version less than 4.0 Actual Result: App crashes on launch Expected Result: App should launch and tab group should be displayed. **Note that this iOS version will not be supported in 1.8.0""""",title+description
TIMOB-5935,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink - Updating row's causes application to crash""","""""""1) Launch KitchenSink from titanium_mobile demo's folder.  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update Row  3) Click Change Me (No Anim)   Results: Row changes to New Row 1 Title  4) Click to go title (above)  Results: I am a title  5) Click New Row 1 Title    Results: KitchenSink crashes    Notes:   This seems to be a regression as I could not reproduce it in 1.7.4 (version=1.7.4, timestamp=10/31/11 10:30, githash=9b47b22).  Attached a log file of error.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink - Updating row's causes application to crash
Description: """"1) Launch KitchenSink from titanium_mobile demo's folder. 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update Row 3) Click Change Me (No Anim) Results: Row changes to New Row 1 Title 4) Click to go title (above) Results: I am a title 5) Click New Row 1 Title Results: KitchenSink crashes Notes: This seems to be a regression as I could not reproduce it in 1.7.4 (version=1.7.4, timestamp=10/31/11 10:30, githash=9b47b22). Attached a log file of error. """"",title+description
