TIMOB-5900,12,"""iOS5: Closing camera or gallery closes modal""","""""""If you open the camera or a photo gallery from a modal window, when you close this window, titanium also closes the modal window.  This does not happen on iOS4.    To reproduce, load app on device, click 'Launch Modal"""""""", then click """"""""Camera"""""""", take a picture and click """"""""Use"""""""".  Image should appear on the screen under the """"""""Camera"""""""" button on the """"""""Modal"""""""" window.  This works on iOS 4 devices.    {code:title = app.js}  var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(  {      title: """"""""window 1""""""""  });    var button1 = Titanium.UI.createButton(  {      color: '#999',      title: 'Launch Modal',      width: '200dp',      height: '60dp'  });    win1.add(button1);    button1.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function()  {      modal = Ti.UI.createWindow(      {          modal: true,          title: """"""""modal""""""""      });        var cameraButton = Ti.UI.createButton(      {          title: """"""""camera"""""""",          top: """"""""50dp"""""""",          width: """"""""150dp"""""""",          height: """"""""60dp""""""""      });      modal.add(cameraButton);      imageViewResize = Ti.UI.createImageView(      {          top: """"""""200dp"""""""",          height: """"""""200dp"""""""",          width: """"""""200dp""""""""      });      modal.add(imageViewResize);        cameraButton.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function()      {          Titanium.Media.showCamera(          {              success: function(event)              {                  imageViewResize.image = event.media;              },                error: function()              {              },                cancel: function()              {              },                saveToPhotoGallery: true,              allowEditing: true,              mediaTypes: [Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO],              showControls: true          });      });      modal.open();  });    win1.open();  {code}  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS5: Closing camera or gallery closes modal
Description: """"If you open the camera or a photo gallery from a modal window, when you close this window, titanium also closes the modal window. This does not happen on iOS4. To reproduce, load app on device, click 'Launch Modal"""""""", then click """"""""Camera"""""""", take a picture and click """"""""Use"""""""". Image should appear on the screen under the """"""""Camera"""""""" button on the """"""""Modal"""""""" window. This works on iOS 4 devices. {code:title = app.js} var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow( { title: """"""""window 1"""""""" }); var button1 = Titanium.UI.createButton( { color: '#999', title: 'Launch Modal', width: '200dp', height: '60dp' }); win1.add(button1); button1.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function() { modal = Ti.UI.createWindow( { modal: true, title: """"""""modal"""""""" }); var cameraButton = Ti.UI.createButton( { title: """"""""camera"""""""", top: """"""""50dp"""""""", width: """"""""150dp"""""""", height: """"""""60dp"""""""" }); modal.add(cameraButton); imageViewResize = Ti.UI.createImageView( { top: """"""""200dp"""""""", height: """"""""200dp"""""""", width: """"""""200dp"""""""" }); modal.add(imageViewResize); cameraButton.addEventListener(""""""""click"""""""", function() { Titanium.Media.showCamera( { success: function(event) { imageViewResize.image = event.media; }, error: function() { }, cancel: function() { }, saveToPhotoGallery: true, allowEditing: true, mediaTypes: [Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO], showControls: true }); }); modal.open(); }); win1.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-5893,12,"""iOS: iPad - Reopening grouped tableview renders additional blank space on the top of the window""","""""""h3.Problem  Grouped tableviews on iPad will display right against the top of the window the first time they are displayed, the second time the window is opened the  tableView has some extra padding on top. This issue exists only on iPad.    h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Run the following test case on iPad  2. Press the giant button  3. Observe the table view against the top of the window  4. Click the TableView to close the window  5. Press the giant button again  6. Observe spacing between top of TableView and window.    h3.Sample Code        h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-559499""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad - Reopening grouped tableview renders additional blank space on the top of the window
Description: """"h3.Problem Grouped tableviews on iPad will display right against the top of the window the first time they are displayed, the second time the window is opened the tableView has some extra padding on top. This issue exists only on iPad. h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Run the following test case on iPad 2. Press the giant button 3. Observe the table view against the top of the window 4. Click the TableView to close the window 5. Press the giant button again 6. Observe spacing between top of TableView and window. h3.Sample Code h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-559499""""",title+description
TIMOB-5891,12,"""iOS: Screen does not rotate to landscape on first launch if tiapp orientation is set to portrait""","""""""1) Import the attached application  2) Hold device in landscape mode and launch app    Results: Splash screen appears in portrait mode as expected, but app.js screen appears in portrait mode as well and does not rotate to landscape mode as expected.  After rotating the device into landscape mode the app will work as expected in any orientation mode.     Notes:  This only occurs on first launch.  Subsequent launches work as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Screen does not rotate to landscape on first launch if tiapp orientation is set to portrait
Description: """"1) Import the attached application 2) Hold device in landscape mode and launch app Results: Splash screen appears in portrait mode as expected, but app.js screen appears in portrait mode as well and does not rotate to landscape mode as expected. After rotating the device into landscape mode the app will work as expected in any orientation mode. Notes: This only occurs on first launch. Subsequent launches work as expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5890,12,"""Android: Passing the wrong time to analytics. Need to decide on local time + offest or UTC time with no offset""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Run test case 1000 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan    Actual Result:  {""""""""id"""""""":""""""""a91452a9-dbe3-4725-abbf-fa0acc0a5fa7:62aa69827255df19"""""""",""""""""sid"""""""":""""""""fc6d2a62-5bcd-4b00-b158-3f036d9f6fb7"""""""",""""""""ts"""""""":""""""""2011-10-27T21:22:20.767-0800"""""""",""""""""event"""""""":""""""""ti.enroll""""""""    Expected Result:  To either display local time with offset: 2011-10-27 15:37:55-07:00  Or  UTC time with no offset: 2011-10-27T22:23:44.162+0000    Note:  If we decide on local time with offset, we need to put a parity bug for iOS to fix, as they are currently using UTC time with no offset""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Passing the wrong time to analytics. Need to decide on local time + offest or UTC time with no offset
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Run test case 1000 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan Actual Result: {""""""""id"""""""":""""""""a91452a9-dbe3-4725-abbf-fa0acc0a5fa7:62aa69827255df19"""""""",""""""""sid"""""""":""""""""fc6d2a62-5bcd-4b00-b158-3f036d9f6fb7"""""""",""""""""ts"""""""":""""""""2011-10-27T21:22:20.767-0800"""""""",""""""""event"""""""":""""""""ti.enroll"""""""" Expected Result: To either display local time with offset: 2011-10-27 15:37:55-07:00 Or UTC time with no offset: 2011-10-27T22:23:44.162+0000 Note: If we decide on local time with offset, we need to put a parity bug for iOS to fix, as they are currently using UTC time with no offset""""",title+description
TIMOB-5889,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink - Changing a basic slider has an intermediate animation""","""""""1) In KitchenSink, navigate to Controls -> Slider -> Basic  2) Press 'Change Basic Slider'    Expected results:  Basic slider becomes similar to the custom slider without any intermediate animations/sliders.    Actual results:  There briefly appears a slider similar in size to the basic sliders original size, but with a skull instead of a button.  The slider then becomes longer and the skull moves back into its expected position.    Notes:  For convenience, I uploaded a video of this occurring:  http://vimeo.com/31224414    This is reproducible in 1.7.3 and SDK 1.7.4.v20111025165811    EDIT: Changed to 1.8.0  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink - Changing a basic slider has an intermediate animation
Description: """"1) In KitchenSink, navigate to Controls -> Slider -> Basic 2) Press 'Change Basic Slider' Expected results: Basic slider becomes similar to the custom slider without any intermediate animations/sliders. Actual results: There briefly appears a slider similar in size to the basic sliders original size, but with a skull instead of a button. The slider then becomes longer and the skull moves back into its expected position. Notes: For convenience, I uploaded a video of this occurring: http://vimeo.com/31224414 This is reproducible in 1.7.3 and SDK 1.7.4.v20111025165811 EDIT: Changed to 1.8.0 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5888,12,"""MobileWeb: Build system does not support dynamic filenames in Ti.includes""","""""""The build system attempts to scan the user's application code for all Ti.includes, then will serialize the contents of those includes into the compiled titanium.js.    The problem is when you try to include a file that is dynamically defined:        The problem takes place in the expand_ti_includes() function of compiler.py.  It's important that the function analyzes the filename and determine if it's a valid filename and that the file exists.  If it isn't or doesn't exist, don't error, just return.  If it does exist, then add it to self.ti_includes[src].    You'll have to test this by building a dummy app and creating a dynamic include, then building the mobile web app.  You will need to run builder.py from the command line to see any errors.    You can open the compiled titanium.js file to confirm the includes have been found and inlined properly at the bottom like this:      """"""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: Build system does not support dynamic filenames in Ti.includes
Description: """"The build system attempts to scan the user's application code for all Ti.includes, then will serialize the contents of those includes into the compiled titanium.js. The problem is when you try to include a file that is dynamically defined: The problem takes place in the expand_ti_includes() function of compiler.py. It's important that the function analyzes the filename and determine if it's a valid filename and that the file exists. If it isn't or doesn't exist, don't error, just return. If it does exist, then add it to self.ti_includes[src]. You'll have to test this by building a dummy app and creating a dynamic include, then building the mobile web app. You will need to run builder.py from the command line to see any errors. You can open the compiled titanium.js file to confirm the includes have been found and inlined properly at the bottom like this: """"",title+description
TIMOB-5887,12,"""Map annotation with external left button raises exception on clicking""","""""""A map annotation created with an external left button raises a FileNotFoundException on clicking. Although an exception occurs, I can see the left image getting displayed.    This can be reproduced in KitchenSink->Views->Map View. In *Resources/examples/map_view.js*, at around line 33 we have:    {code:title=Resources/examples/map_view.js|borderStyle=solid}  var atlantaParams = {                  latitude:33.74511,                  longitude:-84.38993,                  title:""""""""Atlanta, GA"""""""",                  subtitle:'Atlanta Braves Stadium\nfoo',                  animate:true,                  leftButton: '../images/atlanta.jpg',                  rightButton: Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.DISCLOSURE,                  myid:3 // CUSTOM ATTRIBUTE THAT IS PASSED INTO EVENT OBJECTS  };  {code}    *leftButton* is set to a local image here. Clicking on the Atlanta annotation works fine at this point. Now change *leftButton* to http://www.espncricinfo.com/favicon.png or http://facebook.com/favicon.ico or any other externally hosted PNG image. Now rebuild & click on the Atlanta annotation - you should see an exception being raised even though the left image was successfully displayed. This wasn't happening on 1.7.0 at least.    The logcat output corresponding to the exception is attached.""""""",Bug,"Title: Map annotation with external left button raises exception on clicking
Description: """"A map annotation created with an external left button raises a FileNotFoundException on clicking. Although an exception occurs, I can see the left image getting displayed. This can be reproduced in KitchenSink->Views->Map View. In *Resources/examples/map_view.js*, at around line 33 we have: {code:title=Resources/examples/map_view.js|borderStyle=solid} var atlantaParams = { latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993, title:""""""""Atlanta, GA"""""""", subtitle:'Atlanta Braves Stadium\nfoo', animate:true, leftButton: '../images/atlanta.jpg', rightButton: Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.DISCLOSURE, myid:3 // CUSTOM ATTRIBUTE THAT IS PASSED INTO EVENT OBJECTS }; {code} *leftButton* is set to a local image here. Clicking on the Atlanta annotation works fine at this point. Now change *leftButton* to http://www.espncricinfo.com/favicon.png or http://facebook.com/favicon.ico or any other externally hosted PNG image. Now rebuild & click on the Atlanta annotation - you should see an exception being raised even though the left image was successfully displayed. This wasn't happening on 1.7.0 at least. The logcat output corresponding to the exception is attached.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5886,12,"""TiAPI: Support additional datatypes for the functions in Ti.Utils""","""""""The functions in Ti.Utils currently are restricted to take TiBlob and String as argument. More datatypes will be supported for those functions: streams, buffers and other datatypes that could be encoded in a valid way.""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Support additional datatypes for the functions in Ti.Utils
Description: """"The functions in Ti.Utils currently are restricted to take TiBlob and String as argument. More datatypes will be supported for those functions: streams, buffers and other datatypes that could be encoded in a valid way.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5885,12,"""Android: Hero 2.1. Request to hide soft keyboard does nothing""","""""""Step To Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Base UI > Hide Soft Keyboard (Android)  2. Click in the text field to bring up the soft keyboard  3. Click on the """"""""Request Hide Keyboard"""""""" button    Actual:  Does Nothing    Expected:  Should hide the keyboard    Note: Seems to be a 2.1 issue, see it on emulator also""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Hero 2.1. Request to hide soft keyboard does nothing
Description: """"Step To Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Base UI > Hide Soft Keyboard (Android) 2. Click in the text field to bring up the soft keyboard 3. Click on the """"""""Request Hide Keyboard"""""""" button Actual: Does Nothing Expected: Should hide the keyboard Note: Seems to be a 2.1 issue, see it on emulator also""""",title+description
TIMOB-5883,12,"""Ti API: Support Click Events on Pickers""","""""""The picker should be able to emit """"""""click"""""""" events. This is seen for example in Facebook's app if you press the All Stories button, where the user closes the picker window by clicking an item in the picker. To do that, the picker should fire not only change events, but also click events. """"""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: Support Click Events on Pickers
Description: """"The picker should be able to emit """"""""click"""""""" events. This is seen for example in Facebook's app if you press the All Stories button, where the user closes the picker window by clicking an item in the picker. To do that, the picker should fire not only change events, but also click events. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5881,12,"""Ti API: DB result set: fieldCount is a property on Android, function on iPhone""","""""""{{resultset.fieldCount}} on Android    and    {{resultset.fieldCount()}} on iPhone    Can we have some parity please?  At this point, you'll probably have to support fieldCount as both a function and a property on both platforms, to avoid breaking existing code.    h3. This code will run on iOS, but fail on Android  {code:JavaScript|title:app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();  win.open();    var db = Titanium.Database.open('mydb');    db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS DATABASETEST (ID INTEGER, NAME TEXT)');    db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',1,'Name 1');  db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',2,'Name 2');  db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',3,'Name 3');  db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',4,'Name 4');    var rows = db.execute('SELECT * FROM DATABASETEST');    Ti.API.info(rows.fieldCount());    rows.close();  db.close();        This makes the code harder to write since developers but call a different code depending on the platform they are running. Also, there is a very subtle difference between the two, this makes this kind of error very easy to overlook. There should be a common way (either function or property) to access this information on all platforms.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti API: DB result set: fieldCount is a property on Android, function on iPhone
Description: """"{{resultset.fieldCount}} on Android and {{resultset.fieldCount()}} on iPhone Can we have some parity please? At this point, you'll probably have to support fieldCount as both a function and a property on both platforms, to avoid breaking existing code. h3. This code will run on iOS, but fail on Android {code:JavaScript|title:app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); win.open(); var db = Titanium.Database.open('mydb'); db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS DATABASETEST (ID INTEGER, NAME TEXT)'); db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',1,'Name 1'); db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',2,'Name 2'); db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',3,'Name 3'); db.execute('INSERT INTO DATABASETEST (ID, NAME ) VALUES(?,?)',4,'Name 4'); var rows = db.execute('SELECT * FROM DATABASETEST'); Ti.API.info(rows.fieldCount()); rows.close(); db.close(); This makes the code harder to write since developers but call a different code depending on the platform they are running. Also, there is a very subtle difference between the two, this makes this kind of error very easy to overlook. There should be a common way (either function or property) to access this information on all platforms.""""",title+description
