TIMOB-5863,12,"""Android: Missing null/undefined checks for some functions in android/modules/utils/UtilsModule.java""","""""""In android/modules/utils/UtilsModule.java, some functions take a string as an argument but don't have null/undefined checks. Therefore it will crash by running:                   Ti.Utils.sha1(null);       or                                   Ti.Utils.sha1(undefined);    {code:title=app.js}  Ti.Utils.base64encode(null);    Ti.Utils.base64decode(null);  Ti.Utils.base64decode(undefined);    Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest(null);  Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest(undefined);    Ti.Utils.sha1(null);  Ti.Utils.sha1(undefined);  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Missing null/undefined checks for some functions in android/modules/utils/UtilsModule.java
Description: """"In android/modules/utils/UtilsModule.java, some functions take a string as an argument but don't have null/undefined checks. Therefore it will crash by running: Ti.Utils.sha1(null); or Ti.Utils.sha1(undefined); {code:title=app.js} Ti.Utils.base64encode(null); Ti.Utils.base64decode(null); Ti.Utils.base64decode(undefined); Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest(null); Ti.Utils.md5HexDigest(undefined); Ti.Utils.sha1(null); Ti.Utils.sha1(undefined); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-5861,12,"""iOS: scrollView is not updated correctly.""","""""""h4. Steps To Reproduce:  1. Create a project to run the following app.js.  2. Hit the button then try to move the scrollable contents horizontally.  3. Hit the button again then try to move the scrollable contents horizontally.    Expected results: After resize the scrollView's width/height and its contentWidth/contentHeight, the scroll view should get updated immediately.  Actual results: After resizing, the scroll view is not updated until the view is refreshed(happened when the button is hit again).        h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-113112  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: scrollView is not updated correctly.
Description: """"h4. Steps To Reproduce: 1. Create a project to run the following app.js. 2. Hit the button then try to move the scrollable contents horizontally. 3. Hit the button again then try to move the scrollable contents horizontally. Expected results: After resize the scrollView's width/height and its contentWidth/contentHeight, the scroll view should get updated immediately. Actual results: After resizing, the scroll view is not updated until the view is refreshed(happened when the button is hit again). h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-113112 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5860,12,"""iOS: network.httpclient drillbit test case fails""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Run Drillbit  2. Run network.httpclient test on iOS    Actual Result:        clearCookiePositiveTest_as_async   false  Timed out waiting for HTTP onload        clearCookieUnaffectedCheck_as_async false  Timed out waiting for HTTP onload    Expected Result:  Should pass""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: network.httpclient drillbit test case fails
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Run Drillbit 2. Run network.httpclient test on iOS Actual Result: clearCookiePositiveTest_as_async false Timed out waiting for HTTP onload clearCookieUnaffectedCheck_as_async false Timed out waiting for HTTP onload Expected Result: Should pass""""",title+description
TIMOB-5859,12,"""MobileWeb: Implement require() function""","""""""Need to add support for the require() function. This function will accept a string of the module to load, then synchronously fetches the module, evaluates the module, caches the API, and returns the API.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Implement require() function
Description: """"Need to add support for the require() function. This function will accept a string of the module to load, then synchronously fetches the module, evaluates the module, caches the API, and returns the API.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5858,12,"""MobileWeb: Update index.html and build process to use mako template engine for variable insertion""","""""""There are a number of places that constants are injected into the mobile web's index.html template and various JavaScript files where these constants are not properly escaped. If a project name has a < or > in it, it will cause invalid HTML markup.  Or if the project description has an unescaped quote, it will break the JavaScript.    Integrate the mako template engine into the build <USER>and escape the variable insertions using the correct mako filters.    Refer to the mako filtering documentation for more information: http://www.makotemplates.org/docs/documentation.html#filtering.""""""",New Feature,"Title: MobileWeb: Update index.html and build process to use mako template engine for variable insertion
Description: """"There are a number of places that constants are injected into the mobile web's index.html template and various JavaScript files where these constants are not properly escaped. If a project name has a < or > in it, it will cause invalid HTML markup. Or if the project description has an unescaped quote, it will break the JavaScript. Integrate the mako template engine into the build <USER>and escape the variable insertions using the correct mako filters. Refer to the mako filtering documentation for more information: http://www.makotemplates.org/docs/documentation.html#filtering.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5857,12,"""KitchenSink: Launching in landscape on iPhone 4s with iOS 5.0 results in gap at top of screen""","""""""Description:  While testing pull 582 across all iOS devices, the iPhone 4s showed a gap at the control tab when the app loaded. This did not occur on any other device we tested (all of them in our inventory)including other iOS 5.0 devices.    Steps to repro:  1) Install KS 1.7.x built with SDK 1.7.4.v20111021181815+ (the next build should have the pull code)  2) Hold device in landscape  3) Launch KS    Result:  See screenshot. There is a gap at the top of the screen, between the nab and status bars.    Expected:  No gap  """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Launching in landscape on iPhone 4s with iOS 5.0 results in gap at top of screen
Description: """"Description: While testing pull 582 across all iOS devices, the iPhone 4s showed a gap at the control tab when the app loaded. This did not occur on any other device we tested (all of them in our inventory)including other iOS 5.0 devices. Steps to repro: 1) Install KS 1.7.x built with SDK 1.7.4.v20111021181815+ (the next build should have the pull code) 2) Hold device in landscape 3) Launch KS Result: See screenshot. There is a gap at the top of the screen, between the nab and status bars. Expected: No gap """"",title+description
TIMOB-5856,12,"""Android: Landscape splash not appearing or appears stretched when device held in landscape during app launch""","""""""Description:  I was trying to determine the behavior of the android devices when held in landscape while launching an app. I was unable to get the faster devices to display any splash in landscape. This differs from the behavior while launching in portrait mode. I was able on subsequent launches to get the slower devices to flash a red splash, but it looks like the portrait one stretched. The sample code generated by Studio for a mobile android project contains 11 images for various resolutions. I was trying to determine which is used in landscape for various devices.    I was unable to capture a screenshot since the splash when displayed is only there for a split second.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Create a new Ti Mobile project in studio  2) Examine the folder structure to verify the various images at resources/android/images/res*  3) Install on device  4) Rotate to landscape orientation  5) Launch app    Result:  Splash screen not displayed on first launch    Expected:  Splash screen displayed""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Landscape splash not appearing or appears stretched when device held in landscape during app launch
Description: """"Description: I was trying to determine the behavior of the android devices when held in landscape while launching an app. I was unable to get the faster devices to display any splash in landscape. This differs from the behavior while launching in portrait mode. I was able on subsequent launches to get the slower devices to flash a red splash, but it looks like the portrait one stretched. The sample code generated by Studio for a mobile android project contains 11 images for various resolutions. I was trying to determine which is used in landscape for various devices. I was unable to capture a screenshot since the splash when displayed is only there for a split second. Steps to reproduce: 1) Create a new Ti Mobile project in studio 2) Examine the folder structure to verify the various images at resources/android/images/res* 3) Install on device 4) Rotate to landscape orientation 5) Launch app Result: Splash screen not displayed on first launch Expected: Splash screen displayed""""",title+description
TIMOB-5855,12,"""iOS: emailDialog crashes if opened with animated:false""","""""""If you try to open the emailDialog with animated true it crashes the app.    Step 1: run the code below  Step 2: click on the screen  Step 3: see the app crash  Step 4: remove '{animated:true}' from the open  Step 5: run again  Step 6: see the dialog open as it should    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'blue'  });    win.addEventListener('click',function(e){   // works fine with modal windows   // var newWin = Ti.UI.createWindow({modal:true});   // newWin.open({animated:false});      var email = Ti.UI.createEmailDialog();   email.open({animated:true});  });    win.open();    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: emailDialog crashes if opened with animated:false
Description: """"If you try to open the emailDialog with animated true it crashes the app. Step 1: run the code below Step 2: click on the screen Step 3: see the app crash Step 4: remove '{animated:true}' from the open Step 5: run again Step 6: see the dialog open as it should {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'blue' }); win.addEventListener('click',function(e){ // works fine with modal windows // var newWin = Ti.UI.createWindow({modal:true}); // newWin.open({animated:false}); var email = Ti.UI.createEmailDialog(); email.open({animated:true}); }); win.open(); """"",title+description
TIMOB-5853,12,"""iOS: Debugger: 10.6.8 only: Running the basic breakpoint in debugger cause simulator to eventually exit on it on""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:   1. Run Test case 1013 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Debugger+Test+Plan  2. Go through all the steps from top to bottom    Actual Result:  By step 21-22 the simulator exits on its own     Expected Result:  Should not exit    Exit info:  shell-init: error retrieving current directory: getcwd: cannot access parent directories: No such file or directory  [DEBUG] Session did end with error Error Domain=DTiPhoneSimulatorErrorDomain Code=1 UserInfo=0x103001600 """"""""The simulated application quit.""""""""  [INFO] Application has exited from Simulator  Note:   Last working with 1.7.4.v20111020142213 and 1.7.3   Occurs on Snow Leopard only. Lion works fine""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Debugger: 10.6.8 only: Running the basic breakpoint in debugger cause simulator to eventually exit on it on
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run Test case 1013 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Debugger+Test+Plan 2. Go through all the steps from top to bottom Actual Result: By step 21-22 the simulator exits on its own Expected Result: Should not exit Exit info: shell-init: error retrieving current directory: getcwd: cannot access parent directories: No such file or directory [DEBUG] Session did end with error Error Domain=DTiPhoneSimulatorErrorDomain Code=1 UserInfo=0x103001600 """"""""The simulated application quit."""""""" [INFO] Application has exited from Simulator Note: Last working with 1.7.4.v20111020142213 and 1.7.3 Occurs on Snow Leopard only. Lion works fine""""",title+description
