TIMOB-5836,12,"""iOS: Application does not recognize upside down portrait orientation mode ""","""""""1) Create a new project and place the following in the app.js    2) Place the grouch.jpg in the Resources folder  3) Launch project    Expected results:  Application launches normally and image appears in upside portrait mode    Actual results: Application Error: Result of expression 'win.orientationModes' [undefined] is not an object. at app.js (line 1)     Notes:  Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT is recognized as a valid orientation mode when there are other orientation modes in win.orientationModes[].  This error only occurs when there is only Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT in win.orientationModes[].    In SDK 1.7.2 and 1.7.3, the error appears as 'null' instead of 'undefined'    EDIT: Fixed syntax""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Application does not recognize upside down portrait orientation mode
Description: """"1) Create a new project and place the following in the app.js 2) Place the grouch.jpg in the Resources folder 3) Launch project Expected results: Application launches normally and image appears in upside portrait mode Actual results: Application Error: Result of expression 'win.orientationModes' [undefined] is not an object. at app.js (line 1) Notes: Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT is recognized as a valid orientation mode when there are other orientation modes in win.orientationModes[]. This error only occurs when there is only Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT in win.orientationModes[]. In SDK 1.7.2 and 1.7.3, the error appears as 'null' instead of 'undefined' EDIT: Fixed syntax""""",title+description
TIMOB-5835,12,"""iOS: Application error message is not giving the correct line number of an error""","""""""1) Create a new project and place the following in the app.js (notice the syntax error at line 7)    2) Place grouch.png in Resources folder  3) Launch the application    Results:   Application Error: Parse error at app.js (line 1)    Error message shows an error at line 1, even though it is at line 7.    Notes:  This was reproducible in 1.7.3.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Application error message is not giving the correct line number of an error
Description: """"1) Create a new project and place the following in the app.js (notice the syntax error at line 7) 2) Place grouch.png in Resources folder 3) Launch the application Results: Application Error: Parse error at app.js (line 1) Error message shows an error at line 1, even though it is at line 7. Notes: This was reproducible in 1.7.3.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5834,12,"""Kitchen Sink crash on launch in iPad 1 (os version 3.2.2) in landscape orientation""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Install 1_7_x branch of Kitchen Sink on iPad 1 with iOS version 3.2.2  2. Launch Kitchen Sink in landscape    Actual result:    Kitchen Sink crashes on launch in landscape orientation.    Expected result:    Kitchen Sink should launch in landscape orientation.    Notes:  Last working build is 1.7.2  Does not reproduce on iPad1 running 4X or any iPad2""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchen Sink crash on launch in iPad 1 (os version 3.2.2) in landscape orientation
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Install 1_7_x branch of Kitchen Sink on iPad 1 with iOS version 3.2.2 2. Launch Kitchen Sink in landscape Actual result: Kitchen Sink crashes on launch in landscape orientation. Expected result: Kitchen Sink should launch in landscape orientation. Notes: Last working build is 1.7.2 Does not reproduce on iPad1 running 4X or any iPad2""""",title+description
TIMOB-5833,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Nav Group: Nav Group navBar does not resize on rotation. ""","""""""Description:  While testing KS, Base UI>Nav Group, I encountered a problem with the Nav Group NavBar. It was no resizing on device rotation. If you launched the test in landscape, it would remain in landscape. If it launched in portrait the navBar would remain the portrait size. This results in a blank band after rotation when starting landscape, opening the nab group, then rotating and closing. Please see attached image.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Launch KS built with 1.7.4  2) Navigate to Base UI>Nav Group  4) Change to landscape orientation  5) Click """"""""open tab group"""""""" button  6) Rotate device to portrait    Result:  NavBar remains the small landscape size, causing a gap to appear at the top of the displayed window    Expected result:  NavBar resizes to portrait size""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Nav Group: Nav Group navBar does not resize on rotation.
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Nav Group, I encountered a problem with the Nav Group NavBar. It was no resizing on device rotation. If you launched the test in landscape, it would remain in landscape. If it launched in portrait the navBar would remain the portrait size. This results in a blank band after rotation when starting landscape, opening the nab group, then rotating and closing. Please see attached image. Steps to reproduce: 1) Launch KS built with 1.7.4 2) Navigate to Base UI>Nav Group 4) Change to landscape orientation 5) Click """"""""open tab group"""""""" button 6) Rotate device to portrait Result: NavBar remains the small landscape size, causing a gap to appear at the top of the displayed window Expected result: NavBar resizes to portrait size""""",title+description
TIMOB-5832,12,"""iOS5, modal windows - partial curl: rotating with partial curl up does not rotate the underlying window""","""""""1. KS > Base UI > modal windows  2. on the left side of the picker, scroll down to partial curl  3. select an option on the right, and tap """"""""show modal""""""""  4. rotate the device    results: the curl rotates, but the underlying window does not. not seen on the pre ios5""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS5, modal windows - partial curl: rotating with partial curl up does not rotate the underlying window
Description: """"1. KS > Base UI > modal windows 2. on the left side of the picker, scroll down to partial curl 3. select an option on the right, and tap """"""""show modal"""""""" 4. rotate the device results: the curl rotates, but the underlying window does not. not seen on the pre ios5""""",title+description
TIMOB-5831,12,"""Facebook module - after entering an incorrect password, password mask is not invoked""","""""""1. Ks > FB > log  2. enter a valid id, then enter the wrong password  3. after the password is rejected, re-enter it    results: password mask is not invoked. see screen shot""""""",Bug,"Title: Facebook module - after entering an incorrect password, password mask is not invoked
Description: """"1. Ks > FB > log 2. enter a valid id, then enter the wrong password 3. after the password is rejected, re-enter it results: password mask is not invoked. see screen shot""""",title+description
TIMOB-5830,12,"""Android: Facebook dialog window crashes (login dialog for 2.2, wall post dialog for 2.1)""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Mash Up > Facebook > Publish Stream > Publish wall post with DIALOG    Actual Result:  Crash    Expected Result:  To be able to publish wall post with dialog    Note:  Reference TIMOB-1419 (iOS bug)    Additional notes: 2.1 crashes, 2.2 does not keep a log in dialog up, 2.3.X and 3.X work as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook dialog window crashes (login dialog for 2.2, wall post dialog for 2.1)
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Mash Up > Facebook > Publish Stream > Publish wall post with DIALOG Actual Result: Crash Expected Result: To be able to publish wall post with dialog Note: Reference TIMOB-1419 (iOS bug) Additional notes: 2.1 crashes, 2.2 does not keep a log in dialog up, 2.3.X and 3.X work as expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5828,12,"""Kitchensink: Navbar does not change size when rotating to landscape on main windows.""","""""""Description:  When launching Kitchen sink, on any of the main windows, the navbar does not resize when rotating the device to landscape then back to portrait. This did not occur with 1.7.2 GA or 1.7.3 GA, but does also occur with with 1.8.0.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS with 1.7.4 build  2) Launch KS  3) Rotate the device to landscape    result:  Navbar remains full size (portrait size)    expected:  Navbar resizes based on orientation    Notes:  Using the orientation test (Phone>Orientation) and clicking """"""""set landscape"""""""" forces the navbar to the thinner size. After this the navbar remains small despite orientation""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Navbar does not change size when rotating to landscape on main windows.
Description: """"Description: When launching Kitchen sink, on any of the main windows, the navbar does not resize when rotating the device to landscape then back to portrait. This did not occur with 1.7.2 GA or 1.7.3 GA, but does also occur with with 1.8.0. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS with 1.7.4 build 2) Launch KS 3) Rotate the device to landscape result: Navbar remains full size (portrait size) expected: Navbar resizes based on orientation Notes: Using the orientation test (Phone>Orientation) and clicking """"""""set landscape"""""""" forces the navbar to the thinner size. After this the navbar remains small despite orientation""""",title+description
TIMOB-5827,12,"""iOS: Opening window in full screen does not cover the nav bar""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Compile the attached app.js   2. Run on device    Actual:  The status bar displays a black bar    Expected:  The new window should be full screen and cover the status bar    Note:  Works with 1.7.3""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Opening window in full screen does not cover the nav bar
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Compile the attached app.js 2. Run on device Actual: The status bar displays a black bar Expected: The new window should be full screen and cover the status bar Note: Works with 1.7.3""""",title+description
TIMOB-5826,12,"""iOS: Enabled Not Working for labels in TabbedBar""","""""""The enabled property of the labels for a TabbedBar do not render the tab disabled if enabled is set to false. This only happens on creation of the TabbedBar.    http://developer.<USER>com/question/122744/tabbedbar-enable-issue    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Enabled Not Working for labels in TabbedBar
Description: """"The enabled property of the labels for a TabbedBar do not render the tab disabled if enabled is set to false. This only happens on creation of the TabbedBar. http://developer.<USER>com/question/122744/tabbedbar-enable-issue """"",title+description
TIMOB-5825,12,"""App restarts with error in log when it is reopened""","""""""# Open KitchenSink.  # Go to  Base UI > Views > Web Views > Local URL.  # Then cause the app to close. NOT by force-stopping it from Settings > Applications[1], but by opening enough other applications to use up memory. (you may need to open around 4-5 apps)  # Now reopen KitchenSink. It will restart.    In logcat, you will get an error like:        (Restarting is probably the correct behavior, but we should not be showing these errors in logcat)""""""",Bug,"Title: App restarts with error in log when it is reopened
Description: """"# Open KitchenSink. # Go to Base UI > Views > Web Views > Local URL. # Then cause the app to close. NOT by force-stopping it from Settings > Applications[1], but by opening enough other applications to use up memory. (you may need to open around 4-5 apps) # Now reopen KitchenSink. It will restart. In logcat, you will get an error like: (Restarting is probably the correct behavior, but we should not be showing these errors in logcat)""""",title+description
TIMOB-5824,12,"""Android: WebView.evalJS Causes Form Input Fields to Lost/Not Retain Focus""","""""""h4. Problem Description  I'm using the WebView's evalJS function in a setInterval() to act as a bridge between Titanium and a web app from a remote web server.  However, form fields in the web app on Android do not work -- I can tap into the form field, but the keyboard never comes up, or if it does, it disappears immediately.    h4. Actual Results  The keyboard never comes up, with an error like this:    ERROR: Error: Only the original thread that created a view hierarchy can touch its views.      h4. Expected Results  The keyboard working just fine.       h4. Test Case  1. Create new mobile project  2. Drop the following in app.js and run it on a simulator or actual device.  Tap into the Google search box, and the keyboard may briefly appear before disappearing; either way you won't be able to type into the box.      h4. Extra info     I have noticed that removing the try/catch block in the """"""""doSomething"""""""" method causes the entire app to crash with a Java error, something about """"""""JavaException: android.view.ViewRoot$CalledFromWrongThreadException: Only the original thread that created a view hierarchy can touch its views.""""""""  To get around that error, I tried creating the WebView in the doSomething() method so that the WebView was created in the same thread in which it was used.  This seemed to fix the error in the example given above, but in the app I'm building (which I unfortunately can't share in this public setting) the input boxes still lost focus.      This same problem was reported on the Q&A several months ago, with no apparent resolution:    http://developer.<USER>com/question/119845/using-webviewevaljs-and-lost-focus-android#comment-100385    I should add that the """"""""lost focus"""""""" problem does not appear on the iOS simulator, using the app.js listed here.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: WebView.evalJS Causes Form Input Fields to Lost/Not Retain Focus
Description: """"h4. Problem Description I'm using the WebView's evalJS function in a setInterval() to act as a bridge between Titanium and a web app from a remote web server. However, form fields in the web app on Android do not work -- I can tap into the form field, but the keyboard never comes up, or if it does, it disappears immediately. h4. Actual Results The keyboard never comes up, with an error like this: ERROR: Error: Only the original thread that created a view hierarchy can touch its views. h4. Expected Results The keyboard working just fine. h4. Test Case 1. Create new mobile project 2. Drop the following in app.js and run it on a simulator or actual device. Tap into the Google search box, and the keyboard may briefly appear before disappearing; either way you won't be able to type into the box. h4. Extra info I have noticed that removing the try/catch block in the """"""""doSomething"""""""" method causes the entire app to crash with a Java error, something about """"""""JavaException: android.view.ViewRoot$CalledFromWrongThreadException: Only the original thread that created a view hierarchy can touch its views."""""""" To get around that error, I tried creating the WebView in the doSomething() method so that the WebView was created in the same thread in which it was used. This seemed to fix the error in the example given above, but in the app I'm building (which I unfortunately can't share in this public setting) the input boxes still lost focus. This same problem was reported on the Q&A several months ago, with no apparent resolution: http://developer.<USER>com/question/119845/using-webviewevaljs-and-lost-focus-android#comment-100385 I should add that the """"""""lost focus"""""""" problem does not appear on the iOS simulator, using the app.js listed here. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5822,12,"""iOS: navbar size wrong after orientation change""","""""""Navbar size is scrambled in several ways:     1) does not get thinner when rotating to landscape    2) is repainted at wrong size (thin instead of full) after orientation change back to portrait. E.g.:   - on a win with orientationModes set to portrait, open (in tab) a new win with all orientationModes allowed  - rotate to landscape, then go back: the previous win forces rotation back to portrait, but its navbar is repainted as if 32px high instead of the correct 44px      Neither was a problem in previous SDK versions up to and including 1.7.1    {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: 'white',      navBarHidden:false  });  win.orientationModes = [Ti.UI.PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT]    var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({   top:100, width:200, height:50,   title:""""""""Open landscape win""""""""  });  btn.addEventListener('click', function () {   var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({    navBarHidden:false, backgroundColor:'gray'   });   win2.orientationModes = [Ti.UI.PORTRAIT,Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT,Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT]      var message = Ti.UI.createLabel({    top:60, left:20, right:20, height:'auto',    text:""""""""1) Rotate to landscape: navBar is NOT changing to 32px high...\n2) Now press back WHILE IN LANDSCAPE and look at the navBar of root win!""""""""   });   win2.add(message);   tab1.open(win2);  });  win.add(btn);    var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup({});  var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({window:win});  tabGroup.addTab(tab1);  tabGroup.setActiveTab(1);  tabGroup.open();  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: navbar size wrong after orientation change
Description: """"Navbar size is scrambled in several ways: 1) does not get thinner when rotating to landscape 2) is repainted at wrong size (thin instead of full) after orientation change back to portrait. E.g.: - on a win with orientationModes set to portrait, open (in tab) a new win with all orientationModes allowed - rotate to landscape, then go back: the previous win forces rotation back to portrait, but its navbar is repainted as if 32px high instead of the correct 44px Neither was a problem in previous SDK versions up to and including 1.7.1 {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white', navBarHidden:false }); win.orientationModes = [Ti.UI.PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT] var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ top:100, width:200, height:50, title:""""""""Open landscape win"""""""" }); btn.addEventListener('click', function () { var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ navBarHidden:false, backgroundColor:'gray' }); win2.orientationModes = [Ti.UI.PORTRAIT,Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT,Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT] var message = Ti.UI.createLabel({ top:60, left:20, right:20, height:'auto', text:""""""""1) Rotate to landscape: navBar is NOT changing to 32px high...\n2) Now press back WHILE IN LANDSCAPE and look at the navBar of root win!"""""""" }); win2.add(message); tab1.open(win2); }); win.add(btn); var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup({}); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({window:win}); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.setActiveTab(1); tabGroup.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-5821,12,"""Android SDK r14 tooling breaks scons""","""""""Description:  While setting up our new QE team members, we encountered a problem with scons failing. After speaking with Don, this is caused by the naming convention used for new installations for the API 7 folder in <android_sdk>/add-ons. Details of the console output are:    Traceback (most recent call last):    File """"""""/usr/local/bin/scons"""""""", line 5, in <module>      pkg_resources.run_script('scons==2.1.0', 'scons')    File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.7/Extras/lib/python/pkg_resources.py"""""""", line 489, in run_script      self.require(requires)[0].run_script(script_name, ns)    File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.7/Extras/lib/python/pkg_resources.py"""""""", line 1207, in run_script      execfile(script_filename, namespace, namespace)    File """"""""/Library/Python/2.7/site-packages/scons-2.1.0-py2.7.egg/EGG-INFO/scripts/scons"""""""", line 187, in <module>      import SCons.Script  ImportError: No module named SCons.Script    Steps to reproduce:  1) Perform a clean installation of the Android SDK API 14  2) In terminal go to your titanium_mobile GIT repository  3) try to scons    Result:  scons fails with console error as listed above    Expected:  scons completes successfully    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android SDK r14 tooling breaks scons
Description: """"Description: While setting up our new QE team members, we encountered a problem with scons failing. After speaking with Don, this is caused by the naming convention used for new installations for the API 7 folder in <android_sdk>/add-ons. Details of the console output are: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/usr/local/bin/scons"""""""", line 5, in <module> pkg_resources.run_script('scons==2.1.0', 'scons') File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.7/Extras/lib/python/pkg_resources.py"""""""", line 489, in run_script self.require(requires)[0].run_script(script_name, ns) File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.7/Extras/lib/python/pkg_resources.py"""""""", line 1207, in run_script execfile(script_filename, namespace, namespace) File """"""""/Library/Python/2.7/site-packages/scons-2.1.0-py2.7.egg/EGG-INFO/scripts/scons"""""""", line 187, in <module> import SCons.Script ImportError: No module named SCons.Script Steps to reproduce: 1) Perform a clean installation of the Android SDK API 14 2) In terminal go to your titanium_mobile GIT repository 3) try to scons Result: scons fails with console error as listed above Expected: scons completes successfully """"",title+description
TIMOB-5820,12,"""Titanium.UI.WebView.repaint() method causes exception""","""""""Using the repaint method of a webview causes exception    h2. Testcase        h2. Result    The webview is rendered, but repaint then causes the following exception:      h2. Possible Cause    While there are references to repaint in the ios source, none exist in Android. Is this platform-specific function, that requires an APIDoc rather than an Android ticket?  """"""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.UI.WebView.repaint() method causes exception
Description: """"Using the repaint method of a webview causes exception h2. Testcase h2. Result The webview is rendered, but repaint then causes the following exception: h2. Possible Cause While there are references to repaint in the ios source, none exist in Android. Is this platform-specific function, that requires an APIDoc rather than an Android ticket? """"",title+description
TIMOB-5819,12,"""Android: Percentage-based views need to be re-drawn on device rotation""","""""""Views that have widths or positioning points based on percentages do not properly get updated on device rotation.    Sample Code      As shown in the images, when started in Portrait, the views are shown properly.  On turning the emulator/ device to landscape, the white space between the two views can be noticed. Also, the bottoms of views are not visible.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Percentage-based views need to be re-drawn on device rotation
Description: """"Views that have widths or positioning points based on percentages do not properly get updated on device rotation. Sample Code As shown in the images, when started in Portrait, the views are shown properly. On turning the emulator/ device to landscape, the white space between the two views can be noticed. Also, the bottoms of views are not visible. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5818,12,"""Ti API: View proxies should behave like real JS objects - or they should be wrapped""","""""""Component: Ti API    If view proxies aren't going to behave like real JS objects (e.g. nested properties of proxy objects are immutable), and that isn't going to change, I propose we should develop a pure-JS API that wraps the proxies.    I've begun wrapping Ti views in my [SproutCore-Titanium project|https://github.com/<USER>sproutcore-titanium].    Let's get a discussion started.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Ti API: View proxies should behave like real JS objects - or they should be wrapped
Description: """"Component: Ti API If view proxies aren't going to behave like real JS objects (e.g. nested properties of proxy objects are immutable), and that isn't going to change, I propose we should develop a pure-JS API that wraps the proxies. I've begun wrapping Ti views in my [SproutCore-Titanium project|https://github.com/<USER>sproutcore-titanium]. Let's get a discussion started.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5816,12,"""MobileWeb: TableViewRow.js ClickEvent fails due to undefined variables in addEventListener""","""""""Line 427 checks for variables _hasCheckObj, _hasChildObj, and _hasDetailObj to see if they're equiv to event.srcElement, but the above variables are no where to be found.     Offending code:   tableView.addEventListener('click', function(e) {  ...    Fix:   Comment out line 427 of tableviewrow.js (for now)  //detail: event.srcElement == _hasCheckObj || event.srcElement == _hasChildObj || event.srcElement == _hasDetailObj || false,""""""",Bug,"Title: MobileWeb: TableViewRow.js ClickEvent fails due to undefined variables in addEventListener
Description: """"Line 427 checks for variables _hasCheckObj, _hasChildObj, and _hasDetailObj to see if they're equiv to event.srcElement, but the above variables are no where to be found. Offending code: tableView.addEventListener('click', function(e) { ... Fix: Comment out line 427 of tableviewrow.js (for now) //detail: event.srcElement == _hasCheckObj || event.srcElement == _hasChildObj || event.srcElement == _hasDetailObj || false,""""",title+description
TIMOB-5815,12,"""iOS: Native JS Modules not taken in consideration when running the optimalizer for a release build""","""""""When a release build (run on iOS device) is done, a set of defines are generated to strip the binairy down to the API parts that are used in the App. When certain API's are only used in a JS module and not in the App, the application will crash since they are missing. Define (pseudo) calls to the API's in the app, and the module works.    In the simulator, all API's are included so everything works as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Native JS Modules not taken in consideration when running the optimalizer for a release build
Description: """"When a release build (run on iOS device) is done, a set of defines are generated to strip the binairy down to the API parts that are used in the App. When certain API's are only used in a JS module and not in the App, the application will crash since they are missing. Define (pseudo) calls to the API's in the app, and the module works. In the simulator, all API's are included so everything works as expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5814,12,"""Should be able to set borderStyle on Titanium.UI.TextArea""","""""""You should be able to set borderStyle, e.g. to Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED on Titanium.UI.TextArea (as you can on Titanium.UI.TextField)    for instance:  """"""",Bug,"Title: Should be able to set borderStyle on Titanium.UI.TextArea
Description: """"You should be able to set borderStyle, e.g. to Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED on Titanium.UI.TextArea (as you can on Titanium.UI.TextField) for instance: """"",title+description
TIMOB-5813,12,"""TableView issue with className - Wrong row(s) updated!""","""""""Greetings,    I have created a TableView, added a handful of rows then update one of those rows. The problem is that the wrong row or rows are being updated. If I turn the phone on the side and then back again, the rows show the correct information. I found that if I do not add """"""""className"""""""" then it works fine. However I am under the impression that """"""""className"""""""" is utilized internally to improve performance.    We are also having problems with wrong check boxes on rows being updated. I wonder if this is related.    The following code reproduces the issue. I have simplified everything, removing all of the complexities of my actual application.        In the above example, the row labeled '6' should show 'OnTimeout', all the reset should show 1-9. The 6th row does show 'OnTimeout' correctly however, the 8th row also shows 'OnTimeout', which is incorrect.    Turn the phone on the side and the rows will magically be displayed correctly!    Change the code as follow and it works fine...        The only difference is that """"""""className"""""""" is not set!""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView issue with className - Wrong row(s) updated!
Description: """"Greetings, I have created a TableView, added a handful of rows then update one of those rows. The problem is that the wrong row or rows are being updated. If I turn the phone on the side and then back again, the rows show the correct information. I found that if I do not add """"""""className"""""""" then it works fine. However I am under the impression that """"""""className"""""""" is utilized internally to improve performance. We are also having problems with wrong check boxes on rows being updated. I wonder if this is related. The following code reproduces the issue. I have simplified everything, removing all of the complexities of my actual application. In the above example, the row labeled '6' should show 'OnTimeout', all the reset should show 1-9. The 6th row does show 'OnTimeout' correctly however, the 8th row also shows 'OnTimeout', which is incorrect. Turn the phone on the side and the rows will magically be displayed correctly! Change the code as follow and it works fine... The only difference is that """"""""className"""""""" is not set!""""",title+description
TIMOB-5811,12,"""iOS: Add scrollEnabled to Titanium.UI.ScrollableView""","""""""It should be possible to disable scrolling (by swiping) in the iOS ScrollableView.     A jumping off point for this can be found here - http://developer.<USER>com/question/124461/disable-scrolling-on-scrollview-by-touch""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add scrollEnabled to Titanium.UI.ScrollableView
Description: """"It should be possible to disable scrolling (by swiping) in the iOS ScrollableView. A jumping off point for this can be found here - http://developer.<USER>com/question/124461/disable-scrolling-on-scrollview-by-touch""""",title+description
TIMOB-5810,12,"""Android: maxLength propery on TextField and TextArea""","""""""TextField and TextArea needs a property to control the max length of the input text.    Though this can be done using an eventlistener and a length check. It would be very useful if this was built-in.        1. Run code  2. Check log, make sure maxLength is -1  3. Click on button  4. Start typing, the content should not exceed 10 characters.  5. Re-run code, this time enter 20+ characters before click on button  6. Click on button, text now should truncate to 10 characters  7. Repeat 1-6 on textArea.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: maxLength propery on TextField and TextArea
Description: """"TextField and TextArea needs a property to control the max length of the input text. Though this can be done using an eventlistener and a length check. It would be very useful if this was built-in. 1. Run code 2. Check log, make sure maxLength is -1 3. Click on button 4. Start typing, the content should not exceed 10 characters. 5. Re-run code, this time enter 20+ characters before click on button 6. Click on button, text now should truncate to 10 characters 7. Repeat 1-6 on textArea.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5808,12,"""Android: Unexpected """"Ghost-Margin"""" in a Vertical layout!""","""""""I try to create an article with some paragraphs (see example sourcecode: uiLabelRed, uiLabelBlue and uiLabelGreen). I use vertical layout! Each paragraph should have 10dp space (by adding top:'10dp', see example and screenshot)    On the appended screenshot you see the strange result. I already tried to find a workaround (encapsulate the labels), but this also dont work. See forum. http://developer.<USER>com/question/124783/unwanted-ghost-padding-in-a-vertical-layout#answer-217498     """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Unexpected """"Ghost-Margin"""" in a Vertical layout!
Description: """"I try to create an article with some paragraphs (see example sourcecode: uiLabelRed, uiLabelBlue and uiLabelGreen). I use vertical layout! Each paragraph should have 10dp space (by adding top:'10dp', see example and screenshot) On the appended screenshot you see the strange result. I already tried to find a workaround (encapsulate the labels), but this also dont work. See forum. http://developer.<USER>com/question/124783/unwanted-ghost-padding-in-a-vertical-layout#answer-217498 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5807,12,"""getResponseHeader('WWW-Authenticate') on 401 returns null""","""""""Retrieving WWW-Authenticate header when the server status code is 401 returns null.    Usecase:       WWW-Authenticate is needed to create a Digest Auth system.  """"""",Bug,"Title: getResponseHeader('WWW-Authenticate') on 401 returns null
Description: """"Retrieving WWW-Authenticate header when the server status code is 401 returns null. Usecase: WWW-Authenticate is needed to create a Digest Auth system. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5804,12,"""iOS: Cannot launch app on device.""","""""""1) Create a new project  2) Try and run it on device    Results:  Build fails.  See attached console.txt for TiStudio console output.    Notes:  Cleaning the project's build folder does not help.  This is a new regression to 1.7.4.  When I switched SDK 1.7.3, launching to device worked as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot launch app on device.
Description: """"1) Create a new project 2) Try and run it on device Results: Build fails. See attached console.txt for TiStudio console output. Notes: Cleaning the project's build folder does not help. This is a new regression to 1.7.4. When I switched SDK 1.7.3, launching to device worked as expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5803,12,"""iOS: Button background image does not scale correctly on click""","""""""When the image used by a button is larger than the size of the button, the image will correctly scale down to fit the button when the button is in the normal state. However, when the button is in the """"""""pressed"""""""" state, the backgroundImage no longer scales correctly.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Button background image does not scale correctly on click
Description: """"When the image used by a button is larger than the size of the button, the image will correctly scale down to fit the button when the button is in the normal state. However, when the button is in the """"""""pressed"""""""" state, the backgroundImage no longer scales correctly. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5801,12,"""iOS: UI - Add support for underPageBackgroundColor""","""""""The color underPageBackgroundColor is available in iOS 5. So it should be made available:  http://developer.apple.com/library/IOS/#documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIColor_Class/Reference/Reference.html""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: UI - Add support for underPageBackgroundColor
Description: """"The color underPageBackgroundColor is available in iOS 5. So it should be made available: http://developer.apple.com/library/IOS/#documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIColor_Class/Reference/Reference.html""""",title+description
TIMOB-5800,12,"""iOS - Unable to build with 1.7.4""","""""""1.grab the 1.7.4 build from CI  2.try to build for device or sim    resultds:      File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.4.v20111019101414/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1325      if command in ['simulator', 'build']:       ^  IndentationError: expected an indented bloc""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Unable to build with 1.7.4
Description: """"1.grab the 1.7.4 build from CI 2.try to build for device or sim resultds: File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.4.v20111019101414/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1325 if command in ['simulator', 'build']: ^ IndentationError: expected an indented bloc""""",title+description
TIMOB-5798,12,"""Android: KS - Error Callback is unable to resolve host""","""""""1) Launch KitchenSink  2) Open Platform -> XHR -> Error Callback    Actual results:   UTF-8 GET  Unable to resolve host """"""""www.fre100.com"""""""": No address associated with hostname    Expected results:  UTF-8 GET  www.fre100.com    Notes:  This seems to be a Android 4.0 issue only. I tested it on the same emulator with Google API's Android 2.3.3 and a Nexus One 2.2.2 where the results showed the expected results.    I'm not sure if this is a bug, or if it is just a change in behavior in Android 4.0.  It may be working as expected, so perhaps this JIRA is just noting the new behavior.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS - Error Callback is unable to resolve host
Description: """"1) Launch KitchenSink 2) Open Platform -> XHR -> Error Callback Actual results: UTF-8 GET Unable to resolve host """"""""www.fre100.com"""""""": No address associated with hostname Expected results: UTF-8 GET www.fre100.com Notes: This seems to be a Android 4.0 issue only. I tested it on the same emulator with Google API's Android 2.3.3 and a Nexus One 2.2.2 where the results showed the expected results. I'm not sure if this is a bug, or if it is just a change in behavior in Android 4.0. It may be working as expected, so perhaps this JIRA is just noting the new behavior. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5797,12,"""Android: KS - Playing a local movie causes a runtime error""","""""""1) Launch KitchenSink  2) Open Phone -> Play Movie -> Local    Results:   Runtime error.  Location: [31,0]app://examples/movie_local.js  Message:  Wrapped java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Expected org.<USER>titanium.proxy.TiViewProxy type for argument """"""""child"""""""" in """"""""add"""""""", but got [Ti.Media.VideoPlayer] (app://examples//movie_local.js#31)    Notes:   This seems to be a Android 4.0 issue only.  I tested it on the same emulator with Google API's Android 2.3.3 and a Nexus One 2.2.2 where the video played normally.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KS - Playing a local movie causes a runtime error
Description: """"1) Launch KitchenSink 2) Open Phone -> Play Movie -> Local Results: Runtime error. Location: [31,0]app://examples/movie_local.js Message: Wrapped java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Expected org.<USER>titanium.proxy.TiViewProxy type for argument """"""""child"""""""" in """"""""add"""""""", but got [Ti.Media.VideoPlayer] (app://examples//movie_local.js#31) Notes: This seems to be a Android 4.0 issue only. I tested it on the same emulator with Google API's Android 2.3.3 and a Nexus One 2.2.2 where the video played normally.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5795,12,"""iOS: facebook dialog error""","""""""h3.Problem  Publishing to the Facebook wall using dialog does not work - shows an error.    h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Open the kitchen sink  2. Go to Mashups->Facebook->Login/Logout and do the login to Facebook  2. Go to Mashups->Facebook->Public Stream and press the """"""""Publish wall post with DIALOG"""""""" button    h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-328995""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: facebook dialog error
