TIMOB-5768,12,"""iOS: Black bar added over navBar when rotating back from full screen""","""""""If tiapp.xml is set to portrait only and you run the code below which goes to a fullscreen window then back to a non-fullscreen window, a black bar appears on top of a portion of the navBar. Screenshot: http://screencast.com/t/QhDdHvLUXtN  {code:title = tiapp.xml}  <orientations device=""""""""iphone"""""""">       <orientation>Ti.UI.PORTRAIT</orientation>  </orientations>  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Black bar added over navBar when rotating back from full screen
Description: """"If tiapp.xml is set to portrait only and you run the code below which goes to a fullscreen window then back to a non-fullscreen window, a black bar appears on top of a portion of the navBar. Screenshot: http://screencast.com/t/QhDdHvLUXtN {code:title = tiapp.xml} <orientations device=""""""""iphone""""""""> <orientation>Ti.UI.PORTRAIT</orientation> </orientations> """"",title+description
TIMOB-5766,12,"""iOS: tabbedBar doesn't consistently fire click events""","""""""h3.Problem  TabbedBar does not consistently fire click event.    h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Execute the sample code  2. Click on the TabbedBar buttons 4-5 times (after the 2nd time the event won't be fired anymore)    h3.Sample Code      h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-318632  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: tabbedBar doesn't consistently fire click events
Description: """"h3.Problem TabbedBar does not consistently fire click event. h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Execute the sample code 2. Click on the TabbedBar buttons 4-5 times (after the 2nd time the event won't be fired anymore) h3.Sample Code h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-318632 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5765,12,"""iOS: Image appears in portrait mode when application's orientation mode is set the landscape right only""","""""""1) Create a new project and put the following the app.js    2) Put the attached grouch.jpg into the Resources folder  3) Hold the device in portrait mode and launch the application    Actual results: Image initially appears in portrait mode.  The image will rotate to the correct orientation once the devices orientation is changed to landscape right. After it is in landscape right mode, it will not change to any other orientation mode.       Expected results:  Image only appears in landscape right mode.    Notes:  This only occurs on the first launch of the app.    This issue is a regression.  When tested in 1.7.2, the image appears momentarily in portrait mode before redrawing itself in landscape mode.  It does not require changing the devices orientation to draw the image in the correct position.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Image appears in portrait mode when application's orientation mode is set the landscape right only
Description: """"1) Create a new project and put the following the app.js 2) Put the attached grouch.jpg into the Resources folder 3) Hold the device in portrait mode and launch the application Actual results: Image initially appears in portrait mode. The image will rotate to the correct orientation once the devices orientation is changed to landscape right. After it is in landscape right mode, it will not change to any other orientation mode. Expected results: Image only appears in landscape right mode. Notes: This only occurs on the first launch of the app. This issue is a regression. When tested in 1.7.2, the image appears momentarily in portrait mode before redrawing itself in landscape mode. It does not require changing the devices orientation to draw the image in the correct position.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5764,12,"""Android: Splash screen stretches when orientation modes are set to landscape in app.js""","""""""1) Create a new project and add the following to the app.js    2) Put the attached grouch.jpg in the Resources folder  3) Hold device in portrait mode and launch app    Actual results: Splash screen initially appears in portrait mode and then stretches into landscape mode.  Image and status bar appear normally in landscape mode.    Expected results: Splash screen appears in portrait mode.  Image and status bar appear in landscape mode.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Splash screen stretches when orientation modes are set to landscape in app.js
Description: """"1) Create a new project and add the following to the app.js 2) Put the attached grouch.jpg in the Resources folder 3) Hold device in portrait mode and launch app Actual results: Splash screen initially appears in portrait mode and then stretches into landscape mode. Image and status bar appear normally in landscape mode. Expected results: Splash screen appears in portrait mode. Image and status bar appear in landscape mode.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5763,12,"""Android: Launching an app with portrait orientation in landscape causes image to be redrawn""","""""""1) Create a new project and put the following in app.js    2) Put the attached grouch.jpg in the Resources folder  3) Hold the device in landscape mode and launch application    Actual results: Image and status bar momentarily shows up in landscape mode before quickly being redrawn in portrait mode    Expected results: Image and status bar only appear in portrait mode    Notes:  Seems to only be reproducible on first launch of the app""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Launching an app with portrait orientation in landscape causes image to be redrawn
Description: """"1) Create a new project and put the following in app.js 2) Put the attached grouch.jpg in the Resources folder 3) Hold the device in landscape mode and launch application Actual results: Image and status bar momentarily shows up in landscape mode before quickly being redrawn in portrait mode Expected results: Image and status bar only appear in portrait mode Notes: Seems to only be reproducible on first launch of the app""""",title+description
TIMOB-5762,12,"""Closing a window in nav group doesn't destroy window nor it's contents even after nulling out""","""""""Attached is a basic example showing the issue:    Windows opened in a navgroup do not get GC'd despite attempts to null out the window after it's closed in the navgroup.  In the example I'm using a commonJS module to add to the new window, open it, etc.  Even nulling out 'exports' yields no results.    NOTE:  If you hit the auto generated back button - the window DOES get GC'd.  Only if you close it programmatically does it retain the windows.    Here is a video example - first click on the auto generated buttons, which do release - then clicking the button to programmatically close it, which never releases:  http://screencast.com/t/MtzkI4ZRhn""""""",Bug,"Title: Closing a window in nav group doesn't destroy window nor it's contents even after nulling out
Description: """"Attached is a basic example showing the issue: Windows opened in a navgroup do not get GC'd despite attempts to null out the window after it's closed in the navgroup. In the example I'm using a commonJS module to add to the new window, open it, etc. Even nulling out 'exports' yields no results. NOTE: If you hit the auto generated back button - the window DOES get GC'd. Only if you close it programmatically does it retain the windows. Here is a video example - first click on the auto generated buttons, which do release - then clicking the button to programmatically close it, which never releases: http://screencast.com/t/MtzkI4ZRhn""""",title+description
TIMOB-5761,12,"""Rotation causes redraw of white static like lines against the right edge""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Base UI > Views > Table Views > Composite (Partial Size)  2. Rotate device to landscape  3. Watch the right edge and rotate it back to portrait     Actual Result:  See that there is these white dots like static line drawn against the right edge    Expected Result:  Should not have redraw issue  """"""",Bug,"Title: Rotation causes redraw of white static like lines against the right edge
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Base UI > Views > Table Views > Composite (Partial Size) 2. Rotate device to landscape 3. Watch the right edge and rotate it back to portrait Actual Result: See that there is these white dots like static line drawn against the right edge Expected Result: Should not have redraw issue """"",title+description
TIMOB-5760,12,"""iOS5: Header bar gets stuck in the middle of the screen after a search""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Base UI > Views > Table Views > Headers  2. Type B in the search and click search    Actual Result:  The header covers half of the table view content (see attached image)    Expected Result:  Should align correctly  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS5: Header bar gets stuck in the middle of the screen after a search
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Base UI > Views > Table Views > Headers 2. Type B in the search and click search Actual Result: The header covers half of the table view content (see attached image) Expected Result: Should align correctly """"",title+description
TIMOB-5759,12,"""iOS5: Closing the open window  with nav bar visible has a weird redraw of the button drag""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Base UI > Window (Standalone)  2. Press Open (Nav Bar Visible)  3. Press Close    Actual Result:  See that the close button drags from the top to the bottom    Expected Result:  Should close with no redraw""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS5: Closing the open window with nav bar visible has a weird redraw of the button drag
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Base UI > Window (Standalone) 2. Press Open (Nav Bar Visible) 3. Press Close Actual Result: See that the close button drags from the top to the bottom Expected Result: Should close with no redraw""""",title+description
