TIMOB-5473,12,"""Android: HTML5 video gets stuck while trying to load the video (on webview)""","""""""h3.Problem  Video streaming (HTML5) does not work on webview. While trying to play the HTML5 video it gets stucked in the loading part.  While entering to the HTML5 through the Android browser we are able to play the video correctly.    h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Execute the example code  2. Press the Play button on the video (on the top of the page)    h3.Sample Code      h3.Logs - tested on devices with Android 2.2.1      h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-442427""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTML5 video gets stuck while trying to load the video (on webview)
Description: """"h3.Problem Video streaming (HTML5) does not work on webview. While trying to play the HTML5 video it gets stucked in the loading part. While entering to the HTML5 through the Android browser we are able to play the video correctly. h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Execute the example code 2. Press the Play button on the video (on the top of the page) h3.Sample Code h3.Logs - tested on devices with Android 2.2.1 h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-442427""""",title+description
TIMOB-5472,12,"""Crash when playing sound""","""""""We can force a crash - in simulator only - when trying to play a sound. The crash occurs in -[AVAudioPlayer prepareToPlay] whether explicitly or implicitly called. Reproduction steps, in KS:    Phone -> Sound -> Local with File (Crash)    This is almost certainly a simulator bug, but we should work around it if possible. This ticket is primarily for somebody to investigate outside Titanium and file a radar bug if necessary.""""""",Bug,"Title: Crash when playing sound
Description: """"We can force a crash - in simulator only - when trying to play a sound. The crash occurs in -[AVAudioPlayer prepareToPlay] whether explicitly or implicitly called. Reproduction steps, in KS: Phone -> Sound -> Local with File (Crash) This is almost certainly a simulator bug, but we should work around it if possible. This ticket is primarily for somebody to investigate outside Titanium and file a radar bug if necessary.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5471,12,"""iOS: webview.reload() bug if website has iframe(s)""","""""""h4.Problem  webview.reload() bug if website has iframe(s). If website is reloaded from Safari entire site is shown.    h5.Tested on  iOS Simulator 4.3 & iPod 4.2    h5.Repro sequence  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();    //webview toolbar buttons  var btnBack = Ti.UI.createButton({   width: 50,title:'<',   //image: '../img/icon_arrow_left.png',   enabled: false  });     //event: back   btnBack.addEventListener('click', function(){    webView.goBack();      });    var btnFwd = Ti.UI.createButton({   width: 50,title:'>',   //image: '../img/icon_arrow_right.png',   enabled: false  });     //event: forward   btnFwd.addEventListener('click', function(){    webView.goForward();      });    var btnReload = Ti.UI.createButton({   systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.REFRESH,    visible: false  });     //event: reload   btnReload.addEventListener('click', function(){    webView.reload();      });    var btnLoading = Ti.UI.createButton({   systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.SPINNER,  });    var btnSpace = Titanium.UI.createButton({   systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.FLEXIBLE_SPACE  });      //webview  var webView = Ti.UI.createWebView({   url: 'http://www.borsen.dk'  });  win.add(webView);     //event: before load   webView.addEventListener('beforeload',function(e){    webViewToolbar.items = [btnBack, btnFwd, btnSpace, btnLoading, btnSpace];   });       //event: load   webView.addEventListener('load',function(e){      webViewToolbar.items = [btnBack, btnFwd, btnSpace, btnReload, btnSpace];      //ctrl: back    if(webView.canGoBack()){     btnBack.enabled = true;    } else {                 btnBack.enabled = false;    }      //ctrl: fwd    if(webView.canGoForward()){     btnFwd.enabled = true;    } else {                 btnFwd.enabled = false;    }      });        //webview toolbar  var webViewToolbar = Ti.UI.createToolbar({   items: [btnBack, btnFwd, btnSpace, btnReload, btnLoading, btnSpace],   bottom: 0,   barColor: win.barColor  });  win.add(webViewToolbar);    win.open();  {code}    h5.Associated HD ticket  APP-555912""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: webview.reload() bug if website has iframe(s)
Description: """"h4.Problem webview.reload() bug if website has iframe(s). If website is reloaded from Safari entire site is shown. h5.Tested on iOS Simulator 4.3 & iPod 4.2 h5.Repro sequence {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); //webview toolbar buttons var btnBack = Ti.UI.createButton({ width: 50,title:'<', //image: '../img/icon_arrow_left.png', enabled: false }); //event: back btnBack.addEventListener('click', function(){ webView.goBack(); }); var btnFwd = Ti.UI.createButton({ width: 50,title:'>', //image: '../img/icon_arrow_right.png', enabled: false }); //event: forward btnFwd.addEventListener('click', function(){ webView.goForward(); }); var btnReload = Ti.UI.createButton({ systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.REFRESH, visible: false }); //event: reload btnReload.addEventListener('click', function(){ webView.reload(); }); var btnLoading = Ti.UI.createButton({ systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.SPINNER, }); var btnSpace = Titanium.UI.createButton({ systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.FLEXIBLE_SPACE }); //webview var webView = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url: 'http://www.borsen.dk' }); win.add(webView); //event: before load webView.addEventListener('beforeload',function(e){ webViewToolbar.items = [btnBack, btnFwd, btnSpace, btnLoading, btnSpace]; }); //event: load webView.addEventListener('load',function(e){ webViewToolbar.items = [btnBack, btnFwd, btnSpace, btnReload, btnSpace]; //ctrl: back if(webView.canGoBack()){ btnBack.enabled = true; } else { btnBack.enabled = false; } //ctrl: fwd if(webView.canGoForward()){ btnFwd.enabled = true; } else { btnFwd.enabled = false; } }); //webview toolbar var webViewToolbar = Ti.UI.createToolbar({ items: [btnBack, btnFwd, btnSpace, btnReload, btnLoading, btnSpace], bottom: 0, barColor: win.barColor }); win.add(webViewToolbar); win.open(); {code} h5.Associated HD ticket APP-555912""""",title+description
TIMOB-5470,12,"""iOS: regionChanged is fired 4 times on initialization ""","""""""the regionChanged event is fired 4 times when you first open a mapview.  See log output in example:  {code:title = app.js}  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow();    var mapView = Ti.Map.createView({    mapType: Ti.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,    region:{      latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993,      latitudeDelta:0.5, longitudeDelta:0.5    },    animate:true,    regionFit:true,    userLocation:true  });    var count = 1    mapView.addEventListener('regionChanged', function(e) {    var latitude = e.latitude;    var longitude = e.longitude;    var latitudeDelta = e.latitudeDelta;    var longitudeDelta = e.longitudeDelta;    Ti.API.info(count+"""""""" latitude: """""""" + latitude + """""""" longitude: """""""" + longitude + """""""" latitudeDelta: """""""" + latitudeDelta + """""""" longitudeDelta: """""""" + longitudeDelta);    count++;  });    win1.add(mapView);    win1.open();  {code}    h4. Extra info  As a collateral effect of this, adding the listener significantly changes the lat/long delta that I specified (therefore, changing the specified geolocation that centers the map).     h4. Community Discussion    http://developer.<USER>com/question/135900/regionchanged-odd-behavior""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: regionChanged is fired 4 times on initialization
Description: """"the regionChanged event is fired 4 times when you first open a mapview. See log output in example: {code:title = app.js} var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); var mapView = Ti.Map.createView({ mapType: Ti.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, region:{ latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993, latitudeDelta:0.5, longitudeDelta:0.5 }, animate:true, regionFit:true, userLocation:true }); var count = 1 mapView.addEventListener('regionChanged', function(e) { var latitude = e.latitude; var longitude = e.longitude; var latitudeDelta = e.latitudeDelta; var longitudeDelta = e.longitudeDelta; Ti.API.info(count+"""""""" latitude: """""""" + latitude + """""""" longitude: """""""" + longitude + """""""" latitudeDelta: """""""" + latitudeDelta + """""""" longitudeDelta: """""""" + longitudeDelta); count++; }); win1.add(mapView); win1.open(); {code} h4. Extra info As a collateral effect of this, adding the listener significantly changes the lat/long delta that I specified (therefore, changing the specified geolocation that centers the map). h4. Community Discussion http://developer.<USER>com/question/135900/regionchanged-odd-behavior""""",title+description
TIMOB-5469,12,"""Don't store app data in root of sd card directory""","""""""We currently store app data under the /mnt/sdcard/<appid>.  This does not get removed when the app is deleted. We may want to move it to where getExternalFilesDir() is located, since that should be removed along with the app.  We can't use getExternalFilesDir() since it's only available API level 8+.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Don't store app data in root of sd card directory
Description: """"We currently store app data under the /mnt/sdcard/<appid>. This does not get removed when the app is deleted. We may want to move it to where getExternalFilesDir() is located, since that should be removed along with the app. We can't use getExternalFilesDir() since it's only available API level 8+.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5468,12,"""iOS: backgroundLeftCap stretches on TableViewRow""","""""""h4.Problem  backgroundLeftCap stretches on TableViewRow.    The screenshot shows that backgroundLeftCap displays fine on buttons and views, but not on TableViewRows.    h5.Tested on  iOS 4.3 Simulator & iPad 2 v4.3    h4.Repro sequence  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor : 'white'  });  win.open();    var t = Ti.UI.createTableView();  win.add(t);    for(var i = 0, max = 10; i < max; i++) {   t.appendRow(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({    title : 'ajskld ' + i,    backgroundColor : 'transparent',    height : 84,    backgroundImage : 'WKButton84.png',    backgroundLeftCap : 10   }));  }    win.add(Ti.UI.createView({   width : 200,    top : 10,   height : 84,   backgroundImage : 'WKButton84.png',   backgroundLeftCap : 10  }));    win.add(Ti.UI.createButton({   height : 84,   width : 200,   bottom : 10,   backgroundImage : 'WKButton84.png',   backgroundLeftCap : 10  }));  {code}    h5.Associated HD ticket  APP-981824""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: backgroundLeftCap stretches on TableViewRow
Description: """"h4.Problem backgroundLeftCap stretches on TableViewRow. The screenshot shows that backgroundLeftCap displays fine on buttons and views, but not on TableViewRows. h5.Tested on iOS 4.3 Simulator & iPad 2 v4.3 h4.Repro sequence {code:title=app.js} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : 'white' }); win.open(); var t = Ti.UI.createTableView(); win.add(t); for(var i = 0, max = 10; i < max; i++) { t.appendRow(Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ title : 'ajskld ' + i, backgroundColor : 'transparent', height : 84, backgroundImage : 'WKButton84.png', backgroundLeftCap : 10 })); } win.add(Ti.UI.createView({ width : 200, top : 10, height : 84, backgroundImage : 'WKButton84.png', backgroundLeftCap : 10 })); win.add(Ti.UI.createButton({ height : 84, width : 200, bottom : 10, backgroundImage : 'WKButton84.png', backgroundLeftCap : 10 })); {code} h5.Associated HD ticket APP-981824""""",title+description
TIMOB-5467,12,"""iOS: Switching build targets without clean causes build to fail.""","""""""Related to:  http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-5138    Steps to repro:    1. Create simple app.  2. Build app for simulator.  3. Build app for device.  4. Build fails with error.        This happens when switching back to building for simulator after building for device as well.      Note: If you clean your project before switching build targets, everything works as expected, however you have to clean your project each time before you switching targets.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Switching build targets without clean causes build to fail.
Description: """"Related to: http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-5138 Steps to repro: 1. Create simple app. 2. Build app for simulator. 3. Build app for device. 4. Build fails with error. This happens when switching back to building for simulator after building for device as well. Note: If you clean your project before switching build targets, everything works as expected, however you have to clean your project each time before you switching targets.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5465,12,"""iOS: Tapping Tab Orphans Windows on Tab's Stack""","""""""h1. Problem  Tapping the tab's button to return to the root window of the tab orphans any windows between the current window and the root window.    h2. Why This Is A Problem  Orphaned windows equate to leaked memory.    h2. Expected Behavior  Tapping the tab's button should close every window that is open on that tab's stack, not just the current window.    h2. Reproduction  Drop the following in an app.js. Touch """"""""S1: Touch Me"""""""", then """"""""S2: Touch Me"""""""". Notice in the log which windows were opened, and which were closed.  {code:title=app.js}  var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();    function openWindowOnStack(i) {      var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({          title: 'I Am ' + i      });      win.addEventListener('open', function() {          Ti.API.info('opened ' + i + '!');          if (i < 4) {              openWindowOnStack(i + 1);          }      });      win.addEventListener('close', function() {          Ti.API.info('closed ' + i + '!');      });      tab.open(win);  }    var outer = Ti.UI.createWindow({      title: 'I Am Parent',      rightNavButton: Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'S1: Touch Me' })  });  var tab = Ti.UI.createTab({      window: outer, title: 'S2: Touch Me'  });  tabGroup.addTab(tab);    outer.rightNavButton.addEventListener('click', function() {      openWindowOnStack(0);  });    tabGroup.open();      h2. Expected Output  {code:title=Expected Output}  [INFO] opened 0!  [INFO] opened 1!  [INFO] opened 2!  [INFO] opened 3!  [INFO] opened 4!  [INFO] closed 3!  [INFO] closed 2!  [INFO] closed 1!  [INFO] closed 0!  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tapping Tab Orphans Windows on Tab's Stack
Description: """"h1. Problem Tapping the tab's button to return to the root window of the tab orphans any windows between the current window and the root window. h2. Why This Is A Problem Orphaned windows equate to leaked memory. h2. Expected Behavior Tapping the tab's button should close every window that is open on that tab's stack, not just the current window. h2. Reproduction Drop the following in an app.js. Touch """"""""S1: Touch Me"""""""", then """"""""S2: Touch Me"""""""". Notice in the log which windows were opened, and which were closed. {code:title=app.js} var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); function openWindowOnStack(i) { var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'I Am ' + i }); win.addEventListener('open', function() { Ti.API.info('opened ' + i + '!'); if (i < 4) { openWindowOnStack(i + 1); } }); win.addEventListener('close', function() { Ti.API.info('closed ' + i + '!'); }); tab.open(win); } var outer = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'I Am Parent', rightNavButton: Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'S1: Touch Me' }) }); var tab = Ti.UI.createTab({ window: outer, title: 'S2: Touch Me' }); tabGroup.addTab(tab); outer.rightNavButton.addEventListener('click', function() { openWindowOnStack(0); }); tabGroup.open(); h2. Expected Output {code:title=Expected Output} [INFO] opened 0! [INFO] opened 1! [INFO] opened 2! [INFO] opened 3! [INFO] opened 4! [INFO] closed 3! [INFO] closed 2! [INFO] closed 1! [INFO] closed 0! {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-5463,12,"""iOS 5 - push notifications while app is launched are not respecting banner settings""","""""""1. settings > General make sure your apps notification settings are for banner   2. with an ti app running in the foreground (ks) push to it via urban airship.     results: notification appears as a the blue modal one. In all other cases (app in the back ground, or app not launched but registered for push)    expected: I believe we should show only banner style when the user set to as such """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS 5 - push notifications while app is launched are not respecting banner settings
Description: """"1. settings > General make sure your apps notification settings are for banner 2. with an ti app running in the foreground (ks) push to it via urban airship. results: notification appears as a the blue modal one. In all other cases (app in the back ground, or app not launched but registered for push) expected: I believe we should show only banner style when the user set to as such """"",title+description
TIMOB-5462,12,"""Hash in url when using openURL gets escaped - 1.7.2 / 1.8.x""","""""""h4.Problem  Titanium.Platform.openURL method causes the url to break if URL is escaped with special characters.    e.g. http://mobile.twitter.com/?status=the free mom&#39;s Helper app from Fisher-Price    That will show: the free mom    h4.Repro sequence  //If URL has an apostrophe shows like &# 39 ;   Titanium.Platform.openURL(""""""""http://mobile.twitter.com/?status=the free mom's Helper app from Fisher-Price"""""""");    h4.Tested on  iOS Simulator & iPad 2 v4.3.3    h4.Associated HD ticket  APP-619486  """"""",Bug,"Title: Hash in url when using openURL gets escaped - 1.7.2 / 1.8.x
Description: """"h4.Problem Titanium.Platform.openURL method causes the url to break if URL is escaped with special characters. e.g. http://mobile.twitter.com/?status=the free mom&#39;s Helper app from Fisher-Price That will show: the free mom h4.Repro sequence //If URL has an apostrophe shows like &# 39 ; Titanium.Platform.openURL(""""""""http://mobile.twitter.com/?status=the free mom's Helper app from Fisher-Price""""""""); h4.Tested on iOS Simulator & iPad 2 v4.3.3 h4.Associated HD ticket APP-619486 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5461,12,"""Android: View with border radius crashes Honeycomb when hardware acceleration on""","""""""Honeycomb introduced hardware acceleration which can be turned on with a setting in the <application> node of AndroidManifest.xml.  When it's turned on, and a view has a borderRadius set (> 0), the app crashes because we use clipPath, which is not supported with hw accel. (cf http://android-developers.blogspot.com/2011/03/android-30-hardware-acceleration.html).    Re-creation steps:    * Create an app.  * Make the tiapp.xml's <android> section so:    {code:title=tiapp.xml}   <android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"""""""">    <tool-api-level>11</tool-api-level>    <manifest>     <application android:hardwareAccelerated=""""""""true""""""""/>    </manifest>   </android>      * Run the app on the honeycomb device and it will crash.  (When testing the fix, it should not crash of course.).    Typical crash logcat entry looks like:        """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: View with border radius crashes Honeycomb when hardware acceleration on
Description: """"Honeycomb introduced hardware acceleration which can be turned on with a setting in the <application> node of AndroidManifest.xml. When it's turned on, and a view has a borderRadius set (> 0), the app crashes because we use clipPath, which is not supported with hw accel. (cf http://android-developers.blogspot.com/2011/03/android-30-hardware-acceleration.html). Re-creation steps: * Create an app. * Make the tiapp.xml's <android> section so: {code:title=tiapp.xml} <android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""> <tool-api-level>11</tool-api-level> <manifest> <application android:hardwareAccelerated=""""""""true""""""""/> </manifest> </android> * Run the app on the honeycomb device and it will crash. (When testing the fix, it should not crash of course.). Typical crash logcat entry looks like: """"",title+description
TIMOB-5460,12,"""Android: Support Animation of backgroundColor""","""""""add ability to animate backgroundColor. Note the view MUST have a backgroundColor and no backgroundImages for this to work.    {code:title=app.js}    Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('black');    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'black'  });    var fromColor = '#2d6e32';  var toColor = '#35883b';    var v = Ti.UI.createView({   width: '100dp',   height: '100dp',   backgroundColor: fromColor  });    var b = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: 'Animate',   bottom: '10dp',   left: '10dp'  });    b.addEventListener('click', function() {   v.animate({    backgroundColor: toColor,    duration: 500   });  });    var b1 = Ti.UI.createButton({   title: 'Reset',   bottom: '10dp',   right: '10dp'   });    b1.addEventListener('click', function() {   v.backgroundColor = toColor;   v.backgroundColor = fromColor;  });    var v1 = Ti.UI.createView({   width : '50dp',   height: '50dp',   backgroundColor: 'white'  });    win.add(v);  win.add(b);  win.add(b1);  win.add(v1);    win.open();  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support Animation of backgroundColor
Description: """"add ability to animate backgroundColor. Note the view MUST have a backgroundColor and no backgroundImages for this to work. {code:title=app.js} Ti.UI.setBackgroundColor('black'); var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'black' }); var fromColor = '#2d6e32'; var toColor = '#35883b'; var v = Ti.UI.createView({ width: '100dp', height: '100dp', backgroundColor: fromColor }); var b = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Animate', bottom: '10dp', left: '10dp' }); b.addEventListener('click', function() { v.animate({ backgroundColor: toColor, duration: 500 }); }); var b1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Reset', bottom: '10dp', right: '10dp' }); b1.addEventListener('click', function() { v.backgroundColor = toColor; v.backgroundColor = fromColor; }); var v1 = Ti.UI.createView({ width : '50dp', height: '50dp', backgroundColor: 'white' }); win.add(v); win.add(b); win.add(b1); win.add(v1); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-5459,12,"""iOS: Animation applied to a view is not properly transitioning when addEventListener is applied""","""""""1) Add the following code to a new projects app.js    2) Run the application    Expected result:  The view will animate from red to black to orange.  Actual results:  The view animates from red to black.  It never transitions to orange.    Notes:  The code sample is from the following doc: http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.Animation-object    Here is another example which is perhaps easier to see:      Here the view should go from white to red to black, but only goes from white to red.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Animation applied to a view is not properly transitioning when addEventListener is applied
Description: """"1) Add the following code to a new projects app.js 2) Run the application Expected result: The view will animate from red to black to orange. Actual results: The view animates from red to black. It never transitions to orange. Notes: The code sample is from the following doc: http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.Animation-object Here is another example which is perhaps easier to see: Here the view should go from white to red to black, but only goes from white to red.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5458,12,"""Kitchensink: Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout, Login screen does not rotate with soft KB up""","""""""Description:  While testing KS, Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout, I started filling out the login account name and then rotated the device with the keyboard up. All the UI with the exception of the login window rotated with the device.    See image for details.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout  3) Set force Dialog to """"""""true""""""""  4) Click """"""""login""""""""  5) Focus on one of the text fields to get the Soft KB  6) Rotate the device    Result:  The UI rotates, but the login window does not.    Expected:  The login window should rotate with the rest of the UI.""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout, Login screen does not rotate with soft KB up
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout, I started filling out the login account name and then rotated the device with the keyboard up. All the UI with the exception of the login window rotated with the device. See image for details. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout 3) Set force Dialog to """"""""true"""""""" 4) Click """"""""login"""""""" 5) Focus on one of the text fields to get the Soft KB 6) Rotate the device Result: The UI rotates, but the login window does not. Expected: The login window should rotate with the rest of the UI.""""",title+description
