TIMOB-5448,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Modal Windows, Navbar and status bar can get out of sync with UI""","""""""Description:  While testing KS, Base UI>Modal Windows, I was able to get the UI out of sync with the device. This initially resulted in a smaller """"""""landscape-style"""""""" navbar, but an additional device rotation had the status bar rotate alone.    See images for details.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Base UI>Modal Windows  3) set picker to """"""""Flip horizontal""""""""  4) Click """"""""show modal""""""""  5) Rotate to landscape  6) Close the modal window  7) Rotate again    Result:  On modal close, the navbar will be small with some whitespace below. When rotated as in step 7, the status bar will rotate, but the rest of the UI will not.    Expected:  UI remains in sync with device    Note:  Did not occur with iOS 4.3.x or 1.7.2 SDK  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Modal Windows, Navbar and status bar can get out of sync with UI
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Modal Windows, I was able to get the UI out of sync with the device. This initially resulted in a smaller """"""""landscape-style"""""""" navbar, but an additional device rotation had the status bar rotate alone. See images for details. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Base UI>Modal Windows 3) set picker to """"""""Flip horizontal"""""""" 4) Click """"""""show modal"""""""" 5) Rotate to landscape 6) Close the modal window 7) Rotate again Result: On modal close, the navbar will be small with some whitespace below. When rotated as in step 7, the status bar will rotate, but the rest of the UI will not. Expected: UI remains in sync with device Note: Did not occur with iOS 4.3.x or 1.7.2 SDK """"",title+description
TIMOB-5447,12,"""iPad 2, iOS5 - no notifications apear when backgrounding KS""","""""""1. install KS onto an ipad 2 running ios5 gm seed (no other ti apps were installed on the device)  2. Launch the application  3. hit the home button    results: nothing occurs consle shows:  Oct  5 13:23:45 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x774c][160] <Notice>: [DEBUG] fire app event: pause  Oct  5 13:23:45 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x774c][160] <Notice>: [INFO] app was paused from the foreground    expected: notifications to appear    fwiw, the same app running on ipad2 4.3 works as expected. Believe this worked as expected on B5""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad 2, iOS5 - no notifications apear when backgrounding KS
Description: """"1. install KS onto an ipad 2 running ios5 gm seed (no other ti apps were installed on the device) 2. Launch the application 3. hit the home button results: nothing occurs consle shows: Oct 5 13:23:45 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x774c][160] <Notice>: [DEBUG] fire app event: pause Oct 5 13:23:45 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x774c][160] <Notice>: [INFO] app was paused from the foreground expected: notifications to appear fwiw, the same app running on ipad2 4.3 works as expected. Believe this worked as expected on B5""""",title+description
TIMOB-5446,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Window NavBar, button with image animates well in advance of navbar size change""","""""""Description:   While testing Base UI>Window NavBar, I clicked """"""""Button with image"""""""" and then """"""""title prompt"""""""". This is not the order I usually followed. When I clicked """"""""title prompt"""""""", the navbar gets larger. At that point I noticed that the button with image moved well in advance of the navbar size change.     Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS on device  2) Navigate to Base UI>Window NavBar  3) Click """"""""button with image""""""""  4) Click """"""""title prompt""""""""    Result:  The button with image moves well ahead of the navbar size change    Expected result:  The button with image moves at the same time as the navbar size increases.""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Window NavBar, button with image animates well in advance of navbar size change
Description: """"Description: While testing Base UI>Window NavBar, I clicked """"""""Button with image"""""""" and then """"""""title prompt"""""""". This is not the order I usually followed. When I clicked """"""""title prompt"""""""", the navbar gets larger. At that point I noticed that the button with image moved well in advance of the navbar size change. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on device 2) Navigate to Base UI>Window NavBar 3) Click """"""""button with image"""""""" 4) Click """"""""title prompt"""""""" Result: The button with image moves well ahead of the navbar size change Expected result: The button with image moves at the same time as the navbar size increases.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5445,12,"""iOS: Kitchensink Base UI>Views>Map View, console reports """"client does not have appropriate entitlement to change prompt behaviour""""""","""""""Description:  While testing Kitchensink, Base UI>Views>Map View, I noticed the following in the console:  Oct  4 17:18:24 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>pushtest[0xb549][234] <Notice>: [DEBUG] loading: /var/mobile/Applications/A560C4C3-450C-4F4B-9DDE-16B14FF0A38F/KitchenSink.app/examples/map_view.js, resource: examples/map_view_js  Oct  4 17:18:25 unknown com.apple.locationd[28] <Notice>: Client com.<USER>pushtest does not have appropriate entitlement to change prompt behaviour    I did not see this in the same KS on iOS 4.3.x  I did not see this in the same KS but built with 1.7.2    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install and launch KS  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Map View  3) Check console output    Result:  Console notice logged    Expected:  No unexpected console output""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchensink Base UI>Views>Map View, console reports """"client does not have appropriate entitlement to change prompt behaviour""""
Description: """"Description: While testing Kitchensink, Base UI>Views>Map View, I noticed the following in the console: Oct 4 17:18:24 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>pushtest[0xb549][234] <Notice>: [DEBUG] loading: /var/mobile/Applications/A560C4C3-450C-4F4B-9DDE-16B14FF0A38F/KitchenSink.app/examples/map_view.js, resource: examples/map_view_js Oct 4 17:18:25 unknown com.apple.locationd[28] <Notice>: Client com.<USER>pushtest does not have appropriate entitlement to change prompt behaviour I did not see this in the same KS on iOS 4.3.x I did not see this in the same KS but built with 1.7.2 Steps to reproduce: 1) Install and launch KS 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Map View 3) Check console output Result: Console notice logged Expected: No unexpected console output""""",title+description
TIMOB-5444,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls, after navigating around, clicking """"back"""" then """"reload"""" loads the wrong page""","""""""Description:  While testing Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls, I clicked on the images link then clicked """"""""back"""""""" and then """"""""reload"""""""". Instead of reloading the main google page, the images page was opened and reloaded. This does not occur with iOS 4.3.x    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install and launch KS on iOS5 device  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls  3) Click a link  4) Click the """"""""back"""""""" button to return to Google homepage  5) Click the """"""""reload"""""""" button    Result:  The link you clicked in step 3 will open and reload.    Expected:  The main google page reloads.    Note:  This seems independent of SDK. A device with iOS 5 but with SDK 1.7.2 also exhibits the behavior.""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls, after navigating around, clicking """"back"""" then """"reload"""" loads the wrong page
Description: """"Description: While testing Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls, I clicked on the images link then clicked """"""""back"""""""" and then """"""""reload"""""""". Instead of reloading the main google page, the images page was opened and reloaded. This does not occur with iOS 4.3.x Steps to reproduce: 1) Install and launch KS on iOS5 device 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls 3) Click a link 4) Click the """"""""back"""""""" button to return to Google homepage 5) Click the """"""""reload"""""""" button Result: The link you clicked in step 3 will open and reload. Expected: The main google page reloads. Note: This seems independent of SDK. A device with iOS 5 but with SDK 1.7.2 also exhibits the behavior.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5443,12,"""iOS: EmailDialog not sending attachments""","""""""h3.Problem  While sending the image files as a attachment using EmailDialog the receive image is empty.     h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Execute the project that was attached  2. Install the application to some iOS device  3. Send an email to you  4. Check your inbox - the image received is empty    h3.Sample Code      h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-353882""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: EmailDialog not sending attachments
Description: """"h3.Problem While sending the image files as a attachment using EmailDialog the receive image is empty. h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Execute the project that was attached 2. Install the application to some iOS device 3. Send an email to you 4. Check your inbox - the image received is empty h3.Sample Code h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-353882""""",title+description
TIMOB-5441,12,"""iOS: Adding TableViewRow doesn't update index for SearchBar""","""""""The customer is trying to have a TableView-attached SearchBar perform remote (API) searches. This mostly works... you can retrieve the data, and append the new rows to the table, but """"""""No Results"""""""" still shows up. Closing the search via """"""""Cancel"""""""" will slide the """"""""No Results"""""""" down, revealing the remote data that was added to the TableView.    It seems like, perhaps, the filter attribute index on the search is not being updated. Example code:        REPRO STEPS:  - Open the app  - Notice """"""""Local Data""""""""  - Search for """"""""Remote""""""""  - Notice """"""""No Results"""""""", should say """"""""Remote Data""""""""  - Cancel search  - Notice """"""""Remote Data""""""""""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Adding TableViewRow doesn't update index for SearchBar
Description: """"The customer is trying to have a TableView-attached SearchBar perform remote (API) searches. This mostly works... you can retrieve the data, and append the new rows to the table, but """"""""No Results"""""""" still shows up. Closing the search via """"""""Cancel"""""""" will slide the """"""""No Results"""""""" down, revealing the remote data that was added to the TableView. It seems like, perhaps, the filter attribute index on the search is not being updated. Example code: REPRO STEPS: - Open the app - Notice """"""""Local Data"""""""" - Search for """"""""Remote"""""""" - Notice """"""""No Results"""""""", should say """"""""Remote Data"""""""" - Cancel search - Notice """"""""Remote Data""""""""""""",title+description
TIMOB-5440,12,"""iOS: Kitchensink - Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View, rotating the device results in visible view changing to another""","""""""Description:  While testing Kitchensink on an iPhone 4 with iOS 5 and SDK 1.7.3.v20110928143011, I launched Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View. I added a view and then swiped to show the view on the far right. When I rotated the device, the view changed from view 5 to view 3. When I returned the device to portrait once again, the view went from view 3 to view 4. This also occurred with 1.7.2 SDK and iOS 4.3.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install and launch KS  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View  3) Swipe or navigate to the right-most view  4) Rotate to landscape  5) Rotate to portrait    Results:  The view changes on rotation    Expected:  No view change on rotation""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Kitchensink - Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View, rotating the device results in visible view changing to another
Description: """"Description: While testing Kitchensink on an iPhone 4 with iOS 5 and SDK 1.7.3.v20110928143011, I launched Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View. I added a view and then swiped to show the view on the far right. When I rotated the device, the view changed from view 5 to view 3. When I returned the device to portrait once again, the view went from view 3 to view 4. This also occurred with 1.7.2 SDK and iOS 4.3. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install and launch KS 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View 3) Swipe or navigate to the right-most view 4) Rotate to landscape 5) Rotate to portrait Results: The view changes on rotation Expected: No view change on rotation""""",title+description
TIMOB-5439,12,"""iOS: Expose the setContentOffset:animated: method to false""","""""""h3.Problem:    Customer is using scrollView and need to scroll to a specific point WITHOUT the smooth scrolling (no animation).    In the native iPhone SDK there is more arguments to setContentOffset, ie: [scrollView setContentOffset: bottomOffset animated: YES];    Where """"""""animated: NO"""""""" means no animation to the scrolling.      h3. Expected behavior.  Customer wants to scroll to specific point without the smooth scrolling.    h3. Additional information:  Section:Scrolling to a Specific Offset  http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/WindowsViews/Conceptual/UIScrollView_pg/ScrollingViewContent/ScrollingViewContent.html    https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIScrollView.m#L172    h3. Associated HD Ticket:  APP-212915""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Expose the setContentOffset:animated: method to false
Description: """"h3.Problem: Customer is using scrollView and need to scroll to a specific point WITHOUT the smooth scrolling (no animation). In the native iPhone SDK there is more arguments to setContentOffset, ie: [scrollView setContentOffset: bottomOffset animated: YES]; Where """"""""animated: NO"""""""" means no animation to the scrolling. h3. Expected behavior. Customer wants to scroll to specific point without the smooth scrolling. h3. Additional information: Section:Scrolling to a Specific Offset http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/WindowsViews/Conceptual/UIScrollView_pg/ScrollingViewContent/ScrollingViewContent.html https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUIScrollView.m#L172 h3. Associated HD Ticket: APP-212915""""",title+description
TIMOB-5437,12,"""iOS: Expose applicationState property of UIApplication Class""","""""""h4.Feature  Expose the applicationState property through Titanium API so we can know the application was frontmost when it received a notification.    http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIApplication_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/occ/instm/UIApplication/applicationState    h5.Customer notes  The applicationState property is not exposed in titanium, thus, there is no way take proper action in response to a remote notification.    Specifically, if the app is in the background and receives a push notification, the notification popup displays, and when the app is launched from the popup, the messageCallback is invoked. There is no way to determine from within this callback whether the system had already displayed the popup to the user.    h5.Associated HD ticket  APP-185982""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Expose applicationState property of UIApplication Class
Description: """"h4.Feature Expose the applicationState property through Titanium API so we can know the application was frontmost when it received a notification. http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/UIKit/Reference/UIApplication_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/occ/instm/UIApplication/applicationState h5.Customer notes The applicationState property is not exposed in titanium, thus, there is no way take proper action in response to a remote notification. Specifically, if the app is in the background and receives a push notification, the notification popup displays, and when the app is launched from the popup, the messageCallback is invoked. There is no way to determine from within this callback whether the system had already displayed the popup to the user. h5.Associated HD ticket APP-185982""""",title+description
TIMOB-5435,12,"""HTTPClient: add properties username, password and domain""","""""""Developers would like an easier way to set username, domain and password for a HTTP request in Titanium.  If those three properties could be added to Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient it would make authentication much easier for app development.""""""",New Feature,"Title: HTTPClient: add properties username, password and domain
Description: """"Developers would like an easier way to set username, domain and password for a HTTP request in Titanium. If those three properties could be added to Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient it would make authentication much easier for app development.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5434,12,"""Android: require() in a non-root context breaks any include() statements below it.""","""""""If an app has a second (or third, or fourth...) Javascript execution context (via a window being opened with a {{url}} property), a {{require()}} statement anywhere in that context will break any {{include()}} statements below it.    Reproduction of the failcase (and test of the fix):    In a new app use this app.js:    {code:title=app.js}  Ti.UI.createWindow({   url: """"""""win.js"""""""", // causes new JS context   backgroundColor: """"""""#000"""""""",   exitOnClose: true  }).open();      And this module.js:    {code:title=module.js}  exports.x = function() {}; //not important      When you run that, you'll get an error in the failcase, saying that {{includedWord}} is not defined.    When testing the fix, you should see an alert dialog telling you """"""""The included word is test"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: require() in a non-root context breaks any include() statements below it.
Description: """"If an app has a second (or third, or fourth...) Javascript execution context (via a window being opened with a {{url}} property), a {{require()}} statement anywhere in that context will break any {{include()}} statements below it. Reproduction of the failcase (and test of the fix): In a new app use this app.js: {code:title=app.js} Ti.UI.createWindow({ url: """"""""win.js"""""""", // causes new JS context backgroundColor: """"""""#000"""""""", exitOnClose: true }).open(); And this module.js: {code:title=module.js} exports.x = function() {}; //not important When you run that, you'll get an error in the failcase, saying that {{includedWord}} is not defined. When testing the fix, you should see an alert dialog telling you """"""""The included word is test"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-5433,12,"""iOS 5: When application is background the first time, relaunching it displays a black screen before displaying the content of the application""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Launch KS  2. Wait for it to background  3. When you get the alert that the application has background, swipe arrow that shows slide to relau... (must do it when it shows that, once it changes to slide to unlock you will not see the problem)    Actual Result:  Displays a black screen before displaying the content    Expected Result:  Should display the content immediately like all other subsequent launches""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 5: When application is background the first time, relaunching it displays a black screen before displaying the content of the application
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Launch KS 2. Wait for it to background 3. When you get the alert that the application has background, swipe arrow that shows slide to relau... (must do it when it shows that, once it changes to slide to unlock you will not see the problem) Actual Result: Displays a black screen before displaying the content Expected Result: Should display the content immediately like all other subsequent launches""""",title+description
TIMOB-5432,12,"""iOS: Warning messages thrown when eventlistener is called on battery state change""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch KS > Platform > Platform Data  2. Go back out and relaunch the test again  3. Get the Alert about the battery notification.  4. View Console logs    Actual Result:  Sometime you will get a double alert, so dismiss it and you will see it again.  Console Message:  Oct  4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: [WARN] Exception in event callback. {  Oct  4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>:     line = 2;  Oct  4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>:     message = """"""""*** -[__NSArrayM objectAtIndex:]: index 1 beyond bounds [0 .. 0]"""""""";  Oct  4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>:     sourceId = 210698176;  Oct  4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>:     sourceURL = """"""""file://localhost/var/mobile/Applications/EF78A16D-3D30-4349-A893-19A9DDC848DB/KitchenSink.app/examples/platform.js"""""""";  Oct  4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: }     Expected Result:  To display the alert message only once and not throw any warning message    Note:  Also occurred with 1.7.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Warning messages thrown when eventlistener is called on battery state change
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch KS > Platform > Platform Data 2. Go back out and relaunch the test again 3. Get the Alert about the battery notification. 4. View Console logs Actual Result: Sometime you will get a double alert, so dismiss it and you will see it again. Console Message: Oct 4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: [WARN] Exception in event callback. { Oct 4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: line = 2; Oct 4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: message = """"""""*** -[__NSArrayM objectAtIndex:]: index 1 beyond bounds [0 .. 0]""""""""; Oct 4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: sourceId = 210698176; Oct 4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: sourceURL = """"""""file://localhost/var/mobile/Applications/EF78A16D-3D30-4349-A893-19A9DDC848DB/KitchenSink.app/examples/platform.js""""""""; Oct 4 17:27:26 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x97f8][443] <Notice>: } Expected Result: To display the alert message only once and not throw any warning message Note: Also occurred with 1.7.2""""",title+description
