TIMOB-5393,12,"""Tooling: Win 7 or XP space in path to SD card causes Android emulator r13 fail to launch from Studio ""","""""""h4. Description:   Since Google released r13 tooling which includes a fix for the """"""""space in the path"""""""" issue introduced with r12, we updated our XP and Win 7 test systems to the new SDK. Attempting to launch the emulator with studio fails with the following console output:    {code:lang=none}  [DEBUG] SDCard: C:\Users\<USER>Tester\.titanium\android2.sdcard  [DEBUG] AVD ID: 21  [DEBUG] AVD Skin: WVGA800  [DEBUG] SDK: C:\android-sdk  [DEBUG] C:\android-sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe start-server  [INFO] Creating 64M SD card for use in Android emulator  [DEBUG] C:\android-sdk\tools\mksdcard.exe 64M """"""""C:\Users\<USER>Tester\.titanium\titanium_21_WVGA800.sdcard""""""""  [INFO] Creating new Android Virtual Device (21 WVGA800)  [DEBUG] C:\android-sdk\tools\emulator.exe -avd titanium_21_WVGA800 -port 5560 -sdcard C:\Users\<USER>Tester\.titanium\titanium_21_WVGA800.sdcard -logcat *:d,* -no-boot-anim -partition-size 128  invalid command-line parameter: Tester\.titanium\titanium_21_WVGA800.sdcard.  Hint: use '@foo' to launch a virtual device named 'foo'.  please use -help for more information  [DEBUG] signal caught: 3  [DEBUG] calling emulator kill on 2544  ERROR: The <USER>""""""""2544"""""""" not found.  {code}    As you can see, the text after the space is treated as an invalid parameter. We were hoping the change to the Android SDK would resolve this problem, but it doesn't seem to have made a difference.    h4. Steps to reproduce:  # Install Android SDK r13 on Windows 7 or XP  # Ensure your user account has a space in the Name on Win 7  #* If on XP, the path should include """"""""Documents and Settings"""""""" regardless of user account  # Create a new project in Titanium Studio  # Attempt to run the project in the emulator    h4. Result:  Emulator fails to launch    h4. Expected:  Emulator launches """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: Win 7 or XP space in path to SD card causes Android emulator r13 fail to launch from Studio
Description: """"h4. Description: Since Google released r13 tooling which includes a fix for the """"""""space in the path"""""""" issue introduced with r12, we updated our XP and Win 7 test systems to the new SDK. Attempting to launch the emulator with studio fails with the following console output: {code:lang=none} [DEBUG] SDCard: C:\Users\<USER>Tester\.titanium\android2.sdcard [DEBUG] AVD ID: 21 [DEBUG] AVD Skin: WVGA800 [DEBUG] SDK: C:\android-sdk [DEBUG] C:\android-sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe start-server [INFO] Creating 64M SD card for use in Android emulator [DEBUG] C:\android-sdk\tools\mksdcard.exe 64M """"""""C:\Users\<USER>Tester\.titanium\titanium_21_WVGA800.sdcard"""""""" [INFO] Creating new Android Virtual Device (21 WVGA800) [DEBUG] C:\android-sdk\tools\emulator.exe -avd titanium_21_WVGA800 -port 5560 -sdcard C:\Users\<USER>Tester\.titanium\titanium_21_WVGA800.sdcard -logcat *:d,* -no-boot-anim -partition-size 128 invalid command-line parameter: Tester\.titanium\titanium_21_WVGA800.sdcard. Hint: use '@foo' to launch a virtual device named 'foo'. please use -help for more information [DEBUG] signal caught: 3 [DEBUG] calling emulator kill on 2544 ERROR: The <USER>""""""""2544"""""""" not found. {code} As you can see, the text after the space is treated as an invalid parameter. We were hoping the change to the Android SDK would resolve this problem, but it doesn't seem to have made a difference. h4. Steps to reproduce: # Install Android SDK r13 on Windows 7 or XP # Ensure your user account has a space in the Name on Win 7 #* If on XP, the path should include """"""""Documents and Settings"""""""" regardless of user account # Create a new project in Titanium Studio # Attempt to run the project in the emulator h4. Result: Emulator fails to launch h4. Expected: Emulator launches """"",title+description
TIMOB-5392,12,"""Android - G2 Only: crash when exiting clipboard test case""","""""""1.build and install KS using master 1.8.0  2.Platform > Clipboard  3.enter text into top field  4. Tap copy  5.Taop into the bottom text field and tap copy  6.hit back button 2X, once to dimiss keyboard,once to go back to test list    results:the test list loads, and some strange redraw happens before the app crashes.    Pastie:http://pastie.org/2613024""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - G2 Only: crash when exiting clipboard test case
Description: """"1.build and install KS using master 1.8.0 2.Platform > Clipboard 3.enter text into top field 4. Tap copy 5.Taop into the bottom text field and tap copy 6.hit back button 2X, once to dimiss keyboard,once to go back to test list results:the test list loads, and some strange redraw happens before the app crashes. Pastie:http://pastie.org/2613024""""",title+description
TIMOB-5391,12,"""Android: Image Bitmap Loaded Multiple Times in ImageView""","""""""While evaluating bitmap allocation, we discovered that bitmaps are fetched and scaled-down twice for each ImageView, which should not be necessary. We are working to fix that in core code.    Reproduce in 1.7.2:    * Create a new app with this app.js:    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Test',      backgroundColor:'#000',   exitOnClose: true  });    win.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({   image: """"""""KS_nav_ui.png""""""""  }));    win.open();  {code}    * Launch the app from Ti Studio *to an emulator*.    * In Ti Studio, down at the console view, turn off the two """"""""Show console when..."""""""" options.    * Switch to the FastDev Process console.    * When the app loads, you'll notice in the FastDev Process console that KS_nav_ui.png is fetched three times.  *It should only be fetched twice* -- once for getting bitmap size in order to calculate a sample size, and once to load the whole thing.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image Bitmap Loaded Multiple Times in ImageView
Description: """"While evaluating bitmap allocation, we discovered that bitmaps are fetched and scaled-down twice for each ImageView, which should not be necessary. We are working to fix that in core code. Reproduce in 1.7.2: * Create a new app with this app.js: {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#000', exitOnClose: true }); win.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: """"""""KS_nav_ui.png"""""""" })); win.open(); {code} * Launch the app from Ti Studio *to an emulator*. * In Ti Studio, down at the console view, turn off the two """"""""Show console when..."""""""" options. * Switch to the FastDev Process console. * When the app loads, you'll notice in the FastDev Process console that KS_nav_ui.png is fetched three times. *It should only be fetched twice* -- once for getting bitmap size in order to calculate a sample size, and once to load the whole thing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5389,12,"""Android: Support animation of background color""","""""""As of 1.7.x we do not support animating the background color of a view as is currently supported on iOS.  It would be good to add in this functionality on the Android side as well.    From a community member, found one potential point to start researching:  http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2614545/animate-change-of-view-background-color-in-android""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support animation of background color
Description: """"As of 1.7.x we do not support animating the background color of a view as is currently supported on iOS. It would be good to add in this functionality on the Android side as well. From a community member, found one potential point to start researching: http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2614545/animate-change-of-view-background-color-in-android""""",title+description
TIMOB-5388,12,"""Android: Filenames beginning with _ are not supported by Android""","""""""Android resource compiler does not allow files to begin with '_' (underscore) if such files are detected. Error out of build with a log entry stating that fact.    Testing  1) Add an javascript file. (e.g. _myfile.js) to an existing project  2) deploy to emulator or device.  3) unzip app-unsigned.apk and notice the file does not get included    When fixed, build should have log entries and fail.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Filenames beginning with _ are not supported by Android
Description: """"Android resource compiler does not allow files to begin with '_' (underscore) if such files are detected. Error out of build with a log entry stating that fact. Testing 1) Add an javascript file. (e.g. _myfile.js) to an existing project 2) deploy to emulator or device. 3) unzip app-unsigned.apk and notice the file does not get included When fixed, build should have log entries and fail.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5387,12,"""Tabgroups don't work with fastdev""","""""""Using tabgroups with fastdev causes the app to stay in the splash screen.        This is most likely caused by a deadlock.  You may need to run the app several times to reproduce.    I have attached the log from the emulator when this happens.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Tabgroups don't work with fastdev
Description: """"Using tabgroups with fastdev causes the app to stay in the splash screen. This is most likely caused by a deadlock. You may need to run the app several times to reproduce. I have attached the log from the emulator when this happens. """"",title+description
