Description: """"We have a js.jar and a js-debug.jar, identical files. Our build scripts still rely on there being two, but let's fix that.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5384,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Tab Groups> Close/animate Tab group fails to close, white screen appears on iPad""","""""""Description:  When using KS 1.7.2 (synced from 1_7_X branch) and built with 1.7.2 SDK on an iPad 2 running iOS 5.0, launching the test and clicking the button """"""""Close/Animate Tab Group"""""""" results in a white screen with only a status bar. Running the same app on an iPhone running iOS 5.0 results in the tab group closing as expected.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Sync to 1_7_X branch  2) Import KS into Studio  3) Target iOS 4.3 or iOS 5.0 and SDK 1.7.2 GA  4) Install on iPad  5) Navigate to Base UI>Tab Groups and click """"""""Close/Animate Tab Group""""""""    Result:  Screen fades to white screen with only status bar    Expected:  Tab group close and returns to base UI tab    Notes:  Occurred on 1.8.0 KS and 1.7.2 KS  Occurred on 1.7.2 SDK and 1.8.0 SDK  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Tab Groups> Close/animate Tab group fails to close, white screen appears on iPad
Description: """"Description: When using KS 1.7.2 (synced from 1_7_X branch) and built with 1.7.2 SDK on an iPad 2 running iOS 5.0, launching the test and clicking the button """"""""Close/Animate Tab Group"""""""" results in a white screen with only a status bar. Running the same app on an iPhone running iOS 5.0 results in the tab group closing as expected. Steps to reproduce: 1) Sync to 1_7_X branch 2) Import KS into Studio 3) Target iOS 4.3 or iOS 5.0 and SDK 1.7.2 GA 4) Install on iPad 5) Navigate to Base UI>Tab Groups and click """"""""Close/Animate Tab Group"""""""" Result: Screen fades to white screen with only status bar Expected: Tab group close and returns to base UI tab Notes: Occurred on 1.8.0 KS and 1.7.2 KS Occurred on 1.7.2 SDK and 1.8.0 SDK """"",title+description
TIMOB-5383,12,"""Android: Window children property is never null unlike iOS""","""""""Overview:    The children property of a Ti.UI.window is never null on Android where iOS it can be.    Explanation:  `var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();`    On iOS `win.children` will be 'null'.  On Android, it will not be null.  An Android developer can check: `win.children[0]' to see if it's null.  However this will throw an error in iOS since it's really null and not an array.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window children property is never null unlike iOS
Description: """"Overview: The children property of a Ti.UI.window is never null on Android where iOS it can be. Explanation: `var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();` On iOS `win.children` will be 'null'. On Android, it will not be null. An Android developer can check: `win.children[0]' to see if it's null. However this will throw an error in iOS since it's really null and not an array.""""",title+description
