TIMOB-5312,12,"""Android: Write remote images to disk fails""","""""""When download an image gallery and save it to the phones filesystem, problems occur.   It works great with 30-50 images at the time. But a large amount of images resolves in some of the images are not saved to disk. The skipped images are random each time I test this. Sometimes it is only a few that are left out, other times its 20 images out of 150.    Its the same behaviour on iOS and Android.     Here is my json loader of the remote images:       The below is my save to disk function. It works great when the app is handling 50 images at the time, but once its higher, some of the images are not stored, even though this below function is called.           json feed: http://cph.napp.dk/index.php?option=com_phocagallery&view=napp&format=json    There are no errors or exceptions I can paste in, due to the fact that Titanium does not make """"""""errors"""""""" it just skips a lot of files.   Yes, it has nothing to do with the server. I have tried without the """"""""write remote to disk functionality"""""""" and the gallery works great.  Q&A Thread at [save 100+ remote images to disk|http://developer.<USER>com/question/123769/save-100-remote-images-to-disk]""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Write remote images to disk fails
Description: """"When download an image gallery and save it to the phones filesystem, problems occur. It works great with 30-50 images at the time. But a large amount of images resolves in some of the images are not saved to disk. The skipped images are random each time I test this. Sometimes it is only a few that are left out, other times its 20 images out of 150. Its the same behaviour on iOS and Android. Here is my json loader of the remote images: The below is my save to disk function. It works great when the app is handling 50 images at the time, but once its higher, some of the images are not stored, even though this below function is called. json feed: http://cph.napp.dk/index.php?option=com_phocagallery&view=napp&format=json There are no errors or exceptions I can paste in, due to the fact that Titanium does not make """"""""errors"""""""" it just skips a lot of files. Yes, it has nothing to do with the server. I have tried without the """"""""write remote to disk functionality"""""""" and the gallery works great. Q&A Thread at [save 100+ remote images to disk|http://developer.<USER>com/question/123769/save-100-remote-images-to-disk]""""",title+description
TIMOB-5311,12,"""iOS: Scrollable View currentPage Doesn't Change When Scrolling 50%, Despite Comments in Code""","""""""h1. Problem  The currentPage of a scrollable view does not always sync up with the visible dot. This happens because the dot is updated when the user scrolls over 50%, and the currentPage only updates when the underlying scroll view ends decelerating.    This is a problem because the app may act based on the currentPage of the scrollable view. So if the user swipes, and then hits a button that shows different content based on the currentPage, the wrong content can show up.    h2. Reproduction  Drop the following in an app.js, and swipe right and left to the various pages of the scrollable view. Down at the bottom, I have placed a label that is updated with the currentPage.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: '#fff'  });    var scroll = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({      bottom: 30,      views: [          Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'cyan' }),          Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'magenta' }),          Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'yellow' })      ],      pagingControlColor: '#000',      pagingControlHeight: 30  });  win.add(scroll);    var currentPageLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({      text: 'Current Page: Loading...', textAlign: 'center',      bottom: 0, right: 0, left: 0,      height: 30,      color: '#fff', backgroundColor: '#000'  });  win.add(currentPageLabel);  setInterval(function() {      currentPageLabel.text = 'Current Page: ' + scroll.currentPage;  }, 50);    win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Scrollable View currentPage Doesn't Change When Scrolling 50%, Despite Comments in Code
Description: """"h1. Problem The currentPage of a scrollable view does not always sync up with the visible dot. This happens because the dot is updated when the user scrolls over 50%, and the currentPage only updates when the underlying scroll view ends decelerating. This is a problem because the app may act based on the currentPage of the scrollable view. So if the user swipes, and then hits a button that shows different content based on the currentPage, the wrong content can show up. h2. Reproduction Drop the following in an app.js, and swipe right and left to the various pages of the scrollable view. Down at the bottom, I have placed a label that is updated with the currentPage. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var scroll = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({ bottom: 30, views: [ Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'cyan' }), Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'magenta' }), Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'yellow' }) ], pagingControlColor: '#000', pagingControlHeight: 30 }); win.add(scroll); var currentPageLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'Current Page: Loading...', textAlign: 'center', bottom: 0, right: 0, left: 0, height: 30, color: '#fff', backgroundColor: '#000' }); win.add(currentPageLabel); setInterval(function() { currentPageLabel.text = 'Current Page: ' + scroll.currentPage; }, 50); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-5310,12,"""Android: addAnnotations method does not exist""","""""""h3.Problem  While using addAnnotations method with Android it throws an error: """"""""TypeError: Cannot find function addAnnotations in object [Ti.Map.View]."""""""". This method works correctly on iOS.    h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Execute the sample code (the error message would appear)    h3.Description of addAnnotations method  http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Map.MapView-object    h3.Sample Code      """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: addAnnotations method does not exist
