TIMOB-5289,12,"""iOS: TableView searchHidden property is ignored ""","""""""h3.Problem  Setting the data dynamically to the TableView makes it ignore the searchHidden property.    h3.Reproducible Steps  1. Run the code  2. Press """"""""press"""""""" button    h3.Expected behavior  After using the setData() method within the tableView it should respect the previous searchHidden property set.    h3.Remarks  The TableView instance was created with the property """"""""searchHidden: true"""""""". It works correctly for the first time (the searchBar is hidden).  After setting the new data into the tableView using setData() method looks like it overrides the searchHidden property and sets it to FALSE. The searchBar is not anymore hidden.    h3.Code      h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket  http://appc.me/a/APP-912357""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView searchHidden property is ignored
Description: """"h3.Problem Setting the data dynamically to the TableView makes it ignore the searchHidden property. h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Run the code 2. Press """"""""press"""""""" button h3.Expected behavior After using the setData() method within the tableView it should respect the previous searchHidden property set. h3.Remarks The TableView instance was created with the property """"""""searchHidden: true"""""""". It works correctly for the first time (the searchBar is hidden). After setting the new data into the tableView using setData() method looks like it overrides the searchHidden property and sets it to FALSE. The searchBar is not anymore hidden. h3.Code h3.Associated HelpDesk Ticket http://appc.me/a/APP-912357""""",title+description
TIMOB-5288,12,"""Android: Tables not supported in email message body""","""""""Tables in HTML emails not working on Android. Tested on-device with my Droid original. Reported in the Q&A http://developer.<USER>com/question/125566/html-table-tags-are-not-working    Sample code works on iOS. See [https://skitch.com/<USER>f38fg/tablesnotworking] for output on Android.    {code:lang=javascript}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var msgBody = """"""""<table><thead><tr><th>Heading 1</th><th>Heading 2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cell 1</td><td>Cell 2</td></tr><tr><td>Cell 3</td><td>Cell 4</td></tr></tbody></table>"""""""";    var emailDialog = Ti.UI.createEmailDialog({   html:true,   messageBody: msgBody,   subject: 'Testing tables',   toRecipients: ['<EMAIL>']  });  emailDialog.setHtml(true);    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({   title:'send a note',   width: 200,   height:40,   top: 20  });  button.addEventListener('click', function(){   emailDialog.open();  });  win.add(button);  win.open();  {code}    Might be related to http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3544""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tables not supported in email message body
Description: """"Tables in HTML emails not working on Android. Tested on-device with my Droid original. Reported in the Q&A http://developer.<USER>com/question/125566/html-table-tags-are-not-working Sample code works on iOS. See [https://skitch.com/<USER>f38fg/tablesnotworking] for output on Android. {code:lang=javascript} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var msgBody = """"""""<table><thead><tr><th>Heading 1</th><th>Heading 2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cell 1</td><td>Cell 2</td></tr><tr><td>Cell 3</td><td>Cell 4</td></tr></tbody></table>""""""""; var emailDialog = Ti.UI.createEmailDialog({ html:true, messageBody: msgBody, subject: 'Testing tables', toRecipients: ['<EMAIL>'] }); emailDialog.setHtml(true); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'send a note', width: 200, height:40, top: 20 }); button.addEventListener('click', function(){ emailDialog.open(); }); win.add(button); win.open(); {code} Might be related to http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-3544""""",title+description
