TIMOB-5268,12,"""iOS: Redraw is shown when a view with a vertical layout is hidden/shown""","""""""When hiding or showing a view with a vertical layout, the view's children are shown """"""""flickering"""""""" for a moment as the view appears to be re-drawn with the vertical layout.  Tested on 4.3 simulator and iPod Touch 4th gen with iOS 4.3.  Same behavior is not displayed on Android versions I tested.  Tested on mobile SDK 1.7.2 (current production release) and on 1.8.x continuous build, issue is present in both SDKs.    Simple example:    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Redraw is shown when a view with a vertical layout is hidden/shown
Description: """"When hiding or showing a view with a vertical layout, the view's children are shown """"""""flickering"""""""" for a moment as the view appears to be re-drawn with the vertical layout. Tested on 4.3 simulator and iPod Touch 4th gen with iOS 4.3. Same behavior is not displayed on Android versions I tested. Tested on mobile SDK 1.7.2 (current production release) and on 1.8.x continuous build, issue is present in both SDKs. Simple example: """"",title+description
TIMOB-5267,12,"""Android: Flow Layout""","""""""Currently, layout:""""""""horizontal"""""""" works differently between Android and iOS, with Android placing each view to the right of the previous view _indefinitely_ and iOS placing in the same way until the views reach the right-hand edge of the screen, in which case the views is wrapped underneath. This is described in TIMOB-3256, which states (also confirmed by Don) that the intention is to fix the horizontal behavior in iOS and introduce a new """"""""flow"""""""" layout that wraps views, just as iOS currently does.    As many of our developers rely on the current horizontal-flowing behavior on iOS (speak to Pedro about the number of solutions he has provided that use it), I have raised this ticket to track the progress of the new flow layout, and to insure that the flow layout is implemented *BEFORE* the current iOS behavior is removed, as otherwise this will cause many problems.    {code:lang=javascript}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({  backgroundColor:""""""""black"""""""",  navBarHidden:false,  title:""""""""Main Window""""""""  });    var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({  backgroundColor:'blue',    layout:'horizontal'  //  layout:'flow'  // layout:'vertical'  });    for(var i=0;i<100;i++){  var view = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'green',    width:94,    height:94,    top:10,    left:10  });  scrollView.add(view);  }    win.add(scrollView);    win.open();  {code}  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Flow Layout
Description: """"Currently, layout:""""""""horizontal"""""""" works differently between Android and iOS, with Android placing each view to the right of the previous view _indefinitely_ and iOS placing in the same way until the views reach the right-hand edge of the screen, in which case the views is wrapped underneath. This is described in TIMOB-3256, which states (also confirmed by Don) that the intention is to fix the horizontal behavior in iOS and introduce a new """"""""flow"""""""" layout that wraps views, just as iOS currently does. As many of our developers rely on the current horizontal-flowing behavior on iOS (speak to Pedro about the number of solutions he has provided that use it), I have raised this ticket to track the progress of the new flow layout, and to insure that the flow layout is implemented *BEFORE* the current iOS behavior is removed, as otherwise this will cause many problems. {code:lang=javascript} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:""""""""black"""""""", navBarHidden:false, title:""""""""Main Window"""""""" }); var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({ backgroundColor:'blue', layout:'horizontal' // layout:'flow' // layout:'vertical' }); for(var i=0;i<100;i++){ var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'green', width:94, height:94, top:10, left:10 }); scrollView.add(view); } win.add(scrollView); win.open(); {code} """"",title+description
