TIMOB-5245,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, launching test in landscape mode causes poorly organized dashboard""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, I entered the test in landscape mode and the dashboard had compressed icons and the layout was not correct. This could also occur when already in the test and rotating. The easier way to reproduce is to simply enter the test in landscape however. Rotating back to portrait does not fix the layout. See screen shot for more information.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on device  2) Rotate device to Landscape orientation  3) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Dashboard view  4) Launch test    Result:  Poorly formatted screen items    Expected:  Icons and formatting look good, as they do in portrait.    Notes:  This does not occur in 1.7.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, launching test in landscape mode causes poorly organized dashboard
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, I entered the test in landscape mode and the dashboard had compressed icons and the layout was not correct. This could also occur when already in the test and rotating. The easier way to reproduce is to simply enter the test in landscape however. Rotating back to portrait does not fix the layout. See screen shot for more information. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on device 2) Rotate device to Landscape orientation 3) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Dashboard view 4) Launch test Result: Poorly formatted screen items Expected: Icons and formatting look good, as they do in portrait. Notes: This does not occur in 1.7.2""""",title+description
