TIMOB-5235,12,"""Project cannot reinstall after build folder is cleaned""","""""""1) Create an Android project and run it in the emulator.  2) After the project has successfully installed on the emulator, close the emulator.  3) Clean the project (either through Project -> Clean... or by deleting the build files manually in the project file: Titanium Studio Workspace\<project name>\build\android\)  4) Run the project in the emulator again    Expected: Project installs normally and autolaunches in emulator  Actual: Project never reinstalls in emulator.  If you look in Debug perspective, the Application Installer exit value is 1 instead of the expected 0    Notes:  - Happens regardless of Fastdev being on or off.  - Reproducible in build 1.0.2.201107130739    Workaround:  Exit and relaunch TiStudio.  Application will now properly install on emulator.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Project cannot reinstall after build folder is cleaned
Description: """"1) Create an Android project and run it in the emulator. 2) After the project has successfully installed on the emulator, close the emulator. 3) Clean the project (either through Project -> Clean... or by deleting the build files manually in the project file: Titanium Studio Workspace\<project name>\build\android\) 4) Run the project in the emulator again Expected: Project installs normally and autolaunches in emulator Actual: Project never reinstalls in emulator. If you look in Debug perspective, the Application Installer exit value is 1 instead of the expected 0 Notes: - Happens regardless of Fastdev being on or off. - Reproducible in build 1.0.2.201107130739 Workaround: Exit and relaunch TiStudio. Application will now properly install on emulator. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5234,12,"""Android: When splash screen orientation is set to landscape, splash screen appears stretched momentarily before being displayed normally.""","""""""When launching the attached TiTest app, the splash screen momentarily appears as stretched in landscape mode and then quickly appears normally in landscape mode. This is not very noticeable in faster phones (though I was briefly able to see it on a Nexus S running 2.3.4), but can be better seen in slower phones such as the HTC Hero running 2.1 Update1.    A way I was able to reproduce this consistently was by letting the phone go to sleep and then activating it again. When I do this, the splash screen appears normally in portrait mode, then stretched in landscape mode, and then normally in landscape mode.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: When splash screen orientation is set to landscape, splash screen appears stretched momentarily before being displayed normally.
Description: """"When launching the attached TiTest app, the splash screen momentarily appears as stretched in landscape mode and then quickly appears normally in landscape mode. This is not very noticeable in faster phones (though I was briefly able to see it on a Nexus S running 2.3.4), but can be better seen in slower phones such as the HTC Hero running 2.1 Update1. A way I was able to reproduce this consistently was by letting the phone go to sleep and then activating it again. When I do this, the splash screen appears normally in portrait mode, then stretched in landscape mode, and then normally in landscape mode. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5232,12,"""Allow HTTP POST of multiple files to the same parameter""","""""""In [TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m], the """"""""send"""""""" method currently uses the setFile and setData methods of the """"""""ASIFormDataRequest"""""""" object for POST'ing files/images (TiBlob) via Ajax. The SDK should support posting multiple files/images (TiBlob) to the same POST parameter (e.g., http://example.com?file=image1.jpg&file=image2.jpg&file=image3.jpg).     This could be accomplished by using the addData and addFile methods of the """"""""ASIFormDataRequest"""""""" class instead.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Allow HTTP POST of multiple files to the same parameter
Description: """"In [TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiNetworkHTTPClientProxy.m], the """"""""send"""""""" method currently uses the setFile and setData methods of the """"""""ASIFormDataRequest"""""""" object for POST'ing files/images (TiBlob) via Ajax. The SDK should support posting multiple files/images (TiBlob) to the same POST parameter (e.g., http://example.com?file=image1.jpg&file=image2.jpg&file=image3.jpg). This could be accomplished by using the addData and addFile methods of the """"""""ASIFormDataRequest"""""""" class instead.""""",title+description
