TIMOB-5187,12,"""Titanium Mobile 1.7 not dying on errors correctly""","""""""This ticket is in response to http://developer.<USER>com/question/121717/titanium-mobile-17-not-dying-on-errors-correctly    Not all exceptions properly show up in the UI and logs with 1.7.1:    The exception in the onload function does not show up:        I'd say the sample code says it all. Maybe there is something going on related to threads (maybe callbacks run in a different thread or something like that)?    """"""",Bug,"Title: Titanium Mobile 1.7 not dying on errors correctly
Description: """"This ticket is in response to http://developer.<USER>com/question/121717/titanium-mobile-17-not-dying-on-errors-correctly Not all exceptions properly show up in the UI and logs with 1.7.1: The exception in the onload function does not show up: I'd say the sample code says it all. Maybe there is something going on related to threads (maybe callbacks run in a different thread or something like that)? """"",title+description
TIMOB-5186,12,"""iOS: Feature Request to Add TextField hintTextColor and Size attributes""","""""""h6.Feature Request  It would be great to be able to specify the hintText color and size for TiUITextFields.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Feature Request to Add TextField hintTextColor and Size attributes
Description: """"h6.Feature Request It would be great to be able to specify the hintText color and size for TiUITextFields.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5185,12,"""Resizing label on orientationchange messes up bottom of page""","""""""I have a TableView with rows containing Labels to enable spanning multiple rows of text in a single TableViewRow. I have an orientationchange event listener that resets the width of the label and the height of the row it belongs to to make sure the rows properly display in landscape mode. If the height of the row shrinks (e.g. when the orientation changes from portrait to landscape), the bottom part of the display becomes messed up (see screenshot_landscape_lower.png).    See attachments for screenshots and the code below to reproduce the issue.    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      orientationModes : [         Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT,       Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,       Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT      ]  });    var tableview = Ti.UI.createTableView({    allowsSelection: false,    style: Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED,    scrollable: true  });    var rows = [];  rows.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewSection({ headerTitle: 'Title 1'}));    /* Multi-line tableviewrow */  var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({    height: 'auto'  });  var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({      height: 'auto',      width: Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth - 2 * (10+10),      text: 'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Nulla tristique purus sed magna accumsan id mollis velit ornare. Donec ut magna tempor erat fermentum interdum.',      top: 10,      bottom: 10,      left: 10,      right: 10,      font: { fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold' }  });  row.add(label);  rows.push(row);    /* More single line table view rows */  for (var i = 2; i <= 5; i++) {    rows.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewSection({ headerTitle: 'Title ' + i}));    rows.push({ title: 'Lorem ipsum dolor ' + i});  }  tableview.data = rows;  win.add(tableview);  win.open();    /* Recalculate label width on orientation change */  Ti.Gesture.addEventListener(""""""""orientationchange"""""""", function(event) {    label.width = Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth - 2 * (10+10);    row.height = 'auto'; /* Otherwise the row maintains its height */  });  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Resizing label on orientationchange messes up bottom of page
Description: """"I have a TableView with rows containing Labels to enable spanning multiple rows of text in a single TableViewRow. I have an orientationchange event listener that resets the width of the label and the height of the row it belongs to to make sure the rows properly display in landscape mode. If the height of the row shrinks (e.g. when the orientation changes from portrait to landscape), the bottom part of the display becomes messed up (see screenshot_landscape_lower.png). See attachments for screenshots and the code below to reproduce the issue. {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ orientationModes : [ Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT ] }); var tableview = Ti.UI.createTableView({ allowsSelection: false, style: Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED, scrollable: true }); var rows = []; rows.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewSection({ headerTitle: 'Title 1'})); /* Multi-line tableviewrow */ var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ height: 'auto' }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ height: 'auto', width: Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth - 2 * (10+10), text: 'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Nulla tristique purus sed magna accumsan id mollis velit ornare. Donec ut magna tempor erat fermentum interdum.', top: 10, bottom: 10, left: 10, right: 10, font: { fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold' } }); row.add(label); rows.push(row); /* More single line table view rows */ for (var i = 2; i <= 5; i++) { rows.push(Ti.UI.createTableViewSection({ headerTitle: 'Title ' + i})); rows.push({ title: 'Lorem ipsum dolor ' + i}); } tableview.data = rows; win.add(tableview); win.open(); /* Recalculate label width on orientation change */ Ti.Gesture.addEventListener(""""""""orientationchange"""""""", function(event) { label.width = Ti.Platform.displayCaps.platformWidth - 2 * (10+10); row.height = 'auto'; /* Otherwise the row maintains its height */ }); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-5184,12,"""iOS: ToolBar missing its content (buttons) while orientation change on ScrollableView""","""""""h3.Problem  When we have more than 5 views inside the ScrollableView and in every view different instance of ToolBar than after changing the orientation some of the ToolBars are missing their content/components (buttons, labels). Please see the screenshots.    h3.Reproducible Steps    1. Execute the attached code.  2. Stay with Portrait orientation  3. Go to the 6th view  4. Change from Portrait orientation into Landscape and than go back to Portrait  5. Go back to the 5th view  6. Now you can see an empty ToolBar - the components that were there are missing (buttons, labels)    h3.Regression  Works correctly with SDK 1.6.3    h3.Sample Code        h3.Associated Helpdesk ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-659713    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ToolBar missing its content (buttons) while orientation change on ScrollableView
Description: """"h3.Problem When we have more than 5 views inside the ScrollableView and in every view different instance of ToolBar than after changing the orientation some of the ToolBars are missing their content/components (buttons, labels). Please see the screenshots. h3.Reproducible Steps 1. Execute the attached code. 2. Stay with Portrait orientation 3. Go to the 6th view 4. Change from Portrait orientation into Landscape and than go back to Portrait 5. Go back to the 5th view 6. Now you can see an empty ToolBar - the components that were there are missing (buttons, labels) h3.Regression Works correctly with SDK 1.6.3 h3.Sample Code h3.Associated Helpdesk ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-659713 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5183,12,"""Android - openMusicLibrary Feature""","""""""h3. Feature Request    Expose the Ti.Media.openMusicLibrary() for android    h3. What would be ideal    1. A list (array) of all the music in the music player  2. A list of the videos in the music player  3. Being able to reproduce the above media items within an app  4. Being able to copy, add, or remove videos or mp3 from within the app    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android - openMusicLibrary Feature
Description: """"h3. Feature Request Expose the Ti.Media.openMusicLibrary() for android h3. What would be ideal 1. A list (array) of all the music in the music player 2. A list of the videos in the music player 3. Being able to reproduce the above media items within an app 4. Being able to copy, add, or remove videos or mp3 from within the app """"",title+description
TIMOB-5182,12,"""TiAPI: Titanium.Contacts.Person.URL should be lowercase""","""""""By convention, uppercase properties are constants. We should deprecate .URL and implement .url or use a different name if that's more appropriate.    Please update the documentation when this is implemented.""""""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: Titanium.Contacts.Person.URL should be lowercase
Description: """"By convention, uppercase properties are constants. We should deprecate .URL and implement .url or use a different name if that's more appropriate. Please update the documentation when this is implemented.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5180,12,"""iOS: Ti.API.info crashes if passed a window when debugging""","""""""If you pass Ti.API.info() a window in when debugging, the app will crash. If you just run the app in the simulator without debugging it works as expected and does not crash.    Step 1: run the code below in *debug* mode  Step 2: notice the app crash    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor:""""""""#fff"""""""",    title:""""""""My App""""""""  });  win.open();    Ti.API.info(win);  // Ti.API.info(""""""""win: """"""""+win);      h4. Workaround  concatenate the window with a string.  Ti.API.info(""""""""win: """"""""+win);    h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  httP://appc.me/c/APP-794556""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.API.info crashes if passed a window when debugging
Description: """"If you pass Ti.API.info() a window in when debugging, the app will crash. If you just run the app in the simulator without debugging it works as expected and does not crash. Step 1: run the code below in *debug* mode Step 2: notice the app crash {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:""""""""#fff"""""""", title:""""""""My App"""""""" }); win.open(); Ti.API.info(win); // Ti.API.info(""""""""win: """"""""+win); h4. Workaround concatenate the window with a string. Ti.API.info(""""""""win: """"""""+win); h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket httP://appc.me/c/APP-794556""""",title+description
TIMOB-5179,12,"""Android / New Feature: Gallery Widget""","""""""In Titanium Mobile 1.7.2 there is a component named {{CoverFlowView}} that is unfortunately ios-only    Within {{android.widget}} exits *Gallery* that is a layout widget used to display items in  a horizontally scrolling list and positions the current selection at the center of the view.    See http://developer.android.com/reference/android/widget/Gallery.html    This component is similar than {{CoverFlowView}} but exclusive for Android.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android / New Feature: Gallery Widget
Description: """"In Titanium Mobile 1.7.2 there is a component named {{CoverFlowView}} that is unfortunately ios-only Within {{android.widget}} exits *Gallery* that is a layout widget used to display items in a horizontally scrolling list and positions the current selection at the center of the view. See http://developer.android.com/reference/android/widget/Gallery.html This component is similar than {{CoverFlowView}} but exclusive for Android. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5178,12,"""TiAPI: Duplicate Symbol conflict with Async APIs""","""""""When attempting to use a module that includes a 3rd party library, receiving Duplicate Symbol errors with several 'Async...' symbols. Specifically,    - AsyncSocket  - AsyncSpecialPacket  - AsyncWritePacket  - AsyncReadPacket    The 3rd party library also defines these same symbols and so it is unable to link.  """"""",Bug,"Title: TiAPI: Duplicate Symbol conflict with Async APIs
Description: """"When attempting to use a module that includes a 3rd party library, receiving Duplicate Symbol errors with several 'Async...' symbols. Specifically, - AsyncSocket - AsyncSpecialPacket - AsyncWritePacket - AsyncReadPacket The 3rd party library also defines these same symbols and so it is unable to link. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5177,12,"""Android: scaled images in ImageView are stretched if aspect ratio of view doesn't match source image.""","""""""Given the attached large photo """"""""julia.jpg"""""""" and the following app.js:    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({   title : 'Test',   backgroundColor : '#000',   exitOnClose : true  });    var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({   image : """"""""julia.jpg"""""""",   top : 0,   left : 0,   width : """"""""300dp"""""""",   height : """"""""100dp"""""""",   backgroundColor : """"""""red""""""""  });    win.add(img);  win.open();  {code}    The aspect ratio of the image (w/h) is 0.75.  The aspect ratio of the created ImageView is 3.0.  If you run the app in iOS, you'll see that iOS makes a """"""""best fit"""""""" for image, being sure to display all of it *and* at the correct aspect ratio.  Our Android implementation, on the other hand, will stretch to fit the entirety of the ImageView, meaning it forces the 0.75 aspect ratio photo into a 3.0 aspect ratio, causing it to stretch horizontally and look bad.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: scaled images in ImageView are stretched if aspect ratio of view doesn't match source image.
Description: """"Given the attached large photo """"""""julia.jpg"""""""" and the following app.js: {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title : 'Test', backgroundColor : '#000', exitOnClose : true }); var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image : """"""""julia.jpg"""""""", top : 0, left : 0, width : """"""""300dp"""""""", height : """"""""100dp"""""""", backgroundColor : """"""""red"""""""" }); win.add(img); win.open(); {code} The aspect ratio of the image (w/h) is 0.75. The aspect ratio of the created ImageView is 3.0. If you run the app in iOS, you'll see that iOS makes a """"""""best fit"""""""" for image, being sure to display all of it *and* at the correct aspect ratio. Our Android implementation, on the other hand, will stretch to fit the entirety of the ImageView, meaning it forces the 0.75 aspect ratio photo into a 3.0 aspect ratio, causing it to stretch horizontally and look bad.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5176,12,"""Android images in imageview won't scale without explicit width and height""","""""""Given the attached large photo """"""""julia.jpg"""""""" and this app.js:    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Test',      backgroundColor:'#000',   exitOnClose: true  });    var v = Ti.UI.createView({   top: """"""""33%"""""""", height: """"""""33%"""""""", left: """"""""33%"""""""", right: """"""""33%"""""""",   backgroundColor: """"""""blue""""""""  });    var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({image: """"""""julia.jpg""""""""});  v.add(img);    win.add(v);  win.open();  {code}    Our iOS implementation will scale that graphic to make it fit and look good in the ImageView.  Our Android implementation won't scale it at all but rather just show part of the center of the image.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android images in imageview won't scale without explicit width and height
Description: """"Given the attached large photo """"""""julia.jpg"""""""" and this app.js: {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#000', exitOnClose: true }); var v = Ti.UI.createView({ top: """"""""33%"""""""", height: """"""""33%"""""""", left: """"""""33%"""""""", right: """"""""33%"""""""", backgroundColor: """"""""blue"""""""" }); var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({image: """"""""julia.jpg""""""""}); v.add(img); win.add(v); win.open(); {code} Our iOS implementation will scale that graphic to make it fit and look good in the ImageView. Our Android implementation won't scale it at all but rather just show part of the center of the image.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5174,12,"""Android: Implement a dual-scrolling Ti.UI.ScrollView""","""""""On iOS, scrollview can move both vertically and horizontally but on Android this is not the case.  We should perhaps create new HorizontalScrollview and VeriticalScrollview types rather than forcing a developer to manually set the scroll type on Android only.  We should also consider creating a iOS style scrollview on Android.    If the above approach is taken, we should remove the Android only scrollType property on the scrollview for simplicity sake.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Implement a dual-scrolling Ti.UI.ScrollView
Description: """"On iOS, scrollview can move both vertically and horizontally but on Android this is not the case. We should perhaps create new HorizontalScrollview and VeriticalScrollview types rather than forcing a developer to manually set the scroll type on Android only. We should also consider creating a iOS style scrollview on Android. If the above approach is taken, we should remove the Android only scrollType property on the scrollview for simplicity sake.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5173,12,"""Android: window proxy is not set correctly on light weight window""","""""""Exception is throw when trying to get window proxy for light weight window.  Attached source should trigger the exception when the open event fires and the orientation is set.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: window proxy is not set correctly on light weight window
Description: """"Exception is throw when trying to get window proxy for light weight window. Attached source should trigger the exception when the open event fires and the orientation is set. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5171,12,"""Move Ti.UI.TabbedBar into Ti.UI.iOS namespace""","""""""Android does not support Ti.UI.TabbedBar like iOS does and thus applications that rely on this across both iOS and Android encounter problems.  Move to the iOS namespace, remembering to DEPRECATE the availability on Ti.UI.""""""",Bug,"Title: Move Ti.UI.TabbedBar into Ti.UI.iOS namespace
Description: """"Android does not support Ti.UI.TabbedBar like iOS does and thus applications that rely on this across both iOS and Android encounter problems. Move to the iOS namespace, remembering to DEPRECATE the availability on Ti.UI.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5170,12,"""Android:  Ti.UI.ScrollableView showPagingControl sould be false by default""","""""""showPagingControl should be false by default to achieve parity with iOS""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.ScrollableView showPagingControl sould be false by default
Description: """"showPagingControl should be false by default to achieve parity with iOS""""",title+description
TIMOB-5169,12,"""Android: Implement new ScrollableView behaving more similar to iOS""","""""""When moving a scrollable view in iOS, the view follows the finger until a threshold is met that triggers the paging mechanism to show the next/previous """"""""page"""""""".  In Android, the view does not follow the finger up until the threshold.  This ticket exists to track the discussion of the parity difference and the fix if one is agreed upon.    UPDATED DESCRIPTION:  I (Bill) changed this ticket to doing the actual implementation of a """"""""follow-the-finger"""""""" scrollable view.  Original title of this item was """"""""TiAPI: Spec / Tech discussion about ScrollableView"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Implement new ScrollableView behaving more similar to iOS
Description: """"When moving a scrollable view in iOS, the view follows the finger until a threshold is met that triggers the paging mechanism to show the next/previous """"""""page"""""""". In Android, the view does not follow the finger up until the threshold. This ticket exists to track the discussion of the parity difference and the fix if one is agreed upon. UPDATED DESCRIPTION: I (Bill) changed this ticket to doing the actual implementation of a """"""""follow-the-finger"""""""" scrollable view. Original title of this item was """"""""TiAPI: Spec / Tech discussion about ScrollableView"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-5168,12,"""Android: background image does not show up on Button when backgroundImage is set""","""""""background image does not show up on Button when backgroundImage is set.  A simple work around to the issue is to set the image as the """"""""image"""""""" property on the button.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: background image does not show up on Button when backgroundImage is set
Description: """"background image does not show up on Button when backgroundImage is set. A simple work around to the issue is to set the image as the """"""""image"""""""" property on the button.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5167,12,"""iOS: Immutable objects on Window object""","""""""When you attach an object to a Window on iOS the object is immutable, yet on Android it works fine.  For example, win.myCustomObject = { id: val } works as expected.  However, when you then try and change a value within that object, the changes are never made i.e. win.myCustomObject.id = newVal, the id stays the same.    Code example requires two files:    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor: '#000',    url: 'window_object_win.js',    layout:'vertical'  });    win.data = {    text: 'Initialized'  };    win.open();    win.addEventListener('modifyData', function() {    win.data.text = 'This should be updated if this object is mutable';    win.fireEvent('dataUpdated');  });    win.addEventListener('replaceData', function() {    win.data = { text: 'If the data has changed now then replacing the entire data object works ' };    win.fireEvent('dataUpdated');  });  {code}    {code:javascript|title='window_object_win.js'}  var modifyButton = Ti.UI.createButton({    title: 'Modify window .data object',    top: 60,    width: 250,    height: 80  });    var replaceButton = Ti.UI.createButton({    title: 'Replace window .data object',    top: 60,    width: 250,    height: 80  });    var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({    color: '#FFF',    top: 20,    height: 200  });    Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(modifyButton);  Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(replaceButton);  Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(label);    modifyButton.addEventListener('click', function() {    Ti.UI.currentWindow.fireEvent('modifyData');  });    replaceButton.addEventListener('click', function() {    Ti.UI.currentWindow.fireEvent('replaceData');  });    var counter = 0;    var updateLabelFromData = function() {    label.text = 'Text (' + counter++ + ' presses) = ' + Ti.UI.currentWindow.data.text;  };    Ti.UI.currentWindow.addEventListener('dataUpdated', updateLabelFromData);    updateLabelFromData();  {code}    To replicate this issue with this code example, load up the app, click on the bottom button (to modify values) and you will see that the value does not change.  However, if you click on the button above that which replaces the entire object on the window, it works fine.  On Android both buttons work as expected.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Immutable objects on Window object
Description: """"When you attach an object to a Window on iOS the object is immutable, yet on Android it works fine. For example, win.myCustomObject = { id: val } works as expected. However, when you then try and change a value within that object, the changes are never made i.e. win.myCustomObject.id = newVal, the id stays the same. Code example requires two files: {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#000', url: 'window_object_win.js', layout:'vertical' }); win.data = { text: 'Initialized' }; win.open(); win.addEventListener('modifyData', function() { win.data.text = 'This should be updated if this object is mutable'; win.fireEvent('dataUpdated'); }); win.addEventListener('replaceData', function() { win.data = { text: 'If the data has changed now then replacing the entire data object works ' }; win.fireEvent('dataUpdated'); }); {code} {code:javascript|title='window_object_win.js'} var modifyButton = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Modify window .data object', top: 60, width: 250, height: 80 }); var replaceButton = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Replace window .data object', top: 60, width: 250, height: 80 }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color: '#FFF', top: 20, height: 200 }); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(modifyButton); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(replaceButton); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(label); modifyButton.addEventListener('click', function() { Ti.UI.currentWindow.fireEvent('modifyData'); }); replaceButton.addEventListener('click', function() { Ti.UI.currentWindow.fireEvent('replaceData'); }); var counter = 0; var updateLabelFromData = function() { label.text = 'Text (' + counter++ + ' presses) = ' + Ti.UI.currentWindow.data.text; }; Ti.UI.currentWindow.addEventListener('dataUpdated', updateLabelFromData); updateLabelFromData(); {code} To replicate this issue with this code example, load up the app, click on the bottom button (to modify values) and you will see that the value does not change. However, if you click on the button above that which replaces the entire object on the window, it works fine. On Android both buttons work as expected.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5166,12,"""iOS: Move iOS-specific constants from Ti.UI to Ti.UI.iOS""","""""""We need to move a number of constants from Ti.UI to Ti.UI.iOS - these include (but may not be limited to...)    * ANIMATION_*  * AUTODETECT_*  * BLEND_*    Remember to keep backwards-compatibile constants for 1.8, and DEPRECATE for 1.9.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Move iOS-specific constants from Ti.UI to Ti.UI.iOS
Description: """"We need to move a number of constants from Ti.UI to Ti.UI.iOS - these include (but may not be limited to...) * ANIMATION_* * AUTODETECT_* * BLEND_* Remember to keep backwards-compatibile constants for 1.8, and DEPRECATE for 1.9.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5165,12,"""Create tests for iOS Ti.Blob image manipulations""","""""""We need tests for all of the image manipulation APIs that are currently on blob. As we migrate to a new API set that specifically works with image data, we can change these tests over, but for now they'll give us some coverage information.""""""",Bug,"Title: Create tests for iOS Ti.Blob image manipulations
Description: """"We need tests for all of the image manipulation APIs that are currently on blob. As we migrate to a new API set that specifically works with image data, we can change these tests over, but for now they'll give us some coverage information.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5164,12,"""Categorize some iOS proxies as modules for coverage""","""""""Currently, some submodules (and even modules?) are categorized as proxies in the generated iOS coverage. In particular, we need to ensure that the following are categorized as modules:    * Ti.App.Properties  * Ti.App.iOS  * Ti.Network.Socket    ... Among many others. The entire coverage output should be skimmed and checked to make sure that proxies aren't duplicating module information, AND that those things which are submodules and iOS-only are being classified as modules.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Categorize some iOS proxies as modules for coverage
Description: """"Currently, some submodules (and even modules?) are categorized as proxies in the generated iOS coverage. In particular, we need to ensure that the following are categorized as modules: * Ti.App.Properties * Ti.App.iOS * Ti.Network.Socket ... Among many others. The entire coverage output should be skimmed and checked to make sure that proxies aren't duplicating module information, AND that those things which are submodules and iOS-only are being classified as modules. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5163,12,"""iOS: Migrate Ti.Facebook.LoginButton constants to Ti.Facebook and rename""","""""""The constants on Ti.Facebook.LoginButton (STYLE_WIDE and STYLE_NORMAL) need to be:    * Moved to Ti.Facebook  * Renamed to BUTTON_STYLE_WIDE, BUTTON_STYLE_NORMAL    Please keep the original names in for backwards compatibility in 1.9 and deprecate.  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  NOTE FOR QE: While testing, its worth noting that now in Mashup/Facebook/  *login/logout & photos would show a wide faceebook button.  *Query,Properties, Publish Stream show a normal facebook button.  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Migrate Ti.Facebook.LoginButton constants to Ti.Facebook and rename
Description: """"The constants on Ti.Facebook.LoginButton (STYLE_WIDE and STYLE_NORMAL) need to be: * Moved to Ti.Facebook * Renamed to BUTTON_STYLE_WIDE, BUTTON_STYLE_NORMAL Please keep the original names in for backwards compatibility in 1.9 and deprecate. ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- NOTE FOR QE: While testing, its worth noting that now in Mashup/Facebook/ *login/logout & photos would show a wide faceebook button. *Query,Properties, Publish Stream show a normal facebook button. ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------""""",title+description
TIMOB-5161,12,"""Unit tests for Ti.Contacts on iOS""","""""""There's already a suite of tests for contacts on Android in drillbit, but we need tests on iOS which test full functionality. Because we can't rely on each device/sim having the same contacts information on it, we will need to test the full infrastructure, starting with createPerson/createGroup, setting properties, retrieving them, etc.    Any unit test will necessarily involve secondary verification that these were actually entered into the Contacts DB.""""""",Bug,"Title: Unit tests for Ti.Contacts on iOS
Description: """"There's already a suite of tests for contacts on Android in drillbit, but we need tests on iOS which test full functionality. Because we can't rely on each device/sim having the same contacts information on it, we will need to test the full infrastructure, starting with createPerson/createGroup, setting properties, retrieving them, etc. Any unit test will necessarily involve secondary verification that these were actually entered into the Contacts DB.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5159,12,"""Create 'class blacklist' / blacklist TiColor on iOS""","""""""We need to prevent information from being generated from some classes (such as TiColor) during the coverage generation <USER> these are proxies, but appear to be for internal use only, and as a result may be obsolete. We need to do the following:    * Evaluate Ti.Color as a standalone class and either:  ** Blacklist it (not public knowledge)  ** Document it (should be publicly available)    In the event that blacklisting all methods/properties from TiColor does not remove it from the coverage chart, we also need to update the blacklisting mechanism to handle the blacklisting of classes.""""""",Bug,"Title: Create 'class blacklist' / blacklist TiColor on iOS
Description: """"We need to prevent information from being generated from some classes (such as TiColor) during the coverage generation <USER> these are proxies, but appear to be for internal use only, and as a result may be obsolete. We need to do the following: * Evaluate Ti.Color as a standalone class and either: ** Blacklist it (not public knowledge) ** Document it (should be publicly available) In the event that blacklisting all methods/properties from TiColor does not remove it from the coverage chart, we also need to update the blacklisting mechanism to handle the blacklisting of classes.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5158,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink Facebook login popup does not change from portrait to landscape""","""""""Steps to reproduce:  1) In KitchenSink, navigate to Mashup > Facebook > Login/Logout   2) Click the 'Login with Facebook' button  3) Click either the email or password field to bring focus to the field and cause keyboard to appear  4) Change from portrait to landscape layout    Expected results:  The login popup and keyboard adjust properly to landscape layout    Actual results:  The keyboard adjusts properly to landscape layout, but the popin stays in its portrait position.  See screenshot. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink Facebook login popup does not change from portrait to landscape
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1) In KitchenSink, navigate to Mashup > Facebook > Login/Logout 2) Click the 'Login with Facebook' button 3) Click either the email or password field to bring focus to the field and cause keyboard to appear 4) Change from portrait to landscape layout Expected results: The login popup and keyboard adjust properly to landscape layout Actual results: The keyboard adjusts properly to landscape layout, but the popin stays in its portrait position. See screenshot. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5157,12,"""iPad: barImage does not change when orientation changes""","""""""Steps to recreate:    Drop the following in to an app.js, and click the button. A modal window will pop up, then close itself after one second. Watch the nav bar, which will have KS_nav_ui.png set as its barImage (make sure this image is available).    Repeat this a couple of times and then change the orientation of the iPad.    Actual Result:  barImage still would have the same position and size as it was in previos orientation.    Expected Result:  barImage should change its position and size according to the new orientation.    Note: this would happen only for the first time. After the first time, the image changes according to the new orientation.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iPad: barImage does not change when orientation changes
Description: """"Steps to recreate: Drop the following in to an app.js, and click the button. A modal window will pop up, then close itself after one second. Watch the nav bar, which will have KS_nav_ui.png set as its barImage (make sure this image is available). Repeat this a couple of times and then change the orientation of the iPad. Actual Result: barImage still would have the same position and size as it was in previos orientation. Expected Result: barImage should change its position and size according to the new orientation. Note: this would happen only for the first time. After the first time, the image changes according to the new orientation. """"",title+description
