TIMOB-5140,12,"""Android: Application gets stuck for 2-3 minutes when fastdev server is stopped from terminal""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Make sure you have the environment set up by adding following to ~/.bash_profile    alias titanium=$HOME/.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/1.7.0/titanium.py    2. Once your environment is setup, you will be able to run 'titanium' command in terminal.  It should look like following:    $ titanium  <USER>Titanium  Copyright (c) 2010-2011 by <USER> Inc.    commands:    create - create a project  run - run an existing project  emulator - start the emulator (android)  docgen - generate html docs for a module (android)  fastdev - management for the Android fastdev server  help - get help    After that:    1. Create a Titanium Mobile project for android in Titanium Studio.  2. Launch the application in Emulator  3. Stop the fastdev server from terminal using following command in terminal:          titanium fastdev stop    4. Press back button on Emulator.  5. Launch the application again from within Emulator using application icon    Expected Result:    Should display: Warning: Fastdev mode is disabled. Error Message:/<ip_address:port> Connection Refused    and then it should launch the application.    Actual Result:    It gets stuck on Red <USER>screen for 2-3 minutes and then displays the error message and launches the application.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Application gets stuck for 2-3 minutes when fastdev server is stopped from terminal
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Make sure you have the environment set up by adding following to ~/.bash_profile alias titanium=$HOME/.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/1.7.0/titanium.py 2. Once your environment is setup, you will be able to run 'titanium' command in terminal. It should look like following: $ titanium <USER>Titanium Copyright (c) 2010-2011 by <USER> Inc. commands: create - create a project run - run an existing project emulator - start the emulator (android) docgen - generate html docs for a module (android) fastdev - management for the Android fastdev server help - get help After that: 1. Create a Titanium Mobile project for android in Titanium Studio. 2. Launch the application in Emulator 3. Stop the fastdev server from terminal using following command in terminal: titanium fastdev stop 4. Press back button on Emulator. 5. Launch the application again from within Emulator using application icon Expected Result: Should display: Warning: Fastdev mode is disabled. Error Message:/<ip_address:port> Connection Refused and then it should launch the application. Actual Result: It gets stuck on Red <USER>screen for 2-3 minutes and then displays the error message and launches the application.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5139,12,"""Android: command 'titanium fastdev restart' does not update window's label ""","""""""Steps to reproduce:    1. Make sure you have the environment set up by adding following to ~/.bash_profile        alias titanium=$HOME/.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/1.7.0/titanium.py    2. Once your environment is setup, you will be able to run 'titanium' command in terminal.     It should look like following:      $ titanium  <USER>Titanium  Copyright (c) 2010-2011 by <USER> Inc.     commands:       create      - create a project    run         - run an existing project    emulator    - start the emulator (android)    docgen      - generate html docs for a module (android)    fastdev     - management for the Android fastdev server    help        - get help      After that:    1. Create a Titanium mobile project for Android in studio.  2. Launch the application from TiStudio.  3. Open app.js and Change label2.text: 'Version: ' + Titanium.App.getVersion(),   4. Restart the application from terminal using following fastdev command in terminal           titanium fastdev restart-app    Expected Result:    Able to see new label with version number.    Actual Result:    Same window label is shown. It does not get updated.       """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: command 'titanium fastdev restart' does not update window's label
Description: """"Steps to reproduce: 1. Make sure you have the environment set up by adding following to ~/.bash_profile alias titanium=$HOME/.titanium/mobilesdk/linux/1.7.0/titanium.py 2. Once your environment is setup, you will be able to run 'titanium' command in terminal. It should look like following: $ titanium <USER>Titanium Copyright (c) 2010-2011 by <USER> Inc. commands: create - create a project run - run an existing project emulator - start the emulator (android) docgen - generate html docs for a module (android) fastdev - management for the Android fastdev server help - get help After that: 1. Create a Titanium mobile project for Android in studio. 2. Launch the application from TiStudio. 3. Open app.js and Change label2.text: 'Version: ' + Titanium.App.getVersion(), 4. Restart the application from terminal using following fastdev command in terminal titanium fastdev restart-app Expected Result: Able to see new label with version number. Actual Result: Same window label is shown. It does not get updated. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5138,12,"""Android: After building for emulator, application crashes on launch on device""","""""""New:  1.create a simple app with 1.8.0  2.run it in the emulator  3.install to device  4.eyeball device    results:app crashes on launch      OLD steps:  Steps to reproduce:    1. Create a titanium mobile project for android using TiMob: 1.8.0.v20110819142548  2. Add following to tiapp.xml within <android> and </android> tags which would look something like this:    <android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"""""""">   <manifest>    <supports-screens android:normalScreens=""""""""true""""""""                   android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/>   </manifest>  </android>    3. Build and run it on Android Emulator.  4. Install it on Android device. (It works on Android Emulator though.)  5. Try to run the application.  6. It would say. sorry, app quits unexpectedly. (Note: I runs properly if we directly install it on device without running it in Emulator)    adb logcat output is pasted below.    Note:  If you create the mobile with TiMob 1.7.2 and follow above from steps2 to step6, application would run properly. Also, if you first create the project with TiMob 1.7.2 and then change it to TiMob 1.8.0.v20110819142548 from tiapp.xml, and then repeat the steps from step2 to step6, it will again run properly.       """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: After building for emulator, application crashes on launch on device
Description: """"New: 1.create a simple app with 1.8.0 2.run it in the emulator 3.install to device 4.eyeball device results:app crashes on launch OLD steps: Steps to reproduce: 1. Create a titanium mobile project for android using TiMob: 1.8.0.v20110819142548 2. Add following to tiapp.xml within <android> and </android> tags which would look something like this: <android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""> <manifest> <supports-screens android:normalScreens=""""""""true"""""""" android:anyDensity=""""""""false""""""""/> </manifest> </android> 3. Build and run it on Android Emulator. 4. Install it on Android device. (It works on Android Emulator though.) 5. Try to run the application. 6. It would say. sorry, app quits unexpectedly. (Note: I runs properly if we directly install it on device without running it in Emulator) adb logcat output is pasted below. Note: If you create the mobile with TiMob 1.7.2 and follow above from steps2 to step6, application would run properly. Also, if you first create the project with TiMob 1.7.2 and then change it to TiMob 1.8.0.v20110819142548 from tiapp.xml, and then repeat the steps from step2 to step6, it will again run properly. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5137,12,"""Kitchensink: Phone>Contacts>contact images choosing a contact with image and then another without displays the image from the first contact selected. ""","""""""Description:  While testing Phone>Contacts>contact images, I chose a contact with images (Thanks Dawson) and the image appeared as expected. A second attempt to choose a contact with no image resulted in the text, """"""""no image' appearing, but the previous image was present. See screenshot.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S  2) Navigate to Phone>Contacts>contact images  3) With the device in portrait, click """"""""Set landscape""""""""  4) Click """"""""open window""""""""    Result:  The UI rotates to Portrait, then the window opens in portrait.    Expected result:  The UI remains in landscape and the window opens in landscape.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Phone>Contacts>contact images choosing a contact with image and then another without displays the image from the first contact selected.
Description: """"Description: While testing Phone>Contacts>contact images, I chose a contact with images (Thanks Dawson) and the image appeared as expected. A second attempt to choose a contact with no image resulted in the text, """"""""no image' appearing, but the previous image was present. See screenshot. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S 2) Navigate to Phone>Contacts>contact images 3) With the device in portrait, click """"""""Set landscape"""""""" 4) Click """"""""open window"""""""" Result: The UI rotates to Portrait, then the window opens in portrait. Expected result: The UI remains in landscape and the window opens in landscape. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5136,12,"""Android: """"instanceof check"""" fails""","""""""1.see it in KS, when the app is first launched (adb logcat)  2. the failure line is     Ti.API.info(""""""""instanceof check, should be false => """""""" + (Ti.UI.createView() instanceof Ti.UI.createWindow())); """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: """"instanceof check"""" fails
Description: """"1.see it in KS, when the app is first launched (adb logcat) 2. the failure line is Ti.API.info(""""""""instanceof check, should be false => """""""" + (Ti.UI.createView() instanceof Ti.UI.createWindow())); """"",title+description
TIMOB-5135,12,"""Android: Kitchensink Phone>Orientation> opening a window after clicking """"set landscape"""" with device in portrait rotates UI before window opens""","""""""Description:  While testing Phone>Orientation>, with the device in portrait mode, I clicked """"""""set landscape"""""""". This sets the UI to landscape. Then I clicked """"""""open window"""""""" and the UI rotated to portrait before the window opened. On iOS, the window opens, and the UI remains in landscape mode.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S  2) Navigate to Phone>Orientation>  3) With the device in portrait, click """"""""Set landscape""""""""  4) Click """"""""open window""""""""    Result:  The UI rotates to Portrait, then the window opens in portrait.    Expected result:  The UI remains in landscape and the window opens in landscape.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Kitchensink Phone>Orientation> opening a window after clicking """"set landscape"""" with device in portrait rotates UI before window opens
Description: """"Description: While testing Phone>Orientation>, with the device in portrait mode, I clicked """"""""set landscape"""""""". This sets the UI to landscape. Then I clicked """"""""open window"""""""" and the UI rotated to portrait before the window opened. On iOS, the window opens, and the UI remains in landscape mode. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S 2) Navigate to Phone>Orientation> 3) With the device in portrait, click """"""""Set landscape"""""""" 4) Click """"""""open window"""""""" Result: The UI rotates to Portrait, then the window opens in portrait. Expected result: The UI remains in landscape and the window opens in landscape. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5134,12,"""Kitchensink: Phone>Sound>Remote streaming """"unpause streaming"""" button does not unpause stream as expected. ""","""""""Description:  While testing Phone>Sound>Remote streaming, I started a stream via the """"""""Start Streaming"""""""" button and then tapped the """"""""Pause streaming"""""""" button. Attempting to restart the paused stream, I tapped """"""""Unpause streaming"""""""" and nothing happened.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S  2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote streaming  3) Tap """"""""start streaming""""""""   4) When sound is heard, tap """"""""Pause streaming""""""""  5) When sound stops, tap """"""""unease streaming""""""""      Result:  Nothing happens    Expected result:  The stream continues where it left off    Notes:  Also occurs with 1.7.2  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Phone>Sound>Remote streaming """"unpause streaming"""" button does not unpause stream as expected.
Description: """"Description: While testing Phone>Sound>Remote streaming, I started a stream via the """"""""Start Streaming"""""""" button and then tapped the """"""""Pause streaming"""""""" button. Attempting to restart the paused stream, I tapped """"""""Unpause streaming"""""""" and nothing happened. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote streaming 3) Tap """"""""start streaming"""""""" 4) When sound is heard, tap """"""""Pause streaming"""""""" 5) When sound stops, tap """"""""unease streaming"""""""" Result: Nothing happens Expected result: The stream continues where it left off Notes: Also occurs with 1.7.2 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5133,12,"""Kitchensink: Phone>Geolocation test does not alert when Reverse Geo call returns an error.""","""""""Description:  While testing Phone>Geolocation, no Reverse Geo information is populated on screen. Knowing that iOS produces an alert in this situation, I examined the code to see if there were some iOS specific lines preventing this alert form appearing on Android, and there is no reason I could find that this would not have parity on Android. After running a few tests, I am still unable to get the alert to appear.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S  2) Navigate to Phone>Geolocation  3) Stand in a location with both a clear view of the sky and a nice wifi signal   4) Wait for """"""""Updated location field"""""""" to populate as this should trigger the reverse geo call      Result:  No reverse geo content, no alert.    Expected result:  Either reverse geo populates, or  """"""""reverse geo error"""""""" alert.    Notes:  Also occurs with 1.7.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Phone>Geolocation test does not alert when Reverse Geo call returns an error.
Description: """"Description: While testing Phone>Geolocation, no Reverse Geo information is populated on screen. Knowing that iOS produces an alert in this situation, I examined the code to see if there were some iOS specific lines preventing this alert form appearing on Android, and there is no reason I could find that this would not have parity on Android. After running a few tests, I am still unable to get the alert to appear. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S 2) Navigate to Phone>Geolocation 3) Stand in a location with both a clear view of the sky and a nice wifi signal 4) Wait for """"""""Updated location field"""""""" to populate as this should trigger the reverse geo call Result: No reverse geo content, no alert. Expected result: Either reverse geo populates, or """"""""reverse geo error"""""""" alert. Notes: Also occurs with 1.7.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-5132,12,"""Kitchensink: Phone>Sound>Remote tests, stop stream button acts as pause stream ""","""""""Description:  While testing Kitchensink,Phone>Sound>Remote tests, I pressed the """"""""stop"""""""" button and expected the stream to stop. When I started the stream again, the stream started again from the locations where I stopped it. This behavior is the same as the """"""""pause"""""""" button.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S  2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote tests  3) Start the stream  4) Press """"""""stop""""""""  5) Start the stream again    Result:  The stream continues from where it was """"""""stopped""""""""    Expected result:  The stream resets and begins from the start of the stream again    Notes:  Also occurs with 1.7.2  """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Phone>Sound>Remote tests, stop stream button acts as pause stream
Description: """"Description: While testing Kitchensink,Phone>Sound>Remote tests, I pressed the """"""""stop"""""""" button and expected the stream to stop. When I started the stream again, the stream started again from the locations where I stopped it. This behavior is the same as the """"""""pause"""""""" button. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote tests 3) Start the stream 4) Press """"""""stop"""""""" 5) Start the stream again Result: The stream continues from where it was """"""""stopped"""""""" Expected result: The stream resets and begins from the start of the stream again Notes: Also occurs with 1.7.2 """"",title+description
TIMOB-5131,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View does not log view click or touchend events""","""""""Description:  While testing Kitchensink, Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View, I tapped the view which has two attached listeners. Neither the click event or the touchend event were logged. This works as expected on iOS.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View  3) Tap on the view with the """"""""Click me (View 2 - see log)"""""""" label  4) Examine the log    Result:  No event logged    Expected result:  The following is from iOS:  Fri Aug 26 11:46:53 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x9940][1051] <Notice>: [INFO] ScrollView received click event, source = [object TiUIView]  Fri Aug 26 11:46:53 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x9940][1051] <Notice>: [INFO] ScrollView received touchend event, source = [object TiUIView]    Notes:  Occurs with 1.7.2  Occurs with 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View does not log view click or touchend events
Description: """"Description: While testing Kitchensink, Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View, I tapped the view which has two attached listeners. Neither the click event or the touchend event were logged. This works as expected on iOS. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Scroll Views>Scrollable View 3) Tap on the view with the """"""""Click me (View 2 - see log)"""""""" label 4) Examine the log Result: No event logged Expected result: The following is from iOS: Fri Aug 26 11:46:53 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x9940][1051] <Notice>: [INFO] ScrollView received click event, source = [object TiUIView] Fri Aug 26 11:46:53 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>titanium[0x9940][1051] <Notice>: [INFO] ScrollView received touchend event, source = [object TiUIView] Notes: Occurs with 1.7.2 Occurs with 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-5130,12,"""Kitchensink: Base UI>Vertical Layout>Table View has text cut off at bottom of some of the table rows""","""""""Description:  While testing Kitchensink, Base UI>Vertical Layout>Table View, I scrolled the tableview and noticed some of the row text at the bottom of some of the rows is cut off.  See attached screenshot.    Occurs on:  Nexus S 2.3.4  Nexus One 2.2.2  Xoom, 3.2 (portrait only)    Does not occur on:  Galaxy Tab 2.3.4    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S  2) Navigate to Base UI>Vertical Layout>Table View  3) scroll the table and examine the text in each row.      Result:  The text of some of the rows is cut off at the bottom of the row.    Expected result:  Text for each row fully visible in the row.    Notes:  Also occurs with 1.7.2    """"""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Base UI>Vertical Layout>Table View has text cut off at bottom of some of the table rows
Description: """"Description: While testing Kitchensink, Base UI>Vertical Layout>Table View, I scrolled the tableview and noticed some of the row text at the bottom of some of the rows is cut off. See attached screenshot. Occurs on: Nexus S 2.3.4 Nexus One 2.2.2 Xoom, 3.2 (portrait only) Does not occur on: Galaxy Tab 2.3.4 Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.8.0 on Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base UI>Vertical Layout>Table View 3) scroll the table and examine the text in each row. Result: The text of some of the rows is cut off at the bottom of the row. Expected result: Text for each row fully visible in the row. Notes: Also occurs with 1.7.2 """"",title+description
