TIMOB-5088,12,"""Android: webView does not support openDatabase""","""""""openDatabase does not work in a webView but it does in the Android browser.    Step 1: create a file called test.html  Step 2: host it  Step 3: run the code below (changing the url to point to test.html)  Step 4: notice that the database is not created  Step 5: use the android browser and go to the same file  Step 6: notice that the database is created successfully    {code:title=""""""""app.js""""""""}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();    var webView = Ti.UI.createWebView({   url: """"""""http://192.168.1.137/~<USER>test/test.html""""""""  });  win.add(webView);    win.open();        h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-323498    h4. Another customer having the same issue    I need to use web SQL in a Titanium web View. I've used the following code snippet to test the functionality. This code works fine on iPhone, but it fails on Android. Can you please provide assistance in this regard.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: webView does not support openDatabase
Description: """"openDatabase does not work in a webView but it does in the Android browser. Step 1: create a file called test.html Step 2: host it Step 3: run the code below (changing the url to point to test.html) Step 4: notice that the database is not created Step 5: use the android browser and go to the same file Step 6: notice that the database is created successfully {code:title=""""""""app.js""""""""} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var webView = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url: """"""""http://192.168.1.137/~<USER>test/test.html"""""""" }); win.add(webView); win.open(); h4. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-323498 h4. Another customer having the same issue I need to use web SQL in a Titanium web View. I've used the following code snippet to test the functionality. This code works fine on iPhone, but it fails on Android. Can you please provide assistance in this regard. """"",title+description
TIMOB-5087,12,"""docgen unable to accept array of types""","""""""docgen is unable to accept an array of custom types.  For an example of the behavior, please refer to pull request #371 and the associated ticket timob-4916 where it is desirable to give an array of rows to the appendRow method on table view.""""""",Bug,"Title: docgen unable to accept array of types
