TIMOB-5080,12,"""Android: Titanium.Network.addEventListener does not fire after creating new tabgroup""","""""""h3.Bug    h3.Problem:    Titanium.Network.addEventListener does not fire after creating new tabgroup.    h3. Reproducible steps:    1.Run the code below.  2.Without clicking on 'Log In' button please change the network status on your Android device - the Titanium.Network event should be fired  3.Click on the 'Log In' button, after that new tabgroup will be created.  4.Change network status on your Android device - the event is no longer fired.    h3.Expected behavior    Customer wants that the Titanium.Network.addEventListener would be a global listener (that would appear only once in the code). That should be the correct behaviour.    h3.Sample Code:      h3. HelpDesk.    APP-287557          """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.Network.addEventListener does not fire after creating new tabgroup
Description: """"h3.Bug h3.Problem: Titanium.Network.addEventListener does not fire after creating new tabgroup. h3. Reproducible steps: 1.Run the code below. 2.Without clicking on 'Log In' button please change the network status on your Android device - the Titanium.Network event should be fired 3.Click on the 'Log In' button, after that new tabgroup will be created. 4.Change network status on your Android device - the event is no longer fired. h3.Expected behavior Customer wants that the Titanium.Network.addEventListener would be a global listener (that would appear only once in the code). That should be the correct behaviour. h3.Sample Code: h3. HelpDesk. APP-287557 """"",title+description
