TIMOB-5060,12,"""Geolocation should be handled by the mobile device""","""""""Mobile apps can currently get (forward and reverse) geolocation lookups from Titanium by way of a call to our API.  We are deprecating support for this service (see: CLOUDENG-376).    Titanium Mobile should directly access a service, such as [Google's Geolocation API|http://code.google.com/apis/maps/documentation/geocoding/] directly.  For example, version 3 of the Google API doesn't require API keys and rate limits by IP/device.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Geolocation should be handled by the mobile device
Description: """"Mobile apps can currently get (forward and reverse) geolocation lookups from Titanium by way of a call to our API. We are deprecating support for this service (see: CLOUDENG-376). Titanium Mobile should directly access a service, such as [Google's Geolocation API|http://code.google.com/apis/maps/documentation/geocoding/] directly. For example, version 3 of the Google API doesn't require API keys and rate limits by IP/device.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5059,12,"""""""302 Found"""" redirect drop authorization header""","""""""{html}<div><p>The Titanium.Network.HTTPClient correctly follows a """"""""302 Found""""""""  redirect. On the iPhone however it does not carry the http  authorization header in the next request (ending in a 401 response  from the server). I have not had this a problem with android, ie,  the authorization header is in the redirected request.</p>  <p>Problem found using SDK 1.6.0 &amp; 1.6.1 and iOS 4.2 (device  and simulator).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: """"302 Found"""" redirect drop authorization header
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The Titanium.Network.HTTPClient correctly follows a """"""""302 Found"""""""" redirect. On the iPhone however it does not carry the http authorization header in the next request (ending in a 401 response from the server). I have not had this a problem with android, ie, the authorization header is in the redirected request.</p> <p>Problem found using SDK 1.6.0 &amp; 1.6.1 and iOS 4.2 (device and simulator).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
