Description: """"We need to be mapping the TopTi namespace into the toplevel Titanium namespace for iOS, so that the correct coverage information is being generated.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5018,12,"""Coverage: Allow blacklisting updates based on coverage """"deltas""""""","""""""We need to be able to update the backlists via the blacklister instead of just automatically updating them. In order to do this, we should have the ability to <USER>the """"""""delta"""""""" information generated as part of the coverage run, which gives data about what API points were added/removed - obviously we can remove blacklist info for API points that were deleted, and add in blacklists for API points that were added which fit the criteria for blacklisting by cross-referencing with the coverage matrix (if this data isn't available in the delta itself).""""""",Bug,"Title: Coverage: Allow blacklisting updates based on coverage """"deltas""""
Description: """"We need to be able to update the backlists via the blacklister instead of just automatically updating them. In order to do this, we should have the ability to <USER>the """"""""delta"""""""" information generated as part of the coverage run, which gives data about what API points were added/removed - obviously we can remove blacklist info for API points that were deleted, and add in blacklists for API points that were added which fit the criteria for blacklisting by cross-referencing with the coverage matrix (if this data isn't available in the delta itself).""""",title+description
TIMOB-5017,12,"""Coverage: Enable get/set autocreated functions for iOS, and allow the blacklist to remove them""","""""""This bug covers two things:    - We used to create get/set functions for iOS properties automatically in the coverage data, because this is done for us as part of the internal redirect (p.x= and p.setX() are equivalent, p.x (rvalue) and p.getX() are equivalent). This used to be done, so this is probably as easy as uncommenting something in coverage, or checking a property to see if it's get/set, etc.  Could possibly include some changes to the AST parser so that it detects RO/RW properties correctly.    - We need to blacklist those get/set functions which should NOT appear as part of the public API - it's debatable whether or not we should only have """"""""some"""""""" synonyms, but that is a parity discussion with Android. Until this is resolved, we need to be able to blacklist certain properties as """"""""nogetter"""""""" and """"""""nosetter"""""""".""""""",Bug,"Title: Coverage: Enable get/set autocreated functions for iOS, and allow the blacklist to remove them
Description: """"This bug covers two things: - We used to create get/set functions for iOS properties automatically in the coverage data, because this is done for us as part of the internal redirect (p.x= and p.setX() are equivalent, p.x (rvalue) and p.getX() are equivalent). This used to be done, so this is probably as easy as uncommenting something in coverage, or checking a property to see if it's get/set, etc. Could possibly include some changes to the AST parser so that it detects RO/RW properties correctly. - We need to blacklist those get/set functions which should NOT appear as part of the public API - it's debatable whether or not we should only have """"""""some"""""""" synonyms, but that is a parity discussion with Android. Until this is resolved, we need to be able to blacklist certain properties as """"""""nogetter"""""""" and """"""""nosetter"""""""".""""",title+description
TIMOB-5016,12,"""Coverage.py for iOS needs to properly detect sub-submodules""","""""""We need to ensure that sub-submodules (i.e. Ti.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle) are picked up in coverage, and are properly parsed/examined. They may be getting picked up right now, but processed in the wrong namespace.""""""",Bug,"Title: Coverage.py for iOS needs to properly detect sub-submodules
Description: """"We need to ensure that sub-submodules (i.e. Ti.UI.iPhone.ActivityIndicatorStyle) are picked up in coverage, and are properly parsed/examined. They may be getting picked up right now, but processed in the wrong namespace.""""",title+description
TIMOB-5015,12,"""Coverage.py for iOS needs to properly detect submodules""","""""""We need to make sure that the coverage script is picking up certain things as submodules, and not as proxies. This is the case for {{Ti.Network.Socket}} and {{Ti.UI.Clipboard}} in particular; these are two modules which don't seem to be getting picked up.""""""",Bug,"Title: Coverage.py for iOS needs to properly detect submodules
Description: """"We need to make sure that the coverage script is picking up certain things as submodules, and not as proxies. This is the case for {{Ti.Network.Socket}} and {{Ti.UI.Clipboard}} in particular; these are two modules which don't seem to be getting picked up.""""",title+description
