TIMOB-4983,12,"""Android: Support """"ant install"""" In the Build Scripts For Modules""","""""""h1. Feature  Add support to the build scripts to let you """"""""ant install"""""""" a module's example project from the terminal directly to the device. (Note that this is the parallel feature to """"""""ant run"""""""" launching the emulator with the generated project from the example.)    h2. Platform Support  Android first, and iOS later. I can program the Android side (and have successfully), but iOS is a bit beyond me. We'll need to split off another ticket.    h2. Pull Request  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/360""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support """"ant install"""" In the Build Scripts For Modules
Description: """"h1. Feature Add support to the build scripts to let you """"""""ant install"""""""" a module's example project from the terminal directly to the device. (Note that this is the parallel feature to """"""""ant run"""""""" launching the emulator with the generated project from the example.) h2. Platform Support Android first, and iOS later. I can program the Android side (and have successfully), but iOS is a bit beyond me. We'll need to split off another ticket. h2. Pull Request https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/360""""",title+description
TIMOB-4982,12,"""Geolocation not working consistently on Android WebView (with suggested patch)""","""""""My experience shows that geolocation doesn't work consistently in an Android WebView, even when {{android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION}} is added to {{tiapp.xml}}.     To replicate:    * Create simple app that loads a web page that uses geolocation APIs. In this case I used the KitchenSink app and changed the external URL in [web_views.js|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/demos/KitchenSink/Resources/examples/web_views.js] to a test page for W3C browser geolocation, http://code.google.com/apis/maps/documentation/javascript/examples/map-geolocation.html.  * Add to tiapp.xml:  ** {code:lang=xml}<uses-permission android:name=""""""""android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION"""""""" />  public void onGeolocationPermissionsShowPrompt(String origin, android.webkit.GeolocationPermissions.Callback callback) {       callback.invoke(origin, true, false);  }{code}  * Build and update {{titanium-ui.jar}}.  * Clean and build project and install new build to Android device.   * Open KitchenSink on Android device and go to Base UI > Views > Web Views > External URL. Geolocation test succeeds!  """"""",Bug,"Title: Geolocation not working consistently on Android WebView (with suggested patch)
Description: """"My experience shows that geolocation doesn't work consistently in an Android WebView, even when {{android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION}} is added to {{tiapp.xml}}. To replicate: * Create simple app that loads a web page that uses geolocation APIs. In this case I used the KitchenSink app and changed the external URL in [web_views.js|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/demos/KitchenSink/Resources/examples/web_views.js] to a test page for W3C browser geolocation, http://code.google.com/apis/maps/documentation/javascript/examples/map-geolocation.html. * Add to tiapp.xml: ** {code:lang=xml}<uses-permission android:name=""""""""android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION"""""""" /> public void onGeolocationPermissionsShowPrompt(String origin, android.webkit.GeolocationPermissions.Callback callback) { callback.invoke(origin, true, false); }{code} * Build and update {{titanium-ui.jar}}. * Clean and build project and install new build to Android device. * Open KitchenSink on Android device and go to Base UI > Views > Web Views > External URL. Geolocation test succeeds! """"",title+description
TIMOB-4981,12,"""Android: Analytics send ti.end a few minutes later than actual end""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run Analytics application from Barcelona/QE/TestFiles/FeatureTest  2. Launch application  3. Click Feature Event  4. Click Nav Event  5. Click Setting Event  6. Click User Event  7. Press the home button    Actual Result:  """"""""id"""""""":""""""""379ea05d-2fc2-4559-9be5-a9a200400a1a:443fca8aacd792be"""""""",""""""""sid"""""""":""""""""88a57ad8-e852-4cb0-bf1d-abb8bfd20572"""""""",""""""""ts"""""""":""""""""2011-08-10T21:16:17.430+0000"""""""",""""""""event"""""""":""""""""featureEvent.testButton"""""""",""""""""data"""""""":[],""""""""seq"""""""":3,""""""""mid"""""""":""""""""443fca8aacd792be"""""""",""""""""ver"""""""":""""""""2"""""""",""""""""type"""""""":""""""""app.feature"""""""",""""""""aguid"""""""":""""""""bc4628b5-99eb-4877-91df-aa9a4771920e""""""""}  {""""""""id"""""""":""""""""63b0cac6-a8b7-4653-8090-24685cd37c14:443fca8aacd792be"""""""",""""""""sid"""""""":""""""""88a57ad8-e852-4cb0-bf1d-abb8bfd20572"""""""",""""""""ts"""""""":""""""""2011-08-10T21:16:18.648+0000"""""""",""""""""event"""""""":""""""""navEvent.testButton"""""""",""""""""data"""""""":{""""""""to"""""""":""""""""there"""""""",""""""""data"""""""":[],""""""""event"""""""":""""""""navEvent.testButton"""""""",""""""""from"""""""":""""""""here""""""""},""""""""seq"""""""":4,""""""""mid"""""""":""""""""443fca8aacd792be"""""""",""""""""ver"""""""":""""""""2"""""""",""""""""type"""""""":""""""""app.nav"""""""",""""""""aguid"""""""":""""""""bc4628b5-99eb-4877-91df-aa9a4771920e""""""""}  {""""""""id"""""""":""""""""954af0f2-4008-4ae5-89b1-215218dfcf79:443fca8aacd792be"""""""",""""""""sid"""""""":""""""""88a57ad8-e852-4cb0-bf1d-abb8bfd20572"""""""",""""""""ts"""""""":""""""""2011-08-10T21:16:19.846+0000"""""""",""""""""event"""""""":""""""""settingsEvent.testButton"""""""",""""""""data"""""""":[],""""""""seq"""""""":5,""""""""mid"""""""":""""""""443fca8aacd792be"""""""",""""""""ver