TIMOB-4922,12,"""Android: Fix eclipse build""","""""""We currently have a broken development model from Eclipse, mostly due to recent changes in ADT as well as various shortcomings in our ant build system and Eclipse. This needs to be fixed -- right now, debugging and building Titanium from Eclipse is almost entirely broken.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Fix eclipse build
Description: """"We currently have a broken development model from Eclipse, mostly due to recent changes in ADT as well as various shortcomings in our ant build system and Eclipse. This needs to be fixed -- right now, debugging and building Titanium from Eclipse is almost entirely broken.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4917,12,"""iOS: change Table View appendRow to support an array of rows or row data""","""""""Change Ti.UI.TableView.appendRow to support taking a array of row proxies or dictionary of creation args.  This change should be made in order to accommodate further implementation styles for table view that may improve performance.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: change Table View appendRow to support an array of rows or row data
Description: """"Change Ti.UI.TableView.appendRow to support taking a array of row proxies or dictionary of creation args. This change should be made in order to accommodate further implementation styles for table view that may improve performance.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4916,12,"""Android: change Table View appendRow to support an array of rows or row data""","""""""Change Ti.UI.TableView.appendRow to support taking a array of row proxies or dictionary of creation args.  This change should be made in order to accommodate further implementation styles for table view that may improve performance.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: change Table View appendRow to support an array of rows or row data
Description: """"Change Ti.UI.TableView.appendRow to support taking a array of row proxies or dictionary of creation args. This change should be made in order to accommodate further implementation styles for table view that may improve performance.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4915,12,"""iOS: Implement """"file"""" property on Titanium.Blob""","""""""We currently have a """"""""nativePath"""""""" property on Titanium.Blob that returns the file's path as a file:// URL, but iOS also exposes a """"""""path"""""""" property that returns the full path (without the URL prefix) that we need to match for parity.    UPDATE:  further discussion between iOS and Android teams decided that instead of a path property, we should instead expose a """"""""file"""""""" property that returns the File proxy that represents the blob data or return null if no valid file was found.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Implement """"file"""" property on Titanium.Blob
Description: """"We currently have a """"""""nativePath"""""""" property on Titanium.Blob that returns the file's path as a file:// URL, but iOS also exposes a """"""""path"""""""" property that returns the full path (without the URL prefix) that we need to match for parity. UPDATE: further discussion between iOS and Android teams decided that instead of a path property, we should instead expose a """"""""file"""""""" property that returns the File proxy that represents the blob data or return null if no valid file was found.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4913,12,"""Android: Drillbit needs to bump the default emulator to version 7 for SDK 1.7+""","""""""Drillbit is currently launching version 4 emulator and it is no longer supported with SDK 1.7 and above. User needs to self launch a different emulator for drillbit to work""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Drillbit needs to bump the default emulator to version 7 for SDK 1.7+
Description: """"Drillbit is currently launching version 4 emulator and it is no longer supported with SDK 1.7 and above. User needs to self launch a different emulator for drillbit to work""""",title+description
TIMOB-4912,12,"""Move Ti.UI.CoverflowView into Ti.UI.iOS.CoverflowView""","""""""Self-explanitory; Coverflow is an iOS-only UI element and needs to be moved into the iOS namespace. In the <USER>of doing so we need to make sure that the old Ti.UI.createCoverflowView() method is DEPRECATED but still functions until the next release.""""""",Bug,"Title: Move Ti.UI.CoverflowView into Ti.UI.iOS.CoverflowView
Description: """"Self-explanitory; Coverflow is an iOS-only UI element and needs to be moved into the iOS namespace. In the <USER>of doing so we need to make sure that the old Ti.UI.createCoverflowView() method is DEPRECATED but still functions until the next release.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4911,12,"""Move Ti.UI.Toolbar into Ti.UI.iOS.Toolbar""","""""""Self-explanitory; Toolbar is an iOS-only UI element and needs to be moved into the iOS namespace. In the <USER>of doing so we need to make sure that the old Ti.UI.createToolbar() method is DEPRECATED but still functions until the next release.""""""",Bug,"Title: Move Ti.UI.Toolbar into Ti.UI.iOS.Toolbar
Description: """"Self-explanitory; Toolbar is an iOS-only UI element and needs to be moved into the iOS namespace. In the <USER>of doing so we need to make sure that the old Ti.UI.createToolbar() method is DEPRECATED but still functions until the next release.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4910,12,"""iOS: Filter coverage from iOS to remove non-public APIs""","""""""Currently, the iOS API extraction tool extracts all APIs which match the function signature of those functions which are pubicly available. While this is useful for us to determine what we """"""""accidentally"""""""" expose, these methods/properties need to be backlisted in a JSON file (or dictionary, or something) for the coverage script, so that we can get more accurate coverage numbers.    This is expected to be an ongoing task, handled weekly with Marshall during the parity meetings, but there will need to be an initial pass on existing coverage to blacklist stuff we can identify right now.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Filter coverage from iOS to remove non-public APIs
Description: """"Currently, the iOS API extraction tool extracts all APIs which match the function signature of those functions which are pubicly available. While this is useful for us to determine what we """"""""accidentally"""""""" expose, these methods/properties need to be backlisted in a JSON file (or dictionary, or something) for the coverage script, so that we can get more accurate coverage numbers. This is expected to be an ongoing task, handled weekly with Marshall during the parity meetings, but there will need to be an initial pass on existing coverage to blacklist stuff we can identify right now.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4908,12,"""getPersonByID crashes if ID does not exist""","""""""If you try to reference Ti.Contacts.getPersonByID(); with an ID that is invalid, it crashes the application.  Using an if statement or a try/catch still crashes.  See example below:    {code:title=app.js}    var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow();    /*Use to find a valid ID  Ti.Contacts.showContacts({      animated: true,      selectedPerson: function(e) {          alert(e.person.recordId);      }  });  */    p = Ti.Contacts.getPersonByID(3);  alert(p.fullName);    win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: getPersonByID crashes if ID does not exist
Description: """"If you try to reference Ti.Contacts.getPersonByID(); with an ID that is invalid, it crashes the application. Using an if statement or a try/catch still crashes. See example below: {code:title=app.js} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); /*Use to find a valid ID Ti.Contacts.showContacts({ animated: true, selectedPerson: function(e) { alert(e.person.recordId); } }); */ p = Ti.Contacts.getPersonByID(3); alert(p.fullName); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-4907,12,"""Deprecate redundant functions in iOS Ti.Network""","""""""We need to deprecate the following functions on Ti.Network:    - addConnectivityListener  - removeConnectivityListener    These are aliases for add/removeEventListener('change',...)    Deprecation should probably be done via a DEPRECATE(in,removed) macro, where 'in' is a string representing a version number the function is deprecated in, and 'removed' indicating the version in which it will be removed. This function will log a warning of some type, although we may want to take other action as well.""""""",Bug,"Title: Deprecate redundant functions in iOS Ti.Network
Description: """"We need to deprecate the following functions on Ti.Network: - addConnectivityListener - removeConnectivityListener These are aliases for add/removeEventListener('change',...) Deprecation should probably be done via a DEPRECATE(in,removed) macro, where 'in' is a string representing a version number the function is deprecated in, and 'removed' indicating the version in which it will be removed. This function will log a warning of some type, although we may want to take other action as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4905,12,"""Test values of platform-specific Ti.Media constants (Ti.Media unit tests)""","""""""Where possible, we need to create tests to ensure the constant values off of the Ti.Media module obey the following:    - They are, in fact, constant (cannot be modified and/or even if modified, always return the same value)  - They align with """"""""expected"""""""" values where these are known; note that this may not be possible due to the iOS SDK changing values of constants between releases.""""""",Bug,"Title: Test values of platform-specific Ti.Media constants (Ti.Media unit tests)
Description: """"Where possible, we need to create tests to ensure the constant values off of the Ti.Media module obey the following: - They are, in fact, constant (cannot be modified and/or even if modified, always return the same value) - They align with """"""""expected"""""""" values where these are known; note that this may not be possible due to the iOS SDK changing values of constants between releases.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4904,12,"""Tooling: Add postbuild hook for builder plugins to iOS builder.py""","""""""We added postbuild functionality with this pull request:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/327    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Add postbuild hook for builder plugins to iOS builder.py
Description: """"We added postbuild functionality with this pull request: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/327 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4903,12,"""Android: Add postbuild hook for builder plugins""","""""""This was done with a community pull request:  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/327""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add postbuild hook for builder plugins
Description: """"This was done with a community pull request: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/327""""",title+description
TIMOB-4902,12,"""Android: webview.reload() on a webview that points to a local html file does not refresh""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Compile the attached application with app.js and webview.html  2. Press the Click me to reload view button    Actual:  Get the alert that it has been reloaded, but the webview never reloads    Expected:  Should get the alert and then reload the webview    Note:   Used 1.7 and 1.6, never seem to work""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: webview.reload() on a webview that points to a local html file does not refresh
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Compile the attached application with app.js and webview.html 2. Press the Click me to reload view button Actual: Get the alert that it has been reloaded, but the webview never reloads Expected: Should get the alert and then reload the webview Note: Used 1.7 and 1.6, never seem to work""""",title+description
TIMOB-4901,12,"""Tooling: Build scripts need to handle <guid/> tags appropriately""","""""""There is currently an issue (TISTUD-559) with XML serialization outputting empty XML tags when they have no contents, as opposed to a start tag/end tag pair. Some of our build scripts rely on end-tag searching (GUID placement for command-line builds and modules) and so we need to modify them so that they can handle empty tags.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: Build scripts need to handle <guid/> tags appropriately
Description: """"There is currently an issue (TISTUD-559) with XML serialization outputting empty XML tags when they have no contents, as opposed to a start tag/end tag pair. Some of our build scripts rely on end-tag searching (GUID placement for command-line builds and modules) and so we need to modify them so that they can handle empty tags. """"",title+description
TIMOB-4900,12,"""view images (for tabs of custom tabBar) not displayed in Tweetanium when FastDev enabled""","""""""When FastDev server is running, images (on/off) of the tabbar in Tweetanium are not displayed.  If the FastDev property is set to false in tiapp.xml, all images are displayed.    See [ApplicationWindow.js|https://github.com/<USER>titans/tweetanium/blob/master/mobile/Tweetanium/Resources/tweetanium/ui/ApplicationWindow.js]    Before running the project I removed the build directory and cleaned the project.  The project is installed in the default Titanium workspace folder in Windows 7.  In my case the first time doesn't show the images in the tabbar, only the one in the top-right corner (after closing the Account window) is showed correctly.    Setting the property """"""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" to false in tiapp.xml solved the problem.    I also find a workaround to work with FastDev server enabled by copying the tabbar images   to the platform specific directory of Android (Recources/android/images/res-hdpi etc.)""""""",Bug,"Title: view images (for tabs of custom tabBar) not displayed in Tweetanium when FastDev enabled
Description: """"When FastDev server is running, images (on/off) of the tabbar in Tweetanium are not displayed. If the FastDev property is set to false in tiapp.xml, all images are displayed. See [ApplicationWindow.js|https://github.com/<USER>titans/tweetanium/blob/master/mobile/Tweetanium/Resources/tweetanium/ui/ApplicationWindow.js] Before running the project I removed the build directory and cleaned the project. The project is installed in the default Titanium workspace folder in Windows 7. In my case the first time doesn't show the images in the tabbar, only the one in the top-right corner (after closing the Account window) is showed correctly. Setting the property """"""""ti.android.fastdev"""""""" to false in tiapp.xml solved the problem. I also find a workaround to work with FastDev server enabled by copying the tabbar images to the platform specific directory of Android (Recources/android/images/res-hdpi etc.)""""",title+description
