TIMOB-4811,12,"""Expose new APIs from Layout spec""","""""""Need to expose all of the new APIs from the layout spec, and ensure their functionality and ability to plug into the internal layout API layer in the correct manner.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Expose new APIs from Layout spec
Description: """"Need to expose all of the new APIs from the layout spec, and ensure their functionality and ability to plug into the internal layout API layer in the correct manner.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4810,12,"""Update Horizontal/Vertical layouts to use the new Layout manager (& Composite rules)""","""""""Need to update the Horizontal and Vertical layouts to use the new layout management system. This task can theoretically be completed as soon as the Graphite API is finalized/approved (or mostly so), but cannot be functional tested until the API layer is complete. Will also help to have the Composite rules finished beforehand because they largely inform how Horiz/Vert work (and rules for H/V are even included in the composite behavior spec, I believe).""""""",New Feature,"Title: Update Horizontal/Vertical layouts to use the new Layout manager (& Composite rules)
Description: """"Need to update the Horizontal and Vertical layouts to use the new layout management system. This task can theoretically be completed as soon as the Graphite API is finalized/approved (or mostly so), but cannot be functional tested until the API layer is complete. Will also help to have the Composite rules finished beforehand because they largely inform how Horiz/Vert work (and rules for H/V are even included in the composite behavior spec, I believe).""""",title+description
TIMOB-4809,12,"""iOS: Implement a generalized ignore file mechanism for the copy resources phase of compiler.py""","""""""Developers often have cruft sitting in their Resource folders that they don't want copied into their product Resource directory.  Additionally, we get requests from customers and the field (including pull requests) asking for changes to compiler.py to exclude their files (i.e. .bundle directories, etc.).  We should implement a generalized solution, akin to a .gitignore file that compiler.py refers to for ignoring files during the copy resources phase.  Formatting should be simple; one pattern per line matched against the files for exclusion.  I'd like to see this in 1.8 so I can disregard and close a pending pull request and avoid further pull requests and possible Jira filings.""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Implement a generalized ignore file mechanism for the copy resources phase of compiler.py
Description: """"Developers often have cruft sitting in their Resource folders that they don't want copied into their product Resource directory. Additionally, we get requests from customers and the field (including pull requests) asking for changes to compiler.py to exclude their files (i.e. .bundle directories, etc.). We should implement a generalized solution, akin to a .gitignore file that compiler.py refers to for ignoring files during the copy resources phase. Formatting should be simple; one pattern per line matched against the files for exclusion. I'd like to see this in 1.8 so I can disregard and close a pending pull request and avoid further pull requests and possible Jira filings.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4808,12,"""Develop API/spec for new UI Layout layer (""""Graphite"""")""","""""""Need to sketch out the APIs for the new drawing layer for layouts, and get feedback from both Marshall and the rest of the iOS team as to feasibility, coverage of issues we might expect, fit with our existing API (expected to be low...) and other assorted ridiculousness.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Develop API/spec for new UI Layout layer (""""Graphite"""")
Description: """"Need to sketch out the APIs for the new drawing layer for layouts, and get feedback from both Marshall and the rest of the iOS team as to feasibility, coverage of issues we might expect, fit with our existing API (expected to be low...) and other assorted ridiculousness.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4807,12,"""Android: Ti.Buffer.byteOrder should return system byte order by default""","""""""We need to make sure that byteOrder is set to the native system byte order by default for created buffers.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.Buffer.byteOrder should return system byte order by default
Description: """"We need to make sure that byteOrder is set to the native system byte order by default for created buffers.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4804,12,"""iOS: the 'value' of the text field is not cleared when clearOnEdit: is true, unless you type in a new value manually""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch KS -> Phone -> Music -> Music query  2. Press Query! [Check your log] button - See results in log  3. Type a title to filter to return a single value - See results in log  4. Tap the text field to clear data - Press query again    Actual Result:  Returns the single value again    Expected Value  Should query all value as empty string, but it is keeping value of text field even after clearing the text field""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: the 'value' of the text field is not cleared when clearOnEdit: is true, unless you type in a new value manually
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch KS -> Phone -> Music -> Music query 2. Press Query! [Check your log] button - See results in log 3. Type a title to filter to return a single value - See results in log 4. Tap the text field to clear data - Press query again Actual Result: Returns the single value again Expected Value Should query all value as empty string, but it is keeping value of text field even after clearing the text field""""",title+description
TIMOB-4803,12,"""Android: validate xml.js drillbit test and remove unnecessary bug-related comments after all pending bug pull requests have been merged.""","""""""After all linked bugs have had their pull requests put in and are resolved, do final passthrough of xml.js to verify everything works and also remove comments that refer to the resolved bugs.""""""",Story,"Title: Android: validate xml.js drillbit test and remove unnecessary bug-related comments after all pending bug pull requests have been merged.
Description: """"After all linked bugs have had their pull requests put in and are resolved, do final passthrough of xml.js to verify everything works and also remove comments that refer to the resolved bugs.""""",title+description
