TIMOB-4773,12,"""iOS: Size text area is utilizing the entire parent space even when the content does not require the entire space""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run test 1069 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/UI+Composite+Layout+Behavior+Test+Case    Actual Result:  For the first letter test, it should not take up the entire parent space    Expected Result:  Should display some green space and only utilize the space needed for that letter  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Size text area is utilizing the entire parent space even when the content does not require the entire space
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run test 1069 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/UI+Composite+Layout+Behavior+Test+Case Actual Result: For the first letter test, it should not take up the entire parent space Expected Result: Should display some green space and only utilize the space needed for that letter """"",title+description
TIMOB-4772,12,"""Android: Size text area is not enlarging the area to display all the text, and is not scrollable""","""""""Steps To Reproduce:  1. Run test 1069 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/UI+Composite+Layout+Behavior+Test+Case    Actual Result:  Text area too small, cannot scroll    Expected Result:  Should be able to display all the text in the area and allow it to scroll    iOS:  utilizes the entire window space even when not needed, but allows scrolling for the longer text  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Size text area is not enlarging the area to display all the text, and is not scrollable
Description: """"Steps To Reproduce: 1. Run test 1069 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/UI+Composite+Layout+Behavior+Test+Case Actual Result: Text area too small, cannot scroll Expected Result: Should be able to display all the text in the area and allow it to scroll iOS: utilizes the entire window space even when not needed, but allows scrolling for the longer text """"",title+description
