TIMOB-4753,12,"""Kitchensink: Scrolling table quickly in Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update row objects causes speech bubble redraw to occasionally occur out of place""","""""""While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update row objects, I was scrolling the table view and when you do this quickly, the image located in each row (a blue speech bubble) is rendered about an inch to the left of where it should. This happens only when scrolling quickly, and only on some attempts.    Steps to Reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.7.2  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update row objects and launch test  3) Scroll rapidly up and down      Result:  Speech bubble image is not always rendered on the right border of the row    Expected result:  Speech bubbles rendered at the right border every time    Notes:""""""",Bug,"Title: Kitchensink: Scrolling table quickly in Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update row objects causes speech bubble redraw to occasionally occur out of place
Description: """"While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update row objects, I was scrolling the table view and when you do this quickly, the image located in each row (a blue speech bubble) is rendered about an inch to the left of where it should. This happens only when scrolling quickly, and only on some attempts. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.2 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Update row objects and launch test 3) Scroll rapidly up and down Result: Speech bubble image is not always rendered on the right border of the row Expected result: Speech bubbles rendered at the right border every time Notes:""""",title+description
TIMOB-4752,12,"""AudioPlayer progress should be measured in milliseconds""","""""""Via mail from <USER>    Given that every other time unit in our platform is measured in milliseconds - this should have been treated as a BUG in iOS, not a consistency problem in Android.  Now everything is a MS except this property, which is SEC.  I'd suggest a revert and consider this a regression.    http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4019  """"""",Bug,"Title: AudioPlayer progress should be measured in milliseconds
Description: """"Via mail from <USER> Given that every other time unit in our platform is measured in milliseconds - this should have been treated as a BUG in iOS, not a consistency problem in Android. Now everything is a MS except this property, which is SEC. I'd suggest a revert and consider this a regression. http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4019 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4751,12,"""Random crash using getElementsByTagName to parse XML""","""""""The application randomly crashes while trying to parse xml documents by calling .getElementsByTagName    I'm attaching my example app.js ad the stacktrace.txt  I'm using 1000 iterations to be sure to tirgger the bug on my system, if you can't see it try with 10k iterations. In a real and more complex application it happens sooner.    It does not happen with Ti 1.6.2 <-   It still happens in 1.7.2 after fixing http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4610    I posted this problem also on community Q&A at : http://developer.<USER>com/question/122828/badaccess-using-getelementsbytag-in-a-event-handler    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');    var app = {};    var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   title: """"""""Nope""""""""  });    var test = Ti.XML.parseString (""""""""<stops><lat>ciao</lat></stops>"""""""");  var result = [];  function crashIt () {   for (var i=0; i<1000; i++) {    var foo = test.getElementsByTagName (""""""""lat"""""""").item (0).text;    result.push (i + """""""" - """""""" + foo);   }  }  crashIt ();    //Ti.API.debug (result);    win.open ();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Random crash using getElementsByTagName to parse XML
Description: """"The application randomly crashes while trying to parse xml documents by calling .getElementsByTagName I'm attaching my example app.js ad the stacktrace.txt I'm using 1000 iterations to be sure to tirgger the bug on my system, if you can't see it try with 10k iterations. In a real and more complex application it happens sooner. It does not happen with Ti 1.6.2 <- It still happens in 1.7.2 after fixing http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4610 I posted this problem also on community Q&A at : http://developer.<USER>com/question/122828/badaccess-using-getelementsbytag-in-a-event-handler {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var app = {}; var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: """"""""Nope"""""""" }); var test = Ti.XML.parseString (""""""""<stops><lat>ciao</lat></stops>""""""""); var result = []; function crashIt () { for (var i=0; i<1000; i++) { var foo = test.getElementsByTagName (""""""""lat"""""""").item (0).text; result.push (i + """""""" - """""""" + foo); } } crashIt (); //Ti.API.debug (result); win.open (); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-4750,12,"""Android: images in a project using fastDev do not show in a webView""","""""""Step 0: Make sure fastDev is enabled  Step 1: Add an image to your project (don't point to appicon.png, add another image)  Step 2: Run the app below  Step 3: Notice the image in the webview does not display    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({});  var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({    image: 'checked.png',    top: 100  });  var webview = Titanium.UI.createWebView({      html: '<html><body><img src=""""""""checked.png""""""""></body></html>',    });  win.add(webview);  win.add(iv);  win.open();  {code}    h3. Workaround  After you add images to your project, disable fastdev and build it once, and the reenable fastdev.    h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-777584""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: images in a project using fastDev do not show in a webView
Description: """"Step 0: Make sure fastDev is enabled Step 1: Add an image to your project (don't point to appicon.png, add another image) Step 2: Run the app below Step 3: Notice the image in the webview does not display {code:title=app.js} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({}); var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'checked.png', top: 100 }); var webview = Titanium.UI.createWebView({ html: '<html><body><img src=""""""""checked.png""""""""></body></html>', }); win.add(webview); win.add(iv); win.open(); {code} h3. Workaround After you add images to your project, disable fastdev and build it once, and the reenable fastdev. h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-777584""""",title+description
