TIMOB-4727,12,"""KitchenSink: Repeatedly launching Mashups>SOAP test results in logged warnings of messaging a dead thread""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink I noticed some new log behavior I hadn't seen in other passes. I was able to find a reproducible case by launching the Mashups>SOAP test, hitting back and launching the test again. By approximately the third attempt, the following will appear in the log:    07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): Handler{40acfa10} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): java.lang.RuntimeException: Handler{40acfa10} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at android.os.MessageQueue.enqueueMessage(MessageQueue.java:196)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at android.os.Handler.sendMessageAtTime(Handler.java:457)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at android.os.Handler.sendMessageDelayed(Handler.java:430)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at android.os.Handler.post(Handler.java:248)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:162)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:96)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:91)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:471)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:462)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.setReadyState(TiHTTPClient.java:494)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$ClientRunnable.run(TiHTTPClient.java:1013)  07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534):     at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1019)    Steps to Reproduce:  1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2  2) Ensure you are loggings  3) Navigate to Mashups>SOAP  4) Tap """"""""back""""""""  5) Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you see the log output      Result:  Warnings logged:  java.lang.RuntimeException: Handler{40aa1810} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread    Expected results:  No warnings logged  """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Repeatedly launching Mashups>SOAP test results in logged warnings of messaging a dead thread
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink I noticed some new log behavior I hadn't seen in other passes. I was able to find a reproducible case by launching the Mashups>SOAP test, hitting back and launching the test again. By approximately the third attempt, the following will appear in the log: 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): Handler{40acfa10} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): java.lang.RuntimeException: Handler{40acfa10} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at android.os.MessageQueue.enqueueMessage(MessageQueue.java:196) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at android.os.Handler.sendMessageAtTime(Handler.java:457) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at android.os.Handler.sendMessageDelayed(Handler.java:430) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at android.os.Handler.post(Handler.java:248) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:162) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:96) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:91) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:471) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:462) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.setReadyState(TiHTTPClient.java:494) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$ClientRunnable.run(TiHTTPClient.java:1013) 07-19 11:22:28.157: WARN/MessageQueue(2534): at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1019) Steps to Reproduce: 1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2 2) Ensure you are loggings 3) Navigate to Mashups>SOAP 4) Tap """"""""back"""""""" 5) Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you see the log output Result: Warnings logged: java.lang.RuntimeException: Handler{40aa1810} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread Expected results: No warnings logged """"",title+description
TIMOB-4726,12,"""iOS: Bug when try to compile a mobile_sdk with spaces in the name""","""""""1. Rename mobile sdk and add spaces in it. /Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/     (e.g: 1.8.0 pull 241)  2. Create a project in TitaniumStudio.  3. Run the project using the sdk with the space in the name  4. Error Seen Currently:    [ERROR]   [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):    File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1139, in main      execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % link_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=__LOG__ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s %s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version,debugstr)],False)    File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1057, in execute_xcode      output = run.run(args,False,False,o)    File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run      sys.exit(rc)  SystemExit: 65    5. Desired Error after Fixes:    [ERROR]    Error: Space available in the sdk name.   Error: sdk """"""""1.8.0 pull 241"""""""" does not exist.    SystemExit: 65""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Bug when try to compile a mobile_sdk with spaces in the name
Description: """"1. Rename mobile sdk and add spaces in it. /Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/ (e.g: 1.8.0 pull 241) 2. Create a project in TitaniumStudio. 3. Run the project using the sdk with the space in the name 4. Error Seen Currently: [ERROR] [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1139, in main execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % link_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=__LOG__ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s %s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version,debugstr)],False) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1057, in execute_xcode output = run.run(args,False,False,o) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65 5. Desired Error after Fixes: [ERROR] Error: Space available in the sdk name. Error: sdk """"""""1.8.0 pull 241"""""""" does not exist. SystemExit: 65""""",title+description
TIMOB-4725,12,"""KitchenSink: unpausing a paused stream fails to function in Phone>Sound>Remote streaming""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink, Phone>Sound>Remote streaming, I Started the test and began the streaming.I then pressed the """"""""Pause streaming"""""""" button. After the stream paused, I pressed """"""""Unpause streaming"""""""". Nothing happened.     This also occurs with 1.7.1.     Steps to Reproduce:  1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2  2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote streaming  3) Start the stream  4) While the stream is running, pause the stream  5) Attempt to unpause the stream    Result:  Nothing happens and the stream does not continue    Expected results:  The stream continues from the point where is was paused    Notes:  Also occurs with 1.7.1""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: unpausing a paused stream fails to function in Phone>Sound>Remote streaming
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Phone>Sound>Remote streaming, I Started the test and began the streaming.I then pressed the """"""""Pause streaming"""""""" button. After the stream paused, I pressed """"""""Unpause streaming"""""""". Nothing happened. This also occurs with 1.7.1. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote streaming 3) Start the stream 4) While the stream is running, pause the stream 5) Attempt to unpause the stream Result: Nothing happens and the stream does not continue Expected results: The stream continues from the point where is was paused Notes: Also occurs with 1.7.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-4724,12,"""KitchenSink: Runtime error after selecting gallery image in Base UI>Views>Email Dialog""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Email Dialog, I Started the test, the gallery opened to choose a photo attachment and I selected one. When I did this, I got a runtime error dialog.    This does not occur with 1.7.1. This also occurs on the Galaxy Tab.    Steps to Reproduce:  1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2  2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog  3) Select a photo from the gallery    Result:  Runtime error    Expected results:  image selected and email prepared    Notes:  See attached image  Does not occur with 1.7.1""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Runtime error after selecting gallery image in Base UI>Views>Email Dialog
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Email Dialog, I Started the test, the gallery opened to choose a photo attachment and I selected one. When I did this, I got a runtime error dialog. This does not occur with 1.7.1. This also occurs on the Galaxy Tab. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog 3) Select a photo from the gallery Result: Runtime error Expected results: image selected and email prepared Notes: See attached image Does not occur with 1.7.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-4723,12,"""KitchenSink: Basic Picker has some graphic corruption on Nexus S in landscape""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink in landscape mode, Controls>Picker>Basic Picker, I noticed there were some lines on the picker itself. The lines are not present in portrait mode. The lines change slightly when the picker is pressed and held. See attached images for details.    I did not see the same behavior on Galaxy Tab (2.3.4)    Steps to Reproduce:  1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2  2) Navigate to Controls>Picker>Basic Picker  3) Rotate to Landscape  4) Observe and the tap and hold the picker    Result:  Unexpected lines are visible in landscape but not portrait    Expected results:  No lines    Notes:  See attached images  Also occurs with 1.7.1""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Basic Picker has some graphic corruption on Nexus S in landscape
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink in landscape mode, Controls>Picker>Basic Picker, I noticed there were some lines on the picker itself. The lines are not present in portrait mode. The lines change slightly when the picker is pressed and held. See attached images for details. I did not see the same behavior on Galaxy Tab (2.3.4) Steps to Reproduce: 1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2 2) Navigate to Controls>Picker>Basic Picker 3) Rotate to Landscape 4) Observe and the tap and hold the picker Result: Unexpected lines are visible in landscape but not portrait Expected results: No lines Notes: See attached images Also occurs with 1.7.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-4722,12,"""Twitter, Galaxy pad - scrolling very slowly results in jerky stuttered scrolling""","""""""1.Ks > mashups > twitter  2.place your finger on the table view and very slowly scroll up or down    results: stuttered, jerky scrolling. Speed it up a little and it gets better. Not seen on any other devices, been there since at least 1.7.0""""""",Bug,"Title: Twitter, Galaxy pad - scrolling very slowly results in jerky stuttered scrolling
Description: """"1.Ks > mashups > twitter 2.place your finger on the table view and very slowly scroll up or down results: stuttered, jerky scrolling. Speed it up a little and it gets better. Not seen on any other devices, been there since at least 1.7.0""""",title+description
TIMOB-4721,12,"""KitchenSink: Some text fields are not displaying tops of hint text or inputted characters""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Window layout, I noticed the hint text (or any text) was cut off at the tops.     Steps to Reproduce:  1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2  2) Navigate to Base UI>Window layout  3) Observe the text field    Result:  Text is cut off at the top. Very little of the cross-bar of a capital """"""""T"""""""" is visible.    Expected results:  Fully visible text    Notes:  See attached image  Also occurs with 1.7.1  """"""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink: Some text fields are not displaying tops of hint text or inputted characters
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Window layout, I noticed the hint text (or any text) was cut off at the tops. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Launch KS, built with 1.7.2 2) Navigate to Base UI>Window layout 3) Observe the text field Result: Text is cut off at the top. Very little of the cross-bar of a capital """"""""T"""""""" is visible. Expected results: Fully visible text Notes: See attached image Also occurs with 1.7.1 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4720,12,"""Android: Unexpose toBase64 in Titanium.Blob""","""""""""""""""toBase64"""""""" was accidentally exposed on Titanium.Blob (and shouldn't have been)    Use `Titanium.Utils.base64encode` instead.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Unexpose toBase64 in Titanium.Blob
Description: """"""""""""toBase64"""""""" was accidentally exposed on Titanium.Blob (and shouldn't have been) Use `Titanium.Utils.base64encode` instead.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4719,12,"""Android: Implement """"file"""" property on Titanium.Blob""","""""""We currently have a """"""""nativePath"""""""" property on Titanium.Blob that returns the file's path as a file:// URL, but iOS also exposes a """"""""path"""""""" property that returns the full path (without the URL prefix) that we need to match for parity.    UPDATE:  further discussion between iOS and Android teams decided that instead of a path property, we should instead expose a """"""""file"""""""" property that returns the File proxy that represents the blob data or return null if no valid file was found.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Implement """"file"""" property on Titanium.Blob
Description: """"We currently have a """"""""nativePath"""""""" property on Titanium.Blob that returns the file's path as a file:// URL, but iOS also exposes a """"""""path"""""""" property that returns the full path (without the URL prefix) that we need to match for parity. UPDATE: further discussion between iOS and Android teams decided that instead of a path property, we should instead expose a """"""""file"""""""" property that returns the File proxy that represents the blob data or return null if no valid file was found.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4718,12,"""Android: CharacterData.substringData - If the sum of offset and count exceeds the length exception is thrown instead of returning entire string""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run XML test case for drillbit     Actual Result:  CData fails when the sum of offset and count exceeds length    Expected Result:  Should return the entire string""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: CharacterData.substringData - If the sum of offset and count exceeds the length exception is thrown instead of returning entire string
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run XML test case for drillbit Actual Result: CData fails when the sum of offset and count exceeds length Expected Result: Should return the entire string""""",title+description
TIMOB-4717,12,"""Android: Implement """"ok"""" and """"okid"""" in Titanium.UI.AlertDialog""","""""""iOS implements the """"""""ok"""""""" property to allow setting the OK button's label. """"""""okid"""""""" is also exposed to allow the property to be pulled from locale strings""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Implement """"ok"""" and """"okid"""" in Titanium.UI.AlertDialog
Description: """"iOS implements the """"""""ok"""""""" property to allow setting the OK button's label. """"""""okid"""""""" is also exposed to allow the property to be pulled from locale strings""""",title+description
