TIMOB-4709,12,"""Android: XML document.getElementsByTagNameNS seems not to work""","""""""Sample XML, put this in a test app's Resources folder:    {code:title=with_ns.xml}  <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?>  <response xmlns:abc=""""""""http://example.com"""""""">      <something>123</something>      <something>456</something>      <abc:cake>yummy</abc:cake>      <abc:cake>very yummy</abc:cake>      <abc:pie>also yummy</abc:pie>  </response>      The log message will say """"""""Matching elements: 0.0"""""""".  It should be 2.0.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: XML document.getElementsByTagNameNS seems not to work
Description: """"Sample XML, put this in a test app's Resources folder: {code:title=with_ns.xml} <?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""UTF-8""""""""?> <response xmlns:abc=""""""""http://example.com""""""""> <something>123</something> <something>456</something> <abc:cake>yummy</abc:cake> <abc:cake>very yummy</abc:cake> <abc:pie>also yummy</abc:pie> </response> The log message will say """"""""Matching elements: 0.0"""""""". It should be 2.0.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4708,12,"""Win 7 Only: Fastdev manually stopped and application relaunched takes a long time to get connection time out warning message and fails occassionally""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch an application to emulator from TiStudio (Fastdev server should start)  2. Manually stop the fastdev server with 'titanium fastdev stop'  3. Press the home button from emulator  4. Relaunch the application from emulator    Actual Result:  Takes ~2-3 minute to relaunch to see the warning Warning: Fastdev mode is disabled. Error Message: Connection timed out, occassionally it will crash the application    Expected   Should launch without crashing    Note:  In 1.7.1 it takes longer to launch than Mac but did not encounter crash""""""",Bug,"Title: Win 7 Only: Fastdev manually stopped and application relaunched takes a long time to get connection time out warning message and fails occassionally
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch an application to emulator from TiStudio (Fastdev server should start) 2. Manually stop the fastdev server with 'titanium fastdev stop' 3. Press the home button from emulator 4. Relaunch the application from emulator Actual Result: Takes ~2-3 minute to relaunch to see the warning Warning: Fastdev mode is disabled. Error Message: Connection timed out, occassionally it will crash the application Expected Should launch without crashing Note: In 1.7.1 it takes longer to launch than Mac but did not encounter crash""""",title+description
TIMOB-4707,12,"""Android: XML Document.getElementById(id) causes NPE if id doesn't exist""","""""""Failcase app.js:    {code:title=app.js}  var doc = Ti.XML.parseString(""""""""<a/>"""""""");  var elem = doc.getElementById(""""""""no_such_thing""""""""); // NPE  {code}    According to spec (http://www.w3.org/TR/2000/REC-DOM-Level-2-Core-20001113/core.html#i-Document) passing {{getElementById}} an ID that does not exist should result in null being returned.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: XML Document.getElementById(id) causes NPE if id doesn't exist
Description: """"Failcase app.js: {code:title=app.js} var doc = Ti.XML.parseString(""""""""<a/>""""""""); var elem = doc.getElementById(""""""""no_such_thing""""""""); // NPE {code} According to spec (http://www.w3.org/TR/2000/REC-DOM-Level-2-Core-20001113/core.html#i-Document) passing {{getElementById}} an ID that does not exist should result in null being returned.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4706,12,"""Android: Cannot debug an application while using require('some_js_module')""","""""""h2.Problem  Cannot debug an application in the Android emulator while using a require('some_js_module') in the application    h3.Steps to reproduce  Step 1: Run the code below.    Step 2: Run Indie bug mode and watch it crash.    h3.Console log when debugging (Crash)    The following is logged when debugging (trace level):        h3.Reproduction code  {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}  // app.js  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor: 'blue'  });    var ui = require('ui');   var button = Ti.UI.createButton({    title: 'Test',    top: 20,    height: 50,    width: 200  });  button.addEventListener('click', function(e){    ui.alertIt('hi');  });  win.add(button);  win.open();    // ui.js  exports.alertIt = function(e) {    alert(e);  };      ...then create a ui.js file and put the following inside    {code:title=ui.js|borderStyle=solid}  exports.alertIt = function(e) {    alert(e);  };  {code}    ... then try to debug the application on Android    ...the debugger throws an exception as soon as it reaches var ui = require('ui'); and the application stops there.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot debug an application while using require('some_js_module')
Description: """"h2.Problem Cannot debug an application in the Android emulator while using a require('some_js_module') in the application h3.Steps to reproduce Step 1: Run the code below. Step 2: Run Indie bug mode and watch it crash. h3.Console log when debugging (Crash) The following is logged when debugging (trace level): h3.Reproduction code {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} // app.js var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'blue' }); var ui = require('ui'); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Test', top: 20, height: 50, width: 200 }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e){ ui.alertIt('hi'); }); win.add(button); win.open(); // ui.js exports.alertIt = function(e) { alert(e); }; ...then create a ui.js file and put the following inside {code:title=ui.js|borderStyle=solid} exports.alertIt = function(e) { alert(e); }; {code} ... then try to debug the application on Android ...the debugger throws an exception as soon as it reaches var ui = require('ui'); and the application stops there.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4705,12,"""Android: Reading XML document doctype property causes NPE when there is no doctype""","""""""  Fail case app.js:    {code:title=app.js}  var doc = Ti.XML.parseString(""""""""<a/>"""""""");  var x = doc.doctype; // NPE  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Reading XML document doctype property causes NPE when there is no doctype
