TIMOB-4697,12,"""iOS: Analytics - settingsEvent is returning a  [WARN] Exception in event callback.""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run 1005 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan  2. view console logs    Actual Behavior:  Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: [WARN] Exception in event callback. {  Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>:     line = 1;  Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>:     message = """"""""-[NSCFString objectAtIndex:]: unrecognized selector sent to instance 0x31cf50"""""""";  Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>:     sourceId = 76783640;  Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>:     sourceURL = """"""""file://localhost/var/mobile/Applications/BA07A6ED-77E6-46AA-8C50-C9F5713B703D/Analytics.app/app.js"""""""";  Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: }      Expected Behavior:  [INFO] Analytics->settingsEvent with event: settingsEvent.testButton    Note:  Also occur in 1.7.1""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Analytics - settingsEvent is returning a [WARN] Exception in event callback.
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run 1005 from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Analytics+Test+Plan 2. view console logs Actual Behavior: Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: [WARN] Exception in event callback. { Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: line = 1; Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: message = """"""""-[NSCFString objectAtIndex:]: unrecognized selector sent to instance 0x31cf50""""""""; Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: sourceId = 76783640; Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: sourceURL = """"""""file://localhost/var/mobile/Applications/BA07A6ED-77E6-46AA-8C50-C9F5713B703D/Analytics.app/app.js""""""""; Fri Jul 15 12:55:18 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>analytics[0xe55][35513] <Notice>: } Expected Behavior: [INFO] Analytics->settingsEvent with event: settingsEvent.testButton Note: Also occur in 1.7.1""""",title+description
TIMOB-4696,12,"""iOS: Cannot retrieve property value set in tiapp.xml using Ti.App.Properties API""","""""""We cannot retrieve the property value set in tiapp.xml using Ti.App.properties API even though it is documented in the WIKI.  http://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/tiapp.xml+and+timodule.xml+Reference#tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-Applicationproperties    Step1: Copy the following code in app.js  {code:title='app.js'}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('white');    var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow();  alert(Ti.App.Properties.getString(""""""""appstate""""""""));  win.open();  {code}  Step2: Add the following line to tiapp.xml  <property name=""""""""appstate"""""""" type=""""""""string"""""""">DEV</property>  Step3: Run the app, and you can see the alert message is null.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot retrieve property value set in tiapp.xml using Ti.App.Properties API
Description: """"We cannot retrieve the property value set in tiapp.xml using Ti.App.properties API even though it is documented in the WIKI. http://wiki.<USER>org/display/guides/tiapp.xml+and+timodule.xml+Reference#tiapp.xmlandtimodule.xmlReference-Applicationproperties Step1: Copy the following code in app.js {code:title='app.js'} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('white'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); alert(Ti.App.Properties.getString(""""""""appstate"""""""")); win.open(); {code} Step2: Add the following line to tiapp.xml <property name=""""""""appstate"""""""" type=""""""""string"""""""">DEV</property> Step3: Run the app, and you can see the alert message is null. """"",title+description
TIMOB-4695,12,"""GlobalPoint coordinates do not update with rotation""","""""""The globalPoint coordinates returned from touch events on an element do not update once the device is rotated; when in portrait mode the X coordinate will increase as you touch from left-to-right, but if you switch to landscape mode the X coordinate becomes the Y coordinate, and vice versa. Sample code below; to reproduce, start in portrait mode and drag left to right (X coordinate increases as expected)... then flip into landscape and drag from left to right; X coordinate does not change as expected.    """"""",Bug,"Title: GlobalPoint coordinates do not update with rotation
Description: """"The globalPoint coordinates returned from touch events on an element do not update once the device is rotated; when in portrait mode the X coordinate will increase as you touch from left-to-right, but if you switch to landscape mode the X coordinate becomes the Y coordinate, and vice versa. Sample code below; to reproduce, start in portrait mode and drag left to right (X coordinate increases as expected)... then flip into landscape and drag from left to right; X coordinate does not change as expected. """"",title+description
TIMOB-4694,12,"""Android:  fix timeout error when running Android.UI test in drillbit.""",,Bug,Title: Android: fix timeout error when running Android.UI test in drillbit.,title-only
TIMOB-4693,12,"""Drillbit: Fix too deep recursion errors in Android tests""","""""""In some tests (stream, yahoo, maybe others), There doesn't seem to be a stack size large enough to ensure that the dreaded """"""""too deep recursion"""""""" error doesn't occur for some of our more complicated async tests.""""""",Bug,"Title: Drillbit: Fix too deep recursion errors in Android tests
Description: """"In some tests (stream, yahoo, maybe others), There doesn't seem to be a stack size large enough to ensure that the dreaded """"""""too deep recursion"""""""" error doesn't occur for some of our more complicated async tests.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4692,12,"""iPad: downloading and then saving a large movie file crashes the app""","""""""h3.Problem  Once the app has downloaded a mp4 file, as large as 140MB, when attempting to save the file it hangs, then it looks like the iPad is being restarted.    Note: Smaller videos work well, no crashing (15MB)    h3.Associated HD Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-314474  """"""",Bug,"Title: iPad: downloading and then saving a large movie file crashes the app
Description: """"h3.Problem Once the app has downloaded a mp4 file, as large as 140MB, when attempting to save the file it hangs, then it looks like the iPad is being restarted. Note: Smaller videos work well, no crashing (15MB) h3.Associated HD Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-314474 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4691,12,"""Add support for local caching for XHR content (using disk cache)""","""""""This will dramatically improve performance and should function like a browser for support for client-side caching.    The latest version of ASIHttpRequest already supports this and I'm sure the android httpclient already has something similar.    """"""",New Feature,"Title: Add support for local caching for XHR content (using disk cache)
Description: """"This will dramatically improve performance and should function like a browser for support for client-side caching. The latest version of ASIHttpRequest already supports this and I'm sure the android httpclient already has something similar. """"",title+description
TIMOB-4689,12,"""iOS:globalPoint property is undefined in a tableview click event""","""""""The globalpoint property in a click event on a tableview is undefined. It does not return the screen co-ordinates.    Step1: Copy the below code in app.js  {code:title='app.js'}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('white');    var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow();  var data = [{title:""""""""Row 1""""""""},{title:""""""""Row 2""""""""}];  var table = Titanium.UI.createTableView({data:data,backgroundColor:'#336699'});    table.addEventListener('click',function(e)    {   Ti.API.info('globalpoint dictionary is...' +e.globalPoint);   Ti.API.info('X co-ordinate is'+e.x);   Ti.API.info('Y co-ordinate is'+e.y);  }    );  win.add(table);  win.open();  {code}  Step2: The globalPoint property is undefined    Workaround: to obtain the screen co-ordinates using e.x and e.y    h3.Associated helpdesk ticket:  http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-152774""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS:globalPoint property is undefined in a tableview click event
Description: """"The globalpoint property in a click event on a tableview is undefined. It does not return the screen co-ordinates. Step1: Copy the below code in app.js {code:title='app.js'} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('white'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); var data = [{title:""""""""Row 1""""""""},{title:""""""""Row 2""""""""}]; var table = Titanium.UI.createTableView({data:data,backgroundColor:'#336699'}); table.addEventListener('click',function(e) { Ti.API.info('globalpoint dictionary is...' +e.globalPoint); Ti.API.info('X co-ordinate is'+e.x); Ti.API.info('Y co-ordinate is'+e.y); } ); win.add(table); win.open(); {code} Step2: The globalPoint property is undefined Workaround: to obtain the screen co-ordinates using e.x and e.y h3.Associated helpdesk ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-152774""""",title+description
