TIMOB-4628,12,"""Android: Titanium.buildHash is off by one character""","""""""To reproduce the failcase (and test the fix):    * Run {{git log}} in your source folder and jot down the top build hash.    * Build and release the SDK if you haven't already.    * Build and run the app (app.js) below.    In the failcase, you'll see only a 6-character build hash which is missing the first character of the real hash.  In the fixed case, you'll see the full 7-character build hash.    Here's the app.js:    {code:title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Test',      backgroundColor:'#000',   exitOnClose: true  });  win.add(Ti.UI.createTextArea({   value: """"""""Build Hash: """""""" + Ti.buildHash +     """"""""\nBuild Date: """""""" + Ti.buildDate +     """"""""\nTitanium Version: """""""" + Ti.version,   top: """"""""25%"""""""",   left: """"""""10dp"""""""",   right: """"""""10dp"""""""",   height: """"""""200dp""""""""  }));  win.open();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Titanium.buildHash is off by one character
Description: """"To reproduce the failcase (and test the fix): * Run {{git log}} in your source folder and jot down the top build hash. * Build and release the SDK if you haven't already. * Build and run the app (app.js) below. In the failcase, you'll see only a 6-character build hash which is missing the first character of the real hash. In the fixed case, you'll see the full 7-character build hash. Here's the app.js: {code:title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#000', exitOnClose: true }); win.add(Ti.UI.createTextArea({ value: """"""""Build Hash: """""""" + Ti.buildHash + """"""""\nBuild Date: """""""" + Ti.buildDate + """"""""\nTitanium Version: """""""" + Ti.version, top: """"""""25%"""""""", left: """"""""10dp"""""""", right: """"""""10dp"""""""", height: """"""""200dp"""""""" })); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-4627,12,"""Android: Sample map code from TIMOB-4205 crashes on re-launch""","""""""Description:  While testing a fix for TIMOB-4205, I used the sample code to generate an app and installed on Xoom and Droid 1. After launching and checking the fix, I revisited the application and it crashed. I re-launched on the Droid 1 and had the same behavior. I cleaned the sdcard of the app folder and uninstalled via ADB. I updated my SDK to the latest 1_7_X and recompiled and installed. Same behavior. The only difference was on the Xoom it took me two tries to crash with the later SDK.     See attached logcat log    Steps to reproduce:  1) Create an application using the attached app.js  2) Install on android device  3) Launch the application  4) Tap """"""""Back"""""""" button to return to home  5) Launch application again  6) If no crash, repeat steps 4 and 5    Result:  Crash    Expected:  No crash""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Sample map code from TIMOB-4205 crashes on re-launch
Description: """"Description: While testing a fix for TIMOB-4205, I used the sample code to generate an app and installed on Xoom and Droid 1. After launching and checking the fix, I revisited the application and it crashed. I re-launched on the Droid 1 and had the same behavior. I cleaned the sdcard of the app folder and uninstalled via ADB. I updated my SDK to the latest 1_7_X and recompiled and installed. Same behavior. The only difference was on the Xoom it took me two tries to crash with the later SDK. See attached logcat log Steps to reproduce: 1) Create an application using the attached app.js 2) Install on android device 3) Launch the application 4) Tap """"""""Back"""""""" button to return to home 5) Launch application again 6) If no crash, repeat steps 4 and 5 Result: Crash Expected: No crash""""",title+description
