TIMOB-4554,12,"""iOS: Default Module build.py Doesn't Ignore .DS_Store when building documentation""","""""""h1. Problem  The build.py included with new modules will run any file in the documentation folder through markdown, including .DS_Store and other files that should be ignored. This results in an error being thrown, and the documentation not being generated.    h2. How To Reproduce  1. Create a new module for iOS  2. Copy a .DS_Store file in to the documentation directory  3. ./build.py and you will see an error message; the resulting zip will not have documentation in it    h2. Pull Request  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/184""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Default Module build.py Doesn't Ignore .DS_Store when building documentation
Description: """"h1. Problem The build.py included with new modules will run any file in the documentation folder through markdown, including .DS_Store and other files that should be ignored. This results in an error being thrown, and the documentation not being generated. h2. How To Reproduce 1. Create a new module for iOS 2. Copy a .DS_Store file in to the documentation directory 3. ./build.py and you will see an error message; the resulting zip will not have documentation in it h2. Pull Request https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/184""""",title+description
TIMOB-4552,12,"""iOS: Z-Index on Map Annotations and Rooutes""","""""""h3. Feature  This is a feature request to add z-index to the mapview's annotations and routes.    h3. Problem  When annotations and routes come together, it is unpredictable which one will be on top.    h3. Example Code    This is an example code from the customer requesting this feature    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Z-Index on Map Annotations and Rooutes
Description: """"h3. Feature This is a feature request to add z-index to the mapview's annotations and routes. h3. Problem When annotations and routes come together, it is unpredictable which one will be on top. h3. Example Code This is an example code from the customer requesting this feature """"",title+description
