TIMOB-4524,12,"""iOS: 3DMatrix toImage does not capture transformation""","""""""If you load an image and then transform it with a 3Dmatrix and then try to save the new image, the image is saved as the original.  Using the exact same code but using 2Dmatrix, it works as expected.    {code:title=app.js}  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var view = Ti.UI.createView({width:'auto', height:'auto'});    var img = Titanium.UI.createImageView({    height:43,    width:98,    top:10,    image:'KS_nav_ui.png', //image file    transform:Ti.UI.create3DMatrix().rotate(180, 0, 1, 0),    //transform:Ti.UI.create2DMatrix().rotate(180, 0, 1, 0),    preventDefaultImage: false  });    view.add(img);    win.add(view);    var save = Titanium.UI.createButton({    title:'Save',    width:120,    height:40,    bottom:20,    right:0,    });    save.addEventListener('click', function()  {                 alert('File saved here: '+Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory);             // file system        var photoname= new Date().getTime()+"""""""".png"""""""";        var f = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,photoname);        f.write(view.toImage());      });  win.add(save);     win.open();  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: 3DMatrix toImage does not capture transformation
Description: """"If you load an image and then transform it with a 3Dmatrix and then try to save the new image, the image is saved as the original. Using the exact same code but using 2Dmatrix, it works as expected. {code:title=app.js} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({width:'auto', height:'auto'}); var img = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ height:43, width:98, top:10, image:'KS_nav_ui.png', //image file transform:Ti.UI.create3DMatrix().rotate(180, 0, 1, 0), //transform:Ti.UI.create2DMatrix().rotate(180, 0, 1, 0), preventDefaultImage: false }); view.add(img); win.add(view); var save = Titanium.UI.createButton({ title:'Save', width:120, height:40, bottom:20, right:0, }); save.addEventListener('click', function() { alert('File saved here: '+Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory); // file system var photoname= new Date().getTime()+"""""""".png""""""""; var f = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,photoname); f.write(view.toImage()); }); win.add(save); win.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-4523,12,"""Upgrade to later version of JavaScriptCore""","""""""We need to upgrade our version of JavaScriptCore to gain performance enhancements and bug fixes from Apple.  This may also address TIMOB-4237.""""""",Story,"Title: Upgrade to later version of JavaScriptCore
Description: """"We need to upgrade our version of JavaScriptCore to gain performance enhancements and bug fixes from Apple. This may also address TIMOB-4237.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4522,12,"""Android 3.1 does not have default image of that size supported""","""""""Steps to Reproduce  1. Create a new titanium mobile project  2. Launch in a 3.0 Android Emulator    Actual Result:  The splash screen is gray    Expected Result:  Should be displaying our red branding splash screen""""""",Bug,"Title: Android 3.1 does not have default image of that size supported
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce 1. Create a new titanium mobile project 2. Launch in a 3.0 Android Emulator Actual Result: The splash screen is gray Expected Result: Should be displaying our red branding splash screen""""",title+description
TIMOB-4520,12,"""iOS: Empty TableView in TabGroup Doesn't Have Separators""","""""""h1. Problem  Empty TableViews normally have separators every 40ish pixels or so for the empty rows; but as of 1.7.0, they don't show up if the TableView is in a TabGroup.    h2. Expected Behavior  There should be separators every 40ish pixels, even in an empty TableView in a TabGroup.    h2. Example Code  Drop the following in an app.js and you will see a large white box. This is the table view. Touch """"""""2. Click Me"""""""" and a row will be added. Notice that the row has a separator, but that there aren't any other separators beneath it.  {code:title=bad app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      title: '1. Look @ White Table',      backgroundColor: '#000'  });    var table = Ti.UI.createTableView({      top: 0, height: 200,      separatorColor: 'green'  });  win.add(table);    var addRow = Ti.UI.createButton({      bottom: 0, height: 50,      title: '2. Click Me'  });  addRow.addEventListener('click', function() {      table.appendRow({ title: '3. Look @ My Separator' });  });  win.add(addRow);    var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();  tabGroup.addTab(Ti.UI.createTab({      window: win  }));  tabGroup.open();      h2. Screenshots  Attached.    h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-372136""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Empty TableView in TabGroup Doesn't Have Separators
Description: """"h1. Problem Empty TableViews normally have separators every 40ish pixels or so for the empty rows; but as of 1.7.0, they don't show up if the TableView is in a TabGroup. h2. Expected Behavior There should be separators every 40ish pixels, even in an empty TableView in a TabGroup. h2. Example Code Drop the following in an app.js and you will see a large white box. This is the table view. Touch """"""""2. Click Me"""""""" and a row will be added. Notice that the row has a separator, but that there aren't any other separators beneath it. {code:title=bad app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: '1. Look @ White Table', backgroundColor: '#000' }); var table = Ti.UI.createTableView({ top: 0, height: 200, separatorColor: 'green' }); win.add(table); var addRow = Ti.UI.createButton({ bottom: 0, height: 50, title: '2. Click Me' }); addRow.addEventListener('click', function() { table.appendRow({ title: '3. Look @ My Separator' }); }); win.add(addRow); var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); tabGroup.addTab(Ti.UI.createTab({ window: win })); tabGroup.open(); h2. Screenshots Attached. h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-372136""""",title+description
TIMOB-4519,12,"""Android: filename generated when pulling image from gallery to send via http request does not have a dot before extension""",,Bug,Title: Android: filename generated when pulling image from gallery to send via http request does not have a dot before extension,title-only
TIMOB-4518,12,"""Android: defaultImage doesn't appear when a remote image is loading on a ImageView""","""""""{quote}  h6.When I click the button, its event creates 20 remote images. The issue is happened when the images are  h6.loading but the defaultImage doesn't show.  {quote}    {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid}    var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor:'white'  });  var view = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'blue',    top:10,    bottom:10,    right:10,    left:10  });    var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({     title: 'Click',     top:230  });    button.addEventListener('click',function(e)  {    for (var i=0; i<30; i++)    {        var tempImage = Titanium.UI.createImageView({          defaultImage:""""""""android.png"""""""",          image:'http://www.hetemeel.com/einsteinshow.php?text=test' + i.toString(),          top:20,          width:200,          height:150        });        view.add(tempImage);    }  });  view.add(button);  win.add(view);  win.open();  {code}    h5.Associated Helpdesk Ticket:  http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-773771    h5.Associated Jira Ticket  http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-91""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: defaultImage doesn't appear when a remote image is loading on a ImageView
Description: """"{quote} h6.When I click the button, its event creates 20 remote images. The issue is happened when the images are h6.loading but the defaultImage doesn't show. {quote} {code:title=app.js|borderStyle=solid} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'white' }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'blue', top:10, bottom:10, right:10, left:10 }); var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({ title: 'Click', top:230 }); button.addEventListener('click',function(e) { for (var i=0; i<30; i++) { var tempImage = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ defaultImage:""""""""android.png"""""""", image:'http://www.hetemeel.com/einsteinshow.php?text=test' + i.toString(), top:20, width:200, height:150 }); view.add(tempImage); } }); view.add(button); win.add(view); win.open(); {code} h5.Associated Helpdesk Ticket: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-773771 h5.Associated Jira Ticket http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TC-91""""",title+description
TIMOB-4517,12,"""Android: default.png file is a gray image, should be the red default image""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Create a new titanium mobile project  2. Go to Project/Resources/android and open default.png    Actual Result:  Image is gray    Expected Result:  Should be the red default image""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: default.png file is a gray image, should be the red default image
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new titanium mobile project 2. Go to Project/Resources/android and open default.png Actual Result: Image is gray Expected Result: Should be the red default image""""",title+description
TIMOB-4516,12,"""Ti.Network.HTTPClient.validatesSecureCertificate initial value is 'undefined'""","""""""Exactly as described in bug title.  Initial value should be 'false' as per defined value on iOS; if this behavior should be different, please let me know.    Linked to iOS ticket for similar bug.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Network.HTTPClient.validatesSecureCertificate initial value is 'undefined'
Description: """"Exactly as described in bug title. Initial value should be 'false' as per defined value on iOS; if this behavior should be different, please let me know. Linked to iOS ticket for similar bug.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4515,12,"""Android: Drillbit database test fails in Honeycomb because field(index) does not raise exception when index is out of bounds""","""""""Weirdly, {{AbstractWindowedCursor.isNull(index)}} returns {{true}} when {{index}} is out of bounds.  So in our API, {{rs.field(9999)}} (where rs is a {{ResultSet}}) does not cause an error but rather returns null, even if there is only one column in the result set.  Our drillbit database suite test {{testDatabaseExceptions}} expects an exception to be thrown.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Drillbit database test fails in Honeycomb because field(index) does not raise exception when index is out of bounds
Description: """"Weirdly, {{AbstractWindowedCursor.isNull(index)}} returns {{true}} when {{index}} is out of bounds. So in our API, {{rs.field(9999)}} (where rs is a {{ResultSet}}) does not cause an error but rather returns null, even if there is only one column in the result set. Our drillbit database suite test {{testDatabaseExceptions}} expects an exception to be thrown.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4514,12,"""Add UITableViewCellStyleValue2 Table Styling To iOS SDK""","""""""It would be great if Titanium provided a standardized way to style a tableview to fit Apple's UITableViewCellStyleValue2 style (with row subtitle in blue at left and title in black on right). Providing a way to automatically render this specific style, which is consistent with Map Detail View, Individual Contact Detail View and Twitter Individual User View, I feel would vastly speed up app development.    More Info From Apple Developer: [UITableViewCellStyleValue2|http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#DOCUMENTATION/UIKit/Reference/UITableViewCell_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/c/econst/UITableViewCellStyleValue2]    !http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/DOCUMENTATION/UserExperience/Conceptual/TableView_iPhone/Art/tvcellstyle_value2.jpg!  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Add UITableViewCellStyleValue2 Table Styling To iOS SDK
Description: """"It would be great if Titanium provided a standardized way to style a tableview to fit Apple's UITableViewCellStyleValue2 style (with row subtitle in blue at left and title in black on right). Providing a way to automatically render this specific style, which is consistent with Map Detail View, Individual Contact Detail View and Twitter Individual User View, I feel would vastly speed up app development. More Info From Apple Developer: [UITableViewCellStyleValue2|http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#DOCUMENTATION/UIKit/Reference/UITableViewCell_Class/Reference/Reference.html#//apple_ref/c/econst/UITableViewCellStyleValue2] !http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/DOCUMENTATION/UserExperience/Conceptual/TableView_iPhone/Art/tvcellstyle_value2.jpg! """"",title+description
TIMOB-4513,12,"""Ti.Network.HTTPClient.validatesSecureCertificate exposed as BOOL""","""""""This is a publicly available property and should either be removed in favor of being read directly from dynprops, or exposed as an NSNumber so that it can be properly managed.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Network.HTTPClient.validatesSecureCertificate exposed as BOOL
Description: """"This is a publicly available property and should either be removed in favor of being read directly from dynprops, or exposed as an NSNumber so that it can be properly managed.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4512,12,"""Drillbit: Need to ensure that asynchronous tests always run""","""""""Drillbit won't run concurrent asynchronous tests on occasion, particularly when one fails. See the attached drillbit test file for an example (a slightly modified HTTP client test, from one of our pull requests).""""""",Bug,"Title: Drillbit: Need to ensure that asynchronous tests always run
Description: """"Drillbit won't run concurrent asynchronous tests on occasion, particularly when one fails. See the attached drillbit test file for an example (a slightly modified HTTP client test, from one of our pull requests).""""",title+description
TIMOB-4511,12,"""Orientation properties report differing values on Android, and differ from iOS""","""""""h1. Problem  On Android, Ti.Gesture.orientation is returning different values than e.orientation, and neither are differentiating landscape left and right.    h2. Sample Code  The following code reports the different orientation values. Run it on iOS, and you will see the Ti.Gesture.orientation is in sync with the evt.orientation. But run it on Android, and you will see they differ.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' });  var lblOrientation = Ti.UI.createLabel({      color: '#999',      text: 'Ti.Gesture.orientation',      font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' },      textAlign: 'center',      width: 'auto', height: 'auto',      top: 20  });  win.add(lblOrientation);  var lblEvtOrientation = Ti.UI.createLabel({      color: '#999',      text: 'e.orientation',      font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' },      textAlign: 'center',      width: 'auto', height: 'auto',      top: 50  });  win.add(lblEvtOrientation);  var lblIsPortrait = Ti.UI.createLabel({      color: '#999',      text: 'isPortrait',      font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' },      textAlign: 'center',      width: 'auto',      height: 'auto',      top: 80  });  win.add(lblIsPortrait);  var lblIsLandscape = Ti.UI.createLabel({      color: '#999',      text: 'isLandscape',      font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' },      textAlign: 'center',      width: 'auto', height: 'auto',      top: 110  });  win.add(lblIsLandscape);    Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange', function(evt) {      lblOrientation.text = Ti.Gesture.orientation;      lblEvtOrientation.text = evt.orientation;      lblIsPortrait.text = evt.source.isPortrait();      lblIsLandscape.text = evt.source.isLandscape();  });    win.open();  {code}    h2. Screenshots  See attached screens.    h2. May Duplicate  [TIMOB-1294]""""""",Bug,"Title: Orientation properties report differing values on Android, and differ from iOS
Description: """"h1. Problem On Android, Ti.Gesture.orientation is returning different values than e.orientation, and neither are differentiating landscape left and right. h2. Sample Code The following code reports the different orientation values. Run it on iOS, and you will see the Ti.Gesture.orientation is in sync with the evt.orientation. But run it on Android, and you will see they differ. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var lblOrientation = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color: '#999', text: 'Ti.Gesture.orientation', font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' }, textAlign: 'center', width: 'auto', height: 'auto', top: 20 }); win.add(lblOrientation); var lblEvtOrientation = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color: '#999', text: 'e.orientation', font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' }, textAlign: 'center', width: 'auto', height: 'auto', top: 50 }); win.add(lblEvtOrientation); var lblIsPortrait = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color: '#999', text: 'isPortrait', font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' }, textAlign: 'center', width: 'auto', height: 'auto', top: 80 }); win.add(lblIsPortrait); var lblIsLandscape = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color: '#999', text: 'isLandscape', font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' }, textAlign: 'center', width: 'auto', height: 'auto', top: 110 }); win.add(lblIsLandscape); Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange', function(evt) { lblOrientation.text = Ti.Gesture.orientation; lblEvtOrientation.text = evt.orientation; lblIsPortrait.text = evt.source.isPortrait(); lblIsLandscape.text = evt.source.isLandscape(); }); win.open(); {code} h2. Screenshots See attached screens. h2. May Duplicate [TIMOB-1294]""""",title+description
TIMOB-4509,12,"""Drillbit: Random failures via FileNotFoundException (test.js)""","""""""At least three of us (marshall, bill & don) are getting into situations where drillbit just stops because of this error.  Has a weird randomness to it -- sometimes we make it all the way through all suites, sometimes it fails within the first few suites, and it doesn't need to be the same suite that fails each time.  Weird.    The trace:    http://pastie.org/2131526    """"""",Bug,"Title: Drillbit: Random failures via FileNotFoundException (test.js)
Description: """"At least three of us (marshall, bill & don) are getting into situations where drillbit just stops because of this error. Has a weird randomness to it -- sometimes we make it all the way through all suites, sometimes it fails within the first few suites, and it doesn't need to be the same suite that fails each time. Weird. The trace: http://pastie.org/2131526 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4508,12,"""iOS: Need the pinch gesture exposed for TIUIView event listeners""","""""""We need to have the event handler for pinch gestures available for TIUIView objects and their derivatives    This is needed for many projects we've been a apart of.    We recently implemented this in the soon to be available openGL module development project (ios only so far) and it seems to work for our needs there.    Having this available for all views and objects that are based on view objects would be very useful.    Here are the code snippets from the IOS side:    Added this to the view initialization:           UIPinchGestureRecognizer *pinchRecognizer;         pinchRecognizer=[[UIPinchGestureRecognizer alloc]                           initWithTarget:self                          action:@selector(foundPinch:)];         [controller.view addGestureRecognizer:pinchRecognizer];         [pinchRecognizer release];    here's the callback:    - (void)foundPinch:(UIPinchGestureRecognizer *)recognizer {     NSDictionary *event = [NSDictionary dictionaryWithObjectsAndKeys:NUMDOUBLE(recognizer.scale), @""""""""scale"""""""", NUMDOUBLE(recognizer.velocity), @""""""""velocity"""""""", nil];     [self.proxy fireEvent:@""""""""pinch"""""""" withObject:event];  }      here's how we use it now on the opengl view     opengl.addEventListener('pinch', function {     scale = e.scale;  });  """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Need the pinch gesture exposed for TIUIView event listeners
Description: """"We need to have the event handler for pinch gestures available for TIUIView objects and their derivatives This is needed for many projects we've been a apart of. We recently implemented this in the soon to be available openGL module development project (ios only so far) and it seems to work for our needs there. Having this available for all views and objects that are based on view objects would be very useful. Here are the code snippets from the IOS side: Added this to the view initialization: UIPinchGestureRecognizer *pinchRecognizer; pinchRecognizer=[[UIPinchGestureRecognizer alloc] initWithTarget:self action:@selector(foundPinch:)]; [controller.view addGestureRecognizer:pinchRecognizer]; [pinchRecognizer release]; here's the callback: - (void)foundPinch:(UIPinchGestureRecognizer *)recognizer { NSDictionary *event = [NSDictionary dictionaryWithObjectsAndKeys:NUMDOUBLE(recognizer.scale), @""""""""scale"""""""", NUMDOUBLE(recognizer.velocity), @""""""""velocity"""""""", nil]; [self.proxy fireEvent:@""""""""pinch"""""""" withObject:event]; } here's how we use it now on the opengl view opengl.addEventListener('pinch', function { scale = e.scale; }); """"",title+description
