TIMOB-4506,12,"""iOS: Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer 'complete' event always returns reason '0' or 'PLAYBACK_ENDED'""","""""""iOS 4.3 and Ti mobile SDK 1.7rc1    This involves the Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer object. In the 'complete' event, whether the video actually finishes or playback is exited by the user, the reason passed to the event always returns '0' or Titanium.Media.VIDEO_FINISH_REASON_PLAYBACK_ENDED.     Accompanying Q&A Issue:  http://developer.<USER>com/question/121674/complete-event-firing-when-changing-url-on-video-player""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer 'complete' event always returns reason '0' or 'PLAYBACK_ENDED'
Description: """"iOS 4.3 and Ti mobile SDK 1.7rc1 This involves the Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer object. In the 'complete' event, whether the video actually finishes or playback is exited by the user, the reason passed to the event always returns '0' or Titanium.Media.VIDEO_FINISH_REASON_PLAYBACK_ENDED. Accompanying Q&A Issue: http://developer.<USER>com/question/121674/complete-event-firing-when-changing-url-on-video-player""""",title+description
