TIMOB-4478,12,"""reverseGeocoder Platform Inconsistency""","""""""h1. Problem  The """"""""country code"""""""" property is inconsistent between the platforms. On iOS it is """"""""country_code"""""""", while for Android it is """"""""CountryCode"""""""".    h2. Solution  Pick one, and deprecate the other. Both platforms should expose the one chosen, and one can have the antiquated property for a couple more releases.    h2. Sample Code  {code:title=app.js}  Ti.Geolocation.addEventListener('location', function(e) {      Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder(e.coords.latitude, e.coords.longitude, function(evt) {          alert(evt);      });  });  {code}    h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-455583""""""",Bug,"Title: reverseGeocoder Platform Inconsistency
Description: """"h1. Problem The """"""""country code"""""""" property is inconsistent between the platforms. On iOS it is """"""""country_code"""""""", while for Android it is """"""""CountryCode"""""""". h2. Solution Pick one, and deprecate the other. Both platforms should expose the one chosen, and one can have the antiquated property for a couple more releases. h2. Sample Code {code:title=app.js} Ti.Geolocation.addEventListener('location', function(e) { Ti.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder(e.coords.latitude, e.coords.longitude, function(evt) { alert(evt); }); }); {code} h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-455583""""",title+description
