TIMOB-4352,12,"""Android: MapView does not refresh map if created before the parent window is open""","""""""If you create and add a mapView to its parent window before that window is open then the map image will not load when you zoom in and out.    Step 1: run the code below  Step 2: notice that when you move the map or zoom out, the map does not refresh  Step 3: remove the comments from the open event listener  Step 4: run the code again  Step 5: notice that the map image refreshes when you zoom in or out    {code:title=""""""""app.js""""""""}  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        backgroundColor:'#fff',    fullscreen:true  });    win.open();    // win.addEventListener('open', function(e){    var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({      mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,      region:{latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993, latitudeDelta:0.5, longitudeDelta:0.5},      animate:true,      regionFit:true,      userLocation:true    });      win.add(mapview);  // });  {code}    h3. Workaround  create and add the mapview to the window in the window open event listener.    h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-399811""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: MapView does not refresh map if created before the parent window is open
Description: """"If you create and add a mapView to its parent window before that window is open then the map image will not load when you zoom in and out. Step 1: run the code below Step 2: notice that when you move the map or zoom out, the map does not refresh Step 3: remove the comments from the open event listener Step 4: run the code again Step 5: notice that the map image refreshes when you zoom in or out {code:title=""""""""app.js""""""""} var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen:true }); win.open(); // win.addEventListener('open', function(e){ var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({ mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, region:{latitude:33.74511, longitude:-84.38993, latitudeDelta:0.5, longitudeDelta:0.5}, animate:true, regionFit:true, userLocation:true }); win.add(mapview); // }); {code} h3. Workaround create and add the mapview to the window in the window open event listener. h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-399811""""",title+description
TIMOB-4351,12,"""iOS: Add """"canScale"""" to ImageView for Parity with Android""","""""""h1. Feature  The """"""""canScale"""""""" property exists on Android, but not on iOS. It lets you pinch around an image.    h2. Workaround  On iOS, you can dump the image in a scroll view. But it takes quite a bit more code to get it to work properly.    h2. Sample Code  The following shows a large remote image (~500kb). It may take a moment for the sample to come up. Feel free to download the image locally to speed it up. It demonstrates the Android and iOS approaches to a scalable image.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#000' });    var image = Ti.UI.createImageView({      image: 'http://appc.me/content/appceleratorHat.jpg',      width: 'auto', height: 'auto', canScale: true  });  if (Ti.Android) {      // this simple code works in Android      win.add(image);  }  else {      // but iOS requires all of this      var scroll = Ti.UI.createScrollView({          contentHeight: 'auto', contentWidth: 'auto',          maxZoomScale: 1, minZoomScale: 0.16      });      image.addEventListener('load', function() {          scroll.zoomScale = 0.16;      });      scroll.add(image);      win.add(scroll);  }  win.open();  {code}    h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/APP-121155 http://appc.me/APP-422217 http://appc.me/APP-768251""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add """"canScale"""" to ImageView for Parity with Android
Description: """"h1. Feature The """"""""canScale"""""""" property exists on Android, but not on iOS. It lets you pinch around an image. h2. Workaround On iOS, you can dump the image in a scroll view. But it takes quite a bit more code to get it to work properly. h2. Sample Code The following shows a large remote image (~500kb). It may take a moment for the sample to come up. Feel free to download the image locally to speed it up. It demonstrates the Android and iOS approaches to a scalable image. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#000' }); var image = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'http://appc.me/content/appceleratorHat.jpg', width: 'auto', height: 'auto', canScale: true }); if (Ti.Android) { // this simple code works in Android win.add(image); } else { // but iOS requires all of this var scroll = Ti.UI.createScrollView({ contentHeight: 'auto', contentWidth: 'auto', maxZoomScale: 1, minZoomScale: 0.16 }); image.addEventListener('load', function() { scroll.zoomScale = 0.16; }); scroll.add(image); win.add(scroll); } win.open(); {code} h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/APP-121155 http://appc.me/APP-422217 http://appc.me/APP-768251""""",title+description
TIMOB-4350,12,"""Android: ImageView Pinch to Zoom and Double Tap Smart Zoom""","""""""h1. Feature  Add support to the image view on Android for pinching and zooming.    h2. Sample Code  The following shows a large remote image (~500kb). It may take a moment for the sample to come up. Feel free to download the image locally to speed it up.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#000' });  win.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({      image: 'http://appc.me/content/appceleratorHat.jpg',      width: 'auto', height: 'auto', canScale: true  }));  win.open();  {code}    h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/APP-121155 http://appc.me/APP-422217 http://appc.me/APP-768251""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: ImageView Pinch to Zoom and Double Tap Smart Zoom
Description: """"h1. Feature Add support to the image view on Android for pinching and zooming. h2. Sample Code The following shows a large remote image (~500kb). It may take a moment for the sample to come up. Feel free to download the image locally to speed it up. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#000' }); win.add(Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'http://appc.me/content/appceleratorHat.jpg', width: 'auto', height: 'auto', canScale: true })); win.open(); {code} h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/APP-121155 http://appc.me/APP-422217 http://appc.me/APP-768251""""",title+description
TIMOB-4349,12,"""iOS: Cannot launch emulator gives error on build script on Lion""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Run TiDeveloper  2. Create a simple project  3. Run in iOS emulatore    Actual Result:  [ERROR]  [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):  File """"""""/Users/nataliehuynh/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.2/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1091, in main  execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % link_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=__LOG__ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version)],False)  File """"""""/Users/nataliehuynh/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.2/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1012, in execute_xcode  output = run.run(args,False,False,o)  File """"""""/Users/nataliehuynh/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.2/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run  sys.exit(rc)  SystemExit: 65    Expected Result:  Should Launch""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot launch emulator gives error on build script on Lion
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run TiDeveloper 2. Create a simple project 3. Run in iOS emulatore Actual Result: [ERROR] [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Users/nataliehuynh/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.2/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1091, in main execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % link_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=__LOG__ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version)],False) File """"""""/Users/nataliehuynh/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.2/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1012, in execute_xcode output = run.run(args,False,False,o) File """"""""/Users/nataliehuynh/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.2/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65 Expected Result: Should Launch""""",title+description
