TIMOB-4309,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Phone>Sound>Audio session mode, iPod will not play sound in """"record and play"""" mode.""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink,Phone>Sound>Audio session mode, I could not get the iPod to play in the """"""""record and play"""""""" mode. This may be due to the lack of microphone on the iPod 3rd gen.   Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Audio 3) Set audio mode to """"""""record and play"""""""" mode 4) Attempt to play  Result: No sound  Expected Result: Sound plays  Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Phone>Sound>Audio session mode, iPod will not play sound in """"record and play"""" mode.
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink,Phone>Sound>Audio session mode, I could not get the iPod to play in the """"""""record and play"""""""" mode. This may be due to the lack of microphone on the iPod 3rd gen. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Audio 3) Set audio mode to """"""""record and play"""""""" mode 4) Attempt to play Result: No sound Expected Result: Sound plays Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4308,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming 2, iPhone 3GS finishes movie with no still shot in view""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink, Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming 2, when the movie finishes playing on all other iOS devices the movie still appears on the view. For iPhone 3 GS, the movie is gone, and the view is blank.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming 2 3) Play movie until completion  Result: View is left blank  Expected Result: Movie still remains on view  Notes: OCCURS in 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming 2, iPhone 3GS finishes movie with no still shot in view
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming 2, when the movie finishes playing on all other iOS devices the movie still appears on the view. For iPhone 3 GS, the movie is gone, and the view is blank. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Remote streaming 2 3) Play movie until completion Result: View is left blank Expected Result: Movie still remains on view Notes: OCCURS in 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4307,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>Picker, all devices with all pickers have images appearing outside the picker frame while rotating picker.""",,Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>Picker, all devices with all pickers have images appearing outside the picker frame while rotating picker.",title-only
TIMOB-4306,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>Picker, all devices with all pickers have images appearing outside the picker frame while rotating picker.""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink, Controls>Picker, I noticed while rotating the picker that the picker images were visible outside the grey frame of the picker as they passed by the bottom of the picker.  See attached image.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Controls>Picker and choose any picker 3) Utilize the picker, rotating items by the bottom of the picker  Result: Images bleed outside the bottom of the picker  Expected Result: no images bleeding outside the picker.  Notes: Occurs in 1.6.2 """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>Picker, all devices with all pickers have images appearing outside the picker frame while rotating picker.
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Controls>Picker, I noticed while rotating the picker that the picker images were visible outside the grey frame of the picker as they passed by the bottom of the picker. See attached image. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Controls>Picker and choose any picker 3) Utilize the picker, rotating items by the bottom of the picker Result: Images bleed outside the bottom of the picker Expected Result: no images bleeding outside the picker. Notes: Occurs in 1.6.2 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4305,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>text field>Toolbar, iPhone 3GS does not show toolbar in landscape mode""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink,Controls>text field>Toolbar, The toolbar would not show in landscape orientation. The toolbar performed as expected on the other iOS devices in the test. When in landscape, the """"""""focus to show keyboard with toolbar"""""""" could be focused, and the toolbar would flash briefly near the status bar. While this occurs on 1.6.2 as well, the toolbar is never seen while in landscape, not even briefly.   Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Controls>text field>Toolbar 3) Focus to show keyboard with toolbar 4) change orientation to landscape  Result: No toolbar visible  Expected Result: Toolbar visible  Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 Does not occur on iPad, iPhone 4, iPod touch 3rd gen. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>text field>Toolbar, iPhone 3GS does not show toolbar in landscape mode
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink,Controls>text field>Toolbar, The toolbar would not show in landscape orientation. The toolbar performed as expected on the other iOS devices in the test. When in landscape, the """"""""focus to show keyboard with toolbar"""""""" could be focused, and the toolbar would flash briefly near the status bar. While this occurs on 1.6.2 as well, the toolbar is never seen while in landscape, not even briefly. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS (SDK 1.7.X) onto device 2) Navigate to Controls>text field>Toolbar 3) Focus to show keyboard with toolbar 4) change orientation to landscape Result: No toolbar visible Expected Result: Toolbar visible Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 Does not occur on iPad, iPhone 4, iPod touch 3rd gen. """"",title+description
TIMOB-4304,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Nav Group, Code sets modal window background to """"red"""" but only iPad shows the setting""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink,Base UI>Nav Group, I noticed that the iPad has a red background to the modal window, while the other devices were grey. Turns out the iPad was the only correct one of the 4 devices in test. A check of the code  (navgroup.js) shows: var modalWin = Ti.UI.createWindow({  backgroundColor:""""""""red"""""""" });  Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS onto device  2) Navigate to Base UI>Nav Group 3) Examine the background  Result:  Color is grey  Expected Result: Color is red  Notes: OCCURS in 1.6.2 Blain mentions that this seems to be due to a clear versus colored background for the grouped table view. """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Nav Group, Code sets modal window background to """"red"""" but only iPad shows the setting
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink,Base UI>Nav Group, I noticed that the iPad has a red background to the modal window, while the other devices were grey. Turns out the iPad was the only correct one of the 4 devices in test. A check of the code (navgroup.js) shows: var modalWin = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:""""""""red"""""""" }); Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS onto device 2) Navigate to Base UI>Nav Group 3) Examine the background Result: Color is grey Expected Result: Color is red Notes: OCCURS in 1.6.2 Blain mentions that this seems to be due to a clear versus colored background for the grouped table view. """"",title+description
TIMOB-4303,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Animation>Animation Points, iPhone 3GS renders """"stop animation"""" button with no bottom border""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Animation>Animation Points, the """"""""stop animation"""""""" button is rendered without a bottom border. See attached image. This only occurs on the iPhone 3 GS.  Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS onto device  2) Navigate to Base UI>Animation>Animation Points  3) Examine the """"""""Stop Animation"""""""" button  Result: Button is rendered incompletely  Expected Result: Fully formed button  Notes:  OCCURS in 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Animation>Animation Points, iPhone 3GS renders """"stop animation"""" button with no bottom border
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Animation>Animation Points, the """"""""stop animation"""""""" button is rendered without a bottom border. See attached image. This only occurs on the iPhone 3 GS. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS onto device 2) Navigate to Base UI>Animation>Animation Points 3) Examine the """"""""Stop Animation"""""""" button Result: Button is rendered incompletely Expected Result: Fully formed button Notes: OCCURS in 1.6.2""""",title+description
