TIMOB-4301,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: iPhone 3GS fails to display activity indicator in some tests""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink,I noted that a particular type of activity indicator was not being shown on the 3GS, but was displayed on the other test devices.  Here are the tests with the missing indicator: Base UI>Views>Web Views>Basic Auth Base UI>Views>Web Views>PDF URL Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls   Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS onto device 2) Navigate to any of the listed tests above 3) Look for the indicator  Result: No indicator displayed  Expected Result: Indicator displays  Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: iPhone 3GS fails to display activity indicator in some tests
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink,I noted that a particular type of activity indicator was not being shown on the 3GS, but was displayed on the other test devices. Here are the tests with the missing indicator: Base UI>Views>Web Views>Basic Auth Base UI>Views>Web Views>PDF URL Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS onto device 2) Navigate to any of the listed tests above 3) Look for the indicator Result: No indicator displayed Expected Result: Indicator displays Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4300,12,"""iOS: status bar appears when video is played""","""""""This is in reference to a bug that was marked as resolved in my opinion incorrectly: TIMOB-2768     <USER>is indeed correct that showing the statusbar upon a video launch is correct behaviour, and Apple indeed make a valid argument.     But however.    Upon pressing DONE, the statusbar DOES NOT hide again, and is VISIBLE OVER the navbar, a bug. And Apple have confirmed this and are rejecting apps because of this bug.    So who is right here? <USER>or Apple? In my opinion this is a bug in <USER>that the statusbar is visible AFTER the video has been CLOSED (using the DONE button) or has finished playing.     The original thread is as follows:    In tiapp.xml, setting the status bar hidden, hides the status bar as expected. But when a movie is played using 'createVideoPlayer' the status bar appears and cannot be hidden again. This is from a Help Desk ticket:  http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63571    Here is a sample code: http://pastie.org/private/qvp8jfkqm2jgi33qvurniq    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: status bar appears when video is played
Description: """"This is in reference to a bug that was marked as resolved in my opinion incorrectly: TIMOB-2768 <USER>is indeed correct that showing the statusbar upon a video launch is correct behaviour, and Apple indeed make a valid argument. But however. Upon pressing DONE, the statusbar DOES NOT hide again, and is VISIBLE OVER the navbar, a bug. And Apple have confirmed this and are rejecting apps because of this bug. So who is right here? <USER>or Apple? In my opinion this is a bug in <USER>that the statusbar is visible AFTER the video has been CLOSED (using the DONE button) or has finished playing. The original thread is as follows: In tiapp.xml, setting the status bar hidden, hides the status bar as expected. But when a movie is played using 'createVideoPlayer' the status bar appears and cannot be hidden again. This is from a Help Desk ticket: http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63571 Here is a sample code: http://pastie.org/private/qvp8jfkqm2jgi33qvurniq """"",title+description
TIMOB-4297,12,"""iOS: Debugger: Subsequent launches of debugger on a project causes it to fail to connect""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new project in TiStudio 2. Set a breakpoint in the app.js 3. Run in debug 4. Quit  5. Rerun in debug  Actual Result: Debugger fails to connect  Expected Result: To connect to debugger everytime""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Debugger: Subsequent launches of debugger on a project causes it to fail to connect
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new project in TiStudio 2. Set a breakpoint in the app.js 3. Run in debug 4. Quit 5. Rerun in debug Actual Result: Debugger fails to connect Expected Result: To connect to debugger everytime""""",title+description
TIMOB-4296,12,"""Android: slider does not work properly when it is rotated""","""""""When you rotate a slider, it seems to stop working. If you tap across the area that the slider would be if it had not been rotated (middle of the the slider), then you will see that it is sliding within the area where the slider would have been. But the rest of the slider seems frozen.     Step 1: run the code below  Step 2: notice that the slider only works if you tap it in the middle        h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-771485    h3. Tested With  TiSDK 1.7.0.RC1  Android 2.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: slider does not work properly when it is rotated
Description: """"When you rotate a slider, it seems to stop working. If you tap across the area that the slider would be if it had not been rotated (middle of the the slider), then you will see that it is sliding within the area where the slider would have been. But the rest of the slider seems frozen. Step 1: run the code below Step 2: notice that the slider only works if you tap it in the middle h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-771485 h3. Tested With TiSDK 1.7.0.RC1 Android 2.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4282,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink unreproducible crash while running Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Empty AppendRow""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink, I experienced a crash that seemed to relate to a table append that was out of sync with the contents of the table.  I could not reproduce this failure in 5 attempts.  Please see the log and console output attached.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Unknown, but occurred about 2 hours into testing.  Result: Crash   Expected Result: No crash  Notes: Could not reproduce on 1.6.2 (5 attempts) or 1.7.0 (5 attempts)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink unreproducible crash while running Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table Empty AppendRow
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, I experienced a crash that seemed to relate to a table append that was out of sync with the contents of the table. I could not reproduce this failure in 5 attempts. Please see the log and console output attached. Steps to reproduce: 1) Unknown, but occurred about 2 hours into testing. Result: Crash Expected Result: No crash Notes: Could not reproduce on 1.6.2 (5 attempts) or 1.7.0 (5 attempts)""""",title+description
TIMOB-4281,12,"""splitWindow not opening window URL""","""""""When using a url for the window in a splitWindow, the window gets added, but the js file in the URL is not run/opened  {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var orientation_modes = [Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT];  masterWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({   orientationModes:orientation_modes,   url:'master.js' //or any js file }); detailWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({   orientationModes:orientation_modes,     url:'detail.js' //or any js file });  splitView = Ti.UI.iPad.createSplitWindow({   masterView: masterWindow,   detailView: detailWindow });  splitView.open(); {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: splitWindow not opening window URL
Description: """"When using a url for the window in a splitWindow, the window gets added, but the js file in the URL is not run/opened {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var orientation_modes = [Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT]; masterWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({ orientationModes:orientation_modes, url:'master.js' //or any js file }); detailWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({ orientationModes:orientation_modes, url:'detail.js' //or any js file }); splitView = Ti.UI.iPad.createSplitWindow({ masterView: masterWindow, detailView: detailWindow }); splitView.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-4280,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files, arrow graphics in landscape view get compressed""","""""""Description: When testing KitchenSink Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files and rotating to landscape, the view navigation arrows get compressed (see  attached image)  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPhone 4 with SDK 1.7.X 2) Navigate to UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files 3) Rotate the device to landscape  Result: View navigation arrows are not attractive  Expected Result: Well-formed arrows  Notes: Could not verify in 1.6.2 because the KS test did not allow orientation change.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files, arrow graphics in landscape view get compressed
Description: """"Description: When testing KitchenSink Base UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files and rotating to landscape, the view navigation arrows get compressed (see attached image) Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPhone 4 with SDK 1.7.X 2) Navigate to UI>Views>Coverflow view>Coverflow Local Files 3) Rotate the device to landscape Result: View navigation arrows are not attractive Expected Result: Well-formed arrows Notes: Could not verify in 1.6.2 because the KS test did not allow orientation change.""""",title+description
