TIMOB-4206,12,"""Android: Image on table view cannot be dynamically changed""","""""""Tried with two different codes:    And this one:    This creates a simple table view with an image view on each row. The goal is to change the image inside the rows when a row is clicked.  h3. What's supposed to happen:  When a row from the table view is clicker, the image within should change to the other one on the listener. This happens with iOS.  h3. What happens:  Nothing changes    h4. Helpdesk ticket:  APP-377288""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image on table view cannot be dynamically changed
Description: """"Tried with two different codes: And this one: This creates a simple table view with an image view on each row. The goal is to change the image inside the rows when a row is clicked. h3. What's supposed to happen: When a row from the table view is clicker, the image within should change to the other one on the listener. This happens with iOS. h3. What happens: Nothing changes h4. Helpdesk ticket: APP-377288""""",title+description
TIMOB-4205,12,"""Android: Map Centers on selectAnnotation""","""""""h1. Problem  Given a map view, if you call """"""""selectAnnotation"""""""" on a particular annotation, the map will automatically center on that annotation. This is a problem if you don't want it to automatically do this. It's also an inconsistency with iOS.    h2. Solution  Provide an argument to selectAnnotation that can disable this behavior. Something like """"""""doNotAutoCenter"""""""".    h2. Sample Code  The following app.js should select the annotation on the map and bump the map up north of the annotation. With Android's current behavior, it will center on the annotation.  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' });  var map = Ti.Map.createView({      mapType: Ti.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,      regionFit: true  });  var annotation = Ti.Map.createAnnotation({      latitude: 59.93473,      longitude: 10.760797,      title: 'Print House AS',      subtitle: 'Sandakerveien 24 C Bygg A2, 0473 Oslo',      animate: true,      pincolor: Ti.Map.ANNOTATION_PURPLE  });  map.addAnnotation(annotation);  map.selectAnnotation(annotation);  map.setLocation({ latitude: 60, longitude: 10.760797, latitudeDelta: 0.035, longitudeDelta: 0.035 });    win.add(map);  win.open();  {code}    h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/RSN-92979-828""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Map Centers on selectAnnotation
Description: """"h1. Problem Given a map view, if you call """"""""selectAnnotation"""""""" on a particular annotation, the map will automatically center on that annotation. This is a problem if you don't want it to automatically do this. It's also an inconsistency with iOS. h2. Solution Provide an argument to selectAnnotation that can disable this behavior. Something like """"""""doNotAutoCenter"""""""". h2. Sample Code The following app.js should select the annotation on the map and bump the map up north of the annotation. With Android's current behavior, it will center on the annotation. {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var map = Ti.Map.createView({ mapType: Ti.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, regionFit: true }); var annotation = Ti.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude: 59.93473, longitude: 10.760797, title: 'Print House AS', subtitle: 'Sandakerveien 24 C Bygg A2, 0473 Oslo', animate: true, pincolor: Ti.Map.ANNOTATION_PURPLE }); map.addAnnotation(annotation); map.selectAnnotation(annotation); map.setLocation({ latitude: 60, longitude: 10.760797, latitudeDelta: 0.035, longitudeDelta: 0.035 }); win.add(map); win.open(); {code} h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/RSN-92979-828""""",title+description
TIMOB-4204,12,"""Android: Window focus event does not fire in a tab group when using the 'back' button""","""""""When navigating back to a previous window in a tabgroup (back button) the window focus event does not fire.  Added to Kitchen sink's main_windows/controls.js to test: http://pastie.org/1968193    Tested in RC1, CI, latest from today, 1.6.x - same results""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window focus event does not fire in a tab group when using the 'back' button
Description: """"When navigating back to a previous window in a tabgroup (back button) the window focus event does not fire. Added to Kitchen sink's main_windows/controls.js to test: http://pastie.org/1968193 Tested in RC1, CI, latest from today, 1.6.x - same results""""",title+description
TIMOB-4203,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink:  Base UI>Views>Email Dialog photo picker non functional on iPad with 4.3, ok on 3.2.2""","""""""Description: While attempting to close another bug, I navigated to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog and when the page loaded, the photo picker was rendered, but then collapsed and was unusable. THis behavior was not noted on the other iPad running 3.2.2.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on an iPad running 4.3 2) Launch KS and navigate to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog  Result: Picker drawn but then collapses  Expected Result: Picker functional  Notes: OCCURS ON:  iPad 1 (4.3) iPad 2 (4.3.2)  DOES NOT OCCUR on: iPad 3.2.2 """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Views>Email Dialog photo picker non functional on iPad with 4.3, ok on 3.2.2
Description: """"Description: While attempting to close another bug, I navigated to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog and when the page loaded, the photo picker was rendered, but then collapsed and was unusable. THis behavior was not noted on the other iPad running 3.2.2. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on an iPad running 4.3 2) Launch KS and navigate to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog Result: Picker drawn but then collapses Expected Result: Picker functional Notes: OCCURS ON: iPad 1 (4.3) iPad 2 (4.3.2) DOES NOT OCCUR on: iPad 3.2.2 """"",title+description
