TIMOB-4198,12,"""iOS: removeEventListener Removes All Events""","""""""h1. Problem  Removing an event listener from an object causes that object and all children objects to not receive any events (including events that were not removed from it).    h2. Sample Code  {code:title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' });    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({      title: 'Remove A Listener',      top: 10, left: 10, right: 10, height: 50  });  function listenerToRemove() {}  win.addEventListener('junk', listenerToRemove);  button.addEventListener('click', function () {      alert('Removed!');      win.removeEventListener('junk', listenerToRemove);  });  win.add(button);    win.open();  {code}    h2. How To Reproduce  # Drop the above code in an app.js  # When the app launches, a listener will be added for the """"""""junk"""""""" event  # Click the button, and """"""""junk"""""""" will no longer be listened for  # Try to click the button again. If nothing happens, this bug exists.    h2. Tested On  BROKEN in iPhone Simulator 4.2 on Ti Mobile SDK 1.7.0.RC1  BROKEN in iPhone Simulator 4.2 on Ti Mobile SDK 1.6.2  WORKS on Android Samsung EPIC 4G 2.3 on Ti Mobile SDK 1.7.0.RC1    h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-445715""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: removeEventListener Removes All Events
Description: """"h1. Problem Removing an event listener from an object causes that object and all children objects to not receive any events (including events that were not removed from it). h2. Sample Code {code:title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Remove A Listener', top: 10, left: 10, right: 10, height: 50 }); function listenerToRemove() {} win.addEventListener('junk', listenerToRemove); button.addEventListener('click', function () { alert('Removed!'); win.removeEventListener('junk', listenerToRemove); }); win.add(button); win.open(); {code} h2. How To Reproduce # Drop the above code in an app.js # When the app launches, a listener will be added for the """"""""junk"""""""" event # Click the button, and """"""""junk"""""""" will no longer be listened for # Try to click the button again. If nothing happens, this bug exists. h2. Tested On BROKEN in iPhone Simulator 4.2 on Ti Mobile SDK 1.7.0.RC1 BROKEN in iPhone Simulator 4.2 on Ti Mobile SDK 1.6.2 WORKS on Android Samsung EPIC 4G 2.3 on Ti Mobile SDK 1.7.0.RC1 h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-445715""""",title+description
TIMOB-4197,12,"""Android: Kitchensink Base UI> Views> Image Views> Animated: Set Duration to 0 ms results in app stopping unexpectedly""","""""""Description: If you set the Duration between frames in Base UI> Views> Image Views> Animate to 0, the app unexpectedly quits.   Steps to reproduce: 1) Using KS 1.7.0 or KS 1.6.2, install on an Android device 2) Navigate to Base UI> Views> Image Views> Animate 3) Set duration to 0 ms 4) stop animation (to take the ms change) 5) Start animation  Result: Dialog stating app unexpectedly quit  Expected Result: Super fast animation  Notes: Occurred on Droid, Nexus S, KS 1.7.0 and KS 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Kitchensink Base UI> Views> Image Views> Animated: Set Duration to 0 ms results in app stopping unexpectedly
Description: """"Description: If you set the Duration between frames in Base UI> Views> Image Views> Animate to 0, the app unexpectedly quits. Steps to reproduce: 1) Using KS 1.7.0 or KS 1.6.2, install on an Android device 2) Navigate to Base UI> Views> Image Views> Animate 3) Set duration to 0 ms 4) stop animation (to take the ms change) 5) Start animation Result: Dialog stating app unexpectedly quit Expected Result: Super fast animation Notes: Occurred on Droid, Nexus S, KS 1.7.0 and KS 1.6.2""""",title+description
