TIMOB-4185,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink:  Rotating during animation causes window UI layout problems""","""""""Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Animation>transitions, it is possible get the UI layout be rendering for the wrong orientation. See screenshots attached.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Animation>transitions in Landscape view 3) Click full window and rotate while the animation plays (timing is critical) 4) Tap close  Result: Rendered window expects portrait  Expected Result: UI matches orientation  Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Rotating during animation causes window UI layout problems
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Animation>transitions, it is possible get the UI layout be rendering for the wrong orientation. See screenshots attached. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Animation>transitions in Landscape view 3) Click full window and rotate while the animation plays (timing is critical) 4) Tap close Result: Rendered window expects portrait Expected Result: UI matches orientation Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4184,12,"""Android: Win 7: New titanium mobile project does not display icon images on the tabs""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new titanium mobile project in TiStudio 2. Launch Emulator  Actual Result: The icon images are not displayed above the tabs  Expected Result: To display the correct icon above each tab  Worked with 1.6.2  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Win 7: New titanium mobile project does not display icon images on the tabs
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Create a new titanium mobile project in TiStudio 2. Launch Emulator Actual Result: The icon images are not displayed above the tabs Expected Result: To display the correct icon above each tab Worked with 1.6.2 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4183,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink:  Base UI>Window NavBar rendering problems after orientation change""","""""""Description:  When testing Base UI>Window NavBar, a rotation change can result in a poorly rendered Nav bar area.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad  2) Navigate to Base UI>Window NavBar in portrait orientation  3) Tap """"""""bar color""""""""  4) Tap """"""""set bar image""""""""  5) Rotate to landscape  (for added fun, then tap """"""""title prompt"""""""")    Result:  Nav bar area rendered poorly    Expected Result:  Correctly rendered nav bar    Notes:  OCCURS on 1.6.2  OCCURS on iPad 2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Window NavBar rendering problems after orientation change
Description: """"Description: When testing Base UI>Window NavBar, a rotation change can result in a poorly rendered Nav bar area. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 2) Navigate to Base UI>Window NavBar in portrait orientation 3) Tap """"""""bar color"""""""" 4) Tap """"""""set bar image"""""""" 5) Rotate to landscape (for added fun, then tap """"""""title prompt"""""""") Result: Nav bar area rendered poorly Expected Result: Correctly rendered nav bar Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4182,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink:  Base UI>Views>Map View, zooming can cause out-of -memory warnings and crash on home button press on iPad""","""""""Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Map View, I zoomed the view all the way in and started receiving low memory warnings. I then pressed the home button and the console reported a crash. I could not reproduce the crash on the iPad 2 or on the iPad 1 with KS 1.6.2, but I could get the low memory warnings. See attached console output.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Map View 3) Zoom all the way in and watch the console   Result: Low memory warnings under the right conditions  Expected Result: No memory warnings  Notes: DOES NOT OCCUR on iPad 2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Views>Map View, zooming can cause out-of -memory warnings and crash on home button press on iPad
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Map View, I zoomed the view all the way in and started receiving low memory warnings. I then pressed the home button and the console reported a crash. I could not reproduce the crash on the iPad 2 or on the iPad 1 with KS 1.6.2, but I could get the low memory warnings. See attached console output. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Map View 3) Zoom all the way in and watch the console Result: Low memory warnings under the right conditions Expected Result: No memory warnings Notes: DOES NOT OCCUR on iPad 2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4181,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Status bar can get our of sync with UI on Phone>Play Movie>* tests""","""""""Description: When testing Phone>Play Movie>, and changing orientation after going full screen, the status bar will appear on the side while other elements will be rendered normally.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie> Embedded, Remote streaming, or Remote streaming 2 3) start in landscape 4) Go full screen with the video 5) Rotate the device to portrait 6) Come out of full screen video  Result: The status bar is on the side of the screen  Expected Result: The status bar should be at the top of the screen  Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 DOES NOT OCCUR on iPad 2 """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Status bar can get our of sync with UI on Phone>Play Movie>* tests
Description: """"Description: When testing Phone>Play Movie>, and changing orientation after going full screen, the status bar will appear on the side while other elements will be rendered normally. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie> Embedded, Remote streaming, or Remote streaming 2 3) start in landscape 4) Go full screen with the video 5) Rotate the device to portrait 6) Come out of full screen video Result: The status bar is on the side of the screen Expected Result: The status bar should be at the top of the screen Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 DOES NOT OCCUR on iPad 2 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4180,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker: Picker not rendered on iPad.""","""""""Description:  When testing Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker, the picker did not render. The iPad 2 had slightly better results with a little bit of the picker rendered, and some black text was seen.      Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1  2) Navigate to Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker    Result:  Picker is not rendered correctly    Expected Result:  Beautiful picker displayed    Notes:  OCCURS on 1.6.2  OCCURS on iPad 2 (except no bar and black letter visible.  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker: Picker not rendered on iPad.
Description: """"Description: When testing Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker, the picker did not render. The iPad 2 had slightly better results with a little bit of the picker rendered, and some black text was seen. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Controls>Picker>Countdown Picker Result: Picker is not rendered correctly Expected Result: Beautiful picker displayed Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2 (except no bar and black letter visible. """"",title+description
TIMOB-4179,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Modal Windows, choosing page curl then changing orientation results in poor animation""","""""""Description: When testing Base UI>Modal Windows, I brought up partial page curl, then rotated the device. The page curl did not rotate with the view. Closing the view in the state causes the animation to lewd bad since the curl has to move then animate.   Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Modal Windows 3) Choose page curl 4) Change orientation 5) Click close  Result: Curl stays in place during orientation change, then on close, animates poorly  Expected Result: Page curl moves with other UI elements  Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2 """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Modal Windows, choosing page curl then changing orientation results in poor animation
Description: """"Description: When testing Base UI>Modal Windows, I brought up partial page curl, then rotated the device. The page curl did not rotate with the view. Closing the view in the state causes the animation to lewd bad since the curl has to move then animate. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Modal Windows 3) Choose page curl 4) Change orientation 5) Click close Result: Curl stays in place during orientation change, then on close, animates poorly Expected Result: Page curl moves with other UI elements Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2 """"",title+description
TIMOB-4178,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink:  Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video will not play on iPad 1 ""","""""""Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video, I could not get the video to play in either 1.7.0 or 1.6.2. This test worked fine on the iPad 2.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video 3) Tap the movie   Result: The movie does not play. You may see a quick flash of the play arrow icon overlay the movie, but it quickly disappears.  Expected Result: The movie plays  Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 DOES NOT OCCUR on iPad 2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video will not play on iPad 1
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video, I could not get the video to play in either 1.7.0 or 1.6.2. This test worked fine on the iPad 2. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>HTML5 Video 3) Tap the movie Result: The movie does not play. You may see a quick flash of the play arrow icon overlay the movie, but it quickly disappears. Expected Result: The movie plays Notes: OCCURS on 1.6.2 DOES NOT OCCUR on iPad 2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4177,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink:  Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls loads blank page""","""""""Description: While testing KS, ase UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls, a simple sequence results in a blank page.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) When page loads, select any link 3) Tap """"""""back"""""""" 4) Tap """"""""reload""""""""  Result: Empty page is loaded  Expected Result: Google home page is reloaded  Notes: DOES NOT OCCUR ON 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Base UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls loads blank page
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, ase UI>Views>Web Views>Webview controls, a simple sequence results in a blank page. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) When page loads, select any link 3) Tap """"""""back"""""""" 4) Tap """"""""reload"""""""" Result: Empty page is loaded Expected Result: Google home page is reloaded Notes: DOES NOT OCCUR ON 1.6.2 OCCURS on iPad 2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4176,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink:  on some tests orientation change causes last few rows to animate poorly ""","""""""Description: While testing some tableview tests and changing the orientation, the last row or few rows animate by popping the content right during the animation (generally only from portrait to landscape). This happens on:  Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table with remote images (Occurs on 1.6.2 and iPad 2) Base UI>Views>Table Views>Delete Mode (Occurs on 1.6.2 and iPad 2) Base UI>Views>Table Views>Pull to Refresh (DOES NOT OCCUR on 1.6.2, occurs on iPad 2)   Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to one of the affected test cases (for """"""""pull to refresh"""""""", refresh enough to fill the screen with rows) 3) Start in portrait and watch the bottom of the table 4) Rotate to landscape  Result: Bottom of table animates poorly and out of sync with the other table contents  Expected Result: Animation of all items in sync without unneeded item moves  Notes:""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: on some tests orientation change causes last few rows to animate poorly
Description: """"Description: While testing some tableview tests and changing the orientation, the last row or few rows animate by popping the content right during the animation (generally only from portrait to landscape). This happens on: Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table with remote images (Occurs on 1.6.2 and iPad 2) Base UI>Views>Table Views>Delete Mode (Occurs on 1.6.2 and iPad 2) Base UI>Views>Table Views>Pull to Refresh (DOES NOT OCCUR on 1.6.2, occurs on iPad 2) Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to one of the affected test cases (for """"""""pull to refresh"""""""", refresh enough to fill the screen with rows) 3) Start in portrait and watch the bottom of the table 4) Rotate to landscape Result: Bottom of table animates poorly and out of sync with the other table contents Expected Result: Animation of all items in sync without unneeded item moves Notes:""""",title+description
TIMOB-4175,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink: Orientation change loses focus/delete button/closes view ""","""""""Description: When exercising various KS tests, orientation changes remove selections, delete buttons, and remove focus from text fields (and dismiss the KB if it's shown). Here are a list of the offending test cases: Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table View w/Text Field : Loses text field focus and dismisses keyboard (occurs on 1.6.2) Base UI>Views>Table Views>Delete Mode : If you select edit, then the minus to bring up delete button, delete button is gone after rotation (occurs on 1.6.2) Base UI>Animation>transitions (Occurs on 1.6.2) : Choose full view, then rotate to landscape, view is dismissed   Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table View w/Text Field  Tap on text field to give focus and invoke keyboard OR 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Delete Mode  Select edit then select minus to bring up delete button OR 2) Navigate to Base UI>Animation>transitions  Choose full view   4) Rotate device  Result: Path 1: KB dismissed, text field loses focus Path 2: Delete button removed Path 3: View is disposed  Expected Result: Textfield focus remains, KB still active. Delete button remains View remains  Notes:""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink: Orientation change loses focus/delete button/closes view
Description: """"Description: When exercising various KS tests, orientation changes remove selections, delete buttons, and remove focus from text fields (and dismiss the KB if it's shown). Here are a list of the offending test cases: Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table View w/Text Field : Loses text field focus and dismisses keyboard (occurs on 1.6.2) Base UI>Views>Table Views>Delete Mode : If you select edit, then the minus to bring up delete button, delete button is gone after rotation (occurs on 1.6.2) Base UI>Animation>transitions (Occurs on 1.6.2) : Choose full view, then rotate to landscape, view is dismissed Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on iPad 1 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Table View w/Text Field Tap on text field to give focus and invoke keyboard OR 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Table Views>Delete Mode Select edit then select minus to bring up delete button OR 2) Navigate to Base UI>Animation>transitions Choose full view 4) Rotate device Result: Path 1: KB dismissed, text field loses focus Path 2: Delete button removed Path 3: View is disposed Expected Result: Textfield focus remains, KB still active. Delete button remains View remains Notes:""""",title+description
