Description: """"To bring iOS in line with Android, expose SQL exceptions.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4170,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout, canceling login dialog loads odd """"page not found""""""","""""""Description: When running the Facebook tests, and bringing up the login dialog, choosing """"""""cancel"""""""" will load a """"""""page not found"""""""" page. See attached image.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink on Verizon iPhone 2) Navigate to Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout 3) Click login 4) when the login window is presented, click cancel  Result: Page not found loads  Expected Result: Dialog is disposed and user returned to test  Notes: Occurs with 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout, canceling login dialog loads odd """"page not found""""
Description: """"Description: When running the Facebook tests, and bringing up the login dialog, choosing """"""""cancel"""""""" will load a """"""""page not found"""""""" page. See attached image. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink on Verizon iPhone 2) Navigate to Mashups>Facebook>login/Logout 3) Click login 4) when the login window is presented, click cancel Result: Page not found loads Expected Result: Dialog is disposed and user returned to test Notes: Occurs with 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4169,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink Phone>Play Movie>Local can have appcelerator media control bar partially obscured by tab bar""","""""""Description: With a few steps, it's possible to get the <USER>media controls to appear partially behind the tab bar.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink on Verizon iPhone 2) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Local 3) play the movie. 4) enter fullscreen playback 5) Rotate to landscape 6) rotate to portrait 7) Return from fullscreen playback  Result: Media controls partially behind tab bar  Expected Result: Media controls fully visible  Notes: Could not reproduce on 1.6.2 because test does not allow orientation change""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink Phone>Play Movie>Local can have appcelerator media control bar partially obscured by tab bar
Description: """"Description: With a few steps, it's possible to get the <USER>media controls to appear partially behind the tab bar. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink on Verizon iPhone 2) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Local 3) play the movie. 4) enter fullscreen playback 5) Rotate to landscape 6) rotate to portrait 7) Return from fullscreen playback Result: Media controls partially behind tab bar Expected Result: Media controls fully visible Notes: Could not reproduce on 1.6.2 because test does not allow orientation change""""",title+description
TIMOB-4168,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink Controls>text field>Events, it's possible to focus, type, and see visible autospell text in hidden text field""","""""""Description: It is possible to hide the text field in Controls>text field>Events, then give it focus and type. While you do not see anything until you show the field, the autospell text suggestions appear as you type.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on Verizon iPhone 4 2) Navigate to Controls>text field>Events 3) Hide the field with """"""""Hide/Show"""""""" button 4) Give the field focus with """"""""focus"""""""" button 5) begin typing, try """"""""hellp"""""""" to get auto correct """"""""hello""""""""  Result: Auto spell text appears, and portion of field is highlighted (I assume where the text is present)   Expected Result: Auto Spell off, or does not appear when field is hidden.  Notes: Occurs in 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink Controls>text field>Events, it's possible to focus, type, and see visible autospell text in hidden text field
Description: """"Description: It is possible to hide the text field in Controls>text field>Events, then give it focus and type. While you do not see anything until you show the field, the autospell text suggestions appear as you type. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on Verizon iPhone 4 2) Navigate to Controls>text field>Events 3) Hide the field with """"""""Hide/Show"""""""" button 4) Give the field focus with """"""""focus"""""""" button 5) begin typing, try """"""""hellp"""""""" to get auto correct """"""""hello"""""""" Result: Auto spell text appears, and portion of field is highlighted (I assume where the text is present) Expected Result: Auto Spell off, or does not appear when field is hidden. Notes: Occurs in 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4167,12,"""iOS: KitchenSink Base UI>Views>Email Dialog does not present """"complete"""" alert when sending mail""","""""""Description: When testing Kitchen sink Base UI>Views>Email Dialog, there is no alert indicating that the mail was sent. There is the standard iOS """"""""Whoosh"""""""" sound as the mail is sent however.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on the Verizon iPhone 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog 3) Enter a real email address (to confirm receipt) 4) Send the mail  Result: Whoosh sound but no alert.  Expected Result: Alert (similar to iPad image attached)  Notes: Did not occur in 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: KitchenSink Base UI>Views>Email Dialog does not present """"complete"""" alert when sending mail
Description: """"Description: When testing Kitchen sink Base UI>Views>Email Dialog, there is no alert indicating that the mail was sent. There is the standard iOS """"""""Whoosh"""""""" sound as the mail is sent however. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS on the Verizon iPhone 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Email Dialog 3) Enter a real email address (to confirm receipt) 4) Send the mail Result: Whoosh sound but no alert. Expected Result: Alert (similar to iPad image attached) Notes: Did not occur in 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4166,12,"""Scroll when not dragging a Table View""","""""""Quick question for the iOS team...    An enterprise customer sent in pull request 85 on Titanium Mobile a while ago  https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/85    This makes it so the """"""""scroll"""""""" event of a table view fires after the user has stopped dragging the table.    But taking this as is would break existing code -- the event would fire more than anticipated, and it would operate inconsistently with Android (right now, they work the same).    So... my idea is we add a flag to let the user trigger this behavior. Something like """"""""fireScrollOnlyWhenDragging"""""""". This defaults to false, but can be set to true on a particular table view.    That would let us...        Resulting in a happy client and a consistent cross platform experience.    Thoughts?""""""",Story,"Title: Scroll when not dragging a Table View
Description: """"Quick question for the iOS team... An enterprise customer sent in pull request 85 on Titanium Mobile a while ago https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/85 This makes it so the """"""""scroll"""""""" event of a table view fires after the user has stopped dragging the table. But taking this as is would break existing code -- the event would fire more than anticipated, and it would operate inconsistently with Android (right now, they work the same). So... my idea is we add a flag to let the user trigger this behavior. Something like """"""""fireScrollOnlyWhenDragging"""""""". This defaults to false, but can be set to true on a particular table view. That would let us... Resulting in a happy client and a consistent cross platform experience. Thoughts?""""",title+description
TIMOB-4165,12,"""Android: openURL(""""tel:xxxxxxxxxx,xxx"""") command does not send paused tel: dial string""","""""""openURL(""""""""tel:xxxxxxxxxx"""""""") command does not send paused tel: dial string from Android  For iPhone the call would be """"""""tel:07966794444,1111"""""""" - which works  However for Anroid when trying """"""""tel:07966794444,1111"""""""" and """"""""tel:07966794444p1111"""""""" neither works   """"""""tel:07966794444,1111"""""""" just sends the first part - ie. 07966794444 but does not include the section after the comma   """"""""tel:07966794444p1111"""""""" removes the 'p' and sends the whole string as one - ie. 079667944441111  This functionality is required for functions such as calling card applications, conference call dialling, and automated extension calling  Is there a way to get this bug resolved/functionality built in?   Other apps (not built on Titanium) send the pause on Android, so it doesn't seem to be a core API issue  Output from the Dalvik Debug Monitor is   and  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: openURL(""""tel:xxxxxxxxxx,xxx"""") command does not send paused tel: dial string
Description: """"openURL(""""""""tel:xxxxxxxxxx"""""""") command does not send paused tel: dial string from Android For iPhone the call would be """"""""tel:07966794444,1111"""""""" - which works However for Anroid when trying """"""""tel:07966794444,1111"""""""" and """"""""tel:07966794444p1111"""""""" neither works """"""""tel:07966794444,1111"""""""" just sends the first part - ie. 07966794444 but does not include the section after the comma """"""""tel:07966794444p1111"""""""" removes the 'p' and sends the whole string as one - ie. 079667944441111 This functionality is required for functions such as calling card applications, conference call dialling, and automated extension calling Is there a way to get this bug resolved/functionality built in? Other apps (not built on Titanium) send the pause on Android, so it doesn't seem to be a core API issue Output from the Dalvik Debug Monitor is and """"",title+description
TIMOB-4164,12,"""iOS: NavBar Doesn't Update Properly When Touching """"More"""" to Return""","""""""h1. Problem  Given a tab group with more than 5 tabs, touching the """"""""More"""""""" tab to return to the list of """"""""More"""""""" results in the nav bar messing up. Let me quantify """"""""messing up"""""""": the title disappears, and the back button still exists.    It will be easier to understand what I mean if you run the sample code.    h2. Sample Code  Drop the following in an app.js then do the following:  # Touch the """"""""More"""""""" tab  # Touch """"""""Tab 4""""""""  # Touch the """"""""More"""""""" tab again (note: touch the TAB at the bottom of the screen, not the back button!)  # Observe the nav bar      h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-492924""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: NavBar Doesn't Update Properly When Touching """"More"""" to Return
Description: """"h1. Problem Given a tab group with more than 5 tabs, touching the """"""""More"""""""" tab to return to the list of """"""""More"""""""" results in the nav bar messing up. Let me quantify """"""""messing up"""""""": the title disappears, and the back button still exists. It will be easier to understand what I mean if you run the sample code. h2. Sample Code Drop the following in an app.js then do the following: # Touch the """"""""More"""""""" tab # Touch """"""""Tab 4"""""""" # Touch the """"""""More"""""""" tab again (note: touch the TAB at the bottom of the screen, not the back button!) # Observe the nav bar h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-492924""""",title+description
