TIMOB-4155,12,"""iOS: Ti.App.fireEvent strips native items from the event payload, despite this working fine when ""","""""""If you do a Ti.App.fireEvent('foo',{'bar':Ti.UI.createButton()}); the button is intentionally stripped. However, doing a Ti.UI.currentWindow.fireEvent('foo',{'bar':Ti.UI.createButton()}); does the right thing.    The issue lies in AppModule.m, lines 148-154.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.App.fireEvent strips native items from the event payload, despite this working fine when
Description: """"If you do a Ti.App.fireEvent('foo',{'bar':Ti.UI.createButton()}); the button is intentionally stripped. However, doing a Ti.UI.currentWindow.fireEvent('foo',{'bar':Ti.UI.createButton()}); does the right thing. The issue lies in AppModule.m, lines 148-154.""""",title+description
TIMOB-4154,12,"""Android: KitchenSink Phone>Sound>Remote streaming causes crash on Droid""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink Phone>Sound>Remote streaming, I clicked """"""""start streaming"""""""" before remembering that this particular link has already been reported broken. I then pressed """"""""back"""""""" and realizing this was the last test in the category, pressed """"""""back"""""""" again. The device crashed (see log attached).  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on Droid 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote streaming 3) Press """"""""start streaming"""""""" 4) Give up, and press """"""""back"""""""" on device 5) Press """"""""back"""""""" once more   Result: crash  Expected Result: continuing on with testing  Notes: Occurs on 1.6.2 as well. Does not occur on Nexus S""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink Phone>Sound>Remote streaming causes crash on Droid
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink Phone>Sound>Remote streaming, I clicked """"""""start streaming"""""""" before remembering that this particular link has already been reported broken. I then pressed """"""""back"""""""" and realizing this was the last test in the category, pressed """"""""back"""""""" again. The device crashed (see log attached). Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on Droid 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Remote streaming 3) Press """"""""start streaming"""""""" 4) Give up, and press """"""""back"""""""" on device 5) Press """"""""back"""""""" once more Result: crash Expected Result: continuing on with testing Notes: Occurs on 1.6.2 as well. Does not occur on Nexus S""""",title+description
TIMOB-4153,12,"""Android: KitchenSink Phone>Play Movie>Local in landscape mode with notifications present shows part of notification over movie""","""""""Description:  While testing KitchenSink Phone>Play Movie>Local, I rotated to landscape mode. I noticed a white bar obscuring part of the movie. This turned out to be a notification (fully viewed by pulling down the menu from the nav bar). PLease refer to screenshot. THis did not occur with 1.6.2.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KS 1.7.0 on Droid  2) ensure a notification is present (see additional screenshot)  3) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Local  4) Rotate to landscape    Result:  Notification visible    Expected Result:  Nothing but video visible    Notes:  Does not occur on 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink Phone>Play Movie>Local in landscape mode with notifications present shows part of notification over movie
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink Phone>Play Movie>Local, I rotated to landscape mode. I noticed a white bar obscuring part of the movie. This turned out to be a notification (fully viewed by pulling down the menu from the nav bar). PLease refer to screenshot. THis did not occur with 1.6.2. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on Droid 2) ensure a notification is present (see additional screenshot) 3) Navigate to Phone>Play Movie>Local 4) Rotate to landscape Result: Notification visible Expected Result: Nothing but video visible Notes: Does not occur on 1.6.2""""",title+description
