TIMOB-4142,12,"""Android: Rotating the device triggers the animation to start playing ""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Base UI > Views > Image Views > Animated 3. Stop the animation 4. Rotate the device  Actual Result: The animation starts playing again  Expected Result: The animation should not start playing  Note: Bug existed in 1.6.2 also""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Rotating the device triggers the animation to start playing
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Base UI > Views > Image Views > Animated 3. Stop the animation 4. Rotate the device Actual Result: The animation starts playing again Expected Result: The animation should not start playing Note: Bug existed in 1.6.2 also""""",title+description
TIMOB-4141,12,"""Compress / Change Size of Images when taken from the camera""","""""""Ability to change the compression / size of images in an app.     Example use case:  Developer wants a user to take a pic then immediately upload to a server.  iPhone 4's camera takes large pictures that might not be suitable in all scenarios.  The ability to choose the compression rate of the new image would be ideal.      It looks like we're using this method in TiBlob.m but would be nice to choose what the second arg value is instead of hardcoding it to '1' - http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/uikit/reference/UIKitFunctionReference/Reference/reference.html#//apple_ref/c/func/UIImageJPEGRepresentation""""""",New Feature,"Title: Compress / Change Size of Images when taken from the camera
Description: """"Ability to change the compression / size of images in an app. Example use case: Developer wants a user to take a pic then immediately upload to a server. iPhone 4's camera takes large pictures that might not be suitable in all scenarios. The ability to choose the compression rate of the new image would be ideal. It looks like we're using this method in TiBlob.m but would be nice to choose what the second arg value is instead of hardcoding it to '1' - http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/uikit/reference/UIKitFunctionReference/Reference/reference.html#//apple_ref/c/func/UIImageJPEGRepresentation""""",title+description
