TIMOB-4136,12,"""Android: VideoPlayer Doesn't Fire """"error"""" Event, Shows Alert Dialog Instead""","""""""h1. Problem  The """"""""error"""""""" event of a Ti.Media.VideoPlayer doesn't fire on Android.    h2. Expected Behavior  """"""""error"""""""" should be called, and the alert dialog should not appear by its own volition.    h2. Sample Code  The following code attempts to play a video that does not exist; this results in an alert dialog popping up saying """"""""Video View // Unknown error"""""""". The """"""""error"""""""" event is never fired on the VideoPlayer we created.      h2. Trace Log      h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-197698  http://appc.me/c/APP-584886""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: VideoPlayer Doesn't Fire """"error"""" Event, Shows Alert Dialog Instead
Description: """"h1. Problem The """"""""error"""""""" event of a Ti.Media.VideoPlayer doesn't fire on Android. h2. Expected Behavior """"""""error"""""""" should be called, and the alert dialog should not appear by its own volition. h2. Sample Code The following code attempts to play a video that does not exist; this results in an alert dialog popping up saying """"""""Video View // Unknown error"""""""". The """"""""error"""""""" event is never fired on the VideoPlayer we created. h2. Trace Log h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-197698 http://appc.me/c/APP-584886""""",title+description
TIMOB-4135,12,"""iOS: VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_ONE repeats forever""","""""""h1. Problem  """"""""VIDEO_REPEAT_MORE_ONE"""""""" (herewithin """"""""ONE"""""""") repeats the video forever. The docs state, """"""""the video will repeat once"""""""", so something is not quite right.    h2. Solution  Add a third constant, """"""""VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_INFINITE"""""""", and bind that to the existing behavior of """"""""ONE"""""""". Then fix """"""""ONE"""""""" so that it will repeat just once.    h2. Sample Code  The following code will repeat forever if the bug is present. Drop it in an app.js, and it will download the mp4 before it plays it.      h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/APP-667723""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_ONE repeats forever
Description: """"h1. Problem """"""""VIDEO_REPEAT_MORE_ONE"""""""" (herewithin """"""""ONE"""""""") repeats the video forever. The docs state, """"""""the video will repeat once"""""""", so something is not quite right. h2. Solution Add a third constant, """"""""VIDEO_REPEAT_MODE_INFINITE"""""""", and bind that to the existing behavior of """"""""ONE"""""""". Then fix """"""""ONE"""""""" so that it will repeat just once. h2. Sample Code The following code will repeat forever if the bug is present. Drop it in an app.js, and it will download the mp4 before it plays it. h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-667723""""",title+description
TIMOB-4134,12,"""iOS - rowHeight on tableView not working if data is empty""","""""""Setting """"""""rowHeight"""""""" or """"""""minRowHeight"""""""" on an empty tableview (ie. no rows) used to result in the rows respecting the height. Now it seems the rows always default to the standard 44 height until rows are added.    Here's a basic example:    The workaround being used by the customer right now is to define the tableview as:    This used to work with the 1.4.2    Helpdesk ticket:  http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-445788/homepage""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - rowHeight on tableView not working if data is empty
