TIMOB-4123,12,"""iOS: Label height set to auto should return """"auto"""" for Android parity.""","""""""Description: Setting label.height to 'auto' then reading the height value returns """"""""2"""""""". This bug was originally in the Android component as TIMOB-3202 and was fixed (set to return 'auto'). For parity, iOS should follow suit.  steps to reproduce: 1) Create sample app and replace app.js with:  var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({  backgroundColor:'white' });  win.open();  var label = Ti.UI.createLabel(); label.height = 'auto';  alert('Label height is: '+label.height);  2) launch the app  Result: The alert reports """"""""2""""""""  Expected: The alert reports """"""""auto"""""""" (for android parity)""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Label height set to auto should return """"auto"""" for Android parity.
Description: """"Description: Setting label.height to 'auto' then reading the height value returns """"""""2"""""""". This bug was originally in the Android component as TIMOB-3202 and was fixed (set to return 'auto'). For parity, iOS should follow suit. steps to reproduce: 1) Create sample app and replace app.js with: var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'white' }); win.open(); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel(); label.height = 'auto'; alert('Label height is: '+label.height); 2) launch the app Result: The alert reports """"""""2"""""""" Expected: The alert reports """"""""auto"""""""" (for android parity)""""",title+description
TIMOB-4121,12,"""Android: Orientation Change Doesn't Fire from Outside Tab Group""","""""""h1. Problem  The """"""""orientationchange"""""""" event on Ti.Gesture won't fire from app.js if you also create a tab group.    h2. Sample Code  Drop the following in an app.js and run it. Reorient the device, and an alert should be shown if the orientation change event fires, but this does not happen. If you take out the first 10 lines and uncomment the line that creates and opens a window, the event will properly fire.        h2. Who This Affects  There are a number of customers, pro and not, affected by this.    h2. Split From  This ticket was split from 2590, as it manifests the same issue but in a different scenario.  http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-2590""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Orientation Change Doesn't Fire from Outside Tab Group
Description: """"h1. Problem The """"""""orientationchange"""""""" event on Ti.Gesture won't fire from app.js if you also create a tab group. h2. Sample Code Drop the following in an app.js and run it. Reorient the device, and an alert should be shown if the orientation change event fires, but this does not happen. If you take out the first 10 lines and uncomment the line that creates and opens a window, the event will properly fire. h2. Who This Affects There are a number of customers, pro and not, affected by this. h2. Split From This ticket was split from 2590, as it manifests the same issue but in a different scenario. http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-2590""""",title+description
