TIMOB-4025,12,"""Android: KitchenSink sound tests - no audible volume difference above .3 level on Nexus S""","""""""Description: While testing KS, Phone>Sound>Local, the sound volume increased as I moved from .1 through .3. .4 - 1.0 sounded the same level as .3. This occurred with all the sound tests using the cricket sound: Phone>Sound>Local, Phone>Sound>Local with file, and Phone>Sound>Local with file URL. This did not occur on the eris. It is best heard through headphones also this is not a requirement.  Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Local and launch test 3) change volume from .3 to .4 and above  Result: No volume change  Expected Result: Smooth gain increase throughout the range  Notes:""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink sound tests - no audible volume difference above .3 level on Nexus S
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Phone>Sound>Local, the sound volume increased as I moved from .1 through .3. .4 - 1.0 sounded the same level as .3. This occurred with all the sound tests using the cricket sound: Phone>Sound>Local, Phone>Sound>Local with file, and Phone>Sound>Local with file URL. This did not occur on the eris. It is best heard through headphones also this is not a requirement. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Phone>Sound>Local and launch test 3) change volume from .3 to .4 and above Result: No volume change Expected Result: Smooth gain increase throughout the range Notes:""""",title+description
TIMOB-4024,12,"""Android: KitchenSink Soft Input test can leave soft KB active when closing test""","""""""Description: While testing KS, Controls>text field>Soft Input Focus, the soft keyboard remains on screen if the close button is clicked while it is visible.  Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base Controls>text field>Soft Input Focus and launch test 3) Click the 3rd field to bring up keyboard 4) Click the """"""""close"""""""" button  Result: Keyboard remains  Expected Result: Keyboard Hidden  Notes: Also occurs on 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink Soft Input test can leave soft KB active when closing test
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Controls>text field>Soft Input Focus, the soft keyboard remains on screen if the close button is clicked while it is visible. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base Controls>text field>Soft Input Focus and launch test 3) Click the 3rd field to bring up keyboard 4) Click the """"""""close"""""""" button Result: Keyboard remains Expected Result: Keyboard Hidden Notes: Also occurs on 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4023,12,"""Android: KitchenSink Options Dialog test will load upside down when device is rotated 90 degree clockwise""","""""""Description: If you launch the test Base UI>Views>Options Dialog while the device is rotated 90 degrees clockwise, the test loads upside down. This does not occur with 1.6.2.  Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on Nexus S 2) Rotate device 90 degrees clockwise 3) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Options Dialog and launch  Result: The test loads upside down  Expected Result: The test should load with the correct orientation (or at least fix to portrait)  Notes: """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink Options Dialog test will load upside down when device is rotated 90 degree clockwise
Description: """"Description: If you launch the test Base UI>Views>Options Dialog while the device is rotated 90 degrees clockwise, the test loads upside down. This does not occur with 1.6.2. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on Nexus S 2) Rotate device 90 degrees clockwise 3) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Options Dialog and launch Result: The test loads upside down Expected Result: The test should load with the correct orientation (or at least fix to portrait) Notes: """"",title+description
TIMOB-4022,12,"""Android: KitchenSink Local URL test - Zoom Controls do not function reliably until box """"Click above to hide me"""" is hidden""","""""""Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL, the view can be zoomed in and out using controls that appear when the view is manipulated. It seems that the controls are being interfered with by the box with the text: """"""""Click above to hide me"""""""". They usually don't function, but it's possible to get some activity when clicking on certain parts of the control. When this box is not present, then controls function as expected.  Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL and launch test 3) Touch and drag on view to bring up Zoom controls 4) Attempt to use zoom controls  Result: Zoom controls do not function or function partially  Expected Result: Zoom controls function as intended  Notes: Does not occur on 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink Local URL test - Zoom Controls do not function reliably until box """"Click above to hide me"""" is hidden
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL, the view can be zoomed in and out using controls that appear when the view is manipulated. It seems that the controls are being interfered with by the box with the text: """"""""Click above to hide me"""""""". They usually don't function, but it's possible to get some activity when clicking on certain parts of the control. When this box is not present, then controls function as expected. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL and launch test 3) Touch and drag on view to bring up Zoom controls 4) Attempt to use zoom controls Result: Zoom controls do not function or function partially Expected Result: Zoom controls function as intended Notes: Does not occur on 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-4021,12,"""Android: KitchenSink Local URL test - clicking """"hide me"""" causes webView to center""","""""""Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL, the instructions call for clicking on the text """"""""Click Me to Hide the Toolbar"""""""". When this is done, the webView shifts to the left. It seems like it is trying to center itself.  Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL and launch test 3) Follow instructions and click on text: """"""""Click Me to Hide the Toolbar""""""""  Result: View shifts to the left  Expected Result: No view shift  Notes: Does not occur on 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchenSink Local URL test - clicking """"hide me"""" causes webView to center
Description: """"Description: While testing KS, Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL, the instructions call for clicking on the text """"""""Click Me to Hide the Toolbar"""""""". When this is done, the webView shifts to the left. It seems like it is trying to center itself. Steps to Reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 on a Nexus S 2) Navigate to Base UI>Views>Web Views>Local URL and launch test 3) Follow instructions and click on text: """"""""Click Me to Hide the Toolbar"""""""" Result: View shifts to the left Expected Result: No view shift Notes: Does not occur on 1.6.2""""",title+description
