TIMOB-4016,12,"""AudioPlayer Progress is in milliseconds (iOS is Seconds)""","""""""For cross platform consistency we need to display the AudioPlayer progress in seconds instead of milliseconds.    Android Screen Shot: http://screencast.com/t/nMZzKcRg4 iOS Screen Shot: http://screencast.com/t/cdTMg9Vg0mr  For testing use Kitchensink>Phone>Sounds>Remote Streaming (KS Stream url seems to be broken so use: http://watoo.net:8000/INTRODUCTION.mp3)  HD Ticket Reference: http://appc.me/c/APP-964699""""""",Bug,"Title: AudioPlayer Progress is in milliseconds (iOS is Seconds)
Description: """"For cross platform consistency we need to display the AudioPlayer progress in seconds instead of milliseconds. Android Screen Shot: http://screencast.com/t/nMZzKcRg4 iOS Screen Shot: http://screencast.com/t/cdTMg9Vg0mr For testing use Kitchensink>Phone>Sounds>Remote Streaming (KS Stream url seems to be broken so use: http://watoo.net:8000/INTRODUCTION.mp3) HD Ticket Reference: http://appc.me/c/APP-964699""""",title+description
TIMOB-4015,12,"""TiAPI: Support BLOB data conversion""","""""""Support conversion of SQLite BLOB data.    Although it is understood that performance may be an issue, developers would like the ability to use BLOB data out of a database if necessary.  We currently only support 'blob' data not 'BLOB' data, so adding that support would allow for situations when an app may be passed BLOB data, the app could still <USER>the BLOB into an image or other file format.    This feature has been requested by a customer in the HD Ticket below.    HD Ticket Reference: http://appc.me/c/IKW-63226-771""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Support BLOB data conversion
Description: """"Support conversion of SQLite BLOB data. Although it is understood that performance may be an issue, developers would like the ability to use BLOB data out of a database if necessary. We currently only support 'blob' data not 'BLOB' data, so adding that support would allow for situations when an app may be passed BLOB data, the app could still <USER>the BLOB into an image or other file format. This feature has been requested by a customer in the HD Ticket below. HD Ticket Reference: http://appc.me/c/IKW-63226-771""""",title+description
TIMOB-4013,12,"""Debugger: Correctly scope variable info requests""","""""""For finding property values in frames:  We have to handle the following nasty connundrum:        function(x) { setTimeout(function() { Ti.API.info(x); }, 10000); }  Here, the IDE will make a request for frame[0].x if we have the variable highlighted PRIOR to the timeout callback (and this is the correct frame; the callback will be frame[0] unless it's initiated at some weird time) but x is not in the current scope chain - it is in the previous scope chain (due to the fact that the timeout function is a closure). """"""",Bug,"Title: Debugger: Correctly scope variable info requests
Description: """"For finding property values in frames: We have to handle the following nasty connundrum: function(x) { setTimeout(function() { Ti.API.info(x); }, 10000); } Here, the IDE will make a request for frame[0].x if we have the variable highlighted PRIOR to the timeout callback (and this is the correct frame; the callback will be frame[0] unless it's initiated at some weird time) but x is not in the current scope chain - it is in the previous scope chain (due to the fact that the timeout function is a closure). """"",title+description
TIMOB-4012,12,"""Smoketest""",,Sub-task,Title: Smoketest,title-only
TIMOB-4007,12,"""Closing a window in a nav group doesn't destroy the window""","""""""Scenario:  Inside a window that was opened in a tabgroup - when clicking the back button, the window closes but there is no easy way to set the closed window to null.  In this context, when the back button UI is generated automatically, the platform should handle freeing up the resources for the developer.  Attached is an examples that tries to mimic a customer's app as much as possible, although it's not an ideal way of doing this, it demonstrates the point..""""""",Bug,"Title: Closing a window in a nav group doesn't destroy the window
Description: """"Scenario: Inside a window that was opened in a tabgroup - when clicking the back button, the window closes but there is no easy way to set the closed window to null. In this context, when the back button UI is generated automatically, the platform should handle freeing up the resources for the developer. Attached is an examples that tries to mimic a customer's app as much as possible, although it's not an ideal way of doing this, it demonstrates the point..""""",title+description
