Description: """"h1. Feature Add support to the build scripts and Titanium Studio to generate an .IPA file with a distribution provisioning profile, instead of an .APP file. h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/APP-782151""""",title+description
TIMOB-3991,12,"""iOS: Intermittently, video record and save does not complete save process, hangs with progress indicator""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink 1.7.0, Phone>Camera>Video record, the video would begin to save, and would hang in this state with the progress indicator spinning.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 2) Launch Phone>Camera> Video record 3) Click """"""""record video"""""""" button 4) Click """"""""Stop"""""""" button  Result: A spinning progress indicator is displayed, and the device stays in this state  Expected Result: Progress indicator displayed for only a few moments, until the video is saved  Notes: Could not reproduce in 5 attempts on KS 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Intermittently, video record and save does not complete save process, hangs with progress indicator
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink 1.7.0, Phone>Camera>Video record, the video would begin to save, and would hang in this state with the progress indicator spinning. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KS 1.7.0 2) Launch Phone>Camera> Video record 3) Click """"""""record video"""""""" button 4) Click """"""""Stop"""""""" button Result: A spinning progress indicator is displayed, and the device stays in this state Expected Result: Progress indicator displayed for only a few moments, until the video is saved Notes: Could not reproduce in 5 attempts on KS 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-3990,12,"""iOS: Text change occurs, but flashes some intermediate text during transform""","""""""Description: While testing KitchenSink, Controls>label>Basic, clicking the """"""""change label 2"""""""" button once, then again will change the text as expected, but the text goes into an intermediate state before being enlarged.  Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink 1.7.0 on a supported iOS device 2) Launch Controls>label>Basic 3) Click """"""""change label 2"""""""" button 4) Click """"""""change label 2"""""""" again to restore the label to it's original format   Result: Before the label is restored to the large-font, shadowed text, it flashes into some other format prior to its end state.  Expected Result: Smooth text transformation between two formats  Notes: Also occurs with KS 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Text change occurs, but flashes some intermediate text during transform
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Controls>label>Basic, clicking the """"""""change label 2"""""""" button once, then again will change the text as expected, but the text goes into an intermediate state before being enlarged. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink 1.7.0 on a supported iOS device 2) Launch Controls>label>Basic 3) Click """"""""change label 2"""""""" button 4) Click """"""""change label 2"""""""" again to restore the label to it's original format Result: Before the label is restored to the large-font, shadowed text, it flashes into some other format prior to its end state. Expected Result: Smooth text transformation between two formats Notes: Also occurs with KS 1.6.2""""",title+description
TIMOB-3989,12,"""iOS: Controls>Picker>Time Picker - output time/date wrong seems wrong""","""""""1. Controls>Picker>Time Picker 2. tap a time, check the time values results: +00000  expected value off gmt - 7 I believe  exists in 1.6.2, seems verizon iphone specific """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Controls>Picker>Time Picker - output time/date wrong seems wrong
Description: """"1. Controls>Picker>Time Picker 2. tap a time, check the time values results: +00000 expected value off gmt - 7 I believe exists in 1.6.2, seems verizon iphone specific """"",title+description
TIMOB-3988,12,"""iOS: Rotating landscape to portrait makes click sound when index is not at 0""","""""""Steps to Reproduce:  1. Launch Kitchen Sink  2. Run Controls>Picker>Picker Custom Images  3. Up the volume on the device  4. Rotate the device to landscape  5. Rotate the device to portrait  6. Change the picker index to 1  7. Rotate the device to landscape  8. Rotate the device to portrait    Actual Result:  Hear a click sound    Expected Result:  To hear a click sound for every index or not at all""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Rotating landscape to portrait makes click sound when index is not at 0
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Controls>Picker>Picker Custom Images 3. Up the volume on the device 4. Rotate the device to landscape 5. Rotate the device to portrait 6. Change the picker index to 1 7. Rotate the device to landscape 8. Rotate the device to portrait Actual Result: Hear a click sound Expected Result: To hear a click sound for every index or not at all""""",title+description
TIMOB-3987,12,"""iOS: Close button pops to upper left of window as the window animates and closes""","""""""Description:   While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, clicking a dashboard icon (other than the first two icons) a window opens with a close button. When you click the close button, the button is moved to the upper left hand corner of the window and animates with the window as it closes.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KitchenSink 1.7.0 on an iPhone or other device  2) Launch Base UI>Views>Dashboard  3) Click an icon other than the first two to open the new window  4) Click the close button    Result:  The close button moves to the upper left-hand of the window and stays as the animation progresses    Expected Result:  The close button is removed, then the window animates as it closes    Notes:""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Close button pops to upper left of window as the window animates and closes
Description: """"Description: While testing KitchenSink, Base UI>Views>Dashboard view, clicking a dashboard icon (other than the first two icons) a window opens with a close button. When you click the close button, the button is moved to the upper left hand corner of the window and animates with the window as it closes. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink 1.7.0 on an iPhone or other device 2) Launch Base UI>Views>Dashboard 3) Click an icon other than the first two to open the new window 4) Click the close button Result: The close button moves to the upper left-hand of the window and stays as the animation progresses Expected Result: The close button is removed, then the window animates as it closes Notes:""""",title+description
