TIMOB-3976,12,"""iOS: Webview reload button loads original Google page even if navigated away from that page.""","""""""Description:  While testing using KitchenSink, specifically Base UI>Views>WebView Controls, I navigated away from the Google page loaded at the start of the test. Clicking the """"""""reload"""""""" button loaded the Google page again instead of reloading the page I was on.    Steps to reproduce:  1) Install KitchenSink 1.7.0 on the Verizon iPhone 4  2) Choose Base UI>Views>WebView Controls  3) When the page has loaded, choose any link on the page  4) Click the """"""""reload"""""""" button at the bottom of the page    Result:  The main Google page loads and displays    Expected Result:  The page you navigated to should reload and display    Notes:  Does not occur with KS 1.6.2""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Webview reload button loads original Google page even if navigated away from that page.
Description: """"Description: While testing using KitchenSink, specifically Base UI>Views>WebView Controls, I navigated away from the Google page loaded at the start of the test. Clicking the """"""""reload"""""""" button loaded the Google page again instead of reloading the page I was on. Steps to reproduce: 1) Install KitchenSink 1.7.0 on the Verizon iPhone 4 2) Choose Base UI>Views>WebView Controls 3) When the page has loaded, choose any link on the page 4) Click the """"""""reload"""""""" button at the bottom of the page Result: The main Google page loads and displays Expected Result: The page you navigated to should reload and display Notes: Does not occur with KS 1.6.2""""",title+description
