TIMOB-3911,12,"""Android: Creating a Module Fails if android-4 Not Available""","""""""If the Android SDK API Level 4 {{android-4}} is not available in the tooling. You are unable to create a module, also it prints a success message instead of a failure message.  1) Make sure your titanium command is aliased to the 1.7.0 build (Module docs)  2) If you have {{android-4}} in your platforms, rename the folder so it won't be recognized as installed.  3) At the command line attempt to create a module.     In fail state you get something like  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Creating a Module Fails if android-4 Not Available
Description: """"If the Android SDK API Level 4 {{android-4}} is not available in the tooling. You are unable to create a module, also it prints a success message instead of a failure message. 1) Make sure your titanium command is aliased to the 1.7.0 build (Module docs) 2) If you have {{android-4}} in your platforms, rename the folder so it won't be recognized as installed. 3) At the command line attempt to create a module. In fail state you get something like """"",title+description
TIMOB-3910,12,"""Android: App with Tabs that is pushed to Android 2.1 Emulator """"first launch"""" will crash""","""""""h4. Reproduce:  # Make sure all emulators are closed. # Open Ti Studio or Ti Developer.  If Ti Studio, set your default Android emulator to a 2.1 emulator. # Create a new project. # Launch the project to a 2.1 emulator.  h4. Result:  The emulator is launched (of course), but when the app is installed and then starts, it crashes:    After choosing to force close the app, it works fine on relaunch.  h4. Expected Result  Emulator launches, and app launches into it without crashing.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: App with Tabs that is pushed to Android 2.1 Emulator """"first launch"""" will crash
Description: """"h4. Reproduce: # Make sure all emulators are closed. # Open Ti Studio or Ti Developer. If Ti Studio, set your default Android emulator to a 2.1 emulator. # Create a new project. # Launch the project to a 2.1 emulator. h4. Result: The emulator is launched (of course), but when the app is installed and then starts, it crashes: After choosing to force close the app, it works fine on relaunch. h4. Expected Result Emulator launches, and app launches into it without crashing.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3909,12,"""Regression: iOS label click highlight does not work when clicking label""","""""""From KS:  * Control->Button * Click on 'Click Me' in label bounding box (on top of label, or around it) * --- Does not highlight label (should be green) * Click on 'Click Me' away from label bounding box (far left side of the button) * --- Does highlight the label (turns green)  Blain says the issue is related to the label swallowing certain types of touch info.""""""",Bug,"Title: Regression: iOS label click highlight does not work when clicking label
Description: """"From KS: * Control->Button * Click on 'Click Me' in label bounding box (on top of label, or around it) * --- Does not highlight label (should be green) * Click on 'Click Me' away from label bounding box (far left side of the button) * --- Does highlight the label (turns green) Blain says the issue is related to the label swallowing certain types of touch info.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3908,12,"""BlackBerry builder.py hard code a path to the JavaLoader.exe""","""""""The Titanium Studio is installing the RIM plugin as an eclipse plugin. However, it looks like the lookup for the JavaLoader executable is wrong in this case. The path that is constructed for the lookup is something like C:\eclipse\plugins\net.rim.ejde\vmTools\JavaLoader.exe, while the path on the plugged-in RIM plugin is something like C:\eclipse\plugins\net.rim.ejde.componentpack5.0.0_5.0.0.25\components\bin\JavaLoader.exe.  The path should probably be located by a look-up into the net.rim.ejde structure. If it's not there, like in the plug-in version, locate it at the latest version of the installed componentpack, probably under components\bin.    At the moment, this issue blocks TISTUD-323 from working well without a workaround of creating a plugins\net.rim.ejde\vmTools\ directory structure and manually copy the files into it. """"""",Bug,"Title: BlackBerry builder.py hard code a path to the JavaLoader.exe
Description: """"The Titanium Studio is installing the RIM plugin as an eclipse plugin. However, it looks like the lookup for the JavaLoader executable is wrong in this case. The path that is constructed for the lookup is something like C:\eclipse\plugins\net.rim.ejde\vmTools\JavaLoader.exe, while the path on the plugged-in RIM plugin is something like C:\eclipse\plugins\net.rim.ejde.componentpack5.0.0_5.0.0.25\components\bin\JavaLoader.exe. The path should probably be located by a look-up into the net.rim.ejde structure. If it's not there, like in the plug-in version, locate it at the latest version of the installed componentpack, probably under components\bin. At the moment, this issue blocks TISTUD-323 from working well without a workaround of creating a plugins\net.rim.ejde\vmTools\ directory structure and manually copy the files into it. """"",title+description
