Description: """"1.phone > sound > remote streaming 2.tap start 3.tap back button 4.tap back button again results: after a few seconds. app will crash. happens in 1.6.2 as well.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3884,12,"""Ti.Network.Socket.TCP.write() does not work on device""","""""""Turns out that on device, writing to a connected socket may fill the buffer and lock up the I/O because the condition never gets signaled.  Witness:  KS->Platform->Sockets->Listening socket Open the listener Connect via telnet Click 'write' -- About 1/3rd of text appears, everything locks up.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Network.Socket.TCP.write() does not work on device
Description: """"Turns out that on device, writing to a connected socket may fill the buffer and lock up the I/O because the condition never gets signaled. Witness: KS->Platform->Sockets->Listening socket Open the listener Connect via telnet Click 'write' -- About 1/3rd of text appears, everything locks up.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3883,12,"""Implement close() on the stream interface""",,Bug,Title: Implement close() on the stream interface,title-only
TIMOB-3876,12,"""iOS - Embedded video player bug - NavBar moves out of place""","""""""You will see the 'top' of the window shifts down at the same height as the status bar.    To reproduce in KS:    1. Go to Phone > Play Movie > Embedded Video in KS  (top video will start)   2. Click the arrows to go fullscreen while playing  3. Turn the simulator of device left or right orientation at least once. (You can stay landscape or go back to portrait)   4. Let the movie complete itself. (Do not press 'done')    This only seems to happen when the movie completes itself.     Clicking to another tab and back again appears to reset the top of the window back again.    Helpdesk ticket that reported this:  http://support.<USER>com/tickets/KYR-94554-295/homepage""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Embedded video player bug - NavBar moves out of place
Description: """"You will see the 'top' of the window shifts down at the same height as the status bar. To reproduce in KS: 1. Go to Phone > Play Movie > Embedded Video in KS (top video will start) 2. Click the arrows to go fullscreen while playing 3. Turn the simulator of device left or right orientation at least once. (You can stay landscape or go back to portrait) 4. Let the movie complete itself. (Do not press 'done') This only seems to happen when the movie completes itself. Clicking to another tab and back again appears to reset the top of the window back again. Helpdesk ticket that reported this: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/KYR-94554-295/homepage""""",title+description
TIMOB-3873,12,"""iOS: file.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_WRITE) crashes simulator if file doesn't exist""","""""""If a file doesn't yet exist, it should still be able to be open()'d writable.  This fails:  {code:title=example.js} var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory, 'not_exist.xx'); var stream = f.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_WRITE); // crash {code}  Problem is """"""""handle = \[NSFileHandle fileHandleForUpdatingAtPath:filePath\];"""""""" which requires the file to exist.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: file.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_WRITE) crashes simulator if file doesn't exist
Description: """"If a file doesn't yet exist, it should still be able to be open()'d writable. This fails: {code:title=example.js} var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory, 'not_exist.xx'); var stream = f.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_WRITE); // crash {code} Problem is """"""""handle = \[NSFileHandle fileHandleForUpdatingAtPath:filePath\];"""""""" which requires the file to exist.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3872,12,"""iOS: file.open(mode) crashes iOS simulator""","""""""Following code crashes:  {code:title=example.js} var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile('KS_nav_ui.png'); var stream = f.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_READ); // CRASH stream.close(); {code}  See [trace|http://pastie.org/private/jlvmqb1todzkhoywyahwng].""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: file.open(mode) crashes iOS simulator
Description: """"Following code crashes: {code:title=example.js} var f = Ti.Filesystem.getFile('KS_nav_ui.png'); var stream = f.open(Ti.Filesystem.MODE_READ); // CRASH stream.close(); {code} See [trace|http://pastie.org/private/jlvmqb1todzkhoywyahwng].""""",title+description
