TIMOB-3865,12,"""Android: App crash with combination of functioning debug session but failed fastdev session""","""""""I'm not sure if it's just this combination of circumstances, but I'm launching in debug mode from Ti Studio to an emulator session that is not working correctly in Fastdev.  The result is a crash because of an unprepared looper.  [See logcat|http://pastie.org/private/ae2lna7nohaevpovqsfpfq].""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: App crash with combination of functioning debug session but failed fastdev session
Description: """"I'm not sure if it's just this combination of circumstances, but I'm launching in debug mode from Ti Studio to an emulator session that is not working correctly in Fastdev. The result is a crash because of an unprepared looper. [See logcat|http://pastie.org/private/ae2lna7nohaevpovqsfpfq].""""",title+description
TIMOB-3864,12,"""Android: Fastdev """"connection refused"""" is not recoverable and doesn't revert to non-fastdev mode""","""""""My emulator is refusing the connection (for whatever reason -- see below).  When that happens, the builder.py <USER>continues on as though fastdev is enabled and doesn't do a """"""""full"""""""" rebuild but rather continues with the """"""""fast"""""""", highly optimized launch that Marshall instituted.  The only way at that point to get updated code to the emulator would be to touch tiapp.xml, which we should try to avoid telling users to do.  (Regarding the connection being refused: don't know why, so not sure what to put in a new ticket regarding that.  It was working, but then later wasn't.  Does the server shutdown at a certain point?  I left it running and unused for several hours (probably at least 5 hours), then when I started using it again it refused connection.)  [See trace.|http://pastie.org/private/s7gphpnblll0sdrfxok5jw]""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Fastdev """"connection refused"""" is not recoverable and doesn't revert to non-fastdev mode
Description: """"My emulator is refusing the connection (for whatever reason -- see below). When that happens, the builder.py <USER>continues on as though fastdev is enabled and doesn't do a """"""""full"""""""" rebuild but rather continues with the """"""""fast"""""""", highly optimized launch that Marshall instituted. The only way at that point to get updated code to the emulator would be to touch tiapp.xml, which we should try to avoid telling users to do. (Regarding the connection being refused: don't know why, so not sure what to put in a new ticket regarding that. It was working, but then later wasn't. Does the server shutdown at a certain point? I left it running and unused for several hours (probably at least 5 hours), then when I started using it again it refused connection.) [See trace.|http://pastie.org/private/s7gphpnblll0sdrfxok5jw]""""",title+description
