TIMOB-3799,12,"""iOS: in tableView using setData(rows) and data = rows  to set the rows keeps all of the previous rows in memory""","""""""If you use table.setData(rows); or table.data = rows; the rows that are being overwritten will be saved in memory.  Step 1: run the code below Step 2: run Instruments search for proxy (see that #Living grows each time and does not release, should release) Step 3: click the 'Reset Data' button Step 4: notice that the number of 'Labels' and 'Rows' grows by 100 on every button click    h3. Workaround  Did not work in (1.6.2). Worked with (1.7.0 Apr 27 2011 16:40 r3fb01972) here: http://builds.<USER>com.s3.amazonaws.com/mobile/master/mobilesdk-1.7.0-20110427164044-osx.zip  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: in tableView using setData(rows) and data = rows to set the rows keeps all of the previous rows in memory
Description: """"If you use table.setData(rows); or table.data = rows; the rows that are being overwritten will be saved in memory. Step 1: run the code below Step 2: run Instruments search for proxy (see that #Living grows each time and does not release, should release) Step 3: click the 'Reset Data' button Step 4: notice that the number of 'Labels' and 'Rows' grows by 100 on every button click h3. Workaround Did not work in (1.6.2). Worked with (1.7.0 Apr 27 2011 16:40 r3fb01972) here: http://builds.<USER>com.s3.amazonaws.com/mobile/master/mobilesdk-1.7.0-20110427164044-osx.zip """"",title+description
