TIMOB-3748,12,"""iOS: setInterval leaks CFStrings, CFDates and KrollInvocations""","""""""h1. The Problem setInterval leaks objects (and memory) on iOS. Even without anything in it, this can still be observed.  h2. Sample Code If you are feeling particularly adventurous, lower the period of the below code to 1 instead of 30. It will increase the rate of the leak and slow your computer down a bit, but the same behavior can be observed at higher periods such as 30 or 200. I did not test on anything longer than 200.    I ran the above code alone in an app.js using XCode's """"""""Profile"""""""" > """"""""Allocations"""""""" feature. It leaks at a rate of approximately 100 CFStrings, 100 CFDates, and 30ish KrollInvocations per second.  h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket There isn't one. I noticed this in one of our co-dev apps.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: setInterval leaks CFStrings, CFDates and KrollInvocations
Description: """"h1. The Problem setInterval leaks objects (and memory) on iOS. Even without anything in it, this can still be observed. h2. Sample Code If you are feeling particularly adventurous, lower the period of the below code to 1 instead of 30. It will increase the rate of the leak and slow your computer down a bit, but the same behavior can be observed at higher periods such as 30 or 200. I did not test on anything longer than 200. I ran the above code alone in an app.js using XCode's """"""""Profile"""""""" > """"""""Allocations"""""""" feature. It leaks at a rate of approximately 100 CFStrings, 100 CFDates, and 30ish KrollInvocations per second. h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket There isn't one. I noticed this in one of our co-dev apps.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3747,12,"""iOS - MapView route does not draw completely""","""""""There is a bug with the addRoute() of the Map View in iOS,  To test this open the Kitchen Sink.    - Base UI  - Views  - Map View with Routing    You can see on the left side of the MapView that some of the route is missing. You can tell because as soon as you move the map, the missing section of the route appears.    There is a helpdesk ticket that encounter this: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-997833""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - MapView route does not draw completely
Description: """"There is a bug with the addRoute() of the Map View in iOS, To test this open the Kitchen Sink. - Base UI - Views - Map View with Routing You can see on the left side of the MapView that some of the route is missing. You can tell because as soon as you move the map, the missing section of the route appears. There is a helpdesk ticket that encounter this: http://support.<USER>com/tickets/APP-997833""""",title+description
TIMOB-3746,12,"""Standardize Ti.Stream asynch callback responses""","""""""Need to standardize the results of Ti.Stream callback responses.  In particular:  - errorDescription should be an empty string if there is no error - errorState is a Number - errorState should be 0 if there is no error  Error codes are to be standardized at some point.""""""",Bug,"Title: Standardize Ti.Stream asynch callback responses
Description: """"Need to standardize the results of Ti.Stream callback responses. In particular: - errorDescription should be an empty string if there is no error - errorState is a Number - errorState should be 0 if there is no error Error codes are to be standardized at some point.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3745,12,"""Ti.Stream needs to call TiStreamProxy wrappers, not impls directly""","""""""Ti.Stream methods need to call wrappers for read/write (although not writeStream/pump - although that should be changed too). Right now they only call the internal implementations, due to wackiness that was caused by socket streams; instead, we should treat every call as synchronous.  This will involve some finessing of TCP sockets as well, to ensure that when an asynch operation is """"""""blocking"""""""", there are broadcasts on error.    This will also substantially reduce the complexity of some current code.""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Stream needs to call TiStreamProxy wrappers, not impls directly
Description: """"Ti.Stream methods need to call wrappers for read/write (although not writeStream/pump - although that should be changed too). Right now they only call the internal implementations, due to wackiness that was caused by socket streams; instead, we should treat every call as synchronous. This will involve some finessing of TCP sockets as well, to ensure that when an asynch operation is """"""""blocking"""""""", there are broadcasts on error. This will also substantially reduce the complexity of some current code.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3743,12,"""iOS: Closing a window containing a tableView causes the tableView data to be destroyed""","""""""If you close a window that contains a tableView, the tableView data will be destroyed, but the table is still intact.  Step 1: run the example below Step 2: click the test button Step 3: notice the [object TiUITableViewSection] alert Step 4: click the open button Step 5: click the close button Step 6: click the test button Step 7: notice the TiUITableViewSection does not exist    h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/IBS-79527-881""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Closing a window containing a tableView causes the tableView data to be destroyed
Description: """"If you close a window that contains a tableView, the tableView data will be destroyed, but the table is still intact. Step 1: run the example below Step 2: click the test button Step 3: notice the [object TiUITableViewSection] alert Step 4: click the open button Step 5: click the close button Step 6: click the test button Step 7: notice the TiUITableViewSection does not exist h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/IBS-79527-881""""",title+description
TIMOB-3742,12,"""Android: Date toLocaleString Doesn't Respect 24-hour Format""","""""""h1. The Problem  On Android, the JavaScript """"""""Date"""""""" object's """"""""toLocaleString"""""""" function doesn't respect the """"""""Use 24-hour format"""""""" setting in the """"""""Date & time settings"""""""".    h2. Code Sample  For example, place the following in an app.js.  * It will create a new Date on October 1st, 2011 at 1pm.  * Go in to the device's Settings app, then Date & time settings, and check """"""""Use 24-hour format"""""""".  * When you run the app, it will alert if the first 2 characters of theDate.toLocaleString() are 13, and thus if the 24-hour format is being used.        h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket  http://appc.me/c/WPP-21246-756""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Date toLocaleString Doesn't Respect 24-hour Format
Description: """"h1. The Problem On Android, the JavaScript """"""""Date"""""""" object's """"""""toLocaleString"""""""" function doesn't respect the """"""""Use 24-hour format"""""""" setting in the """"""""Date & time settings"""""""". h2. Code Sample For example, place the following in an app.js. * It will create a new Date on October 1st, 2011 at 1pm. * Go in to the device's Settings app, then Date & time settings, and check """"""""Use 24-hour format"""""""". * When you run the app, it will alert if the first 2 characters of theDate.toLocaleString() are 13, and thus if the 24-hour format is being used. h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/WPP-21246-756""""",title+description
TIMOB-3741,12,"""iOS - Install KS to device and emulator fails with errors""","""""""1. use the noted CI build 2. install a simple project to device or sim  fails with errors:  [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1306, in main     execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False)   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1066, in execute_xcode     output = run.run(args,False,False,o)   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.0/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run     sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65  NOtes: creating a new project works fine, seems to be about KS. injected since the pass last week""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Install KS to device and emulator fails with errors
Description: """"1. use the noted CI build 2. install a simple project to device or sim fails with errors: [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1306, in main execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1066, in execute_xcode output = run.run(args,False,False,o) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.7.0/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65 NOtes: creating a new project works fine, seems to be about KS. injected since the pass last week""""",title+description
