TIMOB-3687,12,"""Android: Facebook - publish stream - droid 1, after scrolling, buttons do not respond to touch ""","""""""1.Mashups > facebook go ahead and log in 2.go to publihs stream, and tap """"""""publish wall post with dialog"""""""" to invoke dialog 3.scroll up and down in dialog 4.try using the buttons results: you cannot, the buttons do not respond to touch  not seen on 2.3 or on 2.2.2 galaxy tab""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook - publish stream - droid 1, after scrolling, buttons do not respond to touch
Description: """"1.Mashups > facebook go ahead and log in 2.go to publihs stream, and tap """"""""publish wall post with dialog"""""""" to invoke dialog 3.scroll up and down in dialog 4.try using the buttons results: you cannot, the buttons do not respond to touch not seen on 2.3 or on 2.2.2 galaxy tab""""",title+description
TIMOB-3686,12,"""Android - 2.2 - webview zoom controls do not reflect zoom and do not function (on specific test) ""","""""""1.base UI > view > webview > local 2.drag your finger to invoke webview controls 3.tap them  results: they do not respond to touch expected: if we invoke them, let them work. 2.3 working as expected. other webview tests work as expected in regards to controls  new test / functionality so not a regression by definition""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - 2.2 - webview zoom controls do not reflect zoom and do not function (on specific test)
Description: """"1.base UI > view > webview > local 2.drag your finger to invoke webview controls 3.tap them results: they do not respond to touch expected: if we invoke them, let them work. 2.3 working as expected. other webview tests work as expected in regards to controls new test / functionality so not a regression by definition""""",title+description
TIMOB-3685,12,"""Android: Facebook - d-pad fires off 2X events for certain test cases""","""""""1.droid1 or N1 2.Base UI > window standalone 3.use dpad to launch a window 4.use touch to close (note it does not close), tap a second time  results: 2 windows were spawned.  also  1.Base UI > Window properties 2.use the d pad to give focus to and select """"""""layout dimension properties button""""""""  results: objects appear then dissapear quickly expecetd: as when using touch, one tap to spwan, one tap to dismiss""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook - d-pad fires off 2X events for certain test cases
Description: """"1.droid1 or N1 2.Base UI > window standalone 3.use dpad to launch a window 4.use touch to close (note it does not close), tap a second time results: 2 windows were spawned. also 1.Base UI > Window properties 2.use the d pad to give focus to and select """"""""layout dimension properties button"""""""" results: objects appear then dissapear quickly expecetd: as when using touch, one tap to spwan, one tap to dismiss""""",title+description
