TIMOB-3682,12,"""HTTPRequest objects don't seem to be released""","""""""HTTPRequest object does not seem to be released in some contexts.  Attached is a sample project with an example.  In the test app, it will build up but then show this for a few seconds and then disappear while still showing that the HTTP objects are being retained:  https://img.skitch.com/20110425-rext1pyqn2k33u1pjkapfqpbgp.jpg  then after a few seconds:  https://img.skitch.com/20110425-nj2h41y5kexrbya23yt1hgd34s.jpg""""""",Bug,"Title: HTTPRequest objects don't seem to be released
Description: """"HTTPRequest object does not seem to be released in some contexts. Attached is a sample project with an example. In the test app, it will build up but then show this for a few seconds and then disappear while still showing that the HTTP objects are being retained: https://img.skitch.com/20110425-rext1pyqn2k33u1pjkapfqpbgp.jpg then after a few seconds: https://img.skitch.com/20110425-nj2h41y5kexrbya23yt1hgd34s.jpg""""",title+description
TIMOB-3679,12,"""Android: Nexus One Only: The basic image does not load, but when you click the cloud image loads""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Base UI > Views > Image Views > Basic 3. Tap on where the titanium logo usually loads  Actual Result: The titanium logo is not loaded, but when you click the area it works as expected  Expected Result: To load the titanium logo""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Nexus One Only: The basic image does not load, but when you click the cloud image loads
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Base UI > Views > Image Views > Basic 3. Tap on where the titanium logo usually loads Actual Result: The titanium logo is not loaded, but when you click the area it works as expected Expected Result: To load the titanium logo""""",title+description
TIMOB-3678,12,"""Android: Track ball and D-pad control does not navigate to the first item of the list when navigating from tab""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Use the track ball to navigate around the tabs 3. From Base UI Tab navigate down with the track ball  Actual Result: Goes to preferences (Some random location on the list)  Expected Result: Should select the first item in the list""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Track ball and D-pad control does not navigate to the first item of the list when navigating from tab
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Use the track ball to navigate around the tabs 3. From Base UI Tab navigate down with the track ball Actual Result: Goes to preferences (Some random location on the list) Expected Result: Should select the first item in the list""""",title+description
TIMOB-3677,12,"""Android: Socket connection,  on connect second screen does not display """"Well, hello there!"""", cannot write or disconnect ""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run test plan from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Sockets+Test+Plan  Actual Result: Cannot write or disconnect After connecting to telnet the device cannot communicate  Expected Result: To get the same behavior as shown in the test plan""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Socket connection, on connect second screen does not display """"Well, hello there!"""", cannot write or disconnect
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Run test plan from http://wiki.<USER>org/display/tp/Sockets+Test+Plan Actual Result: Cannot write or disconnect After connecting to telnet the device cannot communicate Expected Result: To get the same behavior as shown in the test plan""""",title+description
TIMOB-3676,12,"""Android: Facebook - rotating the publish dialog to landscape hides the button and scrolling does not display the buttons""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Mashups > Facebook > Publish Stream 3. Login to facebook 4. Select Publish wall post with DIALOG 5. Rotate to landscape  Actual Behavior: Allows the user to scroll into a white space but never displays the publish or skip button  Expected Behavior: Should be able to get to the buttons """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook - rotating the publish dialog to landscape hides the button and scrolling does not display the buttons
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Mashups > Facebook > Publish Stream 3. Login to facebook 4. Select Publish wall post with DIALOG 5. Rotate to landscape Actual Behavior: Allows the user to scroll into a white space but never displays the publish or skip button Expected Behavior: Should be able to get to the buttons """"",title+description
TIMOB-3675,12,"""Android : Facebook - publish with dialog allows the user to scroll an empty white space""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Mashups > Facebook > Publish Stream 3. Login to facebook 4. Select Publish wall post with DIALOG 5. Scroll in the window  Actual Behavior: Allows the user to scroll into a white space  Expected Behavior: Should not allow to scroll if there is no content below""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : Facebook - publish with dialog allows the user to scroll an empty white space
Description: """"Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Mashups > Facebook > Publish Stream 3. Login to facebook 4. Select Publish wall post with DIALOG 5. Scroll in the window Actual Behavior: Allows the user to scroll into a white space Expected Behavior: Should not allow to scroll if there is no content below""""",title+description
TIMOB-3674,12,"""iOS: non-listened Label added to button suppresses touchdown button taps in the label's area""","""""""Go to Kitchen sink, Button, tap the 'click me' green button.    Compare tapping on the area taken by the label to the area of the button not covered by the label. They both fire 'click' events, but the button and label do not appear to hilight when tapping the label.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: non-listened Label added to button suppresses touchdown button taps in the label's area
Description: """"Go to Kitchen sink, Button, tap the 'click me' green button. Compare tapping on the area taken by the label to the area of the button not covered by the label. They both fire 'click' events, but the button and label do not appear to hilight when tapping the label.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3673,12,"""Black status bar area turns white after camera use""","""""""Go to Kitchen Sink, Phone, Camera, Camera Basic, take photo, use. Note that there is a white bar above the nav bar.  Go to Base UI, Window (standalone), Open (Fullscreen), close, note that the white bar has turned back to black.""""""",Bug,"Title: Black status bar area turns white after camera use
Description: """"Go to Kitchen Sink, Phone, Camera, Camera Basic, take photo, use. Note that there is a white bar above the nav bar. Go to Base UI, Window (standalone), Open (Fullscreen), close, note that the white bar has turned back to black.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3672,12,"""Drillbit tests fail for Titanium.Network.Socket.TCP""",,Bug,Title: Drillbit tests fail for Titanium.Network.Socket.TCP,title-only
TIMOB-3671,12,"""Android: Facebook module popup windows display in background if called from a fb event listener in a window created with the url property""","""""""If a window is opened using the url property and an alert or dialog window is called inside that window in a 'Titanium.Facebook.addEventListener' function the alert or dialog will open behind all windows.  Step 1: Run the code below Step 2: click the login button Step 3: the 'postToFeed()' dialog will appear behind the open windows. Step 4: hit the back button a couple times to see it Step 5: click the logout button. Step 6: an alert will fire but you will not see it. Step 7: hit the back button a few times to see the alert.  If you include the code from fb.js into app.js and not use the url property to open the window, the alert and dialog will open properly as expected even if you use a heavyweight window.  If you hit the 'Post' button after you are logged in, the dialog will pop up as expected. It is not called from a facebook event listener function.  app.js  fb.js   h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/IAQ-38639-246""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook module popup windows display in background if called from a fb event listener in a window created with the url property
Description: """"If a window is opened using the url property and an alert or dialog window is called inside that window in a 'Titanium.Facebook.addEventListener' function the alert or dialog will open behind all windows. Step 1: Run the code below Step 2: click the login button Step 3: the 'postToFeed()' dialog will appear behind the open windows. Step 4: hit the back button a couple times to see it Step 5: click the logout button. Step 6: an alert will fire but you will not see it. Step 7: hit the back button a few times to see the alert. If you include the code from fb.js into app.js and not use the url property to open the window, the alert and dialog will open properly as expected even if you use a heavyweight window. If you hit the 'Post' button after you are logged in, the dialog will pop up as expected. It is not called from a facebook event listener function. app.js fb.js h3. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://appc.me/c/IAQ-38639-246""""",title+description
