TIMOB-3667,12,"""iOS: Grouped Table, Contents Spill Out of Row Borders""","""""""h1. Problem In iOS, when setting the style of a table to grouped (iPhone) - the child object contents (tableviewrow and its children as well like images, views, etc) are not correctly bound by the table's borders. They flow beyond the table.  h2. Sample Code Below is sample code to reproduce the problem - the red box should be bound by the row it is in. Instead, it spills out.    h2. Tested On Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (04/05/11 10:30 731db9c...)  h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-386446""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Grouped Table, Contents Spill Out of Row Borders
Description: """"h1. Problem In iOS, when setting the style of a table to grouped (iPhone) - the child object contents (tableviewrow and its children as well like images, views, etc) are not correctly bound by the table's borders. They flow beyond the table. h2. Sample Code Below is sample code to reproduce the problem - the red box should be bound by the row it is in. Instead, it spills out. h2. Tested On Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (04/05/11 10:30 731db9c...) h2. Associated Helpdesk Ticket http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-386446""""",title+description
