TIMOB-3635,12,"""iOS: Set after Append (row obj) is mis-aligned when in landscape mode""","""""""Steps to Reproduce: 1. Launch Kitchen Sink 2. Run Base UI > Views > Table Views > Empty Table View 3. Rotate device to landscape 4. Append (row obj) twice 5. Scroll to the bottom 6. Press set  Actual Result: Top row is partially cut off (see image)  Expected Result: Should display from top of the row""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Set after Append (row obj) is mis-aligned when in landscape mode
