Description: """"{html}<div><p>Push notifications being included in every binary are causing apps to be rejected.</p> <p>I personally tried with an update to an app and got a rejection letter immediately after submission.</p> <p>For reference:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/118496/app-update-rejected-please-help""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/118496/app-update-reject...</a><br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/118492/problem-submitting-an-application---rejected""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/118492/problem-submittin...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3593,12,"""Android: Tapping to zoom in and out causes white flicker and sometime screen get cut in half""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps To Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink<br> 2. Run Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Web Views &gt; Local URL<br> 3. Double tap to zoom in and out</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Zooming out causes the screen to flicker and sometimes the screen get cut in half (see attached image)</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> Should not flicker on zoom and page size should not change</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)<br> Droid 1 2.2.1 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tapping to zoom in and out causes white flicker and sometime screen get cut in half
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps To Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink<br> 2. Run Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Web Views &gt; Local URL<br> 3. Double tap to zoom in and out</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Zooming out causes the screen to flicker and sometimes the screen get cut in half (see attached image)</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> Should not flicker on zoom and page size should not change</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)<br> Droid 1 2.2.1 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3592,12,"""Android: Creating new project fails if Android 1.6 (api 4) is not installed, though our base is now 2.1 (7)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Re-create (on 1.7.0):</p> <ul> <li>Go to your android sdk folder, and if """"""""android-4"""""""" is under platforms/, rename it to something else temporarily.</li> <li>Use Titanium Studio to try to create a new project for the 1.7.0 (current master) SDK.</li> </ul> <p>It will fail. The reason is shown in this trace:</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] No """"""""android-4"""""""" or """"""""android-1.6"""""""" in the Android SDK</code> </pre> <p>Somewhere we are incorrectly requiring Android API 4 (Android 1.6).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Creating new project fails if Android 1.6 (api 4) is not installed, though our base is now 2.1 (7)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Re-create (on 1.7.0):</p> <ul> <li>Go to your android sdk folder, and if """"""""android-4"""""""" is under platforms/, rename it to something else temporarily.</li> <li>Use Titanium Studio to try to create a new project for the 1.7.0 (current master) SDK.</li> </ul> <p>It will fail. The reason is shown in this trace:</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] No """"""""android-4"""""""" or """"""""android-1.6"""""""" in the Android SDK</code> </pre> <p>Somewhere we are incorrectly requiring Android API 4 (Android 1.6).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3591,12,"""ios_proxy_registration - intermittent crashes on 3g iphone""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.7.0.0.6c9e23f 3g iphone (3.1.3). Not seen in master, and not seen when using the 4gt ipod touch running 4.3</p> <p>1.No reliable repro steps, but seen 5X during todays run.<br> 2.Base UI &gt; Window (Standalone)</p> <p>results: while loading, or while tapping Open tab animation the app locks upa nd will crash.</p> <p>crash log attached, fwiw.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ios_proxy_registration - intermittent crashes on 3g iphone
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.7.0.0.6c9e23f 3g iphone (3.1.3). Not seen in master, and not seen when using the 4gt ipod touch running 4.3</p> <p>1.No reliable repro steps, but seen 5X during todays run.<br> 2.Base UI &gt; Window (Standalone)</p> <p>results: while loading, or while tapping Open tab animation the app locks upa nd will crash.</p> <p>crash log attached, fwiw.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3590,12,"""Android: Aborting large download causes runtime error""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink<br> 2. Run Platform &gt; XHR &gt; File Download<br> 3. Click on Large File Download<br> 4. See the progress bar run and then click abort<br> 5. Wait and error will display</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Runtime Error: Attempted read on closed stream</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> abort download without runtime error</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Aborting large download causes runtime error
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink<br> 2. Run Platform &gt; XHR &gt; File Download<br> 3. Click on Large File Download<br> 4. See the progress bar run and then click abort<br> 5. Wait and error will display</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Runtime Error: Attempted read on closed stream</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> abort download without runtime error</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3589,12,"""Android: After selecting a contact with image and then one without, the image still stays""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink<br> 2. Run Phone &gt; Contacts &gt; Contact Images<br> 3. Click get image from picker<br> 4. Select a contact with image<br> 5. Click get image from picker<br> 6. Select a contact without image</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Image from previous contact is still displayed</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To no display the last contact's image</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: After selecting a contact with image and then one without, the image still stays
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink<br> 2. Run Phone &gt; Contacts &gt; Contact Images<br> 3. Click get image from picker<br> 4. Select a contact with image<br> 5. Click get image from picker<br> 6. Select a contact without image</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Image from previous contact is still displayed</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To no display the last contact's image</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3587,12,"""Android: Setting """"Clear on Edit"""" clears the text when the user completes typing instead of when edit is invoked""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch KitchenSink<br> 2. Run Controls &gt; TextField &gt; The Rest<br> 3. Type something into the text field<br> 4. Click on """"""""Clear on Edit""""""""<br> 5. Click into the text field</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Text is not cleared, gets cleared when you hit done</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> Clear the text when edit is invoked</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Setting """"Clear on Edit"""" clears the text when the user completes typing instead of when edit is invoked
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch KitchenSink<br> 2. Run Controls &gt; TextField &gt; The Rest<br> 3. Type something into the text field<br> 4. Click on """"""""Clear on Edit""""""""<br> 5. Click into the text field</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Text is not cleared, gets cleared when you hit done</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> Clear the text when edit is invoked</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2 Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3586,12,"""Android: Tapping on the Window displays: you clicked on undefined""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch KitchenSink<br> 2. Run Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Events Propagation<br> 3. Rotate the phone to landscape<br> 4. Continue to click on """"""""D""""""""</p> <p>Actual:<br> You will see """"""""Window: You clicked on undefined""""""""</p> <p>Expected:<br> To return the clicked value everytime</p> <p>Note:<br> Also happens on portrait, but easier to reproduce on landscape</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2<br> Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1) and reproducible in 1.6.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tapping on the Window displays: you clicked on undefined
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch KitchenSink<br> 2. Run Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Events Propagation<br> 3. Rotate the phone to landscape<br> 4. Continue to click on """"""""D""""""""</p> <p>Actual:<br> You will see """"""""Window: You clicked on undefined""""""""</p> <p>Expected:<br> To return the clicked value everytime</p> <p>Note:<br> Also happens on portrait, but easier to reproduce on landscape</p> <p>Tested on:<br> Nexus S 2.3.2<br> Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (Apr 12 2011 15:24 rcc9dd9e1) and reproducible in 1.6.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3585,12,"""iOS - return to app after phone call""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is a feature request to return to the running app after a  phone call. There is a <a href=  """"""""http://stackoverflow.com/questions/3319805/detecting-call-state-in-ios4"""""""">  StackOverflow question</a> with an Obj-C answer, and a helpdesk  ticket (<a href=  """"""""http://support.<USER>com/tickets/WXM-61586-181/homepage"""""""">WXM-61586-181</a>)  asking for this feature.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS - return to app after phone call
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is a feature request to return to the running app after a phone call. There is a <a href= """"""""http://stackoverflow.com/questions/3319805/detecting-call-state-in-ios4""""""""> StackOverflow question</a> with an Obj-C answer, and a helpdesk ticket (<a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>com/tickets/WXM-61586-181/homepage"""""""">WXM-61586-181</a>) asking for this feature.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3584,12,"""ios_proxy_registration branch - crash cycling through modal windows""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.7.0.0.6c9e23f - 4gt ipod touch</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; modal windows<br> 2.cover vertical and fullscreen &gt; show modal &gt; close<br> 3.Flip horizontal and fullscreen &gt; show modal &gt; close<br> 4.cross dissolve and fullscreen &gt; show modal &gt; close</p> <p>results: I crash 8 out of 10 times with these steps. crash log attached.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ios_proxy_registration branch - crash cycling through modal windows
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.7.0.0.6c9e23f - 4gt ipod touch</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; modal windows<br> 2.cover vertical and fullscreen &gt; show modal &gt; close<br> 3.Flip horizontal and fullscreen &gt; show modal &gt; close<br> 4.cross dissolve and fullscreen &gt; show modal &gt; close</p> <p>results: I crash 8 out of 10 times with these steps. crash log attached.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3583,12,"""ios_proxy_registration - Windows (stand alone) """"toggle window"""" - window spawned does not close when spawning js is closed, and buttons flash when it draws in. ""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.7.0.0.6c9e23f 3g iphone (3.1.3). Not in master or 1.6.1</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; windows standalone<br> 2.Tap """"""""toggle window"""""""" and watch buttons on the bottom of screen</p> <p>results: the buttons flash as the window is drawn (not seen in master or 1.6.1)</p> <p>3.tap the base ui button to close the window and nav back</p> <p>results: the spawned window in step 1 persists (not seen in master or 1.6.1).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ios_proxy_registration - Windows (stand alone) """"toggle window"""" - window spawned does not close when spawning js is closed, and buttons flash when it draws in.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.7.0.0.6c9e23f 3g iphone (3.1.3). Not in master or 1.6.1</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; windows standalone<br> 2.Tap """"""""toggle window"""""""" and watch buttons on the bottom of screen</p> <p>results: the buttons flash as the window is drawn (not seen in master or 1.6.1)</p> <p>3.tap the base ui button to close the window and nav back</p> <p>results: the spawned window in step 1 persists (not seen in master or 1.6.1).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
