TIMOB-3467,12,"""ks-ipad + tiStud - issues with """"illegal"""" char in name""","""""""{html}<div><p>TiStudio is treating the """"""""-"""""""" as error, so the user experience when opening the project is one of immediatelty encountering an issue (though its a minor one).</p> <p>seems like we can work around this by renaming the project without using a """"""""-"""""""" (or other illegal char)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ks-ipad + tiStud - issues with """"illegal"""" char in name
Description: """"{html}<div><p>TiStudio is treating the """"""""-"""""""" as error, so the user experience when opening the project is one of immediatelty encountering an issue (though its a minor one).</p> <p>seems like we can work around this by renaming the project without using a """"""""-"""""""" (or other illegal char)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3465,12,"""Android: XML Cannot call method parseString if only defined inside an event listener""","""""""{html}<div><p>On Android, If parseString is only defined inside an event  listener then you will get an error.<br></p>  <h3>Note</h3>  <p>This only happens until you define it outside of the  eventListener once. After that it will work fine in that  application even if it is inside an event listener. In order to  reproduce this error you MUST create a new application.</p>  <p>Step 1: Create a NEW application<br>  Step 2: Paste the example below into app.js<br>  Step 3: Run the app<br>  Step 4: Click 'Find Foo'<br>  Step 5: Notice Runtime Error (picture of error attached)</p>  <pre>  <code class=  """"""""javascript"""""""">var xmlString = '&lt;items&gt;&lt;foo&gt;FOO&lt;/foo&gt;&lt;bar&gt;BAR&lt;/bar&gt;&lt;/items&gt;';    var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: 'green'  });    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({      title: 'Find Foo',      height: 60,      width: 100,    top: 40  });  button.addEventListener('click', function(e){      var xml = Titanium.XML.parseString(xmlString);    var element = xml.getElementsByTagName(""""""""foo"""""""");    Ti.API.info( element.item(0).text );  });    window.add(button);  window.open();</code>  </pre>  <h3>Tested on</h3>  <p>TiSDK 1.6.1, Android SDK 2.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: XML Cannot call method parseString if only defined inside an event listener
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On Android, If parseString is only defined inside an event listener then you will get an error.<br></p> <h3>Note</h3> <p>This only happens until you define it outside of the eventListener once. After that it will work fine in that application even if it is inside an event listener. In order to reproduce this error you MUST create a new application.</p> <p>Step 1: Create a NEW application<br> Step 2: Paste the example below into app.js<br> Step 3: Run the app<br> Step 4: Click 'Find Foo'<br> Step 5: Notice Runtime Error (picture of error attached)</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var xmlString = '&lt;items&gt;&lt;foo&gt;FOO&lt;/foo&gt;&lt;bar&gt;BAR&lt;/bar&gt;&lt;/items&gt;'; var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'green' }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Find Foo', height: 60, width: 100, top: 40 }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e){ var xml = Titanium.XML.parseString(xmlString); var element = xml.getElementsByTagName(""""""""foo""""""""); Ti.API.info( element.item(0).text ); }); window.add(button); window.open();</code> </pre> <h3>Tested on</h3> <p>TiSDK 1.6.1, Android SDK 2.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3464,12,"""Android: Throws NullPointerException when tag not found""","""""""{html}<div><p>In Android, when you getElementsByTagName() and element that  doesn't exist, It throws a NPE.<br>  note: iOS does not throw an exception</p>  <p>Step 0: Notice 'bas' is not in the xmlString in the example<br>  Step 1: Paste example code below into appi.js<br>  Step 2: Run example<br>  Step 3: Click 'Find Bas'<br>  Step 4: Notice the Null Pointer Exception</p>  <pre>  <code class=  """"""""javascript"""""""">var xmlString = '&lt;items&gt;&lt;foo&gt;FOO&lt;/foo&gt;&lt;bar&gt;BAR&lt;/bar&gt;&lt;/items&gt;';    var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: 'green'  });    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({      title: 'Find Foo',      height: 60,      width: 100,    top: 40  });  button.addEventListener('click', function(e){      var xml = Titanium.XML.parseString(xmlString);    var element = xml.getElementsByTagName(""""""""foo"""""""");    Ti.API.info( element.item(0).text );  });    var button2 = Ti.UI.createButton({      title: 'Find Bas',      height: 60,      width: 100,    top: 140  });  button2.addEventListener('click', function(e){      var xml = Titanium.XML.parseString(xmlString);    var element = xml.getElementsByTagName(""""""""bas"""""""");    Ti.API.info( element.item(0).text );  });    window.add(button);  window.add(button2);  window.open();</code>  </pre>  <h3>Tested On</h3>  <p>TiSDK 1.6.1, Android SDK 2.1</p>  <h3>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h3>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/WEJ-65612-589"""""""">http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/WEJ-65612-589</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Throws NullPointerException when tag not found
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In Android, when you getElementsByTagName() and element that doesn't exist, It throws a NPE.<br> note: iOS does not throw an exception</p> <p>Step 0: Notice 'bas' is not in the xmlString in the example<br> Step 1: Paste example code below into appi.js<br> Step 2: Run example<br> Step 3: Click 'Find Bas'<br> Step 4: Notice the Null Pointer Exception</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var xmlString = '&lt;items&gt;&lt;foo&gt;FOO&lt;/foo&gt;&lt;bar&gt;BAR&lt;/bar&gt;&lt;/items&gt;'; var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'green' }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Find Foo', height: 60, width: 100, top: 40 }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e){ var xml = Titanium.XML.parseString(xmlString); var element = xml.getElementsByTagName(""""""""foo""""""""); Ti.API.info( element.item(0).text ); }); var button2 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Find Bas', height: 60, width: 100, top: 140 }); button2.addEventListener('click', function(e){ var xml = Titanium.XML.parseString(xmlString); var element = xml.getElementsByTagName(""""""""bas""""""""); Ti.API.info( element.item(0).text ); }); window.add(button); window.add(button2); window.open();</code> </pre> <h3>Tested On</h3> <p>TiSDK 1.6.1, Android SDK 2.1</p> <h3>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h3> <p><a href= """"""""http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/WEJ-65612-589"""""""">http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/WEJ-65612-589</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3463,12,"""Can't have a """"é"""" in my app name...""","""""""{html}<div><p>Any compile is ok,but when my app's name contains """"""""&eacute;"""""""", there is an error:</p> <p>Install Error</p> <p>Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 850, in main</p> <pre> <code>os.system(""""""""/usr/bin/plutil -convert binary1 \""""""""%s\"""""""""""""""" % app_stylesheet)</code> </pre> <p>UnicodeEncodeError: 'ascii' codec can't encode character u'\u0301' in position 69: ordinal not in range(128)</p> <p>How can I fix that?</p> <p>Thanks;</p> <p>Ivan.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Can't have a """"é"""" in my app name...
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Any compile is ok,but when my app's name contains """"""""&eacute;"""""""", there is an error:</p> <p>Install Error</p> <p>Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 850, in main</p> <pre> <code>os.system(""""""""/usr/bin/plutil -convert binary1 \""""""""%s\"""""""""""""""" % app_stylesheet)</code> </pre> <p>UnicodeEncodeError: 'ascii' codec can't encode character u'\u0301' in position 69: ordinal not in range(128)</p> <p>How can I fix that?</p> <p>Thanks;</p> <p>Ivan.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
