TIMOB-3460,12,"""iOS: TabGroup Reaction to Orientation Changes""","""""""{html}<div><p>So I have 3 tabs added to my TabGroup, with 1 window per  tab.</p>  <pre>  <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow();    var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win1});  var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win2});  var tab3 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win3});</code>  </pre>  <p>So I want win1 to allow the following orientations:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>Ti.UI.PORTRAIT  Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT  Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT  Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT</code>  </pre>  <p>But only allow win2 and win3 the first two (PORTRAIT and  UPSIDE_PORTRAIT), so I set the orientationModes of the  windows:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup({barColor:'#000'});    var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow();    win1.orientationModes = [      Ti.UI.PORTRAIT,      Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT,      Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT,      Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT  ];  win2.orientationModes = [      Ti.UI.PORTRAIT,      Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT  ];  win3.orientationModes = [      Ti.UI.PORTRAIT,      Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT  ];    var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win1});  var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win2});  var tab3 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win3});    tabGroup.addTab(tab1);  tabGroup.addTab(tab2);  tabGroup.addTab(tab3);  tabGroup.open();</code>  </pre>  <p>So when you are in win1 and change the orientation of the  device/simulator to landscape and then click onto either of tab2 or  tab3 (Switching to win2 or win3), the orientation will change but  the tabs will react oddly.</p>  <p>The third one will simply disappear with the first two (tab1  &amp; tab2) resizing to be half the tabGroup. After that, there  seems to be no way to get the tab back without closing the app.</p>  <p>Note that this is using <strong>Titanium Mobile 1.6.1</strong>,  <strong>Titanium Developer 1.3.0</strong>, and using <strong>iOS  4.3[.1]</strong>.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TabGroup Reaction to Orientation Changes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>So I have 3 tabs added to my TabGroup, with 1 window per tab.</p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win1}); var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win2}); var tab3 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win3});</code> </pre> <p>So I want win1 to allow the following orientations:<br></p> <pre> <code>Ti.UI.PORTRAIT Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT</code> </pre> <p>But only allow win2 and win3 the first two (PORTRAIT and UPSIDE_PORTRAIT), so I set the orientationModes of the windows:<br></p> <pre> <code>var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup({barColor:'#000'}); var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); win1.orientationModes = [ Ti.UI.PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT, Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT ]; win2.orientationModes = [ Ti.UI.PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT ]; win3.orientationModes = [ Ti.UI.PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT ]; var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win1}); var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win2}); var tab3 = Ti.UI.createTab({window:win3}); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.addTab(tab2); tabGroup.addTab(tab3); tabGroup.open();</code> </pre> <p>So when you are in win1 and change the orientation of the device/simulator to landscape and then click onto either of tab2 or tab3 (Switching to win2 or win3), the orientation will change but the tabs will react oddly.</p> <p>The third one will simply disappear with the first two (tab1 &amp; tab2) resizing to be half the tabGroup. After that, there seems to be no way to get the tab back without closing the app.</p> <p>Note that this is using <strong>Titanium Mobile 1.6.1</strong>, <strong>Titanium Developer 1.3.0</strong>, and using <strong>iOS 4.3[.1]</strong>.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3459,12,"""Android Basic picker shows up behind heavyweight window""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using the code attached, if the window is set as a heavyweight window, the option dialogue will show up behind the window.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Basic picker shows up behind heavyweight window
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using the code attached, if the window is set as a heavyweight window, the option dialogue will show up behind the window.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3458,12,"""iOS: ScrollableView not firing swipe or touchend events""","""""""{html}<div><p>I've added code and description of the issue here:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117589/scrollableview-not-firing-swipe-nor-touchend-events"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/117589/scrollableview-no...</a></p>  <p>Currently if a user swipes quickly a scrollableview, then there  is no way of knowing on what page they are until they stop  scrolling.</p>  <p>Another issue is described here:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117588/scrollableview-not-firing-scroll-event-always"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/117588/scrollableview-no...</a></p>  <p>That has an example of the scroll event not getting fired all  the time.</p>  <p>This has been tested with Ti 1.6 and several iPhones from 3 to  4.2</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollableView not firing swipe or touchend events
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I've added code and description of the issue here:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117589/scrollableview-not-firing-swipe-nor-touchend-events""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/117589/scrollableview-no...</a></p> <p>Currently if a user swipes quickly a scrollableview, then there is no way of knowing on what page they are until they stop scrolling.</p> <p>Another issue is described here:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117588/scrollableview-not-firing-scroll-event-always""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/117588/scrollableview-no...</a></p> <p>That has an example of the scroll event not getting fired all the time.</p> <p>This has been tested with Ti 1.6 and several iPhones from 3 to 4.2</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3456,12,"""omitting borderStyle for TextField causes it to be invisible""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you do not specify a borderStyle property on iOS, the text field is not displayed in a window despite having a height, width, etc. There should be a default for this value if none is supplied, and the text field should still be displayed.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: omitting borderStyle for TextField causes it to be invisible
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you do not specify a borderStyle property on iOS, the text field is not displayed in a window despite having a height, width, etc. There should be a default for this value if none is supplied, and the text field should still be displayed.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3453,12,"""Android: plain picker fires change event immediately (bug reintroduced)""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is old bug, here is a ticket:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobile/tickets/1723""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobi...</a></p> <p>I've tested fail case code on Galaxy Tab, it works fine with Titanium SDK 1.5, but it doesn't work with 1.6 branch.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: plain picker fires change event immediately (bug reintroduced)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is old bug, here is a ticket:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobile/tickets/1723""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobi...</a></p> <p>I've tested fail case code on Galaxy Tab, it works fine with Titanium SDK 1.5, but it doesn't work with 1.6 branch.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3452,12,"""Android: Must click TextField twice in TableViewRow in 2nd Tab inside TabGroup to display keyboard""","""""""{html}<div><p>Environment:</p>  <ul>  <li>TiDev 1.2.2</li>  <li>Ti SDK 1.6.1</li>  <li>Android SDK 2.2</li>  <li>tested in emulator only</li>  </ul>  <p>This issue was first discovered by user """"""""JH"""""""" in this <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117540/textfield-on-tableview-loses-focus-android#"""""""">  Q&amp;A post</a></p>  <p>With a textField added to a tableViewRow on a secondary tab, the  user must click it twice to display a numeric keyboard. This is  demonstrated by the following code:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({    title:""""""""Window 1""""""""  });    var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({    title:""""""""Tab 1"""""""",    window: win1  });     var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({    title:""""""""Window 2""""""""  });    var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({});  var tF = Ti.UI.createTextField({    keyboardType:Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_NUMBERS_PUNCTUATION,    width:300  });    row.add(tF);  var tV = Ti.UI.createTableView({data:[row]});  //win1.add(tV); // this works as expected  win2.add(tV); // this demonstrates the issue     var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({      title:'Tab 2',    window: win2  });     var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();  tabGroup.addTab(tab1);  tabGroup.addTab(tab2);  tabGroup.open();</code>  </pre>  <p>The issue does not exist when a tableView or tabGroup are not  used, and 1.5.1 exhibits the correct behavior</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Must click TextField twice in TableViewRow in 2nd Tab inside TabGroup to display keyboard
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Environment:</p> <ul> <li>TiDev 1.2.2</li> <li>Ti SDK 1.6.1</li> <li>Android SDK 2.2</li> <li>tested in emulator only</li> </ul> <p>This issue was first discovered by user """"""""JH"""""""" in this <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117540/textfield-on-tableview-loses-focus-android#""""""""> Q&amp;A post</a></p> <p>With a textField added to a tableViewRow on a secondary tab, the user must click it twice to display a numeric keyboard. This is demonstrated by the following code:<br></p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title:""""""""Window 1"""""""" }); var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({ title:""""""""Tab 1"""""""", window: win1 }); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title:""""""""Window 2"""""""" }); var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({}); var tF = Ti.UI.createTextField({ keyboardType:Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_NUMBERS_PUNCTUATION, width:300 }); row.add(tF); var tV = Ti.UI.createTableView({data:[row]}); //win1.add(tV); // this works as expected win2.add(tV); // this demonstrates the issue var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({ title:'Tab 2', window: win2 }); var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.addTab(tab2); tabGroup.open();</code> </pre> <p>The issue does not exist when a tableView or tabGroup are not used, and 1.5.1 exhibits the correct behavior</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3451,12,"""Android: TextField in TableViewRow in 2nd Tab in TabGroup loses focus on keyboard display""","""""""{html}<div><p>Environment:</p>  <ul>  <li>TiDev 1.2.2</li>  <li>Ti SDK 2.0.1GA2</li>  <li>Android SDK 2.2</li>  <li>tested in emulator only</li>  </ul>  <p>This issue was first discovered by user """"""""JH"""""""" in this <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117540/textfield-on-tableview-loses-focus-android#"""""""">  Q&amp;A post</a></p>  <p>With a textField added to a tableViewRow on a secondary tab, the  user clicks it and the keyboard appears but the textField loses  focus. This is demonstrated by the following code:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({    title:""""""""Window 1""""""""  });    var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({    title:""""""""Tab 1"""""""",    window: win1  });     var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({    title:""""""""Window 2""""""""  });    var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({});  var tF = Ti.UI.createTextField({  //  keyboardType:Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_NUMBERS_PUNCTUATION, // another issue reported in next ticket    width:300  });    row.add(tF);  var tV = Ti.UI.createTableView({data:[row]});  //win1.add(tV); // this works as expected  win2.add(tV); // this demonstrates the issue     var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({      title:'Tab 2',    window: win2  });     var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();  tabGroup.addTab(tab1);  tabGroup.addTab(tab2);  tabGroup.open();</code>  </pre>  <p>The issue does not exist when a tableView or tabGroup are not  used, and 1.5.1 exhibits the correct behavior</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TextField in TableViewRow in 2nd Tab in TabGroup loses focus on keyboard display
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Environment:</p> <ul> <li>TiDev 1.2.2</li> <li>Ti SDK 2.0.1GA2</li> <li>Android SDK 2.2</li> <li>tested in emulator only</li> </ul> <p>This issue was first discovered by user """"""""JH"""""""" in this <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117540/textfield-on-tableview-loses-focus-android#""""""""> Q&amp;A post</a></p> <p>With a textField added to a tableViewRow on a secondary tab, the user clicks it and the keyboard appears but the textField loses focus. This is demonstrated by the following code:<br></p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title:""""""""Window 1"""""""" }); var tab1 = Ti.UI.createTab({ title:""""""""Tab 1"""""""", window: win1 }); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title:""""""""Window 2"""""""" }); var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({}); var tF = Ti.UI.createTextField({ // keyboardType:Ti.UI.KEYBOARD_NUMBERS_PUNCTUATION, // another issue reported in next ticket width:300 }); row.add(tF); var tV = Ti.UI.createTableView({data:[row]}); //win1.add(tV); // this works as expected win2.add(tV); // this demonstrates the issue var tab2 = Ti.UI.createTab({ title:'Tab 2', window: win2 }); var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.addTab(tab2); tabGroup.open();</code> </pre> <p>The issue does not exist when a tableView or tabGroup are not used, and 1.5.1 exhibits the correct behavior</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3450,12,"""iOS table view ""","""""""{html}<div><pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(w, {animated: true});   ...   b.addEventListener('click',function() {     w.close({animated:true});   });</code> </pre> <p>fade in animation exists for title and nav buttons when opening (window slide in from the right)<br> but fade out animation doesn not exist</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS table view
Description: """"{html}<div><pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(w, {animated: true}); ... b.addEventListener('click',function() { w.close({animated:true}); });</code> </pre> <p>fade in animation exists for title and nav buttons when opening (window slide in from the right)<br> but fade out animation doesn not exist</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3449,12,"""Android: ImageView with remote image fails in Honeycomb""","""""""{html}<div><p>Fail-case app.js, which is supposed to show <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/assets/img/a-logo.png"""""""">this image</a> in an ImageView:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({     height: """"""""auto"""""""", width: """"""""auto"""""""",     image: 'http://developer.<USER>com/assets/img/a-logo.png' }); win.add(iv); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>When you run it in Honeycomb, the image will not appear and you will see this exception if you look at logcat:</p> <pre> <code>E/TiDownloadManager( 1920): java.lang.NullPointerException E/TiDownloadManager( 1920):     at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiResponseCache.makeLowerCaseHeaders(TiResponseCache.java:302) E/TiDownloadManager( 1920):     at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiResponseCache.put(TiResponseCache.java:314) etc...</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView with remote image fails in Honeycomb
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Fail-case app.js, which is supposed to show <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/assets/img/a-logo.png"""""""">this image</a> in an ImageView:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({ height: """"""""auto"""""""", width: """"""""auto"""""""", image: 'http://developer.<USER>com/assets/img/a-logo.png' }); win.add(iv); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>When you run it in Honeycomb, the image will not appear and you will see this exception if you look at logcat:</p> <pre> <code>E/TiDownloadManager( 1920): java.lang.NullPointerException E/TiDownloadManager( 1920): at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiResponseCache.makeLowerCaseHeaders(TiResponseCache.java:302) E/TiDownloadManager( 1920): at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiResponseCache.put(TiResponseCache.java:314) etc...</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3448,12,"""Android: cannot retrieve EXTRA_STREAM from Intent (no getUriExtra)""","""""""{html}<div><p>I'm using Titanium Mobile 1.5/1.6's support for native Android intents and activities to let our StatusNet Mobile app accept text and image attachments from other social networking apps and the system Gallery and Camera apps.</p> <p>Unfortunately I'm having some trouble accepting images, which are attached as a Uri object in the EXTRA_STREAM extra field. Calling intent.getStringExtra(Ti.Android.EXTRA_STREAM) fails, because the returned object is a Uri, not a string:</p> <pre> <code>W/Bundle  ( 1569): Key android.intent.extra.STREAM expected String but value was a android.net.Uri$HierarchicalUri.  The default value &lt;null&gt; was returned. W/Bundle  ( 1569): Attempt to cast generated internal exception: W/Bundle  ( 1569): java.lang.ClassCastException: android.net.Uri$HierarchicalUri W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.os.Bundle.getString(Bundle.java:1040) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.content.Intent.getStringExtra(Intent.java:3368) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.proxy.IntentProxy.getStringExtra(IntentProxy.java:239) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.proxy.IntentProxyBindingGen$3.invoke(IntentProxyBindingGen.java:187) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollMethod.call(KrollMethod.java:51) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpretLoop(Interpreter.java:1711) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpret(Interpreter.java:854) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.mozilla.javascript.InterpretedFunction.call(InterpretedFunction.java:164) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ContextFactory.doTopCall(ContextFactory.java:426) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.doTopCall(ScriptRuntime.java:3161) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.mozilla.javascript.InterpretedFunction.call(InterpretedFunction.java:162) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:139) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:113) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:108) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:104) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollProxy.fireSingleEvent(KrollProxy.java:629) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollEventManager$KrollListener.invoke(KrollEventManager.java:143) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollEventManager.dispatchEvent(KrollEventManager.java:273) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>kroll.KrollProxy.fireSyncEvent(KrollProxy.java:600) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.TiBaseActivity.onCreate(TiBaseActivity.java:294) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at org.<USER>titanium.TiLaunchActivity.onCreate(TiLaunchActivity.java:97) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.app.Instrumentation.callActivityOnCreate(Instrumentation.java:1047) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.app.ActivityThread.performLaunchActivity(ActivityThread.java:2627) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.app.ActivityThread.handleLaunchActivity(ActivityThread.java:2679) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.app.ActivityThread.access$2300(ActivityThread.java:125) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.app.ActivityThread$H.handleMessage(ActivityThread.java:2033) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:99) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at android.app.ActivityThread.main(ActivityThread.java:4627) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at java.lang.reflect.Method.invokeNative(Native Method) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:521) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit$MethodAndArgsCaller.run(ZygoteInit.java:868) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit.main(ZygoteInit.java:626) W/Bundle  ( 1569):  at dalvik.system.NativeStart.main(Native Method)</code> </pre> <p>I notice in ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2587"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2587"""""""">#2587</a>, someone encountered the same problem when <em>creating</em> such intents to send to other applications, and an Intent.putUriExtra() was added to accommodate it, converting from a string parameter to a Uri.</p> <p>It looks like it would be helpful to add an Intent.getUriExtra(), or else tweak things such that there's some other clear way to retrieve it.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: cannot retrieve EXTRA_STREAM from Intent (no getUriExtra)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I'm using Titanium Mobile 1.5/1.6's support for native Android intents and activities to let our StatusNet Mobile app accept text and image attachments from other social networking apps and the system Gallery and Camera apps.</p> <p>Unfortunately I'm having some trouble accepting images, which are attached as a Uri object in the EXTRA_STREAM extra field. Calling intent.getStringExtra(Ti.Android.EXTRA_STREAM) fails, because the returned object is a Uri, not a string:</p> <pre> <code>W/Bundle ( 1569): Key android.intent.extra.STREAM expected String but value was a android.net.Uri$HierarchicalUri. The default value &lt;null&gt; was returned. W/Bundle ( 1569): Attempt to cast generated internal exception: W/Bundle ( 1569): java.lang.ClassCastException: android.net.Uri$HierarchicalUri W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.os.Bundle.getString(Bundle.java:1040) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.content.Intent.getStringExtra(Intent.java:3368) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.proxy.IntentProxy.getStringExtra(IntentProxy.java:239) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.proxy.IntentProxyBindingGen$3.invoke(IntentProxyBindingGen.java:187) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>kroll.KrollMethod.call(KrollMethod.java:51) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpretLoop(Interpreter.java:1711) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpret(Interpreter.java:854) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.mozilla.javascript.InterpretedFunction.call(InterpretedFunction.java:164) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.mozilla.javascript.ContextFactory.doTopCall(ContextFactory.java:426) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.doTopCall(ScriptRuntime.java:3161) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.mozilla.javascript.InterpretedFunction.call(InterpretedFunction.java:162) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:139) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:113) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:108) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callSync(KrollCallback.java:104) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>kroll.KrollProxy.fireSingleEvent(KrollProxy.java:629) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>kroll.KrollEventManager$KrollListener.invoke(KrollEventManager.java:143) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>kroll.KrollEventManager.dispatchEvent(KrollEventManager.java:273) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>kroll.KrollProxy.fireSyncEvent(KrollProxy.java:600) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.TiBaseActivity.onCreate(TiBaseActivity.java:294) W/Bundle ( 1569): at org.<USER>titanium.TiLaunchActivity.onCreate(TiLaunchActivity.java:97) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.app.Instrumentation.callActivityOnCreate(Instrumentation.java:1047) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.app.ActivityThread.performLaunchActivity(ActivityThread.java:2627) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.app.ActivityThread.handleLaunchActivity(ActivityThread.java:2679) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.app.ActivityThread.access$2300(ActivityThread.java:125) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.app.ActivityThread$H.handleMessage(ActivityThread.java:2033) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:99) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123) W/Bundle ( 1569): at android.app.ActivityThread.main(ActivityThread.java:4627) W/Bundle ( 1569): at java.lang.reflect.Method.invokeNative(Native Method) W/Bundle ( 1569): at java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:521) W/Bundle ( 1569): at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit$MethodAndArgsCaller.run(ZygoteInit.java:868) W/Bundle ( 1569): at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit.main(ZygoteInit.java:626) W/Bundle ( 1569): at dalvik.system.NativeStart.main(Native Method)</code> </pre> <p>I notice in ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2587"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2587"""""""">#2587</a>, someone encountered the same problem when <em>creating</em> such intents to send to other applications, and an Intent.putUriExtra() was added to accommodate it, converting from a string parameter to a Uri.</p> <p>It looks like it would be helpful to add an Intent.getUriExtra(), or else tweak things such that there's some other clear way to retrieve it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3447,12,"""iOS: Large file Download gives error: """"Unable to create request (bad url?)""""""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink on Device<br> 2. Run Platform &gt; XHR &gt; File Download<br> 3. Click on Large File Download</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Unable to create request (bad url?) (see attached image)</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To complete download without error</p> <p>Note: Also run Drillbit Ti.Network.HTTPClient<br> largeFileWithRedirect<br> false</p> <p>Error Domain=ASIHTTPRequestErrorDomain Code=5 """"""""Unable to create request (bad url?)"""""""" UserInfo=0xe057c60 {NSLocalizedDescription=Unable to create request (bad url?)}</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Large file Download gives error: """"Unable to create request (bad url?)""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Launch Kitchen Sink on Device<br> 2. Run Platform &gt; XHR &gt; File Download<br> 3. Click on Large File Download</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Unable to create request (bad url?) (see attached image)</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To complete download without error</p> <p>Note: Also run Drillbit Ti.Network.HTTPClient<br> largeFileWithRedirect<br> false</p> <p>Error Domain=ASIHTTPRequestErrorDomain Code=5 """"""""Unable to create request (bad url?)"""""""" UserInfo=0xe057c60 {NSLocalizedDescription=Unable to create request (bad url?)}</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3446,12,"""iOS: UI.Picker - add support for locale property and setLocale method""","""""""h2. Expected Result  Setting the {{locale}} property of a date picker, or using picker.setLocale() method, should localize a picker    Stramer posted the following comment on this topic in [this post|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1269/files#r389756], """"""""We may be able to file a bug/feature request to support custom localizations on iOS. Instead of setting the locale directly, we can probably set the picker's calendar type.""""""""    h2. Actual Result  Does nothing    h2. Test case    Test using the KS:    * Launch Kitchen Sink on Device  * Run Controls > Picker > Date Picker  * Click """"""""Change locale"""""""" button to programmatically change to locale """"""""ru""""""""    ...or test using the following code:    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');    var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor:'white',   fullscreen:false,   exitOnClose:true  });    var minDate = new Date(2011,11,1);    var maxDate = new Date(2012,11,31);    var value = new Date();    var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({   locale:'fr',   type:Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_DATE_AND_TIME,   minDate:minDate,   maxDate:maxDate,   value:value  });  picker.setLocale('fr');  Ti.API.info('The current picker value is: ' + picker.value)  win1.add(picker);    win1.open();  {code}    """"""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: UI.Picker - add support for locale property and setLocale method
Description: """"h2. Expected Result Setting the {{locale}} property of a date picker, or using picker.setLocale() method, should localize a picker Stramer posted the following comment on this topic in [this post|https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/1269/files#r389756], """"""""We may be able to file a bug/feature request to support custom localizations on iOS. Instead of setting the locale directly, we can probably set the picker's calendar type."""""""" h2. Actual Result Does nothing h2. Test case Test using the KS: * Launch Kitchen Sink on Device * Run Controls > Picker > Date Picker * Click """"""""Change locale"""""""" button to programmatically change to locale """"""""ru"""""""" ...or test using the following code: {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'white', fullscreen:false, exitOnClose:true }); var minDate = new Date(2011,11,1); var maxDate = new Date(2012,11,31); var value = new Date(); var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({ locale:'fr', type:Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_DATE_AND_TIME, minDate:minDate, maxDate:maxDate, value:value }); picker.setLocale('fr'); Ti.API.info('The current picker value is: ' + picker.value) win1.add(picker); win1.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-3445,12,"""iOS: Button bar displays """"You clicked undefined"""" intermittently ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Run Kitchen Sink on Device<br> 2. Run Base UI &gt; Window Constructor<br> 3. Click Open a New Window<br> 4. In the new Window Click """"""""One"""""""" and """"""""Two"""""""" about 5-10 times dismissing the dialog each time</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Intermittently you will see """"""""You clicked undefined"""""""" (see attached image)</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To always return the clicked value</p> <p>Tested with Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...) on<br> iPhone 4 4.3</p> <p>Note:<br> Also happens on<br> Controls &gt; Button Bar<br> Controls &gt; Tabbed bar</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Button bar displays """"You clicked undefined"""" intermittently
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Run Kitchen Sink on Device<br> 2. Run Base UI &gt; Window Constructor<br> 3. Click Open a New Window<br> 4. In the new Window Click """"""""One"""""""" and """"""""Two"""""""" about 5-10 times dismissing the dialog each time</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> Intermittently you will see """"""""You clicked undefined"""""""" (see attached image)</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To always return the clicked value</p> <p>Tested with Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...) on<br> iPhone 4 4.3</p> <p>Note:<br> Also happens on<br> Controls &gt; Button Bar<br> Controls &gt; Tabbed bar</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3444,12,"""iOS: issues tapping into text with keyboard up and test field partially obscured in landscape""","""""""{html}<div><p>exists in 1.6.1 as well. All supported devices, Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <p>1.controls &gt; text field &gt; text field in scroll view<br> 2.rotate to landscape<br> 3.tap into a field to invoke the kayboard<br> 4.with keyboard up, scroll the second text field so the text in it is obscured by the keyboard<br> 5.tap the field</p> <p>results: field goes flying off screen before coming back. landscape only</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: issues tapping into text with keyboard up and test field partially obscured in landscape
Description: """"{html}<div><p>exists in 1.6.1 as well. All supported devices, Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <p>1.controls &gt; text field &gt; text field in scroll view<br> 2.rotate to landscape<br> 3.tap into a field to invoke the kayboard<br> 4.with keyboard up, scroll the second text field so the text in it is obscured by the keyboard<br> 5.tap the field</p> <p>results: field goes flying off screen before coming back. landscape only</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3443,12,"""iOS: time picker value diferences for gmt across devices/ios sdk versions ""","""""""{html}<div><p>nothing new about this, just noting to see if such things are under our control/an actual bug<br> Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; Picker &gt; Time Picker<br> 2.select any value on the picker and check the text label on top of the screen (the last value shown), specifically time off gtm</p> <p>results:<br> 3g iphone: -0700<br> iphone4 (4.3): +0000<br> 4gt ipod touch (4.3): +0000<br> ipad2(4.3): +0000</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: time picker value diferences for gmt across devices/ios sdk versions
Description: """"{html}<div><p>nothing new about this, just noting to see if such things are under our control/an actual bug<br> Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; Picker &gt; Time Picker<br> 2.select any value on the picker and check the text label on top of the screen (the last value shown), specifically time off gtm</p> <p>results:<br> 3g iphone: -0700<br> iphone4 (4.3): +0000<br> 4gt ipod touch (4.3): +0000<br> ipad2(4.3): +0000</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3442,12,"""iOS:  Slider event issues on < 3.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>shows on the 3g running 3.1.3 only. repros in 1.6.1 as well as current 1.7.0 build Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <ol> <li>Controls &gt; Slider &gt; Basic<br></li> <li>slide the top slider to the end and check output in console</li> </ol> <p>results: no touch start is fired, and touch end is fired twice.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Slider event issues on < 3.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>shows on the 3g running 3.1.3 only. repros in 1.6.1 as well as current 1.7.0 build Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <ol> <li>Controls &gt; Slider &gt; Basic<br></li> <li>slide the top slider to the end and check output in console</li> </ol> <p>results: no touch start is fired, and touch end is fired twice.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3441,12,"""iOS: controls draw to wrong place initially tableviews with controls""","""""""{html}<div><p>All supported ios devices - This broke in 1.6.1, last working build was 1.5.1GA</p> <ol> <li>Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Table Views &gt; Table View (layout 3)<br></li> <li>tap the + icon<br></li> <li>tap the - icon while looking at where the + wil be drawing back in</li> </ol> <p>results:<br> as the + icon draws in, it is incorrectly placed, flashes and lands on the correct location</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: controls draw to wrong place initially tableviews with controls
Description: """"{html}<div><p>All supported ios devices - This broke in 1.6.1, last working build was 1.5.1GA</p> <ol> <li>Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Table Views &gt; Table View (layout 3)<br></li> <li>tap the + icon<br></li> <li>tap the - icon while looking at where the + wil be drawing back in</li> </ol> <p>results:<br> as the + icon draws in, it is incorrectly placed, flashes and lands on the correct location</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3440,12,"""iOS: headers with filter - after searching aligment and cosmetic issues""","""""""{html}<div><p>All supported devices, Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <p>new to 1.7.0, does not repro in 1.6.1</p> <p>1.Base Ui &gt; Table Views &gt; headers with filter<br> 2.tap into the search bar, then type a char<br> 3.check out the table view</p> <p>results: cosmetic issues (see screen shot) and alignment issues</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: headers with filter - after searching aligment and cosmetic issues
