TIMOB-3439,12,"""iOS : crash on table view search after searching and tapping revealed item ""","""""""{html}<div><p>All supported devices - Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <p>new to 1.7.0, does not reproduce in 1.6.1</p> <p>1.BaseUI &gt; Views &gt; Table Views &gt; Headers<br> 2.scroll list to bottom, scroll list to top<br> 3.tap into search bar and type """"""""fran""""""""<br> 4.tap either item revealed by search</p> <p>results: crash</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1705798"""""""">http://pastie.org/1705798</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : crash on table view search after searching and tapping revealed item
Description: """"{html}<div><p>All supported devices - Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...)</p> <p>new to 1.7.0, does not reproduce in 1.6.1</p> <p>1.BaseUI &gt; Views &gt; Table Views &gt; Headers<br> 2.scroll list to bottom, scroll list to top<br> 3.tap into search bar and type """"""""fran""""""""<br> 4.tap either item revealed by search</p> <p>results: crash</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1705798"""""""">http://pastie.org/1705798</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3438,12,"""iOS: Double alerts are displayed in the wrong order""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br>  1. Create a project with the attached .js file<br>  2. Compile and run on Device/Emulator<br>  3. Click on the Double Alert button</p>  <p>Actual Result:<br>  The alert buttons are displayed in the wrong order</p>  <p>Expected Result:<br>  To display the last one called first as it is displayed on top of  the <USER>stack</p>  <p>Tested with Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50  87caf1e...) on<br>  iPhone 4 4.3<br>  Simulator 4.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Double alerts are displayed in the wrong order
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Create a project with the attached .js file<br> 2. Compile and run on Device/Emulator<br> 3. Click on the Double Alert button</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> The alert buttons are displayed in the wrong order</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To display the last one called first as it is displayed on top of the <USER>stack</p> <p>Tested with Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/23/11 09:50 87caf1e...) on<br> iPhone 4 4.3<br> Simulator 4.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3436,12,"""iOS: tableview """"scroll"""" event only fires when dragging""","""""""{html}<div><p>TiUITableView only fires the """"""""scroll"""""""" event when the underlying scrollView is being dragged. There is actually a check for scrollView.isDragging in the scrollViewDidScroll delegate method around line 2020. We actually need to be notified at all times that the tableview is scrolling, regardless of whether or not it's being dragged. This is standard functionality that is available in native iOS and allows us to do much more with the UI. It also allows us to deal with the content inset issues when using headerPullview.</p> <p>When you listen to a ScrollView's """"""""scroll"""""""" event you get a boolean called """"""""dragging"""""""" on the event, this should also be available on the TableView's """"""""scroll"""""""" event. We already modified the Titanium code-base to support this in our project. We removed 3 lines of code and added one line. The required changes are outlined bedlow. Also the documentation for a TableView's """"""""scroll"""""""" event would need to be updated to show the new boolean """"""""dragging"""""""".</p> <p>TiUITableView.m<br> Goto line 2020 and into the method - (void)scrollViewDidScroll:(UIScrollView *)scrollView<br> Remove the scrollView.isDragging check<br> Add the following to the event NSMutableDictionary:<br> [event setObject:NUMBOOL([scrollView isDragging]) forKey:@""""""""dragging""""""""];</p> <p>Best,</p> <p><USER>/p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: tableview """"scroll"""" event only fires when dragging
Description: """"{html}<div><p>TiUITableView only fires the """"""""scroll"""""""" event when the underlying scrollView is being dragged. There is actually a check for scrollView.isDragging in the scrollViewDidScroll delegate method around line 2020. We actually need to be notified at all times that the tableview is scrolling, regardless of whether or not it's being dragged. This is standard functionality that is available in native iOS and allows us to do much more with the UI. It also allows us to deal with the content inset issues when using headerPullview.</p> <p>When you listen to a ScrollView's """"""""scroll"""""""" event you get a boolean called """"""""dragging"""""""" on the event, this should also be available on the TableView's """"""""scroll"""""""" event. We already modified the Titanium code-base to support this in our project. We removed 3 lines of code and added one line. The required changes are outlined bedlow. Also the documentation for a TableView's """"""""scroll"""""""" event would need to be updated to show the new boolean """"""""dragging"""""""".</p> <p>TiUITableView.m<br> Goto line 2020 and into the method - (void)scrollViewDidScroll:(UIScrollView *)scrollView<br> Remove the scrollView.isDragging check<br> Add the following to the event NSMutableDictionary:<br> [event setObject:NUMBOOL([scrollView isDragging]) forKey:@""""""""dragging""""""""];</p> <p>Best,</p> <p><USER>/p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3435,12,"""TableViewSection.headerView broken on Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>HeaderView option works on a TableView, but not on a  TableViewSection on Android.</p>  <p>Assigning a custom view to a TableViewSection.headerView will  not result in that view being drawn on display.<br>  It does work on iOS without problems, I would love to see it  working on Android too so I could do a nice GUI.</p>  <p>Documentation doesn't seem to mention anything related to  this.<br>  The code I tested with is similar to KitchenSink demo. I can't run  the KitchenSink demo on android, since it<br>  will not install due to the fact it can't find a required library  for google maps. There's no error display when<br>  trying to install KitchenSink on my Android phone. (Yes I  downloaded the latest version from github)</p>  <p>Expected output (similar to iOS):<br>  <a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4yR0"""""""">http://imm.io/4yR0</a></p>  <p>Actual output (on Android):<br>  <a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4yR1"""""""">http://imm.io/4yR1</a></p>  <p>Titanium SDK 1.6.1<br>  Titanium Developer 1.2.2<br>  Compiled for Android SDK 2.2, Android tools version 10</p>  <p>Code attached for test, simple app.js<br>  <a href=  """"""""https://gist.github.com/886885"""""""">https://gist.github.com/886885</a></p>  <p>Thank you for your time.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableViewSection.headerView broken on Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>HeaderView option works on a TableView, but not on a TableViewSection on Android.</p> <p>Assigning a custom view to a TableViewSection.headerView will not result in that view being drawn on display.<br> It does work on iOS without problems, I would love to see it working on Android too so I could do a nice GUI.</p> <p>Documentation doesn't seem to mention anything related to this.<br> The code I tested with is similar to KitchenSink demo. I can't run the KitchenSink demo on android, since it<br> will not install due to the fact it can't find a required library for google maps. There's no error display when<br> trying to install KitchenSink on my Android phone. (Yes I downloaded the latest version from github)</p> <p>Expected output (similar to iOS):<br> <a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4yR0"""""""">http://imm.io/4yR0</a></p> <p>Actual output (on Android):<br> <a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4yR1"""""""">http://imm.io/4yR1</a></p> <p>Titanium SDK 1.6.1<br> Titanium Developer 1.2.2<br> Compiled for Android SDK 2.2, Android tools version 10</p> <p>Code attached for test, simple app.js<br> <a href= """"""""https://gist.github.com/886885"""""""">https://gist.github.com/886885</a></p> <p>Thank you for your time.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3434,12,"""ScrollView: Not able to set default scroll position of content to be viewed.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Howdy!</p> <p>After/during creating a scrollView, I would like to be able to set the default starting position of the content viewed.</p> <p>e.g.</p> <p><code><br> var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({</code></p> {mkd-extraction-47bdccb44f8a2210a9ce265263aa5916} <p>});</p> <p>or</p> <p><code><br> var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({</code></p> {mkd-extraction-03d353c087c05a7679e3039f2021f6fc} <p>}); scrollView.scrollTo(250, 0); &lt;-- works but straight after this event is fired, another scroll event sets the position to 0,0. I think the """"""""resetting/default scroll event"""""""" occurs when the window is opened.<br> // add more content to scrollView</p> <p>win.add(scrollView);<br> win.open();<br></p> <p>I think the property """"""""defaultScrollPosition: [250, 0]"""""""" would be great.</p> <p>Tested on the KitchenSink example - scroll_views_tabs.js</p> <p>Thanks in advance!</p> <p>TM</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ScrollView: Not able to set default scroll position of content to be viewed.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Howdy!</p> <p>After/during creating a scrollView, I would like to be able to set the default starting position of the content viewed.</p> <p>e.g.</p> <p><code><br> var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({</code></p> {mkd-extraction-47bdccb44f8a2210a9ce265263aa5916} <p>});</p> <p>or</p> <p><code><br> var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({</code></p> {mkd-extraction-03d353c087c05a7679e3039f2021f6fc} <p>}); scrollView.scrollTo(250, 0); &lt;-- works but straight after this event is fired, another scroll event sets the position to 0,0. I think the """"""""resetting/default scroll event"""""""" occurs when the window is opened.<br> // add more content to scrollView</p> <p>win.add(scrollView);<br> win.open();<br></p> <p>I think the property """"""""defaultScrollPosition: [250, 0]"""""""" would be great.</p> <p>Tested on the KitchenSink example - scroll_views_tabs.js</p> <p>Thanks in advance!</p> <p>TM</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3433,12,"""Sluggish performance with static table view""","""""""{html}<div><p>""""""""Sluggish performance with static table view""""""""</p> <ul> <li>We have used static table view in one of the screens under titanium based application</li> <li>When we move onto that screen then sometimes it just doesn't load completely or sometimes some of the rows doesn't appear.</li> <li>When we come on this screen then after a moment all the labels in this table view slid 1px up from its current position - no idea why?</li> </ul> <p>If anybody has any idea about this and some guideline material as how to optimize performance for titanium application when using specific controls etc. then please let us know because for simple/static screens we are facing very slow application performance for now.</p> <p>Thanks,<br> DPK</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Sluggish performance with static table view
Description: """"{html}<div><p>""""""""Sluggish performance with static table view""""""""</p> <ul> <li>We have used static table view in one of the screens under titanium based application</li> <li>When we move onto that screen then sometimes it just doesn't load completely or sometimes some of the rows doesn't appear.</li> <li>When we come on this screen then after a moment all the labels in this table view slid 1px up from its current position - no idea why?</li> </ul> <p>If anybody has any idea about this and some guideline material as how to optimize performance for titanium application when using specific controls etc. then please let us know because for simple/static screens we are facing very slow application performance for now.</p> <p>Thanks,<br> DPK</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3431,12,"""defines.h files is not generated properly for HW builds when files are placed in /Resources/iphone directory""","""""""{html}<div><p>My files where placed in /Resources/iphone and the emulator builds worked fine but when I did HW builds the application would crash on start on HW and even subsequent emulator builds.</p> <p>I traced it down to the build/iphone/Classes/defines.h file being re-created wrong by the HW build <USER></p> <p>Taking my files our of /Resources/iphone directly into /Resources fixed the problem.</p> <p>Titanium SDK 1.2.2, Mobile SDK 1.6.1 and XCode 4 on Mac OS 10.6</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: defines.h files is not generated properly for HW builds when files are placed in /Resources/iphone directory
Description: """"{html}<div><p>My files where placed in /Resources/iphone and the emulator builds worked fine but when I did HW builds the application would crash on start on HW and even subsequent emulator builds.</p> <p>I traced it down to the build/iphone/Classes/defines.h file being re-created wrong by the HW build <USER></p> <p>Taking my files our of /Resources/iphone directly into /Resources fixed the problem.</p> <p>Titanium SDK 1.2.2, Mobile SDK 1.6.1 and XCode 4 on Mac OS 10.6</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3429,12,"""TableView creates multiple row selection if scrollable""","""""""{html}<div><p>Information on this bug (and reproducing code sample) can be  found in HD: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76470#c362847"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76470#c362847</a></p>  <p>If a TableView has more rows than can be displayed at once (view  is scrollable) and allowSelection is set to TRUE, when selecting  one row another row off-view will be selected as well. For  instance, if there are 20 rows but only 10 are visible: select row  1, scroll down, and row 12 will also be selected.</p>  <p><strong>VERSIONS</strong></p>  <p>TI 1.6.0<br>  IOS SDK 4.2</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView creates multiple row selection if scrollable
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Information on this bug (and reproducing code sample) can be found in HD: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76470#c362847"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76470#c362847</a></p> <p>If a TableView has more rows than can be displayed at once (view is scrollable) and allowSelection is set to TRUE, when selecting one row another row off-view will be selected as well. For instance, if there are 20 rows but only 10 are visible: select row 1, scroll down, and row 12 will also be selected.</p> <p><strong>VERSIONS</strong></p> <p>TI 1.6.0<br> IOS SDK 4.2</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3428,12,"""ScrollableView bug when rotating device""","""""""{html}<div><p>SDK version: 1.6.1<br> Titanium Version: 1.2.2<br> iOS version: 4.2</p> <p>I'm using a ScrollableView to browse images.<br> If a rotate from portrait to landscape, and pinch and zoom one image and scroll the images, when I rotate back to portrait, the view doesn't rotate.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ScrollableView bug when rotating device
Description: """"{html}<div><p>SDK version: 1.6.1<br> Titanium Version: 1.2.2<br> iOS version: 4.2</p> <p>I'm using a ScrollableView to browse images.<br> If a rotate from portrait to landscape, and pinch and zoom one image and scroll the images, when I rotate back to portrait, the view doesn't rotate.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3426,12,"""Android: utilize exif data, by implementing ExifInterface""","""""""{html}<div><p>As Exif data is stored in photo files created using the device camera, it can be exploited to simplify apps as the information does not need to be implemented/duplicated using the DB. Hence, propose <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/ExifInterface.html""""""""> ExifInterface</a> be considered for inclusion in a future release.</p> <p>Note that equivalent functionality is available for iOS from version 4.0, according to <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63941"""""""">this HD ticket</a>.</p> <p>This request also raised for iOS, in <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3427"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3427"""""""">#3427</a>.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: utilize exif data, by implementing ExifInterface
Description: """"{html}<div><p>As Exif data is stored in photo files created using the device camera, it can be exploited to simplify apps as the information does not need to be implemented/duplicated using the DB. Hence, propose <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/ExifInterface.html""""""""> ExifInterface</a> be considered for inclusion in a future release.</p> <p>Note that equivalent functionality is available for iOS from version 4.0, according to <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63941"""""""">this HD ticket</a>.</p> <p>This request also raised for iOS, in <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3427"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3427"""""""">#3427</a>.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3424,12,"""iOS: Label with backgroundImage Error""","""""""h5. Problem  Error message shows in Ti Console when using a backgroundImage  on a label.   h5. Error Message:          h5. Test Code           h5. Ticket Reference       http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76638 """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Label with backgroundImage Error
Description: """"h5. Problem Error message shows in Ti Console when using a backgroundImage on a label. h5. Error Message: h5. Test Code h5. Ticket Reference http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76638 """"",title+description
TIMOB-3422,12,"""iOS - TableViewRow more properties request""","""""""{html}<div><p>According to <a href=  """"""""http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/uikit/reference/UITableViewCell_Class/Reference/Reference.html%23//apple_ref/doc/c_ref/UITableViewCell"""""""">  Apple's API Documentation</a>, the tableViewRows, AKA tableViewCell  have some properties that are not available in Titanium.<br>  This is a feature request to add:</p>  <ul>  <li>detailTextLabel</li>  <li>The four different """"""""Cell Styles"""""""":  <ol>  <li>UITableViewCellStyleDefault,</li>  <li>UITableViewCellStyleValue1,</li>  <li>UITableViewCellStyleValue2,</li>  <li>UITableViewCellStyleSubtitle</li>  </ol>  </li>  </ul>  <p>There is a <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76625"""""""">helpdesk  ticket</a> asking for this, and an <a href=  """"""""http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/userexperience/conceptual/mobilehig/Art/value1_value2_used.jpg"""""""">  image attached</a> referring to some of these properties</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS - TableViewRow more properties request
Description: """"{html}<div><p>According to <a href= """"""""http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/uikit/reference/UITableViewCell_Class/Reference/Reference.html%23//apple_ref/doc/c_ref/UITableViewCell""""""""> Apple's API Documentation</a>, the tableViewRows, AKA tableViewCell have some properties that are not available in Titanium.<br> This is a feature request to add:</p> <ul> <li>detailTextLabel</li> <li>The four different """"""""Cell Styles"""""""": <ol> <li>UITableViewCellStyleDefault,</li> <li>UITableViewCellStyleValue1,</li> <li>UITableViewCellStyleValue2,</li> <li>UITableViewCellStyleSubtitle</li> </ol> </li> </ul> <p>There is a <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76625"""""""">helpdesk ticket</a> asking for this, and an <a href= """"""""http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/documentation/userexperience/conceptual/mobilehig/Art/value1_value2_used.jpg""""""""> image attached</a> referring to some of these properties</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3421,12,"""iOS - Distributed apps missing icon and version on Xcode 4 ""","""""""{html}<div><p>As shown in <a href= """"""""http://pedruqui.s3.amazonaws.com/20110323173805.png"""""""">this image</a> when distributing a app through Titanium Developer, the app seems to be missing it's version number and icon image.</p> <p>Issue encountered on helpdesk ticket <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76616"""""""">76616</a></p> <p>Tested with Ti Dev 1.3 and Ti SDK 1.6.2<br> Xcode 4.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Distributed apps missing icon and version on Xcode 4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>As shown in <a href= """"""""http://pedruqui.s3.amazonaws.com/20110323173805.png"""""""">this image</a> when distributing a app through Titanium Developer, the app seems to be missing it's version number and icon image.</p> <p>Issue encountered on helpdesk ticket <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76616"""""""">76616</a></p> <p>Tested with Ti Dev 1.3 and Ti SDK 1.6.2<br> Xcode 4.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3420,12,"""iOS: Videoplayer closed before loaded still plays""","""""""{html}<div><p><em>Problem</em></p>  <p>If a window containing a videoplayer is on a window that is  closed before the video loads, the video will still play even if it  is stopped, released and/or removed.</p>  <p><em>Test Code</em></p>  <p>Paste at the bottom of default app.js<br></p>  <pre>  <code>// TESTING VIDEO PLAYER  var openVideo = function () {      var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow();      var videoPlayer = Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer({          url: 'http://clips.vorwaerts-gmbh.de/VfE_html5.mp4',          //autoplay:false      });            tab1.open(win3);      win3.add(videoPlayer);            videoPlayer.addEventListener('loadstate',function(e){      Ti.API.info(e.loadState);      //if(e.loadState == 1){videoPlayer.autoplay = true;}      });            win3.addEventListener('close', function () {          Ti.API.info('Window Closed');          videoPlayer.stop();          videoPlayer.release();          win3.remove(videoPlayer);      });        };    win1.addEventListener('click', function () {      openVideo();  });</code>  </pre>  <p>As a work around, you can set autoplay to false and then turn it  on when the loadstate is 1.</p>  <p><em>Ticket Reference</em></p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76612"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76612</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Videoplayer closed before loaded still plays
Description: """"{html}<div><p><em>Problem</em></p> <p>If a window containing a videoplayer is on a window that is closed before the video loads, the video will still play even if it is stopped, released and/or removed.</p> <p><em>Test Code</em></p> <p>Paste at the bottom of default app.js<br></p> <pre> <code>// TESTING VIDEO PLAYER var openVideo = function () { var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var videoPlayer = Ti.Media.createVideoPlayer({ url: 'http://clips.vorwaerts-gmbh.de/VfE_html5.mp4', //autoplay:false }); tab1.open(win3); win3.add(videoPlayer); videoPlayer.addEventListener('loadstate',function(e){ Ti.API.info(e.loadState); //if(e.loadState == 1){videoPlayer.autoplay = true;} }); win3.addEventListener('close', function () { Ti.API.info('Window Closed'); videoPlayer.stop(); videoPlayer.release(); win3.remove(videoPlayer); }); }; win1.addEventListener('click', function () { openVideo(); });</code> </pre> <p>As a work around, you can set autoplay to false and then turn it on when the loadstate is 1.</p> <p><em>Ticket Reference</em></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76612"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76612</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3419,12,"""Android  - SQLite insert is very slow""","""""""{html}<div><p>A <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76471"""""""">helpdesk  ticket</a> has reported that inserting rows in a SQLite database  takes too long. I have create a sample app and ran it against both  Android and iOS. This is the code: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/private/iar8wglepgcilffp6tnpra"""""""">link to the  code</a></p>  <p>And in <a href=  """"""""http://pedruqui.s3.amazonaws.com/20110322222050.png"""""""">this  image</a> you can see the difference between both platforms in  milliseconds after the insert.</p>  <p>Tested Agains iPhone Simulator 4.3 and Android APIs 2.2<br>  Titanium SDK 1.6.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - SQLite insert is very slow
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76471"""""""">helpdesk ticket</a> has reported that inserting rows in a SQLite database takes too long. I have create a sample app and ran it against both Android and iOS. This is the code: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/private/iar8wglepgcilffp6tnpra"""""""">link to the code</a></p> <p>And in <a href= """"""""http://pedruqui.s3.amazonaws.com/20110322222050.png"""""""">this image</a> you can see the difference between both platforms in milliseconds after the insert.</p> <p>Tested Agains iPhone Simulator 4.3 and Android APIs 2.2<br> Titanium SDK 1.6.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
