TIMOB-3386,12,"""Android: Write to File in Append Mode""","""""""You cannot use MODE_APPEND to set the write mode to append when writing to a file, despite the properties listed in [Titanium.Filesystem|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Filesystem-module].    MODE_APPEND is not demonstrated anywhere in the KitchenSink - have raised ticket TIMOB-4212 to address.    In Android only, you can pass a boolean to write() to use append mode, as in the example below, but this is not documented.    {code:lang=javascript}  var newFile = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,'newfile.txt');  newFile.write('line 1\n');  newFile.write('line 2\n', true);    Ti.API.info('newfile: '+newFile.read());</code>  {code}    Ticket TIMOB-4213 has been raised to address this APIDoc issue.    Associated Helpdesk Ticket:  [http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76562]    Remaining on this ticket:  * determine whether the write() boolean argument and/or MODE_APPEND should work on each platforms, and test to ensure that they are in parity""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Write to File in Append Mode
Description: """"You cannot use MODE_APPEND to set the write mode to append when writing to a file, despite the properties listed in [Titanium.Filesystem|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Filesystem-module]. MODE_APPEND is not demonstrated anywhere in the KitchenSink - have raised ticket TIMOB-4212 to address. In Android only, you can pass a boolean to write() to use append mode, as in the example below, but this is not documented. {code:lang=javascript} var newFile = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,'newfile.txt'); newFile.write('line 1\n'); newFile.write('line 2\n', true); Ti.API.info('newfile: '+newFile.read());</code> {code} Ticket TIMOB-4213 has been raised to address this APIDoc issue. Associated Helpdesk Ticket: [http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76562] Remaining on this ticket: * determine whether the write() boolean argument and/or MODE_APPEND should work on each platforms, and test to ensure that they are in parity""""",title+description
TIMOB-3385,12,"""iOS: Write to File in Append Mode ""","""""""{html}<div><p>You cannot use MODE_APPEND to set the write mode to append when writing to a file.<br> API docs say that Titanium.Filesystem.MODE_APPEND should be used.<br> No way to write in append mode on iOS</p> <h3>Tested With</h3> <p>iOS 4.3, TiSDK 1.6.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Write to File in Append Mode
Description: """"{html}<div><p>You cannot use MODE_APPEND to set the write mode to append when writing to a file.<br> API docs say that Titanium.Filesystem.MODE_APPEND should be used.<br> No way to write in append mode on iOS</p> <h3>Tested With</h3> <p>iOS 4.3, TiSDK 1.6.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3384,12,"""apidoc: Change markdown dependency to markdown2""","""""""{html}<div><p>Since api.jsca needs to be generated during builds, we've made the build machines become dependent on markdown. We already ship with markdown2 in the SDK, however (support/module/support/markdown2.py). We should reconcile these so we don't ship with two markdown processors.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: apidoc: Change markdown dependency to markdown2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Since api.jsca needs to be generated during builds, we've made the build machines become dependent on markdown. We already ship with markdown2 in the SDK, however (support/module/support/markdown2.py). We should reconcile these so we don't ship with two markdown processors.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3383,12,"""Hard crash on syntax error""","""""""If you forget to specify an event handler type (as in the example below), the application crashes and does not provide any feedback to the developer aside from an Objective-C stack trace in the console which does not indicate the source of the problem. Marking as high priority because this is very difficult for a developer to debug if they have made this typo. The corresponding error on Android provides a line number and an IllegalArgumentException, indicating that two arguments were expected, which is enough information to debug.    """"""",Bug,"Title: Hard crash on syntax error
Description: """"If you forget to specify an event handler type (as in the example below), the application crashes and does not provide any feedback to the developer aside from an Objective-C stack trace in the console which does not indicate the source of the problem. Marking as high priority because this is very difficult for a developer to debug if they have made this typo. The corresponding error on Android provides a line number and an IllegalArgumentException, indicating that two arguments were expected, which is enough information to debug. """"",title+description
TIMOB-3381,12,"""Upgrade to 1.6.1 - Apps no longer install on Ipod""","""""""{html}<div><p>App was working an installing fine in 1.6.0. I recently upgraded to 1.6.1.</p> <p>Now, I build (in fact do a clean/total rebuild), then move the .app to iTunes (this is on a MacBook, Mac OS X v10.6.6), by the usual drag-and-drop method. Perform a sync, and get the following message, after the app uploads"""""""":</p> <p>The app """"""""xxxxxxxxxx"""""""" was not installed on the iPod """"""""yyyyyyyyyy"""""""" because an unknown error occurred (0xE800801C).</p> <p>The app does not get installed onto the iPod, but is still on iTunes.</p> <p>Note, this also happens with the Kitchen Sink app as well.<br> (Also note, everything works in the iOS/iPhone emulator... no problem.)</p> <p>FYI:<br> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.1<br> iPhone SDK version: 4.2<br> Mac OS X version: 10.6.6<br> (Titanium Developer version: 1.2.2)</p> <p>Please help!<br> - <USER>/p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Upgrade to 1.6.1 - Apps no longer install on Ipod
Description: """"{html}<div><p>App was working an installing fine in 1.6.0. I recently upgraded to 1.6.1.</p> <p>Now, I build (in fact do a clean/total rebuild), then move the .app to iTunes (this is on a MacBook, Mac OS X v10.6.6), by the usual drag-and-drop method. Perform a sync, and get the following message, after the app uploads"""""""":</p> <p>The app """"""""xxxxxxxxxx"""""""" was not installed on the iPod """"""""yyyyyyyyyy"""""""" because an unknown error occurred (0xE800801C).</p> <p>The app does not get installed onto the iPod, but is still on iTunes.</p> <p>Note, this also happens with the Kitchen Sink app as well.<br> (Also note, everything works in the iOS/iPhone emulator... no problem.)</p> <p>FYI:<br> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.1<br> iPhone SDK version: 4.2<br> Mac OS X version: 10.6.6<br> (Titanium Developer version: 1.2.2)</p> <p>Please help!<br> - <USER>/p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3380,12,"""Android: PRAGMA statements that set data don't work""","""""""On android, when running the following select statement: """"""""PRAGMA user_version=5;"""""""" the user_version is never updated. The same statement works fine when manually ran through sqlite3.    I've looked into the code in TiDatabaseProxy.java and it seems that any pragma statements are automatically put through the rawQuery function, which shouldn't be used for queries that insert data.    Seems that the fix for ticket TIMOB-2147 probably introduced this issue.    I've attached a patch that I think should fix the issue, although I've not tested it yet as I don't have a proper build environment set up for titanium mobile.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: PRAGMA statements that set data don't work
Description: """"On android, when running the following select statement: """"""""PRAGMA user_version=5;"""""""" the user_version is never updated. The same statement works fine when manually ran through sqlite3. I've looked into the code in TiDatabaseProxy.java and it seems that any pragma statements are automatically put through the rawQuery function, which shouldn't be used for queries that insert data. Seems that the fix for ticket TIMOB-2147 probably introduced this issue. I've attached a patch that I think should fix the issue, although I've not tested it yet as I don't have a proper build environment set up for titanium mobile.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3379,12,"""Require doesn't handle relative paths.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Similar to <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/3349"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #3349"""""""">#3349</a>, Require doesn't do relative pathing properly, but instead does everything relative to the root of the resources dire, despite the current path of the js executing. The issue lies around krollBridge.mm:631. This should be standardized.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Require doesn't handle relative paths.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Similar to <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/3349"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #3349"""""""">#3349</a>, Require doesn't do relative pathing properly, but instead does everything relative to the root of the resources dire, despite the current path of the js executing. The issue lies around krollBridge.mm:631. This should be standardized.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3378,12,"""Android: ScrollView.remove() doesn't really remove on android""","""""""{html}<div><p>It seems to me that the remove() method on ScrollView doesn't do  its job on Android (build 1.6.0+ from continous builds). Here is a  test code where a button should be removed from the view when it's  clicked:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Scrollview test window',      backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var scrollview = Ti.UI.createScrollView({layout: 'vertical'});    win.add(scrollview);    function onButtonClick(event){      var button = event.source;      var n = Ti.UI.createNotification({message: 'Removed button """"""""' + button.title + '""""""""'});      n.duration = Ti.UI.NOTIFICATION_DURATION_LONG;      button.removeEventListener('click', onButtonClick);      scrollview.remove(button);      n.show();  }    var i, button;  for (i = 0; i &lt; 30; i++) {      button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: String.format('Click to remove #%d', i)});      button.addEventListener('click', onButtonClick);      scrollview.add(button);  }    win.open();</code>  </pre>  <p>I've attached a test project containing this code for you to  enjoy.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ScrollView.remove() doesn't really remove on android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It seems to me that the remove() method on ScrollView doesn't do its job on Android (build 1.6.0+ from continous builds). Here is a test code where a button should be removed from the view when it's clicked:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Scrollview test window', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var scrollview = Ti.UI.createScrollView({layout: 'vertical'}); win.add(scrollview); function onButtonClick(event){ var button = event.source; var n = Ti.UI.createNotification({message: 'Removed button """"""""' + button.title + '""""""""'}); n.duration = Ti.UI.NOTIFICATION_DURATION_LONG; button.removeEventListener('click', onButtonClick); scrollview.remove(button); n.show(); } var i, button; for (i = 0; i &lt; 30; i++) { button = Ti.UI.createButton({title: String.format('Click to remove #%d', i)}); button.addEventListener('click', onButtonClick); scrollview.add(button); } win.open();</code> </pre> <p>I've attached a test project containing this code for you to enjoy.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3377,12,"""Android: VM Heap grows until app crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>Please review the Private HD ticket for details on this  issue.</p>  <p><em>Problem</em></p>  <p>The customer's app crashes if you load it on device and click  Missions, and then the back button about 8-16 times (back and  forth). We tried to make a test app that narrowed down the problem,  but we were unsuccessful. It seems there is either a memory leak  when opening and closing windows, or possibly when parsing json.  The test apps that we were able to replicate the issue were usually  paired down from the original app, but when we installed a new  project, we were unable to replicate.</p>  <p><em>HD Ticket</em></p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76437"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76437</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: VM Heap grows until app crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Please review the Private HD ticket for details on this issue.</p> <p><em>Problem</em></p> <p>The customer's app crashes if you load it on device and click Missions, and then the back button about 8-16 times (back and forth). We tried to make a test app that narrowed down the problem, but we were unsuccessful. It seems there is either a memory leak when opening and closing windows, or possibly when parsing json. The test apps that we were able to replicate the issue were usually paired down from the original app, but when we installed a new project, we were unable to replicate.</p> <p><em>HD Ticket</em></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76437"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76437</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3376,12,"""left- and rightNavButton fade in""","""""""{html}<div><p>When adding a left or rightNavButton to a window, the button fades into view. The expected behavior would be for the button to become immediately visible when the window/tabGroup opens:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup(); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Tab 1',     backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({       icon:'KS_nav_views.png',     title:'Tab 1',     window:win1 });  win1.setRightNavButton(Ti.UI.createButton({     title:'foobar' }));  var win2 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Tab 2',     backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var tab2 = Titanium.UI.createTab({       icon:'KS_nav_ui.png',     title:'Tab 2',     window:win2 });  tabGroup.addTab(tab1);   tabGroup.addTab(tab2); tabGroup.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: left- and rightNavButton fade in
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When adding a left or rightNavButton to a window, the button fades into view. The expected behavior would be for the button to become immediately visible when the window/tabGroup opens:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup(); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({ icon:'KS_nav_views.png', title:'Tab 1', window:win1 }); win1.setRightNavButton(Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'foobar' })); var win2 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Tab 2', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var tab2 = Titanium.UI.createTab({ icon:'KS_nav_ui.png', title:'Tab 2', window:win2 }); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.addTab(tab2); tabGroup.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3374,12,"""T9 word hints appear on Android for password fields""","""""""{html}<div><p>I'm using version 1.6.1 of the Titanium Mobile API</p> <p>When I use the following code for a textfield, the password the user is typing appears in the T9 suggestions in Android. I'm using Android 2.2 and 2.3.3 for my testing, but I'd assume this is happening on all versions.</p> <p>var password = Titanium.UI.createTextField({<br></p> <pre> <code>    id: 'password', className:'textfields', borderStyle:Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED, autocorrect:false, passwordMask:true, keyboardType: Titanium.UI.KEYBOARD_DEFAULT, returnKeyType: Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_GO, autocapitalization: Titanium.UI.TEXT_AUTOCAPITALIZATION_NONE, enableReturnKey: true</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: T9 word hints appear on Android for password fields
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I'm using version 1.6.1 of the Titanium Mobile API</p> <p>When I use the following code for a textfield, the password the user is typing appears in the T9 suggestions in Android. I'm using Android 2.2 and 2.3.3 for my testing, but I'd assume this is happening on all versions.</p> <p>var password = Titanium.UI.createTextField({<br></p> <pre> <code> id: 'password', className:'textfields', borderStyle:Titanium.UI.INPUT_BORDERSTYLE_ROUNDED, autocorrect:false, passwordMask:true, keyboardType: Titanium.UI.KEYBOARD_DEFAULT, returnKeyType: Titanium.UI.RETURNKEY_GO, autocapitalization: Titanium.UI.TEXT_AUTOCAPITALIZATION_NONE, enableReturnKey: true</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3373,12,"""Android: hasOwnProperty function fails""","""""""{html}<div><p>The JSLint parser barfs warnings in Developer if you do a 'for'  iteration through an object's properties. It states that you need  to wrap the for loop's logic with an 'if' condition to filter out  properties from the prototype. JSLint is not happy until you do  so.</p>  <p>Using the Object.hasOwnProperty(p) function is necessary to do  so. So, I dutifully implemented it, and the warnings went away.  Then I ran my app on Android. Puke! Android doesn't like that  function.</p>  <p>I hereby nominate DT to fix this, because Don seems to rock the  known universe.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: hasOwnProperty function fails
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The JSLint parser barfs warnings in Developer if you do a 'for' iteration through an object's properties. It states that you need to wrap the for loop's logic with an 'if' condition to filter out properties from the prototype. JSLint is not happy until you do so.</p> <p>Using the Object.hasOwnProperty(p) function is necessary to do so. So, I dutifully implemented it, and the warnings went away. Then I ran my app on Android. Puke! Android doesn't like that function.</p> <p>I hereby nominate DT to fix this, because Don seems to rock the known universe.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3372,12,"""Negative Height on ImageView Crashes""","""""""{html}<div><pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var iconImageGradient = Titanium.UI.createImageView({     top: 0,     left: 0,     width: 30,     height: -14.666,     image: 'icon-gradient.png' });</code> </pre> <p>This crashed the application on android.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Negative Height on ImageView Crashes
Description: """"{html}<div><pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var iconImageGradient = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ top: 0, left: 0, width: 30, height: -14.666, image: 'icon-gradient.png' });</code> </pre> <p>This crashed the application on android.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3371,12,"""Wrong SDKs are used from iphonesim when multiple XCode installs exist""","""""""{html}<div><p>The embedded iphonesim launcher would only refer to SDKs located in developer tools installed in /Developer.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Wrong SDKs are used from iphonesim when multiple XCode installs exist
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The embedded iphonesim launcher would only refer to SDKs located in developer tools installed in /Developer.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3370,12,"""iOS: WebView: fires load event multiple times""","""""""I am using the following code to listen for the load event of a WebView:        When running this in the iPhone simulator, the load event appears to be getting fired 10 times. This listener is triggered 10 times and thus I get 10 alert's that pop up after the WebView has loaded.    *Update: The original PR created a side effect of if the remote webpage loaded uses JavaScript to POST a form to itself (i.e. the same URL), the WebView load event never fires.*""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: WebView: fires load event multiple times
Description: """"I am using the following code to listen for the load event of a WebView: When running this in the iPhone simulator, the load event appears to be getting fired 10 times. This listener is triggered 10 times and thus I get 10 alert's that pop up after the WebView has loaded. *Update: The original PR created a side effect of if the remote webpage loaded uses JavaScript to POST a form to itself (i.e. the same URL), the WebView load event never fires.*""""",title+description
TIMOB-3369,12,"""iOS: Tableview scrollToTop method does not work as expected ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to reproduce:<br> 1. Create a project with the following app.js<br> 2. Run the application on device/emulator<br> 3. If you click on row 5, you should see row 13 scroll to the top of the table view.</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> There is a slight movement upward</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To display row 13 at the top of the screen</p> <p>Tested with Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/17/11 10:02 630a276) on<br> iPad 4.3<br> Simulator 4.1<br> iPhone4 4.3<br> Clicking on row 5 just slightly moves it does not bring row 13 to top</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tableview scrollToTop method does not work as expected
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to reproduce:<br> 1. Create a project with the following app.js<br> 2. Run the application on device/emulator<br> 3. If you click on row 5, you should see row 13 scroll to the top of the table view.</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> There is a slight movement upward</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> To display row 13 at the top of the screen</p> <p>Tested with Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/17/11 10:02 630a276) on<br> iPad 4.3<br> Simulator 4.1<br> iPhone4 4.3<br> Clicking on row 5 just slightly moves it does not bring row 13 to top</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3368,12,"""Markers on the Titanium.Map""","""""""{html}<div><p>From what I've been able to research, it is not possible on the iPhone to change the image for pins/markers that are displayed on a map created with Titanium. The only way to use custom markers on a map if you are using Titanium is to use Google Maps instead of the native Titanium.Map. This is a very big issue and would hope this can be addressed in a future release.</p> <p>In summary, the request is to add the ability to use custom images as map pins/markers for the iPhone/iPad. So this would be a custom image for the Titanium.Map.Annotation.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Markers on the Titanium.Map
Description: """"{html}<div><p>From what I've been able to research, it is not possible on the iPhone to change the image for pins/markers that are displayed on a map created with Titanium. The only way to use custom markers on a map if you are using Titanium is to use Google Maps instead of the native Titanium.Map. This is a very big issue and would hope this can be addressed in a future release.</p> <p>In summary, the request is to add the ability to use custom images as map pins/markers for the iPhone/iPad. So this would be a custom image for the Titanium.Map.Annotation.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3367,12,"""Android: testDatabaseRollback from Drillbit fails on Android only""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Run Drillbit and execute test Ti.Database tests<br> 2. Select the test to be ran on iOS and Android</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> All test pass on iOS<br> Android Emulator 2.1: fails: testDatabaseRollback false 136 should be: """"""""0"""""""", was: """"""""30""""""""</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> Should all Pass</p> <p>Tested with build: Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/17/11 10:02 630a276)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: testDatabaseRollback from Drillbit fails on Android only
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to Reproduce:<br> 1. Run Drillbit and execute test Ti.Database tests<br> 2. Select the test to be ran on iOS and Android</p> <p>Actual Result:<br> All test pass on iOS<br> Android Emulator 2.1: fails: testDatabaseRollback false 136 should be: """"""""0"""""""", was: """"""""30""""""""</p> <p>Expected Result:<br> Should all Pass</p> <p>Tested with build: Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (03/17/11 10:02 630a276)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3366,12,"""iOS: event.media.size reporting incorrect file size after camera/picker""","""""""While building an app which uses the camera or picker to choose or take photos, I've come across a bizarre bug.    After choosing a photo from the album, I needed to know the file size. Also I needed to know the width and height. So, using:        I can see the dimensions fine.    But when I tried to use event.media.size it returned the width*height !!?? (See line 74 in TiBlob.m !) Most bizarre.    When I then decide to write this file to the application data directory (as my app needs), this works fine as the blob's .size property does then respond with the correct filesize in bytes.    Is this being caused by some confusion form using the word 'size' for a filesize in one case (a blob) and then by using the word 'size' for a dictionary containing width and height for an image.    Either way, responding with width*height for an image 'size' seems like a nasty (but easily solved) error/bug.""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: event.media.size reporting incorrect file size after camera/picker
Description: """"While building an app which uses the camera or picker to choose or take photos, I've come across a bizarre bug. After choosing a photo from the album, I needed to know the file size. Also I needed to know the width and height. So, using: I can see the dimensions fine. But when I tried to use event.media.size it returned the width*height !!?? (See line 74 in TiBlob.m !) Most bizarre. When I then decide to write this file to the application data directory (as my app needs), this works fine as the blob's .size property does then respond with the correct filesize in bytes. Is this being caused by some confusion form using the word 'size' for a filesize in one case (a blob) and then by using the word 'size' for a dictionary containing width and height for an image. Either way, responding with width*height for an image 'size' seems like a nasty (but easily solved) error/bug.""""",title+description
TIMOB-3365,12,"""iOS: Cannot set an empty array for the picker rows""","""""""{html}<div><p>The below code snippet dies a horrible death:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">    var rows = [];      var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker();      picker.add(rows);</code>  </pre>  <p>I think it should be possible to set an empty array as the rows.  I realize it does not make too much sense but one could e.g add  rows later to the picker. It's unexpected that the application  crashes, in my opinion.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Cannot set an empty array for the picker rows
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The below code snippet dies a horrible death:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var rows = []; var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker(); picker.add(rows);</code> </pre> <p>I think it should be possible to set an empty array as the rows. I realize it does not make too much sense but one could e.g add rows later to the picker. It's unexpected that the application crashes, in my opinion.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3364,12,"""How to open front camera first in iphone4 instead of backside camera?""","""""""{html}<div><p>I use following code:<br></p> <pre> <code>       Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_REAR);      if (Ti.Media.camera == Ti.Media.CAMERA_REAR)     {         Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_FRONT);     }</code> </pre> <p>but it does not help me to open front camera first instead of back camera.</p> <p>I get -- <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> invalid state. in -[MediaModule switchCamera:] (MediaModule.m:644)</p> <p>please help me to solve this issue.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: How to open front camera first in iphone4 instead of backside camera?
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I use following code:<br></p> <pre> <code> Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_REAR); if (Ti.Media.camera == Ti.Media.CAMERA_REAR) { Ti.Media.switchCamera(Ti.Media.CAMERA_FRONT); }</code> </pre> <p>but it does not help me to open front camera first instead of back camera.</p> <p>I get -- <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> invalid state. in -[MediaModule switchCamera:] (MediaModule.m:644)</p> <p>please help me to solve this issue.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3363,12,"""Percentage width of views not respected""","""""""Note that although the title mentions widths and views, other dimensions and UI objects have not been tested. Thus, this issue _may_ extend to any UI object and any dimensions where percentages are used.    Behavior exhibited using:  * emulator  Android 2.2  Ti 1.6.0 and 1.6.1    Also tested on Samsung Galaxy S running 2.2.1, with same results.    With the following code (which will work in app.js without modification), although the percentage width of the view (set at a value of 90%) initially seems to work, if the orientation is toggled a couple of times, the width is changed to 90% of the _other_ orientation. In other words, when the orientation is portrait, the view is set to 90% of the landscape view, and vice versa.          When the above bug has been resolved, please also check that it works for tabgroups, as per [http://developer.<USER>com/question/117316/percentage-width-still-doesnt-work]    The following code can be used to test this scenario:    """"""",Bug,"Title: Percentage width of views not respected
Description: """"Note that although the title mentions widths and views, other dimensions and UI objects have not been tested. Thus, this issue _may_ extend to any UI object and any dimensions where percentages are used. Behavior exhibited using: * emulator Android 2.2 Ti 1.6.0 and 1.6.1 Also tested on Samsung Galaxy S running 2.2.1, with same results. With the following code (which will work in app.js without modification), although the percentage width of the view (set at a value of 90%) initially seems to work, if the orientation is toggled a couple of times, the width is changed to 90% of the _other_ orientation. In other words, when the orientation is portrait, the view is set to 90% of the landscape view, and vice versa. When the above bug has been resolved, please also check that it works for tabgroups, as per [http://developer.<USER>com/question/117316/percentage-width-still-doesnt-work] The following code can be used to test this scenario: """"",title+description
TIMOB-3362,12,"""iOS: showCamera does not work on iPad2 if running iPad app""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you run an iPad application on the iPad Titanium.Media.showCamera doesn't work.<br> If you run an iPhone application on the iPad, Titanium.Media.showCamera camera works properly.</p> <p>-fail with iPad app Step 1: make an app for 'iPad' and paste in the code below.<br> step 2: run the app on an iPad 2<br> Step 3: click the 'camera' button<br> Step 4: notice the camera overlay fly out the top of the page</p> <p>-pass with iPhone app Step 1: make an application for 'iPhone' and paste in the code below<br> step 2: run the app on an iPad 2<br> Step 3: click the 'camera' button<br> Step 4: notice the camera works properly</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Tab 1',     backgroundColor:'#fff' });  var camera_button = Titanium.UI.createButton ({     title:'Camera',     height:60,     bottom: 10,     width:160 }); camera_button.addEventListener ('click', function(e) {            Titanium.Media.showCamera ({                  saveToPhotoGallery: true,         allowEditing: true,         // top:100,         // width:'auto',                  success: function(event){             var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({                 title: 'You did it!'             });             a.show();         },                  error: function(error){             var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({                 title: 'Uh Oh...'             });             if (error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_CAMERA || error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_VIDEO) {                 a.setMessage('Sorry, this device does not have a camera. You knew that, right?');             }             else {                 a.setMessage('Unexpected error: ' + error.code);             }             a.show();         }                      });  });  win1.add(camera_button); win1.open();</code> </pre> <h3>Resources</h3> <p>ScreenShot and Video attached</p> <h3>Tested With</h3> <p>TiSDK 1.6.1, iPad 2, iOS 4.3</p> <h3>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h3> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76504"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76504</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: showCamera does not work on iPad2 if running iPad app
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you run an iPad application on the iPad Titanium.Media.showCamera doesn't work.<br> If you run an iPhone application on the iPad, Titanium.Media.showCamera camera works properly.</p> <p>-fail with iPad app Step 1: make an app for 'iPad' and paste in the code below.<br> step 2: run the app on an iPad 2<br> Step 3: click the 'camera' button<br> Step 4: notice the camera overlay fly out the top of the page</p> <p>-pass with iPhone app Step 1: make an application for 'iPhone' and paste in the code below<br> step 2: run the app on an iPad 2<br> Step 3: click the 'camera' button<br> Step 4: notice the camera works properly</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var camera_button = Titanium.UI.createButton ({ title:'Camera', height:60, bottom: 10, width:160 }); camera_button.addEventListener ('click', function(e) { Titanium.Media.showCamera ({ saveToPhotoGallery: true, allowEditing: true, // top:100, // width:'auto', success: function(event){ var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({ title: 'You did it!' }); a.show(); }, error: function(error){ var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({ title: 'Uh Oh...' }); if (error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_CAMERA || error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_VIDEO) { a.setMessage('Sorry, this device does not have a camera. You knew that, right?'); } else { a.setMessage('Unexpected error: ' + error.code); } a.show(); } }); }); win1.add(camera_button); win1.open();</code> </pre> <h3>Resources</h3> <p>ScreenShot and Video attached</p> <h3>Tested With</h3> <p>TiSDK 1.6.1, iPad 2, iOS 4.3</p> <h3>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h3> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76504"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76504</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3361,12,"""Actual tableView scrollEnd/""""scrollComplete"""" event?""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi guys,</p>  <p>I've added the scroll and scrollEnd events to my  tableView(iPhone) but...</p>  <p>When I """"""""swipe""""""""/scroll the tableView, the """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" event is  only fired when I let go of my mouse click(in simulator) instead of  when the tableView scrolls to a complete stop.</p>  <p>I need to listen for an event when the tableView scrolling comes  to a complete stop and not the end of my """"""""scroll swipe""""""""/flick.</p>  <p>Is it a bug or a new feature? I'll leave it up to you.</p>  <p>Thanks in advance! :)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Actual tableView scrollEnd/""""scrollComplete"""" event?
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi guys,</p> <p>I've added the scroll and scrollEnd events to my tableView(iPhone) but...</p> <p>When I """"""""swipe""""""""/scroll the tableView, the """"""""scrollEnd"""""""" event is only fired when I let go of my mouse click(in simulator) instead of when the tableView scrolls to a complete stop.</p> <p>I need to listen for an event when the tableView scrolling comes to a complete stop and not the end of my """"""""scroll swipe""""""""/flick.</p> <p>Is it a bug or a new feature? I'll leave it up to you.</p> <p>Thanks in advance! :)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3360,12,"""iOS: """"302 Found"""" redirect drop authorization header""","""""""{html}<div><p>The Titanium.Network.HTTPClient correctly follows a """"""""302 Found""""""""  redirect. On the iPhone however it does not carry the http  authorization header in the next request (ending in a 401 response  from the server). I have not had this a problem with android, ie,  the authorization header is in the redirected request.</p>  <p>Problem found using SDK 1.6.0 &amp; 1.6.1 and iOS 4.2 (device  and simulator).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: """"302 Found"""" redirect drop authorization header
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The Titanium.Network.HTTPClient correctly follows a """"""""302 Found"""""""" redirect. On the iPhone however it does not carry the http authorization header in the next request (ending in a 401 response from the server). I have not had this a problem with android, ie, the authorization header is in the redirected request.</p> <p>Problem found using SDK 1.6.0 &amp; 1.6.1 and iOS 4.2 (device and simulator).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3359,12,"""Android: Remove supports-screens from template AndroidManifest.xml so as to accept Android 2.1 defaults""","""""""{html}<div><p>Since our base Android api level is now 7 (Android 2.1) and that version supports the """"""""anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""""""""""" configuration by default, take out our template AndroidManifest.xml's supports-screens section because it's setting anyDensity to false, which is no longer in line with Android defaults. We should mimic android defaults.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Remove supports-screens from template AndroidManifest.xml so as to accept Android 2.1 defaults
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Since our base Android api level is now 7 (Android 2.1) and that version supports the """"""""anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""""""""""" configuration by default, take out our template AndroidManifest.xml's supports-screens section because it's setting anyDensity to false, which is no longer in line with Android defaults. We should mimic android defaults.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3358,12,"""Android:  HTTP POST send argument with null value causes exception""","""""""{html}<div><p>When sending a HTTP POST request where one of the send arguments has a null value and exception will occur. Correct behavior should be to ignore the key / value pair when the value is null.</p> <p>Example use case:<br> xhr.send({ somearg: 'ok', thisCrashesApp: null });</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTP POST send argument with null value causes exception
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When sending a HTTP POST request where one of the send arguments has a null value and exception will occur. Correct behavior should be to ignore the key / value pair when the value is null.</p> <p>Example use case:<br> xhr.send({ somearg: 'ok', thisCrashesApp: null });</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3357,12,"""Unable to forward exception to javascript…""","""""""{html}<div><p>This issue has been described en detail in the <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117330/catching-objc-exception-from-iphone-module-instead-of-crashing"""""""" title=""""""""Q&amp;A section"""""""">Q &amp; A section</a>&#8230;</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Unable to forward exception to javascript…
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This issue has been described en detail in the <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/117330/catching-objc-exception-from-iphone-module-instead-of-crashing"""""""" title=""""""""Q&amp;A section"""""""">Q &amp; A section</a>&#8230;</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3356,12,"""iOS: Support TableView Auto Height (on the table itself)""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>If you set the height of a table view to """"""""auto"""""""", its height will end up as 0 regardless of its content.</p> <h1>Expected Behavior</h1> <p>A table view with height: 'auto' should calculate its height based on the heights of its rows.</p> <h1>Log</h1> <pre> <code>[WARN] [object TiUITableView] has an auto height value of 0, meaning this view may not be visible.</code> </pre> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <p>The following code demonstrates the problem. Note that you can set """"""""workaround"""""""" to true to calculate the height by spinning through the rows.</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor: '#999' });  var rows = [     { title: """"""""Row 1"""""""", height: 30 },     { title: """"""""Row 2"""""""", height: 45 },     { title: """"""""Row 3"""""""", height: 15 },     { title: """"""""Row 4"""""""", height: 30 },     { title: """"""""Row 5"""""""", height: 25 } ]; var table = Titanium.UI.createTableView({     top: 0,     data: rows,     height: 'auto' }); var workaround = false; if (workaround) {     var height = 0;     for (var i = 0, l = rows.length; i &lt; l; i++) {         height += rows[i].height;     }     table.height = height; }  win.add(table);  win.open();</code> </pre> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76514"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76514</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Support TableView Auto Height (on the table itself)
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>If you set the height of a table view to """"""""auto"""""""", its height will end up as 0 regardless of its content.</p> <h1>Expected Behavior</h1> <p>A table view with height: 'auto' should calculate its height based on the heights of its rows.</p> <h1>Log</h1> <pre> <code>[WARN] [object TiUITableView] has an auto height value of 0, meaning this view may not be visible.</code> </pre> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <p>The following code demonstrates the problem. Note that you can set """"""""workaround"""""""" to true to calculate the height by spinning through the rows.</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#999' }); var rows = [ { title: """"""""Row 1"""""""", height: 30 }, { title: """"""""Row 2"""""""", height: 45 }, { title: """"""""Row 3"""""""", height: 15 }, { title: """"""""Row 4"""""""", height: 30 }, { title: """"""""Row 5"""""""", height: 25 } ]; var table = Titanium.UI.createTableView({ top: 0, data: rows, height: 'auto' }); var workaround = false; if (workaround) { var height = 0; for (var i = 0, l = rows.length; i &lt; l; i++) { height += rows[i].height; } table.height = height; } win.add(table); win.open();</code> </pre> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76514"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76514</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3355,12,"""iPad: SQL insert error happens only in iOS 4.3""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is an odd error that sprung up today testing with iOS 4.3  with an iPad. The exact same SQL statement works in iOS 4.2 - using  the same Ti SDK for both. Snippet from customer:</p>  <pre>  <code class=  """"""""javascript"""""""">Database.Queries.Create.Log = """"""""CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS MDE_SYS_LOG (LOG_DATE TEXT NOT NULL, LOG_TEXT TEXT)"""""""";    // ...  Database.Connection = Ti.Database.open('mmxdb');    // ...    Database.Connection.execute(Database.Queries.Create.Log);</code>  </pre>  <p>The app doesn't crash but throws this error: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1678411"""""""">http://pastie.org/1678411</a></p>  <p>I would say that in this particular issue it's not a show  stopper since they are using this statement for logging in a local  database. However if this one sql statement that works in iOS 4.2  works but does not in iOS 4.3, I worry that this could cause other  issues down the road. We've had no other errors around SQL  statements so far today in testing.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad: SQL insert error happens only in iOS 4.3
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is an odd error that sprung up today testing with iOS 4.3 with an iPad. The exact same SQL statement works in iOS 4.2 - using the same Ti SDK for both. Snippet from customer:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Database.Queries.Create.Log = """"""""CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS MDE_SYS_LOG (LOG_DATE TEXT NOT NULL, LOG_TEXT TEXT)""""""""; // ... Database.Connection = Ti.Database.open('mmxdb'); // ... Database.Connection.execute(Database.Queries.Create.Log);</code> </pre> <p>The app doesn't crash but throws this error: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1678411"""""""">http://pastie.org/1678411</a></p> <p>I would say that in this particular issue it's not a show stopper since they are using this statement for logging in a local database. However if this one sql statement that works in iOS 4.2 works but does not in iOS 4.3, I worry that this could cause other issues down the road. We've had no other errors around SQL statements so far today in testing.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3354,12,"""TextView within TableViewRow scrolling/jumping when focussed""","""""""{html}<div><p><strong>Titanium Version 1.2.2 with Mobile 1.6.0 for iOS</strong></p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> If you create a modal window with <em>TableView</em> that contains <em>TableViewRows</em> with <em>TextField</em> controls, the <em>TableView</em> is scrolling/jumping to a wrong position when focussed.</p> <p><strong>Additional note:</strong> Scrolling/jumping does not occure when the height of all <em>TableViewRows</em> is greater than the available screen height. You can use a pseudo-workaround by setting the height of <em>TableView</em> to the exact height of all <em>TableViewRows</em>, but this helps in Simulator (no Retina) only.</p> <p><strong>How to reproduce:</strong> Create an empty Titanium project and replace the content of <em>app.js</em> with the source in this <a href=""""""""https://gist.github.com/854344"""""""">GIST</a>, then run iOS-Simulator for testing.</p> <p><strong>New temporary workaround</strong> You can fill up the empty space at the bottom of the TableView by setting the """"""""footerTitle"""""""" property to linebreaks only. Example:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.UI.createTableView({footerTitle: '\n\n\n\n\n'});</code> </pre> <p>Note: You may need to add additional linebreaks depending on how many rows the TableView has&hellip;</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TextView within TableViewRow scrolling/jumping when focussed
Description: """"{html}<div><p><strong>Titanium Version 1.2.2 with Mobile 1.6.0 for iOS</strong></p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> If you create a modal window with <em>TableView</em> that contains <em>TableViewRows</em> with <em>TextField</em> controls, the <em>TableView</em> is scrolling/jumping to a wrong position when focussed.</p> <p><strong>Additional note:</strong> Scrolling/jumping does not occure when the height of all <em>TableViewRows</em> is greater than the available screen height. You can use a pseudo-workaround by setting the height of <em>TableView</em> to the exact height of all <em>TableViewRows</em>, but this helps in Simulator (no Retina) only.</p> <p><strong>How to reproduce:</strong> Create an empty Titanium project and replace the content of <em>app.js</em> with the source in this <a href=""""""""https://gist.github.com/854344"""""""">GIST</a>, then run iOS-Simulator for testing.</p> <p><strong>New temporary workaround</strong> You can fill up the empty space at the bottom of the TableView by setting the """"""""footerTitle"""""""" property to linebreaks only. Example:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.UI.createTableView({footerTitle: '\n\n\n\n\n'});</code> </pre> <p>Note: You may need to add additional linebreaks depending on how many rows the TableView has&hellip;</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3353,12,"""Label with auto height shows a display inconsistency on text value update.""","""""""{html}<div><pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">//Using Titanium 1.6.1 on iOS 4.2  var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow(); row.hasChild = true;  var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: """"""""Updating"""""""", textAlign: 'left', font: {    fontSize: 13 }, bottom: 5, height: 16, left: 10,  right: 50 });  row.add(label);  //update text after database query //Case 1: label.text = """"""""Some long text that would cause it to display on two lines""""""""  //Case 2: label.text = """"""""Some short text""""""""  //event called after a remote server updated our local info //this happens in a closure to keep a reference to label Ti.App.addEventListener('someEvent', function(e) {     label.text = """"""""Some other long text to display possibly on two lines"""""""" });  // [More code not related ...] // Add row to a table view, and the table view to the current tab window</code> </pre> <p>Test results:<br> Case 1:<br> At this moment as the view is attached to the window the label is displayed on two lines.</p> <p>The event is triggered, at a later time, the new text is put on two lines.</p> <p>Case 2:<br> At this moment as the view is attached to the window the label is displayed on one line, since the text is short enough to fit on one line.</p> <p>The event is triggered, at a later time, the new text which too long for a single ine is cut off and '...' attached to the end of the text</p> <p>So it looks like the view will not grow automatically at a later time. I don't know what the intended behavior is.<br> And I could not find any setting to choose a default behavior.</p> <p>I hope this is clear enough.<br> Thank you for your time guys.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Label with auto height shows a display inconsistency on text value update.
Description: """"{html}<div><pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">//Using Titanium 1.6.1 on iOS 4.2 var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow(); row.hasChild = true; var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: """"""""Updating"""""""", textAlign: 'left', font: { fontSize: 13 }, bottom: 5, height: 16, left: 10, right: 50 }); row.add(label); //update text after database query //Case 1: label.text = """"""""Some long text that would cause it to display on two lines"""""""" //Case 2: label.text = """"""""Some short text"""""""" //event called after a remote server updated our local info //this happens in a closure to keep a reference to label Ti.App.addEventListener('someEvent', function(e) { label.text = """"""""Some other long text to display possibly on two lines"""""""" }); // [More code not related ...] // Add row to a table view, and the table view to the current tab window</code> </pre> <p>Test results:<br> Case 1:<br> At this moment as the view is attached to the window the label is displayed on two lines.</p> <p>The event is triggered, at a later time, the new text is put on two lines.</p> <p>Case 2:<br> At this moment as the view is attached to the window the label is displayed on one line, since the text is short enough to fit on one line.</p> <p>The event is triggered, at a later time, the new text which too long for a single ine is cut off and '...' attached to the end of the text</p> <p>So it looks like the view will not grow automatically at a later time. I don't know what the intended behavior is.<br> And I could not find any setting to choose a default behavior.</p> <p>I hope this is clear enough.<br> Thank you for your time guys.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3352,12,"""Android TextField drawing broken when using % width inside a tab window""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hello everybody,</p> <p>I've been implementing a configuration screen for my application.<br> This is a tabbed layout, with a configuration tab displaying 3 textFields to type in your username, password and company in order to login into a web service.</p> <p>I've chose to display the text fields inside a grouped tableView. So I could separate the Login details and Company details with a nice header. The bug happens with or without using the grouping of table rows.<br> On iOS there are no problems, but on android 2.2, using TItanium 1.6 / 1.6.1 SDK the text fields do not show, except for the last textField in the last table row.</p> <p>This happens in the demo app I provided in the GISTs mentioned bellow. In my main app the textFields do show, but as soon you would click to enter text, they would go away.<br> I've tested on a HTC Desire, same issue as in the emulator (Android 2.2)</p> <p>By using a fixed width, in px, or dip everything looks OK</p> <p>I've also attached a test project.</p> <h3>Photos:</h3> <h4>Desired:</h4> <p><a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4moz"""""""">http://imm.io/4moz</a></p> <h4>Actual output (Titanium 1.6 and 1.6.1)</h4> <p><a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4moy"""""""">http://imm.io/4moy</a></p> <h3>Gist:</h3> <p><a href= """"""""https://gist.github.com/870605"""""""">https://gist.github.com/870605</a><br> Thank you for your time</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android TextField drawing broken when using % width inside a tab window
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hello everybody,</p> <p>I've been implementing a configuration screen for my application.<br> This is a tabbed layout, with a configuration tab displaying 3 textFields to type in your username, password and company in order to login into a web service.</p> <p>I've chose to display the text fields inside a grouped tableView. So I could separate the Login details and Company details with a nice header. The bug happens with or without using the grouping of table rows.<br> On iOS there are no problems, but on android 2.2, using TItanium 1.6 / 1.6.1 SDK the text fields do not show, except for the last textField in the last table row.</p> <p>This happens in the demo app I provided in the GISTs mentioned bellow. In my main app the textFields do show, but as soon you would click to enter text, they would go away.<br> I've tested on a HTC Desire, same issue as in the emulator (Android 2.2)</p> <p>By using a fixed width, in px, or dip everything looks OK</p> <p>I've also attached a test project.</p> <h3>Photos:</h3> <h4>Desired:</h4> <p><a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4moz"""""""">http://imm.io/4moz</a></p> <h4>Actual output (Titanium 1.6 and 1.6.1)</h4> <p><a href=""""""""http://imm.io/4moy"""""""">http://imm.io/4moy</a></p> <h3>Gist:</h3> <p><a href= """"""""https://gist.github.com/870605"""""""">https://gist.github.com/870605</a><br> Thank you for your time</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3351,12,"""Install Error with Titanium Mobile 1.6.1 and iPad App""","""""""{html}<div><p>With Titanium Mobile 1.6.1, the """"""""Run on device"""""""" command fails. With XCode 3 I get this error message:</p> <pre> <code>Install Error    /Users/&#8230;/App/build/iphone/Classes/ApplicationRouting.m:14: error: no type or storage class may be specified here before 'implementation' [ERROR]  [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1238, in main     execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False)   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1012, in execute_xcode     output = run.run(args,False,False,o)   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run     sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 1</code> </pre> <p>And with XCode 4 this error:</p> <pre> <code>Install Error   [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last):   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1238, in main     execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False)   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1012, in execute_xcode     output = run.run(args,False,False,o)   File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run     sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65</code> </pre> <p>build.log with Xcode 4 has this error line:</p> <pre> <code>UnicodeDecodeError: 'ascii' codec can't decode byte 0xcc in position 96: ordinal not in range(128) Command /bin/sh failed with exit code 1</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Install Error with Titanium Mobile 1.6.1 and iPad App
Description: """"{html}<div><p>With Titanium Mobile 1.6.1, the """"""""Run on device"""""""" command fails. With XCode 3 I get this error message:</p> <pre> <code>Install Error /Users/&#8230;/App/build/iphone/Classes/ApplicationRouting.m:14: error: no type or storage class may be specified here before 'implementation' [ERROR] [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1238, in main execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1012, in execute_xcode output = run.run(args,False,False,o) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 1</code> </pre> <p>And with XCode 4 this error:</p> <pre> <code>Install Error [ERROR] Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1238, in main execute_xcode(""""""""iphoneos%s"""""""" % iphone_version,args,False) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1012, in execute_xcode output = run.run(args,False,False,o) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.1/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 39, in run sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 65</code> </pre> <p>build.log with Xcode 4 has this error line:</p> <pre> <code>UnicodeDecodeError: 'ascii' codec can't decode byte 0xcc in position 96: ordinal not in range(128) Command /bin/sh failed with exit code 1</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3350,12,"""showPagingControl [ScrollableView] doesn't work""","""""""{html}<div><pre> <code>var view = Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var view2 = Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor:'#fff'});  var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({     views:[view,view2],     showPagingControl:false,     pagingControlColor:'#999',     pagingControlHeight:15,     currentPage:0 });  Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(scrollView);</code> </pre> <p>Whether or not the """"""""showPagingControl"""""""" property is set to true or false, as long as pagingControlColor and pagingControlHeight are set, the pagingControl bar at the bottom will be shown. Built using Titanium Developer 1.2.2 and Mobile SDK 1.6.1 on iOS 4.3.</p> <p>If just one of the pagingControlColor/pagingControlHeight properties are <strong>NOT</strong> set (Regardless of showPagingControl property), the pagingController will not be viewable. Will only show if both are set, regardless of showPagingControl property.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: showPagingControl [ScrollableView] doesn't work
Description: """"{html}<div><pre> <code>var view = Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var view2 = Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({ views:[view,view2], showPagingControl:false, pagingControlColor:'#999', pagingControlHeight:15, currentPage:0 }); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(scrollView);</code> </pre> <p>Whether or not the """"""""showPagingControl"""""""" property is set to true or false, as long as pagingControlColor and pagingControlHeight are set, the pagingControl bar at the bottom will be shown. Built using Titanium Developer 1.2.2 and Mobile SDK 1.6.1 on iOS 4.3.</p> <p>If just one of the pagingControlColor/pagingControlHeight properties are <strong>NOT</strong> set (Regardless of showPagingControl property), the pagingController will not be viewable. Will only show if both are set, regardless of showPagingControl property.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3349,12,"""iOS: Ti.include() not handling relative pathing properly""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is the companion ticket to <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/2585"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #2585"""""""">#2585</a>.</p> <p>The tests are already in drillbit -- see the """"""""includes"""""""" test suite in drillbit. So for purposes of meeting our ticketing guideline for """"""""Reproduction sequence"""""""", the drillbit suite suffices.</p> <p>But here's a short summary example as well:</p> <p><strong>Resources/app.js</strong></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Ti.include(""""""""l2/l2_included.js"""""""");</code> </pre> <p><strong>Resources/l2/l2_included.js</strong></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.include(""""""""../l1_included.js"""""""");  // Fails</code> </pre> <p><strong>Resources/l1_included.js</strong></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.API.info(""""""""You've reached Resources/l1_included.js"""""""");</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.include() not handling relative pathing properly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is the companion ticket to <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/2585"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #2585"""""""">#2585</a>.</p> <p>The tests are already in drillbit -- see the """"""""includes"""""""" test suite in drillbit. So for purposes of meeting our ticketing guideline for """"""""Reproduction sequence"""""""", the drillbit suite suffices.</p> <p>But here's a short summary example as well:</p> <p><strong>Resources/app.js</strong></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Ti.include(""""""""l2/l2_included.js"""""""");</code> </pre> <p><strong>Resources/l2/l2_included.js</strong></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.include(""""""""../l1_included.js""""""""); // Fails</code> </pre> <p><strong>Resources/l1_included.js</strong></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.API.info(""""""""You've reached Resources/l1_included.js"""""""");</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3348,12,"""Ti.Media.Sound url bug""","""""""{html}<div><p>This works:</p>  <pre>  <code>var sound = Titanium.Media.createSound();  sound.url='../cricket.wav';  sound.play();</code>  </pre>  <p>But if I try to change the url after that, sound plays still the  cricket.wav sound.<br></p>  <pre>  <code>sound.url='../other_sound.wav';  sound.play(); /* plays cricket.wav */</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Media.Sound url bug
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This works:</p> <pre> <code>var sound = Titanium.Media.createSound(); sound.url='../cricket.wav'; sound.play();</code> </pre> <p>But if I try to change the url after that, sound plays still the cricket.wav sound.<br></p> <pre> <code>sound.url='../other_sound.wav'; sound.play(); /* plays cricket.wav */</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3347,12,"""iOS: scrollToView scrolls to requested position, then back to original location""","""""""{html}<div><p>HD post with code sample can be found here: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76488"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76488</a></p>  <p>If you create a scrollableView and then call scrollToView() it  does not always scroll to the desired location (tends to scroll  near requested location, then back to original index), and when it  does it will usually scroll too far before snapping back (for  instance, when going from index 0 to index 1 it will go  0-&gt;2-&gt;1). Setting the scrollableView.currentPage to the  desired index <em>does</em> work.</p>  <p><strong>VERSIONS</strong></p>  <p>TI 1.6.0<br>  IOS 4.3</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: scrollToView scrolls to requested position, then back to original location
Description: """"{html}<div><p>HD post with code sample can be found here: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76488"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76488</a></p> <p>If you create a scrollableView and then call scrollToView() it does not always scroll to the desired location (tends to scroll near requested location, then back to original index), and when it does it will usually scroll too far before snapping back (for instance, when going from index 0 to index 1 it will go 0-&gt;2-&gt;1). Setting the scrollableView.currentPage to the desired index <em>does</em> work.</p> <p><strong>VERSIONS</strong></p> <p>TI 1.6.0<br> IOS 4.3</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3345,12,"""iOS: REGRESSION: Unable to open splitview in KS-iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>How to reproduce:</p> <ul> <li>Start KS-iPad</li> <li> <p>Click 'Open Main Tests'</p> </li> <li> <p>BEHAVIOR: Doesn't open split view for main tests</p> </li> <li>EXPECTED: Opens split view</li> </ul></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: REGRESSION: Unable to open splitview in KS-iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>How to reproduce:</p> <ul> <li>Start KS-iPad</li> <li> <p>Click 'Open Main Tests'</p> </li> <li> <p>BEHAVIOR: Doesn't open split view for main tests</p> </li> <li>EXPECTED: Opens split view</li> </ul></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3344,12,"""iOS: Update socket implementation to match w/Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>iOS ticket for <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2120"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2120"""""""">#2120</a>; we need to create a new Socket class to match with Android and have a cross-platform implementation. TCPSocket will be deprecated, but remain through 1.7.0 for backwards compatibility.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Update socket implementation to match w/Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iOS ticket for <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2120"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2120"""""""">#2120</a>; we need to create a new Socket class to match with Android and have a cross-platform implementation. TCPSocket will be deprecated, but remain through 1.7.0 for backwards compatibility.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3342,12,"""Module build.py missing LICENSE""","""""""{html}<div><p><strong>Problem</strong></p> <p>When you build a module from Titanium.py the build.py file that is created is not finding the LICENSE file.</p> <p><strong>Error</strong></p> <pre> <code>Traceback (most recent call last):   File """"""""/mymodule/build.py"""""""", line 187, in &lt;module&gt;     validate_license()   File """"""""/mymodule/build.py"""""""", line 99, in validate_license     c = open('LICENSE').read() IOError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'LICENSE'</code> </pre> <p><strong>Suggested Fix</strong></p> <p>Modify lines 99-100 to:<br></p> <pre> <code> path = os.path.join(cwd,'LICENSE')             x = open(path)             c = x.read()</code> </pre> <p><strong>Ticket Reference</strong></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76398"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76398</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Module build.py missing LICENSE
Description: """"{html}<div><p><strong>Problem</strong></p> <p>When you build a module from Titanium.py the build.py file that is created is not finding the LICENSE file.</p> <p><strong>Error</strong></p> <pre> <code>Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/mymodule/build.py"""""""", line 187, in &lt;module&gt; validate_license() File """"""""/mymodule/build.py"""""""", line 99, in validate_license c = open('LICENSE').read() IOError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'LICENSE'</code> </pre> <p><strong>Suggested Fix</strong></p> <p>Modify lines 99-100 to:<br></p> <pre> <code> path = os.path.join(cwd,'LICENSE') x = open(path) c = x.read()</code> </pre> <p><strong>Ticket Reference</strong></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76398"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76398</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3341,12,"""iOS: navGroup closing window turns black before animation""","""""""{html}<div><p>When you have a navGroup and open a new window using it and then  close the window using the navGroup the window turns black before  the navGroup goes back. If you click the back button the window  does not turn black before the navGroup goes back to the previous  page.</p>  <p>Step 1: launch the sample code below<br>  Step 2: tap the red window to open the blue window<br>  Step 3: click the 'close' button on the blue window to go back to  the red one<br>  Step 4: notice that the blue window turns black before the slide  animation back to the red window<br>  Step 5: click on the red window again<br>  Step 6: tap the left nav button<br>  Step 7: notice that the blue window does not turn black before  going back to the red window</p>  <h3>app.js</h3>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow();    var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor:""""""""red"""""""",      title:""""""""Red Window""""""""  });  win1.addEventListener('click', function(){      nav.open(toolsWindow);  });    var nav = Titanium.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup({     window: win1  });    var toolsWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({      title: 'Blue Window',      url: 'tools_window.js',      nav: nav,      exitOnClose: false,      backgroundColor: 'blue'  });    win.add(nav);  win.open();</code>  </pre>  <h3>tools_window.js</h3>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;    var button = Ti.UI.createButton({      title: 'close',      height: 40,      width: 300,    });  button.addEventListener('click', function(e) {      Ti.API.info('clicked close');      win.nav.close(win);  });    win.add(button);</code>  </pre>  <h3>Tested on</h3>  <p>TiSDK 1.5.1, 1.6.0, iOS SDK 4.2</p>  <h3>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h3>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76439"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76439</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: navGroup closing window turns black before animation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When you have a navGroup and open a new window using it and then close the window using the navGroup the window turns black before the navGroup goes back. If you click the back button the window does not turn black before the navGroup goes back to the previous page.</p> <p>Step 1: launch the sample code below<br> Step 2: tap the red window to open the blue window<br> Step 3: click the 'close' button on the blue window to go back to the red one<br> Step 4: notice that the blue window turns black before the slide animation back to the red window<br> Step 5: click on the red window again<br> Step 6: tap the left nav button<br> Step 7: notice that the blue window does not turn black before going back to the red window</p> <h3>app.js</h3> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow(); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:""""""""red"""""""", title:""""""""Red Window"""""""" }); win1.addEventListener('click', function(){ nav.open(toolsWindow); }); var nav = Titanium.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup({ window: win1 }); var toolsWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Blue Window', url: 'tools_window.js', nav: nav, exitOnClose: false, backgroundColor: 'blue' }); win.add(nav); win.open();</code> </pre> <h3>tools_window.js</h3> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'close', height: 40, width: 300, }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e) { Ti.API.info('clicked close'); win.nav.close(win); }); win.add(button);</code> </pre> <h3>Tested on</h3> <p>TiSDK 1.5.1, 1.6.0, iOS SDK 4.2</p> <h3>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h3> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76439"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/76439</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3340,12,"""Webview loses bindings to Ti/Titanium when navigation occurs on iPhone""","""""""{html}<div><p>I'm observing a problem that appears to already be described by ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1212"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1212"""""""">#1212</a>, though I'm only seeing it on the iPhone. From looking at the patch associated with <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1212"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1212"""""""">#1212</a>, it looks like the issue may only have been fixed for Android.</p> <p>The problem can be demonstrated by using the zip file attached to <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1212"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1212"""""""">#1212</a>.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Webview loses bindings to Ti/Titanium when navigation occurs on iPhone
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I'm observing a problem that appears to already be described by ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1212"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1212"""""""">#1212</a>, though I'm only seeing it on the iPhone. From looking at the patch associated with <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1212"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1212"""""""">#1212</a>, it looks like the issue may only have been fixed for Android.</p> <p>The problem can be demonstrated by using the zip file attached to <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1212"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1212"""""""">#1212</a>.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3339,12,"""On focus window function executed twice in android once in iPhone.""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have the following code in my app:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">win.addEventListener('focus', function(e){     doSomething(); });  function doSomething(){     alert('adasdasd'); }</code> </pre> <p>The alert in android is shown twice while in iPhone once only (as I expect, I don't know which of them is correct).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: On focus window function executed twice in android once in iPhone.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have the following code in my app:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">win.addEventListener('focus', function(e){ doSomething(); }); function doSomething(){ alert('adasdasd'); }</code> </pre> <p>The alert in android is shown twice while in iPhone once only (as I expect, I don't know which of them is correct).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3338,12,"""Application crashes without error message""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I'm trying to add a database to my project and for some reason it doesn't work. The app just crashes.</p> <p>Attachments:</p> <ul> <li>app.js minimalistic file to reproduce this scenario. Commenting away line 8 (database.execute()) keeps the app running.</li> <li>log: the logging information from Titanium Developer - in debug mode</li> </ul> <p>Regards,<br> Sven</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Application crashes without error message
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I'm trying to add a database to my project and for some reason it doesn't work. The app just crashes.</p> <p>Attachments:</p> <ul> <li>app.js minimalistic file to reproduce this scenario. Commenting away line 8 (database.execute()) keeps the app running.</li> <li>log: the logging information from Titanium Developer - in debug mode</li> </ul> <p>Regards,<br> Sven</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3337,12,"""Android:  window context is not set correctly when HW window is closed""","""""""{html}<div><p>Window context is not set back to launch context when heavy weight window is closed.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: window context is not set correctly when HW window is closed
