TIMOB-3176,12,"""Android - yql + flickr crash after running the test with no network connection, then running with one""","""""""{html}<div><p>Feb 17 2011 19:50 r929334e2 all tested devices (1.6 - 2.3)</p> <p>1.disconnect wifi - my devices do not have sim cards, so maybe airplane mode if you have a sim?<br> 2.mashups &gt; YQL + Flickr<br> 3.dismiss runtime error, home screen, connect to wifis<br> 4.run test again</p> <p>results: crash (uncaught exception)</p> <p>pastie : <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1579780"""""""">http://pastie.org/1579780</a></p> <p>does not occur using the same steps and 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - yql + flickr crash after running the test with no network connection, then running with one
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Feb 17 2011 19:50 r929334e2 all tested devices (1.6 - 2.3)</p> <p>1.disconnect wifi - my devices do not have sim cards, so maybe airplane mode if you have a sim?<br> 2.mashups &gt; YQL + Flickr<br> 3.dismiss runtime error, home screen, connect to wifis<br> 4.run test again</p> <p>results: crash (uncaught exception)</p> <p>pastie : <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1579780"""""""">http://pastie.org/1579780</a></p> <p>does not occur using the same steps and 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3175,12,"""iOS: new app will not run on SDK 3.2 TiSDK 1.5.1""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you create a new app in Titanium and try to run it on iOS SDK  3.2 without running a newer version of the iOS SDK first it will  not run. If you build with a newer SDK and then with 3.2 it will  work fine.</p>  <p>Error log on helpdesk ticket:<br></p>  <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73671#c351731"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73671#c351731</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: new app will not run on SDK 3.2 TiSDK 1.5.1
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you create a new app in Titanium and try to run it on iOS SDK 3.2 without running a newer version of the iOS SDK first it will not run. If you build with a newer SDK and then with 3.2 it will work fine.</p> <p>Error log on helpdesk ticket:<br></p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73671#c351731"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73671#c351731</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3174,12,"""iOS: Iterating Over XML Element Attributes""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1>  <p>We can't iterate over attributes in a node. We can only access  them by their name. We do expose the """"""""attributes"""""""" property, which  toStrings as a """"""""[object TiDOMNamedNodeMap]"""""""". The length property of  attributes correctly returns the number of attributes an element  has, but there is no way to access an individual attribute by index  (for example, node.attributes[0] is undefined).</p>  <h1>Solution</h1>  <p>Fix the attributes property to let you access each attribute by  index, or expose a function to let you do this. The former approach  would be more inline with major browsers.</p>  <h1>Sample Code</h1>  <p>The following sample code will write 'FAIL: some message' in a  label if it isn't able to grab an attribute out of a simple XML  string. Otherwise, it will write out the attribute name and value  in a happy green color.</p>  <pre>  <code class=  """"""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' });  var label = Ti.UI.createLabel();  win.add(label);    label.color = '#f00';  label.text += 'FAIL: If you have time to read this, then we never finished reading the attributes.';    var dDocument = Titanium.XML.parseString('&lt;?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""utf-8""""""""?&gt;\r\n&lt;root foo=""""""""bar"""""""" /&gt;');  var node = dDocument.documentElement;  label.text = 'Found ' + node.attributes.length + ' attributes, ';  for (var i = 0; i &lt; node.attributes.length; i++) {      var attribute = node.attributes[i];      if (attribute) {          label.color = '#0f0';          label.text += attribute.name + """""""" = """""""" + attribute.value;      }      else {          label.color = '#f00';          label.text += 'FAIL: attribute undefined.';      }  }    win.open();</code>  </pre>  <h1>Tested On</h1>  <p>Pulled from GitHub master last night: Titanium SDK version:  1.7.0 (02/17/11 20:28 316c2c7)<br>  BROKEN on iPhone Simulator 4.2</p>  <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73221"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73221</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Iterating Over XML Element Attributes
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>We can't iterate over attributes in a node. We can only access them by their name. We do expose the """"""""attributes"""""""" property, which toStrings as a """"""""[object TiDOMNamedNodeMap]"""""""". The length property of attributes correctly returns the number of attributes an element has, but there is no way to access an individual attribute by index (for example, node.attributes[0] is undefined).</p> <h1>Solution</h1> <p>Fix the attributes property to let you access each attribute by index, or expose a function to let you do this. The former approach would be more inline with major browsers.</p> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <p>The following sample code will write 'FAIL: some message' in a label if it isn't able to grab an attribute out of a simple XML string. Otherwise, it will write out the attribute name and value in a happy green color.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel(); win.add(label); label.color = '#f00'; label.text += 'FAIL: If you have time to read this, then we never finished reading the attributes.'; var dDocument = Titanium.XML.parseString('&lt;?xml version=""""""""1.0"""""""" encoding=""""""""utf-8""""""""?&gt;\r\n&lt;root foo=""""""""bar"""""""" /&gt;'); var node = dDocument.documentElement; label.text = 'Found ' + node.attributes.length + ' attributes, '; for (var i = 0; i &lt; node.attributes.length; i++) { var attribute = node.attributes[i]; if (attribute) { label.color = '#0f0'; label.text += attribute.name + """""""" = """""""" + attribute.value; } else { label.color = '#f00'; label.text += 'FAIL: attribute undefined.'; } } win.open();</code> </pre> <h1>Tested On</h1> <p>Pulled from GitHub master last night: Titanium SDK version: 1.7.0 (02/17/11 20:28 316c2c7)<br> BROKEN on iPhone Simulator 4.2</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73221"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73221</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
