TIMOB-3169,12,"""iOS: Implement forceDialogAuth property in Facebook module""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently the iOS Facebook module -- on 4.x multi-tasking devices -- involves the user in authentication/authorization via suspending the app and heading over to the official Facebook app (if installed) or Safari. Some users would like the ability to revert to the legacy, in-app login dialog.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Implement forceDialogAuth property in Facebook module
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently the iOS Facebook module -- on 4.x multi-tasking devices -- involves the user in authentication/authorization via suspending the app and heading over to the official Facebook app (if installed) or Safari. Some users would like the ability to revert to the legacy, in-app login dialog.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3168,12,"""Android:  orientation is not respected when set on lightweight window""","""""""{html}<div><p>Orientation changes set on lightweight are not respected. Currently they must be set on a heavyweight window in order for them to take effect. The issue can be worked around by setting a reference to the heavyweight window on the child lightweight window but a real fix is required.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: orientation is not respected when set on lightweight window
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Orientation changes set on lightweight are not respected. Currently they must be set on a heavyweight window in order for them to take effect. The issue can be worked around by setting a reference to the heavyweight window on the child lightweight window but a real fix is required.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3167,12,"""iOS - close/animate tab group fails 4.0 -4.2.1""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using Feb 17 2011 09:34 ra2a14522. Iphone4 4.2.1 (and all other checked platforms)</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Tab Groups<br> 2.Tap Close/animate tab group</p> <p>results: app hangs on white screen</p> <p>expected: previously (on &gt;3.2) the tab group would go white, then return to base ui group.</p> <p>output seen in console: Wed Dec 31 17:14:04 eWorld UIKitApplication:com.<USER>pushtest[0xc6cb][271] : <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> While executing Timer, received script error. 'Result of expression 'e.tab' <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/undefined"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [undefined]"""""""">[undefined]</a> is not an object. at app.js (line 8)'</p> <p>regression.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - close/animate tab group fails 4.0 -4.2.1
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using Feb 17 2011 09:34 ra2a14522. Iphone4 4.2.1 (and all other checked platforms)</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Tab Groups<br> 2.Tap Close/animate tab group</p> <p>results: app hangs on white screen</p> <p>expected: previously (on &gt;3.2) the tab group would go white, then return to base ui group.</p> <p>output seen in console: Wed Dec 31 17:14:04 eWorld UIKitApplication:com.<USER>pushtest[0xc6cb][271] : <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> While executing Timer, received script error. 'Result of expression 'e.tab' <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/undefined"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [undefined]"""""""">[undefined]</a> is not an object. at app.js (line 8)'</p> <p>regression.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3166,12,"""significant memory leak with thumbnails in tableview""","""""""{html}<div><p>We are using Titanium 1.6RC1 with Developer 1.2.2 and think we have found a significant memory leak when displaying remote thumbnails in a tableview. Below is the code to reproduce.</p> <p>Upon running the code, just attach to the <USER>using XCode Instruments. Then click the """"""""Photos"""""""" button to bring up the grid of photos, then click back to close the window. Continue to do this over and over again and you will see the living memory allocations continue to increase to extremely high levels.</p> <p>Why doesn't closing a window free up all it's memory usage? I come from the Objective-C world and have created this same screen natively with no memory leaks. Am I missing something in our javascript code? This is a showstopper for us if we cannot find a solution.</p> <p>Thanks!</p> <p><USER>/p> <pre> <code>var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup({id:'tabGroup1'});   win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({id:'win1',backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title:'Photos',width:100, height:100});   button.addEventListener('click', function() {     var photosWindow = Titanium.UI.createWindow({fullscreen:false});     var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({         separatorStyle:Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewSeparatorStyle.NONE     });     photosWindow.add(tableView);       tab1.open(photosWindow, {animated:true});       var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient();     xhr.onload = function() {         var list = JSON.parse(this.responseText).List;         var rowData = [];         for (var i = 0,count = list.length; i &lt; count; i += 4) {             var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({                 height:'auto',                 selectedBackgroundColor: '#fff',                 backgroundSelectedColor: '#fff',                 className:'tvRow'             }),imgDimensions = 80;                 var offSet = 0;             for (var j = 0; j &lt; 4; j++) {                 var photo = list[i + j];                 if (photo) {                     var photoView = Ti.UI.createImageView({                         top:0,                         left:offSet,                         height:imgDimensions,                         width:imgDimensions,                         image:photo.ThumbnailUrl                     });                     row.add(photoView);                     offSet += imgDimensions;                 }             }             rowData.push(row);         }         tableView.setData(rowData);     };     var url = """"""""http://idancemobile.com/event/e2e530/api/2.0/images/0"""""""";     xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""", url);     xhr.send(); });   win.add(button);   var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({     id:'tab1',     window:win });   tabGroup.addTab(tab1);   tabGroup.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: significant memory leak with thumbnails in tableview
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We are using Titanium 1.6RC1 with Developer 1.2.2 and think we have found a significant memory leak when displaying remote thumbnails in a tableview. Below is the code to reproduce.</p> <p>Upon running the code, just attach to the <USER>using XCode Instruments. Then click the """"""""Photos"""""""" button to bring up the grid of photos, then click back to close the window. Continue to do this over and over again and you will see the living memory allocations continue to increase to extremely high levels.</p> <p>Why doesn't closing a window free up all it's memory usage? I come from the Objective-C world and have created this same screen natively with no memory leaks. Am I missing something in our javascript code? This is a showstopper for us if we cannot find a solution.</p> <p>Thanks!</p> <p><USER>/p> <pre> <code>var tabGroup = Titanium.UI.createTabGroup({id:'tabGroup1'}); win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({id:'win1',backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({title:'Photos',width:100, height:100}); button.addEventListener('click', function() { var photosWindow = Titanium.UI.createWindow({fullscreen:false}); var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({ separatorStyle:Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewSeparatorStyle.NONE }); photosWindow.add(tableView); tab1.open(photosWindow, {animated:true}); var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function() { var list = JSON.parse(this.responseText).List; var rowData = []; for (var i = 0,count = list.length; i &lt; count; i += 4) { var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ height:'auto', selectedBackgroundColor: '#fff', backgroundSelectedColor: '#fff', className:'tvRow' }),imgDimensions = 80; var offSet = 0; for (var j = 0; j &lt; 4; j++) { var photo = list[i + j]; if (photo) { var photoView = Ti.UI.createImageView({ top:0, left:offSet, height:imgDimensions, width:imgDimensions, image:photo.ThumbnailUrl }); row.add(photoView); offSet += imgDimensions; } } rowData.push(row); } tableView.setData(rowData); }; var url = """"""""http://idancemobile.com/event/e2e530/api/2.0/images/0""""""""; xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""", url); xhr.send(); }); win.add(button); var tab1 = Titanium.UI.createTab({ id:'tab1', window:win }); tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3165,12,"""Android: Galaxy tab only - unable to disable text field entry ""","""""""{html}<div><p>mobile sdk - Feb 17 2011 09:34 ra2a14522. Galaxy tab, 2.2.2. Not seen on any other android platforms</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; Text field &gt; the rest<br> 2.Tap enabled</p> <p>results: no state change - all other android sdk platforms will show the field being disabled.</p> <p>not new to this build</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Galaxy tab only - unable to disable text field entry
Description: """"{html}<div><p>mobile sdk - Feb 17 2011 09:34 ra2a14522. Galaxy tab, 2.2.2. Not seen on any other android platforms</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; Text field &gt; the rest<br> 2.Tap enabled</p> <p>results: no state change - all other android sdk platforms will show the field being disabled.</p> <p>not new to this build</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3164,12,"""Android: Expose MediaScannerConnection""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>When you save an image to the SDCard, the media scanner won't pick it up until the next time it runs (when the phone restarts).</p> <h1>Solution</h1> <p>Exposing the MediaScannerConnection would let developers get the image into the gallery right away.</p> <h1>Android Documentation</h1> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaScannerConnection.html""""""""> http://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaScannerCo...</a></p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69031"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69031</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose MediaScannerConnection
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>When you save an image to the SDCard, the media scanner won't pick it up until the next time it runs (when the phone restarts).</p> <h1>Solution</h1> <p>Exposing the MediaScannerConnection would let developers get the image into the gallery right away.</p> <h1>Android Documentation</h1> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaScannerConnection.html""""""""> http://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaScannerCo...</a></p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69031"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69031</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3163,12,"""Tooling: Android Built-in Modules Need Native Resource Support""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/3161"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #3161"""""""">#3161</a> needs support added to the Android build to allow native resources to be used in components. For example the cancel icon on searchbar needs to be density aware. I can also forsee needing localization support as well.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Android Built-in Modules Need Native Resource Support
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/3161"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #3161"""""""">#3161</a> needs support added to the Android build to allow native resources to be used in components. For example the cancel icon on searchbar needs to be density aware. I can also forsee needing localization support as well.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3161,12,"""Android: Add Multiple Density Images for Cancel Button""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>The built in Cancel button, visible when you add a search bar to an app, doesn't support multiple densities right now. So when you view it on a high density display, it is much smaller than it should be.</p> <h1>Solution</h1> <p>Add multiple images for the various densities.</p> <h1>Where Is It</h1> <p>Looking at the source, it is located here:</p> <pre> <code>android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/searchbar/cancel.png</code> </pre> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <p>Taken from our documentation:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var search = Titanium.UI.createSearchBar({     barColor:'#000',      showCancel:true,     height:""""""""43dp"""""""",     top:0, });</code> </pre> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73761"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73761</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add Multiple Density Images for Cancel Button
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>The built in Cancel button, visible when you add a search bar to an app, doesn't support multiple densities right now. So when you view it on a high density display, it is much smaller than it should be.</p> <h1>Solution</h1> <p>Add multiple images for the various densities.</p> <h1>Where Is It</h1> <p>Looking at the source, it is located here:</p> <pre> <code>android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/searchbar/cancel.png</code> </pre> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <p>Taken from our documentation:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var search = Titanium.UI.createSearchBar({ barColor:'#000', showCancel:true, height:""""""""43dp"""""""", top:0, });</code> </pre> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73761"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73761</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3160,12,"""iOS: removeEventListener crashes when passed 'this'""","""""""{html}<div><p>Application crashes when you try to use 'this' in  removeEventListener to remove an addEventListener who's function  you are in.</p>  <p>This code sample if from the code example at <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.Animation-object"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI....</a></p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">  var view = Titanium.UI.createView({     backgroundColor:'red'  });  var animation = Titanium.UI.createAnimation();  animation.backgroundColor = 'black';  animation.duration = 1000;  animation.addEventListener('complete',function()  {     animation.removeEventListener('complete',this);     animation.backgroundColor = 'orange';     view.animate(animation);  });  view.animate(animation);</code>  </pre>  <p>tested with 1.5.1, 1.6.0RC1, iOS SDK 4.2</p>  <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73881"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73881</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: removeEventListener crashes when passed 'this'
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Application crashes when you try to use 'this' in removeEventListener to remove an addEventListener who's function you are in.</p> <p>This code sample if from the code example at <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.Animation-object""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI....</a></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var view = Titanium.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'red' }); var animation = Titanium.UI.createAnimation(); animation.backgroundColor = 'black'; animation.duration = 1000; animation.addEventListener('complete',function() { animation.removeEventListener('complete',this); animation.backgroundColor = 'orange'; view.animate(animation); }); view.animate(animation);</code> </pre> <p>tested with 1.5.1, 1.6.0RC1, iOS SDK 4.2</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73881"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73881</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3159,12,"""Android: Setting Orientation on Single window not recoginized""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you allow all orientation modes in the application but then  set one window to a certain orientation, the orientation is not  respected for that window.</p>  <p>Ticket Reference: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73831"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73831</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Setting Orientation on Single window not recoginized
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you allow all orientation modes in the application but then set one window to a certain orientation, the orientation is not respected for that window.</p> <p>Ticket Reference: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73831"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/73831</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3158,12,"""Android: Activity indicator crashes app with """"is your activity running?""""""","""""""{html}<div><p>split off from <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/3099"""""""" title=  """"""""Ticket #3099"""""""">#3099</a>. Seen on a nexus s (2.3.1) running  <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title=  """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/08/11  20:55 bd9d124...)</p>  <p>1.Mashups &gt; YQL &gt; YQL + Flickr</p>  <p>results: intermittent crash - pastie here: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1550070"""""""">http://pastie.org/1550070</a></p>  <p>E/TiUncaughtHandler( 7825):  android.view.WindowManager$BadTokenException: Unable to add window  -- token android.os.BinderProxy@40512ad8 is not valid; is your  activity running?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Activity indicator crashes app with """"is your activity running?""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>split off from <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/3099"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #3099"""""""">#3099</a>. Seen on a nexus s (2.3.1) running <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/08/11 20:55 bd9d124...)</p> <p>1.Mashups &gt; YQL &gt; YQL + Flickr</p> <p>results: intermittent crash - pastie here: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1550070"""""""">http://pastie.org/1550070</a></p> <p>E/TiUncaughtHandler( 7825): android.view.WindowManager$BadTokenException: Unable to add window -- token android.os.BinderProxy@40512ad8 is not valid; is your activity running?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3157,12,"""iOS: app:// URL specifier may cause crashes""","""""""{html}<div><p>Can be viewed by loading the following HTML into a window with  the KS movie.mp4 resource present in the appropriate location:</p>  <pre>  <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC """"""""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN"""""""" """"""""http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd""""""""&gt;  &lt;html&gt;  &lt;head&gt;      &lt;link rel=""""""""stylesheet"""""""" type=""""""""text/css"""""""" href=""""""""../test.css"""""""" /&gt;      &lt;script type=""""""""text/javascript"""""""" src=""""""""../jquery-1.3.2.js""""""""&gt;&lt;/script&gt;      &lt;meta name=""""""""format-detection"""""""" content=""""""""telephone=no""""""""/&gt;  &lt;/head&gt;  &lt;body id=""""""""mybody"""""""" style=""""""""height:500px;background-color:#999;background-image:url(../images/bg.png)""""""""&gt;  &lt;video src=""""""""app://movie.mp4"""""""" autoplay controls /&gt;     &lt;/body&gt;  &lt;/html&gt;</code>  </pre>  <p>Causes a crash in +[TiUtils loadAppResource:] via:  <code>'NSRangeException', reason: '*** -[NSCFString  characterAtIndex:]: Range or index out of bounds'</code></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: app:// URL specifier may cause crashes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Can be viewed by loading the following HTML into a window with the KS movie.mp4 resource present in the appropriate location:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC """"""""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN"""""""" """"""""http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd""""""""&gt; &lt;html&gt; &lt;head&gt; &lt;link rel=""""""""stylesheet"""""""" type=""""""""text/css"""""""" href=""""""""../test.css"""""""" /&gt; &lt;script type=""""""""text/javascript"""""""" src=""""""""../jquery-1.3.2.js""""""""&gt;&lt;/script&gt; &lt;meta name=""""""""format-detection"""""""" content=""""""""telephone=no""""""""/&gt; &lt;/head&gt; &lt;body id=""""""""mybody"""""""" style=""""""""height:500px;background-color:#999;background-image:url(../images/bg.png)""""""""&gt; &lt;video src=""""""""app://movie.mp4"""""""" autoplay controls /&gt; &lt;/body&gt; &lt;/html&gt;</code> </pre> <p>Causes a crash in +[TiUtils loadAppResource:] via: <code>'NSRangeException', reason: '*** -[NSCFString characterAtIndex:]: Range or index out of bounds'</code></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3156,12,"""iOS, Publish stream test succeeds but callback fails""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/15/11 12:42 b9a4f2c...)</p> <p>iPhone4, ipad 3.2</p> <p>1.install and fire up the facebook test<br> 2.log in then go to publish stream<br> 3.tap """"""""publish wall post with dialog""""""""</p> <p>results: checking fb, the post was logged, but we get back an error condition that FB did not send back any data.</p> <p>""""""""success, but no data from FB. I am guessing you cancelled the dialog.""""""""</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS, Publish stream test succeeds but callback fails
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/15/11 12:42 b9a4f2c...)</p> <p>iPhone4, ipad 3.2</p> <p>1.install and fire up the facebook test<br> 2.log in then go to publish stream<br> 3.tap """"""""publish wall post with dialog""""""""</p> <p>results: checking fb, the post was logged, but we get back an error condition that FB did not send back any data.</p> <p>""""""""success, but no data from FB. I am guessing you cancelled the dialog.""""""""</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
