TIMOB-3127,12,"""iOS < 3.2 - KS crash on launch""","""""""{html}<div><p>seen on ipad 3.2 and iphone 3.1.3, <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/14/11 09:55 bd9d124)</p> <p>1.Using noted pull, install KS to device (3.1.3 or 3.2)<br> 2.launch</p> <p>results: crash on launch, crash log attached</p> <p>Dyld Error Message:<br> Library not loaded: /System/Library/Frameworks/CoreMedia.framework/CoreMedia Referenced from: /var/mobile/Applications/FA54C320-9AE2-414C-9AD1-6A66637BECBF/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink Reason: image not found Dyld Version: 149</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS < 3.2 - KS crash on launch
Description: """"{html}<div><p>seen on ipad 3.2 and iphone 3.1.3, <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/14/11 09:55 bd9d124)</p> <p>1.Using noted pull, install KS to device (3.1.3 or 3.2)<br> 2.launch</p> <p>results: crash on launch, crash log attached</p> <p>Dyld Error Message:<br> Library not loaded: /System/Library/Frameworks/CoreMedia.framework/CoreMedia Referenced from: /var/mobile/Applications/FA54C320-9AE2-414C-9AD1-6A66637BECBF/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink Reason: image not found Dyld Version: 149</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3125,12,"""Android : borders not working for lightweight windows""","""""""{html}<div><p>(1.6.0.bd9d124), emulator and device</p> <p>1.use the following snippet:</p> <p>var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>        backgroundColor:'white',         borderWidth:3,         borderColor:'#336699',     });</code> </pre> <p>win1.open();</p> <p>works as expected on iOS and in android 1.5.1</p> <p>came via: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/111751/16-rc-border-not-working-on-lightweight-window""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/111751/16-rc-border-not-...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : borders not working for lightweight windows
Description: """"{html}<div><p>(1.6.0.bd9d124), emulator and device</p> <p>1.use the following snippet:</p> <p>var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code> backgroundColor:'white', borderWidth:3, borderColor:'#336699', });</code> </pre> <p>win1.open();</p> <p>works as expected on iOS and in android 1.5.1</p> <p>came via: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/111751/16-rc-border-not-working-on-lightweight-window""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/111751/16-rc-border-not-...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3124,12,"""Android: Cannot restart stream in AudioPlayer after stream is stopped.""","""""""{html}<div><p>In android, if you stop an audioplayer stream and then start the  stream again, the audio plays for a couple seconds (presumably what  remains in the buffer) and then the audio stops.</p>  <p>This does not seem recoverable currently, you MUST quit the app  and restart to get audio playing again.</p>  <p>There is a discussion <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/64781/audioplayer-streaming-mp3-in-android#120341""""""""  title=""""""""here"""""""">Here</a> on how this problem is fixed in the Android  SDK, exposing reset() and prepare() methods to  Titanium.Media.audioPlayer should allow users to overcome this  problem on Android.</p>  <p>Titanium SDK 1.5.1 and 1.6.0.RC1<br>  Testing on Android 2.2</p>  <p>Thanks!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Cannot restart stream in AudioPlayer after stream is stopped.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In android, if you stop an audioplayer stream and then start the stream again, the audio plays for a couple seconds (presumably what remains in the buffer) and then the audio stops.</p> <p>This does not seem recoverable currently, you MUST quit the app and restart to get audio playing again.</p> <p>There is a discussion <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/64781/audioplayer-streaming-mp3-in-android#120341"""""""" title=""""""""here"""""""">Here</a> on how this problem is fixed in the Android SDK, exposing reset() and prepare() methods to Titanium.Media.audioPlayer should allow users to overcome this problem on Android.</p> <p>Titanium SDK 1.5.1 and 1.6.0.RC1<br> Testing on Android 2.2</p> <p>Thanks!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3123,12,"""Android: webview link with new or blank target (ie """"popup"""") does not open""","""""""{html}<div><p>Android """"""""APIs 2.2"""""""" / Titanium 1.6.0 (11 Feb 2011)</p>  <p>It isn't surprising that this does not work, but I am creating  the ticket in the interests of completeness, as the issue has been  opened for iOS in ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1603""""""""  title=""""""""Ticket #1603"""""""">#1603</a> and seems to be confirmed by core  devs. Note that the iOS ticket claims that these types of links can  be browsed on iOS 4.</p>  <p>Clicking a link in a webview that has a target (new, blank) that  would ordinarily open a new window in a standard browser is  ignored. The following code demonstrates the behavior:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: 'white',      exitOnClose:true  });    Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');    var webView = Ti.UI.createWebView({      url: """"""""http://www.cnn.com/2010/TECH/social.media/08/12/delta.facebook.ticket.window/index.html"""""""",      top: 0,      left: 0,      width: '100%',      height: '100%'    });    webView.addEventListener('load',function(e) {      Ti.API.info(""""""""Load event caught with: """""""" + e.url);  });    webView.addEventListener('beforeload',function(e) {      Ti.API.info(""""""""beforeload event caught with: """""""" + e.url);  });    win.add(webView);    win.open();</code>  </pre>  <p>The built-in browser <strong>does</strong> recognize the  link:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor: 'white',      exitOnClose:true  });      Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');    win.open();  Ti.Platform.openURL('http://www.cnn.com/2010/TECH/social.media/08/12/delta.facebook.ticket.window/index.html');</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: webview link with new or blank target (ie """"popup"""") does not open
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Android """"""""APIs 2.2"""""""" / Titanium 1.6.0 (11 Feb 2011)</p> <p>It isn't surprising that this does not work, but I am creating the ticket in the interests of completeness, as the issue has been opened for iOS in ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1603"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1603"""""""">#1603</a> and seems to be confirmed by core devs. Note that the iOS ticket claims that these types of links can be browsed on iOS 4.</p> <p>Clicking a link in a webview that has a target (new, blank) that would ordinarily open a new window in a standard browser is ignored. The following code demonstrates the behavior:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white', exitOnClose:true }); Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var webView = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url: """"""""http://www.cnn.com/2010/TECH/social.media/08/12/delta.facebook.ticket.window/index.html"""""""", top: 0, left: 0, width: '100%', height: '100%' }); webView.addEventListener('load',function(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Load event caught with: """""""" + e.url); }); webView.addEventListener('beforeload',function(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""beforeload event caught with: """""""" + e.url); }); win.add(webView); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>The built-in browser <strong>does</strong> recognize the link:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'white', exitOnClose:true }); Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); win.open(); Ti.Platform.openURL('http://www.cnn.com/2010/TECH/social.media/08/12/delta.facebook.ticket.window/index.html');</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3122,12,"""iOS: ImageView animation ignores repeatCount upon second call to start()""","""""""If you {{start()}} an animation created with an imageView, it will  honor the repeatCount setting the first time. However, if you call  {{start()}} again, the animation will repeat indefinitely. Tested on  all versions of supported iOS.  Code to demonstrate:  """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ImageView animation ignores repeatCount upon second call to start()
Description: """"If you {{start()}} an animation created with an imageView, it will honor the repeatCount setting the first time. However, if you call {{start()}} again, the animation will repeat indefinitely. Tested on all versions of supported iOS. Code to demonstrate: """"",title+description
TIMOB-3121,12,"""Does Not Fire Resume Event When Returning from iOS Multitasking Bar""","""""""{html}<div><p>In iOS when a user double taps the home button to bring up the  multitasking bar, Titanium fires a pause event. If the user double  taps the home button again to dismiss the multitasking bar,  Titanium does NOT fire a resume event.</p>  <p>Found the same results when testing SDK versions 1.5.1,  1.6.0.RC1, 1.7.0 w/ iOS SDK version 4.2</p>  <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/72951"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/72951</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Does Not Fire Resume Event When Returning from iOS Multitasking Bar
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In iOS when a user double taps the home button to bring up the multitasking bar, Titanium fires a pause event. If the user double taps the home button again to dismiss the multitasking bar, Titanium does NOT fire a resume event.</p> <p>Found the same results when testing SDK versions 1.5.1, 1.6.0.RC1, 1.7.0 w/ iOS SDK version 4.2</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/72951"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/72951</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3120,12,"""TiDev Feature Request:  remove dependency on build folders""","""""""{html}<div><p>Deleting build/android or iphone folder and restarting TiDev makes that tab disappear, because TiDev uses the folder to detect if the tab should display. This should be defined in the tiapp.xml or elsewhere to remove this dependency on the physical folder being there.</p> <p>Reference Ticket:<a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70351"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70351</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiDev Feature Request: remove dependency on build folders
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Deleting build/android or iphone folder and restarting TiDev makes that tab disappear, because TiDev uses the folder to detect if the tab should display. This should be defined in the tiapp.xml or elsewhere to remove this dependency on the physical folder being there.</p> <p>Reference Ticket:<a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70351"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70351</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
