TIMOB-3096,12,"""touchstart eventListener disables all input text fields""","""""""{html}<div><p>Adding a 'touchstart' eventListener to a tableview causes any textField in the table to become non-enterable. Comment out the touchstart eventListener and all is well. This works fine in iOS.</p> <p>I've attached a sample program below.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: touchstart eventListener disables all input text fields
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Adding a 'touchstart' eventListener to a tableview causes any textField in the table to become non-enterable. Comment out the touchstart eventListener and all is well. This works fine in iOS.</p> <p>I've attached a sample program below.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3095,12,"""Android: Our download cache does not respect the standard of case-insensitive headers""","""""""{html}<div><p>For example, we check for """"""""Cache-Control"""""""" and would miss """"""""cache-control"""""""". According to <a href= """"""""http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec4.html#sec4.2"""""""">this</a> headers are case-insensitive.</p> <p>Failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#000',     exitOnClose: true }); var thisURL = """"""""module=MultiSites&amp;action=getEvolutionGraph&amp;period=day&amp;date=2011-01-04,2011-02-02&amp;evolutionBy=visits&amp;columns=nb_visits&amp;idSite=7&amp;idsite=7&amp;viewDataTable=sparkline"""""""";  var paramArray = thisURL.split(""""""""&amp;""""""""); for(var i=0,ilen=paramArray.length;i&lt;ilen;i++){     var thisKeyValue = paramArray[i].split(""""""""="""""""");     thisKeyValue[1] = Ti.Network.encodeURIComponent(thisKeyValue[1]);     paramArray[i] = thisKeyValue.join(""""""""=""""""""); } var encodedURI = paramArray.join(""""""""&amp;""""""""); var encodedURL = """"""""http://demo.piwik.org/index.php?"""""""" + encodedURI; Ti.API.info(encodedURL);  var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({     image: encodedURL });   win.add(imageView); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>Follow these steps:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Create a new titanium project and make the code above its app.js.</p> </li> <li> <p>Run the app. The app will crash because of <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3094"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3094"""""""">#3094</a>, but that's okay because it's already written to the cache.</p> </li> <li> <p>At the command line do the following commands.</p> </li> </ul> <pre> <code>adb shell cd /sdcard/[your app id]/remote-image-cache ls cat *.hdr</code> </pre> <p>(But of course replace [your app id] with your app's id.)</p> <p>After entering the <code>ls</code> command, you will see files listed. There should not be any, because the file that is being cached there should not have been cached. You can see that because of the <code>cat</code> command which shows you the http headers retrieved upon getting the remote file. One of the headers is <code>cache-control</code> and it indicates that the file should <strong>not</strong> be cached. But it was, and the reason is because we were looking for <code>Cache-Control</code> in a case-sensitive fashion, so we missed <code>cache-control</code>.</p> <p><strong>Important notes re testing the fix</strong></p> <p>Once you're ready to test the fix, you need to be sure to <strong>clear the cache</strong> to get rid of those files that shouldn't have been there in the first place.</p> <pre> <code>adb shell cd /sdcard rm -r [your app id]</code> </pre> <p>And when you test the fix, don't be shocked if no image at all appears on screen. That's bug <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3093"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3093"""""""">#3093</a>. For this test, you just want to be sure that after you launch the app there is nothing in the remote-image-cache for your app.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Our download cache does not respect the standard of case-insensitive headers
Description: """"{html}<div><p>For example, we check for """"""""Cache-Control"""""""" and would miss """"""""cache-control"""""""". According to <a href= """"""""http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec4.html#sec4.2"""""""">this</a> headers are case-insensitive.</p> <p>Failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#000', exitOnClose: true }); var thisURL = """"""""module=MultiSites&amp;action=getEvolutionGraph&amp;period=day&amp;date=2011-01-04,2011-02-02&amp;evolutionBy=visits&amp;columns=nb_visits&amp;idSite=7&amp;idsite=7&amp;viewDataTable=sparkline""""""""; var paramArray = thisURL.split(""""""""&amp;""""""""); for(var i=0,ilen=paramArray.length;i&lt;ilen;i++){ var thisKeyValue = paramArray[i].split(""""""""=""""""""); thisKeyValue[1] = Ti.Network.encodeURIComponent(thisKeyValue[1]); paramArray[i] = thisKeyValue.join(""""""""=""""""""); } var encodedURI = paramArray.join(""""""""&amp;""""""""); var encodedURL = """"""""http://demo.piwik.org/index.php?"""""""" + encodedURI; Ti.API.info(encodedURL); var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: encodedURL }); win.add(imageView); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>Follow these steps:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Create a new titanium project and make the code above its app.js.</p> </li> <li> <p>Run the app. The app will crash because of <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3094"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3094"""""""">#3094</a>, but that's okay because it's already written to the cache.</p> </li> <li> <p>At the command line do the following commands.</p> </li> </ul> <pre> <code>adb shell cd /sdcard/[your app id]/remote-image-cache ls cat *.hdr</code> </pre> <p>(But of course replace [your app id] with your app's id.)</p> <p>After entering the <code>ls</code> command, you will see files listed. There should not be any, because the file that is being cached there should not have been cached. You can see that because of the <code>cat</code> command which shows you the http headers retrieved upon getting the remote file. One of the headers is <code>cache-control</code> and it indicates that the file should <strong>not</strong> be cached. But it was, and the reason is because we were looking for <code>Cache-Control</code> in a case-sensitive fashion, so we missed <code>cache-control</code>.</p> <p><strong>Important notes re testing the fix</strong></p> <p>Once you're ready to test the fix, you need to be sure to <strong>clear the cache</strong> to get rid of those files that shouldn't have been there in the first place.</p> <pre> <code>adb shell cd /sdcard rm -r [your app id]</code> </pre> <p>And when you test the fix, don't be shocked if no image at all appears on screen. That's bug <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3093"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3093"""""""">#3093</a>. For this test, you just want to be sure that after you launch the app there is nothing in the remote-image-cache for your app.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3094,12,"""Android: NumberFormatException if cached file does not have a content-length""","""""""{html}<div><p>Failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#000',     exitOnClose: true }); var thisURL = """"""""module=MultiSites&amp;action=getEvolutionGraph&amp;period=day&amp;date=2011-01-04,2011-02-02&amp;evolutionBy=visits&amp;columns=nb_visits&amp;idSite=7&amp;idsite=7&amp;viewDataTable=sparkline"""""""";  var paramArray = thisURL.split(""""""""&amp;""""""""); for(var i=0,ilen=paramArray.length;i&lt;ilen;i++){     var thisKeyValue = paramArray[i].split(""""""""="""""""");     thisKeyValue[1] = Ti.Network.encodeURIComponent(thisKeyValue[1]);     paramArray[i] = thisKeyValue.join(""""""""=""""""""); } var encodedURI = paramArray.join(""""""""&amp;""""""""); var encodedURL = """"""""http://demo.piwik.org/index.php?"""""""" + encodedURI; Ti.API.info(encodedURL);  var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({     image: encodedURL });   win.add(imageView); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>This app will crash when you run it.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: NumberFormatException if cached file does not have a content-length
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#000', exitOnClose: true }); var thisURL = """"""""module=MultiSites&amp;action=getEvolutionGraph&amp;period=day&amp;date=2011-01-04,2011-02-02&amp;evolutionBy=visits&amp;columns=nb_visits&amp;idSite=7&amp;idsite=7&amp;viewDataTable=sparkline""""""""; var paramArray = thisURL.split(""""""""&amp;""""""""); for(var i=0,ilen=paramArray.length;i&lt;ilen;i++){ var thisKeyValue = paramArray[i].split(""""""""=""""""""); thisKeyValue[1] = Ti.Network.encodeURIComponent(thisKeyValue[1]); paramArray[i] = thisKeyValue.join(""""""""=""""""""); } var encodedURI = paramArray.join(""""""""&amp;""""""""); var encodedURL = """"""""http://demo.piwik.org/index.php?"""""""" + encodedURI; Ti.API.info(encodedURL); var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: encodedURL }); win.add(imageView); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>This app will crash when you run it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3093,12,"""Android: Non-cached network images will not appear in TiUIImageView""","""""""{html}<div><p>If our cache implementation does not cache an image (such as if the http header when retrieving that image says to not cache it), it fails to appear in the image view.</p> <p>Failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#000',     exitOnClose: true }); var thisURL = """"""""module=MultiSites&amp;action=getEvolutionGraph&amp;period=day&amp;date=2011-01-04,2011-02-02&amp;evolutionBy=visits&amp;columns=nb_visits&amp;idSite=7&amp;idsite=7&amp;viewDataTable=sparkline"""""""";  var paramArray = thisURL.split(""""""""&amp;""""""""); for(var i=0,ilen=paramArray.length;i&lt;ilen;i++){     var thisKeyValue = paramArray[i].split(""""""""="""""""");     thisKeyValue[1] = Ti.Network.encodeURIComponent(thisKeyValue[1]);     paramArray[i] = thisKeyValue.join(""""""""=""""""""); } var encodedURI = paramArray.join(""""""""&amp;""""""""); var encodedURL = """"""""http://demo.piwik.org/index.php?"""""""" + encodedURI; Ti.API.info(encodedURL);  var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({     image: encodedURL });   win.add(imageView); win.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Non-cached network images will not appear in TiUIImageView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If our cache implementation does not cache an image (such as if the http header when retrieving that image says to not cache it), it fails to appear in the image view.</p> <p>Failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#000', exitOnClose: true }); var thisURL = """"""""module=MultiSites&amp;action=getEvolutionGraph&amp;period=day&amp;date=2011-01-04,2011-02-02&amp;evolutionBy=visits&amp;columns=nb_visits&amp;idSite=7&amp;idsite=7&amp;viewDataTable=sparkline""""""""; var paramArray = thisURL.split(""""""""&amp;""""""""); for(var i=0,ilen=paramArray.length;i&lt;ilen;i++){ var thisKeyValue = paramArray[i].split(""""""""=""""""""); thisKeyValue[1] = Ti.Network.encodeURIComponent(thisKeyValue[1]); paramArray[i] = thisKeyValue.join(""""""""=""""""""); } var encodedURI = paramArray.join(""""""""&amp;""""""""); var encodedURL = """"""""http://demo.piwik.org/index.php?"""""""" + encodedURI; Ti.API.info(encodedURL); var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: encodedURL }); win.add(imageView); win.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3091,12,"""iPhone: Audio queue creation failed""","""""""{html}<div><p>I randomly get """"""""Audio queue creation failed. err: !fmt 560360820"""""""" errors. There is no special system for when they pop up, but it occurs quite often. The error itself is not a big problem, but once this error occurs many things in the app break.</p> <p>In my situation it breaks functions and animations. For example, appending, animating or removing a view will be very buggy.</p> <pre> <code>2011-01-13 23:32:04.836 Radio HD[10357:6e47] Audio queue creation failed. err: !fmt 560360820  [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt;  [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt;  [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt;  [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt;  [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt;  [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animation guard triggered, we exceeded the timeout on waiting for view to become ready</code> </pre> <p>This error occurs in one of my apps, and after the error it really becomes useless and everything gets messed up. Seeing how this error randomly pops up when start() is executed, I created a project that will try to start a new stream every 10 seconds. Doing so you don't have to press button yourself while waiting for the error, it will however not show how the rest of the app can be affected by the error. This now hosted on GitHub and can be found here: <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>streamError"""""""">http://github.com/<USER>streamError</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/100331/audio-queue-error-renders-app-useless""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/100331/audio-queue-error...</a><br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/78481/catch-error-audio-queue-creation-failed""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/78481/catch-error-audio-...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Audio queue creation failed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I randomly get """"""""Audio queue creation failed. err: !fmt 560360820"""""""" errors. There is no special system for when they pop up, but it occurs quite often. The error itself is not a big problem, but once this error occurs many things in the app break.</p> <p>In my situation it breaks functions and animations. For example, appending, animating or removing a view will be very buggy.</p> <pre> <code>2011-01-13 23:32:04.836 Radio HD[10357:6e47] Audio queue creation failed. err: !fmt 560360820 [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animated called and we're not ready ... (will try again) &gt; [DEBUG] animation guard triggered, we exceeded the timeout on waiting for view to become ready</code> </pre> <p>This error occurs in one of my apps, and after the error it really becomes useless and everything gets messed up. Seeing how this error randomly pops up when start() is executed, I created a project that will try to start a new stream every 10 seconds. Doing so you don't have to press button yourself while waiting for the error, it will however not show how the rest of the app can be affected by the error. This now hosted on GitHub and can be found here: <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>streamError"""""""">http://github.com/<USER>streamError</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/100331/audio-queue-error-renders-app-useless""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/100331/audio-queue-error...</a><br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/78481/catch-error-audio-queue-creation-failed""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/78481/catch-error-audio-...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3090,12,"""Generate HTML docs from mark down on Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>Need to have the Android platform generate HTML docs from the mark down file as the iOS side does.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Generate HTML docs from mark down on Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Need to have the Android platform generate HTML docs from the mark down file as the iOS side does.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3089,12,"""iPhone: SearchBar UI Doesn't get fully rendered when focus() is added before the window is opened""","""""""{html}<div><p>This could be a defect or just an issue of what is best  practice.</p>  <p>If you set a focus() on the SearchBar before the window is  opened it doesn't get fully rendered (see customer's example)  <em>or</em> will draw it on the canvas realtime (See video link  below). The workaround is simple: place the focus() after the  window is opened or delay the focus event a few ms.</p>  <p>Sample Code: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1545123"""""""">http://pastie.org/1545123</a><br>  Video: <a href=  """"""""http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/4a51feee-e70e-4cd0-bfcd-b751661d3943"""""""">  http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/4...</a><br>  HD Ticket (Customer's sample code there): <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66091#c340591"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66091#c340591</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: SearchBar UI Doesn't get fully rendered when focus() is added before the window is opened
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This could be a defect or just an issue of what is best practice.</p> <p>If you set a focus() on the SearchBar before the window is opened it doesn't get fully rendered (see customer's example) <em>or</em> will draw it on the canvas realtime (See video link below). The workaround is simple: place the focus() after the window is opened or delay the focus event a few ms.</p> <p>Sample Code: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1545123"""""""">http://pastie.org/1545123</a><br> Video: <a href= """"""""http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/4a51feee-e70e-4cd0-bfcd-b751661d3943""""""""> http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/4...</a><br> HD Ticket (Customer's sample code there): <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66091#c340591"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66091#c340591</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3088,12,"""iOS: 1.5.2 - initWithWindow - Private API rejected by Apple - CRITICAL""","""""""{html}<div><p>When I posted the application made for the iPad 1.5.2, the response of the review of<br> application was:</p> <p>""""""""The non-public API that is included in your application is initWithWindow:. If you Have set the method in your source code with the name The Same this API, we Suggest<br> altering your name method so that it no longer collides with Apple's private API to<br> Avoid Being flagged you application in future submissions. """"""""</p> <p>I searched for this Palava is encountering it in the file TiUIWindowProxy.m.</p> <p>I'm sure this is critical and should be treated with the utmost speed, as<br> means that no application is approved by Apple.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: 1.5.2 - initWithWindow - Private API rejected by Apple - CRITICAL
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When I posted the application made for the iPad 1.5.2, the response of the review of<br> application was:</p> <p>""""""""The non-public API that is included in your application is initWithWindow:. If you Have set the method in your source code with the name The Same this API, we Suggest<br> altering your name method so that it no longer collides with Apple's private API to<br> Avoid Being flagged you application in future submissions. """"""""</p> <p>I searched for this Palava is encountering it in the file TiUIWindowProxy.m.</p> <p>I'm sure this is critical and should be treated with the utmost speed, as<br> means that no application is approved by Apple.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3087,12,"""e.sorce.id undefined""","""""""{html}<div><p>hi. when i try to pull the parameter from a tableview on a click event, i get e.source.id as undefined.<br> pasted below is my sample code.</p> <p>tableView.addEventListener('click', function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info(e.source.ID);</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>i get a error stating source undefined.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: e.sorce.id undefined
Description: """"{html}<div><p>hi. when i try to pull the parameter from a tableview on a click event, i get e.source.id as undefined.<br> pasted below is my sample code.</p> <p>tableView.addEventListener('click', function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info(e.source.ID);</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>i get a error stating source undefined.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3086,12,"""Android: G1/1.6 table view performance issues""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/08/11 17:02 0c5c937) G1/1.6</p> <p>1.Base UI<br> 2.Tap Table views and watch what happens</p> <p>results: its takes 2-3 seconds to load, this used to take about half the time (1.5.1). Feels quite laggy. 2.2 and 2.3 devices are not showing the same lag.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: G1/1.6 table view performance issues
