TIMOB-3063,12,"""Android: Ti.UI.currentWindow not respected on back button click (Android)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi. I'm using Android APIs 2.2 and Titanium 1.5.1.</p>  <p>I'm trying to implement a menu button which fires an event to  the current window (i.e. Window A) on click. This window also  contains a button which opens another modal window (i.e. Window B).  I can only access Window B from Window A.</p>  <p>When I open Window B (the modal window) first, and then hit the  back button to go back to window A, Ti.UI.currentWindow points  towards the modal window, Window B instead of Window A. I fired an  event from the menu button click, and this event was caught by the  modal window instead of the window which I am currently in (after  pressing the back-button).</p>  <p>Here is some code to try out:</p>  <p>app.js: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1535949"""""""">http://pastie.org/1535949</a></p>  <p>winA.js: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1535954"""""""">http://pastie.org/1535954</a></p>  <p>winB.js: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1535956"""""""">http://pastie.org/1535956</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.UI.currentWindow not respected on back button click (Android)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi. I'm using Android APIs 2.2 and Titanium 1.5.1.</p> <p>I'm trying to implement a menu button which fires an event to the current window (i.e. Window A) on click. This window also contains a button which opens another modal window (i.e. Window B). I can only access Window B from Window A.</p> <p>When I open Window B (the modal window) first, and then hit the back button to go back to window A, Ti.UI.currentWindow points towards the modal window, Window B instead of Window A. I fired an event from the menu button click, and this event was caught by the modal window instead of the window which I am currently in (after pressing the back-button).</p> <p>Here is some code to try out:</p> <p>app.js: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1535949"""""""">http://pastie.org/1535949</a></p> <p>winA.js: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1535954"""""""">http://pastie.org/1535954</a></p> <p>winB.js: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1535956"""""""">http://pastie.org/1535956</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3062,12,"""JSON.parse changes order of data""","""""""{html}<div><p>I am using Mobile SDK 1.5.1 and when I recieve JSON from my server, I can see its in a particular order.<br> These are reverse order timestamp posts from a phpBB forum.</p> <p>When I JSON.parse the response I get them in a different order on both Android and iOS.<br> If I run eval the results are in the correct original order.</p> <p>I can see with Ti.API.info that the app is getting the original JSON in the correct order.</p> <p>Heres how the JSON looks:</p> <pre> <code>{ """"""""3"""""""":{ """"""""isUnread"""""""":"""""""""""""""", """"""""title"""""""":""""""""Games"""""""", """"""""replies"""""""":""""""""1987"""""""", """"""""startedBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPostTime"""""""":""""""""Mon Oct 04, 2010 8:39 pm"""""""", """"""""lastPostBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPosterUID"""""""":""""""""4"""""""" }, """"""""5"""""""":{ """"""""isUnread"""""""":"""""""""""""""", """"""""title"""""""":""""""""General"""""""", """"""""replies"""""""":""""""""2689"""""""", """"""""startedBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPostTime"""""""":""""""""Mon Oct 04, 2010 8:38 pm"""""""", """"""""lastPostBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPosterUID"""""""":""""""""4"""""""" },  """"""""163"""""""":{ """"""""isUnread"""""""":"""""""""""""""", """"""""title"""""""":""""""""Europeland"""""""", """"""""replies"""""""":""""""""313"""""""", """"""""startedBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPostTime"""""""":""""""""Mon Oct 04, 2010 8:00 pm"""""""", """"""""lastPostBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPosterUID"""""""":""""""""2"""""""" }, """"""""END"""""""":""""""""END"""""""" }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: JSON.parse changes order of data
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I am using Mobile SDK 1.5.1 and when I recieve JSON from my server, I can see its in a particular order.<br> These are reverse order timestamp posts from a phpBB forum.</p> <p>When I JSON.parse the response I get them in a different order on both Android and iOS.<br> If I run eval the results are in the correct original order.</p> <p>I can see with Ti.API.info that the app is getting the original JSON in the correct order.</p> <p>Heres how the JSON looks:</p> <pre> <code>{ """"""""3"""""""":{ """"""""isUnread"""""""":"""""""""""""""", """"""""title"""""""":""""""""Games"""""""", """"""""replies"""""""":""""""""1987"""""""", """"""""startedBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPostTime"""""""":""""""""Mon Oct 04, 2010 8:39 pm"""""""", """"""""lastPostBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPosterUID"""""""":""""""""4"""""""" }, """"""""5"""""""":{ """"""""isUnread"""""""":"""""""""""""""", """"""""title"""""""":""""""""General"""""""", """"""""replies"""""""":""""""""2689"""""""", """"""""startedBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPostTime"""""""":""""""""Mon Oct 04, 2010 8:38 pm"""""""", """"""""lastPostBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPosterUID"""""""":""""""""4"""""""" }, """"""""163"""""""":{ """"""""isUnread"""""""":"""""""""""""""", """"""""title"""""""":""""""""Europeland"""""""", """"""""replies"""""""":""""""""313"""""""", """"""""startedBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPostTime"""""""":""""""""Mon Oct 04, 2010 8:00 pm"""""""", """"""""lastPostBy"""""""":""""""""User"""""""", """"""""lastPosterUID"""""""":""""""""2"""""""" }, """"""""END"""""""":""""""""END"""""""" }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3059,12,"""iOS replacing the No Results from a searchable tableview""","""""""{html}<div><p>Feature Request:</p>  <p>When searching a tableview, if there are no matches, the  tableview is replaced with an empty tableview and """"""""No Results""""""""  appears on the second row. This is expected behavior. It would be  nice if the we could decide wether to show the """"""""No Results""""""""  tableview or a customized row instead in which we can add, for  example, a button or label where the user can click to make  something else happen (like calling the server to look for more  results). Basically, imitating the native mail app.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS replacing the No Results from a searchable tableview
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Feature Request:</p> <p>When searching a tableview, if there are no matches, the tableview is replaced with an empty tableview and """"""""No Results"""""""" appears on the second row. This is expected behavior. It would be nice if the we could decide wether to show the """"""""No Results"""""""" tableview or a customized row instead in which we can add, for example, a button or label where the user can click to make something else happen (like calling the server to look for more results). Basically, imitating the native mail app.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3058,12,"""Android: If heavyweight window's JS code immediately opens a lightweight window, lightweight window is never seen""","""""""{html}<div><p>The fail case is the KS -&gt; Controls -&gt; Slider -&gt; Min/Max Range test. When you run it, you only see a black window.</p> <p>It's a very strangely written test, and I'm pretty sure it's actually a mistake (the way it's written). (Nevertheless, it should -- and did -- work.)</p> <p>It's strange because when you tap the row to start the test, it opens a new window (as do basically all of our KS tests) using tabgroup.open(win) (thus that new window is heavy). That window has its own url property. And in the JS of that URL, a second window (light) is created and opened in order to display the test. (This second window is obviously totally unnecessary, but anyway...)</p> <p>The reason we see a blank window is because it's the heavy window that is showing. (The JS for the heavy window does not contain any code that puts a view on the window.) The lightweight window never gets seen. And we can see why in this screen shot of some logcat output that I've annotated:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://skitch.com/<USER>rpdeu/projects-grep-137x29"""""""">https://skitch.com/<USER>rpdeu/projects-grep-137x29</a></p> <p>So when the lightweight window starts opening, the heavyweight window hasn't finished opening yet (obviously, since part of the code running when the heavyweight window opens is to open the lightweight window.) And when a lightweight window is created (constructor of <code>TiUIWindow</code>), it immediately runs through <code>handleWindowCreated</code> and <code>handleBooted</code>, thus putting out its layout right away. Meanwhile the heavyweight window has to wait until its <code>handleBooted</code> gets called. When it does, the heavyweight window puts <strong>its</strong> layout on the activity, thus hiding the lightweight window's layout.</p> <p>So the test is bizarre and probably should be changed. But the use case of having a heavy open a light immediately is perhaps valid. Like maybe the heavy's code checks some condition and if it exists they want to popup a light window for a second to display an elaborate message with an OK button that closes the light so its re-shows the heavy.</p> <p>'N' stuff, and yeah but no but yeah but no.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: If heavyweight window's JS code immediately opens a lightweight window, lightweight window is never seen
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The fail case is the KS -&gt; Controls -&gt; Slider -&gt; Min/Max Range test. When you run it, you only see a black window.</p> <p>It's a very strangely written test, and I'm pretty sure it's actually a mistake (the way it's written). (Nevertheless, it should -- and did -- work.)</p> <p>It's strange because when you tap the row to start the test, it opens a new window (as do basically all of our KS tests) using tabgroup.open(win) (thus that new window is heavy). That window has its own url property. And in the JS of that URL, a second window (light) is created and opened in order to display the test. (This second window is obviously totally unnecessary, but anyway...)</p> <p>The reason we see a blank window is because it's the heavy window that is showing. (The JS for the heavy window does not contain any code that puts a view on the window.) The lightweight window never gets seen. And we can see why in this screen shot of some logcat output that I've annotated:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://skitch.com/<USER>rpdeu/projects-grep-137x29"""""""">https://skitch.com/<USER>rpdeu/projects-grep-137x29</a></p> <p>So when the lightweight window starts opening, the heavyweight window hasn't finished opening yet (obviously, since part of the code running when the heavyweight window opens is to open the lightweight window.) And when a lightweight window is created (constructor of <code>TiUIWindow</code>), it immediately runs through <code>handleWindowCreated</code> and <code>handleBooted</code>, thus putting out its layout right away. Meanwhile the heavyweight window has to wait until its <code>handleBooted</code> gets called. When it does, the heavyweight window puts <strong>its</strong> layout on the activity, thus hiding the lightweight window's layout.</p> <p>So the test is bizarre and probably should be changed. But the use case of having a heavy open a light immediately is perhaps valid. Like maybe the heavy's code checks some condition and if it exists they want to popup a light window for a second to display an elaborate message with an OK button that closes the light so its re-shows the heavy.</p> <p>'N' stuff, and yeah but no but yeah but no.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3057,12,"""Android 1.6 : Win not response to focus event""","""""""{html}<div><p>It was working fine on 1.6.0-20110202152401 but most current built (1.6.0-20110204150802) killed it.</p> <p>win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>win.addEventListener('focus',function(e){<br> Ti.API.info('focused')<br> });</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android 1.6 : Win not response to focus event
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It was working fine on 1.6.0-20110202152401 but most current built (1.6.0-20110204150802) killed it.</p> <p>win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>win.addEventListener('focus',function(e){<br> Ti.API.info('focused')<br> });</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3056,12,"""Android: Crash when ImageViews can't get their parent width""","""""""{html}<div><p>The KS Views &gt; Image View &gt; Image View Scaling test crashes when it tries to get the parent window size before it's finished showing</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Crash when ImageViews can't get their parent width
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The KS Views &gt; Image View &gt; Image View Scaling test crashes when it tries to get the parent window size before it's finished showing</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3055,12,"""iOS app crashes when video is finished if playbackState listener is attached""","""""""{html}<div><p>Please use the code provided on HD ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70041#c335911"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70041#c335911</a></p> <p>If the following lines are removed, not a problem, but with them on it, the app will crash after the movie is over</p> <pre> <code>activeMovie.addEventListener('playbackState',function(e){     Ti.API.info('Event PlaybackState Fired: '+e.playbackState);     Ti.API.info('activeMovie.endPlaybackTime: '+activeMovie.endPlaybackTime);     Ti.API.info('activeMovie.playableDuration: '+activeMovie.playableDuration); });</code> </pre> <p>Tested on iPhone Simulator 4.2<br> Ti SDK 1.6 (Feb 3 2011 22:28 r0f017b3a)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS app crashes when video is finished if playbackState listener is attached
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Please use the code provided on HD ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70041#c335911"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70041#c335911</a></p> <p>If the following lines are removed, not a problem, but with them on it, the app will crash after the movie is over</p> <pre> <code>activeMovie.addEventListener('playbackState',function(e){ Ti.API.info('Event PlaybackState Fired: '+e.playbackState); Ti.API.info('activeMovie.endPlaybackTime: '+activeMovie.endPlaybackTime); Ti.API.info('activeMovie.playableDuration: '+activeMovie.playableDuration); });</code> </pre> <p>Tested on iPhone Simulator 4.2<br> Ti SDK 1.6 (Feb 3 2011 22:28 r0f017b3a)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3054,12,"""Android - 1.6 only""","""""""{html}<div><p>G1 (1.6) not seeing this on the newer device running 2.2 + <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/04/11 10:00 7bb9911)</p> <p>1.install KS using noted build on a G1<br> 2.tap on a list view item and watch what occurs</p> <p>results: the list itens take the initial focus state, and does nothing for a second, changes to down state and then finally loads the the next window. This takes 2-3 seconds, when 1.5.1 is used the load happens almost instantly (even if the resulting window takes a second to load).</p> <p>very noticeable regression from 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - 1.6 only
Description: """"{html}<div><p>G1 (1.6) not seeing this on the newer device running 2.2 + <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/04/11 10:00 7bb9911)</p> <p>1.install KS using noted build on a G1<br> 2.tap on a list view item and watch what occurs</p> <p>results: the list itens take the initial focus state, and does nothing for a second, changes to down state and then finally loads the the next window. This takes 2-3 seconds, when 1.5.1 is used the load happens almost instantly (even if the resulting window takes a second to load).</p> <p>very noticeable regression from 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3053,12,"""Android: showCamera executes immediately (before parent activity is finished drawing)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Caused by lifecycle refactor. We might just need to post showCamera on to the UI thread directly instead of processing it in our loop iteration. The result in the KS Camera Basic test is a deadlock or exception showing the image after the photo has been taken.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: showCamera executes immediately (before parent activity is finished drawing)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Caused by lifecycle refactor. We might just need to post showCamera on to the UI thread directly instead of processing it in our loop iteration. The result in the KS Camera Basic test is a deadlock or exception showing the image after the photo has been taken.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3052,12,"""Android: Ti.Filesystem.File.write should return boolean""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>On iOS, the """"""""write"""""""" function on a Ti.Filesystem.File returns true or false depending on if the write was successful, or false if it's not possible to write to the file or blob. Android doesn't return anything.</p> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var file = Titanium.Filesystem.createTempFile(); if (file.write('my super cool data') === true) {    alert('PASS: I wrote to a file! YESSS!'); } else {    alert('FAIL: I am sad, for I could not tell you I wrote to the file. Weep weep weep.'); }</code> </pre> <h1>Tested On</h1> <p>Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/02/11 15:22 a02f7db...)<br> PASSES on iOS Simulator 4.2<br> FAILS on Android Simulator 2.2</p> <h1>Related Documentation</h1> <p>The docs already state that """"""""write"""""""" returns a boolean, most likely because that's what iOS does.<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Filesystem.File.write-method.html""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Fil...</a></p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70481"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70481</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Ti.Filesystem.File.write should return boolean
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>On iOS, the """"""""write"""""""" function on a Ti.Filesystem.File returns true or false depending on if the write was successful, or false if it's not possible to write to the file or blob. Android doesn't return anything.</p> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var file = Titanium.Filesystem.createTempFile(); if (file.write('my super cool data') === true) { alert('PASS: I wrote to a file! YESSS!'); } else { alert('FAIL: I am sad, for I could not tell you I wrote to the file. Weep weep weep.'); }</code> </pre> <h1>Tested On</h1> <p>Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (02/02/11 15:22 a02f7db...)<br> PASSES on iOS Simulator 4.2<br> FAILS on Android Simulator 2.2</p> <h1>Related Documentation</h1> <p>The docs already state that """"""""write"""""""" returns a boolean, most likely because that's what iOS does.<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Filesystem.File.write-method.html""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Fil...</a></p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70481"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/70481</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3051,12,"""Android: Requesting battery state hangs up the app""","""""""{html}<div><p>See the KS Platform &gt; Platform Data tests. It hangs while waiting for batteryState / batteryLevel.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Requesting battery state hangs up the app
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See the KS Platform &gt; Platform Data tests. It hangs while waiting for batteryState / batteryLevel.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3050,12,"""iOS: bug in typecasting of big integers from the database""","""""""I just discovered a bug in the database code, in that it does not properly typecast big integers coming from the database.    Running this code:    {code:title=app.js}  var db = Titanium.Database.open('bigint_test');  db.execute(""""""""DROP TABLE `test`"""""""")  db.execute(""""""""CREATE TABLE `test` (`val1` BIGINT, `val2` BIGINT)"""""""");  db.execute(""""""""DELETE FROM `test`"""""""");  db.execute(""""""""INSERT INTO test (val1, val2) VALUES (1, 1296802544867)"""""""");     Titanium.API.info(1296802544867);  Titanium.API.info(db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM `test`"""""""").field(0));  Titanium.API.info(db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM `test`"""""""").field(1));    var table_info = db.execute(""""""""PRAGMA table_info(test)"""""""")  for (var i=0; i &lt; table_info.fieldCount(); i++) {    Titanium.API.info(table_info.fieldName(i) + """""""": """""""" + table_info.field(i));  };    [INFO] 1296802544867  [INFO] 1  [INFO] -277578525  [INFO] cid: 0  [INFO] name: val1  [INFO] type: BIGINT  [INFO] notnull: 0  [INFO] dflt_value: null  [INFO] pk: 0  {code}      So you can see that the last log line is wrong it should be 1296802544867.    Looking at the .sql file from the iPhone Simulator, I can tell you that the right value is stored in the db, and that other sqlite clients give the right value back.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: bug in typecasting of big integers from the database
Description: """"I just discovered a bug in the database code, in that it does not properly typecast big integers coming from the database. Running this code: {code:title=app.js} var db = Titanium.Database.open('bigint_test'); db.execute(""""""""DROP TABLE `test`"""""""") db.execute(""""""""CREATE TABLE `test` (`val1` BIGINT, `val2` BIGINT)""""""""); db.execute(""""""""DELETE FROM `test`""""""""); db.execute(""""""""INSERT INTO test (val1, val2) VALUES (1, 1296802544867)""""""""); Titanium.API.info(1296802544867); Titanium.API.info(db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM `test`"""""""").field(0)); Titanium.API.info(db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM `test`"""""""").field(1)); var table_info = db.execute(""""""""PRAGMA table_info(test)"""""""") for (var i=0; i &lt; table_info.fieldCount(); i++) { Titanium.API.info(table_info.fieldName(i) + """""""": """""""" + table_info.field(i)); }; [INFO] 1296802544867 [INFO] 1 [INFO] -277578525 [INFO] cid: 0 [INFO] name: val1 [INFO] type: BIGINT [INFO] notnull: 0 [INFO] dflt_value: null [INFO] pk: 0 {code} So you can see that the last log line is wrong it should be 1296802544867. Looking at the .sql file from the iPhone Simulator, I can tell you that the right value is stored in the db, and that other sqlite clients give the right value back. """"",title+description
TIMOB-3049,12,"""APIDOC: Ti.UI.createSound in an example, instead of Ti.Media""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>The example at the bottom of the docs for the Ti.Media.Sound object calls """"""""Ti.UI.createSound"""""""", when it should be, """"""""Ti.Media.createSound"""""""" (UI, instead of Media).</p> <h1>Link to Affected Page</h1> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.Sound-object""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Med...</a></p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/71041"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/71041</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: APIDOC: Ti.UI.createSound in an example, instead of Ti.Media
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>The example at the bottom of the docs for the Ti.Media.Sound object calls """"""""Ti.UI.createSound"""""""", when it should be, """"""""Ti.Media.createSound"""""""" (UI, instead of Media).</p> <h1>Link to Affected Page</h1> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Media.Sound-object""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Med...</a></p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/71041"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/71041</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
