TIMOB-3004,12,"""Android: Remote images in tableview cause performance issues while scrolling""","""""""{html}<div><p>I tested the lighthouse ticket here - <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1508-android-remote-images-in-imageview-get-reloaded-inside-a-tableviewrow""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1508-...</a> - with the latest build from today on my Galaxy (Android 2.2). The images now show up but the table performance while scrolling is odd.</p> <p>Using the KS RSS XML example: You'll see the images there but when scrolling it jitter-scrolls down slowly and then rapidly scrolls to the end as if it's catching up to where it is supposed to be. Sometimes doing a slow scroll it will stay in place or jump to where it should be, making it look like a scroll didn't happen.<br> I'm debugging an HD ticket that is having the issue as well. I'll get specifics from him on how his table is performing. <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67491"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67491</a></p> <p>Tested - Android 2.2 Galaxy, Ti 1.6 CI</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Remote images in tableview cause performance issues while scrolling
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I tested the lighthouse ticket here - <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1508-android-remote-images-in-imageview-get-reloaded-inside-a-tableviewrow""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1508-...</a> - with the latest build from today on my Galaxy (Android 2.2). The images now show up but the table performance while scrolling is odd.</p> <p>Using the KS RSS XML example: You'll see the images there but when scrolling it jitter-scrolls down slowly and then rapidly scrolls to the end as if it's catching up to where it is supposed to be. Sometimes doing a slow scroll it will stay in place or jump to where it should be, making it look like a scroll didn't happen.<br> I'm debugging an HD ticket that is having the issue as well. I'll get specifics from him on how his table is performing. <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67491"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67491</a></p> <p>Tested - Android 2.2 Galaxy, Ti 1.6 CI</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3003,12,"""iOS: Problems with Grouped TableView""","""""""{html}<div><p>if I open a window with inside a tableview with  <em>transparent</em> background, will be fine the first time I open  that window, but then if I open it again I will see an empty  tableview in the background.</p>  <p>Project type <strong>iPad</strong><br>  iOS SDK <strong>4.2</strong><br>  Titanium SDK <strong>1.6.0</strong><br>  Titanium Developer <strong>1.2.2</strong></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Problems with Grouped TableView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>if I open a window with inside a tableview with <em>transparent</em> background, will be fine the first time I open that window, but then if I open it again I will see an empty tableview in the background.</p> <p>Project type <strong>iPad</strong><br> iOS SDK <strong>4.2</strong><br> Titanium SDK <strong>1.6.0</strong><br> Titanium Developer <strong>1.2.2</strong></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3002,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.createLabel with text set as value of 0.07 gives 0.07000000000001""","""""""{html}<div><pre>  <code>currentValue = 0.07;                var currentReadingValueLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({                  text: currentValue,                  left: 110,                  top: 22,                  height: 'auto',                  color: '#fff',                  width: 150,                  textAlign: 'left',                  font:{                      fontSize: 24,                      fontStyle: 'bold'                  }              });</code>  </pre>  <p>When displayed in both the iphone simulator and on the device  (iPhone 3GS, iOS 4.1) I don't get just 0.07 but something like  0.07000000000001. Using Dev 1.2.2 with iOS SDK 4.2 and Titanium  Mobile 1.5.1 (latest).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.createLabel with text set as value of 0.07 gives 0.07000000000001
Description: """"{html}<div><pre> <code>currentValue = 0.07; var currentReadingValueLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: currentValue, left: 110, top: 22, height: 'auto', color: '#fff', width: 150, textAlign: 'left', font:{ fontSize: 24, fontStyle: 'bold' } });</code> </pre> <p>When displayed in both the iphone simulator and on the device (iPhone 3GS, iOS 4.1) I don't get just 0.07 but something like 0.07000000000001. Using Dev 1.2.2 with iOS SDK 4.2 and Titanium Mobile 1.5.1 (latest).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-3001,12,"""Request: Move i18n into Resources folder""","""""""{html}<div><p>Feature request - please move the i18n folder within Resources. This will make it easier to manage version control with SVN/etc. I could then version control the Resources folder for a project and know I'd be grabbing all the files needed to re-create the project or a development stage.</p> <p>I don't use version control on the PROJECT folder because build folder is dynamic and I don't want to waste repository space for it.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Request: Move i18n into Resources folder
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Feature request - please move the i18n folder within Resources. This will make it easier to manage version control with SVN/etc. I could then version control the Resources folder for a project and know I'd be grabbing all the files needed to re-create the project or a development stage.</p> <p>I don't use version control on the PROJECT folder because build folder is dynamic and I don't want to waste repository space for it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2999,12,"""iOS: XCode Project Settings and Base SDK""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Feature</h1>  <p>Customer wants to be able to specify a custom Base SDK in a  Titanium file, and have it influence the generated XCode project.  Also, future customers may want control of other XCode Project  Settings.</p>  <h1>Proposed Solution</h1>  <p>Added additional elements to the iphone element in the tiapp.xml  to allow the user to customize the XCode Project Settings. The  relevant Titanium scripts would take these into account when  generating an XCode project.</p>  <h1>What Properties Need To Be Exposed</h1>  <p>I will ask the customer to comment on the specific properties  they would like exposed.</p>  <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68641"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68641</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: XCode Project Settings and Base SDK
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Feature</h1> <p>Customer wants to be able to specify a custom Base SDK in a Titanium file, and have it influence the generated XCode project. Also, future customers may want control of other XCode Project Settings.</p> <h1>Proposed Solution</h1> <p>Added additional elements to the iphone element in the tiapp.xml to allow the user to customize the XCode Project Settings. The relevant Titanium scripts would take these into account when generating an XCode project.</p> <h1>What Properties Need To Be Exposed</h1> <p>I will ask the customer to comment on the specific properties they would like exposed.</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68641"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68641</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2998,12,"""iOS: ScrollableView continues to play video""","""""""{html}<div><p>While manually managing the views array in a scrollableView I  can successfully remove a video player view but the video / audio  continues to play. Here's a code example.</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1515560"""""""">http://pastie.org/1515560</a></p>  <p>Related HD ticket (that expands much broader than just this one  issue): <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64751"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64751</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollableView continues to play video
Description: """"{html}<div><p>While manually managing the views array in a scrollableView I can successfully remove a video player view but the video / audio continues to play. Here's a code example.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1515560"""""""">http://pastie.org/1515560</a></p> <p>Related HD ticket (that expands much broader than just this one issue): <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64751"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64751</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2997,12,"""iphone crash when creating a new contact group while exchange is enabled""","""""""{html}<div><p>It can be reproduced by having an exchange account, like Google, and enabling contact-sync. Under this condition, var testGroup = Titanium.Contacts.createGroup() crashes the application.<br> Tested for 1.5.1 and 1.5.0 with SDK 4.2.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iphone crash when creating a new contact group while exchange is enabled
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It can be reproduced by having an exchange account, like Google, and enabling contact-sync. Under this condition, var testGroup = Titanium.Contacts.createGroup() crashes the application.<br> Tested for 1.5.1 and 1.5.0 with SDK 4.2.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2996,12,"""Android: Some AVD properties aren't separated by newline""","""""""{html}<div><p>When we create an AVD it looks like some of the properties in it's config.ini aren't separated by newlines (hw.gps, hw.camera, etc)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Some AVD properties aren't separated by newline
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When we create an AVD it looks like some of the properties in it's config.ini aren't separated by newlines (hw.gps, hw.camera, etc)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2995,12,"""webview link doesn't click""","""""""{html}<div><p>I've found a bug with the webview module for titanium mobile. If a website loaded through the url property contains an html link such as</p> <pre> <code>&lt;a href=""""""""test.html""""""""&gt;Test Link&lt;/a&gt;</code> </pre> <p>nothing happens when this link is clicked. If the link is changed to container an absolute url, it works just fine:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;a href=""""""""/test.html""""""""&gt;Test Link&lt;/a&gt;</code> </pre> <p>OR</p> <pre> <code>&lt;a href=""""""""http://www.somewebsite.com/test.html""""""""&gt;Test Link&lt;/a&gt;</code> </pre> <p>If I load this html through the html property it clicks just fine.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: webview link doesn't click
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I've found a bug with the webview module for titanium mobile. If a website loaded through the url property contains an html link such as</p> <pre> <code>&lt;a href=""""""""test.html""""""""&gt;Test Link&lt;/a&gt;</code> </pre> <p>nothing happens when this link is clicked. If the link is changed to container an absolute url, it works just fine:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;a href=""""""""/test.html""""""""&gt;Test Link&lt;/a&gt;</code> </pre> <p>OR</p> <pre> <code>&lt;a href=""""""""http://www.somewebsite.com/test.html""""""""&gt;Test Link&lt;/a&gt;</code> </pre> <p>If I load this html through the html property it clicks just fine.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2994,12,"""iOS: Add label to Ti:UI.DashboardItem""","""""""{html}<div><p>Please allow a text label to be specified in the  Titanium.UI.createDashboardItem() function. Forcing the developer  to create the label in the image is horrible for localization.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add label to Ti:UI.DashboardItem
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Please allow a text label to be specified in the Titanium.UI.createDashboardItem() function. Forcing the developer to create the label in the image is horrible for localization.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2993,12,"""Android Bug:  Search TextField produces duplicate RETURN events""","""""""{html}<div><p>Reference Ticket: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69271"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69271</a></p>  <p>Test Code:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>var mywin = Ti.UI.createWindow();<br>  <br>      <br>  var tf1 = Ti.UI.createTextField({<br>  <br>      </code>  </pre>  <pre>  <code><code>top: 50,  left: 10,   height: 35,   width: 250,  returnKeyType: Ti.UI.RETURNKEY_SEARCH,  //causes duplicate (2) 'return' interrupts in Android  font: {fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue'},  backgroundColor:'white'</code></code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  });    <br>  var tf2 = Ti.UI.createTextField({    </pre>  <pre>  <code>top: 100, left: 10, height: 35, width: 250,  font: {fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue'},  backgroundColor:'white' });</code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  tf1.addEventListener('return', function(e) {    </pre>  <pre>  <code>Ti.API.info('RETURN: src=' + e.source + ', type=' + e.type);</code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  });  tf2.addEventListener('return', function(e) {    </pre>  <pre>  <code>Ti.API.info('RETURN: src=' + e.source + ', type=' + e.type);</code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  });  mywin.add(tf1);  mywin.add(tf2);    <br>  mywin.open();  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Bug: Search TextField produces duplicate RETURN events
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Reference Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69271"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/69271</a></p> <p>Test Code:<br></p> <pre> <code>var mywin = Ti.UI.createWindow();<br> <br> <br> var tf1 = Ti.UI.createTextField({<br> <br> </code> </pre> <pre> <code><code>top: 50, left: 10, height: 35, width: 250, returnKeyType: Ti.UI.RETURNKEY_SEARCH, //causes duplicate (2) 'return' interrupts in Android font: {fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue'}, backgroundColor:'white'</code></code> </pre> <pre> <br> }); <br> var tf2 = Ti.UI.createTextField({ </pre> <pre> <code>top: 100, left: 10, height: 35, width: 250, font: {fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue'}, backgroundColor:'white' });</code> </pre> <pre> <br> tf1.addEventListener('return', function(e) { </pre> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info('RETURN: src=' + e.source + ', type=' + e.type);</code> </pre> <pre> <br> }); tf2.addEventListener('return', function(e) { </pre> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info('RETURN: src=' + e.source + ', type=' + e.type);</code> </pre> <pre> <br> }); mywin.add(tf1); mywin.add(tf2); <br> mywin.open(); </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2992,12,"""Android - Labels don't truncate ""","""""""{html}<div><p>If a label has a height set and the text does not fit, it is cut off without the three ellipsis dots.<br> Example:<br></p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'#ccc'}); var commentLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({   color:'#000',   backgroundColor:'#999',   font:{fontSize:18, fontFamily:'Arial'},   left:5,   top:20,   height:18,   width:300,   text:'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Fusce mollis vestibulum dapibus. Donec dapibus blandit nisi sagittis molestie. Nulla facilisi. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus. Donec id enim at arcu suscipit dapibus',   ellipsize: true,   minimumFontSize: 10 }); win.add(commentLabel); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>This behavior is also seen in the Kitchen Sink. Controls -&gt; Label -&gt; Basic. Blue text is cut off at the bottom.</p> <p>Android SDK = APIs 2.2, Screen = HVGA<br> Ti SDK 1.6 (Jan 27 2011 18:59 re46f49ac)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - Labels don't truncate
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If a label has a height set and the text does not fit, it is cut off without the three ellipsis dots.<br> Example:<br></p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'#ccc'}); var commentLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color:'#000', backgroundColor:'#999', font:{fontSize:18, fontFamily:'Arial'}, left:5, top:20, height:18, width:300, text:'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Fusce mollis vestibulum dapibus. Donec dapibus blandit nisi sagittis molestie. Nulla facilisi. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus. Donec id enim at arcu suscipit dapibus', ellipsize: true, minimumFontSize: 10 }); win.add(commentLabel); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>This behavior is also seen in the Kitchen Sink. Controls -&gt; Label -&gt; Basic. Blue text is cut off at the bottom.</p> <p>Android SDK = APIs 2.2, Screen = HVGA<br> Ti SDK 1.6 (Jan 27 2011 18:59 re46f49ac)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2991,12,"""iOS Bug:  ScrollView can't carry 2 tableviews""","""""""{html}<div><p>If a user has 2 tableViews that they want to scroll through as a Grouped tables, one and then the other. Scrollview either does not scroll, or puts one table on top of the other.</p> <p>Ticket Reference: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68531"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68531</a></p> <p>Test Code:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var view = Ti.UI.createView({}); var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({   contentHeight:'auto',   contentWidth:'auto',    top:0,    opacity:0.5 });  var table1 = Ti.UI.createTableView({   style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED,    top:0   }); var table2 = Ti.UI.createTableView({   style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED,    top:0   });  var count = 20; var data = [];  for (var c=0;c&lt;count;c++) {   var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:""""""""Row """"""""+(c+1)});   data[c] = row; }  table1.data = data;  var inputData = [   {title:'row 1', header:'Header 1'},   {title:'row 2'},   {title:'row 3'},   {title:'row 4', header:'Header 2'},   {title:'row 5'} ];  table2.data = inputData;  scrollView.add(table2);  scrollView.add(table1);  win.add(scrollView);  win.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Bug: ScrollView can't carry 2 tableviews
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If a user has 2 tableViews that they want to scroll through as a Grouped tables, one and then the other. Scrollview either does not scroll, or puts one table on top of the other.</p> <p>Ticket Reference: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68531"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/68531</a></p> <p>Test Code:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var view = Ti.UI.createView({}); var scrollView = Ti.UI.createScrollView({ contentHeight:'auto', contentWidth:'auto', top:0, opacity:0.5 }); var table1 = Ti.UI.createTableView({ style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED, top:0 }); var table2 = Ti.UI.createTableView({ style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED, top:0 }); var count = 20; var data = []; for (var c=0;c&lt;count;c++) { var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:""""""""Row """"""""+(c+1)}); data[c] = row; } table1.data = data; var inputData = [ {title:'row 1', header:'Header 1'}, {title:'row 2'}, {title:'row 3'}, {title:'row 4', header:'Header 2'}, {title:'row 5'} ]; table2.data = inputData; scrollView.add(table2); scrollView.add(table1); win.add(scrollView); win.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2990,12,"""Android: Window / Activity lifecycle events don't fire""","""""""{html}<div><p>Our current activity lifecycle events aren't being fired for activities created from a heavy weight Ti.UI.Window. JS Activities seem to work because their lifecycle seems to be the right order, specifically:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""java""""""""> // pseudo code public void onCreate() {   createLayout();   initCurrentActivity(this);   runScript();   fireEvent(""""""""create""""""""); }</code> </pre> <p>The heavy weight window lifecycle however looks more like:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""java""""""""> // pseudo code public TiUIWindow() {   startActivity(); } public void onActivityCreated() {   // script isn't even executed until after onCreate()   initCurrentActivity(this);   runScript(); }</code> </pre> <p>This is affecting a lot of our new sensor and sound API refactors that depend on pause/resume to work for correct add/remove event listener behavior.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window / Activity lifecycle events don't fire
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Our current activity lifecycle events aren't being fired for activities created from a heavy weight Ti.UI.Window. JS Activities seem to work because their lifecycle seems to be the right order, specifically:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""java""""""""> // pseudo code public void onCreate() { createLayout(); initCurrentActivity(this); runScript(); fireEvent(""""""""create""""""""); }</code> </pre> <p>The heavy weight window lifecycle however looks more like:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""java""""""""> // pseudo code public TiUIWindow() { startActivity(); } public void onActivityCreated() { // script isn't even executed until after onCreate() initCurrentActivity(this); runScript(); }</code> </pre> <p>This is affecting a lot of our new sensor and sound API refactors that depend on pause/resume to work for correct add/remove event listener behavior.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2989,12,"""iOS: FB module failures 4.0.1-4.2 ""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a).</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2988"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2988"""""""">#2988</a> for 3.1.3 behavior. New to 1.6.0</p> <p>1.log in<br> results: launches browser<br> 2.log in<br> 3.browser says page invalid</p> <p>expected: be able to log in and use module</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: FB module failures 4.0.1-4.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a).</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2988"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2988"""""""">#2988</a> for 3.1.3 behavior. New to 1.6.0</p> <p>1.log in<br> results: launches browser<br> 2.log in<br> 3.browser says page invalid</p> <p>expected: be able to log in and use module</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2988,12,"""iOS: FB module crash on tests - 3.1.3 ""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a) iphone 3, 3.1.3 only.</p> <p>1.Ks &gt; Mashups &gt; Facebook<br> 2.log in<br> 3.do the query test (or any other)</p> <p>results app crashes. crash log attached</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: FB module crash on tests - 3.1.3
