Description: """"{html}<div><p>When using a custom barImage for your navBar, occasionally there is a brief flash that shows an unstyled / default navbar before the custom image appears.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2958,12,"""When leftNavButton used as a back button, navbar transition animation fails""","""""""{html}<div><p>When creating a custom back button with leftNavButton, and calling win.close(), the navBar does not transition as expected. This is the case in the KitchenSink app under window_navbar.js for the """"""""Back button BG"""""""" example.</p> <p>If you test that back button against any other in that example, you'll see that the animation is off.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: When leftNavButton used as a back button, navbar transition animation fails
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When creating a custom back button with leftNavButton, and calling win.close(), the navBar does not transition as expected. This is the case in the KitchenSink app under window_navbar.js for the """"""""Back button BG"""""""" example.</p> <p>If you test that back button against any other in that example, you'll see that the animation is off.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2957,12,"""Android: Expose MODE_WORLD_READABLE""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1>  <p>On the incredible there is no external data storage so when I  wrote a file I need the ability to set the privilege on it so it  can be accessed by another activity not belonging to my app  (Context.MODE_WORLD_READABLE).</p>  <h1>Solution</h1>  <p>Expose MODE_WORLD_READABLE through the Ti.Filesystem module on  Android. I will ask the enterprise client to post more information  on their preference for this exposure.</p>  <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://appc.me/c/NCI-43191-678"""""""">http://appc.me/c/NCI-43191-678</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose MODE_WORLD_READABLE
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>On the incredible there is no external data storage so when I wrote a file I need the ability to set the privilege on it so it can be accessed by another activity not belonging to my app (Context.MODE_WORLD_READABLE).</p> <h1>Solution</h1> <p>Expose MODE_WORLD_READABLE through the Ti.Filesystem module on Android. I will ask the enterprise client to post more information on their preference for this exposure.</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://appc.me/c/NCI-43191-678"""""""">http://appc.me/c/NCI-43191-678</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2956,12,"""Map crashes when clicking twice on annotation""","""""""{html}<div><p>Tested with Kitchen Sink:<br> Base UI =&gt; Views =&gt; Map View</p> <ol> <li>Click on map to deselect the selected pin<br></li> <li>Click on the pin to select it again<br></li> <li>Click on the right arrow of the annotation message<br></li> <li>Crash</li> </ol> <p>Ti SDK 1.6 (Jan 25 2011 17:39 r1ead074f)<br> iPhone Simulator 4.2<br> iPhone 4 running 4.2.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Map crashes when clicking twice on annotation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Tested with Kitchen Sink:<br> Base UI =&gt; Views =&gt; Map View</p> <ol> <li>Click on map to deselect the selected pin<br></li> <li>Click on the pin to select it again<br></li> <li>Click on the right arrow of the annotation message<br></li> <li>Crash</li> </ol> <p>Ti SDK 1.6 (Jan 25 2011 17:39 r1ead074f)<br> iPhone Simulator 4.2<br> iPhone 4 running 4.2.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
