TIMOB-2953,12,"""iOS Feature Request: ImageView validatesSecureCertificate property""","""""""{html}<div><p>Users would like to be able to call remote images with a  self-signed certificate.</p>  <p>Adding a validatesSecureCertificate property to ImageView would  allow that.</p>  <p>Reference Ticket: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67561"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67561</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS Feature Request: ImageView validatesSecureCertificate property
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Users would like to be able to call remote images with a self-signed certificate.</p> <p>Adding a validatesSecureCertificate property to ImageView would allow that.</p> <p>Reference Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67561"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67561</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2952,12,"""Android: backgroundSelectColor on row are not being recognized when a button is present""","""""""{html}<div><p>Tested with 1.6 SDK (Build from today - 1-26). Tested on an  Android device running 2.2</p>  <p>Workaround is to create a view, apply backgroundSelectedColor to  the view, add all row elements to the view. This works fine. It  doesn't work if the button is the immediate child of the row.</p>  <p>Ticket here: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66071#c320941"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66071#c320941</a></p>  <p>Code to reproduce:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">  var mywin = Titanium.UI.createWindow({      title: 'Test',      backgroundColor: '#fff'  });    var mycolls = [];    for (var i = 0; i &lt; 6; ++i) {        var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({          height: 40,          backgroundSelectedColor: '#AA0000'      });        var icost = Ti.UI.createButton({          title: '$20',          top: 18,          right: 10,          width: 60,          height: 20,          font: {              fontSize: 12,              fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue'          }      });      row.add(icost);        mycolls.push(row);  }    var tview = Ti.UI.createTableView({      data: mycolls  });  tview.addEventListener('click',  function(e) {      Ti.API.info('**EVENT**:' + ' index=' + e.index + ', row=' + e.row + ', type=' + e.type +      ', src=' + e.source);  });    mywin.add(tview);    mywin.open();</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: backgroundSelectColor on row are not being recognized when a button is present
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Tested with 1.6 SDK (Build from today - 1-26). Tested on an Android device running 2.2</p> <p>Workaround is to create a view, apply backgroundSelectedColor to the view, add all row elements to the view. This works fine. It doesn't work if the button is the immediate child of the row.</p> <p>Ticket here: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66071#c320941"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/66071#c320941</a></p> <p>Code to reproduce:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var mywin = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Test', backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var mycolls = []; for (var i = 0; i &lt; 6; ++i) { var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ height: 40, backgroundSelectedColor: '#AA0000' }); var icost = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: '$20', top: 18, right: 10, width: 60, height: 20, font: { fontSize: 12, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' } }); row.add(icost); mycolls.push(row); } var tview = Ti.UI.createTableView({ data: mycolls }); tview.addEventListener('click', function(e) { Ti.API.info('**EVENT**:' + ' index=' + e.index + ', row=' + e.row + ', type=' + e.type + ', src=' + e.source); }); mywin.add(tview); mywin.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2950,12,"""Tooling: Add support for platform and default """"version"""" for modules in tiapp.xml""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently there isn't a way for an app to specify what platform(s) a module should be enabled for, and the version number is also a hard requirement. We should allow any of the following methods for defining a module dependency in tiapp.xml:</p> <pre> <code> &lt;!-- the way it works today, use version 0.1 of com.company.module for all platforms--&gt; &lt;module version=""""""""0.1""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt;  &lt;!-- use version 0.1 of com.company.module only for Android --&gt; &lt;module version=""""""""0.1"""""""" platform=""""""""android""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt;  &lt;!-- use the most recently installed version of com.company.module for all platforms --&gt; &lt;module&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt;</code> </pre> <p>We should also allow users to combine the rules above in multiple <code>&lt;module&gt;</code> tags, i.e:</p> <pre> <code> &lt;!-- use com.company.module 1.0 for android, 1.1 for iphone --&gt; &lt;module platform=""""""""android"""""""" version=""""""""1.0""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt; &lt;module platform=""""""""iphone"""""""" version=""""""""1.1""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Tooling: Add support for platform and default """"version"""" for modules in tiapp.xml
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently there isn't a way for an app to specify what platform(s) a module should be enabled for, and the version number is also a hard requirement. We should allow any of the following methods for defining a module dependency in tiapp.xml:</p> <pre> <code> &lt;!-- the way it works today, use version 0.1 of com.company.module for all platforms--&gt; &lt;module version=""""""""0.1""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt; &lt;!-- use version 0.1 of com.company.module only for Android --&gt; &lt;module version=""""""""0.1"""""""" platform=""""""""android""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt; &lt;!-- use the most recently installed version of com.company.module for all platforms --&gt; &lt;module&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt;</code> </pre> <p>We should also allow users to combine the rules above in multiple <code>&lt;module&gt;</code> tags, i.e:</p> <pre> <code> &lt;!-- use com.company.module 1.0 for android, 1.1 for iphone --&gt; &lt;module platform=""""""""android"""""""" version=""""""""1.0""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt; &lt;module platform=""""""""iphone"""""""" version=""""""""1.1""""""""&gt;com.company.module&lt;/module&gt;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2949,12,"""createImageView within tableview causes crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>I wanted to add an icon flush left in my tableviewrows. I replicated the kitchen sink remote images example exactly.</p> <p>This works fine in 1.5.1 but when I upgraded to the nightly build 1.6.0-20110125173952-osx and also 1.6.0-20110125194352-osx I crashes immediately. I tried setting a unique className for each row but that didnt solve the problem. Reverting back to 1.5.1 and all works well again.</p> <p>Hope this helps.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: createImageView within tableview causes crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I wanted to add an icon flush left in my tableviewrows. I replicated the kitchen sink remote images example exactly.</p> <p>This works fine in 1.5.1 but when I upgraded to the nightly build 1.6.0-20110125173952-osx and also 1.6.0-20110125194352-osx I crashes immediately. I tried setting a unique className for each row but that didnt solve the problem. Reverting back to 1.5.1 and all works well again.</p> <p>Hope this helps.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2948,12,"""Ipad emulator won't launch  - errors out on 3.2 and launches iPhone emulator on 4.0-4.2""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a)</p> <p>1.create or have an ipad project<br> 2.attempt to launch in emulator</p> <p>results: with 3.2 selected, errors out, with 4.0-4.2 launches iphone sim and errors out</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ipad emulator won't launch - errors out on 3.2 and launches iPhone emulator on 4.0-4.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a)</p> <p>1.create or have an ipad project<br> 2.attempt to launch in emulator</p> <p>results: with 3.2 selected, errors out, with 4.0-4.2 launches iphone sim and errors out</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2946,12,"""DashboardView breaks after stopEditing() while moving items""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a DashboardView with some DashboardItems. I would like to prevent moving the items. I tried to add an eventListener:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">dashboard.addEventListener('edit', function(e){   e.source.stopEditing(); });</code> </pre> This code leaves the Dashboard in an inconsistent state (see attachment). <p>I'm using Apple SDK 4.2 with Titanium SDK 1.5.1.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: DashboardView breaks after stopEditing() while moving items
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have a DashboardView with some DashboardItems. I would like to prevent moving the items. I tried to add an eventListener:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">dashboard.addEventListener('edit', function(e){ e.source.stopEditing(); });</code> </pre> This code leaves the Dashboard in an inconsistent state (see attachment). <p>I'm using Apple SDK 4.2 with Titanium SDK 1.5.1.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2945,12,"""Android: Database - ResultSet.fieldCount property should be ResultSet.fieldCount() method""","""""""The APIDOCs at [Titanium.Database.ResultSet|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Database.ResultSet-object.html] state that [fieldCount|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Database.ResultSet.fieldCount-method.html] is a method. While this exists on iOS, Android provides it as a property.    Hence, this is a request to remove the property on Android and to replace it with a method.    See the following testcase provided by Ketan:    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  /**   * Initializes the test environment, creating a simple table """"""""data"""""""" that has 150   * rows in it and just 2 fields   */  var testRowCount = 150;  var db = Ti.Database.open('data');  db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS data (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, val TEXT)');  db.execute('DELETE FROM data WHERE 1=1');  for (var i = 1; i <= testRowCount; i++) {      db.execute('INSERT INTO data (val) VALUES(?)','our value:' + i);  }    /**   * FIELD COUNT WORKS AS A METHOD AS EXPECTED ON IOS BUT RETURNS ERROR ON ANDROID.   * EXPECTED RESULT: 2   *   * REAL BEHAVIOR IN 1.8.3: ANDROID SAYS: Uncaught TypeError: Property 'fieldCount' of object #<TiResultSet> is not a function   */  function testFieldCountCrashesOnAndroid() {      // now select out our data from the database      var rows = db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM data"""""""");      var fieldCount = rows.fieldCount();      Ti.API.info('*** SHOULD WORK ON BOTH iOS & ANDROID ***');      Ti.API.info('rows.fieldCount() = ' + fieldCount);  }    testFieldCountCrashesOnAndroid();    /**   * FIELD COUNT WORKS AS A METHOD AS EXPECTED ON IOS BUT RETURNS ERROR ON ANDROID. You will need to comment out line 27 above to test it working on android.   * EXPECTED RESULT: 2   *    * REAL BEHAVIOR IN 1.8.0.1 RC3: iOS only sees the result set object and no longer gets the field count value, although android now returns the value 2.   */  function testFieldCountWorksOnAndroid() {      // now select out our data from the database      var rows = db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM data"""""""");      var fieldCount = rows.fieldCount; // Changed to a property not a method call.      Ti.API.info('*** NOW WORKS ON ANDROID NOT iOS ***');      Ti.API.info('rows.fieldCount = ' + fieldCount);  }    testFieldCountWorksOnAndroid();  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Database - ResultSet.fieldCount property should be ResultSet.fieldCount() method
Description: """"The APIDOCs at [Titanium.Database.ResultSet|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Database.ResultSet-object.html] state that [fieldCount|http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Database.ResultSet.fieldCount-method.html] is a method. While this exists on iOS, Android provides it as a property. Hence, this is a request to remove the property on Android and to replace it with a method. See the following testcase provided by Ketan: {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} /** * Initializes the test environment, creating a simple table """"""""data"""""""" that has 150 * rows in it and just 2 fields */ var testRowCount = 150; var db = Ti.Database.open('data'); db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS data (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, val TEXT)'); db.execute('DELETE FROM data WHERE 1=1'); for (var i = 1; i <= testRowCount; i++) { db.execute('INSERT INTO data (val) VALUES(?)','our value:' + i); } /** * FIELD COUNT WORKS AS A METHOD AS EXPECTED ON IOS BUT RETURNS ERROR ON ANDROID. * EXPECTED RESULT: 2 * * REAL BEHAVIOR IN 1.8.3: ANDROID SAYS: Uncaught TypeError: Property 'fieldCount' of object #<TiResultSet> is not a function */ function testFieldCountCrashesOnAndroid() { // now select out our data from the database var rows = db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM data""""""""); var fieldCount = rows.fieldCount(); Ti.API.info('*** SHOULD WORK ON BOTH iOS & ANDROID ***'); Ti.API.info('rows.fieldCount() = ' + fieldCount); } testFieldCountCrashesOnAndroid(); /** * FIELD COUNT WORKS AS A METHOD AS EXPECTED ON IOS BUT RETURNS ERROR ON ANDROID. You will need to comment out line 27 above to test it working on android. * EXPECTED RESULT: 2 * * REAL BEHAVIOR IN 1.8.0.1 RC3: iOS only sees the result set object and no longer gets the field count value, although android now returns the value 2. */ function testFieldCountWorksOnAndroid() { // now select out our data from the database var rows = db.execute(""""""""SELECT * FROM data""""""""); var fieldCount = rows.fieldCount; // Changed to a property not a method call. Ti.API.info('*** NOW WORKS ON ANDROID NOT iOS ***'); Ti.API.info('rows.fieldCount = ' + fieldCount); } testFieldCountWorksOnAndroid(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2944,12,"""Android, 2.3 only : TableView layout (layout) - intermittent, rotating device clears content of TV ""","""""""{html}<div><p>only seen 2X, both times on the 2.3 nexus S<br> 1.Base UI &gt; Views &gt; table views &gt; Table View (layout 2)<br> 2.tap on any item on the topmost row<br> 3.rotate to landscape</p> <p>results: 2X, all contents except the text indicating what was tapped on have been cleared (row delimiters still appeared)</p> <p>logcat did not show anything, logging in case dev knows whats up.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android, 2.3 only : TableView layout (layout) - intermittent, rotating device clears content of TV
Description: """"{html}<div><p>only seen 2X, both times on the 2.3 nexus S<br> 1.Base UI &gt; Views &gt; table views &gt; Table View (layout 2)<br> 2.tap on any item on the topmost row<br> 3.rotate to landscape</p> <p>results: 2X, all contents except the text indicating what was tapped on have been cleared (row delimiters still appeared)</p> <p>logcat did not show anything, logging in case dev knows whats up.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2943,12,"""Android: 2.3 only,  visual issue with icon when selecting KS from recent apps menu (first time only) ""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a) Nexus S (2.3.1) Droid 1 (2.2.1) G1 (1.6) sim 2.1 nexus 1 (2.2.2)</p> <p>1.Launch KS on a 2.3 device<br> 2.hit the home button after it launches<br> 3.hold the home button down until you invoke the list of recent apps<br> 4.taop the KS icon whiel watching it</p> <p>results: strange redraw. WIll not happen the second time you try it (quit the app and restart to see it a a second time). not seen on any other devices or with other apps on device.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: 2.3 only, visual issue with icon when selecting KS from recent apps menu (first time only)
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a) Nexus S (2.3.1) Droid 1 (2.2.1) G1 (1.6) sim 2.1 nexus 1 (2.2.2)</p> <p>1.Launch KS on a 2.3 device<br> 2.hit the home button after it launches<br> 3.hold the home button down until you invoke the list of recent apps<br> 4.taop the KS icon whiel watching it</p> <p>results: strange redraw. WIll not happen the second time you try it (quit the app and restart to see it a a second time). not seen on any other devices or with other apps on device.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2942,12,"""Android: Galaxy Tab; Name/Phone keyboard invokes last keyboard selected ""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a) Galaxy tab (2.2.2) only</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; Text Field &gt; Keyboard<br> 2.Select any keyboard other than Name/phone<br> 3.after invoking a keyboard, invoke name/phone</p> <p>results: previously selected keyboard is invoked</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Galaxy Tab; Name/Phone keyboard invokes last keyboard selected
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/24/11 08:14 e1cb22a) Galaxy tab (2.2.2) only</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; Text Field &gt; Keyboard<br> 2.Select any keyboard other than Name/phone<br> 3.after invoking a keyboard, invoke name/phone</p> <p>results: previously selected keyboard is invoked</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
