Description: """"{html}<div><p>since at least 1.4.2, not a new issue</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; XHR &gt; BInary data with console open</p> <p>results: test succeeds, output says: Tue Jan 18 15:46:00 Apple- sandboxd[2848] : KitchenSink(2623) deny file-write-data /private/var/mobile/Media/PhotoData</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2874,12,"""Android: Expose fireSyncEvent method""","""""""{html}<div><p>Greetings, in our application we have found the need to use the Ti.App.fireEvent method. However, we have also found some use cases where we want the method to fire the event synchronously. For instance, currently as a work around to the android menu implementation we have to open up a new window, specify a url, and in this file fire an event to return the menu. Since it's async, the menu doesn't display the first time. The fireSyncEvent method for droid is already exposed so it just needs the kroll annotations, I will submit a pull request in github shortly. Would be great if we could get this pulled into 1.6. Thanks!</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose fireSyncEvent method
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Greetings, in our application we have found the need to use the Ti.App.fireEvent method. However, we have also found some use cases where we want the method to fire the event synchronously. For instance, currently as a work around to the android menu implementation we have to open up a new window, specify a url, and in this file fire an event to return the menu. Since it's async, the menu doesn't display the first time. The fireSyncEvent method for droid is already exposed so it just needs the kroll annotations, I will submit a pull request in github shortly. Would be great if we could get this pulled into 1.6. Thanks!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2873,12,"""Android: Rotate + Scale animations need to support relative anchorPoints""","""""""{html}<div><p>The new Matrix based animations only support absolute positions in anchorPoint, not 0-1 like our current API dictates. This will require us to save us a Matrix array internally so we can correctly apply the rotate() operation with the calculated width/height of the child.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Rotate + Scale animations need to support relative anchorPoints
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The new Matrix based animations only support absolute positions in anchorPoint, not 0-1 like our current API dictates. This will require us to save us a Matrix array internally so we can correctly apply the rotate() operation with the calculated width/height of the child.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2872,12,"""iOS: Feature Request: DashboardView add editable:false""","""""""{html}<div><p>Reference Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67131"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67131</a></p> <p>Add the ability to turn off edit mode on the dashboardView.</p> <p>Something like</p> <p>Ti.UI.dashboardView({editable:false});</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Feature Request: DashboardView add editable:false
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Reference Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67131"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/67131</a></p> <p>Add the ability to turn off edit mode on the dashboardView.</p> <p>Something like</p> <p>Ti.UI.dashboardView({editable:false});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
