TIMOB-2835,12,"""Android: Expose properties on NotificationManager.Notification""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently the notification proxy only accept the properties as creation args. Expose the properties to allow the values to be queried and updated where appropriate. Make sure to update the apidoc with the changes.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose properties on NotificationManager.Notification
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently the notification proxy only accept the properties as creation args. Expose the properties to allow the values to be queried and updated where appropriate. Make sure to update the apidoc with the changes.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2834,12,"""BarImage breaks Title text in navigation group""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you have a barImage in a NavigationGroup, it deletes the  title Text on child windows, only after one child window is called.  The barImage works correctly on the parent and on the first child  window called but not subsequent child images</p>  <p>Code can be found at <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1461234"""""""">http://pastie.org/1461234</a><br>  barTop.png needs to be placed in the Resources directory</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: BarImage breaks Title text in navigation group
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you have a barImage in a NavigationGroup, it deletes the title Text on child windows, only after one child window is called. The barImage works correctly on the parent and on the first child window called but not subsequent child images</p> <p>Code can be found at <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1461234"""""""">http://pastie.org/1461234</a><br> barTop.png needs to be placed in the Resources directory</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2833,12,"""Platform specific images are not being picked up from the Resources/iphone directory""","""""""{html}<div><p>If I place an image in:</p>  <p>Resources/iphone/images/myimage.png</p>  <p>and reference it in app.js as:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({    backgroundImage:'images/myimage.png',    title:'foo'  });</code>  </pre>  <p>it does not work - I have to place the image in:</p>  <p>Resources/images/myimage.png</p>  <p>for it to show up as the background image of my button. It's  possible this extends to other resource types as well (JS files,  etc), but I have not tested that</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Platform specific images are not being picked up from the Resources/iphone directory
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If I place an image in:</p> <p>Resources/iphone/images/myimage.png</p> <p>and reference it in app.js as:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ backgroundImage:'images/myimage.png', title:'foo' });</code> </pre> <p>it does not work - I have to place the image in:</p> <p>Resources/images/myimage.png</p> <p>for it to show up as the background image of my button. It's possible this extends to other resource types as well (JS files, etc), but I have not tested that</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2832,12,"""iOS Feature Request: Custom Pop-up on touch events (Like Select,Copy,Paste)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Reference: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62771"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62771</a></p>  <p>Customer would like to be able to customize what the users see  when they touch and hold on text, rather than seeing the copy,paste  option. There is an example given in the ticket.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS Feature Request: Custom Pop-up on touch events (Like Select,Copy,Paste)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Reference: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62771"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62771</a></p> <p>Customer would like to be able to customize what the users see when they touch and hold on text, rather than seeing the copy,paste option. There is an example given in the ticket.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
