TIMOB-2828,12,"""VideoPlayer on iPad - Orientations issues""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>There is a serious issues with VideoPlayer orientations.<br> If you launch the KitchenSinkIpad demo in landscape &gt; Open Main Tests &gt; Embedded Video &gt; Play the movie &gt; Launch in fullscreen &gt; Rotate in portrait and then, click where you want. Now everything is broken (see the attachment). The player is upside down (see the status bar). When you leave the fullscreen mode, the splitview is upside down too.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: VideoPlayer on iPad - Orientations issues
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>There is a serious issues with VideoPlayer orientations.<br> If you launch the KitchenSinkIpad demo in landscape &gt; Open Main Tests &gt; Embedded Video &gt; Play the movie &gt; Launch in fullscreen &gt; Rotate in portrait and then, click where you want. Now everything is broken (see the attachment). The player is upside down (see the status bar). When you leave the fullscreen mode, the splitview is upside down too.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2827,12,"""iOS: Integrate latest ASIHTTPRequest for network object caching""","""""""{html}<div><p>There have been several requests for image caching in the  Q&amp;A section. The latest version of ASIHTTPRequest comes with  support for this, so instad of implementing my own strategy, I'd  love to see this lib upgraded and support for caching added.</p>  <p>See <a href=  """"""""http://allseeing-i.com/ASIHTTPRequest/How-to-use#using_a_download_cache"""""""">  http://allseeing-i.com/ASIHTTPRequest/How-to-use#using_a_download_c...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Integrate latest ASIHTTPRequest for network object caching
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There have been several requests for image caching in the Q&amp;A section. The latest version of ASIHTTPRequest comes with support for this, so instad of implementing my own strategy, I'd love to see this lib upgraded and support for caching added.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://allseeing-i.com/ASIHTTPRequest/How-to-use#using_a_download_cache""""""""> http://allseeing-i.com/ASIHTTPRequest/How-to-use#using_a_download_c...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2826,12,"""iOS optionDialog clickEvent.cancel should be boolean""","""""""{html}<div><p>Problem:</p> <p>According to the docs*, the <code>cancel</code> property of the <code>optionDialog</code> click event is a """"""""boolean to indicate if the cancel button was pressed"""""""", but it is the index of the button that was originally passed to the <code>createOptionDialog</code>.</p> <p>Example:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">// index 4 is the cancel button var opts = ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'Cancel'];  var dialog = Ti.UI.createOptionDialog({     title: 'Test',     options: opts,     cancel: opts.length -1 });  dialog.addEventListener('click', function(e) {     Ti.API.info(e); })</code> </pre> <p>When clicking the 'Cancel' option with the above code, the result is:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] { cancel = 4; destructive = """"""""-1""""""""; index = 4; source = """"""""[object TiUIOptionDialog]""""""""; type = click; }</code> </pre> <p>Expected result:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] { cancel = True; destructive = """"""""-1""""""""; index = 4; source = """"""""[object TiUIOptionDialog]""""""""; type = click; }</code> </pre> <p>So this is either a bug in the click event object construction or the documentation.</p> <p>I'm using 1.5.1.</p> <p>[*] <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.OptionDialog-object""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI....</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS optionDialog clickEvent.cancel should be boolean
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Problem:</p> <p>According to the docs*, the <code>cancel</code> property of the <code>optionDialog</code> click event is a """"""""boolean to indicate if the cancel button was pressed"""""""", but it is the index of the button that was originally passed to the <code>createOptionDialog</code>.</p> <p>Example:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">// index 4 is the cancel button var opts = ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'Cancel']; var dialog = Ti.UI.createOptionDialog({ title: 'Test', options: opts, cancel: opts.length -1 }); dialog.addEventListener('click', function(e) { Ti.API.info(e); })</code> </pre> <p>When clicking the 'Cancel' option with the above code, the result is:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] { cancel = 4; destructive = """"""""-1""""""""; index = 4; source = """"""""[object TiUIOptionDialog]""""""""; type = click; }</code> </pre> <p>Expected result:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] { cancel = True; destructive = """"""""-1""""""""; index = 4; source = """"""""[object TiUIOptionDialog]""""""""; type = click; }</code> </pre> <p>So this is either a bug in the click event object construction or the documentation.</p> <p>I'm using 1.5.1.</p> <p>[*] <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.OptionDialog-object""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI....</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2825,12,"""Android: ResponseCache throws IllegalStateException in Gingerbread""","""""""{html}<div><p>getHeaderField() is apparently re-entrant on getInputStream() now. You can see the trace by loading the Remote ImageView test in KS</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ResponseCache throws IllegalStateException in Gingerbread
Description: """"{html}<div><p>getHeaderField() is apparently re-entrant on getInputStream() now. You can see the trace by loading the Remote ImageView test in KS</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2824,12,"""Android: Add support for app name localization""","""""""Add support for the """"""""app.xml"""""""" file in localization - this file is located in {{i18n/<LOCALE>}} and contains properties which are not strings used by the app, but strings used by the OS for localization (for example, the app name display on the dash). This file is laid out exactly like {{strings.xml}} but the string {{name}} property keys are used to set appropriate properties for display.    Currently the only available key is:    {{appname}}: The name of the app displayed on the dash    This file is OPTIONAL. If not provided the settings in tiapp.xml for app properties take effect.    Currently there is a shortcircuit in {{localecompiler.py}} to ignore the {{app.xml}} file on Android.    See bug Ticket #2584 (/projects/32238/tickets/2584) for iOS ticket &amp; solution commit.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add support for app name localization
Description: """"Add support for the """"""""app.xml"""""""" file in localization - this file is located in {{i18n/<LOCALE>}} and contains properties which are not strings used by the app, but strings used by the OS for localization (for example, the app name display on the dash). This file is laid out exactly like {{strings.xml}} but the string {{name}} property keys are used to set appropriate properties for display. Currently the only available key is: {{appname}}: The name of the app displayed on the dash This file is OPTIONAL. If not provided the settings in tiapp.xml for app properties take effect. Currently there is a shortcircuit in {{localecompiler.py}} to ignore the {{app.xml}} file on Android. See bug Ticket #2584 (/projects/32238/tickets/2584) for iOS ticket &amp; solution commit.""""",title+description
TIMOB-2823,12,"""Cannot use  '&' for Description, Publisher or Copyright (in tiapp.xml)""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you use a '&amp;' symbol in the Description, Publisher or Copyright fields of an app, the app will not run. This is the error generated:</p> <pre> <code>Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Users/alanleard/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1269, in &lt;module&gt; main(sys.argv) File """"""""/Users/alanleard/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 378, in main ti = TiAppXML(tiapp_xml) File """"""""/Users/alanleard/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.0/iphone/../tiapp.py"""""""", line 50, in __init__ self.dom = parseString(data.read().encode('utf-8')) File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.6/lib/python2.6/xml/dom/minidom.py"""""""", line 1928, in parseString return expatbuilder.parseString(string) File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.6/lib/python2.6/xml/dom/expatbuilder.py"""""""", line 940, in parseString return builder.parseString(string) File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.6/lib/python2.6/xml/dom/expatbuilder.py"""""""", line 223, in parseString parser.Parse(string, True) xml.parsers.expat.ExpatError: not well-formed (invalid token): line 8, column 31</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Cannot use '&' for Description, Publisher or Copyright (in tiapp.xml)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you use a '&amp;' symbol in the Description, Publisher or Copyright fields of an app, the app will not run. This is the error generated:</p> <pre> <code>Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Users/alanleard/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 1269, in &lt;module&gt; main(sys.argv) File """"""""/Users/alanleard/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 378, in main ti = TiAppXML(tiapp_xml) File """"""""/Users/alanleard/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.6.0/iphone/../tiapp.py"""""""", line 50, in __init__ self.dom = parseString(data.read().encode('utf-8')) File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.6/lib/python2.6/xml/dom/minidom.py"""""""", line 1928, in parseString return expatbuilder.parseString(string) File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.6/lib/python2.6/xml/dom/expatbuilder.py"""""""", line 940, in parseString return builder.parseString(string) File """"""""/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.6/lib/python2.6/xml/dom/expatbuilder.py"""""""", line 223, in parseString parser.Parse(string, True) xml.parsers.expat.ExpatError: not well-formed (invalid token): line 8, column 31</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2822,12,"""iOS 4+, background/foreground app - every 4-5 times the splash appears""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/13/11 08:11 7ca73a3)</p> <p>1.install KS on a iOS4 + based device<br> 2.launch KS, the hit the home button to bg, then quickly tap the app to launch it again<br> 3.repeat 4-5X</p> <p>results: about every 4 or 5 times, the splash will appear. to stramer as per our brief chat. nothing new about this.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 4+, background/foreground app - every 4-5 times the splash appears
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/13/11 08:11 7ca73a3)</p> <p>1.install KS on a iOS4 + based device<br> 2.launch KS, the hit the home button to bg, then quickly tap the app to launch it again<br> 3.repeat 4-5X</p> <p>results: about every 4 or 5 times, the splash will appear. to stramer as per our brief chat. nothing new about this.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2820,12,"""URLs not automaticcaly encoded anymore in 1.6.0?""","""""""{html}<div><p>I'm not sure if this is a feature or a bug.</p> <p>In 1.4.2 this used to work:<br> Titanium.Platform.openURL('<a href= """"""""http://mydomain.com/two"""""""">http://mydomain.com/two</a> words');</p> <p>In 1.6.0 it doesn't anymore. However, encodeURIComponent() allows for an easy solution.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: URLs not automaticcaly encoded anymore in 1.6.0?
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I'm not sure if this is a feature or a bug.</p> <p>In 1.4.2 this used to work:<br> Titanium.Platform.openURL('<a href= """"""""http://mydomain.com/two"""""""">http://mydomain.com/two</a> words');</p> <p>In 1.6.0 it doesn't anymore. However, encodeURIComponent() allows for an easy solution.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2819,12,"""iOS - loading a @2x image with hires set to true does not scale to imageView""","""""""{html}<div><p>notes from, <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1543"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1543"""""""">#1543</a> (#2805 has also been logged against 2X image scaling). Works as expected in 1.5.1 <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e)</p> <p>""""""""The 2x image loaded, but it seems that the image scaling code was not modified to take this into account. 2x images appear visually to be half the size they should be. Example:<br> I have a 60x60 Ti.UI.ImageView. On a iPhone 3, my remote image loads, and is scaled to fill the 60x60 space.<br> However, on an iPhone 4, the high-res image seems to have scaled to only take up half of the space. I believe the image scaled to literally 60x60px, instead of 60x60 points on the screen (aka 120x120px).<br> My code:<br></p> <pre> <code>// left image var updateImage = Titanium.UI.createImageView({     defaultImage:'images/loading_60.png',     image:thisUpdate.updateCauseIcon,     top:5,     left:10,     width:60,     height:60 }); // iPhone 4 display if (Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.dpi == 320) {     updateImage.image = thisUpdate.updateCauseIcon2x;     updateImage.hires = true; }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - loading a @2x image with hires set to true does not scale to imageView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>notes from, <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1543"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1543"""""""">#1543</a> (#2805 has also been logged against 2X image scaling). Works as expected in 1.5.1 <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e)</p> <p>""""""""The 2x image loaded, but it seems that the image scaling code was not modified to take this into account. 2x images appear visually to be half the size they should be. Example:<br> I have a 60x60 Ti.UI.ImageView. On a iPhone 3, my remote image loads, and is scaled to fill the 60x60 space.<br> However, on an iPhone 4, the high-res image seems to have scaled to only take up half of the space. I believe the image scaled to literally 60x60px, instead of 60x60 points on the screen (aka 120x120px).<br> My code:<br></p> <pre> <code>// left image var updateImage = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ defaultImage:'images/loading_60.png', image:thisUpdate.updateCauseIcon, top:5, left:10, width:60, height:60 }); // iPhone 4 display if (Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.dpi == 320) { updateImage.image = thisUpdate.updateCauseIcon2x; updateImage.hires = true; }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2818,12,"""ScrollableView inside TableView causes duplication of data""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is an offshoot of:<br> <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2812-scrollabeview-inside-tableview-crashes-regularly-after-scrolling""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2812-...</a></p> <p>The only difference is adding the ScrollableView to a View before adding it to the TableViewRow.</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://gist.github.com/778054"""""""">https://gist.github.com/778054</a></p> <p>Mobile SDK 1.5.1<br> Android 2.2<br> Titanium Developer 1.2.2</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ScrollableView inside TableView causes duplication of data
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is an offshoot of:<br> <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2812-scrollabeview-inside-tableview-crashes-regularly-after-scrolling""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2812-...</a></p> <p>The only difference is adding the ScrollableView to a View before adding it to the TableViewRow.</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://gist.github.com/778054"""""""">https://gist.github.com/778054</a></p> <p>Mobile SDK 1.5.1<br> Android 2.2<br> Titanium Developer 1.2.2</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2817,12,"""Printing for IOS (IPad)""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need printing (webview should be enough) for IOS on an IPad. I found only one helpdesk ticket regarding this topic: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62261"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62261</a></p> <p>Is there any timeline for printing functions?</p> <p>Any workaround would be great!</p> <p>Priority: Very high</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Printing for IOS (IPad)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need printing (webview should be enough) for IOS on an IPad. I found only one helpdesk ticket regarding this topic: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62261"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62261</a></p> <p>Is there any timeline for printing functions?</p> <p>Any workaround would be great!</p> <p>Priority: Very high</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
