Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium.Geolocation.reverseGeocoder will output the names of cities, etc, only in English. There is a HD ticket asking to have an option of changing the default language output as a feature request.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/65451"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/65451</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2810,12,"""Changing table row BG color doesn't redisplay with new color""","""""""{html}<div><p>Example code:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:""""""""white""""""""});  // create table view data object var rows = [     Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 1'}),     Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 2'}),     Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 3'}),     Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 4'}) ];  var tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({     data:rows });  var tableRowSelect = function(rows, index, tableView) {  for (var i=0;i&lt;rows.length;i++) {    Ti.API.log('Checking row index '+i);    if(i == index) {      Ti.API.log('Selected');      rows[i].backgroundColor = '#fff';    } else {      Ti.API.log('Deselected');      rows[i].backgroundColor = '#d6d6d6';    }  } };  tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e) {        tableRowSelect(rows, e.index, tableview); });  win.add(tableview); win.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Changing table row BG color doesn't redisplay with new color
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Example code:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:""""""""white""""""""}); // create table view data object var rows = [ Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 1'}), Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 2'}), Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 3'}), Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Row 4'}) ]; var tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({ data:rows }); var tableRowSelect = function(rows, index, tableView) { for (var i=0;i&lt;rows.length;i++) { Ti.API.log('Checking row index '+i); if(i == index) { Ti.API.log('Selected'); rows[i].backgroundColor = '#fff'; } else { Ti.API.log('Deselected'); rows[i].backgroundColor = '#d6d6d6'; } } }; tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e) { tableRowSelect(rows, e.index, tableview); }); win.add(tableview); win.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2809,12,"""iOS: Intermittent crash when using ARti demo""","""""""{html}<div><p>found using <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 14:54 ff401e1) and Scotts iPhone 4. Console and crash log attached.</p> <p>repro steps:<br> 1.launch the ARti app and log in if need be<br> 2.tap the """"""""whats around me"""""""" button<br> 3.tap the icon in the top right to invoke the camera on overlay<br> 4.move around until an object is presented to tap, and tap it.<br> 5.back out and repeat</p> <p>results: 2X I crashed, once after around a half dozen selections, the other after about a dozen, seems intermittent though.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Intermittent crash when using ARti demo
Description: """"{html}<div><p>found using <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 14:54 ff401e1) and Scotts iPhone 4. Console and crash log attached.</p> <p>repro steps:<br> 1.launch the ARti app and log in if need be<br> 2.tap the """"""""whats around me"""""""" button<br> 3.tap the icon in the top right to invoke the camera on overlay<br> 4.move around until an object is presented to tap, and tap it.<br> 5.back out and repeat</p> <p>results: 2X I crashed, once after around a half dozen selections, the other after about a dozen, seems intermittent though.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2808,12,"""iOS: expose allowsAirPlay property of MPMoviePlayerController""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Feature</h1> <p>Expose the allowsAirPlay property of MPMoviePlayerController through Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer so that we can stream video and audio to Apple TV.</p> <h1>Customer Notes</h1> <p>There have been changes made to the MPMoviePlayerController object within iOS adding the property allowsAirPlay. This property allows videos to be played over airplay.</p> <p>I have tested 1.4.2 and can verify that a Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer object will send audio to an Apple TV. [But it will not send video without the property being exposed.]</p> <p>I was hoping that this new feature could be exposed since they note: """"""""You must explicitly opt-in to AirPlay playback for any movie players you create. The allowsAirPlay property of MPMoviePlayerController is set to NO by default.""""""""</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/65801"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/65801</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: expose allowsAirPlay property of MPMoviePlayerController
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Feature</h1> <p>Expose the allowsAirPlay property of MPMoviePlayerController through Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer so that we can stream video and audio to Apple TV.</p> <h1>Customer Notes</h1> <p>There have been changes made to the MPMoviePlayerController object within iOS adding the property allowsAirPlay. This property allows videos to be played over airplay.</p> <p>I have tested 1.4.2 and can verify that a Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer object will send audio to an Apple TV. [But it will not send video without the property being exposed.]</p> <p>I was hoping that this new feature could be exposed since they note: """"""""You must explicitly opt-in to AirPlay playback for any movie players you create. The allowsAirPlay property of MPMoviePlayerController is set to NO by default.""""""""</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/65801"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/65801</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2807,12,"""iOS - unhandled exception on launch of app on 3.1.3""","""""""{html}<div><p>This repros in all builds including <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e)</p> <p>1.install the project (emailed to Blain) and launch on a 3.1.3 device</p> <p>results: crash. console and crashlog attached. Content emailed to Blain.</p> <p>Came via Kevin W.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - unhandled exception on launch of app on 3.1.3
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This repros in all builds including <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e)</p> <p>1.install the project (emailed to Blain) and launch on a 3.1.3 device</p> <p>results: crash. console and crashlog attached. Content emailed to Blain.</p> <p>Came via Kevin W.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2806,12,"""Android: module api: assets/ folder contents not being included.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Reproduce:</p> <ul> <li>Create a new module or use an existing one.</li> <li>Put a file such as a PNG in the assets/ folder below the module root.</li> <li>Build the project using ant.</li> <li>In the dist folder, use <code>jar tf [jarfile]</code> and <code>unzip -l [zipfile]</code> to confirm that the asset file was not put anywhere.</li> </ul></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: module api: assets/ folder contents not being included.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Reproduce:</p> <ul> <li>Create a new module or use an existing one.</li> <li>Put a file such as a PNG in the assets/ folder below the module root.</li> <li>Build the project using ant.</li> <li>In the dist folder, use <code>jar tf [jarfile]</code> and <code>unzip -l [zipfile]</code> to confirm that the asset file was not put anywhere.</li> </ul></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2805,12,"""iOS -  """"@2x~iphone"""" images on retina screens are no longer fullscreen""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e), 4GT ipods running 4.2.1 and 4.1</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Hi Rez image 2<br> 2.compare to 1.5.1</p> <p>results: its a fullscreen image in 1.5.1, and a scaled image in the bottom left on 1.6.0. Images with """"""""@2x.jpg"""""""" do not show this behavior</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - """"@2x~iphone"""" images on retina screens are no longer fullscreen
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e), 4GT ipods running 4.2.1 and 4.1</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Hi Rez image 2<br> 2.compare to 1.5.1</p> <p>results: its a fullscreen image in 1.5.1, and a scaled image in the bottom left on 1.6.0. Images with """"""""@2x.jpg"""""""" do not show this behavior</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2804,12,"""iOS emulator - [info] build output soes not include date or hash like android does.""","""""""{html}<div><p>goes back to 1.4.0 at least</p> <p>1.create a simple iOS project and launch it in the emulator<br> 2.check the ouput in TiDev<br> 3.do the same on android and compare</p> <p>iOS:[INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0<br> Android:[INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e)</p> <p>the info shown by android is useful and should be included on the iOS side.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS emulator - [info] build output soes not include date or hash like android does.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>goes back to 1.4.0 at least</p> <p>1.create a simple iOS project and launch it in the emulator<br> 2.check the ouput in TiDev<br> 3.do the same on android and compare</p> <p>iOS:[INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0<br> Android:[INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/12/11 09:38 db09d1e)</p> <p>the info shown by android is useful and should be included on the iOS side.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2802,12,"""iOS: movieControlStyle Not Deprecated, mediaControlStyle doesn't work""","""""""{html}<div><p>It seems that movieControlStyle is NOT depricated and that  mediaControlStyle does not work within  Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer.<br></p>  <p>Tested on iOS with 1.4.2, 1.5.1 and 1.6</p>  <p>This works:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br>  <br>      </code>  </pre>  <pre>  <code><code>    title: 'Test'      });</code></code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer    </pre>  <pre>  <code>({      sourceType: Ti.Media.VIDEO_SOURCE_TYPE_FILE,      url: 'movie.mp4',      backgroundColor:'#000',  scalingMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT,  movieControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_NONE  });</code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  win.add(activeMovie);    <br>  win.open();  </pre>  <p>This doesn't:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br>  <br>      </code>  </pre>  <pre>  <code><code>    title: 'Test'      });</code></code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer    </pre>  <pre>  <code>({      sourceType: Ti.Media.VIDEO_SOURCE_TYPE_FILE,      url: 'movie.mp4',      backgroundColor:'#000',  scalingMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT,  mediaControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_NONE  });</code>  </pre>  <pre>      <br>  win.add(activeMovie);    <br>  win.open();  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: movieControlStyle Not Deprecated, mediaControlStyle doesn't work
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It seems that movieControlStyle is NOT depricated and that mediaControlStyle does not work within Titanium.Media.VideoPlayer.<br></p> <p>Tested on iOS with 1.4.2, 1.5.1 and 1.6</p> <p>This works:<br></p> <pre> <code>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br> <br> </code> </pre> <pre> <code><code> title: 'Test' });</code></code> </pre> <pre> <br> var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer </pre> <pre> <code>({ sourceType: Ti.Media.VIDEO_SOURCE_TYPE_FILE, url: 'movie.mp4', backgroundColor:'#000', scalingMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT, movieControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_NONE });</code> </pre> <pre> <br> win.add(activeMovie); <br> win.open(); </pre> <p>This doesn't:<br></p> <pre> <code>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br> <br> </code> </pre> <pre> <code><code> title: 'Test' });</code></code> </pre> <pre> <br> var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer </pre> <pre> <code>({ sourceType: Ti.Media.VIDEO_SOURCE_TYPE_FILE, url: 'movie.mp4', backgroundColor:'#000', scalingMode: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_ASPECT_FIT, mediaControlStyle: Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_NONE });</code> </pre> <pre> <br> win.add(activeMovie); <br> win.open(); </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2800,12,"""iPhone : crash when trying to get a contact email (contacts synchronized)""","""""""{html}<div><p>When we synchronize contacts with external systems such as google, the email labels are not set correctly.<br> Instead of having 'home', 'work', 'other' labels, we get 'email' emails.</p> <p>Then if we get a contact using:</p> <pre> <code> selectedContact = Titanium.Contacts.getPeopleWithName(contactName);</code> </pre> <p>and then try to get the emails by doing :<br></p> <pre> <code> var emails = selectedContact[0].email;</code> </pre> Then, the app crashes.</div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone : crash when trying to get a contact email (contacts synchronized)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When we synchronize contacts with external systems such as google, the email labels are not set correctly.<br> Instead of having 'home', 'work', 'other' labels, we get 'email' emails.</p> <p>Then if we get a contact using:</p> <pre> <code> selectedContact = Titanium.Contacts.getPeopleWithName(contactName);</code> </pre> <p>and then try to get the emails by doing :<br></p> <pre> <code> var emails = selectedContact[0].email;</code> </pre> Then, the app crashes.</div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2799,12,"""iPhone: Change label width on swipe""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a tableView that contains a label visible and a hidden button. When I swipe the row it should reduces the width of the label for the button to display. This works perfectly with SDK 1.4.3 but not with 1.5.1.<br> I attach source code that proves the above:</p> <pre> <code>var tableView = Titanium.UI.createTableView(); var rows = []; var row = Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow();  var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({     text:'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Suspendisse adipiscing.',     width:300,     font:{fontSize:12,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'}, }); row.add(label1);  var b1 = Ti.UI.createButton({     title:'button',     height:30,     width:90,     right:10,     visible: false }); row.add(b1);  var swiped = ''; row.addEventListener('swipe', function (e) {swiped = e.direction;}); row.addEventListener('touchend', function (e) {     if (swiped == 'left'){         label1.width = 200;         b1.show();     } });  rows.push(row);  tableView.setData(rows); Titanium.UI.currentWindow.add(tableView);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Change label width on swipe
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have a tableView that contains a label visible and a hidden button. When I swipe the row it should reduces the width of the label for the button to display. This works perfectly with SDK 1.4.3 but not with 1.5.1.<br> I attach source code that proves the above:</p> <pre> <code>var tableView = Titanium.UI.createTableView(); var rows = []; var row = Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow(); var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({ text:'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Suspendisse adipiscing.', width:300, font:{fontSize:12,fontFamily:'Helvetica Neue'}, }); row.add(label1); var b1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'button', height:30, width:90, right:10, visible: false }); row.add(b1); var swiped = ''; row.addEventListener('swipe', function (e) {swiped = e.direction;}); row.addEventListener('touchend', function (e) { if (swiped == 'left'){ label1.width = 200; b1.show(); } }); rows.push(row); tableView.setData(rows); Titanium.UI.currentWindow.add(tableView);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2798,12,"""Android: xhr NPE for posts with empty http body""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a page that returns a 200 response, but nothing in the body.<br></p> <pre> <code>var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function() {Ti.API.info('I am in utf-8 onload for POST');}; xhr.onerror = function() {Ti.API.info('I am in utf-8 error for POST');}; xhr.open(""""""""POST"""""""",""""""""http://mywebsite.com/script.cfm""""""""); xhr.send({""""""""a"""""""":""""""""hi"""""""", """"""""b"""""""":""""""""there""""""""});</code> </pre> If the sript I post to doesn't return a body, only a 200, then the NPE happens. If I change the script to return any text at all the NPE is avoided. <p>The resulting log of the NPE looks like:<br></p> <pre> <code>[TRACE] E/TiUIView( 1729): (main) [5383,101697] TAP, TAP, TAP on [Ti.UI.Button] [TRACE] D/TiHttpClient( 1729): (kroll$3) [10,101707] Setting ready state to 1 [TRACE] D/dalvikvm( 1729): GC_FOR_MALLOC freed 12700 objects / 611088 bytes in 124ms [TRACE] D/dalvikvm( 1729): GC_FOR_MALLOC freed 1967 objects / 297312 bytes in 369ms [TRACE] D/TiHttpClient( 1729): (TiHttpClient-2) [2521,104228] Setting ready state to 2 [TRACE] D/TiHttpClient( 1729): (TiHttpClient-2) [0,104228] Setting ready state to 3 [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): (TiHttpClient-2) [2,104230] HTTP Error (java.lang.NullPointerException): java.lang.NullPointerException [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): java.lang.NullPointerException [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$LocalResponseHandler.finishedReceivingEntityData(TiHTTPClient.java:321) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$LocalResponseHandler.handleResponse(TiHTTPClient.java:257) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$LocalResponseHandler.handleResponse(TiHTTPClient.java:166) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at org.apache.http.impl.client.AbstractHttpClient.execute(AbstractHttpClient.java:657) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at org.apache.http.impl.client.AbstractHttpClient.execute(AbstractHttpClient.java:637) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$ClientRunnable.run(TiHTTPClient.java:1010) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1096) [TRACE] I/TiHttpClient( 1729): (TiHttpClient-2) [3,104233] Sending error java.lang.NullPointerException</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: xhr NPE for posts with empty http body
