AbstractHttpClient.execute(AbstractHttpClient.java:637) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$ClientRunnable.run(TiHTTPClient.java:1010) [TRACE] E/TiHttpClient( 1729): at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1096) [TRACE] I/TiHttpClient( 1729): (TiHttpClient-2) [3,104233] Sending error java.lang.NullPointerException</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2797,12,"""Ti.UI.currentTab is null""","""""""{html}<div><p>The Q&amp;A section describes this pretty well.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/98501/titaniumuicurrenttab-is-null""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/98501/titaniumuicurrentt...</a></p> <p>As <USER>Wright mentioned, it should really be the job of the framework to handle this. Espeially, since you propagate the one-context approach in your documents. I'm running into this very problem today.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.UI.currentTab is null
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The Q&amp;A section describes this pretty well.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/98501/titaniumuicurrenttab-is-null""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/98501/titaniumuicurrentt...</a></p> <p>As <USER>Wright mentioned, it should really be the job of the framework to handle this. Espeially, since you propagate the one-context approach in your documents. I'm running into this very problem today.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
