TIMOB-2768,12,"""status bar appears when video is played""","""""""{html}<div><p>In tiapp.xml, setting the status bar hidden, hides the status bar as expected. But when a movie is played using 'createVideoPlayer' the status bar appears and cannot be hidden again. This is from a Help Desk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63571"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63571</a></p> <p>Here is a sample code: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/private/qvp8jfkqm2jgi33qvurniq"""""""">http://pastie.org/private/qvp8jfkqm2jgi33qvurniq</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: status bar appears when video is played
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In tiapp.xml, setting the status bar hidden, hides the status bar as expected. But when a movie is played using 'createVideoPlayer' the status bar appears and cannot be hidden again. This is from a Help Desk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63571"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63571</a></p> <p>Here is a sample code: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/private/qvp8jfkqm2jgi33qvurniq"""""""">http://pastie.org/private/qvp8jfkqm2jgi33qvurniq</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2767,12,"""Titanium.UI.XXX components with font-xxxx properties fail JSLint/crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>Just noticed this when I was attempting to make a zombie Ti.js file for my auto-completion hack in NetBeans using the api.json file for 1.5.1</p> <p>A number of Ti.UI.XXXX components that have text metrics (button, label, etc.) now have properties like """"""""font-family"""""""" and """"""""font-size"""""""" in addition to the original """"""""font"""""""" property. Problem is that the """"""""-"""""""" in the property name is malformed Javascript and blows up both the JSLint pass during compilation (which only gives a warning) and then makes an app that crashes on the first instance of such.</p> <p>Shouldn't these be JS friendly camel-cased, like fontFamily, fontWeight, fontStyle, etc.?</p> <p>Thnx,<br> Etienne</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.UI.XXX components with font-xxxx properties fail JSLint/crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Just noticed this when I was attempting to make a zombie Ti.js file for my auto-completion hack in NetBeans using the api.json file for 1.5.1</p> <p>A number of Ti.UI.XXXX components that have text metrics (button, label, etc.) now have properties like """"""""font-family"""""""" and """"""""font-size"""""""" in addition to the original """"""""font"""""""" property. Problem is that the """"""""-"""""""" in the property name is malformed Javascript and blows up both the JSLint pass during compilation (which only gives a warning) and then makes an app that crashes on the first instance of such.</p> <p>Shouldn't these be JS friendly camel-cased, like fontFamily, fontWeight, fontStyle, etc.?</p> <p>Thnx,<br> Etienne</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2766,12,"""Android: cosmetic issue with first scroll when scrollviews are in a table view""","""""""{html}<div><p>spun off after closing <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1787"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1787"""""""">#1787</a></p> <p>Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/06/11 08:47 8b2fd0e), seen only on the G1 running 1.6</p> <p>1.create a test app with the following snippet</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');<br> var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen: true</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var views = [];<br> for (var i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) {<br></p> <pre> <code>views.push(     Ti.UI.createTableView({         data: [ Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title: 'Row for view ' + i}) ]     }) );</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>win.add(Ti.UI.createScrollableView({ views: views }));<br> win.open();</p> <p>2.install onto a 1.6 device<br> 3.watch the scroll view, and scroll right (to the second scrollView)</p> <p>results: no animation (should animate from left to right as swipe occurs)</p> <p>4.repeat from 1 - 2 again</p> <p>results: animation now occurs.</p> <p>notes: only happens to the first swipe and only affects the first tableView.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: cosmetic issue with first scroll when scrollviews are in a table view
Description: """"{html}<div><p>spun off after closing <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1787"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1787"""""""">#1787</a></p> <p>Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/06/11 08:47 8b2fd0e), seen only on the G1 running 1.6</p> <p>1.create a test app with the following snippet</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');<br> var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen: true</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var views = [];<br> for (var i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) {<br></p> <pre> <code>views.push( Ti.UI.createTableView({ data: [ Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({title: 'Row for view ' + i}) ] }) );</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>win.add(Ti.UI.createScrollableView({ views: views }));<br> win.open();</p> <p>2.install onto a 1.6 device<br> 3.watch the scroll view, and scroll right (to the second scrollView)</p> <p>results: no animation (should animate from left to right as swipe occurs)</p> <p>4.repeat from 1 - 2 again</p> <p>results: animation now occurs.</p> <p>notes: only happens to the first swipe and only affects the first tableView.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2765,12,"""iOS < 3.2 - app crashes on load with bus error 1.5.1/1.6.0""","""""""{html}<div><p>repros only on a device running 3.1.3, 3.2 and newer do not show the behavior.</p> <p>1.get the resources file from <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63201#c294921"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63201#c294921</a> and create the app<br> 2. install onto a 3.1.3 device and launch</p> <p>results: crash on launch with bus error. Runs as expected on other Os's devices.</p> <p>crash log and console attached.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS < 3.2 - app crashes on load with bus error 1.5.1/1.6.0
Description: """"{html}<div><p>repros only on a device running 3.1.3, 3.2 and newer do not show the behavior.</p> <p>1.get the resources file from <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63201#c294921"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63201#c294921</a> and create the app<br> 2. install onto a 3.1.3 device and launch</p> <p>results: crash on launch with bus error. Runs as expected on other Os's devices.</p> <p>crash log and console attached.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2764,12,"""iOS < 3.2 - app crashes on load with bus error 1.5.1/1.6.0""","""""""{html}<div><p>repros only on a device running 3.1.3, 3.2 and newer do not show the behavior.</p> <p>1.get the resources file from <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63201#c294921"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63201#c294921</a> nand create the app<br> 2. install onto a 3.1.3 device and launch</p> <p>results: crash on launch with bus error. Runs as expecetd on other Os's devices.</p> <p>crash log and console attached.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS < 3.2 - app crashes on load with bus error 1.5.1/1.6.0
