TIMOB-2763,12,"""iOS Bug 1.5.1 - webViews get extra bottom padding when the orientation changes""","""""""{html}<div><p>When a webView, added to a scrollview, changes orientation there is a lot of extra padding added to the inside of the webView. Verified on 1.5.1</p> <p>Original Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63311"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63311</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Bug 1.5.1 - webViews get extra bottom padding when the orientation changes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When a webView, added to a scrollview, changes orientation there is a lot of extra padding added to the inside of the webView. Verified on 1.5.1</p> <p>Original Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63311"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63311</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2762,12,"""Android Ent Defect: Can't Add Menu to currentActivity In app.js""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>In the app.js, """"""""Titanium.Android.currentActivity.onCreateOptionsMenu = ..."""""""" does nothing. Launching the app and pressing the menu button results in no menu popping up.</p> <h1>Workaround</h1> <p>Open a window with a URL set, and the nav bar hidden, modal true, or fullscreen true. In that JavaScript context, you can then properly set the menu.</p> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <p>The following code, placed alone in an app.js, demonstrates the problem. Launch the app and press the hardware Menu button to see that nothing pops up.</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">// add a menu. Titanium.Android.currentActivity.onCreateOptionsMenu = function (e) {     var menuItem = e.menu.add({ title: 'Window ' + i });     menuItem.setIcon('KS_nav_ui.png');     menuItem.addEventListener('click', function (e) {         alert('Clicked!');     }); }; // add some stuff to the window var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({     title: 'Window One',     backgroundColor: '#fff' }); win.add(Titanium.UI.createLabel({     color: '#999',     text: 'I am Window One',     font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' },     textAlign: 'center',     width: 'auto' })); win.open();</code> </pre> <h1>My Guess at The Problem</h1> <p>Perhaps Titanium.Android.currentActivity is not getting set in app.js.</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><USER>Sandberg, an enterprise client, reported this issue.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Ent Defect: Can't Add Menu to currentActivity In app.js
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>In the app.js, """"""""Titanium.Android.currentActivity.onCreateOptionsMenu = ..."""""""" does nothing. Launching the app and pressing the menu button results in no menu popping up.</p> <h1>Workaround</h1> <p>Open a window with a URL set, and the nav bar hidden, modal true, or fullscreen true. In that JavaScript context, you can then properly set the menu.</p> <h1>Sample Code</h1> <p>The following code, placed alone in an app.js, demonstrates the problem. Launch the app and press the hardware Menu button to see that nothing pops up.</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">// add a menu. Titanium.Android.currentActivity.onCreateOptionsMenu = function (e) { var menuItem = e.menu.add({ title: 'Window ' + i }); menuItem.setIcon('KS_nav_ui.png'); menuItem.addEventListener('click', function (e) { alert('Clicked!'); }); }; // add some stuff to the window var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Window One', backgroundColor: '#fff' }); win.add(Titanium.UI.createLabel({ color: '#999', text: 'I am Window One', font: { fontSize: 20, fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue' }, textAlign: 'center', width: 'auto' })); win.open();</code> </pre> <h1>My Guess at The Problem</h1> <p>Perhaps Titanium.Android.currentActivity is not getting set in app.js.</p> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><USER>Sandberg, an enterprise client, reported this issue.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2761,12,"""iOS Feature: Animation Options for Nav Bar Toggling""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>Client wants to be able to control how the nav bar hides and shows.</p> <h1>Current Behavior</h1> <p>Right now you can only call window.showNavBar({animated:true}), or hideNavBar.</p> <h1>Requested Changes</h1> <p>Expose the view for the navBar so that animations can be run on it such as the following:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var hideAnimation = Ti.UI.createAnimation({ opacity: 0, duration: 1000 }); hideAnimation.animate(Ti.UI.currentWindow.navBar);</code> </pre> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/61791"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/61791</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS Feature: Animation Options for Nav Bar Toggling
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>Client wants to be able to control how the nav bar hides and shows.</p> <h1>Current Behavior</h1> <p>Right now you can only call window.showNavBar({animated:true}), or hideNavBar.</p> <h1>Requested Changes</h1> <p>Expose the view for the navBar so that animations can be run on it such as the following:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var hideAnimation = Ti.UI.createAnimation({ opacity: 0, duration: 1000 }); hideAnimation.animate(Ti.UI.currentWindow.navBar);</code> </pre> <h2>Associated Helpdesk Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/61791"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/61791</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2759,12,"""Android: menu icons with """"app://"""" paths do not fetch resource images""","""""""{html}<div><p>cf helpdesk <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/60941"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/60941</a><br> cf related <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2627"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2627"""""""">#2627</a></p> <p>To reproduce:</p> <p>app.js</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#fff',     fullscreen: true,     exitOnClose: true,     url: 'win.js' }).open();</code> </pre> <p>Then make this win.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; Ti.Android.currentActivity.onCreateOptionsMenu = function(e) {     var m1 = e.menu.add({         itemId : 1,         groupId : 0,         order : 0,         title: 'I am a menu item'     });     m1.setIcon(""""""""app://images/test.png""""""""); };</code> </pre> <p>Then ...</p> <ul> <li>Create Resources/android/images/medium</li> <li>Copy KS_nav_ui.png to Resources/android/images/medium/test.png</li> </ul> <p>Run the app. When the blank window comes up, press the emulator/phone menu button. You <em>should</em> see a menu item with an icon on it, but you will only see text on the menu item.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: menu icons with """"app://"""" paths do not fetch resource images
Description: """"{html}<div><p>cf helpdesk <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/60941"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/60941</a><br> cf related <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/2627"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #2627"""""""">#2627</a></p> <p>To reproduce:</p> <p>app.js</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen: true, exitOnClose: true, url: 'win.js' }).open();</code> </pre> <p>Then make this win.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; Ti.Android.currentActivity.onCreateOptionsMenu = function(e) { var m1 = e.menu.add({ itemId : 1, groupId : 0, order : 0, title: 'I am a menu item' }); m1.setIcon(""""""""app://images/test.png""""""""); };</code> </pre> <p>Then ...</p> <ul> <li>Create Resources/android/images/medium</li> <li>Copy KS_nav_ui.png to Resources/android/images/medium/test.png</li> </ul> <p>Run the app. When the blank window comes up, press the emulator/phone menu button. You <em>should</em> see a menu item with an icon on it, but you will only see text on the menu item.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2758,12,"""Android: Picker in TableViewRow does not display its options dialog""","""""""{html}<div><p>cf Helpdesk <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64181"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64181</a></p> <p>See attached app.js.</p> <p>Behavior: A picker (standard picker) added to a TableViewRow does not show its options dialog (the """"""""dropdown"""""""" containing the picker's options) when that picker is added to a TableViewRow and then clicked-on.</p> <p>Expected: You should always see the picker's options dialog when you click it.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Picker in TableViewRow does not display its options dialog
Description: """"{html}<div><p>cf Helpdesk <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64181"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/64181</a></p> <p>See attached app.js.</p> <p>Behavior: A picker (standard picker) added to a TableViewRow does not show its options dialog (the """"""""dropdown"""""""" containing the picker's options) when that picker is added to a TableViewRow and then clicked-on.</p> <p>Expected: You should always see the picker's options dialog when you click it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2757,12,"""addEventListener on TableView in iOS 4 callback param behavior""","""""""{html}<div><p>iOS version 4<br> master branch</p> <p>This breaks (in iOS only, works with Android):<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e){   Ti.API.info(e.rowData.id); }</code> </pre> This doesn't break: <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e){   if(e.rowData) {     Ti.API.info(e.rowData.id);   } }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: addEventListener on TableView in iOS 4 callback param behavior
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iOS version 4<br> master branch</p> <p>This breaks (in iOS only, works with Android):<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e){ Ti.API.info(e.rowData.id); }</code> </pre> This doesn't break: <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e){ if(e.rowData) { Ti.API.info(e.rowData.id); } }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2756,12,"""master branch is broken with < iOS 4.1""","""""""{html}<div><p>The code has less than or equal to and it should be greater than or equal to. Or at least that's what fixes my build.</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/3c217f5f24d8565e8fa4879f491fd9a7319a1fe4""""""""> https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/3c217f5f24d8...</a></p> <p>I have submitted the patch in a pull request.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: master branch is broken with < iOS 4.1
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The code has less than or equal to and it should be greater than or equal to. Or at least that's what fixes my build.</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/3c217f5f24d8565e8fa4879f491fd9a7319a1fe4""""""""> https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/3c217f5f24d8...</a></p> <p>I have submitted the patch in a pull request.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2755,12,"""row.hasCheck on Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>i'm trying to change the hasCheck property when a row is clicked but the check icon never shows. i'm using the sdk 1.5.1 and works only for ios.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: row.hasCheck on Android
