TIMOB-2754,12,"""KitchenSink Fails to build for samsung galaxy tab Emulator (chokes on maps shared library)""","""""""{html}<div><p>I do not have a device to try it on, but I am guessing this is due to lack of api support in the android sdk right now, so perhaps it will run on device.</p> <p>1.install the most recent pull from 1.6.0 (or any pull past the writing of this bug)<br> 2.install the sdk, import KS<br> 3.on emulator tab, select """"""""GALAXY Tab addon 2.2"""""""" from SDK and """"""""GALAXY Tab"""""""" from screen<br> 4. launch</p> <p>results:<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/TRACE"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [TRACE]"""""""">[TRACE]</a> E/PackageManager( 60): Package com.<USER>pushtest requires unavailable shared library com.google.android.maps; failing!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink Fails to build for samsung galaxy tab Emulator (chokes on maps shared library)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I do not have a device to try it on, but I am guessing this is due to lack of api support in the android sdk right now, so perhaps it will run on device.</p> <p>1.install the most recent pull from 1.6.0 (or any pull past the writing of this bug)<br> 2.install the sdk, import KS<br> 3.on emulator tab, select """"""""GALAXY Tab addon 2.2"""""""" from SDK and """"""""GALAXY Tab"""""""" from screen<br> 4. launch</p> <p>results:<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/TRACE"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [TRACE]"""""""">[TRACE]</a> E/PackageManager( 60): Package com.<USER>pushtest requires unavailable shared library com.google.android.maps; failing!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2753,12,"""iOS: Background Geolocation""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is basically the same ticket as: <a href=  """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1930-allow-geolocation-in-background"""""""">  https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1930-...</a>  for Android</p>  <p>""""""""Currently (even in the current github sources) Geolocation  cannot do background processing. Is this a matter of removing the  instructions from the onPause()/onResume() routines? I think  allowing a user to specify allowBackGround: true in their initial  construction of a Geolocation object would be wise. This way, we  can still do background processing and not have to worry about the  app losing focus, and data being randomly sent askew.""""""""</p>  <p>Customer(s) ticket: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57011"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57011</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Background Geolocation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is basically the same ticket as: <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1930-allow-geolocation-in-background""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1930-...</a> for Android</p> <p>""""""""Currently (even in the current github sources) Geolocation cannot do background processing. Is this a matter of removing the instructions from the onPause()/onResume() routines? I think allowing a user to specify allowBackGround: true in their initial construction of a Geolocation object would be wise. This way, we can still do background processing and not have to worry about the app losing focus, and data being randomly sent askew.""""""""</p> <p>Customer(s) ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57011"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57011</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2752,12,"""Android: Support for android.app.AlarmManager""","""""""Integrated in to Titanium.Android.Service""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support for android.app.AlarmManager
Description: """"Integrated in to Titanium.Android.Service""""",title+description
TIMOB-2751,12,"""Row/section indexes not updated after """"delete""""""","""""""{html}<div><p>Just what it says. Not visible when interacting with the  tableview via regular means, but any method which requires getting  the row index to compute the NSIndexPath will be affected. Behavior  is visible in KS by:</p>  <ul>  <li>Base UI-&gt;Views-&gt;Table View-&gt;Delete Mode (2)</li>  <li>Delete a row</li>  <li>Click on the last row while still in edit mode</li>  </ul>  <p>Repro steps rely on (currently pending) fix for <a href=  """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1330"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1330"""""""">#1330</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Row/section indexes not updated after """"delete""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Just what it says. Not visible when interacting with the tableview via regular means, but any method which requires getting the row index to compute the NSIndexPath will be affected. Behavior is visible in KS by:</p> <ul> <li>Base UI-&gt;Views-&gt;Table View-&gt;Delete Mode (2)</li> <li>Delete a row</li> <li>Click on the last row while still in edit mode</li> </ul> <p>Repro steps rely on (currently pending) fix for <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1330"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1330"""""""">#1330</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2750,12,"""iOS: Tabbed bar- red tabs do not respond to """"set tab 0 active"""" ""","""""""{html}<div><p>iOS 4.1 4GT iPod touch. Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/04/11 08:01 e49700d)<br> missed during 1.5.0</p> <p>Tabbed bar- red tabs do not repsond to """"""""set tab 0 active""""""""<br> 1.Controls &gt; Tabbed bar<br> 2.tap the red tabs so that tab """"""""two"""""""" is active<br> 3.Tap the """"""""set tab 0 active"""""""" button</p> <p>results: does not change the red tabs to 0 tab</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Tabbed bar- red tabs do not respond to """"set tab 0 active""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iOS 4.1 4GT iPod touch. Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/04/11 08:01 e49700d)<br> missed during 1.5.0</p> <p>Tabbed bar- red tabs do not repsond to """"""""set tab 0 active""""""""<br> 1.Controls &gt; Tabbed bar<br> 2.tap the red tabs so that tab """"""""two"""""""" is active<br> 3.Tap the """"""""set tab 0 active"""""""" button</p> <p>results: does not change the red tabs to 0 tab</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2749,12,"""iOS: should scroll bars draw under the keyboard? ""","""""""{html}<div><p>iOS 4.1 4GT iPod touch. Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/04/11 08:01 e49700d)</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; text Field &gt; textfield in scrollview<br> 2.tap into any of the field to invoke keyboard, the scroll<br> 3.note the scrolling indicator dissapears behind the keyboard - the user has no indicator of if there is more info to reveal.</p> <p>not a regression</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: should scroll bars draw under the keyboard?
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iOS 4.1 4GT iPod touch. Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/04/11 08:01 e49700d)</p> <p>1.Controls &gt; text Field &gt; textfield in scrollview<br> 2.tap into any of the field to invoke keyboard, the scroll<br> 3.note the scrolling indicator dissapears behind the keyboard - the user has no indicator of if there is more info to reveal.</p> <p>not a regression</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2748,12,"""iOS: no keyboard in upside down portrait""","""""""{html}<div><p>iOS 4.1 4GT iPod touch. Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/04/11 08:01 e49700d)</p> <p>1.controls&gt;text field &gt; events<br> 2.invoke keyboard and rotoate through the orientations, note upside down portrait</p> <p>results: keyboard/app does not repsond to upside down portrait - should it?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: no keyboard in upside down portrait
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iOS 4.1 4GT iPod touch. Titanium SDK version: 1.6.0 (01/04/11 08:01 e49700d)</p> <p>1.controls&gt;text field &gt; events<br> 2.invoke keyboard and rotoate through the orientations, note upside down portrait</p> <p>results: keyboard/app does not repsond to upside down portrait - should it?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
