TIMOB-2736,12,"""iOS Bug - Keyboard Toolbar Oddities on Focus / Blur""","""""""{html}<div><p>Focusing back and forth between fields does not update the keyboard toolbar. When trying to programmatically set the contents of the toolbar - the toolbar stays stationary on the page when the keyboard is closed (the field is blurred). Tested on 1.5.1, 1.6.</p> <p>Original Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63561"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63561</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Bug - Keyboard Toolbar Oddities on Focus / Blur
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Focusing back and forth between fields does not update the keyboard toolbar. When trying to programmatically set the contents of the toolbar - the toolbar stays stationary on the page when the keyboard is closed (the field is blurred). Tested on 1.5.1, 1.6.</p> <p>Original Ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63561"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63561</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2735,12,"""iOS: Images in the /iphone/ directory don't show up on the device.""","""""""{html}<div><p>When referencing images from the iphone directory (i.e.  /iphone/images/somePic.png or even /iphone/somePic.png) - works on  the sim but not on the device. I tested with an imageView and a  tab. Confirmed the issue with 1.6, 1.5.1, 1.4.3.</p>  <p>Original ticket: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63521"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63521</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Images in the /iphone/ directory don't show up on the device.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When referencing images from the iphone directory (i.e. /iphone/images/somePic.png or even /iphone/somePic.png) - works on the sim but not on the device. I tested with an imageView and a tab. Confirmed the issue with 1.6, 1.5.1, 1.4.3.</p> <p>Original ticket: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63521"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63521</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2734,12,"""android facebook query fails after login event is fired.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Android facebbook query fails after login event is fired.</p> <p>If the device has an active facebook session ( after first login )</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62821"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62821</a></p> <p>function query_all_friends()<br> {</p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info('Query all friends of '+Titanium.Facebook.userId); var query = """"""""SELECT uid,name,pic_square FROM user WHERE uid IN (SELECT uid2 FROM friend WHERE uid1 = """""""" + Titanium.Facebook.userId + """""""")"""""""";  Titanium.Facebook.query(query, function(r) {     Ti.API.info('Query recieved for '+Titanium.Facebook.userId);      var c = 0;     var data = [];      for (c=0;c&lt;r.data.length;c++)     {         var row = r.data[c];         data.push({className:'friends', title:row.name, chosen_name:row.name, leftImage:row.pic_square, uid:row.uid, chosen_pic:row.pic_square, selectedColor:'#ff6600'});               }//end if iphone      var tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({ data:data, top: '60', height: 286, filterAttribute:'chosen_name' });               tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e) { Ti.API.info('rowClicked: ' + e.row.chosen_name ); });          win.add(tableview); });</code> </pre> <p>}//end query_all_friends</p> <p>Ti.Facebook.addEventListener('login', function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>query_all_friends();</code> </pre> <p>});//end</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: android facebook query fails after login event is fired.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Android facebbook query fails after login event is fired.</p> <p>If the device has an active facebook session ( after first login )</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62821"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62821</a></p> <p>function query_all_friends()<br> {</p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info('Query all friends of '+Titanium.Facebook.userId); var query = """"""""SELECT uid,name,pic_square FROM user WHERE uid IN (SELECT uid2 FROM friend WHERE uid1 = """""""" + Titanium.Facebook.userId + """""""")""""""""; Titanium.Facebook.query(query, function(r) { Ti.API.info('Query recieved for '+Titanium.Facebook.userId); var c = 0; var data = []; for (c=0;c&lt;r.data.length;c++) { var row = r.data[c]; data.push({className:'friends', title:row.name, chosen_name:row.name, leftImage:row.pic_square, uid:row.uid, chosen_pic:row.pic_square, selectedColor:'#ff6600'}); }//end if iphone var tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({ data:data, top: '60', height: 286, filterAttribute:'chosen_name' }); tableview.addEventListener('click', function(e) { Ti.API.info('rowClicked: ' + e.row.chosen_name ); }); win.add(tableview); });</code> </pre> <p>}//end query_all_friends</p> <p>Ti.Facebook.addEventListener('login', function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>query_all_friends();</code> </pre> <p>});//end</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2732,12,"""Android: geo location droid 1 only - runtime error invoked on geolocation test ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Same in 1.5.1, device specific - found in 1.6.0 (01/03/11 08:14  11dd2b6), droid 1 (2.2.1)</p>  <p>1.Phone&gt;geolocation</p>  <p>results: runtime error<br>  location: 342,0 app://examples/geolocation.js<br>  message: wrapped java.lang.IllegalArgumentsException: Expected 2  arguments for log, got 1 (app://examples/geolocation.js#342)</p>  <p>not seen on nexus 1, g1 or g2</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: geo location droid 1 only - runtime error invoked on geolocation test
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Same in 1.5.1, device specific - found in 1.6.0 (01/03/11 08:14 11dd2b6), droid 1 (2.2.1)</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;geolocation</p> <p>results: runtime error<br> location: 342,0 app://examples/geolocation.js<br> message: wrapped java.lang.IllegalArgumentsException: Expected 2 arguments for log, got 1 (app://examples/geolocation.js#342)</p> <p>not seen on nexus 1, g1 or g2</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2731,12,"""Android: droid 1 - video controls are misplaced on orientation change (sometimes first, sometimes second) while video plays. ""","""""""{html}<div><p>found in 1.6.0 (01/03/11 08:14 11dd2b6), droid 1 (2.2.1)<br> not a regression and may be device specific, unable to repro on the G2 or nexus 1</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;video<br> 2.tap the screen so the label reflects the action (""""""""you've tapped the label"""""""" - this step may not be required)<br> 3.rotate the device to landscape<br> 4.back to portrait, then to landscape</p> <p>results: about 25% of the time the controls are misplaced (see screen shot)<br> goes back to 1.5.1 at least</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: droid 1 - video controls are misplaced on orientation change (sometimes first, sometimes second) while video plays.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>found in 1.6.0 (01/03/11 08:14 11dd2b6), droid 1 (2.2.1)<br> not a regression and may be device specific, unable to repro on the G2 or nexus 1</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;video<br> 2.tap the screen so the label reflects the action (""""""""you've tapped the label"""""""" - this step may not be required)<br> 3.rotate the device to landscape<br> 4.back to portrait, then to landscape</p> <p>results: about 25% of the time the controls are misplaced (see screen shot)<br> goes back to 1.5.1 at least</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
