TIMOB-2703,12,"""TiAPI: Localizing Strings in tiapp.xml""","""""""h4. Problem    Application is being released in United States and Spain under two different names, but tiapp.xml only allows you to specify a single name.    h4. Workaround    Customer has duplicated their application with two different tiapp.xmls with the names in the two languages.    h4.Solution    Add localization support for the language dependent settings in tiapp.xml. This could include:  * Name  * Publisher  * Description  * Copyright  * Icon""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Localizing Strings in tiapp.xml
Description: """"h4. Problem Application is being released in United States and Spain under two different names, but tiapp.xml only allows you to specify a single name. h4. Workaround Customer has duplicated their application with two different tiapp.xmls with the names in the two languages. h4.Solution Add localization support for the language dependent settings in tiapp.xml. This could include: * Name * Publisher * Description * Copyright * Icon""""",title+description
TIMOB-2702,12,"""Request fot imageAsThumbnail on API docs iOS""","""""""{html}<div><p>There is a feature on the TiBlob.m called imageAsThumbnail. It works but there are no docs about it. An HD ticket is asking for this:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63061"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63061</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Request fot imageAsThumbnail on API docs iOS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There is a feature on the TiBlob.m called imageAsThumbnail. It works but there are no docs about it. An HD ticket is asking for this:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63061"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/63061</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2701,12,"""Regression issue: iPad - Ti 1.5: Textfield and Textareas inside a table cause oddities""","""""""{html}<div><p>A Quickstart customer of ours is having an issue with textfield and textareas inside table rows. When the table loads the textfields and textareas briefly appear to the far left and then get placed in the correct position (it's mal-positioned for a split second). The problem does not happen in 1.4.2 / 1.4.3 - only 1.5 and the latest build of 1.6 (as of today). (using iOS SDK 4.2).</p> <p>I do not have his code yet as a sample to show you so I tried to duplicate it on my end. Below is a video of it happening to me though it is happening when I scroll the table (the customer's issue happens when the table is loaded). In my test, the problem does not happen in 1.4.3 / 1.4.2 but does in 1.5 / 1.6.<br></p> <p>Video: <a href= """"""""http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/afe36c46-8f90-477d-87d4-b49c3f9f2316""""""""> http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/a...</a><br> Code Snippet from my example: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1411262"""""""">http://pastie.org/1411262</a></p> <p>NOTE: In my tests, the problem persists with / without a className in the table. The problem does not occur if there is no table style (group) associated with it. However, in the customer's case, he has 'style: Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.PLAIN' set and the textfield / textarea jump still occurs.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Regression issue: iPad - Ti 1.5: Textfield and Textareas inside a table cause oddities
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A Quickstart customer of ours is having an issue with textfield and textareas inside table rows. When the table loads the textfields and textareas briefly appear to the far left and then get placed in the correct position (it's mal-positioned for a split second). The problem does not happen in 1.4.2 / 1.4.3 - only 1.5 and the latest build of 1.6 (as of today). (using iOS SDK 4.2).</p> <p>I do not have his code yet as a sample to show you so I tried to duplicate it on my end. Below is a video of it happening to me though it is happening when I scroll the table (the customer's issue happens when the table is loaded). In my test, the problem does not happen in 1.4.3 / 1.4.2 but does in 1.5 / 1.6.<br></p> <p>Video: <a href= """"""""http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/afe36c46-8f90-477d-87d4-b49c3f9f2316""""""""> http://www.screencast.com/users/XiDScreencasts/folders/Jing/media/a...</a><br> Code Snippet from my example: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1411262"""""""">http://pastie.org/1411262</a></p> <p>NOTE: In my tests, the problem persists with / without a className in the table. The problem does not occur if there is no table style (group) associated with it. However, in the customer's case, he has 'style: Ti.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.PLAIN' set and the textfield / textarea jump still occurs.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2700,12,"""Android: Spinner-style Picker needs to support more than 3 columns""","""""""{html}<div><p>To match the iPhone capabilities, the (custom) Android version of the Titanium Picker object needs to support the same number of columns, but at least four. It is currently limited to three.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Spinner-style Picker needs to support more than 3 columns
Description: """"{html}<div><p>To match the iPhone capabilities, the (custom) Android version of the Titanium Picker object needs to support the same number of columns, but at least four. It is currently limited to three.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
