Description: """"{html}<div><p>See this HD ticket for explanation:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62611"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62611</a></p> <p>Assigning to Steven as he and I have discussed it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2696,12,"""Andoird: inital tab opened even if not active when call tabgroup.open""","""""""{html}<div><p>sample of my code:</p> <p>tabGroup.addTab(tabSession);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabResults);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabMessages);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabNews);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabSettings);</p> <p>tabGroup.setActiveTab(4);<br> tabGroup.open();</p> <p>tabSettings is opened as expected, but tabSession is opened too. This breaks my application as when tabSession opens it downloads a list. This list is then put into tabSettings instead of tabSession because it is the active window.</p> <p>What I expected, and what happens in iOS, is that tabSettings is opened initially, and tabSession is not, until you click the Sessions tab</p> <p>this is in Titanium Mobile 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Andoird: inital tab opened even if not active when call tabgroup.open
Description: """"{html}<div><p>sample of my code:</p> <p>tabGroup.addTab(tabSession);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabResults);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabMessages);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabNews);<br> tabGroup.addTab(tabSettings);</p> <p>tabGroup.setActiveTab(4);<br> tabGroup.open();</p> <p>tabSettings is opened as expected, but tabSession is opened too. This breaks my application as when tabSession opens it downloads a list. This list is then put into tabSettings instead of tabSession because it is the active window.</p> <p>What I expected, and what happens in iOS, is that tabSettings is opened initially, and tabSession is not, until you click the Sessions tab</p> <p>this is in Titanium Mobile 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2695,12,"""iOS crop property to image views.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Feature request for cropping of images.<br> Several HD tickets are asking for this, most recent one being this one <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62781"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62781</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS crop property to image views.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Feature request for cropping of images.<br> Several HD tickets are asking for this, most recent one being this one <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62781"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62781</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2694,12,"""Android: ImageViews inside a TableView are always fetched async even when using cache""","""""""{html}<div><p>we need to use TiResponseCache.peek() to check for cached images, and set them synchronously instead of incurring the cost of an async download and response job.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageViews inside a TableView are always fetched async even when using cache
Description: """"{html}<div><p>we need to use TiResponseCache.peek() to check for cached images, and set them synchronously instead of incurring the cost of an async download and response job.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2693,12,"""Add background cleanup handlers for termination/suspend""","""""""It looks like there are points in shutdown/suspend where we need to ensure that certain operations are completed (such as  user-defined callbacks, analytics, etc.) We need to ensure that all of these are done before suspend/termination is complete on iOS 4.0+.    In particular, see the comment on this commit: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/3165d74ad25b899f6d820b2ca76352fe13d9001a""""""",Bug,"Title: Add background cleanup handlers for termination/suspend
Description: """"It looks like there are points in shutdown/suspend where we need to ensure that certain operations are completed (such as user-defined callbacks, analytics, etc.) We need to ensure that all of these are done before suspend/termination is complete on iOS 4.0+. In particular, see the comment on this commit: https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/3165d74ad25b899f6d820b2ca76352fe13d9001a""""",title+description
TIMOB-2692,12,"""activeTab undefined""","""""""{html}<div><p>In 1.5.1 and 1.6.0 as of today, the <code>activeTab</code> property of the tab group is undefined after the tab group is initially created. To reproduce, add the following code to a default Titanium-generated project:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> tabGroup.addTab(tab1);   tabGroup.addTab(tab2);   tabGroup.setActiveTab(tab2);  // open tab group tabGroup.open();    Ti.API.info(""""""""tabGroup: """""""" + tabGroup.activeTab);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: activeTab undefined
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In 1.5.1 and 1.6.0 as of today, the <code>activeTab</code> property of the tab group is undefined after the tab group is initially created. To reproduce, add the following code to a default Titanium-generated project:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> tabGroup.addTab(tab1); tabGroup.addTab(tab2); tabGroup.setActiveTab(tab2); // open tab group tabGroup.open(); Ti.API.info(""""""""tabGroup: """""""" + tabGroup.activeTab);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2691,12,"""Gradient on window""","""""""{html}<div><p>Someone suggested I post this as a bug. I switched my code to  using an Image vs a Gradient and I'm ok for now. I'd still like to  find a solution.</p>  <p>Here is the post outlining the issue:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/94291/controls-created-from-sub-window"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/94291/controls-created-f...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Gradient on window
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Someone suggested I post this as a bug. I switched my code to using an Image vs a Gradient and I'm ok for now. I'd still like to find a solution.</p> <p>Here is the post outlining the issue:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/94291/controls-created-from-sub-window""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/94291/controls-created-f...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2690,12,"""Tooling: new projects don't add .gitignore to ignore autogenerated *.pyc files""","""""""{html}<div><p>This means that pyc files can easily be inadvertently added to versioning control, and consequently cause annoyance when switching branches (as changes must be resolved/stashed/committed) before switching.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Tooling: new projects don't add .gitignore to ignore autogenerated *.pyc files
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This means that pyc files can easily be inadvertently added to versioning control, and consequently cause annoyance when switching branches (as changes must be resolved/stashed/committed) before switching.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
