TIMOB-2678,12,"""Android: 2.3, new UI feedback - New yellow flash to denote scroll end ( was - when scrolling tabs to end - scrollable tab + many on a screen""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.5.1 + hvga skinned 2.3 emulator</p> <p>1.Base UI&gt; Views &gt;scrolling tabs<br> 2. grab either scroll tab and the scroll the contents to end</p> <p>many on a screen, scroll the views around. note the yellow affect is not rounded as the view is. this may be a cosmetic bug if the beahvior is now as expected.</p> <p>results: there is a new visual yellow gradient, possibly intentional?</p> <p>see it on all table views by scrolling to end.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: 2.3, new UI feedback - New yellow flash to denote scroll end ( was - when scrolling tabs to end - scrollable tab + many on a screen
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.5.1 + hvga skinned 2.3 emulator</p> <p>1.Base UI&gt; Views &gt;scrolling tabs<br> 2. grab either scroll tab and the scroll the contents to end</p> <p>many on a screen, scroll the views around. note the yellow affect is not rounded as the view is. this may be a cosmetic bug if the beahvior is now as expected.</p> <p>results: there is a new visual yellow gradient, possibly intentional?</p> <p>see it on all table views by scrolling to end.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2677,12,"""Android: TableView rows don't update recursively""","""""""{html}<div><p>When a row's views are updated via proxy, they don't seem to be updated recursively.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TableView rows don't update recursively
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When a row's views are updated via proxy, they don't seem to be updated recursively.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2676,12,"""Titanium Mobile Android HttpClient Unable to Handle 204 Error Code""","""""""The Android HttpClient module in 1.5.1 is unable to handle a missing entity. This is possible when encountering a 204 HTTP status code (no content).    The following is stated in the Apache HttpClient """"""""http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/HttpEntity.html"""""""" Java API doc:    """"""""An entity that can be sent or received with an HTTP message. Entities can be found in some requests and in responses, where they are optional.""""""""    Currently lines 203 - 208 in TiHTTPClient.java assume that any status code less then 300 will have an entity. However this is not true. Other codes may not. This includes 204 (no content) and 201 (created).    Requests made that result in these response codes will currently result in null pointer exceptions when executing line 209:        The iPhone version does not appear to suffer from the same issue.""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium Mobile Android HttpClient Unable to Handle 204 Error Code
Description: """"The Android HttpClient module in 1.5.1 is unable to handle a missing entity. This is possible when encountering a 204 HTTP status code (no content). The following is stated in the Apache HttpClient """"""""http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/HttpEntity.html"""""""" Java API doc: """"""""An entity that can be sent or received with an HTTP message. Entities can be found in some requests and in responses, where they are optional."""""""" Currently lines 203 - 208 in TiHTTPClient.java assume that any status code less then 300 will have an entity. However this is not true. Other codes may not. This includes 204 (no content) and 201 (created). Requests made that result in these response codes will currently result in null pointer exceptions when executing line 209: The iPhone version does not appear to suffer from the same issue.""""",title+description
TIMOB-2675,12,"""Can't set Content-Type request header""","""""""{html}<div><p>Self-explanitory. Sample code from <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1983"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1983"""""""">#1983</a>:</p> <pre> <code>var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function() {        Ti.API.info('I am in utf-8 onload for POST'); }; xhr.onerror = function() {        Ti.API.info('I am in utf-8 error for POST'); }; xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""setoutside"""""""", """"""""one""""""""); xhr.open(""""""""POST"""""""",""""""""http://api.localmedia.fm/files/endpoint_webform.cfm""""""""); xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""content-type"""""""", """"""""multipart/form-data""""""""); xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""setinside"""""""", """"""""two""""""""); xhr.send({""""""""a"""""""":""""""""hi"""""""", """"""""b"""""""":""""""""there""""""""});</code> </pre> <p>The response is always:</p> <pre> <code>Content-Type     application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=utf-8</code> </pre> <p>Should be considered part of the XHR refactor.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Can't set Content-Type request header
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Self-explanitory. Sample code from <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1983"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1983"""""""">#1983</a>:</p> <pre> <code>var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function() { Ti.API.info('I am in utf-8 onload for POST'); }; xhr.onerror = function() { Ti.API.info('I am in utf-8 error for POST'); }; xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""setoutside"""""""", """"""""one""""""""); xhr.open(""""""""POST"""""""",""""""""http://api.localmedia.fm/files/endpoint_webform.cfm""""""""); xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""content-type"""""""", """"""""multipart/form-data""""""""); xhr.setRequestHeader(""""""""setinside"""""""", """"""""two""""""""); xhr.send({""""""""a"""""""":""""""""hi"""""""", """"""""b"""""""":""""""""there""""""""});</code> </pre> <p>The response is always:</p> <pre> <code>Content-Type application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=utf-8</code> </pre> <p>Should be considered part of the XHR refactor.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2674,12,"""iOS: transport.py for Xcode compile errors""","""""""{html}<div><p>References:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/LTZ-54399-431"""""""">http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/LTZ-54399-431</a></p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/RXZ-87893-642"""""""">http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/RXZ-87893-642</a></p>  <p>Custom modules are not being packaged in the transport.py  script.</p>  <p>Users receiving the package are still having problems building  the project without installing Titanium.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: transport.py for Xcode compile errors
Description: """"{html}<div><p>References:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/LTZ-54399-431"""""""">http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/LTZ-54399-431</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/RXZ-87893-642"""""""">http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/RXZ-87893-642</a></p> <p>Custom modules are not being packaged in the transport.py script.</p> <p>Users receiving the package are still having problems building the project without installing Titanium.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2673,12,"""iPhone Map: Adding regionChanged listener causes map region to change""","""""""{html}<div><p>When creating a map view, if you add a regionChanged listener then it changes the displayed region, as illustrated by <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/77481/map-region-doesnt-fit-in-mapview-of-titanium-when-catch-event-regionchanged""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/77481/map-region-doesnt-...</a></p> <p>This is because when firing the event the code alters the region object when it should simply read it.<br> TiMapView.m in the github master as of today reads (around line 516):</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""objc"""""""">if ([self.proxy _hasListeners:@""""""""regionChanged""""""""])     {         region = [mapView region];</code> </pre> <p>It should not be modifying the region instance variable, so simply changing this line to read <code>MKCoordinateRegion region = [mapView region];</code> solves the problem.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone Map: Adding regionChanged listener causes map region to change
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When creating a map view, if you add a regionChanged listener then it changes the displayed region, as illustrated by <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/77481/map-region-doesnt-fit-in-mapview-of-titanium-when-catch-event-regionchanged""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/77481/map-region-doesnt-...</a></p> <p>This is because when firing the event the code alters the region object when it should simply read it.<br> TiMapView.m in the github master as of today reads (around line 516):</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""objc"""""""">if ([self.proxy _hasListeners:@""""""""regionChanged""""""""]) { region = [mapView region];</code> </pre> <p>It should not be modifying the region instance variable, so simply changing this line to read <code>MKCoordinateRegion region = [mapView region];</code> solves the problem.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2671,12,"""poor performance when table view row has image background""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have tried sdk 1.4.3, 1.5.2 and 1.6 on iPhone, they all showed poor performance when table view row has image background. My table has about 100 rows ( actually, it is kind of slow when it has only 20 rows too), each row has a nice image as its background. I set rowclass, prepopulated the rows into an array then set it to tableData, it is fast in simulator (of course it is fast with 12 CPUs), but it took 5 seconds even in iPhone 4. I ended up with a trick, I only set 8 rows to tableData first (user can only see first 8 anyway), then append the rest of rows to tableview with a setTimeout function. It kind of works in iPhone 4, but not good in older version of device.</p> <p>I would really appreciate you look into this performance issue, since table view is most widely used UI widget.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: poor performance when table view row has image background
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have tried sdk 1.4.3, 1.5.2 and 1.6 on iPhone, they all showed poor performance when table view row has image background. My table has about 100 rows ( actually, it is kind of slow when it has only 20 rows too), each row has a nice image as its background. I set rowclass, prepopulated the rows into an array then set it to tableData, it is fast in simulator (of course it is fast with 12 CPUs), but it took 5 seconds even in iPhone 4. I ended up with a trick, I only set 8 rows to tableData first (user can only see first 8 anyway), then append the rest of rows to tableview with a setTimeout function. It kind of works in iPhone 4, but not good in older version of device.</p> <p>I would really appreciate you look into this performance issue, since table view is most widely used UI widget.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2670,12,"""iOS:UI - searchBar barColor property not supported""","""""""h2. Problem    barColor of the searchBar is black when it's loaded to the first time, even if barColor isn't empty.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript}  var searchBar = Ti.UI.createSearchBar({    barColor:'#f90',    height:43,    top:0,    visible:true  });  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS:UI - searchBar barColor property not supported
Description: """"h2. Problem barColor of the searchBar is black when it's loaded to the first time, even if barColor isn't empty. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript} var searchBar = Ti.UI.createSearchBar({ barColor:'#f90', height:43, top:0, visible:true }); {code} """"",title+description
