TIMOB-2668,12,"""Android: Tableview Click Event Missing Properties""","""""""{html}<div><p>Commit <a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/3ffe548cf7e1e12bf55f82aecf3860ab66e9c8c3/android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/tableview/TiTableView.java""""""""> 3ffe548c</a> removed several event properties that are expected and documented. The previous commit <a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/e18980e31ba5c0e061da3ababd711467471bffeb/android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/tableview/TiTableView.java""""""""> e18980e</a> is sending the correct properties.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62621"""""""">Helpdesk 62621</a></p> <p>This needs to go on the 1_5_X branch as well.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tableview Click Event Missing Properties
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Commit <a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/3ffe548cf7e1e12bf55f82aecf3860ab66e9c8c3/android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/tableview/TiTableView.java""""""""> 3ffe548c</a> removed several event properties that are expected and documented. The previous commit <a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/e18980e31ba5c0e061da3ababd711467471bffeb/android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/tableview/TiTableView.java""""""""> e18980e</a> is sending the correct properties.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62621"""""""">Helpdesk 62621</a></p> <p>This needs to go on the 1_5_X branch as well.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2667,12,"""Problem displaying image from Google Maps API (Android)""","""""""{html}<div><p>On the emulators I have tried (1.5.1 on APIs 2.2, 2.1, and 1.6) the following code is causing a crash:</p> <pre> <code>var window = Titanium.UI.createWindow({fullscreen: false});   var imageMap = Titanium.UI.createImageView({     image: """"""""http://maps.google.com/maps/api/staticmap?center=11.5558762589,104.921697935&amp;zoom=13&amp;size=250x70&amp;maptype=roadmap&amp;markers=color:green|11.5558762589,104.921697935&amp;sensor=false"""""""",     height: 90,     width: 200,     borderColor: """"""""#FFF"""""""" });  window.add(imageMap); window.open();</code> </pre> <p>Paste in an app.js file to recreate the error. Image seems to load up fine in the browser.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Problem displaying image from Google Maps API (Android)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On the emulators I have tried (1.5.1 on APIs 2.2, 2.1, and 1.6) the following code is causing a crash:</p> <pre> <code>var window = Titanium.UI.createWindow({fullscreen: false}); var imageMap = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ image: """"""""http://maps.google.com/maps/api/staticmap?center=11.5558762589,104.921697935&amp;zoom=13&amp;size=250x70&amp;maptype=roadmap&amp;markers=color:green|11.5558762589,104.921697935&amp;sensor=false"""""""", height: 90, width: 200, borderColor: """"""""#FFF"""""""" }); window.add(imageMap); window.open();</code> </pre> <p>Paste in an app.js file to recreate the error. Image seems to load up fine in the browser.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2666,12,"""tiapp.xml configuration not respected""","""""""{html}<div><p>For iOS, many of the standard tiapp.xml configuration parameters are being ignored:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;icon&gt;appicon2.png&lt;/icon&gt; &lt;prerendered-icon&gt;true&lt;/prerendered-icon&gt; &lt;statusbar-style&gt;black&lt;/statusbar-style&gt; &lt;statusbar-hidden&gt;true&lt;/statusbar-hidden&gt; &lt;fullscreen&gt;true&lt;/fullscreen&gt; &lt;navbar-hidden&gt;true&lt;/navbar-hidden&gt;</code> </pre> <p>This will preclude any application from specifying these parameters without hacking the generated projects. I have reproduced this in a brand new 1.5.1 project and in an existing project I updated to 1.5.1.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: tiapp.xml configuration not respected
Description: """"{html}<div><p>For iOS, many of the standard tiapp.xml configuration parameters are being ignored:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;icon&gt;appicon2.png&lt;/icon&gt; &lt;prerendered-icon&gt;true&lt;/prerendered-icon&gt; &lt;statusbar-style&gt;black&lt;/statusbar-style&gt; &lt;statusbar-hidden&gt;true&lt;/statusbar-hidden&gt; &lt;fullscreen&gt;true&lt;/fullscreen&gt; &lt;navbar-hidden&gt;true&lt;/navbar-hidden&gt;</code> </pre> <p>This will preclude any application from specifying these parameters without hacking the generated projects. I have reproduced this in a brand new 1.5.1 project and in an existing project I updated to 1.5.1.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2665,12,"""Using semi-color or double quotes in Description returns error""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using a semi-color or double quotes in project description (in Titanium Developer 1.2.2) throws an error during build and forces the application to quit when it runs.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Using semi-color or double quotes in Description returns error
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using a semi-color or double quotes in project description (in Titanium Developer 1.2.2) throws an error during build and forces the application to quit when it runs.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2664,12,"""setTimeout(0) on xhr on iOS does not make it not timeout""","""""""{html}<div><p>When using setTimeout(0) on an xhr call, this should not timeout. Currently this does not happen. After talking with Steven, he says it will never be 100% reliable but we can get it close.</p> <p>HD Ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57451"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57451</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: setTimeout(0) on xhr on iOS does not make it not timeout
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When using setTimeout(0) on an xhr call, this should not timeout. Currently this does not happen. After talking with Steven, he says it will never be 100% reliable but we can get it close.</p> <p>HD Ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57451"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57451</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2663,12,"""Android: Opacity problem""","""""""{html}<div><h3>Problem#1:</h3>  <p>When initializing an object (such as a view) and setting its'  opacity to 0 initially (e.g. opacity: 0), then changing it using  obj.animate(opacity: 0.6, duration: 1) yields no result. For  example:</p>  <pre>  <code>var viewObj = Ti.UI.createView({      // other properties      opacity: 0  });    // inside some handler; onClick if we try changing opacity  viewObj.animate({      opacity: 0.6,      duration: 1  });    // yeilds no result</code>  </pre>  <h3>Problem#2:</h3>  <p>Changing the opacity with direct assignment or using the  """"""""setOpacity"""""""" method doesn't update the object with the new opacity,  but outputting it on to the console shows the opacity property has  been changed however.</p>  <p>For more information kindly refer to this thread; <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/92891/android-setopacity-problem"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/92891/android-setopacity...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Opacity problem
Description: """"{html}<div><h3>Problem#1:</h3> <p>When initializing an object (such as a view) and setting its' opacity to 0 initially (e.g. opacity: 0), then changing it using obj.animate(opacity: 0.6, duration: 1) yields no result. For example:</p> <pre> <code>var viewObj = Ti.UI.createView({ // other properties opacity: 0 }); // inside some handler; onClick if we try changing opacity viewObj.animate({ opacity: 0.6, duration: 1 }); // yeilds no result</code> </pre> <h3>Problem#2:</h3> <p>Changing the opacity with direct assignment or using the """"""""setOpacity"""""""" method doesn't update the object with the new opacity, but outputting it on to the console shows the opacity property has been changed however.</p> <p>For more information kindly refer to this thread; <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/92891/android-setopacity-problem""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/92891/android-setopacity...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2661,12,"""android : regression with responseXML from 1.2.0 to 1.5.1 - slow XML parsing""","""""""{html}<div><p>an XML with 100 rows (on iphone xml parsing is very fast)</p> <p>on android &amp; SDK1.2.0 only 1 second to enter the loop (and seeing the actInd.message = 'loading : '+x+'/'+items.length;)<br> with SDK1.5.1 it can take up to 20 seconds.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var actInd = Titanium.UI.createActivityIndicator({message:'Waiting...'}); actInd.show();  var xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""",""""""""distant_XML""""""""); xhr.onload = function() {     try     {         var doc = this.responseXML.documentElement;         var items = doc.getElementsByTagName(""""""""tag"""""""");         var x = 0;         for (var c=0;c&lt;items.length;c++)         {                 actInd.message = 'loading : '+x+'/'+items.length;         }                        }     catch(E){} };  xhr.send();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: android : regression with responseXML from 1.2.0 to 1.5.1 - slow XML parsing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>an XML with 100 rows (on iphone xml parsing is very fast)</p> <p>on android &amp; SDK1.2.0 only 1 second to enter the loop (and seeing the actInd.message = 'loading : '+x+'/'+items.length;)<br> with SDK1.5.1 it can take up to 20 seconds.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var actInd = Titanium.UI.createActivityIndicator({message:'Waiting...'}); actInd.show(); var xhr = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.open(""""""""GET"""""""",""""""""distant_XML""""""""); xhr.onload = function() { try { var doc = this.responseXML.documentElement; var items = doc.getElementsByTagName(""""""""tag""""""""); var x = 0; for (var c=0;c&lt;items.length;c++) { actInd.message = 'loading : '+x+'/'+items.length; } } catch(E){} }; xhr.send();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2660,12,"""Android 2.3, model - when closing modal window button is removed before window is dismissed""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.5.1 and 2.3 emulator, KS</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt;window standalone<br> 2.Open (Nav Bar Covered) or open full screen<br> 3.hit close on the resulting window, wathc the button</p> <p>results: the button dissapears before the window is dismisses - see the orphaned """"""""close"""""""" label before the window dismisses</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android 2.3, model - when closing modal window button is removed before window is dismissed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.5.1 and 2.3 emulator, KS</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt;window standalone<br> 2.Open (Nav Bar Covered) or open full screen<br> 3.hit close on the resulting window, wathc the button</p> <p>results: the button dissapears before the window is dismisses - see the orphaned """"""""close"""""""" label before the window dismisses</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2659,12,"""Android: 2.3 emulator crashes while loading some image view tests""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using shipping 1.5.1 and 2.3 emulator, running KS</p> <p>basic image test crash<br> 1.Base UI&gt; Views &gt; image view<br> also remote view</p> <p>results: crash</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1399143"""""""">http://pastie.org/1399143</a></p> <p>E/TiUncaughtHandler( 527): java.lang.RuntimeException: An error occured while executing doInBackground()</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: 2.3 emulator crashes while loading some image view tests
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using shipping 1.5.1 and 2.3 emulator, running KS</p> <p>basic image test crash<br> 1.Base UI&gt; Views &gt; image view<br> also remote view</p> <p>results: crash</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1399143"""""""">http://pastie.org/1399143</a></p> <p>E/TiUncaughtHandler( 527): java.lang.RuntimeException: An error occured while executing doInBackground()</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2658,12,"""Crash on app resume""","""""""{html}<div><p>Under certain (very rare) circumstances, apps will crash upon resume. This appears to be because in iOS 4.0, an app may still be in the """"""""terminating"""""""" state when it is re-resumed if the system determined that it should be shut down. If the app is locked and waiting on the main thread for a response, this may cause the OS to terminate the app for not responding in time when resuming.</p> <p>The issue appears to come from -[AnalyticsModule shutdown:], where an HTTP request is scheduled on the main thread. Marking medium because it's such a weird corner case and hard to reproduce.</p> <p>Bug may not be reproducible enough to reliably test a fix. This one is 100% crash log.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Crash on app resume
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Under certain (very rare) circumstances, apps will crash upon resume. This appears to be because in iOS 4.0, an app may still be in the """"""""terminating"""""""" state when it is re-resumed if the system determined that it should be shut down. If the app is locked and waiting on the main thread for a response, this may cause the OS to terminate the app for not responding in time when resuming.</p> <p>The issue appears to come from -[AnalyticsModule shutdown:], where an HTTP request is scheduled on the main thread. Marking medium because it's such a weird corner case and hard to reproduce.</p> <p>Bug may not be reproducible enough to reliably test a fix. This one is 100% crash log.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2657,12,"""modal window + navBarHidden: true = Bug""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ok so I found a bug on the iphone, havent tested on droid.</p> <p>When opening a modal window, if the windows navBarHidden property is set to true, opening it the first time is fine. After closing it and reopening it, the modal window shows up behind the phones status bar at the top (where the signal, clock etc is).</p> <p>I've attached a zip file of a very basic demo showing the bug.</p> <p>Import the new project and compile. I've left the navBarHidden property set to false (in app.js on var activity) so you can see how it SHOULD behave.</p> <p>Once you open and close the modal window a few times, open up app.js and change the navBarHidden property to true on var activity. Then open and close the modal window a couple times and you will see the second time and any time after that, it goes behind the status bar.</p> <p>I am using iphone sdk 4.2 and Ti sdk 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: modal window + navBarHidden: true = Bug
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ok so I found a bug on the iphone, havent tested on droid.</p> <p>When opening a modal window, if the windows navBarHidden property is set to true, opening it the first time is fine. After closing it and reopening it, the modal window shows up behind the phones status bar at the top (where the signal, clock etc is).</p> <p>I've attached a zip file of a very basic demo showing the bug.</p> <p>Import the new project and compile. I've left the navBarHidden property set to false (in app.js on var activity) so you can see how it SHOULD behave.</p> <p>Once you open and close the modal window a few times, open up app.js and change the navBarHidden property to true on var activity. Then open and close the modal window a couple times and you will see the second time and any time after that, it goes behind the status bar.</p> <p>I am using iphone sdk 4.2 and Ti sdk 1.5.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2656,12,"""Problem with redirects on POST""","""""""{html}<div><hr> <p>Reported by <USER>| October 26th, 2010 @ 08:52 AM | in 1.2.0</p> <p>Hi,</p> <p>I'm using createHTTPClient to POST to a page. I receive a 302. Titanium seems to follow through the 302 with another POST, not a GET.</p> <p>Any idea why it's that way ? Is it a bug ?</p> <h2>Thanks.</h2> <p>I'm filing this ticket for <USER>as it was in Desktop, and it is a Mobile issue which still exists on the 1.5.1 Mobile SDK.</p> <p><USER>did test and verify it on the 1.5.1 SDK for me. I'm assigning this to Marshall, but feel free to move to anyone else.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Problem with redirects on POST
Description: """"{html}<div><hr> <p>Reported by <USER>| October 26th, 2010 @ 08:52 AM | in 1.2.0</p> <p>Hi,</p> <p>I'm using createHTTPClient to POST to a page. I receive a 302. Titanium seems to follow through the 302 with another POST, not a GET.</p> <p>Any idea why it's that way ? Is it a bug ?</p> <h2>Thanks.</h2> <p>I'm filing this ticket for <USER>as it was in Desktop, and it is a Mobile issue which still exists on the 1.5.1 Mobile SDK.</p> <p><USER>did test and verify it on the 1.5.1 SDK for me. I'm assigning this to Marshall, but feel free to move to anyone else.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2655,12,"""Dragging Between TableViewSections in iOS Crashes if new Section has no Rows""","""""""{html}<div><p>Several issues presently exist with dragging between sections in  a TableView in iOS (I have not tested this issue in Android).</p>  <ul>  <li>Create a UITableView with the """"""""GROUPED"""""""" iOS style and give it  multiple sections.</li>  <li>Populate one or more of the sections with rows, leave at least  one empty.</li>  <li>Enable editing mode on the TableView (giving it  dragability)</li>  <li>Drag a row from a populated section to the section that has no  rows.</li>  </ul>  <p>== First Problem ==</p>  <p>*** Terminating app due to uncaught exception  'NSInternalInconsistencyException', reason: 'Invalid update:  invalid number of rows in section 1. The number of rows contained  in an existing section after the update (0) must be equal to the  number of rows contained in that section before the update (2),  plus or minus the number of rows inserted or deleted from that  section (0 inserted, 0 deleted).</p>  <p>This exception is thrown when I have 3 sections, one that has 4  rows and the other two empty. I can drag a row from the top  (populated) section down to the middle section and that error is  thrown. I can not drag a row to the bottom section.</p>  <p>== Second Problem ==</p>  <p><strong><em>Terminating app due to uncaught exception  'NSRangeException', reason: '</em></strong> -[NSMutableArray  objectAtIndex:]: index 1 beyond bounds [0 .. 0]'</p>  <p>This exception is thrown when I have any number of sections,  populated or not, and drag a row from one section to the BOTTOM of  another section. Dragging a row to the top or center or any other  row but the bottom results in no errors.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Dragging Between TableViewSections in iOS Crashes if new Section has no Rows
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Several issues presently exist with dragging between sections in a TableView in iOS (I have not tested this issue in Android).</p> <ul> <li>Create a UITableView with the """"""""GROUPED"""""""" iOS style and give it multiple sections.</li> <li>Populate one or more of the sections with rows, leave at least one empty.</li> <li>Enable editing mode on the TableView (giving it dragability)</li> <li>Drag a row from a populated section to the section that has no rows.</li> </ul> <p>== First Problem ==</p> <p>*** Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'NSInternalInconsistencyException', reason: 'Invalid update: invalid number of rows in section 1. The number of rows contained in an existing section after the update (0) must be equal to the number of rows contained in that section before the update (2), plus or minus the number of rows inserted or deleted from that section (0 inserted, 0 deleted).</p> <p>This exception is thrown when I have 3 sections, one that has 4 rows and the other two empty. I can drag a row from the top (populated) section down to the middle section and that error is thrown. I can not drag a row to the bottom section.</p> <p>== Second Problem ==</p> <p><strong><em>Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'NSRangeException', reason: '</em></strong> -[NSMutableArray objectAtIndex:]: index 1 beyond bounds [0 .. 0]'</p> <p>This exception is thrown when I have any number of sections, populated or not, and drag a row from one section to the BOTTOM of another section. Dragging a row to the top or center or any other row but the bottom results in no errors.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2654,12,"""Android: HTTPClient Events Do Not Provide Event Source""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62281"""""""">Helpdesk</a></p> <p>Basically,</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">xhr.onload = function(e) {     Ti.API.error(""""""""Received request for property: """"""""+ e.source.someProperty); };</code> </pre> <p><code>e.source</code> is <code>undefined</code></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient Events Do Not Provide Event Source
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/62281"""""""">Helpdesk</a></p> <p>Basically,</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">xhr.onload = function(e) { Ti.API.error(""""""""Received request for property: """"""""+ e.source.someProperty); };</code> </pre> <p><code>e.source</code> is <code>undefined</code></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2652,12,"""iOS: tableView's index not working without headers""","""""""{html}<div><p>Problem:</p>  <p>Having an index in a tableView whose rows lack the header  attribute breaks the index: all items in the index will point to  the top of the table.</p>  <p>How to reproduce:</p>  <p>In KitchenSink's  KitchenSink/Resources/examples/table_view_headers_filter.js remove  all """"""""header"""""""" attributes in the data array, like this <a href=  """"""""http://www.pastie.org/1396915"""""""">http://www.pastie.org/1396915</a>  and compile.</p>  <p>Ugly workaround:</p>  <p>To assign assign the header attribute as an empty string in all  rows.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: tableView's index not working without headers
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Problem:</p> <p>Having an index in a tableView whose rows lack the header attribute breaks the index: all items in the index will point to the top of the table.</p> <p>How to reproduce:</p> <p>In KitchenSink's KitchenSink/Resources/examples/table_view_headers_filter.js remove all """"""""header"""""""" attributes in the data array, like this <a href= """"""""http://www.pastie.org/1396915"""""""">http://www.pastie.org/1396915</a> and compile.</p> <p>Ugly workaround:</p> <p>To assign assign the header attribute as an empty string in all rows.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
