TIMOB-2643,12,"""ScrollableView default values - regression""","""""""{html}<div><p>On TiMobile 1.5.1, if I set the property showPagingControl to true, the pagingControlHeight require to be set to 20 to be displayed.</p> <p>The documentation specify """"""""the height in pixels of the paging control, if visible. defaults to 20"""""""".</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ScrollableView default values - regression
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On TiMobile 1.5.1, if I set the property showPagingControl to true, the pagingControlHeight require to be set to 20 to be displayed.</p> <p>The documentation specify """"""""the height in pixels of the paging control, if visible. defaults to 20"""""""".</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2642,12,"""Android : Kroll get method for properties does not work correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>Kroll get method returns undefined due to the """"""""get"""""""" name check in KrollBindingUtils.java : createAccessorMethod never actually being passed when a get method is invoked. The name that is checked for either """"""""get"""""""" or """"""""set"""""""" is actually the name of the property without either of the prefixed modifiers.</p> <p>The """"""""get"""""""" check always fails so the execution passes to the """"""""set"""""""" block and so set calls work correctly. When a get call is made, a null value is returned because the set logic is executed but no argument is passed in for a new value like a real set call would contain.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : Kroll get method for properties does not work correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Kroll get method returns undefined due to the """"""""get"""""""" name check in KrollBindingUtils.java : createAccessorMethod never actually being passed when a get method is invoked. The name that is checked for either """"""""get"""""""" or """"""""set"""""""" is actually the name of the property without either of the prefixed modifiers.</p> <p>The """"""""get"""""""" check always fails so the execution passes to the """"""""set"""""""" block and so set calls work correctly. When a get call is made, a null value is returned because the set logic is executed but no argument is passed in for a new value like a real set call would contain.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2641,12,"""WebView.reload() breaks fireEvent/listener connection ""","""""""{html}<div><p>I encounter some weird behavior and found there was a previous issue concerning <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/58681/android-tiappfireevent-looses-connection-to-event-listener"""""""" title=""""""""WebView.url(newUrl)"""""""">WebView.url(newUrl)</a>.</p> <p>When I call WebView.reload() after a screen rotation (else the WebView doesn't resize it's content) then the connection is broken.</p> <p>More info about what happens:<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">    function openDocument(docURL) {<br> <br>   </code> </pre> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript""""""""><code>    alert('webview click received // ' + docURL);     Ti.App.fireEvent('customOpenDocument', {url:docURL});     alert('webview click received CALL ENDED'); };&lt;/code&gt;</code></code> </pre> <pre>   <br> </pre> The first alert shows up. But I never receive the fired event, and the 2nd alert doesn't show up. However I no reload() was previously called, then the event is received and the 2nd alert show. <p>SDK 1.5.1 / iPad</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: WebView.reload() breaks fireEvent/listener connection
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I encounter some weird behavior and found there was a previous issue concerning <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/58681/android-tiappfireevent-looses-connection-to-event-listener"""""""" title=""""""""WebView.url(newUrl)"""""""">WebView.url(newUrl)</a>.</p> <p>When I call WebView.reload() after a screen rotation (else the WebView doesn't resize it's content) then the connection is broken.</p> <p>More info about what happens:<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> function openDocument(docURL) {<br> <br> </code> </pre> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript""""""""><code> alert('webview click received // ' + docURL); Ti.App.fireEvent('customOpenDocument', {url:docURL}); alert('webview click received CALL ENDED'); };&lt;/code&gt;</code></code> </pre> <pre> <br> </pre> The first alert shows up. But I never receive the fired event, and the 2nd alert doesn't show up. However I no reload() was previously called, then the event is received and the 2nd alert show. <p>SDK 1.5.1 / iPad</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2640,12,"""creating and opening a second tabgroup on android fails. ""","""""""{html}<div><p>creating and opening a second tabgroup on android fails.</p> <p>reference app:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/61231#c280711"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/61231#c280711</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: creating and opening a second tabgroup on android fails.
