TIMOB-2576,12,"""iOS: Calendar control""","""""""{html}<div><p>It is possible to have a Calendar control?</p>  <p>In a lot of situations it would be better to pick a date from a  month view (like the native calendar in iPhone's Agenda) than from  the date picker.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Calendar control
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It is possible to have a Calendar control?</p> <p>In a lot of situations it would be better to pick a date from a month view (like the native calendar in iPhone's Agenda) than from the date picker.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2575,12,"""APIDoc: Introduce language type for <code> sections in docgen.py""","""""""{html}<div><p>The guess_lexer() function in pygments doesn't seem to guess the right language in all situations. It might be best to explicitly set each code section with a """"""""type"""""""" attribute and just pass along to pygments.lexers.get_lexer_by_name</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: APIDoc: Introduce language type for <code> sections in docgen.py
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The guess_lexer() function in pygments doesn't seem to guess the right language in all situations. It might be best to explicitly set each code section with a """"""""type"""""""" attribute and just pass along to pygments.lexers.get_lexer_by_name</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2574,12,"""iOS: Expose verticalAlign for Labels""","""""""h2. Problem    The same way it is possible to do Vertical Alignment with TextFields, it wold be great to have the property verticalAlign: on Labels as well    verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_TOP  verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_MIDDLE  verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_BOTTOM    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({   backgroundColor: 'black',   exitOnClose: true,   fullscreen: false,   layout: 'vertical',   title: 'Label verticalAlign Demo'  });    var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({   backgroundColor: 'white',   color: 'black',   text: 'this is a test',   verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_BOTTOM,   height: 100  });  win.add(label);  win.open();  {code}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Expose verticalAlign for Labels
Description: """"h2. Problem The same way it is possible to do Vertical Alignment with TextFields, it wold be great to have the property verticalAlign: on Labels as well verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_TOP verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_MIDDLE verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_BOTTOM h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'black', exitOnClose: true, fullscreen: false, layout: 'vertical', title: 'Label verticalAlign Demo' }); var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ backgroundColor: 'white', color: 'black', text: 'this is a test', verticalAlign:Ti.UI.TEXT_VERTICAL_ALIGNMENT_BOTTOM, height: 100 }); win.add(label); win.open(); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2573,12,"""HttpClient drops properties while doing a callback""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is actually due to a compromise in order to reduce memory issues due to recursive XHR call chains, as we intentionally jettison the request holding the internal data. This will be fixed in the great XHR refactor.</p> <p>To recreate:</p> <pre> <code>var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function(e){     Ti.API.info('onload');     Ti.API.info(xhr.location);     // Ti.API.info(xhr.responseText); }; xhr.onerror = function(e){     Ti.API.info('onerror');     // Ti.API.info(xhr.responseText); }; xhr.open('GET','http://www.motorsport-total.com/f1/live/htdocs/ticker.php'); xhr.send();</code> </pre> <p>Expected result:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] test/1.0 (1.5.1_9819ce0_13122010.9819ce0) [INFO] onload [INFO] http://www.motorsport-total.com/f1/live/htdocs/ticker.php?strecken_id=19&amp;event_id=7&amp;kunde=default</code> </pre> <p>Actual result:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] test/1.0 (1.5.1_9819ce0_13122010.9819ce0) [INFO] onload [INFO] &lt;null&gt;</code> </pre> <p>Workaround:</p> <p>Use this.location and this.responseText.</p> <p>Credit to <USER>for the sample code.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: HttpClient drops properties while doing a callback
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is actually due to a compromise in order to reduce memory issues due to recursive XHR call chains, as we intentionally jettison the request holding the internal data. This will be fixed in the great XHR refactor.</p> <p>To recreate:</p> <pre> <code>var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function(e){ Ti.API.info('onload'); Ti.API.info(xhr.location); // Ti.API.info(xhr.responseText); }; xhr.onerror = function(e){ Ti.API.info('onerror'); // Ti.API.info(xhr.responseText); }; xhr.open('GET','http://www.motorsport-total.com/f1/live/htdocs/ticker.php'); xhr.send();</code> </pre> <p>Expected result:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] test/1.0 (1.5.1_9819ce0_13122010.9819ce0) [INFO] onload [INFO] http://www.motorsport-total.com/f1/live/htdocs/ticker.php?strecken_id=19&amp;event_id=7&amp;kunde=default</code> </pre> <p>Actual result:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] test/1.0 (1.5.1_9819ce0_13122010.9819ce0) [INFO] onload [INFO] &lt;null&gt;</code> </pre> <p>Workaround:</p> <p>Use this.location and this.responseText.</p> <p>Credit to <USER>for the sample code.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2572,12,"""iOS: View positioning doesn't work in camera overlay""","""""""{html}<div><p>See the developer center post: <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/58051/dynamic-adjusting-position-of-views-inside-camera-overlay-view"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/58051/dynamic-adjusting-...</a></p>  <p>Exactly as described. Behavior can be seen by modifying the  camera_overlay.js test to mod the box by a size or boundary  constraint upon taking the picture. Presumably has to do with (1)  the proxy not having a proper 'parent' and (2) thus no bounding  box.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: View positioning doesn't work in camera overlay
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See the developer center post: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/58051/dynamic-adjusting-position-of-views-inside-camera-overlay-view""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/58051/dynamic-adjusting-...</a></p> <p>Exactly as described. Behavior can be seen by modifying the camera_overlay.js test to mod the box by a size or boundary constraint upon taking the picture. Presumably has to do with (1) the proxy not having a proper 'parent' and (2) thus no bounding box.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2571,12,"""Dashboard view should be available for Android platform ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently the Titanium.UI.DashboardView API is not available for the android platform. To help increase platform independance it would be great if this could be implemented for 'droid. It's certainly possible to create using simple views but that means I still need to add some if/elses checking the platform type in my controllers.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Dashboard view should be available for Android platform
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently the Titanium.UI.DashboardView API is not available for the android platform. To help increase platform independance it would be great if this could be implemented for 'droid. It's certainly possible to create using simple views but that means I still need to add some if/elses checking the platform type in my controllers.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2570,12,"""JSS files are not properly rebuilt when launching emulator""","""""""{html}<div><p>If a jss file is modified after a full rebuild has already been completed, the changes do not take effect. To reproduce:</p> <p>Create a simple app.js file, add a button and add it to the window.</p> <p>var button = Ti.UI.createButton({id:'b'})</p> <p>Create app.js and add some properties for the button:</p> <p>#b { width:100; height: 90; title: """"""""tyskland""""""""; }</p> <p>Launch the app. If this is the first time the project has been run, the build <USER>will take place and the app will start. The button will appear as expected. Now modify the title for the button. Save the file and re-deploy with the emulator. Notice that the new title is not displayed, the old title is still visible.</p> <p>Reproduced against 1.5 RC2 running iphone simulator.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: JSS files are not properly rebuilt when launching emulator
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If a jss file is modified after a full rebuild has already been completed, the changes do not take effect. To reproduce:</p> <p>Create a simple app.js file, add a button and add it to the window.</p> <p>var button = Ti.UI.createButton({id:'b'})</p> <p>Create app.js and add some properties for the button:</p> <p>#b { width:100; height: 90; title: """"""""tyskland""""""""; }</p> <p>Launch the app. If this is the first time the project has been run, the build <USER>will take place and the app will start. The button will appear as expected. Now modify the title for the button. Save the file and re-deploy with the emulator. Notice that the new title is not displayed, the old title is still visible.</p> <p>Reproduced against 1.5 RC2 running iphone simulator.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2569,12,"""Expose geolocation error codes""","""""""{html}<div><p>Exactly as described. Add a 'code' property to success=false  callback responses on geolocation, and expose the internal error  codes. In particular this can be used to detect when an app has  been denied access without the new 'authorization' property in 4.2  being used.</p></div>{html}      Reopened due to request for same property on android.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Expose geolocation error codes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Exactly as described. Add a 'code' property to success=false callback responses on geolocation, and expose the internal error codes. In particular this can be used to detect when an app has been denied access without the new 'authorization' property in 4.2 being used.</p></div>{html} Reopened due to request for same property on android.""""",title+description
TIMOB-2568,12,"""Android: Service """"type"""" attribute in tiapp.xml accidentally making it into AndroidManifest.xml""","""""""{html}<div><p>You define an Android Service in tiapp.xml with a block such as this:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""&gt;     &lt;services&gt;         &lt;service url=""""""""myservice.js"""""""" type=""""""""interval""""""""/&gt;     &lt;/services&gt; &lt;/android&gt;</code> </pre> <p>When build the app, the <code>type</code> attribute above is accidentally making it into the generated AndroidManifest.xml as <code>service_type</code>. It's confusing and ugly but doesn't actually hurt anything. It looks like this:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;service      android:name=""""""""com.<USER>myservice.MyserviceService""""""""     service_type=""""""""interval"""""""" /&gt;</code> </pre> <p>So that <code>service_type</code> attribute should <strong>not</strong> be there.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Service """"type"""" attribute in tiapp.xml accidentally making it into AndroidManifest.xml
Description: """"{html}<div><p>You define an Android Service in tiapp.xml with a block such as this:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""&gt; &lt;services&gt; &lt;service url=""""""""myservice.js"""""""" type=""""""""interval""""""""/&gt; &lt;/services&gt; &lt;/android&gt;</code> </pre> <p>When build the app, the <code>type</code> attribute above is accidentally making it into the generated AndroidManifest.xml as <code>service_type</code>. It's confusing and ugly but doesn't actually hurt anything. It looks like this:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;service android:name=""""""""com.<USER>myservice.MyserviceService"""""""" service_type=""""""""interval"""""""" /&gt;</code> </pre> <p>So that <code>service_type</code> attribute should <strong>not</strong> be there.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2567,12,"""selectAnnotation stopped work since Titanium Developer 1.2.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>the selectAnnotation seems stopped working just after the upgrade to Titanium Developer 1.2.2</p> <p>any clue on it?</p> <pre> <code>    win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({     // url:e.rowData.test,     backButtonTitle:'Back',     title:e.rowData.tip_user,     barColor:'#336699',     tabBarHidden:true }); pin = Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({     latitude:e.rowData.lat,     longitude:e.rowData.lng,     title:e.rowData.venue_name, //venue name     subtitle:e.rowData.tip_text, //tips     pincolor:Titanium.Map.ANNOTATION_RED,     animate:true,     myid:1 // CUSTOM ATTRIBUTE THAT IS PASSED INTO EVENT OBJECTS });  win.add(mapview);    win.add(mapToolbar); mapview.selectAnnotation(mapview.annotations[0],true);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: selectAnnotation stopped work since Titanium Developer 1.2.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>the selectAnnotation seems stopped working just after the upgrade to Titanium Developer 1.2.2</p> <p>any clue on it?</p> <pre> <code> win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ // url:e.rowData.test, backButtonTitle:'Back', title:e.rowData.tip_user, barColor:'#336699', tabBarHidden:true }); pin = Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:e.rowData.lat, longitude:e.rowData.lng, title:e.rowData.venue_name, //venue name subtitle:e.rowData.tip_text, //tips pincolor:Titanium.Map.ANNOTATION_RED, animate:true, myid:1 // CUSTOM ATTRIBUTE THAT IS PASSED INTO EVENT OBJECTS }); win.add(mapview); win.add(mapToolbar); mapview.selectAnnotation(mapview.annotations[0],true);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2566,12,"""iOS - issues with push notifications""","""""""{html}<div><p>using 1.5.19819ce0 and urban airship test.</p> <ul> <li>3g iPhone (3.1.3) no notifications are recieved.</li> <li>iPod touch/iPad (3.2 - 4.2.1) the app badge is not being set</li> </ul> <p>see email sent for test instructions (do not want pot put username/pw info here)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - issues with push notifications
Description: """"{html}<div><p>using 1.5.19819ce0 and urban airship test.</p> <ul> <li>3g iPhone (3.1.3) no notifications are recieved.</li> <li>iPod touch/iPad (3.2 - 4.2.1) the app badge is not being set</li> </ul> <p>see email sent for test instructions (do not want pot put username/pw info here)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2565,12,"""Android: Video Player can't be added to a parent view (incompatible with iOS)""","""""""{html}<div><p>It may not be possible to implement this the way iOS did, but we  should at least expose open() as a synonym for play(). The  VideoPlayer API in general may need to be reigned in when we work  out the layout/view system for 1.5.1. Thoughts?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Video Player can't be added to a parent view (incompatible with iOS)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It may not be possible to implement this the way iOS did, but we should at least expose open() as a synonym for play(). The VideoPlayer API in general may need to be reigned in when we work out the layout/view system for 1.5.1. Thoughts?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2564,12,"""Android: Expose PendingIntent FLAG_* constants in Android module""","""""""{html}<div><p>Needed for the """"""""flags"""""""" option when creating a PendingIntent</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose PendingIntent FLAG_* constants in Android module
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Needed for the """"""""flags"""""""" option when creating a PendingIntent</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2563,12,"""Android: region-specific i18n files need to be copied to res with """"r"""" in front of region""","""""""{html}<div><p>Yourproject/i18n/pt-PT/strings.xml works fine for iOS, but when built for Android it causes a build error:</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] invalid resource directory name: /Users/bill/projects/ti/Strings/build/android/res/values-pt-BR [ERROR] Error generating R.java from manifest</code> </pre> <p>Reason is because in android it needs to be values-pt-rBR (the little 'r' before BR). See Language and Region section of Android's <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/resources/providing-resources.html""""""""> Providing Resources</a> doc.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: region-specific i18n files need to be copied to res with """"r"""" in front of region
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Yourproject/i18n/pt-PT/strings.xml works fine for iOS, but when built for Android it causes a build error:</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] invalid resource directory name: /Users/bill/projects/ti/Strings/build/android/res/values-pt-BR [ERROR] Error generating R.java from manifest</code> </pre> <p>Reason is because in android it needs to be values-pt-rBR (the little 'r' before BR). See Language and Region section of Android's <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/resources/providing-resources.html""""""""> Providing Resources</a> doc.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2562,12,"""iOS: shah1 algorithm, only returning 32 of 40 chars""","""""""{html}<div><p>from ticket <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/55611/sha1-algorithm-not-working-missing-last-8-characters""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/55611/sha1-algorithm-not...</a></p> <p>from the helpdesk ticket</p> <p>I'm trying to create an SHA-1 hash, and the built-in function is only returning 32 characters instead of the required 40. The first 32 characters are correct, but I need to have the last 8 as well. Any help on this would be greatly appreciated.<br> NOTE: this bug only exists in the iPhone implementation of Ti.Utils.sha1(). The Android implementation works correctly.</p> <p>as per <USER> must fix for 1.5.0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: shah1 algorithm, only returning 32 of 40 chars
Description: """"{html}<div><p>from ticket <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/55611/sha1-algorithm-not-working-missing-last-8-characters""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/55611/sha1-algorithm-not...</a></p> <p>from the helpdesk ticket</p> <p>I'm trying to create an SHA-1 hash, and the built-in function is only returning 32 characters instead of the required 40. The first 32 characters are correct, but I need to have the last 8 as well. Any help on this would be greatly appreciated.<br> NOTE: this bug only exists in the iPhone implementation of Ti.Utils.sha1(). The Android implementation works correctly.</p> <p>as per <USER> must fix for 1.5.0</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2561,12,"""Network error when invoking a Http request multiple times""","""""""{html}<div><p>I am getting the following error when a function calling a Ti.Network.createHTTPClient() -&gt; send() is invoked a second time. First time it works well and good</p> <p>WARN/MessageQueue(367): Handler{43f82b30} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread<br> java.lang.RuntimeException: Handler{43f82b30} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread<br></p> <pre> <code>at android.os.MessageQueue.enqueueMessage(MessageQueue.java:179) at android.os.Handler.sendMessageAtTime(Handler.java:457) at android.os.Handler.sendMessageDelayed(Handler.java:430) at android.os.Handler.post(Handler.java:248) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.post(KrollContext.java:123) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:154) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:89) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:84) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:468) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:459) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.setReadyState(TiHTTPClient.java:491) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$ClientRunnable.run(TiHTTPClient.java:989) at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1096)</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Network error when invoking a Http request multiple times
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I am getting the following error when a function calling a Ti.Network.createHTTPClient() -&gt; send() is invoked a second time. First time it works well and good</p> <p>WARN/MessageQueue(367): Handler{43f82b30} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread<br> java.lang.RuntimeException: Handler{43f82b30} sending message to a Handler on a dead thread<br></p> <pre> <code>at android.os.MessageQueue.enqueueMessage(MessageQueue.java:179) at android.os.Handler.sendMessageAtTime(Handler.java:457) at android.os.Handler.sendMessageDelayed(Handler.java:430) at android.os.Handler.post(Handler.java:248) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.post(KrollContext.java:123) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:154) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:89) at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollCallback.callAsync(KrollCallback.java:84) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:468) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.fireCallback(TiHTTPClient.java:459) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient.setReadyState(TiHTTPClient.java:491) at ti.modules.titanium.network.TiHTTPClient$ClientRunnable.run(TiHTTPClient.java:989) at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1096)</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2560,12,"""Android: Locale strings with quotes/apostrophes cause syntax errors in generated strings.xml""","""""""{html}<div><p>Android strings inside a <code>&lt;string&gt;</code> tag must be escaped if they use quotes or apostrophes. From the ADT strings.xml editor:<br> """"""""If you use an apostrophe or a quote in your string, you must either escape it or enclose the whole string in the other kind of enclosing quotes.""""""""</p> <p>The escape character is simply """"""""\""""""""</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Locale strings with quotes/apostrophes cause syntax errors in generated strings.xml
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Android strings inside a <code>&lt;string&gt;</code> tag must be escaped if they use quotes or apostrophes. From the ADT strings.xml editor:<br> """"""""If you use an apostrophe or a quote in your string, you must either escape it or enclose the whole string in the other kind of enclosing quotes.""""""""</p> <p>The escape character is simply """"""""\""""""""</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
