TIMOB-2557,12,"""Android: tableView properties headerTitle and footerTitle do not display""","""""""{html}<div><p>Environment: android 2.2, TiDev 1.2.1. Tested using 1.4.X (21Nov) &amp; 1.5.X (09Dec)</p> <p>The following code demonstrates the issue:</p> <pre> <code>var tableData = [     { title: """"""""Mountain View (North America)\nCloudy"""""""" },     { title: """"""""Washington, DC (North America)\nMostly Cloudy"""""""" },     { title: """"""""Brasilia (South America)\nThunderstorm"""""""" },     { title: """"""""Buenos Aires (South America)\nClear"""""""" },     { title: """"""""Sucre (South America)\nMostly Cloudy"""""""" },     { title: """"""""London (Europe)\nOvercast"""""""" },     { title: """"""""Moscow (Europe)\nPartly Cloudy"""""""" },     { title: """"""""Prague (Europe)\nClear"""""""" },     { title: """"""""St Petersburg (Europe)\nSnow"""""""" }, ];  var table = Ti.UI.createTableView({     backgroundColor:""""""""white"""""""",     data: tableData,     headerTitle:""""""""The Weather App"""""""",     footerTitle:""""""""[data and icons supplied by Google Weather API]"""""""",     top:10,     width:320 });  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       backgroundColor:'#333' });  win1.add(table); win1.open();</code> </pre> <p>Screenshot:</p> <p><img src=""""""""http://a.yfrog.com/img375/9876/screenshot036h.png"""""""" alt=""""""""screenshot""""""""></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: tableView properties headerTitle and footerTitle do not display
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Environment: android 2.2, TiDev 1.2.1. Tested using 1.4.X (21Nov) &amp; 1.5.X (09Dec)</p> <p>The following code demonstrates the issue:</p> <pre> <code>var tableData = [ { title: """"""""Mountain View (North America)\nCloudy"""""""" }, { title: """"""""Washington, DC (North America)\nMostly Cloudy"""""""" }, { title: """"""""Brasilia (South America)\nThunderstorm"""""""" }, { title: """"""""Buenos Aires (South America)\nClear"""""""" }, { title: """"""""Sucre (South America)\nMostly Cloudy"""""""" }, { title: """"""""London (Europe)\nOvercast"""""""" }, { title: """"""""Moscow (Europe)\nPartly Cloudy"""""""" }, { title: """"""""Prague (Europe)\nClear"""""""" }, { title: """"""""St Petersburg (Europe)\nSnow"""""""" }, ]; var table = Ti.UI.createTableView({ backgroundColor:""""""""white"""""""", data: tableData, headerTitle:""""""""The Weather App"""""""", footerTitle:""""""""[data and icons supplied by Google Weather API]"""""""", top:10, width:320 }); var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#333' }); win1.add(table); win1.open();</code> </pre> <p>Screenshot:</p> <p><img src=""""""""http://a.yfrog.com/img375/9876/screenshot036h.png"""""""" alt=""""""""screenshot""""""""></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2556,12,"""iOS: Add support for Localizing Property List Values""","""""""{html}<div><p>Would be great if titanium supports the Localizing Property List  Values. THe implementation could be as simple as if there is a  InfoPlist.strings in the i18n folder on my Titanium Project, just  copy these file to the lproj directory on the Xcode Project.</p>  <p>Apple Reference:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/General/Reference/InfoPlistKeyReference/Articles/AboutInformationPropertyListFiles.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40009254-SW1"""""""">  http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/General/Refer...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add support for Localizing Property List Values
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Would be great if titanium supports the Localizing Property List Values. THe implementation could be as simple as if there is a InfoPlist.strings in the i18n folder on my Titanium Project, just copy these file to the lproj directory on the Xcode Project.</p> <p>Apple Reference:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/General/Reference/InfoPlistKeyReference/Articles/AboutInformationPropertyListFiles.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40009254-SW1""""""""> http://developer.apple.com/library/ios/#documentation/General/Refer...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2555,12,"""Android: tiapp.xml changes to android->application element only work if other manifest-related entries exist""","""""""{html}<div><p>Example: If you have this in tiapp.xml:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""&gt;  &lt;manifest&gt;   &lt;application android:debuggable=""""""""true""""""""/&gt;  &lt;/manifest&gt; &lt;/android&gt;</code> </pre> <p>... that debuggable attribute doesn't make it to AndroidManifest.xml. But if you add in something else under manifest in tiapp.xml, it does:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""&gt;  &lt;manifest&gt;   &lt;application android:debuggable=""""""""true""""""""/&gt;     &lt;supports-screens              android:smallScreens=""""""""false""""""""             android:normalScreens=""""""""true""""""""             android:largeScreens=""""""""true""""""""             android:anyDensity=""""""""true""""""""         /&gt;   &lt;/manifest&gt; &lt;/android&gt;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: tiapp.xml changes to android->application element only work if other manifest-related entries exist
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Example: If you have this in tiapp.xml:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""&gt; &lt;manifest&gt; &lt;application android:debuggable=""""""""true""""""""/&gt; &lt;/manifest&gt; &lt;/android&gt;</code> </pre> <p>... that debuggable attribute doesn't make it to AndroidManifest.xml. But if you add in something else under manifest in tiapp.xml, it does:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;android xmlns:android=""""""""http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android""""""""&gt; &lt;manifest&gt; &lt;application android:debuggable=""""""""true""""""""/&gt; &lt;supports-screens android:smallScreens=""""""""false"""""""" android:normalScreens=""""""""true"""""""" android:largeScreens=""""""""true"""""""" android:anyDensity=""""""""true"""""""" /&gt; &lt;/manifest&gt; &lt;/android&gt;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2554,12,"""Android - naming a project """"package"""" breaks packaging""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.create a simple android project and call it """"""""package""""""""<br> 2.go through the steps to package it for distribution</p> <p>results:the <USER>fails. As per Bill """"""""package"""""""" is a reserved term. We should either prevent users from using this to name projects or allow it.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - naming a project """"package"""" breaks packaging
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.create a simple android project and call it """"""""package""""""""<br> 2.go through the steps to package it for distribution</p> <p>results:the <USER>fails. As per Bill """"""""package"""""""" is a reserved term. We should either prevent users from using this to name projects or allow it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2553,12,"""iOS: support TiBlob.nativePath""","""""""{html}<div><p>Android <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1778"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1778"""""""">#1778</a></p> <p>returns null if blob is not of file-type, else the nativePath if it is based on a file</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: support TiBlob.nativePath
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Android <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1778"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1778"""""""">#1778</a></p> <p>returns null if blob is not of file-type, else the nativePath if it is based on a file</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2552,12,"""Android:  cosmetic focus rect issues after mutli line entry below the keyboard (scrollViews>TextArea)""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (12/10/10 09:14 0c31e15). G2 (2.2), nexus 1 (2.2.1)</p> <ol> <li>BaseUI &gt; Views &gt;Scroll Views &gt; scrollViews Text area<br></li> <li>give focus to the bottom most text field and hit return 4 times<br></li> <li>give focus to the text field above</li> </ol> <p>results: cosmetic issue with focus rect (see screen shot)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: cosmetic focus rect issues after mutli line entry below the keyboard (scrollViews>TextArea)
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (12/10/10 09:14 0c31e15). G2 (2.2), nexus 1 (2.2.1)</p> <ol> <li>BaseUI &gt; Views &gt;Scroll Views &gt; scrollViews Text area<br></li> <li>give focus to the bottom most text field and hit return 4 times<br></li> <li>give focus to the text field above</li> </ol> <p>results: cosmetic issue with focus rect (see screen shot)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2551,12,"""iOS: Using tabGroup.setActiveTab to switch to a tab in """"More..."""" fails to initialize window""","""""""h6.Problem  There is a bug with tabGroup. When I want to switch to a tab  under the """"""""More..."""""""" tab with tabGroup.setActiveTab, the content of  the window is not initialized. If I first click to More then try to  switch with setActiveTab it works good.    h6.Small snippet  <p>An example. Click the last button.</p>      h6.Additional details  All Titanium version is affected. I've tried this with the  latest version from git as well. (With the latest Ti from git some tab has no title randomly, but  it is another bug I think)    h6.Associated thread  http://developer.<USER>com/question/128978/how-i-can-set-active-tab-if-tabgroup-have-more-than-5-tabs""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Using tabGroup.setActiveTab to switch to a tab in """"More..."""" fails to initialize window
Description: """"h6.Problem There is a bug with tabGroup. When I want to switch to a tab under the """"""""More..."""""""" tab with tabGroup.setActiveTab, the content of the window is not initialized. If I first click to More then try to switch with setActiveTab it works good. h6.Small snippet <p>An example. Click the last button.</p> h6.Additional details All Titanium version is affected. I've tried this with the latest version from git as well. (With the latest Ti from git some tab has no title randomly, but it is another bug I think) h6.Associated thread http://developer.<USER>com/question/128978/how-i-can-set-active-tab-if-tabgroup-have-more-than-5-tabs""""",title+description
TIMOB-2550,12,"""iOS - intermittent connection issues with multiple devices and bonjour""","""""""{html}<div><p>Occurs in 1.4.1 - 1.5.0</p> <p>1.Use 2 or more devices. OS and hardware does not seem to matter, bug seen on ipod and iapd, 3.2-4.2<br> 2.Platform &gt; bonjour<br> 3.repeat with other device.<br> 4.try a few times, or with a bunch of devices.</p> <p>results: intermittantly not all devices see each other</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - intermittent connection issues with multiple devices and bonjour
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Occurs in 1.4.1 - 1.5.0</p> <p>1.Use 2 or more devices. OS and hardware does not seem to matter, bug seen on ipod and iapd, 3.2-4.2<br> 2.Platform &gt; bonjour<br> 3.repeat with other device.<br> 4.try a few times, or with a bunch of devices.</p> <p>results: intermittantly not all devices see each other</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
