( 400): at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpretLoop(Interpreter.java:1524) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at script(app://app.js:1) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.mozilla.javascript.Interpreter.interpret(Interpreter.java:854) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.mozilla.javascript.InterpretedFunction.call(InterpretedFunction.java:164) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.mozilla.javascript.ContextFactory.doTopCall(ContextFactory.java:426) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.mozilla.javascript.ScriptRuntime.doTopCall(ScriptRuntime.java:3161) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.mozilla.javascript.InterpretedFunction.exec(InterpretedFunction.java:175) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.mozilla.javascript.Context.evaluateReader(Context.java:1142) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.evaluateScript(KrollContext.java:195) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.handleEvalFile(KrollContext.java:220) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.handleMessage(KrollContext.java:115) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123) [TRACE] E/KrollContext( 400): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollHandlerThread.run(KrollHandlerThread.java:73) [TRACE] E/TiContext( 400): (kroll$1) [24,964] Rhino Error: app://app.js:1,0 [TRACE] E/TiContext( 400): (kroll$1) [2,966] Message: TypeError: Cannot find function createPerson in object [Ti.Contacts]. (app://app.js#1) [TRACE] E/TiContext( 400): (kroll$1) [1,967] Source: null</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2541,12,"""API document bug - Table View rowAtIndex""","""""""{html}<div><p>There are a few tickets at the Q&amp;A about the rowAtIndex not working, for example this one:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/8461/rowatindex-function-appears-to-be-broken""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/8461/rowatindex-function...</a></p> <p>But as Clint pointed out in this HD ticket, this is a document bug<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51121"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51121</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: API document bug - Table View rowAtIndex
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There are a few tickets at the Q&amp;A about the rowAtIndex not working, for example this one:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/8461/rowatindex-function-appears-to-be-broken""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/8461/rowatindex-function...</a></p> <p>But as Clint pointed out in this HD ticket, this is a document bug<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51121"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51121</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2540,12,"""Android: Menu Group Methods""","""""""{html}<div><p>Allow enabled, visible, and remove for group by id. Writing examples/tests found these had been missed.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Menu Group Methods
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Allow enabled, visible, and remove for group by id. Writing examples/tests found these had been missed.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2538,12,"""Android: Image view defaultImage won't show if main image is network url""","""""""{html}<div><p>(Noticed by GG.) This appears to be a regression that I introduced. Steps to reproduce:</p> <ul> <li>Install KS on phone / emulator.</li> <li><em>IMPORTANT</em> Delete the KS image cache by doing the following from terminal / command-line:</li> </ul> <pre> <code>&gt; adb shell &gt; cd /sdcard &gt; rm -r com.<USER>titanium* &gt; exit</code> </pre> <ul> <li>On the phone / emulator, disable all network stuff. (The point is, we're testing that a defaultImage appears in an image view whose main image is available only via http.)</li> <li>Run the Base UI -&gt; Views -&gt; Image Views -&gt; Remote Image test.<br></li> </ul> <p>There are supposed to be two clouds showing, but you'll see only one.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image view defaultImage won't show if main image is network url
Description: """"{html}<div><p>(Noticed by GG.) This appears to be a regression that I introduced. Steps to reproduce:</p> <ul> <li>Install KS on phone / emulator.</li> <li><em>IMPORTANT</em> Delete the KS image cache by doing the following from terminal / command-line:</li> </ul> <pre> <code>&gt; adb shell &gt; cd /sdcard &gt; rm -r com.<USER>titanium* &gt; exit</code> </pre> <ul> <li>On the phone / emulator, disable all network stuff. (The point is, we're testing that a defaultImage appears in an image view whose main image is available only via http.)</li> <li>Run the Base UI -&gt; Views -&gt; Image Views -&gt; Remote Image test.<br></li> </ul> <p>There are supposed to be two clouds showing, but you'll see only one.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2537,12,"""Android: Compiled JS won't show (or won't always show) our rhino error dialog""","""""""{html}<div><p>Simple failcase app.js, shows the error dialog in uncompiled js but not compiled:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">beelzebub.getAllFlies();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Compiled JS won't show (or won't always show) our rhino error dialog
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Simple failcase app.js, shows the error dialog in uncompiled js but not compiled:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">beelzebub.getAllFlies();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2536,12,"""Android: Activity lifecycle events should be synchronous callbacks""","""""""{html}<div><p>The current """"""""create"""""""", """"""""pause"""""""", """"""""resume"""""""", """"""""destroy"""""""", etc lifecycle events on ActivityProxy should be made into synchronous callbacks so apps can participate in the lifecycle</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Activity lifecycle events should be synchronous callbacks
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The current """"""""create"""""""", """"""""pause"""""""", """"""""resume"""""""", """"""""destroy"""""""", etc lifecycle events on ActivityProxy should be made into synchronous callbacks so apps can participate in the lifecycle</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2535,12,"""iOS: XHR getAllResponseHeaders() returns NSDictionary instead of String""","""""""I know you guys are going to re-visit XHR compliance in the future, I thought I'd throw this one in because our Android implementation supports it and it's in the spec.    There's already a drillbit test for it in network.httpclient.js (test: responseHeadersBug), but I avoid running the getAllResponseHeaders stuff if it's iphone os, until you implement it. So after you implement it, just take out the if block and - bang! - you've got your drillbit test!""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: XHR getAllResponseHeaders() returns NSDictionary instead of String
Description: """"I know you guys are going to re-visit XHR compliance in the future, I thought I'd throw this one in because our Android implementation supports it and it's in the spec. There's already a drillbit test for it in network.httpclient.js (test: responseHeadersBug), but I avoid running the getAllResponseHeaders stuff if it's iphone os, until you implement it. So after you implement it, just take out the if block and - bang! - you've got your drillbit test!""""",title+description
TIMOB-2534,12,"""User-defined hash keys with capital letters are null in Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>If a program-specific key is added to a Titanium object, it will return null when the application is built for Android.</p> <p>The following Table Row has a <code>Name</code> key. Using Android, the <code>Name</code> key will be <code>null</code> when requesting <code>row.Name</code><br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var row = Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({<br> <br>   </code> </pre> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""><code>height : 'auto', Name: 'Hello'</code></code> </pre> <pre>   <br> }); </pre> <p>If instead we were to write the following, <code>row.name</code> would give me the proper 'Hello' value:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var row = Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({<br> <br>   </code> </pre> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""><code>height : 'auto', name: 'Hello'</code></code> </pre> <pre>   <br> }); </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: User-defined hash keys with capital letters are null in Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If a program-specific key is added to a Titanium object, it will return null when the application is built for Android.</p> <p>The following Table Row has a <code>Name</code> key. Using Android, the <code>Name</code> key will be <code>null</code> when requesting <code>row.Name</code><br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var row = Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({<br> <br> </code> </pre> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""><code>height : 'auto', Name: 'Hello'</code></code> </pre> <pre> <br> }); </pre> <p>If instead we were to write the following, <code>row.name</code> would give me the proper 'Hello' value:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var row = Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({<br> <br> </code> </pre> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""><code>height : 'auto', name: 'Hello'</code></code> </pre> <pre> <br> }); </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
