TIMOB-2526,12,"""iOS: Option to set default image or have no default image on coverflow view""","""""""{html}<div><p>Option to set default image or have no default image on  coverflow view.</p>  <p>Currently it defaults as per the comments here:<br>  <a href=  """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/930-coverflow-bug"""""""">  https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/930-c...</a></p>  <p>It would be great if it we were able to set our own default  image or have no default image at all while waiting for remote  images to load.</p>  <p>Thanks,<br>  <USER>/p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Option to set default image or have no default image on coverflow view
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Option to set default image or have no default image on coverflow view.</p> <p>Currently it defaults as per the comments here:<br> <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/930-coverflow-bug""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/930-c...</a></p> <p>It would be great if it we were able to set our own default image or have no default image at all while waiting for remote images to load.</p> <p>Thanks,<br> <USER>/p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2525,12,"""TableView using TableSection with custom headerView rendering iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,<br> I didn't try on iOS devices but only on the iPad, but I have a rendering problem with the following snippet :</p> <p>There is a similar titled issue <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobile/tickets/2282""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobi...</a> but I runned the given snippet and it doesn't seems related to the issue I encounter.</p> <p>Is is a bug or a bad usage of the APIs ?</p> <p>NB: the rendering behavior is correct if you comment the line """"""""tableSection.headerView = customHeader;""""""""</p> <p>function createCustomTableSection() {<br></p> <pre> <code>var tableSection = Titanium.UI.createTableViewSection({     headerTitle: 'Monday 05 July 2010' });  var customHeader = Titanium.UI.createView({     height: 45,     backgroundImage: 'table_section_bg.png' }); var dateLabel = Titanium.UI.createLabel({     text:'Monday 05 July 2010',     color:'#b4d0ee',     top: 5,     left: 5 }); customHeader.add(dateLabel); tableSection.headerView = customHeader;  tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Monday 05 July 2010'})); tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Tuesday 06 July 2010'})); tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Wednesday 07 July 2010'})); tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Thursday 08 July 2010'})); return tableSection;</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow();</p> <p>// Create header var header = Titanium.UI.createView({<br></p> <pre> <code>backgroundImage: 'home_header.png', top: 0, height: 43</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var l = Titanium.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>text: 'Plenary sessions', color: 'white', font:{fontSize: 18}, height: 'auto', right: 'auto', top: 5, left: 10, width: 150</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>header.add(l);<br> win.add(header);</p> <p>var sections = [];<br> for (var i = 0; i &lt; 8; i++) {<br></p> <pre> <code>sections[i] = createCustomTableSection();</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>var tableView = Titanium.UI.createTableView();<br> tableView.setData(sections);</p> <p>win.add(tableView);<br> win.open();</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView using TableSection with custom headerView rendering iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,<br> I didn't try on iOS devices but only on the iPad, but I have a rendering problem with the following snippet :</p> <p>There is a similar titled issue <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobile/tickets/2282""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238-titanium-mobi...</a> but I runned the given snippet and it doesn't seems related to the issue I encounter.</p> <p>Is is a bug or a bad usage of the APIs ?</p> <p>NB: the rendering behavior is correct if you comment the line """"""""tableSection.headerView = customHeader;""""""""</p> <p>function createCustomTableSection() {<br></p> <pre> <code>var tableSection = Titanium.UI.createTableViewSection({ headerTitle: 'Monday 05 July 2010' }); var customHeader = Titanium.UI.createView({ height: 45, backgroundImage: 'table_section_bg.png' }); var dateLabel = Titanium.UI.createLabel({ text:'Monday 05 July 2010', color:'#b4d0ee', top: 5, left: 5 }); customHeader.add(dateLabel); tableSection.headerView = customHeader; tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Monday 05 July 2010'})); tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Tuesday 06 July 2010'})); tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Wednesday 07 July 2010'})); tableSection.add(Titanium.UI.createTableViewRow({title:'Thursday 08 July 2010'})); return tableSection;</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow();</p> <p>// Create header var header = Titanium.UI.createView({<br></p> <pre> <code>backgroundImage: 'home_header.png', top: 0, height: 43</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var l = Titanium.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>text: 'Plenary sessions', color: 'white', font:{fontSize: 18}, height: 'auto', right: 'auto', top: 5, left: 10, width: 150</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>header.add(l);<br> win.add(header);</p> <p>var sections = [];<br> for (var i = 0; i &lt; 8; i++) {<br></p> <pre> <code>sections[i] = createCustomTableSection();</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>var tableView = Titanium.UI.createTableView();<br> tableView.setData(sections);</p> <p>win.add(tableView);<br> win.open();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2524,12,"""Mailto in webView does not work""","""""""{html}<div><p>Mailto links within a webView are not working. This is the error I am getting: <a href= """"""""http://screencast.com/t/WnYHizHy5Nk"""""""">http://screencast.com/t/WnYHizHy5Nk</a></p> <p>Issue reported here: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/59091"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/59091</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Mailto in webView does not work
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Mailto links within a webView are not working. This is the error I am getting: <a href= """"""""http://screencast.com/t/WnYHizHy5Nk"""""""">http://screencast.com/t/WnYHizHy5Nk</a></p> <p>Issue reported here: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/59091"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/59091</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2523,12,"""iOS: ScrollableView problems showing imageviews larger than screen""","""""""{html}<div><p>I submit a simple example of a scrollableview with 3 imageviews  which are wider than the window's width.</p>  <p>The imageviews of three images 1024x1440 pixels (placed as  backgrounds to allow zooming) are sized to the maximum height of  the window, and therefore with a wider width; than added to the  scrollableview.<br>  The images are double pages of a catalog.</p>  <p>Scrollableview correctly shows just the visible part of the  image, but trying to move right showing the other part of the  image, it scrolls to the following view.<br>  If you try to first pinch in or out the image (zooming), then  scrollableview acts correctly first panning and then scrolling.</p>  <p>The attachments contains app.js, scrollview_problem.js and the  three images.<br>  Put them in the resource folder of a new project.<br>  I have Titanium developer 1.2.1, iphone SDK 4.2 and mobile titanium  sdk 1.4.2.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollableView problems showing imageviews larger than screen
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I submit a simple example of a scrollableview with 3 imageviews which are wider than the window's width.</p> <p>The imageviews of three images 1024x1440 pixels (placed as backgrounds to allow zooming) are sized to the maximum height of the window, and therefore with a wider width; than added to the scrollableview.<br> The images are double pages of a catalog.</p> <p>Scrollableview correctly shows just the visible part of the image, but trying to move right showing the other part of the image, it scrolls to the following view.<br> If you try to first pinch in or out the image (zooming), then scrollableview acts correctly first panning and then scrolling.</p> <p>The attachments contains app.js, scrollview_problem.js and the three images.<br> Put them in the resource folder of a new project.<br> I have Titanium developer 1.2.1, iphone SDK 4.2 and mobile titanium sdk 1.4.2.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
