Description: """"{html}<div><p>See this ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/58251"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/58251</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2473,12,"""Android: UI - remote imageView in tableView load 5X slower than earlier Titanium versions""","""""""h2. Problem    Load 6 rows and display 6 same images took 6-8 seconds - it is too slow.  Same test in Titanium 1.4.2 took only 1-2 seconds. It is faster by 5X compared with 1.5.0!    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js}  var data = [];    for (var i = 0; i < 20; i++) {    var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({      height: '70',      hasChild: true    });      var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({      image: 'http://lig.cn/prd_imgs/f/b/fb2df843d08ac0474c799daf0cbc2409_60x60.jpg',      height: 60,      width: 60,      left: 5,      top: 5    });    row.add(img);    data.push(row);  }    var tableview = Ti.UI.createTableView({    data:data  });    Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(tableview);  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: UI - remote imageView in tableView load 5X slower than earlier Titanium versions
Description: """"h2. Problem Load 6 rows and display 6 same images took 6-8 seconds - it is too slow. Same test in Titanium 1.4.2 took only 1-2 seconds. It is faster by 5X compared with 1.5.0! h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript|title=app.js} var data = []; for (var i = 0; i < 20; i++) { var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ height: '70', hasChild: true }); var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: 'http://lig.cn/prd_imgs/f/b/fb2df843d08ac0474c799daf0cbc2409_60x60.jpg', height: 60, width: 60, left: 5, top: 5 }); row.add(img); data.push(row); } var tableview = Ti.UI.createTableView({ data:data }); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(tableview); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2472,12,"""Android: Geolocation pause not working as expected""","""""""{html}<div><p>on 1.4.2 ks, after running the geolocation test and backgrounding the app, the icon goes away. Same device, 1.5.0, the icon persists</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Geolocation pause not working as expected
Description: """"{html}<div><p>on 1.4.2 ks, after running the geolocation test and backgrounding the app, the icon goes away. Same device, 1.5.0, the icon persists</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2471,12,"""Android: Phone > contacts addresses are not being displayed (erroneous """"no address found"""" alert)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2)</p> <p>1.Phone &gt; contacts &gt; display people<br> 2.select a contact that has an address associated with it.<br> 3.read results</p> <p>results: """"""""No addresses to show""""""""</p> <p>missed on last weeks pass, occurs in 1.5.0.91838a as well. Functionality did not exist in 1.4.2, so no regression tag or priority set by me.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Phone > contacts addresses are not being displayed (erroneous """"no address found"""" alert)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2)</p> <p>1.Phone &gt; contacts &gt; display people<br> 2.select a contact that has an address associated with it.<br> 3.read results</p> <p>results: """"""""No addresses to show""""""""</p> <p>missed on last weeks pass, occurs in 1.5.0.91838a as well. Functionality did not exist in 1.4.2, so no regression tag or priority set by me.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2470,12,"""Android: allow high-density-only resource overrides""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is best explained by example. Say I have an app with the following resource, sized for a 320x480 screen:</p> <p>images/header.png</p> <p>Both my iPhone and Android builds pull it in fine. When I want to use a higher-res version for the iPhone 4, I add the following:</p> <p>images/<a href=""""""""mailto:<EMAIL>""""""""><EMAIL></a></p> <p>That works fine too. Now I want to pull in a higher-res version for the Android, so I add the following (using the latest SDK from master):</p> <p>android/images/high/header.png</p> <p>Doesn't work! I then copy images/header.png to:</p> <p>android/images/medium/header.png</p> <p>And the high-res one shows up now. Ideally I don't want the low-res header.png duplicated in two spots, so it would be great if having that image also in /medium wouldn't be required.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: allow high-density-only resource overrides
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is best explained by example. Say I have an app with the following resource, sized for a 320x480 screen:</p> <p>images/header.png</p> <p>Both my iPhone and Android builds pull it in fine. When I want to use a higher-res version for the iPhone 4, I add the following:</p> <p>images/<a href=""""""""mailto:<EMAIL>""""""""><EMAIL></a></p> <p>That works fine too. Now I want to pull in a higher-res version for the Android, so I add the following (using the latest SDK from master):</p> <p>android/images/high/header.png</p> <p>Doesn't work! I then copy images/header.png to:</p> <p>android/images/medium/header.png</p> <p>And the high-res one shows up now. Ideally I don't want the low-res header.png duplicated in two spots, so it would be great if having that image also in /medium wouldn't be required.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2469,12,"""Android: orientation - unexpected results for """"set portrait"""" after setting """"allow landscape only"""" ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>change in behavior since last weeks 1.5.0.591838a pull</p> <p>1.Phone &gt; orientation<br> 2.hold it in portrait<br> 3.Tap """"""""allow landscape only""""""""<br> 4.tap """"""""set portrait""""""""</p> <p>results (you may need to repeat this once if you don't see it first time, it is a little bit intermittent) the app briefly draws in portrait, then returns to landscape. broke between 1.5.0.591838a and now</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: orientation - unexpected results for """"set portrait"""" after setting """"allow landscape only""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>change in behavior since last weeks 1.5.0.591838a pull</p> <p>1.Phone &gt; orientation<br> 2.hold it in portrait<br> 3.Tap """"""""allow landscape only""""""""<br> 4.tap """"""""set portrait""""""""</p> <p>results (you may need to repeat this once if you don't see it first time, it is a little bit intermittent) the app briefly draws in portrait, then returns to landscape. broke between 1.5.0.591838a and now</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2468,12,"""Android: orientation - orientation returns app orientation (not device orientation) ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>behavior change since last weeks pull (1.5.0.91838a)</p> <p>1.Phone &gt; orientation<br> 2.hold it in portrait<br> 3.Tap set landscape</p> <p>results: app goes to landscape, on screen values report """"""""landscape left"""""""", while the device is being held in portrait</p> <p>expected: report back device orientation</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: orientation - orientation returns app orientation (not device orientation)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>behavior change since last weeks pull (1.5.0.91838a)</p> <p>1.Phone &gt; orientation<br> 2.hold it in portrait<br> 3.Tap set landscape</p> <p>results: app goes to landscape, on screen values report """"""""landscape left"""""""", while the device is being held in portrait</p> <p>expected: report back device orientation</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2467,12,"""Android: Facebook - publish stream/status invokes blank log in window when user is logged in ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>1.Mashups &gt; Facebook &gt; Publish Stream (be logged in, or log in on this screen)<br> 2.tap either status or stream</p> <p>results: blank log in window is invoked (dismissing dialog invokes """"""""null"""""""" alert)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Facebook - publish stream/status invokes blank log in window when user is logged in
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>1.Mashups &gt; Facebook &gt; Publish Stream (be logged in, or log in on this screen)<br> 2.tap either status or stream</p> <p>results: blank log in window is invoked (dismissing dialog invokes """"""""null"""""""" alert)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2466,12,"""Android: XHR > Binary data > image is being unexpectedly scaled (also BaseUI>Views>IMageViews>Basic)""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; XHR &gt; Binary data<br> 2.BaseUI &gt; Views &gt; IMageViews &gt; Basic</p> <p>results: image is being scaled - appears somewhat distorted. Also occurs in build 1.5.0.91838a (last weeks pull). works as expected in 1.4.2</p> <p>missed on last weeks pass.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: XHR > Binary data > image is being unexpectedly scaled (also BaseUI>Views>IMageViews>Basic)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.5.0 (11/29/10 08:10 faa27c7). G2 (2.2) some G1 (1.6) some droid 1 (2.2) and a bit of sim (2.1)</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; XHR &gt; Binary data<br> 2.BaseUI &gt; Views &gt; IMageViews &gt; Basic</p> <p>results: image is being scaled - appears somewhat distorted. Also occurs in build 1.5.0.91838a (last weeks pull). works as expected in 1.4.2</p> <p>missed on last weeks pass.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2465,12,"""Can't record with MP3 or AIFF formats - only WAVE""","""""""{html}<div><p>Have only tested MP3, AIFF and WAVE formats on the iPad. Of the three, only WAVE is working.</p> <p>See note at top of app.js.</p> <p>Tried testing this file with latest builds 1.4.3 SDK and 1.5.0 SDK and neither would run the app. But Ti 1.4.2 SDK/iOS 4.2 SDK does.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var recording = Ti.Media.createAudioRecorder(); recording.compression = Ti.Media.AUDIO_FORMAT_ULAW; recording.format = Ti.Media.AUDIO_FILEFORMAT_WAVE; // _MP3, _AIFF recording.type = Ti.Media.AUDIO_MICROPHONE;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Can't record with MP3 or AIFF formats - only WAVE
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Have only tested MP3, AIFF and WAVE formats on the iPad. Of the three, only WAVE is working.</p> <p>See note at top of app.js.</p> <p>Tried testing this file with latest builds 1.4.3 SDK and 1.5.0 SDK and neither would run the app. But Ti 1.4.2 SDK/iOS 4.2 SDK does.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var recording = Ti.Media.createAudioRecorder(); recording.compression = Ti.Media.AUDIO_FORMAT_ULAW; recording.format = Ti.Media.AUDIO_FILEFORMAT_WAVE; // _MP3, _AIFF recording.type = Ti.Media.AUDIO_MICROPHONE;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
