TIMOB-2460,12,"""Android: Error message displayed to Ti Developer user when emulator is closed""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ever since <a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/c8d81b85e64dd28df2f511bc2819146b0df1287b""""""""> this commit</a>, if you use Titanium Developer to launch an application into the Android emulator and then later close the emulator (with Developer still running), you get a """"""""red"""""""" error message and python traceback in the Developer console (see screenshot).</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] Error in compiler. Traceback (most recent call last):     File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/DEV_1.5.0/android/builder.py"""""""", line 1502, in &lt;module&gt;     s.run_emulator(avd_id,avd_skin)     File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/DEV_1.5.0/android/builder.py"""""""", line 389, in run_emulator    sys.exit(rc)   SystemExit: 0</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Error message displayed to Ti Developer user when emulator is closed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ever since <a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/c8d81b85e64dd28df2f511bc2819146b0df1287b""""""""> this commit</a>, if you use Titanium Developer to launch an application into the Android emulator and then later close the emulator (with Developer still running), you get a """"""""red"""""""" error message and python traceback in the Developer console (see screenshot).</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] Error in compiler. Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/DEV_1.5.0/android/builder.py"""""""", line 1502, in &lt;module&gt; s.run_emulator(avd_id,avd_skin) File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/DEV_1.5.0/android/builder.py"""""""", line 389, in run_emulator sys.exit(rc) SystemExit: 0</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2459,12,"""iOS: ScrollableView and Webview - 1.5.0 (11/29/2010)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi, i see this bug a lot of times reported here, but none of  them with a correction.</p>  <p>When i put WebViews in Scrollable view, first view was showed,  but none of others was before i scroll up or down.</p>  <p>But a 2 days old, was reported that bug is fixed: <a href=  """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2093-webviews-in-a-scrollable-view-fail-to-render-until-a-scroll-updown-happens"""""""">  https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2093-...</a></p>  <p>But none in 1.5.0 (11/29/2010) or git was resolved this for me  in iPad.</p>  <p>If i use this code above, work correctly in simulator, but NOT  in real iPad.</p>  <pre>  <code>  var sc = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({ showPagingControl:true });     var wb1 = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url:'1.html' });  var wb2 = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url:'2.html' });  var wb3 = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url:'3.html' });     sc.addView(wb1);  sc.addView(wb2);  sc.addView(wb3);</code>  </pre>  <p>Sorry for my poor english, i'm Brazilian.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: ScrollableView and Webview - 1.5.0 (11/29/2010)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi, i see this bug a lot of times reported here, but none of them with a correction.</p> <p>When i put WebViews in Scrollable view, first view was showed, but none of others was before i scroll up or down.</p> <p>But a 2 days old, was reported that bug is fixed: <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2093-webviews-in-a-scrollable-view-fail-to-render-until-a-scroll-updown-happens""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/2093-...</a></p> <p>But none in 1.5.0 (11/29/2010) or git was resolved this for me in iPad.</p> <p>If i use this code above, work correctly in simulator, but NOT in real iPad.</p> <pre> <code> var sc = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({ showPagingControl:true }); var wb1 = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url:'1.html' }); var wb2 = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url:'2.html' }); var wb3 = Ti.UI.createWebView({ url:'3.html' }); sc.addView(wb1); sc.addView(wb2); sc.addView(wb3);</code> </pre> <p>Sorry for my poor english, i'm Brazilian.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2458,12,"""iPad Orientation Bug on start""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi, everbody<br>  I have a serious problem in iPad orientation.</p>  <p>This error ocurred in 1.4.3 and 1.5.0 (11/29/2010).</p>  <p>My app has this code:</p>  <pre>  <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundImage: 'img/bkg.png',      orientationModes: [Ti.UI.PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT, Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT]  });</code>  </pre>  <p>and in tiapp.xml:</p>  <pre>  <code>&lt;orientations device=""""""""ipad""""""""&gt;              &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.PORTRAIT&lt;/orientation&gt;              &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT&lt;/orientation&gt;              &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT&lt;/orientation&gt;              &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT&lt;/orientation&gt;          &lt;/orientations&gt;</code>  </pre>  <p>My app start normal in Portrait, and rotate normal, but if i put  iPad on Landscape before, and open my app, it show a landscape  splash and switch to a portrait window in landscape mode.</p>  <p>Creating a window that is cut down and with black border the  side.</p>  <p>Sorry for my poor english, i'm Brazilian.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad Orientation Bug on start
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi, everbody<br> I have a serious problem in iPad orientation.</p> <p>This error ocurred in 1.4.3 and 1.5.0 (11/29/2010).</p> <p>My app has this code:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundImage: 'img/bkg.png', orientationModes: [Ti.UI.PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT, Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT, Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT] });</code> </pre> <p>and in tiapp.xml:</p> <pre> <code>&lt;orientations device=""""""""ipad""""""""&gt; &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.PORTRAIT&lt;/orientation&gt; &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT&lt;/orientation&gt; &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT&lt;/orientation&gt; &lt;orientation&gt;Ti.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT&lt;/orientation&gt; &lt;/orientations&gt;</code> </pre> <p>My app start normal in Portrait, and rotate normal, but if i put iPad on Landscape before, and open my app, it show a landscape splash and switch to a portrait window in landscape mode.</p> <p>Creating a window that is cut down and with black border the side.</p> <p>Sorry for my poor english, i'm Brazilian.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2457,12,"""Error in Label on Button on 1.5.0 (11/29/2010)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,<br> I'm creating an app for iPad, tested in 3.2.2 and 4.2.1<br> I use a custom button to create an iPhone style button.</p> <pre> <code>var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({         backgroundImage:'img/btn.png',         backgroundSelectedImage:'img/btn_o.png',         height:57,         width:200     }); var lblBtn = Ti.UI.createLabel({         color:'#fff',         font:{fontSize:12,fontWeight:'bold'},         shadowColor:'#000',         shadowOffset:{x:1,y:1},         right:0,         left:0,         height:'auto',         text:'My button',         textAlign:'center'     }) btn.add(lblBtn);</code> </pre> <p>This code reproduce a button with a title with shaddow. This work perfectly in 1.4.3, but NOT in 1.5.0.<br> If my image is opaque i don't see this label, but if has an opacity, i see the label below the backgroundImage.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Error in Label on Button on 1.5.0 (11/29/2010)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,<br> I'm creating an app for iPad, tested in 3.2.2 and 4.2.1<br> I use a custom button to create an iPhone style button.</p> <pre> <code>var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ backgroundImage:'img/btn.png', backgroundSelectedImage:'img/btn_o.png', height:57, width:200 }); var lblBtn = Ti.UI.createLabel({ color:'#fff', font:{fontSize:12,fontWeight:'bold'}, shadowColor:'#000', shadowOffset:{x:1,y:1}, right:0, left:0, height:'auto', text:'My button', textAlign:'center' }) btn.add(lblBtn);</code> </pre> <p>This code reproduce a button with a title with shaddow. This work perfectly in 1.4.3, but NOT in 1.5.0.<br> If my image is opaque i don't see this label, but if has an opacity, i see the label below the backgroundImage.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2456,12,"""TiUIWebView::webViewDidStartLoad and webViewDidFinishLoad""","""""""{html}<div><p>In the TiUIWebView class webViewDidStartLoad and webViewDidFinishLoad methods that are used for calling the event listeners:<br> The events that are generated will not provide the correct URL's.</p> <p>The problem seems to be in this line:<br></p> <pre> <code>NSDictionary *event = url == nil ? nil : [NSDictionary dictionaryWithObject:[url absoluteString] forKey:@""""""""url""""""""];</code> </pre> <p>The instance variable url seems to be commonly nil, so nothing is returned.</p> <p>The expected behavior for the listeners would rather be:<br></p> <pre> <code>NSString *url__ = [self url]; NSDictionary *event = url__ == nil ? nil : [NSDictionary dictionaryWithObject:url__ forKey:@""""""""url""""""""];</code> </pre> <p>Because it will give access to the URL that is actually used in the request that is causing the events.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TiUIWebView::webViewDidStartLoad and webViewDidFinishLoad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In the TiUIWebView class webViewDidStartLoad and webViewDidFinishLoad methods that are used for calling the event listeners:<br> The events that are generated will not provide the correct URL's.</p> <p>The problem seems to be in this line:<br></p> <pre> <code>NSDictionary *event = url == nil ? nil : [NSDictionary dictionaryWithObject:[url absoluteString] forKey:@""""""""url""""""""];</code> </pre> <p>The instance variable url seems to be commonly nil, so nothing is returned.</p> <p>The expected behavior for the listeners would rather be:<br></p> <pre> <code>NSString *url__ = [self url]; NSDictionary *event = url__ == nil ? nil : [NSDictionary dictionaryWithObject:url__ forKey:@""""""""url""""""""];</code> </pre> <p>Because it will give access to the URL that is actually used in the request that is causing the events.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2455,12,"""Blob Object does not provide access to the raw data ""","""""""{html}<div><p>What I am trying to do is hash an image. Unfortunately (using SDK 1.4.1.1 and iOS 3.2) it does not appear that there is any way to access the raw data (in an array of bytes or as a string etc). So the built in MD5 digest function throws an error, and other javascript based hashing algorithms are not useful either.</p> <p>For the Blob object, access to the raw data should be provided.</p> <p>Thank you.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Blob Object does not provide access to the raw data
Description: """"{html}<div><p>What I am trying to do is hash an image. Unfortunately (using SDK 1.4.1.1 and iOS 3.2) it does not appear that there is any way to access the raw data (in an array of bytes or as a string etc). So the built in MD5 digest function throws an error, and other javascript based hashing algorithms are not useful either.</p> <p>For the Blob object, access to the raw data should be provided.</p> <p>Thank you.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2454,12,"""ScrollableView Push Views bug on 1.5  ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Opening a ticket and uploading a test case following this Q&amp;A:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/83731/scrollableview-push-views-bug-on-15#152371""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/83731/scrollableview-pus...</a></p> <hr> <p>Hi,<br> 1.5 seems to have a bug when pushing a new array of Views to an existing scrollableView.<br> The previous views are still visible in the background and the app starts to lag a lot...<br> Anyone experiencing this? The workaround is to loop through all the views and removing them one by one using removeView, but if you pass an empty array, the old views are still present in the background.<br> Thanks, <USER>/p> <hr> <pre> <code>var w = Ti.UI.createWindow(); w.open();  var sv = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({height:200, showPagingControl:true}); w.add(sv);  var v = [];  Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e){   v = [];      var color;   if(e.orientation == 1 || e.orientation == 2){     color = """"""""#00ff00"""""""";   }else{     color = """"""""#ff0000"""""""";   }   for (var j = 0;j &lt; 5;j++){     v.push(Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor:color}));   }      sv.views = v; });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ScrollableView Push Views bug on 1.5
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Opening a ticket and uploading a test case following this Q&amp;A:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/83731/scrollableview-push-views-bug-on-15#152371""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/83731/scrollableview-pus...</a></p> <hr> <p>Hi,<br> 1.5 seems to have a bug when pushing a new array of Views to an existing scrollableView.<br> The previous views are still visible in the background and the app starts to lag a lot...<br> Anyone experiencing this? The workaround is to loop through all the views and removing them one by one using removeView, but if you pass an empty array, the old views are still present in the background.<br> Thanks, <USER>/p> <hr> <pre> <code>var w = Ti.UI.createWindow(); w.open(); var sv = Ti.UI.createScrollableView({height:200, showPagingControl:true}); w.add(sv); var v = []; Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e){ v = []; var color; if(e.orientation == 1 || e.orientation == 2){ color = """"""""#00ff00""""""""; }else{ color = """"""""#ff0000""""""""; } for (var j = 0;j &lt; 5;j++){ v.push(Ti.UI.createView({backgroundColor:color})); } sv.views = v; });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2453,12,"""Android: navBarHidden ignored in createWindow""","""""""{html}<div><p>Regression during refactor to TiBaseActivity.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: navBarHidden ignored in createWindow
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Regression during refactor to TiBaseActivity.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2452,12,"""Android: Image rotates around top-left not anchor point""","""""""{html}<div><p>I can get an image to rotate around its top-left corner.  Supposedly, by setting an anchorPoint on the image I should be able  to rotate around another point also. I cannot. It rotates around  the top-left.</p>  <p>Info &amp; code, see:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57431"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57431</a><br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/84171/rotate-an-image-around-its-center"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/84171/rotate-an-image-ar...</a></p>  <p>Using SDK 1.5, timestamp=11/23/10 14:42, githash=df00caa with  Android SDK 1.6.</p>  <p>Perhaps also related to <a href=  """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/839-implement-animations-in-android"""""""">  https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/839-i...</a></p>  <p>Thanks,<br>  Tim</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image rotates around top-left not anchor point
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I can get an image to rotate around its top-left corner. Supposedly, by setting an anchorPoint on the image I should be able to rotate around another point also. I cannot. It rotates around the top-left.</p> <p>Info &amp; code, see:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57431"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/57431</a><br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/84171/rotate-an-image-around-its-center""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/84171/rotate-an-image-ar...</a></p> <p>Using SDK 1.5, timestamp=11/23/10 14:42, githash=df00caa with Android SDK 1.6.</p> <p>Perhaps also related to <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/839-implement-animations-in-android""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/839-i...</a></p> <p>Thanks,<br> Tim</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2451,12,"""iOS: Sound crash when unplugging then plugging headphones back in  (3gt ipod touch only) ""","""""""{html}<div><p>3gt ipod touch (4.0.2) TiMobile 1.5.0.faa27c7. Not repro'ing on 4th gen touch</p> <p>1.Phone &gt; Sound &gt; record<br> 2.hi def or no, start recording with headphones plugged in<br> 3.unplug, replug and hit stop</p> <p>results:</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:20 Apple- kernel[0] : i2s0: transmitter underrun (0)</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:20 Apple- kernel[0] : i2s0: transmitter underrun (0)</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:21 Apple- UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x5a06][5058] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Input availability changed: false</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:22 Apple- UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x5a06][5058] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Input availability changed: true</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:24 Apple- mediaserverd[20] : 13:39:24.323 WARNING translating CMSession error: 560947818</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:24 Apple- UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x5a06][5058] : terminate called after throwing an instance of 'CAXException'</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:25 Apple- ReportCrash[5060] : Formulating crash report for <USER>KitchenSink[5058]</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:25 Apple- com.apple.launchd<a>1</a> : (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x5a06]) Job appears to have crashed: Abort trap</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:25 Apple- SpringBoard[28] : Application 'KitchenSink' exited abnormally with signal 6: Abort trap</p> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:25 Apple- gamed[1637] : GKDataRequestManager.m:776 - -[GKDataRequestManager appStateChanged:] - appState for client (null) changed from 0 to 1 -- userinfo = {<br></p> <pre> <code>    SBApplicationStateDisplayIDKey = """"""""com.<USER>KitchenSink"""""""";     SBApplicationStateKey = 1;     SBApplicationStateProcessIDKey = 0;     SBMostElevatedStateForProcessID = 1; }</code> </pre> <p>Mon Nov 29 13:39:25 Apple- ReportCrash[5060] : Saved crashreport to /var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter/KitchenSink_2010-11-29-133924_Apple-.plist using uid: 0 gid: 0, synthetic_euid: 501 egid: 0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Sound crash when unplugging then plugging headphones back in (3gt ipod touch only)
