TIMOB-2361,12,"""Android: window, createWindow does not respect title property""","""""""{html}<div><p>Environment: android 1.4.X (12 Nov), emulator, on ubuntu</p> <p>As per <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/80191/changing-title-in-new-windows""""""""> this user's post</a> to the Q&amp;A, and my subsequent tests shown below, I can confirm that the title property is not respected when set at creation time, and the window is not modal/heavyweight.</p> <p>The problem exists also when a new context is created (win3.js below), and a further context thereafter (not shown).</p> <p>To workaround this issue, users may set navBarHidden:false, but there may be reasons why they need a lightweight view. Thus, this issue may be regarded as trivial, if this is a rare case.</p> <p>app.js:</p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor: """"""""red"""""""",     title: """"""""window title: win1"""""""",     exitOnClose: true }); win1.open(); var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({title:'label: window 1'}); win1.add(label1);   var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor: """"""""green"""""""",     title: """"""""window title: win2"""""""" }); win2.open(); var label2 = Ti.UI.createLabel({title:'label: window 2'}); win2.add(label2);   var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor: """"""""blue"""""""",     title: """"""""window title: win3"""""""",     url:'win3.js' }); win3.open();</code> </pre> <p>win3.js:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({title:'label: window 3'}); win.add(label);  var win4 = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor: """"""""yellow"""""""",     title: """"""""window title: win4"""""""",     url:'win4.js' }); win4.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: window, createWindow does not respect title property
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Environment: android 1.4.X (12 Nov), emulator, on ubuntu</p> <p>As per <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/80191/changing-title-in-new-windows""""""""> this user's post</a> to the Q&amp;A, and my subsequent tests shown below, I can confirm that the title property is not respected when set at creation time, and the window is not modal/heavyweight.</p> <p>The problem exists also when a new context is created (win3.js below), and a further context thereafter (not shown).</p> <p>To workaround this issue, users may set navBarHidden:false, but there may be reasons why they need a lightweight view. Thus, this issue may be regarded as trivial, if this is a rare case.</p> <p>app.js:</p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: """"""""red"""""""", title: """"""""window title: win1"""""""", exitOnClose: true }); win1.open(); var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({title:'label: window 1'}); win1.add(label1); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: """"""""green"""""""", title: """"""""window title: win2"""""""" }); win2.open(); var label2 = Ti.UI.createLabel({title:'label: window 2'}); win2.add(label2); var win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: """"""""blue"""""""", title: """"""""window title: win3"""""""", url:'win3.js' }); win3.open();</code> </pre> <p>win3.js:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({title:'label: window 3'}); win.add(label); var win4 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: """"""""yellow"""""""", title: """"""""window title: win4"""""""", url:'win4.js' }); win4.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2360,12,"""add support for canOpenURL on iOS""","""""""{html}<div><p>We have a request to add support for canOpenURL on iOS.</p> <p>HD TIcket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/54051"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/54051</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: add support for canOpenURL on iOS
