TIMOB-2336,12,"""iOS: Filesystem.isExteralStoragePresent mispelled and always returns false""","""""""{html}<div><p>ENVIRONMENT:<br> version=1.5.0<br> timestamp=11/12/10 10:37<br> githash=937631f</p> <p>STEPS TO REPRODUCE:<br> 1) Note that code in titanium_mobile/iphone/Classes/FilesystemModule.m, method isExteralSpaceAvailable<br> always returns """"""""false"""""""" (despite existing external storage options) - """"""""as designed"""""""" in Titanium API?<br> 2) Note also """"""""exteral"""""""" is misspelled, should be """"""""external"""""""" with an 'n'<br> 3) Both 1) and 2) are reflected in the tdoc file Filesystem.tdoc</p> <p>SUGGESTED FIX:<br> Use a macro or method to direct both the misspelled and correctly spelled method both work, or add the correct spelling and depcreate the incorrect? It's also misspelled in the tdoc file</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Filesystem.isExteralStoragePresent mispelled and always returns false
Description: """"{html}<div><p>ENVIRONMENT:<br> version=1.5.0<br> timestamp=11/12/10 10:37<br> githash=937631f</p> <p>STEPS TO REPRODUCE:<br> 1) Note that code in titanium_mobile/iphone/Classes/FilesystemModule.m, method isExteralSpaceAvailable<br> always returns """"""""false"""""""" (despite existing external storage options) - """"""""as designed"""""""" in Titanium API?<br> 2) Note also """"""""exteral"""""""" is misspelled, should be """"""""external"""""""" with an 'n'<br> 3) Both 1) and 2) are reflected in the tdoc file Filesystem.tdoc</p> <p>SUGGESTED FIX:<br> Use a macro or method to direct both the misspelled and correctly spelled method both work, or add the correct spelling and depcreate the incorrect? It's also misspelled in the tdoc file</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2335,12,"""iOS: Filesystem method spaceAvailable should return bytes available instead of a boolean [API SCRUB]""","""""""{html}<div><p>ENVIRONMENT:</p> <p>[From titanium_mobile/dist/os x/&#8230;/version.txt] version=1.5.0<br> timestamp=11/12/10 10:37<br> githash=937631f</p> <p>STEPS TO REPRODUCE:<br> 1) Pull down the latest titanium_mobile from github<br> 2) Note &#8230;/apidoc/ File.tdoc says:<br> spaceAvailable: return boolean to indicate if the path has space available for storage<br> 3) Note implementation (code in TiFilesystemProxy.m) returns TRUE if space available, FALSE if not</p> <p>SUGGESTED FIX:<br> Return an integer (unsigned, 64-bit?) that shows the number of bytes available; use 0 for none.<br> (Easy to do per code, and the android 2.0 tdoc apparently already says this: platform deviation?)</p> <p>ISSUES:<br> &#8226; How to sync up with Android folks on the new """"""""spec"""""""" created from comparing iOS and Android """"""""realities""""""""<br> &#8226; Thomas helped me write this per QA """"""""Best Practices"""""""" but RFC is always welcome on how to improve the first of many LH tickets<br> (Request for Comments)</p> <p>ISSUES:</p> <p>I don't have Lighthouse permissions / access to set """"""""Who's responsible""""""""</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Filesystem method spaceAvailable should return bytes available instead of a boolean [API SCRUB]
Description: """"{html}<div><p>ENVIRONMENT:</p> <p>[From titanium_mobile/dist/os x/&#8230;/version.txt] version=1.5.0<br> timestamp=11/12/10 10:37<br> githash=937631f</p> <p>STEPS TO REPRODUCE:<br> 1) Pull down the latest titanium_mobile from github<br> 2) Note &#8230;/apidoc/ File.tdoc says:<br> spaceAvailable: return boolean to indicate if the path has space available for storage<br> 3) Note implementation (code in TiFilesystemProxy.m) returns TRUE if space available, FALSE if not</p> <p>SUGGESTED FIX:<br> Return an integer (unsigned, 64-bit?) that shows the number of bytes available; use 0 for none.<br> (Easy to do per code, and the android 2.0 tdoc apparently already says this: platform deviation?)</p> <p>ISSUES:<br> &#8226; How to sync up with Android folks on the new """"""""spec"""""""" created from comparing iOS and Android """"""""realities""""""""<br> &#8226; Thomas helped me write this per QA """"""""Best Practices"""""""" but RFC is always welcome on how to improve the first of many LH tickets<br> (Request for Comments)</p> <p>ISSUES:</p> <p>I don't have Lighthouse permissions / access to set """"""""Who's responsible""""""""</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2334,12,"""setting image to allow edit is broken on the ipad.""","""""""{html}<div><p>on 3.2 using 1.5 images from the photo gallery cannot be resized.</p> <p>code:<br> Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({</p> <pre> <code>    success:function(event)     {         var cropRect = event.cropRect;         var image = event.media;          // set image view         Ti.API.debug('Our type was: '+event.mediaType);         if(event.mediaType == Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO)         {             imageView.image = image;         }         else         {          }          Titanium.API.info('PHOTO GALLERY SUCCESS cropRect.x ' + cropRect.x + ' cropRect.y ' + cropRect.y  + ' cropRect.height ' + cropRect.height + ' cropRect.width ' + cropRect.width);      },     cancel:function()     {         var nm_dialog = Ti.UI.createAlertDialog({             message: 'Canceled',             buttonNames: ['Ok']         });          nm_dialog.show();      },     error:function(error)     {     },     allowEditing:true, //  popoverView:popoverView,     arrowDirection:arrowDirection,     mediaTypes:[Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO,Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO], });</code> </pre> <p>HD Ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/53841"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/53841</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: setting image to allow edit is broken on the ipad.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>on 3.2 using 1.5 images from the photo gallery cannot be resized.</p> <p>code:<br> Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({</p> <pre> <code> success:function(event) { var cropRect = event.cropRect; var image = event.media; // set image view Ti.API.debug('Our type was: '+event.mediaType); if(event.mediaType == Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO) { imageView.image = image; } else { } Titanium.API.info('PHOTO GALLERY SUCCESS cropRect.x ' + cropRect.x + ' cropRect.y ' + cropRect.y + ' cropRect.height ' + cropRect.height + ' cropRect.width ' + cropRect.width); }, cancel:function() { var nm_dialog = Ti.UI.createAlertDialog({ message: 'Canceled', buttonNames: ['Ok'] }); nm_dialog.show(); }, error:function(error) { }, allowEditing:true, // popoverView:popoverView, arrowDirection:arrowDirection, mediaTypes:[Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO,Ti.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_PHOTO], });</code> </pre> <p>HD Ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/53841"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/53841</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2333,12,"""Need to have dialect-specific locale in Ti.Platform.locale""","""""""{html}<div><p>On Android, Ti.Platform.locale returns 'en' for standard English, which is fine. For Canadian and United Kingdom English, Ti.Platform.locale still returns 'en', when it should return 'en-CA' or 'en-GB' respectively. We should also, as much as possible, make sure the dialect strings for Android match exactly what is returned by iOS for cross-platform goodness. iOS seems to use the format 'en-CA' with the dialect capitalized at the end of the string, separated by a hyphen.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Need to have dialect-specific locale in Ti.Platform.locale
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On Android, Ti.Platform.locale returns 'en' for standard English, which is fine. For Canadian and United Kingdom English, Ti.Platform.locale still returns 'en', when it should return 'en-CA' or 'en-GB' respectively. We should also, as much as possible, make sure the dialect strings for Android match exactly what is returned by iOS for cross-platform goodness. iOS seems to use the format 'en-CA' with the dialect capitalized at the end of the string, separated by a hyphen.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2332,12,"""Saving Video to gallery produces crash on iOS""","""""""{html}<div><p>Running on iOS 4.1 using latest 1.5 when saving a video to the photogallery produces a random crash. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn't.</p> <p>Code:</p> <pre> <code>Titanium.Media.showCamera({  success:function(event) {     var video = event.media;     Titanium.Media.saveToPhotoGallery(video); }, cancel:function() {  }, error:function(error) {     // create alert     var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({title:'Video'});      // set message     if (error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_VIDEO)     {         a.setMessage('Device does not have video recording capabilities');     }     else     {         a.setMessage('Unexpected error: ' + error.code);     }      // show alert     a.show(); }, mediaTypes: Titanium.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO, videoMaximumDuration:10000, videoQuality:Titanium.Media.QUALITY_HIGH</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>HD Ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46701"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46701</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Saving Video to gallery produces crash on iOS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Running on iOS 4.1 using latest 1.5 when saving a video to the photogallery produces a random crash. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn't.</p> <p>Code:</p> <pre> <code>Titanium.Media.showCamera({ success:function(event) { var video = event.media; Titanium.Media.saveToPhotoGallery(video); }, cancel:function() { }, error:function(error) { // create alert var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({title:'Video'}); // set message if (error.code == Titanium.Media.NO_VIDEO) { a.setMessage('Device does not have video recording capabilities'); } else { a.setMessage('Unexpected error: ' + error.code); } // show alert a.show(); }, mediaTypes: Titanium.Media.MEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO, videoMaximumDuration:10000, videoQuality:Titanium.Media.QUALITY_HIGH</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>HD Ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46701"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46701</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2331,12,"""Android: TiResourceHelper doesn't expose android stock resources""","""""""{html}<div><p>RHelper (<a href=  """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/25"""""""">https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/25</a>)  fixes this. It is also:</p>  <ul>  <li>generally as fast as TiResourceHelper</li>  <li>significantly faster than TiResourceHelper when cache is  populated</li>  <li>should have better memory usage in general</li>  <li>can free its memory under low-memory constraints</li>  </ul></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TiResourceHelper doesn't expose android stock resources
Description: """"{html}<div><p>RHelper (<a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/25"""""""">https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/25</a>) fixes this. It is also:</p> <ul> <li>generally as fast as TiResourceHelper</li> <li>significantly faster than TiResourceHelper when cache is populated</li> <li>should have better memory usage in general</li> <li>can free its memory under low-memory constraints</li> </ul></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2330,12,"""Android: Detect and Respond to Low Memory Broadcasts""","""""""{html}<div><p>We have several internal caches that should provide a clear method that could be called in low memory alerts from the system and potentially on other cases where we need memory for bitmap processing. Kroll binding cache is one example.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Detect and Respond to Low Memory Broadcasts
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We have several internal caches that should provide a clear method that could be called in low memory alerts from the system and potentially on other cases where we need memory for bitmap processing. Kroll binding cache is one example.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
