TIMOB-2328,12,"""Android: Database - ResultSet.fieldCount method on iOS (as per APIDOCs) but property on Android""","""""""1. Run this code on both iOS/Android and make sure there's no error on both platforms.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Database - ResultSet.fieldCount method on iOS (as per APIDOCs) but property on Android
Description: """"1. Run this code on both iOS/Android and make sure there's no error on both platforms. """"",title+description
TIMOB-2327,12,"""Android: Froyo ID is Non-Unique""","""""""{html}<div><p>There is a bug in Froyo devices and we should probably just generate an ID for each app on device and give up on relying on the platform ID.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Froyo ID is Non-Unique
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There is a bug in Froyo devices and we should probably just generate an ID for each app on device and give up on relying on the platform ID.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2326,12,"""Multiple createLabel() calls inside ScrollableView freeze/crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>I am attaching a sample project that should be reproducible. Simply use the attached files, app.js and scrollview.js.</p> <p>This will create a scrollable view, with every page having a title, Page <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/num"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [num]"""""""">[num]</a>. When started, the app will show page 2, and as you scroll to the right, new pages will be added dynamically.</p> <p>Keep scrolling to the right in a swift pace, and the application will eventually freeze or crash. I usually can't get past page 10, though it should go up to 29.</p> <p>With the 1.4.x SDK, the application freezes, with the latest 1.5.0 it will crash.</p> <p>iPhone SDK is 4.1.</p> <p>I have not run this application on the physical phone yet, only in the simulator.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Multiple createLabel() calls inside ScrollableView freeze/crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I am attaching a sample project that should be reproducible. Simply use the attached files, app.js and scrollview.js.</p> <p>This will create a scrollable view, with every page having a title, Page <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/num"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [num]"""""""">[num]</a>. When started, the app will show page 2, and as you scroll to the right, new pages will be added dynamically.</p> <p>Keep scrolling to the right in a swift pace, and the application will eventually freeze or crash. I usually can't get past page 10, though it should go up to 29.</p> <p>With the 1.4.x SDK, the application freezes, with the latest 1.5.0 it will crash.</p> <p>iPhone SDK is 4.1.</p> <p>I have not run this application on the physical phone yet, only in the simulator.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2325,12,"""iOS: prevent add child to widget (ie. label added to button)""","""""""h2. Problem    Developers should be prevented from adding children to widgets, but it is currently possible on iOS.    Android exhibits the correct behavior.    h2. Test case    {code:lang=javascript}  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({      title:'Window 1',      backgroundColor:'#fff'  });    var moreBtn = Titanium.UI.createButton({      bottom:25,      borderRadius:5,      height:40,      width:120  });    var buttonLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({      backgroundColor:'transparent',      text: 'Find Out More',      color: '#000',      textAlign:'center',      width: 'auto',      height:'auto'  });    moreBtn.add(buttonLabel);  win1.add(moreBtn);  win1.open();    moreBtn.addEventListener('click', function(){      Ti.Platform.openURL('http://www.google.com');  });  {code}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: prevent add child to widget (ie. label added to button)
Description: """"h2. Problem Developers should be prevented from adding children to widgets, but it is currently possible on iOS. Android exhibits the correct behavior. h2. Test case {code:lang=javascript} var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Window 1', backgroundColor:'#fff' }); var moreBtn = Titanium.UI.createButton({ bottom:25, borderRadius:5, height:40, width:120 }); var buttonLabel = Ti.UI.createLabel({ backgroundColor:'transparent', text: 'Find Out More', color: '#000', textAlign:'center', width: 'auto', height:'auto' }); moreBtn.add(buttonLabel); win1.add(moreBtn); win1.open(); moreBtn.addEventListener('click', function(){ Ti.Platform.openURL('http://www.google.com'); }); {code}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2324,12,"""iOS: barImage on iPhone disappears when showing modal window""","""""""h1. Problem  Whenever I have the 'barImage' property set on a window, and then show a modal window on top of that, the bar image on the original window disappears as the modal window is animating. However, the image is restored upon closing the modal window.    h2. Sample Code  Drop the following in to an app.js, and click the button. A modal window will pop up, then close itself after one second. Watch the nav bar, which will have KS_nav_ui.png set as its barImage (make sure this image is available). It will flicker as you click the button.    """"""",Bug,"Title: iOS: barImage on iPhone disappears when showing modal window
Description: """"h1. Problem Whenever I have the 'barImage' property set on a window, and then show a modal window on top of that, the bar image on the original window disappears as the modal window is animating. However, the image is restored upon closing the modal window. h2. Sample Code Drop the following in to an app.js, and click the button. A modal window will pop up, then close itself after one second. Watch the nav bar, which will have KS_nav_ui.png set as its barImage (make sure this image is available). It will flicker as you click the button. """"",title+description
TIMOB-2323,12,"""Android: KitchensSink crashes on launch with uncaught exception""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.5.0.ed78ae2 Android, G2 and droid 1 tested, 2.2 sim</p> <p>1.build and install kitchensink<br> 2.launch it on the device</p> <p>results: crash, full pastie here: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1287757"""""""">http://pastie.org/1287757</a></p> <p>partial log:<br> D/KrollContext( 5276): (kroll$1) [19,634] Running evaluated script: file:///android_asset/Resources/welcome.js<br> I/dalvikvm( 5276): Could not find method org.apache.commons.codec.digest.DigestUtils.md5Hex, referenced from method org.<USER>titanium.util.TiUIHelper.getRAKeyForImage<br> W/dalvikvm( 5276): VFY: unable to resolve static method 2436: Lorg/apache/commons/codec/digest/DigestUtils;.md5Hex (Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/String;<br> D/dalvikvm( 5276): VFY: replacing opcode 0x71 at 0x0088<br> D/dalvikvm( 5276): VFY: dead code 0x008b-00a0 in Lorg/<USER>titanium/util/TiUIHelper;.getRAKeyForImage (Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/String;</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: KitchensSink crashes on launch with uncaught exception
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.5.0.ed78ae2 Android, G2 and droid 1 tested, 2.2 sim</p> <p>1.build and install kitchensink<br> 2.launch it on the device</p> <p>results: crash, full pastie here: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1287757"""""""">http://pastie.org/1287757</a></p> <p>partial log:<br> D/KrollContext( 5276): (kroll$1) [19,634] Running evaluated script: file:///android_asset/Resources/welcome.js<br> I/dalvikvm( 5276): Could not find method org.apache.commons.codec.digest.DigestUtils.md5Hex, referenced from method org.<USER>titanium.util.TiUIHelper.getRAKeyForImage<br> W/dalvikvm( 5276): VFY: unable to resolve static method 2436: Lorg/apache/commons/codec/digest/DigestUtils;.md5Hex (Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/String;<br> D/dalvikvm( 5276): VFY: replacing opcode 0x71 at 0x0088<br> D/dalvikvm( 5276): VFY: dead code 0x008b-00a0 in Lorg/<USER>titanium/util/TiUIHelper;.getRAKeyForImage (Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/String;</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2322,12,"""4.2 compatibility: Test & Package > Distribute Tab and Run on Device Tab - unexpected values appear  ""","""""""{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.install Ralf's 1.4.2 sdk build<br> 2.open an existing ipad or iphone project<br> 3.nav to the distribute tab on test and package<br> 4.check the sdk value drop downs<br> 5.Nav to Run on Device<br> 6.check the sdk value drop downs</p> <p>results: 3.2, 4.0, 4.1, 4.2<br> expected: 4.2 only</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: 4.2 compatibility: Test & Package > Distribute Tab and Run on Device Tab - unexpected values appear
Description: """"{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.install Ralf's 1.4.2 sdk build<br> 2.open an existing ipad or iphone project<br> 3.nav to the distribute tab on test and package<br> 4.check the sdk value drop downs<br> 5.Nav to Run on Device<br> 6.check the sdk value drop downs</p> <p>results: 3.2, 4.0, 4.1, 4.2<br> expected: 4.2 only</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2321,12,"""4.2 compatibility: Invalid targets appear in run emulator Tab for iPad ""","""""""{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.use Ralf's 1.4.2 build, launch developer and open an existing iPad project. Edit tab&gt; select the sdk you installed in step 1<br> 2.open the sim tab, check the sdk drop down for values</p> <p>results: 3.2, 4.0, 4.1, 4.2.<br> expected:3.2 and 4.2 are the only valid ipad sim targets</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: 4.2 compatibility: Invalid targets appear in run emulator Tab for iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.use Ralf's 1.4.2 build, launch developer and open an existing iPad project. Edit tab&gt; select the sdk you installed in step 1<br> 2.open the sim tab, check the sdk drop down for values</p> <p>results: 3.2, 4.0, 4.1, 4.2.<br> expected:3.2 and 4.2 are the only valid ipad sim targets</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2320,12,"""4.2 compatibility: Usability - 3.2 iPhone launches iPad sim (app in iphone idiom) same as xcode ""","""""""{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.Use Ralf's 1.4.2 build<br> 2.Create or open a mobile project. Edit tab&gt; select the sdk you installed in step 1<br> 3.on the sim tab, select 3.2 as the target<br> 4.launch it</p> <p>results: it launches the ipad sim with the app in iphone idiom mode. The user si wondering why they are looking at an ipad when the app they created was specifically not an ipad app (as per TiDev workflow). I belie this is an FOL, but looks odd.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: 4.2 compatibility: Usability - 3.2 iPhone launches iPad sim (app in iphone idiom) same as xcode
Description: """"{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.Use Ralf's 1.4.2 build<br> 2.Create or open a mobile project. Edit tab&gt; select the sdk you installed in step 1<br> 3.on the sim tab, select 3.2 as the target<br> 4.launch it</p> <p>results: it launches the ipad sim with the app in iphone idiom mode. The user si wondering why they are looking at an ipad when the app they created was specifically not an ipad app (as per TiDev workflow). I belie this is an FOL, but looks odd.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2319,12,"""4.2 compatibility: TiDev hangs on when creating a new iPad project on """"checking for iPad prerequisites"""" ""","""""""{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.Use ralf's 1.4.2 sdk build<br> 2.launch tidev, click new project.<br> 3.select ipad</p> <p>results: status window (not sure what to call the window on the top right of developer) shows """"""""checking for iPad prerequisites"""""""", this screen is never dismissed, no project or files are not created</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: 4.2 compatibility: TiDev hangs on when creating a new iPad project on """"checking for iPad prerequisites""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>3.5.4 xcode, iOS sdk 4.2, Ralfs 1.4.2 mobile sdk build. 10.6.4</p> <p>1.Use ralf's 1.4.2 sdk build<br> 2.launch tidev, click new project.<br> 3.select ipad</p> <p>results: status window (not sure what to call the window on the top right of developer) shows """"""""checking for iPad prerequisites"""""""", this screen is never dismissed, no project or files are not created</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
