TIMOB-2316,12,"""iPad - Unexpected behavior for video in split view (Video begins playing on main test screen - does not play on test screen) ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05, Ipad 3g running 4.2</p> <p>1.KS-IPad on 4.2 (occurrs when published from 1.4.1.1 or 1.5.0)<br> 2.launch the app and listen</p> <p>results:audio is heard</p> <p>3.nav to Main tests&gt;embedded video</p> <p>results: video is black with spinner, unexpected """"""""hello"""""""" alerts appear</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad - Unexpected behavior for video in split view (Video begins playing on main test screen - does not play on test screen)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05, Ipad 3g running 4.2</p> <p>1.KS-IPad on 4.2 (occurrs when published from 1.4.1.1 or 1.5.0)<br> 2.launch the app and listen</p> <p>results:audio is heard</p> <p>3.nav to Main tests&gt;embedded video</p> <p>results: video is black with spinner, unexpected """"""""hello"""""""" alerts appear</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2315,12,"""Drillbit: platform-specific resource subfolders don't get created and their files copied""","""""""{html}<div><p>Unless I'm doing it wrong... See my test android/res-img-oom -- it uses platform specific image file which in a real mobile app would go in Resources/android/images/medium/test.png. In Drillbit, processing just stops at """"""""init"""""""" phase.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Drillbit: platform-specific resource subfolders don't get created and their files copied
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Unless I'm doing it wrong... See my test android/res-img-oom -- it uses platform specific image file which in a real mobile app would go in Resources/android/images/medium/test.png. In Drillbit, processing just stops at """"""""init"""""""" phase.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2314,12,"""Android: isExternalStoragePresent Is not Expose as a Method""","""""""{html}<div><p>the method isExternalStoragePresent needs to be annotated and exposed in 1.5. Found while reading source.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: isExternalStoragePresent Is not Expose as a Method
Description: """"{html}<div><p>the method isExternalStoragePresent needs to be annotated and exposed in 1.5. Found while reading source.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2313,12,"""Android: bitmaps fetched by resource id more susceptible to out-of-memory errors""","""""""{html}<div><p>Our internal code that loads bitmaps using resource ids does not have the protection afforded by using certain BitmapFactory.Options which we use when loading the bitmaps by url (instead of resource id). This was an oversight.</p> <p>Failcase:</p> <p>Put the attached PNG into Resources/android/images/medium, then run this app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */ Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#fff',     fullscreen: true,     exitOnClose: true }); win.open();  var tv = Ti.UI.createTableView(); var i = 0; win.add(tv);  var images = []; for (i = 0; i &lt; 25; i++) {     images.push('images/test.png'); }  for (i = 0 ; i &lt; 50; i++) {     var tr = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow();     tr.add(         Ti.UI.createImageView({images: images})     );     tv.appendRow(tr); }</code> </pre> <p>The app should crash and if you look at the logcat you should see similar to:</p> <pre> <code>E/AndroidRuntime(  450): java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: bitmap size exceeds VM budget E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.nativeDecodeAsset(Native Method) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeStream(BitmapFactory.java:447) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeResourceStream(BitmapFactory.java:323) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeResource(BitmapFactory.java:346) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeResource(BitmapFactory.java:372) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiUIHelper.getResourceBitmap(TiUIHelper.java:543) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIImageView.createBitmap(TiUIImageView.java:137) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIImageView$Loader.run(TiUIImageView.java:268) E/AndroidRuntime(  450):    at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1096)</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: bitmaps fetched by resource id more susceptible to out-of-memory errors
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Our internal code that loads bitmaps using resource ids does not have the protection afforded by using certain BitmapFactory.Options which we use when loading the bitmaps by url (instead of resource id). This was an oversight.</p> <p>Failcase:</p> <p>Put the attached PNG into Resources/android/images/medium, then run this app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */ Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen: true, exitOnClose: true }); win.open(); var tv = Ti.UI.createTableView(); var i = 0; win.add(tv); var images = []; for (i = 0; i &lt; 25; i++) { images.push('images/test.png'); } for (i = 0 ; i &lt; 50; i++) { var tr = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow(); tr.add( Ti.UI.createImageView({images: images}) ); tv.appendRow(tr); }</code> </pre> <p>The app should crash and if you look at the logcat you should see similar to:</p> <pre> <code>E/AndroidRuntime( 450): java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: bitmap size exceeds VM budget E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.nativeDecodeAsset(Native Method) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeStream(BitmapFactory.java:447) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeResourceStream(BitmapFactory.java:323) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeResource(BitmapFactory.java:346) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at android.graphics.BitmapFactory.decodeResource(BitmapFactory.java:372) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiUIHelper.getResourceBitmap(TiUIHelper.java:543) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIImageView.createBitmap(TiUIImageView.java:137) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIImageView$Loader.run(TiUIImageView.java:268) E/AndroidRuntime( 450): at java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1096)</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2312,12,"""iOS: Scroll bars on autosize webview are not constrained to view ""","""""""{html}<div><p>3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod. 4.1 and 4.2</p> <p>1.Base UI&gt; Views&gt;Web Views&gt;Autosize<br> 2.place your finger on the view, then move left right a little to vinoke scroll bars (must do it this way to see issue)<br> 3.look at the scroll bars</p> <p>results: they extend above and to the side of the view:</p> <p>expected: constrain scroll bars to view.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Scroll bars on autosize webview are not constrained to view
Description: """"{html}<div><p>3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod. 4.1 and 4.2</p> <p>1.Base UI&gt; Views&gt;Web Views&gt;Autosize<br> 2.place your finger on the view, then move left right a little to vinoke scroll bars (must do it this way to see issue)<br> 3.look at the scroll bars</p> <p>results: they extend above and to the side of the view:</p> <p>expected: constrain scroll bars to view.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2311,12,"""iOS: Foursquare crash  on load""","""""""{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod</p> <p>1.Ks &gt; Mashups &gt; Foursquare<br> 2.enter valid log in credentials<br> 3.tap log in</p> <p>results: on button press, crash. Occurs in 4.1. and 4.2, regression</p> <p>Mon Nov 8 16:29:39 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874][1471] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> starting geo<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:39 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874][1471] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> received geo response<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:39 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874][1471] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> sending foursquare API request for 37.390380859375,-122.0811767578125<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown ReportCrash[1482] : Formulating crash report for <USER>KitchenSink[1471]<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] : (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874]) Job appears to have crashed: Segmentation fault<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown SpringBoard[44] : Application 'KitchenSink' exited abnormally with signal 11: Segmentation fault<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown ReportCrash[1482] : Saved crashreport to /var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter/KitchenSink_2010-11-08-162939_Mr-Pink-iPod.plist using uid: 0 gid: 0, synthetic_euid: 501 egid: 0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Foursquare crash on load
Description: """"{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod</p> <p>1.Ks &gt; Mashups &gt; Foursquare<br> 2.enter valid log in credentials<br> 3.tap log in</p> <p>results: on button press, crash. Occurs in 4.1. and 4.2, regression</p> <p>Mon Nov 8 16:29:39 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874][1471] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> starting geo<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:39 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874][1471] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> received geo response<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:39 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874][1471] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> sending foursquare API request for 37.390380859375,-122.0811767578125<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown ReportCrash[1482] : Formulating crash report for <USER>KitchenSink[1471]<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] : (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x4874]) Job appears to have crashed: Segmentation fault<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown SpringBoard[44] : Application 'KitchenSink' exited abnormally with signal 11: Segmentation fault<br> Mon Nov 8 16:29:40 unknown ReportCrash[1482] : Saved crashreport to /var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter/KitchenSink_2010-11-08-162939_Mr-Pink-iPod.plist using uid: 0 gid: 0, synthetic_euid: 501 egid: 0</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2310,12,"""iOS: Crash on load (bus error) on File download test""","""""""{html}<div><p>3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod occurs in 4.1 and 4.2</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; XHR &gt; File Download</p> <p>results: crashes on load, console:</p> <p>Mon Nov 8 15:08:52 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] : (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x52d8]) Job appears to have crashed: Bus error</p> <p>regression</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Crash on load (bus error) on File download test
Description: """"{html}<div><p>3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod occurs in 4.1 and 4.2</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; XHR &gt; File Download</p> <p>results: crashes on load, console:</p> <p>Mon Nov 8 15:08:52 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] : (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x52d8]) Job appears to have crashed: Bus error</p> <p>regression</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2309,12,"""iOS: Playing remote streaming test case embedded video results in a brief bit of audio from the previous movie playing (4.2 only) ""","""""""{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen) running 4.2</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Play Movie&gt;Embedded Video<br> 2.let the video play to the end, no interaction<br> 3.Dismiss alerts and tap """"""""Remote streaming""""""""</p> <p>results: screen is white and a second or so of the audio fomr the previous test plays before the stream kicks in</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Playing remote streaming test case embedded video results in a brief bit of audio from the previous movie playing (4.2 only)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen) running 4.2</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Play Movie&gt;Embedded Video<br> 2.let the video play to the end, no interaction<br> 3.Dismiss alerts and tap """"""""Remote streaming""""""""</p> <p>results: screen is white and a second or so of the audio fomr the previous test plays before the stream kicks in</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2308,12,"""iOS: Switch test case fails to draw with error ""","""""""{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore<br> 4.1 and 4.2 tested</p> <p>1.Controls&gt;Switch<br> 2.view output</p> <p>Mon Nov 8 13:28:54 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xd446][1038] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Script Error = Result of expression 'Ti.UI.Android' <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/undefined"""""""" title=""""""""Changeset [undefined]"""""""">[undefined]</a> is not an object. at switch.js (line 22).<br> Mon Nov 8 13:28:54 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xd446][1038] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> application received error: Result of expression 'Ti.UI.Android' <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/undefined"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [undefined]"""""""">[undefined]</a> is not an object. at switch.js (line 22)</p> <p>regression</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Switch test case fails to draw with error
Description: """"{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore<br> 4.1 and 4.2 tested</p> <p>1.Controls&gt;Switch<br> 2.view output</p> <p>Mon Nov 8 13:28:54 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xd446][1038] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Script Error = Result of expression 'Ti.UI.Android' <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/undefined"""""""" title=""""""""Changeset [undefined]"""""""">[undefined]</a> is not an object. at switch.js (line 22).<br> Mon Nov 8 13:28:54 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xd446][1038] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> application received error: Result of expression 'Ti.UI.Android' <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/undefined"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [undefined]"""""""">[undefined]</a> is not an object. at switch.js (line 22)</p> <p>regression</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2307,12,"""iOS: TableView layout 4, perf and scrolling issues ""","""""""{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen). seen on 4.1 and 4.2. new since last week.</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt;Views &gt;Table Views&gt; Table Views layout<br> 2.scroll the test</p> <p>results: terrible scrolling performance</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView layout 4, perf and scrolling issues
Description: """"{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen). seen on 4.1 and 4.2. new since last week.</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt;Views &gt;Table Views&gt; Table Views layout<br> 2.scroll the test</p> <p>results: terrible scrolling performance</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2306,12,"""iOS: Invalid method error breaking platform data test (4.2 only) - intermittent, repro'd 3 times, then it worked (?!) ""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen) running 4.2</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; Platform<br> 2.note values</p> <p>results: nothing after """"""""maccadress"""""""" is being shown, console shows the test choking with the following error:<br> Mon Nov 8 09:50:16 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x7c42][826] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Script Error = invalid method 'toString:' at platform.js (line 9).</p> <p>intermittent - not seen later in the day??? Unable to repro, saw it 3X this morning... hate logging these!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Invalid method error breaking platform data test (4.2 only) - intermittent, repro'd 3 times, then it worked (?!)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen) running 4.2</p> <p>1.Platform &gt; Platform<br> 2.note values</p> <p>results: nothing after """"""""maccadress"""""""" is being shown, console shows the test choking with the following error:<br> Mon Nov 8 09:50:16 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x7c42][826] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Script Error = invalid method 'toString:' at platform.js (line 9).</p> <p>intermittent - not seen later in the day??? Unable to repro, saw it 3X this morning... hate logging these!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2305,12,"""iOS - need to post new TiJsCore.a file""","""""""{html}<div><p>We are now going to use a non JIT version of TiJsCore (version 9 as per Blain). We need to have this file posted on amazon.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - need to post new TiJsCore.a file
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We are now going to use a non JIT version of TiJsCore (version 9 as per Blain). We need to have this file posted on amazon.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2304,12,"""iOS: Vertical layout, tableView - scrolling stutters when image is revealed. (3.1.3 - 4.2) ""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen) running 4.2. seen on all supported os's</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; Vertical Layout &gt; Table View<br> 2.do a throw scrolling gesture to move the list rapidly, watch the scroll bar as the image is revealed.</p> <p>results: the scrolling stuttters right as the image is revealed.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Vertical layout, tableView - scrolling stutters when image is revealed. (3.1.3 - 4.2)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is xcode 3.5.4 + iOS4.2 + itunes 10.1+ running mobile sdk version 1.5.0.1f46b05 + the nonJIT version of TiJsCore on an ipod (4th gen) running 4.2. seen on all supported os's</p> <p>1.Base UI &gt; Vertical Layout &gt; Table View<br> 2.do a throw scrolling gesture to move the list rapidly, watch the scroll bar as the image is revealed.</p> <p>results: the scrolling stuttters right as the image is revealed.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2303,12,"""iOS - Need to update scripts to reflect new TiJsCore (1.4.1.1 and 1.5.0)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Now that 4.2 is coming and we have identified the need to go to version 9 for future proofing and to handle various issue between TiDEv and Xcode.</p> <p>The scons build scripts need to be update from 7 to refer to version 9.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Need to update scripts to reflect new TiJsCore (1.4.1.1 and 1.5.0)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Now that 4.2 is coming and we have identified the need to go to version 9 for future proofing and to handle various issue between TiDEv and Xcode.</p> <p>The scons build scripts need to be update from 7 to refer to version 9.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2302,12,"""Android: VideoPlayer doesn't follow HTTP redirects""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is actually an android bug:<br> <a href= """"""""http://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=10810"""""""">http://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=10810</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: VideoPlayer doesn't follow HTTP redirects
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is actually an android bug:<br> <a href= """"""""http://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=10810"""""""">http://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=10810</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2301,12,"""Android: Allow Explicity Attempt to Hide Soft Keyboard""","""""""{html}<div><p>There are various circumstances where an app developer might want to hide the soft input method. Expose a method <code>Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard()</code> to allow them to make the request.</p> <p>Note: Hiding is globally possible, showing doesn't seem to work unless there is an explicit view that accepts input.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Allow Explicity Attempt to Hide Soft Keyboard
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There are various circumstances where an app developer might want to hide the soft input method. Expose a method <code>Ti.UI.Android.hideSoftKeyboard()</code> to allow them to make the request.</p> <p>Note: Hiding is globally possible, showing doesn't seem to work unless there is an explicit view that accepts input.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2300,12,"""HIde Master Popover on iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need to be able to close the Master Popover via code.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: HIde Master Popover on iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need to be able to close the Master Popover via code.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2299,12,"""Some ASI objects leaked""","""""""{html}<div><p>Looks like some ASI objects are not released. Running the following test in instruments revealed that no ASIFormDataRequest objects are ever deallocated:</p> <pre> <code>var count = 0; function runXHR(){     var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient();      xhr.onload = function()     {         count++;         Ti.API.log('available memory:' + Titanium.Platform.availableMemory + ' cnt: ' + count);     };     // open the client     xhr.open('GET','http://www.developedit.com/test.json');      // send the data     xhr.send(); }  runXHR();  setInterval(function() {     runXHR(); },1000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Some ASI objects leaked
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Looks like some ASI objects are not released. Running the following test in instruments revealed that no ASIFormDataRequest objects are ever deallocated:</p> <pre> <code>var count = 0; function runXHR(){ var xhr = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhr.onload = function() { count++; Ti.API.log('available memory:' + Titanium.Platform.availableMemory + ' cnt: ' + count); }; // open the client xhr.open('GET','http://www.developedit.com/test.json'); // send the data xhr.send(); } runXHR(); setInterval(function() { runXHR(); },1000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2298,12,"""Android: Activity refactor""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need to refactor TiActivity and TiBaseActivity in the android module so both are using the same parent class (we can reuse things like TiActivitySupport implementation, etc).</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Activity refactor
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need to refactor TiActivity and TiBaseActivity in the android module so both are using the same parent class (we can reuse things like TiActivitySupport implementation, etc).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2297,12,"""Android: tableView property moving:false not working ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Setting the property moving:false on a tableView does not prevent the table from scrolling.<br> See this modified <a href= """"""""https://gist.github.com/667398"""""""">table_view_basic.js</a> from the KS that demonstrates the issue.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: tableView property moving:false not working
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Setting the property moving:false on a tableView does not prevent the table from scrolling.<br> See this modified <a href= """"""""https://gist.github.com/667398"""""""">table_view_basic.js</a> from the KS that demonstrates the issue.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
