g,"Title: Analytics causes app to crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See this ticket for description and code. Crash happens on iOS 4.1 and 1.5</p> <p>HD Ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52971"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52971</a></p> <p>Console output:<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> The application has crashed with an unhandled exception. Stack trace: 0 CoreFoundation 0x03834b7c <strong>exceptionPreprocess + 156<br> 1 libobjc.A.dylib 0x0398440e objc_exception_throw + 47<br> 2 CoreFoundation 0x0382e7a1 -[</strong>NSArrayM insertObject:atIndex:] + 225<br> 3 CoreFoundation 0x03829bf4 -[<strong>NSArrayM addObject:] + 68<br> 4 nrapp 0x00105666 -[AnalyticsModule flushEventQueue] + 2206<br> 5 Foundation 0x005c776c -[NSThread main] + 81<br> 6 Foundation 0x005c76f8</strong> NSThread<strong>main</strong> + 1387<br> 7 libSystem.B.dylib 0x91d0681d <em>pthread_start + 345<br> 8 libSystem.B.dylib 0x91d066a2 thread_start + 34<br> 2010-11-07 18:50:58.203 nrapp[30829:6f17] <strong><em>Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException', reason: '</em></strong> -[NSMutableArray insertObject:atIndex:]: attempt to insert nil object at 0'<br> *** Call stack at first throw: ( 0 CoreFoundation 0x03834b99 <strong>exceptionPreprocess + 185<br> 1 libobjc.A.dylib 0x0398440e objc_exception_throw + 47<br> 2 CoreFoundation 0x0382e7a1 -[</strong>NSArrayM insertObject:atIndex:] + 225<br> 3 CoreFoundation 0x03829bf4 -[<strong>NSArrayM addObject:] + 68<br> 4 nrapp 0x00105666 -[AnalyticsModule flushEventQueue] + 2206<br> 5 Foundation 0x005c776c -[NSThread main] + 81<br> 6 Foundation 0x005c76f8</strong> NSThread<strong>main</strong> + 1387<br> 7 libSystem.B.dylib 0x91d0681d</em> pthread_start + 345<br> 8 libSystem.B.dylib 0x91d066a2 thread_start + 34<br> ) terminate called after throwing an instance of 'NSException'</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2295,12,"""iOS 4.2: Issue with music picker (blank window, not tabs) and test, 4.2 only ""","""""""{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1, noJIT TiJsCore. iPod touch 4th gen 4.2</p> <p>1.build KS with noted config<br> 2.Phone&gt;Music<br> 3.tap display library, select a song<br> 4.tap play<br> 5.check for the name of song and prog bar to appear</p> <p>rsults: does not</p> <p>6.tap picker settings, the tap library again</p> <p>results: a blank window appears with no tabs (see screen shot). No output seen in console</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 4.2: Issue with music picker (blank window, not tabs) and test, 4.2 only
Description: """"{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1, noJIT TiJsCore. iPod touch 4th gen 4.2</p> <p>1.build KS with noted config<br> 2.Phone&gt;Music<br> 3.tap display library, select a song<br> 4.tap play<br> 5.check for the name of song and prog bar to appear</p> <p>rsults: does not</p> <p>6.tap picker settings, the tap library again</p> <p>results: a blank window appears with no tabs (see screen shot). No output seen in console</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2294,12,"""iOS, 4.2 - shake not being fired (4.2 only) ""","""""""{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1, noJIT TiJsCore. iPod touch 4th gen 4.2</p> <p>1.build KS with noted config<br> 2.Phone&gt;Shake<br> 3.shake the crap out of it</p> <p>results: nada</p> <p>same test on the same hardware running 4.1 had the event fired</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS, 4.2 - shake not being fired (4.2 only)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1, noJIT TiJsCore. iPod touch 4th gen 4.2</p> <p>1.build KS with noted config<br> 2.Phone&gt;Shake<br> 3.shake the crap out of it</p> <p>results: nada</p> <p>same test on the same hardware running 4.1 had the event fired</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2293,12,"""iOS, 4.2 - Image being unexpectedly rotated and scaled on background image test case (4.2 only)  ""","""""""{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1, the no jit TiJsCore</p> <p>1.take a couple shots with the camera in portrait orientation<br> 2.Phone&gt;Save to gallery&gt;Background image<br> 3.select an image<br> 4.note its appearance on the screen</p> <p>results, the image was rotated 90&deg; and was scaled/stretched. not seen with same app on 4.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS, 4.2 - Image being unexpectedly rotated and scaled on background image test case (4.2 only)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1, the no jit TiJsCore</p> <p>1.take a couple shots with the camera in portrait orientation<br> 2.Phone&gt;Save to gallery&gt;Background image<br> 3.select an image<br> 4.note its appearance on the screen</p> <p>results, the image was rotated 90&deg; and was scaled/stretched. not seen with same app on 4.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2292,12,"""iOS, 1.4.1.1, 4.2 noJIT : Remote streaming - """"audio qeue get current timer failed"""" when plugging in/out headphones while stream is playing (4.2 only)""","""""""{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1</p> <p>1.build KS with the noted config<br> 2.Phone&gt;Sound remote streaming<br> 3.start with headphones plugged in or not, while the stream is playing plug it in/ unplug it</p> <p>results:""""""""audio qeue get current timer failed"""""""" and the audio stops. Not seen on same hardware running 4.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS, 1.4.1.1, 4.2 noJIT : Remote streaming - """"audio qeue get current timer failed"""" when plugging in/out headphones while stream is playing (4.2 only)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1</p> <p>1.build KS with the noted config<br> 2.Phone&gt;Sound remote streaming<br> 3.start with headphones plugged in or not, while the stream is playing plug it in/ unplug it</p> <p>results:""""""""audio qeue get current timer failed"""""""" and the audio stops. Not seen on same hardware running 4.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2291,12,"""1.4.1.1, No JIT, 4.2: geolocation test - no reverse geo or update location (4.2 specific issue)""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.use 1.4.1.1. and the no JIT libTiCore (you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1)<br> 2.publish kitchen sink and install on a device running 4.2<br> 3.Phone&gt;Geolocation<br> 4.look at values under updated location and reverse Geo</p> <p>results:updated not fired and reverse geo is never populated. same hardware running 4.1 shows expected behavior on this test.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: 1.4.1.1, No JIT, 4.2: geolocation test - no reverse geo or update location (4.2 specific issue)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.use 1.4.1.1. and the no JIT libTiCore (you'll need xcode 3.5.4,iOSsdk4.2 and itunes 10.1)<br> 2.publish kitchen sink and install on a device running 4.2<br> 3.Phone&gt;Geolocation<br> 4.look at values under updated location and reverse Geo</p> <p>results:updated not fired and reverse geo is never populated. same hardware running 4.1 shows expected behavior on this test.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2290,12,"""KitchenSink errors on launch about Default.png case-insensitive equivalent to default.png""","""""""{html}<div><p>When TiDev creates projects currently, the default.png file in Resources/android is lowercase. Maybe the file currently in the KS was before this was the case. Anyway, it's worth renaming to prevent the error.</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] /opt/android-sdk-linux_86/platforms/android-4/tools/aapt /home/personal/mydir/projects/development/titanium_mobile/demos/KitchenSink/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/Default.png: ERROR File is case-insensitive equivalent to: /home/personal/mydir/projects/development/titanium_mobile/demos/KitchenSink/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/default.png</code> </pre> <p>Discovered on android - not sure if iphone default.png needs to be changed.</p> <p>Pull request to follow...</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink errors on launch about Default.png case-insensitive equivalent to default.png
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When TiDev creates projects currently, the default.png file in Resources/android is lowercase. Maybe the file currently in the KS was before this was the case. Anyway, it's worth renaming to prevent the error.</p> <pre> <code>[ERROR] /opt/android-sdk-linux_86/platforms/android-4/tools/aapt /home/personal/mydir/projects/development/titanium_mobile/demos/KitchenSink/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/Default.png: ERROR File is case-insensitive equivalent to: /home/personal/mydir/projects/development/titanium_mobile/demos/KitchenSink/build/android/bin/assets/Resources/default.png</code> </pre> <p>Discovered on android - not sure if iphone default.png needs to be changed.</p> <p>Pull request to follow...</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2289,12,"""DrillBit: Can't Have More Than Four Test Directories""","""""""{html}<div><p>I tried adding a folder for drillbit tests with various names and it refused to load the folder. When I moved the test up a level it worked.</p> <pre> <code>drwxr-xr-x  3 <USER> staff  102 Nov  3 21:43 android drwxr-xr-x  3 <USER> staff  102 Nov  3 21:43 iphone -rw-r--r--@ 1 <USER> staff  164 Nov  3 21:43 kroll.js -rw-r--r--@ 1 <USER> staff  183 Nov  6 18:22 lh-2288.js drwxr-xr-x  4 <USER> staff  136 Nov  3 21:43 tiapp drwxr-xr-x  3 <USER> staff  102 Nov  6 12:29 tidb</code> </pre> <p>I tried adding <code>drillbit</code>, <code>tidrillbit</code>, <code>tidbit</code> none of which would show up in the UI.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: DrillBit: Can't Have More Than Four Test Directories
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I tried adding a folder for drillbit tests with various names and it refused to load the folder. When I moved the test up a level it worked.</p> <pre> <code>drwxr-xr-x 3 <USER> staff 102 Nov 3 21:43 android drwxr-xr-x 3 <USER> staff 102 Nov 3 21:43 iphone -rw-r--r--@ 1 <USER> staff 164 Nov 3 21:43 kroll.js -rw-r--r--@ 1 <USER> staff 183 Nov 6 18:22 lh-2288.js drwxr-xr-x 4 <USER> staff 136 Nov 3 21:43 tiapp drwxr-xr-x 3 <USER> staff 102 Nov 6 12:29 tidb</code> </pre> <p>I tried adding <code>drillbit</code>, <code>tidrillbit</code>, <code>tidbit</code> none of which would show up in the UI.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2288,12,"""DrillBit: shouldBeFunction fails on Proxy Methods""","""""""{html}<div><p><code>valueOf(Ti.API.debug).shouldBeFunction()</code> fails. It's type is object.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: DrillBit: shouldBeFunction fails on Proxy Methods
Description: """"{html}<div><p><code>valueOf(Ti.API.debug).shouldBeFunction()</code> fails. It's type is object.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2287,12,"""DrillBit: Build Doesn't Detect Changes""","""""""{html}<div><p>There are several instances where it fails.</p> <p>1) If the app is on emulator, it never seems to pick up changes.<br> 2) It doesn't detect that you've scons'd</p> <p>To work around I used the following two command lines in OSX.</p> <pre> <code>adb -e uninstall org.<USER>titanium.testharness &amp;&amp; scons &amp;&amp; drillbit/drillbit.py --android -force -build</code> </pre> <p>and to just do a test change</p> <pre> <code>adb -e uninstall org.<USER>titanium.testharness &amp;&amp; drillbit/drillbit.py --android -force -build</code> </pre> <p>this takes much longer than it should so fewer roundtrips are possible in a given timeframe.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: DrillBit: Build Doesn't Detect Changes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There are several instances where it fails.</p> <p>1) If the app is on emulator, it never seems to pick up changes.<br> 2) It doesn't detect that you've scons'd</p> <p>To work around I used the following two command lines in OSX.</p> <pre> <code>adb -e uninstall org.<USER>titanium.testharness &amp;&amp; scons &amp;&amp; drillbit/drillbit.py --android -force -build</code> </pre> <p>and to just do a test change</p> <pre> <code>adb -e uninstall org.<USER>titanium.testharness &amp;&amp; drillbit/drillbit.py --android -force -build</code> </pre> <p>this takes much longer than it should so fewer roundtrips are possible in a given timeframe.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2286,12,"""DrillBit: Allow Source To Be Viewed for Successful Test""","""""""{html}<div><p>It would be good to see the source when clicking on the line number for a test. That way you can guarantee that it actually ran the code you're expecting.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: DrillBit: Allow Source To Be Viewed for Successful Test
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It would be good to see the source when clicking on the line number for a test. That way you can guarantee that it actually ran the code you're expecting.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2285,12,"""DrillBit: Remember Configuration Between Runs""","""""""{html}<div><p>It would be helpful if drillbit could remember window placement,  size information as well as what tests were selected.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: DrillBit: Remember Configuration Between Runs
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It would be helpful if drillbit could remember window placement, size information as well as what tests were selected.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2284,12,"""Android: regression - picker add method causes exception""","""""""{html}<div><p>Latest build of 1.5.X exhibits exception when picker add()  method is executed.<br>  Tested using <a href=  """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/demos/KitchenSink/Resources/examples/picker_basic.js"""""""">  KS picker_basic.js</a>, which fails at line 15,  picker.add(data);</p>  <p>See <a href=""""""""http://hals-paste.pastebin.com/4kqeYRkM"""""""">trace  log</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: regression - picker add method causes exception
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Latest build of 1.5.X exhibits exception when picker add() method is executed.<br> Tested using <a href= """"""""https://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/demos/KitchenSink/Resources/examples/picker_basic.js""""""""> KS picker_basic.js</a>, which fails at line 15, picker.add(data);</p> <p>See <a href=""""""""http://hals-paste.pastebin.com/4kqeYRkM"""""""">trace log</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2283,12,"""DrillBit: Detect Changed Source""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently, drillbit only rebuilds the app and includes test changes if you restart it. When writing tests or working on test code and app code, it's very cumbersome to have to restart drillbit, toggle tests, select the one test, then select run tests.</p> <p>At a minimum the harness app source should be updated with all source just in case something changed. Ideally, the currently selected tests should be examined for changes and updated within the test harness to reduce round-trip time.</p> <p>Additionally, a refresh option should be added as a global option to force the harness source to be cleaned and then completely regenerated w/o having to restart the framework.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: DrillBit: Detect Changed Source
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently, drillbit only rebuilds the app and includes test changes if you restart it. When writing tests or working on test code and app code, it's very cumbersome to have to restart drillbit, toggle tests, select the one test, then select run tests.</p> <p>At a minimum the harness app source should be updated with all source just in case something changed. Ideally, the currently selected tests should be examined for changes and updated within the test harness to reduce round-trip time.</p> <p>Additionally, a refresh option should be added as a global option to force the harness source to be cleaned and then completely regenerated w/o having to restart the framework.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2282,12,"""iOS: TableView with header and section not working correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>If i use a TableView with a header and a section. The section  has the same height like the TableView header.</p>  <p>how can i fix this.</p>  <p>thanks Marcel</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">  var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({      title: 'Tab 1',      backgroundColor: '#fff'  });     var data = [];     var hv = Titanium.UI.createView({      backgroundColor: '#c3c3c3',      height: 'auto'  });              var hlv = Titanium.UI.createLabel({      text: 'Views',      left: 80,      font: {          fontSize: 14      },      height: 40  });  hv.add(hlv);     var section = Titanium.UI.createTableViewSection({      height: 40,      headerView: hv  });     data.push(section);           data.push({      title: """"""""Row 1""""""""  });     data.push({      title: """"""""Row 2""""""""  });        var view4 = Ti.UI.createView({      backgroundColor: 'black'  });  var l4 = Ti.UI.createLabel({      text: 'View 4',      color: '#fff',      width: 'auto',      height: 'auto'  });  view4.add(l4);     var view3 = Ti.UI.createView({      backgroundColor: 'black'  });  var l3 = Ti.UI.createLabel({      text: 'View 3',      color: '#fff',      width: 'auto',      height: 'auto'  });  view3.add(l3);     var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({      views: [view3, view4],      showPagingControl: true,      pagingControlHeight: 30,      maxZoomScale: 2.0,      currentPage: 1,      height: 150,      top: 0  });              var table = Titanium.UI.createTableView({      headerView: scrollView,      data: data,  });  win1.add(table);</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TableView with header and section not working correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If i use a TableView with a header and a section. The section has the same height like the TableView header.</p> <p>how can i fix this.</p> <p>thanks Marcel</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Tab 1', backgroundColor: '#fff' }); var data = []; var hv = Titanium.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: '#c3c3c3', height: 'auto' }); var hlv = Titanium.UI.createLabel({ text: 'Views', left: 80, font: { fontSize: 14 }, height: 40 }); hv.add(hlv); var section = Titanium.UI.createTableViewSection({ height: 40, headerView: hv }); data.push(section); data.push({ title: """"""""Row 1"""""""" }); data.push({ title: """"""""Row 2"""""""" }); var view4 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'black' }); var l4 = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'View 4', color: '#fff', width: 'auto', height: 'auto' }); view4.add(l4); var view3 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'black' }); var l3 = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'View 3', color: '#fff', width: 'auto', height: 'auto' }); view3.add(l3); var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({ views: [view3, view4], showPagingControl: true, pagingControlHeight: 30, maxZoomScale: 2.0, currentPage: 1, height: 150, top: 0 }); var table = Titanium.UI.createTableView({ headerView: scrollView, data: data, }); win1.add(table);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2281,12,"""iOS: option to download directly to a file""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently it is not possible to download files larger than free memory, and XHR is prone to leaking (see <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/50581"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/50581</a> for a reproducible test case). Providing the ability to save directly to a file (which is supported by ASIHTTPRequest) would work around these issues.</p> <p>Android suffers from the same problem which is being tracked on <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1381""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1381</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: option to download directly to a file
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently it is not possible to download files larger than free memory, and XHR is prone to leaking (see <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/50581"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/50581</a> for a reproducible test case). Providing the ability to save directly to a file (which is supported by ASIHTTPRequest) would work around these issues.</p> <p>Android suffers from the same problem which is being tracked on <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1381""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1381</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2280,12,"""iOS using iOS sdk 4.2 and 1.4.1.1 mobile sdk app crashes on launch in simulator with warning""","""""""{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 ios sdk 4.2, mobile sdk 1.4.1.1</p> <p>1.use the iOS sdk 4.2 and ti mobile 1.4.1.1<br> 2.target the 4.2 sim and launch</p> <p>results, crash with:</p> <p>Detected an attempt to call a symbol in system libraries that is not present on the iPhone:<br> mmap$UNIX2003 called from function _Z20TCMalloc_SystemAllocmPmm in image OldTiJSCore.<br> If you are encountering this problem running a simulator binary within gdb, make sure you 'set start-with-shell off' first.</p> <p>this will be invalidated by the new tiJsCore</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS using iOS sdk 4.2 and 1.4.1.1 mobile sdk app crashes on launch in simulator with warning
Description: """"{html}<div><p>xcode 3.5.4 ios sdk 4.2, mobile sdk 1.4.1.1</p> <p>1.use the iOS sdk 4.2 and ti mobile 1.4.1.1<br> 2.target the 4.2 sim and launch</p> <p>results, crash with:</p> <p>Detected an attempt to call a symbol in system libraries that is not present on the iPhone:<br> mmap$UNIX2003 called from function _Z20TCMalloc_SystemAllocmPmm in image OldTiJSCore.<br> If you are encountering this problem running a simulator binary within gdb, make sure you 'set start-with-shell off' first.</p> <p>this will be invalidated by the new tiJsCore</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2279,12,"""Android: Adview integration needed""","""""""{html}<div><p>Need a supportable AdView (or something similar) for users to attempt to monetize their applications.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Adview integration needed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Need a supportable AdView (or something similar) for users to attempt to monetize their applications.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2278,12,"""Android: aapt warnings are treated as errors""","""""""{html}<div><p>If aapt issues warnings on stderr, builder.py forcefully exits even though in some cases the warnings may not be fatal. As a test put a file starting with a """"""""."""""""" under a directory in platform/android/res, and there should be a """"""""skipping file"""""""" warning.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: aapt warnings are treated as errors
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If aapt issues warnings on stderr, builder.py forcefully exits even though in some cases the warnings may not be fatal. As a test put a file starting with a """"""""."""""""" under a directory in platform/android/res, and there should be a """"""""skipping file"""""""" warning.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2277,12,"""docgen: no alert or advice to user when python SetupTools (and hence easy_install) is missing""","""""""{html}<div><p>If SetupTools is missing and user chooses some other method to install python markdown, they are likely to install an old incompatible version, whereas easy_update installs a compatible version. A message of advice is required.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: docgen: no alert or advice to user when python SetupTools (and hence easy_install) is missing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If SetupTools is missing and user chooses some other method to install python markdown, they are likely to install an old incompatible version, whereas easy_update installs a compatible version. A message of advice is required.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2276,12,"""Android: Services""","""""""{html}<div><ul> <li>Implement Titanium simple services (that are called back on an interval), see spec on <a href= """"""""http://groups.google.com/group/<USER>titanium/browse_thread/thread/fd58557563408bae?hl=en""""""""> Google Groups</a></li> </ul></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Services
Description: """"{html}<div><ul> <li>Implement Titanium simple services (that are called back on an interval), see spec on <a href= """"""""http://groups.google.com/group/<USER>titanium/browse_thread/thread/fd58557563408bae?hl=en""""""""> Google Groups</a></li> </ul></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2275,12,"""Android: Support for min/max/target/tooling SDK in tiapp.xml""","""""""{html}<div><p>We should detect the platform / SDK version based on settings in tiapp.xml (and fall back to r4 if one isn't specified). We'll also need to copy those settings into the AndroidManifest.xml</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support for min/max/target/tooling SDK in tiapp.xml
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We should detect the platform / SDK version based on settings in tiapp.xml (and fall back to r4 if one isn't specified). We'll also need to copy those settings into the AndroidManifest.xml</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2273,12,"""Drillbit: Allow Jump/Filter Log Support""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ideally we should be able to filter the log for a specific test and possibly use """"""""markers"""""""" when viewing the entire log to jump around more easily.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Drillbit: Allow Jump/Filter Log Support
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ideally we should be able to filter the log for a specific test and possibly use """"""""markers"""""""" when viewing the entire log to jump around more easily.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2272,12,"""Drillbit: Clear Log Support""","""""""{html}<div><p>Need the ability to clear the log before starting a test run.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Drillbit: Clear Log Support
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Need the ability to clear the log before starting a test run.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2271,12,"""Drillbit: Add Copy Log Support""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need the ability to copy the log and/or save the log to a  file. Eventually we'll want selection, but for now getting the text  to the clipboard or file is sufficient.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Drillbit: Add Copy Log Support
