TIMOB-2254,12,"""Android: implement new Facebook Graph SDK as module""","""""""{html}<div><p>Facebook is moving away from the REST api &amp; old Facebook Connect stuff. Particularly with Android, they expect developers to use the official SDK (<a href= """"""""https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk)"""""""">https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk)</a>. See esp <a href= """"""""http://bugs.developers.facebook.net/show_bug.cgi?id=13186#c18"""""""">this comment</a> from an internal FB dev in a bug report:</p> <blockquote> <p>The only supported way of logging in via Android apps is to use the Facebook Android SDK which we released last May:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk"""""""">https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk</a></p> <p>It uses OAuth, which is a more future-proof and stable authentication method than the older login.php style that you're using. While we are maintaining backwards compatibliity for the iPhone SDK (well, with the exception of unintentional bugs like this one), we have never supported that mechanism for other devices. I suggest you upgrade the SDK.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: implement new Facebook Graph SDK as module
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Facebook is moving away from the REST api &amp; old Facebook Connect stuff. Particularly with Android, they expect developers to use the official SDK (<a href= """"""""https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk)"""""""">https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk)</a>. See esp <a href= """"""""http://bugs.developers.facebook.net/show_bug.cgi?id=13186#c18"""""""">this comment</a> from an internal FB dev in a bug report:</p> <blockquote> <p>The only supported way of logging in via Android apps is to use the Facebook Android SDK which we released last May:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk"""""""">https://github.com/facebook/facebook-android-sdk</a></p> <p>It uses OAuth, which is a more future-proof and stable authentication method than the older login.php style that you're using. While we are maintaining backwards compatibliity for the iPhone SDK (well, with the exception of unintentional bugs like this one), we have never supported that mechanism for other devices. I suggest you upgrade the SDK.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2253,12,"""Build issues for First Time Developers""","""""""{html}<div><p>SUMMARY<br> When developing with Titanium on Mac OS X (e.g. 10.6.4) for the first time, a test project may likely fail. This happened to me internally, and per Ralf, an external OS X developer following the same prescribed set of steps and versions of all software. The behavior is the difference between downloading Titanium Mobile 1.4.1.1 with the test working, but using git to <USER>1.5.0 (the latest stable release), and scons to build it, results in """"""""execute_xcode"""""""" reporting an ERROR per the output below:</p> <p>DIAGNOSTIC OUTPUT<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 866, in main<br> execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % iphone_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=<strong>LOG</strong>ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version)],False)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 789, in execute_xcode<br> output = run.run(args,False,False,o)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 31, in run<br> sys.exit(rc)<br> SystemExit: 1</p> <p>For further detail, if one sees this behavior, there's more information in build.log (under &lt;YOUR_PROJECT&gt;/build/iphone/build/build.log.<br></p> <p>WORKAROUND:<br> First by deleting the files in the project's build/iphone directory, and then rebuilding, the error went away.</p> <p>Ralf couldn't reproduce this:<br> &#8226; a recent change (unknown at this point) may have created a """"""""build by-products"""""""" issue (i.e. in 1.5.0 from earlier),<br> &#8226; an external developer ran into the same symptoms (see Ralf): Titanium Developer outputs: """"""""builder.py <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a>"""""""" (see above)</p> <p>IMPACT:<br> Developers starting from scratch, like a new (a clean Mac, fresh installs), may benefit from this workaround, but we should explored it more detail</p> <p>ISSUES<br> - Potentially renaming or moving the Titanium SDK folder doesn't change the outcome, and adding spaces like 1.5.0 11_01 may worsens it - Adding spaces to the Titanium SDK path may reveal further bugs and should be tested</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Build issues for First Time Developers
Description: """"{html}<div><p>SUMMARY<br> When developing with Titanium on Mac OS X (e.g. 10.6.4) for the first time, a test project may likely fail. This happened to me internally, and per Ralf, an external OS X developer following the same prescribed set of steps and versions of all software. The behavior is the difference between downloading Titanium Mobile 1.4.1.1 with the test working, but using git to <USER>1.5.0 (the latest stable release), and scons to build it, results in """"""""execute_xcode"""""""" reporting an ERROR per the output below:</p> <p>DIAGNOSTIC OUTPUT<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 866, in main<br> execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % iphone_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=<strong>LOG</strong>ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version)],False)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 789, in execute_xcode<br> output = run.run(args,False,False,o)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 31, in run<br> sys.exit(rc)<br> SystemExit: 1</p> <p>For further detail, if one sees this behavior, there's more information in build.log (under &lt;YOUR_PROJECT&gt;/build/iphone/build/build.log.<br></p> <p>WORKAROUND:<br> First by deleting the files in the project's build/iphone directory, and then rebuilding, the error went away.</p> <p>Ralf couldn't reproduce this:<br> &#8226; a recent change (unknown at this point) may have created a """"""""build by-products"""""""" issue (i.e. in 1.5.0 from earlier),<br> &#8226; an external developer ran into the same symptoms (see Ralf): Titanium Developer outputs: """"""""builder.py <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a>"""""""" (see above)</p> <p>IMPACT:<br> Developers starting from scratch, like a new (a clean Mac, fresh installs), may benefit from this workaround, but we should explored it more detail</p> <p>ISSUES<br> - Potentially renaming or moving the Titanium SDK folder doesn't change the outcome, and adding spaces like 1.5.0 11_01 may worsens it - Adding spaces to the Titanium SDK path may reveal further bugs and should be tested</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2252,12,"""UIImageView objects do not obey size restrictions in tableview""","""""""{html}<div><p>Images are initially drawn at a scaled down size, but upon row refresh/redraw, are the appropriate size.</p> <p>Visible in KS-&gt;Base UI-&gt;Views-&gt;Table View-&gt;Update Row Objects.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: UIImageView objects do not obey size restrictions in tableview
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Images are initially drawn at a scaled down size, but upon row refresh/redraw, are the appropriate size.</p> <p>Visible in KS-&gt;Base UI-&gt;Views-&gt;Table View-&gt;Update Row Objects.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2251,12,"""Android: bottom border of textfield is thicker than the rest""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href=""""""""http://gist.github.com/660457"""""""">this revised  version</a> of textfield_borders.js from the KS and a screenshot  <a href=""""""""http://yfrog.com/f/86screenshot090cp/"""""""">here</a> that  demonstrate this issue.</p>  <p>textArea may well be exhibiting the same problem, although I  haven't had a chance to check.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: bottom border of textfield is thicker than the rest
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href=""""""""http://gist.github.com/660457"""""""">this revised version</a> of textfield_borders.js from the KS and a screenshot <a href=""""""""http://yfrog.com/f/86screenshot090cp/"""""""">here</a> that demonstrate this issue.</p> <p>textArea may well be exhibiting the same problem, although I haven't had a chance to check.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2250,12,"""iOS, iPad: iPhone idiom - _NSAutoreleaseNoPool() leak warning on app shutdown""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2 - Mobile sdk build 1.5.0.8846d87</p> <p>1.install and launch KS (iphone idiom)<br> 2.change tabs, then close the app and check output</p> <p>Tue Nov 2 11:39:19 <USER>Haynies-iPad KitchenSink[18167] : *** _NSAutoreleaseNoPool(): Object 0x4dd6a0 of class NSCFArray autoreleased with no pool in place - just leaking<br> Stack: (0x30363e5b 0x30335d49 0x30335d1b 0x314dd819 0x599d5 0x23e3d 0x23189 0x314deffb 0x26b81 0x30343bd1 0x303afcff 0x33b6678d 0x33b5c078)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS, iPad: iPhone idiom - _NSAutoreleaseNoPool() leak warning on app shutdown
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2 - Mobile sdk build 1.5.0.8846d87</p> <p>1.install and launch KS (iphone idiom)<br> 2.change tabs, then close the app and check output</p> <p>Tue Nov 2 11:39:19 <USER>Haynies-iPad KitchenSink[18167] : *** _NSAutoreleaseNoPool(): Object 0x4dd6a0 of class NSCFArray autoreleased with no pool in place - just leaking<br> Stack: (0x30363e5b 0x30335d49 0x30335d1b 0x314dd819 0x599d5 0x23e3d 0x23189 0x314deffb 0x26b81 0x30343bd1 0x303afcff 0x33b6678d 0x33b5c078)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2249,12,"""iPad video player will not play after being paused""","""""""{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>When a movie is paused outside the default controls the movie will not play again. Using the default controls still works.</p> <h1>Code</h1> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Win' });   var player = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({     contentURL:'ACCESSO_ANTERIORE_XVID.mp4',     scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_MODE_FILL,     width:400,     height:300,     autoplay:false });   var button = Ti.UI.createButton({     title:'Toggle',     height:60,     bottom:120 });   button.addEventListener('click',function() {        if(player.playbackState==Titanium.Media.VIDEO_PLAYBACK_STATE_PLAYING){         player.pause();     }     else{         player.play();      } });   win.add(player); win.add(button); win.open();</code> </pre> <h2>HD Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52221#c238621"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52221#c238621</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad video player will not play after being paused
Description: """"{html}<div><h1>Problem</h1> <p>When a movie is paused outside the default controls the movie will not play again. Using the default controls still works.</p> <h1>Code</h1> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Win' }); var player = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({ contentURL:'ACCESSO_ANTERIORE_XVID.mp4', scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_MODE_FILL, width:400, height:300, autoplay:false }); var button = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Toggle', height:60, bottom:120 }); button.addEventListener('click',function() { if(player.playbackState==Titanium.Media.VIDEO_PLAYBACK_STATE_PLAYING){ player.pause(); } else{ player.play(); } }); win.add(player); win.add(button); win.open();</code> </pre> <h2>HD Ticket</h2> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52221#c238621"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52221#c238621</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2248,12,"""iOS: transform parent and child leads to flicker""","""""""{html}<div><p>Applying transforms to a child and parent views leads to  flickering.<br>  To be more explicit it looks like there is a lag between the  applied transforms.</p>  <p>I trying to apply a rotate transform to 2 views child-parent on  the touchmove.</p>  <p>The initial testcase is this: <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1263792"""""""">http://pastie.org/1263792</a></p>  <p>After some talking on the forum I change it to set the 2d( also  tried with 3d) matrix on touchstart and only modify it on  touchmove. The effect is the same.</p>  <p>The attached screen capture shows the issue. The bike image  should stay steady, but sometimes it moves with the parent view(  the red one) then comes back in position.</p>  <p>Thank you.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: transform parent and child leads to flicker
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Applying transforms to a child and parent views leads to flickering.<br> To be more explicit it looks like there is a lag between the applied transforms.</p> <p>I trying to apply a rotate transform to 2 views child-parent on the touchmove.</p> <p>The initial testcase is this: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1263792"""""""">http://pastie.org/1263792</a></p> <p>After some talking on the forum I change it to set the 2d( also tried with 3d) matrix on touchstart and only modify it on touchmove. The effect is the same.</p> <p>The attached screen capture shows the issue. The bike image should stay steady, but sometimes it moves with the parent view( the red one) then comes back in position.</p> <p>Thank you.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2247,12,"""iOS: with videoMaximumDuration:10000, resulting video is 9 seconds""","""""""{html}<div><p>found on 3g iphone (3.1.2) 4th gen ipod (4.1) mobile sdk build  1.5.0.8846d87</p>  <p>1.Phone&gt;Record movie let it record until it stops, not the  length (10 seconds)<br>  2.play it back by way of button on stage, chekc the ui for  length</p>  <p>results: 9 second video. should be 10. same in 1.4.1.1.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: with videoMaximumDuration:10000, resulting video is 9 seconds
Description: """"{html}<div><p>found on 3g iphone (3.1.2) 4th gen ipod (4.1) mobile sdk build 1.5.0.8846d87</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Record movie let it record until it stops, not the length (10 seconds)<br> 2.play it back by way of button on stage, chekc the ui for length</p> <p>results: 9 second video. should be 10. same in 1.4.1.1.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2246,12,"""iOS: Coverflow remote images fail to load""","""""""{html}<div><p>found on 3g iphone (3.1.2) 4th gen ipod (4.1) mobile sdk build 1.5.0.8846d87</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;Coverflow Remote<br> 2.wait for the images to load</p> <p>they do not</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Coverflow remote images fail to load
