TIMOB-2239,12,"""iOS: Activity indicator is no longer appearing""","""""""{html}<div><p>found on 3g iphone (3.1.2) 4th gen ipod (4.1) mobile sdk build 1.5.0.8846d87</p> <p>1.Controls&gt;activity indicator<br> 2.tap any of buttons to invoke the activity indicator</p> <p>results: not working any more (this is seen everywhere an activity indicator should appear within the tests)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Activity indicator is no longer appearing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>found on 3g iphone (3.1.2) 4th gen ipod (4.1) mobile sdk build 1.5.0.8846d87</p> <p>1.Controls&gt;activity indicator<br> 2.tap any of buttons to invoke the activity indicator</p> <p>results: not working any more (this is seen everywhere an activity indicator should appear within the tests)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2238,12,"""iOS: Add 9-patch functionality, as already implemented in Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>Don Thorpe mentioned that it would not be too difficult to port to iOS the code for 9-patch that has already been implemented in the Android branch.</p> <p>For some background reading, see <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/graphics/2d-graphics.html#nine-patch""""""""> 9-patch info</a> and <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/developing/tools/draw9patch.html""""""""> draw9patch tool</a>.</p> <p>This would obviously make designing layouts for both platforms so much simpler.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add 9-patch functionality, as already implemented in Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Don Thorpe mentioned that it would not be too difficult to port to iOS the code for 9-patch that has already been implemented in the Android branch.</p> <p>For some background reading, see <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/graphics/2d-graphics.html#nine-patch""""""""> 9-patch info</a> and <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/developing/tools/draw9patch.html""""""""> draw9patch tool</a>.</p> <p>This would obviously make designing layouts for both platforms so much simpler.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2237,12,"""Android: TiUIScrollableView showPager() Assumes !null""","""""""{html}<div><p>On 1_4_X branch line 84 <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/1_4_X/android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIScrollableView.java""""""""> TiUIScrollableView.java</a> the showPager method assumes that the scrollable view has """"""""showPagingControl"""""""" as a property.</p> <p>Using the trackball on a G1 caused a customer app to crash with a NPE. See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52401"""""""">Helpdesk 52401</a></p> <p>~~~</p> <p>E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): (main) [2072,15484] Sending event: exception on thread: main msg:java.lang.NullPointerException<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): java.lang.NullPointerException<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiConvert.toBoolean(TiConvert.java:223)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIScrollableView.showPager(TiUIScrollableView.java:84)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at ti.modules.titanium.ui.ScrollableViewProxy.handleMessage(ScrollableViewProxy.java:69)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at android.app.ActivityThread.main(ActivityThread.java:4203)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at java.lang.reflect.Method.invokeNative(Native Method)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:521)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit$MethodAndArgsCaller.run(ZygoteInit.java:791)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit.main(ZygoteInit.java:549)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at dalvik.system.NativeStart.main(Native Method)<br> ~~~</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: TiUIScrollableView showPager() Assumes !null
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On 1_4_X branch line 84 <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/1_4_X/android/modules/ui/src/ti/modules/titanium/ui/widget/TiUIScrollableView.java""""""""> TiUIScrollableView.java</a> the showPager method assumes that the scrollable view has """"""""showPagingControl"""""""" as a property.</p> <p>Using the trackball on a G1 caused a customer app to crash with a NPE. See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/52401"""""""">Helpdesk 52401</a></p> <p>~~~</p> <p>E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): (main) [2072,15484] Sending event: exception on thread: main msg:java.lang.NullPointerException<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): java.lang.NullPointerException<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiConvert.toBoolean(TiConvert.java:223)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at ti.modules.titanium.ui.widget.TiUIScrollableView.showPager(TiUIScrollableView.java:84)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at ti.modules.titanium.ui.ScrollableViewProxy.handleMessage(ScrollableViewProxy.java:69)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at android.app.ActivityThread.main(ActivityThread.java:4203)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at java.lang.reflect.Method.invokeNative(Native Method)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:521)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit$MethodAndArgsCaller.run(ZygoteInit.java:791)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit.main(ZygoteInit.java:549)<br> E/TiUncaughtHandler( 919): at dalvik.system.NativeStart.main(Native Method)<br> ~~~</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2236,12,"""Android: Can't Update Properties of a Map Annotation""","""""""Updating the properties (ex: title, subtitle) of an annotation proxy are being ignored.    h3. Test Case      1. Try clicking the annotation.  2. An alert should pop up saying """"""""click"""""""".  3. Check if the title and subtitle got updated.    Expected: title and subtitle changed  Actual: No changes happen, property updates ignored.  """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Can't Update Properties of a Map Annotation
Description: """"Updating the properties (ex: title, subtitle) of an annotation proxy are being ignored. h3. Test Case 1. Try clicking the annotation. 2. An alert should pop up saying """"""""click"""""""". 3. Check if the title and subtitle got updated. Expected: title and subtitle changed Actual: No changes happen, property updates ignored. """"",title+description
TIMOB-2235,12,"""Ti.Database.ResultSet.fieldName() mangles the database column names""","""""""{html}<div><p>CREATE TABLE foo (myColumn INT);</p> <p>var rs = db.execute(""""""""SELECT myColumn FROM foo"""""""");<br> alert(rs.fieldName(0));</p> <p>On android, the output is 'myColumn'.<br> On iphone, the output is 'mycolumn'. This is wrong.</p> <p>The root cause is logic which provides case-insensitive matching for rs.fieldByName('mycolumn'). This behavior is correct, but the rs.fieldName(0) behavior is not (on iphone only).</p> <p>I've already fixed this in my titanium branch. I've created a merge request here: <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11"""""""">http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Database.ResultSet.fieldName() mangles the database column names
Description: """"{html}<div><p>CREATE TABLE foo (myColumn INT);</p> <p>var rs = db.execute(""""""""SELECT myColumn FROM foo"""""""");<br> alert(rs.fieldName(0));</p> <p>On android, the output is 'myColumn'.<br> On iphone, the output is 'mycolumn'. This is wrong.</p> <p>The root cause is logic which provides case-insensitive matching for rs.fieldByName('mycolumn'). This behavior is correct, but the rs.fieldName(0) behavior is not (on iphone only).</p> <p>I've already fixed this in my titanium branch. I've created a merge request here: <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11"""""""">http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/pull/11</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2234,12,"""iOS: Opening files does not release vnodes""","""""""{html}<div><p>Files which we open never have their vnodes cleaned up. Could be  an Apple bug. Only a problem when opening ~1250 vnodes; this seems  to be the iPhone's limit on the vnode table.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Opening files does not release vnodes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Files which we open never have their vnodes cleaned up. Could be an Apple bug. Only a problem when opening ~1250 vnodes; this seems to be the iPhone's limit on the vnode table.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2233,12,"""Android: Support Alternate Resource Specifiers""","""""""{html}<div><p>The density qualifiers """"""""low"""""""" | """"""""medium"""""""" | """"""""high"""""""" are not sufficient to deal with display sized resources. Add support in android/images to specify other directories to be processed. Note: Special directory naming might be required to force processing unless we limit that folder to only contain processed images. <code>Resources/android/images</code>.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/resources/providing-resources.html#AlternativeResources""""""""> Resource Naming</a> for conventions.</p> <p>The goal is to allow the developer to easily specify images and have the names mangled correctly across all resource folders for Titanium Android apps.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support Alternate Resource Specifiers
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The density qualifiers """"""""low"""""""" | """"""""medium"""""""" | """"""""high"""""""" are not sufficient to deal with display sized resources. Add support in android/images to specify other directories to be processed. Note: Special directory naming might be required to force processing unless we limit that folder to only contain processed images. <code>Resources/android/images</code>.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/resources/providing-resources.html#AlternativeResources""""""""> Resource Naming</a> for conventions.</p> <p>The goal is to allow the developer to easily specify images and have the names mangled correctly across all resource folders for Titanium Android apps.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2232,12,"""iPhones Activity Indicator continues spinning ""","""""""{html}<div><p>After finishing a XHR request at the current nightly build of 1.4.2, the iPhone Activity Indicator does not stop to spin. The error did not occur in a nightly build from the 24th of September. The big issue is that the user thinks that there is still traffic and gets nervous about his/her phone bill.</p> <p>Please see here:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/65381/iphones-activity-indicator-continues-after-load""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/65381/iphones-activity-i...</a></p> <p>Thanks for an urgent fix!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhones Activity Indicator continues spinning
Description: """"{html}<div><p>After finishing a XHR request at the current nightly build of 1.4.2, the iPhone Activity Indicator does not stop to spin. The error did not occur in a nightly build from the 24th of September. The big issue is that the user thinks that there is still traffic and gets nervous about his/her phone bill.</p> <p>Please see here:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/65381/iphones-activity-indicator-continues-after-load""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/65381/iphones-activity-i...</a></p> <p>Thanks for an urgent fix!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2230,12,"""Android: Resolve URL Failing from Event Context""","""""""{html}<div><p>I've attached a sample program.</p> <p>Basically if you have this structure.</p> <p>app.js<br> ParentWindow.js<br> FolderA/ChildWindow.js</p> <p>app.js creates a window using FolderA/ChildWindow.js</p> <p>then in a button click handler in the event an attempt is made to create another new window using """"""""/ParentWindow.js"""""""".</p> <p>This is broken in various forms in 1.4.0, 1.4.2 and 1.5.0</p> <pre> <code>I/WindowProxy(  613): (main) [2,6466] handleOpen E/TiUIWindow(  613): (main) [3,6469] BASEURL: app://FolderA/ E/TiUIWindow(  613): (main) [1,6470] RELURL: /ParentWindow.js I/TiUIWindow(  613): (main) [1,6471] Window has URL: app:/null/ParentWindow.js E/TiContext(  613): (main) [1,6472] BaseURL for context is app:/null D/TiContext(  613): (main) [16,6488] Setting JS Context on org.<USER>titanium.TiContext@44cac1b8 to org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollBridge@44c9a768 D/TiContext(  613): (main) [6,6494] Setting JS Context on org.<USER>titanium.TiContext@44cac1b8 to org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollBridge@44c9a768 D/TiFileFactory(  613): (kroll$3) [7,6501] getting initial from parts: app:/null/ParentWindow.js E/KrollContext(  613): (kroll$3) [10,6511] IOException reading file: app:/null/ParentWindow.js E/KrollContext(  613): java.io.FileNotFoundException: /data/data/net.donthorp.adhoc/app_appdata/app:/null/ParentWindow.js E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.apache.harmony.luni.platform.OSFileSystem.open(OSFileSystem.java:244) E/KrollContext(  613):  at java.io.FileInputStream.&lt;init&gt;(FileInputStream.java:77) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.io.TiFile.getInputStream(TiFile.java:219) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.evaluateScript(KrollContext.java:191) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.handleEvalFile(KrollContext.java:218) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.handleMessage(KrollContext.java:115) E/KrollContext(  613):  at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95) E/KrollContext(  613):  at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollHandlerThread.run(KrollHandlerThread.java:73) E/KrollContext(  613): (kroll$3) [38,6549] Error evaluating source: Wrapped java.io.FileNotFoundException: /data/data/net.donthorp.adhoc/app_appdata/app:/null/ParentWindow.js E/KrollContext(  613): org.mozilla.javascript.WrappedException: Wrapped java.io.FileNotFoundException: /data/data/net.donthorp.adhoc/app_appdata/app:/null/ParentWindow.js E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.mozilla.javascript.Context.throwAsScriptRuntimeEx(Context.java:1781) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.evaluateScript(KrollContext.java:196) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.handleEvalFile(KrollContext.java:218) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.handleMessage(KrollContext.java:115) E/KrollContext(  613):  at android.os.Handler.dispatchMessage(Handler.java:95) E/KrollContext(  613):  at android.os.Looper.loop(Looper.java:123) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollHandlerThread.run(KrollHandlerThread.java:73) E/KrollContext(  613): Caused by: java.io.FileNotFoundException: /data/data/net.donthorp.adhoc/app_appdata/app:/null/ParentWindow.js E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.apache.harmony.luni.platform.OSFileSystem.open(OSFileSystem.java:244) E/KrollContext(  613):  at java.io.FileInputStream.&lt;init&gt;(FileInputStream.java:77) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.io.TiFile.getInputStream(TiFile.java:219) E/KrollContext(  613):  at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.evaluateScript(KrollContext.java:191)</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Resolve URL Failing from Event Context
