TIMOB-2205,12,"""Android regression: typeof returns """"object"""" instead of """"function"""" for native functions""","""""""{html}<div><p>Functions on native proxies and modules are being reported as 'object' by the typeof operator on Android in current 1.5 code from git; they should probably return 'function' to keep from confusing code.</p> <p>This source:<br></p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info('typeof Ti.API.info is: ' + typeof Ti.API.info);</code> </pre> <p>On iOS gives the expected """"""""function"""""""":</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] typeof Ti.API.info is: function</code> </pre> <p>On Android with git trunk we get unexpected """"""""object"""""""":</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] [4,427] typeof Ti.API.info is: object</code> </pre> <p>Whereas under 1.4.1.1 we got """"""""function"""""""" as we expected:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] [2,364] typeof Ti.API.info is: function</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android regression: typeof returns """"object"""" instead of """"function"""" for native functions
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Functions on native proxies and modules are being reported as 'object' by the typeof operator on Android in current 1.5 code from git; they should probably return 'function' to keep from confusing code.</p> <p>This source:<br></p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info('typeof Ti.API.info is: ' + typeof Ti.API.info);</code> </pre> <p>On iOS gives the expected """"""""function"""""""":</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] typeof Ti.API.info is: function</code> </pre> <p>On Android with git trunk we get unexpected """"""""object"""""""":</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] [4,427] typeof Ti.API.info is: object</code> </pre> <p>Whereas under 1.4.1.1 we got """"""""function"""""""" as we expected:</p> <pre> <code>[INFO] [2,364] typeof Ti.API.info is: function</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2204,12,"""1.5.0 regression: Errors accessing custom attributes off of tableViewRow objects (includes testcase)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Seems to have happened recently. Here's a small test case. This same code works under 1.4.1 fine and iPhone fine:</p> <pre> <code>var testDate = new Date(); var dateObj = {bla:""""""""foo"""""""", testDateObj:testDate}; var noDateObj = {bla:""""""""foo""""""""};  var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({     _dateObj: dateObj,     _noDateObj: noDateObj,     _testDate: testDate });  Ti.API.info(""""""""works: """""""" + row._noDateObj.bla); Ti.API.info(""""""""fails: """""""" + row._dateObj.bla); //Constructor for """"""""Date"""""""" not found Ti.API.info(""""""""fails: """""""" + row._dateObj.testDateObj); Ti.API.info(""""""""fails: """""""" + row._testDate);  //Also, may be of interest: //Ti.API.info(""""""""1: """""""" + row._noDateObj); //""""""""cannot find default value for object"""""""" ...is that what should happen? //Ti.API.info(""""""""2: """""""" + row._dateObj); //""""""""cannot find default value for object"""""""" as well</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: 1.5.0 regression: Errors accessing custom attributes off of tableViewRow objects (includes testcase)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Seems to have happened recently. Here's a small test case. This same code works under 1.4.1 fine and iPhone fine:</p> <pre> <code>var testDate = new Date(); var dateObj = {bla:""""""""foo"""""""", testDateObj:testDate}; var noDateObj = {bla:""""""""foo""""""""}; var row = Ti.UI.createTableViewRow({ _dateObj: dateObj, _noDateObj: noDateObj, _testDate: testDate }); Ti.API.info(""""""""works: """""""" + row._noDateObj.bla); Ti.API.info(""""""""fails: """""""" + row._dateObj.bla); //Constructor for """"""""Date"""""""" not found Ti.API.info(""""""""fails: """""""" + row._dateObj.testDateObj); Ti.API.info(""""""""fails: """""""" + row._testDate); //Also, may be of interest: //Ti.API.info(""""""""1: """""""" + row._noDateObj); //""""""""cannot find default value for object"""""""" ...is that what should happen? //Ti.API.info(""""""""2: """""""" + row._dateObj); //""""""""cannot find default value for object"""""""" as well</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2203,12,"""Android: Support runnable threads""","""""""{html}<div><p>Is it possible to build in runnable threads? Too many times I've been running intensive XHR requests, and they lock up the UI portion of the app. Would it be possible to implement such a feature to allow the request to run in the background, whilst still keeping the UI free?</p> <p>I've thrown around some code today that isn't of any quality, but with the Ti proxies and such, I don't think it would be hard to implement a ThreadManager module (for namesake).</p> <p>Andrew</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Support runnable threads
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Is it possible to build in runnable threads? Too many times I've been running intensive XHR requests, and they lock up the UI portion of the app. Would it be possible to implement such a feature to allow the request to run in the background, whilst still keeping the UI free?</p> <p>I've thrown around some code today that isn't of any quality, but with the Ti proxies and such, I don't think it would be hard to implement a ThreadManager module (for namesake).</p> <p>Andrew</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2202,12,"""iOS - intermittent behavior with Facebook (including crash)""","""""""{html}<div><p>occurs in 1.4.1.1 and 1.5.0</p> <p>1.KS&gt;Mashups&gt;Facebook<br> 2.log in, then try other tests</p> <p>results: intermittently the app will crash. We've had reports that call backs are failing as well, unable to repro that. crash log attached.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - intermittent behavior with Facebook (including crash)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>occurs in 1.4.1.1 and 1.5.0</p> <p>1.KS&gt;Mashups&gt;Facebook<br> 2.log in, then try other tests</p> <p>results: intermittently the app will crash. We've had reports that call backs are failing as well, unable to repro that. crash log attached.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
