TIMOB-2197,12,"""iOS 3.2.2 and older (iPad/iPod/iPhone) : ScrollViews/text area - scroll view not scrolling with keyboard up after tapping out of the first field.""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2, TiMobile sdk version 1.5.0.5dc262e</p> <p>1.KS (iPhone idiom)&gt;baseUI&gt;Views&gt;Scroll Views TextArea<br> 2.tap into a text area to invoke keyboard, then try and scroll the view (works)<br> 3.tap into a second text area, then try to scroll the view</p> <p>results: scrolling no longer works for the view. 3.2.2 and earlier only. Not seeing this on 4.0 or 4.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS 3.2.2 and older (iPad/iPod/iPhone) : ScrollViews/text area - scroll view not scrolling with keyboard up after tapping out of the first field.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2, TiMobile sdk version 1.5.0.5dc262e</p> <p>1.KS (iPhone idiom)&gt;baseUI&gt;Views&gt;Scroll Views TextArea<br> 2.tap into a text area to invoke keyboard, then try and scroll the view (works)<br> 3.tap into a second text area, then try to scroll the view</p> <p>results: scrolling no longer works for the view. 3.2.2 and earlier only. Not seeing this on 4.0 or 4.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2196,12,"""iOS: iPad - PhotoGallery - preview does not allow user to change image positioning""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2, TiMobile sdk version 1.5.0.5dc262e</p>  <p>1.Phone&gt; Photo Gallery<br>  2.select an image from your library when promtped to do so<br>  3.in the resulting window, try to change the positioning of the  image</p>  <p>results: you can't, on release the image returns to its original  position.<br>  This differs from ipod/iphone</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad - PhotoGallery - preview does not allow user to change image positioning
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2, TiMobile sdk version 1.5.0.5dc262e</p> <p>1.Phone&gt; Photo Gallery<br> 2.select an image from your library when promtped to do so<br> 3.in the resulting window, try to change the positioning of the image</p> <p>results: you can't, on release the image returns to its original position.<br> This differs from ipod/iphone</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2195,12,"""iOS: Titanium.Platform.batteryLevel always reports back -1 on iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2, TiMobile sdk version 1.5.0.5dc262e</p>  <p>1.query Titanium.Platform.batteryLevel on an ipad that is  plugged in<br>  2.repeat with it unplugged</p>  <p>results: -1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Titanium.Platform.batteryLevel always reports back -1 on iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2, TiMobile sdk version 1.5.0.5dc262e</p> <p>1.query Titanium.Platform.batteryLevel on an ipad that is plugged in<br> 2.repeat with it unplugged</p> <p>results: -1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2194,12,"""iOS: Contexts are not closed""","""""""{html}<div><p>Contexts are not currently closed. This is because there were a  series of bugs involving contexts where closing a context  would:</p>  <ul>  <li>Invalidate certain windows which were opened from inside a  context which was then closed</li>  <li>Closing a context could interact unfavorably with certain types  of event listeners</li>  </ul>  <p>Unfortunately I no longer have the specific bug #s for bugs  caused by context shutdown so that context cleanup can be  tested.</p>  <p>Context cleanup is an extremely important task and this should  be considered a <strong>CRITICAL BUG</strong>.</p>  <p>Assigning to Blain for bookkeeping.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Contexts are not closed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Contexts are not currently closed. This is because there were a series of bugs involving contexts where closing a context would:</p> <ul> <li>Invalidate certain windows which were opened from inside a context which was then closed</li> <li>Closing a context could interact unfavorably with certain types of event listeners</li> </ul> <p>Unfortunately I no longer have the specific bug #s for bugs caused by context shutdown so that context cleanup can be tested.</p> <p>Context cleanup is an extremely important task and this should be considered a <strong>CRITICAL BUG</strong>.</p> <p>Assigning to Blain for bookkeeping.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2193,12,"""iOS: Dynamic load/unload of scrollable view frames""","""""""{html}<div><p>At some point we need to investigate whether or not we can  dynamically load and unload views used by scrollableview, so that  we can provide better memory management for them.</p>  <p>Assigning this to Blain for record keeping.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Dynamic load/unload of scrollable view frames
Description: """"{html}<div><p>At some point we need to investigate whether or not we can dynamically load and unload views used by scrollableview, so that we can provide better memory management for them.</p> <p>Assigning this to Blain for record keeping.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2191,12,"""Android: Add View support to AlertDialog""","""""""{html}<div><p>Add support for property 'androidView' as a platform specific option for AlertDialog. Note in the example I added a second invisible view to force the size of the message container. It's a side-effect of view as a top-most container.</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : 'white'}); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({     title : 'Open Dialog' });  btn.addEventListener('click', function(e) {     var dialog = null;     var view = Ti.UI.createView({         backgroundColor : 'red',         width : 200,         height : 200     });          var v2 = Ti.UI.createView({         wrap : false,         width : 300,         height : 300     });     view.add(v2);          var viewBtn = Ti.UI.createButton({         title : 'Click Me',         width : 200,         height : 200     });     view.add(viewBtn);          viewBtn.addEventListener('click', function(e) {         dialog.hide();     });      dialog = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({         buttonNames : ['Cancel'],         title:'I am a title',             androidView : view     });       dialog.addEventListener('click', function(e) {         Ti.API.error(""""""""CLICK - ID: """""""" + e.index + """""""" cancel: """""""" + e.cancel + """""""" button: """""""" + e.button);     });          dialog.show(); }); win.add(btn); win.open({animated:false});</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add View support to AlertDialog
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Add support for property 'androidView' as a platform specific option for AlertDialog. Note in the example I added a second invisible view to force the size of the message container. It's a side-effect of view as a top-most container.</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : 'white'}); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Open Dialog' }); btn.addEventListener('click', function(e) { var dialog = null; var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor : 'red', width : 200, height : 200 }); var v2 = Ti.UI.createView({ wrap : false, width : 300, height : 300 }); view.add(v2); var viewBtn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Click Me', width : 200, height : 200 }); view.add(viewBtn); viewBtn.addEventListener('click', function(e) { dialog.hide(); }); dialog = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog({ buttonNames : ['Cancel'], title:'I am a title', androidView : view }); dialog.addEventListener('click', function(e) { Ti.API.error(""""""""CLICK - ID: """""""" + e.index + """""""" cancel: """""""" + e.cancel + """""""" button: """""""" + e.button); }); dialog.show(); }); win.add(btn); win.open({animated:false});</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2190,12,"""iOS : Slider touch end event seems to be fired at least 2X""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.using this script:</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;<br> var slider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({<br> min:0,<br> max:100,<br> value:5,<br> width:100,<br> height:'auto',<br> top:30<br> });</p> <p>slider.addEventListener('touchend', function(e){<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""touchend"""""""");<br> }); win.add(slider);</p> <p>2.drag the slider some and relase - view output</p> <p>results:<br> Mon Oct 25 15:01:50 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>QAtests[0x3e9c][128] : <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> touchend<br> Mon Oct 25 15:01:50 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>QAtests[0x3e9c][128] : <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> touchend</p> <p>I can't seem to get less than 2X events, sometimes more (when dragging to end).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Slider touch end event seems to be fired at least 2X
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.using this script:</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;<br> var slider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({<br> min:0,<br> max:100,<br> value:5,<br> width:100,<br> height:'auto',<br> top:30<br> });</p> <p>slider.addEventListener('touchend', function(e){<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""touchend"""""""");<br> }); win.add(slider);</p> <p>2.drag the slider some and relase - view output</p> <p>results:<br> Mon Oct 25 15:01:50 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>QAtests[0x3e9c][128] : <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> touchend<br> Mon Oct 25 15:01:50 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>QAtests[0x3e9c][128] : <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> touchend</p> <p>I can't seem to get less than 2X events, sometimes more (when dragging to end).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2189,12,"""iOS: Text field in scroll view - with keyboard up, tapping into the bottom most field forces it offscreen, then back onscreen""","""""""{html}<div><p>4th gen ipod running 4.1, 3g iphone 3.1.2 .5.0.77ad8ac</p> <p>1.controls&gt;text field&gt;textfield in scroll view<br> 2.tap into the top most field to invoke keybard<br> 3.scroll down to reveal the text field on the bottom (labeled """"""""bottom"""""""")<br> 4.tap in and watch field</p> <p>result:it forces the field off screen, then it scrolls back<br> expected: no animation, field is visible, just invoke keyboard.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Text field in scroll view - with keyboard up, tapping into the bottom most field forces it offscreen, then back onscreen
Description: """"{html}<div><p>4th gen ipod running 4.1, 3g iphone 3.1.2 .5.0.77ad8ac</p> <p>1.controls&gt;text field&gt;textfield in scroll view<br> 2.tap into the top most field to invoke keybard<br> 3.scroll down to reveal the text field on the bottom (labeled """"""""bottom"""""""")<br> 4.tap in and watch field</p> <p>result:it forces the field off screen, then it scrolls back<br> expected: no animation, field is visible, just invoke keyboard.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2188,12,"""iOS : Duplicate alerts followed by a crash on remote video test case""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPod 4th gen (4.1), 3rd gen 4.0.2 with mobile sdk build 1.5.0.77ad8ac</p> <p>1.KS&gt;phone&gt;play movie&gt;remote streaming<br> 2.scrub till you have about 20 seconds left, let it play through<br> 3.see the alerts (completed, X2, then window closed, then movie completed again)<br> 4.Nav back a level</p> <p>results: crash</p> <p>Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown KitchenSink[4435] : KitchenSink(4435,0x72e9000) malloc: *** error for object 0x4afc40: pointer being freed was not allocated<br></p> <pre> <code>*** set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug</code> </pre> <p>Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbc59][4435] : KitchenSink(4435,0x72e9000) malloc: <strong><em>error for object 0x4afc40: pointer being freed was not allocated<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbc59][4435] :</em></strong> set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown ReportCrash[4441] : Formulating crash report for <USER>KitchenSink[4435]<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:10 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] : (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbc59]) Job appears to have crashed: Abort trap<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:10 unknown SpringBoard[27] : Application 'KitchenSink' exited abnormally with signal 6: Abort trap<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:10 unknown ReportCrash[4441] : Saved crashreport to /var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter/KitchenSink_2010-10-25-114609_eWorld.plist using uid: 0 gid: 0, synthetic_euid: 501 egid: 0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Duplicate alerts followed by a crash on remote video test case
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPod 4th gen (4.1), 3rd gen 4.0.2 with mobile sdk build 1.5.0.77ad8ac</p> <p>1.KS&gt;phone&gt;play movie&gt;remote streaming<br> 2.scrub till you have about 20 seconds left, let it play through<br> 3.see the alerts (completed, X2, then window closed, then movie completed again)<br> 4.Nav back a level</p> <p>results: crash</p> <p>Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown KitchenSink[4435] : KitchenSink(4435,0x72e9000) malloc: *** error for object 0x4afc40: pointer being freed was not allocated<br></p> <pre> <code>*** set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug</code> </pre> <p>Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbc59][4435] : KitchenSink(4435,0x72e9000) malloc: <strong><em>error for object 0x4afc40: pointer being freed was not allocated<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbc59][4435] :</em></strong> set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:09 unknown ReportCrash[4441] : Formulating crash report for <USER>KitchenSink[4435]<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:10 unknown com.apple.launchd[1] : (UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbc59]) Job appears to have crashed: Abort trap<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:10 unknown SpringBoard[27] : Application 'KitchenSink' exited abnormally with signal 6: Abort trap<br> Mon Oct 25 11:46:10 unknown ReportCrash[4441] : Saved crashreport to /var/mobile/Library/Logs/CrashReporter/KitchenSink_2010-10-25-114609_eWorld.plist using uid: 0 gid: 0, synthetic_euid: 501 egid: 0</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2187,12,"""iOS:  Double completion alerts when video reaches end of scrubber""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPod 4th gen (4.1), 3rd gen 4.0.2 with mobile sdk build 1.5.0.77ad8ac</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Play movie&gt;any of the tests<br> 2.allow them to play to the end or drag the scrubber to the end<br> 3.watch thre alerts when the movie is done</p> <p>results: 2X - 3X """"""""movie completed""""""""</p> <p>expected: just one (remote streaming produces 3X alerts)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Double completion alerts when video reaches end of scrubber
