TIMOB-2178,12,"""Black does not work in a background gradient iOS""","""""""{html}<div><p>Running on the iphone, setting a background gradient color to black does not work, Setting it to 000001 does work however.</p> <p>Code:<br> var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var view = Titanium.UI.createView({<br></p> <pre> <code>top:0, left:0, //height:height, //width:width, backgroundGradient:{         type:'linear',         colors:[{color:'#50FFFF',position:0.0},{color:'#000000',position:1.0}]     }</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(view);</p> <p>HD ticket<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51211"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51211</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Black does not work in a background gradient iOS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Running on the iphone, setting a background gradient color to black does not work, Setting it to 000001 does work however.</p> <p>Code:<br> var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var view = Titanium.UI.createView({<br></p> <pre> <code>top:0, left:0, //height:height, //width:width, backgroundGradient:{ type:'linear', colors:[{color:'#50FFFF',position:0.0},{color:'#000000',position:1.0}] }</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(view);</p> <p>HD ticket<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51211"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/51211</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2177,12,"""Changing hardware in the middle of playback/recording may cause crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>Easiest to test on an iPod. With headphones+mic plugged in:</p> <p>KS-&gt;Phone-&gt;Sound-&gt;Record<br> Begin Recording<br> After recording a message, yank the headphones (do NOT click the 'stop recording' button)<br> Click 'playback' (you will hear nothing, and the button will never change from 'stop playback')<br> Plug headphones back in<br> Click 'record' again<br> CRASH</p> <p>The first part of the bug (no playback) probably has something to do with how the recorder handles audio queues and whether or not it even saves the file produced by the recording. Second part of the bug is probably a session issue, where the audio session continues to try and use the previous hardware.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Changing hardware in the middle of playback/recording may cause crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Easiest to test on an iPod. With headphones+mic plugged in:</p> <p>KS-&gt;Phone-&gt;Sound-&gt;Record<br> Begin Recording<br> After recording a message, yank the headphones (do NOT click the 'stop recording' button)<br> Click 'playback' (you will hear nothing, and the button will never change from 'stop playback')<br> Plug headphones back in<br> Click 'record' again<br> CRASH</p> <p>The first part of the bug (no playback) probably has something to do with how the recorder handles audio queues and whether or not it even saves the file produced by the recording. Second part of the bug is probably a session issue, where the audio session continues to try and use the previous hardware.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2176,12,"""Android - custom slider crashes (device and sim)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using the following script and TiMobile 1.5.0.70ce98 g2 running 2.2 crashes on load.</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>backgroundColor : 'white'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var customSlider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({<br></p> <pre> <code>min:0, max:100, value:25, width:268, height:40, top:90, thumbImage: 'images/custom-slider-handle.png', leftTrackImage: 'images/custom-slider-left.9.png', rightTrackImage: 'images/custom-slider-right.9.png'</code> </pre> <p>}); win.add(customSlider);<br> win.open();</p> <p>pastie crash log: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1241601"""""""">http://pastie.org/1241601</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android - custom slider crashes (device and sim)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using the following script and TiMobile 1.5.0.70ce98 g2 running 2.2 crashes on load.</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>backgroundColor : 'white'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var customSlider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({<br></p> <pre> <code>min:0, max:100, value:25, width:268, height:40, top:90, thumbImage: 'images/custom-slider-handle.png', leftTrackImage: 'images/custom-slider-left.9.png', rightTrackImage: 'images/custom-slider-right.9.png'</code> </pre> <p>}); win.add(customSlider);<br> win.open();</p> <p>pastie crash log: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1241601"""""""">http://pastie.org/1241601</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2175,12,"""Removing a view from the middle of the ScollableView index causes an exception""","""""""{html}<div><p>Please see this <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/72621/scrollableview-removeview-and-addview-behaviour-on-android""""""""> Q&amp;A</a> for a description of the problem.</p> <p>The following code demonstrates the issue. Run the script and click the first button - this is the workaround I have described in the Q&amp;A. Then restart the script and click the second button to see the exception.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/641174"""""""">http://gist.github.com/641174</a></p> <p>Note: This is definitely an issue on android. Need confirmation whether the same bug exists on IOS.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Removing a view from the middle of the ScollableView index causes an exception
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Please see this <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/72621/scrollableview-removeview-and-addview-behaviour-on-android""""""""> Q&amp;A</a> for a description of the problem.</p> <p>The following code demonstrates the issue. Run the script and click the first button - this is the workaround I have described in the Q&amp;A. Then restart the script and click the second button to see the exception.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/641174"""""""">http://gist.github.com/641174</a></p> <p>Note: This is definitely an issue on android. Need confirmation whether the same bug exists on IOS.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2174,12,"""Android: Expose ThumbOffset on Slider""","""""""{html}<div><p>By default the thumb graphic is offset by half the image. Expose the value to the developer as <code>thumbOffset</code> (android only) and default it to 0 offset.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose ThumbOffset on Slider
Description: """"{html}<div><p>By default the thumb graphic is offset by half the image. Expose the value to the developer as <code>thumbOffset</code> (android only) and default it to 0 offset.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
