TIMOB-2151,12,"""Android: Set Row data test case leaves rows (the next row not shown on screen)""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.5.0.70ce98 g2 running 2.2, G1 running 1.6, sim 2.2.</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;TableViews&gt;Set Row Data<br> 2.go portrait<br> 3.Tap set 1 (no animation)<br> 4.repeat in landscape</p> <p>results: in both cases the table view is gone and the first row that was offscreen before button press is shown.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Set Row data test case leaves rows (the next row not shown on screen)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.5.0.70ce98 g2 running 2.2, G1 running 1.6, sim 2.2.</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;TableViews&gt;Set Row Data<br> 2.go portrait<br> 3.Tap set 1 (no animation)<br> 4.repeat in landscape</p> <p>results: in both cases the table view is gone and the first row that was offscreen before button press is shown.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2150,12,"""Android, parse problem with URLs that contain @ in username ""","""""""{html}<div><p>When sending a request to XHR to the following URL:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Private.svc/GetCustomer""""""""> http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Priva...</a></p> <p>The request is directed to demandocat.com instead of api.lafitness.com.</p> <p>Some sort of issue exists parsing URLs that contain username/passwords when they contain the @ char.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android, parse problem with URLs that contain @ in username
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When sending a request to XHR to the following URL:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Private.svc/GetCustomer""""""""> http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Priva...</a></p> <p>The request is directed to demandocat.com instead of api.lafitness.com.</p> <p>Some sort of issue exists parsing URLs that contain username/passwords when they contain the @ char.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2149,12,"""Android, parse problem with URLs that contain @ in username ""","""""""{html}<div><p>When sending a request to XHR to the following URL:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Private.svc/GetCustomer""""""""> http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Priva...</a></p> <p>The request is directed to demandocat.com instead of api.lafitness.com.</p> <p>Some sort of issue exists parsing URLs that contain username/passwords when they contain the @ char.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android, parse problem with URLs that contain @ in username
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When sending a request to XHR to the following URL:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Private.svc/GetCustomer""""""""> http://<EMAIL>:<EMAIL>/Services/Priva...</a></p> <p>The request is directed to demandocat.com instead of api.lafitness.com.</p> <p>Some sort of issue exists parsing URLs that contain username/passwords when they contain the @ char.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2148,12,"""IOS: sound_record.js from KS crashes when inoked in another app""","""""""{html}<div><p>I am using the exact sound_record.js file from KS in another app.</p> <p>The repro steps are:</p> <p>hit the start recording button<br> """"""""say something"""""""" hit the stop recording button</p> <p>Note: It will not flip the button label back to [start recording], as it does in KS<br> (maybe it is stil recording?)</p> <p>When you leave the window, the app crashes (log attached)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: IOS: sound_record.js from KS crashes when inoked in another app
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I am using the exact sound_record.js file from KS in another app.</p> <p>The repro steps are:</p> <p>hit the start recording button<br> """"""""say something"""""""" hit the stop recording button</p> <p>Note: It will not flip the button label back to [start recording], as it does in KS<br> (maybe it is stil recording?)</p> <p>When you leave the window, the app crashes (log attached)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2147,12,"""Android: PRAGMA and non-SELECT statements return null from Ti.Database.DB.execute() instead of ResultSet""","""""""{html}<div><p>I'm attempting to upgrade a database table from a prior revision of my app by checking if fields are present on a table. To do this, I'm using SQLite's PRAGMA statement:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""sql"""""""">  PRAGMA table_info(account)</code> </pre> <p>On iOS w/ current git-master code this works fine, as well as directly hitting databases with 'sqlite3'. However on Android, DB.execute() returns null instead of a ResultSet object, so I cannot access any of the returned data.</p> <p>This appears to be because the Android TiDatabaseProxy.java assumes that only SELECT statements can ever return data:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""java"""""""">if(sql.trim().toLowerCase().startsWith(""""""""select"""""""")) {     c = db.rawQuery(sql, newArgs);     if (c != null) {         rs = new TiResultSetProxy(getTiContext(), c);         if (rs.isValidRow()) {             rs.next(); // Position on first row if we have data.         }     } else {         rs = new TiResultSetProxy(getTiContext(), null); // because iPhone does it this way.     } } else {     if (args != null) {         db.execSQL(sql, args);     } else {         db.execSQL(sql);     } }</code> </pre> <p>The iPhone implementation on the other hand doesn't make any such assumption, and ships every query through the same code paths. If the result info from the DB has no columns, then it returns null instead of a ResultSet.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: PRAGMA and non-SELECT statements return null from Ti.Database.DB.execute() instead of ResultSet
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I'm attempting to upgrade a database table from a prior revision of my app by checking if fields are present on a table. To do this, I'm using SQLite's PRAGMA statement:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""sql""""""""> PRAGMA table_info(account)</code> </pre> <p>On iOS w/ current git-master code this works fine, as well as directly hitting databases with 'sqlite3'. However on Android, DB.execute() returns null instead of a ResultSet object, so I cannot access any of the returned data.</p> <p>This appears to be because the Android TiDatabaseProxy.java assumes that only SELECT statements can ever return data:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""java"""""""">if(sql.trim().toLowerCase().startsWith(""""""""select"""""""")) { c = db.rawQuery(sql, newArgs); if (c != null) { rs = new TiResultSetProxy(getTiContext(), c); if (rs.isValidRow()) { rs.next(); // Position on first row if we have data. } } else { rs = new TiResultSetProxy(getTiContext(), null); // because iPhone does it this way. } } else { if (args != null) { db.execSQL(sql, args); } else { db.execSQL(sql); } }</code> </pre> <p>The iPhone implementation on the other hand doesn't make any such assumption, and ships every query through the same code paths. If the result info from the DB has no columns, then it returns null instead of a ResultSet.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2146,12,"""Android: setData not always updating""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/50231"""""""">Helpdesk 50231</a> for example.</p> <p>Not marking as a regression yet. Bill if you think it is, please tag it that way.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: setData not always updating
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/50231"""""""">Helpdesk 50231</a> for example.</p> <p>Not marking as a regression yet. Bill if you think it is, please tag it that way.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2145,12,"""Need to capture key press events in text fields (or in general?)""","""""""{html}<div><p>We have a need to capture key press events on a text field - in our case we are interested in the delete key, but obviously other key presses should be exposed as well.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Need to capture key press events in text fields (or in general?)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We have a need to capture key press events on a text field - in our case we are interested in the delete key, but obviously other key presses should be exposed as well.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2144,12,"""Android: ScrollView bottom padding property""","""""""{html}<div><p>With a ScrollView, when the contentHeight is set to 'auto', the  very bottom of the scrolling contents ends very abruptly at the  bottom edge of the last view.</p>  <p>My workaround currently is to add an extra (otherwise  superfluous) transparent view after the final view.</p>  <p>It would be useful to have a bottom padding property for this  situation.</p>  <p>Note: this ticket was raised with DonThorp's approval.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: ScrollView bottom padding property
Description: """"{html}<div><p>With a ScrollView, when the contentHeight is set to 'auto', the very bottom of the scrolling contents ends very abruptly at the bottom edge of the last view.</p> <p>My workaround currently is to add an extra (otherwise superfluous) transparent view after the final view.</p> <p>It would be useful to have a bottom padding property for this situation.</p> <p>Note: this ticket was raised with DonThorp's approval.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2143,12,"""iOS Crash: infinite loop on createButton top with non-integer value""","""""""{html}<div><p>(bug from David Richey, logged by <USER>pending creating of account for David.)</p> <p>Environment<br> OS 10.6.4, XCode 4.0, iPhone emulator 4.0 SDK, Titanium Desktop 1.2.1, Titanium Mobile 1.4</p> <p>Steps to reproduce</p> <p>The following code works:</p> <p>var pass = Titanium.UI.createButton({<br></p> <pre> <code>    backgroundImage: 'add3_button_pass.png',     title: 'New',     font: {fontWeight:'bold'},     color: '#white',     top:    Math.floor(goalBanner.height * 0.15),     height: Math.floor(goalBanner.height * 0.68),     left:   Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.86),     width:  Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.13),     zIndex: 10</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>You can make it fail by removing the Math.floor(...) from the top: property, thus:</p> <p>var pass = Titanium.UI.createButton({<br></p> <pre> <code>    backgroundImage: 'add3_button_pass.png',     title: 'New',     font: {fontWeight:'bold'},     color: '#white',     top:    (goalBanner.height * 0.15),     height: Math.floor(goalBanner.height * 0.68),     left:   Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.86),     width:  Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.13),     zIndex: 10</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>Failure mode:<br> On Launch from Titanium Developer, app loads and then immediately crashes. (""""""""Application exited from Simulator"""""""")</p> <p>Crash log:</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS Crash: infinite loop on createButton top with non-integer value
Description: """"{html}<div><p>(bug from David Richey, logged by <USER>pending creating of account for David.)</p> <p>Environment<br> OS 10.6.4, XCode 4.0, iPhone emulator 4.0 SDK, Titanium Desktop 1.2.1, Titanium Mobile 1.4</p> <p>Steps to reproduce</p> <p>The following code works:</p> <p>var pass = Titanium.UI.createButton({<br></p> <pre> <code> backgroundImage: 'add3_button_pass.png', title: 'New', font: {fontWeight:'bold'}, color: '#white', top: Math.floor(goalBanner.height * 0.15), height: Math.floor(goalBanner.height * 0.68), left: Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.86), width: Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.13), zIndex: 10</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>You can make it fail by removing the Math.floor(...) from the top: property, thus:</p> <p>var pass = Titanium.UI.createButton({<br></p> <pre> <code> backgroundImage: 'add3_button_pass.png', title: 'New', font: {fontWeight:'bold'}, color: '#white', top: (goalBanner.height * 0.15), height: Math.floor(goalBanner.height * 0.68), left: Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.86), width: Math.floor(platformWidth * 0.13), zIndex: 10</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>Failure mode:<br> On Launch from Titanium Developer, app loads and then immediately crashes. (""""""""Application exited from Simulator"""""""")</p> <p>Crash log:</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2142,12,"""Android: Module Resolution Doesn't Handle Packages Correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ti.UI.Android and Ti.Android are not detected as separate namespaces. If both modules are included in boot, and Ti.UI.Android is added last, calling <code>Ti.Android.createActivity</code> throws an exception because it's looking in the Ti.UI.Android module</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Module Resolution Doesn't Handle Packages Correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ti.UI.Android and Ti.Android are not detected as separate namespaces. If both modules are included in boot, and Ti.UI.Android is added last, calling <code>Ti.Android.createActivity</code> throws an exception because it's looking in the Ti.UI.Android module</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2141,12,"""Android: Ti.include with Array Is Broken""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ti.include([myfile.js]);</p> <p>Doesn't handle the array type.</p> <pre> <code>10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): Caused by: java.io.FileNotFoundException: Resources/[Ljava.lang.Object;@45020db8 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419):     at android.content.res.AssetManager.openAsset(Native Method) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419):     at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:313) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419):     at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:287) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419):     at org.<USER>titanium.io.TiResourceFile.getInputStream(TiResourceFile.java:78) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419):     at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.evaluateScript(KrollContext.java:191) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419):     ... 21 more</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.include with Array Is Broken
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ti.include([myfile.js]);</p> <p>Doesn't handle the array type.</p> <pre> <code>10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): Caused by: java.io.FileNotFoundException: Resources/[Ljava.lang.Object;@45020db8 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): at android.content.res.AssetManager.openAsset(Native Method) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:313) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): at android.content.res.AssetManager.open(AssetManager.java:287) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): at org.<USER>titanium.io.TiResourceFile.getInputStream(TiResourceFile.java:78) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): at org.<USER>titanium.kroll.KrollContext.evaluateScript(KrollContext.java:191) 10-20 23:42:04.380: ERROR/KrollContext(419): ... 21 more</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2140,12,"""iPad simulator - selecting 4.1 (the default) on run emulator tab results in an invalid emulator""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.have iOS 4.1 sdk installed<br> 2.create a new iPad project<br> 3.select the """"""""Run Emulator"""""""" tab, hit Launch<br> 4.once the sim launches, go to the iPhone Hardware menu item, and check the values under device and version.</p> <p>results: ipad running 4.1</p> <p>expected - this is not a real world config and will never appear in the wild. We should at least default to 3.2 until 4.2 support is out.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad simulator - selecting 4.1 (the default) on run emulator tab results in an invalid emulator
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.have iOS 4.1 sdk installed<br> 2.create a new iPad project<br> 3.select the """"""""Run Emulator"""""""" tab, hit Launch<br> 4.once the sim launches, go to the iPhone Hardware menu item, and check the values under device and version.</p> <p>results: ipad running 4.1</p> <p>expected - this is not a real world config and will never appear in the wild. We should at least default to 3.2 until 4.2 support is out.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2139,12,"""GPS cuts out sporadically""","""""""{html}<div><p>I noticed this on the kitchenshink app and have also confirmed  with a very simple app.js (<a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1233923"""""""">http://pastie.org/1233923</a>) Load and  wait for 10-20 seconds and the GPS will start shutting off then  back on.</p>  <p>I am seeing this on my droid running 2.2, and 1.4.1.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: GPS cuts out sporadically
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I noticed this on the kitchenshink app and have also confirmed with a very simple app.js (<a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1233923"""""""">http://pastie.org/1233923</a>) Load and wait for 10-20 seconds and the GPS will start shutting off then back on.</p> <p>I am seeing this on my droid running 2.2, and 1.4.1.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2138,12,"""""""Heavyweight"""" windows interfering with GPS (android)""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a simple app I wrote to debug another gps issue here:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/71611/gps-cuts-out-sporadically-android""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/71611/gps-cuts-out-spora...</a></p> <p>On further exploration if I make that window a """"""""heavyweight"""""""" window, then the GPS will never turn on and activate. Here is the original code <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1233923"""""""">http://pastie.org/1233923</a> to see the problem add """"""""navBarHidden: false"""""""" to the window properties and run again, and the GPS will never activate or fire.</p> <p>Note this is on my motorola droid, running 2.2. Running 1.4.1.1 on the titanium side.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: """"Heavyweight"""" windows interfering with GPS (android)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have a simple app I wrote to debug another gps issue here:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/71611/gps-cuts-out-sporadically-android""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/71611/gps-cuts-out-spora...</a></p> <p>On further exploration if I make that window a """"""""heavyweight"""""""" window, then the GPS will never turn on and activate. Here is the original code <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1233923"""""""">http://pastie.org/1233923</a> to see the problem add """"""""navBarHidden: false"""""""" to the window properties and run again, and the GPS will never activate or fire.</p> <p>Note this is on my motorola droid, running 2.2. Running 1.4.1.1 on the titanium side.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2137,12,"""iOS: Opening a modal window over another modal causes issues""","""""""{html}<div><p>Demonstrated in the following code:</p>  <pre>  <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'white'});  var modal1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'blue', modal:true});  var modal2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'red', modal:true});    var open1 = Ti.UI.createButton({      title:'Open modal1',      width:200,      height:40  });  open1.addEventListener('click', function() {      modal1.open();  });  win.add(open1);    var open2 = Ti.UI.createButton({      title:'Open modal2',      width:200,      height:40  });  open2.addEventListener('click', function() {      modal2.open();  });  modal1.add(open2);    var close1 = Ti.UI.createButton({      title:'Close modal1',      top:40,      width:200,      height:40  });  close1.addEventListener('click', function() {      modal1.close();  });  modal2.add(close1);    var close2 = Ti.UI.createButton({      title:'Close modal2',      top:100,      width:200,      height:40  });  close2.addEventListener('click', function() {      modal2.close();  });  modal2.add(close2);    win.open();</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Opening a modal window over another modal causes issues
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Demonstrated in the following code:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'white'}); var modal1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'blue', modal:true}); var modal2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'red', modal:true}); var open1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Open modal1', width:200, height:40 }); open1.addEventListener('click', function() { modal1.open(); }); win.add(open1); var open2 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Open modal2', width:200, height:40 }); open2.addEventListener('click', function() { modal2.open(); }); modal1.add(open2); var close1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Close modal1', top:40, width:200, height:40 }); close1.addEventListener('click', function() { modal1.close(); }); modal2.add(close1); var close2 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Close modal2', top:100, width:200, height:40 }); close2.addEventListener('click', function() { modal2.close(); }); modal2.add(close2); win.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2136,12,"""Android: Annotation processor doesn't handle deleted/renamed properties/methods properly""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you delete or rename a property or method, the annotation generator keeps the old name around in the JSON model and still generates code for it.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Annotation processor doesn't handle deleted/renamed properties/methods properly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you delete or rename a property or method, the annotation generator keeps the old name around in the JSON model and still generates code for it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2135,12,"""iOS: Audioplayer change state inconsistencies""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,</p>  <p>I'm currently finding that when I create an event listener that  listens to the audioPlayer change state, the state reported varies  widely across platforms and even devices.</p>  <p>Take the following code for instance (no affiliation with the  URL, just for example purposes:)</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">  Ti.API.log(""""""""Audio Stream App Started"""""""");     var url ='http://www.parishiltonjustme.com/downloads/audio/08_Screwed.mp3';     var streamer1 = Ti.Media.createAudioPlayer();     streamer1.addEventListener('change',function(e)  {       Ti.API.log(""""""""AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : """"""""+e.description);  });     streamer1.url = url;     streamer1.start();</code>  </pre>  <p>When this runs, i get several different results depending on  device OS and even device vs. emulator.(see below)</p>  <p>In some instances,there is no report of a stopping or stopped  state. Considering this, for instance, how might one go about  creating a music stream player that auto-advances on all devices in  Titanium Mobile?</p>  <p>I first tried the developer support forum on this one a couple  weeks back, although no responses there.</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/68291/audioplayer-change-state-inconsistencies"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/68291/audioplayer-change...</a></p>  <p>Thanks,<br>  Darin</p>  <p>iPhone 4.1 Emulator<br></p>  <pre>  <code>[INFO] Audio Stream App Started  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : waiting_for_data  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : waiting_for_data  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : waiting_for_queue  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopping  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopped  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized</code>  </pre>  Android 1.6 Emulator<br>  <pre>  <code>[INFO] Audio Stream App Started  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : starting  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing</code>  </pre>  ^never reports stopping or stopped^  <p>Andriod 2.2 Emulator<br></p>  <pre>  <code>[INFO] Audio Stream App Started  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : starting  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopping  [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopped</code>  </pre>  Android 2.2 T- Mobile G2 (ADB logcat)<br>  <pre>  <code>I/TiAPI   ( 4260): (kroll$3) [22,25] [Audio Stream App Started] null  I/TiAPI   ( 4260): (kroll$3) [2207,2232] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : starting] null  I/TiAPI   ( 4260): (kroll$3) [33,2265] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized] null  I/TiAPI   ( 4260): (kroll$3) [4,2269] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing] null  I/TiAPI   ( 4260): (kroll$3) [2,2271] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing] null</code>  </pre>  ^never reports stopping or stopped^</div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Audioplayer change state inconsistencies
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I'm currently finding that when I create an event listener that listens to the audioPlayer change state, the state reported varies widely across platforms and even devices.</p> <p>Take the following code for instance (no affiliation with the URL, just for example purposes:)</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> Ti.API.log(""""""""Audio Stream App Started""""""""); var url ='http://www.parishiltonjustme.com/downloads/audio/08_Screwed.mp3'; var streamer1 = Ti.Media.createAudioPlayer(); streamer1.addEventListener('change',function(e) { Ti.API.log(""""""""AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : """"""""+e.description); }); streamer1.url = url; streamer1.start();</code> </pre> <p>When this runs, i get several different results depending on device OS and even device vs. emulator.(see below)</p> <p>In some instances,there is no report of a stopping or stopped state. Considering this, for instance, how might one go about creating a music stream player that auto-advances on all devices in Titanium Mobile?</p> <p>I first tried the developer support forum on this one a couple weeks back, although no responses there.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/68291/audioplayer-change-state-inconsistencies""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/68291/audioplayer-change...</a></p> <p>Thanks,<br> Darin</p> <p>iPhone 4.1 Emulator<br></p> <pre> <code>[INFO] Audio Stream App Started [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : waiting_for_data [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : waiting_for_data [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : waiting_for_queue [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopping [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopped [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized</code> </pre> Android 1.6 Emulator<br> <pre> <code>[INFO] Audio Stream App Started [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : starting [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing</code> </pre> ^never reports stopping or stopped^ <p>Andriod 2.2 Emulator<br></p> <pre> <code>[INFO] Audio Stream App Started [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : starting [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopping [INFO] AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : stopped</code> </pre> Android 2.2 T- Mobile G2 (ADB logcat)<br> <pre> <code>I/TiAPI ( 4260): (kroll$3) [22,25] [Audio Stream App Started] null I/TiAPI ( 4260): (kroll$3) [2207,2232] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : starting] null I/TiAPI ( 4260): (kroll$3) [33,2265] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : initialized] null I/TiAPI ( 4260): (kroll$3) [4,2269] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing] null I/TiAPI ( 4260): (kroll$3) [2,2271] [AudioPlayer addEventListener 'change' says : playing] null</code> </pre> ^never reports stopping or stopped^</div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2134,12,"""Build Support: Add modules Element to tiapp.xml on Project Creation""","""""""{html}<div><p>Add</p> <pre> <code>&lt;modules&gt; &lt;/modules&gt;</code> </pre> <p>to the template tiapp.xml file.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Build Support: Add modules Element to tiapp.xml on Project Creation
