Description: """"{html}<div><p>steps and test case to follow, for tracking.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2096,12,"""Popover hide doesn't work""","""""""{html}<div><p>This example from the Q/A shows the issue. If you call popover.hide() the popover will remain visible. This example is tying into the orientationchange event but it also fails in a click event.</p> <pre> <code>var masterWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow ({     backgroundColor:'#000' });   var navButton = Ti.UI.createButton({     title:'A Button' });   var detailWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor:'#fff',     top:0,     title:'Test',     leftNavButton:navButton });   var masterDetail = Ti.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup( {   window: detailWindow,     right:0,     top:0 });   masterWindow.add(masterDetail);   var navPopover = Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover({     width:320,     height:850,     navBarHidden:true });  navButton.addEventListener('click', function(){   navPopover.show({view:navButton}); });   Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e) {      if(e.orientation == 3 || e.orientation == 4)     {         navPopover.hide();     } });   masterWindow.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Popover hide doesn't work
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This example from the Q/A shows the issue. If you call popover.hide() the popover will remain visible. This example is tying into the orientationchange event but it also fails in a click event.</p> <pre> <code>var masterWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow ({ backgroundColor:'#000' }); var navButton = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'A Button' }); var detailWindow = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#fff', top:0, title:'Test', leftNavButton:navButton }); var masterDetail = Ti.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup( { window: detailWindow, right:0, top:0 }); masterWindow.add(masterDetail); var navPopover = Ti.UI.iPad.createPopover({ width:320, height:850, navBarHidden:true }); navButton.addEventListener('click', function(){ navPopover.show({view:navButton}); }); Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e) { if(e.orientation == 3 || e.orientation == 4) { navPopover.hide(); } }); masterWindow.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2095,12,"""iOS - Titanium.UI.Slider 'touchend' event is fired 2X""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.use the script below, and note how many times the event is fired<br> results:the event is fired twice. works as expected on android.</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;<br> var slider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({</p> <p>min:0,<br> max:100,<br> value:5,<br> width:100,<br> height:'auto',<br> top:30<br> });</p> <p>slider.addEventListener('touchend', function(e){<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""touchend"""""""");<br> }); win.add(slider);</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Titanium.UI.Slider 'touchend' event is fired 2X
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.use the script below, and note how many times the event is fired<br> results:the event is fired twice. works as expected on android.</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;<br> var slider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({</p> <p>min:0,<br> max:100,<br> value:5,<br> width:100,<br> height:'auto',<br> top:30<br> });</p> <p>slider.addEventListener('touchend', function(e){<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""touchend"""""""");<br> }); win.add(slider);</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2094,12,"""[android - XML] Bug on Parse XML and non existing Node""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I tried to parse a XML, and made a control on Node Value :</p> <p> if(objItems.list.item(c).getElementsByTagName(""""""""description"""""""")){<br></p> <pre> <code>           desc = objItems.list.item(c).getElementsByTagName(""""""""description"""""""").item(0).text;             Ti.API.info('DESCRIPTION :' +desc);</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>This Node don't exist in my XML document, but with this test i can passthru normaly, on Iphone it's true, the test return """"""""NULL""""""""</p> <p>But On Android, the test return with Ti.API.Info(""""""""DESCRIPTION :""""""""+objItems.list.item(c).getElementsByTagName(""""""""description""""""""))</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> [15,22418] DESCRIPTION :ti.modules.titanium.xml.NodeListProxy@44046fb8</p> <p>I work on Android 2.2, and this code works on Iphone</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: [android - XML] Bug on Parse XML and non existing Node
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I tried to parse a XML, and made a control on Node Value :</p> <p> if(objItems.list.item(c).getElementsByTagName(""""""""description"""""""")){<br></p> <pre> <code> desc = objItems.list.item(c).getElementsByTagName(""""""""description"""""""").item(0).text; Ti.API.info('DESCRIPTION :' +desc);</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>This Node don't exist in my XML document, but with this test i can passthru normaly, on Iphone it's true, the test return """"""""NULL""""""""</p> <p>But On Android, the test return with Ti.API.Info(""""""""DESCRIPTION :""""""""+objItems.list.item(c).getElementsByTagName(""""""""description""""""""))</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> [15,22418] DESCRIPTION :ti.modules.titanium.xml.NodeListProxy@44046fb8</p> <p>I work on Android 2.2, and this code works on Iphone</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2093,12,"""Webviews in a scrollable view fail to render until a scroll up/down happens""","""""""{html}<div><p>On the iPad, if webviews are used as the views for a scrollable view, the content does not render correctly after a scroll event in the scrollable view. The content will show if the webview itself is scrolled up or down.</p> <p>Code attached.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Webviews in a scrollable view fail to render until a scroll up/down happens
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On the iPad, if webviews are used as the views for a scrollable view, the content does not render correctly after a scroll event in the scrollable view. The content will show if the webview itself is scrolled up or down.</p> <p>Code attached.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2092,12,"""zIndex doesn't work in tabGroup for label""","""""""{html}<div><p>When you create 2 labels, first the """"""""frontlabel"""""""" and then the """"""""backlabel"""""""", it shows the backlabel on top of the frontlabel. To change this, you can give the backlabel the zIndex of (for example) 2, and the frontlabel a zIndex of (for example) 8. This works perfect in a clean window. But not in a window inside a tabgroup. See the project in the attached zip file for an example.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: zIndex doesn't work in tabGroup for label
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When you create 2 labels, first the """"""""frontlabel"""""""" and then the """"""""backlabel"""""""", it shows the backlabel on top of the frontlabel. To change this, you can give the backlabel the zIndex of (for example) 2, and the frontlabel a zIndex of (for example) 8. This works perfect in a clean window. But not in a window inside a tabgroup. See the project in the attached zip file for an example.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2091,12,"""Android: Support Android Notification Service""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/NotificationManager.html""""""""> Notification Manager</a>, <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Notification.html""""""""> Notification</a>, and <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/notifiers/notifications.html""""""""> Guide</a></p> <p>Use <code>Titanium.Android.NotificationManager</code> as the module have it provide a <code>createNotification()</code> method that accepts a dictionary.</p> <p>NotificationManager will expose<br> - notify(int id, NotificationProxy proxy) - cancel(int id) - cancelAll() - createNotification({/ <em>create options</em> /}</p> <p>Requires support from Intent, PendingIntent, and Activity</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support Android Notification Service
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/NotificationManager.html""""""""> Notification Manager</a>, <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Notification.html""""""""> Notification</a>, and <a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/notifiers/notifications.html""""""""> Guide</a></p> <p>Use <code>Titanium.Android.NotificationManager</code> as the module have it provide a <code>createNotification()</code> method that accepts a dictionary.</p> <p>NotificationManager will expose<br> - notify(int id, NotificationProxy proxy) - cancel(int id) - cancelAll() - createNotification({/ <em>create options</em> /}</p> <p>Requires support from Intent, PendingIntent, and Activity</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2090,12,"""iOS: Song titles are not displayed (Intermittant) on iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2 mobilesdk 1.5.0.d02c264</p>  <p>1.ks iPhone Idiom &gt; Phone &gt; Music (have some music on the  device)<br>  2.invoke picker, pick a song and play it, look for label to appear  with the song info and prog bar.</p>  <p>results: it doesn't appear. After trying a few songs, it started  working, at which point I could no longer get it to fail.</p>  <p>seen in 1.4.1.1</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Song titles are not displayed (Intermittant) on iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2 mobilesdk 1.5.0.d02c264</p> <p>1.ks iPhone Idiom &gt; Phone &gt; Music (have some music on the device)<br> 2.invoke picker, pick a song and play it, look for label to appear with the song info and prog bar.</p> <p>results: it doesn't appear. After trying a few songs, it started working, at which point I could no longer get it to fail.</p> <p>seen in 1.4.1.1</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2089,12,"""Errors on launch of Kitchensink on iOS 3.2.2 and 3.1.2 ""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.install KS (regular, not ks-ipad) on a device running 3.2 or earlier (ipad, iphone etc)<br> 2.view output</p> <p>results: Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbe57][13418] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DEBUG"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DEBUG]"""""""">[DEBUG]</a> default_not_set <USER>Titanium/1.5.0 (iPad/3.2.2; iPhone OS; en_US;)</p> <p>Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad KitchenSink[13418] : *** +[NSDateFormatter localizedStringFromDate:dateStyle:timeStyle:]: unrecognized selector sent to class 0x38088fa4</p> <p>Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbe57][13418] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Script Error = *** +[NSDateFormatter localizedStringFromDate:dateStyle:timeStyle:]: unrecognized selector sent to class 0x38088fa4.</p> <p>Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbe57][13418] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> application received error: *** +[NSDateFormatter localizedStringFromDate:dateStyle:timeStyle:]: unrecognized selector sent to class 0x38088fa4</p> <p>expected: a bunch fo tets values, guessing this is the reason they are not being shown.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Errors on launch of Kitchensink on iOS 3.2.2 and 3.1.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.install KS (regular, not ks-ipad) on a device running 3.2 or earlier (ipad, iphone etc)<br> 2.view output</p> <p>results: Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbe57][13418] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DEBUG"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DEBUG]"""""""">[DEBUG]</a> default_not_set <USER>Titanium/1.5.0 (iPad/3.2.2; iPhone OS; en_US;)</p> <p>Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad KitchenSink[13418] : *** +[NSDateFormatter localizedStringFromDate:dateStyle:timeStyle:]: unrecognized selector sent to class 0x38088fa4</p> <p>Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbe57][13418] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Script Error = *** +[NSDateFormatter localizedStringFromDate:dateStyle:timeStyle:]: unrecognized selector sent to class 0x38088fa4.</p> <p>Wed Oct 13 14:04:42 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xbe57][13418] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> application received error: *** +[NSDateFormatter localizedStringFromDate:dateStyle:timeStyle:]: unrecognized selector sent to class 0x38088fa4</p> <p>expected: a bunch fo tets values, guessing this is the reason they are not being shown.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2088,12,"""iPad: Unexpected analytics error on launch of kitchensink (iPhoneIdiom)""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.install and launch kitchensink (iPhone idiom) on an ipad<br> 2.view output</p> <p>results:Wed Oct 13 15:40:21 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x8351][13788] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DEBUG"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DEBUG]"""""""">[DEBUG]</a> attempt to send analytics event but no network. will try again in 15 seconds</p> <p>notes: network is available, not seeing this with a version of ks I had previously published with 1.4.1.1.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad: Unexpected analytics error on launch of kitchensink (iPhoneIdiom)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.install and launch kitchensink (iPhone idiom) on an ipad<br> 2.view output</p> <p>results:Wed Oct 13 15:40:21 <USER>Haynies-iPad UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0x8351][13788] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DEBUG"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DEBUG]"""""""">[DEBUG]</a> attempt to send analytics event but no network. will try again in 15 seconds</p> <p>notes: network is available, not seeing this with a version of ks I had previously published with 1.4.1.1.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2087,12,"""iOS: iPad: KS, Display library - music picker does not draw tabs to the bottom of window""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2 mobilesdk 1.5.0.d02c264</p>  <p>1.Phone&gt;Music tap display library (regular ks on ipad)<br>  2.view tab on the bottom (see screen shot).happens in 2x mode as  well.</p>  <p>results: they do not align, the window navbar is partially  obscured as well (whole window is drawn too far up)</p>  <p>seen in 1.4.1 as well</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad: KS, Display library - music picker does not draw tabs to the bottom of window
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPad 3.2.2 mobilesdk 1.5.0.d02c264</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Music tap display library (regular ks on ipad)<br> 2.view tab on the bottom (see screen shot).happens in 2x mode as well.</p> <p>results: they do not align, the window navbar is partially obscured as well (whole window is drawn too far up)</p> <p>seen in 1.4.1 as well</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2086,12,"""iPad/iOS: Error stopping the simulator in TiDev""","""""""{html}<div><p>mobilesdk 1.5.0.d02c264, Ti 1.2.1, xcode 3.2.4, iOS sdk 4.1</p> <p>1.launch an iPad or IOS project in the simulator<br> 2.hit stop once its running (in TiDev)<br> 3.view the output in TiDEv</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 863, in main<br> execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % iphone_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=<strong>LOG</strong>ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version)],False)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 786, in execute_xcode<br> output = run.run(args,False,False,o)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 11, in run<br> line = proc.stdout.readline()<br> KeyboardInterrupt</p> <p>regression, new to 1.5.0.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad/iOS: Error stopping the simulator in TiDev
Description: """"{html}<div><p>mobilesdk 1.5.0.d02c264, Ti 1.2.1, xcode 3.2.4, iOS sdk 4.1</p> <p>1.launch an iPad or IOS project in the simulator<br> 2.hit stop once its running (in TiDev)<br> 3.view the output in TiDEv</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error: Traceback (most recent call last): File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 863, in main<br> execute_xcode(""""""""iphonesimulator%s"""""""" % iphone_version,[""""""""GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=<strong>LOG</strong>ID__=%s DEPLOYTYPE=development TI_DEVELOPMENT=1 DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=%s"""""""" % (log_id,sdk_version)],False)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/builder.py"""""""", line 786, in execute_xcode<br> output = run.run(args,False,False,o)<br> File """"""""/Library/Application Support/Titanium/mobilesdk/osx/1.5.0/iphone/run.py"""""""", line 11, in run<br> line = proc.stdout.readline()<br> KeyboardInterrupt</p> <p>regression, new to 1.5.0.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2085,12,"""file.createTimeStamp returns unexpected date on iOS 3.2.2 and earlier""","""""""{html}<div><p>spun off of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1642"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1642"""""""">#1642</a></p> <p>1.run the script below on an an iOS device running 3.2.2 or older.</p> <p>var filename = 'iphone_coming_soon.png'; var timeStampOfFile = ''; var file = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,filename); if ( file.exists() ) { Ti.API.info('IF IS TRUE'); timeStampOfFile = file.createTimestamp(); }</p> <p>Ti.API.info('The value of timeStampOfFile is: ' + timeStampOfFile);</p> <p>results: <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> newfile.txt created: Wed Dec 31 1969 16:00:00 GMT-0800 (PST)</p> <p>expected: return actual date,</p> <p>notes: Setting to medium</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: file.createTimeStamp returns unexpected date on iOS 3.2.2 and earlier
Description: """"{html}<div><p>spun off of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1642"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1642"""""""">#1642</a></p> <p>1.run the script below on an an iOS device running 3.2.2 or older.</p> <p>var filename = 'iphone_coming_soon.png'; var timeStampOfFile = ''; var file = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,filename); if ( file.exists() ) { Ti.API.info('IF IS TRUE'); timeStampOfFile = file.createTimestamp(); }</p> <p>Ti.API.info('The value of timeStampOfFile is: ' + timeStampOfFile);</p> <p>results: <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> newfile.txt created: Wed Dec 31 1969 16:00:00 GMT-0800 (PST)</p> <p>expected: return actual date,</p> <p>notes: Setting to medium</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2084,12,"""make titanium compatible with newer versions of python (3.0)""","""""""{html}<div><p>&#8224; When I attempt to update my computer it installed a new version of python 3.0 causing <USER>not to work... but when I regressed down to 2.7 again it worked. please consider fixing to work with 3.0<br> Thanks</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: make titanium compatible with newer versions of python (3.0)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>&#8224; When I attempt to update my computer it installed a new version of python 3.0 causing <USER>not to work... but when I regressed down to 2.7 again it worked. please consider fixing to work with 3.0<br> Thanks</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2083,12,"""aacp radio stream""","""""""Does titanium Titanium support aacp radio stream? If yes then any one tell me what should i write for it? I tried using this but with no success:    {code:lang=javascript}  var s = """"""""http://in.ast.com/nt-live-64"""""""";  var sound = Ti.Media.createAudioPlayer({url:s,preload:true,audioFormat:AUDIO_FORMAT_AAC,allowBackground:true});    sound.start();  {code}    Also see [TIMOB-4238|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4238] for the equivalent iOS ticket.""""""",Bug,"Title: aacp radio stream
Description: """"Does titanium Titanium support aacp radio stream? If yes then any one tell me what should i write for it? I tried using this but with no success: {code:lang=javascript} var s = """"""""http://in.ast.com/nt-live-64""""""""; var sound = Ti.Media.createAudioPlayer({url:s,preload:true,audioFormat:AUDIO_FORMAT_AAC,allowBackground:true}); sound.start(); {code} Also see [TIMOB-4238|http://jira.<USER>org/browse/TIMOB-4238] for the equivalent iOS ticket.""""",title+description
