TIMOB-2007,12,"""Android: crash when reloading webviews (same as #1936?)""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.4.2.4ce7ff G1 running 1.6, 2.2 simulator</p> <p>Possible dupe of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1936"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1936"""""""">#1936</a>, logging to be sure.</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;Web Views&gt;Local Url (or any of the top 3 tests)<br> 2.load the test case, back out, reload<br> results:<br> crash - log here: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1201203"""""""">http://pastie.org/1201203</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: crash when reloading webviews (same as #1936?)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.4.2.4ce7ff G1 running 1.6, 2.2 simulator</p> <p>Possible dupe of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1936"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1936"""""""">#1936</a>, logging to be sure.</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;Web Views&gt;Local Url (or any of the top 3 tests)<br> 2.load the test case, back out, reload<br> results:<br> crash - log here: <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1201203"""""""">http://pastie.org/1201203</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2006,12,"""Table View Headers - typing into search bar produces """"D/TiTableView(  485): (main) [397,2662480] *************  weird thing ********""""""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.4.2.4ce7ff G1 running 1.6, 2.2 simulator</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;VIews&gt;TableViews&gt;Headers<br> 2.type into the search bar and check adb output</p> <p>results: D/TiTableView( 485): (main) [397,2662480] <strong><strong><strong><strong>***** weird thing</strong></strong></strong></strong></p> <p>regression, I do believe</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Table View Headers - typing into search bar produces """"D/TiTableView( 485): (main) [397,2662480] ************* weird thing ********""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.4.2.4ce7ff G1 running 1.6, 2.2 simulator</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;VIews&gt;TableViews&gt;Headers<br> 2.type into the search bar and check adb output</p> <p>results: D/TiTableView( 485): (main) [397,2662480] <strong><strong><strong><strong>***** weird thing</strong></strong></strong></strong></p> <p>regression, I do believe</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2005,12,"""Android: Image scaling test does not scale image""","""""""{html}<div><p>Image scaling test does not scale image<br> 1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;Image Views&gt; Image scaling<br> 2.note size of image</p> <p>results:loading the image path into a browser shows the same size icon as in the test. On iOS the image scales up quite a bit.</p> <p>code:</p> <p>var imageView = Titanium.UI.createImageView({<br></p> <pre> <code>    url:'http://www.<USER>com/wp-content/uploads/2009/06/titanium_desk.png' });</code> </pre> <p>var l = Titanium.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>text:'', bottom:30, color:'#999', height:20, width:300, textAlign:'center'</code> </pre> <p>}); win.add(l);</p> <p>setTimeout(function() {<br></p> <pre> <code>// wait for URL to load var blob = imageView.toBlob(); l.text = blob.width + """"""""x"""""""" + blob.height;</code> </pre> <p>}, 2000);</p> <p>not new behavior, goes back to 1.4.0 at least</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Image scaling test does not scale image
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Image scaling test does not scale image<br> 1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;Image Views&gt; Image scaling<br> 2.note size of image</p> <p>results:loading the image path into a browser shows the same size icon as in the test. On iOS the image scales up quite a bit.</p> <p>code:</p> <p>var imageView = Titanium.UI.createImageView({<br></p> <pre> <code> url:'http://www.<USER>com/wp-content/uploads/2009/06/titanium_desk.png' });</code> </pre> <p>var l = Titanium.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>text:'', bottom:30, color:'#999', height:20, width:300, textAlign:'center'</code> </pre> <p>}); win.add(l);</p> <p>setTimeout(function() {<br></p> <pre> <code>// wait for URL to load var blob = imageView.toBlob(); l.text = blob.width + """"""""x"""""""" + blob.height;</code> </pre> <p>}, 2000);</p> <p>not new behavior, goes back to 1.4.0 at least</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2003,12,"""switching images continuously cause app crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>On the iPad using 4.1 &amp; 3.2 with latest 1.4.2 switching an image views image during events continuously causes the app to crash after about 15-20 seconds of switching.<br> See this ticket:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46581"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46581</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: switching images continuously cause app crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On the iPad using 4.1 &amp; 3.2 with latest 1.4.2 switching an image views image during events continuously causes the app to crash after about 15-20 seconds of switching.<br> See this ticket:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46581"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/46581</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2002,12,"""Systems buttons cannot be used in a view set to right/left nav button""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using iOS 4.1 and 1.4.2.d4ce7ff when using a system button style does not work if the buttons are put in a view and that view is set as the right/left nav button.</p> <p>See attached code</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Systems buttons cannot be used in a view set to right/left nav button
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using iOS 4.1 and 1.4.2.d4ce7ff when using a system button style does not work if the buttons are put in a view and that view is set as the right/left nav button.</p> <p>See attached code</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2001,12,"""Create a Multicolumn picker with imageView""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hello,<br> I want to create Multicolumn picker with imageView but I'm having the images only on the first column</p> <p>function add_to_row(i){<br></p> <pre> <code>var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({image :'../images/tabs/' + selected_categ_images[i]}); var row = Titanium.UI.createPickerRow(); row.add(img); return row;</code> </pre> <p>} for(var i=0;i&lt;4;i++){<br></p> <pre> <code>picker_data[i] = add_to_row(i);</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>var picker1 = Titanium.UI.createPicker({<br></p> <pre> <code>selectionIndicator : true, type : Titanium.UI.PICKER_TYPE_PLAIN</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>picker1.add(Titanium.UI.createPickerColumn({rows : picker_data}));<br> picker1.add(Titanium.UI.createPickerColumn({rows : picker_data}));</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Create a Multicolumn picker with imageView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hello,<br> I want to create Multicolumn picker with imageView but I'm having the images only on the first column</p> <p>function add_to_row(i){<br></p> <pre> <code>var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({image :'../images/tabs/' + selected_categ_images[i]}); var row = Titanium.UI.createPickerRow(); row.add(img); return row;</code> </pre> <p>} for(var i=0;i&lt;4;i++){<br></p> <pre> <code>picker_data[i] = add_to_row(i);</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>var picker1 = Titanium.UI.createPicker({<br></p> <pre> <code>selectionIndicator : true, type : Titanium.UI.PICKER_TYPE_PLAIN</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>picker1.add(Titanium.UI.createPickerColumn({rows : picker_data}));<br> picker1.add(Titanium.UI.createPickerColumn({rows : picker_data}));</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-2000,12,"""Android: Module name collision between Ti.UI.Android and Ti.Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you run this app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */ Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); Ti.API.info('Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN = ' + Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN); Ti.API.info('Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS = ' + Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS);</code> </pre> <p>The result <strong>should</strong> be:</p> <pre> <code>I/TiAPI   ( 1127): (kroll$1) [1,147] Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN = 32 I/TiAPI   ( 1127): (kroll$1) [0,169] Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS = android.intent.action.ALL_APPS</code> </pre> <p>But the actual result is:</p> <pre> <code>I/TiAPI   ( 1127): (kroll$1) [1,147] Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN = 32 I/TiAPI   ( 1127): (kroll$1) [0,169] Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS = null</code> </pre> <p>The second one fails because KrollObject.get() grabs the cached module named Android, which comes from Ti.UI.Android since it was called first.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Module name collision between Ti.UI.Android and Ti.Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you run this app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */ Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); Ti.API.info('Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN = ' + Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN); Ti.API.info('Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS = ' + Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS);</code> </pre> <p>The result <strong>should</strong> be:</p> <pre> <code>I/TiAPI ( 1127): (kroll$1) [1,147] Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN = 32 I/TiAPI ( 1127): (kroll$1) [0,169] Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS = android.intent.action.ALL_APPS</code> </pre> <p>But the actual result is:</p> <pre> <code>I/TiAPI ( 1127): (kroll$1) [1,147] Ti.UI.Android.SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_PAN = 32 I/TiAPI ( 1127): (kroll$1) [0,169] Ti.Android.ACTION_ALL_APPS = null</code> </pre> <p>The second one fails because KrollObject.get() grabs the cached module named Android, which comes from Ti.UI.Android since it was called first.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1999,12,"""Android: Implement custom images for Slider""","""""""{html}<div><p>Support thumbImage, leftTrackingImage, and rightTrackingImage.</p> <p>NOTE: To work correctly, the developer must provide the appropriate nine-patch images for the tracking images.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Implement custom images for Slider
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Support thumbImage, leftTrackingImage, and rightTrackingImage.</p> <p>NOTE: To work correctly, the developer must provide the appropriate nine-patch images for the tracking images.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1998,12,"""iOS: fullscreen toggle missing from video controls ""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.4c5cd4a. think maybe this  came as an os update.</p>  <p>1.Phone&gt;camera&gt;Video record or any video test<br>  2.take a video, then play it back<br>  3.while playing, pinch out to go fullscreen, then tap on the screen  to invoke the player UI<br>  4.look for the view toggle on the upper right hand side of the  video controls</p>  <p>also seen here:<br>  Phone&gt;play movie&gt;embedded video<br>  Phone&gt;play movie&gt;local</p>  <p>results: its missing</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: fullscreen toggle missing from video controls
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.4c5cd4a. think maybe this came as an os update.</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;camera&gt;Video record or any video test<br> 2.take a video, then play it back<br> 3.while playing, pinch out to go fullscreen, then tap on the screen to invoke the player UI<br> 4.look for the view toggle on the upper right hand side of the video controls</p> <p>also seen here:<br> Phone&gt;play movie&gt;embedded video<br> Phone&gt;play movie&gt;local</p> <p>results: its missing</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1997,12,"""iOS: remote streaming and remote streaming 2 memory leaks""","""""""{html}<div><p>Sim and iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.4c5cd4a</p> <p>Using instruments and the simulator:<br> 1.phone&gt;play movie&gt;remote streaming<br> 2.phone&gt;play movie&gt;remote streaming2</p> <p>Leaked Object # Address Size Responsible Library Responsible Frame<br> Malloc 32 Bytes 0xb430f50 32 MediaToolbox FigCFHTTPWillUseTLS<br> Malloc 48 Bytes 0xb047680 48 AudioToolbox SimAggregateDevice::SimAggregateDevice(<strong>CFString const*,</strong> CFString const<em>, long&amp;)<br> Malloc 32 Bytes 0xb047660 32 AudioToolbox CreateDictionaryForDevice(unsigned long)<br> Malloc 32 Bytes 0xb047640 32 AudioToolbox CreateDictionaryForDevice(unsigned long)<br> <strong>NSCFDictionary 0xb047610 48 AudioToolbox CreateDictionaryForDevice(unsigned long)<br> Malloc 32 Bytes 0xb0475f0 32 AudioToolbox SimAggregateDevice::SimAggregateDevice(</strong>CFString const</em>, <strong>CFString const*, long&amp;)<br> Malloc 32 Bytes 0xb0475d0 32 AudioToolbox CreateDictionaryForDevice(unsigned long)<br> Malloc 32 Bytes 0xb0475b0 32 AudioToolbox CreateDictionaryForDevice(unsigned long)<br> Malloc 32 Bytes 0xb047580 32 AudioToolbox SimAggregateDevice::SimAggregateDevice(</strong>CFString const<em>, __CFString const</em>, long&amp;)<br> <strong>NSCFDictionary 0xb047550 48 AudioToolbox CreateDictionaryForDevice(unsigned long)<br></strong>NSCFArray 0xb047530 32 AudioToolbox SimAggregateDevice::SimAggregateDevice(<strong>CFString const*,</strong> CFString const<em>, long&amp;)<br> <strong>NSCFDictionary 0xb0474f0 48 AudioToolbox SimAggregateDevice::SimAggregateDevice(</strong>CFString const</em>, __CFString const*, long&amp;)<br> NSURL 0x7b41f40 48 MediaToolbox FigByteFlumeCreateWithHTTP</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: remote streaming and remote streaming 2 memory leaks
