TIMOB-1959,12,"""Ti.include can not use absolute paths in iOS""","""""""{html}<div><p>There doesn't seem to be anyway to do an absolute path using Ti.include in iOS. I've tried the following with various modifications of each with no success:</p> <p>Ti.include('/windows/menu.js');<br> Ti.include('app://windows/menu.js');<br> Ti.include(Ti.fileSystem.resourcesDirectory+'/windows/menu.js');</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> error loading path: file://localhost/Users/eddie/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/4.1/Applications/CE687F4B-F7E7-4543-8217-898478D9B6B0/Manatee.app//Users/eddie/Dropbox/Mobile%20Apps/Manatee/Resources/windows/menu.js, Error Domain=NSCocoaErrorDomain Code=260 """"""""The operation couldn&#8217;t be completed. (Cocoa error 260.)"""""""" UserInfo=0x7e34260 {NSFilePath=/Users/eddie/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/4.1/Applications/CE687F4B-F7E7-4543-8217-898478D9B6B0/Manatee.app//Users/eddie/Dropbox/Mobile Apps/Manatee/Resources/windows/menu.js</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.include can not use absolute paths in iOS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There doesn't seem to be anyway to do an absolute path using Ti.include in iOS. I've tried the following with various modifications of each with no success:</p> <p>Ti.include('/windows/menu.js');<br> Ti.include('app://windows/menu.js');<br> Ti.include(Ti.fileSystem.resourcesDirectory+'/windows/menu.js');</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> error loading path: file://localhost/Users/eddie/Library/Application%20Support/iPhone%20Simulator/4.1/Applications/CE687F4B-F7E7-4543-8217-898478D9B6B0/Manatee.app//Users/eddie/Dropbox/Mobile%20Apps/Manatee/Resources/windows/menu.js, Error Domain=NSCocoaErrorDomain Code=260 """"""""The operation couldn&#8217;t be completed. (Cocoa error 260.)"""""""" UserInfo=0x7e34260 {NSFilePath=/Users/eddie/Library/Application Support/iPhone Simulator/4.1/Applications/CE687F4B-F7E7-4543-8217-898478D9B6B0/Manatee.app//Users/eddie/Dropbox/Mobile Apps/Manatee/Resources/windows/menu.js</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1958,12,"""Can't display Titanium.Contacts.Person with Ti.API.info""","""""""{html}<div><p>On 1.4.1 and 1.4.2 continuous builds I get a crash in the iPhone simulator if I try to display an array of Titanium.Contacts.Person or just a single Titanium.Contacts.Person object.</p> <p>Example</p> <pre> <code>// This works var peeps = Ti.Contacts.getAllPeople();  // This crashes Ti.API.info(peeps);</code> </pre> <p>BTW - This is also true of the Kitchen Sink app. Edit contacts_db.js around line 7 and add a line to display a person while walking the array of contacts. It will crash immediately and if you remove the Ti.API.info it will work.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Can't display Titanium.Contacts.Person with Ti.API.info
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On 1.4.1 and 1.4.2 continuous builds I get a crash in the iPhone simulator if I try to display an array of Titanium.Contacts.Person or just a single Titanium.Contacts.Person object.</p> <p>Example</p> <pre> <code>// This works var peeps = Ti.Contacts.getAllPeople(); // This crashes Ti.API.info(peeps);</code> </pre> <p>BTW - This is also true of the Kitchen Sink app. Edit contacts_db.js around line 7 and add a line to display a person while walking the array of contacts. It will crash immediately and if you remove the Ti.API.info it will work.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1957,12,"""iOS: iPad orientation change does not update label (set to auto)""","""""""{html}<div><p>var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({<br></p>  <pre>  <code>color:'#999',  text:'This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels v v This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixelsThis is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels',  width:'auto',  height:'auto'</code>  </pre>  <p>});</p>  <p>1.start in either landscape or portrait.<br>  2.change orientation, view text</p>  <p>results: the text draws like it did in the previous  orientation.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad orientation change does not update label (set to auto)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>var label1 = Titanium.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>color:'#999', text:'This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels v v This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels This is enough text to stretch to 480 pixelsThis is enough text to stretch to 480 pixels', width:'auto', height:'auto'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>1.start in either landscape or portrait.<br> 2.change orientation, view text</p> <p>results: the text draws like it did in the previous orientation.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
