TIMOB-1933,12,"""Multiple routes (polylines) on map""","""""""{html}<div><p>The app I'm trying develop is for a collection of hiking and biking trails. Each trail may have multiple offshoots or different surface types (which would require a different route color), but currently adding multiple routes to the same mapview only shows the one. Couldn't there be an addRoutes like the working addAnnotations? I have tried loading the route as part of SQLite return while and as part of an array, but neither work.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Multiple routes (polylines) on map
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The app I'm trying develop is for a collection of hiking and biking trails. Each trail may have multiple offshoots or different surface types (which would require a different route color), but currently adding multiple routes to the same mapview only shows the one. Couldn't there be an addRoutes like the working addAnnotations? I have tried loading the route as part of SQLite return while and as part of an array, but neither work.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1932,12,"""iOS: add support for sending crash logs to analytics""","""""""{html}<div><p>For parity with Android. Here's what android is sending:</p>  <p>D/TiApplication( 438): (main) [32,2561] Analytics Event:  type=ti.crash<br>  D/TiApplication( 438): event=ti.crash<br>  D/TiApplication( 438): timestamp=2010-09-28T18:21:18.845+0000<br>  D/TiApplication( 438): mid=200145da5524d59d<br>  D/TiApplication( 438): sid=04c81fda-9098-4aa7-bbd1-61105d7b3358<br>  D/TiApplication( 438): aguid=6fe33f33fd1f4e95a06d2d217170866d<br>  D/TiApplication( 438): isJSON=true<br>  D/TiApplication( 438):payload={<a href=""""""""""""""""></a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: add support for sending crash logs to analytics
Description: """"{html}<div><p>For parity with Android. Here's what android is sending:</p> <p>D/TiApplication( 438): (main) [32,2561] Analytics Event: type=ti.crash<br> D/TiApplication( 438): event=ti.crash<br> D/TiApplication( 438): timestamp=2010-09-28T18:21:18.845+0000<br> D/TiApplication( 438): mid=200145da5524d59d<br> D/TiApplication( 438): sid=04c81fda-9098-4aa7-bbd1-61105d7b3358<br> D/TiApplication( 438): aguid=6fe33f33fd1f4e95a06d2d217170866d<br> D/TiApplication( 438): isJSON=true<br> D/TiApplication( 438):payload={<a href=""""""""""""""""></a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1931,12,"""Android: Switch not clickable""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.4.2 (09/27/10 10:22 30a188)<br> Android SDK: 2.1 APIs</p> <p>In my app or even KitchenSink, when clicking on a switch nothing happens (visually or programmatically). Only when I do the following to it does it begin working properly:</p> <p>mySwitch.addEventListener('click', function() {});</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Switch not clickable
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium SDK version: 1.4.2 (09/27/10 10:22 30a188)<br> Android SDK: 2.1 APIs</p> <p>In my app or even KitchenSink, when clicking on a switch nothing happens (visually or programmatically). Only when I do the following to it does it begin working properly:</p> <p>mySwitch.addEventListener('click', function() {});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1930,12,"""Allow Geolocation in background""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently (even in the current github sources) Geolocation cannot do background processing. Is this a matter of removing the instructions from the onPause()/onResume() routines? I think allowing a user to specify allowBackGround: true in their initial construction of a Geolocation object would be wise. This way, we can still do background processing and not have to worry about the app losing focus, and data being randomly sent askew.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Allow Geolocation in background
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently (even in the current github sources) Geolocation cannot do background processing. Is this a matter of removing the instructions from the onPause()/onResume() routines? I think allowing a user to specify allowBackGround: true in their initial construction of a Geolocation object would be wise. This way, we can still do background processing and not have to worry about the app losing focus, and data being randomly sent askew.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1929,12,"""Android: Add Checkbox Widget""","""""""{html}<div><p>Same semantics as switch, just use underlying Checkbox control.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add Checkbox Widget
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Same semantics as switch, just use underlying Checkbox control.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1928,12,"""iOS -info and warning when backgrounding, then foregrounding KS""","""""""{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.e6bd67</p> <p>1.launch KS (be plugged in and viewing console)<br> 2.press the home button<br> 3.tap the icon to open the app and check output</p> <p>Mon Sep 27 14:02:37 unknown /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[343] : dnssd_clientstub write_all(9) DEFUNCT<br> Mon Sep 27 14:02:37 unknown /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[343] : dnssd_clientstub deliver_request ERROR: write_all(9, 62 bytes) failed<br> Mon Sep 27 14:02:37 unknown /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[343] : dnssd_clientstub write_all(9) DEFUNCT</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS -info and warning when backgrounding, then foregrounding KS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.e6bd67</p> <p>1.launch KS (be plugged in and viewing console)<br> 2.press the home button<br> 3.tap the icon to open the app and check output</p> <p>Mon Sep 27 14:02:37 unknown /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[343] : dnssd_clientstub write_all(9) DEFUNCT<br> Mon Sep 27 14:02:37 unknown /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[343] : dnssd_clientstub deliver_request ERROR: write_all(9, 62 bytes) failed<br> Mon Sep 27 14:02:37 unknown /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[343] : dnssd_clientstub write_all(9) DEFUNCT</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1927,12,"""iOS: window drawn prior to animation finishing""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.e6bd67</p>  <p>1.Phone&gt;Sound&gt;Local (or any of the first 3)<br>  2.tap and watch the as the window animates out, when the new window  draws in</p>  <p>results: the animation is still occuring when the new window  draws in, there is a brief period where both windows appear (though  only in a small part of the left side of the screen - unable to  grab a screenshot during the short period it happens).</p>  <p>seen in 1.4.0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: window drawn prior to animation finishing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.e6bd67</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Sound&gt;Local (or any of the first 3)<br> 2.tap and watch the as the window animates out, when the new window draws in</p> <p>results: the animation is still occuring when the new window draws in, there is a brief period where both windows appear (though only in a small part of the left side of the screen - unable to grab a screenshot during the short period it happens).</p> <p>seen in 1.4.0</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1926,12,"""iOS: new video fails to overwrite existing (""""File exists"""") when the second video is taken in landscape orientation. ""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.e6bd67</p>  <p>1.Phone&gt;Record video, record a short video in portrait. The  tap play movie and view<br>  2.back out a level, then tap into the record video test case  again.<br>  3.Tap """"""""record Movie"""""""" then switch to landscape orientation and start  the recording<br>  4,stop and play back</p>  <p>results:Mon Sep 27 12:02:05 unknown  /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[205]  : open on  /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/Documents/mymovie.mov:  File exists</p>  <p>the new movie does not play, the previous does. A little  intermittant, but reliably repro with a few attempts.</p>  <p>Also seen in 1.4.0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: new video fails to overwrite existing (""""File exists"""") when the second video is taken in landscape orientation.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.e6bd67</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Record video, record a short video in portrait. The tap play movie and view<br> 2.back out a level, then tap into the record video test case again.<br> 3.Tap """"""""record Movie"""""""" then switch to landscape orientation and start the recording<br> 4,stop and play back</p> <p>results:Mon Sep 27 12:02:05 unknown /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/KitchenSink.app/KitchenSink[205] : open on /var/mobile/Applications/B6DFF6C6-4120-4FD2-9E39-69269B4F077A/Documents/mymovie.mov: File exists</p> <p>the new movie does not play, the previous does. A little intermittant, but reliably repro with a few attempts.</p> <p>Also seen in 1.4.0</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1925,12,"""iOS: """"shake"""" not firing""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.e6bd67</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Shake<br> 2.Sake and look for the alert</p> <p>results: no alert, 1.4.0 KS works as expected on same device.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: """"shake"""" not firing
