TIMOB-1919,12,"""Android: Support push notifications""","""""""{html}<div><p>Right now Ti.Network.registerForPushNotifications only works  with iPhone.</p>  <p>Android 2.2 (Froyo) just added push notifications, called C2DM:  <a href=  """"""""http://android-developers.blogspot.com/2010/05/android-cloud-to-device-messaging.html"""""""">  http://android-developers.blogspot.com/2010/05/android-cloud-to-dev...</a><br>  Problem is this only works with v2.2 devices and up.</p>  <p>Urban Airship has an approach that works with almost all android  devices...but I'm not sure how much you want to marry to them:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://blog.urbanairship.com/blog/2010/09/08/push-notifications-on-android-faq/"""""""">  http://blog.urbanairship.com/blog/2010/09/08/push-notifications-on-...</a></p>  <p>In any case, some kind of built-in support for push on Android  would be great.</p></div>{html}    h3. Additional notes  Customer ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-684245""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support push notifications
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Right now Ti.Network.registerForPushNotifications only works with iPhone.</p> <p>Android 2.2 (Froyo) just added push notifications, called C2DM: <a href= """"""""http://android-developers.blogspot.com/2010/05/android-cloud-to-device-messaging.html""""""""> http://android-developers.blogspot.com/2010/05/android-cloud-to-dev...</a><br> Problem is this only works with v2.2 devices and up.</p> <p>Urban Airship has an approach that works with almost all android devices...but I'm not sure how much you want to marry to them:<br> <a href= """"""""http://blog.urbanairship.com/blog/2010/09/08/push-notifications-on-android-faq/""""""""> http://blog.urbanairship.com/blog/2010/09/08/push-notifications-on-...</a></p> <p>In any case, some kind of built-in support for push on Android would be great.</p></div>{html} h3. Additional notes Customer ticket: http://support-admin.<USER>com/display/APP-684245""""",title+description
TIMOB-1918,12,"""Android: E-mail address in label gets cut at first dot""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is happening because of automatic wordwrap which, in the absence of any spaces, is breaking on the first period: (app.js)</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#fff',     fullscreen: true,     exitOnClose: true });  var l = Ti.UI.createLabel({     text: '<EMAIL>',     width: 100, height:40,top:0, left:0 }); win.add(l); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>Obviously this is not what a user would want to see.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: E-mail address in label gets cut at first dot
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is happening because of automatic wordwrap which, in the absence of any spaces, is breaking on the first period: (app.js)</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen: true, exitOnClose: true }); var l = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: '<EMAIL>', width: 100, height:40,top:0, left:0 }); win.add(l); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>Obviously this is not what a user would want to see.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1917,12,"""Android: Implement borderStyle for TextField and TextArea""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""https://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/45611"""""""">Helpdesk 45611</a>.</p> <p>Note: the current documentation doesn't show borderStyle for TextArea or any of the border style constants.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Implement borderStyle for TextField and TextArea
