TIMOB-1916,12,"""randomly xhr requests do not kill the loading indicator""","""""""{html}<div><p>On the iphone, sdks 4.x and Ti sdk 1.4.x at random xhr requests do not kill the loading indicator when the onload event fires. Customer reproduced this using the KS xhr examples.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: randomly xhr requests do not kill the loading indicator
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On the iphone, sdks 4.x and Ti sdk 1.4.x at random xhr requests do not kill the loading indicator when the onload event fires. Customer reproduced this using the KS xhr examples.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1915,12,"""iOS: Analytics crash (SIGABRT) when using featureEvent""","""""""{html}<div><p>SDK 1.4.1.1 on iOS SDK 4.1. I figured I'd use Ti.Analytics  custom events to get more info out of my app. So, I added a number  of them around my codebase, using syntax such as:</p>  <p>Ti.Analytics.featureEvent(""""""""myevent1"""""""");<br>  Ti.Analytics.featureEvent(""""""""myevent2"""""""", {extraData: """"""""test""""""""});<br>  (seems pretty sane, along what the docs say).</p>  <p>However, when I start my app up, after the first analytics call  the app will predictably crash within 30 seconds with EXC_CRASH  (SIGABRT) and a reason of """"""""NSMutableArray insertObject:atIndex:]:  attempt to insert nil object at 0'"""""""". This crash happens in both the  simulator, and on a device (both iOS 3.1.3 and 4.1). Removing just  these calls and deleting/reinstalling the app on the  phone/simulator makes the app run fine without crashes, and adding  them back in starts the crashes again.</p>  <p>I've tried removing the build directory and regenerating it, and  am going from a fresh install of Titanium that works fine with  everything else.</p>  <p>A full trace of the crashes is at: <a href=  """"""""http://pastebin.com/Gvf39NLg"""""""">http://pastebin.com/Gvf39NLg</a></p>  <p>P.S. Looking at AnalyiticsModule.m (<a href=  """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/AnalyticsModule.m"""""""">http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/C...</a>)  line 164 could be the culprit...if for some reason what's coming  back in line 163 is nil (as no validation is done to it).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Analytics crash (SIGABRT) when using featureEvent
Description: """"{html}<div><p>SDK 1.4.1.1 on iOS SDK 4.1. I figured I'd use Ti.Analytics custom events to get more info out of my app. So, I added a number of them around my codebase, using syntax such as:</p> <p>Ti.Analytics.featureEvent(""""""""myevent1"""""""");<br> Ti.Analytics.featureEvent(""""""""myevent2"""""""", {extraData: """"""""test""""""""});<br> (seems pretty sane, along what the docs say).</p> <p>However, when I start my app up, after the first analytics call the app will predictably crash within 30 seconds with EXC_CRASH (SIGABRT) and a reason of """"""""NSMutableArray insertObject:atIndex:]: attempt to insert nil object at 0'"""""""". This crash happens in both the simulator, and on a device (both iOS 3.1.3 and 4.1). Removing just these calls and deleting/reinstalling the app on the phone/simulator makes the app run fine without crashes, and adding them back in starts the crashes again.</p> <p>I've tried removing the build directory and regenerating it, and am going from a fresh install of Titanium that works fine with everything else.</p> <p>A full trace of the crashes is at: <a href= """"""""http://pastebin.com/Gvf39NLg"""""""">http://pastebin.com/Gvf39NLg</a></p> <p>P.S. Looking at AnalyiticsModule.m (<a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/AnalyticsModule.m"""""""">http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/C...</a>) line 164 could be the culprit...if for some reason what's coming back in line 163 is nil (as no validation is done to it).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1914,12,"""JSON data logged to the console outputs at all output levels""","""""""{html}<div><p>No matter what the output level is set at, JSON data is displayed in green.</p> <p>See this ticket.<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44111"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44111</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: JSON data logged to the console outputs at all output levels
Description: """"{html}<div><p>No matter what the output level is set at, JSON data is displayed in green.</p> <p>See this ticket.<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44111"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44111</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1913,12,"""Setting url of Sound object outside create method causes crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>On the iphone, when creating a sound object, if the url is set outside the create method, the app crashes and does not log anything to the console window.</p> <p>Sample Code:<br> var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var newSound = Titanium.Media.createSound();<br> newSound.url = 'cricket.wav';<br> newSound.play();</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Setting url of Sound object outside create method causes crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On the iphone, when creating a sound object, if the url is set outside the create method, the app crashes and does not log anything to the console window.</p> <p>Sample Code:<br> var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var newSound = Titanium.Media.createSound();<br> newSound.url = 'cricket.wav';<br> newSound.play();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1912,12,"""Turning off format detection on the iPhone""","""""""{html}<div><p>This ticket has been created in response to this pro support ticket;</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44241"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44241</a></p> <h2>Summary</h2> <p>I have numbers in a webview that are being converted to phone number links. I see that the UIWebView class in Object C has a dataDetectorTypes property where you can set what types of data will automatically be formatted into links.</p> <p>If turning off the automatic detection it is an option in the native environment shouldn't you be able to duplicate the functionality in Titanium?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Turning off format detection on the iPhone
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This ticket has been created in response to this pro support ticket;</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44241"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44241</a></p> <h2>Summary</h2> <p>I have numbers in a webview that are being converted to phone number links. I see that the UIWebView class in Object C has a dataDetectorTypes property where you can set what types of data will automatically be formatted into links.</p> <p>If turning off the automatic detection it is an option in the native environment shouldn't you be able to duplicate the functionality in Titanium?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1911,12,"""Android: Titanium apps can't survive an activity relaunch""","""""""{html}<div><p>Because of the cleanup code in TiUIWindow (see  <code>release()</code>), Titanium apps can't survive an activity  relaunch. Even the simplest app:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */  Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');  Titanium.UI.createWindow({        title:'Test',      backgroundColor:'#fff',      fullscreen: true,      exitOnClose: true  }).open();</code>  </pre>  <p>To cause an activity relaunch, change the locale while the  activity is running. Example:</p>  <ul>  <li>  <p>Open a titanium app.</p>  </li>  <li>  <p>Keeping it open (i.e., don't back out), hit your Home key.</p>  </li>  <li>  <p>Go to Settings -&gt; Language &amp; Keyboard -&gt; Select  language, then change the language.</p>  </li>  <li>  <p>Go back to the Titanium app -- it will crash.</p>  </li>  </ul>  <p>What's happening can be shown in the attached  relaunch_activity.png graphic. Apparently Android forces the  activity to relaunch if the locale has changed. This causes  <code>onDestroy</code>, which in our code results in the window  cleaning up itself, but then activity create occurs again. Now the  <code>handler</code> object is null, however, and all views are  gone.</p>  <p>Is there some way for us to determine if <code>onDestroy</code>  is occurring because of a relaunch?</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Titanium apps can't survive an activity relaunch
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Because of the cleanup code in TiUIWindow (see <code>release()</code>), Titanium apps can't survive an activity relaunch. Even the simplest app:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */ Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen: true, exitOnClose: true }).open();</code> </pre> <p>To cause an activity relaunch, change the locale while the activity is running. Example:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Open a titanium app.</p> </li> <li> <p>Keeping it open (i.e., don't back out), hit your Home key.</p> </li> <li> <p>Go to Settings -&gt; Language &amp; Keyboard -&gt; Select language, then change the language.</p> </li> <li> <p>Go back to the Titanium app -- it will crash.</p> </li> </ul> <p>What's happening can be shown in the attached relaunch_activity.png graphic. Apparently Android forces the activity to relaunch if the locale has changed. This causes <code>onDestroy</code>, which in our code results in the window cleaning up itself, but then activity create occurs again. Now the <code>handler</code> object is null, however, and all views are gone.</p> <p>Is there some way for us to determine if <code>onDestroy</code> is occurring because of a relaunch?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1910,12,"""Add a removeAllChildren method to views and windows""","""""""Add the ability to clear all children from a view or a window.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Add a removeAllChildren method to views and windows
Description: """"Add the ability to clear all children from a view or a window.""""",title+description
TIMOB-1909,12,"""zIndex doesn't exist on non TiUIViews""","""""""{html}<div><p>When doing performZIndexRepositioning, zIndex was assumed on the subviews, which caused problems with scrollable and scroll views, as this was done before a check on if the child views are TiUIViews, which UIScrollView is not. This led to a crashing exception.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: zIndex doesn't exist on non TiUIViews
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When doing performZIndexRepositioning, zIndex was assumed on the subviews, which caused problems with scrollable and scroll views, as this was done before a check on if the child views are TiUIViews, which UIScrollView is not. This led to a crashing exception.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1908,12,"""Android: contacts picker callbacks never fired if showContacts called from other context""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is yet another context/activity issue.</p> <p>failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */ Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({       title:'Test',     backgroundColor:'#fff',     fullscreen: true,     exitOnClose: true });  var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({     title: 'contacts' }); btn.addEventListener('click', function() {     Ti.Contacts.showContacts({         selectedPerson: function(){Ti.API.info('!!!!!!!!! SELECTED');}     }); });  win.add(btn); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>So in this example, the button to open the picker is in a heavyweight window. But the button was placed there -- and the listener added -- from the root context.</p> <p>Debugging in Eclipse, I can see that the picker activity <code>onResult</code> is not even hit.</p> <p>If you move the code that creates the button/event listener into the heavyweight window's own JS file, it works.</p> <p>If you look in our <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/android_native_refactor/android/modules/contacts/src/ti/modules/titanium/contacts/ContactsModule.java#L126""""""""> ContactsModule.java</a> on the line where we setup calling the picker activity (using TiActivitySupport), you can see we're using the activity of the context, which in our example above will be the root context and therefore not correspond to the Activity of the heavyweight window.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: contacts picker callbacks never fired if showContacts called from other context
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is yet another context/activity issue.</p> <p>failcase app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">/*global Ti, Titanium, alert, JSON */ Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title:'Test', backgroundColor:'#fff', fullscreen: true, exitOnClose: true }); var btn = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'contacts' }); btn.addEventListener('click', function() { Ti.Contacts.showContacts({ selectedPerson: function(){Ti.API.info('!!!!!!!!! SELECTED');} }); }); win.add(btn); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>So in this example, the button to open the picker is in a heavyweight window. But the button was placed there -- and the listener added -- from the root context.</p> <p>Debugging in Eclipse, I can see that the picker activity <code>onResult</code> is not even hit.</p> <p>If you move the code that creates the button/event listener into the heavyweight window's own JS file, it works.</p> <p>If you look in our <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/android_native_refactor/android/modules/contacts/src/ti/modules/titanium/contacts/ContactsModule.java#L126""""""""> ContactsModule.java</a> on the line where we setup calling the picker activity (using TiActivitySupport), you can see we're using the activity of the context, which in our example above will be the root context and therefore not correspond to the Activity of the heavyweight window.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1907,12,"""on iphone video player does not report playing flag correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>When the video player is playing a remote video, the playing flag is not being set correctly. This happens on iOS 4.</p> <p>See this ticket for code:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44561#c204831"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44561#c204831</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: on iphone video player does not report playing flag correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When the video player is playing a remote video, the playing flag is not being set correctly. This happens on iOS 4.</p> <p>See this ticket for code:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44561#c204831"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44561#c204831</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1906,12,"""Android: Event Source Gets Reset""","""""""{html}<div><p>When an event is fired in a child and propagated up the tree, the source is getting set to the proxy that's firing it and does not preserve the initial source.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/45061"""""""">Helpdesk 45061</a></p> <pre> <code>var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : 'blue' , name : 'w'}); w.addEventListener('focus', function(e) {     Ti.API.info(""""""""Window Focus: """""""" + e.type + """""""" """""""" + e.source + """""""" """""""" + e.source.name); });  var b = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Click Me', width : 100, height : 50 , top : 20, name : 'b'}); b.addEventListener('focus', function(e) {     Ti.API.info(""""""""Button Focus: """""""" + e.type + """""""" """""""" + e.source + """""""" """""""" + e.source.name); });  var b1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Click Me', width : 100, height : 50, top : 90, name : 'b1' }); b1.addEventListener('focus', function(e) {     Ti.API.info(""""""""Button 1 Focus: """""""" + e.type + """""""" """""""" + e.source + """""""" """""""" + e.source.name); });  w.add(b); w.add(b1);  w.open({ animated : false});</code> </pre> <p><img src= """"""""http://img.skitch.com/20100924-xt69d7yk3s5n5w81rfrapamgp6.png"""""""" alt=""""""""screenshot""""""""></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Event Source Gets Reset
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When an event is fired in a child and propagated up the tree, the source is getting set to the proxy that's firing it and does not preserve the initial source.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/45061"""""""">Helpdesk 45061</a></p> <pre> <code>var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor : 'blue' , name : 'w'}); w.addEventListener('focus', function(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Window Focus: """""""" + e.type + """""""" """""""" + e.source + """""""" """""""" + e.source.name); }); var b = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Click Me', width : 100, height : 50 , top : 20, name : 'b'}); b.addEventListener('focus', function(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Button Focus: """""""" + e.type + """""""" """""""" + e.source + """""""" """""""" + e.source.name); }); var b1 = Ti.UI.createButton({ title : 'Click Me', width : 100, height : 50, top : 90, name : 'b1' }); b1.addEventListener('focus', function(e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Button 1 Focus: """""""" + e.type + """""""" """""""" + e.source + """""""" """""""" + e.source.name); }); w.add(b); w.add(b1); w.open({ animated : false});</code> </pre> <p><img src= """"""""http://img.skitch.com/20100924-xt69d7yk3s5n5w81rfrapamgp6.png"""""""" alt=""""""""screenshot""""""""></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1905,12,"""Setting a blob to a webviews data property causes an error""","""""""{html}<div><p>When fetching an image and using the blob of the image set to the data property of a webview causes the following error:</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error loading: , Error: Error Domain=WebKitErrorDomain Code=102 """"""""Frame load interrupted"""""""" UserInfo=0x7e40790 {NSErrorFailingURLKey=about:blank, NSErrorFailingURLStringKey=about:blank, NSLocalizedDescription=Frame load interrupted}</p> <p>see this ticket for code:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/42211"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/42211</a></p> <p>happens on iOS 4 with latest titanium sdk (1.4.2)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Setting a blob to a webviews data property causes an error
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When fetching an image and using the blob of the image set to the data property of a webview causes the following error:</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error loading: , Error: Error Domain=WebKitErrorDomain Code=102 """"""""Frame load interrupted"""""""" UserInfo=0x7e40790 {NSErrorFailingURLKey=about:blank, NSErrorFailingURLStringKey=about:blank, NSLocalizedDescription=Frame load interrupted}</p> <p>see this ticket for code:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/42211"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/42211</a></p> <p>happens on iOS 4 with latest titanium sdk (1.4.2)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1904,12,"""Android: textfield, verticalAlign seems to set text align to left""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.KS&gt;controls&gt;textfield&gt;The Rest<br> 2.tap text align so its either middle or right<br> 3.tap the vert align button</p> <p>results: the text has been set to left align</p> <p>expected: respect the current alignment</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: textfield, verticalAlign seems to set text align to left
