TIMOB-1901,12,"""Android: XML parser unable to correctly handle numeric entities""","""""""{html}<div><p>split off of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1831"""""""" title=  """"""""Ticket #1831"""""""">#1831</a> (as per Don), other platforms worked as  expected.</p>  <p>1.using the attached files, play the app back on a g1 (1.6)<br>  2.look at the text being displayed (specifically """"""""element  text"""""""")</p>  <p>results:""""""""e grave is"""""""" (xml is e grave is &egrave;) expected is """"""""e  grave is &egrave;"""""""" the &egrave; char is not being displayed</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: XML parser unable to correctly handle numeric entities
Description: """"{html}<div><p>split off of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1831"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1831"""""""">#1831</a> (as per Don), other platforms worked as expected.</p> <p>1.using the attached files, play the app back on a g1 (1.6)<br> 2.look at the text being displayed (specifically """"""""element text"""""""")</p> <p>results:""""""""e grave is"""""""" (xml is e grave is &egrave;) expected is """"""""e grave is &egrave;"""""""" the &egrave; char is not being displayed</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1900,12,"""Application Events: Close, Resume, Pause  - Pause never fired""","""""""{html}<div><p>To me it seems like the pause event is never fired. The only  event fired is the resume event. Close only seems to be fired when  the UIBackgroundModes have been set.<br>  Tested using iOS SDK 4.1, Titanium SDK 1.4.0 on iPhone 3GS.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Application Events: Close, Resume, Pause - Pause never fired
Description: """"{html}<div><p>To me it seems like the pause event is never fired. The only event fired is the resume event. Close only seems to be fired when the UIBackgroundModes have been set.<br> Tested using iOS SDK 4.1, Titanium SDK 1.4.0 on iPhone 3GS.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1899,12,"""borderRadius causes exception when modal:true is used""","""""""{html}<div><p>The following use case produces an error. Commenting borderRadius:5 of createWindow prevents the error, but obviously the aesthetically this may not be desirable.</p> <p>var winView1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>    backgroundColor:'#b1b1bd',     borderRadius:5,     url:""""""""view1.js"""""""",     modal: true, //  modal:false,     title: """"""""View1"""""""",     width: 280,     height: 300 }); winView1.open();</code> </pre> <hr> <p>view1.js<br></p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; var viewView1 = Ti.UI.createView({     backgroundColor: '#ffb1bd',     borderRadius:10,     top:10,     width:280,     height:280 }); win.add(viewView1);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: borderRadius causes exception when modal:true is used
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The following use case produces an error. Commenting borderRadius:5 of createWindow prevents the error, but obviously the aesthetically this may not be desirable.</p> <p>var winView1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code> backgroundColor:'#b1b1bd', borderRadius:5, url:""""""""view1.js"""""""", modal: true, // modal:false, title: """"""""View1"""""""", width: 280, height: 300 }); winView1.open();</code> </pre> <hr> <p>view1.js<br></p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; var viewView1 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: '#ffb1bd', borderRadius:10, top:10, width:280, height:280 }); win.add(viewView1);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1898,12,"""Android: support structured addresses for contacts""","""""""{html}<div><p>Our original iteration of the contacts api for Android uses the native 1.6 (api level 4) contacts api. That did not support structured addresses (street, postcode, country, etc.)</p> <p>As part of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1860"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1860"""""""">#1860</a> we now have easy access to the newer (api level 5+) contacts api, so it should be easy putting in structured addresses when the device has 2.0 or higher.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: support structured addresses for contacts
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Our original iteration of the contacts api for Android uses the native 1.6 (api level 4) contacts api. That did not support structured addresses (street, postcode, country, etc.)</p> <p>As part of <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1860"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1860"""""""">#1860</a> we now have easy access to the newer (api level 5+) contacts api, so it should be easy putting in structured addresses when the device has 2.0 or higher.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1897,12,"""Window width and height not respected on Android""","""""""When creating a modal window, with width and height specified, a full screen window is produced. This use case demonstrates the  problem:    {code:title=app.js}  var winView1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({      backgroundColor:'#b1b1bd',  //  borderRadius:5,      url:""""""""view1.js"""""""",      modal: true,  //  modal:false,      title: """"""""View1"""""""",      width: 280,      height: 300  });  winView1.open();</code>      Furthermore, if borderRadius is used, an exception is produced.    I'll raise that in another ticket, but the code above also demonstrates this if the createWindow borderRadius property is  uncommented above.""""""",Bug,"Title: Window width and height not respected on Android
Description: """"When creating a modal window, with width and height specified, a full screen window is produced. This use case demonstrates the problem: {code:title=app.js} var winView1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#b1b1bd', // borderRadius:5, url:""""""""view1.js"""""""", modal: true, // modal:false, title: """"""""View1"""""""", width: 280, height: 300 }); winView1.open();</code> Furthermore, if borderRadius is used, an exception is produced. I'll raise that in another ticket, but the code above also demonstrates this if the createWindow borderRadius property is uncommented above.""""",title+description
TIMOB-1896,12,"""Android: Window width and height not respected""","""""""{html}<div><p>var winView1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p>  <pre>  <code>    backgroundColor:'#b1b1bd',  //  borderRadius:5,      url:""""""""view1.js"""""""",      modal: true,  //  modal:false,      title: """"""""View1"""""""",      width: 280,      height: 300  });  winView1.open();</code>  </pre>  <hr>  <p>view1.js<br></p>  <pre>  <code>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;  var viewView1 = Ti.UI.createView({      backgroundColor: '#ffb1bd',      borderRadius:10,      top:10,      width:280,      height:280  });  win.add(viewView1);</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window width and height not respected
Description: """"{html}<div><p>var winView1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code> backgroundColor:'#b1b1bd', // borderRadius:5, url:""""""""view1.js"""""""", modal: true, // modal:false, title: """"""""View1"""""""", width: 280, height: 300 }); winView1.open();</code> </pre> <hr> <p>view1.js<br></p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; var viewView1 = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: '#ffb1bd', borderRadius:10, top:10, width:280, height:280 }); win.add(viewView1);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1894,12,"""Android: support read-write contacts""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently the android implementation of our contacts api is  read-only. We don't support modifications of contacts or creation  of new contacts. We should.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: support read-write contacts
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently the android implementation of our contacts api is read-only. We don't support modifications of contacts or creation of new contacts. We should.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
