TIMOB-1892,12,"""Ask again for geolocation on device""","""""""{html}<div><p>When asking permission to use the users location on a device, if they refuse, we need to ask again instead of throwing an error. This is what happens when running in the simulator, but not on the device. iphone, ipad.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ask again for geolocation on device
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When asking permission to use the users location on a device, if they refuse, we need to ask again instead of throwing an error. This is what happens when running in the simulator, but not on the device. iphone, ipad.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1891,12,"""Android: Transparent view with border color & width properties results in completely opaque view""","""""""Currently, when the view is created, it is not possible to set a different border color on a transparent view, as in the following:    !http://jira.<USER>org/secure/attachment/22711/screenshot_332.png!    Intuitively, I would expect the following code to produce this:    {code:language=javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor: '#7B6700',    fullscreen:false,    exitOnClose:true  });    var viewBackground = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor: 'black',    top:120,    width:400,    height:30  });    var view = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'white',    borderColor:'gray',    borderRadius:7,    borderWidth:10,    opacity: 0.7,    top:10,    height:300,    width:200  });    win.add(viewBackground);  win.add(view);  win.open();  {code}    However, this produces a completely opaque view, as follows:    !http://jira.<USER>org/secure/attachment/22712/screenshot_333.png!    As a workaround, create a  transparent, different-colored, container view with rounded corners and add a smaller view inside which is also transparent (this produces exactly as desired, as per the first screenshot):    {code:javascript|title=app.js}  var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({    backgroundColor: '#7B6700',    fullscreen:false,    exitOnClose:true  });    var viewBackground = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor: 'black',    top:120,    width:400,    height:30  });    var viewTransparent = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'gray',    borderRadius:7,    opacity: 0.7,    top:60,    width:200,    height:300  });    var viewInner = Ti.UI.createView({    backgroundColor:'white',    opacity: 0.7,    top:10,    width:viewTransparent.width-20,    height:viewTransparent.height-20  });    win.add(viewBackground);  win.add(viewTransparent);  viewTransparent.add(viewInner);  win.open();  {code}    """"""",Bug,"Title: Android: Transparent view with border color & width properties results in completely opaque view
Description: """"Currently, when the view is created, it is not possible to set a different border color on a transparent view, as in the following: !http://jira.<USER>org/secure/attachment/22711/screenshot_332.png! Intuitively, I would expect the following code to produce this: {code:language=javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#7B6700', fullscreen:false, exitOnClose:true }); var viewBackground = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'black', top:120, width:400, height:30 }); var view = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'white', borderColor:'gray', borderRadius:7, borderWidth:10, opacity: 0.7, top:10, height:300, width:200 }); win.add(viewBackground); win.add(view); win.open(); {code} However, this produces a completely opaque view, as follows: !http://jira.<USER>org/secure/attachment/22712/screenshot_333.png! As a workaround, create a transparent, different-colored, container view with rounded corners and add a smaller view inside which is also transparent (this produces exactly as desired, as per the first screenshot): {code:javascript|title=app.js} var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: '#7B6700', fullscreen:false, exitOnClose:true }); var viewBackground = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor: 'black', top:120, width:400, height:30 }); var viewTransparent = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'gray', borderRadius:7, opacity: 0.7, top:60, width:200, height:300 }); var viewInner = Ti.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'white', opacity: 0.7, top:10, width:viewTransparent.width-20, height:viewTransparent.height-20 }); win.add(viewBackground); win.add(viewTransparent); viewTransparent.add(viewInner); win.open(); {code} """"",title+description
TIMOB-1890,12,"""Android: VideoPlayer Missing hide()""","""""""{html}<div><p>The video play needs a hide method. See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44821"""""""">Helpdesk 44821</a>.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: VideoPlayer Missing hide()
