TIMOB-1878,12,"""iOS - warning when creating a switch in a titleControl or toolbar""","""""""{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;WindowNavbar<br> 2.Tap """"""""title control"""""""" with device plugged in, read output</p> <p>Wed Sep 22 10:25:02 eWorld UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xb7e6][1533] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/WARN"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [WARN]"""""""">[WARN]</a> [object TiUISwitch] has an auto height value of 0, meaning this view may not be visible.</p> <p>I found this confusing as in our API there is no way to set """"""""auto height"""""""" - only height.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - warning when creating a switch in a titleControl or toolbar
Description: """"{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;WindowNavbar<br> 2.Tap """"""""title control"""""""" with device plugged in, read output</p> <p>Wed Sep 22 10:25:02 eWorld UIKitApplication:com.<USER>KitchenSink[0xb7e6][1533] : <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/WARN"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [WARN]"""""""">[WARN]</a> [object TiUISwitch] has an auto height value of 0, meaning this view may not be visible.</p> <p>I found this confusing as in our API there is no way to set """"""""auto height"""""""" - only height.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1877,12,"""iOS - errors and intermittent crash with email test case""","""""""{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;views&gt;Email dialog<br> 2.select an image (I used a previous screen shot) and enter a valid email, send it<br> 3.check output while its happening</p> <p>output:Wed Sep 22 10:07:37 eWorld sandboxd[1536] : KitchenSink(1533) deny file-write-data /private/var/mobile/Media/PhotoData</p> <p>Wed Sep 22 10:08:04 eWorld KitchenSink[1533] : DA|Could not open the lock file at /tmp/DAAccountsLoading.lock. We'll load the accounts anyway, but bad things may happen</p> <p>Wed Sep 22 10:08:04 eWorld sandboxd[1539] : KitchenSink(1533) deny file-read-data /private/var/tmp/DAAccountsLoading.lock</p> <p>I crashed once at this point. Not sure if this a downstream crash from a mem leak or not.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - errors and intermittent crash with email test case
Description: """"{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;views&gt;Email dialog<br> 2.select an image (I used a previous screen shot) and enter a valid email, send it<br> 3.check output while its happening</p> <p>output:Wed Sep 22 10:07:37 eWorld sandboxd[1536] : KitchenSink(1533) deny file-write-data /private/var/mobile/Media/PhotoData</p> <p>Wed Sep 22 10:08:04 eWorld KitchenSink[1533] : DA|Could not open the lock file at /tmp/DAAccountsLoading.lock. We'll load the accounts anyway, but bad things may happen</p> <p>Wed Sep 22 10:08:04 eWorld sandboxd[1539] : KitchenSink(1533) deny file-read-data /private/var/tmp/DAAccountsLoading.lock</p> <p>I crashed once at this point. Not sure if this a downstream crash from a mem leak or not.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1876,12,"""iOS - Hide with keyboard up hides/reveals hides search bar ""","""""""{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;TableViews&gt;Table Search<br> 2.tap Show<br> 3.Tap into the search field to invoke keyboard<br> 4.tap hide</p> <p>results: the search bar hides, reveals, then hides again. Only happens with keyboard up.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Hide with keyboard up hides/reveals hides search bar
Description: """"{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod touch (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;TableViews&gt;Table Search<br> 2.tap Show<br> 3.Tap into the search field to invoke keyboard<br> 4.tap hide</p> <p>results: the search bar hides, reveals, then hides again. Only happens with keyboard up.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1875,12,"""iOS - Events propagation- label appears briefly in the wrong position before drawing in the correct place ""","""""""{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>this is a little tricky to reproduce. if you don't see it right away, try tapping an object a few times, then tap another object</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;Event Propagation<br> 2.tap the objects and look at the bottom right of the screen</p> <p>results:labels appear on the bottom right then are drawn in the correct location.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - Events propagation- label appears briefly in the wrong position before drawing in the correct place
Description: """"{html}<div><p>4th gen iPod (4.1) with mobile sdk build 1.4.2.dc7b90</p> <p>this is a little tricky to reproduce. if you don't see it right away, try tapping an object a few times, then tap another object</p> <p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;Event Propagation<br> 2.tap the objects and look at the bottom right of the screen</p> <p>results:labels appear on the bottom right then are drawn in the correct location.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1874,12,"""Android: AlertDialog Doesn't Indicate Cancel State on Back""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44381"""""""">Helpdesk 44381</a></p> <p>Gist of discussion</p> <p>I pulled up the API Docs <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-object""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-object</a> doesn't look like iPhone sends a close either. They do allow setting the index of the cancel and the event coming back is suppose to have cancel true/false</p> <p>So how about when the back button is hit, I set cancel to true in the event and if there is an index on creation, set index to what you passed on creation, otherwise -1?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: AlertDialog Doesn't Indicate Cancel State on Back
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/44381"""""""">Helpdesk 44381</a></p> <p>Gist of discussion</p> <p>I pulled up the API Docs <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-object""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.AlertDialog-object</a> doesn't look like iPhone sends a close either. They do allow setting the index of the cancel and the event coming back is suppose to have cancel true/false</p> <p>So how about when the back button is hit, I set cancel to true in the event and if there is an index on creation, set index to what you passed on creation, otherwise -1?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1873,12,"""Android: SoftInputChange Fails on API 8 and Droid2""","""""""{html}<div><p>It looks like API 8 and Droid 2 require <code>InputMethodManager.SHOW_FORCED</code> to make the keyboard appear.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: SoftInputChange Fails on API 8 and Droid2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It looks like API 8 and Droid 2 require <code>InputMethodManager.SHOW_FORCED</code> to make the keyboard appear.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
