TIMOB-1811,12,"""iOS: iPad video remote streaming  sticks on """"loading"""" when waking device up after sleep.""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.phone&gt;remote streaming<br>  2.start the playback, the put the device to sleep<br>  3.wake the device, check the movie</p>  <p>results:movie stays in """"""""loading movie"""""""" state, never begins  playback - tapping the video does not show the UI controls.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: iPad video remote streaming sticks on """"loading"""" when waking device up after sleep.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.phone&gt;remote streaming<br> 2.start the playback, the put the device to sleep<br> 3.wake the device, check the movie</p> <p>results:movie stays in """"""""loading movie"""""""" state, never begins playback - tapping the video does not show the UI controls.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1810,12,"""iOS: IPad Multiple Popovers""","""""""{html}<div><p>To Reproduce:<br>  Create a single button bar and add two buttons to it.<br>  Create event listeners to open popovers for each.<br>  Click button 1<br>  Click button 2</p>  <p>Result: Both popovers are open at once, the the most recent  overlapping.<br>  Expected: All other popovers should close before opening another  (either close on first click, open new on second, or close/open in  one press).</p>  <p>EXTRA CREDIT:<br>  If buttons are on separate button bars, popovers behave as  expected. First click closes existing popover, second opens new  one.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: IPad Multiple Popovers
Description: """"{html}<div><p>To Reproduce:<br> Create a single button bar and add two buttons to it.<br> Create event listeners to open popovers for each.<br> Click button 1<br> Click button 2</p> <p>Result: Both popovers are open at once, the the most recent overlapping.<br> Expected: All other popovers should close before opening another (either close on first click, open new on second, or close/open in one press).</p> <p>EXTRA CREDIT:<br> If buttons are on separate button bars, popovers behave as expected. First click closes existing popover, second opens new one.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1809,12,"""can't build any apps""","""""""{html}<div><p>Have tried to email this twice (replying to diff issues earlier), and use previous helpdesk links (which now just seem to go to get_help - what system shold I be using for my premium support???)</p> <p>Have downloaded continuous build of 1.4.1 (as suggested by Bill to resolve an Android issue) now titanium has lost all my apps, I've tried importing them again but they won't build/run the simulator or on the device (even tried creating new project and copying the resource folder across) - no errors, just stops with the following...<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> One moment, building ... <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: cont-1.4.1 <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> iPhone Device family: ipad <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> iPhone SDK version: 3.2</p> <p>If I try to go back to 1.4.0 in the edit tab the sdk box on Test page just gets """"""""loading..."""""""" (had this problem before) - tried removing the cont-1.4.1 directory and restarting, but makes no difference</p> <p>Help (first sent this in on 13th - was urgent then as can't develop anything!) - have assigned to Nolan simply as he helped with the last time something similar happened - not sure this is the right place to raise this, but am desperate!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: can't build any apps
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Have tried to email this twice (replying to diff issues earlier), and use previous helpdesk links (which now just seem to go to get_help - what system shold I be using for my premium support???)</p> <p>Have downloaded continuous build of 1.4.1 (as suggested by Bill to resolve an Android issue) now titanium has lost all my apps, I've tried importing them again but they won't build/run the simulator or on the device (even tried creating new project and copying the resource folder across) - no errors, just stops with the following...<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> One moment, building ... <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> Titanium SDK version: cont-1.4.1 <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> iPhone Device family: ipad <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> iPhone SDK version: 3.2</p> <p>If I try to go back to 1.4.0 in the edit tab the sdk box on Test page just gets """"""""loading..."""""""" (had this problem before) - tried removing the cont-1.4.1 directory and restarting, but makes no difference</p> <p>Help (first sent this in on 13th - was urgent then as can't develop anything!) - have assigned to Nolan simply as he helped with the last time something similar happened - not sure this is the right place to raise this, but am desperate!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1808,12,"""Blackberry: Build script leaves old files in bin/resources""","""""""{html}<div><p>For example, if a file is deleted from project resources, it doesn't get deleted from bin/resources. Causes bloat.</p> <p>We fixed this for Android recently:<br> <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/11ce7cd45d41aff5ee09f68aa8abf978858b0178""""""""> http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/11ce7cd45d41a...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Blackberry: Build script leaves old files in bin/resources
Description: """"{html}<div><p>For example, if a file is deleted from project resources, it doesn't get deleted from bin/resources. Causes bloat.</p> <p>We fixed this for Android recently:<br> <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/11ce7cd45d41aff5ee09f68aa8abf978858b0178""""""""> http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/commit/11ce7cd45d41a...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1807,12,"""Android: Return Key Type Send Fires Return Listener Twice""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you use the SEND return key. Pressing the return key only sends one event. Clicking the SEND button fires it twice.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Return Key Type Send Fires Return Listener Twice
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you use the SEND return key. Pressing the return key only sends one event. Clicking the SEND button fires it twice.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1806,12,"""Android: add support for TiPoint""","""""""{html}<div><p>It appears that android does not currently support TiPoint.</p> <p>as per Don, 1.6.0, priority low, assigned to Don</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: add support for TiPoint
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It appears that android does not currently support TiPoint.</p> <p>as per Don, 1.6.0, priority low, assigned to Don</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1805,12,"""Android: Too deep recursion""","""""""{html}<div><p>Some apps will cause Rhino / Dalvik to reach a  StackOverflowError and show an error message """"""""Too deep recursion  when parsing"""""""". We need to either increase the stack size of the  Thread that parses the Javascript, or pre-compile the AST so the  parsing doesn't happen on device (the latter might be good for  speed anyway)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Too deep recursion
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Some apps will cause Rhino / Dalvik to reach a StackOverflowError and show an error message """"""""Too deep recursion when parsing"""""""". We need to either increase the stack size of the Thread that parses the Javascript, or pre-compile the AST so the parsing doesn't happen on device (the latter might be good for speed anyway)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1804,12,"""Android: Add Click Support for Focusable Views""","""""""{html}<div><p>Accept RETURN, DPAD_CENTER as click on focusable views with focus.</p> <p>if no click handler is present, keys are forwarded to underlying control. Otherwise, handler should return true that it handled the key. Action to be taken on UP.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add Click Support for Focusable Views
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Accept RETURN, DPAD_CENTER as click on focusable views with focus.</p> <p>if no click handler is present, keys are forwarded to underlying control. Otherwise, handler should return true that it handled the key. Action to be taken on UP.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
