TIMOB-1752,12,"""ChildNodes for Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hello,</p> <p>I'm using the childNodes property for iPhone and Android. On iPhone, it works fine and return the children nodes correctly. But, on Android, it returns something very strange. According DOMNode documentation to childNodes property: """"""""Returns a DOMNodeList that contains all children of this node. If there are no children, this is an empty DOMNodeList"""""""". You can see the Ti.DOMNodeList object for both (android and iPhone) but if you call childNodes.length on Android it returns a """"""""magic"""""""" number different of the real number of childrens that is returned properly on iPhone. In other words, on iPhone is everything fine, on Android the childNodes property doesn't works properly.</p> <p>Regards.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ChildNodes for Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hello,</p> <p>I'm using the childNodes property for iPhone and Android. On iPhone, it works fine and return the children nodes correctly. But, on Android, it returns something very strange. According DOMNode documentation to childNodes property: """"""""Returns a DOMNodeList that contains all children of this node. If there are no children, this is an empty DOMNodeList"""""""". You can see the Ti.DOMNodeList object for both (android and iPhone) but if you call childNodes.length on Android it returns a """"""""magic"""""""" number different of the real number of childrens that is returned properly on iPhone. In other words, on iPhone is everything fine, on Android the childNodes property doesn't works properly.</p> <p>Regards.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1751,12,"""Android: video - rotating with controls shown results in misplaced controls in new orientation""","""""""{html}<div><p>screen shots attached. repro'd on 1.6 and 2.2</p> <p>1.Begin in either orientation, start the video playback (phone&gt;play movie)<br> 2.Tap to get the video UI up<br> 3.rotate<br> 4.repeat starting in the orientation not used in step 1</p> <p>results: control redraw issue (see screen shots)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: video - rotating with controls shown results in misplaced controls in new orientation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>screen shots attached. repro'd on 1.6 and 2.2</p> <p>1.Begin in either orientation, start the video playback (phone&gt;play movie)<br> 2.Tap to get the video UI up<br> 3.rotate<br> 4.repeat starting in the orientation not used in step 1</p> <p>results: control redraw issue (see screen shots)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1750,12,"""toLocaleUpperCase function doesn't work as expected""","""""""{html}<div><p>The function toLocaleUpperCase doesn't return an uppercase string if the source string contains unicode characters. I have string """"""""La Jet&eacute;e"""""""" and call toLocaleUpperCase on it and it returns """"""""La Jet&eacute;e"""""""" instead of the expected """"""""LA JET&Eacute;E"""""""". I've also tried this with """"""""pi&ntilde;ata"""""""" and """"""""g&ouml;the"""""""". I get the same results.</p> <p>An example of what I'm doing:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var str = 'Jet&eacute;e'; str = str.toLocaleUpperCase();</code> </pre> <p>The result is Jet&eacute;e instead of JET&Eacute;E.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: toLocaleUpperCase function doesn't work as expected
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The function toLocaleUpperCase doesn't return an uppercase string if the source string contains unicode characters. I have string """"""""La Jet&eacute;e"""""""" and call toLocaleUpperCase on it and it returns """"""""La Jet&eacute;e"""""""" instead of the expected """"""""LA JET&Eacute;E"""""""". I've also tried this with """"""""pi&ntilde;ata"""""""" and """"""""g&ouml;the"""""""". I get the same results.</p> <p>An example of what I'm doing:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var str = 'Jet&eacute;e'; str = str.toLocaleUpperCase();</code> </pre> <p>The result is Jet&eacute;e instead of JET&Eacute;E.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1749,12,"""iPad - app crashes on orientation change with low mem warning""","""""""{html}<div><p>I tried compressing the images form ~350k to 72k with no change in behavior. Content locate on shared drive at Data/Users/Thomas/bugs/41751</p> <p>1.import project, load onto device<br> 2.launch and rotate</p> <p>results: crash (console and crash logs attached)</p> <p>this came from helpdesk ticket 41751</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad - app crashes on orientation change with low mem warning
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I tried compressing the images form ~350k to 72k with no change in behavior. Content locate on shared drive at Data/Users/Thomas/bugs/41751</p> <p>1.import project, load onto device<br> 2.launch and rotate</p> <p>results: crash (console and crash logs attached)</p> <p>this came from helpdesk ticket 41751</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1748,12,"""Android : list of KS cases in which trackball does not give focus to onscreen elements""","""""""{html}<div><p>The following test cases require the user to tap the screen before the focus rect appears by way of the trackball. In some cases, if I use a tap to get to the test, the track ball works, but if I use the trackball to to make the selection, the resulting test wil not show the focus rect.</p> <p>so,<br> trackball to make selection in list&gt;trackball fails in test<br> finger tap in list&gt;trackball works. That make any sense? :-P</p> <p>Base UI&gt;tab groups<br> Base UI&gt;window Properties<br> Base UI&gt;window layout<br> Base UI&gt;window (Stand Alone) (all generated windows from this test)<br> Base UI&gt;Custom Events<br> Base UI&gt;View&gt;scroll view&gt;scrollable view (unable to focus on ui on bottom)<br> Base UI&gt;Views&gt;Table&gt;Update rows<br> Base UI&gt;views&gt;options dialog</p> <p>controls&gt;slider<br> controls &gt;button</p> <p>Phone&gt;sound</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android : list of KS cases in which trackball does not give focus to onscreen elements
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The following test cases require the user to tap the screen before the focus rect appears by way of the trackball. In some cases, if I use a tap to get to the test, the track ball works, but if I use the trackball to to make the selection, the resulting test wil not show the focus rect.</p> <p>so,<br> trackball to make selection in list&gt;trackball fails in test<br> finger tap in list&gt;trackball works. That make any sense? :-P</p> <p>Base UI&gt;tab groups<br> Base UI&gt;window Properties<br> Base UI&gt;window layout<br> Base UI&gt;window (Stand Alone) (all generated windows from this test)<br> Base UI&gt;Custom Events<br> Base UI&gt;View&gt;scroll view&gt;scrollable view (unable to focus on ui on bottom)<br> Base UI&gt;Views&gt;Table&gt;Update rows<br> Base UI&gt;views&gt;options dialog</p> <p>controls&gt;slider<br> controls &gt;button</p> <p>Phone&gt;sound</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1747,12,"""iOS - displayCaps returns unexpected value on everything but iphone 4""","""""""{html}<div><p>on a 3g/3gs/ipod touch (4g or older) = """"""""low""""""""<br> iPad = """"""""high""""""""<br> iPhone4 = """"""""high""""""""</p> <p>expected:iPad and 3g/3gs/ipod touch should be """"""""medium"""""""", retina displays to return """"""""high""""""""</p> <p>script snippet for repro:</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;<br> Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#FFF');</p> <p>var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>width:""""""""auto"""""""", height:""""""""auto"""""""", top:10, left:10, right:10, text : 'value goes here',</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>label.text = Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.density;</p> <p>win.add(label);</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - displayCaps returns unexpected value on everything but iphone 4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>on a 3g/3gs/ipod touch (4g or older) = """"""""low""""""""<br> iPad = """"""""high""""""""<br> iPhone4 = """"""""high""""""""</p> <p>expected:iPad and 3g/3gs/ipod touch should be """"""""medium"""""""", retina displays to return """"""""high""""""""</p> <p>script snippet for repro:</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;<br> Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#FFF');</p> <p>var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>width:""""""""auto"""""""", height:""""""""auto"""""""", top:10, left:10, right:10, text : 'value goes here',</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>label.text = Titanium.Platform.displayCaps.density;</p> <p>win.add(label);</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
