TIMOB-1683,12,"""Android: 1-length arrays aren't converted from JSON correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>We're calling the wrong Array constructor when there's only 1 element in the Array</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: 1-length arrays aren't converted from JSON correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We're calling the wrong Array constructor when there's only 1 element in the Array</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1681,12,"""Gesture not wotking properly with iOS4 and iPhone SDK 4.0""","""""""{html}<div><p>On a iPhone with iOS 4.0 or with the iPhone SDK 4.0 simulator, the gesture event in only triggered once.</p> <p>To replicate this,<br> - Use KitchenSink as of August 4 - Test it with Titanium SDK 1.4.0 and iPhone SDK 4.0 - Go to Phone -&gt; Shake - Trigger the shake gesture in the simulator - The popup """"""""it worked !"""""""" does appear - click ok on the popup - Trigger the gesture again - !! The popup is not displayed !!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Gesture not wotking properly with iOS4 and iPhone SDK 4.0
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On a iPhone with iOS 4.0 or with the iPhone SDK 4.0 simulator, the gesture event in only triggered once.</p> <p>To replicate this,<br> - Use KitchenSink as of August 4 - Test it with Titanium SDK 1.4.0 and iPhone SDK 4.0 - Go to Phone -&gt; Shake - Trigger the shake gesture in the simulator - The popup """"""""it worked !"""""""" does appear - click ok on the popup - Trigger the gesture again - !! The popup is not displayed !!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1680,12,"""iOS regression: ImageView loaded from local file no longer scales in current git build""","""""""{html}<div><p>In StatusNet Mobile, we're saving avatar and site icon images from the network to local filesystem storage. Within the webview where we show some content everything's fine, but images that we load directly into ImageViews are no longer scaled to the size of the ImageView on iPhone in current builds from git.</p> <p>Example (use any 256x256 PNG file):</p> <pre> <code>var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({     backgroundColor: 'black' });  var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({     image: '256x256.png',     width: 128,     height: 128,     canScale: true, // only used by Android     enableZoomControls: false // only used by Android }); window.add(img); window.open();</code> </pre> <p>Expected behavior: image should be scaled to 128x128 in logical coordinates</p> <p>Actual behavior on Android: as expected</p> <p>Actual behavior on iPhone w/ 1.3.2: as expected</p> <p>Actual behavior on iPhone w/ 1.4.0: as expected</p> <p>Actual behavior on iPhone w/ current git build: image shows at its original size in logical coordinates (256x256).</p> <p>Screenshot showing the above attached.</p> <p>Images loaded directly from a remote URL are still scaled to the correct logical display size.</p> <p>This bug put a halt to today's beta push for StatusNet Mobile; I can work around it by disabling our filesystem caching on iPhone for the affected parts, but this will leave us unable to show cached icons when offline. Assigning to our support contact.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS regression: ImageView loaded from local file no longer scales in current git build
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In StatusNet Mobile, we're saving avatar and site icon images from the network to local filesystem storage. Within the webview where we show some content everything's fine, but images that we load directly into ImageViews are no longer scaled to the size of the ImageView on iPhone in current builds from git.</p> <p>Example (use any 256x256 PNG file):</p> <pre> <code>var window = Ti.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor: 'black' }); var img = Ti.UI.createImageView({ image: '256x256.png', width: 128, height: 128, canScale: true, // only used by Android enableZoomControls: false // only used by Android }); window.add(img); window.open();</code> </pre> <p>Expected behavior: image should be scaled to 128x128 in logical coordinates</p> <p>Actual behavior on Android: as expected</p> <p>Actual behavior on iPhone w/ 1.3.2: as expected</p> <p>Actual behavior on iPhone w/ 1.4.0: as expected</p> <p>Actual behavior on iPhone w/ current git build: image shows at its original size in logical coordinates (256x256).</p> <p>Screenshot showing the above attached.</p> <p>Images loaded directly from a remote URL are still scaled to the correct logical display size.</p> <p>This bug put a halt to today's beta push for StatusNet Mobile; I can work around it by disabling our filesystem caching on iPhone for the affected parts, but this will leave us unable to show cached icons when offline. Assigning to our support contact.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1679,12,"""Loading spinners not dismissed for video - first launch""","""""""{html}<div><p>2 ways to see it...</p> <p>Local Video test case show spinner that won't dismiss on clean install/first launch<br> 1.install a new version of KS or KS-ipad onto the relevant device<br> 2.go to the video tests and kick off a video (iphone - Phone&gt;Play Movie&gt;Local. iPad - Open Main tests&gt;Embedded video<br> 3.play and watch the video spinner</p> <p>results: I can reliably repro a spinner that never goes away with local video, but its seems to be first launch only.</p> <p>4g - Record Movie - spinner occurs on first record playback</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Record Video<br> 2.record a short, video, play it back</p> <p>results: first time you do this test, there will be an endless spinner showed on the video. Subsequent tests do not show this behavior, only the first one.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Loading spinners not dismissed for video - first launch
Description: """"{html}<div><p>2 ways to see it...</p> <p>Local Video test case show spinner that won't dismiss on clean install/first launch<br> 1.install a new version of KS or KS-ipad onto the relevant device<br> 2.go to the video tests and kick off a video (iphone - Phone&gt;Play Movie&gt;Local. iPad - Open Main tests&gt;Embedded video<br> 3.play and watch the video spinner</p> <p>results: I can reliably repro a spinner that never goes away with local video, but its seems to be first launch only.</p> <p>4g - Record Movie - spinner occurs on first record playback</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;Record Video<br> 2.record a short, video, play it back</p> <p>results: first time you do this test, there will be an endless spinner showed on the video. Subsequent tests do not show this behavior, only the first one.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1678,12,"""iOS:  sound.destroy crash ""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.KS&gt;Phone&gt;Sound<br> 2.Tap Local<br> 3.tap Play<br> 4.tap Stop and back out a level</p> <p>results:Crash</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: sound.destroy crash
