TIMOB-1667,12,"""Changing label view's font.fontSize property after view is rendered has no effect.""","""""""{html}<div><p><strong>Environment:</strong> Titanium Developer 1.40 and iPhone Simulator (iphone and iphone4). Also tested on iPhone4 device with same results.</p> <p><strong>Issue:</strong> Changing the fontSize property of a label after label is rendered has no effect. The following code does not work.</p> <p><strong>Example code:</strong> (notice 2 methods for defining new font size - neither work)</p> <pre> <code>var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var b = Ti.UI.createButton({    title:'Click Me',    top:10,    height:40,    width:200 }); var lab = Ti.UI.createLabel({    text: 'test',    top: 150,    height: 140,    width: 300,    font:{fontSize:20},    color: '#c00',    backgroundColor: '#ccc' });  w.add(b); w.add(lab);  b.addEventListener('click', function() {    lab.font = '{fontSize:100}';    // lab.font.fontSize = 100; // this also doesn't work });  w.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Changing label view's font.fontSize property after view is rendered has no effect.
Description: """"{html}<div><p><strong>Environment:</strong> Titanium Developer 1.40 and iPhone Simulator (iphone and iphone4). Also tested on iPhone4 device with same results.</p> <p><strong>Issue:</strong> Changing the fontSize property of a label after label is rendered has no effect. The following code does not work.</p> <p><strong>Example code:</strong> (notice 2 methods for defining new font size - neither work)</p> <pre> <code>var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({backgroundColor:'#fff'}); var b = Ti.UI.createButton({ title:'Click Me', top:10, height:40, width:200 }); var lab = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'test', top: 150, height: 140, width: 300, font:{fontSize:20}, color: '#c00', backgroundColor: '#ccc' }); w.add(b); w.add(lab); b.addEventListener('click', function() { lab.font = '{fontSize:100}'; // lab.font.fontSize = 100; // this also doesn't work }); w.open();</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1666,12,"""Attempting to SELECT from a non-existant table crashes the app""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have this code:</p>  <pre>  <code>try {      var rs = db.execute('SELECT * FROM meta');  } catch (e) {      Ti.API.info(""""""""Error: """""""" + e);  }</code>  </pre>  <p>which results in my app crashing with this error in the OS X  Console:</p>  <pre>  <code>8/28/10 4:15:45 PM  BillingWorks3[17336]    *** Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'org.billingworks3.TiDatabaseProxy', reason: 'invalid SQL statement. Error Domain=com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase Code=3 """"""""An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement."""""""" UserInfo=0x911bcf0 {com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.code=1, NSLocalizedDescription=An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement., com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.query.string=SELECT * FROM meta, com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.string=no such table: meta}  in -[TiDatabaseProxy execute:] (TiDatabaseProxy.m:134)'</code>  </pre>  <p>I would have expected my error handler to have caught the  exception rather than crashing the app.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Attempting to SELECT from a non-existant table crashes the app
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have this code:</p> <pre> <code>try { var rs = db.execute('SELECT * FROM meta'); } catch (e) { Ti.API.info(""""""""Error: """""""" + e); }</code> </pre> <p>which results in my app crashing with this error in the OS X Console:</p> <pre> <code>8/28/10 4:15:45 PM BillingWorks3[17336] *** Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'org.billingworks3.TiDatabaseProxy', reason: 'invalid SQL statement. Error Domain=com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase Code=3 """"""""An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement."""""""" UserInfo=0x911bcf0 {com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.code=1, NSLocalizedDescription=An error occured parsing the provided SQL statement., com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.query.string=SELECT * FROM meta, com.plausiblelabs.pldatabase.error.vendor.string=no such table: meta} in -[TiDatabaseProxy execute:] (TiDatabaseProxy.m:134)'</code> </pre> <p>I would have expected my error handler to have caught the exception rather than crashing the app.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1665,12,"""Ti.Platform.displayCaps.density returns bad values on iPhone 2G/3G, iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ti.Platform.displayCaps.density is documented to return 'low' for iPhone and 'high' for iPad, which it does in fact do... but this seems really wrong, and is inconsistent with the density strings used for Android:</p> <p>low: circa 120dpi (close to iPad's 132dpi)<br> medium: circa 160dpi (close to iPhone 2G/3G's 163dpi, which we report as 160dpi)<br> high: 240dpi (halfway between medium and iPhone 4's 326dpi)</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps-object""""""""> https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Pl...</a></p> <p>In particular, returning 'high' for both iPad (132dpi) and iPhone 4 (326dpi) seems a bit wrong. :)</p> <p>Since the value's not reliable, currently we just check the dpi directly for StatusNet Mobile when determining what resolution images to fetch from the network, which requires our patch for <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1349"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1349"""""""">#1349</a> to fix the bogus dpi value on iPhone 4: <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1349-titaniumplatformdisplaycapsdpi-returns-wrong-value-on-iphone-4""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1349-...</a></p> <p>Assigning to our support contact.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Platform.displayCaps.density returns bad values on iPhone 2G/3G, iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ti.Platform.displayCaps.density is documented to return 'low' for iPhone and 'high' for iPad, which it does in fact do... but this seems really wrong, and is inconsistent with the density strings used for Android:</p> <p>low: circa 120dpi (close to iPad's 132dpi)<br> medium: circa 160dpi (close to iPhone 2G/3G's 163dpi, which we report as 160dpi)<br> high: 240dpi (halfway between medium and iPhone 4's 326dpi)</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Platform.DisplayCaps-object""""""""> https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.Pl...</a></p> <p>In particular, returning 'high' for both iPad (132dpi) and iPhone 4 (326dpi) seems a bit wrong. :)</p> <p>Since the value's not reliable, currently we just check the dpi directly for StatusNet Mobile when determining what resolution images to fetch from the network, which requires our patch for <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1349"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1349"""""""">#1349</a> to fix the bogus dpi value on iPhone 4: <a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1349-titaniumplatformdisplaycapsdpi-returns-wrong-value-on-iphone-4""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1349-...</a></p> <p>Assigning to our support contact.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1664,12,"""Tableview loses layout after scrolling, iOS 4, iphone""","""""""{html}<div><p>this helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38311#c172381"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38311#c172381</a></p> <p>has all the details. run the code, select a table item, the next window, scroll it up and down and you will notice some rows loose the padding on the bottom of the row. I do not see this running 1.4 but I do see it in a build from HEAD yesterday.Customer needs 1.4.1 for another bug that is fixed.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Tableview loses layout after scrolling, iOS 4, iphone
Description: """"{html}<div><p>this helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38311#c172381"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38311#c172381</a></p> <p>has all the details. run the code, select a table item, the next window, scroll it up and down and you will notice some rows loose the padding on the bottom of the row. I do not see this running 1.4 but I do see it in a build from HEAD yesterday.Customer needs 1.4.1 for another bug that is fixed.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1663,12,"""Selection displaced in grouped tableView""","""""""{html}<div><p>When selecting a row in a grouped tableView, the selection gets displaced and the side borders dissappear. This happens for the middle and bottom rows in a grouped tableView, but not for a top row.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Selection displaced in grouped tableView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When selecting a row in a grouped tableView, the selection gets displaced and the side borders dissappear. This happens for the middle and bottom rows in a grouped tableView, but not for a top row.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1662,12,"""Included .js files cannot see previously declared vars""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a project in which I use Ti.include('filename.js') to keep the app design modular. So here's the scenario.</p> <p>app.js declares variable mySetting<br> app.js includes file doSomethingWithSetting.js</p> <p>The code in doSomethingWithSetting.js cannot find the variable mySetting.</p> <p>A Q&amp;A has also been created previously by someone else experiencing the same problem: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/49751/working-code-cant-see-vars-after-moving-into-an-include-file""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/49751/working-code-cant-...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Included .js files cannot see previously declared vars
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have a project in which I use Ti.include('filename.js') to keep the app design modular. So here's the scenario.</p> <p>app.js declares variable mySetting<br> app.js includes file doSomethingWithSetting.js</p> <p>The code in doSomethingWithSetting.js cannot find the variable mySetting.</p> <p>A Q&amp;A has also been created previously by someone else experiencing the same problem: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/49751/working-code-cant-see-vars-after-moving-into-an-include-file""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/49751/working-code-cant-...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1660,12,"""Not allowed to amend ticket 1654""","""""""{html}<div><p>Re-statement of problem:</p> <p>The input character only disappears if the value of the text area is saved to Properties while using the PinYin keyboard.</p> <p>The problem does not happen in any other language e.g. Arabic with a third-party keyboard.</p> <p>The issue should therefore be restated as 'Cannot save changed value of Text Area to Properties when using PinYin keyboard'.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Not allowed to amend ticket 1654
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Re-statement of problem:</p> <p>The input character only disappears if the value of the text area is saved to Properties while using the PinYin keyboard.</p> <p>The problem does not happen in any other language e.g. Arabic with a third-party keyboard.</p> <p>The issue should therefore be restated as 'Cannot save changed value of Text Area to Properties when using PinYin keyboard'.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1659,12,"""(Android) toImage functions blowing up with UI widgets""","""""""{html}<div><p>Calling toImage seems to blow up. I've tried it on buttons and views now and I get the same results. It seems to work fine on iPhone. (iOS 4.0.2 and Titanium Mobile SDK 1.4.1 from GitHub.)</p> <pre> <code>var appDirName = Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory; var imageFile = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(appDirName, 'image.jpg');  if (!imageFile.exists()) {     Titanium.API.debug(""""""""File """""""" + imageFile.name + """""""" does not exist yet.""""""""); }  var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({     title:'Gargargar!',     height:40,     width:200,     top:10 });  imageFile.write(button.toImage()); // blows up on Android  if (imageFile.exists()) {     // Note: Titanium.Filesystem.File.size attribute not mentioned in the API docs     Titanium.API.debug(imageFile.name + """""""" exists, size: """""""" + imageFile.size); }</code> </pre> <p>Android stack trace:</p> <pre> <code>D/TiAPI   (  569): (kroll$1) [880,926] File image.jpg does not exist yet. I/ActivityManager(   67): Displayed activity net.status.tstest/.TstestActivity: 4723 ms (total 4723 ms) W/TiAnalyticsSvc(  569): (Thread-10) [517,1443] Analytics Service Started D/AndroidRuntime(  569): Shutting down VM W/dalvikvm(  569): threadid=1: thread exiting with uncaught exception (group=0x4001d800) E/TiUncaughtHandler(  569): (main) [123,1566] Sending event: exception on thread: main msg:java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: width and height must be &gt; 0 E/TiUncaughtHandler(  569): java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: width and height must be &gt; 0 E/TiUncaughtHandler(  569):     at android.graphics.Bitmap.nativeCreate(Native Method) E/TiUncaughtHandler(  569):     at android.graphics.Bitmap.createBitmap(Bitmap.java:468) E/TiUncaughtHandler(  569):     at org.<USER>titanium.util.TiUIHelper.viewToImage(TiUIHelper.java:417) E/TiUncaughtHandler(  569):     at org.<USER>titanium.view.TiUIView.toImage(TiUIView.java: