TIMOB-1658,12,"""iOS: Ti.File.write always returns false for binary data""","""""""On the iPhone, Titanium.Filesystem.File.write always returns  false when writing binary data to files. It works correctly for  text data. (There doesn't seem to be a problem on Android.)        {html}  <p>iPhone:</p>  <pre>  <code>[DEBUG] File foobar.txt does not exist yet.  [DEBUG] File foobar.bin does not exist yet.  [DEBUG] I successfully wrote text to the file.  [DEBUG] I was not able to write a blob to the file. Oh no!  [DEBUG] foobar.txt exists, contents: Sudo make me a sandwich.  [DEBUG] foobar.bin exists, size: 15</code>  </pre>  <p>Android:</p>  <pre>  <code>D/TiAPI   (  532): (kroll$1) [615,1099] File foobar.txt does not exist yet.  D/TiAPI   (  532): (kroll$1) [21,1120] File foobar.bin does not exist yet.  D/TiAPI   (  532): (kroll$1) [154,1274] I successfully wrote text to the file.  D/TiAPI   (  532): (kroll$1) [725,1999] I successfully wrote a blob to the file.  D/TiAPI   (  532): (kroll$1) [87,2086] foobar.txt exists, contents: Sudo make me a sandwich.  D/TiAPI   (  532): (kroll$1) [18,2104] foobar.bin exists, size: 15</code>  </pre>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.File.write always returns false for binary data
Description: """"On the iPhone, Titanium.Filesystem.File.write always returns false when writing binary data to files. It works correctly for text data. (There doesn't seem to be a problem on Android.) {html} <p>iPhone:</p> <pre> <code>[DEBUG] File foobar.txt does not exist yet. [DEBUG] File foobar.bin does not exist yet. [DEBUG] I successfully wrote text to the file. [DEBUG] I was not able to write a blob to the file. Oh no! [DEBUG] foobar.txt exists, contents: Sudo make me a sandwich. [DEBUG] foobar.bin exists, size: 15</code> </pre> <p>Android:</p> <pre> <code>D/TiAPI ( 532): (kroll$1) [615,1099] File foobar.txt does not exist yet. D/TiAPI ( 532): (kroll$1) [21,1120] File foobar.bin does not exist yet. D/TiAPI ( 532): (kroll$1) [154,1274] I successfully wrote text to the file. D/TiAPI ( 532): (kroll$1) [725,1999] I successfully wrote a blob to the file. D/TiAPI ( 532): (kroll$1) [87,2086] foobar.txt exists, contents: Sudo make me a sandwich. D/TiAPI ( 532): (kroll$1) [18,2104] foobar.bin exists, size: 15</code> </pre>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1657,12,"""JS compiler hangs""","""""""{html}<div><p>The following const statement makes the build and Ti Developer hang:</p> <p>var utils = (function() {<br></p> <pre> <code>const DAY_MILLIS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;  // lots more...</code> </pre> <p>})();</p> <p>Changing const to var works.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: JS compiler hangs
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The following const statement makes the build and Ti Developer hang:</p> <p>var utils = (function() {<br></p> <pre> <code>const DAY_MILLIS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000; // lots more...</code> </pre> <p>})();</p> <p>Changing const to var works.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1656,12,"""API inconsistency: TiBlob has 'length' property on Android, 'size' on iOS""","""""""{html}<div><p>In StatusNet Mobile, I'm trying to get the byte size of a blob I've read from a file when passing a saved photo from one context to another. The undocumented TiBlob type has a lot of differences in its interface between the iOS and Android implementations, and it's hitting here...</p> <p>On Android there's a 'length' property:</p> <pre> <code>public int getLength() {     switch (type) {         case TYPE_FILE:             return (int) ((TiBaseFile)data).getNativeFile().length();         case TYPE_DATA:         case TYPE_IMAGE:             return ((byte[])data).length;         default:             // this is probably overly expensive.. is there a better way?             return getBytes().length;     } }</code> </pre> <p>But on iOS, there's a 'size' property:</p> <p>-(NSInteger)size {</p> <pre> <code>[self ensureImageLoaded]; if (image!=nil) {     return image.size.width * image.size.height; } switch (type) {     case TiBlobTypeData:     {         return [data length];     }     case TiBlobTypeFile:     {         NSFileManager *fm = [NSFileManager defaultManager];         NSError *error = nil;          NSDictionary * resultDict = [fm attributesOfItemAtPath:path error:&amp;error];         id result = [resultDict objectForKey:NSFileSize];         if (error!=NULL)         {             return 0;         }         return [result intValue];     } } return 0;</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>They also don't have matching behavior for image blobs: Android appears to return the byte size of whatever raw data the image is using (is this source file? uncompressed? what bit depth?), while on iOS it returns the number of pixels in the image. (Shouldn't make a difference in this case though, since I'm reading straight from a saved temporary file.)</p> <p>Referencing my previous bug on the missing API documentation for the Blob type on mobile:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1580-titaniumblob-tiblob-missing-from-mobile-api-documentation""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1580-...</a></p> <p>Note that the Desktop docs do have documentation for the Blob type there:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/desktop/latest/Titanium.Blob-object""""""""> https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/desktop/latest/Titanium.B...</a></p> <p>Desktop's blob type has a 'length' property, matching the Android implementation (though I'm uncertain whether there are image blobs on Desktop, and it doesn't say how it would return a length for those).</p> <p>Assigning to StatusNet's support contact.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: API inconsistency: TiBlob has 'length' property on Android, 'size' on iOS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In StatusNet Mobile, I'm trying to get the byte size of a blob I've read from a file when passing a saved photo from one context to another. The undocumented TiBlob type has a lot of differences in its interface between the iOS and Android implementations, and it's hitting here...</p> <p>On Android there's a 'length' property:</p> <pre> <code>public int getLength() { switch (type) { case TYPE_FILE: return (int) ((TiBaseFile)data).getNativeFile().length(); case TYPE_DATA: case TYPE_IMAGE: return ((byte[])data).length; default: // this is probably overly expensive.. is there a better way? return getBytes().length; } }</code> </pre> <p>But on iOS, there's a 'size' property:</p> <p>-(NSInteger)size {</p> <pre> <code>[self ensureImageLoaded]; if (image!=nil) { return image.size.width * image.size.height; } switch (type) { case TiBlobTypeData: { return [data length]; } case TiBlobTypeFile: { NSFileManager *fm = [NSFileManager defaultManager]; NSError *error = nil; NSDictionary * resultDict = [fm attributesOfItemAtPath:path error:&amp;error]; id result = [resultDict objectForKey:NSFileSize]; if (error!=NULL) { return 0; } return [result intValue]; } } return 0;</code> </pre> <p>}</p> <p>They also don't have matching behavior for image blobs: Android appears to return the byte size of whatever raw data the image is using (is this source file? uncompressed? what bit depth?), while on iOS it returns the number of pixels in the image. (Shouldn't make a difference in this case though, since I'm reading straight from a saved temporary file.)</p> <p>Referencing my previous bug on the missing API documentation for the Blob type on mobile:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1580-titaniumblob-tiblob-missing-from-mobile-api-documentation""""""""> https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/32238/tickets/1580-...</a></p> <p>Note that the Desktop docs do have documentation for the Blob type there:</p> <p><a href= """"""""https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/desktop/latest/Titanium.Blob-object""""""""> https://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/desktop/latest/Titanium.B...</a></p> <p>Desktop's blob type has a 'length' property, matching the Android implementation (though I'm uncertain whether there are image blobs on Desktop, and it doesn't say how it would return a length for those).</p> <p>Assigning to StatusNet's support contact.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1655,12,"""Android: Support Tabs with No Title""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38661"""""""">Helpdesk 38661</a>. Title is being used as the <code>tag</code> on the TabSpec. If title is non-existant or null, use URL of the icon as the tag. If that fails use toString() of the TabProxy.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Support Tabs with No Title
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38661"""""""">Helpdesk 38661</a>. Title is being used as the <code>tag</code> on the TabSpec. If title is non-existant or null, use URL of the icon as the tag. If that fails use toString() of the TabProxy.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1654,12,"""Text Area does not accept PinYin keyboard input""","""""""{html}<div><p>It is not possible to insert characters into a Text Area using the iPad/iPhone Simplified Chinese PinYin keyboard. The characters are destroyed, apparently by a backspace, immediately they are typed.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Text Area does not accept PinYin keyboard input
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It is not possible to insert characters into a Text Area using the iPad/iPhone Simplified Chinese PinYin keyboard. The characters are destroyed, apparently by a backspace, immediately they are typed.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1653,12,"""Android: Need support for Android long press event""","""""""{html}<div><p>It's not currently possible to add an event listener for a 'long  press' event on Android (pressing and holding the finger on a  widget for a second or two), which is very frequently used for  things like context menus on Android.</p>  <p>In StatusNet Mobile's accounts list we're trying to use a  long-click to trigger a context menu for controls such as deletion  to provide a more native-feeling interface (on iPhone we use the  TableView's native editing mode, which is iOS-specific).</p>  <p>Since the native event isn't available, for now we're trying to  emulate it by listening for touchstart, touchend etc. This seems to  interfere with the natural behavior of the tableview rows; here's  the entry in our bug tracker for this:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://status.net/open-source/issues/2571"""""""">http://status.net/open-source/issues/2571</a></p>  <p>On the Android side, SimpleGestureListener has an onLongPress  stub method which could be overridden to fire a 'longpress' event;  it looks like long press support might need to be activated on the  GestureDetector by calling setIsLongpressEnabled (I'm uncertain  what the default value is, but if it's on scroll events don't work,  so perhaps it should only be set when a listener is present):</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector.SimpleOnGestureListener.html"""""""">  http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector...</a></p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector.html"""""""">  http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Need support for Android long press event
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It's not currently possible to add an event listener for a 'long press' event on Android (pressing and holding the finger on a widget for a second or two), which is very frequently used for things like context menus on Android.</p> <p>In StatusNet Mobile's accounts list we're trying to use a long-click to trigger a context menu for controls such as deletion to provide a more native-feeling interface (on iPhone we use the TableView's native editing mode, which is iOS-specific).</p> <p>Since the native event isn't available, for now we're trying to emulate it by listening for touchstart, touchend etc. This seems to interfere with the natural behavior of the tableview rows; here's the entry in our bug tracker for this:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://status.net/open-source/issues/2571"""""""">http://status.net/open-source/issues/2571</a></p> <p>On the Android side, SimpleGestureListener has an onLongPress stub method which could be overridden to fire a 'longpress' event; it looks like long press support might need to be activated on the GestureDetector by calling setIsLongpressEnabled (I'm uncertain what the default value is, but if it's on scroll events don't work, so perhaps it should only be set when a listener is present):</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector.SimpleOnGestureListener.html""""""""> http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector...</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector.html""""""""> http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/GestureDetector...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1652,12,"""Android: showCamera()'s success callback does not work for HTC phones""","""""""{html}<div><p>The success callback is supposed to have the cropRect and media properties... The media property however is always returned as undefined, and the cropRect property only returns the default values. The image itself is successfully saved in the DCIM/Camera directory, but there is no way to access the image in that callback function.</p> <p>Tested on HTC Droid Eris 2.1 and HTC Evo 2.2. I'm not sure if this is an issue for all Android phones or not.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: showCamera()'s success callback does not work for HTC phones
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The success callback is supposed to have the cropRect and media properties... The media property however is always returned as undefined, and the cropRect property only returns the default values. The image itself is successfully saved in the DCIM/Camera directory, but there is no way to access the image in that callback function.</p> <p>Tested on HTC Droid Eris 2.1 and HTC Evo 2.2. I'm not sure if this is an issue for all Android phones or not.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1649,12,"""Android: HTTPClient.send with no Argument causes NPE""","""""""{html}<div><p>Treat no argument as <code>send({});</code>. See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38031"""""""">Helpdesk 38031</a></p> <p>To work around simply use an empty dictionary. <code>http.send({});</code></p> <p>Simple fail case app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var http = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient(); http.onerror = function(e) {     Ti.API.error(e.error); }; http.open('POST','http://www.<USER>com'); http.send(); Ti.API.info('after send call');</code> </pre> <p>In the console you will see an error notice of a NullPointerException</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient.send with no Argument causes NPE
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Treat no argument as <code>send({});</code>. See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38031"""""""">Helpdesk 38031</a></p> <p>To work around simply use an empty dictionary. <code>http.send({});</code></p> <p>Simple fail case app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000'); var http = Ti.Network.createHTTPClient(); http.onerror = function(e) { Ti.API.error(e.error); }; http.open('POST','http://www.<USER>com'); http.send(); Ti.API.info('after send call');</code> </pre> <p>In the console you will see an error notice of a NullPointerException</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1648,12,"""Android: createDirectory/deleteDirectory not functioning correctly.""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38231"""""""">Helpdesk 38231</a></p> <p>createDirectory should return boolean.<br> deleteDirectory should delete directory.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: createDirectory/deleteDirectory not functioning correctly.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/38231"""""""">Helpdesk 38231</a></p> <p>createDirectory should return boolean.<br> deleteDirectory should delete directory.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1647,12,"""Navigation Group on iPad does not destroy custom left & right nav buttons""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using 1.4 on 3.2 when a window sets a left &amp; right nav button when that window is closed via the nav, those buttons are not destroyed from view. below code demonstrates.</p> <p>// app.js //</p> <p>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>backgroundColor: 'white', title: 'Nav Group'</code> </pre> <p>}); var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>text: 'Open Child Window', left: 10, top: 10</code> </pre> <p>}); win1.add(label1);</p> <p>var group = Ti.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup({<br></p> <pre> <code>window: win1</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var main = Ti.UI.createWindow();<br> main.add(group);</p> <p>main.open();</p> <p>label1.addEventListener('click',function() {<br></p> <pre> <code>var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({     title: 'Child Window',     backgroundColor: 'white' });   var nextButton = Ti.UI.createButton({     title: 'Next' });  var backButton = Ti.UI.createButton({     title: 'Back' });  win2.rightNavButton = nextButton;</code> </pre> <p>// win2.leftNavButton = backButton;</p> <pre> <code>backButton.addEventListener('click',function() {     group.close(win2); }); group.open(win2);</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Navigation Group on iPad does not destroy custom left & right nav buttons
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using 1.4 on 3.2 when a window sets a left &amp; right nav button when that window is closed via the nav, those buttons are not destroyed from view. below code demonstrates.</p> <p>// app.js //</p> <p>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>backgroundColor: 'white', title: 'Nav Group'</code> </pre> <p>}); var label1 = Ti.UI.createLabel({<br></p> <pre> <code>text: 'Open Child Window', left: 10, top: 10</code> </pre> <p>}); win1.add(label1);</p> <p>var group = Ti.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup({<br></p> <pre> <code>window: win1</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var main = Ti.UI.createWindow();<br> main.add(group);</p> <p>main.open();</p> <p>label1.addEventListener('click',function() {<br></p> <pre> <code>var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ title: 'Child Window', backgroundColor: 'white' }); var nextButton = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Next' }); var backButton = Ti.UI.createButton({ title: 'Back' }); win2.rightNavButton = nextButton;</code> </pre> <p>// win2.leftNavButton = backButton;</p> <pre> <code>backButton.addEventListener('click',function() { group.close(win2); }); group.open(win2);</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1646,12,"""iOS: Accelerometer update event is unresponsive if window loses focus and is then refocused""","""""""{html}<div><p>accelerometer (iphone) stops working after you leave the window  or page, even when it is refocused. see example code:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://gist.github.com/7e01744a05975c1a3182"""""""">http://gist.github.com/7e01744a05975c1a3182</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Accelerometer update event is unresponsive if window loses focus and is then refocused
Description: """"{html}<div><p>accelerometer (iphone) stops working after you leave the window or page, even when it is refocused. see example code:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/7e01744a05975c1a3182"""""""">http://gist.github.com/7e01744a05975c1a3182</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1645,12,"""Keyboard in 3.2 causes weird scrolling in table views that have textfields""","""""""{html}<div><p>This helpdesk ticket has the issue:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31531"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31531</a></p> <p>How to reproduce, fire up the app, rotate the sim, click login button at the top of the screen, then select a text field</p> <p>What happens:<br> once the text field is clicked, the keyboard appears and the table view scrolls even though it doesn't need to because the form is in a popover.</p> <p>this happens with 3.2 &amp; 1.4</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Keyboard in 3.2 causes weird scrolling in table views that have textfields
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This helpdesk ticket has the issue:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31531"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31531</a></p> <p>How to reproduce, fire up the app, rotate the sim, click login button at the top of the screen, then select a text field</p> <p>What happens:<br> once the text field is clicked, the keyboard appears and the table view scrolls even though it doesn't need to because the form is in a popover.</p> <p>this happens with 3.2 &amp; 1.4</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1644,12,"""file.createTimeStamp returns either 0 or 1""","""""""{html}<div><p>In iOS 4 and 4.0.2 using sdk 1.4 the following code to create a timestamp of a file returns a 1 and not the date</p> <p>var filename = 'iphone_coming_soon.png'; var timeStampOfFile = ''; var file = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,filename); if ( file.exists() ) { Ti.API.info('IF IS TRUE'); timeStampOfFile = file.createTimestamp(); }</p> <p>Ti.API.info('The value of timeStampOfFile is: ' + timeStampOfFile);</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: file.createTimeStamp returns either 0 or 1
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In iOS 4 and 4.0.2 using sdk 1.4 the following code to create a timestamp of a file returns a 1 and not the date</p> <p>var filename = 'iphone_coming_soon.png'; var timeStampOfFile = ''; var file = Titanium.Filesystem.getFile(Titanium.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory,filename); if ( file.exists() ) { Ti.API.info('IF IS TRUE'); timeStampOfFile = file.createTimestamp(); }</p> <p>Ti.API.info('The value of timeStampOfFile is: ' + timeStampOfFile);</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1643,12,"""Scrollview more than 10 children views cause app freeze""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ok, if a scrollview is placed in a window and more than 10 child views are added, any new children views added cause the app to freeze.</p> <p>Another scenario is that if the window is opened before child views are added to the scroll view, only 10 views can be added without causing a freeze. The code below demonstrates this.</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({<br> borderSize: 1, borderColor: 'blue', maxZoomScale: 1, minZoomScale: 1, contentHeight: 'auto' }); win.add(scrollView);</p> <p>// Load fisrt page for (var i=0; i&lt;50; i++) {<br> scrollView.add(Titanium.UI.createView({</p> <pre> <code>   left: (i % 4) * 70,    top: parseInt(i / 4) * 70,    width: 64,    height: 64,    backgroundColor: '#ccc'</code> </pre> <p>})); }</p> <p>alert('Application is NOT freezed');</p> <p>win.open();</p> <p>setTimeout(function(){<br></p> <pre> <code>win.remove(scrollView);</code> </pre> <p>},1000);</p> <p>setTimeout(function(){<br></p> <pre> <code>alert('Application is NOT freezed');  var scrollView2 = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({    borderSize: 1,    borderColor: 'blue',    maxZoomScale: 1,    minZoomScale: 1,    contentHeight: 'auto' }); win.add(scrollView2);  for (var i=0; i&lt;50; i++) {    scrollView2.add(Titanium.UI.createView({        left: (i % 4) * 70,        top: parseInt(i / 4) * 70,        width: 64,        height: 64,        backgroundColor: '#000'    })); };</code> </pre> <p>},3000)</p> <p>run on the iphone, iOS 4.0.2 Ti SDK 1.4</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Scrollview more than 10 children views cause app freeze
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ok, if a scrollview is placed in a window and more than 10 child views are added, any new children views added cause the app to freeze.</p> <p>Another scenario is that if the window is opened before child views are added to the scroll view, only 10 views can be added without causing a freeze. The code below demonstrates this.</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({<br> borderSize: 1, borderColor: 'blue', maxZoomScale: 1, minZoomScale: 1, contentHeight: 'auto' }); win.add(scrollView);</p> <p>// Load fisrt page for (var i=0; i&lt;50; i++) {<br> scrollView.add(Titanium.UI.createView({</p> <pre> <code> left: (i % 4) * 70, top: parseInt(i / 4) * 70, width: 64, height: 64, backgroundColor: '#ccc'</code> </pre> <p>})); }</p> <p>alert('Application is NOT freezed');</p> <p>win.open();</p> <p>setTimeout(function(){<br></p> <pre> <code>win.remove(scrollView);</code> </pre> <p>},1000);</p> <p>setTimeout(function(){<br></p> <pre> <code>alert('Application is NOT freezed'); var scrollView2 = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({ borderSize: 1, borderColor: 'blue', maxZoomScale: 1, minZoomScale: 1, contentHeight: 'auto' }); win.add(scrollView2); for (var i=0; i&lt;50; i++) { scrollView2.add(Titanium.UI.createView({ left: (i % 4) * 70, top: parseInt(i / 4) * 70, width: 64, height: 64, backgroundColor: '#000' })); };</code> </pre> <p>},3000)</p> <p>run on the iphone, iOS 4.0.2 Ti SDK 1.4</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1642,12,"""Transitioning between windows causes a crash, iOS 4/4.0.2 sdk 1.4""","""""""{html}<div><p>We have a customer that reports that when quickly moving from one window to another causes a crash.</p> <p>I cannot reproduce the crash but since the customer can I am creating this ticket.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31431"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31431</a> - this has the code</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Transitioning between windows causes a crash, iOS 4/4.0.2 sdk 1.4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We have a customer that reports that when quickly moving from one window to another causes a crash.</p> <p>I cannot reproduce the crash but since the customer can I am creating this ticket.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31431"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/31431</a> - this has the code</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1641,12,"""Android: Support Event Handlers on Hardware Buttons""","""""""{html}<div><p>Add support for overriding hardware buttons on Android devices. Not all devices will have all buttons. The following buttons should be supported.</p> <p>Back, Camera, Focus (Half-Press of Camera), Search, Volume Up, and Volume Down.</p> <p>If an event is added for any of these buttons, it takes sole responsibility for the action of the button. There will be no method to conditionally forward to the original handler. Removal of the event listener will restore default handling.</p> <p>These handlers are allowed on Ti.UI.Window and will only function when attached to """"""""heavyweight"""""""" windows. When <code>Ti.Android.Activity</code> is released handlers will be settable on <code>Ti.Android.currentActivity</code>.</p> <p>No additional data is passed in the event object.</p> <p>Example.</p> <pre> <code>win.addEventListener('android:back', function(e) {     Ti.API.Info(""""""""Pressing Back Will Not Close The Activity/Window""""""""); });</code> </pre> <p>Event Names:<br> android:back, android:camera, android:focus, android:search, android:volup, android:voldown</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Support Event Handlers on Hardware Buttons
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Add support for overriding hardware buttons on Android devices. Not all devices will have all buttons. The following buttons should be supported.</p> <p>Back, Camera, Focus (Half-Press of Camera), Search, Volume Up, and Volume Down.</p> <p>If an event is added for any of these buttons, it takes sole responsibility for the action of the button. There will be no method to conditionally forward to the original handler. Removal of the event listener will restore default handling.</p> <p>These handlers are allowed on Ti.UI.Window and will only function when attached to """"""""heavyweight"""""""" windows. When <code>Ti.Android.Activity</code> is released handlers will be settable on <code>Ti.Android.currentActivity</code>.</p> <p>No additional data is passed in the event object.</p> <p>Example.</p> <pre> <code>win.addEventListener('android:back', function(e) { Ti.API.Info(""""""""Pressing Back Will Not Close The Activity/Window""""""""); });</code> </pre> <p>Event Names:<br> android:back, android:camera, android:focus, android:search, android:volup, android:voldown</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1640,12,"""ISO Date formatting does not work in iOS""","""""""{html}<div><p>this returns an invalid date</p> <p>var start = new Date(""""""""2010-09-16T12:30:00Z"""""""");<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""Start:"""""""" + start); // prints """"""""Start: Invalid date""""""""</p> <p>a customer is requesting that we support this.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: ISO Date formatting does not work in iOS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>this returns an invalid date</p> <p>var start = new Date(""""""""2010-09-16T12:30:00Z"""""""");<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""Start:"""""""" + start); // prints """"""""Start: Invalid date""""""""</p> <p>a customer is requesting that we support this.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1639,12,"""Camera crashes in Android Froyo (2.2)""","""""""{html}<div><p>When trying to use the camera to take a picture in either the emulator or a device running APIs 2.2, it crashes.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Camera crashes in Android Froyo (2.2)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When trying to use the camera to take a picture in either the emulator or a device running APIs 2.2, it crashes.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1638,12,"""iOS: enhancement to removeProperty - make it synchronous""","""""""{html}<div><p>a premium customer reported the following:</p>  <p>I read that property setting has been made asynchronous  (<a href=""""""""https://twitter.com/titanium_github/status/21614464002)"""""""">https://twitter.com/titanium_github/status/21614464002)</a>,  can this pleeeeze also be applied to 'removeProperty', as I have a  series of complex properties I need to 'clear out' and it seems to  be generating many threads when it does.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: enhancement to removeProperty - make it synchronous
Description: """"{html}<div><p>a premium customer reported the following:</p> <p>I read that property setting has been made asynchronous (<a href=""""""""https://twitter.com/titanium_github/status/21614464002)"""""""">https://twitter.com/titanium_github/status/21614464002)</a>, can this pleeeeze also be applied to 'removeProperty', as I have a series of complex properties I need to 'clear out' and it seems to be generating many threads when it does.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1637,12,"""iOS: Controls fire 'change' event on initial value set""","""""""{html}<div><p>Controls fire a 'change' event when the value is initially set.  We should probably find a way to suppress this.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Controls fire 'change' event on initial value set
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Controls fire a 'change' event when the value is initially set. We should probably find a way to suppress this.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1636,12,"""Two switches cause repeated event firing""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that they were trying to have 2 switches be linked to each other so that when one value changed the other switch changed. The below code, when run, causes many many events to fire when the window is opened. This was run on the iphone, sdk 4.0.2 &amp; 1.4.1</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var sw1= Titanium.UI.createSwitch({ value:false, left:215,top:100});<br> win.add(sw1);</p> <p>var sw2= Titanium.UI.createSwitch({ value:true, left:215,top:200});<br> win.add(sw2);</p> <p>sw1.addEventListener('change',function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>sw2.value = !sw2.value;</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>sw2.addEventListener('change',function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>sw1.value = !sw1.value;</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Two switches cause repeated event firing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that they were trying to have 2 switches be linked to each other so that when one value changed the other switch changed. The below code, when run, causes many many events to fire when the window is opened. This was run on the iphone, sdk 4.0.2 &amp; 1.4.1</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var sw1= Titanium.UI.createSwitch({ value:false, left:215,top:100});<br> win.add(sw1);</p> <p>var sw2= Titanium.UI.createSwitch({ value:true, left:215,top:200});<br> win.add(sw2);</p> <p>sw1.addEventListener('change',function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>sw2.value = !sw2.value;</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>sw2.addEventListener('change',function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>sw1.value = !sw1.value;</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1635,12,"""Android: Errors with """"logging and Unicode"""" test cases""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;WebViews&gt;Loggin and unicode<br> 2.check console output</p> <p>results:<br> E/Web Console( 627): Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'API' of undefined at file:///android_asset/Resources/examples/webview_logging.html:5<br> D/TiAPI ( 627): (kroll$31) [102,344500] webview loaded: file:///android_asset/Resources/examples/webview_logging.html</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Errors with """"logging and Unicode"""" test cases
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;WebViews&gt;Loggin and unicode<br> 2.check console output</p> <p>results:<br> E/Web Console( 627): Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read property 'API' of undefined at file:///android_asset/Resources/examples/webview_logging.html:5<br> D/TiAPI ( 627): (kroll$31) [102,344500] webview loaded: file:///android_asset/Resources/examples/webview_logging.html</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1634,12,"""iPad - invoking a modal window from split views detail window breaks orientation behavior.""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.KS-pad&gt;split view with Nav group<br> 2.from the detail window, tap """"""""open window"""""""" then tap """"""""show modal""""""""<br> 3.dismiss the modal window and rotate the device</p> <p>results: app gets into a bad state, details and master have diff orientations, whole app draws partially off screen etc.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad - invoking a modal window from split views detail window breaks orientation behavior.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.KS-pad&gt;split view with Nav group<br> 2.from the detail window, tap """"""""open window"""""""" then tap """"""""show modal""""""""<br> 3.dismiss the modal window and rotate the device</p> <p>results: app gets into a bad state, details and master have diff orientations, whole app draws partially off screen etc.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
