TIMOB-1529,12,"""Android: Window opacity + backgroundImage doesn't seem to do anything""","""""""Run Base UI > Window Properties > Toggle BG Image, Toggle Opacity. Nothing happens.    In iOS, Toggle opacity in this test seems to go partially transparent back to the window's background color. I need to talk w/ Stephen about parity to verify the correct behavior for Android to implement.""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window opacity + backgroundImage doesn't seem to do anything
Description: """"Run Base UI > Window Properties > Toggle BG Image, Toggle Opacity. Nothing happens. In iOS, Toggle opacity in this test seems to go partially transparent back to the window's background color. I need to talk w/ Stephen about parity to verify the correct behavior for Android to implement.""""",title+description
TIMOB-1528,12,"""Android: Only one object appears when multiple views should be  drawn.""","""""""{html}<div><p>found against 1.4.1 f88b9e</p> <p>1.use the script below and run the content</p> <p>results: only one object shows, there should be 4 (one on each side) as on iPhone.</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var view = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, top:5 });</p> <p>var view1 = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, bottom:5 });</p> <p>var view2 = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, right:5 });</p> <p>var view3 = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, left:5 }); win.add(view,view1,view2,view3);</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Only one object appears when multiple views should be drawn.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>found against 1.4.1 f88b9e</p> <p>1.use the script below and run the content</p> <p>results: only one object shows, there should be 4 (one on each side) as on iPhone.</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var view = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, top:5 });</p> <p>var view1 = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, bottom:5 });</p> <p>var view2 = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, right:5 });</p> <p>var view3 = Titanium.UI.createView({<br> borderRadius:10, backgroundColor:'red', width:50, height:50, left:5 }); win.add(view,view1,view2,view3);</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
