TIMOB-1494,12,"""Slider Bug in SDK 1.4 on (at least) Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>Setting max has no effect in certain situations.</p> <p>Here is the demo code:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1079331"""""""">http://pastie.org/1079331</a> (or see attachment)</p> <p>Note, that the thumb should be in the middle of the ruler after the code has executed, but ends up closer to the beginning of the ruler, as if max wasn't changed.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Slider Bug in SDK 1.4 on (at least) Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Setting max has no effect in certain situations.</p> <p>Here is the demo code:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1079331"""""""">http://pastie.org/1079331</a> (or see attachment)</p> <p>Note, that the thumb should be in the middle of the ruler after the code has executed, but ends up closer to the beginning of the ruler, as if max wasn't changed.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1493,12,"""iOS: MapView user interaction disabled when removing event listener""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you attach an event listener to a MapView and then remove it,  the MapView will stay frozen, e.g. no user interaction will be  possible.</p>  <p>To reproduce the problem, run the attached app.js file and try  this:</p>  <ol>  <li>Click the """"""""Add listener"""""""" button<br></li>  <li>Note you can move and pinch the map<br></li>  <li>Click the """"""""Remove listener"""""""" button<br></li>  <li>MapView """"""""freezes"""""""", you are not able to move or pinch the  map.</li>  </ol>  <p>The issue seems to come from  <em>handleListenerRemovedWithEvent</em> in  <strong>TiUIView.m</strong>, specifically this part:<br></p>  <pre>  <code>self.userInteractionEnabled = NO;  self.multipleTouchEnabled = NO;</code>  </pre>  User interaction should probably stay enabled with MapView even  when there aren't any touch event listeners attached.</div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: MapView user interaction disabled when removing event listener
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you attach an event listener to a MapView and then remove it, the MapView will stay frozen, e.g. no user interaction will be possible.</p> <p>To reproduce the problem, run the attached app.js file and try this:</p> <ol> <li>Click the """"""""Add listener"""""""" button<br></li> <li>Note you can move and pinch the map<br></li> <li>Click the """"""""Remove listener"""""""" button<br></li> <li>MapView """"""""freezes"""""""", you are not able to move or pinch the map.</li> </ol> <p>The issue seems to come from <em>handleListenerRemovedWithEvent</em> in <strong>TiUIView.m</strong>, specifically this part:<br></p> <pre> <code>self.userInteractionEnabled = NO; self.multipleTouchEnabled = NO;</code> </pre> User interaction should probably stay enabled with MapView even when there aren't any touch event listeners attached.</div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1492,12,"""fullscreen windows in landscape orientation have click event problems""","""""""{html}<div><p>when using a fullscreen window in landscape, buttons placed to the right of 320 pixels will not be clickable. if you place the button at left=300, then the left-most 20 pixels will be clickable, but not the rest of the button.</p> <p>if you're using a regular window (fullscreen = false), then there is no problem.</p> <p>this is for iPhone, not sure about Android.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: fullscreen windows in landscape orientation have click event problems
Description: """"{html}<div><p>when using a fullscreen window in landscape, buttons placed to the right of 320 pixels will not be clickable. if you place the button at left=300, then the left-most 20 pixels will be clickable, but not the rest of the button.</p> <p>if you're using a regular window (fullscreen = false), then there is no problem.</p> <p>this is for iPhone, not sure about Android.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1491,12,"""Android: Auto Encode Network URLs""","""""""{html}<div><p>See iPhone Impl. <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUtils.m#L507""""""""> http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUtils.m#L507</a></p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/34201"""""""">Helpdesk 34201</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Auto Encode Network URLs
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See iPhone Impl. <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUtils.m#L507""""""""> http://github.com/<USER>titanium_mobile/blob/master/iphone/Classes/TiUtils.m#L507</a></p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/34201"""""""">Helpdesk 34201</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1490,12,"""Android: Race condition of Window focus/blur""","""""""{html}<div><p>Not sure how to address this one. It appears that the Android OS doesn't guarantee when it will call events on activities. For example it's possible for a hidden activity to have onStart called before onStop. Or it at least appears that way. It doesn't provide. Therefore it's not possible to successfully destroy a single resource like MapView.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/30371"""""""">Helpdesk 30371</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Race condition of Window focus/blur
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Not sure how to address this one. It appears that the Android OS doesn't guarantee when it will call events on activities. For example it's possible for a hidden activity to have onStart called before onStop. Or it at least appears that way. It doesn't provide. Therefore it's not possible to successfully destroy a single resource like MapView.</p> <p>See <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/30371"""""""">Helpdesk 30371</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1489,12,"""Android: Setting Background Image can cause Out of Memory""","""""""{html}<div><p>Setting the background image can cause out of memory issues. If a couple of large images are set as background it's still possible to get OOM. VM budget exceeded.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Setting Background Image can cause Out of Memory
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Setting the background image can cause out of memory issues. If a couple of large images are set as background it's still possible to get OOM. VM budget exceeded.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1488,12,"""Cannot reset the url of a sound object""","""""""{html}<div><p>In iphone sdk 4 and 1.4 and 1.4.1 changing the url property  dynamically does not work. Attaching code to reproduce this.</p>  <p>Helpdesk ticket that reported the issue:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/33391"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/33391</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Cannot reset the url of a sound object
