Description: """"{html}<div><p>Provide support to stop transitions for Activities. This is an API Level 5 feature. API Level 4 will do what it's going to do.</p> <p>Should work on open and close.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1483,12,"""Run on device -> install error""","""""""{html}<div><p>I had an application that runs in Ti SDK 1.3.0/ iPhone SDK 4.0 and it works fine in simulator and on device.<br> I upgrade the Ti SDK to 1.4.0 today and now, i can't run my app on device anymore, it shows me 'install error'. If i change the Ti SDK of my app to 1.3.0 and try run on device it works fine! any suggestions?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Run on device -> install error
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I had an application that runs in Ti SDK 1.3.0/ iPhone SDK 4.0 and it works fine in simulator and on device.<br> I upgrade the Ti SDK to 1.4.0 today and now, i can't run my app on device anymore, it shows me 'install error'. If i change the Ti SDK of my app to 1.3.0 and try run on device it works fine! any suggestions?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1482,12,"""iOS - titleImage initially draws in the incorrect location when drawing transition during setActiveTab""","""""""{html}<div><p>in kitchenSink:</p>  <p>1.Base UI&gt; views<br>  2.tap the base UI tab again while looking at the title image</p>  <p>results, the image jumps from the top right to the final  location.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - titleImage initially draws in the incorrect location when drawing transition during setActiveTab
Description: """"{html}<div><p>in kitchenSink:</p> <p>1.Base UI&gt; views<br> 2.tap the base UI tab again while looking at the title image</p> <p>results, the image jumps from the top right to the final location.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1481,12,"""SDK 1.4 does not pick up appicon on iOS 4""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that when they pushed thier app to a device,  Developer did not pick up the appicon.png. I have verified this  with my own test project.</p>  <p>How to reporduce.</p>  <p>Create a project, alter the appicon.png in the iphone directory  under Resources. Push app to a device. The icon will either be  white or the original icon.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: SDK 1.4 does not pick up appicon on iOS 4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that when they pushed thier app to a device, Developer did not pick up the appicon.png. I have verified this with my own test project.</p> <p>How to reporduce.</p> <p>Create a project, alter the appicon.png in the iphone directory under Resources. Push app to a device. The icon will either be white or the original icon.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
