Description: """"{html}<div><p>Add the constants for top, center, bottom</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1477,12,"""Standalone window with grouped view does not display section rows""","""""""{html}<div><p>Community member reported the following issue with table views  which I have confirmed on a 1.4.0 and 1.4.1 pre-release build.  Here's the Q&amp;A issue:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/48511/tableview-without-a-tabgroup--no-rows-bug"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/48511/tableview-without-...</a></p>  <p>To see it in action, try to open this window standalone in  app.js (i.e. not in a tab group), and you will notice that the rows  added to the table view section do not display. If you add the same  window to a tab group, the rows are displayed fine.</p>  <p>app.js:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1068568"""""""">http://pastie.org/1068568</a></p>  <p>newWindow.js:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://pastie.org/1068569"""""""">http://pastie.org/1068569</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Standalone window with grouped view does not display section rows
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Community member reported the following issue with table views which I have confirmed on a 1.4.0 and 1.4.1 pre-release build. Here's the Q&amp;A issue:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/48511/tableview-without-a-tabgroup--no-rows-bug""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/48511/tableview-without-...</a></p> <p>To see it in action, try to open this window standalone in app.js (i.e. not in a tab group), and you will notice that the rows added to the table view section do not display. If you add the same window to a tab group, the rows are displayed fine.</p> <p>app.js:<br> <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1068568"""""""">http://pastie.org/1068568</a></p> <p>newWindow.js:<br> <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1068569"""""""">http://pastie.org/1068569</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1475,12,"""Map Annotations do not animate on initial drop 1.4 iOS 4""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer brought to our attention that with 1.4 on iOS 4 (iphone) map annotations do not animate when they drop. The following code shows this. I also verified with the latest KS map_view.js as well.</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;<br></p> <p>// Karta</p> <pre> <code>var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({     mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,     region: {latitude:41.846715, longitude:-87.9587622, latitudeDelta:0.01, longitudeDelta:0.01},     animate:true,     regionFit:true,     userLocation:true, });  win.add(mapview);  for (i=0;i&lt;=15;i++){ var ann1 = Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({     latitude:'41.84' + Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + '715',     longitude:'-87.95' + Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + '7622',     title:""""""""Starbucks """""""" + i,     subtitle: Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + '' + Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + ' Main Street, Greenwood,  Indiana 46143',     pincolor:Titanium.Map.ANNOTATION_GREEN,     animate:true,     rightButton: Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.DISCLOSURE,     myid: i // CUSTOM ATTRIBUTE THAT IS PASSED INTO EVENT OBJECTS });  mapview.addAnnotation(ann1); //put pin on map }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Map Annotations do not animate on initial drop 1.4 iOS 4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer brought to our attention that with 1.4 on iOS 4 (iphone) map annotations do not animate when they drop. The following code shows this. I also verified with the latest KS map_view.js as well.</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;<br></p> <p>// Karta</p> <pre> <code>var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({ mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, region: {latitude:41.846715, longitude:-87.9587622, latitudeDelta:0.01, longitudeDelta:0.01}, animate:true, regionFit:true, userLocation:true, }); win.add(mapview); for (i=0;i&lt;=15;i++){ var ann1 = Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:'41.84' + Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + '715', longitude:'-87.95' + Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + '7622', title:""""""""Starbucks """""""" + i, subtitle: Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + '' + Math.floor(Math.random()*9) + ' Main Street, Greenwood, Indiana 46143', pincolor:Titanium.Map.ANNOTATION_GREEN, animate:true, rightButton: Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.DISCLOSURE, myid: i // CUSTOM ATTRIBUTE THAT IS PASSED INTO EVENT OBJECTS }); mapview.addAnnotation(ann1); //put pin on map }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1474,12,"""Incorrectly adding percent escapes to URL with a custom port number""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is on iOS.</p> <p>say I have a url '<a href= """"""""http://localhost:3000/login'"""""""">http://localhost:3000/login'</a>, it'll get escaped wrongly and fail:</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error loading: , Error: Error Domain=NSURLErrorDomain Code=-1003 """"""""A server with the specified hostname could not be found."""""""" UserInfo=0x7c4c830 {NSErrorFailingURLStringKey=<a href= """"""""https://localhost%3a3000/login"""""""">https://localhost%3a3000/login</a>, NSErrorFailingURLKey=<a href= """"""""https://localhost%3a3000/login"""""""">https://localhost%3a3000/login</a>, NSLocalizedDescription=A server with the specified hostname could not be found., NSUnderlyingError=0x7c4e470 """"""""A server with the specified hostname could not be found.""""""""}</p> <p>I removed the : from the usage of CFURLCreateStringByAddingPercentEscapes in TiUtils.m and NetworkModule.m temporarily for my purposes, though I suppose it does need to be escaped, just not in that part of the URL.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Incorrectly adding percent escapes to URL with a custom port number
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is on iOS.</p> <p>say I have a url '<a href= """"""""http://localhost:3000/login'"""""""">http://localhost:3000/login'</a>, it'll get escaped wrongly and fail:</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Error loading: , Error: Error Domain=NSURLErrorDomain Code=-1003 """"""""A server with the specified hostname could not be found."""""""" UserInfo=0x7c4c830 {NSErrorFailingURLStringKey=<a href= """"""""https://localhost%3a3000/login"""""""">https://localhost%3a3000/login</a>, NSErrorFailingURLKey=<a href= """"""""https://localhost%3a3000/login"""""""">https://localhost%3a3000/login</a>, NSLocalizedDescription=A server with the specified hostname could not be found., NSUnderlyingError=0x7c4e470 """"""""A server with the specified hostname could not be found.""""""""}</p> <p>I removed the : from the usage of CFURLCreateStringByAddingPercentEscapes in TiUtils.m and NetworkModule.m temporarily for my purposes, though I suppose it does need to be escaped, just not in that part of the URL.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1473,12,"""Android: Expose Window Soft Input Mode ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Since we have a generic activity, it's beneficial to expose <code>windowSoftInputMode</code> as a property on Window. It may only be used with """"""""heavyweight"""""""" windows (TiActivity). Constants need to be defined for the different values.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Expose Window Soft Input Mode
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Since we have a generic activity, it's beneficial to expose <code>windowSoftInputMode</code> as a property on Window. It may only be used with """"""""heavyweight"""""""" windows (TiActivity). Constants need to be defined for the different values.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
