TIMOB-1462,12,"""Countdown Picker returns the wrong values in 1.4.0 & sdk 4""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer submitted a ticket in the helpdesk that with iOS 4  and 1.4.0 the count down picker is not returning the proper values.  I see the same behavior.</p>  CODE  <p>var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p>  <pre>  <code>backgroundColor:'black'</code>  </pre>  <p>});</p>  <p>var duration = 60000 * 5; // 5 minutes<br></p>  <p>var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({<br></p>  <pre>  <code>type:Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_COUNT_DOWN_TIMER,  countDownDuration:duration</code>  </pre>  <p>});</p>  <p>picker.selectionIndicator = true;<br></p>  <p>win1.add(picker);<br></p>  <p>picker.addEventListener('change',function(e)<br>  {</p>  <pre>  <code>Ti.API.info('value = ' + picker.value);</code>  </pre>  <p>});</p>  <p>win1.open({modal:false});<br>  ########################</p>  <p>CONSOLE OUTPUT<br>  <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title=  """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Wed Nov 29 0000 23:58:58  GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title=  """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Wed Nov 29 0000 23:59:58  GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title=  """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Thu Nov 30 0000 00:00:58  GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title=  """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Thu Nov 30 0000 00:01:58  GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title=  """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Thu Nov 30 0000 00:02:58  GMT-0800 (PST)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Countdown Picker returns the wrong values in 1.4.0 & sdk 4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer submitted a ticket in the helpdesk that with iOS 4 and 1.4.0 the count down picker is not returning the proper values. I see the same behavior.</p> CODE <p>var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>backgroundColor:'black'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var duration = 60000 * 5; // 5 minutes<br></p> <p>var picker = Ti.UI.createPicker({<br></p> <pre> <code>type:Ti.UI.PICKER_TYPE_COUNT_DOWN_TIMER, countDownDuration:duration</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>picker.selectionIndicator = true;<br></p> <p>win1.add(picker);<br></p> <p>picker.addEventListener('change',function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.info('value = ' + picker.value);</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win1.open({modal:false});<br> ########################</p> <p>CONSOLE OUTPUT<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Wed Nov 29 0000 23:58:58 GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Wed Nov 29 0000 23:59:58 GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Thu Nov 30 0000 00:00:58 GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Thu Nov 30 0000 00:01:58 GMT-0800 (PST) <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> value = Thu Nov 30 0000 00:02:58 GMT-0800 (PST)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1461,12,"""HTTP PUT method fails with SDK 1.4.0 due to url-encoded path""","""""""{html}<div><p>We upgraded to Titanium Mobile SDK from 1.3.0 to 1.4.0 and use the same code base, but the effect differs.</p> <p>Trying to perform a HTTP request with PUT method fails and results always in call of onerror and in a 404 errorcode.<br> Due to Wireshark analysis of HTTP request, we figured out that the path part of uri is url-encoded now.</p> <p>Requests towards uris like<br> <a href= """"""""http://www.ourdomain.com/our,comma,separated,path/"""""""">http://www.ourdomain.com/our,comma,separated,path/</a><br> will not work anymore in titanium mobile sdk 1.4.0</p> <p>Following code snippet works with 1.3.0 on iOS 3.1.3 and does not work with 1.4.0 on iOS 4.0.1</p> <pre> <code>        var xhrPut = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient();         xhrPut.onload = function()         {             if (this.status===204){                 log(""""""""calling succes callback."""""""");             }else{                 log(""""""""error loading """"""""+this.status+"""""""" """"""""+this.responseData);             }         };         xhrPut.onerror = function()         {             log(""""""""error loading """"""""+this.status+"""""""" """"""""+this.responseData);         };          xhrPut.open(""""""""PUT"""""""",baseuri+uri);         xhrPut.setRequestHeader('Authorization','Basic '+authstrPut);         xhrPut.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json; charset=utf-8');         xhrPut.setRequestHeader('Accept', 'application/json');         xhrPut.send(JSON.stringify(params));          //variables: baseuri, uri, authstrPut, params</code> </pre> <p>With regards.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: HTTP PUT method fails with SDK 1.4.0 due to url-encoded path
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We upgraded to Titanium Mobile SDK from 1.3.0 to 1.4.0 and use the same code base, but the effect differs.</p> <p>Trying to perform a HTTP request with PUT method fails and results always in call of onerror and in a 404 errorcode.<br> Due to Wireshark analysis of HTTP request, we figured out that the path part of uri is url-encoded now.</p> <p>Requests towards uris like<br> <a href= """"""""http://www.ourdomain.com/our,comma,separated,path/"""""""">http://www.ourdomain.com/our,comma,separated,path/</a><br> will not work anymore in titanium mobile sdk 1.4.0</p> <p>Following code snippet works with 1.3.0 on iOS 3.1.3 and does not work with 1.4.0 on iOS 4.0.1</p> <pre> <code> var xhrPut = Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(); xhrPut.onload = function() { if (this.status===204){ log(""""""""calling succes callback.""""""""); }else{ log(""""""""error loading """"""""+this.status+"""""""" """"""""+this.responseData); } }; xhrPut.onerror = function() { log(""""""""error loading """"""""+this.status+"""""""" """"""""+this.responseData); }; xhrPut.open(""""""""PUT"""""""",baseuri+uri); xhrPut.setRequestHeader('Authorization','Basic '+authstrPut); xhrPut.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json; charset=utf-8'); xhrPut.setRequestHeader('Accept', 'application/json'); xhrPut.send(JSON.stringify(params)); //variables: baseuri, uri, authstrPut, params</code> </pre> <p>With regards.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1460,12,"""App Compilation Broken After Upgrading To 1.4.0""","""""""{html}<div><p>I just upgraded my version of Titanium to 1.4.0 and for some reason, my custom app is not working with the Android emulator, the iPhone on-device testing or for Android Market distribution.</p> <p>The Android tab isn't there at all on the Run on Device page and it says that my """"""""project is not configured to run for Android"""""""" on the Distribution page's Android tab. This wasn't happening before I upgraded.</p> <p>I can run KitchenSink fine and everything there (on-device and simulator) works fine for Android, but only on the KitchenSink project; not on my custom project. For reference, my Android SDK path is set to /Users/*/Downloads/android-sdk-mac_86/platforms/android-8 .</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: App Compilation Broken After Upgrading To 1.4.0
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I just upgraded my version of Titanium to 1.4.0 and for some reason, my custom app is not working with the Android emulator, the iPhone on-device testing or for Android Market distribution.</p> <p>The Android tab isn't there at all on the Run on Device page and it says that my """"""""project is not configured to run for Android"""""""" on the Distribution page's Android tab. This wasn't happening before I upgraded.</p> <p>I can run KitchenSink fine and everything there (on-device and simulator) works fine for Android, but only on the KitchenSink project; not on my custom project. For reference, my Android SDK path is set to /Users/*/Downloads/android-sdk-mac_86/platforms/android-8 .</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1459,12,"""Label object using backgroundImage and backgroundpadding moves unexpectedly when changing the backgroundImage value""","""""""{html}<div><p>Enterprise customer issue.</p> <p>Using the provided content:<br> 1.launch the app and watch the label<br> results: 2 seconds after the content loads, the backgroundImage is changed, at which point the label moves to the left unexpectedly</p> <p>expected:label to retain positioning when backgroundImage value is changed</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Label object using backgroundImage and backgroundpadding moves unexpectedly when changing the backgroundImage value
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Enterprise customer issue.</p> <p>Using the provided content:<br> 1.launch the app and watch the label<br> results: 2 seconds after the content loads, the backgroundImage is changed, at which point the label moves to the left unexpectedly</p> <p>expected:label to retain positioning when backgroundImage value is changed</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1458,12,"""WebView doesn't keep html""","""""""{html}<div><p>If I add a local string to the html-attribute and try to get the string back, I'll only get an empty html tag.</p> <pre> <code>var html = '&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;Text&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;'; var view = Titanium.UI.createWebView(); view.html = html; alert(view.html);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: WebView doesn't keep html
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If I add a local string to the html-attribute and try to get the string back, I'll only get an empty html tag.</p> <pre> <code>var html = '&lt;html&gt;&lt;body&gt;Text&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;'; var view = Titanium.UI.createWebView(); view.html = html; alert(view.html);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1457,12,"""iOS: Rotate transform animate flickers to rotate 0 with each turn""","""""""{html}<div><p>When trying to spin an imageView with controlled degrees on each  call without any duration in the animation, the image resets to  0deg before the transform is applied with the animate. More  description and example found here:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/32961/continuous-rotation"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/32961/continuous-rotation</a>  and here<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/10181/multiple-rotates-of-view-with-animation-part-2"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/10181/multiple-rotates-o...</a></p>  <p>A possible solution would be to be able to apply the transform  directly on the UI object without having to call animate when you  just want it to instantly move without taking the time to do an  animation.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Rotate transform animate flickers to rotate 0 with each turn
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When trying to spin an imageView with controlled degrees on each call without any duration in the animation, the image resets to 0deg before the transform is applied with the animate. More description and example found here:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/32961/continuous-rotation""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/32961/continuous-rotation</a> and here<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/10181/multiple-rotates-of-view-with-animation-part-2""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/10181/multiple-rotates-o...</a></p> <p>A possible solution would be to be able to apply the transform directly on the UI object without having to call animate when you just want it to instantly move without taking the time to do an animation.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1456,12,"""Crash with Switch control in TableView""","""""""{html}<div><p>This can be seen by loading table_view_controls_2.js in KitchenSink</p> <p>stacktrace here:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/505881"""""""">http://gist.github.com/505881</a></p> <p>Tested against continuous build mobilesdk-1.4.1-20100801235900-osx.zip</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Crash with Switch control in TableView
