TIMOB-1370,12,"""iOS: Returning from landscape, scroll view inside scroller view loses its current images (goes blank)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Returning from landscape, scroll view inside scroller view loses  its current images (goes blank)<br>  Have to scroll to reset it back.</p>  <pre>  <code class=  """"""""javascript"""""""">var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({backgroundColor:'#ffffff', contentHeight:'auto', layout:'vertical', contentWidth:320,  top:0,  showVerticalScrollIndicator:true,   showHorizontalScrollIndicator:false});      var image_scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({top:20,left:10,width:300,height:190,views:photo_array,showPagingControl:true,pagingControlColor:'#999',pagingControlHeight:5,maxZoomScale:2.0  });  scrollView.add(image_scrollView);</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Returning from landscape, scroll view inside scroller view loses its current images (goes blank)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Returning from landscape, scroll view inside scroller view loses its current images (goes blank)<br> Have to scroll to reset it back.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollView({backgroundColor:'#ffffff', contentHeight:'auto', layout:'vertical', contentWidth:320, top:0, showVerticalScrollIndicator:true, showHorizontalScrollIndicator:false}); var image_scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({top:20,left:10,width:300,height:190,views:photo_array,showPagingControl:true,pagingControlColor:'#999',pagingControlHeight:5,maxZoomScale:2.0 }); scrollView.add(image_scrollView);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1369,12,"""iOS: Images in scrollview gets jambled up in landscape""","""""""{html}<div><p>I got a small scrollview in portrait inside a scollerview, which  works okay (stops accepting vertial scroll if only one image is  there). Then when u turn the phone sideways, a second window opens  with a landscape imageview, this worked in 1.3 but now it goes  crazy monkey and every thing is jumbled up</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">      Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e)      {   //Titanium.UI.orientation = e.orientation;          if(e.orientation == Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT || e.orientation == Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT)          {                 (function(photo_array)              {   var gallery_win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({                      url:'gallery.js',                      backgroundColor:'#000000',                      fullscreen: true,                      orientationModes: [Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT]                  });                  gallery_win.photo_array = photo_array;                    gallery_win.open();                                })(photo_array);          }             });    //gallery.js  var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow;    var image_scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({views:win.photo_array, maxZoomScale:2.0, fullscreen:true, height: 'auto', width:  'auto' });  win.add(image_scrollView);    Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e){      if(e.orientation == Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT)      {   win.close();      }  });</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Images in scrollview gets jambled up in landscape
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I got a small scrollview in portrait inside a scollerview, which works okay (stops accepting vertial scroll if only one image is there). Then when u turn the phone sideways, a second window opens with a landscape imageview, this worked in 1.3 but now it goes crazy monkey and every thing is jumbled up</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e) { //Titanium.UI.orientation = e.orientation; if(e.orientation == Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT || e.orientation == Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT) { (function(photo_array) { var gallery_win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ url:'gallery.js', backgroundColor:'#000000', fullscreen: true, orientationModes: [Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT] }); gallery_win.photo_array = photo_array; gallery_win.open(); })(photo_array); } }); //gallery.js var win = Titanium.UI.currentWindow; var image_scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({views:win.photo_array, maxZoomScale:2.0, fullscreen:true, height: 'auto', width: 'auto' }); win.add(image_scrollView); Ti.Gesture.addEventListener('orientationchange',function(e){ if(e.orientation == Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT) { win.close(); } });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1368,12,"""tabview back button  background image shrinks""","""""""{html}<div><p>The tabview back button on top left, when i set its background image. it shrinks it so it shows up in the middle.</p> <p>Image size is 97 x 31 png</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascipt"""""""">  function open_property_detail(oid) {   var property_detail_win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({         titlePrompt: ' ',         barImage: 'images/title_bg.png',             backgroundColor:'#000000',         backButtonTitleImage: 'images/back_btn.png',         url:'view.js'         //orientationModes: [Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT]     });     property_detail_win.oid = oid;     Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(property_detail_win,{animated:true}); }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: tabview back button background image shrinks
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The tabview back button on top left, when i set its background image. it shrinks it so it shows up in the middle.</p> <p>Image size is 97 x 31 png</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascipt""""""""> function open_property_detail(oid) { var property_detail_win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ titlePrompt: ' ', barImage: 'images/title_bg.png', backgroundColor:'#000000', backButtonTitleImage: 'images/back_btn.png', url:'view.js' //orientationModes: [Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_RIGHT, Titanium.UI.LANDSCAPE_LEFT] }); property_detail_win.oid = oid; Titanium.UI.currentTab.open(property_detail_win,{animated:true}); }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1367,12,"""iOS : flashing/redraw issue when dismissing modal windows and using partial curl""","""""""{html}<div><p>See it using kitchensink and a 3.2+ device.</p> <p>1.nav to BaseUI&gt;Modal Windows&gt; and from the picker, select """"""""partial curl"""""""" (from the left side) and any of the option on the right (""""""""current ctx"""""""" seems to be the worst of it)<br> 2.Tap show modal, then tap close from the resulting window.<br> 3.watch the area being redrawn (bottom area)</p> <p>results: there is a flashing white during the transition.</p> <p>expected: ideally, no such flashing/redraw issues</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : flashing/redraw issue when dismissing modal windows and using partial curl
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See it using kitchensink and a 3.2+ device.</p> <p>1.nav to BaseUI&gt;Modal Windows&gt; and from the picker, select """"""""partial curl"""""""" (from the left side) and any of the option on the right (""""""""current ctx"""""""" seems to be the worst of it)<br> 2.Tap show modal, then tap close from the resulting window.<br> 3.watch the area being redrawn (bottom area)</p> <p>results: there is a flashing white during the transition.</p> <p>expected: ideally, no such flashing/redraw issues</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1366,12,"""iOS : Changing label while label is hidden behaves differently than when its shown""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using KitchenSink:<br> 1.Nav to Controls&gt;Label<br> 2.Tap """"""""Change Label 2)<br> 3.Tap """"""""Hide/Show""""""""<br> 4.Tap """"""""Change Label 2)<br> 5.Tap """"""""Hide/Show""""""""</p> <p>results: """"""""AP..."""""""" (see screen shot)</p> <p>expected: """"""""<USER>"""""" do the same steps without hiding the label to see expected behavior.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : Changing label while label is hidden behaves differently than when its shown
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using KitchenSink:<br> 1.Nav to Controls&gt;Label<br> 2.Tap """"""""Change Label 2)<br> 3.Tap """"""""Hide/Show""""""""<br> 4.Tap """"""""Change Label 2)<br> 5.Tap """"""""Hide/Show""""""""</p> <p>results: """"""""AP..."""""""" (see screen shot)</p> <p>expected: """"""""<USER>"""""" do the same steps without hiding the label to see expected behavior.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1365,12,"""iOS : unexpected behavior on progress bar test in KS""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.fire up KS on an iOS device<br>  2.nav to controls&gt;Progress Bar<br>  3.Tap """"""""Start Progress button"""""""" and the test complete.<br>  4,Tap the button a second time</p>  <p>results: on the second time through the test, the progress bars  in the toolBar and NavBar do not appear.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS : unexpected behavior on progress bar test in KS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.fire up KS on an iOS device<br> 2.nav to controls&gt;Progress Bar<br> 3.Tap """"""""Start Progress button"""""""" and the test complete.<br> 4,Tap the button a second time</p> <p>results: on the second time through the test, the progress bars in the toolBar and NavBar do not appear.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1364,12,"""iOS: dismissing an activity indicator from the Toolbar or Navbar takes ~2 seconds""","""""""{html}<div><p>this reproduces in the simulator as well as the device. You can see it using KS by:</p> <p>1.Nav to Controls&gt;Activity indicator<br> 2.Tap """"""""Show Indicator (toolBar)"""""""" then tap hide. NOte how long it takes to dismiss<br> 3.repeat with """"""""Show Indicator (NavBar)""""""""<br> 4.repeat with any of the other locations indicators can be.</p> <p>results:all indicators except those in the toolbar and navbar dismiss immediately, whilst indicators in the the toolbar and navbar take about 2 seconds to dismiss.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: dismissing an activity indicator from the Toolbar or Navbar takes ~2 seconds
Description: """"{html}<div><p>this reproduces in the simulator as well as the device. You can see it using KS by:</p> <p>1.Nav to Controls&gt;Activity indicator<br> 2.Tap """"""""Show Indicator (toolBar)"""""""" then tap hide. NOte how long it takes to dismiss<br> 3.repeat with """"""""Show Indicator (NavBar)""""""""<br> 4.repeat with any of the other locations indicators can be.</p> <p>results:all indicators except those in the toolbar and navbar dismiss immediately, whilst indicators in the the toolbar and navbar take about 2 seconds to dismiss.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1363,12,"""iOS - difference in handling of html5 video with iOS4 and iOS3.1.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>1.using KitchenSink, navigate to BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;webviews&gt;html5 video<br> 2.note the appearance of the video on load</p> <p>results:on iOS4. the video shows the first frame on load, on 3.1.2 it shows a generic video icon</p> <p>3.in portrait, tap the movie icon to start playback</p> <p>results:on iOS4, the video starts playing in portrait. On 3.1.2 it begins playback in landscape. If you rotate to landscape and back, it will show portrait.</p> <p>expected: The video on 3.1.2 should play in the current orientation. parity between iOS4 and 3.1.2 if possible.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS - difference in handling of html5 video with iOS4 and iOS3.1.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>1.using KitchenSink, navigate to BaseUI&gt;Views&gt;webviews&gt;html5 video<br> 2.note the appearance of the video on load</p> <p>results:on iOS4. the video shows the first frame on load, on 3.1.2 it shows a generic video icon</p> <p>3.in portrait, tap the movie icon to start playback</p> <p>results:on iOS4, the video starts playing in portrait. On 3.1.2 it begins playback in landscape. If you rotate to landscape and back, it will show portrait.</p> <p>expected: The video on 3.1.2 should play in the current orientation. parity between iOS4 and 3.1.2 if possible.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1362,12,"""Debugging Info is Not working 4.0.1 SDK""","""""""{html}<div><p>On new SDK 4.0.1 no debug output is posting to the Titanium console. 3.2 SDK shows proper output, but not for 4.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Debugging Info is Not working 4.0.1 SDK
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On new SDK 4.0.1 no debug output is posting to the Titanium console. 3.2 SDK shows proper output, but not for 4.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1361,12,"""createTextField in a createTableViewRow doesn't render""","""""""{html}<div><p>Version 1.3.2 adding a text field as part of a row works without issue. In version 1.3.3 the table row size increases and no text field shows. This is also true for switches. Simple table, no styles applied. This can be replicated with the 3.2 and 4.0 iPhone SDKs. 1.3.2 works as expected on both 3.2 and 4.0.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: createTextField in a createTableViewRow doesn't render
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Version 1.3.2 adding a text field as part of a row works without issue. In version 1.3.3 the table row size increases and no text field shows. This is also true for switches. Simple table, no styles applied. This can be replicated with the 3.2 and 4.0 iPhone SDKs. 1.3.2 works as expected on both 3.2 and 4.0.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1360,12,"""iOS: issue with 4 letter extension when copying to """"Documents"""" folder on device""","""""""{html}<div><p>bug came via <a href= """"""""http://anovice.com/2010/07/16/installing-app-files-with-<USER>titanium/""""""""> http://anovice.com/2010/07/16/installing-app-files-with-appcelerato...</a></p> <p>the issue is that when copying files from Apps """"""""Resources"""""""" folder to the devices """"""""Documents"""""""" folder, using a 4 letter extension (html vs htm) fails. This does work in the simulator.</p> <p>replace htm with html in the following example.</p> <p>if (Ti.App.Properties.getInt(""""""""installComplete"""""""") == null) {<br></p> <pre> <code> var imgOriginal = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory + """"""""/image.jpg"""""""");  var imgInstall = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory + """"""""/image.jpg"""""""");  imgInstall.write(imgOriginal);   var dataOrig = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory + """"""""/foo.html"""""""");  var dataInstall = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory + """"""""/foo.html"""""""");  var dataContent = dataOrig.read();  dataInstall.write(dataContent);   Ti.App.Properties.setInt(""""""""installComplete"""""""", 1);</code> </pre> <p>}</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: issue with 4 letter extension when copying to """"Documents"""" folder on device
Description: """"{html}<div><p>bug came via <a href= """"""""http://anovice.com/2010/07/16/installing-app-files-with-<USER>titanium/""""""""> http://anovice.com/2010/07/16/installing-app-files-with-appcelerato...</a></p> <p>the issue is that when copying files from Apps """"""""Resources"""""""" folder to the devices """"""""Documents"""""""" folder, using a 4 letter extension (html vs htm) fails. This does work in the simulator.</p> <p>replace htm with html in the following example.</p> <p>if (Ti.App.Properties.getInt(""""""""installComplete"""""""") == null) {<br></p> <pre> <code> var imgOriginal = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory + """"""""/image.jpg""""""""); var imgInstall = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory + """"""""/image.jpg""""""""); imgInstall.write(imgOriginal); var dataOrig = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.resourcesDirectory + """"""""/foo.html""""""""); var dataInstall = Ti.Filesystem.getFile(Ti.Filesystem.applicationDataDirectory + """"""""/foo.html""""""""); var dataContent = dataOrig.read(); dataInstall.write(dataContent); Ti.App.Properties.setInt(""""""""installComplete"""""""", 1);</code> </pre> <p>}</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1359,12,"""Blackberry: Add Support for .buildHash and .buildDate""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium.buildHash and Titanium.buildDate return null on blackberry.</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DST"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DST]"""""""">[DST]</a> Implementation Note: Log the information at the top of each builder.py run with our other diagnostic information at the INFO level. This will make it easier to diagnose then going into the app.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Blackberry: Add Support for .buildHash and .buildDate
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium.buildHash and Titanium.buildDate return null on blackberry.</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DST"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DST]"""""""">[DST]</a> Implementation Note: Log the information at the top of each builder.py run with our other diagnostic information at the INFO level. This will make it easier to diagnose then going into the app.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1358,12,"""Android - add support for .buildHash and .buildDate""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium.buildHash and Titanium.buildDate return null on android, return values on iOS.</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DST"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DST]"""""""">[DST]</a> Implementation Note: Log the information at the top of each builder.py run with our other diagnostic information at the INFO level. This will make it easier to diagnose then going into the app.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android - add support for .buildHash and .buildDate
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium.buildHash and Titanium.buildDate return null on android, return values on iOS.</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/DST"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [DST]"""""""">[DST]</a> Implementation Note: Log the information at the top of each builder.py run with our other diagnostic information at the INFO level. This will make it easier to diagnose then going into the app.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1357,12,"""iOS: App Close event on IOS4 not fired""","""""""{html}<div><p>The App's close event is not fired under iOS4.</p>  <p>If you press the home button, double click the home button and  close the app from the """"""""running tasks"""""""" bar (which is the way to  really close an app under iOS4) no log output appears and no  properties are saved with this code:</p>  <pre>  <code class=  """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.App.addEventListener('close',function() {      Ti.API.info(""""""""Saving close event info"""""""");      Ti.App.Properties.setInt('closeevent', 1);  });</code>  </pre>  <p>Dont't mix up with <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/982"""""""" title=  """"""""Ticket #982"""""""">#982</a> - this is a iOS4 problem. The above code  works with iPhone OS 3.2.</p>  <p>Tested in simulator and on device.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: App Close event on IOS4 not fired
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The App's close event is not fired under iOS4.</p> <p>If you press the home button, double click the home button and close the app from the """"""""running tasks"""""""" bar (which is the way to really close an app under iOS4) no log output appears and no properties are saved with this code:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Ti.App.addEventListener('close',function() { Ti.API.info(""""""""Saving close event info""""""""); Ti.App.Properties.setInt('closeevent', 1); });</code> </pre> <p>Dont't mix up with <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/982"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #982"""""""">#982</a> - this is a iOS4 problem. The above code works with iPhone OS 3.2.</p> <p>Tested in simulator and on device.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1355,12,"""Android: Ti.Filesystem.createTempFile throws Exception""","""""""{html}<div><p>See origina Q&amp;A:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/37571/createtempfile-failing-on-android""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/37571/createtempfile-fai...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Ti.Filesystem.createTempFile throws Exception
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See origina Q&amp;A:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/37571/createtempfile-failing-on-android""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/37571/createtempfile-fai...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1354,12,"""Orientation and layout issues""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/45041/switching-between-landscapeportrait--screwed-up-table-views""""""""> Community Q&amp;A item</a></p> <p>It seems that text is not properly reformatted when the application switches between landscape and portrait mode. I put together a very small sample app (~100 lines of code): <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1054148"""""""">http://pastie.org/1054148</a></p> <p>To see what I mean, just fire up the code and do the following:</p> <ol> <li>In Tab1, switch to landscape mode (command + left arrow).<br></li> <li>Then move to Tab2, and notice that the text has not been reformatted.<br></li> <li>While still in Tab2, switch back to portrait mode (command + right arrow)<br></li> <li>Move back to Tab1, and notice the text is also screwed up there</li> </ol> <p>NOTE:</p> <p>I duplicated this behavior on 1.3.3 version from head.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Orientation and layout issues
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/45041/switching-between-landscapeportrait--screwed-up-table-views""""""""> Community Q&amp;A item</a></p> <p>It seems that text is not properly reformatted when the application switches between landscape and portrait mode. I put together a very small sample app (~100 lines of code): <a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1054148"""""""">http://pastie.org/1054148</a></p> <p>To see what I mean, just fire up the code and do the following:</p> <ol> <li>In Tab1, switch to landscape mode (command + left arrow).<br></li> <li>Then move to Tab2, and notice that the text has not been reformatted.<br></li> <li>While still in Tab2, switch back to portrait mode (command + right arrow)<br></li> <li>Move back to Tab1, and notice the text is also screwed up there</li> </ol> <p>NOTE:</p> <p>I duplicated this behavior on 1.3.3 version from head.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1353,12,"""Unable to Use Custom Fonts""","""""""{html}<div><p>Instructions for using custom fonts are given here:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/12051/custom-fonts"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/question/12051/custom-fonts</a><br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/blog/2010/04/adding-custom-fonts-to-ipad.html""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/blog/2010/04/adding-custom-fonts-...</a></p> <p>Comments on those posts, as well as this one indicate that this functionality doesn't work:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/32691/use-custom-font-for-label""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/32691/use-custom-font-fo...</a></p> <p>I, personally, have tried everything and cannot get this to work.</p> <p>Something must have happened since SDK 3.2 when this was originally available that breaks this functionality.</p> <p>Please provide a fix as soon as possible.</p> <p>Thank you!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Unable to Use Custom Fonts
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Instructions for using custom fonts are given here:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/12051/custom-fonts"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/question/12051/custom-fonts</a><br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/blog/2010/04/adding-custom-fonts-to-ipad.html""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/blog/2010/04/adding-custom-fonts-...</a></p> <p>Comments on those posts, as well as this one indicate that this functionality doesn't work:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/32691/use-custom-font-for-label""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/32691/use-custom-font-fo...</a></p> <p>I, personally, have tried everything and cannot get this to work.</p> <p>Something must have happened since SDK 3.2 when this was originally available that breaks this functionality.</p> <p>Please provide a fix as soon as possible.</p> <p>Thank you!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1352,12,"""Ability to pad hasCheck & hasDetail graphics in tableViewRow, to allow then to line up with other graphics""","""""""{html}<div><p>Platform: Android</p> <p>Currently the hasChild graphic (and hasDetail, when it is implemented for Android) is shown at a set distance from the right hand edge of the table, and it is currently not affected by the """"""""right"""""""" property. A way to line these up with graphics in other rows would be useful.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ability to pad hasCheck & hasDetail graphics in tableViewRow, to allow then to line up with other graphics
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Platform: Android</p> <p>Currently the hasChild graphic (and hasDetail, when it is implemented for Android) is shown at a set distance from the right hand edge of the table, and it is currently not affected by the """"""""right"""""""" property. A way to line these up with graphics in other rows would be useful.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
