TIMOB-1303,12,"""TableView scrollable property after it loses focus""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ok, a customer reported that when a table view has scrollable set to false, and the table loses focus, like when a text field gains focus, the scrollable flag goes away. I verified this with the KS table_view_layout_2.js on iphone OS 4 and our latest from HEAD.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView scrollable property after it loses focus
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ok, a customer reported that when a table view has scrollable set to false, and the table loses focus, like when a text field gains focus, the scrollable flag goes away. I verified this with the KS table_view_layout_2.js on iphone OS 4 and our latest from HEAD.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1302,12,"""Android: addEventListener listener argument should allow DOM2 spec's handleEvent property""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href=  """"""""http://www.w3.org/TR/DOM-Level-2-Events/events.html#Events-registration"""""""">  W3C DOM2 Events Registration Spec</a></p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://www.w3.org/TR/DOM-Level-2-Events/events.html#Events-EventListener"""""""">  W3C DOM2 EventListener Spec</a></p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://ajaxian.com/archives/an-alternative-way-to-addeventlistener"""""""">  Ajaxian -- An alternative way to addEventListener</a> following  <a href=""""""""http://twitter.com/SubtleGradient/status/18388549003""""""""  title=""""""""I can't believe none of us knew DOM2&hellip;"""""""">my recent  Tweet</a></p>  <p><a href=""""""""http://gist.github.com/446641#LID1081"""""""">Apple's iAD.js  uses handleEvent a <strong>lot</strong></a></p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">listener = {      p: """"""""Hello world!"""""""",      handleEvent: function(e){ alert(this.p) }  }    view.addEventListener('click', listener)</code>  </pre>  <p><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/"""""""" title=  """"""""This page details some differences between ECMAScript bindings implementations in different UAs"""""""">  ECMAScript binding tests</a></p>  <ul>  <li><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/#t025"""""""">025  &mdash; Registering an EventListener with an object with a  handleEvent property</a></li>  <li><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/#t026"""""""">026  &mdash; Registering an EventListener with a function object that  also has a handleEvent property</a></li>  <li><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/#t027"""""""">027  &mdash; Registering an EventListener with an object whose  handleEvent property comes from the prototype</a></li>  </ul></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: addEventListener listener argument should allow DOM2 spec's handleEvent property
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://www.w3.org/TR/DOM-Level-2-Events/events.html#Events-registration""""""""> W3C DOM2 Events Registration Spec</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://www.w3.org/TR/DOM-Level-2-Events/events.html#Events-EventListener""""""""> W3C DOM2 EventListener Spec</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://ajaxian.com/archives/an-alternative-way-to-addeventlistener""""""""> Ajaxian -- An alternative way to addEventListener</a> following <a href=""""""""http://twitter.com/SubtleGradient/status/18388549003"""""""" title=""""""""I can't believe none of us knew DOM2&hellip;"""""""">my recent Tweet</a></p> <p><a href=""""""""http://gist.github.com/446641#LID1081"""""""">Apple's iAD.js uses handleEvent a <strong>lot</strong></a></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">listener = { p: """"""""Hello world!"""""""", handleEvent: function(e){ alert(this.p) } } view.addEventListener('click', listener)</code> </pre> <p><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/"""""""" title= """"""""This page details some differences between ECMAScript bindings implementations in different UAs""""""""> ECMAScript binding tests</a></p> <ul> <li><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/#t025"""""""">025 &mdash; Registering an EventListener with an object with a handleEvent property</a></li> <li><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/#t026"""""""">026 &mdash; Registering an EventListener with a function object that also has a handleEvent property</a></li> <li><a href=""""""""http://mcc.id.au/2007/05/binding-tests/#t027"""""""">027 &mdash; Registering an EventListener with an object whose handleEvent property comes from the prototype</a></li> </ul></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1301,12,"""Labels do not honor touchEnabled false""","""""""{html}<div><p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var cell = Ti.UI.createView();</p> <p>var title = Ti.UI.createLabel({text:'label 1',touchEnabled:false,height:35,top:0});<br> var source = Ti.UI.createLabel({text:'label 1',touchEnabled:false,height:35,top:40});<br> var excerpt = Ti.UI.createLabel({text:'label 1',touchEnabled:false,height:35,top:80});</p> <p>cell.add(title);<br> cell.add(source);<br> cell.add(excerpt);</p> <p>cell.addEventListener('swipe', function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.log(e.source);</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>title.addEventListener('touchstart',function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.log('title was touched');</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(cell);</p> <p>when run on our latest HEAD on OS 4 the labels still receive touch events.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Labels do not honor touchEnabled false
Description: """"{html}<div><p>var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow;</p> <p>var cell = Ti.UI.createView();</p> <p>var title = Ti.UI.createLabel({text:'label 1',touchEnabled:false,height:35,top:0});<br> var source = Ti.UI.createLabel({text:'label 1',touchEnabled:false,height:35,top:40});<br> var excerpt = Ti.UI.createLabel({text:'label 1',touchEnabled:false,height:35,top:80});</p> <p>cell.add(title);<br> cell.add(source);<br> cell.add(excerpt);</p> <p>cell.addEventListener('swipe', function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.log(e.source);</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>title.addEventListener('touchstart',function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code>Ti.API.log('title was touched');</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(cell);</p> <p>when run on our latest HEAD on OS 4 the labels still receive touch events.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
