TIMOB-1282,12,"""Picker setSelectedRow OS 4 SDK 1.3.3 (HEAD)""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that with SDK 1.3.2, after adding a picker to a window, using the setSelectedRow worked and this does not work in 1.3.3 from HEAD.</p> <p>I was able to reproduce this with picker_basic.js in the Kitchen Sink. I was able to get it to work with a setTimeout of 100ms though which leaves me to believe that there is a delay in component creation and being able to use methods on a component. My picker_basic.js is attached and the setTimeout is at the bottom of the file.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Picker setSelectedRow OS 4 SDK 1.3.3 (HEAD)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that with SDK 1.3.2, after adding a picker to a window, using the setSelectedRow worked and this does not work in 1.3.3 from HEAD.</p> <p>I was able to reproduce this with picker_basic.js in the Kitchen Sink. I was able to get it to work with a setTimeout of 100ms though which leaves me to believe that there is a delay in component creation and being able to use methods on a component. My picker_basic.js is attached and the setTimeout is at the bottom of the file.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1281,12,"""iOS: Detecting Video Orientation""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported this:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/27631"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/27631</a></p>  <p>Basically, Apple's Quicktime will auto rotate a video so that it  will view 'in a correct orientation' even when the video was taken  in landscape. Non quicktime video viewers do not do this so they  will not show 'correctly'.</p>  <p>These Apple forum posts talk about this:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00148.html"""""""">  http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00148.html</a></p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00149.html"""""""">  http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00149.html</a></p>  <p>This customer is asking that we detect the orientation and flip  it to be correct.</p>  <p>iPhone OS 4</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Detecting Video Orientation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported this:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/27631"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/helpdesk/view/27631</a></p> <p>Basically, Apple's Quicktime will auto rotate a video so that it will view 'in a correct orientation' even when the video was taken in landscape. Non quicktime video viewers do not do this so they will not show 'correctly'.</p> <p>These Apple forum posts talk about this:<br> <a href= """"""""http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00148.html""""""""> http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00148.html</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00149.html""""""""> http://lists.apple.com/archives/quicktime-api/2009/Jan/msg00149.html</a></p> <p>This customer is asking that we detect the orientation and flip it to be correct.</p> <p>iPhone OS 4</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1280,12,"""Geolocation watchPosition""","""""""{html}<div><p>Implement watchPosition - allowing a user to be notified should the device be within the radius of a location.<br> Re: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/41491/geolocation-documentation""""""""> Q&amp;A</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Geolocation watchPosition
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Implement watchPosition - allowing a user to be notified should the device be within the radius of a location.<br> Re: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/41491/geolocation-documentation""""""""> Q&amp;A</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1279,12,"""Allow preferred location provider to be set""","""""""{html}<div><p>Allow the preferred location provider to be set by the user - re: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/40741/geolocation-force-network-instead-of-gps""""""""> Q&amp;A</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Allow preferred location provider to be set
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Allow the preferred location provider to be set by the user - re: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/40741/geolocation-force-network-instead-of-gps""""""""> Q&amp;A</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1278,12,"""leftNavButton not showing up in simulator on iPhone OS 4 and sdk 1.3.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hey all, I can't get the leftNavButton to show up in modal windows after upgrading to to iPhone OS 4 and sdk 1.3.2. They worked in iPhone OS 3.2.1 and sdk 1.3.0. Possible bug?</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">// create the close button and listener for the main window var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({     title:'Close' }); // create first window and the navigation group var first = Titanium.UI.createWindow({     title: """"""""Courses"""""""",     barColor: '#005a84',     leftNavButton: button }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e) {     main.close(); });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: leftNavButton not showing up in simulator on iPhone OS 4 and sdk 1.3.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hey all, I can't get the leftNavButton to show up in modal windows after upgrading to to iPhone OS 4 and sdk 1.3.2. They worked in iPhone OS 3.2.1 and sdk 1.3.0. Possible bug?</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">// create the close button and listener for the main window var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({ title:'Close' }); // create first window and the navigation group var first = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ title: """"""""Courses"""""""", barColor: '#005a84', leftNavButton: button }); button.addEventListener('click', function(e) { main.close(); });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1277,12,"""Touchmove not tracking properly""","""""""{html}<div><p>Code similar to the following used to work fine, prior to 1.4  RC1:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/28951/to-drag-and-drop-or-not"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/28951/to-drag-and-drop-o...</a></p>  <p>The object would move with the touchmove coordinates and,  although at times a bit laggy, would move right along from the  touchstart coordinates to touchend. Now it's as if there are  multiple events being fired with varying coordinates because the  object jumps all over the screen and falls behind as you """"""""drag"""""""" the  object in a straight line from one point to another.</p>  <p>Or take a more straight-forward example like this to see how the  object tracks behind the current touch position and never catches  up:</p>  <p>//Box is a box to be dragged (I've tested with an imageview and  label with same result) box.addEventListener(""""""""touchmove"""""""",  function(e){<br></p>  <pre>  <code>   e.source.center = {x:e.x,y:e.y};</code>  </pre>  <p>});</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Touchmove not tracking properly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Code similar to the following used to work fine, prior to 1.4 RC1:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/28951/to-drag-and-drop-or-not""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/28951/to-drag-and-drop-o...</a></p> <p>The object would move with the touchmove coordinates and, although at times a bit laggy, would move right along from the touchstart coordinates to touchend. Now it's as if there are multiple events being fired with varying coordinates because the object jumps all over the screen and falls behind as you """"""""drag"""""""" the object in a straight line from one point to another.</p> <p>Or take a more straight-forward example like this to see how the object tracks behind the current touch position and never catches up:</p> <p>//Box is a box to be dragged (I've tested with an imageview and label with same result) box.addEventListener(""""""""touchmove"""""""", function(e){<br></p> <pre> <code> e.source.center = {x:e.x,y:e.y};</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1276,12,"""Going from More tab to window with right button still shows """"Edit""""""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a tab that's hidden away in the More section. When I go through to the window, which has both left and right buttons assigned, the left button replaces the arrow back to the More tab (as expected), but the right button stays as """"""""Edit"""""""" from the More tab. Pressing it does the expected action for the window, however. It is just the button's text that does not change to the correct text.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Going from More tab to window with right button still shows """"Edit""""
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have a tab that's hidden away in the More section. When I go through to the window, which has both left and right buttons assigned, the left button replaces the arrow back to the More tab (as expected), but the right button stays as """"""""Edit"""""""" from the More tab. Pressing it does the expected action for the window, however. It is just the button's text that does not change to the correct text.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1275,12,"""UtilsModule.decodeBase64 incorrectly converting back to String""","""""""{html}<div><p>Should use TiBlob.blobFromData and the decoded bytes, instead of TiBlob.blobFromString.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: UtilsModule.decodeBase64 incorrectly converting back to String
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Should use TiBlob.blobFromData and the decoded bytes, instead of TiBlob.blobFromString.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1274,12,"""Swipe doesn't change direction after orientation change""","""""""{html}<div><p>In 1.3.0, I have a window set to orientation mode LANDSCAPE_LEFT.<br> A left to right or right to left swipe triggers an event on a view in that window.</p> <p>In 1.3.2 the orientation mode bug causes the app to not switch to LANDSCAPE_LEFT.</p> <p>So I rotate the phone to change the orientation view to the correct view, but the swipe event now requires the swipe to be up to down or down to up to fire the event.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Swipe doesn't change direction after orientation change
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In 1.3.0, I have a window set to orientation mode LANDSCAPE_LEFT.<br> A left to right or right to left swipe triggers an event on a view in that window.</p> <p>In 1.3.2 the orientation mode bug causes the app to not switch to LANDSCAPE_LEFT.</p> <p>So I rotate the phone to change the orientation view to the correct view, but the swipe event now requires the swipe to be up to down or down to up to fire the event.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1273,12,"""Scrolling the table after pressing ""","""""""{html}<div><p>using kitchen sink:</p> <p>1.Base UI&gt;Views&gt;Table Views&gt;Empty Table view.<br> 2.tap """"""""append (row obj)"""""""" then tap """"""""set"""""""", followed by tapping append again. Note the presence of unexpected characters hat appear in the table row<br> 3.use your finger to scroll the table up and down until the app crashes (about 4-6) times</p> <p>attached crash log</p> <p>seen using the ipod touch, not seen on android or in the iOS emulator.</p> <p>Ugh - the title should have read """"""""scrolling the table after tapping append a second time""""""""</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Scrolling the table after pressing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>using kitchen sink:</p> <p>1.Base UI&gt;Views&gt;Table Views&gt;Empty Table view.<br> 2.tap """"""""append (row obj)"""""""" then tap """"""""set"""""""", followed by tapping append again. Note the presence of unexpected characters hat appear in the table row<br> 3.use your finger to scroll the table up and down until the app crashes (about 4-6) times</p> <p>attached crash log</p> <p>seen using the ipod touch, not seen on android or in the iOS emulator.</p> <p>Ugh - the title should have read """"""""scrolling the table after tapping append a second time""""""""</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1272,12,"""Android: ImageView does not support children""","""""""{html}<div><p>Label shows in iPhone, not in Android:</p>  <pre>  <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({    top: 0,    width: 100,    left: 0,    height: 200  });    win.add(iv);    var l = Ti.UI.createLabel({    left: 0,    top: 0,    width: 100,    height: 40,    text: 'test'  });    iv.add(l);</code>  </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView does not support children
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Label shows in iPhone, not in Android:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var iv = Ti.UI.createImageView({ top: 0, width: 100, left: 0, height: 200 }); win.add(iv); var l = Ti.UI.createLabel({ left: 0, top: 0, width: 100, height: 40, text: 'test' }); iv.add(l);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1271,12,"""Custom resources not working in latest build""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that platform resources was not picking up files in subdirectories, only top level files. I tried to reproduce this with latest from HEAD and in my test, the files in Resources/iphone were not being picked up at all.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Custom resources not working in latest build
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that platform resources was not picking up files in subdirectories, only top level files. I tried to reproduce this with latest from HEAD and in my test, the files in Resources/iphone were not being picked up at all.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
