TIMOB-1266,12,"""Split views without nav group have display problems""","""""""{html}<div><p>Run the Split View Plain test in iPad-KS, and note the layout requirements for buttons, etc. If you remove left/top/etc. boundaries on the button then there are issues; there are also issues presenting modal windows that are not present when displaying them in a navigation controller. Supersedes <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1137"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1137"""""""">#1137</a>.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Split views without nav group have display problems
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Run the Split View Plain test in iPad-KS, and note the layout requirements for buttons, etc. If you remove left/top/etc. boundaries on the button then there are issues; there are also issues presenting modal windows that are not present when displaying them in a navigation controller. Supersedes <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/1137"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #1137"""""""">#1137</a>.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1265,12,"""imageView.toBlob() returns null""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium Mobile SDK 1.3.2, the ImageView.toBlob() function returns null (was working in 1.3.0).</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">        var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({             width: 'auto',             height: 'auto'         });         imageView.addEventListener('load', function()             {                 var blob = imageView.toBlob();                 //  ^^^^ is null             });         imageView.image = pUrl;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: imageView.toBlob() returns null
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium Mobile SDK 1.3.2, the ImageView.toBlob() function returns null (was working in 1.3.0).</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript""""""""> var imageView = Ti.UI.createImageView({ width: 'auto', height: 'auto' }); imageView.addEventListener('load', function() { var blob = imageView.toBlob(); // ^^^^ is null }); imageView.image = pUrl;</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1264,12,"""Image fade in...""","""""""{html}<div><p>is there an image fade in/fade out that works on iPHONE and ANDROID?<br> if not, I suppose I can use a timer and the opacity?<br> I dont want to tackle this problem unless you have a solution that works on both platforms.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Image fade in...
Description: """"{html}<div><p>is there an image fade in/fade out that works on iPHONE and ANDROID?<br> if not, I suppose I can use a timer and the opacity?<br> I dont want to tackle this problem unless you have a solution that works on both platforms.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1263,12,"""{animated:false} not being respected on window close""","""""""{html}<div><p>see in kitchensink:<br> 1.Base UI&gt; Window (Standalone)<br> 2.Tap """"""""open tab w/o animation"""""""" and from the resulting window tap """"""""Close w/o animation""""""""</p> <p>results: window slides out (animation)<br></p> <p>the following does not seem to be respected:</p> <p>b.addEventListener('click',function()<br></p> <pre> <code>    {         w.close({animated:false});     });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: {animated:false} not being respected on window close
Description: """"{html}<div><p>see in kitchensink:<br> 1.Base UI&gt; Window (Standalone)<br> 2.Tap """"""""open tab w/o animation"""""""" and from the resulting window tap """"""""Close w/o animation""""""""</p> <p>results: window slides out (animation)<br></p> <p>the following does not seem to be respected:</p> <p>b.addEventListener('click',function()<br></p> <pre> <code> { w.close({animated:false}); });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1262,12,"""Video toolbar does not sit at the top of the window""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that the toolbar in the video player does not sit at the top of the window on OS 4. I confirmed this by running the KS movie_local.js file.</p> <p>tried on iphone os 4 running the latest from HEAD</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Video toolbar does not sit at the top of the window
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that the toolbar in the video player does not sit at the top of the window on OS 4. I confirmed this by running the KS movie_local.js file.</p> <p>tried on iphone os 4 running the latest from HEAD</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1261,12,"""Using the pinch gesture on video creates unexpected results""","""""""{html}<div><p>using kitchensink:</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;play movie&gt;local (any file will show the behavior)<br> 2.tap to go full screen (or pinch out)<br> 3.use the pinch gesture on the video<br> result:<br> the video is in letterbox<br> 4.try to get the video back to it's original view</p> <p>result: you cannot - the letter box is sticky<br> expected:be able to return to the view first shown</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Using the pinch gesture on video creates unexpected results
Description: """"{html}<div><p>using kitchensink:</p> <p>1.Phone&gt;play movie&gt;local (any file will show the behavior)<br> 2.tap to go full screen (or pinch out)<br> 3.use the pinch gesture on the video<br> result:<br> the video is in letterbox<br> 4.try to get the video back to it's original view</p> <p>result: you cannot - the letter box is sticky<br> expected:be able to return to the view first shown</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1260,12,"""InsertRowAfter & insertRowbefore do not respect the header property of createTableRow""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using the attached file (code came from the kitchen sink), if a new table row is created via insertRowAfter/Before, setting the header property is ignored. Using appendRow does honor that property though. I have run this using OS 4(iphone project) and our latest from HEAD today.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: InsertRowAfter & insertRowbefore do not respect the header property of createTableRow
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using the attached file (code came from the kitchen sink), if a new table row is created via insertRowAfter/Before, setting the header property is ignored. Using appendRow does honor that property though. I have run this using OS 4(iphone project) and our latest from HEAD today.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1259,12,"""bug on creation of module in SDK 1.3.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I post my bug in the Forum, but i think it's more usefull here.</p> <p>I want to make a new Module (like the doc <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/doc/mobile/iphone/module_sdk)"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/doc/mobile/iphone/module_sdk)</a>, and have an error message in my console with the file """"""""build.py"""""""", when i try to build the module :</p> <p>build.py"""""""", line 89<br></p> <pre> <code>for dn in ('assets','documentation','example'):                                               ^</code> </pre> <p>IndentationError: unindent does not match any outer indentation level</p> <p>Think it's a bug, in the source files generated....</p> <p>Post in the Forum for more details : <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/40431/bug-create-module-on-titanium-132""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/40431/bug-create-module-...</a></p> <p>I use Titanium 1.2.1 with SDK 1.3.2</p> <p>Note that i reinstall Titanium after trying to create module, because i had a lot of bug for buiding apps.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: bug on creation of module in SDK 1.3.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I post my bug in the Forum, but i think it's more usefull here.</p> <p>I want to make a new Module (like the doc <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/doc/mobile/iphone/module_sdk)"""""""">http://developer.<USER>com/doc/mobile/iphone/module_sdk)</a>, and have an error message in my console with the file """"""""build.py"""""""", when i try to build the module :</p> <p>build.py"""""""", line 89<br></p> <pre> <code>for dn in ('assets','documentation','example'): ^</code> </pre> <p>IndentationError: unindent does not match any outer indentation level</p> <p>Think it's a bug, in the source files generated....</p> <p>Post in the Forum for more details : <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/40431/bug-create-module-on-titanium-132""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/40431/bug-create-module-...</a></p> <p>I use Titanium 1.2.1 with SDK 1.3.2</p> <p>Note that i reinstall Titanium after trying to create module, because i had a lot of bug for buiding apps.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
