TIMOB-1230,12,"""Titanium Desktop runtime desn't work on latest ubuntu/debian (Lucid Lynx/Sid)""","""""""{html}<div><p>The gtk libraries shipped with the Titanium Desktop (1.0?) runtime installed by Titanium Developer conflict with system libraries, GTK complains about exported symbols. The temporary fix is to delete libglib <em>libgobject</em> libgthread* and so on from ~/.titanium installation. Hope for a renewed packaging so that dwployment is doable.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium Desktop runtime desn't work on latest ubuntu/debian (Lucid Lynx/Sid)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The gtk libraries shipped with the Titanium Desktop (1.0?) runtime installed by Titanium Developer conflict with system libraries, GTK complains about exported symbols. The temporary fix is to delete libglib <em>libgobject</em> libgthread* and so on from ~/.titanium installation. Hope for a renewed packaging so that dwployment is doable.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1229,12,"""App crashes when setRightNavButton is used. Confirmed in KS""","""""""{html}<div><ol> <li>Open KS<br></li> <li>Go to Base UI<br></li> <li>Choose Window NavBar<br></li> <li>Choose 'Right Nav'<br></li> <li>Click back button</li> </ol> <p>KS will then crash</p> <p>Crash log shows:<br></p> <pre> <code>Exception Type:  EXC_BAD_INSTRUCTION (SIGILL) Exception Codes: 0x0000000000000001, 0x0000000000000000 Crashed Thread:  0  Dispatch queue: com.apple.main-thread<br> <br>   <br> Application Specific Information: iPhone Simulator 3.2 (193.8), iPhone OS 3.1.2 (iPhone/7D11) objc[17661]: FREED(id): message respondsToSelector: sent to freed object=0x5167df0</code> </pre> <p>This is holding me up somewhat! ;)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: App crashes when setRightNavButton is used. Confirmed in KS
Description: """"{html}<div><ol> <li>Open KS<br></li> <li>Go to Base UI<br></li> <li>Choose Window NavBar<br></li> <li>Choose 'Right Nav'<br></li> <li>Click back button</li> </ol> <p>KS will then crash</p> <p>Crash log shows:<br></p> <pre> <code>Exception Type: EXC_BAD_INSTRUCTION (SIGILL) Exception Codes: 0x0000000000000001, 0x0000000000000000 Crashed Thread: 0 Dispatch queue: com.apple.main-thread<br> <br> <br> Application Specific Information: iPhone Simulator 3.2 (193.8), iPhone OS 3.1.2 (iPhone/7D11) objc[17661]: FREED(id): message respondsToSelector: sent to freed object=0x5167df0</code> </pre> <p>This is holding me up somewhat! ;)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1228,12,"""ImageView will not resize on orientation change on iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that an image view would not dynamically resize on an orientation change. I have verified that this does not work on the iPad running 3.2 but does work on an iphone running os4 (simulator).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ImageView will not resize on orientation change on iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that an image view would not dynamically resize on an orientation change. I have verified that this does not work on the iPad running 3.2 but does work on an iphone running os4 (simulator).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1227,12,"""iPhone: fix crash in multiple alerts""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you call multiple alerts from different JS contexts (or the same) the app will crash. Also, alert should be synchronous like the browser and not async.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: fix crash in multiple alerts
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you call multiple alerts from different JS contexts (or the same) the app will crash. Also, alert should be synchronous like the browser and not async.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1226,12,"""TiAPI: Two Finger - Move,Pinch, Zoom and Rotate Touch Events on Views""","""""""{html}<div><p>Move, Pinch, Zoom and Rotate Touch Events on Views are  missing.</p>  <p>Please implement it.</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://stackoverflow.com/questions/1303030/two-finger-rotation-gesture-on-the-iphone"""""""">  http://stackoverflow.com/questions/1303030/two-finger-rotation-gest...</a></p>  <p>A possible solution is change twofingertap event.<br>  Now twofingertap returns only 1 point, if it would return 2 points  then is possible get the rotation, distance, etc.</p>  <p>Thanks.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Two Finger - Move,Pinch, Zoom and Rotate Touch Events on Views
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Move, Pinch, Zoom and Rotate Touch Events on Views are missing.</p> <p>Please implement it.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://stackoverflow.com/questions/1303030/two-finger-rotation-gesture-on-the-iphone""""""""> http://stackoverflow.com/questions/1303030/two-finger-rotation-gest...</a></p> <p>A possible solution is change twofingertap event.<br> Now twofingertap returns only 1 point, if it would return 2 points then is possible get the rotation, distance, etc.</p> <p>Thanks.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1225,12,"""horizontal layout doesn't work in Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>Horizontal layout doesn't work on Android. It is very difficult to put labels next to each other without horizontal layout.</p> <p>For the following code the two labels are right on top of each other in the center of the view.<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var view= Ti.UI.createView({ width: 'auto', layout: 'horizontal' }); view.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'foo' })); view.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'bar' }));</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: horizontal layout doesn't work in Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Horizontal layout doesn't work on Android. It is very difficult to put labels next to each other without horizontal layout.</p> <p>For the following code the two labels are right on top of each other in the center of the view.<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var view= Ti.UI.createView({ width: 'auto', layout: 'horizontal' }); view.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'foo' })); view.add(Ti.UI.createLabel({ text: 'bar' }));</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1224,12,"""createCoverFlowView's images array does not accept remote Images. ""","""""""{html}<div><p>The following does not work, it gives an error.</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var imagesCoverflow = [];</p> <p>imagesCoverflow.push('<a href= """"""""http://www.mnit.ac.in/literary09/1.png')"""""""">http://www.mnit.ac.in/literary09/1.png')</a>;<br> imagesCoverflow.push('<a href= """"""""http://www.moviemeads.com/videos/2.png')"""""""">http://www.moviemeads.com/videos/2.png')</a>;</p> <p>var coverflowView = Titanium.UI.createCoverFlowView({<br></p> <pre> <code>images:imagesCoverflow, backgroundColor:'transparent'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(coverflowView);</p> <p>win.open();</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: createCoverFlowView's images array does not accept remote Images.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The following does not work, it gives an error.</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var imagesCoverflow = [];</p> <p>imagesCoverflow.push('<a href= """"""""http://www.mnit.ac.in/literary09/1.png')"""""""">http://www.mnit.ac.in/literary09/1.png')</a>;<br> imagesCoverflow.push('<a href= """"""""http://www.moviemeads.com/videos/2.png')"""""""">http://www.moviemeads.com/videos/2.png')</a>;</p> <p>var coverflowView = Titanium.UI.createCoverFlowView({<br></p> <pre> <code>images:imagesCoverflow, backgroundColor:'transparent'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(coverflowView);</p> <p>win.open();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1223,12,"""Dynamic properties not carried across contexts""","""""""{html}<div><p>By """"""""dynamic properties"""""""" here we mean """"""""unofficial"""""""" (unregistered) properties, such as if a developer just sets a property in JS on one of our proxies, like:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); win.secret = """"""""my secret message"""""""";</code> </pre> <p>""""""""secret"""""""" is not a registered property of WindowProxy. In Android/BB, we handle the assignment by passing it on to the scriptable -- we don't give it to the proxy. Later, if the proxy is wrapped again into a different KrollObject, and code tries to get the property value, it will fail.</p> <p>This happens with currentWindow, for example, when a new context is created for a window and then Ti.UI.currentWindow is set to a wrapped instance of that window proxy. Here's a complete fail case example:</p> <p>File: app.js<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">// .... var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({url:'win1.js'}); win.secret = """"""""My secret message""""""""; Ti.API.info(win.secret); // ok -- .secret is on the scriptable win.open(); // causes new context win1.js</code> </pre> <p>File: win1.js<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; Ti.API.info(win.secret); // fails -- currentWindow is different scriptable than win was in previous context</code> </pre> <p>In our iPhone/iPad implementation, these unregistered properties are put right into the proxy's (target's) dynprops collection and are therefore available even if the proxy gets wrapped into a different scriptable.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Dynamic properties not carried across contexts
Description: """"{html}<div><p>By """"""""dynamic properties"""""""" here we mean """"""""unofficial"""""""" (unregistered) properties, such as if a developer just sets a property in JS on one of our proxies, like:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); win.secret = """"""""my secret message"""""""";</code> </pre> <p>""""""""secret"""""""" is not a registered property of WindowProxy. In Android/BB, we handle the assignment by passing it on to the scriptable -- we don't give it to the proxy. Later, if the proxy is wrapped again into a different KrollObject, and code tries to get the property value, it will fail.</p> <p>This happens with currentWindow, for example, when a new context is created for a window and then Ti.UI.currentWindow is set to a wrapped instance of that window proxy. Here's a complete fail case example:</p> <p>File: app.js<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">// .... var win = Ti.UI.createWindow({url:'win1.js'}); win.secret = """"""""My secret message""""""""; Ti.API.info(win.secret); // ok -- .secret is on the scriptable win.open(); // causes new context win1.js</code> </pre> <p>File: win1.js<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var win = Ti.UI.currentWindow; Ti.API.info(win.secret); // fails -- currentWindow is different scriptable than win was in previous context</code> </pre> <p>In our iPhone/iPad implementation, these unregistered properties are put right into the proxy's (target's) dynprops collection and are therefore available even if the proxy gets wrapped into a different scriptable.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1222,12,"""Row headers are being pushed down when there is a table header view. ""","""""""{html}<div><p>When you set a header view to the table and then set headers to table rows, the rows are pushed down leaving extra space depending on how big the headerview was.</p> <p>I attached screenshots to demo the issue. Notice how the first one with the headerview has a lot of space before the row header starts. In the second one, the headerview removed from the tableview, the extra space is gone. It seems like the headerview height is being copied over to each rowheader somehow.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Row headers are being pushed down when there is a table header view.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When you set a header view to the table and then set headers to table rows, the rows are pushed down leaving extra space depending on how big the headerview was.</p> <p>I attached screenshots to demo the issue. Notice how the first one with the headerview has a lot of space before the row header starts. In the second one, the headerview removed from the tableview, the extra space is gone. It seems like the headerview height is being copied over to each rowheader somehow.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1221,12,"""Add in landscape/fullscreen video player support""","""""""{html}<div><p>With the movie player changes in 3.2, we removed support for landscape/fullscreen video players in the """"""""old style."""""""" There is specifically a new Cocoa Touch class to emulate the old behavior; we should add in an option to make them.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Add in landscape/fullscreen video player support
Description: """"{html}<div><p>With the movie player changes in 3.2, we removed support for landscape/fullscreen video players in the """"""""old style."""""""" There is specifically a new Cocoa Touch class to emulate the old behavior; we should add in an option to make them.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
