Description: """"{html}<div><p>KS -&gt; Base UI -&gt; Views -&gt; Scrollable View -&gt; w/o clipping</p> <p>The test does not render the view correctly.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1219,12,"""Android: setOrientation regression""","""""""{html}<div><p>In between 1.3.0 and 1.3.2 being able to force orientation on Android was broken.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: setOrientation regression
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In between 1.3.0 and 1.3.2 being able to force orientation on Android was broken.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1218,12,"""Ti/Titanium in webviews""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have the following codes:</p> <p>app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var w = Ti.UI.createWindow(); Ti.App.addEventListener('testEvent', function(e) {     Ti.Api.info('testEvent'); }); wv = Ti.UI.createWebView({     html: '&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;script type=""""""""text/javascript"""""""" src=""""""""/local.js""""""""&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;a id=""""""""t"""""""" onclick=""""""""webFunc();"""""""" href=""""""""#"""""""" &gt;click&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/body&gt;' }); w.add(wv); w.open();</code> </pre> <p>local.js:<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">function webFunc(){ document.getElementById('t').innerHTML = 'click2'; Titanium.App.fireEvent('testEvent'); }</code> </pre> <p>TestEvent will never occur, while the link is become 'click2'.</p> <p>This technique worked in 1.2.0 maybe 1.3.0 (I can't test it now).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti/Titanium in webviews
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have the following codes:</p> <p>app.js:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var w = Ti.UI.createWindow(); Ti.App.addEventListener('testEvent', function(e) { Ti.Api.info('testEvent'); }); wv = Ti.UI.createWebView({ html: '&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;script type=""""""""text/javascript"""""""" src=""""""""/local.js""""""""&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;a id=""""""""t"""""""" onclick=""""""""webFunc();"""""""" href=""""""""#"""""""" &gt;click&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/body&gt;' }); w.add(wv); w.open();</code> </pre> <p>local.js:<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">function webFunc(){ document.getElementById('t').innerHTML = 'click2'; Titanium.App.fireEvent('testEvent'); }</code> </pre> <p>TestEvent will never occur, while the link is become 'click2'.</p> <p>This technique worked in 1.2.0 maybe 1.3.0 (I can't test it now).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1217,12,"""Button style properties""","""""""{html}<div><p>The following code seems not to work on buttons - are people supposed to be able to set the backgroundColor, etc. style properties on buttons?</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1024079"""""""">http://pastie.org/1024079</a></p> <p>Screenshot:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://skitch.com/<USER>dkcx7/iphone-simulator"""""""">http://skitch.com/<USER>dkcx7/iphone-simulator</a></p> <p>If not, erroneous properties should be removed from the docs:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.Button-object.html""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI....</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Button style properties
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The following code seems not to work on buttons - are people supposed to be able to set the backgroundColor, etc. style properties on buttons?</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/1024079"""""""">http://pastie.org/1024079</a></p> <p>Screenshot:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://skitch.com/<USER>dkcx7/iphone-simulator"""""""">http://skitch.com/<USER>dkcx7/iphone-simulator</a></p> <p>If not, erroneous properties should be removed from the docs:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI.Button-object.html""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/apidoc/mobile/latest/Titanium.UI....</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1216,12,"""Open a modal window inside of a modal causes the parent modal to be non responsive .""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you open a modal window from a modal window, and once the sub-modal window is closed, the parent modal window doesn't response to any clicks.</p> <p>Attached sample app.js. Click on the button to open modal window and another button to open the sub modal window. Then close the sub modal window and try to click the button again, it's unclickable.</p> <p>iPhone 4.0 sdk (had this same problem with 3.1.3) with the latest build from head.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Open a modal window inside of a modal causes the parent modal to be non responsive .
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you open a modal window from a modal window, and once the sub-modal window is closed, the parent modal window doesn't response to any clicks.</p> <p>Attached sample app.js. Click on the button to open modal window and another button to open the sub modal window. Then close the sub modal window and try to click the button again, it's unclickable.</p> <p>iPhone 4.0 sdk (had this same problem with 3.1.3) with the latest build from head.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1215,12,"""Ti.UI.TableView.data.length returns the original no of rows in table, rather than *current* number of rows""","""""""{html}<div><p>Platform: Android, emulator, Ti 1.3.2</p> <p>Ti.UI.TableView.data.length returns the original no of rows in table, rather than <em>current</em> number of rows</p> <p>A good example of this problem is in the KitchenSink at <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>KitchenSink/blob/master/KitchenSink/Resources/examples/table_view_row_delete.js""""""""> table_view_row_delete.js</a> which results in an exception after row 5 is deleted, because tableview.data.length-1 on line 52 always returns 4 (and after row 5 is deleted, id 4 no longer exists).</p> <p>Inserting this code at line 49 and opening the delete row page will make the problem clear:</p> <p>Ti.API.info(' <em>* * * * * * * * * * * *</em> ');<br> Ti.API.info(typeof(tableview));<br> Ti.API.info(typeof(tableview.data));<br> Ti.API.info(typeof(tableview.data.length));<br> Ti.API.info('Number of table rows: '+tableview.data.length);<br> tableview.deleteRow(tableview.data.length-1);<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""deleting row"""""""");<br> Ti.API.info('Number of table rows: '+tableview.data.length);<br> Ti.API.info(' <em>* * * * * * * * * * * *</em> ');</p> <p>Incidentally, another issue that may be related is that getData() does not work currently, demonstrated by Ti.API.info('getData type: '+typeof(tableview.getData())); producing an exception.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.UI.TableView.data.length returns the original no of rows in table, rather than *current* number of rows
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Platform: Android, emulator, Ti 1.3.2</p> <p>Ti.UI.TableView.data.length returns the original no of rows in table, rather than <em>current</em> number of rows</p> <p>A good example of this problem is in the KitchenSink at <a href= """"""""http://github.com/<USER>KitchenSink/blob/master/KitchenSink/Resources/examples/table_view_row_delete.js""""""""> table_view_row_delete.js</a> which results in an exception after row 5 is deleted, because tableview.data.length-1 on line 52 always returns 4 (and after row 5 is deleted, id 4 no longer exists).</p> <p>Inserting this code at line 49 and opening the delete row page will make the problem clear:</p> <p>Ti.API.info(' <em>* * * * * * * * * * * *</em> ');<br> Ti.API.info(typeof(tableview));<br> Ti.API.info(typeof(tableview.data));<br> Ti.API.info(typeof(tableview.data.length));<br> Ti.API.info('Number of table rows: '+tableview.data.length);<br> tableview.deleteRow(tableview.data.length-1);<br> Ti.API.info(""""""""deleting row"""""""");<br> Ti.API.info('Number of table rows: '+tableview.data.length);<br> Ti.API.info(' <em>* * * * * * * * * * * *</em> ');</p> <p>Incidentally, another issue that may be related is that getData() does not work currently, demonstrated by Ti.API.info('getData type: '+typeof(tableview.getData())); producing an exception.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1214,12,"""Android: Tableview row content right edge depends on indicator""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is a special case for layout. If the indicator is present, it reduces the size of the content region. If it's not present the content region is assumed to be the true right edge.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Tableview row content right edge depends on indicator
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is a special case for layout. If the indicator is present, it reduces the size of the content region. If it's not present the content region is assumed to be the true right edge.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
