TIMOB-1203,12,"""setTimeout Android Issue""","""""""{html}<div><p>The following usecase demonstrates that setTimeout() periods of 1000ms complete successfully for this specific code, whereas those with 3000ms periods do not run.<br></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastebin.com/raw.php?i=4Fzdx1qG"""""""">http://pastebin.com/raw.php?i=4Fzdx1qG</a><br></p> <p>I speculate that the reason for this is the script has completed execution within the 3000ms timeout period, causing the timeout to be disregarded. Conversely, 1000ms is long enough for the command/function inside setTimeout() to fire before the script finishes.<br></p> <p>Please do not rely on my previous assumptions of tabGroups being the cause of the issue. Also, opening a window is not a reliable workaround - it may have seemed to resolve the issue in some cases, but I think this was simply due to the fact that doing so extended the script execution time long enough for setTimeout to complete.</p> <p>Please note that investigation into the true cause of this issue is required - the script execution idea I stated above is just a theory.</p> <p>Please also note <USER>s ticket <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3083"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3083"""""""">#3083</a> regarding setTimeout, which may possibly be relevant.</p> <p>Original poster noted that the setTimeout timer keeps on ticking away, as evident from the trace.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: setTimeout Android Issue
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The following usecase demonstrates that setTimeout() periods of 1000ms complete successfully for this specific code, whereas those with 3000ms periods do not run.<br></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastebin.com/raw.php?i=4Fzdx1qG"""""""">http://pastebin.com/raw.php?i=4Fzdx1qG</a><br></p> <p>I speculate that the reason for this is the script has completed execution within the 3000ms timeout period, causing the timeout to be disregarded. Conversely, 1000ms is long enough for the command/function inside setTimeout() to fire before the script finishes.<br></p> <p>Please do not rely on my previous assumptions of tabGroups being the cause of the issue. Also, opening a window is not a reliable workaround - it may have seemed to resolve the issue in some cases, but I think this was simply due to the fact that doing so extended the script execution time long enough for setTimeout to complete.</p> <p>Please note that investigation into the true cause of this issue is required - the script execution idea I stated above is just a theory.</p> <p>Please also note <USER>s ticket <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/3083"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #3083"""""""">#3083</a> regarding setTimeout, which may possibly be relevant.</p> <p>Original poster noted that the setTimeout timer keeps on ticking away, as evident from the trace.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1202,12,"""Image View breaks if borderWidth and defaultImage used together is sdk 4 ""","""""""{html}<div><p>a customer submitted code that when run against sdk 4 and borderWidth &amp; defaultImage is used the imageView fails to render images. I am attaching the sample project that shows this. I tried this against iphone sdk 3.1.x and it works so it seems sdk 4 broke/changed something.</p> <p>helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3447"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3447</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Image View breaks if borderWidth and defaultImage used together is sdk 4
