TIMOB-1195,12,"""Ability to create Safari like navbar with multiple buttons""","""""""{html}<div><p>Right now, can only add 1 button to the left and right. Or add a buttonBar, but this doesn't look very good.</p> <p>I think supporting the ability to add multiple buttons to the navbar, like in Safari, is a must, when you support iPad.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ability to create Safari like navbar with multiple buttons
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Right now, can only add 1 button to the left and right. Or add a buttonBar, but this doesn't look very good.</p> <p>I think supporting the ability to add multiple buttons to the navbar, like in Safari, is a must, when you support iPad.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1194,12,"""Android: minRowHeight not respected everywhere (TableViewProxy)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Changes in <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1094"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1094"""""""">#1094</a> only fix the row height problem if the row has already been added to a view (i.e., getParent() is not null). We need to work out all other scenarios, including:</p> <ul> <li> <p>What to do if the property is changed in the parent (TableViewProxy) -- trickle down to child rows.</p> </li> <li> <p>Handle in other spots in code: update, append, set, layout, etc.</p> </li> </ul></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: minRowHeight not respected everywhere (TableViewProxy)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Changes in <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1094"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1094"""""""">#1094</a> only fix the row height problem if the row has already been added to a view (i.e., getParent() is not null). We need to work out all other scenarios, including:</p> <ul> <li> <p>What to do if the property is changed in the parent (TableViewProxy) -- trickle down to child rows.</p> </li> <li> <p>Handle in other spots in code: update, append, set, layout, etc.</p> </li> </ul></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1193,12,"""Corrupted Table rows with different layouts and no class names""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you have enough rows to scroll a table view, and one or more of the rows are different than the rest, those rows will cause redrawing issues because of incorrectly returned """"""""convertViews"""""""" from TiTableView.getView()</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Corrupted Table rows with different layouts and no class names
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you have enough rows to scroll a table view, and one or more of the rows are different than the rest, those rows will cause redrawing issues because of incorrectly returned """"""""convertViews"""""""" from TiTableView.getView()</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1192,12,"""Slider does not honor a set value at creation 1.3.2 & sdk 4""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that when a slider's value was set to a decimal, ie 1.5, the slider was not honoring that value. Here is what I found. If the value of the slider was set to anything below 1, it was honored. Anytime the value was set to higher than 1, the slider always reported 1. A work around I found is that using a setTimeout at 100ms to set the value works.</p> <p>see this helpdesk ticket.<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3437"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3437</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Slider does not honor a set value at creation 1.3.2 & sdk 4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that when a slider's value was set to a decimal, ie 1.5, the slider was not honoring that value. Here is what I found. If the value of the slider was set to anything below 1, it was honored. Anytime the value was set to higher than 1, the slider always reported 1. A work around I found is that using a setTimeout at 100ms to set the value works.</p> <p>see this helpdesk ticket.<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3437"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3437</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1191,12,"""single row grouped view has squared bottom image on select""","""""""{html}<div><p>self explanatory</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: single row grouped view has squared bottom image on select
Description: """"{html}<div><p>self explanatory</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1190,12,"""Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton crash""","""""""{html}<div><p>When I use a SystemButtom on iPhone and want to enable/disable it, the application will crash. The crash depends on the type of the SystemButton.</p> <p>The buttons I've tested and cause crash:<br> SPINNER, CONTACT_ADD, DISCLOSURE, INFO_DARK, INFO_LIGHT (the newer buttons in the TiUISystemButtonProxy.h)</p> <p>The code to test:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup();  var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({}); var btnAdd = Ti.UI.createButton({     systemButton: Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.CONTACT_ADD,     enabled: false }); w.setRightNavButton(btnAdd);  tabTest = Ti.UI.createTab({     title:'Test',     window: w }); tabGroup.addTab(tabTest);  tabGroup.open({transition:Titanium.UI.iPhone.AnimationStyle.FLIP_FROM_LEFT});  setTimeout(function(){     btnAdd.enabled = true; }, 3000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When I use a SystemButtom on iPhone and want to enable/disable it, the application will crash. The crash depends on the type of the SystemButton.</p> <p>The buttons I've tested and cause crash:<br> SPINNER, CONTACT_ADD, DISCLOSURE, INFO_DARK, INFO_LIGHT (the newer buttons in the TiUISystemButtonProxy.h)</p> <p>The code to test:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var tabGroup = Ti.UI.createTabGroup(); var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({}); var btnAdd = Ti.UI.createButton({ systemButton: Ti.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.CONTACT_ADD, enabled: false }); w.setRightNavButton(btnAdd); tabTest = Ti.UI.createTab({ title:'Test', window: w }); tabGroup.addTab(tabTest); tabGroup.open({transition:Titanium.UI.iPhone.AnimationStyle.FLIP_FROM_LEFT}); setTimeout(function(){ btnAdd.enabled = true; }, 3000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1189,12,"""memory issue with image view causes crash""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2983"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2983</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: memory issue with image view causes crash
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2983"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2983</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1188,12,"""Ti.Map.createView region property problem""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>When I create a map, and set the region, the latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta properties are interpreted wrong. After the view was added to the window, the same region object works good.</p> <p>I use the latest 1.3.2 from git.</p> <p>An example:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({});  var startRegion = {""""""""longitude"""""""":19.01759147644043,""""""""latitude"""""""":47.46166758068304,""""""""longitudeDelta"""""""":0.0274658203125,""""""""latitudeDelta"""""""":0.01990384287526581};  var mapview = Ti.Map.createView({     mapType: Ti.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,     region: startRegion,     animate: true,     regionFit: true,     userLocation: false });  w.add(mapview); w.open();  setTimeout(function() {     mapview.region = startRegion; }, 2000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Ti.Map.createView region property problem
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>When I create a map, and set the region, the latitudeDelta and longitudeDelta properties are interpreted wrong. After the view was added to the window, the same region object works good.</p> <p>I use the latest 1.3.2 from git.</p> <p>An example:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">var w = Ti.UI.createWindow({}); var startRegion = {""""""""longitude"""""""":19.01759147644043,""""""""latitude"""""""":47.46166758068304,""""""""longitudeDelta"""""""":0.0274658203125,""""""""latitudeDelta"""""""":0.01990384287526581}; var mapview = Ti.Map.createView({ mapType: Ti.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, region: startRegion, animate: true, regionFit: true, userLocation: false }); w.add(mapview); w.open(); setTimeout(function() { mapview.region = startRegion; }, 2000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1187,12,"""Selected state for tableView with single row has square corners on bottom""","""""""{html}<div><p>Related to ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/433"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #433"""""""">#433</a>, mobileSDK 1.3.2, iOS 4</p> <p>When you have a tableView with one row (or a tableview where the first row is separated from the second row by a Header) the selected state only has curves on the top of the row, while the bottom of the row is square. Looking at the fix for 433, my guess is that you need a 4th state (TiCellBackgroundViewPositionSingle perhaps) with curved top and bottom.</p> <p>screenshot one (single_row.png) is a tableView with a single row<br> screenshot two (multi_rows.png) is a tableView where the second row has a blank header to achieve the separation</p> <hr> <pre> <code>// create table view data object var data = [     {title:'Score Game', hasChild:true, test:'score.js', header:'Header text',         leftImage: 'images/13-target.png'},     {title:'Settings', hasChild:true, test:'../examples/table_view_perf.js', header:'',         leftImage: 'images/20-gear2.png'},     {title:'Help', hasChild:true, test:'../examples/table_view_perf.js',         leftImage: 'images/90-lifebuoy.png'},     {title:'Cornhole Rules', hasChild:true, url:'rules.html',         leftImage: 'images/96-book.png'} ];</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Selected state for tableView with single row has square corners on bottom
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Related to ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/433"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #433"""""""">#433</a>, mobileSDK 1.3.2, iOS 4</p> <p>When you have a tableView with one row (or a tableview where the first row is separated from the second row by a Header) the selected state only has curves on the top of the row, while the bottom of the row is square. Looking at the fix for 433, my guess is that you need a 4th state (TiCellBackgroundViewPositionSingle perhaps) with curved top and bottom.</p> <p>screenshot one (single_row.png) is a tableView with a single row<br> screenshot two (multi_rows.png) is a tableView where the second row has a blank header to achieve the separation</p> <hr> <pre> <code>// create table view data object var data = [ {title:'Score Game', hasChild:true, test:'score.js', header:'Header text', leftImage: 'images/13-target.png'}, {title:'Settings', hasChild:true, test:'../examples/table_view_perf.js', header:'', leftImage: 'images/20-gear2.png'}, {title:'Help', hasChild:true, test:'../examples/table_view_perf.js', leftImage: 'images/90-lifebuoy.png'}, {title:'Cornhole Rules', hasChild:true, url:'rules.html', leftImage: 'images/96-book.png'} ];</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1186,12,"""Image View rendering is jacked [REGRESSION ISSUE]""","""""""{html}<div><p>on 3.1.x run the following:</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();<br> var imageView = Titanium.UI.createImageView({<br> image: '<a href= """"""""http://www.findlawactivitytracker.com/charts/display?image=contactSummary-92505-200904-201003'"""""""">http://www.findlawactivitytracker.com/charts/display?image=contactS...</a>,<br> top: 0,<br> left: 0,<br> width: 300,<br> height: 'auto'<br> }); win.add(imageView);<br> win.open()</p> <p>image view is not position correctly</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Image View rendering is jacked [REGRESSION ISSUE]
Description: """"{html}<div><p>on 3.1.x run the following:</p> <p>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();<br> var imageView = Titanium.UI.createImageView({<br> image: '<a href= """"""""http://www.findlawactivitytracker.com/charts/display?image=contactSummary-92505-200904-201003'"""""""">http://www.findlawactivitytracker.com/charts/display?image=contactS...</a>,<br> top: 0,<br> left: 0,<br> width: 300,<br> height: 'auto'<br> }); win.add(imageView);<br> win.open()</p> <p>image view is not position correctly</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1185,12,"""expose UIScreen so iPad applications can support the VGA adapter""","""""""{html}<div><p>I would like my iPad application to support displaying content to an external device using Apple's VGA adapter. It would be great if Titanium Mobile exposed UIScreen to make this easy.</p> <p>See the section on """"""""Support for External Displays and Projectors"""""""" at <a href= """"""""http://developer.apple.com/iphone/library/documentation/General/Conceptual/iPadProgrammingGuide/AboutThePlatform/AboutThePlatform.html""""""""> http://developer.apple.com/iphone/library/documentation/General/Con...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: expose UIScreen so iPad applications can support the VGA adapter
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I would like my iPad application to support displaying content to an external device using Apple's VGA adapter. It would be great if Titanium Mobile exposed UIScreen to make this easy.</p> <p>See the section on """"""""Support for External Displays and Projectors"""""""" at <a href= """"""""http://developer.apple.com/iphone/library/documentation/General/Conceptual/iPadProgrammingGuide/AboutThePlatform/AboutThePlatform.html""""""""> http://developer.apple.com/iphone/library/documentation/General/Con...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1184,12,"""Android: Option menu no longer works with tabbed windows in 1.3.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3365"""""""">Helpdesk Item 3365</a> test code attached. The test worked when built with 1.3.0, failed on 1.3.2.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Option menu no longer works with tabbed windows in 1.3.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3365"""""""">Helpdesk Item 3365</a> test code attached. The test worked when built with 1.3.0, failed on 1.3.2.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1183,12,"""Android: swipe events no longer detected""","""""""{html}<div><p>The fix for <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/945"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #945"""""""">#945</a>, removing the glass pane, exposed an problem with swipe events not being detected at all.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: swipe events no longer detected
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The fix for <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/945"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #945"""""""">#945</a>, removing the glass pane, exposed an problem with swipe events not being detected at all.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1181,12,"""Images using Ti.UI.createImageView vs Ti.UI.createWebView""","""""""{html}<div><p>I'm trying to use Ti.UI.createWebView to display text and images in a tab. The text and HTML formatting works fine but the image resolves as 404/broken image. Attached is a screenshot of it running in simulator.</p> <p>If the image is called using Ti.Ui.createImageView then the image does show but the developer is then dependent on absolute positioning as opposed to relative positioning which (relative positioning) is ideal.</p> <p>Also attached is a quick and dirty example project.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Images using Ti.UI.createImageView vs Ti.UI.createWebView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I'm trying to use Ti.UI.createWebView to display text and images in a tab. The text and HTML formatting works fine but the image resolves as 404/broken image. Attached is a screenshot of it running in simulator.</p> <p>If the image is called using Ti.Ui.createImageView then the image does show but the developer is then dependent on absolute positioning as opposed to relative positioning which (relative positioning) is ideal.</p> <p>Also attached is a quick and dirty example project.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1180,12,"""Recording audio crashes on 3GS device (but not in emulator!) under iOS 4.0 Ti 1.3.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have the below code to allow the user to press a button and record (other buttons etc to playback of course). The code is pretty much taken straight from KS and works perfectly in the emulator and on a pre- iOS 4.0 device. In the app, I tap the record button, app sits for a second and then crashes back to Springboard. I'm not 100% the crash is happening in the record, but I get no response from the app between the tapping of the record button and the crash.<br> And again, it works fine in the emulator. Any ideas? Thanks in advance!</p> <pre> <code>// create record button var buttonRecord = Ti.UI.createButton ({     backgroundImage:'../images/record.png',     width:50,     height:60,     left:107,     top:4 }); buttonRecord.addEventListener( 'click', function() {     if ( recording.recording )     {         file = recording.stop();         buttonRecord.backgroundImage = '../images/record.png';         buttonPlay.enabled = true;     }     else     {         buttonRecord.backgroundImage = '../images/stop.png';         recording.start();         buttonPlay.enabled = false;     } }); buttonView.add( buttonRecord );</code> </pre> <p>If I comment out """"""""recording.start();"""""""" there are (of course) no crashes.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Recording audio crashes on 3GS device (but not in emulator!) under iOS 4.0 Ti 1.3.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have the below code to allow the user to press a button and record (other buttons etc to playback of course). The code is pretty much taken straight from KS and works perfectly in the emulator and on a pre- iOS 4.0 device. In the app, I tap the record button, app sits for a second and then crashes back to Springboard. I'm not 100% the crash is happening in the record, but I get no response from the app between the tapping of the record button and the crash.<br> And again, it works fine in the emulator. Any ideas? Thanks in advance!</p> <pre> <code>// create record button var buttonRecord = Ti.UI.createButton ({ backgroundImage:'../images/record.png', width:50, height:60, left:107, top:4 }); buttonRecord.addEventListener( 'click', function() { if ( recording.recording ) { file = recording.stop(); buttonRecord.backgroundImage = '../images/record.png'; buttonPlay.enabled = true; } else { buttonRecord.backgroundImage = '../images/stop.png'; recording.start(); buttonPlay.enabled = false; } }); buttonView.add( buttonRecord );</code> </pre> <p>If I comment out """"""""recording.start();"""""""" there are (of course) no crashes.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1179,12,"""test""","""""""{html}<div><p>test</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: test
Description: """"{html}<div><p>test</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1178,12,"""Android: Online check results in NPE""","""""""{html}<div><p>There is a race condition where checking online state was can be called before the Activity used to get the ConnectionManager is available. Since a specific Context is not required to look up the service. Use the Application as the Context instead of the Activity.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Online check results in NPE
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There is a race condition where checking online state was can be called before the Activity used to get the ConnectionManager is available. Since a specific Context is not required to look up the service. Use the Application as the Context instead of the Activity.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1177,12,"""iOS: Device resource folder not working in simulator""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using 1.3.1, resources contained in the device specific  directory do not copy to the resources folder. However, they do  when deployed to the actual device.</p>  <p>For example, for 'logo.png' in the iphone directory: when  launched in the simulator, it fails to load, but when launched on  the device, it is successful.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Device resource folder not working in simulator
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using 1.3.1, resources contained in the device specific directory do not copy to the resources folder. However, they do when deployed to the actual device.</p> <p>For example, for 'logo.png' in the iphone directory: when launched in the simulator, it fails to load, but when launched on the device, it is successful.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1176,12,"""Percentage widths and heights don't work""","""""""{html}<div><p>On the off chance that a fix for this can be included in the 1.4 release, and as it's sucha blocker for me, I raise it here.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/36791/percentage-width-and-height-dont-work""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/36791/percentage-width-a...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Percentage widths and heights don't work
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On the off chance that a fix for this can be included in the 1.4 release, and as it's sucha blocker for me, I raise it here.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/36791/percentage-width-and-height-dont-work""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/36791/percentage-width-a...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1175,12,"""CoverFlowView remote images failing""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a coverflow view in an iPhone app populated with remote images from a flickr YQL query, with the 1.3.2 API's the images fail to load altogether, the following errors are shown in the log:</p> <p><a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Couldn't load coverflow image url: <a href= """"""""http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4071/4660464890_a3b94f286c_m.jpg"""""""">http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4071/4660464890_a3b94f286c_m.jpg</a> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Couldn't load coverflow image url: <a href= """"""""http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4008/4659841639_73040c1030_m.jpg"""""""">http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4008/4659841639_73040c1030_m.jpg</a> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Couldn't load coverflow image url: <a href= """"""""http://farm2.static.flickr.com/1269/4659840991_b30865090e_m.jpg"""""""">http://farm2.static.flickr.com/1269/4659840991_b30865090e_m.jpg</a> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Couldn't load coverflow image url: <a href= """"""""http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4025/4660461598_d7da6ea5a1_m.jpg"""""""">http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4025/4660461598_d7da6ea5a1_m.jpg</a> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Couldn't load coverflow image url: <a href= """"""""http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4031/4660460410_eeb6187d60_m.jpg"""""""">http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4031/4660460410_eeb6187d60_m.jpg</a> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Couldn't load coverflow image url: <a href= """"""""http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4002/4659835939_337e82ddeb_m.jpg"""""""">http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4002/4659835939_337e82ddeb_m.jpg</a> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> Couldn't load coverflow image url: <a href= """"""""http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4061/4659835365_d454f887b7_m.jpg"""""""">http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4061/4659835365_d454f887b7_m.jpg</a></p> <p>The app works fine under 1.3.0 and is published to the app store as such, the relevant code for generating the coverflowview is as follows (Snipped):</p> <p>Titanium.Yahoo.yql('select * from flickr.photos.search('+flickrlimit+') where user_id=""""""""'+flickruser+'""""""""',function(e)<br></p> <pre> <code>{      var data = e.data;      for (var c=0;c&lt;data.photo.length;c++)     {         var photo = data.photo[c];         // form the flickr url         var url = 'http://farm' + photo.farm + '.static.flickr.com/' + photo.server + '/' + photo.id + '_' + photo.secret + '_m.jpg';         images[c] = url;     }      //create coverflow view with images     var view = Titanium.UI.createCoverFlowView({         images:images,         backgroundColor:'#000'     });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: CoverFlowView remote images failing
