TIMOB-1147,12,"""TableView style=Grouped is inconsistent""","""""""{html}<div><p>TableViews that are 'grouped' (i.e. style: Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED) render as normal tables 50% of the time.</p> <p>This is happening on both the Simulator and the device.</p> <p>This does NOT happen using any SDK 4.0 on an iPhone OS 3.x device.</p> <p>This does NOT happen using any SDK other than 4.0.</p> <p>This is currently happening in the KitchenSink application. Base UI -&gt; Views -&gt; Table Views</p> <p>Simply toggle between Views and Table Views repeatedly to see inconsistent rendering.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView style=Grouped is inconsistent
Description: """"{html}<div><p>TableViews that are 'grouped' (i.e. style: Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED) render as normal tables 50% of the time.</p> <p>This is happening on both the Simulator and the device.</p> <p>This does NOT happen using any SDK 4.0 on an iPhone OS 3.x device.</p> <p>This does NOT happen using any SDK other than 4.0.</p> <p>This is currently happening in the KitchenSink application. Base UI -&gt; Views -&gt; Table Views</p> <p>Simply toggle between Views and Table Views repeatedly to see inconsistent rendering.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1146,12,"""Projects with Spaces in the name break pathing""","""""""{html}<div><p>We have a premium customer who has a project that uses web views and CSS. If he creates a project with spaces in the name, the CSS does not load. If the project has no spaces in the name, everything works. I have recreated this as well.</p> <p>Helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3135"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3135</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Projects with Spaces in the name break pathing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We have a premium customer who has a project that uses web views and CSS. If he creates a project with spaces in the name, the CSS does not load. If the project has no spaces in the name, everything works. I have recreated this as well.</p> <p>Helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3135"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3135</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1145,12,"""Android: Orientation issues?""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/879"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #879"""""""">#879</a> mentioned that there might be orientation issues on Android which could be duplicated by the following code:</p> <pre> <code>var webView = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'http://google.com'}); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({fullscreen: true});  win.orientationModes = [  Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT, Titanium.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT ];  win.add(webView); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>May have been fixed at some point, maybe not.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Orientation issues?
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/879"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #879"""""""">#879</a> mentioned that there might be orientation issues on Android which could be duplicated by the following code:</p> <pre> <code>var webView = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'http://google.com'}); var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({fullscreen: true}); win.orientationModes = [ Titanium.UI.PORTRAIT, Titanium.UI.UPSIDE_PORTRAIT ]; win.add(webView); win.open();</code> </pre> <p>May have been fixed at some point, maybe not.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1144,12,"""Disable button in toolbar doesn't refresh button""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have a button that has both a backgroundImage and a backgroundDisabledImage. When the button is added to a window, enabling/disabling the button works as expected. When it's added to the toolbar, the button image doesn't get refreshed. I've tried setting the toolbar to null and then setting it again, but no success. Here is some code I've tried: <a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/434467"""""""">http://gist.github.com/434467</a></p> <p>Note: this used to work in Titanium 1.2.0.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Disable button in toolbar doesn't refresh button
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have a button that has both a backgroundImage and a backgroundDisabledImage. When the button is added to a window, enabling/disabling the button works as expected. When it's added to the toolbar, the button image doesn't get refreshed. I've tried setting the toolbar to null and then setting it again, but no success. Here is some code I've tried: <a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/434467"""""""">http://gist.github.com/434467</a></p> <p>Note: this used to work in Titanium 1.2.0.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1143,12,"""Events not fired from web views in 1.3 & 1.3.1""","""""""{html}<div><p>Ok, a customer reported that when using Ti events in web views under 1.3 do not fire. I have confirmed this as well. Attaching 2 files that show this behavior.</p> <p>this is the helpdesk ticket as well:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3154"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3154</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Events not fired from web views in 1.3 & 1.3.1
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Ok, a customer reported that when using Ti events in web views under 1.3 do not fire. I have confirmed this as well. Attaching 2 files that show this behavior.</p> <p>this is the helpdesk ticket as well:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3154"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3154</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1142,12,"""Videos in Photo Gallery""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need to expose videos when the openPhotoGallery method is called. Right now, only photos are exposed.</p> <p>Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({</p> <pre> <code>success:function(event) {     var cropRect = event.cropRect;     var image = event.media;      // set image view     imageView.image = image;      Titanium.API.info('PHOTO GALLERY SUCCESS cropRect.x ' + cropRect.x + ' cropRect.y ' + cropRect.y  + ' cropRect.height ' + cropRect.height + ' cropRect.width ' + cropRect.width);  }, cancel:function() {  }, error:function(error) { }, allowImageEditing:true,</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Videos in Photo Gallery
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need to expose videos when the openPhotoGallery method is called. Right now, only photos are exposed.</p> <p>Titanium.Media.openPhotoGallery({</p> <pre> <code>success:function(event) { var cropRect = event.cropRect; var image = event.media; // set image view imageView.image = image; Titanium.API.info('PHOTO GALLERY SUCCESS cropRect.x ' + cropRect.x + ' cropRect.y ' + cropRect.y + ' cropRect.height ' + cropRect.height + ' cropRect.width ' + cropRect.width); }, cancel:function() { }, error:function(error) { }, allowImageEditing:true,</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1141,12,"""Text Field focus kills gesture listener""","""""""{html}<div><p>this heldesk ticket brought this bug to light:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3143"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3143</a></p> <p>The help desk ticket really explains it, but here is what I did to reproduce it.</p> <p>Create a default project that creates 2 windows and 2 tabs. Add a text field to window 2 and add the gesture event listener in app.js. At this point the shake gesture works. Now, navigate to window 2 and click in the text field. Now, go back to window 1(or even stay on this window) and the shake gesture no longer works.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Text Field focus kills gesture listener
Description: """"{html}<div><p>this heldesk ticket brought this bug to light:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3143"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3143</a></p> <p>The help desk ticket really explains it, but here is what I did to reproduce it.</p> <p>Create a default project that creates 2 windows and 2 tabs. Add a text field to window 2 and add the gesture event listener in app.js. At this point the shake gesture works. Now, navigate to window 2 and click in the text field. Now, go back to window 1(or even stay on this window) and the shake gesture no longer works.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1140,12,"""update issues""","""""""{html}<div><p>Downloaded update to the mobile SDK but...</p> <p>1) The title bar still says 1.2.1<br> 2) My app no longer works.</p> <p>The app gets and parses data via YQL</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: update issues
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Downloaded update to the mobile SDK but...</p> <p>1) The title bar still says 1.2.1<br> 2) My app no longer works.</p> <p>The app gets and parses data via YQL</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1139,12,"""Image orientations from gallery or camera wrong when imageEditing is false on device""","""""""{html}<div><p>After taking a photo, or choosing a photo from the gallery on a the device WITHOUT using imageEditing to crop the photo, the orientation is always wrong.</p> <p>To test, see the KS demo in: Phone &gt; Save To Gallery &gt; Background Image</p> <p>Select a photo which was taken with the iPhone and you'll see that photos taken in portrait are set to the background rotated right 90 degrees. Also, photos which are taken in landscape-upside down (camera at the bottom) are rotated 180 degrees when applied to a background.</p> <p>This works on the simulator fine, but not on the iPhone.<br> Also, it works OK after imageEditing has been used to make the square version.</p> <p>The only photos which appear correctly are those which are taken in landscape (with the camera at the top of the phone as you hold it)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Image orientations from gallery or camera wrong when imageEditing is false on device
Description: """"{html}<div><p>After taking a photo, or choosing a photo from the gallery on a the device WITHOUT using imageEditing to crop the photo, the orientation is always wrong.</p> <p>To test, see the KS demo in: Phone &gt; Save To Gallery &gt; Background Image</p> <p>Select a photo which was taken with the iPhone and you'll see that photos taken in portrait are set to the background rotated right 90 degrees. Also, photos which are taken in landscape-upside down (camera at the bottom) are rotated 180 degrees when applied to a background.</p> <p>This works on the simulator fine, but not on the iPhone.<br> Also, it works OK after imageEditing has been used to make the square version.</p> <p>The only photos which appear correctly are those which are taken in landscape (with the camera at the top of the phone as you hold it)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1138,12,"""Webviews loading indicator no longer shows while loading a remote web page""","""""""{html}<div><p>See the demo in KS:</p> <p>Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Webview controls</p> <p>While loading the web page in the webView 'browser', it used to show a white spinning indicator in the center of the screen. This no longer shows. (Nor does it show network activity with the status bar spinner). Without this, the user is just looking a white screen with no idea if anything is loading.</p> <p>Once this is fixed, it would also be nice to have the spinner show again when a link is clicked with the webView 'browser' - other wise there is no indication of activity at all when a user cliks a link within a remote web page.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Webviews loading indicator no longer shows while loading a remote web page
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See the demo in KS:</p> <p>Base UI &gt; Views &gt; Webview controls</p> <p>While loading the web page in the webView 'browser', it used to show a white spinning indicator in the center of the screen. This no longer shows. (Nor does it show network activity with the status bar spinner). Without this, the user is just looking a white screen with no idea if anything is loading.</p> <p>Once this is fixed, it would also be nice to have the spinner show again when a link is clicked with the webView 'browser' - other wise there is no indication of activity at all when a user cliks a link within a remote web page.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1137,12,"""Modal windows in split view completely screwed""","""""""{html}<div><p>Run the following (slightly modified) <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/929"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #929"""""""">#929</a> test:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow();  var data = [ {title:'May 6, 2010 Report - Week 1', hasChild:false, test:1, header:'May 2010'}, {title:'April 26, 2010 Report - Week 4', hasChild:false, test:2, header:'April 2010'} ]   var nav = Ti.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup({    window: win });  tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({     data:data,     style: Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED,     backgroundColor:'transparent',     rowBackgroundColor:'white' });   var newView1 = Titanium.UI.createView({     backgroundColor:'blue' });  newImageView = Titanium.UI.createImageView({     url:'default_app_logo.png',     top:100,     left:100,     height:100,     width:100 });  newImageView.addEventListener('click', function(e) {     var w = Titanium.UI.createWindow({          backgroundColor:'#336699',              title:'Modal Window',         barColor:'black',         url:'largechart_scrollable.js',         modal:true     });          var flexSpace = Titanium.UI.createButton({         systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.FLEXIBLE_SPACE     });      var bb = Titanium.UI.createButton({         title:'Return to Thumbnail View',         style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.BORDERED          });      // Add a toolbar     var toolbar1 = Titanium.UI.createToolbar({         items:[bb,flexSpace],         top:0,         borderTop:true,         borderBottom:true     });      bb.addEventListener('click', function()     {         w.close();     });          w.add(toolbar1);     w.open(); });  newView1.add(newImageView);  //create the scrollable (right-hand view) var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({     views:[newView1], // can add in addition views here     showPagingControl:true,     pagingControlHeight:30,     maxZoomScale:2.0,     currentPage:0 });  win.add(scrollView);   var splitwin = Ti.UI.iPad.createSplitWindow({     detailView:nav,     masterView:tableview });   splitwin.addEventListener('visible',function(e) {     if (e.view == 'detail')     {         e.button.title = """"""""Master"""""""";         win.leftNavButton = e.button;     }     else if (e.view == 'master')     {         win.leftNavButton = null;     } });   splitwin.open();</code> </pre> <p>Click on the image to make the modal window appear. Which direction will it slide in from? How will the view re-orient? Nobody knows.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Modal windows in split view completely screwed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Run the following (slightly modified) <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/tickets/929"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #929"""""""">#929</a> test:</p> <pre> <code>var win = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var data = [ {title:'May 6, 2010 Report - Week 1', hasChild:false, test:1, header:'May 2010'}, {title:'April 26, 2010 Report - Week 4', hasChild:false, test:2, header:'April 2010'} ] var nav = Ti.UI.iPhone.createNavigationGroup({ window: win }); tableview = Titanium.UI.createTableView({ data:data, style: Titanium.UI.iPhone.TableViewStyle.GROUPED, backgroundColor:'transparent', rowBackgroundColor:'white' }); var newView1 = Titanium.UI.createView({ backgroundColor:'blue' }); newImageView = Titanium.UI.createImageView({ url:'default_app_logo.png', top:100, left:100, height:100, width:100 }); newImageView.addEventListener('click', function(e) { var w = Titanium.UI.createWindow({ backgroundColor:'#336699', title:'Modal Window', barColor:'black', url:'largechart_scrollable.js', modal:true }); var flexSpace = Titanium.UI.createButton({ systemButton:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButton.FLEXIBLE_SPACE }); var bb = Titanium.UI.createButton({ title:'Return to Thumbnail View', style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.BORDERED }); // Add a toolbar var toolbar1 = Titanium.UI.createToolbar({ items:[bb,flexSpace], top:0, borderTop:true, borderBottom:true }); bb.addEventListener('click', function() { w.close(); }); w.add(toolbar1); w.open(); }); newView1.add(newImageView); //create the scrollable (right-hand view) var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({ views:[newView1], // can add in addition views here showPagingControl:true, pagingControlHeight:30, maxZoomScale:2.0, currentPage:0 }); win.add(scrollView); var splitwin = Ti.UI.iPad.createSplitWindow({ detailView:nav, masterView:tableview }); splitwin.addEventListener('visible',function(e) { if (e.view == 'detail') { e.button.title = """"""""Master""""""""; win.leftNavButton = e.button; } else if (e.view == 'master') { win.leftNavButton = null; } }); splitwin.open();</code> </pre> <p>Click on the image to make the modal window appear. Which direction will it slide in from? How will the view re-orient? Nobody knows.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
