TIMOB-1135,12,"""iOS: Ability to set font properties on a tableViewRow""","""""""{html}<div><p>This was first asked in Q &amp; A and then submitted by a  premium customer. Users want to be able to set font properties on a  table without needing to use a label.</p>  <p>Q&amp;A question:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/33581/bug-table-row-font-doesnt-work-on-iphone#header"""""""">  http://developer.<USER>com/question/33581/bug-table-row-font...</a></p>  <p>Things to be able to set are size, font weight, and font.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Ability to set font properties on a tableViewRow
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This was first asked in Q &amp; A and then submitted by a premium customer. Users want to be able to set font properties on a table without needing to use a label.</p> <p>Q&amp;A question:<br> <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/33581/bug-table-row-font-doesnt-work-on-iphone#header""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/33581/bug-table-row-font...</a></p> <p>Things to be able to set are size, font weight, and font.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1134,12,"""Create TiDate object""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need some good way to represent dates. Displaying (and reading them) in a particular UTC format is a burden on the user.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Create TiDate object
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need some good way to represent dates. Displaying (and reading them) in a particular UTC format is a burden on the user.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1133,12,"""Allow for ordering of property setting""","""""""{html}<div><p>Right now view properties are set in any order because of how -[TiProxy allKeys] works (namely, it returns the properties in any generic order). For some classes, properties need to be set in a very specific order, since some properties rely on others being pre-set; so far we've had to jury-rig systems which take this into account. Maybe a -[TiUIView propertyConfigurationOrder] function or something that will handle this?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Allow for ordering of property setting
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Right now view properties are set in any order because of how -[TiProxy allKeys] works (namely, it returns the properties in any generic order). For some classes, properties need to be set in a very specific order, since some properties rely on others being pre-set; so far we've had to jury-rig systems which take this into account. Maybe a -[TiUIView propertyConfigurationOrder] function or something that will handle this?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1132,12,"""removeEventListener not removing events""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have not been able to get the removeEventListener to work and have included a simple example below.</p> <p>Basically if you click button one, you get an alert event. Clicking button two should remove the click eventListener from button 1.... but its doesn't.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var testButton = Titanium.UI.createButton({     top:30,     width:100,     height:33,     title:'button 1' }); testButton.addEventListener('click', function() {     alert('Hello, world!'); });   var testButton2 = Titanium.UI.createButton({     top:70,     width:100,     height:33,     title:'button 2' }); testButton2.addEventListener('click', function() {     testButton.removeEventListener('click'); });   win1.add(testButton); win1.add(testButton2);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: removeEventListener not removing events
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have not been able to get the removeEventListener to work and have included a simple example below.</p> <p>Basically if you click button one, you get an alert event. Clicking button two should remove the click eventListener from button 1.... but its doesn't.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">var testButton = Titanium.UI.createButton({ top:30, width:100, height:33, title:'button 1' }); testButton.addEventListener('click', function() { alert('Hello, world!'); }); var testButton2 = Titanium.UI.createButton({ top:70, width:100, height:33, title:'button 2' }); testButton2.addEventListener('click', function() { testButton.removeEventListener('click'); }); win1.add(testButton); win1.add(testButton2);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1131,12,"""preventDefault not working in web view""","""""""{html}<div><p>Base UI =&gt; Views =&gt; Mixing Views</p> <p>top view is a web with this:</p> <p>document.body.addEventListener(""""""""touchmove"""""""", function(e) {e.preventDefault();}, false);</p> <p>but it still scrolls - this had worked previously</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: preventDefault not working in web view
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Base UI =&gt; Views =&gt; Mixing Views</p> <p>top view is a web with this:</p> <p>document.body.addEventListener(""""""""touchmove"""""""", function(e) {e.preventDefault();}, false);</p> <p>but it still scrolls - this had worked previously</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1130,12,"""Slider breaks when value is set to 0""","""""""{html}<div><p>A premium customer submitted a ticket that when they set a sliders value to 0 the slider became unusable. I have reproduced this as well. Code below.</p> <p>var basicSlider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({<br></p> <pre> <code>min:0, max:10, value:0, width:100, height:'auto', top:30</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>Helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3061"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3061</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Slider breaks when value is set to 0
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A premium customer submitted a ticket that when they set a sliders value to 0 the slider became unusable. I have reproduced this as well. Code below.</p> <p>var basicSlider = Titanium.UI.createSlider({<br></p> <pre> <code>min:0, max:10, value:0, width:100, height:'auto', top:30</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>Helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3061"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/3061</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1129,12,"""Android: Label doesn't appear multiline in scrollview""","""""""{html}<div><p>Need to inform the label to be multiline when it has a constrained width and an unconstrained height. The view itself will size correctly, but it doesn't draw the text w/o saying it's multiline.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Label doesn't appear multiline in scrollview
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Need to inform the label to be multiline when it has a constrained width and an unconstrained height. The view itself will size correctly, but it doesn't draw the text w/o saying it's multiline.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
