TIMOB-1124,12,"""Android: Add support for backgroundGradient on views""","""""""Implement backgroundGradient support on Android.    Note: Only linear gradient is supported. A future task will  be created to implement radial support.    h3. Linear Gradient Test Case      Compare rendering against iOS & MobileWeb to verify correct behavior.  """"""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add support for backgroundGradient on views
Description: """"Implement backgroundGradient support on Android. Note: Only linear gradient is supported. A future task will be created to implement radial support. h3. Linear Gradient Test Case Compare rendering against iOS & MobileWeb to verify correct behavior. """"",title+description
TIMOB-1123,12,"""Orientation Change not working correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>In sdk 1.3.1 the first orientation change is not honored when setting the orientation mode to PORTRAIT only. The code below shows that the window rotates to landscape on the first rotation only, then it follows what was set in orientation modes. Just a note: this is holding up the app of the customer that found this.</p> <p>// this sets the background color of the master UIView (when there are no windows/tab groups on it) Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');</p> <p>// // create base UI tab and root window // var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win1.add( Ti.UI.createLabel( { text: 'label to show orientation', top:50, left:10}));</p> <p>win1.orientationModes =[Ti.UI.PORTRAIT];<br> win1.orientation = Ti.UI.PORTRAIT;</p> <p>// open tab group win1.open();</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Orientation Change not working correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In sdk 1.3.1 the first orientation change is not honored when setting the orientation mode to PORTRAIT only. The code below shows that the window rotates to landscape on the first rotation only, then it follows what was set in orientation modes. Just a note: this is holding up the app of the customer that found this.</p> <p>// this sets the background color of the master UIView (when there are no windows/tab groups on it) Titanium.UI.setBackgroundColor('#000');</p> <p>// // create base UI tab and root window // var win1 = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win1.add( Ti.UI.createLabel( { text: 'label to show orientation', top:50, left:10}));</p> <p>win1.orientationModes =[Ti.UI.PORTRAIT];<br> win1.orientation = Ti.UI.PORTRAIT;</p> <p>// open tab group win1.open();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1122,12,"""Geolocation listener fires repeatedly""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium.Geolocation.addEventListener gets fired 50-75/sec on app startup with no location changes. My understanding was that this was only supposed to fire when the location changed. On the iphone simulator, I'm seeing this fire every 3 seconds. On the devices its many, many times a second. It slows down the app start-up and causes time-outs.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/994622"""""""">http://pastie.org/994622</a></p> <p>In the console log, you can see the first location request and then the following 187 are lines are the location listenter.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Geolocation listener fires repeatedly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium.Geolocation.addEventListener gets fired 50-75/sec on app startup with no location changes. My understanding was that this was only supposed to fire when the location changed. On the iphone simulator, I'm seeing this fire every 3 seconds. On the devices its many, many times a second. It slows down the app start-up and causes time-outs.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/994622"""""""">http://pastie.org/994622</a></p> <p>In the console log, you can see the first location request and then the following 187 are lines are the location listenter.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1121,12,"""Android: Video gallery (upload)""","""""""{html}<div><p>There is need to implement video upload after choosing from openphotogallery function or capturing from ShowCamera function. I'm not sure if it's already available with iphone device because i only develop with simulator and camera is not available on this. Very urgent if not!!</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Video gallery (upload)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There is need to implement video upload after choosing from openphotogallery function or capturing from ShowCamera function. I'm not sure if it's already available with iphone device because i only develop with simulator and camera is not available on this. Very urgent if not!!</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
