Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have a customer that has reported this warning on an iPhone app that has nested scroll views. I have not been able to reproduce this warning but I have seen it today in an iPad app when using pop-overs.</p> <p>This is the iphone helpdesk ticket:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2839"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2839</a></p> <p>This is the iPad app:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2910"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2910</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1099,12,"""__IPHONE_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED will not work when compiling to lower OS versions""","""""""{html}<div><p>When compiling under an SDK which supports 3.2 or 4.0 for 3.1.x OS, you get the 3.2&gt;= specific code. Need to evaluate how to deal with this.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: __IPHONE_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED will not work when compiling to lower OS versions
