TIMOB-1095,12,"""Expose if email is enabled on a device""","""""""{html}<div><p>Have a customer request to expose whether or not an email account has been setup on a device for when an email dialog is being used.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Expose if email is enabled on a device
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Have a customer request to expose whether or not an email account has been setup on a device for when an email dialog is being used.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1094,12,"""Android: incorrect auto height calculation""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you run the Facebook demo (Query), you'll see that the layout is not correctly calculating the height of each row.</p> <p><img src= """"""""http://img.skitch.com/20100602-r1p3yefp5xb7g2rten62jiedrp.png"""""""" alt=""""""""android""""""""></p> <p><img src= """"""""http://img.skitch.com/20100602-8kchc8ne1hsaumc3pn394skjrd.png"""""""" alt=""""""""iphone""""""""></p> <p>iPhone is correctly displaying.</p> <p>It appears that maybe Android is disregarding the minRowHeight property on the table view.</p> <pre> <code>var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({minRowHeight:100});</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: incorrect auto height calculation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you run the Facebook demo (Query), you'll see that the layout is not correctly calculating the height of each row.</p> <p><img src= """"""""http://img.skitch.com/20100602-r1p3yefp5xb7g2rten62jiedrp.png"""""""" alt=""""""""android""""""""></p> <p><img src= """"""""http://img.skitch.com/20100602-8kchc8ne1hsaumc3pn394skjrd.png"""""""" alt=""""""""iphone""""""""></p> <p>iPhone is correctly displaying.</p> <p>It appears that maybe Android is disregarding the minRowHeight property on the table view.</p> <pre> <code>var tableView = Ti.UI.createTableView({minRowHeight:100});</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1093,12,"""Android: setInterval continues after exiting the test""","""""""{html}<div><p>seems to continue to run (from console logging) after you exit from the test.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: setInterval continues after exiting the test
Description: """"{html}<div><p>seems to continue to run (from console logging) after you exit from the test.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
