TIMOB-1091,12,"""Opening pickers over navbar may remove settings""","""""""{html}<div><p>In particular since the photo gallery, iPod, and Contacts set up their own navigation controllers for the picker, we may have a situation where the navigation bar gets messed up.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Opening pickers over navbar may remove settings
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In particular since the photo gallery, iPod, and Contacts set up their own navigation controllers for the picker, we may have a situation where the navigation bar gets messed up.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1090,12,"""Memory Usage on ImageViews""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer has created a slide show type of application and on a device is reporting that after view 4-5 images, the app will become unresponsive and crash.</p> <p>View this ticket for reference:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2782"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2782</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Memory Usage on ImageViews
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer has created a slide show type of application and on a device is reporting that after view 4-5 images, the app will become unresponsive and crash.</p> <p>View this ticket for reference:<br> <a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2782"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2782</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1089,12,"""Updating a table row crashes an app""","""""""{html}<div><p>A customer reported that when using the kitchen sink app, if they clicked a row twice in Table row update example, the app crashes. I have reproduced this as well.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Updating a table row crashes an app
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A customer reported that when using the kitchen sink app, if they clicked a row twice in Table row update example, the app crashes. I have reproduced this as well.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1088,12,"""Android: DB Field operations throw exceptions""","""""""{html}<div><p>SQLite doesn't retrieve an schema information if there are no rows in a result. Access fields by name on and empty result set will throw an exception. iPhone apparently just returns 0 instead. Update to catch the exception and return 0.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: DB Field operations throw exceptions
Description: """"{html}<div><p>SQLite doesn't retrieve an schema information if there are no rows in a result. Access fields by name on and empty result set will throw an exception. iPhone apparently just returns 0 instead. Update to catch the exception and return 0.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1087,12,"""XML CData parsing issue""","""""""A customer reported on the helpdesk that this feed, http://www.atlasquest.com/api/1.0/search.html?gTypeId=1&amp;gCache=1&amp;gName=Christmas%20Letter%20box, causes a null in a xhr request responseText and responseXML, which I was able to produce. I found that this feed and lines of plus signs (+) in one of the cdata blocks. I took the +'s out and the feed works. I am not sure if this is a parsing issue on our side or if this would break other parsers.    This feed, http://www.atlasquest.com/api/1.0/search.html?gTypeId=1&amp;gCache=1&amp;gName=Yuri, works just fine but it does not have all the +'s.    See this ticket as a reference. http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2897""""""",Bug,"Title: XML CData parsing issue
Description: """"A customer reported on the helpdesk that this feed, http://www.atlasquest.com/api/1.0/search.html?gTypeId=1&amp;gCache=1&amp;gName=Christmas%20Letter%20box, causes a null in a xhr request responseText and responseXML, which I was able to produce. I found that this feed and lines of plus signs (+) in one of the cdata blocks. I took the +'s out and the feed works. I am not sure if this is a parsing issue on our side or if this would break other parsers. This feed, http://www.atlasquest.com/api/1.0/search.html?gTypeId=1&amp;gCache=1&amp;gName=Yuri, works just fine but it does not have all the +'s. See this ticket as a reference. http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2897""""",title+description
TIMOB-1086,12,"""XML Parsing""","""""""{html}<div><p>We have a request to <em>fix</em> our DOM xml functionality. See  the helpdesk ticket for reference.</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2819"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2819</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: XML Parsing
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We have a request to <em>fix</em> our DOM xml functionality. See the helpdesk ticket for reference.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2819"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2819</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1084,12,"""Android: Failure during forwardGeo causes NPE""","""""""{html}<div><p>The error code path wasn't handled correctly.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Failure during forwardGeo causes NPE
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The error code path wasn't handled correctly.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1083,12,"""iPhone sample project crashes when built against SDK 3.2""","""""""{html}<div><p><strong>Expected:</strong> iPhone apps built against SDK 3.2 will launch in iPad emulator centered at iPhone screen size.</p> <p><strong>Observed:</strong> iPad emulator launches with centered all black iPhone screen. Error <code>Failed to load NSMainNibFile MainWindow_ipad' appears in logs.</code></p> <p><strong>Steps to reproduce:</strong></p> <ol> <li>Click New Project<br></li> <li>Select type 'mobile'<br></li> <li>Complete form<br></li> <li>Click Test &amp; Package tab<br></li> <li>Select SDK 3.2 in iPhone tab</li> </ol> <p><strong>Resulting log:</strong></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""text"""""""">[INFO] Compiling JavaScript...one moment [INFO] No JavaScript errors detected. [INFO] One moment, building ... [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.3.0 [INFO] iPhone Device family: iphone [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 3.2 [INFO] Performing full rebuild. This will take a little bit. Hold tight... [INFO] Executing XCode build... [INFO] Executing XCode Compiler [toggle output] [DEBUG] executing command: xcodebuild -target iPhone on iPad -configuration Debug -sdk iphonesimulator3.2 GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=__LOG__ID__=4666dd69-40c6-46be-a427-d4baf552914f DEPLOYTYPE=development DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=1.3.0 IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=3.1 TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY=1 Build settings from command line: GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS = __LOG__ID__=4666dd69-40c6-46be-a427-d4baf552914f DEPLOYTYPE=development DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=1.3.0 IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 3.1 PLATFORM_NAME = iphonesimulator SDKROOT = /Developer/Platforms/iPhoneSimulator.platform/Developer/SDKs/iPhoneSimulator3.2.sdk TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY = 1 === BUILD NATIVE TARGET iPhone on iPad OF PROJECT iPhone on iPad WITH CONFIGURATION Debug === Check dependencies ProcessInfoPlistFile """"""""build/Debug-iphonesimulator/iPhone on iPad.app/Info.plist"""""""" Info.plist cd """"""""/Users/jschulz/Sites/Titanium/iPhone on iPad/build/iphone""