TIMOB-1082,12,"""iPhone build fails if word 'Titanium' is in project name""","""""""{html}<div><p><strong>Expected:</strong> There are no restrictions on project names</p> <p><strong>Observed:</strong> iPhone apps do not build if the word Titanium) is in the project name</p> <p><strong>Steps to reproduce:</strong></p> <ol> <li>Click New Project<br></li> <li>Choose mobile<br></li> <li>Use a project which includes the word Titanium (must be a capital T)<br></li> <li>Try to build iPhone app.</li> </ol> <p>Resulting log:<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""text"""""""">[INFO] Compiling JavaScript...one moment [INFO] No JavaScript errors detected. [INFO] One moment, building ... [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.3.0 [INFO] iPhone Device family: iphone [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 3.1 [INFO] Performing full rebuild. This will take a little bit. Hold tight... [INFO] Executing XCode build... [INFO] Executing XCode Compiler [toggle output] [DEBUG] executing command: xcodebuild -target Capital T Titanium -configuration Debug -sdk iphonesimulator3.1 GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=<strong>LOG</strong>ID<strong>=a9696903-af02-446f-a7a8-fafe09404935 DEPLOYTYPE=development DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=1.3.0 IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=3.1 TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY=1 [ERROR] Unknown target: Capital T Titanium Usage: xcodebuild [-project &lt;projectname&gt;] [-activetarget] [-alltargets] [-target &lt;targetname&gt;]... [-parallelizeTargets] [-activeconfiguration] [-configuration &lt;configurationname&gt;] [-sdk &lt;sdkfullpath&gt;|&lt;sdkname&gt;] [-xcconfig &lt;filepath&gt;] [&lt;buildsetting&gt;=&lt;value&gt;]... [&lt;buildaction&gt;]... xcodebuild [-version [-sdk [&lt;sdkfullpath&gt;|&lt;sdkname&gt;] [&lt;item&gt;] ] xcodebuild [-showsdks] xcodebuild [-find &lt;binary&gt; -sdk &lt;sdkfullpath&gt;|&lt;sdkname&gt;] xcodebuild [-list] Build settings from command line: GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS = </strong>LOG<strong>ID</strong>=a9696903-af02-446f-a7a8-fafe09404935 DEPLOYTYPE=development DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=1.3.0 IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 3.1 PLATFORM_NAME = iphonesimulator SDKROOT = /Developer/Platforms/iPhoneSimulator.platform/Developer/SDKs/iPhoneSimulator3.1.sdk TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY = 1 [INFO] Compile completed in 0.422 seconds [ERROR] Build Failed (Missing app at /Users/jschulz/Sites/Titanium/Capital T Titanium/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Capital T Titanium.app/Capital T Titanium). Please see output for more details</code> </pre> <p><strong>Notes:</strong></p> <ol> <li>Does not affect Android apps<br></li> <li>titanium (lower case t) works as expected</li> </ol></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone build fails if word 'Titanium' is in project name
Description: """"{html}<div><p><strong>Expected:</strong> There are no restrictions on project names</p> <p><strong>Observed:</strong> iPhone apps do not build if the word Titanium) is in the project name</p> <p><strong>Steps to reproduce:</strong></p> <ol> <li>Click New Project<br></li> <li>Choose mobile<br></li> <li>Use a project which includes the word Titanium (must be a capital T)<br></li> <li>Try to build iPhone app.</li> </ol> <p>Resulting log:<br></p> <pre> <code class=""""""""text"""""""">[INFO] Compiling JavaScript...one moment [INFO] No JavaScript errors detected. [INFO] One moment, building ... [INFO] Titanium SDK version: 1.3.0 [INFO] iPhone Device family: iphone [INFO] iPhone SDK version: 3.1 [INFO] Performing full rebuild. This will take a little bit. Hold tight... [INFO] Executing XCode build... [INFO] Executing XCode Compiler [toggle output] [DEBUG] executing command: xcodebuild -target Capital T Titanium -configuration Debug -sdk iphonesimulator3.1 GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS=<strong>LOG</strong>ID<strong>=a9696903-af02-446f-a7a8-fafe09404935 DEPLOYTYPE=development DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=1.3.0 IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=3.1 TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY=1 [ERROR] Unknown target: Capital T Titanium Usage: xcodebuild [-project &lt;projectname&gt;] [-activetarget] [-alltargets] [-target &lt;targetname&gt;]... [-parallelizeTargets] [-activeconfiguration] [-configuration &lt;configurationname&gt;] [-sdk &lt;sdkfullpath&gt;|&lt;sdkname&gt;] [-xcconfig &lt;filepath&gt;] [&lt;buildsetting&gt;=&lt;value&gt;]... [&lt;buildaction&gt;]... xcodebuild [-version [-sdk [&lt;sdkfullpath&gt;|&lt;sdkname&gt;] [&lt;item&gt;] ] xcodebuild [-showsdks] xcodebuild [-find &lt;binary&gt; -sdk &lt;sdkfullpath&gt;|&lt;sdkname&gt;] xcodebuild [-list] Build settings from command line: GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS = </strong>LOG<strong>ID</strong>=a9696903-af02-446f-a7a8-fafe09404935 DEPLOYTYPE=development DEBUG=1 TI_VERSION=1.3.0 IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 3.1 PLATFORM_NAME = iphonesimulator SDKROOT = /Developer/Platforms/iPhoneSimulator.platform/Developer/SDKs/iPhoneSimulator3.1.sdk TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY = 1 [INFO] Compile completed in 0.422 seconds [ERROR] Build Failed (Missing app at /Users/jschulz/Sites/Titanium/Capital T Titanium/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator/Capital T Titanium.app/Capital T Titanium). Please see output for more details</code> </pre> <p><strong>Notes:</strong></p> <ol> <li>Does not affect Android apps<br></li> <li>titanium (lower case t) works as expected</li> </ol></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1081,12,"""iOS: Ti.UI.iPhone.MODAL_TRANSITION_STYLE_PARTIAL_CURL not triggering close on exit.""","""""""{html}<div><p>I'm opening a modal window via  Ti.UI.iPhone.MODAL_TRANSITION_STYLE_PARTIAL_CURL. Really cool  effect but when the user clicks on the curled up window, the modal  window closes without firing anything. Is there a way to display  this click or atleast fire """"""""close"""""""" or """"""""blur"""""""" when the user clicks  out? It's really frustrating because i would like the user to not  able to exit out without going thru the selection on the  screen.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Ti.UI.iPhone.MODAL_TRANSITION_STYLE_PARTIAL_CURL not triggering close on exit.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I'm opening a modal window via Ti.UI.iPhone.MODAL_TRANSITION_STYLE_PARTIAL_CURL. Really cool effect but when the user clicks on the curled up window, the modal window closes without firing anything. Is there a way to display this click or atleast fire """"""""close"""""""" or """"""""blur"""""""" when the user clicks out? It's really frustrating because i would like the user to not able to exit out without going thru the selection on the screen.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1080,12,"""Android: WebView scalesToFit not Implemented""","""""""{html}<div><p>iPhone has a scalesToFit property. Android needs to support it.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: WebView scalesToFit not Implemented
Description: """"{html}<div><p>iPhone has a scalesToFit property. Android needs to support it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1079,12,"""Android: add support for minWidth, minHeight""","""""""You get into a situation when you use negative positioning (like top: -10) with auto where you're get smaller than intended calculations of the height/width. Need ability to set a floor with 2 new properties: """"""""minHeight"""""""", """"""""minWidth""""""""""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: add support for minWidth, minHeight
Description: """"You get into a situation when you use negative positioning (like top: -10) with auto where you're get smaller than intended calculations of the height/width. Need ability to set a floor with 2 new properties: """"""""minHeight"""""""", """"""""minWidth""""""""""""",title+description
TIMOB-1078,12,"""iPhone: ability to support minWidth, minHeight when using auto.""","""""""{html}<div><p>You get into a situation when you use negative positioning (like top: -10) with auto where you're get smaller than intended calculations of the height/width. Need ability to set a floor with 2 new properties: """"""""minHeight"""""""", """"""""minWidth""""""""</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: ability to support minWidth, minHeight when using auto.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>You get into a situation when you use negative positioning (like top: -10) with auto where you're get smaller than intended calculations of the height/width. Need ability to set a floor with 2 new properties: """"""""minHeight"""""""", """"""""minWidth""""""""</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1077,12,"""Titanium.App.getArguments() not working on OS4 beta4""","""""""{html}<div><p>Titanium.App.getArguments() seems to not work on Iphone OS4 beta 4.</p> <p>When calling a Custom URL schema passing some query strings arguments, ON the App it does not get the arguments.</p> <p>Used to work on 3.x</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.App.getArguments() not working on OS4 beta4
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Titanium.App.getArguments() seems to not work on Iphone OS4 beta 4.</p> <p>When calling a Custom URL schema passing some query strings arguments, ON the App it does not get the arguments.</p> <p>Used to work on 3.x</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1076,12,"""iPad orientation problem after launch""","""""""{html}<div><p>there is an issue with launch orientations and app widths. if you launch the KitchenSink-Ipad demo on the device in landscape, the initial window is ok then open one of the spilt screen examples - you'll see that the widths of the page are wrong.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPad orientation problem after launch
Description: """"{html}<div><p>there is an issue with launch orientations and app widths. if you launch the KitchenSink-Ipad demo on the device in landscape, the initial window is ok then open one of the spilt screen examples - you'll see that the widths of the page are wrong.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1075,12,"""iOS: Add Annotation pincolor Accepting colors""","""""""{html}<div><p>See Android <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1074"""""""" title=  """"""""Ticket #1074"""""""">#1074</a></p>  <p>User contributed feature on Android allowing colors to be  specified for the simple pin in addition to the 3 color  constants.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: iOS: Add Annotation pincolor Accepting colors
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See Android <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/1074"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #1074"""""""">#1074</a></p> <p>User contributed feature on Android allowing colors to be specified for the simple pin in addition to the 3 color constants.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-1074,12,"""Android:  Allow Annotations to specify colors.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Add support for setting colors on markers instead of limiting to the three hardcoded constants. Support all Titanium colors and color formats.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Allow Annotations to specify colors.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Add support for setting colors on markers instead of limiting to the three hardcoded constants. Support all Titanium colors and color formats.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
