TIMOB-998,12,"""Importing CSS/JS files broken for new Mobile SDK 1.3.0 WebViews on iPad""","""""""{html}<div><p>Create a new project with Mobile SDK 1.3.0 for iPad.</p> <p>Create a WebView for this app that opens a local HTML file (e.g. test.html) in Resources folder</p> <p>Put a test.css and test.js file also in your Resources folder.</p> <p>Try to include the CSS file with a link tag and try to include the JS file with a script tag from test.html</p> <p>Run the app in the iPad simulator.</p> <p>The test.css and test.js files will not be included.</p> <p>I would suspect that the files are either not being included in the build, or that the include path from test.html is incorrect.</p> <p>Also important: You can create a 1.2.0 Mobile SDK project, and follow the above steps, and you will have no problems. The bug does not happen.</p> <p>Even more interesting: After you create that 1.2.0 project, you can convert it to 1.3.0 from the Edit Project page, and when you run in the simulator, everything works fine. The bug does not affect converted projects, only original 1.3.0 projects.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Importing CSS/JS files broken for new Mobile SDK 1.3.0 WebViews on iPad
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Create a new project with Mobile SDK 1.3.0 for iPad.</p> <p>Create a WebView for this app that opens a local HTML file (e.g. test.html) in Resources folder</p> <p>Put a test.css and test.js file also in your Resources folder.</p> <p>Try to include the CSS file with a link tag and try to include the JS file with a script tag from test.html</p> <p>Run the app in the iPad simulator.</p> <p>The test.css and test.js files will not be included.</p> <p>I would suspect that the files are either not being included in the build, or that the include path from test.html is incorrect.</p> <p>Also important: You can create a 1.2.0 Mobile SDK project, and follow the above steps, and you will have no problems. The bug does not happen.</p> <p>Even more interesting: After you create that 1.2.0 project, you can convert it to 1.3.0 from the Edit Project page, and when you run in the simulator, everything works fine. The bug does not affect converted projects, only original 1.3.0 projects.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
