TIMOB-965,12,"""iPhone: Regression problem in video player""","""""""{html}<div><p>there's a very simple regression issue in video player.</p> <p>simple test case:</p> <p>var media_url = """"""""<a href= """"""""http://phreadz.com/service/encoder.php?g=5LPOKP754&amp;iph=1&quot;"""""""">http://phreadz.com/service/encoder.php?g=5LPOKP754&amp;amp;iph=1""""""""</a>;<br> var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({<br></p> <pre> <code>                        url:media_url,                         backgroundColor:'#111',                         movieControlMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_DEFAULT,                         scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_MODE_FILL                     });</code> </pre> <p>activeMovie.play();</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Regression problem in video player
Description: """"{html}<div><p>there's a very simple regression issue in video player.</p> <p>simple test case:</p> <p>var media_url = """"""""<a href= """"""""http://phreadz.com/service/encoder.php?g=5LPOKP754&amp;iph=1&quot;"""""""">http://phreadz.com/service/encoder.php?g=5LPOKP754&amp;amp;iph=1""""""""</a>;<br> var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({<br></p> <pre> <code> url:media_url, backgroundColor:'#111', movieControlMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_DEFAULT, scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_MODE_FILL });</code> </pre> <p>activeMovie.play();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-964,12,"""Modal windows will not reopen""","""""""{html}<div><p>Sample:</p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ barColor:'black', backgroundColor:'white', });  win1.open(); setTimeout(function () {win2.open({modal:true});}, 1000); setTimeout(function () {win2.close();}, 2000); setTimeout(function () {win2.open({modal:true});}, 3000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Modal windows will not reopen
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Sample:</p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ barColor:'black', backgroundColor:'white', }); win1.open(); setTimeout(function () {win2.open({modal:true});}, 1000); setTimeout(function () {win2.close();}, 2000); setTimeout(function () {win2.open({modal:true});}, 3000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-963,12,"""Modal window does not open properly if {modal:true} set on window instead of in open""","""""""{html}<div><p>Sample:</p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ barColor:'black', backgroundColor:'white', modal:true });  win1.open(); setTimeout(function () {win2.open();}, 1000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Modal window does not open properly if {modal:true} set on window instead of in open
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Sample:</p> <pre> <code>var win1 = Ti.UI.createWindow(); var win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({ barColor:'black', backgroundColor:'white', modal:true }); win1.open(); setTimeout(function () {win2.open();}, 1000);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-962,12,"""transparent pngs on toolbar do not render properly""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2487"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2487</a></p> <p>worked on 1.2.0. attached is the source to reproduce</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: transparent pngs on toolbar do not render properly
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2487"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2487</a></p> <p>worked on 1.2.0. attached is the source to reproduce</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-961,12,"""Web View doesn't load local jQuery""","""""""{html}<div><p>This can be seen running the KitchenSink 1.3 on Titanium 1.3, in both the iPhone and iPad emulator.</p> <p>In """"""""Local URL"""""""", the word """"""""hello"""""""" should be changed to """"""""Click Me to Hide the Toolbar"""""""", using jQuery, but that doesn't happen.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Web View doesn't load local jQuery
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This can be seen running the KitchenSink 1.3 on Titanium 1.3, in both the iPhone and iPad emulator.</p> <p>In """"""""Local URL"""""""", the word """"""""hello"""""""" should be changed to """"""""Click Me to Hide the Toolbar"""""""", using jQuery, but that doesn't happen.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-960,12,"""videoPlayer issue with 'proxied' urls (php etc.) - quite urgent""","""""""{html}<div><p>Something appears to have recently changed in how the videoPlayer works.</p> <p>I'm often seeing this output:<br></p> <pre> <code>[INFO] VIDEO!!http://phreadz.com/service/encoder.php?g=5LPOKP754&amp;iph=1 [WARN] Invalid type passed to function. Tried to play movie player without a valid url, media, or contentURL property in -<a>TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy play:</a><br> <br>   <br> [INFO] VIDEO!!http://api.12seconds.tv/videosrv/389492.mp4 [WARN] Invalid type passed to function. Tried to play movie player without a valid url, media, or contentURL property in -<a>TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy play:</a></code> </pre> <p>As you can see the url I'm sending it from phreadz needs to be a php file.<br> This provides privacy controls and mp4 encoding triggers, if needed, and the resulting output is always an MP4 url, with the correct video/mp4 mimetype set in the header. This all worked fine before the recent changes to TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy.m</p> <p>Quite a few providers of mp4 files which Phreadz supports do so through redirects and proxies on their servers, but do end up providing the correct mimetype and a compatible video file.</p> <p>I'm calling the videoPlayer like this:<br></p> <pre> <code>                        Ti.API.info('VIDEO!!'+media_url);<br> <br>   </code> </pre> <pre> <code><code>                    var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({                         url:media_url,                         backgroundColor:'#111',                         movieControlMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_DEFAULT,                         scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_MODE_FILL                     });</code></code> </pre> <pre>   <br> activeMovie.play(); </pre> <p>I did try setting mediaTypes or sourceTypes to the video constants too.</p> <p>This is very urgent for a few apps I'm building for some vip clients.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: videoPlayer issue with 'proxied' urls (php etc.) - quite urgent
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Something appears to have recently changed in how the videoPlayer works.</p> <p>I'm often seeing this output:<br></p> <pre> <code>[INFO] VIDEO!!http://phreadz.com/service/encoder.php?g=5LPOKP754&amp;iph=1 [WARN] Invalid type passed to function. Tried to play movie player without a valid url, media, or contentURL property in -<a>TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy play:</a><br> <br> <br> [INFO] VIDEO!!http://api.12seconds.tv/videosrv/389492.mp4 [WARN] Invalid type passed to function. Tried to play movie player without a valid url, media, or contentURL property in -<a>TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy play:</a></code> </pre> <p>As you can see the url I'm sending it from phreadz needs to be a php file.<br> This provides privacy controls and mp4 encoding triggers, if needed, and the resulting output is always an MP4 url, with the correct video/mp4 mimetype set in the header. This all worked fine before the recent changes to TiMediaVideoPlayerProxy.m</p> <p>Quite a few providers of mp4 files which Phreadz supports do so through redirects and proxies on their servers, but do end up providing the correct mimetype and a compatible video file.</p> <p>I'm calling the videoPlayer like this:<br></p> <pre> <code> Ti.API.info('VIDEO!!'+media_url);<br> <br> </code> </pre> <pre> <code><code> var activeMovie = Titanium.Media.createVideoPlayer({ url:media_url, backgroundColor:'#111', movieControlMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_CONTROL_DEFAULT, scalingMode:Titanium.Media.VIDEO_SCALING_MODE_FILL });</code></code> </pre> <pre> <br> activeMovie.play(); </pre> <p>I did try setting mediaTypes or sourceTypes to the video constants too.</p> <p>This is very urgent for a few apps I'm building for some vip clients.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-959,12,"""Primitive array types don't make it back to JS""","""""""{html}<div><p>In Android, if we have a primitive array type (i.e. a double array) in a TiDict, when the value is retrieved back from JS, the """"""""fromNative"""""""" logic misses it since it is a primitive array, (which isn't autoboxed).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Primitive array types don't make it back to JS
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In Android, if we have a primitive array type (i.e. a double array) in a TiDict, when the value is retrieved back from JS, the """"""""fromNative"""""""" logic misses it since it is a primitive array, (which isn't autoboxed).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-958,12,"""EmailDialog doesn't show up when using splitWindow""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi.</p> <p>When the application is using a splitWindow, the modal window of the EmailDialog won't show up.</p> <p>Sample app.js attached.<br> The code worked with tabGroup instead of splitWindow.</p> <p>Platform:<br> iPad, MobileSDK 1.3.0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: EmailDialog doesn't show up when using splitWindow
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi.</p> <p>When the application is using a splitWindow, the modal window of the EmailDialog won't show up.</p> <p>Sample app.js attached.<br> The code worked with tabGroup instead of splitWindow.</p> <p>Platform:<br> iPad, MobileSDK 1.3.0</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-957,12,"""Removing annotations from MapView breaks map evens""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I've outlined the issue on Q&amp;A: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/26471/mapview-click-event-does-not-fire-after-changing-annotations""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/26471/mapview-click-even...</a>.</p> <p>Calling mapview.removeAnnotations seems to break the mapview 'click' event listener.</p> <p>The following reproduces the issue:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">//create two sets of pins var pins1 = [   Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.390749, longitude:-122.081651, title:""""""""pins1: A"""""""" }),   Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.74511, longitude:-84.38993, title:""""""""pins1: B"""""""" }), ];   var pins2 = [   Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.390749, longitude:-122.081651, title:""""""""pins2: A"""""""" }),   Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.74511, longitude:-84.38993, title:""""""""pins2: B"""""""" }), ];   var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({     mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE,     animate:true,     userLocation:false,     annotations:pins1 //the initial setup, both pins will handle click events correctly }); mapview.addEventListener('click', function(e) {   Ti.API.log('- mapview click event : ' + e.clicksource); }); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(mapview);     //add a button to change the pins var changePins = Titanium.UI.createButton({     title:'change pins',     style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.BORDERED });   changePins.addEventListener('click',function() {   //removing the initial pins and adding the seconds set - the second pind does not fire the clicked event      mapview.removeAnnotations(pins1);     mapview.addAnnotations(pins2); });   Ti.UI.currentWindow.setToolbar([changePins]);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Removing annotations from MapView breaks map evens
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi,</p> <p>I've outlined the issue on Q&amp;A: <a href= """"""""http://developer.<USER>com/question/26471/mapview-click-event-does-not-fire-after-changing-annotations""""""""> http://developer.<USER>com/question/26471/mapview-click-even...</a>.</p> <p>Calling mapview.removeAnnotations seems to break the mapview 'click' event listener.</p> <p>The following reproduces the issue:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">//create two sets of pins var pins1 = [ Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.390749, longitude:-122.081651, title:""""""""pins1: A"""""""" }), Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.74511, longitude:-84.38993, title:""""""""pins1: B"""""""" }), ]; var pins2 = [ Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.390749, longitude:-122.081651, title:""""""""pins2: A"""""""" }), Titanium.Map.createAnnotation({ latitude:37.74511, longitude:-84.38993, title:""""""""pins2: B"""""""" }), ]; var mapview = Titanium.Map.createView({ mapType: Titanium.Map.STANDARD_TYPE, animate:true, userLocation:false, annotations:pins1 //the initial setup, both pins will handle click events correctly }); mapview.addEventListener('click', function(e) { Ti.API.log('- mapview click event : ' + e.clicksource); }); Ti.UI.currentWindow.add(mapview); //add a button to change the pins var changePins = Titanium.UI.createButton({ title:'change pins', style:Titanium.UI.iPhone.SystemButtonStyle.BORDERED }); changePins.addEventListener('click',function() { //removing the initial pins and adding the seconds set - the second pind does not fire the clicked event mapview.removeAnnotations(pins1); mapview.addAnnotations(pins2); }); Ti.UI.currentWindow.setToolbar([changePins]);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-956,12,"""Toggling views in landscape mode screws up if statusbar toggled too""","""""""{html}<div><p>Drop the following code into app.js: <a href= """"""""http://pastebin.com/7wszjAev"""""""">http://pastebin.com/7wszjAev</a></p> <p>In portrait mode, notice how going back and forth works fine. If you then go to landscape mode and click a button, everything is messed up.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Toggling views in landscape mode screws up if statusbar toggled too
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Drop the following code into app.js: <a href= """"""""http://pastebin.com/7wszjAev"""""""">http://pastebin.com/7wszjAev</a></p> <p>In portrait mode, notice how going back and forth works fine. If you then go to landscape mode and click a button, everything is messed up.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-955,12,"""WebView + addEventListener('swipe', ...) disables scrolling""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi there.</p>  <p>When you add a EventListener for swipe either on a window (with  a webview) or at a webview, it'll disable scrolling the  webView.</p>  <p>Howto reproduce:</p>  <p>1) Create a new project<br>  2) Add a webView to one of the windows (with enough content, so it  scrolls...)<br>  3) Add the EventListener to the window or view  """"""""foo.addEventListener('swipe', function (e) {} )""""""""</p>  <p>Every function will do, even empty ones.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: WebView + addEventListener('swipe', ...) disables scrolling
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi there.</p> <p>When you add a EventListener for swipe either on a window (with a webview) or at a webview, it'll disable scrolling the webView.</p> <p>Howto reproduce:</p> <p>1) Create a new project<br> 2) Add a webView to one of the windows (with enough content, so it scrolls...)<br> 3) Add the EventListener to the window or view """"""""foo.addEventListener('swipe', function (e) {} )""""""""</p> <p>Every function will do, even empty ones.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-954,12,"""cancel-button in searchbar has wrong color""","""""""{html}<div><p>just check """"""""Search Bar"""""""" in KitchenSink where barColor is set to '#000' but the button has this standard blue.<br> this happens only in 1.3, in 1.2 the color of the button was correctly set to the color defined in barColor.<br> tested with Ti developer 1.2.1, mobile sdk 1.3 and SDK 3.1.3 on simulator and device.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: cancel-button in searchbar has wrong color
Description: """"{html}<div><p>just check """"""""Search Bar"""""""" in KitchenSink where barColor is set to '#000' but the button has this standard blue.<br> this happens only in 1.3, in 1.2 the color of the button was correctly set to the color defined in barColor.<br> tested with Ti developer 1.2.1, mobile sdk 1.3 and SDK 3.1.3 on simulator and device.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-953,12,"""allow buttons in toolbars to support any valid color value (instead of just white)""","""""""{html}<div><p>self explanatory</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: allow buttons in toolbars to support any valid color value (instead of just white)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>self explanatory</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-952,12,"""View click event listeners not being invoked on """"empty"""" view space""","""""""{html}<div><p>Fail case: <a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/403933"""""""">http://gist.github.com/403933</a> - the click event only fires if you click into the text field. If you click on an uninhabited portion of the view, you don't get it.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: View click event listeners not being invoked on """"empty"""" view space
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Fail case: <a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/403933"""""""">http://gist.github.com/403933</a> - the click event only fires if you click into the text field. If you click on an uninhabited portion of the view, you don't get it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
