TIMOB-902,12,"""ide integration w/jetbrains""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2306"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2306</a></p> <p>jet brains integration - from ticket: If you guys would create some stub files that expose the API interface, I believe I could include them in the WebStorm IDE. I asked the JetBrains people about this and they replied with this message:</p> <hr> <p>Author: Alexey Gopachenko (neuro159), Message:<br> I suppose the Titanium apps are developed in javascript?<br> You just need to get/create/generate .js file(s) with signatures for the objects/functions you are accessing (I believe that Titanium guys will be easily able to help you with that) and attach it to WebIDE project in any way (i.e. via Settings|Directories).<br> Anyway once you've got the stub files we will be able to help you with setting up our IDE.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: ide integration w/jetbrains
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2306"""""""">http://helpdesk.<USER>net/tickets/2306</a></p> <p>jet brains integration - from ticket: If you guys would create some stub files that expose the API interface, I believe I could include them in the WebStorm IDE. I asked the JetBrains people about this and they replied with this message:</p> <hr> <p>Author: Alexey Gopachenko (neuro159), Message:<br> I suppose the Titanium apps are developed in javascript?<br> You just need to get/create/generate .js file(s) with signatures for the objects/functions you are accessing (I believe that Titanium guys will be easily able to help you with that) and attach it to WebIDE project in any way (i.e. via Settings|Directories).<br> Anyway once you've got the stub files we will be able to help you with setting up our IDE.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
