TIMOB-888,12,"""Android: ImageView Filled from Remote Source Cycles through multiples""","""""""{html}<div><p>Basically, in a tableview since items are reused, the background tasks used to download the images, update when they're done. The effect is to have a mini slideshow in an imageview..this isn't the desired effect.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: ImageView Filled from Remote Source Cycles through multiples
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Basically, in a tableview since items are reused, the background tasks used to download the images, update when they're done. The effect is to have a mini slideshow in an imageview..this isn't the desired effect.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-887,12,"""tableView (auto-height) rows with labels containing unicode ""","""""""{html}<div><p>tableView (auto-height) rows with labels containing unicode characters seems to be calculating the height incorrectly.</p> <p>I've noticed since a recent build of 1.3.0 that the rows seems to 'animate' to their required height as the table displays.</p> <p>Some rows with unicode characters in the labels (with are themselves within a view within the row) do not appear to have the height set correctly.</p> <p>This then manifests itself further with subsequent rows.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: tableView (auto-height) rows with labels containing unicode
Description: """"{html}<div><p>tableView (auto-height) rows with labels containing unicode characters seems to be calculating the height incorrectly.</p> <p>I've noticed since a recent build of 1.3.0 that the rows seems to 'animate' to their required height as the table displays.</p> <p>Some rows with unicode characters in the labels (with are themselves within a view within the row) do not appear to have the height set correctly.</p> <p>This then manifests itself further with subsequent rows.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
