TIMOB-851,12,"""textfield focus disables gesture and orientation events""","""""""{html}<div><p>On iPhone,<br> When we focus a textfield the Titanium.Gesture events ( shake, orientationchange ) does not fire anymore.<br> Even if we """"""""blur"""""""" the textfield or try to recreate the gesture event, it won't fire anymore.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: textfield focus disables gesture and orientation events
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On iPhone,<br> When we focus a textfield the Titanium.Gesture events ( shake, orientationchange ) does not fire anymore.<br> Even if we """"""""blur"""""""" the textfield or try to recreate the gesture event, it won't fire anymore.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-850,12,"""HTTPClient keep-alive connections""","""""""{html}<div><p>hi,</p> <p>Currently there is no way to create a keep-alive connections using Titanium.Network.HTTPClient</p> <p>This is a MUST in cases where the Server response is chunked (Transfer-Encoding: chunked)</p> <p>This is very urgent - for cases such as returning large JSON Strings etc.</p> <p>Also - using keep alive-alive connections can boost performance since the OS can reuse the connection.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: HTTPClient keep-alive connections
Description: """"{html}<div><p>hi,</p> <p>Currently there is no way to create a keep-alive connections using Titanium.Network.HTTPClient</p> <p>This is a MUST in cases where the Server response is chunked (Transfer-Encoding: chunked)</p> <p>This is very urgent - for cases such as returning large JSON Strings etc.</p> <p>Also - using keep alive-alive connections can boost performance since the OS can reuse the connection.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
