TIMOB-640,12,"""Only first webview is visible in scrollable views ""","""""""{html}<div><p>If adding more than one web view to a scrollable view, only the first web view is shown.</p> <p>This appear to be a new in 1.1.2</p> <p>var wv1 = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'<a href= """"""""http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/terror.html'})"""""""">http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/terror.html'})</a>;<br> var wv2 = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'<a href= """"""""http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/naboer.html'})"""""""">http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/naboer.html'})</a>;<br> &nbsp;<br> var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({views:[wv1,wv2],showPagingControl:false});<br> &nbsp;<br> win.add(scrollView);<br> win.show(scrollView);</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Only first webview is visible in scrollable views
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If adding more than one web view to a scrollable view, only the first web view is shown.</p> <p>This appear to be a new in 1.1.2</p> <p>var wv1 = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'<a href= """"""""http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/terror.html'})"""""""">http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/terror.html'})</a>;<br> var wv2 = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'<a href= """"""""http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/naboer.html'})"""""""">http://www.thorson.dk/saxotimes/naboer.html'})</a>;<br> &nbsp;<br> var scrollView = Titanium.UI.createScrollableView({views:[wv1,wv2],showPagingControl:false});<br> &nbsp;<br> win.add(scrollView);<br> win.show(scrollView);</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-639,12,"""Crash with createButtonBar on Android Simulator""","""""""{html}<div><p>//Titanium version 1.1.2</p> <p>I have a NullPointerExeption when I created a ButtonBar in app.js :</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var buttonBar = Titanium.UI.createButtonBar({id:'buttonbar', labels:['Left', 'Right'],backgroundColor:'#336699'});</p> <p>//button Bar is null</p> <p>buttonBar.addEventListener('click',function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog(); a.setTitle('Buttonbar Test'); a.setMessage('You click button index = ' + e.index); a.show();</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(buttonBar);</p> <p>win.open();</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Crash with createButtonBar on Android Simulator
Description: """"{html}<div><p>//Titanium version 1.1.2</p> <p>I have a NullPointerExeption when I created a ButtonBar in app.js :</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br></p> <pre> <code>title:'Tab 1', backgroundColor:'#fff'</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>var buttonBar = Titanium.UI.createButtonBar({id:'buttonbar', labels:['Left', 'Right'],backgroundColor:'#336699'});</p> <p>//button Bar is null</p> <p>buttonBar.addEventListener('click',function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>var a = Titanium.UI.createAlertDialog(); a.setTitle('Buttonbar Test'); a.setMessage('You click button index = ' + e.index); a.show();</code> </pre> <p>});</p> <p>win.add(buttonBar);</p> <p>win.open();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-638,12,"""Dropping first (Table)view when ScrollView has more than 3 views""","""""""{html}<div><p>When constructing a scrollView containing one Tableview followed by 2 ordinary views all was well.</p> <p>When a fourth view was added, scrolling to the third and back is OK, but scrolling to the fourth and back to the first: the tableview has been dropped.</p> <p>example app.js attached to aid reproduction and diagnosis.</p> <p>cheers,<br> <USER></p> <p>P.S<br> Mac OSX 10.6.2 iPhone SDK 3.1.3, Ti Mobile 1.0.0</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Dropping first (Table)view when ScrollView has more than 3 views
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When constructing a scrollView containing one Tableview followed by 2 ordinary views all was well.</p> <p>When a fourth view was added, scrolling to the third and back is OK, but scrolling to the fourth and back to the first: the tableview has been dropped.</p> <p>example app.js attached to aid reproduction and diagnosis.</p> <p>cheers,<br> <USER></p> <p>P.S<br> Mac OSX 10.6.2 iPhone SDK 3.1.3, Ti Mobile 1.0.0</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
