TIMOB-566,12,"""KitchenSink crashes on device when not in USB debugging mode (ANDROID)""","""""""{html}<div><p>If your phone has USB debugging turned on, it does not crash and works great. But as soon as you turn off USB debugging, i can reliably crash the app every time.</p> <p>Base UI &gt; Window (Standalone) &gt; Open (plain)</p> <p>Unfortunately due to the nature of the crash (doesnt happen in debug mode) i can provide no trace log.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: KitchenSink crashes on device when not in USB debugging mode (ANDROID)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If your phone has USB debugging turned on, it does not crash and works great. But as soon as you turn off USB debugging, i can reliably crash the app every time.</p> <p>Base UI &gt; Window (Standalone) &gt; Open (plain)</p> <p>Unfortunately due to the nature of the crash (doesnt happen in debug mode) i can provide no trace log.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-565,12,"""XML getElementsByTagName(""""*"""") not working anymore since 0.9.1""","""""""{html}<div><p>To iterate within a TiDOMNodeList, the function getElementsByTagName(""""""""*"""""""") used to work in 0.9.1<br> Nevertheless, it did not work anymore since 0.9.1 (nor in 0.9.3 neither in 1.0.0).</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: XML getElementsByTagName(""""*"""") not working anymore since 0.9.1
Description: """"{html}<div><p>To iterate within a TiDOMNodeList, the function getElementsByTagName(""""""""*"""""""") used to work in 0.9.1<br> Nevertheless, it did not work anymore since 0.9.1 (nor in 0.9.3 neither in 1.0.0).</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-564,12,"""Accuracy of compass and accelerometer""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hi, I'm working on augmented reality, so I need to use accelerometer and compass features.<br> The problem is the measurement accuracy. The measurement difference of the accelerometer with a little movement of the iPhone it's about 2-3%, while in other application like AroundMe or iHandyLevel it seems to be more accurate. Is it possible to change/increase the accuracy on iPhone? Thanks a lot, Flavio</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Accuracy of compass and accelerometer
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hi, I'm working on augmented reality, so I need to use accelerometer and compass features.<br> The problem is the measurement accuracy. The measurement difference of the accelerometer with a little movement of the iPhone it's about 2-3%, while in other application like AroundMe or iHandyLevel it seems to be more accurate. Is it possible to change/increase the accuracy on iPhone? Thanks a lot, Flavio</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-563,12,"""imageView scaling issues""","""""""{html}<div><p>An imageView can no longer scale up larger than it's original size.</p> <p>The imageView itself gets bigger, but the contained image never scales up to a set .width or .height</p> <p>It seems to be able to scale down but since the latest builds it can no longer scale larger.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: imageView scaling issues
Description: """"{html}<div><p>An imageView can no longer scale up larger than it's original size.</p> <p>The imageView itself gets bigger, but the contained image never scales up to a set .width or .height</p> <p>It seems to be able to scale down but since the latest builds it can no longer scale larger.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-562,12,"""Titanium.UI.Label incorrectly reports width in size.height property""","""""""{html}<div><p>See the following code:</p> <pre> <code>var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({     text:'some text',     font:{fontSize:14},     height:20,     width:300,     left:10 }); Ti.API.info(""""""""label.size.height = """""""" + label.size.height); Ti.API.info(""""""""label.size.width = """""""" + label.size.width);</code> </pre> <p>Output is:<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> label.size.height = 300 <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> label.size.width = 300</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.UI.Label incorrectly reports width in size.height property
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See the following code:</p> <pre> <code>var label = Ti.UI.createLabel({ text:'some text', font:{fontSize:14}, height:20, width:300, left:10 }); Ti.API.info(""""""""label.size.height = """""""" + label.size.height); Ti.API.info(""""""""label.size.width = """""""" + label.size.width);</code> </pre> <p>Output is:<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> label.size.height = 300 <a href= """"""""/projects/32238/changesets/INFO"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [INFO]"""""""">[INFO]</a> label.size.width = 300</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-561,12,"""Request:  ability to open DB from any path and filename""","""""""{html}<div><p>We often need to download database files and store them in the appDataDirectory. It would be nice if we could simply call DB.open(""""""""filename"""""""") and pass a fully-qualified path and filename to the database.</p> <p>We should not be required to place databases in a specific folder, nor should we be forced to append a """""""".sql"""""""" extension to the end of a database filename.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Request: ability to open DB from any path and filename
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We often need to download database files and store them in the appDataDirectory. It would be nice if we could simply call DB.open(""""""""filename"""""""") and pass a fully-qualified path and filename to the database.</p> <p>We should not be required to place databases in a specific folder, nor should we be forced to append a """""""".sql"""""""" extension to the end of a database filename.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-560,12,"""Downloading large files with Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient crashes""","""""""{html}<div><p>When files are downloaded via Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(), data is stored in memory before the file is written to """"""""disk"""""""". If a file is too large (over a few megs) this causes the app to crash.</p> <p>See example in Kitchen Sink source code file: xhr_filedownload.js</p> <p>(To duplicate, simply replace the download filename here with the name of a large, remote file. Start downloading, and wait a few minutes. An out-of-memory error will show up in the trace.)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Downloading large files with Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient crashes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When files are downloaded via Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient(), data is stored in memory before the file is written to """"""""disk"""""""". If a file is too large (over a few megs) this causes the app to crash.</p> <p>See example in Kitchen Sink source code file: xhr_filedownload.js</p> <p>(To duplicate, simply replace the download filename here with the name of a large, remote file. Start downloading, and wait a few minutes. An out-of-memory error will show up in the trace.)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-557,12,"""Android: Window Title Not Set""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/2357-android-window-title-not-set""""""""> Support Item</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Window Title Not Set
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/2357-android-window-title-not-set""""""""> Support Item</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-556,12,"""createSoundPlayer doesn't work on Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>I tried to stream audio from web server (Jamendo here) on Android plateform. Titanium says:</p> <p>java.lang.ClassNotFoundException: ti.modules.titanium.media.SoundPlayerProxy</p> <p>I cannot try on iPhone... no Mac... no iPhone...</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: createSoundPlayer doesn't work on Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I tried to stream audio from web server (Jamendo here) on Android plateform. Titanium says:</p> <p>java.lang.ClassNotFoundException: ti.modules.titanium.media.SoundPlayerProxy</p> <p>I cannot try on iPhone... no Mac... no iPhone...</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-555,12,"""Android: focus/blur data on tab change is incorrect""","""""""{html}<div><p>The tabchange event comes long after the focus/blur occurs. This wasn't a problem before 0.9 because tabchange was separate from focus/blur.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: focus/blur data on tab change is incorrect
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The tabchange event comes long after the focus/blur occurs. This wasn't a problem before 0.9 because tabchange was separate from focus/blur.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
