TIMOB-549,12,"""titleControls move to top left after changing tabs (also occurs in KS)""","""""""{html}<div><p>In KS:</p> <p>Go to:</p> <p>Base UI &gt; Window Navbar</p> <p>Click Title Control (you should see the switch in the navbar title)</p> <p>Now click on another tab : Controls.</p> <p>Now click back to the Base UI tab.</p> <p>The switch is now stuck up in the top left corner.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: titleControls move to top left after changing tabs (also occurs in KS)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In KS:</p> <p>Go to:</p> <p>Base UI &gt; Window Navbar</p> <p>Click Title Control (you should see the switch in the navbar title)</p> <p>Now click on another tab : Controls.</p> <p>Now click back to the Base UI tab.</p> <p>The switch is now stuck up in the top left corner.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-548,12,"""Impossible to load any Application example for version 0.8 and 0.9.x with Titanium 1.0""","""""""{html}<div><p>Hello Guys, How are you today ? Me very Bad :(</p> <p>Nowadays, I am trying to develop a little application for iPad with Titanium 1.0 (+ Apple SDK 3.2).</p> <p>I created an application """"""""Test"""""""" just to see if everything work very well with a last version of Titanium (1.0). Unfortunately, when I double click on the icon of my test application, it doesn't arrive at the end and I have again the home screen of my iPad (emulator).</p> <p>When I use the same environment (Titanium 1.0 + Apple SDK 3.2 beta) to laod some applications examples wrote with titanium version 0.9.x (Example - The Kitchen Sink), they don't work. I have to use Titanium 1.0 + release apple SDK include between 3.1 and 3.1.2 if I want to run the Titanium applications examples.</p> <p>However, since my update to Titanium 1.0 and my update to Apple SDK 3.2 that include some improve for iPad Development, the url param seems to be depreciated when I write:</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({url:'index.html'});<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> url not supported in a window. index.html --</p> <p>Please, Could You Help me ?</p> <p>All my apologies for the quality of my English because it isn't my mother tongue. I speak French :)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Impossible to load any Application example for version 0.8 and 0.9.x with Titanium 1.0
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Hello Guys, How are you today ? Me very Bad :(</p> <p>Nowadays, I am trying to develop a little application for iPad with Titanium 1.0 (+ Apple SDK 3.2).</p> <p>I created an application """"""""Test"""""""" just to see if everything work very well with a last version of Titanium (1.0). Unfortunately, when I double click on the icon of my test application, it doesn't arrive at the end and I have again the home screen of my iPad (emulator).</p> <p>When I use the same environment (Titanium 1.0 + Apple SDK 3.2 beta) to laod some applications examples wrote with titanium version 0.9.x (Example - The Kitchen Sink), they don't work. I have to use Titanium 1.0 + release apple SDK include between 3.1 and 3.1.2 if I want to run the Titanium applications examples.</p> <p>However, since my update to Titanium 1.0 and my update to Apple SDK 3.2 that include some improve for iPad Development, the url param seems to be depreciated when I write:</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({url:'index.html'});<br> <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/changesets/ERROR"""""""" title= """"""""Changeset [ERROR]"""""""">[ERROR]</a> url not supported in a window. index.html --</p> <p>Please, Could You Help me ?</p> <p>All my apologies for the quality of my English because it isn't my mother tongue. I speak French :)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-547,12,"""control over web view contents""","""""""{html}<div><p>A feature has been requested for web views that display external web content - would like to be able to reload/cancel the content, go forward and back - generally have more granular control over the contents of the web view and being able to modify that dynamically. An example of the level of control desired would be the external link viewer in the Twitterrific Twitter client.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: control over web view contents
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A feature has been requested for web views that display external web content - would like to be able to reload/cancel the content, go forward and back - generally have more granular control over the contents of the web view and being able to modify that dynamically. An example of the level of control desired would be the external link viewer in the Twitterrific Twitter client.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
