TIMOB-504,12,"""auto focus textarea on window open has slight up/down motion after focus""","""""""{html}<div><p>here's the code (put into an app.js)</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br> backgroundColor:'#ccc' });</p> <p>var textarea = Titanium.UI.createTextArea({<br> left: 10, top: 40, width: 100, height: 100, });</p> <p>win.add(textarea);</p> <p>win.addEventListener('open', function()<br> {</p> <pre> <code>    textarea.focus();</code> </pre> <p>}) win.open();</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: auto focus textarea on window open has slight up/down motion after focus
Description: """"{html}<div><p>here's the code (put into an app.js)</p> <p>var win = Titanium.UI.createWindow({<br> backgroundColor:'#ccc' });</p> <p>var textarea = Titanium.UI.createTextArea({<br> left: 10, top: 40, width: 100, height: 100, });</p> <p>win.add(textarea);</p> <p>win.addEventListener('open', function()<br> {</p> <pre> <code> textarea.focus();</code> </pre> <p>}) win.open();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-503,12,"""Titanium.include path not relative to file calling it 0.9.2""","""""""{html}<div><p>When you use Titanium.include from script that was itself included, the path is computed as if you called Titanium.include from the originating script.</p> <p>Assuming these files:</p> <pre> <code>Folder1 -&gt; OriginalScript.js  Folder2 -&gt; Include1.js -&gt; Include2.js</code> </pre> <p>If from OriginalScript.js you call Titanium.include(""""""""../Folder2/Include1.js"""""""") and then from Include1.js you call Titanium(""""""""Include2.js""""""""), it will fail to find Include1.js because it is looking in Folder1.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.include path not relative to file calling it 0.9.2
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When you use Titanium.include from script that was itself included, the path is computed as if you called Titanium.include from the originating script.</p> <p>Assuming these files:</p> <pre> <code>Folder1 -&gt; OriginalScript.js Folder2 -&gt; Include1.js -&gt; Include2.js</code> </pre> <p>If from OriginalScript.js you call Titanium.include(""""""""../Folder2/Include1.js"""""""") and then from Include1.js you call Titanium(""""""""Include2.js""""""""), it will fail to find Include1.js because it is looking in Folder1.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
