TIMOB-388,12,"""Version info in website / download process""","""""""{html}<div><p>The <USER>com site doesn't give any indication of exactly what one receives when clicking the """"""""DOWNLOAD TITANIUM"""""""" link. The result page also has no version or file info. The dmg file has no version info in its filename, and upon mounting and opening, there's no readme file or other way I could see to determine exactly what I'd downloaded. The only option seems to be to install the program.</p> <p>Somewhere (preferably before starting the download) this info should be displayed.</p> <p>My use case: When I start Titanium Developer, I see a message about version numbers at the top of the window. (screenshot) I don't quite understand if it's correct, and want to verify if I have the latest version installed. Due to the lack of displayed version info, I'm unable to.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Version info in website / download process
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The <USER>com site doesn't give any indication of exactly what one receives when clicking the """"""""DOWNLOAD TITANIUM"""""""" link. The result page also has no version or file info. The dmg file has no version info in its filename, and upon mounting and opening, there's no readme file or other way I could see to determine exactly what I'd downloaded. The only option seems to be to install the program.</p> <p>Somewhere (preferably before starting the download) this info should be displayed.</p> <p>My use case: When I start Titanium Developer, I see a message about version numbers at the top of the window. (screenshot) I don't quite understand if it's correct, and want to verify if I have the latest version installed. Due to the lack of displayed version info, I'm unable to.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-387,12,"""Android Notification""","""""""{html}<div><p>Add the functionality to create an android background service in order for an application to add notifications to the Android notification bar when it is minimised in the background.</p> <p>E.g.</p> <p>Scan the current gps location and if in range show a notification.</p> <p>Thanks</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Notification
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Add the functionality to create an android background service in order for an application to add notifications to the Android notification bar when it is minimised in the background.</p> <p>E.g.</p> <p>Scan the current gps location and if in range show a notification.</p> <p>Thanks</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-386,12,"""Local phone number issue: Titanium.Platform.phoneNumber does not work (ver 0.8.2)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Here's the code I am using:</p> <p><br> <br> <br> function helloJS(){<br></p> <pre> <code>document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML=''; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.model; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.version; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.availableMemory; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.ostype; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.architecture; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.phoneNumber; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;"""""""";</code> </pre> <p>}<br> <br> <br></p> <br> <br> <p>I compiled and installed the app on my iphone and I get the following output:</p> <p>iPhone 3GS<br> 3.1.2<br> 9.6171875<br> 32bit<br> arm<br> undefined</p> <p>So, apparently, all properties under Titanium.Platform work fine EXCEPT phoneNumber.<br> The simulator shows the same result.<br> Is there anybody experiencing the same issue?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Local phone number issue: Titanium.Platform.phoneNumber does not work (ver 0.8.2)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Here's the code I am using:</p> <p><br> <br> <br> function helloJS(){<br></p> <pre> <code>document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML=''; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.model; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.version; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.availableMemory; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.ostype; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.architecture; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;""""""""; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=Titanium.Platform.phoneNumber; document.getElementById('table0').innerHTML+=""""""""&lt;br&gt;"""""""";</code> </pre> <p>}<br> <br> <br></p> <br> <br> <p>I compiled and installed the app on my iphone and I get the following output:</p> <p>iPhone 3GS<br> 3.1.2<br> 9.6171875<br> 32bit<br> arm<br> undefined</p> <p>So, apparently, all properties under Titanium.Platform work fine EXCEPT phoneNumber.<br> The simulator shows the same result.<br> Is there anybody experiencing the same issue?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-385,12,"""iPhone : height of a TableView""","""""""{html}<div><p>The height of the Table view (the view !) did not work whith the new version of Titanium : <USER>titanium_mobile-cf7d3d6</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone : height of a TableView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The height of the Table view (the view !) did not work whith the new version of Titanium : <USER>titanium_mobile-cf7d3d6</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-384,12,"""TableView loading/displaying data is slow.""","""""""{html}<div><p>I and another developer would like the native table widget to load &amp; display (""""""""render""""""""?) data faster. For example, I have a search screen, which queries a sqlite database with each 'change' event. The database i/o and query time doesn't seem to be an issue. (Subjective impression, haven't definitively determined this.) In my app, I need to limit the SELECT results to 5 rows in order to make the interaction speed acceptable on an iphone gs.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView loading/displaying data is slow.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I and another developer would like the native table widget to load &amp; display (""""""""render""""""""?) data faster. For example, I have a search screen, which queries a sqlite database with each 'change' event. The database i/o and query time doesn't seem to be an issue. (Subjective impression, haven't definitively determined this.) In my app, I need to limit the SELECT results to 5 rows in order to make the interaction speed acceptable on an iphone gs.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-383,12,"""Android: SDCard targeting Network Location""","""""""{html}<div><p>On Windows if <code>%HOMEDRIVE%</code> and <code>%HOMEPATH%</code> don't match <code>%USERPROFILE%</code> then the AVD will fail to load.</p> <p>Marshall has already pushed the fix for 0.9. Testing patch for 0.8 users.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: SDCard targeting Network Location
Description: """"{html}<div><p>On Windows if <code>%HOMEDRIVE%</code> and <code>%HOMEPATH%</code> don't match <code>%USERPROFILE%</code> then the AVD will fail to load.</p> <p>Marshall has already pushed the fix for 0.9. Testing patch for 0.8 users.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-382,12,"""Titanium.Database.install Options to Force Rewrite on sql File""","""""""{html}<div><p>It'd be great if the install can overwrite the writable sqlite3 db file with a given option.</p> <p>Changes made to the schema of a database change a lot while on development, and it seems that the install method would just use the existing one if it already exists.</p> <p>Proposed implementation:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, options);</code> </pre> <p>Where options, for now, has the following options:<br> <strong>force</strong> {boolean} Overwrites target name when true. Defaults to false.</p> <p>The following code will use the target_name, not replace it:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name); Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, {}); Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, { force: false });</code> </pre> <p>The following code will replace target_name with resource_name<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, { force: true });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.Database.install Options to Force Rewrite on sql File
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It'd be great if the install can overwrite the writable sqlite3 db file with a given option.</p> <p>Changes made to the schema of a database change a lot while on development, and it seems that the install method would just use the existing one if it already exists.</p> <p>Proposed implementation:</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, options);</code> </pre> <p>Where options, for now, has the following options:<br> <strong>force</strong> {boolean} Overwrites target name when true. Defaults to false.</p> <p>The following code will use the target_name, not replace it:<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name); Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, {}); Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, { force: false });</code> </pre> <p>The following code will replace target_name with resource_name<br></p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.Database.install(resource_name, target_name, { force: true });</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-381,12,"""Implement Titanium.Network.createHTTPServer for Titanium Mobile""","""""""{html}<div><p>I think it would be great to have  Titanium.Network.createHTTPServer implemented for Titanium  Mobile</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Implement Titanium.Network.createHTTPServer for Titanium Mobile
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I think it would be great to have Titanium.Network.createHTTPServer implemented for Titanium Mobile</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-380,12,"""Would like API access to toolbar, tabbar and navbar colors.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently, it seems that the API only allows """"""""barColor"""""""" to be set, which sets both the toolbar and the navbar, and does not affect the tabbar.</p> <p>However, it'd be a real advantage to be able to set these three colors individually. I've attached a screenshot of a well designed app showing a subtle shade difference between the navbar and the tabbar which contributes to the graphic design.</p> <p>I'm using a similar design for an app, and when I set the barColor, the toolBar is too """"""""bright"""""""". (Since it's lower on the page, it should be darker - in my design.)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Would like API access to toolbar, tabbar and navbar colors.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently, it seems that the API only allows """"""""barColor"""""""" to be set, which sets both the toolbar and the navbar, and does not affect the tabbar.</p> <p>However, it'd be a real advantage to be able to set these three colors individually. I've attached a screenshot of a well designed app showing a subtle shade difference between the navbar and the tabbar which contributes to the graphic design.</p> <p>I'm using a similar design for an app, and when I set the barColor, the toolBar is too """"""""bright"""""""". (Since it's lower on the page, it should be darker - in my design.)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-379,12,"""Search bar: only show cancel button when search input has the focus.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Enhancement suggestion: Currently, when cancel is 'true', the cancel button is always displayed. It's disabled if the search input doesn't have the focus.</p> <p>I believe that a different behavior would create a cleaner UI: Make the cancel button invisible instead of disabled when the search bar doesn't have the focus. On the iPhone platform, the disabled state is still somewhat 'active'-looking. The presence of the disabled button is also unnecessary clutter.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Search bar: only show cancel button when search input has the focus.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Enhancement suggestion: Currently, when cancel is 'true', the cancel button is always displayed. It's disabled if the search input doesn't have the focus.</p> <p>I believe that a different behavior would create a cleaner UI: Make the cancel button invisible instead of disabled when the search bar doesn't have the focus. On the iPhone platform, the disabled state is still somewhat 'active'-looking. The presence of the disabled button is also unnecessary clutter.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-378,12,"""EmailDialog - crashes w/ newlines in message body""","""""""{html}<div><p>Steps to reproduce:</p> <p>ed.setMessageBody(""""""""Hello \n\n there""""""""); // Same effect with single quotes.<br> ed.open();</p> <p>For me this is a blocker for using the EmailDialog: I need some way to do a bare minimum of formatting of the email message body.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: EmailDialog - crashes w/ newlines in message body
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Steps to reproduce:</p> <p>ed.setMessageBody(""""""""Hello \n\n there""""""""); // Same effect with single quotes.<br> ed.open();</p> <p>For me this is a blocker for using the EmailDialog: I need some way to do a bare minimum of formatting of the email message body.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-377,12,"""Android: getList returns String""","""""""{html}<div><p>See support item <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1463-titaniumapppropertiesgetlist-issue""""""""> Titanium.App.Properties.getList issue</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: getList returns String
