TIMOB-376,12,"""E-Mail client - place focus on field""","""""""{html}<div><p>A request has been made to put focus on specific fields in the e-mail client so the user could begin typing in the field in question immediately - here's the support ticket on the topic:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1441-createemaildialog-focusing-subject-or-body""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1441-createemai...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: E-Mail client - place focus on field
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A request has been made to put focus on specific fields in the e-mail client so the user could begin typing in the field in question immediately - here's the support ticket on the topic:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1441-createemaildialog-focusing-subject-or-body""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1441-createemai...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-375,12,"""Access to camera as a barcode reader""","""""""{html}<div><p>Google have open source libraries to do this (QR Codes), would be nice to see this accessible in Titanium</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Access to camera as a barcode reader
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Google have open source libraries to do this (QR Codes), would be nice to see this accessible in Titanium</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-374,12,"""getBadge as companion to setBadge""","""""""{html}<div><p>Would be good to be able to retrieve the current badge value in an iPhone app for a tab. We have <code>setBadge</code> - maybe add a <code>getBadge</code> also? Here's the community thread for reference:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/429-get-value-of-tab-badge""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: getBadge as companion to setBadge
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Would be good to be able to retrieve the current badge value in an iPhone app for a tab. We have <code>setBadge</code> - maybe add a <code>getBadge</code> also? Here's the community thread for reference:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/429-get-value-of-tab-badge""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-373,12,"""Android: HTTPClient.DONE is missing.""","""""""{html}<div><p>Define DONE on a returned HTTPClient. See <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1395-xhrdone-not-working-on-android""""""""> Support Item</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient.DONE is missing.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Define DONE on a returned HTTPClient. See <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1395-xhrdone-not-working-on-android""""""""> Support Item</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-372,12,"""iPhone: Titanium.UI.TextField.getValue is documented but does not work""","""""""{html}<div><p>Although there is <a href= """"""""http://www.codestrong.com/timobile/api/titanium/UI/TextField/getValue/""""""""> documentation for .getValue() on a TextField</a> this method does not work, results in """"""""[undefined] is not a function"""""""".</p> <p>This method is not used in the KitchenSink either.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Titanium.UI.TextField.getValue is documented but does not work
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Although there is <a href= """"""""http://www.codestrong.com/timobile/api/titanium/UI/TextField/getValue/""""""""> documentation for .getValue() on a TextField</a> this method does not work, results in """"""""[undefined] is not a function"""""""".</p> <p>This method is not used in the KitchenSink either.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-371,12,"""Composite View Y Position [iPhone]""","""""""{html}<div><p>have created a composite view with webviews<br> wanting scrollable page with custom header/footer<br> scrollable view centres to screen instead of using y value in setup object</p> <p>eg.<br> var ViewBack = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'ViewBack.html'});<br> var ViewText = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'ViewText.html'});</p> <p>var compositeViewAbout = Titanium.UI.createCompositeView();<br> compositeViewAbout.addView(ViewBack,{x:0,y:0,width:320,height:460,zIndex:1});<br> compositeViewAbout.addView(ViewText,{x:0,y:80,width:320,height:340,zIndex:2});</p> <p>all works fine the ViewText view scrolls - just that ViewText view centres to screen - not at 80.<br> is there a way to resolve this?</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Composite View Y Position [iPhone]
Description: """"{html}<div><p>have created a composite view with webviews<br> wanting scrollable page with custom header/footer<br> scrollable view centres to screen instead of using y value in setup object</p> <p>eg.<br> var ViewBack = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'ViewBack.html'});<br> var ViewText = Titanium.UI.createWebView({url:'ViewText.html'});</p> <p>var compositeViewAbout = Titanium.UI.createCompositeView();<br> compositeViewAbout.addView(ViewBack,{x:0,y:0,width:320,height:460,zIndex:1});<br> compositeViewAbout.addView(ViewText,{x:0,y:80,width:320,height:340,zIndex:2});</p> <p>all works fine the ViewText view scrolls - just that ViewText view centres to screen - not at 80.<br> is there a way to resolve this?</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-370,12,"""iPhone: Activity indicator dialog""","""""""{html}<div><p>Often when waiting for a server response you want to stop the user in their tracks and present a 'Loading' dialog with activity indicator.</p> <p>Attached image as an example.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Activity indicator dialog
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Often when waiting for a server response you want to stop the user in their tracks and present a 'Loading' dialog with activity indicator.</p> <p>Attached image as an example.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-369,12,"""iOS: Search bar - return button strangeness""","""""""{html}<div><p>In the Kitchen Sink custom table view example (the Facebook  knock off), when you search the table view and press """"""""Search"""""""", the  return key displays the text """"""""return"""""""" for maybe a split second.  Easy to miss, but it definitely happens - I noticed it on my iPhone  3G, and it was reported by a community member as well.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: Search bar - return button strangeness
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In the Kitchen Sink custom table view example (the Facebook knock off), when you search the table view and press """"""""Search"""""""", the return key displays the text """"""""return"""""""" for maybe a split second. Easy to miss, but it definitely happens - I noticed it on my iPhone 3G, and it was reported by a community member as well.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-368,12,"""Scrolling search bar and table view""","""""""{html}<div><p>In the Kitchen Sink, check out the custom table view (the Facebook knock off) and search the table. When the search bar come up, you can flick and scroll it and the underlying native table view. This has been confirmed on iPhone.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Scrolling search bar and table view
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In the Kitchen Sink, check out the custom table view (the Facebook knock off) and search the table. When the search bar come up, you can flick and scroll it and the underlying native table view. This has been confirmed on iPhone.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-367,12,"""Android: Remove padding in TableView with SearchBar""","""""""{html}<div><p>Remove the non-configurable padding from TableView when SearchBar is enabled.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Remove padding in TableView with SearchBar
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Remove the non-configurable padding from TableView when SearchBar is enabled.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-366,12,"""Titanium.Database.execute should support indexed arguments in an array ""","""""""{html}<div><p>.execute(sql, args) currently does not support .execute(string, array), which would come in very handy in certain cases. As I understand, the Desktop version already supports that way of calling execute, at least when I read the comments in Ticket 146 (<a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/25719/tickets/146"""""""">https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/25719/tickets/146</a>) in Titanium Desktop. So it should be doable.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.Database.execute should support indexed arguments in an array
Description: """"{html}<div><p>.execute(sql, args) currently does not support .execute(string, array), which would come in very handy in certain cases. As I understand, the Desktop version already supports that way of calling execute, at least when I read the comments in Ticket 146 (<a href= """"""""https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/25719/tickets/146"""""""">https://<USER>lighthouseapp.com/projects/25719/tickets/146</a>) in Titanium Desktop. So it should be doable.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-365,12,"""No XML content is readable in Titanium 0.8.1""","""""""{html}<div><p>I've tried numerous XML-spitting services and flat XML files, and none is readable by the 0.8.1 HTTPClient - here's a simple test case to reproduce:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/795397"""""""">http://pastie.org/795397</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: No XML content is readable in Titanium 0.8.1
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I've tried numerous XML-spitting services and flat XML files, and none is readable by the 0.8.1 HTTPClient - here's a simple test case to reproduce:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/795397"""""""">http://pastie.org/795397</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-364,12,"""Enable Transactions for Titanium.Database (Mobile)""","""""""{html}<div><p>It would be very helpful if Transactions were enabled in Titanium.Database (Mobile) -- be it by exposing/wrapping the PLSQLite Transaction methods in Titanium.Database or by allowing the corresponding SQLite SQL Statements (BEGIN; ROLLBACK; COMMIT)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Enable Transactions for Titanium.Database (Mobile)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>It would be very helpful if Transactions were enabled in Titanium.Database (Mobile) -- be it by exposing/wrapping the PLSQLite Transaction methods in Titanium.Database or by allowing the corresponding SQLite SQL Statements (BEGIN; ROLLBACK; COMMIT)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-363,12,"""Full screen splash image""","""""""{html}<div><p>A community member has commented that it would be nice to have a full-screen splash image for an app while it is loading (i.e. hide the status bar). As of 0.8.1 I don't think this is possible. Here's the original thread:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1304-splash-screen-and-status-bar""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1304-splash-scr...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Full screen splash image
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A community member has commented that it would be nice to have a full-screen splash image for an app while it is loading (i.e. hide the status bar). As of 0.8.1 I don't think this is possible. Here's the original thread:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1304-splash-screen-and-status-bar""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1304-splash-scr...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-362,12,"""Layout lost when filtering table view""","""""""{html}<div><p>When using the search feature for table views, any custom filtering/formatting is lost. A few community members have commented on this, including in this issue:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1156-layout-template-lost-from-searchbar-results""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1156-layout-tem...</a></p> <p>Logging an issue here to decide whether or not we want to support keeping table view row layouts in the filtering view.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Layout lost when filtering table view
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When using the search feature for table views, any custom filtering/formatting is lost. A few community members have commented on this, including in this issue:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1156-layout-template-lost-from-searchbar-results""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1156-layout-tem...</a></p> <p>Logging an issue here to decide whether or not we want to support keeping table view row layouts in the filtering view.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-361,12,"""Keyboard toolbar issues""","""""""{html}<div><p>The attached Titanium project shows two issues:</p> <p>One:<br> If the keyboardToolbarHeight value is set greater then 30 the keyboard does not resize correctly in landscape view. If you set this value to 30 it seems to be alright. You can see this in the attached example or in the kitchensink demo.<br> 1) On the index.html page in the iPhone simulator rotate to the right (or left)<br> 2) Press the button<br> 3) You will see the keyboard layout issue. This only happens if the keyboardToolbarHeight value is greater then 30.</p> <p>Two:<br> In landscape view the textArea seems to set the focus at the bottom of the control. When you type you can not see what you are typing without scrolling to the top of the control. Is there anyway that the focus could be set to the top of the control when in landscape mode? The attached same shows this behavior in landscape mode. You can also see this behavior in the Text Fields example in the kitchenSink demo.</p> <p>Community Thread:<br> <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1209-textarea-keyboardtoolbar-issues""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Keyboard toolbar issues
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The attached Titanium project shows two issues:</p> <p>One:<br> If the keyboardToolbarHeight value is set greater then 30 the keyboard does not resize correctly in landscape view. If you set this value to 30 it seems to be alright. You can see this in the attached example or in the kitchensink demo.<br> 1) On the index.html page in the iPhone simulator rotate to the right (or left)<br> 2) Press the button<br> 3) You will see the keyboard layout issue. This only happens if the keyboardToolbarHeight value is greater then 30.</p> <p>Two:<br> In landscape view the textArea seems to set the focus at the bottom of the control. When you type you can not see what you are typing without scrolling to the top of the control. Is there anyway that the focus could be set to the top of the control when in landscape mode? The attached same shows this behavior in landscape mode. You can also see this behavior in the Text Fields example in the kitchenSink demo.</p> <p>Community Thread:<br> <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1209-textarea-keyboardtoolbar-issues""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-360,12,"""scrollTo on Table View doesn't appear to work""","""""""{html}<div><p>The scrollTo function on table views doesn't appear to do anything - I've tried calling it from a few different places and it has not had any effect. The code to duplicate the issue is here:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/788956"""""""">http://pastie.org/788956</a></p> <p>and can replace the custom table view example in the Kitchen Sink for verification. Community issue:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1500-uitableviewscrolltoindex-not-working""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: scrollTo on Table View doesn't appear to work
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The scrollTo function on table views doesn't appear to do anything - I've tried calling it from a few different places and it has not had any effect. The code to duplicate the issue is here:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://pastie.org/788956"""""""">http://pastie.org/788956</a></p> <p>and can replace the custom table view example in the Kitchen Sink for verification. Community issue:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1500-uitableviewscrolltoindex-not-working""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-359,12,"""Feature Request - Multiple Select Option Group""","""""""{html}<div><p>Community member feature request - support multi-option select in native controls (similar to Clock.app on iPhone):</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1377-creating-a-multi-select-option-group""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Feature Request - Multiple Select Option Group
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Community member feature request - support multi-option select in native controls (similar to Clock.app on iPhone):</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1377-creating-a-multi-select-option-group""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-358,12,"""Build failure after removing all Titanium JavaScript (iPhone)""","""""""{html}<div><p>When you create a new project with Titanium Developer, open up index.js and remove all the code within the onload function - when you try and build and deploy the simulator, the build fails with the error I have attached. Reported by a community member, verified on my machine as well.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1153-removing-javascript-from-new-project-makes-the-build-fail""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1153-removing-j...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Build failure after removing all Titanium JavaScript (iPhone)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When you create a new project with Titanium Developer, open up index.js and remove all the code within the onload function - when you try and build and deploy the simulator, the build fails with the error I have attached. Reported by a community member, verified on my machine as well.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1153-removing-javascript-from-new-project-makes-the-build-fail""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1153-removing-j...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-357,12,"""Modal Window Wackiness""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you try and create a modal window while a modal window pointing to the same file is being closed, it causes the app to crash. The following files will allow you to quickly recreate the issue/</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Modal Window Wackiness
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you try and create a modal window while a modal window pointing to the same file is being closed, it causes the app to crash. The following files will allow you to quickly recreate the issue/</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-356,12,"""Titanium.Network.networkType == 1 for both 3G and WiFi""","""""""{html}<div><p>As the title of the issues suggests, Titanium.Network.networkType == 1 for both 3G and WiFi connections, which precludes apps from segregating content based on the user's current connection speed. Bug verified on Titanium 0.8.1 and an iPhone 3G.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Titanium.Network.networkType == 1 for both 3G and WiFi
Description: """"{html}<div><p>As the title of the issues suggests, Titanium.Network.networkType == 1 for both 3G and WiFi connections, which precludes apps from segregating content based on the user's current connection speed. Bug verified on Titanium 0.8.1 and an iPhone 3G.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-355,12,"""Implement the input attribute for tableViews on Android""","""""""{html}<div><p>Please see here;</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1160-example-code-showing-how-to-use-the-input-attribute-for-a-tableview#comment_726839""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>We're very keen to get this implemented so that our Android settings page can be implemented just like nearly every other Android app's settings page.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Implement the input attribute for tableViews on Android
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Please see here;</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1160-example-code-showing-how-to-use-the-input-attribute-for-a-tableview#comment_726839""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>We're very keen to get this implemented so that our Android settings page can be implemented just like nearly every other Android app's settings page.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-354,12,"""Opening remote URLs via createWindow is slow on iPhone""","""""""{html}<div><p>Please see <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1234-tm-081-opening-a-remote-url-in-a-window-is-slow-on-iphone""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Opening remote URLs via createWindow is slow on iPhone
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Please see <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1234-tm-081-opening-a-remote-url-in-a-window-is-slow-on-iphone""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-353,12,"""Image view scaling""","""""""{html}<div><p>A request has been made that would allow image scaling in the image view component. Basically, would need a way to make the dimensions of an image scale out to fit the horizontal width given the current orientation of the phone. Here's the support ticket around the request:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/860-image-view-scaling-problem""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Image view scaling
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A request has been made that would allow image scaling in the image view component. Basically, would need a way to make the dimensions of an image scale out to fit the horizontal width given the current orientation of the phone. Here's the support ticket around the request:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/860-image-view-scaling-problem""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-352,12,"""JSLint not working on JS files in subdirectories""","""""""{html}<div><p>JSLint is not being run on JS files in subdirectories of Resources - a community member has a test case:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1446-jslint-not-working""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: JSLint not working on JS files in subdirectories
