TIMOB-348,12,"""Feature request - Text field in keyboard toolbar""","""""""{html}<div><p>Would be nice to be able to include a text field in a keyboard toolbar, as per this support request:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1315-mimic-messages-text-input-toolbar""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>Would this be possible with the new 0.9 stuff? Would be a cool thing to be able to do.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Feature request - Text field in keyboard toolbar
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Would be nice to be able to include a text field in a keyboard toolbar, as per this support request:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1315-mimic-messages-text-input-toolbar""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>Would this be possible with the new 0.9 stuff? Would be a cool thing to be able to do.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-347,12,"""Unconfirmed - Developer and Multiple Users""","""""""{html}<div><p>I have noticed that if I wanted to use a different user account for Titanium, I have to delete the /Library/Application Support/Titanium folder so that Titanium will re-download the sdk files again. Seems kind of buggy if this needs to be done.</p> <p>Needs to be confirmed, let's not work it until I can do so.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Unconfirmed - Developer and Multiple Users
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I have noticed that if I wanted to use a different user account for Titanium, I have to delete the /Library/Application Support/Titanium folder so that Titanium will re-download the sdk files again. Seems kind of buggy if this needs to be done.</p> <p>Needs to be confirmed, let's not work it until I can do so.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-346,12,"""TiAPI: Response JSON""","""""""{html}<div><p>An interesting idea from the community - maybe include a  JSON-serialized xhr.responseJSON field on XHR objects that accept  applcaition/json. This would be a nice convenience for  JSON-spitting web services. Credit to the following community  member:</p>  <p><a href=  """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/202-xhr-responsejson"""""""">  http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: TiAPI: Response JSON
Description: """"{html}<div><p>An interesting idea from the community - maybe include a JSON-serialized xhr.responseJSON field on XHR objects that accept applcaition/json. This would be a nice convenience for JSON-spitting web services. Credit to the following community member:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/202-xhr-responsejson""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-344,12,"""Issue with Composite Views as Child Views in ScrollView""","""""""{html}<div><p>There seems to be issues with using Composite Views as child views in a ScrollView. The order of the views are not maintained within the composite views.</p> <p>Please see forum thread for sample project <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1387-issue-with-scrollviews-with-composite-child-views""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Issue with Composite Views as Child Views in ScrollView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>There seems to be issues with using Composite Views as child views in a ScrollView. The order of the views are not maintained within the composite views.</p> <p>Please see forum thread for sample project <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1387-issue-with-scrollviews-with-composite-child-views""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-343,12,"""Android: Background image download support""","""""""See http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1191-remote-images-very-jerky-on-android-okay-on-iphone    When pulling images from a remote URL, find a way to download in the background and make them available at a later time.""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Background image download support
Description: """"See http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1191-remote-images-very-jerky-on-android-okay-on-iphone When pulling images from a remote URL, find a way to download in the background and make them available at a later time.""""",title+description
TIMOB-342,12,"""Feature request: allow setting the color of the hasChild indicator""","""""""{html}<div><p>Please see <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1378-haschild-indicator-color-how-do-i-set-it""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Feature request: allow setting the color of the hasChild indicator
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Please see <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1378-haschild-indicator-color-how-do-i-set-it""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-341,12,"""Feature request: searchBar & other button options""","""""""{html}<div><p>In TM 0.8.1 there is only the option to have a cancel button. I'd like to request we have more than this available.. such as a standard search button and that kind of thing.. whatever is standard on both the iPhone and Android platforms.</p> <p>Android seems to be something like this (see Marketplace Search):</p> <p>Optional Graphic (does nothing but let you indicate what you're searching for) Search box Search icon (magnifying glass)</p> <p>I'm sure there are lots of UI recommendations for the iPhone :)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Feature request: searchBar & other button options
Description: """"{html}<div><p>In TM 0.8.1 there is only the option to have a cancel button. I'd like to request we have more than this available.. such as a standard search button and that kind of thing.. whatever is standard on both the iPhone and Android platforms.</p> <p>Android seems to be something like this (see Marketplace Search):</p> <p>Optional Graphic (does nothing but let you indicate what you're searching for) Search box Search icon (magnifying glass)</p> <p>I'm sure there are lots of UI recommendations for the iPhone :)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-340,12,"""Table View background color not being recognized on creation""","""""""{html}<div><p>When you create a table view on Android, the backgroundColor attribute is ignored. You can set this property at runtime and have it work.</p> <p>Support ticket:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1086-deleting-a-published-appdownload-page-from-the-<USER>cloud""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1086-deleting-a...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Table View background color not being recognized on creation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When you create a table view on Android, the backgroundColor attribute is ignored. You can set this property at runtime and have it work.</p> <p>Support ticket:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1086-deleting-a-published-appdownload-page-from-the-<USER>cloud""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/1086-deleting-a...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-338,12,"""Set bar image after the window creation""","""""""{html}<div><p>I would like to be able to set the bar image anywhere. There's currently a setBarColor and an option in the tiapp.xml but nothing for images.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.currentWindow.setBarImage(""""""""img/toolbar.png"""""""");</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Set bar image after the window creation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I would like to be able to set the bar image anywhere. There's currently a setBarColor and an option in the tiapp.xml but nothing for images.</p> <pre> <code class= """"""""javascript"""""""">Titanium.UI.currentWindow.setBarImage(""""""""img/toolbar.png"""""""");</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-337,12,"""Custom attributes on map annotations""","""""""{html}<div><p>Being able to refer to map annotations only by their title attribute becomes major issue as soon as one or more share a common title. The only option at present to somehow make each title unique, which means you are forced to display an identifier to the user regardless of whether it's meaningful to them or not.</p> <p>methods with arguments like <code>mapViewInstance.removeAnnotation(myAttribute,aValue){&#8230;}</code>, and also passing these attributes to annotation events, would give you total control over annotations regardless of what information you wanted to display to the user.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Custom attributes on map annotations
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Being able to refer to map annotations only by their title attribute becomes major issue as soon as one or more share a common title. The only option at present to somehow make each title unique, which means you are forced to display an identifier to the user regardless of whether it's meaningful to them or not.</p> <p>methods with arguments like <code>mapViewInstance.removeAnnotation(myAttribute,aValue){&#8230;}</code>, and also passing these attributes to annotation events, would give you total control over annotations regardless of what information you wanted to display to the user.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
