TIMOB-325,12,"""setData fails to refresh active header""","""""""{html}<div><p>setData does not refresh the active header when swapping between data sets.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1187-setdata-causes-wrong-header-to-be-displayed""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>Confirmed by Nolan on 22 December 2009.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: setData fails to refresh active header
Description: """"{html}<div><p>setData does not refresh the active header when swapping between data sets.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1187-setdata-causes-wrong-header-to-be-displayed""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>Confirmed by Nolan on 22 December 2009.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-324,12,"""Facebook API: Allow app to pre-set the content of the user_message for setting status / streamPublish / etc.""","""""""{html}<div><p>If the content is based on something that the user had done, it would be a good extension of the current API to allow the app to pre-populate the user message field in the feed dialog. (See here: <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1207-facebook-status-or-stream-defaulting-text""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a>)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Facebook API: Allow app to pre-set the content of the user_message for setting status / streamPublish / etc.
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If the content is based on something that the user had done, it would be a good extension of the current API to allow the app to pre-populate the user message field in the feed dialog. (See here: <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1207-facebook-status-or-stream-defaulting-text""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a>)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-323,12,"""Android: Allow listener disconnect override""","""""""{html}<div><p>Currently, modules are designed to obey lifecycle events and  disconnect when the activity is paused. Consider adding a flag in  options to circumvent the behavior. Default must be to conserve  power.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Allow listener disconnect override
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Currently, modules are designed to obey lifecycle events and disconnect when the activity is paused. Consider adding a flag in options to circumvent the behavior. Default must be to conserve power.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-322,12,"""Support setObject/getObject in Properties API""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is a feature request for:</p> <pre> <code>Titanium.App.Properties.setObject(obj) Titanium.App.Properties.getObject(obj)</code> </pre> <p>At present, if we want to store a non-array object (such as a hash map) we have to create an array containing a single element which holds the object, and then use setList and getList.</p> <p>This is a bit messy and it would be much easier if we could simply store the object directly.</p> <p>Thanks</p> <p><strong>Edit:</strong> Someone has already tried to write their own custom methods <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/399-adding-an-object-to-appproperties""""""""> here</a>.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Support setObject/getObject in Properties API
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is a feature request for:</p> <pre> <code>Titanium.App.Properties.setObject(obj) Titanium.App.Properties.getObject(obj)</code> </pre> <p>At present, if we want to store a non-array object (such as a hash map) we have to create an array containing a single element which holds the object, and then use setList and getList.</p> <p>This is a bit messy and it would be much easier if we could simply store the object directly.</p> <p>Thanks</p> <p><strong>Edit:</strong> Someone has already tried to write their own custom methods <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/399-adding-an-object-to-appproperties""""""""> here</a>.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-321,12,"""iPhone: Long headers in custom GroupedViews don't display correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>Long headers in custom GroupedViews don't display correctly when a text color is not specified.</p> <p>The problem can be reproduced by making these changes to custom_grouped_view.html in KitchenSink:</p> <ol> <li>In section 1, amend the header from <code>Header</code> to <code>This grouped view provides an example of an unusually long header</code>.<br></li> <li>In section 1, omit the line which reads <code>color:'white'</code>.</li> </ol> <p>When the color parameter is omitted, the start of the header is forced off the top of the screen and can't be seen.</p> <p>The expected result is that which occurs when a text color is specified - i.e. the header is truncated and an ellipsis is added. (But note that there have been <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/661-overlapping-text-in-groupedsection""""""""> other requests</a> for this behaviour to be modified e.g. by optionally text-wrapping instead of truncating.)</p> <p><strong>Examples and screenshots</strong></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1049-header-in-custom-grouped-view""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1115-long-header-not-displaying-correctly-with-grouped-view""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1131-since-upgrading-to-08-this-has-been-happening""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Long headers in custom GroupedViews don't display correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Long headers in custom GroupedViews don't display correctly when a text color is not specified.</p> <p>The problem can be reproduced by making these changes to custom_grouped_view.html in KitchenSink:</p> <ol> <li>In section 1, amend the header from <code>Header</code> to <code>This grouped view provides an example of an unusually long header</code>.<br></li> <li>In section 1, omit the line which reads <code>color:'white'</code>.</li> </ol> <p>When the color parameter is omitted, the start of the header is forced off the top of the screen and can't be seen.</p> <p>The expected result is that which occurs when a text color is specified - i.e. the header is truncated and an ellipsis is added. (But note that there have been <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/661-overlapping-text-in-groupedsection""""""""> other requests</a> for this behaviour to be modified e.g. by optionally text-wrapping instead of truncating.)</p> <p><strong>Examples and screenshots</strong></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1049-header-in-custom-grouped-view""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1115-long-header-not-displaying-correctly-with-grouped-view""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1131-since-upgrading-to-08-this-has-been-happening""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-320,12,"""iPhone: Defect in selected text color on custom TableView and GroupedView""","""""""{html}<div><p>When templates are specified for TableViews and GroupedViews, the default selected text color for row elements breaks.</p> <p>It should be white for the duration of the window animation but instead is shown as black.</p> <p>The problem can be reproduced by changing the TableView in ui.html in KitchenSink to include a basic template:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript"""""""">    // tableview object     var tableView = Titanium.UI.createTableView({template:{layout:[{type:'text', name:'title'}]},data:data,title:'UI API',isPrimary:true}, function(eventObject)     ...</code> </pre> <p>If a touch is held down on a row, the correct selected text color of white is shown, but as soon as the touch is released the text color turns black. If the touch is not held down, no white text is seen at all.</p> <p>The expected result is the same as what happens if no template is specified - i.e. the selected text color remains white for the duration of the selection or window animation.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1144-just-a-few-small-things""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Defect in selected text color on custom TableView and GroupedView
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When templates are specified for TableViews and GroupedViews, the default selected text color for row elements breaks.</p> <p>It should be white for the duration of the window animation but instead is shown as black.</p> <p>The problem can be reproduced by changing the TableView in ui.html in KitchenSink to include a basic template:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> // tableview object var tableView = Titanium.UI.createTableView({template:{layout:[{type:'text', name:'title'}]},data:data,title:'UI API',isPrimary:true}, function(eventObject) ...</code> </pre> <p>If a touch is held down on a row, the correct selected text color of white is shown, but as soon as the touch is released the text color turns black. If the touch is not held down, no white text is seen at all.</p> <p>The expected result is the same as what happens if no template is specified - i.e. the selected text color remains white for the duration of the selection or window animation.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1144-just-a-few-small-things""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-319,12,"""iPhone: Native pickers don't render on preload""","""""""{html}<div><p>Pickers don't render if they're used in a window which has preload set to true.</p> <p>The problem can be reproduced by editing tiapp.xml in KitchenSink so that any one of the preloaded windows points to picker1.html.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1179-picker-fails-to-render-on-preload""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iPhone: Native pickers don't render on preload
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Pickers don't render if they're used in a window which has preload set to true.</p> <p>The problem can be reproduced by editing tiapp.xml in KitchenSink so that any one of the preloaded windows points to picker1.html.</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1179-picker-fails-to-render-on-preload""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-318,12,"""Android: Menu labels missing in 2.0 and 2.1""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1197-possible-menu-bug-on-android""""""""> Possible menu bug on android</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Menu labels missing in 2.0 and 2.1
