TIMOB-284,12,"""Android: expose verticalAlign property for text fields""","""""""{html}<div><p>See <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/283"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #283"""""""">#283</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: expose verticalAlign property for text fields
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/283"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #283"""""""">#283</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-283,12,"""expose verticalAlign property for text fields""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need to expose this property for text fields</p> <p>verticalAlign:'top'<br> verticalAlign:'middle'<br> verticalAlign:'bottom'</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: expose verticalAlign property for text fields
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need to expose this property for text fields</p> <p>verticalAlign:'top'<br> verticalAlign:'middle'<br> verticalAlign:'bottom'</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-282,12,"""Can't close a new window when created from a menu item""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you create a window from a button click listener, then call  Titanium.UI.currentWindow.close() from the opened window it will  work.</p>  <p>But if you create a window from an menu.addItem call (and the  win object is scoped to the callback with a """"""""var"""""""") you can't close  the window.</p>  <p>Sample files attached here:<br>  <a href=  """"""""http://gist.github.com/247895"""""""">http://gist.github.com/247895</a></p>  <p>index.html shows the bug<br>  test.html new window opened by index.html<br>  works.html shows moving the win out of the callback scope makes it  work.</p>  <p>Not sure if it's a """"""""real"""""""" bug or an implementation detail, but I  wanted to report it.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Can't close a new window when created from a menu item
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you create a window from a button click listener, then call Titanium.UI.currentWindow.close() from the opened window it will work.</p> <p>But if you create a window from an menu.addItem call (and the win object is scoped to the callback with a """"""""var"""""""") you can't close the window.</p> <p>Sample files attached here:<br> <a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/247895"""""""">http://gist.github.com/247895</a></p> <p>index.html shows the bug<br> test.html new window opened by index.html<br> works.html shows moving the win out of the callback scope makes it work.</p> <p>Not sure if it's a """"""""real"""""""" bug or an implementation detail, but I wanted to report it.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-281,12,"""Using a keyboard toolbar breaks future keyboard usage when not using toolbar""","""""""{html}<div><p>The keyboard appears to not completely slide out once you have used the keyboard toolbar. I have not tried this in any other app other than the Kitchen Sink demo, but attached screenshots should show the bug.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Using a keyboard toolbar breaks future keyboard usage when not using toolbar
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The keyboard appears to not completely slide out once you have used the keyboard toolbar. I have not tried this in any other app other than the Kitchen Sink demo, but attached screenshots should show the bug.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-280,12,"""Android: responseText not getting populated on status code >= 300""","""""""{html}<div><p>This is needed to see the error data. Found the issue when getting an error from a status update to twitter.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: responseText not getting populated on status code >= 300
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This is needed to see the error data. Found the issue when getting an error from a status update to twitter.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-279,12,"""Android: HTTPClient expects continue, prevents posting to twitter""","""""""{html}<div><p>The underlying HTTPClient implementation now defaults to Expect Continue == true. The default needs to be false.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: HTTPClient expects continue, prevents posting to twitter
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The underlying HTTPClient implementation now defaults to Expect Continue == true. The default needs to be false.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-278,12,"""Android: Missing userLocation option in Map.createView causes NPE""","""""""{html}<div><p>If userLocation is not present in the option set on create, a NullPointerException is thrown.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Missing userLocation option in Map.createView causes NPE
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If userLocation is not present in the option set on create, a NullPointerException is thrown.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-277,12,"""Android Menu Items differ with different SDK""","""""""{html}<div><p>Using this code to create a Menu in Android:<br> <a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/246835"""""""">http://gist.github.com/246835</a></p> <p>This is what it looks like with the 1.5 SDK:<br> <a href= """"""""http://skitch.com/<USER>nj218/titanium-0.7.0-android"""""""">http://skitch.com/<USER>nj218/titanium-0.7.0-android</a></p> <p>Everything looks fine, icon and text.</p> <p>Now using the 2.0 SDK with the same code:<br> <a href= """"""""http://skitch.com/<USER>nj2ub/titanium-android-sdk-2.0"""""""">http://skitch.com/<USER>nj2ub/titanium-android-sdk-2.0</a></p> <p>All you get are big icons, but no text.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Menu Items differ with different SDK
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Using this code to create a Menu in Android:<br> <a href= """"""""http://gist.github.com/246835"""""""">http://gist.github.com/246835</a></p> <p>This is what it looks like with the 1.5 SDK:<br> <a href= """"""""http://skitch.com/<USER>nj218/titanium-0.7.0-android"""""""">http://skitch.com/<USER>nj218/titanium-0.7.0-android</a></p> <p>Everything looks fine, icon and text.</p> <p>Now using the 2.0 SDK with the same code:<br> <a href= """"""""http://skitch.com/<USER>nj2ub/titanium-android-sdk-2.0"""""""">http://skitch.com/<USER>nj2ub/titanium-android-sdk-2.0</a></p> <p>All you get are big icons, but no text.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-276,12,"""Problem with space in file name for projects""","""""""{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/979-project-folders-being-automatically-deleted""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>looks to be a regression in 0.8</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Problem with space in file name for projects
Description: """"{html}<div><p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/979-project-folders-being-automatically-deleted""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>looks to be a regression in 0.8</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-275,12,"""Using fontWeight and fontFamily in a layout""","""""""{html}<div><p>If an element has fontWeight:'bold', all other elements must explicitly set the fontWeight or they will inherit the bold property.</p> <p>Using the fontFamily property on a row element negates the fontWeight property (i.e., fontFamily negates a bold fontWeight)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Using fontWeight and fontFamily in a layout
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If an element has fontWeight:'bold', all other elements must explicitly set the fontWeight or they will inherit the bold property.</p> <p>Using the fontFamily property on a row element negates the fontWeight property (i.e., fontFamily negates a bold fontWeight)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
