TIMOB-167,12,"""API - Add Mapkit Support""","""""""{html}<div><p>I've seen your Mapkit integration in the 0.7.0 screencast; loved it. Don't know much about how you prioritize features, but I'm desperate to see Mapkit in 0.7.1 or one of the next releases.</p> <p>I found this: <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/29-titanium-mobile-iphone-map-kit-support""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>but Mapkit does not seem to be part of the official release plan yet. At least not on Lighthouse.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: API - Add Mapkit Support
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I've seen your Mapkit integration in the 0.7.0 screencast; loved it. Don't know much about how you prioritize features, but I'm desperate to see Mapkit in 0.7.1 or one of the next releases.</p> <p>I found this: <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/29-titanium-mobile-iphone-map-kit-support""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>but Mapkit does not seem to be part of the official release plan yet. At least not on Lighthouse.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-166,12,"""Problem with sending POST body as string / xml""","""""""{html}<div><p>Trying to use the web services API from Backpack and it requires XML POST body. However, we assume dictionary (key/value pairs) and so you can't send data correctly.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Problem with sending POST body as string / xml
