TIMOB-153,12,"""Android Properties api not typecasting to Javascript objects correctly""","""""""{html}<div><p>getString and possibly other methods are returning the underlying Java object and not forcing it to the Javascript type. This causes problems with HTTPClient and possibly other APIs that are expecting objects of type string.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Properties api not typecasting to Javascript objects correctly
Description: """"{html}<div><p>getString and possibly other methods are returning the underlying Java object and not forcing it to the Javascript type. This causes problems with HTTPClient and possibly other APIs that are expecting objects of type string.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-152,12,"""Android: Add support for application properties that can be configured outside app""","""""""{html}<div><p>need to add support for application properties which are loaded  into the application at compile time but are outside the source  code (both to be configurable and more secure). properties should  be compiled in and made available via  Titanium.App.Properties.getString. file format is java properties  (key=value). file will automatically be picked up during compile if  located in project.dir/appdata.cfg.</p></div>{html}""""""",New Feature,"Title: Android: Add support for application properties that can be configured outside app
Description: """"{html}<div><p>need to add support for application properties which are loaded into the application at compile time but are outside the source code (both to be configurable and more secure). properties should be compiled in and made available via Titanium.App.Properties.getString. file format is java properties (key=value). file will automatically be picked up during compile if located in project.dir/appdata.cfg.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
