Description: """"{html}<div><p>W/TiWebView( 738): (main) Handling load source message: file:///android_asset/Resources/shorter.html<br></p> <pre> <code>I/ActivityManager( 583): Displayed activity com.catechizeme.full/org.<USER>titanium.TitaniumActivity: 323 ms E/TiSwitch( 738): (WebViewCoreThread) {""""""""image"""""""":""""""""images/first.png""""""""} E/TiSwitch( 738): (WebViewCoreThread) {""""""""image"""""""":""""""""images/back.png""""""""} E/TiSwitch( 738): (WebViewCoreThread) {""""""""image"""""""":""""""""images/sync.png""""""""} E/TiSwitch( 738): (WebViewCoreThread) {""""""""image"""""""":""""""""images/forward.png""""""""} E/TiSwitch( 738): (WebViewCoreThread) {""""""""image"""""""":""""""""images/last.png""""""""} E/TiSwitch( 738): (WebViewCoreThread) {""""""""systemButton"""""""":-1} D/WebCore ( 738): Console: TypeError: Result of expression 'Titanium.UI.currentWindow.setToolbar' [undefined] is not a function. line: 23 source: file:///android_asset/Resources/javascripts/cards.min.js</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-123,12,"""Android html view in TableView doesn't handle styles""","""""""{html}<div><p>The html support which I was using for html list items used TagSoup which ignores styles. To be more consistent with iPhone the items should use WebViews when rendering html.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android html view in TableView doesn't handle styles
Description: """"{html}<div><p>The html support which I was using for html list items used TagSoup which ignores styles. To be more consistent with iPhone the items should use WebViews when rendering html.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-122,12,"""Support JS Touch Events ""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need to support JS touch events as well as other capabilities that are free with a web view. There are probably two options:</p> <p>1) We need to make the existing web view support touch events</p> <p>or</p> <p>2) We need to create a new type of view. For example, the existing web view could become a HybridView or Composite View and we could create a new web view that supports the appropriate JS events/capabilities</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Support JS Touch Events
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need to support JS touch events as well as other capabilities that are free with a web view. There are probably two options:</p> <p>1) We need to make the existing web view support touch events</p> <p>or</p> <p>2) We need to create a new type of view. For example, the existing web view could become a HybridView or Composite View and we could create a new web view that supports the appropriate JS events/capabilities</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
