TIMOB-102,12,"""TableView appendRow""","""""""{html}<div><p>We need to make it easy for people to simply add rows to existing table views.</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> tableView.appendRow(rowData, {animationStyle:Titanium.UI.iPhone.RowAnimationStyle.DOWN});  Note animationStyle is only supported on iPhone currently</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView appendRow
Description: """"{html}<div><p>We need to make it easy for people to simply add rows to existing table views.</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> tableView.appendRow(rowData, {animationStyle:Titanium.UI.iPhone.RowAnimationStyle.DOWN}); Note animationStyle is only supported on iPhone currently</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-101,12,"""Set control values dynamically after creation""","""""""{html}<div><p>see <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/100"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #100"""""""">#100</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Set control values dynamically after creation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>see <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/100"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #100"""""""">#100</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-100,12,"""Set control values dynamically after creation""","""""""{html}<div><p>This affects:</p> <ul> <li> <p>textfields</p> </li> <li> <p>sliders</p> </li> <li> <p>switches</p> </li> <li> <p>textareas</p> </li> <li> <p>tabbedbars (iPhone only)</p> </li> </ul> <p>Setting values:</p> <p>textfield.setValue('newValue');</p> <p>Getting values:</p> <p>var val = textfield.getValue();</p> <p>or</p> <p>var val = textfield.value;</p> <p>Also, for the tabbed bar, we should probably do something like:</p> <p>tabbedbar.setIndex(index);</p> <p>var activeIndex = tabbedbar.index</p> <p>or</p> <p>var activeIndex = tabbedbar.getIndex();</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Set control values dynamically after creation
Description: """"{html}<div><p>This affects:</p> <ul> <li> <p>textfields</p> </li> <li> <p>sliders</p> </li> <li> <p>switches</p> </li> <li> <p>textareas</p> </li> <li> <p>tabbedbars (iPhone only)</p> </li> </ul> <p>Setting values:</p> <p>textfield.setValue('newValue');</p> <p>Getting values:</p> <p>var val = textfield.getValue();</p> <p>or</p> <p>var val = textfield.value;</p> <p>Also, for the tabbed bar, we should probably do something like:</p> <p>tabbedbar.setIndex(index);</p> <p>var activeIndex = tabbedbar.index</p> <p>or</p> <p>var activeIndex = tabbedbar.getIndex();</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-99,12,"""Support non-standard data in TableViews and GroupedViews ""","""""""{html}<div><p>see <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/98"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #98"""""""">#98</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Support non-standard data in TableViews and GroupedViews
Description: """"{html}<div><p>see <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/98"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #98"""""""">#98</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-98,12,"""Support non-standard data in TableViews and GroupedViews ""","""""""{html}<div><p>Allow a developer to pass additional attributes into the TableView/GroupedView JSON data object, then ensure that these attributes are available in the event data of the click event. Here's an example</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var data = [     {title:'foo', name:'George'},     {title:'foo', name:'Fred'} ];  var a = Titanium.UI.createTableView({data:data}, function(e) {     e.rowData.name // should be name attribute for clicked row based on above JSON object }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Support non-standard data in TableViews and GroupedViews
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Allow a developer to pass additional attributes into the TableView/GroupedView JSON data object, then ensure that these attributes are available in the event data of the click event. Here's an example</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var data = [ {title:'foo', name:'George'}, {title:'foo', name:'Fred'} ]; var a = Titanium.UI.createTableView({data:data}, function(e) { e.rowData.name // should be name attribute for clicked row based on above JSON object }</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-97,12,"""TableView update bug""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you create a table view using the 'title' attribute, then update a row using the 'html' attribute, you cannot then update the row again using a 'title' attribute</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: TableView update bug
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you create a table view using the 'title' attribute, then update a row using the 'html' attribute, you cannot then update the row again using a 'title' attribute</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-96,12,"""Single library build for iPhone""","""""""{html}<div><p>build a single libTitanium.a that will work regardless of the version of the phone or simulator OS version.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Single library build for iPhone
Description: """"{html}<div><p>build a single libTitanium.a that will work regardless of the version of the phone or simulator OS version.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-95,12,"""Override built-in XMLHttpRequest to use Titanium.Network""","""""""{html}<div><p>To make it seamless to support libraries such as jQuery, Mootools, YUI, etc that have their own AJAX convenience methods, we need to patch XMLHttpRequest to use Titanium.Network.createHttpClient</p> <p>such as:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> window.XMLHttpRequest = function() {     return new Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient() };</code> </pre> <p>test case w/ jquery:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> $.getJSON(""""""""http://api.flickr.com/services/feeds/photos_public.gne?tags=cat&amp;tagmode=any&amp;format=json&amp;jsoncallback=?"""""""",                 function(data) {          $.each(data.items, function(i,item){         $(""""""""&lt;img/&gt;"""""""").attr(""""""""src"""""""", item.media.m).appendTo(""""""""#log"""""""");                      if ( i == 3 ) return false;         }); });</code> </pre> <p>(make sure you create a div with id log in HTML)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Override built-in XMLHttpRequest to use Titanium.Network
Description: """"{html}<div><p>To make it seamless to support libraries such as jQuery, Mootools, YUI, etc that have their own AJAX convenience methods, we need to patch XMLHttpRequest to use Titanium.Network.createHttpClient</p> <p>such as:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> window.XMLHttpRequest = function() { return new Titanium.Network.createHTTPClient() };</code> </pre> <p>test case w/ jquery:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> $.getJSON(""""""""http://api.flickr.com/services/feeds/photos_public.gne?tags=cat&amp;tagmode=any&amp;format=json&amp;jsoncallback=?"""""""", function(data) { $.each(data.items, function(i,item){ $(""""""""&lt;img/&gt;"""""""").attr(""""""""src"""""""", item.media.m).appendTo(""""""""#log""""""""); if ( i == 3 ) return false; }); });</code> </pre> <p>(make sure you create a div with id log in HTML)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-94,12,"""Enable setBadge for any tab (iPhone only)""","""""""{html}<div><p>Enable the ability to set the badge for any tab. The API is:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> // get tabs array (or you can get by name) var tabs = Titanium.UI.getTabs();  // set first tab to 1 tabs[0].setBadge(1);  // set second tab to 2 tabs[1].setBadge(2);  // set third tab to 3  tabs[2].setBadge(3);  // set fourth tab to 4 tabs[3].setBadge(4);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Enable setBadge for any tab (iPhone only)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Enable the ability to set the badge for any tab. The API is:</p> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> // get tabs array (or you can get by name) var tabs = Titanium.UI.getTabs(); // set first tab to 1 tabs[0].setBadge(1); // set second tab to 2 tabs[1].setBadge(2); // set third tab to 3 tabs[2].setBadge(3); // set fourth tab to 4 tabs[3].setBadge(4);</code> </pre></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-93,12,"""Support tabchange event listener""","""""""{html}<div><p>Support the ability to listener for tab change events:</p> <p>Here's the API spec:</p> <p>Titanium.UI.addEventListener('tabchange',function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>e.index  // the index of the newly active tab  e.name   // the name of the newly active tab (from the &lt;id&gt; window attribute in tiapp.xml  e.prevIndex // the previously active index  e.prevName  // the previously active name</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Support tabchange event listener
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Support the ability to listener for tab change events:</p> <p>Here's the API spec:</p> <p>Titanium.UI.addEventListener('tabchange',function(e)<br> {</p> <pre> <code>e.index // the index of the newly active tab e.name // the name of the newly active tab (from the &lt;id&gt; window attribute in tiapp.xml e.prevIndex // the previously active index e.prevName // the previously active name</code> </pre> <p>});</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-92,12,"""Support ability to set active tab""","""""""{html}<div><p>Support the ability to set the active tab programatically (both Android and iPhone)</p> <p>1) get the tabs</p> <p>Method 1:</p> <p>var tabs = Titanium.UI.getTabs();</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setActiveTab(tabs[0]);</p> <p>Method 2:</p> <p>var tab = Titanium.UI.getTabByName('Views');</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setActiveTab(tab);</p> <p>The name of the tab is the field specified in the tiapp.xml file</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Support ability to set active tab
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Support the ability to set the active tab programatically (both Android and iPhone)</p> <p>1) get the tabs</p> <p>Method 1:</p> <p>var tabs = Titanium.UI.getTabs();</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setActiveTab(tabs[0]);</p> <p>Method 2:</p> <p>var tab = Titanium.UI.getTabByName('Views');</p> <p>Titanium.UI.setActiveTab(tab);</p> <p>The name of the tab is the field specified in the tiapp.xml file</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
