TIMOB-66,12,"""AndroidManifest.xml is missing minSDKVersion""","""""""{html}<div><p>See tender issue <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/183-uploading-an-app-to-google-android""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/183-uploading-a...</a></p> <p>&lt;uses-sdk minSdkVersion=""""""""3"""""""" /&gt; needs to be added right after the manifest tag. Apparently the Market XML parser is order dependent.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: AndroidManifest.xml is missing minSDKVersion
Description: """"{html}<div><p>See tender issue <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/183-uploading-an-app-to-google-android""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/183-uploading-a...</a></p> <p>&lt;uses-sdk minSdkVersion=""""""""3"""""""" /&gt; needs to be added right after the manifest tag. Apparently the Market XML parser is order dependent.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-65,12,"""Via Tender: Titanium Developer doesn't work when Safari 4 is installed""","""""""{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/41-titanium-developer-doesnt-work-when-safari-4-is-installed""""""""> Tender issue #41</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>Hello there. I already asked concerning this issue, but the google group got lost ... Here is my issue: The previous Beta worked fine (the one without the login), but after the last update i can't even log in to Titanium Developer under OS X. I registered successfully, but every time I try to login, it just say's: """"""""request timed out, make sure u are connected to internet."""""""" Thats frustrating. I installed Safari 4 too. Maybe it has to do with that. It can't be a firewall issue, I already tried without. I wozld really feel happy if someone could help me out with that.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Via Tender: Titanium Developer doesn't work when Safari 4 is installed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/41-titanium-developer-doesnt-work-when-safari-4-is-installed""""""""> Tender issue #41</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>Hello there. I already asked concerning this issue, but the google group got lost ... Here is my issue: The previous Beta worked fine (the one without the login), but after the last update i can't even log in to Titanium Developer under OS X. I registered successfully, but every time I try to login, it just say's: """"""""request timed out, make sure u are connected to internet."""""""" Thats frustrating. I installed Safari 4 too. Maybe it has to do with that. It can't be a firewall issue, I already tried without. I wozld really feel happy if someone could help me out with that.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""",title+description
