TIMOB-62,12,"""Build scripts not correctly propagating app name changes""","""""""{html}<div><p>If you change the name for a project (for iPhone at least), those changes aren't propagated to the build artifacts for the project. Reported in the following support case:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/74-importing-a-site-and-changing-the-nameinfo-fails-on-test""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/74-importing-a-...</a></p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Build scripts not correctly propagating app name changes
Description: """"{html}<div><p>If you change the name for a project (for iPhone at least), those changes aren't propagated to the build artifacts for the project. Reported in the following support case:</p> <p><a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/74-importing-a-site-and-changing-the-nameinfo-fails-on-test""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/74-importing-a-...</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-61,12,"""Android Icons aren't Documented""","""""""{html}<div><p>From tender <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/73-what-are-all-of-the-possible-properties-of-titaniumuiandroidsystemicon-object""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>Need to document the icons in Titanium.UI</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Icons aren't Documented
Description: """"{html}<div><p>From tender <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/73-what-are-all-of-the-possible-properties-of-titaniumuiandroidsystemicon-object""""""""> http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discuss...</a></p> <p>Need to document the icons in Titanium.UI</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-60,12,"""iOS: TM won't build when there's an apostrophe in folder names""","""""""{html}<div><p>I had this problem with Titanium Mobile 0.5.0 and 0.5.2.</p>  <p>I originally put my project in a folder that had an apostrophe  in it. But when I tried to run """"""""launch app"""""""" under the """"""""test &amp;  package"""""""" tab in Titanium Developer, I got this message:</p>  <p>sh: -c: line 0: unexpected EOF while looking for matching  <code>''&lt;br/&gt; sh: -c: line 1: syntax error: unexpected end of  file&lt;br/&gt; App Spec: specified by path /<USER>s  Folder/mobiletest/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator/mobiletest.app&lt;br/&gt;  SDK Root:  path=/Developer/Platforms/iPhoneSimulator.platform/Developer/SDKs/iPhoneSimulator3.0.sdk  version=3.0 name=Simulator - iPhone OS 3.0&lt;br/&gt; Session could  not be started: Error Domain=DTiPhoneSimulatorErrorDomain Code=1  UserInfo=0x2214c0 """"""""Unknown error.""""""""One moment, building  ...&lt;br/&gt; kill simulator called&lt;br/&gt; signal caught:  3&lt;br/&gt; calling log kill on 2044&lt;br/&gt; kill simulator  called</code></p>  <p>I also got an Apple warning with a yellow triangle that  said:</p>  <p>""""""""The Application Python Quit Unexpectedly, Mac OSX and other  programs are not affected"""""""" (the usual screen you get when one of  your programs quits without warning).</p>  <p>It took a couple hours to figure it out, but once I put the  project in a folder that didn't have an apostrophe (or space) it  built correctly. Perhaps you could have a look, maybe make it more  clear that you can't have an apostrophe anywhere in the path to  your Titanium Mobile files? Thanks a million; I love your  program.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: iOS: TM won't build when there's an apostrophe in folder names
Description: """"{html}<div><p>I had this problem with Titanium Mobile 0.5.0 and 0.5.2.</p> <p>I originally put my project in a folder that had an apostrophe in it. But when I tried to run """"""""launch app"""""""" under the """"""""test &amp; package"""""""" tab in Titanium Developer, I got this message:</p> <p>sh: -c: line 0: unexpected EOF while looking for matching <code>''&lt;br/&gt; sh: -c: line 1: syntax error: unexpected end of file&lt;br/&gt; App Spec: specified by path /<USER>s Folder/mobiletest/build/iphone/build/Debug-iphonesimulator/mobiletest.app&lt;br/&gt; SDK Root: path=/Developer/Platforms/iPhoneSimulator.platform/Developer/SDKs/iPhoneSimulator3.0.sdk version=3.0 name=Simulator - iPhone OS 3.0&lt;br/&gt; Session could not be started: Error Domain=DTiPhoneSimulatorErrorDomain Code=1 UserInfo=0x2214c0 """"""""Unknown error.""""""""One moment, building ...&lt;br/&gt; kill simulator called&lt;br/&gt; signal caught: 3&lt;br/&gt; calling log kill on 2044&lt;br/&gt; kill simulator called</code></p> <p>I also got an Apple warning with a yellow triangle that said:</p> <p>""""""""The Application Python Quit Unexpectedly, Mac OSX and other programs are not affected"""""""" (the usual screen you get when one of your programs quits without warning).</p> <p>It took a couple hours to figure it out, but once I put the project in a folder that didn't have an apostrophe (or space) it built correctly. Perhaps you could have a look, maybe make it more clear that you can't have an apostrophe anywhere in the path to your Titanium Mobile files? Thanks a million; I love your program.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
