TIMOB-56,12,"""Android: Race condition in HTTPClient when invoking readystate callback""","""""""{html}<div><p>A race condition exists where the readyState function invocations were being queued up by the WebViewCoreThread and only executing after readyState had been set to 4. So in normal usage patterns the code executed when the document was loaded was getting run 3 or 4 times depending on whether the callback was set before or after open.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android: Race condition in HTTPClient when invoking readystate callback
Description: """"{html}<div><p>A race condition exists where the readyState function invocations were being queued up by the WebViewCoreThread and only executing after readyState had been set to 4. So in normal usage patterns the code executed when the document was loaded was getting run 3 or 4 times depending on whether the callback was set before or after open.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
