Description: """"{html}<div><p>Spec is in ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/18"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #18"""""""">#18</a></p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-54,12,"""Android Not Launching tel: URL""","""""""{html}<div><p>Described in <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/147-inconsistent-iphone-and-android-tableview-behavior-with-phone-numbers""""""""> this</a> support issue.</p> <p>Basically, to activate feature protocols tel: mailto: geo: I need to launch activities on the device for those urls.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Android Not Launching tel: URL
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Described in <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/147-inconsistent-iphone-and-android-tableview-behavior-with-phone-numbers""""""""> this</a> support issue.</p> <p>Basically, to activate feature protocols tel: mailto: geo: I need to launch activities on the device for those urls.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-53,12,"""createWindow in Android does not allow external access""","""""""{html}<div><p>Per this support item <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/146-inconsistent-iphone-and-android-tableview-behavior-with-external-url""""""""> Subject: Inconsistent iphone and android tableview behavior with external url</a></p> <p>Android should allow createWindow to open an embedded webview that has no access to Titanium functionality.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: createWindow in Android does not allow external access
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Per this support item <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/146-inconsistent-iphone-and-android-tableview-behavior-with-external-url""""""""> Subject: Inconsistent iphone and android tableview behavior with external url</a></p> <p>Android should allow createWindow to open an embedded webview that has no access to Titanium functionality.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-52,12,"""Image path resolution (iPhone only)""","""""""{html}<div><p>When you create a project that has spaces in the app name, trying to include images in an HTML file fails in the simulator. Reported by a community member and confirmed by me on the 0.5.0 release.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Image path resolution (iPhone only)
Description: """"{html}<div><p>When you create a project that has spaces in the app name, trying to include images in an HTML file fails in the simulator. Reported by a community member and confirmed by me on the 0.5.0 release.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-50,12,"""API - Titanium.UI.createSwitch (Android)""",""""""".h3 Description    The purpose of this API is to create a switch native control. (copied from iPhone ticket)    .h3 Example        .h3 API Arguments    * id: optional. HTML element id for where the switch will be placed if placed in webview  *  value: the initial value. default is true.  * color: optional. text color  * backgroundColor: optional. background color of field""""""",Bug,"Title: API - Titanium.UI.createSwitch (Android)
Description: """".h3 Description The purpose of this API is to create a switch native control. (copied from iPhone ticket) .h3 Example .h3 API Arguments * id: optional. HTML element id for where the switch will be placed if placed in webview * value: the initial value. default is true. * color: optional. text color * backgroundColor: optional. background color of field""""",title+description
TIMOB-49,12,"""API - Titanium.UI.createButton (Android)""","""""""{html}<div><h2>Description</h2> <p>The purpose of this API is to create a button native control. (Copied from iPhone ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/22"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #22"""""""">#22</a>)</p> <h2>Example</h2> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({id:'foo',title:'My Title', icon:'images/foo.png'})   // add event listneer button.addEventListener('click',function(event) { });</code> </pre> <h2>API Arguments</h2> <p><strong>id</strong> : optional. HTML element id for where the button will be placed if placed in webview</p> <p><strong>title</strong> : optional. title text on button</p> <p><strong>icon</strong> : optional. path to image file</p> <p><strong>style</strong> : pre-defined button style</p> <p><strong>systemButton</strong> : pre-defined system icon or button (iPhone only)</p> <p><strong>width</strong> : optional. width of button</p> <p><strong>height</strong> : optional. height of button</p> <p><strong>backgroundImage</strong> : optional. path to a background image to be used as the background for the button</p> <p><strong>color</strong> : optional. text color</p> <p><strong>backgroundColor</strong> : optional. background color of field</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: API - Titanium.UI.createButton (Android)
Description: """"{html}<div><h2>Description</h2> <p>The purpose of this API is to create a button native control. (Copied from iPhone ticket <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/22"""""""" title=""""""""Ticket #22"""""""">#22</a>)</p> <h2>Example</h2> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var button = Titanium.UI.createButton({id:'foo',title:'My Title', icon:'images/foo.png'}) // add event listneer button.addEventListener('click',function(event) { });</code> </pre> <h2>API Arguments</h2> <p><strong>id</strong> : optional. HTML element id for where the button will be placed if placed in webview</p> <p><strong>title</strong> : optional. title text on button</p> <p><strong>icon</strong> : optional. path to image file</p> <p><strong>style</strong> : pre-defined button style</p> <p><strong>systemButton</strong> : pre-defined system icon or button (iPhone only)</p> <p><strong>width</strong> : optional. width of button</p> <p><strong>height</strong> : optional. height of button</p> <p><strong>backgroundImage</strong> : optional. path to a background image to be used as the background for the button</p> <p><strong>color</strong> : optional. text color</p> <p><strong>backgroundColor</strong> : optional. background color of field</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-48,12,"""Difficult to tell Android application is successfully installed""","""""""{html}<div><p>[]()</p> <p>Since we're currently unable to reliably launch an Android application from developer. Log output should be more helpful letting the user know we're installing and that the app is installed and where to look.</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Difficult to tell Android application is successfully installed
Description: """"{html}<div><p>[]()</p> <p>Since we're currently unable to reliably launch an Android application from developer. Log output should be more helpful letting the user know we're installing and that the app is installed and where to look.</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-47,12,"""Database.ResultSet.isValidRow() returns true for CREATE statements""","""""""{html}<div><p>After running a CREATE query (may occur with others, only CREATE verified as of yet) Database.ResultSet.isValidRow() returns true, when it should return false. (data extraction methods may not be called on the ResultSet after such a query)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Database.ResultSet.isValidRow() returns true for CREATE statements
Description: """"{html}<div><p>After running a CREATE query (may occur with others, only CREATE verified as of yet) Database.ResultSet.isValidRow() returns true, when it should return false. (data extraction methods may not be called on the ResultSet after such a query)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
