TIMOB-42,12,"""API - Titanium.UI.createTabbedBar""","""""""{html}<div><h2>Description</h2> <p>The purpose of this API is to create a tabbed bar native control.</p> <h2>Example</h2> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var tabbedBar = Titanium.UI.createTabbedBar({id:'foo', labels:[button1, button2], color:'#336699'});  Note: a tabbedBar can be inserted on the toolbar or navbar like a normal button</code> </pre> <h2>API Arguments</h2> <p><strong>id</strong> : optional. HTML element id for where the button bar will be placed if placed in webview</p> <p><strong>labels</strong> : array of button title strings</p> <p><strong>activeIndex</strong> : optional. default is 0. the index of the active tab</p> <p><strong>images</strong> : array of button images</p> <p><strong>color</strong> : hex web color for buttons (e.g., <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/336699"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #336699"""""""">#336699</a>)</p> <p><strong>backgroundColor</strong> : optional. background color of button</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: API - Titanium.UI.createTabbedBar
Description: """"{html}<div><h2>Description</h2> <p>The purpose of this API is to create a tabbed bar native control.</p> <h2>Example</h2> <pre> <code class=""""""""javascript""""""""> var tabbedBar = Titanium.UI.createTabbedBar({id:'foo', labels:[button1, button2], color:'#336699'}); Note: a tabbedBar can be inserted on the toolbar or navbar like a normal button</code> </pre> <h2>API Arguments</h2> <p><strong>id</strong> : optional. HTML element id for where the button bar will be placed if placed in webview</p> <p><strong>labels</strong> : array of button title strings</p> <p><strong>activeIndex</strong> : optional. default is 0. the index of the active tab</p> <p><strong>images</strong> : array of button images</p> <p><strong>color</strong> : hex web color for buttons (e.g., <a href=""""""""/projects/32238/tickets/336699"""""""" title= """"""""Ticket #336699"""""""">#336699</a>)</p> <p><strong>backgroundColor</strong> : optional. background color of button</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-41,12,"""WindowsError: [Error 3] The system cannot find the path specified""","""""""{html}<div><ol> <li>create new project for android sdk</li> </ol> <p>Name: PF5<br> App ID: com.rmm.pf5<br> App icon: appicon.png<br> Titanium SDK: 0.42</p> <ol> <li>Test and Package<br></li> <li>""""""""Run andoird emulator""""""""</li> </ol> <h2>Error</h2> <p>Launching Android emulator...one moment<br> Launching Android emulator...one moment<br> Traceback (most recent call last):<br> File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\mobilesdk\win32\0.4.2\android\builder.py"""""""", line 315, in<br> s.run_emulator()<br> File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\mobilesdk\win32\0.4.2\android\builder.py"""""""", line 69, in run_emulator<br> """"""""'<em>:d</em> '"""""""" File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\modules\win32\python\0.4.4\lib\subprocess.py"""""""", line 594, in <strong>init</strong><br> errread, errwrite)<br> File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\modules\win32\python\0.4.4\lib\subprocess.py"""""""", line 822, in _execute_child<br> startupinfo)<br></p> <h2>WindowsError: [Error 3] The system cannot find the path specified</h2> <p>Please help me get past this error so I can start Android development.</p> <p>Thank you :)</p></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: WindowsError: [Error 3] The system cannot find the path specified
Description: """"{html}<div><ol> <li>create new project for android sdk</li> </ol> <p>Name: PF5<br> App ID: com.rmm.pf5<br> App icon: appicon.png<br> Titanium SDK: 0.42</p> <ol> <li>Test and Package<br></li> <li>""""""""Run andoird emulator""""""""</li> </ol> <h2>Error</h2> <p>Launching Android emulator...one moment<br> Launching Android emulator...one moment<br> Traceback (most recent call last):<br> File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\mobilesdk\win32\0.4.2\android\builder.py"""""""", line 315, in<br> s.run_emulator()<br> File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\mobilesdk\win32\0.4.2\android\builder.py"""""""", line 69, in run_emulator<br> """"""""'<em>:d</em> '"""""""" File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\modules\win32\python\0.4.4\lib\subprocess.py"""""""", line 594, in <strong>init</strong><br> errread, errwrite)<br> File """"""""C:\ProgramData\Titanium\modules\win32\python\0.4.4\lib\subprocess.py"""""""", line 822, in _execute_child<br> startupinfo)<br></p> <h2>WindowsError: [Error 3] The system cannot find the path specified</h2> <p>Please help me get past this error so I can start Android development.</p> <p>Thank you :)</p></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-40,12,"""Via Tender: Bug in modules/tiui/ui.js with console.log function on line 99""","""""""{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/10-bug-in-modulestiuiuijs-with-consolelog-function-on-line-99""""""""> Tender issue #10</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>There seems to be an bug in the modules/tiui/ui.js which is loaded by every Titanium app. The problem is on line 99:</p> <pre> <code>// // override console.log to also send into our API logger // var old_log = console.log; console.log = function(msg) {     Titanium.API.debug(msg);     return old_log(msg); // line 99 };</code> </pre> <p>The reported error is a Type Error and occurs as soon as one uses the console.log function line """"""""console.log('something')"""""""".</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Via Tender: Bug in modules/tiui/ui.js with console.log function on line 99
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/10-bug-in-modulestiuiuijs-with-consolelog-function-on-line-99""""""""> Tender issue #10</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>There seems to be an bug in the modules/tiui/ui.js which is loaded by every Titanium app. The problem is on line 99:</p> <pre> <code>// // override console.log to also send into our API logger // var old_log = console.log; console.log = function(msg) { Titanium.API.debug(msg); return old_log(msg); // line 99 };</code> </pre> <p>The reported error is a Type Error and occurs as soon as one uses the console.log function line """"""""console.log('something')"""""""".</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-39,12,"""Via Tender: Printing Support""","""""""{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/suggestions/5-printing-support""""""""> Tender issue #5</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>It would be nice to be able to use window.print(); or even a silent_print(); feature which would allow Point of Sale developers to print receipts without the prompt window.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Via Tender: Printing Support
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/suggestions/5-printing-support""""""""> Tender issue #5</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>It would be nice to be able to use window.print(); or even a silent_print(); feature which would allow Point of Sale developers to print receipts without the prompt window.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-38,12,"""Via Tender: Maemo Support""","""""""{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1-maemo-support""""""""> Tender issue #1</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>Hello,</p> <p>I noticed that Titanium supports both iPhone and Android. I was wondering if it intends on supporting the Maemo OS by Nokia?</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Via Tender: Maemo Support
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/titanium-mobile-discussion/1-maemo-support""""""""> Tender issue #1</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>Hello,</p> <p>I noticed that Titanium supports both iPhone and Android. I was wondering if it intends on supporting the Maemo OS by Nokia?</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""",title+description
TIMOB-37,12,"""Via Tender: Test &amp; Package screen is blank""","""""""{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/72-test-package-screen-is-blank""""""""> Tender issue #72</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>I'm running Ubuntu Jaunty, updated to the latest mobile sdk and developer versions. I have a project that I imported from my mac successfully but when I click on """"""""Test &amp; Package"""""""" the screen is blank.</p> <p>This same project back on my Mac is fine and I can test and package. The mac is running the latest versions of everything as well.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""""",Bug,"Title: Via Tender: Test &amp; Package screen is blank
Description: """"{html}<div><p>Assigned to <a href= """"""""http://support.<USER>net/discussions/support/72-test-package-screen-is-blank""""""""> Tender issue #72</a>. As reported in Tender:</p> <blockquote> <p>I'm running Ubuntu Jaunty, updated to the latest mobile sdk and developer versions. I have a project that I imported from my mac successfully but when I click on """"""""Test &amp; Package"""""""" the screen is blank.</p> <p>This same project back on my Mac is fine and I can test and package. The mac is running the latest versions of everything as well.</p> </blockquote></div>{html}""""",title+description
